{"queueIndex":1,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_fib_tbsa_anterior_mix_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,61],"fullStemEn":"An adult client arrives after a thermal injury. Estimate the percentage of total body surface area (%TBSA) represented by the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns on the diagram. Record the answer as a number.","fullStemZh":"一名成年患者因热损伤就诊。根据图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤，估算其体表总面积百分比（%TBSA）。请以数字形式记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record the answer as a number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请以数字形式记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Estimate the percentage of total body surface area (%TBSA) represented by the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns on the diagram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤，估算其体表总面积百分比（%TBSA）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"%TBSA","zh":"%体表面积"},"acceptable":["27","27%"],"numeric":{"value":27,"unit":"%TBSA","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the anterior trunk (18%), anterior head (4.5%), and anterior left arm (4.5%). The total is 18 + 4.5 + 4.5 = 27% TBSA.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为躯干前侧（18%）、头部前侧（4.5%）和左上肢前侧（4.5%）。合计为 18 + 4.5 + 4.5 = 27% TBSA。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For Rule-of-Nines visuals, name each shaded body surface before adding. Do not count unshaded posterior or opposite-side surfaces.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做九分法图示题时，先逐一说出每个阴影身体表面，再相加。不要计入未阴影的背侧或对侧表面。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; Minnesota Department of Health Rule of Nines Adults","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_mc_resuscitation_threshold_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[214,282],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,79],"fullStemEn":"A facility protocol states that adults with deep partial- or full-thickness burns involving 20% TBSA or more should have formal IV burn-fluid resuscitation initiated while urine output and perfusion are monitored. Based on the shaded burn diagram, which action matches the protocol?","fullStemZh":"某机构方案规定：成人深二度或三度烧伤面积达到或超过20% TBSA时，应开始正式的静脉烧伤补液复苏，并监测尿量和灌注。根据阴影烧伤示意图，哪项措施符合该方案？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the shaded burn diagram, which action matches the protocol?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据阴影烧伤示意图，哪项措施符合该方案？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A facility protocol states that adults with deep partial- or full-thickness burns involving 20% TBSA or more should have formal IV burn-fluid resuscitation initiated while urine output and perfusion are monitored.","penultimateSentenceZh":"某机构方案规定：成人深二度或三度烧伤面积达到或超过20% TBSA时，应开始正式的静脉烧伤补液复苏，并监测尿量和灌注。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Initiate formal IV burn-fluid resuscitation and monitor response.","zh":"开始正式的静脉烧伤补液复苏并监测反应。"},{"id":"C","en":"Delay fluid planning until the burns are remeasured with a pediatric chart.","zh":"推迟补液计划，直到使用儿童图表重新测量烧伤面积。"},{"id":"B","en":"Treat the burns as below the protocol threshold and provide oral fluids only.","zh":"按低于方案阈值处理，仅给予口服液体。"},{"id":"D","en":"Exclude the anterior leg burn because extremity burns are not counted in TBSA.","zh":"排除下肢前侧烧伤，因为四肢烧伤不计入TBSA。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the anterior trunk (18%) and anterior left leg (9%), for a total of 27% TBSA. This meets the stated protocol threshold of 20% TBSA or more, so formal IV burn-fluid resuscitation with monitoring is appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为躯干前侧（18%）和左下肢前侧（9%），合计27% TBSA。该数值达到题干所述20% TBSA或以上的方案阈值，因此应进行正式静脉烧伤补液复苏并监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a protocol threshold is stated in the stem, first calculate the visual value, then compare it directly with the stated cutoff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干给出方案阈值时，先计算图示数值，再直接与该截止值比较。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; NCBI StatPearls Parkland Formula","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":3,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_fib_parkland_total_posterior_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[214,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[88,97],"fullStemEn":"An 80 kg adult has the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA over the first 24 hours), calculate the total fluid volume in milliliters for the first 24 hours. Record the answer as a whole number.","fullStemZh":"一名80 kg成年人有图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤。使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，在最初24小时内给予），计算最初24小时的总补液量（mL）。请以整数记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record the answer as a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请以整数记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA over the first 24 hours), calculate the total fluid volume in milliliters for the first 24 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，在最初24小时内给予），计算最初24小时的总补液量（mL）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL in first 24 hours","zh":"最初24小时毫升数"},"acceptable":["10080","10,080"],"numeric":{"value":10080,"unit":"mL","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the posterior trunk (18%), posterior left leg (9%), and posterior right arm (4.5%), totaling 31.5% TBSA. Parkland total = 4 × 80 × 31.5 = 10,080 mL in the first 24 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为躯干后侧（18%）、左下肢后侧（9%）和右上肢后侧（4.5%），合计31.5% TBSA。Parkland总量 = 4 × 80 × 31.5 = 10,080 mL，用于最初24小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Keep 31.5 as 31.5, not 32. Rounding the TBSA before the formula can change a strict keyed calculation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将31.5保留为31.5，不要先四舍五入为32。先对TBSA取整可能改变严格计分的计算答案。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; NCBI StatPearls Parkland Formula","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":4,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_fib_parkland_rate_arm_trunk_genitalia_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[243,279],"terminalOffsetsZh":[96,105],"fullStemEn":"A 60 kg adult is admitted with the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half of the total volume infused over the first 8 hours), calculate the first-8-hour infusion rate in mL/hr. Record the answer as a whole number.","fullStemZh":"一名60 kg成年人因图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤入院。使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，总量的一半在最初8小时内输注），计算最初8小时的输液速率（mL/hr）。请以整数记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record the answer as a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请以整数记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half of the total volume infused over the first 8 hours), calculate the first-8-hour infusion rate in mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，总量的一半在最初8小时内输注），计算最初8小时的输液速率（mL/hr）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/hr"},"acceptable":["420","420 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":420,"unit":"mL/hr","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Shaded regions: anterior trunk (18%) + entire left arm (4.5% anterior + 4.5% posterior) + genitalia (1%) = 28% TBSA. Parkland total = 4 × 60 × 28 = 6,720 mL. Half is 3,360 mL over the first 8 hours: 3,360 ÷ 8 = 420 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域：躯干前侧（18%）+ 整个左上肢（前侧4.5% + 后侧4.5%）+ 会阴/生殖器（1%）= 28% TBSA。Parkland总量 = 4 × 60 × 28 = 6,720 mL。一半为3,360 mL，在最初8小时内输注：3,360 ÷ 8 = 420 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For first-8-hour rate questions, do not stop at the total. Parkland asks for half of the total over the first 8 hours.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到最初8小时速率题时，不要停在总量。Parkland要求最初8小时给予总量的一半。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; NCBI StatPearls Parkland Formula","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":5,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_matrix_parkland_values_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[252,320],"terminalOffsetsZh":[98,116],"fullStemEn":"A nurse checks another nurse's burn-resuscitation worksheet for a 72 kg adult. The shaded diagram shows the client's deep partial- and full-thickness burns. The worksheet uses the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half over the first 8 hours). For each worksheet entry, select whether it is correct or incorrect.","fullStemZh":"护士核对另一名护士为一名72 kg成年患者填写的烧伤补液复苏计算表。图中阴影显示患者的深二度及三度烧伤。该计算表使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，最初8小时给予一半）。请判断每个计算表条目是正确还是错误。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each worksheet entry, select whether it is correct or incorrect.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每个计算表条目是正确还是错误。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The worksheet uses the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half over the first 8 hours).","penultimateSentenceZh":"该计算表使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，最初8小时给予一半）。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"TBSA: 31.5%","zh":"TBSA：31.5%"},{"id":"r2","en":"Total Parkland volume: 9,072 mL","zh":"Parkland总量：9,072 mL"},{"id":"r3","en":"First-8-hour volume: 4,536 mL","zh":"最初8小时补液量：4,536 mL"},{"id":"r4","en":"First-8-hour rate: 454 mL/hr","zh":"最初8小时速率：454 mL/hr"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Correct","zh":"正确"},{"id":"c2","en":"Incorrect","zh":"错误"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the whole head (9%), posterior trunk (18%), and anterior right arm (4.5%) = 31.5% TBSA. Total Parkland volume = 4 × 72 × 31.5 = 9,072 mL. Half is 4,536 mL over the first 8 hours. The first-8-hour rate is 4,536 ÷ 8 = 567 mL/hr, so 454 mL/hr is incorrect.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为整个头部（9%）、躯干后侧（18%）和右上肢前侧（4.5%）= 31.5% TBSA。Parkland总量 = 4 × 72 × 31.5 = 9,072 mL。一半为4,536 mL，在最初8小时内输注。最初8小时速率为 4,536 ÷ 8 = 567 mL/hr，因此454 mL/hr错误。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In matrix calculations, verify each row independently. One correct worksheet value does not make the next row correct.","testTakingStrategyZh":"矩阵计算题要逐行独立核对。一个计算表数值正确并不代表下一行也正确。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; NCBI StatPearls Parkland Formula","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":6,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_sata_parkland_chain_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[76,84],"fullStemEn":"A 90 kg adult has the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half over the first 8 hours), which statements are correct? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名90 kg成年人有图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤。使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，最初8小时给予一半），哪些说法正确？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half over the first 8 hours), which statements are correct?","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，最初8小时给予一半），哪些说法正确？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"The first-8-hour rate rounds to 709 mL/hr.","zh":"最初8小时速率四舍五入为709 mL/hr。"},{"id":"C","en":"The first-8-hour volume is 5,670 mL.","zh":"最初8小时补液量为5,670 mL。"},{"id":"B","en":"The total Parkland volume is 11,340 mL.","zh":"Parkland总量为11,340 mL。"},{"id":"E","en":"The burn size is 22.5% TBSA.","zh":"烧伤面积为22.5% TBSA。"},{"id":"A","en":"The burn size is 31.5% TBSA.","zh":"烧伤面积为31.5% TBSA。"},{"id":"F","en":"The first-8-hour volume is 11,340 mL.","zh":"最初8小时补液量为11,340 mL。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the anterior trunk (18%), anterior head (4.5%), anterior left arm (4.5%), and anterior right arm (4.5%) = 31.5% TBSA. Total Parkland volume = 4 × 90 × 31.5 = 11,340 mL. Half over the first 8 hours is 5,670 mL. The rate is 5,670 ÷ 8 = 708.75 mL/hr, which rounds to 709 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为躯干前侧（18%）、头部前侧（4.5%）、左上肢前侧（4.5%）和右上肢前侧（4.5%）= 31.5% TBSA。Parkland总量 = 4 × 90 × 31.5 = 11,340 mL。最初8小时给予一半，即5,670 mL。速率为 5,670 ÷ 8 = 708.75 mL/hr，四舍五入为709 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For select-all calculation chains, separate the chain into TBSA, total volume, first-half volume, and hourly rate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择所有适用的计算链题时，将计算拆成TBSA、总量、前一半补液量和每小时速率。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; NCBI StatPearls Parkland Formula","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":7,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_mc_posterior_tbsa_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,37],"fullStemEn":"An adult client has the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns on the diagram. What burn size should the nurse document?","fullStemZh":"一名成年患者有图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤。护士应记录的烧伤面积是多少？","terminalSentenceEn":"What burn size should the nurse document?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录的烧伤面积是多少？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An adult client has the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns on the diagram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名成年患者有图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"36% TBSA","zh":"36% TBSA"},{"id":"B","en":"27% TBSA","zh":"27% TBSA"},{"id":"A","en":"18% TBSA","zh":"18% TBSA"},{"id":"D","en":"45% TBSA","zh":"45% TBSA"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the posterior trunk (18%), posterior left leg (9%), and posterior right leg (9%). The total is 18 + 9 + 9 = 36% TBSA.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为躯干后侧（18%）、左下肢后侧（9%）和右下肢后侧（9%）。合计为 18 + 9 + 9 = 36% TBSA。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Posterior and anterior surfaces are separate. Count only the visible shaded surface named in the visual.","testTakingStrategyZh":"后侧和前侧表面是分开计算的。只计算图示中被阴影标出的表面。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; Minnesota Department of Health Rule of Nines Adults","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":8,"bankPath":"banks/burn-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5244b8d37daa49adbd1fbed7991f4ede52ded8ce710e26821841ef5e2ce3719f","topLevelQuestionId":"burn_fib_parkland_first8h_leg_arm_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,272],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,95],"fullStemEn":"A 75 kg adult has the shaded deep partial- and full-thickness burns. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half of the total volume given in the first 8 hours), how many milliliters should be infused in the first 8 hours? Record the answer as a whole number.","fullStemZh":"一名75 kg成年人有图中阴影所示的深二度及三度烧伤。使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，总量的一半在最初8小时给予），最初8小时应输注多少毫升？请以整数记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record the answer as a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请以整数记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL × kg × %TBSA, with half of the total volume given in the first 8 hours), how many milliliters should be infused in the first 8 hours?","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用Parkland公式（4 mL × kg × %TBSA，总量的一半在最初8小时给予），最初8小时应输注多少毫升？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL in first 8 hours","zh":"最初8小时毫升数"},"acceptable":["3375","3,375"],"numeric":{"value":3375,"unit":"mL","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the entire left leg (9% anterior + 9% posterior = 18%) and anterior right arm (4.5%), totaling 22.5% TBSA. Parkland total = 4 × 75 × 22.5 = 6,750 mL. Half is given in the first 8 hours: 6,750 ÷ 2 = 3,375 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为整个左下肢（前侧9% + 后侧9% = 18%）和右上肢前侧（4.5%），合计22.5% TBSA。Parkland总量 = 4 × 75 × 22.5 = 6,750 mL。最初8小时给予一半：6,750 ÷ 2 = 3,375 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read the unit carefully: mL for the first 8 hours is a volume; mL/hr would require one more step.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细看单位：最初8小时的mL是总量；若是mL/hr则还需要再做一步计算。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Rule of Nines; NCBI StatPearls Parkland Formula","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":9,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,66],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who presents with severe shortness of breath. The continuous end-tidal CO2 (EtCO2) monitor displays the following capnogram. Which of the following conditions is most consistent with this finding?","fullStemZh":"护士正在照顾一名表现为严重呼吸短促的患者。持续呼气末二氧化碳（EtCO2）监护仪显示以下二氧化碳波形图。下列哪种情况与此发现最相符？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following conditions is most consistent with this finding?","terminalSentenceZh":"下列哪种情况与此发现最相符？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The continuous end-tidal CO2 (EtCO2) monitor displays the following capnogram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"持续呼气末二氧化碳（EtCO2）监护仪显示以下二氧化碳波形图。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Acute asthma exacerbation","zh":"急性哮喘发作"},{"id":"D","en":"Pulmonary edema","zh":"肺水肿"},{"id":"A","en":"Pneumothorax","zh":"气胸"},{"id":"C","en":"Hyperventilation syndrome","zh":"过度换气综合征"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The capnogram shows a 'shark-fin' morphology, characterized by a sloped Phase II upstroke and loss of the flat Phase III alveolar plateau. This indicates delayed emptying of alveoli due to bronchospasm, which is a hallmark of an acute asthma exacerbation. Other conditions like pulmonary edema typically produce a crisp, upright rectangular waveform.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二氧化碳波形图显示了“鲨鱼鳍”形态，其特征是倾斜的第二阶段上升支和缺失平坦的第三阶段肺泡平台。这表明由于支气管痉挛导致肺泡排空延迟，这是急性哮喘发作的标志。其他情况（如肺水肿）通常会产生清晰、直立的矩形波形。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate a 'shark-fin' capnogram with obstructive airway diseases like asthma or COPD.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“鲨鱼鳍”二氧化碳波形与阻塞性气道疾病（如哮喘或慢性阻塞性肺疾病）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":"LITFL - Capnography","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":10,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[260,300],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,79],"fullStemEn":"Immediately after endotracheal intubation of a client with absent spontaneous respirations, the nurse connects the capnography sensor. The monitor displays the following waveform. The nurse auscultates gurgling over the epigastrium and observes no chest rise. Which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"在对无自主呼吸的患者进行气管插管后，护士立即连接二氧化碳监测传感器。监护仪显示以下波形。护士听诊上腹部有咕噜声，且未观察到胸廓起伏。护士下一步应采取什么行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士下一步应采取什么行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse auscultates gurgling over the epigastrium and observes no chest rise.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士听诊上腹部有咕噜声，且未观察到胸廓起伏。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Suction the endotracheal tube to clear secretions.","zh":"通过气管插管吸痰以清除分泌物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Secure the endotracheal tube and request a chest x-ray.","zh":"固定气管插管并要求进行胸部X线检查。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove the endotracheal tube and ventilate with a bag-valve-mask.","zh":"拔除气管插管并使用球囊面罩通气。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer an additional dose of a paralytic agent.","zh":"给予额外剂量的肌肉松弛剂。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The capnogram shows a completely flat waveform (EtCO2 = 0) immediately after intubation. Combined with the clinical signs of epigastric gurgling and absent chest rise, this indicates esophageal intubation. The tube must be removed immediately, and the client must be oxygenated with a bag-valve-mask before reattempting intubation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"插管后二氧化碳波形图立即显示完全平坦的波形（EtCO2 = 0）。结合上腹部咕噜声和无胸廓起伏的临床体征，这表明插管进入了食管。必须立即拔除插管，并在再次尝试插管前使用球囊面罩为患者供氧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A flat capnogram immediately post-intubation indicates the tube is not in the trachea.","testTakingStrategyZh":"插管后立即出现平坦的二氧化碳波形表明导管不在气管内。","sourceMetadata":"AHA CPR Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":11,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[230,284],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,75],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is participating in the resuscitation of a client in cardiac arrest. The client is intubated, and high-quality chest compressions are ongoing. The nurse observes the following change on the continuous capnography monitor. Which interpretation of this finding is most accurate?","fullStemZh":"一名护士正在参与心脏骤停患者的复苏。患者已气管插管，正在进行高质量的胸外按压。护士在持续二氧化碳监护仪上观察到以下变化。对这一发现最准确的解释是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation of this finding is most accurate?","terminalSentenceZh":"对这一发现最准确的解释是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes the following change on the continuous capnography monitor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在持续二氧化碳监护仪上观察到以下变化。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The client has achieved return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC).","zh":"患者已实现自主循环恢复（ROSC）。"},{"id":"D","en":"The endotracheal tube has become disconnected.","zh":"气管插管已断开连接。"},{"id":"A","en":"Chest compression depth has become inadequate.","zh":"胸外按压深度变得不足。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client has developed a tension pneumothorax.","zh":"患者发生了张力性气胸。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An abrupt, sustained increase in EtCO2 (typically > 40 mmHg) during CPR is a primary indicator of Return of Spontaneous Circulation (ROSC). The capnogram shows a 'step-up' from a low-amplitude trace generated by compressions to a much higher amplitude, signifying the heart is pumping CO2-rich blood to the lungs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心肺复苏期间EtCO2突然持续增加（通常> 40 mmHg）是自主循环恢复（ROSC）的主要指标。波形图显示从按压产生的低振幅轨迹“跃升”到高得多的振幅，表明心脏正在将富含二氧化碳的血液泵入肺部。","testTakingStrategyEn":"During CPR, a sudden spike in EtCO2 means blood flow has suddenly improved, indicating ROSC.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在心肺复苏期间，EtCO2的突然飙升意味着血流突然改善，表明自主循环恢复。","sourceMetadata":"AHA CPR Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":12,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,49],"fullStemEn":"A client is under general anesthesia. The nurse anesthetist notes the following capnography tracing. Which of the following is the most likely cause of this abnormal finding?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受全身麻醉。麻醉护士注意到以下的二氧化碳波形图。下列哪项是这一异常发现最可能的原因？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following is the most likely cause of this abnormal finding?","terminalSentenceZh":"下列哪项是这一异常发现最可能的原因？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse anesthetist notes the following capnography tracing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"麻醉护士注意到以下的二氧化碳波形图。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Accidental extubation","zh":"意外拔管"},{"id":"A","en":"Complete airway obstruction","zh":"完全性气道梗阻"},{"id":"C","en":"Esophageal intubation","zh":"食管插管"},{"id":"B","en":"Exhausted soda lime in the anesthesia circuit","zh":"麻醉回路中的钠石灰已耗尽"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The capnogram shows a 'rebreathing' pattern, where the inspiratory baseline fails to return to zero. This indicates the client is rebreathing exhaled carbon dioxide. Common causes in a closed anesthesia circuit include exhausted soda lime (CO2 absorbent) or a faulty expiratory valve.","rationaleCorrectZh":"波形图显示了“重复呼吸”模式，其吸气基线未能回落至零。这表明患者正在重复吸入呼出的二氧化碳。在闭合麻醉回路中，常见原因包括钠石灰（二氧化碳吸收剂）耗尽或呼气阀发生故障。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Notice that the lowest point of the waveform (the baseline) does not touch the bottom zero line. This means CO2 is present during inspiration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"注意波形的最低点（基线）没有接触底部的零线。这意味着吸气时存在CO2。","sourceMetadata":"LITFL - Capnography","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":13,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[145,243],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,74],"fullStemEn":"A client presents to the emergency department with severe dyspnea, orthopnea, and pink frothy sputum. The nurse obtains the following capnogram. Based on the client's presentation and the capnogram, what is the most appropriate interpretation?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因严重呼吸困难、端坐呼吸和咳粉红色泡沫痰来到急诊室。护士获得了以下的二氧化碳波形图。基于患者的临床表现和二氧化碳波形图，最合适的解释是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the client's presentation and the capnogram, what is the most appropriate interpretation?","terminalSentenceZh":"基于患者的临床表现和二氧化碳波形图，最合适的解释是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse obtains the following capnogram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士获得了以下的二氧化碳波形图。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The crisp rectangular waveform confirms an absence of severe lower airway bronchospasm.","zh":"清晰的矩形波形证实不存在严重的下气道支气管痉挛。"},{"id":"C","en":"The capnogram indicates the endotracheal tube is misplaced in the esophagus.","zh":"二氧化碳波形图表明气管插管错位在食管中。"},{"id":"D","en":"The patient is experiencing acute hyperventilation syndrome.","zh":"患者正在经历急性过度换气综合征。"},{"id":"A","en":"The waveform shape suggests the primary issue is a severe asthma exacerbation.","zh":"波形形状提示主要问题是严重的哮喘发作。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The capnogram displays a 'normal' morphology (crisp upright waveform with a flat alveolar plateau), despite the patient's severe respiratory distress from pulmonary edema (indicated by orthopnea and pink frothy sputum). A crisp waveform means there is no significant bronchospasm. Asthma or COPD would cause a sloped 'shark-fin' waveform.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管患者因肺水肿（以端坐呼吸和粉红色泡沫痰为标志）而出现严重的呼吸窘迫，但二氧化碳波形图显示了“正常”的形态（清晰直立的波形，带有平坦的肺泡平台）。清晰的波形意味着不存在明显的支气管痉挛。哮喘或慢性阻塞性肺疾病会导致倾斜的“鲨鱼鳍”波形。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that a normal rectangular capnogram rules out bronchospasm (like asthma). The patient's symptoms point to heart failure/pulmonary edema.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到正常的矩形二氧化碳波形排除了支气管痉挛（如哮喘）。患者的症状指向心力衰竭/肺水肿。","sourceMetadata":"NUEM - Capnography in the ED","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":14,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[169,245],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,61],"fullStemEn":"A young adult client presents with acute anxiety, numbness in the fingers, and rapid breathing. The nurse connects an EtCO2 monitor and observes the following waveform. Which of the following conditions is most consistent with this presentation?","fullStemZh":"一名年轻成年患者出现急性焦虑、手指麻木和呼吸急促。护士连接了EtCO2监护仪并观察到以下波形。下列哪种情况与此表现最一致？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following conditions is most consistent with this presentation?","terminalSentenceZh":"下列哪种情况与此表现最一致？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse connects an EtCO2 monitor and observes the following waveform.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士连接了EtCO2监护仪并观察到以下波形。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Acute severe asthma","zh":"急性重症哮喘"},{"id":"D","en":"Pulmonary embolism","zh":"肺栓塞"},{"id":"B","en":"Hyperventilation syndrome","zh":"过度换气综合征"},{"id":"A","en":"Opiate overdose","zh":"阿片类药物过量"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The capnogram shows a fast respiratory rate with a crisp, rectangular morphology and a low EtCO2 value. This lack of bronchospasm (crisp waveform) combined with the low EtCO2 (blowing off carbon dioxide) is classic for hyperventilation syndrome.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二氧化碳波形图显示呼吸频率快，具有清晰的矩形形态且EtCO2值低。缺乏支气管痉挛（波形清晰）加上低EtCO2（排出过多的二氧化碳），这是过度换气综合征的经典表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look at the shape first. It is rectangular, meaning no airway obstruction. Then look at the rate (fast) and EtCO2 number (low). This equals hyperventilation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先看形状。它是矩形的，意味着没有气道梗阻。然后看频率（快）和EtCO2数值（低）。这等于过度换气。","sourceMetadata":"NUEM - Capnography","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":15,"bankPath":"banks/capnography-canonical.json","bankSha256":"36d72a89405fe4400f27b3b8969cdbe1c51f3217151f8b2592b7f877d636f20c","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,64],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving an intravenous antibiotic suddenly develops facial swelling, tachycardia, and respiratory distress. The continuous capnogram changes to the pattern shown. Which medication should the nurse administer first?","fullStemZh":"一名正在接受静脉抗生素治疗的患者突然出现面部肿胀、心动过速和呼吸窘迫。持续的二氧化碳波形图变为所示模式。护士应首先给予哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse administer first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先给予哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The continuous capnogram changes to the pattern shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"持续的二氧化碳波形图变为所示模式。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Albuterol via nebulizer","zh":"通过雾化器吸入沙丁胺醇"},{"id":"B","en":"Methylprednisolone intravenously","zh":"静脉注射甲泼尼龙"},{"id":"D","en":"Diphenhydramine intravenously","zh":"静脉注射苯海拉明"},{"id":"C","en":"Epinephrine intramuscularly","zh":"肌内注射肾上腺素"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient is experiencing anaphylaxis (facial swelling, tachycardia). The capnogram shows a 'shark-fin' pattern, confirming severe bronchospasm. The first-line and life-saving medication for anaphylaxis with airway compromise is intramuscular epinephrine.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在经历过敏性休克（面部肿胀、心动过速）。波形图显示了“鲨鱼鳍”模式，证实了严重的支气管痉挛。治疗伴有气道受损的过敏性休克的一线抢救药物是肌内注射肾上腺素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The combination of allergen exposure, facial swelling, and bronchospasm (shark-fin capnogram) equals anaphylaxis. Always give epinephrine first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"接触过敏原、面部肿胀和支气管痉挛（鲨鱼鳍波形图）的组合等于过敏性休克。始终首先给予肾上腺素。","sourceMetadata":"Resuscitation Council UK Anaphylaxis Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":16,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_acute_mi_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,56],"fullStemEn":"A client reports sudden crushing substernal chest pain rated 9 out of 10, radiating to the left arm, with diaphoresis and nausea for the past 20 minutes. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一位患者报告突发挤压性胸骨后胸痛，评分9/10，向左臂放射，伴出汗和恶心，持续20分钟。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client reports sudden crushing substernal chest pain rated 9 out of 10, radiating to the left arm, with diaphoresis and nausea for the past 20 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者报告突发挤压性胸骨后胸痛，评分9/10，向左臂放射，伴出汗和恶心，持续20分钟。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer nitroglycerin 0.4 mg sublingually without further assessment.","zh":"不做进一步评估，直接舌下含服硝酸甘油0.4毫克。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assist the client to walk to the cardiac monitoring unit.","zh":"协助患者步行前往心脏监护室。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer supplemental oxygen at 4 L/min via nasal cannula.","zh":"经鼻导管以4升/分钟给予补充氧气。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain a 12-lead ECG and notify the provider immediately.","zh":"立即行12导联心电图并通知医护提供者。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority in suspected acute MI is obtaining a 12-lead ECG to confirm ischemia and immediately notifying the provider so time-sensitive reperfusion therapy can be initiated. Current guidelines recommend supplemental oxygen only if SpO2 falls below 90%.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似急性心肌梗死的优先措施是行12导联心电图确认缺血，并立即通知医护提供者以启动时间敏感的再灌注治疗。目前指南仅在SpO2低于90%时才推荐补充给氧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For suspected MI, assess and confirm first (ECG), then treat. Avoid actions that assume diagnosis without diagnostic confirmation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"疑似心肌梗死时，先评估确认（心电图），再治疗。避免未经确认诊断就进行假设性处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":17,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_hf_discharge_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[149,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client with heart failure which signs and symptoms to report to the provider immediately. Which findings should be included? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教一位心力衰竭患者哪些症状和体征需要立即向医护提供者报告。应包括哪些发现？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"应包括哪些发现？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Need to sleep with extra pillows to breathe comfortably.","zh":"需要用额外枕头才能舒适呼吸（端坐呼吸）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Occasional mild heartburn after a large meal.","zh":"大餐后偶尔出现轻度胃灼热。"},{"id":"F","en":"Mild fatigue in the afternoon that resolves fully with a short rest.","zh":"午后轻度疲劳，短暂休息后完全缓解。"},{"id":"D","en":"Resting heart rate consistently greater than 100 beats per minute.","zh":"静息心率持续超过100次/分。"},{"id":"E","en":"New or worsening swelling in the feet and ankles that does not improve with leg elevation.","zh":"足踝新出现或加重的水肿，抬高腿部后不缓解。"},{"id":"A","en":"Weight gain of 2 or more pounds in a 24-hour period.","zh":"24小时内体重增加2磅（约0.9公斤）或以上。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rapid weight gain reflects fluid retention, orthopnea indicates worsening pulmonary congestion, tachycardia at rest may signal decompensation, and persistent dependent edema signals fluid overload — all require prompt provider notification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"快速体重增加反映液体潴留，端坐呼吸表明肺淤血加重，静息心动过速可能预示失代偿，持续依赖性水肿提示体液过多，均需及时通知医护提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge teaching, distinguish acute changes from baseline discomforts. Sudden weight gain, orthopnea, and persistent edema are red flags for HF.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出院教育题应区分急性变化与基线不适。突然体重增加、端坐呼吸和持续水肿是心衰红旗症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":18,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_dabigatran_teaching_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,33],"fullStemEn":"A client with atrial fibrillation is newly prescribed dabigatran. Which statement by the client indicates a need for further teaching?","fullStemZh":"一位心房颤动患者新开具了达比加群。患者哪项陈述表明需要进一步指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the client indicates a need for further teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者哪项陈述表明需要进一步指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with atrial fibrillation is newly prescribed dabigatran.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位心房颤动患者新开具了达比加群。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"\"I must not stop this medication without talking to my provider first.\"","zh":"\"我不能在未与医护提供者沟通前停药。\""},{"id":"D","en":"\"I can take this medication with or without food.\"","zh":"\"我可以随餐或空腹服用这种药物。\""},{"id":"B","en":"\"I should report any unusual bruising or blood in my urine.\"","zh":"\"我应该报告任何异常瘀伤或尿血。\""},{"id":"A","en":"\"I will have my INR checked every month to monitor the medication.\"","zh":"\"我每个月会检查INR来监测药物效果。\""}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"INR monitoring is used to adjust warfarin doses. Dabigatran is a direct thrombin inhibitor and does not require routine INR monitoring, making this statement incorrect and in need of correction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"INR监测用于调整华法林剂量。达比加群是直接凝血酶抑制剂，不需要常规INR监测，因此该陈述不正确，需要纠正。","testTakingStrategyEn":"DOACs (dabigatran, rivaroxaban, apixaban) do NOT require routine INR monitoring — that is a warfarin-specific requirement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"直接口服抗凝药（达比加群、利伐沙班、阿哌沙班）不需要常规INR监测——这是华法林特有的要求。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":19,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_fib_dopamine_drip_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,77],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes dopamine 5 mcg/kg/min for a client weighing 80 kg. The IV bag contains dopamine 400 mg in 250 mL D5W. At how many mL/hr should the nurse set the infusion pump?","fullStemZh":"医护提供者为一位体重80公斤的患者开具多巴胺5 mcg/kg/分钟。输液袋含多巴胺400毫克溶于250毫升5%葡萄糖水。护士应将输液泵设为多少mL/小时？","terminalSentenceEn":"At how many mL/hr should the nurse set the infusion pump?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将输液泵设为多少mL/小时？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The IV bag contains dopamine 400 mg in 250 mL D5W.","penultimateSentenceZh":"输液袋含多巴胺400毫克溶于250毫升5%葡萄糖水。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Enter mL/hr.","zh":"输入mL/小时。"},"acceptable":["15","15 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":15,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1 — Concentration: 400 mg / 250 mL = 1.6 mg/mL = 1,600 mcg/mL. Step 2 — Dose needed: 5 mcg/kg/min × 80 kg = 400 mcg/min. Step 3 — Rate: 400 mcg/min ÷ 1,600 mcg/mL = 0.25 mL/min × 60 = 15 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第1步—浓度：400 mg ÷ 250 mL = 1.6 mg/mL = 1,600 mcg/mL。第2步—所需剂量：5 mcg/kg/分 × 80 kg = 400 mcg/分。第3步—速率：400 mcg/分 ÷ 1,600 mcg/mL = 0.25 mL/分 × 60 = 15 mL/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For weight-based infusions: find concentration (mg or mcg per mL), calculate dose per minute using weight, then convert to mL/hr.","testTakingStrategyZh":"体重给药输注计算：先求浓度（mg或mcg/mL），用体重计算每分钟剂量，再换算为mL/小时。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":20,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_matrix_asthma_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,46],"fullStemEn":"A client with asthma is being treated in the emergency department. For each finding, select whether it is an expected response to treatment or requires immediate follow-up.","fullStemZh":"一位哮喘患者正在急诊室接受治疗。对于每项发现，请选择其属于对治疗的预期反应还是需要立即跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is an expected response to treatment or requires immediate follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请选择其属于对治疗的预期反应还是需要立即跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with asthma is being treated in the emergency department.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位哮喘患者正在急诊室接受治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Mild expiratory wheeze present during the first 15 minutes of assessment.","zh":"评估最初15分钟内存在轻度呼气性哮鸣音。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Respiratory rate 32/min with no improvement after two albuterol treatments.","zh":"经两次沙丁胺醇治疗后，呼吸频率32次/分且无改善。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Oxygen saturation 96% on room air after 30 minutes of treatment.","zh":"治疗30分钟后，室内空气下血氧饱和度96%。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Client unable to speak in complete sentences due to breathlessness.","zh":"患者因气短无法说完整句子。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Mild hand tremor and heart rate increase after albuterol administration.","zh":"使用沙丁胺醇后出现轻度手颤和心率加快。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected response to treatment","zh":"对治疗的预期反应"},{"id":"c2","en":"Requires immediate follow-up","zh":"需要立即跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Initial wheeze, improving saturation, and albuterol-related tremor/tachycardia are expected. Persistent tachypnea unresponsive to two bronchodilator treatments and inability to speak in full sentences signal severe exacerbation requiring escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"初始哮鸣音、血氧饱和度改善以及沙丁胺醇引起的震颤/心动过速是预期表现。两次支气管扩张剂治疗后呼吸急促持续不缓解及无法说完整句子提示严重发作，需要升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In asthma, inability to speak, no bronchodilator response, and persistent tachypnea are danger signs; mild tremor after albuterol is expected.","testTakingStrategyZh":"哮喘中，无法说话、支气管扩张剂无反应和持续呼吸急促是危险信号；沙丁胺醇后轻度震颤是预期的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":21,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_oxygen_device_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,43],"fullStemEn":"A client with COPD requires supplemental oxygen. The provider prescribes a precise oxygen concentration of 28%. Which oxygen delivery device should the nurse select?","fullStemZh":"一位COPD患者需要补充氧气。医护提供者开具精确氧浓度28%。护士应选择哪种给氧装置？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which oxygen delivery device should the nurse select?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应选择哪种给氧装置？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider prescribes a precise oxygen concentration of 28%.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医护提供者开具精确氧浓度28%。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Nonrebreather mask","zh":"非重复呼吸面罩"},{"id":"C","en":"Venturi mask","zh":"文丘里面罩"},{"id":"B","en":"Simple face mask","zh":"简单面罩"},{"id":"A","en":"Nasal cannula at 6 L/min","zh":"6升/分钟鼻导管"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Venturi mask delivers a precise, fixed fraction of inspired oxygen regardless of the client's respiratory pattern. This is especially important in COPD, where excessive oxygen can blunt the hypoxic drive in some clients.","rationaleCorrectZh":"文丘里面罩无论患者呼吸模式如何，都能提供精确固定的吸入氧浓度。这在COPD患者中尤为重要，因为过高的氧浓度可能抑制部分患者的低氧驱动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When precision matters (especially in COPD), the Venturi mask is the answer. Match the device to the clinical need for controlled FiO2.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当精确度重要时（尤其是COPD），文丘里面罩是答案。将装置与控制FiO2的临床需求相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":22,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_tracheostomy_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,39],"fullStemEn":"A client has a tracheostomy in place. Which nursing actions are appropriate when performing tracheostomy care? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位患者已行气管造口术。进行气管造口护理时，哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate when performing tracheostomy care?","penultimateSentenceZh":"进行气管造口护理时，哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Place a split gauze dressing around the tracheostomy site after cleaning.","zh":"清洁后在气管造口处放置剪开的纱布敷料。"},{"id":"C","en":"Suction the airway before beginning tracheostomy care if secretions are present.","zh":"如存在分泌物，在开始气管造口护理前先吸痰。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use sterile technique throughout the care procedure.","zh":"整个护理过程中保持无菌技术。"},{"id":"E","en":"Rinse the inner cannula with sterile normal saline after cleaning.","zh":"清洁后用无菌生理盐水冲洗内套管。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use the same disposable inner cannula for 48 hours before discarding.","zh":"同一个一次性内套管使用48小时后再丢弃。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove both tracheostomy holder ties simultaneously before replacing them.","zh":"同时移除两侧气管造口固定带后再更换。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sterile technique prevents infection, pre-suctioning clears the airway before care, split gauze absorbs secretions without fraying, and rinsing the inner cannula removes cleaning residue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无菌技术预防感染，护理前吸痰清理气道，剪开的纱布吸收分泌物且不产生棉絮，冲洗内套管去除清洁残余。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For tracheostomy care, think infection prevention (sterile) and airway safety (never remove both ties at once).","testTakingStrategyZh":"气管造口护理应想到预防感染（无菌）和气道安全（切勿同时移除两侧固定带）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":23,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_metoprolol_assessment_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"Before administering metoprolol 50 mg by mouth to a client with hypertension, which assessment should the nurse perform first?","fullStemZh":"给高血压患者口服美托洛尔50毫克前，护士首先应进行哪项评估？","terminalSentenceEn":"Before administering metoprolol 50 mg by mouth to a client with hypertension, which assessment should the nurse perform first?","terminalSentenceZh":"给高血压患者口服美托洛尔50毫克前，护士首先应进行哪项评估？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Measure the client's heart rate and blood pressure, then compare them with the prescribed hold parameters.","zh":"测量患者的心率和血压，并与医嘱规定的暂停给药参数进行比较。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's pain level on a 0–10 scale.","zh":"使用0-10量表评估患者疼痛程度。"},{"id":"B","en":"Measure the client's oxygen saturation.","zh":"测量患者血氧饱和度。"},{"id":"C","en":"Review the client's serum cholesterol levels.","zh":"查看患者血清胆固醇水平。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Metoprolol can lower both heart rate and blood pressure. Assess both before administration and follow the patient's prescribed hold and notification parameters. A heart rate below 60/min may be used in a specific order or facility protocol, but it is not a universal hold threshold for every client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"美托洛尔可降低心率和血压。给药前应评估两者，并遵循该患者医嘱规定的暂停给药及通知参数。心率低于60次/分可作为特定医嘱或机构流程中的参数，但并非适用于所有患者的统一暂停给药阈值。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a medication that can lower both heart rate and blood pressure, assess both and compare the findings with patient-specific administration parameters.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于可同时降低心率和血压的药物，给药前应评估两者，并将结果与患者特定的给药参数进行比较。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":24,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_ace_inhibitor_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.8","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.8.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.8.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,58],"fullStemEn":"A client newly prescribed lisinopril reports, \"I've had a dry, persistent cough since I started this medication. Should I be worried?\" Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一位新开具赖诺普利的患者说：\"我自从开始服用这种药后一直有干燥的持续性咳嗽。我应该担心吗？\"护士最恰当的回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最恰当的回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Should I be worried?\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"我应该担心吗？\"","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"\"A dry cough is a common side effect of lisinopril. You should report it to your provider, who may consider switching your medication.\"","zh":"\"干咳是赖诺普利的常见副作用。您应该向医护提供者报告，他们可能会考虑换药。\""},{"id":"C","en":"\"A cough is not related to lisinopril. You probably have a cold.\"","zh":"\"咳嗽与赖诺普利无关。您可能感冒了。\""},{"id":"D","en":"\"Drink extra water each day to suppress the cough while continuing the medication.\"","zh":"\"每天多喝水以抑制咳嗽，同时继续服药。\""},{"id":"A","en":"\"That cough means the medication is not working. Stop taking it right away.\"","zh":"\"这种咳嗽意味着药物没有效果。请立即停药。\""}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A persistent dry cough is a well-known side effect of ACE inhibitors, caused by bradykinin accumulation. The provider should be notified because the client may need to switch to an ARB, which causes the same blood pressure effects without the cough.","rationaleCorrectZh":"持续干咳是ACE抑制剂的已知副作用，由缓激肽积累引起。应通知医护提供者，因为患者可能需要换用ARB类药物，后者具有相同的降压效果但不引起咳嗽。","testTakingStrategyEn":"ACE inhibitor dry cough = bradykinin accumulation = expected side effect, not danger. Notify provider for possible switch to an ARB.","testTakingStrategyZh":"ACE抑制剂干咳=缓激肽积累=预期副作用，不是危险信号。通知医护提供者考虑换用ARB。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":25,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_eps_haloperidol_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.9","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.9.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.9.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[146,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,52],"fullStemEn":"A client taking haloperidol reports muscle stiffness and an inability to remain still. Which findings indicate extrapyramidal side effects (EPS)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位服用氟哌啶醇的患者报告肌肉僵硬和无法保持静止。哪些发现提示锥体外系副作用（EPS）？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings indicate extrapyramidal side effects (EPS)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现提示锥体外系副作用（EPS）？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Shuffling gait and masklike facial expression.","zh":"拖曳步态和面具样表情。"},{"id":"B","en":"Constant restless urge to move; unable to sit still.","zh":"持续的坐立不安冲动；无法静坐。"},{"id":"C","en":"Sudden painful sustained neck muscle contraction causing twisting to one side.","zh":"突发痛苦的持续性颈肌收缩导致头颈向一侧扭转。"},{"id":"A","en":"Involuntary arm and leg muscle rigidity.","zh":"手臂和腿部不自主肌肉僵硬。"},{"id":"F","en":"Elevated mood and pressured speech.","zh":"情绪高涨和急促言语。"},{"id":"D","en":"Dry mouth and urinary retention.","zh":"口干和尿潴留。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"EPS includes drug-induced parkinsonism (rigidity, shuffling gait, masked face), akathisia (restless urge to move), and acute dystonia (sudden muscle contractions causing abnormal postures). These are caused by dopamine D2 blockade in the basal ganglia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"EPS包括药物性帕金森症（僵硬、拖曳步态、面具脸）、静坐不能（不安运动冲动）和急性肌张力障碍（导致异常体位的突发肌肉收缩）。这些由基底节多巴胺D2受体阻断引起。","testTakingStrategyEn":"EPS clusters: dystonia (abnormal postures), akathisia (restlessness), parkinsonism (rigidity, shuffle, mask). Anticholinergic effects are separate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"EPS簇：肌张力障碍（异常体位）、静坐不能（不安）、帕金森症（僵硬、拖步、面具）。抗胆碱能效应是分开的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which findings indicate extrapyramidal side effects (EPS)?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些发现提示锥体外系副作用（EPS）？"}
{"queueIndex":26,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_metformin_contrast_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.10","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.10.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.10.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,42],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes taking metformin is scheduled for a CT scan with IV contrast dye. Which action should the nurse take regarding the metformin?","fullStemZh":"一位服用二甲双胍的2型糖尿病患者计划进行静脉对比剂CT扫描。护士应如何处理二甲双胍？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take regarding the metformin?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何处理二甲双胍？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes taking metformin is scheduled for a CT scan with IV contrast dye.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位服用二甲双胍的2型糖尿病患者计划进行静脉对比剂CT扫描。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Switch the client to insulin permanently before CT scanning.","zh":"CT扫描前将患者永久改为胰岛素治疗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the metformin with a large glass of water 1 hour before the scan.","zh":"检查前1小时用大量水服用二甲双胍。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the metformin as directed before the procedure and for 48 hours after, pending renal function reassessment.","zh":"按指导在检查前暂停二甲双胍，检查后暂停48小时，待肾功能重新评估后再决定。"},{"id":"D","en":"Double the metformin dose the day of the procedure to compensate for potential glucose elevation.","zh":"检查当天将二甲双胍剂量加倍，以补偿潜在血糖升高。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"IV contrast can cause acute kidney injury, which may reduce metformin clearance and increase the risk of lactic acidosis. Metformin is typically held before contrast procedures and withheld for 48 hours afterward until renal function is confirmed stable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"静脉对比剂可导致急性肾损伤，减少二甲双胍清除，增加乳酸酸中毒风险。二甲双胍通常在对比剂检查前暂停，检查后暂停48小时，直到确认肾功能稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Metformin + IV contrast = hold before and 48 hours after due to lactic acidosis risk from impaired renal clearance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"二甲双胍+静脉对比剂=检查前后暂停48小时，因肾脏清除受损导致乳酸酸中毒风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":27,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_or_iv_push_safety_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.11","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.11.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.11.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,29],"fullStemEn":"A nurse prepares to administer an IV push medication. Place the following steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一位护士准备给予静脉推注药物。请将以下步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将以下步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse prepares to administer an IV push medication.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位护士准备给予静脉推注药物。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Draw up the medication in the correct syringe and label it.","zh":"在正确的注射器中抽取药物并标注标签。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify the client using two patient identifiers.","zh":"使用两种患者识别方式核实患者身份。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer the medication at the prescribed rate.","zh":"按医嘱速率给予药物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Compare the medication label to the medication administration record.","zh":"将药物标签与给药记录进行核对。"},{"id":"D","en":"Flush the IV line with a compatible solution after administration.","zh":"给药后用相容溶液冲洗静脉管路。"}],"correct":["C","A","B","E","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe IV push follows the five rights sequence: verify the medication, prepare the dose, confirm the patient identity, administer at the correct rate (E), then flush to clear the line.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全的静脉推注遵循五对给药顺序：核对药物（C）、准备剂量（A）、确认患者身份（B）、按正确速率给药（E）、最后冲管（D）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The safe medication administration sequence: verify (order) → prepare → identify patient → give → flush.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全给药顺序：核对（医嘱）→准备→确认患者→给药→冲管。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":28,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_fib_amoxicillin_pediatric_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.12","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.12.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.12.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,79],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes amoxicillin 40 mg/kg/day PO in divided doses every 8 hours for a child weighing 15 kg. The suspension available is amoxicillin 250 mg/5 mL. How many mL should the nurse administer per dose?","fullStemZh":"医护提供者为一位体重15公斤的儿童开具阿莫西林40 mg/kg/天口服，每8小时分次给药。现有混悬液为阿莫西林250 mg/5 mL。护士每次应给予多少mL？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer per dose?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士每次应给予多少mL？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The suspension available is amoxicillin 250 mg/5 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现有混悬液为阿莫西林250 mg/5 mL。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Enter mL per dose.","zh":"输入每次剂量的mL数。"},"acceptable":["4","4 mL"],"numeric":{"value":4,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1 — Daily dose: 40 mg/kg × 15 kg = 600 mg/day. Step 2 — Per dose (every 8 hours = 3 doses/day): 600 mg ÷ 3 = 200 mg/dose. Step 3 — Volume: 200 mg ÷ (250 mg/5 mL) = 200 × 5 ÷ 250 = 4 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第1步—每日剂量：40 mg/kg × 15 kg = 600 mg/天。第2步—每次剂量（每8小时=每天3次）：600 mg ÷ 3 = 200 mg/次。第3步—体积：200 mg ÷ (250 mg/5 mL) = 200 × 5 ÷ 250 = 4 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pediatric weight-based dosing: calculate total daily dose first, divide by frequency for per-dose amount, then calculate volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"儿科体重给药：先计算每日总剂量，除以给药频率得每次剂量，再计算体积。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":29,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_matrix_anticoagulant_monitoring_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.13","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.13.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.13.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"For each anticoagulant therapy listed, select whether routine laboratory monitoring is indicated or not required.","fullStemZh":"对于以下每种抗凝治疗，选择是否需要常规实验室监测。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each anticoagulant therapy listed, select whether routine laboratory monitoring is indicated or not required.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于以下每种抗凝治疗，选择是否需要常规实验室监测。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Warfarin (vitamin K antagonist) for atrial fibrillation.","zh":"华法林（维生素K拮抗剂）用于心房颤动。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Continuous unfractionated heparin infusion.","zh":"持续普通肝素输注。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Apixaban (direct oral anticoagulant) for stroke prevention.","zh":"阿哌沙班（直接口服抗凝药）用于卒中预防。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Standard prophylactic dose enoxaparin in a non-obese adult.","zh":"非肥胖成人标准预防剂量依诺肝素。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"No routine laboratory monitoring required","zh":"不需要常规实验室监测"},{"id":"c1","en":"Routine laboratory monitoring indicated","zh":"需要常规实验室监测"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warfarin requires INR monitoring for dose adjustment. Unfractionated heparin infusions require aPTT or anti-Xa monitoring. DOACs such as apixaban and standard prophylactic LMWH do not require routine coagulation lab monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林需要INR监测以调整剂量。普通肝素输注需要aPTT或抗Xa监测。直接口服抗凝药（如阿哌沙班）和标准预防剂量低分子肝素不需要常规凝血实验室监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Warfarin = INR monitoring; UFH infusion = aPTT monitoring; DOACs and standard LMWH = no routine monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"华法林=INR监测；普通肝素输注=aPTT监测；直接口服抗凝药和标准低分子肝素=无需常规监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":30,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_thyroid_storm_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.14","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.14.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.14.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,59],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalized client with hyperthyroidism develops a temperature of 104 °F (40 °C), heart rate of 152/min, and extreme agitation. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一位住院的甲状腺功能亢进患者出现体温104 °F (40 °C)、心率152次/分和极度激越。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A hospitalized client with hyperthyroidism develops a temperature of 104 °F (40 °C), heart rate of 152/min, and extreme agitation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位住院的甲状腺功能亢进患者出现体温104 °F (40 °C)、心率152次/分和极度激越。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer levothyroxine as previously scheduled.","zh":"按原计划给予左甲状腺素。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply cooling measures and notify the provider immediately.","zh":"立即采取降温措施并通知医护提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Schedule radioactive iodine therapy for the next available appointment.","zh":"安排下次可用预约时间进行放射性碘治疗。"},{"id":"A","en":"Restrict fluids and encourage the client to rest quietly.","zh":"限制液体并鼓励患者安静休息。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thyroid storm is a life-threatening emergency characterized by extreme hyperthermia, tachycardia, and agitation from massive thyroid hormone excess. Immediate cooling and urgent provider notification are the first steps before specific pharmacological treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺危象是危及生命的急症，由大量甲状腺激素过多引起，表现为极度高热、心动过速和激越。立即降温和紧急通知医护提供者是特异性药物治疗前的首要步骤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Extreme fever + tachycardia in a client with hyperthyroidism = thyroid storm. Treat the emergency (cool, notify) before long-term interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"甲亢患者出现极度高热+心动过速=甲状腺危象。在长期干预前处理急症（降温、通知）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":31,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_addisonian_crisis_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.15","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.15.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.15.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,230],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,56],"fullStemEn":"A client with Addison's disease is brought to the emergency department with profound weakness, hypotension, and nausea after abruptly stopping corticosteroid therapy. Which IV fluid should the nurse anticipate administering first?","fullStemZh":"一位艾迪生病患者突然停用皮质激素治疗后，出现严重虚弱、低血压和恶心，被送至急诊。护士应预期首先给予哪种静脉液体？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which IV fluid should the nurse anticipate administering first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期首先给予哪种静脉液体？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Addison's disease is brought to the emergency department with profound weakness, hypotension, and nausea after abruptly stopping corticosteroid therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位艾迪生病患者突然停用皮质激素治疗后，出现严重虚弱、低血压和恶心，被送至急诊。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hypotonic 0.45% sodium chloride only","zh":"单纯低渗0.45%氯化钠"},{"id":"C","en":"Potassium chloride in 0.45% sodium chloride","zh":"0.45%氯化钠中含氯化钾"},{"id":"D","en":"5% albumin solution","zh":"5%白蛋白溶液"},{"id":"B","en":"0.9% sodium chloride with dextrose (D5NS)","zh":"0.9%氯化钠加葡萄糖（D5NS）"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Addisonian crisis presents with hypovolemia, hyponatremia, and hypoglycemia from glucocorticoid and mineralocorticoid deficiency. D5NS (isotonic saline with dextrose) corrects sodium deficit, volume loss, and low blood glucose simultaneously.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艾迪生危象表现为低血容量、低钠血症和低血糖，由糖皮质激素和盐皮质激素缺乏引起。D5NS（含葡萄糖的等渗盐水）同时纠正钠缺乏、容量丢失和低血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Addisonian crisis = low sodium, low glucose, low volume + high potassium. Choose fluids that address sodium and glucose simultaneously.","testTakingStrategyZh":"艾迪生危象=低钠、低血糖、低容量+高钾。选择同时解决钠和葡萄糖问题的液体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with Addison's disease is brought to the emergency department with profound weakness, hypotension, and nausea after abruptly stopping corticosteroid therapy.","controlSentenceZh":"一位艾迪生病患者突然停用皮质激素治疗后，出现严重虚弱、低血压和恶心，被送至急诊。"}
{"queueIndex":32,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_ckd_diet_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.16","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.16.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.16.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,38],"fullStemEn":"A client with stage 4 chronic kidney disease receives dietary education. Which client statements indicate correct understanding? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位4期慢性肾病患者接受饮食教育。哪些患者陈述表明理解正确？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which client statements indicate correct understanding?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些患者陈述表明理解正确？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"\"I can eat as many phosphate-containing foods as I like.\"","zh":"\"我可以随意吃含磷食物。\""},{"id":"E","en":"\"I will avoid adding extra salt to my food.\"","zh":"\"我会避免在食物中额外加盐。\""},{"id":"B","en":"\"I should add extra protein to my diet each day by eating more meat.\"","zh":"\"我每天应该多吃肉来增加蛋白质摄入。\""},{"id":"F","en":"\"Drinking extra milk every day will protect my bones.\"","zh":"\"每天多喝牛奶可以保护我的骨骼。\""},{"id":"C","en":"\"I will monitor my total daily fluid intake as my provider directs.\"","zh":"\"我将按医护提供者指导监测每日液体总摄入量。\""},{"id":"A","en":"\"I will limit foods high in potassium, such as bananas, potatoes, and orange juice.\"","zh":"\"我会限制富含钾的食物，如香蕉、土豆和橙汁。\""}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In stage 4 CKD, the kidneys cannot adequately excrete potassium, sodium, phosphorus, or fluid. Limiting high-potassium foods, monitoring fluid, and avoiding excess sodium are key dietary strategies.","rationaleCorrectZh":"4期慢性肾病中，肾脏无法充分排泄钾、钠、磷或液体。限制高钾食物、监测液体和避免过多钠是关键饮食策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In CKD, think about what the kidneys cannot excrete: potassium, phosphorus, sodium, and fluid — all must be restricted.","testTakingStrategyZh":"慢性肾病时，想想肾脏无法排泄的物质：钾、磷、钠和液体——均需限制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":33,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_cloze_aki_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.17","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.17.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.17.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,63],"fullStemEn":"A client who underwent major abdominal surgery 24 hours ago has urine output of 20 mL/hr for three consecutive hours, serum creatinine that has risen from 0.9 to 2.4 mg/dL, and is 3 kg heavier than the preoperative weight.","fullStemZh":"一位24小时前接受腹部大手术的患者连续三小时尿量为20毫升/小时，血清肌酐从0.9升至2.4 mg/dL，体重比术前重3公斤。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client who underwent major abdominal surgery 24 hours ago has urine output of 20 mL/hr for three consecutive hours, serum creatinine that has risen from 0.9 to 2.4 mg/dL, and is 3 kg heavier than the preoperative weight.","terminalSentenceZh":"一位24小时前接受腹部大手术的患者连续三小时尿量为20毫升/小时，血清肌酐从0.9升至2.4 mg/dL，体重比术前重3公斤。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize {{1}}, anticipate the provider will order {{2}}, and monitor the client closely for {{3}}.","zh":"护士应识别{{1}}，预期医护提供者将开具{{2}}，并密切监测患者的{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"hepatic failure","zh":"肝功能衰竭"},{"id":"o2","en":"expected postoperative diuresis","zh":"预期的术后利尿"},{"id":"o1","en":"acute kidney injury","zh":"急性肾损伤"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"fluid status assessment and possible diuretic or fluid challenge per protocol","zh":"液体状态评估及可能的按方案利尿剂或液体挑战"},{"id":"o3","en":"immediate discharge with outpatient nephrology follow-up","zh":"立即出院并门诊肾内科随访"},{"id":"o2","en":"a high-protein diet and iron supplementation","zh":"高蛋白饮食和铁补充"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"hyperkalemia and fluid overload","zh":"高钾血症和体液过多"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypernatremia and pulmonary fibrosis","zh":"高钠血症和肺纤维化"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypoglycemia and skin breakdown","zh":"低血糖和皮肤破损"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Oliguria (less than 30 mL/hr), rising creatinine, and postoperative weight gain together indicate acute kidney injury. The provider must assess fluid balance and manage potential complications including hyperkalemia and fluid overload.","rationaleCorrectZh":"少尿（低于30毫升/小时）、肌酐升高和术后体重增加共同提示急性肾损伤。医护提供者必须评估液体平衡并处理潜在并发症，包括高钾血症和体液过多。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Postop oliguria + rising creatinine + weight gain = AKI. Watch for hyperkalemia (cardiac risk) and fluid overload (pulmonary risk).","testTakingStrategyZh":"术后少尿+肌酐升高+体重增加=急性肾损伤。警惕高钾血症（心脏风险）和体液过多（肺部风险）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":34,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_hip_replacement_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.18","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.18.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.18.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,63],"fullStemEn":"A client returns to the unit after a posterior-approach total hip replacement. The surgeon's postoperative orders specify standard posterior hip precautions. Which position should the nurse instruct the client to avoid?","fullStemZh":"一位患者在接受后路入路全髋关节置换术后返回病房。外科医生的术后医嘱规定采用标准后路髋关节预防措施。护士应指导患者避免哪种体位？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which position should the nurse instruct the client to avoid?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应指导患者避免哪种体位？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The surgeon's postoperative orders specify standard posterior hip precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"外科医生的术后医嘱规定采用标准后路髋关节预防措施。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Side-lying on the non-operative side with a pillow between the legs.","zh":"侧卧于非手术侧，两腿之间夹枕头。"},{"id":"A","en":"Supine position with the head of bed elevated 30 degrees.","zh":"仰卧位，床头抬高30度。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hip flexion greater than 90 degrees.","zh":"髋关节屈曲超过90度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Sitting at the edge of the bed with feet flat on the floor.","zh":"坐在床边，双脚平放在地板上。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When standard posterior hip precautions are prescribed, the client should avoid hip flexion greater than 90 degrees, internal rotation, and adduction past the midline because these combined positions can increase dislocation risk. Precautions should follow the surgeon's individualized postoperative orders.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当医嘱规定标准后路髋关节预防措施时，患者应避免髋关节屈曲超过90度、内旋及内收过中线，因为这些组合体位会增加脱位风险。具体预防措施应遵循外科医生的个体化术后医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Hip precautions are approach- and surgeon-specific. When standard posterior precautions are ordered, avoid flexion beyond 90 degrees, internal rotation, and adduction past midline.","testTakingStrategyZh":"髋关节预防措施取决于手术入路和外科医生医嘱。当医嘱规定标准后路预防措施时，应避免屈曲超过90度、内旋及内收过中线。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":35,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_ng_tube_placement_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.19","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.19.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.19.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,33],"fullStemEn":"The nurse inserts a nasogastric tube for a client. Which method is the most reliable for confirming placement before initiating tube feeding?","fullStemZh":"护士为患者置入鼻胃管。在开始管饲前，哪种方法最可靠地确认管路位置？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which method is the most reliable for confirming placement before initiating tube feeding?","terminalSentenceZh":"在开始管饲前，哪种方法最可靠地确认管路位置？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse inserts a nasogastric tube for a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士为患者置入鼻胃管。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Observing whether the tube produces bubbles when submerged in water.","zh":"将管路浸入水中观察是否产生气泡。"},{"id":"C","en":"Measuring the pH of aspirated gastric contents.","zh":"测量抽出的胃内容物pH值。"},{"id":"B","en":"Auscultating the epigastrium while injecting 10 mL of air.","zh":"注射10毫升空气时听诊上腹部。"},{"id":"A","en":"Confirming placement with a radiograph of the chest or abdomen.","zh":"通过胸部或腹部X线平片确认管路位置。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Radiographic confirmation is the gold standard for verifying nasogastric tube placement. It directly visualizes the tube tip and is the only method that can definitively rule out inadvertent pulmonary placement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"X线平片确认是核实鼻胃管位置的金标准。它直接显示管路尖端，是唯一能明确排除意外肺部置入的方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For definitive NG tube confirmation before initiating feeding: radiograph is the gold standard. pH is helpful but not definitive; air auscultation is no longer acceptable alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"开始管饲前确定性鼻胃管确认：X线平片是金标准。pH有帮助但非确定性；单独听诊注气法不再可接受。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":36,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_or_colostomy_care_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.20","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.20.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.20.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,97],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,29],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client to change a colostomy pouch. Place the steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教一位患者更换结肠造口袋。请将步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is teaching a client to change a colostomy pouch.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教一位患者更换结肠造口袋。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Press the new pouch firmly against the skin and hold for 30 to 60 seconds.","zh":"将新造口袋紧压在皮肤上并按压30至60秒。"},{"id":"C","en":"Cut or adjust the wafer opening to the correct stoma size.","zh":"将底盘开口剪切或调整至正确造口尺寸。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove the old pouch and gently clean the peristomal skin.","zh":"取下旧造口袋，温和清洁造口周围皮肤。"},{"id":"A","en":"Measure the stoma to determine the correct opening size.","zh":"测量造口以确定正确的开口尺寸。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply skin barrier paste or powder to protect the peristomal skin if indicated.","zh":"如需要，在造口周围涂抹皮肤保护膏或粉末。"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence is: remove the old pouch and clean the skin, measure the stoma, cut the wafer to size, apply skin barrier protection, then secure the new pouch.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确顺序是：取下旧造口袋并清洁皮肤，测量造口，剪切底盘至合适尺寸，涂抹皮肤屏障保护，然后固定新造口袋。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Ostomy care sequence: remove and clean → measure → cut → protect skin → apply and seal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"造口护理顺序：取下并清洁→测量→剪切→保护皮肤→粘贴并密封。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":37,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_fib_iv_drip_rate_25","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.21","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.21.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.21.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,55],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes 1,000 mL of lactated Ringer's solution to infuse over 8 hours. The IV tubing has a drop factor of 20 drops per mL. How many drops per minute should the nurse count?","fullStemZh":"医护提供者开具乳酸林格液1,000毫升，8小时内输完。静脉输液管滴系数为20滴/毫升。护士应计数每分钟多少滴？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many drops per minute should the nurse count?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应计数每分钟多少滴？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The IV tubing has a drop factor of 20 drops per mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"静脉输液管滴系数为20滴/毫升。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Enter drops per minute (round to nearest whole number).","zh":"输入每分钟滴数（四舍五入至整数）。"},"acceptable":["42","42 gtts/min","42 drops/min"],"numeric":{"value":42,"tolerance":1,"unit":"gtts/min"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Formula: (Volume in mL × Drop factor) ÷ Time in minutes = (1,000 × 20) ÷ (8 × 60) = 20,000 ÷ 480 = 41.67, rounded to 42 drops/min.","rationaleCorrectZh":"公式：（液体量（mL）× 滴系数）÷ 时间（分钟）= (1,000 × 20) ÷ (8 × 60) = 20,000 ÷ 480 = 41.67，四舍五入为42滴/分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Manual drip rate: (mL × drop factor) ÷ total minutes. Always convert hours to minutes before dividing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"手动滴速：（mL × 滴系数）÷ 总分钟数。计算前务必将小时转换为分钟。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":38,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_matrix_wound_assessment_26","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.22","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.22.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.22.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"For each postoperative wound finding, select whether it represents expected healing or requires nurse follow-up.","fullStemZh":"针对每项术后伤口发现，选择其属于预期愈合还是需要护士跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each postoperative wound finding, select whether it represents expected healing or requires nurse follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项术后伤口发现，选择其属于预期愈合还是需要护士跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Small amount of clear serous drainage at the incision site 24 hours after surgery.","zh":"手术24小时后切口处少量清亮浆液性渗出。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Wound edges well-approximated with no separation on postoperative day 3.","zh":"术后第3天伤口边缘对合良好，无裂开。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Purulent yellow drainage with surrounding redness and warmth on postoperative day 5.","zh":"术后第5天脓性黄色渗出，周围皮肤发红发热。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Wound edges separating with visible subcutaneous tissue.","zh":"伤口边缘裂开，可见皮下组织。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Mild bruising around the suture line on postoperative day 1.","zh":"术后第1天缝合线周围轻度瘀斑。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected healing","zh":"预期愈合"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Small serous drainage, approximated edges, and mild bruising in the early postoperative period are normal. Purulent drainage with erythema suggests infection; wound dehiscence with visible tissue requires immediate action.","rationaleCorrectZh":"术后早期少量浆液渗出、边缘对合和轻度瘀斑是正常的。脓性渗出伴红肿提示感染；伤口裂开伴可见组织需要立即处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected early changes (serous drainage, bruising, approximated edges) from infection signs (purulence, erythema) and dehiscence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分预期早期变化（浆液渗出、瘀斑、对合边缘）与感染征兆（脓液、红肿）和裂开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":39,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_cauti_prevention_27","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.23","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.23.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.23.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[45,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,41],"fullStemEn":"A client has an indwelling urinary catheter. Which nursing action is most important for preventing catheter-associated urinary tract infection (CAUTI)?","fullStemZh":"一位患者留有留置导尿管。哪项护理措施对于预防导管相关尿路感染（CAUTI）最重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is most important for preventing catheter-associated urinary tract infection (CAUTI)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项护理措施对于预防导管相关尿路感染（CAUTI）最重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client has an indwelling urinary catheter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者留有留置导尿管。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Clamp the catheter for 4 hours between drainage intervals to train the bladder.","zh":"引流间隔期间夹闭导尿管4小时以训练膀胱。"},{"id":"D","en":"Change the catheter tubing every 24 hours to prevent bacterial colonization.","zh":"每24小时更换导尿管管路以防止细菌定植。"},{"id":"C","en":"Irrigate the catheter with normal saline every 8 hours.","zh":"每8小时用生理盐水冲洗导尿管。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain a closed drainage system and keep the collection bag below bladder level at all times.","zh":"维持密闭引流系统，并始终将集尿袋保持在膀胱水平以下。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A closed drainage system prevents bacteria from entering through open connections, and keeping the bag below bladder level prevents backflow of colonized urine into the bladder.","rationaleCorrectZh":"密闭引流系统防止细菌通过开放连接进入，将集尿袋保持在膀胱水平以下防止已定植尿液反流入膀胱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"CAUTI prevention: keep the system closed, keep drainage flowing downward (bag below bladder), remove the catheter as soon as it is no longer needed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"CAUTI预防：保持系统密闭，保持向下引流（集尿袋低于膀胱），不再需要时立即拔除。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":40,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_pancreatitis_care_28","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.24","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.24.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.24.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,33],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with acute pancreatitis. Which nursing actions are appropriate during the acute phase? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位患者因急性胰腺炎入院。急性期哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate during the acute phase?","penultimateSentenceZh":"急性期哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administer IV fluid resuscitation as prescribed.","zh":"按医嘱给予静脉补液。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain NPO status as prescribed to allow the pancreas to rest.","zh":"按医嘱维持禁食状态，让胰腺休息。"},{"id":"E","en":"Monitor blood glucose levels for hyperglycemia.","zh":"监测血糖水平，警惕高血糖。"},{"id":"B","en":"Position the client in a side-lying or knee-to-chest position to reduce pain.","zh":"将患者摆放为侧卧或膝胸卧位以减轻疼痛。"},{"id":"F","en":"Encourage immediate ambulation in the hallway to promote GI motility.","zh":"鼓励患者立即在走廊行走以促进胃肠蠕动。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage a high-fat clear liquid diet to maintain caloric intake.","zh":"鼓励高脂清流食以维持热量摄入。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"NPO rests the pancreas, positioning provides comfort, IV fluids correct dehydration, and glucose monitoring detects endocrine dysfunction from pancreatic cell damage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"禁食使胰腺休息，体位提供舒适，静脉补液纠正脱水，血糖监测发现胰腺细胞损伤引起的内分泌功能障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Acute pancreatitis management: rest the pancreas (NPO), replace fluids (IV), position for comfort, monitor for complications (glucose, pain, infection).","testTakingStrategyZh":"急性胰腺炎处理：使胰腺休息（禁食）、补充液体（静脉）、体位舒适、监测并发症（血糖、疼痛、感染）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":41,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_non_opioid_first_29","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.25","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.25.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.25.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[145,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,57],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative client rates pain at 3 out of 10 and requests pain relief. The provider has prescribed both acetaminophen PRN and oxycodone PRN. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一位术后患者疼痛评分3/10，要求止痛。医护提供者已开具对乙酰氨基酚PRN和羟考酮PRN。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider has prescribed both acetaminophen PRN and oxycodone PRN.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医护提供者已开具对乙酰氨基酚PRN和羟考酮PRN。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the oxycodone because it acts faster.","zh":"给予羟考酮，因为起效更快。"},{"id":"B","en":"Apply ice to the site and reassess in 2 hours before giving any medication.","zh":"在部位冰敷并2小时后重新评估，再给予任何药物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Offer the acetaminophen first, as opioids are reserved for moderate to severe pain.","zh":"先给予对乙酰氨基酚，因为阿片类药物用于中至重度疼痛。"},{"id":"C","en":"Withhold all medication until the pain reaches 7 out of 10.","zh":"等疼痛达到7/10再给予任何药物。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The WHO analgesic ladder and current guidelines recommend non-opioid analgesics for mild pain before escalating to opioids, which are appropriate for moderate to severe pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"WHO镇痛阶梯和当前指南建议轻度疼痛先使用非阿片类镇痛药，然后升级到适用于中重度疼痛的阿片类药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When both opioid and non-opioid PRNs are available, match analgesic strength to pain intensity. Mild pain (1–3) → non-opioid first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当阿片类和非阿片类PRN均可用时，将镇痛强度与疼痛强度匹配。轻度疼痛（1-3）→先用非阿片类。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":42,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_cloze_postop_ileus_30","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.26","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.26.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.26.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"A client on postoperative day 2 after bowel resection has a distended abdomen, absent bowel sounds, and has not passed flatus since surgery.","fullStemZh":"一位肠切除术后第2天的患者腹部膨胀、肠鸣音消失，术后未排气。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client on postoperative day 2 after bowel resection has a distended abdomen, absent bowel sounds, and has not passed flatus since surgery.","terminalSentenceZh":"一位肠切除术后第2天的患者腹部膨胀、肠鸣音消失，术后未排气。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize {{1}}, anticipate that the provider will {{2}}, and teach the client that {{3}} helps promote the return of bowel function.","zh":"护士应识别{{1}}，预期医护提供者将{{2}}，并告知患者{{3}}有助于促进肠功能恢复。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"expected normal bowel sound recovery","zh":"预期的正常肠鸣音恢复"},{"id":"o3","en":"a mechanical bowel obstruction requiring reoperation","zh":"需要再次手术的机械性肠梗阻"},{"id":"o1","en":"signs consistent with postoperative ileus","zh":"与术后肠梗阻一致的体征"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"immediately advance the diet to solid foods","zh":"立即将饮食推进至固体食物"},{"id":"o3","en":"discharge the client with outpatient dietary instructions","zh":"让患者出院并给予门诊饮食指导"},{"id":"o1","en":"continue NPO status and monitor for return of bowel function","zh":"继续禁食并监测肠功能恢复"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"prolonged bed rest","zh":"长期卧床休息"},{"id":"o3","en":"fluid restriction","zh":"液体限制"},{"id":"o1","en":"early ambulation","zh":"早期下床活动"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Absent bowel sounds, distension, and no flatus after bowel surgery define postoperative ileus. Management includes NPO status with monitoring; early ambulation is the key nursing intervention to stimulate gut motility.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肠鸣音消失、腹胀和肠道手术后未排气定义为术后肠梗阻。处理包括禁食监测；早期下床活动是刺激肠蠕动的关键护理干预。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Postoperative ileus: absent sounds + distension + no flatus. Management = NPO + early ambulation. Never advance diet before motility returns.","testTakingStrategyZh":"术后肠梗阻：肠鸣音消失+腹胀+未排气。处理=禁食+早期活动。肠蠕动恢复前不推进饮食。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":43,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_delirium_features_32","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.27","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.27.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.27.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[123,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"An older adult client is admitted to the medical unit. Which findings are characteristic of delirium rather than dementia? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位老年患者入住内科病房。哪些发现是谵妄而非痴呆的特征？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings are characteristic of delirium rather than dementia?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现是谵妄而非痴呆的特征？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Severe inattention with difficulty following a simple conversation.","zh":"严重注意力不集中，难以跟上简单对话。"},{"id":"A","en":"Acute onset of confusion over the past 12 hours.","zh":"过去12小时内急性发作的意识混乱。"},{"id":"F","en":"Sleep-wake cycle reversal: sleeping during the day and awake and agitated at night.","zh":"睡眠-觉醒周期颠倒：白天睡觉，夜间清醒且激越。"},{"id":"C","en":"Memory loss that has been gradually worsening over the past 3 years.","zh":"过去3年逐渐加重的记忆力减退。"},{"id":"B","en":"Level of consciousness that fluctuates between alertness and drowsiness throughout the day.","zh":"全天意识水平在清醒和嗜睡之间波动。"},{"id":"E","en":"Difficulty recalling a granddaughter's name, present for approximately 18 months.","zh":"无法记住孙女姓名，此症状已持续约18个月。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Delirium is characterized by acute onset, fluctuating course, inattention, and disturbed sleep-wake cycle. Dementia has a gradual onset and progressive decline without fluctuating consciousness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"谵妄以急性发作、波动病程、注意力不集中和睡眠-觉醒周期紊乱为特征。痴呆有渐进性发作和进行性衰退，无意识水平波动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Delirium = ACUTE onset, FLUCTUATING level of consciousness, inattention. Dementia = GRADUAL progressive decline. Onset and duration differentiate them.","testTakingStrategyZh":"谵妄=急性发作、意识波动、注意力不集中。痴呆=渐进性下降。起病和持续时间区分两者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":44,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_anorexia_priority_33","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.28.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,30],"fullStemEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is admitted to the inpatient unit. Which finding is the nurse's priority concern?","fullStemZh":"一位神经性厌食症患者入住住院病房。哪项发现是护士优先关注的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding is the nurse's priority concern?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项发现是护士优先关注的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is admitted to the inpatient unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位神经性厌食症患者入住住院病房。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Body mass index of 15.8 kg/m².","zh":"体重指数为15.8 kg/m²。"},{"id":"B","en":"Refusal to discuss meal plans with the dietitian.","zh":"拒绝与营养师讨论饮食计划。"},{"id":"C","en":"Client states she feels fat despite her low weight.","zh":"患者表示尽管体重低仍感觉自己很胖。"},{"id":"A","en":"Blood pressure 82/54 mm Hg with a heart rate of 44/min.","zh":"血压82/54毫米汞柱，心率44次/分。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe hypotension and bradycardia represent hemodynamic instability from malnutrition-related electrolyte imbalances and cardiac muscle wasting. This is an immediate life threat.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重低血压和心动过缓代表营养不良相关电解质失衡和心肌消耗引起的血流动力学不稳定。这是立即的生命威胁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In eating disorders, assess physiology first. Bradycardia + hypotension = life-threatening cardiac compromise; always takes priority over psychological findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在饮食失调中，先评估生理状况。心动过缓+低血压=危及生命的心脏功能受损；始终优先于心理发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is admitted to the inpatient unit.","controlSentenceZh":"一位神经性厌食症患者入住住院病房。"}
{"queueIndex":45,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_or_palliative_care_34","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.29.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,48],"fullStemEn":"A nurse assesses a nonverbal client in the final stages of life. Place the nurse's comfort-focused actions in priority order.","fullStemZh":"一位护士评估一位处于生命最后阶段的无语言表达能力患者。请将护士以舒适为重点的行动按优先顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's comfort-focused actions in priority order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士以舒适为重点的行动按优先顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse assesses a nonverbal client in the final stages of life.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位护士评估一位处于生命最后阶段的无语言表达能力患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Reposition the client and perform mouth care.","zh":"为患者翻身并进行口腔护理。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer prescribed comfort medications for pain or breathing difficulty.","zh":"给予已处方的舒适药物缓解疼痛或呼吸困难。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the spiritual care provider if spiritual needs were previously expressed.","zh":"如患者此前表达过精神需求，通知灵性关怀提供者。"},{"id":"E","en":"Provide supportive presence to family members at the bedside.","zh":"为床旁家属提供支持性陪伴。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess for signs of pain and dyspnea using a behavioral pain tool.","zh":"使用行为疼痛工具评估疼痛和呼吸困难体征。"}],"correct":["B","C","D","E","A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assessment of distress guides intervention. Pharmacological relief follows, then physical comfort measures, then family support, and finally coordinating spiritual care after immediate physical needs are addressed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"痛苦评估指导干预。然后是药物缓解，再进行身体舒适措施，然后家庭支持，最后在即时身体需求解决后协调灵性关怀。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Palliative care priority: assess distress → relieve symptoms → physical comfort → family support → coordinate other services.","testTakingStrategyZh":"姑息护理优先顺序：评估痛苦→缓解症状→身体舒适→家庭支持→协调其他服务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":46,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_hipaa_disclosure_35","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.30.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,232],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,47],"fullStemEn":"A person calls the unit and identifies as the client's employer, requesting the client's diagnosis and reason for hospitalization. The client has not provided written authorization for disclosure. Which response is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一位自称患者雇主的人致电病区，要求了解患者诊断和住院原因。患者未提供书面授权。哪种回应最恰当？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种回应最恰当？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has not provided written authorization for disclosure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者未提供书面授权。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Decline to confirm or deny any patient information without written authorization.","zh":"在没有书面授权的情况下，拒绝确认或否认任何患者信息。"},{"id":"B","en":"Confirm that the client is a patient and provide general status information only.","zh":"确认患者在院，仅提供一般状态信息。"},{"id":"C","en":"Transfer the call to the charge nurse to handle the request.","zh":"将电话转给护士长处理该请求。"},{"id":"A","en":"Provide discharge information only, since that is public record.","zh":"仅提供出院信息，因为这是公共记录。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA prohibits disclosing any protected health information — including confirming that someone is a patient — without written authorization. An employer has no automatic right to this information.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA禁止在没有书面授权的情况下披露任何受保护的健康信息，包括确认某人是否为患者。雇主没有自动获取此类信息的权利。","testTakingStrategyEn":"HIPAA: no disclosure without written patient authorization. This includes even confirming or denying that the person is a patient.","testTakingStrategyZh":"HIPAA：没有患者书面授权不得披露。这包括确认/否认该人是否为患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":47,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_matrix_therapeutic_comm_36","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.31.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"For each nurse response to a client expressing anxiety about a new diagnosis, classify the response as therapeutic or non-therapeutic.","fullStemZh":"针对护士对一位对新诊断感到焦虑的患者的每种回应，将其分类为治疗性或非治疗性。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nurse response to a client expressing anxiety about a new diagnosis, classify the response as therapeutic or non-therapeutic.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对护士对一位对新诊断感到焦虑的患者的每种回应，将其分类为治疗性或非治疗性。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"\"It sounds like you are feeling frightened about what this diagnosis means for you.\"","zh":"\"听起来您对这个诊断对您意味着什么感到害怕。\""},{"id":"r2","en":"\"Don't worry — the doctors here are the best, so everything will be fine.\"","zh":"\"别担心——这里的医生是最好的，所以一切都会好的。\""},{"id":"r3","en":"\"What questions or concerns do you have that I can help with right now?\"","zh":"\"您现在有什么问题或顾虑是我可以帮助的？\""},{"id":"r4","en":"\"You really shouldn't feel that way — many people with this condition live normal lives.\"","zh":"\"您真的不应该这么感觉——许多有这种病的人过着正常生活。\""},{"id":"r5","en":"\"Tell me more about what is worrying you the most right now.\"","zh":"\"告诉我更多关于您现在最担心的是什么。\""}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Therapeutic","zh":"治疗性"},{"id":"c2","en":"Non-therapeutic","zh":"非治疗性"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic responses reflect feelings, invite expression, and explore concerns. Non-therapeutic responses offer false reassurance or invalidate the client's emotions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性回应反映感受、邀请表达并探索顾虑。非治疗性回应给予虚假保证或否定患者的情绪。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic = reflects feelings, open questions, validates experience. Non-therapeutic = false reassurance, minimizing, telling the client how to feel.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性=反映感受、开放式问题、认可体验。非治疗性=虚假保证、淡化、告诉患者如何感受。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":48,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_restraint_alternative_37","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.32.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,42],"fullStemEn":"An older adult client with dementia repeatedly attempts to pull out the IV catheter. Which intervention should the nurse try before applying physical restraints?","fullStemZh":"一位患有痴呆的老年患者反复尝试拔出静脉留置针。护士在使用身体约束前应先尝试哪项干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention should the nurse try before applying physical restraints?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在使用身体约束前应先尝试哪项干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An older adult client with dementia repeatedly attempts to pull out the IV catheter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患有痴呆的老年患者反复尝试拔出静脉留置针。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Apply soft wrist restraints to both arms to prevent access to the IV site.","zh":"对双臂使用软性腕部约束，防止接触静脉穿刺部位。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request an immediate provider order for sedation to decrease the behavior.","zh":"申请立即镇静的医嘱以减少该行为。"},{"id":"C","en":"Offer a familiar comfort object or hand activity to redirect the client's attention.","zh":"提供熟悉的安慰物或手部活动，以转移患者注意力。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a private room with minimal stimulation.","zh":"将患者单独置于刺激最少的私人房间。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The least-restrictive approach is required before physical restraints. Redirection with a comfort item or hand activity satisfies the client's need to engage their hands without restricting movement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用身体约束前需要采用最少限制的方法。用安慰物或手部活动进行转移注意力，满足患者使用双手的需求，而不限制其活动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Before restraints, always try the least restrictive option first. For dementia behaviors: redirection, familiar objects, and distraction are preferred alternatives.","testTakingStrategyZh":"约束前总是先尝试最少限制的选项。对于痴呆行为：转移注意力、熟悉物品和分心是首选替代措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":49,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_cultural_eol_38","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.33.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,223],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,60],"fullStemEn":"A client from a cultural background where family members traditionally serve as the primary decision-makers is approaching the end of life. Which nursing actions demonstrate culturally sensitive care? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位来自家庭成员传统上担任主要决策者的文化背景的患者正在走向生命终点。哪些护理行动体现了文化敏感性护理？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions demonstrate culturally sensitive care?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理行动体现了文化敏感性护理？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Consult cultural or spiritual resources identified by the client or family.","zh":"咨询患者或家属确认的文化或精神资源。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document the client's preferred decision-making structure in the care plan.","zh":"在护理计划中记录患者首选的决策结构。"},{"id":"D","en":"Invite family members the client designates to participate in care discussions.","zh":"邀请患者指定的家庭成员参与护理讨论。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client privately whether they wish to make their own decisions or prefer family involvement.","zh":"私下询问患者是否希望自己做决定，还是希望家庭参与。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assume the family will make all decisions because that is the cultural norm.","zh":"假设家庭将做出所有决定，因为这是文化规范。"},{"id":"E","en":"Insist that the client complete an individual advance directive before receiving care.","zh":"坚持要求患者在接受护理前填写个人预立医疗指示。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Culturally sensitive end-of-life care begins by assessing the individual's actual preferences rather than assuming cultural norms apply universally. Documenting, involving designated family, and utilizing cultural resources all honor the client's values.","rationaleCorrectZh":"文化敏感性临终护理从评估个人实际偏好开始，而不是假设文化规范普遍适用。记录、纳入指定家庭成员并利用文化资源都能尊重患者的价值观。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Never assume cultural norms — always ask the individual first. Then document and honor their stated preferences. Insisting on Western-style individual directives can be culturally inappropriate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"永远不要假设文化规范——总是先询问个人。然后记录并尊重其陈述的偏好。坚持西方式个人指示可能在文化上不恰当。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":50,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_bipolar_mania_39","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.34.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,49],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is admitted in an acute manic phase. The client has not slept in 3 days, is pacing continuously, and is speaking very rapidly. Which nursing intervention is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一位双相情感障碍患者因急性躁狂发作入院。患者3天未入睡，持续踱步，语速极快。哪项护理干预是优先的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing intervention is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项护理干预是优先的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has not slept in 3 days, is pacing continuously, and is speaking very rapidly.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者3天未入睡，持续踱步，语速极快。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Allow the client to pace freely in the milieu to expend excess energy safely.","zh":"允许患者在环境中自由踱步以安全消耗多余能量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide a structured, low-stimulation environment and promote rest.","zh":"提供有结构、低刺激的环境并促进休息。"},{"id":"B","en":"Present a detailed written schedule of all planned daily activities.","zh":"提供所有计划的每日活动的详细书面时间表。"},{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the client to join a group therapy session with other patients.","zh":"鼓励患者与其他患者参加团体治疗。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In acute mania, reducing environmental stimulation and promoting rest addresses the physiological and safety risks of prolonged sleep deprivation and hyperactivity. A calm, structured setting lowers escalation risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在急性躁狂中，减少环境刺激并促进休息解决了长期睡眠剥夺和过度活跃带来的生理和安全风险。平静有结构的环境降低了升级风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Acute mania priority: decrease stimulation, promote safety and rest. Group activities and detailed schedules add stimulation and worsen the state.","testTakingStrategyZh":"急性躁狂优先：减少刺激，促进安全和休息。团体活动和详细时间表增加刺激并加重病情。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":51,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_cloze_ptsd_40","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.35.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,56],"fullStemEn":"A veteran is seen in the outpatient mental health clinic. The client reports recurrent nightmares, hypervigilance, avoidance of crowded places, and flashbacks since returning from deployment 8 months ago.","fullStemZh":"一位退伍军人在门诊心理健康诊所就诊。患者报告自8个月前服役归来后出现反复噩梦、过度警觉、回避人多场所和闪回症状。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client reports recurrent nightmares, hypervigilance, avoidance of crowded places, and flashbacks since returning from deployment 8 months ago.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者报告自8个月前服役归来后出现反复噩梦、过度警觉、回避人多场所和闪回症状。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A veteran is seen in the outpatient mental health clinic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位退伍军人在门诊心理健康诊所就诊。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize these findings as consistent with {{1}}, anticipate that the priority nursing goal is {{2}}, and plan to educate the client that {{3}} is a recommended first-line treatment.","zh":"护士应识别这些发现与{{1}}一致，预期优先护理目标是{{2}}，并计划告知患者{{3}}是推荐的一线治疗方法。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"generalized anxiety disorder","zh":"广泛性焦虑障碍"},{"id":"o1","en":"post-traumatic stress disorder","zh":"创伤后应激障碍"},{"id":"o3","en":"acute stress disorder","zh":"急性应激障碍"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"encouraging immediate exposure to all avoided triggers","zh":"鼓励立即接触所有回避的触发因素"},{"id":"o3","en":"eliminating all anxiety symptoms within one week","zh":"在一周内消除所有焦虑症状"},{"id":"o1","en":"establishing safety and reducing acute distress","zh":"建立安全感并减轻急性痛苦"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"long-term benzodiazepine therapy","zh":"长期苯二氮䓬类药物治疗"},{"id":"o3","en":"social isolation to avoid re-traumatization","zh":"社交隔离以避免再次创伤"},{"id":"o1","en":"trauma-focused cognitive behavioral therapy","zh":"创伤聚焦认知行为治疗"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The symptom cluster (flashbacks, hypervigilance, avoidance, nightmares for >1 month after trauma) meets the criteria for PTSD. Safety is the foundational goal, and trauma-focused CBT is a first-line evidence-based treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"症状群（创伤后超过1个月的闪回、过度警觉、回避、噩梦）符合PTSD标准。安全是基础性目标，创伤聚焦认知行为治疗是一线循证治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"PTSD hallmarks: flashbacks, hypervigilance, avoidance, nightmares, >1 month post-trauma. First-line treatment: trauma-focused CBT, not benzodiazepines.","testTakingStrategyZh":"PTSD特征：闪回、过度警觉、回避、噩梦，创伤后持续超过1个月。一线治疗：创伤聚焦认知行为治疗，而非苯二氮䓬类。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":52,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_postpartum_fundus_41","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.36.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse assesses a postpartum client 1 hour after vaginal delivery. The uterine fundus is boggy and displaced to the right of midline. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一位护士在阴道分娩1小时后评估一位产后患者。子宫底部松弛，向中线右侧移位。护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The uterine fundus is boggy and displaced to the right of midline.","penultimateSentenceZh":"子宫底部松弛，向中线右侧移位。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer oxytocin as prescribed for uterine atony.","zh":"按医嘱给予催产素治疗子宫收缩乏力。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assist the client to the bathroom to void.","zh":"协助患者去洗手间排尿。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider of a suspected uterine inversion.","zh":"通知医护提供者疑似子宫翻转。"},{"id":"C","en":"Perform vigorous fundal massage for at least 5 minutes.","zh":"进行至少5分钟的用力子宫底按摩。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A boggy, displaced fundus is the classic sign of a full bladder preventing uterine contraction. Voiding is the first intervention because a distended bladder is the most common cause of fundal displacement and uterine atony in the early postpartum period.","rationaleCorrectZh":"松弛、移位的子宫底是膀胱充盈阻碍子宫收缩的典型体征。排尿是首选干预，因为膨胀的膀胱是产后早期子宫底移位和子宫收缩乏力最常见的原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Boggy + displaced fundus in early postpartum = think full bladder first. Have the client void before escalating to massage or medications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产后早期子宫底松弛+移位=首先考虑膀胱充盈。让患者排尿后再升级为按摩或药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":53,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_neonatal_jaundice_42","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.37.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[155,177],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a term newborn at 30 hours of life who has visible yellowing of the skin. Which findings are consistent with physiological jaundice? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位护士正在护理一位出生30小时、皮肤出现明显黄染的足月新生儿。哪些发现与生理性黄疸一致？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings are consistent with physiological jaundice?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现与生理性黄疸一致？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The newborn's skin and sclera appear yellow.","zh":"新生儿皮肤和巩膜呈黄色。"},{"id":"D","en":"A positive direct Coombs test is documented on the newborn's chart.","zh":"新生儿病历中记录了直接抗球蛋白试验阳性。"},{"id":"B","en":"Jaundice was noted within the first 24 hours of life.","zh":"黄疸在出生后24小时内被注意到。"},{"id":"E","en":"Bilirubin levels are expected to peak around day 3 to 5 and resolve by 1 to 2 weeks.","zh":"胆红素水平预计在第3至5天达到峰值，并在1至2周内消退。"},{"id":"A","en":"Jaundice first appeared on the face and is progressing toward the trunk.","zh":"黄疸首先出现在面部，正向躯干方向进展。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Physiological jaundice follows a cephalocaudal pattern, appears after 24 hours, causes yellow skin and sclera, peaks at days 3–5, and resolves by 1–2 weeks. Earlier onset, a positive Coombs test, or rapidly rising levels suggest pathological causes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生理性黄疸遵循头尾方向规律，出现在24小时后，引起皮肤和巩膜黄染，在第3-5天达峰，在1-2周内消退。更早的发病、直接抗球蛋白试验阳性或快速上升的水平提示病理性原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Physiological jaundice: appears AFTER 24 hours, cephalocaudal, peaks day 3–5, resolves by 2 weeks. Any deviation (early onset, positive Coombs, prolonged) = pathological.","testTakingStrategyZh":"生理性黄疸：出现在24小时后，头尾方向，第3-5天达峰，2周内消退。任何偏差（早期发病、直接抗球蛋白阳性、延长）=病理性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":54,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_reye_syndrome_43","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.38.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,37],"fullStemEn":"The parent of a 6-year-old with confirmed influenza asks the nurse which medication is safe for fever management at home. Which response is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一位流感确诊的6岁儿童的家长询问护士在家中安全的退热药物。哪种回答最恰当？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种回答最恰当？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The parent of a 6-year-old with confirmed influenza asks the nurse which medication is safe for fever management at home.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位流感确诊的6岁儿童的家长询问护士在家中安全的退热药物。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"No fever medication should be given; only lukewarm sponge baths are safe for children.","zh":"不应给予任何退热药物；只有温水擦浴对儿童是安全的。"},{"id":"C","en":"Aspirin is safe and effective for fever control in children with viral illnesses.","zh":"阿司匹林对病毒性疾病儿童的退热安全有效。"},{"id":"B","en":"Antibiotics should be started immediately to prevent secondary bacterial infections.","zh":"应立即开始抗生素治疗以预防继发性细菌感染。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ibuprofen or acetaminophen are the recommended options for fever management in children.","zh":"布洛芬或对乙酰氨基酚是儿童退热的推荐选择。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aspirin is contraindicated in children with viral illnesses due to its association with Reye syndrome, a rare but life-threatening condition causing liver failure and encephalopathy. Ibuprofen and acetaminophen are the safe, recommended alternatives.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阿司匹林因与瑞氏综合征相关而禁用于病毒性疾病儿童，这是一种罕见但危及生命的病症，导致肝衰竭和脑病。布洛芬和对乙酰氨基酚是安全、推荐的替代品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Aspirin + viral illness + child = Reye syndrome risk. Always recommend acetaminophen or ibuprofen for pediatric fever with viral illness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"阿司匹林+病毒性疾病+儿童=瑞氏综合征风险。病毒性疾病儿科退热始终推荐对乙酰氨基酚或布洛芬。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":55,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_fib_infant_acetaminophen_45","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.39.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,78],"fullStemEn":"A 6-month-old infant weighs 6.4 kg. The provider orders acetaminophen 15 mg/kg per dose every 4 hours PRN for fever. The available concentration is 160 mg/5 mL. Calculate the volume (mL) to administer for one dose.","fullStemZh":"一名6个月大的婴儿体重6.4公斤。医护提供者开具对乙酰氨基酚每剂15毫克/公斤，每4小时按需给药退热。现有浓度为160毫克/5毫升。计算每剂给药量（毫升）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the volume (mL) to administer for one dose.","terminalSentenceZh":"计算每剂给药量（毫升）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The available concentration is 160 mg/5 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现有浓度为160毫克/5毫升。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL per dose","zh":"毫升/剂"},"acceptable":["3","3 mL","3.0","3.0 mL"],"numeric":{"value":3,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1: Calculate the dose — 15 mg/kg × 6.4 kg = 96 mg. Step 2: Calculate the volume — 96 mg ÷ 160 mg × 5 mL = 3 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步：计算剂量——15毫克/公斤×6.4公斤=96毫克。第二步：计算体积——96毫克÷160毫克×5毫升=3毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Dosage calc: (weight × dose per kg) ÷ concentration × volume = answer. Always verify units are consistent before calculating.","testTakingStrategyZh":"剂量计算：（体重×每公斤剂量）÷浓度×体积=答案。计算前始终核查单位一致性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":56,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_matrix_neonatal_assessment_46","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.40.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,41],"fullStemEn":"For each finding noted during a newborn assessment at 12 hours of life, indicate whether the finding is expected or requires nurse follow-up.","fullStemZh":"对于出生后12小时新生儿评估中发现的每项情况，指出该发现是预期的还是需要护士跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding noted during a newborn assessment at 12 hours of life, indicate whether the finding is expected or requires nurse follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于出生后12小时新生儿评估中发现的每项情况，指出该发现是预期的还是需要护士跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Respiratory rate of 52 breaths/min with occasional irregular rhythm.","zh":"呼吸频率52次/分，偶有不规则节律。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Pink skin centrally with blue discoloration of both hands and feet.","zh":"中央皮肤粉红，双手双足皮肤发绀。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Mottled skin with axillary temperature of 96.8 °F (36 °C) and respiratory rate of 30/min.","zh":"皮肤花斑，腋温96.8 °F (36 °C)，呼吸频率30次/分。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Overlapping cranial sutures with elongated head shape.","zh":"颅缝重叠，头部形状拉长。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Soft, flat, pulsating anterior fontanelle.","zh":"前囟软、平、有搏动。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected finding","zh":"预期发现"},{"id":"c2","en":"Requires follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Normal newborn RR is 30–60; mild irregularity is normal. Acrocyanosis (blue extremities) is expected in the first 48 hours. Mottling with a low-normal temperature warrants assessment for cold stress. Molding is expected after vaginal delivery. A soft, flat, pulsating fontanelle is normal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正常新生儿呼吸频率为30-60次/分；轻度不规则是正常的。肢端发绀（四肢发蓝）在出生后48小时内是预期的。花斑皮肤伴低正常体温需要评估冷应激。颅缝重叠在阴道分娩后是预期的。软、平、有搏动的前囟是正常的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Newborn normals: RR 30–60, acrocyanosis OK for 48 h, molding expected, flat soft fontanelle normal. Flag: mottling + low temp, central cyanosis, bulging fontanelle.","testTakingStrategyZh":"新生儿正常值：呼吸频率30-60，肢端发绀48小时内正常，颅缝重叠预期，软平前囟正常。警惕：花斑+低温、中央性发绀、前囟突出。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":57,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_breastfeeding_latch_47","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.41.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,116],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,32],"fullStemEn":"A postpartum nurse is observing a new mother breastfeed for the first time. Which finding indicates D correct latch?","fullStemZh":"一位产后护士正在观察一位新妈妈第一次哺乳。哪项发现表明含接正确？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding indicates D correct latch?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项发现表明含接正确？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A postpartum nurse is observing a new mother breastfeed for the first time.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位产后护士正在观察一位新妈妈第一次哺乳。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The infant's mouth covers most of the areola with lips flanged outward.","zh":"婴儿嘴巴覆盖大部分乳晕，嘴唇向外翻出。"},{"id":"A","en":"The infant's lips are tightly pursed around the nipple only.","zh":"婴儿嘴唇紧紧撅起，仅含住乳头。"},{"id":"D","en":"Audible smacking sounds are heard with each suck.","zh":"每次吸吮时可听到响亮的咂嘴声。"},{"id":"B","en":"The mother reports a sharp pinching pain with each suck.","zh":"母亲报告每次吸吮时有剧烈刺痛。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An effective latch requires the infant to take in most of the areola, not just the nipple, with lips flanged outward. This allows effective milk transfer and prevents nipple trauma.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效含接要求婴儿含住大部分乳晕而非仅是乳头，嘴唇向外翻出。这允许有效的乳汁转移并防止乳头损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Correct latch: wide open, covers areola (not just nipple), lips flanged OUT. Incorrect latch signs: pain, smacking sounds, nipple only, lips tucked in.","testTakingStrategyZh":"正确含接：大开口，覆盖乳晕（不仅是乳头），嘴唇向外翻出。错误含接征象：疼痛、咂嘴声、仅含乳头、嘴唇向内缩。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":58,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_sata_mmr_vaccine_48","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.42.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,52],"fullStemEn":"A parent asks the nurse about the MMR (measles, mumps, rubella) vaccine at the child's 12-month well visit. Which statements should the nurse include in the education? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位家长在12个月健康访视时向护士询问麻腮风（MMR）疫苗。护士应在教育中包含哪些内容？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements should the nurse include in the education?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在教育中包含哪些内容？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"A mild runny nose is a contraindication to receiving the vaccine today.","zh":"轻微流鼻涕是今天接种疫苗的禁忌证。"},{"id":"D","en":"A second dose is recommended at 4 to 6 years of age.","zh":"推荐在4至6岁时接种第二剂。"},{"id":"E","en":"The vaccine provides full immunity within 24 hours of administration.","zh":"疫苗在接种后24小时内提供完全免疫。"},{"id":"C","en":"The vaccine is contraindicated in children who are severely immunocompromised.","zh":"该疫苗禁用于严重免疫功能低下的儿童。"},{"id":"A","en":"The MMR vaccine is a live-attenuated vaccine given by subcutaneous injection.","zh":"麻腮风疫苗是一种通过皮下注射给予的减毒活疫苗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Common adverse effects include low-grade fever and a mild rash appearing 7 to 12 days after injection.","zh":"常见不良反应包括注射后7至12天出现低热和轻度皮疹。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MMR is a live-attenuated subcutaneous vaccine with common delayed adverse effects. It is contraindicated in severe immunosuppression because the live virus can cause disease. A two-dose schedule at 12–15 months and 4–6 years provides sustained immunity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"麻腮风是一种减毒活皮下注射疫苗，有常见的延迟不良反应。严重免疫抑制时禁忌使用，因为活病毒可能引起疾病。12-15个月和4-6岁的两剂程序提供持续免疫。","testTakingStrategyEn":"MMR: live vaccine → subQ route → contraindicated with severe immunosuppression → delayed rash/fever at 7–12 days is normal → 2-dose series. Mild illness alone does not defer.","testTakingStrategyZh":"麻腮风：减毒活疫苗→皮下注射→严重免疫抑制禁忌→7-12天延迟皮疹/低热是正常的→2剂系列。仅轻度疾病不推迟接种。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which statements should the nurse include in the education?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应在教育中包含哪些内容？"}
{"queueIndex":59,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_alendronate_teaching_49","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.43.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,54],"fullStemEn":"A client with osteoporosis has a new prescription for alendronate (Fosamax) 70 mg once weekly. Which instruction is most important for the nurse to include in discharge teaching?","fullStemZh":"一位骨质疏松症患者新开了阿仑膦酸钠（福善美）70毫克每周一次的处方。护士在出院宣教中最重要的是包含哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction is most important for the nurse to include in discharge teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在出院宣教中最重要的是包含哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with osteoporosis has a new prescription for alendronate (Fosamax) 70 mg once weekly.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位骨质疏松症患者新开了阿仑膦酸钠（福善美）70毫克每周一次的处方。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Take the tablet with a full glass of orange juice to enhance calcium absorption.","zh":"用一整杯橙汁送服药片以促进钙的吸收。"},{"id":"D","en":"Take the tablet first thing in the morning with a full glass of plain water and remain upright for at least 30 minutes.","zh":"早晨起床后立即用一整杯白开水服药，并保持直立至少30分钟。"},{"id":"A","en":"Crush the tablet and sprinkle it on soft food if swallowing is difficult.","zh":"如果吞咽困难，将药片压碎撒在软食上服用。"},{"id":"C","en":"Lie down for 30 minutes after taking the medication to prevent dizziness.","zh":"服药后躺下30分钟以防头晕。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bisphosphonates like alendronate can cause esophageal irritation and ulceration. Taking it with a full glass of water on an empty stomach maximizes absorption; remaining upright for at least 30 minutes prevents esophageal reflux of the medication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阿仑膦酸钠等双膦酸盐可引起食管刺激和溃疡。空腹用一整杯水服用可最大化吸收；保持直立至少30分钟防止药物食管反流。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Alendronate rules: empty stomach + plain water only + first thing AM + stay UPRIGHT ≥30 minutes. Never crush, never lie down, never take with food or juice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"阿仑膦酸钠规则：空腹+仅用白开水+早晨第一件事+保持直立≥30分钟。不要压碎、不要躺下、不要与食物或果汁同服。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":60,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_a_mc_surgical_timeout_50","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.44.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,210],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,60],"fullStemEn":"The surgical team is preparing to begin an elective procedure. The circulating nurse calls for a time-out immediately before the incision. Which element is the primary focus of this Universal Protocol time-out?","fullStemZh":"手术团队正在准备开始一项择期手术。巡回护士在切开前立即要求暂停（time-out）。这一通用协议暂停的主要关注点是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which element is the primary focus of this Universal Protocol time-out?","terminalSentenceZh":"这一通用协议暂停的主要关注点是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The circulating nurse calls for a time-out immediately before the incision.","penultimateSentenceZh":"巡回护士在切开前立即要求暂停（time-out）。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Confirming that the facility has received insurance authorization for the scheduled procedure.","zh":"确认医疗机构已获得计划手术的保险授权。"},{"id":"B","en":"Reviewing the postoperative care plan and discharge instructions with the anesthesiologist.","zh":"与麻醉科医生共同审查术后护理计划和出院指导。"},{"id":"D","en":"Verifying the correct patient identity, the correct surgical site, and the correct procedure.","zh":"核实正确的患者身份、正确的手术部位和正确的手术操作。"},{"id":"A","en":"Completing the count of all instruments, sponges, and sharps before the case begins.","zh":"在手术开始前完成所有器械、纱布和锐器的清点。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Universal Protocol time-out, mandated by The Joint Commission, is designed to prevent wrong-patient, wrong-site, and wrong-procedure errors. All team members must actively confirm these three elements before the incision.","rationaleCorrectZh":"联合委员会规定的通用协议暂停旨在防止错误患者、错误部位和错误手术操作的错误。所有团队成员必须在切开前主动确认这三个要素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Universal Protocol time-out = right patient + right site + right procedure, conducted immediately before the incision with all team members present and actively participating.","testTakingStrategyZh":"通用协议暂停=正确患者+正确部位+正确手术，在切开前立即进行，所有团队成员在场并积极参与。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":61,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_jun05_moc_case_mgmt_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.45.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,275],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,88],"fullStemEn":"A nurse case manager is finalizing the discharge plan for a client recovering from a total hip arthroplasty who will require continued intravenous antibiotics and physical therapy at home. Which action best demonstrates effective case management to ensure continuity of care?","fullStemZh":"一名护士个案管理者正在为一名全髋关节置换术后康复的患者制定出院计划，该患者出院后仍需在家中继续接受静脉抗生素治疗和物理治疗。哪项行动最能体现有效的个案管理，以确保护理的连续性？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action best demonstrates effective case management to ensure continuity of care?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项行动最能体现有效的个案管理，以确保护理的连续性？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse case manager is finalizing the discharge plan for a client recovering from a total hip arthroplasty who will require continued intravenous antibiotics and physical therapy at home.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名护士个案管理者正在为一名全髋关节置换术后康复的患者制定出院计划，该患者出院后仍需在家中继续接受静脉抗生素治疗和物理治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Delegate coordination of the home services to the unlicensed assistive personnel before discharge.","zh":"在出院前将家庭服务的协调工作委派给无执照的辅助人员。"},{"id":"C","en":"Instruct the client to telephone the surgeon's office if any problems develop after returning home.","zh":"指导患者在回家后如出现任何问题时致电外科医生办公室。"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide the client with written discharge instructions and verify that a family member can drive the client home.","zh":"向患者提供书面出院指导，并确认有家属可以开车送患者回家。"},{"id":"A","en":"Arrange home health services and confirm that home infusion therapy and physical therapy are scheduled before the client is discharged.","zh":"安排家庭健康服务，并在患者出院前确认家庭输液治疗和物理治疗均已预约安排妥当。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective case management coordinates resources across the care continuum so that needed services are in place at the moment of transition. Arranging home health and confirming that IV infusion and physical therapy are actually scheduled before discharge prevents gaps that could lead to missed antibiotic doses, infection, or rehospitalization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的个案管理会在整个护理连续体中协调资源，以确保在过渡的时刻所需服务已经到位。安排家庭健康服务并在出院前确认静脉输液和物理治疗确实已预约，可以防止可能导致漏用抗生素、感染或再次住院的护理缺口。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For case management questions, choose the option that proactively secures the specific services the client will need after transition, rather than reactive or generic discharge steps. Match the action to the stated ongoing needs (here, IV antibiotics and physical therapy).","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于个案管理类题目，应选择能主动落实患者过渡后所需具体服务的选项，而非被动或笼统的出院步骤。将行动与题干所述的持续需求（此处为静脉抗生素和物理治疗）相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":62,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_jun05_moc_referral_slp_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.46.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,297],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,88],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is coordinating care for a client recovering from a stroke who coughs and chokes when drinking thin liquids and has noticeable difficulty swallowing. To best address this specific problem, the nurse should initiate a referral to collaborate with which member of the interdisciplinary team?","fullStemZh":"一名护士正在为一名脑卒中后康复的患者协调护理，该患者在饮用稀薄液体时会咳嗽和呛咳，并存在明显的吞咽困难。为最好地解决这一具体问题，护士应发起转介，与跨学科团队中的哪位成员协作？","terminalSentenceEn":"To best address this specific problem, the nurse should initiate a referral to collaborate with which member of the interdisciplinary team?","terminalSentenceZh":"为最好地解决这一具体问题，护士应发起转介，与跨学科团队中的哪位成员协作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is coordinating care for a client recovering from a stroke who coughs and chokes when drinking thin liquids and has noticeable difficulty swallowing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名护士正在为一名脑卒中后康复的患者协调护理，该患者在饮用稀薄液体时会咳嗽和呛咳，并存在明显的吞咽困难。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Respiratory therapist","zh":"呼吸治疗师"},{"id":"A","en":"Speech-language pathologist","zh":"言语-语言病理治疗师"},{"id":"B","en":"Registered dietitian","zh":"注册营养师"},{"id":"D","en":"Physical therapist","zh":"物理治疗师"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The speech-language pathologist is the interdisciplinary team member who performs a formal swallowing (dysphagia) evaluation, determines aspiration risk, and recommends safe diet textures, liquid consistencies, and swallowing techniques. Coordinating this referral best matches the client's specific swallowing problem and protects against aspiration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"言语-语言病理治疗师是跨学科团队中负责进行正式吞咽（吞咽困难）评估、判断误吸风险并推荐安全的食物质地、液体稠度及吞咽技巧的成员。协调这一转介最契合该患者的具体吞咽问题，并可防止误吸。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For referral questions, match the client's specific problem to the discipline whose scope of practice directly addresses it. Swallowing/dysphagia evaluation is the speech-language pathologist's domain; the dietitian's role follows once safe textures are established.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于转介类题目，应将患者的具体问题与执业范围能直接处理该问题的学科相匹配。吞咽/吞咽困难评估属于言语-语言病理治疗师的领域；在确定安全质地后才轮到营养师发挥作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is coordinating care for a client recovering from a stroke who coughs and chokes when drinking thin liquids and has noticeable difficulty swallowing.","controlSentenceZh":"一名护士正在为一名脑卒中后康复的患者协调护理，该患者在饮用稀薄液体时会咳嗽和呛咳，并存在明显的吞咽困难。"}
{"queueIndex":63,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_jun05_moc_quality_improvement_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.47.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[165,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,71],"fullStemEn":"A nurse serving on a unit quality improvement committee notes that the rate of catheter-associated urinary tract infections (CAUTI) has risen over the past quarter. Which action represents the most appropriate first step in the quality improvement process?","fullStemZh":"一名参与病区质量改进委员会的护士注意到，过去一个季度导尿管相关尿路感染（CAUTI）的发生率有所上升。哪项行动是质量改进流程中最恰当的第一步？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action represents the most appropriate first step in the quality improvement process?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项行动是质量改进流程中最恰当的第一步？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse serving on a unit quality improvement committee notes that the rate of catheter-associated urinary tract infections (CAUTI) has risen over the past quarter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名参与病区质量改进委员会的护士注意到，过去一个季度导尿管相关尿路感染（CAUTI）的发生率有所上升。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Schedule disciplinary meetings with the nurses who cared for the clients who developed infections.","zh":"安排与曾照护发生感染患者的护士进行纪律处分会谈。"},{"id":"C","en":"Purchase a different brand of indwelling catheter kits for the entire unit.","zh":"为整个病区采购另一品牌的留置导尿管套装。"},{"id":"D","en":"Collect and analyze data on current catheter insertion and maintenance practices and compare them with evidence-based guidelines.","zh":"收集并分析当前导尿管置入和维护操作的数据，并将其与循证指南进行比较。"},{"id":"A","en":"Issue a memo informing all staff that the current infection rate is unacceptable and must improve immediately.","zh":"下发通知，告知所有员工当前的感染率不可接受，必须立即改善。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Quality improvement begins by identifying and measuring the problem: gathering objective data on current practices and comparing them against evidence-based standards reveals where the process is breaking down. Only after the gap is understood can the team design and test a targeted intervention. Quality improvement is systems-focused and non-punitive.","rationaleCorrectZh":"质量改进首先要识别和测量问题：收集当前操作的客观数据并与循证标准进行比较，可以揭示流程在何处出现偏差。只有在理解了差距之后，团队才能设计并测试有针对性的干预措施。质量改进以系统为导向，且不带惩罚性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Quality improvement is a systematic, non-punitive process. The first step is always to identify and measure the problem with data before choosing or testing any solution. Eliminate options that punish staff or jump to a fix.","testTakingStrategyZh":"质量改进是一个系统化、非惩罚性的流程。第一步始终是用数据识别和测量问题，然后再选择或测试任何解决方案。排除惩罚员工或直接跳到解决方案的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":64,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_jun05_pharm_pca_opioid_safety_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.48.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[215,336],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,86],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving intravenous morphine through a patient-controlled analgesia (PCA) pump for postoperative pain becomes difficult to arouse, with a respiratory rate of 7 breaths/min and shallow, slow respirations. After stopping the PCA pump and applying supplemental oxygen, which medication should the nurse anticipate administering?","fullStemZh":"一名术后疼痛患者正通过患者自控镇痛（PCA）泵接受静脉注射吗啡，现出现难以唤醒，呼吸频率为 7 次/分，呼吸浅而慢。在停止 PCA 泵并给予吸氧后，护士应预期给予哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"After stopping the PCA pump and applying supplemental oxygen, which medication should the nurse anticipate administering?","terminalSentenceZh":"在停止 PCA 泵并给予吸氧后，护士应预期给予哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receiving intravenous morphine through a patient-controlled analgesia (PCA) pump for postoperative pain becomes difficult to arouse, with a respiratory rate of 7 breaths/min and shallow, slow respirations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名术后疼痛患者正通过患者自控镇痛（PCA）泵接受静脉注射吗啡，现出现难以唤醒，呼吸频率为 7 次/分，呼吸浅而慢。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Protamine sulfate","zh":"硫酸鱼精蛋白"},{"id":"B","en":"Flumazenil","zh":"氟马西尼"},{"id":"C","en":"Naloxone","zh":"纳洛酮"},{"id":"D","en":"Acetylcysteine","zh":"乙酰半胱氨酸"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is showing opioid-induced respiratory depression and sedation from the morphine PCA. Naloxone is the opioid antagonist that reverses these effects. The nurse should titrate it carefully to restore adequate respirations while avoiding acute withdrawal and uncontrolled pain, and continue to monitor because naloxone's duration may be shorter than the opioid's.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者表现为吗啡 PCA 引起的阿片类药物所致呼吸抑制和镇静。纳洛酮是能逆转这些作用的阿片类拮抗剂。护士应谨慎滴定给药以恢复足够的呼吸，同时避免急性戒断和疼痛失控，并持续监测，因为纳洛酮的作用时间可能短于阿片类药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the antidote to the drug class: opioids (morphine) are reversed by naloxone, benzodiazepines by flumazenil, acetaminophen by acetylcysteine, and heparin by protamine. A respiratory rate under 12 with sedation on an opioid signals opioid-induced respiratory depression.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将解毒剂与药物类别相匹配：阿片类（吗啡）用纳洛酮逆转，苯二氮䓬类用氟马西尼，对乙酰氨基酚用乙酰半胱氨酸，肝素用硫酸鱼精蛋白。使用阿片类药物时呼吸频率低于 12 次/分并伴镇静，提示阿片类药物所致呼吸抑制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":65,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_jun05_pharm_clozapine_teaching_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.49","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.49.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.49.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,51],"fullStemEn":"A client with treatment-resistant schizophrenia is starting clozapine. Which instructions should the nurse include in the teaching plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名难治性精神分裂症患者即将开始使用氯氮平。护士应在教学计划中纳入下列哪些指导内容？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include in the teaching plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在教学计划中纳入下列哪些指导内容？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Change positions slowly, since the medication can cause dizziness when you stand up.","zh":"请缓慢改变体位，因为该药物可能在您站起时引起头晕。"},{"id":"C","en":"Report new or worsening constipation, because this medication can cause serious bowel problems.","zh":"如出现新发或加重的便秘，请报告，因为该药物可能导致严重的肠道问题。"},{"id":"F","en":"Routine blood count monitoring can be discontinued after the first month of therapy.","zh":"治疗第一个月后即可停止常规的血细胞计数监测。"},{"id":"B","en":"Keep all appointments for the scheduled blood tests that monitor your white blood cell count.","zh":"请按时完成所有用于监测白细胞计数的预定血液检查预约。"},{"id":"E","en":"You may stop taking the medication on your own once your symptoms improve.","zh":"一旦症状好转，您可以自行停药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Report a sore throat, fever, or other signs of infection to your provider right away.","zh":"如出现咽喉痛、发热或其他感染征象，请立即报告您的医疗服务提供者。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clozapine can cause severe neutropenia/agranulocytosis, so the client must report early signs of infection (sore throat, fever) and adhere to the required ongoing absolute neutrophil count (ANC) monitoring throughout therapy. It also causes serious gastrointestinal hypomotility (severe constipation, possible ileus) and orthostatic hypotension, so the client should report worsening constipation and change positions slowly. The drug must not be stopped abruptly, and monitoring continues for the duration of treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氯氮平可引起严重中性粒细胞减少/粒细胞缺乏症，因此患者必须报告感染的早期征象（咽喉痛、发热），并在整个治疗期间坚持所需的中性粒细胞绝对计数（ANC）持续监测。该药还会引起严重的胃肠动力低下（重度便秘，可能发生肠梗阻）和直立性低血压，因此患者应报告加重的便秘并缓慢改变体位。该药不可骤然停用，且监测须贯穿整个治疗期。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor clozapine teaching to its hallmark risks: agranulocytosis (report infection signs, keep ANC monitoring appointments), severe constipation/ileus, and orthostatic hypotension. Reject any option that stops the drug or its monitoring early.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将氯氮平的宣教锚定于其标志性风险：粒细胞缺乏症（报告感染征象、坚持 ANC 监测预约）、重度便秘/肠梗阻以及直立性低血压。排除任何提前停药或提前停止监测的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":66,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_bcc_rehab_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.50.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[356,499],"terminalOffsetsZh":[88,120],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is completing a Braden Scale assessment for a 72-year-old client admitted to an inpatient rehabilitation unit after a left-hemisphere stroke. The client has right-sided hemiplegia, requires a mechanical lift for all transfers, is incontinent of urine, eats approximately 50% of meals, and reports no discomfort when positioned on bony prominences. For each client finding, indicate whether it places the client at increased risk or does not increase the risk for pressure injury development.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名72岁左侧大脑半球卒中后入住康复科的患者进行Braden量表评估。该患者右侧偏瘫，所有转移均需使用机械升降器，存在尿失禁，每餐进食约50%，当压在骨突时不诉不适。请针对每项患者发现，判断该因素是否增加患者发生压力性损伤的风险。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client finding, indicate whether it places the client at increased risk or does not increase the risk for pressure injury development.","terminalSentenceZh":"请针对每项患者发现，判断该因素是否增加患者发生压力性损伤的风险。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has right-sided hemiplegia, requires a mechanical lift for all transfers, is incontinent of urine, eats approximately 50% of meals, and reports no discomfort when positioned on bony prominences.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者右侧偏瘫，所有转移均需使用机械升降器，存在尿失禁，每餐进食约50%，当压在骨突时不诉不适。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Right-sided hemiplegia requiring mechanical lift","zh":"右侧偏瘫、需要机械升降器转移"},{"id":"r2","en":"Urinary incontinence","zh":"尿失禁"},{"id":"r3","en":"Consuming approximately 50% of meals","zh":"每餐进食约50%"},{"id":"r4","en":"Absence of discomfort sensation over bony prominences","zh":"骨突部位无不适感觉"},{"id":"r5","en":"Age of 72 years","zh":"72岁高龄"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Does not increase risk for pressure injury","zh":"不增加压力性损伤风险"},{"id":"c1","en":"Increased risk for pressure injury","zh":"增加压力性损伤风险"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"All five findings increase the risk for pressure injury. The Braden Scale evaluates sensory perception, moisture, activity, mobility, nutrition, and friction/shear. Hemiplegia severely limits mobility and activity, urinary incontinence creates a moist environment that macerates skin, inadequate nutrition impairs tissue integrity, impaired sensation prevents the client from perceiving early tissue damage, and advanced age is associated with thinner, less elastic skin and slower wound healing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"以上五项发现均增加压力性损伤风险。Braden量表从感觉感知、潮湿度、活动度、移动能力、营养状况及摩擦力/剪切力进行评估。偏瘫严重限制移动和活动能力；尿失禁使皮肤处于潮湿环境中导致浸渍；营养摄入不足损害组织完整性；感觉减退使患者无法感知早期组织损伤；高龄则导致皮肤变薄、弹性下降并延缓伤口愈合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the six Braden Scale subscales—sensory perception, moisture, activity, mobility, nutrition, and friction/shear—and map each client finding to a subscale. Any finding that lowers a subscale score increases overall risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆Braden量表六个子量表——感觉感知、潮湿度、活动度、移动能力、营养状况、摩擦力/剪切力——将每项患者发现与子量表对应。任何降低子量表评分的发现都会增加总体风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client has right-sided hemiplegia, requires a mechanical lift for all transfers, is incontinent of urine, eats approximately 50% of meals, and reports no discomfort when positioned on bony prominences.","controlSentenceZh":"该患者右侧偏瘫，所有转移均需使用机械升降器，存在尿失禁，每餐进食约50%，当压在骨突时不诉不适。"}
{"queueIndex":67,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_bcc_rehab_2026_06_10_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.51","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.51.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.51.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,69],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is developing a pressure injury prevention plan for a rehabilitation client who is wheelchair-bound for 8 hours per day and has a Braden Scale score of 14. Complete the following sentences by selecting the correct option from each dropdown.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名每日坐轮椅8小时、Braden量表评分14分的康复患者制定压力性损伤预防计划。请从每个下拉菜单中选择正确选项以完成以下句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the following sentences by selecting the correct option from each dropdown.","terminalSentenceZh":"请从每个下拉菜单中选择正确选项以完成以下句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is developing a pressure injury prevention plan for a rehabilitation client who is wheelchair-bound for 8 hours per day and has a Braden Scale score of 14.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名每日坐轮椅8小时、Braden量表评分14分的康复患者制定压力性损伤预防计划。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client's Braden Scale score of 14 indicates the client is at {{1}} risk for pressure injury. While seated in the wheelchair, the client should perform weight shifts at least every {{2}}. The most appropriate support surface for this client's wheelchair is a {{3}}.","zh":"该患者Braden量表评分为14分，表明其压力性损伤风险等级为{{1}}。坐在轮椅上时，患者应至少每{{2}}进行一次重心转移减压。该患者轮椅上最合适的支撑面为{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"1c","en":"high","zh":"高度"},{"id":"1b","en":"moderate","zh":"中度"},{"id":"1d","en":"very high","zh":"极高度"},{"id":"1a","en":"low","zh":"低度"}],"correct":"1b"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"2a","en":"15 minutes","zh":"15分钟"},{"id":"2b","en":"30 minutes","zh":"30分钟"},{"id":"2c","en":"1 hour","zh":"1小时"},{"id":"2d","en":"2 hours","zh":"2小时"}],"correct":"2a"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"3c","en":"folded bath blanket","zh":"折叠浴毯"},{"id":"3d","en":"standard vinyl wheelchair seat","zh":"标准乙烯基轮椅座面"},{"id":"3a","en":"foam ring (donut) cushion","zh":"环形泡沫垫（甜甜圈垫）"},{"id":"3b","en":"pressure-redistributing gel or air cushion","zh":"压力再分配凝胶或气垫"}],"correct":"3b"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A Braden Scale score of 14 places the client at moderate risk (scores 13–14). Evidence-based guidelines recommend wheelchair-bound clients perform weight shifts every 15 minutes to relieve ischial pressure. A pressure-redistributing gel or air cushion is the standard of care for wheelchair seating to distribute pressure away from bony prominences.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Braden量表14分属于中度风险（13–14分）。循证指南建议坐轮椅的患者每15分钟进行一次重心转移以减轻坐骨压力。压力再分配凝胶或气垫是轮椅座椅的标准配置，能将压力从骨突部位分散开来。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the Braden Scale risk thresholds and match prevention interventions to the level of risk. Remember that ring cushions are always contraindicated because they concentrate pressure along their edges.","testTakingStrategyZh":"牢记Braden量表各风险阈值，并将预防措施与风险等级匹配。注意环形垫因将压力集中于边缘始终属于禁忌。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":68,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_bcc_rehab_2026_06_10_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.52.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[187,263],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,70],"fullStemEn":"A rehabilitation nurse is providing perineal skin care to a client who has urinary incontinence and is at risk for incontinence-associated dermatitis (IAD) and secondary pressure injury. Place the following nursing actions in the correct order from first to last.","fullStemZh":"康复科护士正在为一名有尿失禁且面临失禁相关性皮炎（IAD）及继发压力性损伤风险的患者进行会阴皮肤护理。请将以下护理操作按正确的先后顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct order from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将以下护理操作按正确的先后顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A rehabilitation nurse is providing perineal skin care to a client who has urinary incontinence and is at risk for incontinence-associated dermatitis (IAD) and secondary pressure injury.","penultimateSentenceZh":"康复科护士正在为一名有尿失禁且面临失禁相关性皮炎（IAD）及继发压力性损伤风险的患者进行会阴皮肤护理。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Pat the skin completely dry with a soft cloth — do not rub","zh":"用柔软布料将皮肤轻拍至完全干燥，不可摩擦"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove the soiled incontinence brief, gently remove excess urine from the skin, and cleanse the perineal skin with a pH-balanced, no-rinse incontinence cleanser","zh":"去除污染的失禁垫，轻柔地擦去皮肤上多余的尿液，并使用pH平衡的免冲洗失禁专用清洁剂清洗会阴皮肤"},{"id":"E","en":"Inspect the perineal skin for signs of erythema, erosion, or fungal infection","zh":"检查会阴皮肤有无红斑、糜烂或真菌感染征象"},{"id":"F","en":"Apply a clean, appropriately sized incontinence brief and document skin assessment findings","zh":"更换清洁且大小合适的失禁垫，并记录皮肤评估结果"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply a moisture-barrier cream or dimethicone-based skin protectant to intact skin","zh":"在完整皮肤上涂抹防潮隔离霜或含二甲硅油的皮肤保护剂"}],"correct":["A","C","E","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence follows evidence-based incontinence skin care: first remove the soiled brief, blot excess urine, and cleanse with a gentle pH-balanced no-rinse cleanser; pat dry without rubbing to avoid friction injury; inspect the skin to identify any existing damage that would change the plan of care; apply a moisture-barrier protectant to intact skin; and finally apply a clean brief and document findings. Inspection must occur after the skin is clean and dry so findings are accurate; the barrier cream is applied only after confirming intact skin.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确顺序遵循循证失禁皮肤护理流程：先去除污染垫、擦去多余尿液并使用pH平衡的免冲洗清洁剂清洗，轻拍干燥避免摩擦损伤，随后检查皮肤以识别已有损伤从而调整护理方案，确认皮肤完整后涂抹防潮保护剂，最后更换清洁失禁垫并记录评估结果。检查须在皮肤清洁干燥后进行以确保准确；隔离霜仅在确认皮肤完整后使用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of the logical flow: remove contamination and cleanse (one unit), dry, assess, protect, then document. Assessment comes after cleaning so findings are accurate, and the barrier product is applied only after confirming the skin is intact.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按逻辑流程思考：去除污染并清洗（视为一个整体步骤），干燥，评估，保护，最后记录。评估在清洗干燥后进行以保证准确，保护产品须在确认皮肤完整后方可使用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":69,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_bcc_rehab_2026_06_10_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.53","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.53.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.53.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[309,343],"terminalOffsetsZh":[71,100],"fullStemEn":"A rehabilitation client weighs 176 lb (80 kg) and has a Stage 2 pressure injury on the sacrum. The dietitian recommends a high-protein diet providing 1.5 g of protein per kilogram of body weight per day to support wound healing. Calculate the total daily protein requirement for this client in grams per day. Round to the nearest whole number.","fullStemZh":"一名康复患者体重176磅（80公斤），骶部有II期压力性损伤。营养师建议给予高蛋白饮食，每日蛋白质摄入量为每公斤体重1.5克，以促进伤口愈合。请计算该患者每日所需蛋白质总量（克/日），四舍五入至整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算该患者每日所需蛋白质总量（克/日），四舍五入至整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the total daily protein requirement for this client in grams per day.","penultimateSentenceZh":"营养师建议给予高蛋白饮食，每日蛋白质摄入量为每公斤体重1.5克，以促进伤口愈合。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Total daily protein requirement (g/day):","zh":"每日蛋白质总需求量（克/日）："},"acceptable":["120","120 g","120 g/day"],"numeric":{"value":120,"tolerance":0,"unit":"g/day"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The calculation is: 80 kg × 1.5 g/kg/day = 120 g/day. Clients with existing pressure injuries require 1.25–1.5 g/kg/day of protein (some guidelines recommend up to 2 g/kg/day for Stage 3–4 injuries). Adequate protein is essential for collagen synthesis, immune function, and granulation tissue formation during wound healing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算过程：80 kg × 1.5 g/kg/day = 120 g/day。已有压力性损伤的患者每日蛋白质需求为1.25–1.5 g/kg（III–IV期损伤部分指南建议可达2 g/kg/day）。充足的蛋白质对胶原合成、免疫功能和肉芽组织形成至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Confirm the weight is in kilograms before multiplying. If given in pounds, divide by 2.2 first. Then multiply weight in kg by the prescribed protein factor. Double-check that 80 × 1.5 = 120.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算前确认体重单位为公斤。若给出磅数，先除以2.2换算。然后将公斤体重乘以规定的蛋白质系数。复核80 × 1.5 = 120。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":70,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_bcc_rehab_2026_06_10_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.54.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,64],"fullStemEn":"A nurse on a rehabilitation unit is evaluating the safe use of assistive devices by four different clients. For each client scenario, determine whether the nurse should intervene (the action is unsafe) or allow the action to continue (the action is safe).","fullStemZh":"康复科护士正在评估四位患者使用辅助器具的安全性。请针对每个患者情境，判断护士是否需要干预（操作不安全）还是允许继续（操作安全）。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client scenario, determine whether the nurse should intervene (the action is unsafe) or allow the action to continue (the action is safe).","terminalSentenceZh":"请针对每个患者情境，判断护士是否需要干预（操作不安全）还是允许继续（操作安全）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse on a rehabilitation unit is evaluating the safe use of assistive devices by four different clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"康复科护士正在评估四位患者使用辅助器具的安全性。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"A client with left-leg weakness advances the walker, then steps forward with the right (strong) leg first","zh":"左下肢无力的患者先移动助行器，然后右侧（健侧）腿先迈步"},{"id":"r2","en":"A client using a single-point cane holds it in the hand opposite to the affected leg","zh":"使用单点手杖的患者用患肢对侧手握持手杖"},{"id":"r3","en":"A client with right-hip arthroplasty sits in a standard low chair with the hips flexed beyond 90 degrees","zh":"右侧全髋关节置换术后患者坐在标准低矮椅子上，髋关节屈曲超过90度"},{"id":"r4","en":"A client ascends stairs by leading with the stronger leg while holding the handrail and cane","zh":"患者上楼梯时健侧腿先上，同时扶扶手和持手杖"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Allow to continue (safe action)","zh":"允许继续（安全操作）"},{"id":"c1","en":"Intervene (unsafe action)","zh":"需干预（不安全操作）"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client with left-leg weakness should advance the weaker (left) leg first after moving the walker to keep the stronger leg as the stable base of support, so stepping with the strong leg first is incorrect and requires intervention. Holding a cane on the opposite side of the affected leg is the standard technique that widens the base of support and promotes a normal gait pattern. Sitting with hips flexed beyond 90 degrees violates total hip arthroplasty precautions and risks posterior dislocation. The rule for stairs is 'up with the good, down with the bad,' so leading with the stronger leg going upstairs is correct.","rationaleCorrectZh":"左下肢无力患者移动助行器后应先迈患侧（左腿），让健侧腿作为稳定支撑，因此先迈健侧腿是错误的，需要干预。手杖持于患肢对侧是标准用法，可扩大支撑面并促进正常步态。髋关节屈曲超过90度违反全髋关节置换术后注意事项，有后脱位风险。上下楼口诀为“好腿先上、坏腿先下”，因此健腿先上楼是正确的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember two key rules: with a walker, the weak leg advances first; for stairs, 'up with the good, down with the bad.' For hip arthroplasty, recall the three movements to avoid: flexion >90°, adduction past midline, and internal rotation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住两条关键规则：使用助行器时患肢先行；上下楼遵循“好腿先上、坏腿先下”。全髋置换后记住三个禁忌动作：屈曲>90°、内收超过中线、内旋。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":71,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_bcc_rehab_2026_06_10_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.55","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.55.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.55.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,287],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,74],"fullStemEn":"A rehabilitation nurse is evaluating the healing progress of a client's sacral pressure injury over a 4-week period. Arrange the following wound assessment findings in the order that indicates progressive healing from earliest sign of improvement (first) to most advanced healing (last).","fullStemZh":"康复科护士正在评估一名患者骶部压力性损伤在4周内的愈合进展。请将以下伤口评估发现按照从最早出现的愈合迹象（最先）到愈合最成熟的阶段（最后）依次排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the following wound assessment findings in the order that indicates progressive healing from earliest sign of improvement (first) to most advanced healing (last).","terminalSentenceZh":"请将以下伤口评估发现按照从最早出现的愈合迹象（最先）到愈合最成熟的阶段（最后）依次排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A rehabilitation nurse is evaluating the healing progress of a client's sacral pressure injury over a 4-week period.","penultimateSentenceZh":"康复科护士正在评估一名患者骶部压力性损伤在4周内的愈合进展。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Necrotic tissue loosens and separates from the wound bed through autolytic debridement","zh":"坏死组织通过自溶性清创从伤口基底松动脱落"},{"id":"C","en":"Pink epithelial tissue migrates inward from wound margins","zh":"粉红色上皮组织从伤口边缘向中心迁移"},{"id":"B","en":"Inflammatory exudate decreases and wound base transitions from yellow slough to red granulation tissue","zh":"炎性渗出减少，伤口基底由黄色腐肉转变为红色肉芽组织"},{"id":"A","en":"Wound edges contract and wound dimensions decrease measurably","zh":"伤口边缘收缩，伤口面积可测量地缩小"},{"id":"E","en":"Wound fully resurfaces with new epithelium; scar tissue matures and remodels","zh":"伤口完全被新生上皮覆盖，瘢痕组织成熟并重塑"}],"correct":["D","B","A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Wound healing follows a predictable sequence: during the inflammatory/debridement phase, necrotic tissue must first separate and be removed to prepare the wound bed; as the proliferative phase begins, slough clears and healthy red granulation tissue fills the wound bed; wound contraction then draws the edges closer together, reducing the wound size; epithelial cells migrate from the wound margins across the granulation tissue to resurface the wound; finally, in the maturation/remodeling phase, epithelial coverage is complete and the underlying collagen scar matures and strengthens over weeks to months.","rationaleCorrectZh":"伤口愈合遵循可预测的顺序：炎症/清创期坏死组织首先松动脱落以准备伤口基底；进入增殖期后腐肉清除，健康红色肉芽组织填充伤口基底；伤口收缩使边缘靠拢，面积缩小；上皮细胞从伤口边缘沿肉芽组织向中心迁移覆盖伤口表面；最终进入成熟/重塑期，上皮完全覆盖，深层胶原瘢痕在数周至数月内成熟增强。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the wound healing phases in order: hemostasis → inflammation/debridement → proliferation (granulation, contraction, epithelialization) → maturation/remodeling. Match each assessment finding to its phase to determine the correct sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按顺序记忆伤口愈合阶段：止血→炎症/清创→增殖（肉芽形成、伤口收缩、上皮化）→成熟/重塑。将每项评估发现与其所属阶段对应，即可确定正确顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":72,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.56","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.56.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[714,762],"terminalOffsetsZh":[181,195],"fullStemEn":"Caregiver Burden in a Spouse Caring for a Partner with Advanced Parkinson Disease Mrs. Linda Chen, 67 years old, is the sole family caregiver for her 72-year-old husband, Mr. Wei Chen, who was diagnosed with Parkinson disease 9 years ago. Mr. Chen's disease has progressed to advanced Parkinson disease: he uses a wheelchair for most mobility, has frequent freezing episodes and falls, experiences dysphagia requiring a mechanically altered diet, and has mild cognitive impairment with visual hallucinations managed with low-dose quetiapine. The couple lives alone; their adult daughter lives 3 hours away and visits monthly. Mrs. Chen retired early from her teaching career 4 years ago to provide full-time care. The home health nurse is making a routine visit.","fullStemZh":"照顾晚期帕金森病配偶的照护者负担 陈林达女士，67岁，是其72岁丈夫陈伟先生的唯一家庭照护者。陈先生9年前确诊帕金森病，目前已进展为晚期帕金森病：多数移动需使用轮椅，频繁出现冻结步态和跌倒，吞咽困难需进食质地改良饮食，伴轻度认知障碍和视幻觉（小剂量喹硫平控制）。夫妇二人独居，成年女儿住在3小时车程外，每月探望一次。陈女士4年前提前从教师岗位退休以全职照护丈夫。居家护理护士正进行常规家访。","terminalSentenceEn":"The home health nurse is making a routine visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"居家护理护士正进行常规家访。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Chen retired early from her teaching career 4 years ago to provide full-time care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"陈女士4年前提前从教师岗位退休以全职照护丈夫。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows the NCJMM sequence through the experience of a primary family caregiver showing progressive signs of caregiver role strain. The nurse must recognize verbal and nonverbal cues of burden, analyze contributing psychosocial factors, prioritize the most pressing concerns, generate solutions including respite care and community referrals, select therapeutic communication responses, and evaluate the effectiveness of interventions over time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例按照NCJMM序列展开，围绕一位出现渐进性照护者角色压力的主要家庭照护者。护士需识别负担的语言和非语言线索，分析促成因素，确定最紧迫的问题优先级，提出包括喘息服务和社区转介在内的解决方案，选择治疗性沟通回应，并随时间评价干预效果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Approach each embedded question by identifying where it falls in the clinical judgment sequence. Recognize cues first, then analyze their meaning, before jumping to solutions. Remember that therapeutic communication validates feelings before offering advice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"解答每道嵌套题时先判断它对应临床判断序列的哪个阶段。先识别线索、再分析其含义，然后才提出解决方案。记住治疗性沟通应先认可感受，再给建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":73,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01a","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Based on the case exhibits, identify whether each finding is a cue relevant to caregiver role strain or a finding not directly relevant to caregiver role strain.","fullStemZh":"根据病例资料，判断每项发现是否为与照护者角色压力直接相关的线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the case exhibits, identify whether each finding is a cue relevant to caregiver role strain or a finding not directly relevant to caregiver role strain.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据病例资料，判断每项发现是否为与照护者角色压力直接相关的线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Mrs. Chen reports sleeping only 3–4 hours per night","zh":"陈女士报告每晚只睡3–4小时"},{"id":"r2","en":"Medication organizer is filled correctly for the week","zh":"分药盒本周药物分装正确"},{"id":"r3","en":"Mrs. Chen winces during transfers and reports back pain but has not sought medical care","zh":"陈女士转移患者时面露痛苦、报告腰痛但未就医"},{"id":"r4","en":"Mrs. Chen withdrew from her support group and has lost social connections","zh":"陈女士退出了互助小组并失去了社交联系"},{"id":"r5","en":"Mr. Chen is clean, well-dressed, and well-nourished","zh":"陈先生清洁、穿着得体、营养状况良好"},{"id":"r6","en":"Mrs. Chen expresses fear of making a medication error or dropping her husband","zh":"陈女士表达了对自己弄错药物或摔倒丈夫的恐惧"},{"id":"r7","en":"Unwashed dishes and unopened mail are accumulating in the home","zh":"家中堆积未洗的碗碟和未拆的信件"},{"id":"r8","en":"Grab bars are installed in the bathroom","zh":"卫生间已安装扶手"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Cue relevant to caregiver role strain","zh":"与照护者角色压力相关的线索"},{"id":"c2","en":"Finding not directly relevant to caregiver role strain","zh":"与照护者角色压力无直接关联的发现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r7","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r8","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Chronic sleep deprivation, neglect of one's own health, social isolation, fear of caregiving errors, and declining self-care (evidenced by household deterioration and unchanged clothing) are classic cues of caregiver role strain. The correctly filled medication organizer, Mr. Chen's good condition, and bathroom grab bars reflect adequate care of the patient and appropriate environmental modifications — they do not directly indicate caregiver burden.","rationaleCorrectZh":"慢性睡眠剥夺、忽视自身健康、社交孤立、对护理失误的恐惧以及自我照顾能力下降（表现为家务荒废和衣物未换）都是照护者角色压力的经典线索。分药盒正确分装、陈先生状况良好以及卫生间扶手反映了对患者的充分照护和适当环境改造，并不直接指向照护者负担。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between cues about the caregiver's own well-being versus findings about the patient's care quality or the home environment setup. Caregiver strain cues focus on the caregiver's physical health, emotional state, social functioning, and self-care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分关于照护者自身状况的线索与关于患者护理质量或家庭环境设置的发现。照护者压力线索聚焦于照护者的身体健康、情绪状态、社会功能和自我照顾。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":74,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01b","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is analyzing the factors that contribute most to Mrs. Chen's caregiver burden. Complete the following clinical analysis by selecting the correct option from each dropdown.","fullStemZh":"护士正在分析对陈女士照护者负担影响最大的因素。请从每个下拉菜单中选择正确选项以完成以下临床分析。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the following clinical analysis by selecting the correct option from each dropdown.","terminalSentenceZh":"请从每个下拉菜单中选择正确选项以完成以下临床分析。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Chen's caregiver burden.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在分析对陈女士照护者负担影响最大的因素。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Mrs. Chen's Zarit Burden Interview score of 34 indicates {{1}} burden. The factor most likely contributing to her sleep deprivation is {{2}}. Her statement 'I feel like I'm disappearing' most closely reflects the psychosocial concept of {{3}}.","zh":"陈女士Zarit照护者负担量表得分34分，表明其负担程度为{{1}}。最可能导致她睡眠剥夺的因素是{{2}}。她说「我觉得自己在消失」最贴切地反映了{{3}}这一心理社会概念。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"1a","en":"little or no","zh":"几乎无"},{"id":"1c","en":"high","zh":"高"},{"id":"1b","en":"mild to moderate","zh":"轻至中度"},{"id":"1d","en":"moderate-to-severe category","zh":"中至重度类别"}],"correct":"1c"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"2d","en":"The daughter's infrequent visits","zh":"女儿探望不频繁"},{"id":"2b","en":"Mr. Chen's nocturnal confusion and attempts to get out of bed","zh":"陈先生夜间意识混乱和试图下床"},{"id":"2c","en":"Mrs. Chen's unresolved back pain","zh":"陈女士未处理的腰痛"},{"id":"2a","en":"Mr. Chen's dysphagia requiring dietary modifications","zh":"陈先生吞咽困难需要饮食调整"}],"correct":"2b"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"3d","en":"learned helplessness","zh":"习得性无助"},{"id":"3b","en":"loss of personal identity and role engulfment","zh":"个人身份丧失与角色吞没"},{"id":"3a","en":"anticipatory grieving","zh":"预期性悲伤"},{"id":"3c","en":"codependency","zh":"共依存"}],"correct":"3b"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A Zarit score of 34 on the 12-item Zarit Burden Interview falls in the high burden range (>20; 21–48 in this exhibit). Nocturnal confusion with attempts to get out of bed is the direct cause of Mrs. Chen's sleep interruption, as she explicitly describes waiting for the bed alarm and sleeping only 3–4 hours. The metaphor of 'disappearing' reflects loss of personal identity and role engulfment — the caregiver's own identity, interests, and social roles are progressively consumed by the caregiving role until the person feels they no longer exist as an individual.","rationaleCorrectZh":"12项Zarit量表34分属于高负担范围（>20分；本病例资料中列为21–48分）。夜间意识混乱伴试图下床是导致陈女士睡眠中断的直接原因，她明确描述了等待床边报警器响起、每晚仅睡3–4小时的情况。「消失」的比喻反映了个人身份丧失与角色吞没——照护者的个人身份、兴趣和社会角色被照护角色逐步吞噬，直到感觉自己不再作为独立个体存在。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the client's own words to psychosocial concepts. 'Disappearing' is about the self ceasing to exist — that maps to identity loss, not grief or helplessness. For contributing factors, trace the chain of cause and effect directly from the interview data.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将患者自己的用词与心理社会概念对应。「消失」说的是自我不复存在——指向身份丧失，而非悲伤或无助。分析促成因素时，从访谈数据中直接追溯因果链。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":75,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01c","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,179],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse has identified multiple concerns for Mrs. Chen. Rank the following nursing priorities from highest (first) to lowest (last) based on the urgency of the identified needs.","fullStemZh":"护士已识别出陈女士的多个问题。请根据需求的紧迫程度，将以下护理优先事项从最高（最先）到最低（最后）排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Rank the following nursing priorities from highest (first) to lowest (last) based on the urgency of the identified needs.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据需求的紧迫程度，将以下护理优先事项从最高（最先）到最低（最后）排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Chen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士已识别出陈女士的多个问题。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Explore options for nighttime respite or supervision to restore Mrs. Chen's sleep","zh":"探讨夜间喘息服务或看护方案以恢复陈女士的睡眠"},{"id":"B","en":"Facilitate evaluation and treatment for Mrs. Chen's chronic back pain","zh":"协助陈女士进行腰痛的诊疗"},{"id":"D","en":"Re-engage Mrs. Chen in social support networks and the caregiver support group","zh":"帮助陈女士重新建立社交支持网络并回归照护者互助小组"},{"id":"E","en":"Discuss long-term care planning and community resources with Mrs. Chen and her daughter","zh":"与陈女士及其女儿讨论长期照护规划和社区资源"},{"id":"A","en":"Address Mrs. Chen's safety concern about potential medication errors and unsafe transfers due to exhaustion","zh":"针对陈女士因疲惫可能导致的用药错误和不安全转移进行安全干预"}],"correct":["A","C","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety is always the highest priority: Mrs. Chen has identified a real risk of medication errors and unsafe transfers that could directly harm Mr. Chen. Next, addressing the root cause of her exhaustion — nocturnal caregiving without relief — is essential because sleep deprivation compounds every other problem. Her own untreated back pain is the third priority because it affects her physical ability to provide safe care and will worsen without treatment. Social reconnection addresses emotional well-being and is important but less immediately urgent. Long-term planning is critical for sustainability but is appropriately addressed after acute safety and health needs are stabilized.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全始终是最高优先级：陈女士已识别出可能直接伤害陈先生的用药错误和不安全转移风险。其次应解决疲惫的根本原因——无人替代的夜间照护，因为睡眠剥夺会加重所有其他问题。她自身未治疗的腰痛排第三，因其影响安全照护的体力能力且会持续恶化。社交重建关乎情感健康，重要但紧迫性稍低。长期规划对可持续性至关重要，但适合在急性安全和健康需求稳定后再着手。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply Maslow's hierarchy: safety first, then physiological needs (sleep, pain), then love/belonging (social support), then long-term planning. When a caregiver's exhaustion creates a direct safety risk for the patient, that becomes the top priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"运用Maslow需求层次：安全为先，然后是生理需求（睡眠、疼痛），再是爱与归属（社会支持），最后是长期规划。当照护者的疲惫直接威胁患者安全时，它就成为最高优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":76,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01d","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,70],"fullStemEn":"During the visit, Mrs. Chen becomes tearful and says, 'I know I should ask for help, but I feel like I'm failing him if I can't do this alone.' Select the most therapeutic nurse response for each part of the interaction.","fullStemZh":"家访过程中，陈女士泪流满面地说：「我知道应该寻求帮助，但如果我一个人做不到，我觉得是在辜负他。」请为互动的每个部分选择最具治疗性的护士回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the most therapeutic nurse response for each part of the interaction.","terminalSentenceZh":"请为互动的每个部分选择最具治疗性的护士回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Chen becomes tearful and says, 'I know I should ask for help, but I feel like I'm failing him if I can't do this alone.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"家访过程中，陈女士泪流满面地说：「我知道应该寻求帮助，但如果我一个人做不到，我觉得是在辜负他。」","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's most appropriate initial response is: {{1}}. After Mrs. Chen expresses her feelings further, the nurse should then {{2}}.","zh":"护士最恰当的初始回应是：{{1}}。在陈女士进一步表达感受后，护士应当{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"1c","en":"\"Have you considered that accepting help would actually be better for your husband's safety?\"","zh":"「您有没有想过，接受帮助其实对您丈夫的安全更有利？」"},{"id":"1b","en":"\"Caring for someone you love this much is incredibly demanding. It sounds like you're carrying a heavy weight and it's taking a toll on you.\"","zh":"「照顾一个您如此深爱的人是非常艰辛的。听起来您承受着很大的压力，这正在消耗您自己。」"},{"id":"1a","en":"\"You shouldn't feel guilty — you're doing an amazing job and he's lucky to have you.\"","zh":"「您不应该有负疚感——您做得非常好，他有您是他的福气。」"},{"id":"1d","en":"\"Many caregivers feel the way you do. Let me give you some brochures about respite services.\"","zh":"「很多照护者都有和您一样的感受。我给您一些喘息服务的宣传册吧。」"}],"correct":"1b"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"2a","en":"reframe seeking help as an act of strength by saying, \"Accepting support is not failing — it's making sure you can continue to be there for Wei safely and for a long time.\"","zh":"将寻求帮助重新定义为力量的表现：「接受支持不是失败——而是确保您能安全地、长久地陪伴老伟。」"},{"id":"2c","en":"advise Mrs. Chen to call her daughter and insist on more frequent visits","zh":"建议陈女士打电话给女儿，要求女儿更频繁地探望"},{"id":"2d","en":"tell Mrs. Chen that if she does not accept help, the nurse may need to report the situation as caregiver neglect","zh":"告诉陈女士如果她不接受帮助，护士可能需要将此情况作为照护者疏忽进行上报"},{"id":"2b","en":"change the subject to discuss Mr. Chen's medication schedule to reduce Mrs. Chen's emotional distress","zh":"转换话题讨论陈先生的用药安排，以减轻陈女士的情绪困扰"}],"correct":"2a"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The therapeutic sequence is to first validate the caregiver's feelings with empathy before offering reframing or solutions. Option 1b uses reflective listening and empathic acknowledgment without dismissing the guilt or rushing to fix the problem. After feelings are validated, option 2a gently reframes help-seeking as a means to sustain caregiving — addressing the guilt directly while respecting Mrs. Chen's autonomy and devotion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性沟通的顺序是先以共情方式认可照护者的感受，然后再提供重新框架或解决方案。选项1b运用了反映性倾听和共情认可，未否定内疚感或急于解决问题。在感受被认可后，选项2a温和地将寻求帮助重新定义为维持照护能力的方式——直接回应内疚感同时尊重陈女士的自主性和奉献精神。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In therapeutic communication questions, always choose the response that acknowledges feelings first. Eliminate options that use false reassurance, give directive advice, change the subject, or use threats. After validation, look for responses that empower the client rather than dictate actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在治疗性沟通题目中，始终选择先认可感受的回应。排除使用虚假保证、给出指令性建议、转换话题或使用威胁的选项。在认可感受后，选择赋权而非指令性的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":77,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01e","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[68,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,41],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is developing a comprehensive support plan for Mrs. Chen. For each proposed intervention, determine whether it is an appropriate or inappropriate action for the nurse to include in the plan at this time.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为陈女士制定综合支持计划。请判断以下每项拟议干预措施目前是否适合纳入计划。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each proposed intervention, determine whether it is an appropriate or inappropriate action for the nurse to include in the plan at this time.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断以下每项拟议干预措施目前是否适合纳入计划。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Chen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为陈女士制定综合支持计划。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Refer to a social worker or case manager to explore payer and community resources for expanded home aide or respite hours","zh":"转介社工或个案管理师，以了解可增加居家护理员或喘息服务时数的支付和社区资源"},{"id":"r2","en":"Arrange a nighttime home health aide or overnight respite volunteer to address sleep deprivation","zh":"安排夜间居家护理员或通宵喘息志愿者以改善睡眠剥夺"},{"id":"r3","en":"Recommend Mrs. Chen place Mr. Chen in a long-term care facility immediately","zh":"建议陈女士立即将陈先生送入长期照护机构"},{"id":"r4","en":"Train the home health aide on managing Parkinson freezing episodes so Mrs. Chen can step away with confidence","zh":"培训居家护理员如何处理帕金森冻结步态，使陈女士能放心离开"},{"id":"r5","en":"Schedule a telehealth appointment for Mrs. Chen's back pain to eliminate the barrier of leaving Mr. Chen","zh":"为陈女士安排远程医疗就诊治疗腰痛，消除无法离开陈先生的障碍"},{"id":"r6","en":"Contact the daughter without Mrs. Chen's consent to demand she provide more caregiving support","zh":"未经陈女士同意联系其女儿，要求女儿提供更多照护支持"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate intervention","zh":"不适当的干预措施"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate intervention","zh":"适当的干预措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate interventions address identified needs while respecting Mrs. Chen's autonomy, values, and stated preference to keep her husband at home. Social work or case management referral for payer and community-resource assistance, nighttime respite to address sleep deprivation, aide training to build trust in delegated care, and telehealth for her own health barrier are all client-centered and practical. Recommending immediate facility placement disregards Mrs. Chen's clearly expressed wishes and values; contacting the daughter without consent violates patient confidentiality and the caregiver's autonomy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当的干预措施在尊重陈女士自主权、价值观和希望丈夫居家照护意愿的同时解决已识别的需求。社工或个案管理转介以获得支付和社区资源援助、夜间喘息服务以解决睡眠剥夺、护理员培训以建立委托照护的信任、以及远程医疗解决就医障碍均以患者为中心且切实可行。建议立即送入机构无视陈女士明确表达的意愿和价值观；未经同意联系女儿违反保密原则和照护者自主权。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate each intervention against three criteria: (1) Does it address an identified need from the assessment? (2) Does it respect the client's autonomy and stated values? (3) Does it fall within the nurse's legal and ethical scope? Interventions that violate autonomy or confidentiality are inappropriate regardless of good intent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按三项标准评判每项干预：（1）是否针对评估中识别的需求？（2）是否尊重患者自主权和明确表达的价值观？（3）是否在护士法律和伦理执业范围内？即使出于善意，违反自主权或保密原则的干预也是不适当的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":78,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_psi_caregiver_2026_06_10_01f","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,43],"fullStemEn":"Two weeks after implementing the support plan, the nurse conducts a follow-up visit. For each finding, determine whether it indicates the interventions are effective or whether the finding requires further intervention.","fullStemZh":"在实施支持计划两周后，护士进行随访。请判断每项发现是表明干预有效，还是需要进一步干预。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, determine whether it indicates the interventions are effective or whether the finding requires further intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是表明干预有效，还是需要进一步干预。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two weeks after implementing the support plan, the nurse conducts a follow-up visit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在实施支持计划两周后，护士进行随访。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Mrs. Chen reports sleeping 6–7 hours per night since a trained overnight aide began three nights per week","zh":"陈女士报告自从每周三晚有受过培训的通宵护理员以来，每晚可睡6–7小时"},{"id":"r2","en":"Mrs. Chen attended one caregiver support group meeting but says, 'It was okay, but I kept checking my phone the whole time'","zh":"陈女士参加了一次照护者互助小组会议，但表示「还行，不过我全程一直在看手机」"},{"id":"r3","en":"The telehealth provider prescribed physical therapy for Mrs. Chen's back pain, but she has not scheduled the first appointment","zh":"远程医疗医生为陈女士的腰痛开具了物理治疗处方，但她尚未预约首次就诊"},{"id":"r4","en":"Mrs. Chen's Zarit Burden Interview score has decreased from 34 to 27","zh":"陈女士的Zarit负担量表评分从34分降至27分"},{"id":"r5","en":"Mrs. Chen states, 'I still feel guilty when the aide is here, but I know Wei is safe and I actually ate dinner sitting down last night'","zh":"陈女士说：「护理员在时我还是有负疚感，但我知道老伟是安全的，昨晚我终于坐下来好好吃了顿晚饭。」"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Intervention effective","zh":"干预有效"},{"id":"c2","en":"Requires further intervention","zh":"需要进一步干预"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Improvement in sleep duration from 3–4 hours to 6–7 hours demonstrates effective nighttime respite. The Zarit score decrease from 34 to 27 shows measurable burden reduction, although both scores remain in the high-burden range for the 12-item short form. Mrs. Chen's statement about eating dinner sitting down — while acknowledging residual guilt — shows emerging self-care behavior and growing trust in the aide, indicating positive progress. However, constant phone-checking at the support group suggests persistent separation anxiety that limits the benefit of social re-engagement. Failure to schedule physical therapy indicates a continuing barrier to self-care that needs to be explored and addressed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"睡眠时间从3–4小时增加至6–7小时表明夜间喘息服务有效。Zarit评分从34分降至27分显示负担有可测量的减轻，但按12项简版评分两者仍属于高负担范围。陈女士关于坐下来吃晚饭的陈述——虽然承认仍有内疚——显示自我照顾行为正在恢复、对护理员的信任在增长，表明积极进展。然而在互助小组全程看手机提示分离焦虑持续存在，限制了社交重建的效果。未预约物理治疗说明自我照顾的障碍仍在，需进一步探讨和解决。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When evaluating outcomes, compare each finding against the baseline data from the initial assessment. Look for measurable changes (e.g., sleep hours, Zarit score) and qualitative shifts in the client's statements. Partial progress still counts as effective if the trend is positive; however, when a prescribed action has not been initiated at all, further intervention is needed regardless of other improvements.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果时，将每项发现与初始评估的基线数据对比。关注可测量的变化（如睡眠时数、Zarit评分）和患者陈述中的质性转变。如果趋势积极，部分进步仍视为有效；但若处方措施完全未启动，则无论其他方面是否改善都需要进一步干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":79,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.57","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.57.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[942,973],"terminalOffsetsZh":[301,335],"fullStemEn":"Advance directive clarification and code status escalation in metastatic lung cancer with acute respiratory decline. Mr. Harold Jeffries is a 55-year-old man admitted five days ago to a medical-surgical unit with progressive dyspnea and right-sided pleural effusion secondary to metastatic non-small cell lung cancer (stage IV). He is receiving palliative carboplatin-based chemotherapy. Current orders include supplemental oxygen via nasal cannula titrated to maintain SpO₂ > 92%. The attending is a pulmonologist currently in the OR; the covering provider is a hospitalist. The medical record contains no advance directive, POLST, or healthcare power of attorney. The code status is 'Full Code' (default). His daughter Keisha is the emergency contact. At 0700, he states unprompted: 'I've been thinking about this all night. I don't want to be kept alive by machines. If something happens, I don't want them to put a tube down my throat... I just want to be comfortable.'","fullStemZh":"伴有急性呼吸衰退的转移性肺癌中的预立医疗指示澄清和抢救状态升级。 Harold Jeffries 先生是一位 55 岁的男性，五天前因转移性非小细胞肺癌（IV期）继发的进行性呼吸困难和右侧胸腔积液收治于内外科病房。他正在接受以卡铂为基础的姑息性化疗。目前的医嘱包括通过鼻导管吸氧以维持 SpO₂ > 92%。主治医生是目前在手术室的呼吸科医生；代班医生是住院医师。病历中没有预立医疗指示、维持生命治疗医生医嘱（POLST）或医疗委托书。抢救状态为“全面抢救 (Full Code)”（默认）。他的女儿 Keisha 是紧急联系人。在 0700，他自发地说道：“我整晚都在想这件事。我不想靠机器维持生命。如果发生什么事，我不想他们把管子插进我喉咙里……我只想舒舒服服的。”","terminalSentenceEn":"I just want to be comfortable.'","terminalSentenceZh":"如果发生什么事，我不想他们把管子插进我喉咙里……我只想舒舒服服的。”","penultimateSentenceEn":"If something happens, I don't want them to put a tube down my throat...","penultimateSentenceZh":"我不想靠机器维持生命。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case demonstrates the nurse's role in protecting a capacitated patient's expressed end-of-life wishes when the documented code status does not yet match the patient's current preferences. The nurse should assess and document decision-making capacity and verbatim statements, explain that a DNAR/DNI order requires an authorized provider, notify the charge nurse and providers, escalate proportionally as the client deteriorates, communicate the active refusal during rapid response handoff, continue ordered oxygen and comfort medications, and verify loop closure after the order is entered. Effective advocacy includes confirming the DNAR/DNI order and visual identifiers are in place, notifying the appropriate family member or healthcare proxy, documenting contemporaneously, and reporting system delays through the appropriate quality/safety process.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例展示了当病历中的抢救状态尚未反映患者当前意愿时，护士如何保护一名有决策能力患者所表达的临终照护意愿。护士应评估并记录患者的决策能力和原话，说明 DNAR/DNI 医嘱需要由有权限的医嘱开立者下达，通知护士长和医嘱开立者，并随着患者病情恶化按紧急程度逐级上报。在快速反应交接时，护士必须主动说明患者正在拒绝插管，同时继续执行已有医嘱中的吸氧和舒适用药。医嘱下达后，有效的倡导还包括核实 DNAR/DNI 医嘱和视觉标识已经落实，通知合适的家属或医疗代理人，进行同期、客观的记录，并按机构质量/安全流程报告系统延迟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Review each exhibit carefully as the patient's condition changes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"随着患者病情的变化，请仔细复习每份附件。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":80,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,85],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,36],"fullStemEn":"At 0700, what is the nurse's priority action in response to Mr. Jeffries's statement?","fullStemZh":"在 0700，针对 Jeffries 先生的陈述，护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Jeffries's statement?","terminalSentenceZh":"在 0700，针对 Jeffries 先生的陈述，护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0700, what is the nurse's priority action in response to Mr.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Assess and document his decision-making capacity and verbatim statements in the medical record.","zh":"评估并记录他的决策能力，并将他的原话记录在病历中。"},{"id":"B","en":"Acknowledge his feelings with empathy and mention it to the provider during rounds.","zh":"带着同理心认可他的感受，并在查房时向有权限的医嘱开立者提及此事。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assure the patient that the healthcare team will not intubate him.","zh":"向患者保证医疗团队不会为他插管。"},{"id":"D","en":"Immediately enter a temporary DNAR/DNI order pending the provider's evaluation.","zh":"在等待有权限的医嘱开立者评估期间，立即下达临时的 DNAR/DNI 医嘱。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must actively listen, assess and document that the patient has decision-making capacity, document his verbatim statements immediately, explain honestly that a provider order is required, and begin the escalation process. Documentation creates a contemporaneous legal and clinical record that protects the patient's autonomy if he later loses capacity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士必须积极倾听，评估并记录患者具有决策能力，立即记录他的原话，如实解释需要有权限的医嘱开立者下达医嘱，并开始升级流程。文件记录创建了同期的法律和临床记录，在患者随后丧失能力时保护其自主权。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the action that legally and ethically safeguards the patient's autonomy within the nurse's scope of practice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"找出在护士执业范围内在法律和伦理上保障患者自主权的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":81,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[19,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,49],"fullStemEn":"At 0800, after Dr. Reeves indicates he will visit the patient around 1100, which action is most appropriate for the nurse?","fullStemZh":"在 0800，当 Reeves 医生表示他将在 1100 左右探视患者后，护士最合适的行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Reeves indicates he will visit the patient around 1100, which action is most appropriate for the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"在 0800，当 Reeves 医生表示他将在 1100 左右探视患者后，护士最合适的行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0800, after Dr.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Document the conversation, inform the charge nurse, and plan to re-escalate if the patient's condition changes or the provider does not arrive.","zh":"记录对话内容，通知护士长，并计划在患者病情改变或医生未到达时再次上报。"},{"id":"D","en":"Inform the patient that his code status has been updated to DNAR/DNI since the provider acknowledged the message.","zh":"通知患者由于有权限的医嘱开立者已确认消息，他的抢救状态已更新为 DNAR/DNI。"},{"id":"C","en":"Immediately escalate to the nursing supervisor and the administrator on call to demand an earlier evaluation.","zh":"立即上报给护理主管和值班行政人员，要求提早进行评估。"},{"id":"B","en":"Accept the provider's plan but avoid documenting the delay to maintain interprofessional respect.","zh":"接受有权限的医嘱开立者的计划，但避免记录该延误以保持跨专业尊重。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At 0800, the patient is stable, so the risk of an unwanted code is present but not imminent. The appropriate nursing action is to document the provider's response, notify the charge nurse for safety planning, and plan follow-up if the patient deteriorates.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 0800，患者情况稳定，所以不想要的抢救风险存在但并不紧迫。合适的护理行动是记录有权限的医嘱开立者的回复，通知护士长进行安全规划，并计划在患者病情恶化时跟进。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the current clinical stability of the patient when determining the level of escalation needed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在确定需要上报的级别时，请考虑患者目前的临床稳定性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":82,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,78],"fullStemEn":"By 1030, Mr. Jeffries remains hypoxemic and increasingly fatigued despite escalation of oxygen, and his code status remains 'Full Code.' Which action is correct?","fullStemZh":"到了 1030，尽管增加了吸氧量，Jeffries 先生仍然存在低氧血症且越来越疲劳，其抢救状态仍为“全面抢救 (Full Code)”。哪项行动是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项行动是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Jeffries remains hypoxemic and increasingly fatigued despite escalation of oxygen, and his code status remains 'Full Code.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"到了 1030，尽管增加了吸氧量，Jeffries 先生仍然存在低氧血症且越来越疲劳，其抢救状态仍为“全面抢救 (Full Code)”。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Communicate the refusal immediately, activate the rapid response team/chain of command, and ensure an authorized provider evaluates capacity and enters orders.","zh":"立即沟通拒绝意愿，启动快速反应小组/指挥链，并确保有权限的医嘱开立者评估其能力并下达医嘱。"},{"id":"B","en":"Physically assist the rapid response team in forcing intubation since Full Code is in the chart.","zh":"既然病历中是全面抢救，就在快速反应小组强行插管时提供物理协助。"},{"id":"D","en":"Unilaterally change the code status to DNAR/DNI based on the patient's prior statements.","zh":"根据患者先前的陈述单方面将抢救状态更改为 DNAR/DNI。"},{"id":"C","en":"Withhold PRN morphine due to the risk of respiratory depression in a hypoxemic patient.","zh":"因低氧血症患者有呼吸抑制风险而停用按需使用的吗啡。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A conscious, capacitated patient has the right to actively refuse medical interventions. The nurse must immediately communicate this refusal to the responding team, escalate urgently, continue treating within orders, and get a provider evaluation. The nurse cannot unilaterally change the code status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"清醒且有能力的患者有权积极拒绝医疗干预。护士必须立即向响应小组传达这一拒绝意愿，紧急上报，在医嘱范围内继续治疗，并获得有权限的医嘱开立者的评估。护士不能单方面更改抢救状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between actions within the RN scope and those requiring a provider, especially during ethical dilemmas involving patient autonomy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分在注册护士范围内的行动和需要医生的行动，特别是在涉及患者自主权的伦理困境期间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":83,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,35],"fullStemEn":"At 1100, the nurse activates the rapid response team (RRT). What is essential to include in the handoff?","fullStemZh":"在 1100，护士启动了快速反应小组 (RRT)。交接中必须包括什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is essential to include in the handoff?","terminalSentenceZh":"交接中必须包括什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1100, the nurse activates the rapid response team (RRT).","penultimateSentenceZh":"在 1100，护士启动了快速反应小组 (RRT)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The unresolved code status, the patient's expressed wishes against intubation, his assessed capacity, and the escalation history.","zh":"未解决的抢救状态、患者明确表示反对插管的意愿、其经评估的能力以及上报历史。"},{"id":"B","en":"Only the clinical data, assuming the RRT physician will review the nursing notes in the chart.","zh":"仅包括临床数据，假设 RRT 医生会查阅病历中的护理记录。"},{"id":"D","en":"A recommendation that the RRT stand down because the patient has verbally refused treatment.","zh":"因为患者已口头拒绝治疗，建议 RRT 撤退。"},{"id":"C","en":"A request for the RRT nurse to immediately administer procedural sedation for intubation.","zh":"要求 RRT 护士立即给予程序性镇静以进行插管。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The handoff must prominently feature the unresolved code status, the patient's clear refusal of intubation, capacity assessment, and escalation history. This information directly determines what the RRT can and should do.","rationaleCorrectZh":"交接必须突出未解决的抢救状态、患者明确拒绝插管、能力评估和上报历史。这些信息直接决定了 RRT 可以和应该做什么。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the handoff approach that provides a complete picture of both clinical acuity and ethical constraints.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择既能提供临床危重程度又能提供伦理限制全貌的交接方法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":84,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_code_status_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,49],"fullStemEn":"At 1130, after the DNAR/DNI order is entered, which actions evaluate the effectiveness of the advocacy process? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在 1130，下达 DNAR/DNI 医嘱后，哪些行动可以评估倡导流程的有效性？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1130, after the DNAR/DNI order is entered, which actions evaluate the effectiveness of the advocacy process?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在 1130，下达 DNAR/DNI 医嘱后，哪些行动可以评估倡导流程的有效性？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Verifying the DNAR/DNI order is correctly entered in the electronic health record.","zh":"核实 DNAR/DNI 医嘱已正确输入电子健康病历中。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ensuring the code status is visually confirmed per policy (e.g., wristband, door sign).","zh":"确保按照政策通过视觉确认抢救状态（例如腕带、门标）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notifying the healthcare proxy of the clinical deterioration and advance directive.","zh":"将临床恶化情况和预立医疗指示通知医疗代理人。"},{"id":"D","en":"Filing an incident report regarding the system vulnerability caused by the delayed provider response.","zh":"针对因医生延迟回复而引起的系统漏洞提交事件报告。"},{"id":"E","en":"Writing a single retrospective note at the end of the shift summarizing the events.","zh":"在交班结束时写一份单一的回顾性记录总结事件。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Evaluating the advocacy process involves ensuring the order is properly implemented in all systems (EHR, wristbands), the family/proxy is informed, and recognizing system failures (like delayed provider response) for quality improvement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"评估倡导流程包括确保在所有系统（EHR、腕带）中正确执行了医嘱，通知了家属/代理人，并识别出系统故障（如有权限的医嘱开立者延迟回复）以进行质量改进。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select choices that represent thorough loop-closure for safety, communication, and system improvement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择那些体现了在安全、沟通和系统改进方面彻底闭环的选择。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":85,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.58","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.58.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,104],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: vancomycin infusion reaction and nephrotoxicity A 67-year-old man with MRSA bacteremia, stage 3b chronic kidney disease, diabetes, hypertension treated with lisinopril and carvedilol, and baseline bilateral sensorineural hearing loss begins pharmacy-guided vancomycin therapy.","fullStemZh":"展开式案例：万古霉素输注反应与肾毒性 一名 67 岁男性因 MRSA 菌血症开始由药师指导的万古霉素治疗；既往有 3b 期慢性肾病、糖尿病、使用赖诺普利和卡维地洛治疗的高血压，以及基线双侧感音神经性听力下降。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: vancomycin infusion reaction and nephrotoxicity A 67-year-old man with MRSA bacteremia, stage 3b chronic kidney disease, diabetes, hypertension treated with lisinopril and carvedilol, and baseline bilateral sensorineural hearing loss begins pharmacy-guided vancomycin therapy.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开式案例：万古霉素输注反应与肾毒性 一名 67 岁男性因 MRSA 菌血症开始由药师指导的万古霉素治疗；既往有 3b 期慢性肾病、糖尿病、使用赖诺普利和卡维地洛治疗的高血压，以及基线双侧感音神经性听力下降。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case tests recognition of a rate-related vancomycin infusion reaction, safe documentation that preserves future treatment options, dose clarification when troughs are supratherapeutic, individualized ototoxicity screening, and escalation when acute kidney injury and tinnitus emerge despite a trough that appears within the institutional target range.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例考查识别与输注速度相关的万古霉素反应、安全记录以保留未来治疗选择、在谷浓度超治疗范围时进行给药澄清、个体化耳毒性筛查，以及即使谷浓度看似在机构目标范围内，出现急性肾损伤和耳鸣时仍需升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In medication cases, do not rely on a single lab value. Compare the timing of symptoms, the pattern of findings, organ-function trends, and the medication's known toxicities before deciding whether a dose is safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"药物案例中不要只依赖单一化验值。决定是否安全给药前，要比较症状出现时间、体征模式、器官功能趋势以及该药已知毒性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":86,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01_q1_infusion_reaction","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[290,331],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,98],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Fifteen minutes after the vancomycin loading dose begins, the client develops intense itching, flushing limited to the face/neck/upper trunk, chest wheals, tachycardia, and mild hypotension. He has no wheezing, stridor, tongue swelling, throat tightness, or generalized urticaria. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"阶段 1：万古霉素负荷剂量开始 15 分钟后，患者出现剧烈瘙痒，潮红局限于面部、颈部和上半身，胸前有风团，心动过速并轻度低血压。无哮鸣、喘鸣、舌肿、喉咙发紧或全身性荨麻疹。护士首先应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"He has no wheezing, stridor, tongue swelling, throat tightness, or generalized urticaria.","penultimateSentenceZh":"无哮鸣、喘鸣、舌肿、喉咙发紧或全身性荨麻疹。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Continue the infusion at the same rate because flushing is an expected effect during the first dose.","zh":"按原速度继续输注，因为首次给药时潮红是预期反应。"},{"id":"E","en":"Remove the peripheral IV catheter and request an alternative antibiotic immediately.","zh":"拔除外周静脉导管，并立即请求改用另一种抗生素。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer intramuscular epinephrine and document a vancomycin allergy.","zh":"肌内注射肾上腺素，并记录为万古霉素过敏。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop the infusion, keep the IV patent with normal saline, place the client supine with legs slightly elevated, obtain vital signs, and notify the provider.","zh":"停止输注，用生理盐水保持静脉通路通畅，使患者仰卧并轻度抬高双腿，测量生命体征并通知医嘱者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Slow the infusion rate without stopping it, then reassess when the dose is complete.","zh":"不停止输注，仅降低输注速度，待本次剂量完成后再评估。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The regional upper-body flushing, pruritus, timing soon after the infusion starts, absence of airway findings, and absence of generalized urticaria are most consistent with vancomycin flushing syndrome. The immediate nursing response is to stop the infusion, maintain access, support circulation, reassess, and notify the provider. Antihistamine administration and restarting at a slower rate may follow provider orders.","rationaleCorrectZh":"局限于上半身的潮红、瘙痒、输注开始后很快出现、无气道表现且无全身性荨麻疹，最符合万古霉素潮红综合征。护士的即时处理是停止输注、保持静脉通路、支持循环、重新评估并通知医嘱者。随后可按医嘱给予抗组胺药，并以较慢速度重新输注。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate anaphylaxis from infusion reactions by looking for airway compromise, bronchospasm, angioedema, generalized hives, and circulatory collapse. Regional upper-body flushing during vancomycin points to a rate-related reaction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分过敏性休克和输注反应时，寻找气道受损、支气管痉挛、血管性水肿、全身风团和循环崩溃。万古霉素输注期间出现局限性上半身潮红提示与输注速度相关的反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":87,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01_q2_documentation_cloze","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,61],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: The flushing and itching resolve after the infusion is stopped and diphenhydramine is administered. The provider restarts the remaining dose at a slower rate without recurrence of symptoms. Complete the nursing documentation and handoff statement.","fullStemZh":"阶段 1：停止输注并给予苯海拉明后，潮红和瘙痒缓解。医嘱者以较慢速度重新开始剩余剂量，症状未复发。完成护士记录和交接说明。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing documentation and handoff statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护士记录和交接说明。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider restarts the remaining dose at a slower rate without recurrence of symptoms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱者以较慢速度重新开始剩余剂量，症状未复发。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The event should be documented as {{1}}, and future vancomycin doses should include {{2}}.","zh":"该事件应记录为 {{1}}，以后万古霉素给药应包括 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a true vancomycin allergy","zh":"真正的万古霉素过敏"},{"id":"o3","en":"vancomycin-induced anaphylaxis","zh":"万古霉素诱发的过敏性休克"},{"id":"o1","en":"an infusion-related adverse drug reaction","zh":"输注相关不良药物反应"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"routine epinephrine before each dose","zh":"每次给药前常规给予肾上腺素"},{"id":"o2","en":"permanent avoidance of all glycopeptide antibiotics","zh":"永久避免所有糖肽类抗生素"},{"id":"o1","en":"premedication as ordered and an infusion rate no faster than 10 mg/min","zh":"按医嘱预处理，并以不快于 10 mg/分钟的速度输注"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The clinical pattern and successful slower rechallenge support a rate-related infusion reaction rather than a true IgE-mediated allergy. Documenting the exact reaction, interventions, and future rate/premedication needs protects the client from both recurrence and unnecessary loss of a key MRSA therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"临床表现以及以较慢速度再次输注成功，支持与输注速度相关的反应，而不是真正的 IgE 介导过敏。记录具体反应、干预措施以及未来所需的输注速度和预处理，既可预防复发，也可避免不必要地失去重要的 MRSA 治疗选择。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a medication reaction is rate-related and resolves with slowing or premedication, document the specific reaction and prevention plan. Avoid broad allergy labels unless the evidence supports true allergy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当药物反应与输注速度相关，并通过减慢速度或预处理缓解时，应记录具体反应和预防方案。除非证据支持真正过敏，否则避免使用宽泛的过敏标签。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The provider restarts the remaining dose at a slower rate without recurrence of symptoms.","controlSentenceZh":"医嘱者以较慢速度重新开始剩余剂量，症状未复发。"}
{"queueIndex":88,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01_q3_supratherapeutic_trough_order","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[200,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,87],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The vancomycin trough returns at 22.4 mcg/mL 30 minutes before the next scheduled 1,250 mg dose. The pharmacist recommends a dose reduction and is contacting the infectious disease provider. Arrange the nurse's actions in the safest order.","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：下一次预定 1,250 mg 剂量前 30 分钟，万古霉素谷浓度返回为 22.4 mcg/mL。药师建议减量，并正在联系感染科医嘱者。请按最安全顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nurse's actions in the safest order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最安全顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The pharmacist recommends a dose reduction and is contacting the infectious disease provider.","penultimateSentenceZh":"药师建议减量，并正在联系感染科医嘱者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document the trough, held dose, notifications, verified new order, and monitoring plan.","zh":"记录谷浓度、暂缓给药、通知情况、已核实的新医嘱以及监测计划。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the scheduled 1,250 mg vancomycin dose while the order is being clarified.","zh":"在澄清医嘱期间，暂缓预定的 1,250 mg 万古霉素剂量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Contact the prescriber to confirm the revised dosing order recommended by pharmacy.","zh":"联系医嘱者，确认药师建议的修订剂量医嘱。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the revised dose using the ordered premedication and slower infusion precautions.","zh":"按已下达的预处理和较慢输注预防措施，给予修订后的剂量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Verify that the new 1,000 mg vancomycin order is active in the medication administration record.","zh":"核实新的 1,000 mg 万古霉素医嘱已在给药记录中生效。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A supratherapeutic trough in a client with impaired renal clearance makes the current scheduled dose unsafe to administer without clarification. The nurse should hold the dose, obtain the revised provider order, verify it in the MAR, administer only the corrected regimen with the ordered precautions, and document the safety actions and monitoring plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肾清除功能受损的患者出现超治疗范围谷浓度时，若不澄清医嘱，当前预定剂量不安全。护士应暂缓给药，取得医嘱者修订医嘱，在给药记录中核实后，仅按纠正后的方案和已下达预防措施给药，并记录安全行动和监测计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For ordered-response medication safety items, protect the client first, then clarify the order, verify the corrected order, administer only when safe, and document after action is taken.","testTakingStrategyZh":"药物安全排序题中，先保护患者，再澄清医嘱，核实纠正后的医嘱，确认安全后才给药，最后记录已采取的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":89,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01_q4_ototoxicity_screening","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,54],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The pharmacist recommends increased ototoxicity monitoring. The client has baseline bilateral hearing loss and uses hearing aids. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：药师建议加强耳毒性监测。患者基线已有双侧听力下降，并使用助听器。哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client to remove hearing aids and perform a repeatable bedside hearing screen, such as a whispered voice test in each ear.","zh":"请患者取下助听器，并进行可重复的床旁听力筛查，例如分别测试每只耳朵的耳语测试。"},{"id":"D","en":"Chart hearing as within normal limits because the client can converse while wearing hearing aids.","zh":"因患者佩戴助听器时可交流，记录听力在正常范围内。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask specifically about new tinnitus, dizziness, vertigo, or subjective hearing change.","zh":"具体询问是否有新的耳鸣、头晕、眩晕或主观听力变化。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document a dated patient-specific baseline and compare future assessments with that baseline.","zh":"记录有日期的、针对该患者的基线，并将后续评估与该基线比较。"},{"id":"E","en":"Delay further screening until the client reports complete hearing loss.","zh":"等到患者报告完全听力丧失后再进一步筛查。"},{"id":"F","en":"Focus only on serum creatinine because ototoxicity cannot be screened at the bedside by a nurse.","zh":"只关注血清肌酐，因为护士无法在床旁筛查耳毒性。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ototoxicity monitoring within RN scope includes a repeatable bedside hearing screen, targeted symptom questions, and documentation of an individualized baseline. This is especially important because pre-existing hearing loss reduces auditory reserve; future concern is based on change from this client's baseline, not comparison with normal hearing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士职责范围内的耳毒性监测包括可重复的床旁听力筛查、针对性症状询问，以及记录个体化基线。患者已有听力下降，听觉储备较低，因此尤其重要；后续担忧应基于与该患者自身基线相比的变化，而不是与正常听力相比。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client has an abnormal baseline, the safest answer usually establishes and trends that client's own baseline instead of assuming normal findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者基线本来异常时，最安全的答案通常是建立并追踪该患者自身基线，而不是假设结果正常。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":90,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01_q5_aki_cue_matrix","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,41],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: Classify each finding based on how it should affect the nurse's interpretation of the scheduled 0800 vancomycin dose.","fullStemZh":"阶段 3：根据每项发现对护士解读 0800 预定万古霉素剂量安全性的影响进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 3: Classify each finding based on how it should affect the nurse's interpretation of the scheduled 0800 vancomycin dose.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 3：根据每项发现对护士解读 0800 预定万古霉素剂量安全性的影响进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Creatinine increased to 2.4 mg/dL with urine output 180 mL in 12 hours.","zh":"肌酐升至 2.4 mg/dL，12 小时尿量 180 mL。"},{"id":"r2","en":"New persistent bilateral tinnitus began overnight.","zh":"夜间开始出现新的持续性双侧耳鸣。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Vancomycin trough is 18.6 mcg/mL, within the institutional surrogate target range.","zh":"万古霉素谷浓度为 18.6 mcg/mL，在机构替代目标范围内。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Repeat blood cultures show no growth at 48 hours.","zh":"复查血培养 48 小时无生长。"},{"id":"r5","en":"The AV fistula site has less erythema and drainage.","zh":"动静脉瘘部位红斑和引流减少。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Priority toxicity cue: hold and escalate","zh":"优先毒性线索：暂缓并升级报告"},{"id":"c2","en":"Does not prove the next dose is safe","zh":"不能证明下一剂安全"},{"id":"c3","en":"Infection improving, but not a reason to ignore toxicity","zh":"感染改善，但不能因此忽视毒性"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The creatinine rise with oliguria and new tinnitus are priority toxicity cues, even though the trough appears within the institutional target range. The trough does not prove safety when end-organ toxicity is present. Improving cultures and fistula appearance are favorable infection-response cues, but they do not justify administering another vancomycin dose into worsening renal clearance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肌酐升高伴少尿以及新的耳鸣是优先毒性线索，即使谷浓度看似在机构目标范围内。存在终末器官毒性时，谷浓度不能证明安全。血培养和瘘管外观改善是感染反应好转的有利线索，但不能成为在肾清除恶化时继续给予下一剂万古霉素的理由。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In trend questions, worsening organ function and new neurologic or sensory symptoms outweigh a single reassuring number. Ask whether the client can safely clear the next dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"趋势题中，器官功能恶化以及新的神经或感觉症状比单一看似安心的数值更重要。要问：患者是否能安全清除下一剂药物？","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":91,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_vanco_case_01_q6_lisinopril_aki","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[297,322],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,98],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: Vancomycin has been held and the antibiotic plan is being changed because of acute kidney injury and new tinnitus. The nurse reviews the medication administration record and sees that lisinopril 10 mg daily is still active and the morning dose has not been given. Potassium is 5.1 mEq/L. What should the nurse do?","fullStemZh":"阶段 3：因急性肾损伤和新的耳鸣，万古霉素已被暂停，抗生素方案正在更改。护士查看给药记录，发现赖诺普利 10 mg 每日一次仍为有效医嘱，晨间剂量尚未给予。钾为 5.1 mEq/L。护士应怎么做？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse do?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应怎么做？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Potassium is 5.1 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"钾为 5.1 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administer lisinopril and recheck potassium with the next morning laboratory draw.","zh":"给予赖诺普利，并在次日晨间抽血时复查钾。"},{"id":"D","en":"Discontinue lisinopril permanently in the medication administration record without contacting the provider.","zh":"不联系医嘱者，直接在给药记录中永久停用赖诺普利。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer lisinopril because it is a home medication and the blood pressure is 148/88 mm Hg.","zh":"给予赖诺普利，因为这是家庭用药且血压为 148/88 mm Hg。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the lisinopril dose and notify the provider to clarify whether it should be temporarily discontinued.","zh":"暂缓赖诺普利剂量，并通知医嘱者澄清是否应暂时停用。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The clinical picture has changed: the client now has acute kidney injury, oliguria, and potassium 5.1 mEq/L. An ACE inhibitor can further reduce glomerular filtration pressure and can worsen hyperkalemia. The nurse should hold the dose for safety and promptly clarify the order with the provider rather than administering it as routine or independently discontinuing it permanently.","rationaleCorrectZh":"临床情况已经改变：患者现在有急性肾损伤、少尿，钾 5.1 mEq/L。ACE 抑制剂可能进一步降低肾小球滤过压力，并加重高钾血症。护士应出于安全暂缓该剂量，并及时向医嘱者澄清，而不是按常规给药或自行永久停药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a routine medication becomes unsafe because of new assessment data, do not give it simply because it is scheduled. Hold, assess, and clarify with the prescriber.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当新的评估资料显示常规药物不安全时，不要仅因已排程就给药。应暂缓、评估，并向医嘱者澄清。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":92,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.59","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.59.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[172,319],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,95],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: discharge coordination after right total hip arthroplasty An 82-year-old Mandarin-speaking client is recovering from elective right total hip arthroplasty. The nurse must coordinate language access, mobility readiness, medication safety, home health services, and handoff planning before discharge home.","fullStemZh":"展开病例：右全髋关节置换术后的出院协调 一名82岁、主要讲普通话的患者正在从择期右全髋关节置换术中恢复。护士必须在患者回家出院前协调语言服务、活动能力准备、用药安全、居家护理服务和交接计划。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must coordinate language access, mobility readiness, medication safety, home health services, and handoff planning before discharge home.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须在患者回家出院前协调语言服务、活动能力准备、用药安全、居家护理服务和交接计划。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: discharge coordination after right total hip arthroplasty An 82-year-old Mandarin-speaking client is recovering from elective right total hip arthroplasty.","penultimateSentenceZh":"展开病例：右全髋关节置换术后的出院协调 一名82岁、主要讲普通话的患者正在从择期右全髋关节置换术中恢复。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes that safe discharge after hip arthroplasty requires more than stable vital signs and a written discharge order. The nurse must verify language access, teach-back, mobility and stair safety, anticoagulant monitoring, home health acceptance, equipment, follow-up, and a practical communication plan before releasing a high-risk older adult home.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例强调，髋关节置换术后安全出院不仅需要生命体征稳定和书面出院医嘱。护士必须在高风险老年患者回家前确认语言服务、回教效果、活动和楼梯安全、抗凝药监测、居家护理机构接受、设备、随访以及实际可行的沟通计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding discharge cases, track each barrier over time and ask whether it has been resolved, delegated to the right discipline, or converted into a confirmed community plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"展开式出院病例中，要持续追踪每个障碍，并判断它是否已解决、已交给合适专业人员处理，或已转化为确认的社区照护计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":93,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,51],"fullStemEn":"Postoperative day 0: The admission record lists Mandarin as the client's primary language, but no ongoing postoperative language-access plan is documented. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"术后第0天：入院记录显示患者主要语言为普通话，但未记录持续的术后语言服务计划。护士首先应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Postoperative day 0: The admission record lists Mandarin as the client's primary language, but no ongoing postoperative language-access plan is documented.","penultimateSentenceZh":"术后第0天：入院记录显示患者主要语言为普通话，但未记录持续的术后语言服务计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Wait for the surgical team to update the language-access plan during morning rounds.","zh":"等待外科团队在晨间查房时更新语言服务计划。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the son to interpret by telephone because he will help after discharge.","zh":"请儿子通过电话解释，因为他出院后会协助照护。"},{"id":"B","en":"Activate qualified interpreter services now, document the preferred language in the care plan, and flag the need for interpreter-supported discharge teaching.","zh":"立即启用合格解释服务，在护理计划中记录首选语言，并标记出院教育需要解释员支持。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use simple English phrases and gestures until the formal discharge teaching session.","zh":"在正式出院教育前先使用简单英语短语和手势沟通。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should act immediately on the identified language-access gap. Qualified interpreter services are needed for assessment, symptom reporting, safety teaching, and informed participation in care; documenting the need also allows the team to plan complex discharge teaching ahead of time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应立即处理已识别的语言服务缺口。评估、症状报告、安全教育和参与护理决策都需要合格解释服务；记录该需求也能让团队提前安排复杂的出院教育。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a language barrier affects safety or consent, choose the action that establishes qualified communication immediately rather than relying on nodding, family, or delay.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当语言障碍影响安全或知情参与时，应选择立即建立合格沟通的措施，而不是依赖点头、家属或拖延。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":94,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[238,267],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,71],"fullStemEn":"Postoperative day 1: The nurse uses an English handout to teach hip precautions and rivaroxaban safety. With interpreter phone assistance, the client cannot state the medication name, purpose, bleeding signs, or missed-dose instructions. Which nursing action is best?","fullStemZh":"术后第1天：护士用英文资料讲解髋关节注意事项和利伐沙班安全。借助电话解释服务，患者仍不能说出药名、用途、出血征象或漏服处理。哪项护理措施最佳？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项护理措施最佳？","penultimateSentenceEn":"With interpreter phone assistance, the client cannot state the medication name, purpose, bleeding signs, or missed-dose instructions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"借助电话解释服务，患者仍不能说出药名、用途、出血征象或漏服处理。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Repeat the same English handout more slowly and ask yes/no questions to confirm understanding.","zh":"用更慢的速度重复同一份英文资料，并用是/否问题确认理解。"},{"id":"C","en":"Send the client home with written instructions because home health nursing will reinforce teaching tomorrow.","zh":"给患者书面说明后安排回家，因为居家护士明天会强化教育。"},{"id":"A","en":"Document the failed teach-back, do not treat the client as discharge-ready, and arrange qualified Mandarin interpreter-supported comprehensive teaching.","zh":"记录回教失败，不将患者视为已具备出院准备，并安排合格普通话解释员支持的全面健康教育。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the son to interpret the medication instructions by phone and document education as completed.","zh":"请儿子通过电话解释用药说明，并记录健康教育已完成。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teach-back failure is evidence that the client does not yet understand information required for safe self-care. The nurse should change the teaching approach, arrange qualified language support, and delay discharge-readiness clearance until understanding is demonstrated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"回教失败说明患者尚未理解安全自我照护所需的信息。护士应改变教育方式，安排合格语言支持，并在患者能证明理解前不确认出院准备充分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A failed teach-back is not a documentation task only; it is a clinical cue that the education plan must change before discharge can be considered safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回教失败不仅是记录问题；它是提示教育计划必须改变的临床线索，只有这样才能考虑安全出院。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":95,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[356,378],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,114],"fullStemEn":"Postoperative day 1: The client is medically stable, but the discharge-readiness screen shows unsafe walker use, no confirmed home support, no home health referral, incomplete teaching, no stair assessment, and a rising creatinine while taking rivaroxaban. Which nursing actions are necessary to address the discharge barriers before the client goes home? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"术后第1天：患者医学状况稳定，但出院准备筛查显示助行器使用不安全、无确认居家支持、未转介居家护理、教育未完成、尚未评估楼梯能力，并且服用利伐沙班期间肌酐上升。为在患者回家前处理这些出院障碍，护士需要采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are necessary to address the discharge barriers before the client goes home?","penultimateSentenceZh":"为在患者回家前处理这些出院障碍，护士需要采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Notify the charge nurse and surgical team that the planned discharge may be unsafe until barriers are addressed.","zh":"通知责任护士长和外科团队：在障碍解决前，原计划出院可能不安全。"},{"id":"E","en":"Reassess and document discharge readiness after services, teaching, mobility, equipment, follow-up, and medication-safety plans are confirmed.","zh":"在服务、教育、活动能力、设备、随访和用药安全计划均确认后，重新评估并记录出院准备情况。"},{"id":"F","en":"Proceed with the planned discharge because vital signs and the incision are stable, and arrange home services after discharge if problems occur.","zh":"按原计划出院，因为生命体征和切口稳定；如出院后出现问题，再安排居家服务。"},{"id":"D","en":"Coordinate with PT for additional walker training, stair assessment, and equipment recommendations.","zh":"与物理治疗师协调进一步的助行器训练、楼梯评估和设备建议。"},{"id":"B","en":"Request social work/case management involvement to evaluate support, payer requirements, home health needs, and alternative post-acute options.","zh":"请求社会工作/个案管理介入，以评估支持系统、保险要求、居家护理需求和其他出院后照护选择。"},{"id":"C","en":"Arrange certified Mandarin interpreter-supported discharge teaching and translated written materials.","zh":"安排合格普通话医疗解释员支持的出院教育和翻译后的书面资料。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"All of the barrier-focused actions are needed: the team must be alerted that discharge is not yet safe, social work/case management must address support and post-acute services, certified interpreter-supported teaching and translated materials must be arranged, PT must complete mobility/stair/equipment planning, and the nurse must reassess readiness after the plans are confirmed. Stable vital signs and a clean incision do not make discharge safe when mobility, teaching, anticoagulant monitoring, language access, and home support barriers remain unresolved.","rationaleCorrectZh":"所有针对障碍的措施都是必要的：必须提醒团队目前出院尚不安全；社会工作/个案管理需处理支持系统和出院后服务；需安排合格解释员支持的教育和翻译资料；PT需完成活动能力、楼梯和设备计划；护士还必须在各项计划确认后重新评估出院准备情况。即使生命体征稳定、切口清洁，只要活动、教育、抗凝监测、语言沟通和居家支持障碍仍未解决，出院仍不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge-readiness questions, separate medical stability from safe transition readiness. Select actions that address each unresolved barrier and reject answers that defer essential services until after discharge.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理出院准备题时，要区分“医学稳定”和“安全过渡准备充分”。选择能处理每个未解决障碍的措施，并排除把关键服务推迟到出院后的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":96,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[253,337],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,122],"fullStemEn":"Postoperative day 2: The client's creatinine rose from 1.4 mg/dL to 1.5 mg/dL on postoperative day 1 and improved to 1.4 mg/dL after hydration. eGFR is 39 mL/min. The client is prescribed rivaroxaban 10 mg once daily for 35 days after hip arthroplasty. For each proposed nursing action, select whether it is appropriate or inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"术后第2天：患者肌酐从1.4 mg/dL在术后第1天升至1.5 mg/dL，补液后改善至1.4 mg/dL。eGFR为39 mL/min。患者医嘱为髋关节置换术后利伐沙班10 mg每日一次，共35天。请判断每项拟采取的护理措施是适当还是不适当。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each proposed nursing action, select whether it is appropriate or inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项拟采取的护理措施是适当还是不适当。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is prescribed rivaroxaban 10 mg once daily for 35 days after hip arthroplasty.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者医嘱为髋关节置换术后利伐沙班10 mg每日一次，共35天。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Notify the prescribing provider of the creatinine/eGFR trend and confirm the anticoagulant plan.","zh":"将肌酐/eGFR趋势通知开药医嘱提供者，并确认抗凝计划。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hold the rivaroxaban independently because the creatinine increased on postoperative day 1.","zh":"因术后第1天肌酐升高，护士自行停用利伐沙班。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Teach the client to report blood in urine or stool, black stools, unusual bruising, bleeding gums, dizziness, or weakness.","zh":"教育患者报告尿血或便血、黑便、异常瘀斑、牙龈出血、头晕或乏力。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Tell the client that the 10 mg dose must be taken with a full meal for absorption.","zh":"告知患者10 mg剂量必须随正餐服用以利吸收。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Include renal-function trend, anticoagulant adherence, and bleeding surveillance in the home health handoff.","zh":"在居家护理交接中纳入肾功能趋势、抗凝药依从性和出血监测。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不适当"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse recognizes a relevant renal-function trend, communicates it to the prescriber, reinforces bleeding precautions and missed-dose safety, and includes monitoring needs in the handoff. The nurse should not independently hold an ordered anticoagulant, and the 10 mg rivaroxaban dose for hip replacement prophylaxis may be taken with or without food.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应识别相关肾功能趋势，告知开药者，强化出血预防和漏服安全，并在交接中纳入监测需求。护士不应自行停用已开具的抗凝药；髋关节置换术后预防用利伐沙班10 mg可随餐或不随餐服用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For medication-safety questions, separate RN responsibilities—recognize trends, notify, teach, monitor, document—from prescriber responsibilities such as changing or stopping the medication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"用药安全题要区分RN职责（识别趋势、通知、教育、监测、记录）和开药者职责（更改或停用药物）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client is prescribed rivaroxaban 10 mg once daily for 35 days after hip arthroplasty.","controlSentenceZh":"患者医嘱为髋关节置换术后利伐沙班10 mg每日一次，共35天。"}
{"queueIndex":97,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[232,254],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,68],"fullStemEn":"Postoperative day 2: Interpreter-supported teach-back is successful, but the client states she cannot independently navigate the surgeon's English-language phone system. Which actions should the nurse include in the discharge plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"术后第2天：在解释员支持下回教成功，但患者表示无法独自应对外科医生办公室的英文电话系统。护士应在出院计划中纳入哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse include in the discharge plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在出院计划中纳入哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Provide large-print Mandarin instructions with the surgeon and home health phone numbers, or help set up accessible landline speed-dial instructions.","zh":"提供大字体普通话说明，写明外科医生和居家护理电话号码，或协助设置可用的座机快速拨号说明。"},{"id":"E","en":"Ask the surgeon's office to schedule a Mandarin interpreter for the follow-up appointment.","zh":"请求外科医生办公室为随访预约安排普通话解释员。"},{"id":"F","en":"Take no further action because the client correctly repeated when to seek help.","zh":"不再采取其他措施，因为患者已正确复述何时需要求助。"},{"id":"C","en":"Tell the client to call 911 for all postoperative questions because she cannot use the office phone tree.","zh":"告诉患者因无法使用诊所电话系统，所有术后问题都应拨打911。"},{"id":"D","en":"Communicate the phone-access barrier and family-contact plan to the home health agency during handoff.","zh":"在交接时向居家护理机构沟通电话联系障碍和家属联系计划。"},{"id":"A","en":"Confirm that the son agrees to serve as the designated phone contact for the surgeon's office and document the plan.","zh":"确认儿子同意作为联系外科医生办公室的指定电话联系人，并记录该计划。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A safe discharge plan must account for the client's actual ability to access help, not only her ability to name danger signs. The nurse should build redundancy through a documented family contact, accessible written/phone supports, home health reinforcement, and interpreter support for follow-up care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全出院计划必须考虑患者实际获得帮助的能力，而不只是能说出危险征象。护士应通过记录家属联系人、可及的书面/电话支持、居家护理强化和随访解释员支持来建立多重保障。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In discharge questions, look beyond knowledge. A client must also have the functional, language, phone, transportation, and support systems needed to carry out the plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出院题不要只看知识掌握。患者还必须具备执行计划所需的功能能力、语言支持、电话途径、交通和支持系统。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":98,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,48],"fullStemEn":"Postoperative day 3: The nurse is giving a verbal SBAR handoff to the receiving home health nurse. Which information is essential to include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"术后第3天：护士正在向接收的居家护理护士进行SBAR口头交接。哪些信息必须纳入？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which information is essential to include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些信息必须纳入？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The client requires Mandarin interpretation for teaching and clinical communication.","zh":"患者在健康教育和临床沟通中需要普通话解释服务。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client lives alone in a second-floor walk-up after the son leaves, and home safety/stair navigation need assessment.","zh":"儿子离开后患者独自住在二楼无电梯公寓，需要评估居家安全和上下楼梯。"},{"id":"C","en":"Creatinine trended up transiently and returned to baseline; ongoing renal-function awareness is needed.","zh":"肌酐曾短暂升高后回到基础水平；仍需关注肾功能。"},{"id":"F","en":"Equipment, functional status, follow-up appointment, and son's role as the phone contact have been confirmed.","zh":"设备、功能状态、随访预约以及儿子作为电话联系人的角色均已确认。"},{"id":"B","en":"Rivaroxaban 10 mg daily is prescribed for 35 days; adherence and bleeding signs need monitoring.","zh":"医嘱为利伐沙班10 mg每日一次，共35天；需要监测依从性和出血征象。"},{"id":"E","en":"The client preferred hot tea during hospitalization and declined the last two oxycodone doses.","zh":"患者住院期间偏好热茶，并拒绝了最近两次羟考酮。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The handoff must transmit the risks that could cause transition failure: language needs, anticoagulant adherence and bleeding monitoring, renal-function context, social isolation and home layout, mobility/equipment needs, follow-up, and the designated communication contact. These data allow the home health nurse to continue the safety plan without information loss.","rationaleCorrectZh":"交接必须传递可能导致转衔失败的风险：语言需求、抗凝药依从性和出血监测、肾功能背景、社会孤立和居家环境、活动/设备需求、随访以及指定沟通联系人。这些资料能让居家护理护士在不丢失信息的情况下延续安全计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For handoff items, choose information that changes the receiving clinician's monitoring, teaching, safety checks, or follow-up actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"交接题应选择会改变接收方临床人员监测、教育、安全检查或随访行动的信息。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":99,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.60","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.60.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1117,1166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[412,429],"fullStemEn":"Clostridioides difficile infection with dehydration and contact-precaution teaching for family visitors. A 71-year-old woman is transferred from a skilled nursing facility to a medical-surgical unit with a three-day history of profuse, watery, foul-smelling diarrhea. She completed a 10-day course of oral amoxicillin-clavulanate for community-acquired pneumonia six days ago. Her medical history includes type 2 diabetes managed with metformin 1,000 mg twice daily, hypertension treated with lisinopril 20 mg daily, osteoarthritis, and mild chronic kidney disease (baseline creatinine 1.4 mg/dL, baseline eGFR 42 mL/min/1.73 m²). She lives with her adult daughter and son-in-law, who visit daily and assist with meals and hygiene. On admission, the provider orders contact precautions, stool specimen for C. difficile toxin PCR, IV lactated Ringer's 500 mL bolus over 1 hour, then maintain at 125 mL/hr, strict intake and output, daily basic metabolic panel, and oral vancomycin 125 mg every 6 hours per facility protocol for suspected C. difficile infection. Metformin is held pending evaluation of renal function. A Braden scale assessment is ordered every shift.","fullStemZh":"艰难梭菌感染伴脱水以及家属探视的接触隔离宣教。 一名71岁女性患者因连续3天出现大量水样、恶臭腹泻，从专业护理机构转入内外科病房。她于6天前完成了为期10天的口服阿莫西林-克拉维酸治疗社区获得性肺炎的疗程。既往病史包括2型糖尿病（规律服用二甲双胍1000 mg，每日两次）、高血压（规律服用赖诺普利20 mg，每日一次）、骨关节炎以及轻度慢性肾脏病（基线肌酐1.4 mg/dL，基线eGFR 42 mL/min/1.73 m²）。她与成年的女儿和女婿同住，他们每天来探视并协助进食和个人卫生。入院时，考虑到疑似艰难梭菌感染，医生下达医嘱：接触隔离，留取粪便标本行艰难梭菌毒素PCR检测，静脉输注乳酸林格氏液 500 mL 负荷量（1小时内滴完），随后以 125 mL/hr 维持，严格记录出入量，每日复查基础代谢指标（BMP），并根据机构方案给予口服万古霉素125 mg，每6小时一次。二甲双胍暂停使用，待评估肾功能后决定。每班进行一次Braden量表评估。","terminalSentenceEn":"A Braden scale assessment is ordered every shift.","terminalSentenceZh":"每班进行一次Braden量表评估。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Metformin is held pending evaluation of renal function.","penultimateSentenceZh":"二甲双胍暂停使用，待评估肾功能后决定。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires the nurse to synthesize positive C. difficile testing with ongoing watery diarrhea, hypovolemia, prerenal acute kidney injury, hypokalemia, infection-control risk, and moisture-associated skin breakdown. Priority nursing care includes correcting fluid and electrolyte losses, enforcing contact precautions with gown and gloves plus soap-and-water hand hygiene, protecting macerated perianal skin with gentle cleansing and barrier cream, and delaying metformin resumption until renal function and hydration have recovered further. Improvement is evaluated by trends across stool output, vital signs, urine output, renal labs, lactate, WBC count, oral intake, wound stability, and family return-demonstration of infection-control practices.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例要求护士综合判断艰难梭菌检测阳性、持续水样腹泻、低血容量、肾前性急性肾损伤、低钾血症、感染控制风险以及潮湿相关性皮肤损伤。护理重点包括纠正液体和电解质丢失，严格执行接触隔离（穿隔离衣、戴手套，并用肥皂和水洗手），通过轻柔清洁和防潮隔离霜保护浸渍的肛周皮肤，并在肾功能和水合状态进一步恢复前暂缓恢复二甲双胍。病情改善应通过排便情况、生命体征、尿量、肾功能指标、乳酸、白细胞计数、经口摄入、伤口稳定性以及家属感染控制操作回示等趋势综合评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read all tabs before answering.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在回答之前阅读所有选项卡。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":100,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,36],"fullStemEn":"Based on the assessment findings and laboratory data at Stage 1, which physiological condition poses the most immediate threat to the patient?","fullStemZh":"根据阶段1的评估结果和实验室数据，哪种生理状况对患者构成了最直接的威胁？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the assessment findings and laboratory data at Stage 1, which physiological condition poses the most immediate threat to the patient?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据阶段1的评估结果和实验室数据，哪种生理状况对患者构成了最直接的威胁？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Progression of intrinsic chronic kidney disease","zh":"原发性慢性肾脏病的进展"},{"id":"D","en":"Primary electrolyte disorder requiring isolated replacement","zh":"需要单独纠正的原发性电解质紊乱"},{"id":"C","en":"Systemic sepsis originating from the gastrointestinal tract","zh":"源自胃肠道的全身性脓毒症"},{"id":"B","en":"Volume depletion causing prerenal acute kidney injury","zh":"容量不足导致的肾前性急性肾损伤"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient's rising creatinine (from a baseline of 1.4 to 2.1), elevated BUN with an acute creatinine rise from baseline, oliguria, tachycardia, hypotension, weight loss of 4 kg, and dry mucous membranes collectively point to moderate-to-severe dehydration. The large-volume fluid losses from C. difficile diarrhea have led to volume depletion and a prerenal acute kidney injury. Identifying this fluid deficit as the immediate driver of the renal injury and hemodynamic instability directs the nurse to prioritize fluid resuscitation. Note: The patient's WBC count > 15 ×10³/µL and creatinine > 1.5 mg/dL also meet criteria for severe C. difficile infection, but the immediate physiological threat causing acute instability is the severe volume depletion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者的肌酐升高（从基线1.4升至2.1）、BUN升高以及肌酐较基线急性升高、少尿、心动过速、低血压、体重减轻4 kg以及黏膜干燥，共同提示中重度脱水。艰难梭菌性腹泻导致的大量液体丢失引起了容量不足和肾前性急性肾损伤。将这种液体缺乏识别为肾损伤和血流动力学不稳定的直接原因，指导护士优先进行液体复苏。 注：患者的白细胞计数 > 15 ×10³/µL 和肌酐 > 1.5 mg/dL 也符合重度艰难梭菌感染的标准，但导致急性不稳定的最直接生理威胁是严重的容量不足。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the cluster of signs: weight loss, dry mucous membranes, tachycardia, hypotension, oliguria, and an acute creatinine rise from baseline indicate dehydration and prerenal AKI.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别体征群：体重下降、黏膜干燥、心动过速、低血压、少尿，以及肌酐较基线急性升高，提示脱水和肾前性急性肾损伤（AKI）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":101,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,57],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the nurse observes the daughter entering the room in gloves but no gown, and the son-in-law entering without any personal protective equipment. Which action should the nurse take immediately?","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，护士观察到女儿戴着手套但未穿隔离衣进入病房，女婿未穿戴任何个人防护装备进入病房。护士应立即采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take immediately?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应立即采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the nurse observes the daughter entering the room in gloves but no gown, and the son-in-law entering without any personal protective equipment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段1，护士观察到女儿戴着手套但未穿隔离衣进入病房，女婿未穿戴任何个人防护装备进入病房。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Instruct both visitors to use alcohol-based hand sanitizer immediately before touching the patient.","zh":"指示两名探视者在接触患者之前立即使用免洗手消液。"},{"id":"C","en":"Let them finish the visit because they have already exposed themselves, and educate them before they leave.","zh":"让他们完成探视，因为他们已经暴露，并在他们离开前进行宣教。"},{"id":"B","en":"Interrupt the visit and ask both visitors to step out, perform hand hygiene with soap and water, and don both a gown and gloves.","zh":"中断探视，要求两名探视者退出病房，用肥皂和水进行手卫生，然后穿上隔离衣并戴上手套。"},{"id":"A","en":"Allow the daughter to remain since she has gloves, but ask the son-in-law to don gloves.","zh":"允许女儿留下，因为她戴了手套，但要求女婿也戴上手套。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct action is to politely but promptly interrupt the visit to correct the PPE breach. Contact precautions for C. difficile require all persons entering the room to wear both a gown and gloves, because spores heavily contaminate environmental surfaces. Furthermore, alcohol-based hand sanitizer does not kill C. difficile spores; proper hand washing with soap and water is required.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的做法是礼貌但果断地中断探视，以纠正违反个人防护装备（PPE）规定的行为。艰难梭菌的接触隔离要求所有进入病房的人员必须穿隔离衣并戴手套，因为孢子会严重污染环境表面。此外，免洗手消液不能杀死艰难梭菌孢子；必须用肥皂和水正确洗手。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For C. difficile, contact precautions mean gown and gloves for everyone entering the room, and hand hygiene must be with soap and water, not alcohol-based sanitizer.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于艰难梭菌，接触隔离意味着每个进入病房的人都要穿隔离衣和戴手套，手卫生必须使用肥皂和水，而不是免洗手消液。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":102,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[187,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,63],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the daughter asks the nurse if she can use hand sanitizer instead of washing her hands, and whether she needs to wear a gown and gloves if she is 'just sitting in the chair.' How should the nurse respond?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，女儿问护士是否可以使用免洗手消液代替洗手，以及如果她“只是坐在椅子上”，是否还需要穿隔离衣和戴手套。护士应如何回答？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse respond?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何回答？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the daughter asks the nurse if she can use hand sanitizer instead of washing her hands, and whether she needs to wear a gown and gloves if she is 'just sitting in the chair.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，女儿问护士是否可以使用免洗手消液代替洗手，以及如果她“只是坐在椅子上”，是否还需要穿隔离衣和戴手套。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Tell her she can use hand sanitizer, but only after washing with soap and water first.","zh":"告诉她可以使用免洗手消液，但前提必须是先用肥皂和水洗手。"},{"id":"A","en":"Explain that hand sanitizer is acceptable if she doesn't touch the patient, but a gown is still required.","zh":"解释说如果她不接触患者，可以使用免洗手消液，但仍然需要穿隔离衣。"},{"id":"B","en":"Reinforce that soap and water is required every time, and a gown and gloves are necessary even when just sitting in the room.","zh":"强调每次都必须用肥皂和水洗手，即使只是坐在病房里也必须穿隔离衣和戴手套。"},{"id":"D","en":"State that gown and gloves are optional if she remains in the chair and does not touch environmental surfaces.","zh":"说明如果她一直坐在椅子上并且不接触环境表面，隔离衣和手套是可选的。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. difficile spores resist alcohol denaturation, meaning alcohol-based hand sanitizer is ineffective; mechanical removal through soap-and-water friction is required. Additionally, spores widely contaminate environmental surfaces in the room, including chairs and side tables. Therefore, a gown and gloves are required for anyone entering the room, regardless of whether they intend to physically touch the patient.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艰难梭菌孢子能抵抗酒精的变性作用，这意味着免洗手消液是无效的；必须通过肥皂和水的机械摩擦来清除孢子。此外，孢子会广泛污染病房内的环境表面，包括椅子和床边桌。因此，无论是否打算进行身体接触，任何进入病房的人员都必须穿隔离衣和戴手套。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the absolute rule for C. difficile: soap and water for hand hygiene, and gown and gloves for all persons entering the room, regardless of intended patient contact.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住艰难梭菌的绝对规则：手卫生必须用肥皂和水，所有进入病房的人都必须穿戴隔离衣和手套，无论是否打算接触患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":103,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,55],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the nurse assesses worsening perianal skin maceration and partial-thickness skin loss. Which intervention is the priority for protecting the patient's skin integrity?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，护士评估发现肛周皮肤浸渍加重并出现部分皮层缺失。为了保护患者的皮肤完整性，哪项干预措施是优先考虑的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention is the priority for protecting the patient's skin integrity?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了保护患者的皮肤完整性，哪项干预措施是优先考虑的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the nurse assesses worsening perianal skin maceration and partial-thickness skin loss.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，护士评估发现肛周皮肤浸渍加重并出现部分皮层缺失。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Leave the area open to air to completely dry the maceration.","zh":"将该区域暴露在空气中以完全风干浸渍。"},{"id":"C","en":"Request a prescription for a topical antifungal cream.","zh":"要求医生开具局部抗真菌药膏的处方。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply a moisture barrier cream or ointment after gentle cleansing.","zh":"轻柔清洁后涂抹防潮隔离霜或软膏。"},{"id":"A","en":"Vigorously clean the area with dry wipes after each stool.","zh":"每次排便后用干湿巾大力清洁该区域。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Moisture-associated skin damage from frequent alkaline liquid stool rapidly worsens without a physical barrier. The priority is to gently cleanse the area (avoiding friction) and apply a moisture barrier product (such as a dimethicone or zinc oxide-based cream/ointment) to create a protective layer between the compromised epidermis and the stool.","rationaleCorrectZh":"频繁的碱性液态粪便会导致潮湿相关性皮肤损伤，如果没有物理屏障，损伤会迅速恶化。首要任务是轻柔地清洁该区域（避免摩擦），并涂抹防潮隔离产品（如二甲基硅油或氧化锌基底的乳霜/软膏），在受损表皮和粪便之间形成保护层。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For diarrhea-induced skin breakdown, the key principles are gentle cleansing (no friction) and the application of a thick moisture barrier cream.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于腹泻引起的皮肤破溃，关键原则是轻柔清洁（无摩擦）和涂抹厚厚的防潮隔离霜。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":104,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[169,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,83],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the provider asks the nurse to evaluate whether the patient's home metformin should be restarted. The patient's eGFR is now 33 mL/min/1.73 m² (baseline 42). Which response by the nurse is the most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，医生要求护士评估是否应重新开始使用患者居家服用的二甲双胍。患者目前的eGFR为 33 mL/min/1.73 m²（基线为42）。护士最恰当的回答是哪一项？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is the most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最恰当的回答是哪一项？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The patient's eGFR is now 33 mL/min/1.73 m² (baseline 42).","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者目前的eGFR为 33 mL/min/1.73 m²（基线为42）。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"\"Yes, we should resume it at the previous dose since the eGFR is trending upward.\"","zh":"“是的，我们应该以先前的剂量恢复使用，因为eGFR呈现上升趋势。”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"I recommend holding it for now because the eGFR has not yet returned to her baseline and remains in a caution range.\"","zh":"“我建议暂时停用，因为eGFR尚未恢复到她的基线水平，并且仍处于需要谨慎使用的范围内。”"},{"id":"D","en":"\"We can restart it, but we need to monitor her blood glucose closely for signs of hypoglycemia.\"","zh":"“我们可以重新开始使用，但我们需要密切监测她的血糖，注意低血糖的迹象。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"Metformin is permanently contraindicated now because her eGFR is below 45 mL/min/1.73 m².\"","zh":"“现在二甲双胍是永久禁忌的，因为她的eGFR低于 45 mL/min/1.73 m²。”"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Metformin carries a risk of lactic acidosis that increases with renal impairment. Although the eGFR has improved from 24 to 33 mL/min/1.73 m², it has not returned to her baseline of 42. Furthermore, an eGFR of 30-45 represents a caution range where dosage adjustment and close monitoring are required if initiated or continued. Restarting the medication while the patient is still recovering from acute kidney injury and dehydration is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二甲双胍具有引起乳酸酸中毒的风险，该风险随肾功能损害而增加。虽然eGFR已从24改善至 33 mL/min/1.73 m²，但尚未恢复到其基线水平42。此外，eGFR 30-45属于需要谨慎使用的范围，如果在该范围内开始或继续使用，需要调整剂量并密切监测。在患者仍从急性肾损伤和脱水中恢复时重新开始使用该药物是不安全的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Metformin and kidney disease: remember that poor renal function (especially eGFR < 30) increases the risk of lactic acidosis. Wait for renal recovery before resuming.","testTakingStrategyZh":"二甲双胍与肾脏疾病：记住，不良的肾功能（特别是 eGFR < 30）会增加乳酸酸中毒的风险。在恢复肾功能之前应等待。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The patient's eGFR is now 33 mL/min/1.73 m² (baseline 42).","controlSentenceZh":"患者目前的eGFR为 33 mL/min/1.73 m²（基线为42）。"}
{"queueIndex":105,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus20_case_cdiff_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,56],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse synthesizes the patient's data to evaluate the response to treatment. For each finding, determine if it indicates clinical improvement or requires ongoing monitoring.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，护士综合患者的数据以评估治疗反应。对于每一项发现，请判断它是否表明临床病情改善，或者是否需要持续监测。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, determine if it indicates clinical improvement or requires ongoing monitoring.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每一项发现，请判断它是否表明临床病情改善，或者是否需要持续监测。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse synthesizes the patient's data to evaluate the response to treatment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3，护士综合患者的数据以评估治疗反应。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Stool frequency of two formed-to-semiformed stools in 12 hours","zh":"12小时内排便两次，为成形至半成形便"},{"id":"r2","en":"White blood cell (WBC) count decreasing from 18.2 ×10³/µL to 12.4 ×10³/µL","zh":"白细胞 (WBC) 计数从 18.2 ×10³/µL 降至 12.4 ×10³/µL"},{"id":"r3","en":"eGFR of 33 mL/min/1.73 m² (baseline 42)","zh":"eGFR 为 33 mL/min/1.73 m²（基线为 42）"},{"id":"r4","en":"Urine output of 50 mL/hour","zh":"尿量为 50 mL/hour"},{"id":"r5","en":"Lactate level of 1.2 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸水平为 1.2 mmol/L"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Indicates Improvement","zh":"表明病情改善"},{"id":"c2","en":"Requires Ongoing Monitoring","zh":"需要持续监测"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Decreased stool frequency, a dropping WBC count, restoring urine output, and a normal lactate level all indicate clinical improvement and positive response to treatment. However, an eGFR of 33 mL/min/1.73 m² remains below the patient's baseline of 42, indicating residual renal impairment that requires ongoing monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"排便频率降低、白细胞计数下降、尿量恢复以及乳酸水平正常均表明临床病情改善且对治疗有积极反应。然而，eGFR 为 33 mL/min/1.73 m² 仍低于患者的基线 42，表明存在残留的肾功能损害，需要持续监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by looking at the trend, not just the absolute number. A WBC dropping from 18,200 to 12,400 is an improving trend, even if it has not yet reached the normal range (<10,000).","testTakingStrategyZh":"通过观察趋势而不仅仅是绝对数值来评估结果。即使尚未达到正常范围（<10,000），WBC 从 18,200 降至 12,400 也是一种改善的趋势。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":106,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.61","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.61.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1133,1430],"terminalOffsetsZh":[365,468],"fullStemEn":"Warfarin initiation with enoxaparin bridge therapy at discharge following acute deep vein thrombosis. A 63-year-old man is being prepared for discharge from a medical-surgical unit after a five-day hospitalization for an acute left lower-extremity proximal deep vein thrombosis (DVT) extending from the popliteal to the common femoral vein, confirmed by duplex ultrasonography on admission day. His medical history includes obesity (BMI 34), type 2 diabetes managed with metformin 1,000 mg twice daily, hypertension treated with amlodipine 10 mg daily, and osteoarthritis for which he has been taking over-the-counter ibuprofen 400 mg as needed, typically three to four times per week. He has no history of prior venous thromboembolism, no known bleeding disorders, and no prior exposure to anticoagulants. He lives with his wife, manages his own medications, and works as a long-haul truck driver. He was started on a therapeutic enoxaparin dose of 1 mg/kg subcutaneously every 12 hours on admission day, and warfarin 5 mg daily was initiated on the evening of hospital day 2. His renal function is normal (eGFR 88 mL/min/1.73 m²). The facility's specific discharge protocol calls for continuing the enoxaparin bridge at home until the INR is therapeutic (2.0–3.0) on two consecutive measurements at least 24 hours apart, which is stricter than the standard minimum of five days of overlap with an INR ≥2.0 for at least 24 hours.","fullStemZh":"急性深静脉血栓形成后出院时依诺肝素桥接治疗联合华法林初始治疗。 一名63岁男性患者在内外科病房住院5天后准备出院。他因左下肢近端急性深静脉血栓形成（DVT）（从腘静脉延伸至股总静脉）入院，入院当天通过多普勒超声确认。他的病史包括肥胖（BMI 34）、服用二甲双胍1000 mg，每日两次控制的2型糖尿病、服用氨氯地平10 mg，每日一次控制的高血压，以及骨关节炎，为此他按需服用非处方布洛芬400 mg，通常每周3至4次。他没有既往静脉血栓栓塞史，没有已知的出血性疾病，既往未曾使用过抗凝剂。他与妻子同住，自己管理药物，是一名长途卡车司机。入院当天他开始接受治疗剂量的依诺肝素，1 mg/kg，皮下注射，每12小时一次，并在住院第2天晚上开始每天服用华法林5 mg。他的肾功能正常（eGFR 88 mL/min/1.73 m²）。该机构的具体出院方案要求在家中继续依诺肝素桥接治疗，直到至少相隔24小时的连续两次测量中INR达到治疗范围（2.0-3.0），这比依诺肝素和华法林至少重叠五天且INR≥2.0至少24小时的标准下限更为严格。","terminalSentenceEn":"The facility's specific discharge protocol calls for continuing the enoxaparin bridge at home until the INR is therapeutic (2.0–3.0) on two consecutive measurements at least 24 hours apart, which is stricter than the standard minimum of five days of overlap with an INR ≥2.0 for at least 24 hours.","terminalSentenceZh":"该机构的具体出院方案要求在家中继续依诺肝素桥接治疗，直到至少相隔24小时的连续两次测量中INR达到治疗范围（2.0-3.0），这比依诺肝素和华法林至少重叠五天且INR≥2.0至少24小时的标准下限更为严格。","penultimateSentenceEn":"His renal function is normal (eGFR 88 mL/min/1.73 m²).","penultimateSentenceZh":"他的肾功能正常（eGFR 88 mL/min/1.73 m²）。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This unfolding case tests clinical judgment regarding safely bridging a patient on enoxaparin while initiating warfarin for acute deep vein thrombosis. It evaluates the learner's ability to recognize subtherapeutic INR thresholds and bridge protocol requirements, identify the severe bleeding risk of NSAID use with dual anticoagulation, correct improper enoxaparin injection technique (aspiration), categorize and respond to different urgencies of bleeding signs, provide evidence-based teaching on vitamin K consistency rather than elimination, and address occupational safety concerns for long-haul truck driving before therapeutic anticoagulation is established.","rationaleCorrectZh":"此展开式病例考察了关于在治疗急性深静脉血栓形成时，如何在使用依诺肝素桥接期间安全地起始华法林治疗的临床判断。它评估了学习者识别低于治疗水平的 INR 阈值和桥接方案要求、识别双重抗凝联合使用 NSAID 的严重出血风险、纠正不正确的依诺肝素注射技术（回抽）、对不同紧急程度的出血体征进行分类和响应、提供基于证据的关于维生素 K 摄入需保持一致而不是消除的教育，以及在建立治疗性抗凝之前解决长途卡车驾驶的职业安全问题的能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze the clinical course and ensure you are answering based on the specific stage's findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析临床病程，并确保您是根据特定阶段的检查结果来回答的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":107,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,50],"fullStemEn":"After reviewing the INR result with the patient and his wife at Stage 1, which of the following is the most appropriate response by the nurse regarding the enoxaparin bridge?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 1 与患者及其妻子回顾 INR 结果后，关于依诺肝素桥接治疗，护士最恰当的回答是下列哪一项？","terminalSentenceEn":"After reviewing the INR result with the patient and his wife at Stage 1, which of the following is the most appropriate response by the nurse regarding the enoxaparin bridge?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 1 与患者及其妻子回顾 INR 结果后，关于依诺肝素桥接治疗，护士最恰当的回答是下列哪一项？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_1_1","en":"Explain that the INR of 1.9 is subtherapeutic and the enoxaparin bridge must continue to meet the protocol requirement of consecutive therapeutic values.","zh":"解释 INR 为 1.9 是低于治疗水平的，必须继续依诺肝素桥接治疗以满足方案中连续达到治疗值的要求。"},{"id":"opt_1_2","en":"Inform the patient that an INR of 1.9 is close enough to the target range to discontinue the enoxaparin injections.","zh":"告知患者 INR 为 1.9 已足够接近目标范围，可以停止注射依诺肝素。"},{"id":"opt_1_3","en":"Advise that because the INR is trending upward, the bridge is working well and can be safely stopped today.","zh":"建议由于 INR 呈上升趋势，表明桥接治疗效果良好，今天可以安全停止。"},{"id":"opt_1_4","en":"State that enoxaparin can be discontinued because the patient has already reached three days of overlap therapy.","zh":"说明可以停用依诺肝素，因为患者已经达到了三天的重叠治疗。"}],"correct":["opt_1_1"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The INR of 1.9 has not reached the target range of 2.0–3.0. Furthermore, even if it had reached 2.0, the facility protocol requires two consecutive therapeutic INR values at least 24 hours apart before discontinuing enoxaparin. The patient has had less than five days of overlap so far. Warfarin initially depletes protein C and protein S (natural anticoagulants) before fully suppressing procoagulant factors, creating a paradoxical hypercoagulable state. Stopping the bridge prematurely exposes the patient to thrombus extension or embolization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"INR 为 1.9 尚未达到 2.0-3.0 的目标范围。此外，即使达到了 2.0，该机构的方案也要求在停用依诺肝素前，至少相隔 24 小时的连续两次 INR 达到治疗水平。到目前为止，患者的重叠治疗时间少于 5 天。华法林最初会消耗蛋白 C 和蛋白 S（天然抗凝剂），然后才完全抑制促凝因子，从而产生矛盾的高凝状态。过早停止桥接治疗会使患者面临血栓扩散或栓塞的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that 'close enough' is not an acceptable clinical standard for high-risk medications like anticoagulants. Evidence-based protocols require strict adherence to thresholds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要认识到，对于抗凝剂等高危药物，“足够接近”不是可接受的临床标准。基于循证医学的方案要求严格遵守阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":108,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,42],"fullStemEn":"Based on the medication reconciliation list and the patient's statements at Stage 1, what is the nurse's priority action regarding the patient's ibuprofen use?","fullStemZh":"根据阶段 1 的药物核对清单和患者的陈述，关于患者使用布洛芬，护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the medication reconciliation list and the patient's statements at Stage 1, what is the nurse's priority action regarding the patient's ibuprofen use?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据阶段 1 的药物核对清单和患者的陈述，关于患者使用布洛芬，护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_2_1","en":"Hold the discharge reconciliation and notify the provider to request an alternative analgesic.","zh":"暂停出院药物核对，并通知医生要求开具替代止痛药。"},{"id":"opt_2_4","en":"Confirm that over-the-counter ibuprofen is safe to continue since it is already on the medication list.","zh":"确认可以继续服用非处方布洛芬，因为它已经在药物清单上了。"},{"id":"opt_2_3","en":"Advise the patient to reduce the ibuprofen dose to 200 mg to minimize bleeding risk.","zh":"建议患者将布洛芬剂量减至 200 mg，以尽量减少出血风险。"},{"id":"opt_2_2","en":"Instruct the patient to take the ibuprofen with a full meal to prevent gastrointestinal bleeding.","zh":"指导患者在进食全餐时服用布洛芬，以防止胃肠道出血。"}],"correct":["opt_2_1"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ibuprofen is an NSAID, which inhibits platelet aggregation and independently increases the risk of gastrointestinal bleeding. Combined with warfarin and enoxaparin, ibuprofen substantially raises the risk of a major bleeding event. This is a clinically significant drug interaction that warrants removal from the discharge list and substitution.","rationaleCorrectZh":"布洛芬是一种非甾体抗炎药（NSAID），会抑制血小板凝集并独立增加胃肠道出血的风险。结合华法林和依诺肝素，布洛芬会显著增加发生大出血事件的风险。这是一种具有临床意义的药物相互作用，应当从出院清单中移除并更换其他药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the '3 Gs' and NSAIDs rule for anticoagulants: NSAIDs increase bleeding risk when taken with blood thinners, regardless of whether they are prescribed or over-the-counter.","testTakingStrategyZh":"牢记抗凝药的“3G”和 NSAID 规则：当与血液稀释剂一起服用时，NSAID 会增加出血风险，无论其是处方药还是非处方药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":109,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,48],"fullStemEn":"During the return demonstration at Stage 2, the nurse observes the wife preparing to aspirate before injecting the enoxaparin. What is the appropriate nursing action?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2 的回示教过程中，护士观察到妻子在注射依诺肝素前准备回抽。护士应采取的恰当行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the appropriate nursing action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应采取的恰当行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During the return demonstration at Stage 2, the nurse observes the wife preparing to aspirate before injecting the enoxaparin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段 2 的回示教过程中，护士观察到妻子在注射依诺肝素前准备回抽。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_3_2","en":"Praise the wife for checking for blood return to ensure the medication is not injected into a muscle.","zh":"表扬妻子检查回血以确保药物没有注射到肌肉中。"},{"id":"opt_3_1","en":"Gently correct the technique, explaining that aspiration is not performed with subcutaneous enoxaparin injections.","zh":"温和地纠正该技术，解释皮下注射依诺肝素时不进行回抽。"},{"id":"opt_3_3","en":"Stop the demonstration and instruct the wife to inject into the thigh instead of the abdomen.","zh":"停止示教并指导妻子在腿部而不是腹部进行注射。"},{"id":"opt_3_4","en":"Allow the aspiration but remind the wife to expel the air bubble from the syringe before injecting.","zh":"允许回抽，但提醒妻子在注射前将注射器中的气泡排出。"}],"correct":["opt_3_1"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct technique for subcutaneous enoxaparin is to insert the needle at a 90-degree angle into a pinched abdominal skin fold, inject slowly, and not aspirate. Aspiration increases local tissue trauma and bruising. Correcting this before discharge is essential to prevent injection-site complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"皮下注射依诺肝素的正确技术是以 90 度角将针头刺入捏起的腹部皮肤皱褶，缓慢注射，且不回抽。回抽会增加局部组织创伤和瘀伤。在出院前纠正这一点对于预防注射部位并发症至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For enoxaparin injections, remember the 'Don'ts': Don't aspirate, don't massage the site, and don't expel the air bubble.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于依诺肝素注射，请记住“三个不要”：不要回抽，不要按摩注射部位，不要排出气泡。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":110,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,65],"fullStemEn":"The nurse educates the patient at Stage 2 on recognizing bleeding signs. Categorize each sign based on whether the patient should seek immediate emergency care (call 911) or contact the anticoagulation clinic the same day.","fullStemZh":"护士在阶段 2 对患者进行了识别出血体征的教育。请根据患者应寻求紧急医疗救护（拨打911）还是当天联系抗凝诊所对每个体征进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Categorize each sign based on whether the patient should seek immediate emergency care (call 911) or contact the anticoagulation clinic the same day.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据患者应寻求紧急医疗救护（拨打911）还是当天联系抗凝诊所对每个体征进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse educates the patient at Stage 2 on recognizing bleeding signs.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在阶段 2 对患者进行了识别出血体征的教育。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"columns":[{"id":"col_clinic","en":"Same-Day Clinic Contact","zh":"当天联系诊所"},{"id":"col_emergent","en":"Immediate Emergency Care","zh":"立即寻求紧急救护"}],"rows":[{"id":"row_1","en":"Sudden severe headache with confusion","zh":"突然剧烈头痛伴意识模糊"},{"id":"row_2","en":"Vomiting coffee-ground emesis","zh":"呕吐咖啡渣样呕吐物"},{"id":"row_3","en":"New bruising disproportionate to injury","zh":"与外伤不成比例的新发瘀伤"},{"id":"row_4","en":"A small nosebleed that stops after 10 minutes of firm pressure but recurs later the same day","zh":"施加重压10分钟后停止，但在同一天晚些时候复发的小量鼻出血"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"row_1","columnIds":["col_emergent"]},{"rowId":"row_2","columnIds":["col_emergent"]},{"rowId":"row_3","columnIds":["col_clinic"]},{"rowId":"row_4","columnIds":["col_clinic"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Patients on dual anticoagulation must categorize bleeding by urgency. Sudden headache/confusion suggests intracranial hemorrhage (emergent). Coffee-ground emesis indicates active gastrointestinal bleeding (emergent). New excessive bruising and recurrent superficial bleeding that responds to pressure require prompt evaluation and possible dosage adjustment but are generally managed via the clinic unless bleeding is massive or uncontrolled.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接受双重抗凝治疗的患者必须按紧急程度对出血体征进行分类。突然头痛/意识模糊提示颅内出血（紧急）。呕吐咖啡渣样物表明活动性胃肠道出血（紧急）。新的明显瘀伤以及经按压可止住但复发的浅表出血，需要及时评估并可能调整剂量；除非出血量大或无法控制，通常可通过诊所处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between signs of internal organ bleeding (brain, GI tract), which are life-threatening emergencies, and superficial bleeding (skin, mucosa), which require prompt clinic follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分内脏出血（大脑、胃肠道）的体征（这是危及生命的紧急情况）和浅表出血（皮肤、粘膜）（需要及时到诊所随访）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse educates the patient at Stage 2 on recognizing bleeding signs.","controlSentenceZh":"护士在阶段 2 对患者进行了识别出血体征的教育。"}
{"queueIndex":111,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, how should the nurse address the dietary plans regarding vitamin K and green vegetables?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 3，护士应如何处理关于维生素 K 和绿色蔬菜的饮食计划？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, how should the nurse address the dietary plans regarding vitamin K and green vegetables?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 3，护士应如何处理关于维生素 K 和绿色蔬菜的饮食计划？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_5_4","en":"Advise the patient to only eat green vegetables on the days his INR falls below the target range.","zh":"建议患者只在 INR 降至目标范围以下的那些天吃绿色蔬菜。"},{"id":"opt_5_3","en":"Encourage the daily consumption of spinach and kale to prevent anemia associated with blood thinners.","zh":"鼓励每天食用菠菜和羽衣甘蓝，以预防与血液稀释剂相关的贫血。"},{"id":"opt_5_1","en":"Clarify that the goal is to maintain a consistent daily intake of vitamin K, rather than completely avoiding or abruptly increasing these foods.","zh":"澄清目标是保持每天摄入一致的维生素 K，而不是完全避免或突然增加这些食物。"},{"id":"opt_5_2","en":"Agree with the wife's plan to eliminate all leafy greens to prevent the warfarin from becoming ineffective.","zh":"同意妻子停止食用所有绿叶蔬菜的计划，以防止华法林失效。"}],"correct":["opt_5_1"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warfarin inhibits vitamin K–dependent clotting factors. Abrupt elimination causes INR to rise unpredictably (bleeding risk), while large increases in intake decrease INR (clot risk). Consistency is the evidence-based guidance. Furthermore, warfarin does not cause anemia through nutrient depletion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林抑制依赖维生素K的凝血因子。突然消除会导致 INR 不可预测地上升（出血风险），而大量增加摄入会降低 INR（血栓风险）。保持一致性是基于证据的指导方针。此外，华法林不会通过消耗营养素而导致贫血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For warfarin dietary questions, 'consistency' is almost always the correct answer over 'avoidance' or 'increase'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于华法林饮食的问题，“一致”几乎总是正确答案，而不是“避免”或“增加”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":112,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,43],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the patient asks about returning to work as a long-haul truck driver in four days. What is the most appropriate response by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 3，患者询问关于四天后重返长途卡车司机工作岗位的事情。护士最恰当的回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most appropriate response by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最恰当的回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the patient asks about returning to work as a long-haul truck driver in four days.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段 3，患者询问关于四天后重返长途卡车司机工作岗位的事情。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_6_4","en":"Suggest that the patient discuss this with his employer, as return-to-work clearance is an administrative matter.","zh":"建议患者与他的雇主讨论此事，因为重返工作岗位的许可是行政事务。"},{"id":"opt_6_2","en":"Inform the patient that he can return to work as long as he stops every two hours to stretch his legs.","zh":"告知患者他可以重返工作，只要他每两小时停下来伸展一下腿即可。"},{"id":"opt_6_1","en":"Advise the patient not to return to driving until cleared by the provider, and document this occupational concern for follow-up.","zh":"建议患者在获得医生许可前不要恢复驾驶，并记录这一职业安全顾虑以便随访。"},{"id":"opt_6_3","en":"Tell the patient that driving is safe since he will be on dual anticoagulation to prevent any further clots.","zh":"告诉患者驾驶是安全的，因为他将接受双重抗凝治疗以防止产生更多血栓。"}],"correct":["opt_6_1"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient is on dual anticoagulation with a subtherapeutic INR. Long-haul truck driving involves prolonged immobility (a DVT risk factor), limited access to emergency care, and potential impairment from bleeding events. This poses a significant safety risk that requires provider evaluation before clearance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正接受双重抗凝治疗，且 INR 低于治疗水平。长途卡车驾驶涉及长时间不动（DVT的危险因素）、难以获得急救医疗服务以及出血事件可能造成的损害。这构成了重大的安全风险，需要医生在批准前进行评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that 'prolonged immobility' is a primary risk factor for DVT. Discharging an acute DVT patient back into a high-risk environment without medical clearance is unsafe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到“长时间不动”是 DVT 的主要危险因素。在没有医疗许可的情况下让急性 DVT 患者出院回到高风险环境是不安全的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":113,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.62","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.62.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,379],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,110],"fullStemEn":"Postpartum Depression With Intrusive Thoughts of Infant Harm A 29-year-old primipara is evaluated six weeks after an uncomplicated vaginal birth after screening positive for postpartum depression. She is breastfeeding, recently started sertraline, and reports distressing unwanted thoughts about accidental harm to her infant while maintaining reality testing and denying intent.","fullStemZh":"产后抑郁伴关于伤害婴儿的侵入性想法 一名29岁初产妇在无并发症阴道分娩后6周接受评估，产后抑郁筛查阳性。她正在母乳喂养，最近开始服用舍曲林，并报告关于婴儿意外受伤的痛苦、非自愿想法；她现实检验能力完整，并否认有伤害意图。","terminalSentenceEn":"She is breastfeeding, recently started sertraline, and reports distressing unwanted thoughts about accidental harm to her infant while maintaining reality testing and denying intent.","terminalSentenceZh":"她正在母乳喂养，最近开始服用舍曲林，并报告关于婴儿意外受伤的痛苦、非自愿想法；她现实检验能力完整，并否认有伤害意图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Postpartum Depression With Intrusive Thoughts of Infant Harm A 29-year-old primipara is evaluated six weeks after an uncomplicated vaginal birth after screening positive for postpartum depression.","penultimateSentenceZh":"产后抑郁伴关于伤害婴儿的侵入性想法 一名29岁初产妇在无并发症阴道分娩后6周接受评估，产后抑郁筛查阳性。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on distinguishing ego-dystonic intrusive thoughts in postpartum depression/anxiety from psychosis or intent to harm. The nurse first completes a structured safety assessment, then uses the client's distress, insight, intact reality testing, denial of intent, and protective behavior to support therapeutic education rather than reflexive separation. At follow-up, expanding intrusive thoughts, compulsive checking, and avoidance indicate inadequate response with functional impairment, requiring organized communication with the prescriber while continuing CBT. Later improvement is evaluated across symptoms, screening scores, sleep, function, bonding behaviors, and reduced avoidance. Ongoing teaching should emphasize prescriber-guided medication decisions, continued therapy, breastfeeding-informed discussion, relapse prevention, and early planning for future pregnancies.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的核心是区分产后抑郁/焦虑中的自我不协调侵入性想法，与精神病性症状或伤害意图。护士首先完成结构化安全评估，然后根据患者的痛苦、洞察力、现实检验完整、否认意图和保护性行为，进行治疗性宣教，而不是反射性母婴分离。随访时，侵入性想法扩大、强迫性检查和回避行为提示反应不足并有功能受损，需要将有组织的资料传达给开药者，同时继续认知行为治疗。之后的改善应从症状、筛查分数、睡眠、功能、亲子互动行为和回避减少等方面综合评估。持续宣教应强调由开药者指导用药决定、继续治疗、结合母乳喂养情况讨论、预防复发，以及为未来妊娠提前计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding psychosocial cases, establish immediate safety first, then interpret cues by intent, insight, reality testing, function, and change over time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式心理社会病例中，先确认即时安全，再根据意图、洞察力、现实检验、功能和随时间变化来解读线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":114,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,69],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, classify each cue after the structured safety assessment.","fullStemZh":"在阶段1完成结构化安全评估后，对每项线索进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, classify each cue after the structured safety assessment.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段1完成结构化安全评估后，对每项线索进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The client says the thoughts horrify her and she would never hurt the infant.","zh":"患者说这些想法让她非常恐惧，并表示自己绝不会伤害婴儿。"},{"id":"r2","en":"She identifies the thoughts as her own unwanted thoughts, not voices or commands.","zh":"她认为这些是自己不想要的想法，不是声音或命令。"},{"id":"r3","en":"She has no delusions or disorganized thinking and remains oriented.","zh":"她没有妄想或思维紊乱，定向力保持完整。"},{"id":"r4","en":"She reports poor sleep, anhedonia, guilt, and a PHQ-9 score of 18.","zh":"她报告睡眠差、快感缺失、内疚，PHQ-9为18分。"},{"id":"r5","en":"She denies suicidal ideation and denies intent or plan to harm the infant.","zh":"她否认自杀意念，也否认有伤害婴儿的意图或计划。"},{"id":"r6","en":"If present, command hallucinations or delusional belief that the infant is evil would change the priority.","zh":"如果出现命令性幻听或认为婴儿邪恶的妄想性信念，护理优先级会改变。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Supports depression/anxiety severity but does not by itself indicate psychosis","zh":"支持抑郁/焦虑严重程度，但本身不表示精神病性症状"},{"id":"c3","en":"Would suggest psychosis or an emergency safety risk if present","zh":"如果存在，则提示精神病性症状或紧急安全风险"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports ego-dystonic intrusive thoughts with intact reality testing","zh":"支持自我不协调的侵入性想法，且现实检验完整"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client's distress, insight, denial of intent, intact reality testing, and protective avoidance support ego-dystonic intrusive thoughts associated with postpartum depression/anxiety rather than postpartum psychosis. Depression severity cues are clinically important but do not alone establish psychosis. Command hallucinations, delusions, disorganization, or intent to harm would require urgent escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者对想法感到痛苦、保有洞察力、否认意图、现实检验完整，并采取保护性回避，这些支持产后抑郁/焦虑相关的自我不协调侵入性想法，而不是产后精神病。抑郁严重程度线索很重要，但单独不能证明精神病性症状。命令性幻听、妄想、思维紊乱或伤害意图则需要紧急升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For intrusive postpartum harm thoughts, first separate content from intent and reality testing. Distress and avoidance are different from command hallucinations or delusions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到产后伤害相关侵入性想法时，先区分“想法内容”和“意图及现实检验”。痛苦和回避不同于命令性幻听或妄想。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":115,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,60],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the structured safety assessment shows no intent to harm, no psychosis, and intact ability to care for the infant. Which nursing responses are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，结构化安全评估显示患者无伤害意图、无精神病性症状，并且照护婴儿能力完整。哪些护理回应是合适的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing responses are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理回应是合适的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Document the risk assessment, denial of intent, protective behaviors, teaching, and follow-up plan.","zh":"记录风险评估、患者否认意图、保护性行为、宣教内容和随访计划。"},{"id":"E","en":"Reassure the mother privately by sharing the client's detailed assessment results without asking the client.","zh":"不询问患者，私下向母亲说明患者详细评估结果以让母亲放心。"},{"id":"C","en":"Explain that unwanted, distressing intrusive thoughts can occur in postpartum depression/anxiety and are different from intent to harm.","zh":"解释不想要且令人痛苦的侵入性想法可见于产后抑郁/焦虑，并不同于伤害意图。"},{"id":"B","en":"Tell the client that any thought about infant harm requires immediate separation from the infant.","zh":"告诉患者，任何关于伤害婴儿的想法都需要立即与婴儿分离。"},{"id":"A","en":"Thank the client for disclosing the thoughts and validate that the thoughts are frightening to her.","zh":"感谢患者说出这些想法，并肯定这些想法对她来说很可怕。"},{"id":"D","en":"With the client's permission, include her mother or partner in education and the support plan.","zh":"经患者同意，将母亲或伴侣纳入宣教和支持计划。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After safety has been established, the nurse should respond therapeutically, reduce shame, explain the difference between intrusive thoughts and intent, protect confidentiality, involve supports with permission, and document assessment and planning. Blanket separation or disclosure to family without permission would be inappropriate when the assessment does not show intent, psychosis, or unsafe care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"确认安全后，护士应进行治疗性回应，减少羞耻感，解释侵入性想法与意图的区别，保护保密性，经同意纳入支持者，并记录评估和计划。在评估未显示意图、精神病性症状或照护不安全时，一概要求母婴分离或未经许可向家属透露详情都是不合适的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic reassurance is safest when it follows a documented assessment. Pair validation with confidentiality and a concrete safety plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性安慰在有记录的评估之后最安全。将肯定、保密和具体安全计划结合起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":116,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, complete the clinical judgment statement about the symptom trajectory.","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，完成关于症状变化轨迹的临床判断陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, complete the clinical judgment statement about the symptom trajectory.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段2，完成关于症状变化轨迹的临床判断陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The Stage 2 findings are most consistent with {{1}}; the nurse should {{2}}.","zh":"阶段2的发现最符合 {{1}}；护士应 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"inadequate response with emerging obsessive-compulsive features and functional impairment","zh":"反应不足，并出现强迫相关特征和功能受损"},{"id":"o3","en":"probable sertraline adverse effect requiring the client to stop the medication immediately","zh":"可能是舍曲林不良反应，需要患者立即停药"},{"id":"o1","en":"adequate early response that requires only routine reassurance","zh":"早期反应充分，只需要常规安慰"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"tell the client to wait silently until the current dose works because intrusive thoughts always resolve quickly","zh":"告诉患者安静等待现剂量起效，因为侵入性想法总会很快消失"},{"id":"o1","en":"notify the prescribing provider with screening-score trends, functional changes, and safety assessment findings","zh":"将筛查分数趋势、功能变化和安全评估结果通知开药提供者"},{"id":"o3","en":"independently increase the sertraline dose because the client asked","zh":"因为患者询问，就由护士自行增加舍曲林剂量"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At Stage 2, depression scores and sleep have improved only slightly, while intrusive thoughts have expanded, checking has become repetitive, and avoidance now limits bathing and leaving the house. This pattern suggests undertreated symptoms with obsessive-compulsive features and functional impairment. The nurse should communicate organized assessment data to the prescriber and reinforce ongoing CBT; dose changes remain a prescriber decision.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在阶段2，抑郁评分和睡眠仅轻度改善，但侵入性想法扩大，检查行为反复，回避行为已限制洗澡和出门。这种模式提示症状治疗不足，并有强迫相关特征和功能受损。护士应将有组织的评估资料传达给开药者，并强化继续认知行为治疗；剂量调整仍由开药者决定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not judge response by one score alone. Compare symptom intensity, function, safety, sleep, and validated tools over time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只凭一个评分判断治疗反应。要纵向比较症状强度、功能、安全、睡眠和量表结果。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":117,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,107],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,34],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the client asks, \"Should my sertraline dose be increased?\" Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，患者问：“我的舍曲林剂量应该增加吗？”护士的哪项回应最佳？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项回应最佳？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the client asks, \"Should my sertraline dose be increased?\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，患者问：“我的舍曲林剂量应该增加吗？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"\"Because you are breastfeeding, you should stop sertraline rather than increase it.\"","zh":"“因为你在母乳喂养，所以应该停用舍曲林，而不是增加剂量。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"Dose changes are not part of nursing care, so you should ask someone else at your next visit.\"","zh":"“剂量调整不属于护理，所以你下次就诊时问别人。”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"That is an appropriate question. I will give the prescriber your symptom changes, screening scores, and safety assessment so the dose can be reviewed.\"","zh":"“这个问题很合适。我会把你的症状变化、筛查分数和安全评估结果提供给开药者，以便复核剂量。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"Your symptoms have not improved enough, so I will tell you to increase the dose tonight.\"","zh":"“你的症状改善不够，所以我会让你今晚增加剂量。”"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse stays within scope by acknowledging the concern, gathering and communicating relevant clinical data, and advocating for timely prescriber review. The nurse should not independently change a prescription, dismiss the question, or recommend stopping sertraline solely because the client is breastfeeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在执业范围内应承认患者担忧，收集并传达相关临床资料，并倡导及时由开药者复核。护士不应自行改变处方、不应忽视问题，也不应仅因患者母乳喂养就建议停用舍曲林。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When medication titration is requested, choose the answer that gathers data, communicates with the prescriber, and avoids independent prescribing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者询问药物调剂量时，选择收集资料、联系开药者、避免护士自行开药的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":118,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,38],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which statements should the nurse include when evaluating the treatment response and providing anticipatory guidance? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，护士评估治疗反应并提供预期指导时，应包括哪些说明？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which statements should the nurse include when evaluating the treatment response and providing anticipatory guidance?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3，护士评估治疗反应并提供预期指导时，应包括哪些说明？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"\"A history of postpartum depression can increase recurrence risk in a future pregnancy, so early screening and a prevention plan are important.\"","zh":"“有产后抑郁史可能增加以后妊娠复发风险，因此早期筛查和预防计划很重要。”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"Keep using the CBT strategies and follow up with the prescriber before making any medication changes.\"","zh":"“继续使用认知行为治疗策略，在做任何药物改变前先随访开药者。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"Sertraline is commonly considered compatible with breastfeeding, but continue discussing infant and maternal monitoring with the prescriber and pediatric clinician.\"","zh":"“舍曲林通常被认为与母乳喂养相容，但仍应继续与开药者和儿科医生讨论母婴监测。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"Your sleep, appetite, functioning, screening scores, and ability to care for the baby show meaningful improvement.\"","zh":"“你的睡眠、食欲、功能、筛查分数以及照护婴儿的能力都显示出有意义的改善。”"},{"id":"D","en":"\"Because you feel better, you can stop sertraline abruptly today.\"","zh":"“既然你感觉好转，今天就可以突然停用舍曲林。”"},{"id":"E","en":"\"The duration of medication treatment should be individualized with the prescriber; many plans continue medication for several months after remission to reduce relapse risk.\"","zh":"“用药持续时间应由你和开药者个体化决定；许多方案会在症状缓解后继续用药数月，以降低复发风险。”"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stage 3 shows a positive but incomplete response: improved sleep, appetite, function, bonding behaviors, fewer intrusive thoughts, and lower EPDS and PHQ-9 scores. Teaching should support ongoing CBT, prescriber-guided medication decisions, breastfeeding-compatible treatment discussions, relapse prevention, and early planning for future pregnancies. Abrupt discontinuation after early improvement can increase relapse risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阶段3显示积极但尚未完全结束的治疗反应：睡眠、食欲、功能、亲子互动行为改善，侵入性想法减少，EPDS和PHQ-9下降。宣教应支持继续认知行为治疗、由开药者指导药物决定、讨论与母乳喂养相容的治疗、预防复发，以及为未来妊娠提前计划。早期好转后突然停药可能增加复发风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For outcome evaluation, look for improvement across tools and daily function, then choose teaching that prevents relapse rather than ending treatment prematurely.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估疗效时，要看量表和日常功能的多方面改善；宣教应预防复发，而不是过早结束治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":119,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.63","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.63.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[303,430],"terminalOffsetsZh":[108,148],"fullStemEn":"Elder neglect with medication mismanagement in a home health setting An 81-year-old woman with HFrEF, type 2 diabetes, mild cognitive impairment, CKD stage 3a, and a stage II sacral pressure injury is seen by home health 10 days after discharge for heart failure. Her adult son is the listed caregiver. The nurse finds clinical decline, poor intake, inconsistent medication use, no monitoring logs, and a worsened pressure injury.","fullStemZh":"居家护理中的老年人疏忽照护与用药管理不当 一名81岁女性患有射血分数降低型心力衰竭、2型糖尿病、轻度认知障碍、3a期慢性肾病和骶尾部II期压力性损伤。因心衰住院后出院10天，居家护士进行随访。其成年儿子为主要照护者。护士发现患者病情恶化、进食饮水不足、用药不一致、没有监测记录，且压力性损伤加重。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse finds clinical decline, poor intake, inconsistent medication use, no monitoring logs, and a worsened pressure injury.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士发现患者病情恶化、进食饮水不足、用药不一致、没有监测记录，且压力性损伤加重。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her adult son is the listed caregiver.","penultimateSentenceZh":"其成年儿子为主要照护者。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires the nurse to integrate home-environment evidence, caregiver behavior, medication fill patterns, wound deterioration, and objective physiologic instability. The Stage 1 priority is not to attribute the decline only to chronic disease: the pattern supports suspected elder neglect while severe hypokalemia, dehydration, AKI, and hyperglycemia require clinical escalation. Stage 2 emphasizes safe protocol-based IV potassium and magnesium replacement with telemetry and pump control. Stage 3 shows partial physiologic response but persistent renal, wound, nutrition, glucose, and discharge-safety concerns; the nurse collaborates with social work, APS processes, wound care, nutrition, and providers rather than independently forcing placement or prematurely returning the client to an unsafe setting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求护士整合家庭环境证据、照护者行为、药物余量模式、伤口恶化和客观生理不稳定。阶段1的重点不是把恶化完全归因于慢性病；整体模式支持疑似老年人疏忽照护，同时严重低钾、脱水、急性肾损伤和高血糖需要临床升级处理。阶段2强调按方案安全静脉补钾和补镁，并使用心电监护和输液泵控制。阶段3显示生理状况部分好转，但肾功能、伤口、营养、血糖和出院安全问题仍存在；护士应与社工、APS流程、伤口护理、营养和提供者合作，而不是单独强制安置或过早让患者回到不安全环境。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding cases, track what data are available at each stage, identify the immediate physiologic threat, and also act on legal/ethical safety duties when the pattern supports suspected neglect.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做展开式病例时，要追踪每个阶段可用的数据，识别即时生理威胁；当模式支持疑似疏忽照护时，也要履行法律和伦理安全职责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":120,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,52],"fullStemEn":"At the first home visit, classify each finding according to whether it supports suspected elder neglect by the responsible caregiver or is primarily a medical finding that still requires follow-up.","fullStemZh":"在第一次居家随访时，将每项发现分类为支持怀疑主要照护者存在老年人疏忽照护，或主要属于仍需跟进的医学发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"At the first home visit, classify each finding according to whether it supports suspected elder neglect by the responsible caregiver or is primarily a medical finding that still requires follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"在第一次居家随访时，将每项发现分类为支持怀疑主要照护者存在老年人疏忽照护，或主要属于仍需跟进的医学发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"No blood glucose log or daily weights despite discharge teaching","zh":"出院教育后仍没有血糖记录或每日体重记录"},{"id":"r2","en":"Soiled incontinence brief reportedly unchanged since the previous evening","zh":"据患者称失禁尿裤从前一晚起未更换"},{"id":"r3","en":"Potassium bottle nearly full and insulin pen appears unused","zh":"氯化钾瓶几乎满，胰岛素笔看似未使用"},{"id":"r4","en":"Mild cognitive impairment documented 6 months earlier","zh":"6个月前记录有轻度认知障碍"},{"id":"r5","en":"Sacral pressure injury is larger with maceration and drainage","zh":"骶尾部压力性损伤增大，并有浸渍和渗液"},{"id":"r6","en":"Sodium is 149 mEq/L and BUN is 48 mg/dL","zh":"钠149 mEq/L，BUN 48 mg/dL"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Supports suspected neglect pattern","zh":"支持疑似疏忽照护模式"},{"id":"c2","en":"Medical finding requiring follow-up but not specific to neglect by itself","zh":"需医学跟进，但单独看并非特异性疏忽证据"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pattern of omitted monitoring, unchanged soiled brief, medication evidence inconsistent with the prescribed regimen, and a worsened pressure injury after prolonged sitting supports suspected neglect. Cognitive impairment and abnormal labs require care, but by themselves they do not prove neglect; they become concerning when integrated with caregiver failures and environmental evidence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未进行监测、失禁尿裤长时间未更换、用药证据与医嘱不符，以及长期坐位后压力性损伤加重，这些共同支持疑似疏忽照护。认知障碍和异常化验需要处理，但单独不能证明疏忽；当它们与照护者未履行照护任务和环境证据结合时才更令人担忧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for a pattern across client condition, environment, caregiver behavior, and objective evidence rather than treating each cue in isolation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要孤立看每个线索，要把患者状况、环境、照护者行为和客观证据合并判断是否形成模式。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":121,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"Which medication-related problem is the most immediate safety priority at the first home visit?","fullStemZh":"第一次居家随访时，哪一项用药相关问题是最紧急的安全优先事项？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication-related problem is the most immediate safety priority at the first home visit?","terminalSentenceZh":"第一次居家随访时，哪一项用药相关问题是最紧急的安全优先事项？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Carvedilol should be doubled because the client no longer has leg edema","zh":"因患者下肢不再水肿，应将卡维地洛加倍"},{"id":"B","en":"Metformin appears to have been taken as prescribed, so the client should receive an extra dose to lower the glucose","zh":"二甲双胍似乎按医嘱服用，因此应额外服用一次以降低血糖"},{"id":"C","en":"The unused insulin pen explains the hyperglycemia, so glucose correction is more urgent than the potassium result","zh":"未使用的胰岛素笔解释了高血糖，因此纠正血糖比处理钾值更紧急"},{"id":"A","en":"Furosemide appears to have been given while potassium chloride was likely omitted, contributing to severe hypokalemia with bradycardia and hypotension","zh":"呋塞米似乎已服用，而氯化钾很可能漏用，导致严重低钾并伴心动过缓和低血压"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nearly empty furosemide bottle with a nearly full potassium bottle, potassium 2.9 mEq/L, bradycardia, hypotension, and later ECG changes point to immediate cardiac risk from hypokalemia. Hyperglycemia from missed insulin is important, but the potassium deficit with hemodynamic and conduction risk is the priority to escalate for provider-directed treatment and monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呋塞米瓶几乎空、氯化钾瓶几乎满，加上钾2.9 mEq/L、心动过缓、低血压以及随后出现的心电图改变，提示低钾带来的即时心脏风险。漏用胰岛素导致高血糖也重要，但伴血流动力学和传导风险的低钾更需要优先升级处理并按提供者医嘱监测治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several problems exist, prioritize the one most likely to cause rapid deterioration: unstable vital signs plus a dangerous electrolyte abnormality outrank a moderate glucose elevation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"多个问题同时存在时，优先处理最可能迅速恶化的问题：不稳定生命体征加危险电解质异常，高于中度血糖升高。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":122,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,30],"fullStemEn":"After completing the first home assessment, which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"完成第一次居家评估后，哪些护理措施是合适的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After completing the first home assessment, which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"完成第一次居家评估后，哪些护理措施是合适的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document objective findings, medication evidence, caregiver statements, and notifications made","zh":"记录客观发现、用药证据、照护者陈述以及已通知的对象"},{"id":"F","en":"Teach the son again and leave the client at home because no one has confirmed neglect yet","zh":"再次教育儿子，并因尚未确认疏忽照护而让患者留在家中"},{"id":"D","en":"Wait to report until the nurse can prove the son intentionally caused harm","zh":"等到护士能证明儿子故意造成伤害后再报告"},{"id":"C","en":"Initiate the agency mandatory reporting process for suspected elder neglect according to state law and facility policy","zh":"按照州法律和机构政策启动机构关于疑似老年人疏忽照护的强制报告流程"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the home health agency supervisor and primary care provider about the acute findings and suspected neglect","zh":"向居家护理机构主管和初级保健提供者报告急性发现和疑似疏忽照护"},{"id":"B","en":"Arrange emergency department evaluation as directed for electrolyte derangements, dehydration, and acute kidney injury","zh":"按指示安排急诊评估电解质紊乱、脱水和急性肾损伤"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has acute clinical instability that exceeds home health capability and a pattern that meets the threshold for suspected neglect. The nurse should escalate clinically, arrange emergency evaluation as ordered, follow mandatory reporting policy, and document objective findings and communications. Proof of intent is not required to report suspicion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者存在超出居家护理能力的急性临床不稳定，同时表现出达到疑似疏忽照护报告门槛的模式。护士应进行临床升级处理，按医嘱安排急诊评估，遵循强制报告政策，并记录客观发现和沟通内容。报告疑似情况不需要证明故意伤害。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In abuse or neglect questions, separate treatment of acute medical instability from protective reporting duties; both may need to happen.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到虐待或疏忽照护题时，要区分急性医学不稳定的处理和保护性报告义务；两者可能都需要执行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":123,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,67],"fullStemEn":"In the emergency department, the provider orders potassium chloride 10 mEq in 100 mL NS over 1 hour through a peripheral IV. Which nursing actions are appropriate before and during administration? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在急诊，提供者开立氯化钾10 mEq加入100 mL NS，经外周静脉1小时输注。给药前和给药过程中哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate before and during administration?","penultimateSentenceZh":"给药前和给药过程中哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Use an infusion pump for the potassium infusion","zh":"使用输液泵输注氯化钾"},{"id":"F","en":"Continue to monitor rhythm, repeat labs as ordered, and assess for signs of overcorrection","zh":"继续监测心律、按医嘱复查化验，并评估是否出现纠正过度的迹象"},{"id":"E","en":"Confirm that magnesium replacement is being administered as ordered","zh":"确认镁剂补充正按医嘱执行"},{"id":"D","en":"Give the dose by IV push because the potassium is severely low","zh":"因钾严重偏低而静脉推注该剂量"},{"id":"C","en":"Monitor the peripheral IV site for pain, infiltration, or phlebitis","zh":"监测外周静脉部位是否疼痛、渗漏或静脉炎"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify continuous telemetry is active before starting the infusion","zh":"开始输注前确认持续心电监护已开启"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The order matches the ED protocol stated in the case: 10 mEq/hr and 10 mEq/100 mL through a peripheral line, using an infusion pump with continuous telemetry. The nurse also monitors the IV site, rhythm, and follow-up labs. Magnesium repletion supports potassium correction when magnesium is low. IV push potassium is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该医嘱符合病例中列出的急诊方案：外周静脉10 mEq/hr，浓度10 mEq/100 mL，使用输液泵并持续心电监护。护士还需监测静脉部位、心律和后续化验。低镁时补镁有助于纠正低钾。静脉推注氯化钾不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-alert IV electrolytes, check the prescribed concentration, route, rate-control device, monitoring, and follow-up labs before focusing on less urgent tasks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理高警示静脉电解质时，先核对浓度、途径、速度控制设备、监测和复查化验，再考虑次要任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":124,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,64],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse reviews the provider order to discontinue metformin because the client's eGFR dropped to 28 mL/min/1.73 m2 during the acute kidney injury. Which interpretation is best?","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，护士复核提供者因患者急性肾损伤期间eGFR降至28 mL/min/1.73 m2而停用二甲双胍的医嘱。哪项理解最恰当？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项理解最恰当？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse reviews the provider order to discontinue metformin because the client's eGFR dropped to 28 mL/min/1.73 m2 during the acute kidney injury.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3，护士复核提供者因患者急性肾损伤期间eGFR降至28 mL/min/1.73 m2而停用二甲双胍的医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The order is appropriate; metformin should remain held until renal function is reassessed and the provider determines whether it is safe to resume","zh":"该医嘱合适；二甲双胍应继续暂停，直到重新评估肾功能并由提供者判断是否可安全恢复"},{"id":"B","en":"The nurse should restart metformin because the repeat eGFR improved to 33 mL/min/1.73 m2","zh":"护士应重新开始二甲双胍，因为复查eGFR已改善至33 mL/min/1.73 m2"},{"id":"D","en":"Metformin is the priority medication to treat the client's acute hypokalemia","zh":"二甲双胍是治疗患者急性低钾的优先药物"},{"id":"C","en":"Metformin should be continued because the client has taken it chronically","zh":"因患者长期服用二甲双胍，所以应继续使用"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client had acute kidney injury with eGFR 28 mL/min/1.73 m2, and metformin accumulation in significant renal impairment increases lactic acidosis risk. Even though the repeat eGFR improved to 33, the nurse should not independently restart it; renal function must be reassessed and provider clearance is required.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者出现急性肾损伤，eGFR曾为28 mL/min/1.73 m2；在明显肾功能受损时二甲双胍蓄积会增加乳酸性酸中毒风险。即使复查eGFR改善至33，护士也不应自行恢复用药；需要重新评估肾功能并由提供者批准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For medication-safety questions, compare the drug with current organ function and ask whether the nurse has authority to resume or alter it independently.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到用药安全题时，将药物与当前器官功能相对照，并判断护士是否有权独立恢复或调整该药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":125,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,44],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which findings show that continued monitoring or interdisciplinary planning is still needed before discharge back to the same home environment? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，哪些发现表明在出院回到同一家庭环境前仍需继续监测或跨专业计划？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which findings show that continued monitoring or interdisciplinary planning is still needed before discharge back to the same home environment?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3，哪些发现表明在出院回到同一家庭环境前仍需继续监测或跨专业计划？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"U waves resolved and the QT interval shortened","zh":"U波消失，QT间期缩短"},{"id":"F","en":"Blood pressure and heart rate improved after treatment","zh":"治疗后血压和心率改善"},{"id":"E","en":"APS referral and safe-discharge care conference are still in progress","zh":"APS转介和安全出院护理会议仍在进行中"},{"id":"A","en":"Potassium improved to 3.4 mEq/L but remains below the usual normal range","zh":"钾改善至3.4 mEq/L，但仍低于通常正常范围"},{"id":"C","en":"Creatinine remains above the client's baseline after initial fluids","zh":"初始补液后肌酐仍高于患者基线"},{"id":"D","en":"The pressure injury is still worsened and nutrition markers are low","zh":"压力性损伤仍然恶化，营养指标偏低"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is improving, but improvement is not resolution. Potassium remains low, kidney function has not returned to baseline, the wound and nutrition deficits need active treatment, and the protective services/discharge-safety process is unresolved. Resolved U waves and improved vital signs are reassuring response cues, not reasons to stop planning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在改善，但改善不等于问题完全解决。钾仍偏低，肾功能尚未回到基线，伤口和营养缺陷仍需积极处理，保护服务和出院安全流程尚未完成。U波消失和生命体征改善是令人放心的治疗反应线索，而不是停止计划的理由。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In outcome-evaluation items, distinguish response to treatment from full readiness for discharge; persistent physiologic, wound, nutrition, and safety risks still matter.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做结局评估题时，要区分治疗有反应和完全可出院；持续存在的生理、伤口、营养和安全风险仍然重要。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":126,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.64","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.64.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[428,513],"terminalOffsetsZh":[115,138],"fullStemEn":"Tuberculosis rule-out in a newly admitted patient with chronic cough and immunosuppression A 47-year-old man is admitted for evaluation of a 6-week productive cough with occasional blood-streaked sputum, drenching night sweats, 7 kg weight loss, and fatigue. He takes methotrexate and chronic prednisone for rheumatoid arthritis and works as a long-haul bus driver with frequent travel through crowded, poorly ventilated buses. He is placed in an airborne infection isolation room while tuberculosis is evaluated.","fullStemZh":"新入院免疫抑制患者因慢性咳嗽接受结核病排查 一名47岁男性因持续6周的咳嗽入院评估，咳少量黄痰并偶有血丝，伴盗汗、体重下降7公斤和乏力。他因类风湿关节炎长期使用甲氨蝶呤和泼尼松，并从事长途客车驾驶，常处于拥挤、通风不良的车厢环境。因需排查结核病，患者被安置在空气传播隔离病房。","terminalSentenceEn":"He is placed in an airborne infection isolation room while tuberculosis is evaluated.","terminalSentenceZh":"因需排查结核病，患者被安置在空气传播隔离病房。","penultimateSentenceEn":"He takes methotrexate and chronic prednisone for rheumatoid arthritis and works as a long-haul bus driver with frequent travel through crowded, poorly ventilated buses.","penultimateSentenceZh":"他因类风湿关节炎长期使用甲氨蝶呤和泼尼松，并从事长途客车驾驶，常处于拥挤、通风不良的车厢环境。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests the integrated nursing management of suspected and confirmed pulmonary TB in an immunosuppressed patient. Key cues include chronic productive cough, blood-streaked sputum, night sweats, weight loss, right upper lobe cavitary lesion, positive IGRA, positive AFB smears, and positive NAAT. Safe nursing care prioritizes airborne isolation with staff N95 protection, correct patient source control during transport, public-health coordination for contact investigation, baseline vision testing before ethambutol, safe handling of chronic prednisone through tapering, close monitoring of hepatotoxicity using the provider's stated threshold, and psychosocial support to promote adherence and reduce isolation-related distress.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查免疫抑制患者疑似并确诊肺结核时的综合护理管理。关键线索包括慢性咳嗽咳痰、痰中带血、盗汗、体重下降、右上肺空洞性病灶、IGRA阳性、AFB涂片阳性和NAAT阳性。安全护理的重点包括：空气传播隔离和工作人员N95防护；患者转运时正确进行源头控制；与公共卫生部门协调接触者调查；乙胺丁醇前进行基线视力检查；长期泼尼松需逐渐减量；按医嘱阈值密切监测肝毒性；并提供心理社会支持，以促进治疗依从性、减轻隔离相关痛苦。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding infection-control cases, track when data become available and separate three decisions: protecting staff now, coordinating public health follow-up, and monitoring treatment safety over time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式感染控制病例中，要追踪信息何时出现，并区分三类决策：立即保护工作人员、协调公共卫生随访、以及随时间监测治疗安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":127,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,50],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the nursing assistant asks whether she may enter the AIIR wearing only a standard surgical mask to take vital signs quickly. Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，护理助理询问是否可以只戴普通外科口罩进入AIIR快速测量生命体征。护士最合适的回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最合适的回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the nursing assistant asks whether she may enter the AIIR wearing only a standard surgical mask to take vital signs quickly.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段1，护理助理询问是否可以只戴普通外科口罩进入AIIR快速测量生命体征。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"You may enter with a surgical mask because the exposure will be brief.","zh":"可以只戴外科口罩进入，因为接触时间很短。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the patient to cover his mouth with tissues so staff can use droplet precautions instead.","zh":"请患者用纸巾遮住口鼻，这样工作人员可以改用飞沫隔离措施。"},{"id":"B","en":"Do not enter unless you are wearing the required fit-tested N95 respirator for this airborne isolation room.","zh":"除非佩戴本空气传播隔离房间要求的、经密合性测试的N95呼吸防护口罩，否则不要进入。"},{"id":"C","en":"A surgical mask is acceptable if the patient also wears a surgical mask while you are in the room.","zh":"如果患者在你进入房间时也戴外科口罩，那么你戴外科口罩即可。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient is in airborne infection isolation for suspected or confirmed infectious TB. Staff entering the AIIR need the required respiratory protection; a standard surgical mask is for patient source control during transport and does not replace staff N95 protection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者因疑似或确诊具有传染性的结核病接受空气传播隔离。进入AIIR的工作人员需要规定的呼吸防护；普通外科口罩用于患者转运时的源头控制，不能替代工作人员的N95防护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For isolation questions, separate protection for staff from source control for the patient. TB is airborne, so staff entering the room require respirator-level protection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到隔离题时，要区分工作人员防护和患者源头控制。结核病按空气传播处理，工作人员进入房间需要呼吸防护级别的防护。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":128,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,42],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the patient asks, 'Does my coworker need to be tested for TB?' Which response best supports safe care coordination?","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，患者问：“我的同事需要接受结核病检测吗？”哪项回应最能支持安全的照护协调？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response best supports safe care coordination?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项回应最能支持安全的照护协调？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the patient asks, 'Does my coworker need to be tested for TB?'","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段1，患者问：“我的同事需要接受结核病检测吗？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Your coworker does not need testing unless they have symptoms.","zh":"除非你的同事有症状，否则不需要检测。"},{"id":"D","en":"Anyone who has ever ridden with you in the bus must immediately start tuberculosis medications.","zh":"任何曾经坐过你车的人都必须立即开始抗结核药物治疗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give me your coworker's phone number and I will personally tell them to come to the hospital for testing today.","zh":"把你同事的电话号码给我，我会亲自通知他们今天来医院检测。"},{"id":"B","en":"I will explain that the public health team will conduct a contact investigation and determine who needs evaluation based on exposure details.","zh":"我会说明公共卫生团队会进行接触者调查，并根据暴露细节决定谁需要评估。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Contact investigation is coordinated through public health and is based on exposure duration, proximity, ventilation, and individual risk. The nurse should explain the process and coordinate, not independently decide who does or does not need testing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接触者调查由公共卫生部门协调，并根据暴露时间、距离、通风情况和个体风险来判断。护士应解释流程并协助协调，而不是自行决定谁需要或不需要检测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a public health process is involved, choose the answer that explains and coordinates the process without overstepping the nurse's role.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到涉及公共卫生流程的题目，选择能解释并协调流程、但不超越护士职责的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":129,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,138],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,37],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, ethambutol is prescribed as part of the initial four-drug TB regimen. Which nursing action is essential before the first dose?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，乙胺丁醇被纳入初始四联抗结核方案。首次给药前哪项护理措施最重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is essential before the first dose?","terminalSentenceZh":"首次给药前哪项护理措施最重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, ethambutol is prescribed as part of the initial four-drug TB regimen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，乙胺丁醇被纳入初始四联抗结核方案。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Teach the patient that orange urine is the dose-limiting toxicity of ethambutol.","zh":"告知患者橙色尿液是乙胺丁醇的剂量限制性毒性。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold ethambutol until all three AFB cultures are finalized.","zh":"等到3份AFB培养全部最终报告后再给乙胺丁醇。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify that baseline visual acuity and red-green color discrimination testing are documented.","zh":"确认已记录基线视力和红绿色觉检查。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the drug only if the patient has received BCG vaccine.","zh":"只有患者接种过卡介苗时才给予该药。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ethambutol can cause optic neuritis, so baseline visual acuity and color discrimination testing create a reference point for detecting drug-related visual changes. The case order specifically requires this testing before the first dose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乙胺丁醇可导致视神经炎，因此基线视力和色觉检查可作为发现药物相关视觉变化的参照。病例医嘱也明确要求首次给药前进行这些检查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link each anti-TB medication to its key safety monitoring. Ethambutol points to vision and red-green color discrimination.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将每种抗结核药物与关键安全监测相联系。乙胺丁醇对应视力和红绿色觉监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":130,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, complete the statement explaining why the patient's long-term prednisone is tapered rather than stopped abruptly.","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，补全句子，说明为什么患者长期使用的泼尼松要逐渐减量而不是突然停药。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, complete the statement explaining why the patient's long-term prednisone is tapered rather than stopped abruptly.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段2，补全句子，说明为什么患者长期使用的泼尼松要逐渐减量而不是突然停药。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The prednisone is tapered rather than abruptly stopped because chronic exogenous corticosteroid use can suppress the {{1}}, and abrupt discontinuation may precipitate {{2}}.","zh":"泼尼松需要逐渐减量而不是突然停药，因为长期外源性糖皮质激素使用可抑制 {{1}}，突然停药可能诱发 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system","zh":"肾素-血管紧张素-醛固酮系统"},{"id":"o3","en":"parasympathetic nervous system","zh":"副交感神经系统"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis","zh":"下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"adrenal insufficiency or adrenal crisis","zh":"肾上腺功能不全或肾上腺危象"},{"id":"o3","en":"thyrotoxic crisis","zh":"甲状腺危象"},{"id":"o2","en":"serotonin syndrome","zh":"血清素综合征"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient has taken prednisone daily for two years. Chronic corticosteroid therapy can suppress endogenous adrenal response through the HPA axis, so abrupt cessation can cause adrenal insufficiency or crisis. A taper is the safer ordered approach.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者已每日服用泼尼松2年。长期糖皮质激素治疗可通过HPA轴抑制机体自身肾上腺反应，因此突然停药可能导致肾上腺功能不全或危象。按医嘱逐渐减量更安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For chronic steroids, think suppression and taper. Do not pair long-term prednisone with abrupt discontinuation unless directed by a specific emergency plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到长期使用类固醇，要想到“抑制”和“逐渐减量”。除非有特定紧急方案，不要把长期泼尼松与突然停药配对。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":131,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[233,278],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,103],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 4, the patient's AST is 86 U/L, ALT is 104 U/L, and total bilirubin is 1.8 mg/dL. The infectious disease provider states that hepatotoxic agents will be held if the next ALT exceeds 120 U/L with any hepatotoxicity symptoms. Which nursing action is most appropriate now?","fullStemZh":"在阶段4，患者AST为86 U/L，ALT为104 U/L，总胆红素1.8 mg/dL。感染病科医嘱说明：若下一次ALT超过120 U/L并伴有任何肝毒性症状，将暂停肝毒性药物。此时护士最合适的措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is most appropriate now?","terminalSentenceZh":"此时护士最合适的措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The infectious disease provider states that hepatotoxic agents will be held if the next ALT exceeds 120 U/L with any hepatotoxicity symptoms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"感染病科医嘱说明：若下一次ALT超过120 U/L并伴有任何肝毒性症状，将暂停肝毒性药物。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Continue the medications as ordered, assess for hepatotoxicity symptoms, notify the provider of the upward trend as appropriate, and obtain the repeat labs as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱继续用药，评估肝毒性症状，适当通知医师肝酶上升趋势，并按医嘱复查实验室指标。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ignore the laboratory trend because mild nausea is expected during early TB therapy.","zh":"忽略实验室趋势，因为抗结核治疗早期轻度恶心是预期反应。"},{"id":"B","en":"Independently hold isoniazid, rifampin, and pyrazinamide immediately because ALT has risen above admission baseline.","zh":"因ALT高于入院基线，立即自行暂停异烟肼、利福平和吡嗪酰胺。"},{"id":"D","en":"Give acetaminophen for discomfort and delay repeat liver tests until discharge.","zh":"给予对乙酰氨基酚缓解不适，并将肝功能复查推迟到出院时。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The provider has defined an objective action threshold for this patient. The ALT is rising but has not reached the stated hold threshold, so the nurse should continue the prescribed regimen while monitoring symptoms and labs closely and communicating the trend.","rationaleCorrectZh":"医嘱已为该患者设定明确的处理阈值。ALT正在上升，但尚未达到医嘱规定的暂停阈值，因此护士应按处方继续治疗，同时密切监测症状和实验室指标，并沟通趋势变化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a case gives a protocol threshold, use that threshold exactly. Avoid both premature independent action and passive failure to monitor.","testTakingStrategyZh":"病例给出方案阈值时，要精确使用该阈值。既不要过早自行处理，也不要被动不监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":132,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus25_case_tb_airborne_treatment_monitoring_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,49],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the patient feels guilty, hopeless, and worried about whether he is contagious forever. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，患者感到内疚、绝望，并担心自己是否会永远具有传染性。哪些护理措施合适？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Tell the patient he is no longer contagious because he has already received three doses of therapy.","zh":"告诉患者，因为他已经接受3剂治疗，所以已不再具有传染性。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the patient's guilt, hopelessness, coping, and any thoughts of self-harm.","zh":"评估患者的内疚感、绝望感、应对方式以及是否有自伤想法。"},{"id":"C","en":"Request social work or case-management support for financial concerns and treatment-access barriers.","zh":"为经济问题和治疗可及性障碍申请社会工作或个案管理支持。"},{"id":"D","en":"Coordinate with public health and assess home-isolation concerns such as whether high-risk individuals live in the home.","zh":"与公共卫生部门协调，并评估居家隔离相关问题，例如家中是否有高风险人群。"},{"id":"F","en":"Explain that a positive AFB smear means he must stay hospitalized until every smear is negative.","zh":"解释AFB涂片阳性意味着他必须一直住院，直到所有涂片都转阴。"},{"id":"B","en":"Provide accurate, non-guaranteed teaching that infectiousness usually decreases with effective therapy and that isolation decisions will be guided by the care team and public health.","zh":"提供准确但不做绝对保证的教育：有效治疗后传染性通常会下降，隔离相关决定将由医疗团队和公共卫生部门指导。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient's distress can undermine adherence and safety. Appropriate care includes assessing mood and safety, giving accurate conditional teaching, involving social work/case management, and coordinating public health and home-isolation planning. The nurse should avoid false guarantees about infectiousness or discharge requirements.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者的痛苦可能影响依从性和安全。合适的照护包括评估情绪和安全、提供准确且有条件的教育、让社会工作/个案管理介入，并协调公共卫生和居家隔离计划。护士应避免对传染性或出院要求作出不真实的保证。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For psychosocial NCLEX items, combine emotional safety, accurate teaching, and concrete resource coordination. Reject answers that give false certainty.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到心理社会类NCLEX题，要结合情绪安全、准确信息和具体资源协调。排除给出虚假确定性的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？"}
{"queueIndex":133,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.65","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.65.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[203,383],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,135],"fullStemEn":"Refeeding syndrome risk in severe anorexia nervosa A 22-year-old woman with severe anorexia nervosa is admitted after syncope and several weeks of intake under 400 kcal/day. Admission BMI is 14.8 kg/m². Refeeding begins with telemetry, strict intake and output, daily weights, electrolyte monitoring, thiamine, multivitamin supplementation, meal supervision, and restricted activity.","fullStemZh":"重度神经性厌食患者的再喂养综合征风险 一名22岁女性因重度神经性厌食入院。她在晕厥后被送医，过去数周每日摄入少于400千卡。入院BMI为14.8 kg/m²。治疗开始时包括持续心电监护、严格记录出入量、每日体重、电解质监测、硫胺素和复合维生素补充、进餐监督以及活动限制。","terminalSentenceEn":"Refeeding begins with telemetry, strict intake and output, daily weights, electrolyte monitoring, thiamine, multivitamin supplementation, meal supervision, and restricted activity.","terminalSentenceZh":"治疗开始时包括持续心电监护、严格记录出入量、每日体重、电解质监测、硫胺素和复合维生素补充、进餐监督以及活动限制。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Admission BMI is 14.8 kg/m².","penultimateSentenceZh":"入院BMI为14.8 kg/m²。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows a severely malnourished client through early refeeding. The key clinical arc is recognizing that falling phosphorus and potassium after nutrition starts are early cues of refeeding syndrome risk, applying the stated protocol by holding caloric advancement and notifying the provider, and escalating immediately when electrolyte depletion is accompanied by QTc prolongation and PVCs. Expected discomforts such as bloating and mild refeeding edema require supportive care and monitoring, not unsupervised caloric reduction or diuretics. Readiness for calorie advancement depends on the provider's protocol and the next confirmatory electrolyte draw, not on one improved set of labs alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例呈现一名重度营养不良患者早期再喂养的过程。关键临床判断是：营养开始后磷和钾下降提示再喂养综合征风险，应按既定方案暂停增加热量并通知医护提供者；当电解质耗竭伴QTc延长和PVCs时必须立即升级处理。腹胀和轻度再喂养水肿等预期不适需要支持性护理和监测，而不是擅自减少热量或使用利尿剂。是否可以增加热量取决于医护提供者方案和下一次确认性电解质结果，而不是单次改善的实验室结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding cases, anchor each answer to the data available at that stage and to any stated protocol. Do not override a refeeding prescription because symptoms are uncomfortable; escalate when objective electrolyte and rhythm cues show instability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式病例中，将每个答案锚定在该阶段可获得的数据和已写明的方案上。不要因为症状令人不适就擅自改变再喂养处方；当客观电解质和心律线索显示不稳定时应升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":134,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,46],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which nursing actions are required based on the 12-hour laboratory results and the admission refeeding protocol? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，根据12小时实验室结果和入院再喂养方案，护士需要采取哪些护理措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which nursing actions are required based on the 12-hour laboratory results and the admission refeeding protocol?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段1，根据12小时实验室结果和入院再喂养方案，护士需要采取哪些护理措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hold any planned caloric advancement.","zh":"暂停任何计划中的热量增加。"},{"id":"F","en":"Start IV potassium phosphate because the phosphorus is below 2.5 mg/dL.","zh":"因磷低于2.5 mg/dL而开始静脉磷酸钾。"},{"id":"E","en":"Independently increase the meal plan because the glucose has improved.","zh":"因血糖改善而由护士自行增加进餐计划。"},{"id":"C","en":"Initiate oral sodium phosphate per the pharmacy protocol.","zh":"按药房方案开始口服磷酸钠。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider immediately about the phosphorus and potassium threshold crossings.","zh":"立即将磷和钾低于方案阈值的情况通知医护提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Wait for the next scheduled 12-hour laboratory draw before acting.","zh":"等到下一次计划的12小时抽血结果出来后再处理。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Phosphorus 2.4 mg/dL is below the protocol threshold of 2.5 mg/dL, and potassium 3.4 mEq/L is below the protocol threshold of 3.5 mEq/L. The nurse should hold caloric advancement, notify the provider immediately with both threshold crossings, and implement the ordered pharmacy protocol for oral sodium phosphate because the phosphorus is between 2.0 and 2.5 mg/dL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"磷2.4 mg/dL低于方案阈值2.5 mg/dL，钾3.4 mEq/L低于方案阈值3.5 mEq/L。护士应暂停增加热量，立即将两个阈值被突破的情况通知医护提供者，并因磷处于2.0至2.5 mg/dL之间而执行已医嘱授权的药房方案，给予口服磷酸钠。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a protocol gives numeric action thresholds, compare each current value directly with the threshold before deciding whether to wait or escalate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当方案给出数字化处理阈值时，先将每个当前数值与阈值逐一比较，再决定是等待还是升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":135,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[132,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,48],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the client reports bloating, mild nausea, and abdominal cramping after meals and asks the nurse to reduce her portions. Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，患者报告餐后腹胀、轻度恶心和腹部绞痛，并要求护士减少她的餐量。护士最合适的回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最合适的回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the client reports bloating, mild nausea, and abdominal cramping after meals and asks the nurse to reduce her portions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段1，患者报告餐后腹胀、轻度恶心和腹部绞痛，并要求护士减少她的餐量。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Acknowledge the discomfort, offer comfort measures, document the symptoms, and communicate them to the provider and dietitian while maintaining the prescribed meal plan.","zh":"认可患者不适，提供舒适措施，记录症状，并将情况告知医护提供者和营养师，同时维持已开立的进餐方案。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tell the client that the symptoms prove she is not medically ready for oral nutrition.","zh":"告诉患者这些症状证明她尚未具备经口营养的医学条件。"},{"id":"B","en":"Allow the client to skip the next snack because nausea means the calories are being advanced too quickly.","zh":"允许患者跳过下一次加餐，因为恶心说明热量增加过快。"},{"id":"C","en":"Reduce each meal portion by half until the abdominal cramping resolves.","zh":"在腹部绞痛缓解前，将每餐份量减少一半。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mild bloating, nausea, and cramping can occur early in refeeding because prolonged starvation slows gastrointestinal motility. The nurse should validate discomfort, use comfort measures, document and communicate symptoms, and maintain the prescribed meal plan rather than independently reducing intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"长期饥饿会使胃肠动力减慢，因此再喂养早期可出现轻度腹胀、恶心和绞痛。护士应认可患者不适，采取舒适措施，记录并沟通症状，同时维持已开立的进餐方案，而不是擅自减少摄入。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected discomfort from danger signs. An uncomfortable but expected symptom does not give the nurse authority to change a prescribed refeeding plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分预期不适和危险信号。令人不适但预期可见的症状，并不授权护士改变已开立的再喂养方案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":136,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,78],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the telemetry strip is shown. The monitor reports QTc 480 ms, and labs show potassium 3.1 mEq/L, phosphorus 1.9 mg/dL, and magnesium 1.4 mg/dL. What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，心律条如图所示。监护仪报告QTc 480 ms，实验室显示钾3.1 mEq/L、磷1.9 mg/dL、镁1.4 mg/dL。护士的优先措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的优先措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The monitor reports QTc 480 ms, and labs show potassium 3.1 mEq/L, phosphorus 1.9 mg/dL, and magnesium 1.4 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"监护仪报告QTc 480 ms，实验室显示钾3.1 mEq/L、磷1.9 mg/dL、镁1.4 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Document the rhythm change and continue the current oral phosphorus replacement until the next scheduled laboratory draw.","zh":"记录心律变化，并继续当前口服补磷，等到下一次计划实验室复查。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to eat more of the next meal to correct the electrolyte levels naturally.","zh":"鼓励患者下一餐多吃一些，以自然纠正电解质水平。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer potassium chloride only, because the dysrhythmia is caused by hypokalemia.","zh":"仅给予氯化钾，因为心律失常是由低钾引起的。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the provider immediately of the new PVCs, QTc prolongation, and worsening potassium, phosphorus, and magnesium; anticipate stat IV electrolyte replacement orders.","zh":"立即将新出现的PVCs、QTc延长以及钾、磷、镁继续恶化通知医护提供者；预期立即静脉补充电解质医嘱。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New ventricular ectopy and QTc prolongation in the setting of worsening hypokalemia, hypophosphatemia, and hypomagnesemia indicate clinically significant instability. The priority is to notify the provider immediately with the complete rhythm-and-electrolyte picture and anticipate stat IV replacement orders, including IV potassium phosphate per the stated protocol for phosphorus below 2.0 mg/dL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在低钾、低磷、低镁继续恶化的背景下，新出现室性异位搏动和QTc延长提示临床不稳定。优先措施是立即将完整的心律和电解质情况通知医护提供者，并预期获得立即静脉补充电解质的医嘱，包括因磷低于2.0 mg/dL而按既定方案给予静脉磷酸钾。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In priority questions, an acute change in cardiac rhythm plus worsening electrolytes outranks comfort, routine documentation, or isolated replacement of one electrolyte.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在优先级题中，急性心律改变合并电解质恶化，优先级高于舒适护理、常规记录或只补充某一种电解质。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":137,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,56],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the client is tearful, says the food is making her sick, asks to stop eating, and is observed hiding food in a napkin. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，患者哭泣，说食物让她生病，要求停止进食，并被观察到把食物藏在餐巾中。哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"State that the food is not the cause of harm, while acknowledging that her symptoms and fears are real.","zh":"说明食物并非伤害的原因，同时认可她的症状和恐惧是真实存在的。"},{"id":"B","en":"Explain calmly that the team is monitoring her closely and that the nutrition plan is medically necessary.","zh":"平静解释团队正在密切监测她，营养计划具有医学必要性。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document the food-hiding behavior objectively and communicate it to the treatment team.","zh":"客观记录藏食行为，并将情况告知治疗团队。"},{"id":"D","en":"Agree to stop meals until she feels that eating is safe.","zh":"同意停止进餐，直到她觉得进食安全。"},{"id":"A","en":"Validate that the situation feels frightening and uncomfortable for her.","zh":"认可这种情况让她感到害怕和不适。"},{"id":"E","en":"Tell her that if she keeps hiding food, a feeding tube will be placed as punishment.","zh":"告诉她如果继续藏食，就会作为惩罚放置喂食管。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should validate emotional distress, give calm factual reassurance that the team is monitoring medical safety, maintain the ordered refeeding plan, and document/report food-hiding objectively because actual intake affects electrolyte monitoring. The nurse should not agree that food is harmful, stop refeeding, or use punitive threats.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应认可患者的情绪痛苦，用平静事实性语言说明团队正在监测医学安全，维持已开立的再喂养方案，并客观记录/报告藏食行为，因为实际摄入量会影响电解质监测。护士不应同意“食物有害”、停止再喂养或使用惩罚性威胁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic communication can validate feelings without validating unsafe illness-driven conclusions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性沟通可以认可感受，但不认可由疾病驱动的不安全结论。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":138,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,257],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,72],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, electrolytes have improved and the follow-up telemetry strip is shown. The nurse notes new mild 1+ bilateral ankle edema with clear lungs and a cumulative weight gain of 1.1 kg over 60 hours. Which interpretation and action are most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，电解质改善，复查心律条如图所示。护士发现新出现的双踝轻度1+水肿，双肺清，60小时累计体重增加1.1 kg。最合适的判断和措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation and action are most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"最合适的判断和措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes new mild 1+ bilateral ankle edema with clear lungs and a cumulative weight gain of 1.1 kg over 60 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现新出现的双踝轻度1+水肿，双肺清，60小时累计体重增加1.1 kg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Request a diuretic immediately because the weight gain confirms fluid overload.","zh":"立即请求利尿剂，因为体重增加证实液体过多。"},{"id":"D","en":"Restrict all oral fluids without notifying the provider because ankle edema is always caused by excessive intake.","zh":"不通知医护提供者而限制所有口服液体，因为踝部水肿总是由摄入过多导致。"},{"id":"A","en":"Recognize likely mild refeeding edema, assess respiratory status and lung sounds, document and report the finding, and avoid diuretics unless specifically ordered after evaluation.","zh":"识别为可能的轻度再喂养水肿，评估呼吸状态和肺音，记录并报告该发现，除非评估后有明确医嘱，否则避免利尿剂。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hold all meals because edema means refeeding syndrome is worsening despite normalized electrolytes.","zh":"暂停所有进餐，因为水肿说明尽管电解质恢复正常，再喂养综合征仍在恶化。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mild peripheral edema and modest weight gain can occur during early refeeding because of sodium and water retention. With clear lungs and stable respiratory status, the nurse should continue assessment, document and report the finding, and avoid diuretics because they can worsen electrolyte instability.","rationaleCorrectZh":"早期再喂养可因钠水潴留出现轻度外周水肿和适度体重增加。在双肺清且呼吸状态稳定的情况下，护士应继续评估，记录并报告该发现，避免使用利尿剂，因为利尿剂可能加重电解质不稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Before treating edema, decide whether the client has objective signs of pulmonary fluid overload or whether the edema fits the expected clinical context.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理水肿前，先判断患者是否有肺部液体过多的客观表现，还是该水肿符合当前临床背景下的预期现象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":139,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[155,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,66],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the provider is considering advancing calories from 1,200 to 1,400 kcal/day beginning tomorrow if electrolytes remain stable on the next draw. Complete the nursing judgment statement.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，若下一次抽血显示电解质仍稳定，医护提供者正考虑从明天开始将热量从每日1,200千卡增加到1,400千卡。完成护理判断陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing judgment statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护理判断陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the provider is considering advancing calories from 1,200 to 1,400 kcal/day beginning tomorrow if electrolytes remain stable on the next draw.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3，若下一次抽血显示电解质仍稳定，医护提供者正考虑从明天开始将热量从每日1,200千卡增加到1,400千卡。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client's current electrolyte values are {{1}}, so the nurse should {{2}} before caloric advancement.","zh":"患者目前的电解质数值{{1}}，因此在增加热量前，护士应{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"above the stated hold thresholds but not enough alone to prove ongoing stability","zh":"高于已写明的暂停阈值，但单凭这一次结果不足以证明持续稳定"},{"id":"o3","en":"irrelevant once the PVCs have resolved","zh":"一旦PVCs消失就不再相关"},{"id":"o2","en":"below the stated hold thresholds and require stopping all oral intake","zh":"低于已写明的暂停阈值，需要停止所有经口摄入"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"advance the diet immediately because the 60-hour labs improved","zh":"因为60小时实验室结果改善而立即增加饮食"},{"id":"o3","en":"request a diuretic first to remove the ankle edema","zh":"先请求利尿剂以消除踝部水肿"},{"id":"o1","en":"communicate that the next electrolyte draw must confirm stability","zh":"沟通需要下一次电解质检查确认稳定"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The current potassium, phosphorus, and magnesium values are above the protocol thresholds, but the provider's plan depends on the next confirmatory laboratory draw. The nurse should communicate that advancement should wait until that stability criterion is met.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前钾、磷和镁均高于方案阈值，但医护提供者的计划取决于下一次确认性实验室结果。护士应沟通：只有在该稳定性标准满足后才应增加热量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For conditional orders, identify the exact condition that must still be satisfied before the action becomes appropriate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于有条件的医嘱或计划，先找出行动前仍必须满足的具体条件。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":140,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.66","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.66.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[406,480],"terminalOffsetsZh":[121,150],"fullStemEn":"Intimate partner violence disclosure during routine prenatal care A 28-year-old gravida 2 para 1 client at 26 weeks gestation arrives for a scheduled prenatal visit with her partner. The pregnancy has been uncomplicated. Her partner usually accompanies her and answers questions directed to the client. The clinic uses routine IPV screening with a validated tool and requires screening to occur privately. The nurse notices behavioral cues and bruising that raise concern for IPV.","fullStemZh":"常规产前护理中亲密伴侣暴力的披露 一名28岁、孕2产1、孕26周的患者由伴侣陪同来做预约产检。妊娠至今无并发症。她的伴侣通常每次陪诊，并代替患者回答本应由患者回答的问题。诊所使用经验证的工具进行常规亲密伴侣暴力筛查，并要求筛查必须在私下进行。护士注意到患者的行为线索和瘀伤，提示可能存在亲密伴侣暴力。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse notices behavioral cues and bruising that raise concern for IPV.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士注意到患者的行为线索和瘀伤，提示可能存在亲密伴侣暴力。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The clinic uses routine IPV screening with a validated tool and requires screening to occur privately.","penultimateSentenceZh":"诊所使用经验证的工具进行常规亲密伴侣暴力筛查，并要求筛查必须在私下进行。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case centers on safe response to IPV disclosure during prenatal care. The nurse should first create privacy using a routine clinical reason, because screening in the suspected abuser's presence can increase danger and suppress disclosure. After disclosure, the nurse should be honest about confidentiality limits, document the client's own words, involve the provider, and avoid notifying the partner or law enforcement unless the stated mandatory-reporting triggers apply. Because the child has witnessed violence, the nurse must consult the provider and follow state child-welfare reporting requirements if applicable. The client should not be pressured to leave before she is ready; instead, the nurse supports autonomy, discreet resources, safe communication planning, and a truthful non-revealing response when the partner returns.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的核心是在产前护理中安全回应亲密伴侣暴力披露。护士应先用常规临床理由创造私下环境，因为在疑似施暴者在场时筛查可能增加危险并抑制患者披露。患者披露后，护士应如实说明保密的界限，使用患者原话记录，通知医疗服务提供者，并且除非符合病例中列明的强制报告触发条件，否则不通知伴侣或执法部门。由于孩子曾目睹暴力，护士必须与提供者沟通，并在适用时依照州儿童福利报告要求处理。不能在患者尚未准备好时逼迫其离开；应支持患者自主权，提供隐蔽资源，规划安全联系方式，并在伴侣返回时作出真实但不透露筛查内容的回应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For IPV questions, protect privacy and safety first. Separate the client from the suspected abuser, avoid absolute promises, know reporting limits from the case facts, and support autonomy with safety planning.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到亲密伴侣暴力题，首先保护隐私和安全。将患者与疑似施暴者分开，避免绝对承诺，根据病例事实判断报告界限，并通过安全计划支持患者自主。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The clinic uses routine IPV screening with a validated tool and requires screening to occur privately.","controlSentenceZh":"诊所使用经验证的工具进行常规亲密伴侣暴力筛查，并要求筛查必须在私下进行。"}
{"queueIndex":141,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Initial presentation: Which nursing action is most appropriate before asking IPV screening questions?","fullStemZh":"初始表现：在询问亲密伴侣暴力筛查问题前，护士最合适的行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Initial presentation: Which nursing action is most appropriate before asking IPV screening questions?","terminalSentenceZh":"初始表现：在询问亲密伴侣暴力筛查问题前，护士最合适的行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Tell the client she must explain the bruises before the prenatal visit can continue.","zh":"告诉患者必须解释瘀伤原因后，产检才能继续。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the partner to leave the room using a routine clinic reason, such as urine collection and the physical examination.","zh":"以常规诊所理由请伴侣离开房间，例如留尿和身体检查。"},{"id":"C","en":"Confront the partner directly about the bruises before separating him from the client.","zh":"在将伴侣与患者分开前，直接质问伴侣关于瘀伤的情况。"},{"id":"B","en":"Begin the IPV screening while the partner is present so the nurse can observe his reaction.","zh":"在伴侣在场时开始亲密伴侣暴力筛查，以便观察他的反应。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case protocol requires IPV screening to be done privately. A routine clinical explanation separates the client from the partner without signaling suspicion and reduces the risk of retaliation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"病例中的诊所流程要求亲密伴侣暴力筛查必须私下进行。使用常规临床解释可在不引起伴侣警觉的情况下将患者与伴侣分开，降低报复风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When abuse is suspected, the first safe step is privacy without alerting the suspected abuser.","testTakingStrategyZh":"怀疑虐待时，第一步是安全地创造隐私，同时不要惊动疑似施暴者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":142,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Complete the statement describing the nurse's best response to the client's request for a promise of secrecy.","fullStemZh":"第1阶段：补全句子，说明护士对患者要求保密承诺的最佳回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Complete the statement describing the nurse's best response to the client's request for a promise of secrecy.","terminalSentenceZh":"第1阶段：补全句子，说明护士对患者要求保密承诺的最佳回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{1}} and explain that the disclosure will be {{2}}.","zh":"护士应{{1}}，并解释该披露内容将{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"call the partner back into the room to clarify the account","zh":"叫伴侣回到房间以澄清事情经过"},{"id":"o2","en":"avoid promising absolute confidentiality and describe the limits honestly","zh":"避免承诺绝对保密，并如实说明保密界限"},{"id":"o1","en":"promise that no one else will be told","zh":"保证不会告诉任何其他人"},{"id":"o4","en":"tell the client that the nurse cannot continue unless she agrees to police involvement","zh":"告诉患者除非同意警方介入，否则护士不能继续处理"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"shared with the clinical team for safety planning and not disclosed to her partner","zh":"为安全计划与临床团队共享，但不会透露给她的伴侣"},{"id":"o2","en":"automatically sent to her partner through the after-visit summary","zh":"通过离诊总结自动发送给她的伴侣"},{"id":"o3","en":"reported to law enforcement in every adult IPV disclosure","zh":"每次成年患者披露亲密伴侣暴力时都报告给执法部门"},{"id":"o4","en":"left out of the medical record so no one can access it","zh":"不写入病历，这样任何人都无法看到"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should not promise absolute secrecy. The case protocol requires documentation and provider notification for safety planning, while also protecting the client from disclosure to the partner and avoiding law-enforcement contact unless a stated reporting trigger is present.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士不应承诺绝对保密。病例流程要求为安全计划进行记录并通知医疗服务提供者，同时也要保护患者，不向伴侣披露；除非存在病例中列出的报告触发条件，否则不联系执法部门。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not promise absolute confidentiality. State who must know for care, what will not be disclosed, and which specific reporting triggers apply.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要承诺绝对保密。说明哪些人因护理需要必须知情、哪些信息不会被披露，以及哪些具体情况会触发报告义务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":143,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,33],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The client reports that her 3-year-old son has witnessed the partner pushing and grabbing her. Which response is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"第2阶段：患者报告3岁儿子曾目睹伴侣推搡、抓拽她。哪项回应最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项回应最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: The client reports that her 3-year-old son has witnessed the partner pushing and grabbing her.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第2阶段：患者报告3岁儿子曾目睹伴侣推搡、抓拽她。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Consult the provider and follow state child-welfare reporting requirements if the child's exposure meets reporting criteria.","zh":"与医疗服务提供者沟通；若孩子目睹暴力符合报告标准，则按州儿童福利报告要求处理。"},{"id":"C","en":"Call law enforcement immediately because every adult IPV disclosure must be reported to police.","zh":"立即报警，因为每次成年患者披露亲密伴侣暴力都必须报告警方。"},{"id":"A","en":"Explain that there is no child-safety concern because the child has not been directly struck.","zh":"解释说孩子没有被直接打到，所以不存在儿童安全问题。"},{"id":"D","en":"Warn the client that she will lose custody if she does not leave the relationship today.","zh":"警告患者如果今天不离开这段关系，就会失去孩子监护权。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case protocol names suspected child abuse or neglect as a mandatory-reporting trigger. A child witnessing domestic violence may create a child-welfare concern, so the nurse should involve the provider and follow applicable reporting requirements while communicating transparently and non-punitively with the client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"病例流程将疑似儿童虐待或忽视列为强制报告触发条件。儿童目睹家庭暴力可能构成儿童福利风险，因此护士应让医疗服务提供者参与，并按适用报告要求处理，同时以透明、非惩罚性的方式与患者沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate adult autonomy from child-safety reporting. The same IPV disclosure can require different actions when a child may be at risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分成年人自主权与儿童安全报告。同一亲密伴侣暴力披露在儿童可能受影响时，可能需要不同处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":144,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,51],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The client says she is not ready to leave and asks, 'Do you think I'm a bad mother?' Which nursing responses are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第2阶段：患者说她还没准备好离开，并问：'你觉得我是个坏母亲吗？'哪些护理回应合适？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing responses are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理回应合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Say, 'The abuse is not your fault, and asking for help does not make you a bad mother.'","zh":"说：'遭受虐待不是你的错，寻求帮助并不表示你是坏母亲。'"},{"id":"B","en":"Tell her that leaving is her decision and that the team can help with safety planning and resources.","zh":"告诉她离开与否由她决定，团队可以协助安全计划和资源安排。"},{"id":"D","en":"Explore safe contacts, transportation barriers, essential documents, and ways to hide resources safely.","zh":"了解安全联系人、交通障碍、重要证件，以及如何安全隐藏资源。"},{"id":"E","en":"Advise her to stop prenatal care until she is willing to separate from the partner.","zh":"建议她在愿意与伴侣分开之前暂停产前护理。"},{"id":"C","en":"Tell her she must leave today because staying means she is choosing the abuse.","zh":"告诉她今天必须离开，因为留下就等于选择继续受虐。"},{"id":"F","en":"Offer discreet resource information without requiring her to call a hotline during the visit.","zh":"提供隐蔽的资源信息，但不要求她在本次就诊时拨打热线。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Patient-centered IPV care affirms that abuse is not the client's fault, respects her autonomy, and offers safety planning and resources without forcing immediate separation. Practical safety planning is especially important because the partner controls finances, monitors the phone, and limits transportation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"以患者为中心的亲密伴侣暴力护理应肯定受虐不是患者的错，尊重其自主权，并在不强迫立即分开的情况下提供安全计划和资源。由于伴侣控制经济、监控手机并限制交通，实际可行的安全计划尤其重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid judgmental or coercive IPV responses. Choose options that validate, preserve autonomy, and build a realistic safety plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"避免评判性或胁迫性的亲密伴侣暴力回应。选择能肯定患者、维护自主权并建立现实安全计划的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":145,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,49],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: The client asks whether the disclosure will be in her chart and whether her partner can see it. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段：患者询问披露内容是否会写入病历，以及伴侣是否能看到。哪些护理行动合适？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理行动合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Document the disclosure using the client's own words for continuity of care and safety planning.","zh":"使用患者原话记录披露内容，以便连续护理和安全计划。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use only the contact method the client identifies as safe and provide discreet written resource information.","zh":"只使用患者确认安全的联系方式，并提供隐蔽的书面资源信息。"},{"id":"E","en":"Leave a detailed voicemail about IPV resources on the primary phone number listed in the chart.","zh":"在病历中登记的主要电话号码上留下关于亲密伴侣暴力资源的详细语音留言。"},{"id":"D","en":"Send IPV resource links through the patient portal because electronic health records are automatically safe from partner monitoring.","zh":"通过患者门户发送亲密伴侣暴力资源链接，因为电子健康记录自动不受伴侣监控。"},{"id":"C","en":"Explain that protected health information generally is not released to the partner without the client's authorization, while also assessing practical access risks.","zh":"解释受保护健康信息通常不会在患者未授权时提供给伴侣，同时评估实际访问风险。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask whether the partner has portal access, proxy access, shared-device access, insurance-document access, or access to her phone before sending messages or links.","zh":"在发送消息或链接前，询问伴侣是否能访问患者门户、代理权限、共用设备、保险文件或她的手机。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The disclosure should be documented for clinical continuity, but the nurse must address the realistic ways an abuser may access information, including portal credentials, proxy access, shared devices, insurance documents, and monitored phones. The nurse should use only client-approved safe contact methods and avoid unsafe electronic communication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"披露内容应被记录以保证临床连续性，但护士必须处理施暴者可能获取信息的实际途径，包括患者门户账号、代理访问、共用设备、保险文件和被监控手机。护士应只使用患者认可的安全联系方式，并避免不安全的电子沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Confidentiality is not only a legal concept; in IPV care, always assess practical access to phones, portals, devices, and paperwork.","testTakingStrategyZh":"保密不仅是法律概念；在亲密伴侣暴力护理中，始终评估手机、患者门户、设备和文件的实际访问风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":146,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,41],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: The partner returns and asks, 'Everything okay? What took so long?' Which response by the nurse best protects the client's safety?","fullStemZh":"第3阶段：伴侣回来后问：'一切都好吗？怎么这么久？'护士哪项回应最能保护患者安全？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse best protects the client's safety?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士哪项回应最能保护患者安全？","penultimateSentenceEn":"What took so long?'","penultimateSentenceZh":"怎么这么久？'","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"'Nothing happened. Ask her why she made the visit take so long.'","zh":"'没发生什么。你问她为什么让就诊拖这么久。'"},{"id":"A","en":"'We had routine lab work and screening to review today, and we talked about some third-trimester planning.'","zh":"'今天我们复查了一些常规实验室检查和筛查内容，也谈了一些孕晚期计划。'"},{"id":"C","en":"'Her blood pressure is dangerously high, so the visit took longer.'","zh":"'她的血压非常危险，所以就诊时间久了一些。'"},{"id":"B","en":"'She told me where the bruises came from, and we need to talk with you about it.'","zh":"'她告诉我瘀伤是怎么来的，我们需要和你谈谈这件事。'"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A truthful but non-revealing response normalizes the length of the visit without disclosing the IPV screening. It avoids alerting the partner and avoids fabricating a medical complication that could create further problems.","rationaleCorrectZh":"真实但不透露隐私的回应可以把较长就诊时间正常化，同时不披露亲密伴侣暴力筛查内容。这样既避免惊动伴侣，也避免编造可能带来后续问题的医疗并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the suspected abuser returns, choose a response that is truthful, routine, calm, and non-revealing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"疑似施暴者返回时，选择真实、常规、冷静且不透露隐私的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":147,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.67","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.67.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1846,2050],"terminalOffsetsZh":[580,639],"fullStemEn":"Lithium toxicity in a patient with bipolar disorder A 52-year-old woman with a fifteen-year history of bipolar I disorder, well controlled on lithium carbonate 900 mg orally twice daily, is admitted to a medical-surgical unit from the emergency department. She also carries diagnoses of type 2 diabetes managed with metformin 1000 mg twice daily and newly diagnosed stage 1 hypertension. Ten days ago her primary care provider started hydrochlorothiazide (HCTZ) 25 mg daily for the hypertension. She lives alone, works as a librarian, and has a strong therapeutic alliance with her outpatient psychiatrist, whom she sees every three months. Her last outpatient lithium level, drawn six weeks ago, was 0.9 mEq/L (therapeutic range per her psychiatry clinic protocol: 0.6–1.2 mEq/L). She has no history of renal disease; her most recent outpatient creatinine four months ago was 0.9 mg/dL. She reports that over the past week she has had poor oral intake because of persistent nausea and has been urinating frequently. She attributes the nausea to \"a stomach bug\" and did not contact either provider. Her current medication administration record includes lithium carbonate 900 mg PO BID, HCTZ 25 mg PO daily, and metformin 1000 mg PO BID. There is no standing order for lithium level monitoring on admission; the admitting provider has ordered a stat serum lithium level, a basic metabolic panel, and a 12-lead ECG.\n\nThe patient arrives on the unit at 0800 accompanied by her adult daughter. She is drowsy but arousable to voice, oriented to person and place but not to date. She complains of unrelenting nausea, coarse bilateral hand tremor, and feeling \"shaky all over.\" Her daughter reports that over the past two days the patient has become increasingly confused, has had several episodes of vomiting and diarrhea, and \"can't keep water down.\" The daughter adds that her mother has seemed \"not herself\" for about a week — more irritable, unsteady on her feet, and slurring words intermittently — but the family initially attributed this to fatigue.","fullStemZh":"双相情感障碍患者的锂中毒 一名有15年双相I型情感障碍病史的52岁女性，服用碳酸锂900 mg每日两次口服控制良好，从急诊科收入内外科病房。她还诊断出患有2型糖尿病，服用二甲双胍1000 mg每日两次，以及新诊断的1级高血压。10天前，她的初级保健医生为她开了氢氯噻嗪（HCTZ）25 mg每日一次治疗高血压。她独居，是一名图书管理员，与门诊精神科医生治疗联盟良好，每三个月就诊一次。她最近一次门诊的锂浓度是六周前，为0.9 mEq/L（其精神科诊所方案的治疗范围：0.6–1.2 mEq/L）。她没有肾病史；她最近一次门诊肌酐是四个月前，为0.9 mg/dL。她报告说，在过去的一周里，由于持续的恶心和尿频，她的口服摄入量很差。她将恶心归因于“胃病”，并没有联系任何医生。她目前的给药记录包括碳酸锂900 mg PO BID，HCTZ 25 mg PO daily和二甲双胍1000 mg PO BID。入院时没有监测锂浓度的常规医嘱；收治医生开具了急查血清锂浓度、基础代谢组合和12导联心电图的医嘱。\n\n患者于0800在成年女儿的陪同下到达病房。她昏昏欲睡，但可被声音唤醒，对人和地点有定向力，但对日期没有。她抱怨持续的恶心、双侧手部粗大震颤，并感到“全身发抖”。她的女儿报告说，在过去的整整两天里，患者变得越来越困惑，发作了几次呕吐和腹泻，“喝不下水”。女儿补充说，大约一周以来，她母亲似乎“不太正常”——更容易烦躁、步态不稳、间歇性言语不清——但家人最初将其归因于疲劳。","terminalSentenceEn":"The daughter adds that her mother has seemed \"not herself\" for about a week — more irritable, unsteady on her feet, and slurring words intermittently — but the family initially attributed this to fatigue.","terminalSentenceZh":"女儿补充说，大约一周以来，她母亲似乎“不太正常”——更容易烦躁、步态不稳、间歇性言语不清——但家人最初将其归因于疲劳。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her daughter reports that over the past two days the patient has become increasingly confused, has had several episodes of vomiting and diarrhea, and \"can't keep water down.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"她的女儿报告说，在过去的整整两天里，患者变得越来越困惑，发作了几次呕吐和腹泻，“喝不下水”。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A case study evaluating the nursing care of a patient with severe lithium toxicity precipitated by hydrochlorothiazide and volume depletion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"一项评估由氢氯噻嗪和容量消耗诱发的严重锂中毒患者护理的案例研究。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Review the timeline of medication additions, hydration status, and neurological changes to understand the disease progression.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回顾增加药物、水合状态和神经系统变化的时间线，以了解疾病进展。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Her daughter reports that over the past two days the patient has become increasingly confused, has had several episodes of vomiting and diarrhea, and \"can't keep water down.\"","controlSentenceZh":"她的女儿报告说，在过去的整整两天里，患者变得越来越困惑，发作了几次呕吐和腹泻，“喝不下水”。"}
{"queueIndex":148,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"Based on the admission data, which of the following is the primary mechanism that precipitated the patient's toxic lithium level?","fullStemZh":"根据入院数据，下列哪一项是导致患者出现中毒性锂浓度的主要机制？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the admission data, which of the following is the primary mechanism that precipitated the patient's toxic lithium level?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据入院数据，下列哪一项是导致患者出现中毒性锂浓度的主要机制？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hydrochlorothiazide directly increased the absorption of lithium in the gastrointestinal tract.","zh":"氢氯噻嗪直接增加了锂在胃肠道的吸收。"},{"id":"C","en":"The patient's long-term lithium dose was too high for her baseline renal clearance.","zh":"对于她的基线肾脏清除率来说，该患者的长期锂剂量过高。"},{"id":"A","en":"The thiazide diuretic increased sodium and water excretion, causing volume depletion and a compensatory increase in proximal tubular reabsorption of sodium and lithium.","zh":"噻嗪类利尿剂增加了钠和水的排泄，导致容量消耗，代偿性地增加了近端肾小管对钠和锂的重吸收。"},{"id":"B","en":"Dehydration from poor oral intake and vomiting alone caused the toxicity without a medication interaction.","zh":"仅由口服摄入差和呕吐引起的脱水导致了毒性，没有药物相互作用。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lithium is almost entirely renally excreted and is handled like sodium in the proximal tubule. Any state that increases proximal sodium reabsorption — such as volume depletion from thiazide diuretics — reduces lithium clearance and raises serum levels. The interaction between HCTZ and lithium, compounded by dehydration, is the precipitant.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锂几乎完全经肾脏排泄，并且在近端肾小管中的处理方式与钠相似。任何增加近端钠重吸收的状态——例如噻嗪类利尿剂引起的容量消耗——都会降低锂的清除率并升高血清浓度。HCTZ和锂之间的相互作用，加上脱水，是诱发因素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that lithium and sodium share renal transport mechanisms; interventions that deplete sodium often cause lithium retention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想一下，锂和钠具有共同的肾脏转运机制；消耗钠的干预措施通常会导致锂潴留。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":149,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,198],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,53],"fullStemEn":"At 0930 (Stage 1), after the patient vomits and exhibits declining neurological status and hemodynamic instability, which set of actions is the highest priority for the nurse to perform immediately?","fullStemZh":"在0930（阶段1），在患者呕吐并表现出神经状态下降和血流动力学不稳定后，护士立即执行的首要操作是哪一组？","terminalSentenceEn":"At 0930 (Stage 1), after the patient vomits and exhibits declining neurological status and hemodynamic instability, which set of actions is the highest priority for the nurse to perform immediately?","terminalSentenceZh":"在0930（阶段1），在患者呕吐并表现出神经状态下降和血流动力学不稳定后，护士立即执行的首要操作是哪一组？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Redraw a stat serum lithium level and perform a full neurological assessment.","zh":"重新急查血清锂浓度，并进行全面的神经系统评估。"},{"id":"A","en":"Position the patient laterally, suction the airway, and notify the provider.","zh":"将患者置于侧卧位，吸引气道，并通知医生。"},{"id":"D","en":"Increase the rate of the continuous normal saline infusion and assess capillary refill.","zh":"增加持续静脉滴注生理盐水的速度，并评估毛细血管充盈时间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer an antiemetic to stop the vomiting and position the patient upright.","zh":"给予止吐药以止吐，并将患者置于直立位。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient's declining level of consciousness with active vomiting creates an aspiration risk; airway compromise is the most immediate life threat. The worsening obtundation and hypotension signal that the current treatment plan is insufficient. Protecting the airway and notifying the provider are the priority pair.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者意识水平下降伴活动性呕吐造成了误吸风险；气道受损是最直接的生命威胁。恶化的迟钝和低血压表明目前的治疗方案是不够的。保护气道和通知医生是首要任务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation). An obtunded patient who is vomiting is at immediate risk of losing their airway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用ABCs（气道、呼吸、循环）原则。呕吐的迟钝患者有立即失去气道的风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":150,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,58],"fullStemEn":"At 1200 (Stage 2), the nephrologist recommends emergent hemodialysis. The nurse understands that which combination of findings provides the strongest clinical indication for this intervention?","fullStemZh":"在1200（阶段2），肾脏内科医生建议进行紧急血液透析。护士理解以下哪种表现组合为这一干预提供了最强有力的临床指征？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse understands that which combination of findings provides the strongest clinical indication for this intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士理解以下哪种表现组合为这一干预提供了最强有力的临床指征？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1200 (Stage 2), the nephrologist recommends emergent hemodialysis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在1200（阶段2），肾脏内科医生建议进行紧急血液透析。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A lithium level of 2.6 mEq/L with persistent nausea and vomiting.","zh":"锂浓度为2.6 mEq/L伴持续恶心和呕吐。"},{"id":"D","en":"Inadequate urine output of 0.5 mL/kg/hr with isolated hypokalemia.","zh":"尿量不足0.5 mL/kg/hr伴孤立性低钾血症。"},{"id":"A","en":"Decreased level of consciousness and progressive neurotoxicity with impaired renal clearance despite IV hydration.","zh":"尽管进行了静脉补液，但意识水平下降和进行性神经毒性伴随肾脏清除率受损。"},{"id":"C","en":"An eGFR of 30 mL/min/1.73 m² with hyperactive bowel sounds and normal saline bolus completion.","zh":"eGFR为30 mL/min/1.73 m²伴肠鸣音活跃和生理盐水推注完成。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Dialysis is indicated because severe lithium toxicity is accompanied by decreased level of consciousness/progressive neurotoxicity and impaired renal clearance, with minimal improvement after IV fluids. The neurotoxicity is the decisive escalation cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"提示需要透析，因为严重的锂中毒伴随着意识水平下降/进行性神经毒性和肾脏清除受损，且静脉补液后改善极小。神经毒性是决定性的升级信号。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that severe neurological symptoms (like altered level of consciousness and myoclonus) combined with poor renal clearance are key indications for extracorporeal removal of lithium.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住，严重的神经系统症状（如意识水平改变和肌阵挛）结合肾脏清除不良，是体外清除锂的关键指征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":151,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,64],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the provider orders potassium chloride 20 mEq IV in 100 mL NS over one hour via peripheral line on an infusion pump. Which action should the nurse take before administering this medication?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，医生医嘱氯化钾20 mEq静脉滴注（100 mL NS，超过一小时，外周静脉，输液泵）。在给药前，护士应采取哪项操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take before administering this medication?","terminalSentenceZh":"在给药前，护士应采取哪项操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the provider orders potassium chloride 20 mEq IV in 100 mL NS over one hour via peripheral line on an infusion pump.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，医生医嘱氯化钾20 mEq静脉滴注（100 mL NS，超过一小时，外周静脉，输液泵）。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administer the infusion by gravity drip rather than an infusion pump to decrease the risk of phlebitis.","zh":"通过重力滴注而不是输液泵给药，以降低静脉炎的风险。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensure the patient's serum calcium level is drawn prior to initiating the infusion.","zh":"在开始输液之前确保抽取了患者的血清钙浓度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the infusion and clarify the order because the ordered concentration and rate exceed usual peripheral limits.","zh":"暂停输液并澄清医嘱，因为医嘱的浓度和速度超过了常见的外周静脉限制。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the infusion exactly as ordered because it is on an infusion pump and the patient has cardiac monitoring.","zh":"完全按医嘱给药，因为使用了输液泵并且患者有心电监护。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Before administering, the nurse checks the facility IV potassium protocol and recognizes that the ordered rate/concentration (20 mEq in 100 mL) exceeds the unit’s usual peripheral limit (typically 10 mEq/100 mL). The nurse holds the infusion and clarifies the order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在给药前，护士检查设施的静脉补钾方案，并认识到医嘱的速度/浓度（100 mL中20 mEq）超过了病房通常的外周限制（通常为10 mEq/100 mL）。护士暂停输液并澄清医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"IV potassium chloride is a high-alert medication. Always verify maximum peripheral concentrations and rates before administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"静脉注射氯化钾是高危药物。给药前务必核实外周最大浓度和速度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":152,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[109,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,53],"fullStemEn":"At 0200, the patient's lithium level rises to 1.3 mEq/L from the immediate post-dialysis level of 1.1 mEq/L. How should the nurse interpret this finding?","fullStemZh":"在0200，患者的锂浓度从透析后即刻的1.1 mEq/L上升至1.3 mEq/L。护士应如何解释这一发现？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse interpret this finding?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何解释这一发现？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0200, the patient's lithium level rises to 1.3 mEq/L from the immediate post-dialysis level of 1.1 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在0200，患者的锂浓度从透析后即刻的1.1 mEq/L上升至1.3 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"This indicates the hemodialysis was ineffective and must be restarted immediately.","zh":"这表明血液透析无效，必须立即重新开始。"},{"id":"A","en":"This represents expected post-dialysis lithium rebound due to redistribution from tissue compartments, requiring continued serial monitoring.","zh":"这代表了预期的透析后锂反弹，由于组织室的重新分布所致，需要继续连续监测。"},{"id":"C","en":"This suggests the patient has secretly ingested additional lithium while on the unit.","zh":"这提示患者在病房内秘密摄入了额外的锂。"},{"id":"D","en":"This represents definitive resolution of the toxicity and indicates lithium levels no longer need to be monitored.","zh":"这代表了毒性的彻底消除，并表明不再需要监测锂浓度。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The rise from 1.1 to 1.3 mEq/L represents lithium rebound — redistribution of lithium from the intracellular and tissue compartments back into the serum after dialysis has cleared the extracellular lithium. This is expected.","rationaleCorrectZh":"从1.1上升到1.3 mEq/L代表锂的反弹——透析清除了细胞外液中的锂后，锂从细胞内和组织室重新分布回血清。这是预期内的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that hemodialysis rapidly clears blood levels, but intracellular lithium takes time to equilibrate, leading to a typical 'rebound' increase in blood levels post-dialysis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想一下，血液透析能迅速清除血液中的浓度，但细胞内锂需要时间来平衡，从而导致透析后血液浓度的典型“反弹”增加。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":153,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,54],"fullStemEn":"The daughter states she feels guilty and asks if the patient will have brain damage and if lithium should be stopped permanently. What are the most appropriate nursing responses? (Select all that apply)","fullStemZh":"女儿表示她感到内疚，并询问患者是否会有脑损伤以及是否应永久停用锂。最合适的护理回应是什么？（选择所有适用的）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用的）","penultimateSentenceEn":"What are the most appropriate nursing responses?","penultimateSentenceZh":"最合适的护理回应是什么？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"She will recover completely without any lasting effects.","zh":"她将完全康复，没有任何后遗症。"},{"id":"A","en":"The improvement in her alertness is a positive sign, but the medical team will continue to monitor her closely.","zh":"她警觉性的提高是一个积极的信号，但医疗团队将继续密切监测她。"},{"id":"C","en":"The decision to restart lithium will be made together by the psychiatrist and your mother once she is fully recovered.","zh":"一旦你母亲完全康复，精神科医生和她将共同做出是否重新开始服用锂的决定。"},{"id":"F","en":"Let's focus on her current treatment plan rather than dwelling on the past.","zh":"让我们把重点放在她目前的治疗计划上，而不是纠结于过去。"},{"id":"E","en":"Because of this severe reaction, she should never take lithium again.","zh":"因为这种严重的反应，她不应该再服用锂了。"},{"id":"B","en":"This toxicity was caused by a specific drug interaction and dehydration, not by anything you failed to do.","zh":"这种毒性是由特定的药物相互作用和脱水引起的，而不是因为你没做什么。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Psychosocial support and accurate health teaching are within RN scope and essential for therapeutic alliance. Acknowledging guilt, giving factual reassurance without false promises, and deferring future medical decisions to providers are appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心理社会支持和准确的健康宣教在注册护士的执业范围内，对治疗联盟至关重要。承认内疚，在没有虚假承诺的情况下给予基于事实的保证，以及将未来的医疗决策留给医生是合适的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic communication should acknowledge feelings, provide facts, and avoid false reassurance or making medical promises.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性沟通应承认患者的感受，提供事实，并避免虚假的保证或做出医疗承诺。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"What are the most appropriate nursing responses?","controlSentenceZh":"最合适的护理回应是什么？（"}
{"queueIndex":154,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_lithium_toxicity_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.68","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.68.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.68.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[252,341],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,115],"fullStemEn":"A 52-year-old woman with bipolar I disorder on stable lithium therapy presents with obtundation, new myoclonic jerks, and facial fasciculations. Ten days ago, she was started on hydrochlorothiazide. Her serum lithium is 2.6 mEq/L and eGFR is impaired. Despite aggressive IV hydration, her symptoms and lithium level show minimal improvement.","fullStemZh":"一名患有双相I型情感障碍的52岁女性，接受稳定的锂治疗，表现出迟钝、新发肌阵挛抽搐和面部肌束颤动。10天前，她开始服用氢氯噻嗪。她的血清锂浓度为2.6 mEq/L，eGFR受损。尽管进行了积极的静脉补液，她的症状和锂浓度改善极小。","terminalSentenceEn":"Despite aggressive IV hydration, her symptoms and lithium level show minimal improvement.","terminalSentenceZh":"尽管进行了积极的静脉补液，她的症状和锂浓度改善极小。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her serum lithium is 2.6 mEq/L and eGFR is impaired.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她的血清锂浓度为2.6 mEq/L，eGFR受损。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond1","en":"Severe lithium toxicity","zh":"严重的锂中毒"},{"id":"cond3","en":"Acute gastroenteritis","zh":"急性胃肠炎"},{"id":"cond2","en":"Bipolar disorder exacerbation","zh":"双相情感障碍恶化"}],"correct":"cond1"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act1","en":"Prepare the patient for emergent hemodialysis","zh":"为患者进行紧急血液透析做准备"},{"id":"act3","en":"Continue IV fluid resuscitation as the sole treatment","zh":"继续静脉补液作为唯一的治疗"},{"id":"act4","en":"Administer next scheduled dose of lithium","zh":"给予下一次预定的锂剂量"},{"id":"act2","en":"Maintain aspiration precautions","zh":"维持防误吸预防措施"}],"correct":["act1","act2"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param4","en":"Serum calcium","zh":"血清钙"},{"id":"param2","en":"Neurological status","zh":"神经系统状态"},{"id":"param1","en":"Serial serum lithium levels","zh":"连续血清锂浓度"},{"id":"param3","en":"Serum glucose","zh":"血清葡萄糖"}],"correct":["param1","param2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most likely condition is severe lithium toxicity precipitated by thiazide diuretic–lithium interaction and volume depletion. Emergent hemodialysis is required due to minimal clearance with IV fluids and progressive neurotoxicity. Protecting the airway remains a priority. Serial lithium levels and neurological status must be monitored to evaluate the effectiveness of dialysis and detect potential rebound.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能的病况是由噻嗪类利尿剂-锂的相互作用和容量消耗诱发的严重锂中毒。由于静脉补液清除极小以及进行性神经毒性，需要进行紧急血液透析。保护气道仍然是优先事项。必须连续监测锂浓度和神经系统状态，以评估透析的有效性并发现潜在的反弹。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In severe lithium toxicity, the presence of progressive neurotoxicity demands extracorporeal removal, as the kidneys alone cannot compensate fast enough.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在严重的锂中毒中，进行性神经毒性的出现需要体外清除，因为单靠肾脏无法足够快地代偿。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Her serum lithium is 2.6 mEq/L and eGFR is impaired.","controlSentenceZh":"她的血清锂浓度为2.6 mEq/L，eGFR受损。"}
{"queueIndex":155,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_deleg_uap_hl_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.69","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.69.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.69.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,45],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse is planning the shift for a stable medical client. Highlight the tasks that are appropriate to delegate to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名病情稳定的内科患者安排班次。请标出适合委派给无执照辅助人员（UAP）的任务。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the tasks that are appropriate to delegate to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出适合委派给无执照辅助人员（UAP）的任务。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A registered nurse is planning the shift for a stable medical client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名病情稳定的内科患者安排班次。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Assist the client to the bathroom and provide perineal care.","zh":"协助患者如厕并进行会阴护理。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Measure and record routine vital signs on the stable client.","zh":"为该病情稳定的患者测量并记录常规生命体征。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Record the client's oral intake and urine output.","zh":"记录患者的经口摄入量和尿量。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Reposition the client every 2 hours and apply prescribed lotion.","zh":"每2小时为患者翻身并涂抹医嘱规定的润肤露。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Perform the admission assessment for a newly arrived client.","zh":"为新入院患者完成入院评估。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Teach the client how to use the incentive spirometer.","zh":"教患者如何使用激励式肺量计。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Evaluate whether the client's pain has improved after analgesia.","zh":"评估患者用镇痛药后疼痛是否缓解。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Adjust the IV infusion rate for the client's antibiotic.","zh":"调整患者抗生素静脉输注的速度。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"UAP may perform standardized, predictable tasks for stable clients with predictable outcomes: hygiene and ADLs, routine vital signs, recording intake and output, and routine repositioning. The RN retains the activities that require nursing judgment — assessment (including admission assessment), client teaching, evaluation of responses to care, and management of IV medications. This split reflects the NCSBN/ANA National Guidelines for Nursing Delegation and the Five Rights of Delegation (right task, circumstance, person, direction, supervision).","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于病情稳定、结果可预测的患者，UAP 可执行标准化、可预测的任务：卫生和日常生活活动、常规生命体征、记录出入量以及常规翻身。护士保留需要护理判断的活动——评估（包括入院评估）、患者教育、评价护理反应以及静脉药物管理。该划分依据 NCSBN/ANA《护理委派国家指南》和委派五项原则（正确的任务、情境、人员、指导和监督）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Delegate the predictable and standardized; keep assessment, teaching, evaluation, and medication management with the RN.","testTakingStrategyZh":"可委派可预测、标准化的任务；评估、教育、评价和药物管理仍由护士保留。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":156,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_unsafe_orders_hl_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.70","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.70.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.70.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews newly written orders for a 70-year-old client. Highlight the orders the nurse must clarify with the prescriber before carrying them out.","fullStemZh":"护士审阅一名70岁患者的新医嘱。请标出护士在执行前必须先与开具医嘱者核实的医嘱。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the orders the nurse must clarify with the prescriber before carrying them out.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出护士在执行前必须先与开具医嘱者核实的医嘱。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse reviews newly written orders for a 70-year-old client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士审阅一名70岁患者的新医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Potassium chloride 20 mEq IV push now.","zh":"氯化钾20 mEq静脉推注，立即执行。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Furosemide 40 mg IV once daily.","zh":"呋塞米40 mg静脉注射，每日一次。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Heparin 'titrate per protocol' with no order for baseline labs or the protocol referenced.","zh":"肝素“按方案滴定”，但未开具基线化验，也未注明所依据的方案。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Metoprolol 25 mg PO twice daily, hold for heart rate below 60.","zh":"美托洛尔25 mg口服，每日两次，心率低于60时暂停。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Morphine 10 mg IV every 1 hour PRN for an opioid-naive client.","zh":"吗啡10 mg静脉注射，每1小时按需一次，用于未使用过阿片类药物的患者。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours PRN for pain.","zh":"对乙酰氨基酚650 mg口服，每6小时按需一次，用于疼痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Regular diet as tolerated.","zh":"普通饮食，耐受即可。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s3","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Three orders are unsafe or incomplete and must be clarified. Concentrated potassium chloride is never given by IV push — it is a high-alert medication that must be diluted and infused; rapid IV potassium can cause fatal dysrhythmia (ISMP high-alert list). A heparin titration order with no protocol named and no baseline coagulation studies is incomplete and unsafe. Morphine 10 mg IV every hour for an opioid-naive older adult is an excessive dose/frequency and risks respiratory depression. Furosemide, metoprolol with a hold parameter, PRN acetaminophen, and a regular diet are all reasonable as written. Questioning an unsafe order is the first step in the chain of command.","rationaleCorrectZh":"其中三条医嘱不安全或不完整，必须核实。浓氯化钾绝不可静脉推注——它是高警示药物，必须稀释后输注；快速静脉补钾可致命性心律失常（ISMP 高警示药物清单）。肝素滴定医嘱未注明方案、也无基线凝血检查，属不完整且不安全。对未使用过阿片类的老年人每小时静脉注射吗啡10 mg剂量/频率过高，有呼吸抑制风险。呋塞米、带暂停参数的美托洛尔、按需对乙酰氨基酚和普通饮食按医嘱执行均合理。质疑不安全医嘱是启动指挥链的第一步。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Scan for high-alert routes/doses (IV push potassium, opioid excess) and incomplete orders (no protocol, no parameters) — those are the ones to clarify.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点查找高警示给药途径/剂量（静脉推注钾、阿片过量）和不完整医嘱（无方案、无参数）——这些需要核实。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":157,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_informed_consent_hl_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.71","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.71.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.71.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,44],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for surgery and has signed the consent form. Highlight the findings that mean the nurse should pause and notify the surgeon before the client proceeds.","fullStemZh":"一名患者已安排手术并签署了同意书。请标出提示护士应暂停并在患者继续前通知外科医生的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that mean the nurse should pause and notify the surgeon before the client proceeds.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出提示护士应暂停并在患者继续前通知外科医生的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is scheduled for surgery and has signed the consent form.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者已安排手术并签署了同意书。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The client says, 'I'm not really sure what they're removing or why.'","zh":"患者说：“我其实不太清楚他们要切除什么、为什么切。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The client received IV midazolam 20 minutes before signing.","zh":"患者在签字前20分钟接受了静脉咪达唑仑。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client asks to speak with the surgeon again about the risks.","zh":"患者要求再次与外科医生讨论风险。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The consent form is signed, dated, and witnessed.","zh":"同意书已签名、注明日期并有见证。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client states the planned procedure and expected benefit in their own words.","zh":"患者用自己的话说出了计划的手术及预期获益。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client's spouse is present and supportive.","zh":"患者的配偶在场并表示支持。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Valid informed consent requires that the client understand the procedure, risks, benefits, and alternatives, and consent voluntarily while competent. The nurse advocates by stopping the process when consent appears invalid. A client who cannot describe what is being done or why does not have adequate understanding; consent signed after a sedative (midazolam) may not be valid because the client was not fully competent; and a request to speak with the surgeon again about risks means the disclosure is incomplete — the provider, not the nurse, obtains informed consent. A complete, witnessed form, an accurate teach-back, and a supportive spouse are reassuring, not red flags.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的知情同意要求患者理解手术、风险、获益和替代方案，并在具备行为能力时自愿同意。当同意似乎无效时，护士通过暂停流程来维护患者权益。无法说明手术内容或原因的患者理解不充分；在使用镇静剂（咪达唑仑）后签署的同意可能无效，因为患者并非完全具备行为能力；要求再次与外科医生讨论风险说明告知不完整——获取知情同意的是医生而非护士。完整且有见证的同意书、准确的回授以及支持性的配偶是令人安心的，而非警示信号。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consent is invalid if the client lacks understanding or competence (sedation) or still has unanswered questions. The provider — not the nurse — discloses and obtains it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"若患者缺乏理解、缺乏行为能力（镇静）或仍有未解答的问题，同意即无效。告知并获取同意的是医生，而非护士。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":158,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_incident_doc_hl_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.72","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.72.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.72.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[32,116],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,29],"fullStemEn":"A client fell while ambulating. Highlight the entries that the nurse should document in the client's medical record.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在行走时跌倒。请标出护士应记录在患者病历中的内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entries that the nurse should document in the client's medical record.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出护士应记录在患者病历中的内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client fell while ambulating.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在行走时跌倒。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Objective description of how the client was found and the time.","zh":"对发现患者时情形和时间的客观描述。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Assessment findings after the fall, including vital signs and any injury.","zh":"跌倒后的评估发现，包括生命体征和有无损伤。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The provider was notified and the time of notification.","zh":"已通知医生及通知的时间。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Interventions performed and the client's response.","zh":"已实施的护理措施及患者的反应。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"A note that an incident report was completed and filed.","zh":"注明已填写并提交事件报告。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The nurse's opinion that staffing was too low and the fall was the hospital's fault.","zh":"护士关于人手不足、跌倒是医院过错的个人看法。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The medical record should contain only objective, factual clinical information: how and when the client was found, post-event assessment and vital signs, provider notification with time, and interventions with the client's response. The chart must NOT state that an incident (occurrence) report was filed — the incident report is a separate internal quality/risk-management document, and referencing it in the record can make it discoverable and undermine its protected purpose. The chart should also never contain blame, opinions, or speculation about fault. This reflects standard risk-management and documentation practice.","rationaleCorrectZh":"病历只应包含客观、事实性的临床信息：发现患者的方式与时间、事件后评估与生命体征、通知医生及时间、护理措施及患者反应。病历中绝不可写明已填写事件（不良事件）报告——事件报告是单独的内部质量/风险管理文件，在病历中引用可能使其可被司法调取，破坏其受保护的用途。病历中也绝不应出现指责、个人观点或对过错的猜测。这符合标准的风险管理与记录规范。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Chart objective facts, assessment, notification, and response. Keep the incident report — and all blame/opinion — out of the medical record.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记录客观事实、评估、通知和反应。事件报告及一切指责/观点都不写入病历。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":159,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_discharge_coord_bt_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.73","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.73.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.73.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[267,386],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,99],"fullStemEn":"An older adult is being discharged after a heart-failure admission with new daily weights, a low-sodium diet, several new medications, and a planned home oxygen setup. The client lives alone, has limited mobility, and cannot reliably read the discharge instructions. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely problem, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名独居老人因心力衰竭住院后即将出院，新增每日称重、低钠饮食、数种新药以及计划中的家庭氧疗。患者活动受限，且无法可靠阅读出院说明。请完成蝶形图：选择最可能的问题、两项优先护理措施和两项需监测的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely problem, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝶形图：选择最可能的问题、两项优先护理措施和两项需监测的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client lives alone, has limited mobility, and cannot reliably read the discharge instructions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者活动受限，且无法可靠阅读出院说明。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_nonadh","en":"Intentional nonadherence to the treatment plan","zh":"对治疗方案的故意不依从"},{"id":"c_delay","en":"No discharge concern; the client is medically stable","zh":"无出院顾虑；患者病情稳定"},{"id":"c_risk","en":"Risk for an unsafe discharge with unmet self-care and home-support needs","zh":"存在不安全出院风险，自我照护和居家支持需求未得到满足"}],"correct":"c_risk"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_cps","en":"Report the client to adult protective services for living alone","zh":"因患者独居而向成人保护服务机构举报"},{"id":"a_referrals","en":"Coordinate referrals for home health and durable medical equipment, and confirm the oxygen setup before discharge","zh":"协调家庭护理和耐用医疗设备转介，并在出院前确认氧疗设备到位"},{"id":"a_discharge_now","en":"Discharge as scheduled and document that the client verbalized understanding","zh":"按计划出院，并记录患者口头表示理解"},{"id":"a_teachback","en":"Use plain-language teaching with teach-back and provide pictorial/written instructions the client can use","zh":"采用通俗语言教学并进行回授，提供患者可使用的图示/书面说明"}],"correct":["a_referrals","a_teachback"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_teachback","en":"The client's teach-back of daily weights, medications, and when to call for help","zh":"患者对每日称重、用药及何时求助的回授情况"},{"id":"p_room","en":"The client's preference for a private room","zh":"患者对单人病房的偏好"},{"id":"p_followup","en":"Confirmed follow-up appointment and home-health visit are in place","zh":"已落实的随访预约和家庭护理上门访视"},{"id":"p_satisfaction","en":"Hospital satisfaction-survey score as the main discharge outcome","zh":"将医院满意度调查评分作为主要出院结局"}],"correct":["p_followup","p_teachback"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The combination of living alone, limited mobility, low health literacy, and a complex new regimen creates a high risk for an unsafe discharge — this is a care-coordination problem, not willful nonadherence. The nurse's priority actions are to arrange the interdisciplinary supports the client needs (home health, durable medical equipment, confirmed home oxygen) and to teach in a way the client can actually use (plain language, teach-back, pictorial instructions). Effectiveness is monitored by confirming the follow-up and home-health visit are actually in place and by the client's teach-back of the key self-care behaviors. Discharging on schedule with only 'verbalized understanding,' or making an unwarranted protective-services report, do not address the unmet needs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"独居、活动受限、健康素养低再加上复杂的新方案，造成不安全出院的高风险——这是护理协调问题，而非故意不依从。护士的优先措施是安排患者所需的跨学科支持（家庭护理、耐用医疗设备、确认家庭氧疗），并以患者真正能使用的方式进行教学（通俗语言、回授、图示说明）。通过确认随访和家庭护理访视确实落实、以及患者对关键自我照护行为的回授来监测效果。仅凭“口头表示理解”就按时出院，或作出无依据的保护服务举报，都无法解决未满足的需求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When discharge needs exceed the client's resources, the answer is coordination and usable teaching — then verify the supports are actually in place.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当出院需求超出患者资源时，答案是协调和可用的教学——然后核实支持确实到位。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":160,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_escalation_bt_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.74","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.74.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.74.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[192,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,63],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative client's condition is worsening: blood pressure is falling, heart rate is rising, and urine output has dropped. The nurse pages the first-year resident twice with no response. Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's management priority.","fullStemZh":"一名术后患者病情恶化：血压下降、心率升高、尿量减少。护士两次呼叫第一年住院医师均无回应。请完成蝶形图，确定护士的管理优先事项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's management priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝶形图，确定护士的管理优先事项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse pages the first-year resident twice with no response.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士两次呼叫第一年住院医师均无回应。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_wait","en":"An expected postoperative course that requires no escalation","zh":"属预期的术后过程，无需上报"},{"id":"c_deter","en":"Clinical deterioration with an unanswered escalation that the nurse must move up the chain of command","zh":"临床病情恶化且上报未获回应，护士必须沿指挥链继续上报"},{"id":"c_doc","en":"A documentation problem to be resolved at the end of shift","zh":"属在班末处理的记录问题"}],"correct":"c_deter"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_wait_resident","en":"Keep paging only the first-year resident and wait for a callback","zh":"仅继续呼叫第一年住院医师并等待回电"},{"id":"a_chart_only","en":"Document the unanswered pages and address it in the morning","zh":"记录未获回应的呼叫，留待早上处理"},{"id":"a_rrt","en":"Stay with the client, initiate the rapid response team, and continue monitoring per protocol","zh":"留在患者身边，启动快速反应团队，并按方案持续监测"},{"id":"a_chain","en":"Escalate up the chain of command (charge nurse, attending/supervising provider) until the client is evaluated","zh":"沿指挥链上报（责任护士、主治/上级医生），直至患者得到评估"}],"correct":["a_rrt","a_chain"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_time","en":"Time to provider evaluation and time to intervention","zh":"至医生评估的时间和至干预的时间"},{"id":"p_vitals","en":"Trend in vital signs, urine output, and level of consciousness","zh":"生命体征、尿量和意识水平的变化趋势"},{"id":"p_pref","en":"The client's room-temperature preference","zh":"患者对室温的偏好"},{"id":"p_staff","en":"Staff lunch-break schedule","zh":"工作人员午休时间安排"}],"correct":["p_vitals","p_time"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Falling blood pressure, rising heart rate, and dropping urine output signal clinical deterioration (possible hypovolemia/shock). When the first responder does not answer, the nurse must not simply keep paging the same resident — patient safety requires both immediate support (stay with the client, activate the rapid response team) and moving up the chain of command until a qualified provider evaluates the client. Effectiveness is judged by the trend in the client's status and by how quickly evaluation and intervention occur. Documenting and waiting until morning, or repeatedly paging only the unresponsive resident, delays needed care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血压下降、心率升高、尿量减少提示临床恶化（可能为低血容量/休克）。当第一应答者无回应时，护士不能只是继续呼叫同一住院医师——患者安全要求既给予即时支持（留在患者身边、启动快速反应团队），又沿指挥链向上上报，直至有资质的医生评估患者。效果通过患者状态的变化趋势以及评估和干预发生的速度来判断。记录后等到早上、或反复只呼叫无回应的住院医师，都会延误所需的护理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Deterioration plus an unanswered call = stay, get rapid help (RRT), and climb the chain of command. Never just re-page and wait.","testTakingStrategyZh":"病情恶化加上呼叫无回应＝留下、寻求快速支援（RRT）、并沿指挥链上报。绝不能只是反复呼叫并等待。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":161,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_informed_refusal_bt_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.75","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.75.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.75.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,62],"fullStemEn":"A competent, alert adult client refuses a scheduled blood transfusion that the provider has recommended. The client says, 'I understand the risks, but I do not want it.' Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's response.","fullStemZh":"一名有行为能力、清醒的成年患者拒绝医生建议的预定输血。患者说：“我了解风险，但我不想输。”请完成蝶形图，确定护士的处理方式。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝶形图，确定护士的处理方式。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client says, 'I understand the risks, but I do not want it.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者说：“我了解风险，但我不想输。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely situation","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_emergency","en":"An emergency that allows treatment without consent","zh":"属于可在无同意下施治的紧急情况"},{"id":"c_incompetent","en":"An incompetent client who cannot make decisions","zh":"无行为能力、不能作出决定的患者"},{"id":"c_refusal","en":"A competent client exercising the right to refuse treatment (informed refusal)","zh":"有行为能力的患者行使拒绝治疗的权利（知情拒绝）"}],"correct":"c_refusal"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_guilt","en":"Tell the client they could die and that refusing is irresponsible","zh":"告诉患者拒绝就可能死亡、是不负责任的行为"},{"id":"a_support","en":"Ensure the client understands the consequences, explore concerns, and respect the decision","zh":"确认患者理解后果，了解其顾虑，并尊重其决定"},{"id":"a_notify_doc","en":"Notify the provider of the refusal and document the client's decision and stated understanding","zh":"通知医生患者拒绝，并记录患者的决定及其所表述的理解"},{"id":"a_force","en":"Administer the transfusion anyway because the provider ordered it","zh":"因医生已开具医嘱而仍然执行输血"}],"correct":["a_notify_doc","a_support"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_understanding","en":"The client's continued understanding and any change in the decision","zh":"患者持续的理解情况及决定是否有变化"},{"id":"p_status","en":"The client's clinical status related to the refused treatment","zh":"与所拒绝治疗相关的患者临床状态"},{"id":"p_room","en":"The client's meal-tray preferences","zh":"患者对餐盘的偏好"},{"id":"p_nurse_pref","en":"The nurse's personal opinion about the choice","zh":"护士本人对该选择的个人意见"}],"correct":["p_understanding","p_status"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A competent, informed adult has the legal and ethical right to refuse any treatment, even life-sustaining treatment such as a transfusion. The nurse advocates by confirming the client understands the consequences and exploring concerns, then respecting the decision, notifying the provider, and documenting the informed refusal. Forcing treatment is battery; using guilt or coercion violates the client's autonomy. Monitoring focuses on continued understanding, any change of mind, and the clinical status affected by the refusal — not on the nurse's personal opinion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有行为能力且知情的成年人拥有拒绝任何治疗的法律和伦理权利，即使是输血等维持生命的治疗。护士通过确认患者理解后果并了解其顾虑来维护其权益，然后尊重决定、通知医生并记录知情拒绝。强行施治构成侵权（人身侵犯）；使用内疚感或胁迫则侵犯患者自主权。监测聚焦于患者持续的理解、是否改变主意以及受拒绝影响的临床状态——而非护士的个人意见。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A competent client may refuse anything. Confirm understanding, respect the choice, notify the provider, and document — never coerce.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有行为能力的患者可拒绝任何治疗。确认理解、尊重选择、通知医生并记录——绝不胁迫。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":162,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_deleg_matrix_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.76","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.76.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.76.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,234],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,68],"fullStemEn":"For each task, select the lowest-level team member to whom the registered nurse can appropriately assign it on a medical-surgical unit. Assume a common U.S. med-surg scope where the state Nurse Practice Act and facility policy permit.","fullStemZh":"对于每项任务，请选择在内外科病区护士可恰当委派的最低层级团队成员。假设是在相关州《护理执业法》和机构政策允许的常见美国内外科执业范围内。","terminalSentenceEn":"Assume a common U.S. med-surg scope where the state Nurse Practice Act and facility policy permit.","terminalSentenceZh":"假设是在相关州《护理执业法》和机构政策允许的常见美国内外科执业范围内。","penultimateSentenceEn":"For each task, select the lowest-level team member to whom the registered nurse can appropriately assign it on a medical-surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"对于每项任务，请选择在内外科病区护士可恰当委派的最低层级团队成员。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Bathing and feeding a stable client","zh":"为病情稳定的患者洗澡和喂食"},{"id":"r2","en":"Administering a scheduled oral medication to a stable client","zh":"为病情稳定的患者给予一次定时口服药"},{"id":"r3","en":"Reinforcing previously taught discharge instructions","zh":"强化先前已教过的出院指导"},{"id":"r4","en":"Performing the initial assessment of a newly admitted client","zh":"为新入院患者进行首次评估"},{"id":"r5","en":"Developing and revising the nursing care plan","zh":"制定和修订护理计划"},{"id":"r6","en":"Administering IV push medication and titrating a vasoactive drip","zh":"静脉推注药物并滴定血管活性药物"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_rn","en":"RN only","zh":"仅注册护士"},{"id":"c_uap","en":"UAP","zh":"UAP（无执照辅助人员）"},{"id":"c_lpn","en":"LPN/LVN","zh":"LPN/LVN（实用/职业护士）"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c_uap"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c_lpn"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c_lpn"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c_rn"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c_rn"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c_rn"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assign at the lowest level whose scope safely covers the task. UAP perform standardized ADL care for stable clients (bathing/feeding). LPN/LVN may administer most routine oral/IM/SubQ medications and reinforce teaching the RN already provided. The RN retains the activities requiring independent nursing judgment: the initial/admission assessment, creating and revising the care plan, and high-risk medication administration such as IV push drugs and titration of vasoactive infusions. (Scope varies by state Nurse Practice Act and facility policy; this reflects common U.S. acute-care delegation rules and the NCSBN/ANA delegation guidelines.)","rationaleCorrectZh":"在能安全覆盖任务的最低层级进行委派。UAP 为病情稳定的患者提供标准化的日常生活照护（洗澡/喂食）。LPN/LVN 可给予多数常规口服/肌注/皮下药物，并强化护士已提供的教学。护士保留需要独立护理判断的活动：首次/入院评估、制定和修订护理计划，以及高风险给药如静脉推注和血管活性药物滴定。（执业范围因各州《护理执业法》和机构政策而异；此处反映美国急症护理常见的委派规则及 NCSBN/ANA 委派指南。）","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the task to the lowest safe scope: UAP = stable ADLs; LPN = routine meds + reinforcing teaching; RN = assessment, care planning, teaching, high-risk meds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将任务匹配到最低的安全执业范围：UAP＝稳定患者的日常照护；LPN＝常规给药＋强化教学；RN＝评估、护理计划、教学、高风险给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":163,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_notify_matrix_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.77","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.77.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.77.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"For each finding during routine rounds, classify whether the nurse should notify the provider promptly or document it as a routine finding.","fullStemZh":"对于常规查房中的每项发现，请判断护士应及时通知医生，还是作为常规发现进行记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding during routine rounds, classify whether the nurse should notify the provider promptly or document it as a routine finding.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于常规查房中的每项发现，请判断护士应及时通知医生，还是作为常规发现进行记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"New onset of confusion in a previously alert client","zh":"原本清醒的患者出现新发意识混乱"},{"id":"r2","en":"Urine output of 15 mL/hr for the last 3 hours","zh":"过去3小时尿量为15 mL/小时"},{"id":"r3","en":"Oxygen saturation that dropped from 96% to 84% on room air","zh":"室内空气下血氧饱和度从96%降至84%"},{"id":"r4","en":"Blood pressure 122/76, unchanged from baseline","zh":"血压122/76，与基线相比无变化"},{"id":"r5","en":"A healed surgical incision with sutures intact","zh":"已愈合的手术切口，缝线完整"},{"id":"r6","en":"A client sleeping comfortably with normal vital signs","zh":"患者安睡，生命体征正常"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_routine","en":"Routine documentation","zh":"常规记录"},{"id":"c_notify","en":"Notify provider promptly","zh":"及时通知医生"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c_notify"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c_notify"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c_notify"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c_routine"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c_routine"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c_routine"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Promptly report findings that represent a meaningful change or a threat to safety: new confusion (possible hypoxia, infection, stroke, or metabolic cause), oliguria of 15 mL/hr (well below the ~30 mL/hr adequacy threshold, suggesting hypovolemia or AKI), and a significant oxygen desaturation to 84%. Stable, expected, or normal findings — an unchanged baseline blood pressure, a healed incision, and a comfortably sleeping client with normal vitals — are documented routinely. The skill is distinguishing a clinically significant change from an expected normal finding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应及时上报代表显著变化或威胁安全的发现：新发意识混乱（可能为缺氧、感染、卒中或代谢原因）、尿量15 mL/小时的少尿（远低于约30 mL/小时的充足阈值，提示低血容量或急性肾损伤）以及降至84%的明显血氧下降。稳定、预期或正常的发现——与基线相同的血压、已愈合的切口、生命体征正常且安睡的患者——按常规记录。关键能力是区分有临床意义的变化与预期的正常发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Report new changes and threats to safety; document the stable, expected, and normal. Ask: is this different from baseline and clinically meaningful?","testTakingStrategyZh":"上报新变化和安全威胁；记录稳定、预期和正常的发现。自问：这是否不同于基线且有临床意义？","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":164,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_referrals_sata_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.78","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.78.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.78.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[205,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,63],"fullStemEn":"A client recovering from a stroke has new swallowing difficulty, weakness on one side, financial worries about home care, and questions about medication costs. Which referrals should the nurse coordinate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名卒中康复期患者出现新的吞咽困难、一侧肢体无力、对居家护理的经济担忧以及关于药费的疑问。护士应协调哪些转介？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which referrals should the nurse coordinate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应协调哪些转介？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Speech-language pathology for a swallowing evaluation","zh":"言语-语言治疗（言语病理）以评估吞咽功能"},{"id":"b","en":"Physical and occupational therapy for mobility and self-care","zh":"物理治疗和作业治疗以改善活动和自我照护"},{"id":"d","en":"Pharmacy for medication review and cost/assistance options","zh":"药剂科进行用药审查及费用/援助方案咨询"},{"id":"e","en":"No referrals are needed; the nurse will manage all needs alone","zh":"无需转介；护士将独自处理所有需求"},{"id":"f","en":"Delay all referrals until the client is discharged","zh":"将所有转介推迟到患者出院后"},{"id":"c","en":"Social work or case management for home-care and financial concerns","zh":"社会工作或个案管理以解决居家护理和经济顾虑"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Care coordination means matching each identified need to the right interdisciplinary resource. New swallowing difficulty warrants a speech-language pathology referral (and aspiration precautions) before further oral intake; one-sided weakness warrants physical and occupational therapy; financial and home-care concerns are addressed by social work/case management; and medication-cost questions are addressed by pharmacy. Managing everything alone or delaying referrals until discharge fails the client and is unsafe — early referral is what makes a safe, supported transition possible.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护理协调意味着将每项已识别的需求匹配到合适的跨学科资源。新发吞咽困难需在进一步经口进食前转介言语-语言治疗（并采取防误吸措施）；一侧肢体无力需物理治疗和作业治疗；经济和居家护理顾虑由社会工作/个案管理处理；药费问题由药剂科处理。独自处理一切或将转介拖到出院后会辜负患者且不安全——尽早转介才能实现安全、有支持的过渡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match each need to its discipline (swallowing→SLP, mobility→PT/OT, money/home→social work, drug cost→pharmacy). Coordinating early beats doing it all alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将每项需求匹配到相应学科（吞咽→言语治疗、活动→物理/作业治疗、经济/居家→社会工作、药费→药剂科）。尽早协调胜过独自包揽。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":165,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_ama_sata_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.79","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.79.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.79.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,45],"fullStemEn":"A competent adult client states they want to leave the hospital against medical advice (AMA). Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名有行为能力的成年患者表示要违背医嘱（AMA）离院。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"c","en":"Determine why the client wants to leave and try to resolve fixable barriers","zh":"了解患者想离院的原因，并尝试解决可解决的障碍"},{"id":"d","en":"Provide discharge instructions, any provider-written prescriptions, and follow-up information","zh":"提供出院指导、任何医生开具的处方以及随访信息"},{"id":"b","en":"Explain the risks of leaving and the benefits of staying in understandable terms","zh":"用患者可理解的语言说明离院的风险和留院的获益"},{"id":"a","en":"Notify the provider that the client wishes to leave AMA","zh":"通知医生患者希望违背医嘱离院"},{"id":"f","en":"Document the client's decision, the teaching provided, and their stated understanding","zh":"记录患者的决定、所提供的教育及其表述的理解"},{"id":"e","en":"Physically prevent the competent client from leaving until they sign the form","zh":"在患者签字前以人身方式阻止这名有行为能力的患者离开"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","f"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A competent client may leave AMA. The nurse notifies the provider, explains the risks of leaving and benefits of staying in understandable language, explores and tries to resolve the reasons for leaving (pain, childcare, cost, fear), still provides discharge instructions, provider-written prescriptions, and follow-up so the client can be as safe as possible, and documents the decision, teaching, and the client's understanding. The nurse may NOT physically detain a competent client — false imprisonment is unlawful, and signing the AMA form is requested but cannot be forced. Care and documentation continue regardless of whether the form is signed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有行为能力的患者可违背医嘱离院。护士通知医生，用可理解的语言说明离院风险和留院获益，了解并尝试解决离院原因（疼痛、照顾孩子、费用、恐惧），仍提供出院指导、医生开具的处方和随访以使患者尽可能安全，并记录决定、教育及患者的理解。护士不得以人身方式拘留一名有行为能力的患者——非法拘禁属违法，签署 AMA 表格可请求但不能强迫。无论是否签署表格，护理和记录都应继续。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For AMA: notify, educate, explore barriers, still give instructions/scripts, and document. You may not physically detain a competent client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于 AMA：通知、教育、了解障碍、仍提供指导/处方并记录。不得以人身方式拘留有行为能力的患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":166,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_med_error_order_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.80","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.80.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.80.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers that a client was just given a medication intended for a different client. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一名患者刚被给予了本应给另一名患者的药物。请将护士的措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers that a client was just given a medication intended for a different client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现一名患者刚被给予了本应给另一名患者的药物。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Assess the client for any adverse effects and ensure immediate safety","zh":"评估患者有无不良反应并确保即时安全"},{"id":"c","en":"Carry out new orders and monitor the client as directed","zh":"执行新医嘱并按指示监测患者"},{"id":"b","en":"Notify the provider and the charge nurse of the error","zh":"通知医生和责任护士发生了差错"},{"id":"e","en":"Complete an incident report per facility policy","zh":"按机构政策填写事件报告"},{"id":"d","en":"Document the facts and the client's response in the medical record","zh":"在病历中记录事实及患者的反应"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Client safety comes first: immediately assess for adverse effects and stabilize the client. Next notify the provider and charge nurse so corrective orders and monitoring can be given, then carry out those orders and monitor as directed. Document the objective facts and the client's response in the medical record. Finally, complete the incident report per facility policy — a separate internal risk-management document that is NOT referenced in the chart. Safety and provider notification precede paperwork; the incident report is completed last.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者安全第一：立即评估有无不良反应并稳定患者。接着通知医生和责任护士，以便下达纠正性医嘱和监测，然后执行这些医嘱并按指示监测。在病历中记录客观事实及患者的反应。最后按机构政策填写事件报告——这是一份单独的内部风险管理文件，不在病历中提及。安全和通知医生先于文书工作；事件报告最后完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After an error: client first (assess/stabilize), then notify, then carry out orders, then document facts, then incident report last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"差错后：先患者（评估/稳定），再通知，再执行医嘱，再记录事实，事件报告放在最后。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":167,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_deleg_process_order_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.81","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.81.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.81.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,44],"fullStemEn":"A charge nurse is delegating a task to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP). Place the steps of safe delegation in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"责任护士正在将一项任务委派给无执照辅助人员（UAP）。请将安全委派的步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps of safe delegation in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将安全委派的步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A charge nurse is delegating a task to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","penultimateSentenceZh":"责任护士正在将一项任务委派给无执照辅助人员（UAP）。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Confirm the task is within the UAP's role and right for this client's situation","zh":"确认该任务在 UAP 的岗位职责范围内，且适合该患者的具体情况"},{"id":"b","en":"Verify the UAP is competent and available to take the task","zh":"核实该 UAP 有能力且有空承担该任务"},{"id":"e","en":"Follow up, evaluate the outcome, and give feedback","zh":"跟进、评价结果并给予反馈"},{"id":"c","en":"Give clear directions, expected outcomes, limits, and when to report back","zh":"给予清晰的指示、预期结果、界限以及何时回报"},{"id":"d","en":"Have the UAP perform the task while remaining available","zh":"让 UAP 执行任务，同时保持可联系"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe delegation follows the Five Rights in sequence. First confirm the right task and right circumstance — is this task delegatable and appropriate for this specific client right now? Then the right person — verify the UAP is competent and available. Then the right direction/communication — give clear, specific instructions, the expected outcome, limits, and when to report. The UAP performs the task while the RN remains available. Finally the right supervision/evaluation — follow up, evaluate the outcome, and give feedback. The RN remains accountable for the delegation decision and outcome throughout.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全委派按顺序遵循五项原则。首先确认正确的任务和正确的情境——该任务是否可委派，且当下是否适合这名具体患者？然后是正确的人员——核实 UAP 有能力且有空。接着是正确的指导/沟通——给予清晰、具体的指示、预期结果、界限以及何时回报。UAP 执行任务，护士保持可联系。最后是正确的监督/评价——跟进、评价结果并给予反馈。整个过程中，护士对委派决定及结果始终负有责任。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the Five Rights in order: task/circumstance, person, direction, then supervise and evaluate. The RN stays accountable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按顺序遵循五项原则：任务/情境、人员、指导，然后监督和评价。护士始终负责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A charge nurse is delegating a task to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","controlSentenceZh":"责任护士正在将一项任务委派给无执照辅助人员（UAP）。"}
{"queueIndex":168,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_assignment_mc_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.82","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.82.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.82.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,51],"fullStemEn":"A charge nurse must assign a client to a licensed practical nurse (LPN/LVN). Which client is most appropriate to assign to the LPN/LVN?","fullStemZh":"责任护士需要为一名实用/职业护士（LPN/LVN）分配患者。将哪名患者分配给 LPN/LVN 最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client is most appropriate to assign to the LPN/LVN?","terminalSentenceZh":"将哪名患者分配给 LPN/LVN 最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A charge nurse must assign a client to a licensed practical nurse (LPN/LVN).","penultimateSentenceZh":"责任护士需要为一名实用/职业护士（LPN/LVN）分配患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"c","en":"A client receiving a first dose of IV chemotherapy","zh":"一名正在接受首剂静脉化疗的患者"},{"id":"b","en":"A newly admitted client who has not yet had an initial assessment","zh":"一名尚未完成首次评估的新入院患者"},{"id":"a","en":"A stable client with a chronic wound who needs a scheduled dressing change","zh":"一名病情稳定、有慢性伤口、需要按时换药的患者"},{"id":"d","en":"An unstable client requiring frequent reassessment and titration of a drip","zh":"一名病情不稳定、需要频繁再评估并滴定输液的患者"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assign to the LPN/LVN a stable client with a predictable plan of care. A scheduled dressing change on a stable client with a chronic wound is well within the LPN/LVN scope. The newly admitted client needs the RN's initial assessment; a first dose of IV chemotherapy and an unstable client requiring frequent reassessment and drip titration all require the RN's judgment and are not appropriate for the LPN/LVN. Match the most stable, predictable client to the LPN/LVN and keep unstable or not-yet-assessed clients with the RN.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应将病情稳定、护理计划可预测的患者分配给 LPN/LVN。为病情稳定的慢性伤口患者按时换药完全在 LPN/LVN 执业范围内。新入院患者需要护士的首次评估；首剂静脉化疗以及需要频繁再评估并滴定输液的不稳定患者都需要护士判断，不适合 LPN/LVN。将最稳定、最可预测的患者匹配给 LPN/LVN，而把不稳定或尚未评估的患者留给护士。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Give the LPN/LVN the most stable, predictable client. Keep unstable, not-yet-assessed, and first-dose/high-risk clients with the RN.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把最稳定、最可预测的患者交给 LPN/LVN。不稳定、尚未评估以及首剂/高风险的患者留给护士。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":169,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_lpn_deleg_hl_b01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.83","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.83.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.83.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,54],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse is delegating to a licensed practical/vocational nurse (LPN/LVN) on a medical-surgical unit. Highlight the tasks that are appropriate to delegate to the LPN/LVN.","fullStemZh":"在内外科病区，护士正在向实用/职业护士（LPN/LVN）委派任务。请标出适合委派给 LPN/LVN 的任务。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the tasks that are appropriate to delegate to the LPN/LVN.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出适合委派给 LPN/LVN 的任务。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A registered nurse is delegating to a licensed practical/vocational nurse (LPN/LVN) on a medical-surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在内外科病区，护士正在向实用/职业护士（LPN/LVN）委派任务。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Administer scheduled oral and subcutaneous medications to a stable client.","zh":"为病情稳定的患者给予定时的口服和皮下药物。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Perform a sterile dressing change on a chronic, stable wound.","zh":"为慢性、稳定的伤口进行无菌换药。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Reinforce diet teaching the RN already provided.","zh":"强化护士已经提供的饮食教学。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Monitor and record findings on a stable client and report changes to the RN.","zh":"监测并记录病情稳定患者的发现，并将变化报告给护士。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Perform the initial admission assessment of a new client.","zh":"为新患者进行入院首次评估。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Develop the nursing care plan for a newly admitted client.","zh":"为新入院患者制定护理计划。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Provide the first teaching about a new diabetes diagnosis.","zh":"首次为新诊断的糖尿病进行教学。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Administer the first dose of IV chemotherapy.","zh":"给予首剂静脉化疗。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The LPN/LVN scope covers routine, stable care: administering most scheduled oral/SubQ/IM medications, performing sterile dressing changes on stable wounds, reinforcing teaching the RN initiated, and monitoring stable clients and reporting to the RN. The RN retains the activities requiring independent nursing judgment: the initial admission assessment, developing the care plan, providing the initial teaching for a new diagnosis, and high-risk care such as the first dose of IV chemotherapy. This reflects the NCSBN/ANA delegation guidelines; exact scope varies by state Nurse Practice Act and facility policy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN/LVN 的执业范围涵盖常规、稳定的护理：给予多数定时的口服/皮下/肌注药物、为稳定伤口进行无菌换药、强化护士发起的教学，以及监测稳定患者并向护士报告。护士保留需要独立护理判断的活动：入院首次评估、制定护理计划、为新诊断进行首次教学，以及如首剂静脉化疗等高风险护理。此处依据 NCSBN/ANA 委派指南；具体范围因各州《护理执业法》和机构政策而异。","testTakingStrategyEn":"LPN/LVN = routine, stable, reinforcing. RN keeps initial assessment, care planning, initial teaching, and high-risk meds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"LPN/LVN＝常规、稳定、强化。护士保留首次评估、护理计划、首次教学和高风险给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":170,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_intervene_cues_hl_b02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.84","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.84.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.84.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,26],"fullStemEn":"A nurse receives report on a postoperative client. Highlight the findings that require the nurse's immediate intervention.","fullStemZh":"护士接班一名术后患者。请标出需要护士立即处理的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require the nurse's immediate intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要护士立即处理的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse receives report on a postoperative client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士接班一名术后患者。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Oxygen saturation is 85% with increasing respiratory effort.","zh":"血氧饱和度为85%，呼吸费力加重。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Systolic blood pressure has fallen from 118 to 84 over the last hour.","zh":"收缩压在过去一小时内从118降至84。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client is increasingly difficult to arouse.","zh":"患者越来越难以唤醒。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The surgical dressing has a small amount of dried serosanguineous drainage.","zh":"手术敷料上有少量干涸的浆液血性渗液。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client reports incisional pain of 4/10, relieved with repositioning.","zh":"患者诉切口疼痛4/10，翻身后缓解。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Urine output has been 30-40 mL/hr.","zh":"尿量为30–40 mL/小时。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The client is anxious and asking when they can see family.","zh":"患者焦虑，询问何时能见家属。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate intervention is required for threats to airway, breathing, and circulation and for a falling level of consciousness. An oxygen saturation of 85% with increasing effort is a breathing emergency; a systolic pressure dropping from 118 to 84 signals possible hemorrhage/shock; and a client who is increasingly difficult to arouse has a deteriorating neurologic status. Dried serosanguineous drainage, incisional pain relieved by repositioning, urine output of 30-40 mL/hr, and situational anxiety are expected or stable and do not require immediate action. Use the ABC framework to separate emergent cues from expected postoperative findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对气道、呼吸、循环的威胁以及意识水平下降需要立即处理。血氧85%伴呼吸费力加重是呼吸急症；收缩压从118降至84提示可能出血/休克；越来越难唤醒的患者神经状态在恶化。干涸的浆液血性渗液、翻身后缓解的切口疼痛、30–40 mL/小时的尿量以及情境性焦虑均属预期或稳定，无需立即处理。用 ABC 框架将紧急线索与预期术后发现区分开。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Airway/breathing/circulation and a dropping level of consciousness come first; expected, stable, or relieved findings can wait.","testTakingStrategyZh":"气道/呼吸/循环和意识水平下降优先；预期、稳定或已缓解的发现可以等待。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":171,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_hipaa_breach_hl_b03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.85","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.85.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.85.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the nurse actions that are breaches of client confidentiality.","fullStemZh":"请标出属于侵犯患者隐私（保密）的护士行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nurse actions that are breaches of client confidentiality.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出属于侵犯患者隐私（保密）的护士行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Discussing a client's diagnosis with a coworker in a crowded elevator.","zh":"在拥挤的电梯里与同事讨论某患者的诊断。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Sharing a client's lab results with a friend who asks out of concern.","zh":"因朋友出于关心询问，便向其透露患者的化验结果。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Leaving the electronic health record open and unattended at the nurses' station.","zh":"在护士站让电子病历处于打开且无人看管的状态。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Giving a verbal handoff to the oncoming nurse assigned to the client.","zh":"向接班并负责该患者的护士进行口头交接。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Reporting a suspected case of a communicable disease to public health as required by law.","zh":"依法向公共卫生部门报告疑似传染病病例。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Verifying identity before discussing care with a person on the client's approved contact list.","zh":"在与患者批准的联系人讨论护理前先核实其身份。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Confidentiality is breached when protected health information is shared with or exposed to people who do not have a need to know. Discussing a diagnosis in a public elevator, telling a friend about lab results, and leaving the medical record open and unattended all expose information improperly. In contrast, a handoff to the assigned oncoming nurse is sharing for treatment, legally mandated communicable-disease reporting is a permitted disclosure under the HIPAA Privacy Rule, and verifying identity before speaking with an approved contact protects confidentiality.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当受保护的健康信息被分享给或暴露给无需知晓的人时，即构成保密性被侵犯。在公共电梯讨论诊断、把化验结果告诉朋友、让病历打开且无人看管，都是不当地暴露信息。相反，向接班负责的护士交接属于为治疗目的分享，依法的传染病上报在 HIPAA《隐私规则》下属许可披露，而在与获批准联系人交谈前核实身份则是在保护保密性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A breach is sharing/exposing PHI to those without a need to know. Treatment handoffs, mandated reports, and identity-verified approved contacts are permitted.","testTakingStrategyZh":"违规＝向无需知晓者分享/暴露受保护健康信息。治疗交接、法定上报、经身份核实的获批联系人均被许可。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":172,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_supervision_hl_b04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.86","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.86.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.86.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is supervising unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP). Highlight the UAP actions that require the nurse to intervene.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监督无执照辅助人员（UAP）。请标出需要护士介入纠正的 UAP 行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the UAP actions that require the nurse to intervene.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要护士介入纠正的 UAP 行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is supervising unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监督无执照辅助人员（UAP）。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The UAP tells a client newly ordered nothing-by-mouth that it is fine to drink water.","zh":"UAP 告诉一名新医嘱禁食禁饮的患者可以喝水。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The UAP reapplies a wrist restraint tied to the movable side rail.","zh":"UAP 将腕部约束带重新系在可活动的床栏上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The UAP interprets a client's new lab result and advises a diet change.","zh":"UAP 解读患者的新化验结果并建议改变饮食。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The UAP assists a stable client to ambulate in the hallway with a gait belt.","zh":"UAP 使用步态带协助一名病情稳定的患者在走廊行走。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The UAP records the client's intake and output on the flowsheet.","zh":"UAP 在流程表上记录患者的出入量。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The UAP measures and reports a routine blood pressure on a stable client.","zh":"UAP 为病情稳定的患者测量并报告常规血压。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must intervene when a UAP acts outside their role or unsafely. Overriding an NPO order risks aspiration and harm; tying a restraint to a movable side rail is a serious safety hazard because the rail can move and injure the client (restraints are anchored to the non-movable bed frame); and interpreting labs and advising a diet change requires nursing judgment outside the UAP scope. Assisting a stable client to ambulate with a gait belt, recording intake and output, and reporting a routine blood pressure on a stable client are all appropriate UAP tasks that need no intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当 UAP 超出其职责或行为不安全时，护士必须介入。擅自取消禁食禁饮医嘱有误吸和伤害风险；将约束带系在可活动床栏上是严重安全隐患，因为床栏移动可能伤及患者（约束应固定在不可活动的床架上）；解读化验并建议改变饮食需要超出 UAP 范围的护理判断。用步态带协助稳定患者行走、记录出入量、为稳定患者报告常规血压，都是恰当的 UAP 任务，无需介入。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Intervene when the UAP overrides orders, acts unsafely, or uses nursing judgment. Leave appropriate, in-scope tasks alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当 UAP 擅自更改医嘱、行为不安全或行使护理判断时介入。对恰当、范围内的任务不予干涉。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":173,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_triage_priority_bt_b05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.87","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.87.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.87.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[266,318],"terminalOffsetsZh":[78,97],"fullStemEn":"A nurse begins the shift with four clients: (A) a client with new audible inspiratory stridor and rising respiratory effort; (B) a client due for routine oral medications; (C) a client requesting discharge teaching; (D) a client with stable chronic pain rated 3/10. Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's first priority.","fullStemZh":"护士开始接班时有四名患者：（A）出现新发可闻及的吸气性喘鸣且呼吸费力加重；（B）到了常规口服给药时间；（C）要求出院教学；（D）慢性疼痛稳定、评分3/10。请完成蝶形图，确定护士的首要优先事项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's first priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝶形图，确定护士的首要优先事项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse begins the shift with four clients: (A) a client with new audible inspiratory stridor and rising respiratory effort; (B) a client due for routine oral medications; (C) a client requesting discharge teaching; (D) a client with stable chronic pain rated 3/10.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士开始接班时有四名患者：（A）出现新发可闻及的吸气性喘鸣且呼吸费力加重；（B）到了常规口服给药时间；（C）要求出院教学；（D）慢性疼痛稳定、评分3/10。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Highest-priority client problem","zh":"最高优先级的患者问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_teach","en":"Client C: discharge teaching that should be completed soon","zh":"患者C：应尽快完成的出院教学"},{"id":"c_meds","en":"Client B: routine medications that are slightly overdue","zh":"患者B：略微逾期的常规给药"},{"id":"c_airway","en":"Client A: a threatened airway requiring immediate assessment and intervention","zh":"患者A：气道受威胁，需要立即评估和干预"}],"correct":"c_airway"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_rrt","en":"Call for help/activate the rapid response team and prepare emergency airway support","zh":"呼叫支援/启动快速反应团队，并准备紧急气道支持"},{"id":"a_meds_first","en":"Pass Client B's routine medications before seeing Client A","zh":"在看患者A之前先给患者B发放常规药物"},{"id":"a_teach_first","en":"Complete Client C's discharge teaching first because they are ready to leave","zh":"因患者C准备离院，先完成其出院教学"},{"id":"a_assess_airway","en":"Go to Client A first, assess the airway and breathing, and position to maximize the airway","zh":"首先到患者A处，评估气道和呼吸，并摆位以最大程度保持气道通畅"}],"correct":["a_assess_airway","a_rrt"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_satisfaction","en":"Client C's satisfaction with the timing of teaching","zh":"患者C对教学时机的满意度"},{"id":"p_loc","en":"Level of consciousness and response to airway interventions","zh":"意识水平及对气道干预的反应"},{"id":"p_med_time","en":"How many minutes late Client B's routine dose was given","zh":"患者B的常规剂量延迟了多少分钟"},{"id":"p_airway","en":"Airway patency, work of breathing, and oxygen saturation","zh":"气道通畅度、呼吸做功和血氧饱和度"}],"correct":["p_airway","p_loc"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the ABC framework, a threatened airway is always the first priority. New inspiratory stridor with rising effort signals airway compromise that can progress to obstruction, so the nurse goes to Client A first, assesses and positions the airway, and calls for help/activates the rapid response team while preparing emergency support. Routine medications, discharge teaching, and stable chronic pain are lower priority and can be delegated or deferred briefly. Effectiveness is monitored by airway patency, work of breathing, oxygen saturation, and level of consciousness — not by medication timing or satisfaction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"依据 ABC 框架，气道受威胁始终是首要优先。新发吸气性喘鸣伴呼吸费力加重提示气道受损，可能进展为梗阻，因此护士先到患者A处，评估并摆正气道，呼叫支援/启动快速反应团队，同时准备紧急支持。常规给药、出院教学和稳定的慢性疼痛优先级较低，可委派或短暂推迟。效果通过气道通畅度、呼吸做功、血氧和意识水平来监测——而非给药时机或满意度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Airway beats everything. The stridor client is seen first; routine meds and teaching wait.","testTakingStrategyZh":"气道高于一切。喘鸣患者最先处理；常规给药和教学需等待。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":174,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_advance_directive_bt_b06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.88","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.88.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.88.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,65],"fullStemEn":"A client has a valid do-not-resuscitate (DNR) order and a living will declining resuscitation. The client's adult child arrives and insists that 'everything be done.' Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's response.","fullStemZh":"一名患者有有效的不复苏（DNR）医嘱和拒绝复苏的生前预嘱。患者的成年子女到达并坚持“全力抢救”。请完成蝶形图，确定护士的处理方式。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝶形图，确定护士的处理方式。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's adult child arrives and insists that 'everything be done.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的成年子女到达并坚持“全力抢救”。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Guiding principle","zh":"指导原则"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_family","en":"Follow the adult child's wishes because family makes the final decision","zh":"听从成年子女的意愿，因为由家属作最终决定"},{"id":"c_honor","en":"Honor the competent client's valid advance directive and right to self-determination","zh":"尊重有行为能力患者的有效预嘱及其自我决定权"},{"id":"c_full","en":"Default to full resuscitation whenever any family member objects","zh":"只要有家属反对就默认全力复苏"}],"correct":"c_honor"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_revoke","en":"Revoke the DNR at the bedside because the family objects","zh":"因家属反对，在床旁撤销 DNR"},{"id":"a_support","en":"Support the family's emotions while explaining the client's documented wishes are followed","zh":"在解释将遵循患者已记录意愿的同时，安抚家属情绪"},{"id":"a_ignore_family","en":"Ignore the family's distress and refuse to discuss the situation","zh":"无视家属的痛苦并拒绝讨论该情况"},{"id":"a_notify_clarify","en":"Notify the provider and arrange for the team to clarify the directive and answer the family's questions","zh":"通知医生，并安排团队向家属澄清预嘱并解答其疑问"}],"correct":["a_notify_clarify","a_support"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_understanding","en":"The family's understanding and any change in the client's own wishes","zh":"家属的理解情况以及患者本人意愿是否有变化"},{"id":"p_visiting","en":"The number of visitors at the bedside","zh":"床旁探视者的人数"},{"id":"p_pref","en":"The family's preference for the client's room assignment","zh":"家属对患者病房分配的偏好"},{"id":"p_order","en":"That the DNR order and advance directive remain current and documented in the record","zh":"DNR 医嘱和预嘱在病历中保持有效并已记录"}],"correct":["p_order","p_understanding"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A competent client's valid advance directive must be honored; the right to self-determination is protected (Patient Self-Determination Act). A family member cannot override a competent client's documented wishes, and the nurse does not revoke a DNR at the bedside because family objects. The nurse notifies the provider, arranges for the team to clarify the directive and answer questions, and supports the family's emotions while explaining that the client's wishes are followed. Monitoring confirms the DNR/advance directive remains current and documented and tracks the family's understanding and any change in the client's own wishes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有行为能力患者的有效预嘱必须得到尊重；自我决定权受保护（《患者自我决定法》）。家属不能推翻有行为能力患者的已记录意愿，护士也不会因家属反对而在床旁撤销 DNR。护士通知医生，安排团队澄清预嘱并解答疑问，在解释将遵循患者意愿的同时安抚家属情绪。监测确认 DNR/预嘱保持有效并已记录，并跟踪家属的理解以及患者本人意愿是否有变化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A competent client's directive wins over family objection. Honor it, involve the provider/team, support the family — never revoke at the bedside.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有行为能力患者的预嘱优先于家属反对。尊重预嘱、让医生/团队参与、安抚家属——绝不在床旁撤销。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":175,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_uap_supervision_bt_b07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.89","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.89.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.89.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[183,229],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,75],"fullStemEn":"A nurse delegated vital-sign measurement to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP). The UAP reports that a postoperative client's blood pressure is 86/48 and the client 'seems sleepy.' Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's response.","fullStemZh":"护士将测量生命体征委派给无执照辅助人员（UAP）。UAP 报告一名术后患者血压为86/48，且患者“似乎昏昏欲睡”。请完成蝶形图，确定护士的处理方式。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie for the nurse's response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝶形图，确定护士的处理方式。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The UAP reports that a postoperative client's blood pressure is 86/48 and the client 'seems sleepy.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"UAP 报告一名术后患者血压为86/48，且患者“似乎昏昏欲睡”。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_uap","en":"A UAP performance problem to be addressed at the staff meeting","zh":"属在员工会议上处理的 UAP 表现问题"},{"id":"c_normal","en":"An expected postoperative finding that needs no action","zh":"属预期的术后发现，无需处理"},{"id":"c_deter","en":"Possible clinical deterioration requiring the RN's own assessment and judgment","zh":"可能的临床恶化，需要护士亲自评估和判断"}],"correct":"c_deter"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_notify","en":"Notify the provider of the abnormal findings and intervene per orders/protocol","zh":"将异常发现通知医生，并按医嘱/方案进行干预"},{"id":"a_document_only","en":"Document the UAP's report and continue routine rounds","zh":"记录 UAP 的报告并继续常规查房"},{"id":"a_delegate_recheck","en":"Tell the UAP to recheck the blood pressure in one hour and document it","zh":"让 UAP 一小时后再测血压并记录"},{"id":"a_assess","en":"Go to the bedside and personally reassess blood pressure, level of consciousness, and other vital signs","zh":"到床旁亲自重新评估血压、意识水平和其他生命体征"}],"correct":["a_assess","a_notify"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_room","en":"The client's television preference","zh":"患者对电视节目的偏好"},{"id":"p_vitals","en":"Trend in blood pressure, heart rate, and level of consciousness","zh":"血压、心率和意识水平的变化趋势"},{"id":"p_uap_schedule","en":"The UAP's break schedule","zh":"UAP 的休息时间安排"},{"id":"p_perfusion","en":"Signs of perfusion such as urine output and skin color/temperature","zh":"灌注体征，如尿量和皮肤颜色/温度"}],"correct":["p_vitals","p_perfusion"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Although measuring vital signs can be delegated, interpreting an abnormal result and assessing a client are the RN's responsibility and cannot be delegated. A blood pressure of 86/48 with new sleepiness suggests possible deterioration (hypovolemia, hemorrhage, or shock), so the nurse must personally reassess at the bedside and notify the provider, intervening per orders. Telling the UAP to recheck in an hour or merely documenting the report delays recognition of a deteriorating client. Monitoring focuses on the vital-sign trend, level of consciousness, and perfusion indicators.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管测量生命体征可以委派，但解读异常结果和评估患者是护士的职责，不能委派。血压86/48伴新发嗜睡提示可能的恶化（低血容量、出血或休克），因此护士必须亲自到床旁重新评估并通知医生，按医嘱干预。让 UAP 一小时后再测、或仅记录报告，都会延误对病情恶化患者的识别。监测聚焦于生命体征趋势、意识水平和灌注指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"You can delegate measuring a vital sign, never interpreting it. An abnormal result = the RN assesses now and notifies.","testTakingStrategyZh":"可以委派测量生命体征，但绝不能委派对其的解读。结果异常＝护士立即评估并通知。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":176,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_independent_action_matrix_b08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.90","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.90.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.90.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"Classify each nursing action as an independent nursing action the RN may initiate without a provider order, or an action that requires a provider order.","fullStemZh":"请将每项护理行为分类为护士无需医嘱即可发起的独立护理行为，或需要医嘱的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing action as an independent nursing action the RN may initiate without a provider order, or an action that requires a provider order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每项护理行为分类为护士无需医嘱即可发起的独立护理行为，或需要医嘱的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Repositioning a client every 2 hours to protect skin","zh":"每2小时为患者翻身以保护皮肤"},{"id":"r2","en":"Teaching relaxation and coping techniques for anxiety","zh":"教授缓解焦虑的放松和应对技巧"},{"id":"r3","en":"Elevating the head of the bed for a client reporting dyspnea","zh":"为诉呼吸困难的患者抬高床头"},{"id":"r4","en":"Administering a PRN analgesic","zh":"给予按需镇痛药"},{"id":"r5","en":"Inserting an indwelling urinary catheter","zh":"留置导尿管"},{"id":"r6","en":"Applying physical restraints","zh":"使用身体约束"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_indep","en":"Independent nursing action","zh":"独立护理行为"},{"id":"c_order","en":"Requires a provider order","zh":"需要医嘱"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c_indep"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c_indep"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c_indep"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c_order"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c_order"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c_order"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Independent nursing actions are within the RN's scope and require no provider order: repositioning to protect skin, teaching coping and relaxation techniques, and positioning such as elevating the head of the bed for comfort and breathing. Actions that require a provider order include administering medications (even PRN, which still requires an order), inserting an indwelling urinary catheter, and applying physical restraints (which require a provider order with strict time limits and monitoring, or emergency application per policy with a prompt order). Distinguishing independent from dependent/collaborative actions is core to safe scope of practice.","rationaleCorrectZh":"独立护理行为在护士执业范围内，无需医嘱：翻身保护皮肤、教授应对和放松技巧、以及为舒适和呼吸而抬高床头等体位调整。需要医嘱的行为包括给药（即使是按需药也仍需医嘱）、留置导尿、以及使用身体约束（需要包含严格时限和监测的医生医嘱，或在紧急情况下根据机构政策先使用并立即获取医嘱）。区分独立行为与依赖/协作行为是安全执业范围的核心。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Positioning, hygiene, teaching, and comfort = independent. Medications, invasive devices, and restraints = need an order.","testTakingStrategyZh":"体位、卫生、教学和舒适措施＝独立行为。给药、侵入性装置和约束＝需要医嘱。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":177,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_see_first_matrix_b09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.91","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.91.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.91.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"For each client, classify whether the nurse should assess them first (urgent) or whether they can wait.","fullStemZh":"对于每名患者，请判断护士应先评估（紧急）还是可以稍后处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client, classify whether the nurse should assess them first (urgent) or whether they can wait.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每名患者，请判断护士应先评估（紧急）还是可以稍后处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"A client reporting new crushing chest pain and diaphoresis","zh":"一名诉新发压榨性胸痛伴大汗的患者"},{"id":"r2","en":"A client with an oxygen saturation of 86% and labored breathing","zh":"一名血氧饱和度86%、呼吸费力的患者"},{"id":"r3","en":"A postoperative client whose blood pressure is trending down with tachycardia","zh":"一名血压呈下降趋势伴心动过速的术后患者"},{"id":"r4","en":"A client requesting a PRN laxative for mild constipation","zh":"一名因轻度便秘请求按需通便剂的患者"},{"id":"r5","en":"A stable client ready for scheduled discharge teaching","zh":"一名病情稳定、可进行预定出院教学的患者"},{"id":"r6","en":"A client with chronic stable knee pain due for a scheduled dose","zh":"一名慢性稳定膝痛、到了预定给药时间的患者"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_first","en":"Assess first (urgent)","zh":"先评估（紧急）"},{"id":"c_wait","en":"Can wait","zh":"可以稍后"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c_first"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c_first"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c_first"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c_wait"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c_wait"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c_wait"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assess first the clients with potentially life-threatening, unstable problems: new crushing chest pain with diaphoresis (possible acute coronary syndrome), an oxygen saturation of 86% with labored breathing (a breathing emergency), and a postoperative client with a falling blood pressure and tachycardia (possible hemorrhage/shock). A PRN laxative request, scheduled discharge teaching for a stable client, and a scheduled dose for chronic stable pain are important but not urgent and can wait. The principle is to see unstable, ABC-threatening clients before stable, predictable ones.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应先评估存在潜在危及生命、病情不稳定问题的患者：新发压榨性胸痛伴大汗（可能为急性冠脉综合征）、血氧86%伴呼吸费力（呼吸急症）、以及血压下降伴心动过速的术后患者（可能出血/休克）。按需通便剂请求、稳定患者的预定出院教学、慢性稳定疼痛的预定给药虽重要但不紧急，可以稍后。原则是先看不稳定、威胁 ABC 的患者，再看稳定、可预测的患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Unstable and ABC-threatening clients are assessed first; stable, scheduled, and comfort needs can wait.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不稳定、威胁 ABC 的患者先评估；稳定、预定和舒适类需求可以稍后。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":178,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_telephone_order_sata_b10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.92","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.92.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.92.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse takes a telephone order from a provider for a client. Which actions ensure the order is handled safely? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士接收医生为某患者下达的电话医嘱。哪些做法能确保该医嘱被安全处理？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions ensure the order is handled safely?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些做法能确保该医嘱被安全处理？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"e","en":"Ensure the provider co-signs the order within the facility's required time frame.","zh":"确保医生在机构规定的时限内补签该医嘱。"},{"id":"b","en":"Read the order back to the provider and receive confirmation.","zh":"向医生复述医嘱并获得确认。"},{"id":"a","en":"Write down the complete order as it is given.","zh":"按下达内容完整记录该医嘱。"},{"id":"c","en":"Clarify anything unclear, including spelling of the drug if needed.","zh":"对任何不清楚之处进行澄清，必要时核对药名拼写。"},{"id":"d","en":"Document the order, date, time, provider name, and that it was read back.","zh":"记录医嘱、日期、时间、医生姓名以及已复述确认。"},{"id":"f","en":"Carry out the order first and clarify any concerns later if there is time.","zh":"先执行医嘱，若有时间再澄清疑问。"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe verbal/telephone order practice requires writing down the complete order, reading it back (read-back) and receiving confirmation, clarifying anything unclear (including drug spelling), and documenting the order with date, time, provider name, and that it was read back. The provider must co-sign within the facility's required time frame. Read-back/verification before carrying out the order is a Joint Commission patient-safety expectation; carrying out an order before clarifying concerns is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全的口头/电话医嘱处理要求：完整记录医嘱、复述（read-back）并获得确认、澄清任何不清楚之处（包括药名拼写），并记录医嘱及日期、时间、医生姓名和已复述确认。医生必须在机构规定时限内补签。在执行前复述/核实是联合委员会的患者安全要求；在澄清疑问前就执行医嘱并不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Write it, read it back, clarify, document, and get the co-signature. Never act on an unclear order.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记录、复述、澄清、记录在案、获取补签。绝不在医嘱不清时贸然执行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":179,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_impaired_colleague_sata_b11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.93","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.93.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.93.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[182,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,56],"fullStemEn":"A nurse notices that a coworker has slurred speech, smells of alcohol, and has several unexplained discrepancies in controlled-substance counts. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一名同事言语含糊、身上有酒味，且管制药品清点存在多处无法解释的差异。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"b","en":"Report the concern to the charge nurse or supervisor promptly.","zh":"及时将该顾虑报告给责任护士或主管。"},{"id":"e","en":"Say nothing to avoid getting a colleague in trouble.","zh":"保持沉默，以免给同事惹麻烦。"},{"id":"a","en":"Ensure clients assigned to the coworker are currently safe.","zh":"确保该同事所负责的患者目前安全。"},{"id":"d","en":"Document the objective observations factually.","zh":"客观、如实记录所观察到的情况。"},{"id":"c","en":"Follow facility policy for suspected impairment and controlled-substance discrepancies.","zh":"遵循机构关于疑似受损执业和管制药品差异的政策。"},{"id":"f","en":"Confront the coworker alone and let them drive themselves home.","zh":"独自质问该同事，并让其自行开车回家。"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Client safety comes first: ensure the coworker's clients are safe, then report the concern promptly to the charge nurse/supervisor, follow facility policy for suspected impairment and controlled-substance discrepancies, and document objective observations factually. Nurses have an ethical and often legal duty to report impaired or unsafe practice (ANA Code of Ethics; state reporting requirements) — staying silent endangers clients. The nurse should not handle it alone or let a possibly impaired colleague drive; the situation is managed through the chain of command and policy, which also connects the colleague to help.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者安全第一：先确保该同事的患者安全，然后及时向责任护士/主管报告顾虑，遵循机构关于疑似受损执业和管制药品差异的政策，并客观如实记录所观察到的情况。护士有伦理乃至法律上的义务报告受损或不安全的执业（ANA 伦理守则；各州上报要求）——保持沉默会危及患者。护士不应独自处理，也不应让可能受损的同事开车；应通过指挥链和政策处理，这也能让该同事获得帮助。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Protect clients first, then report up the chain and follow policy. Reporting impaired practice is a duty, not optional — and not a solo confrontation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先保护患者，再沿指挥链上报并遵循政策。报告受损执业是义务而非可选——也不是单独质问。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":180,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_chain_command_order_b12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.94","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.94.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.94.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,34],"fullStemEn":"A nurse believes a newly written order is unsafe for the client. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士认为一条新开具的医嘱对患者不安全。请将护士的措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse believes a newly written order is unsafe for the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士认为一条新开具的医嘱对患者不安全。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"e","en":"Document the concern, the people notified, and the actions taken.","zh":"记录该顾虑、已通知的人员以及所采取的措施。"},{"id":"c","en":"If still unresolved, escalate further up the chain (e.g., nursing administration/medical director).","zh":"若仍未解决，沿指挥链进一步上报（如护理管理层/医务主任）。"},{"id":"a","en":"Hold implementation of the order and contact the prescribing provider to clarify the concern.","zh":"暂缓执行该医嘱，并联系开具医嘱的医生以澄清疑虑."},{"id":"d","en":"Do not carry out an order that remains unsafe.","zh":"不执行仍然不安全的医嘱。"},{"id":"b","en":"If unresolved, notify the charge nurse and nursing supervisor.","zh":"若仍未解决，通知责任护士和护理主管。"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When an order appears unsafe, the nurse first holds its implementation and contacts the prescriber to clarify — most concerns resolve here. If it is not resolved, the nurse moves up the chain of command: charge nurse and nursing supervisor, then further (nursing administration/medical director) as needed. A nurse must never carry out an order they believe is unsafe — doing so does not relieve the nurse of accountability. Throughout, the nurse documents the concern, who was notified, and the actions taken. Patient safety, not hierarchy, drives the process.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当医嘱看似不安全时，护士首先暂缓执行并联系开嘱医生澄清——多数疑虑在此解决。若未解决，护士沿指挥链上报：责任护士和护理主管，必要时再向上（护理管理层/医务主任）。护士绝不能执行其认为不安全的医嘱——执行并不能免除护士的责任。整个过程中，护士记录该顾虑、通知了谁以及所采取的措施。驱动该流程的是患者安全，而非层级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Clarify with the prescriber, then climb the chain, never carry out an unsafe order, and document throughout.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先与开嘱医生澄清，再沿指挥链上报，绝不执行不安全医嘱，并全程记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":181,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_discharge_process_order_b13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.95","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.95.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.95.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[45,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,31],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for discharge. Place the steps for a safe discharge in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患者办理出院。请将安全出院的步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps for a safe discharge in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将安全出院的步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for discharge.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患者办理出院。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Verify the provider's written discharge order.","zh":"核实医生书面出院医嘱。"},{"id":"b","en":"Complete medication reconciliation and discharge teaching with teach-back.","zh":"完成用药核对，并通过回授进行出院教学。"},{"id":"e","en":"Document the discharge and the client's condition, then escort the client out with belongings.","zh":"记录出院情况及患者状况，然后陪同患者携个人物品离开。"},{"id":"d","en":"Provide written instructions and prescriptions the client understands.","zh":"提供患者能理解的书面说明和处方。"},{"id":"c","en":"Confirm follow-up appointments, transportation, and any home-care referrals.","zh":"确认随访预约、交通安排以及任何居家护理转介。"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A safe discharge begins with verifying the provider's written discharge order — the client cannot be discharged without it. Next the nurse completes medication reconciliation and discharge teaching with teach-back to confirm understanding, then confirms follow-up appointments, transportation, and home-care referrals so the transition is supported. The client is given written instructions and prescriptions they understand, and finally the nurse documents the discharge and the client's condition and escorts the client out with their belongings. Confirming the order and ensuring understanding precede the physical departure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全出院首先要核实医生书面出院医嘱——没有它就不能让患者出院。接着护士完成用药核对，并通过回授进行出院教学以确认理解，然后确认随访预约、交通安排和居家护理转介，使过渡得到支持。向患者提供其能理解的书面说明和处方，最后护士记录出院情况及患者状况，并陪同患者携个人物品离开。先确认医嘱并确保理解，再让患者实际离开。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Order first, then teach and reconcile, confirm follow-up, give written materials, document, and escort out last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先有医嘱，再教学和核对，确认随访，提供书面材料，记录，最后陪同离开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":182,"bankPath":"banks/claude-canonical.json","bankSha256":"b59035ecb717fd279fb9278e3ae678c1b420a6a896b9bf6ff638614f6233b5ce","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_moc_priority_mc_b14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.96","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.96.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.96.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[41,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[9,21],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is responsible for four clients. Which client should the nurse assess first?","fullStemZh":"护士负责四名患者。护士应首先评估哪名患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the nurse assess first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先评估哪名患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is responsible for four clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士负责四名患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"b","en":"A client requesting pain medication for chronic, stable back pain.","zh":"一名因慢性稳定性背痛请求止痛药的患者。"},{"id":"a","en":"A client with new shortness of breath and an oxygen saturation of 88%.","zh":"一名新发气短、血氧饱和度88%的患者。"},{"id":"d","en":"A client who wants to review discharge instructions before leaving tomorrow.","zh":"一名希望在明天离院前复习出院说明的患者。"},{"id":"c","en":"A client asking for help ordering a meal tray.","zh":"一名请求协助点餐的患者。"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the ABC framework, the client with new shortness of breath and an oxygen saturation of 88% has a breathing problem and must be assessed first — a low oxygen saturation is a threat to oxygenation that can deteriorate quickly. Requesting medication for chronic stable pain, help ordering a meal, and reviewing discharge instructions for a departure tomorrow are all important but lower priority and can be addressed after the client with the airway/breathing concern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"依据 ABC 框架，新发气短、血氧88%的患者存在呼吸问题，必须最先评估——低血氧是对氧合的威胁，可能迅速恶化。慢性稳定性疼痛的止痛请求、协助点餐、以及为明天离院复习出院说明都重要但优先级较低，可在处理完有气道/呼吸问题的患者后再处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply ABCs: a breathing problem with low oxygen saturation outranks pain, meals, and tomorrow's discharge.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用 ABC：低血氧的呼吸问题优先于疼痛、餐食和明天的出院。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":183,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_pca_basal_opioid_naive_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,58],"fullStemEn":"An opioid-naïve adult is prescribed morphine patient-controlled analgesia after surgery. The nurse reviews the pump screen before initiating therapy. Which setting should the nurse question first?","fullStemZh":"一名未曾使用过阿片类药物的成年人术后被医嘱使用吗啡患者自控镇痛。护士在开始治疗前查看泵屏幕。护士首先应质疑哪项设置？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which setting should the nurse question first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应质疑哪项设置？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the pump screen before initiating therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在开始治疗前查看泵屏幕。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The 1 mg patient demand dose","zh":"1 mg患者需求剂量"},{"id":"A","en":"The continuous basal infusion","zh":"持续基础输注"},{"id":"D","en":"The displayed drug concentration","zh":"显示的药物浓度"},{"id":"B","en":"The 10-minute lockout interval","zh":"10分钟锁定间隔"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The screen shows PCA+basal mode with a continuous basal opioid infusion. A basal opioid infusion in an opioid-naïve client can deliver opioid when the client is asleep or not requesting medication, increasing the risk for oversedation and respiratory depression. The nurse should question this setting before starting the pump.","rationaleCorrectZh":"屏幕显示PCA+基础输注模式，并设置了持续基础阿片类输注。对未曾使用过阿片类药物的患者，基础输注可能在患者睡眠或未主动请求用药时继续给药，增加过度镇静和呼吸抑制风险。护士应在启动泵前质疑该设置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For PCA questions, first ask whether the client is opioid-naïve. Continuous basal opioid delivery is the high-risk cue.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到PCA题目时，先判断患者是否未曾使用过阿片类药物。持续基础阿片类给药是高风险线索。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ PSNet and ISMP PCA safety guidance; institutional PCA policy","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":184,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_pca_lockout_max_demands_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[238,260],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,75],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is verifying how many patient demand doses could be delivered in 1 hour if the client presses the PCA button whenever it is available. Using the pump screen shown, calculate the maximum number of delivered demand doses in 1 hour. Record a whole number.","fullStemZh":"护士正在核对如果患者每次PCA按键可用时都按键，1小时内最多可给予多少次患者需求剂量。根据所示泵屏幕，计算1小时内最多可给予的需求剂量次数。记录整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the pump screen shown, calculate the maximum number of delivered demand doses in 1 hour.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示泵屏幕，计算1小时内最多可给予的需求剂量次数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"maximum delivered demand doses in 1 hour","zh":"1小时内最多给予的需求剂量次数"},"acceptable":["7"],"numeric":{"value":7,"unit":"doses","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The lockout interval is 8 minutes. Maximum delivered demand doses in 1 hour = floor(60 ÷ 8) = floor(7.5) = 7 doses. The partial interval does not allow another full dose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锁定间隔为8分钟。1小时内最多给予的需求剂量次数 = floor(60 ÷ 8) = floor(7.5) = 7次。不完整的间隔不能再给予一次完整剂量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a lockout calculation, divide 60 minutes by the lockout time and round down because a partial lockout period cannot deliver a dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算锁定间隔题时，用60分钟除以锁定时间并向下取整，因为不完整的锁定时段不能给药。","sourceMetadata":"PCA pump programming math: complete lockout intervals per hour","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":185,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_pca_max_dose_basal_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[231,271],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,73],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is checking the maximum hydromorphone dose that could be delivered in 1 hour if the client presses the PCA button whenever it is available. Using the pump screen shown, calculate the maximum milligrams delivered in 1 hour. Record your answer to the nearest tenth.","fullStemZh":"护士正在核对如果患者每次PCA按键可用时都按键，1小时内最多可能给予多少氢吗啡酮。根据所示泵屏幕，计算1小时内最多给予的毫克数。答案保留到十分位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record your answer to the nearest tenth.","terminalSentenceZh":"答案保留到十分位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the pump screen shown, calculate the maximum milligrams delivered in 1 hour.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示泵屏幕，计算1小时内最多给予的毫克数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mg in 1 hour","zh":"1小时内毫克数"},"acceptable":["1.4","1.4 mg"],"numeric":{"value":1.4,"unit":"mg","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The lockout is 10 minutes, so at most floor(60 ÷ 10) = 6 demand doses can be delivered in 1 hour. Six 0.2 mg doses = 1.2 mg. Because the screen shows PCA+basal mode, add the basal 0.2 mg/hr: 1.2 + 0.2 = 1.4 mg in 1 hour.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锁定间隔为10分钟，因此1小时内最多可给予 floor(60 ÷ 10) = 6次需求剂量。6次 × 0.2 mg = 1.2 mg。由于屏幕显示PCA+基础输注模式，还要加上0.2 mg/hr的基础输注：1.2 + 0.2 = 1.4 mg。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Check the PCA mode before doing the math. Basal opioid dose is included only when the screen shows basal mode.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算前先查看PCA模式。只有屏幕显示基础输注模式时，才计入基础阿片类剂量。","sourceMetadata":"PCA pump programming math; AHRQ PSNet PCA safety overview","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":186,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_pca_delivered_total_no_basal_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[238,278],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,70],"fullStemEn":"At the end of a postoperative assessment period, the nurse documents how much hydromorphone the client received from delivered PCA demand doses. Using the pump screen shown, calculate the total delivered demand-dose amount in milligrams. Record your answer to the nearest tenth.","fullStemZh":"在术后评估时段结束时，护士记录患者通过PCA需求剂量实际获得了多少氢吗啡酮。根据所示泵屏幕，计算已给予需求剂量的总毫克数。答案保留到十分位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record your answer to the nearest tenth.","terminalSentenceZh":"答案保留到十分位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the pump screen shown, calculate the total delivered demand-dose amount in milligrams.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示泵屏幕，计算已给予需求剂量的总毫克数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"total delivered demand-dose amount","zh":"已给予需求剂量总量"},"acceptable":["1.8","1.8 mg"],"numeric":{"value":1.8,"unit":"mg","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The screen shows PCA only mode, so there is no basal dose to add. Delivered demand doses = 9, and each demand dose is 0.2 mg. Total delivered amount = 9 × 0.2 = 1.8 mg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"屏幕显示仅PCA模式，因此没有基础剂量需要相加。已给予需求剂量为9次，每次0.2 mg。总已给剂量 = 9 × 0.2 = 1.8 mg。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish attempts from delivered doses. Dose received is based on delivered doses, not every button press.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分尝试次数和已给予次数。患者实际获得的剂量按已给予次数计算，而不是每次按键都计算。","sourceMetadata":"PCA pump dose-history documentation math","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":187,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_pca_delivered_total_basal_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,210],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,55],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reconciling the morphine administered during a 4-hour postoperative period. Using the PCA screen shown, calculate the total morphine delivered during the 4 hours in milligrams. Record a whole number.","fullStemZh":"护士正在核对术后4小时时段内给予的吗啡总量。根据所示PCA屏幕，计算4小时内实际给予的吗啡总毫克数。记录整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the PCA screen shown, calculate the total morphine delivered during the 4 hours in milligrams.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示PCA屏幕，计算4小时内实际给予的吗啡总毫克数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"total morphine delivered in 4 hours","zh":"4小时内给予的吗啡总量"},"acceptable":["7","7 mg"],"numeric":{"value":7,"unit":"mg","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The screen shows PCA+basal mode. Delivered demand doses = 5 doses × 1 mg = 5 mg. Basal infusion = 0.5 mg/hr × 4 hours = 2 mg. Total morphine delivered = 5 + 2 = 7 mg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"屏幕显示PCA+基础输注模式。已给予需求剂量 = 5次 × 1 mg = 5 mg。基础输注 = 0.5 mg/hr × 4小时 = 2 mg。总吗啡剂量 = 5 + 2 = 7 mg。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a PCA screen includes basal mode, total delivered dose equals demand-dose delivery plus basal dose over time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当PCA屏幕包含基础输注模式时，总给药量等于需求剂量给药量加上该时段内的基础输注量。","sourceMetadata":"PCA pump dose-history documentation math","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":188,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_infusion_duration_vtbi_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[209,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,57],"fullStemEn":"A nurse checks an IV infusion pump while planning the next assessment. Using the screen shown, calculate how many minutes remain until the programmed volume to be infused is complete if the rate is unchanged. Record a whole number.","fullStemZh":"护士在计划下一次评估时查看静脉输液泵。根据所示屏幕，如果速率不变，计算距离设定待输注量完成还剩多少分钟。记录整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the screen shown, calculate how many minutes remain until the programmed volume to be infused is complete if the rate is unchanged.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示屏幕，如果速率不变，计算距离设定待输注量完成还剩多少分钟。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minutes remaining","zh":"剩余分钟数"},"acceptable":["120","120 min"],"numeric":{"value":120,"unit":"min","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pump shows VTBI 250 mL and rate 125 mL/hr. Time = VTBI ÷ rate × 60 = 250 ÷ 125 × 60 = 120 minutes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"泵显示待输注量250 mL，速率125 mL/hr。时间 = 待输注量 ÷ 速率 × 60 = 250 ÷ 125 × 60 = 120分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pump time, divide volume by mL/hr to get hours, then multiply by 60 for minutes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算泵剩余时间时，用体积除以mL/hr得到小时，再乘以60得到分钟。","sourceMetadata":"Infusion pump volume-rate-time calculation","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":189,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_enteral_volume_shift_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[279,301],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,77],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving continuous enteral feeding. The nurse reviews the pump screen at the start of an 8-hour shift and calculates the volume expected to infuse during the shift if the settings are unchanged. Using the screen shown, calculate the expected volume in milliliters. Record a whole number.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受连续肠内营养。护士在8小时班次开始时查看泵屏幕，并计算如果设置不变，本班次预计输注的体积。根据所示屏幕，计算预计输注量（毫升）。记录整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the screen shown, calculate the expected volume in milliliters.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示屏幕，计算预计输注量（毫升）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"expected volume during 8 hours","zh":"8小时预计输注量"},"acceptable":["600","600 mL"],"numeric":{"value":600,"unit":"mL","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The enteral pump rate is 75 mL/hr. Over 8 hours, volume = 75 × 8 = 600 mL. This is the same as 75 × 480 ÷ 60 = 600 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肠内营养泵速率为75 mL/hr。8小时内输注量 = 75 × 8 = 600 mL。也可计算为75 × 480 ÷ 60 = 600 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For expected volume, multiply the mL/hr rate by the number of hours the pump will run.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算预计输注量时，用mL/hr速率乘以泵运行的小时数。","sourceMetadata":"Enteral pump volume-rate-time calculation","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":190,"bankPath":"banks/device-canonical.json","bankSha256":"83d5a6ac7219524f4c528265291cbee2ed5b2f17c13fbeb3649342bae2e4aac5","topLevelQuestionId":"dev_high_alert_kcl_pump_mismatch_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[210,232],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,73],"fullStemEn":"A provider prescribes potassium chloride 10 mEq in 100 mL IVPB to infuse over 1 hour. Before starting the infusion, the nurse compares the order with the pump screen shown. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为氯化钾10 mEq加入100 mL静脉小壶输注，1小时输完。开始输注前，护士将医嘱与所示泵屏幕进行比较。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Ignore the pump display if the medication label matches the order.","zh":"如果药物标签与医嘱一致，就忽略泵屏幕显示。"},{"id":"D","en":"Leave the rate unchanged because the VTBI is 100 mL.","zh":"因为待输注量是100 mL，所以保持当前速率不变。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain the required independent double-check for the high-alert electrolyte infusion according to policy.","zh":"按机构政策对高警讯电解质输注进行所需的独立双人核对。"},{"id":"B","en":"Reprogram the pump so the 100 mL infusion runs over 1 hour per the order and policy.","zh":"重新设置泵，使100 mL按医嘱和机构政策在1小时内输完。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer the potassium chloride IV push if the infusion pump cannot be corrected promptly.","zh":"如果输液泵不能及时纠正，则将氯化钾静脉推注。"},{"id":"A","en":"Do not start the infusion with the pump programmed as shown.","zh":"不要按屏幕所示设置启动输注。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The order is 100 mL over 1 hour, but the pump screen is programmed at 200 mL/hr with a 30-minute duration. The nurse should not start the infusion as shown, should reprogram the pump to match the order and policy, and should complete the required independent double-check for a high-alert electrolyte infusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"医嘱为100 mL在1小时内输完，但泵屏幕设置为200 mL/hr，持续30分钟。护士不应按当前设置启动输注，应按医嘱和机构政策重新设置泵，并对高警讯电解质输注完成所需的独立双人核对。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-alert infusions, compare the order, medication, and pump screen. A correct bag does not make an incorrect pump setting safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到高警讯输注时，要比较医嘱、药物和泵屏幕。药袋正确并不代表错误泵设置是安全的。","sourceMetadata":"ISMP high-alert medication guidance; institutional potassium infusion policy","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":191,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_advance_directives_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[324,370],"terminalOffsetsZh":[96,109],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for an older adult client who is terminally ill. The client has a signed living will stating that no life-sustaining measures, including cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR), should be performed. The client's adult children arrive and insist that the medical team perform CPR if the client's heart stops. Which action by the nurse is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名处于绝症晚期的老年患者。患者签署了一份生前遗嘱，声明不应进行包括心肺复苏（CPR）在内的任何生命支持措施。患者的成年子女到来并坚持要求医疗团队在患者心脏停止跳动时进行 CPR。护士采取的哪项行动最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士采取的哪项行动最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's adult children arrive and insist that the medical team perform CPR if the client's heart stops.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的成年子女到来并坚持要求医疗团队在患者心脏停止跳动时进行 CPR。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Advise the family to contact an attorney to override the living will.","zh":"建议家属联系律师以推翻生前遗嘱。"},{"id":"D","en":"Inform the medical provider to update the code status to full code.","zh":"通知医疗服务提供者将抢救状态更新为全心肺复苏（Full Code）。"},{"id":"A","en":"Explain to the family that the client's living will must be honored.","zh":"向家属解释必须尊重患者的生前遗嘱。"},{"id":"C","en":"Reassure the family that CPR will be performed to honor their wishes.","zh":"向家属保证将进行 CPR 以尊重他们的意愿。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A living will is a legally binding advance directive that reflects the autonomous wishes of a competent client. The nurse and healthcare team must honor the client's documented preferences, which take precedence over the wishes of the family members.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生前遗嘱是一份具有法律约束力的预立医疗指示，反映了有认知能力的患者的自主意愿。护士和医疗团队必须尊重患者书面记录的偏好，这些偏好优先于家属的意愿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the client's autonomy and legal rights. Advance directives reflect the client's wishes and take precedence over the preferences of family members.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注患者的自主权和法律权利。预立医疗指示反映了患者的意愿，并优先于家属的偏好。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":192,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_cane_ambulation_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,47],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to ambulate a client who has left-sided weakness following a stroke. The client will be using a single-point cane. Which instruction should the nurse provide to the client?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备协助一名脑卒中后左侧偏瘫的患者下床活动。患者将使用单点手杖。护士应该给患者哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse provide to the client?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该给患者哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client will be using a single-point cane.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者将使用单点手杖。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hold the cane in your left hand and advance it with your right leg.","zh":"左手握杖，并与右腿一起向前迈出。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the cane in your left hand and advance it with your left leg.","zh":"左手握杖，并与左腿一起向前迈出。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold the cane in your right hand and advance it with your right leg.","zh":"右手握杖，并与右腿一起向前迈出。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the cane in your right hand and advance it with your left leg.","zh":"右手握杖，并与左腿一起向前迈出。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A cane should be held on the stronger (unaffected) side of the body to provide support and balance. In this case, the client has left-sided weakness, so the cane must be held in the right hand. The cane is then advanced simultaneously or slightly before the weaker leg (left leg) to distribute weight and maintain stability.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手杖应握在身体较强健（未受影响）的一侧，以提供支持和平衡。在这种情况下，患者左侧偏瘫，因此手杖必须握在右手。手杖应与较弱的腿（左腿）同时或在其稍前迈出，以分担体重并保持稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the mnemonic 'COAL' (Cane Opposite Affected Leg) to remember which hand holds the cane. The cane always moves with the weaker leg to share the load.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用助记词“COAL”（Cane Opposite Affected Leg，手杖在受累腿的对侧）来记住哪只手握杖。手杖总是与较弱的腿一起移动以分担负荷。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":193,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_airborne_precautions_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[200,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,57],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assigned to care for a client who is admitted to the medical-surgical unit with suspected active pulmonary tuberculosis (TB). Which infection control measures should the nurse implement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士被分配护理一名因疑似活动性肺结核（TB）入院入住内外科病房的患者。护士应实施哪些感染控制措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which infection control measures should the nurse implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪些感染控制措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Wear a fitted N95 respirator when entering the client's room.","zh":"进入患者病房时佩戴贴合的 N95 口罩/呼吸器。"},{"id":"D","en":"Wear a clean gown and gloves for all interactions, regardless of body fluid exposure.","zh":"在所有互动中穿清洁隔离衣并戴手套，无论是否接触体液。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure the client wears a surgical mask when leaving the room for diagnostic tests.","zh":"确保患者在离开病房进行诊断检查时佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep the client's room door closed at all times.","zh":"始终保持患者病房门关闭。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a negative-pressure airflow room.","zh":"将患者安置在负压气流病房中。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Active pulmonary tuberculosis requires airborne precautions. This includes placing the client in a private room with negative-pressure airflow, keeping the door closed to prevent the spread of droplet nuclei, wearing an N95 respirator for healthcare workers, and having the client wear a surgical mask if transport outside the room is necessary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"活动性肺结核需要实施空气传播预防措施。这包括将患者安置在带负压气流的单人病房中，保持房门关闭以防止微粒传播，医护人员佩戴 N95 呼吸器，以及在必须移出病房时让患者佩戴外科口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate pulmonary tuberculosis with Airborne precautions. Remember the specific requirements: negative pressure room, N95 respirator for healthcare workers, and a surgical mask for the client if they must leave the room.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将肺结核与空气传播预防（Airborne precautions）联系起来。记住具体要求：负压病房、医务人员佩戴 N95 呼吸器、患者必须离开病房时佩戴外科口罩。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":194,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_alcohol_withdrawal_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[275,297],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,73],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the detoxification unit with a history of chronic heavy alcohol consumption. The nurse is monitoring the client for signs of alcohol withdrawal delirium (delirium tremens). Which clinical manifestations should the nurse associate with this condition? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名有慢性重度饮酒史的患者入住解毒病房。护士正在监测患者是否出现酒精戒断性谵妄（震颤谵妄）。护士应将哪些临床表现与该病症联系起来？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse associate with this condition?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些临床表现与该病症联系起来？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Fever and agitation","zh":"发热和烦躁不安"},{"id":"D","en":"Tachypnea and diaphoresis","zh":"呼吸急促和大汗"},{"id":"A","en":"Visual hallucinations","zh":"视幻觉"},{"id":"C","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"B","en":"Extreme tremors","zh":"极度震颤"},{"id":"E","en":"Hypotension","zh":"低血压"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Alcohol withdrawal delirium (delirium tremens) is a medical emergency that typically occurs 48 to 96 hours after the cessation of alcohol. It is characterized by severe autonomic hyperactivity (tachycardia, tachypnea, diaphoresis, hypertension, fever), severe tremors, vivid hallucinations (usually visual or tactile), disorientation, and extreme agitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"酒精戒断性谵妄（震颤谵妄）是一种医疗紧急情况，通常在停止饮酒后 48 至 96 小时内发生。其特点是严重的自主神经亢进（心动过速、呼吸急促、大汗、高血压、发热）、严重震颤、生动的幻觉（通常是视幻觉或触幻觉）、定向力障碍和极度烦躁不安。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that alcohol is a central nervous system (CNS) depressant. When it is suddenly withdrawn, the CNS and sympathetic nervous system become hyperactive ('wired' state: tachycardia, hypertension, diaphoresis, tremors, hallucinations).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住酒精是一种中枢神经系统（CNS）抑制剂。当突然撤除时，CNS和交感神经系统会变得过度活跃（呈现“兴奋”状态：心动过速、高血压、大汗、震颤、幻觉）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse associate with this condition?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些临床表现与该病症联系起来？"}
{"queueIndex":195,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_transfusion_reaction_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[194,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,65],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is administering a unit of packed red blood cells (PRBCs) to a client. Fifteen minutes after the transfusion begins, the client reports chills, low back pain, and shortness of breath. Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在给一名患者输注红细胞悬液（PRBCs）。输血开始 15 分钟后，患者自诉畏寒、腰痛和气促。请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Fifteen minutes after the transfusion begins, the client reports chills, low back pain, and shortness of breath.","penultimateSentenceZh":"输血开始 15 分钟后，患者自诉畏寒、腰痛和气促。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Stop the transfusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止输血。"},{"id":"A","en":"Disconnect the blood tubing and infuse normal saline through new IV tubing to maintain IV patency.","zh":"断开输血皮条，并通过新的输液器输注生理盐水以保持静脉通畅。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and the blood bank.","zh":"通知医疗服务提供者和血库。"},{"id":"D","en":"Return the blood bag, tubing, and a completed reaction report form to the blood bank.","zh":"将血袋、输血器以及填写完整的输血反应报告单送回血库。"}],"correct":["C","A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate priority when a blood transfusion reaction is suspected is to stop the transfusion to prevent further exposure to the incompatible blood. Next, the nurse should disconnect the blood tubing and hang new tubing with normal saline to maintain venous access without infusing remaining blood from the tubing. The healthcare provider and blood bank should then be notified to obtain orders for treatment and laboratory evaluation. Finally, the blood container, tubing, and paperwork are returned for laboratory analysis to identify the cause of the reaction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当怀疑发生输血反应时，首要任务是立即停止输血（C），以防止进一步接触不相容的血液。接下来，护士应断开输血管路并用新的输液管路挂生理盐水（A），以维持静脉通道，同时不输入管路中残留的血液。然后应通知医疗服务提供者和血库（B），以获取治疗和实验室评估医嘱。最后，将血袋、输液管路和文件送回（D）进行实验室分析，以确定输血反应的原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In any transfusion reaction, the primary goal is patient safety. Stop the offending agent first. Never flush the line containing the blood; disconnect it and use new tubing for saline.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在任何输血反应中，首要目标是患者安全。首先停止致敏源。切勿冲洗含有残留血液的管路；应断开它，并使用新的输液管路输注生理盐水。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":196,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_fib_aminoglycoside_calc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[281,322],"terminalOffsetsZh":[93,106],"fullStemEn":"The healthcare provider prescribes gentamicin 2 mg/kg IV every 8 hours for a pediatric client who weighs 44 lbs. The medication is available in a vial concentration of 20 mg/mL. How many mL of gentamicin should the nurse administer per dose? (Record your answer as a whole number. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"医疗服务提供者为一名体重为 44 磅的儿童患者开具了每 8 小时静脉注射 2 mg/kg 庆大霉素的医嘱。该药物的瓶装浓度为 20 mg/mL。护士每次应给药多少毫升？（以整数记录答案。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以整数记录答案。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["2"],"numeric":{"value":2,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, convert the client's weight from pounds (lbs) to kilograms (kg): 44 lbs / 2.2 = 20 kg. Next, calculate the prescribed dosage: 20 kg * 2 mg/kg = 40 mg. Finally, calculate the volume to administer: 40 mg / 20 mg/mL = 2 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步，将患者的体重从磅（lbs）换算为千克（kg）：44 lbs / 2.2 = 20 kg。第二步，计算开具的剂量：20 kg * 2 mg/kg = 40 mg。第三步，计算要给药的体积：40 mg / 20 mg/mL = 2 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always check weight conversions first (1 kg = 2.2 lbs). Then calculate the total dose in mg, and finally use dimensional analysis or the formula (Desired/Have) * Quantity to find the volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先应进行体重换算（1 kg = 2.2 lbs）。然后计算以 mg 为单位的总剂量，最后使用因次分析法或公式（欲求量/已有量）* 数量来求出体积。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":197,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_asthma_exacerbation_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,349],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,92],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the emergency department with a severe asthma exacerbation. The nurse administers nebulized albuterol and intravenous methylprednisolone as prescribed. The nurse performs a reassessment. For each clinical finding, click to specify if the finding indicates that the client's condition is improving or deteriorating/unimproved.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因严重哮喘发作被送往急诊科。护士按照医嘱给予雾化沙丁胺醇和静脉注射甲基泼尼松龙。护士进行重新评估。对于每个临床表现，点击以指定该表现是表明患者的病情有所改善还是恶化/未见好转。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, click to specify if the finding indicates that the client's condition is improving or deteriorating/unimproved.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个临床表现，点击以指定该表现是表明患者的病情有所改善还是恶化/未见好转。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse performs a reassessment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士进行重新评估。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Oxygen saturation increases from 88% to 94% on room air.","zh":"吸入空气时血氧饱和度从 88% 升至 94%。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Wheezing decreases and breath sounds are now diminished with minimal air movement.","zh":"喘鸣音减弱，且目前呼吸音减低，伴随极少的气体移动（静音胸）。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Use of intercostal muscles for breathing has resolved and respiratory rate is 18/min.","zh":"呼吸时使用肋间肌（辅助呼吸肌）的情况已消失，呼吸频率为 18 次/分。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client is unable to speak in full sentences and is sitting in a tripod position.","zh":"患者无法说出完整的句子，呈前倾端坐呼吸体位（三脚架体位）。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Deteriorating / Unimproved","zh":"恶化/未见好转"},{"id":"c1","en":"Improving","zh":"改善"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An increase in oxygen saturation (r1) and normalization of respiratory rate/effort (r3) indicate improvement. Diminished breath sounds with minimal air movement ('silent chest', r2) is a sign of impending respiratory failure and severe bronchoconstriction, indicating deterioration. Inability to speak in full sentences and tripoding (r4) are signs of severe respiratory distress and lack of improvement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血氧饱和度上升（r1）和呼吸频率/努力程度恢复正常（r3）表明病情有所改善。呼吸音减低且气体流动极少（“静音胸”，r2）是即将发生呼吸衰竭和严重支气管痉挛的迹象，表明病情恶化。无法说出完整句子和呈三脚架体位（r4）是严重呼吸困难且未见好转的迹象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between real improvement and signs of exhaustion. 'Diminished wheezing' can be a false sign of improvement if it is caused by reduced airflow (silent chest) rather than bronchodilation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分真正的改善和呼吸肌疲劳衰竭的表现。如果“喘鸣音减少”是由于气流减少（静音胸）而不是由于支气管扩张引起的，这可能是一个虚假的改善迹象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":198,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_cloze_breastfeeding_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,36],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a postpartum client who is breastfeeding her newborn. The client reports nipple soreness during feedings.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名进行母乳喂养的产后患者。该患者诉在喂养过程中有乳头酸痛。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client reports nipple soreness during feedings.","terminalSentenceZh":"该患者诉在喂养过程中有乳头酸痛。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is teaching a postpartum client who is breastfeeding her newborn.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在指导一名进行母乳喂养的产后患者。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To prevent nipple soreness, the nurse should teach the client that the infant's mouth should cover {{1}} and the infant's lips should be {{2}}.","zh":"为防止乳头酸痛，护士应指导患者，婴儿的嘴应覆盖 {{1}}，并且婴儿的嘴唇应 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the nipple and a large portion of the areola","zh":"乳头和大部分乳晕"},{"id":"o1","en":"only the tip of the nipple","zh":"仅乳头尖端"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"flanged outward (everted)","zh":"向外翻（外翻）"},{"id":"o1","en":"turned inward (inverted)","zh":"向内缩（内翻）"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Proper latch is the most critical factor in preventing nipple soreness. The infant's mouth should cover the nipple and a large portion of the areola (o2 for dropdown 1) to ensure the nipple is drawn deep into the mouth where it is protected from friction. The infant's lips should be flanged outward (o2 for dropdown 2), forming a wide seal against the breast.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的含接是预防乳头酸痛最关键的因素。婴儿的嘴应覆盖乳头和大部分乳晕（下拉菜单1的o2），以确保乳头被吸入嘴部深处，免受摩擦。婴儿的嘴唇应向外翻起（下拉菜单2的o2），与乳房形成宽阔的密封。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for options that promote a deep latch and minimize trauma to maternal breast tissue. Everted lips and taking in a large portion of the areola are indicators of a correct, comfortable breastfeeding position.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找能促进深部含接并尽量减少母体乳房组织损伤的选项。外翻的嘴唇和含入大部分乳晕是正确、舒适的母乳喂养姿势的指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":199,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_confidentiality_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.8","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.8.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.8.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[221,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,64],"fullStemEn":"A nurse receives a telephone call at the nursing station from an individual claiming to be the sibling of a newly admitted client. The caller asks for details about the client's current medical status and treatment plan. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士在护士站接到电话，来电者声称是新入院患者的兄弟。来电者询问有关患者当前医疗状况和治疗计划的详细信息。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The caller asks for details about the client's current medical status and treatment plan.","penultimateSentenceZh":"来电者询问有关患者当前医疗状况和治疗计划的详细信息。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Refer the caller to the healthcare provider for medical updates.","zh":"建议来电者联系医疗服务提供者获取最新医疗信息。"},{"id":"D","en":"Inform the caller that no information can be shared without the client's consent.","zh":"告知来电者，未经患者同意，不得分享任何信息。"},{"id":"B","en":"Provide the requested information after confirming the caller's sibling relationship.","zh":"在确认来电者的兄弟关系后，提供所请求的信息。"},{"id":"C","en":"Transfer the telephone call to the client's room so they can speak directly.","zh":"将电话转接至患者病房，以便他们直接通话。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Under HIPAA and professional nursing standards, a client's medical information is confidential. The nurse cannot confirm admission or share any health information with anyone, including family members, without the client's explicit consent or a verification code/password established by the facility and the client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据 HIPAA 和专业护理标准，患者的医疗信息是保密的。未经患者明确同意或出示医院和患者制定的验证码/密码，护士不能向任何人（包括家属）确认患者入院或分享任何健康信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always protect client confidentiality. Unless the client has explicitly authorized disclosure (e.g., using a disclosure code), do not share any details or confirm their hospital presence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终保护患者隐私。除非患者已明确授权披露（例如，使用披露代码），否则不要分享任何细节或确认其在院情况。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":200,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_compartment_syndrome_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.9","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.9.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.9.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[352,399],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,101],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the orthopedic unit with a severe lower extremity fracture and has a fiberglass cast applied. Two hours later, the client reports severe, progressive pain in the extremity that is not relieved by the prescribed intravenous morphine. The nurse notes that the pain is significantly worsened when the toes are passively stretched. Which action should the nurse take immediately?","fullStemZh":"一名下肢严重骨折的患者入住骨科病房，并敷贴了玻璃纤维石膏。两小时后，患者诉下肢出现严重的进行性疼痛，且静脉注射所开具的吗啡后未能缓解。护士注意到，当被动拉伸脚趾时，疼痛明显加剧。护士应立即采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take immediately?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应立即采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes that the pain is significantly worsened when the toes are passively stretched.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到，当被动拉伸脚趾时，疼痛明显加剧。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administer an additional dose of intravenous morphine.","zh":"再给予一次静脉注射吗啡。"},{"id":"D","en":"Contact the healthcare provider immediately.","zh":"立即联系医疗服务提供者。"},{"id":"A","en":"Apply an ice pack to the cast to reduce swelling.","zh":"在石膏上放置冰袋以减轻肿胀。"},{"id":"B","en":"Elevate the extremity above the level of the heart.","zh":"将下肢抬高至心脏水平以上。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is exhibiting signs of compartment syndrome (severe pain unrelieved by narcotics, pain with passive stretch), which is a surgical emergency. The nurse must immediately notify the provider because a fasciotomy may be required to prevent permanent nerve and muscle damage or limb loss.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表现出骨筋膜室综合征的症状（麻醉性镇痛药无法缓解的剧烈疼痛、被动拉伸时疼痛），这是一项外科急症。护士必须立即通知医疗服务提供者，因为可能需要进行骨筋膜室切开术，以防止永久性的神经和肌肉损伤或截肢。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the hallmark signs of compartment syndrome: pain out of proportion to the injury, pain with passive stretch, and lack of relief from opioids. Once suspected, prioritize immediate notification of the provider over comfort measures.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别骨筋膜室综合征的特征性体征：疼痛与损伤程度不成比例、被动拉伸时疼痛、以及阿片类药物无法缓解。一旦怀疑，应优先立即通知医疗服务提供者，而不是采取舒适护理措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":201,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_central_line_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.10","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.10.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.10.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[223,245],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,73],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with a triple-lumen central venous catheter (CVC) in the subclavian vein. Which interventions should the nurse implement to prevent central line-associated bloodstream infections (CLABSIs)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名锁骨下静脉留置三腔中心静脉导管（CVC）的患者。护士应实施哪些干预措施以预防导管相关性血流感染（CLABSIs）？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse implement to prevent central line-associated bloodstream infections (CLABSIs)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪些干预措施以预防导管相关性血流感染（CLABSIs）？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Apply an antibiotic ointment to the catheter insertion site with every dressing change.","zh":"每次更换敷料时在导管穿刺点处涂抹抗生素软膏。"},{"id":"E","en":"Regularly assess the necessity of the central line and advocate for its removal when no longer needed.","zh":"定期评估中心静脉导管的必要性，并在不再需要时提倡将其拔除。"},{"id":"B","en":"Perform hand hygiene before touching the catheter or performing a dressing change.","zh":"在接触导管或更换敷料前进行手部卫生。"},{"id":"C","en":"Change the transparent semipermeable membrane dressing every 7 days unless soiled.","zh":"除非被污染，否则每 7 天更换一次半透膜透明敷料。"},{"id":"A","en":"Scrub the catheter hub with an antiseptic swab for at least 15 seconds before accessing.","zh":"在接通导管接头前，使用消毒棉签擦拭接头至少 15 秒。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To prevent CLABSIs, the nurse should scrub the hub (antiseptic barrier scrubbing for 15 seconds), perform hand hygiene, change transparent dressings every 7 days (or immediately if loose or soiled), and evaluate the daily need for the catheter. Antibiotic ointment is NOT recommended at the insertion site because it can promote fungal infections and antimicrobial resistance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为了预防 CLABSIs，护士应擦拭接头（消毒屏障擦拭 15 秒）、进行手部卫生、每 7 天更换一次透明敷料（如果松动或污染则立即更换），并每日评估导管的必要性。不推荐在穿刺部位涂抹抗生素软膏，因为这会促进真菌感染和产生耐药性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on evidence-based CLABSI bundle practices: strict hand hygiene, scrubbing the hub, regular dressing changes, and removing unnecessary lines. Avoid options containing antibiotics on insertion sites unless specifically impregnated in standard dressings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注基于证据的 CLABSI 组合防控措施：严格的手部卫生、擦拭接头、定期更换敷料以及拔除不必要的导管。避免选择穿刺点涂抹抗生素的选项，除非是在标准的专用敷料中预浸防感染成分。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":202,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_cdiff_precautions_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.11","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.11.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.11.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[212,234],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,68],"fullStemEn":"During a facility C. difficile outbreak, the nurse is preparing to care for a client with confirmed C. difficile infection and active watery diarrhea. Which infection control measures should the nurse implement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在医疗机构发生艰难梭菌暴发期间，护士正准备护理一名确诊艰难梭菌感染并伴有活动性水样泻的患者。护士应实施哪些感染控制措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which infection control measures should the nurse implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪些感染控制措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Clean dedicated medical equipment with a facility-approved sporicidal disinfectant.","zh":"使用医疗机构批准的杀芽孢消毒剂清洁专用医疗设备。"},{"id":"D","en":"Wash hands with soap and water after removing gloves.","zh":"脱下手套后用肥皂和水洗手。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a private room with contact precautions.","zh":"将患者安置在单人病房中并实施接触隔离措施。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wear a mask and eye protection when entering the client's room.","zh":"进入患者病房时佩戴口罩和眼部防护装置。"},{"id":"C","en":"Perform hand hygiene using alcohol-based hand sanitizer after direct client contact.","zh":"直接接触患者后，使用含酒精的手部消毒剂进行手部卫生。"}],"correct":["A","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. difficile requires Contact precautions, including appropriate placement, gown, and gloves. Perform hand hygiene according to facility policy; soap and water is preferred when hands are visibly soiled and during high endemic rates or outbreaks because alcohol lacks sporicidal activity. Use a facility-approved sporicidal disinfectant for equipment and environmental surfaces. Masks are used when Standard Precautions indicate splash risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艰难梭菌感染需要接触传播预防措施，包括适当安置、隔离衣和手套。应按医疗机构政策进行手部卫生；当手部明显污染以及艰难梭菌高流行或暴发期间，因酒精不具杀芽孢活性而首选肥皂和水。设备和环境表面应使用医疗机构批准的杀芽孢消毒剂。存在喷溅风险时按标准预防措施使用口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For C. difficile, prioritize gloves, careful removal, facility-directed hand hygiene, and sporicidal environmental cleaning; soap and water is preferred in outbreak/high-endemic settings and when hands are visibly soiled.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于艰难梭菌，应优先重视手套、谨慎脱除、按医疗机构要求进行手部卫生以及杀芽孢环境清洁；暴发或高流行期间及手部明显污染时首选肥皂和水。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":203,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_chest_tube_disconnection_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.12","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.12.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.12.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[202,260],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,70],"fullStemEn":"A client with a left pneumothorax has a chest tube connected to a closed water-seal drainage system. While turning the client, the chest tube accidentally becomes disconnected from the drainage tubing. Place the nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"一名左侧气胸患者留置有连接在密闭式水封瓶引流系统上的胸腔引流管。在协助患者翻身时，胸腔引流管意外与引流管路脱开。请按正确的顺序排列护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"While turning the client, the chest tube accidentally becomes disconnected from the drainage tubing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在协助患者翻身时，胸腔引流管意外与引流管路脱开。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Immerse the distal end of the chest tube in a bottle of sterile water.","zh":"将胸腔引流管的远端浸入一瓶无菌生理盐水/无菌水中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Obtain and set up a new sterile chest drainage system.","zh":"获取并组装一套新的无菌胸腔引流系统。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's breath sounds and respiratory effort.","zh":"评估患者的呼吸音和呼吸努力程度。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider of the event.","zh":"将该事件通知医疗服务提供者。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate priority when a chest tube disconnects from its system is to submerge the distal end in 2 cm of sterile water. This acts as a temporary water seal and prevents air from rushing back into the pleural space, causing a tension pneumothorax. Next, the nurse should immediately assess the client's respiratory status. Following assessment, the provider should be notified, and finally, a new sterile drainage system should be prepared and connected.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当胸腔引流管与系统断开时，首要任务是立即将引流管的远端浸入 2 厘米深的无菌水中（A）。这起到临时水封的作用，可防止空气涌回胸膜腔，引发张力性气胸。接下来，护士应立即评估患者的呼吸状况（B）。评估后，应通知医生（C），最后，准备并连接新的无菌引流系统（D）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the hierarchy of interventions. Creating a temporary water seal (submerging in sterile water) prevents immediate life-threatening injury and must be performed before assessment and notification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住干预措施的层级关系。建立临时水封（浸入无菌水中）可防止即刻危及生命的伤害，必须在评估和通知之前进行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":204,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_client_elopement_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.13","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.13.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.13.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,60],"fullStemEn":"A nurse on the inpatient geriatric unit realizes that a client with moderate dementia is missing. The client was last seen 30 minutes ago. Place the nurse's actions in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"老年病房的护士发现一名患有中度痴呆症的患者失踪。该患者最后一次露面是在 30 分钟前。请按正确的顺序排列护士的操作步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列护士的操作步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client was last seen 30 minutes ago.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者最后一次露面是在 30 分钟前。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Complete an incident/variance report document.","zh":"填写不良事件/异常情况报告单。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify facility security and the nursing supervisor of the suspected elopement.","zh":"将疑似失踪事件通知医院安全部门和护理主管。"},{"id":"C","en":"Contact the healthcare provider and the client's family.","zh":"联系医疗服务提供者和患者家属。"},{"id":"A","en":"Search the immediate unit, including the client's room, bathrooms, and common areas.","zh":"搜索本病区，包括患者病房、盥洗室和公共区域。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate nursing action when a client is missing is to perform an immediate physical search of the unit. If the client is not found, security and the supervisor must be notified immediately to initiate a facility-wide search and lock doors. Once security is involved, the healthcare provider and the client's family are contacted. Finally, after the acute situation is managed, the nurse documents the event by completing an incident report.","rationaleCorrectZh":"发现患者失踪时，护士的直接行动是立即对本病区进行实地搜寻（A）。如果未找到患者，必须立即通知保安部门和护理主管（B），以启动全院搜寻并锁门。安全部门介入后，联系医疗服务提供者和患者家属（C）。最后，在处理完紧急情况后，护士填写事故报告表以记录该事件（D）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always perform the most local, direct clinical safety action first (searching the unit), then escalate the alert level (security/supervisor), inform stakeholders (provider/family), and complete documentation last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终首先执行最局部、最直接的临床安全行动（搜寻病区），然后升级警报级别（安全/主管），通知相关方（医生/家属），最后完成文件记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":205,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_fib_copd_med_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.14","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.14.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.14.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[329,370],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,119],"fullStemEn":"The healthcare provider prescribes methylprednisolone sodium succinate 60 mg intravenously every 12 hours for a client with a history of acute COPD exacerbation. The medication is supplied in a single-dose vial with a concentration of 40 mg/mL. How many mL should the nurse administer per dose? (Record your answer as a decimal. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"医疗服务提供者为一名有急性 COPD 加重史的患者开具了每 12 小时静脉注射 60 mg 琥珀酸钠甲基泼尼松龙的医嘱。该药物由单剂量小瓶提供，浓度为 40 mg/mL。护士每次应给药多少毫升？（以小数记录答案。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a decimal.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以小数记录答案。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["1.5"],"numeric":{"value":1.5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To calculate the volume to administer, use the formula: (Desired Dose / Available Dose) * Quantity. Here, Desired Dose is 60 mg, and Available Dose is 40 mg/mL. Calculation: (60 mg / 40 mg) * 1 mL = 1.5 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"要计算给药体积，使用公式：（欲求剂量 / 已有剂量）* 数量。在此，欲求剂量为 60 mg，已有剂量浓度为 40 mg/mL。计算过程：（60 mg / 40 mg）* 1 mL = 1.5 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the standard calculation formula: D/H * Q. Double-check your division (60 divided by 40 is 1.5). Always verify the unit requested (mL) and avoid adding it in the numeric input box.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用标准计算公式：D/H * Q。双重检查你的除法运算（60 除以 40 是 1.5）。始终验证所要求的单位（mL），并避免在数字输入框中填写单位。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":206,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_pancreatitis_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.15","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.15.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.15.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[210,332],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,85],"fullStemEn":"A client is hospitalized with acute pancreatitis. The client has been placed on NPO (nothing by mouth) status and has a nasogastric tube to low intermittent suction. The nurse performs a clinical reassessment. For each client finding, click to specify if the finding indicates a therapeutic response (improvement) or a complication.","fullStemZh":"一名急性胰腺炎患者入院治疗。患者已禁食（NPO），并置有进行低压间歇吸引的胃管。护士进行临床重新评估。对于每个患者表现，点击以指定该表现是表明治疗反应（改善）还是并发症。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client finding, click to specify if the finding indicates a therapeutic response (improvement) or a complication.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个患者表现，点击以指定该表现是表明治疗反应（改善）还是并发症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse performs a clinical reassessment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士进行临床重新评估。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Serum amylase and lipase levels are returning toward the normal reference range.","zh":"血清淀粉酶和脂肪酶水平正在恢复至正常参考范围。"},{"id":"r2","en":"The client develops spasm and flexion of the wrist and fingers when a blood pressure cuff is inflated.","zh":"当充气血压计袖带时，患者手腕和手指发生痉挛和屈曲。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Abdominal pain is rated as 2 on a 0-10 scale after resting the bowel.","zh":"在肠道休息禁食后，腹痛评分为 2 分（总分 0-10 分）。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client has a rigid, board-like abdomen and a temperature of 101.3 °F (38.5 °C).","zh":"患者腹部呈板状强直，体温为 101.3 °F (38.5 °C)。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Therapeutic Response / Improvement","zh":"治疗反应/改善"},{"id":"c2","en":"Complication","zh":"并发症"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Normalization of pancreatic enzymes (r1) and reduction of abdominal pain (r3) indicate therapeutic improvement. Spasm of the wrist/fingers during blood pressure measurement (Trousseau sign, r2) indicates hypocalcemia, a common complication of pancreatitis caused by soap formation in necrotic tissue. A rigid, board-like abdomen and fever (r4) indicate peritonitis, which is a life-threatening complication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胰腺酶恢复正常（r1）和腹痛减轻（r3）表示治疗改善。测量血压时手腕/手指痉挛（特鲁索征，r2）表示低钙血症，这是胰腺炎中坏死组织中皂化反应引起的常见并发症。板状腹和发热（r4）表明发生了腹膜炎，这是一种危及生命的并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between indications that the therapy is working (enzymes dropping, pain lessening) and signs of clinical emergencies. Hypocalcemia (Trousseau/Chvostek signs) and peritonitis (board-like abdomen) are classic complications of acute pancreatitis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分治疗有效的表现（酶下降，疼痛减轻）与临床紧急情况的体征。低钙血症（特鲁索征/契夫斯泰克征）和腹膜炎（板状腹）是急性胰腺炎的经典并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":207,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_cloze_anaphylaxis_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.16","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.16.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.16.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[255,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,75],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is administering intravenous penicillin to a hospitalized client. Five minutes into the infusion, the client reports sudden-onset chest tightness, difficulty breathing, and severe itching. The nurse observes diffuse hives on the client's trunk. The nurse must take immediate action.","fullStemZh":"护士正在给一名住院患者静脉输入青霉素。输注五分钟后，患者诉突然感到胸闷、呼吸困难和严重的瘙痒。护士观察到患者躯干有弥漫性荨麻疹。护士必须立即采取行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must take immediate action.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须立即采取行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes diffuse hives on the client's trunk.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士观察到患者躯干有弥漫性荨麻疹。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's immediate priority action is to {{1}}, followed by the administration of {{2}} intramuscularly.","zh":"护士的当务之急是 {{1}}，随后应肌肉注射 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"administer supplemental oxygen via nasal cannula","zh":"通过鼻导管给予辅助氧气"},{"id":"o1","en":"stop the infusion of penicillin","zh":"停止输注青霉素"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"epinephrine","zh":"肾上腺素"},{"id":"o1","en":"diphenhydramine","zh":"苯海拉明"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is experiencing anaphylaxis, a life-threatening systemic hypersensitivity reaction. The first action must be to remove the offending allergen by stopping the infusion (o1 for dropdown 1). The first-line drug of choice for anaphylaxis is epinephrine (o2 for dropdown 2) administered intramuscularly, which causes bronchodilation and vasoconstriction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在经历过敏性休克，这是一种危及生命的全身性超敏反应。第一步行动必须是通过停止输液来清除致敏过敏原（下拉菜单1的o1）。治疗过敏性休克的首选一线药物是肌肉注射肾上腺素（下拉菜单2的o2），可引起支气管扩张和血管收缩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For any medication-related reaction, the first and most critical action is to stop the medication. Recall that Epinephrine is the primary drug for anaphylaxis, whereas antihistamines (diphenhydramine) and steroids are secondary therapies.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于任何与药物相关的反应，第一步也是最关键的行动是停药。记住肾上腺素是过敏性反应的主要首选药物，而抗组胺药（苯海拉明）和糖皮质激素是二级辅助治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":208,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_cardiac_cath_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.17","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.17.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.17.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,324],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,84],"fullStemEn":"A client returns to the nursing unit following a diagnostic cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery. The client is on bed rest with the right leg straight. The nurse performs a postoperative assessment. For each assessment finding, click to specify if the finding is expected or requires immediate intervention.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在经右股动脉进行诊断性心脏导管插入术后返回病区。患者处于卧床休息状态，右腿伸直。护士进行术后评估。对于每个评估发现，点击以指定该发现是预期的还是需要立即干预的。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, click to specify if the finding is expected or requires immediate intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个评估发现，点击以指定该发现是预期的还是需要立即干预的。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse performs a postoperative assessment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士进行术后评估。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The right pedal pulse is palpable and equal in strength to the left pedal pulse.","zh":"右侧足背动脉搏动可扪及且与左侧足背动脉搏动强度相等。"},{"id":"r2","en":"A firm, rapidly expanding mass is palpable under the skin at the right groin insertion site.","zh":"右腹股沟穿刺点皮肤下可触及一坚硬、快速扩大的包块。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The client reports mild soreness at the groin insertion site when coughing.","zh":"咳嗽时患者诉腹股沟穿刺点有轻度酸痛。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client's right foot is cold and pale, with a capillary refill time of 5 seconds.","zh":"患者右脚发冷、苍白，毛细血管充盈时间为 5 秒。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires Immediate Intervention","zh":"需要立即干预"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected Finding","zh":"预期表现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Normal peripheral perfusion (palpable bilateral pedal pulses, r1) and mild groin discomfort (r3) are expected findings after femoral cardiac catheterization. An expanding mass at the groin (r2) indicates a hematoma or arterial pseudoaneurysm. A cold, pale foot with delayed capillary refill (r4) indicates acute arterial occlusion. Both r2 and r4 require immediate intervention to prevent severe hemorrhage or limb ischemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"股动脉心脏介入术后，正常的周围灌注（双侧足背动脉搏动相等，r1）和轻微的腹股沟不适（r3）属于预期表现。腹股沟处出现扩大的包块（r2）表明发生了血肿或动脉假性动脉瘤。右脚发冷、苍白且毛细血管再充盈延迟（r4）表明发生了急性动脉阻塞。r2和r4均需要立即干预，以防止严重出血或肢体缺血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the complications of arterial puncture. Look for indicators of bleeding/hematoma (expanding mass) or vascular occlusion (cold, pale extremity, loss of pulse). Normal findings include stable vital signs, intact pulses, and minor soreness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于动脉穿刺的并发症。寻找出血/血肿（扩大的包块）或血管阻塞（下肢发冷、苍白、脉搏消失）的指标。正常表现包括生命体征稳定、脉搏完好以及轻微酸痛。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":209,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_urine_output_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.18","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.18.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.18.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,283],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,73],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the intake and output record of an adult client who is recovering from major abdominal surgery. The client has an indwelling urinary catheter. The nurse notes that the total urine output over the past 4 hours is 80 mL. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名腹部大手术后恢复期成年患者的入量和出量记录。该患者留置有尿管。护士注意到过去4小时的总尿量为 80 毫升。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes that the total urine output over the past 4 hours is 80 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到过去4小时的总尿量为 80 毫升。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer a prescribed dose of a loop diuretic.","zh":"给予开具剂量的袢利尿剂。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the healthcare provider of the low urine output.","zh":"将尿量偏低的情况通知医疗服务提供者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Increase the rate of the client's intravenous fluids.","zh":"增加患者静脉输液的速度。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check the catheter tubing for kinks or obstruction.","zh":"检查导尿管管路是否有折叠或阻塞。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The minimum expected urine output for an adult client is 0.5 mL/kg/hr or at least 30 mL/hr. A total of 80 mL over 4 hours is low (20 mL/hr) and indicates oliguria. The nurse's first action should be to check the equipment for mechanical problems such as kinks, twists, or obstructions in the catheter tubing, which is the least invasive and most common cause of sudden low urine output in catheterized patients.","rationaleCorrectZh":"成年患者的预期最低尿量为 0.5 mL/kg/h 或至少 30 mL/h。4小时共80毫升偏低（20 mL/h），表示少尿。护士的首要行动应当是检查设备是否存在机械故障，如导尿管折叠、扭曲或阻塞，这是留置尿管患者出现突发低尿量最无创且最常见的原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always rule out simple, mechanical, and least invasive issues (like kinks in tubes or catheters) before escalating care or implementing invasive/medical interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在升级护理或实施侵入性/医疗干预之前，始终先排除简单的、机械的以及最少侵入性的问题（例如管路或导尿管折叠）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":210,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_bowel_elimination_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.19","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.19.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.19.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,59],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge teaching to a client with a history of chronic constipation. Which interventions should the nurse include in the teaching plan to promote healthy bowel elimination? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名有慢性便秘史的患者提供出院指导。护士应在教学计划中纳入哪些干预措施以促进健康的肠道排泄？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the teaching plan to promote healthy bowel elimination?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在教学计划中纳入哪些干预措施以促进健康的肠道排泄？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Use a stimulant laxative daily to ensure regular bowel movements.","zh":"每日使用刺激性泻药以确保定期排便。"},{"id":"B","en":"Incorporate high-fiber foods such as whole grains, fruits, and vegetables into the diet.","zh":"在饮食中加入全谷物、水果和蔬菜等高纤维食物。"},{"id":"E","en":"Engage in regular physical activity or daily walks.","zh":"进行规律的体育活动或每日散步。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase daily fluid intake to 2 to 3 liters, unless contraindicated.","zh":"除非有禁忌，否则将每日饮水量增加至 2 到 3 升。"},{"id":"D","en":"Establish a regular routine for defecation, such as shortly after meals.","zh":"建立规律的排便习惯，如在饭后不久。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Promoting healthy bowel elimination includes increasing fluid intake (2-3 L/day) to soften stool, high-fiber foods to add bulk, establishing a set time for elimination to take advantage of the gastrocolic reflex, and regular physical activity (E) to stimulate peristalsis. Daily stimulant laxatives are contraindicated as they cause dependency and decrease bowel muscle tone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"促进健康排便包括增加饮水量（2-3升/天）以软化粪便（A）、吃高纤维食物（B）以增加体积、建立固定的排便时间（D）以利用胃结肠反射，以及进行规律的体育活动（E）以刺激肠蠕动。每日使用刺激性泻药（C）是禁忌的，因为这会产生依赖性并降低肠道肌张力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for natural, non-pharmacological lifestyle changes for health promotion. Avoid any options that suggest long-term or daily dependence on stimulant laxatives.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找用于健康促进的自然、非药物的生活方式改变。避免选择任何暗示长期或每日依赖刺激性泻药的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":211,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_delegation_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.20","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.20.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.20.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,63],"fullStemEn":"The registered nurse (RN) is planning care for a client who is 1 day postoperative following a total knee arthroplasty. Which task is most appropriate for the RN to delegate to the unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","fullStemZh":"注册护士（RN）正在为一名全膝关节置换术后 1 天的患者制定护理计划。以下哪项任务最适合 RN 委派给无证辅助人员（UAP）？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which task is most appropriate for the RN to delegate to the unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项任务最适合 RN 委派给无证辅助人员（UAP）？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The registered nurse (RN) is planning care for a client who is 1 day postoperative following a total knee arthroplasty.","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士（RN）正在为一名全膝关节置换术后 1 天的患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's surgical incision for signs of infection.","zh":"评估患者的伤口手术切口是否有感染迹象。"},{"id":"D","en":"Adjust the settings on the client's continuous passive motion (CPM) machine.","zh":"调整患者连续被动运动（CPM）机上的设置。"},{"id":"C","en":"Teach the client how to perform postoperative ankle pumps.","zh":"指导患者如何进行术后踝泵运动。"},{"id":"B","en":"Empty and measure the drainage from the closed-wound drainage system.","zh":"倾倒并测量闭合式伤口引流系统中的引流量。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The RN can delegate standard, routine tasks that do not require clinical judgment, assessment, teaching, or medication administration to UAPs. Emptying and measuring drainage is a mechanical, measurable task that fits these criteria. Assessments, patient education, and managing medical device settings require specialized nursing knowledge and judgment and cannot be delegated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"RN 可以将不需要临床判断、评估、指导或给药的标准化、常规任务委派给 UAP。倾倒和测量引流量（B）是一项机械的、可测量的任务，符合这些标准。评估（A）、患者教育（C）和管理医疗设备设置（D）需要专业的护理知识和判断，不能委派。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the rules of delegation: do not delegate assessment, teaching, clinical judgment, or evaluation (EAT: Evaluate, Assess, Teach) to UAP.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住委派规则：不要将评估、教学、临床判断或评价（缩写“EAT”：Evaluate-评价, Assess-评估, Teach-教学）委派给 UAP。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":212,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_delirium_22","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.21","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.21.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.21.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[239,343],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,86],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is evaluating an older adult client who was admitted to the hospital with a urinary tract infection. The client's family reports that the client has suddenly become confused, disoriented, and is seeing things that are not there. For each clinical characteristic, click to specify if it is more characteristic of delirium or dementia.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名因尿路感染入院治疗的老年患者。患者家属报告说，患者突然变得糊涂、定向力障碍，并能看到不存在的东西。对于每个临床特征，点击以指定它是更符合谵妄还是痴呆的特征。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical characteristic, click to specify if it is more characteristic of delirium or dementia.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个临床特征，点击以指定它是更符合谵妄还是痴呆的特征。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's family reports that the client has suddenly become confused, disoriented, and is seeing things that are not there.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者家属报告说，患者突然变得糊涂、定向力障碍，并能看到不存在的东西。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Onset of symptoms is sudden, acute, and fluctuates throughout the day.","zh":"症状发作突然、呈急性，且全天波动。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Onset of symptoms is slow, gradual, and progressive over months or years.","zh":"症状发作缓慢、渐进，时间跨度达数月或数年。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Level of consciousness is altered and fluctuates (e.g., lethargy to hyperactivity).","zh":"意识水平发生改变且发生波动（例如，从嗜睡到过度活跃）。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Attention span is severely impaired, and the condition is typically reversible once the underlying cause is treated.","zh":"注意力范围严重受损，并且一旦潜在病因得到治疗，病症通常是可逆的。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Delirium","zh":"谵妄"},{"id":"c2","en":"Dementia","zh":"痴呆"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Delirium is characterized by an acute, sudden onset (r1), altered level of consciousness (r3), impaired attention, and reversibility once the underlying cause (e.g., infection) is treated (r4). Dementia is a slow, progressive, irreversible decline in cognitive function with a stable level of consciousness (r2).","rationaleCorrectZh":"谵妄的特征是急性、突然发作（r1）、意识水平发生改变（r3）、注意力受损，且在潜在病因（如感染）得到治疗后具有可逆性（r4）。痴呆则是一种缓慢、渐进、不可逆的认知功能下降，且意识水平保持稳定（r2）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare the onset and reversibility. Delirium is acute, fluctuating, and reversible. Dementia is chronic, progressive, and irreversible.","testTakingStrategyZh":"比较发病过程和可逆性。谵妄是急性的、波动的、可逆的。痴呆是慢性的、渐进的、不可逆的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":213,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_cloze_depression_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.22","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.22.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.22.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[219,261],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,74],"fullStemEn":"A client diagnosed with major depressive disorder is admitted to the psychiatric unit. During the initial interview, the client states, 'I just don't see any point in going on. Everyone would be better off without me.' The nurse must assess the client's safety.","fullStemZh":"一名诊断为重度抑郁症的患者入住精神科病房。在初次访谈中，患者说：“我真的觉得活下去没有任何意义。没有我，大家都会过得更好。”护士必须评估患者的安全。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must assess the client's safety.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须评估患者的安全。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Everyone would be better off without me.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"没有我，大家都会过得更好。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's immediate action should be to ask the client {{1}} and to place the client on {{2}}.","zh":"护士应立即采取的行动是询问患者 {{1}}，并对患者实施 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"about their relationship with their family members","zh":"关于他们与家庭成员的关系"},{"id":"o2","en":"directly if they have a specific plan for suicide","zh":"直接询问他们是否有具体的自杀计划"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"one-on-one continuous observation","zh":"一对一持续观察（专人值守）"},{"id":"o2","en":"routine 15-minute safety checks","zh":"常规每 15 分钟安全巡查"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When a client expresses suicidal ideation, the nurse must ask directly about suicide and whether they have a specific plan (o2 for dropdown 1) to determine the level of risk. Because the client is expressing active hopelessness and suicidal intent, the immediate safety intervention is to place them under one-on-one continuous line-of-sight observation (o1 for dropdown 2) to prevent self-harm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当患者表达自杀念头时，护士必须直接询问其自杀意向及是否有具体计划（下拉菜单1的o2），以确定风险级别。因为患者表达了主动的绝望感和自杀意图，直接的安全干预措施是将他们置于一对一持续视线监护之下（下拉菜单2的o1），以防止自残行为。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In psychiatric nursing, safety is always the first priority. Direct questions about suicide are necessary and do not plant the idea in the client's mind. Active suicidal intent requires the highest level of observation (one-on-one).","testTakingStrategyZh":"在精神科护理中，安全始终是第一位的。直接询问有关自杀的问题是必要的，这并不会在患者脑海中植入自杀念头。主动自杀企图需要最高级别的观察（一对一专人监护）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":214,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_diabetes_sick_day_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.23","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.23.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.23.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,59],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client with type 1 diabetes mellitus about managing the disease during illness ('sick-day rules'). Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名 1 型糖尿病患者如何进行患病期间的疾病管理（“患病期规则”）。护士应该包括哪些指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应该包括哪些指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Stop taking insulin if you are unable to eat or have nausea.","zh":"如果无法进食或感到恶心，请停止使用胰岛素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check urine for ketones if blood glucose is greater than 240 mg/dL.","zh":"如果血糖大于 240 mg/dL，检查尿液中的酮体。"},{"id":"D","en":"Drink plenty of non-caloric fluids to prevent dehydration.","zh":"饮用充足的无热量液体以防脱水。"},{"id":"A","en":"Monitor blood glucose levels at least every 4 hours.","zh":"至少每 4 小时监测一次血糖水平。"},{"id":"E","en":"Call the healthcare provider if you have a fever that does not respond to acetaminophen.","zh":"如果发热且使用对乙酰氨基酚后无改善，请联系医疗服务提供者。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During illness, the body is under stress, which raises blood glucose. The client must monitor glucose frequently and test for ketones if glucose exceeds 240 mg/dL. Hydration is critical to prevent DKA. Persistent fever or inability to tolerate fluids requires medical notification (E). Stopping insulin is dangerous because stress hormone release increases the need for insulin, even without food intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生病期间，机体处于应激状态，这会升高血糖。患者必须经常监测血糖（A），并在血糖超过 240 mg/dL 时测试酮体（B）。补水对于预防 DKA 至关重要（D）。持续发热或无法耐受液体需要通知医生（E）。停止使用胰岛素（C）是危险的，因为应激激素的释放会增加对胰岛素的需求，即使在没有进食的情况下也是如此。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: NEVER teach a diabetic patient to stop taking insulin when they are sick. The stress of illness raises blood glucose, so insulin remains essential.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：绝对不要指导糖尿病患者在生病时停用胰岛素。疾病应激会使血糖升高，因此胰岛素仍然是不可或缺的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":215,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_dka_management_25","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.24","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.24.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.24.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[169,253],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,73],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the intensive care unit with diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA). The client's blood glucose is 480 mg/dL, and they are experiencing severe dehydration. Place the following nursing interventions in the correct order of clinical priority.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）入住重症监护病房。患者的血糖为 480 mg/dL，且正在经历严重脱水。请按临床优先顺序排列下列护理干预措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing interventions in the correct order of clinical priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按临床优先顺序排列下列护理干预措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's blood glucose is 480 mg/dL, and they are experiencing severe dehydration.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的血糖为 480 mg/dL，且正在经历严重脱水。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Add dextrose to the intravenous fluids when blood glucose reaches 250 mg/dL.","zh":"当血糖降至 250 mg/dL 时，在静脉输液中加入葡萄糖。"},{"id":"B","en":"Start the prescribed continuous intravenous regular insulin infusion after confirming the potassium level is safe.","zh":"确认血钾水平安全后，开始按医嘱持续静脉输注普通胰岛素。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess serum potassium levels and replace potassium as prescribed.","zh":"评估血清钾水平并按医嘱补钾。"},{"id":"A","en":"Initiate rapid intravenous infusion of 0.9% normal saline.","zh":"开始快速静脉输注 0.9% 生理盐水。"}],"correct":["A","D","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In DKA, the absolute first priority is fluid resuscitation to restore perfusion and intravascular volume. Potassium must then be assessed and replaced as prescribed before insulin is started or continued, because insulin shifts potassium into cells and can precipitate life-threatening hypokalemia. Once potassium is safe, the prescribed continuous regular insulin infusion is started to stop ketone production and correct acidosis. Finally, dextrose is added to IV fluids when blood glucose reaches about 250 mg/dL so insulin can continue safely while ketoacidosis resolves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 DKA 中，首要任务是液体复苏（A），以恢复灌注和血管内容量。随后必须评估血钾并按医嘱补钾（D），再开始或继续胰岛素治疗，因为胰岛素会促使钾离子进入细胞内，可能引发危及生命的低钾血症。确认血钾安全后，开始按医嘱持续静脉输注普通胰岛素（B），以停止酮体生成并纠正酸中毒。最后，当血糖降至约 250 mg/dL 时，在静脉液体中加入葡萄糖（C），使胰岛素能够安全持续使用，直到酮症酸中毒纠正。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For DKA, think fluids first, then potassium safety, then insulin. Shock and severe hypovolemia take precedence over correcting hyperglycemia, and insulin should not outrun potassium assessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理 DKA 时，先想到补液，其次确认血钾安全，再使用胰岛素。休克和严重低血容量优先于纠正高血糖，胰岛素治疗不能早于血钾评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":216,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_digoxin_toxicity_26","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.25","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.25.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.25.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[171,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,63],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer the daily dose of digoxin to a client with heart failure. The client reports nausea, anorexia, and seeing yellow halos around lights. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备给一名心力衰竭患者服用每日剂量的地高辛。患者诉有恶心、食欲减退，并能看到光线周围有黄色光晕。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports nausea, anorexia, and seeing yellow halos around lights.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者诉有恶心、食欲减退，并能看到光线周围有黄色光晕。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Request an order for an antiemetic to relieve the nausea.","zh":"申请止吐药医嘱以缓解恶心。"},{"id":"B","en":"Withhold the dose and notify the healthcare provider immediately.","zh":"暂停给药并立即通知医疗服务提供者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the digoxin as scheduled and document the symptoms.","zh":"按计划给药地高辛并记录症状。"},{"id":"A","en":"Withhold the dose and check the client's apical pulse for 1 minute.","zh":"暂停给药，并听诊患者的心尖搏动1分钟。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is experiencing classic signs of digoxin toxicity (nausea, anorexia, visual changes like yellow-green halos). The nurse must immediately withhold the medication and contact the healthcare provider to obtain a serum digoxin level and check electrolytes (especially potassium, as hypokalemia potentiates toxicity).","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者表现出地高辛中毒的经典症状（恶心、食欲减退、黄绿视等视觉改变）。护士必须立即暂停给药并联系医生，以获取血清地高辛浓度检测和电解质检查（尤其是钾水平，因为低钾血症会加重地高辛中毒）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the systemic and visual cues of digoxin toxicity (GI distress, yellow vision). Once recognized, the priority action is to withhold the dose and notify the healthcare provider.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别地高辛中毒的全身和视觉线索（胃肠道不适、黄视）。一旦识别，首要行动就是停药并通知医疗服务提供者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":217,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_disaster_triage_27","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.26","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.26.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.26.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,246],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,87],"fullStemEn":"The nurse responds to a mass casualty incident following an explosion. Using the Simple Triage and Rapid Treatment (START) method, the nurse assesses multiple victims. For each victim description, click to specify the correct triage tag category.","fullStemZh":"护士应对一起爆炸发生后的群体伤亡事件。使用简单分类和快速治疗（START）方法，护士评估多名伤员。对于每个伤员描述，点击以指定正确的预检分类标签（Triage Tag）类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each victim description, click to specify the correct triage tag category.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个伤员描述，点击以指定正确的预检分类标签（Triage Tag）类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Simple Triage and Rapid Treatment (START) method, the nurse assesses multiple victims.","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用简单分类和快速治疗（START）方法，护士评估多名伤员。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"A victim who is alert, walking around, and has minor abrasions and superficial cuts.","zh":"一名神志清醒、能四处走动，仅有轻微擦伤和表浅伤口的伤员。"},{"id":"r2","en":"A victim who is apneic, and does not start breathing even after the airway is opened.","zh":"一名无自主呼吸，且在开放气道后仍未开始呼吸的伤员。"},{"id":"r3","en":"A victim who has an open femur fracture, is conscious, has a respiratory rate of 24/min, and a palpable radial pulse.","zh":"一名股骨开放性骨折、神志清楚、呼吸频率为 24 次/分且可扪及桡动脉搏动的伤员。"},{"id":"r4","en":"A victim who is unconscious, has a respiratory rate of 34/min, and capillary refill of 4 seconds.","zh":"一名意识丧失、呼吸频率为 34 次/分且毛细血管充盈时间为 4 秒的伤员。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Red (Immediate / Life-threatening)","zh":"红标（危重、需立即抢救）"},{"id":"c2","en":"Yellow (Delayed)","zh":"黄标（有伤、可延迟处理）"},{"id":"c1","en":"Green (Minor / Walking Wounded)","zh":"绿标（轻伤/可行走的伤员）"},{"id":"c4","en":"Black (Deceased / Expectant)","zh":"黑标（死亡/无抢救希望）"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c4"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Under the START system: Walking wounded are tagged Green (r1). Apneic victims who do not breathe after airway positioning are tagged Black (r2). Victims with injuries that need care but have normal perfusion/mental status (RR < 30, radial pulse present, follows commands) are tagged Yellow (r3). Victims who are unconscious, have RR > 30, or delayed capillary refill (>2s) are tagged Red (r4).","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 START 系统中：可行走的轻伤员贴绿标（r1）。在开放气道后仍无呼吸的伤员贴黑标（r2）。有严重创伤但循环和意识状态正常（呼吸<30，桡动脉搏动存在，能服从指令）的伤员贴黄标（r3）。意识丧失、呼吸>30或毛细血管再充盈延迟（>2秒）的伤员贴红标（r4）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the START criteria: '30-2-Can Do' (Respirations over 30, Capillary refill over 2 seconds, and ability to follow commands). Any failure in these parameters automatically tags the victim Red.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 START 分类指标：“30-2-Can Do”（呼吸是否大于30次/分，毛细血管充盈是否大于2秒，是否能服从指令）。任何一项指标异常均使伤员归入红标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Using the Simple Triage and Rapid Treatment (START) method, the nurse assesses multiple victims.","controlSentenceZh":"使用简单分类和快速治疗（START）方法，护士评估多名伤员。"}
{"queueIndex":218,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_fib_reconstitution_28","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.27","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.27.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.27.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[358,399],"terminalOffsetsZh":[131,144],"fullStemEn":"The healthcare provider prescribes cefazolin 500 mg intravenously every 8 hours for a surgical client. The nurse reconstitutes a vial of cefazolin powder by adding 2.5 mL of sterile water, resulting in a total volume of 3.0 mL with a concentration of 330 mg/mL. How many mL of cefazolin should the nurse administer? (Record your answer to the nearest tenth. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"医疗服务提供者为一名手术患者开具了每 8 小时静脉注射 500 mg 头孢唑林的医嘱。护士通过加入 2.5 毫升无菌注射用水来稀释一瓶头孢唑林粉针剂，最终配制成浓度为 330 mg/mL 的 3.0 毫升药液。护士应该给药多少毫升？（四舍五入保留到小数点后一位。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer to the nearest tenth.","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入保留到小数点后一位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["1.5","1.5 mL"],"numeric":{"value":1.5,"tolerance":0.1,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Use the formula: (Desired Dose / Have Dose) * Volume. Desired is 500 mg. Reconstituted concentration is 330 mg/mL. Calculation: (500 / 330) * 1 mL = 1.515 mL. Rounding to the nearest tenth gives 1.5 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用公式：（欲求剂量 / 已有剂量）* 体积。欲求剂量为 500 mg。稀释后的浓度为 330 mg/mL。计算过程：（500 / 330）* 1 mL = 1.515 mL。四舍五入保留到小数点后一位是 1.5 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the final concentration after reconstitution (330 mg/mL) rather than the diluent volume added (2.5 mL). Use D/H * Q to find the volume, and round precisely as instructed (nearest tenth).","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定稀释后的终浓度（330 mg/mL），而不是加入的稀释液体积（2.5 mL）。使用 D/H * Q 求解体积，并按照指示精确舍入（保留至小数点后一位）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":219,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_dysphagia_29","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.28.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,47],"fullStemEn":"A swallowing evaluation for a client with post-stroke dysphagia recommends a chin-down posture during oral intake. Which intervention should the nurse implement during meals?","fullStemZh":"一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者的吞咽评估建议在经口进食时采用低头姿势。护士在进餐期间应实施哪项干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention should the nurse implement during meals?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在进餐期间应实施哪项干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A swallowing evaluation for a client with post-stroke dysphagia recommends a chin-down posture during oral intake.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者的吞咽评估建议在经口进食时采用低头姿势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a semi-Fowler position during meals.","zh":"进餐时让患者处于半坐卧位（semi-Fowler）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Instruct the client to tuck their chin down toward the chest when swallowing.","zh":"指导患者在吞咽时将下巴向下收紧，靠近胸口（低头吞咽）。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to tilt their head backward when swallowing.","zh":"鼓励患者在吞咽时将头部向后仰。"},{"id":"B","en":"Offer thin liquids, such as water or juice, to wash down solid foods.","zh":"提供稀液体如水或果汁以冲服固体食物。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should follow the individualized swallowing recommendation and cue the prescribed chin-down posture. This maneuver may improve airway protection for selected swallowing impairments. The client should be upright, while liquid consistency and other postural strategies should follow the swallowing assessment rather than universal rules.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应遵循个体化吞咽建议，提示患者采用医嘱规定的低头姿势。该动作可改善部分特定吞咽障碍患者的气道保护。患者应保持直立，而液体稠度及其他姿势策略应依据吞咽评估决定，而非采用统一规则。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the swallowing evaluation and individualized feeding plan to choose posture and liquid consistency; chin-down is useful for selected swallowing patterns, not all dysphagia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应依据吞咽评估和个体化进食计划选择姿势与液体稠度；低头动作适用于部分吞咽模式，而非所有吞咽困难。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":220,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_enteral_feeding_30","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.29.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer an enteral feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube to a client. Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备通过鼻胃管（NG tube）为一名患者进行肠内营养灌注。请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer an enteral feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube to a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备通过鼻胃管（NG tube）为一名患者进行肠内营养灌注。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Aspirate gastric contents and measure the gastric residual volume.","zh":"抽吸胃内容物并测量胃残留量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Elevate the head of the bed to 30 to 45 degrees.","zh":"抬高床头至 30 到 45 度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the placement of the nasogastric tube using an approved method (e.g., pH testing or checking markings).","zh":"使用批准的方法（如 pH 值测试或检查管路标记）验证鼻胃管的位置。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer the enteral formula infusion.","zh":"开始灌注肠内营养液。"},{"id":"D","en":"Flush the nasogastric tube with 30 mL of sterile or tap water.","zh":"用 30 毫升无菌水或自来水冲洗鼻胃管。"}],"correct":["C","A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Before beginning any enteral feeding, the first step is to elevate the head of the bed to prevent aspiration. Next, the nurse must verify tube placement to ensure it is in the stomach. Once placement is confirmed, the nurse measures gastric residual volume to evaluate gastric emptying. The tube is then flushed with water to ensure patency before infusing the feeding formula (E).","rationaleCorrectZh":"在开始任何肠内营养之前，第一步是抬高床头（C）以防误吸。接下来，护士必须验证导管位置（A）以确保其在胃内。确认位置后，护士测量胃残留量（B）以评估胃排空情况。然后用温水冲洗导管（D）以确保通畅，最后输入营养液（E）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Positioning always comes first to ensure client safety during assessments and tube manipulation. Always verify placement and patency before introducing fluid or formula.","testTakingStrategyZh":"体位调整总是第一位的，以确保在评估和导管操作期间的患者安全。在引入液体或营养液之前，务必先验证位置和通畅性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":221,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_preeclampsia_31","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.30.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[226,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,67],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is performing an assessment on a pregnant client at 34 weeks gestation who is diagnosed with preeclampsia. Which clinical findings should the nurse identify as signs of worsening preeclampsia or impending eclampsia? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名孕 34 周、诊断为子痫前期的孕妇进行评估。护士应将哪些临床表现识别为子痫前期加重或即将发生子痫的征兆？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical findings should the nurse identify as signs of worsening preeclampsia or impending eclampsia?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些临床表现识别为子痫前期加重或即将发生子痫的征兆？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Right upper quadrant or epigastric pain","zh":"右上腹或上腹部疼痛"},{"id":"D","en":"Increase in urine output to 60 mL/hr","zh":"尿量增加至 60 毫升/小时"},{"id":"B","en":"Visual disturbances, such as flashing lights or double vision","zh":"视觉障碍，如闪光感或重影"},{"id":"A","en":"Persistent, severe frontal headache","zh":"持续的、严重的额部头痛"},{"id":"E","en":"Hyperactive deep tendon reflexes (4+ with clonus)","zh":"腱反射亢进（4+，伴有踝阵挛）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Signs of worsening preeclampsia indicating central nervous system involvement include severe, persistent headache, visual changes, and hyperreflexia/clonus (E). Epigastric/RUQ pain reflects hepatic swelling/ischemia and is a critical warning sign. Increased urine output is a reassuring sign, whereas oliguria is associated with worsening preeclampsia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"子痫前期加重提示累及中枢神经系统的表现包括严重的持续头痛（A）、视觉改变（B）和反射亢进/阵挛（E）。上腹部/右上腹疼痛（C）反映肝脏肿胀/缺血，是一项关键警示体征。尿量增加（D）是一个令人放心的体征，而少尿则与子痫前期加重有关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the pathopharmacology of preeclampsia (vasospasm). Look for signs indicating cerebral edema (headache, vision changes), liver involvement (RUQ pain), and neuromuscular excitability (hyperreflexia).","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注子痫前期的病理药理生理学（血管痉挛）。寻找提示脑水肿（头痛、视力改变）、肝脏受累（右上腹痛）和神经肌肉兴奋性增高（反射亢进）的体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":222,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_pph_priority_32","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.31.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[334,374],"terminalOffsetsZh":[90,103],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing a client who gave birth vaginally 2 hours ago. The nurse notes that the client's perineal pad is saturated with rubra lochia within 15 minutes. The nurse supports the lower uterine segment and massages the fundus until it becomes firm, but the fundus remains displaced upward and to the right of the umbilicus. Which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名2小时前经阴道分娩的产妇。护士注意到患者的会阴垫在 15 分钟内即被红色恶露浸透。护士支托子宫下段并按摩子宫底，直到子宫底变硬，但子宫底仍向右上方移位、高于脐水平。护士下一步应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士下一步应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse supports the lower uterine segment and massages the fundus until it becomes firm, but the fundus remains displaced upward and to the right of the umbilicus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士支托子宫下段并按摩子宫底，直到子宫底变硬，但子宫底仍向右上方移位、高于脐水平。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Perform fundal massage to stimulate contraction.","zh":"按摩子宫底以刺激收缩。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the prescribed intravenous oxytocin infusion.","zh":"给予医嘱开的静脉缩宫素输注。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider of the heavy bleeding.","zh":"将大量出血的情况通知医疗服务提供者。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assist the client to the bathroom to void.","zh":"协助患者去洗手间排尿。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The fundus has already been massaged until firm, but it remains displaced upward and to the right, which is a classic sign of bladder distention. A full bladder prevents the uterus from staying midline and contracting effectively, increasing postpartum bleeding. The nurse should next assist the client to empty the bladder, which allows the uterus to return to midline and maintain tone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"子宫底已经被按摩至变硬，但仍向右上方移位，这是膀胱充盈的典型表现。充盈的膀胱会阻止子宫保持在中线并有效收缩，从而增加产后出血。护士下一步应协助患者排空膀胱（B），使子宫回到中线并维持张力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate tone from position. A boggy fundus needs massage; a firm fundus that remains elevated and displaced to the right points to bladder distention, so the next action is to help the client void.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分子宫张力和位置。子宫底松弛需要按摩；如果子宫底已变硬但仍升高并偏向右侧，提示膀胱充盈，下一步应协助患者排尿。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":223,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_epiglottitis_33","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.32.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[169,237],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,66],"fullStemEn":"A 4-year-old child is brought to the emergency department with suspected acute epiglottitis. The child is drooling, sitting in a tripod position, and is highly anxious. Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"一名 4 岁儿童因疑似急性会厌炎被送往急诊科。患儿流口水、呈前倾端坐位（三脚架体位），并且极度焦虑。请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The child is drooling, sitting in a tripod position, and is highly anxious.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患儿流口水、呈前倾端坐位（三脚架体位），并且极度焦虑。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer prescribed intravenous antibiotics after airway management is underway.","zh":"在气道处理已经启动后，按医嘱给予静脉抗生素。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer humidified oxygen as tolerated without causing agitation.","zh":"在不引起烦躁的情况下，给予患儿可以耐受的湿化氧气。"},{"id":"A","en":"Keep the child calm and in a comfortable sitting position on the parent's lap, avoiding invasive procedures.","zh":"让患儿保持安静，坐在父母大腿上采取舒适的坐位，避免任何侵入性操作。"},{"id":"B","en":"Prepare emergency intubation or tracheostomy equipment at the bedside.","zh":"在床旁准备紧急气管插管或气管切开设备。"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For suspected epiglottitis, the first safety priority is to prepare emergency airway equipment at the bedside because complete airway occlusion can occur rapidly. The child should then be kept calm in a position of comfort to reduce crying and agitation that can worsen airway obstruction. Humidified oxygen is administered gently as tolerated. After airway management is underway, prescribed intravenous antibiotics are given to treat the underlying bacterial infection. The nurse should not inspect the throat with a tongue blade or obtain a throat culture because stimulation can precipitate complete obstruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于疑似会厌炎，首要安全任务是在床旁准备紧急气道设备（B），因为完全性气道梗阻可能迅速发生。随后应让患儿保持安静并采取舒适体位（A），以减少哭闹和烦躁，避免加重气道梗阻。在患儿可耐受且不被激惹的情况下，温和给予湿化氧气（C）。气道处理已经启动后，按医嘱给予静脉抗生素（D），以治疗潜在的细菌感染。护士不应使用压舌板检查咽喉或采集咽拭子，因为刺激可能诱发完全性气道梗阻。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the classic signs of epiglottitis: drooling, dysphonia, dysphagia, and distress (the '4 Ds'). The absolute rule is to NEVER inspect the throat with a tongue blade or swab, as this can cause total airway obstruction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别会厌炎的经典征象：流涎（drooling）、发音困难（dysphonia）、吞咽困难（dysphagia）和呼吸困难（distress）（合称“4 D”）。绝对性规则是绝不能使用压舌板或拭子检查咽喉，因为这会导致完全性气道梗阻。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":224,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_seizure_precautions_34","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.33.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is establishing seizure precautions for a client who was admitted following a generalized tonic-clonic seizure. Which interventions should the nurse implement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名因强直阵挛性发作入院的患者制定癫痫防范措施。护士应实施哪些干预措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪些干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Keep oxygen and suction equipment at the bedside.","zh":"在床旁备齐吸氧和吸引设备。"},{"id":"A","en":"Pad the side rails of the client's bed.","zh":"在患者病床的护栏上加装保护垫。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensure that the client's bed is kept in the lowest position.","zh":"确保患者的病床保持在最低位置。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep the side rails of the bed elevated (usually 2 to 4 rails, per protocol).","zh":"保持病床护栏抬起（通常根据规程抬起 2 至 4 个护栏）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place a padded tongue blade at the bedside to insert during a seizure.","zh":"在床旁放置带有保护垫的压舌板，以便在癫痫发作时插入。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Seizure precautions involve protecting the client from injury. This includes padding the side rails, ensuring emergency suction and oxygen are at the bedside, keeping the bed in the lowest position, and keeping side rails raised (E). Inserting a tongue blade or any object into a client's mouth during a seizure is strictly contraindicated as it can cause airway obstruction, dental damage, or bites to the nurse's fingers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"癫痫防范措施包括保护患者免受伤害。这包括在护栏上加防护垫（A）、确保床旁备有应急吸引器和氧气（B）、保持病床在最低位置（D）以及抬起病床护栏（E）。在癫痫发作时向患者口中插入压舌板或任何物体（C）是禁忌的，因为这会导致气道阻塞、牙齿损伤或咬伤护士手指。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on client safety. The most important clinical safety concept for seizures is: NEVER insert anything (like a tongue blade) into the mouth during an active seizure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于患者安全。针对癫痫发作最核心的临床安全概念是：在活动性发作期间，切勿将任何东西（如压舌板）塞入口中。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":225,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_autonomic_dysreflexia_35","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.34.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,316],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,109],"fullStemEn":"A client with a spinal cord injury at the T6 level is admitted to the rehabilitation unit. The nurse is monitoring the client for signs of autonomic dysreflexia. For each clinical manifestation, click to specify if the finding is associated with autonomic activity below or above the level of the spinal cord injury.","fullStemZh":"一名胸6（T6）水平脊髓损伤的患者入住康复病房。护士正在监测患者是否出现自主神经反射亢进（Autonomic Dysreflexia）。对于每个临床表现，点击以指定该表现是与脊髓损伤水平以下还是以上的自主神经活动相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical manifestation, click to specify if the finding is associated with autonomic activity below or above the level of the spinal cord injury.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个临床表现，点击以指定该表现是与脊髓损伤水平以下还是以上的自主神经活动相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring the client for signs of autonomic dysreflexia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测患者是否出现自主神经反射亢进（Autonomic Dysreflexia）。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Severe vasoconstriction, pale skin, and cold extremities.","zh":"严重的血管收缩、皮肤苍白以及肢体发冷。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Profuse sweating and skin flushing.","zh":"大汗淋漓和皮肤潮红。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Nasal congestion and headache.","zh":"鼻塞和头痛。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Goosebumps (piloerection).","zh":"鸡皮疙瘩（立毛肌收缩）。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Above the Level of Injury","zh":"损伤水平以上"},{"id":"c1","en":"Below the Level of Injury","zh":"损伤水平以下"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In autonomic dysreflexia, a noxious stimulus below the level of injury triggers uninhibited sympathetic activity, causing severe vasoconstriction, pale skin, and goosebumps (r1, r4) below the injury level. The brain detects the high blood pressure and attempts to compensate via parasympathetic activity above the level of injury, causing vasodilation (flushing, sweating, nasal congestion, headache) (r2, r3) above the injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在自主神经反射亢进中，损伤水平以下的有害刺激会触发不受抑制的交感神经活动，导致损伤水平以下发生严重的血管收缩、皮肤苍白和鸡皮疙瘩（r1, r4）。大脑监测到高血压并试图通过损伤水平以上的副交感神经活动进行代偿，导致损伤水平以上发生血管扩张（潮红、荒燥、鼻塞、头痛）（r2, r3）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast the two regions: Below the injury is sympathetic (vasoconstriction, pale, cold, goosebumps). Above the injury is parasympathetic (vasodilation, flushed, sweaty, headache).","testTakingStrategyZh":"对比这两个区域：损伤水平以下是交感神经占优势（血管收缩、苍白、冷、鸡皮疙瘩）。损伤水平以上是副交感/代偿血管扩张占优势（血管扩张、潮红、出汗、头痛）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":226,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_lithium_toxicity_36","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.35.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,46],"fullStemEn":"A client is prescribed lithium carbonate for the treatment of bipolar disorder. Which clinical finding should the nurse identify as an early sign of lithium toxicity?","fullStemZh":"一名患者开具了碳酸锂用于治疗双相情感障碍。护士应将哪项临床表现识别为地高辛锂中毒的早期体征？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which clinical finding should the nurse identify as an early sign of lithium toxicity?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将哪项临床表现识别为地高辛锂中毒的早期体征？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is prescribed lithium carbonate for the treatment of bipolar disorder.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者开具了碳酸锂用于治疗双相情感障碍。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Fine hand tremors, mild thirst, and nausea.","zh":"轻微手震颤、轻度口渴和恶心。"},{"id":"D","en":"Rapid weight gain and generalized edema.","zh":"体重快速增加和全身性水肿。"},{"id":"C","en":"Cardiovascular collapse, seizures, and severe oliguria.","zh":"心血管虚脱、癫痫发作和严重少尿。"},{"id":"A","en":"Coarse hand tremors, persistent gastrointestinal upset, and mental confusion.","zh":"粗大性手震颤、持续胃肠道不适和精神错乱。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fine hand tremors, mild thirst, and transient mild nausea are expected, common side effects of lithium therapy that occur at therapeutic levels (0.6-1.2 mEq/L). Early signs of actual lithium toxicity (levels 1.5-2.0 mEq/L) include coarse hand tremors, persistent diarrhea, vomiting, muscle weakness, and mild cognitive confusion. Severe toxicity (>2.0 mEq/L) leads to seizures, cardiovascular collapse, and multi-organ damage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"轻微手震颤、轻度口渴和一过性轻度恶心（A）是锂治疗在治疗浓度水平（0.6-1.2 mEq/L）下的预期、常见副作用。锂中毒的早期体征（浓度 1.5-2.0 mEq/L）包括粗大性手震颤、持续性腹泻、呕吐、肌无力和轻度认知错乱（B）。严重中毒（>2.0 mEq/L）可导致癫痫发作、心血管虚脱和多器官损伤（C）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between normal side effects (fine tremors) and toxic symptoms (coarse tremors, worsening confusion). Fine = Fine/Normal, Coarse = Complication/Toxic.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分正常的副作用（细微震颤）和中毒症状（粗大震颤、加重的认知障碍）。细（Fine）= 细小/正常，粗（Coarse）= 粗大/并发症/中毒。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":227,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_cloze_siadh_di_38","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.36.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,279],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,80],"fullStemEn":"A client who recently underwent transsphenoidal hypophysectomy for a pituitary tumor is being monitored by the nurse. The nurse notes that the client has developed polyuria, with a urine output of 500 mL/hr, and reports extreme thirst. The nurse suspects diabetes insipidus (DI).","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名因垂体瘤近期接受了经蝶骨窦垂体切除术的患者。护士注意到患者出现多尿，尿量达 500 毫升/小时，并诉极度口渴。护士怀疑患者发生了尿崩症（DI）。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse suspects diabetes insipidus (DI).","terminalSentenceZh":"护士怀疑患者发生了尿崩症（DI）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes that the client has developed polyuria, with a urine output of 500 mL/hr, and reports extreme thirst.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到患者出现多尿，尿量达 500 毫升/小时，并诉极度口渴。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse expects the client with diabetes insipidus to exhibit a {{1}} urine specific gravity and a {{2}} serum sodium level.","zh":"护士预计尿崩症患者会表现出 {{1}} 的尿比重和 {{2}} 的血清钠水平。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"high (increased)","zh":"升高（增高）"},{"id":"o1","en":"low (decreased)","zh":"降低（减低）"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"high (hypernatremia)","zh":"升高（高钠血症）"},{"id":"o1","en":"low (hyponatremia)","zh":"降低（低钠血症）"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Diabetes insipidus (DI) is caused by a deficiency of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), leading to the inability of kidneys to concentrate urine. This results in massive excretion of dilute urine with a low specific gravity (<1.005) (o1 for dropdown 1). Due to excessive water loss, the blood becomes concentrated, causing hypernatremia (high serum sodium >145 mEq/L) (o2 for dropdown 2). SIADH is the opposite (fluid retention, high urine specific gravity, dilutional hyponatremia).","rationaleCorrectZh":"尿崩症（DI）是由于抗利尿激素（ADH）缺乏引起的，导致肾脏无法浓缩尿液。这导致排出大量稀释的尿液，尿比重降低（<1.005）（下拉菜单1的o1）。由于水分过度流失，血液被浓缩，导致高钠血症（血清钠增高>145 mEq/L）（下拉菜单2的o2）。SIADH 则相反（液体潴留、高尿比重、稀释性低钠血症）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast DI and SIADH. DI = Dry Inside (high urine output, low urine specific gravity, dry/high blood sodium). SIADH = Soaked Inside (low urine output, high urine specific gravity, wet/low blood sodium).","testTakingStrategyZh":"对比 DI 和 SIADH。DI = 内部干燥（Dry Inside：高尿量、低尿比重、干燥/高血钠）。SIADH = 内部浸湿（Soaked Inside：低尿量、高尿比重、潮湿/低血钠）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":228,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_cushings_addisons_39","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.37.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,177],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results of a client with suspected Addison's disease (adrenal insufficiency). Which set of findings is most consistent with this diagnosis?","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名疑似艾迪生病（肾上腺皮质功能不全）患者的实验室检查结果。以下哪组结果与该诊断最吻合？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which set of findings is most consistent with this diagnosis?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪组结果与该诊断最吻合？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results of a client with suspected Addison's disease (adrenal insufficiency).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查一名疑似艾迪生病（肾上腺皮质功能不全）患者的实验室检查结果。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hypoglycemia, hypernatremia, and hyperkalemia","zh":"低血糖、高钠血症和高钾血症"},{"id":"B","en":"Hypoglycemia, hyponatremia, and hyperkalemia","zh":"低血糖、低钠血症和高钾血症"},{"id":"C","en":"Hyperglycemia, hyponatremia, and hypokalemia","zh":"高血糖、低钠血症 and 低钾血症"},{"id":"A","en":"Hyperglycemia, hypernatremia, and hypokalemia","zh":"高血糖、高钠血症和低钾血症"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Addison's disease is characterized by hyposecretion of adrenal hormones (aldosterone, cortisol). Deficiency of aldosterone causes loss of sodium (hyponatremia) and retention of potassium (hyperkalemia). Deficiency of cortisol leads to decreased gluconeogenesis, causing hypoglycemia. Cushing's syndrome represents the opposite state (excess cortisol/aldosterone leading to hypernatremia, hypokalemia, and hyperglycemia).","rationaleCorrectZh":"艾迪生病的特征是肾上腺激素（醛固酮、皮质醇）分泌不足。醛固酮缺乏导致钠流失（低钠血症）和钾潴留（高钾血症）。皮质醇缺乏导致糖异生减少，引起低血糖（B）。库欣综合征代表相反的状态（皮质醇/醛固酮过多，导致高钠血症、低钾血症和高血糖）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the role of aldosterone: it normally saves sodium and excretes potassium. In Addison's (insufficiency), the lack of aldosterone leads to the exact opposite: low sodium (hyponatremia) and high potassium (hyperkalemia).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住醛固酮的作用：它通常保留钠并排泄钾。在艾迪生病（不足）中，缺乏醛固酮会导致完全相反的结果：低钠（低钠血症）和高钾（高钾血症）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results of a client with suspected Addison's disease (adrenal insufficiency).","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在审查一名疑似艾迪生病（肾上腺皮质功能不全）患者的实验室检查结果。"}
{"queueIndex":229,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_thyroid_storm_40","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.38.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,84],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with thyroid storm (thyrotoxic crisis) secondary to Graves' disease. The client has a heart rate of 160/min and a temperature of 104.2 °F (40.1 °C). Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因 Graves 病继发甲状腺危象（甲亢危象）入院。患者的心率为 160 次/分，体温为 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)。请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列下列护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has a heart rate of 160/min and a temperature of 104.2 °F (40.1 °C).","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的心率为 160 次/分，体温为 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer the prescribed beta-blocker (e.g., propranolol) intravenously.","zh":"静脉注射开具的 β 受体阻滞剂（如普萘洛尔）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer prescribed antithyroid medications (e.g., propylthiouracil or methimazole).","zh":"给予开具的抗甲状腺药物（如丙硫氧嘧啶或甲巯咪唑）。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain a patent airway and administer high-flow oxygen.","zh":"保持气道通畅，并给予高流量氧气。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply cooling blankets and administer acetaminophen for hyperthermia.","zh":"使用降温毯，并给予对乙酰氨基酚治疗高热。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In thyroid storm, oxygenation and airway are the first priority. Cardiopulmonary stabilization using IV beta-blockers is performed next to rapidly control extreme tachycardia and block peripheral conversion of T4 to T3. Antithyroid drugs are administered to block new hormone synthesis. Symptom management for hyperthermia is performed alongside these steps. Note: Aspirin is contraindicated for hyperthermia as it displaces thyroid hormone from binding proteins.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在甲状腺危象中，给氧和气道通畅（A）是首要任务。接下来使用静脉注射 β 受体阻滞剂（B）进行心肺功能稳定，以快速控制极度心动过速并阻断外周 T4 向 T3 的转化。给予抗甲状腺药物（C）以阻断新激素的合成。针对高热的症状管理（D）与这些步骤一起进行。注意：高热时禁用阿司匹林，因为它会使甲状腺激素从结合蛋白中游离出来。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use ABCs first. Airway/Oxygen comes before medications. Cardiopulmonary stabilization (beta-blocker) takes precedence over hormonal blockade. Remember: NEVER give aspirin to a client with thyroid storm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先使用 ABC 原则。气道/吸氧优于药物。心肺功能稳定（β受体阻滞剂）优先于阻断激素合成。记住：切勿给甲状腺危象患者服用阿司匹林。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client has a heart rate of 160/min and a temperature of 104.2 °F (40.1 °C).","controlSentenceZh":"患者的心率为 160 次/分，体温为 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)。"}
{"queueIndex":230,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_pacemaker_41","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.39.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge education to a client who recently had a permanent cardiac pacemaker implanted. Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名近期植入了永久性心脏起搏器的患者提供出院指导。护士应该包括哪些指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应该包括哪些指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Carry a pacemaker identification card at all times.","zh":"始终随身携带起搏器标识卡。"},{"id":"A","en":"Avoid lifting the arm on the pacemaker side above shoulder level for 4 weeks.","zh":"术后4周内避免将起搏器侧的手臂抬高至肩膀水平以上。"},{"id":"C","en":"It is safe to undergo a standard magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scan without special device clearance.","zh":"无需对设备进行特殊确认，就可以安全接受标准核磁共振成像（MRI）检查。"},{"id":"E","en":"Avoid standing near anti-theft security systems in stores for prolonged periods.","zh":"避免长时间站在商店的防盗安全系统附近。"},{"id":"D","en":"Take and record the pulse rate daily for 1 full minute.","zh":"每日测量并记录脉搏率，持续整1分钟。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pacemaker precautions include avoiding shoulder extension (lifting the arm above the shoulder, A) to prevent lead dislodgement, carrying an ID card, checking the pulse daily, and avoiding prolonged exposure near anti-theft systems (E). MRI is not automatically safe after pacemaker implantation; some devices are MRI-conditional, but MRI requires device-specific clearance, appropriate programming, monitoring, and facility protocol. Therefore, stating that MRI is safe without device-specific clearance is not an appropriate discharge instruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"起搏器防范措施包括避免肩部过度伸展（将起搏器侧手臂抬高超过肩部，A）以防导线移位，随身携带起搏器识别卡（B），每日测量脉搏（D），以及避免长时间停留在防盗系统附近（E）。植入起搏器后 MRI 并非自动安全；有些设备属于 MRI 条件兼容型，但接受 MRI 前必须进行设备特异性确认、适当程控、监测，并遵循机构流程。因此，告知患者无需特殊设备评估即可安全进行 MRI 检查不是恰当的出院指导。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For implanted devices, avoid absolute assumptions. Pacemaker clients should get device-specific clearance before MRI, and early postoperative teaching focuses on preventing lead displacement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到植入设备时，避免绝对化假设。起搏器患者接受 MRI 前应进行设备特异性确认；术后早期教育重点是防止导线移位。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应该包括哪些指导？"}
{"queueIndex":231,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_ect_prep_42","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.40.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,46],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing a client for electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) scheduled in the morning. Which action should the nurse include in the client's pre-procedure care?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名将在上午接受电休克治疗（ECT）的患者做准备。护士在术前护理中应包括哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse include in the client's pre-procedure care?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在术前护理中应包括哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing a client for electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) scheduled in the morning.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名将在上午接受电休克治疗（ECT）的患者做准备。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the client to drink water right up until the procedure to prevent hypotension.","zh":"鼓励患者在手术前一直喝水，以防低血压。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure the client remains NPO (nothing by mouth) for 6 to 8 hours before the procedure.","zh":"确保患者在术前禁食（NPO）6 至 8 小时。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the prescribed anticonvulsant medication with a sip of water.","zh":"给患者服用开具的抗癫痫药物（抗惊厥药），喝一口水送服。"},{"id":"B","en":"Apply hair gel or spray to secure the electrodes to the scalp.","zh":"使用发胶或发喷，以将电极牢固固定在头皮上。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ECT requires general anesthesia and a muscle relaxant. Therefore, the client must remain NPO (nothing by mouth) for at least 6 to 8 hours before the procedure to prevent aspiration. Anticonvulsant medications should be withheld before ECT because they raise the seizure threshold, making the treatment ineffective. Hair must be clean and dry without gel/sprays to prevent burns. Drinking water right before violates the NPO status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ECT 需要全身麻醉和肌肉松弛剂。因此，患者在术前必须禁食（NPO）至少 6 至 8 小时（A）以防误吸。术前应暂停使用抗惊厥药物（C），因为它们会升高抽搐阈值，使治疗失效。头发必须清洁、干燥，不能使用发胶/喷雾（D）以防灼伤。术前直接饮水（B）违反了禁食规定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Understand that ECT involves inducing a controlled seizure under anesthesia. Anything that prevents seizures (anticonvulsants) or compromises anesthesia safety (violating NPO) must be avoided.","testTakingStrategyZh":"理解 ECT 涉及在麻醉下诱导控制性抽搐。任何阻止抽搐发生（抗惊厥药）或损害麻醉安全（违反禁食）的事情都必须避免。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":232,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_ocd_interventions_43","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.41.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[214,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,69],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD) who has a ritual of washing hands for 15 minutes before every meal. Which interventions should the nurse include in the client's care plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名患有强迫症（OCD）的患者，该患者习惯在每餐前洗手 15 分钟。护士应在患者的护理计划中纳入哪些干预措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the client's care plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在患者的护理计划中纳入哪些干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Teach the client alternative coping mechanisms, such as deep breathing or guided imagery.","zh":"向患者传授其他应对机制，如深呼吸或引导想象。"},{"id":"B","en":"Allow the client sufficient time for the ritual early in the treatment.","zh":"在治疗初期，为患者的仪式保留足够的时间。"},{"id":"C","en":"Help the client identify triggers that increase anxiety and the need for rituals.","zh":"帮助患者识别增加焦虑和对仪式需求的触发因素。"},{"id":"A","en":"Prevent the client from performing the handwashing ritual immediately upon admission.","zh":"在入院时立即强行阻止患者进行洗手仪式。"},{"id":"D","en":"Gradually limit the time allowed for the ritualistic behavior in collaboration with the client.","zh":"与患者合作，逐步限制允许进行仪式性行为的时间。"}],"correct":["B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Initially, preventing rituals causes severe panic and escalation of anxiety, so the nurse should allow time for the ritual early in treatment. The goal is to gradually limit the time while teaching coping skills (E) and identifying triggers. Gradually reducing the time is a key component of systematic desensitization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最初强行阻止仪式（A）会引起严重的恐慌和焦虑加剧，因此护士在治疗初期应允许仪式时间（B）。目标是逐步限制时间（D），同时教授应对技巧（E）并识别诱因（C）。逐步减少时间是系统脱敏疗法的关键组成部分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid extreme, sudden clinical actions. Preventing a ritual immediately is too abrupt and harmful. Choose options that reflect gradual limits, collaboration, and teaching replacement coping mechanisms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"避免极端的、突然的临床行动。立即强行阻止仪式太突然且有害。选择反映逐步限制、合作和教授替代应对机制的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":233,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_gerd_lifestyle_44","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.42.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[183,205],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,62],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client diagnosed with gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) about lifestyle modifications to reduce symptoms. Which recommendations should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名诊断为胃食管反流病（GERD）的患者如何通过生活方式的调整来减轻症状。护士应该包括哪些建议？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which recommendations should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应该包括哪些建议？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Avoid eating within 3 hours of bedtime.","zh":"睡前 3 小时内避免进食。"},{"id":"D","en":"Limit intake of caffeine, chocolate, and peppermint.","zh":"限制咖啡因、巧克力和薄荷的摄入。"},{"id":"E","en":"Lie down and rest for 30 minutes after eating a large meal.","zh":"饱餐后躺下休息 30 分钟。"},{"id":"B","en":"Elevate the head of the bed by 6 to 8 inches using blocks.","zh":"使用床垫垫高块将床头抬高 6 到 8 英寸。"},{"id":"C","en":"Consume small, frequent meals rather than large ones.","zh":"少食多餐，而不是暴饮暴食。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"GERD lifestyle modifications focus on preventing acid reflux. This includes remaining upright after eating (avoiding lying down for at least 2 hours after meals, making E incorrect), not eating near bedtime, elevating the head of the bed to let gravity keep acid down, eating small meals to avoid gastric distention, and avoiding foods that relax the lower esophageal sphincter (LES) such as caffeine, chocolate, and peppermint.","rationaleCorrectZh":"GERD 的生活方式调整侧重于预防酸反流。这包括在进食后保持直立（饭后至少2小时内避免躺下，故E错误）、临睡前不吃东西（A）、抬高床头（B）利用重力阻止酸上升、少食多餐（C）以避免胃部过度充盈，以及避免食用降低食管下括约肌（LES）张力的食物，如咖啡因、巧克力和薄荷（D）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use basic gravity principles. Lying down after eating (E) is counterproductive to preventing reflux. Always recommend remaining upright and avoiding late meals.","testTakingStrategyZh":"利用基本的重力原理。饭后躺下（E）对预防反流起反作用。始终建议保持直立并避免太晚进食。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":234,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_appendicitis_45","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.43.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,281],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,135],"fullStemEn":"A client presents to the emergency department with acute lower abdominal pain. The nurse performs an assessment to evaluate for acute appendicitis. For each diagnostic sign, click to specify if the description matches the Rovsing sign, Obturator sign, Psoas sign, or McBurney sign.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因急性下腹部疼痛到急诊科就诊。护士进行评估以筛查急性阑尾炎。对于每个诊断性体征，点击以指定该描述是符合罗夫辛征（Rovsing sign）、闭孔内肌征（Obturator sign）、腰大肌征（Psoas sign）还是麦氏点压痛（McBurney sign）。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each diagnostic sign, click to specify if the description matches the Rovsing sign, Obturator sign, Psoas sign, or McBurney sign.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个诊断性体征，点击以指定该描述是符合罗夫辛征（Rovsing sign）、闭孔内肌征（Obturator sign）、腰大肌征（Psoas sign）还是麦氏点压痛（McBurney sign）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse performs an assessment to evaluate for acute appendicitis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士进行评估以筛查急性阑尾炎。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Pain elicited in the right lower quadrant when palpation pressure is applied to the left lower quadrant.","zh":"按压左下腹时，右下腹产生疼痛。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Severe tenderness elicited upon palpation at a point two-thirds of the distance from the umbilicus to the right anterior superior iliac spine.","zh":"按压脐与右髂前上棘连线中外1/3交界处时产生严重压痛。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Pain elicited in the right lower quadrant when the client's right hip and knee are flexed and the hip is internally rotated.","zh":"弯曲患者右髋和右膝并内旋右髋时，右下腹产生疼痛。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Pain elicited in the right lower quadrant when the client's right hip is passively extended while lying on their left side.","zh":"患者左侧卧位时被动伸展右髋，右下腹产生疼痛。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"McBurney Sign","zh":"麦氏点压痛"},{"id":"c1","en":"Rovsing Sign","zh":"罗夫辛征（结肠充气试验）"},{"id":"c3","en":"Obturator Sign","zh":"闭孔内肌征"},{"id":"c4","en":"Psoas Sign","zh":"腰大肌征"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Palpating the LLQ causing RLQ pain is Rovsing sign (r1). McBurney point tenderness is located two-thirds from the umbilicus to the right anterior superior iliac spine (r2). Flexion and internal rotation of the hip causing pain is Obturator sign (r3), indicating pelvic appendix irritation. Passive extension of the hip causing pain is Psoas sign (r4), indicating retrocecal appendix irritation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"按压左下腹引起右下腹痛为罗夫辛征（r1）。麦氏点压痛位于脐与髂前上棘连线中外1/3交界处（r2）。屈曲并内旋髋关节引起疼痛为闭孔内肌征（r3），提示盆腔位阑尾炎。被动伸展髋关节引起疼痛为腰大肌征（r4），提示盲肠后位阑尾炎。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate movement types: Internal rotation = Obturator muscle/sign. Extension of hip = Psoas muscle/sign. Pressing opposite side = Rovsing sign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"联系动作类型：内旋 = 闭孔肌/征。伸展髋关节 = 腰大肌/征。按压对侧 = 罗夫辛征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":235,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_ibd_diet_46","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.44.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,56],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the medical unit during an acute flare-up of ulcerative colitis. The client reports frequent bloody diarrhea and abdominal cramping. Which dietary prescription is most appropriate for the nurse to implement?","fullStemZh":"一名溃疡性结肠炎急性发作期的患者入住内科病房。患者诉频繁出现血性腹泻和腹部绞痛。护士应实施哪项最合适的饮食医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which dietary prescription is most appropriate for the nurse to implement?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪项最合适的饮食医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports frequent bloody diarrhea and abdominal cramping.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者诉频繁出现血性腹泻和腹部绞痛。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Low-residue, high-protein, high-calorie diet.","zh":"低渣、高蛋白、高热量饮食。"},{"id":"C","en":"Low-protein, high-residue diet with restricted fluids.","zh":"限制液体的低蛋白、高渣饮食。"},{"id":"A","en":"Regular diet with raw fruits and nuts.","zh":"包含新鲜水果和坚果的普通饮食。"},{"id":"D","en":"High-fiber diet with plenty of raw vegetables.","zh":"富含大量生蔬菜的高纤维饮食。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During an acute flare-up of ulcerative colitis, the bowel is inflamed and hypermotile. The patient requires a low-residue (low-fiber) diet to minimize bowel irritation, decrease stool volume, and promote healing. To address malnutrition and muscle wasting caused by protein loss and malabsorption, a high-protein, high-calorie diet is essential. High-fiber foods are contraindicated during flare-ups as they exacerbate symptoms.","rationaleCorrectZh":"溃疡性结肠炎急性发作期，肠道有炎症且蠕动亢进。患者需要低渣（低纤维）饮食（B），以最大程度减少肠道刺激、减少粪便体积并促进愈合。为解决因蛋白质丢失和吸收不良引起的营养不良和肌肉萎缩，高蛋白、高热量饮食是必不可少的。在发作期，禁食高纤维食物（A, C, D），因为它们会加重症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the principles of bowel rest during acute inflammation. Minimize irritation by selecting low-residue (low-fiber) options. Supplement loss of protein and calories from chronic diarrhea.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想急性炎症期间让肠道休息的原则。通过选择低渣（低纤维）选项来最大程度地减少刺激。补充慢性腹泻流失的蛋白质和热量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":236,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_fib_parkland_burn_47","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.45.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[352,393],"terminalOffsetsZh":[107,120],"fullStemEn":"An adult client weighing 176 lbs has sustained second- and third-degree burns covering 30% of the total body surface area (TBSA). The nurse uses the Parkland formula to calculate fluid resuscitation. How many mL of lactated Ringer's solution should the nurse administer during the first 8 hours of resuscitation? (Record your answer as a whole number. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"一名体重为 176 磅的成年患者遭受了覆盖全身总表面积（TBSA）30% 的二度和三度烧伤。护士使用 Parkland 公式计算液体复苏量。护士在复苏的前 8 小时内应给予多少毫升的乳酸林格氏液？（以整数记录答案。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以整数记录答案。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["4800"],"numeric":{"value":4800,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1: Convert weight from lbs to kg: 176 lbs / 2.2 = 80 kg. Step 2: Use the Parkland formula (4 mL * kg * %TBSA) to find total 24-hour fluid: 4 mL * 80 kg * 30 = 9,600 mL. Step 3: Calculate the volume for the first 8 hours, which is half of the 24-hour total: 9,600 mL / 2 = 4,800 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步：将体重从磅转换为千克：176 lbs / 2.2 = 80 kg。第二步：使用 Parkland 公式（4 mL * kg * %TBSA）计算 24 小时总补液量：4 mL * 80 kg * 30 = 9,600 毫升。第三步：计算前 8 小时内的补液量，为 24 小时总量的一半：9,600 mL / 2 = 4,800 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always check weight conversion first (lbs to kg). Calculate the total 24-hour volume using Parkland (4 mL * kg * TBSA%). Finally, divide by 2 to find the volume for the first 8 hours.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终先检查体重转换（磅至千克）。使用 Parkland 公式（4 mL * kg * TBSA%）计算 24 小时总容积。最后，除以 2 得到前 8 小时的输液量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":237,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_cloze_glaucoma_48","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.46.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,43],"fullStemEn":"A client is presenting to the ophthalmology clinic with progressive vision loss. The nurse performs an assessment to differentiate between cataracts and primary open-angle glaucoma.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因渐进性视力下降到眼科诊所就诊。护士进行评估以鉴别白内障与原发性开角型青光眼。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse performs an assessment to differentiate between cataracts and primary open-angle glaucoma.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士进行评估以鉴别白内障与原发性开角型青光眼。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is presenting to the ophthalmology clinic with progressive vision loss.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因渐进性视力下降到眼科诊所就诊。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize that cataracts cause a gradual, painless {{1}} of vision, while primary open-angle glaucoma is characterized by a gradual, painless {{2}}.","zh":"护士应认识到，白内障会导致渐进、无痛性的 {{1}}，而原发性开角型青光眼的特征是渐进、无痛性的 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"loss of peripheral vision","zh":"周边视力丧失（管状视野）"},{"id":"o1","en":"blurring or cloudiness","zh":"视物模糊或浑浊"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"blurring or cloudiness","zh":"视物模糊或浑浊"},{"id":"o2","en":"loss of peripheral vision","zh":"周边视力丧失（管状视野）"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cataracts are caused by opacity of the lens, which blocks light entry and causes generalized blurring or cloudiness (o1 for dropdown 1). Primary open-angle glaucoma is caused by increased intraocular pressure damaging the optic nerve, leading to progressive tunnel vision or loss of peripheral vision (o2 for dropdown 2).","rationaleCorrectZh":"白内障是由于晶状体浑浊引起的，阻挡了光线进入，导致普遍的视物模糊或浑浊（下拉菜单1的o1）。原发性开角型青光眼是由于眼压增高损伤视神经引起的，导致渐进性管状视野或周边视力丧失（下拉菜单2的o2）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate cataracts with lens opacity (leading to blurred vision) and glaucoma with high pressure/optic nerve damage (leading to peripheral field loss/tunnel vision).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将白内障与晶状体浑浊（导致视物模糊）联系起来，将青光眼与高眼压/视神经损伤（导致周边视野缺失/管状视野）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":238,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_sata_joint_protection_49","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.47.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,53],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client with rheumatoid arthritis (RA) about joint protection and energy conservation techniques. Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名类风湿关节炎（RA）患者关于关节保护和能量保存的技术。护士应包括哪些指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use the fingers and knuckles to push up when rising from a chair.","zh":"从椅子上站起时，用手指和指关节向上推。"},{"id":"E","en":"Turn doorknobs and jar lids toward the pinky finger (ulnar side).","zh":"朝小指侧（尺侧）转动门把手和罐头盖。"},{"id":"A","en":"Carry objects close to the body and slide them instead of lifting.","zh":"将物品贴近身体携带，并尽可能滑行移动而不是提起。"},{"id":"C","en":"Select utensils, pens, and tools with built-up, larger handles.","zh":"选择手柄加粗、较大的餐具、笔和工具。"},{"id":"D","en":"Carry a shoulder bag on the shoulder rather than holding a handbag by the fingers.","zh":"把单肩包挎在肩膀上，而不是用手指提着手提包。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use warm baths or showers in the morning to decrease joint stiffness.","zh":"早晨进行温水浴或淋浴以减轻关节僵硬。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Joint protection aims to minimize stress on affected joints, avoid ulnar deviation, and use larger muscle groups. Sliding items, using built-up handles, carrying bags on the shoulder, and applying morning heat (F) are all indicated. Using fingers to push up from a chair and turning knobs toward the ulnar side (E) increase stress and promote deformities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关节保护旨在最大限度地减少受累关节的压力，避免尺侧偏斜，并使用较大的肌群。滑动滑行物品（A）、使用加粗手柄（C）、肩膀挎包（D）以及早晨热敷（F）都是适应证。用手指支撑起立（B）以及向小指（尺侧）旋转把手（E）会增加关节应力并促进畸形形成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for options that emphasize using larger joints, avoiding twisting motions that force the fingers toward the pinky side, and using heat for morning stiffness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找强调使用大关节、避免迫使手指朝向小指侧的扭转动作以及利用热敷缓解早晨僵硬的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":239,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_hip_precautions_50","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.48.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[123,260],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,78],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who is postoperative day 1 following a total hip arthroplasty using a posterior approach. For each nursing intervention, specify whether the action is indicated (appropriate) or contraindicated (harmful) for this client's care.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）术后第1天的患者。对于以下每项护理措施，请选择该操作对该患者的护理是属于“适应证”（合适）还是“禁忌证”（有害）。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing intervention, specify whether the action is indicated (appropriate) or contraindicated (harmful) for this client's care.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于以下每项护理措施，请选择该操作对该患者的护理是属于“适应证”（合适）还是“禁忌证”（有害）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who is postoperative day 1 following a total hip arthroplasty using a posterior approach.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）术后第1天的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Place an abduction wedge or pillow between the client's legs when in bed.","zh":"患者在床上时，在其两腿之间放置外展楔或外展枕。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Assist the client to lean forward and tie their shoes before ambulating.","zh":"协助患者向前倾身并在下床活动前系鞋带。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Instruct the client to cross their legs at the ankles when sitting in a chair.","zh":"指导患者在椅子上坐着时，在踝关节处交叉双腿。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Keep the head of the bed elevated at 45 to 60 degrees during meals.","zh":"进餐时将床头抬高 45 至 60 度。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Use a raised toilet seat for the client's bathroom use.","zh":"使用加高座便器供患者上厕所。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Indicated","zh":"适应证"},{"id":"c2","en":"Contraindicated","zh":"禁忌证"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To prevent dislocation after a posterior-approach total hip arthroplasty, the client must avoid hip flexion >90 degrees, adduction (crossing midline), and internal rotation. Placing an abduction wedge (r1) and using a raised toilet seat (r5) prevent adduction and flexion. Elevating the head of bed to 45-60 degrees (r4) is safe because it is <90 degrees. Bending forward to tie shoes (r2) and crossing legs (r3) violate these precautions and are contraindicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为了预防全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）术后的关节脱位，患者必须避免髋关节屈曲超过90度、内收（交叉过中线）和内旋。放置外展楔（r1）和使用加高座便器（r5）可防止内收和过度屈曲。将床头抬高45-60度（r4）是安全的，因为小于90度。向前倾身系鞋带（r2）和交叉双腿（r3）违反了这些预防措施，属于禁忌证。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize the angles and movements. Any action that bends the hip past a right angle (90 degrees) or brings the legs together/crossed is contraindicated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象角度和运动。任何弯曲髋关节超过直角（90度）或使双腿靠拢/交叉的动作都是禁忌证。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":240,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_trach_suction_51","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.49","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.49.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.49.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,52],"fullStemEn":"A client with a tracheostomy has thick, copious secretions and requires suctioning. Put the nurse's actions in the correct chronological order.","fullStemZh":"一名配有气管套管的患者气道内有大量粘稠分泌物，需要进行吸痰。请将护士的护理操作按正确的先后顺序进行排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Put the nurse's actions in the correct chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的护理操作按正确的先后顺序进行排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a tracheostomy has thick, copious secretions and requires suctioning.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名配有气管套管的患者气道内有大量粘稠分泌物，需要进行吸痰。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Insert the suction catheter gently into the tracheostomy until resistance is met.","zh":"将吸痰管轻轻插入气管套管，直至遇到阻力。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hyperoxygenate the client with 100% oxygen.","zh":"用 100% 氧气对患者进行过度给氧。"},{"id":"E","en":"Auscultate lung sounds and reassess the client's oxygen saturation.","zh":"听诊肺部音并重新评估患者的血氧饱和度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply intermittent suction and rotate the catheter while withdrawing it over 10-15 seconds.","zh":"施加间歇性负压，并在 10-15 秒内旋转吸痰管将其缓慢退出。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene and don sterile gloves.","zh":"进行手卫生并戴上无菌手套。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence for tracheostomy suctioning begins with performing hand hygiene and donning sterile gloves to maintain asepsis. The nurse then hyperoxygenates the client to prevent hypoxemia during the procedure. The catheter is inserted gently without suction until resistance is met or the client coughs. Intermittent suction is applied while withdrawing and rotating the catheter to prevent mucosal damage, limiting suction to 10-15 seconds. Finally, the nurse auscultates the lungs to evaluate the effectiveness of the suctioning and checks oxygen saturation (E).","rationaleCorrectZh":"气管套管吸痰的正确顺序是：首先进行手卫生并戴上无菌手套以维持无菌操作（A）。随后，护士对患者进行过度给氧以预防吸痰过程中的低氧血症（B）。在不施加负压的情况下，轻轻插入吸痰管直到遇到阻力或患者咳嗽（C）。在缓慢退出吸痰管时进行间歇性抽吸并旋转吸痰管，以防粘膜损伤，时间限制在10-15秒内（D）。最后，护士听诊肺部评估吸痰效果，并检查血氧饱和度（E）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Order actions logically: prioritize safety and sterile technique (prep first), prepare the patient (hyperoxygenate), perform the core action (insert then withdraw), and evaluate results (auscultate).","testTakingStrategyZh":"按逻辑排列操作：优先考虑安全和无菌技术（先准备），准备好患者（过度给氧），执行核心操作（先插入后退出），并评估结果（听诊）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":241,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_schizo_boundary_52","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.50.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,259],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,67],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with schizophrenia who is experiencing persecutory delusions. The client points to the medication cup and says, 'This pill is poison! You and the doctors are trying to kill me!' Which response by the nurse is most therapeutic?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名患有精神分裂症并伴有被害妄想的患者。患者指向药杯并说：“这颗药是毒药！你和医生想杀了我！”护士的哪项回应最具有治疗性？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is most therapeutic?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项回应最具有治疗性？","penultimateSentenceEn":"You and the doctors are trying to kill me!'","penultimateSentenceZh":"你和医生想杀了我！”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"If you don't take your medicine, I will have to notify your doctor and document that you are non-compliant.","zh":"如果您不吃药，我将不得不通知您的医生，并记录您不服从治疗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Why would we want to kill you? We have been taking care of you for three days without any issues.","zh":"我们为什么要杀您？我们已经照顾您三天了，没出过任何问题。"},{"id":"D","en":"No one here is trying to kill you. We are healthcare professionals who are bound by law to help you.","zh":"这里没有人想杀您。我们是医护人员，法律规定我们要帮助您。"},{"id":"A","en":"I know you are feeling frightened, but this is your daily blood pressure medicine. I am here to keep you safe.","zh":"我知道您感到害怕，但这是您每天服用的血压药。我在这里是为了保证您的安全。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When a client has persecutory delusions, the nurse should validate the client's feelings of fear (validating emotion) without reinforcing or validating the delusion itself. Reassuring safety and presenting reality calmly is the most therapeutic approach. Defensive statements, challenging questions, or threats escalate client anxiety and destroy therapeutic trust.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当患者存在被害妄想时，护士应确认患者害怕的感受（确认情感），而不要强化或承认妄想本身。冷静地提供安全保证并呈现现实（B）是最具治疗性的方法。防御性陈述（A）、挑战性提问（C）或威胁（D）会加剧患者焦虑并破坏治疗性信任关系。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Rule out answers that argue with, challenge, or support the delusion. Choose the response that focuses on the feeling/emotion behind the delusion and provides safety reassurance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除争论、挑战或支持妄想的选项。选择着眼于妄想背后的感受/情绪并提供安全保证的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":242,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_fib_heparin_calc_53","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.51","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.51.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.51.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[315,356],"terminalOffsetsZh":[132,145],"fullStemEn":"A client with deep vein thrombosis is prescribed a continuous heparin infusion. The order is to infuse heparin at a rate of 1,200 units/hour. The IV bag contains heparin 25,000 units in 250 mL of 0.9% normal saline. At how many mL/hour should the nurse set the infusion pump? (Record your answer as a whole number. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"一名患有深静脉血栓的患者被开具了持续静脉输注肝素的医嘱。医嘱要求以 1,200 单位/小时的速率输注肝素。输液袋中含有 25,000 单位的肝素溶于 250 毫升 0.9% 生理盐水中。护士应将输液泵的流速设置为多少毫升/小时（mL/hour）？（以整数记录答案。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以整数记录答案。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/小时"},"acceptable":["12"],"numeric":{"value":12,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1: Calculate the concentration of heparin per mL: 25,000 units / 250 mL = 100 units/mL. Step 2: Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hour: 1,200 units/hour / 100 units/mL = 12 mL/hour.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步：计算每毫升溶液中所含的肝素单位数（浓度）：25,000 单位 / 250 毫升 = 100 单位/毫升。第二步：计算每小时输注的毫升数（流速）：1,200 单位/小时 / 100 单位/毫升 = 12 毫升/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the standard formula for IV rate: (Desired units/hr / Available units) * Available volume (mL). Verify the units match before computing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住静脉输液流速的标准公式：(所需单位/小时 / 可得单位) * 可得体积(mL)。计算前确认单位匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":243,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_mc_pad_care_54","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.52.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,58],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge teaching to a client newly diagnosed with peripheral arterial disease (PAD). Which statement by the client indicates a correct understanding of the home care instructions?","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名新诊断为外周动脉疾病（PAD）的患者进行出院指导。患者的哪项陈述表明其正确理解了出院后的家庭护理指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the client indicates a correct understanding of the home care instructions?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者的哪项陈述表明其正确理解了出院后的家庭护理指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing discharge teaching to a client newly diagnosed with peripheral arterial disease (PAD).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在对一名新诊断为外周动脉疾病（PAD）的患者进行出院指导。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"I will wear tight-fitting support stockings to improve blood flow in my legs.","zh":"我会穿紧身弹力袜以改善腿部的血流。"},{"id":"A","en":"I should apply a heating pad to my feet every night to keep them warm.","zh":"我应该每天晚上在脚上用电热垫，以保持双脚温暖。"},{"id":"D","en":"I should avoid crossing my legs at the knees when sitting.","zh":"我坐着时应该避免在膝盖处跷二郎腿。"},{"id":"B","en":"I will elevate my legs above the level of my heart when sitting in my recliner.","zh":"当我坐在躺椅上时，我会把腿抬高到高于心脏水平的位置。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In peripheral arterial disease (PAD), blood flow to the lower extremities is impaired. Actions that cause vasoconstriction or mechanical obstruction to blood flow must be avoided. Crossing legs at the knees restricts arterial flow and is contraindicated. Applying heat directly is dangerous because of decreased sensation. Elevating legs above heart level decreases gravity-assisted blood flow, worsening ischemia. Tight support stockings are used for venous disease but restrict arterial flow in PAD.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在外周动脉疾病（PAD）中，下肢血流受损。必须避免引起血管收缩或对血流产生机械性阻碍的动作。坐着时跷二郎腿（D）会限制动脉血流，是禁忌动作。直接使用热敷（A）由于患者感觉减退而非常危险。将双腿抬高到心脏水平以上（B）会减少重力辅助的血流，加重缺血。紧身弹力袜（C）用于静脉疾病，但在PAD中会限制动脉血流。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For PAD, think 'keep blood flowing DOWN' (dependent position) and protect from trauma/burns. Contrast this with venous disease (where elevation and compression are indicated).","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于外周动脉疾病，应考虑“保持血液向下流动”（低垂体位）并防止外伤/烫伤。将其与静脉疾病相区分（静脉疾病需要抬高和压迫）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":244,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_cloze_croup_55","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.53","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.53.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.53.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,149],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,46],"fullStemEn":"A 2-year-old child is brought to the emergency department with a harsh, barking cough, inspiratory stridor, and mild intercostal retractions at rest.","fullStemZh":"一名2岁儿童因出现刺耳的犬吠样咳嗽、吸气性喉鸣以及静息状态下轻度肋间凹陷而被送往急诊科就诊。","terminalSentenceEn":"A 2-year-old child is brought to the emergency department with a harsh, barking cough, inspiratory stridor, and mild intercostal retractions at rest.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名2岁儿童因出现刺耳的犬吠样咳嗽、吸气性喉鸣以及静息状态下轻度肋间凹陷而被送往急诊科就诊。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize that these findings are characteristic of {{1}}, and prioritize the administration of {{2}} to reduce airway inflammation.","zh":"护士应认识到这些发现是 {{1}} 的特征，并优先给予 {{2}} 以减轻气道炎症。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"bronchiolitis due to RSV","zh":"RSV引起的毛细支气管炎"},{"id":"o1","en":"laryngotracheobronchitis (croup)","zh":"喉气管支气管炎（哮吼）"},{"id":"o2","en":"acute epiglottitis","zh":"急性会厌炎"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"intravenous ampicillin","zh":"静脉注射氨苄西林"},{"id":"o2","en":"oral or intramuscular dexamethasone","zh":"口服或肌内注射地塞米松"},{"id":"o1","en":"nebulized albuterol","zh":"雾化沙丁胺醇"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Laryngotracheobronchitis (croup) is characterized by viral inflammation of the larynx, trachea, and bronchi, presenting with a barking cough and inspiratory stridor (o1 for dropdown 1). Corticosteroids like dexamethasone (o2 for dropdown 2) are the cornerstone of therapy to reduce subglottic swelling and inflammation. Acute epiglottitis lacks a barking cough and requires urgent intubation prep. RSV bronchiolitis causes expiratory wheezing rather than upper airway stridor.","rationaleCorrectZh":"喉气管支气管炎（哮吼）是以喉、气管和支气管的病毒性炎症为特征，表现为犬吠样咳嗽和吸气性喉鸣（下拉菜单1的o1）。像地塞米松这样的糖皮质激素（下拉菜单2的o2）是治疗的基石，可减轻声门下水肿和炎症。急性会厌炎没有犬吠样咳嗽，且需要紧急气道保护准备。RSV引起的毛细支气管炎导致呼气性哮鸣音，而不是上呼吸道喉鸣。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate viral croup (barking cough, low grade fever) from acute epiglottitis (drooling, high fever, toxic appearance, no barking cough). Corticosteroids are key for croup airway swelling.","testTakingStrategyZh":"鉴别病毒性哮吼（犬吠样咳嗽、低热）与急性会厌炎（流涎、高热、面色中毒病容、无犬吠样咳嗽）。糖皮质激素是缓解哮吼气道水肿的关键。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":245,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_or_ppe_donning_56","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.54.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[100,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,59],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client who requires airborne and contact precautions. Place the nurse's steps for donning personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct chronological order.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备进入一名需要空气传播和接触预防措施患者的病房。请将护士穿戴个人防护装备（PPE）的步骤按正确的先后顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's steps for donning personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士穿戴个人防护装备（PPE）的步骤按正确的先后顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client who requires airborne and contact precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备进入一名需要空气传播和接触预防措施患者的病房。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Put on the gown.","zh":"穿上隔离衣。"},{"id":"E","en":"Put on the gloves.","zh":"戴上手套。"},{"id":"D","en":"Put on the goggles or face shield.","zh":"戴上护目镜或面罩。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene.","zh":"进行手卫生。"},{"id":"C","en":"Put on the mask or respirator (N95).","zh":"戴上口罩或呼吸防护器（N95）。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to CDC guidelines, the correct sequence for donning PPE is: 1. Hand hygiene is performed to prevent contamination. 2. The gown is put on first to cover the torso. 3. The mask or respirator is secured next. 4. Goggles or a face shield are applied to protect the eyes. 5. Gloves (E) are donned last, extending to cover the cuffs of the gown.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据美国CDC指南，穿戴个人防护装备（PPE）的正确顺序是：1. 进行手卫生（A）以防止污染。2. 先穿上隔离衣（B）以覆盖躯干。3. 接着戴上并固定好口罩或呼吸防护器（C）。4. 佩戴护目镜或面罩（D）以保护眼睛。5. 最后戴上手套（E），并拉长套住隔离衣的袖口。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For donning, think 'bottom up' (Gown -> Mask -> Goggles -> Gloves). Hand hygiene is always first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关于穿戴（Donning），可以考虑“自下而上”的逻辑（隔离衣 -> 口罩 -> 护目镜 -> 手套）。手卫生总是第一位的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":246,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_matrix_consent_57","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.55","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.55.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.55.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,254],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,76],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for an elective laparoscopic cholecystectomy. The nurse is participating in the informed consent process. For each action, click to specify whether it is the primary responsibility of the health care provider (surgeon) or the nurse.","fullStemZh":"一名患者计划进行择期腹腔镜胆囊切除术。护士正在参与知情同意过程。对于以下每项操作，点击以指定它是属于医护提供者（外科医生）的主要职责还是护士的主要职责。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each action, click to specify whether it is the primary responsibility of the health care provider (surgeon) or the nurse.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于以下每项操作，点击以指定它是属于医护提供者（外科医生）的主要职责还是护士的主要职责。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is participating in the informed consent process.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在参与知情同意过程。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Explain the risks, benefits, and alternative treatment options to the client.","zh":"向患者解释手术风险、益处及替代治疗方案。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Witness the client's signature on the consent form.","zh":"见证患者在同意书上签字。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Assess whether the client appears competent and is signing voluntarily.","zh":"评估患者是否具有签署同意书的行为能力，以及是否自愿签署。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Describe the details of the surgical procedure and potential complications.","zh":"描述手术步骤的细节以及潜在的并发症。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Verify that the signed consent form is present in the client's medical record.","zh":"核实已签署的同意书是否存在于患者的医疗记录中。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Health care provider (surgeon)","zh":"医护提供者（外科医生）"},{"id":"c2","en":"Nurse","zh":"护士"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The primary provider (surgeon) is solely responsible for explaining the surgical procedure (r4), including risks, benefits, alternatives, and complications (r1). The nurse's role is administrative and advocacy-based: witnessing the signature (r2), assessing competency and voluntariness (r3), and verifying that the consent form is on the chart before surgery (r5). If the client has questions about the procedure, the nurse must contact the provider to explain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"主要提供者（外科医生）独自负责解释手术步骤（r4），包括风险、益处、替代方案和并发症（r1）。护士的角色是行政和患者权益维护：见证签字（r2），评估患者的能力和自愿性（r3），以及核实术前同意书是否归档（r5）。如果患者对手术步骤有疑问，护士必须联系医生来解答。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: Providers EXPLAIN (the 'what' and 'why'). Nurses WITNESS and ADVOCATE. If the patient does not understand the procedure, the nurse does not explain it; they call the surgeon.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：提供者负责解释（手术“是什么”和“为什么”）。护士负责见证和维护。如果患者不懂手术，护士不能去解释，应给外科医生打电话。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":247,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_a_fib_peds_calc_58","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.56.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[276,317],"terminalOffsetsZh":[117,130],"fullStemEn":"A pediatric client weighing 22 lbs is prescribed liquid acetaminophen 15 mg/kg by mouth. The pharmacy supplies acetaminophen oral suspension labeled 160 mg/5 mL. How many mL of acetaminophen should the nurse administer for this dose? (Record your answer to the nearest tenth. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"一名体重为 22 磅的儿科患者被开具了口服对乙酰氨基酚 15 mg/kg 的医嘱。药房提供的对乙酰氨基酚口服混悬液标签为 160 mg/5 mL。护士应给予多少毫升（mL）的对乙酰氨基酚以完成该剂量？（答案四舍五入保留到小数点后一位。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer to the nearest tenth.","penultimateSentenceZh":"答案四舍五入保留到小数点后一位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["4.7","4.7 mL"],"numeric":{"value":4.7,"tolerance":0.05,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1: Convert weight from lbs to kg: 22 lbs / 2.2 = 10 kg. Step 2: Calculate the required dose in mg: 10 kg * 15 mg/kg = 150 mg. Step 3: Calculate the volume to administer: (150 mg / 160 mg) * 5 mL = 4.6875 mL. Step 4: Round to the nearest tenth: 4.6875 mL rounds to 4.7 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步：将体重从磅（lbs）转换为千克（kg）：22 磅 / 2.2 = 10 千克。第二步：计算所需的药物剂量（mg）：10 kg * 15 mg/kg = 150 毫克。第三步：计算需要给药的毫升数（mL）：（150 mg / 160 mg）* 5 mL = 4.6875 毫升。第四步：四舍五入到最近的十分位（小数点后一位）：4.6875 毫升四舍五入为 4.7 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always calculate in kg first (lbs to kg by dividing by 2.2). Pay close attention to rounding instructions; rounding too early can lead to a calculation error.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终先计算千克体重（磅除以2.2转换为千克）。密切关注四舍五入说明；过早进行四舍五入可能会导致计算错误。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":248,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.57.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[180,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,59],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the immunization history of a 12-month-old child. Which of the following immunizations are typically administered at this age according to the CDC schedule? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名 12 个月大儿童的免疫接种史。根据 CDC 时间表，通常在该年龄段接种以下哪些疫苗？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following immunizations are typically administered at this age according to the CDC schedule?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据 CDC 时间表，通常在该年龄段接种以下哪些疫苗？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hepatitis A","zh":"甲型肝炎疫苗"},{"id":"D","en":"Rotavirus","zh":"轮状病毒疫苗"},{"id":"B","en":"Varicella","zh":"水痘疫苗"},{"id":"E","en":"Human papillomavirus (HPV)","zh":"人乳头瘤病毒 (HPV)"},{"id":"A","en":"Measles, mumps, rubella (MMR)","zh":"麻疹、腮腺炎、风疹 (MMR)"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MMR, Varicella, and Hepatitis A (1st dose) are typically given between 12-15 months.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MMR、水痘疫苗和甲型肝炎疫苗（第一剂）通常在 12-15 个月之间接种。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that live vaccines (MMR, Varicella) are generally not given before 12 months of age.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住活疫苗（MMR、水痘）通常在 12 个月大之前不接种。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":249,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.58.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[90,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is leaving a client's room where contact and droplet precautions were in place. Place the steps for removing personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正离开一间采取了接触和飞沫预防措施的病房。请按正确顺序排列移除个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps for removing personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列移除个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is leaving a client's room where contact and droplet precautions were in place.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正离开一间采取了接触和飞沫预防措施的病房。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Mask or respirator","zh":"口罩或呼吸器"},{"id":"A","en":"Gloves","zh":"手套"},{"id":"C","en":"Gown","zh":"隔离衣"},{"id":"B","en":"Goggles or face shield","zh":"护目镜或面罩"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The standard sequence for doffing PPE is gloves, followed by goggles/face shield, then gown, and finally mask/respirator.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脱卸 PPE 的标准顺序是手套，然后是护目镜/面罩，接着是隔离衣，最后是口罩/呼吸器。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think 'alphabetical' for doffing: G-G-G-M (Gloves, Goggles, Gown, Mask). Note: some protocols vary, but this is the standard CDC sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"脱卸时记住字母顺序：G-G-G-M（手套、护目镜、隔离衣、口罩）。注意：某些方案可能有所不同，但这是标准的 CDC 顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":250,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.59.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,89],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Which action by the nurse is essential when caring for a client in mechanical restraints?","fullStemZh":"护士在护理使用机械约束的患者时，哪项操作是必不可少的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is essential when caring for a client in mechanical restraints?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在护理使用机械约束的患者时，哪项操作是必不可少的？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Obtain a PRN (as needed) order for the restraints from the provider.","zh":"从医疗服务提供者处获取约束的 PRN（按需）医嘱。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure that the restraint is tight enough that one finger cannot fit underneath.","zh":"确保约束带足够紧，以至于一根手指都伸不进去。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use a quick-release knot to secure the restraints.","zh":"使用活结（快速释放结）固定约束带。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tie the restraints to the side rails of the bed.","zh":"将约束带系在床侧护栏上。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Restraints must be secured with a quick-release knot to the bed frame (not side rails) for safety in case of emergency.","rationaleCorrectZh":"约束带必须用活结固定在床架上（而非侧栏），以便在紧急情况下安全释放。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first: Quick-release knots and bed frame attachment are standard safety practices for restraints.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一：活结和连接床架是约束的标准安全做法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":251,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.60.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,74],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Which immunization is recommended for a healthy child to receive at birth?","fullStemZh":"建议健康儿童在出生时接种哪种疫苗？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which immunization is recommended for a healthy child to receive at birth?","terminalSentenceZh":"建议健康儿童在出生时接种哪种疫苗？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Pneumococcal conjugate (PCV13)","zh":"肺炎球菌结合疫苗 (PCV13)"},{"id":"C","en":"Hepatitis B","zh":"乙型肝炎疫苗"},{"id":"A","en":"Inactivated poliovirus (IPV)","zh":"灭活脊髓灰质炎病毒疫苗 (IPV)"},{"id":"D","en":"Haemophilus influenzae type b (Hib)","zh":"b 型流感嗜血杆菌疫苗 (Hib)"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Hepatitis B vaccine is the only vaccine recommended at birth.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乙型肝炎疫苗是出生时唯一建议接种的疫苗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize 'Hep B at Birth' as a key immunization milestone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“出生即打乙肝”是一个关键的免疫里程碑。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":252,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.61.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,26],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is performing hand hygiene using soap and water. Place the steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在用肥皂和水进行手卫生。请按正确顺序排列步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is performing hand hygiene using soap and water.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在用肥皂和水进行手卫生。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Dry hands with a disposable towel.","zh":"用一次性毛巾擦干双手。"},{"id":"B","en":"Apply soap and rub hands vigorously for at least 20 seconds.","zh":"涂抹肥皂并剧烈摩擦双手至少 20 秒。"},{"id":"A","en":"Wet hands with water.","zh":"用水打湿双手。"},{"id":"C","en":"Rinse hands with water.","zh":"用水冲洗双手。"},{"id":"E","en":"Turn off the faucet using a paper towel.","zh":"用纸巾关掉水龙头。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The proper sequence for handwashing includes wetting, lathering/scrubbing, rinsing, drying, and then using a towel to turn off the faucet to avoid recontamination.","rationaleCorrectZh":"洗手的正确顺序包括打湿、涂抹肥皂/擦洗、冲洗、擦干，然后用毛巾关掉水龙头以避免再次污染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety: Never use bare hands to turn off a faucet after washing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全：洗手后绝不要用裸手关水龙头。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":253,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.62.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,38],"fullStemEn":"A client is in bilateral wrist restraints. Which of the following nursing interventions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者被使用了双侧腕部约束。以下哪些护理干预措施是恰当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing interventions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些护理干预措施是恰当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Check the client's skin integrity and circulation every 2 hours.","zh":"每 2 小时检查一次患者的皮肤完整性和血液循环。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep the restraints on for at least 24 hours before re-evaluating.","zh":"在重新评估之前，保持约束至少 24 小时。"},{"id":"C","en":"Offer fluids and toileting every 2 hours.","zh":"每 2 小时提供一次液体和如厕。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove restraints one at a time to provide range-of-motion exercises.","zh":"一次移除一个约束带以进行关节活动度练习。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the behavior that necessitated the restraints.","zh":"记录导致必须使用约束的行为。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate care for restraints includes frequent monitoring (q2h), range-of-motion, basic needs (fluids/toileting), and clear documentation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当的约束护理包括频繁监测（每 2 小时）、关节活动、基本需求（液体/如厕）和清晰的记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the 'every 2 hours' rule for monitoring and care of clients in restraints.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住对受约束患者进行监测和护理的“每 2 小时”原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":254,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.63.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"When applying standard precautions, which of the following is the most important action to prevent the spread of infection?","fullStemZh":"在实施标准预防措施时，以下哪项是防止感染扩散的最重要操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"When applying standard precautions, which of the following is the most important action to prevent the spread of infection?","terminalSentenceZh":"在实施标准预防措施时，以下哪项是防止感染扩散的最重要操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Recapping used needles before disposal.","zh":"在弃置前为使用过的针头重新盖帽。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wearing gloves for all client contact.","zh":"在与所有患者接触时佩戴手套。"},{"id":"D","en":"Performing hand hygiene before and after client contact.","zh":"在与患者接触前后进行手卫生。"},{"id":"C","en":"Wearing a mask for all clients with a cough.","zh":"为所有咳嗽的患者佩戴口罩。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hand hygiene is consistently identified as the single most effective way to prevent the spread of healthcare-associated infections.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手卫生一直被认为是防止医疗相关感染扩散的最有效单一方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the most fundamental and effective intervention. Hand hygiene almost always takes priority in infection control questions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找最基本和有效的干预措施。在感染控制问题中，手卫生几乎总是优先考虑。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":255,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p1_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.64.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,149],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,38],"fullStemEn":"A 50-year-old client who has no significant health history asks the nurse about the pneumococcal vaccine. Which information should the nurse provide?","fullStemZh":"一位 50 岁且无重大病史的患者向护士询问肺炎球菌疫苗。护士应提供哪些信息？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which information should the nurse provide?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应提供哪些信息？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 50-year-old client who has no significant health history asks the nurse about the pneumococcal vaccine.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位 50 岁且无重大病史的患者向护士询问肺炎球菌疫苗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"This vaccine is only recommended for clients with chronic lung disease.","zh":"此疫苗仅建议患有慢性肺病的患者接种。"},{"id":"C","en":"The vaccine provides lifelong immunity after a single dose given in childhood.","zh":"该疫苗在童年时期接种一剂后可提供终身免疫。"},{"id":"B","en":"It is recommended that adults age 50 and older receive the pneumococcal vaccine series.","zh":"建议 50 岁及以上的成年人接种肺炎球菌系列疫苗。"},{"id":"D","en":"The pneumococcal vaccine should be avoided if the client has already received the annual flu shot.","zh":"如果患者已经接种了年度流感疫苗，则应避免接种肺炎球菌疫苗。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The CDC (ACIP) updated guidelines in 2024 to recommend pneumococcal vaccination (PCV20 or PCV15) for all adults aged 50 years and older. Previously, the routine age was 65. Health promotion for this group also includes the annual flu shot, the shingles vaccine (starting at 50), and the RSV vaccine (shared decision-making for 60-74, or routine for 75+).","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDC (ACIP) 在 2024 年更新了指南，建议所有 50 岁及以上的成年人接种肺炎球菌疫苗（PCV20 或 PCV15）。此前，常规接种年龄为 65 岁。该人群的健康促进还包括年度流感疫苗、带状疱疹疫苗（从 50 岁开始）和 RSV 疫苗（60-74 岁由医患共同决策，或 75 岁及以上常规接种）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Knowledge of health promotion for adults: Pneumococcal (now 50+), Shingles (50+), and RSV vaccines are key current recommendations.","testTakingStrategyZh":"成年人健康促进知识：肺炎球菌（现在为 50 岁以上）、带状疱疹（50 岁以上）和 RSV 疫苗是当前的关键推荐。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A 50-year-old client who has no significant health history asks the nurse about the pneumococcal vaccine.","controlSentenceZh":"一位 50 岁且无重大病史的患者向护士询问肺炎球菌疫苗。"}
{"queueIndex":256,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_1","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.65.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[159,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,57],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is in the manic phase and is moving rapidly around the unit, interrupting other clients' conversations and demanding attention. Which nursing intervention is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一名患有双相情感障碍的患者正处于躁狂期，他在病房内快速走动，干扰其他患者的谈话并要求关注。以下哪项护理干预最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing intervention is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项护理干预最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is in the manic phase and is moving rapidly around the unit, interrupting other clients' conversations and demanding attention.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有双相情感障碍的患者正处于躁狂期，他在病房内快速走动，干扰其他患者的谈话并要求关注。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Guide the client to a quiet area with low stimuli.","zh":"引导患者进入刺激较小的安静区域。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the client to lead a group activity to channel their energy.","zh":"请该患者领导一项小组活动以引导其能量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Explain to the client that their behavior is disruptive to others.","zh":"向患者解释其行为干扰了他人。"},{"id":"B","en":"Place the client in physical restraints to prevent injury.","zh":"对患者实施身体约束以防止受伤。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During the manic phase, clients are hyperactive and easily distracted. Reducing environmental stimuli helps to decrease agitation and provide a safe environment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在躁狂期，患者过度活跃且容易分心。减少环境刺激有助于减少躁动并提供安全的环境。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the phase (manic) and the goal (safety and stabilization). Choose the least restrictive intervention that addresses hyperactivity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别所处阶段（躁狂）和目标（安全与稳定）。选择能够应对过度活跃的最少限制性干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":257,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_2","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.66.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,39],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is performing a suicide risk assessment for a client. Which factors increase the risk of a completed suicide? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名患者进行自杀风险评估。以下哪些因素会增加自杀既遂的风险？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which factors increase the risk of a completed suicide?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些因素会增加自杀既遂的风险？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"A stable support system of family and friends.","zh":"稳定的家人和朋友支持系统。"},{"id":"F","en":"Verbalizing future plans and goals.","zh":"用语言表达未来的计划和目标。"},{"id":"B","en":"History of previous suicide attempts.","zh":"既往自杀未遂史。"},{"id":"E","en":"Recent loss of a job or spouse.","zh":"最近失去工作或配偶。"},{"id":"A","en":"Access to lethal means, such as a firearm.","zh":"拥有致命工具，如枪支。"},{"id":"D","en":"Sudden improvement in mood after a deep depression.","zh":"深度抑郁后情绪突然好转。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Access to lethal means, history of attempts, sudden mood improvement (which may indicate a decision to act), and recent loss are all high-risk indicators.","rationaleCorrectZh":"拥有致命工具、自杀史、情绪突然好转（可能表明已决定采取行动）以及最近的损失都是高风险指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between risk factors and protective factors. Sudden mood change in depression is a classic NCLEX indicator of imminent risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分风险因素和保护性因素。抑郁症中情绪的突然转变是NCLEX中迫在眉睫风险的经典指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":258,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_3","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.67.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,45],"fullStemEn":"A client with a long history of chronic alcohol use was admitted 48 hours ago for a fractured hip. The client is now experiencing tremors, tachycardia, and visual hallucinations.","fullStemZh":"一名有长期慢性饮酒史的患者因髋部骨折于48小时前入院。该患者目前出现震颤、心动过速和幻视。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client is now experiencing tremors, tachycardia, and visual hallucinations.","terminalSentenceZh":"该患者目前出现震颤、心动过速和幻视。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a long history of chronic alcohol use was admitted 48 hours ago for a fractured hip.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名有长期慢性饮酒史的患者因髋部骨折于48小时前入院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse recognizes that the client is most likely experiencing {{1}}, which is a medical emergency that requires immediate treatment with {{2}}.","zh":"护士意识到患者最有可能正在经历 {{1}}，这是一种医疗紧急情况，需要立即使用 {{2}} 进行治疗。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"delirium tremens","zh":"震颤性谵妄"},{"id":"o3","en":"Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome","zh":"韦尼克-科萨科夫综合征"},{"id":"o1","en":"alcohol toxicity","zh":"酒精中毒"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"disulfiram","zh":"双硫仑"},{"id":"o1","en":"benzodiazepines","zh":"苯二氮䓬类药物"},{"id":"o3","en":"methadone","zh":"美沙酮"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Delirium tremens (DTs) usually occurs 48–72 hours after the last drink. It is characterized by severe autonomic hyperactivity and hallucinations. Benzodiazepines are the gold standard for preventing and treating alcohol withdrawal seizures and DTs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"震颤性谵妄（DTs）通常在最后一次饮酒后48-72小时发生。其特征是严重的自主神经亢进和幻觉。苯二氮䓬类药物是预防和治疗酒精戒断性癫痫发作和DTs的金标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the timeline of alcohol withdrawal. DTs peak at 48-72 hours. Benzodiazepines are always the priority med for acute withdrawal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注酒精戒断的时间表。DTs在48-72小时达到高峰。苯二氮䓬类药物始终是急性戒断的首选药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":259,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_4","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.68","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.68.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.68.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,30],"fullStemEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department after being sexually assaulted. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名遭受性侵犯的患者被送往急诊科。护士首先应该采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应该采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department after being sexually assaulted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名遭受性侵犯的患者被送往急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Contact the local police department to report the crime.","zh":"联系当地警察局报案。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assist the client with a shower to promote comfort.","zh":"协助患者洗澡以提高舒适度。"},{"id":"B","en":"Obtain written consent for a forensic examination.","zh":"获得法医检查的书面同意书。"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide a private, safe environment for the client.","zh":"为患者提供一个私密、安全的环境。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety and psychological stability are the priorities. Providing a private, safe environment is the first step in trauma-informed care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全和心理稳定是首要任务。提供私密、安全的环境是创伤知情护理的第一步。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply Maslow's hierarchy or trauma-informed care principles. Safety and psychological needs come first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用马斯洛需求层次理论或创伤知情护理原则。安全和心理需求排在第一位。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":260,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_5","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.69","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.69.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.69.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,36],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing a severe panic attack in the outpatient clinic. Which nursing interventions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在门诊诊所出现严重的惊恐发作。以下哪些护理干预是合适的？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing interventions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些护理干预是合适的？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Ask the client to explain the cause of their anxiety.","zh":"要求患者解释焦虑的原因。"},{"id":"C","en":"Encourage the client to take deep, slow breaths.","zh":"鼓励患者进行缓慢的深呼吸。"},{"id":"F","en":"Teach the client new coping mechanisms during the attack.","zh":"在发作期间教患者新的应对机制。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stay with the client and remain calm.","zh":"陪伴在患者身边并保持冷静。"},{"id":"E","en":"Place the client in a quiet, low-stimulus room.","zh":"将患者安置在安静、低刺激的房间内。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use simple, short sentences when speaking.","zh":"说话时使用简单、短促的句子。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During a panic attack, the priority is to provide safety, reduce stimuli, and use simple communication because the client's ability to process information is severely impaired.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在惊恐发作期间，首要任务是提供安全保障、减少刺激并使用简单的沟通方式，因为患者处理信息的能力严重受损。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the client's cognitive state during a level 4 (panic) anxiety. They cannot learn or analyze; they need safety and simple directions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考患者在4级（惊恐）焦虑期间的认知状态。他们无法学习或分析；他们需要安全和简单的指令。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":261,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.70","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.70.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.70.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,58],"fullStemEn":"A client with Anorexia Nervosa and a BMI of 14 is admitted for malnutrition. Within 24 hours of starting nutritional replacement, the client develops edema and generalized weakness.","fullStemZh":"一名患有神经性厌食症且BMI为14的患者因营养不良入院。在开始营养替代治疗后的24小时内，患者出现了水肿和全身无力。","terminalSentenceEn":"Within 24 hours of starting nutritional replacement, the client develops edema and generalized weakness.","terminalSentenceZh":"在开始营养替代治疗后的24小时内，患者出现了水肿和全身无力。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Anorexia Nervosa and a BMI of 14 is admitted for malnutrition.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有神经性厌食症且BMI为14的患者因营养不良入院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse suspects the client is experiencing {{1}}, which is primarily caused by a rapid shift in the electrolyte {{2}}.","zh":"护士怀疑患者正在经历 {{1}}，这主要是由于电解质 {{2}} 的快速转移引起的。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"refeeding syndrome","zh":"再摄食综合征"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypovolemic shock","zh":"低血容量性休克"},{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic alkalosis","zh":"代谢性碱中毒"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"calcium","zh":"钙"},{"id":"o2","en":"phosphorus","zh":"磷"},{"id":"o1","en":"sodium","zh":"钠"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Refeeding syndrome occurs when a malnourished person receives nutrients too quickly, leading to insulin release and the movement of phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium into the cells. Hypophosphatemia is the hallmark sign.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当营养不良的人过快摄入营养时，会发生再摄食综合征，导致胰岛素释放以及磷、钾和镁向细胞内移动。低磷血症是其标志性特征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the high-risk scenario (severely low BMI and refeeding). Recall that phosphorus is the key electrolyte shifted in refeeding syndrome.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别高风险情景（BMI极低和再摄食）。回想磷是再摄食综合征中转移的关键电解质。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":262,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_7","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.71","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.71.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.71.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,55],"fullStemEn":"A client hospitalized with major depressive disorder tells the nurse, 'Things will be much better soon; I've finally found a way to stop the pain.' What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"一名因重度抑郁症住院的患者告诉护士：“事情很快就会好转的；我终于找到了停止痛苦的方法。”护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client hospitalized with major depressive disorder tells the nurse, 'Things will be much better soon; I've finally found a way to stop the pain.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因重度抑郁症住院的患者告诉护士：“事情很快就会好转的；我终于找到了停止痛苦的方法。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to talk more about their positive feelings.","zh":"鼓励患者多谈谈他们的积极感受。"},{"id":"B","en":"Document the client's improvement in mood.","zh":"记录患者情绪的好转。"},{"id":"A","en":"Alert the family that the client is ready for discharge.","zh":"提醒家属患者已准备好出院。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the client directly, 'Are you thinking of killing yourself?'","zh":"直接询问患者：“你是在考虑自杀吗？”"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Vague statements about 'ending the pain' or things getting better after a deep depression are warning signs of suicide. The nurse must assess the risk directly and specifically.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关于“结束痛苦”或深度抑郁后事情好转的含糊陈述是自杀的警告信号。护士必须直接且具体地评估风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client makes a coded or ambiguous statement about death, the safest and most therapeutic response is direct assessment of suicide risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者发表关于死亡的含糊或暗示性陈述时，最安全、最具治疗性的反应是直接评估自杀风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":263,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_8","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.72","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.72.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.72.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with schizophrenia who is experiencing auditory hallucinations. Which interventions should the nurse implement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名患有精神分裂症且出现幻听的患者。护士应实施以下哪些干预措施？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施以下哪些干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to listen to music through headphones.","zh":"鼓励患者用耳机听音乐。"},{"id":"E","en":"Leave the client alone to allow them to process the hallucinations.","zh":"让患者独自一人，让他们处理幻觉。"},{"id":"B","en":"Tell the client that the voices are not real.","zh":"告诉患者那些声音不是真实的。"},{"id":"C","en":"Validate that the client is hearing something but state that you do not hear it.","zh":"承认患者听到了声音，但声明你没听到。"},{"id":"F","en":"Monitor for signs of increased anxiety or agitation.","zh":"监测焦虑或躁动增加的迹象。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client, 'What are the voices telling you?'","zh":"询问患者：“那些声音在告诉你什么？”"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assessing the content of hallucinations (especially command hallucinations) is crucial for safety. Validating the client's experience without agreeing with the hallucination is therapeutic. Distraction and monitoring for agitation are also key.","rationaleCorrectZh":"评估幻觉内容（尤其是命令性幻觉）对于安全至关重要。承认患者的经历而不认同幻觉内容具有治疗作用。转移注意力和监测躁动也是关键。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on safety first (command hallucinations) and then therapeutic communication (presenting reality). Distraction is a common coping strategy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先关注安全（命令性幻觉），然后是治疗性沟通（呈现现实）。转移注意力是一种常用的应对策略。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":264,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_9","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.73","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.73.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.73.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,70],"fullStemEn":"A client tells the nurse, 'You are the only one who really understands me. The other nurses are so mean. Can you give me your personal phone number so I can call you after I'm discharged?' Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"一名患者告诉护士：“你是唯一真正理解我的人。其他护士太刻薄了。你能给我你的个人电话号码吗，这样我出院后可以给你打电话？”护士哪种回答最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士哪种回答最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Can you give me your personal phone number so I can call you after I'm discharged?'","penultimateSentenceZh":"你能给我你的个人电话号码吗，这样我出院后可以给你打电话？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"You shouldn't say those things about the other nurses; they are trying their best.","zh":"你不应该那样说其他护士；他们已经在尽力了。"},{"id":"D","en":"It is important that we maintain a professional relationship; I cannot give you my personal number.","zh":"保持专业关系非常重要；我不能给你我的个人号码。"},{"id":"C","en":"I'm glad we connect well; I'll give you my number as long as you promise not to share it.","zh":"我很高兴我们相处得很好；只要你保证不告诉别人，我就把号码给你。"},{"id":"A","en":"It sounds like you're feeling unsupported by the rest of the team.","zh":"听起来你觉得团队其他成员没有给你足够的支持。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must maintain clear professional boundaries. Giving out personal contact information is a boundary violation. Directly stating the professional nature of the relationship is necessary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士必须保持明确的职业界限。提供个人联系方式是违反界限的行为。有必要直接说明关系的职业性质。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the boundary issue. Choose the response that is professional, direct, and maintains the nurse-client relationship without crossing lines.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别界限问题。选择专业、直接且在不逾矩的情况下维持护患关系的回答。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":265,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p10_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.74","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.74.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.74.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,56],"fullStemEn":"A client with Borderline Personality Disorder (BPD) frequently asks different staff members for special favors, leading to disagreements among the nursing team about the client's care plan.","fullStemZh":"一名患有边缘型人格障碍（BPD）的患者经常向不同的工作人员寻求特殊照顾，导致护理团队对该患者的护理计划产生分歧。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with Borderline Personality Disorder (BPD) frequently asks different staff members for special favors, leading to disagreements among the nursing team about the client's care plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患有边缘型人格障碍（BPD）的患者经常向不同的工作人员寻求特殊照顾，导致护理团队对该患者的护理计划产生分歧。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse identifies this behavior as {{1}} and understands that the priority intervention is to {{2}}.","zh":"护士将此行为识别为 {{1}}，并理解优先干预措施是 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"regression","zh":"退行"},{"id":"o1","en":"splitting","zh":"分裂"},{"id":"o2","en":"projection","zh":"投影"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"assign different nurses each shift","zh":"每班分配不同的护士"},{"id":"o3","en":"allow the client to choose their primary nurse","zh":"允许患者选择他们的责任护士"},{"id":"o2","en":"hold a staff meeting to ensure consistency","zh":"召开员工会议以确保一致性"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Splitting is a hallmark of BPD where the client pits staff against each other. Consistency and limit-setting among all team members are essential to manage this behavior.","rationaleCorrectZh":"分裂是BPD的一个标志，患者让工作人员互相对立。所有团队成员之间的一致性和限度设定对于管理这种行为至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the defense mechanism (splitting). The answer for BPD behavior almost always involves consistency and staff communication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别防御机制（分裂）。针对BPD行为的答案几乎总是涉及一致性和员工沟通。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":266,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.75","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.75.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.75.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[149,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,55],"fullStemEn":"A client diagnosed with terminal cancer says to the nurse, 'I don't know why I should continue with chemotherapy. It's not going to cure me anyway.' Which response by the nurse is therapeutic?","fullStemZh":"一名被诊断为癌症晚期的患者对护士说：“我不知道为什么要继续化疗。反正也治不好我。”护士的哪种回答具有治疗意义？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is therapeutic?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪种回答具有治疗意义？","penultimateSentenceEn":"It's not going to cure me anyway.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"反正也治不好我。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"You shouldn't give up hope; many people live longer than expected.","zh":"你不应该放弃希望；许多人的寿命比预期的要长。"},{"id":"D","en":"Why do you feel that way? Your family wants you to keep fighting.","zh":"你为什么会那样想？你的家人希望你继续战斗。"},{"id":"A","en":"It sounds like you are feeling discouraged about your treatment plan.","zh":"听起来你对自己的治疗计划感到很沮丧。"},{"id":"B","en":"I will call the chaplain to come and talk with you about your feelings.","zh":"我会请牧师来和你谈谈你的感受。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reflecting the client's feelings is a therapeutic communication technique that encourages the client to express more about their experience and shows empathy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反映患者的感受是一种具有治疗意义的沟通技巧，它鼓励患者表达更多关于他们经历的信息并表达同理心。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for options that address the client's underlying feelings and avoid 'why' questions or false reassurance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找能够解决患者潜在感受的选项，并避免“为什么”问题或虚假保证。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":267,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.76","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.76.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.76.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,42],"fullStemEn":"During a mental health interview, the nurse wants to encourage the client to talk more about their childhood. Which open-ended question is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在心理健康面试期间，护士希望鼓励患者更多地谈论他们的童年。以下哪项开放式提问最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which open-ended question is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项开放式提问最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During a mental health interview, the nurse wants to encourage the client to talk more about their childhood.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在心理健康面试期间，护士希望鼓励患者更多地谈论他们的童年。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Tell me what it was like for you growing up.","zh":"告诉我你成长的经历。"},{"id":"C","en":"Were you close to your parents when you were young?","zh":"你年轻的时候和父母关系亲近吗？"},{"id":"D","en":"Do you think your childhood affects your current behavior?","zh":"你认为你的童年影响了你现在的行为吗？"},{"id":"B","en":"Did you have a happy childhood?","zh":"你有一个快乐的童年吗？"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"'Tell me about...' is a classic open-ended prompt that allows the client to choose what information to share and does not limit the response to a 'yes' or 'no'.","rationaleCorrectZh":"“告诉我关于……”是一个经典的开放式提示，它允许患者选择分享哪些信息，并且不会将回答限制为“是”或“否”。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid questions that can be answered with 'yes' or 'no' when the goal is to encourage verbalization.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当目标是鼓励言语表达时，避免可以用“是”或“否”回答的问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":268,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.77","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.77.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.77.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,108],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"A client arrives at the emergency department in a state of acute anxiety after witnessing a traumatic event.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在目睹了一次创伤性事件后，处于急性焦虑状态，来到急诊室。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client arrives at the emergency department in a state of acute anxiety after witnessing a traumatic event.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患者在目睹了一次创伤性事件后，处于急性焦虑状态，来到急诊室。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's priority action is to {{1}} and use {{2}} to communicate.","zh":"护士的首要行动是 {{1}} 并使用 {{2}} 进行沟通。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"administer a high dose of sedative","zh":"给予大剂量的镇静剂"},{"id":"o1","en":"ensure the client's physical safety","zh":"确保患者的人身安全"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"complex explanations of the event","zh":"对事件的复杂解释"},{"id":"o1","en":"short, simple sentences","zh":"简短、简单的句子"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety is the priority in acute anxiety. Clients in a state of high anxiety have difficulty processing information, so simple and direct communication is necessary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在急性焦虑状态下，安全是首要任务。处于高度焦虑状态的患者难以处理信息，因此需要简单直接的沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply Maslow's hierarchy of needs: physical safety comes first. Consider the client's cognitive state when choosing communication styles.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用马斯洛的需求层次理论：人身安全第一。在选择沟通方式时，要考虑患者的认知状态。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":269,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.78","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.78.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.78.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse from the postpartum unit is floated to the medical-surgical unit for the shift. Which client assignment is most appropriate for this floating nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名来自产后病房的护士被临时调派到内外科病房轮班。对于这名调派护士来说，哪项患者分配最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client assignment is most appropriate for this floating nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于这名调派护士来说，哪项患者分配最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse from the postpartum unit is floated to the medical-surgical unit for the shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名来自产后病房的护士被临时调派到内外科病房轮班。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client who is 2 days postoperative following a total hip replacement.","zh":"一名全髋关节置换术后 2 天的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with a new diagnosis of type 1 diabetes requiring insulin teaching.","zh":"一名新诊断为 1 型糖尿病，需要进行胰岛素教学的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with a chest tube who is being monitored for a pneumothorax.","zh":"一名插有胸管，正在接受气胸监测的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client receiving a continuous heparin infusion for a pulmonary embolism.","zh":"一名因肺栓塞接受持续肝素输注的患者。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When a nurse floats, they should be assigned stable clients with conditions that match their general nursing skills. A stable postoperative client is the best choice among these options.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当护士轮换时，应分配给他们病情稳定且与其一般护理技能相匹配的患者。在这些选项中，稳定的术后患者是最佳选择。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Assign floating nurses to 'stable' and 'predictable' clients whose care involves basic nursing skills.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将调派护士分配给“稳定”且“可预测”的患者，其护理涉及基础护理技能。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse from the postpartum unit is floated to the medical-surgical unit for the shift.","controlSentenceZh":"一名来自产后病房的护士被临时调派到内外科病房轮班。"}
{"queueIndex":270,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.79","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.79.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.79.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,79],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"To ensure safe delegation, the nurse must follow the five rights of delegation.","fullStemZh":"为了确保安全委派，护士必须遵循委派的五个正确原则。","terminalSentenceEn":"To ensure safe delegation, the nurse must follow the five rights of delegation.","terminalSentenceZh":"为了确保安全委派，护士必须遵循委派的五个正确原则。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"When delegating a task, the nurse must ensure the right {{1}} and providing the right {{2}}.","zh":"在委派任务时，护士必须确保正确的 {{1}} 并提供正确的 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"circumstance","zh":"情境"},{"id":"o2","en":"cost of care","zh":"护理成本"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"payment for services","zh":"服务报酬"},{"id":"o1","en":"direction and communication","zh":"指导和沟通"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The five rights of delegation are: Right Task, Right Circumstance, Right Person, Right Direction/Communication, and Right Supervision/Evaluation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"委派的五个正确原则是：正确的任务、正确的情境、正确的人员、正确的指导/沟通以及正确的监督/评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the five rights of delegation as they are fundamental to management of care questions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住委派的五个正确原则，因为它们是护理管理问题的基础。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":271,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.80","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.80.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.80.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,71],"fullStemEn":"A client is being treated for a substance use disorder. During a session, the client states, 'I only drink when I'm stressed by my boss's unreasonable demands.' The nurse identifies this as which defense mechanism?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受物质使用障碍的治疗。在一次会谈中，患者陈述道：“我只有在因老板不合理的要求而感到压力时才会喝酒。”护士将这识别为哪种防御机制？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse identifies this as which defense mechanism?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士将这识别为哪种防御机制？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During a session, the client states, 'I only drink when I'm stressed by my boss's unreasonable demands.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"在一次会谈中，患者陈述道：“我只有在因老板不合理的要求而感到压力时才会喝酒。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Displacement","zh":"置换/移情"},{"id":"C","en":"Rationalization","zh":"合理化"},{"id":"A","en":"Projection","zh":"投射"},{"id":"D","en":"Sublimation","zh":"升华"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rationalization involves justifying illogical or unreasonable ideas or actions by developing acceptable explanations that satisfy the teller and the listener.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合理化涉及通过制定令叙述者和倾听者满意的、可接受的解释，来为不合逻辑或不合理的想法或行为辩护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the difference between justifying behavior (rationalization) and blaming others for one's own traits (projection).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别为行为辩护（合理化）和因自己的特质而指责他人（投射）之间的区别。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":272,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.81","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.81.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.81.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,69],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing end-of-life care to a client and their family.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患者及其家属提供临终关怀。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing end-of-life care to a client and their family.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患者及其家属提供临终关怀。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should demonstrate {{1}} and use {{2}} when words are not enough.","zh":"护士应表现出 {{1}}，并在言语不足以表达时使用 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"presence","zh":"陪伴/临在"},{"id":"o2","en":"detachment","zh":"情感疏离"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"avoidance of the family","zh":"回避家属"},{"id":"o1","en":"therapeutic touch","zh":"治疗性触摸"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Presence and therapeutic touch are important non-verbal communication techniques in end-of-life care, providing comfort and emotional support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"陪伴和治疗性触摸是临终关怀中重要的非言语沟通技巧，能够提供安慰和情感支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In end-of-life care, focus on 'being with' the client and family rather than 'doing for'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在临终关怀中，重点在于“陪伴”患者和家属，而不仅仅是“为他们做”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":273,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.82","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.82.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.82.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,93],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,25],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use a walker. Which instruction should the nurse include?","fullStemZh":"护士正在教患者如何使用助行器。护士应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use a walker.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教患者如何使用助行器。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Move the unaffected leg forward first after moving the walker.","zh":"移动助行器后，先向前移动健肢。"},{"id":"B","en":"Advance the walker 12 inches (30 cm) ahead of the feet.","zh":"将助行器向前推进12英寸（30厘米）。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use the walker to pull yourself up from a sitting position.","zh":"从坐位起身时，使用助行器将自己拉起来。"},{"id":"A","en":"Move the walker, then the affected leg, then the unaffected leg.","zh":"先移动助行器，然后移动患肢，最后移动健肢。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence for using a walker is to move the walker forward about 6 inches, then move the weak (affected) leg, followed by the strong (unaffected) leg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用助行器的正确顺序是将助行器向前推进约6英寸，然后移动弱侧（患侧）腿，接着移动强侧（健侧）腿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the safety and stability of the client when using assistive devices.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在使用辅助设备时，重点关注患者的安全性和稳定性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":274,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.83","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.83.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.83.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[55,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for an elective surgery. What is the nurse's primary responsibility regarding informed consent?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名接受择期手术的患者做准备。关于知情同意，护士的首要职责是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's primary responsibility regarding informed consent?","terminalSentenceZh":"关于知情同意，护士的首要职责是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for an elective surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名接受择期手术的患者做准备。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Explaining the risks and benefits of the surgical procedure.","zh":"解释手术程序的风险和益处。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtaining the client's signature after describing alternatives.","zh":"在描述替代方案后获取患者签名。"},{"id":"B","en":"Witnessing the client's signature on the consent form.","zh":"见证患者在同意书上签名。"},{"id":"A","en":"Evaluating if the client fully understands the procedure.","zh":"评估患者是否完全理解该程序。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse's role in informed consent is to witness the signature, ensuring that the client is competent and signed voluntarily.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在知情同意中的角色是见证签名，确保患者有能力并自愿签名。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between the healthcare provider's role (obtaining consent) and the nurse's role (witnessing the signature).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分医疗提供者的角色（获取同意）和护士的角色（见证签名）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for an elective surgery.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名接受择期手术的患者做准备。"}
{"queueIndex":275,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.84","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.84.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.84.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[41,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,33],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for a colonoscopy. Which instruction should the nurse prioritize during the pre-procedure teaching?","fullStemZh":"一名患者计划进行结肠镜检查。护士在术前教育期间应优先考虑哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse prioritize during the pre-procedure teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在术前教育期间应优先考虑哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is scheduled for a colonoscopy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者计划进行结肠镜检查。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Stop all clear liquids at midnight before the test, regardless of the scheduled procedure time.","zh":"无论检查安排在几点，都应从检查前一晚午夜开始停止所有清流质。"},{"id":"D","en":"Report any abdominal cramping immediately after the test.","zh":"测试后立即报告任何腹部绞痛。"},{"id":"A","en":"Follow the prescribed day-before low-residue or clear-liquid plan and take the bowel preparation in split doses as directed.","zh":"遵循处方的检查前一天低残渣或清流质计划，并按医嘱分次服用肠道准备液。"},{"id":"B","en":"You will receive a general anesthetic for the procedure.","zh":"您将在手术过程中接受全身麻醉。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Proper bowel preparation is critical for visualization. Current routine guidance generally limits dietary restrictions to the day before and recommends taking the prescribed preparation in split doses, with individualized fasting instructions from the procedural team.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当的肠道准备对清晰观察至关重要。现行常规指导通常将饮食限制在检查前一天，并建议按处方分次服用准备液，同时遵循操作团队提供的个体化禁食指导。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that visualization is the goal of a colonoscopy; bowel prep is key.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住结肠镜检查的目标是观察；肠道准备是关键。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":276,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.85","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.85.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.85.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,41],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to logroll a client who recently had spinal surgery. Which action by the nurse is essential?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名最近接受过脊柱手术的患者进行轴向翻身。护士的哪项操作是必不可少的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is essential?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项操作是必不可少的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to logroll a client who recently had spinal surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名最近接受过脊柱手术的患者进行轴向翻身。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Perform the procedure with only one other staff member.","zh":"仅与一名其他工作人员一起执行该程序。"},{"id":"C","en":"Turn the client's upper body first, then the lower body.","zh":"先翻动患者的上半身，然后是下半身。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the client to reach for the side rail during the turn.","zh":"翻身过程中要求患者去抓侧栏。"},{"id":"B","en":"Place a pillow between the client's legs before turning.","zh":"翻身前在患者两腿之间放一个枕头。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A pillow between the legs prevents adduction and maintains spinal alignment during the logroll.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在轴向翻身过程中，两腿之间的枕头可防止内收并保持脊柱对齐。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The goal of logrolling is to prevent any twisting of the spine.","testTakingStrategyZh":"轴向翻身的目标是防止脊柱发生任何扭转。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":277,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.86","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.86.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.86.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,49],"fullStemEn":"Before a client undergoes a computed tomography (CT) scan with intravenous contrast media, the nurse must assess the client for an allergy to ________.","fullStemZh":"在患者进行静脉注射造影剂的计算机断层扫描（CT）之前，护士必须评估患者是否对________过敏。","terminalSentenceEn":"Before a client undergoes a computed tomography (CT) scan with intravenous contrast media, the nurse must assess the client for an allergy to ________.","terminalSentenceZh":"在患者进行静脉注射造影剂的计算机断层扫描（CT）之前，护士必须评估患者是否对________过敏。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Allergen","zh":"过敏原"},"acceptable":["shellfish","iodine","seafood"],"numeric":null}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Allergies to iodine or shellfish are contraindicated with iodine-based contrast media used in CT scans.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对碘或贝类过敏是使用CT扫描中含碘造影剂的禁忌症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the common cross-sensitivity associated with iodine-based contrast.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别与含碘造影剂相关的常见交叉敏感性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":278,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.87","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.87.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.87.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"When teaching a client with left-sided weakness how to use a cane, the nurse should instruct the client to hold the cane on the ________ side.","fullStemZh":"在教导左侧无力的患者如何使用手杖时，护士应指导患者将手杖握在________侧。","terminalSentenceEn":"When teaching a client with left-sided weakness how to use a cane, the nurse should instruct the client to hold the cane on the ________ side.","terminalSentenceZh":"在教导左侧无力的患者如何使用手杖时，护士应指导患者将手杖握在________侧。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Side of body","zh":"身体侧"},"acceptable":["right","unaffected","stronger","strong"],"numeric":null}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A cane should be held on the unaffected (stronger) side to provide balance and support for the opposite weak side.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手杖应握在健侧（较强的一侧），以为对侧弱肢提供平衡和支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The cane goes on the 'good' side to support the 'bad' side.","testTakingStrategyZh":"手杖放在“好”的一侧以支持“坏”的一侧。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":279,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.88","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.88.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.88.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"According to standard preoperative guidelines, a healthy adult client should be NPO (nothing by mouth) for clear liquids for a minimum of ____ hours before elective surgery.","fullStemZh":"根据标准术前指南，健康的成年患者在择期手术前至少应禁食透明液体____小时。","terminalSentenceEn":"According to standard preoperative guidelines, a healthy adult client should be NPO (nothing by mouth) for clear liquids for a minimum of ____ hours before elective surgery.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据标准术前指南，健康的成年患者在择期手术前至少应禁食透明液体____小时。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"hours","zh":"小时"},"acceptable":["2","two"],"numeric":{"value":2,"tolerance":0,"unit":"hours"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The current American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) guidelines allow for clear liquids up to 2 hours before surgery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"目前的美国麻醉医师协会（ASA）指南允许在手术前2小时内饮用透明液体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Standard NPO guidelines vary by food type; clear liquids have the shortest required fasting time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"标准禁食指南因食物类型而异；透明液体的禁食时间要求最短。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":280,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.89","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.89.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.89.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,37],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing complications related to immobility. Match each complication to its appropriate body system.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查与固定不动相关的并发症。将每种并发症与其相应的身体系统相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each complication to its appropriate body system.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种并发症与其相应的身体系统相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing complications related to immobility.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查与固定不动相关的并发症。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Atelectasis","zh":"肺不张"},{"id":"r2","en":"Deep vein thrombosis (DVT)","zh":"深静脉血栓形成"},{"id":"r3","en":"Constipation","zh":"便秘"},{"id":"r4","en":"Pressure injury","zh":"压力性损伤"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Respiratory","zh":"呼吸系统"},{"id":"c3","en":"Gastrointestinal","zh":"胃肠系统"},{"id":"c4","en":"Integumentary","zh":"皮肤系统"},{"id":"c2","en":"Cardiovascular","zh":"心血管系统"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Each complication of immobility is associated with a specific body system.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每种固定不动导致的并发症都与特定的身体系统相关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the physiological effect of immobility to the corresponding system.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将固定不动的生理效应与相应的系统相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":281,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.90","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.90.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.90.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,41],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is screening a client for an MRI. Identify whether each finding is an absolute contraindication or is generally safe/requires caution.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患者进行MRI筛查。识别每项发现是绝对禁忌症还是通常安全/需要谨慎。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify whether each finding is an absolute contraindication or is generally safe/requires caution.","terminalSentenceZh":"识别每项发现是绝对禁忌症还是通常安全/需要谨慎。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is screening a client for an MRI.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患者进行MRI筛查。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Traditional (non-MRI-conditional) cardiac pacemaker","zh":"传统（非MRI兼容型）心脏起搏器"},{"id":"r2","en":"Traditional cochlear implant","zh":"传统人工耳蜗"},{"id":"r3","en":"Titanium hip prosthesis","zh":"钛合金髋关节假体"},{"id":"r4","en":"Intrauterine device (IUD) - Copper","zh":"宫内节育器（IUD）- 铜"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Absolute Contraindication","zh":"绝对禁忌症"},{"id":"c2","en":"Generally Safe / Caution","zh":"通常安全/谨慎"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Traditional (non-MRI-conditional) pacemakers and cochlear implants are absolute contraindications because their ferromagnetic components can be displaced, deactivated, or damaged by MRI magnetic fields. Modern MRI-conditional devices may be allowed with strict protocols and device-specific clearance — the nurse must always confirm device compatibility before scheduling the study. Titanium prostheses are non-ferromagnetic and generally safe. Copper IUDs are generally safe but require documentation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"传统（非MRI兼容型）起搏器和人工耳蜗是绝对禁忌症，因为其铁磁性组件在MRI磁场中可能发生移位、失效或损坏。现代MRI兼容型设备在严格遵守规程和特定设备许可的情况下可能被允许——护士在安排检查前必须确认设备兼容性。钛合金假体无铁磁性，通常是安全的。铜IUD通常是安全的，但需要记录在案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Key question: Is the implant ferromagnetic? Traditional pacemakers and cochlear implants are ferromagnetic and contraindicated. Modern MRI-conditional devices require device-specific clearance. Titanium and copper are safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关键问题：植入物是否具有铁磁性？传统起搏器和人工耳蜗具有铁磁性，属于禁忌症。现代MRI兼容型设备需要特定设备的许可。钛和铜是安全的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":282,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p3_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.91","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.91.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.91.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,44],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing a client for elective surgery. For each medication, indicate whether it is typically held before surgery or typically continued.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名患者进行择期手术。对于每种药物，说明是通常在手术前停用还是通常继续使用。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each medication, indicate whether it is typically held before surgery or typically continued.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每种药物，说明是通常在手术前停用还是通常继续使用。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing a client for elective surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名患者进行择期手术。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Warfarin","zh":"华法林"},{"id":"r2","en":"Atenolol","zh":"阿替洛尔"},{"id":"r3","en":"Metformin","zh":"二甲双胍"},{"id":"r4","en":"Daily Multivitamin","zh":"每日多种维生素"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Typically Held Before Surgery","zh":"通常在手术前停用"},{"id":"c2","en":"Typically Continued","zh":"通常继续使用"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Anticoagulants (Warfarin), oral hypoglycemics (Metformin), and supplements are usually held. Beta-blockers (Atenolol) are often continued to prevent rebound tachycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"抗凝剂（华法林）、口服降糖药（二甲双胍）和补充剂通常停用。β受体阻滞剂（阿替洛尔）通常继续使用以防止反跳性心动过速。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the risk of bleeding or hypoglycemia versus cardiac stability during surgery.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑手术期间出血或低血糖风险与心脏稳定性之间的关系。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":283,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.92","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.92.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.92.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,52],"fullStemEn":"A client taking lisinopril for hypertension presents to the emergency department with rapidly progressing swelling of the lips, tongue, and throat. Which action should the nurse prioritize?","fullStemZh":"一名因高血压服用赖诺普利的患者来到急诊科，表现为口唇、舌头和喉部快速进展的肿胀。护士应优先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse prioritize?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client taking lisinopril for hypertension presents to the emergency department with rapidly progressing swelling of the lips, tongue, and throat.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因高血压服用赖诺普利的患者来到急诊科，表现为口唇、舌头和喉部快速进展的肿胀。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Document the allergy in the medical record.","zh":"在医疗记录中记录该过敏反应。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's airway patency.","zh":"评估患者的气道通畅性。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer an oral antihistamine.","zh":"给予口服抗组胺药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Obtain a 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG).","zh":"进行12导联心电图（ECG）检查。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Angioedema is a life-threatening side effect of ACE inhibitors. Maintaining and assessing airway patency is the priority intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血管性水肿是ACE抑制剂的一种危及生命的副作用。维持和评估气道通畅是首选的干预措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABC (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) priority framework.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）优先级框架。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client taking lisinopril for hypertension presents to the emergency department with rapidly progressing swelling of the lips, tongue, and throat.","controlSentenceZh":"一名因高血压服用赖诺普利的患者来到急诊科，表现为口唇、舌头和喉部快速进展的肿胀。"}
{"queueIndex":284,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.93","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.93.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.93.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the medical records of several clients. Which conditions are considered prerenal causes of acute kidney injury (AKI)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在查阅几名患者的医疗记录。哪些情况被认为是急性肾损伤（AKI）的肾前性原因？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which conditions are considered prerenal causes of acute kidney injury (AKI)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些情况被认为是急性肾损伤（AKI）的肾前性原因？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hypovolemia due to severe hemorrhage","zh":"严重出血导致的低血容量"},{"id":"C","en":"Anaphylactic shock","zh":"过敏性休克"},{"id":"F","en":"Renal calculi","zh":"肾结石"},{"id":"B","en":"Nephrotoxic medication use (e.g., Gentamicin)","zh":"使用肾毒性药物（如庆大霉素）"},{"id":"D","en":"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)","zh":"良性前列腺增生（BPH）"},{"id":"E","en":"Severe dehydration","zh":"严重脱水"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Prerenal AKI is caused by factors that reduce systemic circulation, causing a decrease in renal blood flow. Hypovolemia, anaphylactic shock, and severe dehydration all lead to decreased renal perfusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肾前性AKI是由减少全身循环、导致肾血流量减少的因素引起的。低血容量、过敏性休克和严重脱水都会导致肾灌注减少。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between prerenal (perfusion), intrarenal (tissue damage), and postrenal (obstruction) causes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分肾前性（灌注）、肾性（组织损伤）和肾后性（梗阻）原因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":285,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.94","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.94.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.94.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,55],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for clients with suspected myocardial infarction (MI). For each clinical finding, indicate whether it is most characteristic of STEMI or NSTEMI.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理疑似心肌梗死（MI）的患者。对于每一项临床发现，请指出它是STEMI还是NSTEMI的最典型特征。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, indicate whether it is most characteristic of STEMI or NSTEMI.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每一项临床发现，请指出它是STEMI还是NSTEMI的最典型特征。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for clients with suspected myocardial infarction (MI).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理疑似心肌梗死（MI）的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Complete occlusion of a major coronary artery","zh":"冠状动脉主干完全闭塞"},{"id":"r2","en":"ST-segment depression or T-wave inversion on ECG","zh":"心电图ST段压低或T波倒置"},{"id":"r3","en":"Persistent ST-segment elevation in two contiguous leads","zh":"两个连续导联出现持续性ST段抬高"},{"id":"r4","en":"Partial occlusion of a coronary artery","zh":"冠状动脉部分闭塞"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"NSTEMI","zh":"NSTEMI"},{"id":"c1","en":"STEMI","zh":"STEMI"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"STEMI is characterized by complete occlusion and ST-segment elevation. NSTEMI usually involves partial occlusion and presents with ST-segment depression or T-wave changes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"STEMI的特点是完全闭塞和ST段抬高。NSTEMI通常涉及部分闭塞，表现为ST段压低或T波改变。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the pathophysiological differences and ECG presentations of STEMI vs NSTEMI.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想STEMI与NSTEMI的病理生理差异和心电图表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for clients with suspected myocardial infarction (MI).","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在护理疑似心肌梗死（MI）的患者。"}
{"queueIndex":286,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.95","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.95.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.95.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,63],"fullStemEn":"A client taking warfarin for atrial fibrillation has an INR of 5.2 and active major gastrointestinal bleeding. Which medication should the nurse anticipate as part of urgent warfarin reversal?","fullStemZh":"一名因心房颤动服用华法林的患者 INR 为 5.2，并出现活动性重大胃肠道出血。护士应预期紧急逆转华法林治疗中会使用哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse anticipate as part of urgent warfarin reversal?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期紧急逆转华法林治疗中会使用哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client taking warfarin for atrial fibrillation has an INR of 5.2 and active major gastrointestinal bleeding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因心房颤动服用华法林的患者 INR 为 5.2，并出现活动性重大胃肠道出血。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Enoxaparin","zh":"依诺肝素"},{"id":"A","en":"Protamine sulfate","zh":"硫酸鱼精蛋白"},{"id":"D","en":"Vitamin K (Phytonadione)","zh":"维生素K（植物甲萘醌）"},{"id":"C","en":"Clopidogrel","zh":"氯吡格雷"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Active major bleeding during warfarin therapy requires urgent reversal. IV vitamin K is administered with four-factor prothrombin complex concentrate when available. An INR of 5.2 without clinically relevant bleeding would not routinely require vitamin K.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林治疗期间发生活动性重大出血需要紧急逆转。若可获得，应静脉给予维生素 K 并同时使用四因子凝血酶原复合物浓缩物。若 INR 为 5.2 但无临床相关出血，通常不常规给予维生素 K。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Warfarin reversal depends on bleeding severity, not the INR alone. Major bleeding calls for rapid reversal with IV vitamin K plus four-factor PCC when available.","testTakingStrategyZh":"华法林逆转取决于出血严重程度，而不仅是 INR。重大出血需要静脉维生素 K，并在可获得时联合四因子 PCC 快速逆转。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":287,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.96","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.96.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.96.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge education to a client newly prescribed enalapril. Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名新开具依那普利处方的患者提供出院教育。护士应包括哪些说明？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些说明？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Rise slowly from a sitting or lying position.","zh":"从坐位或卧位起立时动作要缓慢。"},{"id":"B","en":"Report a persistent dry cough to the provider.","zh":"向医生报告持续性的干咳。"},{"id":"E","en":"Take the medication with a full glass of grapefruit juice.","zh":"用一整杯葡萄柚汁送服药物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Increase intake of potassium-rich foods like bananas.","zh":"增加富含钾的食物（如香蕉）的摄入。"},{"id":"D","en":"Avoid using salt substitutes containing potassium.","zh":"避免使用含有钾的代盐。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ACE inhibitors can cause orthostatic hypotension (rise slowly) and dry cough. They also increase the risk of hyperkalemia, so potassium intake should be monitored and potassium-containing salt substitutes avoided.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ACE抑制剂可引起体位性低血压（起立缓慢）和干咳。它们还会增加高钾血症的风险，因此应监测钾的摄入，并避免使用含钾的代盐。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the common side effects and electrolyte shifts associated with ACE inhibitors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考与ACE抑制剂相关的常见副作用和电解质变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":288,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.97","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.97.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.97.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,52],"fullStemEn":"A client in the oliguric phase of acute kidney injury (AKI) has a potassium level of 6.8 mEq/L. Which ECG change should the nurse expect to see first?","fullStemZh":"一名处于急性肾损伤（AKI）少尿期的患者血钾水平为6.8 mEq/L。护士预估首先会看到哪种心电图改变？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which ECG change should the nurse expect to see first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预估首先会看到哪种心电图改变？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in the oliguric phase of acute kidney injury (AKI) has a potassium level of 6.8 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名处于急性肾损伤（AKI）少尿期的患者血钾水平为6.8 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Tall, peaked T waves","zh":"高尖的T波"},{"id":"C","en":"Widened QRS complex","zh":"QRS波群增宽"},{"id":"A","en":"ST-segment elevation","zh":"ST段抬高"},{"id":"D","en":"Prominent U waves","zh":"明显的U波"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tall, peaked T waves are typically the earliest ECG sign of hyperkalemia. As potassium levels rise further, other changes like PR interval prolongation and QRS widening occur.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高尖的T波通常是高钾血症最早的心电图征象。随着钾水平进一步升高，会出现PR间期延长和QRS增宽等其他变化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the earliest ECG manifestation of hyperkalemia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别高钾血症最早的心电图表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":289,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.98","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.98.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.98.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[209,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,62],"fullStemEn":"An older female client reports to the nurse that she has been feeling 'not right' for two days. Which symptoms should the nurse recognize as potential atypical signs of a myocardial infarction in this client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名高龄女性患者向护士报告她这两天感觉“不太对劲”。护士应将哪些症状识别为该患者心肌梗死潜在的非典型征象？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which symptoms should the nurse recognize as potential atypical signs of a myocardial infarction in this client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些症状识别为该患者心肌梗死潜在的非典型征象？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Shortness of breath","zh":"呼吸短促"},{"id":"A","en":"Crushing substernal chest pain","zh":"压榨性胸骨后胸痛"},{"id":"B","en":"Extreme fatigue","zh":"极度疲乏"},{"id":"E","en":"Pain radiating down the left arm","zh":"放射至左臂的疼痛"},{"id":"C","en":"Epigastric pain or indigestion","zh":"上腹部疼痛或消化不良"}],"correct":["B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Women, older adults, and clients with diabetes often present with atypical MI symptoms such as fatigue, indigestion, and dyspnea instead of classic crushing chest pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"女性、老年人和糖尿病患者通常表现为非典型MI症状，如疲乏、消化不良和呼吸困难，而非典型的压榨性胸痛。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the word 'atypical' and the specific client population (female, older adult).","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注“非典型”一词和特定的患者群体（女性、老年人）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":290,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.99","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.99.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.99.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,32],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer anticoagulants. Match the medication with its correct monitoring parameter and antidote.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备给予抗凝剂。请将药物与其正确的监测参数和解毒剂相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match the medication with its correct monitoring parameter and antidote.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将药物与其正确的监测参数和解毒剂相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer anticoagulants.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备给予抗凝剂。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Unfractionated Heparin (IV)","zh":"普通肝素（静脉）"},{"id":"r2","en":"Warfarin","zh":"华法林"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Platelet count; Flumazenil","zh":"血小板计数；氟马西尼"},{"id":"c1","en":"aPTT; Protamine Sulfate","zh":"aPTT；硫酸鱼精蛋白"},{"id":"c2","en":"PT/INR; Vitamin K","zh":"PT/INR；维生素K"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Heparin is monitored by aPTT and reversed by protamine sulfate. Warfarin is monitored by PT/INR and reversed by Vitamin K.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝素由aPTT监测，由硫酸鱼精蛋白逆转。华法林由PT/INR监测，由维生素K逆转。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pair the monitoring test and antidote correctly for each medication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"为每种药物正确配对监测检查和解毒剂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":291,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.100","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.100.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.100.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,39],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute chest pain is admitted to the emergency department. Which medication should the nurse expect to be administered immediately to inhibit platelet aggregation?","fullStemZh":"一名患有急性胸痛的患者进入急诊科。护士预估应立即给予哪种药物以抑制血小板聚集？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse expect to be administered immediately to inhibit platelet aggregation?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预估应立即给予哪种药物以抑制血小板聚集？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with acute chest pain is admitted to the emergency department.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有急性胸痛的患者进入急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Aspirin","zh":"阿司匹林"},{"id":"C","en":"Morphine sulfate","zh":"硫酸吗啡"},{"id":"D","en":"Atropine","zh":"阿托品"},{"id":"A","en":"Nitroglycerin","zh":"硝酸甘油"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aspirin is administered immediately in suspected MI to inhibit platelet aggregation and prevent further clot formation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在疑似MI中立即给予阿司匹林，以抑制血小板聚集并防止血栓进一步形成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the functions of medications in the MONA protocol (Morphine, Oxygen, Nitroglycerin, Aspirin).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分MONA方案（吗啡、氧气、硝酸甘油、阿司匹林）中各种药物的功能。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":292,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p4_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.101","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.101.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.101.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client with acute kidney injury. Which findings would indicate the client is experiencing fluid volume overload? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名急性肾损伤患者。哪些发现表明患者正在经历体液容量过负荷？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings would indicate the client is experiencing fluid volume overload?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现表明患者正在经历体液容量过负荷？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Crackles upon lung auscultation","zh":"肺部听诊有湿啰音"},{"id":"B","en":"Jugular venous distention (JVD)","zh":"颈静脉怒张（JVD）"},{"id":"E","en":"Dependent edema","zh":"下垂性水肿"},{"id":"C","en":"Bounding peripheral pulses","zh":"周围脉搏洪大"},{"id":"D","en":"Tenting of the skin","zh":"皮肤帐篷状（弹性差）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Signs of fluid overload include crackles, JVD, bounding pulses, and edema. Skin tenting is a sign of dehydration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"体液过负荷的体征包括湿啰音、颈静脉怒张、脉搏洪大和水肿。皮肤帐篷状是脱水的征象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between signs of fluid overload and signs of fluid deficit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分体液过负荷的征象和体液不足的征象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":293,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.102","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.102.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.102.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,55],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic heart failure reports sudden weight gain of 3 lbs (1.36 kg) in 24 hours and increased shortness of breath. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名慢性心力衰竭患者报告在24小时内体重突然增加3磅（1.36公斤），且呼吸困难加重。护士应首先采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with chronic heart failure reports sudden weight gain of 3 lbs (1.36 kg) in 24 hours and increased shortness of breath.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名慢性心力衰竭患者报告在24小时内体重突然增加3磅（1.36公斤），且呼吸困难加重。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assess for peripheral edema in the lower extremities.","zh":"评估下肢周围水肿情况。"},{"id":"A","en":"Check the client's blood pressure and heart rate.","zh":"检查患者的血压和心率。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer a prescribed PRN dose of furosemide.","zh":"给予医嘱中的必要时剂量呋塞米。"},{"id":"C","en":"Auscultate the client's lung sounds.","zh":"听诊患者的肺部音。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the ABC (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) priority framework, the nurse should first assess the client's respiratory status by auscultating lung sounds to check for crackles, which indicate pulmonary edema—a common complication of heart failure exacerbation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用ABC（呼吸道、呼吸、循环）优先级框架，护士应首先通过听诊肺部是否有啰音来评估患者的呼吸状况，啰音提示肺水肿——这是心力衰竭加重的常见并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs. Respiratory symptoms (shortness of breath) require immediate assessment of the respiratory system (lung sounds).","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用ABC原则。呼吸系统症状（呼吸困难）需要立即评估呼吸系统（肺部音）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":294,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.103","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.103.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.103.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,43],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the hospital with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis (TB). Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find during the assessment? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名疑似肺结核（TB）患者入院。护士在评估期间预计会发现哪些临床表现？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find during the assessment?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在评估期间预计会发现哪些临床表现？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hemoptysis","zh":"咯血"},{"id":"A","en":"Night sweats","zh":"盗汗"},{"id":"B","en":"Low-grade afternoon fever","zh":"午后低热"},{"id":"C","en":"Unexplained weight gain","zh":"不明原因的体重增加"},{"id":"F","en":"Anorexia and fatigue","zh":"食欲减退和疲劳"},{"id":"E","en":"Dull chest pain","zh":"胸部钝痛"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Common signs of pulmonary tuberculosis include night sweats, low-grade afternoon fever, weight loss (not gain), hemoptysis (coughing up blood), chest pain, anorexia, and fatigue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肺结核的常见体征包括盗汗、午后低热、体重减轻（而非增加）、咯血、胸痛、食欲减退和疲劳。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the classic presentation of tuberculosis, which involves 'wasting' symptoms (weight loss) and systemic signs of infection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想肺结核的经典表现，包括“消瘦”症状（体重减轻）和感染的全身体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":295,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.104","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.104.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.104.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[207,252],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,81],"fullStemEn":"A healthcare provider prescribes heparin 5,000 units subcutaneously every 12 hours for a client post-surgery. The available vial is labeled 10,000 units/mL. How many mL should the nurse administer per dose? (Record your answer as a numeric value only.)","fullStemZh":"医疗保健人员为一名手术后患者开具了每12小时皮下注射肝素5,000单位的医嘱。现有的药瓶标签为10,000单位/毫升。护士每剂应注射多少毫升？（仅记录数值答案。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a numeric value only.)","terminalSentenceZh":"仅记录数值答案。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer per dose?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士每剂应注射多少毫升？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["0.5"],"numeric":{"value":0.5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: (Desired Dose / Available Dose) x Volume = (5,000 units / 10,000 units) x 1 mL = 0.5 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算：(需求剂量 / 现有剂量) x 体积 = (5,000 单位 / 10,000 单位) x 1 毫升 = 0.5 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the formula: Desired over Have times Quantity. Ensure the units match before calculating.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用公式：需求量除以现有量乘以体积。计算前确保单位一致。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":296,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.105","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.105.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.105.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[57,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,57],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing clients with thyroid dysfunction. For each clinical finding, click to specify if it is associated with hyperthyroidism or hypothyroidism.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估甲状腺功能障碍的患者。对于每一项临床发现，请点击以指明它是与甲状腺功能亢进症还是甲状腺功能减退症相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, click to specify if it is associated with hyperthyroidism or hypothyroidism.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每一项临床发现，请点击以指明它是与甲状腺功能亢进症还是甲状腺功能减退症相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is assessing clients with thyroid dysfunction.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估甲状腺功能障碍的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Heat intolerance","zh":"畏热"},{"id":"r2","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"r3","en":"Weight gain despite poor appetite","zh":"尽管食欲不佳但体重增加"},{"id":"r4","en":"Diarrhea or frequent bowel movements","zh":"腹泻或排便频繁"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Hyperthyroidism","zh":"甲状腺功能亢进"},{"id":"c2","en":"Hypothyroidism","zh":"甲状腺功能减退"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hyperthyroidism involves a high metabolic rate (heat intolerance, diarrhea). Hypothyroidism involves a low metabolic rate (bradycardia, weight gain).","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺功能亢进涉及高代谢率（畏热、腹泻）。甲状腺功能减退涉及低代谢率（心动过缓、体重增加）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of hyperthyroidism as 'everything sped up' and hypothyroidism as 'everything slowed down'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将甲状腺功能亢进想象为“一切都加速了”，将甲状腺功能减退想象为“一切都减慢了”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":297,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.106","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.106.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.106.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,89],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"A nurse in the emergency department is assessing four clients who arrived simultaneously.","fullStemZh":"急诊科的一名护士正在评估同时到达的四名患者。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse in the emergency department is assessing four clients who arrived simultaneously.","terminalSentenceZh":"急诊科的一名护士正在评估同时到达的四名患者。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first assess the client with {{1}} because this client is at highest risk for {{2}}.","zh":"护士应首先评估患有 {{1}} 的患者，因为该患者发生 {{2}} 的风险最高。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"sudden onset of the 'worst headache of my life'","zh":"突然发作的“一生中最严重的头痛”"},{"id":"o3","en":"a history of controlled hypertension asking for a refill","zh":"有受控高血压病史并要求续药"},{"id":"o2","en":"a closed fracture of the right radius","zh":"右桡骨闭合性骨折"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"compartment syndrome","zh":"骨筋膜室综合征"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypertensive crisis","zh":"高血压危象"},{"id":"o1","en":"hemorrhagic stroke","zh":"出血性脑卒中"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The description 'worst headache of my life' is a classic sign of a ruptured cerebral aneurysm causing a subarachnoid hemorrhage. This is a life-threatening emergency compared to a closed fracture or a simple medication refill.","rationaleCorrectZh":"“一生中最严重的头痛”这一描述是脑动脉瘤破裂导致蛛网膜下腔出血的经典体征。与闭合性骨折或简单的药物续方相比，这是一种危及生命的紧急情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize sudden, severe symptoms that suggest neurological or cardiovascular emergencies.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先处理提示神经系统或心血管系统紧急情况的突然、严重的症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":298,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.107","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.107.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.107.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,63],"fullStemEn":"A client was admitted 48 hours ago for a fractured femur and is now experiencing tremors, agitation, and a blood pressure of 160/100 mmHg. Which assessment finding is the most critical for the nurse to report immediately?","fullStemZh":"一名患者48小时前因股骨骨折入院，现在出现震颤、激动，血压为160/100 mmHg。护士最需要立即报告的关键评估发现是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding is the most critical for the nurse to report immediately?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最需要立即报告的关键评估发现是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client was admitted 48 hours ago for a fractured femur and is now experiencing tremors, agitation, and a blood pressure of 160/100 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者48小时前因股骨骨折入院，现在出现震颤、激动，血压为160/100 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hand tremors when reaching for a cup.","zh":"拿杯子时手部震颤。"},{"id":"C","en":"Visual hallucinations of insects crawling on the wall.","zh":"看到墙上有昆虫爬行的幻视。"},{"id":"B","en":"Report of being restless and unable to sleep.","zh":"报告焦躁不安且无法入睡。"},{"id":"D","en":"Occasional diaphoresis and nausea.","zh":"偶尔出汗和恶心。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hallucinations indicate that the client may be progressing to alcohol withdrawal delirium (delirium tremens), which is a medical emergency with a high mortality rate if untreated. Tremors and restlessness are earlier and less critical signs of withdrawal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"幻觉表明患者可能正在进展为酒精戒断性谵妄（震颤谵妄），如果不及早治疗，这是一种死亡率很高的一类内科急症。震颤和焦躁是戒断早期且不太关键的体征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In withdrawal scenarios, differentiate between minor symptoms and major symptoms that indicate a life-threatening change in status (like hallucinations or seizures).","testTakingStrategyZh":"在戒断情境中，区分轻微症状和提示危及生命的状态变化（如幻觉或癫痫发作）的主要症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client was admitted 48 hours ago for a fractured femur and is now experiencing tremors, agitation, and a blood pressure of 160/100 mmHg.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患者48小时前因股骨骨折入院，现在出现震颤、激动，血压为160/100 mmHg。"}
{"queueIndex":299,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.108","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.108.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.108.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[175,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for an older adult client who is on bed rest following hip surgery. Which interventions should the nurse implement to prevent complications of immobility? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名髋关节手术后卧床的老年患者。护士应实施哪些干预措施来预防不活动的并发症？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse implement to prevent complications of immobility?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪些干预措施来预防不活动的并发症？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Increase oral fluid intake unless contraindicated.","zh":"增加口服液体摄入量，除非有禁忌。"},{"id":"B","en":"Perform passive range-of-motion exercises on all joints.","zh":"对所有关节进行被动全范围关节运动练习。"},{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the use of an incentive spirometer every hour while awake.","zh":"鼓励在清醒时每小时使用一次激励性肺活量计。"},{"id":"D","en":"Maintain the client in a supine position for the majority of the day.","zh":"全天大部分时间让患者保持仰卧位。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply sequential compression devices (SCDs) while in bed.","zh":"在床上时应用顺序加压装置 (SCD)。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Prevention of immobility complications focuses on pulmonary hygiene (incentive spirometry), venous thromboembolism prevention (SCDs), and hydration (fluids). Performing passive ROM on ALL joints is inappropriate because post-hip-surgery patients have specific hip precautions that restrict certain movements; indiscriminate ROM risks dislocating the operative hip. Maintaining a client in a supine position worsens immobility complications rather than preventing them.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防制动并发症的重点在于肺部卫生（呼吸训练器）、静脉血栓栓塞预防（序贯加压装置）和补液。对所有关节进行被动关节活动范围锻炼是不合适的，因为髋关节术后患者有特定的髋关节注意事项，限制某些动作；不加区分的关节活动训练有髋关节脱位的风险。将患者长时间保持仰卧位会加重而非预防制动并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on nursing actions that address multiple systems affected by immobility: respiratory, cardiovascular, and gastrointestinal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注针对受不活动影响的多个系统（呼吸、心血管和胃肠道）的护理措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":300,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.109","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.109.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.109.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,58],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who requires physical restraints due to violent behavior. For each nursing action, click to specify if it is a correct or incorrect practice according to safety standards.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名因暴力行为而需要身体约束的患者。对于每一项护理操作，请根据安全标准点击以指明它是正确还是错误的做法。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing action, click to specify if it is a correct or incorrect practice according to safety standards.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每一项护理操作，请根据安全标准点击以指明它是正确还是错误的做法。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who requires physical restraints due to violent behavior.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名因暴力行为而需要身体约束的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Tie the restraint to the side rails of the bed.","zh":"将约束带系在床栏上。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Use a quick-release knot when securing the restraint.","zh":"固定约束带时使用活结（快速释放结）。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Assess skin integrity and neurovascular status every 2 hours.","zh":"每2小时评估一次皮肤完整性和神经血管状态。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Renew the restraint order every 48 hours.","zh":"每48小时更新一次约束医嘱。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Incorrect","zh":"错误"},{"id":"c1","en":"Correct","zh":"正确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Restraints must be tied to the bed frame (not rails) using quick-release knots. Assessment occurs frequently (at least every 2 hours). For violent behavior, the order must typically be renewed much more frequently (e.g., every 4 hours for adults).","rationaleCorrectZh":"必须使用活结将约束带系在床架（而非床栏）上。评估应频繁进行（至少每2小时一次）。对于暴力行为，通常必须更频繁地更新医嘱（例如，成人每4小时一次）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the primary safety rule for restraints: 'Bed frame, quick-release knot, and frequent monitoring'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住约束的主要安全规则：“床架、活结和频繁监测”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":301,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p5_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.110","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.110.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.110.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,132],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,51],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes is admitted with a blood glucose of 550 mg/dL, arterial pH of 7.25, and serum bicarbonate of 14 mEq/L.","fullStemZh":"一名1型糖尿病患者入院，血糖为550 mg/dL，动脉pH为7.25，血清碳酸氢盐为14 mEq/L。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes is admitted with a blood glucose of 550 mg/dL, arterial pH of 7.25, and serum bicarbonate of 14 mEq/L.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名1型糖尿病患者入院，血糖为550 mg/dL，动脉pH为7.25，血清碳酸氢盐为14 mEq/L。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's first priority is to initiate {{1}}. Once the blood glucose drops to 250 mg/dL, the nurse should {{2}}.","zh":"护士的首要任务是开始 {{1}}。一旦血糖降至 250 mg/dL，护士应 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"subcutaneous insulin glargine","zh":"皮下注射甘精胰岛素"},{"id":"o1","en":"intravenous fluid resuscitation","zh":"静脉补液复苏"},{"id":"o3","en":"bicarbonate infusion","zh":"碳酸氢盐输注"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"discontinue the insulin drip","zh":"停止胰岛素静脉滴注"},{"id":"o1","en":"add dextrose to the IV fluids","zh":"在静脉输液中加入葡萄糖"},{"id":"o3","en":"bolus additional regular insulin","zh":"额外静推正规胰岛素"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In DKA, the immediate priority is fluid replacement to treat dehydration and restore perfusion. When blood glucose falls below 250 mg/dL, add dextrose to prevent hypoglycemia while insulin continues until ketoacidosis resolves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 DKA 中，当务之急是补液以治疗脱水并恢复灌注。当血糖降至 250 mg/dL 以下时，在静脉输液中加入葡萄糖以预防低血糖，同时继续胰岛素治疗直至酮症酸中毒纠正。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the DKA sequence: fluids first; assess and manage potassium before insulin; then add dextrose below 250 mg/dL so insulin can continue safely.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 DKA 的顺序：先补液；在胰岛素前评估并处理血钾；然后在血糖低于 250 mg/dL 时加入葡萄糖，使胰岛素可安全持续。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":302,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_burn_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.111","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.111.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.111.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[205,241],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,99],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 154 lbs has sustained 40% total body surface area (TBSA) burns. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA), calculate the total fluid resuscitation volume required in the first 24 hours. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"一名体重 154 磅的患者遭受了 40% 总体表面积 (TBSA) 的烧伤。根据 Parkland 公式（4 mL/kg/%TBSA），计算前 24 小时所需的总补液量。（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA), calculate the total fluid resuscitation volume required in the first 24 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据 Parkland 公式（4 mL/kg/%TBSA），计算前 24 小时所需的总补液量。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["11200"],"numeric":{"value":11200,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Parkland formula is calculated as 4 mL × weight in kg × %TBSA. First, convert weight to kg: 154 lbs / 2.2 = 70 kg. Then, calculate the volume: 4 mL × 70 kg × 40 = 11,200 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Parkland 公式的计算方法为 4 mL × 体重 (kg) × %TBSA。首先，将体重转换为公斤：154 磅 / 2.2 = 70 公斤。然后计算容量：4 mL × 70 kg × 40 = 11,200 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always convert pounds to kilograms first by dividing by 2.2 before applying the Parkland formula.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在应用 Parkland 公式之前，务必先除以 2.2 将磅转换为公斤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":303,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_burn_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.112","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.112.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.112.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,234],"terminalOffsetsZh":[95,108],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 80 kg with 30% TBSA burns is to receive fluid resuscitation using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA). Calculate the IV flow rate in mL/hr for the first 8 hours of resuscitation. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"一名体重 80 公斤、烧伤面积为 30% TBSA 的患者将使用 Parkland 公式 (4 mL/kg/%TBSA) 进行补液。计算复苏前 8 小时的静脉输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the IV flow rate in mL/hr for the first 8 hours of resuscitation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算复苏前 8 小时的静脉输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["600"],"numeric":{"value":600,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total volume for 24 hours = 4 mL × 80 kg × 30 = 9,600 mL. Half of the total volume must be administered in the first 8 hours: 9,600 / 2 = 4,800 mL. The hourly rate for the first 8 hours is 4,800 mL / 8 hr = 600 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"24 小时的总容量 = 4 mL × 80 kg × 30 = 9,600 毫升。总容量的一半必须在前 8 小时内输入：9,600 / 2 = 4,800 毫升。前 8 小时的每小时输液速度为 4,800 mL / 8 hr = 600 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the Parkland formula gives the total 24-hour volume, and half of that total must be given in the first 8 hours from the time of injury.","testTakingStrategyZh":"请记住，Parkland 公式给出的是 24 小时的总容量，其中一半必须在受伤后的前 8 小时内输入。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Calculate the IV flow rate in mL/hr for the first 8 hours of resuscitation.","controlSentenceZh":"计算复苏前 8 小时的静脉输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（"}
{"queueIndex":304,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_iv_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.113","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.113.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.113.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,193],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,82],"fullStemEn":"The healthcare provider orders 1,000 mL of 0.45% normal saline to be infused over 8 hours. The nurse should set the infusion pump to deliver how many mL/hr? (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"医疗服务提供者开具医嘱：8 小时内输入 1,000 毫升 0.45% 生理盐水。护士应将输液泵设置为每小时输送多少毫升 (mL/hr)？（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should set the infusion pump to deliver how many mL/hr?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将输液泵设置为每小时输送多少毫升 (mL/hr)？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["125"],"numeric":{"value":125,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To find the mL/hr rate, divide the total volume by the total time in hours: 1,000 mL / 8 hr = 125 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"要计算 mL/hr 速度，用总容量除以总小时数：1,000 mL / 8 hr = 125 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For basic IV rate calculations, ensure the time is in hours and the volume is in milliliters.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于基础静脉输液速度计算，确保时间单位是小时，容量单位是毫升。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":305,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_iv_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.114","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.114.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.114.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,237],"terminalOffsetsZh":[84,97],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer 500 mL of Lactated Ringer's solution over 4 hours. The drop factor of the manual IV tubing is 20 gtt/mL. At what rate in gtt/min should the nurse set the infusion? (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"护士准备在 4 小时内输注 500 毫升乳酸林格氏液。手动输液器的滴系数为 20 滴/毫升 (gtt/mL)。护士应将输液速度设置为每分钟多少滴 (gtt/min)？（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At what rate in gtt/min should the nurse set the infusion?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将输液速度设置为每分钟多少滴 (gtt/min)？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"gtt/min","zh":"滴/分钟"},"acceptable":["42"],"numeric":{"value":42,"tolerance":0,"unit":"gtt/min"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculate mL/hr first: 500 mL / 4 hr = 125 mL/hr. Then calculate gtt/min: (125 mL/hr × 20 gtt/mL) / 60 min = 41.666... Rounding to the nearest whole number gives 42 gtt/min.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先计算 mL/hr：500 mL / 4 hr = 125 mL/hr。然后计算 gtt/min：(125 mL/hr × 20 gtt/mL) / 60 min = 41.666... 四舍五入到最接近的整数为 42 gtt/min。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the formula: (Total Volume in mL × Drop Factor) / Time in Minutes = gtt/min.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用公式：（总毫升数 × 滴系数）/ 分钟数 = 滴/分钟。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At what rate in gtt/min should the nurse set the infusion?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应将输液速度设置为每分钟多少滴 (gtt/min)？（"}
{"queueIndex":306,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_burn_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.115","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.115.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.115.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[223,259],"terminalOffsetsZh":[118,131],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 60 kg with 50% TBSA burns is being resuscitated using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA). The burns occurred at 12:00 PM. Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr for the period between 8:00 PM and 4:00 AM. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"一名体重 60 公斤、烧伤面积为 50% TBSA 的患者正根据 Parkland 公式 (4 mL/kg/%TBSA) 进行复苏。烧伤发生在中午 12:00。计算晚上 8:00 到凌晨 4:00 期间的输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr for the period between 8:00 PM and 4:00 AM.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算晚上 8:00 到凌晨 4:00 期间的输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["375"],"numeric":{"value":375,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total 24h volume = 4 mL × 60 kg × 50 = 12,000 mL. The first 8 hours (12 PM to 8 PM) require 50% of total: 6,000 mL. The remaining 16 hours (8 PM to 12 PM next day) require the other 50%: 6,000 mL. The question asks for the rate from 8 PM to 4 AM, which is the first half of the remaining 16 hours (often divided into two 8-hour blocks). 6,000 mL / 16 hours = 375 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"24 小时总容量 = 4 mL × 60 kg × 50 = 12,000 毫升。前 8 小时（中午 12 点至晚上 8 点）需要总量的 50%：6,000 毫升。剩余 16 小时（晚上 8 点至次日中午 12 点）需要另外 50%：6,000 毫升。题目要求计算晚上 8 点到凌晨 4 点的速率，这是剩余 16 小时的前一半（通常分为两个 8 小时时段）。6,000 mL / 16 小时 = 375 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The Parkland formula allocates half the volume to the first 8 hours and the remaining half over the following 16 hours. Hourly rates are constant within those specific time blocks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"Parkland 公式在前 8 小时分配一半容量，在接下来的 16 小时分配剩余的一半。在这些特定的时间段内，每小时的速率是恒定的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":307,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_heparin_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.116","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.116.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.116.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,247],"terminalOffsetsZh":[101,114],"fullStemEn":"The provider orders a continuous heparin infusion at 1,100 units/hr. The pharmacy provides a bag containing 25,000 units of heparin in 250 mL of 5% dextrose in water (D5W). Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"服务提供者开具医嘱：连续肝素输注，速度为 1,100 单位/小时。药房提供的一袋药液含 25,000 单位肝素溶于 250 毫升 5% 葡萄糖注射液 (D5W) 中。计算输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["11"],"numeric":{"value":11,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Use the formula: (Desired Dose / Have) × Volume = Rate. (1,100 units/hr / 25,000 units) × 250 mL = 11 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用公式：（所需剂量 / 现有剂量）× 容量 = 速度。(1,100 单位/小时 / 25,000 单位) × 250 mL = 11 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When calculating medication infusion rates, identify the concentration of the drug (units per mL) and apply the desired dose to find the volume per hour.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算药物输注速度时，确定药物浓度（每毫升单位数），并应用所需剂量以计算每小时容量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr.","controlSentenceZh":"计算输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（"}
{"queueIndex":308,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_weight_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.117","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.117.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.117.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[101,114],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 176 lbs is to receive a dopamine infusion at 5 mcg/kg/min. The pharmacy supplies dopamine 400 mg in 250 mL of 0.9% normal saline. Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr. (Round to the nearest tenth).","fullStemZh":"一名体重 176 磅的患者将接受 5 微克/公斤/分钟 (mcg/kg/min) 的多巴胺输注。药房提供 400 毫克多巴胺溶于 250 毫升 0.9% 生理盐水中。计算输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（四舍五入到小数点后一位）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest tenth).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到小数点后一位）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the infusion rate in mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算输液速度（单位：mL/hr）。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["15","15.0"],"numeric":{"value":15,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"1. Convert lbs to kg: 176 / 2.2 = 80 kg. 2. Calculate mcg/min: 5 mcg × 80 kg = 400 mcg/min. 3. Convert mcg/min to mcg/hr: 400 × 60 min = 24,000 mcg/hr. 4. Convert mcg to mg: 24,000 / 1,000 = 24 mg/hr. 5. Calculate mL/hr: (24 mg / 400 mg) × 250 mL = 15 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1. 将磅转换为公斤：176 / 2.2 = 80 kg。2. 计算 mcg/min：5 mcg × 80 kg = 400 mcg/min。3. 将 mcg/min 转换为 mcg/hr：400 × 60 min = 24,000 mcg/hr。4. 将 mcg 转换为 mg：24,000 / 1,000 = 24 mg/hr。5. 计算 mL/hr：(24 mg / 400 mg) × 250 mL = 15 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Perform weight conversion first, then proceed through conversion of minutes to hours and micrograms to milligrams to match the pharmacy's supply concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先进行体重转换，然后将分钟转换为小时，并将微克转换为毫克，以匹配药房提供的浓度规格。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":309,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_peds_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.118","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.118.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.118.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[209,245],"terminalOffsetsZh":[95,108],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer an antibiotic to a child who weighs 44 lbs. The ordered dose is 15 mg/kg. The medication is available as 250 mg/5 mL. How many mL should the nurse administer for one dose? (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"护士准备为一名体重 44 磅的儿童使用抗生素。医嘱剂量为 15 毫克/公斤 (mg/kg)。该药物规格为 250 毫克/5 毫升 (mg/5 mL)。护士单次剂量应给药多少毫升 (mL)？（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer for one dose?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士单次剂量应给药多少毫升 (mL)？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["6"],"numeric":{"value":6,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"1. Convert lbs to kg: 44 lbs / 2.2 = 20 kg. 2. Calculate dose in mg: 20 kg × 15 mg/kg = 300 mg. 3. Calculate volume in mL: (300 mg / 250 mg) × 5 mL = 6 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1. 将磅转换为公斤：44 磅 / 2.2 = 20 公斤。2. 计算以毫克为单位的剂量：20 kg × 15 mg/kg = 300 毫克。3. 计算以毫升为单位的容量：(300 mg / 250 mg) × 5 mL = 6 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always calculate the specific mg dose based on weight first, then convert that mg dose to the volume (mL) available.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终先根据体重计算具体的毫克剂量，然后将该毫克剂量转换为现有的毫升容量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":310,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_iv_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.119","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.119.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.119.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[109,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,72],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving an IV infusion of 1,000 mL at 150 mL/hr. After 4 hours, how many mL remain in the bag? (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"患者正在接受 1,000 毫升的静脉输注，速度为 150 毫升/小时 (mL/hr)。4 小时后，袋中还剩多少毫升？（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After 4 hours, how many mL remain in the bag?","penultimateSentenceZh":"4 小时后，袋中还剩多少毫升？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["400"],"numeric":{"value":400,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"1. Calculate volume infused: 150 mL/hr × 4 hr = 600 mL. 2. Subtract from total volume: 1,000 mL - 600 mL = 400 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1. 计算已输注容量：150 mL/hr × 4 hr = 600 毫升。2. 从总容量中减去：1,000 mL - 600 mL = 400 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Determine the amount of fluid already delivered by multiplying the rate by time, then subtract that from the initial volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"通过将速度乘以时间来确定已输送的液体量，然后从初始容量中减去该数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":311,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p6_burn_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.120","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.120.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.120.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,281],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,104],"fullStemEn":"A pediatric client weighing 20 kg sustained partial-thickness burns to 25% of the body. The healthcare provider orders fluid resuscitation using 3 mL/kg/%TBSA for the first 24 hours. Calculate the total volume of fluid in mL to be administered. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"一名体重 20 公斤的儿科患者身体 25% 面积遭受了深二度烧伤。医疗服务提供者要求在前 24 小时内按 3 mL/kg/%TBSA 进行补液。计算需输入的总液体量（单位：mL）。（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the total volume of fluid in mL to be administered.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算需输入的总液体量（单位：mL）。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["1500"],"numeric":{"value":1500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the specific formula provided in the order: 3 mL × 20 kg × 25 = 1,500 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用医嘱中提供的特定公式：3 mL × 20 kg × 25 = 1,500 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a specific resuscitation formula is provided in the order (e.g., 3 mL/kg/% instead of the standard Parkland 4 mL), always use the value specified in the prompt.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当医嘱中提供特定的复苏公式（例如 3 mL/kg/% 而不是标准的 Parkland 4 mL）时，请务必使用题目中指定的数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":312,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.121","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.121.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.121.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,228],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,67],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client who presents with dyspnea and fatigue. For each assessment finding, click to specify if the finding is more consistent with right-sided heart failure or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名出现呼吸困难和疲劳的患者。对于每个评估结果，请点击以指明该结果是更符合右侧心力衰竭还是慢性阻塞性肺疾病 (COPD)。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, click to specify if the finding is more consistent with right-sided heart failure or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个评估结果，请点击以指明该结果是更符合右侧心力衰竭还是慢性阻塞性肺疾病 (COPD)。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a client who presents with dyspnea and fatigue.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名出现呼吸困难和疲劳的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Jugular venous distension","zh":"颈静脉怒张"},{"id":"r2","en":"Barrel chest","zh":"桶状胸"},{"id":"r3","en":"Dependent edema","zh":"下垂性水肿"},{"id":"r4","en":"Pursed-lip breathing","zh":"缩唇呼吸"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"COPD","zh":"COPD"},{"id":"c1","en":"Right-sided Heart Failure","zh":"右侧心力衰竭"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Jugular venous distension and dependent edema are classic signs of right-sided heart failure due to systemic venous congestion. Barrel chest and pursed-lip breathing are characteristic of COPD due to air trapping and compensatory breathing techniques.","rationaleCorrectZh":"颈静脉怒张和下垂性水肿是由于体循环静脉淤血引起的右侧心力衰竭的经典体征。桶状胸和缩唇呼吸是由于空气滞留和补偿性呼吸技术引起的 COPD 的特征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between systemic circulatory issues (heart failure) and chronic airway/alveolar issues (COPD).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分系统循环问题（心力衰竭）和慢性气道/肺泡问题（COPD）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":313,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.122","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.122.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.122.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,77],"fullStemEn":"A client with heart failure who is taking digoxin and furosemide reports nausea, vomiting, and seeing yellow halos around lights. The client's potassium level is 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L).","fullStemZh":"一名患有心力衰竭并正在服用地高辛和呋塞米的患者报告恶心、呕吐，并看到灯光周围有黄色光晕。该患者的血钾水平为 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L)。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client's potassium level is 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L).","terminalSentenceZh":"该患者的血钾水平为 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L)。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with heart failure who is taking digoxin and furosemide reports nausea, vomiting, and seeing yellow halos around lights.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有心力衰竭并正在服用地高辛和呋塞米的患者报告恶心、呕吐，并看到灯光周围有黄色光晕。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse identifies that the client is experiencing symptoms of {{1}} which is exacerbated by {{2}}.","zh":"护士确定该患者正在经历 {{1}} 的症状，这种情况因 {{2}} 而加剧。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"hypokalemic periodic paralysis","zh":"低钾性周期性麻痹"},{"id":"o2","en":"furosemide overdose","zh":"呋塞米过量"},{"id":"o1","en":"digoxin toxicity","zh":"地高辛中毒"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic alkalosis","zh":"代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypernatremia","zh":"高钠血症"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nausea, vomiting, and visual disturbances (yellow halos) are classic signs of digoxin toxicity. Hypokalemia (potassium < 3.5 mEq/L) sensitizes the myocardium to digoxin, increasing the risk of toxicity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"恶心、呕吐和视觉障碍（黄色光晕）是地高辛中毒的经典体征。低钾血症（钾 < 3.5 mEq/L）会使心肌对地高辛敏感，从而增加中毒风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the relationship between potassium levels and digoxin; low potassium increases the risk of digoxin toxicity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想钾水平与地高辛之间的关系；低钾会增加地高辛中毒的风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":314,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.123","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.123.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.123.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,50],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is evaluating a client's fluid volume status. For each clinical finding, click to specify if the finding is consistent with Fluid Volume Deficit or Fluid Volume Excess.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估患者的体液容量状态。对于每个临床发现，请点击以指明该发现是符合体液量不足还是体液量过多。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, click to specify if the finding is consistent with Fluid Volume Deficit or Fluid Volume Excess.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个临床发现，请点击以指明该发现是符合体液量不足还是体液量过多。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is evaluating a client's fluid volume status.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估患者的体液容量状态。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Bounding pulse","zh":"洪脉"},{"id":"r2","en":"Decreased skin turgor","zh":"皮肤弹性降低"},{"id":"r3","en":"Crackles in lungs","zh":"肺部湿啰音"},{"id":"r4","en":"Orthostatic hypotension","zh":"体位性低血压"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Fluid Volume Deficit","zh":"体液量不足"},{"id":"c2","en":"Fluid Volume Excess","zh":"体液量过多"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fluid volume excess is characterized by bounding pulses and pulmonary congestion (crackles). Fluid volume deficit leads to decreased skin turgor and orthostatic hypotension due to reduced intravascular volume.","rationaleCorrectZh":"体液量过多的特征是洪脉和肺部淤血（湿啰音）。体液量不足由于血管内血容量减少，导致皮肤弹性降低和体位性低血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about 'too much fluid' (excess) vs. 'not enough fluid' (deficit) and how each affects pressure and lung sounds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑“体液过多”（过量）与“体液不足”（缺失），以及每种情况如何影响压力和肺部声音。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is evaluating a client's fluid volume status.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在评估患者的体液容量状态。"}
{"queueIndex":315,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.124","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.124.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.124.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,63],"fullStemEn":"The registered nurse (RN) is planning care for a group of clients. The RN is working with a licensed practical nurse (LPN) and an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在为一组患者制定护理计划。该 RN 与一名执业护士 (LPN) 和一名非持证辅助人员 (UAP) 合作。","terminalSentenceEn":"The RN is working with a licensed practical nurse (LPN) and an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","terminalSentenceZh":"该 RN 与一名执业护士 (LPN) 和一名非持证辅助人员 (UAP) 合作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The registered nurse (RN) is planning care for a group of clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在为一组患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The RN should delegate {{1}} to the LPN and {{2}} to the UAP.","zh":"RN 应将 {{1}} 委派给 LPN，将 {{2}} 委派给 UAP。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"assessing a newly admitted client","zh":"评估新入院的患者"},{"id":"o2","en":"developing a teaching plan for diabetes","zh":"制定糖尿病教学计划"},{"id":"o1","en":"performing a sterile dressing change","zh":"进行无菌伤口换药"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"measuring intake and output","zh":"测量出入量"},{"id":"o2","en":"administering oral medications","zh":"给口服药"},{"id":"o3","en":"evaluating the effectiveness of pain meds","zh":"评估镇痛药的效果"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs can perform sterile procedures like dressing changes. UAPs can perform routine tasks like measuring intake and output. RNs must handle initial assessments, teaching plans, and evaluations.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN 可以执行无菌操作，如伤口换药。UAP 可以执行常规任务，如测量出入量。RN 必须负责初始评估、教学计划和评价。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the 'TAPE' acronym for RN tasks: Teaching, Assessment, Planning, and Evaluation. These cannot be delegated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对 RN 任务使用“TAPE”缩写：教学 (Teaching)、评估 (Assessment)、计划 (Planning) 和评价 (Evaluation)。这些任务不能委派。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":316,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.125","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.125.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.125.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[68,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for clients with different infections. For each condition, click to specify the appropriate type of isolation precautions.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为患有不同感染的患者提供护理。对于每种疾病，请点击以指明适当的隔离预防措施类型。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each condition, click to specify the appropriate type of isolation precautions.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每种疾病，请点击以指明适当的隔离预防措施类型。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for clients with different infections.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为患有不同感染的患者提供护理。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Disseminated Herpes Zoster","zh":"播散性带状疱疹"},{"id":"r2","en":"Clostridium difficile (C. diff)","zh":"艰难梭菌 (C. diff)"},{"id":"r3","en":"Influenza","zh":"流感"},{"id":"r4","en":"Pulmonary Tuberculosis","zh":"肺结核"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Airborne","zh":"空气预防"},{"id":"c1","en":"Contact","zh":"接触预防"},{"id":"c2","en":"Droplet","zh":"飞沫预防"}],"selectionMode":"multiple_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1","c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. diff requires contact precautions. Influenza requires droplet precautions. Pulmonary tuberculosis requires airborne precautions. Disseminated herpes zoster requires both airborne AND contact precautions, because the virus can spread via airborne route from lesions and by direct contact with vesicular fluid.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艰难梭菌需要接触预防。流感需要飞沫预防。肺结核需要空气预防。播散性带状疱疹需要同时采取空气预防和接触预防，因为病毒既可通过病灶的气溶胶传播，也可通过直接接触水疱液传播。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize common diseases for each precaution type. Remember that disseminated herpes zoster requires BOTH airborne and contact precautions — it is an exception that combines two precaution types.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住每种预防措施类型的常见疾病。请记住，播散性带状疱疹需要同时采取空气预防和接触预防——这是一个结合两种预防类型的例外情况。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":317,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.126","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.126.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.126.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,54],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes is admitted with a blood glucose of 850 mg/dL (47.2 mmol/L), profound dehydration, and no ketones in the urine.","fullStemZh":"一名 2 型糖尿病患者入院，血糖为 850 mg/dL (47.2 mmol/L)，极度脱水，尿液中无酮体。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes is admitted with a blood glucose of 850 mg/dL (47.2 mmol/L), profound dehydration, and no ketones in the urine.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名 2 型糖尿病患者入院，血糖为 850 mg/dL (47.2 mmol/L)，极度脱水，尿液中无酮体。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse suspects the client is experiencing {{1}} and the priority intervention is {{2}}.","zh":"护士怀疑该患者正在经历 {{1}}，首选的干预措施是 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","zh":"糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA)"},{"id":"o3","en":"Hypoglycemic Unawareness","zh":"无症状性低血糖"},{"id":"o1","en":"Hyperosmolar Hyperglycemic State (HHS)","zh":"高渗性高血糖状态 (HHS)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"administering sublingual glucose","zh":"给予舌下含服葡萄糖"},{"id":"o1","en":"vigorous fluid resuscitation","zh":"积极的液体复苏"},{"id":"o2","en":"intravenous bicarbonate administration","zh":"静脉注射碳酸氢盐"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HHS is characterized by high blood glucose (>600 mg/dL), dehydration, and lack of ketosis, typically seen in type 2 diabetes. Priority is fluid replacement to correct dehydration and hyperosmolality.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HHS 的特征是高血糖 (>600 mg/dL)、脱水且无酮症，通常见于 2 型糖尿病。首要任务是补液以纠正脱水和高渗透压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast DKA (ketones present, lower glucose) with HHS (no ketones, extremely high glucose). Both require fluids, but HHS needs more volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对比 DKA（有酮体，血糖较低）和 HHS（无酮体，血糖极高）。两者都需要补液，但 HHS 需要更大的容量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":318,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.127","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.127.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.127.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is interacting with clients using various defense mechanisms. For each client statement, click to specify the appropriate defense mechanism.","fullStemZh":"护士正在与使用各种防御机制的患者进行交流。对于每位患者的陈述，请点击以指明适当的防御机制。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client statement, click to specify the appropriate defense mechanism.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每位患者的陈述，请点击以指明适当的防御机制。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is interacting with clients using various defense mechanisms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在与使用各种防御机制的患者进行交流。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"\"I didn't pass the exam because the teacher is bad.\"","zh":"“我考试没及格是因为老师教得不好。”"},{"id":"r2","en":"A person who is angry at their boss goes home and yells at their spouse.","zh":"一个对老板生气的人回家后对配偶大喊大叫。"},{"id":"r3","en":"\"I don't have a drinking problem; I can stop anytime I want.\"","zh":"“我没有酗酒问题；我想戒随时都能戒。”"},{"id":"r4","en":"A person who is aggressive starts taking boxing classes.","zh":"一个有好斗倾向的人开始参加拳击课程。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Rationalization","zh":"合理化"},{"id":"c2","en":"Displacement","zh":"置换/转移"},{"id":"c4","en":"Sublimation","zh":"升华"},{"id":"c1","en":"Denial","zh":"否认"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rationalization involves justifying behaviors with socially acceptable reasons. Displacement shifts emotions to a safer target. Denial is refusing to acknowledge reality. Sublimation channels unacceptable impulses into socially acceptable activities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合理化包括用社会认可的理由来解释行为。置换是将情绪转移到更安全的目标。否认是拒绝承认现实。升华是将不可接受的冲动转化为社会认可的活动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the 'target' of the emotion for displacement and the 'justification' for rationalization.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注置换中情绪的“目标”和合理化中的“辩解”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":319,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.128","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.128.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.128.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,79],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"During a well-child visit, a nurse assesses a 6-month-old infant's development.","fullStemZh":"在一次健康儿童访视中，护士评估了一名 6 个月大婴儿的发育情况。","terminalSentenceEn":"During a well-child visit, a nurse assesses a 6-month-old infant's development.","terminalSentenceZh":"在一次健康儿童访视中，护士评估了一名 6 个月大婴儿的发育情况。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse expects the infant to be able to {{1}} and should advise the parents that {{2}} will typically occur by 12 months.","zh":"护士预计该婴儿能够 {{1}}，并应告知家长，{{2}} 通常会在 12 个月大时出现。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"pincer grasp","zh":"钳式抓握"},{"id":"o1","en":"sit with support","zh":"在有支撑的情况下坐稳"},{"id":"o3","en":"walk independently","zh":"独立行走"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"tripling of birth weight","zh":"体重达到出生时的三倍"},{"id":"o3","en":"closure of the posterior fontanel","zh":"后囟门闭合"},{"id":"o2","en":"doubling of birth weight","zh":"体重达到出生时的两倍"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"By 6 months, infants typically sit with support and double their birth weight. By 12 months, birth weight should triple and the pincer grasp is well-developed. The posterior fontanel closes at 2 months.","rationaleCorrectZh":"到 6 个月时，婴儿通常可以在有支撑的情况下坐稳，且体重翻倍。到 12 个月时，体重应达到出生时的三倍，钳式抓握也发育完善。后囟门在 2 个月大时闭合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the 'double by 6, triple by 12' rule for infant weight gain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住婴儿体重增加的规律：“6个月翻倍，12个月三倍”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":320,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.129","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.129.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.129.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use different mobility aids. For each instruction, click to specify the mobility aid it describes.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教患者如何使用不同的助行器。对于每条指令，请点击以指明它所描述的助行器。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each instruction, click to specify the mobility aid it describes.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每条指令，请点击以指明它所描述的助行器。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use different mobility aids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教患者如何使用不同的助行器。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Advance the aid 6-10 inches, then step with the affected leg.","zh":"将助行器向前推进 6-10 英寸，然后用受影响的腿迈步。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hold the aid on the stronger (unaffected) side.","zh":"将助行器握在健侧（不受影响的一侧）。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Keep a 2-3 finger width gap between the axilla and the top of the aid.","zh":"腋下与助行器顶部之间保持 2-3 个指宽的间隙。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Elbows should be flexed 15-30 degrees when holding the handgrips.","zh":"握住手柄时，肘部应弯曲 15-30 度。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Walker","zh":"助行架"},{"id":"c3","en":"Crutches","zh":"拐杖"},{"id":"c1","en":"Cane","zh":"手杖"}],"selectionMode":"multiple_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1","c2","c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Canes are held on the stronger side. Walkers are moved forward before stepping. Crutches must have space under the axilla to avoid nerve damage. All handgrips require 15-30 degree elbow flexion for proper height.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手杖应握在健侧。助行架在迈步前向前移动。拐杖腋下必须留有空间以避免神经损伤。所有助行器的手柄都需要肘部弯曲 15-30 度以确保高度合适。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for keywords like 'axilla' for crutches and 'stronger side' for canes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找关键词，如拐杖的“腋下”和手杖的“健侧”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":321,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p7_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.130","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.130.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.130.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer intravenous (IV) fluids to a client with cerebral edema.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名患有脑水肿的患者输注静脉 (IV) 液体。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer intravenous (IV) fluids to a client with cerebral edema.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名患有脑水肿的患者输注静脉 (IV) 液体。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should avoid {{1}} solutions and expects the provider to order a {{2}} solution to shift fluid out of the brain cells.","zh":"护士应避免使用 {{1}} 溶液，并预计医生会开出 {{2}} 溶液，以将液体移出脑细胞。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"hypotonic (e.g., 0.45% NaCl)","zh":"低渗（如 0.45% NaCl）"},{"id":"o2","en":"isotonic (e.g., 0.9% NaCl)","zh":"等渗（如 0.9% NaCl）"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypertonic (e.g., 3% NaCl)","zh":"高渗（如 3% NaCl）"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"hypertonic","zh":"高渗"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypotonic","zh":"低渗"},{"id":"o3","en":"colloid","zh":"胶体"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypotonic solutions (like 0.45% NaCl) cause cells to swell, which would worsen cerebral edema. Hypertonic solutions (like 3% NaCl or Mannitol) pull fluid out of the cells and into the vascular space, reducing swelling.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低渗溶液（如 0.45% NaCl）会导致细胞肿胀，从而加重脑水肿。高渗溶液（如 3% NaCl 或甘露醇）会将液体从细胞内拉出进入血管间隙，从而减轻肿胀。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Understand osmosis: water follows solute. High concentration (hypertonic) pulls water out of cells.","testTakingStrategyZh":"理解渗透作用：水随溶质走。高浓度（高渗）会将水从细胞中拉出。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":322,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.131","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.131.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.131.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,128],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,33],"fullStemEn":"The nurse on a medical-surgical unit has received the shift report for four clients. Which client should the nurse assess first?","fullStemZh":"内外科病房的护士收到了四名患者的换班报告。护士应首先评估哪位患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the nurse assess first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先评估哪位患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse on a medical-surgical unit has received the shift report for four clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"内外科病房的护士收到了四名患者的换班报告。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client with acute pancreatitis reporting severe epigastric pain and a fever of 101.2 °F (38.4 °C).","zh":"一名患有急性胰腺炎、报告有严重的上腹部疼痛且发烧 101.2 °F (38.4 °C) 的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client with deep vein thrombosis (DVT) who is receiving heparin and has an aPTT of 70 seconds.","zh":"一名患有深静脉血栓 (DVT)、正在接受肝素治疗且 aPTT 为 70 秒的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with a new-onset atrial fibrillation whose heart rate is 124 beats/minute.","zh":"一名新发心房颤动且心率为 124 次/分钟的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with chronic renal failure whose potassium level is 5.8 mEq/L (5.8 mmol/L).","zh":"一名患有慢性肾功能衰竭且血钾水平为 5.8 mEq/L (5.8 mmol/L) 的患者。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New-onset atrial fibrillation with a rapid ventricular response (RVR) requires immediate assessment and intervention to prevent hemodynamic instability and potential stroke.","rationaleCorrectZh":"伴有快速心室率 (RVR) 的新发心房颤动需要立即评估和干预，以防止血流动力学不稳定和潜在的中风。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) and the concept of stability versus instability. New-onset conditions often take precedence over chronic or expected findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）原则以及稳定与不稳定的概念。新发疾病通常优先于慢性或预期发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":323,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.132","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.132.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.132.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Which task is most appropriate for the nurse to delegate to an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","fullStemZh":"护士最适合将哪项任务委派给非执照辅助人员 (UAP)？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which task is most appropriate for the nurse to delegate to an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最适合将哪项任务委派给非执照辅助人员 (UAP)？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administering a prescribed subcutaneous insulin injection to a stable client.","zh":"给一名稳定的患者注射处方的皮下胰岛素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Evaluating the effectiveness of pain medication administered to a client 30 minutes ago.","zh":"评估 30 分钟前给患者服用的止痛药的效果。"},{"id":"A","en":"Teaching a client how to use an incentive spirometer.","zh":"教患者如何使用激励型肺量计。"},{"id":"D","en":"Collecting a clean-catch urine specimen from a client with a suspected urinary tract infection.","zh":"从疑似尿路感染的患者那里采集中段清洁尿标本。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Collecting a non-invasive specimen like a clean-catch urine sample is within the scope of practice for a UAP.","rationaleCorrectZh":"采集非侵入性标本（如中段清洁尿标本）属于 UAP 的实践范围。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the five rights of delegation. Tasks that involve assessment, teaching, or nursing judgment should not be delegated to UAPs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住委派的五个正确原则。涉及评估、教学或护理判断的任务不应委派给 UAP。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":324,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.133","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.133.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.133.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,45],"fullStemEn":"The registered nurse (RN) is working with a licensed practical nurse (LPN). Which client should the RN assign to the LPN?","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正与一名执业护士 (LPN) 合作。RN 应将哪位患者分配给 LPN？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the RN assign to the LPN?","terminalSentenceZh":"RN 应将哪位患者分配给 LPN？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The registered nurse (RN) is working with a licensed practical nurse (LPN).","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正与一名执业护士 (LPN) 合作。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A client with new-onset seizures who is scheduled for an urgent CT scan.","zh":"一名新发癫痫并计划进行紧急 CT 扫描的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client who is being admitted with a diagnosis of rule-out myocardial infarction.","zh":"一名因疑似心肌梗死而入院的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client with chronic heart failure who requires daily dressing changes and administration of oral medications.","zh":"一名患有慢性心力衰竭，需要每日换药和服用口服药物的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client who just returned from the postanesthesia care unit (PACU) after a thyroidectomy.","zh":"一名刚从麻醉后监测病房 (PACU) 返回的甲状腺切除术后患者。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stable clients with predictable outcomes and routine tasks like oral medications and dressing changes are suitable for LPNs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"结果可预测且有常规任务（如口服药物和换药）的稳定患者适合 LPN。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Assign stable clients with predictable outcomes to LPNs. Unstable, newly admitted, or complex clients should stay with the RN.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将结果可预测的稳定患者分配给 LPN。不稳定、新入院或复杂的患者应由 RN 负责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":325,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.134","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.134.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.134.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,34],"fullStemEn":"A nurse suspects that a client is having an acute hemolytic reaction to a blood transfusion. Place the nursing actions in the correct order of priority.","fullStemZh":"护士怀疑一名患者对输血产生了急性溶血反应。请按优先顺序排列护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse suspects that a client is having an acute hemolytic reaction to a blood transfusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士怀疑一名患者对输血产生了急性溶血反应。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Maintain a patent IV line with normal saline.","zh":"用生理盐水保持静脉通路畅通。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the transfusion.","zh":"停止输血。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and the blood bank.","zh":"通知医疗服务提供者和血库。"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor vital signs and urine output.","zh":"监测生命体征和尿量。"},{"id":"E","en":"Return the blood bag and tubing to the blood bank.","zh":"将血袋和输血管送回血库。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate priority is to stop the infusion of the incompatible blood. Next, maintaining IV access is critical for treating potential complications. Notification and monitoring follow, and finally, returning the blood for testing is necessary to confirm the reaction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"紧迫的优先事项是停止输入不相容的血液。接下来，保持静脉通路对于治疗潜在并发症至关重要。随后是通知和监测，最后，为了确认反应，必须将血液送回检测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In any reaction to an infusion, the first action is always to stop the infusion. Follow the nursing process and safety protocols.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在对输液的任何反应中，第一步行动始终是停止输液。遵循护理程序和安全方案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":326,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.135","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.135.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.135.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,46],"fullStemEn":"During a mass casualty incident, the nurse is triaging victims at the scene. Which victim should the nurse label with a red tag (Immediate)?","fullStemZh":"在一起大规模伤亡事故中，护士正在现场对受害者进行分诊。护士应将哪位受害者标记为红签（紧急）？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which victim should the nurse label with a red tag (Immediate)?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将哪位受害者标记为红签（紧急）？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During a mass casualty incident, the nurse is triaging victims at the scene.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在一起大规模伤亡事故中，护士正在现场对受害者进行分诊。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A victim with an open femur fracture and a pulse rate of 140 beats/minute.","zh":"一名患有股骨开放性骨折且脉搏为 140 次/分钟的受害者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A victim who is unconscious with a massive head injury and no spontaneous respirations.","zh":"一名昏迷不醒、头部受重伤且无自主呼吸的受害者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A victim with multiple abrasions who is walking around and asking for help.","zh":"一名有多处擦伤、正在走动并寻求帮助的受害者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A victim with a minor laceration on the arm and no signs of shock.","zh":"一名手臂有轻微裂伤且无休克征兆的受害者。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A victim with life-threatening injuries who has a high chance of survival with immediate intervention (like severe hemorrhage or shock) is tagged red.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具有生命危险但通过立即干预（如严重出血或休克）有很高存活机会的受害者被标记为红色。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Red tags are for life-threatening but treatable conditions. Black tags are for those who are deceased or have non-survivable injuries. Yellow is delayed, and green is minor.","testTakingStrategyZh":"红色标签用于危及生命但可治疗的情况。黑色标签用于已死亡或伤势无法存活的人。黄色表示延迟，绿色表示轻伤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":327,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.136","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.136.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.136.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[46,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,22],"fullStemEn":"The nurse has just received a handoff report. Which client should the nurse visit first?","fullStemZh":"护士刚收到交班报告。护士应首先探访哪位患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the nurse visit first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先探访哪位患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse has just received a handoff report.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士刚收到交班报告。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"A client with cirrhosis who has abdominal distension and an umbilical hernia.","zh":"一名患有肝硬化并伴有腹胀和脐疝的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client with pneumonia who has a new-onset of confusion and restlessness.","zh":"一名患有肺炎且新发意识模糊和烦躁不安的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with chronic stable angina who reports dull chest pain after ambulating in the hallway.","zh":"一名患有慢性稳定型心绞痛且在走廊行走后报告胸部钝痛的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client who had a stroke 3 days ago and has persistent right-sided hemiparesis.","zh":"一名 3 天前中风且持续存在右侧偏瘫的患者。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New-onset confusion and restlessness in a client with pneumonia are early signs of hypoxia, indicating a worsening respiratory status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肺炎患者新发的意识模糊和烦躁不安是缺氧的早期迹象，表明呼吸状况恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for 'new-onset' or 'sudden changes' in symptoms. These usually indicate an acute change that takes priority over stable or chronic conditions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找症状中的“新发”或“突然变化”。这些通常表明急性变化，优先于稳定或慢性疾病。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":328,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.137","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.137.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.137.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,53],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to admit a client from the emergency department with a diagnosis of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA). Rank the following nursing actions in order of priority.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备接收一名从急诊科转入、诊断为糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 的患者。请按优先顺序排列下列护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Rank the following nursing actions in order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列下列护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to admit a client from the emergency department with a diagnosis of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备接收一名从急诊科转入、诊断为糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Perform a focused head-to-toe assessment.","zh":"进行重点全身评估。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ensure airway patency and administer oxygen.","zh":"确保气道畅通并给氧。"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor potassium levels and cardiac rhythm.","zh":"监测血钾水平和心律。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer continuous intravenous regular insulin.","zh":"持续静脉滴注常规胰岛素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Establish intravenous access and begin fluid resuscitation.","zh":"建立静脉通路并开始补液。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Airway and breathing are assessed first, followed by fluid resuscitation to treat dehydration and restore perfusion. Potassium must be checked before insulin because insulin shifts potassium into cells. If potassium is below 3.5 mEq/L, begin replacement and delay insulin until potassium is above 3.5 mEq/L. Continue cardiac and potassium monitoring during insulin therapy, then complete the focused assessment after initial stabilization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先评估气道和呼吸，随后补液以治疗脱水并恢复灌注。开始胰岛素前必须检查血钾，因为胰岛素会使钾进入细胞。若血钾低于 3.5 mEq/L，应开始补钾并暂缓胰岛素，直到血钾高于 3.5 mEq/L。胰岛素治疗期间继续监测心律和血钾，初步稳定后再完成重点评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABC hierarchy (Airway, Breathing, Circulation). In DKA, hydration (Circulation) usually precedes insulin administration because insulin works better in a hydrated state and can shift potassium levels dangerously.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ABC 等级制度（气道、呼吸、循环）。在 DKA 中，补液（循环）通常在胰岛素给药之前，因为胰岛素在补液状态下效果更好，且可能导致钾水平发生危险的变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":329,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.138","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.138.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.138.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,38],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse on a surgical unit is assigning tasks for the shift. Which client assignment is most appropriate for a licensed practical nurse (LPN)?","fullStemZh":"外科病房的主管护士正在分配班次任务。哪项患者分配最适合执业护士 (LPN)？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client assignment is most appropriate for a licensed practical nurse (LPN)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项患者分配最适合执业护士 (LPN)？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse on a surgical unit is assigning tasks for the shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"外科病房的主管护士正在分配班次任务。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A client who underwent an appendectomy 2 days ago and requires administration of oral antibiotics.","zh":"一名 2 天前接受了阑尾切除术，需要服用口服抗生素的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client scheduled for a cardiac catheterization in 2 hours who needs a pre-procedure assessment.","zh":"一名计划在 2 小时后进行心脏插管，需要进行术前评估的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with unstable blood pressure who is receiving a continuous titration of a vasopressor.","zh":"一名血压不稳定且正在接受血管收缩剂持续滴定治疗的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with a new colostomy who needs teaching on stoma care.","zh":"一名刚做了结肠造口，需要学习造口护理的患者。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stable post-operative clients with routine medications are within the LPN scope of practice.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具有常规药物治疗的稳定手术后患者属于 LPN 的实践范围。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember 'SPARC' for RN tasks: Specialty, Planning, Assessment, RN judgment, Complex/Clinical teaching. These cannot be delegated to LPNs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 RN 任务的“SPARC”原则：专业、计划、评估、RN 判断、复杂/临床教学。这些不能委派给 LPN。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The charge nurse on a surgical unit is assigning tasks for the shift.","controlSentenceZh":"外科病房的主管护士正在分配班次任务。"}
{"queueIndex":330,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.139","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.139.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.139.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,32],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results for four clients. Which result requires the most immediate intervention?","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看四名患者的实验室检查结果。哪项结果需要最及时的干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which result requires the most immediate intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项结果需要最及时的干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results for four clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在查看四名患者的实验室检查结果。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client receiving warfarin with an International Normalized Ratio (INR) of 2.5.","zh":"一名正在接受华法林治疗且国际标准化比值 (INR) 为 2.5 的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with heart failure receiving digoxin with a serum digoxin level of 2.8 ng/mL.","zh":"一名患有心力衰竭、正在接受地高辛治疗且血清地高辛水平为 2.8 ng/mL 的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with diabetes mellitus with a hemoglobin A1c of 8.5%.","zh":"一名患有糖尿病且糖化血红蛋白 A1c 为 8.5% 的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client with chronic kidney disease with a creatinine of 3.2 mg/dL.","zh":"一名患有慢性肾脏病且肌酐为 3.2 mg/dL 的患者。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A digoxin level of 2.8 ng/mL is above the therapeutic range (0.5-2.0 ng/mL) and indicates digoxin toxicity, which can lead to life-threatening arrhythmias.","rationaleCorrectZh":"2.8 ng/mL 的地高辛水平高于治疗范围 (0.5-2.0 ng/mL)，表明发生了地高辛中毒，这可能导致危及生命的心律失常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify which laboratory value is 'critical' or 'toxic' versus those that are 'expected' or reflect 'chronic' conditions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别哪项实验室数值是“临界”或“中毒”的，对比那些“预期”或反映“慢性”状况的数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results for four clients.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在查看四名患者的实验室检查结果。"}
{"queueIndex":331,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p8_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.140","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.140.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.140.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,31],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to insert an indwelling urinary catheter for a female client. Rank the steps in the correct order of performance.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名女性患者插入留置导尿管。请按执行顺序排列步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Rank the steps in the correct order of performance.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按执行顺序排列步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to insert an indwelling urinary catheter for a female client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名女性患者插入留置导尿管。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Perform hand hygiene and apply sterile gloves.","zh":"执行手卫生并戴上无菌手套。"},{"id":"A","en":"Position the client supine with knees flexed and separated.","zh":"患者取仰卧位，双膝弯曲并分开。"},{"id":"E","en":"Inflate the balloon with sterile water and secure the catheter.","zh":"用无菌水充盈气囊并固定导尿管。"},{"id":"D","en":"Lubricate the catheter tip and insert it into the urethral meatus.","zh":"润滑导尿管末端并将其插入尿道口。"},{"id":"C","en":"Cleanse the labia majora and minora with antiseptic-soaked cotton balls.","zh":"用浸有防腐剂的棉球清洗大阴唇和小阴唇。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct order follows aseptic technique: preparation (positioning), hand hygiene/gloving, cleansing (disinfection), insertion, and finally stabilization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的顺序遵循无菌技术：准备（体位）、手卫生/戴手套、清洁（消毒）、插入，最后固定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think through the clinical procedure logically, focusing on maintaining sterile technique throughout.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逻辑性地思考临床操作过程，重点是在整个过程中保持无菌技术。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":332,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.141","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.141.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.141.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing education to a client who is planning to become pregnant. Which nutritional supplement should the nurse recommend to help prevent neural tube defects?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名计划怀孕的客户提供教育。护士应推荐哪种营养补充剂以帮助预防神经管缺陷？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nutritional supplement should the nurse recommend to help prevent neural tube defects?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应推荐哪种营养补充剂以帮助预防神经管缺陷？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing education to a client who is planning to become pregnant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名计划怀孕的客户提供教育。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Iron","zh":"铁"},{"id":"A","en":"Folic acid","zh":"叶酸"},{"id":"B","en":"Calcium","zh":"钙"},{"id":"D","en":"Vitamin C","zh":"维生素 C"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Folic acid (Vitamin B9) is essential for DNA synthesis and the development of the neural tube in the early stages of pregnancy. Adequate intake prior to and during early pregnancy significantly reduces the risk of neural tube defects such as spina bifida.","rationaleCorrectZh":"叶酸（维生素 B9）对于怀孕初期的 DNA 合成和神经管发育至关重要。怀孕前和怀孕初期摄入充足的叶酸可显著降低脊柱裂等神经管缺陷的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the specific outcome mentioned: preventing neural tube defects. Recall that folic acid is the standard recommendation for this purpose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注提到的具体结果：预防神经管缺陷。回想一下，叶酸是针对此目的的标准建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":333,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_sata_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.142","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.142.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,48],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing a physical assessment on a full-term newborn who is 2 hours old. Which findings should the nurse document as normal? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名出生 2 小时的足月新生儿进行体格检查。护士应将哪些发现记录为正常？（多项选择。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings should the nurse document as normal?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些发现记录为正常？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Vernix caseosa in skin folds","zh":"皮肤皱褶处的胎脂"},{"id":"B","en":"Milia on the nose","zh":"鼻部粟粒疹"},{"id":"C","en":"Generalized jaundice","zh":"全身黄疸"},{"id":"E","en":"Nasal flaring","zh":"鼻翼扇动"},{"id":"A","en":"Acrocyanosis","zh":"肢端发绀"},{"id":"F","en":"Mongolian spots on the sacrum","zh":"骶骨部蒙古斑"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acrocyanosis, milia, vernix caseosa, and Mongolian spots are all normal variations or common findings in a healthy full-term newborn.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肢端发绀、粟粒疹、胎脂和蒙古斑都是健康足月新生儿的正常变异或常见发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between normal physiological adaptations and signs of pathology or distress. Identify which findings are benign and which require intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分正常的生理适应与病理或窘迫的迹象。识别哪些发现是良性的，哪些需要干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":334,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_or_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.143","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.143.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.143.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is educating a parent group about gross motor milestones in infants. Place the following milestones in the order they typically occur, from earliest to latest.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向家长小组介绍婴儿的大运动发育里程碑。请将以下里程碑按通常发生的顺序排列，从最早到最晚。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following milestones in the order they typically occur, from earliest to latest.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将以下里程碑按通常发生的顺序排列，从最早到最晚。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is educating a parent group about gross motor milestones in infants.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向家长小组介绍婴儿的大运动发育里程碑。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Walking while holding onto furniture (cruising)","zh":"扶着家具走（巡航）"},{"id":"D","en":"Lifting head while prone","zh":"俯卧位抬头"},{"id":"A","en":"Sitting without support","zh":"独立坐稳"},{"id":"B","en":"Rolling from abdomen to back","zh":"从俯卧翻身为仰卧"}],"correct":["D","B","A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The typical sequence of gross motor development is cephalocaudal: first lifting the head (2-3 months), then rolling over (4-5 months), then sitting without support (6-8 months), and finally cruising or walking (10-12 months).","rationaleCorrectZh":"典型的大运动发育顺序是头尾方向的：首先是抬头（2-3 个月），然后是翻身（4-5 个月），接着是独立坐稳（6-8 个月），最后是扶走或走路（10-12 个月）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the cephalocaudal principle of development (head to toe). Start with milestones involving the head and move downward to the legs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想发育的头尾原则（从头到脚）。从涉及头部的里程碑开始，然后向下移动到腿部。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":335,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_mc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.144","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.144.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.144.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,36],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assisting a postpartum client with breastfeeding. Which observation indicates that the infant has achieved a proper latch?","fullStemZh":"护士正在协助一名产后客户母乳喂养。哪种观察结果表明婴儿已实现正确的含接？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which observation indicates that the infant has achieved a proper latch?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种观察结果表明婴儿已实现正确的含接？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assisting a postpartum client with breastfeeding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在协助一名产后客户母乳喂养。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The infant's lips are tucked inward against the nipple.","zh":"婴儿的嘴唇向内紧贴乳头。"},{"id":"D","en":"The infant's nose and chin are touching the breast.","zh":"婴儿的鼻子和下巴接触乳房。"},{"id":"C","en":"The infant's mouth covers only the tip of the nipple.","zh":"婴儿的嘴只覆盖乳头尖端。"},{"id":"A","en":"The nurse hears clicking sounds during swallowing.","zh":"护士在吞咽时听到“咔哒”声。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A proper latch is characterized by the infant's mouth being wide open, lips flanged outward (not tucked in), and the nose and chin touching the breast. The infant should take in a large portion of the areola, not just the nipple.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确含接的特征是婴儿嘴张大，嘴唇向外翻（不是向内缩），鼻子和下巴接触乳房。婴儿应含住大部分乳晕，而不仅仅是乳头。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the characteristics of an 'asymmetric latch' or 'deep latch'. Eliminate options that describe shallow latching or abnormal sounds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别“不对称含接”或“深层含接”的特征。排除描述浅表含接或异常声音的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":336,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_sata_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.145","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.145.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.145.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing home safety education to parents of a 9-month-old infant who has started crawling. Which interventions should the nurse include? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名开始爬行的 9 个月大婴儿的父母提供居家安全教育。护士应包括哪些干预措施？（多项选择。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place safety gates at the top and bottom of stairs.","zh":"在楼梯的顶部和底部安装安全门。"},{"id":"B","en":"Lower the crib mattress to the lowest position.","zh":"将婴儿床床垫降至最低位置。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep small objects like buttons and coins out of reach.","zh":"将纽扣和硬币等小物件放在够不到的地方。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure that the gaps in the crib slats are no more than 4 inches apart.","zh":"确保婴儿床栏杆之间的间隙不超过 4 英寸。"},{"id":"D","en":"Cover unused electrical outlets with safety plugs.","zh":"用安全插塞覆盖未使用的电源插座。"},{"id":"F","en":"Allow the infant to use a walker to improve mobility.","zh":"允许婴儿使用学步车以提高灵活性。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety gates, lowering the crib mattress, covering outlets, and removing choking hazards are essential safety measures for a mobile infant.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安装安全门、降低婴儿床床垫、覆盖插座和清除窒息危险是移动婴儿必不可少的安全措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the infant's current developmental stage (crawling). Choose interventions that address increased mobility and the tendency to put things in the mouth.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注婴儿当前的发育阶段（爬行）。选择针对增加的活动能力和将东西放入口中的倾向的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":337,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_or_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.146","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.146.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.146.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to perform Leopold maneuvers on a pregnant client. Place the four maneuvers in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备对一名孕妇进行利奥波德手法（Leopold maneuvers）。请按正确顺序排列这四个步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the four maneuvers in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列这四个步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to perform Leopold maneuvers on a pregnant client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备对一名孕妇进行利奥波德手法（Leopold maneuvers）。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Outlining the fetal head to determine the degree of descent/engagement","zh":"勾画胎头以确定下降/衔接程度"},{"id":"B","en":"Palpating the fundus to determine which fetal part is present","zh":"触诊宫底以确定存在的胎儿部分"},{"id":"C","en":"Identifying the fetal back and small parts (limbs)","zh":"识别胎背和小部分（肢体）"},{"id":"A","en":"Identifying the fetal part at the pelvic inlet","zh":"识别骨盆入口处的胎儿部分"}],"correct":["B","C","A","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Leopold maneuvers follow a specific sequence: 1) Fundal grip (determine what is in the fundus), 2) Lateral grip (locate the back), 3) Pawlik's grip (identify part at pelvic inlet), and 4) Pelvic grip (determine engagement and attitude).","rationaleCorrectZh":"利奥波德手法遵循特定顺序：1）宫底握法（确定宫底内容物），2）侧向握法（定位背部），3）帕夫利克握法（识别骨盆入口处的部分），4）骨盆握法（确定衔接和姿势）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the sequence 'Top, Sides, Bottom (one hand), Bottom (two hands facing feet)'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住顺序：‘顶部、侧面、底部（单手）、底部（双手面向足部）’。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":338,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_mc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.147","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.147.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.147.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,45],"fullStemEn":"A 16-year-old adolescent visits a health clinic for a wellness check. Which action by the nurse best promotes open communication and maintains confidentiality?","fullStemZh":"一名 16 岁的青少年到健康诊所进行健康检查。护士的哪项行动最能促进开放式沟通并维护隐私？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse best promotes open communication and maintains confidentiality?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项行动最能促进开放式沟通并维护隐私？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 16-year-old adolescent visits a health clinic for a wellness check.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 16 岁的青少年到健康诊所进行健康检查。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Insist that the parent remains in the room for the entire exam.","zh":"坚持要求家长在整个检查过程中留在房间里。"},{"id":"B","en":"Inform the adolescent that everything said will be shared with the parent.","zh":"告知该青少年，所说的每句话都会与家长分享。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the adolescent to write down any concerns instead of speaking aloud.","zh":"要求该青少年写下任何担忧，而不是大声说出来。"},{"id":"D","en":"Interview the adolescent privately without the parent present.","zh":"在家长不在场的情况下私下采访该青少年。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adolescents are more likely to disclose sensitive information (e.g., regarding sexual health or substance use) when interviewed privately. While complete confidentiality cannot always be guaranteed (e.g., in cases of harm to self or others), providing private time is a standard of care for this age group.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在私下采访时，青少年更有可能透露敏感信息（例如，关于性健康或物质使用）。虽然不能始终保证完全保密（例如，在伤害自己或他人的情况下），但提供私人时间是该年龄段的护理标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the developmental need for autonomy and privacy during adolescence. Choose the option that respects the client's emerging independence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考青春期对自主和隐私的发育需求。选择尊重客户新兴独立性的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":339,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_sata_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.148","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.148.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.148.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[171,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing discharge instructions for a postpartum client. Which symptoms should the nurse instruct the client to report immediately to the healthcare provider? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名产后客户准备出院指导。护士应指示客户立即向医疗保健提供者报告哪些症状？（多项选择。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which symptoms should the nurse instruct the client to report immediately to the healthcare provider?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应指示客户立即向医疗保健提供者报告哪些症状？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A temperature of 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) or higher","zh":"体温达到 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) 或更高"},{"id":"F","en":"Increased thirst and frequent urination","zh":"口渴增加和尿频"},{"id":"B","en":"Mild uterine cramping during breastfeeding","zh":"母乳喂养期间轻微的子宫痉挛"},{"id":"C","en":"Swelling, redness, or pain in one calf","zh":"一条小腿肿胀、发红或疼痛"},{"id":"E","en":"Saturation of a peripad in less than 1 hour","zh":"在不到 1 小时内浸透一块卫生巾"},{"id":"A","en":"Foul-smelling vaginal discharge (lochia)","zh":"有恶臭的阴道分泌物（恶露）"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Signs of infection (fever, foul discharge), hemorrhage (excessive bleeding), and deep vein thrombosis (unilateral calf pain) are critical complications that require immediate medical attention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"感染迹象（发烧、恶臭的分泌物）、出血（过量出血）和深静脉血栓形成（单侧小腿疼痛）是需要立即就医的关键并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify potential life-threatening complications: infection, hemorrhage, and thromboembolism. Distinguish them from normal physiological postpartum changes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别潜在的危及生命的并发症：感染、出血和血栓栓塞。将它们与正常的生理产后变化区分开来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":340,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_mc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.149","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.149.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.149.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,47],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is discussing appropriate play activities with the parents of a 2-year-old child. Which type of play is most characteristic of this developmental stage?","fullStemZh":"护士正在与一名 2 岁儿童的父母讨论合适的玩耍活动。哪种类型的玩耍是这一发育阶段最典型的特征？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which type of play is most characteristic of this developmental stage?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种类型的玩耍是这一发育阶段最典型的特征？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is discussing appropriate play activities with the parents of a 2-year-old child.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在与一名 2 岁儿童的父母讨论合适的玩耍活动。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Associative play","zh":"联合玩耍"},{"id":"B","en":"Solitary play","zh":"独自玩耍"},{"id":"D","en":"Parallel play","zh":"平行玩耍"},{"id":"A","en":"Cooperative play","zh":"合作玩耍"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Toddlers typically engage in parallel play, where they play alongside other children with similar toys but do not interact directly or work toward a common goal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"幼儿通常进行平行玩耍，即他们与其他孩子一起玩类似的玩具，但不直接互动或朝着共同目标努力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate developmental stages with specific play types: Infant = Solitary, Toddler = Parallel, Preschooler = Associative, School-age = Cooperative.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将发育阶段与特定玩耍类型联系起来：婴儿 = 独自，幼儿 = 平行，学龄前儿童 = 联合，学龄儿童 = 合作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":341,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_p9_sata_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.150","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.150.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.150.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a group of pregnant clients about factors that can negatively affect fetal growth and development. Which items should be included? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一组孕妇讲解可能对胎儿生长发育产生负面影响的因素。应包括哪些项目？（多项选择。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which items should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"应包括哪些项目？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Alcohol consumption","zh":"饮酒"},{"id":"F","en":"Daily prenatal vitamins","zh":"每日服用产前维生素"},{"id":"C","en":"Moderate exercise like swimming","zh":"游泳等适度运动"},{"id":"D","en":"Exposure to second-hand smoke","zh":"接触二手烟"},{"id":"B","en":"Consumption of unpasteurized soft cheeses","zh":"食用未经巴氏消毒的软奶酪"},{"id":"A","en":"Cigarette smoking","zh":"吸烟"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Smoking, alcohol, and certain foodborne pathogens (like Listeria in soft cheeses) are known teratogens or risks to fetal development.","rationaleCorrectZh":"吸烟、饮酒和某些食源性病原体（如软奶酪中的李斯特菌）是已知的致畸剂或对胎儿发育的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the term 'negatively affect'. Identify lifestyle choices or exposures that are known to cause harm to the developing fetus.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注术语“负面影响”。识别已知会对发育中的胎儿造成伤害的生活方式选择或暴露。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":342,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_dosage_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.151","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.151.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.151.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,49],"fullStemEn":"The physician orders lisinopril 10 mg PO daily. The pharmacy dispenses lisinopril 5 mg tablets. How many tablets should the nurse administer?","fullStemZh":"医生开具赖诺普利 10 mg 口服，每日一次。药房分发赖诺普利 5 mg 片剂。护士应给予多少片？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many tablets should the nurse administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应给予多少片？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The pharmacy dispenses lisinopril 5 mg tablets.","penultimateSentenceZh":"药房分发赖诺普利 5 mg 片剂。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"tablet(s)","zh":"片"},"acceptable":["2","2 tablets","two"],"numeric":{"value":2,"tolerance":0,"unit":"tablets"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"10 mg divided by 5 mg/tablet equals 2 tablets.","rationaleCorrectZh":"10 mg 除以 5 mg/片等于 2 片。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Verify the prescribed dose and the dose on hand, then apply the formula (Desired / Have) * Quantity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"核对医嘱剂量和现存剂量，然后应用公式（医嘱剂量 / 现存剂量）* 数量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":343,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_dosage_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.152","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.152.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.152.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[133,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,60],"fullStemEn":"The physician orders metoprolol tartrate 25 mg PO twice daily. The available medication is metoprolol tartrate 50 mg scored tablets. How many tablets should the nurse administer per dose?","fullStemZh":"医生开具酒石酸美托洛尔 25 mg 口服，每日两次。现有药物为酒石酸美托洛尔 50 mg 划痕片。护士每剂应给予多少片？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many tablets should the nurse administer per dose?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士每剂应给予多少片？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The available medication is metoprolol tartrate 50 mg scored tablets.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现有药物为酒石酸美托洛尔 50 mg 划痕片。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"tablet(s)","zh":"片"},"acceptable":["0.5","1/2","0.5 tablets"],"numeric":{"value":0.5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"tablets"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"25 mg divided by 50 mg/tablet equals 0.5 tablet.","rationaleCorrectZh":"25 mg 除以 50 mg/片等于 0.5 片。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Calculate the dose using the basic formula. Since the tablet is scored, it can be safely split in half.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用基本公式计算剂量。由于片剂有划痕，可以安全地分成两半。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":344,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_fluid_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.153","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.153.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.153.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,278],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,97],"fullStemEn":"During an 8-hour shift, a client with acute kidney injury has the following intake and output: IV normal saline at 75 mL/hr for 8 hours, 200 mL of oral water with medications, and 150 mL of urine output. Calculate the client's fluid balance in mL (express as a positive number).","fullStemZh":"在8小时的班次内，一名急性肾损伤患者的入量和出量如下：静脉滴注生理盐水 75 mL/小时共8小时，随药口服水 200 mL，尿量 150 mL。计算患者的液体平衡量（以毫升为单位，用正数表示）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's fluid balance in mL (express as a positive number).","terminalSentenceZh":"计算患者的液体平衡量（以毫升为单位，用正数表示）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During an 8-hour shift, a client with acute kidney injury has the following intake and output: IV normal saline at 75 mL/hr for 8 hours, 200 mL of oral water with medications, and 150 mL of urine output.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在8小时的班次内，一名急性肾损伤患者的入量和出量如下：静脉滴注生理盐水 75 mL/小时共8小时，随药口服水 200 mL，尿量 150 mL。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["650","650 mL"],"numeric":{"value":650,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total intake = (75 mL/hr * 8 hrs) + 200 mL = 800 mL. Total output = 150 mL. Fluid balance = 800 mL - 150 mL = 650 mL positive balance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总摄入量 = (75 mL/小时 * 8 小时) + 200 mL = 800 mL。总排出量 = 150 mL。液体平衡 = 800 mL - 150 mL = 650 mL 正平衡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Perform a step-by-step tally of all fluid intake and subtract all output during the designated time period.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逐步计算指定时间段内的所有液体摄入量，并减去所有排出量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":345,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_pediatric_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.154","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.154.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.154.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[55,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,113],"fullStemEn":"A child weighing 15 kg requires maintenance IV fluids. Using the Holliday-Segar method (100 mL/kg for the first 10 kg, 50 mL/kg for the next 10 kg), calculate the child's daily maintenance fluid requirement in mL/day.","fullStemZh":"一名体重为 15 kg 的儿童需要维持性静脉补液。使用 Holliday-Segar 方法（前 10 kg 给予 100 mL/kg，接下来的 10 kg 给予 50 mL/kg），计算该儿童每日的维持液体需求量（毫升/天）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Holliday-Segar method (100 mL/kg for the first 10 kg, 50 mL/kg for the next 10 kg), calculate the child's daily maintenance fluid requirement in mL/day.","terminalSentenceZh":"使用 Holliday-Segar 方法（前 10 kg 给予 100 mL/kg，接下来的 10 kg 给予 50 mL/kg），计算该儿童每日的维持液体需求量（毫升/天）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A child weighing 15 kg requires maintenance IV fluids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名体重为 15 kg 的儿童需要维持性静脉补液。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/day","zh":"毫升/天"},"acceptable":["1250","1250 mL/day"],"numeric":{"value":1250,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/day"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For the first 10 kg: 10 * 100 mL = 1000 mL. For the remaining 5 kg: 5 * 50 mL = 250 mL. Total = 1250 mL/day.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于前 10 kg：10 * 100 mL = 1000 mL。对于剩余的 5 kg：5 * 50 mL = 250 mL。总计 = 1250 mL/天。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the pediatric fluid maintenance formula segmentally based on weight classes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据体重分段应用小儿液体维持量计算公式。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":346,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_dosage_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.155","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.155.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.155.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,104],"fullStemEn":"A client is prescribed a continuous heparin infusion at 1,200 units/hr. The pharmacy supplies a bag labeled heparin 25,000 units in 500 mL of 5% dextrose in water (D5W). At what rate in mL/hr should the infusion pump be programmed?","fullStemZh":"医生为患者开具持续静脉输注肝素，剂量为 1,200 单位/小时。药房提供的药袋标有：5% 葡萄糖注射液 (D5W) 500 mL 中含有肝素 25,000 单位。输液泵应设置为多少毫升/小时 (mL/hr)？","terminalSentenceEn":"At what rate in mL/hr should the infusion pump be programmed?","terminalSentenceZh":"输液泵应设置为多少毫升/小时 (mL/hr)？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The pharmacy supplies a bag labeled heparin 25,000 units in 500 mL of 5% dextrose in water (D5W).","penultimateSentenceZh":"药房提供的药袋标有：5% 葡萄糖注射液 (D5W) 500 mL 中含有肝素 25,000 单位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["24","24 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":24,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Concentration of Heparin = 25,000 units / 500 mL = 50 units/mL. Rate = 1,200 units/hr / 50 units/mL = 24 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝素浓度 = 25,000 单位 / 500 mL = 50 单位/mL。流速 = 1,200 单位/小时 / 50 单位/mL = 24 mL/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Calculate the concentration of the drug in the bag, then divide the ordered rate by this concentration to find mL/hr.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算药袋中药物的浓度，然后将医嘱流速除以该浓度，求出 mL/小时。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":347,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_burn_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.156","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.156.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.156.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,108],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 70 kg has sustained partial-thickness burns to 30% of their body surface area. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL * weight in kg * % BSA burned), calculate the volume of Lactated Ringer's solution that must be administered during the first 8 hours after the burn injury in mL.","fullStemZh":"一名体重 70 kg 的患者发生部分厚度烧伤，烧伤面积为体表面积的 30%。使用 Parkland 公式（4 mL * 体重 kg * 烧伤面积百分比），计算烧伤发生后前 8 小时内必须输入的乳酸林格氏液量（毫升）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL * weight in kg * % BSA burned), calculate the volume of Lactated Ringer's solution that must be administered during the first 8 hours after the burn injury in mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"使用 Parkland 公式（4 mL * 体重 kg * 烧伤面积百分比），计算烧伤发生后前 8 小时内必须输入的乳酸林格氏液量（毫升）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client weighing 70 kg has sustained partial-thickness burns to 30% of their body surface area.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名体重 70 kg 的患者发生部分厚度烧伤，烧伤面积为体表面积的 30%。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["4200","4,200","4200 mL"],"numeric":{"value":4200,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total fluid for the first 24 hours after the burn injury = 4 mL * 70 kg * 30 = 8,400 mL. Half of this volume must be administered in the first 8 hours after injury: 8,400 mL / 2 = 4,200 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"烧伤发生后前 24 小时总补液量 = 4 mL * 70 kg * 30 = 8,400 mL。其中一半必须在烧伤后前 8 小时内输入：8,400 mL / 2 = 4,200 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the Parkland formula yields the total fluid for the first 24 hours after burn injury, and half of that total is infused in the first 8 hours from the time of injury.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 Parkland 公式计算的是烧伤后前 24 小时的总液体量，而该总量的一半应从受伤时间算起在前 8 小时内输注。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":348,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_vital_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.157","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.157.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.157.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,40],"fullStemEn":"A client's blood pressure is measured as 142/88 mmHg. Calculate the client's pulse pressure in mmHg.","fullStemZh":"测得患者的血压为 142/88 mmHg。计算该患者的脉压差（单位：mmHg）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's pulse pressure in mmHg.","terminalSentenceZh":"计算该患者的脉压差（单位：mmHg）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client's blood pressure is measured as 142/88 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"测得患者的血压为 142/88 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mmHg","zh":"毫米汞柱"},"acceptable":["54","54 mmHg"],"numeric":{"value":54,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mmHg"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pulse pressure = Systolic BP - Diastolic BP. 142 mmHg - 88 mmHg = 54 mmHg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脉压差 = 收缩压 - 舒张压。142 mmHg - 88 mmHg = 54 mmHg。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the definition of pulse pressure, which is the mathematical difference between systolic and diastolic blood pressure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆脉压差的定义，即收缩压和舒张压之间的数学差值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":349,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_fluid_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.158","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.158.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.158.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,65],"fullStemEn":"A client consumes 6 ounces of broth, 4 ounces of gelatin, and 12 ounces of water. What is the client's total fluid intake in mL? (1 ounce = 30 mL).","fullStemZh":"一名患者食用了 6 盎司肉汤、4 盎司明胶（果冻）和 12 盎司水。该患者的液体总摄入量是多少毫升？（1 盎司 = 30 毫升）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(1 ounce = 30 mL).","terminalSentenceZh":"1 盎司 = 30 毫升）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"What is the client's total fluid intake in mL?","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者的液体总摄入量是多少毫升？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["660","660 mL"],"numeric":{"value":660,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total ounces = 6 + 4 + 12 = 22 ounces. Total mL = 22 * 30 mL/oz = 660 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总盎司数 = 6 + 4 + 12 = 22 盎司。总毫升数 = 22 * 30 mL/盎司 = 660 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert all fluid amounts into ounces first, sum them up, and then multiply by the conversion factor of 30 mL per ounce.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先将所有液体量转换为盎司，求和，然后乘以每盎司 30 mL 的换算系数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":350,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_fib_dosage_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.159","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.159.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.159.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[193,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[92,106],"fullStemEn":"A pediatrician orders acetaminophen 15 mg/kg PO for a child who weighs 22 lbs. Acetaminophen is available as a suspension of 160 mg/5 mL. How many mL of suspension should the nurse administer? (Round to the nearest tenth. 1 kg = 2.2 lbs).","fullStemZh":"儿科医生为一名体重 22 磅的儿童开具对乙酰氨基酚 15 mg/kg 口服。现有对乙酰氨基酚混悬液规格为 160 mg/5 mL。护士应给予多少毫升混悬液？（四舍五入到最接近的十分位。1 kg = 2.2 磅）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest tenth. 1 kg = 2.2 lbs).","terminalSentenceZh":"1 kg = 2.2 磅）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL of suspension should the nurse administer?","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的十分位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["4.7","4.7 mL"],"numeric":{"value":4.7,"tolerance":0.1,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Child's weight in kg = 22 lbs / 2.2 = 10 kg. Dose needed = 10 kg * 15 mg/kg = 150 mg. Volume to administer = (150 mg / 160 mg) * 5 mL = 4.6875 mL, rounded to 4.7 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"儿童体重 kg = 22 磅 / 2.2 = 10 kg。所需剂量 = 10 kg * 15 mg/kg = 150 mg。给药体积 = (150 mg / 160 mg) * 5 mL = 4.6875 mL，四舍五入为 4.7 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert pounds to kilograms first, calculate the dosage in mg, and then convert mg to mL using the liquid concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先将磅转换为千克，计算出 mg 剂量，然后使用液体药物浓度将 mg 转换为 mL。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"How many mL of suspension should the nurse administer?","controlSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的十分位。"}
{"queueIndex":351,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_vaping_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.160","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.160.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.160.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[123,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,50],"fullStemEn":"An adolescent client admits to using e-cigarettes (vaping) daily and states, 'It's just water vapor, it's not bad for me.' The nurse plans an educational intervention.","fullStemZh":"一名青少年患者承认每天使用电子烟，并声称：“这只是水蒸气，对我没有坏处。”护士计划进行一次教育干预。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse plans an educational intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士计划进行一次教育干预。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An adolescent client admits to using e-cigarettes (vaping) daily and states, 'It's just water vapor, it's not bad for me.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名青少年患者承认每天使用电子烟，并声称：“这只是水蒸气，对我没有坏处。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should explain that e-cigarettes contain {{1}} which can impair brain development, and vaping increases the risk of {{2}}.","zh":"护士应解释说，电子烟含有 {{1}}，这会损害大脑发育，且吸电子烟会增加 {{2}} 的风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"carbon monoxide","zh":"一氧化碳"},{"id":"o3","en":"tar","zh":"焦油"},{"id":"o1","en":"nicotine","zh":"尼古丁"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"lung injury and respiratory symptoms","zh":"肺损伤和呼吸道症状"},{"id":"o3","en":"type 1 diabetes","zh":"1型糖尿病"},{"id":"o2","en":"liver failure","zh":"肝功能衰竭"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"E-cigarettes contain nicotine, an addictive chemical that harms adolescent brain development. Vaping also exposes the lungs to harmful substances that can injure lung tissue and worsen respiratory health.","rationaleCorrectZh":"电子烟含有尼古丁，这是一种成瘾性化学物质，会损害青少年的大脑发育。吸电子烟还会使肺部暴露于有害物质中，可能损伤肺组织并恶化呼吸健康。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the components of e-cigarettes (nicotine) and the primary organ system affected by inhalation (lungs).","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于电子烟的成分（尼古丁）和吸入电子烟受影响的主要器官系统（肺部）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":352,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_ama_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.161","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.161.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.161.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,47],"fullStemEn":"A client hospitalized with pneumonia insists on leaving the hospital against medical advice (AMA). The client is alert and oriented to person, place, and time.","fullStemZh":"一名因肺炎住院的患者坚持要违背医嘱离院（AMA）。该患者神志清醒，对人、地点和时间定向力正常。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client is alert and oriented to person, place, and time.","terminalSentenceZh":"该患者神志清醒，对人、地点和时间定向力正常。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client hospitalized with pneumonia insists on leaving the hospital against medical advice (AMA).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因肺炎住院的患者坚持要违背医嘱离院（AMA）。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's priority action is to {{1}} and then {{2}}.","zh":"护士的首要行动是 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"call security to prevent the client from exiting","zh":"呼叫安保人员阻止患者离开"},{"id":"o3","en":"administer a sedative to keep the client calm","zh":"给予镇静剂以保持患者安静"},{"id":"o1","en":"explain the risks of leaving without treatment","zh":"解释在不接受治疗的情况下离院的风险"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"promises to return if symptoms worsen","zh":"承诺如果症状加重就返回"},{"id":"o3","en":"receives a copy of the entire medical record","zh":"获得一份完整病历的副本"},{"id":"o1","en":"ask the client to sign the AMA form and document refusal if declined","zh":"请患者签署 AMA 表单；若拒签则记录拒签"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must first assess the client's understanding of the risks associated with refusing treatment. If the competent client still chooses to leave, the nurse asks the client to sign the AMA form and documents both the teaching and any refusal to sign.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士必须首先评估患者对拒绝治疗相关风险的理解。如果具有行为能力的患者仍选择离开，护士应请患者签署 AMA 表单，并记录已进行的教育以及任何拒签情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize autonomy and client education regarding risks, then document informed refusal without implying the client can be forced to sign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先尊重自主权并进行风险教育，然后记录知情拒绝；不要暗示可以强迫患者签字。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":353,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_aki_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.162","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.162.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.162.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,40],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute kidney injury (AKI) is in the oliguric phase. The nurse monitors laboratory results and clinical findings.","fullStemZh":"一名患有急性肾损伤 (AKI) 的患者处于少尿期。护士监测实验室结果和临床表现。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse monitors laboratory results and clinical findings.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士监测实验室结果和临床表现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with acute kidney injury (AKI) is in the oliguric phase.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有急性肾损伤 (AKI) 的患者处于少尿期。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"During this phase, the nurse expects to observe {{1}} and should monitor for {{2}}.","zh":"在此期间，护士预计会观察到 {{1}} 并应监测 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"decreased serum potassium levels","zh":"血清钾水平降低"},{"id":"o3","en":"excessive diluted urine output","zh":"排出大量稀释的尿液"},{"id":"o1","en":"elevated blood urea nitrogen (BUN) and creatinine","zh":"血尿素氮 (BUN) 和肌酐升高"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"hyperkalemia and fluid volume excess","zh":"高钾血症和体液过多"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypocalcemia and metabolic alkalosis","zh":"低钙血症和代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypotension and dehydration","zh":"低血压和脱水"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The oliguric phase of AKI is characterized by reduced glomerular filtration, leading to retention of waste products (elevated BUN/creatinine) and potassium (hyperkalemia), along with fluid retention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"AKI的少尿期的特征是肾小球滤过率降低，导致代谢废物（升高BUN/肌酐）和钾蓄积（高钾血症），以及液体潴留。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'oliguric' with renal failure, which results in waste buildup, fluid retention, and electrolyte accumulation (hyperkalemia).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“少尿”与肾衰竭联系起来，后者会导致废物堆积、液体潴留以及电解质积累（高钾血症）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":354,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_depression_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.163","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.163.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.163.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the psychiatric unit with major depressive disorder and reports feeling hopeless and empty.","fullStemZh":"一名患有重度抑郁症的患者收治入院，诉感到绝望和空虚。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client is admitted to the psychiatric unit with major depressive disorder and reports feeling hopeless and empty.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患有重度抑郁症的患者收治入院，诉感到绝望和空虚。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's immediate priority is to assess for {{1}} and implement {{2}}.","zh":"护士当务之急是评估 {{1}} 并实施 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"suicidal ideation and intent","zh":"自杀意念和企图"},{"id":"o2","en":"nutritional intake and weight loss","zh":"营养摄入和体重减轻"},{"id":"o3","en":"sleep disturbance patterns","zh":"睡眠障碍模式"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a high-protein, high-calorie meal plan","zh":"高蛋白、高热量膳食计划"},{"id":"o3","en":"cognitive behavioral therapy group sessions","zh":"认知行为治疗小组会议"},{"id":"o1","en":"one-on-one safety observation if active risk is present","zh":"如果存在活跃风险，实施一对一安全观察"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety is always the primary concern for a client with major depressive disorder, especially when expressing hopelessness. Assessing for suicide risk and implementing appropriate observation levels are top priorities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于患有重度抑郁症的患者，安全始终是首要考虑的问题，尤其是在表达绝望时。评估自杀风险并实施适当的观察级别是重中之重。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first. Hopelessness is a key risk factor for suicide. Choose the interventions that establish a secure environment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一。绝望是自杀的关键风险因素。选择能够建立安全环境的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":355,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_sterile_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.164","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.164.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.164.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,98],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to insert an indwelling urinary catheter and is setting up a sterile field.","fullStemZh":"护士正在准备插入留置尿管，并正在建立无菌区。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to insert an indwelling urinary catheter and is setting up a sterile field.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在准备插入留置尿管，并正在建立无菌区。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should maintain a sterile field by keeping items in visual range and understanding that the outer {{1}} border of the drape is considered contaminated, and objects must be held {{2}}.","zh":"护士应通过保持无菌物品在视野范围内来维护无菌区，并明白无菌巾边缘外侧的 {{1}} 被视为已污染，且物品必须持于 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"2-inch (5.0 cm)","zh":"2英寸 (5.0 cm)"},{"id":"o3","en":"3-inch (7.5 cm)","zh":"3英寸 (7.5 cm)"},{"id":"o1","en":"1-inch (2.5 cm)","zh":"1英寸 (2.5 cm)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"below the level of the table","zh":"在桌子水平以下"},{"id":"o2","en":"close to the chest area","zh":"靠近胸部区域"},{"id":"o1","en":"above the waist level","zh":"腰部水平以上"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard sterile technique dictates that the outer 1-inch border of a sterile drape is contaminated. Furthermore, any sterile object held below the waist is considered unsterile.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标准的无菌技术规定，无菌巾外侧 1 英寸的边缘视为已被污染。此外，持于腰部以下的任何无菌物品均被视为已失去无菌状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall standard textbook definitions for maintaining sterility: the 1-inch border rule and waist-level boundary.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆维持无菌状态的标准教科书定义：1 英寸边缘规则和腰部水平边界。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":356,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_geriatric_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.165","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.165.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.165.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,35],"fullStemEn":"An older adult client is preparing for discharge home after a hip replacement. The nurse performs home safety discharge teaching.","fullStemZh":"一名老年患者正准备在髋关节置换术后出院回家。护士进行家庭安全出院指导。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse performs home safety discharge teaching.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士进行家庭安全出院指导。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An older adult client is preparing for discharge home after a hip replacement.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名老年患者正准备在髋关节置换术后出院回家。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To prevent falls, the nurse should advise the client to remove {{1}} and ensure there is adequate {{2}}.","zh":"为了预防跌倒，护士应建议患者移除 {{1}} 并确保有足够的 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"handrails on stairs","zh":"楼梯扶手"},{"id":"o1","en":"scatter rugs","zh":"块毯/小地毯"},{"id":"o3","en":"grab bars in the bathroom","zh":"浴室扶手"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"ventilation in the kitchen","zh":"厨房通风"},{"id":"o2","en":"humidification in the bedroom","zh":"卧室加湿"},{"id":"o1","en":"lighting, especially at night","zh":"照明，特别是在夜间"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Scatter rugs are a major tripping hazard for older adults and should be removed. Adequate lighting, especially at night (e.g., nightlights), prevents falls by ensuring clear pathway visibility.","rationaleCorrectZh":"块毯是老年人跌倒的主要绊倒危险，应予以移除。充足的照明，尤其是夜间（例如小夜灯），可通过确保清晰的通道可见性来预防跌倒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify which items pose safety hazards (rugs) and which interventions promote environmental safety (lighting).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别哪些物品构成安全隐患（块毯），以及哪些干预措施能促进环境安全（照明）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"An older adult client is preparing for discharge home after a hip replacement.","controlSentenceZh":"一名老年患者正准备在髋关节置换术后出院回家。"}
{"queueIndex":357,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_ipv_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.166","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.166.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.166.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,44],"fullStemEn":"A female client presents to the clinic with multiple bruises in various stages of healing. Her partner refuses to leave the room during the assessment.","fullStemZh":"一名女性患者因身上多处处于不同愈合阶段的瘀伤来到诊所就诊。其伴侣在评估期间拒绝离开房间。","terminalSentenceEn":"Her partner refuses to leave the room during the assessment.","terminalSentenceZh":"其伴侣在评估期间拒绝离开房间。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A female client presents to the clinic with multiple bruises in various stages of healing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名女性患者因身上多处处于不同愈合阶段的瘀伤来到诊所就诊。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse must screen for intimate partner violence by {{1}} and asking {{2}}.","zh":"护士必须通过 {{1}} 并提问 {{2}} 来筛查亲密关系暴力。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"interviewing the client alone","zh":"单独访谈患者"},{"id":"o2","en":"asking the partner directly about the bruises","zh":"直接询问伴侣关于瘀伤的情况"},{"id":"o3","en":"confronting the partner in front of the client","zh":"在患者面前与伴侣对质"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"direct questions about safety and relationship safety","zh":"关于自身安全和伴侣关系安全的直接问题"},{"id":"o2","en":"indirect questions to avoid upsetting the partner","zh":"间接问题以避免激怒伴侣"},{"id":"o3","en":"the client's partner for confirmation of the story","zh":"向患者伴侣核实情况"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To perform a safe and accurate screening for intimate partner violence, the client must be interviewed alone. Direct questions (e.g., 'Do you feel safe at home?') yield the most honest answers and show support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为了安全且准确地进行亲密关系暴力筛查，必须单独对患者进行访谈。直接的问题（例如“你在家里感到安全吗？”）能得到最真实的回答并表明给予支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety is paramount; interviewing a potential victim in front of the suspected perpetrator is a severe safety risk and limits disclosure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全是至高无上的；在嫌疑施暴者面前访谈潜在受害者是严重的安全隐患，并会限制患者说出真相。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":358,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_hipaa_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.167","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.167.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.167.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,44],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to leave the workstation to answer a client call light. The electronic health record (EHR) is currently open on the computer screen.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备离开工作站去接听患者的呼叫铃。此时电脑屏幕上正打开着电子健康档案 (EHR)。","terminalSentenceEn":"The electronic health record (EHR) is currently open on the computer screen.","terminalSentenceZh":"此时电脑屏幕上正打开着电子健康档案 (EHR)。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to leave the workstation to answer a client call light.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备离开工作站去接听患者的呼叫铃。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse must protect client confidentiality by {{1}} before {{2}}.","zh":"护士必须在 {{2}} 之前，通过 {{1}} 来保护患者隐私。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"minimizing the patient record window","zh":"最小化患者记录窗口"},{"id":"o2","en":"turning the computer monitor off","zh":"关闭电脑显示器"},{"id":"o1","en":"logging off the computer workstation","zh":"注销电脑工作站"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"leaving the physical desk area","zh":"离开物理办公桌区域"},{"id":"o3","en":"reviewing another patient's medication list","zh":"查看另一名患者的药物清单"},{"id":"o2","en":"taking a meal or rest break","zh":"用餐或休息"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To maintain HIPAA compliance and protect client confidentiality, nurses must log off any electronic system when walking away from the computer, preventing unauthorized access.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为符合 HIPAA 规定并保护患者机密，护士在离开电脑时必须注销任何电子系统，以防止未经授权的访问。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Simply hiding or turning off screens does not prevent unauthorized users from easily waking the session. Logging off is the only secure action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仅仅隐藏或关闭屏幕并不能防止未经授权的用户轻易唤醒会话。注销是唯一安全的操作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":359,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_dysphagia_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.168","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.168.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.168.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,53],"fullStemEn":"After swallowing assessment, a client with post-stroke dysphagia has an individualized feeding plan that recommends upright positioning and a chin-down posture. The nurse prepares to assist with feeding.","fullStemZh":"一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者接受吞咽评估后，其个体化进食计划建议保持直立并采用低头姿势。护士准备协助患者进食。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse prepares to assist with feeding.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士准备协助患者进食。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After swallowing assessment, a client with post-stroke dysphagia has an individualized feeding plan that recommends upright positioning and a chin-down posture.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者接受吞咽评估后，其个体化进食计划建议保持直立并采用低头姿势。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should position the client at {{1}} and instruct the client to use a {{2}} when swallowing.","zh":"护士应将患者置于 {{1}} 卧位，并指导患者在吞咽时使用 {{2}} 姿势。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"0 degrees (flat supine)","zh":"0度 (平卧位)"},{"id":"o1","en":"90 degrees (high Fowler's)","zh":"90度 (高 Fowler's 卧位)"},{"id":"o2","en":"30 degrees (semi-Fowler's)","zh":"30度 (半 Fowler's 卧位)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"chin-tuck position","zh":"收下颌（下巴触胸）"},{"id":"o3","en":"head-turned-sideways position","zh":"头部转向一侧"},{"id":"o2","en":"neck-hyperextended position","zh":"颈部过伸"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Upright positioning supports safer oral intake. The nurse should also cue the chin-down posture specified in this client's individualized plan; this maneuver may improve airway protection for selected swallowing impairments but is not universal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"直立体位有助于更安全地经口进食。护士还应提示患者采用其个体化计划规定的低头姿势；该动作可改善部分特定吞咽障碍的气道保护，但并非普遍适用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the individualized swallowing plan. Upright positioning is broadly useful, while chin-down and other postures depend on the assessed swallowing impairment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应遵循个体化吞咽计划。直立体位通常有益，而低头及其他姿势取决于评估出的吞咽障碍。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":360,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_cloze_cath_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.169","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.169.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.169.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"A client returns to the unit after a cardiac catheterization via the femoral artery.","fullStemZh":"一名患者经股动脉行心脏导管介入术后返回病房。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client returns to the unit after a cardiac catheterization via the femoral artery.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患者经股动脉行心脏导管介入术后返回病房。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should prioritize monitoring the affected limb for {{1}} and ensure the client maintains {{2}}.","zh":"护士应优先监测受累肢体的 {{1}} 并确保患者保持 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"absent or weakened pedal pulses","zh":"足背动脉搏动消失或减弱"},{"id":"o2","en":"hyperreflexia and muscle spasms","zh":"反射亢进和肌肉痉挛"},{"id":"o3","en":"elevated skin temperature","zh":"皮温升高"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"early ambulation within 1 hour","zh":"在1小时内尽早下床活动"},{"id":"o2","en":"semi-Fowler's position with leg flexed","zh":"半 Fowler's 卧位并屈曲下肢"},{"id":"o1","en":"strict bed rest with the leg straight","zh":"严格卧床休息并将腿伸直"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Femoral artery puncture carries a high risk of arterial occlusion or bleeding. The nurse must check distal perfusion (pedal pulses). Keeping the leg straight and maintaining bed rest prevents arterial sheath dislodgement or bleeding at the site.","rationaleCorrectZh":"股动脉穿刺具有极高动脉闭塞或出血风险。护士必须检查远端灌注（足背动脉搏动）。保持腿部伸直并维持卧床休息可防止动脉鞘移位或穿刺部位出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall standard complications of arterial access: bleeding and occlusion. Bed rest and immobilization are standard methods to prevent hematoma and bleeding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆动脉通路的标准并发症：出血和闭塞。卧床和制动是防止血肿和出血的标准方法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":361,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_autonomic_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.170","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.170.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.170.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,61],"fullStemEn":"A client with a T4 spinal cord injury reports a sudden, throbbing headache. The blood pressure is 185/100 mmHg. Arrange the nurse's actions in order of priority from first to last.","fullStemZh":"一名有 T4 脊髓损伤的患者诉突然出现搏动性头痛。血压为 185/100 mmHg。按首要到最后的顺序排列护士的护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nurse's actions in order of priority from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"按首要到最后的顺序排列护士的护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The blood pressure is 185/100 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压为 185/100 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Elevate the head of the bed to 45 degrees or higher.","zh":"将床头抬高至 45 度或更高。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess for fecal impaction after severe hypertension is controlled.","zh":"在严重高血压得到控制后评估有无大便嵌顿。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer prescribed rapid-acting antihypertensive medication if blood pressure remains dangerously high.","zh":"如果血压仍危险性升高，给予医嘱中的速效降压药。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check the client's urinary catheter or bladder for distention.","zh":"检查患者的尿管或膀胱有无过度充盈。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, raise the head of the bed to promote orthostatic reduction in blood pressure. Second, look for the most common cause of autonomic dysreflexia (bladder distention/kinked catheter). Because the blood pressure is severely elevated, administer prescribed rapid-acting antihypertensive medication if bladder management does not resolve the crisis. Assess for fecal impaction after severe hypertension is controlled because rectal stimulation can worsen dysreflexia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，抬高床头以促进直立性降低血压。第二，寻找自主神经反射异常的最常见原因（膀胱膨胀/尿管折叠）。由于血压严重升高，如果处理膀胱问题后危象仍未解除，应给予医嘱中的速效降压药。严重高血压得到控制后再评估大便嵌顿，因为直肠刺激可能加重自主神经反射异常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Position first, check the bladder next, and treat severe persistent hypertension before rectal stimulation or other potentially provocative assessments.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先调整体位，再检查膀胱；若严重高血压持续存在，应先处理血压，再进行直肠刺激等可能诱发反应的评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":362,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_transfusion_22","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.171","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.171.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.171.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,40],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving a blood transfusion reports chills, lower back pain, and shortness of breath. Place the nurse's immediate interventions in the correct chronological order.","fullStemZh":"正在接受输血的患者诉寒战、腰痛和呼吸急促。将护士的立即干预措施按正确的顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's immediate interventions in the correct chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"将护士的立即干预措施按正确的顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receiving a blood transfusion reports chills, lower back pain, and shortness of breath.","penultimateSentenceZh":"正在接受输血的患者诉寒战、腰痛和呼吸急促。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Stop the transfusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止输血。"},{"id":"B","en":"Infuse normal saline through new tubing to maintain IV access.","zh":"使用新的输液管路输注生理盐水以维持静脉通路。"},{"id":"D","en":"Send the remaining blood bag and administration tubing to the blood bank.","zh":"将剩余的血袋和输血管路送回血库。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the health care provider and the blood bank.","zh":"通知医疗服务提供者和血库。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"1. Stop the transfusion to prevent further exposure to the incompatible blood. 2. Keep the line open with saline using new tubing. 3. Notify the provider and blood bank. 4. Return blood and tubing for investigation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1. 立即停止输血，防止进一步接触不相容的血液。2. 使用新管路输入生理盐水以保持静脉开放。3. 通知提供者和血库。4. 将剩余血和管路退回以便调查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stopping the offending agent is always the first action. Never run saline through the same tubing as the blood, as this pushes remaining blood into the client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"停止有害药物/制剂始终是首要行动。切勿通过与输血相同的管路输注生理盐水，因为这会将残留的血液推入患者体内。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":363,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_eyewash_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.172","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.172.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.172.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,38],"fullStemEn":"A laboratory worker accidentally splashes a chemical solution into their eye. Place the emergency response steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名实验室工作人员不小心将化学溶液溅入眼中。将应急响应步骤按正确的顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the emergency response steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"将应急响应步骤按正确的顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A laboratory worker accidentally splashes a chemical solution into their eye.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名实验室工作人员不小心将化学溶液溅入眼中。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Flush the eye continuously for at least 15 to 20 minutes.","zh":"持续冲洗眼睛至少 15 至 20 分钟。"},{"id":"A","en":"Flush the affected eye at the eyewash station immediately.","zh":"立即在洗眼台冲洗受影响的眼睛。"},{"id":"B","en":"Direct the stream of water from the inner canthus to the outer canthus.","zh":"引导水流从内眦流向外眦。"},{"id":"D","en":"Seek medical evaluation from a provider.","zh":"寻求医疗服务提供者的医疗评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate action is to flush the eye. The flush should flow from inner to outer canthus to prevent chemical wash-off into the other eye. Continue flushing for a minimum of 15-20 minutes to thoroughly dilute and remove the chemical. Afterward, seek medical review.","rationaleCorrectZh":"立即行动是冲洗眼睛。冲洗应从内眦流向外眦，以防化学物质冲入另一只眼睛。持续冲洗至少 15-20 分钟以彻底稀释并清除化学物质。之后，寻求医疗评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Preventing cross-contamination (inner to outer canthus) and ensuring sufficient flush time are crucial steps before moving the client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在移动患者之前，防止交叉污染（从内眦到外眦）并确保足够的冲洗时间是至关重要的步骤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":364,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_trach_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.173","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.173.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.173.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,34],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to perform tracheostomy suctioning for a client. Sequence the steps of the procedure from start to finish.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为患者进行气管切开吸痰。按从开始到结束的顺序排列操作步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the steps of the procedure from start to finish.","terminalSentenceZh":"按从开始到结束的顺序排列操作步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to perform tracheostomy suctioning for a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为患者进行气管切开吸痰。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Apply intermittent suction while rotating and withdrawing the catheter.","zh":"在旋转并退出吸痰管的同时施加间歇性吸引。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hyperoxygenate the client with 100% oxygen.","zh":"用 100% 氧气为患者进行高浓度给氧。"},{"id":"B","en":"Gently insert the suction catheter without applying suction.","zh":"在不施加吸引的情况下轻轻插入吸痰管。"},{"id":"D","en":"Reoxygenate the client and reassess after the suction pass.","zh":"完成一次吸痰后重新给氧并再次评估患者。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"1. Hyperoxygenate first to build reserves. 2. Insert the catheter gently without suction to prevent mucosal trauma. 3. Apply intermittent suction only during withdrawal, limiting the suction pass to 10-15 seconds. 4. Reoxygenate and reassess before deciding whether another pass is needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1. 首先高浓度给氧以建立氧储备。2. 在不进行吸引的情况下轻轻插入吸痰管，防止黏膜损伤。3. 仅在退出吸痰管时进行间歇性吸引，并将每次吸痰控制在 10-15 秒以内。4. 重新给氧并再次评估，再决定是否需要再次吸痰。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Never apply suction during insertion. Apply intermittent suction only while withdrawing, keep the pass brief, and reoxygenate before any repeat attempt.","testTakingStrategyZh":"切勿在插入时施加吸引。只在退出时进行间歇性吸引，吸痰时间要短，并在再次尝试前重新给氧。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":365,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_evisceration_28","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.174","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.174.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.174.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,177],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,51],"fullStemEn":"A client who is post-abdominal surgery calls the nurse and states, 'My incision popped open.' The nurse notes wound evisceration. Place the nurse's actions in order of priority.","fullStemZh":"一名腹部手术后的患者呼叫护士并称：“我的切口裂开了。”护士发现伤口脏器脱出。按优先顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"按优先顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes wound evisceration.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现伤口脏器脱出。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Call for help and have someone notify the healthcare provider.","zh":"呼救并让旁人通知医疗服务提供者。"},{"id":"B","en":"Cover the exposed organs with sterile dressings moistened with sterile normal saline.","zh":"用无菌生理盐水湿润的无菌敷料覆盖脱出的脏器。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess vital signs and monitor for signs of shock.","zh":"评估生命体征并监测休克迹象。"},{"id":"C","en":"Position the client in low Fowler's with knees slightly flexed.","zh":"将患者置于低 Fowler's 卧位，双膝微屈。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"1. Evisceration is a medical emergency; immediately call for assistance. 2. Cover organs to keep them moist and sterile. 3. Position the client to reduce abdominal tension. 4. Check vital signs and prepare for emergency surgery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1. 脏器脱出是医疗紧急情况；立即呼叫协助。2. 覆盖脱出物以保持其湿润和无菌。3. 调整患者体位以减轻腹部张力。4. 检查生命体征并做好紧急手术的准备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety and prevention of infection/necrosis are key. Call for help first, then protect the tissue, then reduce physical stress on the wound.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全和预防感染/坏死是关键。首先呼救，然后保护组织，再减轻伤口受到的物理压力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":366,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_seizure_29","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.175","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.175.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.175.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,42],"fullStemEn":"A client begins having a tonic-clonic seizure while sitting in a chair. Place the nurse's priority actions in the correct chronological order.","fullStemZh":"一名坐在椅子上的患者开始发生强直-阵挛性癫痫发作。将护士的首要行动按正确的顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's priority actions in the correct chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"将护士的首要行动按正确的顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client begins having a tonic-clonic seizure while sitting in a chair.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名坐在椅子上的患者开始发生强直-阵挛性癫痫发作。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Turn the client onto their side.","zh":"协助患者侧卧。"},{"id":"D","en":"Loosen tight clothing around the client's neck.","zh":"解开患者颈部过紧的衣领。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ease the client to the floor.","zh":"协助患者平移到地板上。"},{"id":"C","en":"Clear the surrounding area of sharp objects.","zh":"清除周围区域的尖锐物品。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, prevent injury from falling by easing the client to the floor. Second, turn the client onto their side to maintain a clear airway and prevent aspiration. Third, clear the environment of hazards. Finally, loosen clothing to ease breathing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，通过协助患者降到地板上来防止跌倒受伤。第二，协助患者侧卧以保持气道通畅并防止误吸。第三，清除周围危险物品。最后，解开衣物以利于呼吸。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first. Moving the client to a flat surface protects from falling, and lateral positioning secures the airway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一。将患者移至平坦表面可防跌落，侧卧位可保障气道安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":367,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_jun05_b_or_consent_30","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.176","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.176.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.176.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[48,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,31],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for a surgical procedure. Place the steps of obtaining informed consent in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"一名患者计划进行手术治疗。将获得知情同意的步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps of obtaining informed consent in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"将获得知情同意的步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is scheduled for a surgical procedure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者计划进行手术治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The client signs the consent form.","zh":"患者在知情同意书上签字。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client verbalizes understanding of the explanations.","zh":"患者口头表达对上述解释的理解。"},{"id":"D","en":"The nurse witnesses the client's signature on the form.","zh":"护士见证患者在同意书上签字。"},{"id":"A","en":"The surgeon explains the risks, benefits, and alternatives of the procedure.","zh":"手术医生解释该手术的风险、益处和替代方案。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Informed consent begins with the provider disclosing details. The client must confirm comprehension. The client signs. The nurse acts as witness to the voluntary nature and identity of the signature.","rationaleCorrectZh":"知情同意始于提供者告知详情。患者必须确认理解。患者签字。护士作为见证人，见证签字的自愿性及签字者身份。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the nurse's role is to witness the signature, which can only happen after the provider has explained the procedure and the client has agreed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住护士的职责是见证签字，这只能在医生解释了手术且患者同意之后进行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":368,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.177","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.177.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.177.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,289],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,76],"fullStemEn":"A client who had an acute myocardial infarction (MI) 3 days ago reports sudden onset of shortness of breath and extreme fatigue. Upon assessment, the nurse notes a new high-pitched holosystolic murmur at the apex and crackles in the lung bases. Which complication should the nurse suspect?","fullStemZh":"一名3天前发生急性心肌梗死（MI）的患者诉突发呼吸短促和极度疲劳。评估时，护士发现心尖部出现新的高调全收缩期杂音，且肺底有湿啰音。护士应怀疑哪种并发症？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which complication should the nurse suspect?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应怀疑哪种并发症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Upon assessment, the nurse notes a new high-pitched holosystolic murmur at the apex and crackles in the lung bases.","penultimateSentenceZh":"评估时，护士发现心尖部出现新的高调全收缩期杂音，且肺底有湿啰音。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Right ventricular infarction","zh":"右心室梗死"},{"id":"D","en":"Dressler syndrome","zh":"德雷斯勒综合征"},{"id":"A","en":"Acute papillary muscle rupture","zh":"急性乳头肌断裂"},{"id":"C","en":"Ventricular septal rupture","zh":"室间隔穿孔"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A new holosystolic murmur at the apex following an MI, especially when accompanied by sudden pulmonary edema (crackles, dyspnea), is a classic sign of acute papillary muscle rupture leading to severe mitral regurgitation. This is a life-threatening complication requiring immediate intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心肌梗死后心尖部出现新的全收缩期杂音，特别是伴有突发肺水肿（湿啰音、呼吸困难）时，是急性乳头肌断裂导致严重二尖瓣反流的经典体征。这是一种危及生命的并发症，需要立即干预。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the location (apex) and timing (holosystolic) of the murmur along with the clinical context (post-MI pulmonary edema) to differentiate between complications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注杂音的位置（心尖部）和时相（全收缩期），结合临床背景（心肌梗死后肺水肿）来区分并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":369,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.178","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.178.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.178.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[184,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,56],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing the plan of care for a client with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease). Which of the following interventions and teaching points should be included? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查原发性肾上腺功能不全（艾迪生病）患者的护理计划。下列哪些干预措施和教学重点应当包括在内？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following interventions and teaching points should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"下列哪些干预措施和教学重点应当包括在内？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Increase salt intake during periods of excessive heat or humidity.","zh":"在极度炎热或潮湿期间增加盐摄入量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Wear a medical alert bracelet at all times.","zh":"始终佩戴医疗警示手环。"},{"id":"D","en":"Expect lifelong replacement of glucocorticoids and mineralocorticoids.","zh":"预计需要终生替代糖皮质激素和盐皮质激素。"},{"id":"E","en":"Report weight gain of more than 5 lbs in a week to the provider.","zh":"如果一周内体重增加超过5磅，请报告给医生。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain a low-potassium diet.","zh":"保持低钾饮食。"},{"id":"F","en":"Taper steroid doses slowly when feeling improved.","zh":"感觉好转时缓慢减少激素剂量。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Management of Addison's disease involves preventing crisis and managing electrolyte imbalances. Low-potassium diet is needed as these clients are prone to hyperkalemia. Salt intake must increase with stress/heat due to mineralocorticoid deficiency. Medical alerts are vital for emergencies. Replacement is lifelong. Rapid weight gain (E) can indicate over-replacement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艾迪生病的管理包括预防危机和管理电解质紊乱。由于此类患者易发生高钾血症，因此需要低钾饮食（A）。由于盐皮质激素缺乏，在压力/高温下必须增加盐摄入量（B）。医疗警示（C）对急救至关重要。替代治疗（D）是终生的。体重快速增加（E）可能表示替代过度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember 'Addison's: Add-a-son (need to add hormones/sodium)' and recall that potassium moves opposite to sodium in this condition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“Addison's：Add-a-son（需要增加激素/钠）”，并回想在这种情况下钾的变动方向与钠相反。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":370,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.179","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.179.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.179.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[109,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is evaluating a client with a spinal cord injury who is exhibiting signs of autonomic dysreflexia. Categorize each clinical finding based on the physiological response it represents.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名表现出自主神经反射亢进迹象的脊髓损伤患者。根据其代表的生理反应对每项临床发现进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Categorize each clinical finding based on the physiological response it represents.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据其代表的生理反应对每项临床发现进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is evaluating a client with a spinal cord injury who is exhibiting signs of autonomic dysreflexia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名表现出自主神经反射亢进迹象的脊髓损伤患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Blood pressure 210/110 mmHg","zh":"血压 210/110 mmHg"},{"id":"r2","en":"Heart rate 42 beats/min","zh":"心率 42 次/分"},{"id":"r3","en":"Profuse sweating above T6","zh":"T6水平以上大汗淋漓"},{"id":"r4","en":"Goosebumps below the level of injury","zh":"损伤水平以下起鸡皮疙瘩"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Sympathetic response","zh":"交感神经反应"},{"id":"c2","en":"Parasympathetic response","zh":"副交感神经反应"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Autonomic dysreflexia involves uninhibited sympathetic discharge below the level of injury (vasoconstriction leading to hypertension and piloerection/goosebumps). The parasympathetic system attempts to compensate above the level of injury (vasodilation, sweating, and bradycardia via the vagus nerve).","rationaleCorrectZh":"自主神经反射亢进涉及损伤水平以下的无抑制性交感神经放电（血管收缩导致高血压和毛发竖立/起鸡皮疙瘩）。副交感神经系统试图在损伤水平以上进行补偿（通过迷走神经引起血管扩张、出汗和心动过缓）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 'above' and 'below' the level of injury. Below is sympathetic (constriction), above is parasympathetic (dilation/compensation).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分损伤水平的“以上”和“以下”。以下是交感神经（收缩），以上是副交感神经（扩张/补偿）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":371,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.180","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.180.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.180.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,211],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,45],"fullStemEn":"A client is diagnosed with an inferior wall myocardial infarction. Which of the following clinical manifestations or complications should the nurse specifically monitor for in this client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者被诊断为下壁心肌梗死。护士应特别监测该患者的下列哪些临床表现或并发症？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following clinical manifestations or complications should the nurse specifically monitor for in this client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应特别监测该患者的下列哪些临床表现或并发症？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Nausea and vomiting","zh":"恶心和呕吐"},{"id":"A","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"B","en":"Second-degree AV block, Mobitz Type I","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞，莫氏I型"},{"id":"C","en":"Left bundle branch block","zh":"左束支传导阻滞"},{"id":"D","en":"Right ventricular infarction","zh":"右心室梗死"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Inferior wall MIs (Right Coronary Artery involvement) often involve the SA and AV nodes, leading to bradycardia and Type I AV blocks. They are frequently associated with RV infarction. Vagal stimulation in inferior MIs commonly causes N/V (E). Left bundle branch block is more common in anterior wall MIs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"下壁心肌梗死（涉及右冠状动脉）常波及窦房结和房室结，导致心动过缓（A）和I型房室传导阻滞（B）。它们经常与右心室梗死（D）相关。下壁梗死中的迷走神经刺激通常会引起恶心/呕吐（E）。左束支传导阻滞（C）在前壁梗死中更常见。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link anatomy to function: The RCA supplies the bottom (inferior) of the heart and the electrical 'pacemakers'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将解剖结构与功能联系起来：右冠状动脉供应心脏底部（下壁）和电子“起搏器”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":372,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.181","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.181.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.181.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,38],"fullStemEn":"A client with Addison's disease is admitted to the emergency department with vomiting, diarrhea, and hypotension. Which physician order should the nurse implement first?","fullStemZh":"一名患有艾迪生病的患者因呕吐、腹泻和低血压急诊入院。护士应首先执行哪项医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which physician order should the nurse implement first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先执行哪项医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Addison's disease is admitted to the emergency department with vomiting, diarrhea, and hypotension.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有艾迪生病的患者因呕吐、腹泻和低血压急诊入院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Draw blood for serum electrolyte levels.","zh":"抽血检查血清电解质水平。"},{"id":"D","en":"Obtain an electrocardiogram (ECG).","zh":"进行心电图（ECG）检查。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer IV hydrocortisone 100 mg.","zh":"给予静脉注射氢化可的松 100 mg。"},{"id":"C","en":"Start an IV infusion of 0.9% Normal Saline at 200 mL/hr.","zh":"开始以 200 mL/h 的速度静脉滴注 0.9% 生理盐水。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In an adrenal crisis, the most immediate threat to life is circulatory collapse and hypovolemic shock. Restoring fluid volume with Normal Saline (or D5NS) is the priority to maintain blood pressure. Hormone replacement (hydrocortisone) is critical but follows immediate volume resuscitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在肾上腺危象中，对生命最直接的威胁是循环衰竭和低血容量性休克。使用生理盐水（或 D5NS）恢复血容量是维持血压的首要任务。激素替代（氢化可的松）虽然至关重要，但在即刻容量复苏之后进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABCs. In shock states, 'Circulation' (fluids) is the priority intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ABC 原则。在休克状态下，“循环”（液体）是首要干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":373,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.182","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.182.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.182.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,57],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with a T4 spinal cord injury who develops a pounding headache and nasal congestion. After sitting the client upright, which of the following actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名 T4 脊髓损伤患者，该患者出现了剧烈头痛和鼻塞。让患者坐直后，下列哪些操作是合适的？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"After sitting the client upright, which of the following actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"让患者坐直后，下列哪些操作是合适的？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Lower the head of the bed to improve cerebral perfusion.","zh":"降低床头以改善脑灌注。"},{"id":"A","en":"Check the urinary drainage system for kinks.","zh":"检查尿液引流系统是否有扭结。"},{"id":"B","en":"Perform a digital rectal exam to check for fecal impaction.","zh":"进行数字化直肠检查以检查粪便嵌塞。"},{"id":"D","en":"Check the skin for pressure sores or restrictive clothing.","zh":"检查皮肤是否有压疮或束缚性衣物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer an antihypertensive medication if BP remains elevated.","zh":"如果血压持续升高，给予抗高血压药物。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate management of AD involves removing the stimulus. Most common triggers are bladder distension, fecal impaction, or skin irritation. Antihypertensives are used if initial measures don't lower BP. Sitting the client up is the first step; lowering the HOB (E) would worsen hypertension-induced intracranial pressure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"自主神经反射亢进的适当管理包括移除刺激物。最常见的诱因是膀胱膨胀（A）、粪便嵌塞（B）或皮肤刺激（D）。如果初始措施未能降低血压，则使用抗高血压药物（C）。让患者坐起是第一步；降低床头（E）会加重高血压引起的颅内压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In Autonomic Dysreflexia, the goal is 'Search and Destroy' the stimulus while keeping the head UP.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在自主神经反射亢进中，目标是“搜寻并消除”刺激物，同时保持头部抬高。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":374,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.183","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.183.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.183.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,38],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is administering medications to a client experiencing an acute myocardial infarction. Match each medication to its primary therapeutic goal.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名发生急性心肌梗死的患者给药。将每种药物与其主要治疗目标相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each medication to its primary therapeutic goal.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种药物与其主要治疗目标相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is administering medications to a client experiencing an acute myocardial infarction.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名发生急性心肌梗死的患者给药。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Morphine sulfate IV","zh":"吗啡静脉注射"},{"id":"r2","en":"Nitroglycerin sublingual","zh":"硝酸甘油舌下含服"},{"id":"r3","en":"Aspirin chewed","zh":"阿司匹林嚼服"},{"id":"r4","en":"Beta-blocker PO","zh":"β受体阻滞剂口服"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inhibit platelet aggregation","zh":"抑制血小板聚集"},{"id":"c3","en":"Decrease myocardial oxygen demand","zh":"降低心肌耗氧量"},{"id":"c1","en":"Reduce preload/afterload","zh":"降低前/后负荷"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Morphine and Nitroglycerin are vasodilators (reduce preload/afterload). Aspirin prevents further clotting by inhibiting platelets. Beta-blockers slow heart rate and contractility, reducing the oxygen the heart needs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"吗啡和硝酸甘油是血管扩张剂（降低前/后负荷）。阿司匹林通过抑制血小板防止进一步血栓形成。β受体阻滞剂减慢心率和收缩力，从而降低心脏所需的氧气。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the primary mechanism of action for each MONA-B component.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考 MONA-B 各个组成部分的主要作用机制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":375,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.184","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.184.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.184.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,50],"fullStemEn":"A client is diagnosed with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease). Match each clinical or laboratory finding to its most likely physiological cause.","fullStemZh":"一名患者被诊断为原发性肾上腺功能不全（艾迪生病）。将每项临床或实验室发现与其最可能的生理原因相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each clinical or laboratory finding to its most likely physiological cause.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每项临床或实验室发现与其最可能的生理原因相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is diagnosed with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者被诊断为原发性肾上腺功能不全（艾迪生病）。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Hyponatremia","zh":"低钠血症"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hyperkalemia","zh":"高钾血症"},{"id":"r3","en":"Hypoglycemia","zh":"低血糖"},{"id":"r4","en":"Hyperpigmentation","zh":"色素沉着"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Glucocorticoid deficiency","zh":"糖皮质激素缺乏"},{"id":"c2","en":"Mineralocorticoid deficiency","zh":"盐皮质激素缺乏"},{"id":"c3","en":"ACTH excess","zh":"ACTH过量"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aldosterone (mineralocorticoid) deficiency causes sodium loss and potassium retention. Cortisol (glucocorticoid) deficiency causes decreased gluconeogenesis leading to hypoglycemia. Hyperpigmentation in primary Addison's is due to high ACTH levels which cross-react with melanocytes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"醛固酮（盐皮质激素）缺乏导致钠流失和钾潴留。皮质醇（糖皮质激素）缺乏导致糖异生减少，进而引起低血糖。原发性艾迪生病中的色素沉着是由于高水平的 ACTH 与黑素细胞发生交叉反应所致。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the hormone to the specific metabolic or physical finding. Remember ACTH and MSH come from the same precursor.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将激素与特定的代谢或身体表现相匹配。记住 ACTH 和 MSH 来自同一种前体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":376,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.185","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.185.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.185.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"Which physiologic change explains why bradycardia occurs in autonomic dysreflexia despite severe hypertension?","fullStemZh":"哪种生理变化解释了为什么自主神经反射亢进在严重高血压的情况下仍会出现心动过缓？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which physiologic change explains why bradycardia occurs in autonomic dysreflexia despite severe hypertension?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种生理变化解释了为什么自主神经反射亢进在严重高血压的情况下仍会出现心动过缓？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Release of epinephrine from the adrenal medulla.","zh":"肾上腺髓质释放肾上腺素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Baroreceptor stimulation resulting in increased vagal tone.","zh":"压力感受器受刺激导致迷走神经张力增加。"},{"id":"C","en":"Sympathetic blockade at the level of the spinal injury.","zh":"脊髓损伤水平的交感神经阻滞。"},{"id":"A","en":"Direct stimulation of the sinoatrial node by the noxious stimulus.","zh":"有害刺激直接刺激窦房结。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In AD, massive sympathetic firing below the injury causes extreme hypertension. The brain detects this via baroreceptors in the carotid sinus and aortic arch and sends signals to slow the heart via the vagus nerve. However, these inhibitory signals cannot pass the spinal cord injury to cause vasodilation below.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在自主神经反射亢进中，损伤水平以下的大规模交感神经放电引起极端高血压。大脑通过颈动脉窦和主动脉弓的压力感受器检测到这一点，并通过迷走神经发送减慢心率的信号。然而，这些抑制信号无法穿过脊髓损伤处以引起下方的血管扩张。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the baroreceptor reflex: High pressure -> Slow heart.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想压力感受器反射：高压 -> 慢心。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":377,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b1_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.186","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.186.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.186.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,252],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,76],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with an anterior wall MI. The nurse notes the following rhythm on the monitor: Sinus rhythm with a rate of 72, followed by a sudden drop in the QRS complex without prior PR interval lengthening. What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"一名患有前壁心肌梗死的患者入院。护士在心电监护仪上发现以下心律：窦性心律，心率为72，随后QRS波突然脱落，脱落前无PR间期延长。护士的首要操作是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要操作是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes the following rhythm on the monitor: Sinus rhythm with a rate of 72, followed by a sudden drop in the QRS complex without prior PR interval lengthening.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在心电监护仪上发现以下心律：窦性心律，心率为72，随后QRS波突然脱落，脱落前无PR间期延长。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer Atropine 0.5 mg IV push.","zh":"给予阿托品 0.5 mg 静脉推注。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare for immediate transcutaneous pacing.","zh":"准备立即进行经皮起搏。"},{"id":"A","en":"Continue to monitor and document the finding.","zh":"继续监测并记录发现。"},{"id":"C","en":"Perform a carotid sinus massage.","zh":"进行颈动脉窦按摩。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The description (sudden QRS drop without PR lengthening) indicates Mobitz Type II second-degree AV block. This rhythm is common in anterior MIs and is highly unstable, often progressing to complete heart block. Transcutaneous pacing is the priority intervention. Atropine is generally ineffective for Type II blocks occurring in the His-Purkinje system.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该描述（QRS波突然脱落而无PR间期延长）表示莫氏II型二度房室传导阻滞。这种心律在前壁心肌梗死中很常见且极不稳定，通常会进展为三度房室传导阻滞。经皮起搏是首要干预措施。阿托品对于发生在希氏-浦肯野系统的II型阻滞通常无效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between Type I (Wenckebach - 'Longer, longer, longer, drop') and Type II (Sudden drop). Type II is always much more dangerous.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分 I 型（文氏现象——“越长越长越长，脱落”）和 II 型（突然脱落）。II 型总是危险得多。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse notes the following rhythm on the monitor: Sinus rhythm with a rate of 72, followed by a sudden drop in the QRS complex without prior PR interval lengthening.","controlSentenceZh":"护士在心电监护仪上发现以下心律：窦性心律，心率为72，随后QRS波突然脱落，脱落前无PR间期延长。"}
{"queueIndex":378,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.187","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.187.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.187.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,62],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is planning the client assignments for the shift. Which tasks are appropriate for the RN to delegate to an experienced licensed practical nurse (LPN/VN)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在计划当班的患者分配。哪些任务适合 RN 委派给有经验的执业护士 (LPN/VN)？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which tasks are appropriate for the RN to delegate to an experienced licensed practical nurse (LPN/VN)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些任务适合 RN 委派给有经验的执业护士 (LPN/VN)？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administering oral antihypertensive medications to a stable client.","zh":"给稳定的患者服用口服降压药。"},{"id":"D","en":"Auscultating breath sounds on a client who is 2 days post-op from a thoracotomy.","zh":"为开胸手术后 2 天的患者听诊呼吸音。"},{"id":"C","en":"Developing a plan of care for a client with a new colostomy.","zh":"为新造口的患者制定护理计划。"},{"id":"E","en":"Providing the initial education on the use of an incentive spirometer.","zh":"提供有关使用激励型肺活量计的初始教育。"},{"id":"B","en":"Performing a sterile dressing change on a stage 3 pressure injury.","zh":"为 3 期压力性损伤进行无菌换药。"},{"id":"F","en":"Administering a bolus dose of intravenous morphine for breakthrough pain.","zh":"为爆发性疼痛静脉推注吗啡。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs can administer most medications (except high-risk IV ones in some jurisdictions), perform sterile procedures on stable wounds, and gather data through focused assessments (like breath sounds) on stable clients. Initial education, care planning, and complex IV meds are the responsibility of the RN.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN 可以给大多数药物（某些辖区除外的高风险静脉药），对稳定的伤口执行无菌操作，并对稳定患者进行重点评估（如呼吸音）以收集数据。初始教育、护理计划和复杂的静脉药物是 RN 的责任。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the TAPE mnemonic: RNs do not delegate Teaching, Assessment, Planning, or Evaluation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 TAPE 记忆法：RN 不委派教学 (Teaching)、评估 (Assessment)、计划 (Planning) 或评价 (Evaluation)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":379,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.188","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.188.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.188.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer intravenous vancomycin to a client. Which actions are appropriate for the nurse to take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备给患者静脉滴注万古霉素。护士采取哪些行动是恰当的？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are appropriate for the nurse to take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士采取哪些行动是恰当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Assess the client's hearing and vestibular function.","zh":"评估患者的听力和前庭功能。"},{"id":"F","en":"Monitor the client's serum creatinine and BUN levels.","zh":"监测患者的血清肌酐和 BUN 水平。"},{"id":"A","en":"Infuse the medication over at least 60 minutes.","zh":"输注时间至少在 60 分钟以上。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the medication via rapid IV push.","zh":"通过静脉推注快速给药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain a trough level 30 minutes before the next dose.","zh":"在下次给药前 30 分钟测定谷浓度。"},{"id":"B","en":"Monitor the client for the development of 'red man syndrome.'","zh":"监测患者是否出现“红人综合征”。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Vancomycin must be infused slowly to prevent red man syndrome. It is nephrotoxic and ototoxic, so renal function and hearing must be monitored. Trough levels are essential to ensure therapeutic efficacy and safety.","rationaleCorrectZh":"万古霉素必须缓慢输注以防止红人综合征。它具有肾毒性和耳毒性，因此必须监测肾功能和听力。谷浓度对于确保疗效和安全性至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the major toxicities (ear, kidney) and the specific infusion-related reaction for vancomycin.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想万古霉素的主要毒性（耳、肾）和特定的输注相关反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":380,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.189","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.189.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.189.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,179],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client who is on droplet and contact precautions. In what order should the nurse don the following personal protective equipment (PPE)?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备进入一名采取飞沫和接触预防措施的患者房间。请按顺序列出护士穿戴个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse don the following personal protective equipment (PPE)?","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序列出护士穿戴个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client who is on droplet and contact precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备进入一名采取飞沫和接触预防措施的患者房间。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Mask or respirator","zh":"口罩或呼吸器"},{"id":"D","en":"Gloves","zh":"手套"},{"id":"C","en":"Goggles or face shield","zh":"护目镜或面罩"},{"id":"A","en":"Gown","zh":"隔离衣"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The CDC recommended sequence for donning PPE is: Gown, Mask, Goggles/Face Shield, and finally Gloves (which should cover the cuffs of the gown).","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDC 推荐的 PPE 穿戴顺序是：隔离衣、口罩、护目镜/面罩，最后是手套（手套应覆盖隔离衣的袖口）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of the process as working from the body outwards and from bottom to top of the face, ending with the hands.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将这一过程想象为从身体向外、从面部底部向顶部进行，最后是双手。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":381,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.190","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.190.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.190.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,70],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with a severe traumatic brain injury. Which findings are characteristic of decerebrate posturing? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名患有严重创伤性脑损伤的患者。哪些发现是去大脑强直 (decerebrate posturing) 的特征？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings are characteristic of decerebrate posturing?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现是去大脑强直 (decerebrate posturing) 的特征？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Extension of the legs with plantar flexion.","zh":"腿部伸展伴足跖屈。"},{"id":"D","en":"Pronation of the forearms.","zh":"前臂旋前。"},{"id":"A","en":"Internal rotation and adduction of the arms.","zh":"手臂内旋并内收。"},{"id":"C","en":"Flexion of the wrists and fingers.","zh":"腕部和手指屈曲。"},{"id":"F","en":"Flexion of the hips and knees.","zh":"髋部和膝部屈曲。"},{"id":"B","en":"Extension of the elbows.","zh":"肘部伸展。"}],"correct":["B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Decerebrate posturing (extensor posturing) involves rigid extension of the arms and legs, pronation of the forearms, and plantar flexion. It indicates more severe brainstem damage than decorticate posturing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"去大脑强直（伸肌强直）包括手臂和腿部的僵硬伸展、前臂旋前和足跖屈。它表明比去皮质强直更严重的脑干损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that 'decerebrate' has many 'e's for 'extension'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 'decerebrate' 有很多个 'e'，代表 'extension'（伸展）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":382,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.191","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.191.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.191.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,47],"fullStemEn":"A client with a chest tube is being repositioned when the chest tube becomes disconnected from the drainage system. List the nurse's actions in the correct order of priority.","fullStemZh":"一名置有胸腔引流管的患者在搬动体位时，引流管与引流系统断开。请按优先级顺序列出护士的操作步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"List the nurse's actions in the correct order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先级顺序列出护士的操作步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a chest tube is being repositioned when the chest tube becomes disconnected from the drainage system.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名置有胸腔引流管的患者在搬动体位时，引流管与引流系统断开。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider.","zh":"通知医疗保健提供者。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's respiratory status and lung sounds.","zh":"评估患者的呼吸状况和肺部听诊。"},{"id":"D","en":"Clean the ends of the tube and reconnect to a new drainage system.","zh":"清洁管道末端并重新连接到新的引流系统。"},{"id":"A","en":"Submerge the end of the chest tube in a bottle of sterile water.","zh":"将胸腔引流管末端浸入一瓶无菌水中。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The absolute priority is to restore the water seal to prevent air from entering the pleural space, which is achieved by submerging the tube in sterile water. Assessment and notification follow, before preparing a new system.","rationaleCorrectZh":"绝对优先事项是恢复水封以防止空气进入胸膜腔，这通过将管子浸入无菌水中来实现。随后进行评估和通知，然后准备新的系统。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between the tube being pulled out of the client (occlusive dressing) vs disconnected from the system (water seal).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分引流管从患者体内拔出（密闭敷料）还是从系统断开（水封）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":383,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.192","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.192.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.192.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[132,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client whose spouse died unexpectedly. Which statements by the nurse demonstrate therapeutic communication? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名配偶意外去世的患者。护士的哪些陈述体现了治疗性沟通？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements by the nurse demonstrate therapeutic communication?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士的哪些陈述体现了治疗性沟通？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"'Everything happens for a reason, and you will eventually find peace.'","zh":"“凡事发生皆有原因，你最终会找到平静的。”"},{"id":"A","en":"'I know exactly how you feel; my spouse died last year too.'","zh":"“我完全理解你的感受；我的配偶去年也去世了。”"},{"id":"E","en":"'Would you like me to sit with you for a while?'","zh":"“你愿意让我陪你坐一会儿吗？”"},{"id":"B","en":"'It must be very difficult for you to lose your spouse so suddenly.'","zh":"“如此突然地失去配偶，对你来说一定非常艰难。”"},{"id":"C","en":"'At least your spouse didn't have to suffer through a long illness.'","zh":"“至少你的配偶不必遭受长期疾病的痛苦。”"},{"id":"D","en":"'Tell me more about what your spouse was like.'","zh":"“多跟我讲讲你配偶是个什么样的人吧。”"}],"correct":["B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic communication involves acknowledging feelings, using open-ended statements, and offering presence. Non-therapeutic techniques include giving false reassurance, sharing personal stories that shift focus, and using cliches.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性沟通包括承认感受、使用开放式陈述和提供陪伴。非治疗性技术包括给予虚假安慰、分享转移注意力的个人故事以及使用陈词滥调。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for options that validate the client's experience without passing judgment or shifting the focus away from the client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找那些在不进行评判或不将焦点从客户身上移开的情况下验证客户体验的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":384,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.193","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.193.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.193.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is coordinating discharge for a client with multiple new prescriptions and home health needs. In what order should the nurse prioritize these tasks?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名有多种新处方和家庭健康需求的患者协调出院。护士应该按什么顺序排列这些任务？","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse prioritize these tasks?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该按什么顺序排列这些任务？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is coordinating discharge for a client with multiple new prescriptions and home health needs.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名有多种新处方和家庭健康需求的患者协调出院。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Confirm the client has a reliable means of transportation.","zh":"确认患者有可靠的交通工具。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify that the home health referral has been accepted.","zh":"核实家庭健康转诊是否已被接受。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide written instructions for the follow-up appointment.","zh":"提供随访预约的书面说明。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's understanding of the new medications.","zh":"评估患者对新药物的理解。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Priority in discharge planning starts with assessment of client readiness/knowledge, followed by ensuring necessary support services are in place, then logistics, and finally providing documentation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出院计划的优先事项首先是评估患者的准备情况/知识，然后是确保必要的支持服务到位，接着是物流，最后是提供文件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Assessment is almost always the first step in the nursing process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估几乎总是护理程序的第一个步骤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":385,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b10_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.194","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.194.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.194.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,47],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing an infant with suspected increased intracranial pressure (ICP). Which findings should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名怀疑颅内压 (ICP) 增高的婴儿。护士应该预见到哪些发现？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应该预见到哪些发现？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"High-pitched, shrill cry","zh":"高调、尖锐的哭声"},{"id":"D","en":"Distended scalp veins","zh":"头皮静脉扩张"},{"id":"A","en":"Bulging fontanels","zh":"囟门凸起"},{"id":"E","en":"Irritability and restlessness","zh":"易激惹和躁动"},{"id":"F","en":"Sunsetting eyes","zh":"落日征"},{"id":"C","en":"Increased appetite","zh":"食欲增加"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In infants, increased ICP manifests as bulging fontanels, high-pitched crying, irritability, and physical signs like distended scalp veins and sunsetting eyes (downward deviation of the eyes). Appetite is typically decreased due to nausea/vomiting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在婴儿中，颅内压增高表现为囟门凸起、高调哭闹、易激惹，以及头皮静脉扩张和落日征（眼睛向下偏移）等体征。食欲通常因恶心/呕吐而降低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the clinical signs of ICP in an infant (whose sutures are not fused) versus an adult.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分婴儿（骨缝未闭合）与成人的 ICP 临床体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":386,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.195","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.195.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.195.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,208],"terminalOffsetsZh":[80,92],"fullStemEn":"A client with schizophrenia is receiving haloperidol. The nurse notes a temperature of 103.6 °F (39.8 °C), blood pressure of 160/100 mmHg, and severe muscle rigidity. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名患有精神分裂症的患者正在接受氟哌啶醇治疗。护士发现患者体温为 103.6 °F (39.8 °C)，血压为 160/100 mmHg，且伴有严重的肌肉强直。护士应首先采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes a temperature of 103.6 °F (39.8 °C), blood pressure of 160/100 mmHg, and severe muscle rigidity.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现患者体温为 103.6 °F (39.8 °C)，血压为 160/100 mmHg，且伴有严重的肌肉强直。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Notify the healthcare provider immediately","zh":"立即通知医疗保健人员"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the next dose of haloperidol","zh":"给予下一次剂量的氟哌啶醇"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply a cooling blanket to the client","zh":"给患者使用降温毯"},{"id":"A","en":"Request an order for an anticholinergic medication","zh":"申请开具抗胆碱能药物的医嘱"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is exhibiting signs of Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome (NMS), a life-threatening complication of antipsychotics. Immediate notification of the provider and discontinuation of the medication are the highest priorities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表现出恶性综合征 (NMS) 的体征，这是抗精神病药物的一种危及生命的并发症。立即通知医疗保健人员并停药是最高优先级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the life-threatening condition (NMS) and choose the option that involves immediate notification and cessation of the causative agent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别出危及生命的状况 (NMS)，并选择涉及立即通知和停止致病药物的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":387,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.196","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.196.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.196.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to discharge a client with a new prescription for lisinopril. Which statements should the nurse include in the teaching? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士准备让一名新开具利辛普利处方的患者出院。护士在宣教中应包括哪些陈述？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements should the nurse include in the teaching?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在宣教中应包括哪些陈述？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Increase your intake of leafy green vegetables high in Vitamin K.","zh":"增加富含维生素 K 的绿叶蔬菜的摄入量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Rise slowly from a sitting or lying position.","zh":"从坐位或卧位起身时动作要缓慢。"},{"id":"E","en":"You may experience a metallic taste that will go away over time.","zh":"您可能会感到金属味，这会随着时间的推移而消失。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid using salt substitutes containing potassium.","zh":"避免使用含钾的代盐。"},{"id":"A","en":"Report a persistent dry cough to your healthcare provider.","zh":"如果出现持续性干咳，请报告给您的医疗保健人员。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ACE inhibitors can cause a dry cough, hyperkalemia (hence avoiding potassium-based salt substitutes), and orthostatic hypotension.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ACE 抑制剂可引起干咳、高钾血症（因此要避免使用含钾代盐）和体位性低血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the mnemonic for ACE inhibitor side effects (e.g., CAPTOPRIL: Cough, Angioedema, Potassium excess, etc.) and apply safety precautions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想 ACE 抑制剂副作用的助记词，并应用安全预防措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":388,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.197","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.197.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.197.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is managing several clients on anticoagulant therapy. For each monitoring parameter or intervention, indicate whether it is associated with Heparin or Warfarin.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理几名接受抗凝治疗的患者。对于以下每项监测参数或干预措施，请指出其是与肝素还是华法林相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each monitoring parameter or intervention, indicate whether it is associated with Heparin or Warfarin.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于以下每项监测参数或干预措施，请指出其是与肝素还是华法林相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is managing several clients on anticoagulant therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理几名接受抗凝治疗的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Monitoring Activated Partial Thromboplastin Time (aPTT)","zh":"监测活化部分凝血活酶时间 (aPTT)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Monitoring International Normalized Ratio (INR)","zh":"监测国际标准化比值 (INR)"},{"id":"r3","en":"Antidote is Vitamin K","zh":"解毒剂是维生素 K"},{"id":"r4","en":"Antidote is Protamine Sulfate","zh":"解毒剂是硫酸鱼精蛋白"},{"id":"r5","en":"Administered via subcutaneous or intravenous route","zh":"通过皮下或静脉途径给药"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Heparin","zh":"肝素"},{"id":"c2","en":"Warfarin","zh":"华法林"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Heparin is monitored by aPTT and reversed by protamine sulfate. Warfarin is monitored by PT/INR and reversed by Vitamin K.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝素通过 aPTT 监测，并由硫酸鱼精蛋白拮抗。华法林通过 PT/INR 监测，并由维生素 K 拮抗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Create a mental chart comparing these two common anticoagulants, focusing on lab values and antidotes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"建立一个对比这两项常用抗凝剂的脑图，重点关注实验室数值和解毒剂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":389,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.198","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.198.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.198.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,132],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,35],"fullStemEn":"A client with hypertension is prescribed enalapril for the first time. Which instruction is most important for the nurse to provide?","fullStemZh":"一名患有高血压的患者首次被开具依那普利。护士提供的最重要的指令是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction is most important for the nurse to provide?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士提供的最重要的指令是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with hypertension is prescribed enalapril for the first time.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有高血压的患者首次被开具依那普利。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Expect your urine to turn a brownish-orange color.","zh":"预计您的尿液会变成棕橙色。"},{"id":"D","en":"Check your pulse before taking each dose.","zh":"每次服药前检查脉搏。"},{"id":"C","en":"Take the medication with food to prevent gastric upset.","zh":"随餐服药以防止胃部不适。"},{"id":"B","en":"Rise slowly and report dizziness or fainting after the first dose.","zh":"首次服药后缓慢起身，并报告头晕或晕厥。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Enalapril can cause symptomatic hypotension, especially in clients who are volume depleted or taking diuretics. Teach the client to change position slowly and report dizziness or fainting. Higher-risk first doses may require a lower dose and supervised blood-pressure observation; routine three-hour bed rest is not required for every client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"依那普利可引起症状性低血压，尤其见于容量不足或使用利尿剂的患者。应指导患者缓慢变换体位，并报告头晕或晕厥。高风险患者首次用药时可能需要较低剂量和医疗监督下的血压观察；并非所有患者都需常规卧床 3 小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For ACE inhibitors, prioritize orthostatic safety, symptom reporting, and risk-based blood-pressure monitoring rather than a fixed bed-rest rule.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于 ACE 抑制剂，应优先考虑体位性低血压安全、症状报告及基于风险的血压监测，而不是固定的卧床规则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":390,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.199","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.199.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.199.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client who has been taking chlorpromazine for several months. Which findings would suggest the development of extrapyramidal symptoms (EPS)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名已服用氯丙嗪数月的患者。哪些发现表明出现了锥体外系症状 (EPS)？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings would suggest the development of extrapyramidal symptoms (EPS)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现表明出现了锥体外系症状 (EPS)？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Frequent thirst and excessive urination","zh":"频繁口渴和排尿过多"},{"id":"C","en":"Shuffling gait and mask-like facial expression","zh":"步态蹒跚和面具脸"},{"id":"B","en":"Involuntary tongue protrusion and smacking of lips","zh":"不由自主的舌头突出和咂嘴"},{"id":"A","en":"Restlessness and an uncontrollable need to be in motion","zh":"坐立不安且有无法控制的运动需求"},{"id":"D","en":"Sudden onset of severe muscle spasms in the neck","zh":"颈部突然出现严重的肌肉痉挛"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"EPS includes akathisia, tardive dyskinesia, pseudoparkinsonism, and acute dystonia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"EPS 包括静坐不能、迟发性运动障碍、假性帕金森综合征 和急性肌张力障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify all movement-related side effects commonly linked to first-generation antipsychotics.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别出通常与第一代抗精神病药物相关的所有运动相关副作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":391,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.200","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.200.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.200.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,45],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving enoxaparin for deep vein thrombosis prophylaxis following hip surgery. Which laboratory result should the nurse monitor most closely?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因髋关节手术后预防深静脉血栓正在接受依诺肝素治疗。护士应最密切监测哪项实验室结果？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory result should the nurse monitor most closely?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应最密切监测哪项实验室结果？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving enoxaparin for deep vein thrombosis prophylaxis following hip surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因髋关节手术后预防深静脉血栓正在接受依诺肝素治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Partial thromboplastin time (PTT)","zh":"部分凝血活酶时间 (PTT)"},{"id":"C","en":"Platelet count","zh":"血小板计数"},{"id":"A","en":"Hemoglobin and hematocrit","zh":"血红蛋白和血细胞比容"},{"id":"B","en":"Prothrombin time (PT)","zh":"凝血酶原时间 (PT)"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"While enoxaparin does not require routine coagulation monitoring (like PT or PTT), it carries a risk of Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT). Monitoring the platelet count is essential.","rationaleCorrectZh":"虽然依诺肝素不需要常规的凝血监测（如 PT 或 PTT），但它存在肝素诱导的血小板减少症 (HIT) 的风险。监测血小板计数至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between regular heparin and low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH) in terms of monitoring requirements.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分普通肝素和低分子量肝素 (LMWH) 在监测要求方面的不同。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":392,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.201","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.201.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.201.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,62],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is evaluating two clients who are taking ACE inhibitors. Client A reports a persistent cough. Client B presents with sudden swelling of the lips and tongue. Identify the characteristic for each finding.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估两名服用 ACE 抑制剂的患者。患者 A 报告持续咳嗽。患者 B 出现嘴唇和舌头突然肿胀。请识别每种发现的特征。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify the characteristic for each finding.","terminalSentenceZh":"请识别每种发现的特征。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Client B presents with sudden swelling of the lips and tongue.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者 B 出现嘴唇和舌头突然肿胀。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Persistent dry cough","zh":"持续性干咳"},{"id":"r2","en":"Angioedema","zh":"血管性水肿"},{"id":"r3","en":"Requires immediate medical attention","zh":"需要立即就医"},{"id":"r4","en":"Often resolves by switching to an ARB","zh":"通常通过改用 ARB 解决"},{"id":"r5","en":"Linked to bradykinin accumulation","zh":"与缓激肽积累有关"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Both","zh":"两者均有"},{"id":"c1","en":"Cough Only","zh":"仅咳嗽"},{"id":"c2","en":"Angioedema Only","zh":"仅血管性水肿"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Both side effects are related to bradykinin. Cough is annoying but not an emergency; angioedema is a life-threatening airway emergency. Both usually necessitate switching drug classes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这两种副作用都与缓激肽有关。咳嗽令人烦恼但不是紧急情况；血管性水肿是危及生命的气道紧急情况。两者通常都需要更换药物类别。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between a common 'nuisance' side effect and a rare 'lethal' adverse reaction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分常见的“讨厌”副作用和罕见的“致命”不良反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":393,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.202","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.202.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.202.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,44],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing education to a client prescribed rivaroxaban for atrial fibrillation. Which information should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名因房颤被开具利伐沙班的患者进行宣教。护士应包括哪些信息？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which information should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些信息？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Take the medication with the evening meal to improve absorption.","zh":"随晚餐服用药物以提高吸收。"},{"id":"C","en":"Report any signs of unusual bruising or bleeding.","zh":"报告任何异常瘀伤或出血的迹象。"},{"id":"D","en":"Do not take aspirin or NSAIDs without consulting your doctor.","zh":"未经咨询医生，请勿服用阿司匹林或非甾体抗炎药 (NSAIDs)。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid excessive intake of green leafy vegetables.","zh":"避免过量摄入绿叶蔬菜。"},{"id":"A","en":"Routine blood tests for INR monitoring are not required.","zh":"不需要进行常规的 INR 监测血检。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rivaroxaban (a DOAC) does not require INR monitoring and is not affected by Vitamin K intake. However, it increases bleeding risk, and the 15mg and 20mg doses must be taken with food for optimal absorption.","rationaleCorrectZh":"利伐沙班（一种 DOAC）不需要 INR 监测，不受维生素 K 摄入的影响。然而，它会增加出血风险，且 15mg 和 20mg 剂量必须随餐服用以获得最佳吸收。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Carefully differentiate DOACs (like rivaroxaban) from warfarin regarding diet and monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在饮食和监测方面，仔细区分 DOAC（如利伐沙班）和华法林。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":394,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.203","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.203.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.203.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,43],"fullStemEn":"A client is prescribed clozapine for treatment-resistant schizophrenia. Which laboratory finding would require the nurse to withhold the medication and notify the healthcare provider?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因难治性精神分裂症被开具氯氮平。哪项实验室发现需要护士停药并通知医疗保健人员？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory finding would require the nurse to withhold the medication and notify the healthcare provider?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项实验室发现需要护士停药并通知医疗保健人员？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is prescribed clozapine for treatment-resistant schizophrenia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因难治性精神分裂症被开具氯氮平。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"White blood cell (WBC) count of 2.8 ×10³/µL","zh":"白细胞 (WBC) 计数 2.8 ×10³/µL"},{"id":"A","en":"Blood glucose of 110 mg/dL","zh":"血糖 110 mg/dL"},{"id":"B","en":"Serum potassium of 3.6 mEq/L","zh":"血清钾 3.6 mEq/L"},{"id":"C","en":"Total cholesterol of 210 mg/dL","zh":"总胆固醇 210 mg/dL"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clozapine carries a black box warning for agranulocytosis. A WBC count below 3 ×10³/µL or an absolute neutrophil count (ANC) below 1,500/mm³ requires immediate intervention and possible cessation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氯氮平具有粒细胞缺乏症的黑框警告。白细胞计数低于 3 ×10³/µL 或绝对中性粒细胞计数 (ANC) 低于 1,500/mm³ 需要立即干预并可能停药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the 'Black Box' warnings associated with high-alert medications like clozapine.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注与氯氮平等高风险药物相关的“黑框”警告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":395,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.204","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.204.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.204.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,43],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is instructing a client on warfarin therapy. Which of the following should be included in the dietary instructions? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名接受华法林治疗的患者。饮食指导中应包括以下哪些内容？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following should be included in the dietary instructions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"饮食指导中应包括以下哪些内容？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Completely eliminate spinach and kale from your diet.","zh":"从饮食中完全剔除菠菜和羽衣甘蓝。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid binge drinking of alcohol.","zh":"避免暴饮酒。"},{"id":"D","en":"Be cautious with herbal supplements like Ginkgo biloba.","zh":"对银杏等草本补充剂要保持谨慎。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain a consistent intake of foods high in Vitamin K.","zh":"保持富含维生素 K 食物的摄入量一致。"},{"id":"E","en":"Cranberry juice may increase the effect of warfarin.","zh":"蔓越莓汁可能会增强华法林的效果。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Consistency (not elimination) of Vitamin K is key. Alcohol, certain herbs, and cranberry juice can all interact with warfarin metabolism.","rationaleCorrectZh":"保持维生素 K 摄入的一致性（而非剔除）是关键。酒精、某些草本植物和蔓越莓汁都可能与华法林代谢产生相互作用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for words like 'completely eliminate' which are often too extreme in NCLEX questions. Focus on 'consistency' for Vitamin K and warfarin.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找像“完全剔除”这样的词，这些词在 NCLEX 题目中通常过于极端。对于维生素 K 和华法林，重点关注“一致性”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":396,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.205","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.205.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.205.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to perform a physical assessment on a 15-year-old client. Which action by the nurse is most appropriate to ensure the client's privacy and comfort?","fullStemZh":"护士准备为一名 15 岁的客户进行体格检查。护士采取哪种行动最能确保客户的隐私和舒适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is most appropriate to ensure the client's privacy and comfort?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士采取哪种行动最能确保客户的隐私和舒适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to perform a physical assessment on a 15-year-old client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备为一名 15 岁的客户进行体格检查。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Provide a private space and ask the parent to wait outside during the interview.","zh":"提供私密空间，并要求家长在面谈期间在外面等候。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform the assessment in a semi-private area to save time.","zh":"在半私密区域进行评估以节省时间。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the parent to remain in the room to provide support.","zh":"要求家长留在房间里提供支持。"},{"id":"D","en":"Instruct the client to remain fully dressed throughout the entire exam.","zh":"指示客户在整个检查过程中保持穿着整齐。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adolescents value privacy and may be more open to discussing sensitive health issues without a parent present.","rationaleCorrectZh":"青少年重视隐私，在家长不在场的情况下可能更愿意讨论敏感的健康问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the developmental needs of the adolescent, which include autonomy and privacy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注青少年的发育需求，包括自主权和隐私。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":397,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.206","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.206.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.206.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[175,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is conducting a health screening for a group of high school students. Which of the following topics are priority health promotion areas for the adolescent population? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一组高中生进行健康筛查。以下哪些主题是青少年群体优先考虑的健康促进领域？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following topics are priority health promotion areas for the adolescent population?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些主题是青少年群体优先考虑的健康促进领域？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hospice care options","zh":"临终关怀选择"},{"id":"F","en":"Retirement planning","zh":"退休计划"},{"id":"D","en":"Mental health and suicide prevention","zh":"心理健康和自杀预防"},{"id":"A","en":"Injury prevention and motor vehicle safety","zh":"伤害预防和机动车安全"},{"id":"B","en":"Substance misuse prevention","zh":"物质滥用预防"},{"id":"E","en":"Sexual health and STI prevention","zh":"性健康和性传播感染预防"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Accidents (unintentional injuries), suicide, and substance misuse are leading causes of morbidity and mortality in adolescents. Sexual health is also a critical area.","rationaleCorrectZh":"事故（意外伤害）、自杀和物质滥用是青少年发病和死亡的主要原因。性健康也是一个关键领域。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the major causes of mortality and morbidity for the specific age group.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定特定年龄段发病和死亡的主要原因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":398,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.207","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.207.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.207.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching an adolescent how to use a metered-dose inhaler (MDI) with a spacer. The nurse should explain that the primary purpose of the spacer is to:","fullStemZh":"护士正在教一名青少年如何使用带储雾罐的定量吸入器 (MDI)。护士应解释储雾罐的主要目的是：","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should explain that the primary purpose of the spacer is to:","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应解释储雾罐的主要目的是：","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching an adolescent how to use a metered-dose inhaler (MDI) with a spacer.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教一名青少年如何使用带储雾罐的定量吸入器 (MDI)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Decrease the amount of medication that reaches the lungs.","zh":"减少到达肺部的药物量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Eliminate the need for slow, deep inhalations.","zh":"消除缓慢、深吸气的需要。"},{"id":"A","en":"Enhance delivery of the medication to the lower airways.","zh":"增强药物向较低气道的输送。"},{"id":"D","en":"Increase the sound made by the inhaler to ensure it is working.","zh":"增加吸入器发出的声音以确保其正常工作。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A spacer helps to slow down the speed of the aerosol and traps the medication, allowing the client to inhale more of the dose into the lower airways rather than it hitting the back of the throat.","rationaleCorrectZh":"储雾罐有助于减缓气雾的速度并捕获药物，使客户能够将更多的剂量吸入较低的气道，而不是撞击喉咙后部。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the physics of an MDI. The medication moves fast; a spacer slows it down for better absorption.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑 MDI 的物理原理。药物移动很快；储雾罐将其减慢以更好地吸收。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":399,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.208","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.208.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.208.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is instructing a client on the correct sequence of steps for using a metered-dose inhaler (MDI) without a spacer. Place the steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导客户不带储雾罐使用定量吸入器 (MDI) 的正确步骤顺序。按正确顺序排列步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"按正确顺序排列步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is instructing a client on the correct sequence of steps for using a metered-dose inhaler (MDI) without a spacer.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在指导客户不带储雾罐使用定量吸入器 (MDI) 的正确步骤顺序。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hold breath for 10 seconds (or as long as comfortable).","zh":"憋气 10 秒（或尽可能长的时间，以舒适为准）。"},{"id":"E","en":"Wait 30 to 60 seconds before taking a second puff if prescribed.","zh":"如果医嘱要求，在进行第二次吸入前等待 30 至 60 秒。"},{"id":"B","en":"Exhale comfortably through the mouth.","zh":"通过口部舒适地呼气。"},{"id":"C","en":"Depress the canister while inhaling slowly and deeply through the mouth.","zh":"按下罐体，同时通过口部缓慢而深地吸气。"},{"id":"A","en":"Shake the inhaler vigorously for 3 to 5 seconds.","zh":"剧烈摇晃吸入器 3 至 5 秒。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence is to shake the medication, exhale, activate the inhaler during inspiration, hold the breath to allow deposition, and wait between doses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的顺序是摇匀药物、呼气、在吸气期间启动吸入器、憋气以允许沉积，并在两次剂量之间等待。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize performing the action step-by-step. Preparation (shake), preparation of lungs (exhale), action (inhale/depress), retention (hold), and interval (wait).","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象一下逐步执行该操作。准备（摇晃）、肺部准备（呼气）、行动（吸入/按下）、保留（憋气）和间隔（等待）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":400,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.209","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.209.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.209.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"According to Erikson's stages of psychosocial development, which task is the primary focus of the adolescent stage?","fullStemZh":"根据艾里克森的心理社会发展阶段，青少年阶段的主要重点是哪项任务？","terminalSentenceEn":"According to Erikson's stages of psychosocial development, which task is the primary focus of the adolescent stage?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据艾里克森的心理社会发展阶段，青少年阶段的主要重点是哪项任务？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Identity vs. Role Confusion","zh":"自我认同对角色混乱"},{"id":"B","en":"Industry vs. Inferiority","zh":"勤奋对自卑"},{"id":"C","en":"Intimacy vs. Isolation","zh":"亲密对孤独"},{"id":"D","en":"Trust vs. Mistrust","zh":"信任对不信任"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adolescents (ages 12-18) are in the stage of Identity vs. Role Confusion, where they explore who they are and their place in society.","rationaleCorrectZh":"青少年（12-18 岁）处于自我认同对角色混乱阶段，在此阶段他们探索自己是谁以及在社会中的地位。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the key milestones and age groups associated with Erikson's theory.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住与艾里克森理论相关的关键里程碑和年龄组。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":401,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.210","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.210.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.210.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a 16-year-old client. Which behaviors indicate that the client has reached Piaget's stage of formal operational thought? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名 16 岁的客户。哪些行为表明客户已达到皮亚杰的形式运算思维阶段？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which behaviors indicate that the client has reached Piaget's stage of formal operational thought?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些行为表明客户已达到皮亚杰的形式运算思维阶段？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The client understands the concept of conservation of volume.","zh":"客户理解体积守恒的概念。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client is able to think about abstract concepts such as justice and future goals.","zh":"客户能够思考抽象概念，如正义和未来目标。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client can consider multiple hypothetical outcomes for a single situation.","zh":"客户可以考虑单一情况的多种假设结果。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client uses deductive reasoning to solve problems.","zh":"客户使用演绎推理来解决问题。"},{"id":"E","en":"The client's thinking is primarily egocentric and focused on the present.","zh":"客户的思维主要是以自我为中心并关注当下。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Formal operations (age 11 through adulthood) involve abstract thinking, deductive reasoning, and the ability to handle hypothetical situations.","rationaleCorrectZh":"形式运算（11 岁到成年）涉及抽象思维、演绎推理以及处理假设情况的能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 'concrete' (tangible, here and now) and 'formal' (abstract, logical, future-oriented) thinking.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“具体”（切实的、此时此地）和“形式”（抽象的、逻辑的、面向未来的）思维。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":402,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.211","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.211.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.211.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,53],"fullStemEn":"During a wellness exam, an adolescent female client asks about the normal sequence of pubertal changes. The nurse should explain that which of the following is typically the first sign of puberty in females?","fullStemZh":"在健康体检中，一名青少年女性客户询问青春期变化的正常顺序。护士应解释以下哪项通常是女性青春期的第一个征兆？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should explain that which of the following is typically the first sign of puberty in females?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应解释以下哪项通常是女性青春期的第一个征兆？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During a wellness exam, an adolescent female client asks about the normal sequence of pubertal changes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在健康体检中，一名青少年女性客户询问青春期变化的正常顺序。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Appearance of axillary hair","zh":"腋毛出现"},{"id":"B","en":"Development of breast buds (thelarche)","zh":"乳蕾发育（乳房初育）"},{"id":"C","en":"Onset of menarche","zh":"月经初潮"},{"id":"D","en":"Rapid increase in height (growth spurt)","zh":"身高快速增加（生长突增）"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For most females, the development of breast buds (thelarche) is the first visible sign of puberty, followed by pubic hair development and then menarche.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于大多数女性来说，乳蕾发育（乳房初育）是青春期的第一个可见征兆，随后是阴毛发育，然后是月经初潮。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know the sequential stages of physical development (Tanner stages) for both males and females.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解男性和女性身体发育的连续阶段（丹纳阶段）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":403,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.212","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.212.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.212.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[195,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,56],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing discharge education to an adolescent with asthma regarding the maintenance of their metered-dose inhaler (MDI). Which of the following instructions should the nurse include? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名患有哮喘的青少年提供有关定量吸入器 (MDI) 维护的出院教育。护士应包括以下哪些指令？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括以下哪些指令？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Rinse the mouth with water after using a corticosteroid inhaler.","zh":"使用皮质类固醇吸入器后用水漱口。"},{"id":"F","en":"Check the expiration date on the canister regularly.","zh":"定期检查罐体上的有效期。"},{"id":"B","en":"Boil the medication canister to ensure it is sterile.","zh":"煮沸药物罐体以确保其无菌。"},{"id":"C","en":"Store the inhaler in a cool, dry place.","zh":"将吸入器存放在阴凉干燥的地方。"},{"id":"E","en":"Discard the inhaler when it feels empty, even if the counter says doses remain.","zh":"当吸入器感觉空了时就将其丢弃，即使计数器显示仍有剂量。"},{"id":"A","en":"Clean the plastic mouthpiece at least once a week with warm, soapy water.","zh":"每周至少用温肥皂水清洁一次塑料咬嘴。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Maintenance involves hygiene, proper storage, preventing side effects (like thrush), and ensuring the device is within its effective date.","rationaleCorrectZh":"维护涉及卫生、正确储存、预防副作用（如鹅口疮）以及确保设备在有效期内。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on safety (no heat) and efficacy (cleaning and storage). For steroids, remember the risk of thrush.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注安全（严禁受热）和功效（清洁和储存）。对于类固醇，记住鹅口疮的风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":404,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.213","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.213.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.213.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,48],"fullStemEn":"A 14-year-old client refuses a treatment because 'my friends will think it's weird.' Which developmental concept best explains this behavior?","fullStemZh":"一名 14 岁的客户拒绝接受治疗，因为“我的朋友会觉得这很奇怪”。哪种发育概念最能解释这种行为？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which developmental concept best explains this behavior?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种发育概念最能解释这种行为？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 14-year-old client refuses a treatment because 'my friends will think it's weird.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 14 岁的客户拒绝接受治疗，因为“我的朋友会觉得这很奇怪”。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Imaginary audience","zh":"假想观众"},{"id":"C","en":"Object permanence","zh":"物体恒存"},{"id":"B","en":"Magical thinking","zh":"幻想性思维"},{"id":"A","en":"Animism","zh":"万物有灵论"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The 'imaginary audience' is a common adolescent belief that everyone is watching and evaluating them, leading to extreme self-consciousness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"“假想观众”是青少年的一种普遍信念，即认为每个人都在注视和评价他们，从而导致极度的自我意识。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the age-specific terminology associated with adolescent social development.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别与青少年社会发展相关的特定年龄术语。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":405,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b3_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.214","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.214.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.214.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,47],"fullStemEn":"A 17-year-old client comes to the clinic alone and requests testing for sexually transmitted infections (STIs). Which action should the nurse take?","fullStemZh":"一名 17 岁的客户独自来到诊所，要求进行性传播感染 (STI) 检测。护士应该采取什么行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该采取什么行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 17-year-old client comes to the clinic alone and requests testing for sexually transmitted infections (STIs).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 17 岁的客户独自来到诊所，要求进行性传播感染 (STI) 检测。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Refuse to test until a parent or legal guardian provides consent.","zh":"在家长或法定监护人提供同意之前拒绝检测。"},{"id":"A","en":"Instruct the client to return when they are 18 years old.","zh":"指示客户在 18 岁时再来。"},{"id":"B","en":"Provide the testing and maintain the client's confidentiality.","zh":"提供检测并维护客户的机密性。"},{"id":"C","en":"Call the client's parents to inform them of the request.","zh":"给客户的父母打电话，告知他们这一要求。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In most jurisdictions, minors have the legal right to consent to testing and treatment for STIs without parental involvement or consent.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在大多数司法管辖区，未成年人有合法权利在没有父母参与或同意的情况下，同意进行性传播感染的检测和治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the exceptions to parental consent for minors: STIs, pregnancy, and substance misuse treatment in many areas.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住未成年人无需父母同意的例外情况：在许多地区包括性传播感染、怀孕和物质滥用治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":406,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.215","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.215.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.215.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to admit a client with suspected bacterial meningitis. Which personal protective equipment (PPE) is most essential for the nurse to wear when entering the client's room?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备接收一名疑似细菌性脑膜炎的患者。护士进入病房时最必不可少的个人防护装备（PPE）是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which personal protective equipment (PPE) is most essential for the nurse to wear when entering the client's room?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士进入病房时最必不可少的个人防护装备（PPE）是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to admit a client with suspected bacterial meningitis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备接收一名疑似细菌性脑膜炎的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Surgical mask","zh":"外科口罩"},{"id":"B","en":"N95 respirator","zh":"N95 呼吸器"},{"id":"C","en":"Shoe covers","zh":"鞋套"},{"id":"A","en":"Gown and gloves","zh":"隔离衣和手套"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Meningococcal meningitis is transmitted by respiratory droplets. For Droplet Precautions, the nurse dons a surgical mask upon entry into the client's room or patient space.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脑膜炎球菌性脑膜炎通过呼吸道飞沫传播。实施飞沫传播预防措施时，护士进入患者病房或患者空间即应佩戴外科口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the mode of transmission for bacterial meningitis. Remember 'Droplet' for meningitis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定细菌性脑膜炎的传播途径。记住脑膜炎采用“飞沫”预防措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to admit a client with suspected bacterial meningitis.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正准备接收一名疑似细菌性脑膜炎的患者。"}
{"queueIndex":407,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.216","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.216.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.216.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is admitting a client with high fever, stiff neck, and photophobia. In which order should the nurse perform the following actions? (Arrange the steps in the correct sequence.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在接收一名高热、颈项强直和畏光的患者。护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？（按正确顺序排列步骤。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Arrange the steps in the correct sequence.)","terminalSentenceZh":"按正确顺序排列步骤。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"In which order should the nurse perform the following actions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？（","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Initiate droplet precautions.","zh":"启动飞沫预防措施。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the first dose of prescribed intravenous antibiotics.","zh":"给予第一剂开具的静脉抗生素。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assist with a lumbar puncture.","zh":"协助进行腰椎穿刺。"},{"id":"B","en":"Obtain ordered blood cultures without delaying treatment.","zh":"采集医嘱要求的血培养，同时不延误治疗。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Initiate Droplet Precautions immediately. Obtain ordered blood cultures promptly without delaying therapy, then administer the first prescribed intravenous antibiotics. Assist with lumbar puncture before antibiotics only when it is safe and immediately available; otherwise treatment must not wait for the procedure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"立即启动飞沫传播预防措施。及时采集医嘱要求的血培养且不得延误治疗，随后给予第一剂处方静脉抗生素。仅在安全且能立即进行时才在抗生素前协助腰椎穿刺；否则治疗不得等待该操作。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For suspected bacterial meningitis: isolate, obtain blood cultures without delay, start antibiotics urgently, and perform lumbar puncture promptly only when it will not delay treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"疑似细菌性脑膜炎时：先隔离，在不延误的情况下采集血培养，紧急开始抗生素，并仅在不会延误治疗时及时进行腰椎穿刺。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":408,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.217","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.217.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.217.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,31],"fullStemEn":"A client arrives in the emergency department after a liquid chemical splash to the eyes. What is the priority nursing action?","fullStemZh":"一名患者在眼部溅入液体化学品后到达急诊科。优先护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the priority nursing action?","terminalSentenceZh":"优先护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client arrives in the emergency department after a liquid chemical splash to the eyes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在眼部溅入液体化学品后到达急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Irrigate the eyes with copious amounts of normal saline.","zh":"用大量生理盐水冲洗眼睛。"},{"id":"A","en":"Apply an antibiotic ophthalmic ointment.","zh":"涂抹抗生素眼膏。"},{"id":"B","en":"Identify the specific chemical involved.","zh":"确定涉及的具体化学品。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess the client's visual acuity.","zh":"评估患者的视力。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate irrigation is the priority to minimize tissue damage from chemical burns. This should be done for at least 15-30 minutes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"立即冲洗是首要任务，以最大限度地减少化学烧伤造成的组织损伤。冲洗应持续至少15-30分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In chemical splashes, the priority is always to remove the agent from the body (decontaminate) immediately.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在发生化学性溅入时，首要任务始终是立即清除体内的化学物质（去污）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":409,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.218","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.218.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.218.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing radiation safety protocols. For each action, indicate whether it effectively decreases or increases the nurse's radiation exposure.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查辐射安全方案。针对每项操作，指出其是有效减少还是增加护士的辐射暴露。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each action, indicate whether it effectively decreases or increases the nurse's radiation exposure.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项操作，指出其是有效减少还是增加护士的辐射暴露。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing radiation safety protocols.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查辐射安全方案。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Doubling the distance from the radiation source","zh":"与辐射源的距离增加一倍"},{"id":"r2","en":"Wearing a lead apron during fluoroscopy","zh":"在透视过程中佩戴铅围裙"},{"id":"r3","en":"Clustering nursing care tasks to minimize time in the room","zh":"集中护理任务以减少在病房内的时间"},{"id":"r4","en":"Standing directly at the head of the bed during a portable X-ray","zh":"在进行床边X光检查时直接站在床头"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Increases Exposure","zh":"增加暴露"},{"id":"c1","en":"Decreases Exposure","zh":"减少暴露"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Radiation safety is based on three principles: Time (minimize), Distance (maximize), and Shielding (use lead). Increasing distance, using lead aprons, and clustering care decrease exposure. Standing close to the source increases exposure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"辐射安全基于三个原则：时间（最短化）、距离（最大化）和屏蔽（使用铅防护）。增加距离、使用铅围裙和集中护理可减少暴露。靠近辐射源站立会增加暴露。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the 'Time, Distance, Shielding' rule to each scenario.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“时间、距离、屏蔽”规则应用于每个场景。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":410,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.219","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.219.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.219.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,198],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with confirmed Neisseria meningitidis meningitis. Indicate whether the following interventions are part of Droplet Precautions or Standard Precautions for this client.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名确诊为脑膜炎奈瑟菌脑膜炎的患者。指出以下干预措施属于该患者的飞沫预防措施还是标准预防措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Indicate whether the following interventions are part of Droplet Precautions or Standard Precautions for this client.","terminalSentenceZh":"指出以下干预措施属于该患者的飞沫预防措施还是标准预防措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with confirmed Neisseria meningitidis meningitis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名确诊为脑膜炎奈瑟菌脑膜炎的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Wearing a surgical mask when performing a dressing change","zh":"更换敷料时佩戴外科口罩"},{"id":"r2","en":"Performing hand hygiene before and after client contact","zh":"在接触患者前后进行手部卫生"},{"id":"r3","en":"Placing the client in a private room","zh":"将患者安置在单人病房"},{"id":"r4","en":"Wearing gloves when emptying a urinary drainage bag","zh":"清空尿袋时佩戴手套"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Droplet Precautions","zh":"飞沫预防措施"},{"id":"c2","en":"Standard Precautions","zh":"标准预防措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard precautions apply to all clients (hand hygiene, gloves for body fluids). Droplet precautions specifically include a private room and a surgical mask when in close proximity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标准预防措施适用于所有患者（手部卫生，接触体液时佩戴手套）。飞沫预防措施特别包括单人房间和近距离接触时佩戴外科口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between actions that apply to all patients (Standard) and those specific to the disease's transmission (Droplet).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分适用于所有患者的操作（标准）和针对疾病传播途径的特定操作（飞沫）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":411,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.220.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,43],"fullStemEn":"A client has been exposed to a dry chemical powder on their arms and legs. In what order should the nurse perform decontamination? (Arrange the steps in the correct sequence.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者的胳膊和腿接触了干化学粉末。护士应按什么顺序进行去污？（按正确顺序排列步骤。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Arrange the steps in the correct sequence.)","terminalSentenceZh":"按正确顺序排列步骤。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse perform decontamination?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序进行去污？（","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Flush the affected areas with large amounts of water.","zh":"用大量水冲洗受影响区域。"},{"id":"B","en":"Brush off the dry powder from the skin.","zh":"刷掉皮肤上的干粉。"},{"id":"D","en":"Don personal protective equipment (PPE).","zh":"穿戴个人防护装备（PPE）。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove the client's contaminated clothing.","zh":"脱掉患者受污染的衣服。"}],"correct":["D","B","A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, the nurse must protect themselves (PPE). For dry chemicals, brush the powder off first because water may activate or spread certain dry chemicals. Then remove clothing and finally flush with water.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，护士必须保护自己（PPE）。对于干化学品，应先刷掉粉末，因为水可能会激活或扩散某些干化学品。然后脱掉衣服，最后用水冲洗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: Self-protection (PPE) is always first. For dry chemicals, brushing comes before flushing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：自我保护（PPE）始终第一。对于干化学品，刷掉先于冲洗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":412,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.221.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with an internal radiation implant (brachytherapy). Which action is appropriate for managing soiled linens?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名带有体内放射性植入物（近距离放射治疗）的患者。处理弄脏的床单时，哪项操作是适当的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is appropriate for managing soiled linens?","terminalSentenceZh":"处理弄脏的床单时，哪项操作是适当的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with an internal radiation implant (brachytherapy).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名带有体内放射性植入物（近距离放射治疗）的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Discard linens in a regular trash container.","zh":"将床单丢弃在普通垃圾桶中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Place linens in a lead-lined container in the client's room.","zh":"将床单放在患者病房内的铅衬容器中。"},{"id":"C","en":"Keep linens in the client's room until the radiation source is removed.","zh":"将床单留在患者病房内，直到辐射源被移除。"},{"id":"A","en":"Send linens to the hospital laundry immediately.","zh":"立即将床单送到医院洗衣房。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Linens and trash should be kept in the room to prevent the accidental spread of radiation until the source is removed and checked by the radiation safety officer.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在移除辐射源并由辐射安全官员检查之前，床单和垃圾应留在病房内，以防止辐射意外扩散。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on containment. Any item that might contain radiation should stay in the controlled environment until verified.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点在于控制。任何可能含有辐射的物品都应留在受控环境中，直到通过验证。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":413,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.222","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.222.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.222.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,40],"fullStemEn":"A client with bacterial meningitis must be transported to the radiology department for a CT scan. Which action should the nurse take?","fullStemZh":"一名患有细菌性脑膜炎的患者必须被转运到放射科进行CT扫描。护士应该采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with bacterial meningitis must be transported to the radiology department for a CT scan.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有细菌性脑膜炎的患者必须被转运到放射科进行CT扫描。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Place a surgical mask on the client during transport.","zh":"在转运过程中给患者佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the radiology department to wear N95 respirators.","zh":"通知放射科工作人员佩戴N95呼吸器。"},{"id":"C","en":"Cancel the CT scan until the client has been on antibiotics for 72 hours.","zh":"在患者接受抗生素治疗满72小时之前，取消CT扫描。"},{"id":"A","en":"Wear a gown, gloves, and mask while pushing the stretcher.","zh":"推担架时穿隔离衣、戴手套和口罩。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When transporting a client on droplet precautions, the client must wear a surgical mask to contain secretions. The nurse does not need full PPE while transporting if not in close contact with secretions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在转运处于飞沫预防措施的患者时，患者必须佩戴外科口罩以控制分泌物。如果没有与分泌物密切接触，护士在转运时不需要穿戴全套PPE。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In infection control transport questions, usually, the client is the one who needs to be masked/contained.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在感染控制转运问题中，通常是患者需要佩戴口罩/被控制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":414,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.223","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.223.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.223.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing education to laboratory workers about chemical exposure. Match the type of chemical exposure to the correct immediate first aid action.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向实验室工作人员提供有关化学暴露的教育。将化学暴露类型与正确的即刻急救措施相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match the type of chemical exposure to the correct immediate first aid action.","terminalSentenceZh":"将化学暴露类型与正确的即刻急救措施相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing education to laboratory workers about chemical exposure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向实验室工作人员提供有关化学暴露的教育。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Liquid acid splash to the eyes","zh":"液体酸溅入眼睛"},{"id":"r2","en":"Inhalation of toxic chemical fumes","zh":"吸入有毒化学烟雾"},{"id":"r3","en":"Alkali liquid splash to the skin","zh":"碱性液体溅到皮肤上"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Flush with water for at least 20 minutes","zh":"用水冲洗至少20分钟"},{"id":"c1","en":"Move to fresh air immediately","zh":"立即移至空气新鲜处"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Eye and skin splashes require immediate and prolonged water irrigation to neutralize/remove the chemical. Inhalation requires immediate removal from the source to fresh air.","rationaleCorrectZh":"眼部和皮肤溅入需要立即且长时间的水冲洗以中和/去除化学物质。吸入则需要立即脱离源头移至空气新鲜处。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between dermal/ocular (flush) and respiratory (fresh air) routes of exposure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分皮肤/眼部（冲洗）和呼吸道（空气新鲜）暴露途径。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":415,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b4_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.224","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.224.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.224.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[184,228],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,62],"fullStemEn":"The nurse enters the room of a client with an internal cervical radiation implant and finds the implant lying on the bed. In what order should the nurse perform the following actions? (Arrange the steps in the correct sequence.)","fullStemZh":"护士进入一名带有子宫颈内部放射性植入物患者的病房，发现植入物掉在床上。护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？（按正确顺序排列步骤。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Arrange the steps in the correct sequence.)","terminalSentenceZh":"按正确顺序排列步骤。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse perform the following actions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？（","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and radiation oncologist.","zh":"通知医疗保健提供者和放射肿瘤科医生。"},{"id":"D","en":"Instruct the client to remain still.","zh":"嘱咐患者保持不动。"},{"id":"B","en":"Pick up the implant with long-handled forceps.","zh":"用长柄镊子夹起植入物。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the implant in a lead-lined container.","zh":"将植入物放在铅衬容器中。"}],"correct":["D","B","A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, ensure the client's safety by telling them to remain still. Then, use long-handled forceps to pick up the source (never use hands). Place it in the lead container (shielding). Finally, notify the appropriate medical staff.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，通过嘱咐患者保持不动来确保其安全。然后，使用长柄镊子夹起辐射源（绝不能用手）。将其放入铅容器中（屏蔽）。最后，通知相关的医务人员。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Emergency radiation sequence: Safety -> Shielding (Forceps/Lead) -> Communication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"紧急辐射处理顺序：安全 -> 屏蔽（镊子/铅）-> 沟通。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":416,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.225","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.225.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.225.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[133,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is calculating the caloric intake for a client's snack. The snack contains 15 grams of carbohydrates and 5 grams of protein. How many total calories are provided by this snack?","fullStemZh":"护士正在计算患者零食的热量摄入。该零食含有 15 克碳水化合物和 5 克蛋白质。该零食总共提供多少卡路里？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many total calories are provided by this snack?","terminalSentenceZh":"该零食总共提供多少卡路里？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The snack contains 15 grams of carbohydrates and 5 grams of protein.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该零食含有 15 克碳水化合物和 5 克蛋白质。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"calories","zh":"卡路里"},"acceptable":["80"],"numeric":{"value":80,"tolerance":0,"unit":"calories"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Carbohydrates provide 4 calories per gram, and protein provides 4 calories per gram. (15g carbs × 4 cal/g) + (5g protein × 4 cal/g) = 60 + 20 = 80 calories.","rationaleCorrectZh":"碳水化合物每克提供 4 卡路里，蛋白质每克提供 4 卡路里。(15克碳水 × 4卡/克) + (5克蛋白质 × 4卡/克) = 60 + 20 = 80 卡路里。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the 4-4-9 rule: Carbohydrates = 4 cal/g, Protein = 4 cal/g, Fat = 9 cal/g.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 4-4-9 原则：碳水化合物 = 4 卡/克，蛋白质 = 4 卡/克，脂肪 = 9 卡/克。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":417,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.226","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.226.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.226.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,30],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing education on sleep hygiene to a client with insomnia. Which instruction should the nurse include?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名失眠患者提供睡眠卫生教育。护士应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing education on sleep hygiene to a client with insomnia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名失眠患者提供睡眠卫生教育。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Use the bed for reading, watching television, and working.","zh":"在床上看书、看电视和工作。"},{"id":"D","en":"Drink a glass of red wine before bedtime to promote relaxation.","zh":"睡前喝一杯红酒以促进放松。"},{"id":"B","en":"Exercise vigorously for 30 minutes just before going to sleep.","zh":"睡觉前进行 30 分钟剧烈运动。"},{"id":"C","en":"Maintain a consistent sleep-wake schedule, even on weekends.","zh":"即使在周末，也要保持一致的睡眠-觉醒时间表。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A consistent sleep-wake schedule helps regulate the body's internal clock and improves sleep quality.","rationaleCorrectZh":"一致的睡眠-觉醒时间表有助于调节人体的生物钟并提高睡眠质量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the goal of 'hygiene,' which implies creating healthy routines and habits.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于“卫生”的目标，这意味着建立健康的日常习惯。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":418,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.227","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.227.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.227.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,138],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,37],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving continuous enteral feedings via a nasogastric tube. Which nursing action is most effective in preventing aspiration?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在通过鼻胃管接受持续肠内营养。哪项护理措施在预防误吸方面最有效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is most effective in preventing aspiration?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项护理措施在预防误吸方面最有效？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving continuous enteral feedings via a nasogastric tube.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者正在通过鼻胃管接受持续肠内营养。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Maintaining the head of the bed elevated at 30 to 45 degrees.","zh":"保持床头抬高 30 至 45 度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Flushing the tube with 30 mL of water every 4 hours.","zh":"每 4 小时用 30 毫升水冲洗管路一次。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verifying the tube placement using the air auscultation method.","zh":"使用空气听诊法验证管路位置。"},{"id":"C","en":"Checking the gastric residual volume every 4 hours.","zh":"每 4 小时检查一次胃残留量。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Elevating the head of the bed (HOB) uses gravity to prevent gastric contents from refluxing into the esophagus and airway, which is the primary intervention for aspiration prevention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"抬高床头 (HOB) 利用重力防止胃内容物反流到食管和气道，这是预防误吸的首要干预措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember 'Safety First.' For enteral feeding, aspiration is the biggest safety risk, and positioning is the primary defense.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“安全第一”。对于肠内营养，误吸是最大的安全风险，而体位是首要防御手段。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client is receiving continuous enteral feedings via a nasogastric tube.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患者正在通过鼻胃管接受持续肠内营养。"}
{"queueIndex":419,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.228","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.228.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.228.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing a client's food diary. The client consumed a meal containing 10 grams of fat. How many calories from fat did the client consume? (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查患者的食物日记。该患者摄入了一餐含有 10 克脂肪的食物。该患者摄入了多少卡路里脂肪？（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many calories from fat did the client consume?","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者摄入了多少卡路里脂肪？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"calories","zh":"卡路里"},"acceptable":["90"],"numeric":{"value":90,"tolerance":0,"unit":"calories"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fat provides 9 calories per gram. 10 grams of fat × 9 cal/g = 90 calories.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脂肪每克提供 9 卡路里。10 克脂肪 × 9 卡/克 = 90 卡路里。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Fat is the most energy-dense nutrient, providing 9 cal/g compared to 4 cal/g for protein and carbs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"脂肪是能量密度最高的营养素，每克提供 9 卡路里，而蛋白质和碳水每克提供 4 卡路里。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":420,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.229","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.229.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.229.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,37],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer an intermittent bolus feeding to a client with a gastrostomy tube. What should the nurse do first?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名带有胃造口管的患者进行间歇性推注喂养。护士首先应该做什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse do first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应该做什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer an intermittent bolus feeding to a client with a gastrostomy tube.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名带有胃造口管的患者进行间歇性推注喂养。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Flush the tube with 100 mL of normal saline.","zh":"用 100 毫升生理盐水冲洗管路。"},{"id":"D","en":"Aspirate all gastric contents and discard them.","zh":"抽吸所有胃内容物并将其丢弃。"},{"id":"C","en":"Verify the tube placement and patency.","zh":"验证管路位置和通畅性。"},{"id":"A","en":"Warm the feeding formula in a microwave.","zh":"在微波炉中加热营养液。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety and verification of placement are the priority before any substance is introduced into an enteral tube.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在将任何物质引入肠内管路之前，验证位置和安全性是首要任务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the nursing process: Assessment/Verification always comes before Action/Administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用护理程序：评估/验证始终在行动/给药之前。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":421,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.230","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.230.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.230.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,27],"fullStemEn":"A client reports difficulty falling asleep. Which recommendation should the nurse make regarding caffeine consumption?","fullStemZh":"一名患者报告入睡困难。护士应就咖啡因摄入提出什么建议？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which recommendation should the nurse make regarding caffeine consumption?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应就咖啡因摄入提出什么建议？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client reports difficulty falling asleep.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者报告入睡困难。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Drink tea instead of coffee in the evening.","zh":"晚上喝茶代替咖啡。"},{"id":"A","en":"Limit caffeine to two cups of coffee with dinner.","zh":"将咖啡因限制在晚餐时喝两杯咖啡。"},{"id":"D","en":"Avoid caffeine after 12:00 PM (noon).","zh":"中午 12:00 以后避免摄入咖啡因。"},{"id":"C","en":"Caffeine has no effect on sleep if consumed with food.","zh":"咖啡因如果与食物一起摄入，对睡眠没有影响。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Caffeine is a stimulant that can stay in the system for several hours. Avoiding it in the afternoon and evening is recommended for better sleep hygiene.","rationaleCorrectZh":"咖啡因是一种刺激物，可以在系统中停留几个小时。建议下午和晚上避免摄入咖啡因，以改善睡眠卫生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the half-life of caffeine; it persists long enough that even early afternoon consumption affects some individuals.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑咖啡因的半衰期；它持续时间足够长，甚至下午早些时候的摄入也会影响某些人。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":422,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.231","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.231.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.231.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[43,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,57],"fullStemEn":"A client consumes 2,000 calories in a day. If 50% of these calories come from carbohydrates, how many grams of carbohydrates did the client consume?","fullStemZh":"一名患者一天摄入 2,000 卡路里。如果其中 50% 的卡路里来自碳水化合物，那么该患者摄入了多少克碳水化合物？","terminalSentenceEn":"If 50% of these calories come from carbohydrates, how many grams of carbohydrates did the client consume?","terminalSentenceZh":"如果其中 50% 的卡路里来自碳水化合物，那么该患者摄入了多少克碳水化合物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client consumes 2,000 calories in a day.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者一天摄入 2,000 卡路里。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"grams","zh":"克"},"acceptable":["250"],"numeric":{"value":250,"tolerance":0,"unit":"grams"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, calculate the calories from carbohydrates: 2,000 × 0.50 = 1,000 calories. Then, convert calories to grams (4 cal/g): 1,000 ÷ 4 = 250 grams.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，计算来自碳水化合物的卡路里：2,000 × 0.50 = 1,000 卡路里。然后，将卡路里转换为克（4 卡/克）：1,000 ÷ 4 = 250 克。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Perform the calculation in two steps: total calories to nutrient calories, then nutrient calories to grams.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分两步进行计算：总卡路里到营养素卡路里，然后是营养素卡路里到克。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":423,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.232","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.232.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.232.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,107],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,27],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is administering liquid medications through a client's feeding tube. Which action is appropriate?","fullStemZh":"护士正在通过患者的喂养管给液态药物。哪项操作是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项操作是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is administering liquid medications through a client's feeding tube.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在通过患者的喂养管给液态药物。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Mix all medications together in one syringe to save time.","zh":"将所有药物混合在一个注射器中以节省时间。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use a small 3 mL syringe to ensure high pressure during administration.","zh":"使用 3 毫升小注射器以确保给药期间的高压。"},{"id":"D","en":"Flush the tube with 15–30 mL of water before and after each medication.","zh":"每种药物前后用 15-30 毫升水冲洗管路。"},{"id":"B","en":"Add the medication directly to the enteral feeding container.","zh":"将药物直接加入肠内营养容器中。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Flushing before and after each medication prevents drug-drug interactions and prevents the tube from clogging.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在每种药物前后冲洗可防止药物间相互作用并防止管路堵塞。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Eliminate options that suggest mixing substances or using high pressure, which increase risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除建议混合物质或使用高压的选项，因为这些会增加风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":424,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.233","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.233.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.233.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,33],"fullStemEn":"A client who works night shifts asks the nurse for advice on sleeping during the day. Which intervention is most helpful?","fullStemZh":"一名上夜班的患者向护士寻求关于白天睡眠的建议。哪项干预措施最有效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention is most helpful?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项干预措施最有效？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who works night shifts asks the nurse for advice on sleeping during the day.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名上夜班的患者向护士寻求关于白天睡眠的建议。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Nap for 2–3 hours in the late afternoon before starting work.","zh":"在开始工作前的下午晚些时候睡 2-3 小时。"},{"id":"D","en":"Leave the curtains open to allow natural light into the room.","zh":"拉开窗帘，让自然光进入房间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Consume a large meal right before going to bed.","zh":"睡前吃一顿大餐。"},{"id":"C","en":"Use a white noise machine to mask external sounds.","zh":"使用白噪音机来遮蔽外部声音。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"External noises can be very disruptive during daytime sleep. White noise helps create a stable acoustic environment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"白天睡觉时外部噪音可能会非常有干扰。白噪音有助于创造一个稳定的声学环境。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify factors that create a 'sleep-friendly' environment: dark, quiet, and cool.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定创造“睡眠友好型”环境的因素：黑暗、安静和凉爽。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":425,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b5_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.234","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.234.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.234.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,53],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is checking the gastric residual volume (GRV) of a client receiving continuous enteral nutrition. The GRV is 300 mL. What is the priority nursing action?","fullStemZh":"护士正在检查一名接受持续肠内营养患者的胃残留量 (GRV)。GRV 为 300 毫升。首要护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the priority nursing action?","terminalSentenceZh":"首要护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The GRV is 300 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"GRV 为 300 毫升。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Return the aspirate and reassess the client's tolerance to the feeding.","zh":"返回抽吸物并重新评估患者对喂养的耐受性。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase the rate of feeding to ensure nutritional goals are met.","zh":"增加喂养速度以确保达到营养目标。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop the feeding immediately and notify the healthcare provider.","zh":"立即停止喂养并通知医疗保健提供者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Discard the residual volume to prevent further distention.","zh":"丢弃残留量以防止进一步膨胀。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Current guidelines suggest that a single GRV measurement of 200–500 mL should not automatically lead to stopping the feeding. The nurse should return the aspirate and assess for signs of intolerance (e.g., distention, nausea).","rationaleCorrectZh":"目前的指南建议，200-500 毫升的单次 GRV 测量不应自动导致停止喂养。护士应返回抽吸物并评估不耐受症状（如膨胀、恶心）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Be aware of updated guidelines; high GRV alone (without symptoms) is no longer the sole indicator for stopping feeds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解更新后的指南；单纯的高 GRV（无症状）不再是停止喂养的唯一指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":426,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_mc_chain_of_command_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.235","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.235.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.235.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,267],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,62],"fullStemEn":"A staff nurse identifies that a fellow nurse is consistently failing to document controlled substance administration according to hospital policy. After discussing the issue with the colleague without improvement, what is the most appropriate next step for the nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名病房护士发现同事一直未能按照医院规定记录管制药品的管理情况。在与该同事沟通后情况并未改善，护士接下来的最合适步骤是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"After discussing the issue with the colleague without improvement, what is the most appropriate next step for the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"在与该同事沟通后情况并未改善，护士接下来的最合适步骤是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A staff nurse identifies that a fellow nurse is consistently failing to document controlled substance administration according to hospital policy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名病房护士发现同事一直未能按照医院规定记录管制药品的管理情况。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Report the colleague to the State Board of Nursing.","zh":"向州护理委员会举报该同事。"},{"id":"D","en":"File a report with the local police department.","zh":"向当地警察局报案。"},{"id":"A","en":"Inform the nurse manager about the documentation discrepancies.","zh":"向护士长（护理经理）报告记录不一致的情况。"},{"id":"B","en":"Discuss the concerns with the Chief Nursing Officer.","zh":"与首席护理官讨论这些担忧。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should follow the chain of command. After an initial peer-to-peer discussion fails to resolve a policy violation or safety concern, the next step is to notify the immediate supervisor, which is the nurse manager.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应遵循指挥链。在最初的同行间讨论未能解决违规或安全问题后，下一步是通知直接上级，即护士长（护理经理）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the chain of command principle. Identify the immediate supervisor of the staff nurse.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用指挥链原则。确定该护士的直接上级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":427,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_mc_chain_of_command_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.236","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.236.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.236.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[225,265],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,76],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is concerned that a prescribed medication dose for a client is dangerously high. The nurse contacts the prescribing healthcare provider (HCP), who insists the dose is correct and instructs the nurse to administer it. Which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"一名护士担心为患者开出的药物剂量高得危险。护士联系了开具处方的医疗保健提供者 (HCP)，但对方坚持剂量正确并指示护士执行。护士接下来应该采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士接下来应该采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse contacts the prescribing healthcare provider (HCP), who insists the dose is correct and instructs the nurse to administer it.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士联系了开具处方的医疗保健提供者 (HCP)，但对方坚持剂量正确并指示护士执行。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Notify the nursing supervisor about the disagreement and safety concern.","zh":"向护理督导报告该争议和安全顾虑。"},{"id":"C","en":"Contact the facility's pharmacist to ask for a second opinion.","zh":"联系该机构的药剂师寻求第二意见。"},{"id":"A","en":"Document the HCP’s instructions and the nurse's concerns in the medical record.","zh":"在医疗记录中记录 HCP 的指示和护士的疑虑。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the medication as ordered to avoid delaying treatment.","zh":"按医嘱给药，以避免延误治疗。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"If a nurse questions a medical order and the prescribing HCP refuses to change it, the nurse must follow the chain of command to protect client safety. Notifying a supervisor ensures the issue is escalated appropriately.","rationaleCorrectZh":"如果护士对医嘱产生疑问且开具处方的 HCP 拒绝更改，护士必须遵循指挥链以保护患者安全。通知督导可确保问题得到适当的升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety is the priority. If a provider's order is questionable, do not administer and escalate to the next level of management.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一。如果提供者的医嘱可疑，请勿给药并向上一级管理层反映。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":428,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_mc_conflict_resolution_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.237","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.237.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.237.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,253],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,69],"fullStemEn":"Two nurses are in a conflict regarding who should be responsible for checking the emergency cart. The charge nurse intervenes and suggests that one nurse checks it today and the other checks it tomorrow. Which conflict management strategy is being used?","fullStemZh":"两名护士在谁应该负责检查急救车的问题上发生了冲突。负责护士（组长）介入并建议一名护士今天检查，另一名护士明天检查。使用了哪种冲突管理策略？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which conflict management strategy is being used?","terminalSentenceZh":"使用了哪种冲突管理策略？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse intervenes and suggests that one nurse checks it today and the other checks it tomorrow.","penultimateSentenceZh":"负责护士（组长）介入并建议一名护士今天检查，另一名护士明天检查。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Compromising","zh":"折中/妥协"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoiding","zh":"逃避"},{"id":"D","en":"Collaborating","zh":"协作"},{"id":"A","en":"Competing","zh":"竞争"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Compromising involves both parties giving up something of value or meeting in the middle to resolve the conflict. In this case, each nurse takes on the responsibility half of the time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"折中涉及双方都放弃一些有价值的东西或在中间达成一致以解决冲突。在这种情况下，每名护士承担一半时间的责任。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the outcome of the intervention. Since both parties modified their initial stance to reach a middle ground, it is compromising.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定干预的结果。由于双方都修改了最初的立场以达成中间地带，因此这是折中。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":429,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_mc_informed_consent_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.238","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.238.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.238.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[195,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,71],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for an invasive procedure. The nurse notes that the client has signed the consent form but appears anxious and states, \"I'm still not really sure why they need to do this.\" What is the priority action by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名患者被安排进行侵入性检查。护士注意到患者已签署知情同意书，但看起来很焦虑并说：“我还是不太确定他们为什么要这样做。”护士的首选行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the priority action by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首选行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes that the client has signed the consent form but appears anxious and states, \"I'm still not really sure why they need to do this.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到患者已签署知情同意书，但看起来很焦虑并说：“我还是不太确定他们为什么要这样做。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Witness the signature again to ensure its validity.","zh":"再次见证签名以确保其有效性。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the healthcare provider that the client requires further clarification.","zh":"通知医疗保健提供者患者需要进一步的澄清。"},{"id":"D","en":"Explain the risks and benefits of the procedure to the client.","zh":"向患者解释手术的风险和获益。"},{"id":"B","en":"Reassure the client that the procedure is necessary for diagnosis.","zh":"向患者保证该手术对诊断是必要的。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse's role in informed consent is to witness the signature and ensure the client is competent. If the client expresses a lack of understanding, the nurse must advocate for the client by notifying the HCP, who is responsible for explaining the procedure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在知情同意中的角色是见证签名并确保患者具有认知能力。如果患者表示不理解，护士必须通过通知 HCP（负责解释手术的人）来为患者辩护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Determine the nurse's legal role. The surgeon/provider is responsible for the 'informed' part; the nurse validates the signature and competency.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定护士的法律角色。外科医生/提供者负责“知情”部分；护士验证签名和认知能力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":430,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_mc_informed_consent_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.239","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.239.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.239.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[43,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,34],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for surgery. Which of the following clients can legally provide informed consent?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患者做术前准备。以下哪位患者可以在法律上提供知情同意？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following clients can legally provide informed consent?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪位患者可以在法律上提供知情同意？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患者做术前准备。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A 20-year-old client who does not speak English and has no interpreter present.","zh":"一名不会说英语且没有口译员在场的 20 岁患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A 17-year-old client who is married.","zh":"一名已婚的 17 岁患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A 70-year-old client with advanced dementia and a legal guardian.","zh":"一名患有晚期痴呆症且有法定监护人的 70 岁患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A 45-year-old client who just received a dose of morphine for pain.","zh":"一名刚刚接受了一剂吗啡止痛的 45 岁患者。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An emancipated minor, such as one who is married, is legally allowed to provide informed consent. Other emancipated categories include being a parent, active military duty, or living independently via court order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"获得解放的未成年人（如已婚者）在法律上被允许提供知情同意。其他获得解放的类别包括身为父母、服兵役或根据法院命令独立生活。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the client who is competent and has legal authority. Remember the exceptions for minors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找具有认知能力且拥有法律授权的患者。记住未成年人的例外情况。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":431,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_dc_chain_of_command_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.240","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.240.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.240.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,71],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"A staff nurse observes a colleague appearing intoxicated while on duty.","fullStemZh":"一名病房护士发现同事在值班时似乎处于醉酒状态。","terminalSentenceEn":"A staff nurse observes a colleague appearing intoxicated while on duty.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名病房护士发现同事在值班时似乎处于醉酒状态。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's priority is to ensure {{1}} and then follow the chain of command by {{2}}.","zh":"护士的首要任务是确保 {{1}}，然后通过 {{2}} 遵循指挥链。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"staff privacy","zh":"员工隐私"},{"id":"o1","en":"client safety","zh":"患者安全"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"discussing the behavior with the colleague after the shift","zh":"在交班后与同事讨论该行为"},{"id":"o1","en":"notifying the nursing supervisor immediately","zh":"立即通知护理督导"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Patient safety is always the primary concern. An impaired nurse poses a significant risk. The situation must be reported immediately to a supervisor who can intervene and remove the nurse from duty.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者安全始终是首要关注点。受损的护士会构成重大风险。必须立即向督导报告情况，督导可以介入并将该护士撤离岗位。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the immediate threat and the most direct path to safety through authority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"通过权威机构确定眼前的威胁和最直接的安全路径。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":432,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_dc_chain_of_command_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.241","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.241.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"An experienced nurse disagrees with a new policy implemented by the hospital administration.","fullStemZh":"一名资深护士不同意医院行政部门实施的一项新政策。","terminalSentenceEn":"An experienced nurse disagrees with a new policy implemented by the hospital administration.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名资深护士不同意医院行政部门实施的一项新政策。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To address this concern appropriately, the nurse should first {{1}} and if not satisfied, proceed to {{2}}.","zh":"为了妥善处理这一疑虑，护士应首先 {{1}}，如果不满意，则继续反映至 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"voice the disagreement on social media","zh":"在社交媒体上表达不同意见"},{"id":"o1","en":"discuss the concern with the unit manager","zh":"与单元经理（护士长）讨论疑虑"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the Chief Executive Officer","zh":"首席执行官（CEO）"},{"id":"o1","en":"the nursing director or appropriate committee","zh":"护理总监或适当的委员会"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Professional concerns should be addressed starting with the lowest level in the chain of command (unit manager). Escalation should proceed through each successive level (nursing director) before reaching executive levels.","rationaleCorrectZh":"专业疑虑应从指挥链的最低级别（单元经理）开始处理。升级应在达到行政级别之前经过每一个连续的级别（护理总监）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the hierarchical structure step-by-step.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逐步遵循等级结构。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":433,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_dc_conflict_resolution_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.242","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.242.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"A nurse feels that the workload is unfairly distributed compared to other staff members.","fullStemZh":"一名护士觉得与其他员工相比，工作量分配不公。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse feels that the workload is unfairly distributed compared to other staff members.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名护士觉得与其他员工相比，工作量分配不公。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should use {{1}} to address the conflict, which involves {{2}}.","zh":"护士应使用 {{1}} 来处理冲突，这涉及 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"passive-aggressive behavior","zh":"消极攻击性行为"},{"id":"o1","en":"assertive communication","zh":"断言式沟通"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"stating concerns directly and professionally","zh":"直接且专业地陈述疑虑"},{"id":"o2","en":"complaining to other coworkers during lunch","zh":"午餐时向其他同事抱怨"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assertive communication is a professional way to address conflicts by stating one's needs and concerns clearly and directly while respecting others. It is the preferred method for resolving interpersonal issues in nursing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"断言式沟通是一种专业的冲突处理方式，它在尊重他人的同时，清晰直接地陈述自己的需求和疑虑。它是护理中解决人际问题的首选方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the most professional and direct communication style.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择最专业、最直接的沟通方式。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":434,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_dc_conflict_resolution_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.243","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.243.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.243.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,36],"fullStemEn":"A multidisciplinary team is meeting to discuss a complex client case. There are differing opinions on the discharge plan.","fullStemZh":"一个多学科团队正在开会讨论一个复杂的患者案例。关于出院计划存在不同意见。","terminalSentenceEn":"There are differing opinions on the discharge plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"关于出院计划存在不同意见。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A multidisciplinary team is meeting to discuss a complex client case.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一个多学科团队正在开会讨论一个复杂的患者案例。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The team should aim for {{1}}, a strategy where all parties work together to find a solution that {{2}}.","zh":"团队应致力于 {{1}}，这是一种各方共同努力寻找 {{2}} 的解决方案的策略。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"accommodation","zh":"迁就"},{"id":"o1","en":"collaboration","zh":"协作"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"meets the needs of the client and all team members","zh":"满足患者和所有团队成员的需求"},{"id":"o2","en":"allows the most senior member to decide","zh":"允许最高级的成员做决定"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Collaboration is the 'win-win' approach where all parties work together for a common goal. In a multidisciplinary team, this ensures all professional perspectives are considered for the client's benefit.","rationaleCorrectZh":"协作是一种“双赢”方法，各方为了一个共同的目标而努力。在多学科团队中，这可以确保考虑到所有专业观点以造福患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the goal of team interaction. Collaboration is the most effective and professional method for complex problem solving.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定团队互动的目标。协作是解决复杂问题最有效、最专业的方法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":435,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b6_dc_informed_consent_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.244","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.244.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.244.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to obtain a client's signature on an informed consent form.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备让患者在知情同意书上签名。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to obtain a client's signature on an informed consent form.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正准备让患者在知情同意书上签名。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's primary role as a witness is to verify that the signature is {{1}} and that the client appears to be {{2}}.","zh":"护士作为见证人的主要职责是核实签名是 {{1}} 且患者看起来是 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"legally binding for the family","zh":"对家属具有法律约束力的"},{"id":"o1","en":"authentic","zh":"真实可信的"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"fully aware of all medical alternatives","zh":"完全知晓所有医疗替代方案"},{"id":"o1","en":"competent to make decisions","zh":"有能力做出决定"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When a nurse witnesses a consent form, they are verifying that the person signing is indeed the client, that the signature is authentic, and that the client is competent and not under duress. The HCP is responsible for ensuring the client is aware of alternatives.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当护士见证同意书时，他们是在核实签名的人确实是患者本人，签名是真实的，并且患者具有认知能力且未受到胁迫。HCP 负责确保患者知晓替代方案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between the nurse's role and the provider's role in the consent process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分护士在同意过程中的职责与提供者的职责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":436,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.245","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.245.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.245.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[246,289],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,74],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is performing a physical assessment on a client with suspected appendicitis. The nurse flexes the client's right hip and knee to 90 degrees and then internally rotates the hip. The client reports sharp pain in the right lower quadrant. How should the nurse document this finding?","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名疑似阑尾炎的患者进行体格检查。护士将患者的右髋和右膝弯曲至 90 度，然后内旋髋关节。患者报告右下腹剧烈疼痛。护士应如何记录这一发现？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse document this finding?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何记录这一发现？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports sharp pain in the right lower quadrant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者报告右下腹剧烈疼痛。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Positive Psoas sign","zh":"腰大肌征阳性"},{"id":"A","en":"Positive Obturator sign","zh":"闭孔肌征阳性"},{"id":"D","en":"Positive Rovsing's sign","zh":"罗夫辛氏征 (Rovsing's sign) 阳性"},{"id":"C","en":"Positive Blumberg's sign","zh":"布隆伯格征 (Blumberg's sign) 阳性"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Obturator sign is positive when internal rotation of the flexed right hip causes abdominal pain, indicating irritation of the obturator muscle by an inflamed appendix.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当弯曲的右髋内旋引起腹痛时，闭孔肌征为阳性，表明发炎的阑尾刺激了闭孔肌。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'Rotation' with 'Obturator'. Both start with or contain 'o' sounds in some mnemonic systems, or remember 'R' for rotation doesn't match Psoas (extension).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“旋转 (Rotation)”与“闭孔肌 (Obturator)”联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client reports sharp pain in the right lower quadrant.","controlSentenceZh":"患者报告右下腹剧烈疼痛。"}
{"queueIndex":437,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.246","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.246.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.246.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,400],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,149],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 70 kg is admitted with partial-thickness burns to 40% of the total body surface area (TBSA). The burns occurred at 0800, and the client arrived at the emergency department at 1000. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA), calculate the hourly IV infusion rate (in mL/hr) required to deliver the remaining half of the first 24-hour fluid volume within the first 8 hours of injury.","fullStemZh":"一名体重 70 kg 的患者因 40% 总体表面积 (TBSA) 的部分皮层烧伤入院。烧伤发生在 0800，患者于 1000 到达急诊科。使用 Parkland 公式 (4 mL/kg/%TBSA)，计算在伤后前 8 小时内输注前 24 小时液体总量剩余一半所需的每小时静脉输液速度（mL/hr）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA), calculate the hourly IV infusion rate (in mL/hr) required to deliver the remaining half of the first 24-hour fluid volume within the first 8 hours of injury.","terminalSentenceZh":"使用 Parkland 公式 (4 mL/kg/%TBSA)，计算在伤后前 8 小时内输注前 24 小时液体总量剩余一半所需的每小时静脉输液速度（mL/hr）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The burns occurred at 0800, and the client arrived at the emergency department at 1000.","penultimateSentenceZh":"烧伤发生在 0800，患者于 1000 到达急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/小时"},"acceptable":["933","933.3","933.33"],"numeric":{"value":933.3,"tolerance":1,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total 24h volume = 4 mL * 70 kg * 40 = 11,200 mL. Half of this (5,600 mL) must be given in the first 8 hours post-injury. Since 2 hours have already passed (0800 to 1000), the 5,600 mL must be infused over the remaining 6 hours. 5,600 / 6 = 933.33 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"24 小时总量 = 4 mL * 70 kg * 40 = 11,200 mL。其中一半 (5,600 mL) 必须在伤后前 8 小时内给予。由于已经过去了 2 小时 (0800 到 1000)，因此 5,600 mL 必须在剩余的 6 小时内输注。5,600 / 6 = 933.33 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always calculate the first 8-hour window starting from the time of injury, not the time of hospital arrival.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终从伤后时间开始计算前 8 小时窗口，而不是从入院时间开始。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":438,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.247","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.247.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.247.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[52,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring clients on a surgical unit. Match each postoperative complication with its most appropriate immediate nursing intervention.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测外科病房的患者。将每种术后并发症与其最合适的立即护理干预措施相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each postoperative complication with its most appropriate immediate nursing intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种术后并发症与其最合适的立即护理干预措施相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring clients on a surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测外科病房的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Evisceration of an abdominal wound","zh":"腹部伤口脏器脱出"},{"id":"r2","en":"Suspected pulmonary embolism","zh":"疑似肺栓塞"},{"id":"r3","en":"Signs of hypovolemic shock","zh":"失血性休克迹象"},{"id":"r4","en":"Acute paralytic ileus","zh":"急性麻痹性肠梗阻"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Place supine with legs elevated (passive leg raise)","zh":"取仰卧位并抬高双腿（被动抬腿）"},{"id":"c2","en":"Apply high-flow oxygen and notify Rapid Response","zh":"提供高流量氧气并通知快速反应小组"},{"id":"c1","en":"Cover with sterile saline-soaked dressings","zh":"用无菌生理盐水浸湿的敷料覆盖"},{"id":"c4","en":"Maintain NPO status and prepare for NG tube insertion","zh":"保持禁食状态并准备插入鼻胃管"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Evisceration requires sterile coverage to prevent infection and drying; PE requires immediate oxygenation and rapid intervention; hypovolemic shock requires supine positioning with legs elevated (passive leg raise) to improve venous return; ileus requires bowel rest and decompression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脏器脱出需要无菌覆盖以防止感染和干燥；肺栓塞需要立即给氧和快速干预；休克需要体位调整以增加静脉回流；肠梗阻需要肠道休息和减压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the 'emergency' priority for each specific surgical complication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别每种特定外科并发症的“紧急”优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":439,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.248","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.248.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.248.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,56],"fullStemEn":"The classic point of maximal tenderness in a client with appendicitis is located one-third of the distance from the anterior superior iliac spine to the umbilicus. This specific anatomical site is known as ________ point.","fullStemZh":"阑尾炎患者最典型的压痛点位于髂前上棘至脐部连线的外 1/3 处。这个特定的解剖部位被称为 ________ 点。","terminalSentenceEn":"This specific anatomical site is known as ________ point.","terminalSentenceZh":"这个特定的解剖部位被称为 ________ 点。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The classic point of maximal tenderness in a client with appendicitis is located one-third of the distance from the anterior superior iliac spine to the umbilicus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阑尾炎患者最典型的压痛点位于髂前上棘至脐部连线的外 1/3 处。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Point name","zh":"点名称"},"acceptable":["McBurney's","McBurney","麦氏"],"numeric":null}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"McBurney's point is the standard location for assessment of appendiceal inflammation tenderness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"麦氏点是评估阑尾炎症压痛的标准位置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Knowledge-based question; recall the eponym associated with appendicitis landmarks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"基础知识题；回想与阑尾炎标志相关的专有名词。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":440,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.249","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.249.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.249.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,67],"fullStemEn":"A client is in the emergent phase of care for a 50% TBSA burn. Which clinical finding should the nurse prioritize as a sign of inadequate fluid resuscitation despite following the Parkland formula?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因 50% TBSA 烧伤正处于急症期护理中。尽管遵循了 Parkland 公式，护士应优先将哪项临床发现视为补液不足的征兆？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which clinical finding should the nurse prioritize as a sign of inadequate fluid resuscitation despite following the Parkland formula?","terminalSentenceZh":"尽管遵循了 Parkland 公式，护士应优先将哪项临床发现视为补液不足的征兆？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is in the emergent phase of care for a 50% TBSA burn.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因 50% TBSA 烧伤正处于急症期护理中。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Urine output of 25 mL/hr","zh":"尿量为 25 mL/小时"},{"id":"B","en":"Hematocrit of 52%","zh":"血细胞比容为 52%"},{"id":"D","en":"Heart rate of 110 bpm","zh":"心率为 110 次/分"},{"id":"C","en":"Mean arterial pressure of 75 mmHg","zh":"平均动脉压为 75 mmHg"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Urine output is the most reliable indicator of organ perfusion during burn resuscitation. For an adult, it should be maintained at 0.5 mL/kg/hr or roughly 30-50 mL/hr. 25 mL/hr is below the expected minimum.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尿量是烧伤复苏期间器官灌注最可靠的指标。对于成人，应维持在 0.5 mL/kg/hr 或约 30-50 mL/hr。25 mL/hr 低于预期最小值。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When multiple signs of shock are present, look for the most sensitive 'gold standard' for fluid titration in burns: urine output.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当出现多种休克迹象时，寻找烧伤补液滴定的最敏感“金标准”：尿量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":441,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.250","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.250.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.250.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,59],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who underwent a total abdominal hysterectomy 24 hours ago. Which finding is the most sensitive early indicator of a developing postoperative complication such as pneumonia or pulmonary embolism?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名 24 小时前接受了全腹子宫切除术的患者。哪项发现是术后并发症（如肺炎或肺栓塞）发生的最敏感早期指标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding is the most sensitive early indicator of a developing postoperative complication such as pneumonia or pulmonary embolism?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项发现是术后并发症（如肺炎或肺栓塞）发生的最敏感早期指标？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who underwent a total abdominal hysterectomy 24 hours ago.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名 24 小时前接受了全腹子宫切除术的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Increased respiratory rate and restlessness","zh":"呼吸频率增加和烦躁不安"},{"id":"B","en":"Diminished breath sounds at the bases","zh":"基底部呼吸音减弱"},{"id":"A","en":"Productive cough with yellow sputum","zh":"咳出黄痰"},{"id":"D","en":"Temperature of 100.2 °F (37.9 °C)","zh":"体温为 100.2 °F (37.9 °C)"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tachypnea and mental status changes (restlessness/anxiety) are often the earliest signs of hypoxia and respiratory distress before more obvious symptoms like sputum or high fever appear.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在出现咳痰或高烧等更明显的症状之前，呼吸频率加快和意识状态改变（烦躁/焦虑）通常是缺氧和呼吸窘迫的最早迹象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize 'ABC' (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) and 'Early' signs. Restlessness is a classic NCLEX 'early sign' of hypoxia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先考虑“ABC”（气道、呼吸、循环）和“早期”迹象。烦躁不安是 NCLEX 中经典的缺氧“早期迹象”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":442,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.251","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.251.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.251.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse in the emergency department is evaluating four clients with abdominal pain. Determine if each clinical presentation is more likely to be Appendicitis or a Differential Diagnosis.","fullStemZh":"急诊科护士正在评估四名腹痛患者。确定每种临床表现更可能是阑尾炎还是鉴别诊断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Determine if each clinical presentation is more likely to be Appendicitis or a Differential Diagnosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定每种临床表现更可能是阑尾炎还是鉴别诊断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse in the emergency department is evaluating four clients with abdominal pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急诊科护士正在评估四名腹痛患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Right lower quadrant pain, low-grade fever, and rebound tenderness at McBurney's point.","zh":"右下腹痛、低热以及麦氏点反跳痛。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Sudden onset RLQ pain, missed menstrual period, and right-sided shoulder pain.","zh":"突然发作的右下腹痛、月经推迟以及右侧肩部疼痛。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Right upper quadrant pain radiating to the right scapula following a high-fat meal.","zh":"高脂饮食后右向右肩胛骨放射的右上腹痛。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Severe, episodic flank pain radiating to the labia, accompanied by hematuria.","zh":"严重的、发作性的侧腹痛，放射至阴唇，伴有血尿。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Differential Diagnosis","zh":"鉴别诊断"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appendicitis","zh":"阑尾炎"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"r1 is classic appendicitis. r2 suggests ectopic pregnancy (shoulder pain indicates referred pain from diaphragmatic irritation). r3 suggests cholecystitis. r4 suggests nephrolithiasis (kidney stones).","rationaleCorrectZh":"r1 是经典的阑尾炎。r2 提示异位妊娠（肩部疼痛表示膈肌受刺激引起的放射痛）。r3 提示胆囊炎。r4 提示肾结石。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the specific location and accompanying symptoms (e.g., shoulder pain with ectopic, fatty meal with cholecystitis) to differentiate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注特定的位置和伴随症状（例如，异位妊娠伴肩痛，胆囊炎伴高脂饮食）来进行区分。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":443,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.252","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.252.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.252.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,61],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client weighing 80 kg who is receiving fluid resuscitation for a 45% TBSA burn. Identify if each finding indicates Adequate or Inadequate fluid resuscitation.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名体重 80 kg、因 45% TBSA 烧伤正在接受补液复苏的患者。确定每项发现表示补液复苏充足还是不足。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify if each finding indicates Adequate or Inadequate fluid resuscitation.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定每项发现表示补液复苏充足还是不足。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client weighing 80 kg who is receiving fluid resuscitation for a 45% TBSA burn.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测一名体重 80 kg、因 45% TBSA 烧伤正在接受补液复苏的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Urine output of 45 mL/hr","zh":"尿量为 45 mL/小时"},{"id":"r2","en":"Mean Arterial Pressure (MAP) of 55 mmHg","zh":"平均动脉压 (MAP) 为 55 mmHg"},{"id":"r3","en":"Heart rate of 145 beats per minute","zh":"心率为 145 次/分"},{"id":"r4","en":"Clear sensorium and alert mental status","zh":"意识清晰且精神状态警觉"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inadequate","zh":"不足"},{"id":"c1","en":"Adequate","zh":"充足"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adequate resuscitation is indicated by urine output > 0.5 mL/kg/hr (~40 mL/hr for 80 kg), MAP > 65 mmHg, heart rate < 120 bpm, and clear sensorium. A HR of 145 and MAP of 55 indicate hypovolemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"复苏充足的指标包括尿量 > 0.5 mL/kg/hr（80 kg 约为 40 mL/hr）、MAP > 65 mmHg、心率 < 120 bpm 以及意识清晰。心率 145 和 MAP 55 表示血容量不足。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the specific target parameters for burn resuscitation (UO, HR, MAP, mentation).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住烧伤复苏的具体目标参数（尿量、心率、平均动脉压、精神状态）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":444,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.253","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.253.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.253.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[282,318],"terminalOffsetsZh":[94,106],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a postoperative client for potential bleeding. The client's initial hemoglobin was 14 g/dL. Four hours later, the client is pale, tachycardic, and the hemoglobin has dropped to 10 g/dL. Calculate the percentage (%) decrease in the client's hemoglobin level. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名术后患者是否存在潜在出血。患者的初始血红蛋白为 14 g/dL。四小时后，患者面色苍白，心动过速，血红蛋白降至 10 g/dL。计算患者血红蛋白水平下降的百分比 (%)。（四舍五入到最近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the percentage (%) decrease in the client's hemoglobin level.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算患者血红蛋白水平下降的百分比 (%)。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"% decrease","zh":"下降百分比"},"acceptable":["29"],"numeric":{"value":29,"tolerance":0.5,"unit":"%"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Percentage decrease = ((Original - New) / Original) * 100. ((14 - 10) / 14) * 100 = (4 / 14) * 100 = 28.57%. Rounded to the nearest whole number is 29%.","rationaleCorrectZh":"下降百分比 = ((原始值 - 新值) / 原始值) * 100。((14 - 10) / 14) * 100 = (4 / 14) * 100 = 28.57%。四舍五入到最近的整数为 29%。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Standard percentage change formula. Ensure you use the original value as the divisor.","testTakingStrategyZh":"标准百分比变化公式。确保使用原始值作为除数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":445,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b7_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.254","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.254.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.254.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[220,257],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,64],"fullStemEn":"A client with diagnosed appendicitis is awaiting surgery. The client suddenly reports that the abdominal pain has completely disappeared. On assessment, the nurse finds the abdomen is rigid and board-like with guarding. Which is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"一名确诊为阑尾炎的患者正在等待手术。患者突然报告腹痛完全消失。检查时，护士发现腹部僵硬，呈板状并有防御感。护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"On assessment, the nurse finds the abdomen is rigid and board-like with guarding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"检查时，护士发现腹部僵硬，呈板状并有防御感。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Cancel the scheduled surgery and continue to monitor.","zh":"取消预定的手术并继续监测。"},{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the client to ambulate to promote gas passage.","zh":"鼓励患者走动以促进排气。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the prescribed preoperative opioid analgesic.","zh":"按医嘱给予术前阿片类止痛药。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the healthcare provider immediately of suspected perforation.","zh":"立即通知医疗服务提供者疑似穿孔。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden relief of pain in appendicitis often indicates rupture (perforation). The subsequent rigid, board-like abdomen indicates peritonitis, a surgical emergency.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阑尾炎疼痛突然缓解通常表示破裂（穿孔）。随后出现的僵硬、板状腹部表明腹膜炎，这是一种外科急症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the 'silent killer' sign: sudden relief of pain in a known inflammatory condition. This almost always indicates rupture.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别“无声杀手”迹象：已知炎症情况下疼痛突然缓解。这几乎总是表示破裂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":446,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.255","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.255.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.255.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,45],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder, manic phase, is hyperactive and has lost weight. Which is the most appropriate snack for this client?","fullStemZh":"一名处于躁狂期的双相情感障碍患者表现为活动过度且体重下降。对于该患者，以下哪种零食最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which is the most appropriate snack for this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于该患者，以下哪种零食最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with bipolar disorder, manic phase, is hyperactive and has lost weight.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名处于躁狂期的双相情感障碍患者表现为活动过度且体重下降。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A plate of spaghetti and meatballs","zh":"一盘意大利面和肉丸"},{"id":"B","en":"A glass of low-fat milk","zh":"一杯低脂牛奶"},{"id":"C","en":"A cheese sandwich and an apple","zh":"一份奶酪三明治和一个苹果"},{"id":"A","en":"A bowl of hot vegetable soup","zh":"一碗热蔬菜汤"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients in the manic phase are often too hyperactive to sit down for a full meal. Providing high-calorie, high-protein finger foods (like a sandwich and an apple) allows them to eat while moving and maintain their nutritional status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"躁狂期患者通常由于过度活跃而无法坐下来吃完一顿完整的餐食。提供高热量、高蛋白的“手指食物”（如三明治和苹果）可以让他们边走边吃，从而维持营养状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the client's behavior (hyperactivity) and the priority need (nutrition). Select an option that allows the client to meet the need without requiring a change in behavior.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别患者的行为（活动过度）和优先需求（营养）。选择一个既能满足需求又不需要改变行为的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":447,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.256","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.256.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.256.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,74],"fullStemEn":"A client with borderline personality disorder is being discharged. During the final session, the client tells the nurse, 'You're just like my mother—you're abandoning me just when I need you most.' The nurse recognizes this as which of the following?","fullStemZh":"一名边缘型人格障碍患者即将出院。在最后一次治疗中，患者告诉护士：“你就像我母亲一样——就在我最需要你的时候抛弃了我。”护士意识到这属于以下哪种情况？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse recognizes this as which of the following?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士意识到这属于以下哪种情况？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During the final session, the client tells the nurse, 'You're just like my mother—you're abandoning me just when I need you most.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"在最后一次治疗中，患者告诉护士：“你就像我母亲一样——就在我最需要你的时候抛弃了我。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Countertransference","zh":"反移情"},{"id":"B","en":"Transference","zh":"移情"},{"id":"C","en":"Splitting","zh":"情感分割 (Splitting)"},{"id":"A","en":"Projection","zh":"投射"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Transference is the unconscious redirection of feelings from one person (often a significant figure like a parent) to another (in this case, the nurse). The client is projecting feelings about their mother onto the nurse.","rationaleCorrectZh":"移情是将对一个人的感情（通常是像父母这样的重要人物）无意识地转移到另一个人身上（在这种情况下是护士）。患者正在将对母亲的情感投射到护士身上。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for keywords that connect the caregiver to a significant figure from the client's past. 'Just like my mother' is a strong indicator of transference.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找将护理人员与患者过去的显著人物联系起来的关键短语。“就像我母亲一样”是移情的强烈暗示。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":448,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.257","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.257.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.257.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,81],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department with a suspected opioid overdose.","fullStemZh":"一名疑似阿片类药物过量的患者被送到急诊科。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department with a suspected opioid overdose.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名疑似阿片类药物过量的患者被送到急诊科。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first assess the client's {{1}} and then prepare to administer {{2}}.","zh":"护士应首先评估患者的 {{1}}，然后准备给予 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"oxygen saturation","zh":"血氧饱和度"},{"id":"o2","en":"blood pressure","zh":"血压"},{"id":"o1","en":"respiratory rate","zh":"呼吸频率"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"buprenorphine","zh":"丁丙诺啡"},{"id":"o1","en":"naloxone","zh":"纳洛酮"},{"id":"o2","en":"methadone","zh":"美沙酮"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Respiratory depression is the most life-threatening complication of opioid overdose; therefore, assessing the respiratory rate is the priority. Naloxone is an opioid antagonist used to reverse the effects of opioids quickly.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呼吸抑制是阿片类药物过量最危及生命的并发症；因此，评估呼吸频率是首要任务。纳洛酮是一种阿片类药物拮抗剂，用于快速逆转阿片类药物的作用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In emergency overdose situations, always prioritize the assessment of the airway and breathing (ABC). Choose the medication that serves as the specific antidote for the substance used.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在急诊过量情况下，始终优先评估气道和呼吸（ABC）。选择作为所用物质特定解毒剂的药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":449,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.258","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.258.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.258.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client with antisocial personality disorder. Which nursing intervention should be included in the plan of care?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名反社会型人格障碍患者制定护理计划。护理计划中应包含哪项护理干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing intervention should be included in the plan of care?","terminalSentenceZh":"护理计划中应包含哪项护理干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client with antisocial personality disorder.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名反社会型人格障碍患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Encourage the client to lead a group therapy session","zh":"鼓励患者领导小组治疗会议"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide a flexible schedule to reduce frustration","zh":"提供灵活的时间表以减少挫败感"},{"id":"D","en":"Offer rewards for following the unit rules","zh":"对遵守病房规定的行为给予奖励"},{"id":"A","en":"Set clear and consistent limits on manipulative behavior","zh":"对操纵行为设定明确且一致的限制"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients with antisocial personality disorder often exhibit manipulative behavior and disregard rules. Setting firm, clear, and consistent limits is essential to manage these behaviors and maintain a safe environment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反社会型人格障碍患者通常表现出操纵行为并无视规则。设定坚定、明确且一致的限制对于管理这些行为并维持安全环境至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the core behavioral characteristics of the disorder (manipulation, lack of remorse). Choose interventions that directly address these behaviors through structure and boundaries.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别该障碍的核心行为特征（操纵、缺乏悔意）。选择通过结构化和边界设定直接针对这些行为的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":450,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.259","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.259.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.259.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,45],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute mania is receiving lithium carbonate. The nurse notes the client has coarse hand tremors and is complaining of nausea and blurred vision.","fullStemZh":"一名急性躁狂患者正在接受碳酸锂治疗。护士注意到患者有粗大的手部震颤，并主诉恶心和视力模糊。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse notes the client has coarse hand tremors and is complaining of nausea and blurred vision.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士注意到患者有粗大的手部震颤，并主诉恶心和视力模糊。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with acute mania is receiving lithium carbonate.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名急性躁狂患者正在接受碳酸锂治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"These findings are indicative of {{1}}, and the nurse should {{2}}.","zh":"这些发现表明存在 {{1}}，护士应当 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"therapeutic lithium levels","zh":"治疗性锂水平"},{"id":"o3","en":"early signs of mania","zh":"躁狂的早期症状"},{"id":"o1","en":"lithium toxicity","zh":"锂中毒"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"withhold the next dose and notify the provider","zh":"停服下一剂并通知医生"},{"id":"o3","en":"administer the next dose as scheduled","zh":"按计划服用下一剂"},{"id":"o2","en":"encourage increased fluid intake","zh":"鼓励增加液体摄入量"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Coarse tremors, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, blurred vision, and ataxia are signs of lithium toxicity (typically levels >1.5 mEq/L). If toxicity is suspected, the medication should be withheld and the healthcare provider notified immediately.","rationaleCorrectZh":"粗大震颤、恶心、呕吐、腹泻、视力模糊和共济失调是锂中毒的迹象（通常血锂浓度 >1.5 mEq/L）。如果怀疑中毒，应停药并立即通知医疗人员。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between common side effects (fine tremors) and toxic effects (coarse tremors). In any medication toxicity scenario, the priority action is to stop the medication to prevent further harm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分常见的副作用（细微震颤）和中毒效应（粗大震颤）。在任何药物中毒情况下，优先行动是停药以防止进一步伤害。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":451,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.260","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.260.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.260.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,45],"fullStemEn":"A client who has been using heroin for several years is admitted for detoxification. Which of the following should the nurse expect to observe during opioid withdrawal?","fullStemZh":"一名使用了多年海洛因的患者入院进行戒毒治疗。护士在阿片类药物戒断期间预期会观察到以下哪项？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following should the nurse expect to observe during opioid withdrawal?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在阿片类药物戒断期间预期会观察到以下哪项？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who has been using heroin for several years is admitted for detoxification.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名使用了多年海洛因的患者入院进行戒毒治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Bradycardia and hypotension","zh":"心动过缓和低血压"},{"id":"A","en":"Increased appetite and euphoria","zh":"食欲增加和欣快感"},{"id":"D","en":"Constipation and sedation","zh":"便秘和镇静"},{"id":"C","en":"Dilated pupils and muscle aches","zh":"瞳孔散大和肌肉酸痛"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Opioid withdrawal symptoms include pupillary dilation (mydriasis), muscle aches, rhinorrhea, lacrimation, diarrhea, and insomnia. These are often the opposite of the drug's acute effects (constriction, constipation, sedation).","rationaleCorrectZh":"阿片类药物戒断症状包括瞳孔散大（散瞳）、肌肉酸痛、流涕、流泪、腹泻和失眠。这些通常与药物的急性效应（瞳孔缩小、便秘、镇静）相反。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that withdrawal symptoms are usually the 'rebound' physiological effects of the body adjusting to the absence of the substance. If the drug slows down the body, withdrawal will speed it up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住戒断症状通常是身体在适应物质缺失时的“反弹”生理反应。如果药物减缓了身体机能，那么戒断则会使其加速。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":452,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.261","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.261.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.261.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[264,293],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,74],"fullStemEn":"A client with narcissistic personality disorder is upset because the nurse is caring for another client who was admitted with a life-threatening condition. The client says, 'I've been waiting for my juice for 10 minutes! I'm much more important than that person.' How should the nurse respond?","fullStemZh":"一名自恋型人格障碍患者感到不悦，因为护士正在护理另一名病情危重的患者。该患者说：“我已经等了10分钟果汁了！我比那个人重要得多。”护士应该如何回应？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse respond?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该如何回应？","penultimateSentenceEn":"I'm much more important than that person.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"我比那个人重要得多。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"'It is frustrating to wait, but I am currently caring for someone with an emergency.'","zh":"“等待确实让人沮丧，但我目前正在处理一名急诊患者。”"},{"id":"B","en":"'That other client is in critical condition and needs my help more right now.'","zh":"“那名患者病情危重，现在更需要我的帮助。”"},{"id":"C","en":"'You are being very selfish; please wait your turn.'","zh":"“你太自私了；请按顺序等待。”"},{"id":"D","en":"'I'm sorry, I'll get your juice right away.'","zh":"“对不起，我马上给您拿果汁。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This response acknowledges the client's feelings ('It is frustrating') without reinforcing the client's grandiosity or being defensive. It states the reality of the situation clearly and maintains a professional boundary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这种回应承认了患者的情感（“让人沮丧”），但没有强化患者的自大感，也没有表现出防御性。它清晰地说明了现实情况，并维持了专业边界。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In personality disorders, choose responses that validate feelings while maintaining firm boundaries and stating reality without being judgmental.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在人格障碍中，选择那些既能承认情感，又能维持坚定边界并客观说明现实而不进行评判的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":453,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.262","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.262.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.262.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,69],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client in the manic phase of bipolar disorder.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名处于双相情感障碍躁狂期的患者。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a client in the manic phase of bipolar disorder.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名处于双相情感障碍躁狂期的患者。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is likely to demonstrate {{1}} and may experience {{2}}.","zh":"患者可能会表现出 {{1}}，并且可能经历 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"pressured speech","zh":"迫促语 (Pressured speech)"},{"id":"o2","en":"flat affect","zh":"情感淡漠"},{"id":"o3","en":"poverty of thought","zh":"思维贫乏"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"auditory hallucinations","zh":"言语性幻听"},{"id":"o1","en":"grandiose delusions","zh":"夸大妄想"},{"id":"o3","en":"suicidal ideation","zh":"自杀意念"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pressured speech and grandiose delusions are classic symptoms of mania. Flat affect and poverty of thought are more characteristic of schizophrenia or depression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"迫促语和夸大妄想是躁狂症的典型症状。情感淡漠和思维贫乏更常见于精神分裂症或抑郁症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the clinical manifestations with the specific phase of the disorder. Focus on the increased energy and elevated mood typical of mania.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将临床表现与该障碍的特定阶段相匹配。关注躁狂症典型的精力增加和心境高涨。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":454,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.263","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.263.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.263.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"After administering naloxone to a client with an opioid overdose, which is the most important action for the nurse to take?","fullStemZh":"在给阿片类药物过量的患者服用纳洛酮后，护士最重要的行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"After administering naloxone to a client with an opioid overdose, which is the most important action for the nurse to take?","terminalSentenceZh":"在给阿片类药物过量的患者服用纳洛酮后，护士最重要的行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Prepare to administer a second dose if the respiratory rate decreases again","zh":"如果呼吸频率再次下降，准备给予第二剂"},{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the client to go to sleep to recover","zh":"鼓励患者睡觉以恢复"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor the client for a sudden increase in blood pressure","zh":"监测患者血压是否突然升高"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer an oral dose of methadone to prevent withdrawal","zh":"给予口服美沙酮以防止戒断"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Naloxone has a shorter half-life than most opioids. As the naloxone wears off, the client may return to a state of respiratory depression if the opioid is still active in their system.","rationaleCorrectZh":"纳洛酮的半衰期比大多数阿片类药物短。当纳洛酮药效消失时，如果阿片类药物在体内仍有活性，患者可能会重新进入呼吸抑制状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the pharmacological properties (half-life) of the antidote versus the toxic substance. Always prioritize the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation).","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑解毒剂与有毒物质的药理特性（半衰期）。始终优先考虑 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":455,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b8_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.264","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.264.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.264.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Which behavior is most characteristic of a client with histrionic personality disorder?","fullStemZh":"哪种行为最符合虚构型（表演型）人格障碍患者的特征？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which behavior is most characteristic of a client with histrionic personality disorder?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种行为最符合虚构型（表演型）人格障碍患者的特征？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Displaying a pattern of detachment from social relationships","zh":"表现出一种脱离社会模式的特征"},{"id":"B","en":"Having an extreme need to be taken care of by others","zh":"极度需要被他人照顾"},{"id":"D","en":"Believing that one's thoughts can influence the outcome of events","zh":"相信自己的想法可以影响事件的结果"},{"id":"A","en":"Acting in a seductive or provocative manner to be the center of attention","zh":"以诱惑或挑衅的方式行事以成为关注的中心"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Histrionic personality disorder is characterized by a pervasive pattern of excessive emotionality and attention-seeking. Clients often use physical appearance and provocative behavior to draw attention to themselves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"表演型人格障碍的特征是持久的情绪过度和寻求关注。患者通常利用外表和挑衅行为来吸引他人的注意。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate personality disorders with their most unique 'cluster' traits. Histrionic = Dramatic and Attention-seeking.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将人格障碍与其最独特的“集群”特征联系起来。表演型 = 戏剧化和寻求关注。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":456,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.265","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.265.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.265.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,275],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,72],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is evaluating a client with acute decompensated heart failure who has been receiving IV furosemide and oxygen therapy for 24 hours. For each finding, click to specify if the finding indicates that the client's condition has improved, has not changed, or has worsened.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名接受静脉注射呋塞米和氧疗24小时的急性失代偿性心力衰竭患者。对于每项发现，请点击以指明该发现是说明患者病情改善、无变化还是恶化。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, click to specify if the finding indicates that the client's condition has improved, has not changed, or has worsened.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请点击以指明该发现是说明患者病情改善、无变化还是恶化。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is evaluating a client with acute decompensated heart failure who has been receiving IV furosemide and oxygen therapy for 24 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名接受静脉注射呋塞米和氧疗24小时的急性失代偿性心力衰竭患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Fine crackles heard only at lung bases (previously heard throughout lower lobes)","zh":"仅在肺底闻及细湿啰音（此前在整个下肺叶均可闻及）"},{"id":"r2","en":"Weight decreased by 1.5 kg (3.3 lbs) since admission","zh":"自入院以来体重减轻了1.5公斤（3.3磅）"},{"id":"r3","en":"Brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) level remains at 800 pg/mL","zh":"脑钠肽（BNP）水平仍维持在800 pg/mL"},{"id":"r4","en":"Client reports inability to lie flat due to shortness of breath","zh":"患者报告因呼吸短促而无法平卧"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Improved","zh":"改善"},{"id":"c2","en":"No Change","zh":"无变化"},{"id":"c3","en":"Worsened","zh":"恶化"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Improved lung sounds (crackles retreating to bases) and weight loss indicate effective diuresis. A static BNP level in the acute phase and persistent orthopnea (inability to lie flat) indicate that while there is some improvement, these specific markers haven't changed yet from the acute state.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肺部听诊改善（啰音退至肺底）和体重减轻表明利尿有效。急性期BNP水平保持不变以及持续的端坐呼吸（无法平卧）表明，虽然有所改善，但这些特定指标较急性状态尚未发生变化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on comparing the current findings with expected outcomes of heart failure treatment (diuresis and improved oxygenation).","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点将当前发现与心力衰竭治疗的预期结果（利尿和氧合改善）进行比较。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":457,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.266","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.266.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.266.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,56],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes mellitus is scheduled for a CT scan with IV contrast. The client takes metformin 500 mg twice daily. The nurse reviews the client's pre-procedure instructions.","fullStemZh":"一名患有2型糖尿病的患者预定进行增强CT扫描。该患者每日两次服用二甲双胍500毫克。护士正在审查患者的术前指令。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the client's pre-procedure instructions.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在审查患者的术前指令。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client takes metformin 500 mg twice daily.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者每日两次服用二甲双胍500毫克。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should instruct the client to {{1}} to reduce the risk of {{2}}.","zh":"护士应指示患者{{1}}，以降低{{2}}的风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"switch to insulin therapy for one week before the procedure","zh":"在检查前一周改用胰岛素治疗"},{"id":"o1","en":"discontinue metformin 24-48 hours before the procedure","zh":"在检查前24-48小时停止服用二甲双胍"},{"id":"o2","en":"increase the dose of metformin on the day of the procedure","zh":"在检查当天增加二甲双胍的剂量"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"contrast-induced lactic acidosis","zh":"造影剂诱发的乳酸性酸中毒"},{"id":"o3","en":"acute hyperglycemia","zh":"急性高血糖"},{"id":"o2","en":"severe hypoglycemia","zh":"严重低血糖"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Metformin must be withheld before and for 48 hours after procedures involving iodine-based contrast media to prevent the development of lactic acidosis in case of contrast-induced renal failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在涉及碘造影剂的检查前及检查后48小时内必须停用二甲双胍，以防止在发生造影剂诱发的肾衰竭时出现乳酸性酸中毒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the specific interaction between metformin and IV contrast media regarding renal function and acid-base balance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住二甲双胍与静脉造影剂在肾功能和酸碱平衡方面的特定相互作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":458,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.267","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.267.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.267.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,66],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client who is 4 hours post-total hip arthroplasty. For each intervention, click to specify if the intervention is indicated, non-essential, or contraindicated for this client.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名全髋关节置换术后4小时的患者制定护理计划。对于每项干预措施，请点击以指明该干预措施对该患者是适应症、非必需还是禁忌症。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each intervention, click to specify if the intervention is indicated, non-essential, or contraindicated for this client.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项干预措施，请点击以指明该干预措施对该患者是适应症、非必需还是禁忌症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client who is 4 hours post-total hip arthroplasty.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名全髋关节置换术后4小时的患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Maintain the affected extremity in an abducted position","zh":"保持患肢处于外展位"},{"id":"r2","en":"Apply sequential compression devices (SCDs) to both legs","zh":"双腿均使用间歇充气加压装置（SCD）"},{"id":"r3","en":"Flex the hip more than 90 degrees when sitting","zh":"坐位时髋关节弯曲超过90度"},{"id":"r4","en":"Monitor neurovascular status of the affected limb every 4 hours","zh":"每4小时监测一次患肢的神经血管状态"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Indicated","zh":"适应症"},{"id":"c2","en":"Non-essential","zh":"非必需"},{"id":"c3","en":"Contraindicated","zh":"禁忌症"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Post-hip arthroplasty care requires abduction to prevent dislocation. SCDs are used for VTE prophylaxis. Hip flexion >90 degrees is contraindicated as it increases dislocation risk. Frequent neurovascular checks are essential to monitor for complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"髋关节置换术后的护理需要保持外展以防止脱位。SCD用于预防静脉血栓栓塞。髋关节弯曲超过90度是禁忌的，因为这会增加脱位风险。频繁的神经血管检查对于监测并发症至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on joint protection (avoiding dislocation) and preventing post-operative complications like DVT.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注关节保护（避免脱位）和预防深静脉血栓等术后并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":459,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.268","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.268.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.268.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,237],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,80],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a pregnant client with preeclampsia who is receiving magnesium sulfate via IV infusion. The nurse notes the following: BP 150/94 mmHg, respiratory rate 10 breaths/min, and deep tendon reflexes (DTR) are absent (+0).","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名患有先兆子痫且正在接受硫酸镁静脉输注的孕妇。护士注意到以下情况：血压150/94 mmHg，呼吸频率10次/分钟，深反射（DTR）消失（+0）。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse notes the following: BP 150/94 mmHg, respiratory rate 10 breaths/min, and deep tendon reflexes (DTR) are absent (+0).","terminalSentenceZh":"护士注意到以下情况：血压150/94 mmHg，呼吸频率10次/分钟，深反射（DTR）消失（+0）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a pregnant client with preeclampsia who is receiving magnesium sulfate via IV infusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名患有先兆子痫且正在接受硫酸镁静脉输注的孕妇。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client's assessment findings indicate {{1}}, and the nurse should prioritize the administration of {{2}}.","zh":"患者的评估结果表明存在{{1}}，护士应优先给予{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"magnesium sulfate toxicity","zh":"硫酸镁中毒"},{"id":"o2","en":"therapeutic magnesium levels","zh":"硫酸镁达到治疗水平"},{"id":"o3","en":"worsening preeclampsia","zh":"先兆子痫恶化"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"calcium gluconate","zh":"葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"o2","en":"hydralazine","zh":"肼屈嗪"},{"id":"o3","en":"another bolus of magnesium sulfate","zh":"再次给予硫酸镁负荷量"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Signs of magnesium toxicity include respiratory depression (<12/min) and absent deep tendon reflexes. Calcium gluconate is the specific antidote for magnesium toxicity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"硫酸镁中毒的迹象包括呼吸抑制（<12次/分钟）和深反射消失。葡萄糖酸钙是硫酸镁中毒的特效解毒剂。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the classic signs of magnesium toxicity and know the corresponding reversal agent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别硫酸镁中毒的典型迹象并了解相应的逆转药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":460,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.269","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.269.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.269.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,57],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is evaluating the effectiveness of pressure injury prevention for an immobile client. For each finding, click to specify if it indicates an effective or ineffective outcome of the prevention plan.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估针对一名卧床患者预防压力性损伤的有效性。对于每项发现，请点击以指明其说明预防计划是有效还是无效的结果。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, click to specify if it indicates an effective or ineffective outcome of the prevention plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请点击以指明其说明预防计划是有效还是无效的结果。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is evaluating the effectiveness of pressure injury prevention for an immobile client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估针对一名卧床患者预防压力性损伤的有效性。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Non-blanchable erythema on the sacrum","zh":"骶尾部出现指压不褪色的红斑"},{"id":"r2","en":"Intact skin with no redness over bony prominences","zh":"骨突出处皮肤完整，无发红"},{"id":"r3","en":"Braden Scale score increased from 12 to 16","zh":"Braden量表评分从12分增加到16分"},{"id":"r4","en":"Client turned every 2 hours as scheduled","zh":"按计划每2小时为患者翻身一次"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Ineffective Outcome","zh":"无效结果"},{"id":"c1","en":"Effective Outcome","zh":"有效结果"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Non-blanchable erythema (Stage 1 pressure injury) indicates failure. Intact skin, increasing Braden scores (lower risk), and adherence to turning schedules indicate success.","rationaleCorrectZh":"指压不褪色的红斑（1期压力性损伤）表示失败。皮肤完整、Braden评分增加（风险降低）以及遵守翻身计划表示成功。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between assessment data (Braden score) and physical findings (erythema) to determine outcome effectiveness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分评估数据（Braden评分）和体格检查发现（红斑）以确定结果的有效性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":461,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.270","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.270.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.270.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,198],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,57],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client with a confirmed Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) wound infection. The nurse is planning the required infection control measures.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备进入一名确诊患有耐甲氧西林金黄色葡萄球菌（MRSA）伤口感染患者的房间。护士正在计划所需的感染控制措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is planning the required infection control measures.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在计划所需的感染控制措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client with a confirmed Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) wound infection.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备进入一名确诊患有耐甲氧西林金黄色葡萄球菌（MRSA）伤口感染患者的房间。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should implement {{1}} precautions and must wear {{2}} before providing direct care.","zh":"护士应实施{{1}}预防措施，并且在提供直接护理前必须佩戴{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"contact","zh":"接触"},{"id":"o2","en":"droplet","zh":"飞沫"},{"id":"o3","en":"airborne","zh":"空气"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"an N95 respirator","zh":"N95呼吸器"},{"id":"o1","en":"gown and gloves","zh":"隔离衣和手套"},{"id":"o3","en":"a surgical mask and goggles","zh":"外科口罩和护目镜"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MRSA wound infections require contact precautions. Required PPE for contact precautions includes gown and gloves when entering the room and having contact with the client or environment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MRSA伤口感染需要采取接触预防措施。接触预防措施所需的个人防护装备（PPE）包括进入房间并与患者或环境接触时的隔离衣和手套。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the mode of transmission for common multidrug-resistant organisms (MDROs).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别常见多重耐药菌（MDROs）的传播途径。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":462,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.271","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.271.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.271.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,72],"fullStemEn":"A client with schizophrenia is experiencing auditory hallucinations. The nurse is developing a plan of care to help the client manage these symptoms. For each nursing action, click to specify if the action is appropriate or inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"一名患有精神分裂症的患者正在经历幻听。护士正在制定一项护理计划以帮助患者管理这些症状。对于每项护理行动，请点击以指明该行动是恰当的还是不恰当的。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing action, click to specify if the action is appropriate or inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项护理行动，请点击以指明该行动是恰当的还是不恰当的。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is developing a plan of care to help the client manage these symptoms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在制定一项护理计划以帮助患者管理这些症状。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Ask the client, 'What are the voices telling you?'","zh":"询问患者：“声音在告诉你什么？”"},{"id":"r2","en":"Tell the client, 'I don't hear the voices, but I believe they are real to you.'","zh":"告诉患者：“我听不到那些声音，但我相信对你来说它们是真实的。”"},{"id":"r3","en":"Argue with the client that the voices are not real","zh":"与患者争论那些声音不是真实的"},{"id":"r4","en":"Provide a radio with headphones to help drown out the voices","zh":"提供带有耳机的收音机以帮助淹没这些声音"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"恰当"},{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不恰当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Asking about content is vital for safety (command hallucinations). Validating the client's experience while stating your own reality is therapeutic. Arguing is non-therapeutic. Distraction (music/radio) is a common coping strategy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"询问幻听内容对于安全至关重要（命令性幻听）。在陈述自己现实情况的同时确认患者的经历具有治疗意义。争论是非治疗性的。分散注意力（音乐/收音机）是常用的应对策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on safety (assessing command hallucinations) and therapeutic communication principles (don't argue, present reality).","testTakingStrategyZh":"侧重于安全（评估命令性幻听）和治疗性沟通原则（不要争论，呈现现实）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":463,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.272","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.272.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.272.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,46],"fullStemEn":"A client with Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is being discharged. The nurse provides education on breathing techniques and oxygen safety.","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）的患者即将出院。护士提供了关于呼吸技巧和氧气安全的教育。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse provides education on breathing techniques and oxygen safety.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士提供了关于呼吸技巧和氧气安全的教育。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is being discharged.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）的患者即将出院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse determines that the client understands the instructions when the client states they will use {{1}} to improve exhalation and avoid {{2}} while using home oxygen.","zh":"当患者表示他们将使用{{1}}来改善呼气，并在使用家庭氧疗时避免{{2}}，护士确定患者理解了指示。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"rapid, shallow breaths","zh":"快速、浅呼吸"},{"id":"o2","en":"incentive spirometry","zh":"励力型肺量计"},{"id":"o1","en":"pursed-lip breathing","zh":"缩唇呼吸"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"adjusting the flow rate as prescribed","zh":"按规定调整流速"},{"id":"o1","en":"smoking and open flames","zh":"吸烟和明火"},{"id":"o2","en":"using water-based lubricants","zh":"使用水基润滑剂"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pursed-lip breathing helps prevent airway collapse during exhalation in COPD. Oxygen is highly combustible; avoiding smoking and open flames is critical for safety.","rationaleCorrectZh":"缩唇呼吸有助于防止COPD患者呼气期间的气道塌陷。氧气具有高度助燃性；避免吸烟和明火对于安全至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall specific respiratory interventions for COPD and standard fire safety protocols for oxygen therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想针对COPD的特定呼吸干预措施以及氧疗的标准消防安全协议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":464,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.273","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.273.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.273.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,261],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,73],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is monitoring a client who underwent percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) via the femoral artery 2 hours ago. For each assessment finding, click to specify if the finding is an expected outcome or a complication that requires immediate intervention.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名2小时前经股动脉接受经皮冠状动脉介入治疗（PCI）的患者。对于每项评估结果，请点击以指明该发现是预期结果还是需要立即干预的并发症。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, click to specify if the finding is an expected outcome or a complication that requires immediate intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项评估结果，请点击以指明该发现是预期结果还是需要立即干预的并发症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is monitoring a client who underwent percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) via the femoral artery 2 hours ago.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测一名2小时前经股动脉接受经皮冠状动脉介入治疗（PCI）的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"A 2 cm area of ecchymosis at the insertion site","zh":"穿刺部位出现2厘米范围的瘀斑"},{"id":"r2","en":"A firm, painful mass developing at the insertion site","zh":"穿刺部位出现坚硬、疼痛的肿块"},{"id":"r3","en":"Diminished pedal pulse in the affected extremity","zh":"患肢足背动脉搏动减弱"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client reports a small amount of back pain","zh":"患者报告有轻微背痛"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Complication","zh":"并发症"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected Outcome","zh":"预期结果"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Minor ecchymosis is expected. A firm mass (hematoma) or diminished pulses indicate bleeding or arterial occlusion. Back pain can be a sign of retroperitoneal bleeding after femoral access.","rationaleCorrectZh":"轻微瘀斑是预期的。坚硬的肿块（血肿）或脉搏减弱表明出血或动脉闭塞。背痛可能是股动脉入路后腹膜后出血的征象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the common risks of invasive vascular procedures, particularly bleeding and distal perfusion issues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑侵入性血管检查的常见风险，特别是出血和远端灌注问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":465,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_b9_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.274","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.274.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.274.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,48],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute kidney injury has a serum potassium level of 6.8 mEq/L. The ECG shows peaked T waves. The nurse is preparing to implement prescriptions.","fullStemZh":"一名患有急性肾损伤的患者血清钾水平为6.8 mEq/L。心电图显示T波高尖。护士正准备执行医嘱。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to implement prescriptions.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正准备执行医嘱。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The ECG shows peaked T waves.","penultimateSentenceZh":"心电图显示T波高尖。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first administer {{1}} to protect the myocardium and then prepare for {{2}} to remove potassium from the body.","zh":"护士应首先给予{{1}}以保护心肌，然后准备{{2}}以将钾从体内排出。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"calcium gluconate","zh":"葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"o3","en":"regular insulin with dextrose","zh":"普通胰岛素联合葡萄糖"},{"id":"o2","en":"sodium polystyrene sulfonate","zh":"聚苯乙烯磺酸钠"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"intravenous fluids","zh":"静脉补液"},{"id":"o3","en":"potassium-sparing diuretics","zh":"保钾利尿剂"},{"id":"o1","en":"hemodialysis","zh":"血液透析"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calcium gluconate stabilizes the cardiac membrane in severe hyperkalemia but doesn't lower potassium. Hemodialysis is the most effective and definitive way to remove potassium in acute kidney injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在严重高钾血症中，葡萄糖酸钙可稳定心肌细胞膜，但不能降低钾水平。血液透析是急性肾损伤患者排钾最有效且最明确的方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize interventions based on immediate life-saving actions (protecting the heart) followed by addressing the underlying cause.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据立即救命行动（保护心脏）优先进行干预，然后处理根本原因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":466,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.275","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.275.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.275.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,229],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,72],"fullStemEn":"A client with Stage 4 Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) has a serum potassium level of 6.8 mEq/L and ECG changes including peaked T-waves. Which medication should the nurse expect to administer first to stabilize the cardiac membrane?","fullStemZh":"一名 4 期慢性肾病 (CKD) 患者的血清钾水平为 6.8 mEq/L，且心电图显示 T 波高尖。护士应首先预期给予哪种药物以稳定心肌细胞膜？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse expect to administer first to stabilize the cardiac membrane?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先预期给予哪种药物以稳定心肌细胞膜？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Stage 4 Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) has a serum potassium level of 6.8 mEq/L and ECG changes including peaked T-waves.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 4 期慢性肾病 (CKD) 患者的血清钾水平为 6.8 mEq/L，且心电图显示 T 波高尖。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Sodium polystyrene sulfonate","zh":"聚苯乙烯磺酸钠"},{"id":"A","en":"Sodium bicarbonate","zh":"碳酸氢钠"},{"id":"D","en":"Calcium gluconate","zh":"葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"C","en":"Regular insulin and 50% dextrose","zh":"普通胰岛素和 50% 葡萄糖"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calcium gluconate is administered in severe hyperkalemia to stabilize the myocardial cell membrane and prevent life-threatening dysrhythmias. It does not lower the potassium level but protects the heart while other treatments work to shift or remove potassium.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在严重高钾血症中给予葡萄糖酸钙以稳定心肌细胞膜并预防危及生命的心律失常。它不会降低钾水平，但在其他治疗方法转移或清除钾时保护心脏。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the keyword 'first' and 'stabilize the cardiac membrane.' Calcium equals cardiac stability in hyperkalemia scenarios.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注关键词“首先”和“稳定心肌细胞膜”。在高钾血症场景中，钙代表心脏稳定性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":467,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.276","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.276.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.276.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,57],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge teaching to a client with end-stage renal disease (ESRD). Which dietary choices indicate that the client understands the necessary restrictions? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名终末期肾病 (ESRD) 患者进行出院指导。以下哪些饮食选择表明患者理解了必要的饮食限制？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which dietary choices indicate that the client understands the necessary restrictions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些饮食选择表明患者理解了必要的饮食限制？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Canned vegetable soup","zh":"蔬菜罐头汤"},{"id":"C","en":"Baked potato with skin","zh":"带皮烤土豆"},{"id":"E","en":"Apple slices","zh":"苹果片"},{"id":"B","en":"Grilled chicken breast","zh":"烤鸡胸肉"},{"id":"A","en":"Steamed white rice","zh":"清蒸白米饭"},{"id":"D","en":"Fresh spinach salad","zh":"新鲜菠菜沙拉"}],"correct":["A","B","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients with ESRD must restrict potassium, sodium, and phosphorus. White rice, high-quality proteins like chicken (in limited amounts), and low-potassium fruits like apples are appropriate choices.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ESRD 患者必须限制钾、钠和磷的摄入。白米饭、鸡肉等优质蛋白质（限量）以及苹果等低钾水果是合适的选择。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the process of elimination by identifying high-potassium (potatoes, spinach) and high-sodium (canned goods) items.","testTakingStrategyZh":"通过识别高钾（土豆、菠菜）和高钠（罐头食品）项目，使用排除法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":468,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.277","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.277.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.277.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"Match the following glomerular filtration rate (GFR) values to the corresponding stage of Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD).","fullStemZh":"将以下肾小球滤过率 (GFR) 值与相应的慢性肾病 (CKD) 分期相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match the following glomerular filtration rate (GFR) values to the corresponding stage of Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD).","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下肾小球滤过率 (GFR) 值与相应的慢性肾病 (CKD) 分期相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"GFR 40 mL/min/1.73m²","zh":"GFR 40 毫升/分钟/1.73平方米"},{"id":"r2","en":"GFR 12 mL/min/1.73m²","zh":"GFR 12 毫升/分钟/1.73平方米"},{"id":"r3","en":"GFR 25 mL/min/1.73m²","zh":"GFR 25 毫升/分钟/1.73平方米"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Stage 4","zh":"4 期"},{"id":"c3","en":"Stage 5","zh":"5 期"},{"id":"c1","en":"Stage 3b","zh":"3b 期"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CKD stages are defined by GFR: Stage 3b (30-44), Stage 4 (15-29), and Stage 5 (<15).","rationaleCorrectZh":"CKD 分期由 GFR 定义：3b 期 (30-44)，4 期 (15-29)，5 期 (<15)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the GFR cut-offs for CKD staging, specifically focusing on the threshold for ESRD (Stage 5).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 CKD 分期的 GFR 界限，特别关注终末期肾病（5 期）的阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":469,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.278.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,193],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,75],"fullStemEn":"A client with Addison's disease is admitted to the emergency department with hypotension, tachycardia, and hyponatremia after a severe viral illness. Which intervention is the nurse's priority?","fullStemZh":"一名患有艾迪生病 (Addison's disease) 的患者在严重病毒感染后，因低血压、心动过速和低钠血症被送入急诊科。护士的首要干预措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention is the nurse's priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要干预措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Addison's disease is admitted to the emergency department with hypotension, tachycardia, and hyponatremia after a severe viral illness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有艾迪生病 (Addison's disease) 的患者在严重病毒感染后，因低血压、心动过速和低钠血症被送入急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Initiate a 24-hour urine collection for cortisol","zh":"开始 24 小时尿皮质醇收集"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer oral fludrocortisone","zh":"口服氟氢可的松"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide a high-potassium snack","zh":"提供高钾零食"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer intravenous hydrocortisone bolus","zh":"静脉注射氢化可的松"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This client is experiencing an Addisonian crisis, which is a life-threatening emergency. Immediate IV replacement of cortisol (hydrocortisone) and fluids is necessary to restore vascular tone and electrolyte balance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者正在经历艾迪生危象，这是一种危及生命的紧急情况。需要立即静脉补充皮质醇（氢化可的松）和液体，以恢复血管张力和电解质平衡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the signs of 'crisis' (hypotension, tachycardia) and choose the most rapid-acting intervention (IV route).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别“危象”的迹象（低血压、心动过速）并选择起效最快的干预措施（静脉途径）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with Addison's disease is admitted to the emergency department with hypotension, tachycardia, and hyponatremia after a severe viral illness.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患有艾迪生病 (Addison's disease) 的患者在严重病毒感染后，因低血压、心动过速和低钠血症被送入急诊科。"}
{"queueIndex":470,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.279","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.279.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.279.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,60],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with suspected Cushing's syndrome. Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名疑似库欣综合征 (Cushing's syndrome) 的患者。护士应预期发现哪些临床表现？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预期发现哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hirsutism","zh":"多毛症"},{"id":"E","en":"Hypotension","zh":"低血压"},{"id":"D","en":"Purple striae on the abdomen","zh":"腹部紫色条纹"},{"id":"B","en":"Hyperpigmentation of the skin","zh":"皮肤色素沉着"},{"id":"F","en":"Supraclavicular fat pads ('buffalo hump')","zh":"锁骨上脂肪垫（“水牛背”）"},{"id":"A","en":"Truncal obesity","zh":"躯干肥胖"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cushing's syndrome is caused by an excess of corticosteroids. Typical findings include weight gain in the trunk, hirsutism (due to excess androgens), purple striae (due to skin thinning), and fat redistribution to the upper back.","rationaleCorrectZh":"库欣综合征是由皮质类固醇过多引起的。典型表现包括躯干肥胖、多毛症（由于雄激素过多）、紫色条纹（由于皮肤变薄）以及脂肪重新分布到上背部。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast the signs of 'excess' (Cushing's) with the signs of 'deficiency' (Addison's).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“过量”的迹象（库欣综合征）与“缺乏”的迹象（艾迪生病）进行对比。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应预期发现哪些临床表现？（"}
{"queueIndex":471,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.280.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"Classify the following laboratory findings as typically associated with Cushing's syndrome or Addison's disease.","fullStemZh":"将以下实验室检查结果分类为通常与库欣综合征或艾迪生病相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify the following laboratory findings as typically associated with Cushing's syndrome or Addison's disease.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下实验室检查结果分类为通常与库欣综合征或艾迪生病相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Hyperglycemia and Hypernatremia","zh":"高血糖和高钠血症"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hypoglycemia and Hyponatremia","zh":"低血糖和低钠血症"},{"id":"r3","en":"Hyperkalemia","zh":"高钾血症"},{"id":"r4","en":"Hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Addison's Disease","zh":"艾迪生病"},{"id":"c1","en":"Cushing's Syndrome","zh":"库欣综合征"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cushing's (excess cortisol/aldosterone) leads to high glucose, high sodium, and low potassium. Addison's (deficient cortisol/aldosterone) leads to low glucose, low sodium, and high potassium.","rationaleCorrectZh":"库欣综合征（皮质醇/醛固酮过多）导致高血糖、高钠和低钾。艾迪生病（皮质醇/醛固酮缺乏）导致低血糖、低钠和高钾。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of the function of aldosterone: it retains sodium and water and excretes potassium. Cushing's has too much, Addison's has too little.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考醛固酮的功能：它保留钠和水，排泄钾。库欣综合征患者醛固酮过多，艾迪生病患者则过少。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":472,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.281","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.281.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.281.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,61],"fullStemEn":"A client with a traumatic brain injury (TBI) exhibits rigid extension of the arms and legs, pronation of the arms, and plantar flexion when stimulated. How should the nurse document this finding?","fullStemZh":"一名患有创伤性脑损伤 (TBI) 的患者在受到刺激时表现出双臂和双腿僵直伸展、前臂旋前和足底屈曲。护士应如何记录这一发现？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse document this finding?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何记录这一发现？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a traumatic brain injury (TBI) exhibits rigid extension of the arms and legs, pronation of the arms, and plantar flexion when stimulated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有创伤性脑损伤 (TBI) 的患者在受到刺激时表现出双臂和双腿僵直伸展、前臂旋前和足底屈曲。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Flaccid paralysis","zh":"弛缓性瘫痪"},{"id":"C","en":"Tonic-clonic seizure activity","zh":"强直-阵挛性癫痫发作"},{"id":"A","en":"Decorticate posturing","zh":"去皮质强直"},{"id":"B","en":"Decerebrate posturing","zh":"去大脑强直"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Decerebrate posturing (extensor posturing) is characterized by rigid extension of the limbs and indicates severe damage to the brainstem. It is a more ominous sign than decorticate posturing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"去大脑强直（伸肌强直）的特征是肢体僵直伸展，表明脑干严重受损。这是一个比去皮质强直更不祥的征兆。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: 'e' in decerebrate stands for 'extension'. Extension is usually worse than flexion (decorticate).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：decerebrate（去大脑强直）中的“e”代表 extension（伸展）。伸展通常比屈曲（decorticate）更严重。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":473,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.282.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,58],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing a client's neurological status using the Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS). Which motor responses would be assigned a score of 3 or less? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在使用格拉斯哥昏迷评分 (GCS) 评估患者的神经系统状态。以下哪些运动反应会被评为 3 分或更低？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which motor responses would be assigned a score of 3 or less?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些运动反应会被评为 3 分或更低？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Extension to pain (decerebrate)","zh":"痛觉伸展（去大脑强直）"},{"id":"A","en":"Abnormal flexion (decorticate)","zh":"异常屈曲（去皮质强直）"},{"id":"D","en":"No motor response","zh":"无运动反应"},{"id":"B","en":"Withdrawal from pain","zh":"痛觉回避"},{"id":"E","en":"Localizes to pain","zh":"痛觉定位"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In the GCS motor component: Abnormal flexion (decorticate) = 3, Extension (decerebrate) = 2, No response = 1. Withdrawal from pain = 4, Localizes to pain = 5, and Obeys commands = 6.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 GCS 运动部分：异常屈曲（去皮质）= 3，伸展（去大脑）= 2，无反应 = 1。痛觉回避 = 4，痛觉定位 = 5，遵从指令 = 6。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Review GCS scoring regularly. Higher scores indicate better neurological function.","testTakingStrategyZh":"定期复习 GCS 评分。评分越高表示神经功能越好。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which motor responses would be assigned a score of 3 or less?","controlSentenceZh":"以下哪些运动反应会被评为 3 分或更低？（"}
{"queueIndex":474,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.283","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.283.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.283.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Determine whether the following physical findings are characteristic of decorticate posturing, decerebrate posturing, or both.","fullStemZh":"确定以下体征是去皮质强直、去大脑强直还是两者的特征。","terminalSentenceEn":"Determine whether the following physical findings are characteristic of decorticate posturing, decerebrate posturing, or both.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定以下体征是去皮质强直、去大脑强直还是两者的特征。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Arms flexed at the elbows and held close to the chest","zh":"双臂在肘部屈曲并紧贴胸部"},{"id":"r2","en":"Arms extended, adducted, and internally rotated","zh":"双臂伸展、内收并内旋"},{"id":"r3","en":"Plantar flexion of the feet","zh":"足底屈曲"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Decorticate","zh":"去皮质"},{"id":"c3","en":"Both","zh":"两者均有"},{"id":"c2","en":"Decerebrate","zh":"去大脑"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Decorticate involves flexion towards the 'core'. Decerebrate involves extension. Both include plantar flexion of the feet.","rationaleCorrectZh":"去皮质强直涉及向“核心”屈曲。去大脑强直涉及伸展。两者都包括足底屈曲。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'de-CORE-ticate' with flexion toward the CORE of the body.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“de-CORE-ticate”与向身体核心 (CORE) 的屈曲联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":475,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c1_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.284.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,73],"fullStemEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) is prescribed epoetin alfa. Which laboratory result should the nurse monitor most closely to evaluate the effectiveness of this medication?","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性肾病 (CKD) 的患者被处方给予促红细胞生成素 (epoetin alfa)。护士应最密切监测哪项实验室检查结果以评估该药物的疗效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory result should the nurse monitor most closely to evaluate the effectiveness of this medication?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应最密切监测哪项实验室检查结果以评估该药物的疗效？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) is prescribed epoetin alfa.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有慢性肾病 (CKD) 的患者被处方给予促红细胞生成素 (epoetin alfa)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Serum creatinine","zh":"血清肌酐"},{"id":"B","en":"Hemoglobin","zh":"血红蛋白"},{"id":"D","en":"White Blood Cell (WBC) count","zh":"白细胞 (WBC) 计数"},{"id":"A","en":"Blood Urea Nitrogen (BUN)","zh":"血尿素氮"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Epoetin alfa is a synthetic version of erythropoietin, which stimulates the bone marrow to produce red blood cells. It is used to treat anemia in CKD, and its effectiveness is measured by monitoring hemoglobin and hematocrit levels.","rationaleCorrectZh":"促红细胞生成素 (epoetin alfa) 是促红细胞生成素的合成版本，可刺激骨髓产生红细胞。它用于治疗 CKD 贫血，其疗效通过监测血红蛋白和血细胞比容水平来衡量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the drug class (erythropoiesis-stimulating agent) and link it to the cell type it affects (erythrocytes/red blood cells).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别药物类别（促红细胞生成刺激剂）并将其与它影响的细胞类型（红细胞）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":476,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.285","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.285.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.285.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[240,291],"terminalOffsetsZh":[88,99],"fullStemEn":"A 72-year-old client with a history of a recent urinary tract infection is admitted with a blood pressure of 82/46 mmHg, heart rate 118/min, and a temperature of 102.4 °F (39.1 °C). The client is confused and has cool, mottled extremities. Complete the following clinical judgment statement.","fullStemZh":"一名有近期尿路感染病史的 72 岁患者入院，血压为 82/46 mmHg，心率为 118 次/分，体温为 102.4 °F (39.1 °C)。患者神志不清，四肢发凉、有花斑。完成以下临床判断陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the following clinical judgment statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成以下临床判断陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is confused and has cool, mottled extremities.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者神志不清，四肢发凉、有花斑。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"For immediate hemodynamic support while the sepsis bundle proceeds, the nurse should initiate {{1}} and prepare to administer {{2}} if hypotension persists, targeting {{3}}.","zh":"在败血症综合治疗同步进行时，为立即提供血流动力学支持，护士应开始 {{1}}；若低血压持续，则准备给予 {{2}}，目标为 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"furosemide 40 mg IV push","zh":"呋塞米 40 mg 静脉注射"},{"id":"o1","en":"balanced crystalloid bolus","zh":"平衡晶体液快速输注"},{"id":"o3","en":"broad-spectrum antibiotics","zh":"广谱抗生素"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o6","en":"atropine 0.5 mg IV","zh":"阿托品 0.5 mg 静脉注射"},{"id":"o5","en":"nitroglycerin drip","zh":"硝酸甘油滴注"},{"id":"o4","en":"norepinephrine infusion","zh":"去甲肾上腺素输注"}],"correct":"o4"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o7","en":"an initial mean arterial pressure of 60-65 mmHg","zh":"初始平均动脉压 60-65 mmHg"},{"id":"o9","en":"serum potassium level","zh":"血清钾水平"},{"id":"o8","en":"core temperature < 100 °F (37.8 °C)","zh":"核心体温 < 100 °F (37.8 °C)"}],"correct":"o7"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Septic shock treatment and resuscitation begin immediately, including antimicrobials and hemodynamic support. Use crystalloid for initial resuscitation, with balanced crystalloid preferred over 0.9% saline. If hypotension persists, norepinephrine is first line. For this 72-year-old client, an initial MAP range of 60-65 mmHg is reasonable, with subsequent targets individualized to perfusion and comorbidities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"感染性休克的治疗和复苏应立即开始，包括抗微生物治疗和血流动力学支持。初始复苏使用晶体液，平衡晶体液优于 0.9% 生理盐水。若低血压持续，去甲肾上腺素为一线药物。对于这名 72 岁患者，初始 MAP 目标范围 60-65 mmHg 是合理的，随后应根据灌注和合并症个体化调整。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In septic shock, think simultaneous time-critical care: antimicrobials, crystalloid resuscitation, perfusion reassessment, and norepinephrine when hypotension persists. Individualize the MAP target by age and response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"感染性休克需同步开展时效性治疗：抗微生物药、晶体液复苏、灌注再评估，以及低血压持续时使用去甲肾上腺素。MAP 目标应结合年龄和反应个体化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":477,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.286.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,265],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,72],"fullStemEn":"A 34-year-old pregnant client at 36 weeks gestation presents to the triage unit with a headache and 'seeing spots.' For each assessment finding, select whether the finding is consistent with Preeclampsia with Severe Features or Preeclampsia Without Severe Features.","fullStemZh":"一名怀孕 36 周的 34 岁孕妇因头痛和”看到斑点”来到分诊单元。对于每项评估结果，请选择该结果是与重度子痫前期一致还是与非重度子痫前期一致。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, select whether the finding is consistent with Preeclampsia with Severe Features or Preeclampsia Without Severe Features.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项评估结果，请选择该结果是与重度子痫前期一致还是与非重度子痫前期一致。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 34-year-old pregnant client at 36 weeks gestation presents to the triage unit with a headache and 'seeing spots.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名怀孕 36 周的 34 岁孕妇因头痛和”看到斑点”来到分诊单元。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Blood pressure 164/112 mmHg on two occasions 4 hours apart.","zh":"间隔 4 小时的两次血压测量均为 164/112 mmHg。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Platelet count of 88 ×10³/µL.","zh":"血小板计数为 88 ×10³/µL。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Proteinuria of 300 mg in a 24-hour urine collection.","zh":"24 小时尿蛋白定量为 300 mg。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Serum creatinine 1.2 mg/dL (baseline 0.6 mg/dL).","zh":"血清肌酐 1.2 mg/dL（基线为 0.6 mg/dL）。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Preeclampsia Without Severe Features","zh":"非重度子痫前期"},{"id":"c1","en":"Preeclampsia with Severe Features","zh":"重度子痫前期"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Preeclampsia with severe features is defined by BP ≥160/110 mmHg (r1), thrombocytopenia <100,000/mm³ (r2), renal insufficiency (creatinine >1.1 mg/dL or doubling of baseline, r4), or cerebral/visual disturbances. Proteinuria ≥300 mg/24h (r3) meets the diagnostic threshold for preeclampsia, but is not itself a severe-features criterion — placing it in the 'Without Severe Features' category. Note: gestational hypertension is elevated BP without proteinuria or end-organ damage and is a distinct diagnosis not shown here.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重度子痫前期的诊断标准包括血压 ≥160/110 mmHg（r1）、血小板减少症 <100 ×10³/µL（r2）、肾功能不全（肌酐 >1.1 mg/dL 或较基线翻倍，r4）或脑/视觉症状。24 小时尿蛋白 ≥300 mg（r3）符合子痫前期的诊断阈值，但本身并非重度特征的判断标准，因此归入”非重度子痫前期”类别。注：妊娠期高血压是无尿蛋白或器官损害的高血压，属不同诊断，未在本题中呈现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify systemic involvement (organs) to distinguish severe preeclampsia from gestational or mild hypertension.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别全身受累（器官）以区分重度子痫前期与妊娠期或轻度高血压。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":478,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.287","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.287.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.287.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[230,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[105,120],"fullStemEn":"A client is being treated for Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA). The latest labs show: Blood glucose 240 mg/dL, Potassium 3.4 mEq/L, and pH 7.28. The client is currently receiving 0.9% Normal Saline with 10 units/hr of regular insulin. Complete the statement regarding the next steps in management.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正因糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 接受治疗。最新的实验室检查显示：血糖 240 mg/dL，钾 3.4 mEq/L，pH 7.28。患者目前正在接受 0.9% 生理盐水及每小时 10 单位的普通胰岛素。完成关于下一步管理措施的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement regarding the next steps in management.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成关于下一步管理措施的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is currently receiving 0.9% Normal Saline with 10 units/hr of regular insulin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者目前正在接受 0.9% 生理盐水及每小时 10 单位的普通胰岛素。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should anticipate changing the IV fluid to {{1}} and adding {{2}} to the IV regimen because {{3}}.","zh":"护士应预期将静脉输液更改为 {{1}} 并在静脉方案中添加 {{2}}，因为 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"5% Dextrose with 0.45% Normal Saline","zh":"5% 葡萄糖 0.45% 生理盐水"},{"id":"o2","en":"Lactated Ringer's solution","zh":"乳酸林格氏液"},{"id":"o3","en":"10% Dextrose in Water","zh":"10% 葡萄糖水溶液"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o4","en":"potassium chloride","zh":"氯化钾"},{"id":"o5","en":"sodium bicarbonate","zh":"碳酸氢钠"},{"id":"o6","en":"calcium gluconate","zh":"葡萄糖酸钙"}],"correct":"o4"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o9","en":"hypoglycemia is the primary risk when pH is below 7.30","zh":"当 pH 值低于 7.30 时，低血糖是首要风险"},{"id":"o7","en":"insulin causes potassium to shift into cells and glucose is dropping before ketosis is resolved","zh":"胰岛素导致钾转移到细胞内，且在酮症解决之前血糖正在下降"},{"id":"o8","en":"the client is experiencing hypernatremia and metabolic alkalosis","zh":"患者正经历高钠血症和代谢性碱中毒"}],"correct":"o7"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In DKA management, once blood glucose falls below 250 mg/dL, dextrose is added to the IV fluids (e.g., D5 1/2NS) to prevent hypoglycemia while continuing insulin to resolve ketosis. Potassium must be replaced when levels are low-normal because insulin therapy shifts potassium into the cells, potentially leading to life-threatening hypokalemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 DKA 管理中，一旦血糖降至 250 mg/dL 以下，应在静脉输液中添加葡萄糖（如 D5 1/2NS），以在继续使用胰岛素解决酮症的同时预防低血糖。当钾水平处于低限正常值时必须进行补充，因为胰岛素治疗会将钾转移到细胞内，可能导致危及生命的低钾血症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the 'two-pronged' approach to DKA: resolving the acidosis with insulin while carefully managing electrolytes and preventing rapid glucose drops.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注 DKA 的“两手抓”方法：使用胰岛素解决酸中毒，同时仔细管理电解质并预防血糖快速下降。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":479,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.288.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,246],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,72],"fullStemEn":"A client presents to the emergency department with fever, muscle rigidity, and altered mental status. For each clinical characteristic, select whether it is more commonly associated with Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome (NMS) or Serotonin Syndrome.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因发热、肌肉僵硬和意识状态改变被送往急诊科。对于每项临床特征，请选择它更常见于神经阻滞剂恶性综合征 (NMS) 还是 5-羟色胺综合征。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical characteristic, select whether it is more commonly associated with Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome (NMS) or Serotonin Syndrome.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项临床特征，请选择它更常见于神经阻滞剂恶性综合征 (NMS) 还是 5-羟色胺综合征。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client presents to the emergency department with fever, muscle rigidity, and altered mental status.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因发热、肌肉僵硬和意识状态改变被送往急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Hyperreflexia and myoclonus.","zh":"反射亢进和肌阵挛。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Severe 'lead-pipe' muscle rigidity.","zh":"严重的“铅管样”肌肉强直。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Triggered by dopamine antagonists (e.g., haloperidol).","zh":"由多巴胺拮抗剂（如氟哌啶醇）诱发。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Triggered by SSRIs or MAOIs.","zh":"由 SSRIs 或 MAOIs 诱发。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome (NMS)","zh":"神经阻滞剂恶性综合征 (NMS)"},{"id":"c2","en":"Serotonin Syndrome","zh":"5-羟色胺综合征"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"NMS is characterized by 'lead-pipe' rigidity and is caused by dopamine depletion (antipsychotics). Serotonin syndrome features hyperreflexia, myoclonus, and is caused by excessive serotonin (SSRIs, etc.). Both cause fever and altered mental status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"NMS 的特征是“铅管样”强直，由多巴胺耗竭（抗精神病药物）引起。5-羟色胺综合征的特征是反射亢进、肌阵挛，由 5-羟色胺过量（SSRIs 等）引起。两者都会引起发烧和意识状态改变。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate based on neuromuscular findings: 'Rigid' (NMS) vs. 'Hyper' (Serotonin Syndrome).","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据神经肌肉表现进行区分：“僵硬”（NMS）与“亢进”（5-羟色胺综合征）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client presents to the emergency department with fever, muscle rigidity, and altered mental status.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患者因发热、肌肉僵硬和意识状态改变被送往急诊科。"}
{"queueIndex":480,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.289","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.289.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.289.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[173,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,63],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute decompensated heart failure is presenting with severe dyspnea, orthopnea, and crackles throughout all lung fields. Oxygen saturation is 88% on room air. Complete the nursing priority statement.","fullStemZh":"一名急性失代偿性心力衰竭患者表现为严重呼吸困难、端坐呼吸，全肺野可闻及湿啰音。未吸氧时氧饱和度为 88%。完成护理优先级陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing priority statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护理优先级陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Oxygen saturation is 88% on room air.","penultimateSentenceZh":"未吸氧时氧饱和度为 88%。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's first action should be to place the client in {{1}}, followed by the administration of {{2}} to decrease {{3}}.","zh":"护士的首要行动应是将患者置于 {{1}}，随后给予 {{2}} 以减少 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"high-Fowler's position","zh":"高坐卧位"},{"id":"o2","en":"Trendelenburg position","zh":"趋势伦伯卧位（头低脚高位）"},{"id":"o3","en":"supine position with legs elevated","zh":"仰卧位，双腿抬高"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o5","en":"intravenous fluids (NS 100 mL/hr)","zh":"静脉补液（生理盐水 100 mL/hr）"},{"id":"o4","en":"intravenous furosemide","zh":"静脉注射呋塞米"},{"id":"o6","en":"beta-blockers","zh":"β 受体阻滞剂"}],"correct":"o4"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o8","en":"heart rate and myocardial contractility","zh":"心率和心肌收缩力"},{"id":"o7","en":"preload and pulmonary congestion","zh":"前负荷和肺淤血"},{"id":"o9","en":"systemic vascular resistance","zh":"全身血管阻力"}],"correct":"o7"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Placing the client in high-Fowler's position is the fastest way to improve gas exchange by reducing venous return and allowing maximum lung expansion. IV diuretics like furosemide are essential to remove excess fluid, thereby decreasing preload and alleviating pulmonary congestion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"将患者置于高坐卧位是通过减少回心血量并允许最大程度的肺扩张来改善气体交换的最快方法。静脉利尿剂（如呋塞米）对于排出多余液体至关重要，从而减少前负荷并减轻肺淤血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation). Positioning (Breathing) comes before medication (Circulation/Volume).","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）。体位调整（呼吸）优于药物治疗（循环/容量）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":481,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.290.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,51],"fullStemEn":"A 4-year-old child presents with respiratory distress and stridor. For each clinical finding, select whether it is more characteristic of Epiglottitis or Laryngotracheobronchitis (Croup).","fullStemZh":"一名 4 岁儿童出现呼吸困难和喉鸣。对于每项临床发现，请选择它更符合会厌炎还是喉气管支气管炎（哮吼）。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, select whether it is more characteristic of Epiglottitis or Laryngotracheobronchitis (Croup).","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项临床发现，请选择它更符合会厌炎还是喉气管支气管炎（哮吼）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 4-year-old child presents with respiratory distress and stridor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 4 岁儿童出现呼吸困难和喉鸣。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"High fever and drooling.","zh":"高热和流涎。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Barking, seal-like cough.","zh":"犬吠样咳嗽。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Tripod positioning for breathing.","zh":"呼吸时采取三脚架体位。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Commonly caused by Haemophilus influenzae type b (Hib).","zh":"通常由 b 型流感嗜血杆菌 (Hib) 引起。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Croup","zh":"哮吼"},{"id":"c1","en":"Epiglottitis","zh":"会厌炎"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Epiglottitis is a medical emergency characterized by the '4 Ds': Drooling, Dysphagia, Dysphonia, and Distressed inspiratory efforts (tripod position). It is often bacterial (Hib). Croup is typically viral and characterized by a barking cough and is usually less acutely life-threatening than epiglottitis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"会厌炎是一种医疗急症，其特征是“4 D”：流涎 (Drooling)、吞咽困难 (Dysphagia)、发声困难 (Dysphonia) 和吸气困难 (Distressed)（三脚架体位）。它通常是由细菌（Hib）引起的。哮吼通常是病毒性的，特征是犬吠样咳嗽，通常不像会厌炎那样具有急性生命威胁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'Drooling/Tripod' with the emergency of Epiglottitis and 'Barking cough' with Croup.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“流涎/三脚架体位”与会厌炎急症联系起来，将“犬吠样咳嗽”与哮吼联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":482,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.291","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.291.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.291.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[177,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,73],"fullStemEn":"A client with Graves' disease following a thyroidectomy becomes extremely agitated, with a temperature of 104 °F (40 °C), heart rate 160/min, and new-onset atrial fibrillation. Complete the clinical judgment statement.","fullStemZh":"一名患有格雷夫斯病并在甲状腺切除术后的患者变得极度焦虑，体温 104 °F (40 °C)，心率 160 次/分，新发心房颤动。完成临床判断陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成临床判断陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Graves' disease following a thyroidectomy becomes extremely agitated, with a temperature of 104 °F (40 °C), heart rate 160/min, and new-onset atrial fibrillation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有格雷夫斯病并在甲状腺切除术后的患者变得极度焦虑，体温 104 °F (40 °C)，心率 160 次/分，新发心房颤动。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should immediately prepare to administer {{1}} to control the heart rate and {{2}} to inhibit the synthesis of thyroid hormones, because the priority is to prevent {{3}}.","zh":"护士应立即准备给予 {{1}} 以控制心率，并给予 {{2}} 以抑制甲状腺激素的合成，因为首要任务是预防 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"epinephrine","zh":"肾上腺素"},{"id":"o1","en":"propranolol","zh":"普萘洛尔"},{"id":"o3","en":"levothyroxine","zh":"左旋甲状腺素"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o5","en":"calcium gluconate","zh":"葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"o4","en":"propylthiouracil (PTU)","zh":"丙硫氧嘧啶 (PTU)"},{"id":"o6","en":"magnesium sulfate","zh":"硫酸镁"}],"correct":"o4"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o8","en":"respiratory alkalosis","zh":"呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"o9","en":"myxedema coma","zh":"黏液性水肿昏迷"},{"id":"o7","en":"cardiovascular collapse and heart failure","zh":"心血管虚脱和心力衰竭"}],"correct":"o7"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thyroid storm is a life-threatening hypermetabolic state. Beta-blockers (propranolol) are used to rapidly block the sympathetic effects (tachycardia, AFib). PTU or methimazole is used to block new hormone synthesis. Preventing cardiovascular collapse due to extreme tachycardia and hyperthermia is the priority.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺风暴是一种危及生命的高代谢状态。β 受体阻滞剂（普萘洛尔）用于快速阻断交感神经效应（心动过速、房颤）。PTU 或甲巯咪唑用于阻断新激素的合成。首要任务是预防因极端心动过速和高热导致的心血管虚脱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the goal in hyperthyroid crisis: slow the heart down and stop the production of the hormone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住甲状腺功能亢进危象的目标：减慢心率并停止激素产生。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":483,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.292.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,253],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,96],"fullStemEn":"A 180-lb (81.8 kg) client was admitted 2 hours ago with full-thickness burns to 40% of the body. For each intervention or assessment, select whether it is an expected priority during the resuscitation (emergent) phase or the acute (wound healing) phase.","fullStemZh":"一名体重 180 磅 (81.8 kg) 的患者于 2 小时前入院，全身 40% 面积受深 III 度烧伤。对于每项干预或评估，请选择它是复苏（急症）阶段还是急性（伤口愈合）阶段的预期优先级。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each intervention or assessment, select whether it is an expected priority during the resuscitation (emergent) phase or the acute (wound healing) phase.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项干预或评估，请选择它是复苏（急症）阶段还是急性（伤口愈合）阶段的预期优先级。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 180-lb (81.8 kg) client was admitted 2 hours ago with full-thickness burns to 40% of the body.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名体重 180 磅 (81.8 kg) 的患者于 2 小时前入院，全身 40% 面积受深 III 度烧伤。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Administration of large volumes of Lactated Ringer's.","zh":"输入大量乳酸林格氏液。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Monitoring for hyperkalemia due to cell lysis.","zh":"监测因细胞裂解导致的高钾血症。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Focus on high-protein, high-calorie nutrition and wound debridement.","zh":"重点关注高蛋白、高热量营养和伤口清创。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Strict hourly urine output monitoring (target 30-50 mL/hr).","zh":"严格的每小时尿量监测（目标 30-50 mL/hr）。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Resuscitation Phase","zh":"复苏阶段"},{"id":"c2","en":"Acute Phase","zh":"急性阶段"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The resuscitation phase (first 24-48h) focuses on fluid resuscitation (LR), electrolyte management (hyperkalemia risk), and monitoring organ perfusion (urine output). The acute phase begins when the client is hemodynamically stable and focuses on wound care and nutrition.","rationaleCorrectZh":"复苏阶段（最初 24-48 小时）重点在于液体复苏 (LR)、电解质管理（高钾血症风险）和监测器官灌注（尿量）。急性阶段始于患者血流动力学稳定时，重点在于伤口护理和营养。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate the emergent phase with 'Circulation' (fluids/output/electrolytes) and the acute phase with 'Healing'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将急症阶段与“循环”（液体/排出量/电解质）联系起来，将急性阶段与“愈合”联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":484,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.293","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.293.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.293.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,59],"fullStemEn":"A client with a traumatic brain injury is being monitored for increased intracranial pressure (ICP). The nurse notes a widening pulse pressure, bradycardia, and irregular respirations. Complete the clinical analysis.","fullStemZh":"一名患有创伤性脑损伤的患者正接受颅内压 (ICP) 升高监测。护士注意到脉压增宽、心动过缓和呼吸不规则。完成临床分析。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical analysis.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成临床分析。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes a widening pulse pressure, bradycardia, and irregular respirations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到脉压增宽、心动过缓和呼吸不规则。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse identifies these findings as {{1}}, which indicates {{2}} and requires immediate intervention with {{3}}.","zh":"护士将这些发现识别为 {{1}}，这表明发生了 {{2}}，需要立即使用 {{3}} 进行干预。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Beck's triad","zh":"贝克三联征"},{"id":"o1","en":"Cushing's triad","zh":"库欣三联征"},{"id":"o3","en":"Virchow's triad","zh":"魏尔肖三联征"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o5","en":"hypovolemic shock","zh":"低血容量性休克"},{"id":"o4","en":"impending brainstem herniation","zh":"即将发生的脑干疝"},{"id":"o6","en":"autonomic dysreflexia","zh":"自主神经反射亢进"}],"correct":"o4"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o7","en":"osmotic diuretics (e.g., mannitol)","zh":"渗透性利尿剂（如甘露醇）"},{"id":"o8","en":"aggressive fluid boluses","zh":"积极的液体快速输入"},{"id":"o9","en":"atropine administration","zh":"给予阿托品"}],"correct":"o7"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cushing's triad (widening pulse pressure, bradycardia, irregular respirations) is a late sign of increased ICP and signals impending brainstem herniation. Mannitol is an osmotic diuretic used to rapidly reduce cerebral edema and ICP.","rationaleCorrectZh":"库欣三联征（脉压增宽、心动过缓、呼吸不规则）是颅内压升高的晚期体征，预示着即将发生脑干疝。甘露醇是一种渗透性利尿剂，用于快速减轻脑水肿并降低颅内压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast Cushing's triad (high BP, low HR) with shock (low BP, high HR) to avoid confusion.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将库欣三联征（高血压、低心率）与休克（低血压、高心率）对比，以避免混淆。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":485,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c10_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.294.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"For each assessment finding, select the electrolyte imbalance it most likely represents.","fullStemZh":"对于每项评估结果，请选择它最可能代表的电解质失衡。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, select the electrolyte imbalance it most likely represents.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项评估结果，请选择它最可能代表的电解质失衡。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Positive Chvostek's and Trousseau's signs.","zh":"Chvostek 征和 Trousseau 征阳性。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Tall, peaked T waves and widened QRS on ECG.","zh":"心电图显示高尖 T 波和 QRS 波增宽。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Prominent U waves and flattened T waves on ECG.","zh":"心电图显示明显的 U 波和 T 波平坦。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Extreme thirst, dry mucous membranes, and agitation.","zh":"极度口渴、粘膜干燥和焦虑。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Hyperkalemia","zh":"高钾血症"},{"id":"c3","en":"Hypocalcemia","zh":"低钙血症"},{"id":"c2","en":"Hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"},{"id":"c4","en":"Hypernatremia","zh":"高钠血症"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypocalcemia causes neuromuscular irritability (Chvostek's/Trousseau's). Hyperkalemia causes peaked T waves. Hypokalemia causes U waves and ST depression. Hypernatremia causes signs of dehydration and CNS effects like agitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低钙血症引起神经肌肉兴奋性增高 (Chvostek's/Trousseau's)。高钾血症引起高尖 T 波。低钾血症引起 U 波和 ST 段压低。高钠血症引起脱水体征和中枢神经系统效应，如焦虑。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the specific ECG markers for potassium and the physical signs for calcium imbalances.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住钾失衡的特定心电图标记和钙失衡的体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":486,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.295","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.295.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.295.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,32],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client of the Orthodox Jewish faith who has just died. Which action by the nurse is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚去世的正统犹太教信徒。护士的哪项操作最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项操作最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client of the Orthodox Jewish faith who has just died.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚去世的正统犹太教信徒。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Wrap the body in a linen shroud and turn the face toward Mecca.","zh":"用亚麻布包裹遗体并将脸朝向麦加。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare the body for immediate cremation.","zh":"准备将遗体立即火化。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the family and allow them to stay with the body.","zh":"通知家属并允许他们陪伴遗体。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask the family if they would like an autopsy performed.","zh":"询问家属是否希望进行尸检。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In Orthodox Judaism, it is a common practice for family or community members to stay with the body from the time of death until burial, which usually occurs within 24 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在正统犹太教中，家属或社区成员通常会在从死亡到埋葬（通常在24小时内）的这段时间内一直陪伴在遗体旁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall cultural traditions associated with end-of-life care. Judaism emphasizes respect for the body and rapid burial without cremation or unnecessary autopsy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想与临终关怀相关的文化传统。犹太教强调尊重遗体，并要求快速埋葬，不火化，也不进行不必要的尸检。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":487,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.296.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[187,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing end-of-life care for clients from diverse cultural backgrounds. Which interventions should the nurse include in the plan of care to ensure culturally competent care? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为来自不同文化背景的患者提供临终关怀。护士应在护理计划中包含哪些干预措施以确保具有文化胜任力的护理？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the plan of care to ensure culturally competent care?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在护理计划中包含哪些干预措施以确保具有文化胜任力的护理？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Discourage all non-medical traditional healing practices at the bedside to avoid interference with care.","zh":"劝阻床边所有的非医学传统康复实践，以避免干扰护理。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ensure that the client is never left alone if that is identified as a cultural preference.","zh":"如果这被确定为一种文化偏好，确保患者永远不会被单独留下。"},{"id":"E","en":"Assume that all members of a specific ethnic group will share the same end-of-life preferences.","zh":"假设特定族群的所有成员都会有相同的临终偏好。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the family about specific religious or cultural rituals they wish to perform at the time of death.","zh":"询问家属在死亡时希望进行的特定宗教或文化仪式。"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide a private space for the family to gather, pray, and mourn.","zh":"为家属提供一个聚集、祈祷和哀悼的私人空间。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Culturally competent care involves individual assessment of rituals, accommodating preferences for presence, and providing privacy for mourning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具有文化胜任力的护理包括对仪式的个体化评估、满足陪护偏好以及为哀悼提供隐私。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on options that promote individual assessment and respect for cultural diversity while avoiding those that involve stereotyping or unnecessary restriction of practices.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注那些促进个体化评估和尊重文化多样性的选项，同时避免那些涉及刻板印象或不必要限制实践的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":488,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.297","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.297.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.297.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,205],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,47],"fullStemEn":"An older adult client is admitted with a urinary tract infection and is experiencing acute confusion and visual hallucinations. Which assessment finding most likely indicates delirium rather than dementia?","fullStemZh":"一名老年患者因尿路感染入院，正出现急性意识模糊和视幻觉。哪项评估结果最可能表明是谵妄而非痴呆？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding most likely indicates delirium rather than dementia?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项评估结果最可能表明是谵妄而非痴呆？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An older adult client is admitted with a urinary tract infection and is experiencing acute confusion and visual hallucinations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名老年患者因尿路感染入院，正出现急性意识模糊和视幻觉。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The client's speech is slow and deliberate.","zh":"患者的言语缓慢且慎重。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client's level of consciousness is fluctuating throughout the day.","zh":"患者的意识水平在一天中发生波动。"},{"id":"A","en":"The symptoms developed gradually over several months.","zh":"症状是在几个月内逐渐发展起来的。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client has difficulty remembering names of family members.","zh":"患者难以记住家属的名字。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Delirium is characterized by an acute onset and a fluctuating course of consciousness and cognition. Dementia is typically chronic and progressive with stable consciousness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"谵妄的特点是急性发作，且意识和认知过程呈波动性。痴呆通常是慢性、渐进性的，且意识状态稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the key differences: Delirium is acute, fluctuating, and often reversible; Dementia is chronic, progressive, and stable in consciousness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住关键区别：谵妄是急性的、波动的，通常是可逆的；痴呆是慢性的、渐进性的，且意识状态稳定。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"An older adult client is admitted with a urinary tract infection and is experiencing acute confusion and visual hallucinations.","controlSentenceZh":"一名老年患者因尿路感染入院，正出现急性意识模糊和视幻觉。"}
{"queueIndex":489,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.298.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,51],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client with delirium. Which interventions should the nurse include to promote safety and reduce confusion? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名谵妄患者制定护理计划。护士应包含哪些干预措施以促进安全并减少意识模糊？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include to promote safety and reduce confusion?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包含哪些干预措施以促进安全并减少意识模糊？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Provide a high-stimulation environment with loud music to keep the client alert.","zh":"提供一个高刺激环境并播放大声的音乐以保持患者清醒。"},{"id":"E","en":"Place the client in a room far from the nurses' station to ensure quiet.","zh":"将患者安置在远离护士站的房间以确保安静。"},{"id":"C","en":"Keep the room well-lit during the day and use a dim nightlight at night.","zh":"白天保持房间光线充足，晚上使用昏暗的夜灯。"},{"id":"D","en":"Frequently reorient the client to person, place, and time using clocks and calendars.","zh":"使用时钟和日历频繁地让患者重新定向到人物、地点和时间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use a calm, low-pitched voice when speaking to the client.","zh":"与患者交谈时使用平静、低沉的声音。"}],"correct":["B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective delirium management involves low stimulation, adequate lighting to prevent sensory illusions, and consistent reorientation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的谵妄管理包括低刺激、充足的光线以防止感觉错觉，以及持续的重新定向。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose interventions that minimize sensory overload, provide orientation cues, and ensure the nurse can monitor the client closely for safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择那些能尽量减少感觉过载、提供定向提示并确保护士能密切监测患者安全的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":490,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.299","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.299.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.299.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Identify whether the following clinical characteristics are more indicative of delirium or dementia.","fullStemZh":"确定以下临床特征更代表谵妄还是痴呆。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify whether the following clinical characteristics are more indicative of delirium or dementia.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定以下临床特征更代表谵妄还是痴呆。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Onset is acute (hours to days)","zh":"急性发作（数小时至数天）"},{"id":"r2","en":"Course is stable and slowly progressive","zh":"病程稳定且缓慢进展"},{"id":"r3","en":"Level of consciousness is impaired or fluctuating","zh":"意识水平受损或波动"},{"id":"r4","en":"Thought process is often disorganized and fragmented","zh":"思维过程通常杂乱无章且支离破碎"},{"id":"r5","en":"Condition is usually reversible with treatment of underlying cause","zh":"在治疗潜在原因后，病情通常是可逆的"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Delirium","zh":"谵妄"},{"id":"c2","en":"Dementia","zh":"痴呆"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Delirium is an acute, fluctuating, and reversible syndrome often triggered by medical issues. Dementia is a chronic, stable, and irreversible decline.","rationaleCorrectZh":"谵妄是一种急性的、波动的、可逆的综合征，通常由医疗问题引发。痴呆是一种慢性的、稳定的、不可逆的衰退。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the two by focusing on 'Onset', 'Course', and 'Reversibility'. Acute and fluctuating always points to delirium.","testTakingStrategyZh":"通过关注“发作”、“病程”和“可逆性”来区分两者。急性和波动总是指向谵妄。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":491,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.300.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,38],"fullStemEn":"A client in the psychiatric unit begins pacing rapidly and shouting at other clients. Which is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"精神科病房的一名患者开始快速踱步并向其他患者大声喊叫。护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in the psychiatric unit begins pacing rapidly and shouting at other clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"精神科病房的一名患者开始快速踱步并向其他患者大声喊叫。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer a PRN sedative medication immediately.","zh":"立即给予必要时（PRN）镇静药物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Approach the client in a calm, non-threatening manner and maintain a safe distance.","zh":"以平静、非威胁的方式接近患者，并保持安全距离。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call for additional staff and prepare to use physical restraints.","zh":"呼叫额外工作人员并准备使用物理约束。"},{"id":"A","en":"Firmly tell the client to stop shouting and go back to their room.","zh":"坚定地告诉患者停止喊叫并回到房间。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"De-escalation begins with the least restrictive intervention: a calm, non-threatening approach while ensuring safety for both the nurse and the client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"降级（去升级）从最少限制性的干预开始：在确保护士和患者安全的同时，采用平静、非威胁的方式。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize 'Least Restrictive First'. Calm communication and maintaining personal space are fundamental to de-escalation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先考虑“最少限制优先”。冷静的沟通和保持个人空间是降级的基础。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":492,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.301","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.301.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.301.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is using de-escalation techniques with an agitated client. Which actions demonstrate effective de-escalation? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正对一名躁动患者使用降级（去升级）技巧。哪些行动展示了有效的降级？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions demonstrate effective de-escalation?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些行动展示了有效的降级？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Stand directly in front of the client with arms crossed to show authority.","zh":"双臂交叉直接站在患者面前以显示权威。"},{"id":"D","en":"Listen actively to the client's concerns without interrupting.","zh":"在不打断的情况下积极倾听患者的顾虑。"},{"id":"E","en":"Avoid making direct eye contact if it seems to increase the client's agitation.","zh":"如果直接眼神交流似乎会增加患者的躁动，则应避免。"},{"id":"C","en":"Offer the client clear, simple choices if possible (e.g., 'Would you like to sit down or take a walk?').","zh":"如果可能，为患者提供清晰、简单的选择（例如，“您想坐下还是去散步？”）。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use 'I' statements to express concern and observations.","zh":"使用“我”字句来表达关心和观察结果。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective de-escalation includes empathetic communication, offering control through choices, active listening, and non-threatening body language.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的降级包括共情沟通、通过选择提供控制感、积极倾听以及非威胁性的肢体语言。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify actions that are non-confrontational, empathetic, and promote the client's autonomy and safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别那些非对抗性的、共情的、并能促进患者自主和安全的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":493,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.302.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,51],"fullStemEn":"A client who has a strong dislike for their mother-in-law is observed being overly affectionate and helpful toward her during a family visit. The nurse recognizes this as which defense mechanism?","fullStemZh":"一名非常讨厌婆婆/岳母的患者，在家庭聚会期间被观察到对她过度亲昵且乐于助人。护士认为这是哪种防御机制？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse recognizes this as which defense mechanism?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士认为这是哪种防御机制？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who has a strong dislike for their mother-in-law is observed being overly affectionate and helpful toward her during a family visit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名非常讨厌婆婆/岳母的患者，在家庭聚会期间被观察到对她过度亲昵且乐于助人。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Projection","zh":"投射"},{"id":"D","en":"Displacement","zh":"转移"},{"id":"C","en":"Sublimation","zh":"升华"},{"id":"B","en":"Reaction Formation","zh":"反向形成"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reaction formation is the development of conscious attitudes and behaviors that are the exact opposite of what one actually feels or wants to do.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反向形成是指发展出与一个人实际感受或想做的事情完全相反的有意识的态度和行为。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for a scenario where the behavior is the 'opposite' of the underlying emotion. This is the definition of reaction formation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找行为与潜在情绪“相反”的场景。这就是反向形成的定义。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":494,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.303","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.303.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.303.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,50],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client's use of defense mechanisms. Which of the following examples represent adaptive (healthy) uses of defense mechanisms? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估患者对防御机制的使用。以下哪些例子代表了防御机制的适应性（健康）使用？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following examples represent adaptive (healthy) uses of defense mechanisms?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些例子代表了防御机制的适应性（健康）使用？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"A client with a terminal diagnosis continues to plan a world tour as if they are not ill.","zh":"一名患有绝症的患者继续计划环球旅行，仿佛自己没有生病。"},{"id":"B","en":"A person who was passed over for a promotion says, 'I didn't really want the extra responsibility anyway.'","zh":"一个错过晋升机会的人说：“反正我本来也不想要额外的责任。”"},{"id":"D","en":"A person who is angry at their boss comes home and yells at their children.","zh":"一个生老板气的人回到家对着孩子大喊大叫。"},{"id":"A","en":"A student who is stressed about an upcoming exam goes for a long run to relieve tension.","zh":"一名对即将到来的考试感到压力巨大的学生通过长跑来缓解紧张情绪。"},{"id":"C","en":"A child who was bullied at school starts acting like their favorite superhero to feel stronger.","zh":"一个在学校被欺负的孩子开始表现得像他最喜欢的超级英雄，以让自己感觉更强大。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adaptive defense mechanisms help individuals deal with stress effectively without harming themselves or others. Examples include sublimation, rationalization, and identification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适应性防御机制可以帮助个体有效地应对压力，而不会伤害自己或他人。例子包括升华、合理化和认同。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between mechanisms that solve a problem or relieve stress constructively versus those that are harmful or avoid reality entirely.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分那些能建设性地解决问题或缓解压力的机制，以及那些有害或完全逃避现实的机制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":495,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.304.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"Match each client scenario with the corresponding defense mechanism being demonstrated.","fullStemZh":"将每个患者场景与所展示的相应防御机制相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each client scenario with the corresponding defense mechanism being demonstrated.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每个患者场景与所展示的相应防御机制相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"A client angry at a spouse kicks the family dog.","zh":"一名生配偶气的患者踢了家里的狗。"},{"id":"r2","en":"A person with alcohol use disorder says they only drink 'to be social'.","zh":"一名患有酒精使用障碍的人说他们喝酒只是为了“社交”。"},{"id":"r3","en":"A client with strong aggressive urges joins a competitive karate class.","zh":"一名有强烈攻击冲动的患者参加了竞争性的空手道课程。"},{"id":"r4","en":"A client blames their partner for being 'unfaithful' despite having an affair themselves.","zh":"一名尽管自己有外遇却指责伴侣“不忠”的患者。"},{"id":"r5","en":"A client who failed an exam says the teacher 'didn't cover the material'.","zh":"一名考试不及格的患者说老师“没有涵盖相关内容”。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Sublimation","zh":"升华"},{"id":"c2","en":"Denial","zh":"否认"},{"id":"c5","en":"Rationalization","zh":"合理化"},{"id":"c1","en":"Displacement","zh":"转移"},{"id":"c4","en":"Projection","zh":"投射"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c5"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Defense mechanisms are unconscious psychological strategies used to protect a person from anxiety arising from unacceptable thoughts or feelings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心理防御机制是用于保护一个人免受不可接受的想法或感受所引起的焦虑的潜意识心理策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the specific scenario to the core definition of each mechanism. Focus on the target of the emotion and the nature of the justification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将特定场景与每个机制的核心定义相匹配。关注情绪的目标和辩解的本质。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":496,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.305","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.305.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.305.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[205,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,63],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is planning the client assignments for the shift. Which tasks are appropriate to delegate to a licensed practical nurse (LPN) who is assigned to care for a group of stable clients? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在规划本班次的患者护理分配。哪些任务适合委派给负责一组稳定患者的执业护士 (LPN)？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which tasks are appropriate to delegate to a licensed practical nurse (LPN) who is assigned to care for a group of stable clients?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些任务适合委派给负责一组稳定患者的执业护士 (LPN)？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Suctioning an established tracheostomy","zh":"对已建立的气管造口进行吸痰"},{"id":"C","en":"Developing the initial plan of care for a newly admitted client","zh":"为新入院患者制定初步护理计划"},{"id":"A","en":"Administering a scheduled oral antibiotic","zh":"按时给予口服抗生素"},{"id":"B","en":"Performing a sterile dressing change on a post-operative wound","zh":"对术后伤口进行无菌敷料更换"},{"id":"F","en":"Monitoring the client's skin for breakdown","zh":"监测患者皮肤是否有破损"},{"id":"E","en":"Providing discharge education regarding new medications","zh":"提供关于新药物的出院教育"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs can perform tasks for stable clients including medication administration (with some IV restrictions depending on state law), sterile procedures like dressing changes and suctioning of established sites, and data collection/monitoring. Initial assessments, care planning, and complex teaching are RN responsibilities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN 可以为稳定患者执行任务，包括给药（根据州法律，某些静脉注射受限）、无菌操作（如更换敷料和对已建立部位吸痰）以及数据收集/监测。初始评估、护理计划制定和复杂的教育是 RN 的职责。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the 'EAT' acronym for tasks an RN cannot delegate: Evaluation, Assessment, Teaching. LPNs handle stable clients with predictable outcomes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用“EAT”首字母缩略词来记忆 RN 不能委派的任务：评估 (Evaluation)、评估 (Assessment)、教学 (Teaching)。LPN 处理预后可预测的稳定患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":497,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.306.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,138],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,42],"fullStemEn":"Which actions by a nurse constitute a violation of the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士的哪些行为构成了违反《健康保险隐私及责任法案》(HIPAA)？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions by a nurse constitute a violation of the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士的哪些行为构成了违反《健康保险隐私及责任法案》(HIPAA)？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Leaving a printed laboratory report face down on the nurse's station desk","zh":"将打印的化验报告正面朝下放在护士站桌子上"},{"id":"B","en":"Reviewing the electronic health record of a client assigned to another nurse to 'learn' about an interesting case","zh":"查看分配给另一名护士的患者的电子健康档案，以“学习”一个有趣的案例"},{"id":"A","en":"Discussing a client's condition with a family member who has the client's code word","zh":"与持有患者密码的家属讨论患者的病情"},{"id":"E","en":"Posting a general update about a busy shift on a personal social media page without names","zh":"在个人社交媒体页面上发布关于班次繁忙的概括性更新，未提及姓名"},{"id":"D","en":"Giving a change-of-shift report at the client's bedside with the roommate present","zh":"在有室友在场的情况下，在患者床边进行交接班报告"},{"id":"F","en":"Sharing a computer password with a colleague who needs to document an emergency intervention","zh":"与需要记录紧急干预措施的同事分享电脑密码"}],"correct":["B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Accessing records without a professional 'need to know', failing to maintain privacy during reports (incidental disclosures should be minimized), and sharing passwords are all violations. Discussing with authorized family members is permitted. General updates on social media are risky but if truly de-identified and non-specific, they might not be HIPAA violations (though often against hospital policy). Bedside reports must protect privacy; if a roommate can overhear, it's a risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在没有专业“知情必要”的情况下访问记录、在报告期间未能保护隐私（应尽量减少偶然泄露）以及分享密码均属于违规行为。允许与获得授权的家属讨论。社交媒体上的概括性更新存在风险，但如果确实去除了身份信息且非特异性，可能不属于 HIPAA 违规（尽管通常违反医院政策）。床边报告必须保护隐私；如果室友能听到，则存在风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the 'need to know' principle. If the action isn't directly related to the care of your assigned patient or violates security protocols, it's likely a violation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注“知情必要”原则。如果行为与分配给你的患者的护理不直接相关，或违反了安全协议，则很可能是违规行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which actions by a nurse constitute a violation of the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA)?","controlSentenceZh":"护士的哪些行为构成了违反《健康保险隐私及责任法案》(HIPAA)？"}
{"queueIndex":498,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.307","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.307.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.307.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse notices that a colleague is arriving at work with an odor of alcohol and slurred speech. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士注意到一名同事上班时身上有酒味，且言语不清。护士应该采取哪些行动？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应该采取哪些行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Offer to take over the colleague's client assignments for the shift","zh":"主动承担该同事本班次的患者护理分配"},{"id":"A","en":"Confront the colleague and tell them to go home","zh":"与同事对质并告诉他们回家"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the specific observations made","zh":"记录下观察到的具体情况"},{"id":"F","en":"Notify the house supervisor if the nurse manager is unavailable","zh":"如果护士长不在，通知值班主管"},{"id":"E","en":"Wait to see if the colleague's behavior affects client care before acting","zh":"在采取行动前，先观察同事的行为是否影响了患者护理"},{"id":"B","en":"Report the observations immediately to the nurse manager","zh":"立即向护士长报告观察到的情况"}],"correct":["B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Impairment in the workplace must be reported through the chain of command immediately to ensure client safety. Documentation of objective findings is essential. The nurse should not handle the situation alone or allow the impaired colleague to provide care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"工作场所的行为受损必须立即通过指挥链报告，以确保患者安全。记录客观发现是必不可少的。护士不应单独处理这种情况，也不应允许受损的同事提供护理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first. In situations involving impairment, immediate reporting to a supervisor is the priority action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一。在涉及行为受损的情况下，立即向主管报告是首要行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":499,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.308","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.308.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.308.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,285],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,87],"fullStemEn":"The RN is supervising an LPN and a nursing assistive personnel (NAP) on a busy medical-surgical unit. A client who underwent a total hip arthroplasty 24 hours ago requires a neurovascular assessment, assistance with ambulation for the first time, and administration of pain medication.","fullStemZh":"在繁忙的内外科病房，RN 正在监督一名 LPN 和一名护理助理 (NAP)。一名 24 小时前接受了全髋关节置换术的患者需要进行神经血管评估、首次协助下床活动以及给予止痛药。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client who underwent a total hip arthroplasty 24 hours ago requires a neurovascular assessment, assistance with ambulation for the first time, and administration of pain medication.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名 24 小时前接受了全髋关节置换术的患者需要进行神经血管评估、首次协助下床活动以及给予止痛药。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The RN is supervising an LPN and a nursing assistive personnel (NAP) on a busy medical-surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在繁忙的内外科病房，RN 正在监督一名 LPN 和一名护理助理 (NAP)。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The RN should perform the {{1}} because it requires clinical judgment, while the {{2}} can be delegated to the LPN.","zh":"RN 应该执行 {{1}}，因为这需要临床判断，而 {{2}} 可以委派给 LPN。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"initial ambulation","zh":"首次下床活动"},{"id":"o3","en":"recording of intake and output","zh":"记录入量和出量"},{"id":"o2","en":"pain medication administration","zh":"止痛药给药"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"development of the mobility plan","zh":"制定活动计划"},{"id":"o2","en":"administration of oral analgesics","zh":"口服止痛药给药"},{"id":"o1","en":"neurovascular assessment","zh":"神经血管评估"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First-time ambulation after surgery is high-risk and requires the RN's assessment of stability. LPNs can administer medications to stable clients. Assessment and planning are generally RN roles.","rationaleCorrectZh":"术后首次下床活动风险较高，需要 RN 评估稳定性。LPN 可以为稳定患者给药。评估和计划通常是 RN 的职责。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify which task involves 'first time' or 'unstable' elements; these are RN tasks. Standardized, repetitive tasks for stable clients go to LPNs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别哪些任务涉及“首次”或“不稳定”要素；这些是 RN 的任务。针对稳定患者的标准化、重复性任务由 LPN 承担。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":500,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.309","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.309.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.309.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is approached by a person claiming to be the health care proxy for a client who is currently unconscious. The person asks for the results of the client's latest diagnostic tests.","fullStemZh":"一名自称是目前处于昏迷状态患者的医疗保健代理人的人找到护士，要求告知患者最新的诊断测试结果。","terminalSentenceEn":"The person asks for the results of the client's latest diagnostic tests.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名自称是目前处于昏迷状态患者的医疗保健代理人的人找到护士，要求告知患者最新的诊断测试结果。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is approached by a person claiming to be the health care proxy for a client who is currently unconscious.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Before releasing information, the nurse must first {{1}} and then {{2}}.","zh":"在泄露信息之前，护士必须首先 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"ask the physician for permission","zh":"请求医生许可"},{"id":"o1","en":"verify the person's identity","zh":"核实该人的身份"},{"id":"o3","en":"call the client's emergency contact","zh":"拨打患者的紧急联系人电话"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"wait for the client to regain consciousness","zh":"等待患者恢复意识"},{"id":"o1","en":"confirm the legal status of the proxy document","zh":"确认代理文件的法律地位"},{"id":"o2","en":"provide a full summary of the medical history","zh":"提供病史的完整摘要"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA requires verification of identity and authority before disclosing PHI. A health care proxy only has authority if the document is legally valid and the client lacks capacity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA 要求在披露 PHI 之前核实身份和权限。只有在文件具有法律效力且患者丧失行为能力的情况下，医疗保健代理人才具有权限。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In HIPAA-related questions, always prioritize verification of identity and the legal right to information.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在与 HIPAA 相关的题目中，始终优先考虑核实身份和获得信息的法律权利。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":501,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.310","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.310.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.310.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,61],"fullStemEn":"A staff nurse believes that a physician's prescribed medication dose for a pediatric client is dangerously high. The nurse contacts the physician, who insists that the dose is correct and tells the nurse to 'just give it.'","fullStemZh":"一名病房护士认为医生为儿科患者开具的药物剂量高得危险。护士联系了医生，但医生坚持认为剂量正确，并告诉护士“直接给药就行”。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse contacts the physician, who insists that the dose is correct and tells the nurse to 'just give it.'","terminalSentenceZh":"护士联系了医生，但医生坚持认为剂量正确，并告诉护士“直接给药就行”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A staff nurse believes that a physician's prescribed medication dose for a pediatric client is dangerously high.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名病房护士认为医生为儿科患者开具的药物剂量高得危险。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{1}} and then {{2}} if the issue remains unresolved.","zh":"护士应该 {{1}}，如果问题仍未解决，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"refuse to give the medication","zh":"拒绝给药"},{"id":"o3","en":"ask a colleague to give the medication","zh":"请同事给药"},{"id":"o1","en":"administer the medication as ordered","zh":"按医嘱给药"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"document that the physician was rude","zh":"记录下医生很粗鲁"},{"id":"o2","en":"call the hospital administrator","zh":"给医院行政人员打电话"},{"id":"o1","en":"notify the nursing supervisor","zh":"通知护理主管"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nurses have a legal and ethical duty to protect clients from harm. If a prescription is questioned, the nurse must not implement it if they believe it is unsafe. Following the chain of command (notifying the supervisor) is the next step to resolve the conflict.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在法律和道德上有义务保护患者免受伤害。如果对处方产生怀疑，且护士认为其不安全，则绝不能执行。遵循指挥链（通知主管）是解决冲突的下一步。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The nurse is the last line of defense against medication errors. Never give a medication you believe is unsafe, regardless of the physician's insistence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"护士是防范用药错误最后一道防线。无论医生如何坚持，绝不要给予你认为不安全的药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":502,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.311","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.311.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.311.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,108],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,31],"fullStemEn":"Which of these clients would be the most appropriate to assign to an experienced LPN? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"以下哪些患者最适合分配给经验丰富的 LPN？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of these clients would be the most appropriate to assign to an experienced LPN?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些患者最适合分配给经验丰富的 LPN？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"A client scheduled for discharge teaching later today regarding a new tracheostomy","zh":"一名预定在今天晚些时候进行关于新气管切开术出院教育的患者"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with new-onset atrial fibrillation receiving an initial diltiazem drip","zh":"一名新发房颤并正在接受初始地尔硫卓滴注的患者"},{"id":"B","en":"A client who is 2 days postoperative following a laparoscopic cholecystectomy","zh":"一名腹腔镜胆囊切除术后 2 天的患者"},{"id":"D","en":"A client with a stable stage III pressure injury requiring daily wet-to-dry dressings","zh":"一名患有稳定的 III 期压力性损伤且需要每日进行湿转干敷料更换的患者"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) requiring oxygen titrations","zh":"一名患有慢性阻塞性肺疾病 (COPD) 且需要调整氧流量的患者"},{"id":"F","en":"A client with diabetes mellitus whose blood glucose was 140 mg/dL this morning","zh":"一名今早血糖为 140 mg/dL 的糖尿病患者"}],"correct":["B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs are best assigned to clients with stable, predictable conditions. Post-op day 2, stable pressure injuries, and stable diabetes (F) are within their scope. Oxygen titration, initial IV infusions, and complex teaching (E) require the clinical judgment of an RN.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN 最适合分配给病情稳定且可预测的患者。术后第 2 天、稳定的压力性损伤 和稳定的糖尿病 (F) 属于他们的职责范围。氧流量调整、初始静脉滴注 和复杂的教学 (E) 需要 RN 的临床判断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Eliminate clients with 'newly diagnosed', 'unstable', 'acute', or 'complex' in their description. Choose the ones that are 'stable' or 'chronic'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除描述中含有“新诊断”、“不稳定”、“急性”或“复杂”字样的患者。选择那些“稳定”或“慢性”的患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":503,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.312","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.312.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.312.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,47],"fullStemEn":"Which of the following scenarios describe situations where a nurse can legally disclose confidential client information without the client's consent? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"以下哪些场景描述了护士可以在未经患者同意的情况下合法披露机密患者信息的情况？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following scenarios describe situations where a nurse can legally disclose confidential client information without the client's consent?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些场景描述了护士可以在未经患者同意的情况下合法披露机密患者信息的情况？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Reporting a colleague's suspicious behavior to the state board of nursing","zh":"向州护理委员会报告同事的可疑行为"},{"id":"A","en":"Reporting a case of suspected elder abuse to social services","zh":"向社会服务机构报告疑似虐待老年人的案例"},{"id":"C","en":"Discussing a client's history of drug use with the spouse to help them understand the diagnosis","zh":"与配偶讨论患者的吸毒史，以帮助他们理解诊断结果"},{"id":"B","en":"Sharing information with the public health department about a client with active tuberculosis","zh":"与公共卫生部门共享有关活动性肺结核患者的信息"},{"id":"D","en":"Notifying the police about a client who arrives with a gunshot wound","zh":"向警方通报一名因枪伤就医的患者"},{"id":"E","en":"Responding to a lawyer's telephone request for medical records regarding a personal injury lawsuit","zh":"回应律师关于人身伤害诉讼医疗记录的电话请求"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Legal mandates override confidentiality in cases of suspected abuse, reportable infectious diseases, and certain criminal acts (like gunshot wounds). Spouse's curiosity, legal requests without a subpoena, or reporting a colleague (which is an ethical/administrative duty but not a disclosure of client information per se) do not fit the same criteria for mandated disclosure of PHI.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在疑似虐待、法定传染病和某些犯罪行为（如枪伤）的情况下，法律授权优先于保密性。配偶的好奇心、没有传票的法律请求或报告同事（这是道德/行政义务，但本身不是披露患者信息）不符合强制披露 PHI 的标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of 'Mandatory Reporting' laws. Safety of the public or vulnerable populations (children, elderly) often takes precedence over individual privacy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"联想“强制报告”法律。公众或弱势群体（儿童、老年人）的安全往往优先于个人隐私。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":504,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.313","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.313.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.313.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,44],"fullStemEn":"A new nurse is feeling overwhelmed by the patient load and notices that several medications are being given late. The nurse wants to address this systemic issue.","fullStemZh":"一名新护士对患者负荷感到难以承受，并注意到几种药物给药延迟。护士想要解决这一系统性问题。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse wants to address this systemic issue.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士想要解决这一系统性问题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A new nurse is feeling overwhelmed by the patient load and notices that several medications are being given late.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名新护士对患者负荷感到难以承受，并注意到几种药物给药延迟。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first discuss the concern with the {{1}} and, if the workload persists, should follow the chain of command by contacting the {{2}}.","zh":"护士应首先与 {{1}} 讨论这一顾虑，如果工作负荷持续存在，应通过联系 {{2}} 来遵循指挥链。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"hospital chaplain","zh":"医院牧师"},{"id":"o1","en":"charge nurse","zh":"负责护士/组长"},{"id":"o3","en":"assigned physician","zh":"主管医生"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"board of directors","zh":"董事会"},{"id":"o1","en":"nurse manager","zh":"护士长"},{"id":"o3","en":"local news media","zh":"当地新闻媒体"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate operational issues (like workload on a shift) should be addressed first with the charge nurse. Systemic or ongoing issues are then escalated to the nurse manager.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前的运营问题（如班次的工作负荷）应首先向负责护士/组长反映。系统性或持续存在的问题随后向上级汇报给护士长。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always start with the most immediate level of supervision. In nursing, this is usually the charge nurse or team leader.","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终从最直接的主管级别开始。在护理工作中，这通常是负责护士或团队负责人。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":505,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c3_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.314","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.314.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.314.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,31],"fullStemEn":"The RN is caring for a client with a new diagnosis of diabetes. The LPN is assisting with care.","fullStemZh":"RN 正在护理一名新诊断为糖尿病的患者。LPN 正在协助护理。","terminalSentenceEn":"The LPN is assisting with care.","terminalSentenceZh":"LPN 正在协助护理。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The RN is caring for a client with a new diagnosis of diabetes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"RN 正在护理一名新诊断为糖尿病的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The LPN can be delegated the task of {{1}}, but the RN must perform the {{2}}.","zh":"可以委派 LPN 执行 {{1}} 的任务，但 RN 必须执行 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"evaluating the client's response to therapy","zh":"评估患者对治疗的反应"},{"id":"o1","en":"administering insulin","zh":"注射胰岛素"},{"id":"o2","en":"teaching insulin injection techniques","zh":"教学胰岛素注射技术"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"recording the meal intake","zh":"记录进食量"},{"id":"o2","en":"initial diabetic diet education","zh":"初始糖尿病饮食教育"},{"id":"o1","en":"fingerstick glucose monitoring","zh":"指尖血糖监测"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs can perform technical skills like insulin administration. Initial teaching and education are the responsibility of the RN.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN 可以执行胰岛素注射等技术性技能。初始教学和教育是 RN 的责任。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 'doing' (LPN) and 'teaching' (RN). Skill-based tasks are often delegable, while cognitive/educational ones are not.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“做”(LPN) 和“教”(RN)。基于技能的任务通常是可以委派的，而基于认知/教育的任务则不行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":506,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.315","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.315.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.315.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a client about preventing constipation. Which food choice by the client indicates that the teaching has been effective?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名患者提供关于预防便秘的宣教。患者的哪项食物选择表明宣教有效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which food choice by the client indicates that the teaching has been effective?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者的哪项食物选择表明宣教有效？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a client about preventing constipation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名患者提供关于预防便秘的宣教。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Cheese omelet","zh":"奶酪欧姆蛋"},{"id":"A","en":"Cooked white rice","zh":"煮熟的白米饭"},{"id":"B","en":"White bread","zh":"白面包"},{"id":"C","en":"Apple with skin","zh":"带皮苹果"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"High-fiber foods, such as fresh fruits with their skins, help promote bowel regularity and prevent constipation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高纤维食物，如带皮的新鲜水果，有助于促进肠道规律性并预防便秘。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the subject: preventing constipation. Look for the option that is highest in dietary fiber.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注主题：预防便秘。寻找膳食纤维含量最高的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":507,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.316","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.316.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.316.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,59],"fullStemEn":"A client consumes a snack containing 10 grams of fat, 20 grams of carbohydrates, and 5 grams of protein. Calculate the total number of calories provided by this snack. (Record your answer as a whole number.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者食用了一份含有10克脂肪、20克碳水化合物和5克蛋白质的零食。计算这份零食提供的总热量。（请记录为一个整数。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请记录为一个整数。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the total number of calories provided by this snack.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算这份零食提供的总热量。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"kcal","zh":"千卡"},"acceptable":["190"],"numeric":{"value":190,"tolerance":0,"unit":"kcal"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fat provides 9 kcal/g, carbohydrates provide 4 kcal/g, and protein provides 4 kcal/g. Calculation: (10g fat x 9) + (20g carb x 4) + (5g protein x 4) = 90 + 80 + 20 = 190 kcal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脂肪提供9千卡/克，碳水化合物提供4千卡/克，蛋白质提供4千卡/克。计算方法：(10克脂肪 x 9) + (20克碳水化合物 x 4) + (5克蛋白质 x 4) = 90 + 80 + 20 = 190千卡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the caloric values for macronutrients: Fat=9, Carbohydrate=4, Protein=4. Perform the multiplication and addition carefully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想宏量营养素的热量值：脂肪=9，碳水化合物=4，蛋白质=4。仔细进行乘法和加法运算。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":508,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.317","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.317.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.317.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,64],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is planning care for a client receiving palliative care. For each nursing intervention, click to specify if the intervention is primarily aimed at symptom management or end-of-life care support.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名接受姑息治疗的患者制定护理计划。对于每项护理干预措施，请点击以指明该干预措施的主要目的是症状管理还是临终关怀支持。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing intervention, click to specify if the intervention is primarily aimed at symptom management or end-of-life care support.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项护理干预措施，请点击以指明该干预措施的主要目的是症状管理还是临终关怀支持。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is planning care for a client receiving palliative care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名接受姑息治疗的患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Administering prescribed morphine for dyspnea","zh":"针对呼吸困难给予医嘱吗啡"},{"id":"r2","en":"Providing oral hygiene for a dry mouth","zh":"为口干患者提供口腔卫生护理"},{"id":"r3","en":"Facilitating a meeting with a spiritual counselor","zh":"协助安排与属灵顾问的会面"},{"id":"r4","en":"Assisting the family with funeral arrangements","zh":"协助家属处理葬礼事宜"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Symptom Management","zh":"症状管理"},{"id":"c2","en":"End-of-life Support","zh":"临终支持"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Symptom management focuses on relieving physical distress (e.g., pain, dyspnea, dry mouth). End-of-life support encompasses spiritual, emotional, and practical assistance for the client and family.","rationaleCorrectZh":"症状管理侧重于缓解身体不适（如疼痛、呼吸困难、口干）。临终支持包括为患者及其家属提供精神、情感和实际方面的协助。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between physiological needs (symptom management) and psychosocial/spiritual/practical needs (support).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分生理需求（症状管理）和心理社交/精神/实际需求（支持）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":509,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.318","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.318.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.318.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Which statement by the nurse best describes the primary goal of palliative care?","fullStemZh":"护士的哪项陈述最准确地描述了姑息治疗的主要目标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the nurse best describes the primary goal of palliative care?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项陈述最准确地描述了姑息治疗的主要目标？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The goal is to provide aggressive treatment to cure the underlying disease.","zh":"目标是提供积极的治疗以治愈原发疾病。"},{"id":"A","en":"Palliative care is only available for clients who have less than 6 months to live.","zh":"姑息治疗仅适用于预计寿命不足6个月的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"It focuses on improving quality of life by managing symptoms and providing support.","zh":"它侧重于通过管理症状和提供支持来提高生活质量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Palliative care is designed to hasten death for terminally ill clients.","zh":"姑息治疗旨在加速终末期患者的死亡。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The primary goal of palliative care is to improve the quality of life for both the client and the family by preventing and relieving suffering through early identification, assessment, and treatment of pain and other problems.","rationaleCorrectZh":"姑息治疗的主要目标是通过早期识别、评估和治疗疼痛及其他问题，预防和缓解痛苦，从而提高患者及其家属的生活质量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the answer that emphasizes quality of life and symptom management rather than cure or hastening death.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找强调生活质量和症状管理而非治愈或加速死亡的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":510,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.319","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.319.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.319.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[253,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,91],"fullStemEn":"A client is instructed to consume an additional 500 kcal per day to gain weight. If the client drinks a nutritional supplement that contains 250 kcal per 8-ounce container, how many 8-ounce containers should the client drink each day to meet this goal? (Record your answer as a whole number.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者被指示每天额外摄入500千卡热量以增加体重。如果患者饮用的营养补充剂每8盎司容器含有250千卡热量，那么患者每天应饮用多少个8盎司容器才能达到这个目标？（请记录为一个整数。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请记录为一个整数。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"If the client drinks a nutritional supplement that contains 250 kcal per 8-ounce container, how many 8-ounce containers should the client drink each day to meet this goal?","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果患者饮用的营养补充剂每8盎司容器含有250千卡热量，那么患者每天应饮用多少个8盎司容器才能达到这个目标？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"containers","zh":"容器"},"acceptable":["2"],"numeric":{"value":2,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total additional calories needed = 500 kcal. Calories per container = 250 kcal. Calculation: 500 / 250 = 2 containers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总共需要的额外热量 = 500千卡。每个容器的热量 = 250千卡。计算方法：500 / 250 = 2个容器。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the total goal and the value of one unit, then divide the goal by the unit value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定总目标和单个单位的数值，然后将总目标除以单位数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":511,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.320","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.320.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.320.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,55],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is educating a client on lifestyle modifications to prevent constipation. For each factor, click to specify if it promotes bowel regularity or increases the risk of constipation.","fullStemZh":"护士正在就预防便秘的生活方式调整对患者进行教育。对于每个因素，请点击以指明它是促进肠道规律性还是增加便秘风险。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each factor, click to specify if it promotes bowel regularity or increases the risk of constipation.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个因素，请点击以指明它是促进肠道规律性还是增加便秘风险。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is educating a client on lifestyle modifications to prevent constipation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在就预防便秘的生活方式调整对患者进行教育。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Increasing daily intake of water","zh":"增加每日饮水量"},{"id":"r2","en":"Ignoring the urge to defecate","zh":"忽视排便冲动"},{"id":"r3","en":"Engaging in regular physical exercise","zh":"进行规律的体育锻炼"},{"id":"r4","en":"Using iron supplements regularly","zh":"定期服用铁补充剂"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Promotes Regularity","zh":"促进规律性"},{"id":"c2","en":"Increases Risk","zh":"增加风险"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hydration and exercise stimulate peristalsis and promote regularity. Ignoring the urge to defecate and certain supplements like iron can slow intestinal transit and lead to constipation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"补充水分和锻炼可刺激肠蠕动并促进规律性。忽视排便冲动和某些补充剂（如铁剂）会减慢肠道运输，导致便秘。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about factors that speed up vs. slow down the digestive system.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考加速与减慢消化系统的因素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is educating a client on lifestyle modifications to prevent constipation.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在就预防便秘的生活方式调整对患者进行教育。"}
{"queueIndex":512,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.321","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.321.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.321.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,37],"fullStemEn":"A client asks the nurse which macronutrient provides the most energy per gram. Which response by the nurse is correct?","fullStemZh":"一名患者询问护士哪种宏量营养素每克提供的能量最多。护士的哪项回答是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项回答是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client asks the nurse which macronutrient provides the most energy per gram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者询问护士哪种宏量营养素每克提供的能量最多。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Carbohydrates","zh":"碳水化合物"},{"id":"D","en":"Fats","zh":"脂肪"},{"id":"C","en":"Vitamins","zh":"维生素"},{"id":"A","en":"Proteins","zh":"蛋白质"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fats are the most energy-dense macronutrient, providing 9 calories per gram, compared to 4 calories per gram for carbohydrates and proteins.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脂肪是能量密度最高的宏量营养素，每克提供9卡路里，而碳水化合物和蛋白质每克提供4卡路里。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare the known caloric values: 4, 4, and 9.","testTakingStrategyZh":"比较已知的热量值：4、4和9。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":513,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.322","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.322.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.322.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is encouraging an older adult client to increase fluid intake to prevent constipation. Unless contraindicated, what is the generally recommended daily fluid intake for an adult?","fullStemZh":"护士正在鼓励一名老年患者增加液体摄入量以预防便秘。除非有禁忌症，通常建议成年人每日摄入多少液体？","terminalSentenceEn":"Unless contraindicated, what is the generally recommended daily fluid intake for an adult?","terminalSentenceZh":"除非有禁忌症，通常建议成年人每日摄入多少液体？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is encouraging an older adult client to increase fluid intake to prevent constipation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在鼓励一名老年患者增加液体摄入量以预防便秘。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"1,000 to 1,500 mL","zh":"1,000至1,500毫升"},{"id":"B","en":"2,000 to 3,000 mL","zh":"2,000至3,000毫升"},{"id":"D","en":"500 to 1,000 mL","zh":"500至1,000毫升"},{"id":"C","en":"4,000 to 5,000 mL","zh":"4,000至5,000毫升"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To maintain adequate hydration and promote soft stools, an intake of 2,000 to 3,000 mL of fluid per day is generally recommended for most adults.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为了保持充足的水分并促进软便，通常建议大多数成年人每天摄入2,000至3,000毫升液体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the option that represents a standard, moderate range for adult fluid intake.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择代表成年人液体摄入标准中等范围的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":514,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.323","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.323.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.323.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is explaining the differences between palliative care and hospice care to a family. For each characteristic, click to specify if it applies to palliative care, hospice care, or both.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向家属解释姑息治疗和临终关怀之间的区别。对于每项特征，请点击以指明它适用于姑息治疗、临终关怀还是两者都适用。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each characteristic, click to specify if it applies to palliative care, hospice care, or both.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项特征，请点击以指明它适用于姑息治疗、临终关怀还是两者都适用。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is explaining the differences between palliative care and hospice care to a family.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向家属解释姑息治疗和临终关怀之间的区别。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Focuses on symptom management and quality of life","zh":"侧重于症状管理和生活质量"},{"id":"r2","en":"Can be provided concurrently with curative treatment","zh":"可以与治愈性治疗同时进行"},{"id":"r3","en":"Client is generally expected to have 6 months or less to live","zh":"患者通常预期寿命在6个月或以下"},{"id":"r4","en":"Provides support for the client's family","zh":"为患者家属提供支持"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Hospice Care Only","zh":"仅限临终关怀"},{"id":"c3","en":"Both","zh":"两者皆是"},{"id":"c1","en":"Palliative Care Only","zh":"仅限姑息治疗"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Both palliative and hospice care focus on quality of life and family support. Palliative care can start at diagnosis and continue during curative treatment, while hospice care is typically for those with a terminal prognosis of 6 months or less who are no longer seeking a cure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"姑息治疗和临终关怀都侧重于生活质量和家庭支持。姑息治疗可以在诊断时开始并在治愈性治疗期间继续，而临终关怀通常针对那些预期寿命在6个月或以下且不再寻求治愈的终末期患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that hospice is a specific type of palliative care for the end of life, while palliative care is broader.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想临终关怀是针对生命终结的一种特定类型的姑息治疗，而姑息治疗的范围更广。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":515,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c4_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.324","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.324.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.324.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[183,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,68],"fullStemEn":"A client's daily energy requirement is 2,400 kcal. If the client wants to consume 25% of their total daily calories at breakfast, how many calories should they consume for breakfast? (Record your answer as a whole number.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者的每日能量需求为2,400千卡。如果患者希望在早餐时摄入每日总热量的25%，那么他们早餐应该摄入多少热量？（请记录为一个整数。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请记录为一个整数。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"If the client wants to consume 25% of their total daily calories at breakfast, how many calories should they consume for breakfast?","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果患者希望在早餐时摄入每日总热量的25%，那么他们早餐应该摄入多少热量？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"kcal","zh":"千卡"},"acceptable":["600"],"numeric":{"value":600,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To find 25% of 2,400, multiply 2,400 by 0.25. Calculation: 2,400 x 0.25 = 600 kcal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"要计算2,400的25%，将2,400乘以0.25。计算方法：2,400 x 0.25 = 600千卡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert the percentage to a decimal (25% = 0.25) and multiply by the total value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将百分比转换为小数（25% = 0.25）并乘以总数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":516,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.325","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.325.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.325.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing discharge instructions to a client who is scheduled for a colonoscopy. Which instruction regarding the clear liquid diet is correct?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名预定进行结肠镜检查的患者提供出院指导。关于清流质饮食的哪项指导是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction regarding the clear liquid diet is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"关于清流质饮食的哪项指导是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing discharge instructions to a client who is scheduled for a colonoscopy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名预定进行结肠镜检查的患者提供出院指导。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Red or purple gelatin should be avoided.","zh":"应避免食用红色或紫色的明胶（果冻）。"},{"id":"D","en":"The clear liquid diet should begin 4 hours before the procedure.","zh":"清流质饮食应在检查前4小时开始。"},{"id":"B","en":"Milk and cream are permitted in coffee.","zh":"咖啡中允许加入牛奶和奶油。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client may consume orange juice with pulp.","zh":"患者可以饮用带有果肉的橙汁。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Red, purple, or orange dyes in liquids or gelatin can be mistaken for blood during the colonoscopy and should be avoided.","rationaleCorrectZh":"液体或明胶中的红色、紫色或橙色染料在结肠镜检查期间可能被误认为出血，因此应避免使用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the goal of colonoscopy: a clear view of the colon. Avoid anything that could add residue or mimic blood.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注结肠镜检查的目标：清晰地观察结肠。避免任何可能增加残留物或模仿血液的东西。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":517,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.326","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.326.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.326.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,46],"fullStemEn":"A 52-year-old client reports having irregular menstrual cycles and frequent hot flashes. Which physiological change associated with menopause should the nurse explain to the client?","fullStemZh":"一名52岁的患者报告月经周期不规律且频繁出现潮热。护士应向患者解释哪项与绝经相关的生理变化？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which physiological change associated with menopause should the nurse explain to the client?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应向患者解释哪项与绝经相关的生理变化？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 52-year-old client reports having irregular menstrual cycles and frequent hot flashes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名52岁的患者报告月经周期不规律且频繁出现潮热。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Decrease in follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) levels.","zh":"促卵泡激素 (FSH) 水平下降。"},{"id":"C","en":"Increased production of estrogen by the ovaries.","zh":"卵巢分泌雌激素增加。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increased thickness of the vaginal mucosa.","zh":"阴道粘膜厚度增加。"},{"id":"D","en":"Cessation of ovarian function and decreased estrogen levels.","zh":"卵巢功能停止且雌激素水平下降。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Menopause is characterized by the permanent cessation of ovarian function, leading to a significant decrease in estrogen and progesterone levels.","rationaleCorrectZh":"绝经的特征是卵巢功能的永久性停止，导致雌激素和孕激素水平显著下降。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the endocrine changes in menopause: ovaries stop working, so 'downstream' hormones (estrogen) decrease and 'upstream' hormones (FSH) increase.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想绝经期的内分泌变化：卵巢停止工作，因此“下游”激素（雌激素）减少，“上游”激素（FSH）增加。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":518,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.327","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.327.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.327.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,71],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing education to a group of women about breast cancer screening. According to standard guidelines for average-risk women, at what age should annual mammography typically be offered or recommended?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一群女性提供关于乳腺癌筛查的教育。根据针对一般风险女性的标准指南，通常应在什么年龄提供或建议进行每年一次的乳腺 X 线摄影（乳靶）？","terminalSentenceEn":"According to standard guidelines for average-risk women, at what age should annual mammography typically be offered or recommended?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据针对一般风险女性的标准指南，通常应在什么年龄提供或建议进行每年一次的乳腺 X 线摄影（乳靶）？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing education to a group of women about breast cancer screening.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一群女性提供关于乳腺癌筛查的教育。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Age 21","zh":"21岁"},{"id":"D","en":"Age 30","zh":"30岁"},{"id":"C","en":"Age 65","zh":"65岁"},{"id":"B","en":"Age 45","zh":"45岁"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Many guidelines, including those from the American Cancer Society, recommend that women with an average risk for breast cancer should start annual mammograms at age 45, with the option to start as early as age 40.","rationaleCorrectZh":"许多指南（包括美国癌症协会的指南）建议，乳腺癌一般风险的女性应在45岁开始每年进行一次乳腺 X 线摄影，并可选择早在40岁开始。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between different cancer screenings (Breast vs. Cervical vs. Colorectal) and their respective starting ages.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分不同的癌症筛查（乳腺癌、宫颈癌、结直肠癌）及其各自的开始年龄。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":519,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.328","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.328.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.328.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,49],"fullStemEn":"A client is preparing for a colonoscopy tomorrow morning. Place the preparation actions in the correct order from the day before through the morning of the procedure.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在为明天早上的结肠镜检查做准备。请将从检查前一天到检查当天早晨的准备措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the preparation actions in the correct order from the day before through the morning of the procedure.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将从检查前一天到检查当天早晨的准备措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is preparing for a colonoscopy tomorrow morning.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者正在为明天早上的结肠镜检查做准备。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Begin the second portion 4 to 6 hours before the colonoscopy and finish it at least 2 hours before the procedure.","zh":"在结肠镜检查前4至6小时开始服用第二部分，并至少在检查前2小时完成。"},{"id":"B","en":"Take the first portion of the prescribed polyethylene glycol (PEG) bowel preparation in the evening.","zh":"在傍晚服用处方聚乙二醇 (PEG) 肠道准备液的第一部分。"},{"id":"A","en":"Consume only clear liquids throughout the day.","zh":"全天仅进食清流质。"},{"id":"D","en":"Maintain a low-residue diet for breakfast.","zh":"早餐保持低残渣饮食。"}],"correct":["D","A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For a routine morning colonoscopy, the client may have a low-residue breakfast followed by the prescribed clear-liquid plan. The first portion of a split-dose preparation is taken in the evening. The second portion begins 4 to 6 hours before colonoscopy and is completed at least 2 hours before the procedure, unless individualized instructions require a different schedule.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于常规上午结肠镜检查，患者可先吃低残渣早餐，随后遵循处方清流质计划。分次肠道准备液的第一部分在傍晚服用。第二部分在检查前4至6小时开始，并至少在检查前2小时完成，除非个体化医嘱要求其他时间安排。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a morning colonoscopy, look for a day-before diet followed by an evening dose and a timed morning dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于上午结肠镜检查，应寻找检查前一天的饮食安排、傍晚剂量和定时的晨间剂量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":520,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.329","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.329.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.329.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing health teaching to a perimenopausal client. Which symptoms or risks associated with the decline in estrogen levels should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名围绝经期患者提供健康教育。护士应纳入哪些与雌激素水平下降相关的症状或风险？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which symptoms or risks associated with the decline in estrogen levels should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应纳入哪些与雌激素水平下降相关的症状或风险？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Increased risk of cardiovascular disease","zh":"心血管疾病风险增加"},{"id":"A","en":"Increased risk of osteoporosis","zh":"骨质疏松风险增加"},{"id":"E","en":"Sleep disturbances and night sweats","zh":"睡眠障碍和夜间盗汗"},{"id":"B","en":"Vaginal dryness and dyspareunia","zh":"阴道干燥和性交疼痛"},{"id":"D","en":"Decreased levels of LDL cholesterol","zh":"低密度脂蛋白 (LDL) 胆固醇水平降低"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Decline in estrogen leads to bone loss (osteoporosis), vaginal atrophy (dryness/pain), loss of cardioprotective effects (increased CV risk), and vasomotor symptoms (night sweats/sleep issues). LDL cholesterol typically increases, not decreases, after menopause.","rationaleCorrectZh":"雌激素下降会导致骨丢失（骨质疏松）、阴道萎缩（干燥/疼痛）、心脏保护作用丧失（心血管风险增加）以及血管舒缩症状（夜间盗汗/睡眠问题）。绝经后 LDL 胆固醇通常会增加而非减少。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the widespread effects of estrogen on various body systems (Skeletal, Reproductive, Cardiovascular, Neurological).","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考雌激素对各种身体系统（骨骼、生殖、心血管、神经）的广泛影响。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":521,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.330","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.330.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.330.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,48],"fullStemEn":"A 50-year-old male client with an average risk of colorectal cancer asks the nurse about screening options. Which screening schedule is currently recommended for this client?","fullStemZh":"一名具有一般结直肠癌风险的50岁男性患者询问护士关于筛查的选择。目前建议该患者采取哪项筛查计划？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which screening schedule is currently recommended for this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"目前建议该患者采取哪项筛查计划？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 50-year-old male client with an average risk of colorectal cancer asks the nurse about screening options.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名具有一般结直肠癌风险的50岁男性患者询问护士关于筛查的选择。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Colonoscopy every 10 years.","zh":"每10年进行一次结肠镜检查。"},{"id":"B","en":"Colonoscopy every 5 years.","zh":"每5年进行一次结肠镜检查。"},{"id":"D","en":"Flexible sigmoidoscopy every 10 years.","zh":"每10年进行一次乙状结肠镜检查。"},{"id":"C","en":"Fecal occult blood test (FOBT) every 3 years.","zh":"每3年进行一次粪便隐血试验 (FOBT)。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For average-risk individuals, a colonoscopy every 10 years is a gold standard screening recommendation, starting at age 45 (recently lowered from 50).","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于一般风险的个体，每10年进行一次结肠镜检查是金标准筛查建议，从45岁开始（最近从50岁降低）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the '10' for colonoscopy and the '1' for annual stool tests.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住结肠镜检查的“10”和年度粪便检查的“1”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":522,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.331","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.331.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.331.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,55],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is instructing a client on dietary restrictions for 2 to 3 days prior to a colonoscopy. Which foods should the client be advised to avoid to ensure a low-residue preparation? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导患者在结肠镜检查前2至3天的饮食限制。应建议患者避免食用哪些食物以确保低残渣准备？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which foods should the client be advised to avoid to ensure a low-residue preparation?","penultimateSentenceZh":"应建议患者避免食用哪些食物以确保低残渣准备？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Roasted chicken (skinless)","zh":"烤鸡肉（去皮）"},{"id":"C","en":"Raw vegetables","zh":"生蔬菜"},{"id":"B","en":"White rice","zh":"白米饭"},{"id":"D","en":"Nuts and seeds","zh":"坚果和种子"},{"id":"A","en":"Whole-grain breads","zh":"全麦面包"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A low-residue diet avoids high-fiber foods that leave significant waste in the colon. This includes whole grains, raw fruits and vegetables, and nuts/seeds. White rice and skinless chicken are considered low-residue and are typically permitted.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低残渣饮食会避免在结肠中留下大量废物的多纤维食物。这包括全谷物、生水果和蔬菜以及坚果/种子。白米饭和去皮鸡肉被认为是低残渣的，通常是允许的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify high-fiber/high-residue foods vs. low-fiber/refined foods. The goal is to minimize what stays in the gut.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分高纤维/高残渣食物与低纤维/精制食物。目标是尽量减少留在肠道内的东西。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":523,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.332","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.332.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.332.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,52],"fullStemEn":"A menopausal client with an intact uterus is considering hormone replacement therapy (HRT). Which statement by the nurse best reflects current safety recommendations for this client?","fullStemZh":"一名子宫完整的绝经期患者正在考虑激素替代疗法 (HRT)。护士的哪项陈述最能反映该患者目前的安全性建议？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the nurse best reflects current safety recommendations for this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项陈述最能反映该患者目前的安全性建议？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A menopausal client with an intact uterus is considering hormone replacement therapy (HRT).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名子宫完整的绝经期患者正在考虑激素替代疗法 (HRT)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Estrogen-only therapy is the safest option for you.","zh":"单用雌激素疗法对你来说是最安全的选择。"},{"id":"A","en":"You will need a combination of estrogen and progestin to protect your uterine lining.","zh":"你需要联合使用雌激素和孕激素来保护你的子宫内膜。"},{"id":"C","en":"HRT has no risks and can be taken indefinitely for anti-aging.","zh":"HRT 没有风险，可以无限期服用以抗衰老。"},{"id":"B","en":"Progestin is only needed if you have had a hysterectomy.","zh":"只有在你做过子宫切除术的情况下才需要孕激素。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For women with an intact uterus, estrogen must be combined with progestin (combined HRT) to prevent endometrial hyperplasia and reduce the risk of endometrial cancer.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于子宫完整的女性，雌激素必须与孕激素联合使用（联合 HRT），以预防子宫内膜增生并降低子宫内膜癌的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: No Uterus = Estrogen alone OK; Uterus Present = Must have Progestin (to protect it).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：无子宫 = 单独使用雌激素可以；有子宫 = 必须使用孕激素（以保护它）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":524,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.333","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.333.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.333.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,46],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing screening requirements for a 25-year-old female client. Which screening tests are generally recommended for this age group? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名25岁女性患者的筛查要求。通常建议该年龄段进行哪些筛查测试？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which screening tests are generally recommended for this age group?","penultimateSentenceZh":"通常建议该年龄段进行哪些筛查测试？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Cervical cancer screening (Pap smear) every 3 years","zh":"每3年进行一次宫颈癌筛查（宫颈抹片检查）"},{"id":"C","en":"Blood pressure screening every 3 to 5 years if prior readings are normal and no increased risk is present","zh":"若既往血压正常且无高血压风险增加因素，每3至5年筛查一次血压"},{"id":"E","en":"Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening if increased-risk factors are present","zh":"若存在风险增加因素，进行衣原体和淋病筛查"},{"id":"B","en":"Annual mammography","zh":"年度乳腺 X 线摄影"},{"id":"D","en":"Colonoscopy","zh":"结肠镜检查"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cervical cytology every 3 years is appropriate at age 25. For adults ages 18 to 39 with prior normal blood pressure and no increased risk, screening every 3 to 5 years may be appropriate; annual screening is used for increased risk. At age 25, chlamydia and gonorrhea screening is recommended when increased-risk factors are present. Average-risk mammography and colorectal screening begin later.","rationaleCorrectZh":"25岁时每3年进行一次宫颈细胞学筛查是适当的。对于18至39岁、既往血压正常且无风险增加因素的成年人，每3至5年筛查一次可能适当；风险增加者应每年筛查。25岁及以上女性存在风险增加因素时，建议进行衣原体和淋病筛查。一般风险人群的乳腺癌和结直肠癌筛查起始年龄更晚。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on screenings appropriate for young adulthood vs. middle/older age.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注适合年轻人与中年人/老年人的筛查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":525,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c5_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.334","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.334.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.334.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,43],"fullStemEn":"A client is in the recovery area following a colonoscopy with sedation. Which finding should the nurse prioritize for immediate reporting to the healthcare provider?","fullStemZh":"一名患者在接受镇静下的结肠镜检查后正在恢复区。护士应优先向医疗服务提供者报告哪项发现？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding should the nurse prioritize for immediate reporting to the healthcare provider?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先向医疗服务提供者报告哪项发现？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is in the recovery area following a colonoscopy with sedation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在接受镇静下的结肠镜检查后正在恢复区。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Abdominal distension with rebound tenderness and guarding.","zh":"腹部膨隆伴反跳痛和肌紧张。"},{"id":"D","en":"A small amount of bright red blood on the toilet tissue after the first bowel movement.","zh":"第一次排便后，厕纸上有少量鲜红色血液。"},{"id":"B","en":"Client reports abdominal cramping and flatulence.","zh":"患者报告腹部绞痛和排气（放屁）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Drowsiness and difficulty following complex commands.","zh":"昏昏欲睡且难以执行复杂指令。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abdominal distension, rebound tenderness, and guarding are signs of bowel perforation, a serious complication of colonoscopy that requires immediate intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"腹部膨隆、反跳痛和肌紧张是肠穿孔的迹象，肠穿孔是结肠镜检查的严重并发症，需要立即干预。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify life-threatening complications (Perforation) vs. expected post-procedure side effects (Gas, drowsiness).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别危及生命的并发症（穿孔）与预期的术后副作用（排气、昏睡）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":526,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.335","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.335.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.335.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is cleaning a medical instrument with a caustic chemical solution when some of the liquid splashes into the nurse's right eye. What is the immediate priority action?","fullStemZh":"护士在用腐蚀性化学溶液清洗医疗器械时，部分液体溅入护士的右眼。眼下的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the immediate priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"眼下的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is cleaning a medical instrument with a caustic chemical solution when some of the liquid splashes into the nurse's right eye.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在用腐蚀性化学溶液清洗医疗器械时，部分液体溅入护士的右眼。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Flush the eye with lukewarm water or saline for at least 15 minutes.","zh":"用温水或生理盐水冲洗眼睛至少15分钟。"},{"id":"D","en":"Patch the eye and report to the emergency department.","zh":"包扎眼睛并前往急诊室。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call for assistance to the nearest eyewash station.","zh":"呼叫寻求帮助并前往最近的洗眼站。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the occupational health department.","zh":"通知职业健康部门。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate irrigation of the eye is the priority following a chemical splash to minimize tissue damage and prevent permanent vision loss.","rationaleCorrectZh":"化学品溅入眼睛后，立即冲洗眼睛是首要任务，以尽量减少组织损伤并防止永久性视力丧失。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABCs and 'First' priority. In a chemical exposure, removal of the agent (irrigation) is the most immediate life/organ-saving action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用ABC原则和“首要”优先级。在化学品暴露中，清除病原（冲洗）是最紧急的生命/器官营救行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":527,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.336","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.336.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.336.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse in the endoscopy unit experiences a chemical splash to the face. The nurse must perform an emergency eye irrigation at the eyewash station. Place the following steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"内窥镜室的一名护士面部受到化学品飞溅。护士必须在洗眼站进行紧急眼部冲洗。请按正确顺序排列以下步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列以下步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse must perform an emergency eye irrigation at the eyewash station.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士必须在洗眼站进行紧急眼部冲洗。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Activate the eyewash station to start the flow of water.","zh":"启动洗眼站以开始出水。"},{"id":"E","en":"Flush for a minimum of 15 to 20 minutes.","zh":"冲洗至少15到20分钟。"},{"id":"B","en":"Position the head so the eye is in the stream of water.","zh":"调整头部位置，使眼睛处于水流中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Roll the eye around while flushing to ensure thorough irrigation.","zh":"冲洗时转动眼球，以确保彻底冲洗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hold the eyelids open with the thumb and index finger.","zh":"用拇指和食指撑开眼睑。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence starts with activating the water, positioning the eye, holding it open, ensuring coverage by moving the eye, and maintaining irrigation for the recommended duration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的顺序是从启动水源开始，定位眼睛，撑开眼睑，通过移动眼球确保覆盖，并维持建议时长的冲洗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize the mechanical process of using an eyewash station. You must have water first before you can position and flush.","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象使用洗眼站的机械过程。你必须先有水，然后才能定位和冲洗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":528,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.337","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.337.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.337.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,89],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for a client with suspected Ebola Virus Disease (EVD). For each PPE item or action, indicate whether it is required or not required according to CDC guidelines for EVD for healthcare workers in stable clinical settings.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备护理一名疑似埃博拉病毒病（EVD）患者。对于每项个人防护装备（PPE）项目或行动，请根据CDC针对临床环境稳定状态下医护人员的EVD指南，指出是“需要”还是“不需要”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each PPE item or action, indicate whether it is required or not required according to CDC guidelines for EVD for healthcare workers in stable clinical settings.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项个人防护装备（PPE）项目或行动，请根据CDC针对临床环境稳定状态下医护人员的EVD指南，指出是“需要”还是“不需要”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for a client with suspected Ebola Virus Disease (EVD).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备护理一名疑似埃博拉病毒病（EVD）患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"N95 respirator or powered air-purifying respirator (PAPR)","zh":"N95呼吸器或动力送风过滤式呼吸器 (PAPR)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Double gloves with extended cuffs","zh":"带加长袖口的双层手套"},{"id":"r3","en":"Single-use fluid-impermeable gown","zh":"一次性不透液隔离衣"},{"id":"r4","en":"Boot covers that extend to at least mid-calf","zh":"延伸至至少小腿中部的靴套"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not Required","zh":"不需要"},{"id":"c1","en":"Required","zh":"需要"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ebola precautions require specialized PPE including respiratory protection, double gloves, fluid-impermeable gowns, and boot covers to prevent contact with infectious body fluids.","rationaleCorrectZh":"埃博拉预防措施需要专门的PPE，包括呼吸防护、双层手套、不透液隔离衣和靴套，以防止接触具有传染性的体液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that Ebola requires extreme protection beyond standard contact/droplet. Every part of the body must be covered.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住埃博拉需要超出标准接触/飞沫预防的极端保护。身体的每个部位都必须被覆盖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":529,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.338","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.338.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.338.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,48],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is doffing PPE after providing care to a client with Ebola virus disease. Place the doffing steps in the correct order according to standard high-consequence pathogen protocols.","fullStemZh":"护士在护理完埃博拉病毒病患者后正在脱去PPE。请根据标准高后果病原体方案按正确顺序排列脱卸步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the doffing steps in the correct order according to standard high-consequence pathogen protocols.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据标准高后果病原体方案按正确顺序排列脱卸步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is doffing PPE after providing care to a client with Ebola virus disease.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在护理完埃博拉病毒病患者后正在脱去PPE。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Remove respiratory protection and face shield.","zh":"脱去呼吸防护装置和面罩。"},{"id":"A","en":"Inspect for visible contamination and disinfect outer gloves.","zh":"检查是否有可见污染并对外层手套进行消毒。"},{"id":"C","en":"Remove gown or coverall with the assistance of a trained observer.","zh":"在经过培训的观察员协助下脱去隔离衣或防护服。"},{"id":"E","en":"Perform final hand hygiene.","zh":"进行最后的手部卫生。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove outer gloves and inspect inner gloves.","zh":"脱去外层手套并检查内层手套。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The doffing sequence for Ebola is highly structured, starting with disinfection of the most contaminated items (outer gloves), moving to the suit, and finishing with respiratory protection and hand hygiene.","rationaleCorrectZh":"埃博拉的脱卸顺序是高度结构化的，从对污染最严重的物品（外层手套）进行消毒开始，接着是防护服，最后是呼吸防护和手部卫生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the goal is to remove the most contaminated items first while protecting the mucosal surfaces (eyes, nose, mouth) until the very end.","testTakingStrategyZh":"请记住，目标是首先脱去污染最严重的物品，同时保护粘膜表面（眼、鼻、口）直到最后。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":530,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.339","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.339.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.339.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,34],"fullStemEn":"A client with confirmed Ebola virus disease is being admitted. Which room assignment and environmental control is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一名确诊埃博拉病毒病的患者正在入院。哪种病房分配和环境控制最为合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which room assignment and environmental control is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种病房分配和环境控制最为合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with confirmed Ebola virus disease is being admitted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名确诊埃博拉病毒病的患者正在入院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A semi-private room with another client confirmed with Ebola.","zh":"与其他埃博拉确诊患者共用的半私立病房。"},{"id":"C","en":"A private room with an ante-room and a dedicated bathroom.","zh":"带前室和专用浴室的单人病房。"},{"id":"D","en":"A standard private room with a portable HEPA filter system.","zh":"配备便携式HEPA过滤系统的标准单人病房。"},{"id":"A","en":"A room in the intensive care unit with the door kept open to ensure visibility.","zh":"重症监护室中的病房，门保持打开以确保可见度。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Patients with Ebola must be in a private room with a private bathroom and ideally an ante-room to facilitate safe PPE donning and doffing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"埃博拉患者必须安置在带私人浴室的单人病房中，理想情况下还应有一个前室，以方便安全地穿戴和脱卸PPE。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the intensity of isolation. Ebola is a high-consequence pathogen requiring the highest level of environmental control.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑隔离的强度。埃博拉是一种高后果病原体，需要最高级别的环境控制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":531,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.340","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.340.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.340.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,54],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is becoming increasingly agitated and begins to pace the hallway, shouting at staff. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名越来越焦虑不安的患者，该患者开始在走廊里踱步并对工作人员大声叫喊。护士首先应该采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应该采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is becoming increasingly agitated and begins to pace the hallway, shouting at staff.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名越来越焦虑不安的患者，该患者开始在走廊里踱步并对工作人员大声叫喊。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Provide the client with clear, short instructions in a calm, non-threatening voice.","zh":"以冷静、无威胁的语气向患者提供清晰、简短的指示。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request an order for a PRN intramuscular sedative.","zh":"请求开具一项PRN肌肉注射镇静剂的医嘱。"},{"id":"C","en":"Call for security to initiate a 'Code Gray' for behavioral emergency.","zh":"呼叫安保人员启动针对行为紧急情况的“灰色代码”。"},{"id":"A","en":"Instruct the client to go to their room immediately and stay there.","zh":"指示患者立即回到房间并待在那里。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"De-escalation using verbal communication is the first-line intervention for an agitated client to prevent the escalation to physical violence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于焦虑不安的患者，使用言语沟通进行降温是第一线干预措施，以防止升级为肢体暴力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the least restrictive intervention first. Verbal de-escalation is less restrictive than medications or security calls.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先寻找约束性最小的干预措施。言语降温比药物治疗或安保呼叫的约束性更小。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":532,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.341","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.341.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.341.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,64],"fullStemEn":"A nurse manager is evaluating the unit's environment for potential safety hazards that could contribute to workplace violence. For each environmental factor, classify it as a protective factor or a risk factor for staff safety.","fullStemZh":"护士长正在评估病房环境中可能导致职场暴力的潜在安全隐患。对于每个环境因素，请将其分类为医护人员安全的“保护因素”或“风险因素”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each environmental factor, classify it as a protective factor or a risk factor for staff safety.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个环境因素，请将其分类为医护人员安全的“保护因素”或“风险因素”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse manager is evaluating the unit's environment for potential safety hazards that could contribute to workplace violence.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士长正在评估病房环境中可能导致职场暴力的潜在安全隐患。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Brightly lit, open nursing stations with visibility to the unit.","zh":"光线充足、视野开阔且能观察到病房情况的护士站。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Unrestricted access to patient care areas by the general public.","zh":"普通公众可以无限制地进入患者护理区域。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Presence of functional panic buttons at nursing stations.","zh":"护士站配有功能正常的紧急报警按钮。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Wait times exceeding 4 hours in the emergency department triage.","zh":"急诊分诊台的等待时间超过4小时。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Protective Factor","zh":"保护因素"},{"id":"c2","en":"Risk Factor","zh":"风险因素"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Visibility and emergency communication tools are protective, while lack of access control and long wait times (which increase frustration) are known risk factors for workplace violence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可见性和紧急通讯工具具有保护作用，而缺乏准入控制和漫长的等待时间（会增加挫败感）是已知的职场暴力风险因素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Determine if each factor increases security or increases the likelihood of a stressful, uncontrolled environment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断每个因素是增加了安全性，还是增加了一个压力大、不受控制的环境的可能性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":533,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.342","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.342.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.342.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[163,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is conducting a home health visit. During the assessment, the client's family member becomes verbally abusive and starts throwing objects across the room. What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"护士正在进行家庭访视。在评估过程中，患者家属开始进行言语辱骂并开始在房间里乱扔东西。护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During the assessment, the client's family member becomes verbally abusive and starts throwing objects across the room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在评估过程中，患者家属开始进行言语辱骂并开始在房间里乱扔东西。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Call the local police department immediately from the home.","zh":"立即从家中拨打当地警察局电话。"},{"id":"D","en":"Exit the home immediately and go to a safe location.","zh":"立即离开家并前往安全地点。"},{"id":"A","en":"Attempt to de-escalate the family member's anger.","zh":"尝试缓解家属的愤怒情绪。"},{"id":"B","en":"Document the behavior and report the incident to the supervisor.","zh":"记录该行为并向主管报告该事件。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In a home health setting, the nurse has limited backup. If a situation becomes violent, the priority is to ensure personal safety by leaving immediately.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在家庭健康设置中，护士的后援有限。如果情况变得暴力，首要任务是通过立即离开来确保人身安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety is always the priority. In the community, if you cannot control the environment and it becomes unsafe, you must remove yourself from it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全始终是第一位的。在社区中，如果你无法控制环境且环境变得不安全，你必须离开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":534,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.343","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.343.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.343.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,55],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing safety protocols for managing accidental exposure to hazardous chemicals. For each action listed, classify it as an immediate priority action or a secondary action.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查处理意外接触危险化学品的安全协议。对于列出的每项行动，请将其分类为“紧急首要行动”或“次要行动”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each action listed, classify it as an immediate priority action or a secondary action.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于列出的每项行动，请将其分类为“紧急首要行动”或“次要行动”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is reviewing safety protocols for managing accidental exposure to hazardous chemicals.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查处理意外接触危险化学品的安全协议。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Flush the affected area with large amounts of water.","zh":"用大量水冲洗受影响区域。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Remove contaminated clothing and jewelry.","zh":"脱去受污染的衣服和首饰。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Locate and review the Safety Data Sheet (SDS) for the specific chemical.","zh":"查找并查看特定化学品的安全数据表 (SDS)。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Complete an incident report and notify the supervisor.","zh":"填写事故报告并通知主管。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Immediate Priority Action","zh":"紧急首要行动"},{"id":"c2","en":"Secondary Action","zh":"次要行动"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Decontamination (flushing and removing clothing) must occur immediately to stop the chemical action. Documentation and SDS review occur after initial life-saving steps.","rationaleCorrectZh":"必须立即进行去污（冲洗和脱去衣服）以停止化学作用。记录和SDS审查在最初的救命步骤之后进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that removing the hazard from the body is always the first step in any exposure scenario.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住，在任何暴露场景中，从身上移除危险源始终是第一步。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":535,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c6_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.344.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to transport laboratory specimens from a client with confirmed Ebola virus disease. Which action is essential for safe transport within the facility?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备运送一名确诊埃博拉病毒病患者的实验室标本。在设施内安全运送哪项行动是必不可少的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is essential for safe transport within the facility?","terminalSentenceZh":"在设施内安全运送哪项行动是必不可少的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to transport laboratory specimens from a client with confirmed Ebola virus disease.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备运送一名确诊埃博拉病毒病患者的实验室标本。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Place the primary specimen container in a single leak-proof biohazard bag.","zh":"将主标本容器放在一个防漏的生物危害袋中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Place the primary container in a leak-proof secondary container for transport.","zh":"将主容器放在防漏的辅助容器中进行运送。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hand-carry the specimens directly to the lab while wearing full PPE.","zh":"穿戴整套PPE，将标本直接手提送到实验室。"},{"id":"C","en":"Use the hospital's pneumatic tube system for rapid delivery to the lab.","zh":"使用医院的气动管道系统快速送往实验室。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Specimens from Ebola patients must be double-contained (primary container inside a leak-proof secondary container) and hand-carried to the lab; pneumatic tubes are prohibited to prevent aerosolization risk in case of breakage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"埃博拉患者的标本必须双重封装（主容器放在防漏的辅助容器内）并由人手提送到实验室；禁止使用气动管道，以防止在破裂情况下产生气溶胶风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on environmental safety. In high-risk infections, double-containment and preventing aerosolization are key principles.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注环境安全。在高风险感染中，双重封装和防止气溶胶化是关键原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":536,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.345","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.345.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.345.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[176,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,57],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is taking lithium carbonate 600 mg twice daily. The client reports experiencing persistent thirst, frequent urination, and a slight hand tremor. Which nursing action is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一名患有双相情感障碍的患者每天两次服用600毫克碳酸锂。患者报告出现持续口渴、尿频和轻微手抖。哪项护理措施最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项护理措施最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports experiencing persistent thirst, frequent urination, and a slight hand tremor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者报告出现持续口渴、尿频和轻微手抖。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Advise the client to restrict fluid intake to 1,000 mL daily.","zh":"建议患者将每日液体摄入量限制在1,000毫升。"},{"id":"A","en":"Reinforce the importance of maintaining consistent sodium and fluid intake.","zh":"强调保持稳定的钠和液体摄入量的重要性。"},{"id":"B","en":"Request a prescription for a loop diuretic to manage the polyuria.","zh":"请求开具利尿剂处方以处理多尿症。"},{"id":"D","en":"Instruct the client to stop the medication immediately and go to the emergency room.","zh":"指示患者立即停药并前往急诊室。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thirst, polyuria, and fine hand tremors are common expected side effects of lithium therapy. Consistency in sodium and fluid intake is crucial because lithium is a salt, and fluctuations in either can affect lithium levels (e.g., low sodium can lead to lithium toxicity).","rationaleCorrectZh":"口渴、多尿和细微手抖是锂盐治疗的常见预期副作用。保持钠和液体摄入的一致性至关重要，因为锂是一种盐，任何一方的波动都会影响锂浓度（例如，低钠会导致锂中毒）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between common side effects (fine tremors, polyuria) and toxicity (ataxia, coarse tremors). Focus on maintenance education.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分常见副作用（细微手抖、多尿）和中毒（共济失调、粗大震颤）。重点在于维持治疗的教育。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":537,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.346.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[195,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,57],"fullStemEn":"A client is newly prescribed phenelzine for treatment-resistant depression. Which of the following foods or substances should the nurse instruct the client to avoid while taking this medication? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者因难治性抑郁症新开处方服用苯乙肼。护士应指示患者在服用此药期间避免以下哪些食物或物质？（选择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following foods or substances should the nurse instruct the client to avoid while taking this medication?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应指示患者在服用此药期间避免以下哪些食物或物质？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Freshly brewed green tea","zh":"现泡绿茶"},{"id":"C","en":"Fresh cottage cheese","zh":"新鲜茅屋芝士"},{"id":"D","en":"Over-the-counter pseudoephedrine","zh":"非处方伪麻黄碱"},{"id":"E","en":"Red wine (Chianti)","zh":"红葡萄酒（基安蒂）"},{"id":"A","en":"Aged cheddar cheese","zh":"陈年切达干酪"},{"id":"B","en":"Salami and pepperoni","zh":"萨拉米香肠和意大利香肠"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Phenelzine is an MAOI. Consumption of tyramine-rich foods (aged cheese, cured meats, certain alcohols like red wine) or sympathomimetic drugs (pseudoephedrine) can lead to a hypertensive crisis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"苯乙肼是一种单胺氧化酶抑制剂 (MAOI)。摄入富含酪胺的食物（陈年奶酪、腌制肉类、某些酒精如红葡萄酒）或拟交感神经药物（伪麻黄碱）可能导致高血压危象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the mnemonic for MAOIs: avoid aged, fermented, cured, and overripe foods.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 MAOI 的记忆法：避免陈年、发酵、腌制和过熟的食物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":538,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.347","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.347.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.347.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,268],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,78],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) via a central venous access device. The nurse is monitoring for potential complications. For each finding, click to specify if it is more likely associated with hyperglycemia, fluid volume excess, or air embolism.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正通过中心静脉通路装置接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN)。护士正在监测潜在的并发症。对于每项发现，请点击指明其更可能与高血糖、循环负荷过重或空气栓塞相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, click to specify if it is more likely associated with hyperglycemia, fluid volume excess, or air embolism.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请点击指明其更可能与高血糖、循环负荷过重或空气栓塞相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring for potential complications.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测潜在的并发症。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Crackles on lung auscultation","zh":"肺部听诊闻及湿啰音"},{"id":"r2","en":"Sudden onset of dyspnea and chest pain","zh":"突然发作的呼吸困难和胸痛"},{"id":"r3","en":"Increased thirst and polyuria","zh":"口渴增加和多尿"},{"id":"r4","en":"Jugular venous distention","zh":"颈静脉怒张"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Air Embolism","zh":"空气栓塞"},{"id":"c2","en":"Fluid Volume Excess","zh":"循环负荷过重"},{"id":"c1","en":"Hyperglycemia","zh":"高血糖"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hyperglycemia presents with osmotic diuresis (thirst, polyuria). Fluid volume excess causes crackles and JVD. Air embolism presents with sudden respiratory distress and chest pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高血糖表现为渗透性利尿（口渴、多尿）。循环负荷过重会导致湿啰音和颈静脉怒张。空气栓塞表现为突发性呼吸窘迫和胸痛。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the primary system affected: metabolic (glucose), cardiovascular (fluid), or respiratory (embolism).","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定受影响的主要系统：代谢（血糖）、心血管（液体）或呼吸（栓塞）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":539,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.348.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing a client for lithium toxicity. Which of the following findings should be reported as signs of moderate to severe lithium toxicity? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名患者是否存在锂中毒。下列哪些发现应作为中度至重度锂中毒迹象进行报告？（选择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings should be reported as signs of moderate to severe lithium toxicity?","penultimateSentenceZh":"下列哪些发现应作为中度至重度锂中毒迹象进行报告？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Ataxia and muscular hyperirritability","zh":"共济失调和肌肉过度兴奋"},{"id":"E","en":"Confusion and sedation","zh":"神志不清和镇静感"},{"id":"A","en":"Coarse hand tremors","zh":"粗大震颤"},{"id":"D","en":"Nausea and occasional vomiting","zh":"恶心和偶尔呕吐"},{"id":"C","en":"Fine hand tremors","zh":"细微手抖"},{"id":"F","en":"Mental status changes such as stupor","zh":"意识状态改变，如昏睡"}],"correct":["A","B","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Moderate to severe toxicity (typically level > 1.5-2.0 mEq/L) involves coarse tremors, neurological deficits like ataxia, confusion, and severe mental status changes. Fine tremors and mild GI upset are early side effects or signs of mild toxicity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"中度至重度中毒（通常浓度 > 1.5-2.0 mEq/L）涉及粗大震颤、共济失调等神经功能缺损、神志不清和严重的意识状态改变。细微手抖和轻微胃肠不适是早期副作用或轻度中毒迹象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for worsening of common symptoms (fine becomes coarse) and new neurological symptoms (ataxia, stupor).","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找常见症状的恶化（细微变为粗大）以及新的神经系统症状（共济失调、昏睡）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":540,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.349","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.349.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.349.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[180,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,75],"fullStemEn":"A client taking tranylcypromine for depression reports a sudden, severe pounding headache, nausea, and neck stiffness. The nurse notes the client's blood pressure is 210/118 mmHg. Which is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"一名因抑郁症服用反苯环丙胺的患者报告突然出现严重的搏动性头痛、恶心和颈部僵硬。护士注意到患者的血压为 210/118 mmHg。护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes the client's blood pressure is 210/118 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到患者的血压为 210/118 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to lie down in a supine position.","zh":"鼓励患者平卧位休息。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's dietary intake over the past 24 hours.","zh":"评估患者过去24小时内的饮食摄入情况。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer an oral dose of acetaminophen for the headache.","zh":"口服一剂对乙酰氨基酚以缓解头痛。"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare for the administration of phentolamine IV.","zh":"准备静脉注射酚妥拉明。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is experiencing a hypertensive crisis, a known complication of MAOIs. Phentolamine is an alpha-adrenergic blocker used to rapidly lower blood pressure in this situation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在经历高血压危象，这是 MAOI 的已知并发症。酚妥拉明是一种 α-肾上腺素能阻滞剂，用于在这种情况下迅速降低血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the emergency (Hypertensive Crisis) and choose the intervention that addresses the immediate physiological threat.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别紧急情况（高血压危象），并选择针对直接生理威胁的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":541,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.350.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,57],"fullStemEn":"The Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) solution for a client has run out, and the next bag from the pharmacy is delayed by one hour. What is the most appropriate action for the nurse to take?","fullStemZh":"一名患者的全胃肠外营养 (TPN) 溶液已用完，而药房提供的下一袋药液延迟了一小时。护士采取的最合适的行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most appropriate action for the nurse to take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士采取的最合适的行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) solution for a client has run out, and the next bag from the pharmacy is delayed by one hour.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者的全胃肠外营养 (TPN) 溶液已用完，而药房提供的下一袋药液延迟了一小时。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Hang 10% dextrose in water (D10W) at the same rate as the TPN.","zh":"以与 TPN 相同的速率挂上 10% 葡萄糖水溶液 (D10W)。"},{"id":"C","en":"Capped the central line until the next bag arrives.","zh":"将中心静脉导管封管，直到下一袋药液送达。"},{"id":"A","en":"Infuse 0.9% sodium chloride at the same rate as the TPN.","zh":"以与 TPN 相同的速率输注 0.9% 氯化钠。"},{"id":"D","en":"Increase the rate of the current TPN bag slightly to make it last longer.","zh":"稍微调快当前 TPN 的滴速以使其维持更久（此处逻辑有误，应为调慢，但题目描述为已跑完）。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abrupt discontinuation of TPN, which has a high concentration of glucose, can lead to rebound hypoglycemia. Infusing D10W or D5W (depending on protocol) maintains glucose levels until the next TPN bag is available.","rationaleCorrectZh":"突然停止高浓度葡萄糖的 TPN 可能导致反跳性低血糖。输注 D10W 或 D5W（取决于方案）可维持血糖水平，直到下一袋 TPN 可用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the risk: sudden stop of high glucose = hypoglycemia. Choose the solution containing glucose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定风险：突然停止高糖 = 低血糖。选择含有葡萄糖的溶液。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":542,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.351","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.351.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.351.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,57],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for several clients on lithium therapy. For each serum lithium level, click to specify the most likely clinical manifestation and the corresponding classification of the finding.","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看几名接受锂盐治疗患者的实验室结果。对于每个血清锂水平，请点击指明最可能的临床表现以及该发现的相应分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each serum lithium level, click to specify the most likely clinical manifestation and the corresponding classification of the finding.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个血清锂水平，请点击指明最可能的临床表现以及该发现的相应分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for several clients on lithium therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在查看几名接受锂盐治疗患者的实验室结果。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"0.8 mEq/L","zh":"0.8 mEq/L"},{"id":"r2","en":"1.8 mEq/L","zh":"1.8 mEq/L"},{"id":"r3","en":"2.8 mEq/L","zh":"2.8 mEq/L"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Therapeutic Range","zh":"治疗范围"},{"id":"c2","en":"Early Toxicity (Blurred vision, Diarrhea)","zh":"早期中毒（视力模糊、腹泻）"},{"id":"c3","en":"Severe Toxicity (Seizures, Oliguria)","zh":"严重中毒（癫痫发作、少尿）"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic lithium range is generally 0.6-1.2 mEq/L. Levels above 1.5 start showing toxicity symptoms. Levels > 2.5 are considered medical emergencies with severe symptoms like seizures or renal failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锂的治疗范围通常为 0.6-1.2 mEq/L。超过 1.5 的水平开始出现中毒症状。> 2.5 的水平被认为是医疗紧急情况，会出现癫痫或肾衰竭等严重症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the lithium therapeutic range (0.6-1.2) and the thresholds for toxicity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住锂的治疗范围 (0.6-1.2) 和中毒阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":543,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.352.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about dietary modifications required while taking isocarboxazid. For each food item, click to specify if it is safe to consume or must be avoided.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教育一名患者服用异卡波肼期间所需的饮食调整。对于每种食物，请点击指明它是可以安全食用还是必须避免。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each food item, click to specify if it is safe to consume or must be avoided.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每种食物，请点击指明它是可以安全食用还是必须避免。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about dietary modifications required while taking isocarboxazid.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教育一名患者服用异卡波肼期间所需的饮食调整。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Fresh grilled salmon","zh":"新鲜烤三文鱼"},{"id":"r2","en":"Smoked salmon (Lox)","zh":"烟熏三文鱼 (Lox)"},{"id":"r3","en":"Overripe avocados","zh":"过熟的鳄梨"},{"id":"r4","en":"Commercial canned soup (yeast-free)","zh":"市售罐装汤（不含酵母）"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Avoid","zh":"应避免"},{"id":"c1","en":"Safe to Consume","zh":"可安全食用"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fresh meats and fish are safe. Smoked, cured, or fermented foods (like smoked salmon) and overripe produce (like overripe avocados) contain high levels of tyramine and must be avoided. Yeast-free commercial products are generally safe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新鲜肉类和鱼类是安全的。熏制、腌制或发酵食品（如烟熏三文鱼）和过熟的农产品（如过熟的鳄梨）含有高水平的酪胺，必须避免。不含酵母的市售产品通常是安全的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 'fresh' (safe) and 'aged/smoked/fermented' (unsafe).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“新鲜”（安全）和“陈年/熏制/发酵”（不安全）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":544,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.353","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.353.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.353.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,198],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,64],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) through a central line. Which of the following nursing interventions are essential for the safe administration of TPN? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者正通过中心静脉导管接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN)。下列哪些护理干预措施对于安全实施 TPN 至关重要？（选择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing interventions are essential for the safe administration of TPN?","penultimateSentenceZh":"下列哪些护理干预措施对于安全实施 TPN 至关重要？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Regularly monitor blood glucose levels every 4 to 6 hours.","zh":"每4至6小时定期监测血糖水平。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the solution with another registered nurse before hanging.","zh":"挂药前与另一名注册护士共同核对药液。"},{"id":"B","en":"Change the TPN infusion tubing every 24 hours.","zh":"每24小时更换一次 TPN 输液管路。"},{"id":"F","en":"Maintain sterile technique during dressing changes.","zh":"在更换敷料期间保持无菌技术。"},{"id":"C","en":"Use an inline filter during administration.","zh":"输注过程中使用终端过滤器。"},{"id":"E","en":"Accelerate the rate if the infusion falls behind schedule.","zh":"如果输注进度落后于计划，请加快滴速。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe TPN administration requires verification (like high-alert meds), tubing changes (to prevent infection), filtering (to catch precipitates), glucose monitoring (due to high dextrose), and sterile technique for the central line.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全的 TPN 给药需要核对（类似于高危药物）、更换管路（预防感染）、过滤（拦截沉淀物）、监测血糖（由于高糖浓度）以及对中心静脉导管实施无菌技术。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on infection control, metabolic safety, and patient verification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注感染控制、代谢安全和患者核对。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":545,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c7_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.354.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,211],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,60],"fullStemEn":"A client taking lithium for several years has been diagnosed with a minor respiratory infection and prescribed clarithromycin and ibuprofen. Which part of the client's medical plan should most concern the nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名服用锂盐数年的患者被诊断出患有轻微呼吸道感染，并被开具了克拉霉素和布洛芬。患者医疗计划的哪一部分最应引起护士的关注？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which part of the client's medical plan should most concern the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者医疗计划的哪一部分最应引起护士的关注？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client taking lithium for several years has been diagnosed with a minor respiratory infection and prescribed clarithromycin and ibuprofen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名服用锂盐数年的患者被诊断出患有轻微呼吸道感染，并被开具了克拉霉素和布洛芬。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The risk of lithium toxicity with ibuprofen.","zh":"布洛芬引起锂中毒的风险。"},{"id":"C","en":"The use of an antibiotic with lithium.","zh":"抗生素与锂盐的合用。"},{"id":"A","en":"Potential for increased lithium excretion due to infection.","zh":"感染导致锂排泄增加的可能性。"},{"id":"D","en":"The impact of the respiratory infection on lithium levels.","zh":"呼吸道感染对锂浓度的影响。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) like ibuprofen can significantly increase lithium levels by reducing renal blood flow and lithium excretion, leading to toxicity. Aspirin or sulindac are safer alternatives.","rationaleCorrectZh":"像布洛芬这样的非甾体抗炎药 (NSAID) 会通过减少肾血流量和锂排泄，显著增加锂浓度，从而导致中毒。阿司匹林或舒林酸是更安全的替代品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall common drug-drug interactions with lithium, especially NSAIDs, diuretics, and ACE inhibitors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想锂盐常见的药物相互作用，尤其是 NSAID、利尿剂和 ACE 抑制剂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":546,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.355","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.355.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.355.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,240],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,67],"fullStemEn":"A client with a large pleural effusion is scheduled for a thoracentesis but is unable to sit upright or lean forward due to extreme weakness and hemodynamic instability. In which position should the nurse place the client for the procedure?","fullStemZh":"一位患有大量胸腔积液的患者计划进行胸腔穿刺术，但由于极度虚弱和血流动力学不稳定而无法坐直或向前倾。护士应将患者置于哪种体位以进行操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"In which position should the nurse place the client for the procedure?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将患者置于哪种体位以进行操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a large pleural effusion is scheduled for a thoracentesis but is unable to sit upright or lean forward due to extreme weakness and hemodynamic instability.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患有大量胸腔积液的患者计划进行胸腔穿刺术，但由于极度虚弱和血流动力学不稳定而无法坐直或向前倾。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Prone with a pillow supporting the abdomen and chest.","zh":"俯卧位，腹部和胸部下方垫枕头。"},{"id":"C","en":"Semi-Fowler's position with the affected side tilted toward the mattress.","zh":"半坐卧位，患侧向床垫方向倾斜。"},{"id":"D","en":"Side-lying on the unaffected side with the affected side at the edge of the bed.","zh":"患侧在上，侧卧于健侧，且患侧靠近床边。"},{"id":"B","en":"Supine with the head of the bed elevated 45 degrees.","zh":"仰卧位，床头抬高45度。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"If a client cannot sit up for a thoracentesis, the alternative is the side-lying position on the unaffected side (affected side up) with the head of the bed slightly elevated. This allows the fluid to pool in the dependent area and provides access to the pleural space.","rationaleCorrectZh":"如果患者无法坐起进行胸腔穿刺术，另一种选择是取健侧卧位（患侧在上），床头稍抬高。这使得液体积聚在低位区域，并便于进入胸膜腔。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the goal: accessing pleural fluid in an immobilized client. Visualize where the fluid would go with gravity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于目标：在无法活动的患者中抽取胸腔积液。想象液体在重力作用下的流向。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":547,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.356","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.356.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.356.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,46],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing a client with end-stage liver disease for a therapeutic paracentesis. Arrange the following nursing actions in the correct chronological order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患有终末期肝病的患者准备治疗性腹腔穿刺术。请按正确的时间顺序排列以下护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the following nursing actions in the correct chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的时间顺序排列以下护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing a client with end-stage liver disease for a therapeutic paracentesis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患有终末期肝病的患者准备治疗性腹腔穿刺术。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Measure baseline vital signs, weight, and abdominal girth.","zh":"测量基线生命体征、体重和腹围。"},{"id":"B","en":"Instruct the client to void completely.","zh":"指示患者完全排空膀胱。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify that informed consent has been signed and witnessed.","zh":"核实知情同意书已签署并有见证人。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assist the client into a high-Fowler's position.","zh":"协助患者取高半坐卧位。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Informed consent must be confirmed before any preparations. The client should void immediately before the procedure to minimize the risk of accidental bladder puncture. Baseline measurements are then taken for post-procedure comparison. Finally, the client is positioned just before the sterile field is prepared.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在进行任何准备之前，必须先确认知情同意。患者应在操作前立即排尿，以最大限度地降低意外穿刺膀胱的风险。随后进行基线测量，以便术后对比。最后，在准备无菌区域之前为患者安置体位。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply principles of safety: legal (consent), physical (voiding), and assessment (baseline).","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用安全原则：法律（同意）、物理（排尿）和评估（基线）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":548,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.357","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.357.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.357.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,288],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,82],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assisting with a thoracentesis for a client with a massive pleural effusion. To minimize the risk of re-expansion pulmonary edema and circulatory collapse, the nurse should notify the healthcare provider when the total volume of fluid removed reaches how many milliliters (mL)?","fullStemZh":"护士正在协助为一名患有大量胸腔积液的患者进行胸腔穿刺术。为了最大限度地降低复张性肺水肿和循环衰竭的风险，当抽出的液体总量达到多少毫升（mL）时，护士应通知医疗人员？","terminalSentenceEn":"To minimize the risk of re-expansion pulmonary edema and circulatory collapse, the nurse should notify the healthcare provider when the total volume of fluid removed reaches how many milliliters (mL)?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了最大限度地降低复张性肺水肿和循环衰竭的风险，当抽出的液体总量达到多少毫升（mL）时，护士应通知医疗人员？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assisting with a thoracentesis for a client with a massive pleural effusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在协助为一名患有大量胸腔积液的患者进行胸腔穿刺术。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["1500","1500 mL","1500毫升"],"numeric":{"value":1500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rapid removal of large volumes of pleural fluid (>1,000 to 1,500 mL) can lead to re-expansion pulmonary edema and hypotension. Standard practice is to limit removal to 1,500 mL per procedure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"快速抽取大量胸腔积液（>1,000至1,500毫升）会导致复张性肺水肿和低血压。标准做法是将每次操作的抽取量限制在1,500毫升以内。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall safety limits for fluid removal from the pleural space versus the peritoneal space (which allows larger volumes).","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想胸膜腔与腹膜腔（允许更大容量）液体抽取的安全限制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":549,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.358","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.358.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.358.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,55],"fullStemEn":"Shortly after a paracentesis, a client reports sudden, sharp suprapubic pain and the nurse notes that the client’s urinary output has become grossly bloody. Which complication should the nurse suspect?","fullStemZh":"腹腔穿刺术后不久，患者报告突然出现剧烈的耻骨上疼痛，护士注意到患者的尿液变成了肉眼血尿。护士应怀疑哪种并发症？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which complication should the nurse suspect?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应怀疑哪种并发症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Shortly after a paracentesis, a client reports sudden, sharp suprapubic pain and the nurse notes that the client’s urinary output has become grossly bloody.","penultimateSentenceZh":"腹腔穿刺术后不久，患者报告突然出现剧烈的耻骨上疼痛，护士注意到患者的尿液变成了肉眼血尿。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Internal hemorrhage from a mesenteric vessel.","zh":"肠系膜血管引起的内出血。"},{"id":"A","en":"Bladder puncture during the procedure.","zh":"操作过程中刺破膀胱。"},{"id":"D","en":"Acute renal failure from rapid fluid shift.","zh":"快速液体转移导致的急性肾衰竭。"},{"id":"B","en":"Peritonitis due to bowel perforation.","zh":"肠穿孔导致的腹膜炎。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suprapubic pain and hematuria (bloody urine) following paracentesis are classic signs of accidental bladder puncture. This is why clients are instructed to void before the procedure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"腹腔穿刺术后出现的耻骨上疼痛和血尿是意外刺破膀胱的典型征兆。这就是指示患者在操作前排尿的原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate the anatomical location of the pain (suprapubic) with the nearest organ at risk (bladder).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将疼痛的解剖位置（耻骨上）与附近有风险的器官（膀胱）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":550,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.359","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.359.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.359.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,50],"fullStemEn":"During a thoracentesis, 1,200 mL of fluid is removed. The client suddenly develops a persistent, non-productive cough, shortness of breath, and chest tightness. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"胸腔穿刺术中抽出了1200毫升液体。患者突然出现持续性干咳、呼吸短促和胸闷。护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client suddenly develops a persistent, non-productive cough, shortness of breath, and chest tightness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者突然出现持续性干咳、呼吸短促和胸闷。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Position the client on the affected side to stabilize the lung.","zh":"将患者置于患侧卧位以稳定肺部。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assist the client to take deep breaths to promote lung expansion.","zh":"协助患者深呼吸以促进肺扩张。"},{"id":"D","en":"Instruct the healthcare provider to stop the procedure immediately.","zh":"指示医疗人员立即停止操作。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the prescribed PRN dose of intravenous morphine.","zh":"给予处方的按需（PRN）剂量静脉吗啡。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A persistent cough and chest tightness during thoracentesis can signal re-expansion pulmonary edema or a developing pneumothorax. The most immediate safety action is to stop the removal of fluid.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胸腔穿刺期间持续性咳嗽和胸闷可能预示着复张性肺水肿或正在发生的气胸。最直接的安全措施是停止抽取液体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In any procedure, if the client develops sudden distress, the first action is almost always to 'Stop the procedure'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在任何操作中，如果患者突然出现窘迫，第一步行动几乎总是“停止操作”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":551,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.360","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.360.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.360.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,51],"fullStemEn":"A client has just returned to the room after a large-volume paracentesis where 6 liters of fluid were removed. Place the nurse's post-procedural assessments and interventions in order of priority.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在进行了抽取6升液体的大容量腹腔穿刺术后刚刚回到病房。请按优先级排列护士的术后评估和干预措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's post-procedural assessments and interventions in order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先级排列护士的术后评估和干预措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client has just returned to the room after a large-volume paracentesis where 6 liters of fluid were removed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在进行了抽取6升液体的大容量腹腔穿刺术后刚刚回到病房。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assess the abdominal dressing for leakage or hemorrhage.","zh":"评估腹部敷料是否有渗漏或出血。"},{"id":"A","en":"Check blood pressure and heart rate for signs of hypovolemia.","zh":"检查血压和心率是否有低血容量迹象。"},{"id":"C","en":"Measure abdominal girth and obtain the client's weight.","zh":"测量腹围并称量患者体重。"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor urinary output for evidence of adequate renal perfusion.","zh":"监测尿量以获取肾脏灌注充足的证据。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hemodynamic stability is the highest priority following large-volume paracentesis due to the risk of post-paracentesis circulatory dysfunction (PPCD). Monitoring the site for leakage or bleeding is the next priority. Baseline comparisons (girth/weight) and monitoring renal perfusion (urine output) follow.","rationaleCorrectZh":"由于存在腹腔穿刺后循环功能障碍（PPCD）的风险，血流动力学稳定性是大容量腹腔穿刺术后的最高优先级。监测穿刺部位是否有渗漏或出血是下一个优先级。随后是基线对比（腹围/体重）和监测肾灌注（尿量）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABC (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) framework. Circulation (BP/HR) is the most critical post-fluid shift.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）框架。在液体转移后，循环（血压/心率）是最关键的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client has just returned to the room after a large-volume paracentesis where 6 liters of fluid were removed.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患者在进行了抽取6升液体的大容量腹腔穿刺术后刚刚回到病房。"}
{"queueIndex":552,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.361","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.361.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.361.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[184,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,67],"fullStemEn":"Before a paracentesis, the nurse reviews the laboratory results of a client with cirrhosis. The nurse should notify the provider if the plasma fibrinogen is below what value in mg/dL? (Provide a whole number.)","fullStemZh":"在为肝硬化患者进行腹腔穿刺术之前，护士查看其实验室检查结果。如果血浆纤维蛋白原低于多少 mg/dL，护士应通知医疗人员？（提供整数。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Provide a whole number.)","terminalSentenceZh":"提供整数。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should notify the provider if the plasma fibrinogen is below what value in mg/dL?","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果血浆纤维蛋白原低于多少 mg/dL，护士应通知医疗人员？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"fibrinogen (mg/dL)","zh":"纤维蛋白原 (mg/dL)"},"acceptable":["100"],"numeric":{"value":100,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mg/dL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In cirrhosis, INR alone does not predict procedure-related bleeding and no target INR exists. A fibrinogen level below 100 mg/dL is associated with spontaneous and procedure-related bleeding and should prompt individualized review.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在肝硬化患者中，INR 本身不能预测操作相关出血，且不存在固定的目标 INR。纤维蛋白原低于 100 mg/dL 与自发性及操作相关出血有关，应进行个体化评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cirrhosis, do not use a fixed INR cutoff to predict procedural bleeding. Review the full clinical picture, including fibrinogen and platelet count.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于肝硬化患者，不要使用固定 INR 截止值预测操作出血。应结合纤维蛋白原、血小板计数和整体临床情况评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse should notify the provider if the plasma fibrinogen is below what value in mg/dL?","controlSentenceZh":"如果血浆纤维蛋白原低于多少 mg/dL，护士应通知医疗人员？（"}
{"queueIndex":553,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.362","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.362.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.362.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,33],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client post-thoracentesis. Which finding requires the most immediate intervention by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测胸腔穿刺术后的患者。以下哪项发现需要护士最及时的干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding requires the most immediate intervention by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项发现需要护士最及时的干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client post-thoracentesis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测胸腔穿刺术后的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The client reports sharp, localized pain at the puncture site during deep inspiration.","zh":"患者主诉深吸气时穿刺部位出现剧烈的局部疼痛。"},{"id":"A","en":"The nurse notes asymmetrical chest expansion and tracheal deviation to the unaffected side.","zh":"护士注意到胸廓扩张不对称，且气管向健侧偏移。"},{"id":"B","en":"There is a 2 cm area of serosanguineous drainage on the sterile pressure dressing.","zh":"无菌加压敷料上有2厘米大小的浆液血性渗出区域。"},{"id":"D","en":"Breath sounds are diminished at the lung base on the side where the procedure was performed.","zh":"在进行操作的一侧肺底呼吸音减弱。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Asymmetrical chest expansion and tracheal deviation are classic signs of a tension pneumothorax, a life-threatening complication of thoracentesis that requires immediate needle decompression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胸廓扩张不对称和气管偏移是张力性气胸的典型征象。张力性气胸是胸腔穿刺术的一种危及生命的并发症，需要立即进行针刺减压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between 'expected findings' (mild pain, diminished sounds) and 'life-threatening complications' (tracheal deviation).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“预期发现”（轻微疼痛、声音减弱）和“危及生命的并发症”（气管偏移）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":554,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.363","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.363.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.363.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,33],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assisting a healthcare provider with a bedside thoracentesis. Arrange the steps of the procedure in the order they should be performed.","fullStemZh":"护士正在协助医疗人员进行床边胸腔穿刺术。请按执行顺序排列操作步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the steps of the procedure in the order they should be performed.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按执行顺序排列操作步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assisting a healthcare provider with a bedside thoracentesis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在协助医疗人员进行床边胸腔穿刺术。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Apply a sterile occlusive dressing to the puncture site.","zh":"在穿刺部位涂抹无菌加压敷料。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer a local anesthetic to the subcutaneous tissue and pleura.","zh":"向皮下组织和胸膜注射局部麻醉剂。"},{"id":"C","en":"Advance the thoracentesis needle into the pleural space.","zh":"将胸腔穿刺针推进胸膜腔。"},{"id":"A","en":"Cleanse the skin with an antiseptic solution (e.g., chlorhexidine).","zh":"用防腐溶液（如氯己定）清洁皮肤。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The skin must be cleansed first to maintain sterility. Anesthesia is then administered to minimize pain during the deeper needle insertion. The fluid is then withdrawn, and finally, the site is covered with an occlusive dressing to prevent air entry or infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"必须首先清洁皮肤以保持无菌。随后进行麻醉，以最大限度地减轻深部进针时的疼痛。随后抽取液体，最后用加压敷料覆盖部位，以防止空气进入或感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply standard aseptic technique principles: Clean -> Numb -> Procedural Action -> Protect.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用标准无菌技术原则：清洁 -> 麻醉 -> 操作动作 -> 保护。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":555,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c8_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.364","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.364.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.364.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,320],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,94],"fullStemEn":"A client undergoes a large-volume paracentesis, and 6,000 mL of fluid is removed. To maintain oncotic pressure and prevent circulatory collapse, the nurse expects to administer intravenous albumin. What is the standard concentration (percentage %) of albumin typically used for volume expansion in this clinical context?","fullStemZh":"一名患者接受了大容量腹腔穿刺术，抽出了6,000毫升液体。为了维持胶体渗透压并防止循环衰竭，护士预计将给予静脉注射白蛋白。在这种临床情况下，用于扩容的白蛋白标准浓度（百分比%）通常是多少？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the standard concentration (percentage %) of albumin typically used for volume expansion in this clinical context?","terminalSentenceZh":"在这种临床情况下，用于扩容的白蛋白标准浓度（百分比%）通常是多少？","penultimateSentenceEn":"To maintain oncotic pressure and prevent circulatory collapse, the nurse expects to administer intravenous albumin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"为了维持胶体渗透压并防止循环衰竭，护士预计将给予静脉注射白蛋白。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"%","zh":"%"},"acceptable":["25","25%","25 percent"],"numeric":{"value":25,"tolerance":0,"unit":"percent"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"25% albumin is the hyperoncotic concentration used following large-volume paracentesis to shift fluid from the interstitium into the intravascular space, thereby preventing hypotension.","rationaleCorrectZh":"25%浓度的白蛋白是大容量腹腔穿刺术后使用的高渗浓度，用于将液体从间质转移到血管内空间，从而防止低血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 5% albumin (isooncotic) and 25% albumin (hyperoncotic) use cases.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分5%白蛋白（等渗）和25%白蛋白（高渗）的使用场景。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":556,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.365","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.365.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.365.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is triaging victims at the scene of a train derailment. Which client should be assigned a 'Red' tag (Immediate)?","fullStemZh":"护士正在火车脱轨现场对伤员进行分诊。哪位患者应被标记为“红色”标签（立即救治）？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should be assigned a 'Red' tag (Immediate)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪位患者应被标记为“红色”标签（立即救治）？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is triaging victims at the scene of a train derailment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在火车脱轨现场对伤员进行分诊。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"A client with multiple deep lacerations who is walking around and asking for help.","zh":"一位有多处深度裂伤，正四处走动并寻求帮助的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client with a traumatic amputation of the lower leg, bleeding controlled by a tourniquet.","zh":"一位下肢创伤性截肢的患者，止血带已止血。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with an open pneumothorax and a respiratory rate of 34 breaths/minute.","zh":"一位有开放性气胸且呼吸频率为 34 次/分的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client with a severe head injury, no spontaneous respirations, and a GCS score of 3.","zh":"一位头部严重受伤、无自主呼吸且 GCS 评分为 3 分的患者。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A is assigned a 'Red' tag because an open pneumothorax is a life-threatening respiratory emergency that requires immediate intervention (e.g., occlusive dressing) but is survivable with prompt care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"A 被标记为“红色”标签，因为开放性气胸是一种危及生命的呼吸急症，需要立即干预（如封闭敷料），但通过及时治疗是可以存活的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABC (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) framework. In triage, prioritize clients with treatable life-threatening conditions over those who are stable or those who are unlikely to survive.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）框架。在分诊中，优先考虑患有可治疗的危及生命病症的患者，而不是那些稳定的患者或极难存活的患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":557,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.366","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.366.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.366.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,68],"fullStemEn":"The nurse in the emergency department (ED) is triaging several clients. Which clients require immediate (Level 1 or 2) intervention according to the Emergency Severity Index (ESI)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"急诊科 (ED) 护士正在对几位患者进行分诊。根据急诊严重指数 (ESI)，哪些患者需要立即（1 级或 2 级）干预？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clients require immediate (Level 1 or 2) intervention according to the Emergency Severity Index (ESI)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据急诊严重指数 (ESI)，哪些患者需要立即（1 级或 2 级）干预？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"A 28-year-old with a sudden onset of facial drooping and right-sided weakness.","zh":"一位 28 岁的患者，突然出现面部下垂和右侧肢体无力。"},{"id":"C","en":"A 60-year-old with cool, clammy skin and a heart rate of 130 beats/minute.","zh":"一位 60 岁的患者，皮肤湿冷，心率为 130 次/分。"},{"id":"B","en":"A 45-year-old reporting epigastric pain and nausea after eating a large meal.","zh":"一位 45 岁的患者，自述在大餐后出现上腹部疼痛和恶心。"},{"id":"D","en":"A 12-year-old with a history of asthma who is wheezing and using intercostal muscles to breathe.","zh":"一位有哮喘病史的 12 岁儿童，出现喘鸣并使用肋间肌辅助呼吸。"},{"id":"E","en":"A 75-year-old with a possible hip fracture after a fall, reporting pain as 8/10.","zh":"一位 75 岁的患者，跌倒后可能发生髋部骨折，自述疼痛评分为 8/10。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients with stroke symptoms, signs of shock, and acute respiratory distress are high-acuity (ESI Level 2) because they have life- or organ-threatening conditions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患有中风症状、休克体征 和急性呼吸窘迫 的患者属于高敏锐度（ESI 2 级），因为他们患有危及生命或器官的疾病。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that ESI Level 1 is for those needing immediate life-saving intervention (e.g., cardiac arrest), and Level 2 is for high-risk situations (e.g., severe respiratory distress, potential stroke, signs of shock).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 ESI 1 级针对的是需要立即救命干预的人（如心脏骤停），而 2 级针对的是高风险情况（如严重呼吸窘迫、潜在中风、休克迹象）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":558,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.367","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.367.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.367.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for victims of a 'dirty bomb' explosion who have been exposed to radiation. In what order should the nurse perform the following actions for a client who is contaminated with radioactive material?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理因“脏弹”爆炸而暴露在辐射下的伤员。对于被放射性物质污染的患者，护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse perform the following actions for a client who is contaminated with radioactive material?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于被放射性物质污染的患者，护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for victims of a 'dirty bomb' explosion who have been exposed to radiation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理因“脏弹”爆炸而暴露在辐射下的伤员。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's airway, breathing, and circulation (ABCs).","zh":"评估患者的气道、呼吸和循环 (ABC)。"},{"id":"C","en":"Shower the client with soap and water to decontaminate.","zh":"用肥皂和水为患者淋浴以进行洗消。"},{"id":"D","en":"Don personal protective equipment (PPE), including a respirator.","zh":"穿戴个人防护装备 (PPE)，包括呼吸防护器。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove the client's clothing and place it in a sealed container.","zh":"脱去患者的衣服并将其放入密封容器中。"}],"correct":["D","B","A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority is safety (PPE), followed by stabilization of the client (ABCs), then decontamination by removing outer clothing (which removes most contamination), and finally washing the skin.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要任务是安全 (PPE)，其次是稳定患者 (ABC)，然后通过脱掉外层衣物进行洗消（这可以去除大部分污染），最后清洗皮肤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In any hazmat or radiation scenario, the safety of the responder (PPE) is the absolute first priority to prevent secondary contamination.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在任何危险物质或辐射场景中，响应者的安全 (PPE) 是绝对的第一优先级，以防止二次污染。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":559,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.368","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.368.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.368.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is responding to a chemical spill in a community health clinic. Which interventions are appropriate for chemical decontamination? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在处理社区卫生诊所发生的化学品泄漏。哪些干预措施适用于化学洗消？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions are appropriate for chemical decontamination?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些干预措施适用于化学洗消？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Remove the client's jewelry and contact lenses.","zh":"摘除患者的饰品和隐形眼镜。"},{"id":"C","en":"Neutralize an acidic chemical with a weak base solution.","zh":"用弱碱溶液中和酸性化学物质。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use large amounts of water to flush the skin and eyes.","zh":"使用大量清水冲洗皮肤和眼睛。"},{"id":"A","en":"Scrub the skin vigorously to remove the chemical.","zh":"用力擦洗皮肤以去除化学物质。"},{"id":"E","en":"Double-bag contaminated clothing and seal it.","zh":"将污染的衣物双层装袋并密封。"}],"correct":["B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Irrigation with copious water, removal of items that can trap chemicals, and safe disposal of clothing (E) are standard decontamination practices.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用大量水冲洗、移除可能积聚化学物质的物品 以及安全处理衣物 (E) 是标准的洗消做法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on interventions that effectively remove the substance without causing more damage (like scrubbing or heat-producing reactions).","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注那些能有效去除物质且不会造成更多损害（如擦洗或产热反应）的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":560,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.369","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.369.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.369.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,46],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to care for four post-operative clients returning from the PACU. In what order should the nurse assess these clients?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备护理从 PACU（麻醉恢复室）返回的四位手术后患者。护士应按什么顺序评估这些患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse assess these clients?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序评估这些患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to care for four post-operative clients returning from the PACU.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备护理从 PACU（麻醉恢复室）返回的四位手术后患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client who had a gastrectomy and has a nasogastric (NG) tube that stopped draining.","zh":"一位进行了胃切除术，鼻胃管 (NG) 停止引流的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client who had a thyroidectomy and is reporting a 'tight' feeling in the throat.","zh":"一位进行了甲状腺切除术，自述喉部有“紧迫感”的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client who had a total hip replacement and has a drainage of 100 mL of serosanguinous fluid.","zh":"一位进行了全髋关节置换术，引流量为 100 毫升血清样血性液体的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client who had an appendectomy and has not voided for 6 hours.","zh":"一位进行了阑尾切除术，6 小时未排尿的患者。"}],"correct":["B","A","D","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assess for airway, then circulation/bleeding, then potential surgical complications, and finally routine post-op monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"评估气道，然后是循环/出血，接着是潜在的手术并发症，最后是常规的手术后监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always apply the ABCs. Airway (throat tightness) always comes before circulation (drainage).","testTakingStrategyZh":"始终应用 ABC。气道（喉部紧迫感）总是排在循环（引流）之前。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":561,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.370","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.370.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.370.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is triaging children at a school after a carbon monoxide leak. Which child should be seen first?","fullStemZh":"一处发生一氧化碳泄漏后，护士正在学校对儿童进行分诊。应该先看哪位儿童？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which child should be seen first?","terminalSentenceZh":"应该先看哪位儿童？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is triaging children at a school after a carbon monoxide leak.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一处发生一氧化碳泄漏后，护士正在学校对儿童进行分诊。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A child who is crying loudly and complaining of nausea.","zh":"一位大声哭泣并抱怨恶心的儿童。"},{"id":"C","en":"A child who has a pulse oximetry reading of 98% on room air.","zh":"一位在室内空气下脉搏血氧仪读数为 98% 的儿童。"},{"id":"B","en":"A child reporting a mild headache and feeling tired.","zh":"一位自述轻微头痛且感到疲倦的儿童。"},{"id":"A","en":"A child with bright cherry-red lips and mucous membranes.","zh":"一位嘴唇和粘膜呈鲜艳樱桃红色的儿童。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cherry-red lips and mucous membranes indicate high levels of carboxyhemoglobin, reflecting severe carbon monoxide poisoning which is a life-threatening emergency.","rationaleCorrectZh":"樱桃红色的嘴唇和粘膜表示碳氧血红蛋白水平很高，反映了严重的一氧化碳中毒，这是一种危及生命的急症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know the classic signs of toxic exposures and understand the limitations of diagnostic tools like pulse oximetry in those contexts.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解毒性暴露的典型征象，并理解脉搏血氧仪等诊断工具在这些背景下的局限性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":562,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.371","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.371.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.371.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[203,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,69],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is planning the care for a group of clients on a medical-surgical unit. Which tasks are appropriate for the RN to delegate to an experienced unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在计划内外科病房一组患者的护理工作。哪些任务适合 RN 委派给有经验的非执照辅助人员 (UAP)？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which tasks are appropriate for the RN to delegate to an experienced unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些任务适合 RN 委派给有经验的非执照辅助人员 (UAP)？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Assisting a client with ambulation who is 2 days post-appendectomy.","zh":"协助阑尾切除术后 2 天的患者下地行走。"},{"id":"E","en":"Feeding a client who is at high risk for aspiration.","zh":"给吸入高风险的患者喂食。"},{"id":"F","en":"Collecting a clean-catch urine specimen.","zh":"收集一份中段尿标本。"},{"id":"C","en":"Performing a sterile dressing change on a post-operative wound.","zh":"对手术后伤口进行无菌换药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Measuring and recording vital signs on a stable client.","zh":"测量并记录稳定患者的生命体征。"},{"id":"B","en":"Providing discharge instructions to a client with heart failure.","zh":"为心力衰竭患者提供出院指导。"}],"correct":["A","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"UAPs can perform tasks that are routine, have predictable outcomes, and do not involve the nursing process (assessment, planning, evaluation, or teaching).","rationaleCorrectZh":"UAP 可以执行常规、结果可预测且不涉及护理程序（评估、计划、评价或教学）的任务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not delegate 'EAT': Evaluation, Assessment, or Teaching. Also, consider the stability of the client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要委派“EAT”：评价 (Evaluation)、评估 (Assessment) 或教学 (Teaching)。此外，还要考虑患者的稳定性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which tasks are appropriate for the RN to delegate to an experienced unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些任务适合 RN 委派给有经验的非执照辅助人员 (UAP)？"}
{"queueIndex":563,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.372","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.372.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.372.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,44],"fullStemEn":"According to the Simple Triage and Rapid Treatment (START) protocol, what is the sequence of assessments the nurse should perform to triage an adult victim?","fullStemZh":"根据简易分诊及快速治疗 (START) 方案，护士对成年伤员进行分诊应遵循什么评估顺序？","terminalSentenceEn":"According to the Simple Triage and Rapid Treatment (START) protocol, what is the sequence of assessments the nurse should perform to triage an adult victim?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据简易分诊及快速治疗 (START) 方案，护士对成年伤员进行分诊应遵循什么评估顺序？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Call out to see if the victim can walk.","zh":"呼喊以查看伤员是否能行走。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess Perfusion (Capillary refill or radial pulse).","zh":"评估灌注情况（毛细血管充盈或桡动脉搏动）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess Mental Status (Ability to follow commands).","zh":"评估精神状态（执行指令的能力）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess Respirations (Presence and rate).","zh":"评估呼吸（是否存在及其频率）。"}],"correct":["D","C","A","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The START algorithm follows the order: Mobility ('walking wounded'), then RPM (Respirations, Perfusion, Mental status).","rationaleCorrectZh":"START 算法遵循以下顺序：移动能力（“步行伤员”），然后是 RPM（呼吸、灌注、精神状态）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the 'RPM' mnemonic for START triage and remember that mobility is checked before anything else.","testTakingStrategyZh":"背诵 START 分诊的“RPM”口诀，并记住移动能力的检查排在其他任何项目之前。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":564,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_c9_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.373","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.373.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.373.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,50],"fullStemEn":"A hospital is implementing its disaster plan due to an approaching hurricane. Which client should the nurse recommend for discharge first to make room for potential casualties?","fullStemZh":"由于飓风即将来临，一家医院正在执行其灾难计划。护士应建议优先出院哪位患者，以为潜在伤亡人员腾出空间？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the nurse recommend for discharge first to make room for potential casualties?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应建议优先出院哪位患者，以为潜在伤亡人员腾出空间？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A hospital is implementing its disaster plan due to an approaching hurricane.","penultimateSentenceZh":"由于飓风即将来临，一家医院正在执行其灾难计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A client with chronic stable angina who needs a cardiac catheterization scheduled for tomorrow.","zh":"一位患有慢性稳定型心绞痛，计划明天进行心脏导管插入术的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client who has been receiving IV antibiotics for 48 hours for cellulitis.","zh":"一位因蜂窝织炎已接受 48 小时静脉抗生素治疗的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client admitted 12 hours ago with chest pain and awaiting a stress test.","zh":"一位 12 小时前因胸痛入院，正在等待压力测试的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client who had a laparoscopic cholecystectomy yesterday and is tolerating a liquid diet.","zh":"一位昨天进行了腹腔镜胆囊切除术，且耐受流质饮食的患者。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A client who is post-op day 1 from a routine procedure is the most stable and can be safely managed outside the acute care setting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"一位处于常规手术后第 1 天的患者 最为稳定，可以安全地在急性护理环境之外进行管理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the client who is most stable and requires the least amount of acute nursing care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找最稳定且需要最少急性护理工作的患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":565,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_01_matrix_dka_hhs","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.374","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.374.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.374.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,235],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,74],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results for two clients admitted with hyperglycemic emergencies. For each finding, select whether it is more characteristic of Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) or Hyperosmolar Hyperglycemic State (HHS).","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查两名因高血糖急症入院患者的实验室结果。对于每项发现，请选择其更符合糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 还是高渗高血糖状态 (HHS) 的特征。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is more characteristic of Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) or Hyperosmolar Hyperglycemic State (HHS).","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请选择其更符合糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 还是高渗高血糖状态 (HHS) 的特征。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results for two clients admitted with hyperglycemic emergencies.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查两名因高血糖急症入院患者的实验室结果。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Plasma glucose >600 mg/dL (33.3 mmol/L)","zh":"血浆葡萄糖 >600 mg/dL (33.3 mmol/L)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Arterial pH <7.30","zh":"动脉血 pH <7.30"},{"id":"r3","en":"Serum bicarbonate <18 mEq/L","zh":"血清碳酸氢盐 <18 mEq/L"},{"id":"r4","en":"Serum osmolality >320 mOsm/kg","zh":"血清渗透压 >320 mOsm/kg"},{"id":"r5","en":"Significant ketonuria and ketonemia","zh":"显著的酮尿和酮血症"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","zh":"糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA)"},{"id":"c2","en":"Hyperosmolar Hyperglycemic State (HHS)","zh":"高渗高血糖状态 (HHS)"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"DKA is characterized by metabolic acidosis (low pH and bicarbonate) and the presence of ketones. HHS is characterized by extreme hyperglycemia (>600 mg/dL) and profound hyperosmolality (>320 mOsm/kg) without significant ketoacidosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DKA 的特点是代谢性酸中毒（低 pH 和碳酸氢盐）以及酮体的存在。HHS 的特点是极度高血糖 (>600 mg/dL) 和显著的高渗透压 (>320 mOsm/kg)，且无明显的酮症酸中毒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on 'Acidosis' for DKA and 'Osmolality/Glucose' for HHS. Remember that DKA occurs faster while HHS presents with higher glucose and dehydration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注 DKA 的“酸中毒”和 HHS 的“渗透压/血糖”。请记住，DKA 发生较快，而 HHS 表现为更高的血糖和脱水。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":566,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_02_cloze_hypocalcemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.375","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.375.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.375.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,56],"fullStemEn":"A client returns to the surgical unit after a total thyroidectomy. During the assessment, the nurse notes involuntary contraction of the facial muscles when the facial nerve is tapped in front of the ear.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在接受全甲状腺切除术后返回外科病房。在评估期间，护士注意到当敲击耳前的面神经时，面部肌肉出现不自主收缩。","terminalSentenceEn":"During the assessment, the nurse notes involuntary contraction of the facial muscles when the facial nerve is tapped in front of the ear.","terminalSentenceZh":"在评估期间，护士注意到当敲击耳前的面神经时，面部肌肉出现不自主收缩。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client returns to the surgical unit after a total thyroidectomy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在接受全甲状腺切除术后返回外科病房。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize this as a positive {{1}}, immediately implement {{2}}, and anticipate an order for {{3}}.","zh":"护士应将其识别为 {{1}} 阳性，立即实施 {{2}}，并预期会有 {{3}} 的医嘱。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Trousseau's sign","zh":"特鲁索氏征 (Trousseau's sign)"},{"id":"o1","en":"Chvostek's sign","zh":"薛伯斯泰克氏征 (Chvostek's sign)"},{"id":"o3","en":"Babinski reflex","zh":"巴宾斯基反射 (Babinski reflex)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"Trendelenburg positioning","zh":"特伦德伦堡体位"},{"id":"o1","en":"seizure precautions","zh":"癫痫预防措施"},{"id":"o2","en":"increased fluid intake","zh":"增加液体摄入"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"IV normal saline bolus","zh":"静脉推注生理盐水"},{"id":"o1","en":"IV calcium gluconate","zh":"静脉注射葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"o2","en":"oral potassium chloride","zh":"口服氯化钾"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Chvostek's sign indicates hypocalcemia (often due to accidental parathyroid removal during thyroidectomy). Hypocalcemia increases neuromuscular excitability, leading to tetany and potential seizures. IV calcium gluconate is the standard treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"薛伯斯泰克氏征提示低钙血症（通常由于甲状腺切除术期间意外切除甲状旁腺引起）。低钙血症增加神经肌肉兴奋性，导致手足搐搦和潜在的癫痫发作。静脉注射葡萄糖酸钙是标准治疗方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize signs of hypocalcemia post-thyroidectomy. Link neuromuscular irritability to the need for safety (seizure precautions) and specific replacement (calcium).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别甲状腺切除术后低钙血症的征兆。将神经肌肉易激惹与安全需求（癫痫预防）和特定补充（钙）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":567,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_03_matrix_hypercalcemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.376","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.376.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.376.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,230],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,77],"fullStemEn":"A client with metastatic bone cancer is admitted with a serum calcium level of 12.8 mg/dL (3.2 mmol/L). For each nursing intervention, select whether it is an expected part of the care plan or requires follow-up with the provider.","fullStemZh":"一名转移性骨癌患者入院，血清钙水平为 12.8 mg/dL (3.2 mmol/L)。对于每项护理干预，请选择其属于护理计划的预期部分还是需要向医生跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing intervention, select whether it is an expected part of the care plan or requires follow-up with the provider.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项护理干预，请选择其属于护理计划的预期部分还是需要向医生跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with metastatic bone cancer is admitted with a serum calcium level of 12.8 mg/dL (3.2 mmol/L).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名转移性骨癌患者入院，血清钙水平为 12.8 mg/dL (3.2 mmol/L)。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Increase fluid intake to 3-4 liters per day if not contraindicated.","zh":"如无禁忌，将每日液体摄入量增加至 3-4 升。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Administer furosemide (loop diuretic) as prescribed.","zh":"按医嘱给予呋塞米（回路利尿剂）。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Encourage prolonged bed rest to prevent pathological fractures.","zh":"鼓励长期卧床以防止病理性骨折。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Monitor the ECG for a shortened QT interval.","zh":"监测心电图是否出现 QT 间期缩短。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Administer hydrochlorothiazide for fluid management.","zh":"给予氢氯噻嗪进行液体管理。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected","zh":"预期"},{"id":"c2","en":"Requires Follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hydration, when not contraindicated, and loop diuretics promote renal calcium excretion. Bed rest increases bone resorption, worsening hypercalcemia; weight-bearing activity is preferred. Thiazides decrease calcium excretion and should be avoided.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在无禁忌时补液以及使用回路利尿剂可促进肾脏排钙。卧床休息会增加骨吸收，加重高钙血症；首选负重活动。噻嗪类利尿剂减少钙排泄，应避免使用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between diuretics: Loop = 'Lose' calcium; Thiazide = 'Take' calcium (retain). Also remember that mobility helps keep calcium in the bones.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分利尿剂：回路利尿剂 = “丢失”钙；噻嗪类 = “带走”钙（保留）。还要记住，活动有助于将钙保留在骨骼中。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with metastatic bone cancer is admitted with a serum calcium level of 12.8 mg/dL (3.2 mmol/L).","controlSentenceZh":"一名转移性骨癌患者入院，血清钙水平为 12.8 mg/dL (3.2 mmol/L)。"}
{"queueIndex":568,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_04_cloze_hypomagnesemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.377","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.377.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.377.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,59],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic alcohol use disorder is admitted for malnutrition. Laboratory results reveal a magnesium level of 1.1 mEq/L (0.45 mmol/L).","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性酒精使用障碍的患者因营养不良入院。实验室结果显示镁水平为 1.1 mEq/L (0.45 mmol/L)。","terminalSentenceEn":"Laboratory results reveal a magnesium level of 1.1 mEq/L (0.45 mmol/L).","terminalSentenceZh":"实验室结果显示镁水平为 1.1 mEq/L (0.45 mmol/L)。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with chronic alcohol use disorder is admitted for malnutrition.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有慢性酒精使用障碍的患者因营养不良入院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should identify that the client is at high risk for {{1}}, should prioritize monitoring {{2}}, and anticipate an order for {{3}}.","zh":"护士应识别出该患者患 {{1}} 的风险很高，应优先监测 {{2}}，并预期会有 {{3}} 的医嘱。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Mobitz Type II heart block","zh":"莫氏 II 型心脏传导阻滞"},{"id":"o3","en":"pulmonary embolism","zh":"肺栓塞"},{"id":"o1","en":"Torsades de Pointes","zh":"尖端扭转型室性心动过速 (Torsades de Pointes)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"the ECG for prolonged QT intervals","zh":"心电图是否出现 QT 间期延长"},{"id":"o3","en":"daily weights","zh":"每日体重"},{"id":"o2","en":"urine output every hour","zh":"每小时尿量"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"IV calcium gluconate","zh":"静脉注射葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"o3","en":"oral phosphate binders","zh":"口服磷酸盐结合剂"},{"id":"o1","en":"IV magnesium sulfate","zh":"静脉注射硫酸镁"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypomagnesemia is common in alcoholism and can lead to life-threatening ventricular arrhythmias, specifically Torsades de Pointes. It is associated with a prolonged QT interval. IV magnesium sulfate is the treatment of choice for severe depletion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低镁血症在酒精中毒中很常见，可导致危及生命的室性心律失常，特别是尖端扭转型室性心动过速。它与 QT 间期延长有关。静脉注射硫酸镁是严重镁缺乏的首选治疗方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link 'Alcoholism' with 'Low Magnesium' and 'Torsades de Pointes'. In NCLEX, low Magnesium and low Potassium are critical for cardiac rhythm stability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“酒精中毒”与“低镁”和“尖端扭转型室性心动过速”联系起来。在 NCLEX 中，低镁和低钾对心律稳定性至关重要。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":569,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_05_matrix_hypermagnesemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.378","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.378.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.378.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,274],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,88],"fullStemEn":"A client with end-stage renal disease is admitted with a magnesium level of 5.2 mEq/L (2.15 mmol/L). For each assessment finding, select whether it is an expected manifestation of this magnesium level or requires immediate intervention to prevent cardiac/respiratory arrest.","fullStemZh":"一名患有终末期肾病的患者入院，镁水平为 5.2 mEq/L (2.15 mmol/L)。对于每项评估发现，请选择其属于该镁水平的预期表现，还是需要立即干预以防止心跳/呼吸骤停。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, select whether it is an expected manifestation of this magnesium level or requires immediate intervention to prevent cardiac/respiratory arrest.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项评估发现，请选择其属于该镁水平的预期表现，还是需要立即干预以防止心跳/呼吸骤停。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with end-stage renal disease is admitted with a magnesium level of 5.2 mEq/L (2.15 mmol/L).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有终末期肾病的患者入院，镁水平为 5.2 mEq/L (2.15 mmol/L)。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Absent deep tendon reflexes (DTRs)","zh":"深腱反射 (DTR) 消失"},{"id":"r2","en":"Respiratory rate of 8 breaths/min","zh":"呼吸频率 8 次/分"},{"id":"r3","en":"Hypotension (BP 88/50 mm Hg)","zh":"低血压 (BP 88/50 mm Hg)"},{"id":"r4","en":"Lethargy and drowsiness","zh":"嗜睡和昏沉"},{"id":"r5","en":"Prolonged PR interval on ECG","zh":"心电图 PR 间期延长"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires Immediate Intervention","zh":"需要立即干预"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected Manifestation","zh":"预期表现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypermagnesemia acts as a CNS depressant. DTRs are lost before respiratory depression occurs. Absent DTRs and severe bradypnea (RR <10) are critical warning signs of impending arrest. Hypotension and lethargy are expected at this level but are not as immediately life-threatening as respiratory failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高镁血症起中枢神经系统抑制剂的作用。在发生呼吸抑制之前，深腱反射通常先消失。DTR 消失和严重呼吸减慢 (RR <10) 是即将发生骤停的关键警告信号。该水平下预期会出现低血压和嗜睡，但不像呼吸衰竭那样具有即时的生命威胁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"ABC priority. Respiratory depression and loss of protective reflexes (DTRs) are higher priority than stable hypotension or drowsiness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）优先。呼吸抑制和保护性反射（DTR）消失的优先级高于稳定的低血压或嗜睡。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":570,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_06_cloze_hypophosphatemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.379","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.379.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.379.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,54],"fullStemEn":"A client with severe anorexia is started on total parenteral nutrition (TPN). Three days later, the client develops profound muscle weakness and difficulty weaning from the ventilator.","fullStemZh":"一名患有严重厌食症的患者开始接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN)。三天后，患者出现严重的肌肉无力，且难以脱离呼吸机。","terminalSentenceEn":"Three days later, the client develops profound muscle weakness and difficulty weaning from the ventilator.","terminalSentenceZh":"三天后，患者出现严重的肌肉无力，且难以脱离呼吸机。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with severe anorexia is started on total parenteral nutrition (TPN).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有严重厌食症的患者开始接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN)。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should suspect {{1}}, recognize that the underlying mechanism is {{2}}, and prioritize monitoring for {{3}}.","zh":"护士应怀疑为 {{1}}，识别出其潜在机制是 {{2}}，并优先监测 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"refeeding syndrome","zh":"再摄食综合征 (Refeeding syndrome)"},{"id":"o3","en":"Wernicke's encephalopathy","zh":"韦尼克脑病"},{"id":"o2","en":"dumping syndrome","zh":"倾倒综合征 (Dumping syndrome)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"insulin-induced shift of phosphate into cells","zh":"胰岛素诱导的磷酸盐向细胞内转移"},{"id":"o2","en":"excessive renal excretion of phosphate","zh":"肾脏过度排泄磷酸盐"},{"id":"o3","en":"inadequate intake of dietary phosphorus","zh":"饮食中磷摄入不足"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"respiratory failure","zh":"呼吸衰竭"},{"id":"o2","en":"hyperactive bowel sounds","zh":"肠鸣音亢进"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypertension","zh":"高血压"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Refeeding syndrome occurs when nutrition is reintroduced to a malnourished patient. Insulin release causes phosphate to move into cells for ATP production, causing severe serum hypophosphatemia. This leads to respiratory muscle weakness and failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当给营养不良的患者重新引入营养时，会发生再摄食综合征。胰岛素释放导致磷酸盐进入细胞用于 ATP 生成，从而引起严重的血清低磷血症。这会导致呼吸肌无力和衰竭。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect 'TPN/Malnutrition' with 'Hypophosphatemia' and 'Respiratory Failure'. The 'Low and Slow' rule applies to reintroducing nutrition in these patients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“TPN/营养不良”与“低磷血症”和“呼吸衰竭”联系起来。对此类患者重新引入营养应遵循“低速和缓慢”的原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":571,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_07_matrix_hyperphosphatemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.380","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.380.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.380.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,83],"fullStemEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) has a serum phosphate level of 6.5 mg/dL (2.1 mmol/L). For each clinical finding, select whether it is a manifestation of the resulting electrolyte imbalance or is unrelated.","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性肾病 (CKD) 的患者血清磷酸盐水平为 6.5 mg/dL (2.1 mmol/L)。对于每项临床发现，请选择其是所导致的电解质失衡的表现，还是不相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, select whether it is a manifestation of the resulting electrolyte imbalance or is unrelated.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项临床发现，请选择其是所导致的电解质失衡的表现，还是不相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) has a serum phosphate level of 6.5 mg/dL (2.1 mmol/L).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有慢性肾病 (CKD) 的患者血清磷酸盐水平为 6.5 mg/dL (2.1 mmol/L)。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Serum Calcium 7.5 mg/dL (1.88 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钙 7.5 mg/dL (1.88 mmol/L)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Positive Trousseau's sign","zh":"特鲁索氏征阳性"},{"id":"r3","en":"Soft tissue calcifications","zh":"软组织钙化"},{"id":"r4","en":"Hypoactive deep tendon reflexes","zh":"深腱反射减弱"},{"id":"r5","en":"Itching (pruritus)","zh":"瘙痒 (Pruritus)"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Manifestation","zh":"表现"},{"id":"c2","en":"Unrelated","zh":"不相关"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Phosphorus and Calcium have an inverse relationship. Hyperphosphatemia leads to hypocalcemia (causing Trousseau's sign and pruritus). Calcium-phosphate precipitates can cause soft tissue calcifications. Hypocalcemia causes hyperactive, not hypoactive, reflexes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"磷和钙具有反向关系。高磷血症导致低钙血症（引起特鲁索氏征和瘙痒）。磷酸钙沉淀可导致软组织钙化。低钙血症引起反射亢进，而非减弱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the Phosphorus-Calcium seesaw. If one is high, the other is likely low. Symptoms of high phosphorus are often identical to symptoms of low calcium.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住磷-钙跷跷板。如果一个高，另一个很可能低。高磷的症状通常与低钙的症状相同。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":572,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_08_cloze_dka_mgmt","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.381","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.381.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.381.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,70],"fullStemEn":"A client is being treated for Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA). The initial glucose was 550 mg/dL, and the potassium was 3.8 mEq/L. The nurse is following the hospital's titration protocol.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 治疗。初始血糖为 550 mg/dL，血钾为 3.8 mEq/L。护士正在遵循医院的滴定方案。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is following the hospital's titration protocol.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在遵循医院的滴定方案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The initial glucose was 550 mg/dL, and the potassium was 3.8 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"初始血糖为 550 mg/dL，血钾为 3.8 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"When the glucose level reaches {{1}}, the nurse should anticipate switching the IV fluid to {{2}} to prevent hypoglycemia while insulin continues and should initiate {{3}} even if the level is within normal range.","zh":"当血糖水平达到 {{1}} 时，护士应预期将静脉液体更换为 {{2}}，以便在继续胰岛素治疗时预防低血糖，并且即使血钾在正常范围内也应启动 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"250 mg/dL (13.9 mmol/L)","zh":"250 mg/dL (13.9 mmol/L)"},{"id":"o2","en":"100 mg/dL (5.5 mmol/L)","zh":"100 mg/dL (5.5 mmol/L)"},{"id":"o3","en":"400 mg/dL (22.2 mmol/L)","zh":"400 mg/dL (22.2 mmol/L)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"5% Dextrose with 0.45% saline","zh":"5% 葡萄糖 0.45% 生理盐水 (D5 1/2NS)"},{"id":"o2","en":"0.9% Normal Saline only","zh":"仅 0.9% 生理盐水"},{"id":"o3","en":"3% Hypertonic Saline","zh":"3% 高渗盐水"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"bicarbonate bolus","zh":"碳酸氢盐推注"},{"id":"o3","en":"concentrated insulin bolus","zh":"浓缩胰岛素推注"},{"id":"o1","en":"potassium replacement","zh":"钾补充"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When glucose drops below 250 mg/dL, dextrose is added to prevent hypoglycemia while insulin continues until ketoacidosis resolves. Potassium is monitored and replaced because insulin shifts potassium into cells; if potassium is below 3.5 mEq/L, insulin is delayed until replacement raises it above 3.5 mEq/L.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当血糖降至 250 mg/dL 以下时，加入葡萄糖以预防低血糖，并继续胰岛素治疗直至酮症酸中毒纠正。应监测并补充血钾，因为胰岛素会使钾进入细胞；若血钾低于 3.5 mEq/L，应暂缓胰岛素，直到补钾使其高于 3.5 mEq/L。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In DKA management: fluids first, assess and manage potassium before insulin, then add dextrose when glucose falls below 250 mg/dL so insulin can continue safely until ketoacidosis resolves.","testTakingStrategyZh":"DKA 管理顺序为：先补液，在胰岛素前评估并处理血钾，然后当血糖降至 250 mg/dL 以下时加入葡萄糖，使胰岛素能安全持续至酮症酸中毒纠正。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":573,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_09_matrix_hhs_neuro","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.382","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.382.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.382.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,67],"fullStemEn":"An elderly client is brought to the Emergency Department with profound dehydration and a glucose level of 850 mg/dL. For each finding, select whether it is more consistent with HHS or is typical of DKA.","fullStemZh":"一名老年患者因严重脱水和血糖水平达 850 mg/dL 被送往急诊科。对于每项发现，请选择其更符合 HHS 还是 DKA 的典型特征。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is more consistent with HHS or is typical of DKA.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请选择其更符合 HHS 还是 DKA 的典型特征。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An elderly client is brought to the Emergency Department with profound dehydration and a glucose level of 850 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名老年患者因严重脱水和血糖水平达 850 mg/dL 被送往急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Slow, gradual onset over several days","zh":"几天内缓慢、逐渐发作"},{"id":"r2","en":"Kussmaul respirations and fruity breath odor","zh":"库斯莫尔呼吸和烂苹果味气息"},{"id":"r3","en":"Profound mental status changes (stupor or coma)","zh":"显著的精神状态改变（木僵或昏迷）"},{"id":"r4","en":"Negative or trace urine ketones","zh":"尿酮阴性或微量"},{"id":"r5","en":"Associated with Type 2 Diabetes and illness/infection","zh":"与 2 型糖尿病和疾病/感染有关"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"DKA","zh":"DKA"},{"id":"c1","en":"HHS","zh":"HHS"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HHS typically affects older Type 2 diabetics and has a slower onset, leading to higher glucose and more severe dehydration/neuro changes. DKA presents with Kussmaul breathing (respiratory compensation for metabolic acidosis) and ketones.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HHS 通常影响老年 2 型糖尿病患者，起病较慢，导致更高的血糖和更严重的脱水/神经系统改变。DKA 表现为库斯莫尔呼吸（对代谢性酸中毒的呼吸代偿）和酮体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of HHS as 'DKA without the A (Acidosis)'. Because there is no acidosis, the glucose gets much higher before the patient seeks help, leading to severe neuro symptoms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将 HHS 视为“没有 A（酸中毒）的 DKA”。因为没有酸中毒，患者在寻求帮助前血糖会变得更高，从而导致严重的神经系统症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"An elderly client is brought to the Emergency Department with profound dehydration and a glucose level of 850 mg/dL.","controlSentenceZh":"一名老年患者因严重脱水和血糖水平达 850 mg/dL 被送往急诊科。"}
{"queueIndex":574,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d1_10_cloze_mag_electrolyte_link","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.383","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.383.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.383.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,53],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving aggressive potassium and calcium replacement for hypokalemia and hypocalcemia, but their laboratory values remain stubbornly low despite treatment.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因低钾血症和低钙血症正在接受积极的钾和钙补充治疗，但尽管进行了治疗，其实验室数值仍顽固地处于低位。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client is receiving aggressive potassium and calcium replacement for hypokalemia and hypocalcemia, but their laboratory values remain stubbornly low despite treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患者因低钾血症和低钙血症正在接受积极的钾和钙补充治疗，但尽管进行了治疗，其实验室数值仍顽固地处于低位。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should suspect concurrent {{1}}, recognize that this causes {{2}}, and prioritize advocating for {{3}} first.","zh":"护士应怀疑合并有 {{1}}，识别出这会导致 {{2}}，并优先主张先进行 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"hypernatremia","zh":"高钠血症"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypophosphatemia","zh":"低磷血症"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypomagnesemia","zh":"低镁血症"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"increased intestinal absorption of minerals","zh":"肠道对矿物质的吸收增加"},{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic alkalosis","zh":"代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"o1","en":"renal potassium wasting and PTH resistance","zh":"肾脏排钾增加和 PTH 抵抗"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"increased vitamin D doses","zh":"增加维生素 D 剂量"},{"id":"o3","en":"hemodialysis","zh":"血液透析"},{"id":"o1","en":"magnesium replacement","zh":"镁补充"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Magnesium is required for the proper function of the sodium-potassium pump and for the release/action of Parathyroid Hormone (PTH). Without magnesium, potassium continues to leak from the kidneys, and calcium cannot be mobilized from bone. Magnesium must be corrected first for K and Ca to normalize.","rationaleCorrectZh":"镁是钠钾泵正常运行以及甲状旁腺激素 (PTH) 释放/发挥作用所必需的。没有镁，钾会继续从肾脏流失，并且钙无法从骨骼中动员出来。必须先纠正镁，钾和钙才能恢复正常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of Magnesium as the 'key' that unlocks the door for Potassium and Calcium. If the door won't open (refractory), look for the key (Magnesium).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将镁视为为钾和钙开门的“钥匙”。如果门打不开（顽固性），请寻找钥匙（镁）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":575,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.384","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.384.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.384.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[196,232],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,68],"fullStemEn":"A 72-year-old client with a history of heart failure is admitted with increased shortness of breath, orthopnea, and crackles in all lung fields. The client's oxygen saturation is 88% on room air. The nurse notes pink, frothy sputum.","fullStemZh":"一名有心力衰竭病史的72岁患者因呼吸困难加重、端坐呼吸以及全肺野湿啰音入院。患者在室温空气下的氧饱和度为88%。护士注意到粉红色泡沫痰。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse notes pink, frothy sputum.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士注意到粉红色泡沫痰。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's oxygen saturation is 88% on room air.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者在室温空气下的氧饱和度为88%。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first {{1}} and then prepare to administer {{2}}.","zh":"护士应首先 {{1}}，然后准备给予 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"place the client in High-Fowler's position","zh":"将患者置于高坐卧位"},{"id":"o3","en":"administer a bolus of IV normal saline","zh":"给予静脉注射生理盐水推注"},{"id":"o2","en":"perform a bedside chest X-ray","zh":"进行床边胸部X光检查"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"intravenous furosemide","zh":"静脉注射呋塞米"},{"id":"o2","en":"sublingual nitroglycerin","zh":"舌下含服硝酸甘油"},{"id":"o3","en":"nebulized albuterol","zh":"雾化吸入沙丁胺醇"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"High-Fowler's position maximizes lung expansion and decreases venous return (preload), which is the priority for a client in acute pulmonary edema. IV furosemide is the standard treatment to rapidly reduce fluid volume in heart failure exacerbation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高坐卧位可最大限度地扩大肺部并减少回心血量（前负荷），这是急性肺水肿患者的首要措施。静脉注射呋塞米是快速减少心力衰竭加重期体液量的标准治疗方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the priority action for immediate respiratory distress and the standard pharmacological treatment for volume overload.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注处理急性呼吸窘迫的首要措施以及针对容量负荷过重的标准药物治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":576,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.385","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.385.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.385.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,43],"fullStemEn":"A 65-year-old client with a urinary tract infection is being monitored. The nurse reviews the latest clinical findings to determine the risk of sepsis.","fullStemZh":"正在监测一名患有尿路感染的65岁患者。护士审查最新的临床发现，以确定发生败血症的风险。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the latest clinical findings to determine the risk of sepsis.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士审查最新的临床发现，以确定发生败血症的风险。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 65-year-old client with a urinary tract infection is being monitored.","penultimateSentenceZh":"正在监测一名患有尿路感染的65岁患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Mean Arterial Pressure (MAP) of 58 mmHg","zh":"平均动脉压 (MAP) 为 58 mmHg"},{"id":"r2","en":"Lactate level of 4.2 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸水平为 4.2 mmol/L"},{"id":"r3","en":"Urine output of 50 mL in the last 4 hours","zh":"过去4小时尿量为 50 mL"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not Concerning for Organ Dysfunction or Hypoperfusion","zh":"不提示器官功能障碍或低灌注"},{"id":"c1","en":"Concerning for Organ Dysfunction or Hypoperfusion","zh":"提示器官功能障碍或低灌注"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MAP 58 mmHg, lactate 4.2 mmol/L, and marked oliguria are concerning for organ dysfunction or tissue hypoperfusion in a client with suspected infection and require urgent sepsis evaluation and treatment. None independently diagnoses sepsis or septic shock; diagnosis requires the complete clinical context, and septic shock includes persistent vasopressor need with elevated lactate despite adequate resuscitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在疑似感染患者中，MAP 58 mmHg、乳酸 4.2 mmol/L 和明显少尿均提示器官功能障碍或组织低灌注，需要紧急进行败血症评估和治疗。这些发现均不能单独诊断败血症或感染性休克；诊断需结合完整临床背景，而感染性休克还包括充分复苏后仍需血管加压药且乳酸升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate warning signs from diagnostic criteria. Hypotension, elevated lactate, and oliguria signal hypoperfusion, but sepsis and septic shock require the full infection, organ-dysfunction, resuscitation, and vasopressor context.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分预警信号与诊断标准。低血压、乳酸升高和少尿提示低灌注，但败血症和感染性休克需结合感染、器官功能障碍、复苏及血管加压药使用的完整背景。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":577,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.386","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.386.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.386.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,63],"fullStemEn":"A client with Type 1 diabetes is admitted with DKA. The blood glucose is 450 mg/dL and the potassium is 3.2 mEq/L. The provider orders IV regular insulin and potassium replacement.","fullStemZh":"一名1型糖尿病患者因DKA入院。血糖为450 mg/dL，血钾为3.2 mEq/L。医生开具了静脉注射常规胰岛素和补钾的医嘱。","terminalSentenceEn":"The provider orders IV regular insulin and potassium replacement.","terminalSentenceZh":"医生开具了静脉注射常规胰岛素和补钾的医嘱。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The blood glucose is 450 mg/dL and the potassium is 3.2 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血糖为450 mg/dL，血钾为3.2 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should prioritize {{1}} because insulin administration will {{2}}.","zh":"护士应优先处理 {{1}}，因为给予胰岛素会 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"starting the insulin infusion","zh":"开始输注胰岛素"},{"id":"o1","en":"initiating potassium replacement","zh":"开始补钾"},{"id":"o3","en":"administering sodium bicarbonate","zh":"给予碳酸氢钠"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"cause rapid cerebral edema","zh":"导致快速脑水肿"},{"id":"o1","en":"further decrease serum potassium levels","zh":"进一步降低血清钾水平"},{"id":"o3","en":"increase the risk of hypernatremia","zh":"增加高钠血症的风险"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Insulin shifts potassium into the cells, which can worsen hypokalemia. In DKA, if the potassium is already low, it must be replaced before starting insulin to prevent life-threatening arrhythmias.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胰岛素会使钾离子进入细胞内，这可能会加重低钾血症。在DKA中，如果血钾已经很低，必须在开始输注胰岛素之前进行补钾，以防止发生危及生命的心律失常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the physiological effect of insulin on electrolyte balance, especially potassium.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑胰岛素对电解质平衡（尤其是钾）的生理影响。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":578,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.387","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.387.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.387.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,44],"fullStemEn":"The nurse in the emergency department (ED) receives reports on four clients. The nurse must prioritize which client to see first based on the severity of their condition.","fullStemZh":"急诊科 (ED) 护士收到四名患者的报告。护士必须根据病情严重程度确定优先接诊哪位患者。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must prioritize which client to see first based on the severity of their condition.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须根据病情严重程度确定优先接诊哪位患者。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse in the emergency department (ED) receives reports on four clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急诊科 (ED) 护士收到四名患者的报告。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"6-year-old with barking cough and stridor at rest","zh":"6岁儿童，伴有犬吠样咳嗽和静息性喉鸣"},{"id":"r2","en":"45-year-old with sudden onset 'worst headache of my life'","zh":"45岁患者，突然出现“一生中最严重的头痛”"},{"id":"r3","en":"28-year-old with a compound fracture of the tibia","zh":"28岁患者，胫骨开放性骨折"},{"id":"r4","en":"70-year-old with chronic COPD and O2 saturation of 90%","zh":"70岁患者，患有慢性COPD，血氧饱和度为90%"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Highest Priority","zh":"最高优先级"},{"id":"c3","en":"Medium Priority","zh":"中等优先级"},{"id":"c2","en":"High Priority","zh":"高优先级"},{"id":"c4","en":"Lower Priority","zh":"较低优先级"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The child with stridor at rest has an immediate airway threat. The 'worst headache' suggests a subarachnoid hemorrhage (neurological emergency). The compound fracture is urgent but secondary to airway and neuro. Chronic COPD with 90% saturation is expected and stable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"静息性喉鸣的儿童存在即时气道威胁。“最严重的头痛”提示蛛网膜下腔出血（神经内科急症）。开放性骨折很紧急，但次于气道和神经系统。慢性COPD且血氧饱和度为90%属于预期内且稳定的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) and consider 'actual' vs 'potential' threats.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）原则，并考虑“实际”威胁与“潜在”威胁。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":579,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.388","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.388.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.388.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,40],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis (TB). The nurse must implement appropriate precautions to prevent the spread of the pathogen.","fullStemZh":"一名疑似肺结核 (TB) 患者入院。护士必须采取适当的预防措施以防止病原体传播。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must implement appropriate precautions to prevent the spread of the pathogen.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须采取适当的预防措施以防止病原体传播。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis (TB).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名疑似肺结核 (TB) 患者入院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client should be placed in a {{1}} and healthcare workers must wear a {{2}} when entering the room.","zh":"患者应被安置在 {{1}}，医护人员进入病房时必须佩戴 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"semi-private room","zh":"半私立病房"},{"id":"o2","en":"positive pressure room","zh":"正压病房"},{"id":"o1","en":"negative pressure room","zh":"负压病房"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"N95 respirator mask","zh":"N95 呼吸防护口罩"},{"id":"o3","en":"face shield only","zh":"仅面罩"},{"id":"o2","en":"surgical mask","zh":"外科口罩"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pulmonary TB requires airborne precautions, including a negative pressure room (to keep air from flowing into hallways) and N95 masks (to filter out small droplet nuclei).","rationaleCorrectZh":"肺结核需要空气传播预防措施，包括负压病房（防止空气流向走廊）和 N95 口罩（过滤掉微小的液滴核）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between airborne, droplet, and contact precautions based on the pathogen's transmission route.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据病原体的传播途径区分空气传播、飞沫传播和接触传播预防措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":580,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.389","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.389.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.389.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[90,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,71],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic kidney disease presents with lethargy and deep, rapid respirations. The nurse analyzes the ABG results: pH 7.25, PaCO2 30 mmHg, HCO3 15 mEq/L.","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性肾脏病的患者出现嗜睡以及深快呼吸。护士分析 ABG 结果：pH 7.25，PaCO2 30 mmHg，HCO3 15 mEq/L。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse analyzes the ABG results: pH 7.25, PaCO2 30 mmHg, HCO3 15 mEq/L.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士分析 ABG 结果：pH 7.25，PaCO2 30 mmHg，HCO3 15 mEq/L。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with chronic kidney disease presents with lethargy and deep, rapid respirations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有慢性肾脏病的患者出现嗜睡以及深快呼吸。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Acid-Base Imbalance Type","zh":"酸碱失衡类型"},{"id":"r2","en":"Compensation Status","zh":"代偿状态"},{"id":"r3","en":"Expected Clinical Sign","zh":"预期的临床体征"}],"columns":[{"id":"c4","en":"Not Applicable","zh":"不适用"},{"id":"c3","en":"Kussmaul Respirations","zh":"库斯莫尔呼吸"},{"id":"c2","en":"Partial Compensation","zh":"部分代偿"},{"id":"c1","en":"Metabolic Acidosis","zh":"代谢性酸中毒"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pH < 7.35 and low HCO3 indicate metabolic acidosis. The low PaCO2 shows the lungs are trying to compensate by blowing off CO2 (Kussmaul respirations). Since the pH is not back to normal, it is partially compensated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"pH < 7.35 且 HCO3 低指示代谢性酸中毒。低 PaCO2 表明肺部正试图通过排出 CO2（库斯莫尔呼吸）来进行代偿。由于 pH 值未恢复正常，因此属于部分代偿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ROME (Respiratory Opposite, Metabolic Equal) mnemonic and check the pH for compensation status.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ROME 助记词并检查 pH 值以确定代偿状态。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":581,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.390","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.390.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.390.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,49],"fullStemEn":"An immobile client is assessed for risk of pressure injuries using the Braden Scale. The nurse identifies areas for improvement in the care plan.","fullStemZh":"使用 Braden 量表评估一名卧床患者发生压力性损伤的风险。护士确定了护理计划中需要改进的领域。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse identifies areas for improvement in the care plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士确定了护理计划中需要改进的领域。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An immobile client is assessed for risk of pressure injuries using the Braden Scale.","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用 Braden 量表评估一名卧床患者发生压力性损伤的风险。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To minimize shear force, the head of the bed should be kept at {{1}} or less, and the client should be repositioned every {{2}}.","zh":"为了尽量减少剪切力，床头应保持在 {{1}} 或更低角度，并且应每 {{2}} 为患者更换一次体位。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"60 degrees","zh":"60 度"},{"id":"o1","en":"30 degrees","zh":"30 度"},{"id":"o2","en":"45 degrees","zh":"45 度"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"8 hours","zh":"8 小时"},{"id":"o1","en":"2 hours","zh":"2 小时"},{"id":"o2","en":"4 hours","zh":"4 小时"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Keeping the head of the bed at or below 30 degrees reduces the risk of the client sliding down, which causes shear. Repositioning every 2 hours is the standard evidence-based practice for pressure relief.","rationaleCorrectZh":"将床头保持在 30 度或以下可降低患者下滑的风险，从而减少剪切力。每 2 小时更换一次体位是减轻压力的标准循证实践。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify specific nursing interventions that directly address the mechanical causes of pressure injuries (friction and shear).","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定直接针对压力性损伤机械原因（摩擦力和剪切力）的特定护理干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":582,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.391","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.391.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.391.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[49,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,41],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted for alcohol detoxification. The nurse monitors for signs of withdrawal using the Clinical Institute Withdrawal Assessment (CIWA).","fullStemZh":"一名患者入院进行酒精脱毒。护士使用临床研究所戒断评估 (CIWA) 监测戒断征象。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse monitors for signs of withdrawal using the Clinical Institute Withdrawal Assessment (CIWA).","terminalSentenceZh":"护士使用临床研究所戒断评估 (CIWA) 监测戒断征象。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted for alcohol detoxification.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者入院进行酒精脱毒。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Severe confusion with visual hallucinations and autonomic instability","zh":"严重意识混乱，伴视幻觉和自主神经不稳定"},{"id":"r2","en":"Generalized tonic-clonic seizures","zh":"全身性强直-阵挛性发作"},{"id":"r3","en":"Mild tremors and anxiety","zh":"轻微震颤和焦虑"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Early Withdrawal (6-24h)","zh":"早期戒断 (6-24小时)"},{"id":"c3","en":"Delirium Tremens (>48h)","zh":"震颤性谵妄 (>48小时)"},{"id":"c2","en":"Withdrawal Seizures (12-48h)","zh":"戒断性癫痫 (12-48小时)"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mild tremors/anxiety start early. Seizures typically occur within 12-48 hours. Delirium Tremens (DTs), which includes hallucinations and severe autonomic instability, usually occurs after 48-72 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"轻微震颤/焦虑开始较早。癫痫发作通常发生在 12-48 小时内。震颤性谵妄 (DTs)，包括幻觉和严重的自主神经不稳定，通常发生在 48-72 小时后。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the timeline of alcohol withdrawal symptoms to differentiate between stages.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想酒精戒断症状的时间轴以区分不同阶段。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":583,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.392","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.392.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.392.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,54],"fullStemEn":"A pregnant client at 34 weeks gestation presents with a headache and 'seeing spots'. Her blood pressure is 162/110 mmHg and urinalysis shows 3+ protein.","fullStemZh":"一名孕 34 周的孕妇出现头痛和“眼前冒金星”。她的血压为 162/110 mmHg，尿检显示尿蛋白 3+。","terminalSentenceEn":"Her blood pressure is 162/110 mmHg and urinalysis shows 3+ protein.","terminalSentenceZh":"她的血压为 162/110 mmHg，尿检显示尿蛋白 3+。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A pregnant client at 34 weeks gestation presents with a headache and 'seeing spots'.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名孕 34 周的孕妇出现头痛和“眼前冒金星”。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The priority nursing action is to initiate {{1}} and monitor for {{2}}.","zh":"首要的护理措施是开始 {{1}} 并监测 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"fluid bolus","zh":"液体推注"},{"id":"o1","en":"seizure precautions","zh":"癫痫预防措施"},{"id":"o3","en":"ambulation assistance","zh":"协助走动"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"magnesium toxicity","zh":"镁中毒"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypoglycemia","zh":"低血糖"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypercalcemia","zh":"高钙血症"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe preeclampsia puts the client at high risk for eclampsia (seizures). Seizure precautions are vital. Magnesium sulfate is typically given for prevention, requiring close monitoring for toxicity (e.g., loss of DTRs).","rationaleCorrectZh":"重度子痫前期使患者处于子痫（抽搐）的高风险中。癫痫预防措施至关重要。通常给予硫酸镁进行预防，这需要密切监测中毒情况（例如深反射消失）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize safety (seizure risk) in high-risk obstetric clients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在高风险产科患者中优先考虑安全（抽搐风险）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A pregnant client at 34 weeks gestation presents with a headache and 'seeing spots'.","controlSentenceZh":"一名孕 34 周的孕妇出现头痛和“眼前冒金星”。"}
{"queueIndex":584,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d10_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.393","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.393.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.393.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,34],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving treatment for hyperkalemia. The nurse evaluates the effectiveness of the interventions based on follow-up findings.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受高钾血症治疗。护士根据后续发现评估干预措施的有效性。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates the effectiveness of the interventions based on follow-up findings.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士根据后续发现评估干预措施的有效性。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving treatment for hyperkalemia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者正在接受高钾血症治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"ECG shows peaked T-waves","zh":"心电图显示 T 波高尖"},{"id":"r2","en":"Serum potassium of 4.5 mEq/L","zh":"血清钾为 4.5 mEq/L"},{"id":"r3","en":"Client reports muscle weakness","zh":"患者报告肌肉无力"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Goal Met","zh":"目标达成"},{"id":"c2","en":"Goal Not Met","zh":"目标未达成"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A potassium of 4.5 mEq/L is within the normal range (3.5-5.0), meeting the goal. Peaked T-waves and muscle weakness are signs of hyperkalemia that indicate the condition has not yet resolved.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钾为 4.5 mEq/L 在正常范围内 (3.5-5.0)，达成了目标。T 波高尖和肌肉无力是高钾血症的征象，表明病情尚未解决。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify normal vs abnormal values and clinical manifestations of the condition being treated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分正常值与异常值，以及所治疗疾病的临床表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":585,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_digoxin_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.394","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.394.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.394.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,52],"fullStemEn":"A client with heart failure is taking digoxin 0.125 mg daily. Which clinical manifestation should the nurse recognize as the earliest sign of digoxin toxicity?","fullStemZh":"一名患有心力衰竭的患者每日服用地高辛 0.125 mg。护士应识别出哪种临床表现是地高辛中毒的最早迹象？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestation should the nurse recognize as the earliest sign of digoxin toxicity?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应识别出哪种临床表现是地高辛中毒的最早迹象？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with heart failure is taking digoxin 0.125 mg daily.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有心力衰竭的患者每日服用地高辛 0.125 mg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Photophobia","zh":"畏光"},{"id":"A","en":"Yellow-green halos around lights","zh":"光线周围出现黄绿色光晕"},{"id":"C","en":"Anorexia and nausea","zh":"食欲减退和恶心"},{"id":"B","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Gastrointestinal symptoms such as anorexia, nausea, and vomiting are typically the earliest signs of digoxin toxicity. Visual disturbances (like halos) and cardiac arrhythmias (like bradycardia) usually occur later as toxicity progresses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胃肠道症状如食欲减退、恶心和呕吐通常是地高辛中毒的最早迹象。视觉障碍（如光晕）和心律失常（如心动过缓）通常随着中毒的进展在稍后出现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When asked for the 'earliest' sign of digoxin toxicity, prioritize gastrointestinal symptoms over visual or cardiac changes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当被问及地高辛中毒的“最早”迹象时，优先考虑胃肠道症状，而非视觉或心脏变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":586,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_digoxin_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.395","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.395.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.395.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer digoxin to a client with heart failure. Which laboratory result would most significantly increase the client's risk for developing digoxin toxicity?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名心力衰竭患者给予地高辛。哪项实验室检查结果会最显著地增加患者发生地高辛中毒的风险？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory result would most significantly increase the client's risk for developing digoxin toxicity?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项实验室检查结果会最显著地增加患者发生地高辛中毒的风险？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer digoxin to a client with heart failure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名心力衰竭患者给予地高辛。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Serum magnesium level of 1.8 mg/dL (0.74 mmol/L)","zh":"血清镁水平为 1.8 mg/dL (0.74 mmol/L)"},{"id":"A","en":"Serum calcium level of 8.5 mg/dL (2.1 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钙水平为 8.5 mg/dL (2.1 mmol/L)"},{"id":"D","en":"Serum sodium level of 132 mEq/L (132 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钠水平为 132 mEq/L (132 mmol/L)"},{"id":"C","en":"Serum potassium level of 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钾水平为 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L)"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypokalemia (low potassium) sensitizes the myocardium to digoxin, significantly increasing the risk of toxicity even if the digoxin level is within the therapeutic range. A potassium level of 3.2 mEq/L is below the normal range (3.5–5.0 mEq/L).","rationaleCorrectZh":"低钾血症使心肌对地高辛敏感，即使地高辛水平在治疗范围内，也会显著增加中毒风险。3.2 mEq/L 的钾水平低于正常范围（3.5–5.0 mEq/L）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the relationship: Low Potassium = High Digoxin Risk. Always monitor potassium levels closely for any client on digitalis therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住这个关系：低钾 = 地高辛中毒高风险。对于任何接受洋地黄治疗的患者，务必密切监测血钾水平。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":587,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_doac_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.396","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.396.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.396.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,35],"fullStemEn":"A client is being discharged with a new prescription for apixaban. Which instruction should the nurse include in the discharge teaching?","fullStemZh":"一名患者带着新开具的阿哌沙班处方出院。护士在出院指导中应包含哪项内容？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include in the discharge teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在出院指导中应包含哪项内容？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is being discharged with a new prescription for apixaban.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者带着新开具的阿哌沙班处方出院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"You will need to have your INR checked weekly to adjust the dose.","zh":"您需要每周检查一次 INR 以调整剂量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid green leafy vegetables like spinach and kale.","zh":"避免食用菠菜和羽衣甘蓝等绿叶蔬菜。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use a firm-bristled toothbrush to ensure good oral hygiene.","zh":"使用硬毛牙刷以确保良好的口腔卫生。"},{"id":"C","en":"Do not stop taking this medication without consulting your healthcare provider.","zh":"未经咨询医生，请勿停用此药物。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Direct Oral Anticoagulants (DOACs) like apixaban have a short half-life. Abruptly stopping the medication significantly increases the risk of stroke or systemic embolism. Clients must be instructed to maintain adherence and never stop the drug without medical supervision.","rationaleCorrectZh":"像阿哌沙班这样的直接口服抗凝剂（DOACs）半衰期较短。突然停药会显著增加脑卒中或全身性栓塞的风险。必须指导患者保持服药依从性，未经医疗监督绝不自行停药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between warfarin and DOACs (apixaban, rivaroxaban). DOACs do not require frequent blood monitoring or dietary Vitamin K restrictions, but they do require strict adherence due to their short half-life.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分华法林和 DOACs（阿哌沙班、利伐沙班）。DOACs 不需要频繁的血液监测或维生素 K 饮食限制，但由于半衰期短，需要严格遵守服药规定。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":588,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_doac_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.397","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.397.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.397.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client who has been taking rivaroxaban for three months. Which findings should the nurse prioritize for immediate follow-up? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名已服用利伐沙班三个月的患者。哪些发现是护士应优先立即跟进的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings should the nurse prioritize for immediate follow-up?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现是护士应优先立即跟进的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Sudden, severe headache and blurred vision","zh":"突然的剧烈头痛和视力模糊"},{"id":"E","en":"Increased bruising on the arms","zh":"手臂淤青增多"},{"id":"A","en":"Abdominal pain and coffee-ground emesis","zh":"腹痛和咖啡色呕吐物"},{"id":"B","en":"Nosebleeds that stop within 2 minutes of pressure","zh":"压迫 2 分钟内停止的鼻出血"},{"id":"D","en":"Black, tarry stools","zh":"黑色柏油样便"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Priority findings include signs of major or internal bleeding. Coffee-ground emesis and black tarry stools indicate gastrointestinal bleeding. Sudden, severe headache could indicate an intracranial hemorrhage, which is a life-threatening complication of anticoagulant therapy. Minor nosebleeds and bruising are common side effects that usually do not require immediate emergency intervention unless severe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先考虑的发现包括重大出血或内出血的迹象。咖啡色呕吐物 和黑色柏油样便 提示胃肠道出血。突然剧烈的头痛 可能提示颅内出血，这是抗凝治疗中危及生命的并发症。轻微的鼻出血和淤青是常见的副作用，除非严重，否则通常不需要立即进行急诊干预。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In anticoagulant questions, prioritize signs of major internal bleeding (GI, intracranial) over minor external bleeding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在涉及抗凝药物的问题中，优先处理重大内出血（胃肠道、颅内）的体征，而非轻微的外出血。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":589,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_insulin_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.398","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.398.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.398.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[107,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,60],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to mix 10 units of regular insulin and 20 units of NPH insulin in a single syringe. Which action is correct?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备在同一个注射器中混合 10 单位正规胰岛素（Regular）和 20 单位 NPH 胰岛素。哪项操作是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项操作是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to mix 10 units of regular insulin and 20 units of NPH insulin in a single syringe.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备在同一个注射器中混合 10 单位正规胰岛素（Regular）和 20 单位 NPH 胰岛素。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Inject 20 units of air into the NPH vial first.","zh":"先向 NPH 药瓶中注入 20 单位空气。"},{"id":"B","en":"Draw up the NPH insulin before drawing up the regular insulin.","zh":"在抽取正规胰岛素之前先抽取 NPH 胰岛素。"},{"id":"C","en":"Inject 10 units of air into the regular insulin vial first.","zh":"先向正规胰岛素药瓶中注入 10 单位空气。"},{"id":"A","en":"Shake the NPH vial vigorously to ensure even distribution.","zh":"剧烈摇晃 NPH 药瓶以确保分布均匀。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence for mixing insulin is: 1. Inject air into the NPH (cloudy) vial. 2. Inject air into the regular (clear) vial. 3. Draw up the regular insulin. 4. Draw up the NPH insulin. This sequence prevents contaminating the clear, fast-acting insulin with the longer-acting NPH insulin.","rationaleCorrectZh":"混合胰岛素的正确顺序是：1. 向 NPH（浑浊）瓶中注入空气。2. 向正规（澄清）瓶中注入空气。3. 抽取正规胰岛素。4. 抽取 NPH 胰岛素。该顺序可防止长效 NPH 胰岛素污染澄清的短效胰岛素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the mnemonic 'RN' (Regular before NPH) or 'Clear before Cloudy' for the order of drawing up the insulin. For air injection, it's the reverse: Cloudy then Clear.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用助记词“RN”（Regular before NPH，正规在 NPH 之前）或“先清后浊”来记忆抽药顺序。注气顺序则相反：先浊后清。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":590,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_insulin_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.399","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.399.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.399.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,43],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is administering 8 units of aspart insulin to a client. At what time should the nurse ensure the client consumes their meal?","fullStemZh":"护士正在给患者给予 8 单位门冬胰岛素（Aspart）。护士应确保患者在什么时间进餐？","terminalSentenceEn":"At what time should the nurse ensure the client consumes their meal?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应确保患者在什么时间进餐？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is administering 8 units of aspart insulin to a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在给患者给予 8 单位门冬胰岛素（Aspart）。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Within 5 to 15 minutes of the injection","zh":"注射后 5 至 15 分钟内"},{"id":"A","en":"Immediately before the injection only","zh":"仅在注射前即刻"},{"id":"C","en":"2 hours after the injection","zh":"注射后 2 小时"},{"id":"B","en":"30 to 60 minutes after the injection","zh":"注射后 30 至 60 分钟"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aspart is a rapid-acting insulin with an onset of 10 to 20 minutes. It must be administered when the meal is ready or already present at the bedside to prevent hypoglycemia. The ideal timing is 5 to 15 minutes before eating.","rationaleCorrectZh":"门冬胰岛素是一种超短效胰岛素，起效时间为 10 至 20 分钟。必须在餐食准备好或已送达床头时给药，以防止低血糖。理想的给药时间是餐前 5 至 15 分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the type of insulin. Rapid-acting (aspart/lispro) = 'Eat now'. Short-acting (regular) = 'Wait 30 mins'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注胰岛素的类型。超短效（门冬/赖脯）=“立刻吃”。短效（正规）=“等 30 分钟”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":591,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_insulin_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.400","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.400.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.400.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[302,343],"terminalOffsetsZh":[102,115],"fullStemEn":"The healthcare provider prescribes 15 units of NPH insulin and 5 units of regular insulin for a client with type 2 diabetes. The medication is provided in U-100 vials. What is the total volume in mL that the nurse will have in the syringe after drawing up both doses? (Record your answer as a decimal. Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","fullStemZh":"医疗服务提供者为一名 2 型糖尿病患者开具了 15 单位 NPH 胰岛素和 5 单位正规胰岛素的医嘱。该药物由 U-100 药瓶提供。护士在抽取这两个剂量后，注射器中的总容量是多少毫升？（以小数记录答案。请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not write the unit in the answer box.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请勿在答案框中填写单位。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a decimal.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以小数记录答案。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["0.2"],"numeric":{"value":0.2,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"U-100 insulin means there are 100 units per 1 mL. Total units = 15 (NPH) + 5 (Regular) = 20 units. To find the volume: 20 units / 100 units/mL = 0.2 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"U-100 胰岛素意味着每 1 毫升含有 100 单位。总单位 = 15 (NPH) + 5 (正规) = 20 单位。计算体积：20 单位 / 100 单位/毫升 = 0.2 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Understand that 'U-100' is a concentration (100 units/mL). Always sum the total units before dividing by 100 to find the mL volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"理解“U-100”是一种浓度（100 单位/毫升）。在除以 100 计算毫升体积之前，务必先算出总单位数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a decimal.","controlSentenceZh":"以小数记录答案。"}
{"queueIndex":592,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_digoxin_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.401","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.401.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.401.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,44],"fullStemEn":"A client who takes digoxin for heart failure is admitted with suspected toxicity. Which clinical findings would support this diagnosis? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名因心力衰竭服用地高辛的患者因疑似中毒入院。哪些临床表现支持这一诊断？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical findings would support this diagnosis?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些临床表现支持这一诊断？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Serum digoxin level of 2.4 ng/mL (3.1 nmol/L)","zh":"血清地高辛水平为 2.4 ng/mL (3.1 nmol/L)"},{"id":"E","en":"Nausea and vomiting","zh":"恶心和呕吐"},{"id":"A","en":"Blurry, yellow-tinged vision","zh":"视物模糊、发黄"},{"id":"C","en":"Heart rate of 110 beats/min","zh":"心率为 110 次/分"},{"id":"D","en":"Confusion and lethargy","zh":"意识模糊和嗜睡"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Signs of digoxin toxicity include visual disturbances, elevated serum levels above 2.0 ng/mL, central nervous system changes like confusion, and gastrointestinal symptoms (E). Bradycardia (low heart rate), not tachycardia, is the expected cardiac finding in digoxin toxicity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"地高辛中毒的体征包括视觉障碍、血清水平高于 2.0 ng/mL、中枢神经系统变化如意识模糊 以及胃肠道症状 (E)。地高辛中毒预期的心脏表现是心动过缓（心率低），而非心动过速。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the acronym 'Visual, GI, CNS, Cardiac'. But remember that cardiac changes usually mean the heart rate goes DOWN.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想一下缩写“Visual（视觉）、GI（胃肠）、CNS（中枢神经）、Cardiac（心脏）”。但请记住，心脏变化通常意味着心率下降。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":593,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_doac_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.402","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.402.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.402.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[203,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,57],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing the medications for a client who is prescribed rivaroxaban. Which other medications or supplements should the nurse report to the healthcare provider due to a potential interaction? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名使用利伐沙班患者的药物。由于潜在的相互作用，护士应向医生报告哪些其他药物或补充剂？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which other medications or supplements should the nurse report to the healthcare provider due to a potential interaction?","penultimateSentenceZh":"由于潜在的相互作用，护士应向医生报告哪些其他药物或补充剂？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Ibuprofen for occasional headache","zh":"偶发头痛时服用布洛芬"},{"id":"D","en":"Vitamin C supplement","zh":"维生素 C 补充剂"},{"id":"E","en":"Acetaminophen","zh":"对乙酰氨基酚"},{"id":"C","en":"St. John's Wort","zh":"圣约翰草"},{"id":"A","en":"Aspirin 81 mg daily","zh":"每日服用阿司匹林 81 mg"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aspirin and NSAIDs like ibuprofen increase the risk of bleeding when combined with anticoagulants. St. John's Wort is a potent inducer of CYP3A4 and P-gp, which can decrease the serum levels and efficacy of rivaroxaban. Vitamin C and Acetaminophen (E) generally do not have significant interactions with DOACs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阿司匹林 和布洛芬等非甾体抗炎药 与抗凝药合用时会增加出血风险。圣约翰草 是 CYP3A4 和 P-gp 的强效诱导剂，会降低利伐沙班的血清水平和疗效。维生素 C 和对乙酰氨基酚 (E) 通常与 DOACs 没有显著的相互作用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the 'Three Gs' (Ginkgo, Garlic, Ginseng) and St. John's Wort for herbal interactions, and avoid NSAIDs/Antiplatelets for bleeding risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注“3G”草药（银杏、大蒜、人参）和圣约翰草的相互作用，并避免使用非甾体抗炎药/抗血小板药物以防出血风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":594,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d2_insulin_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.403","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.403.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.403.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,62],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing education to a client who was recently diagnosed with type 1 diabetes. Which statements by the client indicate a correct understanding of insulin storage and administration? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名最近诊断为 1 型糖尿病的患者进行教育。患者的哪些陈述表明其对胰岛素的储存和给药有正确的理解？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements by the client indicate a correct understanding of insulin storage and administration?","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的哪些陈述表明其对胰岛素的储存和给药有正确的理解？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"I should always have a source of fast-acting carbohydrate with me.","zh":"我应该随身携带快速起效的碳水化合物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Once I open a vial, I can keep it at room temperature for up to 28 days.","zh":"药瓶一旦开封，我可以在室温下保存最多 28 天。"},{"id":"E","en":"If I exercise more than usual, I might need to decrease my insulin dose or eat more.","zh":"如果我运动量比平时大，我可能需要减少胰岛素剂量或多吃一点。"},{"id":"B","en":"I should inject my insulin into the same spot every day to ensure absorption.","zh":"我应该每天在同一个位置注射胰岛素以确保吸收。"},{"id":"A","en":"I should store my unopened insulin vials in the refrigerator.","zh":"我应该把未开封的胰岛素瓶存放在冰箱里。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Correct practices include refrigerating unopened insulin, keeping opened vials at room temperature for about a month to reduce injection site irritation, carrying glucose sources for hypoglycemia, and adjusting for exercise (E). Rotating injection sites within one anatomical area is necessary, but injecting into the 'same spot' every day causes lipodystrophy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的做法包括：冷藏未开封的胰岛素；已开封的药瓶可在室温下保存约一个月以减少注射部位刺激；随身携带葡萄糖源以备低血糖；以及根据运动情况进行调整 (E)。在同一个解剖区域内轮换注射部位是必要的，但每天在“同一个点”注射 会导致脂肪营养不良。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for safety and prevention of complications. 'Same spot' is almost always wrong in NCLEX for injections/sites; look for 'rotation'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注安全和预防并发症。在 NCLEX 中，对于注射/部位，“同一个点”几乎总是错误的；应寻找“轮换”一词。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":595,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.404","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.404.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.404.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,53],"fullStemEn":"After a swallowing evaluation, the individualized feeding plan for a client with post-stroke dysphagia recommends a chin-down posture. Which action should the nurse take during swallowing?","fullStemZh":"一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者接受吞咽评估后，其个体化进食计划建议采用低头姿势。护士在患者吞咽时应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take during swallowing?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在患者吞咽时应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"After a swallowing evaluation, the individualized feeding plan for a client with post-stroke dysphagia recommends a chin-down posture.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者接受吞咽评估后，其个体化进食计划建议采用低头姿势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Instruct the client to perform a chin-tuck while swallowing.","zh":"指导患者在吞咽时进行收下颌动作（点头位）。"},{"id":"A","en":"Instruct the client to tilt the head back while swallowing.","zh":"指导患者在吞咽时将头后仰。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide thin liquids to facilitate easier swallowing.","zh":"提供稀薄的液体以促进更容易吞咽。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to use a straw for liquids.","zh":"鼓励患者使用吸管喝液体。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should follow the individualized swallowing plan and cue the prescribed chin-down posture. Chin-down may improve airway protection for selected swallowing impairments, but it is not appropriate for every client with dysphagia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应遵循个体化吞咽计划，提示患者采用医嘱规定的低头姿势。低头姿势可改善部分特定吞咽障碍患者的气道保护，但并非适用于所有吞咽困难患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For dysphagia, follow the swallow-screening results and individualized feeding plan; no single posture or liquid consistency is correct for every client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理吞咽困难时，应遵循吞咽筛查结果和个体化进食计划；没有一种姿势或液体稠度适用于所有患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":596,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.405","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.405.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.405.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,57],"fullStemEn":"A client with obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) is prescribed continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP). Which statement by the client indicates a need for further teaching?","fullStemZh":"一名阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停 (OSA) 患者被开具了持续气道正压通气 (CPAP)。患者的哪项陈述表明需要进一步指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the client indicates a need for further teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者的哪项陈述表明需要进一步指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) is prescribed continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停 (OSA) 患者被开具了持续气道正压通气 (CPAP)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"I can stop using the CPAP machine once I lose enough weight.","zh":"一旦我减掉足够的体重，我就可以停止使用 CPAP 机器了。"},{"id":"A","en":"I should ensure the mask fits snugly but comfortably.","zh":"我应该确保面罩贴合紧密但感觉舒适。"},{"id":"C","en":"The machine will help keep my airway open while I sleep.","zh":"这台机器将帮助我在睡觉时保持气道畅通。"},{"id":"D","en":"I will clean the mask and tubing regularly with mild soap.","zh":"我会定期用温和的肥皂清洗面罩和管道。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"While weight loss can improve OSA, the client should not stop CPAP treatment without medical evaluation and a follow-up sleep study.","rationaleCorrectZh":"虽然减轻体重可以改善 OSA，但在没有进行医疗评估和后续睡眠研究的情况下，患者不应停止 CPAP 治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the answer choice that suggests a self-modification of therapy without professional guidance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找暗示在没有专业指导的情况下自行修改治疗方案的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":597,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.406","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.406.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.406.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to feed a client with dysphagia. Which interventions should the nurse include in the plan of care? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名吞咽困难患者喂食。护士应在护理计划中包括哪些干预措施？多项选择。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the plan of care?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在护理计划中包括哪些干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Position the client in an upright, 90-degree sitting position.","zh":"使患者处于 90 度直立坐位。"},{"id":"D","en":"Mix different textures together to speed up feeding.","zh":"将不同质地的食物混合在一起以加快喂食速度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Monitor for coughing or frequent throat clearing during meals.","zh":"用餐期间监测是否有咳嗽或频繁清嗓子的现象。"},{"id":"E","en":"Minimize distractions in the environment during mealtime.","zh":"用餐期间尽量减少环境中的干扰。"},{"id":"C","en":"Offer small bites and allow the client to swallow twice between bites.","zh":"提供小口食物，并允许患者在两口之间吞咽两次。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Monitoring for signs of aspiration, proper positioning, small bites/double swallowing, and minimizing distractions are all key strategies for safe feeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"监测误吸迹象、正确的体位、小口进食/双重吞咽以及减少干扰都是安全喂食的关键策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify interventions that promote safety and focus during the physiological act of swallowing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别在吞咽这一生理行为中能促进安全和集中注意力的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":598,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.407","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.407.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.407.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,50],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about lifestyle modifications to manage obstructive sleep apnea (OSA). Which recommendations should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导患者通过改变生活方式来管理阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停 (OSA)。护士应包括哪些建议？多项选择。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which recommendations should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些建议？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Avoid alcohol consumption before bedtime.","zh":"睡前避免饮酒。"},{"id":"C","en":"Sleep in a supine position to improve airflow.","zh":"仰卧位睡眠以改善气流。"},{"id":"E","en":"Use a sedative-hypnotic medication to ensure deep sleep.","zh":"使用镇静催眠药物以确保深层睡眠。"},{"id":"D","en":"Stop smoking to reduce airway inflammation.","zh":"戒烟以减少气道炎症。"},{"id":"B","en":"Lose weight if the body mass index (BMI) is elevated.","zh":"如果体重指数 (BMI) 过高，应减轻体重。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Avoiding alcohol, losing weight, and smoking cessation are key lifestyle changes that reduce the severity of OSA.","rationaleCorrectZh":"避免饮酒、减轻体重和戒烟是减轻 OSA 严重程度的关键生活方式改变。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Eliminate choices that would cause muscle relaxation or use gravity to obstruct the airway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除那些会导致肌肉放松或利用重力阻塞气道的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":599,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.408","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.408.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.408.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,66],"fullStemEn":"A healthcare provider orders an enteral feeding of 240 mL to be administered over 4 hours. At what rate should the nurse set the infusion pump in mL/hr? (Enter numerical value only.)","fullStemZh":"医疗保健提供者开具了 240 毫升肠内营养液，要求在 4 小时内输注完毕。护士应将输液泵的速度设置为多少毫升/小时？（仅输入数值。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Enter numerical value only.)","terminalSentenceZh":"仅输入数值。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"At what rate should the nurse set the infusion pump in mL/hr?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将输液泵的速度设置为多少毫升/小时？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["60"],"numeric":{"value":60,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: Total volume (240 mL) divided by total time (4 hours) = 60 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算：总容量 (240 mL) 除以总时间 (4 小时) = 60 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The formula for hourly rate is Total Volume / Number of Hours.","testTakingStrategyZh":"小时速率的公式是：总容量 / 小时数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":600,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.409","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.409.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.409.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,51],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client receiving continuous enteral feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube. Which action is most important for the nurse to perform to prevent complications?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名通过鼻胃 (NG) 管接受持续肠内营养的患者。护士执行哪项操作对于预防并发症最为重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is most important for the nurse to perform to prevent complications?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士执行哪项操作对于预防并发症最为重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client receiving continuous enteral feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名通过鼻胃 (NG) 管接受持续肠内营养的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Flush the tube with 5 mL of water every 8 hours.","zh":"每 8 小时用 5 毫升水冲洗管道。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check the gastric residual volume every 24 hours.","zh":"每 24 小时检查一次胃残留量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the head of the bed elevated at least 30 to 45 degrees.","zh":"保持床头抬高至少 30 到 45 度。"},{"id":"C","en":"Change the feeding bag and tubing every 48 hours.","zh":"每 48 小时更换一次喂食袋和管道。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Keeping the head of the bed (HOB) elevated is the primary intervention to prevent aspiration, the most serious complication of enteral feeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"保持床头 (HOB) 抬高是预防误吸的首要干预措施，而误吸是肠内营养最严重的并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When asked for the 'most important' action, prioritize safety and the prevention of life-threatening complications like aspiration pneumonia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当被问及“最重要”的操作时，优先考虑安全和预防危及生命的并发症，如吸入性肺炎。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":601,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.410","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.410.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.410.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is checking the placement of a nasogastric tube before starting a bolus feeding. Which methods are appropriate to confirm or assess tube placement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士在开始间歇性推注喂食前正在检查鼻胃管的位置。哪些方法适用于确认或评估管道位置？多项选择。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which methods are appropriate to confirm or assess tube placement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些方法适用于确认或评估管道位置？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Verify the results of a recent chest X-ray.","zh":"核实最近一次胸部 X 线的检查结果。"},{"id":"E","en":"Check the marking on the tube at the nare to ensure it has not moved.","zh":"检查鼻孔处管道上的标记，确保其未移动。"},{"id":"C","en":"Auscultate for a 'whoosh' sound while injecting air into the tube.","zh":"在向管内注入空气时听诊是否有“呼啸”声。"},{"id":"B","en":"Measure the pH of the aspirated gastric contents.","zh":"测量抽吸出的胃内容物的 pH 值。"},{"id":"D","en":"Observe the color and consistency of the aspirated fluid.","zh":"观察抽吸液体的颜色和性状。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Radiographic confirmation is the gold standard for initial tube placement. Gastric pH, aspirate appearance, and external tube markings are evidence-based bedside checks used to assess ongoing placement before feeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"影像学确认是初次确认管道位置的金标准。胃液 pH、抽吸物外观以及外部管道标记是喂食前用于持续评估管道位置的循证床边检查方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify evidence-based practices for tube confirmation and ongoing bedside assessment. Remember that auscultation for air is unreliable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别用于管道确认和持续床边评估的循证做法。记住，空气听诊是不可靠的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":602,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.411","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.411.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.411.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,45],"fullStemEn":"A client with dysphagia is prescribed a 'mechanically altered' diet with 'honey-thick' liquids. Which food item would be most appropriate for the nurse to offer?","fullStemZh":"一名吞咽困难患者被开具了“机械改变”饮食及“蜂蜜样稠度”液体。护士提供哪种食物项最为合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which food item would be most appropriate for the nurse to offer?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士提供哪种食物项最为合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with dysphagia is prescribed a 'mechanically altered' diet with 'honey-thick' liquids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名吞咽困难患者被开具了“机械改变”饮食及“蜂蜜样稠度”液体。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Tomato soup with small chunks of vegetables.","zh":"带有小块蔬菜的番茄汤。"},{"id":"A","en":"White bread with peanut butter.","zh":"涂有花生酱的白面包。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apple juice with a thickening agent added.","zh":"加入了增稠剂的苹果汁。"},{"id":"D","en":"Plain water.","zh":"白开水。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients prescribed thickened liquids require a consistency that slows the flow of the liquid to allow time for the swallowing reflex to occur. Honey-thick liquids are significantly thickened.","rationaleCorrectZh":"被开具稠化液体的患者需要一种能减慢液体流速的稠度，以便为吞咽反射的发生留出时间。蜂蜜样稠度是明显增稠的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the option that strictly adheres to the prescribed dietary consistency for safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择严格遵循所开具的饮食稠度以确保安全的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with dysphagia is prescribed a 'mechanically altered' diet with 'honey-thick' liquids.","controlSentenceZh":"一名吞咽困难患者被开具了“机械改变”饮食及“蜂蜜样稠度”液体。"}
{"queueIndex":603,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.412","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.412.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.412.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,52],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client for potential obstructive sleep apnea (OSA). Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名患者是否存在潜在的阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停 (OSA)。护士预期会发现哪些临床表现？多项选择。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect to find?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士预期会发现哪些临床表现？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Weight loss and increased energy.","zh":"体重减轻和能量增加。"},{"id":"B","en":"Morning headaches.","zh":"晨起头痛。"},{"id":"C","en":"Loud snoring with periods of apnea.","zh":"大声打鼾伴有呼吸暂停期。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hypertension.","zh":"高血压。"},{"id":"A","en":"Excessive daytime sleepiness.","zh":"白昼过度嗜睡。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"OSA manifests with daytime sleepiness due to fragmented sleep, headaches from hypoxia/hypercapnia, snoring/apnea, and cardiovascular strain leading to hypertension.","rationaleCorrectZh":"OSA 的表现包括由于睡眠碎片化导致的白天嗜睡、缺氧/高碳酸血症引起的头痛、打鼾/呼吸暂停，以及导致高血压的心血管压力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the physiological effects of repeated airway collapse and oxygen deprivation during the night.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑夜间反复发生的呼吸道塌陷和缺氧的生理影响。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":604,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d3_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.413","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.413.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.413.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,58],"fullStemEn":"A client is to receive 1.5 liters of enteral formula over 24 hours. What is the infusion rate in mL/hr? (Round to the nearest whole number. Enter numerical value only.)","fullStemZh":"患者需在 24 小时内接受 1.5 升肠内营养液。输注速度是多少毫升/小时？（四舍五入到最接近的整数。仅输入数值。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter numerical value only.)","terminalSentenceZh":"仅输入数值。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["63"],"numeric":{"value":63,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: 1.5 liters = 1500 mL. 1500 mL / 24 hours = 62.5 mL/hr. Rounded to the nearest whole number is 63 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算：1.5 升 = 1500 毫升。1500 毫升 / 24 小时 = 62.5 毫升/小时。四舍五入到最接近的整数是 63 毫升/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always convert liters to milliliters (L to mL) before performing rate calculations. Follow rounding instructions carefully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在执行速率计算之前，务必将升转换为毫升（L 转换为 mL）。仔细遵循四舍五入说明。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":605,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.414","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.414.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.414.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,50],"fullStemEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is started on enteral nutrition. Which laboratory finding should the nurse prioritize as an indicator of refeeding syndrome?","fullStemZh":"一名患有神经性厌食症的患者开始进行肠内营养。护士应优先考虑哪项实验室检查结果作为再喂养综合征的指标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory finding should the nurse prioritize as an indicator of refeeding syndrome?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先考虑哪项实验室检查结果作为再喂养综合征的指标？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is started on enteral nutrition.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有神经性厌食症的患者开始进行肠内营养。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Serum magnesium 1.8 mg/dL","zh":"血清镁 1.8 mg/dL"},{"id":"B","en":"Serum potassium 3.6 mEq/L","zh":"血清钾 3.6 mEq/L"},{"id":"C","en":"Serum phosphorus 2.0 mg/dL","zh":"血清磷 2.0 mg/dL"},{"id":"D","en":"Serum sodium 138 mEq/L","zh":"血清钠 138 mEq/L"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypophosphatemia is the hallmark of refeeding syndrome. When a malnourished client receives nutrition, insulin is released, causing a shift of phosphorus from the blood into the cells, which can lead to cardiovascular and respiratory failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低磷血症是再喂养综合征的标志。当营养不良的患者接受营养时，胰岛素被释放，导致磷从血液转移到细胞内，这可能导致心血管和呼吸衰竭。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the topic: refeeding syndrome. Remember that 'phosphorus' is the most critical electrolyte to monitor during nutritional restoration in malnourished patients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注主题：再喂养综合征。请记住，“磷”是营养不良患者在恢复营养期间需要监测的最关键的电解质。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":606,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.415","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.415.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.415.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,42],"fullStemEn":"Before an electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) procedure, the nurse should expect to administer which medication to decrease secretions and prevent bradycardia?","fullStemZh":"在电休克治疗 (ECT) 手术前，护士应预期给予哪种药物以减少分泌物并预防心动过缓？","terminalSentenceEn":"Before an electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) procedure, the nurse should expect to administer which medication to decrease secretions and prevent bradycardia?","terminalSentenceZh":"在电休克治疗 (ECT) 手术前，护士应预期给予哪种药物以减少分泌物并预防心动过缓？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Glycopyrrolate","zh":"格隆溴铵"},{"id":"A","en":"Methohexital","zh":"美索比妥"},{"id":"D","en":"Succinylcholine","zh":"琥珀胆碱"},{"id":"B","en":"Diazepam","zh":"地西泮"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Glycopyrrolate or atropine are anticholinergic medications administered pre-ECT to decrease secretions (reducing aspiration risk) and prevent vagal-induced bradycardia during the seizure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"格隆溴铵或阿托品是 ECT 前给予的抗胆碱能药物，用于减少分泌物（降低误吸风险）并预防抽搐期间迷走神经诱发的心动过缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the goal: 'decrease secretions' and 'prevent bradycardia'. Anticholinergics are the drug class of choice for these effects.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注目标：“减少分泌物”和“预防心动过缓”。抗胆碱能药物是实现这些效果的首选药物类型。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":607,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.416","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.416.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.416.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[172,205],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,66],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is being stabilized on Lithium. The nurse notes the client has hand tremors, polyuria, and diarrhea. The current lithium level is 1.6 mEq/L. Which action is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一名双相情感障碍患者正在接受锂盐稳定治疗。护士注意到患者出现手震颤、多尿和腹泻。目前的锂浓度为 1.6 mEq/L。哪项操作最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项操作最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The current lithium level is 1.6 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"目前的锂浓度为 1.6 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Withhold the dose and request a repeat serum lithium level.","zh":"暂停给药并申请重复测定血清锂水平。"},{"id":"C","en":"Continue the medication as these are expected side effects.","zh":"继续用药，因为这些是预期副作用。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the next dose then notify the provider.","zh":"给予下一次剂量后通知医疗人员。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase fluid intake to 3 liters per day.","zh":"将每日饮水量增加到 3 升。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The therapeutic range for lithium is 0.6-1.2 mEq/L. A level of 1.6 mEq/L indicates toxicity. Early signs of lithium toxicity include diarrhea, vomiting, drowsiness, muscular weakness, and lack of coordination. The dose must be held.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锂的治疗范围是 0.6-1.2 mEq/L。1.6 mEq/L 的水平表示中毒。锂中毒的早期迹象包括腹泻、呕吐、嗜睡、肌肉无力和协调能力差。必须暂停给药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate the lab value first. Recognize that 1.6 mEq/L is above the therapeutic range (0.6-1.2). When a drug level is toxic, the first nursing action is usually to hold the medication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先评估实验室值。识别出 1.6 mEq/L 高于治疗范围 (0.6-1.2)。当药物浓度中毒时，第一个护理操作通常是暂停给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":608,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.417","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.417.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.417.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client immediately following electroconvulsive therapy (ECT). Place the following nursing actions in the correct order of priority.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚接受完电休克治疗 (ECT) 的患者。请按优先级顺序排列以下护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先级顺序排列以下护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client immediately following electroconvulsive therapy (ECT).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚接受完电休克治疗 (ECT) 的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Observe for return of spontaneous respirations.","zh":"观察自主呼吸的恢复情况。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess the client's gag reflex before offering fluids.","zh":"在提供液体前评估患者的咽反射。"},{"id":"B","en":"Orient the client to time, place, and person.","zh":"引导患者了解时间、地点和人物。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain patent airway and monitor vital signs.","zh":"维持气道通畅并监测生命体征。"}],"correct":["A","D","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Post-ECT priority follows the ABCs. First, maintain the airway and monitor vital signs. Second, ensure spontaneous respirations return as the muscle relaxant wears off. Third, provide reorientation due to common post-procedure confusion. Finally, assess the gag reflex before allowing oral intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ECT 后的优先级遵循 ABC 原则。首先，维持气道并监测生命体征。其次，随着肌肉松弛剂药效减弱，确保自主呼吸恢复。第三，针对常见的术后意识模糊进行重新定向。最后，在允许经口进食前评估咽反射。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABC mnemonic (Airway, Breathing, Circulation). Cognitive and functional assessments always follow physiological stability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ABC 记忆法（气道、呼吸、循环）。认知和功能评估总是排在生理稳定之后。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":609,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.418","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.418.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.418.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,117],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,34],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing clients with eating disorders. Match each clinical manifestation to the most likely diagnosis.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估患有进食障碍的患者。将每种临床表现与最可能的诊断相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each clinical manifestation to the most likely diagnosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种临床表现与最可能的诊断相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is assessing clients with eating disorders.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估患有进食障碍的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Lanugo and amenorrhea","zh":"胎毛和闭经"},{"id":"r2","en":"Parotid gland swelling and dental erosion","zh":"腮腺肿胀和牙齿侵蚀"},{"id":"r3","en":"Excessive exercise and extreme fear of weight gain","zh":"过度运动和对体重增加的极端恐惧"},{"id":"r4","en":"Russell's sign on the knuckles","zh":"指关节上的 Russell 征"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Anorexia Nervosa","zh":"神经性厌食症"},{"id":"c2","en":"Bulimia Nervosa","zh":"神经性贪食症"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lanugo and amenorrhea result from starvation and low body fat in Anorexia. Parotid swelling, dental erosion, and Russell's sign (calluses on knuckles) result from repetitive self-induced vomiting in Bulimia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胎毛和闭经是厌食症中饥饿和低体脂的结果。腮腺肿胀、牙齿侵蚀和 Russell 征（指关节上的茧）是贪食症中重复自我诱导呕吐的结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between symptoms of starvation (Anorexia) versus symptoms of purging (Bulimia).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分饥饿症状（厌食症）与催吐/导泻症状（贪食症）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":610,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.419","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.419.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.419.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,44],"fullStemEn":"A client with bulimia nervosa is admitted to the psychiatric unit. Which intervention should the nurse include in the plan of care to prevent purging behavior?","fullStemZh":"一名神经性贪食症患者被送往精神科病房。护士应在护理计划中加入哪项干预措施以防止催吐行为？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention should the nurse include in the plan of care to prevent purging behavior?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应在护理计划中加入哪项干预措施以防止催吐行为？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with bulimia nervosa is admitted to the psychiatric unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名神经性贪食症患者被送往精神科病房。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Weigh the client daily after the first void.","zh":"每天第一次排尿后为患者称重。"},{"id":"A","en":"Restrict the client's access to exercise equipment.","zh":"限制患者接触健身器材。"},{"id":"D","en":"Accompany the client to the bathroom for 1 hour after meals.","zh":"进餐后 1 小时内陪同患者去洗手间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Allow the client to eat meals in their room alone.","zh":"允许患者独自在房间里进餐。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nursing supervision after meals is essential to prevent the client from engaging in purging behaviors such as vomiting. Typically, this supervision lasts 1-2 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"饭后护理监督对于防止患者进行呕吐等催吐行为至关重要。通常，这种监督持续 1-2 小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the primary risk: purging. Look for the intervention that provides direct supervision during the time the risk is highest (post-meals).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别主要风险：催吐。寻找在风险最高的时间段（饭后）提供直接监督的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":611,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.420","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.420.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.420.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is planning care for a client with bipolar I disorder. Identify which interventions are appropriate for the acute manic phase versus the stabilization phase.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患有双相 I 型情感障碍的患者制定护理计划。确定哪些干预措施适用于急性躁狂期与稳定期。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify which interventions are appropriate for the acute manic phase versus the stabilization phase.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定哪些干预措施适用于急性躁狂期与稳定期。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is planning care for a client with bipolar I disorder.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患有双相 I 型情感障碍的患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Provide high-protein, high-calorie finger foods","zh":"提供高蛋白、高热量的手持食物"},{"id":"r2","en":"Assist with identifying triggers for mood swings","zh":"协助识别情绪波动的诱因"},{"id":"r3","en":"Reduce environmental stimuli and provide a private room","zh":"减少环境刺激并提供单人房间"},{"id":"r4","en":"Focus on relapse prevention education","zh":"重点关注预防复发教育"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Acute Manic Phase","zh":"急性躁狂期"},{"id":"c2","en":"Stabilization Phase","zh":"稳定期"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acute mania requires interventions for safety and basic needs (low stimuli, portable nutrition). Stabilization focuses on psychological work, education, and long-term adherence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性躁狂需要针对安全和基本需求（低刺激、便携式营养）进行干预。稳定期侧重于心理工作、教育和长期依从性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the client's ability to focus. In mania, focus is impossible, so interventions are simple and physiological. In stabilization, focus returns, allowing for education.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑患者的注意力。在躁狂状态下，注意力无法集中，因此干预措施是简单且生理性的。在稳定期，注意力恢复，允许进行教育。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":612,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.421","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.421.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.421.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[109,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,62],"fullStemEn":"A client in the manic phase of bipolar disorder is becoming increasingly loud and disruptive in the dayroom. Place the nursing interventions in the order they should be implemented, from least restrictive to most restrictive.","fullStemZh":"一名处于双相情感障碍躁狂期的患者在活动室变得越来越吵闹且具有干扰性。请按实施顺序排列护理干预措施，从限制性最低到限制性最高。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing interventions in the order they should be implemented, from least restrictive to most restrictive.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按实施顺序排列护理干预措施，从限制性最低到限制性最高。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in the manic phase of bipolar disorder is becoming increasingly loud and disruptive in the dayroom.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名处于双相情感障碍躁狂期的患者在活动室变得越来越吵闹且具有干扰性。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Use therapeutic communication to address the behavior.","zh":"使用治疗性沟通来处理该行为。"},{"id":"D","en":"Place the client in seclusion for safety.","zh":"出于安全考虑将患者置于隔离室。"},{"id":"B","en":"Accompany the client to a quiet area away from others.","zh":"陪同患者前往远离他人的安静区域。"},{"id":"A","en":"Offer a PRN sedative medication as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱提供必要的镇静药物 (PRN)。"}],"correct":["C","B","A","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mental health interventions must follow the principle of the 'least restrictive environment.' Start with communication, then move to environmental modification (quiet area), then pharmacological intervention (PRN meds), and finally physical or environmental restriction (seclusion) if safety is threatened.","rationaleCorrectZh":"精神卫生干预必须遵循“限制性最低环境”原则。从沟通开始，然后进行环境调整（安静区域），接着是药物干预（按需给药），最后在安全受到威胁时进行身体或环境限制（隔离）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the 'Least Restrictive' principle. Always try verbal interventions first before physical or chemical interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用“限制性最低”原则。在进行身体或化学干预之前，务必先尝试言语干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":613,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.422","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.422.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.422.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[121,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,45],"fullStemEn":"A client expresses concern about 'forgetting things' after receiving several electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) treatments. Which response by the nurse is most accurate?","fullStemZh":"一名患者对在接受几次电休克治疗 (ECT) 后“忘记事情”表示担忧。护士的哪种回答最准确？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is most accurate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪种回答最准确？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client expresses concern about 'forgetting things' after receiving several electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) treatments.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者对在接受几次电休克治疗 (ECT) 后“忘记事情”表示担忧。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"'We will stop the treatments immediately since you are having memory issues.'","zh":"“既然您出现了记忆问题，我们将立即停止治疗。”"},{"id":"A","en":"'Temporary confusion and memory loss are common side effects.'","zh":"“暂时性意识模糊和记忆丧失是常见的副作用。”"},{"id":"C","en":"'Memory loss after ECT is permanent and will not improve.'","zh":"“ECT 后的记忆丧失是永久性的，不会改善。”"},{"id":"D","en":"'Memory loss only happens if the treatment was not effective.'","zh":"“只有在治疗无效的情况下才会发生记忆丧失。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Retrograde amnesia and confusion are common side effects of ECT. These symptoms are usually temporary and resolve over a period of weeks to months.","rationaleCorrectZh":"逆行性遗忘和意识模糊是 ECT 的常见副作用。这些症状通常是暂时性的，会在几周到几个月内消失。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify common versus rare side effects. Use therapeutic communication to validate the client's concern while providing accurate medical facts.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分常见副作用与罕见副作用。使用治疗性沟通来验证患者的担忧，同时提供准确的医学事实。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":614,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d4_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.423","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.423.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.423.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,208],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,56],"fullStemEn":"A client with severe malnutrition due to anorexia nervosa is at risk for refeeding syndrome. Identify which physiological markers the nurse should expect to be decreased versus increased during this syndrome.","fullStemZh":"一名因神经性厌食症而严重营养不良的患者有发生再喂养综合征的风险。确定护士预期该综合征中哪些生理指标会降低或升高。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify which physiological markers the nurse should expect to be decreased versus increased during this syndrome.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定护士预期该综合征中哪些生理指标会降低或升高。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with severe malnutrition due to anorexia nervosa is at risk for refeeding syndrome.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因神经性厌食症而严重营养不良的患者有发生再喂养综合征的风险。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Serum Phosphorus","zh":"血清磷"},{"id":"r2","en":"Serum Magnesium","zh":"血清镁"},{"id":"r3","en":"Serum Potassium","zh":"血清钾"},{"id":"r4","en":"Plasma Insulin level","zh":"血浆胰岛素水平"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Decreased","zh":"降低"},{"id":"c2","en":"Increased","zh":"升高"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In refeeding syndrome, the reintroduction of glucose leads to an insulin surge (increased). This causes electrolytes (P, Mg, K) to shift from the extracellular fluid into the cells, resulting in decreased serum levels.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在再喂养综合征中，重新引入葡萄糖会导致胰岛素激增（升高）。这导致电解质（磷、镁、钾）从细胞外液转移到细胞内，从而导致血清水平降低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the pathology: Glucose -> Insulin Surge -> Electrolytes move INTO cells -> Serum levels DROP.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住病理过程：葡萄糖 -> 胰岛素激增 -> 电解质进入细胞 -> 血清水平下降。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":615,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.424","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.424.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.424.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[233,305],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,79],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for an older adult client who has been diagnosed with terminal cancer. The client's adult children are insisting that the nurse not inform the client of the diagnosis, fearing it will cause the client to lose hope. Which action by the nurse best demonstrates the role of client advocate?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名被诊断为癌症晚期的老年患者。患者的成年子女坚持要求护士不要将诊断结果告诉患者，担心这会使患者失去希望。护士的哪项行动最能体现患者倡导者的角色？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse best demonstrates the role of client advocate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项行动最能体现患者倡导者的角色？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's adult children are insisting that the nurse not inform the client of the diagnosis, fearing it will cause the client to lose hope.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的成年子女坚持要求护士不要将诊断结果告诉患者，担心这会使患者失去希望。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Inform the provider about the family's request and follow the provider's lead.","zh":"将家属的要求告知医疗服务提供者，并遵循其指示。"},{"id":"A","en":"Respect the children's wishes to protect the client's emotional well-being.","zh":"尊重子女的意愿，以保护患者的情绪健康。"},{"id":"C","en":"Encourage the family to have an open and honest conversation with the client.","zh":"鼓励家属与患者进行公开、诚实的对话。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's desire for information regarding their diagnosis and prognosis.","zh":"评估患者了解其诊断和预后信息的意愿。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"As an advocate, the nurse's primary responsibility is to the client. Autonomy is a key ethical principle, and the client has the right to be informed about their health status. The first step is to assess what the client knows and wants to know.","rationaleCorrectZh":"作为倡导者，护士的首要责任是对患者负责。自主权是一项关键的伦理原则，患者有权了解自己的健康状况。第一步是评估患者已知的信息以及想要了解的信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the client's autonomy and the ethical principle of veracity (truth-telling). Advocacy always prioritizes the client's rights.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注患者的自主权和诚实（告知真相）的伦理原则。倡导工作始终优先考虑患者的权利。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":616,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.425","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.425.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.425.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,48],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to transfer a client to a long-term care facility. Arrange the following actions in the correct order to ensure a safe and effective continuity of care.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备将一名患者转运至长期护理机构。请按正确顺序排列以下操作，以确保安全且有效的护理连续性。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the following actions in the correct order to ensure a safe and effective continuity of care.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列以下操作，以确保安全且有效的护理连续性。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to transfer a client to a long-term care facility.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备将一名患者转运至长期护理机构。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Complete the discharge summary and ensure all necessary documentation is organized.","zh":"完成出院摘要并确保所有必要的证明文件已整理妥当。"},{"id":"D","en":"Reconcile the client's medications and provide a complete list to the facility.","zh":"核对患者的药物，并向机构提供完整的清单。"},{"id":"A","en":"Confirm that the receiving facility has an available bed and is ready for the client.","zh":"确认接收机构有空床位并已为患者做好准备。"},{"id":"B","en":"Communicate a summary of the client's current status and care needs to the receiving nurse.","zh":"向接收护士传达患者当前状态和护理需求的摘要。"}],"correct":["A","D","C","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A safe transfer begins by confirming that the receiving facility is ready for the client. The nurse then reconciles medications, completes and organizes the transfer documentation, and gives the final nurse-to-nurse handoff report.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全转运首先要确认接收机构已为患者做好准备。随后护士核对药物，完成并整理转运文件，最后进行护士之间的交接报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of the process from destination readiness to final communication: confirm, reconcile, document, report.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按照从接收方准备情况到最终沟通的流程思考：确认、核对药物、整理文件、报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":617,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.426","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.426.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.426.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,50],"fullStemEn":"A case manager is reviewing the care plan for a client with multiple chronic conditions who has had frequent readmissions to the hospital. The goal is to optimize outcomes and utilize resources efficiently.","fullStemZh":"一名个案管理员正在审查一名患有多种慢性疾病且频繁再入院患者的护理计划。目标是优化结果并有效利用资源。","terminalSentenceEn":"The goal is to optimize outcomes and utilize resources efficiently.","terminalSentenceZh":"目标是优化结果并有效利用资源。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A case manager is reviewing the care plan for a client with multiple chronic conditions who has had frequent readmissions to the hospital.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名个案管理员正在审查一名患有多种慢性疾病且频繁再入院患者的护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The case manager should first prioritize {{1}} to prevent fragmentation of care, and then focus on {{2}} to reduce the risk of future readmissions.","zh":"个案管理员应首先优先考虑 {{1}} 以防止护理脱节，然后重点关注 {{2}} 以降低未来再入院的风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"strictly following hospital protocols","zh":"严格遵守医院协议"},{"id":"o3","en":"delegating all education to staff nurses","zh":"将所有健康教育委派给病房护士"},{"id":"o1","en":"interdisciplinary collaboration","zh":"跨学科协作"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"post-discharge follow-up and home resources","zh":"出院后随访和家庭资源"},{"id":"o2","en":"increasing the frequency of acute care visits","zh":"增加急性护理就诊频率"},{"id":"o3","en":"implementing stricter dietary restrictions","zh":"实施更严格的饮食限制"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Case management involves coordinating care across various disciplines to ensure a holistic approach (interdisciplinary collaboration). Addressing the transition from hospital to home via follow-up and resources is critical for preventing readmissions in chronic illness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"个案管理涉及协调各学科的护理，以确保采取整体方法（跨学科协作）。通过随访和资源处理从医院到家庭的过渡，对于预防慢性病患者再入院至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the core functions of case management: coordination, collaboration, and resource management. Look for options that address the root cause of frequent readmissions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别个案管理的核心功能：协调、协作和资源管理。寻找能够解决频繁再入院根本原因的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":618,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.427","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.427.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.427.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[191,266],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,68],"fullStemEn":"A nurse in a community clinic is assisting a client who was recently discharged after a stroke. The client requires physical therapy but expresses concern about transportation to the clinic. Which action by the nurse is most appropriate to ensure continuity of care?","fullStemZh":"社区诊所的一名护士正在协助一名最近因中风出院的患者。患者需要物理治疗，但对前往诊所的交通表示担忧。护士采取哪项行动最能确保护理的连续性？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is most appropriate to ensure continuity of care?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士采取哪项行动最能确保护理的连续性？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client requires physical therapy but expresses concern about transportation to the clinic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者需要物理治疗，但对前往诊所的交通表示担忧。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Refer the client to a social worker or case manager to explore transportation resources.","zh":"将患者转介给社会工作者或个案管理员，以寻找交通资源。"},{"id":"B","en":"Contact the physical therapist and request that they visit the client at home.","zh":"联系物理治疗师，请求他们到患者家中进行访问。"},{"id":"D","en":"Advise the client to ask family members or friends for a ride to appointments.","zh":"建议患者请求家属或朋友开车送其赴约。"},{"id":"C","en":"Instruct the client on exercises they can perform at home instead of attending therapy.","zh":"指导患者在家里可以进行的锻炼，以代替参加治疗。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Continuity of care often requires overcoming barriers to access. Social workers and case managers are specialists in identifying and securing community resources like transportation to ensure the client receives necessary follow-up care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护理的连续性通常需要克服就医障碍。社会工作者和个案管理员是识别和获取社区资源（如交通服务）的专家，以确保患者获得必要的后续护理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the role of the interdisciplinary team. Case managers and social workers are the appropriate referrals for resource-related issues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注跨学科团队的角色。个案管理员和社会工作者是处理资源相关问题的适当转介对象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":619,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.428","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.428.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.428.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,237],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,60],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers that a colleague is consistently failing to document controlled substance administration accurately. Arrange the steps the nurse should take in the correct order to fulfill the role of advocate and ensure client safety.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一位同事始终未能准确记录受控物质的给药情况。请按正确顺序排列护士应采取的步骤，以履行倡导者的角色并确保患者安全。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the steps the nurse should take in the correct order to fulfill the role of advocate and ensure client safety.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士应采取的步骤，以履行倡导者的角色并确保患者安全。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers that a colleague is consistently failing to document controlled substance administration accurately.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现一位同事始终未能准确记录受控物质的给药情况。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Follow the facility's formal whistleblowing policy or chain of command if the issue persists.","zh":"如果问题仍然存在，请遵循机构的正式举报政策或指挥系统。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure immediate client safety by checking the clients who received care from the colleague.","zh":"通过检查接受过该同事护理的患者，确保患者的即时安全。"},{"id":"A","en":"Report the observations to the nurse manager or supervisor.","zh":"将观察到的情况报告给护士长或主管。"},{"id":"B","en":"Gather and objectively document the specific instances of inconsistent record-keeping.","zh":"收集并客观记录记录不一致的具体实例。"}],"correct":["C","B","A","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse's first priority is always client safety. After ensuring the clients are safe, the nurse should gather objective data before reporting to a supervisor. If the supervisor does not act or the situation requires further escalation, the chain of command or whistleblowing policies are followed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士的首要任务始终是患者安全。在确保患者安全后，护士应在向主管报告 之前收集客观数据。如果主管不采取行动或情况需要进一步升级，则遵循指挥系统或举报政策。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first! Always prioritize the client's immediate physical well-being. Then move towards objective documentation and reporting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一！始终优先考虑患者的即时身体健康。然后转向客观记录和报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":620,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.429","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.429.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.429.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,40],"fullStemEn":"A client with a new prescription for insulin is being prepared for discharge. The nurse is coordinating the education and equipment needed for home care.","fullStemZh":"一名新开具胰岛素处方的患者正准备出院。护士正在协调家庭护理所需的健康教育和设备。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is coordinating the education and equipment needed for home care.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在协调家庭护理所需的健康教育和设备。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a new prescription for insulin is being prepared for discharge.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名新开具胰岛素处方的患者正准备出院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Effective discharge planning for this client must include {{1}} before leaving the hospital, and the nurse should ensure a {{2}} is scheduled to evaluate the client's technique in the home setting.","zh":"该患者有效的出院计划必须包括在离开医院前进行 {{1}}，并且护士应确保安排 {{2}} 以评估患者在家中的操作技术。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"reading a brochure about diabetes management","zh":"阅读关于糖尿病管理的宣传册"},{"id":"o1","en":"a return demonstration of insulin administration","zh":"回示胰岛素给药操作"},{"id":"o3","en":"signing a waiver of liability for self-injection","zh":"签署自我注射责任豁免书"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"home health nursing referral","zh":"家庭健康护理转介"},{"id":"o2","en":"telephone follow-up call in one month","zh":"一个月后的电话随访"},{"id":"o3","en":"follow-up appointment with the surgeon","zh":"与外科医生的随访预约"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Verification of learning via return demonstration is essential for safety. Since the client is at home, a home health referral provides professional oversight during the transition, ensuring the client can manage the task independently in their own environment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"通过回示验证学习效果对于安全至关重要。由于患者在家里，家庭健康转介在过渡期间提供了专业监督，确保患者能够在自己的环境中独立完成任务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on 'active' learning and 'continuity'. Reading is passive; return demonstration is active. Home health provides continuity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注“主动”学习和“连续性”。阅读是被动的；回示是主动的。家庭健康提供连续性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":621,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.430","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.430.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.430.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,268],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,76],"fullStemEn":"A case manager is coordinating care for a client who is uninsured and requires expensive long-term biological therapy for an autoimmune condition. Which action by the case manager best supports the goal of providing cost-effective care while advocating for the client?","fullStemZh":"个案管理员正在为一名没有保险且因自身免疫性疾病需要昂贵长期生物疗法的患者协调护理。个案管理员的哪项行动最能支持在为患者倡导的同时提供高性价比护理的目标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the case manager best supports the goal of providing cost-effective care while advocating for the client?","terminalSentenceZh":"个案管理员的哪项行动最能支持在为患者倡导的同时提供高性价比护理的目标？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A case manager is coordinating care for a client who is uninsured and requires expensive long-term biological therapy for an autoimmune condition.","penultimateSentenceZh":"个案管理员正在为一名没有保险且因自身免疫性疾病需要昂贵长期生物疗法的患者协调护理。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Request that the provider switch the client to a less expensive but less effective medication.","zh":"请求医疗服务提供者将患者改为使用价格较低但效果较差的药物。"},{"id":"B","en":"Inform the client that they cannot receive the therapy due to lack of financial resources.","zh":"告知患者由于缺乏资金资源，他们无法接受该治疗。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assist the client in applying for a pharmaceutical company's patient assistance program.","zh":"协助患者申请制药公司的患者援助计划。"},{"id":"D","en":"Advise the client to seek emergency room care whenever symptoms exacerbate to avoid upfront costs.","zh":"建议患者在症状加重时寻求急诊护理，以避免预付费用。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Case managers advocate for clients by identifying alternative funding sources or programs that provide access to necessary treatments. Patient assistance programs (PAPs) are a key resource for uninsured clients needing high-cost medications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"个案管理员通过识别替代资金来源或提供必要治疗方案的计划来为患者提供倡导。患者援助计划 (PAP) 是需要高成本药物的无保险患者的关键资源。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the answer that maximizes both quality of care and resource accessibility. Case managers are 'resource experts'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找能使护理质量和资源可及性都达到最大化的答案。个案管理员是“资源专家”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":622,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.431","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.431.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.431.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is witness to a client signing an informed consent form for a surgical procedure. The client asks, 'What happens if they find something else wrong while they are in there?' Which is the most appropriate response by the nurse as an advocate?","fullStemZh":"护士见证了一名患者签署手术知情同意书。患者问：“如果他们在手术过程中发现其他问题怎么办？”作为倡导者，护士最合适的回答是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which is the most appropriate response by the nurse as an advocate?","terminalSentenceZh":"作为倡导者，护士最合适的回答是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client asks, 'What happens if they find something else wrong while they are in there?'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者问：“如果他们在手术过程中发现其他问题怎么办？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"I will call the surgeon back to the room to explain that part of the consent process to you.","zh":"我会请外科医生回到房间，向您解释同意过程中的那部分内容。"},{"id":"B","en":"The surgeon will take care of whatever is found to ensure your health.","zh":"外科医生会处理发现的任何问题，以确保您的健康。"},{"id":"A","en":"This is a common question; usually, they only do what was originally planned.","zh":"这是一个常见的问题；通常情况下，他们只做最初计划的事情。"},{"id":"C","en":"You have already signed the form, which covers all necessary procedures.","zh":"您已经签署了表格，其中涵盖了所有必要的程序。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse's role in informed consent is to witness the signature and advocate for the client's understanding. If the client asks a question about the procedure or its scope, the nurse must ensure the provider (the surgeon) clarifies the information before proceeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在知情同意中的角色是见证签字并为患者的理解提供倡导。如果患者询问有关手术或其范围的问题，护士必须确保医疗服务提供者（外科医生）在继续操作前澄清信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The nurse witnesses the signature, but the surgeon is responsible for the explanation. If the client has questions, the nurse must bring the surgeon back.","testTakingStrategyZh":"护士见证签字，但外科医生负责解释。如果患者有疑问，护士必须请外科医生回来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":623,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.432","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.432.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.432.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[55,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,52],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is giving a hand-off report to the next shift. Arrange the components of the ISBAR communication tool in the correct order for an effective transition of care.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向下一班次进行交班报告。请按正确顺序排列 ISBAR 沟通工具的组成部分，以实现有效的护理过渡。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the components of the ISBAR communication tool in the correct order for an effective transition of care.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列 ISBAR 沟通工具的组成部分，以实现有效的护理过渡。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is giving a hand-off report to the next shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向下一班次进行交班报告。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Recommendation: Suggest specific actions or follow-up needed.","zh":"Recommendation（建议）：提出具体的行动或所需的后续跟进建议。"},{"id":"B","en":"Identification: State your name, role, and the client's name/location.","zh":"Identification（身份识别）：陈述您的姓名、角色以及患者的姓名/位置。"},{"id":"A","en":"Background: Provide relevant clinical history and context.","zh":"Background（背景）：提供相关的临床病史和背景信息。"},{"id":"E","en":"Assessment: Share your clinical findings or analysis of the situation.","zh":"Assessment（评估）：分享您的临床发现或对情况的分析。"},{"id":"D","en":"Situation: Describe the current reason for the report or the client's immediate status.","zh":"Situation（现状）：描述报告的当前原因或患者的即时状态。"}],"correct":["B","D","A","E","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ISBAR stands for Identification, Situation, Background, Assessment, and Recommendation. This structured format ensures all critical information is communicated clearly.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ISBAR 代表身份识别 (Identification)、现状 (Situation)、背景 (Background)、评估 (Assessment) 和建议 (Recommendation)。这种结构化格式可确保所有关键信息都得到清晰传达。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the acronym ISBARR. It is a standard tool used in NCLEX and clinical practice to improve safety during hand-offs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住缩写 ISBARR。它是 NCLEX 和临床实践中用于提高交接班安全性的标准工具。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":624,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d5_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.433","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.433.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.433.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning discharge for a client with a new diagnosis of heart failure who lives alone and has limited financial resources.","fullStemZh":"一名护士正在为一名新诊断为心力衰竭、独居且财务资源有限的患者计划出院。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning discharge for a client with a new diagnosis of heart failure who lives alone and has limited financial resources.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名护士正在为一名新诊断为心力衰竭、独居且财务资源有限的患者计划出院。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To promote continuity of care and prevent readmission, the nurse should first arrange a {{1}} to evaluate home safety and medication adherence, and ensure the client is referred to {{2}}.","zh":"为了促进护理的连续性并预防再入院，护士应首先安排 {{1}} 以评估家庭安全和用药依从性，并确保将患者转介至 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"nutritionist consultation at the clinic","zh":"在诊所咨询营养师"},{"id":"o1","en":"home health nursing visit","zh":"家庭健康护理访问"},{"id":"o2","en":"weekly cardiac rehabilitation session","zh":"每周心脏康复环节"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"a personal trainer for home exercise","zh":"家庭锻炼的私人教练"},{"id":"o2","en":"a support group for family members","zh":"家属支持小组"},{"id":"o1","en":"community resources for financial assistance","zh":"提供经济援助的社区资源"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For high-risk clients (living alone, chronic illness, financial barriers), home health visits provide essential in-person assessment. Referring to community resources addresses the socioeconomic barriers that often lead to medication non-adherence and readmission.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于高风险患者（独居、慢性病、经济障碍），家庭健康访问提供了必要的面对面评估。转介社区资源解决了通常导致不遵医嘱用药和再入院的社会经济障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the 'high risk' factors in the scenario. Living alone and limited resources require 'high-touch' interventions like home health and community assistance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别场景中的“高风险”因素。独居和有限的资源需要家庭健康和社区援助等“高接触”干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":625,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_infant_solids_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.434","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.434.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.434.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing education to the parents of a 6-month-old infant regarding the introduction of solid foods. Which instruction should the nurse include?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名 6 个月大婴儿的父母提供有关引入辅食的教育。护士应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing education to the parents of a 6-month-old infant regarding the introduction of solid foods.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名 6 个月大婴儿的父母提供有关引入辅食的教育。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Begin with complex mixtures of vegetables and meats.","zh":"从蔬菜和肉类的复杂混合物开始。"},{"id":"C","en":"Start with fruit juices to increase vitamin C intake.","zh":"从果汁开始以增加维生素 C 的摄入。"},{"id":"B","en":"Introduce new foods one at a time at 4- to 7-day intervals.","zh":"每隔 4 到 7 天引入一种新食物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Mix cereal into the bottle to help the infant sleep through the night.","zh":"将米粉拌入奶瓶中以帮助婴儿整夜睡眠。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New foods should be introduced one at a time at 4- to 7-day intervals to allow for the identification of potential food allergies or sensitivities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新食物应每隔 4 到 7 天引入一种，以便识别潜在的食物过敏或敏感性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on safety and allergy prevention. The gradual introduction of single ingredients is a core principle of pediatric nutrition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注安全和过敏预防。逐步引入单一成分是儿科营养的核心原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":626,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_toddler_poisoning_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.435","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.435.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.435.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,47],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is conducting a home safety assessment for the parents of an 18-month-old toddler. Which observation regarding household chemicals requires immediate intervention?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名 18 个月大幼儿的父母进行家庭安全评估。关于家用化学品的哪项观察需要立即干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which observation regarding household chemicals requires immediate intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"关于家用化学品的哪项观察需要立即干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is conducting a home safety assessment for the parents of an 18-month-old toddler.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名 18 个月大幼儿的父母进行家庭安全评估。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Liquid drain cleaner is stored in an empty, unlabeled juice bottle.","zh":"液体下水道疏通剂储存在一个空的、未贴标签的果汁瓶中。"},{"id":"C","en":"Vitamins with iron are stored in a container with a child-resistant cap.","zh":"含铁维生素储存在带有儿童安全盖的容器中。"},{"id":"B","en":"Laundry detergent pods are kept in their original container on a high shelf.","zh":"洗衣凝珠保存在原始容器中，放在高处的架子上。"},{"id":"D","en":"Cleaning supplies are stored in a locked cabinet under the kitchen sink.","zh":"清洁用品储存在厨房水槽下方带锁的柜子里。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Toxic substances should never be stored in food or beverage containers, as this significantly increases the risk of accidental ingestion. All chemicals must remain in their original, labeled containers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有毒物质绝不能储存在食物或饮料容器中，因为这会显著增加意外摄入的风险。所有化学品必须保留在原始的、贴有标签的容器中。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the most hazardous practice. Storing poisons in familiar food containers is a high-risk behavior for toddlers who explore their environment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别最危险的做法。将毒物储存在熟悉的食物容器中对于探索环境的幼儿来说是一种高风险行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":627,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_gestational_diabetes_gtt_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.436","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.436.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.436.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[292,331],"terminalOffsetsZh":[102,111],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is explaining the 1-hour oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) to a pregnant client at 24 weeks gestation. The nurse informs the client that a blood glucose level greater than or equal to ____ mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) is considered a positive screen and requires further diagnostic testing. (Record your answer as a whole number.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名怀孕 24 周的患者解释 1 小时口服葡萄糖耐量试验 (OGTT)。护士告知患者，血糖水平大于或等于 ____ mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) 被视为筛选阳性，需要进一步的诊断检查。（以整数记录答案。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.)","terminalSentenceZh":"以整数记录答案。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse informs the client that a blood glucose level greater than or equal to ____ mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) is considered a positive screen and requires further diagnostic testing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士告知患者，血糖水平大于或等于 ____ mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) 被视为筛选阳性，需要进一步的诊断检查。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mg/dL","zh":"mg/dL"},"acceptable":["140"],"numeric":{"value":140,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mg/dL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A 1-hour OGTT result of 140 mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) or higher is typically considered a positive screening result for gestational diabetes, necessitating a follow-up 3-hour OGTT for definitive diagnosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1 小时 OGTT 结果为 140 mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) 或更高通常被视为妊娠期糖尿病的阳性筛选结果，需要进行后续 3 小时 OGTT 以明确诊断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall standard laboratory thresholds for prenatal screening. 140 mg/dL is the key cutoff for the 1-hour glucose screen.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想产前检查的标准实验室阈值。140 mg/dL 是 1 小时血糖筛查的关键界限。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":628,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_toddler_choking_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.437","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.437.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.437.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a group of parents about preventing choking in toddlers. Which food items should the nurse identify as high-risk for choking? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一组父母讲解如何预防幼儿窒息。护士应识别出哪些食物是窒息的高风险食物？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which food items should the nurse identify as high-risk for choking?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应识别出哪些食物是窒息的高风险食物？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Mashed potatoes","zh":"土豆泥"},{"id":"A","en":"Whole grapes","zh":"整颗葡萄"},{"id":"F","en":"Applesauce","zh":"苹果泥"},{"id":"E","en":"Popcorn","zh":"爆米花"},{"id":"D","en":"Raw carrots","zh":"生胡萝卜"},{"id":"B","en":"Hot dog rounds","zh":"热狗圆片"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"High-risk foods for choking in toddlers are typically small, round, firm, or slippery. This includes whole grapes, hot dog rounds, raw carrots, and popcorn. Mashed potatoes and applesauce are soft and considered safe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"幼儿窒息的高风险食物通常是小的、圆的、坚硬的或滑的。这包括整颗葡萄、热狗圆片、生胡萝卜和爆米花。土豆泥和苹果泥质地柔软，被认为是安全的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize the size and consistency of the food. Anything that is small, round, and hard/slippery is a classic choking hazard for young children.","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象食物的大小和质地。任何小的、圆的、硬的/滑的东西都是幼儿典型的窒息危险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":629,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_gestational_diabetes_risk_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.438","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.438.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.438.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the medical records of several pregnant clients. Which factors should the nurse identify as increasing a client's risk for developing gestational diabetes? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查几位孕妇的医疗记录。护士应识别出哪些因素会增加患者患妊娠期糖尿病的风险？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which factors should the nurse identify as increasing a client's risk for developing gestational diabetes?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应识别出哪些因素会增加患者患妊娠期糖尿病的风险？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"History of polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS)","zh":"有多囊卵巢综合征 (PCOS) 史"},{"id":"C","en":"Previous birth of an infant weighing 9 lb (4.1 kg) or more","zh":"曾分娩过体重 9 磅（4.1 千克）或以上的婴儿"},{"id":"A","en":"Body mass index (BMI) greater than 30 kg/m²","zh":"体重指数 (BMI) 大于 30 kg/m²"},{"id":"B","en":"Age older than 25 years","zh":"年龄超过 25 岁"},{"id":"E","en":"Pre-pregnancy weight within normal range","zh":"孕前体重在正常范围内"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Risk factors for gestational diabetes include obesity (BMI > 30), maternal age over 25, previous delivery of a macrosomic infant, and medical conditions like PCOS. A normal pre-pregnancy weight is a protective factor, not a risk factor.","rationaleCorrectZh":"妊娠期糖尿病的风险因素包括肥胖 (BMI > 30)、产妇年龄超过 25 岁、曾分娩过巨大儿，以及 PCOS 等疾病。孕前体重正常是保护因素，而非风险因素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify characteristics that contribute to insulin resistance or indicate a history of glycemic issues. Obesity and age are common physiological risk factors in pregnancy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别导致胰岛素抵抗或提示有血糖问题病史的特征。肥胖和年龄是怀孕期间常见的生理风险因素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":630,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_infant_vitamin_d_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.439","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.439.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.439.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing nutritional guidance to a mother who plans to exclusively breastfeed her newborn. Which supplement should the nurse recommend starting within the first few days of life?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一位计划纯母乳喂养新生儿的母亲提供营养指导。护士应建议在出生后头几天开始补充哪种补充剂？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which supplement should the nurse recommend starting within the first few days of life?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应建议在出生后头几天开始补充哪种补充剂？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing nutritional guidance to a mother who plans to exclusively breastfeed her newborn.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一位计划纯母乳喂养新生儿的母亲提供营养指导。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Iron-fortified cereal","zh":"强化铁米粉"},{"id":"A","en":"Vitamin D (400 IU daily)","zh":"维生素 D（每日 400 IU）"},{"id":"B","en":"Fluoride drops","zh":"氟化物滴剂"},{"id":"D","en":"Multivitamin with minerals","zh":"含矿物质的复合维生素"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The American Academy of Pediatrics recommends that all breastfed infants receive a daily supplement of 400 IU of vitamin D starting shortly after birth to prevent rickets, as breast milk is typically low in vitamin D.","rationaleCorrectZh":"美国儿科学会建议所有母乳喂养的婴儿从出生后不久开始每日补充 400 IU 的维生素 D，以预防佝偻病，因为母乳中的维生素 D 含量通常较低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the specific nutrient that is naturally deficient in human breast milk. Vitamin D is the primary concern for infants who are exclusively breastfed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想人类母乳中天然缺乏的特定营养素。维生素 D 是纯母乳喂养婴儿的首要关注点。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":631,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_toddler_lead_poisoning_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.440","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.440.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.440.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is educating the parents of a 2-year-old child about preventing lead poisoning in their older home. Which actions should the nurse recommend? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名 2 岁儿童的父母如何在其旧房子中预防铅中毒。护士应推荐哪些行动？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse recommend?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应推荐哪些行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Vacuum with a standard vacuum cleaner daily.","zh":"每天使用标准吸尘器吸尘。"},{"id":"C","en":"Wet-mop floors and windowsills rather than dry-sweeping.","zh":"用湿拖把拖地和窗台，而不是干扫。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use hot tap water for cooking and preparing infant formula.","zh":"使用热水龙头的水进行烹饪和冲调婴儿配方奶。"},{"id":"A","en":"Wash the child's hands and toys frequently.","zh":"经常清洗孩子的手和玩具。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensure the child consumes a diet rich in iron and calcium.","zh":"确保孩子摄入富含铁和钙的饮食。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Preventing lead poisoning involves reducing dust (wet mopping, washing hands/toys) and optimizing nutrition. Iron and calcium help decrease lead absorption. Hot tap water can contain higher levels of lead from pipes; cold water should be used. Standard vacuuming (E) can stir up lead dust unless a HEPA filter is used.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防铅中毒包括减少灰尘（湿拖、洗手/玩具）和优化营养。铁和钙有助于减少铅的吸收。热水龙头的水 可能含有来自管道的更高水平的铅；应使用冷水。标准吸尘 (E) 可能会激起铅尘，除非使用 HEPA 过滤器。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about how to minimize exposure and absorption. 'Wet' is better than 'dry' for dust, 'cold' is better than 'hot' for water, and 'good nutrition' helps block lead uptake.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考如何最大限度地减少接触和吸收。对于灰尘，“湿”比“干”好；对于水，“冷”比“热”好；“良好的营养”有助于阻断铅的摄取。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":632,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_gestational_diabetes_diet_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.441","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.441.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.441.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,35],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing dietary instructions to a client newly diagnosed with gestational diabetes. Which recommendation is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名新诊断为妊娠期糖尿病的患者提供饮食指导。哪项建议最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which recommendation is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项建议最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is providing dietary instructions to a client newly diagnosed with gestational diabetes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名新诊断为妊娠期糖尿病的患者提供饮食指导。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Consume the majority of carbohydrates during breakfast.","zh":"在早餐期间摄入大部分碳水化合物。"},{"id":"B","en":"Distribute carbohydrate intake across three meals and two to three snacks.","zh":"将碳水化合物的摄入分配到三餐和两到三顿零食中。"},{"id":"C","en":"Eat three large meals a day to keep glucose levels stable.","zh":"每天吃三顿大餐以保持血糖水平稳定。"},{"id":"A","en":"Avoid all carbohydrates to prevent blood sugar spikes.","zh":"避免摄入所有碳水化合物以防止血糖飙升。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Managing gestational diabetes involves evenly distributing carbohydrates throughout the day across several meals and snacks to prevent glucose fluctuations. Avoiding all carbohydrates is dangerous for both mother and fetus.","rationaleCorrectZh":"管理妊娠期糖尿病包括将碳水化合物均匀地分配到全天的几顿正餐和零食中，以防止血糖波动。避免摄入所有碳水化合物对母亲和胎儿都是危险的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply general diabetic diet principles: consistency and distribution. Eliminate 'extreme' options like 'avoid all carbohydrates'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用一般的糖尿病饮食原则：一致性和分配。排除“极端”选项，如“避免摄入所有碳水化合物”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":633,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_toddler_drowning_safety_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.442","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.442.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.442.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is discussing water safety with the parents of a 2-year-old child who recently installed a backyard swimming pool. Which statement by the parents indicates a need for further teaching?","fullStemZh":"护士正在与刚在后院安装了游泳池的一名 2 岁儿童的父母讨论水上安全。父母的哪项陈述表明需要进一步教学？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the parents indicates a need for further teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"父母的哪项陈述表明需要进一步教学？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is discussing water safety with the parents of a 2-year-old child who recently installed a backyard swimming pool.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在与刚在后院安装了游泳池的一名 2 岁儿童的父母讨论水上安全。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"We are both trained in pediatric cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR).","zh":"我们都接受过小儿心肺复苏 (CPR) 培训。"},{"id":"D","en":"Our child uses inflatable arm floaties, so we can relax while they are in the pool.","zh":"我们的孩子使用充气手臂浮圈，所以他们在泳池里时我们可以放松一下。"},{"id":"B","en":"We have installed a 4-foot fence with a self-closing, self-latching gate around the pool.","zh":"我们在泳池周围安装了一个 4 英尺高的围栏，带有自动关闭、自动锁定的门。"},{"id":"A","en":"We never leave our child alone in or near the water, even for a second.","zh":"我们绝不会让孩子单独待在水里或水边，哪怕是一秒钟。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Inflatable arm floaties (water wings) are toys, not life-saving devices, and can give a false sense of security. They do not replace the need for constant, touch-supervision by an adult.","rationaleCorrectZh":"充气手臂浮圈（水袖）是玩具，而非救生设备，可能会给人一种虚假的安全感。它们不能取代成年人持续的、触手可及的监督需求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the answer that suggests a compromise in supervision or reliance on toys for safety. These are classic indicators of a need for more education.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找暗示在监督上妥协或依靠玩具保证安全的答案。这些是需要更多教育的典型指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":634,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d6_toddler_milk_iron_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.443","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.443.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.443.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[165,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,53],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching the parents of a 2-year-old child about healthy milk consumption. Which guidelines should the nurse include to prevent iron deficiency anemia? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名 2 岁儿童的父母讲解健康的牛奶摄入量。护士应包括哪些准则以预防缺铁性贫血？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which guidelines should the nurse include to prevent iron deficiency anemia?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些准则以预防缺铁性贫血？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Offer iron-rich foods before giving the child milk.","zh":"在给孩子喝牛奶之前先提供富含铁的食物。"},{"id":"E","en":"Serve only skim milk to ensure weight management.","zh":"只提供脱脂牛奶以确保体重管理。"},{"id":"A","en":"Limit cow's milk intake to no more than 24 ounces (710 mL) per day.","zh":"将牛奶摄入量限制在每天不超过 24 盎司（710 毫升）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Encourage the child to drink as much milk as they want since it is a primary source of calcium.","zh":"鼓励孩子想喝多少牛奶就喝多少，因为它是钙的主要来源。"},{"id":"C","en":"Transition from a bottle to a cup by 12 to 15 months of age.","zh":"在 12 到 15 个月大时从奶瓶过渡到杯子。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Excessive cow's milk intake (>24 oz/day) can lead to iron deficiency anemia because it displaces iron-rich foods and may cause microscopic intestinal bleeding. Transitioning to a cup and offering solid foods first are effective strategies. Choosing only skim milk for weight control is not an iron-deficiency prevention strategy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"过量摄入牛奶（每天 > 24 盎司）会导致缺铁性贫血，因为它取代了富含铁的食物，并可能引起微小的肠道出血。过渡到杯子并先提供固体食物是有效的策略。仅为了控制体重而只提供脱脂牛奶，并不是预防缺铁的策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the relationship between calcium/milk and iron absorption. Too much of one often displaces the other in a toddler's diet.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注钙/牛奶与铁吸收之间的关系。在幼儿饮食中，其中一种过多往往会取代另一种。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which guidelines should the nurse include to prevent iron deficiency anemia?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些准则以预防缺铁性贫血？"}
{"queueIndex":635,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.444","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.444.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.444.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers a fire in the trash can of a client's room. According to the RACE mnemonic, which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士发现病人房间的垃圾桶着火了。根据 RACE 缩写，护士应该首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"According to the RACE mnemonic, which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据 RACE 缩写，护士应该首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers a fire in the trash can of a client's room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现病人房间的垃圾桶着火了。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Remove the client from the room","zh":"将病人带离房间"},{"id":"C","en":"Close the door to the room to confine the fire","zh":"关上房门以局限火势"},{"id":"A","en":"Use a fire extinguisher to put out the fire","zh":"使用灭火器扑灭火灾"},{"id":"D","en":"Activate the nearest fire alarm","zh":"激活最近的火警报警器"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first step in the RACE mnemonic is 'Rescue' (R), which involves removing clients from immediate danger. This takes priority over alarm activation or fire confinement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"RACE 缩写的第一步是“救援”（Rescue），即把病人从直接危险中带离。这优于报警或局限火势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the sequence of RACE: Rescue, Alarm, Confine, Extinguish. Always prioritize client safety first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 RACE 的顺序：救援 (Rescue)、报警 (Alarm)、局限 (Confine)、灭火 (Extinguish)。始终优先考虑病人的安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":636,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.445","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.445.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.445.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[41,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,34],"fullStemEn":"A nurse identifies a fire in a facility. Place the actions of the RACE mnemonic in the correct sequential order.","fullStemZh":"护士在设施内发现火灾。请按正确的顺序排列 RACE 准则的操作步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions of the RACE mnemonic in the correct sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列 RACE 准则的操作步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse identifies a fire in a facility.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在设施内发现火灾。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Confine the fire by closing doors","zh":"通过关门来局限火势"},{"id":"D","en":"Extinguish the fire if small or wait for the fire department","zh":"如果火势较小则灭火，或等待消防部门"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the fire alarm system","zh":"激活火警报警系统"},{"id":"C","en":"Rescue and remove clients in immediate danger","zh":"救援并带离处于直接危险中的病人"}],"correct":["C","A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence for fire response is RACE: Rescue, Alarm, Confine, and Extinguish/Evacuate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的火灾应对顺序是 RACE：救援、报警、局限 和灭火/疏散。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the acronym RACE to determine the logical flow of fire safety interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于首字母缩略词 RACE，以确定火灾安全干预措施的逻辑流程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse identifies a fire in a facility.","controlSentenceZh":"护士在设施内发现火灾。"}
{"queueIndex":637,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.446","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.446.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.446.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,36],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is training new staff on the use of a fire extinguisher. Place the steps of the PASS mnemonic in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在培训新员工使用灭火器。请按正确的顺序排列 PASS 准则的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps of the PASS mnemonic in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确的顺序排列 PASS 准则的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is training new staff on the use of a fire extinguisher.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在培训新员工使用灭火器。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Squeeze the handle of the extinguisher","zh":"挤压灭火器的手柄"},{"id":"A","en":"Aim at the base of the fire","zh":"对准火源根部"},{"id":"D","en":"Sweep from side to side at the base of the fire","zh":"在火源根部左右扫射"},{"id":"B","en":"Pull the pin on the fire extinguisher","zh":"拉开灭火器的插销"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The PASS mnemonic for extinguisher use is: Pull the pin, Aim at the base, Squeeze the handle, and Sweep from side to side.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用灭火器的 PASS 准则是：拉开插销、对准根部、挤压手柄 和左右扫射。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualizing the physical actions of using an extinguisher helps in remembering the PASS sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象使用灭火器的实际动作有助于记住 PASS 顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":638,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.447","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.447.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.447.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is collecting a sterile urine specimen from a client with an indwelling urinary catheter. Which action should the nurse take to ensure proper technique?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为留置导尿管的病人采集无菌尿标本。护士应该采取哪项行动以确保技术正确？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take to ensure proper technique?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该采取哪项行动以确保技术正确？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is collecting a sterile urine specimen from a client with an indwelling urinary catheter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为留置导尿管的病人采集无菌尿标本。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Clamp the catheter for 24 hours prior to collecting the specimen","zh":"采集标本前将导尿管夹闭 24 小时"},{"id":"D","en":"Clean the collection port with an alcohol swab and aspirate urine with a sterile syringe","zh":"用酒精棉签清洁采样口，并用无菌注射器抽取尿液"},{"id":"A","en":"Collect the specimen directly from the urinary drainage bag","zh":"直接从集尿袋中采集标本"},{"id":"B","en":"Disconnect the catheter from the drainage tube to collect urine","zh":"将导尿管从排水管上断开以采集尿液"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sterile specimens must be obtained through the collection port using aseptic technique. Urine in the drainage bag is not sterile.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无菌标本必须使用无菌技术通过采样口获取。集尿袋中的尿液不是无菌的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the answer choice that maintains the integrity of a closed drainage system and uses aseptic technique.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找能够维持密闭排水系统完整性并使用无菌技术的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":639,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.448","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.448.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.448.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to transport a stool specimen for a client suspected of having a vancomycin-resistant enterococcus (VRE) infection. Which actions are required? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备运送一名疑似感染耐万古霉素肠球菌 (VRE) 病人的粪便标本。需要采取哪些行动？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are required?","penultimateSentenceZh":"需要采取哪些行动？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Perform hand hygiene after removing gloves","zh":"脱掉手套后进行手部卫生"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensure the outside of the container is free of visible contamination","zh":"确保容器外部没有肉眼可见的污染"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the specimen container in a secondary biohazard bag","zh":"将标本容器放入二级生物安全袋中"},{"id":"B","en":"Label the specimen container at the client's bedside","zh":"在病床旁为标本容器贴上标签"},{"id":"E","en":"Transport the specimen in a pocket of the nurse's scrub top","zh":"将标本放在护士刷手服的口袋里运送"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Specimen handling requires labeling at the bedside to prevent errors, using secondary containment (biohazard bag), ensuring the outside is clean, and strict hand hygiene. Transporting specimens in personal clothing is a safety violation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标本处理要求在床旁贴标签以防止错误，使用二级容器（生物安全袋），确保外部清洁，并严格执行手部卫生。在个人衣物中运送标本是违反安全规定的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate each action for its contribution to identification accuracy and infection control. Eliminate any choice that involves unsafe transport methods.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估每项行动对识别准确性和感染控制的贡献。排除任何涉及不安全运输方法的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":640,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.449","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.449.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.449.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,132],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,49],"fullStemEn":"A client with an absolute neutrophil count (ANC) of 350/mm³ is admitted. Which healthcare provider's order should the nurse clarify?","fullStemZh":"一名绝对嗜中性粒细胞计数 (ANC) 为 350/mm³ 的病人入院。护士应该核实医生的哪项医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which healthcare provider's order should the nurse clarify?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该核实医生的哪项医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with an absolute neutrophil count (ANC) of 350/mm³ is admitted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名绝对嗜中性粒细胞计数 (ANC) 为 350/mm³ 的病人入院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assess temperature every 4 hours","zh":"每 4 小时评估一次体温"},{"id":"C","en":"Insert an indwelling urinary catheter for hourly output monitoring","zh":"留置导尿管以监测每小时出液量"},{"id":"D","en":"Initiate a low-microbial (neutropenic) diet","zh":"开始低微生物（中性粒细胞减少症）饮食"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer filgrastim subcutaneously daily","zh":"每日皮下注射非格司亭"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Invasive procedures such as urinary catheterization should be avoided in neutropenic clients due to the high risk of infection. Rectal temperatures and suppositories are also contraindicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"由于感染风险高，中性粒细胞减少症病人应避免有创操作，如导尿。直肠测温和栓剂也是禁忌的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the option that introduces a high risk of infection into a severely immunocompromised client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别出可能导致严重免疫功能低下病人感染风险极高的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":641,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.450","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.450.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.450.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge teaching to a client with severe neutropenia following chemotherapy. Which instructions should be included? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为化疗后严重中性粒细胞减少的病人进行出院指导。应该包括哪些说明？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"应该包括哪些说明？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Avoid large crowds and people who are sick","zh":"避免去人多的地方和接触生病的人"},{"id":"C","en":"Use a soft-bristled toothbrush for oral care","zh":"使用软毛牙刷进行口腔护理"},{"id":"B","en":"Wash your hands frequently with soap and warm water","zh":"经常用肥皂和温水洗手"},{"id":"D","en":"Eat fresh fruits and vegetables only after washing them thoroughly or peeling them","zh":"新鲜水果和蔬菜应彻底清洗或去皮后再食用"},{"id":"E","en":"Report a temperature over 100.4 °F (38 °C) immediately","zh":"如果体温超过 100.4 °F (38 °C)，立即报告"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teaching for severe neutropenia includes avoiding sick contacts and large crowds, frequent handwashing with ordinary soap and warm water, gentle oral care, safe food handling, and urgent reporting of fever. Fresh produce may be eaten when it can be washed thoroughly or peeled; categorical low-microbial diets have not been shown to reduce infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重度中性粒细胞减少症的指导包括避免接触病人和大型人群、经常用普通肥皂和温水洗手、轻柔口腔护理、安全处理食物以及发热时立即报告。能够彻底清洗或去皮的新鲜农产品可以食用；没有证据表明全面限制新鲜农产品的低微生物饮食可减少感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on infection prevention, safe food handling, and early fever reporting rather than assuming all fresh produce is prohibited.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注感染预防、安全食物处理和发热的早期报告，不要假定所有新鲜农产品都被禁止。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":642,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.451","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.451.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.451.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,132],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is triaging clients following a suspected release of anthrax (Bacillus anthracis). Which statement about anthrax is correct?","fullStemZh":"护士在疑似炭疽（炭疽杆菌）泄漏后对病人进行分诊。关于炭疽，哪项陈述是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement about anthrax is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"关于炭疽，哪项陈述是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is triaging clients following a suspected release of anthrax (Bacillus anthracis).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在疑似炭疽（炭疽杆菌）泄漏后对病人进行分诊。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Cutaneous anthrax presents as a painless, black eschar","zh":"皮肤炭疽表现为无痛性黑色焦痂"},{"id":"B","en":"Anthrax is highly contagious from person to person","zh":"炭疽在人与人之间具有高度传染性"},{"id":"D","en":"Smallpox and anthrax require the same isolation protocols","zh":"天花和炭疽需要相同的隔离方案"},{"id":"C","en":"Inhalation anthrax is treated with airborne precautions","zh":"吸入性炭疽应按空气预防措施处理"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cutaneous anthrax is characterized by a lesion that develops into a painless, necrotic ulcer with a black center (eschar).","rationaleCorrectZh":"皮肤炭疽的特征是皮损发展为中心带有黑色焦痂（痂皮）的无痛性坏死性溃疡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between agents that are contagious (like smallpox) and those that are not (like anthrax).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分具有传染性的病原体（如天花）和不具传染性的病原体（如炭疽）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":643,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.452","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.452.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.452.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[146,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,35],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is participating in a disaster preparedness drill for a smallpox outbreak. Which information should be included in the staff education? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在参加天花爆发的灾难防备演习。员工教育中应包括哪些信息？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which information should be included in the staff education?","penultimateSentenceZh":"员工教育中应包括哪些信息？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Standard, contact, and airborne precautions are necessary","zh":"标准、接触和空气预防措施是必要的"},{"id":"A","en":"Smallpox is transmitted by respiratory droplets and contact with lesions","zh":"天花通过呼吸道飞沫和接触皮损传播"},{"id":"E","en":"Vaccination within 3-4 days of exposure can prevent or lessen the disease","zh":"接触后 3-4 天内接种疫苗可以预防或减轻疾病"},{"id":"B","en":"The rash typically begins on the face and extremities","zh":"皮疹通常从面部和四肢开始"},{"id":"C","en":"Clients are most contagious after the fever subsides","zh":"病人在退烧后传染性最强"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Smallpox is highly contagious (droplet/contact), causes a centrifugal rash (face/extremities), requires strict isolation (airborne/contact), and post-exposure vaccination is effective.","rationaleCorrectZh":"天花具有高度传染性（飞沫/接触），会引起离心性皮疹（面部/四肢），需要严格隔离（空气/接触），且接触后接种疫苗有效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the specific isolation requirements and clinical presentation of smallpox compared to other biological agents.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想与其他生物病原体相比，天花的具体隔离要求和临床表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":644,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d7_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.453","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.453.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.453.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,47],"fullStemEn":"During a fire drill, the nurse practices the 'Confine' step of the RACE mnemonic. Which actions demonstrate proper confinement technique? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在消防演习中，护士练习 RACE 准则中的“局限”步骤。哪些行动证明了正确的局限技术？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions demonstrate proper confinement technique?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些行动证明了正确的局限技术？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Closing all client room doors","zh":"关闭所有病人房间的门"},{"id":"E","en":"Stuffing wet towels under the doors of rooms containing fire","zh":"在着火房间的门下塞进湿毛巾"},{"id":"D","en":"Leaving windows open to let smoke out","zh":"打开窗户排烟"},{"id":"C","en":"Turning off all localized oxygen valves","zh":"关闭所有局部氧气阀门"},{"id":"B","en":"Closing all fire doors in the corridor","zh":"关闭走廊里的所有防火门"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Confining a fire involves closing doors/windows, turning off oxygen to prevent fueling the fire, and using towels to block smoke. Windows should be closed to prevent drafts from feeding the fire.","rationaleCorrectZh":"局限火灾包括关闭门窗、关闭氧气以防止助长火势，以及使用毛巾阻挡烟雾。窗户应该关闭，以防止气流助燃。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider which actions physically limit the spread of fire, smoke, and combustible gases.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑哪些行动能从物理上限制火灾、烟雾和可燃气体的蔓延。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":645,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.454","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.454.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.454.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,73],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing pre-procedure screening for several clients scheduled for Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI). For each client finding, indicate whether the MRI is contraindicated or if it can proceed with precautions.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为几名计划进行核磁共振成像 (MRI) 的患者进行术前筛查。针对每项患者情况，请指出该 MRI 是禁忌还是可以在采取预防措施的情况下进行。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client finding, indicate whether the MRI is contraindicated or if it can proceed with precautions.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项患者情况，请指出该 MRI 是禁忌还是可以在采取预防措施的情况下进行。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is performing pre-procedure screening for several clients scheduled for Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为几名计划进行核磁共振成像 (MRI) 的患者进行术前筛查。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Non-MRI-conditional pacemaker or pacemaker compatibility unknown","zh":"非 MRI 条件性安全的起搏器，或起搏器兼容性未知"},{"id":"r2","en":"Copper intrauterine device (IUD)","zh":"含铜宫内节育器 (IUD)"},{"id":"r3","en":"Titanium orthopedic plate in the right femur","zh":"右股骨钛制骨科钢板"},{"id":"r4","en":"Programmable insulin pump that has not been cleared for MRI","zh":"尚未获得 MRI 安全许可的可编程胰岛素泵"},{"id":"r5","en":"Tattooed eyeliner containing metallic pigment","zh":"含有金属颜料的纹绣眼线"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Proceed with Precautions","zh":"采取预防措施后进行"},{"id":"c1","en":"Contraindicated","zh":"禁忌"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MRI safety screening identifies ferromagnetic materials and electronic devices that may malfunction or cause injury in a strong magnetic field.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MRI 安全筛查旨在识别在强磁场中可能发生故障或造成伤害的铁磁性材料和电子设备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between devices without MRI clearance and items that can proceed after screening and precautions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分尚未取得 MRI 安全许可的设备，以及经过筛查和采取预防措施后可以进行检查的物品。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":646,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.455","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.455.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.455.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,57],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic kidney disease is scheduled for a CT scan with intravenous iodinated contrast. Which client finding requires the nurse's most immediate intervention before the procedure?","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性肾脏疾病的患者计划进行静脉注射碘造影剂的 CT 扫描。在程序开始前，哪项患者情况需要护士最立即的干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client finding requires the nurse's most immediate intervention before the procedure?","terminalSentenceZh":"在程序开始前，哪项患者情况需要护士最立即的干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with chronic kidney disease is scheduled for a CT scan with intravenous iodinated contrast.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有慢性肾脏疾病的患者计划进行静脉注射碘造影剂的 CT 扫描。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Serum potassium level of 5.1 mEq/L","zh":"血清钾水平为 5.1 mEq/L"},{"id":"D","en":"Current prescription for Metformin 500 mg twice daily","zh":"目前处方为二甲双胍 500 mg，每日两次"},{"id":"C","en":"Blood pressure of 152/88 mmHg","zh":"血压为 152/88 mmHg"},{"id":"B","en":"History of a localized skin rash after eating strawberries","zh":"吃草莓后有局部皮疹病史"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Metformin must be held for 48 hours after contrast administration to prevent lactic acidosis if contrast-induced nephropathy occurs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二甲双胍必须在注射造影剂后停药 48 小时，以防止如果发生造影剂诱发的肾病时出现乳酸性酸中毒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the risk of lactic acidosis when metformin is used in combination with contrast media, especially in clients with baseline renal issues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别二甲双胍与造影剂合用时的乳酸性酸中毒风险，特别是对于有基础肾脏问题的患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":647,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.456","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.456.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.456.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[210,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[87,95],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the intensive care unit with suspected salicylate toxicity. The laboratory results show: Sodium 140 mEq/L, Chloride 104 mEq/L, and Bicarbonate (HCO3-) 16 mEq/L. Calculate the anion gap. (Record your answer as a whole number.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者因疑似水杨酸中毒入住重症监护病房。实验室检查结果显示：钠 140 mEq/L，氯 104 mEq/L，碳酸氢盐 (HCO3-) 16 mEq/L。请计算阴离子间隙。（请记录为整数。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Record your answer as a whole number.)","terminalSentenceZh":"请记录为整数。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the anion gap.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请计算阴离子间隙。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Anion Gap","zh":"阴离子间隙"},"acceptable":["20"],"numeric":{"value":20,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The anion gap is calculated using the formula: Na - (Cl + HCO3). In this case: 140 - (104 + 16) = 140 - 120 = 20 mEq/L.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴离子间隙的计算公式为：Na - (Cl + HCO3)。在本例中：140 - (104 + 16) = 140 - 120 = 20 mEq/L。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the basic formula for the anion gap: Na - (Cl + HCO3). Normal range is typically 8-16 mEq/L.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住阴离子间隙的基本公式：Na - (Cl + HCO3)。正常范围通常为 8-16 mEq/L。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":648,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.457","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.457.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.457.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[175,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[83,98],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the arterial blood gas (ABG) results for a client with end-stage COPD who has had persistent vomiting for three days: pH 7.37, PaCO2 65 mmHg, HCO3 36 mEq/L. Which interpretation of these findings is correct?","fullStemZh":"护士查看了一名患有终末期 COPD 且连续三天持续呕吐的患者的动脉血气 (ABG) 结果：pH 7.37, PaCO2 65 mmHg, HCO3 36 mEq/L。对这些结果的哪项解释是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation of these findings is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"对这些结果的哪项解释是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the arterial blood gas (ABG) results for a client with end-stage COPD who has had persistent vomiting for three days: pH 7.37, PaCO2 65 mmHg, HCO3 36 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看了一名患有终末期 COPD 且连续三天持续呕吐的患者的动脉血气 (ABG) 结果：pH 7.37, PaCO2 65 mmHg, HCO3 36 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Mixed respiratory acidosis and metabolic alkalosis","zh":"混合性呼吸性酸中毒和代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"A","en":"Uncompensated respiratory acidosis","zh":"失代偿性呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"C","en":"Partially compensated metabolic alkalosis","zh":"部分代偿性代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"B","en":"Fully compensated respiratory acidosis","zh":"完全代偿性呼吸性酸中毒"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has two primary disorders: respiratory acidosis from COPD (retaining CO2) and metabolic alkalosis from vomiting (losing acid). The normal pH suggests they are counteracting each other, but the extreme values for both CO2 and HCO3 indicate a mixed disorder.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者有两种原发性疾病：COPD 导致的呼吸性酸中毒（二氧化碳潴留）和呕吐导致的代谢性碱中毒（酸流失）。正常的 pH 值表明它们相互抵消，但 CO2 和 HCO3 的极端数值表明存在混合性疾病。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for a normal pH paired with significantly abnormal values in both CO2 and HCO3 in a client with two competing clinical conditions (COPD and vomiting).","testTakingStrategyZh":"在具有两种相互竞争的临床状况（COPD 和呕吐）的患者中，寻找正常的 pH 值以及 CO2 和 HCO3 的显著异常值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":649,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.458","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.458.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.458.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing a client who has been immobilized following a spinal cord injury. For each clinical finding, select the body system complication that it most likely represents.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名因脊髓损伤而卧床不起的患者。针对每项临床表现，请选择其最可能代表的身体系统并发症。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, select the body system complication that it most likely represents.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项临床表现，请选择其最可能代表的身体系统并发症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is assessing a client who has been immobilized following a spinal cord injury.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名因脊髓损伤而卧床不起的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Orthostatic hypotension and increased cardiac workload","zh":"体位性低血压和心脏负荷增加"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hypostatic pneumonia and atelectasis","zh":"坠积性肺炎和肺不张"},{"id":"r3","en":"Renal calculi and hypercalcemia","zh":"肾结石和高钙血症"},{"id":"r4","en":"Negative nitrogen balance and muscle wasting","zh":"负氮平衡和肌肉萎缩"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Musculoskeletal/Urinary","zh":"骨骼肌肉/泌尿系统"},{"id":"c2","en":"Respiratory","zh":"呼吸系统"},{"id":"c1","en":"Cardiovascular","zh":"心血管系统"},{"id":"c4","en":"Metabolic","zh":"代谢系统"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immobility affects all body systems. Understanding the physiological changes helps in early detection and prevention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"卧床不起会影响所有身体系统。了解生理变化有助于早期发现和预防。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect specific symptoms (e.g., nitrogen balance) to the relevant systemic metabolic processes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将特定症状（例如氮平衡）与相关的系统性代谢过程联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":650,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.459","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.459.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.459.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,98],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Which clinical finding in an immobile client would be the most indicative of a pulmonary embolism?","fullStemZh":"对于一名卧床不起的患者，哪项临床表现最能指示肺栓塞？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which clinical finding in an immobile client would be the most indicative of a pulmonary embolism?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于一名卧床不起的患者，哪项临床表现最能指示肺栓塞？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Productive cough with yellow-tinged sputum","zh":"咳出带黄色的痰液"},{"id":"C","en":"Unilateral calf swelling and tenderness","zh":"单侧小腿肿胀和压痛"},{"id":"A","en":"Decreased breath sounds at the lung bases","zh":"肺底呼吸音减弱"},{"id":"B","en":"Sudden onset of dyspnea and chest pain","zh":"突发呼吸困难和胸痛"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden dyspnea and chest pain are classic signs of pulmonary embolism (PE), a life-threatening complication of deep vein thrombosis (DVT) in immobile clients.","rationaleCorrectZh":"突发呼吸困难和胸痛是肺栓塞 (PE) 的经典征兆，这是卧床不起患者深静脉血栓 (DVT) 的致命并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the localized signs of DVT and the systemic, life-threatening signs of PE.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分 DVT 的局部体征和 PE 的系统性、致命性体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":651,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.460","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.460.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.460.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is supervising a newly licensed nurse who is preparing a client for an MRI. Which action by the new nurse requires immediate intervention?","fullStemZh":"护士正在监督一名正在为患者准备 MRI 的新执业护士。该新护士的哪项行为需要立即干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the new nurse requires immediate intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"该新护士的哪项行为需要立即干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is supervising a newly licensed nurse who is preparing a client for an MRI.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监督一名正在为患者准备 MRI 的新执业护士。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Asking the client if they have ever worked as a metal grinder or welder","zh":"询问患者是否曾从事金属研磨工或焊工的工作"},{"id":"A","en":"Taping the client's wedding ring in place with adhesive tape","zh":"用胶带将患者的婚戒固定在原位"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensuring the client has removed their medicated transdermal patch","zh":"确保患者已取下药用经皮贴剂"},{"id":"C","en":"Checking the client's medical history for claustrophobia","zh":"检查患者的幽闭恐惧症病史"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"All jewelry, including wedding rings, should be removed to prevent thermal injury or projectile hazards. Taping is insufficient safety protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"所有珠宝，包括婚戒，都应取下，以防止热损伤或投射风险。使用胶带固定是不充分的安全协议。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the safest way to manage metallic items (removal) rather than temporary fixes like taping.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别处理金属物品的最安全方法（取下），而不是像粘贴这样的临时修补措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":652,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.461","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.461.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.461.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,37],"fullStemEn":"For each set of arterial blood gas (ABG) results, select the clinical interpretation that best describes the client's acid-base status.","fullStemZh":"针对每组动脉血气 (ABG) 结果，请选择最能描述患者酸碱状态的临床解释。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each set of arterial blood gas (ABG) results, select the clinical interpretation that best describes the client's acid-base status.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每组动脉血气 (ABG) 结果，请选择最能描述患者酸碱状态的临床解释。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"pH 7.30, PaCO2 52, HCO3 24","zh":"pH 7.30, PaCO2 52, HCO3 24"},{"id":"r2","en":"pH 7.36, PaCO2 30, HCO3 16","zh":"pH 7.36, PaCO2 30, HCO3 16"},{"id":"r3","en":"pH 7.49, PaCO2 48, HCO3 35","zh":"pH 7.49, PaCO2 48, HCO3 35"},{"id":"r4","en":"pH 7.52, PaCO2 28, HCO3 22","zh":"pH 7.52, PaCO2 28, HCO3 22"}],"columns":[{"id":"c4","en":"Partially Compensated Met Alkalosis","zh":"部分代偿性代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"c2","en":"Uncompensated Resp Alkalosis","zh":"失代偿性呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"c3","en":"Fully Compensated Met Acidosis","zh":"完全代偿性代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"c1","en":"Uncompensated Resp Acidosis","zh":"失代偿性呼吸性酸中毒"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c4"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ABG interpretation requires analyzing the pH, the primary source of the imbalance, and the presence of compensation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ABG 解释需要分析 pH 值、失衡的原发来源以及代偿的存在。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: In fully compensated states, the pH is within the normal range (7.35–7.45).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：在完全代偿状态下，pH 值在正常范围内（7.35–7.45）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":653,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.462","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.462.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.462.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,52],"fullStemEn":"To prevent contrast-induced nephropathy (CIN) in a high-risk client scheduled for a procedure requiring IV contrast, which intervention should the nurse prioritize?","fullStemZh":"为了预防计划进行静脉造影程序的极高风险患者出现造影剂诱发的肾病 (CIN)，护士应优先采取哪项干预措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"To prevent contrast-induced nephropathy (CIN) in a high-risk client scheduled for a procedure requiring IV contrast, which intervention should the nurse prioritize?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了预防计划进行静脉造影程序的极高风险患者出现造影剂诱发的肾病 (CIN)，护士应优先采取哪项干预措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administering oral furosemide immediately after the procedure","zh":"在程序结束后立即给予口服呋塞米"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensuring adequate intravenous hydration with 0.9% normal saline","zh":"确保使用 0.9% 生理盐水进行充足的静脉补液"},{"id":"A","en":"Applying a warm compress to the injection site","zh":"在注射部位进行热敷"},{"id":"B","en":"Instructing the client to remain NPO for 12 hours before the procedure","zh":"指示患者在程序前禁食 12 小时"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adequate hydration is the most effective way to flush contrast media from the kidneys and prevent CIN.","rationaleCorrectZh":"充足的补液是清除肾脏造影剂并预防 CIN 的最有效方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on 'flushing' the contrast out of the system as the primary prevention for renal damage.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“清除”系统中的造影剂作为预防肾损伤的首要措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":654,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d8_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.463","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.463.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.463.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[176,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,70],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing an immobile client's sacral area and finds a wound that is 2 cm deep, with visible subcutaneous fat and slough, but no muscle, tendon, or bone is exposed. How should the nurse document this pressure injury?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名卧床不起患者的骶尾部，发现一个深 2 厘米的伤口，可见皮下脂肪和腐肉，但未暴露肌肉、肌腱或骨骼。护士应如何记录该压力性损伤？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse document this pressure injury?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何记录该压力性损伤？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing an immobile client's sacral area and finds a wound that is 2 cm deep, with visible subcutaneous fat and slough, but no muscle, tendon, or bone is exposed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名卧床不起患者的骶尾部，发现一个深 2 厘米的伤口，可见皮下脂肪和腐肉，但未暴露肌肉、肌腱或骨骼。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Stage 3 pressure injury","zh":"3 期压力性损伤"},{"id":"B","en":"Stage 2 pressure injury","zh":"2 期压力性损伤"},{"id":"C","en":"Unstageable pressure injury","zh":"不可分期压力性损伤"},{"id":"A","en":"Stage 4 pressure injury","zh":"4 期压力性损伤"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stage 3 pressure injuries involve full-thickness skin loss where subcutaneous fat is visible, but deeper structures (bone/tendon/muscle) are not.","rationaleCorrectZh":"3 期压力性损伤涉及全层皮肤缺失，可见皮下脂肪，但不可见深层结构（骨骼/肌腱/肌肉）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use a hierarchical approach: visible fat = stage 3; visible bone/muscle = stage 4.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用分级方法：可见脂肪 = 3 期；可见骨骼/肌肉 = 4 期。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":655,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.464","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.464.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.464.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[257,286],"terminalOffsetsZh":[101,109],"fullStemEn":"A client with 40% total body surface area (TBSA) partial and full-thickness burns is in the first 8 hours of the resuscitation phase. The nurse notes a heart rate of 124 bpm, blood pressure 92/58 mmHg, and a urine output of 20 mL/hr for the last two hours. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一名患有 40% 全身体表面积 (TBSA) 部分和全层烧伤的患者处于复苏阶段的前 8 小时。护士注意到患者心率为 124 次/分，血压为 92/58 mmHg，且过去两小时的尿量为 20 毫升/小时。哪项措施是首选？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施是首选？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes a heart rate of 124 bpm, blood pressure 92/58 mmHg, and a urine output of 20 mL/hr for the last two hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到患者心率为 124 次/分，血压为 92/58 mmHg，且过去两小时的尿量为 20 毫升/小时。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Notify the healthcare provider of suspected acute kidney injury.","zh":"通知医疗保健提供者怀疑发生急性肾损伤。"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare to administer a low-dose dopamine infusion.","zh":"准备输注低剂量多巴胺。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer a 500 mL bolus of 0.45% normal saline.","zh":"给予 500 毫升 0.45% 生理盐水冲洗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Increase the rate of the isotonic IV fluid infusion.","zh":"增加等渗静脉补液的输注速率。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In the resuscitation phase of burn management, the gold standard for assessing the adequacy of fluid resuscitation is urine output (target: 0.5 mL/kg/hr or approx 30-50 mL/hr). Tachycardia, hypotension, and low urine output indicate inadequate volume. The priority is to increase the rate of the prescribed isotonic crystalloid (usually Lactated Ringer's).","rationaleCorrectZh":"在烧伤管理的复苏阶段，评估补液是否充分的金标准是尿量（目标：0.5 毫升/公斤/小时，或约 30-50 毫升/小时）。心动过速、低血压和尿量减少表明血容量不足。首要任务是增加规定的等渗晶体液（通常为乳酸林格氏液）的输注速率。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the resuscitation phase goals. Urine output is the most reliable indicator of fluid status in this phase. Eliminate options that use incorrect fluids (hypotonic) or premature interventions (vasopressors).","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注复苏阶段的目标。尿量是该阶段体液状态最可靠的指标。排除使用错误液体（低渗）或过早干预（血管加压药）的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":656,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.465","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.465.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.465.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,46],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with suspected obstructive shock. Which of the following conditions or clinical findings are consistent with this diagnosis? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名疑似梗阻性休克的患者。下列哪些情况或临床表现与该诊断一致？（择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following conditions or clinical findings are consistent with this diagnosis?","penultimateSentenceZh":"下列哪些情况或临床表现与该诊断一致？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Cardiac tamponade","zh":"心包填塞"},{"id":"D","en":"Decreased systemic vascular resistance (SVR)","zh":"全身血管阻力 (SVR) 降低"},{"id":"C","en":"Massive pulmonary embolism","zh":"大面积肺栓塞"},{"id":"E","en":"Increased central venous pressure (CVP)","zh":"中心静脉压 (CVP) 升高"},{"id":"B","en":"Tension pneumothorax","zh":"张力性气胸"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Obstructive shock occurs when a physical obstruction prevents adequate blood flow. Cardiac tamponade, tension pneumothorax, and pulmonary embolism are classic causes. Because blood flow is blocked, filling pressures like CVP increase due to backflow.","rationaleCorrectZh":"梗阻性休克发生在物理性梗阻阻碍充足血流时。心包填塞、张力性气胸和肺栓塞是典型原因。由于血流受阻，由于回流，中心静脉压 (CVP) 等充盈压会升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the underlying pathophysiology of 'obstruction.' Differentiate between distributive (vasodilation) and obstructive (mechanical block) types.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别“梗阻”的潜在病理生理学。区分分布性（血管扩张）和梗阻性（机械阻塞）类型。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":657,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.466","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.466.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.466.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is interpreting hemodynamic parameters for a client in the Intensive Care Unit. Match each clinical parameter set with the state it most likely indicates.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为重症监护病房的一位患者解释血流动力学参数。将每组临床参数与最可能指示的状态相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each clinical parameter set with the state it most likely indicates.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每组临床参数与最可能指示的状态相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is interpreting hemodynamic parameters for a client in the Intensive Care Unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为重症监护病房的一位患者解释血流动力学参数。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"CVP 1 mmHg, PAWP 4 mmHg","zh":"CVP 1 mmHg, PAWP 4 mmHg"},{"id":"r2","en":"CVP 12 mmHg, PAWP 22 mmHg","zh":"CVP 12 mmHg, PAWP 22 mmHg"},{"id":"r3","en":"SVR 1800 dynes/sec/cm⁻⁵","zh":"SVR 1800 dynes/sec/cm⁻⁵"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Vasoconstriction","zh":"血管收缩"},{"id":"c1","en":"Hypovolemia","zh":"低血容量"},{"id":"c2","en":"Left-sided heart failure","zh":"左侧心力衰竭"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Low filling pressures (CVP, PAWP) indicate hypovolemia. High filling pressures (especially PAWP > 18) indicate left-sided heart failure or fluid overload. Elevated SVR (> 1200) indicates vasoconstriction, often as a compensatory mechanism for low cardiac output.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低充盈压（CVP、PAWP）指示低血容量。高充盈压（尤其是 PAWP > 18）指示左侧心力衰竭或液体负荷过重。SVR 升高（> 1200）指示血管收缩，通常作为低心输出量的代偿机制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember normal ranges: CVP (2-8 mmHg), PAWP (6-12 mmHg), SVR (800-1200 dynes). Use these to categorize the values as low, normal, or high.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住正常范围：CVP (2-8 mmHg)，PAWP (6-12 mmHg)，SVR (800-1200 dynes)。使用这些范围将数值分类为低、正常或高。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":658,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.467","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.467.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.467.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,54],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with major thermal burns. Which physiological changes should the nurse expect to occur during the first 24 hours of the resuscitation phase? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"一名患有严重热烧伤的患者入院。护士应预见在复苏阶段的前 24 小时内会发生哪些生理变化？（选择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which physiological changes should the nurse expect to occur during the first 24 hours of the resuscitation phase?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见在复苏阶段的前 24 小时内会发生哪些生理变化？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Intravascular fluid shift to the interstitium","zh":"血管内液向间质转移"},{"id":"C","en":"Hyperkalemia","zh":"高钾血症"},{"id":"D","en":"Decreased hematocrit","zh":"血细胞比容降低"},{"id":"E","en":"Metabolic acidosis","zh":"代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"A","en":"Increased capillary permeability","zh":"毛细血管通透性增加"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Major burns cause systemic inflammatory response leading to increased capillary permeability and massive intravascular-to-interstitial fluid shifts. Cell destruction releases potassium. Inadequate perfusion leads to anaerobic metabolism and lactic acid buildup (E). Hematocrit typically increases due to hemoconcentration (loss of plasma).","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重烧伤引起全身炎症反应，导致毛细血管通透性增加 和大量血管内液向间质转移。细胞破坏释放钾。灌注不足导致无氧代谢和乳酸堆积 (E)。血细胞比容通常由于血液浓缩（血浆丢失）而增加。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the resuscitation (emergent) phase and the acute phase. In the first 24 hours, everything is 'leaking' and 'shifting.'","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分复苏（紧急）阶段和急性阶段。在前 24 小时内，一切都在“渗漏”和“转移”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":659,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.468","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.468.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.468.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,177],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,47],"fullStemEn":"A client with a suspected tension pneumothorax is exhibiting signs of obstructive shock. Which assessment finding should the nurse identify as a hallmark sign of this condition?","fullStemZh":"一名疑似张力性气胸的患者表现出梗阻性休克的迹象。护士应识别出哪项评估结果是该病症的特征性迹象？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding should the nurse identify as a hallmark sign of this condition?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应识别出哪项评估结果是该病症的特征性迹象？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a suspected tension pneumothorax is exhibiting signs of obstructive shock.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名疑似张力性气胸的患者表现出梗阻性休克的迹象。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Bradycardia and bradypnea.","zh":"心动过缓和呼吸缓慢。"},{"id":"B","en":"Tracheal deviation toward the affected side.","zh":"气管向患侧偏移。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hypotension with a wide pulse pressure.","zh":"低血压伴脉压增宽。"},{"id":"C","en":"Distended neck veins and absent breath sounds on the affected side.","zh":"颈静脉怒张且患侧呼吸音消失。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tension pneumothorax increases intrapleural pressure, collapsing the lung and shifting the mediastinum, which compresses the great vessels and obstructs venous return (leading to distended neck veins). Absent breath sounds confirm the collapsed lung.","rationaleCorrectZh":"张力性气胸增加胸膜内压力，使肺塌陷并导致纵隔移位，从而压迫大血管并阻碍静脉回流（导致颈静脉怒张）。呼吸音消失证实肺已塌陷。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize the mechanical effect of air trapped in the chest. It pushes things away from the air (tracheal deviation away) and stops blood coming back to the heart (JVD).","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象胸部积聚空气的机械效应。它会将物体推离空气（气管向健侧偏移）并阻止血液流回心脏（颈静脉怒张）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":660,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.469","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.469.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.469.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,53],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring hemodynamic characteristics of early septic shock and cardiogenic shock. Identify which shock type each finding is associated with when compared to the other.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测早期感染性休克和心源性休克的血流动力学特征。识别与另一种类型相比，每项发现与哪种休克类型相关。","terminalSentenceEn":"Identify which shock type each finding is associated with when compared to the other.","terminalSentenceZh":"识别与另一种类型相比，每项发现与哪种休克类型相关。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring hemodynamic characteristics of early septic shock and cardiogenic shock.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测早期感染性休克和心源性休克的血流动力学特征。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"High Cardiac Output (CO) / Cardiac Index (CI)","zh":"高心输出量 (CO) / 心指数 (CI)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Low Systemic Vascular Resistance (SVR)","zh":"低全身血管阻力 (SVR)"},{"id":"r3","en":"High Pulmonary Artery Wedge Pressure (PAWP)","zh":"高肺动脉楔压 (PAWP)"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Cardiogenic Shock","zh":"心源性休克"},{"id":"c1","en":"Early Septic Shock","zh":"早期感染性休克"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Early septic shock is hyperdynamic (high CO, low SVR). Cardiogenic shock is a pump failure, leading to low CO and high filling pressures (PAWP) due to blood backing up in the left heart.","rationaleCorrectZh":"早期感染性休克处于高动力状态（高 CO，低 SVR）。心源性休克是泵功能衰竭，导致低 CO 和由于血液在左心淤积引起的高充盈压 (PAWP)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast the 'pump failure' (cardiogenic) with the 'pipe failure' (distributive/sepsis). Pipes that are too wide (low SVR) lead to high flow (CO) initially.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“泵故障”（心源性）与“管道故障”（分布性/败血症）进行对比。管道太宽（低 SVR）最初会导致高流量 (CO)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring hemodynamic characteristics of early septic shock and cardiogenic shock.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在监测早期感染性休克和心源性休克的血流动力学特征。"}
{"queueIndex":661,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.470","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.470.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.470.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,311],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,133],"fullStemEn":"A client weighing 80 kg has sustained 50% total body surface area (TBSA) burns. The injury occurred at 1200. The client arrived at the hospital at 1400. Using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA), at what rate (mL/hr) should the nurse set the infusion pump to complete the first half of the fluid resuscitation?","fullStemZh":"一名体重 80 公斤的患者遭受了 50% 全身体表面积 (TBSA) 的烧伤。受伤发生在 12:00。患者于 14:00 到达医院。使用 Parkland 公式 (4 mL/kg/%TBSA)，护士应将输液泵设置为多大速率 (mL/hr) 以完成前半部分的液体复苏？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Parkland formula (4 mL/kg/%TBSA), at what rate (mL/hr) should the nurse set the infusion pump to complete the first half of the fluid resuscitation?","terminalSentenceZh":"使用 Parkland 公式 (4 mL/kg/%TBSA)，护士应将输液泵设置为多大速率 (mL/hr) 以完成前半部分的液体复苏？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client arrived at the hospital at 1400.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者于 14:00 到达医院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"1,000 mL/hr","zh":"1,000 毫升/小时"},{"id":"A","en":"1,600 mL/hr","zh":"1,600 毫升/小时"},{"id":"C","en":"1,333 mL/hr","zh":"1,333 毫升/小时"},{"id":"B","en":"2,666 mL/hr","zh":"2,666 毫升/小时"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total 24h fluids = 4 mL * 80 kg * 50 = 16,000 mL. Half (8,000 mL) must be given in the first 8 hours FROM THE TIME OF INJURY. Injury was at 1200, so 8 hours later is 2000. Arrival was at 1400, leaving 6 hours (1400 to 2000) to deliver the first 8,000 mL. 8,000 mL / 6 hr = 1,333.33 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"24 小时总液量 = 4 毫升 * 80 公斤 * 50 = 16,000 毫升。一半 (8,000 毫升) 必须在受伤后的前 8 小时内给予。受伤发生在 12:00，所以 8 小时后是 20:00。到达医院是 14:00，剩下 6 小时 (14:00 到 20:00) 来输注前 8,000 毫升。8,000 毫升 / 6 小时 = 1,333.33 毫升/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Key detail: The Parkland clock starts at the time of injury, not arrival at the hospital. Always subtract the delay time from the initial 8-hour window.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关键细节：Parkland 公式的时间从受伤时开始计算，而不是到达医院时。务必从最初的 8 小时窗口中减去延迟时间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":662,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.471","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.471.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.471.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[146,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,52],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with a spinal cord injury at the T2 level and is in neurogenic shock. Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"一名 T2 水平脊髓损伤的患者入院，并处于神经源性休克状态。护士应预见哪些临床表现？（选择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Tachycardia","zh":"心动过速"},{"id":"A","en":"Hypotension","zh":"低血压"},{"id":"C","en":"Warm, dry skin","zh":"皮肤温暖、干燥"},{"id":"B","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"E","en":"Poikilothermia","zh":"变温症/随温症"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Neurogenic shock is caused by the loss of sympathetic tone. This leads to massive vasodilation (hypotension), loss of compensatory tachycardia (bradycardia), and inability to regulate body temperature (poikilothermia). Skin is warm and dry because of vasodilation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"神经源性休克是由于交感神经张力丧失引起的。这导致大规模血管扩张（低血压）、丧失代偿性心动过速（心动过缓）以及无法调节体温（变温症）。由于血管扩张，皮肤温暖而干燥。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the 'unusual' features of neurogenic shock: Bradycardia and Warm skin. Most other shocks present with tachycardia and cool skin.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住神经源性休克的“不寻常”特征：心动过缓和皮肤温暖。大多数其他休克表现为心动过速和皮肤阴冷。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":663,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.472","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.472.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.472.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,244],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,105],"fullStemEn":"A client's hemodynamic profile shows: Cardiac Index (CI) 1.8 L/min/m², Pulmonary Artery Wedge Pressure (PAWP) 22 mmHg, and Systemic Vascular Resistance (SVR) 1800 dynes/sec/cm⁻⁵. Which medication should the nurse anticipate administering first?","fullStemZh":"一名患者的血流动力学特征显示：心指数 (CI) 1.8 L/min/m²，肺动脉楔压 (PAWP) 22 mmHg，全身血管阻力 (SVR) 1800 dynes/sec/cm⁻⁵。护士应预见首先使用哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse anticipate administering first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预见首先使用哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client's hemodynamic profile shows: Cardiac Index (CI) 1.8 L/min/m², Pulmonary Artery Wedge Pressure (PAWP) 22 mmHg, and Systemic Vascular Resistance (SVR) 1800 dynes/sec/cm⁻⁵.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者的血流动力学特征显示：心指数 (CI) 1.8 L/min/m²，肺动脉楔压 (PAWP) 22 mmHg，全身血管阻力 (SVR) 1800 dynes/sec/cm⁻⁵。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"0.9% Normal Saline bolus","zh":"0.9% 生理盐水冲洗"},{"id":"D","en":"Furosemide IV push","zh":"静脉注射呋塞米"},{"id":"C","en":"Dobutamine infusion","zh":"多巴酚丁胺输注"},{"id":"A","en":"Norepinephrine infusion","zh":"去甲肾上腺素输注"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The profile (low CI, high PAWP, high SVR) is consistent with cardiogenic shock. Dobutamine is an inotrope that increases myocardial contractility and decreases SVR, making it the priority to improve pump performance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该特征（低 CI、高 PAWP、高 SVR）与心源性休克一致。多巴酚丁胺是一种正性肌力药，可增加心肌收缩力并降低 SVR，使其成为改善泵性能的首选药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the primary problem. Low CI with High PAWP = Cardiogenic Shock. Treat with inotropes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找主要问题。低 CI 伴高 PAWP = 心源性休克。使用正性肌力药物治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":664,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_d9_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.473","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.473.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.473.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for clients in the acute resuscitation phase of different conditions. Match the laboratory abnormality to the most likely pathophysiology.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查处于不同病症急性复苏阶段的患者的实验室结果。将实验室异常与最可能的病理生理学相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match the laboratory abnormality to the most likely pathophysiology.","terminalSentenceZh":"将实验室异常与最可能的病理生理学相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for clients in the acute resuscitation phase of different conditions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查处于不同病症急性复苏阶段的患者的实验室结果。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Elevated Hematocrit (e.g., 58%)","zh":"血细胞比容升高（例如 58%）"},{"id":"r2","en":"Elevated Lactic Acid and Procalcitonin","zh":"乳酸和降钙素原升高"},{"id":"r3","en":"Elevated Troponin and B-type Natriuretic Peptide (BNP)","zh":"肌钙蛋白和 B 型利尿钠肽 (BNP) 升高"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Burn shock (Hemoconcentration)","zh":"烧伤性休克（血液浓缩）"},{"id":"c2","en":"Septic shock","zh":"感染性休克"},{"id":"c3","en":"Cardiogenic shock","zh":"心源性休克"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Elevated hematocrit in burns is due to plasma loss causing relative concentration of red cells. Procalcitonin is a specific marker for bacterial sepsis. Troponin (myocardial damage) and BNP (heart failure/stretch) are markers for cardiogenic issues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"烧伤时血细胞比容升高是由于血浆丢失导致红细胞相对浓度增加。降钙素原是细菌性败血症的特异性指标。肌钙蛋白（心肌损伤）和 BNP（心力衰竭/拉伸）是心源性问题的标志物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate specific lab markers with their 'home' conditions. Procalcitonin = Infection. BNP = Heart failure. Elevated Hct in emergency = Fluid loss.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将特定的实验室标志物与其“所属”病症联系起来。降钙素原 = 感染。BNP = 心力衰竭。急诊中血细胞比容升高 = 体液丢失。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":665,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.474","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.474.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.474.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,55],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client diagnosed with Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone (SIADH). Which assessment findings should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名被诊断为抗利尿激素分泌异常综合征 (SIADH) 的患者。护士应预见哪些评估结果？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which assessment findings should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见哪些评估结果？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Peripheral edema","zh":"外周水肿"},{"id":"C","en":"Increased urinary output","zh":"尿量增加"},{"id":"E","en":"Decreased serum osmolality","zh":"血浆渗透压降低"},{"id":"A","en":"Serum sodium 128 mEq/L (128 mmol/L)","zh":"血钠 128 mEq/L (128 mmol/L)"},{"id":"B","en":"Urine specific gravity 1.035","zh":"尿比重 1.035"}],"correct":["A","B","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"SIADH causes excessive water retention, leading to dilutional hyponatremia (low serum sodium), concentrated urine (high specific gravity), and decreased serum osmolality. Peripheral edema is typically not seen because the water is retained intracellularly and in the vascular space without significant sodium retention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"SIADH 导致过度的水分滞留，引起稀释性低钠血症（血钠降低）、尿液浓缩（高比重）和血浆渗透压降低。通常不会出现外周水肿，因为水分滞留在细胞内和血管内，而没有明显的钠滞留。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of SIADH as 'Soaked Inside'. Water is retained, so everything in the blood is diluted (low sodium, low osmolality) and everything in the urine is concentrated (high specific gravity).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将 SIADH 想象为“内部浸泡”。水分滞留，因此血液中的所有物质都被稀释（低钠、低渗透压），而尿液中的所有物质都被浓缩（高比重）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":666,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.475","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.475.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.475.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is monitoring a client receiving digoxin for heart failure. Which findings may indicate digoxin toxicity? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名因心力衰竭接受地高辛治疗的患者。哪些表现可能提示地高辛中毒？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings may indicate digoxin toxicity?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些表现可能提示地高辛中毒？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Heart rate of 52 beats/min","zh":"心率 52 次/分"},{"id":"E","en":"Increased urinary output","zh":"尿量增加"},{"id":"A","en":"Anorexia and nausea","zh":"食欲不振和恶心"},{"id":"B","en":"Visual disturbances, such as yellow halos","zh":"视力障碍，如黄视/黄晕"},{"id":"D","en":"Serum potassium level of 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L)","zh":"血钾水平 3.2 mEq/L (3.2 mmol/L)"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Early signs of digoxin toxicity include GI symptoms (anorexia, nausea, vomiting) and neurological symptoms (visual changes like yellow/green halos). Bradycardia is a classic cardiac sign. Hypokalemia increases the risk of toxicity but is not a sign of toxicity itself.","rationaleCorrectZh":"地高辛中毒的早期症状包括胃肠道症状（食欲不振、恶心、呕吐）和神经系统症状（视力变化，如黄/绿视）。心动过缓是经典的心脏体征。低钾血症会增加中毒风险，但其本身不是中毒的体征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the hierarchy of toxicity signs: GI first, then Neuro/Visual, then Cardiac (bradycardia/arrhythmias).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住中毒症状的分级：首先是胃肠道，然后是神经/视觉，最后是心脏（心动过缓/心律失常）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which findings may indicate digoxin toxicity?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些表现可能提示地高辛中毒？（"}
{"queueIndex":667,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.476","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.476.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.476.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with a head injury. Which finding is the most sensitive early indicator of increased intracranial pressure (ICP)?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名头部受伤的患者。哪项发现是颅内压 (ICP) 升高的最敏感早期指标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding is the most sensitive early indicator of increased intracranial pressure (ICP)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项发现是颅内压 (ICP) 升高的最敏感早期指标？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with a head injury.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名头部受伤的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Decerebrate posturing","zh":"去大脑强直姿势"},{"id":"A","en":"Change in level of consciousness (LOC)","zh":"意识状态 (LOC) 的改变"},{"id":"D","en":"Cushing's triad","zh":"库欣三联征 (Cushing's triad)"},{"id":"B","en":"Fixed and dilated pupils","zh":"瞳孔固定且散大"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A change in LOC is the earliest and most sensitive sign of increased ICP. Other signs like Cushing's triad (widening pulse pressure, bradycardia, irregular respirations) and fixed/dilated pupils are late signs indicating impending herniation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"意识状态 (LOC) 的改变是颅内压升高最早且最敏感的体征。其他体征如库欣三联征（脉压增宽、心动过缓、呼吸不规则）和瞳孔固定/散大是提示即将发生脑疝的晚期体征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for keywords like 'earliest' or 'most sensitive'. In neuro assessments, LOC is almost always the answer for the earliest indicator.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找“最早”或“最敏感”等关键词。在神经系统评估中，意识状态几乎总是最早指标的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":668,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.477","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.477.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.477.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is providing discharge instructions to a client newly prescribed warfarin. Which statements by the client indicate a need for further teaching? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名新开具华法林医嘱的患者提供出院指导。患者的哪些陈述表明需要进一步教学？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements by the client indicate a need for further teaching?","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的哪些陈述表明需要进一步教学？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"I should take aspirin if I have a headache.","zh":"如果我头痛，我应该服用阿司匹林。"},{"id":"A","en":"I will increase my intake of spinach and kale to stay healthy.","zh":"我会增加菠菜和羽衣甘蓝的摄入量以保持健康。"},{"id":"B","en":"I will use a soft-bristled toothbrush.","zh":"我会使用软毛牙刷。"},{"id":"E","en":"I will notify my doctor if my stools appear black or tarry.","zh":"如果我的大便呈黑色或柏油样，我会通知我的医生。"},{"id":"D","en":"I will need frequent blood tests to check my INR.","zh":"我需要经常抽血检查我的 INR。"}],"correct":["A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warfarin users must maintain consistent intake of Vitamin K (found in leafy greens like spinach) rather than increasing it, as Vitamin K is the antidote. Aspirin increases bleeding risk and should be avoided. Options B, D, and E are correct safety measures for warfarin therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林使用者必须保持维生素 K（存在于菠菜等绿叶蔬菜中）的摄入量一致，而不是增加，因为维生素 K 是解毒剂。阿司匹林会增加出血风险，应避免使用。使用软毛牙刷、定期监测 INR 以及出现黑便时通知医生是华法林治疗的正确安全措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the 'false' statements since the question asks for 'need for further teaching'. Connect Warfarin with Vitamin K consistency and Bleeding Precautions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别“错误”的陈述，因为题目要求“需要进一步教学”。将华法林与维生素 K 的一致性和出血预防措施联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":669,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.478","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.478.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.478.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,106],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,56],"fullStemEn":"A client's potassium level is 6.8 mEq/L (6.8 mmol/L). Which ECG change should the nurse expect to observe?","fullStemZh":"一名患者的钾水平为 6.8 mEq/L (6.8 mmol/L)。护士应预期观察到哪种心电图 (ECG) 变化？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which ECG change should the nurse expect to observe?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期观察到哪种心电图 (ECG) 变化？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client's potassium level is 6.8 mEq/L (6.8 mmol/L).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者的钾水平为 6.8 mEq/L (6.8 mmol/L)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Shortened PR interval","zh":"PR 间期缩短"},{"id":"D","en":"Tall, peaked T waves","zh":"高尖 T 波"},{"id":"A","en":"Prominent U waves","zh":"明显的 U 波"},{"id":"B","en":"ST-segment depression","zh":"ST 段压低"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hyperkalemia causes tall, peaked T waves, widened QRS complexes, and eventually loss of P waves. Prominent U waves and ST depression are associated with hypokalemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高钾血症导致高尖 T 波、QRS 波群增宽，并最终导致 P 波消失。明显的 U 波和 ST 段压低与低钾血症有关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'High Potassium' with 'High/Peaked' waves (T waves).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“高钾”与“高/尖”波（T 波）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":670,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.479","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.479.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.479.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,32],"fullStemEn":"A client is instructed to use sublingual nitroglycerin for chest pain. Which instruction should the nurse include?","fullStemZh":"一名患者被指示使用舌下含服硝酸甘油治疗胸痛。护士应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is instructed to use sublingual nitroglycerin for chest pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者被指示使用舌下含服硝酸甘油治疗胸痛。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Take one tablet every 15 minutes until pain subsides.","zh":"每 15 分钟服用一片，直到疼痛缓解。"},{"id":"B","en":"If pain persists after the first dose, call 911 immediately.","zh":"如果第一剂后疼痛持续，立即拨打 911。"},{"id":"A","en":"Store the medication in a clear plastic container for easy viewing.","zh":"将药物存放在透明塑料容器中以便查看。"},{"id":"C","en":"Swallow the tablet with a full glass of water.","zh":"用一整杯水吞服药片。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The current standard is to take one dose for chest pain. If pain is not relieved or worsens after 5 minutes, the client should call emergency services (911) before taking further doses. Nitroglycerin should not be swallowed and must be kept in its original dark glass container to prevent light-induced breakdown.","rationaleCorrectZh":"目前的标准是胸痛时服用一剂。如果 5 分钟后疼痛未缓解或加重，患者应在服用后续剂量前拨打急救电话 (911)。硝酸甘油不应吞服，且必须保存在原始的深色玻璃容器中，以防止光引起分解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Priority is safety. If the first dose of a potent vasodilator doesn't work for cardiac pain, it's an emergency.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先考虑安全性。如果第一剂强效血管扩张剂对心源性疼痛无效，那就是紧急情况。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":671,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.480","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.480.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.480.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,37],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing a client after a thyroidectomy. Which findings would indicate hypocalcemia? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对甲状腺切除术后的患者进行评估。哪些表现提示低钙血症？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings would indicate hypocalcemia?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些表现提示低钙血症？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Positive Chvostek's sign","zh":"Chvostek 征阳性"},{"id":"C","en":"Tingling around the mouth (circumoral paresthesia)","zh":"口周麻木感（口周感觉异常）"},{"id":"D","en":"Positive Trousseau's sign","zh":"Trousseau 征阳性"},{"id":"B","en":"Muscle flaccidity","zh":"肌肉松弛"},{"id":"E","en":"Constipation","zh":"便秘"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypocalcemia causes increased neuromuscular excitability. Signs include Chvostek's sign (facial twitch), Trousseau's sign (carpal spasm with BP cuff), and paresthesia. Muscle flaccidity and constipation are signs of hypercalcemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低钙血症导致神经肌肉兴奋性增高。体征包括 Chvostek 征（面部抽搐）、Trousseau 征（血压计袖带引起的腕痉挛）和感觉异常。肌肉松弛和便秘是高钙血症的体征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'Low Calcium' with 'High Excitability' (Twitches/Spasms).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“低钙”与“高兴奋性”（抽搐/痉挛）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":672,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.481","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.481.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.481.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,42],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving a continuous intravenous infusion of heparin for deep vein thrombosis. Which laboratory value should the nurse monitor to evaluate the effectiveness of the therapy?","fullStemZh":"一名深静脉血栓患者正接受持续静脉输注肝素。护士应监测哪项实验室检查值以评估治疗效果？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory value should the nurse monitor to evaluate the effectiveness of the therapy?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应监测哪项实验室检查值以评估治疗效果？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving a continuous intravenous infusion of heparin for deep vein thrombosis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名深静脉血栓患者正接受持续静脉输注肝素。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT)","zh":"活化部分凝血活酶时间 (aPTT)"},{"id":"C","en":"International Normalized Ratio (INR)","zh":"国际标准化比值 (INR)"},{"id":"D","en":"Platelet count","zh":"血小板计数"},{"id":"B","en":"Prothrombin time (PT)","zh":"凝血酶原时间 (PT)"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"aPTT is used to monitor heparin therapy. PT and INR are used to monitor warfarin. While platelet count is monitored for heparin-induced thrombocytopenia (HIT), it does not measure the effectiveness of the anticoagulation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"aPTT 用于监测肝素治疗。PT 和 INR用于监测华法林。虽然监测血小板计数是为了预防肝素诱导的血小板减少症 (HIT)，但它并不衡量抗凝 治疗的效果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"He-PTT (Heparin = aPTT). Use the letters to remember: Heparin has 7 letters, aPTT has 4. Warfarin has 8, PT has 2. (Or just remember the pairing).","testTakingStrategyZh":"He-PTT (肝素 = aPTT)。使用字母来记忆：Heparin 有 7 个字母，aPTT 有 4 个。Warfarin 有 8 个，PT 有 2 个。（或者直接记住配对）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":673,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.482","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.482.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.482.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,106],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Which clinical finding in a client with a chest injury most specifically indicates a tension pneumothorax?","fullStemZh":"胸部损伤患者的哪项临床发现最特异地提示张力性气胸？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which clinical finding in a client with a chest injury most specifically indicates a tension pneumothorax?","terminalSentenceZh":"胸部损伤患者的哪项临床发现最特异地提示张力性气胸？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Absence of breath sounds on the affected side","zh":"患侧呼吸音消失"},{"id":"D","en":"Tachypnea and tachycardia","zh":"呼吸过快和心动过快"},{"id":"B","en":"Tracheal deviation toward the unaffected side","zh":"气管向健侧偏移"},{"id":"C","en":"Severe chest pain","zh":"剧烈胸痛"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tracheal deviation is a hallmark late sign of tension pneumothorax, caused by massive pressure shifting the mediastinum toward the opposite (unaffected) side. Absence of breath sounds (this option) occurs in all pneumothoraces, not just tension.","rationaleCorrectZh":"气管偏移是张力性气胸的标志性晚期体征，由巨大的压力将纵隔推向对侧（健侧）引起。呼吸音消失（该选项）发生在所有气胸中，而不不仅仅是张力性气胸。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the sign that differentiates 'standard' pneumothorax from 'tension' pneumothorax. Tracheal shift is the key differentiator.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找区分“标准”气胸和“张力性”气胸的体征。气管偏移是关键区别点。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":674,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.483","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.483.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.483.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,39],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client who is starting phenytoin for a seizure disorder. Which instructions should be included? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名开始服用苯妥英治疗癫痫发作的患者。应包括哪些指导？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"应包括哪些指导？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Expect the urine to turn dark orange.","zh":"预见尿液会变成深橙色。"},{"id":"E","en":"Increase intake of dairy products to prevent osteoporosis.","zh":"增加乳制品摄入量以预防骨质疏松症。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use a backup method of contraception if taking oral contraceptives.","zh":"如果服用口服避孕药，请使用备用避孕方法。"},{"id":"C","en":"Do not stop taking the medication abruptly.","zh":"不要突然停止服药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform meticulous oral hygiene and see a dentist regularly.","zh":"进行细致的口腔卫生并定期看牙医。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Phenytoin can cause gingival hyperplasia (requires oral care), status epilepticus if stopped abruptly, and it decreases the effectiveness of oral contraceptives. It may turn urine pink/red/brown (not dark orange like Rifampin or Phenazopyridine). Long-term use can affect bone health, but increasing dairy is not a specific standard teaching for phenytoin initiation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"苯妥英可引起牙龈增生（需要口腔护理），如果突然停药可引起癫痫持续状态，且会降低口服避孕药的效果。它可能使尿液变成粉红色/红色/棕色（不像利福平或苯佐吡啶那样呈深橙色）。长期使用可能会影响骨骼健康，但增加乳制品摄入并不是开始使用苯妥英的特定标准教学。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember 'GUNS' for Phenytoin: Gingival hyperplasia, Use of backup birth control, No sudden stop, Serum levels monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住苯妥英的“GUNS”：牙龈增生 (Gingival hyperplasia)、使用备用避孕措施 (Use of backup birth control)、不能突然停药 (No sudden stop)、血清水平监测 (Serum levels monitoring)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":675,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.484","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.484.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.484.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,47],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client in diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA). Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名处于糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 的患者。护士应预见哪些临床表现？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"High serum bicarbonate level","zh":"血清碳酸氢盐水平升高"},{"id":"A","en":"Kussmaul's respirations","zh":"Kussmaul 呼吸（深大呼吸）"},{"id":"B","en":"Fruity breath odor","zh":"烂苹果味（果味）呼气"},{"id":"C","en":"Abdominal pain","zh":"腹痛"},{"id":"D","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"DKA manifestations include Kussmaul respirations (to blow off CO2), fruity breath (from ketones), abdominal pain (common in DKA, not HHS), and tachycardia (from dehydration). Serum bicarbonate will be low (metabolic acidosis), not high.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DKA 的表现包括 Kussmaul 呼吸（排出二氧化碳）、果味呼气（来自酮体）、腹痛（常见于 DKA，而非 HHS）和心动过快（源于脱水）。血清碳酸氢盐会降低（代谢性酸中毒），而不是升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember 'DKA': Dehydration, Ketones/Kussmaul/K+ (imbalance), Acidosis/Abdominal pain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“DKA”：脱水 (Dehydration)、酮体 (Ketones)/Kussmaul 呼吸/钾 (K+) 平衡紊乱、酸中毒 (Acidosis)/腹痛 (Abdominal pain)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":676,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.485","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.485.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.485.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,38],"fullStemEn":"A client is prescribed lithium carbonate for bipolar disorder. Which information should the nurse prioritize in the teaching plan?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因双相情感障碍被开具碳酸锂医嘱。护士应在教学计划中优先考虑哪项信息？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which information should the nurse prioritize in the teaching plan?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应在教学计划中优先考虑哪项信息？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is prescribed lithium carbonate for bipolar disorder.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因双相情感障碍被开具碳酸锂医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Avoid all exercise to prevent sweating.","zh":"避免所有运动以防止出汗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Take the medication only when feeling manic.","zh":"仅在感到躁狂时服药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Limit fluid intake to 1 liter per day.","zh":"将液体摄入量限制在每天 1 升。"},{"id":"D","en":"Maintain a consistent sodium intake.","zh":"保持一致的钠摄入量。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lithium is a salt; low sodium levels cause the kidneys to retain lithium, leading to toxicity. Clients must maintain consistent sodium and fluid intake (2-3 L/day). Medication is taken daily, not as needed. Exercise is allowed, but fluids must be replaced if sweating occurs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锂是一种盐；低钠水平会导致肾脏滞留锂，从而引起中毒。患者必须保持一致的钠和液体摄入量（每天 2-3 升）。药物应每天服用，而不是根据需要服用。允许运动，但如果出汗，必须补充液体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Lithium and Sodium are inversely related in the kidneys. Low Na = High Lithium (Toxicity).","testTakingStrategyZh":"锂和钠在肾脏中呈负相关。低钠 = 高锂（中毒）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":677,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.486","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.486.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.486.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,69],"fullStemEn":"A client with a T4 spinal cord injury reports a sudden, throbbing headache. The nurse notes a BP of 190/100 mmHg and flushing of the face and neck. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名 T4 脊髓损伤患者报告突然出现跳痛性头痛。护士发现血压为 190/100 mmHg，面部和颈部潮红。护士应采取哪些行动？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些行动？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Place the client in a supine position with legs elevated.","zh":"将患者置于仰卧位并抬高双腿。"},{"id":"A","en":"Raise the head of the bed to a high-Fowler's position.","zh":"将床头抬高至高 Fowler 位。"},{"id":"C","en":"Check the client for fecal impaction.","zh":"检查患者是否有粪便嵌塞。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer an antihypertensive if ordered.","zh":"如果有医嘱，给予降压药。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess for bladder distention.","zh":"检查膀胱是否充盈。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"These signs indicate autonomic dysreflexia (emergency). The first action is to sit the client up to lower BP. Then, find the cause (usually distended bladder or bowel impaction). Meds may be needed if the cause isn't immediately fixed. Placing the client supine (Option E) would further increase intracranial pressure and BP.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这些体征提示自主神经反射异常（紧急情况）。第一项行动是让患者坐起以降低血压。然后，寻找原因（通常是膀胱充盈或粪便嵌塞）。如果原因不能立即解决，可能需要药物治疗。将患者置于仰卧位（选项 E）会进一步升高颅内压和血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For AD, 'Sit them up, then search (for the trigger)'. Always start with position change for hypertensive crisis in spinal cord injury.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于自主神经反射异常，“先坐起，后寻找（触发因素）”。对于脊髓损伤中的高血压危象，始终从改变体位开始。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":678,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.487","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.487.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.487.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,124],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,39],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving IV vancomycin develops flushing and a red rash on the face and neck. What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"一名接受静脉注射万古霉素的患者面部和颈部出现潮红和红疹。护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receiving IV vancomycin develops flushing and a red rash on the face and neck.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名接受静脉注射万古霉素的患者面部和颈部出现潮红和红疹。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Slow the rate of the infusion.","zh":"减慢输注速度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer subcutaneous epinephrine.","zh":"皮下注射肾上腺素。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply cool compresses to the affected areas.","zh":"对受影响区域进行冷敷。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop the infusion immediately and notify the healthcare provider of an allergic reaction.","zh":"立即停止输注并通知医疗保健提供者发生了过敏反应。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The description fits 'Red Man Syndrome' (or vancomycin flushing syndrome), which is a rate-related infusion reaction, not a true allergy. The appropriate action is to slow the infusion to at least over 60 minutes. If symptoms were anaphylactic (wheezing, hives, hypotension), the infusion would be stopped.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该描述符合“红人综合征”（或万古霉素潮红综合征），这是一种与速度相关的输注反应，而不是真正的过敏。适当的行动是将输注速度减慢至至少 60 分钟以上。如果症状是过敏性的（喘鸣、荨麻疹、低血压），则应停止输注。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between an infusion reaction (Red Man) and an allergic reaction. Red Man = Slow down. Allergy = Stop.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分输注反应（红人）和过敏反应。红人 = 减速。过敏 = 停止。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client receiving IV vancomycin develops flushing and a red rash on the face and neck.","controlSentenceZh":"一名接受静脉注射万古霉素的患者面部和颈部出现潮红和红疹。"}
{"queueIndex":679,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.488","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.488.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.488.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,37],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client with a fractured femur. Which findings are consistent with fat embolism syndrome? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名股骨骨折的患者。哪些表现与脂肪栓塞综合征一致？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings are consistent with fat embolism syndrome?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些表现与脂肪栓塞综合征一致？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"B","en":"Petechiae on the chest and neck","zh":"胸部和颈部出现瘀点"},{"id":"E","en":"Hypoxemia","zh":"低氧血症"},{"id":"A","en":"Restlessness and confusion","zh":"烦躁和意识模糊"},{"id":"C","en":"Sudden dyspnea","zh":"突然呼吸困难"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fat embolism syndrome (FES) typically presents within 24-48 hours of a long bone fracture. Classic triad: Respiratory distress (dyspnea, hypoxemia), Neurological changes (restlessness, confusion), and Petechial rash (on chest, neck, axilla). Tachycardia is expected, not bradycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脂肪栓塞综合征 (FES) 通常发生在长骨骨折后的 24-48 小时内。经典三联征：呼吸窘迫（呼吸困难、低氧血症）、神经系统改变（烦躁、意识模糊）和瘀点疹（胸部、颈部、腋下）。预期会出现心动过快，而不是心动过缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate long bone fractures with FES. The petechial rash is the unique 'classic' sign that helps differentiate it from a simple pulmonary embolism.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将长骨骨折与 FES 联系起来。瘀点疹是独特的“经典”体征，有助于将其与单纯的肺栓塞区分开来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":680,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.489","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.489.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.489.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,128],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,36],"fullStemEn":"A client is prescribed furosemide for pulmonary edema. Which laboratory results should the nurse monitor? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因肺水肿被开具呋塞米医嘱。护士应监测哪些实验室结果？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which laboratory results should the nurse monitor?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应监测哪些实验室结果？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Blood Urea Nitrogen (BUN) and Creatinine","zh":"血尿素氮 (BUN) 和肌酐"},{"id":"A","en":"Potassium","zh":"钾"},{"id":"E","en":"White blood cell count","zh":"白细胞计数"},{"id":"D","en":"Magnesium","zh":"镁"},{"id":"B","en":"Sodium","zh":"钠"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Furosemide is a loop diuretic that causes excretion of potassium, sodium, and magnesium. It can also cause dehydration, leading to elevated BUN and creatinine (pre-renal azotemia). It does not significantly affect WBC count.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呋塞米是一种袢利尿剂，会导致钾、钠和镁的排出。它还可能导致脱水，从而引起 BUN 和肌酐升高（肾前性氮质血症）。它不会明显影响白细胞计数。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Loop diuretics waste 'everything' (electrolytes) and can stress the kidneys through dehydration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"袢利尿剂会排出“所有物质”（电解质），并可能通过脱水给肾脏带来压力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":681,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.490","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.490.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.490.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"Which assessment finding is a priority for the nurse to report in a client suspected of having thyroid storm?","fullStemZh":"对于疑似发生甲状腺危象的患者，护士应优先报告哪项评估结果？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding is a priority for the nurse to report in a client suspected of having thyroid storm?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于疑似发生甲状腺危象的患者，护士应优先报告哪项评估结果？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Constipation","zh":"便秘"},{"id":"A","en":"Temperature of 104.5 °F (40.3 °C)","zh":"体温 104.5 °F (40.3 °C)"},{"id":"B","en":"Heart rate of 95 beats/min","zh":"心率 95 次/分"},{"id":"C","en":"Dry, scaly skin","zh":"皮肤干燥、脱屑"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thyroid storm is a life-threatening form of hyperthyroidism. Key signs include extreme fever (hyperpyrexia), severe tachycardia, and altered mental status. Dry skin and constipation (Options C and D) are signs of hypothyroidism.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺危象是甲状腺功能亢进的一种危及生命的形式。关键体征包括极高热（高热）、严重的心动过快和精神状态改变。皮肤干燥和便秘（该选项 和 D）是甲状腺功能减退的体征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Thyroid Storm = Everything is 'Fast and Hot'. Fever is the most critical/alarming sign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"甲状腺危象 = 所有一切都是“快且热”。发热是最关键/令人警觉的体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":682,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.491","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.491.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.491.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,46],"fullStemEn":"A client is suspected of having Myasthenia Gravis. The nurse expects which result after the administration of edrophonium (Tensilon)?","fullStemZh":"一名患者疑似患有重症肌无力。护士预期在给予依酚氯铵 (Tensilon) 后会出现哪种结果？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse expects which result after the administration of edrophonium (Tensilon)?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预期在给予依酚氯铵 (Tensilon) 后会出现哪种结果？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is suspected of having Myasthenia Gravis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者疑似患有重症肌无力。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Increased muscle weakness and fasciculations.","zh":"肌肉无力加重和肌束颤动。"},{"id":"C","en":"Decreased heart rate and hypotension.","zh":"心率减慢和低血压。"},{"id":"B","en":"Immediate increase in muscle strength.","zh":"肌肉力量立即增加。"},{"id":"D","en":"Improved pupil reaction to light.","zh":"瞳孔对光反应改善。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Edrophonium is a short-acting acetylcholinesterase inhibitor. In Myasthenia Gravis, it leads to a temporary, dramatic improvement in muscle strength. This confirms the diagnosis. Increased weakness (this option) suggests a cholinergic crisis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"依酚氯铵是一种短效乙酰胆碱酯酶抑制剂。在重症肌无力中，它会导致肌肉力量暂时、显著的改善。这可以确认诊断。无力加重（该选项）提示胆碱能危象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Tensilon test = 'T' for 'Temporary' and 'T' for 'Tough/Strong' muscles.","testTakingStrategyZh":"Tensilon 试验 = “T” 代表“暂时 (Temporary)”，“T” 代表“强壮 (Tough/Strong)”肌肉。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":683,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.492","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.492.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.492.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,39],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring a client who has been taking prednisone for several months. Which potential side effects should the nurse assess for? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名已服用泼尼松数月的患者。护士应评估哪些潜在副作用？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which potential side effects should the nurse assess for?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应评估哪些潜在副作用？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Fluid volume deficit","zh":"体液量不足"},{"id":"B","en":"Hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"},{"id":"A","en":"Hypoglycemia","zh":"低血糖"},{"id":"C","en":"Osteoporosis","zh":"骨质疏松症"},{"id":"D","en":"Increased risk for infection","zh":"感染风险增加"}],"correct":["B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Long-term steroid use causes hyper-glycemia (not hypo), hypokalemia, osteoporosis, fluid retention (not deficit), and immunosuppression (increased infection risk).","rationaleCorrectZh":"长期使用类固醇会导致高血糖（而非低血糖）、低钾血症、骨质疏松症、体液潴留（而非不足）和免疫抑制（感染风险增加）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Glucocorticoids make everything 'High' (Glucose, BP/Fluid) except for 'Low' (Immunity, Potassium, Calcium/Bone).","testTakingStrategyZh":"糖皮质激素使所有一切都变“高”（血糖、血压/体液），除了“低”（免疫力、钾、钙/骨骼）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":684,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.493","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.493.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.493.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,31],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with a pericardial effusion. Which assessment finding indicates the development of cardiac tamponade?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名心包积液患者。哪项评估结果提示发生了心包填塞？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding indicates the development of cardiac tamponade?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项评估结果提示发生了心包填塞？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with a pericardial effusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名心包积液患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Stridor and tracheal deviation","zh":"喘鸣和气管偏移"},{"id":"A","en":"Muffled heart sounds and jugular venous distention (JVD)","zh":"心音遥远（低沉）和颈静脉怒张 (JVD)"},{"id":"C","en":"Bradycardia and hypertension","zh":"心动过缓和高血压"},{"id":"D","en":"Flattened neck veins when supine","zh":"仰卧时颈静脉扁平"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Beck's triad for cardiac tamponade: Hypotension, JVD, and Muffled heart sounds. These occur because the fluid in the pericardial sac compresses the heart, preventing it from filling and contracting effectively.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心包填塞的贝克三联征 (Beck's triad)：低血压、颈静脉怒张 (JVD) 和心音遥远。这些发生是因为心包腔内的液体压迫心脏，阻止其有效地充盈和收缩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember Beck's Triad: Big neck veins (JVD), Extremely low BP, Can't hear heart sounds (Muffled).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 Beck 三联征：粗大的颈静脉 (JVD)、极低的血压、听不到心音（遥远）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":685,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_22","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.494","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.494.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.494.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client about lisinopril. Which adverse effects should the nurse instruct the client to report? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教导患者有关赖诺普利的信息。护士应指示患者报告哪些不良反应？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which adverse effects should the nurse instruct the client to report?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应指示患者报告哪些不良反应？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"},{"id":"D","en":"Dizziness upon standing","zh":"站立时头晕"},{"id":"E","en":"Weight gain of 5 lbs in 2 days","zh":"2天内体重增加 5 磅"},{"id":"B","en":"Swelling of the lips and tongue","zh":"嘴唇和舌头肿胀"},{"id":"A","en":"Persistent dry cough","zh":"持续性干咳"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ACE inhibitors are known for causing a dry cough and angioedema (swelling of lips/tongue), which is an emergency. They also cause orthostatic hypotension (dizziness). They cause hyperkalemia, not hypokalemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ACE 抑制剂以引起干咳和血管性水肿（嘴唇/舌头肿胀）而闻名，后者是紧急情况。它们还会引起体位性低血压（头晕）。它们会引起高钾血症，而不是低钾血症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"ACE Inhibitors: A (Angioedema), C (Cough), E (Elevated K+).","testTakingStrategyZh":"ACE 抑制剂：A（血管性水肿 Angioedema），C（咳嗽 Cough），E（钾升高 Elevated K+）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":686,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.495","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.495.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.495.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,44],"fullStemEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) is being taught about a renal diet. Which food choice indicates that the client understands the teaching?","fullStemZh":"一名慢性肾病 (CKD) 患者正在接受肾病饮食教育。哪种食物选择表明患者理解了教学内容？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which food choice indicates that the client understands the teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种食物选择表明患者理解了教学内容？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) is being taught about a renal diet.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名慢性肾病 (CKD) 患者正在接受肾病饮食教育。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Banana and orange juice","zh":"香蕉和橙汁"},{"id":"B","en":"Canned soup and ham sandwich","zh":"罐装汤和火腿三明治"},{"id":"C","en":"Spinach salad with nuts","zh":"带坚果的菠菜沙拉"},{"id":"A","en":"Baked chicken and white rice","zh":"烤鸡肉和白米饭"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Renal diets typically restrict potassium (found in bananas, oranges, spinach, nuts), phosphorus (found in nuts, dairy), and sodium (found in canned soups, ham). Baked chicken and white rice are relatively low in these components compared to the other options.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肾病饮食通常限制钾（存在于香蕉、橙子、菠菜、坚果中）、磷（存在于坚果、乳制品中）和钠（存在于罐装汤、火腿中）。与其他选项相比，烤鸡肉和白米饭中这些成分的含量相对较低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Eliminate options high in K+ (fruits/veggies), Na+ (processed meats/cans), and Phosphorus.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除高钾（水果/蔬菜）、高钠（加工肉类/罐头）和高磷的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) is being taught about a renal diet.","controlSentenceZh":"一名慢性肾病 (CKD) 患者正在接受肾病饮食教育。"}
{"queueIndex":687,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_ppt_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.496","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.496.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.496.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[146,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,43],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer intravenous potassium chloride to a client with hypokalemia. Which safety precautions must the nurse follow? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备给一名低钾血症患者静脉输注氯化钾。护士必须遵循哪些安全预防措施？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which safety precautions must the nurse follow?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士必须遵循哪些安全预防措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the dose via IV push over 2 minutes.","zh":"通过静脉推注在 2 分钟内给药。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use an infusion pump for administration.","zh":"使用输液泵给药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess for adequate urinary output before starting the infusion.","zh":"开始输注前评估是否有足够的尿量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ensure the infusion rate does not exceed 10 mEq/hr.","zh":"确保输注速度不超过 10 mEq/小时。"},{"id":"E","en":"Dilute the potassium in at least 1000 mL of fluid.","zh":"将钾稀释在至少 1000 毫升的液体中。"}],"correct":["B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium is NEVER given IV push (it can cause cardiac arrest). The maximum safe rate for a peripheral line is 10 mEq/hr. Adequate kidney function (urine output) must be confirmed first because K+ is excreted by the kidneys. An infusion pump is mandatory for safety. Dilution volume depends on the dose, but 1000 mL is not a fixed requirement for all doses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"钾绝对不能静脉推注（会导致心脏骤停）。外周静脉的最大安全速度为 10 mEq/小时。必须首先确认足够的肾功能（尿量），因为钾由肾脏排出。为了安全，强制使用输液泵。稀释体积取决于剂量，但 1000 毫升并不是所有剂量的固定要求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the 'K+ Kills' rule: Never push. Must have pee (urine). Always use a pump.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“钾会杀人”规则：绝不推注。必须有尿。始终使用泵。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":688,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_pa_25","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.497","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.497.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.497.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with a cast on the lower leg. Which findings suggest compartment syndrome? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名下肢打石膏的患者。哪些发现提示骨筋膜室综合征？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings suggest compartment syndrome?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现提示骨筋膜室综合征？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Pain that is unrelieved by opioids","zh":"阿片类药物无法缓解的疼痛"},{"id":"D","en":"Warm, pink skin distal to the cast","zh":"石膏远端皮肤温暖、粉红"},{"id":"B","en":"Pain with passive extension of the toes","zh":"被动伸展脚趾时疼痛"},{"id":"C","en":"Paresthesia in the affected limb","zh":"患肢感觉异常"},{"id":"E","en":"Bounding pedal pulses","zh":"足背动脉搏动有力"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The '6 Ps' of compartment syndrome: Pain (unrelieved and passive), Paresthesia (early sign), Pallor, Paralysis, Pulselessness (late sign), and Pressure. Warm/pink skin and bounding pulses (Options D and E) would be normal/reassuring findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"骨筋膜室综合征的“6 P”：疼痛 (Pain，无法缓解且被动时加重)、感觉异常 (Paresthesia，早期体征)、苍白 (Pallor)、瘫痪 (Paralysis)、脉搏消失 (Pulselessness，晚期体征) 和压力 (Pressure)。皮肤温暖/粉红和搏动有力是正常/令人放心的发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on 'Unusual Pain' (not matching the injury or not responding to meds) as the most critical early sign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注“异常疼痛”（与伤情不符或对药物无反应）作为最关键的早期体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":689,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.498","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.498.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.498.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,41],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning the client assignments for the shift. Which task is most appropriate to delegate to an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","fullStemZh":"护士正在计划该班次的患者任务分配。哪项任务最适合委派给非执业辅助人员 (UAP)？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which task is most appropriate to delegate to an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项任务最适合委派给非执业辅助人员 (UAP)？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning the client assignments for the shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在计划该班次的患者任务分配。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Providing discharge instructions to a client with a new prescription.","zh":"向新开处方的患者提供出院指导。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assessing a client's surgical incision for signs of infection.","zh":"评估患者手术切口是否有感染迹象。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assisting a stable client with a bed bath and oral care.","zh":"协助病情稳定的患者进行床上沐浴和口腔护理。"},{"id":"B","en":"Feeding a client with dysphagia for the first time after a stroke.","zh":"为中风后第一次出现吞咽困难的患者喂食。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"UAPs can perform routine tasks for stable clients, such as hygiene, feeding (if no aspiration risk), and simple vital signs. Tasks involving assessment (this option), teaching (this option), or high-risk feeding (this option) require the judgment and skill of a licensed nurse.","rationaleCorrectZh":"UAP 可以为稳定的患者执行常规任务，如卫生、喂食（如果没有误吸风险）和简单的生命体征测量。涉及评估（该选项）、教学（该选项）或高风险喂食（该选项）的任务需要执业护士的判断和技能。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the acronym EAT (Evaluate, Assess, Teach) to remember tasks that cannot be delegated to UAPs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用首字母缩略词 EAT（评估 Evaluate、评估 Assess、教学 Teach）来记住不能委派给 UAP 的任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":690,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.499","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.499.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.499.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,51],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is supervising a licensed practical nurse (LPN). Which tasks are within the scope of practice for the LPN? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正负责监督一名执业护士 (LPN)。哪些任务属于 LPN 的实践范围？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which tasks are within the scope of practice for the LPN?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些任务属于 LPN 的实践范围？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Initiating the initial head-to-toe assessment on a new admission.","zh":"对新入院患者进行初始的全身评估。"},{"id":"D","en":"Suctioning a client's established tracheostomy.","zh":"为患者已建立的气管切开处进行吸痰。"},{"id":"B","en":"Performing a sterile dressing change on a pressure injury.","zh":"对压力性损伤进行无菌换药。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administering an intravenous (IV) push medication for pain.","zh":"通过静脉推注 (IV push) 给予止痛药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administering an oral antibiotic to a stable client.","zh":"为稳定的患者提供口服抗生素。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs can care for stable clients with predictable outcomes. They can administer oral and most parenteral medications (except IV push in most jurisdictions), perform sterile procedures, and suction established tracheostomies. Initial assessments and high-acuity tasks like IV push meds are typically reserved for RNs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN 可以护理结果可预测的稳定患者。他们可以提供口服和大多数非经肠道药物（在大多数辖区内除静脉推注外），执行无菌操作，并为已建立的气管切开处吸痰。初始评估和静脉推注药物等高敏锐度任务通常由 RN 负责。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of LPNs as 'Stable, Predictable, Technical'. Avoid tasks involving 'Initial', 'Complex', or 'Unstable'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将 LPN 想象为“稳定、可预测、技术性”。避免涉及“初始”、“复杂”或“不稳定”的任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":691,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.500","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.500.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.500.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,27],"fullStemEn":"The nurse has received the change-of-shift report on four clients. Which client should the nurse assess first?","fullStemZh":"护士接到了四名患者的换班报告。护士应首先评估哪位患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the nurse assess first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先评估哪位患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse has received the change-of-shift report on four clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士接到了四名患者的换班报告。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"A client with diabetes mellitus whose morning blood glucose was 150 mg/dL (8.3 mmol/L).","zh":"一名糖尿病患者，晨间血糖为 150 mg/dL (8.3 mmol/L)。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client who had a cholecystectomy 4 hours ago and reports pain as 6 out of 10.","zh":"一名 4 小时前接受了胆囊切除术且报告疼痛为 6 分（总分 10 分）的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with a deep vein thrombosis (DVT) who reports sudden shortness of breath and chest pain.","zh":"一名患有深静脉血栓 (DVT) 且报告突然呼吸困难和胸痛的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) with an oxygen saturation of 90%.","zh":"一名血氧饱和度为 90% 的慢性阻塞性肺疾病 (COPD) 患者。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden shortness of breath and chest pain in a client with DVT are classic signs of a pulmonary embolism (PE), which is a life-threatening emergency (Breathing/Circulation). The other clients are relatively stable or have expected findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DVT 患者突然出现呼吸困难和胸痛是肺栓塞 (PE) 的典型体征，这是一种危及生命的紧急情况（呼吸/循环）。其他患者相对稳定或表现出预期的发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) to prioritize. Sudden changes in respiratory or circulatory status are always the highest priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）原则进行优先级排序。呼吸或循环状态的突然变化始终是最高优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse has received the change-of-shift report on four clients.","controlSentenceZh":"护士接到了四名患者的换班报告。"}
{"queueIndex":692,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.501","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.501.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.501.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is witnessing a client sign an informed consent form for a surgical procedure. What is the nurse's primary responsibility in this process?","fullStemZh":"护士正在见证患者签署手术知情同意书。在此过程中，护士的首要责任是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's primary responsibility in this process?","terminalSentenceZh":"在此过程中，护士的首要责任是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is witnessing a client sign an informed consent form for a surgical procedure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在见证患者签署手术知情同意书。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Describing alternative treatments to the client.","zh":"向患者描述替代疗法。"},{"id":"B","en":"Explaining the risks and benefits of the surgery to the client.","zh":"向患者解释手术的风险和益处。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensuring the healthcare provider has answered all the client's questions.","zh":"确保医疗保健提供者已回答了患者的所有问题。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verifying that the client is signing the form voluntarily and is competent.","zh":"验证患者是否自愿签署表格且具备签署能力。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse's role in informed consent is to witness the signature, ensuring the client is competent, signs voluntarily, and understands that they are signing a consent form. Explaining risks, benefits, and alternatives is the provider's responsibility.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在知情同意中的角色是见证签名，确保患者具备能力、自愿签名，并明白他们正在签署同意书。解释风险、益处和替代方案是提供者的 责任。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between the roles of the nurse (witness) and the provider (educator/provider of information).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分护士（见证人）和提供者（教育者/信息提供者）的角色。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":693,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.502","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.502.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.502.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,36],"fullStemEn":"A client asks the nurse about a durable power of attorney for healthcare. Which statement by the nurse is accurate?","fullStemZh":"一名患者向护士询问有关医疗保健持久授权书的信息。护士的哪项陈述是准确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the nurse is accurate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项陈述是准确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client asks the nurse about a durable power of attorney for healthcare.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者向护士询问有关医疗保健持久授权书的信息。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"\"Once signed, you cannot change the person you have designated.\"","zh":"“一旦签署，你就不能更改你指定的人。”"},{"id":"D","en":"\"It is a document that specifies which medical treatments you want if you are terminal.\"","zh":"“这是一份规定如果你处于末期，你想要哪些医疗待遇的文件。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"It designates a specific person to make medical decisions for you if you become incapacitated.\"","zh":"“它指定了一个特定的人，在你丧失行为能力时为你做出医疗决定。”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"It only applies if you are in a persistent vegetative state.\"","zh":"“它仅在你处于持续植物人状态时适用。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A durable power of attorney for healthcare (health care proxy) appoints a person to make decisions when the client cannot. A living will specifies treatments for end-of-life care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"医疗保健持久授权书（医疗代理人）指定一个人在患者无法做出决定时代为决定。生前遗嘱规定了临终关怀的治疗方案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'Power of Attorney' with a 'Person' (proxy/surrogate). Associate 'Living Will' with 'Wishes' (treatments).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“授权书”与“人”（代理人/替代者）联系起来。将“生前遗嘱”与“意愿”（治疗）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":694,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.503","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.503.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.503.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,138],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse provides pain medication to a client as soon as it is requested and available. Which ethical principle is the nurse demonstrating?","fullStemZh":"护士在患者提出要求且药物可用时，立即为其提供止痛药。护士展示了哪种伦理原则？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which ethical principle is the nurse demonstrating?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士展示了哪种伦理原则？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse provides pain medication to a client as soon as it is requested and available.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在患者提出要求且药物可用时，立即为其提供止痛药。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Justice","zh":"公正原则"},{"id":"C","en":"Beneficence","zh":"行善原则"},{"id":"B","en":"Veracity","zh":"诚实原则"},{"id":"A","en":"Autonomy","zh":"自主原则"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Beneficence is the duty to do good and promote the well-being of others. Relieving pain is a direct application of this principle. Autonomy (this option) relates to the client's right to choose. Veracity (this option) is truth-telling. Justice (this option) is fairness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"行善原则是行善和促进他人福祉的职责。缓解疼痛是这一原则的直接应用。自主原则（该选项）涉及患者的选择权。诚实原则（该选项）是讲真话。公正原则（该选项）是公平。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think: Beneficence = Benefit (doing good). Nonmaleficence = No harm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考：行善原则 (Beneficence) = 获益 (Benefit)（行善）。不伤害原则 (Nonmaleficence) = 不造成伤害。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":695,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.504","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.504.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.504.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,53],"fullStemEn":"An adult client's spouse calls the nurse station asking for the client's latest laboratory results. The client has not given permission to share information with the spouse. What is the most appropriate response by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"一位成年患者的配偶致电护士站，询问患者最近的化验结果。患者尚未允许与配偶分享信息。护士最恰当的回答是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most appropriate response by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最恰当的回答是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has not given permission to share information with the spouse.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者尚未允许与配偶分享信息。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"\"I can provide the results since you are the spouse.\"","zh":"“既然你是配偶，我可以提供结果。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"You should ask the healthcare provider for the results.\"","zh":"“您应该向医疗保健提供者询问结果。”"},{"id":"D","en":"\"I cannot share this information with you without the client's authorization.\"","zh":"“未经患者授权，我不能与您分享此信息。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"The results are within normal limits, so there is nothing to worry about.\"","zh":"“结果在正常范围内，所以没什么好担心的。”"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Under HIPAA, healthcare information cannot be shared with family members or spouses unless the client has explicitly authorized it. Confirming results are 'normal' is still a violation of privacy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据 HIPAA，除非患者明确授权，否则不能与家属或配偶共享医疗保健信息。确认结果“正常”仍然违反了隐私规定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Privacy is absolute unless authorization is present. 'No' is the safest answer when information sharing is requested without proof of consent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"除非获得授权，否则隐私是绝对的。在没有同意证明的情况下要求共享信息时，“不”是最安全的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":696,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.505","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.505.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.505.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,34],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is giving a handoff report to the oncoming nurse. Which information is essential to include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向接班护士进行交接班报告。哪些信息是必须包括的？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which information is essential to include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些信息是必须包括的？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A list of all visitors the client had during the shift.","zh":"该班次期间患者所有访客的名单。"},{"id":"C","en":"Upcoming scheduled procedures or tests.","zh":"即将进行的预定手术或检查。"},{"id":"D","en":"Changes to the client's medication orders.","zh":"患者药物医嘱的变化。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client's current status and any recent changes.","zh":"患者当前的状态及任何最近的变化。"},{"id":"E","en":"The nurse's personal opinion about the client's family.","zh":"护士对患者家属的个人看法。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective handoff reports (SBAR) should focus on clinical facts: current status, changes, medications, and upcoming plans. Non-essential info and personal opinions (Option E) should be excluded to ensure clarity and professionalism.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的交接班报告 (SBAR) 应侧重于临床事实：当前状态、变化、药物和即将进行的计划。应排除非必要信息和个人看法（选项 E），以确保清晰度和专业性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for 'Objective' and 'Clinically Relevant' data. Eliminate 'Subjective' or 'Social' fluff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找“客观”和“临床相关”的数据。剔除“主观”或“社交”琐碎信息。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which information is essential to include?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些信息是必须包括的？（"}
{"queueIndex":697,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.506","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.506.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.506.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,63],"fullStemEn":"A client with full mental capacity insists on leaving the hospital against medical advice (AMA). The nurse threatens to place the client in restraints to prevent them from leaving. Which legal tort has the nurse committed?","fullStemZh":"一名具备完全行为能力的患者坚持违反医嘱 (AMA) 要求出院。护士威胁要对患者实施约束以防止其离开。护士犯了哪种法律侵权行为？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which legal tort has the nurse committed?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士犯了哪种法律侵权行为？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse threatens to place the client in restraints to prevent them from leaving.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士威胁要对患者实施约束以防止其离开。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"False imprisonment","zh":"非法拘禁 (False imprisonment)"},{"id":"D","en":"Defamation","zh":"诽谤 (Defamation)"},{"id":"B","en":"Assault","zh":"恐吓罪 (Assault)"},{"id":"C","en":"Battery","zh":"殴打罪 (Battery)"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assault is the threat of unauthorized touching that causes fear. Since the nurse threatened to restrain the client, it is assault. If the nurse had actually applied the restraints, it would be false imprisonment and battery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"恐吓罪是指导致恐惧的未经授权触摸的威胁。由于护士威胁要约束患者，因此属于恐吓罪。如果护士实际实施了约束，则属于非法拘禁和殴打罪。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Assault = A threat (mental). Battery = Beating (physical contact).","testTakingStrategyZh":"恐吓罪 (Assault) = 威胁（心理）。殴打罪 (Battery) = 殴打（身体接触）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse threatens to place the client in restraints to prevent them from leaving.","controlSentenceZh":"护士威胁要对患者实施约束以防止其离开。"}
{"queueIndex":698,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.507","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.507.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.507.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,52],"fullStemEn":"A client who is scheduled for a bilateral tubal ligation tells the nurse, \"I'm not sure I want to do this anymore.\" Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名预定进行双侧输卵管结扎术的患者告诉护士：“我不确定我是否还想做这个手术。”护士首先应该采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应该采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who is scheduled for a bilateral tubal ligation tells the nurse, \"I'm not sure I want to do this anymore.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名预定进行双侧输卵管结扎术的患者告诉护士：“我不确定我是否还想做这个手术。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and the surgeon of the client's statement.","zh":"将患者的陈述通知医疗保健提供者和外科医生。"},{"id":"A","en":"Tell the client it is too late to change their mind since the surgery is scheduled.","zh":"告诉患者现在改变主意已经太晚了，因为手术已经排好了。"},{"id":"B","en":"Reassure the client that they are just nervous and it's a common procedure.","zh":"安抚患者说他们只是紧张，这是一种常见的手术。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document the client's statement and continue with the preoperative checklist.","zh":"记录患者的陈述并继续执行术前核对清单。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Advocacy involves ensuring the client's wishes are respected. If a client expresses doubt about a procedure, the nurse must notify the provider immediately so the informed consent process can be revisited. A client has the right to withdraw consent at any time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"倡导涉及确保患者的意愿得到尊重。如果患者对手术表示怀疑，护士必须立即通知提供者，以便重新审视知情同意过程。患者有权随时撤回同意。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The client's right to refuse or change their mind is paramount. Choose the answer that stops the process and involves the provider.","testTakingStrategyZh":"患者拒绝或改变主意的权利至高无上。选择能停止流程并涉及提供者的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":699,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.508","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.508.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.508.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,62],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assigning a roommate for a client with an open, draining wound infected with Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA). Which client would be the most appropriate roommate?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患有开放性、渗出性伤口且感染了耐甲氧西林金黄色葡萄球菌 (MRSA) 的患者安排室友。哪位患者是最合适的室友？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client would be the most appropriate roommate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪位患者是最合适的室友？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is assigning a roommate for a client with an open, draining wound infected with Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患有开放性、渗出性伤口且感染了耐甲氧西林金黄色葡萄球菌 (MRSA) 的患者安排室友。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client with a compromised immune system due to chemotherapy.","zh":"一名因化疗导致免疫系统受损的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with a fresh postoperative hip replacement.","zh":"一名刚接受过髋关节置换术的术后患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"Another client with a different draining wound.","zh":"另一名患有不同渗出性伤口的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client with a fractured femur and intact skin.","zh":"一名股骨骨折且皮肤完整的患者。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients with MRSA should ideally be in a private room. If sharing is necessary, the roommate should have intact skin and not be immunocompromised. Surgical clients and immunocompromised clients are at high risk for infection. Another draining wound provides a portal of entry for MRSA.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MRSA 患者理想情况下应住在单人房。如果必须合住，室友应皮肤完整且无免疫受损。手术患者和免疫受损患者感染风险很高。另一个渗出性伤口为 MRSA 提供了入侵门户。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In room assignments, avoid placing an infected client with someone who is 'Clean' (surgical) or 'Weak' (immunocompromised).","testTakingStrategyZh":"在安排病房时，避免将感染患者与“干净”（手术）或“虚弱”（免疫受损）的人放在一起。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":700,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.509","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.509.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.509.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,242],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,62],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers that a client has fallen while attempting to walk to the bathroom alone. After assessing the client and notifying the provider, the nurse completes an incident report. Which action should the nurse take regarding the report?","fullStemZh":"护士发现一名患者在尝试独自走去洗手间时摔倒了。在评估患者并通知提供者后，护士填写了一份事故报告。护士应就该报告采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take regarding the report?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应就该报告采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"After assessing the client and notifying the provider, the nurse completes an incident report.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在评估患者并通知提供者后，护士填写了一份事故报告。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place a copy of the incident report in the client's medical record.","zh":"将事故报告的副本放入患者的医疗记录中。"},{"id":"B","en":"Document in the medical record that an incident report was filed.","zh":"在医疗记录中记载已提交事故报告。"},{"id":"D","en":"Follow the facility's policy for submitting the report to the risk management department.","zh":"按照机构政策将报告提交给风险管理部门。"},{"id":"C","en":"Mention the incident report in the change-of-shift report.","zh":"在交接班报告中提到该事故报告。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Incident reports are internal quality improvement documents and are not part of the legal medical record. They should never be mentioned or placed in the chart. They are sent directly to risk management or administration per facility policy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"事故报告是内部质量改进文件，不属于法律医疗记录的一部分。绝不应在病历中提及或放入病历。它们应根据机构政策直接发送给风险管理部门或管理层。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: The chart and the incident report are two separate worlds. They should never cross paths.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：病历和事故报告是两个独立的世界。它们绝不应产生交集。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":701,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.510","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.510.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.510.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,27],"fullStemEn":"Which responsibilities are characteristic of the nurse's role as a case manager? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些职责属于护士作为案例管理者的角色特征？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which responsibilities are characteristic of the nurse's role as a case manager?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些职责属于护士作为案例管理者的角色特征？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Monitoring the cost-effectiveness of the care provided.","zh":"监测所提供护理的成本效益。"},{"id":"A","en":"Coordinating care among various healthcare disciplines.","zh":"协调不同医疗保健学科之间的护理。"},{"id":"E","en":"Advocating for the client's needs within the healthcare system.","zh":"在医疗保健系统中倡导患者的需求。"},{"id":"C","en":"Facilitating the client's transition to a long-term care facility.","zh":"协助患者转入长期护理机构。"},{"id":"B","en":"Providing direct bedside care for a group of clients throughout the shift.","zh":"在整个班次中为一组患者提供直接的床边护理。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Case managers focus on coordinating resources, managing transitions, ensuring cost-effectiveness, and advocating for the client. They typically do not provide direct bedside care, as their role is focused on the broader trajectory of the client's care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"案例管理者专注于协调资源、管理过渡、确保成本效益并为患者倡导。他们通常不提供直接的床边护理，因为他们的角色专注于患者护理的更广泛轨迹。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Case management is 'Big Picture'. Direct care is 'Small Picture'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"案例管理是“宏观图景”。直接护理是“微观图景”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":702,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.511","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.511.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.511.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"When caring for a client with Clostridioides difficile (C. diff), which hand hygiene method is mandatory?","fullStemZh":"在护理艰难克罗替尼 (C. diff) 患者时，哪种手部卫生方法是强制性的？","terminalSentenceEn":"When caring for a client with Clostridioides difficile (C. diff), which hand hygiene method is mandatory?","terminalSentenceZh":"在护理艰难克罗替尼 (C. diff) 患者时，哪种手部卫生方法是强制性的？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Using a chlorhexidine gluconate (CHG) solution.","zh":"使用葡萄糖酸氯己定 (CHG) 溶液。"},{"id":"A","en":"Washing hands with soap and water.","zh":"用肥皂和水洗手。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wearing gloves eliminates the need for hand hygiene.","zh":"戴手套可以免除对手部卫生的需求。"},{"id":"D","en":"Using an alcohol-based hand rub before and after client contact.","zh":"在接触患者前后使用含酒精的免洗手液。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. diff produces spores that are resistant to alcohol-based sanitizers. Mechanical friction and rinsing with soap and water are necessary to remove these spores from the hands.","rationaleCorrectZh":"C. diff 产生的孢子对含酒精的消毒剂具有抵抗力。必须使用肥皂和水进行机械摩擦和冲洗才能从手上清除这些孢子。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: Spores (C. diff, Anthrax) = Soap (and water).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：孢子（C. diff、炭疽）= 肥皂（和水）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":703,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.512","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.512.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.512.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[68,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,47],"fullStemEn":"A client is placed on droplet precautions for bacterial meningitis. What should staff or visitors do before entering the client's room or patient space?","fullStemZh":"一名细菌性脑膜炎患者正在实施飞沫传播预防措施。工作人员或访客进入患者病房或患者空间前应怎么做？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should staff or visitors do before entering the client's room or patient space?","terminalSentenceZh":"工作人员或访客进入患者病房或患者空间前应怎么做？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is placed on droplet precautions for bacterial meningitis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名细菌性脑膜炎患者正在实施飞沫传播预防措施。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Enter unmasked if remaining 6 feet away.","zh":"若保持6英尺距离，可不戴口罩进入。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wear gloves only and remain 3 feet away.","zh":"仅戴手套并保持3英尺距离。"},{"id":"C","en":"Put on a surgical mask upon entry.","zh":"进入时佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use an N95 respirator for routine room entry.","zh":"常规进入病房时使用N95呼吸防护器。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CDC Droplet Precautions instruct staff to don a mask upon entry into the patient room or patient space. Distance alone does not replace the mask requirement for room entry.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDC飞沫传播预防措施要求工作人员进入患者病房或患者空间时佩戴口罩。进入病房时，仅依靠距离不能替代口罩要求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate Droplet Precautions with a surgical mask donned upon room or patient-space entry.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将飞沫传播预防措施与进入病房或患者空间时佩戴外科口罩联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":704,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.513","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.513.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.513.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,52],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to enter the room of a client on contact precautions for a wound infection. Which personal protective equipment (PPE) is required? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备进入一名因伤口感染而实施接触预防措施的患者房间。需要哪些个人防护装备 (PPE)？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which personal protective equipment (PPE) is required?","penultimateSentenceZh":"需要哪些个人防护装备 (PPE)？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Goggles","zh":"护目镜"},{"id":"E","en":"N95 respirator","zh":"N95 呼吸防护罩"},{"id":"B","en":"Gown","zh":"隔离衣"},{"id":"C","en":"Surgical mask","zh":"外科口罩"},{"id":"A","en":"Gloves","zh":"手套"}],"correct":["A","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard PPE for contact precautions includes a gown and gloves. Masks and eye protection are only added if splashes of body fluids are anticipated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接触预防措施的标准 PPE 包括隔离衣和手套。只有在预期会有体液飞溅时，才会增加口罩和护目镜。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For Contact = Gown + Gloves. Only add 'Face' stuff if 'Fluid' is flying.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于接触 = 隔离衣 + 手套。只有在“体液”飞溅时才增加“面部”装备。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":705,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.514","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.514.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.514.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,51],"fullStemEn":"A nurse has completed care for a client in isolation. What is the correct sequence for removing (doffing) personal protective equipment (PPE)?","fullStemZh":"护士已经完成了对一名隔离患者的护理。脱掉（doffing）个人防护装备 (PPE) 的正确顺序是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the correct sequence for removing (doffing) personal protective equipment (PPE)?","terminalSentenceZh":"脱掉（doffing）个人防护装备 (PPE) 的正确顺序是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse has completed care for a client in isolation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士已经完成了对一名隔离患者的护理。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Mask, Gloves, Gown, Goggles.","zh":"口罩、手套、隔离衣、护目镜。"},{"id":"A","en":"Goggles, Mask, Gloves, Gown.","zh":"护目镜、口罩、手套、隔离衣。"},{"id":"C","en":"Gloves, Goggles, Gown, Mask.","zh":"手套、护目镜、隔离衣、口罩。"},{"id":"B","en":"Gown, Gloves, Mask, Goggles.","zh":"隔离衣、手套、口罩、护目镜。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The CDC recommended sequence for doffing is: Gloves, Goggles (or face shield), Gown, Mask (or respirator). This sequence moves from the most contaminated items to the least contaminated. An alternative is removing gown and gloves together.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDC 建议的脱卸顺序是：手套、护目镜（或面罩）、隔离衣、口罩（或呼吸防护罩）。该顺序从污染最严重的物品移向污染最轻的物品。另一种方法是同时脱掉隔离衣和手套。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think: Alphabetical order for doffing (G-G-G-M): Gloves, Goggles, Gown, Mask.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考：脱卸按字母顺序 (G-G-G-M)：手套 (Gloves)、护目镜 (Goggles)、隔离衣 (Gown)、口罩 (Mask)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":706,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.515","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.515.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.515.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,35],"fullStemEn":"A client is placed in bilateral wrist restraints for safety. Which nursing interventions are required? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"为了安全，患者被实施了双侧腕部约束。需要哪些护理干预措施？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing interventions are required?","penultimateSentenceZh":"需要哪些护理干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Offer food, fluids, and toileting every 2 hours.","zh":"每 2 小时提供一次食物、液体和如厕。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess skin integrity and neurovascular status every 2 hours.","zh":"每 2 小时评估一次皮肤完整性和神经血管状态。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use a quick-release knot to tie the restraints.","zh":"使用活结（快速释放结）系约束带。"},{"id":"A","en":"Secure the restraints to the side rails of the bed.","zh":"将约束带固定在床的侧护栏上。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure a new prescription is obtained every 24 hours for an adult.","zh":"确保成年患者每 24 小时获得一次新医嘱。"}],"correct":["B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Restraints must be secured to the bed frame, not side rails. Assessment, renewing orders (every 24h for adults), quick-release knots for emergencies, and meeting basic needs (food/water/toileting) are mandatory safety standards.","rationaleCorrectZh":"约束带必须固定在床架上，而不是侧护栏上。评估、更新医嘱（成年人每 24 小时一次）、紧急情况下使用的活结以及满足基本需求（食物/水/如厕）是强制性的安全标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Restraints are high-risk. Look for options that emphasize safety, assessment, and basic human needs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"约束是高风险的。寻找强调安全、评估和基本人类需求的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":707,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.516","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.516.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.516.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,30],"fullStemEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in a fall prevention plan for an older adult client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应在老年患者的防跌倒计划中包括哪些干预措施？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in a fall prevention plan for an older adult client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在老年患者的防跌倒计划中包括哪些干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Place the call bell within the client's reach.","zh":"将呼叫铃放在患者够得着的地方。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep all four side rails up at all times.","zh":"始终将所有四个侧护栏全部拉起。"},{"id":"A","en":"Keep the bed in the lowest position.","zh":"保持病床在最低位置。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the use of non-skid footwear.","zh":"鼓励使用防滑鞋。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide adequate lighting in the room and bathroom.","zh":"在房间和洗手间提供充足的照明。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard fall precautions include low beds, reachable call bells, good lighting, and non-skid socks. Keeping all four side rails up (Option E) is considered a physical restraint and can actually increase injury risk if the client tries to climb over them.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标准防跌倒措施包括低位病床、触手可及的呼叫铃、良好的照明和防滑袜。将四个侧护栏全部拉起（选项 E）被视为物理约束，如果患者尝试翻越，实际上可能会增加受伤风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Fall prevention is about environmental safety. Avoid 'Restraint-like' answers (like 4 rails up).","testTakingStrategyZh":"防跌倒涉及环境安全。避免“类似于约束”的答案（如拉起 4 个护栏）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":708,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_22","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.517","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.517.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.517.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,58],"fullStemEn":"While preparing a sterile field for a dressing change, the nurse drops a sterile gauze pad onto the outer 1-inch (2.5 cm) border of the sterile drape. Which action should the nurse take?","fullStemZh":"在为换药准备无菌场时，护士将一块无菌纱布垫掉到了无菌铺单外缘 1 英寸（2.5 厘米）的边界上。护士应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"While preparing a sterile field for a dressing change, the nurse drops a sterile gauze pad onto the outer 1-inch (2.5 cm) border of the sterile drape.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在为换药准备无菌场时，护士将一块无菌纱布垫掉到了无菌铺单外缘 1 英寸（2.5 厘米）的边界上。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Discard the gauze pad and use a new sterile one.","zh":"丢弃该纱布垫并使用新的无菌纱布垫。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use sterile forceps to move the gauze pad to the center of the field.","zh":"使用无菌镊子将纱布垫移至无菌场中心。"},{"id":"C","en":"Consider the gauze pad sterile and use it.","zh":"认为纱布垫是无菌的并使用它。"},{"id":"B","en":"Discard the entire sterile field and start over.","zh":"丢弃整个无菌场并重新开始。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The outer 1-inch border of a sterile field is considered contaminated. Any item touching this border is no longer sterile. However, the rest of the field remains sterile, so only the contaminated item needs to be discarded.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无菌场外缘 1 英寸的边界被视为受污染。任何接触该边界的物品都不再无菌。然而，无菌场的其余部分保持无菌，因此只需丢弃受污染的物品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the '1-inch border rule'. If it touches the edge, it's out.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“1 英寸边界原则”。如果碰到边缘，它就不再无菌。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":709,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.518","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.518.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.518.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[47,107],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,27],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to lift a heavy object. Which technique should the nurse use to prevent back injury?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备搬运重物。护士应使用哪种技术来预防背部受伤？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which technique should the nurse use to prevent back injury?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应使用哪种技术来预防背部受伤？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to lift a heavy object.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备搬运重物。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hold the object as close to the body as possible.","zh":"尽可能将物体靠近身体。"},{"id":"B","en":"Keep the feet close together for stability.","zh":"双脚并拢以保持稳定。"},{"id":"A","en":"Twist the torso while lifting the object.","zh":"抬起物体时扭动躯干。"},{"id":"D","en":"Bend at the waist to pick up the object.","zh":"弯腰捡起物体。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Proper body mechanics include keeping the weight close to the body, bending at the knees (not waist), and keeping a wide base of support. Twisting is a major cause of spinal injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的身体力学包括让重物靠近身体、弯曲膝盖（而不是腰部）并保持较宽的支撑基底。扭转是导致脊柱损伤的主要原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of 'Stability' and 'Support'. Bend knees, don't twist, keep it close.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑“稳定性”和“支撑”。弯曲膝盖，不要扭转，保持靠近。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":710,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.519","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.519.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.519.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,74],"fullStemEn":"During a mass casualty incident, a nurse triages a client who is unresponsive, has a respiratory rate of 6 breaths/min, and has a large open head wound with exposed brain tissue. Which triage tag should the nurse assign?","fullStemZh":"在一次大规模伤亡事故中，护士对一名患者进行分诊：该患者无反应，呼吸频率为 6 次/分钟，且头部有巨大开放性伤口，脑组织外露。护士应分配哪种分诊标签？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which triage tag should the nurse assign?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应分配哪种分诊标签？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During a mass casualty incident, a nurse triages a client who is unresponsive, has a respiratory rate of 6 breaths/min, and has a large open head wound with exposed brain tissue.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在一次大规模伤亡事故中，护士对一名患者进行分诊：该患者无反应，呼吸频率为 6 次/分钟，且头部有巨大开放性伤口，脑组织外露。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Red (Emergent)","zh":"红色（紧急）"},{"id":"B","en":"Green (Non-urgent)","zh":"绿色（非紧急）"},{"id":"A","en":"Yellow (Urgent)","zh":"黄色（亚紧急）"},{"id":"C","en":"Black (Expectant)","zh":"黑色（期待/濒死）"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In mass casualty triage (START method), clients with injuries incompatible with life or those expected to die regardless of treatment are tagged Black. This allows resources to be focused on those with the best chance of survival.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在大规模伤亡分诊（START 方法）中，受伤程度与生命不相容或无论如何治疗都预料会死亡的患者被标记为黑色。这使得资源能够集中在那些生存机会最大的人身上。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In disaster triage, the goal is 'Doing the greatest good for the greatest number'. Don't spend limited resources on those unlikely to survive.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在灾难分诊中，目标是“为最大多数人谋求最大利益”。不要在生存可能性极低的人身上花费有限的资源。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":711,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchB_25","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.520","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.520.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.520.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,41],"fullStemEn":"A client has a known latex allergy. The nurse should assess the client for cross-sensitivities to which foods? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者已知对乳胶过敏。护士应评估该患者对哪些食物是否存在交叉敏感性？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should assess the client for cross-sensitivities to which foods?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应评估该患者对哪些食物是否存在交叉敏感性？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Avocados","zh":"鳄梨"},{"id":"A","en":"Bananas","zh":"香蕉"},{"id":"C","en":"Strawberries","zh":"草莓"},{"id":"D","en":"Kiwis","zh":"奇异果（猕猴桃）"},{"id":"E","en":"Chestnuts","zh":"栗子"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Latex-fruit syndrome involves cross-reactivity between latex and certain foods, most commonly bananas, avocados, kiwis, and chestnuts. Other foods include tomatoes and potatoes. Strawberries are not a primary cross-reactive food for latex.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乳胶-水果综合征涉及乳胶与某些食物之间的交叉反应，最常见的是香蕉、鳄梨、奇异果和栗子。其他食物包括番茄和马铃薯。草莓不是乳胶的主要交叉反应食物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the acronym BACK: Bananas, Avocados, Chestnuts, Kiwis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住首字母缩写 BACK：香蕉 (Bananas)、鳄梨 (Avocados)、栗子 (Chestnuts)、奇异果 (Kiwis)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":712,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.521","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.521.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.521.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,60],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to the parents of a 2-month-old infant about the scheduled immunizations. Which vaccine should the nurse inform the parents their child will receive during this visit?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名 2 个月大婴儿的父母提供关于预定免疫接种的指导。护士应告知父母，他们的孩子在这次就诊期间将接种哪种疫苗？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which vaccine should the nurse inform the parents their child will receive during this visit?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应告知父母，他们的孩子在这次就诊期间将接种哪种疫苗？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to the parents of a 2-month-old infant about the scheduled immunizations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名 2 个月大婴儿的父母提供关于预定免疫接种的指导。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hepatitis A.","zh":"甲型肝炎疫苗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Varicella.","zh":"水痘疫苗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Measles, mumps, and rubella (MMR).","zh":"麻疹、腮腺炎和风疹疫苗 (MMR)。"},{"id":"A","en":"Rotavirus (RV).","zh":"轮状病毒疫苗 (RV)。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The RV vaccine is typically administered at 2, 4, and 6 months of age. MMR and Varicella are first given at 12-15 months. Hepatitis A is typically given at 12 months.","rationaleCorrectZh":"轮状病毒疫苗通常在 2、4 和 6 个月大时接种。MMR 和水痘疫苗首次接种通常在 12-15 个月大。甲型肝炎疫苗通常在 12 个月大时接种。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the pediatric immunization schedule. Live virus vaccines like MMR and Varicella are usually delayed until 1 year of age.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆儿科免疫计划。像 MMR 和水痘这样的活病毒疫苗通常推迟到 1 岁接种。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":713,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.522","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.522.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.522.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,58],"fullStemEn":"A client diagnosed with terminal cancer says to the nurse, 'I don't think I can handle another round of chemotherapy. It's just too much.' Which response by the nurse is therapeutic?","fullStemZh":"一名被诊断为癌症晚期的患者对护士说：“我觉得我无法再承受一轮化疗了。这实在太多了。”护士的哪种回应是具有治疗意义的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is therapeutic?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪种回应是具有治疗意义的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"It's just too much.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"这实在太多了。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"It sounds like you are feeling overwhelmed by the treatment process.","zh":"听起来你对治疗过程感到压力很大。"},{"id":"A","en":"Why do you feel like you can't handle it anymore?","zh":"你为什么觉得你再也承受不了了？"},{"id":"C","en":"Don't say that. You have to keep fighting for your family.","zh":"别那样说。你必须为了你的家人继续奋斗。"},{"id":"D","en":"I understand. Most people feel that way after a few treatments.","zh":"我理解。大多数人在几次治疗后都会有这种感觉。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reflecting the client's feelings and paraphrasing are effective therapeutic techniques that encourage the client to express their emotions. The correct response validates the client's feelings without judgment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反映患者的感受和释义是有效的治疗技巧，可以鼓励患者表达情感。正确的回答在不加评判的情况下肯定了患者的感受。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for responses that reflect feelings or use open-ended statements. Avoid 'why' questions and giving advice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找反映感受或使用开放式陈述的回应。避免使用“为什么”提问和提供建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":714,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.523","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.523.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.523.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching the parents of a 2-year-old toddler about home safety. Which interventions should the nurse include in the teaching? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名 2 岁幼儿的父母讲解居家安全。护士应在教学中包括哪些干预措施？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the teaching?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在教学中包括哪些干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Cover unused electrical outlets with safety plugs.","zh":"用安全插头盖住未使用的电源插座。"},{"id":"C","en":"Keep the pot handles turned toward the back of the stove.","zh":"将锅柄朝向灶台后方。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place safety gates at the top and bottom of stairs.","zh":"在楼梯的顶部和底部安装安全门。"},{"id":"D","en":"Allow the child to play with small balloons under supervision.","zh":"允许孩子在监督下玩小气球。"},{"id":"B","en":"Store household cleaning supplies in a high, locked cabinet.","zh":"将家用清洁用品存放在高处的锁柜中。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Toddlers are at high risk for falls, poisoning, burns, and electrical injuries. Safety gates, locked storage for toxins, turning pot handles, and outlet covers are essential safety measures. Small balloons are a major choking hazard and should be avoided entirely for toddlers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"幼儿面临跌倒、中毒、烫伤和电伤的高风险。安全门、有毒物质的锁柜存储、转动锅柄以及插座盖是必要的安全措施。小气球是主要的窒息风险，应完全避免幼儿接触。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the developmental characteristics of a toddler (curiosity, mobility) and prioritize preventing common household accidents.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑幼儿的发育特点（好奇心、活动能力），并优先预防常见的居家事故。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":715,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.524","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.524.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.524.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[133,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a prenatal class about the benefits of breastfeeding for the infant. Which information should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在开展关于母乳喂养对婴儿益处的产前课程。护士应包括哪些信息？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which information should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些信息？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Lower risk of otitis media (middle ear infections).","zh":"降低中耳炎的风险。"},{"id":"D","en":"Elimination of the need for vitamin D supplementation.","zh":"无需补充维生素 D。"},{"id":"C","en":"Reduced incidence of childhood obesity.","zh":"降低儿童肥胖症的发病率。"},{"id":"B","en":"Enhanced immune system through maternal antibodies.","zh":"通过母体抗体增强免疫系统。"},{"id":"A","en":"Decreased risk of sudden infant death syndrome (SIDS).","zh":"降低婴儿猝死综合征 (SIDS) 的风险。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Breastfeeding provides numerous benefits including reduced risks of SIDS, obesity, and infections (otitis media, respiratory infections). Maternal IgA antibodies are transferred through breast milk. However, breast milk is low in vitamin D, so breastfed infants still require supplementation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"母乳喂养具有许多益处，包括降低 SIDS、肥胖和感染（中耳炎、呼吸道感染）的风险。母体 IgA 抗体通过母乳传递。然而，母乳中维生素 D 含量较低，因此母乳喂养的婴儿仍需补充。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that while breast milk is the 'gold standard', it lacks sufficient vitamin D and iron (after 4-6 months).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住，虽然母乳是“金标准”，但它缺乏足够的维生素 D 和铁（4-6 个月后）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":716,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.525","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.525.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.525.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[165,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,62],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted for alcohol detoxification. Twelve hours after the last drink, the client becomes tremulous, anxious, and reports 'bugs crawling on the walls.' Which medication should the nurse expect to administer?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因酒精脱毒入院。在最后一次饮酒 12 小时后，患者变得震颤、焦虑，并报告“墙上有虫子在爬”。护士应预期给予哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse expect to administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期给予哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Twelve hours after the last drink, the client becomes tremulous, anxious, and reports 'bugs crawling on the walls.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"在最后一次饮酒 12 小时后，患者变得震颤、焦虑，并报告“墙上有虫子在爬”。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Disulfiram.","zh":"双硫仑。"},{"id":"C","en":"Lorazepam.","zh":"劳拉西泮。"},{"id":"B","en":"Naloxone.","zh":"纳洛酮。"},{"id":"A","en":"Methadone.","zh":"美沙酮。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Benzodiazepines like lorazepam or chlordiazepoxide are the first-line treatment for acute alcohol withdrawal symptoms, including tremors, anxiety, and hallucinations (delirium tremens), to prevent seizures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"苯二氮卓类药物（如劳拉西泮或氯氮䓬）是急性酒精戒断症状（包括震颤、焦虑和幻觉/谵妄）的一线治疗药物，旨在预防癫痫发作。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the acute symptoms. Alcohol withdrawal is a medical emergency that requires sedation (benzodiazepines).","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注急性症状。酒精戒断是一种医疗急症，需要镇静治疗（苯二氮卓类药物）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":717,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.526","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.526.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.526.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"According to the American Cancer Society guidelines, at what age should a client with average risk begin regular screening for colorectal cancer?","fullStemZh":"根据美国癌症协会的指南，具有平均风险的患者应从什么年龄开始定期进行结直肠癌筛查？","terminalSentenceEn":"According to the American Cancer Society guidelines, at what age should a client with average risk begin regular screening for colorectal cancer?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据美国癌症协会的指南，具有平均风险的患者应从什么年龄开始定期进行结直肠癌筛查？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"40 years old.","zh":"40 岁。"},{"id":"D","en":"45 years old.","zh":"45 岁。"},{"id":"B","en":"55 years old.","zh":"55 岁。"},{"id":"A","en":"50 years old.","zh":"50 岁。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Updated guidelines now recommend that adults with average risk begin colorectal cancer screening at age 45. This was recently changed from age 50 due to increasing rates of colorectal cancer in younger adults.","rationaleCorrectZh":"更新后的指南现在建议具有平均风险的成年人从 45 岁开始进行结直肠癌筛查。由于年轻人结直肠癌发病率上升，这一建议最近从 50 岁改为 45 岁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stay updated on screening guidelines. NCLEX often tests recent changes in evidence-based practice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解最新的筛查指南。NCLEX 经常考察循证实践中的最新变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":718,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.527","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.527.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.527.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client in the manic phase of bipolar disorder. Which interventions should be included? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名处于双相情感障碍躁狂期的患者制定护理计划。应包括哪些干预措施？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"应包括哪些干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Provide high-calorie finger foods.","zh":"提供高热量的手拿食物。"},{"id":"E","en":"Allow the client to lead group activities to boost self-esteem.","zh":"允许患者领导团体活动以增强自尊心。"},{"id":"B","en":"Encourage the client to participate in competitive group games.","zh":"鼓励患者参加竞争性的团体游戏。"},{"id":"D","en":"Set firm and consistent limits on behavior.","zh":"对行为设定坚定且一致的限制。"},{"id":"C","en":"Maintain a low-stimulation environment.","zh":"保持低刺激环境。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During mania, clients are hyperactive and have difficulty sitting for meals, so finger foods provide necessary nutrition. Low stimulation helps reduce agitation. Firm limits are necessary for safety and structure. Competitive games or leadership roles (Option E) can be overly stimulating and exacerbate manic behavior.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在躁狂发作期间，患者过度活跃，难以坐下来吃饭，因此手拿食物可以提供必要的营养。低刺激有助于减轻躁动。为了安全和结构化，坚定限制是必要的。竞争性游戏或领导角色（选项 E）可能会过度刺激并加剧躁狂行为。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The goal for mania is 'Calm, Safe, and Nutritious'. Avoid anything that increases stimulation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"躁狂症的目标是“冷静、安全、营养”。避免任何增加刺激的事物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which interventions should be included?","controlSentenceZh":"应包括哪些干预措施？（"}
{"queueIndex":719,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.528","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.528.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.528.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[55,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is advising a pregnant client about nutrition. Which food should the nurse instruct the client to avoid to prevent listeriosis?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名孕妇提供营养建议。护士应指示患者避免哪种食物以预防李斯特菌病？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which food should the nurse instruct the client to avoid to prevent listeriosis?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应指示患者避免哪种食物以预防李斯特菌病？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is advising a pregnant client about nutrition.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名孕妇提供营养建议。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Unwashed raw vegetables.","zh":"未洗净的生蔬菜。"},{"id":"D","en":"Soft cheeses made with unpasteurized milk.","zh":"用未经过巴氏杀菌的牛奶制成的软奶酪。"},{"id":"A","en":"Pasteurized milk.","zh":"经过巴氏杀菌的牛奶。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hard cheeses like cheddar.","zh":"硬质奶酪，如切达干酪。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Listeriosis is a foodborne illness caused by Listeria monocytogenes, which can be found in unpasteurized dairy products, deli meats, and soft cheeses (like feta, brie, camembert). It can lead to miscarriage or neonatal infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"李斯特菌病是由单核细胞增生李斯特菌引起的食源性疾病，常见于未经巴氏杀菌的乳制品、熟食肉类和软奶酪（如菲达奶酪、布里奶酪、卡门培尔奶酪）。它可能导致流产或新生儿感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between foods that are healthy versus those that carry specific infectious risks during pregnancy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分健康的食物与怀孕期间带有特定感染风险的食物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":720,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.529","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.529.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.529.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[173,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,63],"fullStemEn":"A client who was passed over for a promotion at work tells the nurse, 'It's actually a good thing I didn't get the job; the extra stress would have been bad for my health.' Which defense mechanism is the client using?","fullStemZh":"一名在工作中未能晋升的患者对护士说：“其实我没得到这份工作是件好事；额外的压力会对我的健康不利。”患者使用了哪种心理防御机制？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which defense mechanism is the client using?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者使用了哪种心理防御机制？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who was passed over for a promotion at work tells the nurse, 'It's actually a good thing I didn't get the job; the extra stress would have been bad for my health.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名在工作中未能晋升的患者对护士说：“其实我没得到这份工作是件好事；额外的压力会对我的健康不利。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Projection.","zh":"投射。"},{"id":"C","en":"Rationalization.","zh":"合理化（找借口）。"},{"id":"A","en":"Displacement.","zh":"置换（转移）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Denial.","zh":"否认。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rationalization involves creating logical or socially acceptable explanations for behaviors or failures to hide true motivations or feelings. The client is making an excuse to justify why they didn't get the promotion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合理化涉及为行为或失败创造逻辑上或社会上可接受的解释，以隐藏真实的动机或感受。患者正在找借口来解释为什么他们没有得到晋升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the key action: making an excuse to justify a situation. This matches the definition of rationalization.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别关键动作：找借口为某种情况辩解。这符合合理化的定义。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":721,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.530","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.530.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.530.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a postmenopausal woman about preventing osteoporosis. Which recommendations should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名绝经后女性如何预防骨质疏松。护士应包括哪些建议？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which recommendations should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些建议？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Participate in weight-bearing exercises like walking.","zh":"参加步行等负重运动。"},{"id":"B","en":"Increase intake of calcium-rich foods such as yogurt.","zh":"增加酸奶等富含钙的食物摄入。"},{"id":"D","en":"Limit alcohol consumption.","zh":"限制饮酒。"},{"id":"E","en":"Take a daily vitamin C supplement of 2000 mg.","zh":"每天补充 2000 毫克维生素 C。"},{"id":"C","en":"Quit smoking.","zh":"戒烟。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Prevention of osteoporosis involves weight-bearing exercise, adequate calcium and vitamin D, and lifestyle modifications like smoking cessation and limiting alcohol. High-dose Vitamin C (Option E) is not a standard recommendation for osteoporosis prevention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防骨质疏松涉及负重运动、充足的钙和维生素 D以及生活方式的改变，如戒烟和限酒。大剂量维生素 C（选项 E）不是预防骨质疏松的标准建议。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on factors that directly affect bone density and calcium metabolism.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注直接影响骨密度和钙代谢的因素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which recommendations should the nurse include?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些建议？（"}
{"queueIndex":722,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.531","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.531.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.531.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[132,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is conducting a suicide risk assessment for a client with depression. Which factors increase the client's risk for suicide? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名抑郁症患者进行自杀风险评估。哪些因素会增加患者的自杀风险？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which factors increase the client's risk for suicide?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些因素会增加患者的自杀风险？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Access to lethal means, such as a firearm.","zh":"拥有致命手段，如枪支。"},{"id":"E","en":"Expressing feelings of hopelessness.","zh":"表达绝望感。"},{"id":"A","en":"A specific plan for the attempt.","zh":"有具体的尝试计划。"},{"id":"D","en":"Recent loss of a spouse.","zh":"最近失去配偶。"},{"id":"C","en":"Strong religious beliefs against suicide.","zh":"有反对自杀的强烈宗教信仰。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suicide risk is increased by having a specific plan, access to means, significant life losses, and hopelessness (Option E). Protective factors like religious beliefs or strong support systems decrease the risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"拥有具体计划、拥有手段、重大的生活损失和绝望感（选项 E）都会增加自杀风险。保护性因素，如宗教信仰或强大的支持系统，会降低风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between risk factors (increase danger) and protective factors (decrease danger).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分风险因素（增加危险）和保护性因素（降低危险）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":723,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.532","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.532.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.532.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,33],"fullStemEn":"When performing a physical assessment on a 6-month-old infant, which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"在对一名 6 个月大的婴儿进行体格检查时，护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"When performing a physical assessment on a 6-month-old infant, which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"在对一名 6 个月大的婴儿进行体格检查时，护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Check for the Moro reflex.","zh":"检查莫罗反射（惊跳反射）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Auscultate the heart and lungs while the infant is quiet.","zh":"在婴儿安静时听诊心肺。"},{"id":"D","en":"Measure the head circumference.","zh":"测量头围。"},{"id":"C","en":"Inspect the throat with a tongue blade.","zh":"用压舌板检查喉咙。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For infants and toddlers, the assessment should proceed from least invasive to most invasive. Auscultating while the infant is quiet (this option) is prioritized because crying will make heart and lung sounds difficult to hear. Invasive or distressing procedures (Options A, C) should be done last.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于婴儿和幼儿，评估应从侵入性最小到侵入性最大的顺序进行。在婴儿安静时听诊（该选项）是优先考虑的，因为哭闹会使心肺音难以听清。侵入性或令人痛苦的操作（该选项、C）应最后进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In pediatric assessment, always do the 'quiet' things first and the 'noisy/disturbing' things last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在儿科评估中，始终先做“安静”的事，最后做“吵闹/干扰”的事。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":724,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.533","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.533.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.533.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who follows Islamic dietary laws. Which food choice by the client would require the nurse to intervene?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名遵守伊斯兰教饮食法的患者。患者的哪种食物选择需要护士干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which food choice by the client would require the nurse to intervene?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者的哪种食物选择需要护士干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who follows Islamic dietary laws.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名遵守伊斯兰教饮食法的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Baked chicken.","zh":"烤鸡。"},{"id":"D","en":"Steamed broccoli.","zh":"清蒸西兰花。"},{"id":"B","en":"Pork sausage.","zh":"猪肉香肠。"},{"id":"C","en":"Fresh fruit salad.","zh":"鲜果沙拉。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Islamic dietary laws (Halal) prohibit the consumption of pork and pork products, alcohol, and certain other items. Pork sausage is not allowed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"伊斯兰教饮食法（清真）禁止食用猪肉和猪肉制品、酒精以及其他某些物品。猪肉香肠是不允许的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate Islam with the prohibition of pork and alcohol.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将伊斯兰教与禁止猪肉和酒精联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":725,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.534","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.534.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.534.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a 2-day-old newborn and notes a yellowish tint to the skin and sclera. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名出生 2 天的新生儿，发现皮肤和巩膜呈黄色。哪项行动是优先的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项行动是优先的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a 2-day-old newborn and notes a yellowish tint to the skin and sclera.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名出生 2 天的新生儿，发现皮肤和巩膜呈黄色。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Inform the mother that this is normal physiological jaundice.","zh":"告知母亲这是正常的生理性黄疸。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain a prescription for a serum bilirubin level.","zh":"获取血清胆红素水平的医嘱。"},{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the mother to feed the infant more frequently.","zh":"鼓励母亲更频繁地喂养婴儿。"},{"id":"B","en":"Place the infant near a sunny window.","zh":"将婴儿放在阳光充足的窗户旁。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"While jaundice at 2 days may be physiological, the nurse must first obtain objective data to determine the severity and ensure it is not pathological. Serum bilirubin levels are the standard for assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"虽然出生 2 天的黄疸可能是生理性的，但护士必须首先获取客观数据以确定严重程度并确保其不是病理性的。血清胆红素水平是评估的标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the nursing process: Assessment (bilirubin level) before intervention or reassurance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遵循护理程序：干预或安慰前先进行评估（胆红素水平）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a 2-day-old newborn and notes a yellowish tint to the skin and sclera.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在评估一名出生 2 天的新生儿，发现皮肤和巩膜呈黄色。"}
{"queueIndex":726,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.535","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.535.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.535.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,226],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,60],"fullStemEn":"A nurse in the emergency department is caring for a client with multiple bruises in various stages of healing. The client's partner is present and answers all questions for the client. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"急诊科护士正在护理一名身上有多处处于不同愈合阶段瘀伤的患者。患者的伴侣在场并代患者回答所有问题。护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's partner is present and answers all questions for the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的伴侣在场并代患者回答所有问题。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Call the police to report suspected domestic violence.","zh":"拨打报警电话报告疑似家庭暴力。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the partner to wait in the lobby so the client can be examined privately.","zh":"请伴侣在候诊大厅等待，以便对患者进行私密检查。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the findings thoroughly in the client's record.","zh":"在患者记录中详尽记录发现的情况。"},{"id":"C","en":"Confront the partner about the client's injuries.","zh":"就患者的伤势与伴侣对质。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority is to provide a safe environment where the client can speak freely. Separating the client from the potential abuser is the first step in screening for domestic violence. Reporting (this option) should follow after private assessment and according to local laws/policies.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要任务是提供一个让患者可以自由交谈的安全环境。将患者与潜在的施虐者分开是筛查家庭暴力的第一步。报告（该选项）应在私密评估后并根据当地法律/政策进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety and private assessment are priorities when abuse is suspected.","testTakingStrategyZh":"怀疑虐待时，安全和私密评估是优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":727,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.536","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.536.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.536.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a group of adolescents about healthy nutrition. Which nutrients should the nurse emphasize as particularly important during this developmental stage? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一群青少年讲解健康营养。护士应强调在这个发育阶段特别重要的哪些营养素？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nutrients should the nurse emphasize as particularly important during this developmental stage?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应强调在这个发育阶段特别重要的哪些营养素？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Iron.","zh":"铁。"},{"id":"A","en":"Calcium.","zh":"钙。"},{"id":"E","en":"Vitamin K.","zh":"维生素 K。"},{"id":"C","en":"Protein.","zh":"蛋白质。"},{"id":"D","en":"Saturated fat.","zh":"饱和脂肪。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adolescence is a period of rapid growth. Calcium is needed for bone development. Iron is needed for expanding blood volume and muscle mass, especially in menstruating females. Protein is essential for overall growth. Saturated fats should be limited.","rationaleCorrectZh":"青春期是一个快速成长的阶段。钙是骨骼发育所必需的。铁是扩大血容量和肌肉量所必需的，特别是对于有月经的女性。蛋白质对整体生长至关重要。饱和脂肪应予以限制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider the physiological changes in adolescence: rapid bone growth and increased blood volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑青春期的生理变化：骨骼快速生长和血容量增加。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which nutrients should the nurse emphasize as particularly important during this developmental stage?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应强调在这个发育阶段特别重要的哪些营养素？（"}
{"queueIndex":728,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.537","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.537.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.537.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,71],"fullStemEn":"A client whose child died 6 months ago says, 'I keep thinking if I had only taken him to the doctor sooner, he would still be alive.' The nurse recognizes this as which stage of grief according to Kübler-Ross?","fullStemZh":"一名孩子在 6 个月前去世的患者说：“我一直在想，如果我早点带他去看医生，他现在还会活着。”根据库伯勒-罗丝模型，护士认为这是悲伤的哪个阶段？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse recognizes this as which stage of grief according to Kübler-Ross?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据库伯勒-罗丝模型，护士认为这是悲伤的哪个阶段？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client whose child died 6 months ago says, 'I keep thinking if I had only taken him to the doctor sooner, he would still be alive.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名孩子在 6 个月前去世的患者说：“我一直在想，如果我早点带他去看医生，他现在还会活着。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Denial.","zh":"否认。"},{"id":"C","en":"Anger.","zh":"愤怒。"},{"id":"A","en":"Bargaining.","zh":"讨价还价（协议）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Acceptance.","zh":"接受。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bargaining often involves 'if only' statements and guilt. The individual attempts to negotiate or replay the past to find a different outcome.","rationaleCorrectZh":"讨价还价通常涉及“如果……就好了”之类的陈述和内疚感。个人试图通过谈判或重演过去来寻找不同的结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for keywords like 'if only' to identify bargaining.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找诸如“如果……就好了”之类的关键词来识别讨价还价。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":729,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.538","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.538.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.538.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[49,124],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is auscultating a client's heart sounds. Where should the nurse place the stethoscope to best hear the mitral valve?","fullStemZh":"护士正在听诊患者的心音。护士应将听诊器放在哪里以最清楚地听到二尖瓣音？","terminalSentenceEn":"Where should the nurse place the stethoscope to best hear the mitral valve?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将听诊器放在哪里以最清楚地听到二尖瓣音？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is auscultating a client's heart sounds.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在听诊患者的心音。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Second intercostal space, left sternal border.","zh":"胸骨左缘第二肋间。"},{"id":"D","en":"Fifth intercostal space, left sternal border.","zh":"胸骨左缘第五肋间。"},{"id":"C","en":"Second intercostal space, right sternal border.","zh":"胸骨右缘第二肋间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Fifth intercostal space, left midclavicular line.","zh":"左锁骨中线第五肋间。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The mitral area (apex of the heart) is located at the fifth intercostal space at the left midclavicular line. This is the best location to hear mitral valve closure (S1) and the apical pulse.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二尖瓣区（心尖部）位于左锁骨中线第五肋间。这是听取二尖瓣关闭音 (S1) 和心尖脉的最佳位置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the mnemonic 'All People Enjoy Time Magazine' (Aortic, Pulmonic, Erb's point, Tricuspid, Mitral) to remember the sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用助记词“All People Enjoy Time Magazine”（主动脉瓣区、肺动脉瓣区、Erb 区、三尖瓣区、二尖瓣区）来记住顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":730,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.539","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.539.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.539.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,57],"fullStemEn":"A client with borderline personality disorder tells the day-shift nurse, 'The night nurse is terrible and incompetent, but you are the best nurse I've ever had.' This behavior is known as:","fullStemZh":"一名患有边缘型人格障碍的患者对白班护士说：“夜班护士太差劲且不称职了，但你是我见过的最好的护士。”这种行为被称为：","terminalSentenceEn":"This behavior is known as:","terminalSentenceZh":"这种行为被称为：","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with borderline personality disorder tells the day-shift nurse, 'The night nurse is terrible and incompetent, but you are the best nurse I've ever had.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有边缘型人格障碍的患者对白班护士说：“夜班护士太差劲且不称职了，但你是我见过的最好的护士。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Idealization.","zh":"理想化。"},{"id":"B","en":"Manipulation.","zh":"操纵。"},{"id":"D","en":"Devaluation.","zh":"贬低。"},{"id":"A","en":"Splitting.","zh":"分裂。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Splitting is a defense mechanism common in borderline personality disorder where the individual views people or situations as 'all good' or 'all bad,' failing to integrate positive and negative qualities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"分裂是边缘型人格障碍中常见的一种防御机制，个体将人或情况视为“全好”或“全坏”，无法整合积极和消极的品质。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client categorizes people into extreme opposites (good vs. bad), suspect splitting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者将人分为极端的对立面（好与坏）时，怀疑是分裂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":731,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.540","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.540.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.540.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client who is experiencing menopausal symptoms. Which strategies should the nurse recommend to manage hot flashes? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导一名出现更年期症状的患者。护士应推荐哪些缓解潮热的策略？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which strategies should the nurse recommend to manage hot flashes?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应推荐哪些缓解潮热的策略？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Drink hot beverages like herbal tea.","zh":"饮用热饮，如草本茶。"},{"id":"C","en":"Avoid spicy foods.","zh":"避免辛辣食物。"},{"id":"A","en":"Dress in layers.","zh":"层叠穿衣。"},{"id":"D","en":"Practice deep-breathing exercises.","zh":"练习深呼吸运动。"},{"id":"E","en":"Maintain a warm environment in the bedroom.","zh":"保持卧室环境温暖。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Managing hot flashes involves cooling strategies and trigger avoidance. Dressing in layers allows for quick adjustment. Spicy foods, caffeine, and alcohol are common triggers. Deep breathing can help reduce the frequency/severity. Hot beverages and warm environments (Option E) worsen hot flashes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"管理潮热涉及冷却策略和避免触发因素。层叠穿衣允许快速调节。辛辣食物、咖啡因和酒精是常见的触发因素。深呼吸有助于降低频率/严重程度。热饮和温暖的环境（选项 E）会加剧潮热。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on 'cooling' and 'calming' interventions for hot flashes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"针对潮热，关注“冷却”和“镇静”干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":732,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_22","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.541","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.541.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.541.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD) who performs repetitive handwashing. Which nursing interventions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名患有强迫症 (OCD) 并表现出重复洗手行为的患者。哪些护理干预措施是合适的？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing interventions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理干预措施是合适的？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Initially allow the client enough time to perform the ritual.","zh":"最初允许患者有足够的时间执行仪式行为。"},{"id":"E","en":"Encourage the client to discuss the reasons for the handwashing.","zh":"鼓励患者讨论洗手的原因。"},{"id":"B","en":"Physically prevent the client from washing their hands.","zh":"身体上阻止患者洗手。"},{"id":"C","en":"Identify triggers that increase the client's anxiety.","zh":"识别增加患者焦虑的诱因。"},{"id":"D","en":"Teach the client relaxation techniques.","zh":"教患者放松技巧。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Initially, the nurse should allow time for the ritual to prevent extreme anxiety. The goal is to gradually limit the time. Identifying triggers and teaching coping skills like relaxation address the underlying anxiety. Abruptly preventing the ritual can cause panic. Clients often know the ritual is irrational, so focusing on 'why' (Option E) is usually not helpful.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最初，护士应允许仪式行为的时间以防止极度焦虑。目标是逐渐限制时间。识别诱因和教授放松等应对技巧旨在解决潜在的焦虑。突然阻止仪式行为会导致恐慌。患者通常知道仪式行为是不合理的，因此关注“为什么”（选项 E）通常没有帮助。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In OCD, the ritual is a way to handle anxiety. Do not stop it abruptly; instead, address the anxiety and gradually reduce the time spent on rituals.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在强迫症中，仪式行为是处理焦虑的一种方式。不要突然停止它；相反，应解决焦虑并逐渐减少花在仪式行为上的时间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":733,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.542","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.542.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.542.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a client about breast self-examination (BSE). When is the best time for a menstruating woman to perform BSE?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名患者讲解乳房自检 (BSE)。有月经的女性进行乳房自检的最佳时间是什么时候？","terminalSentenceEn":"When is the best time for a menstruating woman to perform BSE?","terminalSentenceZh":"有月经的女性进行乳房自检的最佳时间是什么时候？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a client about breast self-examination (BSE).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名患者讲解乳房自检 (BSE)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"One week after the menstrual period begins.","zh":"月经开始后一周。"},{"id":"B","en":"During the first day of the menstrual period.","zh":"月经期的第一天。"},{"id":"C","en":"The day before the menstrual period is expected to start.","zh":"预计月经开始的前一天。"},{"id":"D","en":"On the day ovulation occurs.","zh":"排卵发生的那天。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The best time for BSE is 4 to 7 days after the menstrual period starts, when the breasts are least likely to be tender or swollen due to hormonal changes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乳房自检的最佳时间是月经开始后的 4 到 7 天，此时乳房最不容易因荷尔蒙变化而出现触痛或肿胀。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about when hormone levels (estrogen/progesterone) are lowest and breast tissue is most 'normal'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考什么时候荷尔蒙水平（雌激素/孕激素）最低，且乳腺组织最“正常”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":734,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.543","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.543.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.543.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with anorexia nervosa. Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名患有神经性厌食症的患者。护士应预期哪些临床表现？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预期哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Lanugo.","zh":"毳毛（细软毛发）。"},{"id":"D","en":"Cold intolerance.","zh":"畏寒。"},{"id":"E","en":"Hypertension.","zh":"高血压。"},{"id":"A","en":"Amenorrhea.","zh":"闭经。"},{"id":"C","en":"Tachycardia.","zh":"心动过速。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Anorexia nervosa leads to physiological compensation for starvation, including amenorrhea, growth of lanugo (fine hair) to provide warmth, and cold intolerance due to lack of body fat. Heart rate and blood pressure typically decrease (bradycardia and hypotension), making Options C and E incorrect.","rationaleCorrectZh":"神经性厌食症会导致饥饿的生理补偿，包括闭经、长出毳毛（细软毛发）以保暖以及由于缺乏脂肪而导致的畏寒。心率和血压通常会下降（心动过缓和低血压），因此，心动过速和高血压不是神经性厌食症的预期表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of the body 'slowing down' and trying to conserve energy and heat during starvation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象身体在饥饿期间“减慢速度”并试图保存能量和热量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":735,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchC_25","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.544","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.544.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.544.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[48,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,67],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning a community health program. Which concept best aligns with the foundational goals of Healthy People 2030?","fullStemZh":"护士正在计划一项社区健康计划。哪种理念最符合《健康中国 2030》（此处对应美国 Healthy People 2030）的基础目标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which concept best aligns with the foundational goals of Healthy People 2030?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种理念最符合《健康中国 2030》（此处对应美国 Healthy People 2030）的基础目标？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning a community health program.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在计划一项社区健康计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Limiting health education to healthcare facilities.","zh":"将健康教育局限在医疗机构内。"},{"id":"B","en":"Attaining health equity and eliminating disparities.","zh":"实现健康公平，消除差异。"},{"id":"A","en":"Focusing solely on the treatment of chronic diseases.","zh":"仅专注于慢性病的治疗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Prioritizing individual care over population health.","zh":"优先考虑个体护理而非人群健康。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Healthy People 2030 emphasizes social determinants of health, health equity, and health literacy as foundational to improving the health of all populations.","rationaleCorrectZh":"《健康人民 2030》(Healthy People 2030) 强调健康的社会决定因素、健康公平和健康素养，这是改善所有人群健康的基础。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for broad, inclusive goals related to public health and equity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找与公共卫生和公平相关的广泛、包容性的目标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":736,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.545","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.545.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.545.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who has been on prolonged bed rest. Which of the following findings should the nurse identify as a complication of immobility?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名长期卧床的患者。护士应将以下哪项发现识别为长期卧床的并发症？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings should the nurse identify as a complication of immobility?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将以下哪项发现识别为长期卧床的并发症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who has been on prolonged bed rest.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名长期卧床的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Increased joint flexibility.","zh":"关节灵活性增加。"},{"id":"C","en":"Increased cardiac output.","zh":"心输出量增加。"},{"id":"A","en":"Urinary retention.","zh":"尿潴留。"},{"id":"D","en":"Decreased serum calcium levels.","zh":"血清钙水平降低。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immobility leads to urinary stasis and can cause urinary retention because the lack of gravity makes it difficult for the kidneys to drain into the ureters and bladder.","rationaleCorrectZh":"长期卧床会导致尿液淤滞，并可能引起尿潴留，因为缺乏重力作用使肾脏难以排入输尿管和膀胱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the physiological effects of gravity and movement on each body system. Eliminate options that suggest positive outcomes of immobility.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考重力和运动对各身体系统的生理影响。排除暗示长期卧床有积极结果的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":737,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.546","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.546.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.546.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,54],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing the laboratory results of a client receiving heparin via continuous IV infusion for a pulmonary embolism. Which of the following results should the nurse report to the provider? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看一名因肺栓塞接受肝素持续静脉输注患者的实验室检查结果。护士应向医生汇报以下哪些结果？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following results should the nurse report to the provider?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应向医生汇报以下哪些结果？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Hematocrit of 32%.","zh":"红细胞压积 32%。"},{"id":"A","en":"aPTT of 90 seconds (control: 25-35 seconds).","zh":"aPTT 90 秒（对照组：25-35 秒）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hemoglobin of 14 g/dL.","zh":"血红蛋白 14 g/dL。"},{"id":"B","en":"Platelet count of 95 ×10³/µL.","zh":"血小板计数 95 ×10³/µL。"},{"id":"D","en":"INR of 1.1.","zh":"INR 1.1。"}],"correct":["A","B","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The aPTT is above the stated control-based range and should be managed according to the facility's heparin protocol. A platelet count of 95 ×10³/µL is reportable thrombocytopenia during heparin therapy and requires evaluation; HIT probability depends on the percentage fall, timing, thrombosis, and other causes rather than this absolute count alone. A hematocrit of 32% is low and may indicate occult bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该 aPTT 高于题目所给的对照范围，应按机构肝素方案处理。肝素治疗期间血小板计数 95 ×10³/µL 属于应报告的血小板减少，需要进一步评估；HIT 概率取决于血小板下降百分比、发生时间、血栓及其他原因，而不能仅凭这一绝对计数诊断。红细胞压积 32% 偏低，可能提示隐匿性出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify which lab test is used for heparin (aPTT). Recognize standard normal ranges for blood counts and the potential complications of anticoagulants.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定哪项实验室检查用于肝素（aPTT）。识别血细胞计数的标准正常范围以及抗凝剂的潜在并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":738,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.547","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.547.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.547.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an intermittent enteral feeding to a client via a nasogastric (NG) tube. Which of the following actions should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备通过鼻胃管 (NG) 为患者进行间歇性肠内营养。护士应首先采取以下哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取以下哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an intermittent enteral feeding to a client via a nasogastric (NG) tube.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备通过鼻胃管 (NG) 为患者进行间歇性肠内营养。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Flush the tube with 30 mL of water.","zh":"用 30 毫升水冲洗管道。"},{"id":"C","en":"Measure the gastric residual volume.","zh":"测量胃残留量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Verify the placement of the NG tube.","zh":"核实鼻胃管的位置。"},{"id":"B","en":"Warm the formula to room temperature.","zh":"将配方奶加热至室温。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority action before any intervention via an NG tube is to verify its placement to prevent aspiration into the lungs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在通过鼻胃管进行任何操作之前，首要行动是核实其位置，以防止误吸入肺部。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a question asks for the 'first' or 'priority' action, apply the safety framework. Ensuring the tube is in the right place prevents the most severe complication (aspiration).","testTakingStrategyZh":"当问题询问“首先”或“优先”行动时，应用安全框架。确保管道位于正确位置可防止最严重的并发症（误吸）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":739,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.548","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.548.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.548.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for a colonoscopy. Which of the following instructions should the nurse include in the pre-procedure teaching? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备让患者进行结肠镜检查。护士应在术前指导中包括以下哪些说明？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following instructions should the nurse include in the pre-procedure teaching?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在术前指导中包括以下哪些说明？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Drink the bowel preparation solution quickly to ensure effectiveness.","zh":"快速喝完肠道准备液以确保效果。"},{"id":"E","en":"A signed informed consent is required.","zh":"需要签署知情同意书。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid liquids that contain red or purple dye.","zh":"避免食用含有红色或紫色染料的液体。"},{"id":"D","en":"Follow the anesthesia fasting instructions; clear liquids may generally continue until 2 hours before sedation unless told otherwise.","zh":"遵循麻醉禁食指导；除非另有医嘱，通常可在镇静前2小时以内停止清流质。"},{"id":"A","en":"Follow the prescribed low-residue or clear-liquid diet during the day before the procedure.","zh":"在检查前一天遵循处方的低残渣或清流质饮食。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pre-colonoscopy teaching includes following the prescribed day-before low-residue or clear-liquid plan, avoiding restricted dyes, taking the bowel preparation exactly as directed, following individualized anesthesia fasting instructions, and confirming informed consent. Clear liquids may generally continue until 2 hours before sedation in otherwise healthy patients unless the procedural team gives different instructions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"结肠镜检查前指导包括遵循处方的检查前一天低残渣或清流质计划、避免受限制的染料、严格按医嘱服用肠道准备液、遵循个体化麻醉禁食指导并确认已获得知情同意。对于其他方面健康的患者，除非操作团队另有指示，通常可饮用清流质至镇静前2小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose instructions that follow the prescribed bowel-prep and anesthesia schedule rather than assuming a universal midnight or 6-to-8-hour cutoff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应选择遵循处方肠道准备和麻醉时间表的指导，不要假定所有患者都采用午夜或6至8小时的统一截止时间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":740,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.549","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.549.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.549.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing care for a client with a history of chronic constipation. Which of the following recommendations should the nurse provide to promote regular bowel movements?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名有慢性便秘病史的患者。护士应提供以下哪项建议以促进规律排便？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following recommendations should the nurse provide to promote regular bowel movements?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应提供以下哪项建议以促进规律排便？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing care for a client with a history of chronic constipation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名有慢性便秘病史的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Decrease daily fluid intake to 1 liter.","zh":"将每日液体摄入量减少至 1 升。"},{"id":"B","en":"Take a stimulant laxative every morning.","zh":"每天早晨服用刺激性泻药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase intake of high-fiber foods such as whole grains.","zh":"增加全谷物等高纤维食物的摄入。"},{"id":"D","en":"Limit physical activity to rest the bowel.","zh":"限制体力活动以让肠道休息。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Increasing fiber and fluid intake along with regular exercise are the primary non-pharmacological methods to manage constipation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"增加纤维和液体摄入以及规律锻炼是管理便秘的主要非药物方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the most natural and least invasive solution first. High fiber, high fluid, and high activity is the classic trio for constipation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先寻找最自然、侵入性最小的解决方案。高纤维、高液体和高活动量是治疗便秘的经典三要素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":741,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.550","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.550.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.550.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[176,198],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is 12 hours postoperative following abdominal surgery. Which of the following findings indicate the client may be developing a complication? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名腹部手术后 12 小时的患者。以下哪些发现表明患者可能正在出现并发症？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings indicate the client may be developing a complication?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些发现表明患者可能正在出现并发症？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Absent bowel sounds in all four quadrants.","zh":"四个象限均无肠鸣音。"},{"id":"E","en":"Reporting pain as 7 on a scale of 0 to 10.","zh":"疼痛评分为 7 分（0 到 10 分制）。"},{"id":"C","en":"Temperature of 98.6 °F (37.0 °C).","zh":"体温 98.6 °F (37.0 °C)。"},{"id":"A","en":"Urine output of 20 mL/hr.","zh":"每小时尿量 20 毫升。"},{"id":"D","en":"Sanguineous drainage on the dressing.","zh":"敷料上有血性渗出液。"}],"correct":["A","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Urine output should be at least 30 mL/hr; 20 mL/hr indicates poor renal perfusion or dehydration. Sanguineous (bright red) drainage 12 hours post-op might indicate active bleeding, as drainage should transition to serosanguineous. Absent bowel sounds are expected immediately after abdominal surgery (postoperative ileus).","rationaleCorrectZh":"尿量应至少为每小时 30 毫升；20 毫升/小时提示肾灌注不足或脱水。术后 12 小时出现血性（鲜红色）渗出液可能提示活动性出血，因为此时渗出液应转变为浆液血性。腹部手术后立即出现肠鸣音消失是预料之中的（术后肠梗阻）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between expected postoperative findings (like temporary ileus or pain) and those indicating serious physiological distress (low urine output, fresh bleeding).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分预料中的术后发现（如暂时性肠梗阻或疼痛）和提示严重生理窘迫的发现（低尿量、新鲜出血）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":742,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.551","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.551.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.551.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,31],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing foot care for a client who has diabetes mellitus. Which of the following actions should the nurse take?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名糖尿病患者进行足部护理。护士应采取以下哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions should the nurse take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应采取以下哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is performing foot care for a client who has diabetes mellitus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名糖尿病患者进行足部护理。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Dry the feet thoroughly, especially between the toes.","zh":"彻底擦干双脚，特别是趾间。"},{"id":"A","en":"Soak the feet in warm water for 20 minutes daily.","zh":"每天将脚浸泡在温水中 20 分钟。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply lotion between the toes to prevent cracking.","zh":"在趾间涂抹乳液以防止开裂。"},{"id":"C","en":"Trim toenails in a curved shape to prevent ingrown nails.","zh":"将脚趾甲剪成弧形以防止指甲内陷。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients with diabetes are at high risk for infection. Drying between the toes prevents moisture buildup, which can lead to fungal infections and skin breakdown.","rationaleCorrectZh":"糖尿病患者感染风险很高。擦干趾间可防止水分积聚，从而避免真菌感染和皮肤破损。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on infection prevention and skin integrity for the diabetic client. Avoid actions that cause skin softening or moisture retention in closed areas.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于糖尿病患者的感染预防和皮肤完整性。避免会导致皮肤变软或在封闭区域保留水分的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":743,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.552","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.552.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.552.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,36],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client for early signs of shock. Which of the following clinical manifestations should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估患者的休克早期征兆。护士应预见以下哪些临床表现？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following clinical manifestations should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见以下哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Decreased respiratory rate.","zh":"呼吸频率降低。"},{"id":"D","en":"Increased urine output.","zh":"尿量增加。"},{"id":"C","en":"Cool, clammy skin.","zh":"皮肤湿冷。"},{"id":"E","en":"Narrowing pulse pressure.","zh":"脉压差变窄。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increased heart rate.","zh":"心率加快。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Early signs of shock (compensatory stage) include tachycardia as the heart tries to maintain cardiac output, cool/clammy skin due to peripheral vasoconstriction, and a narrowing pulse pressure. Respiratory rate typically increases, and urine output decreases.","rationaleCorrectZh":"休克早期（代偿期）的征兆包括心脏试图维持心输出量引起的心动过速、由于周围血管收缩引起的皮肤湿冷以及脉压差变窄。呼吸频率通常会增加，尿量会减少。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the body's compensatory mechanisms when blood pressure starts to drop. The sympathetic nervous system ('fight or flight') is activated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考当血压开始下降时身体的代偿机制。交感神经系统（“战斗或逃跑”）被激活。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":744,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.553","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.553.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.553.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,33],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about sleep hygiene to improve the quality of sleep. Which of the following instructions should the nurse include?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向患者讲解睡眠卫生以提高睡眠质量。护士应包括以下哪项说明？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following instructions should the nurse include?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应包括以下哪项说明？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about sleep hygiene to improve the quality of sleep.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向患者讲解睡眠卫生以提高睡眠质量。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Take a 1-hour nap in the late afternoon.","zh":"在傍晚时分午睡 1 小时。"},{"id":"D","en":"Exercise vigorously right before bedtime to induce fatigue.","zh":"睡前进行剧烈运动以诱发疲劳。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use the bed only for sleep and sexual activity.","zh":"床仅用于睡眠和性活动。"},{"id":"A","en":"Drink a glass of red wine to help relax before sleep.","zh":"睡前喝一杯红酒以帮助放松。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stimulus control therapy involves using the bed only for sleep and sex to strengthen the mental association between the bed and sleep.","rationaleCorrectZh":"刺激控制疗法包括仅将床用于睡眠和性生活，以加强大脑对床和睡眠之间的联系。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for habits that promote a consistent routine and a quiet, non-stimulating environment before bed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找在睡前促进一致常规和安静、非刺激性环境的习惯。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":745,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.554","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.554.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.554.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[196,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,68],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with a central venous catheter (CVC). Which of the following actions should the nurse perform to reduce the risk of catheter-related bloodstream infections (CRBSI)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名留置中心静脉导管 (CVC) 的患者。护士应采取以下哪些行动以降低导管相关血流感染 (CRBSI) 的风险？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions should the nurse perform to reduce the risk of catheter-related bloodstream infections (CRBSI)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取以下哪些行动以降低导管相关血流感染 (CRBSI) 的风险？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Scrub the access port with an antiseptic for at least 15 seconds.","zh":"用防腐剂擦拭通路端口至少 15 秒。"},{"id":"C","en":"Change the transparent dressing every 24 hours.","zh":"每 24 小时更换一次透明敷料。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene before touching the catheter or dressing.","zh":"在接触导管或敷料前进行手部卫生。"},{"id":"E","en":"Apply topical antibiotic ointment to the insertion site daily.","zh":"每天在置管处涂抹局部抗生素软膏。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use sterile technique when changing the CVC dressing.","zh":"更换 CVC 敷料时使用无菌技术。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CRBSI prevention bundles include hand hygiene, scrubbing the hub (port) for 15+ seconds, and using maximal sterile barriers/sterile technique for dressing changes. Transparent dressings are usually changed every 7 days unless soiled. Antibiotic ointments are generally not recommended as they can promote fungal infections or resistance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防 CRBSI 的措施包包括手部卫生、擦拭接头（端口）15 秒以上，以及在更换敷料时使用最大无菌屏障/无菌技术。透明敷料通常每 7 天更换一次，除非弄脏。通常不建议使用抗生素软膏，因为它们可能促进真菌感染或产生耐药性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply 'bundle' concepts for infection prevention. Think about evidence-based guidelines for CVC care (CDC guidelines).","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用预防感染的“措施包”概念。思考关于 CVC 护理的循证指南（CDC 指南）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":746,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.555","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.555.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.555.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is discussing the use of herbal supplements with a client who is scheduled for elective surgery in two weeks. Which of the following herbal supplements should the nurse instruct the client to discontinue first?","fullStemZh":"护士正在与一名计划在两周后进行择期手术的患者讨论使用草本补充剂的问题。护士应指导患者首先停止使用以下哪种草本补充剂？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following herbal supplements should the nurse instruct the client to discontinue first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应指导患者首先停止使用以下哪种草本补充剂？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is discussing the use of herbal supplements with a client who is scheduled for elective surgery in two weeks.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在与一名计划在两周后进行择期手术的患者讨论使用草本补充剂的问题。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Glucosamine.","zh":"氨基葡萄糖。"},{"id":"B","en":"Echinacea.","zh":"紫锥菊。"},{"id":"A","en":"Valerian root.","zh":"缬草根。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ginkgo biloba.","zh":"银杏。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ginkgo biloba inhibits platelet aggregation and increases the risk of bleeding during and after surgery. It should be discontinued at least 2 weeks prior.","rationaleCorrectZh":"银杏会抑制血小板聚集，增加手术期间和术后的出血风险。应至少提前 2 周停用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the supplement that affects clotting or bleeding. Remember the 'Gs' that increase bleeding: Ginkgo, Garlic, Ginger, Ginseng.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别影响凝血或出血的补充剂。记住会增加出血风险的“G”字头草药：银杏 (Ginkgo)、大蒜 (Garlic)、生姜 (Ginger)、人参 (Ginseng)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":747,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.556","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.556.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.556.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[160,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,50],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who just returned from a cardiac catheterization via the femoral artery. Which of the following nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚完成经股动脉心脏导管插入术返回病房的患者。以下哪些护理行动是适当的？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些护理行动是适当的？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Maintain the client on bed rest with the affected leg straight.","zh":"保持患者卧床休息，患肢伸直。"},{"id":"C","en":"Encourage increased fluid intake.","zh":"鼓励增加液体摄入。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply a warm compress to the insertion site to reduce discomfort.","zh":"在置管处进行热敷以减轻不适。"},{"id":"E","en":"Monitor the insertion site for hematoma formation.","zh":"监测置管处是否有血肿形成。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check the pedal pulses of the affected extremity every 15 minutes for the first hour.","zh":"在第一个小时内，每 15 分钟检查一次患肢的足背动脉搏动。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Post-cardiac cath care involves immobilization of the affected leg to prevent bleeding, frequent neurovascular checks (pedal pulses), increasing fluids to flush out contrast dye, and monitoring for bleeding/hematoma. Heat is contraindicated as it can cause vasodilation and bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心脏导管术后护理包括使患肢制动以防止出血、频繁的神经血管检查（足背动脉搏动）、增加饮水以排出造影剂，以及监测出血/血肿。热敷是禁忌的，因为它会导致血管扩张和出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the risks associated with an arterial puncture (bleeding, clot) and the risks of the contrast dye (kidney damage).","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考与动脉穿刺相关的风险（出血、血块）以及造影剂的风险（肾损伤）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":748,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.557","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.557.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.557.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client who is receiving total parenteral nutrition (TPN). Which of the following lab values should the nurse monitor most closely for a potential complication of TPN?","fullStemZh":"护士正为一名接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN) 的患者制定护理计划。护士应最密切监测以下哪项实验室指标，以防 TPN 的潜在并发症？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following lab values should the nurse monitor most closely for a potential complication of TPN?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应最密切监测以下哪项实验室指标，以防 TPN 的潜在并发症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning care for a client who is receiving total parenteral nutrition (TPN).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正为一名接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN) 的患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Platelet count.","zh":"血小板计数。"},{"id":"C","en":"Blood glucose.","zh":"血糖。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hemoglobin.","zh":"血红蛋白。"},{"id":"D","en":"Serum sodium.","zh":"血清钠。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"TPN solutions are high in glucose (hypertonic), putting the client at risk for hyperglycemia. Sudden discontinuation can also cause hypoglycemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"TPN 溶液含有高浓度的葡萄糖（高渗），使患者面临高血糖风险。突然停药也可能引起低血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the composition of TPN. It is very high in sugar, which should lead you to prioritize glucose monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想 TPN 的成分。它的含糖量非常高，这应引导你优先考虑血糖监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":749,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.558","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.558.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.558.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,54],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for a client who has a prescription for airborne precautions. Which of the following pieces of personal protective equipment (PPE) should the nurse ensure are available? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备护理一名医嘱为空气传播预防措施的患者。护士应确保备好以下哪些个人防护装备 (PPE)？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following pieces of personal protective equipment (PPE) should the nurse ensure are available?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应确保备好以下哪些个人防护装备 (PPE)？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Face shield.","zh":"面屏。"},{"id":"C","en":"N95 respirator.","zh":"N95 呼吸面罩。"},{"id":"A","en":"Gown.","zh":"隔离衣。"},{"id":"B","en":"Gloves.","zh":"手套。"},{"id":"E","en":"Surgical mask.","zh":"外科口罩。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Airborne precautions require a private room with negative pressure and an N95 respirator. Standard precautions (gloves, gown) are still used if contact with body fluids is expected. A surgical mask is insufficient for airborne pathogens like tuberculosis or measles.","rationaleCorrectZh":"空气传播预防措施需要带有负压的私人房间和 N95 呼吸面罩。如果预计会接触体液，仍需使用标准预防措施（手套、隔离衣）。外科口罩不足以防御结核病或麻疹等空气传播病原体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between airborne, droplet, and contact precautions. Remember 'Airborne = N95'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分空气传播、飞沫和接触预防措施。记住“空气传播 = N95”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":750,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.559","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.559.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.559.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing oral hygiene for an unconscious client. Which of the following actions is the priority for safety?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名意识不清的患者进行口腔卫生。为了安全，哪项行动是优先考虑的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions is the priority for safety?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了安全，哪项行动是优先考虑的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing oral hygiene for an unconscious client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名意识不清的患者进行口腔卫生。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Position the client in a side-lying position.","zh":"将患者置于侧卧位。"},{"id":"B","en":"Apply petroleum jelly to the lips.","zh":"在嘴唇上涂抹凡士林。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use a soft-bristled toothbrush.","zh":"使用软毛牙刷。"},{"id":"D","en":"Clean the tongue with a padded tongue blade.","zh":"用带有垫子的压舌板清洁舌头。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The highest priority when performing oral care for an unconscious client is preventing aspiration. A side-lying position allows secretions to drain out of the mouth rather than into the trachea.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为意识不清的患者进行口腔护理时，最高优先级是预防误吸。侧卧位可以使分泌物从口腔流出，而不是流入气管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation). For an unconscious client, airway protection (preventing aspiration) is always the priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用 ABC 原则（气道、呼吸、循环）。对于意识不清的患者，保护气道（预防误吸）始终是优先事项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":751,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.560","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.560.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.560.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing the lab results for a client with chronic kidney disease (CKD). Which of the following findings should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看一名慢性肾脏病 (CKD) 患者的实验室检查结果。护士应预见以下哪些发现？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见以下哪些发现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hemoglobin 9.0 g/dL.","zh":"血红蛋白 9.0 g/dL。"},{"id":"B","en":"Serum calcium 11.5 mg/dL.","zh":"血清钙 11.5 mg/dL。"},{"id":"C","en":"Serum creatinine 3.2 mg/dL.","zh":"血清肌酐 3.2 mg/dL。"},{"id":"A","en":"Serum potassium 5.8 mEq/L.","zh":"血清钾 5.8 mEq/L。"},{"id":"E","en":"BUN 15 mg/dL.","zh":"BUN 15 mg/dL。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CKD leads to decreased excretion of potassium (hyperkalemia) and nitrogenous waste (elevated creatinine and BUN). Kidney damage also reduces erythropoietin production, leading to anemia (low hemoglobin). Calcium levels typically decrease (hypocalcemia) rather than increase.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CKD 会导致钾（高钾血症）和含氮废物（肌酐和 BUN 升高）的排出减少。肾脏受损还会减少促红细胞生成素的产生，导致贫血（血红蛋白低）。钙水平通常是降低（低钙血症）而非升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the metabolic and endocrine functions of the kidney. If it fails, substances usually excreted (K, Creatinine) build up, and substances usually produced (Erythropoietin) drop.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想肾脏的代谢和内分泌功能。如果肾衰竭，通常排出的物质（钾、肌酐）会堆积，而通常产生的物质（促红细胞生成素）会下降。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":752,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.561","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.561.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.561.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,32],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use a cane for the first time. The client has weakness in the left leg. Which instruction should the nurse include?","fullStemZh":"护士正在教患者第一次使用手杖。患者左腿无力。护士应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has weakness in the left leg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者左腿无力。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Advance the cane 18 inches in front of the feet.","zh":"将手杖向前移出脚前 18 英寸处。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold the cane in the left hand.","zh":"用左手持杖。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the cane in the right hand.","zh":"用右手持杖。"},{"id":"C","en":"Move the right leg forward first, then the cane.","zh":"先迈出右腿，然后迈出手杖。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A cane should be held on the 'strong' side (unaffected side) to provide better balance and support for the weak side.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手杖应握在“强健”侧（患侧的对侧），以便为患侧提供更好的平衡和支撑。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the mnemonic COAL (Cane Opposite Affected Leg). This ensures the client leans on the cane when weight-bearing on the weak leg.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用助记符 COAL（手杖位于患肢对侧）。这可以确保患者在患肢承重时依靠手杖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":753,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.562","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.562.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.562.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[163,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about a scheduled magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scan. Which of the following items should the nurse instruct the client to remove? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在讲解即将进行的核磁共振成像 (MRI) 扫描。护士应指导患者移除以下哪些物品？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following items should the nurse instruct the client to remove?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应指导患者移除以下哪些物品？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Wedding band (gold).","zh":"结婚戒指（金质）。"},{"id":"E","en":"Plastic ID bracelet.","zh":"塑料身份识别手环。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hairpins.","zh":"发夹。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hearing aids.","zh":"助听器。"},{"id":"D","en":"Transdermal medication patch.","zh":"透皮给药贴剂。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MRI uses powerful magnets and radiofrequency fields. Hearing aids and hairpins contain metal and can be damaged or become dangerous projectiles. Transdermal patches often have a metallic foil backing that can cause severe skin burns. All jewelry, including gold wedding bands, must be removed before an MRI because gold is conductive and can heat up under radiofrequency induction, causing burns and image artifacts.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MRI 使用强大的磁铁和射频场。助听器和发夹含有金属，可能会损坏或变成危险的飞行物。透皮贴剂通常具有金属箔背衬，可能会引起严重的皮肤灼伤。在进行 MRI 之前，必须取下所有首饰（包括金质结婚戒指），因为金是导电的，在射频感应下可能会发热，从而导致灼伤和图像伪影。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consider anything that is metallic or contains metallic parts. Do not forget 'hidden' metals like the foil in medication patches.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑任何金属的或含有金属零件的物品。不要忘记“隐藏”金属，如药物贴剂中的金属箔。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":754,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.563","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.563.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.563.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with a full-thickness burn. Which of the following dietary items should the nurse encourage to promote wound healing?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名全层烧伤患者。护士应鼓励摄入以下哪种饮食项目以促进伤口愈合？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following dietary items should the nurse encourage to promote wound healing?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应鼓励摄入以下哪种饮食项目以促进伤口愈合？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with a full-thickness burn.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名全层烧伤患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Fresh fruit salad.","zh":"新鲜水果沙拉。"},{"id":"C","en":"Gelatin dessert.","zh":"明胶甜点。"},{"id":"B","en":"White bread toast.","zh":"白面包吐司。"},{"id":"A","en":"Broiled chicken breast.","zh":"烤鸡胸肉。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Protein is essential for tissue repair and wound healing, especially in burn clients who are in a hypermetabolic state.","rationaleCorrectZh":"蛋白质对于组织修复和伤口愈合至关重要，特别是对于处于高代谢状态的烧伤患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think 'Protein = Repair'. Look for the option with the highest protein content.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考“蛋白质 = 修复”。寻找蛋白质含量最高的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":755,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.564","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.564.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.564.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client with fluid volume excess. Which of the following clinical manifestations should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名血容量过多的患者。护士应预见以下哪些临床表现？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following clinical manifestations should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预见以下哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Distended neck veins.","zh":"颈静脉怒张。"},{"id":"D","en":"Crackles in the lungs.","zh":"肺部湿啰音。"},{"id":"E","en":"Decreased central venous pressure (CVP).","zh":"中心静脉压 (CVP) 降低。"},{"id":"B","en":"Bounding pulse.","zh":"洪脉。"},{"id":"C","en":"Flat neck veins when supine.","zh":"仰卧时颈静脉扁平。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fluid volume excess (hypervolemia) leads to increased intravascular pressure, manifested as distended neck veins (JVD), a bounding pulse, and high CVP. As fluid backs up into the lungs, crackles are heard.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血容量过多（高血容量）导致血管内压力增高，表现为颈静脉怒张 (JVD)、洪脉和高 CVP。随着液体回流到肺部，可听到湿啰音。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about 'plumbing'. If there is too much water in the pipes, what happens to the pressure and the overflow points (neck, lungs)?","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考“管道”。如果管道里水太多，压力和溢出点（颈部、肺部）会发生什么？","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":756,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_21","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.565","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.565.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.565.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about a low-sodium diet. Which of the following food choices by the client indicates an understanding of the teaching?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向患者讲解低钠饮食。患者选择以下哪种食物表明其理解了教学内容？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following food choices by the client indicates an understanding of the teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者选择以下哪种食物表明其理解了教学内容？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client about a low-sodium diet.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向患者讲解低钠饮食。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Canned vegetable soup.","zh":"罐装蔬菜汤。"},{"id":"C","en":"Smoked ham sandwich.","zh":"熏火腿三明治。"},{"id":"D","en":"Dill pickles.","zh":"腌制酸黄瓜。"},{"id":"B","en":"Fresh grilled salmon.","zh":"新鲜烤三文鱼。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fresh foods like grilled salmon are naturally low in sodium compared to processed, canned, smoked, or pickled items.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与加工、罐装、熏制或腌制食品相比，新鲜食品（如烤三文鱼）天然含钠量较低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: Fresh is best for low sodium. Avoid anything in a can, smoked, or cured.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：低钠饮食中新鲜的最好。避免任何罐装、熏制或腌制的食品。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":757,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_22","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.566","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.566.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.566.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,179],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,51],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client for signs of deep vein thrombosis (DVT) following orthopedic surgery. Which of the following findings should the nurse report? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名骨科手术后患者是否有深静脉血栓 (DVT) 迹象。护士应汇报以下哪些发现？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings should the nurse report?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应汇报以下哪些发现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Pale, cool skin on the affected foot.","zh":"患足皮肤苍白、发凉。"},{"id":"A","en":"Unilateral leg swelling.","zh":"单侧腿部肿胀。"},{"id":"B","en":"Pain or tenderness in the calf.","zh":"小腿疼痛或压痛。"},{"id":"C","en":"Bilateral pitting edema in the ankles.","zh":"双侧踝部凹陷性水肿。"},{"id":"D","en":"Warmth and redness in the affected area.","zh":"患处发热和发红。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Classic signs of DVT include unilateral (one-sided) edema, pain/tenderness, and localized warmth/redness. Bilateral edema usually suggests heart failure or systemic fluid issues. Pale, cool skin suggests arterial insufficiency, not venous thrombosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DVT 的典型迹象包括单侧（一侧）水肿、疼痛/压痛以及局部发热/发红。双侧水肿通常提示心力衰竭或全身性液体问题。皮肤苍白、发凉提示动脉功能不全，而非静脉血栓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for unilateral symptoms for DVT. Venous issues cause 'wet, red, warm' symptoms, while arterial issues cause 'dry, pale, cold' symptoms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找 DVT 的单侧症状。静脉问题引起“湿、红、热”的症状，而动脉问题引起“干、白、冷”的症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":758,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_23","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.567","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.567.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.567.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is experiencing severe pain. Which of the following non-pharmacological interventions is an example of cutaneous stimulation?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名正经历剧烈疼痛的患者。以下哪项非药物干预是皮肤刺激的例子？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following non-pharmacological interventions is an example of cutaneous stimulation?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项非药物干预是皮肤刺激的例子？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is experiencing severe pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名正经历剧烈疼痛的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Listening to music.","zh":"听音乐。"},{"id":"D","en":"Guided imagery.","zh":"引导想象。"},{"id":"A","en":"Application of a cold pack.","zh":"应用冰袋。"},{"id":"B","en":"Focused breathing exercises.","zh":"专注呼吸练习。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cutaneous stimulation involves methods like massage, heat/cold application, and TENS that stimulate the skin to interfere with pain signals (Gate Control Theory).","rationaleCorrectZh":"皮肤刺激包括按摩、热敷/冷敷和 TENS 等刺激皮肤以干扰疼痛信号的方法（闸门控制理论）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Define the word 'cutaneous' (skin). Select the option that involves physical contact with the skin.","testTakingStrategyZh":"定义“cutaneous”（皮肤的）一词。选择涉及与皮肤物理接触的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":759,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_24","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.568","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.568.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.568.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is receiving a blood transfusion. Which of the following findings indicate a possible hemolytic transfusion reaction? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名接受输血的患者。以下哪些发现表明可能发生了溶血性输血反应？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings indicate a possible hemolytic transfusion reaction?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些发现表明可能发生了溶血性输血反应？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Fever and chills.","zh":"发热和寒战。"},{"id":"A","en":"Low back pain.","zh":"腰背部疼痛。"},{"id":"D","en":"Distended neck veins.","zh":"颈静脉怒张。"},{"id":"E","en":"Tachycardia.","zh":"心动过速。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apprehension.","zh":"恐惧感。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acute hemolytic reaction signs include low back pain (due to hemoglobin in the kidneys), fever, chills, tachycardia, hypotension, and apprehension. JVD is a sign of fluid overload (TACO), not hemolysis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性溶血反应的迹象包括腰背部疼痛（由于肾脏中的血红蛋白）、发热、寒战、心动过速、低血压和恐惧感。颈静脉怒张是循环负荷过重 (TACO) 的体征，而非溶血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between hemolytic reaction (destruction of RBCs) and fluid overload (too much volume). Hemolytic signs focus on systemic inflammation and kidney impact.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分溶血反应（红细胞破坏）和循环负荷过重（容量过多）。溶血迹象侧重于全身炎症和肾脏影响。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":760,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"trad_batchD_25","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.569","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.569.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.569.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is helping a client with a history of GERD (Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease) choose a snack. Which of the following choices should the nurse recommend?","fullStemZh":"护士正在帮助一名有胃食管反流病 (GERD) 病史的患者选择零食。护士应推荐以下哪种选择？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following choices should the nurse recommend?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应推荐以下哪种选择？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is helping a client with a history of GERD (Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease) choose a snack.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在帮助一名有胃食管反流病 (GERD) 病史的患者选择零食。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Fresh apple slices.","zh":"新鲜苹果片。"},{"id":"D","en":"Peppermint tea and a brownie.","zh":"薄荷茶和布朗尼蛋糕。"},{"id":"C","en":"Potato chips.","zh":"薯片。"},{"id":"A","en":"Chocolate chip cookie.","zh":"巧克力片饼干。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Non-citrus fruits like apples are generally well-tolerated. Chocolate, peppermint, and high-fat foods (chips) decrease lower esophageal sphincter pressure and worsen GERD.","rationaleCorrectZh":"苹果等非柑橘类水果通常耐受性良好。巧克力、薄荷和高脂肪食物（薯片）会降低食管下括约肌压力，加重 GERD。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify foods that weaken the lower esophageal sphincter (LES). Avoid fat, chocolate, peppermint, caffeine, and acidic items.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别会削弱食管下括约肌 (LES) 的食物。避免脂肪、巧克力、薄荷、咖啡因和酸性物品。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":761,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_1","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.570","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.570.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.570.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,39],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client with right-sided weakness how to use a single-ended cane. Which instruction should the nurse include in the teaching?","fullStemZh":"护士正在教一名右侧肢体无力的患者如何使用单头手杖。护士在教学中应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include in the teaching?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在教学中应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client with right-sided weakness how to use a single-ended cane.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教一名右侧肢体无力的患者如何使用单头手杖。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Move the cane forward 15 to 20 inches with each step.","zh":"每一步将手杖向前移动15至20英寸。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the cane in the left hand.","zh":"左手持杖。"},{"id":"C","en":"Move the left leg forward first, then the cane.","zh":"先向前迈左腿，然后移动手杖。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold the cane in the right hand.","zh":"右手持杖。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The cane should be held on the stronger side (the left side in this case) to provide maximum support and stability. It should move forward simultaneously with the weaker leg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手杖应握在健侧（本例中为左侧），以提供最大的支撑和稳定性。手杖应与患侧腿同时向前移动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the mnemonic 'COAL': Cane Opposite Affected Leg.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住缩写‘COAL’：手杖位于患侧腿的对侧。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":762,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_2","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.571","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.571.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.571.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[149,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing dietary teaching to a client with chronic constipation. Which food choices should the nurse recommend to increase fiber intake? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患有慢性便秘的患者提供饮食指导。护士应推荐哪些食物选择以增加纤维摄入量？（选择所有适用项。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which food choices should the nurse recommend to increase fiber intake?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应推荐哪些食物选择以增加纤维摄入量？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Brown rice","zh":"糙米"},{"id":"B","en":"Lentils","zh":"小扁豆"},{"id":"A","en":"White bread","zh":"白面包"},{"id":"C","en":"Pears with skin","zh":"带皮梨"},{"id":"E","en":"Cheese","zh":"奶酪"},{"id":"F","en":"Cooked broccoli","zh":"煮熟的西兰花"}],"correct":["B","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lentils, pears (especially with skin), brown rice, and broccoli are all high-fiber foods that help promote bowel regularity. Fiber adds bulk to the stool and facilitates peristalsis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"小扁豆、梨（尤其是带皮的）、糙米和西兰花都是高纤维食物，有助于促进肠道规律性。纤维可以增加粪便体积并促进肠蠕动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify foods that are 'whole' or 'unrefined' as they typically contain more fiber.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别‘完整’或‘未经精制’的食物，因为它们通常含有更多纤维。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":763,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_3","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.572","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.572.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.572.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing a complete bed bath for a client who is bedbound. In what order should the nurse wash the following body parts?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名卧床患者进行完整的床上擦浴。护士应按什么顺序清洗以下身体部位？","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse wash the following body parts?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序清洗以下身体部位？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is performing a complete bed bath for a client who is bedbound.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名卧床患者进行完整的床上擦浴。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Perineal area","zh":"会阴部"},{"id":"D","en":"Chest and abdomen","zh":"胸部和腹部"},{"id":"A","en":"Arms and hands","zh":"手臂和手"},{"id":"B","en":"Face and eyes","zh":"脸部和眼睛"},{"id":"C","en":"Legs and feet","zh":"腿和脚"}],"correct":["B","A","D","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The standard sequence for a bed bath is to move from the cleanest to the most soiled areas. The face is washed first (starting with the eyes), followed by the upper extremities, trunk, lower extremities, and finally the perineal area.","rationaleCorrectZh":"床上擦浴的标准顺序是从最清洁的部位到最脏的部位。先洗脸（从眼睛开始），然后是上肢、躯干、下肢，最后是会阴部。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the principle of 'clean to dirty' to prevent cross-contamination.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用‘从洁到污’的原则，防止交叉污染。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":764,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_4","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.573","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.573.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.573.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[215,286],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,102],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is calculating the total fluid intake in milliliters (mL) for a client over an 8-hour shift. The client consumed 6 oz of juice, 1 cup of coffee, 4 oz of gelatin, and received 500 mL of continuous IV fluids. Calculate the total intake for the shift. (1 oz = 30 mL; 1 cup = 8 oz).","fullStemZh":"护士正在计算一名患者在8小时班次内的总入液量（毫升，mL）。患者摄入了6盎司果汁、1杯咖啡、4盎司明胶，并接受了500毫升的持续静脉输液。计算该班次的总入液量。（1盎司 = 30毫升；1杯 = 8盎司）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the total intake for the shift. (1 oz = 30 mL; 1 cup = 8 oz).","terminalSentenceZh":"1盎司 = 30毫升；1杯 = 8盎司）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client consumed 6 oz of juice, 1 cup of coffee, 4 oz of gelatin, and received 500 mL of continuous IV fluids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算该班次的总入液量。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["1040"],"numeric":{"value":1040,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, convert all measurements to mL: 6 oz juice * 30 mL/oz = 180 mL. 1 cup coffee = 8 oz * 30 mL/oz = 240 mL. 4 oz gelatin * 30 mL/oz = 120 mL. Add the IV fluids: 180 + 240 + 120 + 500 = 1040 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，将所有测量值转换为毫升：6盎司果汁 * 30毫升/盎司 = 180毫升。1杯咖啡 = 8盎司 * 30毫升/盎司 = 240毫升。4盎司明胶 * 30毫升/盎司 = 120毫升。加上静脉输液：180 + 240 + 120 + 500 = 1040毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Carefully convert each item to the same unit (mL) before adding them together.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在相加之前，仔细将每个项目转换为相同的单位（毫升）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":765,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_5","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.574","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.574.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.574.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,59],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is developing a plan of care for an older adult client at high risk for pressure injuries. For each nursing action, indicate whether it is appropriate or inappropriate for preventing skin breakdown.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名压疮高风险的高龄患者制定护理计划。对于每一项护理措施，请指出其对于预防皮肤受损是‘合适’还是‘不合适’。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing action, indicate whether it is appropriate or inappropriate for preventing skin breakdown.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每一项护理措施，请指出其对于预防皮肤受损是‘合适’还是‘不合适’。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is developing a plan of care for an older adult client at high risk for pressure injuries.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名压疮高风险的高龄患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Apply a donut-shaped cushion when the client is sitting in a chair.","zh":"患者坐在椅子上时使用环形（甜甜圈状）坐垫。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Reposition the client every 2 hours while bedbound.","zh":"对于卧床患者，每2小时更换一次体位。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Massage reddened bony prominences to improve circulation.","zh":"按摩发红的骨突处以改善血液循环。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Limit head-of-bed elevation to 30 degrees or less.","zh":"将床头抬高角度限制在30度或更低。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Apply moisture-barrier cream to the perineum after incontinence episodes.","zh":"在发生失禁后，在会阴部涂抹防潮乳膏。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"},{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Repositioning, limiting HOB elevation (to reduce shear), and using moisture barriers are standard prevention steps. Donut cushions and massaging bony prominences are contraindicated as they can actually increase tissue damage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"更换体位、限制床头抬高角度（以减少剪切力）以及使用防潮保护措施是标准的预防步骤。环形坐垫和按摩骨突处是禁忌的，因为它们实际上会加重组织损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on evidence-based practices for pressure injury prevention; avoid outdated practices like massaging bony prominences.","testTakingStrategyZh":"专注于循证医学中的压疮预防措施；避免使用过时的做法，如按摩骨突处。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":766,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.575","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.575.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.575.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing routine care for a client with an indwelling urinary catheter.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名留置导尿管的患者进行常规护理。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse is performing routine care for a client with an indwelling urinary catheter.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名留置导尿管的患者进行常规护理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To minimize the risk of a catheter-associated urinary tract infection (CAUTI), the nurse should ensure the drainage bag is kept {{1}} and perform perineal care at least twice daily using {{2}}.","zh":"为了最大限度地降低导尿管相关尿路感染（CAUTI）的风险，护士应确保引流袋保持在 {{1}}，并每天至少使用 {{2}} 进行两次会阴护理。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"at the level of the bladder","zh":"与膀胱持平"},{"id":"o2","en":"below the level of the bladder","zh":"低于膀胱水平"},{"id":"o3","en":"above the level of the bladder","zh":"高于膀胱水平"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"sterile saline only","zh":"仅使用无菌生理盐水"},{"id":"o2","en":"soap and water","zh":"肥皂和水"},{"id":"o1","en":"povidone-iodine solution","zh":"聚维酮碘溶液"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The drainage bag must remain below the bladder to prevent the backflow of urine, which can introduce bacteria into the bladder. Routine perineal care with mild soap and water is recommended; antiseptic solutions are not necessary and may cause irritation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"引流袋必须保持在膀胱以下，以防止尿液回流，尿液回流会将细菌带入膀胱。推荐使用温和的肥皂和水进行常规会阴护理；不需要使用防腐溶液，且可能引起刺激。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify interventions that promote gravity drainage and maintain hygiene without using harsh chemicals.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别那些能促进重力引流并在不使用刺激性化学品的情况下保持卫生的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":767,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_7","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.576","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.576.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.576.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,37],"fullStemEn":"A client in a long-term care facility reports difficulty falling asleep at night. Which non-pharmacological intervention should the nurse implement first?","fullStemZh":"长期护理机构的一名患者报告晚上入睡困难。护士应首先实施哪项非药物干预措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which non-pharmacological intervention should the nurse implement first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先实施哪项非药物干预措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in a long-term care facility reports difficulty falling asleep at night.","penultimateSentenceZh":"长期护理机构的一名患者报告晚上入睡困难。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Request a prescription for a hypnotic medication.","zh":"请求开具催眠药物处方。"},{"id":"A","en":"Encourage the client to take a vigorous walk before bedtime.","zh":"鼓励患者在睡前进行剧烈散步。"},{"id":"B","en":"Establish a consistent bedtime routine for the client.","zh":"为患者建立规律的入睡习惯。"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide a caffeinated beverage to relax the client.","zh":"提供含咖啡因的饮料以使患者放松。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Establishing a consistent routine helps regulate the body's internal clock and promotes better sleep hygiene. It is a prioritized non-pharmacological intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建立规律的作息有助于调节人体的生物钟并促进更好的睡眠卫生。这是一项优先考虑的非药物干预措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When multiple options seem helpful, prioritize the least invasive and most foundational care intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个选项看起来都有帮助时，优先选择侵入性最小且最基础的护理干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client in a long-term care facility reports difficulty falling asleep at night.","controlSentenceZh":"长期护理机构的一名患者报告晚上入睡困难。"}
{"queueIndex":768,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_8","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.577","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.577.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.577.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[220,242],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,73],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client with post-stroke dysphagia. The individualized swallowing plan identifies unilateral oral weakness and recommends chin-down swallowing. Which actions should the nurse take during mealtime? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名脑卒中后吞咽困难患者。个体化吞咽计划指出患者存在单侧口腔无力，并建议采用低头吞咽。护士在进餐期间应采取哪些行动？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take during mealtime?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在进餐期间应采取哪些行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Provide thin liquids through a straw without confirming they are permitted by the swallowing plan.","zh":"未确认吞咽计划是否允许，就通过吸管提供稀薄液体。"},{"id":"D","en":"Maintain the client in an upright, 90-degree position during meals.","zh":"进餐时保持患者处于90度垂直坐位。"},{"id":"A","en":"Cue the chin-down posture prescribed in the swallowing plan.","zh":"提示患者采用吞咽计划规定的低头姿势。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place food on the stronger side of the mouth as directed for unilateral oral weakness.","zh":"针对单侧口腔无力，按计划将食物放在口腔较强侧。"},{"id":"E","en":"Check for pocketing of food in the cheeks after the meal.","zh":"餐后检查脸颊内是否有食物残留（藏食）。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Follow the individualized swallowing plan: cue the prescribed chin-down posture, place food on the stronger side for unilateral oral weakness, maintain upright positioning, and check for pocketing. Straw use and liquid consistency must be confirmed from the assessment rather than assumed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应遵循个体化吞咽计划：提示患者采用医嘱规定的低头姿势；针对单侧口腔无力将食物放在较强侧；保持直立；并检查藏食。是否使用吸管及液体稠度必须依据评估确认，不能自行假定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For post-stroke dysphagia, prioritize screening results and the individualized swallowing plan rather than applying one posture, texture, or utensil rule to every client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于脑卒中后吞咽困难，应优先遵循筛查结果和个体化吞咽计划，而不是对所有患者统一使用某种姿势、食物质地或餐具规则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take during mealtime?","controlSentenceZh":"护士在进餐期间应采取哪些行动？"}
{"queueIndex":769,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_9","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.578","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.578.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.578.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to transfer a client with left-sided weakness from the bed to a wheelchair. Arrange the steps in the correct order for a safe transfer.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备将一名左侧肢体无力的患者从床上转移到轮椅上。请按正确顺序排列安全转移的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the steps in the correct order for a safe transfer.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列安全转移的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to transfer a client with left-sided weakness from the bed to a wheelchair.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备将一名左侧肢体无力的患者从床上转移到轮椅上。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Position the wheelchair on the client's right (stronger) side.","zh":"将轮椅放在患者的右侧（健侧）。"},{"id":"E","en":"Ensure the client is wearing non-skid footwear.","zh":"确保患者穿着防滑鞋。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply a gait belt and assist the client to stand and pivot toward the chair.","zh":"系好移位腰带，协助患者站立并向椅子方向转动身体。"},{"id":"B","en":"Help the client sit on the edge of the bed and dangle their feet.","zh":"帮助患者坐在床边，双脚悬空。"},{"id":"C","en":"Securely lock the wheels of both the bed and the wheelchair.","zh":"锁紧床和轮椅的轮子。"}],"correct":["C","E","A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety is the priority. Locking wheels and providing non-skid footwear (E) come first. The wheelchair should be on the stronger side. Then the client sits up and is transferred using a gait belt.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全是首要任务。首先是锁紧轮子 和提供防滑鞋 (E)。轮椅应放在健侧。然后患者坐起，并使用移位腰带进行转移。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always prioritize environmental safety (locking wheels) before moving the client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在移动患者之前，始终优先考虑环境安全（如锁紧轮子）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":770,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch1_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.579","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.579.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.579.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"A client is being positioned in bed following a total hip arthroplasty (posterior approach).","fullStemZh":"一名全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）后的患者正在床上进行体位摆放。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client is being positioned in bed following a total hip arthroplasty (posterior approach).","terminalSentenceZh":"一名全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）后的患者正在床上进行体位摆放。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To prevent dislocation of the prosthesis, the nurse should place an abduction pillow between the client's legs to prevent {{1}} and ensure the client does not {{2}}.","zh":"为了防止假体脱位，护士应在患者双腿之间放置外展枕以防止 {{1}}，并确保患者不 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"external rotation","zh":"外旋"},{"id":"o3","en":"hyperextension","zh":"过伸"},{"id":"o1","en":"adduction","zh":"内收"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"flex the hip more than 90 degrees","zh":"髋关节屈曲超过90度"},{"id":"o3","en":"keep the head of the bed flat","zh":"保持床头平放"},{"id":"o2","en":"extend the knee fully","zh":"将膝盖完全伸直"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Following a posterior approach hip replacement, adduction (crossing the legs) and hip flexion beyond 90 degrees are major risks for dislocation. An abduction pillow keeps the hip in a safe alignment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）后，内收（双腿交叉）和髋关节屈曲超过90度是脱位的主要风险。外展枕使髋关节保持在安全的位置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'posterior hip precautions' with avoiding internal rotation, adduction, and extreme flexion.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将‘髋关节后侧入路注意事项’与避免内旋、内收和过度屈曲联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":771,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch2_5","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.580","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.580.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.580.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,48],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a group of clients with various musculoskeletal conditions. For each condition, indicate whether heat therapy or cold therapy is the appropriate intervention.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一组患有各种肌肉骨骼疾病的患者。对于每种情况，请指出热疗或冷疗是否为合适的干预措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each condition, indicate whether heat therapy or cold therapy is the appropriate intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每种情况，请指出热疗或冷疗是否为合适的干预措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a group of clients with various musculoskeletal conditions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一组患有各种肌肉骨骼疾病的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Acute ankle sprain (within 24 hours)","zh":"急性踝关节扭伤（24小时内）"},{"id":"r2","en":"Chronic osteoarthritis pain","zh":"慢性骨关节炎疼痛"},{"id":"r3","en":"Active localized inflammation/edema","zh":"活动性局部炎症/水肿"},{"id":"r4","en":"Lower back muscle spasm","zh":"腰部肌肉痉挛"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Cold Therapy","zh":"冷疗"},{"id":"c1","en":"Heat Therapy","zh":"热疗"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cold therapy is used for acute injuries (sprains) and inflammation to cause vasoconstriction and reduce edema. Heat therapy is used for chronic pain and muscle spasms to improve circulation and relax tissues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"冷疗用于急性损伤（扭伤）和炎症，引起血管收缩并减少水肿。热疗用于慢性疼痛和肌肉痉挛，以改善循环并放松组织。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think: Cold for 'New' (acute), Heat for 'Old' (chronic) or 'Tight' (spasms).","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考：冷疗用于“新”（急性），热疗用于“旧”（慢性）或“紧”（痉挛）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":772,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch2_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.581","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.581.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.581.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,25],"fullStemEn":"A client reports difficulty falling asleep at night. The nurse provides education on sleep hygiene.","fullStemZh":"一名患者报告晚上入睡困难。护士提供睡眠卫生的教育。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse provides education on sleep hygiene.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士提供睡眠卫生的教育。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client reports difficulty falling asleep at night.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者报告晚上入睡困难。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should advise the client to {{1}} and {{2}} to promote a better sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"护士应建议患者 {{1}} 并且 {{2}}，以促进更好的睡眠-觉醒周期。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"maintain a consistent bedtime","zh":"保持固定的上床时间"},{"id":"o2","en":"take a long nap in the afternoon","zh":"下午睡个长午觉"},{"id":"o3","en":"watch television in bed","zh":"在床上看电视"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"consume a large meal before bed","zh":"睡前大吃一顿"},{"id":"o2","en":"exercise vigorously within an hour of bedtime","zh":"睡前一小时内剧烈运动"},{"id":"o3","en":"avoid caffeine in the evening","zh":"晚上避免摄入咖啡因"}],"correct":"o3"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Consistency in bedtime helps regulate the circadian rhythm. Avoiding stimulants like caffeine in the evening prevents interference with sleep onset.","rationaleCorrectZh":"固定的上床时间有助于调节昼夜节律。晚上避免摄入咖啡因等刺激物可防止干扰入睡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for options that support a regular routine and eliminate environmental or chemical stimulants.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找支持规律作息的选项，并排除环境或化学刺激物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":773,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch2_7","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.582","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.582.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.582.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,35],"fullStemEn":"A client with urge incontinence is participating in a bladder retraining program. Which instruction should the nurse provide?","fullStemZh":"一名患有急迫性尿失禁的患者正在参加膀胱再训练计划。护士应提供哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse provide?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应提供哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with urge incontinence is participating in a bladder retraining program.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有急迫性尿失禁的患者正在参加膀胱再训练计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Wear an adult diaper at all times to prevent leaks.","zh":"始终穿着成人纸尿裤以防止渗漏。"},{"id":"B","en":"Void immediately whenever the urge is felt.","zh":"一旦感到尿意立即排尿。"},{"id":"C","en":"Limit fluid intake to less than 1,000 mL per day.","zh":"将每日液体摄入量限制在1,000毫升以下。"},{"id":"D","en":"Increase the intervals between voiding by small increments.","zh":"以较小的增量增加排尿间隔。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bladder retraining involves gradually increasing the time between voiding to increase bladder capacity and control. The goal is to reach an interval of every 3 to 4 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"膀胱再训练包括逐渐增加排尿间隔，以增加膀胱容量和控制力。目标是达到每3至4小时排尿一次。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The keyword 'training' implies progressive improvement and control, not immediate reaction or restriction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关键词“训练”意味着渐进式的改进和控制，而不是立即反应或限制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":774,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch2_8","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.583","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.583.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.583.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,138],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,35],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is teaching a client with diabetes mellitus about foot care. Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教导一名糖尿病患者关于足部护理。护士应包括哪些指导？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些指导？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Soak feet for 30 minutes daily to soften calluses.","zh":"每天泡脚30分钟以软化老茧。"},{"id":"A","en":"Wash feet daily with warm water and mild soap.","zh":"每天用温水和温和的肥皂洗脚。"},{"id":"C","en":"Dry thoroughly between the toes.","zh":"彻底擦干趾缝。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply lotion between the toes to prevent cracking.","zh":"在趾缝间涂抹润肤乳以防止开裂。"},{"id":"E","en":"Avoid walking barefoot, even indoors.","zh":"避免赤脚走路，即使在室内。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Daily washing and drying prevent infection. Walking barefoot (E) increases risk of injury, which is dangerous in diabetic patients due to poor healing. Soaking and applying lotion between toes increase the risk of skin breakdown and fungal infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每日清洗 和擦干 可防止感染。赤脚走路 (E) 会增加受伤风险，由于糖尿病患者愈合能力差，这非常危险。浸泡 和在趾缝间涂抹乳液 会增加皮肤破损和真菌感染的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that in diabetes, excess moisture (soaking, lotion between toes) is an enemy to skin integrity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住在糖尿病中，过多的水分（浸泡、趾缝间的乳液）是皮肤完整性的敌人。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":775,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_bcc_batch2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.584","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.584.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.584.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,32],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer a continuous enteral tube feeding. Which action is the priority for the nurse to perform to ensure client safety?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备进行连续肠内管饲。护士优先执行哪项操作以确保患者安全？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority for the nurse to perform to ensure client safety?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士优先执行哪项操作以确保患者安全？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer a continuous enteral tube feeding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备进行连续肠内管饲。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Verify the placement of the feeding tube.","zh":"验证喂食管的位置。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check for gastric residual volume.","zh":"检查胃残留量。"},{"id":"A","en":"Flush the tube with 30 mL of water.","zh":"用30毫升水冲洗管路。"},{"id":"D","en":"Warm the formula to room temperature.","zh":"将配方奶加热至室温。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Verifying tube placement is the priority to prevent aspiration into the lungs. This is typically done initially via X-ray and subsequently by checking pH or measuring tube length.","rationaleCorrectZh":"验证插管位置是优先事项，以防止误吸进入肺部。这通常最初通过X射线完成，随后通过检查pH值或测量导管长度完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In nursing priorities, 'Placement' and 'Airway' (preventing aspiration) usually come first in enteral care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在护理优先事项中，“位置”和“气道”（防止误吸）在肠内护理中通常排在第一位。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":776,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.585","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.585.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.585.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,28],"fullStemEn":"Which interventions should the nurse implement for a client who is at high risk for falls? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应为跌倒高危患者实施哪些干预措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse implement for a client who is at high risk for falls?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应为跌倒高危患者实施哪些干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Keep all four side rails in the up position.","zh":"将四个床栏全部拉起。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure the call light is within reach.","zh":"确保呼叫灯在触手可及的范围内。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the bed in the lowest position.","zh":"将床位调至最低位置。"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide non-skid footwear.","zh":"提供防滑鞋。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep the room cluttered to encourage focus.","zh":"保持房间杂乱以鼓励专注。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use a bed alarm system.","zh":"使用离床报警系统。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lowering the bed, ensuring call light access, providing non-skid footwear, and using bed alarms are standard fall prevention strategies. Raising all four side rails is considered a restraint.","rationaleCorrectZh":"降低床位、确保呼叫灯可用、提供防滑鞋以及使用离床报警器是标准的跌倒预防策略。拉起所有四个床栏被视为约束。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on safety and avoiding restrictive measures that could be classified as restraints.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注安全性，避免可能被归类为约束的限制性措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":777,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.586","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.586.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.586.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is identifying the appropriate transmission-based precautions for several clients. Match each infectious condition with the correct precaution type.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为几位患者确定适当的传播预防措施。将每种感染情况与正确的预防措施类型相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each infectious condition with the correct precaution type.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种感染情况与正确的预防措施类型相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is identifying the appropriate transmission-based precautions for several clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为几位患者确定适当的传播预防措施。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Vancomycin-resistant enterococci (VRE)","zh":"耐万古霉素肠球菌 (VRE)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Influenza","zh":"流行性感冒"},{"id":"r3","en":"Disseminated Herpes Zoster","zh":"播散性带状疱疹"},{"id":"r4","en":"Clostridioides difficile","zh":"艰难梭菌"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Droplet Precautions","zh":"飞沫预防措施"},{"id":"c1","en":"Contact Precautions","zh":"接触预防措施"},{"id":"c3","en":"Airborne + Contact Precautions","zh":"空气传播 + 接触预防措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"VRE and C. diff require contact precautions. Influenza requires droplet precautions. Disseminated Herpes Zoster requires both airborne and contact precautions until lesions are crusted over.","rationaleCorrectZh":"VRE 和艰难梭菌需要接触预防措施。流感需要飞沫预防措施。播散性带状疱疹需要空气传播和接触预防措施，直到皮损结痂。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the transmission routes for each pathogen. Note that disseminated conditions often require more stringent precautions than localized ones.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想每种病原体的传播途径。请注意，播散性疾病通常比局限性疾病需要更严格的预防措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":778,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.587","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.587.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.587.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers a large spill of an unidentified liquid chemical in the utility room.","fullStemZh":"护士在杂物间发现大量不明液体化学品泄漏。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers a large spill of an unidentified liquid chemical in the utility room.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在杂物间发现大量不明液体化学品泄漏。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To ensure safety, the nurse should immediately refer to the {{1}} and follow the specific steps for {{2}}.","zh":"为了确保安全，护士应立即查阅 {{1}} 并遵循 {{2}} 的具体步骤。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Hospital's Operating Budget","zh":"医院运营预算"},{"id":"o1","en":"Material Safety Data Sheet (MSDS)","zh":"物质安全数据表 (MSDS)"},{"id":"o3","en":"Patient's Medical Record","zh":"患者病历"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"incineration","zh":"焚烧"},{"id":"o2","en":"containment and cleanup","zh":"遏制和清理"},{"id":"o1","en":"dilution with water","zh":"用水稀释"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MSDS provides critical information about chemical hazards and proper cleanup procedures. Containment and cleanup are the immediate necessary actions for a spill.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MSDS 提供有关化学危害和正确清理程序的关键信息。遏制和清理是泄漏后需要立即采取的行动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about where specialized information for chemicals is stored in a clinical setting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考在临床环境中，有关化学品的专业信息存储在哪里。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":779,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.588","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.588.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.588.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,48],"fullStemEn":"A client has been placed in bilateral wrist restraints due to aggressive behavior. How often must the nurse assess the client's skin integrity and neurovascular status?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因攻击行为被戴上双侧腕部约束带。护士必须每隔多久评估一次患者的皮肤完整性和神经血管状态？","terminalSentenceEn":"How often must the nurse assess the client's skin integrity and neurovascular status?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须每隔多久评估一次患者的皮肤完整性和神经血管状态？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client has been placed in bilateral wrist restraints due to aggressive behavior.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因攻击行为被戴上双侧腕部约束带。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Every 15 minutes","zh":"每 15 分钟一次"},{"id":"D","en":"Every 30 minutes","zh":"每 30 分钟一次"},{"id":"A","en":"Every 2 hours","zh":"每 2 小时一次"},{"id":"C","en":"Once per shift","zh":"每班一次"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard nursing practice for physical restraints requires assessment and release of the restraint at least every 2 hours to check skin, circulation, and range of motion. (Note: Continuous observation or 15-minute checks may be required for behavioral reasons, but the physical assessment is every 2 hours).","rationaleCorrectZh":"物理约束的标准护理实践要求至少每 2 小时评估并松开一次约束，以检查皮肤、循环和活动度。（注：出于行为原因可能需要持续观察或每 15 分钟检查一次，但物理评估是每 2 小时一次）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the safest interval that balances monitoring needs with practical care delivery for physical assessments.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定最安全的时间间隔，以平衡监测需求与物理评估的实际护理提供。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":780,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.589","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.589.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.589.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,138],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is implementing standard precautions for all clients. Which actions are included in standard precautions? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为所有患者实施标准预防措施。标准预防措施包括哪些行动？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are included in standard precautions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"标准预防措施包括哪些行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Recap needles after use to prevent injury.","zh":"使用后重新套上针头以防受伤。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place all clients in a private room.","zh":"将所有患者安置在单人病房。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wear gloves when touching non-intact skin.","zh":"接触不完整的皮肤时佩戴手套。"},{"id":"E","en":"Use a mask and eye protection during procedures likely to generate splashes.","zh":"在可能产生喷溅的操作过程中使用口罩和护目镜。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene after touching blood or body fluids.","zh":"接触血液或体液后进行手部卫生。"}],"correct":["A","B","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard precautions apply to all patients and include hand hygiene, use of gloves for contact with body fluids or non-intact skin, and appropriate PPE for splashes. Recapping needles is never recommended (use safety devices). Private rooms are for transmission-based precautions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标准预防措施适用于所有患者，包括手部卫生、接触体液或不完整皮肤时使用手套，以及针对喷溅使用适当的 PPE。严禁重新套上针头（应使用安全装置）。单人病房用于传播途径预防措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that 'Standard' means 'Every Patient, Every Time'. Avoid choices that are specific to certain transmission types.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“标准”意味着“每个病人，每次都是”。避免选择特定于某些传播类型的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":781,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.590","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.590.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.590.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers a fire in a trash can in a client's room. Place the actions the nurse should take in the correct order based on the RACE acronym.","fullStemZh":"护士在患者病房的垃圾桶里发现起火。请根据 RACE 缩写，按正确顺序排列护士应采取的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions the nurse should take in the correct order based on the RACE acronym.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据 RACE 缩写，按正确顺序排列护士应采取的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers a fire in a trash can in a client's room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在患者病房的垃圾桶里发现起火。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Activate the fire alarm","zh":"激活火警报警器"},{"id":"D","en":"Extinguish the fire if small enough","zh":"如果火势足够小，则扑灭火源"},{"id":"A","en":"Rescue the client from immediate danger","zh":"将患者从即刻危险中营救出来"},{"id":"C","en":"Confine the fire by closing doors and windows","zh":"通过关门窗来控制火势"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"RACE stands for Rescue, Alarm, Confine, Extinguish/Evacuate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"RACE 代表营救 (Rescue)、报警 (Alarm)、局限 (Confine)、扑灭/疏散 (Extinguish/Evacuate)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the acronym RACE for fire priority. Patient safety always comes first (Rescue).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住火灾优先顺序的缩写 RACE。患者安全始终放在第一位（营救）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":782,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch1_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.591","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.591.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.591.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,132],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"After administering an intramuscular injection, what is the most appropriate action for the nurse to take regarding the used needle?","fullStemZh":"肌肉注射后，护士对使用过的针头采取的最合适行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"After administering an intramuscular injection, what is the most appropriate action for the nurse to take regarding the used needle?","terminalSentenceZh":"肌肉注射后，护士对使用过的针头采取的最合适行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Place the needle in a plastic trash bag.","zh":"将针头放入塑料垃圾袋中。"},{"id":"B","en":"Discard the needle in a puncture-resistant container.","zh":"将针头丢弃在耐穿刺容器中。"},{"id":"A","en":"Break the needle before disposal.","zh":"处置前将针头折断。"},{"id":"C","en":"Recap the needle using a two-handed technique.","zh":"使用双手技术重新套上针头。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To prevent needlestick injuries, all sharps should be disposed of immediately in a puncture-resistant (sharps) container. Needles should never be recapped or broken.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为防止针刺伤，所有锐器应立即丢弃在耐穿刺（锐器）容器中。绝不应重新套上或折断针头。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the answer that ensures immediate containment in a safe vessel designed for sharps.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找确保立即装入专门为锐器设计的安全容器的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":783,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_1","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.592","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.592.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.592.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[57,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,37],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with a known infection. Which action by the nurse is the most important for preventing the spread of infection?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一位已知感染的患者。护士采取的哪项行动对预防感染扩散最为重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is the most important for preventing the spread of infection?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士采取的哪项行动对预防感染扩散最为重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with a known infection.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一位已知感染的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Wearing a gown when entering the client's room","zh":"进入患者病房时穿隔离衣"},{"id":"C","en":"Wearing gloves for all client contact","zh":"在所有患者接触中佩戴手套"},{"id":"D","en":"Using alcohol-based hand rub after touching the client's bed rails","zh":"触摸患者床栏后使用含酒精的手部消毒液"},{"id":"B","en":"Performing hand hygiene before and after client contact","zh":"在接触患者前后进行手部卫生"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hand hygiene is the single most effective way to prevent the spread of infection in healthcare settings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手部卫生是医疗环境中预防感染扩散最有效的方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on 'most important' and look for the intervention that is most universally applicable and effective.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注“最重要的”，寻找最普遍适用且有效的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":784,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_2","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.593","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.593.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.593.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,149],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,33],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis. Which of the following interventions should the nurse implement? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"一名疑似肺结核患者入院。护士应实施以下哪些干预措施？（多项选择。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following interventions should the nurse implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施以下哪些干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Wear a surgical mask when providing direct care.","zh":"在提供直接护理时戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a private room with negative pressure.","zh":"将患者安置在带负压的单人病房中。"},{"id":"C","en":"Wear an N95 respirator when entering the room.","zh":"进入病房时戴N95呼吸器。"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the room door closed at all times.","zh":"始终保持病房门关闭。"},{"id":"E","en":"Have the client wear a surgical mask during transport.","zh":"在转运过程中让患者戴上外科口罩。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Airborne precautions for TB include a negative-pressure room, keeping the door closed, and N95 respirator use for staff. Clients wear surgical masks during transport.","rationaleCorrectZh":"结核病的空气传播预防措施包括负压病房、保持房门关闭以及工作人员使用N95呼吸器。患者在转运过程中应佩戴外科口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the specific requirements for 'Airborne' vs. 'Droplet' precautions. TB is a classic airborne example.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“空气传播”与“飞沫传播”预防措施的具体要求。结核病是典型的空气传播案例。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":785,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_3","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.594","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.594.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.594.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,47],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to leave the room of a client on contact and droplet precautions. In which order should the nurse remove the personal protective equipment (PPE)?","fullStemZh":"护士准备离开一位采取接触和飞沫预防措施的患者病房。护士应按什么顺序脱下个人防护装备（PPE）？","terminalSentenceEn":"In which order should the nurse remove the personal protective equipment (PPE)?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序脱下个人防护装备（PPE）？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to leave the room of a client on contact and droplet precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备离开一位采取接触和飞沫预防措施的患者病房。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Gown","zh":"隔离衣"},{"id":"A","en":"Gloves","zh":"手套"},{"id":"D","en":"Mask or respirator","zh":"口罩或呼吸器"},{"id":"B","en":"Goggles or face shield","zh":"护目镜或面罩"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The standard CDC sequence for removing PPE is: 1. Gloves, 2. Goggles/Face shield, 3. Gown, 4. Mask/Respirator. Gloves are the most contaminated and removed first.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDC脱下PPE的标准顺序是：1. 手套，2. 护目镜/面罩，3. 隔离衣，4. 口罩/呼吸器。手套污染最严重，应首先脱下。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the most contaminated item and remove it first. The mask is removed last to protect the respiratory tract as long as possible.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别污染最严重的物品并首先将其脱下。口罩最后脱下，以尽可能长时间保护呼吸道。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":786,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_4","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.595","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.595.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.595.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,56],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer Vancomycin 1 g in 250 mL of Normal Saline over 100 minutes. At what rate should the nurse set the infusion pump in mL/hr?","fullStemZh":"护士准备在100分钟内为患者输注溶于250毫升生理盐水的1克万古霉素。护士应将输液泵的速率设置为多少毫升/小时？","terminalSentenceEn":"At what rate should the nurse set the infusion pump in mL/hr?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将输液泵的速率设置为多少毫升/小时？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer Vancomycin 1 g in 250 mL of Normal Saline over 100 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备在100分钟内为患者输注溶于250毫升生理盐水的1克万古霉素。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["150"],"numeric":{"value":150,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Formula: (Total Volume / Total Minutes) x 60 min = mL/hr. (250 mL / 100 min) x 60 = 150 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"公式：（总容量 / 总分钟数）x 60分钟 = 毫升/小时。(250 mL / 100 min) x 60 = 150 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Standardize units. Always convert minutes to hours if the pump requires mL/hr.","testTakingStrategyZh":"标准化单位。如果输液泵要求毫升/小时，务必将分钟转换为小时。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":787,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.596","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.596.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.596.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"An 82-year-old client with dementia and a history of falls is admitted to the unit.","fullStemZh":"一名患有认知障碍且有跌倒史的82岁患者入院。","terminalSentenceEn":"An 82-year-old client with dementia and a history of falls is admitted to the unit.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患有认知障碍且有跌倒史的82岁患者入院。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should prioritize placing the client in a room {{1}} and ensure that {{2}}.","zh":"护士应优先将患者安置在{{1}}的病房，并确保{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"at the end of the hallway","zh":"在走廊尽头"},{"id":"o3","en":"with a semi-private roommate","zh":"与半私人室友一起"},{"id":"o1","en":"near the nurses' station","zh":"靠近护士站"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"the bed is in the lowest position","zh":"床位处于最低位置"},{"id":"o2","en":"all four side rails are raised","zh":"所有四个床栏都升起"},{"id":"o3","en":"restraints are applied at night","zh":"夜间使用约束装置"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"High-risk clients should be near the nurses' station for frequent observation. Keeping the bed in the lowest position reduces injury risk from falls.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高风险患者应安置在护士站附近以便频繁观察。将床保持在最低位置可降低跌倒造成的伤害风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first. Four side rails are considered a restraint, which should be avoided if possible.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一。四个床栏被视为一种约束，应尽可能避免。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":788,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_8","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.597","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.597.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.597.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,45],"fullStemEn":"A client is placed in bilateral soft wrist restraints due to pulling at a central venous catheter. Which of the following nursing actions are required? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"一名患者因拉扯中心静脉导管而被套上双侧软腕带约束。以下哪些护理操作是必须的？（多项选择。）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing actions are required?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些护理操作是必须的？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Offer fluids and toileting every 2 hours.","zh":"每2小时提供一次液体和如厕。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ensure that two fingers can be inserted under the restraint.","zh":"确保约束带下可以插入两根手指。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess skin integrity and neurovascular status every 2 hours.","zh":"每2小时评估一次皮肤完整性和神经血管状态。"},{"id":"E","en":"Obtain a new prescription for restraints every 48 hours.","zh":"每48小时获取一次新的约束处方。"},{"id":"B","en":"Secure the restraints to the side rails of the bed.","zh":"将约束带固定在床栏上。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Monitoring, comfort care, and ensuring safe fit are essential. Restraints should be secured to the bed frame, not side rails, and prescriptions are usually required every 24 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"监测、舒适护理和确保安全贴合至关重要。约束带应固定在床架上而非床栏上，且处方通常需要每24小时获取一次。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 'bed frame' and 'side rails' for securing devices. Also, know the standard timeframes for restraint orders.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分固定设备的“床架”和“床栏”。此外，了解约束医嘱的标准时限。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":789,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_9","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.598","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.598.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.598.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,40],"fullStemEn":"A fire is discovered in a trash can in a client's room. After removing the client from the room, which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"在患者病房的垃圾桶里发现了火情。在将患者移出病房后，护士接下来应该采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"After removing the client from the room, which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"在将患者移出病房后，护士接下来应该采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A fire is discovered in a trash can in a client's room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在患者病房的垃圾桶里发现了火情。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Confine the fire by closing nearby windows","zh":"通过关闭附近的窗户来限制火势"},{"id":"A","en":"Extinguish the fire using a fire extinguisher","zh":"使用灭火器灭火"},{"id":"B","en":"Close the door to the room","zh":"关闭病房门"},{"id":"D","en":"Activate the fire alarm","zh":"启动火警警报"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to the RACE mnemonic: Rescue (R), Alarm, Confine, Extinguish. After rescuing (removing the client), the next step is to activate the alarm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据RACE记忆法：救援 (R)、报警、限制、灭火。在救援（移出患者）之后，下一步是启动警报。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the RACE acronym to determine the correct order of priorities during a fire.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用RACE缩写来确定火灾期间的正确优先顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A fire is discovered in a trash can in a client's room.","controlSentenceZh":"在患者病房的垃圾桶里发现了火情。"}
{"queueIndex":790,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_sic_batch2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.599","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.599.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.599.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"During a Clostridioides difficile outbreak, the nurse follows the facility's enhanced prevention policy.","fullStemZh":"在艰难梭菌暴发期间，护士遵循医疗机构的强化预防政策。","terminalSentenceEn":"During a Clostridioides difficile outbreak, the nurse follows the facility's enhanced prevention policy.","terminalSentenceZh":"在艰难梭菌暴发期间，护士遵循医疗机构的强化预防政策。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"After removing gloves, the nurse should use {{1}} for hand hygiene and clean the room with {{2}}.","zh":"脱下手套后，护士应使用{{1}}进行手部卫生，并使用{{2}}清洁病房。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"soap and water","zh":"肥皂和水"},{"id":"o2","en":"alcohol-based hand rub","zh":"含酒精的手部消毒液"},{"id":"o3","en":"povidone-iodine","zh":"聚维酮碘"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"quaternary ammonium","zh":"季铵盐"},{"id":"o1","en":"a facility-approved sporicidal disinfectant","zh":"医疗机构批准的杀芽孢消毒剂"},{"id":"o2","en":"an alcohol-based disinfectant","zh":"含酒精消毒剂"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During high endemic CDI rates or outbreaks, CDC prefers soap and water after glove removal because alcohol lacks sporicidal activity. Environmental surfaces should be cleaned with a facility-approved sporicidal disinfectant; hypochlorite is one option.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在艰难梭菌高流行或暴发期间，因酒精不具杀芽孢活性，CDC首选脱下手套后用肥皂和水洗手。环境表面应使用医疗机构批准的杀芽孢消毒剂；次氯酸盐是其中一种选择。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read the setting: CDC specifically prefers soap and water during CDI outbreaks or high endemic rates, together with facility-approved sporicidal cleaning.","testTakingStrategyZh":"注意情境：CDC在艰难梭菌暴发或高流行期间特别首选肥皂和水，并配合医疗机构批准的杀芽孢清洁。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":791,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.600","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.600.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.600.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,56],"fullStemEn":"A client with atrial fibrillation is receiving warfarin. The most recent International Normalized Ratio (INR) is 4.8. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名患有心房颤动的患者正在接受华法林治疗。最近的国际标准化比值 (INR) 为 4.8。护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The most recent International Normalized Ratio (INR) is 4.8.","penultimateSentenceZh":"最近的国际标准化比值 (INR) 为 4.8。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer the scheduled dose of warfarin.","zh":"按计划给药华法林。"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare to administer protamine sulfate.","zh":"准备给予硫酸鱼精蛋白。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and request an order for Vitamin K.","zh":"通知医疗保健人员并请求开具维生素 K 医嘱。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client for signs of abnormal bleeding or bruising.","zh":"评估患者是否有异常出血或瘀斑的迹象。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An INR of 4.8 is significantly above the typical therapeutic range (2.0-3.0). The priority nursing action is to assess the client for any complications, such as active bleeding or hematomas, before notifying the provider or implementing interventions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"INR 为 4.8 明显高于典型的治疗范围 (2.0-3.0)。护士的首要任务是在通知医生或实施干预之前，评估患者是否存在任何并发症，如活动性出血或血肿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the nursing process: assessment always comes before implementation/intervention unless the client is in immediate distress.","testTakingStrategyZh":"运用护理程序：除非患者处于紧急状态，否则评估总是先于实施/干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":792,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.601","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.601.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.601.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[331,380],"terminalOffsetsZh":[138,154],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving a continuous heparin infusion for deep vein thrombosis (DVT). The client's activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT) is 98 seconds. The facility protocol for aPTT > 90 seconds is: 'Hold infusion for 1 hour, then decrease rate by 2 units/kg/hr.' The client weighs 80 kg. The current rate is 1,200 units/hr. What should the new infusion rate be in units/hr?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因深静脉血栓 (DVT) 正在接受持续肝素输注。患者的活化部分凝血活酶时间 (aPTT) 为 98 秒。该机构对于 aPTT > 90 秒的方案是：“停止输注 1 小时，然后将速率降低 2 单位/公斤/小时。”患者体重 80 公斤。当前速率为 1,200 单位/小时。新的输注速率应为多少单位/小时？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the new infusion rate be in units/hr?","terminalSentenceZh":"新的输注速率应为多少单位/小时？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The current rate is 1,200 units/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"当前速率为 1,200 单位/小时。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"units/hr","zh":"单位/小时"},"acceptable":["1040"],"numeric":{"value":1040,"tolerance":0,"unit":"units/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Step 1: Calculate the reduction amount: 2 units/kg/hr * 80 kg = 160 units/hr. Step 2: Subtract from current rate: 1,200 units/hr - 160 units/hr = 1,040 units/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第 1 步：计算减少量：2 单位/公斤/小时 * 80 公斤 = 160 单位/小时。第 2 步：从当前速率中减去：1,200 单位/小时 - 160 单位/小时 = 1,040 单位/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read the titration protocol carefully. Identify the current rate and the specific reduction amount based on body weight.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细阅读滴定方案。根据体重确定当前速率和具体的减少量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":793,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.602","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.602.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.602.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,36],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is monitoring clients after various procedures. Match the procedure with the primary complication that requires immediate assessment.","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测各种手术后的患者。请将手术与需要立即评估的主要并发症相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match the procedure with the primary complication that requires immediate assessment.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将手术与需要立即评估的主要并发症相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is monitoring clients after various procedures.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在监测各种手术后的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Thoracentesis","zh":"胸腔穿刺术"},{"id":"r2","en":"Paracentesis","zh":"腹腔穿刺术"},{"id":"r3","en":"Liver Biopsy","zh":"肝活检"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Pneumothorax","zh":"气胸"},{"id":"c3","en":"Hypovolemic Shock","zh":"低血容量性休克"},{"id":"c2","en":"Hemorrhage","zh":"出血"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thoracentesis involves the pleural space, making pneumothorax the priority risk. Paracentesis removes large fluid volumes, risking sudden fluid shifts and hypovolemic shock. Liver biopsy is performed on a highly vascular organ, making hemorrhage the primary risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胸腔穿刺术涉及胸膜腔，因此气胸是优先风险。腹腔穿刺术移除大量液体，有发生突然体液转移和低血容量性休克的风险。肝活检是在血管极其丰富的器官上进行的，因此出血是主要风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect the anatomical location of the procedure to the most likely organ-specific complication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将手术的解剖位置与最可能发生的器官特异性并发症联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":794,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.603","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.603.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.603.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,79],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the arterial blood gas (ABG) results for a client with COPD: pH 7.32, PaCO2 55 mmHg, HCO3 29 mEq/L, PaO2 78 mmHg.","fullStemZh":"护士查阅了一名 COPD 患者的动脉血气 (ABG) 结果：pH 7.32，PaCO2 55 mmHg，HCO3 29 mEq/L，PaO2 78 mmHg。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the arterial blood gas (ABG) results for a client with COPD: pH 7.32, PaCO2 55 mmHg, HCO3 29 mEq/L, PaO2 78 mmHg.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士查阅了一名 COPD 患者的动脉血气 (ABG) 结果：pH 7.32，PaCO2 55 mmHg，HCO3 29 mEq/L，PaO2 78 mmHg。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"These results indicate {{1}} with {{2}} compensation.","zh":"这些结果表明存在 {{1}}，并伴有 {{2}} 代偿。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic acidosis","zh":"代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"o2","en":"respiratory alkalosis","zh":"呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"o1","en":"respiratory acidosis","zh":"呼吸性酸中毒"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"full","zh":"完全"},{"id":"o1","en":"no","zh":"无"},{"id":"o2","en":"partial","zh":"部分"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pH is low (7.32), indicating acidosis. The PaCO2 is high (55), which aligns with the pH (respiratory). The HCO3 is high (29), showing that the kidneys are attempting to compensate, but since the pH is not yet in the normal range, the compensation is partial.","rationaleCorrectZh":"pH 值低 (7.32)，表明酸中毒。PaCO2 高 (55)，与 pH 值一致（呼吸性）。HCO3 高 (29)，表明肾脏正在尝试代偿，但由于 pH 值尚未回到正常范围，因此是部分代偿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: ROME (Respiratory Opposite, Metabolic Equal). If pH is abnormal but the other value is also shifting to fix it, it is partial compensation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：ROME（呼吸相反，代谢相同）。如果 pH 异常，但另一个数值也在变化以试图纠正它，那就是部分代偿。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":795,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.604","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.604.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.604.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,210],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,54],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results of a client with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Which laboratory value provides the best indication of the client's average blood glucose control over the past 3 months?","fullStemZh":"护士正在查阅一名 2 型糖尿病患者的实验室结果。哪项实验室数值最能说明患者过去 3 个月的平均血糖控制水平？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory value provides the best indication of the client's average blood glucose control over the past 3 months?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项实验室数值最能说明患者过去 3 个月的平均血糖控制水平？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the laboratory results of a client with type 2 diabetes mellitus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在查阅一名 2 型糖尿病患者的实验室结果。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c)","zh":"糖化血红蛋白 (HbA1c)"},{"id":"C","en":"Urine ketones","zh":"尿酮体"},{"id":"A","en":"Fasting blood glucose","zh":"空腹血糖"},{"id":"D","en":"Postprandial glucose","zh":"餐后血糖"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) measures the percentage of hemoglobin that has glucose attached to it, reflecting average blood glucose levels over the 120-day lifespan of a red blood cell.","rationaleCorrectZh":"糖化血红蛋白 (HbA1c) 测量与葡萄糖结合的血红蛋白百分比，反映了红细胞 120 天寿命内的平均血糖水平。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for keywords like '3 months' or 'long-term' which always point toward HbA1c in diabetes questions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找“3 个月”或“长期”等关键词，在糖尿病问题中，这些词总是指向 HbA1c。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":796,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.605","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.605.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.605.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[173,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,57],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving a unit of packed red blood cells reports chills, low back pain, and nausea 10 minutes after the transfusion started. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名正在接受浓缩红细胞输注的患者在输血开始 10 分钟后报告出现寒战、腰背痛和恶心。护士应采取哪些行动？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些行动？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Disconnect the blood tubing and flush the IV line with normal saline.","zh":"断开输血管并用生理盐水冲洗静脉管路。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and the blood bank.","zh":"通知医疗保健人员和血库。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer an antipyretic as prescribed.","zh":"按医嘱给予退烧药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Slow the rate of the transfusion to 50 mL/hr.","zh":"将输血速率降低至 50 毫升/小时。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the transfusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止输血。"},{"id":"F","en":"Send the blood bag and tubing to the blood bank.","zh":"将血袋和输血管送回血库。"}],"correct":["A","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Chills and low back pain are classic signs of an acute hemolytic reaction. Priority is to stop the blood, notify authorities, and send the product for testing (F). Note: Do NOT flush the blood remaining in the tubing into the client; keep the IV patent with a new saline setup.","rationaleCorrectZh":"寒战和腰背痛是急性溶血反应的经典征象。首要任务是停止输血、通知相关部门 并将制品送检 (F)。注意：不要将管路中残留的血液冲入患者体内；使用新的盐水装置保持静脉通畅。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For any 'reaction' question involving an infusion, the first step is almost always to STOP the infusion.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于任何涉及输注的“反应”问题，第一步几乎总是停止输注。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":797,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch1_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.606","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.606.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.606.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,51],"fullStemEn":"A nurse has just inserted a nasogastric (NG) tube for a client with a bowel obstruction. Place the following steps for verifying placement in the correct order, starting with the most definitive method.","fullStemZh":"护士刚为一名肠梗阻患者插入了鼻胃管 (NG)。请按正确顺序排列以下验证位置的步骤，从最确定的方法开始。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following steps for verifying placement in the correct order, starting with the most definitive method.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列以下验证位置的步骤，从最确定的方法开始。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse has just inserted a nasogastric (NG) tube for a client with a bowel obstruction.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士刚为一名肠梗阻患者插入了鼻胃管 (NG)。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Auscultate for a 'whoosh' sound over the epigastrium while injecting air.","zh":"注入空气时，在心窝处听诊是否有“呼啸”声。"},{"id":"B","en":"Aspirate gastric contents and check the pH level.","zh":"抽取胃内容物并检查 pH 值。"},{"id":"C","en":"Measure the external length of the tube.","zh":"测量管子的体外长度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Obtain an X-ray of the chest and abdomen.","zh":"拍摄胸部和腹部 X 线片。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"X-ray is the gold standard (definitive). pH testing is the most reliable bedside method. External measurement monitors for migration. Auscultation is an outdated and unreliable method that should not be used as primary verification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"X 线片是金标准（最确定）。pH 测试是最可靠的床边方法。体外测量可监测管路移位。听诊是一种过时且不可靠的方法，不应作为主要的验证手段。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Rank verification methods by reliability. X-ray always wins for NG tubes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按可靠性对验证方法进行排名。对于鼻胃管，X 线片总是胜出。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":798,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.607","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.607.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.607.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,42],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who just underwent a percutaneous liver biopsy. Which position should the nurse place the client in immediately following the procedure?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚接受过经皮肝穿刺活检的患者。手术后护士应立即将患者置于哪种体位？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which position should the nurse place the client in immediately following the procedure?","terminalSentenceZh":"手术后护士应立即将患者置于哪种体位？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who just underwent a percutaneous liver biopsy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名刚刚接受过经皮肝穿刺活检的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Right side-lying with a small towel roll under the biopsy site","zh":"右侧卧位，活检部位下方垫小毛巾卷"},{"id":"B","en":"Supine with the head of the bed elevated 30 degrees","zh":"仰卧位，床头抬高30度"},{"id":"D","en":"Prone with a pillow under the abdomen","zh":"俯卧位，腹部下方垫枕头"},{"id":"C","en":"Left side-lying with a pillow under the costal margin","zh":"左侧卧位，肋缘下垫枕头"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After a liver biopsy, the client should be placed in a right side-lying position for 2 to 4 hours to apply pressure to the biopsy site and prevent hemorrhage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝活检后，患者应保持右侧卧位2至4小时，以对活检部位施加压力并防止出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the anatomy (liver is on the right) and the priority risk (bleeding). Positioning should apply pressure to the site.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注解剖结构（肝脏在右侧）和优先风险（出血）。体位应能对该部位施加压力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":799,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.608","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.608.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.608.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[160,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to change the dressing of a client's central venous catheter (CVC). Which actions should the nurse take to reduce the risk of infection? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为患者更换中心静脉导管（CVC）敷料。护士应采取哪些行动来降低感染风险？（择所有适用项）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"择所有适用项）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take to reduce the risk of infection?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些行动来降低感染风险？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Apply chlorhexidine gluconate using a back-and-forth friction scrub","zh":"使用葡萄糖酸氯己定进行来回摩擦擦拭"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene before and after the procedure","zh":"在操作前后进行手卫生"},{"id":"C","en":"Cleanse the site with 70% isopropyl alcohol only","zh":"仅使用70%异丙基酒精清洁部位"},{"id":"B","en":"Wear a mask and ask the client to wear a mask or turn their head away","zh":"戴上口罩，并要求患者戴上口罩或将头转向另一侧"},{"id":"F","en":"Change the transparent dressing every 24 hours","zh":"每24小时更换一次透明敷料"},{"id":"D","en":"Use sterile gloves and sterile technique during the dressing change","zh":"在更换敷料期间使用无菌手套和无菌技术"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard evidence-based practices for CVC care include hand hygiene, maximal sterile barriers (masks, sterile gloves/drapes), and chlorhexidine scrub to prevent CLABSI.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CVC护理的标准循证实践包括手卫生、最大无菌屏障（口罩、无菌手套/铺巾）和氯己定擦拭，以预防中心静脉导管相关血流感染（CLABSI）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of 'CLABSI bundle' components. Note that 24-hour changes for transparent dressings are excessive and increase risk by frequent exposure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"考虑“CLABSI捆绑措施”的组成部分。注意每24小时更换一次透明敷料是过度的，且会因频繁暴露而增加风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":800,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.609","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.609.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.609.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,34],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is instructing a client on how to perform a 24-hour urine collection. Place the following steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在指导患者如何进行24小时尿液收集。请按正确顺序排列以下步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列以下步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is instructing a client on how to perform a 24-hour urine collection.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在指导患者如何进行24小时尿液收集。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Label the container with the client's identifying information and the time collection ended.","zh":"在容器上贴上患者的身份信息和收集结束的时间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Keep the collection container on ice or in the refrigerator.","zh":"将收集容器放在冰上或冰箱中。"},{"id":"A","en":"Discard the first voided specimen and record the start time.","zh":"丢弃第一次排出的尿样并记录开始时间。"},{"id":"C","en":"Collect all urine voided for the next 24 hours.","zh":"收集接下来24小时内排出的所有尿液。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the client to void one last time at the end of the 24-hour period and add it to the container.","zh":"要求患者在24小时结束时最后一次排尿，并将尿液加入容器中。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The collection begins by emptying the bladder and discarding that urine. All subsequent urine is saved and chilled. It ends with a final void at exactly 24 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"收集从排空膀胱并丢弃该尿液开始。随后所有的尿液都要保存并冷藏。在恰好24小时进行最后一次排尿后结束。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The first step is always to 'start fresh' by discarding the current urine in the bladder.","testTakingStrategyZh":"第一步总是通过丢弃膀胱中现有的尿液来“重新开始”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":801,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.610","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.610.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.610.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for several clients. Determine if each result is within the expected reference range or is unexpected (abnormal) for an adult client.","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看几名患者的实验室检查结果。确定每项结果是在成人的预期参考范围内还是非预期的（异常）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Determine if each result is within the expected reference range or is unexpected (abnormal) for an adult client.","terminalSentenceZh":"确定每项结果是在成人的预期参考范围内还是非预期的（异常）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for several clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在查看几名患者的实验室检查结果。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Serum Potassium: 5.8 mEq/L (5.8 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钾：5.8 mEq/L (5.8 mmol/L)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Serum Sodium: 138 mEq/L (138 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钠：138 mEq/L (138 mmol/L)"},{"id":"r3","en":"Serum Magnesium: 0.9 mEq/L (0.37 mmol/L)","zh":"血清镁：0.9 mEq/L (0.37 mmol/L)"},{"id":"r4","en":"WBC Count: 8.5 ×10³/µL","zh":"白细胞计数：8.5 ×10³/µL"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Unexpected (Abnormal)","zh":"非预期（异常）"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected Range","zh":"预期范围"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium (3.5-5.0) and Magnesium (1.3-2.1) are abnormal in this set. Sodium (135-145) and WBC (5k-10k) are normal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在这组中，钾 (3.5-5.0) 和镁 (1.3-2.1) 是异常的。钠 (135-145) 和白细胞 (5k-10k) 是正常的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize common electrolyte ranges. Potassium and magnesium are critical values frequently tested.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记忆常见的电解质范围。钾和镁是经常测试的关键数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for several clients.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在查看几名患者的实验室检查结果。"}
{"queueIndex":802,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.611","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.611.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.611.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is monitoring a client after a thoracentesis. The client suddenly reports shortness of breath and the nurse notes decreased breath sounds on the affected side.","fullStemZh":"护士在胸腔穿刺术后监测一名患者。患者突然报告呼吸短促，护士注意到患侧呼吸音减弱。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client suddenly reports shortness of breath and the nurse notes decreased breath sounds on the affected side.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者突然报告呼吸短促，护士注意到患侧呼吸音减弱。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is monitoring a client after a thoracentesis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在胸腔穿刺术后监测一名患者。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is most likely experiencing {{1}} as a complication of the procedure, which requires the nurse to {{2}}.","zh":"该患者最有可能发生了 {{1}} 作为手术并发症，这要求护士 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"pulmonary edema","zh":"肺水肿"},{"id":"o1","en":"pneumothorax","zh":"气胸"},{"id":"o3","en":"pleural effusion","zh":"胸腔积液"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"prepare for chest tube insertion","zh":"准备胸管置入"},{"id":"o3","en":"position the client on the affected side","zh":"将患者置于患侧卧位"},{"id":"o2","en":"administer a rapid bolus of IV fluids","zh":"给予快速静脉补液"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pneumothorax is a common complication of thoracentesis due to accidental lung puncture. Decreased breath sounds and dyspnea are classic signs, often requiring a chest tube.","rationaleCorrectZh":"气胸是胸腔穿刺术的常见并发症，由于意外刺伤肺部引起。呼吸音减弱和呼吸困难是典型体征，通常需要放置胸管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the complication based on the procedure (thoracentesis involves a needle in the pleural space). 'Decreased breath sounds' on one side points to air or fluid in the space; air (pneumothorax) is a sudden procedural risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据手术过程识别并发症（胸腔穿刺涉及胸膜腔内的穿刺针）。一侧“呼吸音减弱”指向该腔隙内的气体或液体；气体（气胸）是突发的手术风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":803,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.612","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.612.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.612.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,61],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the serum lithium level for a client with bipolar disorder and finds it is 1.8 mEq/L (1.8 mmol/L). Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士查看了一名双相情感障碍患者的血清锂水平，发现为 1.8 mEq/L (1.8 mmol/L)。护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the serum lithium level for a client with bipolar disorder and finds it is 1.8 mEq/L (1.8 mmol/L).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看了一名双相情感障碍患者的血清锂水平，发现为 1.8 mEq/L (1.8 mmol/L)。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hold the next dose and notify the healthcare provider.","zh":"暂停下一次剂量并通知医疗保健提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the result as within the therapeutic range.","zh":"将结果记录为在治疗范围内。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase the client's oral fluid intake.","zh":"增加患者的口服液体摄入量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the next scheduled dose as prescribed.","zh":"按医嘱给予下一次计划剂量。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The therapeutic range for lithium is 0.6 to 1.2 mEq/L. A level of 1.8 mEq/L indicates toxicity, necessitating holding the medication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锂的治疗范围为 0.6 至 1.2 mEq/L。1.8 mEq/L 的水平表示中毒，必须停药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know the narrow therapeutic index drugs: Lithium (0.6-1.2), Digoxin (0.5-2.0), Theophylline (10-20). Any value outside these ranges requires action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解治疗指数窄的药物：锂 (0.6-1.2)、地高辛 (0.5-2.0)、茶碱 (10-20)。超出这些范围的任何数值都需要采取行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":804,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_rrp_batch2_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.613","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.613.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.613.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,63],"fullStemEn":"A client with idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura (ITP) has a platelet count of 45 ×10³/µL. Which nursing instruction is most important to include in the plan of care?","fullStemZh":"一名患有特发性血小板减少性紫癜 (ITP) 的患者，血小板计数为 45 ×10³/µL。在护理计划中包含哪项护理指导最为重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing instruction is most important to include in the plan of care?","terminalSentenceZh":"在护理计划中包含哪项护理指导最为重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura (ITP) has a platelet count of 45 ×10³/µL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有特发性血小板减少性紫癜 (ITP) 的患者，血小板计数为 45 ×10³/µL。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Notify the provider if feeling fatigued or weak.","zh":"如果感到疲劳或虚弱，请通知医疗人员。"},{"id":"A","en":"Avoid crowds and people with infections.","zh":"避免去人群拥挤的地方和接触感染者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Use a soft-bristled toothbrush and an electric razor.","zh":"使用软毛牙刷和电动剃须刀。"},{"id":"B","en":"Increase intake of dark green leafy vegetables.","zh":"增加深绿色叶类蔬菜的摄入量。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A platelet count below 50 ×10³/µL indicates a high risk for bleeding. Bleeding precautions (soft toothbrush, electric razor) are critical.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血小板计数低于 50 ×10³/µL 表示出血风险很高。出血预防措施（软毛牙刷、电动剃须刀）至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the lab finding (low platelets) to the specific risk (bleeding). Select the intervention that directly mitigates that risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将实验室发现（血小板低）与特定风险（出血）相匹配。选择能直接降低该风险的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":805,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_1","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.614","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.614.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.614.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a 24-month-old toddler during a well-child visit. Which finding should the nurse identify as a developmental delay?","fullStemZh":"护士在幼儿保健门诊对一名24个月大的幼儿进行评估。护士应将以下哪项发现视为发育迟缓？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding should the nurse identify as a developmental delay?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将以下哪项发现视为发育迟缓？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a 24-month-old toddler during a well-child visit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在幼儿保健门诊对一名24个月大的幼儿进行评估。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The child has a vocabulary of approximately 50 words.","zh":"孩子的词汇量约为50个单词。"},{"id":"B","en":"The child builds a tower of 6 blocks.","zh":"孩子能叠起6块积木。"},{"id":"D","en":"The child is unable to speak in two-word sentences.","zh":"孩子无法说出两个单词组成的句子。"},{"id":"C","en":"The child is unable to hop on one foot.","zh":"孩子无法单脚跳。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"By 24 months, a toddler should be able to speak in two-word sentences ('telegraphic speech'). Failure to do so may indicate a developmental delay.","rationaleCorrectZh":"到24个月时，幼儿应该能够说出由两个单词组成的句子（“电报式语言”）。如果做不到这一点，可能表明发育迟缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall developmental milestones for a 2-year-old (24 months). Focus on the 'Rule of 2s': 2 years old, 2-word phrases, 2/4 of speech understood by strangers.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想2岁（24个月）的发育里程碑。关注“2法则”：2岁，2个单词的短语，陌生人能听懂2/4的言语。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":806,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_2","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.615","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.615.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.615.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,36],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a pregnant client at 12 weeks gestation about nutrition. Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名孕12周的孕妇提供营养教学。护士应包括哪些指导？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些指导？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Increase daily caloric intake by 340 calories during the first trimester.","zh":"在孕早期，每日热量摄入增加340卡路里。"},{"id":"B","en":"Consume at least 600 mcg of folic acid daily.","zh":"每日摄入至少600微克的叶酸。"},{"id":"E","en":"Take iron supplements with milk to increase absorption.","zh":"随牛奶服用铁剂以增加吸收。"},{"id":"C","en":"Limit caffeine intake to no more than 200 mg per day.","zh":"限制咖啡因摄入，每日不超过200毫克。"},{"id":"D","en":"Avoid consuming unpasteurized dairy products and deli meats.","zh":"避免食用未经巴氏消毒的奶制品和熟食肉类。"}],"correct":["B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pregnant women should consume 600 mcg of folic acid to prevent neural tube defects. Caffeine should be limited to 200 mg/day to reduce the risk of miscarriage or IUGR. Unpasteurized products and deli meats should be avoided due to the risk of Listeria.","rationaleCorrectZh":"孕妇应摄入600微克叶酸以预防神经管缺陷。咖啡因应限制在每日200毫克以内，以降低流产或宫内生长受限的风险。应避免未经巴氏消毒的产品和熟食肉类，因为存在李斯特菌风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify specific dietary requirements and restrictions during pregnancy. Eliminate choices that describe wrong trimesters (A) or incorrect absorption methods (E).","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定怀孕期间的具体饮食要求和限制。排除描述错误孕期（A）或错误吸收方法（E）的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":807,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_3","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.616","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.616.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.616.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"According to American Cancer Society guidelines, a 52-year-old female client with an average risk for breast cancer should follow which screening recommendation?","fullStemZh":"根据美国癌症协会指南，一名具有平均乳腺癌风险的52岁女性客户应遵循哪项筛查建议？","terminalSentenceEn":"According to American Cancer Society guidelines, a 52-year-old female client with an average risk for breast cancer should follow which screening recommendation?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据美国癌症协会指南，一名具有平均乳腺癌风险的52岁女性客户应遵循哪项筛查建议？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Clinical breast exam every year, no mammography needed until age 60.","zh":"每年进行一次临床乳腺检查，60岁前不需要进行乳房X光检查。"},{"id":"D","en":"Mammography every 2 years.","zh":"每2年进行一次乳房X光检查。"},{"id":"B","en":"Mammography every 3 years.","zh":"每3年进行一次乳房X光检查。"},{"id":"A","en":"Annual mammography.","zh":"每年进行一次乳房X光检查。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Women aged 45 to 54 should get mammograms every year. Women 55 and older can switch to every 2 years, or continue yearly screening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"45至54岁的女性应每年进行一次乳房X光检查。55岁及以上的女性可以改为每2年一次，或继续每年筛查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know the current screening guidelines for major cancers (breast, colon, cervical). Focus on the age of the client (52) to select the correct interval.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解主要癌症（乳腺癌、结肠癌、宫颈癌）的当前筛查指南。关注客户的年龄（52岁）以选择正确的间隔。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":808,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_4","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.617","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.617.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.617.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,48],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing a skin assessment on an 80-year-old client. Which findings are considered normal physiological changes associated with aging? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名80岁的客户进行皮肤评估。以下哪些发现被认为是与老化相关的正常生理变化？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings are considered normal physiological changes associated with aging?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些发现被认为是与老化相关的正常生理变化？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Thinning of the dermis.","zh":"真皮层变薄。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increased skin elasticity.","zh":"皮肤弹性增加。"},{"id":"B","en":"Decreased subcutaneous fat.","zh":"皮下脂肪减少。"},{"id":"E","en":"Increased production of sweat and sebum.","zh":"汗液和皮脂分泌增加。"},{"id":"D","en":"Presence of cherry angiomas.","zh":"存在樱桃状血管瘤。"}],"correct":["B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aging leads to loss of subcutaneous fat and thinning of the dermis, making the skin fragile. Cherry angiomas are common, benign vascular lesions in older adults.","rationaleCorrectZh":"衰老导致皮下脂肪流失和真皮层变薄，使皮肤变得脆弱。樱桃状血管瘤是老年人常见的良性血管病变。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think about the common characteristics of geriatric skin: thin, dry, and fragile. Eliminate choices that suggest 'increased' function or elasticity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"思考老年皮肤的共同特征：薄、干、脆。排除暗示功能或弹性“增加”的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":809,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_5","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.618","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.618.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.618.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,32],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to perform a physical assessment of a client's abdomen. In which order should the nurse perform the assessment techniques?","fullStemZh":"护士准备对客户的腹部进行体格检查。护士应按什么顺序执行评估技术？","terminalSentenceEn":"In which order should the nurse perform the assessment techniques?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行评估技术？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to perform a physical assessment of a client's abdomen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备对客户的腹部进行体格检查。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Auscultation","zh":"听诊"},{"id":"C","en":"Percussion","zh":"叩诊"},{"id":"B","en":"Inspection","zh":"视诊"},{"id":"A","en":"Palpation","zh":"触诊"}],"correct":["B","D","C","A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For abdominal assessment, the sequence is Inspection, Auscultation, Percussion, and then Palpation. This is done to avoid stimulating bowel sounds or causing pain before listening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"腹部评估的顺序是视诊、听诊、叩诊，然后是触诊。这样做是为了避免在听诊前刺激肠鸣音或引起疼痛。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the pneumonic 'I Am PerPlexed' for abdomen: Inspection, Auscultation, Percussion, Palpation. Note that this differs from other body systems where palpation comes before auscultation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住腹部评估的口诀：视、听、叩、触。注意这与其他身体系统的顺序不同，其他系统中触诊通常在听诊之前。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":810,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.619","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.619.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.619.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,57],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is counseling a client who wants to quit smoking.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名想要戒烟的客户提供咨询。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse is counseling a client who wants to quit smoking.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名想要戒烟的客户提供咨询。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should explain that using nicotine replacement therapy (NRT) is most effective when combined with {{1}}. The nurse should also monitor for {{2}} as a potential adverse effect of nicotine gum.","zh":"护士应解释说，尼古丁替代疗法（NRT）与 {{1}} 结合使用时最有效。护士还应监测 {{2}}，这是尼古丁咀嚼胶的一种潜在不良反应。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"a high-protein diet","zh":"高蛋白饮食"},{"id":"o2","en":"vigorous exercise","zh":"剧烈运动"},{"id":"o1","en":"behavioral counseling","zh":"行为咨询"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"constipation","zh":"便秘"},{"id":"o1","en":"jaw muscle soreness","zh":"下颌肌肉酸痛"},{"id":"o3","en":"bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"NRT is most successful when paired with behavioral support or counseling. Jaw muscle soreness is a specific side effect related to the mechanics of using nicotine gum.","rationaleCorrectZh":"NRT与行为支持或咨询相结合时最为成功。下颌肌肉酸痛是与使用尼古丁咀嚼胶的力学相关的特定副作用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the multi-modal approach to addiction. For the second blank, think about the local effects of the specific NRT delivery method (gum).","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别戒瘾的多模式方法。对于第二个空格，考虑特定NRT输送方法（口香糖）的局部影响。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":811,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_7","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.620","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.620.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.620.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,223],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,73],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a newborn at 1 minute after birth. The newborn has a heart rate of 110/min, a weak cry, some flexion of the extremities, grimacing when stimulated, and a completely pink body. Calculate the APGAR score.","fullStemZh":"护士在出生后1分钟对新生儿进行评估。新生儿心率为110次/分，哭声弱，肢体有一定程度的屈曲，刺激时有皱眉动作，全身皮肤红润。请计算APGAR评分。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the APGAR score.","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算APGAR评分。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The newborn has a heart rate of 110/min, a weak cry, some flexion of the extremities, grimacing when stimulated, and a completely pink body.","penultimateSentenceZh":"新生儿心率为110次/分，哭声弱，肢体有一定程度的屈曲，刺激时有皱眉动作，全身皮肤红润。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"APGAR Score","zh":"APGAR评分"},"acceptable":["7"],"numeric":{"value":7,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Heart rate > 100 (2 points), weak cry (1 point), some flexion (1 point), grimace (1 point), completely pink (2 points). Total = 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 = 7.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心率 > 100（2分），哭声弱（1分），肢体屈曲（1分），皱眉（1分），全身红润（2分）。总分 = 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 = 7分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the APGAR scale components: Appearance, Pulse, Grimace, Activity, Respiration. Assign 0, 1, or 2 points to each.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想APGAR量表的组成部分：外观、脉搏、皱眉（反应）、活动、呼吸。为每一项分配0、1或2分。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":812,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_9","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.621","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.621.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.621.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,59],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is conducting a health screening for a sexually active adolescent. For each finding or statement, indicate whether the nurse should identify it as an 'Expected Outcome' or an 'Indicator of High-Risk Behavior'.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名性活跃的青少年进行健康筛查。对于每项发现或陈述，请指出护士应将其识别为“预期结果”还是“高危行为指标”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding or statement, indicate whether the nurse should identify it as an 'Expected Outcome' or an 'Indicator of High-Risk Behavior'.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现或陈述，请指出护士应将其识别为“预期结果”还是“高危行为指标”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is conducting a health screening for a sexually active adolescent.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名性活跃的青少年进行健康筛查。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Consistent use of latex condoms.","zh":"坚持使用乳胶避孕套。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Having multiple sexual partners.","zh":"拥有多个性伴侣。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Consumption of alcohol before sexual activity.","zh":"在性活动前饮酒。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Discussion of STI status with partners.","zh":"与伴侣讨论性传播感染（STI）状况。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"High-Risk Behavior","zh":"高危行为"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected Outcome","zh":"预期结果"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Expected outcomes for a sexually active individual include safe sex practices like condom use and communication. High-risk behaviors include multiple partners and substance use which can impair judgment and increase transmission risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"性活跃个体的预期结果包括避孕套使用和沟通等安全性行为。高危行为包括多个伴侣和物质滥用，这会损害判断力并增加传播风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify behaviors that increase the risk of STIs or unintended pregnancy. Positive health behaviors are 'Expected Outcomes'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别增加性传播感染或意外怀孕风险的行为。积极的健康行为是“预期结果”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":813,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch1_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.622","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.622.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.622.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a new mother about breastfeeding. Which instruction should the nurse include to ensure a proper latch?","fullStemZh":"护士正在教一位新妈妈如何母乳喂养。为了确保正确的衔乳，护士应包括哪项指导？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction should the nurse include to ensure a proper latch?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了确保正确的衔乳，护士应包括哪项指导？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a new mother about breastfeeding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教一位新妈妈如何母乳喂养。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The infant's mouth should cover the nipple and most of the areola.","zh":"婴儿的嘴应覆盖乳头和大部分乳晕。"},{"id":"A","en":"The infant's nose should be pressed firmly against the breast.","zh":"婴儿的鼻子应紧贴乳房。"},{"id":"D","en":"Wait for the infant to fall asleep before attempting to latch.","zh":"等婴儿入睡后再尝试衔乳。"},{"id":"C","en":"Breastfeeding should be painful for the first 5 minutes of every session.","zh":"每次喂奶的前5分钟应该是疼痛的。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A proper latch involves the infant taking the entire nipple and as much of the areola as possible into the mouth to compress the milk ducts.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的衔乳包括婴儿将整个乳头和尽可能多的乳晕含入口中，以压迫输乳管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize the mechanics of breastfeeding. Look for choices that promote effective feeding and comfort for the mother.","testTakingStrategyZh":"想象母乳喂养的力学过程。寻找能促进有效喂养和母亲舒适感的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":814,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_1","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.623","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.623.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.623.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a client who is planning to become pregnant. Which of the following instructions should the nurse include regarding folic acid intake?","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一位计划怀孕的客户提供教学。关于叶酸摄入，护士应包括以下哪项说明？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following instructions should the nurse include regarding folic acid intake?","terminalSentenceZh":"关于叶酸摄入，护士应包括以下哪项说明？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing teaching to a client who is planning to become pregnant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一位计划怀孕的客户提供教学。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Take 200 mcg of folic acid daily.","zh":"每天服用 200 微克叶酸。"},{"id":"B","en":"Start taking folic acid once you have a positive pregnancy test.","zh":"一旦妊娠试验呈阳性，就开始服用叶酸。"},{"id":"C","en":"Consume 400 mcg of folic acid daily to prevent neural tube defects.","zh":"每天摄入 400 微克叶酸以预防神经管缺陷。"},{"id":"A","en":"Folic acid is only necessary if you have a family history of birth defects.","zh":"只有在有出生缺陷家族史的情况下才需要服用叶酸。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Women of childbearing age should consume 400 mcg of folic acid daily to reduce the risk of neural tube defects in the fetus.","rationaleCorrectZh":"育龄妇女每天应摄入 400 微克叶酸，以降低胎儿发生神经管缺陷的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the recommended dosage and the timing of folic acid supplementation for neural tube defect prevention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注预防神经管缺陷的建议剂量和补充叶酸的时机。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":815,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_3","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.624","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.624.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.624.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse at a community health clinic is advising a 65-year-old client about recommended immunizations. Which of the following vaccines should the nurse recommend?","fullStemZh":"社区健康诊所的护士正在向一位 65 岁的客户建议推荐的免疫接种。护士应建议以下哪种疫苗？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following vaccines should the nurse recommend?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应建议以下哪种疫苗？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse at a community health clinic is advising a 65-year-old client about recommended immunizations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"社区健康诊所的护士正在向一位 65 岁的客户建议推荐的免疫接种。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Pneumococcal polysaccharide vaccine (PPSV23)","zh":"肺炎球菌多糖疫苗 (PPSV23)"},{"id":"B","en":"Meningococcal vaccine","zh":"脑膜炎球菌疫苗"},{"id":"A","en":"Human papillomavirus (HPV) vaccine","zh":"人乳头瘤病毒 (HPV) 疫苗"},{"id":"C","en":"Rotavirus vaccine","zh":"轮状病毒疫苗"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"PPSV23 is recommended for all adults 65 years of age or older to prevent pneumococcal disease.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建议所有 65 岁及以上的成年人接种 PPSV23，以预防肺炎球菌疾病。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the specific vaccine schedule for the geriatric population, especially those turning 65.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想老年人群的特定疫苗接种计划，尤其是年满 65 岁的人群。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":816,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_5","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.625","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.625.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.625.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[255,284],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,77],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is conducting a health screening for a 45-year-old client with no family history of colorectal cancer. At what age should the nurse inform the client that regular colorectal cancer screening should typically begin according to current guidelines? (Enter numerical value only).","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名 45 岁、没有结直肠癌家族史的客户进行健康筛查。根据现行指南，护士应告知该客户，通常应从多少岁开始进行定期的结直肠癌筛查？（仅输入数值）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Enter numerical value only).","terminalSentenceZh":"仅输入数值）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At what age should the nurse inform the client that regular colorectal cancer screening should typically begin according to current guidelines?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据现行指南，护士应告知该客户，通常应从多少岁开始进行定期的结直肠癌筛查？（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"years old","zh":"岁"},"acceptable":["45"],"numeric":{"value":45,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Current guidelines from the American Cancer Society and other organizations now recommend starting regular colorectal cancer screening at age 45 for individuals at average risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"美国癌症协会和其他组织的现行指南目前建议，平均风险人群应从 45 岁开始进行定期的结直肠癌筛查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Note recent updates to screening guidelines which lowered the age for colorectal screening from 50 to 45.","testTakingStrategyZh":"注意筛查指南的最新更新，该更新将结直肠癌筛查年龄从 50 岁降至 45 岁。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":817,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.626","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.626.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.626.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,54],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is performing a developmental assessment on a 12-month-old infant. For each finding, indicate whether it is an expected or unexpected finding for this age group.","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名 12 个月大的婴儿进行发育评估。对于每项发现，请指出其对于该年龄组是预期的还是非预期的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, indicate whether it is an expected or unexpected finding for this age group.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项发现，请指出其对于该年龄组是预期的还是非预期的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is performing a developmental assessment on a 12-month-old infant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在对一名 12 个月大的婴儿进行发育评估。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Triple the birth weight","zh":"体重达到出生时的三倍"},{"id":"r2","en":"Closure of the anterior fontanelle","zh":"前囟门闭合"},{"id":"r3","en":"Walking without assistance","zh":"独立行走"},{"id":"r4","en":"Presence of 6 to 8 teeth","zh":"有 6 到 8 颗牙齿"}],"columns":[{"id":"unexpected","en":"Unexpected","zh":"非预期表现"},{"id":"expected","en":"Expected","zh":"预期表现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["expected"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["expected"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["expected"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["expected"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At 12 months, it is expected that an infant has tripled their birth weight, has 6-8 teeth, and may be walking independently. The anterior fontanelle typically closes between 12 and 18 months.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 12 个月大时，预计婴儿体重已达到出生时的三倍，拥有 6-8 颗牙齿，并且可能已经可以独立行走。前囟门通常在 12 到 18 个月之间闭合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Review growth and development charts for the one-year milestone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"查看一周岁里程碑的生长发育图表。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":818,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_7","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.627","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.627.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.627.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,97],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a perimenopausal client about health maintenance and osteoporosis prevention.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名围绝经期客户教授健康维持和预防骨质疏松症的知识。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a perimenopausal client about health maintenance and osteoporosis prevention.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名围绝经期客户教授健康维持和预防骨质疏松症的知识。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client should increase intake of {{1}} to maintain bone health and is encouraged to perform {{2}} exercise regularly.","zh":"客户应增加 {{1}} 的摄入量以维持骨骼健康，并鼓励定期进行 {{2}} 运动。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Calcium","zh":"钙"},{"id":"o3","en":"Vitamin B12","zh":"维生素 B12"},{"id":"o1","en":"Vitamin C","zh":"维生素 C"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"Stretching","zh":"拉伸"},{"id":"o2","en":"Weight-bearing","zh":"负重"},{"id":"o1","en":"Swimming","zh":"游泳"}],"correct":"o2"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calcium is essential for bone density, and weight-bearing exercise (like walking) stimulates bone formation and slows bone loss during menopause.","rationaleCorrectZh":"钙对于骨密度至关重要，而负重运动（如散步）可以刺激骨形成并减缓绝经期间的骨丢失。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify nutrients and activities specifically linked to bone density in postmenopausal women.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别专门与绝经后妇女骨密度相关的营养素和活动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":819,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_9","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.628","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.628.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.628.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to screen school-age children for scoliosis. Which of the following actions should the nurse take during the screening? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为学龄儿童进行脊柱侧弯筛查。在筛查过程中，护士应采取以下哪些行动？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions should the nurse take during the screening?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在筛查过程中，护士应采取以下哪些行动？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Assess for an asymmetric waistline.","zh":"评估腰线是否不对称。"},{"id":"E","en":"Check for a leg length discrepancy.","zh":"检查是否有腿长差异。"},{"id":"D","en":"Have the child bend forward at the waist.","zh":"让孩子在腰部向前弯腰。"},{"id":"A","en":"Observe for uneven shoulder height.","zh":"观察肩膀高度是否不平。"},{"id":"B","en":"Inspect for a prominent scapula.","zh":"检查肩胛骨是否突出。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Scoliosis screening involves looking for uneven shoulders, a prominent scapula, an asymmetric waistline, and using the Adam's forward bend test. While leg length discrepancy can cause pelvic tilt, it is not a primary focus of screening for idiopathic scoliosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脊柱侧弯筛查包括寻找肩膀不平、肩胛骨突出、腰线不对称，以及使用亚当式前弯测试。虽然腿长差异会导致骨盆倾斜，但它不是特发性脊柱侧弯筛查的主要焦点。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the visual indicators of spinal curvature during a physical examination.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在体格检查中，重点关注脊柱弯曲的视觉指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":820,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_hpm_batch2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.629","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.629.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.629.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[48,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,30],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning a community health program. Which of the following activities is an example of primary prevention?","fullStemZh":"护士正在计划一项社区健康计划。以下哪项活动是初级预防的例子？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following activities is an example of primary prevention?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项活动是初级预防的例子？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning a community health program.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在计划一项社区健康计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Providing physical therapy for a client recovering from a stroke.","zh":"为中风康复期的客户提供物理治疗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Providing a smoking cessation program for clients with COPD.","zh":"为患有 COPD 的客户提供戒烟计划。"},{"id":"B","en":"Teaching high school students about the importance of using seatbelts.","zh":"向高中生讲授使用安全带的重要性。"},{"id":"A","en":"Conducting blood pressure screenings at a local mall.","zh":"在当地购物中心进行血压筛查。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Primary prevention focuses on health promotion and the prevention of injury or disease before it occurs. Teaching about seatbelt use is a primary prevention strategy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"初级预防侧重于在疾病或损伤发生之前进行健康促进和预防。讲授使用安全带的重要性是一种初级预防策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between preventing the onset of disease (primary), early detection (secondary), and managing existing disease (tertiary).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分预防疾病发生（初级）、早期发现（二级）和管理现有疾病（三级）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":821,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_1","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.630","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.630.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.630.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,66],"fullStemEn":"A client newly diagnosed with terminal cancer says to the nurse, 'I don't know why everyone is so worried about me. I feel fine and I'm going back to work tomorrow.' Which response by the nurse is most therapeutic?","fullStemZh":"一名新诊断为晚期癌症的患者对护士说：“我不知道为什么大家都这么担心我。我感觉很好，明天就要回去工作了。” 护士的哪种回答最具治疗性？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is most therapeutic?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪种回答最具治疗性？","penultimateSentenceEn":"I feel fine and I'm going back to work tomorrow.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"我感觉很好，明天就要回去工作了。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":" 'It's good to be optimistic, but you really need to rest.' ","zh":"“乐观是好事，但你真的需要休息。”"},{"id":"C","en":" 'Tell me more about your plans for returning to work.' ","zh":"“告诉我更多关于你重返工作的计划。”"},{"id":"A","en":" 'You seem to be having difficulty accepting your diagnosis.' ","zh":"“你似乎难以接受你的诊断。”"},{"id":"D","en":" 'I understand how you feel, but your cancer is very advanced.' ","zh":"“我理解你的感受，但你的癌症已经很晚期了。”"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"this option uses the therapeutic technique of 'exploring' or 'offering self/seeking clarification'. It allows the client to talk more about their feelings and plans without direct confrontation of their denial, which is a common initial defense mechanism.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该选项使用了“探索”或“提供自我/寻求澄清”的治疗性沟通技巧。它允许患者进一步谈论自己的感受和计划，而没有直接对抗其否认心理（这是一种常见的初期心理防御机制）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for open-ended responses that encourage the client to express feelings. Avoid answers that give advice, use 'why', or directly challenge defense mechanisms in the initial stages.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找鼓励患者表达感受的开放式回答。避免提供建议、使用“为什么”或在初始阶段直接挑战防御机制的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":822,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_2","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.631","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.631.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.631.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client's use of defense mechanisms. Which of the following behaviors are examples of 'displacement'? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估患者对心理防御机制的使用。以下哪些行为是“转移”（displacement）的例子？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following behaviors are examples of 'displacement'?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些行为是“转移”（displacement）的例子？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A client who was abused as a child becomes a counselor for victims of abuse.","zh":"一名童年受过虐待的患者成为了一名针对虐待受害者的咨询师。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client who is angry with their physician yells at the nurse.","zh":"一名对医生生气的患者对护士大声叫喊。"},{"id":"C","en":"An employee who is reprimanded by a boss goes home and kicks the dog.","zh":"一名被老板训斥的员工回家踢了狗。"},{"id":"E","en":"A teenager who is upset with their parents goes for a 5-mile run.","zh":"一名对父母不满的青少年去跑了5英里。"},{"id":"D","en":"A person who failed a test states that the teacher didn't explain the material well.","zh":"一名考试不及格的人声称老师没有把材料讲好。"}],"correct":["A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Displacement is the transfer of feelings from one target to another that is considered less threatening or neutral. Yelling at the nurse instead of the physician and kicking the dog instead of confronting the boss are classic examples.","rationaleCorrectZh":"“转移”是将情感从一个目标转移到另一个被认为威胁较小或中性的目标。对护士大声叫喊而不是对医生，以及踢狗而不是对抗老板，都是经典的例子。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Define the term 'displacement' first: moving feelings to a safer target. Evaluate each scenario against this definition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先定义“转移”一词：将情感移动到更安全的目标。根据这个定义评估每个场景。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":823,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_3","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.632","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.632.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.632.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[149,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is working in an emergency department when a client is brought in after a house fire. the client is distraught, pacing, and unable to focus. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士在急诊科工作时，一名因房屋起火而被送入的患者。患者心烦意乱，不停走动，无法集中注意力。护士应该首先采取什么行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该首先采取什么行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is working in an emergency department when a client is brought in after a house fire. the client is distraught, pacing, and unable to focus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者心烦意乱，不停走动，无法集中注意力。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Ask the client to explain exactly how the fire started.","zh":"要求患者准确解释火灾是如何开始的。"},{"id":"A","en":"Sit with the client and use short, simple sentences.","zh":"陪患者坐在一起，使用简短、简单的句子。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer a prescribed sedative to calm the client down.","zh":"按照医嘱服用镇静剂使患者冷静下来。"},{"id":"B","en":"Provide detailed information about local community resources.","zh":"提供有关当地社区资源的详细信息。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During a crisis, a person's level of anxiety is extremely high, and their ability to process information is severely limited. Sitting with the client provides a sense of safety, and short, simple sentences are necessary for comprehension.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在危机期间，一个人的焦虑程度极高，处理信息的能力受到严重限制。陪患者坐在一起提供了安全感，简短、简单的句子对于理解是必要的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In crisis intervention, the first step is to ensure safety and reduce anxiety using simple, direct communication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在危机干预中，第一步是确保安全并使用简单、直接的沟通来减轻焦虑。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":824,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_4","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.633","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.633.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.633.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,34],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the detoxification unit for alcohol withdrawal. Which assessment finding requires the most immediate intervention by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因酒精戒断入住脱毒单元。护士最需要立即干预的评估发现是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding requires the most immediate intervention by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最需要立即干预的评估发现是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted to the detoxification unit for alcohol withdrawal.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因酒精戒断入住脱毒单元。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Visual hallucinations and agitation","zh":"幻视和激动"},{"id":"A","en":"Nausea and abdominal cramping","zh":"恶心和腹部绞痛"},{"id":"B","en":"Tachycardia and hypertension","zh":"心动过速和高血压"},{"id":"D","en":"Hand tremors and restlessness","zh":"手部震颤和焦躁不安"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Visual hallucinations and severe agitation are signs of alcohol withdrawal delirium (delirium tremens), which is a medical emergency that can lead to death. This requires immediate intervention to ensure safety and prevent complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"幻视和严重的激动是酒精戒断谵妄（震颤性谵妄）的征兆，这是一种可能导致死亡的内科急症。这需要立即干预以确保安全并防止并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) and Maslow's hierarchy of needs, but also recognize psychiatric emergencies that pose an immediate risk to life (like DTs).","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用ABC原则（气道、呼吸、循环）和马斯洛需求层次理论，但也要识别出对生命构成直接风险的精神科急症（如震颤性谵妄）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client is admitted to the detoxification unit for alcohol withdrawal.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患者因酒精戒断入住脱毒单元。"}
{"queueIndex":825,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_6","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.634","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.634.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.634.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the characteristics of various personality disorders. For each behavior listed, identify the personality disorder it most likely represents.","fullStemZh":"护士正在回顾各种人格障碍的特征。对于列出的每种行为，识别其最可能代表的人格障碍。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each behavior listed, identify the personality disorder it most likely represents.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于列出的每种行为，识别其最可能代表的人格障碍。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the characteristics of various personality disorders.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在回顾各种人格障碍的特征。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Pattern of grandiosity and need for admiration","zh":"夸大模式和对赞美的需求"},{"id":"r2","en":"Instability in interpersonal relationships and self-image","zh":"人际关系和自我形象的不稳定性"},{"id":"r3","en":"Disregard for and violation of the rights of others","zh":"漠视并侵犯他人权利"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Antisocial","zh":"反社会型"},{"id":"c2","en":"Borderline","zh":"边缘型"},{"id":"c3","en":"Narcissistic","zh":"自恋型"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Narcissistic personality disorder is characterized by grandiosity and lack of empathy. Borderline is characterized by instability (splitting). Antisocial is characterized by a lack of remorse and violation of laws/rights.","rationaleCorrectZh":"自恋型人格障碍的特征是夸大和缺乏同理心。边缘型人格障碍的特征是不稳定性（分裂）。反社会型人格障碍的特征是缺乏悔意以及违反法律/侵犯权利。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the defining keyword to each disorder: Grandiosity = Narcissistic, Instability = Borderline, Violation of rights = Antisocial.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将定义性关键词与每种障碍相匹配：夸大 = 自恋型，不稳定 = 边缘型，侵犯权利 = 反社会型。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":826,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_7","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.635","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.635.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.635.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,41],"fullStemEn":"A client with schizophrenia is exhibiting a state where they remain in the same fixed position for long periods and exhibit 'waxy flexibility'.","fullStemZh":"一名患有精神分裂症的患者表现出长时间保持同一固定姿势的状态，并表现出“蜡样屈曲”。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with schizophrenia is exhibiting a state where they remain in the same fixed position for long periods and exhibit 'waxy flexibility'.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名患有精神分裂症的患者表现出长时间保持同一固定姿势的状态，并表现出“蜡样屈曲”。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse identifies this as {{1}}, which is a {{2}} symptom of schizophrenia.","zh":"护士将其识别为 {{1}}，这是精神分裂症的一种 {{2}} 症状。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"catatonia","zh":"紧张症"},{"id":"o3","en":"anhedonia","zh":"情感淡漠"},{"id":"o2","en":"akathisia","zh":"静坐不能"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"cognitive","zh":"认知"},{"id":"o2","en":"negative","zh":"阴性"},{"id":"o1","en":"positive","zh":"阳性"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Catatonia includes motor behaviors like waxy flexibility and is considered a positive symptom (an addition to normal behavior).","rationaleCorrectZh":"紧张症包括蜡样屈曲等运动行为，被认为是一种阳性症状（在正常行为基础上的增加）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the definitions of positive vs negative symptoms. Positive symptoms are 'excessive' behaviors (hallucinations, delusions, catatonia), while negative symptoms are 'missing' behaviors (apathy, social withdrawal).","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆阳性症状与阴性症状的定义。阳性症状是“过度的”行为（幻觉、妄想、紧张症），而阴性症状是“缺失的”行为（冷漠、社交退缩）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":827,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch1_8","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.636","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.636.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.636.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,78],"fullStemEn":"The spouse of a client who died unexpectedly says, 'I should have known he was sick. I should have made him go to the doctor sooner.' The nurse identifies this as which stage of grief according to Kübler-Ross?","fullStemZh":"一名意外去世患者的配偶说：“我早该知道他生病了。我早该让他早点去看医生。” 根据库伯勒-罗丝（Kübler-Ross）的理论，护士将此识别为悲伤的哪个阶段？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse identifies this as which stage of grief according to Kübler-Ross?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据库伯勒-罗丝（Kübler-Ross）的理论，护士将此识别为悲伤的哪个阶段？","penultimateSentenceEn":"I should have made him go to the doctor sooner.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"我早该让他早点去看医生。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Denial","zh":"否认期"},{"id":"C","en":"Depression","zh":"忧郁期"},{"id":"A","en":"Anger","zh":"愤怒期"},{"id":"D","en":"Bargaining","zh":"协议期（讨价还价）"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bargaining often involves 'if only' or 'I should have' statements as the individual tries to regain control or make sense of the loss through hypothetical scenarios.","rationaleCorrectZh":"协议期通常涉及“如果当初”或“我本应该”之类的陈述，因为个体试图通过假设情景来重新获得控制权或理解失去的意义。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the stages: Anger is often outward; Bargaining is often inward 'what if' or 'if only' reasoning.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分各个阶段：愤怒通常是向外的；协议期通常是向内的“如果……会怎样”或“如果当初……”的推理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"I should have made him go to the doctor sooner.'","controlSentenceZh":"我早该让他早点去看医生。”"}
{"queueIndex":828,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.637","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.637.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.637.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[146,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,58],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with major depressive disorder tells the nurse, \"I'm a burden to my family. They would be much better off if I weren't around.\" Which of the following is the most therapeutic response by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名因重性抑郁障碍入院的患者告诉护士：“我是家人的负担。如果我不在了，他们会过得更好。”护士以下哪项回应最具治疗性？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following is the most therapeutic response by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士以下哪项回应最具治疗性？","penultimateSentenceEn":"They would be much better off if I weren't around.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果我不在了，他们会过得更好。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"\"I'll stay here with you, and we can talk about something else to distract you.\"","zh":"“我会留在这里陪你，我们可以聊聊别的事情来分散注意力。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"It sounds like you are feeling very worthless and hopeless right now.\"","zh":"“听起来你现在感到非常无价值和绝望。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"Why do you feel like you are a burden?\"","zh":"“为什么你觉得你是负担？”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"Don't think that way; your family loves you and wants you to get better.\"","zh":"“别那样想；你的家人爱你，希望你康复。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct response is an example of reflection and validation of the client's feelings. It acknowledges the client's emotional state without judgment and encourages further expression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的回答是对患者感受的反映和确认。它在不加评判的情况下承认患者的情绪状态，并鼓励进一步表达。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the client's feelings. Avoid \"why\" questions and false reassurance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注患者的感受。避免使用“为什么”提问和虚假的安慰。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":829,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.638","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.638.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.638.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,41],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is monitoring a client who is experiencing alcohol withdrawal. Which of the following clinical manifestations should the nurse expect? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在监测一名正在经历酒精戒断的患者。护士应预期出现以下哪些临床表现？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following clinical manifestations should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预期出现以下哪些临床表现？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"E","en":"Hypotension","zh":"低血压"},{"id":"D","en":"Profuse diaphoresis","zh":"大量出汗"},{"id":"C","en":"Visual hallucinations","zh":"视幻觉"},{"id":"F","en":"Agitation and restlessness","zh":"烦躁不安"},{"id":"A","en":"Fine tremors of the hands","zh":"手部细微震颤"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Alcohol withdrawal typically causes autonomic hyperactivity (tachycardia, diaphoresis), tremors, agitation, and sensory disturbances such as hallucinations.","rationaleCorrectZh":"酒精戒断通常引起自主神经系统过度活跃（心动过速、多汗）、震颤、烦躁以及视幻觉等感觉障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the symptoms of CNS irritability associated with alcohol withdrawal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想与酒精戒断相关的中枢神经系统易激惹症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":830,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.639","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.639.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.639.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[180,241],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,70],"fullStemEn":"A client with schizophrenia is observed talking to the wall and appears to be listening to something. The client says, \"Do you hear them? The voices are telling me I'm in danger!\" Which of the following responses by the nurse is appropriate?","fullStemZh":"护士观察到一名患有精神分裂症的患者正在对着墙说话，似乎在倾听什么。患者说：“你听到了吗？那些声音告诉我我有危险！”护士以下哪项回应是恰当的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following responses by the nurse is appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士以下哪项回应是恰当的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The voices are telling me I'm in danger!\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"那些声音告诉我我有危险！”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"\"What are the voices telling you specifically?\"","zh":"“那些声音具体在告诉你什么？”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"I don't hear any voices, but I can see that you are feeling frightened.\"","zh":"“我没有听到任何声音，但我看得出你感到很害怕。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"Try to ignore the voices; they aren't real.\"","zh":"“试着忽略那些声音；它们不是真的。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"There are no voices. You are safe here in the hospital.\"","zh":"“没有声音。你在医院里很安全。”"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should acknowledge the client's feelings (validation) while also stating their own perception of reality without directly challenging the client's hallucination.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应承认患者的感受（确认），同时也陈述自己对现实的认知，而不是直接挑战患者的幻觉。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Present reality and acknowledge feelings without validating the hallucination content.","testTakingStrategyZh":"呈现现实并承认感受，但不要确认幻觉内容。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":831,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.640","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.640.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.640.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[206,275],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,78],"fullStemEn":"A client on a psychiatric unit becomes increasingly agitated and begins throwing chairs at other clients. Despite verbal de-escalation attempts, the client's behavior escalates, posing an immediate danger. Place the following nursing actions in the correct order of priority.","fullStemZh":"精神科病房的一名患者变得越来越烦躁，并开始向其他患者扔椅子。尽管护士尝试了言语去升级，但患者的行为进一步升级，构成了直接危险。请按优先顺序排列以下护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing actions in the correct order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列以下护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Despite verbal de-escalation attempts, the client's behavior escalates, posing an immediate danger.","penultimateSentenceZh":"尽管护士尝试了言语去升级，但患者的行为进一步升级，构成了直接危险。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Direct other clients to a safe area away from the agitated client.","zh":"引导其他患者到远离烦躁患者的安全区域。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the events leading up to the restraint and the client's response.","zh":"记录导致约束的事件以及患者的反应。"},{"id":"B","en":"Restrain the client using mechanical restraints as per protocol.","zh":"按照规程使用机械约束装置约束患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and obtain a written order for restraints.","zh":"通知医疗保健提供者并获取约束的书面医嘱。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safety is the first priority. First, protect others. Then, use the least restrictive means necessary to stabilize the client, which in an emergency may include immediate restraint. Following the emergency application, a provider's order must be obtained. Documentation follows the intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全是第一位的。首先，保护他人（A）。然后，使用必要的最小限制手段来稳定患者，在紧急情况下可能包括立即约束（B）。在紧急应用之后，必须获得提供者的医嘱（C）。记录（D）在干预之后进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the safety-first principle. Protect others before intervening directly with the source of danger.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用安全第一原则。在直接干预危险源之前，先保护他人。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":832,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.641","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.641.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.641.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[341,369],"terminalOffsetsZh":[95,103],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is being treated with lithium carbonate. The nurse should monitor the client's serum lithium levels closely. What is the therapeutic reference range for lithium during the maintenance phase of treatment? (Enter the lower limit of the range in the first blank and the upper limit in the second blank, in mEq/L. Round to one decimal place.)","fullStemZh":"一名患有双相情感障碍的患者正在接受碳酸锂治疗。护士应密切监测患者的血清锂水平。维持期治疗中锂的治疗参考范围是多少？（在第一个空格中输入范围的下限，在第二个空格中输入上限，单位为 mEq/L。保留一位小数。）","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to one decimal place.)","terminalSentenceZh":"保留一位小数。）","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Enter the lower limit of the range in the first blank and the upper limit in the second blank, in mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第一个空格中输入范围的下限，在第二个空格中输入上限，单位为 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Lower limit (mEq/L)","zh":"下限 (mEq/L)"},"acceptable":["0.6"],"numeric":{"value":0.6,"tolerance":0.1,"unit":"mEq/L"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Upper limit (mEq/L)","zh":"上限 (mEq/L)"},"acceptable":["1.2"],"numeric":{"value":1.2,"tolerance":0.1,"unit":"mEq/L"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The therapeutic range for lithium during maintenance is generally 0.6 to 1.2 mEq/L. Levels above 1.5 mEq/L are considered toxic.","rationaleCorrectZh":"维持期间锂的治疗范围通常为 0.6 至 1.2 mEq/L。高于 1.5 mEq/L 的水平被视为中毒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall standard therapeutic ranges for psychotropic medications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想精神类药物的标准治疗范围。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":833,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.642","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.642.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.642.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,46],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is evaluating clients' use of defense mechanisms. Match each client statement or behavior with the corresponding defense mechanism it illustrates.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估患者对防御机制的使用情况。将每位患者的陈述或行为与它所说明的相应防御机制相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each client statement or behavior with the corresponding defense mechanism it illustrates.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每位患者的陈述或行为与它所说明的相应防御机制相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is evaluating clients' use of defense mechanisms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估患者对防御机制的使用情况。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"\"I didn't get the promotion because my boss is jealous of my skills.\"","zh":"“我没得到晋升是因为我的老板嫉妒我的能力。”"},{"id":"r2","en":"\"I'm not angry with my spouse; I'm just upset with my coworker's laziness.\"","zh":"“我没有生我配偶的气；我只是对我同事的懒惰感到不满。”"},{"id":"r3","en":"A person who was recently diagnosed with cancer starts researching all the latest medical treatments and statistics.","zh":"一个最近被诊断出患有癌症的人开始研究所有最新的医疗方法和统计数据。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Displacement","zh":"转移/置换"},{"id":"c3","en":"Intellectualization","zh":"理智化"},{"id":"c1","en":"Rationalization","zh":"合理化"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rationalization involves justifying behaviors or failures with logical-sounding but incorrect reasons. Displacement is shifting impulses from an unacceptable target to a more acceptable one. Intellectualization is using logic and facts to distance oneself from emotional pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合理化包括用听起来合乎逻辑但错误的原因来证明行为或失败的合理性。转移是将冲动从不可接受的目标转移到更容易接受的目标。理智化是利用逻辑和事实使自己与情感痛苦保持距离。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the key features of various ego defense mechanisms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分各种自我防御机制的关键特征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":834,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.643","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.643.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.643.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,41],"fullStemEn":"A client who recently lost a child in an accident states, \"I can't believe this is happening. There must be some mistake with the identification.\"","fullStemZh":"一名最近在事故中失去孩子的患者说：“我不相信这是真的。身份确认一定出了什么差错。”","terminalSentenceEn":"There must be some mistake with the identification.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"身份确认一定出了什么差错。”","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who recently lost a child in an accident states, \"I can't believe this is happening.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名最近在事故中失去孩子的患者说：“我不相信这是真的。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"According to Kübler-Ross, the client is exhibiting the stage of {{1}}, which is often followed by {{2}} as the client begins to acknowledge the reality of the loss.","zh":"根据库伯勒-罗斯（Kübler-Ross）的理论，该患者表现出 {{1}} 阶段，随后通常是 {{2}}，因为患者开始承认失去的现实。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"Denial","zh":"否认"},{"id":"o2","en":"Bargaining","zh":"讨价还价"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"Anger","zh":"愤怒"},{"id":"o2","en":"Acceptance","zh":"接受"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The initial reaction to loss is often denial, marked by shock and disbelief. Anger typically follows denial in the Kübler-Ross model as the reality sets in.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对失去的最初反应通常是否认，以震惊和怀疑为特征。在库伯勒-罗斯模型中，随着现实的显现，愤怒通常紧随否认之后。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the sequential stages of the Kübler-Ross grief model: Denial, Anger, Bargaining, Depression, Acceptance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想库伯勒-罗斯悲伤模型的顺序阶段：否认、愤怒、讨价还价、抑郁、接受。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":835,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.644","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.644.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.644.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[222,276],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,76],"fullStemEn":"A nurse in an emergency department is assessing a 6-year-old child with multiple bruises in various stages of healing and a fractured arm. The parent's explanation of the injury is inconsistent with the physical findings. Which of the following is the priority nursing action?","fullStemZh":"急诊科护士正在评估一名 6 岁儿童，该儿童身上有处于不同愈合阶段的多处淤伤和一处手臂骨折。家长对伤情的解释与身体检查结果不符。以下哪项是优先的护理措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following is the priority nursing action?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项是优先的护理措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The parent's explanation of the injury is inconsistent with the physical findings.","penultimateSentenceZh":"家长对伤情的解释与身体检查结果不符。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Question the parent further about the details of the accident.","zh":"进一步询问家长关于事故的细节。"},{"id":"A","en":"Provide a safe environment for the child and treat the physical injuries.","zh":"为儿童提供安全的环境并治疗身体损伤。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the child's injuries and the parent's statements in the medical record.","zh":"在医疗记录中记录儿童的伤情和家长的陈述。"},{"id":"B","en":"Report the suspected abuse to the appropriate local authorities.","zh":"向当地有关部门报告疑似虐待行为。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nurses are mandatory reporters of suspected child abuse. Reporting to the appropriate authorities is a legal and professional requirement when abuse is suspected based on findings like inconsistent histories and injuries in different stages of healing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士是疑似儿童虐待的强制报告人。当基于不一致的病史和处于不同愈合阶段的损伤等发现怀疑存在虐待时，向有关部门报告是法律和职业要求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the legal responsibility of mandatory reporting for vulnerable populations.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别对弱势群体进行强制报告的法律责任。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The parent's explanation of the injury is inconsistent with the physical findings.","controlSentenceZh":"家长对伤情的解释与身体检查结果不符。"}
{"queueIndex":836,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.645","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.645.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.645.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,45],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing end-of-life care for a client from a different cultural background. Which of the following actions demonstrate cultural sensitivity? (Select all that apply.)","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名具有不同文化背景的患者提供临终关怀。以下哪些行为体现了文化敏感性？（多选题）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Select all that apply.)","terminalSentenceZh":"多选题）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions demonstrate cultural sensitivity?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些行为体现了文化敏感性？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Assessing who the client identifies as the primary decision-maker in the family.","zh":"评估患者认定的家庭主要决策者是谁。"},{"id":"A","en":"Asking the family about specific religious or spiritual rituals they wish to perform.","zh":"询问家人他们希望进行的具体宗教或精神仪式。"},{"id":"D","en":"Providing a translator if the client or family has limited English proficiency.","zh":"如果患者或家人的英语能力有限，则提供翻译。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assuming the client wants a quiet environment without many visitors.","zh":"假设患者想要一个没有太多访客的安静环境。"},{"id":"E","en":"Encouraging the family to strictly follow the hospital's visiting hour policies.","zh":"鼓励家人严格遵守医院的探视时间政策。"}],"correct":["A","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cultural sensitivity involves active assessment of individual preferences, family dynamics, and communication needs, rather than relying on assumptions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"文化敏感性涉及对个人偏好、家庭动态和沟通需求的积极评估，而不是依赖假设。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid options that involve making assumptions or applying rigid policies to cultural situations.","testTakingStrategyZh":"避免选择涉及做出假设或将僵硬政策应用于文化情境的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":837,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gen_psi_batch2_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.646","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.646.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.646.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[145,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,59],"fullStemEn":"A client with obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD) spends several hours each day performing handwashing rituals, which has caused skin breakdown. Which of the following nursing interventions is most appropriate during the initial phase of treatment?","fullStemZh":"一名患有强迫症（OCD）的患者每天花费数小时进行洗手仪式，这导致了皮肤破损。在治疗的初始阶段，以下哪项护理措施最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing interventions is most appropriate during the initial phase of treatment?","terminalSentenceZh":"在治疗的初始阶段，以下哪项护理措施最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD) spends several hours each day performing handwashing rituals, which has caused skin breakdown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有强迫症（OCD）的患者每天花费数小时进行洗手仪式，这导致了皮肤破损。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Forbid the client from performing the rituals to prevent further skin damage.","zh":"禁止患者进行仪式以防止进一步的皮肤损伤。"},{"id":"C","en":"Allow the client time to perform the rituals but set limits on the frequency.","zh":"允许患者有时间进行仪式，但限制频率。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer anti-anxiety medication immediately before the ritual begins.","zh":"在仪式开始前立即给予抗焦虑药物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Distract the client with other activities whenever the urge to wash hands occurs.","zh":"每当出现洗手的冲动时，用其他活动分散患者的注意力。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In the initial phase of OCD treatment, the nurse should allow the client to perform rituals to prevent extreme anxiety, while gradually setting limits to reduce the behavior and its complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在强迫症治疗的初始阶段，护士应允许患者进行仪式以防止极度焦虑，同时逐渐设定限制以减少该行为及其并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that rituals in OCD are a defense against anxiety; stopping them abruptly without other coping mechanisms is detrimental.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住强迫症中的仪式是对抗焦虑的一种防御；在没有其他应对机制的情况下突然停止仪式是有害的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD) spends several hours each day performing handwashing rituals, which has caused skin breakdown.","controlSentenceZh":"一名患有强迫症（OCD）的患者每天花费数小时进行洗手仪式，这导致了皮肤破损。"}
{"queueIndex":838,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_prioritization_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.647","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.647.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.647.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[35,78],"terminalOffsetsZh":[8,20],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is receiving shift report. Which client should the nurse assess first?","fullStemZh":"护士正在交接班。护士应首先评估哪位患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should the nurse assess first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先评估哪位患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is receiving shift report.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在交接班。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"A client with asthma who has new onset wheezing and shortness of breath.","zh":"患有哮喘且新发喘息和呼吸急促的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client reporting pain of 4 on a 0-10 scale after surgery.","zh":"术后报告疼痛评分为4分（0-10分制）的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client who needs a routine dressing change.","zh":"需要进行常规敷料更换的患者。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client waiting for discharge instructions.","zh":"正在等待出院指导的患者。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to the airway, breathing, circulation (ABC) priority framework, a client with new onset wheezing and shortness of breath requires immediate assessment and intervention to ensure a patent airway and adequate oxygenation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据气道、呼吸、循环（ABC）优先级框架，新发喘息和呼吸急促的患者需要立即评估和干预，以确保气道通畅和充足的氧合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) to prioritize client needs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）原则来优先处理患者的需求。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":839,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_prioritization_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.648","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.648.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.648.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Which task is most appropriate for the registered nurse (RN) to delegate to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","fullStemZh":"注册护士（RN）最适合将哪项任务委托给无执照辅助人员（UAP）？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which task is most appropriate for the registered nurse (RN) to delegate to unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?","terminalSentenceZh":"注册护士（RN）最适合将哪项任务委托给无执照辅助人员（UAP）？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administering oral pain medication.","zh":"给予口服止痛药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assisting a stable client with ambulation to the bathroom.","zh":"协助病情稳定的患者步行去卫生间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Providing teaching on a newly prescribed medication.","zh":"提供关于新开处方药的健康教育。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assessing a client's lung sounds.","zh":"评估患者的肺音。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"UAP are trained to assist with basic activities of daily living (ADLs) such as ambulation, bathing, and feeding for stable clients. Tasks requiring assessment, nursing judgment, or teaching cannot be delegated to UAP.","rationaleCorrectZh":"UAP经过培训，可以协助病情稳定的患者完成基本的日常生活活动（ADL），如行走、洗澡和进食。需要评估、护理判断或健康教育的任务不能委托给UAP。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the rights of delegation. Do not delegate what you can EAT (Evaluate, Assess, Teach).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住委托的权利。不要委托您可以EAT（评估、评价、教育）的内容。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":840,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_prioritization_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.649","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.649.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.649.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,85],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,26],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is planning care for a group of clients. Which client should be seen first?","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一组患者制定护理计划。应该首先看哪位患者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should be seen first?","terminalSentenceZh":"应该首先看哪位患者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is planning care for a group of clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一组患者制定护理计划。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client with a blood glucose level of 120 mg/dL.","zh":"血糖水平为120 mg/dL的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client who is restless and confused, pulling at their IV line.","zh":"烦躁不安且意识模糊，正在拉扯静脉输液管的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client asking for a cup of water.","zh":"要求喝一杯水的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client reporting nausea after receiving chemotherapy.","zh":"接受化疗后报告恶心的患者。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A client who is restless, confused, and pulling at their IV line poses an immediate safety risk. Restlessness can also be an early sign of hypoxia. This client requires prompt assessment to determine the cause of the confusion and ensure safety.","rationaleCorrectZh":"烦躁不安、意识模糊并拉扯静脉输液管的患者存在直接的安全风险。烦躁也可能是缺氧的早期征兆。该患者需要及时评估以确定意识模糊的原因并确保安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for words indicating a sudden change in condition, such as 'restless' or 'confused', which often signal a physiological problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找表示病情突然发生变化的词语，如“烦躁”或“意识模糊”，这通常预示着生理问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":841,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_prioritization_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.650","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.650.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.650.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,48],"fullStemEn":"Which tasks can a registered nurse (RN) safely delegate to a licensed practical nurse (LPN/LVN)? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"注册护士（RN）可以安全地将哪些任务委托给有执照的实习护士（LPN/LVN）？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which tasks can a registered nurse (RN) safely delegate to a licensed practical nurse (LPN/LVN)?","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士（RN）可以安全地将哪些任务委托给有执照的实习护士（LPN/LVN）？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Developing the initial nursing care plan.","zh":"制定初步护理计划。"},{"id":"E","en":"Monitoring vital signs on a stable client.","zh":"监测病情稳定患者的生命体征。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administering oral medications to a stable client.","zh":"为病情稳定的患者给予口服药物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Performing a routine sterile dressing change.","zh":"执行常规无菌敷料更换。"},{"id":"D","en":"Discharging a client to home with new complex instructions.","zh":"为带有复杂新指示的患者办理出院。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"LPNs/LVNs can perform routine tasks on stable clients, including administering oral medications, performing sterile procedures like dressing changes, and monitoring vital signs. They cannot create initial care plans or provide initial complex teaching, as these require RN-level assessment and judgment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"LPN/LVN可以对病情稳定的患者执行常规任务，包括口服给药、执行换药等无菌操作以及监测生命体征。他们不能制定初步护理计划或提供初步的复杂教育，因为这些需要RN级别的评估和判断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate the LPN/LVN role with stable clients and expected outcomes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将LPN/LVN的角色与稳定的患者和预期的结果联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":842,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_prioritization_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.651","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.651.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.651.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,31],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is determining which client requires the most immediate attention. Which finding is the highest priority?","fullStemZh":"护士正在确定哪位患者需要最紧急的关注。哪个发现具有最高优先级？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding is the highest priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪个发现具有最高优先级？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is determining which client requires the most immediate attention.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在确定哪位患者需要最紧急的关注。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A client who is actively bleeding from a surgical wound.","zh":"手术伤口有活动性出血的患者。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client requesting a sleep medication.","zh":"要求服用安眠药的患者。"},{"id":"B","en":"A client with a temperature of 99.2 °F (37.3 °C).","zh":"体温为99.2 °F (37.3 °C)的患者。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with an oxygen saturation of 96% on room air.","zh":"呼吸室内空气时氧饱和度为96%的患者。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Active bleeding is a circulatory emergency that can quickly lead to hypovolemic shock. According to the ABC (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) prioritization framework, this requires immediate intervention to control the hemorrhage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"活动性出血是循环系统急症，可迅速导致低血容量性休克。根据ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）优先级框架，这需要立即干预以控制出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize physiological needs over psychological needs, and acute problems over chronic or stable conditions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先考虑生理需求而不是心理需求，优先处理急性问题而不是慢性或稳定的状况。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":843,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_legal_ethical_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.652","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.652.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.652.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[149,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,49],"fullStemEn":"A client tells the nurse, 'I do not want to receive any more treatments for my cancer.' The nurse respects the client's right to make this decision. Which ethical principle is the nurse demonstrating?","fullStemZh":"患者告诉护士：“我不想再接受任何癌症治疗了。”护士尊重患者做此决定的权利。护士展示了哪项伦理原则？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which ethical principle is the nurse demonstrating?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士展示了哪项伦理原则？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse respects the client's right to make this decision.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士尊重患者做此决定的权利。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Justice","zh":"公正原则"},{"id":"B","en":"Autonomy","zh":"自主原则"},{"id":"C","en":"Beneficence","zh":"行善原则"},{"id":"A","en":"Fidelity","zh":"忠诚原则"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Autonomy is the ethical principle that respects a client's right to self-determination and to make decisions regarding their own health care, even if the health care team disagrees with those decisions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"自主原则是尊重患者自我决定权和对自身医疗保健做出决定的权利的伦理原则，即使医疗团队不同意这些决定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'autonomy' with 'independence' and the 'right to choose'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“自主”与“独立”和“选择的权利”联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":844,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_legal_ethical_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.653","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.653.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.653.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"Before a client undergoes a scheduled surgical procedure, who is responsible for explaining the risks, benefits, and alternatives of the surgery to obtain informed consent?","fullStemZh":"在患者进行计划的手术之前，谁负责解释手术的风险、益处和替代方案以获取知情同意？","terminalSentenceEn":"Before a client undergoes a scheduled surgical procedure, who is responsible for explaining the risks, benefits, and alternatives of the surgery to obtain informed consent?","terminalSentenceZh":"在患者进行计划的手术之前，谁负责解释手术的风险、益处和替代方案以获取知情同意？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"The charge nurse","zh":"护士长/主管护士"},{"id":"B","en":"The registered nurse (RN)","zh":"注册护士（RN）"},{"id":"C","en":"The anesthesiologist","zh":"麻醉师"},{"id":"A","en":"The healthcare provider performing the procedure","zh":"执行手术的医疗保健提供者（医生）"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"It is the legal responsibility of the healthcare provider (e.g., surgeon or physician) performing the procedure to explain the risks, benefits, and alternatives to obtain informed consent. The nurse's role is to witness the client's signature and ensure the client understands.","rationaleCorrectZh":"执行手术的医疗保健提供者（如外科医生或医师）有法律责任解释风险、益处和替代方案以获取知情同意。护士的作用是见证患者的签名并确保患者理解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the person performing the procedure is legally responsible for obtaining informed consent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住执行手术的人在法律上负责获得知情同意。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":845,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_legal_ethical_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.654","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.654.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.654.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,47],"fullStemEn":"A nurse medicates a client with a pain medication without the client's permission because the nurse believes it is best for the client. This action is an example of which intentional tort?","fullStemZh":"护士未经患者允许给患者服用止痛药，因为护士认为这对患者最好。这种行为是哪种故意侵权行为的例子？","terminalSentenceEn":"This action is an example of which intentional tort?","terminalSentenceZh":"这种行为是哪种故意侵权行为的例子？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse medicates a client with a pain medication without the client's permission because the nurse believes it is best for the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士未经患者允许给患者服用止痛药，因为护士认为这对患者最好。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Negligence","zh":"疏忽"},{"id":"D","en":"Assault","zh":"恐吓（Assault）"},{"id":"B","en":"False imprisonment","zh":"非法拘禁"},{"id":"C","en":"Battery","zh":"殴打/非法接触（Battery）"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Battery is the intentional and wrongful physical contact with a person that entails an injury or offensive touching. Administering a medication or performing a procedure without a client's consent constitutes battery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"殴打/非法接触（Battery）是指故意且不当的与人身体接触，导致伤害或冒犯性触摸。未经患者同意给予药物或执行操作构成Battery。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate assault (the threat) from battery (the physical act).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分恐吓（威胁）和非法接触（身体行为）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":846,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_legal_ethical_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.655","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.655.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.655.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,41],"fullStemEn":"A nurse promises to return to a client's room in 15 minutes to provide pain medication and returns exactly as promised. The nurse is demonstrating which ethical principle?","fullStemZh":"护士承诺在15分钟后回到患者病房提供止痛药，并如约返回。护士正在展示哪项伦理原则？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse is demonstrating which ethical principle?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士正在展示哪项伦理原则？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse promises to return to a client's room in 15 minutes to provide pain medication and returns exactly as promised.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士承诺在15分钟后回到患者病房提供止痛药，并如约返回。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Nonmaleficence","zh":"不伤害原则"},{"id":"A","en":"Veracity","zh":"诚实原则"},{"id":"C","en":"Fidelity","zh":"忠诚原则"},{"id":"D","en":"Justice","zh":"公正原则"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fidelity is the ethical principle that involves keeping promises and being faithful to one's commitments. Returning when promised builds trust and demonstrates fidelity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"忠诚原则是涉及信守承诺和忠实于自己承诺的伦理原则。如约返回可以建立信任并展示忠诚原则。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link the word 'fidelity' with 'loyalty' and 'keeping promises'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“忠诚（fidelity）”一词与“忠实”和“信守承诺”联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":847,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_legal_ethical_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.656","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.656.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.656.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Under which circumstance is it legally acceptable for a nurse to breach client confidentiality?","fullStemZh":"在什么情况下，护士泄露患者机密在法律上是可以接受的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Under which circumstance is it legally acceptable for a nurse to breach client confidentiality?","terminalSentenceZh":"在什么情况下，护士泄露患者机密在法律上是可以接受的？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"When a client's employer calls to ask why the client is hospitalized.","zh":"当患者的雇主打电话询问患者为何住院时。"},{"id":"C","en":"When discussing an interesting case with a nurse on another unit.","zh":"在与另一个病区的护士讨论有趣的病例时。"},{"id":"D","en":"When reporting suspected child or elder abuse to authorities.","zh":"当向当局报告疑似虐待儿童或老人的情况时。"},{"id":"A","en":"When the client's adult child asks to see the medical record without the client's permission.","zh":"当患者的成年子女在未经患者允许的情况下要求查看医疗记录时。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nurses are mandated reporters, meaning they are legally required to breach confidentiality and report suspected abuse of vulnerable populations (children and elders) to appropriate authorities to protect them from harm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士是强制报告人，这意味着法律要求他们打破保密规定，向有关当局报告疑似虐待弱势群体（儿童和老人）的情况，以保护他们免受伤害。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that protecting vulnerable populations (like children and the elderly) overrides general confidentiality rules.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住，保护弱势群体（如儿童和老人）的优先级高于一般的保密规定。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":848,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_med_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.657","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.657.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.657.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,36],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer a medication to a client. Which action is the most important to ensure the 'right client' before administration?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备给患者服药。在服药前，为确保是“正确的患者”，哪项行动最重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the most important to ensure the 'right client' before administration?","terminalSentenceZh":"在服药前，为确保是“正确的患者”，哪项行动最重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer a medication to a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备给患者服药。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Check the room number on the client's door.","zh":"核对患者门上的房间号。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the client's visitor to confirm the client's name.","zh":"请患者的访客确认患者的姓名。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask the client, 'Are you Mr. Smith?'","zh":"询问患者：“您是史密斯先生吗？”"},{"id":"A","en":"Check the client's identification band against the Medication Administration Record (MAR).","zh":"将患者的身份识别带与给药记录（MAR）进行核对。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using two acceptable client identifiers (e.g., name and date of birth) by checking the ID band against the MAR is the standard and safest method to ensure the right client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"通过核对身份识别带和给药记录（MAR），使用两种可接受的患者识别信息（如姓名和出生日期）是确保患者身份正确的最标准、最安全的方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the 'Rights of Medication Administration'. Never use room numbers for identification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住“给药原则”。切勿使用房间号进行身份识别。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":849,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_med_safety_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.658","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.658.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.658.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"When should the nurse document that a PRN pain medication was administered to a client?","fullStemZh":"护士应在何时记录给予患者PRN（按需）止痛药的情况？","terminalSentenceEn":"When should the nurse document that a PRN pain medication was administered to a client?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应在何时记录给予患者PRN（按需）止痛药的情况？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"At the end of the shift.","zh":"在班次结束时。"},{"id":"B","en":"Immediately after the medication is administered.","zh":"在给药后立即记录。"},{"id":"A","en":"When the next dose is due.","zh":"在下一次给药时间到时。"},{"id":"D","en":"Before entering the client's room.","zh":"在进入患者病房之前。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Medications must be documented immediately after administration to maintain an accurate, real-time record and prevent another nurse from accidentally administering a duplicate dose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"药物必须在给药后立即记录，以保持准确的实时记录，并防止另一位护士意外重复给药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For any nursing action, documentation should occur 'immediately after' the intervention is completed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于任何护理操作，应在干预完成后“立即”进行记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":850,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_med_safety_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.659","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.659.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.659.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,31],"fullStemEn":"A provider prescribes a medication to be given 'PO'. Which route will the nurse use to administer this medication?","fullStemZh":"医生开具了一种“PO”给药途径的药物。护士将使用哪种途径给药？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which route will the nurse use to administer this medication?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士将使用哪种途径给药？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider prescribes a medication to be given 'PO'.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医生开具了一种“PO”给药途径的药物。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Rectally","zh":"直肠给药"},{"id":"A","en":"Intramuscularly","zh":"肌肉注射"},{"id":"C","en":"Intravenously","zh":"静脉注射"},{"id":"D","en":"By mouth (orally)","zh":"经口（口服）"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The abbreviation 'PO' stands for 'per os', which is Latin for 'by mouth' or orally.","rationaleCorrectZh":"缩写“PO”代表“per os”，这是拉丁语，意为“经口”或口服。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize common medical abbreviations used in pharmacology.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住药理学中常用的医学缩写。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":851,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_med_safety_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.660","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.660.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.660.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,93],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,25],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers a medication error has occurred. What is the nurse's first priority action?","fullStemZh":"护士发现发生了用药错误。护士的首要优先行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's first priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要优先行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers a medication error has occurred.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现发生了用药错误。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Fill out an incident report.","zh":"填写事件报告。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the healthcare provider.","zh":"通知医疗保健提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess the client for adverse effects.","zh":"评估患者是否有不良反应。"},{"id":"B","en":"Inform the nurse manager.","zh":"通知护士长。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first step after a medication error is to assess the client's physiological condition to ensure their safety and identify any immediate harm. Once the client is assessed and stabilized, the nurse will notify the provider and file an incident report.","rationaleCorrectZh":"发生用药错误后的第一步是评估患者的生理状况，以确保他们的安全并确定是否有直接伤害。一旦患者得到评估并稳定下来，护士将通知医生并提交事件报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a mistake happens, always check the client first. Assessment is the first step of the nursing process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"发生错误时，请始终首先检查患者。评估是护理过程的第一步。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":852,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_med_safety_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.661","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.661.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.661.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,76],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Which of the following is a component of a complete medication prescription?","fullStemZh":"以下哪一项是完整药物处方的组成部分？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following is a component of a complete medication prescription?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪一项是完整药物处方的组成部分？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The frequency of administration.","zh":"给药频率。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client's weight.","zh":"患者的体重。"},{"id":"A","en":"The pharmacy's phone number.","zh":"药房的电话号码。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client's room number.","zh":"患者的房间号。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A complete medication prescription must include the client's name, date/time written, medication name, dosage, route, frequency, and provider signature.","rationaleCorrectZh":"完整的药物处方必须包括患者姓名、开具日期/时间、药物名称、剂量、途径、给药频率和医生签名。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the elements of a valid prescription to prevent medication errors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆有效处方的要素，以防止用药错误。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":853,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_adult_health_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.662","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.662.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.662.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,40],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing an acute exacerbation of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). What is the primary goal of nursing care for this client?","fullStemZh":"一位患者正经历慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）急性加重。该患者护理的主要目标是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the primary goal of nursing care for this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"该患者护理的主要目标是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is experiencing an acute exacerbation of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者正经历慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）急性加重。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Preparing the client for a lung transplant.","zh":"准备患者进行肺移植。"},{"id":"C","en":"Encouraging strenuous physical exercise.","zh":"鼓励进行剧烈的体育锻炼。"},{"id":"A","en":"Improving oxygenation and relieving dyspnea.","zh":"改善氧合并缓解呼吸困难。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administering a high-calorie diet.","zh":"给予高热量饮食。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In an acute exacerbation of COPD, the client struggles with gas exchange. The primary goal is to improve oxygenation, relieve shortness of breath (dyspnea), and stabilize the airway.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在COPD急性加重时，患者的气体交换困难。主要目标是改善氧合，缓解呼吸急促（呼吸困难），稳定气道。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs. COPD directly impacts 'B' (Breathing).","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用ABC原则。COPD直接影响“B”（呼吸）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":854,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_adult_health_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.663","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.663.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.663.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing intervention is most effective in preventing pressure injuries in a bedridden older adult?","fullStemZh":"哪项护理干预在预防卧床老年人发生压力性损伤方面最有效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing intervention is most effective in preventing pressure injuries in a bedridden older adult?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项护理干预在预防卧床老年人发生压力性损伤方面最有效？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Using a donut-shaped cushion under the sacrum.","zh":"在骶骨下使用环形垫。"},{"id":"B","en":"Massaging reddened bony prominences vigorously.","zh":"用力按摩发红的骨突处。"},{"id":"C","en":"Repositioning the client every 2 hours.","zh":"每2小时为患者重新翻身定位。"},{"id":"A","en":"Keeping the head of the bed elevated at 90 degrees.","zh":"将床头保持在90度抬高。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Frequent repositioning (at least every 2 hours) is the cornerstone of pressure injury prevention because it relieves sustained pressure on bony prominences.","rationaleCorrectZh":"频繁变换体位（至少每2小时一次）是预防压力性损伤的基石，因为它缓解了骨突处持续的压力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the basics of skin care: relieve pressure and avoid shear.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住皮肤护理的基础知识：缓解压力，避免剪切力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":855,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_adult_health_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.664","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.664.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.664.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[41,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,34],"fullStemEn":"A client is diagnosed with hypertension. Which lifestyle modification should the nurse teach the client to implement first?","fullStemZh":"一位患者被诊断患有高血压。护士应教导患者首先实施哪种生活方式的改变？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which lifestyle modification should the nurse teach the client to implement first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应教导患者首先实施哪种生活方式的改变？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is diagnosed with hypertension.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者被诊断患有高血压。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Drinking 3 glasses of wine a day for heart health.","zh":"每天喝3杯葡萄酒以有益心脏健康。"},{"id":"D","en":"Beginning unsupervised maximal-effort weightlifting.","zh":"开始无人指导的最大强度举重训练。"},{"id":"C","en":"Avoiding all dietary fats.","zh":"避免所有饮食中的脂肪。"},{"id":"A","en":"Reducing dietary sodium intake.","zh":"减少饮食中钠的摄入。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reducing dietary sodium is a primary, evidence-based lifestyle modification for managing hypertension because excess sodium increases fluid retention and blood pressure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"减少饮食中的钠是控制高血压的首要、基于证据的生活方式改变，因为过量的钠会增加体液滞留和血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Hypertension lifestyle care includes sodium reduction, healthy diet, weight management, and regular aerobic or resistance activity. Reject only unsafe or extreme versions of these measures.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高血压生活方式管理包括减少钠摄入、健康饮食、体重管理及规律的有氧或抗阻运动。只排除不安全或极端的做法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":856,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_adult_health_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.665","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.665.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.665.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,27],"fullStemEn":"A client asks why they need to check their blood sugar before meals. What is the nurse's best response?","fullStemZh":"患者询问为什么饭前需要测量血糖。护士的最佳回答是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's best response?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的最佳回答是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client asks why they need to check their blood sugar before meals.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者询问为什么饭前需要测量血糖。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"It tells us how much insulin your pancreas produced yesterday.","zh":"它能告诉我们您的胰腺昨天分泌了多少胰岛素。"},{"id":"B","en":"It prevents you from getting type 1 diabetes.","zh":"它可以防止您患上1型糖尿病。"},{"id":"C","en":"It helps determine the correct dose of insulin you need before eating.","zh":"它有助于确定您进食前所需的正确胰岛素剂量。"},{"id":"D","en":"It confirms that you are drinking enough water.","zh":"它能确认您是否喝了足够的水。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pre-meal blood glucose monitoring is essential for determining how much short- or rapid-acting insulin is needed to cover the carbohydrates about to be eaten (sliding scale or carb-counting).","rationaleCorrectZh":"餐前血糖监测对于确定需要多少短效或速效胰岛素来覆盖即将摄入的碳水化合物（滑动刻度或碳水化合物计数）至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Relate blood glucose monitoring timing to insulin administration protocols.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将血糖监测的时间与胰岛素给药方案联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":857,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_adult_health_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.666","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.666.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.666.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"To promote sleep for a hospitalized adult client, which nursing action is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"为了促进住院成年患者的睡眠，哪项护理行动最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"To promote sleep for a hospitalized adult client, which nursing action is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了促进住院成年患者的睡眠，哪项护理行动最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Leaving the television on at a high volume.","zh":"大音量开着电视。"},{"id":"A","en":"Offering a large cup of coffee right before bed.","zh":"在睡前提供一大杯咖啡。"},{"id":"C","en":"Clustering nursing tasks to avoid frequent interruptions.","zh":"将护理任务集中进行，以避免频繁打扰。"},{"id":"D","en":"Keeping the room brightly lit.","zh":"保持房间明亮。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clustering care minimizes disruptions and allows the client to experience longer, uninterrupted sleep cycles, promoting rest and healing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"集中护理可最大限度地减少干扰，让患者经历更长、不间断的睡眠周期，从而促进休息和愈合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the option that reduces environmental stimuli and interruptions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能减少环境刺激和干扰的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":858,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_perioperative_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.667","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.667.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.667.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,108],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,34],"fullStemEn":"A client is recovering in the Post-Anesthesia Care Unit (PACU). What is the nurse's most immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"患者正在麻醉后护理单元（PACU）恢复。护士最紧迫的优先事项是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's most immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最紧迫的优先事项是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is recovering in the Post-Anesthesia Care Unit (PACU).","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者正在麻醉后护理单元（PACU）恢复。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assessing the client's airway patency.","zh":"评估患者的气道通畅情况。"},{"id":"C","en":"Checking the client's surgical dressing.","zh":"检查患者的手术敷料。"},{"id":"D","en":"Taking the client's temperature.","zh":"测量患者的体温。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administering pain medication.","zh":"给予止痛药。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Following the ABC (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) framework, ensuring an open and patent airway is always the highest priority, especially in a client recovering from anesthesia who is at risk for airway obstruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"遵循ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）框架，确保气道通畅始终是最高优先级，特别是对于正在麻醉恢复中的患者，他们面临气道阻塞的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When asked for the 'most immediate priority', always look for airway issues first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当被问及“最紧迫的优先事项”时，总是先寻找气道问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":859,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_perioperative_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.668","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.668.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.668.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,93],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Why is a client instructed to remain NPO (nothing by mouth) for several hours before surgery?","fullStemZh":"为什么要在手术前要求患者禁食禁水（NPO）数小时？","terminalSentenceEn":"Why is a client instructed to remain NPO (nothing by mouth) for several hours before surgery?","terminalSentenceZh":"为什么要在手术前要求患者禁食禁水（NPO）数小时？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"To make placing an intravenous line easier.","zh":"为了更容易放置静脉输液管。"},{"id":"D","en":"To decrease the need for postoperative pain medication.","zh":"为了减少术后止痛药的需求。"},{"id":"A","en":"To prevent aspiration of stomach contents during anesthesia.","zh":"为了防止麻醉期间胃内容物误吸。"},{"id":"B","en":"To ensure the surgical site stays clean.","zh":"为了确保手术部位保持清洁。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Anesthesia relaxes the esophageal sphincter and abolishes the gag reflex. Fasting prevents food and fluid from regurgitating and being inhaled into the lungs (aspiration), which can cause severe pneumonia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"麻醉会使食管括约肌松弛并消除呕吐反射。禁食可以防止食物和液体反流并吸入肺部（误吸），这可能导致严重的肺炎。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect 'NPO before surgery' to airway protection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“术前NPO”与保护气道联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":860,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_perioperative_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.669","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.669.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.669.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"To prevent postoperative deep vein thrombosis (DVT), which intervention should the nurse encourage?","fullStemZh":"为预防术后深静脉血栓形成（DVT），护士应鼓励哪项干预措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"To prevent postoperative deep vein thrombosis (DVT), which intervention should the nurse encourage?","terminalSentenceZh":"为预防术后深静脉血栓形成（DVT），护士应鼓励哪项干预措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Early ambulation.","zh":"早期下床活动。"},{"id":"C","en":"Crossing the legs while in bed.","zh":"卧床时交叉双腿。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prolonged bed rest.","zh":"长期卧床休息。"},{"id":"A","en":"Placing pillows under the knees.","zh":"在膝盖下放置枕头。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Early ambulation promotes venous return and prevents blood stasis in the lower extremities, significantly reducing the risk of deep vein thrombosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"早期下床活动可促进静脉回流并防止下肢血液淤滞，从而显着降低深静脉血栓形成的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid options that restrict blood flow (crossing legs, pillows under knees). Movement is key for circulation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"避免选择限制血液流动的选项（交叉双腿、膝盖下垫枕头）。运动是循环的关键。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":861,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_perioperative_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.670","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.670.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.670.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,55],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a postoperative client how to use an incentive spirometer. What is the primary purpose of this device?","fullStemZh":"护士正在教导术后患者如何使用诱发性肺量计（Incentive Spirometer）。该设备的主要目的是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the primary purpose of this device?","terminalSentenceZh":"该设备的主要目的是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a postoperative client how to use an incentive spirometer.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教导术后患者如何使用诱发性肺量计（Incentive Spirometer）。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"To measure heart rate.","zh":"测量心率。"},{"id":"D","en":"To prevent atelectasis and pneumonia.","zh":"预防肺不张和肺炎。"},{"id":"B","en":"To deliver aerosolized medications.","zh":"输送气溶胶药物。"},{"id":"A","en":"To clear gastric secretions.","zh":"清除胃分泌物。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An incentive spirometer encourages the client to take deep, sustained breaths. This expands the alveoli, preventing lung collapse (atelectasis) and clearing secretions to prevent pneumonia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"诱发性肺量计鼓励患者进行深长而持久的呼吸。这会扩张肺泡，防止肺萎陷（肺不张）并清除分泌物以预防肺炎。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'spirometer' with the lungs and 'respiratory expansion'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“肺量计”与肺部和“呼吸扩张”联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":862,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_renal_gi_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.671","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.671.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.671.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,31],"fullStemEn":"A client complains of burning during urination and frequent urination. These symptoms are most indicative of which condition?","fullStemZh":"患者主诉排尿时有烧灼感并伴有尿频。这些症状最可能提示什么情况？","terminalSentenceEn":"These symptoms are most indicative of which condition?","terminalSentenceZh":"这些症状最可能提示什么情况？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client complains of burning during urination and frequent urination.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者主诉排尿时有烧灼感并伴有尿频。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Chronic kidney disease","zh":"慢性肾脏病"},{"id":"D","en":"Peptic ulcer disease","zh":"消化性溃疡"},{"id":"A","en":"Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD)","zh":"胃食管反流病（GERD）"},{"id":"C","en":"Urinary tract infection (UTI)","zh":"尿路感染（UTI）"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Burning during urination (dysuria), frequent urination, and urgency are classic symptoms of a urinary tract infection (UTI) due to inflammation of the bladder and urethra.","rationaleCorrectZh":"排尿时的烧灼感（排尿困难）、尿频和尿急是膀胱和尿道炎症引起的尿路感染（UTI）的典型症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize dysuria and frequency as local signs of urinary tract inflammation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到排尿困难和尿频是尿路炎症的局部体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":863,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_renal_gi_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.672","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.672.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.672.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Which dietary modification should a nurse recommend to a client suffering from frequent constipation?","fullStemZh":"对于经常便秘的患者，护士应建议进行哪种饮食调整？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which dietary modification should a nurse recommend to a client suffering from frequent constipation?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于经常便秘的患者，护士应建议进行哪种饮食调整？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Increase fiber intake.","zh":"增加纤维摄入量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Decrease fluid intake.","zh":"减少液体摄入。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid fruits and vegetables.","zh":"避免吃水果和蔬菜。"},{"id":"C","en":"Eat more dairy products.","zh":"多吃乳制品。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Increasing dietary fiber adds bulk to the stool, which stimulates peristalsis and makes the stool easier to pass. Increasing fluid intake is also essential alongside fiber.","rationaleCorrectZh":"增加膳食纤维会增加粪便的体积，这会刺激肠蠕动并使粪便更容易排出。在增加纤维的同时，增加液体摄入量也是必不可少的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Constipation management relies on fluids, fiber, and physical activity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"便秘的治疗依赖于液体、纤维和身体活动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":864,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_renal_gi_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.673","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.673.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.673.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,41],"fullStemEn":"A client with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) has a fistula in their left arm. Which action is contraindicated for this arm?","fullStemZh":"一位患有终末期肾病（ESRD）的患者左臂有动静脉瘘。哪项操作禁止在这条手臂上进行？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is contraindicated for this arm?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项操作禁止在这条手臂上进行？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) has a fistula in their left arm.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患有终末期肾病（ESRD）的患者左臂有动静脉瘘。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Performing range of motion exercises.","zh":"进行关节活动度练习。"},{"id":"A","en":"Palpating for a thrill.","zh":"触诊震颤（thrill）。"},{"id":"D","en":"Washing the arm with soap and water.","zh":"用肥皂和水清洗手臂。"},{"id":"C","en":"Taking blood pressure measurements.","zh":"测量血压。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To protect a hemodialysis fistula, the nurse must avoid taking blood pressures, starting IVs, or drawing blood on the affected arm. Compression can damage the vascular access.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为了保护血液透析瘘，护士必须避免在受影响的手臂上测量血压、进行静脉输液或抽血。压迫会损坏血管通路。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the rule for fistulas: 'No BP, No IV, No blood draws' in the affected arm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住瘘管的规则：受影响的手臂“不测血压，不打点滴，不抽血”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":865,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.674","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.674.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.674.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[40,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,44],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving warfarin therapy. What is the most important instruction for the nurse to provide to prevent complications?","fullStemZh":"患者正在接受华法林（warfarin）治疗。为了防止并发症，护士提供的最重要指示是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most important instruction for the nurse to provide to prevent complications?","terminalSentenceZh":"为了防止并发症，护士提供的最重要指示是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving warfarin therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者正在接受华法林（warfarin）治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Eat a diet very high in vitamin K.","zh":"食用富含维生素K的饮食。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop taking the medication if you feel dizzy.","zh":"如果感到头晕，停止服药。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use a soft-bristled toothbrush and an electric razor.","zh":"使用软毛牙刷和电动剃须刀。"},{"id":"A","en":"Take an aspirin daily for headaches.","zh":"每天服用阿司匹林缓解头痛。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warfarin is an anticoagulant that increases the risk of bleeding. Using a soft-bristled toothbrush and an electric razor minimizes the risk of cuts and mucosal bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林是一种抗凝剂，会增加出血的风险。使用软毛牙刷和电动剃须刀可最大限度地减少割伤和黏膜出血的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate all anticoagulants with 'bleeding precautions'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将所有抗凝剂与“出血预防措施”联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":866,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_anticoag_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.675","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.675.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.675.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"Which laboratory test is used to monitor the effectiveness of continuous intravenous heparin therapy?","fullStemZh":"哪种实验室检查用于监测持续静脉输注肝素（heparin）治疗的有效性？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory test is used to monitor the effectiveness of continuous intravenous heparin therapy?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种实验室检查用于监测持续静脉输注肝素（heparin）治疗的有效性？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"International Normalized Ratio (INR)","zh":"国际标准化比值（INR）"},{"id":"C","en":"Activated Partial Thromboplastin Time (aPTT)","zh":"活化部分凝血活酶时间（aPTT）"},{"id":"D","en":"White Blood Cell count (WBC)","zh":"白细胞计数（WBC）"},{"id":"B","en":"Prothrombin Time (PT)","zh":"凝血酶原时间（PT）"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT) is the specific lab test used to monitor and adjust IV heparin doses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"活化部分凝血活酶时间（aPTT）是用于监测和调整静脉输注肝素剂量的特定实验室检查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the mnemonic: Heparin = PTT (10 letters each, H-E-P-A-R-I-N + P-T-T); Coumadin (Warfarin) = PT (8 letters each, C-O-U-M-A-D-I-N + P-T).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：Heparin（肝素）使用PTT监测；Warfarin/Coumadin（华法林）使用PT/INR监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":867,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_anticoag_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.676","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.676.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.676.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,73],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,15],"fullStemEn":"What is the primary purpose of administering an anticoagulant medication?","fullStemZh":"使用抗凝药物的主要目的是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the primary purpose of administering an anticoagulant medication?","terminalSentenceZh":"使用抗凝药物的主要目的是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"To prevent new blood clots from forming.","zh":"防止形成新的血栓。"},{"id":"D","en":"To dissolve an existing blood clot.","zh":"溶解现有的血栓。"},{"id":"B","en":"To lower high blood pressure.","zh":"降低高血压。"},{"id":"C","en":"To increase the production of red blood cells.","zh":"增加红细胞的产生。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Anticoagulants prevent the formation of new clots and stop existing clots from growing larger. They do not dissolve clots that are already present (thrombolytics do that).","rationaleCorrectZh":"抗凝剂可防止新血栓的形成，并阻止现有血栓扩大。它们不能溶解已经存在的血栓（溶栓剂起这个作用）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between 'anti-coagulants' (prevent clots) and 'thrombo-lytics' (break down clots).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“抗凝剂”（防止血栓）和“溶栓剂”（分解血栓）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":868,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_burns_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.677","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.677.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.677.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,29],"fullStemEn":"A client arrives at the emergency department with severe burn injuries. What is the nurse's immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"一位严重烧伤的患者到达急诊室。护士最紧迫的优先事项是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最紧迫的优先事项是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client arrives at the emergency department with severe burn injuries.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位严重烧伤的患者到达急诊室。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Estimating the total body surface area burned.","zh":"估计全身烧伤面积。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administering intravenous pain medication.","zh":"静脉注射止痛药。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assessing airway patency.","zh":"评估气道通畅情况。"},{"id":"C","en":"Applying sterile dressings to the burns.","zh":"对烧伤处敷贴无菌敷料。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In any trauma or emergency situation, including severe burns, the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) are the priority. Inhalation injury is a major cause of death in burn victims, making airway assessment the absolute first step.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在任何创伤或紧急情况下，包括严重烧伤，ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）都是优先事项。吸入性损伤是烧伤患者死亡的主要原因，因此气道评估绝对是第一步。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always apply the ABCs first for emergency questions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理急救问题时，始终首先应用ABC原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client arrives at the emergency department with severe burn injuries.","controlSentenceZh":"一位严重烧伤的患者到达急诊室。"}
{"queueIndex":869,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_burns_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.678","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.678.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.678.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"During the first 24 hours after a major burn, what is the most critical nursing intervention to prevent hypovolemic shock?","fullStemZh":"在大面积烧伤后的最初24小时内，预防低血容量性休克最关键的护理干预措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"During the first 24 hours after a major burn, what is the most critical nursing intervention to prevent hypovolemic shock?","terminalSentenceZh":"在大面积烧伤后的最初24小时内，预防低血容量性休克最关键的护理干预措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Providing a high-protein diet.","zh":"提供高蛋白饮食。"},{"id":"C","en":"Applying topical antibiotics.","zh":"涂抹局部抗生素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administering oral fluids.","zh":"经口给予液体。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administering massive intravenous fluid resuscitation.","zh":"进行大量静脉液体复苏。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Major burns cause massive fluid shifts from the intravascular space to the interstitial space. Aggressive IV fluid resuscitation is essential to maintain blood volume and prevent fatal hypovolemic shock.","rationaleCorrectZh":"大面积烧伤会导致大量液体从血管内间隙转移到组织间隙。积极的静脉液体复苏对于维持血容量和预防致命的低血容量性休克至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect 'major burn' with 'fluid loss' and the need for 'IV resuscitation'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“大面积烧伤”与“液体流失”以及“静脉复苏”的需求联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":870,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_burns_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.679","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.679.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.679.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,38],"fullStemEn":"A client with severe burns has lost their primary defense against infection. Which action by the nurse is essential to prevent infection?","fullStemZh":"严重烧伤的患者失去了预防感染的主要防线。护士的哪项行动对于预防感染至关重要？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action by the nurse is essential to prevent infection?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的哪项行动对于预防感染至关重要？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with severe burns has lost their primary defense against infection.","penultimateSentenceZh":"严重烧伤的患者失去了预防感染的主要防线。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Keeping the client's room temperature cold.","zh":"保持患者房间温度较低。"},{"id":"C","en":"Performing meticulous hand hygiene.","zh":"执行严格的手卫生。"},{"id":"B","en":"Allowing visitors to bring fresh flowers.","zh":"允许访客带来鲜花。"},{"id":"A","en":"Using clean, rather than sterile, technique for dressing changes.","zh":"在换药时使用清洁（而非无菌）技术。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The skin is the body's first line of defense. Burn victims are at extreme risk for infection. Strict hand hygiene is the most effective way to prevent cross-contamination.","rationaleCorrectZh":"皮肤是人体的第一道防线。烧伤患者面临极高的感染风险。严格的手卫生是防止交叉污染的最有效方法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For any infection control question, hand hygiene is almost always the correct answer or the highest priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于任何感染控制问题，手卫生几乎总是正确答案或最高优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":871,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_resp_infect_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.680","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.680.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.680.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,42],"fullStemEn":"A client with pneumonia is experiencing thick, tenacious respiratory secretions. Which intervention should the nurse encourage to help clear the airway?","fullStemZh":"一位肺炎患者出现粘稠、难以咳出的呼吸道分泌物。护士应鼓励哪种干预措施以帮助清理气道？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention should the nurse encourage to help clear the airway?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应鼓励哪种干预措施以帮助清理气道？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with pneumonia is experiencing thick, tenacious respiratory secretions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位肺炎患者出现粘稠、难以咳出的呼吸道分泌物。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Increasing oral fluid intake.","zh":"增加口服液体摄入。"},{"id":"C","en":"Restricting fluid intake.","zh":"限制液体摄入。"},{"id":"A","en":"Lying flat in bed.","zh":"平躺在床上。"},{"id":"B","en":"Suppressing the urge to cough.","zh":"抑制咳嗽的冲动。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adequate hydration thins respiratory secretions, making them easier to expectorate (cough up). Unless contraindicated, clients with pneumonia should increase their fluid intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"充足的水分可以稀释呼吸道分泌物，使其更容易咳出。除非有禁忌，肺炎患者应增加液体摄入量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Fluids thin secretions. Connect hydration with respiratory clearance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"液体稀释分泌物。将水合作用与呼吸道清除联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":872,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_resp_infect_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.681","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.681.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.681.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,37],"fullStemEn":"A client with active pulmonary tuberculosis (TB) is admitted to the hospital. Which type of isolation precautions should the nurse initiate?","fullStemZh":"一位患有活动性肺结核（TB）的患者入院。护士应启动哪种类型的隔离预防措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which type of isolation precautions should the nurse initiate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应启动哪种类型的隔离预防措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with active pulmonary tuberculosis (TB) is admitted to the hospital.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患有活动性肺结核（TB）的患者入院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Droplet precautions","zh":"飞沫预防"},{"id":"D","en":"Airborne precautions","zh":"空气预防/空气隔离"},{"id":"B","en":"Standard precautions","zh":"标准预防"},{"id":"C","en":"Contact precautions","zh":"接触预防"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tuberculosis is transmitted through small infectious particles suspended in the air. Airborne precautions (negative pressure room, N95 respirator) are required to prevent transmission.","rationaleCorrectZh":"结核病通过悬浮在空气中的感染性小颗粒传播。需要采取空气预防措施（负压病房、N95口罩）以防止传播。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the airborne diseases: Measles, Tuberculosis, Varicella (chickenpox). Remember MTV.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住空气传播疾病：麻疹（Measles）、结核病（Tuberculosis）、水痘（Varicella）。记住缩写 MTV。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with active pulmonary tuberculosis (TB) is admitted to the hospital.","controlSentenceZh":"一位患有活动性肺结核（TB）的患者入院。"}
{"queueIndex":873,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_resp_infect_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.682","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.682.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.682.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,74],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,16],"fullStemEn":"Which statement by a client indicates an understanding of the flu vaccine?","fullStemZh":"患者的哪句话表明其了解流感疫苗？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by a client indicates an understanding of the flu vaccine?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者的哪句话表明其了解流感疫苗？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"'I don't need the vaccine because antibiotics can cure the flu.'","zh":"“我不需要疫苗，因为抗生素可以治愈流感。”"},{"id":"B","en":"'The vaccine will give me a mild case of the flu.'","zh":"“疫苗会让我得轻微的流感。”"},{"id":"D","en":"'I should get the vaccine every year because the flu strains change.'","zh":"“我应该每年接种疫苗，因为流感毒株会发生变化。”"},{"id":"A","en":"'I only need to get the vaccine once in my lifetime.'","zh":"“我一生只需要接种一次疫苗。”"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The influenza virus mutates rapidly. An annual vaccination is required because the vaccine is formulated each year to protect against the strains predicted to be most common.","rationaleCorrectZh":"流感病毒突变迅速。需要每年接种疫苗，因为每年配制的疫苗是为了预防预计最常见的毒株。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that flu viruses mutate, requiring an annual update.","testTakingStrategyZh":"请记住流感病毒会突变，因此需要每年更新。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":874,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_substance_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.683","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.683.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.683.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,35],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the hospital and begins to experience alcohol withdrawal. Which symptom is the nurse most likely to observe early in withdrawal?","fullStemZh":"一位患者入院并开始经历酒精戒断。护士在戒断早期最有可能观察到哪种症状？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which symptom is the nurse most likely to observe early in withdrawal?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在戒断早期最有可能观察到哪种症状？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted to the hospital and begins to experience alcohol withdrawal.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者入院并开始经历酒精戒断。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Bradycardia","zh":"心动过缓"},{"id":"A","en":"Hypotension","zh":"低血压"},{"id":"B","en":"Profound lethargy","zh":"极度嗜睡"},{"id":"D","en":"Tremors","zh":"震颤（手抖）"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Alcohol is a central nervous system depressant. When it is removed, the nervous system becomes hyperactive. Early signs of withdrawal include tremors, anxiety, tachycardia (fast heart rate), and hypertension (high blood pressure).","rationaleCorrectZh":"酒精是中枢神经系统抑制剂。当酒精被移除时，神经系统会变得过度活跃。戒断的早期迹象包括震颤、焦虑、心动过速（心率快）和高血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Withdrawal from a depressant (alcohol) causes stimulant-like effects (hyperactivity, tremors).","testTakingStrategyZh":"停止使用抑制剂（酒精）会导致类似兴奋剂的作用（过度活跃、震颤）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":875,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_substance_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.684","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.684.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.684.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,117],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"Which medication is most commonly administered to a client experiencing acute alcohol withdrawal to prevent seizures?","fullStemZh":"对于经历急性酒精戒断的患者，最常给予哪种药物以预防癫痫发作？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication is most commonly administered to a client experiencing acute alcohol withdrawal to prevent seizures?","terminalSentenceZh":"对于经历急性酒精戒断的患者，最常给予哪种药物以预防癫痫发作？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Lorazepam","zh":"劳拉西泮"},{"id":"D","en":"Haloperidol","zh":"氟哌啶醇"},{"id":"C","en":"Naloxone","zh":"纳洛酮"},{"id":"A","en":"Fluoxetine","zh":"氟西汀"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Benzodiazepines, such as lorazepam, diazepam, or chlordiazepoxide, are the first-line treatment for alcohol withdrawal to prevent severe complications like seizures and delirium tremens.","rationaleCorrectZh":"苯二氮卓类药物（如劳拉西泮、地西泮或氯氮卓）是治疗酒精戒断的一线药物，用于预防癫痫发作和震颤谵妄等严重并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate 'alcohol withdrawal' with 'benzodiazepines' (drugs ending in -pam or -lam).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将“酒精戒断”与“苯二氮卓类药物”（以 -pam 或 -lam 结尾的药物）联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":876,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_substance_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.685","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.685.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.685.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,35],"fullStemEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department with suspected opioid overdose. Which finding is the nurse most likely to assess?","fullStemZh":"一位疑似阿片类药物过量的患者被送到急诊室。护士最有可能评估到哪种体征？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding is the nurse most likely to assess?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最有可能评估到哪种体征？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department with suspected opioid overdose.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位疑似阿片类药物过量的患者被送到急诊室。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Dilated pupils","zh":"瞳孔散大"},{"id":"C","en":"Respiratory depression","zh":"呼吸抑制"},{"id":"B","en":"Diarrhea","zh":"腹泻"},{"id":"A","en":"Hyperactivity","zh":"过度活跃"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Opioids are central nervous system depressants. An overdose leads to the classic triad of pinpoint pupils, respiratory depression, and decreased level of consciousness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阿片类药物是中枢神经系统抑制剂。过量会导致典型的三联征：针尖样瞳孔、呼吸抑制和意识水平下降。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Opioids make everything go 'down' or slow: slow breathing, slow heart rate, small pupils, low consciousness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"阿片类药物使一切变“低”或变慢：呼吸缓慢、心率缓慢、瞳孔缩小、意识低下。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":877,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_substance_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.686","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.686.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.686.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,40],"fullStemEn":"A client is found unresponsive with a respiratory rate of 6 breaths/minute after injecting heroin. Which medication should the nurse prepare to administer?","fullStemZh":"患者在注射海洛因后被发现失去知觉，呼吸频率为6次/分钟。护士应准备给予哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse prepare to administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应准备给予哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is found unresponsive with a respiratory rate of 6 breaths/minute after injecting heroin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者在注射海洛因后被发现失去知觉，呼吸频率为6次/分钟。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Atropine","zh":"阿托品"},{"id":"C","en":"Epinephrine","zh":"肾上腺素"},{"id":"A","en":"Flumazenil","zh":"氟马西尼"},{"id":"B","en":"Naloxone","zh":"纳洛酮"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Naloxone is the specific opioid antagonist used to rapidly reverse respiratory depression caused by opioid (heroin) overdose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"纳洛酮是特异性阿片受体拮抗剂，用于迅速逆转由阿片类药物（海洛因）过量引起的呼吸抑制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know the antidotes: Opioids = Naloxone; Benzodiazepines = Flumazenil.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解解毒剂：阿片类药物 = 纳洛酮；苯二氮卓类 = 氟马西尼。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":878,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_dka_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.687","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.687.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.687.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,41],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes is admitted with diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA). Which type of insulin will the nurse expect to administer intravenously?","fullStemZh":"一位1型糖尿病患者因糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）入院。护士预计会静脉注射哪种胰岛素？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which type of insulin will the nurse expect to administer intravenously?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预计会静脉注射哪种胰岛素？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes is admitted with diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位1型糖尿病患者因糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）入院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"NPH insulin","zh":"中效胰岛素（NPH）"},{"id":"C","en":"Insulin glargine","zh":"甘精胰岛素"},{"id":"A","en":"Insulin detemir","zh":"地特胰岛素"},{"id":"B","en":"Regular insulin","zh":"常规胰岛素（Regular insulin）"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Regular insulin is the standard intravenous insulin used in DKA protocols and is the correct choice among these options. It is not the only insulin formulation with an approved supervised IV route; insulin aspart can also be given intravenously under appropriate monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"常规胰岛素是 DKA 方案中标准的静脉用胰岛素，也是这些选项中的正确答案。但它并非唯一获准在医疗监督下静脉给药的胰岛素制剂；门冬胰岛素也可在适当监测下静脉使用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the phrase: 'Regular insulin goes Right into the Vein'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住这句话：“Regular胰岛素（常规胰岛素）直接进入静脉（Right into the Vein）”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":879,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_dka_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.688","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.688.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.688.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Which breathing pattern is classically associated with diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)?","fullStemZh":"哪种呼吸模式通常与糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）相关？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which breathing pattern is classically associated with diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种呼吸模式通常与糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）相关？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Kussmaul respirations","zh":"库斯莫尔呼吸（Kussmaul）"},{"id":"C","en":"Cheyne-Stokes respirations","zh":"潮式呼吸（Cheyne-Stokes）"},{"id":"B","en":"Shallow breathing","zh":"浅呼吸"},{"id":"A","en":"Apnea","zh":"呼吸暂停"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Kussmaul respirations are deep, rapid breathing patterns that occur as the body attempts to compensate for metabolic acidosis by blowing off excess carbon dioxide (an acid).","rationaleCorrectZh":"库斯莫尔呼吸（Kussmaul respirations）是深而快的呼吸模式，这是身体试图通过排出多余的二氧化碳（一种酸）来代偿代谢性酸中毒的反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate DKA with Ketoacidosis. To fix acidosis, the lungs hyperventilate (Kussmaul).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将DKA与酮症酸中毒联系起来。为了纠正酸中毒，肺部会过度换气（Kussmaul）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":880,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_dka_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.689","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.689.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.689.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"In addition to high blood glucose, what other assessment finding is a hallmark of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)?","fullStemZh":"除了高血糖外，糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）的另一个标志性评估发现是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"In addition to high blood glucose, what other assessment finding is a hallmark of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)?","terminalSentenceZh":"除了高血糖外，糖尿病酮症酸中毒（DKA）的另一个标志性评估发现是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Severe edema in the legs","zh":"腿部严重水肿"},{"id":"A","en":"Cold, clammy skin","zh":"皮肤湿冷"},{"id":"D","en":"Fruity or acetone breath odor","zh":"呼吸有水果味或丙酮味"},{"id":"B","en":"A very slow heart rate","zh":"心率非常慢"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In DKA, the body breaks down fat for energy, producing ketones. Excess ketones are excreted through the lungs, giving the breath a distinct fruity, sweet, or acetone-like odor.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在DKA中，身体分解脂肪获取能量，产生酮体。多余的酮体通过肺部排出，使呼吸带有独特的水果味、甜味或类似丙酮的气味。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Ketones = fruity breath. This is a classic hallmark sign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"酮体=水果味呼吸。这是一个典型的标志性体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":881,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_mental_health_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.690","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.690.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.690.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,46],"fullStemEn":"A client with depression states, 'There's no point in trying anymore. Nothing will ever get better.' What is the nurse's best therapeutic response?","fullStemZh":"一位患有抑郁症的患者说：“再努力也没有用了。情况永远不会好转。”护士最佳的治疗性回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's best therapeutic response?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳的治疗性回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Nothing will ever get better.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"情况永远不会好转。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"'Things will look better tomorrow.'","zh":"“明天事情就会看起来好些的。”"},{"id":"D","en":"'Don't say that, you have a lot to live for.'","zh":"“别那么说，你还有很多值得活下去的理由。”"},{"id":"B","en":"'Why do you feel this way?'","zh":"“你为什么会这样觉得？”"},{"id":"A","en":"'It sounds like you are feeling very hopeless right now.'","zh":"“听起来你现在感到非常绝望。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reflecting the client's feelings ('feeling very hopeless') is a therapeutic communication technique that validates the client's emotions, builds trust, and encourages further dialogue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反映患者的感受（“感到非常绝望”）是一种治疗性沟通技巧，它可以确认患者的情绪，建立信任，并鼓励进一步的对话。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In psychiatric nursing, always choose responses that acknowledge and validate the client's feelings without judgment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在精神科护理中，始终选择承认并验证患者感受且不加评判的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":882,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_mental_health_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.691","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.691.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.691.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,51],"fullStemEn":"A client with schizophrenia is pacing the hall and tells the nurse, 'The voices are telling me I am a bad person.' How should the nurse respond?","fullStemZh":"一位患有精神分裂症的患者在走廊里踱步，并告诉护士：“脑子里的声音告诉我我是个坏人。”护士应该如何回应？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse respond?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应该如何回应？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with schizophrenia is pacing the hall and tells the nurse, 'The voices are telling me I am a bad person.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患有精神分裂症的患者在走廊里踱步，并告诉护士：“脑子里的声音告诉我我是个坏人。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"'Tell the voices to go away.'","zh":"“叫那些声音走开。”"},{"id":"A","en":"'What else are the voices saying?'","zh":"“那些声音还在说什么？”"},{"id":"D","en":"'There are no voices, it is just your imagination.'","zh":"“没有什么声音，那只是你的想象。”"},{"id":"B","en":"'I don't hear the voices, but I understand that they are real to you and are upsetting you.'","zh":"“我没有听到那些声音，但我明白它们对你来说是真实的，并且让你感到心烦。”"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Presenting reality while acknowledging the client's feelings is the best approach for hallucinations. The nurse clarifies that they do not share the perception, but validates that the experience is frightening for the client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在承认患者感受的同时呈现现实是处理幻觉的最佳方法。护士澄清自己没有相同的感知，但承认这种经历对患者来说是可怕的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not argue with hallucinations or delusions, but do not pretend they are real either. Present your reality clearly.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要与幻觉或妄想争辩，但也不要假装它们是真实的。清楚地呈现你的现实。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":883,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_mental_health_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.692","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.692.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.692.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,34],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing severe anxiety and is hyperventilating. What is the nurse's immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"一位患者正经历严重的焦虑并伴有过度换气。护士最紧迫的优先事项是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最紧迫的优先事项是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is experiencing severe anxiety and is hyperventilating.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者正经历严重的焦虑并伴有过度换气。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Teach the client a complex relaxation technique.","zh":"教导患者一项复杂的放松技巧。"},{"id":"D","en":"Stay with the client and encourage slow, deep breaths.","zh":"留在患者身边并鼓励他们进行缓慢的深呼吸。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client to explain exactly what triggered the anxiety.","zh":"要求患者准确解释是什么引发了焦虑。"},{"id":"C","en":"Leave the client alone to calm down.","zh":"让患者独自一人冷静下来。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During a severe panic or anxiety attack, the client cannot learn new information or process complex questions. The nurse's priority is to remain with the client to ensure safety and provide simple, direct instructions to control breathing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在严重的恐慌或焦虑发作期间，患者无法学习新信息或处理复杂问题。护士的首要任务是留在患者身边以确保安全，并提供简单、直接的指示来控制呼吸。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For severe anxiety, safety and physical needs come first. Do not teach or explore feelings until anxiety decreases.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于严重的焦虑，安全和生理需求排在第一位。在焦虑减轻之前，不要进行教育或探索感受。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":884,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_mental_health_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.693","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.693.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.693.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[68,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,33],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a newly admitted client on a psychiatric unit. Which statement by the client requires the most immediate intervention?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估精神科病房新入院的患者。患者的哪句话需要最紧急的干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement by the client requires the most immediate intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者的哪句话需要最紧急的干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a newly admitted client on a psychiatric unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估精神科病房新入院的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"'I haven't slept well in a week.'","zh":"“我已经一周没睡好了。”"},{"id":"A","en":"'I've been thinking about taking all my pills tonight.'","zh":"“我一直在想今晚把所有的药都吃掉。”"},{"id":"C","en":"'I feel so sad all the time.'","zh":"“我一直感到很伤心。”"},{"id":"D","en":"'I am very angry that my family brought me here.'","zh":"“我对家人把我带到这里感到非常生气。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A direct statement indicating suicidal ideation with a plan ('taking all my pills tonight') is a life-threatening emergency and requires immediate intervention, such as placing the client on one-to-one observation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"表明有自杀意念并有计划的直接陈述（“今晚把所有的药都吃掉”）属于危及生命的紧急情况，需要立即干预，例如对患者进行一对一观察。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safety first. Any hint of self-harm or suicide is the top priority in psychiatric nursing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全第一。在精神科护理中，任何自残或自杀的迹象都是首要任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":885,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_cardio_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.694","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.694.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.694.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,29],"fullStemEn":"A client is diagnosed with right-sided heart failure. Which assessment finding should the nurse expect to observe?","fullStemZh":"一位患者被诊断患有右心衰竭。护士预计会观察到哪种评估发现？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assessment finding should the nurse expect to observe?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预计会观察到哪种评估发现？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is diagnosed with right-sided heart failure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者被诊断患有右心衰竭。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Shortness of breath at rest","zh":"静息时呼吸急促"},{"id":"C","en":"A dry, hacking cough","zh":"干咳"},{"id":"B","en":"Crackles in the lungs","zh":"肺部湿啰音"},{"id":"D","en":"Peripheral edema in the legs and feet","zh":"腿部和脚部外周水肿"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Right-sided heart failure causes blood to back up into the systemic circulation, leading to systemic venous congestion. This presents as peripheral edema, jugular vein distention (JVD), and hepatomegaly.","rationaleCorrectZh":"右心衰竭导致血液倒流回体循环，导致全身静脉淤血。这表现为外周水肿、颈静脉怒张（JVD）和肝大。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Right-sided failure = Rest of body (systemic edema). Left-sided failure = Lungs (pulmonary edema).","testTakingStrategyZh":"右心衰竭 = 身体的其余部分（全身水肿）。左心衰竭 = 肺部（肺水肿）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":886,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_cardio_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.695","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.695.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.695.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,37],"fullStemEn":"A client with angina is prescribed sublingual nitroglycerin. What should the nurse teach the client about storing this medication?","fullStemZh":"给患有心绞痛的患者开具了舌下含服硝酸甘油。护士应如何指导患者储存这种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse teach the client about storing this medication?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何指导患者储存这种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with angina is prescribed sublingual nitroglycerin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"给患有心绞痛的患者开具了舌下含服硝酸甘油。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Keep the pills in the refrigerator.","zh":"将药丸放在冰箱中。"},{"id":"A","en":"Carry the pills loose in a pocket for quick access.","zh":"为了方便取用，将药丸散装在口袋里随身携带。"},{"id":"C","en":"Store the pills in a clear, plastic container.","zh":"将药丸存放在透明塑料容器中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the medication in its original dark glass bottle.","zh":"将药物保存在其原装的深色玻璃瓶中。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nitroglycerin is sensitive to light, heat, and moisture, which cause it to lose potency. It must be kept in its original dark glass container.","rationaleCorrectZh":"硝酸甘油对光、热和湿气敏感，这会导致其失去效力。必须将其保存在原装的深色玻璃容器中。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Nitroglycerin degrades easily. Protect it from light and heat.","testTakingStrategyZh":"硝酸甘油容易降解。避光和避热保存。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with angina is prescribed sublingual nitroglycerin.","controlSentenceZh":"给患有心绞痛的患者开具了舌下含服硝酸甘油。"}
{"queueIndex":887,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"easy_cardio_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.696","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.696.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.696.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,74],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"What is the most common symptom of a myocardial infarction (heart attack)?","fullStemZh":"心肌梗死（心脏病发作）最常见的症状是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most common symptom of a myocardial infarction (heart attack)?","terminalSentenceZh":"心肌梗死（心脏病发作）最常见的症状是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A sudden, severe headache","zh":"突发、严重的头痛"},{"id":"C","en":"Pain in the lower right abdomen","zh":"右下腹疼痛"},{"id":"A","en":"Severe, crushing chest pain that radiates to the jaw or arm","zh":"放射至下颌或手臂的剧烈压榨性胸痛"},{"id":"B","en":"Sharp chest pain that worsens with deep breathing","zh":"深呼吸时加剧的剧烈胸痛"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The classic presentation of a myocardial infarction is severe, heavy, or crushing chest pain that does not resolve with rest or nitroglycerin, and often radiates to the left arm, neck, or jaw.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心肌梗死的典型表现是严重的、沉重的或压榨性的胸痛，这种疼痛在休息或含服硝酸甘油后不能缓解，并且经常放射到左臂、颈部或下颌。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the 'crushing' pain radiating to the arm or jaw as the hallmark of a heart attack.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到放射到手臂或下颌的“压榨性”疼痛是心脏病发作的标志。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":888,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.697","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.697.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.697.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,81],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing a client for a scheduled elective cardiac catheterization. The client states, 'I am still not sure what they are going to do during this procedure, and I am nervous about it.' The nurse should recognize that {{1}} because {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名安排进行择期心脏导管插入术的患者做准备。患者陈述道：“我仍然不确定他们在手术过程中要做什么，我很紧张。”护士应认识到 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should recognize that {{1}} because {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应认识到 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client states, 'I am still not sure what they are going to do during this procedure, and I am nervous about it.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者陈述道：“我仍然不确定他们在手术过程中要做什么，我很紧张。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"the nurse must contact the provider to explain the procedure {{1}} because obtaining informed consent is the provider's responsibility {{2}}.","zh":"护士必须联系医疗服务提供者来解释手术过程 {{1}}，因为获取知情同意是提供者的职责 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"to explain the procedure to the client","zh":"向患者解释手术过程"},{"id":"o2","en":"to sign the consent form as the client's proxy","zh":"作为患者代理人签署同意书"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"who is responsible for explaining the nursing care plan","zh":"护士负责解释护理计划"},{"id":"o1","en":"which cannot be delegated to the nurse","zh":"该职责不能委托给护士"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Obtaining informed consent is the sole responsibility of the healthcare provider performing the procedure. The nurse's role is to witness the signature and verify that the client understands, but if the client has questions about the procedure itself, the nurse must notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"获取知情同意是执行手术的医疗服务提供者的唯一职责。护士的角色是见证签字并核实患者是否理解，但如果患者对手术本身有疑问，护士必须通知提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for choices that respect the provider's legal responsibility to explain procedures, rather than the nurse attempting to provide primary clinical explanations of risks and benefits.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找尊重提供者解释手术的法定职责的选项，而不是由护士试图对风险和益处提供首要临床解释。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":889,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.698","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.698.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.698.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is educating a client regarding advance directives. Classify each of the following statements under the appropriate document.","fullStemZh":"护士正在就预设医疗指示对患者进行宣教。将以下每项陈述归类到相应的档下。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following statements under the appropriate document.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每项陈述归类到相应的档下。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is educating a client regarding advance directives.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在就预设医疗指示对患者进行宣教。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Specifies wishes regarding mechanical ventilation and tube feeding if terminal.","zh":"明确指出在终末期时对于机械通气和管饲的意愿。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Designates a surrogate decision-maker when the client loses decision-making capacity.","zh":"在患者失去决策能力时指定一位代理决策者。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Takes effect only when the client is terminally ill or permanently unconscious.","zh":"仅在患者处于终末期或永久无意识时生效。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Allows the surrogate to make healthcare choices not explicitly detailed in writing.","zh":"允许代理人做出书面未明确详述的医疗选择。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Durable Power of Attorney for Healthcare (DPOAH)","zh":"医疗代理人委托书 (DPOAH)"},{"id":"c1","en":"Living Will","zh":"生前遗嘱"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A Living Will specifies specific medical treatments the client wishes to receive or refuse in terminal conditions. A DPOAH designates a health care proxy who can make any healthcare decisions when the client is incapacitated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"“生前遗嘱”明确了患者在终末期状态下希望接受或拒绝的特定医疗措施。“医疗代理人委托书 (DPOAH)”指定了一位医疗代理人，可在患者丧失行为能力时做出任何医疗决策。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between a document outlining static wishes (Living Will) versus one delegating active authority to a person (DPOAH).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分概述静态意愿的档（生前遗嘱）与向人授予主动决策权的档（DPOAH）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":890,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.699","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.699.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.699.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,230],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,69],"fullStemEn":"An elderly client admitted with a severe urinary tract infection refuses to take prescribed oral antibiotics. The client states, 'I just want to go home and let nature take its course.' The nurse should first {{1}} and then {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"一名因严重尿路感染入院的老年患者拒绝服用开具的口服抗生素。患者陈述道：“我只想回家，顺其自然。”护士应首先 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should first {{1}} and then {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client states, 'I just want to go home and let nature take its course.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者陈述道：“我只想回家，顺其自然。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first {{1}} and then {{2}}.","zh":"护士应首先 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"force the client to swallow the tablets","zh":"强迫患者吞下药片"},{"id":"o1","en":"assess the client's understanding of the consequences","zh":"评估患者对拒绝后果的理解"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"document the refusal and notify the healthcare provider","zh":"记录拒绝并通知医疗服务提供者"},{"id":"o2","en":"administer the medication crushed in applesauce","zh":"将药物碾碎在苹果酱中给予"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Every competent client has the right to refuse treatment. The nurse must first act as an advocate by assessing the client's reasoning and understanding of the consequences of refusal. If they still refuse, the nurse must document and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每个有行为能力的患者都有拒绝治疗的权利。护士必须首先履行倡导者职责，评估患者拒绝的原因和对后果的理解。如果患者坚持拒绝，护士必须记录并通知提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the nursing process: assessment always precedes documentation/intervention. Do not select options that force medication administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用护理程序：评估总是先于记录/干预。不要选择强迫给药的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":true,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":true,"clozeStemContainedInStem":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":true},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":891,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.700","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.700.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.700.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[52,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is working on a busy medical-surgical unit. Under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA), classify each of the following actions as Permissible or Non-permissible.","fullStemZh":"护士正在一个繁忙的内外科病房工作。根据《健康保险流通与责任法案》(HIPAA)，将以下每项行为分类为“允许的”或“不允许的”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA), classify each of the following actions as Permissible or Non-permissible.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据《健康保险流通与责任法案》(HIPAA)，将以下每项行为分类为“允许的”或“不允许的”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is working on a busy medical-surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在一个繁忙的内外科病房工作。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Discussing a client's plan of care with the physical therapist assigned to the client.","zh":"与分配给该患者的物理治疗师讨论患者的护理计划。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Sharing a client's lab results with a nurse from another unit who is a close friend of the family.","zh":"与另一病房的、是该家属好朋友的护士分享患者的化验结果。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Providing updates on a client's condition to a family member who is listed in the chart with the correct passcode.","zh":"向病历中列出并提供正确密码的家属提供患者状况的更新。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Accessing the electronic medical record of a former client to see how they are recovering.","zh":"访问前患者的电子病历以查看其恢复情况。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Non-permissible","zh":"不允许的"},{"id":"c1","en":"Permissible","zh":"允许的"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Information sharing is only permissible among members of the healthcare team directly involved in the client's care, or with designated family members authorized by the client (e.g. via passcode). Looking up former clients or sharing with friends/colleagues not involved is a HIPAA violation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"信息共享仅限于直接参与患者护理的医疗团队成员之间，或由患者授权的指定家属（例如通过密码）。查找前患者的信息或与不参与护理的朋友/同事分享属于违反 HIPAA 规定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for 'need-to-know' criteria. A nurse must have active professional involvement in care to access or share medical records.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找“必须知道”的标准。护士必须在护理中具有主动的专业参与，才能访问或共享病历。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":892,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.701","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.701.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.701.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,50],"fullStemEn":"A client who is mentally competent decides to leave the hospital against medical advice (AMA). The nurse should ensure that {{1}} because {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"一名精神上有行为能力的患者决定违背医嘱（AMA）离开医院。护士应确保 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should ensure that {{1}} because {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应确保 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who is mentally competent decides to leave the hospital against medical advice (AMA).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名精神上有行为能力的患者决定违背医嘱（AMA）离开医院。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should ensure that {{1}} because {{2}}.","zh":"护士应确保 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"security is called to restrain the client from leaving","zh":"呼叫保安以约束患者防止其离开"},{"id":"o1","en":"the client is informed of the risks of leaving and signs an AMA form","zh":"告知患者离开的风险并签署 AMA 表单"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"leaving without a signature is a criminal misdemeanor","zh":"不签字离开属于刑事轻罪"},{"id":"o1","en":"competent clients have the legal right to refuse treatment and leave","zh":"有行为能力的患者具有拒绝治疗和离开的法定权利"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Competent adults have the absolute right to refuse treatment, including leaving the hospital AMA. The nurse's duty is to explain the risks of leaving and request the client sign the AMA form to release the hospital from liability. If they refuse to sign, the nurse cannot hold them.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有行为能力的成年人有拒绝治疗的绝对权利，包括违背医嘱 (AMA) 离开医院。护士的职责是解释离开的风险，并请求患者签署 AMA 表单以解除医院的责任。如果他们拒绝签字，护士也不能拘留他们。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Never choose answers that physically restrain, coerce, or threaten a competent client. Acknowledge autonomy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"切勿选择对有行为能力的患者进行身体约束、强迫或威胁的选项。承认自主权。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":true,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":true,"clozeStemContainedInStem":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":true},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":893,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.702","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.702.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.702.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,263],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,80],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is planning to delegate the measurement of post-void residual urine volume using a portable bladder scanner to an experienced unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP). Sequence the nurse's actions to ensure safe delegation, from first to last.","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 计划将使用便携式膀胱扫描仪测量排尿后残余尿量的任务委托给一名有经验的非持牌辅助人员 (UAP)。将护士的行为按先后顺序排列，以确保安全委托。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the nurse's actions to ensure safe delegation, from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"将护士的行为按先后顺序排列，以确保安全委托。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is planning to delegate the measurement of post-void residual urine volume using a portable bladder scanner to an experienced unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP).","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士 (RN) 计划将使用便携式膀胱扫描仪测量排尿后残余尿量的任务委托给一名有经验的非持牌辅助人员 (UAP)。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Monitor the scanner usage and verify the final scanned volume reported by the UAP.","zh":"监督扫描仪的使用并核实 UAP 报告的最终扫描尿量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's clinical stability and suitability for the scan.","zh":"评估患者的临床稳定性和是否适合进行扫描。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the UAP's competency in operating the bladder scanner.","zh":"核实 UAP 操作膀胱扫描仪的能力。"},{"id":"C","en":"Instruct the UAP on when to perform the scan and what parameters to report.","zh":"指示 UAP 何时进行扫描以及要报告哪些参数。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe delegation begins with verifying the competency of the delegatee. Next, the RN must assess the client's condition to ensure it is safe to delegate. Then, clear instructions/parameters must be given. Finally, the RN must supervise, evaluate, and verify the outcomes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全的委托始于核实被委托人的能力。接下来，RN 必须评估患者的状况以确保委托是安全的。然后，必须给予明确的指示/参数。最后，RN 必须监督、评估并核实结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the 5 Rights of Delegation. Verifying delegatee competency and assessing the client are key initial steps before task execution.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想委托的 5 个正确原则。核实被委托人能力和评估患者是任务执行前关键的初始步骤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":894,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.703","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.703.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.703.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,338],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,109],"fullStemEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is delegating care for a stable client who has a newly established tracheostomy. Place the nursing activities in the correct sequence of RN responsibility, from the activity requiring the highest degree of clinical judgment (must be completed by RN) to the one requiring the least (can be delegated to LPN or UAP).","fullStemZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在为一名新建气管切开术且情况稳定的患者委托护理工作。将护理活动按 RN 职责的正确顺序排列，从需要最高临床判断力（必须由 RN 完成）的活动到需要最低判断力（可委托给 LPN 或 UAP）的活动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing activities in the correct sequence of RN responsibility, from the activity requiring the highest degree of clinical judgment (must be completed by RN) to the one requiring the least (can be delegated to LPN or UAP).","terminalSentenceZh":"将护理活动按 RN 职责的正确顺序排列，从需要最高临床判断力（必须由 RN 完成）的活动到需要最低判断力（可委托给 LPN 或 UAP）的活动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A registered nurse (RN) is delegating care for a stable client who has a newly established tracheostomy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士 (RN) 正在为一名新建气管切开术且情况稳定的患者委托护理工作。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Perform routine tracheostomy suctioning and care for the stable client.","zh":"为稳定的患者进行常规气管切开吸痰和护理。"},{"id":"C","en":"Reposition the client in bed to facilitate chest expansion.","zh":"在床上为患者重新调整体位以促进胸部扩张。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform the initial assessment of the tracheostomy site and respiratory status.","zh":"对气管切开部位和呼吸状态进行首次评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Initial assessments and clinical evaluation are non-delegable responsibilities of the RN. Routine care and procedures on stable clients (like suctioning) can be delegated to an LPN. Basic non-invasive tasks like positioning can be delegated to a UAP.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首次评估和临床评价是 RN 不可委托的职责。对稳定患者的常规护理和操作（如吸痰）可以委托给 LPN。基础非侵入性任务如体位摆放可以委托给 UAP。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that RNs cannot delegate assessment, planning, or clinical evaluation (E-A-T: Evaluate, Assess, Teach).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 RN 不能委托评价、评估或临床宣教（E-A-T 原则：评价、评估、宣教）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":895,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.704","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.704.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.704.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,52],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is coordinating the discharge planning for a client recovering from a stroke who will require home health services. Place the steps of the discharge planning process in the correct chronological order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名中风恢复期且需要家庭卫生服务的患者协调出院计划。将出院计划过程的步骤按正确的先后顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps of the discharge planning process in the correct chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"将出院计划过程的步骤按正确的先后顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is coordinating the discharge planning for a client recovering from a stroke who will require home health services.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名中风恢复期且需要家庭卫生服务的患者协调出院计划。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Verify that all home health services and durable medical equipment have been scheduled and confirmed.","zh":"核实所有家庭医疗服务和耐用医疗设备已安排并确认。"},{"id":"C","en":"Review discharge medications and self-care instructions with the client and family.","zh":"与患者及家属一起复习出院药物和自我护理说明。"},{"id":"B","en":"Collaborate with the case manager and interdisciplinary team to identify home care agencies.","zh":"与个案经理和跨学科团队合作，确定家庭护理机构。"},{"id":"A","en":"Conduct a comprehensive assessment of the client's home environment and functional limitations.","zh":"对患者的家庭环境和功能局限性进行全面评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Discharge planning begins immediately upon admission, starting with an assessment of client needs. Next, referrals and collaborative planning are completed. Education of the client/family follows. Finally, setup of all services and equipment must be verified before actual discharge.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出院计划在入院时立即开始，从评估患者需求开始。接下来，完成转诊和协作计划。随后是对患者/家属的教育。最后，在实际出院前必须核实所有服务和设备的配置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the nursing process: assessment (A) always comes first. Verification (D) represents a final quality/safety check and should be last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用护理程序：评估 (A) 总是排在第一位。核实 (D) 代表最后的质量/安全检查，应该排在最后。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is coordinating the discharge planning for a client recovering from a stroke who will require home health services.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名中风恢复期且需要家庭卫生服务的患者协调出院计划。"}
{"queueIndex":896,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.705","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.705.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.705.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,76],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing an SBAR handoff report for a client transferring to the intensive care unit (ICU) due to worsening respiratory failure. Place the components of the handoff report in the correct sequence according to the SBAR (Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation) framework.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名因呼吸衰竭加重转入重症监护病房 (ICU) 的患者准备 SBAR 交接班报告。根据 SBAR 框架，将交接班报告的组成部分按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the components of the handoff report in the correct sequence according to the SBAR (Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation) framework.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据 SBAR 框架，将交接班报告的组成部分按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing an SBAR handoff report for a client transferring to the intensive care unit (ICU) due to worsening respiratory failure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名因呼吸衰竭加重转入重症监护病房 (ICU) 的患者准备 SBAR 交接班报告。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The client is experiencing acute respiratory failure and needs immediate transfer for invasive mechanical ventilation.","zh":"患者出现急性呼吸衰竭，需要立即转科进行有创机械通气。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client's respiratory rate is 32/min, oxygen saturation is 85% on 6L simple mask, and crackles are heard bilaterally.","zh":"患者呼吸频率为 32次/分，使用6升普通面罩吸氧时血氧饱和度为 85%，双侧可闻及湿啰音。"},{"id":"D","en":"I recommend initiating high-flow nasal cannula immediately and preparing the intubation tray at the bedside.","zh":"我建议立即启动高流量鼻导管吸氧，并在床边准备气管插管盘。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client is a 65-year-old with a history of COPD, admitted 2 days ago for community-acquired pneumonia.","zh":"患者 65 岁，有慢性阻塞性肺病 (COPD) 病史，2天前因社区获得性肺炎入院。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to the SBAR communication framework, the correct sequence is: Situation (current acute issue), Background (history and admission details), Assessment (current objective vitals and physical findings), and Recommendation (suggested actions/needs).","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据 SBAR 沟通框架，正确的顺序是：Situation 现状（当前的急性问题）、Background 背景（病史和入院详情）、Assessment 评估（当前的客观生命体征和体格检查结果），以及 Recommendation 建议（建议的行为/需求）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the option details directly to S-B-A-R headings. S = Current crisis, B = History, A = Vitals/Physical findings, R = Suggested actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将选项详情直接匹配到 S-B-A-R 标题下。S = 当前危机，B = 历史病史，A = 生命体征/体检结果，R = 建议的行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":897,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.706","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.706.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.706.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,36],"fullStemEn":"A nurse encounters several ethical situations on a clinical unit. Match each ethical principle with the corresponding clinical action.","fullStemZh":"护士在临床病房中遇到几种伦理情境。将每个伦理原则与相应的临床行为相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each ethical principle with the corresponding clinical action.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每个伦理原则与相应的临床行为相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse encounters several ethical situations on a clinical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在临床病房中遇到几种伦理情境。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Ensuring that pain medication is administered promptly as promised to the client.","zh":"确保按照向患者许诺的那样，及时给予止痛药。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Respecting the client's decision to refuse a blood transfusion due to religious beliefs.","zh":"尊重患者因宗教信仰而拒绝输血的决定。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Refusing to disclose a client's diagnosis to an unauthorized visiting neighbor.","zh":"拒绝向未经授权来访的邻居透露患者的诊断。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Providing the same standard of wound care to all clients regardless of their socioeconomic status.","zh":"无论社会经济地位如何，为所有患者提供相同标准的伤口护理。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Autonomy","zh":"自主原则"},{"id":"c4","en":"Nonmaleficence","zh":"非伤害原则"},{"id":"c2","en":"Justice","zh":"公正原则"},{"id":"c3","en":"Fidelity","zh":"忠实原则"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c4"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fidelity means keeping promises and commitments. Autonomy respects a client's right to self-determination. Nonmaleficence is the duty to do no harm, which includes protecting confidential information from disclosure that might cause social/emotional harm. Justice represents fair treatment for all.","rationaleCorrectZh":"忠实指履行承诺和诺言。自主尊重患者的自我决定权。非伤害是指不伤害的职责，包括保护机密信息不被泄露以防止社交/情感伤害。公正代表对所有人公平对待。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match definitions: Autonomy = self-determination; Justice = fairness; Fidelity = keeping promises; Nonmaleficence = doing no harm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"匹配定义：自主 = 自我决定；公正 = 公平；忠实 = 履行诺言；非伤害 = 不造成伤害。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":898,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.707","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.707.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.707.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[195,298],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,84],"fullStemEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department experiencing sudden onset of severe, crushing substernal chest pain radiating to the left arm, accompanied by diaphoresis and shortness of breath. The triage nurse should assign the client an Emergency Severity Index (ESI) triage level of level ____.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因突然出现严重的、压榨性胸骨后疼痛并放射至左臂，伴有大汗和呼吸急促而被送往急诊科。分诊护士应将该患者的急诊严重指数 (ESI) 分诊级别评估为第 ____ 级。","terminalSentenceEn":"The triage nurse should assign the client an Emergency Severity Index (ESI) triage level of level ____.","terminalSentenceZh":"分诊护士应将该患者的急诊严重指数 (ESI) 分诊级别评估为第 ____ 级。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is brought to the emergency department experiencing sudden onset of severe, crushing substernal chest pain radiating to the left arm, accompanied by diaphoresis and shortness of breath.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因突然出现严重的、压榨性胸骨后疼痛并放射至左臂，伴有大汗和呼吸急促而被送往急诊科。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Level (1-5)","zh":"级别 (1-5)"},"acceptable":["1","level 1","one"],"numeric":{"value":1,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to the Emergency Severity Index (ESI) triage algorithm, a client with an unstable life-threatening condition (such as suspected myocardial infarction with severe cardiopulmonary compromise) requires immediate life-saving intervention and is classified as ESI Level 1.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据急诊严重指数 (ESI) 分诊算法，患有不稳定的危及生命病症（例如疑似心肌梗死伴有严重心肺受累）需要立即进行生命救治干预的患者，被归类为 ESI 1级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall ESI rules: Level 1 = requires immediate life-saving intervention. Level 2 = high risk/confused/severe pain. Level 3 = needs multiple resources. Level 4 = one resource. Level 5 = no resources.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想 ESI 规则：1 级 = 需要立即挽救生命的干预。2 级 = 高危/意识模糊/剧烈疼痛。3 级 = 需要多种资源。4 级 = 单一资源。5 级 = 无需资源。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":899,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.708","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.708.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.708.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[232,372],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,114],"fullStemEn":"During a mass casualty incident, a nurse triage officer assesses a victim who is alert, has a respiratory rate of 22 breaths per minute, a palpable radial pulse, and is complaining of a fractured forearm but can walk independently. According to the START triage algorithm, the nurse should assign this victim a green tag (Minor) which represents a priority number of ____.","fullStemZh":"在一次群死群伤事件中，一名分诊护士评估了一名意识清醒、呼吸频率为 22次/分、桡动脉搏动可触及、主诉前臂骨折但能独立行走的受害者。根据 START 分诊算法，护士应给这名受害者贴上绿色标签（轻伤），代表的优先级数字是 ____。","terminalSentenceEn":"According to the START triage algorithm, the nurse should assign this victim a green tag (Minor) which represents a priority number of ____.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据 START 分诊算法，护士应给这名受害者贴上绿色标签（轻伤），代表的优先级数字是 ____。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During a mass casualty incident, a nurse triage officer assesses a victim who is alert, has a respiratory rate of 22 breaths per minute, a palpable radial pulse, and is complaining of a fractured forearm but can walk independently.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在一次群死群伤事件中，一名分诊护士评估了一名意识清醒、呼吸频率为 22次/分、桡动脉搏动可触及、主诉前臂骨折但能独立行走的受害者。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Priority Level (1-4)","zh":"优先级 (1-4)"},"acceptable":["3","level 3","three","priority 3"],"numeric":{"value":3,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In disaster triage using the START (Simple Triage and Rapid Treatment) algorithm, victims are categorized using color tags: Red (Priority 1, Immediate), Yellow (Priority 2, Delayed), Green (Priority 3, Minor), and Black (Priority 4, Deceased). Walk-in/minor injury patients are tagged Green and classified as Priority 3.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在使用 START 算法的灾难分诊中，受害者被分为不同颜色的标签：红色（1级，立即救治）、黄色（2级，延迟救治）、绿色（3级，轻伤）和黑色（4级，死亡）。可自主行走/轻微伤的患者贴绿色标签，归类为优先级 3。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the lower priority number in disaster triage goes to the most critical patients (Red = 1, Yellow = 2, Green = 3, Black = 4).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住灾难分诊中较低的优先级数字对应最危重的患者（红色 = 1，黄色 = 2，绿色 = 3，黑色 = 4）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":900,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_mc_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.709","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.709.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.709.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,294],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,80],"fullStemEn":"A nurse administers an incorrect dose of medication to a client. The nurse assesses the client, notifies the provider, and prepares to complete an incident report. According to standard institutional policy, the nurse must complete and submit the incident report within ____ hours of the event.","fullStemZh":"护士给患者错误地注射了剂量的药物。护士评估患者，通知医生，并准备填写一份差错报告。根据标准的机构政策，护士必须在事件发生后 ____ 小时内填写并提交事故报告。","terminalSentenceEn":"According to standard institutional policy, the nurse must complete and submit the incident report within ____ hours of the event.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据标准的机构政策，护士必须在事件发生后 ____ 小时内填写并提交事故报告。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse assesses the client, notifies the provider, and prepares to complete an incident report.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士评估患者，通知医生，并准备填写一份差错报告。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"hours","zh":"小时"},"acceptable":["24","24 hours","twenty-four"],"numeric":{"value":24,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Standard hospital quality management policy requires that an incident (or variance) report be completed and submitted within 24 hours of the occurrence of the error. This ensures timely investigation and factual recall.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标准的医院质量管理政策要求差错（或变异）报告必须在差错发生后 24 小时内填写并提交。这确保了调查的及时性和对事实的准确记忆。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know standard timeline windows for quality improvement. 24 hours is the universal timeframe for documentation of deviations from standard care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解质量改进的标准时间窗口。24 小时是记录偏离标准护理事件的通用时间框架。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":901,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.710","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.710.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.710.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,224],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use axillary crutches to climb stairs using the three-point gait (non-weight-bearing on the affected left leg). Sequence the client's actions when ascending the stairs, from first to last.","fullStemZh":"护士正在教学患者如何使用腋下拐杖以三点步态爬楼梯（受累的左腿不承重）。将患者上楼梯时的动作按先后顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the client's actions when ascending the stairs, from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"将患者上楼梯时的动作按先后顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client how to use axillary crutches to climb stairs using the three-point gait (non-weight-bearing on the affected left leg).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在教学患者如何使用腋下拐杖以三点步态爬楼梯（受累的左腿不承重）。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Advance the unaffected right leg up to the step.","zh":"将未受累的右腿向前迈上台阶。"},{"id":"D","en":"Bring the crutches and the affected left leg up to the step.","zh":"将拐杖和受累的左腿一起带上台阶。"},{"id":"C","en":"Transfer body weight to the unaffected right leg.","zh":"将体重转移到未受累的右腿上。"},{"id":"A","en":"Push down on the handgrips of the crutches for support.","zh":"向下推拐杖的手柄以获得支撑。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To ascend stairs, the client should first establish support on the handgrips. Second, advance the unaffected ('good') leg onto the step. Third, shift weight to the unaffected leg. Finally, lift the crutches and the affected ('bad') leg to the same level.","rationaleCorrectZh":"要上楼梯，患者应首先在手柄上建立支撑。第二，将未受累的（“健”）腿迈上台阶。第三，将体重转移到未受累的腿上。最后，将拐杖和受累的（“患”）腿抬到同一水平。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the mnemonic: 'Up with the good, down with the bad.' The unaffected leg always leads when going up, and the crutches/affected leg lead going down.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住口诀：“好腿上行，坏腿下行”。上楼梯时未受累的腿总是领先，下楼梯时拐杖/受累的腿领先。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":902,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.711","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.711.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.711.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[133,254],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,75],"fullStemEn":"A client who is recovering from a right-sided stroke with left-sided weakness is being instructed on how to use a single-ended cane. The nurse should instruct the client to hold the cane on the {{1}} side and advance the cane together with the {{2}} leg.","fullStemZh":"一名因右侧中风导致左侧肢体无力的患者正在接受如何使用单脚手杖的指导。护士应指导患者将手杖握在 {{1}} 侧，并将手杖与 {{2}} 腿一起向前迈出。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should instruct the client to hold the cane on the {{1}} side and advance the cane together with the {{2}} leg.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应指导患者将手杖握在 {{1}} 侧，并将手杖与 {{2}} 腿一起向前迈出。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who is recovering from a right-sided stroke with left-sided weakness is being instructed on how to use a single-ended cane.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因右侧中风导致左侧肢体无力的患者正在接受如何使用单脚手杖的指导。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should instruct the client to hold the cane on the {{1}} and advance the cane together with the {{2}}.","zh":"护士应指导患者将手杖握在 {{1}}，并将手杖与 {{2}} 一起向前迈出。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"left (weak) side","zh":"左（患）侧"},{"id":"o1","en":"right (strong) side","zh":"右（健）侧"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"right (strong) leg","zh":"右（健）腿"},{"id":"o1","en":"left (weak) leg","zh":"左（患）腿"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A cane is held on the unaffected (stronger) side to widen the base of support and mimic natural gait. The cane and the affected (weaker) leg are moved forward together so the cane can share the weight-bearing load.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手杖应握在未受累的（健）侧，以拓宽支撑面并模拟自然步态。手杖和受累的（患）腿一起向前移动，以便手杖分担承重负荷。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the cane represents an extra leg supporting the weak side, but to maintain balance, it must be held on the strong side (C.O.A.L.: Cane Opposite Affected Leg).","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住手杖代表着支撑患侧的额外的一条腿，但为了保持平衡，它必须持于健侧 (C.O.A.L. 原则：手杖在患腿的对侧)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":903,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.712","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.712.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.712.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,41],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assisting a client with left-sided weakness to transfer from the bed to a wheelchair. Sequence the steps of a safe transfer, from first to last.","fullStemZh":"护士正协助一名左侧肢体无力的患者从床转移到轮椅上。将安全转移的步骤按先后顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the steps of a safe transfer, from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"将安全转移的步骤按先后顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assisting a client with left-sided weakness to transfer from the bed to a wheelchair.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正协助一名左侧肢体无力的患者从床转移到轮椅上。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Have the client push down on the mattress, stand, pivot, and lower themselves into the wheelchair.","zh":"让患者向下推床垫、站立、转动身体，然后落座于轮椅中。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the wheelchair at a 45-degree angle to the bed on the client's strong right side.","zh":"将轮椅放在患者健侧（右侧）与床呈 45 度角的位置。"},{"id":"B","en":"Lock the brakes on both the wheelchair and the bed.","zh":"锁定轮椅和床的刹车。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assist the client to a sitting position on the edge of the bed with feet flat on the floor.","zh":"协助患者在床边坐起，双脚平放在地板上。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First, place the wheelchair facing the strong side of the client. Second, lock all brakes to prevent moving during transfer. Third, dangle the patient on the bedside. Lastly, have the patient push up from the stable bed, stand, pivot towards the strong side, and sit down.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先，将轮椅面向患者的健侧放置。第二，锁定所有刹车以防止在转移过程中移动。第三，协助患者在床边垂腿坐。最后，让患者从稳定的床上推起、站立、转向健侧并坐下。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Ensure wheelchair is placed on the stronger side to support the client's weight during the pivot. Safety first implies locking brakes before patient movement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确保将轮椅放置在健侧，以在转动期间支撑患者的体重。安全第一意味着在患者活动前必须锁定刹车。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":904,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.713","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.713.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.713.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[100,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is providing foot care education to a client newly diagnosed with type 2 diabetes mellitus. The nurse should instruct the client to wash feet daily and {{1}} because {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名新诊断为 2 型糖尿病的患者提供足部护理教育。护士应指导患者每天洗脚并 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should instruct the client to wash feet daily and {{1}} because {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应指导患者每天洗脚并 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is providing foot care education to a client newly diagnosed with type 2 diabetes mellitus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名新诊断为 2 型糖尿病的患者提供足部护理教育。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should instruct the client to wash the feet daily and {{1}} because {{2}}.","zh":"护士应指导患者每天洗脚并 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"soak the feet in warm water for 30 minutes daily to soften calluses","zh":"每天将双脚浸泡在温水中 30 分钟以软化老茧"},{"id":"o1","en":"dry thoroughly between the toes and apply lotion only to tops/bottoms, avoiding between toes","zh":"彻底擦干趾缝，并仅在脚背/脚底涂抹乳液，避免涂在趾缝间"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"soaking prevents development of neuropathy","zh":"浸泡可以防止神经病变的发展"},{"id":"o1","en":"moisture between the toes increases the risk of fungal infection and skin breakdown","zh":"趾缝间的潮湿会增加真菌感染和皮肤破损的风险"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Diabetic neuropathy and vascular disease increase the risk of foot injuries and infections. Feet should be dried completely (especially between toes) to avoid moisture buildup. Lotion keeps the skin intact but must not be put between toes to avoid maceration. Soaking is contraindicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"糖尿病神经病变和血管病变会增加足部受伤和感染的风险。双脚应完全擦干（尤其是趾缝间）以避免水分积聚。润肤乳可保持皮肤完整，但绝不能涂在趾缝间以避免浸渍。禁忌浸泡双脚。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Eliminate choices containing 'soaking feet' or 'cutting toenails at angles' as these represent classic nursing hazards for diabetic clients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除包含“浸泡双脚”或“修剪趾甲成锐角”的选项，因为这些代表糖尿病患者的典型护理隐患。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":905,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.714","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.714.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.714.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,79],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is implementing a bladder training program for a client with urge incontinence. The client should be instructed to void on a set schedule every 2 hours and to {{1}} if they feel an urge to urinate before the scheduled time, in order to {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名急迫性尿失禁患者实施膀胱训练计划。应指导患者每 2 小时按设定的时间表排尿一次，如果在预定时间之前感到尿急，则应 {{1}}，以便 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client should be instructed to void on a set schedule every 2 hours and to {{1}} if they feel an urge to urinate before the scheduled time, in order to {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"应指导患者每 2 小时按设定的时间表排尿一次，如果在预定时间之前感到尿急，则应 {{1}}，以便 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is implementing a bladder training program for a client with urge incontinence.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名急迫性尿失禁患者实施膀胱训练计划。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"If the client feels an urge to urinate before the scheduled time, the nurse should instruct them to {{1}}, in order to {{2}}.","zh":"如果患者在预定时间之前感到尿急，护士应指导其 {{1}}，以便 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"immediately rush to the toilet to avoid accidental incontinence","zh":"立即冲向厕所起避免意外尿失禁"},{"id":"o1","en":"perform deep breathing or pelvic floor muscle exercises to suppress the urge","zh":"进行深呼吸或盆底肌锻炼以抑制尿急"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"gradually increase bladder capacity and strengthen detrusor muscle control","zh":"逐渐增加膀胱容量并增强逼尿肌控制"},{"id":"o2","en":"reduce the incidence of catheter-associated urinary tract infections","zh":"降低导尿管相关尿路感染的发生率"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Urge incontinence is managed by bladder training to increase detrusor control. When an urge occurs before the scheduled voiding time, the client should use urge-suppression techniques (like deep breathing or Kegel/pelvic floor exercises) to remain calm and allow the urge to pass, rather than rushing to the toilet, which reinforces urgency.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急迫性尿失禁通过膀胱训练来增加逼尿肌控制。当在预定排尿时间之前出现尿急时，患者应使用尿急抑制技术（如深呼吸或凯格尔/盆底肌运动）以保持平静并让尿急过去，而不是冲向厕所，否则会加重尿急感。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for behavioral, non-pharmacological interventions that focus on strengthening client control over detrusor instability, rather than immediate reactive actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找侧重于加强患者对逼尿肌不稳定控制的行为性、非药物性干预，而不是即刻的反应性行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":906,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.715","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.715.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.715.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,59],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching sleep hygiene strategies to a client with chronic insomnia. Classify each of the following client actions or choices as Indicated or Contraindicated.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名慢性失眠患者教学睡眠卫生策略。将以下每项患者的行为或选择分类为“适应证（适用）”或“禁忌证（不适用）”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following client actions or choices as Indicated or Contraindicated.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每项患者的行为或选择分类为“适应证（适用）”或“禁忌证（不适用）”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching sleep hygiene strategies to a client with chronic insomnia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名慢性失眠患者教学睡眠卫生策略。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Maintaining a consistent sleep-wake schedule, even on weekends.","zh":"即使在周末也保持规律一致的作息时间。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Drinking a warm cup of caffeinated tea 30 minutes before bedtime.","zh":"睡前 30 分钟喝一杯温热的含咖啡因茶。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Using the bedroom only for sleep and sexual activity.","zh":"卧室仅用于睡眠和性活动。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Taking a 2-hour nap in the late afternoon to catch up on sleep.","zh":"在傍晚睡 2 小时物觉以弥补睡眠。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Indicated","zh":"适用"},{"id":"c2","en":"Contraindicated","zh":"不适用"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Proper sleep hygiene includes keeping a consistent routine and restricting bedroom activities to sleep/sex to create a strong mental association. Caffeine and late/long naps disrupt sleep architecture and decrease nighttime sleep drive, making them contraindicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的睡眠卫生包括保持一致的作息，并将卧室活动限制在睡眠/性生活上，以建立强大的心理联想。咖啡因和晚间/长时间的午睡会破坏睡眠结构并降低夜间睡眠驱动力，因此是禁忌的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify options that support the body's natural circadian rhythm (regular schedule, no stimulants, bed association) and separate them from those that disrupt it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别支持身体自然昼夜节律的选项（规律的作息、无兴奋剂、床的联想），并将它们与破坏昼夜节律的选项区分开来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":907,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.716","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.716.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.716.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assessing a client's risk for pressure injuries using the Braden Scale risk factors. Match each Braden Scale risk factor with the corresponding nursing assessment parameter.","fullStemZh":"护士正在使用 Braden 量表风险因素评估患者发生压疮的风险。将每个 Braden 量表风险因素与相应的护理评估参数相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each Braden Scale risk factor with the corresponding nursing assessment parameter.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每个 Braden 量表风险因素与相应的护理评估参数相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assessing a client's risk for pressure injuries using the Braden Scale risk factors.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在使用 Braden 量表风险因素评估患者发生压疮的风险。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Ability to respond meaningfully to pressure-related discomfort.","zh":"对压迫相关不适做出有意义反应的能力。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Degree of physical activity (bedfast, chairfast, walks).","zh":"身体活动度（卧床、坐椅、行走）。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Ability to change and control body position.","zh":"改变和控制身体姿势的能力。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Usual food intake pattern (number of meals, tube feeding, TPN).","zh":"日常食物摄入模式（餐数、管饲、TPN）。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Sensory Perception","zh":"感觉感知"},{"id":"c3","en":"Mobility","zh":"移动能力"},{"id":"c4","en":"Nutrition","zh":"营养状况"},{"id":"c2","en":"Activity","zh":"活动能力"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Braden Scale evaluates 6 subscales: Sensory Perception (response to discomfort), Activity (degree of physical activity), Mobility (ability to change position), Nutrition (food intake pattern), Moisture (skin exposure to wetness), and Friction/Shear. Accurate matching aligns risk factors to their indicators.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Braden 量表评估 6 个子量表：感觉感知（对不适的反应）、活动能力（身体活动程度）、移动能力（改变体位的能力）、营养状况（食物摄入模式）、潮湿（皮肤暴露于潮湿环境中的程度）以及摩擦力和剪切力。准确的匹配将风险因素与其指标相结合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that 'Activity' refers to the frequency of movement (e.g. ambulatory vs bedfast) whereas 'Mobility' refers to the mechanical ability to adjust one's own position in bed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想一下，“活动能力”是指活动的频率（例如行走与卧床），而“移动能力”是指在床上调整自己体位的机械能力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":908,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.717","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.717.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.717.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[43,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,42],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is planning comfort interventions. Classify each of the following heat or cold therapy applications as Appropriate or Inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"护士正在计划舒适护理干预。将以下每项热敷或冷敷疗法的应用分类为“合适”或“不合适”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following heat or cold therapy applications as Appropriate or Inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每项热敷或冷敷疗法的应用分类为“合适”或“不合适”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning comfort interventions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在计划舒适护理干预。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Applying a warm moist compress to a client's localized IV infiltration site.","zh":"在患者局部的输液外渗部位进行温湿敷。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Applying an ice pack directly to the bare skin of a client's sprained ankle.","zh":"将冰袋直接敷在患者扭伤脚踝的裸露皮肤上。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Using a heating pad on the lower abdomen of a client with suspected acute appendicitis.","zh":"在疑似急性阑尾炎患者的下腹部使用加热垫。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Applying a cold compress to a client's forehead to reduce headache discomfort.","zh":"在患者前额进行冷敷以减轻头痛不适。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warm compresses promote vasodilation and absorption of non-vesicant infiltrated IV fluids. Ice packs should never be applied directly to bare skin to prevent tissue damage (frostbite). Heat is contraindicated in acute appendicitis as it can cause vascular congestion and rupture. Cold compresses are safe for symptomatic headache relief.","rationaleCorrectZh":"温敷可促进血管扩张和非发疱性外渗静脉液体的吸收。冰袋绝不能直接涂在裸露的皮肤上以防止组织损伤（冻伤）。在急性阑尾炎中禁用热敷，因为这会引起血管充血和破裂。冷敷用于缓解头痛症状是安全的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that direct cold contact causes tissue damage, and heat should never be applied to areas of active acute inflammation (like appendicitis) due to rupture risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住直接冷接触会引起组织损伤，且由于破裂风险，切勿将热敷应用于活动性急性炎症区域（如阑尾炎）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is planning comfort interventions.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在计划舒适护理干预。"}
{"queueIndex":909,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.718","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.718.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.718.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,49],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an intermittent enteral feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube to a client. Sequence the nursing actions from first to last to ensure safe administration.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备通过鼻胃管 (NG) 为一名患者进行间歇性管饲。按先后顺序排列护士的行为以确保安全给药。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the nursing actions from first to last to ensure safe administration.","terminalSentenceZh":"按先后顺序排列护士的行为以确保安全给药。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an intermittent enteral feeding via a nasogastric (NG) tube to a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备通过鼻胃管 (NG) 为一名患者进行间歇性管饲。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer the enteral formula at room temperature over the prescribed duration.","zh":"在规定的时间内给予常温的肠内营养液。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify NG tube placement by measuring tube length and checking gastric pH.","zh":"通过测量导管长度和检查胃液 pH 值来验证鼻胃管位置。"},{"id":"E","en":"Flush the tube with 30 mL of sterile or tap water.","zh":"用 30 毫升无菌水或自来水冲洗管路。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess gastric residual volume (GRV) to monitor for delayed gastric emptying.","zh":"评估胃残留量 (GRV) 以监测是否存在胃排空延迟。"},{"id":"A","en":"Elevate the head of the bed to 30 to 45 degrees.","zh":"将床头抬高 30 至 45 度。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Before any manipulation, the head of the bed must be elevated to prevent aspiration. Second, the tube placement must be verified to ensure the formula enters the stomach. Third, check residuals to evaluate gastric tolerance. Fourth, administer formula at room temperature. Finally, flush to keep the tube patent and prevent bacterial growth.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在进行任何操作之前，必须抬高床头以防止误吸。第二，必须验证胃管位置以确保营养液进入胃内。第三，检查残留量以评估胃耐受性。第四，在室温下给予营养液。最后，冲洗管路以保持通畅并防止细菌滋生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Aspiration prevention (positioning) is the highest safety priority. The remaining steps proceed from verification, assessment, implementation, to maintenance flushing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"预防误吸（体位）是最高的安全优先级。其余步骤依次为验证、评估、实施以及维持性冲洗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":910,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.719","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.719.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.719.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,228],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,59],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assisting with the positioning of a client who has just returned to the unit after an infratentorial craniotomy. Sequence the nurse's actions to ensure proper positioning and prevent complications, from first to last.","fullStemZh":"护士正在协助为一名刚进行幕下开颅手术返回病房的患者进行体位摆放。按先后顺序排列护士的行为以确保正确的体位并预防并发症。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the nurse's actions to ensure proper positioning and prevent complications, from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"按先后顺序排列护士的行为以确保正确的体位并预防并发症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assisting with the positioning of a client who has just returned to the unit after an infratentorial craniotomy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在协助为一名刚进行幕下开颅手术返回病房的患者进行体位摆放。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Align the head and neck in a neutral, straight position.","zh":"将头部和颈部对齐在居中的直立位置。"},{"id":"D","en":"Reposition the client side-to-side every 2 hours, keeping the neck straight.","zh":"每 2 小时为患者重新调整左右侧卧位，保持颈部直立。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place a small pillow under the head, avoiding flexion of the neck.","zh":"在头部下方垫一个小枕头，避免颈部弯曲。"},{"id":"A","en":"Keep the head of the bed flat or elevated no more than 30 degrees.","zh":"保持床头平放或抬高不超过 30 度。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For an infratentorial craniotomy, the head of the bed must be kept flat or low (no more than 30 degrees) to prevent pressure on the brainstem. The head and neck must be aligned in a neutral, straight position. A small pillow is placed under the head to avoid flexion, and the client is turned side-to-side with neck alignment maintained.","rationaleCorrectZh":"幕下开颅手术后，床头必须保持平放或低位（不超过 30 度），以防止压迫脑干。头部和颈部必须对齐在居中、直立的位置。头部下方放置一个小枕头以避免屈曲，并在保持颈部对齐的同时协助患者左右翻身。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between supratentorial surgery (head of bed elevated 30-45 degrees to prevent ICP) vs infratentorial surgery (head of bed flat or low).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分幕上手术（床头抬高 30-45 度以预防颅内压增高）与幕下手术（床头平放或低位）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":911,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.720","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.720.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.720.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[294,350],"terminalOffsetsZh":[118,143],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is calculating the 8-hour fluid intake for a client. The client consumed: 4 oz of apple juice, 1 bowl of gelatin (equivalent to 120 mL), 1 bowl of ice chips (calculate ice as half the volume, total bowl volume was 200 mL), and received 250 mL of IV normal saline. (Note: 1 oz = 30 mL). The total fluid intake for this 8-hour shift is ____ mL.","fullStemZh":"护士正在计算患者 8 小时的液体摄入量。患者消耗了：4 盎司苹果汁，1 碗明胶（相当于 120 毫升），1 碗冰块（按冰块体积的一半计算液体，整碗体积为 200 毫升），并输入了 250 毫升生理盐水。（注：1 盎司 = 30 毫升）。该班次 8 小时的总液体摄入量为 ____ 毫升。","terminalSentenceEn":"The total fluid intake for this 8-hour shift is ____ mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"该班次 8 小时的总液体摄入量为 ____ 毫升。","penultimateSentenceEn":"(Note: 1 oz = 30 mL).","penultimateSentenceZh":"注：1 盎司 = 30 毫升）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["590","590 mL","590毫升"],"numeric":{"value":590,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: 4 oz of juice = 120 mL (4 * 30). Gelatin = 120 mL. Ice chips are calculated as half their frozen volume to represent actual liquid water (200 mL / 2 = 100 mL). IV normal saline = 250 mL. Total intake = 120 + 120 + 100 + 250 = 590 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算过程：4 盎司果汁 = 120 毫升 (4 * 30)。明胶 = 120 毫升。冰块按其冰冻体积的一半计算，以代表实际液态水（200 毫升 / 2 = 100 毫升）。静脉生理盐水 = 250 毫升。总摄入量 = 120 + 120 + 100 + 250 = 590 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember two conversions: 1 oz = 30 mL, and ice chips volume is cut in half (100 mL of ice chips = 50 mL of water) when calculating intake.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住两个换算：1 盎司 = 30 毫升，且在计算摄入量时冰块体积要减半（100 毫升冰块 = 50 毫升水）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":912,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.721","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.721.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.721.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[100,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,68],"fullStemEn":"A nurse performs a bladder scan on a post-operative client who has been unable to void for 6 hours. According to institutional protocol, urinary catheterization is indicated if the bladder scan reveals a residual urine volume of ____ mL or greater.","fullStemZh":"护士对一名术后 6 小时内无法排尿的患者进行膀胱扫描。根据机构规程，如果膀胱扫描显示残余尿量达到 ____ 毫升或以上，则需要进行导尿。","terminalSentenceEn":"According to institutional protocol, urinary catheterization is indicated if the bladder scan reveals a residual urine volume of ____ mL or greater.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据机构规程，如果膀胱扫描显示残余尿量达到 ____ 毫升或以上，则需要进行导尿。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse performs a bladder scan on a post-operative client who has been unable to void for 6 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士对一名术后 6 小时内无法排尿的患者进行膀胱扫描。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["300","300 mL","300毫升","300ml"],"numeric":{"value":300,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to clinical guidelines, urinary catheterization is indicated for acute urinary retention if the bladder scan reveals 300-400 mL of urine, to prevent detrusor overstretch and urinary tract infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据临床指南，如果膀胱扫描显示有 300-400 毫升的尿液，则对于急性尿潴留需要进行导尿，以防止逼尿肌过度伸展和尿路感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall that 300 mL represents the standard threshold where nursing intervention for retention is indicated to avoid bladder distention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想一下，300 毫升代表了需要进行导尿干预以避免膀胱过度膨胀的标准阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":913,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_bcc_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.722","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.722.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.722.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,234],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,69],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a client who had a total hip arthroplasty (posterior approach) about post-operative movement restrictions. To prevent hip dislocation, the client must avoid flexing the affected hip joint greater than ____ degrees.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名进行了全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）的患者宣教术后运动限制。为了防止髋关节脱位，患者必须避免将受累髋关节屈曲超过 ____ 度。","terminalSentenceEn":"To prevent hip dislocation, the client must avoid flexing the affected hip joint greater than ____ degrees.","terminalSentenceZh":"为了防止髋关节脱位，患者必须避免将受累髋关节屈曲超过 ____ 度。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a client who had a total hip arthroplasty (posterior approach) about post-operative movement restrictions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向一名进行了全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）的患者宣教术后运动限制。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"degrees","zh":"度"},"acceptable":["90","90 degrees","90度"],"numeric":{"value":90,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After a posterior total hip arthroplasty, the client must follow hip precautions to prevent dislocation: avoid hip flexion greater than 90 degrees, avoid adduction past midline (use abduction pillow), and avoid internal rotation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）后，患者必须遵守髋关节预防措施以防止脱位：避免髋关节屈曲超过 90 度，避免内收超过中线（使用外展枕），并避免内旋。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that a right angle (90 degrees) is the absolute limit for safe hip bending post-operatively.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住直角（90 度）是术后髋关节安全弯曲的绝对限制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":914,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.723","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.723.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.723.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,189],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,54],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for a client under contact and droplet precautions. Sequence the steps for donning personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order, from first to last.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备护理一名处于接触和飞沫预防措施下的患者。按正确的先后顺序排列穿戴个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the steps for donning personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order, from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"按正确的先后顺序排列穿戴个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to care for a client under contact and droplet precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备护理一名处于接触和飞沫预防措施下的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Gloves","zh":"手套"},{"id":"B","en":"Mask or respirator","zh":"口罩或呼吸防护器"},{"id":"C","en":"Goggles or face shield","zh":"护目镜或面罩"},{"id":"A","en":"Gown","zh":"隔离衣"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to CDC guidelines, the correct sequence for donning PPE is: 1. Gown, 2. Mask or respirator, 3. Goggles or face shield, 4. Gloves. Gloves are put on last and should cover the cuffs of the gown.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据 CDC 指南，穿戴个人防护装备 (PPE) 的正确顺序是：1. 隔离衣，2. 口罩或呼吸防护器，3. 护目镜或面罩，4. 手套。手套最后戴上，并且应覆盖隔离衣的袖口。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that gloves must always be last when donning, and the gown must be first to allow other barriers to sit securely on top.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住穿戴时手套必须总是排在最后，隔离衣必须排在第一，以便其他屏障牢固地置于其上。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":915,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.724","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.724.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.724.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,223],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,65],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is exiting the room of a client who is on airborne and contact precautions. Sequence the steps for removing personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order, from first to last (standard CDC recommendation).","fullStemZh":"护士正在走出处于空气和接触预防措施下的患者房间。根据标准 CDC 推荐，按正确的先后顺序排列脱下个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the steps for removing personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order, from first to last (standard CDC recommendation).","terminalSentenceZh":"根据标准 CDC 推荐，按正确的先后顺序排列脱下个人防护装备 (PPE) 的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is exiting the room of a client who is on airborne and contact precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在走出处于空气和接触预防措施下的患者房间。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Gloves","zh":"手套"},{"id":"B","en":"Goggles or face shield","zh":"护目镜或面罩"},{"id":"C","en":"Gown","zh":"隔离衣"},{"id":"D","en":"Mask or respirator (remove outside the room)","zh":"口罩或呼吸防护器（在房间外脱下）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to standard CDC guidelines, the sequence for removing PPE is: 1. Gloves (most contaminated), 2. Goggles or face shield, 3. Gown, 4. Mask or respirator (always removed outside the client room for airborne precautions). Hand hygiene must be performed between steps if hands become contaminated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据标准 CDC 指南，脱下个人防护装备 (PPE) 的顺序是：1. 手套（污染最严重），2. 护目镜或面罩，3. 隔离衣，4. 口罩或呼吸防护器（对于空气传播预防措施，务必在患者房间外脱下）。如果手部受到污染，在步骤之间必须进行手卫生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the most contaminated item (gloves) is removed first, and the mask is always removed last (and outside the room for airborne cases) to protect the airway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住污染最严重的物品（手套）首先脱下，口罩总是最后脱下（对于空气传播病例，在房间外脱下）以保护气道。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is exiting the room of a client who is on airborne and contact precautions.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在走出处于空气和接触预防措施下的患者房间。"}
{"queueIndex":916,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.725","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.725.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.725.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,33],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assigning isolation precautions. Classify the barrier or precaution required for each infection type.","fullStemZh":"护士正在分配隔离预防措施。为每种感染类型分类所需的屏障或预防措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify the barrier or precaution required for each infection type.","terminalSentenceZh":"为每种感染类型分类所需的屏障或预防措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is assigning isolation precautions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在分配隔离预防措施。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Pulmonary Tuberculosis (TB)","zh":"肺结核 (TB)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Disseminated Herpes Zoster (Shingles)","zh":"播散性带状疱疹"},{"id":"r3","en":"Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus Aureus (MRSA) Wound Infection","zh":"耐甲氧西林金黄色葡萄球菌 (MRSA) 伤口感染"},{"id":"r4","en":"Seasonal Influenza","zh":"季节性流感"}],"columns":[{"id":"c4","en":"Airborne and Contact Precautions","zh":"空气与接触传播双重预防措施"},{"id":"c3","en":"Droplet Precautions (Surgical Mask)","zh":"飞沫传播预防措施 (外科口罩)"},{"id":"c2","en":"Contact Precautions (Gown + Gloves)","zh":"接触传播预防措施 (隔离衣 + 手套)"},{"id":"c1","en":"Airborne Precautions (N95 + Negative Pressure)","zh":"空气传播预防措施 (N95 + 负压)"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c4"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tuberculosis requires Airborne precautions. Disseminated shingles requires both Airborne and Contact precautions due to the combination of fluid-filled lesions and potential aerosolization. MRSA wound infections require Contact precautions. Influenza requires Droplet precautions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肺结核需要空气传播预防措施。播散性带状疱疹由于充满液体的皮损和潜在的空气溶胶化，需要空气和接触传播双重预防措施。MRSA 伤口感染需要接触传播预防措施。流感需要飞沫传播预防措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate localized shingles (Standard precautions if covered, Contact precautions if uncovered) from disseminated shingles (Airborne and Contact precautions).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分局部带状疱疹（如果覆盖则只需标准预防措施，未覆盖则需接触传播预防措施）与播散性带状疱疹（需要空气和接触传播预防措施）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":917,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.726","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.726.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.726.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,47],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for clients with various respiratory infections. Classify each of the following diseases under the appropriate transmission-based precaution category.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理患有各种呼吸道感染的患者。将以下每种疾病分类到相应的基于传播途径的预防措施类别下。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following diseases under the appropriate transmission-based precaution category.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每种疾病分类到相应的基于传播途径的预防措施类别下。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for clients with various respiratory infections.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理患有各种呼吸道感染的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Rubeola (Measles)","zh":"麻疹"},{"id":"r2","en":"Neisseria meningitidis Pneumonia","zh":"脑膜炎奈瑟菌肺炎"},{"id":"r3","en":"Bordetella pertussis (Whooping Cough)","zh":"百日咳"},{"id":"r4","en":"Varicella (Chickenpox)","zh":"水痘"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Airborne + Contact Precautions","zh":"空气传播 + 接触传播预防措施"},{"id":"c1","en":"Airborne Precautions","zh":"空气传播预防措施"},{"id":"c2","en":"Droplet Precautions","zh":"飞沫传播预防措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Measles requires Airborne precautions. Varicella requires Airborne plus Contact precautions until lesions are dry and crusted. Meningococcal pneumonia and pertussis require Droplet precautions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"麻疹需要空气传播预防措施。水痘在皮损干燥结痂前需要空气传播加接触传播预防措施。脑膜炎球菌性肺炎和百日咳需要飞沫传播预防措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that varicella is an Airborne disease that also requires Contact precautions because infectious lesions can transmit virus by direct contact.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住水痘属于空气传播疾病，同时因感染性皮损可通过直接接触传播而需要接触传播预防措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":918,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.727","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.727.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.727.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[68,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,51],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is managing care for four clients with infectious diseases. Classify each clinical action or choice as Appropriate or Inappropriate for the client's condition.","fullStemZh":"护士正管理四名患有传染病患者的护理。将以下每项临床行为或选择分类为对该患者状况的“合适”或“不合适”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each clinical action or choice as Appropriate or Inappropriate for the client's condition.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每项临床行为或选择分类为对该患者状况的“合适”或“不合适”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is managing care for four clients with infectious diseases.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正管理四名患有传染病患者的护理。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Using soap and water after glove removal during a Clostridioides difficile outbreak.","zh":"在艰难梭菌暴发期间，脱下手套后使用肥皂和水进行手部卫生。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Placing a client with Vancomycin-Resistant Enterococci (VRE) in a room with a client who has a fresh surgical incision.","zh":"将患有耐万古霉素肠球菌 (VRE) 的患者与一名刚做过外科手术切口的患者安置在同一房间。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Having a client with active Tuberculosis wear a surgical mask when leaving the room for diagnostic procedures.","zh":"让活动性结核病患者在离开房间进行诊断检查时佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Transporting a client with droplet precautions without a mask, relying on 3 feet of distance.","zh":"在不戴口罩的情况下转运需要飞沫预防措施的患者，仅依靠 3 英尺的距离。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During a C. difficile outbreak, soap and water is preferred after glove removal because alcohol lacks sporicidal activity. Placing a VRE patient with a postoperative patient is unsafe because of cross-transmission risk. Patients with TB wear surgical masks during transport for source control. Patients on Droplet precautions also wear a mask during necessary transport.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在艰难梭菌暴发期间，因酒精不具杀芽孢活性，脱下手套后首选肥皂和水。将VRE患者与术后患者安置在一起会增加交叉传播风险，因此不安全。结核病患者转运时佩戴外科口罩以进行源头控制。实施飞沫传播预防措施的患者在必要转运时也应佩戴口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that infected patients wear surgical masks during transport to filter outgoing air, whereas healthcare workers wear N95 respirators to filter incoming air.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住感染患者在转运期间佩戴外科口罩以过滤呼出的空气，而医护人员佩戴 N95 呼吸防护器以过滤吸入的空气。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":919,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.728","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.728.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.728.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,54],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is applying soft wrist restraints to a confused client who is pulling at life-support lines. Sequence the nurse's actions from first to last to ensure client safety.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名试图拔掉生命维持管路的意识模糊患者使用软质手腕约束带。按先后顺序排列护士的行为以确保患者安全。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the nurse's actions from first to last to ensure client safety.","terminalSentenceZh":"按先后顺序排列护士的行为以确保患者安全。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is applying soft wrist restraints to a confused client who is pulling at life-support lines.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名试图拔掉生命维持管路的意识模糊患者使用软质手腕约束带。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Obtain a written healthcare provider's order for restraints.","zh":"获得医疗服务提供者开具的书面约束医嘱。"},{"id":"C","en":"Tie the restraint straps to the bed frame using a quick-release knot, not the side rails.","zh":"使用快速释放结将约束带拉带系在床架上，而不是侧栏上。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess skin integrity, pulse, and sensation distal to the restraints every 2 hours.","zh":"每 2 小时评估约束远端的皮肤完整性、脉搏和感觉。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wrap the soft part of the restraint around the client's wrist and secure it with Velcro.","zh":"将约束带的柔软部分包裹在患者的手腕上，并用魔术贴固定。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must have a prescription before applying restraints (or immediately after in an emergency). Apply the soft sleeve to protect the skin first. Tie to the bed frame (never the side rails, as moving rails can cause injury) with a quick-release knot for emergencies. Regularly monitor circulation and skin integrity every 2 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士在实施约束之前必须有处方（或在紧急情况下立即补办）。首先包上柔软的袖套以保护皮肤。用快速释放结将约束带系在床架上（绝不能系在侧栏上，因为移动侧栏会引起拉伤）。每 2 小时定期监测血液循环和皮肤完整性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify safety-critical steps: never tie restraints to side rails (moving parts) and always use a quick-release knot for emergency access.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别关键安全步骤：切勿将约束带系在侧栏上（属于活动部件），并始终使用快速释放结以便在紧急情况下拆除。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":920,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.729","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.729.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.729.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is admitted with severe preeclampsia and is at risk for seizures (eclampsia). The nurse should ensure that {{1}} and {{2}} during a seizure event.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名因重度子痫前期入院且有抽搐风险（子痫）的患者。护士应确保 {{1}} 并在抽搐发作期间 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should ensure that {{1}} and {{2}} during a seizure event.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应确保 {{1}} 并在抽搐发作期间 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is admitted with severe preeclampsia and is at risk for seizures (eclampsia).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名因重度子痫前期入院且有抽搐风险（子痫）的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should ensure that {{1}} and, during a seizure event, {{2}}.","zh":"护士应确保 {{1}}，并在抽搐发作期间 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"the bed side rails are padded and suction equipment is set up at the bedside","zh":"床头侧栏加垫，并在床边设置吸引设备"},{"id":"o2","en":"a padded tongue blade is taped to the wall above the bed for insertion","zh":"将加垫压舌板贴在床头墙壁上以便插入"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"insert a plastic airway immediately and physically restrain the client's limbs","zh":"立即插入塑料气道并身体约束患者的肢体"},{"id":"o1","en":"turn the client to a side-lying position and never insert any objects into the client's mouth","zh":"将患者转向侧卧位，切勿向患者嘴里插入任何物品"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Seizure precautions include padding side rails and having suction/oxygen ready. During a seizure, protecting the airway and preventing aspiration is done by turning the client side-lying. Inserting objects (like tongue blades) into the mouth is contraindicated as it can cause airway obstruction or dental injury. Restraining limbs can cause fractures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"抽搐预防措施包括在侧栏加垫并备好吸引/吸氧装置。在抽搐发作期间，通过将患者转向侧卧位来保护气道并防止误吸。往嘴里插入物品（如压舌板）是禁忌的，因为这会引起气道阻塞或牙齿损伤。强行约束肢体可能会导致骨折。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always eliminate choices advocating inserting items into a seizing client's mouth or using physical force/restraints to hold them down.","testTakingStrategyZh":"一律排除提倡向抽搐患者嘴里插入物品，或使用体力/约束物强行按压住他们的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":921,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.730","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.730.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.730.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,65],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is receiving internal radiation therapy (brachytherapy) for cervical cancer. The nurse should limit visits to {{1}} and ensure that visitor distance is maintained at {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名因宫颈癌接受内放射治疗（近距离放射治疗）的患者。护士应将探视限制在 {{1}}，并确保探视距离保持在 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should limit visits to {{1}} and ensure that visitor distance is maintained at {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将探视限制在 {{1}}，并确保探视距离保持在 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client who is receiving internal radiation therapy (brachytherapy) for cervical cancer.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名因宫颈癌接受内放射治疗（近距离放射治疗）的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should limit visits to {{1}} and ensure that visitor distance is maintained at {{2}}.","zh":"护士应将探视限制在 {{1}}，并确保探视距离保持在 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"60 minutes per day with no visitor restrictions","zh":"每天 60 分钟，不限制探视者"},{"id":"o1","en":"30 minutes per day and restrict pregnant visitors","zh":"每天 30 分钟，并限制孕妇探视"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"3 feet (1 meter) or more from the client","zh":"距离患者 3 英尺（1 米）或以上"},{"id":"o1","en":"6 feet (2 meters) or more from the client","zh":"距离患者 6 英尺（2 米）或以上"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Radiation safety protocols (ALARA: As Low As Reasonably Achievable) dictate minimizing time, maximizing distance, and utilizing shielding. Visits are capped at 30 minutes daily, pregnant visitors/staff are strictly banned, and visitors must stand at least 6 feet away from the radiation source.","rationaleCorrectZh":"辐射安全规程 (ALARA 原则：尽可能低地达到合理可行水平) 要求尽量减少时间、最大化距离并利用屏蔽。探视时间每天限制在 30 分钟以内，严格禁止孕妇探视/工作人员接触，且探视者必须距离辐射源至少 6 英尺。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply ALARA principles: 30 minutes and 6 feet are key thresholds in NCLEX-RN radiation safety guidelines.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用 ALARA 原则：30 分钟和 6 英尺是 NCLEX-RN 辐射安全指南中的关键阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":true,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":true,"clozeStemContainedInStem":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":true},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":922,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.731","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.731.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.731.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,44],"fullStemEn":"After administering an intramuscular injection, the nurse should immediately {{1}} and dispose of the syringe in the sharps container without {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"在进行肌内注射后，护士应立即 {{1}} 并将注射器丢弃在锐器盒中，而不能 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"After administering an intramuscular injection, the nurse should immediately {{1}} and dispose of the syringe in the sharps container without {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"在进行肌内注射后，护士应立即 {{1}} 并将注射器丢弃在锐器盒中，而不能 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should immediately {{1}} and dispose of the syringe in the sharps container without {{2}}.","zh":"护士应立即 {{1}}，并将注射器丢弃在锐器盒中，而不能 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"activate the needle safety device","zh":"启动针头安全装置"},{"id":"o2","en":"wipe the needle with an alcohol swab","zh":"用酒精棉签擦拭针头"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"recapping the needle using a two-handed technique","zh":"使用双手技术重新盖上针帽"},{"id":"o2","en":"verifying the client's identification band","zh":"核对患者的身份识别带"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To prevent needle-stick injuries, used needles must never be recapped using a two-handed technique. The nurse should activate the safety shield immediately after use and discard the entire assembly into a puncture-resistant sharps container.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为防止针刺伤，绝不能使用双手技术重新盖上用过的针头。护士应在使用后立即启动安全保护罩，并将整个组件丢弃在防穿刺锐器盒中。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that safety devices are designed for immediate activation. Recapping single-use needles is forbidden.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到安全装置设计用于立即启动。禁止对一次性针头进行重新戴帽。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":923,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.732","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.732.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.732.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is teaching a student nurse about standard hand hygiene. According to CDC guidelines, when washing hands with soap and water, the nurse should rub hands together vigorously for at least ____ seconds.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向护生教学标准手卫生。根据 CDC 指南，用肥皂和水洗手时，护士应大力揉搓双手至少 ____ 秒。","terminalSentenceEn":"According to CDC guidelines, when washing hands with soap and water, the nurse should rub hands together vigorously for at least ____ seconds.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据 CDC 指南，用肥皂和水洗手时，护士应大力揉搓双手至少 ____ 秒。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is teaching a student nurse about standard hand hygiene.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向护生教学标准手卫生。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"seconds","zh":"秒"},"acceptable":["20","20 seconds","twenty"],"numeric":{"value":20,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) recommends rubbing hands with soap and water for at least 20 seconds to mechanically remove transient pathogens from the skin surface.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疾病预防控制中心 (CDC) 建议用肥皂和水搓手至少 20 秒，以机械方式清除皮肤表面的暂居病原体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate CDC minimum guidelines (20 seconds) from surgical scrub times (2-6 minutes).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分 CDC 最低指南（20 秒）与外科刷手时间（2-6 分钟）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":924,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.733","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.733.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.733.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,76],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client undergoing chemotherapy and monitoring for severe neutropenia. Severe neutropenia exists when the absolute neutrophil count (ANC) falls below ____ cells/mcL.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名接受化疗的患者并监测重度中性粒细胞减少症。当绝对中性粒细胞计数 (ANC) 降至 ____ 个/微升以下时，即存在重度中性粒细胞减少症。","terminalSentenceEn":"Severe neutropenia exists when the absolute neutrophil count (ANC) falls below ____ cells/mcL.","terminalSentenceZh":"当绝对中性粒细胞计数 (ANC) 降至 ____ 个/微升以下时，即存在重度中性粒细胞减少症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client undergoing chemotherapy and monitoring for severe neutropenia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名接受化疗的患者并监测重度中性粒细胞减少症。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"cells/mcL","zh":"个/微升"},"acceptable":["500","five hundred"],"numeric":{"value":500,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An ANC below 500 cells/mcL indicates severe neutropenia and high infection risk. Use individualized infection-prevention measures. CDC's defined Protective Environment, including specialized positive-pressure and HEPA engineering controls, is specifically recommended for allogeneic hematopoietic stem-cell transplant recipients rather than automatically for every chemotherapy client with neutropenia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ANC低于500个/微升表示重度中性粒细胞减少症和较高感染风险。应采用个体化感染预防措施。CDC所定义的保护性环境包括特殊正压和HEPA工程控制，专门建议用于异基因造血干细胞移植受者，而不是所有化疗相关中性粒细胞减少患者自动适用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know lab thresholds: Normal ANC is 1,500-8,000. Moderate risk is 500-1,000. High/severe risk is < 500.","testTakingStrategyZh":"了解实验室检查阈值：正常 ANC 为 1,500-8,000。中度风险为 500-1,000。高度/重度风险为 < 500。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":925,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_sic_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.734","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.734.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.734.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,253],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,61],"fullStemEn":"A client experiences an accidental chemical splash of concentrated hydrochloric acid to the eyes. The nurse should immediately begin flushing the client's eyes with water or saline for a minimum of ____ minutes before seeking further medical evaluation.","fullStemZh":"一名患者的眼睛不慎溅入浓盐酸。在寻求进一步的医疗评估之前，护士应立即开始用水或生理盐水冲洗患者的眼睛至少 ____ 分钟。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should immediately begin flushing the client's eyes with water or saline for a minimum of ____ minutes before seeking further medical evaluation.","terminalSentenceZh":"在寻求进一步的医疗评估之前，护士应立即开始用水或生理盐水冲洗患者的眼睛至少 ____ 分钟。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client experiences an accidental chemical splash of concentrated hydrochloric acid to the eyes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者的眼睛不慎溅入浓盐酸。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minutes","zh":"分钟"},"acceptable":["15","15 minutes","fifteen"],"numeric":{"value":15,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate decontamination of chemical eye injuries is critical. Irrigation with running water or saline must begin immediately at the scene and continue for at least 15 to 20 minutes to dilute and remove the chemical substance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"化学性眼外伤的即刻去污至关重要。必须在现场立即开始用流动水或生理盐水冲洗，并持续至少 15 至 20 分钟，以稀释并清除化学物质。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall standard first aid and OSHA decontamination timelines. 15 minutes is the universally accepted minimum irrigation period for chemical exposure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想标准急救和 OSHA 去污时间。15 分钟是公认的化学暴露最低冲洗时间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":926,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.735","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.735.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.735.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,57],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is administering packed red blood cells to a client who suddenly develops fever, chills, and lower back pain, indicating an acute hemolytic transfusion reaction. Sequence the nurse's actions from first to last.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名患者输注红细胞悬液，患者突然出现发热、寒战和腰痛，提示急性溶血性输血反应。按先后顺序排列护士的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the nurse's actions from first to last.","terminalSentenceZh":"按先后顺序排列护士的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is administering packed red blood cells to a client who suddenly develops fever, chills, and lower back pain, indicating an acute hemolytic transfusion reaction.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名患者输注红细胞悬液，患者突然出现发热、寒战和腰痛，提示急性溶血性输血反应。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Disconnect the blood tubing and infuse normal saline through new tubing to keep the IV line patent.","zh":"断开输血皮条，并通过新输液皮条输入生理盐水以保持静脉通路通畅。"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor vital signs and collect blood and urine samples as protocol requires.","zh":"监测生命体征并按规程要求收集血液和尿液样本。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the healthcare provider and the blood bank.","zh":"通知医疗服务提供者和血库。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the blood transfusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止输血。"},{"id":"E","en":"Return the blood bag and tubing to the blood bank for analysis.","zh":"将血袋和输液管送回血库进行分析。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At the first sign of a transfusion reaction, the nurse must immediately stop the infusion. Next, disconnect the blood line and start normal saline with new tubing to avoid infusing remaining blood in the line. Notify the provider/blood bank, check vitals, obtain specimens (checking for hemolysis), and return the materials for lab review.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在出现输血反应的第一个征兆时，护士必须立即停止输注。接下来，断开输血管并使用新的输液管启动生理盐水，以避免输入管路中残留的血液。通知医生/血库，检查生命体征，获取标本（检查溶血情况），并将材料送回实验室进行审查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Priority actions: stop the trigger first, establish safe alternative IV flow, and then notify. Never flush the blood already in the tubing into the patient.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先行动：首先停止诱发源，建立替代的安全静脉流速，然后通知。切勿将已经存在于管路中的血液冲洗进患者体内。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":927,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.736","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.736.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.736.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an oral medication to a client. Sequence the steps of medication safety checks from first to last to prevent medication errors.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为患者口服给药。按先后顺序排列药物安全检查步骤，以防止用药错误。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the steps of medication safety checks from first to last to prevent medication errors.","terminalSentenceZh":"按先后顺序排列药物安全检查步骤，以防止用药错误。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an oral medication to a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为患者口服给药。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Confirm the client's identity using two identifiers (name and date of birth) at the bedside.","zh":"在床边使用两个标识符（姓名和出生日期）核对患者的身份。"},{"id":"A","en":"Compare the medication label with the Medication Administration Record (MAR) when retrieving the drug.","zh":"取药时将药物标签与给药记录单 (MAR) 进行比对。"},{"id":"B","en":"Compare the medication label with the MAR while preparing the drug dose.","zh":"准备药量时将药物标签与 MAR 进行比对。"},{"id":"D","en":"Compare the medication label with the MAR at the client's bedside before administration.","zh":"给药前在患者床边将药物标签与 MAR 进行比对。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Medication administration safety requires three checks: 1. Upon retrieval from storage, 2. During preparation of the dose, 3. At the bedside. Bedside identity verification occurs immediately prior to this final check and ingestion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"药物给药安全需要进行三次核对：1. 从储藏处取药时，2. 在准备药量时，3. 在床边。在床边核对身份发生在最后一次比对和服药前。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the chronological sequence of drug handling: retrieval, preparation, bedside entry, identification, and final comparison.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识处理药物的时间顺序：取药、准备、进入床边、核对身份和最后比对。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":928,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.737","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.737.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.737.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client receiving Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) via a central venous catheter. Classify each of the following nursing actions as Appropriate or Inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名通过中心静脉导管接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN) 的患者。将以下每项护理行为分类为“合适”或“不合适”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following nursing actions as Appropriate or Inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每项护理行为分类为“合适”或“不合适”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is caring for a client receiving Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) via a central venous catheter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名通过中心静脉导管接受全胃肠外营养 (TPN) 的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Infusing 10% dextrose in water if the TPN bag runs out before the next bag is ready.","zh":"如果 TPN 袋在下一袋准备好之前输完，则输入 10% 葡萄糖水溶液。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Using the TPN line to administer an IV piggyback antibiotic.","zh":"使用 TPN 输液管路输注 IV 间歇性抗生素。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Checking the client's blood glucose level every 6 hours.","zh":"每 6 小时检查一次患者的血糖水平。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Abruptly stopping the TPN infusion to facilitate client ambulation.","zh":"突然停止 TPN 输注以方便患者下床活动。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"TPN contains high glucose concentrations. If discontinued suddenly, it can cause severe hypoglycemia; infusing 10% dextrose in water (D10W) maintains blood glucose levels if a bag runs out. The TPN line is dedicated and must never be used for other infusions due to infection/incompatibility risks. Blood glucose must be checked regularly (usually every 6 hours) due to hyperglycemia risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"TPN 含有高浓度的葡萄糖。如果突然停止，可能引起严重低血糖；如果一袋输完，输入 10% 葡萄糖水溶液 (D10W) 可以维持血糖水平。TPN 管路是专用的，由于感染/配伍禁忌风险，绝不能用于其他输液。由于高血糖风险，必须定期（通常每 6 小时）检查一次血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall key TPN rules: dedicated line (no mixing) and prevent rebound hypoglycemia by never stopping abruptly without replacement dextrose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想 TPN 关键规则：专用管路（不得混合），且在没有替代葡萄糖的情况下切勿突然停止，以防止反弹低血糖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":929,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.738","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.738.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.738.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an intravenous piggyback (IVPB) medication. Classify each of the following nursing actions as Appropriate or Inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"护士正在准备输注静脉滴注（IVPB）药物。将以下每项护理行为分类为“合适”或“不合适”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following nursing actions as Appropriate or Inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下每项护理行为分类为“合适”或“不合适”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer an intravenous piggyback (IVPB) medication.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在准备输注静脉滴注（IVPB）药物。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Hanging the piggyback medication bag higher than the primary infusion bag.","zh":"将 IVPB 药袋挂得比主输液袋更高。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Connecting the IVPB tubing to the lower-most Y-port of the primary line, below the infusion pump.","zh":"将 IVPB 输液管连接到主输液管路最下方的 Y 型接头（在输液泵下方）。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Verifying compatibility of the IVPB drug with the primary running IV fluid.","zh":"核实 IVPB 药物与正在输注的主路静脉液体的配伍禁忌。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Flushing the secondary line with saline before hanging a medication that is incompatible with the prior secondary med.","zh":"在挂入与之前辅助管路药物不配伍的药物之前，先用生理盐水冲洗辅助管路。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For gravity or pump piggyback infusions, the secondary bag must be hung higher than the primary bag so hydrostatic pressure drives the secondary fluid first. Piggyback lines should connect to the upper Y-port (above the pump) so the pump regulates its rate. Compatibility checking is mandatory. Flushing the line clears residues of incompatible prior drugs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于重力或泵控制的间歇输液，辅助袋必须挂得比主袋高，以便静脉压先驱动辅助液体。辅助管路应连接到上方的 Y 型接头（在泵上方），以便泵调节其流速。配伍禁忌检查是强制性的。冲洗管路可清除之前不配伍药物的残留。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify mechanical principles of IV setups. Connecting below the pump bypasses the pump's safety and rate controls for secondary meds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别静脉装置的机械原理。在泵下方连接会绕过泵对辅助药物的安全和流速控制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":930,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.739","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.739.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.739.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,66],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer a mixed dose of insulin containing Regular insulin and NPH insulin. Classify each of the following actions during preparation as Correct or Incorrect.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备注射混合剂量的胰岛素，包含 Regular 胰岛素和 NPH 胰岛素。将以下制备过程中的每项行为分类为“正确”或“错误”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each of the following actions during preparation as Correct or Incorrect.","terminalSentenceZh":"将以下制备过程中的每项行为分类为“正确”或“错误”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing to administer a mixed dose of insulin containing Regular insulin and NPH insulin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备注射混合剂量的胰岛素，包含 Regular 胰岛素和 NPH 胰岛素。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Injecting air into the NPH vial first, without touching the solution.","zh":"首先向 NPH 药瓶中注入空气，且不接触药液。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Injecting air into the Regular vial and immediately drawing up Regular insulin.","zh":"向 Regular 药瓶中注入空气，并立即吸出 Regular 胰岛素。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Drawing up the NPH insulin first, followed by the Regular insulin in the same syringe.","zh":"先吸取 NPH 胰岛素，接着在同一注射器中吸取 Regular 胰岛素。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Inserting the needle back into the NPH vial after drawing Regular insulin to draw NPH.","zh":"在吸取 Regular 胰岛素后，将针头插回 NPH 药瓶中以吸取 NPH。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Incorrect","zh":"错误"},{"id":"c1","en":"Correct","zh":"正确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When mixing insulin in a single syringe, the correct sequence prevents contamination of rapid-acting insulin with intermediate-acting NPH: 1. Inject air into NPH (cloudy), 2. Inject air into Regular (clear), 3. Draw up Regular, 4. Draw up NPH. (Clear before Cloudy). Drawing NPH first is incorrect.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在同一注射器中混合胰岛素时，正确的顺序可防止速效胰岛素受到中效 NPH 的污染：1. 向 NPH（浑浊）中注入空气，2. 向 Regular（澄清）中注入空气，3. 吸取 Regular，4. 吸取 NPH。（先清后浊）。先吸取 NPH 是错误的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the clinical shortcut: 'RN' (Regular then NPH) for drawing up insulin. Clear (Regular) is drawn before Cloudy (NPH) to preserve vial purity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住吸取胰岛素的临床口诀：先“R”后“N”（Regular 澄清，然后 NPH 浑浊）。澄清药液 (Regular) 必须在浑浊药液 (NPH) 之前吸取，以保持药瓶纯度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":931,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.740","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.740.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.740.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,265],"terminalOffsetsZh":[71,99],"fullStemEn":"A physician orders 2 mg of IV morphine sulfate. The medication is available in a prefilled syringe containing 4 mg/mL. The nurse should administer 0.5 mL and waste the remaining 0.5 mL. The nurse must perform the wasting of the narcotic {{1}} and ensure that {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"医生开医嘱静脉注射 2 毫克硫酸吗啡。该药物在含有 4 毫克/毫升的预充式注射器中提供。护士应注射 0.5 毫升，并废弃剩余的 0.5 毫升。护士必须 {{1}} 废弃该麻醉药，并确保 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must perform the wasting of the narcotic {{1}} and ensure that {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须 {{1}} 废弃该麻醉药，并确保 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should administer 0.5 mL and waste the remaining 0.5 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应注射 0.5 毫升，并废弃剩余的 0.5 毫升。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse must perform the wasting of the narcotic {{1}} and ensure that {{2}}.","zh":"护士必须 {{1}} 废弃该麻醉药，并确保 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"in the presence of another licensed nurse witness","zh":"在另一名有执照的护士见证下"},{"id":"o2","en":"alone and document it in the chart","zh":"独自一人进行并在病历中记录"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the wasted amount is returned to the pharmacy","zh":"废弃的药量退回到药房"},{"id":"o1","en":"both nurses sign the narcotic disposal log","zh":"两位护士都在麻醉药处理日志上签字"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Disposal (wasting) of controlled substances requires validation by two licensed nurses to prevent diversion. The witness must physically observe the disposal, and both nurses must co-sign the disposal/waste record immediately.","rationaleCorrectZh":"受控物质的处置（废弃）需要两名有执照的护士进行验证以防止挪用。见证人必须亲眼观察处置过程，且两位护士必须立即共同签署处置/废弃记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that safety rules for narcotics always require a double-check loop (two licensed individuals) for disposal and key verification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住麻醉药的安全规则在处置和关键核对时总是需要双人核对闭环（两个有执照的个人）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":true,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":true,"clozeStemContainedInStem":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":true},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":932,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.741","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.741.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.741.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,73],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving a continuous intravenous heparin infusion for a deep vein thrombosis. The nurse should monitor the client's {{1}} to assess therapeutic effectiveness and adjust the infusion rate, while keeping {{2}} available as the antidote.","fullStemZh":"一名深静脉血栓患者正在接受持续静脉注射肝素输注。护士应监测患者的 {{1}} 以评估治疗效果并调整输注速度，同时保持 {{2}} 作为解毒剂备用。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should monitor the client's {{1}} to assess therapeutic effectiveness and adjust the infusion rate, while keeping {{2}} available as the antidote.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应监测患者的 {{1}} 以评估治疗效果并调整输注速度，同时保持 {{2}} 作为解毒剂备用。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving a continuous intravenous heparin infusion for a deep vein thrombosis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名深静脉血栓患者正在接受持续静脉注射肝素输注。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should monitor the client's {{1}} and keep {{2}} available as the antidote.","zh":"护士应监测患者的 {{1}}，并保持 {{2}} 作为解毒剂备用。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"prothrombin time (PT) and International Normalized Ratio (INR)","zh":"凝血酶原时间 (PT) 和国际标准化比值 (INR)"},{"id":"o1","en":"activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT)","zh":"活化部分凝血活酶时间 (aPTT)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"protamine sulfate","zh":"硫酸鱼精蛋白"},{"id":"o2","en":"phytonadione (vitamin K)","zh":"植物甲萘醌 (维生素 K)"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Continuous IV heparin therapy is monitored using the aPTT lab value, with a therapeutic range typically 1.5 to 2.5 times the control value. The specific reversal agent (antidote) for heparin is protamine sulfate. PT/INR and Vitamin K are associated with warfarin therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"持续静脉注射肝素治疗通过 aPTT 实验室检查值进行监测，治疗范围通常是对照值的 1.5 至 2.5 倍。肝素的特异性拮抗剂（解毒剂）是硫酸鱼精蛋白。PT/INR 和维生素 K 与华法林治疗有关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate: Heparin -> aPTT -> Protamine Sulfate. Warfarin -> PT/INR -> Vitamin K. Do not mix these pairs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"联想记忆：肝素 -> aPTT -> 鱼精蛋白。华法林 -> PT/INR -> 维生素 K。不要混淆这两对。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":933,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.742","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.742.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.742.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,75],"fullStemEn":"A client is prescribed a drug with a half-life of 6 hours. The client takes a single dose of 400 mg. After 24 hours, the nurse should expect that {{1}} of the drug remains in the client's body, which corresponds to {{2}}.","fullStemZh":"患者被开具了半衰期为 6 小时的药物。患者服用单次剂量 400 毫克。24 小时后，护士应预期患者体内残留该药物的 {{1}}，这对应于 {{2}}。","terminalSentenceEn":"After 24 hours, the nurse should expect that {{1}} of the drug remains in the client's body, which corresponds to {{2}}.","terminalSentenceZh":"24 小时后，护士应预期患者体内残留该药物的 {{1}}，这对应于 {{2}}。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client takes a single dose of 400 mg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者服用单次剂量 400 毫克。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should expect that {{1}} of the drug remains in the client's body, which corresponds to {{2}}.","zh":"护士应预期患者体内残留该药物的 {{1}}，这对应于 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"6.25% (4 half-lives)","zh":"6.25% (4 个半衰期)"},{"id":"o2","en":"12.5% (3 half-lives)","zh":"12.5% (3 个半衰期)"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"50 mg","zh":"50 毫克"},{"id":"o1","en":"25 mg","zh":"25 毫克"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: 24 hours divided by the 6-hour half-life equals 4 half-lives. 400 mg decreases as follows: 1st half-life (6h) = 200 mg (50%); 2nd half-life (12h) = 100 mg (25%); 3rd half-life (18h) = 50 mg (12.5%); 4th half-life (24h) = 25 mg (6.25%).","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算过程：24 小时除以 6 小时半衰期等于 4 个半衰期。400 毫克递减过程如下：第1个半衰期 (6h) = 200 毫克 (50%)；第2个半衰期 (12h) = 100 毫克 (25%)；第3个半衰期 (18h) = 50 毫克 (12.5%)；第4个半衰期 (24h) = 25 毫克 (6.25%)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Determine the number of half-lives first by dividing total elapsed time by the drug's half-life. Then divide the starting dose in half for each half-life interval.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先通过将总流逝时间除以药物的半衰期来确定半衰期的个数。然后将每个半衰期间隔的起始剂量减半。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":934,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.743","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.743.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.743.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[171,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[82,92],"fullStemEn":"Order: Liquid acetaminophen 650 mg orally every 6 hours as needed for pain. Available: Acetaminophen suspension 160 mg/5 mL. The nurse should administer ____ mL per dose. (Round answer to one decimal place).","fullStemZh":"医嘱：口服对乙酰氨基酚混悬液 650 毫克，每 6 小时一次，根据疼痛需要。提供：对乙酰氨基酚混悬液 160 毫克/5 毫升。护士每次给药应给予 ____ 毫升。（结果保留一位小数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round answer to one decimal place).","terminalSentenceZh":"结果保留一位小数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should administer ____ mL per dose.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士每次给药应给予 ____ 毫升。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["20.3","20.3 mL","20.3ml"],"numeric":{"value":20.3,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation using Desired over Have formula: (650 mg / 160 mg) * 5 mL = 4.0625 * 5 = 20.3125 mL. Rounding to one decimal place yields 20.3 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用常用计算公式：(650 毫克 / 160 毫克) * 5 毫升 = 4.0625 * 5 = 20.3125 毫升。四舍五入保留一位小数为 20.3 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always pay close attention to rounding instructions in NCLEX math items. Here, rounding to one decimal place is required (tenths place).","testTakingStrategyZh":"在 NCLEX 数学题中务必密切注意四舍五入的指示。这里要求保留一位小数（十分位）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":935,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.744","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.744.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.744.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[78,91],"fullStemEn":"Order: Infuse 1,000 mL of 0.9% normal saline IV over 8 hours. The tubing drop factor is 15 gtt/mL. The nurse should set the manual IV flow rate to ____ gtt/min. (Round to the nearest whole number).","fullStemZh":"医嘱：在 8 小时内静脉输入 1,000 毫升 0.9% 生理盐水。输液皮条滴系数为 15 滴/毫升。护士应将手动静脉输液流速设置为每分钟 ____ 滴。（四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","terminalSentenceEn":"(Round to the nearest whole number).","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should set the manual IV flow rate to ____ gtt/min.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将手动静脉输液流速设置为每分钟 ____ 滴。（","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"gtt/min","zh":"滴/分钟"},"acceptable":["31","31 gtt/min","31滴/分"],"numeric":{"value":31,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Formula: (Total Volume in mL * Drop Factor in gtt/mL) / Total Time in minutes. (1000 mL * 15 gtt/mL) / (8 hours * 60 minutes/hour) = 15000 / 480 = 31.25 gtt/min. Rounding to the nearest whole number yields 31 gtt/min.","rationaleCorrectZh":"公式：（总容积毫升数 * 滴系数滴/毫升）/ 总时间分钟数。(1000 毫升 * 15 滴/毫升) / (8 小时 * 60 分钟/小时) = 15000 / 480 = 31.25 滴/分钟。四舍五入到最接近的整数为 31 滴/分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert hours to minutes in the denominator (8 * 60 = 480) before performing the final division. Round .25 down to the nearest whole drop.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在进行最终除法之前，先将分母中的小时转换为分钟 (8 * 60 = 480)。将 .25 舍入到最接近的整数滴。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":936,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.745","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.745.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.745.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[207,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,93],"fullStemEn":"A pediatric client weighing 33 lbs is prescribed amoxicillin 15 mg/kg/dose orally every 12 hours. Amoxicillin is available as a 250 mg/5 mL oral suspension. How many mL should the nurse administer per dose? ____ mL.","fullStemZh":"一名体重 33 磅的儿科患者被开具了阿莫西林口服，每次 15 毫克/公斤，每 12 小时一次。阿莫西林为 250 毫克/5 毫升口服混悬液。护士每次给药应给予多少毫升？ ____ 毫升。","terminalSentenceEn":"____ mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"____ 毫升。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer per dose?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士每次给药应给予多少毫升？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["4.5","4.5 mL","4.5ml"],"numeric":{"value":4.5,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: 1. Convert weight to kg: 33 lbs / 2.2 = 15 kg. 2. Calculate dose in mg: 15 kg * 15 mg/kg = 225 mg. 3. Calculate volume in mL: (225 mg / 250 mg) * 5 mL = 4.5 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算步骤：1. 将体重换算为公斤：33 磅 / 2.2 = 15 公斤。2. 计算以毫克为单位的剂量：15 公斤 * 15 毫克/公斤 = 225 毫克。3. 计算以毫升为单位的体积：(225 毫克 / 250 毫克) * 5 毫升 = 4.5 毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always perform the weight conversion first: lbs divided by 2.2. Keep track of intermediary calculations before calculating the liquid volume.","testTakingStrategyZh":"务必首先进行体重换算：磅数除以 2.2。在计算液体体积之前，记清中间计算步骤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":937,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gap_50_ppt_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.746","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.746.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.746.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,239],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,91],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving an intravenous heparin infusion at a rate of 24 mL/hr. The heparin concentration is 25,000 units in 250 mL of 5% dextrose in water. The nurse should calculate that the heparin dose being administered is ____ units/hr.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正以 24 毫升/小时的速度接受静脉输注肝素。肝素浓度为 25,000 单位溶于 250 毫升 5% 葡萄糖水溶液中。护士应计算出正在给予的肝素剂量为 ____ 单位/小时。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should calculate that the heparin dose being administered is ____ units/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应计算出正在给予的肝素剂量为 ____ 单位/小时。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The heparin concentration is 25,000 units in 250 mL of 5% dextrose in water.","penultimateSentenceZh":"肝素浓度为 25,000 单位溶于 250 毫升 5% 葡萄糖水溶液中。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"units/hr","zh":"单位/小时"},"acceptable":["2400","2,400","2400 units/hr","2400单位/小时"],"numeric":{"value":2400,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: 1. Determine concentration per mL: 25,000 units / 250 mL = 100 units/mL. 2. Calculate hourly dose: 24 mL/hour * 100 units/mL = 2,400 units/hour.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算步骤：1. 确定每毫升的浓度：25,000 单位 / 250 毫升 = 100 单位/毫升。2. 计算每小时剂量：24 毫升/小时 * 100 单位/毫升 = 2,400 单位/小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Break weight or unit calculations into concentration ratios first: find units/mL, then multiply by the hourly rate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先将重量或单位计算分解为浓度比：找出单位/毫升，然后乘以每小时流速。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":938,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_fib_gcs_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.747","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.747.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.747.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[212,251],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,81],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is assessing a client's neurological status using the Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS). The client opens their eyes in response to speech, is confused but able to converse, and localizes to a painful stimulus. Calculate the client's total GCS score.","fullStemZh":"护士正在使用格拉斯哥昏迷量表（GCS）评估患者的神经系统状态。患者在听到呼唤时睁眼，虽然意识模糊但能进行交谈，并且对疼痛刺激有定位反应。请计算该患者的GCS总分。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's total GCS score.","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算该患者的GCS总分。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client opens their eyes in response to speech, is confused but able to converse, and localizes to a painful stimulus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者在听到呼唤时睁眼，虽然意识模糊但能进行交谈，并且对疼痛刺激有定位反应。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Total GCS Score","zh":"GCS总分"},"acceptable":["12"],"numeric":{"value":12,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Glasgow Coma Scale evaluates three parameters: eye opening, verbal response, and motor response. Opening eyes to speech scores 3 points. Confused conversation scores 4 points. Localizing to pain scores 5 points. Total score = 3 + 4 + 5 = 12.","rationaleCorrectZh":"格拉斯哥昏迷量表评估三个参数：睁眼反应、言语反应和运动反应。对呼唤睁眼得3分。言语模糊、能交谈得4分。对疼痛有定位反应得5分。总分 = 3 + 4 + 5 = 12分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the individual scoring criteria for the GCS: Eye (4 points max), Verbal (5 points max), and Motor (6 points max). Add them carefully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"牢记GCS各项评分标准：睁眼（最高4分）、言语（最高5分）和运动（最高6分）。仔细将它们相加。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":939,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_fib_enteral_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.748","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.748.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.748.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,61],"fullStemEn":"A provider prescribes 250 mL of enteral nutrition formula to be infused via a gastrostomy tube over 30 minutes. The nurse should set the enteral feeding pump to deliver how many mL/hr?","fullStemZh":"医生开具医嘱，要求在30分钟内通过胃造瘘管输注250 mL肠内营养液。护士应将肠内营养输注泵的流速设置为多少 mL/hr？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should set the enteral feeding pump to deliver how many mL/hr?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将肠内营养输注泵的流速设置为多少 mL/hr？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider prescribes 250 mL of enteral nutrition formula to be infused via a gastrostomy tube over 30 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医生开具医嘱，要求在30分钟内通过胃造瘘管输注250 mL肠内营养液。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时 (mL/hr)"},"acceptable":["500","500 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To calculate the hourly rate, divide the total volume by the time in hours. The volume is 250 mL. The time is 30 minutes, which is 0.5 hours. 250 mL / 0.5 hr = 500 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"要计算每小时的流速，用总体积除以以小时为单位的时间。体积为250 mL。时间为30分钟，即0.5小时。250 mL / 0.5 hr = 500 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Ensure time is converted to hours before calculating mL/hr. Divide minutes by 60 to get the fraction of an hour.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在计算 mL/hr 之前，确保将时间转换为小时。将分钟数除以60即可得到小时的分数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":940,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_fib_anc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.749","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.749.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.749.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,271],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,107],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing laboratory results for a client with a severe respiratory infection. The white blood cell (WBC) count is 4 ×10³/µL. The differential shows 50% segmented neutrophils and 10% banded neutrophils. Calculate the client's Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC).","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看一名患有严重呼吸道感染患者的实验室检查结果。白细胞（WBC）计数为 4 ×10³/µL。白细胞分类计数显示分叶核中性粒细胞占50%，杆状核中性粒细胞占10%。请计算该患者的绝对中性粒细胞计数（ANC）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC).","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算该患者的绝对中性粒细胞计数（ANC）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The differential shows 50% segmented neutrophils and 10% banded neutrophils.","penultimateSentenceZh":"白细胞分类计数显示分叶核中性粒细胞占50%，杆状核中性粒细胞占10%。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"ANC (/mm³)","zh":"ANC (/mm³)"},"acceptable":["2400"],"numeric":{"value":2400,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC) is calculated by multiplying the total WBC count by the percentage of total neutrophils (segmented neutrophils + banded neutrophils). Neutrophil percentage = 50% + 10% = 60% (or 0.60). ANC = 4,000 × 0.60 = 2,400/mm³.","rationaleCorrectZh":"绝对中性粒细胞计数（ANC）的计算方法是将总WBC计数乘以总中性粒细胞的百分比（分叶核中性粒细胞 + 杆状核中性粒细胞）。中性粒细胞百分比 = 50% + 10% = 60%（或0.60）。ANC = 4,000 × 0.60 = 2,400/mm³。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the formula for ANC: Total WBC × (% Segs + % Bands). Always convert the percentage to a decimal before multiplying.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住ANC的公式：总WBC ×（分叶核百分比 + 杆状核百分比）。相乘之前，务必将百分比转换为小数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":941,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_fib_tbsa_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.750","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.750.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.750.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,243],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,68],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is admitted to the emergency department with partial-thickness burns. The burns cover the entire anterior trunk and the entire right arm. Using the Rule of Nines, calculate the estimated total body surface area (TBSA) affected.","fullStemZh":"一名成年患者因部分皮层烧伤/二度烧伤被送入急诊科。烧伤面积覆盖整个躯干前部和整个右臂。请使用九分法计算受累的总体表面积（TBSA）估值。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Rule of Nines, calculate the estimated total body surface area (TBSA) affected.","terminalSentenceZh":"请使用九分法计算受累的总体表面积（TBSA）估值。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The burns cover the entire anterior trunk and the entire right arm.","penultimateSentenceZh":"烧伤面积覆盖整个躯干前部和整个右臂。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"% TBSA","zh":"% TBSA"},"acceptable":["27","27%"],"numeric":{"value":27,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to the Rule of Nines for an adult: the anterior trunk is 18%, and the entire right arm (front and back) is 9%. Total estimated TBSA = 18% + 9% = 27%.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据成人九分法：躯干前部占18%，整个右臂（前后）占9%。估计的TBSA总值 = 18% + 9% = 27%。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the Rule of Nines: Head=9%, Arms=9% each, Legs=18% each, Anterior trunk=18%, Posterior trunk=18%, Groin=1%.","testTakingStrategyZh":"熟记九分法：头部=9%，双臂各9%，双腿各18%，躯干前部=18%，躯干后部=18%，腹股沟=1%。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":942,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_fib_bmi_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.751","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.751.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.751.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,54],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is conducting a health screening for an adult client. The client weighs 72 kilograms and is 1.5 meters tall. Calculate the client's Body Mass Index (BMI).","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名成年患者进行健康筛查。该患者体重72公斤，身高1.5米。请计算该患者的身体质量指数（BMI）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's Body Mass Index (BMI).","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算该患者的身体质量指数（BMI）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client weighs 72 kilograms and is 1.5 meters tall.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者体重72公斤，身高1.5米。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"BMI","zh":"BMI"},"acceptable":["32"],"numeric":{"value":32,"tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"BMI is calculated by dividing weight in kilograms by the square of height in meters. Calculation: Height squared = 1.5 × 1.5 = 2.25. BMI = 72 / 2.25 = 32.","rationaleCorrectZh":"BMI 的计算方法是用体重（公斤）除以身高（米）的平方。计算：身高的平方 = 1.5 × 1.5 = 2.25。BMI = 72 / 2.25 = 32。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The BMI formula is weight (kg) / [height (m)]². Make sure to square the height before dividing the weight.","testTakingStrategyZh":"BMI公式为 体重(kg) / [身高(m)]²。在除以体重之前，务必先将身高进行平方计算。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":943,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_fib_iando_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.752","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.752.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.752.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,64],"fullStemEn":"A client on a clear liquid diet consumes 4 oz of apple juice, 8 oz of black coffee, and 6 oz of chicken broth during the shift. Calculate the client's total oral fluid intake in milliliters (mL).","fullStemZh":"一名进食清流质饮食的患者在值班期间饮用了4盎司苹果汁、8盎司黑咖啡和6盎司鸡汤。请计算该患者的经口液体总摄入量（以毫升为单位）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's total oral fluid intake in milliliters (mL).","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算该患者的经口液体总摄入量（以毫升为单位）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client on a clear liquid diet consumes 4 oz of apple juice, 8 oz of black coffee, and 6 oz of chicken broth during the shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名进食清流质饮食的患者在值班期间饮用了4盎司苹果汁、8盎司黑咖啡和6盎司鸡汤。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Total intake (mL)","zh":"总摄入量 (毫升/mL)"},"acceptable":["540","540 mL"],"numeric":{"value":540,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"To calculate total intake in milliliters, first convert ounces (oz) to milliliters (mL). One fluid ounce is equal to 30 mL. Total ounces = 4 + 8 + 6 = 18 oz. Total mL = 18 oz × 30 mL/oz = 540 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"要计算以毫升为单位的总摄入量，首先将盎司（oz）转换为毫升（mL）。1液量盎司等于30毫升。总盎司数 = 4 + 8 + 6 = 18 oz。总毫升数 = 18 oz × 30 mL/oz = 540 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the conversion factor: 1 oz = 30 mL. Add all the ounces together before multiplying by 30 to save time and reduce calculation errors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住换算系数：1 oz = 30 mL。为了节省时间并减少计算错误，请先将所有盎司数相加，然后再乘以30。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":944,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_or_ngmeds_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.753","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.753.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.753.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,48],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer crushed medications via a nasogastric (NG) tube to a client receiving continuous enteral feedings. Order the steps of the procedure.","fullStemZh":"护士准备通过鼻胃管（NG管）为正在接受持续肠内营养的患者管饲研碎的药物。请对该操作步骤进行排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Order the steps of the procedure.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对该操作步骤进行排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer crushed medications via a nasogastric (NG) tube to a client receiving continuous enteral feedings.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备通过鼻胃管（NG管）为正在接受持续肠内营养的患者管饲研碎的药物。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer the diluted crushed medication.","zh":"注入稀释后的研碎药物。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the continuous enteral feeding.","zh":"停止持续肠内营养输注。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify correct tube placement and check gastric residual volume if indicated by facility policy.","zh":"确认胃管位置正确，并根据机构政策指示检查胃内残留量。"},{"id":"E","en":"Flush the tube again with 15 to 30 mL of sterile water.","zh":"再次用15至30毫升无菌水冲洗胃管。"},{"id":"C","en":"Flush the tube with 15 to 30 mL of sterile water.","zh":"用15至30毫升无菌水冲洗胃管。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When administering medications via an NG tube during continuous feeds: 1. Stop the feed to prevent mixing incompatible drugs with the formula. 2. Verify tube placement and residual to ensure safety. 3. Flush the tube with water to clear formula. 4. Administer the medication. 5. Flush the tube again to ensure the drug reaches the stomach and the tube remains patent.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在持续管饲期间通过鼻胃管给药时：1. 停止管饲以防药物与配方奶混合产生不相容。2. 确认导管位置和残留量以确保安全。3. 用水冲管以清除营养液。4. 注入药物。5. 再次冲管以确保药物到达胃部并保持导管通畅。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Visualize the procedure: Stop feed -> Check safety (placement/residual) -> Flush -> Med -> Flush. Never mix medications directly into the enteral feeding formula.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在脑海中模拟操作过程：停止管饲 -> 检查安全性（位置/残留量） -> 冲洗 -> 给药 -> 冲洗。切勿将药物直接混入肠内营养液中。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":945,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_or_paracentesis_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.754","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.754.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.754.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,43],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with ascites who is scheduled for a bedside paracentesis. In what order should the nurse perform the following actions?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名患有腹水并计划在床旁进行腹腔穿刺的患者。护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse perform the following actions?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with ascites who is scheduled for a bedside paracentesis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在护理一名患有腹水并计划在床旁进行腹腔穿刺的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Position the client sitting upright on the edge of the bed.","zh":"协助患者在床沿端坐。"},{"id":"A","en":"Instruct the client to empty the bladder.","zh":"指导患者排空膀胱。"},{"id":"E","en":"Apply a sterile dressing and monitor the puncture site for leakage.","zh":"贴上无菌敷料并监测穿刺部位有无渗液。"},{"id":"B","en":"Measure the client's baseline vital signs and weight.","zh":"测量患者的基础生命体征和体重。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assist the healthcare provider during the fluid drainage.","zh":"在引流积液过程中协助医疗服务提供者。"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For a paracentesis: 1. Obtain baseline vitals/weight. 2. Have the client empty their bladder (critical safety step). 3. Position the client upright. 4. Assist the provider during the procedure. 5. Apply a dressing and monitor post-procedure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"进行腹腔穿刺时：1. 获取基础生命体征/体重。2. 让患者排空膀胱（关键安全步骤）。3. 协助患者端坐。4. 在操作期间协助医疗服务提供者。5. 穿刺后贴上敷料并进行监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think chronologically: Assessment (baseline) -> Pre-op safety (empty bladder) -> Positioning -> Intra-op assist -> Post-op care (dressing).","testTakingStrategyZh":"按时间顺序思考：评估（基线数据） -> 术前安全（排空膀胱） -> 体位摆放 -> 术中协助 -> 术后护理（敷料）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":946,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_or_fire_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.755","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.755.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.755.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse responds to a small trash can fire in the client dayroom and retrieves a fire extinguisher. Sequence the steps for using the fire extinguisher according to the PASS mnemonic.","fullStemZh":"护士发现患者活动室的垃圾桶发生小火灾，并拿来灭火器。请根据“PASS”口诀对使用灭火器的步骤进行排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Sequence the steps for using the fire extinguisher according to the PASS mnemonic.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据“PASS”口诀对使用灭火器的步骤进行排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse responds to a small trash can fire in the client dayroom and retrieves a fire extinguisher.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现患者活动室的垃圾桶发生小火灾，并拿来灭火器。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Pull the pin on the extinguisher.","zh":"拔出灭火器的保险销。"},{"id":"D","en":"Sweep the nozzle from side to side.","zh":"左右扫射喷嘴。"},{"id":"C","en":"Squeeze the handle to release the extinguishing agent.","zh":"握紧压把以释放灭火剂。"},{"id":"B","en":"Aim the nozzle at the base of the fire.","zh":"将喷嘴对准火源根部。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The PASS mnemonic for fire extinguisher use stands for: P - Pull the pin. A - Aim at the base of the fire. S - Squeeze the handle. S - Sweep from side to side.","rationaleCorrectZh":"灭火器使用的 PASS 口诀代表：P - 拔出保险销 (Pull)。A - 瞄准火源根部 (Aim)。S - 握紧把手 (Squeeze)。S - 左右扫射 (Sweep)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"PASS is an acronym where each letter directly corresponds to the order of operations. P=Pull, A=Aim, S=Squeeze, S=Sweep.","testTakingStrategyZh":"PASS 是一个首字母缩略词，每个字母直接对应操作顺序。P=拔出，A=瞄准，S=握紧，S=扫射。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse responds to a small trash can fire in the client dayroom and retrieves a fire extinguisher.","controlSentenceZh":"护士发现患者活动室的垃圾桶发生小火灾，并拿来灭火器。"}
{"queueIndex":947,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_or_abdo_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.756","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.756.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.756.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,39],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is performing a routine screening physical examination of an adult client's abdomen. In what order should the nurse perform the assessment techniques?","fullStemZh":"护士正在对一名成年患者进行常规腹部体格筛查。护士应按什么顺序执行这些评估技术？","terminalSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse perform the assessment techniques?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行这些评估技术？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is performing a routine screening physical examination of an adult client's abdomen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在对一名成年患者进行常规腹部体格筛查。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Auscultate for bowel sounds in all four quadrants.","zh":"听诊四个象限的肠鸣音。"},{"id":"C","en":"Percuss the abdomen to assess for tympany and dullness.","zh":"叩诊腹部以评估鼓音和浊音。"},{"id":"D","en":"Palpate the abdomen lightly to detect tenderness.","zh":"轻触诊腹部以检查有无压痛。"},{"id":"A","en":"Inspect the abdominal contour and skin integrity.","zh":"视诊腹部轮廓和皮肤完整性。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For an abdominal assessment, the correct sequence is Inspection, Auscultation, Percussion, and Palpation. Auscultation is performed before percussion and palpation because manipulating the abdomen can alter bowel sounds and cause false findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于腹部评估，正确的顺序是视诊、听诊、叩诊和触诊。在叩诊和触诊之前进行听诊是因为操作腹部可能会改变肠鸣音，从而导致虚假的发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Normal assessment order is Inspect, Palpate, Percuss, Auscultate (IPPA). However, the abdomen is the major exception: Inspect, Auscultate, Percuss, Palpate (IAPP) to avoid altering bowel sounds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"通常的评估顺序是视、触、叩、听（IPPA）。然而，腹部是主要的例外：视、听、叩、触（IAPP），以避免改变肠鸣音。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":948,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_u5_fib_or_2026_06_09_or_trach_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.757","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.757.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.757.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,41],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to perform open endotracheal suctioning for a client with a new tracheostomy. Order the steps of the procedure.","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名新行气管切开术的患者进行开放式气管内吸痰。请对该操作步骤进行排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Order the steps of the procedure.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对该操作步骤进行排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to perform open endotracheal suctioning for a client with a new tracheostomy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备为一名新行气管切开术的患者进行开放式气管内吸痰。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Apply intermittent suction while rotating and withdrawing the catheter.","zh":"在旋转并拔出吸痰管的同时施加间歇性负压。"},{"id":"B","en":"Insert the suction catheter without applying negative pressure.","zh":"插入吸痰管，插入时不要施加负压。"},{"id":"D","en":"Reassess the client's respiratory status and oxygen saturation.","zh":"重新评估患者的呼吸状态和血氧饱和度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Pre-oxygenate the client with 100% oxygen.","zh":"用100%浓度的氧气为患者进行预充氧。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the amount, color, and consistency of the secretions.","zh":"记录分泌物的量、颜色和性状。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct suctioning sequence is: 1. Pre-oxygenate (hyperoxygenate) to prevent hypoxia. 2. Insert catheter without suction to prevent mucosal trauma. 3. Apply suction intermittently while withdrawing to clear secretions safely. 4. Assess tolerance and oxygenation. 5. Document findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的吸痰顺序是：1. 预充氧（过度给氧）以防止缺氧。2. 在无负压状态下插入吸痰管，防止黏膜损伤。3. 边退管边旋转间歇吸引，安全清除分泌物。4. 评估患者的耐受性和氧合情况。5. 记录观察结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always pre-oxygenate before suctioning to prevent hypoxia. Never apply suction going in; only apply suction while coming out.","testTakingStrategyZh":"吸痰前务必进行预充氧以防缺氧。插入吸痰管时切勿施加负压；只在拔出吸痰管时施加负压。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":949,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.758","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.758.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.758.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Primary Care Visit A 68-year-old male presents to the clinic for a routine checkup.","fullStemZh":"初级保健随访 一名68岁男性来到诊所进行常规体检。","terminalSentenceEn":"Primary Care Visit A 68-year-old male presents to the clinic for a routine checkup.","terminalSentenceZh":"初级保健随访 一名68岁男性来到诊所进行常规体检。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adults over 65 require specific immunizations, including high-dose influenza, pneumococcal, and zoster vaccines. Addressing misconceptions is key to health promotion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"65岁以上的成人需要特定的免疫接种，包括高剂量流感、肺炎球菌和带状疱疹疫苗。纠正误解是健康促进的关键。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on age-related primary prevention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注与年龄相关的初级预防。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":950,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Click to specify if each finding increases the client's risk for vaccine-preventable complications.","fullStemZh":"点击指出以下各项发现是否增加了该患者发生疫苗可预防并发症的风险。","terminalSentenceEn":"Click to specify if each finding increases the client's risk for vaccine-preventable complications.","terminalSentenceZh":"点击指出以下各项发现是否增加了该患者发生疫苗可预防并发症的风险。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Age of 68","zh":"年龄68岁"},{"id":"r2","en":"COPD history","zh":"慢阻肺病史"},{"id":"r3","en":"Independent living","zh":"独立生活"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Does Not Increase Risk","zh":"不增加风险"},{"id":"c1","en":"Increases Risk","zh":"增加风险"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Advanced age (≥65) and chronic lung diseases like COPD increase the risk of severe complications from influenza and pneumococcal infections.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高龄（≥65岁）和慢性肺部疾病（如COPD）会增加流感和肺炎球菌感染引起严重并发症的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify factors that compromise immunity or respiratory function.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别损害免疫力或呼吸功能的因素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":951,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,25],"fullStemEn":"Which vaccines should the nurse anticipate administering to this client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应预计为该患者接种哪些疫苗？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which vaccines should the nurse anticipate administering to this client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预计为该患者接种哪些疫苗？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"o5","en":"Tdap or Td booster (if due or immunization history unknown)","zh":"百白破(Tdap)或破伤风-白喉(Td)加强针（如已到期或免疫接种史不明）"},{"id":"o2","en":"Pneumococcal vaccine","zh":"肺炎球菌疫苗"},{"id":"o4","en":"HPV vaccine","zh":"人乳头瘤病毒(HPV)疫苗"},{"id":"o3","en":"Recombinant zoster vaccine","zh":"重组带状疱疹疫苗"},{"id":"o1","en":"Influenza vaccine (high-dose)","zh":"流感疫苗（高剂量）"}],"correct":["o1","o2","o3","o5"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adults ≥65 need high-dose influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, and Tdap (if due) vaccines. HPV is not indicated for this age group.","rationaleCorrectZh":"≥65岁的成人需要接种高剂量流感、肺炎球菌、带状疱疹和Tdap（如果到期）疫苗。HPV疫苗不适用于该年龄段。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall CDC adult immunization guidelines for clients over 65.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回想CDC针对65岁以上成人的免疫接种指南。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which vaccines should the nurse anticipate administering to this client?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应预计为该患者接种哪些疫苗？"}
{"queueIndex":952,"bankPath":"banks/gemini-canonical.json","bankSha256":"8259ffb6b12c5b3ba267566b8247207ec4fc573d536d9f78fafd5d18655b63c3","topLevelQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gemini_gapfill_case_2026_06_10_case_imm_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.758.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,39],"fullStemEn":"The client states, 'I don't want the flu shot because it gave me the flu last time.' What is the nurse's best response?","fullStemZh":"患者说：“我不想打流感疫苗，因为上次打完我就得流感了。”护士的最佳回答是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's best response?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的最佳回答是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client states, 'I don't want the flu shot because it gave me the flu last time.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者说：“我不想打流感疫苗，因为上次打完我就得流感了。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"'We can skip the flu shot this year since you had a bad reaction.'","zh":"“既然您有不良反应，我们今年可以不打流感疫苗。”"},{"id":"o2","en":"'The injected flu vaccine is inactivated and cannot cause the flu. You may have experienced a mild immune response or a cold.'","zh":"“注射的流感疫苗是灭活的，不会引起流感。您可能经历了轻微的免疫反应或感冒。”"},{"id":"o4","en":"'You should take acetaminophen before the injection to prevent getting sick.'","zh":"“您应该在注射前服用对乙酰氨基酚，以防生病。”"},{"id":"o1","en":"'The flu shot contains a live virus, so mild symptoms are normal.'","zh":"“流感疫苗含有活病毒，所以出现轻微症状是正常的。”"}],"correct":["o2"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The injected influenza vaccine contains inactivated virus and cannot cause influenza. Mild systemic reactions (muscle aches, low fever) are a normal immune response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"注射的流感疫苗含有灭活病毒，不会引起流感。轻微的全身反应（肌肉酸痛、低热）是正常的免疫反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Address misconceptions with factual education.","testTakingStrategyZh":"用事实教育来纠正误解。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
