breathing support.","testTakingStrategyZh":"恐慌题选择陪伴、平静语气、简短指令和呼吸支持。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1202,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_chest_tube_disconnect_052","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.51","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.51.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.51.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,107],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,32],"fullStemEn":"A client's chest tube disconnects from the drainage system. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一位患者的胸腔引流管与引流系统脱开。请按正确顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client's chest tube disconnects from the drainage system.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者的胸腔引流管与引流系统脱开。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place the distal end of the chest tube in sterile water.","zh":"将胸管远端放入无菌水中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the provider after emergency actions are underway.","zh":"紧急措施启动后通知医疗提供者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare or obtain a new drainage system.","zh":"准备或取得新的引流系统。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client's respiratory status.","zh":"评估患者呼吸状态。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate priority is restoring a water seal by placing the tube end in sterile water. Then assess breathing, replace the system, and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要任务是将管端放入无菌水中以恢复水封。随后评估呼吸、更换系统并通知医疗提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When equipment failure threatens breathing, first take the action that immediately protects ventilation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"设备故障威胁呼吸时，先采取立即保护通气的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client's chest tube disconnects from the drainage system.","controlSentenceZh":"一位患者的胸腔引流管与引流系统脱开。"}
{"queueIndex":1203,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_pregnancy_warning_signs_053","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.52.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,98],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,24],"fullStemEn":"Which findings should the nurse teach a pregnant client to report promptly? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应教导孕妇及时报告哪些表现？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings should the nurse teach a pregnant client to report promptly?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应教导孕妇及时报告哪些表现？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Mild ankle swelling after standing all day.","zh":"整天站立后轻度踝部水肿。"},{"id":"A","en":"Severe headache with blurred vision.","zh":"严重头痛并视物模糊。"},{"id":"D","en":"Leakage of fluid from the vagina.","zh":"阴道流出液体。"},{"id":"E","en":"Decreased fetal movement after viability.","zh":"胎儿达到存活期后胎动减少。"},{"id":"C","en":"Vaginal bleeding.","zh":"阴道出血。"},{"id":"F","en":"Persistent right upper quadrant pain.","zh":"持续右上腹疼痛。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe headache or vision changes, bleeding, leaking fluid, decreased fetal movement, and persistent right upper quadrant pain may signal complications needing prompt evaluation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重头痛或视力变化、出血、流液、胎动减少和持续右上腹痛可能提示并发症，需要及时评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pregnancy warning signs often involve bleeding, fluid leakage, fetal movement changes, and severe preeclampsia cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"妊娠警讯常包括出血、流液、胎动变化和严重子痫前期线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1204,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_latex_allergy_054","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.53","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.53.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.53.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,108],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,30],"fullStemEn":"A client reports a severe latex allergy before surgery. Select whether each action is appropriate or unsafe.","fullStemZh":"一位患者术前报告严重乳胶过敏。选择每项措施是适当还是不安全。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select whether each action is appropriate or unsafe.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择每项措施是适当还是不安全。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client reports a severe latex allergy before surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者术前报告严重乳胶过敏。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Place latex-free supplies in the room.","zh":"在房间内放置无乳胶用品。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Use powdered latex gloves because the contact will be brief.","zh":"因接触时间短而使用有粉乳胶手套。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Ask about allergy to bananas, avocados, or kiwis.","zh":"询问是否对香蕉、牛油果或猕猴桃过敏。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Clearly label the chart and room with latex-allergy precautions.","zh":"在病历和房间清楚标示乳胶过敏预防措施。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"},{"id":"c2","en":"Unsafe","zh":"不安全"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Latex allergy precautions include latex-free supplies, visible alerts, and assessment for cross-reactive food allergies. Latex gloves are unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乳胶过敏预防包括使用无乳胶用品、明显警示，并评估交叉反应食物过敏。乳胶手套不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For severe allergies, choose system-level prevention: remove the allergen and alert the team.","testTakingStrategyZh":"严重过敏题选择系统性预防：移除过敏原并提醒团队。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1205,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_oxygen_tank_duration_055","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.54.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,72],"fullStemEn":"An E oxygen cylinder reads 2000 psi. The safe residual pressure is 500 psi. The flow rate is 2 L/min. Using a cylinder factor of 0.28, how many minutes of oxygen are available?","fullStemZh":"一个 E 型氧气瓶压力为 2000 psi。安全剩余压力为 500 psi。流量为 2 L/min。使用气瓶系数 0.28，可用氧气有多少分钟？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using a cylinder factor of 0.28, how many minutes of oxygen are available?","terminalSentenceZh":"使用气瓶系数 0.28，可用氧气有多少分钟？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The flow rate is 2 L/min.","penultimateSentenceZh":"流量为 2 L/min。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minutes available","zh":"可用分钟数"},"acceptable":["210","210 minutes"],"numeric":{"value":210,"tolerance":1,"unit":"minutes"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Available time = (2000 - 500) x 0.28 / 2 = 1500 x 0.28 / 2 = 420 / 2 = 210 minutes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可用时间 = (2000 - 500) x 0.28 / 2 = 1500 x 0.28 / 2 = 420 / 2 = 210 分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For oxygen duration, use usable pressure, not total pressure: (psi - residual) x factor / flow.","testTakingStrategyZh":"氧气时长计算使用可用压力而非总压力：(压力 - 剩余压力) x 系数 / 流量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1206,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_acute_pancreatitis_056","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.55","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.55.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.55.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute pancreatitis has severe epigastric pain, vomiting, tachycardia, and a blood pressure of 88/54 mm Hg.","fullStemZh":"一位急性胰腺炎患者有严重上腹痛、呕吐、心动过速，血压 88/54 mm Hg。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with acute pancreatitis has severe epigastric pain, vomiting, tachycardia, and a blood pressure of 88/54 mm Hg.","terminalSentenceZh":"一位急性胰腺炎患者有严重上腹痛、呕吐、心动过速，血压 88/54 mm Hg。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize risk for {{1}} caused by {{2}}.","zh":"护士应识别由 {{2}} 导致的 {{1}} 风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"fluid volume excess","zh":"体液过多"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypovolemic shock","zh":"低血容量性休克"},{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic alkalosis from overhydration","zh":"补液过多导致代谢性碱中毒"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"slow heart rate and hypertension","zh":"心率缓慢和高血压"},{"id":"o2","en":"increased oral intake","zh":"口服摄入增加"},{"id":"o1","en":"third spacing of fluid and vomiting","zh":"液体第三间隙转移和呕吐"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acute pancreatitis can cause capillary leak and third spacing, while vomiting adds fluid loss. Hypotension and tachycardia are concerning for hypovolemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性胰腺炎可导致毛细血管渗漏和液体第三间隙转移，呕吐进一步造成液体丢失。低血压和心动过速提示低血容量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In pancreatitis, look for systemic instability: hypovolemia, respiratory issues, glucose changes, and severe pain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"胰腺炎题关注全身不稳定：低血容量、呼吸问题、血糖变化和剧痛。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1207,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_mc_staff_assignment_057","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.56.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,34],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse is making assignments on a medical-surgical unit. Which client should be assigned to the most experienced RN?","fullStemZh":"责任护士正在内外科病区分配患者。哪位患者应分配给最有经验的注册护士？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which client should be assigned to the most experienced RN?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪位患者应分配给最有经验的注册护士？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse is making assignments on a medical-surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"责任护士正在内外科病区分配患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A client with pneumonia who is afebrile and awaiting discharge teaching.","zh":"肺炎患者，已无发热，等待出院教学。"},{"id":"C","en":"A client with chronic arthritis requesting assistance with bathing.","zh":"慢性关节炎患者，请求协助洗澡。"},{"id":"A","en":"A client with a urinary tract infection receiving oral antibiotics.","zh":"尿路感染患者，正在服用口服抗生素。"},{"id":"D","en":"A client 2 hours after a thyroidectomy reporting neck tightness and difficulty swallowing.","zh":"甲状腺切除术后 2 小时，报告颈部紧绷和吞咽困难的患者。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Neck tightness and difficulty swallowing after thyroidectomy may indicate bleeding or airway compromise. This client is unstable and needs the most experienced RN.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺切除术后颈部紧绷和吞咽困难可能提示出血或气道受威胁。该患者不稳定，需要最有经验的注册护士。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Assign the strongest nurse to the client with actual or potential airway, bleeding, or rapid deterioration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将最强护士分配给存在实际或潜在气道、出血或快速恶化风险的患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1208,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_osteoporosis_prevention_058","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.57.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,128],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,39],"fullStemEn":"Which teaching points should the nurse include for an adult client who wants to reduce osteoporosis risk? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位成年患者希望降低骨质疏松风险。护士应包括哪些健康教育要点？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which teaching points should the nurse include for an adult client who wants to reduce osteoporosis risk?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些健康教育要点？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Discuss calcium and vitamin D intake with the provider.","zh":"与医疗提供者讨论钙和维生素 D 摄入。"},{"id":"E","en":"Review home fall-prevention measures.","zh":"复习居家防跌倒措施。"},{"id":"D","en":"Stop smoking and limit alcohol intake.","zh":"戒烟并限制酒精摄入。"},{"id":"B","en":"Avoid all sunlight exposure.","zh":"避免所有阳光照射。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use prolonged bed rest to protect bones.","zh":"长期卧床以保护骨骼。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform regular weight-bearing exercise as tolerated.","zh":"在可耐受范围内定期进行负重运动。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Weight-bearing activity, adequate calcium and vitamin D, smoking cessation, limited alcohol, and fall prevention support bone health and reduce fracture risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"负重活动、足够钙和维生素 D、戒烟、限制酒精和防跌倒有助于骨骼健康并降低骨折风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For osteoporosis, choose movement, bone nutrients, risk-factor reduction, and fall prevention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"骨质疏松题选择运动、骨骼营养、减少风险因素和防跌倒。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1209,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_incident_report_fall_059","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.58.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,102],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,35],"fullStemEn":"A nurse finds a client on the floor after an unwitnessed fall. Place the actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一位患者在无人目击的跌倒后躺在地上。请按正确顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse finds a client on the floor after an unwitnessed fall.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现一位患者在无人目击的跌倒后躺在地上。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Document objective assessment data and interventions in the health record.","zh":"在病历中记录客观评估资料和干预措施。"},{"id":"D","en":"Complete an incident report according to facility policy.","zh":"按机构政策完成事件报告。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call for assistance and notify the provider of assessment findings.","zh":"呼叫协助，并将评估结果通知医疗提供者。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client for injury before moving the client.","zh":"移动患者前评估是否受伤。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first assesses for injury and keeps the client safe, then notifies appropriate personnel, documents objective clinical data, and completes the separate incident report.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先评估伤情并确保患者安全，然后通知相关人员，记录客观临床资料，并另行完成事件报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After an incident, client assessment and safety come before paperwork.","testTakingStrategyZh":"事件发生后，患者评估和安全优先于文书工作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1210,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_refeeding_syndrome_060","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.59.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,43],"fullStemEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is beginning nutritional rehabilitation. Select whether each finding or action is expected/appropriate or requires follow-up.","fullStemZh":"一位神经性厌食症患者正在开始营养康复。选择每项表现或措施属于预期/适当，还是需要跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select whether each finding or action is expected/appropriate or requires follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择每项表现或措施属于预期/适当，还是需要跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with anorexia nervosa is beginning nutritional rehabilitation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位神经性厌食症患者正在开始营养康复。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Serum phosphorus decreases after calories are increased.","zh":"热量增加后血磷下降。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Daily weights and electrolyte monitoring are prescribed.","zh":"医嘱每日体重和电解质监测。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Calories are advanced gradually as prescribed.","zh":"按医嘱逐步增加热量。"},{"id":"r4","en":"New peripheral edema and muscle weakness occur.","zh":"出现新的外周水肿和肌无力。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected/appropriate","zh":"预期/适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Refeeding syndrome can cause electrolyte shifts, especially hypophosphatemia, fluid retention, and weakness. Gradual nutrition and close monitoring are appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"再喂养综合征可导致电解质转移，尤其低磷血症、液体潴留和乏力。逐步补充营养和密切监测是适当的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With severe malnutrition, nutrition is treatment but must be restarted carefully with electrolyte monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"严重营养不良时，营养是治疗，但必须在电解质监测下谨慎重新开始。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1211,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_warfarin_teaching_061","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.60.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,35],"fullStemEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include when teaching a client prescribed warfarin? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士为使用华法林的患者进行健康教育时，应包括哪些指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include when teaching a client prescribed warfarin?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士为使用华法林的患者进行健康教育时，应包括哪些指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Report black stools, blood in urine, or prolonged bleeding.","zh":"报告黑便、血尿或出血时间延长。"},{"id":"F","en":"Keep scheduled INR blood tests.","zh":"按时进行 INR 血液检查。"},{"id":"E","en":"Check with the provider before taking aspirin or NSAIDs.","zh":"服用阿司匹林或非甾体抗炎药前先咨询医疗提供者。"},{"id":"A","en":"Keep vitamin K intake consistent from week to week.","zh":"每周维生素 K 摄入量保持稳定。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use a soft toothbrush and electric razor.","zh":"使用软毛牙刷和电动剃须刀。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop taking warfarin whenever bruising occurs.","zh":"只要出现瘀斑就停止服用华法林。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warfarin teaching focuses on consistent vitamin K, bleeding precautions, avoiding interacting drugs unless approved, and INR monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林教育重点是维生素 K 摄入稳定、出血预防、避免未经批准的相互作用药物，以及 INR 监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anticoagulant teaching usually includes bleeding signs, lab monitoring, drug interactions, and injury prevention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝药教育通常包括出血迹象、实验室监测、药物相互作用和防损伤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1212,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_mc_pregnancy_vaccines_062","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.61.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,28],"fullStemEn":"A pregnant client asks which vaccine should be avoided during pregnancy. Which vaccine should the nurse identify?","fullStemZh":"一位孕妇询问怀孕期间应避免哪种疫苗。护士应指出哪种疫苗？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which vaccine should the nurse identify?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应指出哪种疫苗？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A pregnant client asks which vaccine should be avoided during pregnancy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位孕妇询问怀孕期间应避免哪种疫苗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Measles, mumps, and rubella vaccine.","zh":"麻疹、腮腺炎和风疹疫苗。"},{"id":"A","en":"Inactivated influenza vaccine.","zh":"灭活流感疫苗。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tdap vaccine.","zh":"Tdap 疫苗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hepatitis B vaccine when indicated.","zh":"有适应证时的乙肝疫苗。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The measles, mumps, and rubella vaccine is a live attenuated vaccine and is avoided during pregnancy. Inactivated influenza and Tdap are commonly recommended during pregnancy, and hepatitis B may be given when indicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"麻腮风疫苗是减毒活疫苗，孕期应避免。灭活流感疫苗和 Tdap 通常在孕期推荐；有适应证时可接种乙肝疫苗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In pregnancy vaccine questions, live attenuated vaccines are generally avoided; inactivated vaccines may be recommended when indicated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"孕期疫苗题中，通常避免减毒活疫苗；有适应证时可推荐灭活疫苗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A pregnant client asks which vaccine should be avoided during pregnancy.","controlSentenceZh":"一位孕妇询问怀孕期间应避免哪种疫苗。"}
{"queueIndex":1213,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_aminoglycoside_063","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.62.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,40],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving gentamicin IV for a serious infection. The nurse reviews the client's assessment data before the next dose.","fullStemZh":"一位患者因严重感染正在接受庆大霉素静脉治疗。护士在下一剂给药前查看患者评估资料。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the client's assessment data before the next dose.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在下一剂给药前查看患者评估资料。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving gentamicin IV for a serious infection.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者因严重感染正在接受庆大霉素静脉治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should monitor {{1}} because aminoglycosides can cause {{2}}.","zh":"护士应监测 {{1}}，因为氨基糖苷类可导致 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"serum creatinine and hearing changes","zh":"血清肌酐和听力变化"},{"id":"o2","en":"serum calcium and visual acuity","zh":"血钙和视力"},{"id":"o3","en":"platelet count and skin color","zh":"血小板计数和皮肤颜色"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"photosensitivity and tendon rupture","zh":"光敏反应和肌腱断裂"},{"id":"o1","en":"nephrotoxicity and ototoxicity","zh":"肾毒性和耳毒性"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypoglycemia and gingival hyperplasia","zh":"低血糖和牙龈增生"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Aminoglycosides such as gentamicin can injure the kidneys and inner ear. Creatinine, urine output, hearing, tinnitus, and drug levels may be monitored.","rationaleCorrectZh":"庆大霉素等氨基糖苷类可能损伤肾脏和内耳。需监测肌酐、尿量、听力、耳鸣和药物浓度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link aminoglycosides with kidney and ear toxicity; check renal labs and hearing symptoms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把氨基糖苷类与肾脏和耳部毒性联系起来；检查肾功能和听力症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client is receiving gentamicin IV for a serious infection.","controlSentenceZh":"一位患者因严重感染正在接受庆大霉素静脉治疗。"}
{"queueIndex":1214,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_intake_output_064","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.63.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,69],"fullStemEn":"A client drinks 240 mL of water, 120 mL of juice, and 180 mL of soup. The client receives 500 mL IV fluid. Urine output is 700 mL. What is the client's total intake?","fullStemZh":"一位患者饮水 240 mL、果汁 120 mL、汤 180 mL，并接受静脉液体 500 mL。尿量为 700 mL。患者总摄入量是多少？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the client's total intake?","terminalSentenceZh":"患者总摄入量是多少？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Urine output is 700 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"尿量为 700 mL。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"total intake","zh":"总摄入量"},"acceptable":["1040","1040 mL"],"numeric":{"value":1040,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total intake includes oral fluids and IV fluids: 240 + 120 + 180 + 500 = 1040 mL. Urine is output, not intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总摄入量包括口服液体和静脉液体：240 + 120 + 180 + 500 = 1040 mL。尿液属于排出量，不计入摄入量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate intake from output before doing the math.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算前先区分摄入量和排出量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1215,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_asthma_exacerbation_065","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.64.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,41],"fullStemEn":"For each assessment finding in a client with an asthma exacerbation, select whether it is expected in moderate distress or indicates deterioration.","fullStemZh":"针对哮喘急性加重患者的每项评估发现，选择其属于中度窘迫的预期表现还是提示病情恶化。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding in a client with an asthma exacerbation, select whether it is expected in moderate distress or indicates deterioration.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对哮喘急性加重患者的每项评估发现，选择其属于中度窘迫的预期表现还是提示病情恶化。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Wheezing and speaking in short phrases.","zh":"喘鸣，并只能短句说话。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Sudden absence of breath sounds with increasing fatigue.","zh":"呼吸音突然消失并疲劳加重。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Use of accessory muscles.","zh":"使用辅助呼吸肌。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Drowsiness and rising carbon dioxide level.","zh":"嗜睡且二氧化碳水平升高。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Deterioration","zh":"病情恶化"},{"id":"c1","en":"Moderate distress","zh":"中度窘迫"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Wheezing, short phrases, and accessory muscle use are concerning but common in moderate exacerbation. Silent chest, fatigue, drowsiness, and carbon dioxide retention signal impending respiratory failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"喘鸣、短句说话和使用辅助呼吸肌令人担忧，但可见于中度急性加重。胸部无声、疲劳、嗜睡和二氧化碳潴留提示即将发生呼吸衰竭。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In asthma, less wheezing with worse appearance can be more dangerous than loud wheezing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"哮喘题中，喘鸣减少但状态更差可能比响亮喘鸣更危险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1216,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_anaphylaxis_066","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.65.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,41],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving an IV antibiotic develops wheezing, facial swelling, and hypotension. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一位正在接受静脉抗生素的患者出现喘鸣、面部肿胀和低血压。请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receiving an IV antibiotic develops wheezing, facial swelling, and hypotension.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位正在接受静脉抗生素的患者出现喘鸣、面部肿胀和低血压。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administer epinephrine as prescribed or per emergency protocol.","zh":"按医嘱或急救流程给予肾上腺素。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare oxygen and airway support.","zh":"准备氧气和气道支持。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the antibiotic infusion.","zh":"停止抗生素输注。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call the rapid response team and stay with the client.","zh":"呼叫快速反应团队并陪伴患者。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse stops the suspected trigger, activates emergency help, gives epinephrine per protocol, and supports airway and oxygenation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应停止疑似诱因，启动急救帮助，按流程给予肾上腺素，并支持气道和氧合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For anaphylaxis, remove the trigger, call for help, give epinephrine, and protect airway and breathing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"过敏性休克题：移除诱因、呼叫帮助、给予肾上腺素、保护气道和呼吸。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client receiving an IV antibiotic develops wheezing, facial swelling, and hypotension.","controlSentenceZh":"一位正在接受静脉抗生素的患者出现喘鸣、面部肿胀和低血压。"}
{"queueIndex":1217,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_clabsi_prevention_067","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.66","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.66.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.66.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,34],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions help reduce the risk of central line-associated bloodstream infection? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些护理措施有助于降低中心静脉导管相关血流感染风险？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions help reduce the risk of central line-associated bloodstream infection?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施有助于降低中心静脉导管相关血流感染风险？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Leave old blood under the dressing if the edges remain sealed.","zh":"若敷料边缘仍密封，可将旧血留在敷料下。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene before accessing the line.","zh":"接触导管前进行手卫生。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use the central line for routine blood draws even when not needed.","zh":"即使不需要，也用中心线常规抽血。"},{"id":"E","en":"Review daily whether the central line is still needed.","zh":"每日评估中心线是否仍有必要。"},{"id":"C","en":"Change transparent dressings when loose, damp, or soiled.","zh":"透明敷料松动、潮湿或污染时更换。"},{"id":"B","en":"Scrub the catheter hub before each access.","zh":"每次接入前擦拭导管接口。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hand hygiene, hub disinfection, clean intact dressings, and prompt removal of unnecessary lines reduce infection risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手卫生、接口消毒、保持敷料清洁完整以及及时移除不必要导管可降低感染风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For invasive lines, reduce entries, keep everything clean and dry, and remove devices as soon as possible.","testTakingStrategyZh":"侵入性导管题：减少接入、保持清洁干燥，并尽早移除设备。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1218,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_mc_informed_consent_068","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.67","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.67.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.67.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,40],"fullStemEn":"A client who speaks limited English is scheduled for surgery. The adult child offers to interpret the consent discussion. What should the nurse do?","fullStemZh":"一位英语能力有限的患者即将手术。成年子女提出为知情同意讨论做翻译。护士应怎么做？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse do?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应怎么做？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The adult child offers to interpret the consent discussion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"成年子女提出为知情同意讨论做翻译。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Document that consent is implied because surgery is scheduled.","zh":"记录因已安排手术所以默示同意。"},{"id":"A","en":"Allow the adult child to interpret because the client trusts the child.","zh":"允许成年子女翻译，因为患者信任子女。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the client to sign if the client can repeat the procedure name.","zh":"如果患者能复述手术名称，就请其签字。"},{"id":"C","en":"Arrange a qualified medical interpreter for the consent discussion.","zh":"为知情同意讨论安排合格医疗口译员。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A qualified interpreter supports accurate, unbiased communication and informed consent. Family members should not be used for formal consent discussions except in emergencies when no alternative exists.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合格口译员能支持准确、无偏倚的沟通和知情同意。正式知情同意讨论不应使用家属翻译，除非紧急且无其他选择。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Consent requires understanding; language barriers call for a qualified interpreter.","testTakingStrategyZh":"知情同意需要理解；语言障碍时应使用合格口译员。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
