常、苍白和神经血管改变提示骨筋膜室综合征，是威胁肢体的急症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pain unrelieved by opioids plus neurovascular changes after a cast is not normal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"石膏后阿片类药物不能缓解的疼痛加神经血管改变不是正常表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with a lower-leg cast reports severe pain unrelieved by prescribed opioid medication.","controlSentenceZh":"一位小腿石膏固定患者报告严重疼痛，按医嘱使用阿片类药物后仍未缓解。"}
{"queueIndex":1220,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_cefazolin_infusion_070","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.69","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.69.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.69.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,54],"fullStemEn":"The nurse must infuse cefazolin 1 g in 100 mL normal saline over 30 minutes. The pump should be set to how many mL/hr?","fullStemZh":"护士需要在 30 分钟内输注头孢唑林 1 g 加入 100 mL 生理盐水。输液泵应设置为多少 mL/hr？","terminalSentenceEn":"The pump should be set to how many mL/hr?","terminalSentenceZh":"输液泵应设置为多少 mL/hr？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse must infuse cefazolin 1 g in 100 mL normal saline over 30 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士需要在 30 分钟内输注头孢唑林 1 g 加入 100 mL 生理盐水。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"pump rate","zh":"输液泵速度"},"acceptable":["200","200 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":200,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thirty minutes is 0.5 hr. 100 mL divided by 0.5 hr = 200 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"30 分钟为 0.5 小时。100 mL 除以 0.5 小时 = 200 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pump rate is volume divided by time in hours.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输液泵速度等于体积除以小时数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1221,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_diabetes_sick_day_071","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.70","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.70.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.70.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,41],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes reviews sick-day rules. Select whether each statement shows understanding or needs more teaching.","fullStemZh":"一位 1 型糖尿病患者复习生病日规则。选择每句话是否表明理解正确或需要进一步教学。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select whether each statement shows understanding or needs more teaching.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择每句话是否表明理解正确或需要进一步教学。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes reviews sick-day rules.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位 1 型糖尿病患者复习生病日规则。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"I will keep taking insulin even if I am eating less.","zh":"即使吃得少，我也会继续使用胰岛素。"},{"id":"r2","en":"I should check my blood glucose more often when I am sick.","zh":"生病时我应更频繁检查血糖。"},{"id":"r3","en":"If I vomit all day, I should skip fluids until my stomach settles.","zh":"如果我整天呕吐，应先不喝水等胃舒服些。"},{"id":"r4","en":"I will call the provider for moderate or large ketones.","zh":"出现中到大量酮体时我会联系医疗提供者。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Needs teaching","zh":"需要教学"},{"id":"c1","en":"Understands","zh":"理解正确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During illness, insulin needs may continue or increase. The client should monitor glucose and ketones, maintain fluids if possible, and report concerning ketones or persistent vomiting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生病时胰岛素仍可能需要甚至增加。患者应监测血糖和酮体，尽量维持液体摄入，并报告明显酮体或持续呕吐。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Sick-day diabetes rules: continue insulin, monitor more, hydrate, and check ketones.","testTakingStrategyZh":"糖尿病生病日规则：继续胰岛素、增加监测、补液、查酮体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes reviews sick-day rules.","controlSentenceZh":"一位 1 型糖尿病患者复习生病日规则。"}
{"queueIndex":1222,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_suspected_stroke_072","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.71","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.71.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.71.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,29],"fullStemEn":"A client suddenly develops facial droop and right arm weakness. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一位患者突然出现面瘫和右臂无力。请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client suddenly develops facial droop and right arm weakness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者突然出现面瘫和右臂无力。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Prepare the client for urgent brain imaging as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱准备患者进行紧急脑部影像检查。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the stroke response or notify the rapid response team.","zh":"启动卒中响应或通知快速反应团队。"},{"id":"B","en":"Determine the time the client was last known well.","zh":"确定患者最后一次被确认正常的时间。"},{"id":"C","en":"Check blood glucose.","zh":"检查血糖。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected stroke requires rapid activation, last-known-well time, glucose check to rule out mimic, and urgent imaging to guide treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似卒中需要快速启动响应、确认最后正常时间、检查血糖以排除类似表现，并进行紧急影像检查指导治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stroke questions are time questions: activate help, establish last-known-well, check glucose, and prepare for imaging.","testTakingStrategyZh":"卒中题就是时间题：启动帮助、确定最后正常时间、查血糖、准备影像。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client suddenly develops facial droop and right arm weakness.","controlSentenceZh":"一位患者突然出现面瘫和右臂无力。"}
{"queueIndex":1223,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_home_oxygen_073","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.72","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.72.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.72.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,32],"fullStemEn":"Which home safety instructions should the nurse include for a client prescribed home oxygen? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应为使用家庭氧疗的患者提供哪些居家安全指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which home safety instructions should the nurse include for a client prescribed home oxygen?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应为使用家庭氧疗的患者提供哪些居家安全指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Use petroleum jelly on dry nares.","zh":"鼻腔干燥时使用凡士林。"},{"id":"A","en":"Keep oxygen at least several feet away from open flames.","zh":"让氧气设备远离明火至少数英尺。"},{"id":"B","en":"Post no-smoking signs where oxygen is used.","zh":"在使用氧气处张贴禁止吸烟标志。"},{"id":"F","en":"Increase the flow rate whenever shortness of breath occurs without calling the provider.","zh":"只要气短就自行增加流量，不必联系医疗提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Secure oxygen cylinders upright.","zh":"将氧气瓶直立固定。"},{"id":"E","en":"Check that electrical equipment is in good condition.","zh":"检查电气设备状态良好。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Oxygen supports combustion. Clients should avoid flames and smoking, secure tanks, maintain safe electrical equipment, and avoid oil-based products near oxygen.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氧气助燃。患者应避免明火和吸烟，固定氧气瓶，保持电气设备安全，并避免在氧气附近使用油性产品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Oxygen is not flammable, but it feeds fire; eliminate ignition sources and oil-based products.","testTakingStrategyZh":"氧气本身不易燃，但助燃；应消除火源和油性产品。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1224,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_mc_confidentiality_hiv_074","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.73","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.73.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.73.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,34],"fullStemEn":"A visitor asks the nurse, \"Does my neighbor really have HIV?\" What is the nurse's best response?","fullStemZh":"一位访客问护士：“我的邻居真的有 HIV 吗？”护士最佳回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's best response?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A visitor asks the nurse, \"Does my neighbor really have HIV?\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位访客问护士：“我的邻居真的有 HIV 吗？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Only close family members can receive that information.","zh":"只有近亲属可以获得该信息。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask the client directly and then tell me what the client says.","zh":"你直接问患者，然后告诉我患者怎么说。"},{"id":"A","en":"I cannot discuss any client's health information.","zh":"我不能讨论任何患者的健康信息。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client is doing well, so there is no need to worry.","zh":"患者情况不错，所以不用担心。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse protects confidentiality and does not confirm or deny a client's diagnosis to an unauthorized person.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应保护保密性，不向未经授权者确认或否认患者诊断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Confidentiality answers should neither confirm nor deny protected health information.","testTakingStrategyZh":"保密题答案不应确认或否认受保护健康信息。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1225,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_increased_icp_075","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.74","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.74.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.74.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,33],"fullStemEn":"A client with a head injury becomes less responsive. The nurse notes widened pulse pressure, bradycardia, and irregular respirations.","fullStemZh":"一位头部损伤患者反应变差。护士发现脉压增宽、心动过缓和呼吸不规则。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse notes widened pulse pressure, bradycardia, and irregular respirations.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士发现脉压增宽、心动过缓和呼吸不规则。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a head injury becomes less responsive.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位头部损伤患者反应变差。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"These findings suggest {{1}}, and the nurse should {{2}}.","zh":"这些表现提示 {{1}}，护士应 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"fluid volume deficit only","zh":"单纯体液不足"},{"id":"o2","en":"expected opioid sedation","zh":"预期的阿片镇静"},{"id":"o1","en":"late increased intracranial pressure","zh":"颅内压升高晚期表现"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"dim the lights and recheck in 1 hour","zh":"调暗灯光并 1 小时后复查"},{"id":"o2","en":"place the client flat with knees flexed","zh":"让患者平卧并屈膝"},{"id":"o1","en":"notify the provider or rapid response team immediately","zh":"立即通知医疗提供者或快速反应团队"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Widened pulse pressure, bradycardia, and irregular respirations are Cushing response, a late sign of increased intracranial pressure and possible herniation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脉压增宽、心动过缓和呼吸不规则是库欣反应，是颅内压升高和可能脑疝的晚期征象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cushing response is late and dangerous: widened pulse pressure, bradycardia, irregular respirations.","testTakingStrategyZh":"库欣反应是晚期危险征象：脉压增宽、心动过缓、呼吸不规则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1226,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_enteral_feeding_volume_076","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.75","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.75.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.75.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,128],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,53],"fullStemEn":"A client receives tube feeding at 65 mL/hr from 2200 to 0600. How many mL of formula does the client receive during this period?","fullStemZh":"一位患者从 22:00 到 06:00 以 65 mL/hr 接受管饲。此期间患者接受多少 mL 配方液？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many mL of formula does the client receive during this period?","terminalSentenceZh":"此期间患者接受多少 mL 配方液？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receives tube feeding at 65 mL/hr from 2200 to 0600.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者从 22:00 到 06:00 以 65 mL/hr 接受管饲。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"formula received","zh":"接受的配方液量"},"acceptable":["520","520 mL"],"numeric":{"value":520,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"From 2200 to 0600 is 8 hours. 65 mL/hr x 8 hr = 520 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"22:00 到 06:00 为 8 小时。65 mL/hr x 8 hr = 520 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a time crosses midnight, count the hours in two parts if needed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"时间跨过午夜时，可分两段计算小时数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1227,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_wound_assessment_077","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.76","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.76.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.76.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,98],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"For each postoperative wound finding, select whether it is expected healing or requires follow-up.","fullStemZh":"针对每项术后伤口表现，选择其属于预期愈合还是需要跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each postoperative wound finding, select whether it is expected healing or requires follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项术后伤口表现，选择其属于预期愈合还是需要跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Edges approximated with mild pinkness.","zh":"伤口边缘对合，有轻度粉红色。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Thick yellow-green drainage with foul odor.","zh":"浓稠黄绿色渗液并有恶臭。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Small amount of serosanguineous drainage on day 1.","zh":"术后第 1 天少量浆液血性渗液。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Increasing pain, warmth, and swelling around the incision.","zh":"切口周围疼痛、温热和肿胀加重。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected healing","zh":"预期愈合"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Approximated edges and small early serosanguineous drainage can be expected. Purulent foul drainage and worsening inflammatory signs suggest infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"伤口边缘对合和术后早期少量浆液血性渗液可为预期表现。脓性恶臭渗液和炎症表现加重提示感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In wound questions, trend matters: worsening pain, heat, swelling, and purulent odor are not normal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"伤口题看趋势：疼痛、发热、肿胀加重和脓性恶臭不是正常表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1228,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_cord_prolapse_078","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.77","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.77.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.77.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,36],"fullStemEn":"After rupture of membranes, the fetal heart rate drops suddenly and the nurse sees the umbilical cord at the vaginal opening. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"胎膜破裂后，胎心率突然下降，护士在阴道口看到脐带。请按顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After rupture of membranes, the fetal heart rate drops suddenly and the nurse sees the umbilical cord at the vaginal opening.","penultimateSentenceZh":"胎膜破裂后，胎心率突然下降，护士在阴道口看到脐带。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Prepare for emergency birth while maintaining pressure off the cord.","zh":"在持续减轻脐带受压的同时准备紧急分娩。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use a sterile gloved hand to lift the presenting part off the cord.","zh":"用戴无菌手套的手将先露部从脐带上托起。"},{"id":"C","en":"Position the client knee-chest or Trendelenburg.","zh":"让患者采取膝胸位或头低脚高位。"},{"id":"A","en":"Call for help and notify the provider.","zh":"呼叫帮助并通知医疗提供者。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cord prolapse threatens fetal oxygenation. The nurse calls for help, relieves pressure on the cord, positions to reduce compression, and prepares for emergency birth.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脐带脱垂威胁胎儿氧合。护士应呼叫帮助、解除脐带受压、摆位减少压迫，并准备紧急分娩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cord prolapse, think fetal oxygenation: call, relieve pressure, position, prepare for emergency birth.","testTakingStrategyZh":"脐带脱垂题想到胎儿氧合：呼叫、解除压迫、摆位、准备紧急分娩。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1229,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_grief_communication_079","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.78","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.78.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.78.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,94],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,32],"fullStemEn":"A client's spouse died suddenly. Which nurse responses are therapeutic? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一位患者的配偶突然去世。护士哪些回应具有治疗性？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nurse responses are therapeutic?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士哪些回应具有治疗性？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"You need to be strong for your family.","zh":"您需要为了家人坚强起来。"},{"id":"D","en":"Would you like me to call anyone to be with you?","zh":"您希望我帮您联系谁来陪您吗？"},{"id":"F","en":"It is okay to cry here.","zh":"在这里哭是可以的。"},{"id":"B","en":"Tell me what you are thinking about right now.","zh":"告诉我您现在在想什么。"},{"id":"C","en":"At least your spouse did not suffer long.","zh":"至少您的配偶没有受很久的苦。"},{"id":"A","en":"I am so sorry. I can sit with you for a while.","zh":"我很难过。我可以陪您坐一会儿。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic grief communication offers presence, open-ended exploration, practical support, and permission to express emotion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性哀伤沟通提供陪伴、开放式探索、实际支持，并允许表达情绪。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic communication rarely starts with advice; it starts with presence and listening.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性沟通很少以建议开始；它从陪伴和倾听开始。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1230,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_mc_cdiff_precautions_080","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.79","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.79.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.79.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,30],"fullStemEn":"A client has watery diarrhea and a positive Clostridioides difficile test. Which infection-control action is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一位患者水样腹泻，艰难梭菌检测阳性。哪项感染控制措施最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which infection-control action is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项感染控制措施最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client has watery diarrhea and a positive Clostridioides difficile test.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者水样腹泻，艰难梭菌检测阳性。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use alcohol hand rub only because it kills spores reliably.","zh":"只使用酒精手消毒，因为它能可靠杀灭芽孢。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use airborne precautions with an N95 respirator.","zh":"采取空气隔离并佩戴 N95 口罩。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place the client in a protective environment room.","zh":"将患者安置在保护性环境病房。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use contact precautions and wash hands with soap and water after care.","zh":"采取接触隔离，护理后用肥皂和水洗手。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. difficile requires contact precautions. Soap and water are preferred after care because spores are not reliably removed by alcohol hand rub alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艰难梭菌需要接触隔离。护理后首选肥皂和水洗手，因为单用酒精手消毒不能可靠去除芽孢。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For C. difficile, remember contact precautions and soap-and-water handwashing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"艰难梭菌题记住：接触隔离和肥皂水洗手。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1231,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_pulmonary_embolism_081","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.80","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.80.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.80.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,41],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative client suddenly reports sharp chest pain and shortness of breath. Oxygen saturation drops to 86%, and the heart rate is 124/min.","fullStemZh":"一位术后患者突然报告尖锐胸痛和气短。血氧饱和度降至 86%，心率 124 次/分。","terminalSentenceEn":"Oxygen saturation drops to 86%, and the heart rate is 124/min.","terminalSentenceZh":"血氧饱和度降至 86%，心率 124 次/分。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A postoperative client suddenly reports sharp chest pain and shortness of breath.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位术后患者突然报告尖锐胸痛和气短。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should suspect {{1}} and first {{2}}.","zh":"护士应怀疑 {{1}}，并首先 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"atelectasis expected after surgery","zh":"术后预期肺不张"},{"id":"o3","en":"opioid-induced constipation","zh":"阿片类药物导致便秘"},{"id":"o1","en":"pulmonary embolism","zh":"肺栓塞"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"give an oral laxative","zh":"给予口服泻药"},{"id":"o1","en":"apply oxygen and call for immediate help","zh":"给予氧气并立即呼叫帮助"},{"id":"o2","en":"encourage ambulation in the hallway","zh":"鼓励在走廊行走"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden dyspnea, pleuritic chest pain, hypoxemia, and tachycardia after surgery are concerning for pulmonary embolism. Oxygen and rapid escalation are priorities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"术后突然呼吸困难、胸膜性胸痛、低氧和心动过速提示肺栓塞。优先给予氧气并快速升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After surgery, sudden chest pain plus hypoxemia and tachycardia is a pulmonary embolism cue until proven otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"术后突然胸痛加低氧和心动过速，应先视为肺栓塞线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1232,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_pregnancy_due_date_082","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.81","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.81.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.81.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,46],"fullStemEn":"A pregnant client's last menstrual period began on March 10. Using Naegele's rule, what is the estimated due date? Enter the month and day.","fullStemZh":"一位孕妇末次月经开始于 3 月 10 日。使用内格尔法则，预产期是哪一天？请输入月份和日期。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the month and day.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入月份和日期。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using Naegele's rule, what is the estimated due date?","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用内格尔法则，预产期是哪一天？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"estimated due date","zh":"预产期"},"acceptable":["December 17","Dec 17","12/17","12-17"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Naegele's rule subtracts 3 months and adds 7 days to the first day of the last menstrual period. March 10 minus 3 months is December 10; add 7 days = December 17.","rationaleCorrectZh":"内格尔法则为末次月经第一天减 3 个月再加 7 天。3 月 10 日减 3 个月为 12 月 10 日，加 7 天为 12 月 17 日。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For Naegele's rule: minus 3 months, plus 7 days.","testTakingStrategyZh":"内格尔法则：减 3 个月，加 7 天。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1233,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_depression_safety_083","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.82","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.82.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.82.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"For each statement by a client with depression, select whether it is low concern or requires immediate follow-up.","fullStemZh":"针对抑郁症患者的每句话，选择其为较低担忧还是需要立即跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each statement by a client with depression, select whether it is low concern or requires immediate follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对抑郁症患者的每句话，选择其为较低担忧还是需要立即跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"I have been sleeping more than usual this week.","zh":"这周我睡得比平常多。"},{"id":"r2","en":"I gave away my favorite guitar because I will not need it.","zh":"我把最喜欢的吉他送人了，因为我以后用不到了。"},{"id":"r3","en":"I feel sad and have low energy.","zh":"我感到难过并且精力低。"},{"id":"r4","en":"I know exactly how I would end my life.","zh":"我清楚知道自己会怎样结束生命。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Immediate follow-up","zh":"立即跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Low concern","zh":"较低担忧"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sleep and low energy are common depressive symptoms. Giving away valued possessions and having a specific suicide plan require immediate safety assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"睡眠增多和精力低是常见抑郁症状。送出珍贵物品和有具体自杀计划需要立即安全评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In depression, preparation behaviors and a specific suicide plan outrank general symptoms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抑郁题中，准备行为和具体自杀计划优先于一般症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1234,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_medication_error_084","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.83","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.83.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.83.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,30],"fullStemEn":"The nurse realizes that a client received the wrong dose of a medication. Place the actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一位患者接受了错误剂量的药物。请按正确顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse realizes that a client received the wrong dose of a medication.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现一位患者接受了错误剂量的药物。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client for adverse effects.","zh":"评估患者是否有不良反应。"},{"id":"C","en":"Implement prescribed monitoring or treatment.","zh":"执行医嘱监测或治疗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider and charge nurse.","zh":"通知医疗提供者和责任护士。"},{"id":"D","en":"Complete an incident report according to policy.","zh":"按政策完成事件报告。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is assessed first for safety. The nurse then notifies the appropriate team, implements orders, documents clinical facts, and completes the incident report per policy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先评估患者安全。随后通知相关团队，执行医嘱，记录临床事实，并按政策完成事件报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After an error, assess the client first, then notify, treat, document, and report.","testTakingStrategyZh":"错误发生后，先评估患者，再通知、处理、记录和报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1235,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_sata_breastfeeding_085","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.84","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.84.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.84.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,28],"fullStemEn":"Which statements by a postpartum client indicate correct understanding of breastfeeding? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"产后患者哪些陈述表明其正确理解母乳喂养？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements by a postpartum client indicate correct understanding of breastfeeding?","penultimateSentenceZh":"产后患者哪些陈述表明其正确理解母乳喂养？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"I should hear swallowing during effective feeding.","zh":"有效喂养时我应能听到吞咽声。"},{"id":"F","en":"I need to wash my nipples with soap before each feeding.","zh":"每次喂奶前我都需要用肥皂清洗乳头。"},{"id":"E","en":"I will count wet diapers to help know if intake is adequate.","zh":"我会数湿尿布来帮助判断摄入是否足够。"},{"id":"B","en":"The baby's mouth should cover much of the areola, not just the nipple.","zh":"宝宝口中应含住大部分乳晕，而不仅是乳头。"},{"id":"A","en":"I should feed my baby when early hunger cues appear.","zh":"宝宝出现早期饥饿信号时我应喂奶。"},{"id":"C","en":"Painful cracked nipples are expected for the first month.","zh":"最初一个月乳头疼痛皲裂是预期现象。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective breastfeeding includes feeding on cues, deep latch, audible swallowing, and monitoring output. Cracked nipples and harsh washing suggest problems or poor latch.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效母乳喂养包括按信号喂养、深含接、可听到吞咽声和监测排泄。乳头皲裂和过度清洗提示问题或含接不良。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Good breastfeeding signs are deep latch, swallowing, feeding cues, and adequate output.","testTakingStrategyZh":"良好母乳喂养迹象包括深含接、吞咽、按信号喂养和排泄足够。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1236,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_mc_postop_urinary_retention_086","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.85","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.85.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.85.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,40],"fullStemEn":"Six hours after surgery, a client reports lower abdominal discomfort and has not voided. The bladder is distended on palpation. What should the nurse do first?","fullStemZh":"术后 6 小时，一位患者报告下腹不适且尚未排尿。触诊膀胱膨隆。护士首先应做什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse do first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应做什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The bladder is distended on palpation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"触诊膀胱膨隆。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Assist the client to a normal voiding position or bedside commode if safe.","zh":"若安全，协助患者采取正常排尿姿势或使用床旁便椅。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ignore the finding because anesthesia always prevents voiding for 24 hours.","zh":"忽略该情况，因为麻醉总会使 24 小时内无法排尿。"},{"id":"B","en":"Restrict oral fluids for the rest of the shift.","zh":"本班剩余时间限制口服液体。"},{"id":"A","en":"Apply a tight abdominal binder.","zh":"使用紧腹带。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Noninvasive measures such as normal positioning, privacy, running water, or ambulation are often tried first when safe. Persistent retention may require bladder scan and catheterization per order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"若安全，通常先尝试正常姿势、隐私、流水声或下床活动等非侵入性措施。持续尿潴留可能需要膀胱扫描并按医嘱导尿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For stable retention, try safe least-invasive measures before invasive interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"稳定尿潴留题，先尝试安全、最少侵入措施，再考虑侵入性干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1237,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_adult_urine_output_087","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.86","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.86.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.86.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,46],"fullStemEn":"An adult client has a urinary catheter. The nurse expects at least 30 mL/hr of urine output. What is the minimum expected output over 8 hours?","fullStemZh":"一位成年患者留置导尿管。护士预期最低尿量为 30 mL/hr。8 小时内最低预期尿量是多少？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the minimum expected output over 8 hours?","terminalSentenceZh":"8 小时内最低预期尿量是多少？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse expects at least 30 mL/hr of urine output.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士预期最低尿量为 30 mL/hr。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minimum output over 8 hours","zh":"8 小时最低尿量"},"acceptable":["240","240 mL"],"numeric":{"value":240,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Minimum adult urine output is commonly monitored as 30 mL/hr. Over 8 hours: 30 x 8 = 240 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"成人最低尿量常按 30 mL/hr 监测。8 小时为 30 x 8 = 240 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For adult urine output, 30 mL/hr is a common minimum threshold used in nursing questions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"成人尿量题中，30 mL/hr 是护理题常用最低阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse expects at least 30 mL/hr of urine output.","controlSentenceZh":"护士预期最低尿量为 30 mL/hr。"}
{"queueIndex":1238,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_elopement_088","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.87","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.87.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.87.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse enters the room of a client with dementia who is at risk for wandering and finds the client missing. Place the nursing actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士进入一位有走失风险的痴呆患者房间，发现患者不见了。请按正确顺序排列护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse enters the room of a client with dementia who is at risk for wandering and finds the client missing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士进入一位有走失风险的痴呆患者房间，发现患者不见了。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Notify the charge nurse and activate the facility missing-client protocol.","zh":"通知责任护士并启动机构走失患者流程。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the event and update the care plan with prevention measures.","zh":"记录事件，并在护理计划中更新预防措施。"},{"id":"A","en":"Search the client's room, bathroom, and nearby unit areas.","zh":"搜索患者房间、卫生间及病区附近区域。"},{"id":"C","en":"When the client is found, stay with the client and assess for injury.","zh":"找到患者后，陪伴患者并评估是否受伤。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first checks the immediate area because the client may be nearby and in danger. The facility protocol and charge nurse are then activated to broaden the search. After the client is found, the nurse assesses safety before completing documentation and prevention planning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先检查附近区域，因为患者可能就在附近且处于危险中。随后启动机构流程并通知责任护士以扩大搜寻。找到患者后先评估安全，再完成记录和预防计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a missing client, think safety sequence: search nearby, get help, assess the client, then document and prevent recurrence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"走失患者题按安全顺序思考：先就近寻找，再寻求帮助，找到后评估患者，最后记录并预防复发。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1239,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_needlestick_089","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.88","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.88.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.88.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,25],"fullStemEn":"A nurse sustains a needlestick injury from a used hollow-bore needle. Classify each action.","fullStemZh":"护士被使用过的空心针头刺伤。请对每项行动进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项行动进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse sustains a needlestick injury from a used hollow-bore needle.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士被使用过的空心针头刺伤。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Wash the puncture site with soap and water.","zh":"用肥皂和清水清洗刺伤部位。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Squeeze the wound forcefully to make it bleed.","zh":"用力挤压伤口让其出血。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Report the exposure promptly and follow occupational health protocol.","zh":"及时报告暴露并遵循职业健康流程。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Delay reporting until the source client's laboratory results return.","zh":"等感染源患者化验结果回来后再报告。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate initial action","zh":"合适的初始行动"},{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate or delayed action","zh":"不合适或延误的行动"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate first aid and prompt reporting are required after a sharps exposure so postexposure evaluation and treatment can begin. Forceful squeezing and delayed reporting are not recommended.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锐器暴露后需要立即急救并及时报告，以便开始暴露后评估和处理。不建议用力挤压伤口或延迟报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After occupational exposure, choose immediate cleansing and reporting; avoid actions that delay postexposure care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"职业暴露后选择立即清洗和报告；避免任何延误暴露后处理的行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1240,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_oral_rehydration_090","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.89","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.89.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.89.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,63],"fullStemEn":"A child with mild dehydration weighs 12 kg. The discharge plan says to give 10 mL/kg of oral rehydration solution after each loose stool. How many mL should the caregiver give after each loose stool?","fullStemZh":"一名轻度脱水儿童体重 12 kg。出院计划写明每次稀便后给予 10 mL/kg 口服补液盐。照护者每次稀便后应给予多少 mL？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many mL should the caregiver give after each loose stool?","terminalSentenceZh":"照护者每次稀便后应给予多少 mL？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The discharge plan says to give 10 mL/kg of oral rehydration solution after each loose stool.","penultimateSentenceZh":"出院计划写明每次稀便后给予 10 mL/kg 口服补液盐。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL after each loose stool","zh":"每次稀便后的毫升数"},"acceptable":["120","120 mL"],"numeric":{"value":120,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Multiply the prescribed volume by weight: 10 mL/kg x 12 kg = 120 mL after each loose stool.","rationaleCorrectZh":"将医嘱剂量乘以体重：10 mL/kg x 12 kg = 每次稀便后 120 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For weight-based pediatric calculations, multiply the ordered amount per kg by the child's weight in kg.","testTakingStrategyZh":"儿童按体重计算题，将每 kg 医嘱量乘以儿童 kg 体重。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The discharge plan says to give 10 mL/kg of oral rehydration solution after each loose stool.","controlSentenceZh":"出院计划写明每次稀便后给予 10 mL/kg 口服补液盐。"}
{"queueIndex":1241,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_ipv_091","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.90","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.90.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.90.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,54],"fullStemEn":"An adult client has bruises in different stages of healing on both wrists. The client's partner answers most questions and refuses to leave the room. The client looks down and says, \"I'm just clumsy.\"","fullStemZh":"一位成年患者双腕有不同愈合阶段的瘀伤。患者伴侣代答大多数问题并拒绝离开房间。患者低头说：“我只是笨手笨脚。”","terminalSentenceEn":"The client looks down and says, \"I'm just clumsy.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"患者低头说：“我只是笨手笨脚。”","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's partner answers most questions and refuses to leave the room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者伴侣代答大多数问题并拒绝离开房间。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The priority nursing action is to {{1}} and assess safety using {{2}}.","zh":"优先护理行动是 {{1}}，并使用 {{2}} 评估安全。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"speak with the client alone when it is safe","zh":"在安全时单独与患者交谈"},{"id":"o3","en":"tell the client to leave the relationship immediately","zh":"告诉患者必须立即离开这段关系"},{"id":"o2","en":"ask the partner to explain how the bruises occurred","zh":"请伴侣解释瘀伤如何发生"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"leading questions that imply blame","zh":"暗示责备的诱导性问题"},{"id":"o1","en":"direct, nonjudgmental questions","zh":"直接且不评判的问题"},{"id":"o3","en":"questions asked only in front of the partner","zh":"只在伴侣面前提出的问题"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Possible intimate partner violence should be assessed privately and safely. Direct, nonjudgmental questions support disclosure and avoid increasing danger.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似亲密伴侣暴力应在安全、私密环境中评估。直接且不评判的问题有助于患者透露情况，并避免增加危险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With suspected abuse, prioritize privacy, safety, direct assessment, and resources; avoid confronting the suspected abuser.","testTakingStrategyZh":"疑似虐待题优先考虑隐私、安全、直接评估和资源支持；避免当面对质疑似施暴者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1242,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_delirium_092","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.91","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.91.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.91.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[46,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,26],"fullStemEn":"An older adult is hospitalized after surgery. Which findings are cues that require prompt assessment for delirium?","fullStemZh":"一位老年患者术后住院。哪些表现提示需要及时评估谵妄？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which findings are cues that require prompt assessment for delirium?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪些表现提示需要及时评估谵妄？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An older adult is hospitalized after surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位老年患者术后住院。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"New fluctuating inattention during the shift","zh":"本班新出现、波动性的注意力不集中"},{"id":"r2","en":"Gradual memory decline over several years","zh":"数年内逐渐出现的记忆下降"},{"id":"r3","en":"New visual hallucinations with disorganized thinking","zh":"新出现的视幻觉并伴思维混乱"},{"id":"r4","en":"Oriented in the morning but agitated and disoriented at night","zh":"早晨定向力正常，但夜间烦躁且定向障碍"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Prompt delirium assessment","zh":"及时评估谵妄"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not the priority delirium cue","zh":"不是优先谵妄线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Delirium is typically acute and fluctuating, with inattention, altered cognition, hallucinations, or sleep-wake disruption. Gradual memory decline over years is more consistent with dementia and is not the urgent postoperative cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"谵妄通常为急性、波动性，表现为注意力不集中、认知改变、幻觉或睡眠-觉醒紊乱。数年逐渐记忆下降更符合痴呆，不是术后紧急线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Delirium is acute and fluctuating; dementia is usually gradual and chronic.","testTakingStrategyZh":"谵妄是急性、波动性的；痴呆通常是逐渐、慢性的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1243,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_ileostomy_balance_093","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.92","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.92.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.92.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,80],"fullStemEn":"During an 8-hour shift, a client with an ileostomy has 650 mL ostomy output, 400 mL urine output, and 150 mL emesis. Total intake is 1400 mL. What is the client's net fluid balance for the shift?","fullStemZh":"一个 8 小时班次内，一位回肠造口患者造口排出 650 mL、尿量 400 mL、呕吐物 150 mL。总摄入量为 1400 mL。该班次患者净液体平衡是多少？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the client's net fluid balance for the shift?","terminalSentenceZh":"该班次患者净液体平衡是多少？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Total intake is 1400 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"总摄入量为 1400 mL。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"net fluid balance","zh":"净液体平衡"},"acceptable":["200","+200","200 mL","+200 mL","positive 200 mL"],"numeric":{"value":200,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total output is 650 + 400 + 150 = 1200 mL. Net balance is intake minus output: 1400 - 1200 = +200 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总排出量为 650 + 400 + 150 = 1200 mL。净平衡为摄入减排出：1400 - 1200 = +200 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For intake and output, include all measurable fluid losses before calculating net balance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出入量题先纳入所有可测量液体丢失，再计算净平衡。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1244,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_opioid_safety_094","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.93","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.93.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.93.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,48],"fullStemEn":"One hour after receiving IV morphine, a postoperative client is difficult to arouse. Respirations are 8/min, oxygen saturation is 88%, and the pupils are pinpoint.","fullStemZh":"术后患者接受静脉吗啡 1 小时后难以唤醒。呼吸 8 次/分，血氧饱和度 88%，瞳孔针尖样缩小。","terminalSentenceEn":"Respirations are 8/min, oxygen saturation is 88%, and the pupils are pinpoint.","terminalSentenceZh":"呼吸 8 次/分，血氧饱和度 88%，瞳孔针尖样缩小。","penultimateSentenceEn":"One hour after receiving IV morphine, a postoperative client is difficult to arouse.","penultimateSentenceZh":"术后患者接受静脉吗啡 1 小时后难以唤醒。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first {{1}} because the assessment indicates {{2}}.","zh":"护士首先应 {{1}}，因为评估结果提示 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"administer the next opioid dose to prevent uncontrolled pain","zh":"给予下一剂阿片类药以预防疼痛失控"},{"id":"o1","en":"support respirations and administer naloxone per protocol or prescription","zh":"支持呼吸并按流程或医嘱给予纳洛酮"},{"id":"o3","en":"place the client in a chair and encourage ambulation","zh":"让患者坐到椅子上并鼓励下床活动"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"a mild allergic reaction","zh":"轻度过敏反应"},{"id":"o2","en":"expected postoperative sleepiness only","zh":"仅为预期的术后嗜睡"},{"id":"o1","en":"opioid-induced respiratory depression","zh":"阿片类药物导致的呼吸抑制"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A respiratory rate of 8/min, hypoxemia, difficult arousal, and pinpoint pupils indicate opioid toxicity with respiratory depression. Airway and breathing support with naloxone per protocol or prescription is the priority.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呼吸 8 次/分、低氧、难以唤醒和针尖样瞳孔提示阿片中毒并发生呼吸抑制。优先支持气道和呼吸，并按流程或医嘱给予纳洛酮。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With opioids, low respiratory rate and decreased arousal are airway-breathing priorities.","testTakingStrategyZh":"阿片类用药题中，呼吸频率低和意识降低属于气道-呼吸优先事项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1245,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_thyroidectomy_airway_095","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.94","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.94.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.94.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,40],"fullStemEn":"Two hours after a thyroidectomy, a client reports neck tightness and is swallowing frequently. Place the nursing actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"甲状腺切除术后 2 小时，患者报告颈部紧绷并频繁吞咽。请按正确顺序排列护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two hours after a thyroidectomy, a client reports neck tightness and is swallowing frequently.","penultimateSentenceZh":"甲状腺切除术后 2 小时，患者报告颈部紧绷并频繁吞咽。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Document the episode and the client's response after stabilization.","zh":"患者稳定后记录事件及患者反应。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess airway, breathing, oxygen saturation, and the surgical site.","zh":"评估气道、呼吸、血氧饱和度和手术部位。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call for immediate assistance and notify the surgeon.","zh":"立即呼叫协助并通知外科医生。"},{"id":"C","en":"Keep emergency airway equipment available and prepare for prescribed intervention.","zh":"备好紧急气道设备，并准备执行医嘱干预。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Frequent swallowing and neck tightness after thyroidectomy can indicate bleeding or swelling that may compromise the airway. The nurse assesses airway and the site, gets immediate help, prepares for airway or surgical intervention, and documents after the client is stable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺切除术后频繁吞咽和颈部紧绷可能提示出血或肿胀，危及气道。护士先评估气道和伤口，再立即求助，准备气道或手术干预，患者稳定后记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After neck surgery, tightness, swelling, or frequent swallowing points to possible airway risk; assess and get help before paperwork.","testTakingStrategyZh":"颈部手术后出现紧绷、肿胀或频繁吞咽，提示气道风险；先评估和求助，再处理文书。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1246,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_post_cath_096","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.95","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.95.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.95.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,102],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,32],"fullStemEn":"A client returns from cardiac catheterization through the right femoral artery. Classify each finding.","fullStemZh":"一位患者经右股动脉行心导管检查后返回病房。请对每项发现进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each finding.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项发现进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client returns from cardiac catheterization through the right femoral artery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者经右股动脉行心导管检查后返回病房。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Small amount of bruising at the insertion site","zh":"穿刺部位少量瘀斑"},{"id":"r2","en":"Expanding firm swelling in the groin","zh":"腹股沟逐渐增大的坚硬肿胀"},{"id":"r3","en":"Pedal pulse weaker than baseline in the affected leg","zh":"患侧足背脉搏较基线减弱"},{"id":"r4","en":"Client keeps the affected leg straight while supine","zh":"患者仰卧时保持患侧腿伸直"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected or continue monitoring","zh":"预期或继续监测"},{"id":"c2","en":"Requires immediate follow-up","zh":"需要立即跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A small bruise and keeping the leg straight are expected after femoral access. Expanding swelling suggests hematoma or bleeding, and a weaker distal pulse suggests impaired perfusion; both require immediate follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"股动脉入路后少量瘀斑和保持腿伸直属于预期。逐渐增大的肿胀提示血肿或出血，远端脉搏减弱提示灌注受损；两者都需立即跟进。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After arterial procedures, worsening swelling, bleeding, or decreased distal circulation outranks stable expected findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"动脉操作后，肿胀加重、出血或远端循环下降优先于稳定的预期表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1247,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_siadh_097","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.96","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.96.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.96.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,42],"fullStemEn":"A client with a recent head injury has confusion, serum sodium 124 mEq/L, low serum osmolality, and concentrated urine.","fullStemZh":"一位近期头部损伤患者出现意识混乱，血钠 124 mEq/L，血清渗透压低，尿液浓缩。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with a recent head injury has confusion, serum sodium 124 mEq/L, low serum osmolality, and concentrated urine.","terminalSentenceZh":"一位近期头部损伤患者出现意识混乱，血钠 124 mEq/L，血清渗透压低，尿液浓缩。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is most at risk for {{1}}, and the nurse should anticipate {{2}}.","zh":"该患者最有风险发生 {{1}}，护士应预期 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"seizures from severe hyponatremia","zh":"重度低钠血症导致的癫痫发作"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypernatremic dehydration","zh":"高钠性脱水"},{"id":"o3","en":"hypovolemic shock from water loss","zh":"失水导致的低血容量性休克"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"seizure precautions and fluid restriction as prescribed","zh":"按医嘱实施癫痫预防措施和限制液体"},{"id":"o3","en":"encouraging unlimited free water intake","zh":"鼓励无限制摄入清水"},{"id":"o2","en":"rapid infusion of hypotonic IV fluids","zh":"快速输入低渗静脉液体"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Head injury can trigger SIADH, causing water retention, low serum osmolality, concentrated urine, and hyponatremia. Severe hyponatremia can cause confusion and seizures; seizure precautions and prescribed fluid restriction are expected.","rationaleCorrectZh":"头部损伤可诱发抗利尿激素分泌异常综合征，导致水潴留、血清渗透压低、尿液浓缩和低钠血症。重度低钠可导致意识混乱和癫痫发作；应预期实施癫痫预防措施和按医嘱限制液体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SIADH, connect low sodium plus concentrated urine to water retention and neurologic safety risks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"SIADH 题中，将低钠和尿液浓缩联系到水潴留及神经安全风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1248,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_lead_prevention_098","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.97","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.97.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.97.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,107],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,32],"fullStemEn":"The nurse teaches parents how to reduce a toddler's risk for lead exposure. Classify each parent statement.","fullStemZh":"护士向父母讲解如何降低幼儿铅暴露风险。请对每项父母陈述进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each parent statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项父母陈述进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse teaches parents how to reduce a toddler's risk for lead exposure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士向父母讲解如何降低幼儿铅暴露风险。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"I will dry-sweep loose paint chips from the window sill.","zh":"我会干扫窗台上脱落的油漆碎片。"},{"id":"r2","en":"I will wash my child's hands before meals and snacks.","zh":"我会在正餐和点心前给孩子洗手。"},{"id":"r3","en":"We use imported ceramic dishes to serve acidic foods.","zh":"我们用进口陶瓷餐具盛放酸性食物。"},{"id":"r4","en":"I will use cold tap water for drinking or formula after letting it run first.","zh":"我会先放一会儿水，再使用冷自来水饮用或冲配配方奶。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Shows understanding","zh":"表明理解"},{"id":"c1","en":"Needs follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lead prevention includes reducing dust ingestion, handwashing, avoiding unsafe ceramics for food, and using flushed cold water rather than hot tap water for drinking or formula.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防铅暴露包括减少含铅粉尘摄入、洗手、避免使用不安全陶瓷盛食物，以及使用先放流后的冷水而不是热自来水饮用或冲配奶粉。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For prevention teaching, separate actions that reduce exposure from actions that spread dust or introduce unsafe sources.","testTakingStrategyZh":"预防教育题中，区分降低暴露的行为和会传播粉尘或引入不安全来源的行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1249,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_vaping_counseling_099","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.98","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.98.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.98.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,43],"fullStemEn":"A 16-year-old client says, \"I vape every day, but it is not like smoking.\" The parent is in the room and begins lecturing the client.","fullStemZh":"一名 16 岁患者说：“我每天吸电子烟，但这又不是抽烟。”家长在房间里并开始训斥患者。","terminalSentenceEn":"The parent is in the room and begins lecturing the client.","terminalSentenceZh":"家长在房间里并开始训斥患者。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 16-year-old client says, \"I vape every day, but it is not like smoking.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 16 岁患者说：“我每天吸电子烟，但这又不是抽烟。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should use {{1}} and first assess {{2}}.","zh":"护士应使用 {{1}}，并首先评估 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a warning that the client is being irresponsible","zh":"警告患者其行为不负责任"},{"id":"o3","en":"education directed only to the parent","zh":"只向家长进行教育"},{"id":"o1","en":"private, nonjudgmental motivational interviewing","zh":"私下、不评判的动机性访谈"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"readiness to quit and personal triggers","zh":"戒除意愿和个人诱因"},{"id":"o2","en":"whether punishment has been severe enough","zh":"惩罚是否足够严厉"},{"id":"o3","en":"the parent's preferred discipline plan","zh":"家长偏好的管教计划"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adolescents need developmentally appropriate, confidential, nonjudgmental counseling. Motivational interviewing explores readiness, reasons for use, triggers, and realistic cessation support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"青少年需要符合发育阶段、保密且不评判的咨询。动机性访谈可探索戒除意愿、使用原因、诱因和可行的戒除支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For adolescent risk behaviors, choose privacy, rapport, and readiness assessment before advice giving.","testTakingStrategyZh":"青少年风险行为题中，先选择隐私、建立关系和评估改变意愿，再提供建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A 16-year-old client says, \"I vape every day, but it is not like smoking.\"","controlSentenceZh":"一名 16 岁患者说：“我每天吸电子烟，但这又不是抽烟。”"}
{"queueIndex":1250,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_fundal_height_100","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.99","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.99.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.99.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[145,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,45],"fullStemEn":"A pregnant client is 28 weeks' gestation. Beginning in midpregnancy, fundal height in centimeters usually approximates gestational age in weeks. About how many centimeters would the nurse expect?","fullStemZh":"一位孕妇孕 28 周。妊娠中期以后，宫底高度（厘米）通常约等于孕周。护士预期约为多少厘米？","terminalSentenceEn":"About how many centimeters would the nurse expect?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预期约为多少厘米？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Beginning in midpregnancy, fundal height in centimeters usually approximates gestational age in weeks.","penultimateSentenceZh":"妊娠中期以后，宫底高度（厘米）通常约等于孕周。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"fundal height in cm","zh":"宫底高度（厘米）"},"acceptable":["28","28 cm"],"numeric":{"value":28,"tolerance":2,"unit":"cm"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"From about 20 to 36 weeks, fundal height in centimeters is expected to roughly match gestational age in weeks. At 28 weeks, about 28 cm is expected, allowing normal variation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"约 20 至 36 孕周时，宫底高度厘米数通常大致等于孕周。孕 28 周预期约 28 cm，允许正常变异。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For fundal height after midpregnancy, match weeks to centimeters unless data suggest a complication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"妊娠中期后的宫底高度题，若无并发症线索，按孕周约等于厘米数判断。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1251,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_colonoscopy_prep_101","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.100","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.100.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.100.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,36],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for a screening colonoscopy with moderate sedation. Place the teaching points in the best sequence.","fullStemZh":"一位患者计划接受中度镇静下的筛查性结肠镜检查。请按最佳顺序排列教育要点。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the teaching points in the best sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最佳顺序排列教育要点。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is scheduled for a screening colonoscopy with moderate sedation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者计划接受中度镇静下的筛查性结肠镜检查。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Review medication instructions and the bowel-prep schedule before the procedure date.","zh":"在检查日期前复核用药说明和肠道准备时间表。"},{"id":"D","en":"Have a responsible adult available to drive home after sedation.","zh":"镇静后安排一位负责任的成年人开车送其回家。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stop oral intake for the specified time before arrival.","zh":"到达前按规定时间停止口服摄入。"},{"id":"B","en":"Follow clear-liquid and bowel-preparation instructions as prescribed.","zh":"按医嘱遵循清流质和肠道准备说明。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Preparation begins before the procedure with medication review and bowel-prep planning. The client then follows the prep, observes nothing-by-mouth timing, and must have safe transportation after sedation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"准备工作在检查前开始，包括复核用药和计划肠道准备。随后按要求准备、遵守禁食时间，并因镇静后安全需要安排交通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Sequence procedural teaching from preparation days before, to day-before prep, to day-of safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"操作前教育按时间顺序排列：提前准备、前一天准备、当天安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1252,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_newborn_weight_loss_102","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.101","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.101.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.101.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,149],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,64],"fullStemEn":"A newborn weighed 3.2 kg at birth and weighs 2.96 kg before discharge. What percent of birth weight has the newborn lost? Round to the nearest tenth.","fullStemZh":"一名新生儿出生体重 3.2 kg，出院前体重 2.96 kg。该新生儿体重下降占出生体重的百分比是多少？四舍五入到小数点后一位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest tenth.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到小数点后一位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"What percent of birth weight has the newborn lost?","penultimateSentenceZh":"该新生儿体重下降占出生体重的百分比是多少？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"percent weight loss","zh":"体重下降百分比"},"acceptable":["7.5","7.5%"],"numeric":{"value":7.5,"tolerance":0.1,"unit":"%"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Weight loss is 3.2 - 2.96 = 0.24 kg. Divide by birth weight: 0.24 / 3.2 = 0.075, or 7.5%.","rationaleCorrectZh":"体重下降为 3.2 - 2.96 = 0.24 kg。除以出生体重：0.24 / 3.2 = 0.075，即 7.5%。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For percent change, calculate the change first, then divide by the original value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"百分比变化题先算变化量，再除以原始值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
