rategyEn":"For cancer prevention, choose risk reduction and early reporting of suspicious changes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"癌症预防题选择降低风险和及早报告可疑变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1254,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_ppe_doffing_104","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.103","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.103.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.103.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is leaving the room of a client on contact precautions while wearing gloves, gown, goggles, and mask. Place the PPE-removal steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士离开一位接触隔离患者病房，身穿手套、隔离衣、护目镜和口罩。请按正确顺序排列个人防护装备脱卸步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the PPE-removal steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列个人防护装备脱卸步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is leaving the room of a client on contact precautions while wearing gloves, gown, goggles, and mask.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士离开一位接触隔离患者病房，身穿手套、隔离衣、护目镜和口罩。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Perform hand hygiene.","zh":"进行手卫生。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove gloves.","zh":"脱手套。"},{"id":"C","en":"Remove gown.","zh":"脱隔离衣。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove goggles.","zh":"脱护目镜。"},{"id":"D","en":"Remove mask.","zh":"脱口罩。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The CDC recommended standard sequence for doffing is: Gloves are removed first as they are the most contaminated. Goggles are removed next, followed by the gown and the mask. Hand hygiene (E) is performed as the final step immediately after removing all PPE.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDC 推荐的标准脱卸顺序是：手套 污染最严重，最先脱掉。接着脱掉护目镜，随后脱掉隔离衣 和口罩。脱掉所有个人防护装备后，立即进行手卫生 (E) 作为最后一步。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the standard alphabetical doffing sequence: G-G-G-M (Gloves, Goggles, Gown, Mask), followed by hand hygiene.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住标准的按字母顺序脱卸：G-G-G-M（手套 Gloves、护目镜 Goggles、隔离衣 Gown、口罩 Mask），然后进行手卫生。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1255,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_meningitis_precautions_105","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.104","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.104.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.104.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,28],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with suspected bacterial meningitis. Classify each nursing action.","fullStemZh":"一位疑似细菌性脑膜炎患者入院。请对每项护理行动进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项护理行动进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted with suspected bacterial meningitis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位疑似细菌性脑膜炎患者入院。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Place the client on droplet precautions.","zh":"对患者实施飞沫隔离。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Wear a surgical mask when providing close care.","zh":"近距离护理时佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Use only standard precautions because meningitis is not transmissible.","zh":"仅使用标准预防，因为脑膜炎不会传播。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Limit close exposure until effective therapy has been initiated per policy.","zh":"按政策在有效治疗开始前限制近距离暴露。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"},{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected bacterial meningitis requires droplet precautions in addition to standard precautions. Close-care masking and limiting exposure reduce transmission risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似细菌性脑膜炎除标准预防外还需要飞沫隔离。近距离护理佩戴口罩并限制暴露可降低传播风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match respiratory-spread infections to droplet or airborne precautions based on the route of transmission.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据传播途径，将呼吸道传播感染对应到飞沫或空气隔离。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1256,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_scabies_precautions_106","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.105","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.105.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.105.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,86],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,26],"fullStemEn":"A long-term care resident is diagnosed with scabies. Several roommates report itching.","fullStemZh":"一名长期护理机构住民被诊断为疥疮。几位室友报告瘙痒。","terminalSentenceEn":"Several roommates report itching.","terminalSentenceZh":"几位室友报告瘙痒。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A long-term care resident is diagnosed with scabies.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名长期护理机构住民被诊断为疥疮。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should initiate {{1}} and ensure {{2}}.","zh":"护士应启动 {{1}}，并确保 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"airborne precautions","zh":"空气隔离"},{"id":"o1","en":"contact precautions","zh":"接触隔离"},{"id":"o3","en":"protective isolation","zh":"保护性隔离"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"only the resident's hands are treated","zh":"只处理住民双手"},{"id":"o3","en":"roommates are ignored unless a rash is visible","zh":"除非室友出现可见皮疹，否则不予处理"},{"id":"o1","en":"close contacts and linens are managed according to policy","zh":"按政策处理密切接触者和床单衣物"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Scabies spreads through prolonged skin contact and contaminated linens or clothing. Contact precautions, treatment of affected people and close contacts per policy, and linen management reduce spread.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疥疮可通过长时间皮肤接触以及受污染床单衣物传播。接触隔离、按政策治疗患者和密切接触者，并处理床单衣物，可减少传播。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For skin infestations, think contact spread plus treatment and environmental handling.","testTakingStrategyZh":"皮肤寄生感染题中，考虑接触传播、治疗和环境物品处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1257,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_handwashing_time_107","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.106","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.106.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.106.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"The nurse teaches a client to scrub hands with soap and water for at least how many seconds?","fullStemZh":"护士教育患者用肥皂和清水搓洗双手至少多少秒？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse teaches a client to scrub hands with soap and water for at least how many seconds?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士教育患者用肥皂和清水搓洗双手至少多少秒？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"seconds","zh":"秒"},"acceptable":["20","20 seconds"],"numeric":{"value":20,"tolerance":0,"unit":"seconds"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective handwashing teaching commonly includes scrubbing all hand surfaces with soap and water for at least 20 seconds before rinsing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效洗手教育通常包括用肥皂和清水搓洗手部所有表面至少 20 秒后再冲洗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For infection-control teaching, know common minimums such as 20 seconds for soap-and-water handwashing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"感染控制教育题要掌握常见最低标准，如肥皂和清水洗手至少 20 秒。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1258,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_norovirus_outbreak_108","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.107","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.107.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.107.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,31],"fullStemEn":"Several clients on a unit develop sudden vomiting and watery diarrhea. Place the nurse's actions in the best order.","fullStemZh":"病区多名患者突然出现呕吐和水样腹泻。请按最佳顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the best order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最佳顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Several clients on a unit develop sudden vomiting and watery diarrhea.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区多名患者突然出现呕吐和水样腹泻。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Assess affected clients for dehydration and instability.","zh":"评估受影响患者是否脱水或不稳定。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify infection prevention according to facility policy.","zh":"按机构政策通知感染预防部门。"},{"id":"D","en":"Coordinate environmental cleaning with an appropriate disinfectant.","zh":"协调使用合适消毒剂进行环境清洁。"},{"id":"B","en":"Institute contact precautions and reinforce soap-and-water hand hygiene.","zh":"实施接触隔离并强化肥皂和清水手卫生。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Client stability is assessed first. Rapid isolation and hand hygiene reduce spread, infection prevention is notified, and environmental cleaning helps control the outbreak.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先评估患者是否稳定。快速隔离和手卫生可减少传播，随后通知感染预防部门，并通过环境清洁控制暴发。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In outbreak questions, assess safety, isolate, notify infection prevention, then coordinate environmental control.","testTakingStrategyZh":"暴发题按顺序考虑：评估安全、隔离、通知感染预防，再协调环境控制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1259,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_chemical_splash_109","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.108","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.108.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.108.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,77],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,27],"fullStemEn":"A cleaning chemical splashes into a staff member's eye. Classify each action.","fullStemZh":"清洁化学品溅入一名工作人员眼睛。请对每项行动进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项行动进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A cleaning chemical splashes into a staff member's eye.","penultimateSentenceZh":"清洁化学品溅入一名工作人员眼睛。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Begin flushing the eye at the eyewash station immediately.","zh":"立即在洗眼器处冲洗眼睛。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Remove contact lenses if present and easy to remove during irrigation.","zh":"冲洗时如戴隐形眼镜且易取出，应将其取下。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Wait to irrigate until the exact chemical is identified.","zh":"等确认具体化学品后再冲洗。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Report the exposure and seek occupational health evaluation.","zh":"报告暴露并接受职业健康评估。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Chemical eye exposure requires immediate irrigation. Identification and reporting are important, but irrigation should not be delayed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"化学品眼部暴露需要立即冲洗。确认化学品和报告很重要，但不能延误冲洗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For chemical exposure, immediate decontamination comes before investigation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"化学暴露题中，立即去污染先于调查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1260,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_telephone_order_110","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.109","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.109.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.109.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[53,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,31],"fullStemEn":"A provider gives a telephone order for a medication. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"医疗提供者通过电话下达一项用药医嘱。请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider gives a telephone order for a medication.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医疗提供者通过电话下达一项用药医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Read back the medication, dose, route, frequency, and client identifiers.","zh":"回读药物、剂量、途径、频率和患者身份信息。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain confirmation from the provider.","zh":"获得医疗提供者确认。"},{"id":"A","en":"Write down the complete order while it is being given.","zh":"医嘱下达时完整记录。"},{"id":"D","en":"Enter or document the order according to policy.","zh":"按政策录入或记录医嘱。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Telephone orders require writing the complete order, reading it back, receiving confirmation, and documenting or entering it according to policy before implementation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"电话医嘱需要完整记录、回读、获得确认，并按政策记录或录入后再执行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For verbal or telephone orders, prioritize write-down, read-back, confirmation, and policy-based documentation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"口头或电话医嘱题优先考虑记录、回读、确认和按政策记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1261,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_float_assignment_111","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.110","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.110.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.110.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,29],"fullStemEn":"A medical-surgical nurse is floated to the postpartum unit. Which assignments are appropriate for this nurse?","fullStemZh":"一名内外科护士被调派到产后病区。哪些工作适合分配给该护士？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which assignments are appropriate for this nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪些工作适合分配给该护士？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A medical-surgical nurse is floated to the postpartum unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名内外科护士被调派到产后病区。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Care for a stable postoperative client awaiting discharge teaching already completed by the postpartum nurse.","zh":"照护一位病情稳定、产后护士已完成出院教育的术后患者。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Independently assess a newborn with grunting respirations.","zh":"独立评估一名出现呻吟样呼吸的新生儿。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Take routine vital signs for a stable parent while unit staff assess the newborn.","zh":"在本病区人员评估新生儿时，为稳定产妇测量常规生命体征。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Provide initial breastfeeding teaching to a first-time parent.","zh":"为初产妇提供首次母乳喂养教育。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Keep with experienced postpartum staff","zh":"应由有经验的产后护士负责"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate assignment","zh":"合适分配"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Floating nurses should receive assignments consistent with their competency. Stable routine adult care may be appropriate; unstable newborn assessment and specialty teaching require experienced postpartum staff.","rationaleCorrectZh":"调派护士应接受与其能力相符的任务。稳定、常规成人照护可能合适；不稳定新生儿评估和专科教育应由有经验的产后护士负责。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For floating staff, match assignments to demonstrated competency and keep unstable or specialty needs with trained staff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"调派人员题中，将任务与已具备能力匹配，不稳定或专科需求留给受训人员。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1262,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_ama_discharge_112","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.111","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.111.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.111.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,26],"fullStemEn":"A client with chest pain says, \"I am leaving now. I do not care what the provider says.\"","fullStemZh":"一位胸痛患者说：“我现在就要走。我不管医生怎么说。”","terminalSentenceEn":"I do not care what the provider says.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"我不管医生怎么说。”","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with chest pain says, \"I am leaving now.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位胸痛患者说：“我现在就要走。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first {{1}} and then {{2}}.","zh":"护士首先应 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"assess decision-making capacity and reasons for leaving","zh":"评估决策能力和离院原因"},{"id":"o2","en":"lock the exit door to prevent departure","zh":"锁住出口防止离开"},{"id":"o3","en":"remove the call light because the client is refusing care","zh":"因患者拒绝护理而移除呼叫铃"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"document only that the client was difficult","zh":"只记录患者难以合作"},{"id":"o1","en":"notify the provider and explain risks, alternatives, and return precautions","zh":"通知医疗提供者，并说明风险、替代方案和返院注意事项"},{"id":"o2","en":"ask security to restrain the competent client","zh":"要求保安约束有决策能力的患者"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A competent adult may refuse care, but the nurse must assess capacity, explore concerns, notify the provider, teach risks and return precautions, and document objective facts.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有决策能力的成年人可以拒绝治疗，但护士必须评估能力、了解顾虑、通知医疗提供者、说明风险和返院注意事项，并客观记录事实。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For refusal of care, preserve autonomy while assessing capacity, safety, teaching, notification, and documentation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"拒绝治疗题中，尊重自主权，同时评估能力、安全、教育、通知和记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1263,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_organ_donation_referral_113","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.112","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.112.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.112.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,37],"fullStemEn":"A client with a severe brain injury meets facility triggers for organ-donation referral. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一位严重脑损伤患者符合机构器官捐献转介触发条件。请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a severe brain injury meets facility triggers for organ-donation referral.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位严重脑损伤患者符合机构器官捐献转介触发条件。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Contact the organ-procurement organization as required by policy.","zh":"按政策要求联系器官获取组织。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the charge nurse and provider according to policy.","zh":"按政策通知责任护士和医疗提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Allow trained personnel to approach the family about donation.","zh":"由受训人员与家属沟通捐献事宜。"},{"id":"A","en":"Continue prescribed care to maintain physiologic stability.","zh":"继续按医嘱护理以维持生理稳定。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse maintains client stability, follows facility notification policy, makes the required referral, and allows trained organ-donation personnel to discuss donation with the family.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先维持患者稳定，按机构政策通知相关人员，完成所需转介，并由受训的器官捐献人员与家属讨论捐献。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For organ donation, maintain care, follow policy, refer early, and do not personally request donation unless trained and authorized.","testTakingStrategyZh":"器官捐献题中，维持照护、遵循政策、早期转介；未经培训和授权不要自行请求捐献。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with a severe brain injury meets facility triggers for organ-donation referral.","controlSentenceZh":"一位严重脑损伤患者符合机构器官捐献转介触发条件。"}
{"queueIndex":1264,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_chain_of_command_114","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.113","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.113.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.113.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[48,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse questions an order that appears unsafe. The provider says, \"Just give it,\" and refuses to discuss the concern.","fullStemZh":"护士质疑一项看似不安全的医嘱。医疗提供者说：“照做就行”，并拒绝讨论该顾虑。","terminalSentenceEn":"The provider says, \"Just give it,\" and refuses to discuss the concern.","terminalSentenceZh":"医疗提供者说：“照做就行”，并拒绝讨论该顾虑。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse questions an order that appears unsafe.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士质疑一项看似不安全的医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{1}} because the nurse's priority is {{2}}.","zh":"护士应 {{1}}，因为护士的优先事项是 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"ask the family to decide whether the order is safe","zh":"请家属决定医嘱是否安全"},{"id":"o2","en":"administer the medication to avoid conflict","zh":"为避免冲突而给药"},{"id":"o1","en":"hold the order and use the chain of command","zh":"暂缓执行医嘱并启动逐级上报"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"protecting the provider from questions","zh":"保护医疗提供者不被质疑"},{"id":"o1","en":"client safety and advocacy","zh":"患者安全和倡导"},{"id":"o3","en":"finishing tasks quickly","zh":"快速完成任务"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A nurse must not carry out an order believed to be unsafe. If direct clarification fails, the nurse follows the chain of command while protecting the client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士不能执行其认为不安全的医嘱。若直接澄清失败，护士应按逐级上报流程处理，同时保护患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an order seems unsafe, clarify first; if unresolved, escalate through chain of command.","testTakingStrategyZh":"医嘱看似不安全时，先澄清；若未解决，按逐级上报处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1265,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_mania_safety_115","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.114","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.114.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.114.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,44],"fullStemEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is pacing, talking rapidly, and has slept 2 hours in 3 days. The client is intrusive with peers and refuses meals.","fullStemZh":"一位双相障碍患者来回踱步、语速很快，3 天只睡了 2 小时。患者不断打扰同伴并拒绝进食。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client is intrusive with peers and refuses meals.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者不断打扰同伴并拒绝进食。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with bipolar disorder is pacing, talking rapidly, and has slept 2 hours in 3 days.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位双相障碍患者来回踱步、语速很快，3 天只睡了 2 小时。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should provide {{1}} and offer {{2}}.","zh":"护士应提供 {{1}}，并提供 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a loud group activity to use excess energy","zh":"大声的团体活动以消耗过剩精力"},{"id":"o1","en":"a low-stimulation environment with clear limits","zh":"低刺激环境和明确界限"},{"id":"o3","en":"lengthy confrontation about behavior","zh":"长时间对质其行为"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"caffeinated drinks to prevent fatigue","zh":"含咖啡因饮料以预防疲劳"},{"id":"o1","en":"high-calorie finger foods and fluids","zh":"高热量手拿食物和液体"},{"id":"o2","en":"a large meal requiring prolonged sitting","zh":"需要长时间坐着吃的大餐"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mania care focuses on safety, reduced stimulation, simple limits, rest, hydration, and nutrition. Portable high-calorie foods are more realistic than long meals.","rationaleCorrectZh":"躁狂护理重点是安全、减少刺激、简单界限、休息、补液和营养。便于拿取的高热量食物比长时间进餐更现实。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For mania, choose safety, low stimulation, short interactions, and practical nutrition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"躁狂题选择安全、低刺激、简短互动和实际可行的营养支持。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1266,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_ptsd_care_116","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.115","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.115.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.115.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,32],"fullStemEn":"A client with posttraumatic stress disorder is admitted for medical care. Classify each nursing approach.","fullStemZh":"一位创伤后应激障碍患者因躯体疾病入院。请对每种护理方式进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing approach.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每种护理方式进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with posttraumatic stress disorder is admitted for medical care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位创伤后应激障碍患者因躯体疾病入院。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Explain procedures before touching the client.","zh":"触碰患者前解释操作。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Offer choices when possible, such as timing for hygiene.","zh":"尽可能提供选择，例如个人卫生的时间。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Stand between the client and the door during all conversations.","zh":"每次谈话都站在患者和门之间。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Ask what helps the client feel safe during care.","zh":"询问护理过程中什么能帮助患者感到安全。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"May increase distress","zh":"可能增加痛苦"},{"id":"c1","en":"Trauma-informed","zh":"创伤知情"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Trauma-informed care emphasizes safety, predictability, choice, collaboration, and avoiding powerlessness. Blocking the exit can increase distress.","rationaleCorrectZh":"创伤知情护理强调安全、可预期、选择、合作，并避免让患者感到无助。挡住出口可能增加痛苦。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For trauma histories, choose safety, choice, explanation, and collaboration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有创伤史题选择安全、选择、解释和合作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1267,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_or_deescalation_117","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.116","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Mental Health Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.116.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.116.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,39],"fullStemEn":"A client becomes increasingly agitated, clenches fists, and says, \"Everyone needs to leave me alone.\" Place the nurse's actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一位患者越来越激动，握紧拳头并说：“所有人都别来烦我。”请按顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client becomes increasingly agitated, clenches fists, and says, \"Everyone needs to leave me alone.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者越来越激动，握紧拳头并说：“所有人都别来烦我。”","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Set clear limits and offer simple choices.","zh":"设定清楚界限并提供简单选择。"},{"id":"D","en":"Call for additional help if the client cannot regain control.","zh":"若患者无法恢复控制，呼叫额外协助。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use a calm voice and maintain a nonthreatening distance.","zh":"用平静语气并保持不具威胁性的距离。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ensure a safe exit route and reduce environmental stimulation.","zh":"确保安全退路并减少环境刺激。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first protects safety and reduces stimulation, then uses calm communication, sets limits with choices, and seeks help if escalation continues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先保护安全并减少刺激，然后使用平静沟通，设定界限并提供选择；若持续升级则寻求协助。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For agitation, start with staff safety and least restrictive de-escalation before emergency interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"激动题先考虑人员安全和最少限制的降级措施，再考虑紧急干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1268,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_postpartum_depression_118","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.117","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.117.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.117.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,43],"fullStemEn":"A client who gave birth 3 weeks ago says, \"I cry every day. I cannot sleep even when the baby sleeps, and my family would be better without me.\"","fullStemZh":"一位产后 3 周的患者说：“我每天都哭。宝宝睡着时我也睡不着，而且家人没有我会更好。”","terminalSentenceEn":"I cannot sleep even when the baby sleeps, and my family would be better without me.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"宝宝睡着时我也睡不着，而且家人没有我会更好。”","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who gave birth 3 weeks ago says, \"I cry every day.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位产后 3 周的患者说：“我每天都哭。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first assess for {{1}} and then {{2}}.","zh":"护士首先应评估 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"suicidal thoughts and infant safety","zh":"自杀想法和婴儿安全"},{"id":"o2","en":"normal postpartum blues only","zh":"仅为正常产后情绪低落"},{"id":"o3","en":"the client's preferred exercise routine","zh":"患者偏好的运动计划"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"reassure the client that symptoms will resolve without assessment","zh":"安慰患者症状会自行缓解而无需评估"},{"id":"o3","en":"schedule routine follow-up in 6 months","zh":"安排 6 个月后的常规随访"},{"id":"o1","en":"notify the provider and connect the client with urgent mental health support","zh":"通知医疗提供者并为患者连接紧急心理健康支持"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Persistent crying, insomnia, and a statement that others would be better without the client are concerning for postpartum depression with possible suicidal ideation. Immediate safety assessment and urgent referral are required.","rationaleCorrectZh":"持续哭泣、失眠以及“家人没有我会更好”的表述提示产后抑郁并可能有自杀意念。需要立即进行安全评估并紧急转介。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Postpartum mood symptoms plus hopeless or self-harm statements require immediate safety assessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产后情绪症状加绝望或自伤表述时，需要立即安全评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1269,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_fluid_weight_gain_119","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.118","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.118.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.118.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[35,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,70],"fullStemEn":"A client gains 4.4 lb in 24 hours. Using 2.2 lb as approximately 1 kg and 1 kg as approximately 1 L of fluid, about how many liters of fluid has the client retained?","fullStemZh":"一位患者 24 小时内体重增加 4.4 lb。按 2.2 lb 约等于 1 kg，1 kg 约等于 1 L 液体计算，患者约潴留多少升液体？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using 2.2 lb as approximately 1 kg and 1 kg as approximately 1 L of fluid, about how many liters of fluid has the client retained?","terminalSentenceZh":"按 2.2 lb 约等于 1 kg，1 kg 约等于 1 L 液体计算，患者约潴留多少升液体？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client gains 4.4 lb in 24 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者 24 小时内体重增加 4.4 lb。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"liters retained","zh":"潴留升数"},"acceptable":["2","2 L","2 liters"],"numeric":{"value":2,"tolerance":0.1,"unit":"L"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Divide 4.4 lb by 2.2 lb/kg = 2 kg. Each kilogram of acute weight gain approximates 1 L of retained fluid, so the gain is about 2 L.","rationaleCorrectZh":"4.4 lb 除以 2.2 lb/kg = 2 kg。急性体重每增加 1 kg 约等于潴留 1 L 液体，因此约为 2 L。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For acute fluid weight changes, 1 kg approximates 1 liter of fluid.","testTakingStrategyZh":"急性液体相关体重变化题中，1 kg 约等于 1 L 液体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1270,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_matrix_constipation_prevention_120","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.119","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.119.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.119.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,24],"fullStemEn":"The nurse teaches a client how to prevent constipation. Classify each statement.","fullStemZh":"护士教育患者如何预防便秘。请对每项陈述进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项陈述进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse teaches a client how to prevent constipation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士教育患者如何预防便秘。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"I will increase fluids and fiber if not restricted.","zh":"若未受限制，我会增加液体和膳食纤维。"},{"id":"r2","en":"I will ignore the urge to have a bowel movement until bedtime.","zh":"我会忍到睡前再排便。"},{"id":"r3","en":"I will walk daily as tolerated.","zh":"我会在能耐受的情况下每天步行。"},{"id":"r4","en":"I will ask about stool softeners if I start opioid pain medicine.","zh":"如果开始使用阿片类止痛药，我会询问是否需要大便软化剂。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Needs follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Helpful prevention","zh":"有助于预防"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Constipation prevention includes fluids, fiber, activity, responding to the urge to defecate, and anticipating opioid-related constipation when applicable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防便秘包括摄入液体和纤维、活动、及时回应便意，以及在使用阿片类药物时预防相关便秘。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For constipation prevention, choose hydration, fiber, mobility, timely toileting, and opioid planning.","testTakingStrategyZh":"预防便秘题选择补液、纤维、活动、及时如厕和阿片用药计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1271,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_cloze_sleep_hygiene_121","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.120","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.120.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.120.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,117],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,36],"fullStemEn":"An older adult reports difficulty sleeping. The client naps for 3 hours each afternoon and drinks coffee with dinner.","fullStemZh":"一位老年患者报告睡眠困难。患者每天下午午睡 3 小时，并在晚餐时喝咖啡。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client naps for 3 hours each afternoon and drinks coffee with dinner.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者每天下午午睡 3 小时，并在晚餐时喝咖啡。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An older adult reports difficulty sleeping.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位老年患者报告睡眠困难。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recommend {{1}} and {{2}}.","zh":"护士应建议 {{1}} 和 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"staying in bed all day to rest","zh":"整天卧床休息"},{"id":"o1","en":"limiting long daytime naps","zh":"限制白天长时间午睡"},{"id":"o2","en":"sleeping several extra hours during the day","zh":"白天多睡几个小时"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"using alcohol as a sleep aid","zh":"用酒精助眠"},{"id":"o1","en":"avoiding caffeine in the evening","zh":"晚间避免咖啡因"},{"id":"o2","en":"drinking coffee to relax before sleep","zh":"睡前喝咖啡放松"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sleep hygiene includes limiting long daytime naps and avoiding evening caffeine. Alcohol and prolonged daytime bed rest can worsen sleep quality.","rationaleCorrectZh":"睡眠卫生包括限制白天长时间午睡和晚间避免咖啡因。酒精和白天长时间卧床可能恶化睡眠质量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sleep hygiene, remove stimulants and strengthen the day-night routine.","testTakingStrategyZh":"睡眠卫生题中，去除刺激因素并强化昼夜规律。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1272,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_canonical_fib_calorie_intake_122","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.121","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.121.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.121.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[71,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,47],"fullStemEn":"A client on a calorie count eats 75% of a meal that contains 600 kcal. How many kcal should the nurse record?","fullStemZh":"一位患者正在进行热量记录，进食了一餐 600 kcal 的 75%。护士应记录多少 kcal？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many kcal should the nurse record?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录多少 kcal？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client on a calorie count eats 75% of a meal that contains 600 kcal.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一位患者正在进行热量记录，进食了一餐 600 kcal 的 75%。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"kcal consumed","zh":"摄入千卡"},"acceptable":["450","450 kcal"],"numeric":{"value":450,"tolerance":0,"unit":"kcal"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Multiply the meal calories by the portion eaten: 600 kcal x 0.75 = 450 kcal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"将餐食热量乘以进食比例：600 kcal x 0.75 = 450 kcal。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For percent consumed, convert the percent to a decimal and multiply by the total.","testTakingStrategyZh":"摄入百分比题中，将百分比转换为小数再乘以总量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1273,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_vancomycin_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.122","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.122.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.122.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[121,251],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,73],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving IV vancomycin for methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus pneumonia. The next dose is due now. For each finding, select whether the nurse should continue routine monitoring or hold the dose and notify the provider/pharmacist.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因耐甲氧西林金黄色葡萄球菌肺炎正在接受静脉万古霉素治疗。下一剂现在应给药。请判断每项发现是继续常规监测，还是应暂缓给药并通知医嘱者/药师。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether the nurse should continue routine monitoring or hold the dose and notify the provider/pharmacist.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是继续常规监测，还是应暂缓给药并通知医嘱者/药师。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The next dose is due now.","penultimateSentenceZh":"下一剂现在应给药。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Vancomycin trough concentration is 28 mcg/mL.","zh":"万古霉素谷浓度为 28 mcg/mL。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Serum creatinine increased from 0.8 mg/dL to 1.7 mg/dL in 48 hours.","zh":"血清肌酐在 48 小时内从 0.8 mg/dL 升至 1.7 mg/dL。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The client reports new ringing in the ears and dizziness.","zh":"患者新出现耳鸣和头晕。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client reports mild nausea after the previous dose but is drinking fluids.","zh":"患者上一次给药后有轻微恶心，但仍能饮水。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Infusion site is soft, dry, and without redness or swelling.","zh":"输液部位柔软、干燥，无发红或肿胀。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Continue routine monitoring","zh":"继续常规监测"},{"id":"c2","en":"Hold dose and notify provider/pharmacist","zh":"暂缓给药并通知医嘱者/药师"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"High vancomycin concentrations, acute kidney injury, and new ototoxic symptoms require follow-up before another dose. Mild nausea and a normal IV site do not by themselves require holding the medication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"万古霉素浓度过高、急性肾损伤以及新的耳毒性症状都需要在下一剂前跟进。轻微恶心和正常的静脉输液部位本身并不需要暂停用药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For medication-monitoring matrices, separate expected side effects from findings that indicate organ toxicity or unsafe drug levels.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做药物监测类矩阵题时，要区分一般可预期副作用与提示器官毒性或药物浓度不安全的发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1274,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_infection_precautions_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.123","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.123.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.123.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,38],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse is assigning rooms for newly admitted clients. For each client, select the most appropriate infection-control precaution category.","fullStemZh":"主管护士正在为新入院患者安排病房。请为每位患者选择最合适的感染控制隔离类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client, select the most appropriate infection-control precaution category.","terminalSentenceZh":"请为每位患者选择最合适的感染控制隔离类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse is assigning rooms for newly admitted clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"主管护士正在为新入院患者安排病房。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Client with disseminated varicella-zoster lesions","zh":"有播散性水痘-带状疱疹皮损的患者"},{"id":"r2","en":"Client with suspected pertussis and severe coughing spells","zh":"疑似百日咳并有严重阵发性咳嗽的患者"},{"id":"r3","en":"Client with Clostridioides difficile diarrhea","zh":"艰难梭菌感染导致腹泻的患者"},{"id":"r4","en":"Client receiving induction chemotherapy with severe neutropenia","zh":"正在接受诱导化疗且严重中性粒细胞减少的患者"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Contact precautions","zh":"接触隔离"},{"id":"c1","en":"Airborne and Contact precautions","zh":"空气传播隔离和接触隔离"},{"id":"c2","en":"Droplet precautions","zh":"飞沫隔离"},{"id":"c4","en":"Protective/neutropenic precautions","zh":"保护性/中性粒细胞减少隔离"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Precautions are selected by transmission route and host vulnerability: disseminated varicella requires airborne and contact precautions, pertussis requires droplet precautions, C. difficile requires contact precautions, and severe neutropenia requires protective measures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"隔离方式取决于传播途径和宿主易感性：播散性水痘-带状疱疹需空气传播和接触隔离；百日咳需飞沫隔离；艰难梭菌需接触隔离；严重中性粒细胞减少需保护性措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Ask whether the nurse is protecting others from the client's organism or protecting the client from the environment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断护理目标是保护他人免受患者病原体影响，还是保护患者免受环境中的病原体影响。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1275,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_post_thyroidectomy_complications_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.124","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.124.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.124.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[57,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,48],"fullStemEn":"A client is 6 hours postoperative after a thyroidectomy. For each finding, select whether it is an expected postoperative finding or a potential complication requiring prompt action.","fullStemZh":"一名患者甲状腺切除术后 6 小时。请判断每项发现是预期的术后表现，还是需要迅速处理的潜在并发症。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is an expected postoperative finding or a potential complication requiring prompt action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是预期的术后表现，还是需要迅速处理的潜在并发症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is 6 hours postoperative after a thyroidectomy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者甲状腺切除术后 6 小时。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Mild sore throat after endotracheal intubation","zh":"气管插管后轻微咽喉痛"},{"id":"r2","en":"Inspiratory stridor with increasing work of breathing","zh":"吸气性喉鸣并呼吸费力加重"},{"id":"r3","en":"Perioral tingling and hand spasms","zh":"口周麻刺感和手部痉挛"},{"id":"r4","en":"Small amount of dry serosanguineous drainage on the dressing","zh":"敷料上有少量干燥的浆液血性渗液"},{"id":"r5","en":"Neck swelling with a feeling of tightness at the incision","zh":"颈部肿胀并感觉切口处紧绷"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Potential complication requiring prompt action","zh":"需迅速处理的潜在并发症"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected postoperative finding","zh":"预期术后表现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Airway compromise, hypocalcemia, and neck hematoma are priority complications after thyroidectomy. Mild throat discomfort and scant dry drainage can be expected early postoperative findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺切除术后优先关注气道受压、低钙血症和颈部血肿。轻微咽喉不适和少量干燥渗液可为术后早期预期表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After neck surgery, treat airway symptoms and expanding swelling as unstable until proven otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"颈部手术后，凡有气道症状或进行性肿胀，都应先视为不稳定情况。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1276,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_delegation_scope_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.125","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.125.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.125.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,33],"fullStemEn":"The RN is coordinating care on a medical-surgical unit. For each task, select the most appropriate team member assignment.","fullStemZh":"注册护士正在内外科病区协调护理。请为每项任务选择最合适的团队成员。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each task, select the most appropriate team member assignment.","terminalSentenceZh":"请为每项任务选择最合适的团队成员。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The RN is coordinating care on a medical-surgical unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"注册护士正在内外科病区协调护理。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Ambulate a stable postoperative client who walked twice yesterday.","zh":"协助一名稳定的术后患者下床行走，该患者昨天已行走两次。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Administer a scheduled oral antibiotic to a stable client.","zh":"给一名稳定患者按时服用口服抗生素。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Perform the initial assessment of a client reporting new chest pressure.","zh":"对报告新发胸部压迫感的患者进行首次评估。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Reinforce already-taught crutch-walking instructions for a stable client.","zh":"对已接受过教学的稳定患者强化拐杖行走指导。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Develop the discharge teaching plan for a new heart failure diagnosis.","zh":"为新诊断心力衰竭的患者制定出院教学计划。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Delegate to UAP","zh":"委派给无证辅助人员"},{"id":"c2","en":"Assign to LPN/VN","zh":"分配给执照实践/职业护士"},{"id":"c3","en":"RN responsibility","zh":"注册护士职责"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"UAPs can perform routine tasks for stable clients. LPN/VNs can provide medications and reinforce teaching for stable clients, while the RN retains initial assessment, clinical judgment, and care-planning responsibilities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无证辅助人员可为稳定患者执行常规任务。执照实践/职业护士可为稳定患者给药并强化教学；首次评估、临床判断和护理计划制定仍属于注册护士职责。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Delegate predictable tasks for stable clients; keep assessment, new teaching, evaluation, and unstable changes with the RN.","testTakingStrategyZh":"稳定患者的可预测任务可以委派；评估、新教学、评价和不稳定变化应由注册护士负责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1277,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_respiratory_deterioration_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.126","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.126.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.126.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,239],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,73],"fullStemEn":"A client with a COPD exacerbation is receiving bronchodilators and controlled oxygen therapy. For each assessment finding, select whether it indicates concerning respiratory deterioration or can be monitored as less urgent in this context.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性阻塞性肺疾病急性加重患者正在接受支气管扩张剂和控制性氧疗。请判断每项评估发现是提示呼吸状况恶化，还是在此情境下可作为较不紧急情况继续监测。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, select whether it indicates concerning respiratory deterioration or can be monitored as less urgent in this context.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项评估发现是提示呼吸状况恶化，还是在此情境下可作为较不紧急情况继续监测。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a COPD exacerbation is receiving bronchodilators and controlled oxygen therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名慢性阻塞性肺疾病急性加重患者正在接受支气管扩张剂和控制性氧疗。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"New confusion and increasing restlessness","zh":"新发意识混乱并越来越躁动"},{"id":"r2","en":"Oxygen saturation 90% on prescribed low-flow oxygen, with the client speaking in full sentences","zh":"按医嘱低流量吸氧时血氧饱和度 90%，患者能完整说句子"},{"id":"r3","en":"Arterial blood gas shows pH 7.25 and PaCO2 68 mm Hg, worse than baseline","zh":"动脉血气显示 pH 7.25、PaCO2 68 mm Hg，较基线恶化"},{"id":"r4","en":"Productive cough with scattered expiratory wheezes","zh":"有痰咳嗽并散在呼气性哮鸣音"},{"id":"r5","en":"Marked accessory muscle use with minimal breath sounds","zh":"明显使用辅助呼吸肌且呼吸音很弱"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Less urgent; continue monitoring","zh":"较不紧急；继续监测"},{"id":"c1","en":"Concerning respiratory deterioration","zh":"提示呼吸状况恶化"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mental status change, worsening respiratory acidosis, and signs of exhaustion or poor air movement suggest impending respiratory failure. A saturation near the ordered COPD target with full sentences and a productive wheezy cough can be monitored while treatment continues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"意识状态改变、呼吸性酸中毒加重以及疲劳或空气流动差的表现提示可能发生呼吸衰竭。若血氧接近 COPD 医嘱目标、能完整说话，或有痰咳嗽伴哮鸣音，可在治疗继续进行时监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not rank a single oxygen number alone; pair it with mental status, work of breathing, air movement, and blood gas trends.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只凭一个血氧数值排序；要结合意识状态、呼吸做功、空气流动和血气趋势。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1278,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_lithium_toxicity_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.127","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.127.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.127.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,47],"fullStemEn":"A client taking lithium for bipolar disorder reports vomiting, diarrhea, coarse hand tremor, unsteady gait, and slurred speech. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名因双相障碍服用锂盐的患者报告呕吐、腹泻、手部粗大震颤、步态不稳和言语含糊。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client taking lithium for bipolar disorder reports vomiting, diarrhea, coarse hand tremor, unsteady gait, and slurred speech.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因双相障碍服用锂盐的患者报告呕吐、腹泻、手部粗大震颤、步态不稳和言语含糊。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first {{1}} and anticipate obtaining a {{2}} because {{3}} can increase lithium concentration.","zh":"护士应首先 {{1}}，并预计需要检查 {{2}}，因为 {{3}} 可使锂盐浓度升高。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"give the next dose with food","zh":"将下一剂与食物同服"},{"id":"o1","en":"hold the lithium and notify the provider","zh":"暂缓锂盐并通知医嘱者"},{"id":"o3","en":"encourage the client to take an extra dose after vomiting","zh":"鼓励患者呕吐后补服一剂"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"serum digoxin level","zh":"血清地高辛浓度"},{"id":"o3","en":"prothrombin time","zh":"凝血酶原时间"},{"id":"o1","en":"serum lithium level","zh":"血清锂浓度"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a high-protein meal","zh":"高蛋白饮食"},{"id":"o1","en":"sodium and fluid loss","zh":"钠和水分丢失"},{"id":"o3","en":"use of an inhaled bronchodilator","zh":"使用吸入性支气管扩张剂"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Vomiting, diarrhea, coarse tremor, ataxia, and slurred speech are concerning for lithium toxicity. The nurse should hold lithium, notify the provider, and anticipate a serum lithium level because dehydration and sodium loss increase lithium reabsorption.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呕吐、腹泻、粗大震颤、共济失调和言语含糊提示锂中毒。护士应暂缓锂盐、通知医嘱者，并预计检查血清锂浓度，因为脱水和钠丢失会增加锂的重吸收。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a narrow-therapeutic-index medication has neurologic symptoms plus dehydration, think toxicity and hold the medication before more doses are given.","testTakingStrategyZh":"窄治疗指数药物若出现神经症状并伴脱水，要想到中毒，并在继续给药前先暂缓药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1279,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_adrenal_crisis_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.128","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.128.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.128.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[193,224],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,78],"fullStemEn":"A client who stopped long-term prednisone abruptly is brought to the emergency department with severe weakness, vomiting, blood pressure 82/46 mm Hg, sodium 128 mEq/L, and potassium 5.8 mEq/L. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名长期服用泼尼松后突然停药的患者因严重乏力、呕吐被送至急诊，血压 82/46 mm Hg，钠 128 mEq/L，钾 5.8 mEq/L。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who stopped long-term prednisone abruptly is brought to the emergency department with severe weakness, vomiting, blood pressure 82/46 mm Hg, sodium 128 mEq/L, and potassium 5.8 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名长期服用泼尼松后突然停药的患者因严重乏力、呕吐被送至急诊，血压 82/46 mm Hg，钠 128 mEq/L，钾 5.8 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is most likely experiencing {{1}}; the nurse should anticipate administering {{2}} and closely monitor for {{3}}.","zh":"该患者最可能正在发生 {{1}}；护士应预计给予 {{2}}，并密切监测 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"thyroid storm","zh":"甲状腺危象"},{"id":"o1","en":"adrenal crisis","zh":"肾上腺危象"},{"id":"o3","en":"syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion","zh":"抗利尿激素分泌不当综合征"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"fluid restriction and demeclocycline","zh":"限制液体和地美环素"},{"id":"o1","en":"IV hydrocortisone and isotonic fluids as prescribed","zh":"按医嘱给予静脉氢化可的松和等渗液"},{"id":"o2","en":"levothyroxine and cooling measures","zh":"左甲状腺素和降温措施"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"dysrhythmias related to hyperkalemia","zh":"与高钾血症相关的心律失常"},{"id":"o3","en":"respiratory alkalosis from hyperventilation","zh":"过度通气导致的呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"o2","en":"hypocalcemic tetany","zh":"低钙性手足搐搦"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abrupt withdrawal of long-term corticosteroids can precipitate adrenal crisis with hypotension, vomiting, hyponatremia, and hyperkalemia. Treatment includes corticosteroid replacement and volume support; hyperkalemia can cause dangerous dysrhythmias.","rationaleCorrectZh":"长期糖皮质激素突然停用可诱发肾上腺危象，表现为低血压、呕吐、低钠和高钾。治疗包括补充糖皮质激素和容量支持；高钾可导致危险心律失常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link endocrine emergencies to the missing hormone: cortisol deficiency causes vascular collapse, sodium loss, and potassium retention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将内分泌急症与缺乏的激素联系起来：皮质醇缺乏会导致血管性循环崩溃、钠丢失和钾潴留。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1280,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_rhabdomyolysis_aki_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.129","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.129.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.129.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,53],"fullStemEn":"A client with a crush injury has severe muscle pain, tea-colored urine, creatine kinase 18,000 U/L, and rising serum creatinine. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名挤压伤患者出现严重肌肉疼痛、茶色尿、肌酸激酶 18,000 U/L，并且血清肌酐升高。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a crush injury has severe muscle pain, tea-colored urine, creatine kinase 18,000 U/L, and rising serum creatinine.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名挤压伤患者出现严重肌肉疼痛、茶色尿、肌酸激酶 18,000 U/L，并且血清肌酐升高。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is at risk for {{1}}; the nurse should anticipate {{2}} and report {{3}} immediately.","zh":"该患者有发生 {{1}} 的风险；护士应预计 {{2}}，并立即报告 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"fluid overload from low aldosterone","zh":"醛固酮降低导致的液体过多"},{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic alkalosis from prolonged vomiting","zh":"长期呕吐导致的代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"o1","en":"acute kidney injury from myoglobin release","zh":"肌红蛋白释放导致的急性肾损伤"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"strict fluid restriction","zh":"严格限制液体"},{"id":"o3","en":"withholding all urine output measurements","zh":"停止所有尿量测量"},{"id":"o1","en":"aggressive isotonic IV fluids as prescribed","zh":"按医嘱积极给予等渗静脉液体"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"a rising potassium level","zh":"血钾升高"},{"id":"o3","en":"a urine specific gravity within reference range","zh":"尿比重在参考范围内"},{"id":"o2","en":"mild bruising at the injury site","zh":"受伤部位轻微瘀斑"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rhabdomyolysis releases myoglobin that can obstruct and injure renal tubules. Isotonic IV fluids help maintain renal perfusion and urine flow, and hyperkalemia from muscle breakdown can cause life-threatening dysrhythmias.","rationaleCorrectZh":"横纹肌溶解会释放肌红蛋白，可能堵塞并损伤肾小管。等渗静脉液体有助于维持肾灌注和尿流；肌肉分解导致的高钾可引起危及生命的心律失常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In crush injury questions, connect muscle breakdown to kidney injury and potassium release.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到挤压伤题，要把肌肉分解与肾损伤和钾释放联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1281,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_transfusion_trali_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.130","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.130.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.130.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,235],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,67],"fullStemEn":"Twenty minutes after a packed red blood cell transfusion begins, a client develops acute dyspnea, oxygen saturation 84%, fever, hypotension, and bilateral crackles. There is no jugular venous distention. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"浓缩红细胞输注开始 20 分钟后，患者出现急性呼吸困难、血氧饱和度 84%、发热、低血压和双侧湿啰音。未见颈静脉怒张。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"There is no jugular venous distention.","penultimateSentenceZh":"未见颈静脉怒张。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should suspect {{1}}, first {{2}}, and keep the IV line open with {{3}}.","zh":"护士应怀疑 {{1}}，首先 {{2}}，并用 {{3}} 保持静脉通路开放。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"hypoglycemia from missed meals","zh":"漏餐导致的低血糖"},{"id":"o2","en":"mild allergic transfusion reaction","zh":"轻度过敏性输血反应"},{"id":"o1","en":"transfusion-related acute lung injury","zh":"输血相关急性肺损伤"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"raise the head of bed only and continue the transfusion","zh":"仅抬高床头并继续输血"},{"id":"o1","en":"stop the transfusion","zh":"停止输血"},{"id":"o2","en":"slow the transfusion rate and reassess in 30 minutes","zh":"减慢输血速度并 30 分钟后重新评估"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"lactated Ringer solution through the blood tubing","zh":"通过输血管给予乳酸林格液"},{"id":"o2","en":"dextrose 5% in water through the blood tubing","zh":"通过输血管给予 5% 葡萄糖水"},{"id":"o1","en":"0.9% sodium chloride using new tubing","zh":"使用新输液管给予 0.9% 氯化钠"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acute hypoxemia, dyspnea, fever, hypotension, and noncardiogenic pulmonary edema during transfusion are concerning for transfusion-related acute lung injury. The nurse stops the transfusion and maintains IV access with normal saline through new tubing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"输血过程中出现急性低氧、呼吸困难、发热、低血压和非心源性肺水肿，提示输血相关急性肺损伤。护士应停止输血，并用新输液管输入生理盐水维持静脉通路。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For any acute transfusion reaction, the first safety move is to stop the transfusion, then maintain access with normal saline and notify the provider/blood bank.","testTakingStrategyZh":"任何急性输血反应的第一安全措施都是停止输血，然后用生理盐水维持通路并通知医嘱者/血库。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"There is no jugular venous distention.","controlSentenceZh":"未见颈静脉怒张。"}
{"queueIndex":1282,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_febrile_neutropenia_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.131","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.131.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.131.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,75],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving chemotherapy has an absolute neutrophil count of 300/mm3, temperature 101.5 °F (38.6 °C), chills, and a tunneled central venous catheter. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名正在接受化疗的患者中性粒细胞绝对计数为 300/mm3，体温 101.5 °F (38.6 °C)，寒战，并有隧道式中心静脉导管。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receiving chemotherapy has an absolute neutrophil count of 300/mm3, temperature 101.5 °F (38.6 °C), chills, and a tunneled central venous catheter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名正在接受化疗的患者中性粒细胞绝对计数为 300/mm3，体温 101.5 °F (38.6 °C)，寒战，并有隧道式中心静脉导管。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"This client is at highest immediate risk for {{1}}; the nurse should anticipate {{2}} if it does not delay treatment and implement {{3}}.","zh":"该患者当前最高风险是 {{1}}；若不会延误治疗，护士应预计 {{2}}，并实施 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"life-threatening infection or sepsis","zh":"危及生命的感染或脓毒症"},{"id":"o3","en":"fluid volume excess from chemotherapy","zh":"化疗导致的液体容量过多"},{"id":"o2","en":"chronic iron-deficiency anemia","zh":"慢性缺铁性贫血"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"routine stool occult blood testing before notifying the provider","zh":"通知医嘱者前先常规检查粪便隐血"},{"id":"o3","en":"delaying antibiotics until all chemotherapy side effects resolve","zh":"推迟抗生素直至所有化疗副作用消失"},{"id":"o1","en":"blood cultures from appropriate sites before broad-spectrum antibiotics","zh":"在广谱抗生素前从适当部位采集血培养"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"no precautions because fever is expected after chemotherapy","zh":"无需隔离，因为化疗后发热是预期表现"},{"id":"o1","en":"protective/neutropenic precautions with strict hand hygiene","zh":"保护性/中性粒细胞减少隔离并严格手卫生"},{"id":"o2","en":"airborne precautions for all visitors","zh":"对所有访客实施空气传播隔离"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fever in severe neutropenia is an emergency because infection can progress rapidly to sepsis. Cultures are obtained before broad-spectrum antibiotics when this does not delay treatment, and protective precautions reduce exposure to organisms.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重中性粒细胞减少时发热属于急症，因为感染可迅速进展为脓毒症。若不延误治疗，应在广谱抗生素前采集培养；保护性隔离可减少病原体暴露。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In immunocompromised clients, fever is not routine; treat it as possible sepsis until evaluated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"免疫功能低下患者发热不是常规现象；在评估前应视为可能脓毒症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1283,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_heparin_safety_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.132","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.132.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.132.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,51],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving a continuous unfractionated heparin infusion for a pulmonary embolism. For each finding, select whether the nurse should continue routine monitoring or stop the infusion and notify the provider.","fullStemZh":"一名肺栓塞患者正在接受普通肝素持续静脉输注。请判断每项发现是继续常规监测，还是应停止输注并通知医嘱者。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether the nurse should continue routine monitoring or stop the infusion and notify the provider.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是继续常规监测，还是应停止输注并通知医嘱者。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving a continuous unfractionated heparin infusion for a pulmonary embolism.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名肺栓塞患者正在接受普通肝素持续静脉输注。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Activated partial thromboplastin time is within the facility's therapeutic range.","zh":"活化部分凝血活酶时间在本机构治疗范围内。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Platelet count decreased from 240 ×10³/µL to 92 ×10³/µL after 5 days of therapy.","zh":"治疗 5 天后血小板从 240 ×10³/µL 降至 92 ×10³/µL。"},{"id":"r3","en":"New hematuria is present in the urinary catheter bag.","zh":"导尿袋中出现新发血尿。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Small ecchymosis is noted at an old venipuncture site and is not expanding.","zh":"旧静脉穿刺处有小片瘀斑，未扩大。"},{"id":"r5","en":"The client reports sudden severe headache and blurred vision.","zh":"患者报告突发严重头痛和视物模糊。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Stop infusion and notify provider","zh":"停止输注并通知医嘱者"},{"id":"c1","en":"Continue routine monitoring","zh":"继续常规监测"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic aPTT and a small stable bruise can be monitored. A large platelet drop after several days suggests heparin-induced thrombocytopenia, hematuria suggests bleeding, and sudden severe neurologic symptoms may indicate intracranial bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗范围内的 aPTT 和小而稳定的瘀斑可继续监测。用药数天后血小板大幅下降提示肝素诱导性血小板减少；血尿提示出血；突发严重神经症状可能提示颅内出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With anticoagulants, treat active bleeding, sudden neurologic changes, and large platelet drops as unsafe findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到抗凝药题，活动性出血、突发神经变化和血小板大幅下降都应视为不安全发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1284,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_compartment_syndrome_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.133","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.133.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.133.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,56],"fullStemEn":"A client has a long-leg cast after repair of a tibial fracture. For each finding, select whether it is expected after casting or concerning for neurovascular compromise.","fullStemZh":"一名胫骨骨折修复术后患者使用长腿石膏固定。请判断每项发现是石膏固定后的预期表现，还是提示神经血管受损的危险发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is expected after casting or concerning for neurovascular compromise.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是石膏固定后的预期表现，还是提示神经血管受损的危险发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client has a long-leg cast after repair of a tibial fracture.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名胫骨骨折修复术后患者使用长腿石膏固定。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Severe pain unrelieved by prescribed opioid analgesia and elevation","zh":"严重疼痛，按医嘱使用阿片类止痛药并抬高患肢后仍不缓解"},{"id":"r2","en":"Toes are warm with capillary refill less than 3 seconds.","zh":"足趾温暖，毛细血管再充盈时间少于 3 秒。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Numbness and tingling in the affected foot","zh":"患侧足部麻木和刺痛"},{"id":"r4","en":"Slight itching under the dry cast","zh":"干燥石膏下轻微瘙痒"},{"id":"r5","en":"Pain increases when the nurse passively extends the toes.","zh":"护士被动伸展足趾时疼痛加重。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected after casting","zh":"石膏固定后预期表现"},{"id":"c2","en":"Concerning for neurovascular compromise","zh":"提示神经血管受损"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe unrelieved pain, paresthesia, and pain with passive stretch are classic warning signs of compartment syndrome or neurovascular compromise. Warm toes with brisk refill and mild itching under a dry cast are expected findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重且不缓解的疼痛、感觉异常以及被动牵拉时疼痛，是筋膜室综合征或神经血管受损的典型警讯。足趾温暖且再充盈迅速、干石膏下轻微瘙痒属于预期表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After casts or fractures, prioritize the neurovascular findings: pain, pallor, paresthesia, paralysis, pulselessness, and pressure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"石膏或骨折后，优先关注神经血管表现：疼痛、苍白、感觉异常、瘫痪、无脉和压力感。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1285,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_central_line_care_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.134","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.134.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.134.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[65,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,37],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is observing central venous catheter care on the unit. For each action, select whether it is appropriate practice or requires correction.","fullStemZh":"护士正在观察病区中心静脉导管护理。请判断每项操作是合适做法，还是需要纠正。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each action, select whether it is appropriate practice or requires correction.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项操作是合适做法，还是需要纠正。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is observing central venous catheter care on the unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在观察病区中心静脉导管护理。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Scrubs the catheter hub before accessing the line.","zh":"接入管路前擦拭消毒导管接口。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Uses clean gloves to replace a soiled transparent dressing without hand hygiene first.","zh":"未先进行手卫生，只戴清洁手套更换污染的透明敷料。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Changes a damp, loose dressing as soon as it is noticed.","zh":"发现敷料潮湿、松动后立即更换。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Disconnects the line briefly and lays the uncapped end on the bed while gathering supplies.","zh":"短暂断开管路，并在取用品时把未盖帽的管端放在床上。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Assesses the continued need for the central line during daily rounds.","zh":"每日查房时评估是否仍需要中心静脉导管。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires correction","zh":"需要纠正"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate practice","zh":"合适做法"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Central line infection prevention includes hand hygiene, hub disinfection, maintaining a closed and clean system, changing compromised dressings, and removing unnecessary lines. Skipping hand hygiene or placing an uncapped line end on bedding contaminates the system.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防中心静脉导管感染包括手卫生、接口消毒、保持系统封闭清洁、更换受损敷料以及移除不再需要的导管。跳过手卫生或把未盖帽管端放在床上会污染系统。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For invasive-line questions, choose actions that keep the system clean, closed, necessary, and assessed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"侵入性管路题要选择能保持系统清洁、封闭、必要且持续评估的操作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1286,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_shift_report_priority_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.135","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.135.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.135.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,49],"fullStemEn":"The nurse receives shift report for four clients. For each finding, select whether the nurse should assess the client immediately or whether the finding can be addressed after immediate priorities.","fullStemZh":"护士接班时收到四名患者的交班信息。请判断每项发现是需要立即评估，还是可在处理紧急优先事项后再处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether the nurse should assess the client immediately or whether the finding can be addressed after immediate priorities.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是需要立即评估，还是可在处理紧急优先事项后再处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse receives shift report for four clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士接班时收到四名患者的交班信息。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Client with pneumonia has new confusion and respiratory rate 32/min.","zh":"肺炎患者新发意识混乱，呼吸频率 32 次/分。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Client scheduled for discharge requests a printed medication list.","zh":"计划出院的患者要求打印用药清单。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Client 1 day after abdominal surgery reports incisional pain 4/10 after coughing.","zh":"腹部手术后第 1 天患者咳嗽后报告切口痛 4/10。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Client with pancreatitis has restlessness, cool clammy skin, and blood pressure 86/52 mm Hg.","zh":"胰腺炎患者躁动、皮肤湿冷，血压 86/52 mm Hg。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Client with a new tracheostomy has gurgling respirations and oxygen saturation 88%.","zh":"新气管造口患者呼吸有咕噜声，血氧饱和度 88%。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Assess immediately","zh":"立即评估"},{"id":"c2","en":"Address after immediate priorities","zh":"处理紧急优先事项后再处理"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate assessment is needed for acute respiratory deterioration, shock, or airway compromise. Discharge paperwork and expected mild postoperative pain are lower priority when other clients are unstable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性呼吸恶化、休克或气道受损需要立即评估。与不稳定患者相比，出院文件和预期的轻中度术后疼痛优先级较低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When prioritizing, acute changes in airway, breathing, circulation, or mental status outrank scheduled tasks and expected discomfort.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排序时，气道、呼吸、循环或意识状态的急性变化优先于计划性任务和预期不适。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1287,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_matrix_potassium_shift_insulin_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.136","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.136.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.136.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,59],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving IV insulin for severe hyperglycemia with frequent electrolyte monitoring. For each finding, select whether it is expected with insulin therapy or requires prompt follow-up.","fullStemZh":"一名严重高血糖患者正在接受静脉胰岛素治疗，并频繁监测电解质。请判断每项发现是胰岛素治疗中的预期变化，还是需要迅速跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is expected with insulin therapy or requires prompt follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是胰岛素治疗中的预期变化，还是需要迅速跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving IV insulin for severe hyperglycemia with frequent electrolyte monitoring.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名严重高血糖患者正在接受静脉胰岛素治疗，并频繁监测电解质。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Serum potassium decreases from 4.8 mEq/L to 3.1 mEq/L.","zh":"血钾从 4.8 mEq/L 降至 3.1 mEq/L。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Blood glucose decreases from 520 mg/dL to 360 mg/dL over the first 2 hours.","zh":"前 2 小时血糖从 520 mg/dL 降至 360 mg/dL。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The cardiac monitor shows new frequent premature ventricular contractions.","zh":"心电监护显示新发频繁室性早搏。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client reports feeling less thirsty as fluids are administered.","zh":"补液过程中患者表示口渴减轻。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Serum potassium is 2.9 mEq/L before the next insulin-rate increase.","zh":"下一次增加胰岛素速率前血钾为 2.9 mEq/L。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires prompt follow-up","zh":"需要迅速跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected; continue prescribed monitoring","zh":"预期变化；继续按医嘱监测"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Insulin lowers glucose and shifts potassium into cells. Falling potassium to hypokalemic levels or dysrhythmias requires prompt follow-up before continuing or increasing insulin, while improving glucose and thirst are expected treatment responses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胰岛素降低血糖，并使钾转移入细胞。血钾降至低钾范围或出现心律失常，需要在继续或增加胰岛素前迅速跟进；血糖和口渴改善属于预期治疗反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that insulin moves potassium into cells; low or falling potassium becomes a priority even while hyperglycemia is being treated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住胰岛素会把钾移入细胞；治疗高血糖时，低钾或钾持续下降会成为优先问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client is receiving IV insulin for severe hyperglycemia with frequent electrolyte monitoring.","controlSentenceZh":"一名严重高血糖患者正在接受静脉胰岛素治疗，并频繁监测电解质。"}
{"queueIndex":1288,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_theophylline_toxicity_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.137","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.137.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.137.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,47],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic lung disease takes theophylline. The client reports nausea, insomnia, palpitations, and tremor after starting a new antibiotic. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性肺病患者服用茶碱。开始一种新抗生素后，患者报告恶心、失眠、心悸和震颤。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports nausea, insomnia, palpitations, and tremor after starting a new antibiotic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"开始一种新抗生素后，患者报告恶心、失眠、心悸和震颤。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should suspect {{1}}, anticipate checking a {{2}}, and prioritize monitoring for {{3}}.","zh":"护士应怀疑 {{1}}，预计检查 {{2}}，并优先监测 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"iron-deficiency anemia","zh":"缺铁性贫血"},{"id":"o2","en":"opioid withdrawal","zh":"阿片类戒断"},{"id":"o1","en":"theophylline toxicity","zh":"茶碱中毒"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"hemoglobin A1c","zh":"糖化血红蛋白"},{"id":"o3","en":"serum amylase level","zh":"血清淀粉酶"},{"id":"o1","en":"serum theophylline concentration","zh":"血清茶碱浓度"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"dysrhythmias and seizures","zh":"心律失常和癫痫发作"},{"id":"o2","en":"urinary retention only","zh":"仅尿潴留"},{"id":"o3","en":"painless jaundice","zh":"无痛性黄疸"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Theophylline has a narrow therapeutic index, and interacting medications can raise levels. Gastrointestinal upset, insomnia, tremor, and palpitations are toxicity cues; severe toxicity can cause dysrhythmias and seizures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"茶碱治疗指数窄，药物相互作用可升高血药浓度。胃肠不适、失眠、震颤和心悸是中毒线索；严重中毒可导致心律失常和癫痫发作。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a drug has a narrow therapeutic index, new symptoms after an interacting medication should trigger toxicity monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"窄治疗指数药物在加入可能相互作用的药物后出现新症状时，应想到中毒监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client reports nausea, insomnia, palpitations, and tremor after starting a new antibiotic.","controlSentenceZh":"开始一种新抗生素后，患者报告恶心、失眠、心悸和震颤。"}
{"queueIndex":1289,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_myasthenic_crisis_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.138","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.138.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.138.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[165,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,53],"fullStemEn":"A client with myasthenia gravis reports increasing difficulty swallowing and speaking. Assessment shows weak cough, shallow respirations, and oxygen saturation 89%. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名重症肌无力患者报告吞咽和说话越来越困难。评估发现咳嗽无力、呼吸浅、血氧饱和度 89%。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Assessment shows weak cough, shallow respirations, and oxygen saturation 89%.","penultimateSentenceZh":"评估发现咳嗽无力、呼吸浅、血氧饱和度 89%。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first prioritize {{1}}, anticipate measuring {{2}}, and prepare for {{3}} if respiratory effort worsens.","zh":"护士应首先优先处理 {{1}}，预计测量 {{2}}，并在呼吸做功恶化时准备 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"airway and ventilation support","zh":"气道和通气支持"},{"id":"o3","en":"routine morning medication reconciliation","zh":"常规晨间用药核对"},{"id":"o2","en":"diet teaching for weight gain","zh":"增重饮食教学"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"postvoid residual volume","zh":"排尿后残余尿量"},{"id":"o1","en":"vital capacity or negative inspiratory force","zh":"肺活量或负吸气力"},{"id":"o2","en":"ankle-brachial index","zh":"踝肱指数"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"possible intubation and mechanical ventilation","zh":"可能气管插管和机械通气"},{"id":"o3","en":"withholding all respiratory assessment to reduce fatigue","zh":"停止所有呼吸评估以减少疲劳"},{"id":"o2","en":"placing the client flat for rest","zh":"让患者平卧休息"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bulbar weakness, weak cough, shallow respirations, and hypoxemia indicate possible myasthenic crisis with impending respiratory failure. Respiratory mechanics such as vital capacity guide escalation, and ventilatory support may be needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"延髓肌无力、咳嗽无力、呼吸浅和低氧提示可能发生肌无力危象并即将呼吸衰竭。肺活量等呼吸力学指标可指导升级处理，可能需要通气支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In neuromuscular disease, swallowing changes plus weak cough point to airway protection and ventilatory failure risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"神经肌肉疾病中，吞咽改变加咳嗽无力提示气道保护和通气衰竭风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1290,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_hhs_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.139","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.139.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.139.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,68],"fullStemEn":"An older adult with type 2 diabetes is admitted with lethargy, dry mucous membranes, blood glucose 720 mg/dL, serum osmolality 335 mOsm/kg, and negative urine ketones. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名 2 型糖尿病老年患者因嗜睡、黏膜干燥入院，血糖 720 mg/dL，血清渗透压 335 mOsm/kg，尿酮阴性。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An older adult with type 2 diabetes is admitted with lethargy, dry mucous membranes, blood glucose 720 mg/dL, serum osmolality 335 mOsm/kg, and negative urine ketones.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 2 型糖尿病老年患者因嗜睡、黏膜干燥入院，血糖 720 mg/dL，血清渗透压 335 mOsm/kg，尿酮阴性。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is most likely experiencing {{1}}; the nurse should prioritize {{2}} and closely monitor {{3}}.","zh":"该患者最可能发生 {{1}}；护士应优先 {{2}}，并密切监测 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"acute hypoglycemia","zh":"急性低血糖"},{"id":"o1","en":"hyperosmolar hyperglycemic state","zh":"高渗高血糖状态"},{"id":"o2","en":"thyroid storm","zh":"甲状腺危象"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"restoring circulating volume with IV isotonic fluids as prescribed","zh":"按医嘱用等渗静脉液体恢复循环容量"},{"id":"o2","en":"restricting oral and IV fluids until glucose normalizes","zh":"在血糖恢复正常前限制口服和静脉液体"},{"id":"o3","en":"administering oral glucose tablets","zh":"给予口服葡萄糖片"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"only daily weight after discharge","zh":"仅出院后每日体重"},{"id":"o2","en":"pupil color and ear drainage","zh":"瞳孔颜色和耳部分泌物"},{"id":"o1","en":"mental status, urine output, and electrolytes","zh":"意识状态、尿量和电解质"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Very high glucose, hyperosmolality, dehydration, altered mental status, and minimal ketones support hyperosmolar hyperglycemic state. Initial care focuses on volume resuscitation, followed by insulin and electrolyte management as prescribed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"极高血糖、高渗、脱水、意识改变和酮体少，支持高渗高血糖状态。初始护理重点是容量复苏，随后按医嘱进行胰岛素和电解质管理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For extreme hyperglycemia with dehydration and little ketosis, think HHS and prioritize perfusion before fine-tuning glucose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"极高血糖伴脱水且酮体少时，要想到 HHS，并在精细调整血糖前优先恢复灌注。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"An older adult with type 2 diabetes is admitted with lethargy, dry mucous membranes, blood glucose 720 mg/dL, serum osmolality 335 mOsm/kg, and negative urine ketones.","controlSentenceZh":"一名 2 型糖尿病老年患者因嗜睡、黏膜干燥入院，血糖 720 mg/dL，血清渗透压 335 mOsm/kg，尿酮阴性。"}
{"queueIndex":1291,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_acute_pancreatitis_19","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.140","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.140.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.140.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[171,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,64],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with acute pancreatitis has severe epigastric pain radiating to the back, persistent vomiting, calcium 7.4 mg/dL, and oxygen saturation 90% on room air. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名急性胰腺炎患者出现严重上腹痛并放射至背部、持续呕吐、血钙 7.4 mg/dL，室内空气下血氧饱和度 90%。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client admitted with acute pancreatitis has severe epigastric pain radiating to the back, persistent vomiting, calcium 7.4 mg/dL, and oxygen saturation 90% on room air.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名急性胰腺炎患者出现严重上腹痛并放射至背部、持续呕吐、血钙 7.4 mg/dL，室内空气下血氧饱和度 90%。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize risk for {{1}}, monitor for {{2}}, and anticipate {{3}} as prescribed.","zh":"护士应识别该患者有 {{1}} 的风险，监测 {{2}}，并预计按医嘱 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"hyperthyroidism and heat stroke","zh":"甲状腺功能亢进和热射病"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypocalcemia and respiratory compromise","zh":"低钙血症和呼吸受损"},{"id":"o3","en":"urinary retention from spinal anesthesia","zh":"脊麻导致的尿潴留"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"tetany, tingling, worsening oxygenation, and lung sounds","zh":"手足搐搦、麻刺感、氧合恶化和肺部听诊"},{"id":"o2","en":"visual acuity only","zh":"仅视力"},{"id":"o3","en":"weekly hearing screening","zh":"每周听力筛查"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"high-fat meals to stimulate pancreatic enzymes","zh":"高脂饮食以刺激胰酶分泌"},{"id":"o1","en":"IV fluids, analgesia, and oxygen support","zh":"静脉补液、镇痛和氧气支持"},{"id":"o3","en":"withholding pain medication until diagnosis is reconfirmed","zh":"在重新确认诊断前暂停止痛药"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acute pancreatitis can cause third spacing, severe pain, hypocalcemia, and respiratory complications. Nursing care includes monitoring calcium-related neuromuscular signs, oxygenation, lung status, fluid balance, and pain control.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性胰腺炎可导致第三间隙液体转移、严重疼痛、低钙血症和呼吸并发症。护理包括监测低钙相关神经肌肉表现、氧合、肺部情况、液体平衡和疼痛控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In pancreatitis, look beyond abdominal pain for systemic complications: fluid shifts, calcium changes, shock, and respiratory decline.","testTakingStrategyZh":"胰腺炎题不要只看腹痛，还要寻找全身并发症：液体转移、血钙变化、休克和呼吸恶化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1292,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u6_matrix_cloze_2026_06_09_cloze_preeclampsia_magnesium_20","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.141","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.141.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.141.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,61],"fullStemEn":"A client with preeclampsia is receiving magnesium sulfate. The nurse notes respiratory rate 10/min, absent deep tendon reflexes, and urine output 20 mL/hr. Complete the nursing statement.","fullStemZh":"一名子痫前期患者正在接受硫酸镁治疗。护士发现呼吸频率 10 次/分、深腱反射消失、尿量 20 mL/小时。请完成护理判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nursing statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护理判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes respiratory rate 10/min, absent deep tendon reflexes, and urine output 20 mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现呼吸频率 10 次/分、深腱反射消失、尿量 20 mL/小时。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should suspect {{1}}, first {{2}}, and anticipate administering {{3}} as prescribed.","zh":"护士应怀疑 {{1}}，首先 {{2}}，并预计按医嘱给予 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"expected therapeutic sedation","zh":"预期的治疗性镇静"},{"id":"o1","en":"magnesium sulfate toxicity","zh":"硫酸镁中毒"},{"id":"o3","en":"normal postpartum diuresis","zh":"正常产后利尿"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"place the client in a dark room and reassess in 2 hours","zh":"让患者待在暗室中并 2 小时后重新评估"},{"id":"o2","en":"increase the infusion rate to prevent seizure","zh":"增加输注速率以预防癫痫发作"},{"id":"o1","en":"stop the magnesium infusion and notify the provider","zh":"停止硫酸镁输注并通知医嘱者"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"vitamin K","zh":"维生素 K"},{"id":"o2","en":"protamine sulfate","zh":"鱼精蛋白硫酸盐"},{"id":"o1","en":"calcium gluconate","zh":"葡萄糖酸钙"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Respiratory depression, absent deep tendon reflexes, and low urine output indicate magnesium toxicity. The infusion should be stopped, the provider notified, and calcium gluconate prepared as the antidote.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呼吸抑制、深腱反射消失和尿量低提示硫酸镁中毒。应停止输注、通知医嘱者，并准备葡萄糖酸钙作为解毒剂。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For magnesium sulfate, the danger cues are respiratory depression, absent reflexes, and reduced urine output because magnesium is renally cleared.","testTakingStrategyZh":"硫酸镁题的危险线索是呼吸抑制、反射消失和尿量减少，因为镁经肾脏清除。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1293,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_preventive_screening","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.142","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.142.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,59],"fullStemEn":"Adult preventive screening with language and follow-up barriers A stable adult with overdue preventive screenings needs a feasible, language-accessible plan and follow-up after an abnormal screening result.","fullStemZh":"成人预防筛查伴语言和随访障碍 一名病情稳定但多项预防筛查逾期的成人，需要可行、语言可及的计划，并在筛查异常后完成随访。","terminalSentenceEn":"Adult preventive screening with language and follow-up barriers A stable adult with overdue preventive screenings needs a feasible, language-accessible plan and follow-up after an abnormal screening result.","terminalSentenceZh":"成人预防筛查伴语言和随访障碍 一名病情稳定但多项预防筛查逾期的成人，需要可行、语言可及的计划，并在筛查异常后完成随访。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The embedded questions evaluate clinical judgment across the unfolding case.","rationaleCorrectZh":"嵌入问题用于评估在病例进展中的临床判断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track what changed over time and connect each cue to the safest nursing action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"追踪随时间变化的线索，并把每个线索与最安全的护理措施联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1294,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_preventive_screening","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_matrix_screening_01","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"For each finding in the initial visit, indicate whether it supports screening now or does not require action during this visit.","fullStemZh":"根据初次就诊资料，判断每项发现是支持现在筛查，还是本次就诊不需要处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding in the initial visit, indicate whether it supports screening now or does not require action during this visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据初次就诊资料，判断每项发现是支持现在筛查，还是本次就诊不需要处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Age 47 with no prior colorectal cancer screening","zh":"47岁且从未进行结直肠癌筛查"},{"id":"r2","en":"Cervix intact and last cervical cancer screening 9 years ago","zh":"宫颈完整且上次宫颈癌筛查为9年前"},{"id":"r3","en":"Never had a mammogram","zh":"从未做过乳腺X线检查"},{"id":"r4","en":"No first-degree relative with colorectal cancer","zh":"一级亲属无结直肠癌史"},{"id":"r5","en":"No acute symptoms today","zh":"今天无急性症状"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Screening indicated now","zh":"现在需要筛查"},{"id":"c2","en":"No screening action from this cue alone","zh":"仅凭此线索不需要筛查措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The age and overdue screening history support offering colorectal, cervical, and breast cancer screening. Lack of symptoms does not remove the need for preventive screening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"年龄和逾期筛查史支持提供结直肠癌、宫颈癌和乳腺癌筛查。没有症状并不取消预防性筛查的需要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate screening indications from diagnostic workups. A client can need screening even when stable and symptom-free.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分筛查适应证和诊断性检查。即使患者稳定且无症状，也可能需要筛查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1295,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_preventive_screening","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_cloze_counseling_02","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,37],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,10],"fullStemEn":"Complete the nurse's counseling plan.","fullStemZh":"完成护士的咨询计划。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nurse's counseling plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护士的咨询计划。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first use {{1}} and then offer {{2}} so the client can choose a feasible screening plan.","zh":"护士应首先使用 {{1}}，然后提供 {{2}}，使来访者能选择可行的筛查计划。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"a qualified medical interpreter","zh":"合格的医疗口译员"},{"id":"o3","en":"English-only printed instructions","zh":"仅英文书面说明"},{"id":"o2","en":"the client's adult relative as the default interpreter","zh":"默认让来访者的成年亲属担任口译"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a warning that refusal means cancer is likely","zh":"警告拒绝就表示很可能有癌症"},{"id":"o3","en":"all possible guidelines without checking understanding","zh":"列出所有可能指南但不确认理解"},{"id":"o1","en":"plain-language options with follow-up steps","zh":"通俗语言说明的选择和后续步骤"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A qualified interpreter and plain-language options support informed, feasible participation without coercion or jargon.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合格口译员和通俗语言的选择能支持来访者在不被胁迫、不被术语阻碍的情况下做出可行决定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a language barrier is present, fix communication before judging refusal or knowledge.","testTakingStrategyZh":"存在语言障碍时，先解决沟通问题，再判断拒绝或知识水平。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1296,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_preventive_screening","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_mc_positive_fit_03","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[37,75],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,21],"fullStemEn":"The client's FIT result is positive. Which instruction is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"来访者的FIT结果为阳性。哪项指导最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which instruction is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项指导最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's FIT result is positive.","penultimateSentenceZh":"来访者的FIT结果为阳性。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Repeat the FIT in 1 year because the client has no symptoms.","zh":"因来访者无症状，1年后重复FIT。"},{"id":"B","en":"Schedule follow-up colonoscopy and explain that a positive screening test needs diagnostic evaluation.","zh":"安排后续结肠镜检查，并说明筛查阳性需要诊断性评估。"},{"id":"C","en":"Tell the client that the result confirms colorectal cancer.","zh":"告诉来访者该结果确认结直肠癌。"},{"id":"D","en":"Cancel the cervical cancer screening until the colon evaluation is finished.","zh":"取消宫颈癌筛查，直到肠道评估完成。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A positive FIT is a screening result that requires diagnostic follow-up, usually colonoscopy; it does not diagnose cancer by itself.","rationaleCorrectZh":"FIT阳性是需要诊断性随访（通常为结肠镜）的筛查结果；它本身并不能诊断癌症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Screening tests sort risk; abnormal screening results usually need diagnostic follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"筛查用于风险分层；异常筛查结果通常需要诊断性随访。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1297,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_preventive_screening","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_sata_followup_04","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,28],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions best support the client's completion of the follow-up plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些护理措施最能支持来访者完成后续计划？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions best support the client's completion of the follow-up plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施最能支持来访者完成后续计划？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Ask what days and times the client can attend appointments.","zh":"询问来访者哪些日期和时间可以赴约。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tell the client that anxiety is not a valid reason to delay care.","zh":"告诉来访者焦虑不是延迟就医的合理理由。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide Mandarin written instructions with the clinic phone number.","zh":"提供中文书面说明和诊所电话号码。"},{"id":"E","en":"Offer assistance scheduling the colonoscopy before the client leaves.","zh":"在来访者离开前协助预约结肠镜。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use teach-back to confirm the client understands what a positive FIT means.","zh":"使用回授法确认来访者理解FIT阳性的含义。"},{"id":"F","en":"Ask the client's relative to decide which screening the client should complete first.","zh":"请来访者亲属决定来访者应先完成哪项筛查。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Scheduling around work, teach-back, language-concordant instructions, and warm handoff scheduling address the identified barriers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"围绕工作安排预约、回授法、语言一致的说明以及离开前协助预约，能针对已发现的障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose interventions that remove barriers instead of blaming the client for the barriers.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能移除障碍的措施，而不是因障碍责备患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1298,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_preventive_screening","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case01_or_screening_plan_05","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.142.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,90],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the best order when developing the preventive screening plan.","fullStemZh":"为制定预防筛查计划，将护士措施按最佳顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the best order when developing the preventive screening plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"为制定预防筛查计划，将护士措施按最佳顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Assist with scheduling and provide written instructions in the preferred language.","zh":"协助预约并提供偏好语言的书面说明。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client about priorities, fears, transportation, and work schedule.","zh":"询问来访者的优先事项、恐惧、交通和工作时间。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the plan, barriers addressed, and follow-up needs.","zh":"记录计划、已处理的障碍和后续需求。"},{"id":"C","en":"Use teach-back to confirm the client can describe the chosen plan.","zh":"使用回授法确认来访者能说明所选计划。"},{"id":"B","en":"Explain the indicated screenings using short, plain-language statements.","zh":"用简短通俗语言解释应做的筛查。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assessment of barriers comes before teaching; understanding should be verified before scheduling and documentation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在教学前先评估障碍；在预约和记录前应确认理解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In counseling sequences, assess first, teach second, verify third, then implement and document.","testTakingStrategyZh":"咨询排序通常是先评估、再教学、再确认理解，然后执行并记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1299,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_caregiver_burden","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.143","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.143.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.143.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,224],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,65],"fullStemEn":"Caregiver burden and family adaptation in chronic neurologic illness A spouse caregiver shows escalating strain. The nurse must assess safety, preserve the client's abilities, and connect the family with acceptable supports.","fullStemZh":"慢性神经系统疾病中的照护者负担与家庭适应 配偶照护者出现压力升级。护士必须评估安全、维持患者能力，并把家庭与可接受的支持连接起来。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must assess safety, preserve the client's abilities, and connect the family with acceptable supports.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须评估安全、维持患者能力，并把家庭与可接受的支持连接起来。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Caregiver burden and family adaptation in chronic neurologic illness A spouse caregiver shows escalating strain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"慢性神经系统疾病中的照护者负担与家庭适应 配偶照护者出现压力升级。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The embedded questions evaluate clinical judgment across the unfolding case.","rationaleCorrectZh":"嵌入问题用于评估在病例进展中的临床判断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track what changed over time and connect each cue to the safest nursing action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"追踪随时间变化的线索，并把每个线索与最安全的护理措施联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1300,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_caregiver_burden","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_mc_caregiver_priority_01","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,56],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,14],"fullStemEn":"Which cue requires the nurse's most immediate follow-up?","fullStemZh":"哪项线索最需要护士立即跟进？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which cue requires the nurse's most immediate follow-up?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项线索最需要护士立即跟进？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The spouse has not seen friends in months.","zh":"配偶几个月没见朋友。"},{"id":"B","en":"The spouse says, 'I am afraid I will lose control if nothing changes.'","zh":"配偶说：“如果没有改变，我担心自己会失控。”"},{"id":"C","en":"The client can feed self slowly.","zh":"患者能缓慢自行进食。"},{"id":"D","en":"The daughter is unsure how to help.","zh":"女儿不确定如何帮忙。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fear of losing control signals escalating caregiver strain and possible safety risk, requiring immediate assessment and support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"担心失控提示照护者压力升级并可能存在安全风险，需要立即评估和支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several psychosocial cues are present, prioritize statements that hint at immediate safety risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有多个心理社会线索时，优先处理暗示即时安全风险的陈述。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1301,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_caregiver_burden","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_matrix_cues_02","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,38],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,16],"fullStemEn":"Classify each cue from the home visit.","fullStemZh":"对居家访视中的每项线索进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each cue from the home visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"对居家访视中的每项线索进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Spouse reports being awake most nights","zh":"配偶报告大多数夜晚都醒着"},{"id":"r2","en":"Spouse yelled during a freezing episode and feels guilty","zh":"配偶在患者冻结步态时吼叫并感到内疚"},{"id":"r3","en":"Client can feed self slowly","zh":"患者能缓慢自行进食"},{"id":"r4","en":"Spouse has not seen friends in months","zh":"配偶几个月没见朋友"},{"id":"r5","en":"Spouse denies intent to harm the client","zh":"配偶否认有伤害患者的意图"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Preserved client ability or protective cue","zh":"患者保留能力或保护性线索"},{"id":"c1","en":"Caregiver strain cue","zh":"照护者压力线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sleep loss, guilt after yelling, and social isolation are caregiver strain cues. Self-feeding and denial of intent to harm are protective but do not eliminate strain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"睡眠不足、吼叫后的内疚和社交隔离是照护者压力线索。自行进食和否认伤害意图是保护性线索，但不能消除压力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not label every cue as a problem. Identify both risks and strengths for the care plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把每个线索都当成问题。要同时识别风险和优势，用于制定照护计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1302,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_caregiver_burden","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case02_cloze_response_03","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.143.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,42],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,11],"fullStemEn":"Complete the nurse's therapeutic response.","fullStemZh":"完成护士的治疗性回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nurse's therapeutic response.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护士的治疗性回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's best response is to {{1}} and then {{2}}.","zh":"护士最佳回应是 {{1}}，然后 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"focus only on the client's motor symptoms","zh":"只关注患者的运动症状"},{"id":"o2","en":"tell the spouse that yelling is unacceptable and move on","zh":"告诉配偶吼叫不可接受，然后继续下一话题"},{"id":"o1","en":"acknowledge the spouse's exhaustion without judgment","zh":"不带评判地承认配偶的疲惫"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"assess immediate safety and arrange concrete support options","zh":"评估即时安全并安排具体支持选项"},{"id":"o3","en":"ask the daughter to take over all care immediately","zh":"要求女儿立即接管所有照护"},{"id":"o2","en":"advise the spouse to wait until the next routine visit","zh":"建议配偶等到下次常规访视"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The response should validate distress, assess safety, and move toward specific supports such as respite or shared care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"回应应确认痛苦、评估安全，并转向喘息服务或分担照护等具体支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic communication does not stop at empathy when safety cues are present; pair empathy with action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有安全线索时，治疗性沟通不能止于共情；要把共情与行动结合。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
