":"For low health literacy, simplify the message and verify the client's explanation of the action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"面对低健康素养，简化信息并确认患者能说明要做的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1321,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case05_health_literacy_adherence","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case05_sata_adherence_04","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.146.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.146.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.146.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[64,86],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,24],"fullStemEn":"Which strategies should the nurse include to improve adherence? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应包括哪些策略以改善依从性？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which strategies should the nurse include to improve adherence?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些策略以改善依从性？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Assume a basic cell phone cannot support any adherence plan.","zh":"假设基础手机无法支持任何依从性计划。"},{"id":"C","en":"Coordinate refill planning so the client does not run out of medication.","zh":"协调续药计划，避免患者药物用完。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use shame to emphasize that missed doses caused the abnormal lab result.","zh":"用羞辱方式强调漏服导致化验异常。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask permission before involving the nephew in refill reminders.","zh":"让侄子参与续药提醒前先征得患者同意。"},{"id":"A","en":"Help the client link the medication to a consistent waking routine.","zh":"帮助患者把服药与固定起床习惯相连接。"},{"id":"E","en":"Provide instructions in the client's preferred language using short sentences.","zh":"用患者偏好语言和短句提供说明。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adherence improves when the plan is tied to routines, respects permission, prevents refill gaps, and uses accessible language.","rationaleCorrectZh":"把计划与习惯相连、尊重同意、避免续药中断并使用可理解语言，可改善依从性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Adherence interventions should target the reason for missed doses, not simply repeat the instruction louder.","testTakingStrategyZh":"依从性干预应针对漏服原因，而不是只是更大声重复指令。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1322,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case05_health_literacy_adherence","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_premium_2026_06_10_case05_mc_evaluate_05","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.146.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.146.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.146.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,69],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Which follow-up finding best shows that the teaching plan is working?","fullStemZh":"哪项随访发现最能说明教学计划有效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which follow-up finding best shows that the teaching plan is working?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项随访发现最能说明教学计划有效？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"The client throws away all written instructions because the nurse explained them once.","zh":"患者因为护士解释过一次，就丢掉所有书面说明。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client says the picture schedule helped and describes a consistent waking routine for the thyroid pill.","zh":"患者说图片时间表有帮助，并能描述起床后固定服用甲状腺药的习惯。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client says, 'I still take the pill whenever I remember.'","zh":"患者说：“我还是想起来才吃药。”"},{"id":"B","en":"The nephew answers all questions while the client remains silent.","zh":"侄子回答所有问题，而患者保持沉默。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client can describe a consistent routine using the tailored tool, showing practical understanding and improved adherence behavior.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者能使用个体化工具描述固定习惯，显示实际理解和依从行为改善。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Outcome evaluation looks for the client's ability to carry out the plan in real life.","testTakingStrategyZh":"结果评价要寻找患者在现实生活中执行计划的能力。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1323,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_or_caregiver_burden_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.147","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.147.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.147.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[219,265],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,75],"fullStemEn":"The nurse in a primary care clinic receives a call from an adult daughter who cares for a parent with moderate dementia. The daughter says, \"I have not slept, and I yelled at my mother today. I cannot keep doing this.\" Arrange the nurse's actions in priority order.","fullStemZh":"基层诊所护士接到一名成年女儿的电话，她照顾患有中度痴呆的父母。她说：“我一直睡不好，今天还冲母亲吼了。我真的撑不下去了。”请按优先顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nurse's actions in priority order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"I cannot keep doing this.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"我真的撑不下去了。”","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Arrange a follow-up call within 24 to 48 hours to evaluate coping and the safety plan.","zh":"安排在24至48小时内回访，评估应对情况和安全计划。"},{"id":"B","en":"Acknowledge the caregiver's stress and ask what support is available today.","zh":"认可照护者的压力，并询问今天可以获得哪些支持。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess whether the caregiver has thoughts of harming self or the client and whether the client is safe right now.","zh":"评估照护者是否有伤害自己或患者的想法，并确认患者目前是否安全。"},{"id":"C","en":"Consult social work or case management for respite care, adult day services, or home support options.","zh":"请社工或个案管理协助安排喘息照护、成人日间照护或居家支持资源。"},{"id":"D","en":"Teach the caregiver to schedule breaks, keep personal health appointments, and keep emergency contacts visible.","zh":"教导照护者安排休息时间、保留自己的健康就诊，并把紧急联系人放在明显位置。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first priority is immediate safety because the caregiver describes loss of control and exhaustion. After safety is assessed, the nurse uses therapeutic communication, mobilizes community and case-management resources, teaches a practical coping plan, and confirms short-interval follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要任务是确认即时安全，因为照护者描述了失控和极度疲惫。确认安全后，护士再进行治疗性沟通，调动社区和个案管理资源，教导可执行的应对计划，并安排短期随访。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a psychosocial stem includes possible loss of control, address safety before education or referrals.","testTakingStrategyZh":"心理社会题干若出现可能失控的线索，应先处理安全，再进行教育或转介。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1324,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_or_health_literacy_discharge_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.148","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.148.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.148.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,223],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,66],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing discharge teaching for a client who will monitor blood pressure at home. The client nods during teaching but says, \"Medical papers are hard for me to read.\" Arrange the teaching steps in priority order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名出院后需要在家监测血压的患者进行出院指导。患者听讲时点头，但说：“医学资料我读起来很困难。”请按优先顺序排列教学步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the teaching steps in priority order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列教学步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client nods during teaching but says, \"Medical papers are hard for me to read.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者听讲时点头，但说：“医学资料我读起来很困难。”","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use a qualified interpreter if needed and explain two or three key points in plain language.","zh":"如有需要使用合格口译员，并用通俗语言说明两到三个重点。"},{"id":"C","en":"Demonstrate how to measure and record blood pressure, then have the client return-demonstrate.","zh":"示范如何测量并记录血压，然后请患者回示范。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's preferred language, vision or hearing needs, reading comfort, and who helps at home.","zh":"评估患者偏好的语言、视力或听力需求、阅读舒适度，以及家中谁能协助。"},{"id":"E","en":"Provide large-print pictorial instructions and confirm follow-up or community blood-pressure check options.","zh":"提供大字版图示说明，并确认随访或社区血压测量选择。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use teach-back by asking the client to explain when to call the clinic.","zh":"使用回授法，请患者说明何时需要打电话给诊所。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective discharge teaching begins with assessment of communication needs. The nurse then uses plain language and interpreter services when indicated, demonstrates the skill, verifies understanding with teach-back, and reinforces the plan with accessible materials and follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的出院指导应先评估沟通需求。随后护士使用通俗语言，必要时使用口译服务；再示范技能，用回授法确认理解，并以易读材料和随访安排巩固计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For teaching questions, assess learning needs first, teach in an accessible way, then verify understanding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"教学题通常先评估学习需求，再以可理解的方式教学，最后验证理解。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1325,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_or_mobility_progression_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.149","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.149.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.149.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,47],"fullStemEn":"A client in inpatient rehabilitation is ready for the first assisted walk after several days of bed rest for deconditioning. Arrange the nurse's actions in the safest order.","fullStemZh":"一名住院康复患者因体能下降卧床数日后，准备第一次在协助下行走。请按最安全的顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nurse's actions in the safest order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最安全的顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in inpatient rehabilitation is ready for the first assisted walk after several days of bed rest for deconditioning.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名住院康复患者因体能下降卧床数日后，准备第一次在协助下行走。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Ambulate a short planned distance, monitor tolerance, then document distance, assistance level, and response.","zh":"按计划短距离行走，监测耐受情况，然后记录距离、协助程度和反应。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assist the client to stand with the walker using a count of three and allow time to regain balance.","zh":"数到三后协助患者扶助行器站起，并给予时间恢复平衡。"},{"id":"B","en":"Raise the head of the bed, assist the client to sit at the bedside, and assess dizziness before standing.","zh":"抬高床头，协助患者坐到床边，并在站立前评估是否头晕。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply nonskid footwear and a gait belt while the client is sitting; position the walker within reach.","zh":"在患者坐位时穿防滑鞋并系好步态带；将助行器放在可触及处。"},{"id":"A","en":"Review the activity order and assess pain, strength, alertness, and orthostatic-dizziness risk.","zh":"查看活动医嘱，并评估疼痛、力量、清醒程度以及体位性头晕风险。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first verifies that ambulation is appropriate and assesses risks. The client should then progress from sitting and dangling to footwear and gait-belt placement, standing, short ambulation, and documentation of tolerance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先确认适合下床行走并评估风险。随后患者从坐起、垂腿开始，再穿防滑鞋并系步态带，站立，短距离行走，最后记录耐受情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In ordered-response mobility questions, move from assessment to dangling, safety equipment, standing, ambulation, and evaluation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"活动顺序题通常按评估、坐起垂腿、安全设备、站立、行走、评价的顺序思考。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1326,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_or_pressure_injury_prevention_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.150","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.150.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.150.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,48],"fullStemEn":"A client with limited sensation and decreased mobility is admitted to a rehabilitation unit with intact skin. Arrange the nursing actions to prevent a pressure injury.","fullStemZh":"一名感觉减退且活动能力下降的患者入住康复病区，目前皮肤完整。请排列护士预防压力性损伤的行动顺序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nursing actions to prevent a pressure injury.","terminalSentenceZh":"请排列护士预防压力性损伤的行动顺序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with limited sensation and decreased mobility is admitted to a rehabilitation unit with intact skin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名感觉减退且活动能力下降的患者入住康复病区，目前皮肤完整。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Create an individualized turning, mobility, nutrition, and moisture-management plan with the care team.","zh":"与照护团队制定个体化翻身、活动、营养和湿度管理计划。"},{"id":"A","en":"Complete a head-to-toe skin inspection and a standardized pressure-injury risk assessment.","zh":"完成从头到脚的皮肤检查，并进行标准化压力性损伤风险评估。"},{"id":"E","en":"Evaluate skin condition and adherence to the plan each shift and revise the plan if redness or moisture develops.","zh":"每班评估皮肤状况和计划执行情况；若出现发红或潮湿，及时修订计划。"},{"id":"D","en":"Teach the client and caregiver to inspect skin daily and report nonblanchable redness.","zh":"教导患者和照护者每天检查皮肤，并报告不可压白的发红。"},{"id":"B","en":"Relieve pressure from the heels and sacrum and place the client on an appropriate pressure-redistributing surface.","zh":"减轻足跟和骶尾部压力，并让患者使用合适的减压支撑面。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Prevention starts with risk and skin assessment. Immediate pressure relief follows, then an individualized interdisciplinary plan, teaching for continued prevention, and ongoing evaluation with plan revision.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防应从风险和皮肤评估开始。随后立即减压，制定个体化跨专业计划，进行持续预防教育，并持续评价和修订计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For prevention questions, start with risk assessment, then implement targeted measures and evaluate the response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"预防类题目先做风险评估，再实施针对性措施，最后评价效果。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1327,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_or_colorectal_screening_access_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.151","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.151.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.151.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[214,260],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,76],"fullStemEn":"A community health nurse meets a 46-year-old adult who has no primary care provider, limited English proficiency, and no prior colorectal cancer screening. The client reports transportation and insurance barriers. Arrange the nurse's actions in priority order.","fullStemZh":"社区卫生护士遇到一名46岁成年人。该患者没有固定初级保健医生，英语能力有限，从未做过结直肠癌筛查，并表示交通和保险存在障碍。请按优先顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nurse's actions in priority order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports transportation and insurance barriers.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者没有固定初级保健医生，英语能力有限，从未做过结直肠癌筛查，并表示交通和保险存在障碍。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Confirm age, average-risk status, absence of alarm symptoms, preferred language, and permission to discuss resources.","zh":"确认年龄、是否属于平均风险、是否无警示症状、偏好语言，以及是否同意讨论资源。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess barriers such as transportation, cost, work schedule, and ability to complete follow-up testing.","zh":"评估交通、费用、工作时间以及完成后续检查能力等障碍。"},{"id":"B","en":"Use a qualified interpreter and plain language to explain the purpose of screening and available test options.","zh":"使用合格口译员和通俗语言说明筛查目的及可选择的检查方式。"},{"id":"E","en":"Set a reminder or follow-up plan to confirm screening completion and follow-up for abnormal results.","zh":"设定提醒或随访计划，以确认完成筛查，并对异常结果进行后续处理。"},{"id":"D","en":"Connect the client with a low-cost screening program, federally qualified health center, or case-management referral.","zh":"将患者转介至低费用筛查项目、联邦合格健康中心或个案管理服务。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first verifies that routine screening is appropriate and obtains permission to discuss resources. The nurse then provides language-concordant education, identifies barriers, connects the client with accessible services, and plans follow-up so screening is completed and abnormal findings are not lost.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先确认常规筛查是否适合，并获得讨论资源的许可。随后提供语言相符的教育，识别障碍，连接可及服务，并计划随访，以确保筛查完成且异常结果不会失访。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a stem combines prevention and access barriers, verify appropriateness, teach in the client's language, remove barriers, and close the loop.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干同时涉及预防和可及性障碍时，应先确认适用性，用患者语言教育，解决障碍，并闭合随访流程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1328,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_fib_teach_back_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.152","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.152.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.152.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[138,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,44],"fullStemEn":"To check whether discharge instructions were explained clearly, the nurse asks the client to describe the plan in the client's own words. This communication technique is called the _____ method.","fullStemZh":"为确认出院指导是否解释清楚，护士请患者用自己的话描述计划。这种沟通技巧称为_____法。","terminalSentenceEn":"This communication technique is called the _____ method.","terminalSentenceZh":"这种沟通技巧称为_____法。","penultimateSentenceEn":"To check whether discharge instructions were explained clearly, the nurse asks the client to describe the plan in the client's own words.","penultimateSentenceZh":"为确认出院指导是否解释清楚，护士请患者用自己的话描述计划。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"method","zh":"方法"},"acceptable":["teach-back","teach back","teach-back method","teach back method","Teach-back","Teach Back"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teach-back asks the client or caregiver to explain information or actions in their own words. It helps the nurse evaluate whether the teaching was clear and whether more explanation is needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"回授法是请患者或照护者用自己的话说明信息或行动。它帮助护士评估教学是否清楚，以及是否需要进一步解释。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the nurse asks the client to explain instructions in their own words, think teach-back.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当护士请患者用自己的话说明指导内容时，要想到回授法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1329,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_fib_daily_skin_inspection_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.153","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.153.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.153.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,48],"fullStemEn":"A client with decreased sensation in the lower body is learning home skin care. The nurse teaches the client to inspect high-pressure areas at least once each _____.","fullStemZh":"一名下半身感觉减退的患者正在学习居家皮肤护理。护士教导患者至少每_____检查一次高压受力部位。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse teaches the client to inspect high-pressure areas at least once each _____.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士教导患者至少每_____检查一次高压受力部位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with decreased sensation in the lower body is learning home skin care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名下半身感觉减退的患者正在学习居家皮肤护理。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"time period","zh":"时间间隔"},"acceptable":["day","daily","each day","24 hours","twenty-four hours","一天","每天"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients with decreased sensation may not feel early pressure or friction injury. Daily inspection of high-pressure areas supports early identification of redness, moisture damage, or skin breakdown.","rationaleCorrectZh":"感觉减退的患者可能感觉不到早期压力或摩擦损伤。每天检查高压受力部位有助于早期发现发红、潮湿损伤或皮肤破损。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pressure-injury prevention at home, focus on routine inspection, pressure relief, moisture control, and early reporting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"居家预防压力性损伤时，重点是定期检查、减压、控制潮湿和早期报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1330,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_fib_adult_day_services_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.154","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.154.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.154.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,62],"fullStemEn":"A spouse caring for a partner with dementia asks for help because supervision is needed during the day while the spouse works. The nurse suggests supervised daytime activities and respite through adult _____ services.","fullStemZh":"一名配偶照护患有痴呆的伴侣，因为白天工作时需要有人监督而寻求帮助。护士建议通过成人_____服务获得白天监督活动和喘息支持。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse suggests supervised daytime activities and respite through adult _____ services.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士建议通过成人_____服务获得白天监督活动和喘息支持。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A spouse caring for a partner with dementia asks for help because supervision is needed during the day while the spouse works.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名配偶照护患有痴呆的伴侣，因为白天工作时需要有人监督而寻求帮助。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"community resource","zh":"社区资源"},"acceptable":["day","day care","daycare","day health","day services","adult day","日间照护","日间"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adult day services provide supervised activities and support during the day, which can promote social engagement for the client and respite for the caregiver.","rationaleCorrectZh":"成人日间照护服务在白天提供监督、活动和支持，可促进患者社交参与，也能让照护者获得喘息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the resource to the problem: daytime supervision and caregiver respite point to adult day services.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将资源与问题对应：白天监督和照护者喘息通常指向成人日间照护服务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1331,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_fib_smart_goal_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.155","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.155.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.155.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[205,240],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,72],"fullStemEn":"A client with a chronic illness says, \"I want to be healthier.\" The nurse and client revise the goal to: \"I will walk for 10 minutes after breakfast on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday for the next 2 weeks.\" This is an example of a _____ goal.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性病患者说：“我想更健康。”护士和患者把目标改为：“接下来2周，我将在周一、周三和周五早餐后步行10分钟。”这是一个_____目标的例子。","terminalSentenceEn":"This is an example of a _____ goal.","terminalSentenceZh":"这是一个_____目标的例子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse and client revise the goal to: \"I will walk for 10 minutes after breakfast on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday for the next 2 weeks.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士和患者把目标改为：“接下来2周，我将在周一、周三和周五早餐后步行10分钟。”","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"goal type","zh":"目标类型"},"acceptable":["SMART","smart","S.M.A.R.T.","SMART goal","smart goal"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The revised goal is specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, and time-bound. SMART goals help clients turn broad intentions into concrete self-management actions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"修订后的目标具体、可衡量、可达成、相关并有时间限制。SMART目标帮助患者把宽泛意愿转化为具体的自我管理行动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A vague wellness goal becomes stronger when it names the behavior, schedule, and time frame.","testTakingStrategyZh":"模糊的健康目标若明确行为、时间安排和期限，就更有可执行性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1332,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_10_fib_occupational_therapy_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.156","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.156.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.156.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,59],"fullStemEn":"Before discharge from rehabilitation, a client has difficulty bathing and dressing safely with one-sided weakness. The nurse requests a referral for adaptive equipment and activities-of-daily-living training from _____ therapy.","fullStemZh":"康复出院前，一名单侧无力的患者在安全洗澡和穿衣方面有困难。护士请求由_____治疗进行辅助设备和日常生活活动训练评估。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse requests a referral for adaptive equipment and activities-of-daily-living training from _____ therapy.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士请求由_____治疗进行辅助设备和日常生活活动训练评估。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Before discharge from rehabilitation, a client has difficulty bathing and dressing safely with one-sided weakness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"康复出院前，一名单侧无力的患者在安全洗澡和穿衣方面有困难。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"therapy discipline","zh":"治疗专业"},"acceptable":["occupational","occupational therapy","OT","Occupational Therapy","作业","作业治疗"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Occupational therapy focuses on activities of daily living, adaptive equipment, energy conservation, and strategies that support safe function at home.","rationaleCorrectZh":"作业治疗重点关注日常生活活动、辅助设备、节能技巧，以及支持居家安全功能的策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For rehabilitation referrals, connect ADLs and adaptive equipment with occupational therapy; connect gait and strengthening with physical therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"康复转介题中，日常生活活动和辅助设备通常对应作业治疗；步态和肌力训练通常对应物理治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1333,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_post_stroke_outpatient_rehab_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.157","itemType":"case_study","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.157.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.157.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,254],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,61],"fullStemEn":"Case study: post-stroke outpatient rehabilitation and safe feeding A client recovering from stroke receives a home-health rehabilitation visit. The nurse evaluates communication supports, dysphagia precautions, caregiver teaching, and community barriers.","fullStemZh":"病例：卒中后门诊康复与安全进食 一名卒中恢复期患者接受居家康复访视。护士评估沟通支持、吞咽困难预防、照护者教学和社区障碍。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates communication supports, dysphagia precautions, caregiver teaching, and community barriers.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士评估沟通支持、吞咽困难预防、照护者教学和社区障碍。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Case study: post-stroke outpatient rehabilitation and safe feeding A client recovering from stroke receives a home-health rehabilitation visit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病例：卒中后门诊康复与安全进食 一名卒中恢复期患者接受居家康复访视。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case uses exhibit data to guide nursing judgment for post-stroke outpatient rehabilitation and safe feeding, with emphasis on safe assessment, teaching, and follow-up planning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例使用资料中的线索来指导与“Post-stroke outpatient rehabilitation and safe feeding”相关的护理判断，重点是安全评估、教学和随访计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In case studies, match each action to the specific cue in the exhibit rather than relying on a generic care plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"病例题中，应把每项护理措施与资料中的具体线索相匹配，而不是套用笼统护理计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1334,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_post_stroke_outpatient_rehab_09","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_post_stroke_rehab_part_1_matrix_cues","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,38],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,16],"fullStemEn":"Classify each cue from the home visit.","fullStemZh":"对居家访视中的每条线索进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each cue from the home visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"对居家访视中的每条线索进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Coughing after thin water through a straw","zh":"用吸管喝普通清水后咳嗽"},{"id":"r2","en":"Client points accurately to pictures","zh":"患者能准确指图片"},{"id":"r3","en":"Two speech therapy visits canceled because transportation was unavailable","zh":"因无交通，两次言语治疗被取消"},{"id":"r4","en":"Food pocketed in the right cheek","zh":"右颊有食物滞留"},{"id":"r5","en":"Lost 4 lb since discharge","zh":"出院后体重下降4磅"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Care-coordination barrier","zh":"照护协调障碍"},{"id":"c1","en":"Swallowing or nutrition risk","zh":"吞咽或营养风险"},{"id":"c2","en":"Communication support","zh":"沟通支持"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Coughing with thin liquids, wet voice, pocketing, and weight loss indicate swallowing/nutrition risk. Accurate picture pointing and one-step command following show useful communication supports. Missed speech therapy due to transportation is a care-coordination barrier.","rationaleCorrectZh":"喝普通液体后咳嗽、声音湿浊、口腔滞留和体重下降提示吞咽/营养风险。能准确指图片和遵循一步指令显示可用的沟通支持。因交通问题错过言语治疗是照护协调障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the specialist plan in the exhibit to decide whether a caregiver action is safe or unsafe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用资料中的专科计划判断照护者措施是否安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1335,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_post_stroke_outpatient_rehab_09","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_post_stroke_rehab_part_2_order_feeding","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Place the caregiver’s feeding actions in the safest order according to the swallowing plan.","fullStemZh":"根据吞咽计划，将照护者的喂食措施按最安全顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the caregiver’s feeding actions in the safest order according to the swallowing plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据吞咽计划，将照护者的喂食措施按最安全顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Check the right cheek and listen for coughing or a wet-sounding voice during the meal.","zh":"进食中检查右颊，并留意咳嗽或湿浊声音。"},{"id":"E","en":"Stop feeding and contact the rehabilitation team if coughing, wet voice, fever, or reduced intake occurs.","zh":"若出现咳嗽、湿浊声音、发热或摄入减少，停止喂食并联系康复团队。"},{"id":"C","en":"Offer small bites and sips without using a straw.","zh":"给予小口食物和液体，不使用吸管。"},{"id":"B","en":"Position the client upright at 90 degrees before oral intake.","zh":"经口进食前让患者保持90度坐直。"},{"id":"A","en":"Confirm the client is alert and that minced-and-moist foods and mildly thick liquids are prepared.","zh":"确认患者清醒，并准备好细碎湿润食物和轻度增稠液体。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The caregiver should first verify the client is alert and the correct diet/liquid level is available, then position upright, provide small bites/sips without a straw, monitor for pocketing and wet voice/coughing, and stop/contact the team if warning signs occur.","rationaleCorrectZh":"照护者应先确认患者清醒且有正确食物/液体质地，再让患者坐直，使用小口进食/饮用且不使用吸管，监测口腔滞留和湿浊声音/咳嗽；若出现警示信号，应停止并联系团队。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For feeding-safety sequences, prepare and position before offering food, then monitor and escalate if warning signs appear.","testTakingStrategyZh":"喂食安全排序中，先准备和摆位，再提供食物，随后监测并在警示信号出现时升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1336,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_post_stroke_outpatient_rehab_09","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_post_stroke_rehab_part_3_sata_teaching","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,23],"fullStemEn":"Which caregiver teaching points should the nurse reinforce? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应强化哪些照护者教学要点？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which caregiver teaching points should the nurse reinforce?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应强化哪些照护者教学要点？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use the picture board, yes/no questions, one-step instructions, and extra response time.","zh":"使用图片板、是/否问题、一步指令，并给予额外回应时间。"},{"id":"F","en":"Answer questions for the client to reduce frustration.","zh":"为了减少挫败感，替患者回答问题。"},{"id":"C","en":"Call the rehabilitation team for coughing, wet voice, fever, reduced intake, or continued weight loss.","zh":"若出现咳嗽、声音湿浊、发热、摄入减少或持续体重下降，联系康复团队。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask for help arranging transportation so speech therapy visits can resume.","zh":"寻求帮助安排交通，使言语治疗能恢复。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use mildly thick liquids and avoid straws unless the swallowing plan changes.","zh":"使用轻度增稠液体，并在吞咽计划改变前避免吸管。"},{"id":"E","en":"Offer thin water by straw when the client refuses thickened liquids.","zh":"当患者拒绝增稠液体时，用吸管提供普通清水。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teaching should follow the SLP plan, support communication without rushing, and identify warning signs and missed therapy as follow-up needs. Thin liquids through a straw and speaking for the client undermine the plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"教学应遵循言语治疗计划，支持不催促的沟通，并识别警示信号和错过治疗的随访需求。用吸管喝普通液体以及替患者说话会破坏计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Correct caregiver teaching usually reinforces the written interdisciplinary plan and removes barriers to carrying it out.","testTakingStrategyZh":"正确的照护者教学通常强化书面跨专业计划，并消除执行障碍。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1337,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_post_stroke_outpatient_rehab_09","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_post_stroke_rehab_part_4_cloze_priority","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.157.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,41],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,8],"fullStemEn":"Complete the care-coordination statement.","fullStemZh":"完成照护协调句。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the care-coordination statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成照护协调句。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should prioritize {{1}} because the exhibit shows {{2}}.","zh":"护士应优先 {{1}}，因为资料显示 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"encouraging the caregiver to continue the current routine","zh":"鼓励照护者继续当前做法"},{"id":"o3","en":"waiting until the next primary care visit","zh":"等到下次初级保健复诊"},{"id":"o1","en":"contacting the rehabilitation team and arranging transportation support","zh":"联系康复团队并安排交通支持"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"swallowing warning signs and missed therapy visits","zh":"吞咽警示信号和错过治疗预约"},{"id":"o2","en":"normal adaptation to aphasia only","zh":"仅为失语后的正常适应"},{"id":"o3","en":"complete caregiver mastery of the plan","zh":"照护者已完全掌握计划"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority is to contact the rehabilitation team and address transportation barriers because the client has active swallowing warning signs and has missed speech therapy appointments needed for safe recovery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先事项是联系康复团队并处理交通障碍，因为患者有正在出现的吞咽警示信号，并错过了安全康复所需的言语治疗预约。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When two problems interact, choose the action that addresses both safety and the system barrier.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当两个问题相互影响时，选择同时处理安全和系统障碍的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1338,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_grief_depression_safety_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.158","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.158.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.158.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,56],"fullStemEn":"Case study: depression, grief, and safety screening A widowed client has a positive depression screen during a wellness visit. The nurse evaluates safety, therapeutic communication, supports, and follow-up planning.","fullStemZh":"病例：抑郁、哀伤与安全筛查 一名丧偶患者在健康访视中抑郁筛查阳性。护士评估安全、治疗性沟通、支持系统和随访计划。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates safety, therapeutic communication, supports, and follow-up planning.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士评估安全、治疗性沟通、支持系统和随访计划。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Case study: depression, grief, and safety screening A widowed client has a positive depression screen during a wellness visit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病例：抑郁、哀伤与安全筛查 一名丧偶患者在健康访视中抑郁筛查阳性。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case uses exhibit data to guide nursing judgment for depression and grief safety screening, with emphasis on safe assessment, teaching, and follow-up planning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例使用资料中的线索来指导与“Depression and grief safety screening”相关的护理判断，重点是安全评估、教学和随访计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In case studies, match each action to the specific cue in the exhibit rather than relying on a generic care plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"病例题中，应把每项护理措施与资料中的具体线索相匹配，而不是套用笼统护理计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1339,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_grief_depression_safety_10","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_grief_depression_part_1_mc_priority","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,36],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,11],"fullStemEn":"What is the nurse’s priority action?","fullStemZh":"护士的优先措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse’s priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的优先措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Call the daughter immediately and disclose all screening results before speaking further with the client.","zh":"立即打电话给女儿，并在进一步与患者谈话前透露所有筛查结果。"},{"id":"C","en":"Schedule a routine follow-up visit in 1 month to repeat the PHQ-9.","zh":"安排1个月后常规随访并重复PHQ-9。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask directly about suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, and access to lethal means, and notify the provider or crisis clinician before the client leaves.","zh":"直接询问自杀想法、意图、计划和致命手段可及性，并在患者离开前通知医师或危机干预人员。"},{"id":"B","en":"Reassure the client that grief commonly lasts longer than 3 months and provide a brochure.","zh":"安慰患者悲伤通常会超过3个月，并提供宣传册。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The exhibit includes passive death wishes, a positive PHQ-9 item 9, alcohol use, withdrawal, weight loss, and firearm access. The priority is direct suicide risk assessment and escalation according to clinic policy before the client leaves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"资料包含被动死亡愿望、PHQ-9第9项阳性、饮酒、退缩、体重下降和枪支可及性。优先措施是在患者离开前按门诊政策进行直接自杀风险评估并升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Positive safety cues require direct questions; asking about suicide does not “put the idea” in the client’s mind.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全筛查阳性需要直接提问；询问自杀不会“让患者产生这个念头”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1340,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_grief_depression_safety_10","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_grief_depression_part_2_matrix_cues","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,33],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,14],"fullStemEn":"Classify each cue from the visit.","fullStemZh":"对访视中的每条线索进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each cue from the visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"对访视中的每条线索进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"PHQ-9 item 9 marked “several days”","zh":"PHQ-9第9项标记为“有几天”"},{"id":"r2","en":"Stopped church and walking group activities","zh":"停止参加教会和步行小组活动"},{"id":"r3","en":"Spouse’s handgun is locked in a closet at home","zh":"配偶的手枪锁在家中衣柜里"},{"id":"r4","en":"Adult daughter calls weekly and offered to come to appointments","zh":"成年女儿每周打电话并愿意陪同就诊"},{"id":"r5","en":"Drinks 2–3 alcoholic drinks most nights","zh":"多数晚上饮酒2–3杯"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Depression/grief concern","zh":"抑郁/悲伤相关问题"},{"id":"c3","en":"Protective support","zh":"保护性支持"},{"id":"c1","en":"Urgent safety cue","zh":"紧急安全线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Positive item 9, passive death wishes, alcohol use, firearm access, and withdrawal increase safety concern and depression risk. Daughter support is protective. Grief after loss is expected, but the severity and safety cues require more than reassurance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第9项阳性、被动死亡愿望、饮酒、枪支可及性和社交退缩会增加安全问题和抑郁风险。女儿支持是保护因素。丧偶后悲伤可预期，但严重程度和安全线索需要的不只是安慰。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For psychosocial cue questions, identify safety cues separately from expected emotions after loss.","testTakingStrategyZh":"心理社会线索题中，要把安全线索与丧失后的预期情绪区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1341,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_grief_depression_safety_10","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_grief_depression_part_3_cloze_plan","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,41],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,8],"fullStemEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement.","fullStemZh":"完成临床判断句。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成临床判断句。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is at increased risk for {{1}} as evidenced by {{2}}.","zh":"患者发生 {{1}} 的风险增加，依据是 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"delirium from acute infection","zh":"急性感染导致的谵妄"},{"id":"o1","en":"self-harm or suicide","zh":"自伤或自杀"},{"id":"o2","en":"normal bereavement without safety concern","zh":"无安全问题的正常哀伤"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"denial of a current plan only","zh":"仅否认当前计划"},{"id":"o1","en":"positive PHQ-9 item 9, passive death wish, alcohol use, and firearm access","zh":"PHQ-9第9项阳性、被动死亡愿望、饮酒和枪支可及性"},{"id":"o2","en":"weekly calls from the adult daughter only","zh":"仅有成年女儿每周来电"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The best-supported risk is self-harm/suicide risk because the record includes a positive PHQ-9 safety item, passive death wish, alcohol use, and access to a firearm. The client denies a plan, but denial does not remove the need for direct assessment and safety planning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最有证据支持的风险是自伤/自杀风险，因为记录中有PHQ-9安全项阳性、被动死亡愿望、饮酒和枪支可及性。患者否认计划，但这并不能取消直接评估和安全计划的需要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client denies a plan, keep assessing the other risk cues instead of dismissing the concern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者否认计划时，仍要继续评估其他风险线索，而不是排除问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1342,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_grief_depression_safety_10","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_grief_depression_part_4_sata_safety","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.158.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"Which actions should the nurse include in the safety-focused plan before the client leaves? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在患者离开前，护士应在以安全为重点的计划中包括哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse include in the safety-focused plan before the client leaves?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在患者离开前，护士应在以安全为重点的计划中包括哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Ask permission to involve the adult daughter or another support person in the safety plan.","zh":"征求同意，将成年女儿或其他支持者纳入安全计划。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the provider or crisis clinician before the client leaves the clinic.","zh":"在患者离开诊所前通知医师或危机干预人员。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess access to the handgun and discuss safe removal or secure storage according to policy.","zh":"评估手枪可及性，并按政策讨论移除或安全保管。"},{"id":"E","en":"Promise the client that the discussion will stay secret from the care team.","zh":"向患者承诺这次谈话不会告诉照护团队。"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide crisis resources and a written plan for what to do if thoughts worsen.","zh":"提供危机资源和书面计划，说明想法加重时该怎么做。"},{"id":"F","en":"Explain that these feelings are normal grief and no further assessment is needed today.","zh":"解释这些感受是正常悲伤，今天不需要进一步评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The safety plan should include provider/crisis notification, direct assessment, lethal-means safety, supportive involvement with permission, crisis resources, and prompt follow-up. The nurse should not promise secrecy or dismiss the findings as normal grief only.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全计划应包括通知医师/危机干预人员、直接评估、致命手段安全、经同意纳入支持者、危机资源和及时随访。护士不应承诺保密，也不应仅将发现视为正常悲伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In safety questions, confidentiality has limits when there is risk of harm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全题中，当存在伤害风险时，保密有界限。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
