AID暴露支持肾前性AKI并伴肾毒性风险。亚硝酸盐阴性不能解释肾灌注不足。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare current renal values with baseline and connect medication exposure to perfusion status.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将当前肾功能与基线比较，并把药物暴露与灌注状态联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1442,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_aki_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_aki_cloze_02","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,63],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,15],"fullStemEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement using the latest data.","fullStemZh":"使用最新资料完成临床判断陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement using the latest data.","terminalSentenceZh":"使用最新资料完成临床判断陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The priority complication is {{1}} caused by {{2}}.","zh":"优先关注的并发症是由{{2}}导致的{{1}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"life-threatening dysrhythmia","zh":"危及生命的心律失常"},{"id":"o2","en":"fluid volume deficit only","zh":"单纯液体容量不足"},{"id":"o3","en":"uncomplicated viral gastroenteritis","zh":"无并发症的病毒性胃肠炎"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"negative urine nitrites","zh":"尿亚硝酸盐阴性"},{"id":"o1","en":"potassium 6.2 mEq/L with peaked T waves","zh":"钾6.2 mEq/L并出现高尖T波"},{"id":"o2","en":"dry mucous membranes without ECG changes","zh":"黏膜干燥但无心电变化"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe hyperkalemia with ECG changes is immediately dangerous because it can progress to lethal dysrhythmias.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重高钾并伴心电图改变具有即时危险性，可进展为致命心律失常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a lab abnormality has ECG or neurologic changes, treat it as an unstable complication, not a routine lab result.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当实验室异常伴有心电或神经变化时，应视为不稳定并发症，而非常规异常。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1443,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_aki_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_aki_or_03","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,52],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Place the actions in priority order for this client.","fullStemZh":"将该患者的处理措施按优先顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in priority order for this client.","terminalSentenceZh":"将该患者的处理措施按优先顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Prepare to administer prescribed IV calcium and potassium-shifting therapy.","zh":"准备遵医嘱给予静脉钙剂及促钾转移治疗。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client on continuous cardiac monitoring and obtain a stat ECG.","zh":"将患者置于连续心电监护并立即获取心电图。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider/rapid response team of hyperkalemia with ECG changes.","zh":"将高钾伴心电改变通知医嘱提供者/快速反应团队。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop potassium-containing fluids/supplements and hold nephrotoxic or potassium-raising medications pending provider direction.","zh":"停止含钾液体/补充剂，并在医嘱指导前暂停肾毒性或升钾药物。"},{"id":"E","en":"Recheck potassium, glucose, ECG rhythm, and urine output after treatment.","zh":"治疗后复查钾、血糖、心律和尿量。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ECG changes require immediate monitoring, removal of ongoing potassium/renal insults, urgent escalation, prescribed stabilization and shifting therapy, then reassessment for recurrence and treatment effects.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出现心电改变需立即监测，去除持续钾负荷/肾损伤因素，紧急升级处理，按医嘱给予稳定心肌和促钾转移治疗，然后复评复发和治疗效果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Sequence unstable electrolytes by monitoring first, removing contributors, escalating, treating, then reassessing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不稳定电解质问题按监测、去除诱因、升级、治疗、复评排序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1444,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_aki_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_aki_fib_04","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.185.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,40],"fullStemEn":"The client weighs 80 kg. Calculate the urine output for the last 8 hr in mL/kg/hr. Round to the nearest hundredth.","fullStemZh":"患者体重80 kg。计算过去8小时的尿量（mL/kg/hr），四舍五入到百分位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest hundredth.","terminalSentenceZh":"计算过去8小时的尿量（mL/kg/hr），四舍五入到百分位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the urine output for the last 8 hr in mL/kg/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者体重80 kg。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/kg/hr","zh":"mL/kg/hr"},"acceptable":["0.19","0.19 mL/kg/hr"],"numeric":{"value":0.19,"tolerance":0.01,"unit":"mL/kg/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Urine output is 120 mL ÷ 80 kg ÷ 8 hr = 0.1875 mL/kg/hr, rounded to 0.19 mL/kg/hr. This is oliguria and supports ongoing AKI risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尿量=120 mL ÷ 80 kg ÷ 8 hr = 0.1875 mL/kg/hr，四舍五入为0.19 mL/kg/hr。这属于少尿，支持AKI风险仍在持续。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For urine-output calculations, always include both weight and time in the denominator.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算尿量时，分母一定要同时包括体重和时间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
