ecognition is source plus organ dysfunction, not fever alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别脓毒症要看感染源加器官功能障碍，而不是只看发热。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1457,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_urosepsis_05","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_sepsis_cloze_02","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,52],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,10],"fullStemEn":"Complete the statement describing the deterioration.","fullStemZh":"完成描述恶化的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement describing the deterioration.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成描述恶化的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is developing {{1}}, as shown by {{2}}.","zh":"患者正在发展为{{1}}，表现为{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"uncomplicated cystitis","zh":"无并发症膀胱炎"},{"id":"o3","en":"isolated fever without perfusion change","zh":"单纯发热且无灌注改变"},{"id":"o1","en":"septic shock physiology","zh":"脓毒性休克生理状态"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"hypotension after fluid, rising lactate, cool skin, and oliguria","zh":"补液后仍低血压、乳酸升高、皮肤发凉和少尿"},{"id":"o2","en":"positive leukocyte esterase alone","zh":"单纯白细胞酯酶阳性"},{"id":"o3","en":"room-air oxygen saturation of 96%","zh":"室内空气氧饱和度96%"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Persistent hypotension with rising lactate and low urine output indicates worsening perfusion despite initial fluid, consistent with septic shock physiology.","rationaleCorrectZh":"初始补液后仍低血压，伴乳酸升高和尿量低，提示灌注恶化，符合脓毒性休克生理状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not be reassured by normal SpO2 when perfusion markers are worsening.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当灌注指标恶化时，不要因氧饱和度正常而放心。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1458,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_urosepsis_05","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_sepsis_or_03","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,64],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,16],"fullStemEn":"Place the actions in the order the nurse should prioritize them.","fullStemZh":"按护士应优先处理的顺序排列措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in the order the nurse should prioritize them.","terminalSentenceZh":"按护士应优先处理的顺序排列措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Activate the sepsis/rapid response pathway and communicate suspected urinary source with obstruction.","zh":"启动脓毒症/快速反应流程，并沟通疑似梗阻性泌尿感染源。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer prescribed broad-spectrum antibiotics promptly.","zh":"及时遵医嘱给予广谱抗生素。"},{"id":"E","en":"Prepare for vasopressor support and urgent source-control procedures if hypotension persists.","zh":"若低血压持续，准备血管活性药支持和紧急感染源控制操作。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ensure blood and urine cultures and lactate are obtained or verified without delaying antibiotics.","zh":"确保或核实已采集血/尿培养和乳酸，但不延误抗生素。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer prescribed isotonic fluid resuscitation and monitor lung sounds and perfusion.","zh":"遵医嘱给予等渗液体复苏，并监测肺音和灌注。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse escalates immediately, verifies cultures/lactate as part of the sepsis bundle, gives antibiotics promptly, supports perfusion with ordered fluids, and anticipates vasopressors/source control when shock persists.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士立即升级处理，核实培养/乳酸作为脓毒症组合措施的一部分，及时给抗生素，按医嘱补液支持灌注，并在休克持续时预见血管活性药和感染源控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In sepsis, think: escalate, cultures/lactate, antibiotics, fluids, reassess for pressors and source control.","testTakingStrategyZh":"脓毒症可按：升级、培养/乳酸、抗生素、补液、复评是否需升压药和感染源控制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1459,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_urosepsis_05","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_sepsis_fib_04","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.188.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[25,97],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,39],"fullStemEn":"The client weighs 70 kg. Calculate the minimum expected urine output in mL/hr using 0.5 mL/kg/hr.","fullStemZh":"患者体重70 kg。按0.5 mL/kg/hr计算最低预期尿量（mL/hr）。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the minimum expected urine output in mL/hr using 0.5 mL/kg/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"按0.5 mL/kg/hr计算最低预期尿量（mL/hr）。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client weighs 70 kg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者体重70 kg。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/hr"},"acceptable":["35","35 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":35,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"70 kg × 0.5 mL/kg/hr = 35 mL/hr. The current 25 mL/hr remains below the minimum target and suggests ongoing renal hypoperfusion risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"70 kg × 0.5 mL/kg/hr = 35 mL/hr。当前25 mL/hr仍低于最低目标，提示肾低灌注风险持续。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A partial improvement still requires action when it remains below the expected threshold.","testTakingStrategyZh":"即使有所改善，只要仍低于预期阈值就需要继续处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1460,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_anticoag_bleeding_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.189","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.189.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.189.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,56],"fullStemEn":"Heparin complication with occult bleeding and platelet decline A client receiving unfractionated heparin develops supratherapeutic anticoagulation, occult bleeding signs, shock, and a clinically important platelet decline.","fullStemZh":"肝素并发隐匿性出血和血小板下降 接受普通肝素的患者出现抗凝过度、隐匿性出血体征、休克和具有临床意义的血小板下降。","terminalSentenceEn":"Heparin complication with occult bleeding and platelet decline A client receiving unfractionated heparin develops supratherapeutic anticoagulation, occult bleeding signs, shock, and a clinically important platelet decline.","terminalSentenceZh":"肝素并发隐匿性出血和血小板下降 接受普通肝素的患者出现抗凝过度、隐匿性出血体征、休克和具有临床意义的血小板下降。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case study requires recognizing deterioration across serial assessment data and choosing nursing actions that reduce risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求根据连续评估资料识别病情恶化，并选择降低风险的护理措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In an unfolding case, compare the newest data with baseline and act first on unstable airway, breathing, circulation, perfusion, and safety cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理展开式病例时，先把最新资料与基线比较，并优先处理气道、呼吸、循环、灌注和安全方面的不稳定线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1461,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_anticoag_bleeding_06","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_anticoag_matrix_01","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,42],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,16],"fullStemEn":"Classify each finding in the morning data.","fullStemZh":"对上午资料中的每项发现进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each finding in the morning data.","terminalSentenceZh":"对上午资料中的每项发现进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"aPTT 118 seconds with therapeutic range 60-80 seconds","zh":"aPTT 118秒，治疗范围60–80秒"},{"id":"r2","en":"Anti-Xa above therapeutic range","zh":"抗Xa高于治疗范围"},{"id":"r3","en":"Platelet count decreased from 226 to 154 ×10³/µL","zh":"血小板由226降至154 ×10³/µL"},{"id":"r4","en":"Infusion pump settings match the prescription","zh":"输液泵设置与医嘱一致"},{"id":"r5","en":"Improving pleuritic chest pain","zh":"胸膜性胸痛改善"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Reassuring/less concerning","zh":"较放心/较不担心"},{"id":"c1","en":"Requires prompt follow-up","zh":"需要及时跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Supratherapeutic anticoagulation and a falling platelet count require follow-up even if the pump is programmed correctly and PE symptoms are improving.","rationaleCorrectZh":"抗凝过度和血小板下降即使在泵设置正确、肺栓塞症状改善时也需要跟进。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let symptom improvement distract from therapy-monitoring complications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因症状改善而忽视治疗监测中的并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1462,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_anticoag_bleeding_06","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_anticoag_cloze_02","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,58],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,13],"fullStemEn":"Complete the priority interpretation of the sudden change.","fullStemZh":"完成对突发变化的优先解读。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the priority interpretation of the sudden change.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成对突发变化的优先解读。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is most likely experiencing {{1}} evidenced by {{2}}.","zh":"该患者最可能正在发生{{1}}，证据为{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"internal bleeding, possibly retroperitoneal","zh":"内出血，可能为腹膜后出血"},{"id":"o2","en":"expected pulmonary embolism recovery pain","zh":"肺栓塞恢复期预期疼痛"},{"id":"o3","en":"minor bruising without instability","zh":"无不稳定的轻微瘀斑"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"absence of visible external bleeding","zh":"没有可见外出血"},{"id":"o1","en":"new flank/abdominal pain, hypotension, tachycardia, hemoglobin drop, and aPTT >200 seconds","zh":"新发腰/腹痛、低血压、心动过速、血红蛋白下降及aPTT >200秒"},{"id":"o2","en":"improving oxygen saturation and correct pump settings","zh":"氧饱和度改善和泵设置正确"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden flank or abdominal pain with shock signs and a large hemoglobin drop during excessive heparin effect suggests occult internal bleeding such as retroperitoneal hemorrhage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝素作用过强期间突发腰/腹痛，伴休克体征和血红蛋白明显下降，提示隐匿性内出血，如腹膜后出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With anticoagulants, new pain plus shock is bleeding until proven otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用抗凝药时，新发疼痛加休克应先按出血处理，直到证实不是。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1463,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_anticoag_bleeding_06","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_anticoag_or_03","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,36],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,10],"fullStemEn":"Place the actions in priority order.","fullStemZh":"按优先顺序排列措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in priority order.","terminalSentenceZh":"按优先顺序排列措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Stop the heparin infusion according to protocol and keep IV access patent with non-heparinized fluid as appropriate.","zh":"按流程停止肝素输注，并根据情况用非肝素液体保持静脉通路通畅。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess airway, breathing, circulation, pain, neurologic status, and visible/occult bleeding cues.","zh":"评估气道、呼吸、循环、疼痛、神经状态及可见/隐匿出血线索。"},{"id":"C","en":"Activate rapid response/provider notification for suspected major bleeding with shock.","zh":"因疑似重大出血伴休克启动快速反应/通知医嘱提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare for prescribed reversal/supportive therapy, stat CBC/coagulation tests, type and screen, and imaging.","zh":"准备遵医嘱进行拮抗/支持治疗、急查CBC/凝血、备血筛查和影像检查。"},{"id":"E","en":"Continue frequent vital signs, pain, neurovascular checks, and repeat hemoglobin/platelets per protocol.","zh":"按流程继续频繁监测生命体征、疼痛、神经血管情况及复查血红蛋白/血小板。"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first assesses ABC/perfusion severity, stops the medication contributing to bleeding per protocol, escalates urgently, prepares reversal and diagnostic support, and monitors for ongoing hemorrhage or HIT-related complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先评估ABC/灌注严重程度，按流程停止促成出血的药物，紧急升级，准备拮抗和诊断支持，并监测持续出血或HIT相关并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For anticoagulant emergencies, assess first, stop the anticoagulant source, escalate, prepare reversal/diagnostics, then trend response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝急症按：先评估、停止抗凝来源、升级、准备拮抗/诊断、再追踪反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1464,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_case_anticoag_bleeding_06","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gap_2026_06_11_anticoag_fib_04","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.189.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[90,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,49],"fullStemEn":"Calculate the percent decrease in platelet count from baseline 226 ×10³/µL to 96 ×10³/µL. Round to the nearest whole percent.","fullStemZh":"计算血小板从基线226 ×10³/µL降至96 ×10³/µL的百分比下降，四舍五入到整数百分比。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole percent.","terminalSentenceZh":"计算血小板从基线226 ×10³/µL降至96 ×10³/µL的百分比下降，四舍五入到整数百分比。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the percent decrease in platelet count from baseline 226 ×10³/µL to 96 ×10³/µL.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Percent decrease","zh":"下降百分比"},"acceptable":["58","58%","58 percent"],"numeric":{"value":58,"tolerance":1,"unit":"%"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The decrease is 226,000 - 96,000 = 130,000. 130,000 ÷ 226,000 × 100 = 57.5%, rounded to 58%. A fall of about 50% or more during heparin therapy requires HIT evaluation while bleeding is also addressed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"下降量=226,000 - 96,000 = 130,000。130,000 ÷ 226,000 × 100 = 57.5%，四舍五入为58%。肝素治疗期间下降约50%或更多需评估HIT，同时处理出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For platelet trends, the percentage drop can matter even when the absolute count is not extremely low.","testTakingStrategyZh":"血小板趋势中，即使绝对值不是极低，下降百分比也很重要。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1465,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_restraint_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.190","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.190.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.190.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,211],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,61],"fullStemEn":"A client with delirium repeatedly pulls at a new surgical drain despite verbal redirection. A vest restraint is being considered to prevent removal of the drain. Arrange the nursing actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名谵妄患者虽经口头引导仍反复拉扯新置入的手术引流管。护士正考虑使用背心约束以防止引流管被拔出。请按正确顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nursing actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A vest restraint is being considered to prevent removal of the drain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正考虑使用背心约束以防止引流管被拔出。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Explain the reason for the restraint and expected reassessment plan to the client and family in simple terms.","zh":"用简单语言向患者和家属解释约束原因以及后续重新评估计划。"},{"id":"A","en":"Attempt and document least-restrictive alternatives, such as reorientation, pain/toileting needs, family presence, and moving tubes out of reach.","zh":"先尝试并记录限制性最小的替代措施，如重新定向、处理疼痛/如厕需求、请家属陪伴、将管路移至患者不易触及处。"},{"id":"B","en":"Obtain or verify a current, time-limited provider order that specifies the reason and type of restraint.","zh":"取得或核实现行的、有时限的医嘱，明确约束原因和约束类型。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply the restraint according to policy, then assess circulation, skin, breathing, elimination needs, and provide range-of-motion exercises at least every 2 hours.","zh":"按制度正确使用约束，随后至少每2小时评估循环、皮肤、呼吸、排泄需求，并进行关节活动度练习。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document assessments and client response, and reassess whether the restraint can be discontinued as soon as safety permits.","zh":"记录评估结果和患者反应，并持续评估在安全允许时是否可尽快解除约束。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Restraints are used only after less restrictive measures fail, with a current provider order and clear explanation. Once applied, the nurse performs frequent safety assessments, range-of-motion care, documentation, and ongoing reassessment for early discontinuation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"约束只能在限制性较小的措施无效后使用，并且需要有现行医嘱和清楚解释。使用后，护士需频繁进行安全评估、关节活动护理、记录，并持续评估是否可尽早解除。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For restraint questions, think: alternatives first, order and explanation next, monitor frequently, document, and remove as soon as possible.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到约束题，按“先替代措施、再医嘱和解释、频繁监测、记录、尽快解除”的顺序思考。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1466,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_fib_cauti_prevention_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.191","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.191.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.191.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[275,355],"terminalOffsetsZh":[71,105],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing catheter-associated urinary tract infection (CAUTI) prevention with a new graduate nurse. Complete the teaching statement: The single most effective prevention measure is to remove an indwelling urinary catheter when it is no longer medically necessary. Catheter necessity should be reassessed at least every ____ hours, or once ____.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向一名新护士复习导尿管相关尿路感染（CAUTI）的预防措施。完成教学内容：最有效的预防措施是在留置导尿管不再具有医学必要性时将其拔除。应至少每 ____ 小时重新评估导尿管必要性，或每天 ____ 次。","terminalSentenceEn":"Catheter necessity should be reassessed at least every ____ hours, or once ____.","terminalSentenceZh":"应至少每 ____ 小时重新评估导尿管必要性，或每天 ____ 次。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Complete the teaching statement: The single most effective prevention measure is to remove an indwelling urinary catheter when it is no longer medically necessary.","penultimateSentenceZh":"完成教学内容：最有效的预防措施是在留置导尿管不再具有医学必要性时将其拔除。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Maximum hours between catheter-necessity reassessments","zh":"两次导尿管必要性重新评估之间的最长小时数"},"acceptable":["24","24 hours","twenty-four","twenty four"],"numeric":{"value":24,"tolerance":0,"unit":"hours"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Minimum daily reassessment frequency","zh":"最低每日重新评估频率"},"acceptable":["daily","once daily","1","1 time","one time","one"],"numeric":{"value":1,"tolerance":0,"unit":"time per day"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most effective CAUTI prevention strategy is avoiding unnecessary catheter days. A daily or every-24-hour necessity review prompts removal as soon as there is no appropriate indication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防CAUTI最有效的策略是避免不必要的导尿管留置天数。每日或每24小时评估必要性，可促使在没有适应证时尽快拔除导尿管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For device-associated infection prevention, the safest answer often removes the device as soon as it is not needed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到器械相关感染预防题，最安全的答案通常是在不再需要时尽快移除器械。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1467,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_sata_tb_airborne_precautions_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.192","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.192.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.192.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[163,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,50],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with cough, night sweats, weight loss, and a chest x-ray suspicious for active pulmonary tuberculosis. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因咳嗽、盗汗、体重减轻入院，胸片提示疑似活动性肺结核。哪些护理措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Require staff entering the room to wear a fit-tested N95 or higher-level respirator.","zh":"要求进入病房的工作人员佩戴经过适合性测试的N95或更高级别呼吸防护口罩。"},{"id":"C","en":"Have the client wear a surgical mask if transport outside the room is medically necessary.","zh":"如因医学需要必须离开房间转运，患者应佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the door to the isolation room closed except when entering or exiting.","zh":"除进出时外，保持隔离病房门关闭。"},{"id":"E","en":"Notify infection prevention or infection control personnel according to facility policy.","zh":"按机构制度通知感染预防或感染控制人员。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a negative-pressure airborne infection isolation room.","zh":"将患者安置在负压空气传播感染隔离病房。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use droplet precautions with a surgical mask for staff because tuberculosis spreads mainly through large droplets.","zh":"采用飞沫隔离，并让工作人员佩戴外科口罩，因为结核主要通过大飞沫传播。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected active pulmonary TB requires airborne precautions: placement in an airborne infection isolation room, a fit-tested N95 or higher respirator for staff, a surgical mask for medically necessary transport, a closed door, and infection-control notification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似活动性肺结核需要空气传播隔离：安置在空气传播感染隔离病房，工作人员佩戴经过适合性测试的N95或更高级别呼吸防护口罩，必要转运时患者佩戴外科口罩，保持门关闭，并通知感染控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the organism to the transmission route: TB is airborne, so choose AIIR/negative pressure and N95-level respiratory protection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将病原体与传播途径匹配：结核为空气传播，因此选择AIIR/负压和N95级别呼吸防护。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1468,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_sbar_handoff_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.193","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.193.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.193.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is calling the rapid response nurse about a client whose condition is worsening. Arrange the SBAR handoff elements in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在联系快速反应护士，报告一名病情正在恶化的患者。请按正确顺序排列SBAR交接内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the SBAR handoff elements in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列SBAR交接内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is calling the rapid response nurse about a client whose condition is worsening.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在联系快速反应护士，报告一名病情正在恶化的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Background: “He was admitted yesterday with a urinary infection and has received two doses of antibiotics.”","zh":"背景（Background）：“他昨天因尿路感染入院，已接受两剂抗生素。”"},{"id":"C","en":"Assessment: “His temperature is 102.6 °F (39.2 °C), respiratory rate 28/min, blood pressure 88/52 mm Hg, and oxygen saturation 89% on room air.”","zh":"评估（Assessment）：“体温102.6 °F (39.2 °C)，呼吸28次/分，血压88/52 mm Hg，室内空气下血氧饱和度89%。”"},{"id":"A","en":"Situation: “I am calling about Mr. Lee in room 412; he is newly confused and short of breath.”","zh":"情况（Situation）：“我报告412房李先生；他新出现意识混乱和呼吸困难。”"},{"id":"D","en":"Recommendation: “Please come now to evaluate him; I am applying oxygen and will obtain repeat vital signs.”","zh":"建议（Recommendation）：“请立即来评估他；我正在给氧，并会复查生命体征。”"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"SBAR standardizes urgent communication by starting with the immediate situation, then relevant background, current assessment, and a clear recommendation or request.","rationaleCorrectZh":"SBAR通过先说明当前情况，再说明相关背景、当前评估和明确建议/请求，使紧急沟通标准化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember SBAR in order: Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住SBAR顺序：情况、背景、评估、建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1469,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_cloze_teach_back_hf_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.194","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.194.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.194.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,33],"fullStemEn":"A nurse has taught a client with newly diagnosed heart failure about a sodium-restricted diet and daily weights before discharge.","fullStemZh":"护士在出院前已向一名新诊断为心力衰竭的患者讲解限钠饮食和每日称重。","terminalSentenceEn":"A nurse has taught a client with newly diagnosed heart failure about a sodium-restricted diet and daily weights before discharge.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在出院前已向一名新诊断为心力衰竭的患者讲解限钠饮食和每日称重。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To evaluate discharge readiness, the nurse should {{1}} because it {{2}}. If the client cannot demonstrate the skill, the nurse should {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"为评估出院准备情况，护士应 {{1}}，因为这能 {{2}}。如果患者无法展示该技能，护士应 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"ask whether the client has any final questions before leaving","zh":"询问患者离院前是否还有最后的问题"},{"id":"o1","en":"ask the client to explain the weight plan and choose a low-sodium meal from sample labels","zh":"请患者说明每日称重计划，并根据示例食品标签选择低钠餐食"},{"id":"o3","en":"give the client a printed diet sheet and document that teaching is complete","zh":"给患者一张饮食说明单，并记录教学已完成"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"reduces the nurse’s responsibility for follow-up after discharge","zh":"减少护士在出院后随访方面的责任"},{"id":"o1","en":"checks the client’s ability to apply the instructions in realistic home tasks","zh":"检查患者是否能把教学内容应用到真实居家任务中"},{"id":"o3","en":"proves the client will follow every instruction exactly","zh":"证明患者会完全按照每项指示执行"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"mark the client as nonadherent and ask a family member to sign the instructions","zh":"将患者标记为不依从，并请家属签署说明"},{"id":"o2","en":"delay all discharge planning until the provider writes a new diet order","zh":"暂停所有出院计划，直到医生开具新的饮食医嘱"},{"id":"o1","en":"reteach using focused, simpler information and repeat the teach-back","zh":"用更集中、更简单的信息重新教学，并再次进行回授"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"an unsuccessful teach-back signals that the teaching method needs adjustment","zh":"回授不成功提示教学方法需要调整"},{"id":"o3","en":"a family signature is a substitute for client understanding","zh":"家属签字可以替代患者理解"},{"id":"o2","en":"failure to remember teaching means discharge teaching is no longer useful","zh":"记不住教学内容说明出院教育已无用"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teach-back evaluates whether the client can use discharge instructions, not whether the nurse simply delivered information. If the client cannot demonstrate the skill, the nurse should adjust the teaching and reassess understanding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"回授法评估患者是否能使用出院指导，而不只是护士是否讲过内容。若患者无法展示技能，护士应调整教学方式并重新评估理解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge teaching, choose answers that verify what the client can do, then reteach and reassess if the client cannot demonstrate the skill.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到出院教育题，选择能验证患者会做什么的答案；若不能展示技能，则重新教学并再评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1470,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_cloze_anticipatory_grief_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.195","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.195.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.195.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,50],"fullStemEn":"A 71-year-old client with terminal COPD tells the nurse, “I’ve lived a full life, but I’m scared I’ll be in pain at the end.”","fullStemZh":"一名71岁终末期慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）患者对护士说：“我这一生很充实，但我害怕临终时会疼痛。”","terminalSentenceEn":"A 71-year-old client with terminal COPD tells the nurse, “I’ve lived a full life, but I’m scared I’ll be in pain at the end.”","terminalSentenceZh":"一名71岁终末期慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）患者对护士说：“我这一生很充实，但我害怕临终时会疼痛。”","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse’s best initial response is {{1}} because it demonstrates {{2}}. The nurse should avoid {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"护士最佳的初始回应是 {{1}}，因为它体现了 {{2}}。护士应避免 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"“You should focus on the good years you have had.”","zh":"“您应该把注意力放在过去美好的岁月上。”"},{"id":"o3","en":"“I will ask the provider to increase your pain medicine right now.”","zh":"“我现在就请医生增加您的止痛药。”"},{"id":"o1","en":"“Tell me what worries you most about having pain near the end of life.”","zh":"“请告诉我，关于临终时疼痛，您最担心的是什么。”"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"acknowledgment of fear with an open-ended invitation to discuss concerns","zh":"承认恐惧，并以开放式方式邀请患者表达担忧"},{"id":"o3","en":"giving medication information before assessing the meaning of the concern","zh":"在评估担忧含义前先提供用药信息"},{"id":"o2","en":"changing the topic from fear to positive memories","zh":"把话题从恐惧转移到积极回忆"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"saying, “Don’t worry; hospice will make sure you are comfortable.”","zh":"说：“别担心，安宁疗护一定会让您舒服的。”"},{"id":"o3","en":"sitting quietly after the client describes the fear","zh":"患者描述恐惧后安静陪伴。"},{"id":"o2","en":"asking, “What have you been told about pain control options?”","zh":"询问：“关于疼痛控制方案，您已经了解了哪些内容？”"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"false reassurance can block expression of fear and may promise an outcome the nurse cannot guarantee","zh":"虚假安慰会阻碍患者表达恐惧，并可能承诺护士无法保证的结果"},{"id":"o2","en":"discussing pain always increases the client’s anxiety","zh":"讨论疼痛总会增加患者焦虑"},{"id":"o3","en":"clients with terminal illness should not be asked about emotions","zh":"不应询问终末期患者的情绪"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is expressing anticipatory grief and fear about suffering. A therapeutic response acknowledges the emotion and invites further discussion before moving to education or problem-solving.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表达的是预期性悲伤和对痛苦的恐惧。治疗性回应应先承认情绪并邀请进一步表达，然后再进入教育或解决问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In psychosocial questions, first respond to the emotion the client expresses; avoid clichés, false reassurance, and premature advice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"心理社会题中，先回应患者表达的情绪；避免套话、虚假安慰和过早建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1471,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_mc_colostomy_body_image_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.196","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.196.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.196.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,51],"fullStemEn":"A client who had colostomy surgery 2 weeks ago looks away during stoma care and says, “I can never go back to normal.” Which nursing action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一名患者结肠造口术后2周，在造口护理时回避目光并说：“我再也不可能恢复正常了。”护士优先采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士优先采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who had colostomy surgery 2 weeks ago looks away during stoma care and says, “I can never go back to normal.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者结肠造口术后2周，在造口护理时回避目光并说：“我再也不可能恢复正常了。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Reassure the client that the stoma is usually temporary.","zh":"安慰患者造口通常是暂时的。"},{"id":"A","en":"Acknowledge the statement and ask the client to describe what feels most changed.","zh":"认可患者的表达，并请患者描述最让其感觉改变的方面。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide a written pamphlet about colostomy supplies and return later.","zh":"提供关于结肠造口用品的书面资料，然后稍后再回来。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request an immediate psychiatric consultation before continuing stoma teaching.","zh":"在继续造口教学前立即申请精神科会诊。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is showing body image distress. The priority is to acknowledge the feeling and explore the client’s perception before giving information, reassurance, or referrals.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表现出身体形象困扰。优先措施是认可其感受并探索患者的认知，然后再提供信息、安慰或转介。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client expresses altered self-image, first validate and explore; do not jump to reassurance, education, or referral unless safety is at risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者表达自我形象改变时，先确认并探索；除非有安全风险，不要直接跳到安慰、教育或转介。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1472,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_fib_colorectal_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.197","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.197.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.197.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[176,353],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,102],"fullStemEn":"A 42-year-old adult with no personal history of colorectal polyps, inflammatory bowel disease, or family history of colorectal cancer asks when routine screening should begin. For an average-risk adult, colorectal cancer screening should begin at age ____ years; if a screening colonoscopy is normal, the next colonoscopy is typically due in ____ years.","fullStemZh":"一名42岁成人没有结直肠息肉病史、炎症性肠病史或结直肠癌家族史，询问常规筛查何时开始。对于平均风险成人，结直肠癌筛查应从 ____ 岁开始；如果筛查性结肠镜结果正常，通常 ____ 年后进行下一次结肠镜。","terminalSentenceEn":"For an average-risk adult, colorectal cancer screening should begin at age ____ years; if a screening colonoscopy is normal, the next colonoscopy is typically due in ____ years.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于平均风险成人，结直肠癌筛查应从 ____ 岁开始；如果筛查性结肠镜结果正常，通常 ____ 年后进行下一次结肠镜。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 42-year-old adult with no personal history of colorectal polyps, inflammatory bowel disease, or family history of colorectal cancer asks when routine screening should begin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名42岁成人没有结直肠息肉病史、炎症性肠病史或结直肠癌家族史，询问常规筛查何时开始。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Starting age for average-risk colorectal cancer screening","zh":"平均风险结直肠癌筛查起始年龄"},"acceptable":["45","age 45","45 years"],"numeric":{"value":45,"tolerance":0,"unit":"years"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Interval after a normal screening colonoscopy","zh":"筛查性结肠镜正常后的间隔"},"acceptable":["10","10 years","ten","ten years"],"numeric":{"value":10,"tolerance":0,"unit":"years"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Average-risk colorectal cancer screening begins at age 45. When colonoscopy is chosen and the result is normal, the usual repeat interval is 10 years.","rationaleCorrectZh":"平均风险成人结直肠癌筛查从45岁开始。如果选择结肠镜且结果正常，通常每10年重复一次。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For screening questions, first identify whether the client is average risk; risk level determines starting age and interval.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到筛查题，先判断患者是否为平均风险；风险层级决定起始年龄和筛查间隔。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1473,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_matrix_prediabetes_lifestyle_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.198","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.198.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.198.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,245],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,80],"fullStemEn":"A client newly diagnosed with prediabetes has an A1C of 5.8% and asks what changes can lower the risk of type 2 diabetes. For each recommendation, select whether it is an evidence-based lifestyle modification or not recommended/no added benefit.","fullStemZh":"一名新诊断为糖尿病前期的患者A1C为5.8%，询问哪些改变可以降低发生2型糖尿病的风险。请判断每项建议是“有证据支持的生活方式干预”还是“不推荐/无额外益处”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each recommendation, select whether it is an evidence-based lifestyle modification or not recommended/no added benefit.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项建议是“有证据支持的生活方式干预”还是“不推荐/无额外益处”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client newly diagnosed with prediabetes has an A1C of 5.8% and asks what changes can lower the risk of type 2 diabetes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名新诊断为糖尿病前期的患者A1C为5.8%，询问哪些改变可以降低发生2型糖尿病的风险。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Accumulate at least 150 minutes per week of moderate-intensity aerobic activity, as tolerated.","zh":"在能耐受的情况下，每周累计至少150分钟中等强度有氧活动。"},{"id":"r2","en":"If overweight, aim for a 5%–7% body-weight reduction through calorie reduction and activity.","zh":"若超重，通过减少热量摄入和增加活动，目标减重5%–7%。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Start metformin immediately without first discussing a structured lifestyle plan.","zh":"不先讨论结构化生活方式计划，立即开始二甲双胍。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Eliminate all dietary carbohydrates to prevent diabetes.","zh":"完全消除所有膳食碳水化合物以预防糖尿病。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Accept referral to a structured diabetes prevention lifestyle program.","zh":"接受转介参加结构化糖尿病预防生活方式项目。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Use a Mediterranean-style eating pattern emphasizing vegetables, legumes, whole grains, and unsaturated fats.","zh":"采用地中海式饮食模式，强调蔬菜、豆类、全谷物和不饱和脂肪。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not recommended / no added benefit","zh":"不推荐/无额外益处"},{"id":"c1","en":"Evidence-based lifestyle modification","zh":"有证据支持的生活方式干预"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Prediabetes counseling emphasizes structured lifestyle change: regular moderate activity, modest weight loss if overweight, healthy dietary patterns, and referral to diabetes prevention programs. Extreme carbohydrate elimination and medication-first framing are not appropriate general lifestyle recommendations.","rationaleCorrectZh":"糖尿病前期咨询重点是结构化生活方式改变：规律中等强度活动、超重者适度减重、健康饮食模式以及转介糖尿病预防项目。极端完全戒除碳水和以药物为先的表述不适合作为一般生活方式建议。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For health-promotion items, favor sustainable behavior changes supported by guidelines; be cautious with extreme diets or medication-first answers.","testTakingStrategyZh":"健康促进题中，优先选择指南支持、可持续的行为改变；警惕极端饮食或药物优先的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1474,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_nonpharm_pain_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.199","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.199.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.199.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,53],"fullStemEn":"A client reports 6/10 musculoskeletal pain. The prescribed analgesic plan is adequate, and the nurse is adding nonpharmacological comfort measures. Arrange the steps in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者报告肌肉骨骼疼痛6/10。已开具的镇痛方案足够，护士正在加入非药物舒适措施。请按正确顺序排列步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the steps in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The prescribed analgesic plan is adequate, and the nurse is adding nonpharmacological comfort measures.","penultimateSentenceZh":"已开具的镇痛方案足够，护士正在加入非药物舒适措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Apply heat or cold according to the pain type, skin condition, and client preference.","zh":"根据疼痛类型、皮肤状况和患者偏好使用热敷或冷敷。"},{"id":"D","en":"Coach the client in guided breathing, relaxation, or distraction while the comfort measure is in place.","zh":"在舒适措施实施期间，指导患者进行引导呼吸、放松或分散注意力。"},{"id":"B","en":"Help the client change position into therapeutic alignment that avoids strain on the painful area.","zh":"协助患者调整到治疗性体位，使疼痛部位避免受力或牵拉。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the interventions used, the reassessment findings, and the client’s response.","zh":"记录所用干预措施、重新评估结果和患者反应。"},{"id":"A","en":"Reassess the pain rating and functional response 30–60 minutes after the measures are started.","zh":"在措施开始后30–60分钟重新评估疼痛评分和功能反应。"}],"correct":["B","C","D","A","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nonpharmacological pain care begins with positioning to reduce strain, adds appropriate thermal therapy, supports relaxation or distraction, reassesses effectiveness within a reasonable interval, and documents the intervention and response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"非药物疼痛护理先通过体位调整减少牵拉，再加入适当冷热疗法，配合放松或分散注意力，在合理时间内重新评估效果，并记录干预和反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For comfort-measure sequences, implement the intervention before reassessing, then document the response after reassessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"舒适护理排序题中，先实施干预，再重新评估，最后记录反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1475,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_needlestick_exposure_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.200","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.200.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.200.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[121,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse sustains a needlestick injury after giving an injection to a client whose bloodborne pathogen status is unknown. Arrange the actions in the order the nurse should take them.","fullStemZh":"护士给一名血源性病原体状态未知的患者注射后发生针刺伤。请按护士应采取行动的先后顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the actions in the order the nurse should take them.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按护士应采取行动的先后顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse sustains a needlestick injury after giving an injection to a client whose bloodborne pathogen status is unknown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士给一名血源性病原体状态未知的患者注射后发生针刺伤。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Report the exposure immediately to the charge nurse or designated occupational health contact.","zh":"立即向主管护士或指定的职业健康联系人报告暴露事件。"},{"id":"E","en":"Complete the incident report and follow the scheduled follow-up testing plan.","zh":"完成事件报告，并按照计划进行后续检测随访。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain prompt postexposure evaluation, including source-client and baseline employee testing per policy.","zh":"按机构政策及时接受暴露后评估，包括源患者检测和员工基线检测。"},{"id":"A","en":"Wash the puncture site thoroughly with soap and water.","zh":"用肥皂和清水彻底清洗穿刺部位。"},{"id":"D","en":"Start recommended postexposure prophylaxis promptly if it is indicated.","zh":"如有适应证，及时开始推荐的暴露后预防用药。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate first aid comes first: wash a needlestick or cut with soap and water. The exposure must then be reported immediately so postexposure evaluation, source testing, baseline testing, and time-sensitive prophylaxis can begin without delay. Documentation and follow-up testing complete the process but should not delay first aid or evaluation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先要立即进行急救处理：针刺伤或割伤部位应用肥皂和清水清洗。随后必须立即报告，以便尽快进行暴露后评估、源患者检测、员工基线检测以及有时间敏感性的预防用药。记录和后续检测是流程的一部分，但不能延误急救和评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For occupational exposure sequences, do immediate first aid first, then activate reporting and evaluation, then complete documentation and follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到职业暴露排序题，先做立即急救，再启动报告和评估，最后完成记录和随访。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1476,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_fib_norovirus_outbreak_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.201","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.201.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.201.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,320],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,94],"fullStemEn":"A long-term care unit has several clients with acute vomiting and watery diarrhea, and norovirus is suspected. Complete the infection-control teaching: after contact with a symptomatic client or contaminated surface, the nurse should perform hand hygiene with _____; environmental surfaces should be cleaned using _____.","fullStemZh":"某长期护理单元多名患者出现急性呕吐和水样腹泻，怀疑为诺如病毒。请完成感染控制宣教：接触有症状患者或污染表面后，护士应使用 _____ 进行手卫生；环境表面应使用 _____ 进行清洁消毒。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the infection-control teaching: after contact with a symptomatic client or contaminated surface, the nurse should perform hand hygiene with _____; environmental surfaces should be cleaned using _____.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成感染控制宣教：接触有症状患者或污染表面后，护士应使用 _____ 进行手卫生；环境表面应使用 _____ 进行清洁消毒。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A long-term care unit has several clients with acute vomiting and watery diarrhea, and norovirus is suspected.","penultimateSentenceZh":"某长期护理单元多名患者出现急性呕吐和水样腹泻，怀疑为诺如病毒。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Preferred hand hygiene method","zh":"首选手卫生方法"},"acceptable":["soap and water","handwashing with soap and water","wash hands with soap and water","soap-and-water handwashing"]},{"prompt":{"en":"Appropriate environmental disinfectant","zh":"合适的环境消毒剂"},"acceptable":["chlorine bleach solution","bleach solution","EPA-registered disinfectant effective against norovirus","EPA registered disinfectant effective against norovirus","chlorine bleach","norovirus-effective disinfectant"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Norovirus spreads easily through contaminated hands and surfaces. Soap-and-water handwashing is preferred after caring for symptomatic clients or handling contaminated material, and contaminated surfaces require a disinfectant effective against norovirus, such as chlorine bleach solution or an EPA-registered product labeled for norovirus.","rationaleCorrectZh":"诺如病毒很容易通过被污染的手和环境表面传播。护理有症状患者或处理污染物后，首选用肥皂和清水洗手；污染表面需要使用对诺如病毒有效的消毒剂，如含氯漂白液或标明对诺如病毒有效的 EPA 注册产品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For gastroenteritis outbreaks, think contact spread, hands, and high-touch surfaces; match the control measure to the organism’s environmental persistence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到胃肠炎暴发题，想到接触传播、手和高频接触表面；感染控制措施要与病原体在环境中的存活特点相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1477,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_sata_varicella_precautions_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.202","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.202.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.202.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[133,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,42],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with fever and a generalized vesicular rash suspicious for varicella. Which actions should the nurse implement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因发热和全身性水疱样皮疹入院，疑似水痘。护士应实施哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应实施哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use airborne and contact precautions for care.","zh":"护理时采取空气传播和接触传播防护。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in an airborne infection isolation room if available.","zh":"如有条件，将患者安置在空气传播感染隔离病房。"},{"id":"C","en":"Wear a fit-tested N95 or higher-level respirator when entering the room if not immune.","zh":"若工作人员无免疫力，进入房间时佩戴经适合性测试的 N95 或更高级别呼吸防护口罩。"},{"id":"E","en":"Have the client wear a surgical mask and cover lesions if transport outside the room is essential.","zh":"如必须离开房间转运，让患者戴外科口罩并覆盖皮损。"},{"id":"F","en":"Use droplet precautions alone because the rash is visible.","zh":"仅采取飞沫防护，因为皮疹可见。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use gown and gloves for direct client care.","zh":"直接护理患者时穿隔离衣并戴手套。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected varicella requires airborne and contact precautions because transmission can occur through airborne particles and contact with lesion material. Isolation, appropriate respirator use for susceptible staff, gown and gloves, and masking/covering lesions during essential transport reduce transmission. Droplet precautions alone are insufficient.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似水痘需要空气传播和接触传播防护，因为病毒可经空气颗粒传播，也可通过接触皮损物质传播。隔离、易感工作人员佩戴合适呼吸防护、穿隔离衣戴手套，以及必要转运时让患者戴口罩并覆盖皮损，都能降低传播风险。仅采取飞沫防护不足。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a disease spreads by more than one route, choose the combination of precautions that covers every route named by the clinical picture.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当疾病有多种传播途径时，应选择能覆盖所有传播途径的组合防护措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1478,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_critical_result_communication_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.203","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.203.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.203.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,36],"fullStemEn":"The laboratory calls the unit with a critical result for a client. Arrange the nurse's communication actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"实验室打电话给病区报告一名患者的危急值。请按正确顺序排列护士的沟通行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nurse's communication actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士的沟通行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The laboratory calls the unit with a critical result for a client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"实验室打电话给病区报告一名患者的危急值。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Read back the client identifiers and the critical result to confirm accuracy.","zh":"回读患者身份信息和危急值结果以确认准确性。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the responsible provider using concise SBAR information.","zh":"使用简明的 SBAR 信息通知负责的医护提供者。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client for clinical cues related to the result.","zh":"评估患者是否有与该结果相关的临床线索。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the result notification, assessment findings, provider response, and actions taken.","zh":"记录危急值通知、评估发现、提供者回应以及已采取的行动。"},{"id":"D","en":"Clarify and read back any new orders or plan of care.","zh":"澄清并回读任何新的医嘱或护理计划。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Closed-loop communication starts by confirming the information received. The nurse then assesses the client, communicates the result and relevant assessment using SBAR, confirms orders, and documents the notification and response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"闭环沟通首先要确认收到的信息准确。随后护士评估患者，使用 SBAR 沟通危急值和相关评估结果，确认医嘱，最后记录通知和回应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For handoff and reporting items, confirm the data, assess the client, communicate clearly, verify the plan, then document.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到交接和报告题，先确认资料，再评估患者，清楚沟通，核实计划，最后记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1479,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_cloze_interpreter_teaching_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.204","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.204.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.204.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[90,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,40],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing discharge teaching for a client who has limited English proficiency. Complete the statement about evaluating discharge readiness.","fullStemZh":"护士准备为一名英语能力有限的患者进行出院宣教。请完成关于评估出院准备情况的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement about evaluating discharge readiness.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成关于评估出院准备情况的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is preparing discharge teaching for a client who has limited English proficiency.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备为一名英语能力有限的患者进行出院宣教。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{1}} because it {{2}}. If the client gives an incorrect return explanation, the nurse should {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"护士应该 {{1}}，因为这样可以 {{2}}。如果患者复述不正确，护士应 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"give printed English instructions and ask the client to sign the discharge form","zh":"提供英文书面说明，并请患者签署出院表格"},{"id":"o1","en":"use a qualified medical interpreter and ask the client to explain the plan in their own words","zh":"使用合格的医疗口译员，并请患者用自己的话说明计划"},{"id":"o3","en":"ask an adult family member to summarize the instructions so the visit is faster","zh":"请成年家属总结说明，以便更快完成宣教"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"checks understanding through two-way communication rather than assuming comprehension","zh":"通过双向沟通检查理解，而不是假设患者已经理解"},{"id":"o2","en":"proves the client agreed with every instruction","zh":"证明患者同意所有指示"},{"id":"o3","en":"allows the nurse to avoid repeating information","zh":"让护士无需重复信息"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"reteach the key points using plain language and reassess with teach-back","zh":"用通俗语言重新讲解重点，并再次用回授法评估"},{"id":"o2","en":"document nonadherence and end the teaching session","zh":"记录患者不依从并结束宣教"},{"id":"o3","en":"ask the interpreter to decide whether the client is safe for discharge","zh":"让口译员决定患者是否可以安全出院"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"clients with limited English proficiency cannot learn self-care skills","zh":"英语能力有限的患者无法学习自我护理技能"},{"id":"o1","en":"discharge readiness depends on demonstrated understanding, not exposure to information alone","zh":"出院准备取决于能否表现出理解，而不仅仅是听过信息"},{"id":"o3","en":"family interpretation is more accurate than medical interpretation","zh":"家属翻译比医疗口译更准确"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A qualified medical interpreter supports accurate, confidential communication. Teach-back evaluates whether the client can explain the plan in their own words. If understanding is incomplete, the nurse reteaches in plain language and reassesses rather than labeling the client nonadherent or shifting clinical judgment to the interpreter.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合格的医疗口译员能支持准确且保密的沟通。回授法评估患者能否用自己的话解释计划。若理解不完整，护士应使用通俗语言重新讲解并再次评估，而不是把患者贴上不依从标签，也不能把临床判断转给口译员。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge-readiness questions, choose the action that verifies what the client can do or explain, not the action that merely delivers information.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到出院准备题，选择能验证患者能做什么或能解释什么的行动，而不是只传递信息的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1480,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_cloze_caregiver_strain_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.205","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.205.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.205.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,65],"fullStemEn":"A spouse caring for a partner with progressive memory loss says, “I love him, but I have not slept through the night in months. I feel guilty for feeling resentful.” Complete the therapeutic response.","fullStemZh":"一位照护伴侣进行性记忆减退患者的配偶说：“我爱他，但我已经好几个月没有睡过整觉了。我因为自己有怨气而感到内疚。”请完成治疗性回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the therapeutic response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成治疗性回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"I feel guilty for feeling resentful.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"我因为自己有怨气而感到内疚。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's best initial response is {{1}} because it {{2}}. The nurse should avoid {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"护士最佳的初始回应是 {{1}}，因为这样可以 {{2}}。护士应避免 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"“Most caregivers feel this way, so try not to think about it.”","zh":"“大多数照护者都会这样，所以尽量别去想。”"},{"id":"o1","en":"“You sound exhausted and conflicted. What has been the hardest part of caregiving this week?”","zh":"“听起来您非常疲惫，也很矛盾。这周照护中最困难的部分是什么？”"},{"id":"o2","en":"“You should not feel resentful because your partner cannot help it.”","zh":"“您不应该有怨气，因为您的伴侣也不是故意的。”"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"tells the caregiver which decision to make","zh":"告诉照护者该做什么决定"},{"id":"o2","en":"redirects the caregiver away from negative emotions","zh":"让照护者避开负面情绪"},{"id":"o1","en":"validates feelings while assessing coping needs","zh":"肯定其感受，同时评估应对需求"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"asking about available respite supports","zh":"询问可获得的喘息照护支持"},{"id":"o1","en":"minimizing or judging the caregiver's feelings","zh":"淡化或评判照护者的感受"},{"id":"o3","en":"screening for sleep loss and caregiver fatigue","zh":"筛查睡眠不足和照护者疲劳"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"it makes the nurse responsible for providing home care","zh":"这会让护士负责提供居家照护"},{"id":"o1","en":"it can increase guilt and shut down disclosure of support needs","zh":"这会加重内疚，并使其不愿表达支持需求"},{"id":"o3","en":"it prevents the caregiver from receiving any diagnosis","zh":"这会阻止照护者获得任何诊断"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The caregiver is expressing fatigue, guilt, and resentment, which are cues for caregiver role strain. A therapeutic response validates the feelings and opens assessment of coping and support needs. Judging, minimizing, or telling the caregiver how to feel can increase guilt and reduce disclosure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"照护者表达疲劳、内疚和怨气，这是照护者角色紧张的线索。治疗性回应应肯定其感受，并进一步评估应对能力和支持需求。评判、淡化或告诉其应该怎样感受，可能加重内疚并减少其表达。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For psychosocial communication, first acknowledge the emotion and invite more information; avoid judgment, false reassurance, and advice before assessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"心理社会沟通题先承认情绪并邀请进一步表达；评估前避免评判、虚假安慰和直接建议。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1481,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_mc_amputation_body_image_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.206","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.206.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.206.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,53],"fullStemEn":"A client who had a below-the-knee amputation 10 days ago says, “I do not want my spouse to see me. I look broken now.” Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"一名患者膝下截肢术后 10 天，说：“我不想让我配偶看到我。我现在看起来像残缺的人。”护士最佳回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"I look broken now.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"我现在看起来像残缺的人。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"“I will schedule the prosthetist now so you can focus on walking again.”","zh":"“我现在安排义肢师来，这样您就能专注于重新走路。”"},{"id":"B","en":"“Your spouse loves you, so you do not need to worry about appearance.”","zh":"“您的配偶爱您，所以您不需要担心外表。”"},{"id":"A","en":"“It sounds painful to see your body differently. Can you tell me what worries you most about your spouse seeing you?”","zh":"“看到自己的身体变得不同让您很痛苦。您最担心配偶看到您时会发生什么，可以告诉我吗？”"},{"id":"D","en":"“Try not to look at the limb until you feel ready.”","zh":"“在您准备好之前，尽量不要看残肢。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority is to acknowledge the client's body image concern and explore the meaning of the change before giving reassurance or focusing on rehabilitation tasks. This response is therapeutic because it validates the feeling and invites the client to share specific fears.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先措施是承认患者的身体形象困扰，并在给予安慰或转向康复任务前探索这种改变的意义。该回应具有治疗性，因为它肯定感受并邀请患者表达具体担忧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client expresses altered body image, choose the response that validates and explores before reassuring, teaching, or redirecting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者表达身体形象改变时，先选择能肯定并探索感受的回应，再考虑安慰、宣教或转移话题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1482,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_fib_cervical_screening_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.207","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.207.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.207.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,88],"fullStemEn":"For an average-risk client with a cervix, USPSTF cervical cancer screening with cytology alone begins at age _____ years; from ages 21 through 29, cytology alone is repeated every _____ years when results are normal.","fullStemZh":"对于有宫颈且属平均风险的患者，根据 USPSTF 建议，单独宫颈细胞学筛查从 _____ 岁开始；21 至 29 岁期间，如结果正常，单独细胞学筛查每 _____ 年重复一次。","terminalSentenceEn":"For an average-risk client with a cervix, USPSTF cervical cancer screening with cytology alone begins at age _____ years; from ages 21 through 29, cytology alone is repeated every _____ years when results are normal.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于有宫颈且属平均风险的患者，根据 USPSTF 建议，单独宫颈细胞学筛查从 _____ 岁开始；21 至 29 岁期间，如结果正常，单独细胞学筛查每 _____ 年重复一次。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Starting age in years","zh":"开始筛查年龄（岁）"},"acceptable":["21","age 21","21 years"],"numeric":{"value":21,"tolerance":0,"unit":"years"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Cytology-alone interval in years for ages 21-29","zh":"21–29 岁单独细胞学筛查间隔（年）"},"acceptable":["3","3 years","every 3 years"],"numeric":{"value":3,"tolerance":0,"unit":"years"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For average-risk individuals with a cervix, cervical cancer screening begins at age 21. For ages 21 through 29, cytology alone every 3 years is the recommended screening interval when results are normal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于有宫颈且属平均风险者，宫颈癌筛查从 21 岁开始。21 至 29 岁期间，如果结果正常，推荐每 3 年进行一次单独细胞学筛查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Screening items often test age plus interval; separate the starting age from the follow-up interval for a normal result.","testTakingStrategyZh":"筛查题常考开始年龄和筛查间隔；要区分开始筛查年龄与正常结果后的复查间隔。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1483,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_matrix_osteoporosis_prevention_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.208","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.208.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.208.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,36],"fullStemEn":"A 66-year-old woman asks how to lower her risk for osteoporotic fractures. Classify each recommendation.","fullStemZh":"一名 66 岁女性询问如何降低骨质疏松性骨折风险。请对每项建议进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each recommendation.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项建议进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 66-year-old woman asks how to lower her risk for osteoporotic fractures.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 66 岁女性询问如何降低骨质疏松性骨折风险。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Schedule bone density screening with DXA.","zh":"安排 DXA 骨密度筛查。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Perform weight-bearing and muscle-strengthening exercise as tolerated.","zh":"在耐受范围内进行负重运动和肌力训练。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Stop smoking and limit alcohol intake.","zh":"戒烟并限制饮酒。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Avoid all walking and routine activity to prevent falls.","zh":"为防止跌倒，避免所有步行和日常活动。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Use adequate calcium and vitamin D intake as part of a broader prevention plan.","zh":"在综合预防计划中保证足够的钙和维生素 D 摄入。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Rely on supplements alone instead of exercise or fall-risk reduction.","zh":"只依靠补充剂，而不进行运动或降低跌倒风险。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not recommended as stated","zh":"按此表述不推荐"},{"id":"c1","en":"Evidence-based health promotion","zh":"有循证依据的健康促进措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Women 65 years or older should be screened for osteoporosis with bone density testing. Fracture prevention includes weight-bearing and strengthening activity as tolerated, smoking cessation, alcohol moderation, adequate calcium/vitamin D, and fall-risk reduction. Avoiding all activity or relying on supplements alone is not an evidence-based plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"65 岁及以上女性应进行骨密度筛查。预防骨折包括耐受范围内的负重和肌力训练、戒烟、限制饮酒、足够钙和维生素 D 摄入以及降低跌倒风险。避免所有活动或只依赖补充剂并不是循证方案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In prevention matrices, be cautious with absolute words like all, never, or alone; comprehensive risk reduction is usually stronger than a single isolated measure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"预防类矩阵题中要警惕“所有、绝不、只靠”等绝对词；综合降低风险通常比单一措施更合理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1484,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_dysphagia_mealtime_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.209","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.209.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.209.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,48],"fullStemEn":"A client with dysphagia is beginning lunch after the nurse verifies the prescribed diet texture and liquid consistency. Arrange the mealtime assistance actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名吞咽困难患者准备开始午餐，护士已确认医嘱规定的食物质地和液体稠度。请按顺序排列进餐协助措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the mealtime assistance actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列进餐协助措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with dysphagia is beginning lunch after the nurse verifies the prescribed diet texture and liquid consistency.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名吞咽困难患者准备开始午餐，护士已确认医嘱规定的食物质地和液体稠度。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Position the client upright at about 90 degrees before offering food.","zh":"进食前将患者置于约 90 度直立位。"},{"id":"D","en":"Check for pocketing, coughing, wet voice, or fatigue during the meal.","zh":"进食过程中观察食物滞留、咳嗽、湿性嗓音或疲劳。"},{"id":"E","en":"Keep the client upright after the meal and document intake and tolerance.","zh":"进食后保持患者直立，并记录摄入量和耐受情况。"},{"id":"C","en":"Offer small bites or sips at a slow pace, allowing time to swallow.","zh":"缓慢给予小口食物或液体，留出吞咽时间。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ensure dentures, glasses, and adaptive utensils are in place if used.","zh":"如患者使用假牙、眼镜或适应性餐具，确认其已就位。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe mealtime assistance begins with upright positioning, then preparing needed aids, offering small amounts slowly, monitoring for aspiration cues during the meal, and keeping the client upright afterward while documenting intake and tolerance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全进餐协助先从直立体位开始，然后准备所需辅助物品，缓慢给予小量食物或液体，进食中观察误吸线索，进食后保持直立并记录摄入量和耐受情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For basic-care sequences, make the body position safe first, then assist with the activity, monitor response, and document.","testTakingStrategyZh":"基础护理排序题中，先确保体位安全，再协助活动，随后监测反应并记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1485,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_sterile_dressing_change_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.210","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.210.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.210.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,40],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is changing a sterile postoperative abdominal dressing. Arrange the actions in the correct order to maintain surgical asepsis.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为术后腹部伤口更换无菌敷料。请将操作按正确顺序排列，以维持外科无菌原则。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the actions in the correct order to maintain surgical asepsis.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将操作按正确顺序排列，以维持外科无菌原则。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is changing a sterile postoperative abdominal dressing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为术后腹部伤口更换无菌敷料。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Open sterile supplies on a dry, waist-level surface and avoid reaching across the sterile field.","zh":"在干燥、腰部以上的平面上打开无菌物品，并避免跨越无菌区域取物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Perform hand hygiene, identify the client, explain the procedure, provide privacy, and position the client to expose only the wound area.","zh":"进行手卫生，核对患者身份，解释操作，保护隐私，并摆好体位，只暴露伤口区域。"},{"id":"E","en":"Don sterile gloves and cleanse the incision from the least contaminated area toward the more contaminated area, using each swab only once.","zh":"戴无菌手套，从污染较少的区域向污染较多的区域清洁切口，每块棉签只使用一次。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply the sterile dressing, secure it without contaminating the wound surface, dispose of supplies, and document the wound appearance and dressing change.","zh":"敷上无菌敷料，在不污染伤口表面的情况下固定，处理用物，并记录伤口外观和换药情况。"},{"id":"B","en":"Put on clean gloves, remove the soiled dressing, assess drainage and the wound, then remove gloves and perform hand hygiene.","zh":"戴清洁手套，取下污染敷料，评估渗液和伤口，然后脱手套并进行手卫生。"}],"correct":["D","B","A","E","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first prepares and explains the procedure, then removes the old dressing with clean technique to assess the wound. A sterile field is established only after the contaminated dressing is removed and hand hygiene is repeated. Sterile gloves are used for wound cleansing and new dressing placement, followed by disposal and documentation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先准备并解释操作，然后用清洁技术取下旧敷料并评估伤口。污染敷料移除并再次手卫生后，才建立无菌区域。伤口清洁和新敷料放置使用无菌手套，最后处理用物并记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sterile procedures, separate clean removal of contaminated material from sterile placement of new supplies; do not open the sterile field too early.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到无菌操作题，要把污染物的清洁移除与新无菌物品的放置分开；不要过早打开无菌区域。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1486,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_fib_scabies_precautions_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.211","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.211.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.211.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,240],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,72],"fullStemEn":"A client in a long-term care facility has suspected classic scabies. To reduce transmission during hands-on care, the nurse should initiate {{b1}} and avoid direct skin-to-skin contact until at least {{b2}} after effective treatment begins.","fullStemZh":"一名长期护理机构患者疑似普通疥疮。为减少在直接护理中的传播，护士应启动 {{b1}}，并在有效治疗开始后至少 {{b2}} 内避免直接皮肤接触。","terminalSentenceEn":"To reduce transmission during hands-on care, the nurse should initiate {{b1}} and avoid direct skin-to-skin contact until at least {{b2}} after effective treatment begins.","terminalSentenceZh":"为减少在直接护理中的传播，护士应启动 {{b1}}，并在有效治疗开始后至少 {{b2}} 内避免直接皮肤接触。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in a long-term care facility has suspected classic scabies.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名长期护理机构患者疑似普通疥疮。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Transmission-based precaution type","zh":"基于传播途径的隔离类型"},"acceptable":["contact precautions","contact","contact precaution","Contact precautions"]},{"prompt":{"en":"Minimum time after effective treatment begins","zh":"有效治疗开始后的最短时间"},"acceptable":["24 hours","24 hr","24 hrs","at least 24 hours","24"],"numeric":{"value":24,"tolerance":0,"unit":"hours"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Scabies spreads primarily through prolonged skin-to-skin contact. Contact precautions, gloves and careful hand hygiene during hands-on care, and avoiding direct skin contact for at least 24 hours after effective treatment help interrupt transmission.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疥疮主要通过较长时间的皮肤接触传播。接触隔离、直接护理时戴手套并认真手卫生，以及有效治疗后至少24小时避免直接皮肤接触，有助于阻断传播。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the organism's route of spread to the precaution: mites and draining skin-contact conditions point to contact precautions, not airborne isolation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据病原体传播途径选择隔离措施：螨虫和皮肤接触传播提示接触隔离，而不是空气隔离。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1487,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_sata_meningococcal_droplet_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.212","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.212.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.212.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,38],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with suspected meningococcal meningitis. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因疑似脑膜炎球菌性脑膜炎入院。哪些护理措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Notify infection prevention so exposed close contacts can be evaluated for postexposure prophylaxis.","zh":"通知感染防控人员，以便评估暴露的密切接触者是否需要暴露后预防。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a private room using Droplet Precautions in addition to Standard Precautions.","zh":"将患者安置在单人病房，并在标准预防基础上实施飞沫隔离。"},{"id":"B","en":"Wear a surgical mask for close contact with the client or respiratory secretions.","zh":"与患者近距离接触或接触呼吸道分泌物时佩戴外科口罩。"},{"id":"C","en":"Continue Droplet Precautions until at least 24 hours after effective antimicrobial therapy is started.","zh":"持续飞沫隔离，直到有效抗菌治疗开始后至少24小时。"},{"id":"D","en":"Move the client to a negative-pressure room and require an N-95 respirator for all routine care.","zh":"将患者转入负压病房，并要求所有常规护理均佩戴N-95呼吸防护口罩。"},{"id":"F","en":"Discontinue transmission-based precautions as soon as the fever improves after the first antibiotic dose.","zh":"第一次抗生素给药后只要发热好转，就停止基于传播途径的隔离。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected or confirmed meningococcal meningitis requires Standard plus Droplet Precautions until at least 24 hours after effective antimicrobial therapy begins. Staff use a surgical mask for close respiratory exposure, and infection prevention should coordinate evaluation of exposed close contacts for prophylaxis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似或确诊脑膜炎球菌性脑膜炎需要标准预防加飞沫隔离，直到有效抗菌治疗开始后至少24小时。工作人员在近距离呼吸道暴露时佩戴外科口罩，并由感染防控协调评估暴露密切接触者是否需要预防用药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate droplet from airborne infections: meningococcal disease uses surgical-mask droplet precautions, while tuberculosis, measles, and varicella require airborne isolation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分飞沫与空气传播感染：脑膜炎球菌病使用外科口罩的飞沫隔离；结核、麻疹和水痘才需要空气隔离。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1488,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_care_conference_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.213","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.213.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.213.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[121,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,43],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is coordinating an interdisciplinary care conference for an older adult who will need support after discharge. Arrange the coordination steps in the best order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名出院后需要支持的老年患者协调跨专业照护会议。请将协调步骤按最佳顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the coordination steps in the best order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将协调步骤按最佳顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is coordinating an interdisciplinary care conference for an older adult who will need support after discharge.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名出院后需要支持的老年患者协调跨专业照护会议。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Assign follow-up responsibilities, document unresolved issues, and communicate the plan to the receiving care team.","zh":"分配后续责任，记录未解决问题，并将计划传达给接收照护团队。"},{"id":"E","en":"Ask each discipline to give concise updates and recommendations related to the discharge barriers.","zh":"请各专业成员就出院障碍提供简明更新和建议。"},{"id":"C","en":"Review the reason for the conference and identify the client's stated goals and discharge barriers from the chart and recent nursing assessment.","zh":"回顾召开会议的原因，并从病历和近期护理评估中确认患者陈述的目标及出院障碍。"},{"id":"B","en":"Summarize the shared plan in plain language and ask the client to restate the key next steps.","zh":"用通俗语言总结共同照护计划，并请患者复述关键后续步骤。"},{"id":"A","en":"Invite the client and chosen caregiver and confirm who the client wants included in the discussion.","zh":"邀请患者及其选择的照护者，并确认患者希望哪些人参与讨论。"}],"correct":["C","A","E","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective coordination starts with clarifying the purpose, patient goals, and barriers. The patient and chosen caregiver are included, disciplines provide targeted recommendations, the nurse confirms understanding with plain language, and then responsibilities and documentation are completed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效协调先要明确会议目的、患者目标和障碍。随后纳入患者及其选择的照护者，各专业提供针对性建议，护士用通俗语言确认理解，最后完成责任分配和记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For coordination questions, move from assessment and patient goals to team recommendations, then confirmation, documentation, and handoff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"照护协调题通常按“评估和患者目标→团队建议→确认理解→记录与交接”的顺序思考。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is coordinating an interdisciplinary care conference for an older adult who will need support after discharge.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名出院后需要支持的老年患者协调跨专业照护会议。"}
{"queueIndex":1489,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_cloze_low_literacy_wound_teaching_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.214","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.214.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.214.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"A client with low health literacy is learning how to change a simple wound dressing before discharge.","fullStemZh":"一名健康素养较低的患者在出院前学习如何更换简单伤口敷料。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with low health literacy is learning how to change a simple wound dressing before discharge.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名健康素养较低的患者在出院前学习如何更换简单伤口敷料。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should use {{1}} because it {{2}}. If the client cannot perform the skill safely, the nurse should {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"护士应使用 {{1}}，因为它 {{2}}。如果患者不能安全完成该技能，护士应 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a detailed written packet with medical terms","zh":"包含医学术语的详细书面资料包"},{"id":"o3","en":"a yes-or-no question asking whether the client understands","zh":"用是/否问题询问患者是否理解"},{"id":"o1","en":"demonstration followed by return demonstration","zh":"示范后让患者回示范"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"shows whether the client can actually complete the steps","zh":"能显示患者是否真的可以完成步骤"},{"id":"o2","en":"removes the nurse's need to assess readiness","zh":"免除了护士评估准备情况的需要"},{"id":"o3","en":"is faster than individualized teaching","zh":"比个体化教学更快"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"reteach using simpler language, demonstrate again, and reassess performance","zh":"用更简单的语言重新教学，再次示范，并重新评估操作表现"},{"id":"o3","en":"ask a family member to learn instead without involving the client","zh":"改为让家属学习，而不再让患者参与"},{"id":"o2","en":"document nonadherence and proceed with discharge instructions as written","zh":"记录不依从，并按原书面出院指导继续"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"written instructions are the legal proof that teaching occurred","zh":"书面说明是教学已经完成的法律证明"},{"id":"o2","en":"clients with low health literacy cannot safely manage self-care","zh":"健康素养低的患者无法安全进行自我照护"},{"id":"o1","en":"discharge readiness requires verified ability, not simply exposure to information","zh":"出院准备状态需要验证能力，而不仅是接触过信息"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Return demonstration is the best way to evaluate a hands-on discharge skill. If the client cannot perform the dressing change safely, the nurse reteaches in simpler language, demonstrates again, and reassesses because readiness is based on verified ability, not merely receiving information.","rationaleCorrectZh":"回示范是评估出院前动手技能的最佳方法。如果患者不能安全完成换药，护士应使用更简单语言重新教学、再次示范并重新评估，因为出院准备状态取决于已验证的能力，而不是仅仅接受过信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the outcome is a psychomotor skill, choose demonstration and return demonstration over passive reading or yes/no understanding checks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当目标是操作技能时，应选择示范和回示范，而不是被动阅读或是/否式理解检查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1490,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_cloze_spiritual_distress_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.215","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.215.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.215.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"A client with advanced cancer says, \"I do not know if my life had any meaning, and I do not want to die alone.\"","fullStemZh":"一名晚期癌症患者说：“我不知道我的人生是否有意义，也不想孤单地死去。”","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with advanced cancer says, \"I do not know if my life had any meaning, and I do not want to die alone.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"一名晚期癌症患者说：“我不知道我的人生是否有意义，也不想孤单地死去。”","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse's best initial response is to {{1}} because this demonstrates {{2}}. The nurse should avoid {{3}} because it {{4}}.","zh":"护士最佳的初始回应是 {{1}}，因为这体现了 {{2}}。护士应避免 {{3}}，因为它 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"tell the client, \"Everyone feels this way near the end.\"","zh":"告诉患者：“每个人临终前都会这样想。”"},{"id":"o1","en":"sit with the client and ask, \"What has helped you feel comforted or connected in the past?\"","zh":"坐在患者身边并询问：“过去什么事情能让您感到安慰或有联系？”"},{"id":"o3","en":"change the subject to pain medication options","zh":"把话题转到止痛药选择上"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"therapeutic presence and open-ended exploration of meaning","zh":"治疗性陪伴和开放式探索生命意义"},{"id":"o2","en":"reassurance that removes the need for further discussion","zh":"通过安慰消除进一步讨论的需要"},{"id":"o3","en":"rapid redirection away from distressing emotion","zh":"迅速把话题从痛苦情绪上转移开"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"asking whether the client wants a chaplain or spiritual care referral","zh":"询问患者是否希望联系牧灵/灵性照护人员"},{"id":"o3","en":"offering to stay while the client talks","zh":"表示愿意陪伴患者谈话"},{"id":"o1","en":"saying, \"You will be in a better place, so try not to worry\"","zh":"说：“您会去更好的地方，所以别担心”"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"keeps the focus on the client's stated concern","zh":"保持关注患者陈述的关切"},{"id":"o2","en":"encourages the client to describe personal sources of comfort","zh":"鼓励患者描述个人的安慰来源"},{"id":"o1","en":"imposes a belief and blocks expression of fear and meaning","zh":"强加某种信念，并阻断患者表达恐惧和意义感"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is expressing spiritual distress and fear of dying alone. Therapeutic presence and an open-ended question invite the client to explore sources of meaning and comfort. Offering a personal belief-based reassurance blocks expression and may not match the client's values.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表达了灵性痛苦和对孤独死亡的恐惧。治疗性陪伴和开放式问题可邀请患者探索意义和安慰来源。基于个人信念的安慰会阻断表达，也可能不符合患者价值观。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For end-of-life emotion or meaning concerns, choose presence, open-ended exploration, and patient-defined support over reassurance or value-imposing statements.","testTakingStrategyZh":"面对临终情绪或意义问题，应选择陪伴、开放式探索和以患者定义的支持，而不是简单安慰或强加价值观。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1491,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_mc_cultural_beliefs_care_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.216","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.216.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.216.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,193],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,56],"fullStemEn":"A client newly diagnosed with rheumatoid arthritis says, \"I want to use my family's traditional herbal compresses and prayer along with the treatment plan.\" Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"一名新诊断类风湿关节炎的患者说：“我想在治疗计划之外，同时使用家里的传统草药热敷和祈祷。”护士的最佳回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的最佳回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client newly diagnosed with rheumatoid arthritis says, \"I want to use my family's traditional herbal compresses and prayer along with the treatment plan.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名新诊断类风湿关节炎的患者说：“我想在治疗计划之外，同时使用家里的传统草药热敷和祈祷。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"\"Your family should decide which cultural practices you will use at home.\"","zh":"“您的家人应该决定您在家使用哪些文化习俗。”"},{"id":"B","en":"\"It is best to stop traditional practices until the prescribed treatment is finished.\"","zh":"“最好在处方治疗结束前停止传统做法。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"Tell me what the compresses contain and how you use them so we can include what is safe with your care plan.\"","zh":"“请告诉我热敷里有什么、您如何使用，这样我们可以把安全的做法纳入照护计划。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"Prayer is fine, but herbal products are not part of nursing care.\"","zh":"“祈祷可以，但草药产品不属于护理范围。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The best response is culturally respectful and safety-focused. The nurse asks what the practice involves, assesses for skin injury or interactions, and works with the client to incorporate safe preferences into the care plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最佳回应既尊重文化，又关注安全。护士询问具体做法，评估是否会导致皮肤损伤或相互作用，并与患者合作把安全偏好纳入照护计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When cultural practices are mentioned, do not dismiss or automatically approve them; assess what the practice involves and integrate it if safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干提到文化做法时，不要直接否定或自动批准；先评估具体内容，安全时再纳入照护。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1492,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_fib_lung_cancer_screening_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.217","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.217.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.217.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,275],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,89],"fullStemEn":"A 52-year-old adult who currently smokes asks about lung cancer screening. Under current USPSTF criteria, annual low-dose CT screening is considered when smoking exposure is at least {{b1}} pack-years and continues through age {{b2}} if the client remains otherwise eligible.","fullStemZh":"一名52岁且目前吸烟的成年人询问肺癌筛查。根据当前USPSTF标准，若吸烟暴露至少为 {{b1}} 包年，并且患者仍符合其他条件，则每年低剂量CT筛查可持续到 {{b2}} 岁。","terminalSentenceEn":"Under current USPSTF criteria, annual low-dose CT screening is considered when smoking exposure is at least {{b1}} pack-years and continues through age {{b2}} if the client remains otherwise eligible.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据当前USPSTF标准，若吸烟暴露至少为 {{b1}} 包年，并且患者仍符合其他条件，则每年低剂量CT筛查可持续到 {{b2}} 岁。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 52-year-old adult who currently smokes asks about lung cancer screening.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名52岁且目前吸烟的成年人询问肺癌筛查。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Minimum smoking exposure in pack-years","zh":"最低吸烟暴露（包年）"},"acceptable":["20","20 pack-years","20 pack years","twenty"],"numeric":{"value":20,"tolerance":0,"unit":"pack-years"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Upper age through which screening may continue if eligible","zh":"符合条件时可持续筛查的最高年龄"},"acceptable":["80","80 years","age 80","eighty"],"numeric":{"value":80,"tolerance":0,"unit":"years"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"USPSTF recommends annual low-dose CT screening for adults ages 50 through 80 with at least a 20 pack-year smoking history who currently smoke or quit within the past 15 years, when they are healthy enough and willing to undergo curative lung surgery if needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"USPSTF建议年龄50至80岁、至少20包年吸烟史且目前吸烟或戒烟未满15年的成年人每年进行低剂量CT筛查，前提是其健康状况允许且愿意在需要时接受根治性肺部手术。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For screening questions, identify whether the stem asks for eligibility, interval, or stopping criteria; do not mix older thresholds with current criteria.","testTakingStrategyZh":"筛查题要先判断题干问的是资格、间隔还是停止标准；不要把旧标准与当前标准混用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":true,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":true,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1493,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_matrix_adult_physical_activity_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.218","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.218.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.218.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is counseling a sedentary adult about physical activity for health promotion. For each recommendation, select whether it is evidence-based counseling or not recommended/no added benefit.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为一名久坐成年人进行促进健康的身体活动咨询。请判断每项建议是循证建议，还是不推荐/无额外益处。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each recommendation, select whether it is evidence-based counseling or not recommended/no added benefit.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项建议是循证建议，还是不推荐/无额外益处。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is counseling a sedentary adult about physical activity for health promotion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名久坐成年人进行促进健康的身体活动咨询。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Accumulate at least 150 minutes per week of moderate-intensity aerobic activity, as tolerated.","zh":"在可耐受范围内，每周累计至少150分钟中等强度有氧活动。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Include muscle-strengthening activities on at least 2 days per week.","zh":"每周至少2天进行肌肉强化活动。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Count only vigorous exercise; light or moderate activity has no health value.","zh":"只计算剧烈运动；轻度或中等强度活动没有健康价值。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Break up long periods of sitting with light activity when possible.","zh":"尽可能用轻度活动打断长时间久坐。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Avoid starting physical activity until weight loss occurs first.","zh":"在先减重之前不要开始身体活动。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Choose enjoyable activities and gradually increase duration to support adherence.","zh":"选择自己喜欢的活动，并逐渐增加持续时间以促进坚持。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not recommended / no added benefit","zh":"不推荐/无额外益处"},{"id":"c1","en":"Evidence-based lifestyle recommendation","zh":"循证生活方式建议"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adults should aim for at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity aerobic activity weekly and muscle-strengthening activity at least 2 days per week. Reducing sedentary time, choosing enjoyable activities, and gradual progression support adherence. Vigorous exercise is not the only beneficial activity, and activity does not need to wait for weight loss.","rationaleCorrectZh":"成年人应目标每周至少150分钟中等强度有氧活动，并每周至少2天进行肌肉强化活动。减少久坐、选择喜欢的活动并逐步增加，有助于坚持。并非只有剧烈运动才有益，开始活动也不需要等到先减重。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Health promotion counseling should be realistic and sustainable; avoid all-or-nothing statements such as 'only vigorous exercise counts.'","testTakingStrategyZh":"健康促进咨询应现实且可持续；避免“只有剧烈运动才算”等全有全无的说法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is counseling a sedentary adult about physical activity for health promotion.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在为一名久坐成年人进行促进健康的身体活动咨询。"}
{"queueIndex":1494,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun11_or_oral_care_xerostomia_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.219","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.219.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.219.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,44],"fullStemEn":"A client reports dry mouth and discomfort after several days of oxygen therapy. The nurse plans basic oral care. Arrange the actions in the best order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者接受氧疗数日后主诉口干和不适。护士计划进行基础口腔护理。请将操作按最佳顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the actions in the best order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将操作按最佳顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse plans basic oral care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士计划进行基础口腔护理。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Perform hand hygiene, identify the client, assess the mouth for sores, bleeding, dentures, and aspiration risk, and explain the care.","zh":"进行手卫生，核对患者身份，评估口腔是否有溃疡、出血、义齿及误吸风险，并解释护理。"},{"id":"B","en":"Offer lip moisturizer and water-based mouth moisturizer as appropriate, then ensure the call light is within reach.","zh":"按需提供润唇剂和水基口腔保湿剂，然后确保呼叫铃在可及范围。"},{"id":"E","en":"Remove and clean dentures if present, keeping them in a labeled cup when not in use.","zh":"如有义齿，取下并清洁；不用时放入有标签的杯中。"},{"id":"A","en":"Position the client upright or side-lying if aspiration risk is present, and place a towel across the chest.","zh":"如无禁忌让患者坐起；若有误吸风险则取侧卧位，并在胸前铺毛巾。"},{"id":"D","en":"Brush teeth, gums, and tongue gently with a soft toothbrush or foam swab, suctioning pooled fluid if needed.","zh":"用软毛牙刷或海绵棒轻柔清洁牙齿、牙龈和舌头，必要时吸出口腔积液。"}],"correct":["C","A","E","D","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Oral care begins with assessment, identification, explanation, and aspiration-risk screening. The client is positioned safely, dentures are removed and cleaned if present, oral tissues are cleaned gently, and comfort measures such as moisturizers are provided at the end.","rationaleCorrectZh":"口腔护理首先进行评估、核对身份、解释和误吸风险筛查。随后安全摆位，如有义齿则取下清洁，轻柔清洁口腔组织，最后提供保湿等舒适措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For basic care sequences, assess first, position for safety, perform the care, then provide comfort and leave the client safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"基础护理排序题通常先评估，再安全摆位，随后实施护理，最后提供舒适措施并确保患者安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1495,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.220","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.220.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[375,548],"terminalOffsetsZh":[120,168],"fullStemEn":"Clostridioides difficile colitis after broad-spectrum antibiotics Mrs. Dolores Fuentes is a 74-year-old hospitalized client recovering from influenza A complicated by hospital-acquired Pseudomonas pneumonia. She recently completed piperacillin-tazobactam and levofloxacin, takes chronic prednisone and methotrexate for rheumatoid arthritis, and uses a proton pump inhibitor. On hospital day 14, she develops frequent watery foul-smelling stools with fever, leukocytosis, hypokalemia, mild acute kidney injury, dehydration, and abdominal distension.","fullStemZh":"广谱抗生素治疗后的艰难梭菌结肠炎 Dolores Fuentes 女士，74 岁，因甲型流感并发医院获得性铜绿假单胞菌肺炎住院恢复中。她近期完成哌拉西林-他唑巴坦和左氧氟沙星治疗，因类风湿关节炎长期使用泼尼松和甲氨蝶呤，并使用质子泵抑制剂。住院第 14 天，她出现频繁水样恶臭便、发热、白细胞增多、低钾血症、轻度急性肾损伤、脱水和腹胀。","terminalSentenceEn":"On hospital day 14, she develops frequent watery foul-smelling stools with fever, leukocytosis, hypokalemia, mild acute kidney injury, dehydration, and abdominal distension.","terminalSentenceZh":"住院第 14 天，她出现频繁水样恶臭便、发热、白细胞增多、低钾血症、轻度急性肾损伤、脱水和腹胀。","penultimateSentenceEn":"She recently completed piperacillin-tazobactam and levofloxacin, takes chronic prednisone and methotrexate for rheumatoid arthritis, and uses a proton pump inhibitor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她近期完成哌拉西林-他唑巴坦和左氧氟沙星治疗，因类风湿关节炎长期使用泼尼松和甲氨蝶呤，并使用质子泵抑制剂。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes early recognition of CDI risk, immediate contact precautions for suspected infection, soap-and-water hand hygiene, sporicidal cleaning, avoidance of antimotility agents, route-specific CDI therapy, monitoring for fulminant deterioration, and symptom-based discharge decisions rather than a PCR test of cure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例强调：识别 CDI 风险后应立即按疑似感染启动接触隔离；使用肥皂和清水洗手；采用杀芽孢环境清洁；避免止泻性抑制肠蠕动药；理解 CDI 治疗的给药途径逻辑；监测暴发/重症恶化征象；出院判断以症状恢复为主，而不是用 PCR 作为治愈检测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For infection-control cases, first identify the organism and route of transmission, then choose actions that protect others immediately while still treating dehydration, electrolytes, and clinical deterioration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"感染控制题先判断病原体和传播途径，再选择能立即保护他人的措施，同时处理脱水、电解质异常和病情恶化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1496,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,44],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the active MAR and sees loperamide 2 mg PO PRN for diarrhea. Which action is best?","fullStemZh":"护士查看当前用药记录，发现有洛哌丁胺 2 mg 口服 PRN 用于腹泻。最佳措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"最佳措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the active MAR and sees loperamide 2 mg PO PRN for diarrhea.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看当前用药记录，发现有洛哌丁胺 2 mg 口服 PRN 用于腹泻。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Give loperamide only after the stool specimen is collected so the medication does not interfere with testing.","zh":"仅在采集粪便标本后给予洛哌丁胺，以免影响检测。"},{"id":"A","en":"Withhold the loperamide and notify the provider that the order should be discontinued or held for suspected CDI.","zh":"暂缓洛哌丁胺，并通知医师疑似 CDI，应停用或暂停该医嘱。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer loperamide and increase oral fluids before contacting the provider.","zh":"给予洛哌丁胺并增加口服液体，然后再联系医师。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request diphenoxylate-atropine instead because it is stronger than loperamide for severe diarrhea.","zh":"改请医师开地芬诺酯-阿托品，因为它比洛哌丁胺更强，适合严重腹泻。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer loperamide now because reducing stool frequency will prevent dehydration and skin injury.","zh":"立即给予洛哌丁胺，因为减少排便次数可预防脱水和皮肤损伤。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has suspected CDI with fever, leukocytosis, abdominal distension, recent high-risk antibiotics, and frequent watery stools. Antimotility agents can worsen toxin retention and may contribute to ileus or toxic megacolon, so the nurse should hold loperamide and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者有发热、白细胞增多、腹胀、近期高风险抗生素暴露和频繁水样便，符合疑似 CDI。抑制肠蠕动药可能使毒素滞留并增加肠麻痹或中毒性巨结肠风险，因此护士应暂缓洛哌丁胺并通知医师。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When diarrhea may be infectious or inflammatory, avoid reflexively stopping motility; ask whether slowing the gut could trap toxins or worsen distension.","testTakingStrategyZh":"腹泻若可能为感染性或炎症性，不要反射性止泻；先判断减慢肠蠕动是否会滞留毒素或加重腹胀。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1497,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,25],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate during the first hour of care? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护理最初 1 小时内哪些措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate during the first hour of care?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护理最初 1 小时内哪些措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Delay notifying environmental services until the client has a negative follow-up stool test.","zh":"等患者复查粪便阴性后再通知环境服务人员。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use alcohol-based hand rub as the preferred method because gloves were worn during care.","zh":"因为护理时戴了手套，所以首选含酒精手消毒剂。"},{"id":"A","en":"Initiate contact precautions while CDI is suspected rather than waiting for a confirmed result.","zh":"疑似 CDI 时即启动接触隔离，而不是等待确诊结果。"},{"id":"C","en":"Send an unformed stool specimen for C. difficile testing per facility protocol once ordered.","zh":"医嘱开立后，按机构流程送检未成形粪便标本进行艰难梭菌检测。"},{"id":"B","en":"Perform hand hygiene with soap and water after removing gloves and before leaving the room.","zh":"脱手套后、离开房间前使用肥皂和清水进行手卫生。"},{"id":"E","en":"Place a dedicated commode and dedicated assessment equipment in the room.","zh":"在房间内放置患者专用便椅和专用评估设备。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected CDI requires early contact precautions, soap-and-water hand hygiene, appropriate testing of unformed stool, and dedicated equipment to reduce environmental spread. Alcohol-based hand rub is not the preferred exit hand hygiene for CDI, and environmental cleaning should not be delayed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似 CDI 需要尽早接触隔离、肥皂和清水洗手、对未成形粪便进行适当检测，并使用专用设备以减少环境传播。CDI 离室手卫生不首选酒精手消毒，环境清洁也不应延迟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For transmissible infections, act on suspicion when the risk of waiting is spread to other clients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于可传播感染，若等待会导致传播给其他患者，应在疑似时即采取措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1498,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,89],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Complete the teaching statement about why the prescribed vancomycin route is appropriate.","fullStemZh":"完成关于为什么所开万古霉素给药途径合适的教学陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the teaching statement about why the prescribed vancomycin route is appropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成关于为什么所开万古霉素给药途径合适的教学陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"CDI is treated with oral vancomycin because therapy must create high {{1}} drug concentrations. Oral vancomycin is useful for this purpose because it is {{2}} from the gastrointestinal tract. IV vancomycin would not be effective for CDI because it does not reach the {{3}} in therapeutic concentrations.","zh":"CDI 使用口服万古霉素治疗，是因为治疗需要在 {{1}} 形成高药物浓度。口服万古霉素适合此目的，因为它经胃肠道 {{2}}。静脉万古霉素不能有效治疗 CDI，因为它不能以治疗浓度到达 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"intraluminal colonic","zh":"结肠腔内"},{"id":"o3","en":"intracellular leukocyte","zh":"白细胞细胞内"},{"id":"o2","en":"serum","zh":"血清"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"activated by renal filtration","zh":"经肾小球滤过后激活"},{"id":"o1","en":"minimally absorbed","zh":"吸收很少"},{"id":"o2","en":"rapidly absorbed","zh":"迅速吸收"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"colonic lumen","zh":"结肠腔"},{"id":"o2","en":"alveoli","zh":"肺泡"},{"id":"o3","en":"synovial fluid","zh":"关节液"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CDI is a luminal colonic infection. Oral vancomycin is minimally absorbed, allowing high concentrations to remain in the intestinal lumen. IV vancomycin produces systemic levels but does not reliably deliver therapeutic drug into the colonic lumen.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CDI 是结肠腔内感染。口服万古霉素吸收很少，可使高浓度药物留在肠腔内。静脉万古霉素可产生全身血药浓度，但不能可靠地将治疗浓度药物送入结肠腔。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the medication route to the infection site: bloodstream infection needs serum drug levels; luminal gut infection needs drug in the intestinal lumen.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将给药途径与感染部位对应：血流感染需要血药浓度；肠腔感染需要药物在肠腔内。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1499,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,36],"fullStemEn":"For each finding during Stage 2 monitoring, classify whether it is more consistent with expected improvement or requires immediate escalation.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2 监测中，请判断每项表现更符合预期好转，还是需要立即升级处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding during Stage 2 monitoring, classify whether it is more consistent with expected improvement or requires immediate escalation.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 2 监测中，请判断每项表现更符合预期好转，还是需要立即升级处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Stool frequency decreases gradually while the abdomen is softer and vital signs are stable.","zh":"排便次数逐渐减少，同时腹部变软、生命体征稳定。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Diarrhea abruptly stops while abdominal distension increases and bowel sounds become absent.","zh":"腹泻突然停止，但腹胀加重且肠鸣音消失。"},{"id":"r3","en":"WBC decreases from 21.4 ×10³/µL to 18.6 ×10³/µL with improving temperature and blood pressure.","zh":"WBC 从 21.4 ×10³/µL 降至 18.6 ×10³/µL，同时体温和血压改善。"},{"id":"r4","en":"New abdominal rigidity, guarding, and rebound tenderness develop.","zh":"出现新的腹部板状硬、肌紧张和反跳痛。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Blood pressure falls to 86/50, heart rate rises to 118, and lactate increases to 3.0 mmol/L.","zh":"血压降至 86/50，心率升至 118 次/分，乳酸升至 3.0 mmol/L。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Stools become semi-formed, creatinine returns to baseline, and abdominal pain resolves.","zh":"粪便变为半成形，肌酐恢复基线，腹痛消失。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Immediate escalation","zh":"立即升级处理"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected improvement","zh":"预期好转"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Improvement is gradual and paired with softer abdomen, better vital signs, improving labs, and more formed stool. Sudden cessation of diarrhea with worsening distension, peritoneal signs, hypotension, tachycardia, or rising lactate suggests ileus, toxic megacolon, perforation risk, or shock and requires immediate escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"好转应是逐步的，并伴随腹部变软、生命体征改善、实验室指标好转和粪便成形。腹泻突然停止却腹胀加重、出现腹膜刺激征、低血压、心动过速或乳酸升高，提示肠麻痹、中毒性巨结肠、穿孔风险或休克，需要立即升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Never interpret fewer stools in isolation. In CDI, pair stool output with abdominal exam, bowel sounds, vital signs, mental status, WBC, and lactate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要孤立解读排便减少。CDI 中必须结合腹部检查、肠鸣音、生命体征、意识状态、WBC 和乳酸。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1500,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Place the nursing actions in the safest order for the initial response to the Stage 1 findings.","fullStemZh":"请将针对阶段 1 表现的初始护理措施按最安全顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the safest order for the initial response to the Stage 1 findings.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将针对阶段 1 表现的初始护理措施按最安全顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Initiate contact precautions, soap-and-water hand hygiene, and dedicated equipment while CDI is suspected.","zh":"疑似 CDI 时启动接触隔离、肥皂清水手卫生和专用设备。"},{"id":"E","en":"Collect and send an unformed stool specimen as ordered using appropriate precautions, then administer ordered fluids, potassium replacement, and oral vancomycin; continue stool counts, intake/output, abdominal checks, and skin protection.","zh":"按医嘱在适当防护下采集并送检未成形粪便标本，然后给予医嘱补液、补钾和口服万古霉素；继续记录排便、出入量、腹部评估和皮肤保护。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform a focused assessment and recognize the CDI risk pattern from new watery diarrhea, fever, leukocytosis, recent antibiotics, immunosuppression, and abdominal distension.","zh":"进行重点评估，并根据新发水样腹泻、发热、白细胞增多、近期抗生素、免疫抑制和腹胀识别 CDI 风险模式。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the provider using SBAR and request stool testing, fluids, electrolyte replacement, and CDI-directed therapy.","zh":"使用 SBAR 通知医师，请求粪便检测、补液、电解质补充和 CDI 方向治疗。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hold the PRN loperamide and flag the order for provider review.","zh":"暂缓 PRN 洛哌丁胺，并提示医师复核该医嘱。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first recognizes the risk pattern and assesses severity. Because CDI may spread before confirmation, infection-control measures begin immediately. The unsafe PRN antimotility medication is held before provider communication. SBAR then obtains orders for testing and treatment; the stool specimen is collected as ordered before or alongside therapy, and ordered fluids, electrolytes, oral vancomycin, monitoring, and skin protection follow.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先识别风险模式并评估严重程度。由于 CDI 可在确诊前传播，应立即开始感染控制措施。存在风险的 PRN 抑制肠蠕动药应在医师沟通前先暂缓。随后用 SBAR 获取检测和治疗医嘱；按医嘱采集粪便标本，并随后或同步进行补液、补钾、口服万古霉素、监测和皮肤保护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Order responses usually begin with assessment/recognition, then immediate safety isolation, then hold unsafe actions, communicate for orders, collect diagnostics, and implement prescribed therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排序题通常先评估/识别，再立即采取安全隔离措施，然后暂停不安全措施、沟通获取医嘱、采集诊断标本并执行治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1501,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opus5_cdi_immunocompromised_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.220.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,68],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,12],"fullStemEn":"Which discharge teaching statement by the nurse is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"护士哪项出院宣教最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which discharge teaching statement by the nurse is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士哪项出院宣教最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Use hand sanitizer after toileting because it is less irritating than frequent soap-and-water handwashing.","zh":"如厕后使用免洗手消毒剂，因为它比频繁肥皂清水洗手更不刺激皮肤。"},{"id":"E","en":"Restart methotrexate at home as soon as the diarrhea improves so rheumatoid arthritis does not flare.","zh":"腹泻一改善就在家重新开始甲氨蝶呤，以免类风湿关节炎发作。"},{"id":"A","en":"You do not need a repeat C. difficile test if symptoms have resolved. Finish the oral vancomycin course and call the provider if watery diarrhea, fever, or worsening abdominal pain returns.","zh":"如果症状已经缓解，就不需要重复艰难梭菌检测。请完成口服万古霉素疗程；若水样腹泻、发热或腹痛加重再次出现，请联系医师。"},{"id":"B","en":"A repeat PCR must be negative before you can safely stop contact precautions at home.","zh":"必须复查 PCR 阴性后，才能在家中安全停止接触隔离。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stop oral vancomycin when stools become formed for 24 hours because taking extra doses increases resistance.","zh":"粪便成形 24 小时后即可停止口服万古霉素，因为多服会增加耐药。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Resolution is judged clinically. Repeat C. difficile testing is not recommended when symptoms have resolved because colonization or residual genetic material may persist. The client should complete the prescribed oral vancomycin course, use soap-and-water hand hygiene after toileting, follow the plan for holding methotrexate, and report recurrent watery diarrhea, fever, or worsening abdominal pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"是否恢复主要依据临床症状。症状已缓解时不建议重复艰难梭菌检测，因为可持续存在定植或残留遗传物质。患者应完成医嘱口服万古霉素疗程，如厕后用肥皂清水洗手，按计划暂停甲氨蝶呤，并报告水样腹泻、发热或腹痛加重的复发迹象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Discharge questions often test what to do after improvement: complete therapy, avoid unnecessary tests, prevent spread, and know recurrence warning signs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出院题常考好转后的做法：完成疗程、避免不必要检测、预防传播，并了解复发警示征象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1502,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.221","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.221.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,288],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,82],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: supratherapeutic warfarin after mechanical mitral valve replacement A 63-year-old client is readmitted 12 days after mechanical mitral valve replacement with mucocutaneous bleeding, a supratherapeutic INR, recent poor intake, and recent over-the-counter naproxen exposure.","fullStemZh":"展开式病例：机械性二尖瓣置换术后华法林抗凝过量 一名63岁患者在机械性二尖瓣置换术后第12天因黏膜皮肤出血、INR过高、近期进食差及自行使用非处方萘普生而再次入院。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: supratherapeutic warfarin after mechanical mitral valve replacement A 63-year-old client is readmitted 12 days after mechanical mitral valve replacement with mucocutaneous bleeding, a supratherapeutic INR, recent poor intake, and recent over-the-counter naproxen exposure.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开式病例：机械性二尖瓣置换术后华法林抗凝过量 一名63岁患者在机械性二尖瓣置换术后第12天因黏膜皮肤出血、INR过高、近期进食差及自行使用非处方萘普生而再次入院。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests the competing priorities of hemorrhage control and mandatory anticoagulation after mechanical mitral valve replacement. The nurse must hold unsafe warfarin administration, recognize NSAID exposure as a clinically meaningful bleeding-risk amplifier, understand calibrated oral vitamin K for stable minor bleeding, escalate rapidly when hematuria, positive stool guaiac, falling hemoglobin, rising INR, tachycardia, and hypotension signal major hemorrhage, administer urgent reversal products safely, and continue monitoring for both rebleeding and thrombotic complications during the reversal period.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查机械性二尖瓣置换术后“控制出血”与“必须抗凝”之间的竞争性优先事项。护士必须在给华法林不安全时暂停并澄清，识别NSAID暴露会显著放大出血风险，理解稳定轻度出血时低剂量口服维生素K的可控逆转思路；当血尿、粪便隐血阳性、血红蛋白下降、INR升高、心动过速和低血压提示严重出血时迅速升级处理；安全给予紧急逆转制品；并在逆转期持续监测再出血和血栓并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In anticoagulation cases, always hold two risks together: too much anticoagulation causes bleeding, but too little anticoagulation can cause thrombosis when the indication is mandatory, such as a mechanical mitral valve.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝相关病例中，要始终同时考虑两种风险：抗凝过强会出血，但在机械性二尖瓣等必须抗凝的情况下，抗凝不足又会导致血栓。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1503,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,63],"fullStemEn":"At 1030, warfarin 7.5 mg nightly appears on the home medication list. The INR is 5.2 and the client has active gingival oozing and new ecchymoses. Which nursing action is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"1030时，家庭用药清单中有华法林7.5 mg每晚。患者INR为5.2，并有活动性牙龈渗血和新的瘀斑。最合适的护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"最合适的护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The INR is 5.2 and the client has active gingival oozing and new ecchymoses.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者INR为5.2，并有活动性牙龈渗血和新的瘀斑。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the scheduled warfarin because the client has a mechanical mitral valve.","zh":"因患者有机械性二尖瓣，照常给予计划剂量华法林。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the warfarin, verify the hold order or obtain clarification, and notify the provider of the INR and bleeding findings.","zh":"暂停华法林，核实暂停医嘱或取得澄清，并将INR及出血表现通知医生。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask the wife whether she wants the warfarin held because she manages the pill organizer at home.","zh":"询问妻子是否希望暂停华法林，因为她在家负责整理药盒。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give half of the warfarin dose and recheck the INR after the medication is absorbed.","zh":"给予半量华法林，并在药物吸收后复查INR。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should hold and clarify a high-risk medication when current objective data show likely harm. INR 5.2 with active mucocutaneous bleeding makes another warfarin dose unsafe; notifying the provider preserves the medication-order chain while preventing iatrogenic worsening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当当前客观资料显示用药可能造成伤害时，护士应暂停并澄清高危药物。INR 5.2且有活动性黏膜皮肤出血时，再给华法林不安全；通知医生既维持医嘱流程，又避免医源性加重。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-alert medications, compare the order with the current assessment. If the current data make administration dangerous, hold and clarify before giving the dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到高警讯药物时，要把医嘱与当前评估相比较。如果当前资料显示给药危险，应先暂停并澄清，再考虑给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1504,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,50],"fullStemEn":"During medication reconciliation, the wife reports giving naproxen 220 mg twice in the past 2 days. Which nursing responses are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"药物核对时，妻子报告过去2天给患者服用萘普生220 mg两次。哪些护理反应是合适的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing responses are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理反应是合适的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Teach the client and wife to avoid NSAIDs unless specifically approved by the anticoagulation prescriber.","zh":"教育患者和妻子：除非抗凝处方医生明确批准，否则应避免NSAID。"},{"id":"E","en":"Tell the wife that over-the-counter medications should be checked with the anticoagulation clinic or prescriber before use.","zh":"告知妻子，使用非处方药前应先与抗凝门诊或处方医生确认。"},{"id":"D","en":"Instruct the client to stop eating dark green vegetables permanently to prevent future warfarin interactions.","zh":"指导患者永久停止食用深绿色蔬菜，以预防未来华法林相互作用。"},{"id":"C","en":"Explain that NSAIDs can increase bleeding risk through platelet inhibition and gastrointestinal mucosal injury, even when the INR does not fully explain the bleeding.","zh":"解释NSAID可通过抑制血小板和损伤胃肠黏膜增加出血风险，即使INR不能完全解释出血也如此。"},{"id":"F","en":"Reassure the family that two doses of naproxen are too few to be clinically relevant.","zh":"安慰家属，两次萘普生剂量太少，不具有临床意义。"},{"id":"A","en":"Document the naproxen dose and timing and notify the provider because this exposure changes the bleeding-risk assessment.","zh":"记录萘普生剂量和时间，并通知医生，因为该暴露会改变出血风险评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Naproxen exposure is clinically relevant in a client taking warfarin with active bleeding. The nurse should document and escalate the finding, teach avoidance of unapproved NSAIDs, explain the bleeding mechanisms in practical terms, and involve the caregiver who manages medications at home.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于正在使用华法林且有活动性出血的患者，萘普生暴露具有临床意义。护士应记录并上报该发现，教育避免未经批准的NSAID，用实用语言解释出血机制，并让在家管理药物的照护者参与。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an anticoagulated client bleeds, look beyond the prescribed anticoagulant. OTC pain relievers, antibiotics, herbals, poor intake, and kidney or liver changes can all shift risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝患者出血时，不要只看处方抗凝药。非处方止痛药、抗生素、草药、进食差以及肾肝功能变化都可能改变风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1505,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,39],"fullStemEn":"The provider orders vitamin K 2.5 mg by mouth during Stage 1. Complete the teaching statement the nurse should use to explain the plan.","fullStemZh":"阶段1医生医嘱口服维生素K 2.5 mg。完成护士用于解释治疗计划的教育语句。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the teaching statement the nurse should use to explain the plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护士用于解释治疗计划的教育语句。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider orders vitamin K 2.5 mg by mouth during Stage 1.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段1医生医嘱口服维生素K 2.5 mg。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Because the client has {{1}} and also has {{2}}, the goal is to lower the INR carefully without causing {{3}}.","zh":"由于患者有 {{1}}，同时还有 {{2}}，目标是在不导致 {{3}} 的情况下降低INR。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"suspected valve thrombosis","zh":"疑似瓣膜血栓形成"},{"id":"o2","en":"massive hemorrhage with shock","zh":"伴休克的大量出血"},{"id":"o1","en":"minor mucocutaneous bleeding without hemodynamic instability","zh":"无血流动力学不稳定的轻度黏膜皮肤出血"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"a mechanical mitral valve that requires ongoing anticoagulation","zh":"需要持续抗凝的机械性二尖瓣"},{"id":"o3","en":"a contraindication to all vitamin K products","zh":"所有维生素K制剂均禁忌"},{"id":"o2","en":"a bioprosthetic valve that never requires anticoagulation","zh":"绝不需要抗凝的生物瓣"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"loss of platelet production from vitamin K","zh":"维生素K导致血小板生成丧失"},{"id":"o1","en":"overcorrection to a subtherapeutic INR and valve thrombosis risk","zh":"过度逆转至INR低于治疗范围并增加瓣膜血栓风险"},{"id":"o2","en":"immediate hemolysis from oral vitamin K","zh":"口服维生素K导致立即溶血"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At Stage 1 the client is bleeding, but the bleeding is mucocutaneous and hemodynamics are stable. Low-dose oral vitamin K provides a controlled partial reversal, which is important because mechanical mitral valves require ongoing anticoagulation and overcorrection can create thrombosis risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阶段1患者确有出血，但属于黏膜皮肤出血且血流动力学稳定。低剂量口服维生素K可较可控地部分逆转，这一点很重要，因为机械性二尖瓣需要持续抗凝，过度逆转会增加血栓风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match reversal intensity to bleeding severity and thrombotic risk. Stable minor bleeding allows controlled correction; unstable major bleeding requires faster reversal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逆转强度要与出血严重程度和血栓风险匹配。稳定的轻度出血可控制性纠正；不稳定的严重出血需要更快速逆转。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1506,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,81],"fullStemEn":"At 0645, the client has INR 6.8, hemoglobin 9.2 g/dL, new gross hematuria, positive stool guaiac, HR 98, BP 100/60, and lightheadedness. Classify each nursing action.","fullStemZh":"0645时，患者INR 6.8，血红蛋白9.2 g/dL，新发肉眼血尿，粪便隐血阳性，心率98次/分，血压100/60 mmHg，并诉头晕。请对每项护理措施分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项护理措施分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0645, the client has INR 6.8, hemoglobin 9.2 g/dL, new gross hematuria, positive stool guaiac, HR 98, BP 100/60, and lightheadedness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"0645时，患者INR 6.8，血红蛋白9.2 g/dL，新发肉眼血尿，粪便隐血阳性，心率98次/分，血压100/60 mmHg，并诉头晕。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Page/call the provider with a concise STAT report of INR, hemoglobin drop, new bleeding, tachycardia, and hypotension.","zh":"用简洁的STAT报告联系医生，说明INR、血红蛋白下降、新出血、心动过速和低血压。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Position the client supine, raise the legs slightly if tolerated, maintain telemetry, and increase vital signs to every 15 minutes.","zh":"让患者平卧，若能耐受可轻微抬高下肢，维持心电监护，并将生命体征频率增加至每15分钟。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Verify IV access and prepare isotonic fluid bolus/transfusion support according to protocol or rapid provider order.","zh":"确认静脉通路，并按流程或快速医嘱准备等渗液体快速补液/输血支持。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Administer the scheduled metoprolol and furosemide because they are cardiac medications.","zh":"因美托洛尔和呋塞米是心脏用药，照常给予计划剂量。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Perform a focused neurologic assessment and continue close neurologic monitoring.","zh":"进行重点神经系统评估，并继续密切神经系统监测。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Priority action","zh":"优先措施"},{"id":"c2","en":"Unsafe or inappropriate","zh":"不安全或不合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has evolved from minor bleeding to major bleeding with early hemodynamic compromise. The nurse prioritizes escalation, circulation support, preparation for reversal/transfusion, frequent monitoring, and neurologic surveillance while holding medications that may worsen hypovolemia or mask compensation until clarified.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者已由轻度出血进展为伴早期血流动力学受损的严重出血。护士应优先升级报告、支持循环、准备逆转/输血、密切监测及神经系统观察，并在澄清前暂停可能加重低血容量或掩盖代偿反应的药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With acute bleeding plus falling hemoglobin and unstable vital signs, think circulation first: escalate, support perfusion, prepare blood products, and avoid medications that worsen compensation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"急性出血伴血红蛋白下降和生命体征不稳定时，先考虑循环：升级报告、支持灌注、准备血制品，并避免会削弱代偿的药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At 0645, the client has INR 6.8, hemoglobin 9.2 g/dL, new gross hematuria, positive stool guaiac, HR 98, BP 100/60, and lightheadedness.","controlSentenceZh":"0645时，患者INR 6.8，血红蛋白9.2 g/dL，新发肉眼血尿，粪便隐血阳性，心率98次/分，血压100/60 mmHg，并诉头晕。"}
{"queueIndex":1507,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[109,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,42],"fullStemEn":"The provider orders IV vitamin K and 4-factor PCC for major bleeding. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"医生因严重出血开立静脉维生素K和四因子PCC。哪些护理措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Dilute vitamin K as ordered and infuse it by pump over the ordered time rather than giving a rapid IV push.","zh":"按医嘱稀释维生素K，并用输液泵按规定时间输注，而不是快速静推。"},{"id":"E","en":"Reassess vital signs, bleeding sites, urine color and output, neurologic status, hemoglobin, and repeat INR as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱再评估生命体征、出血部位、尿色和尿量、神经状态、血红蛋白及复查INR。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer 4-factor PCC promptly according to institutional protocol with required verification and monitoring.","zh":"按照机构流程经必要核对和监测后及时给予四因子PCC。"},{"id":"F","en":"Delay PCC until the vitamin K infusion is complete and a repeat INR confirms that the vitamin K has not corrected the coagulopathy.","zh":"等维生素K输注完成并复查INR确认尚未纠正凝血异常后，再延迟给予PCC。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the orders, allergies, baseline vital signs, IV patency, product availability, and required second-nurse checks before administration.","zh":"给药前核对医嘱、过敏史、基线生命体征、静脉通路通畅性、制品可用性及所需双人核对。"},{"id":"C","en":"Monitor during vitamin K infusion for hypotension, flushing, dyspnea, chest tightness, or other hypersensitivity findings.","zh":"维生素K输注期间监测低血压、潮红、呼吸困难、胸闷或其他超敏反应表现。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate nursing care includes verification before high-risk products, slow diluted IV vitamin K administration with hypersensitivity monitoring, prompt PCC administration per protocol for rapid factor replacement, and close reassessment of bleeding and laboratory response. These actions may overlap in real practice and should not be forced into a single linear sequence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当的护理包括在高风险制品给药前进行核对，按要求稀释并缓慢输注静脉维生素K且监测超敏反应，按流程及时给予PCC以快速补充凝血因子，并密切复评出血和化验反应。这些措施在实际工作中可能同时进行，不应被强行排成单一线性顺序。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SATA items about urgent reversal, choose actions that are independently safe and necessary; do not assume a rigid order unless the stem explicitly asks for one and the steps are truly sequential.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到紧急逆转相关的多选题时，选择本身安全且必要的措施；除非题干明确要求排序且步骤确实必须先后执行，否则不要假设固定顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1508,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_warfarin_mvr_2026_06_11_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.221.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,84],"fullStemEn":"At 1200, the INR is 3.8, hemoglobin is 9.8 g/dL after transfusion support, blood pressure has improved, urine is clearing, head CT is negative, and GI/urology consults are pending. Which handoff statement best reflects the client's current priority?","fullStemZh":"1200时，INR为3.8，输血支持后血红蛋白为9.8 g/dL，血压改善，尿液正在转清，头颅CT阴性，胃肠科/泌尿科会诊待完成。哪项交班内容最能反映患者当前优先事项？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which handoff statement best reflects the client's current priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项交班内容最能反映患者当前优先事项？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1200, the INR is 3.8, hemoglobin is 9.8 g/dL after transfusion support, blood pressure has improved, urine is clearing, head CT is negative, and GI/urology consults are pending.","penultimateSentenceZh":"1200时，INR为3.8，输血支持后血红蛋白为9.8 g/dL，血压改善，尿液正在转清，头颅CT阴性，胃肠科/泌尿科会诊待完成。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Warfarin should be restarted immediately by the nurse to prevent mechanical valve thrombosis.","zh":"护士应立即重新开始华法林，以预防机械瓣血栓形成。"},{"id":"C","en":"Because the head CT is negative, neurologic checks and fall precautions are no longer necessary.","zh":"由于头颅CT阴性，已不再需要神经系统检查和跌倒预防。"},{"id":"B","en":"The INR is close enough to the target range that routine every-4-hour vital signs are sufficient and hourly urine assessment can stop.","zh":"INR已足够接近目标范围，因此每4小时常规生命体征即可，并可停止每小时尿液评估。"},{"id":"A","en":"The hemorrhagic crisis is improving, but the client still requires close monitoring for both rebleeding and valve thrombosis as reversal continues.","zh":"出血危象正在改善，但随着逆转作用持续，患者仍需密切监测再出血和瓣膜血栓两方面风险。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend is improving but not resolved. The client remains in a transition period: bleeding appears controlled but the bleeding source has not been fully evaluated, and ongoing vitamin K effect may push INR below target, increasing mechanical valve thrombosis risk. Restarting anticoagulation is anticipated but is a provider decision after bleeding control.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势正在改善但尚未完全解决。患者仍处于过渡期：出血似乎受控，但出血来源尚未完全评估；维生素K作用仍可能持续使INR降至目标以下，增加机械瓣血栓风险。重新开始抗凝可预期，但应由医生在出血受控后决定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client improves after emergency treatment, do not assume the case is finished. Identify what is better, what remains unresolved, and what new risk treatment created.","testTakingStrategyZh":"患者经紧急治疗后好转时，不要认为问题已经结束。要识别哪些已改善、哪些尚未解决，以及治疗本身带来了什么新风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1509,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_or_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.222","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.222.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.222.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,48],"fullStemEn":"A client develops fever, chills, and flank pain 15 minutes after a packed red blood cell transfusion is started. Place the nursing actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者开始输注浓缩红细胞 15 分钟后出现发热、寒战和腰背部疼痛。请将护理措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护理措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client develops fever, chills, and flank pain 15 minutes after a packed red blood cell transfusion is started.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者开始输注浓缩红细胞 15 分钟后出现发热、寒战和腰背部疼痛。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Stop the transfusion immediately and disconnect the blood tubing at the IV hub.","zh":"立即停止输血，并在静脉接口处断开输血管路。"},{"id":"E","en":"Obtain blood specimens and a urine sample as required by facility transfusion-reaction protocol.","zh":"按机构输血反应流程采集血标本和尿标本。"},{"id":"B","en":"Maintain IV access and begin infusing 0.9% sodium chloride through new tubing.","zh":"保持静脉通路，并通过新的输液管路输入 0.9% 氯化钠。"},{"id":"D","en":"Return the blood bag and original tubing to the blood bank with a completed transfusion reaction report.","zh":"将血袋和原输血管路连同已填写的输血反应报告送回血库。"},{"id":"F","en":"Document the reaction, interventions, notifications, specimens obtained, and the client's response.","zh":"记录输血反应、已采取的干预、通知对象、已采集的标本以及患者反应。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the prescribing provider and charge nurse of the suspected transfusion reaction.","zh":"通知开嘱医务人员和责任护士/护士长，说明疑似输血反应。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first priority is to stop exposure to the suspected blood product while preserving venous access with normal saline through new tubing. The nurse then escalates care, returns the implicated product and tubing for investigation, obtains required specimens, and documents the clinical course.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要任务是停止继续接触疑似导致反应的血制品，同时用新的管路输入生理盐水以保留静脉通路。随后通知相关人员、将相关血制品和管路送回血库调查、采集所需标本，并记录全过程。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a suspected transfusion reaction, first stop the source, then maintain access with normal saline, then notify, collect/return materials, and document.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到疑似输血反应，先停止来源，再用生理盐水维持通路，然后通知、收集/送回血制品相关材料，最后记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1510,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_fib_drain_monitoring_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.223","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.223.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.223.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[191,311],"terminalOffsetsZh":[73,111],"fullStemEn":"A client returns from open abdominal surgery with a Jackson-Pratt drain. During the first 24 hours after surgery, the nurse should assess and measure drain output at least every _____ hours. If _____ drainage appears suddenly after the first postoperative hour, the nurse should notify the provider immediately.","fullStemZh":"一名患者开放性腹部手术后返回病房，留置 Jackson-Pratt 引流管。术后最初 24 小时内，护士至少每 _____ 小时评估并测量引流量。若术后第 1 小时之后突然出现 _____ 引流液，护士应立即通知医务人员。","terminalSentenceEn":"If _____ drainage appears suddenly after the first postoperative hour, the nurse should notify the provider immediately.","terminalSentenceZh":"若术后第 1 小时之后突然出现 _____ 引流液，护士应立即通知医务人员。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During the first 24 hours after surgery, the nurse should assess and measure drain output at least every _____ hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"术后最初 24 小时内，护士至少每 _____ 小时评估并测量引流量。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Minimum assessment frequency during the first 24 hours post-op","zh":"术后最初 24 小时内的最低评估频率"},"acceptable":["4","4 hours","every 4 hours","q4h","at least every 4 hours"],"numeric":{"value":4,"tolerance":0,"unit":"hours"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Drainage type that requires immediate notification","zh":"需要立即通知的引流液类型"},"acceptable":["bright red","bright red sanguineous","bright-red sanguineous","sanguineous hemorrhagic","frankly bloody","sudden bright red bloody drainage","鲜红色","鲜红色血性","血性"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During the first postoperative day, drain output is assessed at least every 4 hours or more often per acuity and facility policy. A sudden change to bright red, frankly sanguineous drainage after the immediate postoperative period can indicate active bleeding and warrants prompt provider notification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"术后第一天，引流量至少每 4 小时评估一次，必要时根据病情和机构规定更频繁评估。术后早期之后突然变为鲜红色、明显血性引流，可能提示活动性出血，应及时通知医务人员。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For drains, compare amount, color, and timing; sudden bright red output after the earliest recovery period is a bleeding cue.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估引流管时要结合引流量、颜色和发生时间；最早恢复期后突然鲜红色引流是出血线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1511,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_matrix_pressure_injury_staging_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.224","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.224.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.224.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"For each wound description, select the pressure-injury group that best matches the finding.","fullStemZh":"请根据每项伤口描述，选择最符合的压力性损伤分组。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each wound description, select the pressure-injury group that best matches the finding.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据每项伤口描述，选择最符合的压力性损伤分组。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Intact skin over the sacrum is red and does not blanch with fingertip pressure.","zh":"骶尾部皮肤完整，发红，指压后不褪色。"},{"id":"r2","en":"A shallow open ulcer on the heel has a red-pink wound bed and no slough.","zh":"足跟有浅表开放性溃疡，创面呈红粉色，无腐肉。"},{"id":"r3","en":"A full-thickness wound on the trochanter has visible subcutaneous fat, but no tendon, muscle, or bone is exposed.","zh":"大转子处全层皮肤缺损，可见皮下脂肪，但未暴露肌腱、肌肉或骨骼。"},{"id":"r4","en":"A wound on the ankle has exposed tendon and visible bone.","zh":"踝部伤口暴露肌腱并可见骨骼。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Intact skin over the coccyx has localized purple-maroon discoloration and a closed blood-filled blister.","zh":"尾骨处皮肤完整，有局限性紫色/栗色变色，并有闭合性血疱。"},{"id":"r6","en":"The heel wound bed is completely covered by dry, stable eschar, so wound depth cannot be seen.","zh":"足跟创面完全被干燥、稳定的焦痂覆盖，无法看清伤口深度。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Stage 1 or 2 (superficial, intact or partial-thickness)","zh":"1 期或 2 期（浅表、皮肤完整或部分厚度缺损）"},{"id":"c2","en":"Stage 3, 4, deep tissue injury, or unstageable (full-thickness or cannot be staged)","zh":"3 期、4 期、深部组织损伤或不可分期（全层缺损或无法分期）"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stage 1 and 2 injuries are superficial or partial-thickness findings. Stage 3 and 4 injuries involve full-thickness loss or exposed deeper structures, while deep tissue injury and unstageable injury cannot be grouped with superficial staging.","rationaleCorrectZh":"1 期和 2 期属于浅表或部分厚度损伤。3 期和 4 期涉及全层组织缺损或深部结构暴露，深部组织损伤和不可分期损伤也不能归入浅表分组。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stage by the deepest visible tissue; if the base is hidden or discoloration suggests deep damage, do not classify it as superficial.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按可见的最深组织分期；若创面基底被遮盖或颜色提示深部损伤，不要归为浅表损伤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1512,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_cloze_vte_prophylaxis_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.225","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.225.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.225.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,93],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement about VTE prophylaxis after total knee arthroplasty.","fullStemZh":"请完成关于全膝关节置换术后 VTE 预防的临床判断句。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement about VTE prophylaxis after total knee arthroplasty.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成关于全膝关节置换术后 VTE 预防的临床判断句。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is postoperative day 1 after total knee arthroplasty. The nurse finds that the sequential compression device is not applied. The nurse's priority action is to {{1}} because {{2}}. If the client refuses the prescribed low-molecular-weight heparin, the nurse should {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"患者全膝关节置换术后第 1 天。护士发现序贯加压装置未使用。护士的优先措施是 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。如果患者拒绝医嘱的低分子肝素，护士应 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"wait until the next ambulation session to apply the SCD","zh":"等到下一次下床活动时再使用 SCD"},{"id":"o1","en":"apply the SCD now and verify the correct fit and settings","zh":"立即使用 SCD，并确认尺寸和设置正确"},{"id":"o3","en":"remove the SCD order because the client is receiving anticoagulation","zh":"因患者使用抗凝药而取消 SCD 医嘱"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the device is used mainly to reduce incision pain","zh":"该装置主要用于减轻切口疼痛"},{"id":"o1","en":"immobility after joint arthroplasty increases venous stasis and VTE risk","zh":"关节置换术后活动减少会增加静脉淤滞和 VTE 风险"},{"id":"o3","en":"the device replaces early ambulation when anticoagulation is ordered","zh":"开具抗凝药时该装置可替代早期下床活动"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"omit the dose without notification because the client has a right to refuse","zh":"患者有权拒绝，因此不需通知即可漏给该剂量"},{"id":"o3","en":"give the injection when the client is asleep to prevent a missed dose","zh":"在患者睡着时注射，以避免漏用该剂量"},{"id":"o1","en":"assess the reason for refusal, teach VTE risks and benefits, notify the provider, and document the refusal per policy","zh":"评估拒绝原因，宣教 VTE 风险和用药益处，通知医务人员，并按规定记录拒绝用药"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"a missed anticoagulant dose is harmless when the SCD is in place","zh":"只要使用 SCD，漏用抗凝药就没有风险"},{"id":"o1","en":"refusal may leave the client inadequately protected, but informed refusal must be respected and escalated","zh":"拒绝用药可能使患者保护不足，但知情拒绝必须被尊重并上报"},{"id":"o3","en":"documentation in the medication record alone completes the nurse's responsibility","zh":"仅在用药记录中记录即可完成护士职责"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Postoperative joint-replacement clients are at high risk for VTE. The nurse should promptly restore ordered mechanical prophylaxis and, if pharmacologic prophylaxis is refused, assess the reason, educate, notify the provider according to policy, and document the refusal and teaching.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关节置换术后患者发生 VTE 的风险较高。护士应立即恢复医嘱的机械预防措施；若患者拒绝药物预防，应评估原因、进行宣教、按规定通知医务人员，并记录拒绝及宣教内容。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an ordered prevention measure is missing, restore it first if safe; when a client refuses, assess, teach, notify, and document.","testTakingStrategyZh":"若医嘱预防措施遗漏且安全，应先恢复；若患者拒绝，则评估、宣教、通知并记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1513,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_fib_thoracentesis_assessment_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.226","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.226.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.226.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,272],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,64],"fullStemEn":"After assisting with a thoracentesis for pleural effusion, the nurse auscultates breath sounds on the affected side and monitors oxygen saturation to detect the primary early complication of _____. When required, a post-procedure chest radiograph should be obtained _____.","fullStemZh":"协助胸腔穿刺抽液后，护士在患侧听诊呼吸音并监测血氧饱和度，以早期发现主要并发症 _____。如需术后胸片，应 _____ 获取。","terminalSentenceEn":"When required, a post-procedure chest radiograph should be obtained _____.","terminalSentenceZh":"如需术后胸片，应 _____ 获取。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After assisting with a thoracentesis for pleural effusion, the nurse auscultates breath sounds on the affected side and monitors oxygen saturation to detect the primary early complication of _____.","penultimateSentenceZh":"协助胸腔穿刺抽液后，护士在患侧听诊呼吸音并监测血氧饱和度，以早期发现主要并发症 _____。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Primary early complication","zh":"主要早期并发症"},"acceptable":["pneumothorax","气胸"]},{"prompt":{"en":"Chest radiograph timing","zh":"胸片时间"},"acceptable":["as ordered or per facility protocol, commonly within 1-4 hours when required","as ordered or per facility protocol, commonly within 1–4 hours when required","as ordered, commonly within 1-4 hours when required","per facility protocol, commonly within 1-4 hours when required","within 1-4 hours when ordered","1-4 hours when required","1–4 hours when required"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pneumothorax is a key early complication after thoracentesis and is assessed by respiratory status, breath sounds, and oxygenation. A chest radiograph is obtained as ordered or per facility protocol, commonly within 1–4 hours when required, rather than being assumed mandatory after every uncomplicated thoracentesis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"气胸是胸腔穿刺后重要的早期并发症，应通过呼吸状况、呼吸音和氧合情况评估。胸片应按医嘱或机构流程获取，需要时通常在 1–4 小时内完成，而不是所有无并发症穿刺后都必然需要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After procedures involving the pleural space, prioritize respiratory cues and avoid making protocol-dependent imaging sound universal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"胸膜腔相关操作后优先关注呼吸线索；对于依赖流程的影像检查，不要把它表述为普遍强制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1514,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_fib_enteral_feeding_tolerance_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.227","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.227.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.227.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[235,344],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,89],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving continuous gastric tube feeding has abdominal distension, nausea, and a feeling of fullness. A single gastric residual volume of at least _____ mL should prompt the nurse to hold the feeding and notify the provider. To reduce aspiration risk during enteral feeding, maintain the head of the bed at a minimum of _____ degrees.","fullStemZh":"一名接受连续胃内管饲的患者出现腹胀、恶心和饱胀感。单次胃残余量至少 _____ mL 时，护士应暂停管饲并通知医务人员。为降低管饲期间误吸风险，应将床头至少抬高 _____ 度。","terminalSentenceEn":"To reduce aspiration risk during enteral feeding, maintain the head of the bed at a minimum of _____ degrees.","terminalSentenceZh":"为降低管饲期间误吸风险，应将床头至少抬高 _____ 度。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A single gastric residual volume of at least _____ mL should prompt the nurse to hold the feeding and notify the provider.","penultimateSentenceZh":"单次胃残余量至少 _____ mL 时，护士应暂停管饲并通知医务人员。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Single gastric residual volume threshold","zh":"单次胃残余量阈值"},"acceptable":["500","500 mL","500 ml"],"numeric":{"value":500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Minimum head-of-bed elevation","zh":"最低床头抬高角度"},"acceptable":["30","30 degrees","30°","30-45","30-45 degrees","30 to 45 degrees"],"numeric":{"value":30,"tolerance":0,"unit":"degrees"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A single gastric residual volume of 500 mL with signs of intolerance is a defensible threshold to hold a continuous gastric feeding and notify the provider. Head-of-bed elevation of at least 30 degrees, often 30–45 degrees, reduces aspiration risk during enteral feeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在出现不耐受表现时，单次胃残余量 500 mL 是暂停连续胃内管饲并通知医务人员的明确阈值。管饲期间床头至少抬高 30 度（常为 30–45 度）可降低误吸风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the threshold stated by the stem: a single high GRV uses 500 mL, while repeated lower residuals require repeated-check wording.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干情境选阈值：单次高胃残余量用 500 mL；较低阈值需题干说明重复测量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1515,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_or_constipation_management_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.228","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.228.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.228.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,49],"fullStemEn":"A client is on day 3 of hospitalization after elective hip replacement and has not had a bowel movement. Arrange the nursing interventions from least invasive to most invasive.","fullStemZh":"一名患者择期髋关节置换术后住院第 3 天，尚未排便。请按从最少侵入性到较强干预的顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the nursing interventions from least invasive to most invasive.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按从最少侵入性到较强干预的顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is on day 3 of hospitalization after elective hip replacement and has not had a bowel movement.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者择期髋关节置换术后住院第 3 天，尚未排便。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Increase fluids to 2000–2500 mL/day as tolerated and offer high-fiber foods.","zh":"在可耐受情况下将液体摄入增加至每日 2000–2500 mL，并提供高纤维食物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Promote early ambulation and physical activity as cleared by the orthopedic team.","zh":"在骨科团队允许后，促进早期下床活动和身体活动。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the prescribed stool softener, such as docusate sodium.","zh":"给予医嘱的粪便软化剂，如多库酯钠。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer the prescribed stimulant laxative if there is no result after 24 hours of the above measures.","zh":"若上述措施 24 小时后仍无效果，给予医嘱的刺激性泻药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the last bowel movement, usual pattern, diet, opioid use, fluid intake, and mobility.","zh":"评估上次排便时间、平时排便规律、饮食、阿片类药物使用、液体摄入和活动情况。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Constipation management begins with assessment and modifiable nonpharmacologic measures, then progresses to prescribed medications. A stimulant laxative is more aggressive than a stool softener and is used if earlier measures are ineffective.","rationaleCorrectZh":"便秘管理应先评估并处理可改变的非药物因素，再逐步使用医嘱药物。刺激性泻药比粪便软化剂干预更强，通常在前述措施无效后使用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For comfort problems, assess first, try least invasive nonpharmacologic measures, then move to ordered medications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理舒适问题时，先评估，再用最少侵入性的非药物措施，最后逐步使用医嘱药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1516,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_matrix_iv_phlebitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.229","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.229.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.229.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,77],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"For each peripheral IV site finding, select the appropriate nursing response.","fullStemZh":"请根据每项外周静脉输液部位表现，选择适当的护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each peripheral IV site finding, select the appropriate nursing response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据每项外周静脉输液部位表现，选择适当的护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"No redness, swelling, pain, or tenderness at the insertion site.","zh":"穿刺部位无发红、肿胀、疼痛或压痛。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Faint erythema and slight swelling at the site with mild pain on palpation.","zh":"穿刺部位轻微红斑和轻度肿胀，触诊有轻度疼痛。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Marked pain at the site with erythema and swelling along the vein.","zh":"穿刺部位明显疼痛，沿静脉发红并肿胀。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Palpable venous cord extending 3 cm from the insertion site with erythema and swelling.","zh":"可触及从穿刺点延伸 3 cm 的静脉条索，伴发红和肿胀。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Palpable venous cord greater than 3 cm from the site with purulent drainage at the insertion point.","zh":"可触及超过 3 cm 的静脉条索，穿刺点有脓性分泌物。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Discontinue IV, restart at a new site, and notify provider if systemic signs occur","zh":"停止该静脉通路，另选新部位置管；若有全身症状则通知医务人员"},{"id":"c1","en":"Continue IV and reassess per policy","zh":"继续使用该静脉通路，并按规定复评"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"No signs and very mild early irritation can be monitored per policy, but marked pain with erythema/swelling, a palpable cord, or purulent drainage indicates phlebitis that requires discontinuing the IV and restarting at a new site.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无异常或非常轻微的早期刺激可按规定观察；但明显疼痛伴发红/肿胀、可触及条索或脓性分泌物提示静脉炎，需要停止该通路并另选新部位置管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Escalate IV-site findings when pain is marked, inflammation tracks along the vein, a cord is palpable, or drainage appears.","testTakingStrategyZh":"若输液部位疼痛明显、炎症沿静脉延伸、可触及条索或出现分泌物，应升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1517,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_cloze_postop_urinary_retention_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.230","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.230.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.230.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement for a client with possible postoperative urinary retention.","fullStemZh":"请完成关于疑似术后尿潴留患者的临床判断句。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement for a client with possible postoperative urinary retention.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成关于疑似术后尿潴留患者的临床判断句。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"A client is 6 hours post-op from abdominal hysterectomy and has not voided. A bladder scan shows 420 mL. The nurse should first {{1}} because {{2}}. If the client still cannot void after the initial intervention, the nurse should {{3}} because {{4}}.","zh":"患者腹式子宫切除术后 6 小时尚未排尿。膀胱扫描显示 420 mL。护士首先应 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。若初始干预后患者仍不能排尿，护士应 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"insert an indwelling catheter immediately without attempting to void","zh":"不尝试排尿，立即置入留置导尿管"},{"id":"o1","en":"assist the client to a normal voiding position and provide privacy, running water, and adequate analgesia if prescribed","zh":"协助患者采取正常排尿体位，提供隐私、流水声，并按医嘱处理疼痛"},{"id":"o3","en":"encourage the client to wait until the next routine vital-sign round","zh":"鼓励患者等到下一次常规测量生命体征时再处理"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"420 mL suggests retention, but noninvasive measures may allow voiding and avoid unnecessary catheterization","zh":"420 mL 提示尿潴留，但非侵入性措施可能帮助排尿并避免不必要导尿"},{"id":"o3","en":"postoperative clients should not ambulate or sit upright to void","zh":"术后患者不应下床或坐起排尿"},{"id":"o2","en":"the bladder volume is too low to require any nursing action","zh":"膀胱容量太低，不需要任何护理措施"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"notify the provider and perform intermittent straight catheterization if prescribed or allowed by protocol","zh":"通知医务人员，并在有医嘱或流程允许时进行间歇性直导尿"},{"id":"o2","en":"restrict all oral fluids for the rest of the shift","zh":"本班余下时间完全限制口服液体"},{"id":"o3","en":"massage firmly over the lower abdomen until urine drains","zh":"用力按摩下腹部直到尿液排出"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"persistent retention can overdistend the bladder and compromise recovery","zh":"持续尿潴留会使膀胱过度膨胀并影响恢复"},{"id":"o2","en":"intermittent catheterization is used primarily to treat constipation","zh":"间歇导尿主要用于治疗便秘"},{"id":"o3","en":"urinary retention after surgery is expected and should never be reported","zh":"术后尿潴留属于预期情况，永远不需报告"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A bladder scan of 420 mL at 6 hours post-op indicates likely retention requiring action. The nurse first uses noninvasive measures that support spontaneous voiding; if these fail, escalation and intermittent catheterization per order or protocol prevent overdistention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"术后 6 小时膀胱扫描 420 mL 提示可能尿潴留，需要处理。护士应先采取支持自主排尿的非侵入性措施；若无效，应上报并按医嘱或流程进行间歇导尿，以防膀胱过度膨胀。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the least invasive effective action first, but do not ignore objective retention; escalate when supportive measures fail.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先选择有效且最少侵入性的措施，但不能忽视客观尿潴留；支持措施无效时要升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1518,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_jun12_or_near_miss_medication_error_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.231","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.231.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.231.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,224],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,63],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers a near-miss medication error: the wrong dose of metoprolol was selected in the automated dispenser, but the error was caught before administration. Place the quality and safety actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一起接近失误的用药错误：自动取药柜中选取了错误剂量的美托洛尔，但在给药前已被发现。请按正确顺序排列质量与安全处理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the quality and safety actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列质量与安全处理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse discovers a near-miss medication error: the wrong dose of metoprolol was selected in the automated dispenser, but the error was caught before administration.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现一起接近失误的用药错误：自动取药柜中选取了错误剂量的美托洛尔，但在给药前已被发现。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client and confirm that no medication was administered and no client harm occurred.","zh":"评估患者，并确认药物尚未给药且患者未受到伤害。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the charge nurse and the prescribing provider according to facility policy.","zh":"按机构政策通知责任护士/护士长和开嘱医务人员。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document the clinical assessment in the medical record without referencing the occurrence report.","zh":"在病历中记录临床评估，但不提及安全/事件报告。"},{"id":"E","en":"Participate in a debrief or root-cause review if initiated by the unit manager.","zh":"若病区管理者启动复盘或根因分析，则参与其中。"},{"id":"D","en":"Complete the institutional occurrence or safety report in the electronic reporting system.","zh":"在电子报告系统中填写机构的事件/安全报告。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A near-miss still requires a safety response. The nurse first confirms no client harm, then notifies appropriate clinical leaders/providers per policy, documents objective clinical assessment in the medical record without mentioning the occurrence report, completes the institutional safety report, and participates in follow-up review if initiated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接近失误仍需进行安全处理。护士首先确认患者无伤害，然后按政策通知相关临床负责人/医务人员，在病历中客观记录临床评估且不提及事件报告，再完成机构安全报告；若启动后续复盘或根因分析，则参与。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For errors and near misses, separate clinical care documentation from confidential safety reporting; assess harm before paperwork.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理错误和接近失误时，要区分临床护理记录和保密安全报告；先评估伤害，再处理文书。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1519,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_fib_burn_parkland_rate_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.232","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.232.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.232.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[273,307],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,114],"fullStemEn":"An adult client weighing 70 kg arrives immediately after sustaining partial-thickness burns shown on the diagram. Using the traditional Parkland formula (4 mL lactated Ringer's × kg × %TBSA), how many mL/hr should the nurse set for the first 8 hours after the burn injury? Round to the nearest whole number.","fullStemZh":"一名体重 70 kg 的成年患者在发生图中所示的二度烧伤后立即到达。使用传统 Parkland 公式（乳酸林格液 4 mL × kg × %TBSA），护士应将烧伤后前 8 小时的输液速度设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the traditional Parkland formula (4 mL lactated Ringer's × kg × %TBSA), how many mL/hr should the nurse set for the first 8 hours after the burn injury?","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用传统 Parkland 公式（乳酸林格液 4 mL × kg × %TBSA），护士应将烧伤后前 8 小时的输液速度设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/hr"},"acceptable":["630","630 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":630,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the anterior trunk (18%) plus the anterior left leg (9%) plus the anterior right leg (9%), for 36% TBSA. Traditional Parkland volume is 4 × 70 × 36 = 10,080 mL in the first 24 hours; half is 5,040 mL in the first 8 hours from the time of burn. 5,040 ÷ 8 = 630 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为前躯干 18% 加左腿前面 9% 加右腿前面 9%，共 36% TBSA。传统 Parkland 总量为 4 × 70 × 36 = 10,080 mL（前 24 小时）；其中一半 5,040 mL 应在烧伤后前 8 小时给入。5,040 ÷ 8 = 630 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a burn diagram is used, first convert only the shaded partial- or full-thickness areas into %TBSA, then apply the formula named in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到烧伤图时，先把图中阴影的二度或三度烧伤面积换算为 %TBSA，再使用题干指定的公式。","sourceMetadata":"Adult Rule of Nines; traditional Parkland formula 4 mL/kg/%TBSA with half in first 8 hours from time of burn.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1520,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_mc_burn_tbsa_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.233","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.233.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.233.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,43],"fullStemEn":"An adult client has partial-thickness burns shaded on the diagram. Using the adult Rule of Nines, what is the estimated %TBSA burned?","fullStemZh":"一名成年患者有图中阴影所示的二度烧伤。使用成人九分法，估计烧伤面积为多少 %TBSA？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the adult Rule of Nines, what is the estimated %TBSA burned?","terminalSentenceZh":"使用成人九分法，估计烧伤面积为多少 %TBSA？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An adult client has partial-thickness burns shaded on the diagram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名成年患者有图中阴影所示的二度烧伤。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"13.5%","zh":"13.5%"},{"id":"A","en":"9%","zh":"9%"},{"id":"C","en":"18%","zh":"18%"},{"id":"D","en":"22.5%","zh":"22.5%"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shaded regions are the anterior head (4.5%) and the entire left arm (4.5% anterior + 4.5% posterior = 9%). Total TBSA is 4.5% + 9% = 13.5%.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阴影区域为头部前面 4.5% 和整个左上肢（前面 4.5% + 后面 4.5% = 9%）。总面积为 4.5% + 9% = 13.5%。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate anterior and posterior surfaces before adding. A full adult arm is 9%, but one side of the arm is 4.5%.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先区分身体前面和后面再相加。成人一整只手臂是 9%，单侧面是 4.5%。","sourceMetadata":"Adult Rule of Nines.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1521,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_fib_io_net_balance_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.234","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.234.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.234.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,54],"fullStemEn":"Review the intake and output flowsheet for the 0700-1500 shift. What is the client's net fluid balance in mL? Enter a positive number if intake exceeds output.","fullStemZh":"查看 0700-1500 班次的出入量记录。如果摄入量大于排出量，请输入正数。该患者净液体平衡为多少 mL？","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter a positive number if intake exceeds output.","terminalSentenceZh":"该患者净液体平衡为多少 mL？","penultimateSentenceEn":"What is the client's net fluid balance in mL?","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果摄入量大于排出量，请输入正数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"mL"},"acceptable":["640","+640","640 mL"],"numeric":{"value":640,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake is 360 + 750 + 100 = 1,210 mL. Output is 420 + 150 = 570 mL. Net balance is 1,210 − 570 = +640 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"摄入量为 360 + 750 + 100 = 1,210 mL。排出量为 420 + 150 = 570 mL。净平衡为 1,210 − 570 = +640 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For I&O questions, calculate intake and output separately before subtracting; do not combine all numbers in one step.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出入量题先分别计算摄入量和排出量，再相减；不要把所有数字混在一步计算。","sourceMetadata":"Nursing intake/output documentation arithmetic.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1522,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_mc_io_output_total_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.235","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.235.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.235.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[22,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[9,25],"fullStemEn":"Review the flowsheet. Which value should the nurse document as the total output for this shift?","fullStemZh":"查看出入量记录单。护士应记录该班次总排出量为多少？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which value should the nurse document as the total output for this shift?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录该班次总排出量为多少？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the flowsheet.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看出入量记录单。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"1,455 mL","zh":"1,455 mL"},{"id":"B","en":"725 mL","zh":"725 mL"},{"id":"A","en":"660 mL","zh":"660 mL"},{"id":"C","en":"795 mL","zh":"795 mL"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Output includes urine 525 mL, JP drain 70 mL, and loose stool 200 mL. Total output is 525 + 70 + 200 = 795 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"排出量包括尿液 525 mL、JP 引流 70 mL 和稀便 200 mL。总排出量为 525 + 70 + 200 = 795 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look at the requested total. Output totals include fluid leaving the body, not tube feeding or flushes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"看清题目要求的总量。排出量是离开身体的液体，不包括管饲或冲管液。","sourceMetadata":"Nursing intake/output documentation arithmetic.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1523,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_matrix_io_totals_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.236","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.236.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.236.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[40,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[9,25],"fullStemEn":"Review the intake and output flowsheet. For each proposed documentation value, select whether it is accurate.","fullStemZh":"查看出入量记录单。请判断每个拟记录的数值是否正确。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each proposed documentation value, select whether it is accurate.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每个拟记录的数值是否正确。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the intake and output flowsheet.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看出入量记录单。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Intake total: 720 mL","zh":"摄入量总计：720 mL"},{"id":"r2","en":"Output total: 575 mL","zh":"排出量总计：575 mL"},{"id":"r3","en":"Net balance: −145 mL","zh":"净平衡：−145 mL"},{"id":"r4","en":"Net balance: +145 mL","zh":"净平衡：+145 mL"}],"columns":[{"id":"inaccurate","en":"Inaccurate","zh":"不正确"},{"id":"accurate","en":"Accurate","zh":"正确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["accurate"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["accurate"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["inaccurate"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["accurate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake is 600 + 120 = 720 mL. Output is 350 + 225 = 575 mL. Net balance is 720 − 575 = +145 mL, not −145 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"摄入量为 600 + 120 = 720 mL。排出量为 350 + 225 = 575 mL。净平衡为 720 − 575 = +145 mL，而不是 −145 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A positive net balance means retained fluid; a negative net balance means more output than intake.","testTakingStrategyZh":"净平衡为正表示液体潴留；净平衡为负表示排出量多于摄入量。","sourceMetadata":"Nursing intake/output documentation arithmetic.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1524,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_fib_medlabel_heparin_rate_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.237","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.237.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.237.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,55],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes heparin at 1,000 units/hr. Using the medication label, at how many mL/hr should the nurse program the infusion pump? Round to the nearest whole number.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为肝素 1,000 units/hr。根据药品标签，护士应将输液泵设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the medication label, at how many mL/hr should the nurse program the infusion pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据药品标签，护士应将输液泵设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/hr"},"acceptable":["10","10 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":10,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label shows 25,000 units in 250 mL, so the concentration is 100 units/mL. The ordered rate is 1,000 units/hr. 1,000 ÷ 100 = 10 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示 25,000 units 溶于 250 mL，因此浓度为 100 units/mL。医嘱为 1,000 units/hr。1,000 ÷ 100 = 10 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For infusion labels, compute concentration first, then divide the ordered dose rate by that concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输液标签题先算浓度，再用医嘱剂量速度除以浓度。","sourceMetadata":"Medication-label concentration arithmetic; institutional heparin protocols vary and require order verification.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1525,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_mc_medlabel_tablet_quantity_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.238","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.238.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.238.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,124],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,34],"fullStemEn":"The medication order is acetaminophen 650 mg by mouth now. Based on the label, how many tablets should the nurse administer?","fullStemZh":"医嘱为立即口服对乙酰氨基酚 650 mg。根据标签，护士应给多少片？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the label, how many tablets should the nurse administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据标签，护士应给多少片？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The medication order is acetaminophen 650 mg by mouth now.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为立即口服对乙酰氨基酚 650 mg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"3 tablets","zh":"3 片"},{"id":"A","en":"1 tablet","zh":"1 片"},{"id":"D","en":"4 tablets","zh":"4 片"},{"id":"B","en":"2 tablets","zh":"2 片"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Each tablet contains 325 mg. The ordered dose is 650 mg. 650 ÷ 325 = 2 tablets.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每片含 325 mg。医嘱剂量为 650 mg。650 ÷ 325 = 2 片。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the label strength as the denominator: ordered dose divided by dose per tablet.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把标签剂量作为分母：医嘱剂量除以每片剂量。","sourceMetadata":"Medication-label dose arithmetic.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1526,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_matrix_device_pca_basal_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.239","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.239.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.239.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,68],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative adult client who is opioid-naive is receiving morphine by patient-controlled analgesia (PCA). Review the pump screen. For each finding, indicate whether the nurse should follow up before continuing the infusion.","fullStemZh":"一名术后成年患者既往未使用阿片类药物，正在通过患者自控镇痛（PCA）泵接受吗啡。查看泵屏幕。请判断每项发现是否需要护士在继续输注前跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, indicate whether the nurse should follow up before continuing the infusion.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项发现是否需要护士在继续输注前跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the pump screen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看泵屏幕。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"PCA mode includes a basal infusion.","zh":"PCA 模式包含基础持续输注。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Demand dose is 1 mg.","zh":"按需剂量为 1 mg。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Lockout interval is 10 minutes.","zh":"锁定间隔为 10 分钟。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Medication displayed is morphine.","zh":"屏幕显示药物为吗啡。"}],"columns":[{"id":"expected_setting","en":"Expected/verify routinely","zh":"预期设置/常规核对"},{"id":"follow_up","en":"Follow up before continuing","zh":"继续前需要跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["follow_up"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["expected_setting"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["expected_setting"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["expected_setting"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The load-bearing cue is the basal infusion in an opioid-naive client. Basal opioid delivery can increase the risk for oversedation and respiratory depression and should be verified against the order and policy before continuing. The drug, demand dose, and lockout interval require routine verification but are not the specific unsafe cue in this stem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键线索是既往未使用阿片类药物的患者设置了基础持续输注。基础阿片输注会增加过度镇静和呼吸抑制风险，继续前应按医嘱和政策核对。药物、按需剂量和锁定间隔也需常规核对，但不是本题特定的不安全线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With device screens, identify the setting that changes the nursing risk in this client, not just any number that appears on the display.","testTakingStrategyZh":"设备屏幕题要找出会改变该患者护理风险的设置，而不是只看到屏幕上任意数字。","sourceMetadata":"PCA opioid safety principles; basal infusions increase respiratory-depression risk in opioid-naive clients and require order/policy verification.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1527,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_visual_smoke_2026_06_12_fib_device_enteral_duration_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.240","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.240.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.240.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,42],"fullStemEn":"Review the enteral feeding pump screen. If the displayed settings continue unchanged, over how many hours will the volume to be infused run? Round to the nearest whole number.","fullStemZh":"查看肠内营养泵屏幕。如果屏幕设置保持不变，待输注容量将运行多少小时？四舍五入到整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"If the displayed settings continue unchanged, over how many hours will the volume to be infused run?","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果屏幕设置保持不变，待输注容量将运行多少小时？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"hours","zh":"小时"},"acceptable":["4","4 hr","4 hours"],"numeric":{"value":4,"tolerance":0,"unit":"hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pump shows a rate of 60 mL/hr and a volume to be infused of 240 mL. Duration is 240 ÷ 60 = 4 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"泵屏幕显示速率为 60 mL/hr，待输注容量为 240 mL。运行时间为 240 ÷ 60 = 4 小时。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pump duration, divide VTBI by the rate, then convert minutes and hours if needed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算泵运行时间时，用待输注容量除以速率，必要时再换算分钟和小时。","sourceMetadata":"Pump rate-duration arithmetic.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1528,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.241","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.241.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,51],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: COPD discharge with home oxygen A client with COPD is being prepared for discharge with new home oxygen after hospitalization for an exacerbation.","fullStemZh":"展开病例：COPD 患者带居家氧疗出院 一名 COPD 患者因急性加重住院后，准备带新的居家氧疗出院。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: COPD discharge with home oxygen A client with COPD is being prepared for discharge with new home oxygen after hospitalization for an exacerbation.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开病例：COPD 患者带居家氧疗出院 一名 COPD 患者因急性加重住院后，准备带新的居家氧疗出院。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case focuses on safe transition to home oxygen: recognize fire and fall hazards, correct unsafe self-adjustment, coordinate equipment, and verify teach-back before discharge.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例重点是安全过渡到居家氧疗：识别火灾和跌倒风险，纠正不安全的自行调节，协调设备，并在出院前确认回示。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In discharge cases, compare the client's home behaviors with the prescribed plan and the highest-consequence safety risks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出院类病例要将患者居家行为与处方计划及后果最严重的安全风险进行比较。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1529,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,37],"fullStemEn":"Using the initial home oxygen referral note, classify each finding as a safety concern or an expected finding for discharge teaching.","fullStemZh":"根据初始居家氧疗转介记录，将每项发现归类为安全隐患或出院宣教中的预期发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the initial home oxygen referral note, classify each finding as a safety concern or an expected finding for discharge teaching.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据初始居家氧疗转介记录，将每项发现归类为安全隐患或出院宣教中的预期发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Spouse smokes on the apartment balcony while the sliding door is open","zh":"配偶在阳台吸烟，且滑动门开着"},{"id":"r2","en":"Client applies petroleum jelly to dry nares before placing the cannula","zh":"患者放置鼻导管前在干燥鼻腔涂凡士林"},{"id":"r3","en":"Client sets the concentrator to 2 L/min as prescribed","zh":"患者按处方将制氧机设为 2 L/分"},{"id":"r4","en":"Oxygen tubing runs across the bedroom doorway","zh":"氧气管路横跨卧室门口"},{"id":"r5","en":"Portable concentrator battery is fully charged before leaving home","zh":"外出前便携制氧机电池已充满电"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Safety concern","zh":"安全隐患"},{"id":"c2","en":"Expected finding","zh":"预期发现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Smoking exposure, petroleum products near the cannula, and extension tubing across a walkway increase fire or fall risk. Correct oxygen flow use and a charged concentrator backup are expected safety behaviors.","rationaleCorrectZh":"吸烟暴露、鼻导管附近使用含油产品以及延长管横跨走道会增加火灾或跌倒风险。按处方氧流量使用和备有充电的制氧机备用电源属于预期的安全行为。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate oxygen-fire hazards from ordinary equipment teaching; oxygen supports combustion even when it is not flammable itself.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将氧气相关火灾隐患与普通设备宣教分开判断；氧气本身不易燃，但会助燃。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1530,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the Stage 1 teaching session and identifies the discharge issue that must be corrected before the client leaves.","fullStemZh":"护士查看第 1 阶段的宣教记录，并判断患者离院前必须纠正的出院问题。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the Stage 1 teaching session and identifies the discharge issue that must be corrected before the client leaves.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士查看第 1 阶段的宣教记录，并判断患者离院前必须纠正的出院问题。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The priority discharge barrier is {{1}}; the nurse should teach the client to {{2}}.","zh":"优先处理的出院障碍是 {{1}}；护士应教导患者 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"self-adjusting oxygen flow for shortness of breath","zh":"因气短而自行调节氧流量"},{"id":"o2","en":"using pursed-lip breathing during activity","zh":"活动时使用缩唇呼吸"},{"id":"o3","en":"keeping the concentrator plugged into a grounded outlet","zh":"将制氧机插入接地插座"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"increase oxygen until the pulse oximeter reads 100%","zh":"增加氧流量直到血氧仪显示 100%"},{"id":"o3","en":"turn off oxygen during all household ambulation","zh":"在家中走动时都关闭氧气"},{"id":"o1","en":"use the prescribed flow and seek help if symptoms worsen","zh":"按处方流量使用，症状加重时求助"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client's statement about turning the oxygen higher during dyspnea shows unsafe self-adjustment. The nurse should reinforce using the prescribed flow rate and calling the provider or emergency services for worsening symptoms.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表示气促时自行调高氧流量，说明存在不安全的自行调节。护士应强化按处方流量使用，并在症状加重时联系医护人员或急救服务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a home teaching statement includes independent dose or device changes, look for the response that restores the prescribed plan and escalation pathway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"如果居家宣教反馈中出现自行改变剂量或设备设置，应选择能恢复处方计划并明确升级求助路径的回答。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1531,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,36],"fullStemEn":"The client is scheduled for discharge with new home oxygen after Stage 2. Place the nurse's actions in the best order.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段后，患者计划带新的居家氧疗出院。请按最佳顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the best order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最佳顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is scheduled for discharge with new home oxygen after Stage 2.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段后，患者计划带新的居家氧疗出院。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Document discharge readiness and communicate any remaining barriers to the team","zh":"记录出院准备情况，并向团队沟通仍存在的障碍"},{"id":"B","en":"Confirm home equipment delivery, tubing supply, and backup power plan","zh":"确认家用设备送达、管路供应和备用电源计划"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the client and spouse to demonstrate fire-safety and tubing-management steps","zh":"请患者和配偶演示防火和管路管理步骤"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the oxygen prescription, target use instructions, and equipment ordered","zh":"核对氧疗处方、目标使用说明和已订设备"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first verifies the prescription and equipment plan, then confirms delivery and backup arrangements, assesses caregiver teach-back, and finally documents readiness and unresolved barriers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先核对处方和设备计划，然后确认送达与备用安排，再评估照护者回示，最后记录出院准备情况和未解决障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge sequencing, verify the order, arrange the resources, assess learning, then document and hand off unresolved risks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理出院顺序时，先核对医嘱，再安排资源，再评估学习效果，最后记录并交接未解决风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1532,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"During Stage 3 teach-back, which client statement shows correct understanding of home oxygen safety?","fullStemZh":"在第 3 阶段回示中，哪项患者陈述表明其正确理解了居家氧疗安全？","terminalSentenceEn":"During Stage 3 teach-back, which client statement shows correct understanding of home oxygen safety?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第 3 阶段回示中，哪项患者陈述表明其正确理解了居家氧疗安全？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"I will keep oxygen away from flames and post an oxygen-in-use notice.","zh":"我会让氧气远离明火，并张贴正在使用氧气的提示。"},{"id":"A","en":"I can sit near someone smoking if my cannula is under my shirt.","zh":"如果鼻导管放在衣服下，我可以坐在吸烟的人旁边。"},{"id":"C","en":"I should use petroleum jelly daily so my nose does not dry out.","zh":"我应该每天用凡士林，避免鼻子干燥。"},{"id":"D","en":"I will place extra tubing under throw rugs so no one sees it.","zh":"我会把多余管路放在小地毯下面，这样别人看不到。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Posting oxygen-in-use notices and keeping oxygen away from smoking and flames are appropriate fire-safety steps.","rationaleCorrectZh":"张贴正在使用氧气的提示，并让氧气远离吸烟和明火，是恰当的防火措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the statement that reduces both fire and fall risk without changing the prescribed therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择既降低火灾和跌倒风险，又不改变处方治疗的陈述。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1533,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_copd_home_oxygen_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.241.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[190,224],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,73],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3 equipment teaching states: The portable cylinder contains 600 L of usable oxygen. The prescribed flow is 2 L/min for activity. How many minutes of oxygen are available for activity? Round to the nearest whole minute.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段设备宣教写明：便携氧气瓶可用氧气量为 600 L。活动时处方流量为 2 L/分。该氧气瓶可供活动使用多少分钟？四舍五入到最接近的整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole minute.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many minutes of oxygen are available for activity?","penultimateSentenceZh":"该氧气瓶可供活动使用多少分钟？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minutes","zh":"分钟"},"acceptable":["300","300 minutes"],"numeric":{"value":300,"tolerance":0,"unit":"minutes"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Available time equals available volume divided by flow rate: 600 L ÷ 2 L/min = 300 minutes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可用时间等于可用容量除以流量：600 L ÷ 2 L/分 = 300 分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track the units. Liters divided by liters per minute leaves minutes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"注意单位。升除以升/分钟，剩下的单位就是分钟。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1534,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.242","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.242.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: unwitnessed fall in long-term care An older adult resident is found on the floor near the bathroom during night shift.","fullStemZh":"展开病例：长期护理机构内无人目击跌倒 一名老年住民夜班时在卫生间附近地上被发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: unwitnessed fall in long-term care An older adult resident is found on the floor near the bathroom during night shift.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开病例：长期护理机构内无人目击跌倒 一名老年住民夜班时在卫生间附近地上被发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes immediate post-fall assessment before movement, recognition of neurologic and fracture red flags, timely escalation, safe transfer handoff, and least-restrictive fall prevention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例强调跌倒后移动前的立即评估、识别神经和骨折危险信号、及时升级处理、安全转送交接以及最少限制的跌倒预防。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For falls, priority shifts from prevention to injury detection and stabilization once the event has occurred.","testTakingStrategyZh":"跌倒发生后，优先重点从预防转为发现损伤和稳定病情。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1535,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[49,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,35],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1 describes a resident found on the floor. What should the nurse do first?","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段描述一名长期护理机构住民被发现倒在地上。护士首先应做什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse do first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应做什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 1 describes a resident found on the floor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段描述一名长期护理机构住民被发现倒在地上。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Call the family to ask whether the resident has fallen before","zh":"打电话给家属询问住民以前是否跌倒过"},{"id":"C","en":"Complete the occurrence report before providing further care","zh":"先完成事件报告，再继续护理"},{"id":"A","en":"Help the resident back to bed and then obtain vital signs","zh":"先扶住民回床，再测量生命体征"},{"id":"B","en":"Keep the resident still and assess airway, breathing, circulation, pain, and injury","zh":"让住民保持不动，并评估气道、呼吸、循环、疼痛和损伤"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Before moving the resident, the nurse should assess airway, breathing, circulation, level of consciousness, pain, and obvious injury to prevent worsening an occult injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"移动住民前，护士应评估气道、呼吸、循环、意识水平、疼痛和明显损伤，以免加重潜在损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After an unwitnessed fall, do not rush to lift the person. Assess for injury and neurologic change first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"无人目击跌倒后，不要急着扶起。先评估损伤和神经状态变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1536,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,57],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Using Stage 2 data, classify each finding after the fall.","fullStemZh":"根据第 2 阶段资料，将跌倒后的每项发现分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using Stage 2 data, classify each finding after the fall.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第 2 阶段资料，将跌倒后的每项发现分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Resident is oriented to person only; baseline is oriented to person and place","zh":"住民仅能辨认本人；基线为能辨认本人和地点"},{"id":"r2","en":"One episode of emesis after the fall","zh":"跌倒后呕吐一次"},{"id":"r3","en":"Right pupil 5 mm and left pupil 3 mm","zh":"右瞳孔 5 mm，左瞳孔 3 mm"},{"id":"r4","en":"Right leg appears shortened and externally rotated","zh":"右腿看起来短缩并外旋"},{"id":"r5","en":"2-cm elbow abrasion without active bleeding","zh":"肘部 2 cm 擦伤，无活动性出血"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Document and monitor","zh":"记录并监测"},{"id":"c1","en":"Escalate promptly","zh":"立即升级处理"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New confusion, vomiting, unequal pupils, and hip pain with shortening/external rotation require urgent escalation. A small superficial abrasion without active bleeding is expected local trauma but still documented.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新发意识混乱、呕吐、瞳孔不等大以及髋部疼痛伴短缩外旋需要紧急升级处理。小的表浅擦伤且无活动性出血属于局部外伤表现，但仍需记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare each finding with baseline and ask whether it suggests head injury, fracture, or instability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将每项发现与基线比较，并判断是否提示头部损伤、骨折或不稳定。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1537,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,78],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"The nurse prepares to notify the provider after reviewing the fall assessment.","fullStemZh":"护士查看跌倒评估后准备通知医护人员。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse prepares to notify the provider after reviewing the fall assessment.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士查看跌倒评估后准备通知医护人员。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should report concern for {{1}} and maintain {{2}} until further evaluation.","zh":"护士应报告对 {{1}} 的担忧，并在进一步评估前维持 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"chronic dementia without acute change","zh":"无急性变化的慢性痴呆"},{"id":"o1","en":"intracranial injury and possible hip fracture","zh":"颅内损伤和可能髋部骨折"},{"id":"o2","en":"mild bruising from a witnessed low-risk fall","zh":"目击低风险跌倒后的轻微瘀伤"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"range-of-motion exercises to reduce stiffness","zh":"进行关节活动度练习以减少僵硬"},{"id":"o1","en":"spinal and limb precautions with the resident still","zh":"脊柱和肢体防护，保持住民不动"},{"id":"o2","en":"ambulation with two staff to assess gait","zh":"由两名工作人员协助行走以评估步态"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The combination of neurologic changes and possible hip fracture requires provider notification and continued immobilization until evaluated. The resident should not be ambulated to test weight bearing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"神经状态变化合并可能髋部骨折需要通知医护人员，并在评估前继续保持制动。不能让住民走路来测试负重能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When multiple post-fall problems exist, neurologic deterioration and possible fracture both increase urgency.","testTakingStrategyZh":"跌倒后存在多个问题时，神经恶化和可能骨折都会增加紧急性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1538,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"After the provider has been notified and transfer is being arranged, place the nurse's ongoing monitoring actions in order.","fullStemZh":"已通知医护人员并正在安排转送后，请按顺序排列护士的持续监测行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"After the provider has been notified and transfer is being arranged, place the nurse's ongoing monitoring actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"已通知医护人员并正在安排转送后，请按顺序排列护士的持续监测行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Prepare a transfer handoff with baseline status, new findings, medications, and vital signs","zh":"准备转送交接，包含基线状态、新发现、用药和生命体征"},{"id":"D","en":"Complete the internal occurrence report according to facility procedure","zh":"按机构流程完成内部事件报告"},{"id":"B","en":"Repeat focused neurologic, pain, distal pulse, movement, and sensation checks","zh":"重复重点神经、疼痛、远端脉搏、活动和感觉检查"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain fall precautions and keep the resident still with comfort measures","zh":"维持跌倒预防措施，让住民保持不动并给予舒适护理"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first maintains safety and immobilization, then repeats focused neurologic and pain/vascular checks, prepares concise transfer handoff information, and completes the occurrence report after clinical care and handoff needs are addressed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先维持安全和制动，然后重复重点神经评估及疼痛/血管检查，准备简明转送交接信息，最后在临床护理和交接需求处理后完成事件报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In post-event workflows, protect the client, reassess for change, hand off actionable clinical data, then finish safety reporting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"事件后流程中，先保护患者，再复评变化，交接可行动的临床资料，最后完成安全报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1539,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_post_fall_ltc_02_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.242.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,90],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,29],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3 includes an interdisciplinary fall-risk review. Classify each prevention strategy.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段包含跨专业跌倒风险评估。请将每项预防策略分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each prevention strategy.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每项预防策略分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 3 includes an interdisciplinary fall-risk review.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 3 阶段包含跨专业跌倒风险评估。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Request medication review for newly added nighttime sedative","zh":"请求复核新加的夜间镇静药"},{"id":"r2","en":"Offer toileting before usual rest periods","zh":"在平时休息前协助如厕"},{"id":"r3","en":"Place non-skid footwear within reach before transfers","zh":"转移前将防滑鞋袜放在可及处"},{"id":"r4","en":"Apply a vest restraint whenever the resident is in the chair","zh":"住民坐椅时都使用背心约束"},{"id":"r5","en":"Keep call light and walker on the resident's stronger side","zh":"将呼叫铃和助行器放在住民较强侧"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate fall-prevention action","zh":"恰当的跌倒预防措施"},{"id":"c2","en":"Avoid as routine fall prevention","zh":"避免作为常规跌倒预防"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Medication review, scheduled toileting, footwear, adequate lighting, and assistive-device access address modifiable fall risks. Restraints are not a routine fall-prevention strategy and may increase harm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用药复核、定时如厕、合适鞋袜、充足照明和辅助器具可及性可处理可改变的跌倒风险。约束不是常规跌倒预防策略，并可能增加伤害。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Favor least-restrictive interventions that address why the resident tries to get up or loses balance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先选择最少限制且能解决住民为何起身或失衡的干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1540,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_gap_2026_06_12_nonmcq_balanced_case_pressure_injury_nutrition_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.243","itemType":"case_study","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.243.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.243.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,43],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: immobility and poor nutrition A hospitalized client with limited mobility has poor oral intake and new sacral redness.","fullStemZh":"展开病例：不能移动与营养不良 一名住院患者活动受限，口服摄入差，并出现新的骶尾部发红。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: immobility and poor nutrition A hospitalized client with limited mobility has poor oral intake and new sacral redness.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开病例：不能移动与营养不良 一名住院患者活动受限，口服摄入差，并出现新的骶尾部发红。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes pressure injury prevention by recognizing immobility, moisture, nutrition deficits, and early skin changes, then implementing offloading, moisture management, repositioning, and nutrition support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例强调通过识别不能移动、潮湿、营养缺乏和早期皮肤变化，并实施减压、湿度管理、变换体位和营养支持来预防压疮。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When skin risk is multifactorial, the best plan usually combines pressure relief, moisture control, mobility support, and nutrition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"皮肤风险由多因素造成时，最佳计划通常结合减压、控湿、活动支持和营养。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
