akingStrategyEn":"Judge each row independently; a cue can be true in another route but still not support the route shown here.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逐行独立判断；某个线索可能适用于另一种途径，但不一定支持本图显示的途径。","sourceMetadata":"Parenteral route angle/depth reference.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1621,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_injection_smoke_2026_06_15_matrix_route_match_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.277","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.277.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.277.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[45,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,36],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the injection-site visual. Classify whether each statement accurately describes the technique shown.","fullStemZh":"护士查看注射部位图。对每项描述进行分类：它是否准确描述了图中显示的技术？","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify whether each statement accurately describes the technique shown.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每项描述进行分类：它是否准确描述了图中显示的技术？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the injection-site visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看注射部位图。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The medication is placed in the dermis","zh":"药液进入真皮层"},{"id":"r2","en":"The medication is placed in the subcutaneous tissue","zh":"药液进入皮下组织"},{"id":"r3","en":"The needle enters at a 10 to 15 degree angle","zh":"针头以 10 至 15 度角进入"},{"id":"r4","en":"The needle enters at a 45 to 90 degree angle","zh":"针头以 45 至 90 度角进入"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inaccurate","zh":"不准确"},{"id":"c1","en":"Accurate","zh":"准确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The visual shows an intradermal injection, which targets the dermis at a shallow 10 to 15 degree angle.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图示为皮内注射，其目标为真皮层，进针角度较浅（10至15度）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"First identify the route from the image, then evaluate each statement against that route.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先根据图像识别给药途径，然后评估每项描述是否符合该途径。","sourceMetadata":"Parenteral route angle/depth reference.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the injection-site visual.","controlSentenceZh":"护士查看注射部位图。"}
{"queueIndex":1622,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.278","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.278.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,290],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,94],"fullStemEn":"Late postpartum preeclampsia with severe features presenting after discharge A 29-year-old primipara calls on postpartum day 4 with a severe headache, visual spots, new facial edema, and repeated home BP of 162/108 after an uncomplicated term vaginal birth and normotensive prenatal course.","fullStemZh":"出院后出现的迟发性产后子痫前期伴重度特征 一名 29 岁初产妇在产后第 4 天来电，主诉严重头痛、眼前有斑点、新出现面部水肿，家庭血压反复为 162/108。她此前足月顺产且孕期血压正常。","terminalSentenceEn":"Late postpartum preeclampsia with severe features presenting after discharge A 29-year-old primipara calls on postpartum day 4 with a severe headache, visual spots, new facial edema, and repeated home BP of 162/108 after an uncomplicated term vaginal birth and normotensive prenatal course.","terminalSentenceZh":"她此前足月顺产且孕期血压正常。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":"出院后出现的迟发性产后子痫前期伴重度特征 一名 29 岁初产妇在产后第 4 天来电，主诉严重头痛、眼前有斑点、新出现面部水肿，家庭血压反复为 162/108。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires recognizing late postpartum preeclampsia with severe features despite a normotensive pregnancy and recent discharge. The urgent cues are severe headache unrelieved by analgesic, scotomata, new facial edema, repeated severe-range BP, and later hyperreflexia with clonus. Management is not delayed for labs: magnesium sulfate is used for seizure prophylaxis, immediate-release nifedipine is used for acute BP reduction, seizure precautions and close BP monitoring occur concurrently, and response is evaluated by BP trend, CNS symptom improvement, reflex/clonus status, respirations/mentation, and urine output rather than rapid resolution of edema.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求即使患者孕期血压正常且刚出院，也要识别迟发性产后子痫前期伴重度特征。紧急线索包括止痛药不能缓解的严重头痛、暗点、新出现面部水肿、反复重度范围 BP，以及随后出现的反射亢进伴阵挛。处理不能等待实验室结果：硫酸镁用于癫痫预防，速释硝苯地平用于急性降压，癫痫预防措施和密切 BP 监测应并行进行；疗效评估看 BP 趋势、中枢神经症状改善、反射/阵挛状态、呼吸/意识和尿量，而不是期待水肿快速消退。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For postpartum emergencies, compare reported symptoms against severe-feature clusters, then match each intervention to the risk it prevents: seizure, stroke, injury, or medication toxicity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理产后急症题时，先把报告的症状与重度特征组合比较，再把每项干预对应到它预防的风险：癫痫发作、中风、受伤或药物中毒。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1623,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,42],"fullStemEn":"During the postpartum triage call, highlight the findings that form the urgent preeclampsia-with-severe-features cluster requiring immediate emergency evaluation.","fullStemZh":"在产后分诊电话中，请高亮显示构成子痫前期伴重度特征、需要立即急诊评估的紧急发现组合。","terminalSentenceEn":"During the postpartum triage call, highlight the findings that form the urgent preeclampsia-with-severe-features cluster requiring immediate emergency evaluation.","terminalSentenceZh":"在产后分诊电话中，请高亮显示构成子痫前期伴重度特征、需要立即急诊评估的紧急发现组合。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Severe frontal headache rated 8/10 unrelieved by ibuprofen.","zh":"严重额部头痛，8/10，服用布洛芬后未缓解。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Intermittent scotomata described as seeing spots.","zh":"间歇性暗点，描述为“看到斑点”。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"New facial and periorbital edema that is markedly different from yesterday.","zh":"新出现的面部和眼周水肿，与前一天明显不同。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Home BP is 162/108 on two readings five minutes apart.","zh":"家庭血压两次测量均为 162/108，两次间隔 5 分钟。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Lochia has transitioned to light serosa.","zh":"恶露已转为少量浆液性恶露。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Voiding without difficulty with estimated adequate urine output.","zh":"排尿无困难，估计尿量充足。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Denies chest pain and shortness of breath.","zh":"否认胸痛和气短。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Reports poor sleep related to newborn care.","zh":"因照顾新生儿而睡眠不足。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The severe headache unrelieved by analgesic, visual scotomata, new facial/periorbital edema, and repeated BP of 162/108 on postpartum day 4 are an urgent severe-feature cluster. Expected lochia, adequate voiding, no chest pain, and poor sleep do not make the cluster less urgent.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未被止痛药缓解的严重头痛、视觉暗点、新出现的面部/眼周水肿，以及产后第 4 天反复测得 BP 162/108，构成重度特征的紧急组合。恶露符合预期、排尿充足、无胸痛和睡眠不足，不能降低这一组合的紧急性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In postpartum questions, do not normalize a headache when it is severe, unrelieved, paired with visual changes, or paired with severe-range BP.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到产后题目时，只要头痛严重、不能缓解、伴视觉改变或伴重度范围血压，就不要把它当作正常产后不适。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1624,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"At ED arrival, classify each cue according to how it should affect the nurse's interpretation before lab results are available.","fullStemZh":"患者到达急诊时，在实验室结果尚未返回前，请判断每项线索对护士解释病情的意义。","terminalSentenceEn":"At ED arrival, classify each cue according to how it should affect the nurse's interpretation before lab results are available.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者到达急诊时，在实验室结果尚未返回前，请判断每项线索对护士解释病情的意义。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"BP 168/112, repeated as 164/110 five minutes later","zh":"BP 168/112，5 分钟后复测为 164/110"},{"id":"r2","en":"Headache 9/10 with intermittent visual spots","zh":"头痛 9/10，伴间歇性视觉斑点"},{"id":"r3","en":"DTRs 3+ with two beats of ankle clonus","zh":"深腱反射 3+，踝阵挛 2 次"},{"id":"r4","en":"Urine dipstick 3+ protein","zh":"尿试纸蛋白 3+"},{"id":"r5","en":"HELLP laboratory panel is still pending","zh":"HELLP 相关实验室检查仍未返回"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Should not delay treatment","zh":"不应延误治疗"},{"id":"c1","en":"Severe feature or immediate-treatment cue","zh":"重度特征或需立即处理的线索"},{"id":"c2","en":"Supportive but not required for immediate treatment","zh":"有支持意义但不是立即处理的必要条件"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The repeated severe-range BP, CNS symptoms, and hyperreflexia with clonus are enough to classify the presentation as preeclampsia with severe features and begin urgent treatment. Proteinuria supports the diagnosis, but severe BP and CNS findings drive immediate action. Pending labs are drawn concurrently and should not delay treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反复重度范围 BP、中枢神经症状以及伴阵挛的反射亢进，足以将此表现判断为子痫前期伴重度特征并启动紧急治疗。蛋白尿支持诊断，但立即行动由重度 BP 和中枢神经发现驱动。实验室检查应同时进行，不能因此延误治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a severe BP threshold and neurologic symptoms are present, act on the instability first; confirmatory labs should not become a prerequisite for safety treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当出现重度血压阈值和神经系统症状时，先处理不稳定状态；确认性实验室检查不应成为安全治疗的前提。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1625,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,97],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Use the Stage 2 assessment and laboratory results to complete the diagnostic reasoning statement.","fullStemZh":"根据第 2 阶段评估和实验室结果，完成诊断推理陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the Stage 2 assessment and laboratory results to complete the diagnostic reasoning statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第 2 阶段评估和实验室结果，完成诊断推理陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The priority working diagnosis is {{dx}}. HELLP syndrome is less likely because {{hellp_evidence}}, and postpartum hypertension without severe features is less likely because {{severity_evidence}}.","zh":"优先工作诊断是 {{dx}}。HELLP 综合征可能性较低，因为 {{hellp_evidence}}；产后高血压不伴重度特征可能性较低，因为 {{severity_evidence}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"dx","options":[{"id":"dx_htn","en":"postpartum hypertension without severe features","zh":"产后高血压不伴重度特征"},{"id":"dx_hellp","en":"HELLP syndrome","zh":"HELLP 综合征"},{"id":"dx_pre","en":"postpartum preeclampsia with severe features","zh":"产后子痫前期伴重度特征"}],"correct":"dx_pre"},{"id":"hellp_evidence","options":[{"id":"hellp_protein","en":"urine protein-to-creatinine ratio is 0.42","zh":"尿蛋白/肌酐比值为 0.42"},{"id":"hellp_normal","en":"platelets, AST/ALT, and LDH are not showing the HELLP triad","zh":"血小板、AST/ALT 和 LDH 未显示 HELLP 三联征"},{"id":"hellp_uric","en":"uric acid is elevated","zh":"尿酸升高"}],"correct":"hellp_normal"},{"id":"severity_evidence","options":[{"id":"sev_no_ruq","en":"the patient denies right upper quadrant pain","zh":"患者否认右上腹痛"},{"id":"sev_bp_cns","en":"severe-range BP is paired with headache, scotomata, hyperreflexia, and clonus","zh":"重度范围 BP 伴头痛、暗点、反射亢进和阵挛"},{"id":"sev_norm_preg","en":"the prenatal course was normotensive","zh":"孕期血压一直正常"}],"correct":"sev_bp_cns"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stage 2 supports postpartum preeclampsia with severe features: severe-range BP, CNS symptoms, hyperreflexia with clonus, and proteinuria are present. HELLP is not supported because platelets, transaminases, and LDH are not showing the defining pattern. Hypertension without severe features is excluded by the severe BP and neurologic findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第 2 阶段支持产后子痫前期伴重度特征：存在重度范围 BP、中枢神经症状、反射亢进伴阵挛以及蛋白尿。血小板、转氨酶和 LDH 未显示 HELLP 的特征模式，因此不支持 HELLP。重度 BP 和神经系统发现排除了“不伴重度特征”的高血压分类。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use abnormal defining criteria, not tempting associated findings, to separate competing diagnoses.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分竞争诊断时，要抓定义性异常标准，而不是被诱人的相关发现带偏。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1626,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,28],"fullStemEn":"The patient asks, 'Will the magnesium bring my blood pressure down?' Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"患者问：“镁剂会把我的血压降下来吗？”护士哪项回答最佳？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士哪项回答最佳？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The patient asks, 'Will the magnesium bring my blood pressure down?'","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者问：“镁剂会把我的血压降下来吗？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Magnesium sulfate helps prevent seizures; the immediate-release nifedipine is the medication ordered to lower the blood pressure quickly.","zh":"硫酸镁用于帮助预防癫痫发作；医嘱中的速释硝苯地平才是用于快速降低血压的药物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Because you are breastfeeding, both magnesium sulfate and nifedipine should be withheld until lactation consults.","zh":"因为你正在哺乳，应先停用硫酸镁和硝苯地平，等哺乳顾问评估后再说。"},{"id":"C","en":"The extended-release nifedipine capsule would work just as well for this acute severe BP reading.","zh":"缓释硝苯地平胶囊对这次急性重度血压读数同样有效。"},{"id":"B","en":"Magnesium sulfate is the main antihypertensive, so nifedipine can wait until the loading dose is complete.","zh":"硫酸镁是主要降压药，所以硝苯地平可以等负荷剂量结束后再给。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Magnesium sulfate is used for seizure prophylaxis in preeclampsia with severe features; it is not the acute antihypertensive. Immediate-release nifedipine is ordered for rapid BP reduction, while extended-release nifedipine is for maintenance control later.","rationaleCorrectZh":"硫酸镁用于子痫前期伴重度特征的癫痫发作预防；它不是急性降压药。速释硝苯地平的医嘱目的是快速降低 BP，而缓释硝苯地平用于后续维持控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match each medication to its purpose before deciding whether it can be delayed or substituted.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断药物能否延迟或替代前，先把每种药物与其治疗目的对应起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1627,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[139,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,58],"fullStemEn":"At 11:40 AM, the nurse is initiating treatment for confirmed severe-range BP and seizure risk. Which actions should the nurse include now? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"11:40 AM，护士正在为已确认的重度范围 BP 和癫痫发作风险启动治疗。护士现在应包括哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse include now?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士现在应包括哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Implement seizure precautions, including padded side rails, suction at bedside, dim lighting, and minimized stimulation.","zh":"实施癫痫预防措施，包括床栏加垫、床旁备吸引、调暗灯光并减少刺激。"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor BP every 5 minutes for the first 20 minutes, then as ordered.","zh":"前 20 分钟每 5 分钟监测 BP，之后按医嘱监测。"},{"id":"F","en":"Run the magnesium by gravity tubing to save time if the pump is not immediately nearby.","zh":"如果输液泵不在旁边，为节省时间用重力输液管滴注硫酸镁。"},{"id":"A","en":"Start the magnesium sulfate loading dose by infusion pump as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱用输液泵开始硫酸镁负荷剂量。"},{"id":"E","en":"Wait until the magnesium loading dose is complete before giving nifedipine.","zh":"等硫酸镁负荷剂量完成后再给予硝苯地平。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the immediate-release nifedipine 10 mg PO as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱给予速释硝苯地平 10 mg PO。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"These are concurrent priorities: start magnesium safely by pump for seizure prophylaxis, give immediate-release nifedipine for acute BP reduction, create a low-stimulation seizure-safe environment, and perform close serial BP monitoring. The nurse should not force a sequence that delays either medication or safety precautions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这些是同时进行的优先措施：用输液泵安全启动硫酸镁以预防癫痫，给予速释硝苯地平进行急性降压，建立低刺激且防癫痫的环境，并密切连续监测 BP。护士不应人为设置顺序而延误任一药物或安全措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When interventions protect against different immediate risks, decide whether they are concurrent rather than forcing an ordered-response mindset.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多项干预分别针对不同的即时风险时，要判断它们是否应并行，而不是强行套用排序思维。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1628,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.278.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,53],"fullStemEn":"At 1:30 PM, classify each reassessment finding as evidence of improvement/absence of toxicity, a finding requiring continued vigilance, or a finding that is not an acute treatment-response marker.","fullStemZh":"1:30 PM，请将每项复评发现归类为改善/无中毒证据、需要继续警惕的发现，或不是急性治疗反应指标的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"At 1:30 PM, classify each reassessment finding as evidence of improvement/absence of toxicity, a finding requiring continued vigilance, or a finding that is not an acute treatment-response marker.","terminalSentenceZh":"1:30 PM，请将每项复评发现归类为改善/无中毒证据、需要继续警惕的发现，或不是急性治疗反应指标的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"BP has decreased to 138/88","zh":"BP 已降至 138/88"},{"id":"r2","en":"Visual spots have resolved and headache is now 4/10","zh":"视觉斑点已消失，头痛现为 4/10"},{"id":"r3","en":"DTRs are 2+ with no clonus","zh":"深腱反射 2+，无阵挛"},{"id":"r4","en":"Respiratory rate is 16/min and the patient is alert","zh":"呼吸频率 16 次/分，患者清醒"},{"id":"r5","en":"Urine output is 45 mL in the second hour","zh":"第二小时尿量为 45 mL"},{"id":"r6","en":"Facial edema is unchanged","zh":"面部水肿无变化"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Not an acute response marker","zh":"不是急性反应指标"},{"id":"c2","en":"Continue close monitoring","zh":"继续密切监测"},{"id":"c1","en":"Improvement or no magnesium toxicity","zh":"改善或无镁中毒证据"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"BP below the severe range, improved headache/visual symptoms, normalized reflexes without clonus, and stable respirations/mentation indicate treatment response and no current magnesium toxicity. Urine output of 45 mL/hr is above the usual minimum for magnesium clearance but still requires close hourly monitoring. Facial edema often resolves over days and is not the acute marker of response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"BP 低于重度范围、头痛/视觉症状改善、反射恢复且无阵挛、呼吸和意识稳定，提示治疗有效且目前无镁中毒。45 mL/小时的尿量高于通常用于镁清除的最低值，但仍需每小时密切监测。面部水肿常需数天缓解，不是急性治疗反应指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes using the parameter tied to the immediate goal: BP and neurologic signs for preeclampsia response, respirations/reflexes/urine output for magnesium safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果时，要使用与即时目标相关的指标：用 BP 和神经系统体征判断子痫前期反应，用呼吸、反射和尿量判断硫酸镁安全性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1629,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_16_case_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.279","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.279.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.279.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[321,407],"terminalOffsetsZh":[159,185],"fullStemEn":"Postpartum day 4: A previously normotensive primipara presents after discharge with BP 168/112 and 164/110, severe headache, scotomata, new facial edema, DTRs 3+ with ankle clonus, and urine protein-to-creatinine ratio 0.42. Labs show platelets 195 ×10³/µL, AST 34 U/L, ALT 28 U/L, LDH 198 U/L, and creatinine 0.9 mg/dL. Select the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"产后第 4 天：一名此前血压正常的初产妇出院后来院，BP 168/112 和 164/110，严重头痛、暗点、新发面部水肿，深腱反射 3+ 并有踝阵挛，尿蛋白/肌酐比值 0.42。实验室结果：血小板 195 ×10³/µL，AST 34 U/L，ALT 28 U/L，LDH 198 U/L，肌酐 0.9 mg/dL。请选择最可能的病情、两项优先措施和两项需监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的病情、两项优先措施和两项需监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Labs show platelets 195 ×10³/µL, AST 34 U/L, ALT 28 U/L, LDH 198 U/L, and creatinine 0.9 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"实验室结果：血小板 195 ×10³/µL，AST 34 U/L，ALT 28 U/L，LDH 198 U/L，肌酐 0.9 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe","en":"Postpartum preeclampsia with severe features","zh":"产后子痫前期伴重度特征"},{"id":"cond_hellp","en":"HELLP syndrome","zh":"HELLP 综合征"},{"id":"cond_postpartum_htn_no_severe","en":"Postpartum hypertension without severe features","zh":"产后高血压不伴重度特征"}],"correct":"cond_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_hold_antihypertensive","en":"Withhold nifedipine because magnesium is already infusing","zh":"因硫酸镁已经在输注而暂缓硝苯地平"},{"id":"act_mag_load","en":"Administer magnesium sulfate 4 g IV loading dose by pump as ordered","zh":"按医嘱用输液泵给予硫酸镁 4 g IV 负荷剂量"},{"id":"act_ir_nifedipine","en":"Administer immediate-release nifedipine 10 mg PO as ordered","zh":"按医嘱给予速释硝苯地平 10 mg PO"},{"id":"act_er_nifedipine","en":"Substitute extended-release nifedipine for the acute dose","zh":"用缓释硝苯地平替代急性处理剂量"}],"correct":["act_mag_load","act_ir_nifedipine"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_mag_safety","en":"Magnesium safety and seizure-risk markers: RR, LOC, DTR/clonus, urine output, headache/visual symptoms","zh":"硫酸镁安全和癫痫风险指标：RR、LOC、DTR/阵挛、尿量、头痛/视觉症状"},{"id":"param_lochia","en":"Lochia color and amount as the main marker of preeclampsia response","zh":"把恶露颜色和量作为子痫前期反应的主要指标"},{"id":"param_bp_trend","en":"BP trend after acute antihypertensive therapy","zh":"急性降压治疗后的 BP 趋势"},{"id":"param_facial_edema","en":"Facial edema as the marker of acute treatment response","zh":"把面部水肿作为急性治疗反应指标"}],"correct":["param_bp_trend","param_mag_safety"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is postpartum preeclampsia with severe features because severe-range BP is paired with CNS symptoms, clonus, edema, and proteinuria after delivery. The two immediate actions address different life-threatening risks: magnesium sulfate for seizure prophylaxis and immediate-release nifedipine for acute BP reduction. Monitoring must track BP response and magnesium/seizure safety markers.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该病情为产后子痫前期伴重度特征，因为分娩后重度范围 BP 同时伴中枢神经症状、阵挛、水肿和蛋白尿。两项即时措施分别处理不同的危及生命风险：硫酸镁用于癫痫预防，速释硝苯地平用于急性降压。监测必须追踪 BP 反应以及硫酸镁/癫痫安全指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In a bowtie item, first anchor the condition with defining cues, then choose actions that treat different immediate threats, and monitor parameters tied to those threats.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bowtie 题时，先用定义性线索锁定病情，再选择分别处理不同即时威胁的措施，并监测与这些威胁直接相关的参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1630,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.280","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.280.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[342,406],"terminalOffsetsZh":[112,136],"fullStemEn":"Acute hemolytic transfusion reaction following ABO-incompatible red blood cell transfusion A 58-year-old woman with CKD stage 3b, hypertension, and type 2 diabetes is admitted for symptomatic anemia. Her true blood type is A-positive, but a mislabeled pretransfusion specimen leads to issue of an ABO-incompatible packed red blood cell unit. The transfusion begins at 1420 through a 20-gauge peripheral IV.","fullStemZh":"ABO 不相容红细胞输注后的急性溶血性输血反应 一名 58 岁女性，有 3b 期慢性肾病、高血压和 2 型糖尿病，因症状性贫血入院。患者真实血型为 A 阳性，但输血前标本采集时贴错标签，导致发出 ABO 不相容的浓缩红细胞。输血于 1420 经 20G 外周 IV 开始。","terminalSentenceEn":"The transfusion begins at 1420 through a 20-gauge peripheral IV.","terminalSentenceZh":"输血于 1420 经 20G 外周 IV 开始。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her true blood type is A-positive, but a mislabeled pretransfusion specimen leads to issue of an ABO-incompatible packed red blood cell unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者真实血型为 A 阳性，但输血前标本采集时贴错标签，导致发出 ABO 不相容的浓缩红细胞。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This unfolding case teaches recognition and management of acute hemolytic transfusion reaction from ABO-incompatible red cells. The Stage 1 cue cluster—rapid fever/rigors, flank pain, hypotension, tachycardia, sense of impending doom, and hemoglobinuria—requires immediate transfusion cessation, safe maintenance of IV access with 0.9% normal saline through new tubing per protocol, notification of the provider and blood bank, and preservation of the unit/tubing/labels. Later stages show progression to shock, oliguric acute kidney injury, hyperkalemia, and DIC; outcomes must be evaluated by perfusion, urine output, potassium/creatinine, coagulation studies, and vasopressor needs rather than temperature alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例训练识别和处理 ABO 不相容红细胞导致的急性溶血性输血反应。第1阶段的线索组合——快速发热寒战、腰痛、低血压、心动过速、濒危感和血红蛋白尿——要求立即停止输血，按流程用新管路和 0.9% 生理盐水安全维持 IV 通路，通知医护提供者和血库，并保留血袋/管路/标签。后续阶段进展为休克、少尿性急性肾损伤、高钾血症和 DIC；评价结果应看灌注、尿量、钾/肌酐、凝血指标和升压药需求，而不是单看体温。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In transfusion questions, connect timing, symptom cluster, and first nursing action. Severe systemic findings mean stop the transfusion and escalate; do not slow the rate or treat only fever.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输血题要把发生时间、症状组合和首要护理措施联系起来。严重全身表现意味着停止输血并升级处理；不要只是减慢速率或只退热。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1631,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Using the Stage 1 update, highlight the findings that are significant cues requiring immediate nursing action.","fullStemZh":"根据第1阶段更新，标出需要护士立即处理的重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Stage 1 update, highlight the findings that are significant cues requiring immediate nursing action.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第1阶段更新，标出需要护士立即处理的重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Sudden deep bilateral flank and low back pain during the transfusion.","zh":"输血过程中突然出现双侧腰背部深部疼痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The client states, \"something is wrong — I feel like something terrible is about to happen.\"","zh":"患者说：“不对劲——我觉得要出大事了。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Visible rigors with temperature rising from 98.2 °F (36.8 °C) to 101.5 °F (38.6 °C).","zh":"明显寒战，体温从 98.2 °F (36.8 °C) 升至 101.5 °F (38.6 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Heart rate increases from 92/min to 118/min.","zh":"心率从 92 次/分升至 118 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Blood pressure decreases from 108/68 mmHg to 96/58 mmHg.","zh":"血压从 108/68 mmHg 降至 96/58 mmHg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The most recent urine appears dark reddish-brown.","zh":"最近一次尿液呈深红褐色。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The peripheral IV site has no redness, swelling, or streaking.","zh":"外周 IV 部位无发红、肿胀或条索状红线。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5","s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The cue cluster is abrupt flank/back pain, a sense of impending doom, fever with rigors, tachycardia, falling blood pressure, and dark reddish-brown urine within minutes of starting blood. This pattern requires the nurse to treat the event as an acute transfusion reaction and stop the transfusion immediately. The normal IV site is useful because it makes infiltration or phlebitis less likely, but it is not itself a danger cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键线索组合是在输血开始后数分钟内突然出现腰背痛、濒危感、发热寒战、心动过速、血压下降和深红褐色尿液。护士应按急性输血反应处理，立即停止输血。IV 部位正常有助于排除渗漏或静脉炎，但它本身不是危险线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"During a transfusion, sudden systemic changes are more important than a normal IV site. Link timing plus cue cluster before deciding the priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输血过程中，突然出现的全身变化比 IV 部位正常更重要。先把发生时间和线索组合联系起来，再判断优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1632,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,54],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which transfusion reaction is most consistent with fever and rigors, bilateral flank pain, hypotension, a sense of impending doom, and dark reddish-brown urine 12 minutes after the transfusion begins?","fullStemZh":"第1阶段，输血开始 12 分钟后出现发热寒战、双侧腰痛、低血压、濒危感和深红褐色尿液，最符合哪一种输血反应？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which transfusion reaction is most consistent with fever and rigors, bilateral flank pain, hypotension, a sense of impending doom, and dark reddish-brown urine 12 minutes after the transfusion begins?","terminalSentenceZh":"第1阶段，输血开始 12 分钟后出现发热寒战、双侧腰痛、低血压、濒危感和深红褐色尿液，最符合哪一种输血反应？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Febrile non-hemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"非溶血性发热性输血反应"},{"id":"C","en":"Mild allergic transfusion reaction","zh":"轻度过敏性输血反应"},{"id":"E","en":"Delayed hemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"迟发性溶血性输血反应"},{"id":"D","en":"Transfusion-associated circulatory overload","zh":"输血相关循环超负荷"},{"id":"A","en":"Acute hemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"急性溶血性输血反应"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most consistent diagnosis is an acute hemolytic transfusion reaction. The decisive features are very rapid onset during transfusion, flank/back pain, hypotension, hemoglobinuria, fever with rigors, and a sense of impending doom. These findings fit acute intravascular hemolysis from incompatible red cells.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最符合的是急性溶血性输血反应。关键特征是输血过程中快速发作、腰背痛、低血压、血红蛋白尿、发热寒战和濒危感。这些符合不相容红细胞导致的急性血管内溶血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not stop at the word fever. Hemoglobinuria and flank pain shift the diagnosis from a simple febrile reaction to hemolysis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只看到“发热”。血红蛋白尿和腰痛会把判断从单纯发热反应转向溶血反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1633,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which problem is the most immediately life-threatening and should drive the nurse's priority response?","fullStemZh":"第1阶段，哪一个问题最直接危及生命，应该决定护士的优先处理？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which problem is the most immediately life-threatening and should drive the nurse's priority response?","terminalSentenceZh":"第1阶段，哪一个问题最直接危及生命，应该决定护士的优先处理？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The dark reddish-brown urine","zh":"深红褐色尿液"},{"id":"E","en":"The normal-appearing IV site","zh":"IV 部位外观正常"},{"id":"A","en":"The fever and rigors","zh":"发热和寒战"},{"id":"D","en":"The client's nausea","zh":"患者恶心"},{"id":"C","en":"The acute hypotension with tachycardia","zh":"急性低血压伴心动过速"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate threat is cardiovascular collapse: the blood pressure is falling while the heart rate is rising. Fever and hemoglobinuria are important, but inadequate perfusion can become fatal within minutes and must drive the response to stop the antigen exposure and support circulation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最直接的威胁是循环崩溃：血压下降同时心率升高。发热和血红蛋白尿很重要，但灌注不足可在数分钟内危及生命，因此处理重点是停止继续接触抗原并支持循环。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several abnormal findings are present, ask which one can kill the client first. Shock physiology outranks fever control.","testTakingStrategyZh":"多个异常同时存在时，先问哪一个会最快危及生命。休克生理优先于退热处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1634,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,26],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which actions should the nurse take immediately? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第1阶段，护士应立即采取哪些措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which actions should the nurse take immediately?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第1阶段，护士应立即采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Remove the peripheral IV catheter because the line has been exposed to incompatible blood.","zh":"因为该管路接触过不相容血液，所以拔除外周 IV 导管。"},{"id":"B","en":"Disconnect the blood tubing and keep the IV open with 0.9% normal saline through new tubing per protocol.","zh":"断开输血管路，并按流程用新的管路接 0.9% 生理盐水维持 IV 通路。"},{"id":"A","en":"Clamp the blood tubing and stop the transfusion.","zh":"夹闭输血管路并停止输血。"},{"id":"E","en":"Save the blood unit with attached tubing and labels for the blood bank investigation.","zh":"保留血袋、连接管路和标签，供血库调查。"},{"id":"C","en":"Flush the blood remaining in the original tubing before switching to saline.","zh":"在换接生理盐水前，先把原管路中剩余的血液冲入体内。"},{"id":"D","en":"Stay with the client and have another staff member notify the provider and blood bank.","zh":"留在患者身边，并请另一名工作人员通知医护提供者和血库。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should stop the transfusion, maintain venous access with 0.9% normal saline using new tubing according to protocol, notify the provider and blood bank while staying with the client, and preserve the unit/tubing/labels. The nurse should not flush the original tubing because that would infuse more incompatible blood, and should not remove the IV because the client is hypotensive and needs access.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应停止输血，按流程使用新管路和 0.9% 生理盐水维持静脉通路，留在患者身边并通知医护提供者和血库，同时保留血袋、管路和标签。不能冲洗原输血管路，因为会把更多不相容血液输入体内；也不应拔除 IV，因为患者低血压，需要静脉通路。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a suspected severe transfusion reaction, do four things together: stop blood, keep access safely, call for help, and preserve evidence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"疑似严重输血反应时同时抓住四点：停血、以安全方式保留通路、呼叫支援、保留证据。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1635,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,240],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,75],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the client remains hypotensive despite initial saline, has worsening oliguria with port-wine urine, oozing from puncture sites, petechiae, and labs consistent with hemolysis and evolving DIC. What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"第2阶段，患者经初始生理盐水处理后仍低血压，少尿加重且尿呈葡萄酒色，穿刺部位渗血、出现瘀点，实验室结果符合溶血和进展性 DIC。护士的优先措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的优先措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the client remains hypotensive despite initial saline, has worsening oliguria with port-wine urine, oozing from puncture sites, petechiae, and labs consistent with hemolysis and evolving DIC.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第2阶段，患者经初始生理盐水处理后仍低血压，少尿加重且尿呈葡萄酒色，穿刺部位渗血、出现瘀点，实验室结果符合溶血和进展性 DIC。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hold further interventions until the blood bank confirms the exact incompatibility.","zh":"等待血库确认具体不相容类型后再进行进一步干预。"},{"id":"B","en":"Escalate immediately for rapid response or ICU-level care while continuing perfusion support and strict output monitoring.","zh":"立即升级处理，启动快速反应或转入 ICU 级别护理，同时继续支持灌注并严格监测尿量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer acetaminophen and reassess the temperature in 30 minutes.","zh":"给予对乙酰氨基酚，并在 30 分钟后复测体温。"},{"id":"E","en":"Slow the saline infusion because chronic kidney disease makes fluid overload the main priority.","zh":"因患者有慢性肾病，应减慢生理盐水输注，因为容量超负荷是主要优先问题。"},{"id":"A","en":"Complete the transfusion reaction documentation before further escalation.","zh":"先完成输血反应记录表，再进一步升级处理。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is deteriorating with shock, oliguric acute kidney injury, and DIC despite the initial correct response. The nurse should escalate immediately to rapid response or ICU-level care, continue ordered perfusion support, measure urine output closely, and ensure the blood bank workup and compatible components are moving. Documentation and antipyretics must not delay escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者在初步正确处理后仍出现休克、少尿性急性肾损伤和 DIC，说明病情恶化。护士应立即启动快速反应或 ICU 级别护理，继续按医嘱支持灌注，严密测量尿量，并确保血库调查和相容血液成分准备正在进行。记录和退热不能延误升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When initial measures fail and multiple organ systems are worsening, choose escalation rather than task completion or symptom-only care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"初步处理无效且多个器官系统恶化时，应选择升级处理，而不是先完成文书或只处理单一症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1636,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.280.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,149],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding as evidence of stabilization, evidence of continued deterioration, or insufficient by itself to show stabilization.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段，请判断每项发现是提示病情稳定、继续恶化，还是单独看不足以说明病情稳定。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding as evidence of stabilization, evidence of continued deterioration, or insufficient by itself to show stabilization.","terminalSentenceZh":"第3阶段，请判断每项发现是提示病情稳定、继续恶化，还是单独看不足以说明病情稳定。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Urine output is 8 mL in the past hour with persistent hemoglobin-positive dark urine.","zh":"过去 1 小时尿量 8 mL，尿液仍深色且血红蛋白阳性。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Blood pressure is maintained while norepinephrine requirements are decreasing.","zh":"血压可维持，同时去甲肾上腺素需求量正在下降。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Fibrinogen is rising while INR and aPTT are falling toward baseline.","zh":"纤维蛋白原上升，同时 INR 和 aPTT 正向基线下降。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Potassium has increased to 5.9 mEq/L with worsening creatinine.","zh":"钾升至 5.9 mEq/L，肌酐继续恶化。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Temperature has decreased from 102.4 °F (39.1 °C) to 101.1 °F (38.4 °C).","zh":"体温从 102.4 °F (39.1 °C) 降至 101.1 °F (38.4 °C)。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Insufficient by itself","zh":"单独看不足以判断稳定"},{"id":"c1","en":"Stabilization","zh":"病情稳定"},{"id":"c2","en":"Continued deterioration","zh":"继续恶化"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stabilization would be shown by improving perfusion with lower vasopressor needs, improving urine output, and improving coagulation and electrolyte trends. At Stage 3, persistent oliguria with hemoglobinuria, rising creatinine, rising potassium, and worsening coagulation show deterioration. A modest temperature decrease alone does not prove recovery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"病情稳定应表现为灌注改善且升压药需求下降、尿量改善、凝血和电解质趋势改善。第3阶段持续少尿伴血红蛋白尿、肌酐升高、钾升高和凝血恶化提示继续恶化。体温略降本身不能证明恢复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by trends in threatened organ systems, not by one improving vital sign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果时看受威胁器官系统的趋势，不要只看一个好转的生命体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1637,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_acute_hemolytic_transfusion_reaction_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.281","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.281.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.281.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[454,567],"terminalOffsetsZh":[177,215],"fullStemEn":"A client develops fever, rigors, bilateral flank pain, hypotension, hemoglobinuria, and a sense of impending doom within 12 minutes of starting a red blood cell transfusion. Thirty minutes after the transfusion is stopped, the client has worsening hypotension, oliguria with port-wine urine, oozing from puncture sites, platelets 104 ×10³/µL, fibrinogen 140 mg/dL, INR 1.8, aPTT 52 seconds, LDH 1,840 U/L, bilirubin 4.2 mg/dL, and haptoglobin <10 mg/dL. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名患者开始输注红细胞后 12 分钟内出现发热、寒战、双侧腰痛、低血压、血红蛋白尿和濒危感。停止输血 30 分钟后，患者低血压加重，少尿且尿呈葡萄酒色，穿刺部位渗血，血小板 104 ×10³/µL，纤维蛋白原 140 mg/dL，INR 1.8，aPTT 52 秒，LDH 1,840 U/L，胆红素 4.2 mg/dL，结合珠蛋白 <10 mg/dL。请选择最可能的病情、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数来完成 bow-tie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的病情、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数来完成 bow-tie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Thirty minutes after the transfusion is stopped, the client has worsening hypotension, oliguria with port-wine urine, oozing from puncture sites, platelets 104 ×10³/µL, fibrinogen 140 mg/dL, INR 1.8, aPTT 52 seconds, LDH 1,840 U/L, bilirubin 4.2 mg/dL, and haptoglobin <10 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"停止输血 30 分钟后，患者低血压加重，少尿且尿呈葡萄酒色，穿刺部位渗血，血小板 104 ×10³/µL，纤维蛋白原 140 mg/dL，INR 1.8，aPTT 52 秒，LDH 1,840 U/L，胆红素 4.2 mg/dL，结合珠蛋白 <10 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_a","en":"Acute hemolytic transfusion reaction due to ABO incompatibility","zh":"ABO 不相容导致的急性溶血性输血反应"},{"id":"cond_b","en":"Anaphylactic transfusion reaction","zh":"过敏性休克型输血反应"},{"id":"cond_c","en":"Septic transfusion reaction from bacterial contamination","zh":"血液制品细菌污染导致的脓毒性输血反应"}],"correct":"cond_a"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_d","en":"Remove the peripheral IV and plan to obtain new access later.","zh":"拔除外周 IV，并计划稍后重新建立通路。"},{"id":"act_a","en":"Ensure the blood bank receives the stopped unit with attached tubing and a post-reaction patient sample.","zh":"确保血库收到已停止输注的血袋及连接管路，并收到输血反应后的患者血样。"},{"id":"act_c","en":"Give acetaminophen and slow the transfusion rate.","zh":"给予对乙酰氨基酚并减慢输血速率。"},{"id":"act_b","en":"Escalate immediately for higher-level care because shock, DIC, and oliguric acute kidney injury are progressing.","zh":"因休克、DIC 和少尿性急性肾损伤正在进展，立即升级至更高级别护理。"}],"correct":["act_a","act_b"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"par_c","en":"Temperature trend alone","zh":"单独看体温趋势"},{"id":"par_d","en":"Peripheral IV insertion-site appearance","zh":"外周 IV 穿刺部位外观"},{"id":"par_a","en":"Urine output and urine color via the Foley catheter","zh":"通过 Foley 导尿管监测尿量和尿液颜色"},{"id":"par_b","en":"Coagulation studies, especially fibrinogen and platelet count","zh":"凝血指标，尤其是纤维蛋白原和血小板计数"}],"correct":["par_a","par_b"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is acute hemolytic transfusion reaction due to ABO incompatibility. The priority actions are to ensure the blood bank investigation has the unit/tubing and patient sample, and to escalate to higher-level care for shock, DIC, and oliguric acute kidney injury. The best monitoring parameters are renal output/color and coagulation trends because these track the major organ-system threats.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该病情是 ABO 不相容导致的急性溶血性输血反应。优先措施是确保血库调查取得血袋/管路和患者样本，并因休克、DIC 和少尿性急性肾损伤升级至更高级别护理。最佳监测参数是尿量/尿色和凝血趋势，因为它们反映主要受威胁的器官系统。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, match the center condition first, then select actions and monitoring parameters that address that specific pathophysiology.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bow-tie 题时先锁定中心病情，再选择针对该病理生理过程的措施和监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1638,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.282","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.282.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,399],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,116],"fullStemEn":"Superior vena cava syndrome secondary to mediastinal malignancy A 58-year-old man with untreated non-small cell lung cancer and a known right mediastinal mass is admitted with two weeks of progressive facial swelling and dyspnea on exertion. The record unfolds from stable upper-body venous congestion to worsening respiratory distress with stridor, then partial response after emergency escalation.","fullStemZh":"纵隔恶性肿瘤继发上腔静脉综合征 一名58岁男性患有尚未治疗的非小细胞肺癌，并已知存在右纵隔肿块，因两周进行性面部肿胀和活动后呼吸困难入院。病历从相对稳定的上半身静脉淤血，进展到伴喘鸣的呼吸窘迫加重，随后在紧急升级处理后出现部分改善。","terminalSentenceEn":"The record unfolds from stable upper-body venous congestion to worsening respiratory distress with stridor, then partial response after emergency escalation.","terminalSentenceZh":"病历从相对稳定的上半身静脉淤血，进展到伴喘鸣的呼吸窘迫加重，随后在紧急升级处理后出现部分改善。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Superior vena cava syndrome secondary to mediastinal malignancy A 58-year-old man with untreated non-small cell lung cancer and a known right mediastinal mass is admitted with two weeks of progressive facial swelling and dyspnea on exertion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"纵隔恶性肿瘤继发上腔静脉综合征 一名58岁男性患有尚未治疗的非小细胞肺癌，并已知存在右纵隔肿块，因两周进行性面部肿胀和活动后呼吸困难入院。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests recognition and management of malignant SVC syndrome. The key cue cluster is upper-body venous congestion with facial plethora, periorbital edema, non-collapsing JVD, chest-wall venous collaterals, and position-dependent worsening in a client with a known mediastinal mass. Stage 2 becomes an airway emergency when stridor appears with worsening hypoxemia and neck edema. The nurse should optimize oxygenation, maintain upright positioning, escalate immediately, prepare airway equipment, and avoid unreliable upper-extremity IV access. Improvement is judged by airway patency, oxygen requirement in context, respiratory effort, and upper-body edema trends; a single improved saturation on much higher oxygen support is not enough to declare the client stable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查恶性肿瘤相关上腔静脉综合征的识别和处理。关键线索是已知纵隔肿块患者出现上半身静脉淤血，包括面部潮红、眶周水肿、颈静脉扩张且不塌陷、胸壁侧支静脉和体位相关加重。第2阶段出现喘鸣并伴低氧和颈部水肿加重时，情况转为气道急症。护士应改善氧合、保持坐高位、立即升级汇报、准备气道设备，并避免不可靠的上肢IV通路。评估改善应关注气道通畅、氧疗需求的背景、呼吸功和上半身水肿趋势；在更高氧疗支持下单一氧饱和度改善不足以说明患者已经稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the unfolding trend. First localize the edema anatomically, then reprioritize immediately when a new airway sign appears.","testTakingStrategyZh":"跟随病情展开趋势。先从解剖上定位水肿分布；一旦出现新的气道体征，立即重新排序优先级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1639,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,128],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the admission and Stage 1 findings that are significant cues of impaired venous return through the superior vena cava.","fullStemZh":"请标出入院和第1阶段中提示上腔静脉静脉回流受阻的重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the admission and Stage 1 findings that are significant cues of impaired venous return through the superior vena cava.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出入院和第1阶段中提示上腔静脉静脉回流受阻的重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Facial plethora","zh":"面部潮红","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Bilateral periorbital edema","zh":"双侧眶周水肿","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Bilateral external jugular veins that do not collapse with inspiration or 45-degree head elevation","zh":"双侧颈外静脉扩张，吸气或床头抬高45度后仍不塌陷","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Faint dilated superficial venous collaterals across the anterior chest wall","zh":"前胸壁可见轻度扩张的浅表侧支静脉","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Worse head fullness and desaturation when the head of bed is lowered","zh":"床头降低时头部胀满感加重并出现氧饱和度下降","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Sluggish flow through a right forearm IV","zh":"右前臂IV输液流速缓慢","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Diminished breath sounds in the right upper lobe with a known right mediastinal mass","zh":"已知右纵隔肿块且右上肺呼吸音减弱","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"No lower-extremity edema","zh":"无下肢水肿","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Hands and fingers are non-edematous at admission","zh":"入院时双手和手指无水肿","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"Normal neurological findings and no headache","zh":"神经系统检查正常且无头痛","selectable":true},{"id":"s11","en":"Temperature 98.8 °F (37.1 °C)","zh":"体温98.8 °F (37.1 °C)","selectable":true},{"id":"s12","en":"Capillary refill under 2 seconds bilaterally","zh":"双侧毛细血管再充盈时间少于2秒","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5","s6","s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The key pattern is congestion above the diaphragm: facial plethora, periorbital edema, non-collapsing jugular venous distention, chest-wall venous collaterals, position-dependent worsening, impaired upper-extremity IV flow, and findings consistent with the known mediastinal mass. Normal lower extremities and stable nonspecific findings do not rule out SVC obstruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键模式是横膈以上静脉淤血：面部潮红、眶周水肿、颈静脉扩张且不塌陷、胸壁侧支静脉、体位相关加重、上肢IV回流不畅，以及符合已知纵隔肿块的肺部发现。下肢正常和其他稳定的非特异表现不能排除上腔静脉受阻。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cue-recognition items, map each finding to anatomy. SVC obstruction should cluster in the face, neck, upper chest, and upper extremities, not the legs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做线索识别题时，把每个发现对应到解剖位置。上腔静脉受阻的表现应集中在面部、颈部、上胸部和上肢，而不是下肢。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1640,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,71],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which condition best explains the client’s cue cluster: upper-body venous congestion sparing the lower extremities, worsening when the head of bed is lowered, known right mediastinal mass, chest-wall venous collaterals, and a mildly elevated D-dimer?","fullStemZh":"在第1阶段，哪种情况最能解释患者的线索组合：上半身静脉淤血但下肢未受累、床头降低时加重、已知右纵隔肿块、胸壁侧支静脉，以及D-二聚体轻度升高？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which condition best explains the client’s cue cluster: upper-body venous congestion sparing the lower extremities, worsening when the head of bed is lowered, known right mediastinal mass, chest-wall venous collaterals, and a mildly elevated D-dimer?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第1阶段，哪种情况最能解释患者的线索组合：上半身静脉淤血但下肢未受累、床头降低时加重、已知右纵隔肿块、胸壁侧支静脉，以及D-二聚体轻度升高？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Community-acquired pneumonia causing hypoxemia","zh":"社区获得性肺炎导致低氧血症"},{"id":"C","en":"Isolated upper-extremity deep vein thrombosis","zh":"孤立性上肢深静脉血栓"},{"id":"A","en":"Superior vena cava syndrome from extrinsic compression by the mediastinal malignancy","zh":"纵隔恶性肿瘤外压导致的上腔静脉综合征"},{"id":"B","en":"Acute decompensated heart failure with volume overload","zh":"容量负荷过重导致的急性失代偿性心力衰竭"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bilateral face, neck, upper chest, and upper-extremity pattern with collateral veins localizes the problem to the SVC. The known mediastinal mass supplies the mechanism. The mildly elevated D-dimer is nonspecific in malignancy and does not outweigh the anatomic pattern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"双侧面部、颈部、上胸部和上肢受累，并伴有侧支静脉，提示问题定位在上腔静脉。已知纵隔肿块提供了机制。恶性肿瘤患者D-二聚体轻度升高并不特异，不能推翻这个解剖学模式。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not anchor on one abnormal lab. First decide whether the full cue pattern localizes to a body system or an anatomic obstruction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要被一个异常化验值锚定。先判断全部线索是否能定位到某个系统或解剖性阻塞。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1641,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which new or worsening finding is the most immediately life-threatening?","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，哪个新出现或加重的发现最具有立即生命威胁？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which new or worsening finding is the most immediately life-threatening?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第2阶段，哪个新出现或加重的发现最具有立即生命威胁？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Heart rate increased to 110/min","zh":"心率升至110次/分"},{"id":"A","en":"New faint inspiratory stridor over the trachea","zh":"气管上方新出现的轻微吸气性喘鸣"},{"id":"C","en":"Neck circumference increased from 44 cm to 47 cm","zh":"颈围从44 cm增加到47 cm"},{"id":"D","en":"SpO2 decreased to 90% on 2 L nasal cannula","zh":"使用2 L鼻导管时SpO2降至90%"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New inspiratory stridor is the priority because it indicates narrowing of the upper airway. In SVC syndrome, worsening venous congestion can cause airway edema or compression that may progress rapidly to complete obstruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新出现的吸气性喘鸣最优先，因为它提示上气道变窄。在上腔静脉综合征中，静脉淤血加重可导致气道水肿或受压，并可能迅速进展为完全性阻塞。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several findings are abnormal, apply ABCs tightly. A sign of airway narrowing outranks other respiratory or compensatory findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个发现异常时，要严格应用ABC原则。气道变窄的体征优先于其他呼吸或代偿性表现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1642,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which actions should the nurse take first as part of the emergency response? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，护士应首先采取哪些措施作为紧急反应的一部分？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which actions should the nurse take first as part of the emergency response?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第2阶段，护士应首先采取哪些措施作为紧急反应的一部分？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Lower the head of bed to facilitate a full chest assessment.","zh":"降低床头以便完成全面胸部评估。"},{"id":"B","en":"Confirm the head of bed remains at 45 degrees or higher.","zh":"确认床头保持45度或更高。"},{"id":"C","en":"Activate rapid response or the facility emergency escalation process and notify the provider of new stridor.","zh":"启动快速反应或机构紧急升级流程，并通知医护人员新出现喘鸣。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase oxygen delivery using available respiratory distress equipment or protocol.","zh":"根据可用设备或呼吸窘迫流程提高氧气输送。"},{"id":"D","en":"Bring emergency airway equipment, suction, bag-valve-mask, and oxygen escalation supplies to the bedside.","zh":"将紧急气道设备、吸引装置、简易呼吸器和升级氧疗用品准备到床旁。"},{"id":"E","en":"Attempt a new left forearm IV before calling for help.","zh":"在呼叫支援前先尝试置入新的左前臂IV。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has new stridor with worsening hypoxemia and upper-body edema, so immediate nursing priorities are oxygenation, upright positioning, emergency escalation/provider notification, and readiness for airway deterioration. Vascular access is important after the airway response is underway, but an upper-extremity attempt before calling help delays the priority response and is likely to fail.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者出现新发喘鸣，并伴低氧和上半身水肿加重，因此护士的立即优先事项是改善氧合、保持坐高位、启动紧急升级/通知医护人员，并准备应对气道恶化。建立血管通路很重要，但应在气道处理启动后进行；在呼叫支援前先尝试上肢IV会延误优先处理且可能失败。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In SATA emergency-response items, key actions that address the immediate threat and escalation. Exclude tasks that delay ABCs or worsen the physiology.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做多选紧急处理题时，选择能处理立即威胁并升级求援的措施。排除会延误ABC或加重病理生理的任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1643,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"After the infiltrated right forearm IV is discontinued and the airway response is underway, where should the nurse obtain replacement peripheral IV access?","fullStemZh":"在停止已渗出的右前臂IV且气道处理已启动后，护士应在哪里获得替代外周静脉通路？","terminalSentenceEn":"After the infiltrated right forearm IV is discontinued and the airway response is underway, where should the nurse obtain replacement peripheral IV access?","terminalSentenceZh":"在停止已渗出的右前臂IV且气道处理已启动后，护士应在哪里获得替代外周静脉通路？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Coordinate non–upper-extremity peripheral access per facility policy and provider direction.","zh":"按机构政策和医嘱协调非上肢外周静脉通路。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place a new right antecubital IV because it is closer to central circulation.","zh":"在右肘窝重新置入IV，因为它更接近中心循环。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request an upper-extremity PICC line as the fastest reliable access.","zh":"申请上肢PICC作为最快且可靠的通路。"},{"id":"B","en":"Place a peripheral IV in the left hand because the right forearm IV failed.","zh":"因右前臂IV失败，在左手置入外周IV。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Upper-extremity venous return drains through the obstructed SVC, so either arm can have high back-pressure, unreliable flow, and infiltration risk. Non–upper-extremity access, such as lower-extremity access when allowed by policy and ordered/arranged by the team, drains through the IVC and is more appropriate for this anatomy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"上肢静脉回流需要经过受阻的上腔静脉，因此任一手臂都可能出现高回压、输液不可靠和渗出风险。非上肢通路（如政策允许并由团队医嘱/协调的下肢通路）经下腔静脉回流，更符合本病例的解剖情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a vascular-access question is tied to an obstruction, trace the venous drainage route rather than choosing the opposite limb automatically.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当血管通路题与阻塞有关时，要追踪静脉回流路径，而不是自动选择对侧肢体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1644,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.282.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,76],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding when evaluating the response to treatment.","fullStemZh":"在第3阶段，评估治疗反应时请对每个发现进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding when evaluating the response to treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"在第3阶段，评估治疗反应时请对每个发现进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Stridor is no longer audible over the trachea.","zh":"气管上方不再听到喘鸣。"},{"id":"r2","en":"SpO2 is 93%, but only on high-flow nasal cannula at 40 L/min and FiO2 0.50.","zh":"SpO2为93%，但需要高流量鼻导管40 L/min、FiO2 0.50。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Neck circumference is 46 cm, down from 47 cm but still above the 44 cm baseline.","zh":"颈围为46 cm，低于47 cm但仍高于44 cm基线。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client still becomes short of breath with movement.","zh":"患者活动时仍感呼吸困难。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Urine output is 320 mL over the preceding 6 hours.","zh":"过去6小时尿量为320 mL。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_improve","en":"Supports early improvement","zh":"支持早期改善"},{"id":"c_risk","en":"Shows ongoing risk / not resolved","zh":"提示仍有风险/尚未解决"},{"id":"c_not_primary","en":"Not a primary SVC-response marker","zh":"不是主要的SVC反应指标"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c_improve"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c_risk"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c_risk"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c_risk"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c_not_primary"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The absent stridor is the strongest early improvement because it suggests less airway narrowing. However, the client still requires much higher oxygen support, has persistent neck edema above baseline, and remains dyspneic with movement, so the obstruction is not resolved. Urine output is useful for general perfusion but does not track the primary SVC threat.","rationaleCorrectZh":"喘鸣消失是最重要的早期改善信号，因为它提示气道狭窄减轻。但患者仍需要明显更高的氧疗支持，颈部水肿仍高于基线，活动时仍气短，因此阻塞尚未解决。尿量可反映总体灌注，但不是追踪SVC主要威胁的指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare oxygenation in context. A higher saturation on much more support can still mean the client remains unstable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估氧合时必须结合支持强度。若在更高支持下才有较高氧饱和度，患者仍可能不稳定。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1645,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_svc_syndrome_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.283","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.283.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.283.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[383,496],"terminalOffsetsZh":[121,154],"fullStemEn":"A 58-year-old client with untreated non-small cell lung cancer and a known right mediastinal mass has worsening facial and periorbital edema, neck circumference increased from 44 cm to 47 cm, more prominent chest-wall venous collaterals, bilateral upper-extremity pitting edema, SpO2 90% on 2 L nasal cannula, short-phrase speech, and new faint inspiratory stridor over the trachea. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名58岁患者患尚未治疗的非小细胞肺癌，并已知存在右纵隔肿块。现在面部和眶周水肿加重，颈围从44 cm增至47 cm，胸壁侧支静脉更加明显，双上肢出现凹陷性水肿，鼻导管2 L时SpO2为90%，只能短语交流，并且气管上方新出现轻微吸气性喘鸣。请选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数，完成弓形题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数，完成弓形题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 58-year-old client with untreated non-small cell lung cancer and a known right mediastinal mass has worsening facial and periorbital edema, neck circumference increased from 44 cm to 47 cm, more prominent chest-wall venous collaterals, bilateral upper-extremity pitting edema, SpO2 90% on 2 L nasal cannula, short-phrase speech, and new faint inspiratory stridor over the trachea.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现在面部和眶周水肿加重，颈围从44 cm增至47 cm，胸壁侧支静脉更加明显，双上肢出现凹陷性水肿，鼻导管2 L时SpO2为90%，只能短语交流，并且气管上方新出现轻微吸气性喘鸣。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_heart_failure","en":"Acute decompensated heart failure with fluid overload","zh":"容量负荷过重导致的急性失代偿性心力衰竭"},{"id":"cond_svc_airway","en":"SVC syndrome with impending airway compromise from mediastinal malignancy","zh":"纵隔恶性肿瘤导致的上腔静脉综合征并有即将发生气道受威胁"},{"id":"cond_upper_dvt","en":"Isolated upper-extremity deep vein thrombosis","zh":"孤立性上肢深静脉血栓"}],"correct":"cond_svc_airway"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_o2_hob","en":"Increase oxygen delivery and keep the head of bed at 45 degrees or higher","zh":"提高氧气输送并保持床头45度或更高"},{"id":"act_escalate_airway","en":"Activate emergency escalation and report new stridor with concern for airway compromise","zh":"启动紧急升级并报告新发喘鸣及气道受威胁风险"},{"id":"act_lower_hob","en":"Lower the head of bed to facilitate a procedure or assessment","zh":"降低床头以便进行操作或评估"},{"id":"act_left_arm_iv_first","en":"Attempt a new opposite-arm IV before addressing airway and escalation","zh":"在处理气道和升级求援前先尝试对侧手臂IV"}],"correct":["act_o2_hob","act_escalate_airway"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"par_leg_edema","en":"Lower-extremity edema assessment","zh":"下肢水肿评估"},{"id":"par_neck_face_edema","en":"Upper-body edema trend: serial neck circumference and facial/periorbital edema","zh":"上半身水肿趋势：连续颈围及面部/眶周水肿"},{"id":"par_stridor_speech","en":"Airway patency: tracheal stridor, voice quality, and speech pattern","zh":"气道通畅性：气管喘鸣、声音质量和说话模式"},{"id":"par_ddimer_trend","en":"Serial D-dimer values","zh":"连续D-二聚体数值"}],"correct":["par_stridor_speech","par_neck_face_edema"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bow-tie centers on malignant SVC syndrome that has progressed to impending airway compromise. The nurse’s priority is to support oxygenation and upright positioning while activating emergency escalation for possible advanced-airway and definitive obstruction-directed interventions. Monitoring should focus on airway patency and upper-body edema trends.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本弓形题的核心是恶性肿瘤相关上腔静脉综合征已进展为即将发生气道受威胁。护士的优先事项是在维持氧合和坐高位的同时启动紧急升级，以便准备高级气道和针对阻塞的根本性干预。监测重点应放在气道通畅性和上半身水肿趋势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, first name the problem using the whole cue cluster, then choose actions and monitoring parameters that match the immediate threat.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，先根据完整线索群命名问题，再选择与立即威胁相匹配的措施和监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1646,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.284","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.284.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[252,436],"terminalOffsetsZh":[93,153],"fullStemEn":"Immune checkpoint inhibitor-related pneumonitis in a patient receiving pembrolizumab for non-small cell lung cancer A client receiving pembrolizumab for NSCLC develops a new dry cough, exertional dyspnea, crackles, and progressive oxygen desaturation. The nurse must recognize an immune-related adverse event, prioritize oxygenation and ordered corticosteroid therapy, communicate within scope, and evaluate early response to treatment.","fullStemZh":"非小细胞肺癌患者接受pembrolizumab后发生免疫检查点抑制剂相关性肺炎 一名因NSCLC接受pembrolizumab治疗的患者出现新发干咳、活动后气促、爆裂音和进行性血氧下降。护士必须识别免疫相关不良事件，优先处理氧合并执行corticosteroid医嘱，在职责范围内沟通，并评估早期治疗反应。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must recognize an immune-related adverse event, prioritize oxygenation and ordered corticosteroid therapy, communicate within scope, and evaluate early response to treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士必须识别免疫相关不良事件，优先处理氧合并执行corticosteroid医嘱，在职责范围内沟通，并评估早期治疗反应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Immune checkpoint inhibitor-related pneumonitis in a patient receiving pembrolizumab for non-small cell lung cancer A client receiving pembrolizumab for NSCLC develops a new dry cough, exertional dyspnea, crackles, and progressive oxygen desaturation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"非小细胞肺癌患者接受pembrolizumab后发生免疫检查点抑制剂相关性肺炎 一名因NSCLC接受pembrolizumab治疗的患者出现新发干咳、活动后气促、爆裂音和进行性血氧下降。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case arc centers on recognizing an immune checkpoint inhibitor-related pulmonary toxicity before it is dismissed as allergies. The significant cues are new dry cough, lower-respiratory crackles, dyspnea, SpO2 decline from baseline, elevated CRP, and later CT/ABG confirmation. Nursing priorities are to notify oncology, hold the checkpoint inhibitor per orders, correct oxygenation first, initiate ordered corticosteroids per protocol, monitor trends, communicate within scope about cancer-treatment decisions, and teach immediate reporting of worsening dyspnea, cough, fever, chest pain, or recurrence during taper.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的主线是在症状被误认为过敏之前识别免疫检查点抑制剂相关肺毒性。重要线索包括新发干咳、下呼吸道爆裂音、气促、SpO2较基线下降、CRP升高，以及后续CT/ABG确认。护理优先事项包括通知肿瘤科、按医嘱暂停检查点抑制剂、先纠正氧合、按方案执行corticosteroid医嘱、监测趋势、在职责范围内沟通癌症治疗决定，并教育患者在减量期间如气促、咳嗽、发热、胸痛加重或症状复发应立即报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In oncology immunotherapy cases, treat new organ-specific symptoms as potential immune-related adverse events until assessed; then prioritize immediate physiologic threats before education or consultation tasks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在肿瘤免疫治疗病例中，应将新出现的器官特异性症状视为潜在免疫相关不良事件，直到完成评估；随后先处理直接生理威胁，再处理教育或会诊任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1647,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that are clinically significant cues requiring further evaluation for immune-related pneumonitis.","fullStemZh":"请标出提示需要进一步评估免疫相关性肺炎的临床重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that are clinically significant cues requiring further evaluation for immune-related pneumonitis.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出提示需要进一步评估免疫相关性肺炎的临床重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"New dry cough began 4 days ago, 9 days after pembrolizumab cycle 4.","zh":"第4周期pembrolizumab后9天出现新发干咳，已持续4天。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Temperature is 98.8 °F (37.1 °C).","zh":"体温98.8 °F (37.1 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"SpO2 is 93% on room air, down from baseline 96%.","zh":"室内空气SpO2为93%，低于基线96%。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Faint bilateral inspiratory crackles are heard at the lung bases.","zh":"双侧肺底可闻及轻微吸气性爆裂音。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"She pauses briefly to breathe after longer phrases.","zh":"较长语句后会短暂停顿换气。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"No peripheral edema or JVD is present.","zh":"无外周水肿或颈静脉怒张。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"CRP is 18 mg/L with a reference value below 5 mg/L.","zh":"CRP为18 mg/L，参考值低于5 mg/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Creatinine, ALT, AST, and TSH are within the listed reference context.","zh":"肌酐、ALT、AST和TSH在所列参考背景内。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Capillary refill is less than 2 seconds and oral mucosa is moist.","zh":"毛细血管再充盈少于2秒，口腔黏膜湿润。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s3","s4","s5","s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The new dry cough after recent pembrolizumab, falling SpO2 from baseline, bilateral crackles, exertional dyspnea, and elevated CRP form a lower-respiratory inflammatory cue cluster. Afebrile status and normal perfusion or unrelated labs do not make the respiratory change safe to dismiss.","rationaleCorrectZh":"近期pembrolizumab后出现新发干咳、SpO2较基线下降、双侧爆裂音、活动后气促和CRP升高，构成下呼吸道炎症线索组合。无发热以及灌注正常或无关实验室结果，不能说明这些呼吸变化可以忽略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a patient suggests a benign explanation, compare it with objective changes from baseline and organ-specific findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者提出良性解释时，要把它与客观基线变化和器官特异性体征进行比较。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1648,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,69],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, analyze the cue cluster and the patient's self-diagnosis.","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，请分析线索组合和患者的自我判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, analyze the cue cluster and the patient's self-diagnosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段1，请分析线索组合和患者的自我判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The findings best support {{d1}} rather than {{d2}} because the pattern includes lower-respiratory findings, a measurable oxygenation decline, inflammatory elevation, and recent immunotherapy exposure.","zh":"这些表现最支持 {{d1}}，而不是 {{d2}}，因为该模式包括下呼吸道体征、可测量的氧合下降、炎症指标升高，以及近期免疫治疗暴露。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"d1_a","en":"immune-related pneumonitis","zh":"免疫相关性肺炎"},{"id":"d1_c","en":"isolated osteoarthritis flare","zh":"单纯骨关节炎加重"},{"id":"d1_b","en":"uncomplicated allergic rhinitis","zh":"单纯过敏性鼻炎"}],"correct":"d1_a"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"d2_a","en":"seasonal allergies","zh":"季节性过敏"},{"id":"d2_c","en":"acute kidney injury","zh":"急性肾损伤"},{"id":"d2_b","en":"immune-related thyroiditis","zh":"免疫相关性甲状腺炎"}],"correct":"d2_a"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The recent pembrolizumab exposure plus new cough, crackles, desaturation, dyspnea, and CRP elevation fit an immune-mediated lower-respiratory process. Seasonal allergies would more commonly produce sneezing, rhinorrhea, itchy or watery eyes, and upper-airway symptoms rather than crackles and falling oxygen saturation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"近期pembrolizumab暴露，加上新发咳嗽、爆裂音、血氧下降、气促和CRP升高，符合免疫介导的下呼吸道过程。季节性过敏通常表现为打喷嚏、流涕、眼痒或流泪等上气道症状，而不是爆裂音和血氧下降。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not anchor on the patient's explanation when objective respiratory findings point to a higher-risk adverse effect.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当客观呼吸系统发现提示较高风险不良反应时，不要锚定在患者自己的解释上。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1649,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,62],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, CT findings are consistent with immune-related pneumonitis, PaO2 is 68 mmHg on room air, and SpO2 has fallen to 91%. Which ordered intervention is the nurse's immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，CT结果符合免疫相关性肺炎，室内空气PaO2为68 mmHg，SpO2降至91%。护士应优先执行哪项已开立的医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which ordered intervention is the nurse's immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先执行哪项已开立的医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, CT findings are consistent with immune-related pneumonitis, PaO2 is 68 mmHg on room air, and SpO2 has fallen to 91%.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，CT结果符合免疫相关性肺炎，室内空气PaO2为68 mmHg，SpO2降至91%。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_a","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen and titrate to the ordered SpO2 target.","zh":"给予补充氧气，并调整至医嘱规定的SpO2目标。"},{"id":"q3_c","en":"Begin discharge teaching about future cancer-treatment options.","zh":"开始进行未来癌症治疗选择的出院教育。"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Prepare the next pembrolizumab infusion so treatment is not delayed.","zh":"准备下一次pembrolizumab输注，以免治疗延误。"},{"id":"q3_b","en":"Call pulmonology before starting oxygen or corticosteroids.","zh":"在开始吸氧或 corticosteroid 前先致电肺科。"}],"correct":["q3_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The active oxygenation deficit is the immediate physiologic threat. Applying oxygen directly addresses breathing while the nurse then proceeds with corticosteroids, monitoring, and consultation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前氧合不足是最直接的生理威胁。给予氧气直接处理呼吸问题，随后护士再继续执行corticosteroid、监测和会诊相关工作。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several orders are appropriate, choose the one that treats the immediate ABC threat first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多项医嘱都合适时，先选择处理最直接ABC威胁的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1650,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,148],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,42],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the client asks whether her cancer treatment is being stopped permanently. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，患者询问她的癌症治疗是否会被永久停止。哪些护理措施合适？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_c","en":"Promise that pembrolizumab will restart after the cough improves.","zh":"承诺咳嗽改善后会重新开始pembrolizumab。"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"Tell her the oncology team will discuss the long-term treatment plan after she is stabilized.","zh":"告诉她肿瘤团队会在她稳定后讨论长期治疗计划。"},{"id":"q4_d","en":"Initiate methylprednisolone as ordered per the facility protocol.","zh":"按院内方案和医嘱开始给予methylprednisolone。"},{"id":"q4_e","en":"Verify oxygen delivery is maintaining the ordered SpO2 target and arrange every-2-hour pulse oximetry.","zh":"确认给氧能维持医嘱要求的SpO2目标，并安排每2小时脉搏血氧监测。"},{"id":"q4_a","en":"Explain that pembrolizumab is being held now because of serious lung inflammation.","zh":"解释pembrolizumab目前因严重肺部炎症而暂停。"},{"id":"q4_f","en":"Independently tell her the drug is permanently discontinued and that all cancer treatment is over.","zh":"独立告诉她该药已永久停用，而且所有癌症治疗都结束了。"}],"correct":["q4_a","q4_b","q4_d","q4_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse can give truthful, scope-appropriate information: the drug is held now, oncology will decide and explain the long-term plan, and urgent ordered treatment must continue. Promising restart or independently declaring all treatment over is outside nursing scope and inaccurate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士可以提供真实且符合职责范围的信息：该药目前暂停，长期计划由肿瘤科决定并解释，同时必须继续执行紧急医嘱治疗。承诺重启或独立宣布所有治疗结束都超出护理职责且不准确。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate what the nurse can truthfully explain from provider-level decisions, while still carrying out urgent safety interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分护士可以如实解释的内容和医师层级决定，同时继续执行紧急安全干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1651,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,67],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, place the ordered nursing actions in the best sequence.","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，请将已开立的护理措施按最佳顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, place the ordered nursing actions in the best sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段2，请将已开立的护理措施按最佳顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q5_c","en":"Establish every-2-hour pulse oximetry monitoring and document the baseline on-oxygen reading.","zh":"建立每2小时脉搏血氧监测，并记录吸氧后的基线读数。"},{"id":"q5_d","en":"Notify or coordinate with pulmonology for co-management after bedside stabilization is underway.","zh":"在床边稳定措施已开始后，通知或协调肺科共同管理。"},{"id":"q5_b","en":"Initiate methylprednisolone as ordered, verifying dose, route, and rate against the protocol order.","zh":"按医嘱开始methylprednisolone，并根据方案医嘱核对剂量、途径和速度。"},{"id":"q5_a","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen and confirm SpO2 is moving toward the >=94% target.","zh":"给予补充氧气，并确认SpO2正接近>=94%的目标。"}],"correct":["q5_a","q5_b","q5_c","q5_d"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is a clinically real sequence: first correct the immediate oxygenation deficit, then begin the anti-inflammatory corticosteroid treatment, then set up surveillance to detect improvement or deterioration, and then coordinate the consult once urgent bedside actions are underway.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是临床上真实的顺序：先纠正最直接的氧合不足，再开始抗炎的corticosteroid治疗，然后建立监测以发现改善或恶化，最后在紧急床边措施已启动后协调会诊。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use ABCs to start the sequence, then ask which action treats the cause, which action monitors response, and which action coordinates ongoing care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排序时先用ABC确定第一步，再判断哪项治疗病因、哪项监测反应、哪项协调后续护理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1652,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.284.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,76],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding when evaluating the response to treatment.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，评估治疗反应时，请对每项发现进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding when evaluating the response to treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段3，评估治疗反应时，请对每项发现进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"SpO2 is 96% on 3 L nasal cannula after being 91% on room air.","zh":"此前室内空气SpO2为91%，现在鼻导管3 L下SpO2为96%。"},{"id":"r2","en":"PaO2 improved from 68 mmHg on room air to 82 mmHg on 3 L nasal cannula.","zh":"PaO2从室内空气68 mmHg改善为鼻导管3 L下82 mmHg。"},{"id":"r3","en":"CRP decreased from 18 mg/L to 11 mg/L.","zh":"CRP从18 mg/L降至11 mg/L。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Heart rate and respiratory rate decreased to HR 86 and RR 18.","zh":"心率和呼吸频率下降至HR 86、RR 18。"},{"id":"r5","en":"The client says she is not as short of breath.","zh":"患者表示没有那么气促。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Bilateral crackles are still present but similar to slightly less prominent.","zh":"双侧仍有爆裂音，但相似或略减轻。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Does not by itself indicate treatment failure","zh":"单独来看不表示治疗失败"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports improving trend","zh":"支持改善趋势"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is improving because multiple trends are moving in the right direction: oxygenation, vital signs, inflammatory marker, and subjective dyspnea. Persistent crackles at 36 hours do not outweigh the broader improvement because inflammatory lung findings can resolve slowly.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在改善，因为多项趋势都朝正确方向变化：氧合、生命体征、炎症指标和主观气促。36小时仍有爆裂音不能推翻整体改善，因为炎症性肺部体征可能需要更长时间才会消退。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by trends across several systems, not by one persistent abnormal finding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估疗效时看多个系统的趋势，不要只依据一个持续异常体征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1653,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_06_19_case_ici_pneumonitis_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.285","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.285.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.285.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[519,619],"terminalOffsetsZh":[206,237],"fullStemEn":"After pembrolizumab cycle 4, a client develops new dry cough, bilateral basilar crackles, progressive SpO2 decline from 96% baseline to 91% on room air, PaO2 68 mmHg, elevated CRP, and CT showing new bilateral lower-lobe ground-glass opacities without pleural effusion, pulmonary embolism, or lymphangitic carcinomatosis. The oncologist orders pembrolizumab held, admission, oxygen to maintain SpO2 >=94%, methylprednisolone per facility irAE pneumonitis protocol, every-2-hour pulse oximetry, and pulmonology consult. Complete the bow-tie by choosing the condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"第4周期pembrolizumab后，患者出现新发干咳、双侧肺底爆裂音，SpO2从基线96%逐步降至室内空气91%，PaO2 68 mmHg，CRP升高，CT显示新发双侧下肺叶磨玻璃影，无胸腔积液、肺栓塞或淋巴管性癌病。肿瘤科医师开立医嘱：暂停pembrolizumab，收入院，吸氧以维持SpO2 >=94%，按院内irAE肺炎方案给予methylprednisolone，每2小时脉搏血氧监测，并请肺科会诊。请完成bow-tie，选择病情、两个优先措施和两个需监测参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by choosing the condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成bow-tie，选择病情、两个优先措施和两个需监测参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The oncologist orders pembrolizumab held, admission, oxygen to maintain SpO2 >=94%, methylprednisolone per facility irAE pneumonitis protocol, every-2-hour pulse oximetry, and pulmonology consult.","penultimateSentenceZh":"肿瘤科医师开立医嘱：暂停pembrolizumab，收入院，吸氧以维持SpO2 >=94%，按院内irAE肺炎方案给予methylprednisolone，每2小时脉搏血氧监测，并请肺科会诊。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_progression","en":"Progression of NSCLC with lymphangitic carcinomatosis","zh":"NSCLC进展伴淋巴管性癌病"},{"id":"cond_ici_pneumonitis","en":"Immune checkpoint inhibitor-related pneumonitis","zh":"免疫检查点抑制剂相关性肺炎"},{"id":"cond_cap","en":"Community-acquired pneumonia","zh":"社区获得性肺炎"}],"correct":"cond_ici_pneumonitis"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_methylpred","en":"Initiate methylprednisolone per the facility irAE pneumonitis protocol order.","zh":"按院内irAE肺炎方案医嘱开始methylprednisolone。"},{"id":"act_continue_pembro","en":"Administer the next pembrolizumab infusion so cancer treatment is not interrupted.","zh":"给予下一次pembrolizumab输注，以免中断癌症治疗。"},{"id":"act_oxygen","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen to achieve the ordered SpO2 target.","zh":"给予补充氧气以达到医嘱SpO2目标。"},{"id":"act_wait_pulm","en":"Delay oxygen and corticosteroids until pulmonology calls back.","zh":"等肺科回电后再吸氧和给予corticosteroid。"}],"correct":["act_oxygen","act_methylpred"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_rr_wob","en":"Respiratory rate and work of breathing","zh":"呼吸频率和呼吸做功"},{"id":"param_tsh","en":"TSH level at this synthesis moment","zh":"此综合判断时刻的TSH水平"},{"id":"param_platelets","en":"Platelet count at this synthesis moment","zh":"此综合判断时刻的血小板计数"},{"id":"param_spo2","en":"Oxygen saturation trend on ordered pulse oximetry","zh":"按医嘱脉搏血氧监测的SpO2趋势"}],"correct":["param_spo2","param_rr_wob"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is immune checkpoint inhibitor-related pneumonitis because the respiratory cue cluster, CT pattern, oxygenation decline, inflammatory marker, and pembrolizumab timing fit immune-mediated lung inflammation. Priority actions are immediate oxygenation support and ordered corticosteroid therapy. Monitoring SpO2 trend plus respiratory rate/work of breathing evaluates whether gas exchange and ventilatory demand are improving.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该病情为免疫检查点抑制剂相关性肺炎，因为呼吸线索组合、CT模式、氧合下降、炎症指标和pembrolizumab时间关系符合免疫介导的肺部炎症。优先措施是立即支持氧合并执行医嘱corticosteroid治疗。监测SpO2趋势以及呼吸频率/呼吸做功，可评估气体交换和通气需求是否改善。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, lock the center diagnosis from the strongest cue cluster, then choose actions that address the immediate threat and the pathophysiology, followed by monitoring parameters that measure response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做bow-tie题时，先用最强线索组合锁定中心诊断，再选择同时处理直接威胁和病理生理机制的措施，最后选择能衡量反应的监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1654,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.286","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.286.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[283,469],"terminalOffsetsZh":[108,189],"fullStemEn":"Neutropenic fever during chemotherapy nadir A 58-year-old woman with stage IIIB diffuse large B-cell lymphoma is on day 10 of cycle 2 R-CHOP and is in the expected count nadir window. She was admitted two days ago for poor oral intake and dehydration. A triple-lumen PICC is patent. Standing orders require blood cultures and immediate oncology notification for a single oral temperature ≥ 100.9 °F (38.3 °C) or temperature ≥ 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) sustained over one hour.","fullStemZh":"化疗低谷期中性粒细胞减少性发热 一名 58 岁女性，患 IIIB 期弥漫大 B 细胞淋巴瘤，正在第 2 个 R-CHOP 周期第 10 天，处于预期血细胞计数低谷期。她两天前因进食差和脱水入院。三腔 PICC 通畅。常规医嘱要求：单次口温 ≥ 100.9 °F (38.3 °C) 或体温 ≥ 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) 持续 1 小时时，采集血培养并立即通知肿瘤科。","terminalSentenceEn":"Standing orders require blood cultures and immediate oncology notification for a single oral temperature ≥ 100.9 °F (38.3 °C) or temperature ≥ 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) sustained over one hour.","terminalSentenceZh":"常规医嘱要求：单次口温 ≥ 100.9 °F (38.3 °C) 或体温 ≥ 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) 持续 1 小时时，采集血培养并立即通知肿瘤科。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A triple-lumen PICC is patent.","penultimateSentenceZh":"三腔 PICC 通畅。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on recognizing fever during chemotherapy nadir as a neutropenic emergency, preserving culture yield without delaying empiric antibiotics, preventing portals of entry, escalating promptly when perfusion worsens, and teaching exact home return precautions. Stage 2 shows progression toward neutropenic sepsis; Stage 3 shows improvement by reversing perfusion markers while still requiring inpatient antibiotics and follow-up of the positive PICC-lumen culture.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例重点是识别化疗低谷期发热为中性粒细胞减少相关急症，在不延误经验性抗生素的前提下保留培养诊断价值，预防感染入口，灌注恶化时及时升级处理，并用具体标准进行居家返院教育。第 2 阶段显示向中性粒细胞减少性脓毒症进展；第 3 阶段通过灌注指标逆转显示改善，但仍需住院 IV 抗生素并跟进 PICC 管腔培养阳性结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the timeline: first recognize the emergency, then protect diagnostic cultures while starting treatment, then respond to shock cues, then evaluate trends and teach return precautions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按时间线思考：先识别急症，再在开始治疗的同时保护培养诊断价值，然后应对休克线索，最后评估趋势并教育返院标准。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1655,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the Stage 1 findings that are significant cues of a time-critical neutropenic fever emergency.","fullStemZh":"请标出第 1 阶段提示中性粒细胞减少性发热为时间紧迫急症的重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the Stage 1 findings that are significant cues of a time-critical neutropenic fever emergency.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出第 1 阶段提示中性粒细胞减少性发热为时间紧迫急症的重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","selectable":true,"en":"At 1415 the client has visible rigors and says she feels suddenly cold and shaky. ","zh":"1415，患者出现明显寒战，并说自己突然觉得很冷、发抖。"},{"id":"s2","selectable":true,"en":"Oral temperature is 102.0 °F (38.9 °C). ","zh":"口温为 102.0 °F (38.9 °C)。"},{"id":"s3","selectable":true,"en":"HR is 104/min. ","zh":"心率为 104 次/分。"},{"id":"s4","selectable":true,"en":"BP is 108/68 mm Hg. ","zh":"血压为 108/68 mm Hg。"},{"id":"s5","selectable":true,"en":"Fingertips are cool and slightly mottled with capillary refill of 3 seconds. ","zh":"指尖发凉、轻度花斑，毛细血管再充盈时间为 3 秒。"},{"id":"s6","selectable":true,"en":"Lung sounds are clear bilaterally. ","zh":"双肺呼吸音清晰。"},{"id":"s7","selectable":true,"en":"The PICC insertion site is clean, dry, intact, and non-tender. ","zh":"PICC 置管部位清洁、干燥、完整，且无压痛。"},{"id":"s8","selectable":true,"en":"The left buccal mucosa has a small intact area of oral mucositis. ","zh":"左侧颊黏膜有一小处完整的口腔黏膜炎。"},{"id":"s9","selectable":true,"en":"WBC is 0.6 ×10³/µL with ANC 180/µL during the expected chemotherapy nadir. ","zh":"预期化疗低谷期内，WBC 为 0.6 ×10³/µL，ANC 为 180/µL。"},{"id":"s10","selectable":true,"en":"Lactate is 1.4 mmol/L. ","zh":"乳酸为 1.4 mmol/L。"}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s5","s9"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The fever exceeds the standing single-reading threshold, and rigors, tachycardia, severe neutropenia during the nadir, and early peripheral vasoconstriction make this a time-critical emergency. Clear lungs, a normal-appearing PICC site, and normal lactate do not rule out serious infection in a neutropenic client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"体温超过医嘱中单次读数的发热阈值；寒战、心动过速、低谷期严重中性粒细胞减少以及早期外周血管收缩共同提示这是时间紧迫的急症。双肺清晰、PICC 部位外观正常和乳酸正常，并不能排除中性粒细胞减少患者的严重感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In oncology nadir questions, treat fever plus severe neutropenia as the danger signal even when the source exam looks normal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到肿瘤治疗低谷期题目时，即使感染来源检查看似正常，也要把发热加严重中性粒细胞减少视为危险信号。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1656,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Complete the reasoning chain for the Stage 1 cultures-and-antibiotics requirement.","fullStemZh":"请完成第 1 阶段关于培养和抗生素要求的临床推理链。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the reasoning chain for the Stage 1 cultures-and-antibiotics requirement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成第 1 阶段关于培养和抗生素要求的临床推理链。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should obtain ordered blood cultures {{d1}}, then start empiric IV antibiotics {{d2}}, because {{d3}}.","zh":"护士应 {{d1}} 取得医嘱要求的血培养，然后 {{d2}} 开始经验性 IV 抗生素，因为 {{d3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"d1o2","en":"after the antibiotic infusion is complete","zh":"在抗生素输注完成后"},{"id":"d1o3","en":"only if a local source of infection is found","zh":"只有找到局部感染来源时"},{"id":"d1o1","en":"before the first antibiotic dose","zh":"在首次抗生素给药前"}],"correct":"d1o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"d2o1","en":"within the ordered one-hour window","zh":"在医嘱规定的 1 小时窗口内"},{"id":"d2o2","en":"after culture results identify the organism","zh":"等培养结果确定病原体后"},{"id":"d2o3","en":"after the fever has persisted for another hour","zh":"等发热再持续 1 小时后"}],"correct":"d2o1"},{"id":"d3","options":[{"id":"d3o3","en":"neutropenic clients usually produce obvious localizing infection signs","zh":"中性粒细胞减少患者通常会出现明显局部感染体征"},{"id":"d3o2","en":"antibiotics are unsafe until all imaging is completed","zh":"所有影像检查完成前使用抗生素不安全"},{"id":"d3o1","en":"cultures preserve diagnostic yield while rapid empiric therapy limits progression","zh":"培养可保留诊断价值，同时快速经验性治疗可限制病情进展"}],"correct":"d3o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cultures before antibiotics preserve the chance of identifying the organism, but this should take minutes, not delay treatment. The provider order pairs rapid cultures with prompt empiric antibiotics because the severely neutropenic client has little innate immune defense.","rationaleCorrectZh":"抗生素前采集培养可保留识别病原体的机会，但这应在几分钟内完成，不能延误治疗。医嘱将快速采集培养与及时经验性抗生素配对，是因为严重中性粒细胞减少患者几乎没有足够的先天免疫防御。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When two urgent actions seem to compete, ask whether one is a brief prerequisite that protects later care without delaying the lifesaving intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当两个紧急措施看似冲突时，判断其中一个是否是短时间即可完成、能保护后续治疗价值且不延误救命措施的前置步骤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1657,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,53],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, place the nurse's immediate priority actions in the order they should be ensured. Some bedside tasks may overlap, but the sequence should reflect the dominant priorities.","fullStemZh":"在第 2 阶段，请按护士应确保完成的优先顺序排列立即措施。部分床旁操作可重叠进行，但排序应反映主要优先级。","terminalSentenceEn":"Some bedside tasks may overlap, but the sequence should reflect the dominant priorities.","terminalSentenceZh":"部分床旁操作可重叠进行，但排序应反映主要优先级。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, place the nurse's immediate priority actions in the order they should be ensured.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第 2 阶段，请按护士应确保完成的优先顺序排列立即措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q3_c","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen by nasal cannula to support tissue oxygenation during the perfusion crisis.","zh":"经鼻导管给予氧气，以在灌注危机中支持组织氧合。"},{"id":"q3_a","en":"Reposition the client supine and start the ordered isotonic crystalloid bolus while reassessing perfusion and lung status.","zh":"协助患者平卧，并开始医嘱的等渗晶体液快速补液，同时复评灌注和肺部情况。"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Redraw blood cultures from new sites before the antibiotic regimen is broadened.","zh":"在扩大抗生素方案前，从新部位重新采集血培养。"},{"id":"q3_b","en":"Activate the rapid response team and notify the oncologist with the BP drop, HR rise, urine-output decline, and lactate rise.","zh":"启动快速反应团队，并向肿瘤科医生报告血压下降、心率升高、尿量减少和乳酸升高。"}],"correct":["q3_a","q3_b","q3_c","q3_d"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Stage 2 findings show progression toward sepsis with hypotension, rising lactate, oliguria, tachycardia, and slower responses. Restoring perfusion and escalating the team come first; oxygen supports the oxygen-delivery problem, and repeat cultures should precede the antibiotic change without delaying resuscitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第 2 阶段表现为向脓毒症进展：低血压、乳酸升高、少尿、心动过速和反应变慢。首先要恢复灌注并升级团队；氧气支持氧输送问题；重复培养应在调整抗生素前完成，但不能延误复苏。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For deterioration with shock cues, prioritize perfusion restoration and team escalation before diagnostic tasks that can safely follow within minutes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到休克线索的病情恶化时，先恢复灌注并升级团队，再做可在几分钟内随后完成的诊断任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1658,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,38],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing interventions are appropriate modifications for this severely neutropenic client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"对于这名严重中性粒细胞减少患者，哪些护理措施属于适当调整？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing interventions are appropriate modifications for this severely neutropenic client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"对于这名严重中性粒细胞减少患者，哪些护理措施属于适当调整？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_c","en":"Allow fresh flowers if the water is changed daily and the vase is kept away from the bed.","zh":"如果每天换水且花瓶远离床边，可以允许鲜花。"},{"id":"q4_d","en":"Follow the facility low-microbial/food-safety protocol for food brought to the client.","zh":"对患者食物遵循机构低微生物/食品安全方案。"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"Require hand hygiene before entry and restrict visitors who are ill.","zh":"进入病房前必须手卫生，并限制患病访客。"},{"id":"q4_f","en":"Minimize unnecessary invasive procedures and use meticulous aseptic technique for every PICC access.","zh":"尽量减少不必要的侵入性操作，每次使用 PICC 时严格无菌操作。"},{"id":"q4_e","en":"Use gentle oral care with a soft toothbrush and non-alcohol rinse for the mucositis site.","zh":"对口腔黏膜炎部位使用软毛牙刷和无酒精漱口液进行温和口腔护理。"},{"id":"q4_a","en":"Avoid rectal temperatures, rectal medications, enemas, and rectal assessment unless specifically ordered for an overriding reason.","zh":"避免直肠测温、直肠给药、灌肠和直肠评估，除非因更重要原因有明确医嘱。"}],"correct":["q4_a","q4_b","q4_d","q4_e","q4_f"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe neutropenia requires reducing microbial exposure and avoiding preventable mucosal or skin breaks. Rectal instrumentation is avoided, visitors and food are controlled by protocol, oral care should protect fragile mucosa, and all line access must be aseptic and necessary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重中性粒细胞减少需要减少微生物暴露，并避免可预防的黏膜或皮肤破损。应避免直肠操作，按方案管理访客和食物，口腔护理要保护脆弱黏膜，所有管路操作都必须严格无菌且有必要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For neutropenia precautions, think: reduce exposure, protect mucosa, and avoid unnecessary breaks in skin or lines.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断中性粒细胞减少防护时，抓住三点：减少暴露、保护黏膜、避免不必要的皮肤或管路破口。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1659,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,89],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify how each finding should be used to evaluate the client's trajectory.","fullStemZh":"在第 3 阶段，请判断每项发现应如何用于评估患者病情轨迹。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify how each finding should be used to evaluate the client's trajectory.","terminalSentenceZh":"在第 3 阶段，请判断每项发现应如何用于评估患者病情轨迹。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Temperature trend: 39.4 → 38.6 → 100.6 °F (38.1 °C)","zh":"体温趋势：39.4 → 38.6 → 100.6 °F (38.1 °C)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Heart rate trend: 118 → 106 → 96/min","zh":"心率趋势：118 → 106 → 96 次/分"},{"id":"r3","en":"Blood pressure trend: 92/58 → 100/64 → 106/68 mm Hg","zh":"血压趋势：92/58 → 100/64 → 106/68 mm Hg"},{"id":"r4","en":"Urine output improves from 15 mL/hr to 45-55 mL/hr","zh":"尿量从 15 mL/hr 改善至 45-55 mL/hr"},{"id":"r5","en":"Lactate decreases from 3.2 to 2.0 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸从 3.2 降至 2.0 mmol/L"},{"id":"r6","en":"Mental status improves from slower responses to alert and conversational","zh":"精神状态从反应变慢改善为清醒并能交谈"},{"id":"r7","en":"Preliminary Gram-positive organism is reported in the PICC lumen bottle","zh":"PICC 管腔培养瓶初步报告革兰阳性菌"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Needs continued follow-up/communication","zh":"需要继续随访/沟通"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports improving response","zh":"支持治疗反应改善"},{"id":"c3","en":"Indicates continued deterioration","zh":"提示持续恶化"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r7","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The overall trajectory is improving because perfusion and systemic response markers are reversing: lower temperature and heart rate, recovering blood pressure, better urine output, falling lactate, and improved alertness. The positive PICC-lumen culture is important and must be reported, but it does not erase the improving hemodynamic trend.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总体轨迹在改善，因为灌注和全身反应指标正在逆转：体温和心率下降、血压恢复、尿量改善、乳酸下降、意识更清醒。PICC 管腔培养阳性很重要，必须报告，但不会否定血流动力学改善趋势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by trending the same cues that signaled danger; one new lab result can require follow-up without overturning the whole trend.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估效果时，要追踪最初提示危险的同一组线索；一个新的化验结果可能需要跟进，但不一定推翻整体趋势。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1660,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.286.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,41],"fullStemEn":"Which discharge-readiness teaching should the nurse give about seeking emergency care during future chemotherapy nadir periods? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"关于未来化疗低谷期何时需要急诊就医，护士应提供哪些出院准备教育？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which discharge-readiness teaching should the nurse give about seeking emergency care during future chemotherapy nadir periods?","penultimateSentenceZh":"关于未来化疗低谷期何时需要急诊就医，护士应提供哪些出院准备教育？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q6_c","en":"Take acetaminophen or ibuprofen first, then call the clinic the next morning if the fever returns.","zh":"先服用对乙酰氨基酚或布洛芬；如果发热复发，第二天早上再打电话给门诊。"},{"id":"q6_e","en":"Go for immediate evaluation for rigors, shaking chills, sudden lightheadedness, confusion, or rapid heartbeat even if a fever has not yet been confirmed.","zh":"即使尚未确认发热，若出现寒战、发抖、突然头晕、意识混乱或心跳很快，也应立即就医评估。"},{"id":"q6_d","en":"Use an oral thermometer for temperature checks and do not take rectal temperatures.","zh":"使用口温计测量体温，不要测直肠温。"},{"id":"q6_f","en":"If there are no localizing symptoms, wait unless the fever is above 102.2 °F (39 °C).","zh":"如果没有局部症状，除非体温超过 102.2 °F (39 °C)，否则可以等待。"},{"id":"q6_a","en":"Seek emergency care immediately for any single oral temperature of 101 °F (38.3 °C) or higher.","zh":"任何单次口温达到或超过 101 °F (38.3 °C)时，应立即急诊就医。"},{"id":"q6_b","en":"Seek emergency care for oral temperature of 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) or higher that persists for one hour, per oncology instructions.","zh":"按肿瘤科指导，口温达到或超过 100.4 °F (38.0 °C)并持续 1 小时时，应急诊就医。"}],"correct":["q6_a","q6_b","q6_d","q6_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teaching must be specific and action-oriented because fever during the nadir can be the only early sign of life-threatening infection. The client should use oral temperature thresholds from the oncology plan, avoid rectal measurements, avoid masking fever with antipyretics before evaluation, and seek care for systemic illness cues even before a temperature is confirmed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"教育必须具体、以行动为导向，因为低谷期发热可能是危及生命感染的唯一早期征象。患者应使用肿瘤科计划中的口温阈值，避免直肠测温，评估前不要用退热药掩盖发热，并且即使尚未确认体温，出现全身不适线索也应就医。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge teaching, convert the emergency into exact numbers and exact actions the client can follow at home.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做出院教育题时，要把急症转换成患者在家能执行的具体数字和具体行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1661,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_neutropenic_fever_nadir_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.287","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.287.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.287.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,355],"terminalOffsetsZh":[113,145],"fullStemEn":"At 1745, the client with confirmed severe neutropenia has persistent fever, HR 118, BP 92/58, RR 24, SpO₂ 94% on room air, capillary refill 4 seconds, urine output 60 mL over 4 hours, and lactate 3.2 mmol/L after initial empiric antibiotics. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"1745，这名已确认严重中性粒细胞减少的患者在初始经验性抗生素后仍持续发热，HR 118，BP 92/58，RR 24，室内空气 SpO₂ 94%，毛细血管再充盈 4 秒，4 小时尿量 60 mL，乳酸 3.2 mmol/L。请完成蝴蝶结题，选择最可能的状况、两个优先措施和两个需监测参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题，选择最可能的状况、两个优先措施和两个需监测参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1745, the client with confirmed severe neutropenia has persistent fever, HR 118, BP 92/58, RR 24, SpO₂ 94% on room air, capillary refill 4 seconds, urine output 60 mL over 4 hours, and lactate 3.2 mmol/L after initial empiric antibiotics.","penultimateSentenceZh":"1745，这名已确认严重中性粒细胞减少的患者在初始经验性抗生素后仍持续发热，HR 118，BP 92/58，RR 24，室内空气 SpO₂ 94%，毛细血管再充盈 4 秒，4 小时尿量 60 mL，乳酸 3.2 mmol/L。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_drug_reaction","en":"Immediate transfusion or antibiotic allergic reaction","zh":"急性输血反应或抗生素过敏反应"},{"id":"cond_dehydration","en":"Simple dehydration from poor oral intake","zh":"单纯进食差导致的脱水"},{"id":"cond_neutropenic_sepsis","en":"Neutropenic fever progressing toward sepsis","zh":"中性粒细胞减少性发热向脓毒症进展"}],"correct":"cond_neutropenic_sepsis"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_wait","en":"Continue current vital-sign frequency and wait for the next scheduled reassessment","zh":"继续按当前频率测生命体征，等下一次计划复评"},{"id":"act_bolus","en":"Start isotonic crystalloid bolus per sepsis/oncology protocol and position supine","zh":"按脓毒症/肿瘤科方案开始等渗晶体液快速补液并协助平卧"},{"id":"act_culture_first","en":"Delay fluid resuscitation until repeat cultures are drawn and broadened antibiotics are ordered","zh":"延迟补液复苏，直到重复培养采集并获得扩大抗生素医嘱"},{"id":"act_escalate","en":"Activate rapid response and notify oncology with structured deterioration cues","zh":"启动快速反应团队，并用结构化方式向肿瘤科报告恶化线索"}],"correct":["act_bolus","act_escalate"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_lactate","en":"Serum lactate trend","zh":"血清乳酸趋势"},{"id":"param_cxr","en":"Repeat chest X-ray findings as the immediate response marker","zh":"将重复胸片结果作为即时反应指标"},{"id":"param_map_uo","en":"Mean arterial pressure and urine output","zh":"平均动脉压和尿量"},{"id":"param_anc","en":"Repeat WBC/ANC during the acute crisis","zh":"急性危机期间重复 WBC/ANC"}],"correct":["param_map_uo","param_lactate"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Stage 2 picture is neutropenic fever progressing toward sepsis: persistent fever with hypotension, tachycardia, rising lactate, oliguria, delayed refill, and slower responses. The first priorities are perfusion support and rapid escalation; MAP/urine output and lactate trend show whether resuscitation is working.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第 2 阶段图像符合中性粒细胞减少性发热向脓毒症进展：持续发热伴低血压、心动过速、乳酸升高、少尿、再充盈延迟和反应变慢。首要任务是支持灌注和快速升级处理；平均动脉压/尿量及乳酸趋势可显示复苏是否有效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bow-tie items, link the center condition to the strongest cue cluster, then choose actions and monitoring that directly treat and measure that condition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，将中心状况与最强线索群相连，再选择能直接治疗并衡量该状况的措施和监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At 1745, the client with confirmed severe neutropenia has persistent fever, HR 118, BP 92/58, RR 24, SpO₂ 94% on room air, capillary refill 4 seconds, urine output 60 mL over 4 hours, and lactate 3.2 mmol/L after initial empiric antibiotics.","controlSentenceZh":"1745，这名已确认严重中性粒细胞减少的患者在初始经验性抗生素后仍持续发热，HR 118，BP 92/58，RR 24，室内空气 SpO₂ 94%，毛细血管再充盈 4 秒，4 小时尿量 60 mL，乳酸 3.2 mmol/L。"}
{"queueIndex":1662,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.288","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.288.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[374,559],"terminalOffsetsZh":[92,146],"fullStemEn":"Transfusion-associated circulatory overload versus transfusion-related acute lung injury in a client with chronic kidney disease A 74-year-old woman with chronic kidney disease stage 3b, compensated heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, type 2 diabetes, and symptomatic anemia is admitted for packed red blood cell transfusion. Two units are ordered sequentially. Facility protocol requires bedside verification by two RNs, vital-sign monitoring during transfusion, and provider-directed IV furosemide between units if signs of fluid overload occur.","fullStemZh":"慢性肾病患者输血相关循环超负荷与输血相关急性肺损伤的鉴别 一名74岁女性因症状性贫血入院，既往有3b期慢性肾病、代偿期射血分数保留型心力衰竭和2型糖尿病。医嘱连续输注2单位浓缩红细胞。机构流程要求两名注册护士床旁核对、输血期间监测生命体征；若出现液体负荷过重表现，由医嘱给予单位间IV呋塞米。","terminalSentenceEn":"Facility protocol requires bedside verification by two RNs, vital-sign monitoring during transfusion, and provider-directed IV furosemide between units if signs of fluid overload occur.","terminalSentenceZh":"机构流程要求两名注册护士床旁核对、输血期间监测生命体征；若出现液体负荷过重表现，由医嘱给予单位间IV呋塞米。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two units are ordered sequentially.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱连续输注2单位浓缩红细胞。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case shows an acute respiratory transfusion reaction during the second unit of packed red blood cells. The new cue cluster is not simply chronic crackles: it includes abrupt dyspnea, hypoxemia, tachypnea, hypertension, new S3, JVD, worsening peripheral edema, oliguria, pulmonary vascular congestion, cardiomegaly, BNP rise, and rapid improvement with diuresis. Those findings support transfusion-associated circulatory overload rather than TRALI, allergic reaction, anaphylaxis, or a febrile non-hemolytic reaction. The safe nursing arc is to stop the transfusion, support oxygenation and positioning, notify the provider and blood bank, preserve the line with new tubing, administer ordered diuretic therapy for TACO, and evaluate improvement by oxygen weaning, vital-sign trends, urine output, and resolution of congestion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例显示患者在第二单位浓缩红细胞输注期间发生急性呼吸性输血反应。新的线索并不只是慢性肺底湿啰音，而是包括突发气短、低氧、呼吸急促、高血压、新S3、颈静脉怒张、外周水肿加重、少尿、肺血管淤血、心影增大、BNP升高，以及利尿后迅速改善。这些表现支持输血相关循环超负荷，而不是TRALI、过敏反应、过敏性休克或发热性非溶血性输血反应。安全的护理思路是立即停止输血，改善氧合和体位，通知医嘱者和血库，用新管路维持静脉通路，针对TACO给予医嘱利尿治疗，并通过氧气降阶、生命体征趋势、尿量和淤血体征消退来评价疗效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In transfusion reactions, first compare current findings with baseline, then separate respiratory distress caused by volume overload from noncardiogenic lung injury or allergy. Management follows the identified mechanism.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理输血反应题时，先把当前表现与基线比较，再区分由容量超负荷导致的呼吸困难、非心源性肺损伤和过敏反应。处理措施要跟随病理机制。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1663,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the Stage 2 findings that are significant new cues compared with the pre-transfusion baseline.","fullStemZh":"请标出阶段2中相较输血前基线具有临床意义的新线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the Stage 2 findings that are significant new cues compared with the pre-transfusion baseline.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出阶段2中相较输血前基线具有临床意义的新线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The client reports acute shortness of breath and cannot get comfortable.","zh":"患者诉突发气短，并表示怎么都不舒服。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Temperature is 99 °F (37.2 °C), compared with 98.2 °F (36.8 °C) before transfusion.","zh":"体温99 °F (37.2 °C)，输血前为98.2 °F (36.8 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Heart rate is 110/min, increased from 92/min.","zh":"心率110次/分，较92次/分升高。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Blood pressure is 168/96 mm Hg, increased from 138/82 mm Hg.","zh":"血压168/96 mm Hg，较138/82 mm Hg升高。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Respiratory rate is 28/min, increased from 16/min.","zh":"呼吸频率28次/分，较16次/分升高。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"SpO2 is 89% on room air, decreased from 96%.","zh":"室内空气SpO2为89%，较96%下降。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Bilateral crackles now extend from the bases to the mid-lung fields.","zh":"双侧湿啰音现在从肺底延伸至中肺野。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Faint bibasilar crackles were present at baseline.","zh":"基线时已有轻微双肺底湿啰音。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"A new S3 gallop is audible.","zh":"新出现可闻及S3奔马律。","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"JVD is visible at 45 degrees.","zh":"床头45度时可见颈静脉怒张。","selectable":true},{"id":"s11","en":"Lower-extremity edema has increased from trace to 2+ bilateral pitting.","zh":"下肢水肿从轻度增至双侧2+凹陷性水肿。","selectable":true},{"id":"s12","en":"The client's face is flushed without urticaria, hives, angioedema, or wheezing.","zh":"患者面部潮红，但无荨麻疹、风团、血管性水肿或喘鸣。","selectable":true},{"id":"s13","en":"Urine output is 15 mL over the past 45 minutes.","zh":"过去45分钟尿量为15 mL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s14","en":"The client has a new nonproductive cough.","zh":"患者新出现干咳。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s3","s4","s5","s6","s7","s9","s10","s11","s13","s14"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The significant new cues are acute dyspnea, tachycardia, hypertension, tachypnea, oxygen desaturation, crackles extending beyond baseline, new S3, new JVD, worsening edema, oliguria, and new cough. The small temperature change and isolated flushing without allergic features are not the main cue cluster.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有意义的新线索包括突发气短、心动过速、高血压、呼吸急促、氧饱和度下降、湿啰音超过基线范围、新S3、新颈静脉怒张、水肿加重、少尿和新咳嗽。轻微体温变化以及无过敏特征的单纯潮红不是主要线索组合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For recognize-cues items, compare each finding to the client's own baseline rather than treating every abnormal-looking value as new.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做识别线索题时，要把每个发现与患者自身基线比较，不要把所有看起来异常的数值都当作新问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1664,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"Use the Stage 2 findings to identify the most likely transfusion reaction and the strongest differentiating cue cluster.","fullStemZh":"根据阶段2表现判断最可能的输血反应及最能鉴别的线索组合。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the Stage 2 findings to identify the most likely transfusion reaction and the strongest differentiating cue cluster.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据阶段2表现判断最可能的输血反应及最能鉴别的线索组合。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The most likely reaction is {{reaction}} because the client has {{evidence}} during the transfusion.","zh":"最可能的反应是 {{reaction}}，因为患者在输血期间出现 {{evidence}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"reaction","options":[{"id":"r_anaphylaxis","en":"anaphylactic transfusion reaction","zh":"过敏性休克型输血反应"},{"id":"r_taco","en":"transfusion-associated circulatory overload","zh":"输血相关循环超负荷"},{"id":"r_trali","en":"transfusion-related acute lung injury","zh":"输血相关急性肺损伤"},{"id":"r_fnhtr","en":"febrile non-hemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"发热性非溶血性输血反应"}],"correct":"r_taco"},{"id":"evidence","options":[{"id":"e_airway_allergy","en":"angioedema, wheezing, urticaria, hypotension, and throat tightness","zh":"血管性水肿、喘鸣、荨麻疹、低血压和喉咙发紧"},{"id":"e_overload","en":"hypertension with JVD, new S3, worsening edema, pulmonary crackles, oliguria, and high-risk cardiac/renal history","zh":"高血压伴颈静脉怒张、新S3、水肿加重、肺部湿啰音、少尿，以及心肾高危病史"},{"id":"e_isolated_injury","en":"hypoxemia with bilateral infiltrates but no evidence of circulatory overload","zh":"低氧并伴双侧浸润，但无循环超负荷证据"},{"id":"e_fever","en":"fever and chills without respiratory compromise","zh":"发热和寒战，但无呼吸受损"}],"correct":"e_overload"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has acute respiratory distress during transfusion, but the differentiating pattern is circulatory overload: hypertension, JVD, S3, worsening edema, decreased urine output, crackles, older age, CKD, heart failure history, and low albumin. TRALI remains a competing respiratory transfusion reaction, but the presence of multiple volume-overload signs points away from isolated noncardiogenic lung injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者在输血期间出现急性呼吸困难，但最能鉴别的是循环超负荷模式：高血压、颈静脉怒张、S3、水肿加重、尿量减少、湿啰音、高龄、慢性肾病、心衰病史和低白蛋白。TRALI也是呼吸性输血反应的鉴别诊断，但多项容量超负荷体征使单纯非心源性肺损伤的可能性降低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When two transfusion reactions both cause dyspnea, look for the mechanism: volume-overload signs favor TACO; absence of circulatory overload with bilateral infiltrates favors TRALI.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当两种输血反应都可导致气短时，要寻找机制：容量超负荷体征支持TACO；无循环超负荷而有双侧浸润更支持TRALI。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1665,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,71],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which problem requires the nurse's most immediate response?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，哪一个问题最需要护士立即处理？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which problem requires the nurse's most immediate response?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段2，哪一个问题最需要护士立即处理？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_oliguria","en":"Decreased urine output during the second unit","zh":"第二单位输注期间尿量减少"},{"id":"q3_hypertension","en":"Hypertension of 168/96 mm Hg","zh":"血压168/96 mm Hg"},{"id":"q3_oxygenation","en":"Acute hypoxemia with respiratory distress","zh":"急性低氧伴呼吸窘迫"},{"id":"q3_anemia","en":"Ongoing symptomatic anemia after only partial transfusion","zh":"仅部分输血后仍有症状性贫血"}],"correct":["q3_oxygenation"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate threat is impaired oxygenation: SpO2 89%, RR 28, acute dyspnea, and the client's feeling of drowning. The hypertension, oliguria, and anemia matter, but oxygenation and breathing take priority while the transfusion is stopped and volume overload is treated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最直接的威胁是氧合受损：SpO2 89%、RR 28、突发气短，以及患者感觉像被淹死。高血压、少尿和贫血都重要，但在停止输血并处理容量超负荷时，氧合和呼吸优先。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use ABCs for acute deterioration. Treat the cause, but first stabilize breathing and oxygenation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到急性恶化时使用ABC原则。要处理病因，但首先稳定呼吸和氧合。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1666,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[77,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,31],"fullStemEn":"Which actions belong in the management plan for this suspected TACO episode? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"针对这次疑似TACO，哪些措施应纳入处理计划？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions belong in the management plan for this suspected TACO episode?","penultimateSentenceZh":"针对这次疑似TACO，哪些措施应纳入处理计划？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_provider_diuresis_io","en":"Notify the provider, anticipate ordered IV furosemide, and monitor intake and output closely.","zh":"通知医嘱者，预期按医嘱给予IV呋塞米，并密切监测出入量。"},{"id":"q4_stop_kvo","en":"Stop the transfusion and keep the IV line patent with normal saline using new tubing at a keep-vein-open rate.","zh":"停止输血，并用新管路以生理盐水KVO维持静脉通路通畅。"},{"id":"q4_high_fowler","en":"Place the client in high Fowler's position.","zh":"协助患者取高Fowler体位。"},{"id":"q4_oxygen","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen and monitor pulse oximetry.","zh":"给予补充氧并监测脉搏氧饱和度。"},{"id":"q4_restart_slow","en":"Restart the unit at a slower rate once the SpO2 begins to improve.","zh":"一旦SpO2开始改善，就以更慢速度重新开始该单位输血。"},{"id":"q4_fluid_bolus","en":"Administer a rapid IV fluid bolus to support circulation.","zh":"快速给予IV快速补液 以支持循环。"}],"correct":["q4_stop_kvo","q4_high_fowler","q4_oxygen","q4_provider_diuresis_io"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"TACO management begins with stopping the transfusion, maintaining IV access with new tubing, positioning upright, supporting oxygenation, notifying the provider, and using ordered diuresis with close intake/output monitoring. Restarting the transfusion or giving a fluid bolus would worsen the volume problem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"TACO处理首先包括停止输血、用新管路维持静脉通路、取坐位、支持氧合、通知医嘱者，并按医嘱利尿且密切监测出入量。重新输血或快速补液会加重容量问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match treatment to mechanism. TACO is hydrostatic volume overload, so oxygenation support and ordered diuresis fit; fluids and restarting the transfusion do not.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理措施要匹配机制。TACO是静水压性容量超负荷，因此支持氧合和按医嘱利尿合适；补液和重新输血不合适。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1667,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,50],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, classify each action as part of the first-priority concurrent RN response or as a next/protocol step after immediate stabilization begins.","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，请将每项措施分类为护士第一优先、可同时进行的立即反应，或为即时稳定开始后的后续/流程步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, classify each action as part of the first-priority concurrent RN response or as a next/protocol step after immediate stabilization begins.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段2，请将每项措施分类为护士第一优先、可同时进行的立即反应，或为即时稳定开始后的后续/流程步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r_stop","en":"Stop the transfusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止输血。"},{"id":"r_position","en":"Position the client in high Fowler's.","zh":"协助患者取高Fowler体位。"},{"id":"r_oxygen","en":"Apply high-flow oxygen for SpO2 89% with dyspnea.","zh":"因SpO2 89%且气短，给予高流量氧。"},{"id":"r_provider","en":"Notify the provider for assessment and diuretic orders.","zh":"通知医嘱者进行评估并开具利尿剂医嘱。"},{"id":"r_bloodbank","en":"Notify the blood bank and send the blood product, tubing, and ordered samples per protocol.","zh":"通知血库，并按流程送回血制品、管路和规定样本。"},{"id":"r_paperwork","en":"Complete the transfusion reaction report.","zh":"完成输血反应报告。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_first","en":"First-priority concurrent response","zh":"第一优先、同时进行的反应"},{"id":"c_next","en":"Next/protocol step","zh":"后续/流程步骤"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r_stop","columnIds":["c_first"]},{"rowId":"r_position","columnIds":["c_first"]},{"rowId":"r_oxygen","columnIds":["c_first"]},{"rowId":"r_provider","columnIds":["c_next"]},{"rowId":"r_bloodbank","columnIds":["c_next"]},{"rowId":"r_paperwork","columnIds":["c_next"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first-priority concurrent RN actions are stopping the transfusion, placing the client upright, and applying oxygen because they require no new order and directly address ongoing exposure and hypoxemia. Provider notification, blood bank notification/sample handling, and reaction reporting are essential, but they do not replace immediate stabilization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士第一优先、可同时进行的措施是停止输血、让患者坐起和给氧，因为这些不需要新医嘱，并直接处理持续暴露和低氧。通知医嘱者、通知血库/处理样本和填写反应报告都很重要，但不能取代立即稳定患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When steps are simultaneous, avoid forcing a rigid order. Identify which actions are independent, immediate, and harm-reducing, then separate protocol work that can follow.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当措施几乎同时进行时，不要强行排序。先找出独立、立即、能减少伤害的措施，再区分可随后完成的流程性工作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1668,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.288.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,32],"fullStemEn":"Which Stage 3 and Stage 4 findings best show that the TACO episode is resolving? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段3和阶段4哪些发现最能说明TACO正在缓解？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which Stage 3 and Stage 4 findings best show that the TACO episode is resolving?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段3和阶段4哪些发现最能说明TACO正在缓解？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q6_hemoglobin","en":"Post-transfusion hemoglobin is 8.1 g/dL.","zh":"输血后血红蛋白为8.1 g/dL。"},{"id":"q6_vitals_baseline","en":"RR, HR, and BP trend back toward baseline.","zh":"RR、HR和BP向基线回归。"},{"id":"q6_bnp_downtrend","en":"BNP trends down from 890 pg/mL to 420 pg/mL after treatment.","zh":"治疗后BNP从890 pg/mL下降至420 pg/mL。"},{"id":"q6_congestion_resolves","en":"JVD resolves, S3 is no longer audible, edema returns to trace, and lung sounds return to baseline.","zh":"颈静脉怒张消失、S3不再可闻及、水肿恢复至轻度、肺音回到基线。"},{"id":"q6_spo2_wean","en":"SpO2 improves from 89% to 96% while oxygen is weaned from non-rebreather to nasal cannula.","zh":"SpO2从89%改善至96%，同时氧疗从非再呼吸面罩降至鼻导管。"},{"id":"q6_urine_output","en":"Urine output reaches 1,400 mL over 4 hours after furosemide.","zh":"呋塞米后4小时尿量达到1,400 mL。"}],"correct":["q6_spo2_wean","q6_vitals_baseline","q6_urine_output","q6_congestion_resolves","q6_bnp_downtrend"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Resolution of TACO is shown by improving oxygenation with oxygen weaning, normalized respiratory and hemodynamic trends, brisk diuresis after furosemide, disappearance of congestion findings, and a falling BNP trend. Hemoglobin shows transfusion effect, not resolution of pulmonary congestion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"TACO缓解表现为氧合改善并能降阶氧疗、呼吸和血流动力学趋势恢复、呋塞米后明显利尿、淤血体征消退，以及BNP下降趋势。血红蛋白反映输血效果，而不是肺淤血是否缓解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate the outcome that matches the problem. For overload, look for removal of volume and reversal of congestion, not just a successful hemoglobin rise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果要对应问题。对于容量超负荷，要看容量排出和淤血逆转，而不只是血红蛋白上升。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1669,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_taco_vs_trali_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.289","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.289.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.289.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[467,580],"terminalOffsetsZh":[154,186],"fullStemEn":"After the transfusion is stopped, a 74-year-old client with CKD and compensated heart failure has improving dyspnea after oxygen, upright positioning, and ordered IV furosemide. During the second unit she developed SpO2 89% on room air, BP 168/96, JVD, new S3, worsening 2+ edema, oliguria, and bilateral crackles. Chest X-ray shows pulmonary vascular congestion, small pleural effusions, cardiomegaly, and a widened vascular pedicle. BNP rose from 280 to 890 pg/mL. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"停止输血后，一名74岁慢性肾病并代偿期心衰患者在吸氧、坐位和按医嘱IV呋塞米后气短有所改善。第二单位输注期间，她出现室内空气SpO2 89%、BP 168/96、颈静脉怒张、新S3、2+水肿加重、少尿和双侧湿啰音。胸片显示肺血管淤血、少量胸腔积液、心影增大和血管蒂增宽。BNP从280升至890 pg/mL。请完成弓形题：选择最可能状况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题：选择最可能状况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"BNP rose from 280 to 890 pg/mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"BNP从280升至890 pg/mL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_anaphylaxis","en":"Anaphylactic transfusion reaction","zh":"过敏性休克型输血反应"},{"id":"cond_taco","en":"Transfusion-associated circulatory overload","zh":"输血相关循环超负荷"},{"id":"cond_trali","en":"Transfusion-related acute lung injury","zh":"输血相关急性肺损伤"}],"correct":"cond_taco"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_oxygen_position","en":"Maintain high Fowler's position with supplemental oxygen and close respiratory monitoring","zh":"维持高Fowler体位、补充氧并密切监测呼吸状态"},{"id":"act_iv_bolus","en":"Administer IV fluid bolus to support blood pressure","zh":"给予IV快速补液 以支持血压"},{"id":"act_restart_slow","en":"Resume the transfusion at a slower rate once SpO2 improves","zh":"SpO2改善后以较慢速度恢复输血"},{"id":"act_furosemide_io","en":"Administer ordered IV furosemide and monitor urine output","zh":"按医嘱给予IV呋塞米并监测尿量"}],"correct":["act_oxygen_position","act_furosemide_io"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_urine_output","en":"Urine output after diuretic therapy","zh":"利尿治疗后的尿量"},{"id":"param_temperature","en":"Temperature trend as the main marker of resolution","zh":"将体温趋势作为缓解的主要指标"},{"id":"param_spo2_wean","en":"SpO2 trend and ability to wean supplemental oxygen","zh":"SpO2趋势和能否降低氧疗强度"},{"id":"param_hemoglobin","en":"Post-transfusion hemoglobin as the main marker of reaction resolution","zh":"将输血后血红蛋白作为反应缓解的主要指标"}],"correct":["param_spo2_wean","param_urine_output"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is TACO because the respiratory compromise occurs with hypertension, elevated filling-pressure findings, peripheral edema, pulmonary vascular congestion, cardiomegaly, BNP rise, and response to diuresis. Priorities are oxygenation/positioning and ordered diuresis with urine-output monitoring. The most useful monitoring parameters are oxygenation with weaning ability and urine output, because they track pulmonary improvement and volume removal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能状况是TACO，因为呼吸受损同时伴高血压、充盈压升高表现、外周水肿、肺血管淤血、心影增大、BNP升高以及利尿后改善。优先措施是改善氧合/体位和按医嘱利尿并监测尿量。最有用的监测参数是氧合及能否降阶氧疗、尿量，因为它们反映肺部改善和容量排出。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, lock the condition to the strongest cue cluster first, then choose actions and monitoring that match that condition's physiology.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，先用最强线索组合锁定状况，再选择符合该状况生理机制的措施和监测指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1670,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.290","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.290.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[910,982],"terminalOffsetsZh":[283,311],"fullStemEn":"Unsafe assignment outside validated competency for a floated medical-surgical nurse Nurse Dara Okonkwo, RN, BSN, has worked on a 36-bed medical-surgical unit for four years. Her competency file documents validation in telemetry monitoring, PCA pump management, chest-tube care, and routine post-operative assessment. She has never been validated for vasoactive medication titration, hemodynamic monitoring via arterial lines, or neurological assessment protocols specific to the step-down (intermediate care) unit. Her facility's float policy states: \"Floated nurses shall receive assignments consistent with their documented competencies. When patient acuity exceeds the float nurse's validated skills, the charge nurse must adjust the assignment or arrange for competency-matched support.\"\n\nTonight is a twelve-hour night shift during a hospital-wide staffing surge caused by a respiratory illness outbreak. The house supervisor floats Nurse Okonkwo to the step-down unit at 1845.","fullStemZh":"内外科护士被调配至超出其已验证胜任力范围的不安全排班 Dara Okonkwo护士（RN，BSN）在一个有36张床位的内外科病房工作了四年。她的胜任力档案记录了她在遥测监护、PCA泵管理、胸腔引流管护理和常规术后评估方面的资格。她从未获得过血管活性药物滴定、动脉导管血流动力学监测或特级护理（降级）病房特定神经评估方案的验证。她所在机构的调配政策规定：“被调配的护士应接受与其记录的胜任力一致的工作分配。当患者病情超出了被调配护士已验证的技能时，值班主管护士必须调整排班或安排胜任力匹配的支援。”\n\n今晚是一个12小时的夜班，当时由于呼吸道疾病暴发导致全院人手紧缺。总值班主管在1845将Okonkwo护士调配至降级病房。","terminalSentenceEn":"The house supervisor floats Nurse Okonkwo to the step-down unit at 1845.","terminalSentenceZh":"总值班主管在1845将Okonkwo护士调配至降级病房。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Tonight is a twelve-hour night shift during a hospital-wide staffing surge caused by a respiratory illness outbreak.","penultimateSentenceZh":"今晚是一个12小时的夜班，当时由于呼吸道疾病暴发导致全院人手紧缺。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Float nurses frequently face assignments outside their documented competencies. The priority is recognizing when an assignment requires specific validated competencies the nurse lacks (e.g., vasoactive titration, advanced neuro protocols). The nurse has a duty to refuse unsafe aspects of the assignment while continuing care for patients within their competency. Escalating structural concerns through the chain of command ensures patient safety, and objective documentation protects the nurse and patient.","rationaleCorrectZh":"调配护士经常面临超出其记录的胜任力的工作分配。首要任务是识别一项排班任务需要护士所缺乏的特定已验证胜任力时（例如，血管活性药物滴定、高级神经方案）。护士有责任拒绝排班中不安全的部分，同时继续护理其能力范围内的患者。通过指挥链（上报机制）逐级上报结构性隐患可确保患者安全，而客观的记录则能保护护士和患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the root cause of the risk—a mismatch between required competencies and the nurse's training—and prioritize actions that address the system problem while maintaining safe care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"找出风险的根本原因——所需胜任力与护士所受培训之间的不匹配——并优先采取解决系统问题同时维持安全护理的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1671,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[187,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,54],"fullStemEn":"The nurse identifies that the assigned patient load presents a significant safety concern. Which of the following findings from the initial rounds and shift report confirm this mismatch? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士发现所分配的工作量存在重大的安全隐患。初始查房和交班报告中的哪些发现证实了这种不匹配？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following findings from the initial rounds and shift report confirm this mismatch?","penultimateSentenceZh":"初始查房和交班报告中的哪些发现证实了这种不匹配？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q1_o4","en":"Client A's blood pressure is monitored via an arterial line.","zh":"患者A通过动脉导管监测血压。"},{"id":"q1_o2","en":"Client B requires an hourly neuro assessment with unfamiliar grading criteria.","zh":"患者B需要每小时进行一次神经评估，且评分标准不熟悉。"},{"id":"q1_o5","en":"All three clients are hemodynamically stable at the start of the shift.","zh":"在交班开始时，所有三名患者的血流动力学均稳定。"},{"id":"q1_o3","en":"Client C requires a continuous passive motion machine.","zh":"患者C需要持续被动运动机器。"},{"id":"q1_o1","en":"Client A requires active norepinephrine titration.","zh":"患者A需要积极滴定去甲肾上腺素。"}],"correct":["q1_o1","q1_o2","q1_o4"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The significant cues are the mismatch between the nurse's documented competencies and the care requirements of Clients A and B. Specifically, the nurse is not validated to manage vasoactive titration orders, arterial lines, or the unit's unfamiliar structured neuro protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重要线索是护士已记录的胜任力与患者A和B的护理需求之间不匹配。具体而言，该护士未获得管理血管活性药物滴定医嘱、动脉导管或该病房不熟悉的结构化神经方案的验证。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the specific interventions ordered that fall outside the nurse's documented competency list.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注所开出的超出护士已记录的胜任力列表的特定干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1672,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[145,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,67],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse tells Nurse Okonkwo, \"The drips are already set — just don't change them. If something goes wrong, call me and I'll come help.\" Why does this instruction fail to resolve the safety concern?","fullStemZh":"值班主管护士告诉Okonkwo护士，“滴注已经设置好了——别去动它们。如果出问题，叫我，我会来帮忙。”为什么这个指示未能解决安全隐患？","terminalSentenceEn":"Why does this instruction fail to resolve the safety concern?","terminalSentenceZh":"为什么这个指示未能解决安全隐患？","penultimateSentenceEn":"If something goes wrong, call me and I'll come help.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果出问题，叫我，我会来帮忙。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q2_o1","en":"Vasoactive drips are dynamic and require the primary nurse to independently recognize the need for and perform timely titrations.","zh":"血管活性滴注是动态的，要求责任护士独立识别需求并及时进行滴定。"},{"id":"q2_o4","en":"Nurse Okonkwo is not willing to accept any assignment on the step-down unit.","zh":"Okonkwo护士不愿意接受降级病房的任何排班任务。"},{"id":"q2_o2","en":"The charge nurse does not have the authority to alter an assignment made by the house supervisor.","zh":"值班主管护士无权更改总值班主管所做的排班。"},{"id":"q2_o3","en":"The float policy prohibits a float nurse from caring for any patient receiving an intravenous drip.","zh":"调配政策禁止调配护士护理任何正在接受静脉滴注的患者。"}],"correct":["q2_o1"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The charge nurse's statement incorrectly assumes vasoactive drips do not need adjustment. Because hemodynamic status fluctuates, the primary nurse must be competent to titrate the drips independently. Relying on a charge nurse for titrations introduces delays and fails to resolve the safety risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"值班主管护士的说法错误地假设了血管活性滴注不需要调整。由于血流动力学状态会波动，责任护士必须能胜任独立滴定。依赖主管护士进行滴定会导致延误，并且无法解决安全风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze the clinical reality of the ordered interventions. Vasoactive drips are not 'set and forget'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析医嘱干预措施的临床现实。血管活性滴注不是“一设了之”的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"If something goes wrong, call me and I'll come help.\"","controlSentenceZh":"如果出问题，叫我，我会来帮忙。”"}
{"queueIndex":1673,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,50],"fullStemEn":"After Nurse Okonkwo has reported the immediate patient-specific changes to a qualified nurse, what management-of-care problem is the priority to correct?","fullStemZh":"在Okonkwo护士向符合资质的护士报告了即刻特定于患者的病情变化后，首要纠正的管理护理问题是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"After Nurse Okonkwo has reported the immediate patient-specific changes to a qualified nurse, what management-of-care problem is the priority to correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"在Okonkwo护士向符合资质的护士报告了即刻特定于患者的病情变化后，首要纠正的管理护理问题是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_o1","en":"The charge nurse's delayed response time to bedside pages.","zh":"值班主管护士对床边呼叫响应延迟。"},{"id":"q3_o4","en":"Client A's increasing chest tube drainage.","zh":"患者A胸腔引流管引流量增加。"},{"id":"q3_o3","en":"The unsafe structure of the assignment leaving a non-validated nurse as primary caregiver.","zh":"让未经资格验证的护士担任主要护理人员的不安全排班结构。"},{"id":"q3_o2","en":"Client B's potential neurological deterioration.","zh":"患者B潜在的神经功能恶化。"}],"correct":["q3_o3"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority problem is the unsafe assignment structure itself, not any single patient's current vital signs. The individual clinical events are symptoms of the underlying issue: assigning patients to a nurse who lacks the required competencies, resulting in a reactive and delayed pattern of care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要问题是不安全的排班结构本身，而不是任何单一患者当前的生命体征。个别临床事件是潜在问题的症状：将患者分配给缺乏必要胜任力的护士，导致被动和延迟的护理模式。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the systemic issue that connects all the individual clinical problems.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找将所有个体临床问题联系起来的系统性问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1674,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,40],"fullStemEn":"Nurse Okonkwo decides to address the unsafe assignment. Which actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"Okonkwo护士决定解决不安全排班的问题。哪些行动是恰当的？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些行动是恰当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_o5","en":"Propose a safe alternative, such as reassignment of Clients A and B to a validated nurse.","zh":"提出一个安全的替代方案，例如将患者A和B重新分配给已获得资格验证的护士。"},{"id":"q4_o1","en":"Continue providing care for Client C.","zh":"继续为患者C提供护理。"},{"id":"q4_o2","en":"Refuse all patient care and leave the unit immediately.","zh":"拒绝所有的患者护理并立即离开病房。"},{"id":"q4_o4","en":"Call the on-call provider to complain about the staffing assignment.","zh":"打电话给值班医生，抱怨人手分配问题。"},{"id":"q4_o3","en":"Escalate the concern to the nursing supervisor.","zh":"将问题上报给护理主管。"}],"correct":["q4_o1","q4_o3","q4_o5"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The appropriate actions resolve the two conflicting obligations: continuing care within competency while escalating the structural problem. The nurse should continue caring for Client C to avoid abandonment, propose a safe reassignment alternative, and escalate the unresolved concern through the nursing chain of command.","rationaleCorrectZh":"恰当的行动解决了两项相互冲突的义务：在胜任力范围内继续护理，同时上报结构性问题。护士应继续护理患者C以避免遗弃患者，提出安全的重新排班替代方案，并通过护理指挥链（上报机制）上报未解决的隐患。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select options that maintain patient safety within competency and follow the nursing chain of command.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择在胜任力范围内维护患者安全并遵循护理指挥链（上报机制）的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1675,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[55,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,51],"fullStemEn":"Nurse Okonkwo prepares to speak with Supervisor Huang. Evaluate each statement she could make during this call as either 'Appropriate' or 'Inappropriate'.","fullStemZh":"Okonkwo护士准备与主管Huang谈话。评估她在通话中可能发表的每项陈述是“恰当”还是“不恰当”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Evaluate each statement she could make during this call as either 'Appropriate' or 'Inappropriate'.","terminalSentenceZh":"评估她在通话中可能发表的每项陈述是“恰当”还是“不恰当”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Nurse Okonkwo prepares to speak with Supervisor Huang.","penultimateSentenceZh":"Okonkwo护士准备与主管Huang谈话。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"selectionMode":"single_per_row","columns":[{"id":"col_app","en":"Appropriate","zh":"恰当"},{"id":"col_inapp","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不恰当"}],"rows":[{"id":"row_1","en":"\"I have not been validated to titrate vasoactive drips or manage arterial lines.\"","zh":"“我尚未获得滴定血管活性药物或管理动脉导管的资格验证。”"},{"id":"row_2","en":"\"Marcus is being dismissive and lazy because he doesn't want to change the assignment.\"","zh":"“Marcus态度敷衍又懒惰，因为他不想更改排班。”"},{"id":"row_3","en":"\"I can continue caring for Client C, but Clients A and B require a validated nurse.\"","zh":"“我可以继续护理患者C，但患者A和B需要获得资格验证的护士。”"},{"id":"row_4","en":"\"There was a twelve-minute delay when I needed the charge nurse to evaluate a blood pressure parameter.\"","zh":"“当需要主管护士来评估一项血压参数时，耽搁了十二分钟。”"}]},"correct":[{"rowId":"row_1","columnIds":["col_app"]},{"rowId":"row_2","columnIds":["col_inapp"]},{"rowId":"row_3","columnIds":["col_app"]},{"rowId":"row_4","columnIds":["col_app"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective chain-of-command communication is factual, specific, and solution-oriented. Providing concrete evidence of the competency gap and its consequences is appropriate, whereas assigning emotional motives or blame is unprofessional.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的指挥链（上报机制）沟通是基于事实、具体且以解决问题为导向的。提供有关胜任力差距及其后果的具体证据是恰当的，而主观推断动机或指责则是不专业的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Effective professional communication is objective, factual, and focused on safety, avoiding emotional or accusatory language.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有效的专业沟通应当是客观、基于事实且关注安全的，避免使用情绪化或指责性的语言。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1676,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.290.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,37],"fullStemEn":"At 2200, Nurse Okonkwo completes her documentation regarding the assignment concern. Which action is correct?","fullStemZh":"在2200，Okonkwo护士完成了有关排班隐患的记录。哪项行动是正确的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项行动是正确的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 2200, Nurse Okonkwo completes her documentation regarding the assignment concern.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在2200，Okonkwo护士完成了有关排班隐患的记录。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q6_o1","en":"Document in the patient chart that an incident report was filed regarding the unsafe assignment.","zh":"在患者病历中记录针对不安全排班已提交事件报告。"},{"id":"q6_o2","en":"Document factual details of patient assessments, exact notification times, the delayed response time, and the handoff to the relieving nurse.","zh":"记录患者评估的事实细节、确切的通知时间、延迟响应的时间，以及与接班护士的交接。"},{"id":"q6_o3","en":"Document the patient findings but omit the 12-minute delay in charge nurse response to protect unit liability.","zh":"记录患者的评估结果，但省略主管护士延迟响应的12分钟，以保护科室免受责任追究。"},{"id":"q6_o4","en":"Complete a single comprehensive variance report covering all patients instead of charting the events in the individual patient medical records.","zh":"完成一份涵盖所有患者的综合差异报告，而不是将事件记录在个别患者的病历中。"}],"correct":["q6_o2"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Patient medical records should contain objective clinical facts and a clear timeline of care. The nurse must chart accurate assessments, the times providers or charge nurses were notified, delayed responses, and handoff details. Subjective blame or omissions compromise the medical record.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者病历应包含客观的临床事实和清晰的护理时间表。护士必须准确记录评估结果、通知医生或主管护士的时间、延迟响应以及交接细节。主观的指责或遗漏会损害病历的完整性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the option that focuses strictly on objective, chronological, and patient-centered facts without adding emotional or subjective commentary.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择严格关注客观、按时间顺序和以患者为中心的事实的选项，不要添加情感或主观的评论。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1677,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_assignment_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.291","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.291.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.291.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[335,368],"terminalOffsetsZh":[103,113],"fullStemEn":"A medical-surgical float nurse receives an assignment on a step-down unit that includes patients requiring vasoactive drip titration and advanced neurological assessments, which are not within her documented competencies. The charge nurse refuses to change the assignment, telling her to simply call him if she needs to adjust a drip. What should the nurse prioritize?","fullStemZh":"一名内外科调配护士在降级病房收到了一份排班任务，其中包括需要滴定血管活性滴注药物和进行高级神经评估的患者，而这些并不在她的记录胜任力范围内。值班主管护士拒绝更改排班，告诉她如果需要调整滴注，直接呼叫他就行。护士应优先考虑什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What should the nurse prioritize?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先考虑什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse refuses to change the assignment, telling her to simply call him if she needs to adjust a drip.","penultimateSentenceZh":"值班主管护士拒绝更改排班，告诉她如果需要调整滴注，直接呼叫他就行。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_3","en":"Inadequate staffing requiring the nurse to manage with available resources","zh":"人手不足，要求护士利用现有资源进行管理"},{"id":"cond_1","en":"Unsafe assignment outside the nurse's validated competency","zh":"超出护士已验证胜任力的不安全排班"},{"id":"cond_2","en":"Nurse unwillingness to accept a float assignment","zh":"护士不愿意接受调配排班"}],"correct":"cond_1"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_3","en":"Refuse all patient care and leave the unit","zh":"拒绝所有的患者护理并离开病房"},{"id":"act_4","en":"Accept the full assignment without escalation","zh":"在不上报的情况下接受完整的排班任务"},{"id":"act_2","en":"Continue providing care for patients whose needs are within her validated competencies","zh":"继续为护理需求在其已验证胜任力范围内的患者提供护理"},{"id":"act_1","en":"Escalate through the chain of command to the nursing supervisor","zh":"通过指挥链上报至护理主管"}],"correct":["act_1","act_2"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_1","en":"Whether the high-acuity patients are reassigned to a validated nurse","zh":"高危患者是否被重新分配给具备资格的护士"},{"id":"param_4","en":"Whether the charge nurse expresses agreement with the reassignment","zh":"值班主管护士是否表示同意重新排班"},{"id":"param_2","en":"Whether the nurse's remaining assignment consists entirely of patients within her documented competencies","zh":"护士剩余的排班任务是否完全由其胜任力范围内的患者组成"},{"id":"param_3","en":"Whether the patient's MAP remains stable after the norepinephrine increase","zh":"去甲肾上腺素增加后，患者的平均动脉压 (MAP) 是否保持稳定"}],"correct":["param_1","param_2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The root cause of the safety concern is the structural mismatch between the nurse's documented competencies and the clinical interventions required by the assigned patients. Continuing care within competency prevents patient abandonment, while escalating the structural issue through the chain of command ensures patient safety.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全隐患的根本原因是护士已记录的胜任力与所分配患者所需的临床干预措施之间存在结构性不匹配。在其能力范围内继续护理可防止遗弃患者，同时通过指挥链（上报机制）上报该结构性问题以确保患者安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the unsafe situation, advocate through proper channels, and do not abandon care that is within your validated competency.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别不安全的情况，通过适当的渠道进行倡导，并且不要放弃在您已验证的胜任力范围内的护理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1678,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.292","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.292.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[207,338],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,111],"fullStemEn":"Multiple HIPAA disclosure events during one shift Mrs. Elaine Torrance, a 58-year-old postoperative orthopedic client, is stable after open reduction and internal fixation of a left tibial plateau fracture. During the day shift, RN Jordan must recognize, contain, report, and evaluate several privacy risks and unauthorized PHI exposures.","fullStemZh":"同一班次内发生多起HIPAA披露事件 Elaine Torrance女士，58岁，因左胫骨平台骨折行切开复位内固定术后，目前病情稳定。白班期间，Jordan护士必须识别、控制、上报并评价多起隐私风险和未经授权的PHI暴露。","terminalSentenceEn":"During the day shift, RN Jordan must recognize, contain, report, and evaluate several privacy risks and unauthorized PHI exposures.","terminalSentenceZh":"白班期间，Jordan护士必须识别、控制、上报并评价多起隐私风险和未经授权的PHI暴露。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Elaine Torrance, a 58-year-old postoperative orthopedic client, is stable after open reduction and internal fixation of a left tibial plateau fracture.","penultimateSentenceZh":"同一班次内发生多起HIPAA披露事件 Elaine Torrance女士，58岁，因左胫骨平台骨折行切开复位内固定术后，目前病情稳定。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests real-time recognition and response to multiple privacy problems. The nurse must identify unauthorized access, unverified external requests, identifiable images on personal devices, and verbal disclosures without reasonable safeguards. The priority completed exposure is RN Casey's curiosity-based EHR access, which requires immediate containment and formal breach-response reporting. Appropriate management includes refusing unauthorized disclosure, redirecting records requests to HIM, deleting and reporting the student photo, moving report to a private area, notifying the charge nurse and Privacy Officer, preserving audit evidence, and keeping incident reports out of the medical record.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查护士对多起隐私问题的实时识别和处理。护士必须识别未经授权访问、未核实的外部请求、个人设备上的可识别照片，以及未采取合理保护措施的口头披露。最优先且已发生的暴露是Casey护士因好奇访问电子病历，需要立即控制并正式上报。适当处理包括拒绝未授权披露、将病历请求转给HIM、删除并上报护生照片、将交班移到私密区域、通知 charge nurse 和隐私官、保留审计证据，并且不要把事件报告写入病历。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In HIPAA items, do not assume disclosure is harmless because the person seems involved. Verify authorization, limit access to job-related need, contain active exposure first, and use the facility reporting chain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做HIPAA题时，不要因为对方看似相关就认为披露无害。要核实授权，将访问限制在工作需要内，先控制正在发生的暴露，并使用机构上报链。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Elaine Torrance, a 58-year-old postoperative orthopedic client, is stable after open reduction and internal fixation of a left tibial plateau fracture.","controlSentenceZh":"同一班次内发生多起HIPAA披露事件 Elaine Torrance女士，58岁，因左胫骨平台骨折行切开复位内固定术后，目前病情稳定。"}
{"queueIndex":1679,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"Which events from the morning require privacy follow-up by RN Jordan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"上午发生的哪些事件需要Jordan护士进行隐私相关跟进？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which events from the morning require privacy follow-up by RN Jordan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"上午发生的哪些事件需要Jordan护士进行隐私相关跟进？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q1_f","en":"Mrs. Torrance reports pain of 4 out of 10 while the nurse performs the routine morning assessment.","zh":"护士进行常规晨间评估时，Torrance女士报告疼痛4/10。"},{"id":"q1_b","en":"RN Casey opens Mrs. Torrance's operative report and medication record out of curiosity without a care role.","zh":"Casey护士没有照护职责，却因好奇打开Torrance女士的手术记录和用药记录。"},{"id":"q1_a","en":"A caller who is not listed as an authorized contact asks for Mrs. Torrance's laboratory results and discharge timing.","zh":"未列为授权联系人的来电者要求得知Torrance女士的化验结果和出院时间。"},{"id":"q1_d","en":"A nursing student photographs the wound on a personal phone with the hospital identification band visible.","zh":"护生用个人手机拍摄伤口照片，且照片中能看到医院身份腕带。"},{"id":"q1_c","en":"The employer faxes the nursing unit requesting admission records and operative reports without a signed authorization.","zh":"雇主将索取入院记录和手术报告的传真发到护理单元，但未附患者签署的授权书。"},{"id":"q1_e","en":"Two nurses discuss another client's HIV status by name in the hallway where a visitor can hear.","zh":"两名护士在走廊按姓名讨论另一名患者的HIV状态，旁边访客能够听见。"}],"correct":["q1_a","q1_b","q1_c","q1_d","q1_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The unverified caller, curiosity-driven chart access, unauthorised employer request, identifiable photo on a personal device, and hallway report all create actual or potential privacy violations. The pain report during routine assessment is ordinary patient-care information used by the assigned nurse and is not itself a privacy event.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未核实且未授权的来电、因好奇查看病历、雇主未授权索取病历、在个人设备上形成可识别患者身份的照片，以及在走廊可被旁人听到的交班，均属于实际或潜在隐私问题。常规评估中的疼痛报告是负责护士用于照护的信息，本身不是隐私事件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate routine care from disclosure risk. Ask whether an unauthorized person accessed, received, or could hear identifiable health information.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把常规照护与披露风险分开判断。重点看是否有未授权人员访问、接收或可能听到可识别的健康信息。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1680,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,55],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Classify each privacy event using the best description.","fullStemZh":"用最恰当的描述对每个隐私事件进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each privacy event using the best description.","terminalSentenceZh":"用最恰当的描述对每个隐私事件进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q2_r1","en":"RN Casey's curiosity-based EHR access","zh":"Casey护士因好奇访问电子病历"},{"id":"q2_r2","en":"Student's identifiable wound photograph on a personal phone","zh":"护生用个人手机拍摄可识别身份的伤口照片"},{"id":"q2_r3","en":"Employer fax asking for records without authorization","zh":"雇主无授权传真索取病历"},{"id":"q2_r4","en":"Caller claiming to be the patient's husband asks for results","zh":"自称患者丈夫的来电者索要结果"},{"id":"q2_r5","en":"Hallway report about another patient's HIV status","zh":"走廊交班谈及另一名患者HIV状态"}],"columns":[{"id":"q2_c1","en":"Completed impermissible access or identifiable record as it occurred","zh":"已经发生的未经允许访问或形成可识别记录"},{"id":"q2_c2","en":"Conditionally permissible only after authorization or legal basis is verified through the proper process","zh":"只有通过正确流程核实授权或法律依据后才可能允许"},{"id":"q2_c3","en":"Verbal incidental disclosure risk because reasonable safeguards were not used","zh":"因未采取合理保护措施造成的口头偶然披露风险"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q2_r1","columnIds":["q2_c1"]},{"rowId":"q2_r2","columnIds":["q2_c1"]},{"rowId":"q2_r3","columnIds":["q2_c2"]},{"rowId":"q2_r4","columnIds":["q2_c2"]},{"rowId":"q2_r5","columnIds":["q2_c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"RN Casey's access and the student's identifiable photo are completed impermissible events as they occurred. The employer and phone requests might be handled only through proper authorization or legal authority, but they are not disclosures the unit nurse can make as presented. The hallway report is a verbal disclosure risk because staff failed to use reasonable safeguards in a public area.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Casey护士访问病历和护生拍摄可识别照片，是已经发生的不当事件。雇主和电话请求只有在通过正确流程确认授权或法律依据后才可能处理，但按目前情形护理单元不能披露。走廊交班属于口头披露风险，因为工作人员在公共区域未采取合理保护措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Classify the event by the pathway: internal access, external request, or verbal communication. Then ask whether the proper authorization, role, or safeguard exists.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先按路径分类：内部访问、外部请求或口头沟通。再判断是否存在适当授权、工作角色或保护措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1681,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,37],"fullStemEn":"Which event is the clearest completed, non-incidental unauthorized access that requires formal breach-response investigation?","fullStemZh":"哪一项是最明确、已经发生且非偶然的未经授权访问，需要启动正式隐私事件调查？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which event is the clearest completed, non-incidental unauthorized access that requires formal breach-response investigation?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一项是最明确、已经发生且非偶然的未经授权访问，需要启动正式隐私事件调查？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_e","en":"The student's photograph that is still on one device and has not yet been transmitted","zh":"护生照片仍在一台设备上且尚未传送"},{"id":"q3_a","en":"RN Casey's unauthorized access to Mrs. Torrance's EHR","zh":"Casey护士未经授权访问Torrance女士的电子病历"},{"id":"q3_b","en":"The unverified caller's request for results before any information is released","zh":"未核实来电者在信息尚未披露前索要结果"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Mrs. Torrance's concern that her employer may learn details of her condition","zh":"Torrance女士担心雇主会得知她病情细节"},{"id":"q3_c","en":"The employer's fax request before any records are released","zh":"雇主在尚未释放病历前发来的传真请求"}],"correct":["q3_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"RN Casey intentionally opened Mrs. Torrance's operative report and MAR without any care, consultation, payment, or operations role. That is a completed exposure of PHI by a workforce member and requires immediate containment and formal reporting. The photo is also serious, but the skeleton frames RN Casey's EHR access as the broader, logged access with ongoing system-risk implications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Casey护士在没有照护、会诊、付款或运营职责的情况下，故意打开Torrance女士的手术记录和MAR。这是工作人员已完成的PHI暴露，需要立即控制并正式上报。照片同样严重，但本病例将Casey护士的电子病历访问设定为范围更广、可由审计追踪且有持续系统风险的优先事件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several privacy problems occur, prioritize the completed exposure with the broadest scope and ongoing system access risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"多个隐私问题同时发生时，优先处理已经发生、范围较广且有持续系统访问风险的暴露。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1682,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,108],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,34],"fullStemEn":"Which actions should RN Jordan include in the response to the morning privacy events? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"Jordan护士应将哪些措施纳入上午隐私事件的处理？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should RN Jordan include in the response to the morning privacy events?","penultimateSentenceZh":"Jordan护士应将哪些措施纳入上午隐私事件的处理？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_c","en":"Secure the employer fax and redirect the request to HIM rather than releasing records from the nursing unit.","zh":"妥善保管雇主传真并将请求转给HIM，不从护理单元释放病历。"},{"id":"q4_d","en":"Have the student delete the identifiable photo, including recently deleted storage, in the presence of RN Jordan and the instructor; report for Privacy Officer follow-up.","zh":"让护生在Jordan护士和指导老师在场时删除可识别照片，包括最近删除文件夹；并上报由隐私官跟进。"},{"id":"q4_f","en":"Document in Mrs. Torrance's medical record that incident reports were filed for the privacy breaches.","zh":"在Torrance女士病历中记录已为隐私泄露提交事件报告。"},{"id":"q4_e","en":"Interrupt the hallway report and move the nurses to a private space to finish patient-specific communication.","zh":"打断走廊交班，让护士转到私密空间完成涉及患者的信息沟通。"},{"id":"q4_a","en":"Release no information to Robert; ask Mrs. Torrance whether she authorizes him and document her restriction if she declines.","zh":"不向Robert透露信息；询问Torrance女士是否授权他接收信息，如拒绝则记录她的限制。"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"Ask RN Casey to exit the chart, notify the charge nurse, complete the incident report, and keep the report out of the medical record.","zh":"要求Casey护士退出病历，通知 charge nurse，完成事件报告，并且不要把事件报告写入病历。"}],"correct":["q4_a","q4_b","q4_c","q4_d","q4_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct response combines immediate mitigation, proper reporting, and prevention of further disclosure for each event. The nurse should not reference the incident report in the patient's medical record because the incident report is a quality-improvement/risk-management document kept separate from clinical documentation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确处理包括对每个事件立即控制暴露、按正确链条上报，并防止进一步披露。护士不能在患者病历中提及事件报告，因为事件报告属于质量改进/风险管理文件，应与临床病历分开保存。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For privacy events, choose actions that contain the exposure and route the issue to the correct reporting channel. Reject actions that put risk-management documents in the chart.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理隐私事件时，选择能控制暴露并把问题送入正确上报渠道的措施。排除把风险管理文件写入病历的做法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1683,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,52],"fullStemEn":"RN Jordan sees RN Casey actively viewing Mrs. Torrance's record without a care role. What is the nurse's first action?","fullStemZh":"Jordan护士看到Casey护士正在无照护职责地查看Torrance女士病历。护士的第一步行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's first action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的第一步行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Torrance's record without a care role.","penultimateSentenceZh":"Jordan护士看到Casey护士正在无照护职责地查看Torrance女士病历。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q5_a","en":"Ask RN Casey to close the record or log out immediately, then notify the charge nurse and follow the breach-reporting chain.","zh":"立即要求Casey护士关闭病历或退出登录，然后通知 charge nurse 并按隐私事件上报链处理。"},{"id":"q5_c","en":"Tell RN Casey that discipline will be imposed and require her to write an apology to the patient.","zh":"告诉Casey护士将受到纪律处分，并要求她给患者写道歉信。"},{"id":"q5_b","en":"Complete the electronic incident report first, then tell the charge nurse after the report is submitted.","zh":"先完成电子事件报告，提交后再告知 charge nurse。"},{"id":"q5_d","en":"Wait until the end of the shift so all privacy events can be reported together.","zh":"等到本班结束后，将所有隐私事件一起上报。"}],"correct":["q5_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first step is immediate mitigation: stop the active unauthorized access by having RN Casey leave the record. The nurse then notifies the charge nurse and follows the facility's reporting chain. Discipline and patient notification are handled through management and the Privacy Officer's process, not by the discovering nurse acting independently.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步是立即减轻/控制暴露：让Casey护士离开病历，停止正在发生的未经授权访问。随后通知 charge nurse，并按机构上报链处理。纪律处分和正式通知患者应由管理层和隐私官流程处理，而不是发现事件的护士自行处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The first action for an active breach is containment, not paperwork or discipline. Stop the exposure before moving through the reporting chain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"正在发生的隐私事件，第一步是控制暴露，不是先做文书或处分。先停止暴露，再进入上报流程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1684,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.292.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,34],"fullStemEn":"Which findings best show that the privacy events have been contained and appropriately reported? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些发现最能说明这些隐私事件已被控制并得到适当上报？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings best show that the privacy events have been contained and appropriately reported?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现最能说明这些隐私事件已被控制并得到适当上报？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q6_e","en":"Mrs. Torrance's postoperative vital signs remain stable and the wound dressing is clean and dry.","zh":"Torrance女士术后生命体征稳定，伤口敷料清洁干燥。"},{"id":"q6_b","en":"The Privacy Officer has started the breach-determination process and preserved the EHR audit trail.","zh":"隐私官已启动隐私事件判定流程，并保留电子病历审计追踪。"},{"id":"q6_f","en":"Robert has not called back by the end of the shift, so the breach response is complete.","zh":"Robert在本班结束前没有再来电，因此隐私事件处理已完成。"},{"id":"q6_c","en":"No PHI was released to Robert or to the employer from the nursing unit.","zh":"护理单元未向Robert或雇主释放PHI。"},{"id":"q6_d","en":"The student's photo was deleted and reported for investigation of possible cloud syncing, and the nursing program was notified.","zh":"护生照片已删除，并已上报调查可能的云端同步；护理项目也已获通知。"},{"id":"q6_a","en":"Incident reports are complete and are not referenced in Mrs. Torrance's medical record.","zh":"事件报告已完成，且未在Torrance女士病历中提及。"}],"correct":["q6_a","q6_b","q6_c","q6_d"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate outcomes focus on containment, reporting, Privacy Officer investigation, audit-trail preservation, and prevention of unauthorized release. Stable postoperative findings are clinically good but do not evaluate the privacy response. Whether Robert calls again does not determine whether the required breach-response steps were completed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当结局应关注暴露是否被控制、是否完成上报、隐私官是否调查、审计追踪是否保存，以及是否防止未经授权披露。术后稳定是好的临床情况，但不能评价隐私事件处理。Robert是否再次来电，也不能决定必需的隐私事件处理步骤是否完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate privacy outcomes with privacy-process evidence, not physiologic stability. Look for containment, reporting, investigation, and prevention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价隐私事件结局要看隐私流程证据，而不是生理稳定。寻找控制、上报、调查和预防措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1685,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_hipaa_disclosure_breach_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.293","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.293.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.293.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,330],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,114],"fullStemEn":"By the end of the shift, RN Jordan has witnessed a coworker open Mrs. Torrance's electronic record without a care role, stopped further access, and started the facility reporting process. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely privacy condition, two priority actions, and two parameters that best evaluate the response.","fullStemZh":"到本班结束时，Jordan护士已目击一名同事在无照护职责的情况下打开Torrance女士电子病历，已阻止进一步访问，并启动机构上报流程。请完成弓形题：选择最可能的隐私问题、两个优先行动，以及两个最能评价处理效果的监测/确认参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely privacy condition, two priority actions, and two parameters that best evaluate the response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题：选择最可能的隐私问题、两个优先行动，以及两个最能评价处理效果的监测/确认参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Torrance's electronic record without a care role, stopped further access, and started the facility reporting process.","penultimateSentenceZh":"到本班结束时，Jordan护士已目击一名同事在无照护职责的情况下打开Torrance女士电子病历，已阻止进一步访问，并启动机构上报流程。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely privacy condition","zh":"最可能的隐私问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_c2","en":"Incidental disclosure that occurred despite reasonable safeguards","zh":"已采取合理保护措施但仍发生的偶然披露"},{"id":"bt_c3","en":"Permissible healthcare-operations access for education","zh":"为教育目的允许的医疗运营访问"},{"id":"bt_c1","en":"Unauthorized access of PHI requiring breach-response investigation","zh":"未经授权访问PHI，需要隐私事件调查"}],"correct":"bt_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_a4","en":"Accept RN Casey's statement that no disclosure occurred and do not report the access","zh":"接受Casey护士称未披露信息的说法，不上报此次访问"},{"id":"bt_a2","en":"Complete the facility electronic incident report with access details and mitigation steps","zh":"在机构电子事件报告中记录访问细节和控制措施"},{"id":"bt_a3","en":"Document in the medical record that an incident report was filed","zh":"在病历中记录已提交事件报告"},{"id":"bt_a1","en":"Ask RN Casey to exit the record immediately and notify the charge nurse","zh":"立即要求Casey护士退出病历并通知 charge nurse"}],"correct":["bt_a1","bt_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to evaluate response","zh":"用于评价处理效果的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_p4","en":"Whether Robert Torrance calls back before the end of the shift","zh":"Robert Torrance是否在本班结束前再次来电"},{"id":"bt_p2","en":"Implementation of system safeguards such as minimum-necessary education, HIM fax signage, and private-space reporting","zh":"落实系统防护措施，例如最低必要原则教育、HIM传真标识和私密空间交班"},{"id":"bt_p3","en":"Mrs. Torrance's postoperative vital signs, wound appearance, and pain score","zh":"Torrance女士术后生命体征、伤口外观和疼痛评分"},{"id":"bt_p1","en":"Privacy Officer confirmation that breach determination has started and the EHR audit trail is preserved","zh":"隐私官确认已启动隐私事件判定并保留电子病历审计追踪"}],"correct":["bt_p1","bt_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"RN Casey's curiosity-based EHR access is unauthorized PHI access, not incidental disclosure or approved operations access. The immediate nursing actions are to stop further access, notify the charge nurse, and complete the facility incident report with the relevant access and mitigation details. Evaluation focuses on Privacy Officer investigation, audit-trail preservation, and system safeguards; postoperative clinical stability and whether Robert calls back do not measure breach containment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Casey护士因好奇访问电子病历属于未经授权访问PHI，不是偶然披露，也不是被批准的运营/教育访问。护士的即时行动是阻止进一步访问、通知 charge nurse，并在机构事件报告中记录相关访问和控制细节。评价重点是隐私官调查、审计追踪保存和系统防护措施；术后临床稳定以及Robert是否再次来电，不能衡量隐私事件是否被控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a bow-tie, anchor on the central condition first. Then choose actions that treat that condition and parameters that prove the response worked.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，先锁定中心问题。然后选择能处理该问题的行动，以及能证明处理有效的参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1686,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.294","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.294.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[239,430],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,122],"fullStemEn":"Mass-casualty START triage with chemical contamination in a resource-limited emergency department A community ED with limited staff and treatment space receives seven casualties after an industrial explosion and anhydrous-ammonia release. The charge nurse must apply START triage, protect the ED from chemical contamination, allocate scarce resources to salvageable casualties, and evaluate whether the MCI response was effective.","fullStemZh":"资源受限急诊中伴化学污染的大规模伤亡START分诊 一家人员和治疗空间有限的社区急诊在工业爆炸和无水氨释放后接收7名伤员。charge nurse必须应用START分诊，防止急诊被化学污染，将稀缺资源分配给可挽救伤员，并评估MCI应对是否有效。","terminalSentenceEn":"The charge nurse must apply START triage, protect the ED from chemical contamination, allocate scarce resources to salvageable casualties, and evaluate whether the MCI response was effective.","terminalSentenceZh":"charge nurse必须应用START分诊，防止急诊被化学污染，将稀缺资源分配给可挽救伤员，并评估MCI应对是否有效。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Mass-casualty START triage with chemical contamination in a resource-limited emergency department A community ED with limited staff and treatment space receives seven casualties after an industrial explosion and anhydrous-ammonia release.","penultimateSentenceZh":"资源受限急诊中伴化学污染的大规模伤亡START分诊 一家人员和治疗空间有限的社区急诊在工业爆炸和无水氨释放后接收7名伤员。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests disaster nursing judgment: applying START triage objectively, recognizing that expectant categorization changes resuscitation decisions in resource-constrained MCI mode, sequencing contaminated-casualty care to protect staff and the ED, allocating scarce treatment spaces and blood products to salvageable casualties, and evaluating the response by survival of salvageable casualties and absence of secondary contamination rather than by zero mortality.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查灾难护理判断：客观应用START分诊；认识到资源受限MCI中预期死亡分类会改变复苏决策；按顺序处理污染伤员以保护工作人员和急诊；将稀缺治疗空间和血制品分配给可挽救伤员；并以可挽救伤员存活和无二次污染来评价应对，而不是以零死亡为标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor on the disaster protocol first, then apply airway/breathing/circulation and safety within the limits of salvageability, contamination control, and available resources.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先抓住灾难流程，再在可挽救性、污染控制和可用资源限制内应用气道/呼吸/循环和安全原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1687,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,33],"fullStemEn":"Using the Stage 1 triage-point findings, assign the correct START triage category to each casualty.","fullStemZh":"根据第1阶段入口分诊资料，为每名伤员选择正确的START分诊类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Stage 1 triage-point findings, assign the correct START triage category to each casualty.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第1阶段入口分诊资料，为每名伤员选择正确的START分诊类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"selectionMode":"single_per_row","columns":[{"id":"black","en":"Black / expectant","zh":"黑色/预期死亡"},{"id":"green","en":"Green / minor","zh":"绿色/轻伤"},{"id":"red","en":"Red / immediate","zh":"红色/立即"},{"id":"yellow","en":"Yellow / delayed","zh":"黄色/延迟"}],"rows":[{"id":"casualty_a","en":"A: apneic after airway repositioning, pulseless","zh":"A：重新开放气道后仍无呼吸、无脉搏"},{"id":"casualty_b","en":"B: ambulatory, alert, isolated forearm laceration","zh":"B：可行走、清醒、单纯前臂裂伤"},{"id":"casualty_c","en":"C: nonambulatory, RR 32, capillary refill 4 seconds, altered mental status","zh":"C：不能行走，RR 32，毛细血管再充盈4秒，意识改变"},{"id":"casualty_d","en":"D: nonambulatory, RR 32, stridor, chemical contamination","zh":"D：不能行走，RR 32，喘鸣，化学污染"},{"id":"casualty_e","en":"E: nonambulatory burn casualty, RR 26, pulse present, follows commands","zh":"E：不能行走的烧伤伤员，RR 26，有脉搏，能按指令"},{"id":"casualty_f","en":"F: ambulatory, alert, mild headache and tinnitus","zh":"F：可行走、清醒，轻度头痛和耳鸣"},{"id":"casualty_g","en":"G: apneic after airway repositioning, chemically contaminated","zh":"G：重新开放气道后仍无呼吸，且有化学污染"}]},"correct":[{"rowId":"casualty_a","columnIds":["black"]},{"rowId":"casualty_b","columnIds":["green"]},{"rowId":"casualty_c","columnIds":["red"]},{"rowId":"casualty_d","columnIds":["red"]},{"rowId":"casualty_e","columnIds":["yellow"]},{"rowId":"casualty_f","columnIds":["green"]},{"rowId":"casualty_g","columnIds":["black"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"START sorts by walking, breathing, perfusion, and mental status. A and G remain apneic after airway repositioning, so they are black/expectant in this MCI. B and F can walk and have minor complaints, so they are green. C is red because RR is greater than 30, perfusion is poor, and mental status is abnormal. D is red because she is nonambulatory with RR greater than 30 and airway compromise. E is yellow because he is serious but currently breathing under 30, perfusing, and following commands.","rationaleCorrectZh":"START按能否行走、呼吸、灌注和意识状态快速分类。A和G重新开放气道后仍无呼吸，因此在此MCI中为黑色/预期死亡。B和F能行走且主诉较轻，为绿色。C因RR大于30、灌注差且意识异常，为红色。D因不能行走、RR大于30并有气道受损，为红色。E伤势严重但目前RR低于30、灌注尚可且能按指令，因此为黄色。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In START questions, apply the algorithm before emotional or visual severity cues: walk, breathe after airway repositioning, perfusion, mental status.","testTakingStrategyZh":"START题先按算法，不被情绪或视觉冲击带偏：能否行走、开放气道后是否呼吸、灌注、意识状态。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1688,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,133],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"Which explanation best describes why Casualties A and G do not receive CPR or advanced resuscitation during the initial MCI response?","fullStemZh":"哪一项最能解释为什么A和G在MCI初期不接受CPR或高级复苏？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which explanation best describes why Casualties A and G do not receive CPR or advanced resuscitation during the initial MCI response?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一项最能解释为什么A和G在MCI初期不接受CPR或高级复苏？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"contamination_only","en":"Chemical contamination alone makes a casualty ineligible for treatment, regardless of breathing status or resources.","zh":"只要有化学污染，伤员就没有治疗资格，与呼吸状态或资源无关。"},{"id":"mci_utilitarian","en":"In this resource-limited MCI, casualties who remain apneic after airway repositioning are expectant so resuscitation resources can be directed to salvageable casualties.","zh":"在此资源受限MCI中，重新开放气道后仍无呼吸的伤员归为预期死亡，以便将复苏资源用于可挽救伤员。"},{"id":"age_based","en":"They are deprioritized mainly because they are older than the other casualties and younger clients should always be treated first.","zh":"他们主要因为年龄较大而降级，年轻伤员总是应优先治疗。"},{"id":"usual_code","en":"Pulseless adults in the ED must always receive CPR first, even during an activated MCI protocol.","zh":"急诊内无脉搏成人任何时候都必须先CPR，即使已启动MCI流程。"}],"correct":["mci_utilitarian"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Disaster triage shifts from routine one-patient rescue to greatest good for the greatest number. A and G meet the facility's START black criteria after airway repositioning. CPR, ventilator use, and one-to-one nursing would consume scarce resources needed for C, D, and E, who are more salvageable with timely intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"灾难分诊从常规的单个患者全力抢救转为最大多数人的最大利益。A和G在重新开放气道后符合机构START黑色标准。CPR、呼吸机和一对一护理会消耗C、D、E这些及时处理可挽救伤员所需的稀缺资源。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a disaster stem conflicts with routine instincts, name the governing protocol and ask which action preserves resources for salvageable clients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当灾难题干与常规本能冲突时，先找主导流程，再问哪项行动能把资源留给可挽救患者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1689,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[176,232],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,51],"fullStemEn":"Two red-category casualties are present at the start of Stage 1: Casualty C with hemorrhagic shock and no contamination, and Casualty D with stridor and ammonia contamination. Which casualty should enter the ED treatment area first?","fullStemZh":"第1阶段开始时有两名红色伤员：C为失血性休克且无污染，D有喘鸣且被氨污染。哪名伤员应先进入急诊治疗区？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which casualty should enter the ED treatment area first?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪名伤员应先进入急诊治疗区？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two red-category casualties are present at the start of Stage 1: Casualty C with hemorrhagic shock and no contamination, and Casualty D with stridor and ammonia contamination.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第1阶段开始时有两名红色伤员：C为失血性休克且无污染，D有喘鸣且被氨污染。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"e_burn","en":"Move Casualty E first because burns over 18% TBSA are visually severe and need fluid resuscitation.","zh":"先移动E，因为18% TBSA烧伤视觉上严重且需要补液。"},{"id":"c_first","en":"Move Casualty C into the trauma bay while Casualty D completes decontamination outside the ED.","zh":"在D于急诊外完成去污期间，将C送入创伤间。"},{"id":"wait_all","en":"Wait until all seven casualties have full head-to-toe assessments before assigning the trauma bay.","zh":"等7名伤员均完成全身详细评估后再分配创伤间。"},{"id":"d_direct","en":"Bring Casualty D directly into the ED because airway problems always override decontamination barriers.","zh":"因气道问题总是优先于去污屏障，直接将D带入急诊。"}],"correct":["c_first"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C can receive life-saving hemorrhage treatment immediately and is deteriorating. D is also red, but the facility protocol prohibits ED entry until decontamination and re-triage are complete. Using the trauma bay for C during D's required decontamination interval maximizes treatment of salvageable casualties without contaminating the ED.","rationaleCorrectZh":"C可立即接受挽救生命的出血处理且正在恶化。D同样是红色，但机构流程禁止其在完成去污和重新分诊前进入急诊。D必须去污的间隙用于C的创伤救治，既最大化可挽救伤员治疗，又避免污染急诊。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For two immediate clients, add feasibility and safety to ABCs: who can safely receive an effective intervention right now?","testTakingStrategyZh":"两个立即处理患者之间比较时，在ABCs之外加入可行性和安全性：谁现在能安全接受有效干预？","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Two red-category casualties are present at the start of Stage 1: Casualty C with hemorrhagic shock and no contamination, and Casualty D with stridor and ammonia contamination.","controlSentenceZh":"第1阶段开始时有两名红色伤员：C为失血性休克且无污染，D有喘鸣且被氨污染。"}
{"queueIndex":1690,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,34],"fullStemEn":"During Stage 2, which actions are appropriate disaster-phase nursing actions? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第2阶段中，哪些行动属于适当的灾难急性期护理行动？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During Stage 2, which actions are appropriate disaster-phase nursing actions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第2阶段中，哪些行动属于适当的灾难急性期护理行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"mtp_c","en":"Initiate the ordered massive transfusion protocol for Casualty C.","zh":"按医嘱为C启动大量输血流程。"},{"id":"d_airway","en":"Apply high-flow humidified oxygen, administer ordered bronchodilator therapy, and prepare difficult-airway equipment for Casualty D after decontamination.","zh":"D去污后给予高流量湿化氧、按医嘱给予支气管扩张治疗，并准备困难气道设备。"},{"id":"e_parkland","en":"Continue ordered IV burn resuscitation and transfer planning for stable Casualty E.","zh":"继续为稳定的E执行医嘱IV烧伤复苏并安排转运。"},{"id":"cpr_black","en":"Assign one nurse to start CPR on Casualty A or G while the red casualties are being treated.","zh":"在红色伤员处理期间，指派一名护士为A或G开始CPR。"},{"id":"green_defer","en":"Keep Casualties B and F deferred with basic self-care instructions until reinforcement nurses can assess them.","zh":"让B和F暂缓处理并遵循基本自我护理指示，直到增援护士可以评估。"},{"id":"full_assess_first","en":"Require complete head-to-toe assessments and full routine charting on all casualties before starting treatment.","zh":"开始治疗前要求所有伤员先完成从头到脚评估和完整常规记录。"}],"correct":["mtp_c","d_airway","e_parkland","green_defer"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate MCI actions address immediate or near-immediate threats in salvageable casualties using proportionate resources: hemorrhage control and transfusion for C, airway/respiratory treatment for decontaminated D, protocol burn stabilization and transfer for E, and safe deferral of green casualties. CPR on black casualties and routine full assessment before treatment would divert scarce nurse-minutes from salvageable casualties.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当的MCI行动是用相称资源处理可挽救伤员的立即或近立即威胁：C的止血和输血，D去污后的气道/呼吸治疗，E的烧伤流程稳定和转运，以及安全暂缓绿色伤员。为黑色伤员CPR或治疗前进行完整常规评估会把稀缺护理时间从可挽救伤员处转移走。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SATA disaster questions, select actions that save salvageable lives now and reject actions that consume scarce staff for deferrable or futile care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"灾难SATA题选择现在能挽救可救生命的行动，排除为可延后或无效护理消耗稀缺人力的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1691,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Place the steps for safely managing chemically contaminated Casualty D in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"请将安全处理被化学污染的D的步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps for safely managing chemically contaminated Casualty D in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将安全处理被化学污染的D的步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"irrigate","en":"Perform copious water irrigation for the full facility-protocol duration, including eyes and exposed skin.","zh":"按机构流程完成充分清水冲洗，包括眼部和暴露皮肤。"},{"id":"treat_airway","en":"Initiate definitive airway and respiratory treatment with monitoring in the ED.","zh":"在急诊监测下开始明确的气道和呼吸治疗。"},{"id":"ppe","en":"Don appropriate PPE before approaching the contaminated casualty.","zh":"接近被污染伤员前先穿戴适当PPE。"},{"id":"remove_clothes","en":"Remove and bag contaminated clothing and personal items.","zh":"脱去并装袋污染衣物和个人物品。"},{"id":"enter_ed","en":"Move the casualty into the ED treatment area only after decontamination is complete.","zh":"仅在去污完成后将伤员转入急诊治疗区。"},{"id":"reassess","en":"Perform post-decontamination reassessment and re-triage.","zh":"去污后重新评估并重新分诊。"}],"correct":["ppe","remove_clothes","irrigate","reassess","enter_ed","treat_airway"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"PPE protects the nurse before contact. Clothing removal reduces ongoing contamination and prevents transfer. Irrigation completes the facility decontamination requirement, with eyes and skin addressed. Reassessment and re-triage confirm the current status before ED entry. Only then can the patient enter the treatment area for monitored oxygen, medications, and airway backup.","rationaleCorrectZh":"PPE先保护护士再接触患者。脱衣可减少持续污染并避免转移。冲洗完成机构去污要求，重点处理眼部和皮肤。重新评估和重新分诊在进入急诊前确认当前状态。之后患者才可进入治疗区，接受监测下吸氧、用药和气道备用处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For hazardous-materials ordered-response items, rescuer safety and contamination control come before routine treatment location and definitive care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"危险化学品排序题中，救援者安全和污染控制先于常规治疗地点和明确治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1692,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.294.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,33],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which findings indicate the disaster triage and resource allocation were effective? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段中，哪些结果提示灾难分诊和资源分配有效？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which findings indicate the disaster triage and resource allocation were effective?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第3阶段中，哪些结果提示灾难分诊和资源分配有效？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"red_improving","en":"The salvageable red-category casualties, C and D, are alive and clinically improving after timely treatment.","zh":"可挽救的红色伤员C和D在及时治疗后存活并临床改善。"},{"id":"full_charts","en":"Effectiveness is best shown by complete routine nursing charting for every casualty during the acute phase.","zh":"有效性最好由急性期每名伤员完整常规护理记录证明。"},{"id":"green_safe","en":"The green-category casualties, B and F, were safely deferred and then discharged without deterioration.","zh":"绿色伤员B和F被安全暂缓，随后无恶化出院。"},{"id":"no_secondary","en":"No staff or other casualties show evidence of secondary ammonia contamination inside the ED.","zh":"急诊内无工作人员或其他伤员出现二次氨污染证据。"},{"id":"zero_deaths","en":"The response is effective only if all seven casualties survive.","zh":"只有7名伤员全部存活，反应才算有效。"},{"id":"yellow_stable","en":"The yellow-category burn casualty, E, remains stable and has an accepted burn-center transfer.","zh":"黄色烧伤伤员E保持稳定，并已被烧伤中心接收转运。"}],"correct":["red_improving","yellow_stable","green_safe","no_secondary"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"MCI effectiveness is judged by survival and stabilization of salvageable casualties, safe delay of minor casualties, successful transfer of serious delayed casualties, and preservation of staff/environmental safety. Two deaths do not by themselves show failure when those patients met expectant criteria. Routine full documentation is important after the acute phase but is not the key outcome metric during active disaster triage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MCI有效性要看可挽救伤员是否存活并稳定、轻伤员是否能安全延迟处理、严重延迟伤员是否成功稳定转运，以及工作人员和环境是否安全。若两名死亡者符合预期死亡标准，死亡人数本身并不代表失败。常规完整记录在急性期后很重要，但不是主动灾难分诊时的关键结局指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate disaster outcomes against the disaster goal: more salvageable lives saved and no avoidable system harm, not routine ED perfection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价灾难结局要按灾难目标：挽救更多可挽救生命并避免可预防系统伤害，而不是常规急诊的完美标准。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which findings indicate the disaster triage and resource allocation were effective?","controlSentenceZh":"第3阶段中，哪些结果提示灾难分诊和资源分配有效？"}
{"queueIndex":1693,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_mass_casualty_start_triage_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.295","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.295.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.295.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,370],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,113],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the ED is in activated MCI mode after seven casualties arrive from an industrial explosion with ammonia release. START triage is complete, one contaminated red-category casualty has completed decontamination, scarce blood and treatment spaces are being allocated, and the charge nurse must synthesize the safest condition, actions, and monitoring parameters.","fullStemZh":"第2阶段，7名来自工业爆炸并伴氨释放事件的伤员到达后，急诊已启动MCI模式。START分诊已完成，一名被污染的红色伤员已完成去污，有限血制品和治疗空间正在分配，charge nurse必须综合判断最安全的情境、行动和监测参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"START triage is complete, one contaminated red-category casualty has completed decontamination, scarce blood and treatment spaces are being allocated, and the charge nurse must synthesize the safest condition, actions, and monitoring parameters.","terminalSentenceZh":"START分诊已完成，一名被污染的红色伤员已完成去污，有限血制品和治疗空间正在分配，charge nurse必须综合判断最安全的情境、行动和监测参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the ED is in activated MCI mode after seven casualties arrive from an industrial explosion with ammonia release.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第2阶段，7名来自工业爆炸并伴氨释放事件的伤员到达后，急诊已启动MCI模式。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"condition_hazmat_only","en":"Single-problem hazardous-materials exposure without resource-allocation triage","zh":"单一危险化学品暴露事件，不需要资源分配分诊"},{"id":"condition_routine_surge","en":"Conventional ED surge with several trauma patients","zh":"常规急诊高峰并有多名创伤患者"},{"id":"condition_mci_hazmat","en":"Mass-casualty incident exceeding ED resources with required START triage and chemical decontamination","zh":"超过急诊资源能力、需要START分诊和化学去污的大规模伤亡事件"}],"correct":"condition_mci_hazmat"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"action_decon_before_ed","en":"Complete decontamination of contaminated casualties before ED entry","zh":"污染伤员进入急诊前完成去污"},{"id":"action_start_sequence","en":"Apply START categories and use them to sequence treatment of salvageable casualties","zh":"应用START类别并据此安排可挽救伤员的治疗顺序"},{"id":"action_cpr_expectant","en":"Begin full CPR and advanced resuscitation for A or G","zh":"为A或G开始完整CPR和高级复苏"},{"id":"action_bypass_decon","en":"Bring D directly into the ED before decontamination to treat stridor faster","zh":"为更快处理喘鸣，在去污前直接将D带入急诊"}],"correct":["action_start_sequence","action_decon_before_ed"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_secondary_contamination","en":"Absence of secondary contamination among staff, other casualties, and treatment areas","zh":"工作人员、其他伤员和治疗区无二次污染"},{"id":"param_salvageable_trajectory","en":"Clinical trajectory and survival of red/yellow salvageable casualties","zh":"红色/黄色可挽救伤员的临床趋势和存活情况"},{"id":"param_chart_completion","en":"Time to complete routine full nursing documentation for every casualty","zh":"每名伤员完成常规完整护理记录所需时间"},{"id":"param_raw_mortality","en":"Total mortality count as an isolated number","zh":"单独看总死亡人数"}],"correct":["param_salvageable_trajectory","param_secondary_contamination"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The resolved picture is an MCI with a hazardous-materials component, not a routine surge or a single-patient hazmat event. The priority actions are START-based resource allocation and completion of decontamination before ED entry. Outcomes should be monitored by the trajectory of salvageable red/yellow casualties and by the absence of secondary contamination.","rationaleCorrectZh":"综合判断是伴危险化学品因素的MCI，而不是常规高峰或单个化学暴露事件。优先行动是基于START进行资源分配，并在进入急诊前完成去污。应通过可挽救红/黄伤员的趋势以及是否无二次污染来监测结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bowtie items, match the condition to the whole pattern, then choose actions and monitoring that directly follow from that condition while rejecting routine-care reflexes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做bowtie题时，先把病情/情境与整体模式匹配，再选择由该情境直接推出的行动和监测，排除常规护理反射。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1694,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.296","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.296.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,305],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,87],"fullStemEn":"Advocating Against Unsafe Premature Discharge in Acute Decompensated Heart Failure A 71-year-old client recovering from acute decompensated heart failure has an active discharge order despite unresolved functional, comprehension, medication-access, social, environmental, and clinical monitoring concerns.","fullStemZh":"急性失代偿性心衰中反对不安全过早出院的患者倡导 一名 71 岁急性失代偿性心衰恢复期患者已有有效出院医嘱，但仍存在功能、理解、用药取得、社会、环境和临床监测方面未解决的担忧。","terminalSentenceEn":"Advocating Against Unsafe Premature Discharge in Acute Decompensated Heart Failure A 71-year-old client recovering from acute decompensated heart failure has an active discharge order despite unresolved functional, comprehension, medication-access, social, environmental, and clinical monitoring concerns.","terminalSentenceZh":"急性失代偿性心衰中反对不安全过早出院的患者倡导 一名 71 岁急性失代偿性心衰恢复期患者已有有效出院医嘱，但仍存在功能、理解、用药取得、社会、环境和临床监测方面未解决的担忧。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests the difference between clinical improvement and discharge readiness. The patient is responding to diuresis, with improved weight, edema, JVD, and BNP, but Stage 1 shows unresolved discharge barriers: borderline resting respiratory status, exertional desaturation requiring oxygen recovery, failed teach-back, an unaffordable new diuretic that repeats the admission trigger, stairs/living alone/no scale, creatinine above baseline, and low-normal potassium during diuresis. The nurse should advocate to hold or modify the discharge order, document objective concerns, and mobilize case management, social work, pharmacy, home health, and family support. By Stage 3, discharge becomes appropriate only because each barrier has a concrete resolution and the client demonstrates functional tolerance, understanding, medication access, home support, follow-up, and stable clinical trajectory.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查“临床改善”和“出院准备度”的区别。患者对利尿治疗有反应，体重、水肿、颈静脉怒张和 BNP 改善，但第 1 阶段仍显示未解决的出院障碍：静息呼吸状态临界、活动后低氧且需吸氧恢复、回授失败、新利尿剂负担不起并重现入院诱因、楼梯/独居/无体重秤、肌酐高于基线，以及利尿期间钾偏低正常。护士应倡导暂缓或修改出院医嘱，记录客观担忧，并启动个案管理、社工、药师、居家护理和家属支持。到第 3 阶段，只有在每个障碍都有具体解决结果，且患者证明有功能耐受、理解能力、用药取得、居家支持、随访和稳定临床趋势后，出院才合适。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not equate improving heart-failure markers with safe discharge. Ask: Can the client breathe and function in the home environment, understand the plan, obtain the medication, monitor symptoms/weight, and access support and follow-up?","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把心衰指标改善等同于安全出院。要问：患者能否在居家环境中呼吸和活动、理解计划、取得药物、监测症状/体重，并获得支持和随访？","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1695,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"Using the Stage 1 information, highlight the findings that are red flags for unsafe discharge today.","fullStemZh":"根据第 1 阶段资料，标出提示今天出院不安全的危险信号。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Stage 1 information, highlight the findings that are red flags for unsafe discharge today.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第 1 阶段资料，标出提示今天出院不安全的危险信号。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q1_s1","en":"The client is alert and oriented to person, place, time, and situation.","zh":"患者对人、地点、时间和情况均定向力正常。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s2","en":"Resting RR is 22/min with SpO2 93% on room air.","zh":"静息时呼吸频率 22 次/分，室内空气 SpO2 为 93%。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s3","en":"Weight decreased from 84.6 kg on admission to 78.2 kg today.","zh":"体重从入院时 84.6 kg 降至今天 78.2 kg。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s4","en":"Jugular venous distension is no longer visible at 45 degrees.","zh":"床头抬高 45 度时已看不到颈静脉怒张。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s5","en":"Bilateral pedal edema improved from 2+ on admission to trace today.","zh":"双侧足部水肿从入院时 2+ 改善为轻微。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s6","en":"During hallway ambulation of about 40 feet, SpO2 decreased to 89% on room air and oxygen was needed for recovery.","zh":"在走廊步行约 40 英尺时，室内空气 SpO2 降至 89%，需要吸氧后才恢复。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s7","en":"The client cannot explain the purpose of torsemide, what to do for sudden weight gain, or which symptoms require calling the provider.","zh":"患者无法说明 torsemide 的用途、体重突然增加时该怎么做，或哪些症状需要联系医护人员。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s8","en":"The new diuretic has a $95/month copay, and medication cost was the reason she stopped her prior furosemide.","zh":"新的利尿剂每月自付 95 美元，而药费负担正是她之前停用 furosemide 的原因。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s9","en":"She lives alone in a second-floor walk-up apartment and has no home scale.","zh":"她独居在没有电梯的二楼公寓，家中没有体重秤。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s10","en":"BNP decreased from 2,400 pg/mL on admission to 680 pg/mL today.","zh":"BNP 从入院时 2,400 pg/mL 降至今天 680 pg/mL。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s11","en":"Creatinine is 1.8 mg/dL, above her outpatient baseline of 1.4 mg/dL.","zh":"肌酐为 1.8 mg/dL，高于门诊基线 1.4 mg/dL。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q1_s2","q1_s6","q1_s7","q1_s8","q1_s9","q1_s11"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The unsafe-discharge cues are residual respiratory compromise, exertional desaturation requiring oxygen recovery, failed teach-back, unaffordable diuretic therapy, unsafe home environment/no scale, and creatinine above baseline. Improving weight, edema, JVD, and BNP show treatment response but do not prove discharge readiness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出院不安全的线索包括仍有呼吸受限、活动后低氧且需吸氧恢复、回授失败、利尿剂负担不起、居家环境/无体重秤不安全，以及肌酐高于基线。体重、水肿、颈静脉怒张和 BNP 改善说明治疗有效，但不能证明已具备出院准备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge-readiness questions, separate evidence of treatment response from evidence that the client can safely carry out the plan at home.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做出院准备度题时，要把“治疗有反应”和“患者能否在家安全执行计划”分开判断。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1696,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,50],"fullStemEn":"For each Stage 1 finding, classify whether it is an active barrier to safe discharge or a resolved/improving finding that does not remove the other barriers.","fullStemZh":"对每个第 1 阶段发现进行分类：它是安全出院的当前障碍，还是已改善/非障碍且不能抵消其他风险的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each Stage 1 finding, classify whether it is an active barrier to safe discharge or a resolved/improving finding that does not remove the other barriers.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每个第 1 阶段发现进行分类：它是安全出院的当前障碍，还是已改善/非障碍且不能抵消其他风险的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q2_r1","en":"SpO2 decreases to 89% after 40 feet of ambulation.","zh":"步行 40 英尺后 SpO2 降至 89%。"},{"id":"q2_r2","en":"JVD is no longer visible at 45 degrees.","zh":"床头抬高 45 度时已看不到颈静脉怒张。"},{"id":"q2_r3","en":"The client cannot identify when to call the provider for weight gain or symptoms.","zh":"患者无法说明体重增加或症状出现时何时联系医护人员。"},{"id":"q2_r4","en":"The new diuretic costs $95/month and is not affordable.","zh":"新的利尿剂每月 95 美元，患者负担不起。"},{"id":"q2_r5","en":"Weight is down 6.4 kg since admission and 0.8 kg since yesterday.","zh":"体重较入院下降 6.4 kg，较昨天下降 0.8 kg。"},{"id":"q2_r6","en":"The client lives alone in a second-floor walk-up apartment.","zh":"患者独居在没有电梯的二楼公寓。"},{"id":"q2_r7","en":"Creatinine is 1.8 mg/dL, above a baseline of 1.4 mg/dL.","zh":"肌酐 1.8 mg/dL，高于基线 1.4 mg/dL。"},{"id":"q2_r8","en":"The client is afebrile and has no chest pain.","zh":"患者无发热且无胸痛。"},{"id":"q2_r9","en":"Potassium is 3.4 mEq/L while loop diuretic therapy is continuing.","zh":"继续使用袢利尿剂时钾为 3.4 mEq/L。"},{"id":"q2_r10","en":"BNP is trending down from 2,400 to 680 pg/mL.","zh":"BNP 从 2,400 pg/mL 降至 680 pg/mL。"}],"columns":[{"id":"not_barrier","en":"Resolved/improving or not a discharge barrier","zh":"已改善/非出院障碍"},{"id":"active_barrier","en":"Active barrier to safe discharge","zh":"安全出院的当前障碍"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q2_r1","columnIds":["active_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r2","columnIds":["not_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r3","columnIds":["active_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r4","columnIds":["active_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r5","columnIds":["not_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r6","columnIds":["active_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r7","columnIds":["active_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r8","columnIds":["not_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r9","columnIds":["active_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q2_r10","columnIds":["not_barrier"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Active barriers include exertional hypoxemia, failed self-management understanding, medication unaffordability, unsafe home environment/lack of support, creatinine above baseline, and low-normal potassium during diuresis. Improving congestion markers and reassuring negatives do not make discharge safe by themselves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前障碍包括活动后低氧、自我管理理解失败、药物负担不起、居家环境/支持不足、肌酐高于基线，以及利尿期间钾偏低正常。淤血指标改善和阴性体征本身不能说明出院安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a question asks you to classify cues, do not let a single improving trend erase barriers in other domains.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题目要求分类线索时，不要让单一改善趋势掩盖其他领域的障碍。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1697,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,38],"fullStemEn":"The attending cites the downtrending BNP and the need for the bed as reasons to proceed. What is the nurse's priority advocacy stance?","fullStemZh":"医生以 BNP 下降和需要床位为理由要求继续出院。护士优先的倡导立场是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority advocacy stance?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士优先的倡导立场是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The attending cites the downtrending BNP and the need for the bed as reasons to proceed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医生以 BNP 下降和需要床位为理由要求继续出院。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_c","en":"Give extra written instructions and avoid challenging the provider because the discharge order is active.","zh":"提供更多书面说明，不质疑医嘱，因为出院医嘱已经生效。"},{"id":"q3_a","en":"Advocate to hold or modify the discharge because the plan is unsafe despite improving biomarkers.","zh":"主张暂缓或修改出院计划，因为尽管指标改善，目前计划仍不安全。"},{"id":"q3_b","en":"Proceed with discharge because the BNP is lower and the client has completed four hospital days.","zh":"因 BNP 降低且已住院四天，所以按计划出院。"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Delay advocacy until bed management confirms whether an emergency department patient still needs the bed.","zh":"等床位管理确认急诊患者是否仍需要床位后再进行倡导。"}],"correct":["q3_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority concern is patient safety. The nurse should communicate the specific barriers and request that discharge be held or modified pending interdisciplinary evaluation. Bed pressure and improving biomarkers do not override unsafe functional, comprehension, medication-access, and home-environment findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先问题是患者安全。护士应沟通具体障碍，并请求暂缓或修改出院，等待跨专业评估。床位压力和指标改善不能超过功能、理解、用药取得和居家环境方面的不安全发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem includes operational pressure, ask whether it conflicts with client safety. Safety wins.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干出现运营压力时，先判断它是否与患者安全冲突。患者安全优先。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1698,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,33],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions address the identified Stage 1 discharge barriers? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些护理措施可以处理第 1 阶段识别出的出院障碍？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions address the identified Stage 1 discharge barriers?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施可以处理第 1 阶段识别出的出院障碍？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_e","en":"Arrange home health nursing and coordinate immediate family support.","zh":"安排居家护理，并协调近期家属支持。"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"Contact the case manager about transition needs, insurance coverage, and discharge resources.","zh":"联系个案管理师评估过渡需求、保险覆盖和出院资源。"},{"id":"q4_f","en":"Discharge the client as ordered to free the telemetry bed and rely on written instructions.","zh":"按医嘱让患者出院以腾出监护床位，并依赖书面说明。"},{"id":"q4_d","en":"Ask the clinical pharmacist to identify an affordable formulary alternative or assistance program.","zh":"请临床药师寻找可负担的目录内替代药或援助项目。"},{"id":"q4_c","en":"Request social work support for home resources, a scale, and home-safety evaluation.","zh":"请求社工协助居家资源、体重秤和居家安全评估。"},{"id":"q4_a","en":"Document the ambulation result, failed teach-back, medication-cost barrier, and home-safety concerns.","zh":"记录步行结果、回授失败、药费障碍和居家安全担忧。"}],"correct":["q4_a","q4_b","q4_c","q4_d","q4_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should document, involve case management, social work, pharmacy, home health, and family support. These actions target the functional, comprehension, financial, and environmental barriers. Discharging to meet a bed target is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应记录情况，并联络个案管理、社工、药师、居家护理和家属支持。这些措施分别处理功能、理解、经济和环境障碍。为了床位目标出院是不安全的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For multi-domain discharge barriers, choose the actions that match each barrier; avoid one-resource answers for a multi-resource problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"面对多领域出院障碍时，选择能对应每个障碍的措施；多资源问题不要只选单一资源。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions address the identified Stage 1 discharge barriers?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施可以处理第 1 阶段识别出的出院障碍？"}
{"queueIndex":1699,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,43],"fullStemEn":"The discharge order is active with a target discharge time of 11:00 AM. After identifying the unsafe discharge picture, what should the nurse do first?","fullStemZh":"出院医嘱已生效，目标出院时间为上午 11:00。识别出出院不安全后，护士首先应怎么做？","terminalSentenceEn":"After identifying the unsafe discharge picture, what should the nurse do first?","terminalSentenceZh":"识别出出院不安全后，护士首先应怎么做？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The discharge order is active with a target discharge time of 11:00 AM.","penultimateSentenceZh":"出院医嘱已生效，目标出院时间为上午 11:00。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q5_d","en":"Escalate directly to the nursing supervisor before speaking with the attending physician.","zh":"在联系主治医生前直接上报护理主管。"},{"id":"q5_c","en":"Call the daughter first to see if she can solve the transportation and stair problem.","zh":"先致电女儿，看她是否能解决交通和爬楼问题。"},{"id":"q5_a","en":"Call the attending physician with the objective safety concerns and request that the discharge order be held.","zh":"致电主治医生说明客观安全担忧，并请求暂缓出院医嘱。"},{"id":"q5_b","en":"Page the social worker first because financial and home barriers are the root causes.","zh":"先呼叫社工，因为经济和居家障碍是根本原因。"}],"correct":["q5_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first action is direct communication with the ordering provider to request a discharge hold. This stops the unsafe process and creates time for case management, social work, pharmacy, home health, and family coordination. Escalation follows if the provider refuses to address the safety concern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要措施是直接联系开立医嘱的医生，请求暂缓出院。这样才能停止不安全流程，并争取时间协调个案管理、社工、药师、居家护理和家属。若医生拒绝处理安全问题，再逐级上报。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an unsafe process is already moving, choose the action that pauses the unsafe process before arranging secondary supports.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当不安全流程已经启动时，应先选择能暂停该流程的措施，再安排后续支持。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1700,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.296.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,57],"fullStemEn":"Using the Stage 3 re-evaluation, classify each finding as evidence that a specific discharge barrier has been resolved/controlled or as supportive treatment-response data that is not sufficient alone.","fullStemZh":"根据第 3 阶段重新评估，将每项发现分类为“证明某个出院障碍已解决/受控”，或“有帮助但单独不足的治疗反应资料”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Stage 3 re-evaluation, classify each finding as evidence that a specific discharge barrier has been resolved/controlled or as supportive treatment-response data that is not sufficient alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第 3 阶段重新评估，将每项发现分类为“证明某个出院障碍已解决/受控”，或“有帮助但单独不足的治疗反应资料”。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q6_r1","en":"Ambulates 150 feet and completes simulated stairs with SpO2 92% on room air, recovering within 1 minute.","zh":"步行 150 英尺并完成模拟楼梯，室内空气 SpO2 为 92%，1 分钟内恢复。"},{"id":"q6_r2","en":"Correctly explains the diuretic purpose, daily weight plan, call parameters, and warning signs.","zh":"正确说明利尿剂用途、每日称重计划、联系医护的参数和警示症状。"},{"id":"q6_r3","en":"The prescription is revised and a 30-day diuretic supply is provided before discharge.","zh":"处方已修改，且出院前已提供 30 天利尿剂供应。"},{"id":"q6_r4","en":"Daughter will stay for two days, home health visit is scheduled, scale delivery is arranged, and cardiology follow-up is confirmed.","zh":"女儿将陪伴两天，已安排居家护理、体重秤配送，并确认心脏科随访。"},{"id":"q6_r5","en":"Creatinine improves from 1.8 to 1.6 mg/dL, potassium is 4.1 mEq/L, and resting SpO2 is 95%.","zh":"肌酐从 1.8 改善至 1.6 mg/dL，钾为 4.1 mEq/L，静息 SpO2 为 95%。"},{"id":"q6_r6","en":"BNP has decreased to 520 pg/mL.","zh":"BNP 已降至 520 pg/mL。"}],"columns":[{"id":"resolved_barrier","en":"Evidence a specific discharge barrier is resolved or controlled","zh":"证明某个出院障碍已解决或受控"},{"id":"supportive_only","en":"Helpful treatment-response data but not sufficient alone","zh":"有帮助的治疗反应资料，但单独不足"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q6_r1","columnIds":["resolved_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q6_r2","columnIds":["resolved_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q6_r3","columnIds":["resolved_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q6_r4","columnIds":["resolved_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q6_r5","columnIds":["resolved_barrier"]},{"rowId":"q6_r6","columnIds":["supportive_only"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"By Stage 3, the functional, comprehension, medication-access, support/equipment, and clinical-stability barriers have concrete resolutions. BNP is still helpful as treatment-response information, but it remains insufficient by itself to establish discharge readiness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"到第 3 阶段，功能、理解、用药取得、支持/设备和临床稳定性障碍都有具体解决结果。BNP 仍是有帮助的治疗反应资料，但单独仍不足以证明出院准备充分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by matching each original problem to a verifiable resolution; do not clear discharge on a lab trend alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果时，要把每个原始问题对应到可验证的解决结果；不要仅凭一个实验室趋势就认为可以出院。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1701,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_unsafe_premature_discharge_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.297","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.297.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.297.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[395,487],"terminalOffsetsZh":[128,150],"fullStemEn":"At 09:15, a 71-year-old client recovering from acute decompensated heart failure has an active 11:00 discharge order. She desaturates to 89% after walking 40 feet, requires oxygen to recover, fails teach-back about her new medications and warning signs, cannot afford the prescribed diuretic, lives alone in a second-floor walk-up apartment, and has no home scale. BNP and weight are improving. Complete the bow-tie to identify the priority condition, actions, and monitoring parameters.","fullStemZh":"09:15，一名 71 岁急性失代偿性心衰恢复期患者有上午 11:00 的有效出院医嘱。她步行 40 英尺后 SpO2 降至 89%，需要吸氧恢复；对新药和警示症状回授失败；负担不起处方利尿剂；独居在无电梯二楼公寓；家中没有体重秤。BNP 和体重正在改善。完成蝴蝶结题，识别优先问题、措施和监测参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie to identify the priority condition, actions, and monitoring parameters.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题，识别优先问题、措施和监测参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"BNP and weight are improving.","penultimateSentenceZh":"BNP 和体重正在改善。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_routine","en":"Routine discharge with standard written instructions","zh":"常规出院并提供标准书面说明"},{"id":"bt_cond_unsafe","en":"Unsafe premature discharge","zh":"不安全的过早出院"},{"id":"bt_cond_acute","en":"Continued acute decompensation requiring indefinite inpatient treatment","zh":"持续急性失代偿，需要无限期住院治疗"}],"correct":"bt_cond_unsafe"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_act_team","en":"Mobilize case management, social work, clinical pharmacy, home health, and family support","zh":"启动个案管理、社工、临床药师、居家护理和家属支持"},{"id":"bt_act_discharge","en":"Proceed with discharge as ordered to free the telemetry bed","zh":"按医嘱出院以腾出监护床位"},{"id":"bt_act_hold","en":"Advocate to hold the discharge by communicating objective safety concerns and escalating if needed","zh":"沟通客观安全担忧，倡导暂缓出院，必要时逐级上报"},{"id":"bt_act_written","en":"Provide additional written instructions and a follow-up appointment only","zh":"仅提供更多书面说明和随访预约"}],"correct":["bt_act_hold","bt_act_team"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_param_teachback","en":"Repeat teach-back on medication purpose, daily weights, call parameters, and warning signs","zh":"再次回授药物用途、每日称重、联系医护的参数和警示症状"},{"id":"bt_param_function","en":"Repeat ambulation including stair simulation with oxygen saturation and recovery time","zh":"重复步行并模拟爬楼，同时监测氧饱和度和恢复时间"},{"id":"bt_param_bnp","en":"BNP level alone","zh":"单独 BNP 水平"},{"id":"bt_param_weight","en":"Inpatient daily weight trend alone","zh":"单独住院每日体重趋势"}],"correct":["bt_param_teachback","bt_param_function"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority condition is unsafe premature discharge: the client is improving medically but cannot yet safely transition home. The two priority actions are to pause the unsafe discharge through provider communication/escalation and to mobilize interdisciplinary resources that resolve the identified barriers. The key monitoring parameters are repeat teach-back and functional tolerance including stair simulation; BNP and inpatient weight are useful treatment-response data but do not answer whether the discharge barriers have been resolved.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先问题是不安全的过早出院：患者医学上正在改善，但尚不能安全过渡回家。两个优先措施是通过与医生沟通/必要时上报来暂停不安全出院，并调动跨专业资源解决已识别障碍。关键监测参数是再次回授和包括模拟爬楼在内的功能耐受；BNP 和住院体重是有用的治疗反应资料，但不能回答出院障碍是否已解决。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bow-tie items, choose the condition that best explains the whole pattern, then pick actions and monitoring that directly address the condition rather than attractive but incomplete trends.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，先选择最能解释整体模式的问题，再选择直接处理该问题的措施和监测，而不是被看似正向但不完整的趋势吸引。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"BNP and weight are improving.","controlSentenceZh":"BNP 和体重正在改善。"}
{"queueIndex":1702,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.298","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.298.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,273],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,74],"fullStemEn":"Interprofessional conflict resolution: questionable potassium replacement order A 71-year-old post-operative client with stage 3b chronic kidney disease has hypokalemia and receives an overnight potassium replacement order that conflicts with the unit electrolyte protocol.","fullStemZh":"跨专业冲突处理：有安全疑问的补钾医嘱 一名 71 岁术后患者合并 3b 期慢性肾病，出现低钾血症。夜间医生开出的补钾医嘱与病区电解质补充流程不一致。","terminalSentenceEn":"Interprofessional conflict resolution: questionable potassium replacement order A 71-year-old post-operative client with stage 3b chronic kidney disease has hypokalemia and receives an overnight potassium replacement order that conflicts with the unit electrolyte protocol.","terminalSentenceZh":"夜间医生开出的补钾医嘱与病区电解质补充流程不一致。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":"跨专业冲突处理：有安全疑问的补钾医嘱 一名 71 岁术后患者合并 3b 期慢性肾病，出现低钾血症。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on a protocol-based medication-safety conflict. The client truly needs potassium replacement, but the original order for 40 mEq in 100 mL over 1 hour through a peripheral IV conflicts with the stated unit protocol and is riskier because renal function is below baseline. The nurse first identifies the unsafe rate, concentration, access, and renal-function cues; uses assertive safety communication rather than treating the disagreement as a personality issue; withholds the unsafe order; escalates through the chain of command; and documents the facts. The outcome is adequate because the unsafe order is not carried out, a protocol-compliant replacement order is obtained, potassium improves without rhythm or IV-site complications, and follow-up communication with the resident is restored.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的核心是基于流程的用药安全冲突。患者确实需要补钾，但原始医嘱为经外周静脉 1 小时输注 40 mEq/100 mL 氯化钾，与病区流程不符；且患者肾功能低于基线，风险更高。护士首先识别不安全的速度、浓度、静脉通路和肾功能线索；使用明确的安全沟通，而不是把分歧当成人际矛盾；暂缓执行不安全医嘱；按指挥链升级处理；并如实记录。结果是充分的，因为不安全医嘱没有执行，取得了符合流程的补钾医嘱，血钾改善且没有心律或 IV 部位并发症，并且与住院医的后续沟通得到修复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a provider order conflicts with a stated facility protocol, do not debate hierarchy. Identify the exact safety conflict, communicate it clearly, hold the unsafe action, and escalate until a safe plan exists.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当医生医嘱与已给出的机构流程冲突时，不要陷入层级问题。先找出具体安全冲突，清楚沟通，暂缓不安全操作，并升级处理直到有安全方案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1703,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,39],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Which findings are part of the safety concern with the potassium order as written? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段：关于当前补钾医嘱，哪些资料属于安全担忧的一部分？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Which findings are part of the safety concern with the potassium order as written?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段：关于当前补钾医嘱，哪些资料属于安全担忧的一部分？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"The client asks when she can go home.","zh":"患者询问什么时候可以回家。"},{"id":"E","en":"The cardiac monitor shows normal sinus rhythm without ectopy.","zh":"心电监护显示正常窦性心律，无异位搏动。"},{"id":"D","en":"The creatinine is 1.6 mg/dL with eGFR 34 mL/min, worse than baseline.","zh":"肌酐 1.6 mg/dL、eGFR 34 mL/min，较基线恶化。"},{"id":"A","en":"The order is potassium chloride 40 mEq IV over 1 hour.","zh":"医嘱为氯化钾 40 mEq IV 1 小时输完。"},{"id":"B","en":"The order places 40 mEq potassium chloride in 100 mL normal saline.","zh":"医嘱将氯化钾 40 mEq 加入 100 mL 生理盐水。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client has only a 20-gauge peripheral IV and no central venous access.","zh":"患者只有一条 20G 外周静脉通路，没有中心静脉通路。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The unsafe pattern is the combination of excessive peripheral potassium rate, excessive concentration for the stated protocol, absence of central access, and worsened renal function. The client's stable rhythm and discharge question are real assessment findings, but they do not make the order safe or unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"不安全的组合包括：外周补钾速度过快、浓度超过本题给定流程、没有中心静脉通路，以及肾功能较基线恶化。患者心律稳定和询问出院是真实评估资料，但它们并不决定该医嘱是否安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the indication for therapy from the safety of the delivery method. A low potassium level explains why replacement is needed; it does not validate an unsafe route, rate, or concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把治疗适应证和给药方式安全性分开。低钾说明需要补钾，但不能证明不安全的通路、速度或浓度是合理的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1704,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: What is the best interpretation of the disagreement between the nurse and the covering resident?","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段：对护士和值班住院医之间分歧的最佳理解是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: What is the best interpretation of the disagreement between the nurse and the covering resident?","terminalSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段：对护士和值班住院医之间分歧的最佳理解是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"A genuine patient-safety conflict based on a protocol discrepancy and renal-risk concern","zh":"基于流程不一致和肾功能风险的真实患者安全冲突"},{"id":"D","en":"A clinical-preference difference where either potassium administration approach is equally acceptable","zh":"两种补钾方式都同样可接受的临床偏好差异"},{"id":"C","en":"A scope-of-practice conflict because the nurse is trying to prescribe medication","zh":"护士试图开药，因此是执业范围冲突"},{"id":"B","en":"A personality clash caused mainly by the resident's irritated tone","zh":"主要由住院医不耐烦语气导致的人际性格冲突"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The disagreement is driven by an objective safety issue: the order exceeds the stated peripheral potassium protocol and the client's renal function is worse than baseline. The resident's tone is a barrier, but it is not the root cause.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该分歧的根源是客观安全问题：医嘱超过题干给出的外周补钾流程，并且患者肾功能较基线恶化。住院医的语气是沟通障碍，但不是根本原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In conflict-resolution questions, identify whether the conflict has an objective safety anchor. A rude tone can distract you, but protocol violations and patient risk factors drive the nursing response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到冲突处理题，先判断冲突是否有客观安全依据。语气不好可能干扰判断，但流程违规和患者风险因素才决定护士反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1705,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Which priority should guide the nurse's response to the resident's instruction to 'just run it'?","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段：住院医要求“就这样输”时，哪一优先原则应指导护士反应？","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Which priority should guide the nurse's response to the resident's instruction to 'just run it'?","terminalSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段：住院医要求“就这样输”时，哪一优先原则应指导护士反应？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Preserve the working relationship by avoiding further challenge to the resident","zh":"为维持工作关系，避免继续质疑住院医"},{"id":"A","en":"Protect the client from the unsafe rate and concentration while advocating for safe potassium replacement","zh":"保护患者免受不安全速度和浓度的风险，同时争取安全补钾方案"},{"id":"D","en":"Refuse all potassium replacement until the attending evaluates the client in person","zh":"在主治医生亲自评估前拒绝所有补钾"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the order because potassium 3.1 mEq/L means replacement is urgent","zh":"因为血钾 3.1 mEq/L 需要紧急补钾，所以执行原医嘱"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client needs potassium replacement, but the replacement must be delivered safely. The nurse's priority is not to choose between treatment and no treatment; it is to obtain a safe, protocol-consistent treatment plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者需要补钾，但补钾必须安全执行。护士的优先事项不是在治疗和不治疗之间二选一，而是取得安全、符合流程的治疗方案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid false dichotomies. NCLEX often tests whether you can say, 'Do the needed treatment safely,' instead of choosing unsafe treatment or no treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"避免错误二分法。NCLEX 常考你能否选择“安全地完成需要的治疗”，而不是在不安全治疗和完全不治疗之间选择。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1706,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,102],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Which nursing actions are appropriate to resolve this safety conflict? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段：为解决这一安全冲突，哪些护理措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: Which nursing actions are appropriate to resolve this safety conflict?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段：为解决这一安全冲突，哪些护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Request a modified order or an authorized policy-consistent override through the appropriate pathway.","zh":"通过适当途径请求修正医嘱，或取得符合政策授权的例外处理。"},{"id":"F","en":"Ask another nurse to hang the potassium so the assigned nurse is not the one administering it.","zh":"请另一名护士悬挂该钾剂，这样责任护士就不是执行者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Withhold the potassium as written and escalate through the chain of command if the concern remains unresolved.","zh":"在问题未解决时暂缓按原医嘱补钾，并按指挥链升级处理。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the original order, concern, communications, escalation, and outcome factually.","zh":"客观记录原医嘱、担忧、沟通、升级处理和结果。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer the potassium as ordered because the provider has repeated the instruction.","zh":"因为医生重复了指示，所以按原医嘱给予氯化钾。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use CUS or equivalent graded-assertiveness language to state that the order is a safety concern.","zh":"使用 CUS 或类似分级坚定沟通，说明该医嘱是安全问题。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct pathway is graded assertive communication, pursuit of a safe revised or properly authorized order, withholding the unsafe order while escalating if needed, and factual documentation. Compliance or transferring the task to another nurse does not resolve the safety problem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确路径包括分级坚定沟通、争取安全的修正医嘱或有授权的例外处理、必要时暂缓不安全医嘱并升级处理，以及客观记录。盲目执行或把任务转给另一名护士都不能解决安全问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unsafe orders, look for the complete safety loop: clear communication, hold/clarify, chain-of-command escalation, and documentation. Avoid answers that only protect the nurse or only obey hierarchy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到不安全医嘱，寻找完整安全闭环：清楚沟通、暂缓/澄清、按指挥链升级、记录。避免只保护护士自己或只服从层级的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1707,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Immediately after the resident says, 'Just run it,' what is the nurse's best first action?","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段：住院医说“就这样输”后，护士最佳的第一步是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Immediately after the resident says, 'Just run it,' what is the nurse's best first action?","terminalSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段：住院医说“就这样输”后，护士最佳的第一步是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"End the call and immediately contact the chief resident without any further direct safety statement","zh":"结束通话并立即联系 chief resident，不再直接说明安全问题"},{"id":"A","en":"Use CUS/two-challenge language to clearly state the protocol-based safety concern, then escalate if it is still not acknowledged","zh":"使用 CUS/两次挑战式沟通，清楚说明基于流程的安全担忧；若仍不被认可，再升级处理"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the potassium while notifying the charge nurse of the concern","zh":"一边按原医嘱给予氯化钾，一边通知 charge nurse"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the disagreement and wait for the resident to call back later","zh":"记录分歧，然后等待住院医稍后回电"},{"id":"E","en":"File an incident report before speaking with anyone else","zh":"在与任何人沟通前先填写事件报告"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse has already tried a soft clarification. The next first action is a clear second challenge using CUS or equivalent language that identifies a safety issue. If that fails, chain-of-command escalation follows while the order remains withheld.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士已经进行了温和澄清。下一步应使用 CUS 或类似语言进行明确的第二次挑战，指出这是安全问题。若仍无效，则在暂缓医嘱的同时按指挥链升级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a first clarification is dismissed, look for a stronger direct safety statement before escalation. But never choose an answer that administers the unsafe order while the concern remains unresolved.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当第一次澄清被否定时，先找更明确的直接安全陈述，然后再升级。但只要安全问题未解决，就不要选择执行不安全医嘱的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1708,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.298.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: For each finding, indicate whether it supports that the conflict was resolved safely and professionally.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段：对于每项发现，判断它是否支持该冲突已被安全且专业地解决。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 3: For each finding, indicate whether it supports that the conflict was resolved safely and professionally.","terminalSentenceZh":"第 3 阶段：对于每项发现，判断它是否支持该冲突已被安全且专业地解决。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The original 40 mEq/hr peripheral potassium order was not administered.","zh":"原始 40 mEq/hr 外周补钾医嘱未被执行。"},{"id":"r2","en":"A revised order gives 10 mEq in 100 mL over 1 hour via the peripheral line.","zh":"修正医嘱为氯化钾 10 mEq/100 mL，经外周静脉 1 小时输完。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Repeat potassium after two doses is 3.4 mEq/L and the rhythm remains normal sinus.","zh":"两剂后复查血钾为 3.4 mEq/L，心律仍为正常窦性心律。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client denies IV site discomfort, palpitations, or muscle symptoms.","zh":"患者否认 IV 部位不适、心悸或肌肉症状。"},{"id":"r5","en":"The covering resident acknowledges the protocol and asks to receive the repeat result.","zh":"值班住院医承认流程要求，并要求获知复查结果。"},{"id":"r6","en":"The client had asked earlier when she could go home.","zh":"患者早些时候询问什么时候可以回家。"}],"columns":[{"id":"not_resolution_indicator","en":"Not a resolution indicator","zh":"不是处理结果指标"},{"id":"supports_resolution","en":"Supports adequate resolution","zh":"支持处理充分"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["supports_resolution"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["supports_resolution"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["supports_resolution"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["supports_resolution"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["supports_resolution"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["not_resolution_indicator"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adequate resolution requires both patient-safety outcomes and restored professional communication. The unsafe order was withheld, a protocol-consistent order was obtained, the potassium improved without adverse rhythm or IV-site findings, and the resident's follow-up communication became constructive. The earlier discharge question is unrelated to resolving the potassium-order conflict.","rationaleCorrectZh":"充分解决需要同时评估患者安全结果和专业沟通是否恢复。不安全医嘱被暂缓，取得符合流程的医嘱，血钾改善且没有心律或 IV 部位不良表现，住院医后续沟通也变得建设性。早先的出院问题与补钾医嘱冲突的解决无关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluation questions often require more than a lab improvement. Check whether the unsafe process was corrected, harm was avoided, and communication channels remain functional.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果题通常不只看化验改善。还要看不安全流程是否纠正、是否避免伤害，以及沟通渠道是否仍然有效。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1709,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nurse_provider_conflict_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.299","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.299.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.299.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[592,621],"terminalOffsetsZh":[226,240],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3 synthesis: A post-operative client with CKD had a potassium of 3.1 mEq/L. A covering resident ordered potassium chloride 40 mEq in 100 mL normal saline to infuse through a peripheral IV over 1 hour, despite a unit protocol limiting peripheral potassium to 10 mEq/100 mL and 10 mEq/hr and requiring renal-function verification. The nurse questioned the order; the resident insisted it be run without addressing the protocol or eGFR 34 mL/min. The nurse used the chain of command, the unsafe order was not administered, and a revised order of 10 mEq in 100 mL over 1 hour was obtained. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段综合：一名合并 CKD 的术后患者血钾 3.1 mEq/L。值班住院医开出氯化钾 40 mEq 加入 100 mL 生理盐水、经外周 IV 1 小时输完的医嘱；但病区流程规定外周补钾限于 10 mEq/100 mL 和 10 mEq/hr，并要求核对肾功能。护士质疑该医嘱；住院医坚持执行，却未回应流程或 eGFR 34 mL/min 的问题。护士按指挥链处理，未执行不安全医嘱，并取得 10 mEq/100 mL、1 小时输完的修正医嘱。请完成 bow-tie 图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成 bow-tie 图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse used the chain of command, the unsafe order was not administered, and a revised order of 10 mEq in 100 mL over 1 hour was obtained.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士按指挥链处理，未执行不安全医嘱，并取得 10 mEq/100 mL、1 小时输完的修正医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_c_safety_conflict","en":"Unsafe medication order causing an interprofessional safety conflict","zh":"不安全用药医嘱导致的跨专业安全冲突"},{"id":"bt_c_personality","en":"Personality clash or poor bedside manner only","zh":"仅仅是性格冲突或态度不好"},{"id":"bt_c_preference","en":"Equivalent clinical-preference difference about potassium replacement","zh":"关于补钾方式的同等临床偏好差异"}],"correct":"bt_c_safety_conflict"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_a_cus","en":"Use structured assertive safety communication with the ordering provider","zh":"与开嘱医生使用结构化、坚定的安全沟通"},{"id":"bt_a_escalate","en":"Withhold the unsafe order and escalate through the chain of command","zh":"暂缓不安全医嘱并按指挥链升级处理"},{"id":"bt_a_refuse_only","en":"Refuse the order and document, but do not pursue a safe replacement order","zh":"拒绝医嘱并记录，但不继续争取安全补钾医嘱"},{"id":"bt_a_administer","en":"Administer the potassium as originally ordered","zh":"按原始医嘱给予氯化钾"}],"correct":["bt_a_cus","bt_a_escalate"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_p_discharge","en":"Client's question about discharge timing","zh":"患者询问出院时间"},{"id":"bt_p_workload","en":"Number of pages the resident is managing","zh":"住院医正在处理的传呼数量"},{"id":"bt_p_k_rhythm_iv","en":"Potassium trend, cardiac rhythm, and IV-site tolerance during replacement","zh":"补钾期间的血钾趋势、心律和 IV 部位耐受性"},{"id":"bt_p_order","en":"Revised order is protocol-compliant and original unsafe order is not administered","zh":"修正医嘱符合流程，且原始不安全医嘱未被执行"}],"correct":["bt_p_order","bt_p_k_rhythm_iv"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is an unsafe medication-order conflict, not a personality issue. The priority nursing actions are to use structured assertive communication and, when the concern is not resolved, to withhold the unsafe order while escalating through the chain of command. Monitoring should confirm that the unsafe order was replaced by a protocol-compliant order and that the potassium replacement is effective and tolerated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本题的情况是不安全用药医嘱引发的安全冲突，不是单纯人际问题。优先护理措施是使用结构化坚定沟通；若担忧未解决，则暂缓不安全医嘱并按指挥链升级处理。监测应确认不安全医嘱已被符合流程的医嘱取代，并确认补钾有效且患者可耐受。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bow-tie items, keep each zone separate: identify the safety problem, then select nursing actions within scope, then choose monitoring data that proves the plan worked.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bow-tie 题时要分清每个区域：先识别安全问题，再选择护士职责范围内的措施，最后选择能证明方案有效的监测资料。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1710,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.300","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.300.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[222,368],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,148],"fullStemEn":"Client advocacy for a capacitated older adult refusing PEG placement An 82-year-old client with end-stage heart failure, progressive dysphagia, and poor oral intake refuses PEG tube placement after an informed discussion. Her adult children pressure the team to proceed, and her son claims authority under a DPOAHC that activates only if she loses decisional capacity.","fullStemZh":"为有决策能力且拒绝 PEG 置管的老年患者进行护理倡导 一名 82 岁患者患有终末期心力衰竭、进行性吞咽困难和进食不足。在充分知情沟通后，她拒绝放置 PEG 管。她的成年子女要求医疗团队继续置管，其儿子声称自己可根据医疗保健持久授权书（DPOAHC）作决定，但该授权仅在患者丧失决策能力时才生效。","terminalSentenceEn":"Her adult children pressure the team to proceed, and her son claims authority under a DPOAHC that activates only if she loses decisional capacity.","terminalSentenceZh":"她的成年子女要求医疗团队继续置管，其儿子声称自己可根据医疗保健持久授权书（DPOAHC）作决定，但该授权仅在患者丧失决策能力时才生效。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Client advocacy for a capacitated older adult refusing PEG placement An 82-year-old client with end-stage heart failure, progressive dysphagia, and poor oral intake refuses PEG tube placement after an informed discussion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在充分知情沟通后，她拒绝放置 PEG 管。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on protecting a capacitated adult's informed refusal when family pressure and provider ambivalence threaten to override it. The decisive cues are the documented decision-specific capacity assessment, Mrs. Ellison's repeated values-based refusal, absence of coercion changing her decision, and an advance directive that gives the son surrogate authority only if capacity is lost. Appropriate nursing advocacy includes direct communication with the physician, careful documentation, palliative-care and social-work involvement, a structured family meeting, and escalation to ethics or risk management if needed. Effective advocacy is measured by whether the plan of care honors the patient's stated goals and whether she feels heard, not by whether the family agrees.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的核心是在家属压力和医师态度摇摆可能覆盖患者意愿时，保护有决策能力成人的知情拒绝权。关键线索包括：已记录的针对该决定的决策能力评估、Ellison 太太反复且基于价值观的拒绝、没有胁迫改变其决定，以及预立医疗指示明确儿子只有在她丧失能力时才具有代理权。适当的护理倡导包括直接与医师沟通、仔细记录、介入姑息治疗和社工、安排结构化家庭会议，并在需要时升级至伦理委员会或风险管理。倡导是否有效，应看照护计划是否尊重患者目标、患者是否感到被倾听，而不是看家属是否满意。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate medical indication from consent authority. A treatment can be clinically reasonable and still cannot proceed when a capacitated client refuses it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要区分“医学上有理由建议治疗”和“谁有权同意治疗”。某项治疗即使在医学上合理，只要有决策能力的患者拒绝，就不能强行进行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1711,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[57,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Highlight the findings that establish that Mrs. Ellison's refusal is the governing decision.","fullStemZh":"阶段 1：请标出哪些发现能确立 Ellison 太太的拒绝是当前应遵循的决定。","terminalSentenceEn":"Ellison's refusal is the governing decision.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 1：请标出哪些发现能确立 Ellison 太太的拒绝是当前应遵循的决定。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Highlight the findings that establish that Mrs.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Chart review findings:","zh":"病历审查发现："},{"id":"s2","en":"The physician documents that Mrs. Ellison understands the risks and benefits of PEG placement, including continued weight loss without it.","zh":"医师记录 Ellison 太太理解 PEG 置管的风险与获益，包括不置管可能继续体重下降。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"She asks clarifying questions about whether the tube will cure her heart failure and whether she may still eat by mouth.","zh":"她提出澄清性问题，询问管子是否能治愈心力衰竭，以及是否仍可经口进食。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"She states, \"I understand what you're telling me. I don't want a feeding tube. I want to eat what I can and be comfortable.\"","zh":"她说：“我理解你们说的内容。我不想要喂食管。我想吃多少算多少，并且舒服一点。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The advance directive states that the son's DPOAHC authority activates only if Mrs. Ellison loses decisional capacity.","zh":"预立医疗指示说明，儿子的 DPOAHC 权限只有在 Ellison 太太丧失决策能力时才生效。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Mini-Cog score is 4/5 with a normal clock draw.","zh":"Mini-Cog 得分为 4/5，画钟正常。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"David says he is the power of attorney and wants the tube placed.","zh":"David 说自己是授权代理人，并要求放置管子。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Albumin is 2.6 g/dL and prealbumin is 11 mg/dL.","zh":"白蛋白 2.6 g/dL，前白蛋白 11 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Speech-language pathology has followed progressive dysphagia for 6 months.","zh":"言语语言病理科已随访进行性吞咽困难 6 个月。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The governing cues are decision-specific capacity documentation, Mrs. Ellison's demonstrated understanding and clarifying questions, her clear values-based refusal, and the advance directive clause showing that the son's surrogate authority is dormant while she has capacity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键线索是：针对 PEG 决定的能力评估记录、患者表现出理解并提出澄清问题、她清楚且基于价值观地拒绝，以及预立医疗指示说明只要她仍有能力，儿子的代理权就尚未生效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For capacity and consent questions, key the findings that show understanding, reasoning, voluntariness, and who legally holds authority now—not the findings that make the proposed treatment medically reasonable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到决策能力和同意权题目时，优先寻找能证明理解、推理、自愿性以及当前谁有法律权力的线索，而不是只看治疗在医学上是否合理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1712,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,153],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,56],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: David insists that his DPOAHC status allows him to override his mother's refusal and request PEG placement. Whose decision governs at this time?","fullStemZh":"阶段 1：David 坚称自己的 DPOAHC 身份允许他推翻母亲的拒绝并要求放置 PEG。此时应遵循谁的决定？","terminalSentenceEn":"Whose decision governs at this time?","terminalSentenceZh":"此时应遵循谁的决定？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 1: David insists that his DPOAHC status allows him to override his mother's refusal and request PEG placement.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段 1：David 坚称自己的 DPOAHC 身份允许他推翻母亲的拒绝并要求放置 PEG。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"E","en":"The decision should be delayed until Mrs. Ellison's daughter can be physically present.","zh":"应推迟决定，直到 Ellison 太太的女儿能亲自到场。"},{"id":"A","en":"Mrs. Ellison's refusal governs because her decision-making capacity is intact and documented.","zh":"应遵循 Ellison 太太的拒绝，因为她的决策能力完整且已有记录。"},{"id":"B","en":"David's decision governs because a DPOAHC always has priority over the patient's current choice.","zh":"应遵循 David 的决定，因为 DPOAHC 总是优先于患者当前选择。"},{"id":"D","en":"The physician may proceed because PEG placement is medically recommended for poor intake and dysphagia.","zh":"医师可以继续安排，因为 PEG 对进食不足和吞咽困难有医学建议理由。"},{"id":"C","en":"The children should decide together because both adult children agree with PEG placement.","zh":"应由两名成年子女共同决定，因为他们都同意 PEG 置管。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A capacitated adult holds the authority to accept or refuse treatment. The DPOAHC is meaningful but dormant because the activation condition—loss of decisional capacity—has not occurred.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有决策能力的成年人有权接受或拒绝治疗。DPOAHC 文件本身有法律意义，但由于触发生效条件——丧失决策能力——尚未发生，因此目前尚未生效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let the phrase 'power of attorney' automatically shift authority away from a patient. Ask whether the patient currently lacks capacity and whether the document is activated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因为看到“授权代理人”就自动把决定权从患者身上转移。先判断患者当前是否无能力，以及文件是否已经生效。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1713,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,40],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The physician suggests scheduling the PEG consult anyway to calm the family. What is the nurse's priority ethical obligation?","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：医师建议仍先安排 PEG 会诊以安抚家属。护士最优先的伦理职责是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority ethical obligation?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最优先的伦理职责是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: The physician suggests scheduling the PEG consult anyway to calm the family.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段 2：医师建议仍先安排 PEG 会诊以安抚家属。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Advocate for Mrs. Ellison's informed, voluntary refusal so it is not overridden by family pressure or provider ambivalence.","zh":"为 Ellison 太太知情、自愿的拒绝进行倡导，防止其意愿被家属压力或医师摇摆态度覆盖。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prioritize correcting malnutrition because albumin and prealbumin are low.","zh":"优先纠正营养不良，因为白蛋白和前白蛋白偏低。"},{"id":"B","en":"Schedule the consult because allowing GI to speak with her is a neutral way to keep the family calm.","zh":"安排会诊，因为让胃肠科与她谈谈是一种中立方式，也能让家属平静。"},{"id":"E","en":"Tell the family the nurse cannot discuss the situation and avoid further contact with them.","zh":"告诉家属护士不能讨论此事，并避免继续接触他们。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stay neutral and let the physician and family resolve the disagreement without nursing involvement.","zh":"保持中立，让医师和家属自行解决分歧，护士不介入。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate ethical risk is that the patient's autonomous refusal may be undermined. Nursing advocacy means protecting the patient's voice, while still addressing family distress through appropriate interdisciplinary support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前最直接的伦理风险是患者自主拒绝可能被削弱。护理倡导意味着保护患者的声音，同时通过合适的跨专业支持处理家属痛苦。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several concerns compete, identify what is being threatened right now. Here, the threat is not malnutrition alone; it is loss of the patient's autonomous choice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个问题竞争优先级时，要找出当前正在受威胁的是什么。本题中受威胁的不只是营养状态，而是患者自主选择权。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1714,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,47],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Which nursing actions are appropriate to uphold Mrs. Ellison's wishes and address the family conflict? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：哪些护理措施适合用于维护 Ellison 太太的意愿并处理家属冲突？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Ellison's wishes and address the family conflict?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段 2：哪些护理措施适合用于维护 Ellison 太太的意愿并处理家属冲突？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Communicate directly with the physician that scheduling a PEG consult over the documented refusal raises an ethical concern.","zh":"直接与医师沟通：在已有拒绝记录的情况下安排 PEG 会诊存在伦理问题。"},{"id":"A","en":"Confirm with Mrs. Ellison that her decision remains informed and voluntary and assess whether pressure has affected her choice.","zh":"与 Ellison 太太确认其决定仍是知情且自愿的，并评估压力是否影响了她的选择。"},{"id":"E","en":"Encourage Mrs. Ellison to meet with GI and reconsider PEG placement for her family's sake.","zh":"鼓励 Ellison 太太为了家属而见胃肠科医师并重新考虑 PEG 置管。"},{"id":"B","en":"Document her repeated refusal with direct quotes and nursing observations of alertness, orientation, calm affect, and values-based reasoning.","zh":"记录她反复拒绝的内容，包括直接引语，以及护士观察到的清醒、定向力正常、情绪平静和基于价值观的推理。"},{"id":"F","en":"Defer to David's demand because he holds the DPOAHC document and is threatening escalation.","zh":"因为 David 持有 DPOAHC 文件且威胁升级，所以听从他的要求。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request palliative-care/social-work support and help arrange a structured family meeting with Mrs. Ellison's consent and participation as she desires.","zh":"申请姑息治疗和社工支持，并在 Ellison 太太同意且愿意参与的情况下协助安排结构化家庭会议。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate advocacy is coordinated: reassess voluntariness, document clearly, address the physician's plan directly, and bring in palliative care, social work, and a family meeting to support goals-of-care clarification without pressuring the patient.","rationaleCorrectZh":"适当的倡导是多方面协调进行的：重新评估自愿性，清楚记录，直接处理医师拟安排会诊的问题，并引入姑息治疗、社工和家庭会议，在不施压患者的前提下澄清照护目标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SATA advocacy items, select actions that protect the patient, create a record, communicate up the chain, and use team resources. Eliminate actions that persuade, pressure, or defer to the wrong decision-maker.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做多选倡导题时，选择能保护患者、形成记录、向上沟通并使用团队资源的措施。排除劝说、施压或把决定权交给错误对象的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1715,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[32,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,64],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: After reassessing Mrs. Ellison and confirming that she remains alert, informed, voluntary, and consistent in refusing PEG placement, what is the nurse's first advocacy action?","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：护士重新评估 Ellison 太太，并确认她仍然清醒、知情、自愿且一致地拒绝 PEG 置管后，第一项倡导行动应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Ellison and confirming that she remains alert, informed, voluntary, and consistent in refusing PEG placement, what is the nurse's first advocacy action?","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 2：护士重新评估 Ellison 太太，并确认她仍然清醒、知情、自愿且一致地拒绝 PEG 置管后，第一项倡导行动应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: After reassessing Mrs.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Finish documenting the refusal first and wait to speak with the physician after the family meeting is arranged.","zh":"先完成拒绝记录，等家庭会议安排好后再与医师沟通。"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask David to bring the DPOAHC paperwork to the unit before taking further action.","zh":"先请 David 把 DPOAHC 文件带到病区，再采取进一步行动。"},{"id":"A","en":"Respectfully tell the physician without delay that Mrs. Ellison again declined PEG placement, capacity is documented, and scheduling the consult over refusal raises an ethical concern.","zh":"立即且尊重地告知医师：Ellison 太太再次拒绝 PEG，决策能力已有记录，在其拒绝后仍安排会诊存在伦理问题。"},{"id":"C","en":"Call the ethics committee first before addressing the concern with the physician.","zh":"先联系伦理委员会，再与医师处理此问题。"},{"id":"E","en":"Ask Mrs. Ellison whether she will agree to a one-time GI consult so the family can feel reassured.","zh":"询问 Ellison 太太是否愿意接受一次胃肠科会诊，好让家属安心。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The physician's proposed consult is the proximate threat to autonomy. The nurse should use clear structured communication to stop the consult from being placed over the patient's refusal and recommend palliative care and a family meeting instead.","rationaleCorrectZh":"医师拟安排会诊是当前最直接威胁患者自主权的因素。护士应使用清楚、有结构的沟通，防止在患者拒绝后仍安排会诊，并建议转向姑息治疗和家庭会议。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For 'first action' questions, choose the step that addresses the most immediate threat. Here, the consult order is the immediate threat, so direct provider communication comes before slower support processes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做“第一步行动”题时，选择能处理最即时威胁的步骤。本题中会诊医嘱是即时威胁，因此应先直接与医师沟通，再进行较慢的支持流程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1716,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.300.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: For each finding, indicate whether it shows effective advocacy for Mrs. Ellison's autonomous refusal.","fullStemZh":"阶段 3：请判断每项发现是否表明对 Ellison 太太自主拒绝的护理倡导有效。","terminalSentenceEn":"Ellison's autonomous refusal.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 3：请判断每项发现是否表明对 Ellison 太太自主拒绝的护理倡导有效。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 3: For each finding, indicate whether it shows effective advocacy for Mrs.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Nursing notes and the palliative-care assessment consistently document her capacity, values-based reasoning, and refusal.","zh":"护理记录和姑息治疗评估均一致记录她有决策能力、基于价值观推理并拒绝 PEG。"},{"id":"r2","en":"No PEG consult has been placed over the patient's refusal.","zh":"未在患者拒绝后仍安排 PEG 会诊。"},{"id":"r3","en":"A comfort-focused plan and hospice referral are being developed according to her expressed wishes.","zh":"正在根据她表达的意愿制定以舒适为重点的计划并转介临终关怀。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Mrs. Ellison says she is glad someone is listening and asks about hospice options at home.","zh":"Ellison 太太说很高兴有人在听她说话，并询问在家接受临终关怀的选择。"},{"id":"r5","en":"David threatens legal action to obtain a PEG tube placement.","zh":"David 威胁采取法律行动以要求放置 PEG 管。"},{"id":"r6","en":"The admission albumin and prealbumin values were low.","zh":"入院时白蛋白和前白蛋白数值偏低。"}],"columns":[{"id":"effective","en":"Shows effective advocacy","zh":"表明倡导有效"},{"id":"not_indicator","en":"Does not show advocacy effectiveness","zh":"不能表明倡导有效"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["effective"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["effective"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["effective"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["effective"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["not_indicator"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["not_indicator"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective advocacy is shown by documentation, alignment of the plan with the patient's goals, absence of an unauthorized PEG consult, and the patient's perception that her voice is being heard. Ongoing family distress and nutritional lab abnormalities may still exist, but they do not mean advocacy has failed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"倡导有效的证据包括：记录一致、照护计划符合患者目标、未安排未经同意的 PEG 会诊，以及患者感到自己的声音被听见。家属痛苦和营养实验室异常可能仍然存在，但这并不代表倡导失败。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Outcome evaluation should match the goal of the intervention. The goal was not to make everyone agree or normalize labs; it was to protect the patient's informed refusal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果要与干预目标一致。本题目标不是让所有人都同意，也不是让实验室指标正常，而是保护患者的知情拒绝。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1717,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_client_advocacy_refusal_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.301","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.301.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.301.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[275,304],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,96],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3 synthesis: Mrs. Ellison has repeatedly refused PEG placement with documented intact decisional capacity. The physician's suggestion to schedule the consult anyway has been addressed. Palliative care confirms her capacity and wishes, and a family meeting is arranged. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"阶段 3 综合题：Ellison 太太已多次拒绝 PEG 置管，并有完整决策能力的记录。医师曾建议仍安排会诊的问题已被处理。姑息治疗团队确认她有能力且意愿一致，并已安排家庭会议。请完成弓形图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Palliative care confirms her capacity and wishes, and a family meeting is arranged.","penultimateSentenceZh":"姑息治疗团队确认她有能力且意愿一致，并已安排家庭会议。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_active_surrogate","en":"Active surrogate decision-making by the DPOAHC holder","zh":"DPOAHC 持有人已进入有效代理决策状态"},{"id":"bt_cond_autonomous_refusal","en":"Capacitated client's autonomous refusal challenged by dormant surrogate authority","zh":"有决策能力患者的自主拒绝受到尚未生效的代理权挑战"},{"id":"bt_cond_impaired_capacity","en":"Impaired capacity causing an uninformed refusal","zh":"决策能力受损导致的非知情拒绝"}],"correct":"bt_cond_autonomous_refusal"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_action_schedule_peg","en":"Schedule the PEG consult without patient consent to reduce family conflict","zh":"未经患者同意安排 PEG 会诊，以减少家属冲突"},{"id":"bt_action_family_meeting","en":"Facilitate the interdisciplinary family meeting with palliative care and social work support","zh":"在姑息治疗和社工支持下促成跨专业家庭会议"},{"id":"bt_action_physician_direct","en":"Communicate directly with the physician that PEG consult should not proceed over the documented refusal","zh":"直接告知医师，不应在已有拒绝记录的情况下继续安排 PEG 会诊"},{"id":"bt_action_defer_son","en":"Defer to the son's demand because he holds the DPOAHC document","zh":"因儿子持有 DPOAHC 文件而听从其要求"}],"correct":["bt_action_physician_direct","bt_action_family_meeting"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_param_nutrition_labs","en":"Albumin and prealbumin trends","zh":"白蛋白和前白蛋白趋势"},{"id":"bt_param_patient_perception","en":"Mrs. Ellison's statements show she feels heard and free from coercion","zh":"Ellison 太太的表述显示她感到被倾听且未受胁迫"},{"id":"bt_param_plan_alignment","en":"Care plan and orders remain aligned with Mrs. Ellison's stated wishes","zh":"照护计划和医嘱持续符合 Ellison 太太表达的意愿"},{"id":"bt_param_family_satisfaction","en":"Family satisfaction with the decision","zh":"家属对决定的满意度"}],"correct":["bt_param_plan_alignment","bt_param_patient_perception"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The synthesis is an autonomy and advocacy problem, not an active surrogate-decision case. The priority nursing actions are to ensure the refused PEG consult does not proceed and to support a structured family meeting. Monitoring should focus on whether orders and the care plan continue to match the patient's goals and whether she feels respected and not coerced.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本题综合的是自主权和护理倡导问题，而不是有效代理决策情境。优先护理措施是确保患者拒绝后 PEG 会诊不继续进行，并支持结构化家庭会议。监测重点应放在医嘱和照护计划是否持续符合患者目标，以及患者是否感到受尊重且未被胁迫。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bow-tie items, make the center condition match the ethical frame first. Then choose actions and monitoring parameters that follow from that frame, not from the family's preferred outcome.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形图题时，先让中间病情/情况符合伦理框架，再选择由该框架推出的措施和监测指标，而不是依据家属想要的结果。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1718,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.302","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.302.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[348,460],"terminalOffsetsZh":[160,190],"fullStemEn":"Lateral incivility causing a client-safety communication breakdown on a medical-surgical unit Mrs. Dolores Vega, age 71, is hospitalized after hypertensive urgency with CKD stage 3b, HFpEF, and type 2 diabetes. The charge nurse, Marcus Chen, observes a dismissive bedside handoff from senior nurse Renee Talbot to newly licensed nurse Priya Anand. A same-day amlodipine dose increase and q4h blood-pressure monitoring instruction are not verbally communicated.","fullStemZh":"内外科病房中横向不文明行为导致患者安全沟通中断 71 岁的 Dolores Vega 太太因高血压急症后住院，既往有 CKD 3b 期、射血分数保留型心力衰竭和 2 型糖尿病。护士长 Marcus Chen 观察到资深护士 Renee Talbot 向新近取得执照的护士 Priya Anand 进行床旁交接时态度轻慢。当天氨氯地平加量以及每 4 小时监测血压的医嘱未被口头交代。","terminalSentenceEn":"A same-day amlodipine dose increase and q4h blood-pressure monitoring instruction are not verbally communicated.","terminalSentenceZh":"当天氨氯地平加量以及每 4 小时监测血压的医嘱未被口头交代。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse, Marcus Chen, observes a dismissive bedside handoff from senior nurse Renee Talbot to newly licensed nurse Priya Anand.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士长 Marcus Chen 观察到资深护士 Renee Talbot 向新近取得执照的护士 Priya Anand 进行床旁交接时态度轻慢。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case links lateral incivility to a concrete safety failure. Renee's dismissive handoff and omission of a same-day amlodipine increase and q4h monitoring order contributed to missed monitoring. When Mrs. Vega became symptomatic with SBP 186, Marcus appropriately prioritized provider notification and clinical intervention before conduct management. After the BP improved and the headache resolved, Marcus addressed the professional-conduct pattern through private, behavior-focused conversations, coaching, safety reporting, and nurse-manager follow-up. Effective evaluation requires both clinical improvement and evidence that the handoff process changed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例将横向不文明行为与具体安全失败联系起来。Renee 的轻慢交接以及遗漏当天氨氯地平加量和每 4 小时监测医嘱，导致监测漏执行。当 Vega 太太出现症状且 SBP 为 186 时，Marcus 正确地先优先通知住院医并进行临床干预，再处理职业行为问题。BP 改善、头痛消失后，Marcus 通过私下聚焦行为的谈话、指导、安全报告和护士经理跟进来处理专业行为模式。有效评价需要同时看到临床改善和交接流程改变的证据。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding management-of-care cases, follow the safety chain: recognize unprofessional communication, identify how it affects care, close the active client-risk gap, then create accountable follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式护理管理病例中，按安全链思考：识别不专业沟通，判断其如何影响护理，先关闭当前患者风险缺口，再建立可问责的后续处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1719,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,223],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,73],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Highlight the specific cues Marcus should identify as requiring charge-nurse intervention because they show lateral incivility, a safety-relevant handoff omission, or a receiving-nurse response that needs coaching.","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段：请标出 Marcus 应识别为需要护士长介入的具体线索，因为它们显示横向不文明行为、与安全相关的交接遗漏，或接班护士需要指导的反应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Highlight the specific cues Marcus should identify as requiring charge-nurse intervention because they show lateral incivility, a safety-relevant handoff omission, or a receiving-nurse response that needs coaching.","terminalSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段：请标出 Marcus 应识别为需要护士长介入的具体线索，因为它们显示横向不文明行为、与安全相关的交接遗漏，或接班护士需要指导的反应。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Renee speaks rapidly during the bedside handoff.","zh":"Renee 在床旁交接时语速很快。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Renee stands with crossed arms and does not make eye contact.","zh":"Renee 双臂交叉站着，并且没有眼神交流。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Renee says, \"Meds are on the MAR — you can read.\"","zh":"Renee 说：“药物在 MAR 上——你自己会看。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Renee visibly rolls her eyes when Priya asks whether any medications changed, and Mrs. Vega sees it.","zh":"Priya 询问药物是否有变更时，Renee 明显翻白眼，而且 Vega 太太看见了。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Renee says, \"I'm not going to spoon-feed you.\"","zh":"Renee 说：“我不会手把手喂给你。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Renee leaves the room without allowing time for questions.","zh":"Renee 没有留下提问时间就离开病房。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Renee does not verbally communicate that amlodipine was increased from 5 mg to 10 mg and given at 1700.","zh":"Renee 没有口头交代氨氯地平已从 5 mg 增至 10 mg，并已在 1700 给药。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Renee does not verbally communicate the hospitalist's instruction to monitor BP q4h for 24 hours.","zh":"Renee 没有口头交代住院医嘱要求 24 小时内每 4 小时监测 BP。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"In the hallway Renee says, \"She'll be calling you every five minutes to hold her hand.\"","zh":"Renee 在走廊说：“她每五分钟都会叫你去哄她。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"Priya accepts the incomplete report and moves on without clarifying or escalating.","zh":"Priya 接受了不完整的交接，没有进一步澄清或升级处理就继续工作。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3","s4","s5","s6","s7","s8","s9","s10"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The key cues are the dismissive statements, the eye-roll in front of the patient, the failure to allow questions, the omitted medication-change and monitoring-order information, the public belittling comment, and Priya's failure to advocate for a complete report. Rapid speech and crossed arms contribute to tone but are less specific as isolated cues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键线索包括贬低性话语、在患者面前翻白眼、不给提问机会、遗漏药物变更和监测医嘱、公开贬低同事，以及 Priya 未能要求完整交接。语速快和双臂交叉会影响氛围，但单独来看不如这些线索具体。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cue-recognition items, separate vague tone cues from concrete behaviors and omissions that can affect client safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做识别线索题时，要把笼统的语气/态度线索与会影响患者安全的具体行为和遗漏区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1720,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,46],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Classify each communication behavior.","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段：请将每一种沟通行为分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Classify each communication behavior.","terminalSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段：请将每一种沟通行为分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"\"Meds are on the MAR — you can read.\"","zh":"“药物在 MAR 上——你自己会看。”"},{"id":"r2","en":"Visible eye-roll in front of the patient when Priya asks about medication changes","zh":"Priya 询问药物变更时，在患者面前明显翻白眼"},{"id":"r3","en":"Hallway comment that Priya will call every five minutes to \"hold her hand\"","zh":"在走廊说 Priya 会每五分钟叫人去“哄她”"},{"id":"r4","en":"Failure to verbally communicate the amlodipine dose change and q4h BP monitoring order","zh":"未口头交代氨氯地平剂量变更和每 4 小时 BP 监测医嘱"},{"id":"r5","en":"Speaking rapidly during a busy change-of-shift handoff","zh":"在繁忙交接班时语速较快"},{"id":"r6","en":"Privately telling a newer nurse, \"Check the MAR before handoff so we can focus on changes — let's make that our routine.\"","zh":"私下对新护士说：“交接前先查看 MAR，这样我们可以重点讨论变化——以后就按这个流程来。”"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_safety","en":"Patient-safety communication failure/professional lapse","zh":"患者安全沟通失败/专业失误"},{"id":"c_incivility","en":"Lateral incivility","zh":"横向不文明行为"},{"id":"c_assertive","en":"Assertive/acceptable communication or not incivility by itself","zh":"坚定且可接受的沟通，或单独来看不是不文明行为"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c_incivility"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c_incivility"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c_incivility"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c_safety"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c_assertive"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c_assertive"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Incivility is defined by demeaning or disrespectful behavior toward a colleague. The omitted medication and monitoring information is a patient-safety communication failure. Rapid speech alone may reflect workload, and a private, respectful redirect is assertive professional communication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"不文明行为的核心是贬低或不尊重同事。遗漏药物和监测信息属于患者安全沟通失败。单独的语速快可能反映工作负荷；私下、尊重地纠正属于坚定的专业沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Ask whether the behavior corrects practice respectfully or humiliates the person. Firm is not the same as uncivil.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断行为是在尊重地纠正实践，还是在羞辱个人。坚定不等于不文明。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1721,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,96],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Priya reports that Mrs. Vega's BP is 186/102 with a headache, the amlodipine dose change was not communicated, and the 1800 q4h BP check was missed. What is the priority problem for Marcus to address?","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段：Priya 报告 Vega 太太 BP 为 186/102，并有头痛；氨氯地平剂量变更未被交代，1800 的每 4 小时 BP 检查也漏做。Marcus 优先要处理的问题是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the priority problem for Marcus to address?","terminalSentenceZh":"Marcus 优先要处理的问题是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Vega's BP is 186/102 with a headache, the amlodipine dose change was not communicated, and the 1800 q4h BP check was missed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段：Priya 报告 Vega 太太 BP 为 186/102，并有头痛；氨氯地平剂量变更未被交代，1800 的每 4 小时 BP 检查也漏做。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A documentation problem that can be resolved after the shift because the client is alert and oriented","zh":"这是记录问题；患者清醒定向良好，可等班后再处理"},{"id":"B","en":"A client-safety communication breakdown with missed monitoring and a current BP above the provider call threshold","zh":"患者安全沟通中断，导致漏监测，且当前 BP 超过通知医护人员的阈值"},{"id":"C","en":"Priya's inexperience and failure to independently identify the amlodipine dose increase","zh":"Priya 经验不足，未能独立发现氨氯地平剂量增加"},{"id":"A","en":"The interpersonal conflict between Renee and Priya, which should be mediated before contacting the provider","zh":"Renee 和 Priya 之间的人际冲突，应先调解后再联系医护人员"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Client safety is the immediate priority. Mrs. Vega is symptomatic and her SBP of 186 exceeds the hospitalist's call parameter of SBP > 180. The incivility and Priya's learning needs matter, but the active care gap must be closed first.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者安全是立即优先事项。Vega 太太有症状，SBP 186 已超过住院医规定的 SBP > 180 通知阈值。不文明行为和 Priya 的学习需要都重要，但必须先关闭当前护理缺口。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a conduct issue and a client-safety issue coexist, handle the active physiologic/safety risk first, then address the conduct process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当职业行为问题和患者安全问题同时存在时，先处理当前生理/安全风险，再处理行为和流程问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1722,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,97],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,36],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Which actions should Marcus include in the charge-nurse response? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段：Marcus 作为护士长应采取哪些措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: Which actions should Marcus include in the charge-nurse response?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段：Marcus 作为护士长应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Speak privately with Priya to acknowledge the inadequate handoff and coach her to ask clarifying questions or escalate incomplete reports.","zh":"私下与 Priya 交谈，承认交接不足，并指导她对不完整交接提出澄清问题或升级处理。"},{"id":"E","en":"Publicly reprimand Renee at the next staff meeting to set an example.","zh":"在下一次员工会议上公开训斥 Renee，以儆效尤。"},{"id":"A","en":"Instruct Priya to notify the hospitalist now and report the BP, headache, and missed monitoring.","zh":"指导 Priya 立即通知住院医，并报告 BP、头痛和漏监测情况。"},{"id":"F","en":"Do not document the incident because the BP spike was caught before serious harm occurred.","zh":"不要记录此事件，因为血压升高在造成严重伤害前已被发现。"},{"id":"B","en":"Speak privately with Renee, focusing on observed behaviors and the impact on patient care rather than personality.","zh":"私下与 Renee 交谈，聚焦观察到的行为及其对患者护理的影响，而不是评价人格。"},{"id":"D","en":"Complete the appropriate safety/professional-conduct reporting and notify the nurse manager for follow-up.","zh":"完成相应的安全/专业行为报告，并通知护士经理跟进。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Marcus must address the immediate care gap, then use private behavior-focused conversations, coaching, documentation, and manager notification to address the incivility and system failure. Public reprimand escalates incivility, and not documenting removes accountability.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Marcus 必须先处理当前护理缺口，然后通过私下、聚焦行为的谈话、指导、记录和通知护士经理来处理不文明行为和系统失效。公开训斥会升级不文明行为；不记录会移除问责。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For management-of-care SATA items, choose actions that protect the client now and create accountable follow-up later.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做护理管理类多选题时，选择既能立即保护患者、又能建立后续问责的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1723,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,37],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: What should Marcus do first?","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段：Marcus 首先应该做什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 2: What should Marcus do first?","terminalSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段：Marcus 首先应该做什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Take over the primary nurse's role and call the hospitalist himself without involving Priya.","zh":"Marcus 自己接管责任护士角色，直接联系住院医，不让 Priya 参与。"},{"id":"A","en":"Tell Priya to notify the hospitalist now using the stated call parameter and report the current BP, headache, and missed monitoring.","zh":"告诉 Priya 依据明确通知参数立即联系住院医，并报告当前 BP、头痛和漏监测。"},{"id":"C","en":"Complete the incident report before contacting the hospitalist so the event is documented accurately.","zh":"先完成事件报告，确保记录准确后再联系住院医。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call Renee first to hear her perspective on the handoff before taking further action.","zh":"先打电话给 Renee，听取她对交接的看法，再采取进一步措施。"},{"id":"D","en":"Have Priya recheck the BP at the next q4h interval because the headache is mild.","zh":"因为头痛较轻，让 Priya 到下一次每 4 小时间隔时再复测 BP。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first action is to ensure the hospitalist is notified now because the stated SBP > 180 parameter has been crossed and the client has a headache. Supporting Priya through the call preserves patient safety and builds her competence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要措施是确保立即通知住院医，因为明确的 SBP > 180 参数已被触发，且患者有头痛。护士长支持 Priya 完成通话，既保护患者安全，也培养她的能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For first-action questions, identify the intervention that reduces the current risk without unnecessary delay.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做首要措施题时，找出能立即降低当前风险且不造成不必要延误的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1724,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.302.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[123,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,50],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: Which findings best show that Marcus's interventions addressed both the care gap and the communication breakdown? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段：哪些发现最能说明 Marcus 的干预同时处理了护理缺口和沟通中断？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 3: Which findings best show that Marcus's interventions addressed both the care gap and the communication breakdown?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 3 阶段：哪些发现最能说明 Marcus 的干预同时处理了护理缺口和沟通中断？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Renee and Priya become personally friendly and socialize together during breaks.","zh":"Renee 和 Priya 私下变得亲近，并在休息时一起社交。"},{"id":"C","en":"Subsequent handoffs include verbal medication changes, monitoring orders, and time for clarifying questions.","zh":"后续交接包括口头说明药物变更、监测医嘱，并留出澄清问题时间。"},{"id":"A","en":"Mrs. Vega's BP decreases from 186/102 to 162/90 and then 154/86, and her headache resolves.","zh":"Vega 太太 BP 从 186/102 降至 162/90，再到 154/86，头痛消失。"},{"id":"D","en":"No further care omissions related to handoff occur, and nurse-manager follow-up is documented.","zh":"未再发生与交接相关的护理遗漏，并且护士经理的跟进已记录。"},{"id":"B","en":"Priya documents the q4h BP checks and updates the care plan with the current amlodipine dose and monitoring schedule.","zh":"Priya 记录每 4 小时 BP 检查，并在护理计划中更新当前氨氯地平剂量和监测安排。"},{"id":"F","en":"Mrs. Vega's serum creatinine trend improves during the admission.","zh":"Vega 太太住院期间血清肌酐趋势改善。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Resolution requires clinical and process evidence: BP improves and symptoms resolve, monitoring is performed and documented, the care plan reflects the order, handoffs become complete and professional, and manager follow-up occurs. Friendship and creatinine trends do not evaluate the communication breakdown.","rationaleCorrectZh":"解决情况需要临床和流程两方面证据：BP 改善且症状消失，监测已执行并记录，护理计划反映医嘱，交接变得完整且专业，并有护士经理跟进。个人友谊和肌酐趋势不能评价沟通中断是否解决。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Outcome evaluation should match the original problem: check both the client response and the process that caused the risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果时要对应原问题：既看患者反应，也看造成风险的流程是否改善。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1725,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_lateral_incivility_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.303","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.303.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.303.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[297,326],"terminalOffsetsZh":[121,129],"fullStemEn":"At 2200, Priya reports Mrs. Vega's BP is 186/102 with a headache. She has just discovered that the amlodipine dose was increased today, the hospitalist ordered BP monitoring q4h x 24 hours with a call if SBP > 180, and the 1800 monitoring check was missed after an incomplete, dismissive handoff. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"2200，Priya 报告 Vega 太太 BP 为 186/102，并有头痛。她刚发现今天氨氯地平已加量，住院医要求 24 小时内每 4 小时监测 BP，若 SBP > 180 则通知；而由于一次不完整且轻慢的交接，1800 的监测已漏做。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"She has just discovered that the amlodipine dose was increased today, the hospitalist ordered BP monitoring q4h x 24 hours with a call if SBP > 180, and the 1800 monitoring check was missed after an incomplete, dismissive handoff.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她刚发现今天氨氯地平已加量，住院医要求 24 小时内每 4 小时监测 BP，若 SBP > 180 则通知；而由于一次不完整且轻慢的交接，1800 的监测已漏做。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_c1","en":"Client-safety communication breakdown resulting from unresolved lateral incivility","zh":"未解决的横向不文明行为导致患者安全沟通中断"},{"id":"bt_c3","en":"Routine interpersonal friction requiring no formal intervention","zh":"无需正式介入的普通人际摩擦"},{"id":"bt_c2","en":"Isolated knowledge deficit in the new nurse","zh":"新护士单纯知识不足"}],"correct":"bt_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_a1","en":"Have Priya notify the hospitalist immediately with the BP, headache, and missed monitoring intervals","zh":"让 Priya 立即向住院医报告 BP、头痛和漏监测时间段"},{"id":"bt_a2","en":"Speak privately with Renee about specific observed behaviors, patient-care impact, and policy-based documentation","zh":"私下与 Renee 讨论具体观察到的行为、对患者护理的影响，以及按政策记录"},{"id":"bt_a3","en":"Address the interpersonal conflict with Renee before contacting the hospitalist","zh":"先处理与 Renee 的人际冲突，再联系住院医"},{"id":"bt_a4","en":"Do not document or notify the manager because serious harm was avoided","zh":"因为避免了严重伤害，所以不记录也不通知护士经理"}],"correct":["bt_a1","bt_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_p4","en":"Mrs. Vega's serum creatinine trend","zh":"Vega 太太的血清肌酐趋势"},{"id":"bt_p1","en":"Completeness and professionalism of subsequent handoffs, including medication changes and time for questions","zh":"后续交接的完整性和专业性，包括药物变更和提问时间"},{"id":"bt_p2","en":"Adherence to the q4h BP monitoring schedule and absence of further care omissions","zh":"是否遵守每 4 小时 BP 监测安排，并且无进一步护理遗漏"},{"id":"bt_p3","en":"Whether Renee and Priya become personal friends during breaks","zh":"Renee 和 Priya 是否在休息时成为私人朋友"}],"correct":["bt_p1","bt_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bow-tie centers on a client-safety communication breakdown caused by lateral incivility. The immediate action is provider notification because the SBP exceeds the ordered threshold and the client is symptomatic. The second priority is structured, private conduct follow-up with policy-based documentation. Monitoring must evaluate both the corrected BP-monitoring process and the professionalism/completeness of later handoffs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本蝴蝶结题的核心是横向不文明行为导致患者安全沟通中断。立即措施是通知住院医，因为 SBP 超过医嘱阈值且患者有症状。第二个优先事项是进行结构化、私下的行为跟进，并按政策记录。监测必须同时评价 BP 监测流程是否纠正，以及后续交接是否专业且完整。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bow-tie items, choose the condition that explains the whole chain, then pair one immediate safety action with one process action and monitor outcomes that match both.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，选择能解释整条事件链的问题，再搭配一个立即安全措施和一个流程措施，并监测与二者相符的结果。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1726,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.304","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.304.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[470,579],"terminalOffsetsZh":[165,194],"fullStemEn":"Clozapine-associated febrile neutropenia with early myocarditis A 29-year-old man with treatment-resistant schizophrenia is admitted to an inpatient psychiatric unit for clozapine initiation after two adequate antipsychotic trials failed. Baseline ANC is adequate for treatment. Facility policy requires holding clozapine and notifying the provider for temperature 101.3 °F (38.5 °C) or higher, ANC in the moderate or severe neutropenia range, or suspected myocarditis. Standing orders include orthostatic vital signs, bowel monitoring, and metabolic monitoring during titration.","fullStemZh":"氯氮平相关发热性中性粒细胞减少伴早期心肌炎 一名29岁男性因难治性精神分裂症住入精神科病房，既往两种抗精神病药足量足疗程治疗失败后开始氯氮平。基线 ANC 符合用药条件。机构政策规定：体温达到或超过 101.3 °F (38.5 °C)、ANC 达到中度或重度中性粒细胞减少范围，或怀疑心肌炎时，护士应暂停氯氮平并通知医嘱开立者。滴定期间还需按医嘱监测体位性生命体征、排便情况和代谢指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Standing orders include orthostatic vital signs, bowel monitoring, and metabolic monitoring during titration.","terminalSentenceZh":"滴定期间还需按医嘱监测体位性生命体征、排便情况和代谢指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires holding clozapine and notifying the provider for temperature 101.3 °F (38.5 °C) or higher, ANC in the moderate or severe neutropenia range, or suspected myocarditis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：体温达到或超过 101.3 °F (38.5 °C)、ANC 达到中度或重度中性粒细胞减少范围，或怀疑心肌炎时，护士应暂停氯氮平并通知医嘱开立者。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case tests recognition of two simultaneous serious clozapine toxicities. On Day 10, sialorrhea, orthostatic symptoms, constipation, and early metabolic changes are expected clozapine effects that require monitoring and supportive management. On Day 18, fever and sore throat with ANC 980/µL require immediate interruption of clozapine and urgent management of febrile neutropenia. At the same time, new chest pressure, tachycardia, dyspnea, S3, crackles, edema, troponin elevation, CRP elevation, BNP elevation, and echocardiographic dysfunction support clozapine-associated myocarditis. The safe nursing arc is to hold the causative medication per policy, notify the provider, initiate cardiac and neutropenic safety measures, obtain cultures before antibiotics, administer prescribed empiric antibiotics promptly after cultures, and evaluate recovery using ANC, troponin/CRP trends, symptoms, and cardiac function rather than early marginal vital-sign improvement alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例考查对两种同时发生的严重氯氮平毒性的识别。第10天的流涎、体位性症状、便秘和早期代谢改变是氯氮平可预期的不良反应，需要监测和支持处理。第18天，发热、咽痛并伴 ANC 980/µL，要求立即暂停氯氮平并紧急处理发热性中性粒细胞减少。同时，新发胸部压迫感、心动过速、气短、S3、湿啰音、水肿、肌钙蛋白升高、CRP 升高、BNP 升高以及超声心动图功能异常，支持氯氮平相关心肌炎。安全的护理思路是按政策暂停致病药物、通知医嘱开立者、启动心脏和中性粒细胞减少相关安全措施、在抗生素前抽取血培养、抽血培养后及时给予医嘱的经验性抗生素，并用 ANC、肌钙蛋白/CRP 趋势、症状和心功能来评估恢复，而不能仅凭早期生命体征略有改善就放松警惕。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected medication adverse effects from sentinel toxicities. When one medication can explain multiple acute life-threatening changes, stop the ongoing harm first and escalate while protecting airway, circulation, and infection safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要区分可预期的药物不良反应和提示危重毒性的警讯。当同一种药物可以解释多项急性、危及生命的变化时，先停止持续伤害并升级处理，同时保护气道/循环和感染安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1727,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[32,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,54],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2 data are now available. For each finding, classify whether it is an urgent new cue, a previously identified expected clozapine effect, or a nonemergent metabolic monitoring issue.","fullStemZh":"现在可查看阶段2资料。请将每项发现分类为：紧急的新线索、既往已识别的预期氯氮平反应，或非紧急的代谢监测问题。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, classify whether it is an urgent new cue, a previously identified expected clozapine effect, or a nonemergent metabolic monitoring issue.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每项发现分类为：紧急的新线索、既往已识别的预期氯氮平反应，或非紧急的代谢监测问题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2 data are now available.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现在可查看阶段2资料。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Temperature 101.7 °F (38.7 °C) with sore throat","zh":"体温101.7 °F (38.7 °C)并伴咽痛"},{"id":"r2","en":"Resting HR 118 with new chest pressure","zh":"静息 HR 118并有新发胸部压迫感"},{"id":"r3","en":"New S3 gallop, bibasilar crackles, and ankle edema","zh":"新发 S3 奔马律、双肺底湿啰音和踝部水肿"},{"id":"r4","en":"Nighttime drooling noted at Day 10","zh":"第10天已发现夜间流涎"},{"id":"r5","en":"Orthostatic lightheadedness documented at Day 10","zh":"第10天已记录体位性头晕"},{"id":"r6","en":"Fasting glucose 124 mg/dL during titration","zh":"滴定期间空腹血糖124 mg/dL"}],"columns":[{"id":"expected","en":"Expected/previously managed effect","zh":"预期或已处理的不良反应"},{"id":"metabolic","en":"Metabolic monitoring issue","zh":"代谢监测问题"},{"id":"urgent","en":"Urgent new cue","zh":"紧急新线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["urgent"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["urgent"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["urgent"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["expected"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["expected"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["metabolic"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fever with sore throat is a sentinel cue for clozapine-related neutropenia and infection risk. New chest pressure, marked resting tachycardia, dyspnea, S3, crackles, and edema are urgent cardiac cues for myocarditis/heart failure. Drooling and orthostatic symptoms were already identified on Day 10 as expected clozapine adverse effects. Mild hyperglycemia is important for metabolic monitoring but is not the acute emergency.","rationaleCorrectZh":"发热伴咽痛是提示氯氮平相关中性粒细胞减少和感染风险的警讯。新发胸部压迫感、明显静息心动过速、气短、S3、湿啰音和水肿是提示心肌炎/心衰的紧急心脏线索。流涎和体位性症状在第10天已被识别为可预期的氯氮平不良反应。轻度高血糖需要代谢监测，但不是当前急症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize acute changes over known side effects. New fever, infection symptoms, chest pain, dyspnea, and heart-failure signs outrank chronic constipation, drooling, or metabolic trends.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先处理急性变化，而不是已知不良反应。新发发热、感染症状、胸痛、气短和心衰体征，优先级高于慢性便秘、流涎或代谢趋势。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1728,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,20],"fullStemEn":"Which interpretations are supported by the Stage 2 findings? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段2发现支持哪些解释？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interpretations are supported by the Stage 2 findings?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段2发现支持哪些解释？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The ANC decline is best explained by myocarditis alone, so neutropenia-specific precautions can wait.","zh":"ANC 下降最好用单纯心肌炎解释，因此中性粒细胞减少相关防护可以等待。"},{"id":"D","en":"All findings should be treated as anxiety or somatic delusions because the client is on an inpatient psychiatric unit.","zh":"因为患者在精神科病房，所以所有发现都应视为焦虑或躯体妄想。"},{"id":"B","en":"Troponin 0.48 ng/mL, CRP 68 mg/L, BNP 420 pg/mL, tachycardia, S3, crackles, and edema support suspected clozapine-associated myocarditis.","zh":"肌钙蛋白0.48 ng/mL、CRP 68 mg/L、BNP 420 pg/mL、心动过速、S3、湿啰音和水肿，支持疑似氯氮平相关心肌炎。"},{"id":"F","en":"The improving hallucinations make clozapine toxicity unlikely.","zh":"幻听改善说明氯氮平毒性不太可能。"},{"id":"E","en":"The abnormal cardiac biomarkers and heart-failure signs are not explained by the falling ANC alone.","zh":"异常心脏生物标志物和心衰体征不能仅用 ANC 下降解释。"},{"id":"A","en":"The ANC of 980/µL with fever and sore throat supports moderate neutropenia with high infection risk.","zh":"ANC 980/µL 加发热和咽痛，支持中度中性粒细胞减少并有高感染风险。"}],"correct":["A","B","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The data support two concurrent clozapine emergencies: febrile moderate neutropenia and suspected myocarditis. The falling ANC with fever and sore throat creates high infection risk. The troponin/CRP/BNP elevations with tachycardia, S3, crackles, edema, and chest pressure point to myocardial inflammation and early heart-failure physiology. These processes overlap clinically but require distinct management pathways.","rationaleCorrectZh":"资料支持两个同时发生的氯氮平急症：发热性中度中性粒细胞减少和疑似心肌炎。ANC 下降并伴发热、咽痛，造成高感染风险。肌钙蛋白/CRP/BNP 升高，加上心动过速、S3、湿啰音、水肿和胸部压迫感，指向心肌炎症和早期心衰生理。两者临床表现可重叠，但管理路径不同。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When labs and exam findings point in two directions, do not force one diagnosis to explain everything. Ask what each abnormal value physiologically represents.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当实验室和体征指向两个方向时，不要强行用一个诊断解释所有发现。要问每个异常值代表什么生理问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1729,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,77],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which priority and immediate nursing action are most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，最合适的优先问题和立即护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which priority and immediate nursing action are most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段2，最合适的优先问题和立即护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Priority: improved hallucinations; action: administer the next clozapine dose to preserve psychiatric gains.","zh":"优先：幻听改善；措施：给予下一剂氯氮平以维持精神症状改善。"},{"id":"C","en":"Priority: constipation and drooling; action: request an anticholinergic medication before addressing the fever.","zh":"优先：便秘和流涎；措施：在处理发热前先申请抗胆碱药。"},{"id":"E","en":"Priority: anxiety-related chest discomfort; action: provide reassurance and reassess after the next group session.","zh":"优先：焦虑相关胸部不适；措施：给予安慰并在下一次团体治疗后复评。"},{"id":"A","en":"Priority: concurrent life-threatening clozapine toxicities; action: hold clozapine immediately per policy and notify the provider.","zh":"优先：同时发生危及生命的氯氮平毒性；措施：按政策立即暂停氯氮平并通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Priority: metabolic syndrome risk; action: focus first on diet teaching for rising glucose and triglycerides.","zh":"优先：代谢综合征风险；措施：先重点进行血糖和甘油三酯升高的饮食教育。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate priority is the combined acute toxicity: febrile moderate neutropenia and suspected myocarditis. Holding clozapine stops ongoing exposure to the causative medication and is authorized by the facility policy. Provider notification is essential because blood cultures, empiric antibiotics, echocardiography, cardiology consultation, and higher-level monitoring require orders or coordinated escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前立即优先问题是合并急性毒性：发热性中度中性粒细胞减少和疑似心肌炎。暂停氯氮平可停止继续暴露于致病药物，且机构政策允许这样做。必须通知医嘱开立者，因为血培养、经验性抗生素、超声心动图、心内科会诊和更高级别监护需要医嘱或协调升级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a medication causes an acute dangerous reaction, the first safe nursing move is usually to stop or hold the exposure if policy permits, then escalate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当药物导致急性危险反应时，如果政策允许，护士最先的安全措施通常是停止或暂停继续暴露，然后升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1730,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"After holding clozapine and notifying the provider, which interventions should the nurse anticipate or implement for this client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"暂停氯氮平并通知医嘱开立者后，护士应预期或实施哪些干预？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After holding clozapine and notifying the provider, which interventions should the nurse anticipate or implement for this client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"暂停氯氮平并通知医嘱开立者后，护士应预期或实施哪些干预？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Implement neutropenic precautions according to facility protocol and reinforce hand hygiene/visitor screening.","zh":"按机构方案实施中性粒细胞减少防护，并强化手卫生和访客筛查。"},{"id":"F","en":"Delay antibiotics until the ANC has recovered to at least 1,500/µL to avoid masking the trend.","zh":"推迟抗生素，直到 ANC 恢复到至少1,500/µL，以免掩盖趋势。"},{"id":"B","en":"Draw blood cultures as ordered before starting prescribed empiric antibiotics.","zh":"按医嘱在开始经验性抗生素前抽取血培养。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer the next clozapine dose with acetaminophen so the fever decreases while psychiatric symptoms stay controlled.","zh":"给予下一剂氯氮平并合用对乙酰氨基酚，使发热下降并维持精神症状控制。"},{"id":"D","en":"Anticipate orders for serial troponins, ECGs, echocardiography, and cardiology consultation.","zh":"预期会有连续肌钙蛋白、心电图、超声心动图和心内科会诊医嘱。"},{"id":"C","en":"Place the client on continuous cardiac monitoring, apply oxygen as needed, and monitor for worsening hypotension, arrhythmias, dyspnea, and urine-output decline.","zh":"给予连续心电监护，按需吸氧，并监测低血压加重、心律失常、气短加重和尿量下降。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This client needs simultaneous febrile-neutropenia and myocarditis management. Neutropenic precautions reduce exposure to new pathogens. Cultures should be obtained before prescribed empiric antibiotics whenever this can be done without delaying therapy. Continuous cardiac monitoring, oxygen, hemodynamic monitoring, serial biomarkers, ECG/echo assessment, and cardiology involvement track progression and identify deterioration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者需要同时管理发热性中性粒细胞减少和心肌炎。中性粒细胞减少防护可减少接触新病原体。只要不延误治疗，应在给予医嘱的经验性抗生素前抽取血培养。连续心电监护、吸氧、血流动力学监测、连续生物标志物、心电图/超声心动图评估和心内科参与，可追踪病情进展并识别恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For concurrent emergencies, choose interventions that cover both pathways without delaying time-critical care: infection protection/cultures/antibiotics plus cardiac monitoring and diagnostics.","testTakingStrategyZh":"面对并发急症，应选择能覆盖两条处理路径且不延误时效性治疗的措施：感染防护、培养、抗生素，加上心脏监护和诊断。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1731,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,235],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,67],"fullStemEn":"The Stage 2 clozapine dose has not yet been given. Place the time-critical actions in the safest order. Neutropenic precautions should also be initiated, but these options focus on the serial steps that have clear ordering constraints.","fullStemZh":"阶段2的氯氮平剂量尚未给予。请按最安全顺序排列具有时效性的措施。也应启动中性粒细胞减少防护，但以下选项聚焦于有明确先后关系的连续步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Neutropenic precautions should also be initiated, but these options focus on the serial steps that have clear ordering constraints.","terminalSentenceZh":"也应启动中性粒细胞减少防护，但以下选项聚焦于有明确先后关系的连续步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Place the time-critical actions in the safest order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请按最安全顺序排列具有时效性的措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hold clozapine; ensure the scheduled dose is not administered.","zh":"暂停氯氮平；确保本次预定剂量不被给予。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer prescribed empiric broad-spectrum antipseudomonal antibiotics after cultures are obtained.","zh":"培养抽取后给予医嘱的经验性广谱抗假单胞菌抗生素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider using focused SBAR with fever, ANC, chest findings, troponin, CRP, and BNP.","zh":"用聚焦 SBAR 通知医嘱开立者，包含发热、ANC、胸部/心脏发现、肌钙蛋白、CRP 和 BNP。"},{"id":"D","en":"Draw ordered blood cultures before antibiotics.","zh":"在抗生素前按医嘱抽取血培养。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply oxygen as needed and place the client on continuous cardiac monitoring.","zh":"按需吸氧，并将患者置于连续心电监护。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first step is to prevent further clozapine exposure. Provider notification follows immediately because cultures, antibiotics, echocardiography, and consultations require orders. Cardiac monitoring and oxygen are direct safety actions for a symptomatic tachycardic client with suspected myocarditis. Blood cultures should precede antibiotics when possible, and prescribed empiric antibiotics should follow promptly after cultures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一步是防止继续暴露于氯氮平。随后应立即通知医嘱开立者，因为培养、抗生素、超声心动图和会诊需要医嘱。对于有症状、心动过速并疑似心肌炎的患者，心电监护和吸氧是直接安全措施。只要可能，血培养应在抗生素前完成；抽取后应及时给予医嘱的经验性抗生素。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In ordered-response questions, look for true sequencing rules: stop harm first, communicate early for orders, stabilize the client, collect cultures before antibiotics, then give the ordered antibiotics promptly.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做排序题时，寻找真正的先后规则：先停止伤害，尽早沟通取得医嘱，稳定患者，抗生素前先取培养，然后及时给予医嘱抗生素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1732,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.304.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,25],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which evaluations or conclusions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3，哪些评估或结论是合适的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which evaluations or conclusions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3，哪些评估或结论是合适的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Worsening hypotension, increasing tachycardia, new arrhythmias, decreasing urine output, worsening dyspnea, or new infection signs require escalation.","zh":"低血压加重、心动过速增加、新发心律失常、尿量下降、气短加重或新的感染征象需要升级处理。"},{"id":"F","en":"Clozapine can be restarted now because the hallucinations had improved before the adverse reaction.","zh":"现在可以重启氯氮平，因为不良反应前幻听曾改善。"},{"id":"C","en":"Falling troponin/CRP values, symptom improvement, and improved LVEF on repeat echocardiography would support myocarditis recovery.","zh":"肌钙蛋白/CRP 下降、症状改善以及复查超声心动图 LVEF 改善，将支持心肌炎恢复。"},{"id":"B","en":"A rising ANC trend over the next days would support hematologic recovery.","zh":"未来几天 ANC 呈上升趋势将支持血液学恢复。"},{"id":"D","en":"The mild improvement in HR and oxygen saturation proves the toxicities have resolved, so monitoring can be relaxed.","zh":"HR 和血氧饱和度轻度改善证明毒性已经消退，因此可以放松监测。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client is hemodynamically stable but not yet improving because troponin and CRP are still rising and ANC remains low.","zh":"患者血流动力学暂稳定，但尚未改善，因为肌钙蛋白和 CRP 仍在上升，ANC 仍低。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Four hours after holding clozapine is too early to declare resolution. HR and oxygenation are slightly better with rest and oxygen, but ANC remains in the moderate neutropenia range and troponin/CRP are still rising. Recovery should be evaluated with serial ANC, troponin, CRP, symptoms, and cardiac function. Any hemodynamic, rhythm, respiratory, renal-perfusion, or infection deterioration requires escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"暂停氯氮平4小时后还太早，不能宣布问题已解决。休息和吸氧后 HR 和氧合略有改善，但 ANC 仍处于中度中性粒细胞减少范围，肌钙蛋白/CRP 仍在上升。应通过连续 ANC、肌钙蛋白、CRP、症状和心功能评估恢复。任何血流动力学、心律、呼吸、肾灌注或感染方面恶化都需要升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not confuse response to supportive care with resolution of the disease process. Trend the marker that matches the problem: ANC for neutropenia, troponin/CRP/echo for myocarditis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把对支持治疗的反应误认为疾病过程已经解决。根据问题追踪相应指标：中性粒细胞减少看 ANC，心肌炎看肌钙蛋白、CRP 和超声心动图。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1733,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_clozapine_toxicity_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.305","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.305.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.305.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[377,406],"terminalOffsetsZh":[196,204],"fullStemEn":"Day 18–18.5 of clozapine therapy: The client has fever 101.7 °F (38.7 °C), sore throat, ANC 980/µL, new chest pressure, resting HR 118, dyspnea, new S3 gallop, bibasilar crackles, ankle edema, troponin I 0.48 ng/mL rising to 0.52 ng/mL, CRP 68 mg/L rising to 72 mg/L, BNP 420 pg/mL, and echocardiogram showing LVEF 45% with global hypokinesis and a small pericardial effusion. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"氯氮平治疗第18至18.5天：患者体温101.7 °F (38.7 °C)、咽痛、ANC 980/µL、新发胸部压迫感、静息 HR 118、气短、新发 S3 奔马律、双肺底湿啰音、踝部水肿，肌钙蛋白 I 0.48 ng/mL并升至0.52 ng/mL，CRP 68 mg/L并升至72 mg/L，BNP 420 pg/mL，超声心动图显示 LVEF 45%、弥漫性室壁运动减弱和小量心包积液。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Day 18–18.5 of clozapine therapy: The client has fever 101.7 °F (38.7 °C), sore throat, ANC 980/µL, new chest pressure, resting HR 118, dyspnea, new S3 gallop, bibasilar crackles, ankle edema, troponin I 0.48 ng/mL rising to 0.52 ng/mL, CRP 68 mg/L rising to 72 mg/L, BNP 420 pg/mL, and echocardiogram showing LVEF 45% with global hypokinesis and a small pericardial effusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"氯氮平治疗第18至18.5天：患者体温101.7 °F (38.7 °C)、咽痛、ANC 980/µL、新发胸部压迫感、静息 HR 118、气短、新发 S3 奔马律、双肺底湿啰音、踝部水肿，肌钙蛋白 I 0.48 ng/mL并升至0.52 ng/mL，CRP 68 mg/L并升至72 mg/L，BNP 420 pg/mL，超声心动图显示 LVEF 45%、弥漫性室壁运动减弱和小量心包积液。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"cond_dual_toxicity","en":"Concurrent clozapine-induced moderate neutropenia with fever and clozapine-associated myocarditis","zh":"氯氮平导致的发热性中度中性粒细胞减少合并氯氮平相关心肌炎"},{"id":"cond_septic_cardiomyopathy","en":"Sepsis with septic cardiomyopathy as the single primary process","zh":"脓毒症伴脓毒性心肌病作为唯一主要过程"},{"id":"cond_anxiety_reaction","en":"Anxiety-related tachycardia with benign clozapine side effects","zh":"焦虑相关心动过速伴良性氯氮平不良反应"}],"correct":"cond_dual_toxicity"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"act_treat_drooling_first","en":"Focus first on drooling and orthostatic symptoms","zh":"先重点处理流涎和体位性症状"},{"id":"act_continue_clozapine","en":"Continue clozapine because hallucinations are improving","zh":"因幻听改善而继续氯氮平"},{"id":"act_notify_provider","en":"Notify the provider with ANC, fever, cardiac findings, and biomarker changes","zh":"将 ANC、发热、心脏发现和生物标志物变化通知医嘱开立者"},{"id":"act_hold_clozapine","en":"Hold clozapine immediately per facility policy","zh":"按机构政策立即暂停氯氮平"}],"correct":["act_hold_clozapine","act_notify_provider"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"param_troponin_trend","en":"Troponin trend","zh":"肌钙蛋白趋势"},{"id":"param_anc_trend","en":"ANC trend","zh":"ANC 趋势"},{"id":"param_glucose_triglycerides","en":"Fasting glucose and triglycerides","zh":"空腹血糖和甘油三酯"},{"id":"param_aims_score","en":"AIMS score","zh":"AIMS 评分"}],"correct":["param_anc_trend","param_troponin_trend"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bow-tie keys the dual toxicity. Fever and ANC 980/µL require interruption of clozapine and infection-risk management, while troponin/CRP elevation, heart-failure findings, and echocardiographic dysfunction support clozapine-associated myocarditis. Holding clozapine and notifying the provider are the priority nursing actions. ANC and troponin trends directly track hematologic and myocardial recovery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本蝴蝶结题的关键是双重毒性。发热和 ANC 980/µL 要求暂停氯氮平并管理感染风险；肌钙蛋白/CRP 升高、心衰体征和超声心动图功能异常支持氯氮平相关心肌炎。暂停氯氮平并通知医嘱开立者是优先护理措施。ANC 和肌钙蛋白趋势直接追踪血液学和心肌恢复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, match the condition to the entire cue cluster, then choose actions that stop harm and escalate care, and parameters that directly track the selected condition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，先用全部线索群匹配最可能病情，再选择能停止伤害并升级处理的措施，以及能直接追踪该病情的监测指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1734,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.306","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.306.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[448,678],"terminalOffsetsZh":[161,233],"fullStemEn":"Refeeding syndrome during parenteral nutrition initiation in a malnourished post-operative client A 62-year-old woman is admitted to the surgical unit after an open Roux-en-Y revision for a chronic gastrojejunal anastomotic stricture. She had negligible oral or enteral intake for about five weeks before surgery, weighs 46 kg (BMI 17.1), and lost 11 kg over two months. PPN was started in the PACU as a bridge to central TPN after PICC placement. The nutrition consult identifies her as high risk for refeeding syndrome and recommends thiamine before dextrose, electrolyte monitoring every 12 hours for the first 48 hours, and cautious caloric initiation with slow advancement.","fullStemZh":"营养不良术后患者开始肠外营养时发生再喂养综合征 一名 62 岁女性因慢性胃空肠吻合口狭窄接受开放性 Roux-en-Y 修正术后入住外科病区。术前约 5 周几乎不能经口或肠内摄入，体重 46 kg（BMI 17.1），两个月内减重 11 kg。PACU 已开始 PPN，作为 PICC 置管后改用中心静脉 TPN 的过渡。营养会诊判断其为再喂养综合征高风险，建议在给予葡萄糖前先补充硫胺素，术后最初 48 小时每 12 小时监测电解质，并以低热量谨慎开始、缓慢推进。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nutrition consult identifies her as high risk for refeeding syndrome and recommends thiamine before dextrose, electrolyte monitoring every 12 hours for the first 48 hours, and cautious caloric initiation with slow advancement.","terminalSentenceZh":"营养会诊判断其为再喂养综合征高风险，建议在给予葡萄糖前先补充硫胺素，术后最初 48 小时每 12 小时监测电解质，并以低热量谨慎开始、缓慢推进。","penultimateSentenceEn":"PPN was started in the PACU as a bridge to central TPN after PICC placement.","penultimateSentenceZh":"PACU 已开始 PPN，作为 PICC 置管后改用中心静脉 TPN 的过渡。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows a high-risk malnourished post-operative client after parenteral nutrition is started. The key early pattern is a simultaneous fall in phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium with rising glucose, weakness, paresthesias, tachycardia, and decreasing urine output. The Stage 2 deterioration confirms severe refeeding syndrome: worsening hypophosphatemia, hypokalemia, and hypomagnesemia are now accompanied by PVCs, prolonged QT, shallow respirations, muscle weakness, and altered mental status. The possible PICC infection requires paired cultures and antibiotics, but the immediate life threat is electrolyte-driven dysrhythmia and respiratory compromise. Safe management is to urgently notify the provider, reduce rather than abruptly stop the TPN, replace electrolytes aggressively with monitoring, obtain cultures before vancomycin, manage hyperglycemia without making it the priority over potassium/magnesium/phosphate replacement, and evaluate improvement by electrolyte trends, rhythm, respiratory status, mental status, and cautious nutrition advancement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例追踪一名营养不良、术后开始肠外营养的高风险患者。早期关键模式是磷、钾、镁同时下降，并伴血糖升高、无力、感觉异常、心动过速和尿量下降。阶段 2 的恶化证实严重再喂养综合征：低磷、低钾、低镁继续加重，并出现 PVC、QT 延长、浅呼吸、肌无力和意识改变。PICC 可能感染需要配对血培养和抗生素，但最立即危及生命的是电解质导致的心律失常和呼吸受损。安全处理包括紧急通知医嘱者，降低而不是突然停止 TPN，严密监测下强化补充电解质，在 vancomycin 前抽取培养，处理高血糖但不能让其优先于钾/镁/磷补充，并通过电解质趋势、心律、呼吸、意识状态和谨慎推进营养来评价疗效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In parenteral nutrition questions, do not anchor on glucose alone. In a severely malnourished client, a clustered fall in phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium after calories start is the danger signal; then prioritize the organ compromise caused by that shift.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到肠外营养题时，不要只盯着血糖。严重营养不良患者开始供能后，磷、钾、镁成组下降是危险信号；随后要优先处理这种转移造成的器官受损。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1735,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,89],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, highlight the findings that are significant cues requiring nursing attention.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 1，标出需要护士关注的重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, highlight the findings that are significant cues requiring nursing attention.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 1，标出需要护士关注的重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Stage 1 findings:","zh":"阶段 1 发现："},{"id":"s1","en":"Phosphorus decreased from 2.8 to 1.8 mg/dL.","zh":"血磷从 2.8 降至 1.8 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Potassium decreased from 3.5 to 3.1 mEq/L.","zh":"血钾从 3.5 降至 3.1 mEq/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Magnesium decreased from 1.8 to 1.4 mg/dL.","zh":"血镁从 1.8 降至 1.4 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Point-of-care glucose is 204 mg/dL, increased from the earlier glucose of 156 mg/dL.","zh":"床旁血糖 204 mg/dL，较先前 156 mg/dL 升高。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Heart rate is 104/min, increased from 92/min.","zh":"心率 104 次/分，较 92 次/分升高。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client reports shakiness and mild shortness of breath.","zh":"患者诉发抖并轻度气短。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"New generalized weakness, paresthesias, and increasing fatigue are present.","zh":"出现新的全身无力、感觉异常和疲乏加重。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Urine output declined from about 35 mL/hr to 25 mL/hr.","zh":"尿量从约 35 mL/hr 降至 25 mL/hr。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Temperature is 98.8 °F (37.1 °C).","zh":"体温 98.8 °F (37.1 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"The PICC dressing is clean, dry, and intact with no erythema or drainage.","zh":"PICC 敷料清洁、干燥、完整，无红斑或渗液。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5","s6","s7","s8"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The significant cue cluster is the simultaneous decline in phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium after PN initiation, plus rising glucose, tachycardia, neuromuscular symptoms, mild dyspnea, and lower urine output. Together these findings suggest evolving refeeding syndrome and early organ stress. The stable temperature and benign PICC site are not priority cues at Stage 1.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重要线索组合是开始 PN 后磷、钾、镁同时下降，并伴血糖升高、心动过速、神经肌肉症状、轻度气短和尿量下降。这些发现合在一起提示再喂养综合征正在发展并已有早期器官压力。阶段 1 的体温稳定和 PICC 处良好并不是优先线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For recognize-cues items, look for a pattern, not just the largest single number. Three electrolytes falling together after calories start is more important than an isolated moderate glucose elevation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做识别线索题时，要找模式，而不是只看最大的单一数值。开始供能后三种电解质一起下降，比单独中度血糖升高更重要。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1736,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,36],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, use the client's history, new laboratory pattern, and glucose trend to identify the most likely clinical problem.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 1，结合患者病史、新的化验模式和血糖趋势，判断最可能的临床问题。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, use the client's history, new laboratory pattern, and glucose trend to identify the most likely clinical problem.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 1，结合患者病史、新的化验模式和血糖趋势，判断最可能的临床问题。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The Stage 1 cue pattern most strongly indicates {{d1}} because PN carbohydrate delivery has likely caused {{d2}}. The glucose elevation is best interpreted as {{d3}}.","zh":"阶段 1 的线索模式最强烈提示 {{d1}}，因为 PN 的碳水化合物供给很可能导致 {{d2}}。血糖升高最好理解为 {{d3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"d1_o3","en":"isolated parenteral-nutrition hyperglycemia","zh":"单纯肠外营养相关高血糖"},{"id":"d1_o2","en":"catheter-related bloodstream infection","zh":"导管相关血流感染"},{"id":"d1_o1","en":"refeeding syndrome","zh":"再喂养综合征"}],"correct":"d1_o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"d2_o3","en":"bacterial consumption of serum electrolytes","zh":"细菌消耗血清电解质"},{"id":"d2_o1","en":"insulin-mediated intracellular shifting of phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium","zh":"胰岛素介导的磷、钾、镁向细胞内转移"},{"id":"d2_o2","en":"renal wasting from acute kidney injury","zh":"急性肾损伤导致肾性丢失"}],"correct":"d2_o1"},{"id":"d3","options":[{"id":"d3_o2","en":"the primary cause of the falling phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium","zh":"磷、钾、镁下降的主要原因"},{"id":"d3_o3","en":"evidence that infection is already the dominant problem","zh":"感染已经成为主导问题的证据"},{"id":"d3_o1","en":"a concurrent PN complication that does not explain the electrolyte triad","zh":"并发的 PN 问题，但不能解释电解质三联下降"}],"correct":"d3_o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The Stage 1 pattern is best analyzed as refeeding syndrome: severe malnutrition followed by carbohydrate-containing PN, then simultaneous declines in phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium within the expected early window. Hyperglycemia is common during PN and needs treatment, but it does not explain the electrolyte triad. A central-line infection is unlikely at Stage 1 because there is no fever and the PICC site is benign.","rationaleCorrectZh":"阶段 1 的模式最符合再喂养综合征：严重营养不良后给予含碳水化合物的 PN，随后在早期窗口内磷、钾、镁同时下降。PN 期间高血糖常见且需要处理，但不能解释电解质三联下降。阶段 1 无发热且 PICC 处良好，因此中心静脉导管感染不太可能。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a cloze item asks for a mechanism, make every blank agree with one pathophysiologic chain. Here, malnutrition plus carbohydrate delivery should point to insulin-driven electrolyte shifts.","testTakingStrategyZh":"完形题询问机制时，要让每个空都符合同一条病理生理链。本题中，营养不良加碳水供给应指向胰岛素驱动的电解质转移。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1737,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,102],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which problem is the most immediately life-threatening and requires priority intervention?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2，哪一个问题最立即危及生命，需要优先干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which problem is the most immediately life-threatening and requires priority intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 2，哪一个问题最立即危及生命，需要优先干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_D","en":"Post-operative fever requiring routine antipyretic administration before other actions","zh":"术后发热，需要在其他措施前常规给予退热药"},{"id":"q3_C","en":"Parenteral-nutrition hyperglycemia with glucose 226 mg/dL","zh":"肠外营养相关高血糖，血糖 226 mg/dL"},{"id":"q3_A","en":"Electrolyte-driven cardiac and respiratory compromise from worsening refeeding syndrome","zh":"再喂养综合征加重导致的电解质性心脏和呼吸受损"},{"id":"q3_B","en":"Suspected PICC-related bloodstream infection from erythema and purulent drainage","zh":"因红斑和脓性引流怀疑 PICC 相关血流感染"}],"correct":["q3_A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate threat is the worsening electrolyte derangement with active organ effects: phosphorus 1.3 mg/dL, potassium 2.9 mEq/L, magnesium 1.3 mg/dL, frequent PVCs, prolonged QT, shallow respirations, weakness, and altered mental status. These findings carry near-term risk of lethal dysrhythmia and respiratory failure. The PICC site must be cultured and treated, but it does not explain the established electrolyte triad or current rhythm instability.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最立即的威胁是电解质紊乱加重并已影响器官：血磷 1.3 mg/dL、血钾 2.9 mEq/L、血镁 1.3 mg/dL，伴频发 PVC、QT 延长、浅呼吸、无力和意识改变。这些发现有近期致命心律失常和呼吸衰竭风险。PICC 处需要培养和治疗，但不能解释已形成的电解质三联下降或当前心律不稳。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize the problem that is causing active ABC or circulation risk now. A possible infection is important, but PVCs plus prolonged QT from low K/Mg/Phos can deteriorate first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先处理当前正在造成 ABC 或循环风险的问题。可能感染很重要，但低钾/低镁/低磷导致的 PVC 和 QT 延长可能先恶化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1738,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,31],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which actions are safe and indicated for this client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2，哪些措施对该患者是安全且有指征的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which actions are safe and indicated for this client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段 2，哪些措施对该患者是安全且有指征的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_D","en":"Draw blood cultures from the PICC and a peripheral site before starting the first ordered vancomycin dose.","zh":"在首次医嘱 vancomycin 前，从 PICC 和外周部位抽取血培养。"},{"id":"q4_F","en":"Treat the glucose of 226 mg/dL as the first priority with aggressive insulin before correcting potassium and magnesium.","zh":"把 226 mg/dL 的血糖作为第一优先事项，在纠正钾和镁前积极给予胰岛素。"},{"id":"q4_E","en":"Stop the TPN immediately without a provider order or dextrose/glucose-monitoring backup plan.","zh":"无需医嘱或葡萄糖/血糖监测备用计划，立即停止 TPN。"},{"id":"q4_C","en":"Administer higher-tier potassium, phosphate, and magnesium replacement with continuous cardiac monitoring as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱在连续心脏监测下给予高阶钾、磷、镁补充。"},{"id":"q4_B","en":"Anticipate reducing the TPN rate as ordered rather than abruptly stopping it independently.","zh":"预期按医嘱降低 TPN 速率，而不是自行突然停用。"},{"id":"q4_A","en":"Notify the provider urgently about the continued electrolyte decline, rhythm changes, respiratory findings, and PICC-site drainage.","zh":"紧急通知医嘱者：电解质继续下降、心律改变、呼吸发现和 PICC 穿刺处引流。"}],"correct":["q4_A","q4_B","q4_C","q4_D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should urgently escalate the worsening refeeding syndrome, rhythm changes, respiratory compromise, and suspected line infection. Anticipated management is to reduce caloric delivery rather than abruptly stop the high-dextrose infusion independently, replace potassium/phosphate/magnesium aggressively with monitoring, and obtain paired cultures before vancomycin. Hyperglycemia still needs q4h checks and insulin coverage, but aggressive insulin as the first priority could worsen hypokalemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应紧急上报再喂养综合征恶化、心律改变、呼吸受损和疑似导管感染。预期处理是降低热量供给，而不是自行突然停止高葡萄糖输注；在监测下强化补充钾/磷/镁；并在 vancomycin 前抽取配对血培养。高血糖仍需每 4 小时监测并按量表给予胰岛素，但把积极胰岛素作为第一优先可能加重低钾。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SATA safety items, select interventions that treat the mechanism and avoid independent nursing actions that create a new risk. Insulin is not wrong, but timing and priority matter when potassium is dangerously low.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 SATA 安全题时，选择能处理机制且不会因护士自行行动造成新风险的措施。胰岛素本身不是错误，但当血钾危险偏低时，时机和优先级很重要。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1739,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[39,90],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,31],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, orders have been received. For each action, choose the safest timing category.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2，已收到医嘱。请为每项措施选择最安全的执行时机类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each action, choose the safest timing category.","terminalSentenceZh":"请为每项措施选择最安全的执行时机类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, orders have been received.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段 2，已收到医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q5_r1","en":"Reduce the TPN rate by 50% as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱将 TPN 速率降低 50%。"},{"id":"q5_r2","en":"Begin prescribed higher-tier potassium, phosphate, and magnesium repletion with telemetry.","zh":"在遥测监护下开始医嘱的高阶钾、磷、镁补充。"},{"id":"q5_r3","en":"Draw blood cultures from the PICC and a peripheral site.","zh":"从 PICC 和外周部位抽取血培养。"},{"id":"q5_r4","en":"Administer the first ordered dose of vancomycin.","zh":"给予第一剂医嘱 vancomycin。"},{"id":"q5_r5","en":"Increase glucose monitoring to every 4 hours and give sliding-scale insulin coverage.","zh":"将血糖监测增加至每 4 小时，并按滑动量表给予胰岛素覆盖。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q5_c1","en":"Immediate priority; do not delay for the infection workup","zh":"立即优先执行；不要因感染评估而延迟"},{"id":"q5_c3","en":"Give only after cultures are obtained","zh":"仅在抽取培养后给予"},{"id":"q5_c4","en":"Ongoing supportive management; does not delay acute electrolyte actions","zh":"持续支持性管理；不延迟急性电解质处理"},{"id":"q5_c2","en":"Must occur before the first antibiotic dose","zh":"必须在首次抗生素前完成"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q5_r1","columnIds":["q5_c1"]},{"rowId":"q5_r2","columnIds":["q5_c1"]},{"rowId":"q5_r3","columnIds":["q5_c2"]},{"rowId":"q5_r4","columnIds":["q5_c3"]},{"rowId":"q5_r5","columnIds":["q5_c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The rate reduction and electrolyte repletion address the immediate mechanism and dysrhythmia/respiratory risk, so they should not wait for the infection workup. Paired blood cultures must be drawn before vancomycin; vancomycin follows cultures. Glucose monitoring and sliding-scale insulin continue, but they must not delay urgent rate reduction and electrolyte replacement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"降低速率和补充电解质直接处理当前机制以及心律/呼吸风险，因此不应等感染评估完成才做。配对血培养必须在 vancomycin 前抽取；vancomycin 在培养之后给予。血糖监测和滑动量表胰岛素继续进行，但不能延迟紧急降低速率和补充电解质。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When actions can be parallelized, avoid forcing a strict one-by-one sequence. Separate immediate threats from prerequisites, such as cultures before antibiotics.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当措施可并行执行时，不要强行排成完全单线程顺序。要区分立即威胁和前置条件，例如抗生素前先抽培养。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1740,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.306.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding or interpretation based on the client's response to treatment.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 3，根据患者对治疗的反应，对每项发现或解读进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding or interpretation based on the client's response to treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 3，根据患者对治疗的反应，对每项发现或解读进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q6_r1","en":"Potassium 3.4, phosphorus 1.9, and magnesium 1.6 are rising after aggressive replacement.","zh":"强化补充后，血钾 3.4、血磷 1.9、血镁 1.6 正在上升。"},{"id":"q6_r2","en":"Telemetry shows sinus rhythm without PVCs and a shortened QT interval.","zh":"遥测显示窦性心律，无 PVC，QT 间期缩短。"},{"id":"q6_r3","en":"The client is more alert and can lift her arms above her shoulders.","zh":"患者更清醒，并能将双臂举过肩。"},{"id":"q6_r4","en":"Glucose decreased from 226 to 168 mg/dL.","zh":"血糖从 226 降至 168 mg/dL。"},{"id":"q6_r5","en":"The PICC-site erythema has not expanded and cultures are pending.","zh":"PICC 红斑未扩大，培养结果待回。"},{"id":"q6_r6","en":"Because the client is improving, the original TPN rate should be resumed now.","zh":"由于患者正在好转，现在应恢复原 TPN 速率。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q6_c1","en":"Evidence refeeding syndrome is improving","zh":"提示再喂养综合征正在改善"},{"id":"q6_c3","en":"Unsafe interpretation or action","zh":"不安全的解读或措施"},{"id":"q6_c2","en":"Requires continued follow-up for another problem","zh":"另一个问题仍需继续跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q6_r1","columnIds":["q6_c1"]},{"rowId":"q6_r2","columnIds":["q6_c1"]},{"rowId":"q6_r3","columnIds":["q6_c1"]},{"rowId":"q6_r4","columnIds":["q6_c1"]},{"rowId":"q6_r5","columnIds":["q6_c2"]},{"rowId":"q6_r6","columnIds":["q6_c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The improving electrolyte trend, resolution of PVCs/QT shortening, better mental status and muscle strength, and improved glucose all show response to TPN-rate reduction and aggressive repletion. The PICC site has not worsened but cultures are still pending, so infection follow-up continues. The TPN should not return to the original rate yet because electrolytes are improving but not fully normalized and total body stores remain depleted.","rationaleCorrectZh":"电解质上升、PVC 消失/QT 缩短、意识和肌力改善、血糖改善，都说明降低 TPN 速率和强化补充有效。PICC 处未恶化，但培养仍待回，因此感染问题仍需跟进。TPN 不能立即恢复原速率，因为电解质虽在改善但尚未完全正常，全身储备仍然耗竭。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by matching them to the original problem. For refeeding syndrome, improvement means rising phosphate/potassium/magnesium plus improvement in rhythm, breathing, strength, and mental status—not simply one better lab set.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价疗效时，要把结果和原问题对应。再喂养综合征的改善意味着磷/钾/镁上升，并且心律、呼吸、肌力和意识改善；不是只看一次化验变好。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1741,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_refeeding_syndrome_tpn_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.307","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.307.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.307.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[496,525],"terminalOffsetsZh":[201,214],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2 synthesis: A severely malnourished post-operative client has had PN started after about five weeks of negligible intake. Within 30 hours, phosphorus has fallen from 2.8 to 1.8 to 1.3 mg/dL, potassium from 3.5 to 3.1 to 2.9 mEq/L, and magnesium from 1.8 to 1.4 to 1.3 mg/dL. The client is lethargic with proximal weakness, shallow respirations, palpitations, frequent PVCs, prolonged QT interval, and glucose 226 mg/dL. The PICC site has erythema, tenderness, and small purulent drainage. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"阶段 2 综合判断：一名严重营养不良的术后患者，约 5 周几乎无摄入后开始 PN。30 小时内，血磷从 2.8 降至 1.8 再降至 1.3 mg/dL，血钾从 3.5 降至 3.1 再降至 2.9 mEq/L，血镁从 1.8 降至 1.4 再降至 1.3 mg/dL。患者嗜睡、近端肌无力、浅呼吸、心悸、频发 PVC、QT 间期延长，血糖 226 mg/dL。PICC 处有红斑、压痛和少量脓性引流。完成 bow-tie 图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bow-tie 图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The PICC site has erythema, tenderness, and small purulent drainage.","penultimateSentenceZh":"PICC 处有红斑、压痛和少量脓性引流。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_c3","en":"Parenteral-nutrition hyperglycemia","zh":"肠外营养相关高血糖"},{"id":"bt_c1","en":"Refeeding syndrome","zh":"再喂养综合征"},{"id":"bt_c2","en":"Catheter-related bloodstream infection","zh":"导管相关血流感染"}],"correct":"bt_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_a2","en":"Administer aggressive potassium, phosphate, and magnesium replacement with telemetry","zh":"在遥测监护下强化补充钾、磷、镁"},{"id":"bt_a1","en":"Reduce the TPN infusion rate by 50% as ordered","zh":"按医嘱将 TPN 输注速率降低 50%"},{"id":"bt_a3","en":"Independently discontinue TPN abruptly without dextrose backup","zh":"无葡萄糖备用方案而自行突然停用 TPN"},{"id":"bt_a4","en":"Give aggressive insulin first for glucose 226 mg/dL","zh":"因血糖 226 mg/dL 先积极给予胰岛素"}],"correct":["bt_a1","bt_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_p3","en":"Serum glucose alone as the primary outcome","zh":"仅以血糖作为主要疗效指标"},{"id":"bt_p2","en":"Cardiac rhythm, PVCs, and QT interval on telemetry","zh":"遥测心律、PVC 和 QT 间期"},{"id":"bt_p4","en":"White blood cell count as the main marker of this crisis","zh":"将白细胞计数作为此次危机的主要指标"},{"id":"bt_p1","en":"Serum phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium trends","zh":"血清磷、钾、镁变化趋势"}],"correct":["bt_p1","bt_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most likely condition is refeeding syndrome because the dominant pattern is rapid progressive hypophosphatemia, hypokalemia, and hypomagnesemia after PN in a severely malnourished client, with cardiac and respiratory manifestations. Priority actions are to reduce the TPN rate as ordered and aggressively replace the depleted electrolytes with telemetry. The best monitoring parameters are the electrolyte trend and cardiac rhythm/QT response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能的病情是再喂养综合征，因为主导模式是在严重营养不良患者开始 PN 后，血磷、血钾、血镁迅速进行性下降，并出现心脏和呼吸表现。优先措施是按医嘱降低 TPN 速率，并在遥测监护下强化补充耗竭的电解质。最佳监测指标是电解质趋势以及心律/QT 的反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, choose the condition that explains the most dangerous cluster, then match actions and monitoring to that condition rather than to a distracting concurrent problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bow-tie 题时，先选择能解释最危险线索组合的病情，再把措施和监测指标与该病情对应，而不是被并发但次要的问题分散。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1742,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_moc_chain_command_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.308","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.308.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.308.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the note entry that requires the charge nurse to use the chain of command.","fullStemZh":"标出需要护士长/带班护士启动指挥链处理的记录内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the note entry that requires the charge nurse to use the chain of command.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出需要护士长/带班护士启动指挥链处理的记录内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Progress note: A client who had a thyroidectomy 6 hours ago reports increasing neck tightness. ","zh":"病程记录：一名甲状腺切除术后 6 小时的患者主诉颈部越来越紧。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The nurse elevates the head of the bed and assesses the airway. ","zh":"护士抬高床头并评估气道。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The incision dressing is dry, but the anterior neck appears more swollen than during the previous assessment. ","zh":"切口敷料干燥，但颈前部看起来比上次评估时更肿胀。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The provider is notified twice and replies, \"This can wait until morning rounds.\" ","zh":"护士两次通知医嘱提供者，对方回复：“这可以等到早晨查房再说。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client remains in semi-Fowler position while emergency airway equipment is brought to the bedside.","zh":"患者保持半坐卧位，同时将紧急气道设备带至床旁。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A post-thyroidectomy client with increasing neck tightness and swelling may be developing a hematoma that can rapidly obstruct the airway. If the provider does not respond appropriately to an urgent safety threat, the nurse must escalate through the chain of command.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺切除术后患者出现颈部越来越紧和肿胀，可能正在形成血肿并迅速阻塞气道。如果医嘱提供者没有对紧急安全威胁作出适当反应，护士必须通过指挥链升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an urgent client-safety issue is not addressed after provider notification, the nurse does not simply wait; the nurse escalates through the chain of command.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当紧急患者安全问题在通知医嘱提供者后仍未得到处理时，护士不能只是等待；护士应通过指挥链升级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1743,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_moc_interpreter_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.309","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.309.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.309.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the action that violates safe communication standards for a client with limited English proficiency.","fullStemZh":"标出违反英语能力有限患者安全沟通标准的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the action that violates safe communication standards for a client with limited English proficiency.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出违反英语能力有限患者安全沟通标准的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"A Mandarin-speaking client is admitted for a scheduled procedure. ","zh":"一名讲普通话的患者因计划性操作入院。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The nurse asks the client which language they prefer for medical information. ","zh":"护士询问患者希望使用哪种语言接收医疗信息。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The nurse uses a certified medical interpreter to review the preprocedure checklist. ","zh":"护士使用合格的医疗口译员核对术前清单。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse asks the client's adult child to interpret the risks and benefits because the unit is busy. ","zh":"由于病区很忙，护士请患者的成年子女翻译操作的风险和益处。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The nurse documents the interpreter identification number in the chart.","zh":"护士在病历中记录口译员识别号码。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Family members should not be used to interpret complex medical information such as risks and benefits unless there is an emergency and no qualified interpreter is available. A qualified medical interpreter protects accuracy, privacy, and informed decision-making.","rationaleCorrectZh":"除非是紧急情况且无法获得合格口译员，否则不应让家属翻译风险和益处等复杂医疗信息。合格医疗口译员可保障准确性、隐私和知情决策。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For consent, teaching, discharge instructions, and risk/benefit conversations, choose a qualified interpreter instead of relatives or untrained staff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在同意、教学、出院指导以及风险/益处沟通中，应选择合格口译员，而不是亲属或未经培训的工作人员。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1744,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_moc_code_status_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.310","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.310.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.310.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,106],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the documentation finding that must be clarified before transporting the client for a procedure.","fullStemZh":"标出在将患者送去操作前必须澄清的文件记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the documentation finding that must be clarified before transporting the client for a procedure.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出在将患者送去操作前必须澄清的文件记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse reviews the chart before a client is transported for an endoscopy. ","zh":"在患者被送去内镜检查前，护士查阅病历。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The signed consent lists the correct client name and planned procedure. ","zh":"已签署的同意书列有正确的患者姓名和计划操作。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"A portable oxygen tank is full and attached to the transport stretcher. ","zh":"转运担架上连接的便携氧气瓶已充满。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The admission record states \"do not resuscitate,\" but the procedure checklist states \"full code during procedure\" with no provider clarification note. ","zh":"入院记录写着“拒绝复苏”，但操作清单写着“操作期间全码复苏”，且没有医嘱提供者澄清记录。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The most recent vital signs were documented 20 minutes ago.","zh":"最近一次生命体征记录在 20 分钟前。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Conflicting code-status documentation must be clarified before a procedure. The nurse should not assume that a DNR order is automatically suspended or automatically unchanged during a procedure; the client's wishes and provider orders must be clear.","rationaleCorrectZh":"操作前必须澄清相互矛盾的复苏状态记录。护士不能假设 DNR 医嘱在操作期间会自动暂停或自动保持不变；必须明确患者意愿和医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not assume code-status changes. When advance directives, consent, or procedure paperwork conflict, stop and clarify before proceeding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要假设复苏状态会改变。当预立医疗指示、同意书或操作文件相互冲突时，应暂停并澄清后再继续。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1745,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_moc_incident_doc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.311","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.311.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.311.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the charting entry that should be corrected because it is inappropriate documentation.","fullStemZh":"标出因记录方式不当而应被更正的病历记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the charting entry that should be corrected because it is inappropriate documentation.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出因记录方式不当而应被更正的病历记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"After a client fall, the nurse documents the event in the medical record. ","zh":"患者跌倒后，护士在病历中记录事件。"},{"id":"s2","en":"Client found sitting on the floor beside the bed at 0215. ","zh":"0215 发现患者坐在床旁地板上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Client states, \"I tried to reach the bathroom without calling.\" ","zh":"患者说：“我想自己去厕所，没有按铃。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"No visible injury noted; neurologic checks initiated per policy. ","zh":"未见明显损伤；按政策开始神经系统检查。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Incident report completed and sent to risk management.","zh":"事件报告已填写并发送给风险管理部门。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The medical record should objectively document the client's assessment, statements, notifications, and interventions. It should not mention that an incident report was completed because the incident report is a separate risk-management document.","rationaleCorrectZh":"病历应客观记录患者评估、患者陈述、通知对象和护理措施。不应在病历中提到已填写事件报告，因为事件报告是单独的风险管理文件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Chart facts and nursing actions. Do not chart blame, speculation, or the existence of an incident report.","testTakingStrategyZh":"病历记录事实和护理措施。不要记录责备、推测或事件报告的存在。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1746,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_moc_lpn_scope_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.312","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.312.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.312.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the assignment that the charge nurse must change because it is outside the licensed practical/vocational nurse (LPN/LVN) role.","fullStemZh":"标出带班护士必须更改的分工，因为该任务超出执业护士（LPN/LVN）的职责范围。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the assignment that the charge nurse must change because it is outside the licensed practical/vocational nurse (LPN/LVN) role.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出带班护士必须更改的分工，因为该任务超出执业护士（LPN/LVN）的职责范围。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The charge nurse is assigning clients on a medical-surgical unit with one RN, one LPN, and one UAP. ","zh":"内外科病区带班护士正在为一名 RN、一名 LPN 和一名 UAP 分配工作。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The LPN will reinforce coughing and deep-breathing exercises for a stable postoperative client. ","zh":"LPN 将为一名稳定术后患者强化咳嗽和深呼吸练习。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The LPN will administer a scheduled oral antihypertensive medication. ","zh":"LPN 将给予定时口服降压药。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The LPN will titrate an IV heparin infusion according to the aPTT protocol. ","zh":"LPN 将根据 aPTT 方案调整静脉肝素输注速度。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The LPN will change a simple dry dressing on a stable client's surgical incision.","zh":"LPN 将为稳定患者的手术切口更换简单干敷料。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Titrating an IV heparin infusion requires ongoing assessment, interpretation of laboratory data, and clinical judgment. This responsibility belongs to the RN and is not an appropriate LPN/LVN assignment in NCLEX delegation logic.","rationaleCorrectZh":"调整静脉肝素输注需要持续评估、解释实验室数据和临床判断。按照 NCLEX 委派逻辑，这属于 RN 职责，不适合分配给 LPN/LVN。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stable, predictable care may be assigned to LPN/LVN staff. Unstable clients, initial teaching, assessment, evaluation, and titration of high-alert IV medications stay with the RN.","testTakingStrategyZh":"稳定、可预测的护理可分配给 LPN/LVN。病情不稳定、初次教学、评估、评价以及高警示静脉药物滴定应由 RN 负责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1747,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_sic_restraint_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.313","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.313.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.313.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,74],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the restraint-related action that requires immediate correction.","fullStemZh":"标出与约束相关、需要立即纠正的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the restraint-related action that requires immediate correction.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出与约束相关、需要立即纠正的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse checks a client in soft wrist restraints. ","zh":"护士检查一名使用软腕部约束的患者。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The restraints are secured with quick-release knots. ","zh":"约束带使用快速释放结固定。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Two fingers fit between the restraint and the client's wrist. ","zh":"约束带与患者手腕之间可容纳两根手指。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The restraint ties are attached to the movable side rails. ","zh":"约束带系在可移动的床侧栏上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Circulation, skin integrity, and range of motion are assessed according to policy.","zh":"按政策评估循环、皮肤完整性和关节活动度。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Restraints should be attached to the bed frame, not to movable side rails. If the side rail is lowered or moves, the client can be injured or trapped.","rationaleCorrectZh":"约束带应固定在床架上，而不是可移动的床侧栏上。如果侧栏放下或移动，患者可能受伤或被困。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For restraints, look for least-restrictive use, correct fit, frequent monitoring, quick release, and attachment to the bed frame—not side rails.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关于约束，应寻找最少限制原则、合适松紧、频繁监测、可快速释放，以及固定在床架上而不是侧栏上。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1748,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_sic_fire_oxygen_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.314","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.314.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.314.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the home-care finding that creates the greatest immediate fire-safety risk for a client using oxygen.","fullStemZh":"标出居家护理发现中对使用氧气患者造成最大立即火灾安全风险的情况。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the home-care finding that creates the greatest immediate fire-safety risk for a client using oxygen.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出居家护理发现中对使用氧气患者造成最大立即火灾安全风险的情况。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"During a home visit, the nurse assesses a client using oxygen at 2 L/min by nasal cannula. ","zh":"家访期间，护士评估一名经鼻导管以 2 L/min 吸氧的患者。"},{"id":"s2","en":"A \"No Smoking\" sign is posted near the front door. ","zh":"前门附近贴有“禁止吸烟”标志。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The oxygen tubing is routed along the wall to reduce tripping. ","zh":"氧气管沿墙布置以减少绊倒。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client keeps a lit scented candle on the bedside table while oxygen is in use. ","zh":"患者在使用氧气时，将点燃的香薰蜡烛放在床旁桌上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The oxygen cylinder is stored upright in a stand.","zh":"氧气瓶直立放置在支架中。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Oxygen supports combustion. Open flames such as candles, smoking materials, or gas flames should not be near oxygen equipment because they create an immediate fire and burn hazard.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氧气会助燃。蜡烛、吸烟材料或燃气火焰等明火不应靠近氧气设备，因为会造成立即的火灾和烧伤危险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For oxygen safety, choose the option that removes open flame or smoking materials first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关于氧气安全，优先选择移除明火或吸烟材料的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1749,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_sic_airborne_tb_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.315","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.315.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.315.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the infection-control breach in the care of a client with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis.","fullStemZh":"标出照护疑似肺结核患者时的感染控制违规行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the infection-control breach in the care of a client with suspected pulmonary tuberculosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出照护疑似肺结核患者时的感染控制违规行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"A client with a persistent cough, night sweats, weight loss, and hemoptysis is placed on Airborne Precautions. ","zh":"一名持续咳嗽、盗汗、体重下降和咯血的患者被实施空气传播隔离。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The client is assigned to a negative-pressure room. ","zh":"患者被安排在负压病房。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The room door is kept closed except when staff enter and exit. ","zh":"除工作人员进出外，病房门保持关闭。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse enters the room wearing a surgical mask instead of a fit-tested N95 respirator. ","zh":"护士戴着外科口罩而不是经过密合度测试的 N95 呼吸器进入病房。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client wears a surgical mask when transported for an essential test.","zh":"患者因必要检查转运时佩戴外科口罩。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Staff caring for a client with suspected or confirmed pulmonary tuberculosis must wear a fit-tested N95 respirator or higher-level respiratory protection. A standard surgical mask does not provide adequate airborne protection for staff.","rationaleCorrectZh":"照护疑似或确诊肺结核患者的工作人员必须佩戴经过密合度测试的 N95 呼吸器或更高级别呼吸防护。普通外科口罩不能为工作人员提供足够的空气传播防护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For tuberculosis, think Airborne Precautions: negative pressure, closed door, and N95 respirator for staff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到结核病，要想到空气传播隔离：负压、关门、工作人员佩戴 N95 呼吸器。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1750,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_pharm_kcl_order_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.316","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.316.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.316.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the medication order that the nurse must question before administration.","fullStemZh":"标出护士给药前必须质疑的用药医嘱。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the medication order that the nurse must question before administration.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出护士给药前必须质疑的用药医嘱。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse reviews new medication orders for a client with hypokalemia. ","zh":"护士查看一名低钾血症患者的新用药医嘱。"},{"id":"s2","en":"Potassium chloride 20 mEq diluted in 100 mL 0.9% sodium chloride IV over 2 hours via pump. ","zh":"氯化钾 20 mEq 加入 100 mL 0.9% 氯化钠，经输液泵静脉输注 2 小时。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Place the client on continuous cardiac monitoring during replacement. ","zh":"补钾期间给予连续心电监测。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Potassium chloride 10 mEq IV push now for serum potassium 2.9 mEq/L. ","zh":"血清钾 2.9 mEq/L，立即静脉推注氯化钾 10 mEq。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Recheck serum potassium after completion of replacement.","zh":"补钾完成后复查血清钾。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium chloride must never be administered by IV push because rapid administration can cause fatal dysrhythmias and cardiac arrest. The nurse must question and clarify this order before giving the medication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氯化钾绝不能静脉推注，因为快速给药可导致致命性心律失常和心脏骤停。护士在给药前必须质疑并澄清该医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"High-alert medication rule: potassium is diluted and infused by pump; never give IV push.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高警示药物规则：氯化钾需稀释并用泵输注；绝不静脉推注。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1751,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_pharm_maoi_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.317","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.317.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.317.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,116],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the medication-history finding that places the client at risk for a dangerous interaction with phenelzine.","fullStemZh":"标出用药史中会使患者与苯乙肼发生危险相互作用的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the medication-history finding that places the client at risk for a dangerous interaction with phenelzine.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出用药史中会使患者与苯乙肼发生危险相互作用的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse reviews the medication history of a client newly prescribed phenelzine. ","zh":"护士查看一名新开具苯乙肼医嘱患者的用药史。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The client takes acetaminophen occasionally for headaches. ","zh":"患者偶尔服用对乙酰氨基酚治疗头痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client takes a daily multivitamin without iron. ","zh":"患者每天服用不含铁的复合维生素。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client has continued taking sertraline 100 mg every morning. ","zh":"患者仍每天早晨服用舍曲林 100 mg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client uses saline nasal spray for dryness.","zh":"患者使用生理盐水鼻喷雾缓解干燥。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Phenelzine is a monoamine oxidase inhibitor (MAOI). Taking it with an SSRI such as sertraline can cause serotonin syndrome, a potentially life-threatening interaction. The nurse should hold the medication and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"苯乙肼是单胺氧化酶抑制剂（MAOI）。与舍曲林等 SSRI 同用可导致血清素综合征，这是一种可能危及生命的相互作用。护士应暂停给药并通知医嘱提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"MAOIs have major interaction risks. Avoid combining them with SSRIs/SNRIs and many sympathomimetic or serotonergic drugs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"MAOI 有重要相互作用风险。避免与 SSRI/SNRI 以及许多拟交感或促血清素药物合用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1752,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_rrp_postop_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.318","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.318.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.318.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the postoperative assessment finding that requires immediate nursing intervention.","fullStemZh":"标出术后评估中需要护士立即干预的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the postoperative assessment finding that requires immediate nursing intervention.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出术后评估中需要护士立即干预的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse assesses a client 1 hour after abdominal surgery. ","zh":"护士评估一名腹部手术后 1 小时的患者。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The client reports incisional pain rated 5/10. ","zh":"患者主诉切口疼痛 5/10。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The dressing has a 2-cm circle of serosanguineous drainage. ","zh":"敷料上有直径 2 cm 的浆液血性渗液。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Respirations are 8/min after receiving IV hydromorphone 30 minutes ago. ","zh":"30 分钟前接受静脉氢吗啡酮后，呼吸频率为 8 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client is drowsy but awakens when spoken to.","zh":"患者嗜睡，但呼唤时能醒来。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A respiratory rate of 8/min after IV opioid administration indicates opioid-induced respiratory depression. This threatens airway and breathing and requires immediate intervention, such as stimulating the client, supporting ventilation, holding opioids, notifying the provider, and preparing naloxone per protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"静脉阿片类药物给药后呼吸频率 8 次/分，提示阿片所致呼吸抑制。该情况威胁气道和呼吸，需要立即干预，如刺激患者、支持通气、暂停阿片类药物、通知医嘱提供者，并按规程准备纳洛酮。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After opioid administration, prioritize breathing. A low respiratory rate is more urgent than expected postoperative pain or small drainage.","testTakingStrategyZh":"给予阿片类药物后，优先关注呼吸。呼吸频率低比预期术后疼痛或少量渗液更紧急。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1753,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_hl_hpm_immunization_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.319","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.319.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.319.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the immunization plan that requires the nurse to intervene before administration.","fullStemZh":"标出给药前需要护士干预的免疫接种计划。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the immunization plan that requires the nurse to intervene before administration.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出给药前需要护士干预的免疫接种计划。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse reviews immunizations for an adult client receiving high-dose prednisone for a severe autoimmune flare. ","zh":"护士查看一名因严重自身免疫病急性发作而接受大剂量泼尼松治疗的成年患者的免疫接种。"},{"id":"s2","en":"Administer the inactivated influenza vaccine when due. ","zh":"到期时接种灭活流感疫苗。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Administer the recombinant zoster vaccine according to the recommended schedule. ","zh":"按推荐程序接种重组带状疱疹疫苗。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Administer the live attenuated varicella vaccine today. ","zh":"今天接种水痘减毒活疫苗。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Review the client's vaccine history and document contraindications.","zh":"查看患者疫苗史并记录禁忌证。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Live attenuated vaccines are generally contraindicated in clients with significant immunosuppression, such as those receiving high-dose systemic corticosteroids. The nurse should hold the live vaccine and clarify the plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于明显免疫抑制的患者，例如正在接受大剂量全身性糖皮质激素治疗者，减毒活疫苗通常禁用。护士应暂缓接种活疫苗并澄清计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client is immunosuppressed, separate live vaccines from inactivated or recombinant vaccines. Live vaccines are the safety concern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"患者免疫受抑时，要区分活疫苗与灭活或重组疫苗。活疫苗是安全重点。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1754,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_fib_heparin_rate_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.320","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.320.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.320.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,191],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,95],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes heparin 1,200 units/hr IV. The infusion bag contains heparin 25,000 units in 250 mL D5W. Program the infusion pump at how many mL/hr? Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为肝素静脉输注 1,200 units/hr。输液袋含肝素 25,000 units，加在 250 mL D5W 中。输液泵应设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Program the infusion pump at how many mL/hr?","penultimateSentenceZh":"输液泵应设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["12","12 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":12,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The concentration is 25,000 units ÷ 250 mL = 100 units/mL. Required rate: 1,200 units/hr ÷ 100 units/mL = 12 mL/hr. The ordered units must be converted through the bag concentration before programming the pump.","rationaleCorrectZh":"浓度为 25,000 units ÷ 250 mL = 100 units/mL。所需速度为 1,200 units/hr ÷ 100 units/mL = 12 mL/hr。设置输液泵前必须先用输液袋浓度换算。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Set up units so “units” cancel and the remaining unit is mL/hr.","testTakingStrategyZh":"列式时让 “units” 抵消，最后剩下 mL/hr。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1755,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_fib_enoxaparin_volume_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.321","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.321.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.321.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[160,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,80],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes enoxaparin 30 mg subcutaneously now. The prefilled syringe is labeled enoxaparin 40 mg/0.4 mL. How many mL should the nurse administer? Round to the nearest hundredth mL.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为现在皮下注射依诺肝素 30 mg。预充注射器标签为 enoxaparin 40 mg/0.4 mL。护士应给多少 mL？四舍五入到最接近的百分之一 mL。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest hundredth mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的百分之一 mL。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应给多少 mL？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["0.30","0.30 mL","0.3","0.3 mL"],"numeric":{"value":0.3,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"40 mg/0.4 mL equals 100 mg/mL. A 30 mg dose requires 30 ÷ 100 = 0.30 mL. Rounding to the nearest hundredth keeps the answer as 0.30 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"40 mg/0.4 mL 等于 100 mg/mL。30 mg 需要 30 ÷ 100 = 0.30 mL。按百分之一 mL 取整后仍为 0.30 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert the label to mg per mL, then divide the ordered dose by that concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先把标签换算成每 mL 多少 mg，再用医嘱剂量除以浓度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1756,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_fib_cefazolin_rate_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.322","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.322.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.322.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,75],"fullStemEn":"Cefazolin 1 g in 50 mL normal saline is prescribed to infuse over 30 minutes. At how many mL/hr should the nurse program the pump? Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为 cefazolin 1 g 加入 50 mL 生理盐水，30 分钟输完。护士应将泵设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At how many mL/hr should the nurse program the pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将泵设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["100","100 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":100,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thirty minutes is 0.5 hr. Pump rate = volume ÷ time = 50 mL ÷ 0.5 hr = 100 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"30 分钟等于 0.5 小时。泵速 = 容量 ÷ 时间 = 50 mL ÷ 0.5 hr = 100 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pump rates, convert the infusion time to hours before dividing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算输液泵速度时，先把输注时间换算成小时。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1757,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_fib_kcl_rate_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.323","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.323.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.323.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,97],"fullStemEn":"The medication administration record lists potassium chloride 20 mEq diluted in 100 mL normal saline to infuse over 2 hours by pump. At how many mL/hr should the nurse program the pump? Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"给药记录显示 potassium chloride 20 mEq 已稀释于 100 mL 生理盐水中，需用泵 2 小时输完。护士应将泵设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At how many mL/hr should the nurse program the pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将泵设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["50","50 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":50,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The ordered volume is 100 mL over 2 hr. 100 mL ÷ 2 hr = 50 mL/hr. The potassium amount is important for safety verification, but the pump rate comes from volume divided by time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"医嘱容量为 100 mL，2 小时输完。100 mL ÷ 2 hr = 50 mL/hr。钾的总量用于安全核对，但泵速由容量除以时间决定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the dose unit from the volume unit; pump questions usually ask volume per hour.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分剂量单位和容量单位；输液泵题通常问每小时多少毫升。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1758,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_bowtie_opioid_sedation_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.324","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.324.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.324.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[184,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,73],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative client received IV morphine 30 minutes ago. The client is difficult to arouse, has a respiratory rate of 6/min, oxygen saturation 86% on room air, and pinpoint pupils. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名术后患者 30 分钟前接受 IV morphine。现在患者难以唤醒，呼吸 6 次/分，室内空气 SpO₂ 86%，瞳孔针尖样。完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is difficult to arouse, has a respiratory rate of 6/min, oxygen saturation 86% on room air, and pinpoint pupils.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现在患者难以唤醒，呼吸 6 次/分，室内空气 SpO₂ 86%，瞳孔针尖样。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_panic","en":"Panic attack","zh":"惊恐发作"},{"id":"c_opioid_resp","en":"Opioid-induced respiratory depression","zh":"阿片类药物导致的呼吸抑制"},{"id":"c_hypoglycemia","en":"Hypoglycemia","zh":"低血糖"}],"correct":"c_opioid_resp"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_more_morphine","en":"Give the next morphine dose for comfort","zh":"为舒适给予下一剂吗啡"},{"id":"a_stop_opioid","en":"Hold further opioid doses and call for help","zh":"暂停后续阿片剂量并呼叫帮助"},{"id":"a_naloxone","en":"Administer prescribed naloxone per protocol","zh":"按医嘱/流程给予纳洛酮"},{"id":"a_oral_fluids","en":"Offer oral fluids to stimulate breathing","zh":"给口服液体以刺激呼吸"}],"correct":["a_stop_opioid","a_naloxone"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_appetite","en":"Appetite before breakfast","zh":"早餐前食欲"},{"id":"p_urine_color","en":"Urine color only","zh":"只看尿液颜色"},{"id":"p_rr_sedation","en":"Respiratory rate and level of sedation","zh":"呼吸频率和镇静程度"},{"id":"p_spo2_airway","en":"Oxygen saturation and airway status","zh":"血氧饱和度和气道状态"}],"correct":["p_rr_sedation","p_spo2_airway"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The timing after IV morphine plus severe sedation, RR 6/min, hypoxemia, and pinpoint pupils point to opioid-induced respiratory depression. The nurse should stop further opioid exposure, get help, and give prescribed naloxone/protocol reversal while closely monitoring breathing, sedation, SpO₂, and airway. More morphine and oral fluids are unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"IV morphine 后出现重度镇静、呼吸 6 次/分、低氧和针尖样瞳孔，提示阿片类药物导致的呼吸抑制。护士应暂停后续阿片暴露、呼叫帮助，并按医嘱/流程给予纳洛酮，同时严密监测呼吸、镇静程度、SpO₂ 和气道。继续给吗啡或给口服液体都不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In medication-safety bowties, match the drug, timing, and life-threatening assessment finding before choosing actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"药物安全类蝴蝶结题要先把药物、时间和危及生命的评估发现对应起来，再选措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1759,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_bowtie_insulin_hypoglycemia_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.325","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.325.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.325.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,67],"fullStemEn":"A client received scheduled insulin lispro, but the meal tray is delayed. Thirty minutes later the client is awake, shaky, diaphoretic, and says, “I feel weak.” Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名患者已接受定时 insulin lispro，但餐盘延迟。30 分钟后患者清醒，发抖、出汗，并说：“我觉得很虚弱。”完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Thirty minutes later the client is awake, shaky, diaphoretic, and says, “I feel weak.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"30 分钟后患者清醒，发抖、出汗，并说：“我觉得很虚弱。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_low_glucose","en":"Hypoglycemia related to rapid-acting insulin without food","zh":"速效胰岛素后未进食导致低血糖"},{"id":"c_allergic_rxn","en":"Immediate insulin allergy","zh":"胰岛素即刻过敏"},{"id":"c_hyperkalemia","en":"Hyperkalemia from insulin therapy","zh":"胰岛素治疗导致高钾血症"}],"correct":"c_low_glucose"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_give_more_lispro","en":"Administer an additional correction dose of lispro","zh":"再给予额外 lispro 校正剂量"},{"id":"a_check_bg","en":"Check capillary blood glucose now","zh":"立即测指尖血糖"},{"id":"a_delay_assess","en":"Wait until the tray arrives to reassess","zh":"等餐盘到后再评估"},{"id":"a_give_carb","en":"Give 15 g rapid-acting carbohydrate if blood glucose is low","zh":"若血糖低且患者清醒，给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物"}],"correct":["a_check_bg","a_give_carb"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_sputum","en":"Sputum color","zh":"痰液颜色"},{"id":"p_symptoms","en":"Resolution of shakiness, sweating, and weakness","zh":"发抖、出汗和虚弱是否缓解"},{"id":"p_inr","en":"INR trend","zh":"INR 趋势"},{"id":"p_bg_recheck","en":"Blood glucose response after treatment","zh":"处理后的血糖反应"}],"correct":["p_bg_recheck","p_symptoms"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rapid-acting insulin with delayed food can cause hypoglycemia. The nurse should verify the glucose immediately and, if low and the client can swallow, give a rapid carbohydrate and reassess symptoms and glucose. Waiting or giving more insulin can worsen hypoglycemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"速效胰岛素后进食延迟可导致低血糖。护士应立即确认血糖；若血糖低且患者可吞咽，应给予快速作用碳水化合物，并复查症状和血糖。等待或追加胰岛素会加重低血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When rapid-acting insulin is given and food is delayed, think hypoglycemia first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"速效胰岛素已给但食物延迟时，先考虑低血糖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Thirty minutes later the client is awake, shaky, diaphoretic, and says, “I feel weak.”","controlSentenceZh":"30 分钟后患者清醒，发抖、出汗，并说：“我觉得很虚弱。”"}
{"queueIndex":1760,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_highlight_warfarin_rec_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.326","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.326.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.326.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the medication-reconciliation findings that require provider or pharmacist follow-up because they increase bleeding risk.","fullStemZh":"标出因增加出血风险而需要医师或药师进一步跟进的用药核对发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the medication-reconciliation findings that require provider or pharmacist follow-up because they increase bleeding risk.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出因增加出血风险而需要医师或药师进一步跟进的用药核对发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Medication reconciliation note:","zh":"用药核对记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"The client takes warfarin 5 mg every evening for atrial fibrillation.","zh":"患者因房颤每晚服用 warfarin 5 mg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The discharge prescription includes trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole for a urinary tract infection.","zh":"出院处方包括 trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole 治疗尿路感染。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client uses naproxen 500 mg twice daily for knee pain.","zh":"患者因膝痛每天两次服用 naproxen 500 mg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client takes acetaminophen 650 mg once at bedtime.","zh":"患者睡前服用 acetaminophen 650 mg 一次。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client keeps a written list of all prescription medications.","zh":"患者保留所有处方药的书面清单。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Warfarin is an anticoagulant. Starting trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole and using naproxen can increase bleeding risk and should be clarified during medication reconciliation. A single bedtime acetaminophen dose and maintaining a written medication list are not the bleeding-risk red flags in this note.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Warfarin 是抗凝药。开始使用 trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole 以及服用 naproxen 均可能增加出血风险，需在用药核对中澄清。睡前单次 acetaminophen 和保留用药清单不是本记录中的出血风险警讯。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In reconciliation questions, pair each home medication with new prescriptions and ask which combinations create harm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"用药核对题要把居家用药和新处方配对，判断哪些组合会造成伤害。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1761,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_highlight_cefazolin_allergy_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.327","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.327.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.327.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,38],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer the first dose of cefazolin. Highlight the history finding that requires follow-up before administration.","fullStemZh":"护士准备给予第一剂 cefazolin。标出给药前需要进一步跟进的病史发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the history finding that requires follow-up before administration.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出给药前需要进一步跟进的病史发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer the first dose of cefazolin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备给予第一剂 cefazolin。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Pre-administration screen:","zh":"给药前筛查："},{"id":"s2","en":"The client reports throat tightness and hives after cefazolin during a prior surgery.","zh":"患者报告上次手术使用 cefazolin 后出现喉咙紧缩和荨麻疹。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client had nausea with oral iron tablets.","zh":"患者服用口服铁剂时曾恶心。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client says, “Antibiotics sometimes give me loose stools.”","zh":"患者说：“抗生素有时会让我大便变稀。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client completed amoxicillin as a child but does not remember the dose.","zh":"患者小时候完成过 amoxicillin 疗程，但不记得剂量。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Throat tightness and hives after the same antibiotic suggest a potentially serious immediate hypersensitivity history and require follow-up before administering cefazolin. Nausea with iron, loose stools with antibiotics, and not remembering a childhood dose are not the same immediate allergy cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"曾在使用同一种抗生素后出现喉咙紧缩和荨麻疹，提示可能有严重即刻型超敏反应史，给 cefazolin 前必须跟进。铁剂恶心、抗生素导致稀便、不记得童年剂量，都不是同等的即刻过敏线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate side effects from allergy. Airway symptoms, hives, swelling, or anaphylaxis history should stop routine administration until clarified.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分副作用和过敏。气道症状、荨麻疹、肿胀或过敏性休克史，应在澄清前暂停常规给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1762,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_matrix_high_alert_admin_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.328","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.328.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.328.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,98],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"For each medication-administration situation, select whether the nursing action is safe or unsafe.","fullStemZh":"对每个给药情境，选择该护理措施是安全还是不安全。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each medication-administration situation, select whether the nursing action is safe or unsafe.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每个给药情境，选择该护理措施是安全还是不安全。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Draws insulin lispro into an insulin syringe after comparing the vial with the medication administration record.","zh":"核对药瓶与给药记录后，用胰岛素注射器抽取 insulin lispro。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Draws insulin glargine and insulin lispro into the same syringe to reduce injections.","zh":"为减少注射次数，把 insulin glargine 和 insulin lispro 抽入同一支注射器。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Administers potassium chloride by IV push because the client reports muscle cramps.","zh":"因患者主诉肌肉痉挛，将 potassium chloride 静脉推注。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Checks respiratory rate and sedation level before giving a repeat IV hydromorphone dose.","zh":"再次给予 IV hydromorphone 前检查呼吸频率和镇静程度。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Clarifies a heparin bolus order when the current weight is missing from the chart.","zh":"病历缺少当前体重时，先澄清 heparin 负荷剂量医嘱。"}],"columns":[{"id":"safe","en":"Safe","zh":"安全"},{"id":"unsafe","en":"Unsafe","zh":"不安全"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["unsafe"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["unsafe"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["safe"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe high-alert medication practice includes using the correct syringe, checking labels, monitoring before repeat opioids, and clarifying weight-based anticoagulant orders. Insulin glargine should not be mixed with other insulin, and potassium chloride should not be given by IV push.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高警示药物的安全做法包括使用正确注射器、核对标签、重复给阿片前监测，以及澄清按体重给药的抗凝医嘱。Insulin glargine 不应与其他胰岛素混合，potassium chloride 不应静脉推注。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-alert drugs, unsafe shortcuts often involve the wrong device, skipped assessment, skipped clarification, or rapid IV administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高警示药物中，不安全捷径常包括用错器具、跳过评估、跳过澄清或快速静脉给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1763,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_matrix_anticoagulant_teach_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.329","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.329.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.329.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,94],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,25],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing statements from clients taking anticoagulants. Classify each statement.","fullStemZh":"护士正在复习服用抗凝药患者的陈述。请对每句话分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每句话分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing statements from clients taking anticoagulants.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在复习服用抗凝药患者的陈述。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"“I will call the clinic if I notice black, tarry stools.”","zh":"“如果发现黑色柏油样大便，我会打电话给诊所。”"},{"id":"r2","en":"“I started taking aspirin every day because I thought it would protect my heart.”","zh":"“我开始每天服用 aspirin，因为我觉得能保护心脏。”"},{"id":"r3","en":"“I use an electric razor and a soft toothbrush.”","zh":"“我使用电动剃须刀和软毛牙刷。”"},{"id":"r4","en":"“I will stop my apixaban whenever I see a small bruise.”","zh":"“只要看到小瘀青，我就会停用 apixaban。”"},{"id":"r5","en":"“I keep my appointments for INR checks while taking warfarin.”","zh":"“服用 warfarin 期间，我会按时做 INR 检查。”"}],"columns":[{"id":"understanding","en":"Shows understanding","zh":"理解正确"},{"id":"follow_up","en":"Needs follow-up teaching","zh":"需要进一步教学"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["understanding"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["follow_up"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["understanding"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["follow_up"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["understanding"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clients taking anticoagulants should report bleeding signs, reduce injury risk, and keep warfarin INR monitoring. Starting daily aspirin without provider guidance can increase bleeding risk, and stopping apixaban independently can increase clot risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"服用抗凝药的患者应报告出血表现、减少受伤风险，并按时进行 warfarin 的 INR 监测。未经医嘱自行每日服用 aspirin 可增加出血风险；自行停用 apixaban 可增加血栓风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Teaching is correct when it balances bleeding precautions with not stopping anticoagulation independently.","testTakingStrategyZh":"正确教学要同时强调出血预防和不要自行停用抗凝药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1764,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_sata_naloxone_teaching_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.330","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.330.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.330.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse teaches a family member how to respond to a suspected opioid overdose using naloxone nasal spray. Which instructions should the nurse include? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士向家属教学如何使用 naloxone 鼻喷剂处理疑似阿片过量。护士应包括哪些指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应包括哪些指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Check the printed expiration date during routine storage checks.","zh":"日常保存检查时查看包装上印刷的有效期。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give another dose in 2 to 3 minutes if the person does not respond or breathing does not improve.","zh":"若 2 到 3 分钟后无反应或呼吸未改善，再给一剂。"},{"id":"E","en":"Give oral fluids as soon as the person becomes hard to arouse.","zh":"患者难以唤醒时立即给予口服液体。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stay with the person because opioid effects may return after naloxone wears off.","zh":"留在患者身边，因为 naloxone 作用消退后阿片效应可能再次出现。"},{"id":"D","en":"Withhold naloxone until you know exactly which opioid was taken.","zh":"等确定具体服用了哪种阿片后再给 naloxone。"},{"id":"A","en":"Call emergency medical services after giving naloxone.","zh":"给予 naloxone 后呼叫急救服务。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Naloxone is for suspected opioid overdose, but emergency services are still needed. A repeat dose may be needed in 2 to 3 minutes if response or breathing is inadequate, and the person must be observed because naloxone may wear off before the opioid. Routine checks should include the printed expiration date. Waiting to identify the exact opioid or giving oral fluids to a hard-to-arouse person is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Naloxone 用于疑似阿片过量，但仍需急救服务。如果 2 到 3 分钟后反应或呼吸不足，可能需要重复给药；还要持续观察，因为 naloxone 可能先于阿片作用消退。日常检查应查看印刷有效期。等待确认具体阿片或给难以唤醒者口服液体都不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For reversal agents, choose actions that restore breathing and activate emergency response; reject delays and oral intake in decreased consciousness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"解毒/逆转药题要选择恢复呼吸和启动急救的措施；意识下降时拒绝延迟和口服摄入。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1765,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_a_mc_allergy_hold_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.331","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.331.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.331.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,78],"fullStemEn":"The medication administration record lists cefazolin 2 g IV now. Before administration, the client says, “The last time I received cefazolin, my lips swelled and I had trouble breathing.” What is the nurse’s best action?","fullStemZh":"给药记录显示现在给予 cefazolin 2 g IV。给药前，患者说：“上次我接受 cefazolin 时，嘴唇肿了，而且呼吸困难。”护士最佳行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse’s best action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Before administration, the client says, “The last time I received cefazolin, my lips swelled and I had trouble breathing.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"给药前，患者说：“上次我接受 cefazolin 时，嘴唇肿了，而且呼吸困难。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the cefazolin slowly and monitor for nausea.","zh":"缓慢给予 cefazolin，并观察恶心。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the statement and administer the dose because it is due now.","zh":"记录该陈述，但因已到给药时间仍给予该剂量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give diphenhydramine first, then administer cefazolin as ordered.","zh":"先给 diphenhydramine，再按医嘱给予 cefazolin。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the cefazolin and notify the provider/pharmacist for clarification.","zh":"暂停 cefazolin，并通知医师/药师澄清。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lip swelling and trouble breathing after the same antibiotic suggest a serious hypersensitivity reaction. The nurse should hold the medication and clarify before administration. Slowing the infusion, premedicating independently, or giving the dose because it is due ignores an airway-risk allergy history.","rationaleCorrectZh":"同一种抗生素后出现嘴唇肿胀和呼吸困难，提示严重超敏反应。护士应暂停给药并在给药前澄清。单纯放慢速度、自行预先给抗过敏药，或因到时间就给药，都忽视了气道风险过敏史。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an option protects the airway and prevents re-exposure to a suspected allergen, it usually outranks “give and monitor.”","testTakingStrategyZh":"当某选项能保护气道并避免再次接触疑似过敏原时，通常优先于“给药并观察”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1766,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_fib_insulin_infusion_rate_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.332","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.332.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.332.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[205,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[117,135],"fullStemEn":"The medication administration record lists regular insulin 3 units/hr IV. The infusion bag is labeled regular insulin 100 units in 100 mL 0.9% sodium chloride. Program the infusion pump at how many mL/hr? Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"给药记录显示 regular insulin IV 3 units/hr。输液袋标签为 regular insulin 100 units 加入 100 mL 0.9% sodium chloride。输液泵应设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Program the infusion pump at how many mL/hr?","penultimateSentenceZh":"输液泵应设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["3","3 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":3,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bag concentration is 100 units ÷ 100 mL = 1 unit/mL. To deliver 3 units/hr, the pump must run at 3 mL/hr. Insulin is high-alert, so the nurse should calculate from the labeled concentration before programming the pump.","rationaleCorrectZh":"输液袋浓度为 100 units ÷ 100 mL = 1 unit/mL。若需给 3 units/hr，泵速为 3 mL/hr。胰岛素是高警示药物，设置泵前应根据标签浓度计算。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cancel units carefully: units/hr divided by units/mL leaves mL/hr.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细抵消单位：units/hr 除以 units/mL，剩下 mL/hr。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1767,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_fib_vancomycin_rate_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.333","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.333.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.333.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[75,93],"fullStemEn":"Vancomycin 1 g in 250 mL 0.9% sodium chloride is prescribed to infuse over 90 minutes. At how many mL/hr should the nurse program the pump? Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为 vancomycin 1 g 加入 250 mL 0.9% sodium chloride，90 分钟输完。护士应将泵设置为多少 mL/hr？四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At how many mL/hr should the nurse program the pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将泵设置为多少 mL/hr？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["167","167 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":167,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ninety minutes is 1.5 hours. Pump rate = 250 mL ÷ 1.5 hr = 166.7 mL/hr, which rounds to 167 mL/hr. The dose in grams is used to verify the medication order, but the pump rate comes from volume divided by time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"90 分钟等于 1.5 小时。泵速 = 250 mL ÷ 1.5 hr = 166.7 mL/hr，四舍五入为 167 mL/hr。克数用于核对医嘱，泵速由容量除以时间得出。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When time is given in minutes, convert to hours before calculating mL/hr.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题目给分钟时，先换算成小时再计算 mL/hr。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1768,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_fib_morphine_volume_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.334","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.334.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.334.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,83],"fullStemEn":"Morphine 2 mg IV now is prescribed for severe pain. The vial is labeled morphine 4 mg/mL. How many mL should the nurse draw up? Round to the nearest tenth mL.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为现在给予 morphine 2 mg IV 治疗重度疼痛。药瓶标签为 morphine 4 mg/mL。护士应抽取多少 mL？四舍五入到最接近的十分之一 mL。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest tenth mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的十分之一 mL。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse draw up?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应抽取多少 mL？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["0.5","0.5 mL"],"numeric":{"value":0.5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Volume = ordered dose ÷ concentration = 2 mg ÷ 4 mg/mL = 0.5 mL. Drawing up 2 mL would give 8 mg, and drawing up 4 mL would give 16 mg, so the label concentration must be used.","rationaleCorrectZh":"体积 = 医嘱剂量 ÷ 浓度 = 2 mg ÷ 4 mg/mL = 0.5 mL。若抽 2 mL 会给 8 mg，抽 4 mL 会给 16 mg，因此必须按标签浓度计算。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For injectable volumes, divide the ordered dose by the concentration on the vial.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算注射体积时，用医嘱剂量除以药瓶浓度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse draw up?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应抽取多少 mL？"}
{"queueIndex":1769,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_fib_acetaminophen_peds_volume_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.335","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.335.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.335.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[175,205],"terminalOffsetsZh":[87,104],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes acetaminophen 15 mg/kg PO once for a child who weighs 18 kg. The liquid is labeled acetaminophen 160 mg/5 mL. How many mL should the nurse administer? Round to the nearest tenth mL.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为一名体重 18 kg 的儿童一次口服 acetaminophen 15 mg/kg。药液标签为 acetaminophen 160 mg/5 mL。护士应给多少 mL？四舍五入到最接近的十分之一 mL。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest tenth mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的十分之一 mL。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应给多少 mL？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["8.4","8.4 mL"],"numeric":{"value":8.4,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Dose needed: 15 mg/kg × 18 kg = 270 mg. The liquid concentration is 160 mg ÷ 5 mL = 32 mg/mL. Volume = 270 mg ÷ 32 mg/mL = 8.4375 mL, which rounds to 8.4 mL to the nearest tenth.","rationaleCorrectZh":"所需剂量：15 mg/kg × 18 kg = 270 mg。药液浓度为 160 mg ÷ 5 mL = 32 mg/mL。体积 = 270 mg ÷ 32 mg/mL = 8.4375 mL，按十分之一 mL 取整为 8.4 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Weight-based liquid-dose questions usually need two steps: find the mg dose, then convert mg to mL.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按体重计算液体剂量通常分两步：先算 mg 剂量，再把 mg 换算成 mL。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1770,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_bowtie_insulin_hypoglycemia_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.336","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.336.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.336.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[215,244],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,68],"fullStemEn":"A client with diabetes received rapid-acting insulin before lunch, but the meal tray was delayed. The client is awake, shaky, diaphoretic, and reports feeling “weak and hungry.” Capillary blood glucose is 48 mg/dL. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名糖尿病患者午餐前接受速效胰岛素，但餐盘延迟送达。患者清醒、发抖、出汗，并说“虚弱又饿”。指尖血糖为 48 mg/dL。完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Capillary blood glucose is 48 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"指尖血糖为 48 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_hypoglycemia","en":"Hypoglycemia after insulin without food","zh":"胰岛素后未进食导致低血糖"},{"id":"c_hyperglycemia","en":"Hyperglycemia from missed insulin","zh":"漏用胰岛素导致高血糖"},{"id":"c_anaphylaxis","en":"Anaphylaxis to insulin","zh":"对胰岛素发生过敏性休克"}],"correct":"c_hypoglycemia"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_more_insulin","en":"Administer an additional rapid-acting insulin dose","zh":"再给予一剂速效胰岛素"},{"id":"a_fast_carb","en":"Give 15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate now","zh":"立即给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物"},{"id":"a_send_walk","en":"Have the client walk to stimulate appetite","zh":"让患者走动以刺激食欲"},{"id":"a_recheck_15","en":"Recheck blood glucose in 15 minutes","zh":"15 分钟后复查血糖"}],"correct":["a_fast_carb","a_recheck_15"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_neuro","en":"Mental status and hypoglycemia symptoms","zh":"意识状态和低血糖症状"},{"id":"p_daily_weight","en":"Daily weight trend only","zh":"只看每日体重趋势"},{"id":"p_stool","en":"Stool color","zh":"大便颜色"},{"id":"p_glucose","en":"Repeat blood glucose result","zh":"复查血糖结果"}],"correct":["p_glucose","p_neuro"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The low glucose, shakiness, diaphoresis, hunger, and delayed meal after rapid-acting insulin indicate hypoglycemia. Because the client is awake and can swallow, fast-acting carbohydrate and a 15-minute glucose recheck are priority actions. More insulin and activity would worsen hypoglycemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低血糖值、发抖、出汗、饥饿感，以及速效胰岛素后进餐延迟，提示低血糖。患者清醒且能吞咽，应优先给予快速作用碳水化合物并 15 分钟后复查血糖。继续给胰岛素或活动会加重低血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the medication timing to the cue: rapid insulin plus delayed food plus glucose below 70 mg/dL points to hypoglycemia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把给药时间和线索联系起来：速效胰岛素 + 进餐延迟 + 血糖低于 70 mg/dL 指向低血糖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1771,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_bowtie_vancomycin_infusion_reaction_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.337","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.337.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.337.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[214,243],"terminalOffsetsZh":[74,81],"fullStemEn":"Ten minutes after a vancomycin infusion is started, the client reports itching. The nurse notes flushing of the face, neck, and upper chest. Blood pressure is 96/58 mm Hg; respirations are 18/min without wheezing. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"开始输注 vancomycin 10 分钟后，患者诉瘙痒。护士发现面部、颈部和上胸部潮红。血压 96/58 mm Hg；呼吸 18 次/分，无喘鸣。完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Blood pressure is 96/58 mm Hg; respirations are 18/min without wheezing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压 96/58 mm Hg；呼吸 18 次/分，无喘鸣。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_fluid_overload","en":"Fluid volume overload","zh":"液体容量过多"},{"id":"c_vanc_reaction","en":"Vancomycin infusion reaction","zh":"万古霉素输注反应"},{"id":"c_opioid_toxicity","en":"Opioid toxicity","zh":"阿片毒性"}],"correct":"c_vanc_reaction"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_oral_water","en":"Give oral water and leave the infusion running","zh":"给予口服水并继续输注"},{"id":"a_stop_assess","en":"Stop the infusion and assess airway, breathing, and circulation","zh":"停止输注并评估气道、呼吸和循环"},{"id":"a_continue","en":"Continue the infusion at the same rate because itching is expected","zh":"因瘙痒属预期反应，按原速度继续输注"},{"id":"a_notify","en":"Notify the provider/pharmacy for treatment and infusion-rate guidance","zh":"通知医师/药师以获得处理和输注速度指导"}],"correct":["a_stop_assess","a_notify"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_skin_symptoms","en":"Flushing, rash, itching, or progression of symptoms","zh":"潮红、皮疹、瘙痒或症状进展"},{"id":"p_appetite","en":"Appetite after the infusion","zh":"输注后食欲"},{"id":"p_bp_airway","en":"Blood pressure, airway, and respiratory status","zh":"血压、气道和呼吸状态"},{"id":"p_calcium","en":"Serum calcium only","zh":"只看血钙"}],"correct":["p_bp_airway","p_skin_symptoms"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Flushing and itching soon after vancomycin starts are consistent with a vancomycin infusion reaction. The nurse should stop the infusion, assess ABCs and hemodynamic status, and notify the provider/pharmacy for treatment and safe restart-rate guidance. Continuing the infusion or treating with oral water ignores possible progression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Vancomycin 开始后很快出现潮红和瘙痒，符合万古霉素输注反应。护士应停止输注，评估气道、呼吸、循环和血流动力学状态，并通知医师/药师以获得处理及安全重新输注速度指导。继续输注或只给口服水会忽视症状进展风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Infusion reactions are about timing: new symptoms that begin soon after an IV drug starts require stopping the infusion and assessing severity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输注反应关键看时间：IV 药物开始后很快出现新症状，应停止输注并评估严重程度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1772,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_highlight_apixaban_bleeding_rec_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.338","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.338.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.338.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the medication-reconciliation findings that require provider or pharmacist follow-up in the setting of apixaban therapy.","fullStemZh":"标出在 apixaban 治疗背景下需要医师或药师进一步跟进的用药核对发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the medication-reconciliation findings that require provider or pharmacist follow-up in the setting of apixaban therapy.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出在 apixaban 治疗背景下需要医师或药师进一步跟进的用药核对发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Medication reconciliation note:","zh":"用药核对记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"The client takes apixaban 5 mg twice daily for atrial fibrillation.","zh":"患者因房颤服用 apixaban 5 mg，每日两次。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client started taking over-the-counter ibuprofen 600 mg three times daily for back pain.","zh":"患者因背痛开始自行服用非处方 ibuprofen 600 mg，每日三次。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client also takes aspirin 81 mg daily but is unsure who prescribed it.","zh":"患者还每日服用 aspirin 81 mg，但不确定是谁开的。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client reports two black, tarry stools this week.","zh":"患者报告本周有两次黑色柏油样大便。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client uses a pill organizer filled every Sunday.","zh":"患者使用每周日装好的分药盒。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ibuprofen and aspirin can increase bleeding risk when combined with apixaban, especially when the aspirin indication is unclear. Black, tarry stools are a possible sign of gastrointestinal bleeding and require prompt follow-up. Apixaban itself explains the anticoagulant context, and a pill organizer is not a bleeding-risk red flag.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Ibuprofen 和 aspirin 与 apixaban 合用可增加出血风险，尤其是 aspirin 适应证不清时。黑色柏油样大便可能提示胃肠道出血，需要及时跟进。Apixaban 本身提供抗凝背景，分药盒不是出血风险警讯。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With anticoagulants, look for drugs that affect hemostasis and symptoms that suggest active bleeding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到抗凝药，要找影响止血的药物以及提示活动性出血的症状。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1773,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_highlight_gentamicin_toxicity_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.339","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.339.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.339.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[37,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,41],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving IV gentamicin. Highlight the cues that require follow-up before the next scheduled dose.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受 IV gentamicin。标出下一次计划给药前需要跟进的线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the cues that require follow-up before the next scheduled dose.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出下一次计划给药前需要跟进的线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving IV gentamicin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者正在接受 IV gentamicin。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Progress note before scheduled gentamicin dose:","zh":"计划 gentamicin 给药前进展记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"Serum creatinine increased from 0.8 mg/dL to 1.6 mg/dL since therapy began.","zh":"治疗开始后 serum creatinine 从 0.8 mg/dL 升至 1.6 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Urine output has averaged 20 mL/hr for the past 4 hours.","zh":"过去 4 小时尿量平均 20 mL/hr。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client reports new ringing in both ears.","zh":"患者报告双耳新出现耳鸣。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"White blood cell count decreased from 16 ×10³/µL to 11 ×10³/µL.","zh":"白细胞计数从 16 ×10³/µL 降至 11 ×10³/µL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client reports mild nausea after breakfast.","zh":"患者报告早餐后轻度恶心。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Gentamicin is an aminoglycoside associated with nephrotoxicity and ototoxicity. A rising creatinine, low urine output, and new tinnitus require follow-up before another dose. A falling white blood cell count may indicate infection response, and mild nausea alone is not the key toxicity cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Gentamicin 属氨基糖苷类，相关风险包括肾毒性和耳毒性。肌酐升高、尿量低和新发耳鸣都需要在下一剂前跟进。白细胞下降可能提示感染改善，单纯轻度恶心不是关键毒性线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For aminoglycosides, kidney function and hearing/vestibular changes are high-yield safety cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"氨基糖苷类药物中，肾功能和听力/前庭变化是高价值安全线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1774,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_matrix_iv_infusion_safety_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.340","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.340.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.340.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"For each IV medication-safety action, select whether the action is safe or unsafe.","fullStemZh":"对每项 IV 用药安全措施，选择该措施是安全还是不安全。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each IV medication-safety action, select whether the action is safe or unsafe.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每项 IV 用药安全措施，选择该措施是安全还是不安全。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Compare the medication label with the MAR before programming a new infusion.","zh":"设置新输注前，将药物标签与给药记录核对。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Connect a second IV medication to the same Y-site because both are clear solutions.","zh":"因两种 IV 药液都澄清，就把第二种药接到同一个 Y-site。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Stop the infusion and assess the IV site when the client reports burning and swelling at the site.","zh":"患者诉输液部位灼痛并肿胀时，停止输注并评估 IV 部位。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Use the smart-pump drug library when initiating a heparin infusion.","zh":"开始 heparin 输注时使用智能泵药物库。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Silence an occlusion alarm and restart the pump without checking the tubing or IV site.","zh":"消除阻塞报警后，不检查管路或 IV 部位就重新启动泵。"}],"columns":[{"id":"unsafe","en":"Unsafe","zh":"不安全"},{"id":"safe","en":"Safe","zh":"安全"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["unsafe"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["unsafe"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe IV medication practice includes label/MAR verification, assessing possible infiltration/extravasation symptoms, and using smart-pump safety features for high-alert infusions. Y-site compatibility cannot be assumed from appearance, and alarms require assessment rather than bypassing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全的 IV 用药包括核对标签/给药记录、评估可能的渗漏/外渗症状，以及对高警示输注使用智能泵安全功能。不能因外观澄清就假定 Y-site 相容；报警需要评估，不能绕过。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Reject IV shortcuts that assume compatibility, bypass alarms, or ignore site symptoms.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排除那些假定相容性、绕过报警或忽视输液部位症状的 IV 捷径。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1775,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_matrix_patient_teaching_safety_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.341","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.341.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.341.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,102],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"For each client statement, select whether the statement shows safe or unsafe medication understanding.","fullStemZh":"对每个患者陈述，选择该陈述显示安全还是不安全的用药理解。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each client statement, select whether the statement shows safe or unsafe medication understanding.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每个患者陈述，选择该陈述显示安全还是不安全的用药理解。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"“I will call my provider if I have red urine or black stools while taking apixaban.”","zh":"“服用 apixaban 时，如果出现红色尿液或黑便，我会联系医师。”"},{"id":"r2","en":"“If I get a nosebleed, I should skip several doses of apixaban without telling anyone.”","zh":"“如果流鼻血，我应自行跳过几剂 apixaban，不用告诉任何人。”"},{"id":"r3","en":"“I will keep a quick sugar source with me because I use insulin.”","zh":"“因为我使用胰岛素，我会随身带快速糖源。”"},{"id":"r4","en":"“I can drink alcohol with oxycodone at bedtime so I sleep better.”","zh":"“睡前可将酒精和 oxycodone 一起用，这样睡得更好。”"},{"id":"r5","en":"“I should not share my insulin pen with another person.”","zh":"“我不应与他人共用我的胰岛素笔。”"}],"columns":[{"id":"unsafe","en":"Unsafe understanding","zh":"不安全理解"},{"id":"safe","en":"Safe understanding","zh":"安全理解"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["unsafe"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["safe"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["unsafe"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["safe"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe teaching includes reporting possible bleeding while on anticoagulants, carrying a rapid sugar source with insulin, and not sharing insulin pens. Self-stopping several anticoagulant doses can increase clot risk, and combining alcohol with opioids can worsen sedation and respiratory depression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全教学包括抗凝期间报告可能出血、使用胰岛素时随身带快速糖源，以及不共用胰岛素笔。自行停用多剂抗凝药会增加血栓风险；酒精与阿片类合用会加重镇静和呼吸抑制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Teaching items often turn on “report,” “do not share,” and “do not mix sedatives/alcohol with opioids.”","testTakingStrategyZh":"教学题常考“报告异常”、“不要共用”以及“不要把镇静物质/酒精与阿片合用”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1776,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_sata_transfusion_reaction_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.342","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.342.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.342.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,71],"fullStemEn":"Fifteen minutes after packed red blood cells are started, the client develops chills, fever, low back pain, and dark urine. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"开始输注 packed red blood cells 15 分钟后，患者出现寒战、发热、腰背痛和深色尿。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Recheck vital signs and patient/blood product identification.","zh":"复查生命体征和患者/血液制品身份信息。"},{"id":"B","en":"Keep IV access open with 0.9% sodium chloride using new tubing per policy.","zh":"按政策用新管路以 0.9% sodium chloride 保持 IV 通路开放。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider and blood bank/transfusion service.","zh":"通知医师和血库/输血服务。"},{"id":"E","en":"Restart the transfusion at a slower rate after the fever decreases.","zh":"发热下降后以较慢速度重新开始输血。"},{"id":"F","en":"Discard the blood bag and tubing before the blood bank evaluates them.","zh":"血库评估前丢弃血袋和输血管路。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the transfusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止输血。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fever, chills, back pain, and dark urine soon after starting blood are concerning for an acute transfusion reaction. The nurse should stop the transfusion, maintain IV access with normal saline and new tubing per policy, notify the provider and blood bank, and reassess vital signs and identification. The transfusion should not be restarted, and the blood product/tubing should not be discarded before evaluation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"开始输血后很快出现发热、寒战、腰背痛和深色尿，提示急性输血反应。护士应停止输血，按政策用生理盐水和新管路保持 IV 通路，通知医师和血库，并复查生命体征与身份信息。不应重新开始输血，也不应在评估前丢弃血液制品/管路。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For suspected transfusion reactions, choose stop, maintain access with saline, notify, reassess, and preserve the product for workup.","testTakingStrategyZh":"疑似输血反应题，选择停止、用生理盐水保持通路、通知、复评，并保留血液制品以供检查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？"}
{"queueIndex":1777,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pharm_easy_medium_2026_06_21_b_mc_potassium_iv_push_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.343","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.343.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.343.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[71,81],"fullStemEn":"The nurse receives a new order: “Potassium chloride 40 mEq IV push now for potassium 3.0 mEq/L.” What is the nurse’s best action?","fullStemZh":"护士收到新医嘱：“Potassium chloride 40 mEq IV push now，用于 potassium 3.0 mEq/L。”护士最佳行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse’s best action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse receives a new order: “Potassium chloride 40 mEq IV push now for potassium 3.0 mEq/L.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士收到新医嘱：“Potassium chloride 40 mEq IV push now，用于 potassium 3.0 mEq/L。”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer only half of the IV push dose and recheck potassium later.","zh":"只静推一半剂量，稍后复查 potassium。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the potassium chloride IV push slowly over 5 minutes.","zh":"将 potassium chloride 静脉推注，5 分钟内慢慢推完。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give the potassium chloride IM because IV push is unsafe.","zh":"因 IV push 不安全，改为 IM 给予 potassium chloride。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the order and contact the provider/pharmacist to clarify a safe diluted infusion order.","zh":"暂停该医嘱，并联系医师/药师澄清安全稀释输注医嘱。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium chloride must not be given IV push. The nurse should hold the unsafe order and clarify a diluted infusion with appropriate rate and monitoring. Giving it slowly IV push, changing the route to IM, or independently giving half the dose are unsafe workarounds.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Potassium chloride 不应 IV push。护士应暂停不安全医嘱，并澄清稀释输注、适当速度和监测要求。慢速静推、擅自改为 IM 或自行给半量都是不安全变通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an order contains an unsafe route for a high-alert electrolyte, do not modify it independently; hold and clarify.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高警示电解质医嘱若包含不安全途径，不要自行修改；应暂停并澄清。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1778,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.344","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.344.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[340,442],"terminalOffsetsZh":[124,155],"fullStemEn":"Caregiver role strain in home management of moderate Alzheimer's dementia Margaret Tierney is a 78-year-old woman with moderate Alzheimer's dementia who lives with her daughter Diane, her sole caregiver. Diane requested home-health support after two months of worsening nighttime wandering and confusion, stating she cannot continue alone. The case unfolds across an initial home visit, later same-visit disclosures, and a five-day follow-up.","fullStemZh":"中度阿尔茨海默病居家照护中的照护者角色压力 Margaret Tierney，78岁，中度阿尔茨海默病，与女儿 Diane 同住；Diane 是唯一照护者。因过去两个月夜间走失和意识混乱加重，Diane 请求居家护理支持，并表示自己无法再独自承担。病例按初次居家访视、同次访视后续透露信息和5天后复诊逐步展开。","terminalSentenceEn":"The case unfolds across an initial home visit, later same-visit disclosures, and a five-day follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"病例按初次居家访视、同次访视后续透露信息和5天后复诊逐步展开。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Diane requested home-health support after two months of worsening nighttime wandering and confusion, stating she cannot continue alone.","penultimateSentenceZh":"因过去两个月夜间走失和意识混乱加重，Diane 请求居家护理支持，并表示自己无法再独自承担。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on caregiver role strain affecting home safety for a client with moderate dementia. Margaret has cognitive impairment, wandering, unsafe stove use, nutrition and hydration concerns, incontinence-related skin risk, fall risk, and unreliable medication administration. Diane shows sleep deprivation, weight loss, work impairment, tremor, guilt, and unsafe coping strategies. The nurse's role is to preserve trust, mitigate immediate hazards, coordinate provider/pharmacy/social-work/community resources, avoid premature accusation of intentional abuse while still documenting and following reporting policy, and evaluate whether safety and caregiver capacity are improving over time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例核心是照护者角色压力影响中度痴呆患者的居家安全。Margaret 有认知受损、走失、炉灶不安全使用、营养和液体摄入担忧、失禁相关皮肤风险、跌倒风险和用药不可靠。Diane 表现出睡眠剥夺、体重下降、工作受影响、手颤、内疚和不安全应对策略。护士的作用是维护信任、减轻即时危险、协调医师/药师/社工/社区资源，避免过早指控故意虐待，同时仍需记录并按政策处理报告问题，并持续评价安全与照护者能力是否改善。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track the unfolding data by stage. Early questions focus on cue recognition and therapeutic response; later questions add medication, fall, and safety disclosures; follow-up questions test whether partial improvement is enough.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按阶段追踪逐步出现的信息。早期题关注线索识别和治疗性回应；后续题加入用药、跌倒和安全补充信息；复诊题考查部分改善是否足够。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1779,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Using the Stage 1 home-visit data, highlight the findings that are significant cues requiring nursing attention.","fullStemZh":"根据第1阶段居家访视资料，标出需要护理关注的重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the Stage 1 home-visit data, highlight the findings that are significant cues requiring nursing attention.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第1阶段居家访视资料，标出需要护理关注的重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q1_s1","selectable":true,"en":"Margaret is oriented only to her first name.","zh":"Margaret 仅能说出自己的名字，无法定向到日期、季节或地址。"},{"id":"q1_s2","selectable":true,"en":"Her housecoat is urine-stained and has a faint urine odor.","zh":"她的家居服有尿渍并有淡淡尿味。"},{"id":"q1_s3","selectable":true,"en":"Perineal skin is mildly erythematous from urine contact.","zh":"会阴皮肤因尿液接触轻度发红。"},{"id":"q1_s4","selectable":true,"en":"Weight has decreased from 61.6 kg nine months ago to 58 kg today.","zh":"体重从9个月前的61.6 kg下降到今天的58 kg。"},{"id":"q1_s5","selectable":true,"en":"Albumin is 3.1 g/dL and prealbumin is 14 mg/dL.","zh":"白蛋白为3.1 g/dL，前白蛋白为14 mg/dL。"},{"id":"q1_s6","selectable":true,"en":"Oral mucosa is slightly dry.","zh":"口腔黏膜轻度干燥。"},{"id":"q1_s7","selectable":true,"en":"Blood pressure is 148/88 while medication administration is unreliable.","zh":"在用药不可靠的情况下，BP为148/88。"},{"id":"q1_s8","selectable":true,"en":"Gait is slow and wide-based with a slight forward lean.","zh":"步态缓慢、基底较宽，并轻度前倾。"},{"id":"q1_s9","selectable":true,"en":"Skin is intact with no bruising, lacerations, or pressure areas.","zh":"皮肤完整，无瘀斑、裂伤或压迫部位损伤。"},{"id":"q1_s10","selectable":true,"en":"Grip strength is symmetric and adequate.","zh":"握力对称且足够。"},{"id":"q1_s11","selectable":true,"en":"Temperature is 98.2 °F (36.8 °C) and SpO₂ is 97% on room air.","zh":"体温98.2 °F (36.8 °C)，室内空气下SpO₂为97%。"},{"id":"q1_s12","selectable":true,"en":"Diane reports sleeping less than four consecutive hours for weeks.","zh":"Diane 报告数周来连续睡眠不足4小时。"},{"id":"q1_s13","selectable":true,"en":"Diane has lost twelve pounds in two months because she forgets to eat.","zh":"Diane 因忘记吃饭，两个月内减重12磅。"},{"id":"q1_s14","selectable":true,"en":"Diane's hands tremble when she opens the pill bottles.","zh":"Diane 打开药瓶时双手轻微颤抖。"},{"id":"q1_s15","selectable":true,"en":"Diane called in sick to work three times last month.","zh":"Diane 上个月请病假3次。"},{"id":"q1_s16","selectable":true,"en":"Diane becomes tearful and says she promised not to place Margaret in a home.","zh":"Diane 哭泣，并说她承诺过不把 Margaret 送进机构。"},{"id":"q1_s17","selectable":true,"en":"A chair is propped under the bedroom doorknob at night.","zh":"夜间有一把椅子抵在卧室门把手下。"},{"id":"q1_s18","selectable":true,"en":"Pill bottles are open and the wrong-day pill organizer is in use.","zh":"药瓶敞开，且药盒日期使用混乱。"},{"id":"q1_s19","selectable":true,"en":"The front door has a deadbolt Margaret can unlock.","zh":"前门是 Margaret 能打开的普通插销锁。"},{"id":"q1_s20","selectable":true,"en":"Stove knobs are uncovered and enabled.","zh":"炉灶旋钮未加盖，也未停用。"},{"id":"q1_s21","selectable":true,"en":"Throw rugs are present in the kitchen and hallway.","zh":"厨房和走廊有小地毯。"},{"id":"q1_s22","selectable":true,"en":"Cleaning supplies are unlocked under the kitchen sink.","zh":"清洁用品未上锁，放在厨房水槽下方。"},{"id":"q1_s23","selectable":true,"en":"Grab bars and night-lights are already present.","zh":"浴室扶手和夜灯已经安装。"}],"correct":["q1_s1","q1_s2","q1_s3","q1_s4","q1_s5","q1_s6","q1_s7","q1_s8","q1_s12","q1_s13","q1_s14","q1_s15","q1_s16","q1_s17","q1_s18","q1_s19","q1_s20","q1_s21","q1_s22"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The significant cue cluster includes Margaret's cognitive impairment, nutritional decline, possible dehydration, incontinence-related skin risk, elevated BP with unreliable medication administration, gait/fall risk, and multiple environmental hazards. Diane's sleep deprivation, weight loss, tremor, missed work, guilt, unsafe door barricade, and medication disorganization show caregiver role strain that directly affects Margaret's safety. Normal temperature, oxygenation, symmetric grip, intact skin, grab bars, and night-lights do not remove the need for follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重要线索包括 Margaret 的认知受损、营养下降、可能脱水、失禁相关皮肤风险、在用药不可靠情况下的血压升高、步态/跌倒风险以及多项环境危险。Diane 的睡眠剥夺、体重下降、手颤、误工、内疚、不安全挡门和药物混乱显示照护者角色压力，并直接影响 Margaret 的安全。体温、氧合、握力、皮肤完整、扶手和夜灯等正常或保护性发现不能消除跟进需要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In home-care dementia questions, assess two clients: the person with dementia and the caregiver. Normal physical findings can reduce concern for one problem but do not cancel environmental or caregiver-capacity risks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在痴呆居家护理题中，要同时评估两个人：痴呆患者和照护者。正常体征可能降低某一问题的担忧，但不能抵消环境风险或照护能力风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1780,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,90],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which interpretation of the findings and nursing response is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，哪一种对评估发现的解释和护理回应最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which interpretation of the findings and nursing response is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第2阶段，哪一种对评估发现的解释和护理回应最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q2_e","en":"The home situation is unsalvageable because Diane missed a clinic appointment, so the nurse should recommend immediate removal from the home as the first response.","zh":"由于 Diane 错过了门诊复诊，居家照护已无法挽回，因此护士的第一反应应是建议立即离家安置。"},{"id":"q2_d","en":"The problem is only medication nonadherence; the nurse should focus on the pill organizer and avoid discussing caregiver stress or home hazards.","zh":"问题只是服药不依从；护士应只关注药盒，避免讨论照护者压力或居家危险。"},{"id":"q2_c","en":"Because Margaret has no bruises or lacerations, the nurse should reassure Diane that no safety documentation or follow-up is needed.","zh":"因为 Margaret 没有瘀斑或裂伤，护士应安慰 Diane 不需要安全记录或跟进。"},{"id":"q2_b","en":"The chair barricade and raised voice prove intentional physical abuse, so the nurse should accuse Diane and demand immediate facility placement before completing the assessment.","zh":"椅子挡门和提高音量证明存在故意身体虐待，因此护士应指责 Diane，并在完成评估前要求立即机构安置。"},{"id":"q2_a","en":"The pattern best supports caregiver role strain with unsafe compensatory strategies; respond nonjudgmentally, correct immediate hazards, document, notify the provider/supervisor or social work, and follow agency/state APS policy if neglect is suspected or safety cannot be maintained.","zh":"该模式最支持照护者角色压力并伴有不安全的补偿性做法；应以非评判方式回应，纠正即时危险，记录，通知医师/主管或社工，并在怀疑忽视或无法维持安全时按机构/州政策联系成人保护服务。"}],"correct":["q2_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Diane's behavior is unsafe but the overall pattern is most consistent with caregiver role strain: she is exhausted, guilty, tearful, receptive to help, and voluntarily requested support. The nurse should not ignore the hazards or excuse unsafe care; the correct response is nonjudgmental support plus documentation, team notification, safety planning, and policy-guided APS reporting assessment if safety cannot be maintained or neglect is suspected.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Diane 的做法不安全，但整体模式最符合照护者角色压力：她疲惫、内疚、哭泣、愿意接受帮助，并主动请求支持。护士不能忽视危险或纵容不安全照护；正确回应是非评判支持，同时记录、通知团队、制定安全计划，并在无法维持安全或怀疑忽视时按政策评估是否需报告成人保护服务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not classify elder-safety cases from one cue alone. Compare intent, injury pattern, caregiver affect, willingness to accept help, and whether hazards can be modified.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要仅凭单一线索判断老年人安全问题。要比较意图、损伤模式、照护者情绪、接受帮助的意愿，以及危险是否可改变。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1781,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"After the Stage 2 disclosures, which priority should the nurse address before leaving the home today?","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段补充信息后，护士今天离开该家庭前应优先处理什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"After the Stage 2 disclosures, which priority should the nurse address before leaving the home today?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第2阶段补充信息后，护士今天离开该家庭前应优先处理什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_e","en":"Defer environmental changes until the follow-up visit because Margaret is currently calm.","zh":"因为 Margaret 目前平静，所以将环境改变推迟到复诊时再处理。"},{"id":"q3_c","en":"Focus first on rechecking the blood pressure and teaching Diane to restart the Wednesday pill compartment tomorrow.","zh":"首先重新测量血压，并教 Diane 明天重新使用星期三药格。"},{"id":"q3_a","en":"Before Diane leaves today, ensure Margaret is not left in an unsafe environment: remove the bedroom-door barricade, use a nonrestrictive door-alert strategy, prevent unsupervised stove access, orient the neighbor to safety monitoring and emergency contacts, and notify the provider about diphenhydramine use.","zh":"在 Diane 今天离开前，确保 Margaret 不会被留在不安全环境中：移除卧室挡门，采用非限制性的门警报策略，防止无人看护时接触炉灶，向邻居说明安全看护和紧急联系方式，并通知医师有关苯海拉明使用情况。"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Schedule a caregiver support group before addressing the stove, door, or neighbor supervision plan.","zh":"先安排照护者支持小组，再处理炉灶、门或邻居看护计划。"},{"id":"q3_b","en":"Prioritize a dietary consult and weekly weights because the albumin and prealbumin are low.","zh":"优先安排营养会诊和每周称重，因为白蛋白和前白蛋白偏低。"}],"correct":["q3_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate threat is that Margaret may be left with uncontrolled elopement and stove hazards while Diane returns to work. The nurse must replace the unsafe barricade with a nonrestrictive alert strategy, control stove access, orient the temporary caregiver, and contact the provider about diphenhydramine because it worsens confusion and compounds fall and wandering risk. Nutrition, BP, and caregiver support are important but not the most immediate life-safety threats before Diane leaves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"即时威胁是 Diane 回去上班后，Margaret 可能面临未控制的走失和炉灶危险。护士必须用非限制性警报策略替代不安全挡门，控制炉灶接触，指导临时照护者，并就苯海拉明联系医师，因为它会加重意识混乱并增加跌倒和走失风险。营养、血压和照护者支持都重要，但不是 Diane 离开前最紧迫的生命安全威胁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several problems are real, choose the action that prevents the most immediate serious harm before the next handoff or period of reduced supervision.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个问题都真实存在时，选择能在下一次交接或看护减少前防止最即时严重伤害的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1782,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[100,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the Stage 2 home-safety and caregiver-support plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应将哪些干预纳入第2阶段的居家安全和照护者支持计划？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the Stage 2 home-safety and caregiver-support plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些干预纳入第2阶段的居家安全和照护者支持计划？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_d","en":"Contact the provider and pharmacist about medication formulations and diphenhydramine use; set up alarms, a written schedule, and a clarified pill-organizer routine.","zh":"就药物剂型和苯海拉明使用联系医师及药师；设置提醒、书面时间表，并明确药盒流程。"},{"id":"q4_a","en":"Remove the bedroom-door barricade and use door alarms or contact sensors on exterior doors; consider medical identification and a local wandering-response program.","zh":"移除卧室挡门，在外门使用门警报或门磁感应器；考虑医疗识别饰品和当地走失应对项目。"},{"id":"q4_f","en":"Continue diphenhydramine at a lower dose and keep the chair barricade until Margaret stops wandering.","zh":"继续较低剂量苯海拉明，并保留椅子挡门，直到 Margaret 停止走失。"},{"id":"q4_c","en":"Remove throw rugs, lock cleaning supplies, maintain lighting, and coordinate physical therapy for gait and fall-risk assessment.","zh":"移除小地毯，锁好清洁用品，保持照明，并协调物理治疗评估步态和跌倒风险。"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"Prevent unsupervised stove use by using knob covers, removing knobs, or disconnecting the stove when not supervised.","zh":"通过旋钮保护盖、取下旋钮，或在无人看护时断开炉灶，防止无人看护使用炉灶。"},{"id":"q4_e","en":"Address nutrition, incontinence, and caregiver support with dietitian referral, preferred small frequent meals, prompted toileting, moisture barrier, social work, Area Agency on Aging, adult day program, caregiver support group, and Diane's own primary-care visit.","zh":"通过营养师转介、少量多餐且选择偏好食物、定时提醒如厕、皮肤屏障霜、社工、老龄事务机构、成人日间照护、照护者支持小组以及 Diane 自己的初级保健就诊，处理营养、失禁和照护者支持。"}],"correct":["q4_a","q4_b","q4_c","q4_d","q4_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The plan must address both sides of the dyad: Margaret's safety risks and Diane's ability to continue caregiving. Appropriate interventions include nonrestrictive wandering alerts, stove control, fall and hazardous-material prevention, medication-formulation and reminder support, provider notification about diphenhydramine, nutrition and incontinence support, respite/adult day resources, social work, caregiver support, and Diane's own health care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计划必须同时处理照护关系中的两方面：Margaret 的安全风险和 Diane 持续照护的能力。合适干预包括非限制性走失警报、炉灶控制、跌倒和危险物预防、药物剂型与提醒支持、向医师报告苯海拉明、营养和失禁支持、喘息服务/成人日间照护资源、社工、照护者支持以及 Diane 自身就医。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SATA care-plan items, select interventions that are specific, actionable, and tied to a cue. Avoid vague advice or actions that continue the unsafe workaround.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在多选护理计划题中，选择具体、可执行且与线索相对应的干预。避免模糊建议或延续不安全权宜做法的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1783,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,61],"fullStemEn":"During Stage 1, after Margaret is safely away from the stove and Diane says, 'I can't do this anymore. I'm failing her,' which nurse response is most therapeutic?","fullStemZh":"第1阶段，当 Margaret 已安全远离炉灶，而 Diane 说‘我撑不下去了，我辜负了她’时，护士哪种回应最具治疗性？","terminalSentenceEn":"I'm failing her,' which nurse response is most therapeutic?","terminalSentenceZh":"第1阶段，当 Margaret 已安全远离炉灶，而 Diane 说‘我撑不下去了，我辜负了她’时，护士哪种回应最具治疗性？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During Stage 1, after Margaret is safely away from the stove and Diane says, 'I can't do this anymore.","penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q5_d","en":"Immediately list every community resource and safety modification without first responding to Diane's statement that she is failing.","zh":"不先回应 Diane 说自己失败了，而是立即列出所有社区资源和安全改造。"},{"id":"q5_a","en":"After confirming Margaret is away from the stove, say: 'This is incredibly hard, and I can see how exhausted you are. Asking for help does not mean you are failing her. Let's take this one step at a time together.'","zh":"确认 Margaret 已远离炉灶后说：‘这真的非常不容易，我看得出你已经很疲惫。寻求帮助并不表示你辜负了她。我们一起一步一步来。’"},{"id":"q5_e","en":"Tell Diane to leave the room so the nurse can correct Margaret's behavior without family interference.","zh":"告诉 Diane 离开房间，让护士在没有家属干扰的情况下纠正 Margaret 的行为。"},{"id":"q5_c","en":"Say: 'You are doing a great job, and everything will get easier once she settles down.'","zh":"说：‘你做得很好，等她安定下来一切都会变容易。’"},{"id":"q5_b","en":"Say: 'You cannot raise your voice at a person with dementia; if you keep doing that, I will have to report you.'","zh":"说：‘你不能对痴呆患者提高音量；如果你继续这样，我就必须举报你。’"}],"correct":["q5_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first ensures immediate safety, then validates Diane's exhaustion and guilt without judgment. This builds trust and opens the door to later education and safety planning. Lecturing, threatening, false reassurance, premature resource-listing, or excluding Diane bypasses the emotional cue and can reduce engagement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先确保即时安全，然后以非评判方式接纳 Diane 的疲惫和内疚。这能建立信任，为之后教育和安全计划打基础。说教、威胁、虚假安慰、过早罗列资源或排除 Diane 都会绕过情绪线索，并可能降低参与度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In therapeutic communication, answer the feeling before the fact list. Validate distress, avoid false reassurance, and preserve safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性沟通题中，先回应情绪，再处理事实清单。要接纳痛苦、避免虚假安慰，并维持安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1784,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.344.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,53],"fullStemEn":"At the Stage 3 follow-up, classify each finding as evidence of improvement, a remaining gap requiring follow-up, or a finding that should be monitored but is not decisive over this short interval.","fullStemZh":"在第3阶段复诊时，将每项发现分类为改善证据、仍需跟进的缺口，或需要监测但在短期内不能作为决定性依据的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"At the Stage 3 follow-up, classify each finding as evidence of improvement, a remaining gap requiring follow-up, or a finding that should be monitored but is not decisive over this short interval.","terminalSentenceZh":"在第3阶段复诊时，将每项发现分类为改善证据、仍需跟进的缺口，或需要监测但在短期内不能作为决定性依据的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"selectionMode":"single_per_row","columns":[{"id":"gap","en":"Remaining gap requiring follow-up","zh":"仍需跟进的缺口"},{"id":"improving","en":"Improvement / safer trajectory","zh":"改善/更安全的趋势"},{"id":"monitor","en":"Monitor, but not decisive over this short interval","zh":"需监测，但短期内不具决定性"}],"rows":[{"id":"q6_r1","en":"Diane removed the chair from the bedroom door and installed a front-door alarm.","zh":"Diane 移除了卧室门上的椅子，并安装了前门警报器。"},{"id":"q6_r2","en":"Margaret has received medications daily with a phone alarm, amlodipine liquid, and pharmacist-confirmed crushed lisinopril.","zh":"通过手机提醒、氨氯地平液体剂型和药师确认可压碎的赖诺普利，Margaret 已每日服药。"},{"id":"q6_r3","en":"Diphenhydramine was stopped, and Diane reports less morning confusion on nights Margaret slept through.","zh":"苯海拉明已停用；Diane 报告 Margaret 睡整夜后的早晨混乱减少。"},{"id":"q6_r4","en":"Diane contacted the Area Agency on Aging, attended an online caregiver support group, and made her own primary-care appointment.","zh":"Diane 联系了老龄事务机构，参加了一次线上照护者支持小组，并预约了自己的初级保健。"},{"id":"q6_r5","en":"The stove remains unsecured.","zh":"炉灶仍未防护。"},{"id":"q6_r6","en":"Throw rugs remain in place and cleaning supplies are still unlocked.","zh":"小地毯仍在原处，清洁用品仍未上锁。"},{"id":"q6_r7","en":"Margaret is not yet enrolled in the adult day program, and Diane remains the only reliable daily caregiver.","zh":"Margaret 尚未报名成人日间照护，Diane 仍是唯一可靠的日常照护者。"},{"id":"q6_r8","en":"Margaret's weight is 57.6 kg, down 0.4 kg from five days ago.","zh":"Margaret 体重57.6 kg，比5天前下降0.4 kg。"},{"id":"q6_r9","en":"SpO₂ is 98% on room air.","zh":"室内空气下SpO₂为98%。"}]},"correct":[{"rowId":"q6_r1","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"q6_r2","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"q6_r3","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"q6_r4","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"q6_r5","columnIds":["gap"]},{"rowId":"q6_r6","columnIds":["gap"]},{"rowId":"q6_r7","columnIds":["gap"]},{"rowId":"q6_r8","columnIds":["monitor"]},{"rowId":"q6_r9","columnIds":["monitor"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The plan is improving but not adequate yet. Door alarm use, medication reliability, stopping diphenhydramine, and caregiver engagement are positive. The unsecured stove, throw rugs, unlocked cleaning supplies, absent adult-day enrollment, and continued reliance on Diane alone remain safety and sustainability gaps. A 0.4 kg five-day weight drop and normal oxygen saturation should be interpreted cautiously rather than used to declare the plan safe or unsafe by themselves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计划正在改善，但尚不足够。门警报、用药更可靠、停用苯海拉明和照护者参与资源是积极信号。炉灶未防护、小地毯、清洁用品未上锁、未报名成人日间照护以及仍主要依赖 Diane 一人，仍是安全和可持续性缺口。5天内体重下降0.4 kg和氧饱和度正常都应谨慎解释，不能单独用来判定计划安全或不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Outcome evaluation often asks for trajectory, not perfection. Credit partial progress while still identifying uncorrected high-risk gaps.","testTakingStrategyZh":"结局评价常考趋势，而不是完美达标。要承认部分进展，同时识别尚未纠正的高风险缺口。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1785,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.345","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.345.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.345.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[556,669],"terminalOffsetsZh":[175,207],"fullStemEn":"At the end of the initial home-health visit, Margaret has moderate dementia with worsening wandering, stove-use risk, weight loss, incontinence-related skin irritation, a recent unreported fall, medication-administration problems, and bedtime diphenhydramine use. Diane is the sole caregiver and reports severe sleep deprivation, weight loss, missed work, guilt, and fear of being judged. She raised her voice during an agitation episode but did not strike, shove, threaten, or physically restrain Margaret, and she voluntarily requested home-health help. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"初次居家护理访视结束时，Margaret 有中度痴呆，并出现走失加重、炉灶使用风险、体重下降、失禁相关皮肤刺激、近期未报告跌倒、给药困难以及睡前使用苯海拉明。Diane 是唯一照护者，报告严重睡眠剥夺、体重下降、误工、内疚和害怕被评判。她在激动 episode 中提高了音量，但没有打、推、威胁或身体限制 Margaret，并且主动请求居家护理帮助。请完成弓形题：选择最可能状况、两个优先行动和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题：选择最可能状况、两个优先行动和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"She raised her voice during an agitation episode but did not strike, shove, threaten, or physically restrain Margaret, and she voluntarily requested home-health help.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她在激动 episode 中提高了音量，但没有打、推、威胁或身体限制 Margaret，并且主动请求居家护理帮助。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_immediate_removal","en":"Caregiver burnout requiring immediate removal from the home","zh":"需要立即离家安置的照护者耗竭"},{"id":"bt_cond_role_strain","en":"Caregiver role strain","zh":"照护者角色压力"},{"id":"bt_cond_intentional_abuse","en":"Intentional elder abuse or willful neglect as the primary explanation","zh":"以故意虐待老人或蓄意忽视作为主要解释"}],"correct":"bt_cond_role_strain"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_act_resource_list_first","en":"Immediately list community resources during Diane's 'I'm failing her' statement without first validating her distress.","zh":"在 Diane 说‘我辜负了她’时，不先接纳她的痛苦，而是立即列出社区资源。"},{"id":"bt_act_secure_home","en":"Mitigate immediate hazards by replacing the bedroom-door barricade with a nonrestrictive door alarm and preventing unsupervised stove access today.","zh":"今天通过用非限制性门警报替代卧室挡门，并防止无人看护时接触炉灶，减轻即时危险。"},{"id":"bt_act_report_diphenhydramine","en":"Contact the primary care provider about diphenhydramine use and advocate for discontinuation and safer sleep evaluation.","zh":"就苯海拉明使用联系初级保健医生，并倡导停用及进行更安全的睡眠问题评估。"},{"id":"bt_act_accuse_diane","en":"Accuse Diane of intentional abuse based only on the chair barricade and raised voice.","zh":"仅根据椅子挡门和提高音量就指责 Diane 故意虐待。"}],"correct":["bt_act_secure_home","bt_act_report_diphenhydramine"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_par_home_mods","en":"Completion of home safety modifications: door alarm in place, stove secured, throw rugs removed, and cleaning supplies locked.","zh":"居家安全改造完成情况：门警报已安装、炉灶已防护、小地毯已移除、清洁用品已上锁。"},{"id":"bt_par_caregiver_status","en":"Diane's sleep, appetite, support-resource engagement, adult-day enrollment progress, and her own primary-care follow-up.","zh":"Diane 的睡眠、食欲、支持资源参与、成人日间照护报名进展以及她自己的初级保健跟进。"},{"id":"bt_par_spo2","en":"Margaret's oxygen saturation in isolation.","zh":"单独监测 Margaret 的氧饱和度。"},{"id":"bt_par_moca","en":"A short-interval formal cognitive screening score as the main outcome.","zh":"将短期正式认知筛查分数作为主要结局。"}],"correct":["bt_par_home_mods","bt_par_caregiver_status"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most likely condition is caregiver role strain. Diane's exhaustion, weight loss, missed work, guilt, unsafe but problem-directed strategies, and willingness to accept help fit role strain more than intentional abuse or immediate removal. The priority actions are to control same-day elopement and stove hazards and to contact the provider about diphenhydramine because it worsens confusion and risk. Monitoring should focus on completion of concrete safety modifications and Diane's ability to recover sleep, nutrition, support, respite, and health care follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能状况是照护者角色压力。Diane 的疲惫、体重下降、误工、内疚、不安全但针对问题的策略，以及愿意接受帮助，更符合角色压力，而不是故意虐待或需要立即离家安置。优先行动是控制当天的走失和炉灶危险，并就苯海拉明联系医师，因为它会加重混乱和风险。监测应聚焦于具体安全改造是否完成，以及 Diane 的睡眠、营养、支持、喘息服务和自身医疗跟进是否改善。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, identify the central problem first, then choose actions and monitoring parameters that directly match it. Avoid distractors that are punitive, premature, or unrelated to the priority risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，先识别中心问题，再选择与之直接匹配的行动和监测参数。避免惩罚性、过早或与优先风险无关的干扰项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1786,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.346","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.346.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[444,582],"terminalOffsetsZh":[137,173],"fullStemEn":"Cross-contamination prevention during clustered care A day-shift nurse on a medical-surgical unit is caring for four adjacent clients: Client A with Clostridioides difficile infection on contact precautions, Client B with community-acquired pneumonia on standard precautions, Client C with a draining MRSA pressure injury on contact precautions, and Client D with smear-positive pulmonary TB in a functioning airborne infection isolation room. The nurse must model safe practice for a nursing student, teach visitors, and contain several infection-control breaches during the shift.","fullStemZh":"集中照护期间预防交叉污染 一名日班护士在内外科病区照护四名相邻病房的患者：A 患者为艰难梭菌感染并执行接触隔离，B 患者为社区获得性肺炎并执行标准预防，C 患者有引流性 MRSA 3期压力性损伤并执行接触隔离，D 患者为痰涂片阳性肺结核并住在功能正常的空气传播感染隔离病房。护士需要为护生示范正确做法，教育探视者，并在班次中控制多项感染控制漏洞。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must model safe practice for a nursing student, teach visitors, and contain several infection-control breaches during the shift.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士需要为护生示范正确做法，教育探视者，并在班次中控制多项感染控制漏洞。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Cross-contamination prevention during clustered care A day-shift nurse on a medical-surgical unit is caring for four adjacent clients: Client A with Clostridioides difficile infection on contact precautions, Client B with community-acquired pneumonia on standard precautions, Client C with a draining MRSA pressure injury on contact precautions, and Client D with smear-positive pulmonary TB in a functioning airborne infection isolation room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"集中照护期间预防交叉污染 一名日班护士在内外科病区照护四名相邻病房的患者：A 患者为艰难梭菌感染并执行接触隔离，B 患者为社区获得性肺炎并执行标准预防，C 患者有引流性 MRSA 3期压力性损伤并执行接触隔离，D 患者为痰涂片阳性肺结核并住在功能正常的空气传播感染隔离病房。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on preventing cross-contamination while moving between clients with different precautions. Key judgments include recognizing true PPE and hand-hygiene breaches in a CDI room, using organism-specific disinfection and wet-contact time for shared equipment, teaching MRSA contact precautions without blaming family, prioritizing the contaminated stethoscope in the clean utility room because it creates the broadest direct fomite pathway, maintaining AIIR restrictions for smear-positive TB, and evaluating effectiveness through observed behavior and corrected environmental hazards rather than same-shift infection rates.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例核心是护士在不同隔离预防患者之间移动照护时预防交叉污染。关键判断包括识别 CDI 病房中的真实 PPE 和手卫生漏洞；对共用设备使用针对病原体的消毒和湿接触时间；在不责备家属的情况下教育 MRSA 接触隔离；因清洁用物间污染听诊器形成最广、最直接的污染媒介路径而将其列为优先；对涂片阳性肺结核继续维持 AIIR 限制；并通过可观察行为和已纠正的环境危险评价效果，而不是依赖同一班次内的感染发生率。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track the organism, route of transmission, and radius of exposure. The safest answer usually interrupts the most direct route of spread while preserving appropriate family involvement and using the facility policy stated in the chart.","testTakingStrategyZh":"追踪病原体、传播途径和暴露范围。最安全的答案通常是切断最直接的传播路径，同时保留适当的家庭参与，并使用病历中给出的机构制度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Cross-contamination prevention during clustered care A day-shift nurse on a medical-surgical unit is caring for four adjacent clients: Client A with Clostridioides difficile infection on contact precautions, Client B with community-acquired pneumonia on standard precautions, Client C with a draining MRSA pressure injury on contact precautions, and Client D with smear-positive pulmonary TB in a functioning airborne infection isolation room.","controlSentenceZh":"集中照护期间预防交叉污染 一名日班护士在内外科病区照护四名相邻病房的患者：A 患者为艰难梭菌感染并执行接触隔离，B 患者为社区获得性肺炎并执行标准预防，C 患者有引流性 MRSA 3期压力性损伤并执行接触隔离，D 患者为痰涂片阳性肺结核并住在功能正常的空气传播感染隔离病房。"}
{"queueIndex":1787,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Classify each nursing-student behavior in Client A's Clostridioides difficile room.","fullStemZh":"阶段1：请判断护生在 A 患者艰难梭菌病房中的每项行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Classify each nursing-student behavior in Client A's Clostridioides difficile room.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段1：请判断护生在 A 患者艰难梭菌病房中的每项行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q1_r1","en":"Entering the contact-precautions room wearing gloves but no gown","zh":"进入接触隔离病房时只戴手套、未穿隔离衣"},{"id":"q1_r2","en":"Using the blood-pressure cuff dedicated to Room 12","zh":"使用12房专用的血压袖带"},{"id":"q1_r3","en":"Removing gloves and failing to perform hand hygiene immediately afterward","zh":"脱下手套后未立即进行手卫生"},{"id":"q1_r4","en":"Touching the door handle with bare, unwashed hands after client contact","zh":"接触患者后用未清洁的裸手触碰门把手"}],"columns":[{"id":"breach","en":"Breach","zh":"违规/漏洞"},{"id":"not_breach","en":"Not a breach","zh":"不是违规"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q1_r1","columnIds":["breach"]},{"rowId":"q1_r2","columnIds":["not_breach"]},{"rowId":"q1_r3","columnIds":["breach"]},{"rowId":"q1_r4","columnIds":["breach"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Contact precautions require gown and gloves before room entry. The dedicated cuff belongs in Room 12 and is appropriate to use. The major failures are missing the gown, missing immediate hand hygiene after glove removal, and touching a shared surface with contaminated bare hands; in a C. difficile room, the required hand-hygiene method is soap and water.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接触隔离要求进入病房前穿隔离衣并戴手套。12房专用血压袖带可在该房内使用。主要问题是未穿隔离衣、脱手套后未立即手卫生，以及用污染的裸手触碰共用表面；在艰难梭菌病房，所需手卫生方式为肥皂和清水洗手。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate true breaches from correct dedicated-equipment use. For contact precautions, ask: Was full PPE used, was hand hygiene done after doffing, and were shared surfaces protected?","testTakingStrategyZh":"把真正的违规与正确使用专用设备区分开。遇到接触隔离题，追问：是否使用了完整 PPE、脱除后是否手卫生、是否保护了共用表面。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1788,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,46],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Put the steps in the correct order for handling the portable bladder scanner after use on Client A before taking it to Client B.","fullStemZh":"阶段1：将为 A 患者使用便携式膀胱扫描仪后、带去 B 患者房间前的处理步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Put the steps in the correct order for handling the portable bladder scanner after use on Client A before taking it to Client B.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段1：将为 A 患者使用便携式膀胱扫描仪后、带去 B 患者房间前的处理步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q2_d","en":"Perform hand hygiene with soap and water immediately after doffing.","zh":"脱除 PPE 后立即用肥皂和清水进行手卫生。"},{"id":"q2_c","en":"Doff gloves first and then gown inside Room 12 before exiting.","zh":"离开前在12房内先脱手套，再脱隔离衣。"},{"id":"q2_a","en":"Clean any visible soil from the scanner surfaces while still in Room 12 and wearing PPE.","zh":"仍在12房且穿戴 PPE 时，先清除扫描仪表面的可见污物。"},{"id":"q2_b","en":"Disinfect the probe, cord, screen or controls, handle, and touched surfaces with an EPA-registered sporicidal disinfectant effective against C. difficile, keeping surfaces wet for the label contact time.","zh":"使用对艰难梭菌有效的 EPA 注册杀孢子消毒剂，消毒探头、导线、屏幕或控制面板、把手及所有接触表面，并保持标签规定的湿接触时间。"},{"id":"q2_e","en":"Transport the disinfected scanner to Client B's room with clean hands.","zh":"用清洁的手将已消毒的扫描仪带到 B 患者房间。"}],"correct":["q2_a","q2_b","q2_c","q2_d","q2_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Because the scanner was used in a CDI contact-precautions room and must be shared with a standard-precautions client, it must be cleaned, disinfected with a sporicidal product, and allowed full wet-contact time before moving to the next room. Doffing and soap-and-water hand hygiene after the device is disinfected prevent the nurse from recontaminating it during transport.","rationaleCorrectZh":"由于扫描仪先在 CDI 接触隔离病房使用，之后要给仅标准预防的患者使用，因此必须先清洁、使用杀孢子产品消毒，并达到完整湿接触时间后才能进入下一病房。设备消毒后再脱除 PPE，并用肥皂和清水洗手，可避免转运时再次污染设备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For shared equipment, think from dirty to clean: remove soil, disinfect with the organism-specific product and contact time, remove contaminated PPE, clean hands, then move the equipment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理共用设备时按“由脏到净”思考：清除污物，使用针对病原体的消毒剂并达到接触时间，脱除污染 PPE，清洁双手，然后再移动设备。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1789,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,44],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Which nursing actions are appropriate when teaching Client C's daughter about MRSA contact precautions? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段1：护士教育 C 患者女儿有关 MRSA 接触隔离时，哪些措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Which nursing actions are appropriate when teaching Client C's daughter about MRSA contact precautions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段1：护士教育 C 患者女儿有关 MRSA 接触隔离时，哪些措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q3_e","en":"Show her where PPE is located and ask for a return demonstration of donning, doffing, and hand hygiene.","zh":"告诉她 PPE 放置位置，并请她回示穿戴、脱除和手卫生。"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Tell her not to touch or reposition her father until the wound has healed.","zh":"告诉她在伤口愈合前不要触碰或协助父亲翻身。"},{"id":"q3_b","en":"Explain that the draining MRSA wound can spread organisms by direct contact with hands, clothing, or linens.","zh":"解释有引流的 MRSA 伤口可通过手、衣物或床单等直接接触传播病原体。"},{"id":"q3_a","en":"Acknowledge that she was not previously oriented and thank her for helping with care.","zh":"承认她先前未被指导，并感谢她协助照护。"},{"id":"q3_f","en":"Give her a surgical mask as the main protection for MRSA contact precautions.","zh":"给她外科口罩作为 MRSA 接触隔离的主要防护。"},{"id":"q3_c","en":"Teach that gown and gloves are required for room entry and direct contact with the client or bed linens.","zh":"告知进入病房以及直接接触患者或床单时需要穿隔离衣并戴手套。"}],"correct":["q3_a","q3_b","q3_c","q3_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The daughter can remain involved in care, but she needs nonjudgmental teaching, clear explanation of contact spread, gown and glove use, and return demonstration. MRSA is spread mainly by contact in this scenario, so gown, gloves, and hand hygiene are the priority, not a surgical mask.","rationaleCorrectZh":"女儿可以继续参与照护，但需要非评判式指导、清楚解释接触传播、使用隔离衣和手套，并进行回示。本情境中 MRSA 主要通过接触传播，因此重点是隔离衣、手套和手卫生，而不是外科口罩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a visitor makes an isolation error, choose teaching that preserves safe family involvement and verifies the behavior with return demonstration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"探视者出现隔离错误时，选择既能保留安全家庭参与、又能通过回示确认行为的教学措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1790,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,48],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: The charge nurse asks which identified breach posed the greatest cross-contamination risk to other clients on the unit. Which breach should the nurse identify as the priority?","fullStemZh":"阶段3：责任护士询问已发现的哪个漏洞对病区其他患者造成最大的交叉污染风险。护士应优先指出哪一项？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which breach should the nurse identify as the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先指出哪一项？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 3: The charge nurse asks which identified breach posed the greatest cross-contamination risk to other clients on the unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段3：责任护士询问已发现的哪个漏洞对病区其他患者造成最大的交叉污染风险。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q4_a","en":"The nursing student's contaminated bare-hand contact with the Room 12 door handle","zh":"护生用污染裸手触碰12房门把手"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"The standard linen bag used for Client A's soiled linens","zh":"A 患者污染布草被放入普通布草袋"},{"id":"q4_d","en":"Client B's wife stopping at the open doorway of Room 12 to ask a question","zh":"B 患者妻子停在12房开着的门口询问问题"},{"id":"q4_c","en":"Client C's dedicated stethoscope placed on the clean-utility-room counter near the clean supply cart","zh":"C 患者专用听诊器被放在清洁用物间柜台上，靠近清洁物品车"}],"correct":["q4_c"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stethoscope breach has the widest and most direct cross-contamination pathway: a device from a draining MRSA contact-precautions room was placed in a clean supply area used for multiple clients. It could contaminate surfaces, supplies, and staff hands. The door handle and linen bagging errors are serious, but their exposure radius is more contained.","rationaleCorrectZh":"听诊器漏洞具有最广且最直接的交叉污染路径：来自 MRSA 引流伤口接触隔离病房的设备被放到供多名患者使用的清洁物品区域，可能污染表面、物品和工作人员双手。门把手和布草装袋错误也严重，但暴露范围较有限。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritization in infection control is about scope and pathway: choose the breach that can spread organisms to the most clients through the most direct route.","testTakingStrategyZh":"感染控制优先级要看范围和传播路径：选择能通过最直接路径把病原体传播给最多患者的漏洞。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1791,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,58],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Client D has smear-positive pulmonary TB in a functioning AIIR. Her mother asks to take her outside in a wheelchair for fresh air. Which response is best?","fullStemZh":"阶段2：D 患者为痰涂片阳性肺结核，住在功能正常的 AIIR。母亲请求用轮椅带她到室外呼吸新鲜空气。哪项回应最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项回应最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her mother asks to take her outside in a wheelchair for fresh air.","penultimateSentenceZh":"母亲请求用轮椅带她到室外呼吸新鲜空气。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q5_c","en":"Tell the mother she does not need respiratory protection inside the AIIR because negative pressure protects everyone in the room.","zh":"告诉母亲在 AIIR 内不需要呼吸防护，因为负压会保护房内所有人。"},{"id":"q5_a","en":"Explain that a non-essential trip outside the AIIR is not permitted while AFB smears remain positive; offer in-room comfort alternatives and teach the mother to follow the facility airborne-precautions visitor policy, including instruction and offering of an N95 respirator.","zh":"解释 AFB 涂片仍阳性期间不得因非必要原因离开 AIIR；提供病房内舒适替代措施，并指导母亲遵循机构空气传播隔离探视政策，包括说明并提供 N95 呼吸防护口罩。"},{"id":"q5_e","en":"Delay answering until the provider makes rounds because nurses do not teach airborne-precautions restrictions.","zh":"等医务人员查房后再回答，因为护士不负责空气传播隔离限制的教育。"},{"id":"q5_b","en":"Allow a brief outdoor trip if the patient wears a surgical mask the entire time.","zh":"如果患者全程戴外科口罩，就允许短暂到室外。"},{"id":"q5_d","en":"Give the mother a surgical mask and explain that this reliably protects visitors from airborne TB while inside the room.","zh":"给母亲外科口罩，并解释这能在房内可靠保护探视者免受空气传播结核感染。"}],"correct":["q5_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient is still AFB smear-positive, and the case states the AIIR is functioning and precautions must continue. A non-essential outdoor trip would bypass the engineering control. A surgical mask on the patient is used only when medically necessary transport cannot be avoided; it is not a substitute for the AIIR. The nurse should respond compassionately, offer alternatives, and teach visitor respiratory-protection expectations under facility policy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者 AFB 涂片仍阳性，且病例说明 AIIR 功能正常、隔离需继续。非必要外出会绕过负压工程控制。患者外科口罩仅用于不可避免的医学必要转运，不能替代 AIIR。护士应以同理方式回应，提供替代措施，并按机构政策教育探视者呼吸防护要求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let a compassionate request override the isolation category. For airborne TB, ask whether the trip is medically necessary and whether the AIIR can be replaced by a mask; here, it cannot.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要让合情合理的请求凌驾于隔离类别之上。遇到空气传播结核，先问外出是否医学必要，以及口罩能否替代 AIIR；本题不能。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1792,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.346.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,32],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: Which statements show an accurate evaluation of whether the infection-control interventions were effective? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段3：哪些陈述能准确评价感染控制干预是否有效？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 3: Which statements show an accurate evaluation of whether the infection-control interventions were effective?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段3：哪些陈述能准确评价感染控制干预是否有效？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q6_a","en":"Client C's daughter demonstrating correct gown and glove donning and doffing supports that visitor teaching changed behavior.","zh":"C 患者女儿能正确回示隔离衣和手套的穿脱，支持探视者教学已改变行为。"},{"id":"q6_f","en":"The student's isolation-room errors require follow-up education and supervised return demonstration before independent isolation-room contact.","zh":"护生在隔离病房的错误需要后续教育，并在独立接触隔离患者前接受监督下回示。"},{"id":"q6_e","en":"Client D's continued AFB smear positivity means airborne precautions and AIIR confinement remain necessary; the outdoor trip remains inappropriate.","zh":"D 患者 AFB 涂片仍阳性，表示仍需空气传播隔离和 AIIR，室外活动仍不合适。"},{"id":"q6_d","en":"Client A's potassium correction to 3.6 mEq/L means CDI contact precautions can be discontinued.","zh":"A 患者血钾纠正到 3.6 mEq/L 表示可以停止 CDI 接触隔离。"},{"id":"q6_c","en":"Retrieving the stethoscope, disinfecting contacted clean-utility surfaces, handling nearby supplies per policy, and completing wet-contact disinfection before return supports containment of the environmental breach.","zh":"取回听诊器、消毒其接触过的清洁用物间表面、按制度处理附近物品，并完成湿接触消毒后再送回，支持环境污染漏洞已被控制。"},{"id":"q6_b","en":"Because no new infections were diagnosed by the end of the shift, all interventions can be declared fully effective.","zh":"因为班末没有诊断出新感染，所以可宣布所有干预完全有效。"}],"correct":["q6_a","q6_c","q6_e","q6_f"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective infection-control evaluation during the same shift relies on process indicators: observed PPE compliance, return demonstration, correction of environmental contamination, and recognition of ongoing isolation needs. A same-day absence of new infections is not proof of effectiveness, and lab correction does not end CDI precautions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"同一班次内评价感染控制效果主要依赖过程指标：观察到的 PPE 依从性、回示、环境污染纠正，以及识别仍需隔离的风险。当天没有新感染并不能证明完全有效，电解质纠正也不代表可停止 CDI 隔离。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluation questions often mix outcomes and process measures. In short time frames, prioritize observable compliance and corrected hazards over infection rates that require longer surveillance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价类题常混合结局指标和过程指标。在短时间内，优先看可观察到的依从性和已纠正的危险，而不是需要更长监测期的感染率。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1793,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.347","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.347.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.347.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[380,454],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,135],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2 synthesis: The contaminated stethoscope from Client C's MRSA contact-precautions room has been found in the clean utility room near the clean supply cart. The student also contaminated the Room 12 door handle after CDI care, Client A's soiled linens were placed in a standard linen bag, and Client D's mother has asked to remove a smear-positive TB patient from the AIIR. Complete the bow-tie diagram for the priority cross-contamination problem.","fullStemZh":"阶段2综合：来自 C 患者 MRSA 接触隔离病房的污染听诊器被发现放在清洁用物间、靠近清洁物品车。护生在 CDI 照护后也污染了12房门把手，A 患者污染布草被放入普通布草袋，D 患者母亲请求让痰涂片阳性肺结核患者离开 AIIR。请完成针对优先交叉污染问题的蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram for the priority cross-contamination problem.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成针对优先交叉污染问题的蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The student also contaminated the Room 12 door handle after CDI care, Client A's soiled linens were placed in a standard linen bag, and Client D's mother has asked to remove a smear-positive TB patient from the AIIR.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护生在 CDI 照护后也污染了12房门把手，A 患者污染布草被放入普通布草袋，D 患者母亲请求让痰涂片阳性肺结核患者离开 AIIR。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely priority problem","zh":"最可能的优先问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_mrsa_stethoscope","en":"Active cross-contamination risk from a contaminated MRSA dedicated device in the clean utility room","zh":"污染的 MRSA 专用设备进入清洁用物间造成的主动交叉污染风险"},{"id":"bt_cond_linen_error","en":"CDI soiled-linen bagging error in Room 12","zh":"12房 CDI 污染布草装袋错误"},{"id":"bt_cond_cdi_door_handle","en":"CDI door-handle contamination from the student's bare-hand contact","zh":"护生裸手接触造成的 CDI 门把手污染"}],"correct":"bt_cond_mrsa_stethoscope"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_act_scope_too_narrow","en":"Disinfect only the stethoscope and return it to Room 16 without cleaning the counter or assessing nearby supplies.","zh":"只消毒听诊器并送回16房，不清洁柜台，也不评估附近物品。"},{"id":"bt_act_wait_until_end_shift","en":"Wait until the end of the shift to address the stethoscope because the wound dressing change is due.","zh":"因伤口敷料到更换时间，等到班末再处理听诊器。"},{"id":"bt_act_notify_educate_log","en":"Provide immediate corrective education to the staff member involved and notify the charge nurse so the breach is documented for infection-control follow-up.","zh":"立即教育相关工作人员，并通知责任护士记录该漏洞以便感染控制后续追踪。"},{"id":"bt_act_remove_disinfect_area","en":"Remove the stethoscope, disinfect contacted clean-utility surfaces, assess or remove nearby supplies per policy, disinfect the stethoscope with full wet-contact time, and return it to Room 16.","zh":"取走听诊器，消毒其接触过的清洁用物间表面，按制度评估或移除附近物品，完成听诊器全程湿接触消毒后送回16房。"}],"correct":["bt_act_remove_disinfect_area","bt_act_notify_educate_log"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_param_vanco_monitoring","en":"Client C's vancomycin monitoring results","zh":"C 患者万古霉素监测结果"},{"id":"bt_param_ppe_compliance","en":"Visitor and staff PPE compliance on subsequent room entries","zh":"后续进入病房时探视者和工作人员 PPE 依从性"},{"id":"bt_param_equipment_location_cleanliness","en":"Equipment location and cleanliness at each room entry","zh":"每次进入病房时设备位置和清洁状态"},{"id":"bt_param_client_b_sputum","en":"Client B's Streptococcus pneumoniae sputum culture result","zh":"B 患者肺炎链球菌痰培养结果"}],"correct":["bt_param_ppe_compliance","bt_param_equipment_location_cleanliness"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority problem is the contaminated MRSA stethoscope in the clean utility room because it creates a direct fomite pathway from an isolation room into a shared supply area. The nurse must contain the environmental exposure immediately, correct the staff practice, and monitor for sustained compliance and equipment control. Client B's culture and Client C's vancomycin monitoring matter clinically, but they do not measure containment of this cross-contamination breach.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先问题是污染的 MRSA 听诊器进入清洁用物间，因为它把隔离病房污染物直接带入共享清洁供应区域，形成污染媒介传播路径。护士必须立即控制环境暴露，纠正工作人员做法，并监测持续依从性和设备管理。B 患者培养和 C 患者万古霉素监测虽有临床意义，但不能衡量该交叉污染漏洞是否被控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, match the priority condition to the actions and monitoring. The correct chain should address the same hazard from recognition through containment and follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，把优先问题与措施和监测配对。正确链条应从识别、控制到后续追踪都针对同一危险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1794,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.348","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.348.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[160,338],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,101],"fullStemEn":"Home safety risks and anticipatory guidance at a nine-month-old well-child visit Liam is a nine-month-old infant at a first visit with this pediatric practice. He is growing and developing appropriately, but the nurse identifies multiple home-safety and medication-safety teaching needs during history, direct observation, and teach-back.","fullStemZh":"9 个月婴儿保健访视中的居家安全风险与预期性指导 Liam 是一名 9 个月婴儿，这是他第一次到该儿科诊所就诊。他生长发育适当，但护士在询问病史、直接观察和回授过程中发现多项居家安全与用药安全教育需求。","terminalSentenceEn":"He is growing and developing appropriately, but the nurse identifies multiple home-safety and medication-safety teaching needs during history, direct observation, and teach-back.","terminalSentenceZh":"他生长发育适当，但护士在询问病史、直接观察和回授过程中发现多项居家安全与用药安全教育需求。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Home safety risks and anticipatory guidance at a nine-month-old well-child visit Liam is a nine-month-old infant at a first visit with this pediatric practice.","penultimateSentenceZh":"9 个月婴儿保健访视中的居家安全风险与预期性指导 Liam 是一名 9 个月婴儿，这是他第一次到该儿科诊所就诊。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on recognizing a cluster of infant home-safety risks, interpreting them as a caregiver knowledge deficit rather than automatic neglect, prioritizing the immediate medication hazard, teaching in a strengths-based and staged way, correcting a potentially dangerous acetaminophen dosing practice, and evaluating teach-back for both retained knowledge and remaining gaps. The nurse must protect Liam immediately while preserving Danielle's engagement and linking the family to ongoing supports.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例重点是识别一组婴儿居家安全风险；将其判断为照护者知识缺乏，而非自动认定为忽视；优先处理眼前药物危险；以基于优势、分层次的方式教学；纠正可能危险的对乙酰氨基酚给药做法；并通过回授评价哪些知识已掌握、哪些仍有缺口。护士必须立即保护 Liam，同时维持 Danielle 的参与度，并把家庭连接到持续支持资源。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding pediatric safety cases, follow the nursing-process arc: recognize the hazards, analyze whether the pattern is knowledge deficit or maltreatment, remove immediate danger, teach by priority, and evaluate teach-back for specific gaps.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理展开式儿科安全病例时，按护理程序思考：识别危险，分析模式是知识缺乏还是虐待/忽视，移除即时危险，按优先级教学，并通过回授评价具体缺口。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1795,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,45],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the Stage 1 findings that require nursing safety follow-up. Do not highlight normal caregiver or developmental findings.","fullStemZh":"请标出第 1 阶段中需要护士进行安全随访/干预的发现。不要标出正常的照护者行为或发育表现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not highlight normal caregiver or developmental findings.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要标出正常的照护者行为或发育表现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the Stage 1 findings that require nursing safety follow-up.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请标出第 1 阶段中需要护士进行安全随访/干预的发现。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h_carkeys","selectable":true,"en":"Liam is chewing on car keys with a small decorative charm about 1.5 cm in diameter.","zh":"Liam 正在咬一串钥匙，钥匙环上有一个约 1.5 cm 的小装饰物。"},{"id":"h_milk_cereal","selectable":true,"en":"The diaper bag contains a propped bottle of whole cow's milk mixed with cereal.","zh":"尿布包里有一瓶支起来喂的全脂牛奶，并混有婴儿米粉。"},{"id":"h_popcorn","selectable":true,"en":"An open ziplock bag of popcorn is visible in the diaper bag.","zh":"尿布包里可以看到一袋已经打开的爆米花。"},{"id":"h_cosmetics","selectable":true,"en":"A small unlocked cosmetics pouch is accessible at the top of the diaper bag.","zh":"尿布包最上面有一个未上锁的小化妆包，婴儿可以够到。"},{"id":"h_forward_car_seat","selectable":true,"en":"Danielle recently turned Liam's rear-facing infant car seat forward-facing because he screams when he cannot see her.","zh":"Danielle 因为 Liam 看不到她时会哭闹，最近把本应后向安装的婴儿安全座椅改成了前向。"},{"id":"h_bedshare","selectable":true,"en":"Danielle says Liam sleeps in her bed because he will not stay in the crib.","zh":"Danielle 说 Liam 睡在她的床上，因为他不愿意待在婴儿床里。"},{"id":"h_stairs","selectable":true,"en":"The apartment has an open staircase and no baby gate because Danielle thinks Liam has not figured out the stairs yet.","zh":"公寓里有开放式楼梯，但没有安装婴儿安全门，因为 Danielle 认为 Liam 还不会爬楼梯。"},{"id":"h_cleaners","selectable":true,"en":"Cleaning supplies are kept under the kitchen sink without a cabinet lock.","zh":"清洁用品放在厨房水槽下方，柜门没有安全锁。"},{"id":"h_hotdogs_grapes","selectable":true,"en":"Danielle offers Liam small pieces of hot dog and grapes as finger foods.","zh":"Danielle 会给 Liam 吃小块热狗和葡萄作为手抓食物。"},{"id":"h_diphenhydramine","selectable":true,"en":"Danielle asks whether she can give diphenhydramine at night so Liam will sleep through.","zh":"Danielle 询问是否可以晚上给 Liam 服用苯海拉明，让他一觉睡到天亮。"},{"id":"h_warmth","selectable":true,"en":"Danielle makes eye contact, responds to Liam's vocalizations, and repositions him when he squirms.","zh":"Danielle 与 Liam 有眼神交流，会回应他的发声，并在他扭动时调整他的姿势。"},{"id":"h_questions","selectable":true,"en":"Danielle asks several questions and appears genuinely interested in doing the right thing.","zh":"Danielle 问了几个问题，并且看起来真心想把事情做对。"},{"id":"h_stranger_anxiety","selectable":true,"en":"Liam turns toward Danielle and fusses when the nurse reaches for him.","zh":"护士伸手接近 Liam 时，他转向 Danielle 并开始烦躁。"}],"correct":["h_carkeys","h_milk_cereal","h_popcorn","h_cosmetics","h_forward_car_seat","h_bedshare","h_stairs","h_cleaners","h_hotdogs_grapes","h_diphenhydramine"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The safety-relevant cues are the mouthing hazard, unsafe feeding practices, choking hazards, forward-facing car seat, bed-sharing, fall risk, poisoning risks, and proposed diphenhydramine use. Danielle's warmth, questions, and Liam's stranger anxiety are reassuring or developmentally expected and should not be treated as red flags.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与安全相关的线索包括可被放入口中的小物件、不安全喂养、窒息风险、过早前向安全座椅、同床睡眠、跌落风险、中毒风险以及拟使用苯海拉明助眠。Danielle 的温暖互动、主动提问以及 Liam 的陌生人焦虑属于令人放心或符合发育预期的表现，不应被当作危险信号。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In pediatric safety questions, pair the child's developmental ability with the object or practice. A mobile, mouthing infant turns small objects, unlocked products, stairs, and unsafe foods into high-priority safety cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做儿科安全题时，把儿童的发育能力与物品或照护做法配对思考。会移动、爱把东西放入口中的婴儿，会让小物件、未上锁物品、楼梯和不安全食物变成高优先级安全线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1796,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"Which interpretation best explains the Stage 1 pattern of unsafe infant-care practices?","fullStemZh":"哪一种判断最能解释第 1 阶段出现的一系列不安全婴儿照护做法？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation best explains the Stage 1 pattern of unsafe infant-care practices?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一种判断最能解释第 1 阶段出现的一系列不安全婴儿照护做法？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"knowledge_deficit","en":"Caregiver knowledge deficit with reliance on informal advice","zh":"照护者知识缺乏，并依赖非正式建议"},{"id":"intentional_neglect","en":"Intentional neglect requiring an immediate protective-services report based only on these facts","zh":"仅凭目前事实即可认定为故意忽视并需立即报告儿童保护机构"},{"id":"developmental_delay","en":"Infant developmental delay causing caregiver stress","zh":"婴儿发育迟缓导致照护者压力"},{"id":"willful_disregard","en":"Willful disregard because Danielle already knows the practices are dangerous","zh":"明知危险仍故意无视，因为 Danielle 已经知道这些做法有害"}],"correct":["knowledge_deficit"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pattern is most consistent with a knowledge deficit. Danielle relies on a neighbor, partner, and online videos, has no consistent pediatric medical home, openly discloses practices, asks questions, and shows affectionate engagement with Liam. The risks still require documentation, teaching, and follow-up, but the evidence does not support labeling the situation as intentional neglect based on the current facts alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这一模式最符合知识缺乏。Danielle 依赖邻居、伴侣和网络视频，没有稳定的儿科医疗之家，能坦诚说出做法，主动提问，并与 Liam 有亲密、积极的互动。风险仍需要记录、教育和随访，但仅凭当前事实不能认定为故意忽视。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish risk from intent. A child can be in danger because of a knowledge gap, but the nursing response differs from a situation with concealment, refusal, injury, or malicious intent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“存在风险”和“有意伤害”。儿童可能因照护者知识缺乏而处于危险中，但这与隐瞒、拒绝、伤害或恶意情境下的护理应对不同。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1797,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,58],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, Liam is actively pulling out the cosmetics pouch that contains an uncapped bottle of infant acetaminophen. Which risk requires the nurse's immediate intervention right now?","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段，Liam 正在把化妆包拉出来，里面有一瓶未盖好瓶盖的婴儿对乙酰氨基酚。此刻哪一项风险需要护士立即干预？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which risk requires the nurse's immediate intervention right now?","terminalSentenceZh":"此刻哪一项风险需要护士立即干预？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, Liam is actively pulling out the cosmetics pouch that contains an uncapped bottle of infant acetaminophen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段，Liam 正在把化妆包拉出来，里面有一瓶未盖好瓶盖的婴儿对乙酰氨基酚。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"acetaminophen_reach","en":"Remove the accessible pouch containing uncapped acetaminophen from Liam's reach.","zh":"立即把 Liam 能够到、内有未盖好对乙酰氨基酚的化妆包移开。"},{"id":"partner_first","en":"Call protective services immediately because the partner suggested diphenhydramine.","zh":"因伴侣建议使用苯海拉明，立即联系儿童保护机构。"},{"id":"sleep_first","en":"Focus first on stopping bed-sharing because safe sleep is a well-child priority.","zh":"先重点纠正同床睡眠，因为安全睡眠是儿童保健重点。"},{"id":"milk_first","en":"Address whole cow's milk before 12 months before moving objects in the room.","zh":"先处理 12 个月前使用全脂牛奶的问题，再移动房间内物品。"},{"id":"carseat_first","en":"Teach rear-facing car seat use first because vehicle crashes are a major cause of injury.","zh":"先教后向安全座椅使用，因为车祸是重要伤害原因。"}],"correct":["acetaminophen_reach"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The accessible, uncapped medication is the immediate danger in the room. The nurse should remove it from reach before teaching, then assess and address the reported dosing error. Car seat, sleep, nutrition, home safety, and partner-related concerns matter, but they are not as immediate as a medication Liam could ingest within seconds.","rationaleCorrectZh":"房间内最立即的危险是婴儿能够到且未盖好瓶盖的药物。护士应在教学前先将其移到婴儿够不到的地方，然后评估并处理已报告的给药剂量错误。安全座椅、睡眠、营养、居家安全和伴侣相关担忧都重要，但没有眼前可能数秒内发生的药物误服紧急。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several safety problems exist, first remove the hazard that can injure the child immediately and is already within reach.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当存在多个安全问题时，先处理已经在儿童够得到范围内、可立即造成伤害的危险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1798,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,42],"fullStemEn":"Which teaching approaches are appropriate for the nurse to use with Danielle at Stage 2? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段，护士对 Danielle 采用哪些教学方式是合适的？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which teaching approaches are appropriate for the nurse to use with Danielle at Stage 2?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段，护士对 Danielle 采用哪些教学方式是合适的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"resources_followup","en":"Connect the family with parenting support, safety-equipment resources, a medical home, and follow-up.","zh":"为家庭连接育儿支持、安全设备资源、稳定医疗之家和随访。"},{"id":"validate_strengths","en":"Acknowledge Danielle's distress and name her strengths before giving corrections.","zh":"在纠正问题前，先回应 Danielle 的难过情绪，并指出她的照护优势。"},{"id":"teachback","en":"Use demonstration, return demonstration, written instructions, and teach-back.","zh":"使用示范、回示范、书面说明和回授法。"},{"id":"avoid_topics","en":"Avoid discussing safety risks today because Danielle is tearful.","zh":"因为 Danielle 正在哭泣，今天避免讨论安全风险。"},{"id":"prioritize_risks","en":"Prioritize teaching by severity, starting with medication safety and choking hazards.","zh":"按风险严重程度安排教学，从用药安全和窒息风险开始。"},{"id":"rapid_lecture","en":"Correct every unsafe practice rapidly in one directive lecture so no topic is missed.","zh":"用一次快速、命令式讲解纠正所有不安全做法，确保不遗漏任何主题。"}],"correct":["validate_strengths","prioritize_risks","teachback","resources_followup"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Danielle is emotionally overwhelmed but engaged. The nurse should use strengths-based, nonjudgmental teaching; prioritize the highest-severity risks; use demonstration and teach-back; and connect her with ongoing supports. A rapid lecture can overwhelm her, while avoiding safety teaching leaves Liam at risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Danielle 情绪上被压垮，但仍积极参与。护士应采用基于优势、非评判的教学；按严重程度优先处理高风险问题；使用示范和回授法；并为她连接持续支持。快速灌输式讲解可能让她更难吸收，而回避安全教学会让 Liam 继续处于风险中。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Health teaching is both relational and prioritized. The safest answer usually supports the learner emotionally while still addressing the highest-risk behavior today.","testTakingStrategyZh":"健康教育既要建立关系，也要分清优先级。最安全的答案通常会在情绪上支持学习者，同时当天处理最高风险行为。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1799,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,264],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,115],"fullStemEn":"Danielle reports giving Liam about 1 tablespoon (15 mL) of 160 mg/5 mL acetaminophen when he has a fever. The clinic/package table in the record lists 5 mL for Liam's weight band. Which actions should the nurse take before the family leaves? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"Danielle 报告 Liam 发热时会给约 1 汤匙（15 mL）的 160 mg/5 mL 对乙酰氨基酚。病历中的诊所/包装剂量表列明 Liam 体重范围的剂量为 5 mL。家属离开前，护士应采取哪些措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take before the family leaves?","penultimateSentenceZh":"家属离开前，护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"storage_cap","en":"Teach Danielle to replace the child-resistant cap and store the medication out of sight and reach.","zh":"教 Danielle 盖回儿童安全瓶盖，并把药物放在看不见、够不到的位置。"},{"id":"notify_if_exposure","en":"Notify the provider and contact Poison Control as directed if recent or repeated overdosing is reported.","zh":"若报告近期或反复过量给药，应通知医护提供者并按指示联系 Poison Control。"},{"id":"ask_frequency_recency","en":"Ask how often the tablespoon dose has been given and when the last dose occurred.","zh":"询问这次“汤匙剂量”给过多少次/多久一次，以及最后一次给药时间。"},{"id":"appearance_reassurance","en":"Reassure Danielle that no follow-up is needed because Liam looks well today.","zh":"安慰 Danielle 说 Liam 今天看起来很好，因此不需要任何后续处理。"},{"id":"syringe_demo","en":"Demonstrate the ordered/package dose using the medication syringe and have Danielle return-demonstrate.","zh":"用配套给药注射器示范医嘱/包装标示剂量，并请 Danielle 回示范。"},{"id":"serum_labs_by_provider","en":"Prepare for a serum acetaminophen level and hepatic function labs if the provider or Poison Control indicates they are needed.","zh":"若医护提供者或 Poison Control 认为需要，应准备采集血清对乙酰氨基酚水平和肝功能检查。"}],"correct":["ask_frequency_recency","notify_if_exposure","serum_labs_by_provider","syringe_demo","storage_cap"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must assess the exposure history, escalate if the dose was recent or repeated, prepare for labs if directed, correct measurement using the syringe and return demonstration, and ensure safe storage. A well-appearing infant can still require evaluation because acetaminophen toxicity may not be clinically obvious early.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士必须评估暴露史；若近期或反复过量，应升级处理；若被指示则准备相关化验；用注射器和回示范纠正剂量测量；并确保安全存放。即使婴儿外观看起来良好，也可能需要评估，因为对乙酰氨基酚中毒早期可能没有明显临床表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pediatric medication errors, do not stop at education. First quantify exposure, then escalate when toxicity is possible, then correct the caregiver's measurement technique.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到儿科用药错误时，不要只做教育。先量化暴露情况；若可能中毒则升级处理；之后再纠正照护者的量药方法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1800,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.348.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,42],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Classify each Stage 3 teach-back response.","fullStemZh":"请对第 3 阶段每项回授回答进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each Stage 3 teach-back response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对第 3 阶段每项回授回答进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"selectionMode":"single_per_row","columns":[{"id":"adequate","en":"Adequate understanding","zh":"理解充分"},{"id":"barrier","en":"Knowledge present; problem-solve resource barrier","zh":"已理解；需解决资源障碍"},{"id":"reteach","en":"Needs immediate re-teaching","zh":"需要立即再教育"}],"rows":[{"id":"rear_facing","en":"States Liam should remain rear-facing until he reaches the rear-facing height or weight limit of the specific seat.","zh":"说出 Liam 应继续后向乘坐，直到达到该安全座椅后向模式的身高或体重上限。"},{"id":"safe_sleep","en":"States Liam should sleep alone on his back in a crib without loose bedding.","zh":"说出 Liam 应独自仰卧睡在婴儿床中，且无松散床上用品。"},{"id":"no_diphenhydramine","en":"States she should not give diphenhydramine to make Liam sleep.","zh":"说出不应给 Liam 使用苯海拉明来帮助睡眠。"},{"id":"acetaminophen_5ml","en":"States she will use the syringe and give the clinic/package dose of 5 mL.","zh":"说出会使用注射器，并给诊所/包装标示的 5 mL 剂量。"},{"id":"hotdog_circles","en":"Says she will cut hot dogs into small circles and does not mention grapes.","zh":"说会把热狗切成小圆片，且没有提到葡萄。"},{"id":"poison_911","en":"Says she will call 911 for any ingestion but does not mention Poison Control.","zh":"说任何误服都会拨打 911，但没有提到 Poison Control。"},{"id":"try_gates","en":"Says she will try to get gates and cabinet locks this weekend.","zh":"说会尽量在周末买到安全门和柜锁。"}]},"correct":[{"rowId":"rear_facing","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"safe_sleep","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"no_diphenhydramine","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"acetaminophen_5ml","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"hotdog_circles","columnIds":["reteach"]},{"rowId":"poison_911","columnIds":["reteach"]},{"rowId":"try_gates","columnIds":["barrier"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Danielle accurately restates rear-facing car seat use, safe sleep, avoiding diphenhydramine for sleep, and the stated acetaminophen dose. Hot dogs cut into circles and unmentioned grapes require immediate re-teaching because the round/cylindrical shape remains dangerous. Calling 911 for every ingestion is incomplete; Poison Control should be used for a conscious, breathing child, while 911 is for severe symptoms such as unresponsiveness, breathing trouble, or seizure. Her wording about gates and locks suggests a resource/access barrier, not failure to understand the need.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Danielle 能准确复述后向安全座椅、安全睡眠、不用苯海拉明助眠，以及病例所列对乙酰氨基酚剂量。把热狗切成圆片且未提葡萄需要立即再教育，因为圆形/圆柱形仍有危险。任何误服都打 911 的说法不完整；对清醒、能呼吸的儿童应联系 Poison Control，911 用于无反应、呼吸困难或抽搐等严重情况。她关于安全门和柜锁的表述提示资源/获得途径障碍，而不是不知道需要这些设备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In evaluation questions, separate wrong understanding from implementation barriers. Re-teach incorrect content; problem-solve when the caregiver knows what to do but may lack access.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做评价类题时，要区分“理解错误”和“执行障碍”。内容错误要再教育；照护者知道该做什么但可能缺资源时，要协助解决障碍。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1801,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_nine_month_well_child_safety_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.349","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.349.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.349.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[393,514],"terminalOffsetsZh":[172,207],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2 of a nine-month well-child visit, the nurse has identified multiple infant safety hazards. Liam is reaching for a cosmetics pouch containing uncapped acetaminophen. Danielle is warm and engaged but tearful, lacks support, relies on informal advice, and reports giving 15 mL of 160 mg/5 mL acetaminophen when the clinic/package table in the record lists 5 mL for Liam's weight band. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"在一名 9 个月婴儿保健访视的第 2 阶段，护士发现多项婴儿安全危险。Liam 正伸手够一个化妆包，里面有未盖好瓶盖的对乙酰氨基酚。Danielle 温暖且愿意参与，但情绪难过、缺乏支持、依赖非正式建议，并报告在病历中的诊所/包装剂量表列明 Liam 体重范围为 5 mL 的情况下，曾给 15 mL 的 160 mg/5 mL 对乙酰氨基酚。请完成弓形题：选择最可能的状况、两项优先护理措施和两项需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题：选择最可能的状况、两项优先护理措施和两项需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Danielle is warm and engaged but tearful, lacks support, relies on informal advice, and reports giving 15 mL of 160 mg/5 mL acetaminophen when the clinic/package table in the record lists 5 mL for Liam's weight band.","penultimateSentenceZh":"Danielle 温暖且愿意参与，但情绪难过、缺乏支持、依赖非正式建议，并报告在病历中的诊所/包装剂量表列明 Liam 体重范围为 5 mL 的情况下，曾给 15 mL 的 160 mg/5 mL 对乙酰氨基酚。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_ipv","en":"Intimate partner violence or coercive control as the proven driver","zh":"亲密伴侣暴力或控制行为已被证实是驱动因素"},{"id":"cond_knowledge_deficit","en":"Caregiver knowledge deficit with multiple home hazards and acetaminophen dosing error","zh":"照护者知识缺乏，伴多项居家危险和对乙酰氨基酚给药错误"},{"id":"cond_neglect","en":"Child neglect as the primary explanation","zh":"儿童忽视是主要解释"}],"correct":"cond_knowledge_deficit"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_teach_apap_remove_hazards","en":"Teach the stated syringe dose with return demonstration and remove immediate choking/poisoning hazards from Liam's reach","zh":"用回示范教学病例所列注射器剂量，并移除 Liam 够得到的即时窒息/中毒危险"},{"id":"act_defer_teaching","en":"Defer acetaminophen correction to the one-month follow-up to avoid overwhelming Danielle","zh":"为避免 Danielle 负担过重，将对乙酰氨基酚纠正推迟到 1 个月随访"},{"id":"act_cps_now","en":"File a protective-services report based on the unsafe practices alone","zh":"仅根据不安全做法就提交儿童保护报告"},{"id":"act_assess_apap","en":"Assess acetaminophen frequency, recency, and total exposure; escalate to provider/Poison Control if recent or repeated overdosing is reported","zh":"评估对乙酰氨基酚给药频率、最后一次时间和总暴露量；若近期或反复过量则升级给医护提供者/Poison Control"}],"correct":["act_assess_apap","act_teach_apap_remove_hazards"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_growth_hgb","en":"Liam's growth trajectory and hemoglobin after dietary correction","zh":"饮食纠正后 Liam 的生长趋势和血红蛋白"},{"id":"param_teachback","en":"Danielle's follow-up teach-back of dosing, safe food preparation, safe sleep, and car-seat use","zh":"Danielle 随访时对剂量、安全食物处理、安全睡眠和安全座椅使用的回授"},{"id":"param_lead","en":"Lead level trend as the main evaluation of this safety plan","zh":"将血铅趋势作为该安全计划的主要评价指标"},{"id":"param_asq","en":"ASQ-3 developmental score as the main evaluation of hazard correction","zh":"将 ASQ-3 发育评分作为危险纠正的主要评价指标"}],"correct":["param_teachback","param_growth_hgb"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The best synthesis is caregiver knowledge deficit with multiple hazards and an active medication-safety error. Danielle's warmth, voluntary disclosure, engagement, lack of prior guidance, and absence of injury support education and resource connection rather than an automatic neglect label. Priority actions focus on assessing acetaminophen exposure/escalating if needed and correcting the dose while removing immediate hazards. Follow-up evaluation should monitor retained safety teaching and nutritional/growth effects of the prior feeding pattern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最佳综合判断是照护者知识缺乏，伴多项危险和当前用药安全错误。Danielle 的温暖互动、主动披露、参与度、缺乏既往指导以及无伤害表现，支持教育和资源连接，而不是自动贴上忽视标签。优先措施是评估对乙酰氨基酚暴露并在需要时升级处理，同时纠正剂量并移除即时危险。随访评价应监测安全教学是否保留，以及既往喂养模式对营养/生长的影响。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, align the center condition with the whole pattern, not the scariest distractor. Then choose actions that address the active danger and parameters that evaluate whether the teaching changed behavior.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，中心状况要与整体模式一致，而不是选择最吓人的干扰项。之后选择能处理当前危险的措施，以及能评价教学是否改变行为的监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1802,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.350","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.350.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,289],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,95],"fullStemEn":"Opioid use disorder in early recovery: relapse risk, pain management, and safety planning after orthopedic injury A client with OUD in early recovery presents with an acute fracture, severe pain, anxiety about opioid exposure, and progressive emotional isolation during discharge planning.","fullStemZh":"早期恢复期阿片类物质使用障碍：骨科损伤后的复发风险、疼痛管理与安全计划 一名处于早期恢复期的 OUD 患者因急性骨折就诊，存在重度疼痛、对阿片暴露的焦虑，并在出院计划过程中逐渐出现情绪孤立。","terminalSentenceEn":"Opioid use disorder in early recovery: relapse risk, pain management, and safety planning after orthopedic injury A client with OUD in early recovery presents with an acute fracture, severe pain, anxiety about opioid exposure, and progressive emotional isolation during discharge planning.","terminalSentenceZh":"早期恢复期阿片类物质使用障碍：骨科损伤后的复发风险、疼痛管理与安全计划 一名处于早期恢复期的 OUD 患者因急性骨折就诊，存在重度疼痛、对阿片暴露的焦虑，并在出院计划过程中逐渐出现情绪孤立。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Across the case, the nurse must recognize that Marcus’s strongest risk is not withdrawal, drug seeking, or a single vital-sign abnormality, but acute relapse risk caused by converging physical pain, fear, shame, and self-isolation. Safe care preserves OUD treatment, treats pain with a supervised multimodal plan, protects confidentiality, uses nonjudgmental therapeutic communication, activates recovery supports before discharge, teaches naloxone and overdose response with Tanya when Marcus consents, and evaluates readiness by whether supports and follow-up are actually in place.","rationaleCorrectZh":"整个病例中，护士必须识别 Marcus 最大的风险不是戒断、觅药或单一生命体征异常，而是由身体疼痛、恐惧、羞耻和自我孤立共同导致的急性复发风险。安全护理应维持 OUD 治疗，在监督下使用多模式疼痛方案，保护保密性，采用非评判性治疗沟通，在出院前启动恢复支持，并在 Marcus 同意时与 Tanya 进行纳洛酮和过量应对宣教，同时通过支持和随访是否真正落实来评估出院准备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding OUD cases, avoid stigmatizing shortcuts. Follow the changing cue pattern: pain control, support connection, safety reassessment, confidentiality, and harm-reduction readiness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理 OUD 展开病例时，避免污名化捷径。跟随线索变化：疼痛控制、支持连接、安全重新评估、保密性和减害准备。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1803,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,33],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the Stage 1 findings that are significant psychosocial relapse-risk cues requiring nursing attention.","fullStemZh":"请标出阶段 1 中提示心理社会性复发风险、需要护士关注的重要线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the Stage 1 findings that are significant psychosocial relapse-risk cues requiring nursing attention.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出阶段 1 中提示心理社会性复发风险、需要护士关注的重要线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h1","selectable":true,"en":"Marcus says, “Sometimes I think it would be easier if I just didn’t have to deal with any of this anymore.”","zh":"Marcus 说：“有时候我觉得如果不用再面对这些，会不会更容易。”"},{"id":"h2","selectable":true,"en":"He clarifies, “I’m not going to hurt myself.”","zh":"他澄清：“我不会伤害自己。”"},{"id":"h3","selectable":true,"en":"He says recovery is exhausting and he feels “one bad day away from using again.”","zh":"他说恢复很累，并觉得自己“离再次使用只差一个糟糕的一天”。"},{"id":"h4","selectable":true,"en":"Pain is 6/10 after ketorolac and acetaminophen.","zh":"使用酮咯酸和对乙酰氨基酚后疼痛为 6/10。"},{"id":"h5","selectable":true,"en":"HR and BP improved to HR 94 and BP 138/86.","zh":"HR 和 BP 改善至 HR 94、BP 138/86。"},{"id":"h6","selectable":true,"en":"He is tearful, fidgeting, and emotionally distressed.","zh":"他流泪、坐立不安，并表现出情绪痛苦。"},{"id":"h7","selectable":true,"en":"He has not contacted Tanya or his sponsor.","zh":"他尚未联系 Tanya 或赞助人。"},{"id":"h8","selectable":true,"en":"He says he does not want to “bother” his support people.","zh":"他说不想“麻烦”支持他的人。"},{"id":"h9","selectable":true,"en":"He fears any fentanyl or opioid exposure will put him “right back where I started.”","zh":"他担心任何芬太尼或阿片暴露都会让他“马上回到起点”。"},{"id":"h10","selectable":true,"en":"Urine drug screen is positive for prescribed buprenorphine and negative for illicit substances.","zh":"尿药筛查为处方丁丙诺啡阳性，非法物质阴性。"}],"correct":["h1","h3","h6","h7","h8","h9"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The significant cues are the ambiguous “easier if I did not have to deal with this” statement, catastrophic relapse framing, tearful emotional distress, avoidance of Tanya and the sponsor, framing support contact as “bothering” others, and fear that opioid exposure will trigger relapse. The denial of self-harm is important but does not erase the need to monitor; improved vital signs, moderate pain, and a negative illicit UDS are not the primary psychosocial cues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重要线索包括“如果不用面对这些会不会更容易”的含糊表述、灾难化的复发表述、流泪和情绪痛苦、回避 Tanya 和赞助人、把联系支持者说成“麻烦别人”，以及担心阿片暴露会诱发复发。否认自伤很重要，但不能取消继续监测的需要；生命体征改善、中等疼痛和非法物质尿筛阴性不是主要心理社会线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cue recognition, separate expected physiologic responses from behavior changes that show loss of coping or loss of support.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别线索时，要区分预期的生理反应与显示应对能力或支持系统减弱的行为变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1804,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,24],"fullStemEn":"The nurse analyzes the Stage 1 cue cluster. Which interpretation is most accurate?","fullStemZh":"护士分析阶段 1 的线索组合。哪一种解释最准确？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation is most accurate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一种解释最准确？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse analyzes the Stage 1 cue cluster.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士分析阶段 1 的线索组合。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"e","en":"Primary cardiovascular instability from persistent hypertension and tachycardia","zh":"持续高血压和心动过速导致的主要心血管不稳定"},{"id":"c","en":"Drug-seeking behavior because he is asking many questions about sedation","zh":"因反复询问镇静方案而属于觅药行为"},{"id":"b","en":"Active opioid withdrawal requiring withdrawal-protocol medication","zh":"需要戒断方案药物处理的活动性阿片戒断"},{"id":"d","en":"Acute suicidal crisis requiring involuntary safety hold based only on the first statement","zh":"仅凭最初表述即可判定需要非自愿安全留观的急性自杀危机"},{"id":"a","en":"Acute relapse risk from converging pain, fear, shame, and self-isolation","zh":"疼痛、恐惧、羞耻和自我孤立共同导致的急性复发风险"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The cluster best represents acute relapse risk: early recovery, prior relapse and overdose, acute fracture pain, fear of opioid exposure, emotional distress, and withdrawal from supports. There are no objective withdrawal signs; his anxiety is about avoiding opioids rather than obtaining them. He denied suicidal intent and plan, so the nurse monitors and reassesses rather than jumping to an involuntary hold.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该线索组合最符合急性复发风险：早期恢复、既往复发和过量、急性骨折疼痛、害怕阿片暴露、情绪痛苦以及远离支持系统。没有客观戒断体征；他的焦虑是为了避免阿片，而不是索取阿片。他否认自杀意图和计划，因此护士应监测并重新评估，而不是直接做非自愿留观。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several labels seem possible, match the label to objective findings and the patient’s behavior, not to stigma attached to the diagnosis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个标签看似可能时，应将标签与客观发现和患者行为匹配，而不是与诊断相关的污名匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1805,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,54],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which concern should the nurse prioritize?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2，护士应优先处理哪一项问题？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which concern should the nurse prioritize?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 2，护士应优先处理哪一项问题？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"d","en":"Call the MAT prescriber immediately because the buprenorphine plan has not been addressed.","zh":"立即联系 MAT 处方医生，因为丁丙诺啡方案尚未处理。"},{"id":"a","en":"Focus on Marcus’s escalating hopelessness, emotional distress, and isolation using a therapeutic interaction and safety reassessment.","zh":"通过治疗性沟通和安全重新评估，优先处理 Marcus 日益加重的无望感、情绪痛苦和孤立。"},{"id":"e","en":"Repeat the urine drug screen before speaking with Marcus to verify whether Tanya’s concern is true.","zh":"在与 Marcus 谈话前重复尿药筛查，以核实 Tanya 的担忧是否属实。"},{"id":"c","en":"Complete medication discharge teaching first because pain control is the concrete discharge task.","zh":"先完成出院用药宣教，因为疼痛控制是具体的出院任务。"},{"id":"b","en":"Answer Tanya’s hallway question directly because she is frightened and has overdose history context.","zh":"直接回答 Tanya 在走廊的问题，因为她害怕且了解过量史。"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Marcus has shifted from anxious but engaged to hopeless, ashamed, and isolated. That trajectory is the most immediate destabilizing concern because it can precede relapse or self-harm. Tanya’s fear should be validated without violating confidentiality, and she can be included in planning with Marcus’s consent. Medication teaching remains important, but teaching will be poorly retained if the patient is in emotional crisis. The MAT plan has already been clarified.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Marcus 已从焦虑但能参与，转变为无望、羞耻和孤立。这一变化轨迹是最需要立即处理的不稳定因素，因为它可能先于复发或自伤。应支持性地认可 Tanya 的恐惧，但不能违反保密；经 Marcus 同意后可让她参与计划。用药宣教仍重要，但患者处于情绪危机时很难吸收。MAT 方案已经澄清。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In psychosocial prioritization, look for the changing trajectory: worsening hopelessness and isolation outrank tasks that can wait.","testTakingStrategyZh":"心理社会优先排序时，要看变化轨迹：加重的无望感和孤立高于可稍后完成的任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1806,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,64],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing responses are appropriate for Marcus’s Stage 2 statement, “What’s the point of staying clean if everyone still treats you like a junkie?” Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"对于 Marcus 在阶段 2 说“如果所有人还把我当瘾君子，看我保持干净有什么意义？”，哪些护理回应是恰当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing responses are appropriate for Marcus’s Stage 2 statement, “What’s the point of staying clean if everyone still treats you like a junkie?”","penultimateSentenceZh":"对于 Marcus 在阶段 2 说“如果所有人还把我当瘾君子，看我保持干净有什么意义？”，哪些护理回应是恰当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"c","en":"Offer concrete help contacting his sponsor or another recovery support before discharge.","zh":"在出院前提供具体帮助，让他联系赞助人或其他恢复支持者。"},{"id":"e","en":"Tell Marcus that Tanya reported the 2 AM car incident so he understands why she is worried.","zh":"告诉 Marcus，Tanya 报告了凌晨 2 点车内事件，让他理解她为什么担心。"},{"id":"d","en":"Ask Marcus for permission to include Tanya in safety planning while keeping private information confidential.","zh":"请求 Marcus 允许 Tanya 参与安全计划，同时保护隐私信息。"},{"id":"b","en":"Explore “what’s the point” and reassess for suicidal thoughts if his response suggests passive ideation.","zh":"探询“有什么意义”的含义；若回答提示被动意念，则重新评估自杀想法。"},{"id":"f","en":"Use reassurance such as, “You’re doing great; just stay positive and don’t think about using.”","zh":"使用安慰性话语，如：“你做得很好；保持积极，不要想着使用。”"},{"id":"a","en":"Reflect the feeling without judgment: “It sounds like you feel hurt and exhausted by being distrusted.”","zh":"不带评判地反映感受：“听起来你因为被不信任而感到受伤和疲惫。”"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic communication should validate the feeling without endorsing the distortion that recovery is pointless. The nurse should explore the phrase “what’s the point,” reassess safety if passive ideation is suggested, offer concrete support-contact help, and include Tanya only with Marcus’s consent. Disclosing Tanya’s hallway comments or using platitudes would worsen shame and damage trust.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性沟通应肯定情绪，但不强化“恢复没有意义”的认知扭曲。护士应探询“有什么意义”这句话，若提示被动意念则重新评估安全，提供联系支持者的具体帮助，并仅在 Marcus 同意时让 Tanya 参与。透露 Tanya 在走廊的谈话或使用空泛安慰会加重羞耻并破坏信任。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose responses that invite more disclosure and protect trust; avoid responses that argue, reassure superficially, or disclose another person’s private statements.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能促进进一步表达并保护信任的回应；避免争辩、表面安慰或透露他人私下说法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1807,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[94,116],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,34],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which actions should the nurse include in discharge teaching and safety planning? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 3，护士应将哪些措施纳入出院宣教和安全计划？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which actions should the nurse include in discharge teaching and safety planning?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段 3，护士应将哪些措施纳入出院宣教和安全计划？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"b","en":"Teach scheduled acetaminophen and ibuprofen use, acetaminophen daily limit/duplicate-product safety, and avoiding NSAID overlap after ketorolac.","zh":"宣教定时使用对乙酰氨基酚和布洛芬、对乙酰氨基酚每日上限/避免重复含药产品，以及酮咯酸后避免 NSAID 重叠。"},{"id":"c","en":"Reinforce the ordered buprenorphine/naloxone plan and explain that it supports OUD treatment and contributes to analgesia.","zh":"强化已开具的丁丙诺啡/纳洛酮方案，并说明其支持 OUD 治疗且有助于镇痛。"},{"id":"a","en":"Thank him for disclosing craving and reinforce that cravings can occur without meaning relapse is inevitable.","zh":"感谢他坦诚说出渴求，并强调出现渴求并不代表复发不可避免。"},{"id":"f","en":"Tell him to avoid returning to the ED for uncontrolled pain because any opioid discussion could threaten recovery.","zh":"告诉他若疼痛无法控制也应避免回急诊，因为任何阿片讨论都可能威胁恢复。"},{"id":"d","en":"Help him call his sponsor, confirm the MAT follow-up, and problem-solve transportation or remote attendance for the NA meeting before discharge.","zh":"出院前帮助他致电赞助人、确认 MAT 随访，并解决 NA 会议交通或远程参加问题。"},{"id":"e","en":"Review naloxone with Marcus and Tanya: check the printed expiration date, replace expired kits, call 911, administer available naloxone in an overdose emergency, and review overdose signs.","zh":"与 Marcus 和 Tanya 复习纳洛酮：查看包装印刷有效期、替换过期套装、拨打 911、过量紧急情况下使用可用纳洛酮，并复习过量征象。"}],"correct":["a","b","c","d","e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The discharge plan must integrate relapse prevention, pain control, harm reduction, and concrete logistics. Marcus needs validation for honest craving disclosure, a clear scheduled multimodal pain plan, continuation of ordered buprenorphine/naloxone, activated recovery supports, confirmed follow-up, transportation planning, and naloxone/overdose teaching with Tanya. He should have a supervised escalation pathway if pain becomes uncontrolled; avoiding care would increase suffering and relapse risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出院计划必须整合复发预防、疼痛控制、减害和具体后勤安排。Marcus 需要因坦诚报告渴求而得到肯定，需要明确的定时多模式镇痛方案、继续按医嘱使用丁丙诺啡/纳洛酮、启动恢复支持、确认随访、安排交通，并与 Tanya 复习纳洛酮/过量宣教。若疼痛无法控制，应有受监督的升级就医路径；回避照护会增加痛苦和复发风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge in OUD recovery, choose plans that solve the patient’s stated barriers and create an escalation path; do not give “avoid care” instructions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"OUD 恢复期出院题应选择能解决患者已说出障碍并建立升级路径的计划；不要选择“避免就医”的指示。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which actions should the nurse include in discharge teaching and safety planning?","controlSentenceZh":"在阶段 3，护士应将哪些措施纳入出院宣教和安全计划？"}
{"queueIndex":1808,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.350.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,36],"fullStemEn":"Classify each Stage 3 finding as supporting safe discharge with the current plan or requiring escalation before discharge.","fullStemZh":"将每个阶段 3 发现分类为支持按当前计划安全出院，或出院前需要升级处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each Stage 3 finding as supporting safe discharge with the current plan or requiring escalation before discharge.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每个阶段 3 发现分类为支持按当前计划安全出院，或出院前需要升级处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"selectionMode":"single_per_row","columns":[{"id":"escalate","en":"Escalate before discharge","zh":"出院前升级处理"},{"id":"adequate","en":"Supports discharge plan","zh":"支持出院计划"}],"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Marcus contacted his sponsor before leaving and has a confirmed MAT appointment within 48 hours.","zh":"Marcus 离院前已联系赞助人，并确认 48 小时内 MAT 预约。"},{"id":"r2","en":"He verbalizes the scheduled pain plan and knows whom to call or where to return if pain is uncontrolled.","zh":"他能说出定时疼痛方案，并知道疼痛无法控制时该联系谁或去哪里。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Marcus and Tanya can describe opioid overdose signs and naloxone administration steps.","zh":"Marcus 和 Tanya 能描述阿片过量征象及纳洛酮给药步骤。"},{"id":"r4","en":"He denies suicidal ideation on reassessment and is engaged in planning for tonight and tomorrow.","zh":"重新评估时他否认自杀意念，并参与今晚和明天的计划。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Marcus says he intends to use heroin tonight if the pain becomes severe.","zh":"Marcus 说如果今晚疼痛严重，他打算使用海洛因。"},{"id":"r6","en":"He refuses to contact any support, refuses follow-up, and says there is no reason to stay in recovery.","zh":"他拒绝联系任何支持者、拒绝随访，并说没有理由继续保持恢复。"},{"id":"r7","en":"Tanya reports recent self-harm statements and access to a firearm at home.","zh":"Tanya 报告他近期有自伤言论，且家中可接触枪支。"},{"id":"r8","en":"On reassessment, he says, “I might be better off not waking up,” and cannot identify protective reasons to stay safe.","zh":"重新评估时他说：“也许不醒来会更好”，且无法说出保持安全的保护性理由。"}]},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["escalate"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["escalate"]},{"rowId":"r7","columnIds":["escalate"]},{"rowId":"r8","columnIds":["escalate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe discharge is supported when the safety net is active: recovery support contacted, MAT follow-up confirmed, pain and naloxone plans understood, suicidal ideation denied, and the patient is engaged and future-oriented. Escalation is required for intent to use, refusal of all supports/follow-up, loss of protective factors, new suicidal ideation, or collateral information suggesting self-harm risk or weapon access.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当安全网已启动时支持安全出院：已联系恢复支持者、确认 MAT 随访、理解疼痛和纳洛酮方案、否认自杀意念，并能参与计划、面向未来。若出现使用意图、拒绝所有支持/随访、保护因素丧失、新发自杀意念，或旁系信息提示自伤风险/武器可及，则需升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by looking for both objective safety-net markers and qualitative change in engagement, future orientation, and protective factors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估结果时，同时寻找客观安全网标志，以及参与度、未来导向和保护因素的质性变化。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1809,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_opioid_recovery_relapse_risk_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.351","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.351.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.351.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[347,460],"terminalOffsetsZh":[115,149],"fullStemEn":"At discharge, Marcus’s nerve block is wearing off, pain is rising to 5/10, he has resumed buprenorphine/naloxone, and he openly acknowledges craving while stating he does not intend to use. He has not contacted his sponsor, has not confirmed MAT follow-up, is unsure how he will attend NA, and asks about pain escalation and Tanya’s naloxone kit. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"出院时，Marcus 的神经阻滞正在减退，疼痛升至 5/10，他已恢复丁丙诺啡/纳洛酮，并坦诚承认有渴求但表示不打算使用。他尚未联系赞助人、尚未确认 MAT 随访、不确定如何参加 NA，并询问疼痛加重和 Tanya 的纳洛酮套装。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"He has not contacted his sponsor, has not confirmed MAT follow-up, is unsure how he will attend NA, and asks about pain escalation and Tanya’s naloxone kit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"他尚未联系赞助人、尚未确认 MAT 随访、不确定如何参加 NA，并询问疼痛加重和 Tanya 的纳洛酮套装。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"condition_acute_relapse_risk","en":"Acute relapse risk from converging physical and psychosocial stressors","zh":"身体和心理社会压力共同导致的急性复发风险"},{"id":"condition_active_opioid_withdrawal","en":"Active opioid withdrawal","zh":"活动性阿片戒断"},{"id":"condition_suicidal_crisis","en":"Acute suicidal crisis requiring involuntary psychiatric hold","zh":"需要非自愿精神科留观的急性自杀危机"}],"correct":"condition_acute_relapse_risk"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"action_activate_supports","en":"Activate the recovery-support plan before discharge: sponsor/NA logistics/MAT follow-up","zh":"出院前启动恢复支持计划：赞助人、NA 后勤和 MAT 随访"},{"id":"action_paperwork_only","en":"Complete paperwork and written instructions without addressing barriers","zh":"只完成文书和书面说明，不处理障碍"},{"id":"action_pain_naloxone_teaching","en":"Teach the supervised pain plan and naloxone/overdose response with Marcus and Tanya","zh":"与 Marcus 和 Tanya 宣教受监督疼痛方案及纳洛酮/过量应对"},{"id":"action_psych_hold_craving","en":"Request a psychiatric hold solely because he disclosed craving","zh":"仅因他透露渴求而申请精神科留观"}],"correct":["action_activate_supports","action_pain_naloxone_teaching"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"parameter_repeat_uds","en":"Repeat urine drug screen at MAT follow-up as the primary ED safety marker","zh":"以 MAT 随访时重复尿筛作为主要急诊安全指标"},{"id":"parameter_support_engagement","en":"Engagement with recovery supports and confirmed follow-up","zh":"恢复支持参与情况及确认的随访"},{"id":"parameter_pain_trajectory","en":"Pain trajectory over the next 24–48 hours","zh":"未来 24–48 小时的疼痛变化"},{"id":"parameter_serial_vitals","en":"Serial HR and BP monitoring as the primary discharge outcome","zh":"以连续 HR 和 BP 监测作为主要出院结果"}],"correct":["parameter_support_engagement","parameter_pain_trajectory"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bow-tie centers on acute relapse risk, not current withdrawal or an involuntary-hold-level suicidal crisis. The nurse’s two priority actions are to activate the recovery support network and provide integrated pain-management and naloxone teaching. The most useful parameters are whether support/follow-up are actually engaged and whether pain remains controlled over the next 24–48 hours.","rationaleCorrectZh":"蝴蝶结题聚焦急性复发风险，而不是当前戒断或达到非自愿留观级别的自杀危机。护士的两个优先措施是启动恢复支持网络，并提供整合的疼痛管理和纳洛酮宣教。最有用的监测参数是支持/随访是否真正启动，以及未来 24–48 小时疼痛是否得到控制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie questions, anchor the condition first, then choose actions and monitoring parameters that directly test whether that condition is improving.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，先锚定状况，再选择能直接检验该状况是否改善的措施和监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1810,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.352","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.352.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[323,522],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,164],"fullStemEn":"Overdue preventive screening and health literacy barriers in a middle-aged adult Maria Delgado is a 52-year-old woman at a new-patient primary care visit after approximately six years without routine care. She feels well but is overdue for several preventive screenings and vaccines. Her mother had colon cancer at age 58. Maria has a high-deductible insurance plan, rotating work hours, caregiver responsibilities for her mother, and a Newest Vital Sign score consistent with a high likelihood of limited health literacy.","fullStemZh":"中年成人预防性筛查逾期与健康素养障碍 Maria Delgado，52 岁，约 6 年未接受常规初级保健，本次为新患者就诊。她自觉无症状，但多项预防性筛查和疫苗接种逾期。她的母亲 58 岁时患结肠癌。Maria 参加高免赔额保险，工作排班轮换，还要照顾母亲；Newest Vital Sign 得分提示高度可能存在健康素养受限。","terminalSentenceEn":"Maria has a high-deductible insurance plan, rotating work hours, caregiver responsibilities for her mother, and a Newest Vital Sign score consistent with a high likelihood of limited health literacy.","terminalSentenceZh":"Maria 参加高免赔额保险，工作排班轮换，还要照顾母亲；Newest Vital Sign 得分提示高度可能存在健康素养受限。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her mother had colon cancer at age 58.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她的母亲 58 岁时患结肠癌。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on a health-promotion problem rather than an acute disease process: a client with limited health literacy, fear related to a family cancer experience, cost concerns, work constraints, and caregiver responsibilities has delayed preventive care. The nurse first recognizes health-literacy and emotional cues, prioritizes colonoscopy because the clinic protocol places Maria in an increased-risk colorectal-screening group, addresses fear before education, uses teach-back to identify gaps, and builds a concrete plan that reduces scheduling, caregiving, and financial barriers. The final evaluation point is not merely whether Maria can describe the colonoscopy but whether she knows to call promptly for new symptoms rather than waiting for a scheduled screening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的核心不是急性疾病，而是健康促进问题：患者因健康素养受限、家族癌症经历带来的恐惧、费用顾虑、工作限制和照护责任而长期延迟预防保健。护士首先识别健康素养和情绪线索；依据诊所方案，因 Maria 属结直肠癌风险增加人群而优先处理结肠镜；先回应恐惧再进行宣教；通过回授法发现理解缺口；并制定能减少排班、照护和经济障碍的具体计划。最终评价重点不仅是她能否描述结肠镜，而是她是否知道如果出现新症状应及时联系诊所，而不是等到已预约的筛查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In preventive-care cases, separate acute medical instability from health-promotion priorities. Then ask which barrier prevents follow-through and which nursing action makes the plan usable for this specific client.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到预防保健题时，先区分是否有急性不稳定状况；若没有，再判断健康促进的优先事项。随后思考哪个障碍会影响落实，以及哪项护理措施能让这个患者真正执行计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1811,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that are relevant to planning the nurse's communication approach for this visit.","fullStemZh":"请标出与护士本次就诊沟通方式计划相关的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that are relevant to planning the nurse's communication approach for this visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出与护士本次就诊沟通方式计划相关的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q1_static_1","en":"During intake, the nurse notes: ","zh":"接诊时，护士注意到："},{"id":"q1_s1","en":"Maria left several intake sections blank and wrote, \"not sure what this means.\"","zh":"Maria 多处入院表格留空，并写下“not sure what this means”。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s2","en":"Newest Vital Sign score is 1 out of 6.","zh":"Newest Vital Sign 得分为 1/6。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s3","en":"She reads the pamphlet slowly, holds it at arm's length, and sets it down.","zh":"她阅读宣传单很慢，把资料拿得较远，几秒后放下。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s4","en":"She fidgets with her purse strap and avoids eye contact.","zh":"她摆弄手提包带并避免眼神接触。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s5","en":"She says a previous provider used words she did not understand and she just nodded along.","zh":"她说以前的医护人员用了她听不懂的词，她只是点头。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s6","en":"Blood pressure is 124/78 mm Hg.","zh":"血压为 124/78 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s7","en":"Non-fasting fingerstick glucose is 118 mg/dL.","zh":"非空腹指尖血糖为 118 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"q1_s8","en":"There is mild right supraspinatus tenderness without reduced range of motion.","zh":"右冈上肌轻度压痛，但活动范围未受限。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q1_s1","q1_s2","q1_s3","q1_s4","q1_s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Blank forms, a very low health-literacy score, difficulty using the pamphlet, discomfort behaviors, and a statement about nodding along when she did not understand all directly shape the communication plan. They support plain language, pacing, and teach-back. Normal vital signs, a single non-fasting glucose of 118 mg/dL, and mild shoulder tenderness are baseline findings but do not drive the immediate communication strategy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"表格留空、健康素养筛查得分很低、使用宣传单困难、不安行为，以及曾因听不懂而只是点头的陈述，都会直接影响沟通计划。这些线索提示需要使用通俗语言、放慢节奏并采用回授法。正常生命体征、单次非空腹血糖 118 mg/dL 和轻度肩痛属于基础资料，但不决定立即的沟通策略。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For recognize-cues items, group findings by the decision being made. Here the decision is communication planning, not diagnosing diabetes or treating shoulder pain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别线索题要按当前决策来分组。本题决策是沟通计划，而不是诊断糖尿病或处理肩痛。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1812,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"Based on the clinic preventive-care protocol and the Stage 1 data, which overdue screening is the highest priority for the nurse to address first?","fullStemZh":"依据诊所预防保健方案和阶段 1 资料，护士应首先重点处理哪项逾期筛查？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the clinic preventive-care protocol and the Stage 1 data, which overdue screening is the highest priority for the nurse to address first?","terminalSentenceZh":"依据诊所预防保健方案和阶段 1 资料，护士应首先重点处理哪项逾期筛查？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Schedule colorectal cancer screening with colonoscopy.","zh":"安排结肠镜进行结直肠癌筛查。"},{"id":"B","en":"Schedule cervical cancer screening with Pap/HPV co-testing.","zh":"安排 Pap/HPV 联合检测进行宫颈癌筛查。"},{"id":"E","en":"Complete fasting glucose and lipid testing before any cancer screening is scheduled.","zh":"先完成空腹血糖和血脂检查，再安排任何癌症筛查。"},{"id":"C","en":"Schedule screening mammography.","zh":"安排筛查性乳房 X 线摄影。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the influenza vaccine today.","zh":"今天接种流感疫苗。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Maria's mother is a first-degree relative diagnosed with colorectal cancer before age 60. Under the clinic protocol, Maria should have begun colonoscopy at age 40 or 10 years before her mother's diagnosis, whichever was earlier; age 40 is earlier than age 48. At age 52 with no prior colonoscopy, she is 12 years beyond the risk-stratified start point. Cervical and breast screening are also important, and influenza vaccine can be completed today, but colonoscopy is the highest-priority screening risk to address.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Maria 的母亲是一级亲属，且 60 岁前诊断结直肠癌。按诊所方案，Maria 应从 40 岁或比母亲诊断年龄提前 10 年开始结肠镜，以较早者为准；40 岁早于 48 岁。她现在 52 岁且从未做过结肠镜，已超过风险分层起始年龄 12 年。宫颈和乳腺筛查也重要，流感疫苗可今日完成，但结肠镜是最优先处理的筛查风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not equate the quickest task with the highest priority. Rank preventive needs by individualized risk and the strength of the indication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把最快能完成的任务等同于最高优先级。应按个体化风险和适应证强度排序预防需求。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1813,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,208],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,59],"fullStemEn":"When colonoscopy is mentioned, Maria says she does not want to know if she has cancer and cannot take a day off work. She crosses her arms and looks toward the door. Which response by the nurse is best first?","fullStemZh":"提到结肠镜时，Maria 说她不想知道自己是否有癌症，也不能请一天假。她双臂交叉并看向门口。护士首先应如何回应最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应如何回应最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"She crosses her arms and looks toward the door.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她双臂交叉并看向门口。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"\"Colonoscopy is very safe, and survival is much better when cancer is found early.\"","zh":"“结肠镜很安全，而且癌症早发现时存活率高得多。”"},{"id":"D","en":"\"Your health has to come first, even if taking time off is hard.\"","zh":"“即使请假困难，你的健康也必须排第一。”"},{"id":"E","en":"\"I will give you the scheduling number so you can book the procedure when you are ready.\"","zh":"“我把预约电话给你，你准备好时自己安排检查。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"You have no symptoms, so you should not worry about colon cancer right now.\"","zh":"“你现在没有症状，所以现在不用担心结肠癌。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"Your mother's experience sounds frightening, and losing work time is a real concern. Let's talk through both before we decide next steps.\"","zh":"“你母亲的经历听起来很可怕，请假影响工作也是现实担忧。我们先一起谈谈这两点，再决定下一步。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Maria is showing fear and a defensive posture. The nurse should first acknowledge the emotional barrier and validate the practical work barrier without judgment. This builds trust and makes later education possible. Facts, reassurance, or scheduling instructions given before the emotion is addressed are less likely to be heard and may increase avoidance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Maria 表现出恐惧和防御姿态。护士应首先承认情绪障碍，并非评判性地确认工作请假的现实困难。这样能建立信任，使后续宣教成为可能。在情绪未被回应前直接给数据、安慰或安排预约，往往难以被听进去，还可能加重回避。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client shows fear or defensiveness, choose the response that acknowledges feelings before teaching or persuading.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者表现出恐惧或防御时，优先选择先承认感受、再宣教或劝导的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1814,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,48],"fullStemEn":"Classify each part of Maria's Stage 2 teach-back as either adequate understanding or needing targeted reteaching/follow-up.","fullStemZh":"请判断 Maria 在阶段 2 回授中的每一部分，是理解充分，还是需要有针对性地重新宣教/随访。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each part of Maria's Stage 2 teach-back as either adequate understanding or needing targeted reteaching/follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断 Maria 在阶段 2 回授中的每一部分，是理解充分，还是需要有针对性地重新宣教/随访。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q4_r1","en":"She correctly connects the Pap smear, mammogram, and colonoscopy with the appropriate body areas and recognizes the family-history link for colonoscopy.","zh":"她能将 Pap、乳房 X 线和结肠镜与相应身体部位联系起来，并认识到结肠镜与家族史有关。"},{"id":"q4_r2","en":"She says each cancer screening is needed because she might already have cancer.","zh":"她说每项癌症筛查都是因为她可能已经患癌。"},{"id":"q4_r3","en":"She states that the influenza vaccine is to help prevent influenza.","zh":"她说流感疫苗是为了帮助预防流感。"},{"id":"q4_r4","en":"She omits the recombinant zoster vaccine from the plan.","zh":"她没有提到重组带状疱疹疫苗。"},{"id":"q4_r5","en":"She says her blood sugar is fine, so she does not need to worry about anything else.","zh":"她说血糖没事，所以其他都不用担心。"}],"columns":[{"id":"reteach","en":"Needs targeted reteaching/follow-up","zh":"需要针对性重新宣教/随访"},{"id":"adequate","en":"Adequate understanding","zh":"理解充分"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q4_r1","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"q4_r2","columnIds":["reteach"]},{"rowId":"q4_r3","columnIds":["adequate"]},{"rowId":"q4_r4","columnIds":["reteach"]},{"rowId":"q4_r5","columnIds":["reteach"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teach-back is partially correct. Maria can match the screenings to the correct body areas and understands the family-history reason for colonoscopy, and she understands the influenza vaccine. However, she still equates screening with suspected cancer, omits the zoster vaccine, and incorrectly concludes that no other follow-up is needed because the non-fasting glucose was not alarming. These gaps require focused reteaching rather than repeating the entire visit from the beginning.","rationaleCorrectZh":"回授结果部分正确。Maria 能把筛查与正确身体部位对应，也理解结肠镜与家族史有关，并理解流感疫苗作用。但她仍把筛查等同于怀疑已有癌症，遗漏带状疱疹疫苗，并错误认为非空腹血糖不严重就不需其他随访。这些缺口需要有针对性地重新宣教，而不是从头重复整次宣教。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Teach-back is not pass/fail. Identify what is correct, then target the missing or unsafe pieces.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回授不是简单合格/不合格。先找出正确部分，再针对遗漏或不安全部分重新宣教。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1815,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,43],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions best address Maria's barriers while sequencing the remaining preventive-care plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应采取哪些措施，以在安排后续预防保健时处理 Maria 的障碍？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions best address Maria's barriers while sequencing the remaining preventive-care plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施，以在安排后续预防保健时处理 Maria 的障碍？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Offer fasting labs through a walk-in lab or other option that fits her work schedule.","zh":"提供可配合其工作时间的步入式实验室或其他方式完成空腹化验。"},{"id":"F","en":"Schedule the colonoscopy, Pap/HPV test, vaccines, and labs on separate days so each topic can be discussed in isolation.","zh":"将结肠镜、Pap/HPV、疫苗和化验都安排在不同日期，以便每个主题单独讨论。"},{"id":"E","en":"Use plain-language teaching and teach-back at each encounter, including vaccine and follow-up instructions.","zh":"每次接触都使用通俗语言和回授法，包括疫苗和随访说明。"},{"id":"D","en":"Help Maria identify caregiver coverage for her mother on appointment or procedure days.","zh":"帮助 Maria 确认预约或检查当天谁能照看她的母亲。"},{"id":"A","en":"Consolidate appointments when possible, such as pairing Pap/HPV testing with the colonoscopy-prep teaching visit.","zh":"尽可能合并预约，例如将 Pap/HPV 检测与结肠镜准备宣教安排在同一天。"},{"id":"B","en":"Connect Maria with the financial counselor before colonoscopy scheduling is finalized.","zh":"在最终安排结肠镜前，帮助 Maria 联系财务顾问。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Maria's barriers are practical and communication-related: rotating work, caregiver duties, cost concerns, and limited health literacy. The plan should reduce visit burden, address insurance questions before scheduling, make labs feasible, arrange caregiver coverage, and preserve plain-language teach-back. Scheduling everything on separate days increases the number of days off and caregiver arrangements required, which undermines follow-through.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Maria 的障碍包括现实安排和沟通两方面：轮班工作、照护责任、费用担忧和健康素养受限。计划应减少就诊负担，在安排前处理保险问题，使化验可行，安排照护支持，并持续使用通俗语言和回授法。把所有事项分散到不同日期会增加请假和照护安排次数，反而削弱落实可能性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client has adherence barriers, the best nursing actions make the care plan easier to complete without removing required safety steps.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者有落实障碍时，最佳护理措施是在不省略必要安全步骤的前提下，让计划更容易完成。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1816,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.352.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[215,261],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,78],"fullStemEn":"At the follow-up visit, Maria correctly explains why she is having a colonoscopy but says she would wait until the scheduled procedure to mention new blood in stool, bowel habit changes, or unexplained weight loss. How should the nurse evaluate this teach-back?","fullStemZh":"随访时，Maria 能正确解释为什么要做结肠镜，但表示如果在预约前出现便血、排便习惯改变或不明原因体重下降，她会等到结肠镜当天再说。护士应如何评价这次回授？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse evaluate this teach-back?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何评价这次回授？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At the follow-up visit, Maria correctly explains why she is having a colonoscopy but says she would wait until the scheduled procedure to mention new blood in stool, bowel habit changes, or unexplained weight loss.","penultimateSentenceZh":"随访时，Maria 能正确解释为什么要做结肠镜，但表示如果在预约前出现便血、排便习惯改变或不明原因体重下降，她会等到结肠镜当天再说。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"It is incomplete because she must be taught to call the clinic promptly for new symptoms, then repeat teach-back.","zh":"回授不完整；必须教她若出现新症状应立即联系诊所，然后再次回授确认。"},{"id":"E","en":"It indicates the nurse should request FIT instead of colonoscopy because Maria remains anxious.","zh":"这说明她仍焦虑，护士应改为申请 FIT 而不是结肠镜。"},{"id":"D","en":"It indicates she needs detailed cancer survival statistics to motivate faster follow-through.","zh":"这说明她需要详细癌症存活率数据，以促使她更快落实。"},{"id":"C","en":"It indicates she should cancel the screening colonoscopy and wait until symptoms develop.","zh":"这说明她应取消筛查性结肠镜，等出现症状后再检查。"},{"id":"B","en":"It is adequate because she understands the purpose of the colonoscopy and has already scheduled it.","zh":"回授充分，因为她已理解结肠镜目的并已安排检查。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Maria understands the purpose of screening but has a critical safety gap: she would wait to report symptoms that could require earlier diagnostic evaluation. The nurse should correct the misunderstanding calmly, explain that new symptoms change the situation from routine screening to diagnostic follow-up, and repeat teach-back to confirm understanding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Maria 理解筛查目的，但存在关键安全缺口：她会等到预约时才报告可能需要更早诊断性评估的症状。护士应平静地纠正误解，说明新症状会使情况从常规筛查转为诊断性随访，并再次回授确认理解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by looking for unsafe omissions, not just correct statements. A correct explanation can still miss a key safety instruction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价结果时要寻找不安全的遗漏，而不只看说对了什么。即使解释正确，也可能漏掉关键安全指导。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1817,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_overdue_preventive_screening_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.353","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.353.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.353.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[456,485],"terminalOffsetsZh":[133,142],"fullStemEn":"Maria is at the Stage 3 follow-up visit after fear, cost, scheduling, and caregiver barriers have been addressed. Influenza vaccine and the first recombinant zoster vaccine dose have been given. Colonoscopy is scheduled with plan-specific coverage reviewed by the financial counselor, Pap/HPV co-testing is scheduled with the colonoscopy-prep teaching visit, and teach-back has revealed that Maria would wait to report new symptoms before the colonoscopy. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"Maria 已到阶段 3 随访；她的恐惧、费用、排班和照护障碍已被处理。流感疫苗和第一剂重组带状疱疹疫苗已接种。结肠镜已安排，财务顾问已核对其具体保险覆盖；Pap/HPV 联合检测安排在结肠镜准备宣教同一天；回授显示 Maria 若在结肠镜前出现新症状会等待再报告。请完成弓形题图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Colonoscopy is scheduled with plan-specific coverage reviewed by the financial counselor, Pap/HPV co-testing is scheduled with the colonoscopy-prep teaching visit, and teach-back has revealed that Maria would wait to report new symptoms before the colonoscopy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"结肠镜已安排，财务顾问已核对其具体保险覆盖；Pap/HPV 联合检测安排在结肠镜准备宣教同一天；回授显示 Maria 若在结肠镜前出现新症状会等待再报告。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_c3","en":"Undiagnosed chronic disease requiring immediate medication management","zh":"未诊断慢性病，需要立即药物治疗"},{"id":"bt_c1","en":"Limited health literacy with delayed preventive-care engagement and barriers to screening follow-through","zh":"健康素养受限导致预防保健延迟，并存在筛查落实障碍"},{"id":"bt_c2","en":"Noncompliance or deliberate disengagement from care","zh":"不依从或有意脱离医疗护理"}],"correct":"bt_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority nursing actions","zh":"优先护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_a4","en":"Add several new screening and teaching topics at the end of the visit","zh":"在就诊结束时再增加多项新的筛查和宣教主题"},{"id":"bt_a2","en":"Confirm documented dates and support plans for colonoscopy, Pap/HPV testing, and the second zoster vaccine dose","zh":"确认结肠镜、Pap/HPV 检测和第二剂带状疱疹疫苗的日期及支持计划已记录"},{"id":"bt_a1","en":"Correct the symptom-reporting gap and confirm with repeat teach-back","zh":"纠正新症状报告的理解缺口，并再次回授确认"},{"id":"bt_a3","en":"Accept the Stage 3 teach-back as complete because the colonoscopy purpose was explained correctly","zh":"因其能正确说明结肠镜目的，就认为阶段 3 回授已完整"}],"correct":["bt_a1","bt_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bt_p1","en":"Follow-through with scheduled colonoscopy and Pap/HPV appointments","zh":"是否落实已预约的结肠镜和 Pap/HPV 检测"},{"id":"bt_p2","en":"Accuracy and completeness of teach-back at subsequent visits","zh":"后续就诊回授的准确性和完整性"},{"id":"bt_p4","en":"Fasting glucose as the primary outcome for this case","zh":"将空腹血糖作为本病例首要结果指标"},{"id":"bt_p3","en":"Maria's use of professional medical terminology","zh":"Maria 是否使用专业医学术语"}],"correct":["bt_p1","bt_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The resolved problem is limited health literacy and delayed preventive-care engagement with ongoing barriers, not willful noncompliance or an acute chronic-disease medication problem. The priority actions are to close the critical teach-back gap about reporting new symptoms and to confirm that the concrete follow-up plan is documented and supported. The most relevant outcomes are whether Maria attends the planned screenings and whether teach-back remains accurate and complete.","rationaleCorrectZh":"已明确的问题是健康素养受限和预防保健延迟，并伴随持续障碍；不是故意不依从，也不是需要立即药物处理的急性慢病问题。优先措施是弥补关于新症状报告的关键回授缺口，并确认具体随访计划已记录且有支持。最相关的结果是 Maria 是否完成已安排筛查，以及后续回授是否准确完整。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, anchor the condition in the whole case pattern, then choose actions and monitoring parameters that close the highest-risk remaining gaps.","testTakingStrategyZh":"弓形题要先用整个病例模式确定核心情况，再选择能弥补剩余最高风险缺口的措施和监测指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1818,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.354","itemType":"case_study","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.354.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,85],"fullStemEn":"Pressure injury prevention and safe mobility after hip hemiarthroplasty Margaret Tierney is an 82-year-old postoperative hip-hemiarthroplasty client with frailty, poor intake, mild cognitive impairment, pain-limited mobility, and early skin breakdown risk.","fullStemZh":"髋关节半置换术后压力性损伤预防与安全活动 Margaret Tierney，82岁，髋关节半置换术后患者，有虚弱、进食差、轻度认知障碍、疼痛限制活动以及早期皮肤破损风险。","terminalSentenceEn":"Pressure injury prevention and safe mobility after hip hemiarthroplasty Margaret Tierney is an 82-year-old postoperative hip-hemiarthroplasty client with frailty, poor intake, mild cognitive impairment, pain-limited mobility, and early skin breakdown risk.","terminalSentenceZh":"髋关节半置换术后压力性损伤预防与安全活动 Margaret Tierney，82岁，髋关节半置换术后患者，有虚弱、进食差、轻度认知障碍、疼痛限制活动以及早期皮肤破损风险。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows a frail postoperative client whose early Stage 1 coccygeal pressure injury is driven by immobility, moisture, pain, poor intake, and friction/shear. The nurse must recognize actionable cues, synthesize escalating pressure-injury risk beyond the Braden score alone, prioritize safe toileting over routine catheter reinsertion when urgency and fall risk converge, build an integrated plan for pain, mobility, nutrition, moisture, toileting, and pressure redistribution, correct a device-related heel injury, and evaluate both improvements and plan failures over time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例呈现一名虚弱术后患者，早期尾骨1期压力性损伤由不活动、潮湿、疼痛、摄入差及摩擦/剪切力共同驱动。护士必须识别需要处理的线索，综合判断压力性损伤风险升高而不能只看Braden评分，在尿急和跌倒风险并存时优先安全如厕而不是常规重新置管，制定整合疼痛、活动、营养、潮湿、如厕和减压的计划，纠正器械相关足跟损伤，并随时间评价改善与计划失败。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding case studies, track what changed from baseline. Prioritize acute safety threats while preserving prevention measures for slower-developing complications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式病例题中，要追踪相对基线发生的变化。在处理急性安全威胁的同时，不能忽略预防较慢发生并发症的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1819,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"Using the baseline and Stage 1 data, highlight the findings that require nursing attention now.","fullStemZh":"根据基线资料和第1阶段资料，标出现在需要护理关注的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the baseline and Stage 1 data, highlight the findings that require nursing attention now.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据基线资料和第1阶段资料，标出现在需要护理关注的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q1_s1","selectable":true,"en":"Coccygeal skin is intact with a 2 × 3 cm non-blanchable erythematous area that is warm to touch.","zh":"尾骨处皮肤完整，但有约2 × 3 cm不可褪色红斑，触之较周围皮肤温暖。"},{"id":"q1_s2","selectable":true,"en":"The perineum is moist with mild erythema in the gluteal fold.","zh":"会阴部潮湿，臀沟有轻度红斑。"},{"id":"q1_s3","selectable":true,"en":"Pain is 7/10 at rest and she says she is afraid to move because everything hurts.","zh":"静息痛为7/10，患者说因为“哪里都痛”而害怕移动。"},{"id":"q1_s4","selectable":true,"en":"After IV hydromorphone, she is more sedated, drifts off mid-sentence, RR is 12/min, and SpO2 is 94% on 2 L nasal cannula.","zh":"静脉使用氢吗啡酮后，患者更嗜睡，说话中途会睡着，RR 12次/分，鼻导管2 L吸氧下SpO2为94%。"},{"id":"q1_s5","selectable":true,"en":"She has not used the incentive spirometer since arrival on the unit.","zh":"自到达病房后，患者尚未使用激励式肺量计。"},{"id":"q1_s6","selectable":true,"en":"Her daughter reports recent unintentional weight loss of about 7 lb and poor intake.","zh":"女儿报告患者近期非故意体重下降约7磅，进食减少。"},{"id":"q1_s7","selectable":true,"en":"Mucous membranes are dry and she has taken only two sips of ginger ale.","zh":"黏膜干燥，患者只喝了两口姜汁汽水。"},{"id":"q1_s8","selectable":true,"en":"Albumin is 2.8 g/dL and prealbumin is 14 mg/dL.","zh":"白蛋白2.8 g/dL，前白蛋白14 mg/dL。"},{"id":"q1_s9","selectable":true,"en":"Mild edema is present in the right foot and ankle, with warmth, intact sensation, and a palpable 2+ pedal pulse.","zh":"右足和踝部轻度水肿，但肢端温暖、感觉完整，足背/足部脉搏2+可触及。"},{"id":"q1_s10","selectable":true,"en":"Bowel sounds are hypoactive after surgery.","zh":"术后肠鸣音减弱。"},{"id":"q1_s11","selectable":true,"en":"Temperature is 98.2 °F (36.8 °C).","zh":"体温98.2 °F (36.8 °C)。"},{"id":"q1_s12","selectable":true,"en":"Hemoglobin decreased from 11.8 g/dL preoperatively to 10.4 g/dL postoperatively.","zh":"血红蛋白由术前11.8 g/dL降至术后10.4 g/dL。"},{"id":"q1_s13","selectable":true,"en":"Urine output is 350 mL over about 5 hours since surgery.","zh":"术后约5小时尿量为350 mL。"}],"correct":["q1_s1","q1_s2","q1_s3","q1_s4","q1_s5","q1_s6","q1_s7","q1_s8"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The actionable cues show an existing Stage 1 coccygeal pressure injury, moisture-associated skin risk, pain-driven immobility, opioid-related sedation/respiratory monitoring needs, pulmonary hygiene risk, and nutrition/fluid-risk markers. The mild foot edema with intact neurovascular status, hypoactive bowel sounds, normal temperature, stable postoperative hemoglobin change, and adequate urine output are expected or less urgent.","rationaleCorrectZh":"需要处理的线索包括已形成的尾骨1期压力性损伤、潮湿相关皮肤风险、疼痛导致的不活动、阿片相关嗜睡/呼吸监测需求、肺部卫生风险以及营养和液体摄入风险标志。神经血管状态完整下的轻度足部水肿、术后肠鸣音减弱、正常体温、稳定的术后血红蛋白变化和足够尿量，属于预期或较不紧急的发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected postoperative findings from cues that change the plan of care. Intact skin can still be injured when erythema is non-blanchable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把预期的术后表现与会改变护理计划的线索分开。皮肤完整并不代表没有损伤；不可褪色红斑已经提示压力性损伤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1820,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which interpretation best synthesizes the pressure-injury risk cluster?","fullStemZh":"第1阶段，哪项解释最能综合压力性损伤风险线索？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which interpretation best synthesizes the pressure-injury risk cluster?","terminalSentenceZh":"第1阶段，哪项解释最能综合压力性损伤风险线索？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q2_a","en":"High and escalating risk for progressive pressure injury, with an existing Stage 1 coccygeal injury and compounding moisture, nutrition, immobility, and shear risks.","zh":"进行性压力性损伤风险高且正在升高，已有尾骨1期损伤，并叠加潮湿、营养、不活动和剪切力风险。"},{"id":"q2_e","en":"Expected postoperative redness only; no pressure injury is present because the coccygeal skin surface is intact.","zh":"仅为预期术后发红；因尾骨皮肤表面完整，所以没有压力性损伤。"},{"id":"q2_b","en":"Surgical-site infection, because low albumin and poor intake indicate the incision is infected.","zh":"手术切口感染，因为低白蛋白和进食差说明切口已感染。"},{"id":"q2_c","en":"Postoperative hemorrhage as the unifying problem, because hemoglobin decreased after surgery.","zh":"术后出血是统一问题，因为术后血红蛋白下降。"},{"id":"q2_d","en":"Deep vein thrombosis, because postoperative immobility and mild right foot swelling explain the skin findings.","zh":"深静脉血栓，因为术后不活动和右足轻度肿胀可解释皮肤发现。"}],"correct":["q2_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The findings indicate escalating pressure-injury risk with tissue damage already present. Sustained pressure from immobility, moisture, nutrition risk, and friction/shear converge to reduce tissue tolerance. Low albumin and prealbumin reinforce adverse outcome risk but are not direct diagnostic proof of malnutrition.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这些发现提示压力性损伤风险正在升高且已有组织损伤。不活动造成的持续受压、潮湿、营养风险以及摩擦/剪切力共同降低组织耐受性。低白蛋白和低前白蛋白加强了不良结局风险，但不是营养不良的直接诊断依据。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For analyze-cues questions, look for the answer that explains the whole cluster rather than one isolated finding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析线索题要选择能解释整个线索群的答案，而不是只解释单一发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1821,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,57],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which nursing need is the immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"第2阶段，哪项护理需求是当前最优先？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which nursing need is the immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"第2阶段，哪项护理需求是当前最优先？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"q3_b","en":"Reinsert the indwelling urinary catheter because the client requests it and wants to avoid wetting the bed.","zh":"因患者要求且担心尿床，重新置入留置尿管。"},{"id":"q3_c","en":"Delay toileting until pain is 0/10, then attempt bathroom ambulation with one-person assist.","zh":"等疼痛降到0/10后，再一人协助步行去卫生间。"},{"id":"q3_e","en":"Keep her on bedrest and use an absorbent brief to prevent a fall during the orthostatic episode.","zh":"继续卧床并使用吸收性尿裤，以防体位性低血压时跌倒。"},{"id":"q3_d","en":"Focus first on the dietary consult and protein supplement because nutrition is the driver of tissue healing.","zh":"先处理营养会诊和蛋白补充，因为营养是组织愈合的关键驱动因素。"},{"id":"q3_a","en":"Provide safe toileting now: offer the raised bedside commode, give available analgesia to support transfer, use fall precautions and two-person assist, and monitor orthostatic symptoms.","zh":"立即提供安全如厕：使用加高床旁便椅，先给予可用镇痛药以帮助转移，采取防跌倒措施和两人协助，并监测体位性症状。"}],"correct":["q3_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The 420 mL bladder scan with urgency creates an immediate fall and moisture risk. The priority is safe toileting with pain medication as part of the preparation, not catheter reinsertion or postponement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"膀胱扫描420 mL并伴尿急，立即造成跌倒和潮湿风险。优先措施是安全如厕，镇痛是准备过程的一部分，而不是重新留置尿管或推迟处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize the need that can cause immediate harm. Here, bladder urgency plus orthostasis can quickly become a fall or moisture injury.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先处理可能立即造成伤害的问题。此处尿急加体位性低血压，很快可能变成跌倒或潮湿性皮肤损伤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1822,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,108],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,30],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which interventions should the nurse include in the integrated care plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第2阶段，护士应将哪些干预纳入综合护理计划？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which interventions should the nurse include in the integrated care plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第2阶段，护士应将哪些干预纳入综合护理计划？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q4_d","en":"Continue q2h repositioning, maintain the pressure-redistribution overlay, keep linens dry and smooth, apply barrier cream after moisture exposure, and verify heel suspension.","zh":"继续每2小时翻身，保持减压床垫/垫层，床单干燥平整，潮湿后涂屏障霜，并确认足跟完全悬空。"},{"id":"q4_b","en":"Before standing, dangle at the bedside, rise slowly, monitor symptoms/vital signs, use gait belt and assistive device, and keep the call light within reach.","zh":"站立前先坐床边垂腿，缓慢起身，监测症状/生命体征，使用步态带和辅助器具，并确保呼叫铃在手边。"},{"id":"q4_c","en":"Request dietary consultation, offer small frequent high-protein supplements, track intake/output, and encourage preferred foods.","zh":"申请营养会诊，提供少量多餐和高蛋白补充品，记录摄入/排出，并鼓励患者选择偏好的食物。"},{"id":"q4_e","en":"Use prompted voiding every 2–3 hours with the raised bedside commode to prevent urgency-driven unsafe transfers.","zh":"每2–3小时使用加高床旁便椅进行提示排尿，以防尿急导致不安全转移。"},{"id":"q4_a","en":"Premedicate 20–30 minutes before physical therapy or transfers and use pillows, ordered ice, distraction, and hearing aids to improve participation.","zh":"在物理治疗或转移前20–30分钟预先给镇痛药，并使用枕头、医嘱允许的冰敷、转移注意力及佩戴助听器来促进配合。"},{"id":"q4_f","en":"Keep the head of bed above 45 degrees whenever she is supine to reduce aspiration and improve breathing.","zh":"只要仰卧就将床头保持在45度以上，以减少误吸并改善呼吸。"}],"correct":["q4_a","q4_b","q4_c","q4_d","q4_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The plan must address interdependent risks: pain limiting mobility, orthostatic fall risk, poor intake, pressure and moisture exposure, and urgency-driven unsafe toileting. Elevating the head of bed too high while supine can worsen sacral shear.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护理计划必须处理相互关联的风险：疼痛限制活动、体位性跌倒风险、摄入差、压力和潮湿暴露，以及尿急导致的不安全如厕。仰卧时床头过高会加重骶尾部剪切力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For integrated-plan items, choose interventions that match each active driver and avoid actions that solve one concern while worsening another.","testTakingStrategyZh":"综合计划题要选择对应每个活跃风险因素的干预，并避免解决一个问题却加重另一个问题的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1823,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,38],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which actions should the nurse take for the new non-blanchable heel redness? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段，针对新出现的足跟不可褪色红斑，护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which actions should the nurse take for the new non-blanchable heel redness?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第3阶段，针对新出现的足跟不可褪色红斑，护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"q5_d","en":"Notify the provider or wound-care pathway per facility protocol and add the heel to q2h skin checks.","zh":"按机构流程通知医护提供者或伤口护理路径，并将足跟纳入每2小时皮肤检查。"},{"id":"q5_b","en":"Document size, exact location, color, warmth, and intact skin, and identify the finding as a new Stage 1 device-related pressure injury.","zh":"记录大小、准确部位、颜色、温度和皮肤完整性，并识别为新的1期医疗器械相关压力性损伤。"},{"id":"q5_e","en":"Check the opposite heel and teach the nursing assistant to verify device position at every repositioning.","zh":"检查对侧足跟，并指导护理助理每次翻身时确认器械位置。"},{"id":"q5_f","en":"Massage the reddened heel, tighten the strap so the boot will not shift, and continue routine monitoring.","zh":"按摩发红足跟，收紧绑带以防保护靴移位，并继续常规观察。"},{"id":"q5_c","en":"Correct offloading by reapplying a properly fitted boot with no strap pressure or by using pillow suspension under the calf to fully float the heel.","zh":"通过正确佩戴无绑带压迫的足跟保护靴，或用枕头支托小腿使足跟完全悬空，来纠正减压。"},{"id":"q5_a","en":"Remove the boot and inspect the entire right heel and surrounding skin.","zh":"取下足跟保护靴，检查整个右足跟及周围皮肤。"}],"correct":["q5_a","q5_b","q5_c","q5_d","q5_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The boot strap caused a new Stage 1 device-related pressure injury. The nurse must remove and inspect the device site, document and stage the injury, correct offloading, notify per protocol, check the opposite heel, and communicate device-position checks to assistive staff.","rationaleCorrectZh":"足跟保护靴绑带造成新的1期医疗器械相关压力性损伤。护士必须取下并检查器械接触部位，记录并分期，纠正减压方式，按流程通知，检查对侧足跟，并向辅助人员交代器械位置检查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A protective device can become the source of injury. Always assess skin under devices and fix the pressure source, not just the appearance of redness.","testTakingStrategyZh":"保护性器械也可能成为损伤来源。必须评估器械下方皮肤并纠正压力来源，而不只是观察红斑外观。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which actions should the nurse take for the new non-blanchable heel redness?","controlSentenceZh":"第3阶段，针对新出现的足跟不可褪色红斑，护士应采取哪些措施？"}
{"queueIndex":1824,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.354.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,86],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each outcome while evaluating whether the care plan is effective.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段，评价护理计划效果时，请对每项结局进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each outcome while evaluating whether the care plan is effective.","terminalSentenceZh":"第3阶段，评价护理计划效果时，请对每项结局进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"selectionMode":"single_per_row","columns":[{"id":"parallel","en":"Parallel concern, not a pressure-prevention outcome marker","zh":"并行问题，不是压力预防效果指标"},{"id":"needs_change","en":"Plan not fully effective / needs modification","zh":"计划未完全有效/需要调整"},{"id":"working","en":"Plan is working","zh":"计划有效"}],"rows":[{"id":"q6_r1","en":"Coccygeal injury decreased from 2 × 3 cm to 1 × 2 cm and is lighter in color, though still non-blanchable.","zh":"尾骨损伤由2 × 3 cm缩小至1 × 2 cm，颜色变浅，但仍不可褪色。"},{"id":"q6_r2","en":"Pain improved to 3/10 at rest; she walked 15 feet with a walker; orthostatic vital signs improved; she voided on the commode and had a bowel movement.","zh":"静息痛改善至3/10；使用助行器步行15英尺；体位性生命体征改善；能在便椅排尿并已排便。"},{"id":"q6_r3","en":"A new right heel Stage 1 pressure injury appeared where the shifted boot strap crossed the posterior calcaneus.","zh":"右足跟出现新的1期压力性损伤，位置正好在移位保护靴绑带跨过后跟骨处。"},{"id":"q6_r4","en":"She is eating about 50% of meals and albumin/prealbumin remain low adverse-risk markers.","zh":"患者约进食50%的餐食，白蛋白/前白蛋白仍是偏低的不良风险标志。"},{"id":"q6_r5","en":"Hemoglobin drifted from 10.4 g/dL to 9.8 g/dL.","zh":"血红蛋白由10.4 g/dL降至9.8 g/dL。"},{"id":"q6_r6","en":"Sleep remains fragmented into two-hour blocks between repositioning.","zh":"因翻身护理，睡眠仍被分割成约两小时一段。"}]},"correct":[{"rowId":"q6_r1","columnIds":["working"]},{"rowId":"q6_r2","columnIds":["working"]},{"rowId":"q6_r3","columnIds":["needs_change"]},{"rowId":"q6_r4","columnIds":["needs_change"]},{"rowId":"q6_r5","columnIds":["parallel"]},{"rowId":"q6_r6","columnIds":["needs_change"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Evaluation requires comparing multiple trajectories. Sacral skin, pain, mobility, orthostasis, voiding, bowel function, and intake improved, but the new heel injury and persistent nutrition risk show the plan is not fully effective and must be modified. Hemoglobin is a parallel postoperative issue rather than a pressure-prevention outcome.","rationaleCorrectZh":"评价需要比较多个轨迹。骶尾部皮肤、疼痛、活动能力、体位性低血压、排尿、排便和摄入有所改善，但新的足跟损伤和持续营养风险说明计划未完全有效，必须调整。血红蛋白是并行的术后问题，而不是压力预防效果指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not call a plan successful because one outcome improved. Look for new harm, lagging domains, and whether each parameter actually measures the plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因为一个结局改善就认为计划成功。要寻找新的伤害、落后的领域，并判断每个指标是否真正衡量该计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1825,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pressure_injury_prevention_mobility_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.355","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.355.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.355.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[317,429],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,119],"fullStemEn":"On postoperative day 2 after hip hemiarthroplasty, an 82-year-old client has an improving coccygeal Stage 1 pressure injury, improved mobility and voiding, persistent limited intake, and a new intact non-blanchable right heel area exactly where a shifted heel-suspension boot strap contacted the posterior calcaneus. Complete the bow-tie by choosing the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"髋关节半置换术后第2天，一名82岁患者尾骨1期压力性损伤正在改善，活动和排尿改善，但摄入仍有限，并在右足跟出现新的完整皮肤不可褪色区域，位置正好是移位足跟悬吊靴绑带接触后跟骨处。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能情况、两个优先措施和两个监测参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by choosing the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能情况、两个优先措施和两个监测参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"On postoperative day 2 after hip hemiarthroplasty, an 82-year-old client has an improving coccygeal Stage 1 pressure injury, improved mobility and voiding, persistent limited intake, and a new intact non-blanchable right heel area exactly where a shifted heel-suspension boot strap contacted the posterior calcaneus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"髋关节半置换术后第2天，一名82岁患者尾骨1期压力性损伤正在改善，活动和排尿改善，但摄入仍有限，并在右足跟出现新的完整皮肤不可褪色区域，位置正好是移位足跟悬吊靴绑带接触后跟骨处。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_skin","en":"Impaired skin integrity with evolving pressure-injury risk, including device-related heel injury","zh":"皮肤完整性受损并存在进展性压力性损伤风险，包括器械相关足跟损伤"},{"id":"bt_cond_ssi","en":"Surgical-site infection causing the skin changes","zh":"手术切口感染导致皮肤改变"},{"id":"bt_cond_dvt","en":"Deep vein thrombosis presenting as lower-extremity skin changes","zh":"深静脉血栓表现为下肢皮肤改变"}],"correct":"bt_cond_skin"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_action_nutrition","en":"Intensify nutritional support with dietitian follow-up, high-protein supplements, and intake goals","zh":"通过营养师跟进、高蛋白补充和摄入目标来加强营养支持"},{"id":"bt_action_stopturns","en":"Discontinue q2h repositioning because she is now getting out of bed several times daily","zh":"因患者现在每天能多次下床，停止每2小时翻身"},{"id":"bt_action_offload","en":"Correct right heel offloading immediately and verify the heel is fully floated at every repositioning","zh":"立即纠正右足跟减压，并每次翻身确认足跟完全悬空"},{"id":"bt_action_sameboot","en":"Simply reposition the same heel boot without inspecting the heel or changing the offloading method","zh":"只重新摆放同一只足跟保护靴，不检查足跟，也不改变减压方式"}],"correct":["bt_action_offload","bt_action_nutrition"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_param_spirometry","en":"Incentive spirometry volumes as the main indicator of pressure-injury healing","zh":"将激励式肺量计容量作为压力性损伤愈合的主要指标"},{"id":"bt_param_hgb","en":"Hemoglobin trend as the main indicator of skin-plan effectiveness","zh":"将血红蛋白趋势作为皮肤护理计划效果的主要指标"},{"id":"bt_param_intake","en":"Meal and supplement intake compared with dietitian calorie/protein goals","zh":"餐食和补充品摄入量与营养师热量/蛋白目标的比较"},{"id":"bt_param_skin","en":"Serial skin assessments of coccyx and right heel: size, color, blanchability, warmth, and integrity","zh":"连续评估尾骨和右足跟皮肤：大小、颜色、可褪色情况、温度和完整性"}],"correct":["bt_param_skin","bt_param_intake"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The resolved picture is pressure-injury risk with both improvement and failure: the sacral Stage 1 site is smaller, but a new device-related heel Stage 1 injury proves the offloading plan needs modification. Nutrition remains a healing-risk domain. Monitoring should track the actual skin sites and whether nutritional intake meets goals.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最终图像是压力性损伤风险中既有改善也有失败：骶尾部1期区域缩小，但新的器械相关足跟1期损伤证明减压计划需要调整。营养仍是愈合风险领域。监测应跟踪实际皮肤部位，以及营养摄入是否达到目标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, match the condition to the finding that explains the whole pattern, then choose actions and parameters that directly change or measure that condition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，要让“最可能情况”解释整个模式，然后选择能直接改变或衡量该情况的措施和参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1826,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.356","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.356.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.356.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[76,156],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,34],"fullStemEn":"The nurse manager reviews incident-report excerpts from the previous shift. Highlight the entry that describes a confidentiality breach requiring follow-up.","fullStemZh":"护士长查看上一班的事件报告摘录。请标出描述保密违规、需要跟进的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that describes a confidentiality breach requiring follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出描述保密违规、需要跟进的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse manager reviews incident-report excerpts from the previous shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士长查看上一班的事件报告摘录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Incident log excerpt:","zh":"事件记录摘录："},{"id":"s2","en":"A visitor asked for an update at the nurses' station; staff directed the visitor to speak with the client.","zh":"一名访客在护士站询问病情；工作人员请该访客与患者本人沟通。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Two staff members discussed a client's HIV diagnosis in a public elevator while visitors were present.","zh":"两名工作人员在有访客在场的公共电梯里讨论一名患者的 HIV 诊断。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse closed the privacy curtain before assisting a client with perineal care.","zh":"护士在协助患者进行会阴护理前拉上了隐私帘。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The charge nurse moved a printed report from the medication room counter to the locked shred bin.","zh":"责任护士将放在配药室台面上的打印报告移到上锁的碎纸箱中。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Discussing a client's diagnosis in a public elevator where visitors can hear is an unauthorized disclosure of protected health information and requires follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在访客可能听到的公共电梯里讨论患者诊断，属于未经授权披露受保护健康信息，需要跟进处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For confidentiality questions, look for disclosure of identifiable health information to someone without authorization or a need to know.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到保密题时，重点寻找是否把可识别的健康信息透露给未授权或无知情必要的人。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1827,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.357","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.357.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.357.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[92,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,43],"fullStemEn":"A nurse audits transfer handoff notes for clients discharged to skilled nursing facilities. Highlight the note that contains a missing handoff element requiring correction before transfer.","fullStemZh":"护士审核转往专业护理机构患者的交接记录。请标出包含交接信息缺失、转运前必须更正的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the note that contains a missing handoff element requiring correction before transfer.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出包含交接信息缺失、转运前必须更正的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse audits transfer handoff notes for clients discharged to skilled nursing facilities.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士审核转往专业护理机构患者的交接记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Transfer handoff audit:","zh":"转运交接审核："},{"id":"s2","en":"Client A: Medication reconciliation completed; last dose times listed for scheduled medications.","zh":"患者 A：已完成用药核对；列出了定时用药的末次给药时间。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Client B: Wound care order attached; dressing type and next change time documented.","zh":"患者 B：已附伤口护理医嘱；记录了敷料类型和下次更换时间。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Client C: Blood culture result is expected tomorrow; pending result and follow-up provider were not listed in the receiving-facility handoff.","zh":"患者 C：血培养结果预计明天出；交给接收机构的交接中未列出待出结果及负责跟进的医师。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Client D: Family will bring eyeglasses and dentures; belongings list placed in the discharge packet.","zh":"患者 D：家属会带来眼镜和假牙；物品清单已放入出院资料包。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A pending diagnostic result must be communicated during transfer, including who will follow up. Omitting it creates a risk that an abnormal result will not be acted on.","rationaleCorrectZh":"转运交接时必须说明待出的诊断结果以及由谁负责跟进。遗漏该信息会造成异常结果无人处理的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In handoff questions, prioritize unresolved clinical tasks: pending tests, follow-up responsibility, medication changes, and safety needs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"交接题要优先关注未完成的临床任务：待出检查、跟进责任、用药变化和安全需求。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1828,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.358","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.358.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.358.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[312,347],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,98],"fullStemEn":"The nurse receives a discharge order for a client who cannot obtain prescribed home oxygen until the next day. The client becomes short of breath when walking to the bathroom. Per facility policy, unresolved unsafe discharge concerns are escalated through the chain of command after the prescriber is contacted. Place the nurse's actions in order.","fullStemZh":"护士收到一名患者的出院医嘱，但该患者要到第二天才能取得处方的家庭氧气；患者步行到卫生间时会气短。根据机构政策，护士联系开医嘱者后，若不安全出院问题仍未解决，应按指挥链上报。请按顺序排列护士的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护士的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per facility policy, unresolved unsafe discharge concerns are escalated through the chain of command after the prescriber is contacted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据机构政策，护士联系开医嘱者后，若不安全出院问题仍未解决，应按指挥链上报。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Escalate to the nursing supervisor according to the facility chain-of-command policy.","zh":"根据机构指挥链政策向护理主管上报。"},{"id":"B","en":"Contact the prescriber with the safety concern and request clarification of the discharge order.","zh":"联系开医嘱者，说明安全问题，并请求澄清出院医嘱。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the charge nurse and case manager that the unsafe discharge issue remains unresolved.","zh":"通知责任护士和个案管理人员，不安全出院问题仍未解决。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's current respiratory status and keep the client safe in the unit.","zh":"评估患者当前呼吸状态，并确保患者在病区内安全。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document objective assessment findings, notifications, responses, and the current discharge plan.","zh":"记录客观评估结果、通知对象、对方回应以及当前出院计划。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse begins with assessment and safety, then contacts the prescriber to clarify the unsafe discharge order. If the issue remains unresolved, the nurse uses the chain of command and documents objective facts and responses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士从评估和维持安全开始，然后联系开医嘱者澄清不安全的出院医嘱。若问题仍未解决，再按指挥链上报，并记录客观事实和各方回应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For escalation sequences, protect the client, communicate to the responsible provider, then move up the chain of command if the risk remains unresolved.","testTakingStrategyZh":"上报流程题中，保护患者，与负责医嘱者沟通；若风险未解决，再逐级按指挥链上报。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1829,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.359","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.359.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.359.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[267,325],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,82],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews a provider order set for a hospitalized client. The chart contains a signed, scanned directive stating do-not-resuscitate and do-not-intubate preferences. Facility policy requires code-status conflicts to be clarified before orders are implemented. Highlight the order-set entry that requires clarification.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名住院患者的医嘱集。病历中有已签署并扫描的指示文件，说明患者选择不复苏和不插管。机构政策要求在执行医嘱前澄清任何代码状态冲突。请标出需要澄清的医嘱集条目。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the order-set entry that requires clarification.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要澄清的医嘱集条目。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires code-status conflicts to be clarified before orders are implemented.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策要求在执行医嘱前澄清任何代码状态冲突。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Provider order set:","zh":"医嘱集："},{"id":"s2","en":"Diet: regular diet as tolerated after bedside swallow screen.","zh":"饮食：床旁吞咽筛查后按耐受情况给予普通饮食。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Code status: Full code; perform resuscitation and intubation if clinically indicated.","zh":"代码状态：全力抢救；如有临床指征，进行复苏和插管。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Activity: assist with ambulation until gait is steady.","zh":"活动：步态稳定前协助下床行走。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Consult: case management for discharge equipment needs.","zh":"会诊：请个案管理评估出院设备需求。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A full-code order conflicts with the signed directive for do-not-resuscitate and do-not-intubate preferences. The nurse should clarify the conflict before implementing the order set.","rationaleCorrectZh":"全力抢救医嘱与已签署的不复苏、不插管意愿相冲突。护士应在执行医嘱集前澄清该冲突。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an advance directive is present, identify any order that conflicts with the client's expressed treatment preferences and seek clarification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有预立医疗指示时，要找出与患者已表达治疗意愿冲突的医嘱，并请求澄清。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1830,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.360","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.360.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.360.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,41],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse reviews shift notes after a reported staff conflict. Highlight the entry that requires follow-up for unprofessional conflict behavior.","fullStemZh":"责任护士在收到员工冲突报告后查看班次记录。请标出需要因不专业冲突行为而跟进的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that requires follow-up for unprofessional conflict behavior.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要因不专业冲突行为而跟进的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse reviews shift notes after a reported staff conflict.","penultimateSentenceZh":"责任护士在收到员工冲突报告后查看班次记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Shift conflict notes:","zh":"班次冲突记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"The RN asked the respiratory therapist to step into the report room to discuss conflicting oxygen-weaning recommendations.","zh":"注册护士请呼吸治疗师到交班室讨论氧气减量建议不一致的问题。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The RN told the UAP in the hallway, 'If you question me again, I will make sure you never work this unit.' Family members were nearby.","zh":"注册护士在走廊对护理助理说：“你要是再质疑我，我会让你再也不能在这个病区工作。”旁边有家属。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The LPN stated, 'I am concerned we are using different intake totals; can we compare the flowsheet entries?'","zh":"执业护士说：“我担心我们使用的摄入量总数不一致；能否一起核对护理记录单？”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The charge nurse scheduled a brief huddle so both staff members could clarify the plan away from client rooms.","zh":"责任护士安排了简短讨论，让两名员工在患者房间外澄清计划。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Threatening a coworker in a public area is unprofessional, can intimidate staff, and may affect client safety and team communication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在公共区域威胁同事是不专业行为，可能恐吓员工，并影响患者安全和团队沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For conflict-resolution items, separate assertive, private communication from threats, blame, or public confrontation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理冲突题时，要区分坚定且私下的沟通，以及威胁、指责或公开冲突。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1831,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.361","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.361.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.361.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,61],"fullStemEn":"A nurse and another staff member disagree about who will call a client's family with a routine update. Their disagreement is becoming tense at the nurses' station. Place the nurse's actions in order to resolve the conflict professionally.","fullStemZh":"护士与另一名工作人员就谁给患者家属进行常规更新发生分歧，且在护士站气氛变得紧张。请按顺序排列护士以专业方式解决冲突的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in order to resolve the conflict professionally.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护士以专业方式解决冲突的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Their disagreement is becoming tense at the nurses' station.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士与另一名工作人员就谁给患者家属进行常规更新发生分歧，且在护士站气氛变得紧张。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"State the concern using objective language focused on the family update.","zh":"用客观语言说明问题，重点放在给家属更新信息这件事上。"},{"id":"A","en":"Move the discussion away from the public nurses' station.","zh":"将讨论移到公共护士站以外的地方。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the other staff member to describe their understanding of the plan.","zh":"请另一名工作人员说明其对计划的理解。"},{"id":"D","en":"Agree on who will call the family and what information may be shared.","zh":"商定由谁给家属打电话以及可分享哪些信息。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Professional conflict resolution protects privacy, uses objective language, invites the other person's perspective, and ends with a clear shared plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"专业解决冲突应保护隐私，使用客观语言，了解对方观点，并形成明确的共同计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In workplace-conflict sequences, choose actions that reduce public tension, clarify facts, listen, and create a shared plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"职场冲突排序题中，应选择能降低公开紧张气氛、澄清事实、倾听并形成共同计划的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1832,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.362","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.362.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.362.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,36],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews discharge-instruction documentation before a client leaves the unit. Highlight the entry that requires client advocacy before discharge.","fullStemZh":"护士在患者离开病区前查看出院指导记录。请标出出院前需要为患者倡导的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that requires client advocacy before discharge.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出出院前需要为患者倡导的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews discharge-instruction documentation before a client leaves the unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在患者离开病区前查看出院指导记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Discharge-instruction documentation:","zh":"出院指导记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"Client correctly demonstrates use of the walker and states when to call the clinic.","zh":"患者能正确示范助行器使用，并说明何时联系门诊。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Client says, 'I cannot read English well.' Printed instructions are available only in English; no interpreter or translated instructions were requested.","zh":"患者说：“我英文读得不好。”打印指导只有英文版本；未申请口译员或翻译版指导。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Client's spouse will pick up the discharge prescriptions from the pharmacy after leaving the unit.","zh":"患者配偶将在离开病区后到药房领取出院处方。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Client identifies the follow-up appointment date and transportation plan.","zh":"患者能说出复诊日期和交通安排。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A client who cannot read the discharge language needs accessible education, such as interpreter support and translated instructions, before leaving the unit.","rationaleCorrectZh":"如果患者无法阅读出院指导所用语言，出院前需要可理解的教育，例如口译支持和翻译版指导。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Advocacy items often turn on whether the client can actually understand, access, or consent to the plan being implemented.","testTakingStrategyZh":"患者倡导题常考患者是否真正能理解、获得或同意正在执行的计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1833,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.363","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.363.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.363.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,52],"fullStemEn":"The emergency department is notified that a bus crash will bring multiple clients within 15 minutes. The charge nurse is coordinating the initial unit response. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"急诊科接到通知，15 分钟内会有多名公交车事故伤者到达。责任护士正在协调科室初始应对。请按顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse is coordinating the initial unit response.","penultimateSentenceZh":"责任护士正在协调科室初始应对。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Assign team members to triage, treatment areas, documentation, and family communication roles.","zh":"分派团队成员负责分诊、治疗区域、记录和家属沟通角色。"},{"id":"F","en":"Continue situation updates through the incident-command communication channel.","zh":"通过事件指挥沟通渠道持续更新现场情况。"},{"id":"B","en":"Identify currently available beds, staff, supplies, and critical equipment.","zh":"确认当前可用床位、人员、物资和关键设备。"},{"id":"E","en":"Receive arriving clients through the disaster triage process.","zh":"通过灾难分诊流程接收陆续到达的伤者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Move stable clients who meet criteria to designated discharge or holding areas.","zh":"将符合条件的稳定患者转至指定出院区或留观区。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the facility disaster plan and report to the assigned incident-command role.","zh":"启动机构灾难预案，并向指定的事件指挥角色报到。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The initial disaster response uses the facility plan and incident-command structure, rapidly determines capacity, creates space, assigns roles, triages incoming clients, and keeps communication centralized.","rationaleCorrectZh":"初始灾难应对应按照机构预案和事件指挥结构进行，迅速确认容量、腾出空间、分配角色、对到达伤者进行分诊，并保持集中沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For disaster-response sequences, look for activation of the plan, resource assessment, role assignment, triage, and centralized communication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"灾难应对排序题中，寻找启动预案、评估资源、分配角色、分诊以及集中沟通。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1834,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.364","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.364.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.364.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[237,308],"terminalOffsetsZh":[71,86],"fullStemEn":"The night charge nurse reviews escalation-chain notes. Per facility policy, a nurse must notify the nursing supervisor when a prescriber cannot be reached for a time-sensitive safety concern after two contact attempts within 20 minutes. Highlight the entry that requires escalation to the nursing supervisor.","fullStemZh":"夜班责任护士查看上报链记录。根据机构政策，对于有时间敏感性的安全问题，如果 20 分钟内两次联系开医嘱者仍无法取得联系，护士必须通知护理主管。请标出需要上报护理主管的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that requires escalation to the nursing supervisor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要上报护理主管的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per facility policy, a nurse must notify the nursing supervisor when a prescriber cannot be reached for a time-sensitive safety concern after two contact attempts within 20 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据机构政策，对于有时间敏感性的安全问题，如果 20 分钟内两次联系开医嘱者仍无法取得联系，护士必须通知护理主管。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Escalation-chain notes:","zh":"上报链记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"Client A: PRN sleep medication request; prescriber paged once 5 minutes ago; client resting quietly.","zh":"患者 A：请求按需睡眠药；5 分钟前已呼叫开医嘱者一次；患者安静休息。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Client B: Family requests routine update after visiting hours; provider message sent to day team.","zh":"患者 B：家属在探视时间后请求常规更新；已将信息发给白班团队。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Client C: New confusion and pulled central-line dressing; prescriber paged twice over 25 minutes with no response.","zh":"患者 C：新发意识混乱并拉扯中心静脉导管敷料；25 分钟内两次呼叫开医嘱者均无回应。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Client D: Discharge ride delayed until morning; case management follow-up already scheduled.","zh":"患者 D：出院接送延迟到早上；个案管理跟进已安排。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New confusion with disruption of a central-line dressing is a time-sensitive safety concern. The prescriber has not responded after two attempts beyond the facility time frame, so escalation to the nursing supervisor is required.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新发意识混乱并破坏中心静脉导管敷料属于时间敏感的安全问题。开医嘱者在机构规定时间后两次联系仍无回应，因此必须上报护理主管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a facility escalation rule is given, match the facts in the note to every part of the rule: safety risk, contact attempts, and time frame.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干给出机构上报规则时，要把记录事实与规则的每一部分对应：安全风险、联系次数和时间范围。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1835,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_moc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.365","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.365.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.365.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,67],"fullStemEn":"A client is being discharged after a new ostomy creation. The home-health agency can see the client tomorrow, but the client states, 'I watched the video, but I have not practiced changing the pouch.' Place the nurse's discharge workflow actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者造口术后准备出院。居家护理机构明天可以上门，但患者说：“我看过视频，但还没有练习更换造口袋。”请按顺序排列护士的出院流程行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's discharge workflow actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护士的出院流程行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The home-health agency can see the client tomorrow, but the client states, 'I watched the video, but I have not practiced changing the pouch.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"居家护理机构明天可以上门，但患者说：“我看过视频，但还没有练习更换造口袋。”","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client's current understanding and readiness to perform ostomy care.","zh":"评估患者当前对造口护理的理解和操作准备程度。"},{"id":"B","en":"Provide hands-on teaching and have the client demonstrate pouch emptying and changing.","zh":"提供动手教学，并让患者示范清空和更换造口袋。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the teaching, return demonstration, remaining barriers, and follow-up plan.","zh":"记录教学内容、回示操作、仍存在的障碍和跟进计划。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the provider and case manager if the client cannot safely demonstrate required care.","zh":"如果患者无法安全示范必要护理，通知医师和个案管理人员。"},{"id":"C","en":"Clarify the home-health visit date, supply plan, and contact number in the discharge instructions.","zh":"在出院指导中明确居家护理上门日期、用品计划和联系电话。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A safe discharge workflow assesses the learning gap, provides hands-on teaching with return demonstration, confirms follow-up and supplies, notifies the care team if the client cannot perform required care, and documents the plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全出院流程应评估学习缺口，进行动手教学并要求回示，确认随访和用品安排；若患者无法完成必要护理，则通知照护团队，并记录计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge teaching sequences, assess the need, teach and verify skill performance, confirm resources, escalate barriers, and document the final plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出院教学排序题中，应评估需求，教学并确认技能表现，确认资源，上报障碍，并记录最终计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1836,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.366","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.366.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.366.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[401,422],"terminalOffsetsZh":[119,125],"fullStemEn":"A client takes warfarin 5 mg by mouth nightly for atrial fibrillation. The client started trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole 3 days ago. Today the INR is 6.8, and the client reports black, tarry stool and dizziness when standing. Unit protocol states: notify the provider for INR greater than 4.5 or suspected bleeding, and do not administer the next warfarin dose until the provider evaluates the client. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因房颤每晚口服华法林 5 mg。3 天前开始服用甲氧苄啶-磺胺甲噁唑。今天 INR 为 6.8，患者报告黑色柏油样大便，站立时头晕。病区流程规定：INR 大于 4.5 或疑似出血时通知医嘱提供者；在提供者评估前不要给下一剂华法林。完成领结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成领结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unit protocol states: notify the provider for INR greater than 4.5 or suspected bleeding, and do not administer the next warfarin dose until the provider evaluates the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区流程规定：INR 大于 4.5 或疑似出血时通知医嘱提供者；在提供者评估前不要给下一剂华法林。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1_c3","en":"Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia","zh":"肝素诱导性血小板减少"},{"id":"q1_c2","en":"Subtherapeutic anticoagulation","zh":"抗凝不足"},{"id":"q1_c1","en":"Warfarin over-anticoagulation with suspected gastrointestinal bleeding","zh":"华法林抗凝过度并疑似胃肠道出血"},{"id":"q1_c4","en":"New thromboembolism despite therapy","zh":"治疗期间新发血栓栓塞"}],"correct":"q1_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1_a4","en":"Encourage vigorous flossing to assess gum bleeding","zh":"鼓励用力使用牙线以评估牙龈出血"},{"id":"q1_a3","en":"Administer the next warfarin dose to prevent stroke","zh":"为预防卒中继续给予下一剂华法林"},{"id":"q1_a2","en":"Notify the provider with the INR and bleeding findings","zh":"将 INR 和出血表现报告给医嘱提供者"},{"id":"q1_a1","en":"Hold the scheduled warfarin dose per protocol","zh":"按流程暂停预定的华法林剂量"}],"correct":["q1_a1","q1_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1_p2","en":"Blood pressure, heart rate, and visible bleeding","zh":"血压、心率和可见出血"},{"id":"q1_p3","en":"aPTT as the primary anticoagulation target","zh":"将 aPTT 作为主要抗凝目标"},{"id":"q1_p4","en":"Fasting blood glucose before meals","zh":"餐前空腹血糖"},{"id":"q1_p1","en":"INR trend","zh":"INR 变化趋势"}],"correct":["q1_p1","q1_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The very elevated INR plus black, tarry stool and dizziness indicates warfarin over-anticoagulation with suspected bleeding. The stated protocol supports holding warfarin and notifying the provider while monitoring coagulation and bleeding status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"INR 明显升高，加上黑色柏油样大便和站立头晕，提示华法林抗凝过度并疑似出血。题干给出的流程支持暂停华法林并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测凝血和出血状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link the medication, interacting drug, lab value, and symptom cluster. For warfarin, a very high INR plus bleeding cues means hold and escalate according to protocol.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把药物、相互作用药物、实验室数值和症状组合起来判断。华法林患者 INR 很高并有出血线索时，应按流程暂停并上报。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1837,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.367","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.367.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.367.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[302,323],"terminalOffsetsZh":[109,115],"fullStemEn":"A client who takes clozapine 300 mg nightly calls the clinic reporting fever, sore throat, and mouth ulcers. Same-day laboratory results show an absolute neutrophil count of 650/mm3. The clinic protocol states: hold clozapine and notify the prescriber for ANC less than 1000/mm3 or infection symptoms. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名每晚服用氯氮平 300 mg 的患者致电门诊，报告发热、咽痛和口腔溃疡。当天实验室结果显示绝对中性粒细胞计数为 650/mm3。门诊流程规定：ANC 低于 1000/mm3 或出现感染症状时暂停氯氮平并通知处方者。完成领结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成领结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The clinic protocol states: hold clozapine and notify the prescriber for ANC less than 1000/mm3 or infection symptoms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"门诊流程规定：ANC 低于 1000/mm3 或出现感染症状时暂停氯氮平并通知处方者。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2_c2","en":"Serotonin syndrome","zh":"血清素综合征"},{"id":"q2_c1","en":"Clozapine-associated severe neutropenia","zh":"氯氮平相关重度中性粒细胞减少"},{"id":"q2_c3","en":"Lithium toxicity","zh":"锂中毒"},{"id":"q2_c4","en":"Expected anticholinergic effect","zh":"预期的抗胆碱能反应"}],"correct":"q2_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2_a1","en":"Hold clozapine per protocol","zh":"按流程暂停氯氮平"},{"id":"q2_a4","en":"Encourage attending a crowded group activity for mood support","zh":"鼓励参加人群密集的小组活动以获得情绪支持"},{"id":"q2_a3","en":"Advise taking clozapine with a snack and reassessing next month","zh":"建议与点心同服氯氮平，并下个月再评估"},{"id":"q2_a2","en":"Notify the prescriber and report ANC, fever, and sore throat","zh":"通知处方者并报告 ANC、发热和咽痛"}],"correct":["q2_a1","q2_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2_p4","en":"Peak and trough clozapine levels before each dose","zh":"每次给药前的氯氮平峰谷浓度"},{"id":"q2_p1","en":"Absolute neutrophil count trend","zh":"绝对中性粒细胞计数趋势"},{"id":"q2_p2","en":"Temperature and new infection symptoms","zh":"体温和新的感染症状"},{"id":"q2_p3","en":"Serum lithium concentration","zh":"血清锂浓度"}],"correct":["q2_p1","q2_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clozapine can cause severe neutropenia. Fever, sore throat, mouth ulcers, and ANC 650/mm3 meet the stated protocol for holding clozapine and notifying the prescriber.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氯氮平可导致重度中性粒细胞减少。发热、咽痛、口腔溃疡和 ANC 650/mm3 符合题干流程中暂停氯氮平并通知处方者的条件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For clozapine, infection symptoms plus a low ANC are a medication emergency cue. Use the protocol threshold in the stem rather than relying on memory alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到氯氮平时，感染症状加低 ANC 是药物安全的紧急线索。优先使用题干给出的流程阈值，而不是只凭记忆。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1838,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.368","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.368.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.368.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[367,388],"terminalOffsetsZh":[132,138],"fullStemEn":"A client takes lithium carbonate 900 mg/day for bipolar disorder. Hydrochlorothiazide was started 1 week ago. The client now has vomiting, coarse hand tremor, unsteady gait, and new confusion. Serum lithium is 2.1 mEq/L. Unit protocol states: hold lithium and notify the provider for lithium level 1.5 mEq/L or higher, new neurologic changes, or persistent vomiting. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名双相障碍患者每日服用碳酸锂 900 mg。1 周前开始服用氢氯噻嗪。患者现在出现呕吐、明显手颤、步态不稳和新发意识混乱。血清锂浓度为 2.1 mEq/L。病区流程规定：锂浓度达到或超过 1.5 mEq/L、新发神经系统改变或持续呕吐时暂停锂剂并通知医嘱提供者。完成领结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成领结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unit protocol states: hold lithium and notify the provider for lithium level 1.5 mEq/L or higher, new neurologic changes, or persistent vomiting.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区流程规定：锂浓度达到或超过 1.5 mEq/L、新发神经系统改变或持续呕吐时暂停锂剂并通知医嘱提供者。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3_c3","en":"Clozapine-associated neutropenia","zh":"氯氮平相关中性粒细胞减少"},{"id":"q3_c1","en":"Lithium toxicity","zh":"锂中毒"},{"id":"q3_c2","en":"Expected lithium therapeutic effect","zh":"锂剂的预期治疗作用"},{"id":"q3_c4","en":"Warfarin over-anticoagulation","zh":"华法林抗凝过度"}],"correct":"q3_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3_a1","en":"Hold lithium per protocol","zh":"按流程暂停锂剂"},{"id":"q3_a2","en":"Notify the provider with lithium level and neurologic findings","zh":"向医嘱提供者报告锂浓度和神经系统表现"},{"id":"q3_a4","en":"Teach strict sodium restriction during vomiting","zh":"指导患者呕吐期间严格限制钠摄入"},{"id":"q3_a3","en":"Give the next lithium dose with food","zh":"将下一剂锂剂与食物同服"}],"correct":["q3_a1","q3_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3_p3","en":"Serum digoxin level","zh":"血清地高辛浓度"},{"id":"q3_p4","en":"Peak insulin action after meals","zh":"餐后胰岛素作用峰值"},{"id":"q3_p1","en":"Neurologic status, tremor, and gait safety","zh":"神经状态、震颤和步态安全"},{"id":"q3_p2","en":"Serum lithium level and renal function results","zh":"血清锂浓度和肾功能结果"}],"correct":["q3_p1","q3_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The lithium level of 2.1 mEq/L with vomiting, coarse tremor, ataxia, and confusion is consistent with lithium toxicity. The stated protocol directs the nurse to hold lithium and notify the provider while monitoring neurologic and renal-related parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锂浓度 2.1 mEq/L 加上呕吐、明显震颤、共济失调样步态和意识混乱，符合锂中毒。题干流程要求护士暂停锂剂并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测神经和肾功能相关指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a medication has a narrow therapeutic index, treat new neurologic changes and a high drug level as toxicity until proven otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"窄治疗指数药物出现新发神经系统改变并伴药物浓度升高时，应先按中毒处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1839,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.369","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.369.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.369.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving parenteral nutrition requires follow-up for a metabolic complication.","fullStemZh":"一名接受肠外营养的患者需要因代谢并发症进行跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client receiving parenteral nutrition requires follow-up for a metabolic complication.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名接受肠外营养的患者需要因代谢并发症进行跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"A client has parenteral nutrition infusing through a central line at 80 mL/hr. Six hours after initiation, the capillary glucose is 328 mg/dL, and the client reports thirst and frequent urination. The unit protocol states: notify the provider for glucose greater than 300 mg/dL and administer prescribed correction insulin per scale; do not abruptly stop parenteral nutrition unless directed. The nurse should recognize {{d1}}, then {{d2}}, while monitoring {{d3}}.","zh":"一名患者经中心静脉以 80 mL/小时输注肠外营养。开始 6 小时后，床旁血糖为 328 mg/dL，患者诉口渴并尿频。病区流程规定：血糖大于 300 mg/dL 时通知医嘱提供者，并按处方校正胰岛素量表给药；除非有指示，不要突然停止肠外营养。护士应识别为 {{d1}}，随后 {{d2}}，同时监测 {{d3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"d1_o1","en":"parenteral-nutrition-associated hyperglycemia","zh":"肠外营养相关高血糖"},{"id":"d1_o3","en":"fat embolism","zh":"脂肪栓塞"},{"id":"d1_o2","en":"hypoglycemia from abrupt parenteral nutrition discontinuation","zh":"肠外营养突然停止导致的低血糖"},{"id":"d1_o4","en":"allergic reaction to insulin","zh":"对胰岛素的过敏反应"}],"correct":"d1_o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"d2_o2","en":"stop the parenteral nutrition and saline-lock the central line","zh":"停止肠外营养并将中心静脉管路盐水封管"},{"id":"d2_o4","en":"wait for routine morning laboratory results before acting","zh":"等待常规晨间实验室结果后再处理"},{"id":"d2_o3","en":"increase the parenteral nutrition rate to improve calorie delivery","zh":"提高肠外营养速度以增加热量供给"},{"id":"d2_o1","en":"notify the provider and give prescribed correction insulin per protocol","zh":"通知医嘱提供者，并按流程给予处方校正胰岛素"}],"correct":"d2_o1"},{"id":"d3","options":[{"id":"d3_o4","en":"peak and trough antibiotic levels","zh":"抗生素峰谷浓度"},{"id":"d3_o2","en":"pupillary response and intracranial pressure","zh":"瞳孔反应和颅内压"},{"id":"d3_o1","en":"capillary glucose and hydration status","zh":"床旁血糖和水合状态"},{"id":"d3_o3","en":"aPTT and platelet count","zh":"aPTT 和血小板计数"}],"correct":"d3_o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Parenteral nutrition contains concentrated dextrose and can cause hyperglycemia. The stated protocol directs provider notification and prescribed correction insulin for glucose greater than 300 mg/dL, with ongoing monitoring of glucose and hydration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肠外营养含高浓度葡萄糖，可导致高血糖。题干流程规定血糖大于 300 mg/dL 时通知医嘱提供者并给予处方校正胰岛素，同时持续监测血糖和水合状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the protocol value embedded in the stem. A glucose value beyond the stated threshold plus osmotic symptoms points to hyperglycemia requiring action, not observation alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干给出的流程数值。血糖超过阈值并伴渗透性症状时，提示高血糖，需要处理，而不是单纯观察。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1840,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.370","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.370.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.370.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[602,623],"terminalOffsetsZh":[189,195],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes is scheduled to receive insulin glargine 24 units at bedtime and insulin lispro 6 units with dinner. The nurse discovers that another nurse accidentally administered insulin lispro 24 units instead of insulin glargine 24 units 10 minutes ago. The client is awake and reports feeling shaky. Bedside glucose is 92 mg/dL. Unit protocol states: for rapid-acting insulin dose errors, notify the provider, initiate the hypoglycemia monitoring protocol, keep a rapid carbohydrate source available, and check bedside glucose every 15 minutes for at least 1 hour or as prescribed. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名 1 型糖尿病患者睡前应接受甘精胰岛素 24 单位，并在晚餐时接受赖脯胰岛素 6 单位。护士发现另一名护士 10 分钟前误将赖脯胰岛素 24 单位当作甘精胰岛素 24 单位给予。患者清醒，诉发抖。床旁血糖为 92 mg/dL。病区流程规定：发生速效胰岛素剂量错误时，应通知医嘱提供者，启动低血糖监测流程，备好快速碳水来源，并至少 1 小时或按医嘱每 15 分钟复查床旁血糖。完成领结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成领结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unit protocol states: for rapid-acting insulin dose errors, notify the provider, initiate the hypoglycemia monitoring protocol, keep a rapid carbohydrate source available, and check bedside glucose every 15 minutes for at least 1 hour or as prescribed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区流程规定：发生速效胰岛素剂量错误时，应通知医嘱提供者，启动低血糖监测流程，备好快速碳水来源，并至少 1 小时或按医嘱每 15 分钟复查床旁血糖。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely complication","zh":"最可能的并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"q5_c3","en":"Expected postprandial glucose rise","zh":"预期的餐后血糖升高"},{"id":"q5_c2","en":"Diabetic ketoacidosis from missed basal insulin only","zh":"仅因漏用基础胰岛素导致的糖尿病酮症酸中毒"},{"id":"q5_c1","en":"Impending hypoglycemia from rapid-acting insulin overdose","zh":"速效胰岛素过量导致的即将发生低血糖"},{"id":"q5_c4","en":"Allergic reaction to insulin","zh":"胰岛素过敏反应"}],"correct":"q5_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q5_a1","en":"Notify the provider about the rapid-acting insulin dose error","zh":"将速效胰岛素剂量错误通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"q5_a4","en":"Leave the client alone to rest because the glucose is above 70 mg/dL","zh":"因血糖高于 70 mg/dL，让患者独自休息"},{"id":"q5_a3","en":"Give the missed glargine dose immediately without provider input","zh":"不经医嘱提供者确认，立即补给漏用的甘精胰岛素"},{"id":"q5_a2","en":"Initiate the unit hypoglycemia monitoring protocol","zh":"启动病区低血糖监测流程"}],"correct":["q5_a1","q5_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q5_p3","en":"Daily hemoglobin A1c","zh":"每日糖化血红蛋白"},{"id":"q5_p4","en":"Peak serum warfarin level","zh":"血清华法林峰值浓度"},{"id":"q5_p2","en":"Sweating, tremor, confusion, and ability to swallow","zh":"出汗、震颤、意识混乱和吞咽能力"},{"id":"q5_p1","en":"Bedside glucose every 15 minutes per protocol","zh":"按流程每 15 分钟复查床旁血糖"}],"correct":["q5_p1","q5_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A large unintended dose of rapid-acting insulin creates a high risk for hypoglycemia even before the glucose falls below 70 mg/dL. The stated protocol supports provider notification, hypoglycemia monitoring, and frequent bedside glucose checks.","rationaleCorrectZh":"误给大剂量速效胰岛素会造成高低血糖风险，即使血糖尚未低于 70 mg/dL 也需要警惕。题干流程支持通知医嘱提供者、启动低血糖监测，并频繁复查床旁血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-alert medication errors, do not wait for harm to fully develop. Match the expected complication to the medication’s action and use the protocol in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到高警讯药物错误时，不要等到伤害完全出现才处理。把可能并发症与药物作用联系起来，并使用题干给出的流程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1841,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.371","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.371.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.371.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[480,501],"terminalOffsetsZh":[152,158],"fullStemEn":"A severely malnourished client started parenteral nutrition 18 hours ago. The client now reports new weakness and palpitations. Laboratory results show phosphorus 1.4 mg/dL, potassium 3.1 mEq/L, and magnesium 1.4 mg/dL. Unit protocol states: for phosphorus less than 1.8 mg/dL after nutrition initiation, notify the provider, anticipate prescribed electrolyte replacement, and place the client on cardiac monitoring if palpitations or significant electrolyte abnormalities occur. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名重度营养不良患者 18 小时前开始肠外营养。患者现在报告新发乏力和心悸。实验室结果显示磷 1.4 mg/dL、钾 3.1 mEq/L、镁 1.4 mg/dL。病区流程规定：开始营养支持后磷低于 1.8 mg/dL 时，通知医嘱提供者，预期按医嘱补充电解质；如出现心悸或明显电解质异常，应进行心电监测。完成领结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成领结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unit protocol states: for phosphorus less than 1.8 mg/dL after nutrition initiation, notify the provider, anticipate prescribed electrolyte replacement, and place the client on cardiac monitoring if palpitations or significant electrolyte abnormalities occur.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区流程规定：开始营养支持后磷低于 1.8 mg/dL 时，通知医嘱提供者，预期按医嘱补充电解质；如出现心悸或明显电解质异常，应进行心电监测。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely complication","zh":"最可能的并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"q6_c4","en":"Expected adaptation to parenteral nutrition","zh":"对肠外营养的预期适应"},{"id":"q6_c2","en":"Central-line air embolism","zh":"中心静脉空气栓塞"},{"id":"q6_c3","en":"Warfarin over-anticoagulation","zh":"华法林抗凝过度"},{"id":"q6_c1","en":"Refeeding-related electrolyte shift","zh":"再喂养相关电解质转移"}],"correct":"q6_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q6_a3","en":"Increase the parenteral nutrition rate to restore calories faster","zh":"提高肠外营养速度以更快恢复热量"},{"id":"q6_a1","en":"Notify the provider about the low phosphorus and symptoms","zh":"将低磷和症状报告给医嘱提供者"},{"id":"q6_a4","en":"Restrict all oral and intravenous electrolytes","zh":"限制所有口服和静脉电解质"},{"id":"q6_a2","en":"Prepare to administer prescribed electrolyte replacement","zh":"准备给予处方电解质补充"}],"correct":["q6_a1","q6_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q6_p2","en":"Heart rhythm and palpitations","zh":"心律和心悸情况"},{"id":"q6_p3","en":"International normalized ratio","zh":"国际标准化比值"},{"id":"q6_p4","en":"Pupillary light response every 5 minutes","zh":"每 5 分钟检查瞳孔对光反应"},{"id":"q6_p1","en":"Phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium levels","zh":"磷、钾和镁水平"}],"correct":["q6_p1","q6_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe malnutrition followed by nutrition initiation and low phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium suggests a refeeding-related electrolyte shift. The stated protocol supports provider notification, prescribed electrolyte replacement, and rhythm monitoring for palpitations or significant abnormalities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重度营养不良后开始营养支持，并出现低磷、低钾、低镁，提示再喂养相关电解质转移。题干流程支持通知医嘱提供者、按医嘱补充电解质，并因心悸或明显异常进行心律监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After nutrition starts in a severely malnourished client, connect new weakness or palpitations with low phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重度营养不良患者开始营养支持后，若出现新发乏力或心悸，要联想到低磷、低钾和低镁。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1842,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.372","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.372.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.372.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[434,455],"terminalOffsetsZh":[165,171],"fullStemEn":"A client takes digoxin 0.25 mg by mouth daily and furosemide 40 mg by mouth daily. The client reports nausea, seeing yellow halos around lights, and feeling unusually weak. The apical pulse is 52/min. Laboratory results show potassium 3.0 mEq/L and digoxin level 2.6 ng/mL. Unit protocol states: hold digoxin and notify the provider for apical pulse less than 60/min, digoxin level greater than 2.0 ng/mL, or new visual disturbances. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者每日口服地高辛 0.25 mg 和呋塞米 40 mg。患者报告恶心、看灯光时有黄色光圈，并感到异常乏力。心尖脉 52 次/分。实验室结果显示钾 3.0 mEq/L，地高辛浓度 2.6 ng/mL。病区流程规定：心尖脉低于 60 次/分、地高辛浓度高于 2.0 ng/mL 或出现新发视觉异常时，暂停地高辛并通知医嘱提供者。完成领结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成领结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unit protocol states: hold digoxin and notify the provider for apical pulse less than 60/min, digoxin level greater than 2.0 ng/mL, or new visual disturbances.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区流程规定：心尖脉低于 60 次/分、地高辛浓度高于 2.0 ng/mL 或出现新发视觉异常时，暂停地高辛并通知医嘱提供者。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q7_c3","en":"Clozapine-associated neutropenia","zh":"氯氮平相关中性粒细胞减少"},{"id":"q7_c2","en":"Therapeutic digoxin effect","zh":"地高辛治疗作用"},{"id":"q7_c4","en":"Insulin-induced hypoglycemia","zh":"胰岛素诱导低血糖"},{"id":"q7_c1","en":"Digoxin toxicity with hypokalemia","zh":"低钾相关地高辛中毒"}],"correct":"q7_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q7_a2","en":"Notify the provider with pulse, potassium, symptoms, and digoxin level","zh":"向医嘱提供者报告脉搏、钾值、症状和地高辛浓度"},{"id":"q7_a3","en":"Administer the scheduled digoxin to improve contractility","zh":"给予预定地高辛以改善心肌收缩力"},{"id":"q7_a4","en":"Teach that yellow halos are expected and harmless","zh":"告知患者黄色光圈是预期且无害的表现"},{"id":"q7_a1","en":"Hold digoxin per protocol","zh":"按流程暂停地高辛"}],"correct":["q7_a1","q7_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q7_p3","en":"Absolute neutrophil count","zh":"绝对中性粒细胞计数"},{"id":"q7_p2","en":"Potassium and digoxin level trends","zh":"钾和地高辛浓度趋势"},{"id":"q7_p1","en":"Apical pulse and heart rhythm","zh":"心尖脉和心律"},{"id":"q7_p4","en":"Urine ketones before every meal","zh":"每餐前尿酮"}],"correct":["q7_p1","q7_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nausea, yellow halos, weakness, bradycardia, low potassium, and a high digoxin level indicate digoxin toxicity. The stated protocol supports holding digoxin and notifying the provider while monitoring pulse, rhythm, potassium, and digoxin levels.","rationaleCorrectZh":"恶心、黄色光圈、乏力、心动过缓、低钾和高地高辛浓度提示地高辛中毒。题干流程支持暂停地高辛并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测脉搏、心律、钾和地高辛浓度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For digoxin, cluster gastrointestinal symptoms, visual changes, bradycardia, potassium changes, and drug level. A low potassium level increases concern for toxicity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到地高辛题时，把胃肠道症状、视觉改变、心动过缓、钾变化和药物浓度组合判断。低钾会增加中毒风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1843,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_pharm_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.373","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.373.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.373.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,86],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving a heparin infusion has a change in platelet count and new symptoms.","fullStemZh":"一名接受肝素输注的患者出现血小板计数变化和新症状。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client receiving a heparin infusion has a change in platelet count and new symptoms.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名接受肝素输注的患者出现血小板计数变化和新症状。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"A client has been receiving an unfractionated heparin infusion for 6 days after a pulmonary embolism. The platelet count decreased from 228 ×10³/µL at baseline to 92 ×10³/µL today. The client reports new calf pain, and the affected calf is warm and swollen. The facility protocol states: if platelet count drops by 50% or more after heparin exposure or thrombosis is suspected, stop heparin per protocol, notify the provider, and monitor for new thrombosis or bleeding. The nurse should suspect {{d1}}, first take the protocol-directed action to {{d2}}, and monitor {{d3}}.","zh":"一名肺栓塞患者已连续 6 天接受普通肝素输注。血小板计数从基线 228 ×10³/µL 降至今天的 92 ×10³/µL。患者报告新发小腿疼痛，患侧小腿温热并肿胀。机构流程规定：肝素暴露后血小板下降 50% 或以上，或怀疑血栓形成时，应按流程停止肝素、通知医嘱提供者，并监测新的血栓或出血。护士应怀疑 {{d1}}，先按流程 {{d2}}，并监测 {{d3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"d1_o1","en":"heparin-induced thrombocytopenia with possible new thrombosis","zh":"肝素诱导性血小板减少并可能有新血栓"},{"id":"d1_o3","en":"warfarin over-anticoagulation","zh":"华法林抗凝过度"},{"id":"d1_o4","en":"parenteral nutrition refeeding complication","zh":"肠外营养再喂养并发症"},{"id":"d1_o2","en":"expected platelet response to heparin","zh":"肝素的预期血小板反应"}],"correct":"d1_o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"d2_o4","en":"wait for the next routine platelet count before reporting","zh":"等下一次常规血小板计数后再报告"},{"id":"d2_o1","en":"stop the heparin infusion and notify the provider","zh":"停止肝素输注并通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"d2_o2","en":"increase the heparin infusion rate","zh":"提高肝素输注速度"},{"id":"d2_o3","en":"massage the painful calf","zh":"按摩疼痛小腿"}],"correct":"d2_o1"},{"id":"d3","options":[{"id":"d3_o2","en":"capillary glucose before meals only","zh":"仅监测餐前床旁血糖"},{"id":"d3_o3","en":"serum lithium level and hand tremor","zh":"血清锂浓度和手颤"},{"id":"d3_o1","en":"calf swelling, chest pain, shortness of breath, and bleeding","zh":"小腿肿胀、胸痛、气短和出血"},{"id":"d3_o4","en":"visual halos and apical pulse before digoxin","zh":"地高辛给药前的视觉光圈和心尖脉"}],"correct":"d3_o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A platelet drop of more than 50% after several days of heparin exposure plus new calf findings suggests heparin-induced thrombocytopenia with possible thrombosis. The stated protocol directs stopping heparin, notifying the provider, and monitoring for thrombosis and bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝素暴露数天后血小板下降超过 50%，并出现新的小腿表现，提示肝素诱导性血小板减少并可能有血栓。题干流程要求停止肝素、通知医嘱提供者，并监测血栓和出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A falling platelet count during heparin therapy is not always bleeding-focused; pair it with new clot symptoms to recognize heparin-induced thrombocytopenia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"肝素治疗期间血小板下降并不总是只看出血；如果合并新的血栓症状，要想到肝素诱导性血小板减少。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1844,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.374","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.374.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.374.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,75],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the breach in sterile technique documented in the procedure note.","fullStemZh":"请标出操作记录中违反无菌技术的内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the breach in sterile technique documented in the procedure note.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出操作记录中违反无菌技术的内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Procedure note: The nurse performs hand hygiene before opening the sterile dressing tray.","zh":"操作记录：护士在打开无菌换药盘前进行手卫生。"},{"id":"s2","en":"The nurse opens the outer wrapper by moving the far flap away from the body.","zh":"护士先将远侧包布向远离身体的方向打开。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The nurse reaches across the open sterile field to pick up a sterile gauze pad.","zh":"护士越过已经打开的无菌区域去拿取一块无菌纱布。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse keeps sterile-gloved hands above waist level while preparing supplies.","zh":"护士准备物品时将戴无菌手套的双手保持在腰部以上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The nurse adds sterile saline to the basin without touching the bottle lip to the basin.","zh":"护士向容器内倒入无菌生理盐水，瓶口没有接触容器。"}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reaching across an open sterile field contaminates the field because the nurse's arm passes over sterile supplies. The other documented actions maintain the field.","rationaleCorrectZh":"手臂越过已经打开的无菌区域会污染无菌区，因为手臂经过无菌物品上方。其他记录中的做法可维持无菌状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sterile-field questions, look for movement over the field, items below the waist, wet surfaces, or contact between sterile and nonsterile objects.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到无菌区域题时，重点寻找越过无菌区、物品低于腰部、潮湿表面或无菌物品接触非无菌物品等线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1845,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.375","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.375.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.375.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,67],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the documented action that breaches standard precautions.","fullStemZh":"请标出记录中违反标准预防措施的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the documented action that breaches standard precautions.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出记录中违反标准预防措施的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Hygiene note: The nurse wears gloves while emptying a bedside commode.","zh":"卫生记录：护士清空床旁便盆时戴手套。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The nurse avoids touching the uniform with gloved hands.","zh":"护士避免用戴手套的手接触工作服。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The nurse removes the gloves and immediately answers the unit phone before performing hand hygiene.","zh":"护士脱下手套后，在进行手卫生前立即接听护士站电话。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse disinfects the commode seat after emptying the container.","zh":"护士清空容器后对便盆座面进行消毒。"},{"id":"s5","en":"The nurse places used wipes in the designated waste container.","zh":"护士将用过的湿巾放入指定废物容器。"}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hand hygiene is required after removing gloves. Touching a shared phone before hand hygiene can spread microorganisms to equipment and staff.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脱手套后需要进行手卫生。在手卫生前接触共用电话，可能将微生物传播到设备和工作人员。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat gloves as contaminated after use. The safe pattern is gloves for exposure risk, remove gloves, perform hand hygiene, and only then touch clean or shared surfaces.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用后的手套应视为已污染。安全流程是：有暴露风险时戴手套，脱手套，进行手卫生，然后再接触清洁或共用表面。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1846,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.376","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.376.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.376.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,55],"fullStemEn":"Per facility policy, portable oxygen cylinders must be replaced before transport if the pressure gauge reads below 500 psi. Highlight the checklist finding that requires follow-up.","fullStemZh":"根据机构政策，便携式氧气瓶压力表读数低于 500 psi 时，转运前必须更换。请标出需要后续处理的检查单发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the checklist finding that requires follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要后续处理的检查单发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per facility policy, portable oxygen cylinders must be replaced before transport if the pressure gauge reads below 500 psi.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据机构政策，便携式氧气瓶压力表读数低于 500 psi 时，转运前必须更换。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Pre-transport equipment checklist:","zh":"转运前设备检查单："},{"id":"s2","en":"Portable suction canister is attached and tubing is capped.","zh":"便携式吸引瓶已连接，管路已盖好。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Oxygen cylinder pressure gauge reads 350 psi.","zh":"氧气瓶压力表读数为 350 psi。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Wheelchair brakes lock when tested.","zh":"轮椅刹车测试时可以锁定。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Call light is within reach while waiting for transport staff.","zh":"等待转运人员期间，呼叫铃在患者可及范围内。"}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The oxygen cylinder pressure is below the facility's stated 500 psi replacement threshold, so the cylinder must be replaced before transport.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氧气瓶压力低于题干中机构规定的 500 psi 更换阈值，因此转运前必须更换氧气瓶。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem gives a facility threshold, compare each finding directly with that threshold instead of relying on memory.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干给出机构阈值时，应将每个发现直接与该阈值比较，而不是依赖记忆。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1847,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.377","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.377.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.377.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,178],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,61],"fullStemEn":"A nurse wore gloves, gown, face shield, and mask for a procedure with splash risk. Arrange the PPE removal steps in the correct sequence using the unit's posted doffing sequence.","fullStemZh":"护士在有液体飞溅风险的操作中佩戴了手套、隔离衣、面屏和口罩。请根据科室张贴的脱卸流程，将 PPE 脱卸步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the PPE removal steps in the correct sequence using the unit's posted doffing sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据科室张贴的脱卸流程，将 PPE 脱卸步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse wore gloves, gown, face shield, and mask for a procedure with splash risk.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在有液体飞溅风险的操作中佩戴了手套、隔离衣、面屏和口罩。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Remove the face shield by handling the strap or side arms.","zh":"握住面屏的绑带或侧臂取下面屏。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove gloves without touching bare skin.","zh":"脱下手套，避免接触裸露皮肤。"},{"id":"C","en":"Perform hand hygiene.","zh":"进行手卫生。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove the gown by turning the contaminated outside inward.","zh":"脱下隔离衣，将受污染的外面向内卷起。"},{"id":"E","en":"Remove the mask by the ties or ear loops.","zh":"通过系带或耳挂取下口罩。"},{"id":"F","en":"Perform hand hygiene again.","zh":"再次进行手卫生。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The posted sequence removes heavily contaminated gloves and gown, cleans hands, removes face and respiratory protection by clean handling points, and ends with hand hygiene.","rationaleCorrectZh":"张贴流程要求先脱去污染较重的手套和隔离衣，清洁双手，再通过清洁接触点取下面部和呼吸防护用品，并以手卫生结束。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For PPE sequence items, separate contaminated surfaces from clean handling points and place hand hygiene at transition points where contamination could spread.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 PPE 顺序题时，要区分污染表面和清洁接触点，并在污染可能传播的转换环节安排手卫生。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1848,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.378","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.378.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.378.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[137,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,63],"fullStemEn":"Per unit fall-prevention protocol, a client who received an opioid within the past 4 hours must have staff assistance before ambulating. Highlight the safety-note finding that requires follow-up.","fullStemZh":"根据科室跌倒预防流程，过去 4 小时内使用过阿片类药物的患者下床行走前必须由工作人员协助。请标出安全记录中需要后续处理的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the safety-note finding that requires follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出安全记录中需要后续处理的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per unit fall-prevention protocol, a client who received an opioid within the past 4 hours must have staff assistance before ambulating.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据科室跌倒预防流程，过去 4 小时内使用过阿片类药物的患者下床行走前必须由工作人员协助。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Safety note: Client received hydromorphone 1 mg IV at 0930 for postoperative pain.","zh":"安全记录：患者 0930 因术后疼痛接受氢吗啡酮 1 mg 静脉给药。"},{"id":"s2","en":"At 1100, the client states, “I feel a little sleepy but need to use the bathroom.”","zh":"1100，患者说：“我有点困，但需要去卫生间。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The nurse tells the client to press the call light and waits at the bedside.","zh":"护士告知患者按呼叫铃，并在床旁等待。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client’s nonskid socks are on both feet.","zh":"患者双脚均穿着防滑袜。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The bedside table is placed across the room so the path to the bathroom is wider.","zh":"床旁桌被放到房间另一侧，以便通往卫生间的通道更宽。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A bedside table placed across the room may put needed items out of reach and encourage unassisted ambulation. The client recently received an opioid, so staff assistance and reachable items are important fall-prevention measures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"床旁桌放在房间另一侧可能使患者无法拿到所需物品，并促使患者自行下床。患者近期使用过阿片类药物，因此工作人员协助和物品可及是重要的跌倒预防措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For fall-prevention items, look for anything that makes the client choose between waiting for help and reaching or walking alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做跌倒预防题时，注意寻找会让患者在等待帮助和自行伸手或行走之间做选择的因素。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1849,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.379","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.379.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.379.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[56,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,28],"fullStemEn":"The unit is preparing for an internal evacuation drill. Highlight the action that breaches emergency safety procedures.","fullStemZh":"科室正在准备内部疏散演练。请标出违反应急安全流程的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the action that breaches emergency safety procedures.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出违反应急安全流程的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit is preparing for an internal evacuation drill.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室正在准备内部疏散演练。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Evacuation drill note: Charge nurse assigns one staff member to bring the unit census and client acuity list.","zh":"疏散演练记录：主管护士安排一名工作人员携带科室患者名单和病情轻重清单。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Staff place evacuation tags on clients after verifying each identity band.","zh":"工作人员核对每名患者腕带后放置疏散标签。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"A staff member props open a fire door with a linen cart to speed movement through the hallway.","zh":"一名工作人员用布草车顶住防火门，以加快人员通过走廊。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse keeps a battery-powered communication device with the evacuation team.","zh":"护士让疏散小组携带电池供电的通信设备。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Oxygen-dependent clients are paired with staff before relocation.","zh":"依赖氧气的患者在转移前与工作人员配对。"}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fire doors must not be propped open because they help contain smoke and fire. Speeding movement does not justify disabling a fire-safety barrier.","rationaleCorrectZh":"防火门不得被顶开，因为它们有助于阻隔烟雾和火势。为了加快移动而破坏防火屏障是不安全的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In emergency-preparedness questions, do not sacrifice containment, communication, identification, or life support for speed alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做应急准备题时，不要为了单纯追求速度而牺牲隔离控制、沟通、身份识别或生命支持。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1850,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.380","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.380.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.380.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse finds a client sitting on the floor beside the bed after an unwitnessed fall. Arrange the actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一名患者在无人目击的跌倒后坐在床旁地板上。请按正确顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse finds a client sitting on the floor beside the bed after an unwitnessed fall.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士发现一名患者在无人目击的跌倒后坐在床旁地板上。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document objective findings, interventions, notifications, and the client’s response.","zh":"记录客观发现、干预措施、通知情况和患者反应。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call for assistance and stay with the client.","zh":"呼叫协助并留在患者身边。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client for airway, breathing, circulation, pain, deformity, bleeding, and level of consciousness before moving the client.","zh":"移动患者前评估气道、呼吸、循环、疼痛、畸形、出血和意识水平。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assist the client back to bed only after assessment indicates it is safe and enough help is present.","zh":"只有在评估显示安全且有足够人员协助后，才协助患者回到床上。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider using the client’s assessment findings and the fall circumstances.","zh":"根据患者评估结果和跌倒经过通知医护提供者。"}],"correct":["B","A","D","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first stays with the client and calls for help, assesses for injury before moving the client, returns the client to safety only when appropriate, notifies the provider with assessment data, and documents the event objectively.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先留在患者身边并呼叫协助，移动前评估是否受伤，在适当且安全时将患者转回床上，再用评估资料通知医护提供者，并客观记录事件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After a fall, do not move the client first. Stay, get help, assess for injury, then move only if safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"患者跌倒后，不要先移动患者。应留在现场、寻求帮助、评估损伤，然后在安全时再移动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1851,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_sic_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.381","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.381.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.381.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,27],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is setting up a sterile field for a bedside dressing change. Arrange the actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"护士正在为床旁换药建立无菌区域。请按正确顺序排列操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is setting up a sterile field for a bedside dressing change.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在为床旁换药建立无菌区域。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Open the far flap of the sterile wrapper away from the body.","zh":"先将远侧无菌包布向远离身体的方向打开。"},{"id":"D","en":"Open the near flap toward the body while keeping the arm outside the sterile field.","zh":"将近侧包布朝身体方向打开，同时保持手臂不进入无菌区域上方。"},{"id":"E","en":"Add sterile supplies to the field by dropping them gently from above without touching the field edge.","zh":"从上方轻轻投放无菌物品到无菌区域内，避免接触无菌区边缘。"},{"id":"C","en":"Open the side flaps without reaching over the sterile contents.","zh":"打开两侧包布，避免越过无菌物品上方。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene and place the sterile package on a clean, dry work surface above waist level.","zh":"进行手卫生，并将无菌包放在腰部以上清洁、干燥的工作台面上。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A sterile field is opened on a clean, dry surface above waist level. The far flap is opened first, then side flaps, then the near flap, and sterile supplies are added without touching the field edge.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无菌区域应在腰部以上清洁、干燥的表面上打开。先打开远侧包布，再打开两侧包布，然后打开近侧包布，最后在不接触无菌区边缘的情况下加入无菌物品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sterile setup sequences, establish the clean surface first, open the far side before the near side, and avoid reaching over the sterile contents.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做无菌建立顺序题时，先准备清洁表面，先开远侧再开近侧，并避免越过无菌物品上方。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1852,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.382","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.382.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.382.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[159,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,66],"fullStemEn":"Review the medication administration record. Per unit anticoagulant protocol, hold warfarin and notify the provider when the same-day INR is greater than 4.0. Which action should the nurse take at 2100?","fullStemZh":"查看用药记录。根据病区抗凝药物规程，如果当天 INR 大于 4.0，应暂缓华法林并通知医嘱提供者。护士在 2100 应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take at 2100?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在 2100 应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per unit anticoagulant protocol, hold warfarin and notify the provider when the same-day INR is greater than 4.0.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据病区抗凝药物规程，如果当天 INR 大于 4.0，应暂缓华法林并通知医嘱提供者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Give the enoxaparin dose that was administered earlier again.","zh":"再次给予之前已给过的依诺肝素。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the warfarin because it is listed as due.","zh":"因华法林显示到点，应给予该药。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the warfarin and notify the provider.","zh":"暂缓华法林并通知医嘱提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document that no anticoagulant is scheduled at 2100.","zh":"记录 2100 没有安排抗凝药。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows warfarin is due at 2100 and the same-day INR is 4.6. Under the stated protocol, the nurse should hold warfarin and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用药记录显示 2100 华法林到点，且当天 INR 为 4.6。根据题干给出的规程，护士应暂缓华法林并通知医嘱提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a MAR item includes a safety threshold, match the due medication with the relevant lab or status cell before choosing the nursing action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当用药记录题包含安全阈值时，先把到点药物与相关化验或状态格对应起来，再选择护理措施。","sourceMetadata":"closed-world unit anticoagulant protocol stated in stem","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1853,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.383","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.383.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.383.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,149],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,58],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes heparin at 1,000 units/hr IV. Use the medication label to calculate the infusion pump rate. Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为肝素静脉输注 1,000 units/hr。请根据药品标签计算输液泵速率，四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据药品标签计算输液泵速率，四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Use the medication label to calculate the infusion pump rate.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为肝素静脉输注 1,000 units/hr。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/hr"},"acceptable":["10","10 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":10,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label shows 25,000 units in 250 mL, which is 100 units/mL. A prescription for 1,000 units/hr requires 1,000 divided by 100, or 10 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示 250 mL 中含 25,000 units，即 100 units/mL。医嘱 1,000 units/hr 需要 1,000 除以 100，即 10 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For an infusion-label calculation, first compute concentration from the label, then divide the ordered dose rate by that concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输注标签计算题先根据标签算出浓度，再用医嘱剂量速率除以该浓度。","sourceMetadata":"synthetic medication label arithmetic","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1854,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.384","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.384.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.384.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,46],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes morphine sulfate 2 mg IV now for severe postoperative pain. Use the medication label to determine the volume the nurse should prepare.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为立即静脉给予硫酸吗啡 2 mg，用于严重术后疼痛。请根据药品标签判断护士应准备的体积。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the medication label to determine the volume the nurse should prepare.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据药品标签判断护士应准备的体积。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider prescribes morphine sulfate 2 mg IV now for severe postoperative pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为立即静脉给予硫酸吗啡 2 mg，用于严重术后疼痛。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"1 mL","zh":"1 mL"},{"id":"B","en":"0.5 mL","zh":"0.5 mL"},{"id":"D","en":"2 mL","zh":"2 mL"},{"id":"A","en":"0.2 mL","zh":"0.2 mL"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label shows 10 mg in 1 mL, or 10 mg/mL. A 2 mg dose requires 2 divided by 10, which is 0.2 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示 1 mL 中含 10 mg，即 10 mg/mL。2 mg 剂量需要 2 除以 10，即 0.2 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-alert medications, verify that the prepared volume matches the ordered dose and not the total amount in the container.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于高警示药物，要确认准备体积对应医嘱剂量，而不是容器内的总药量。","sourceMetadata":"synthetic medication label arithmetic","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1855,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.385","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.385.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.385.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,43],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving parenteral nutrition through an infusion pump. Use the device screen to calculate how many minutes remain until the programmed volume is infused.","fullStemZh":"患者正在通过输液泵接受肠外营养。请根据设备屏幕计算程序设定的液体量输完还需要多少分钟。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the device screen to calculate how many minutes remain until the programmed volume is infused.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据设备屏幕计算程序设定的液体量输完还需要多少分钟。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is receiving parenteral nutrition through an infusion pump.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者正在通过输液泵接受肠外营养。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minutes","zh":"分钟"},"acceptable":["720","720 minutes"],"numeric":{"value":720,"tolerance":0,"unit":"minutes"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The screen shows VTBI 900 mL and a rate of 75 mL/hr. The infusion duration is 900 divided by 75, then multiplied by 60, which equals 720 minutes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"屏幕显示待输注量 900 mL，速率 75 mL/hr。输注时间为 900 除以 75，再乘以 60，等于 720 分钟。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pump-screen time calculations, divide volume by hourly rate to get hours, then convert hours to minutes if the question asks for minutes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输液泵时间计算题中，用体积除以每小时速率得到小时数；如果题目要求分钟，再换算为分钟。","sourceMetadata":"synthetic infusion pump screen arithmetic","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1856,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.386","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.386.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.386.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[165,208],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,61],"fullStemEn":"Review the medication administration record. Per unit protocol, hold scheduled nutritional insulin and notify the provider when parenteral nutrition is interrupted. Which action should the nurse take at 1800?","fullStemZh":"查看用药记录。根据病区规程，肠外营养中断时应暂缓按营养摄入安排的胰岛素并通知医嘱提供者。护士在 1800 应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take at 1800?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在 1800 应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per unit protocol, hold scheduled nutritional insulin and notify the provider when parenteral nutrition is interrupted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据病区规程，肠外营养中断时应暂缓按营养摄入安排的胰岛素并通知医嘱提供者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Hold the regular insulin, start the protocol backup fluid as prescribed, and notify the provider.","zh":"暂缓常规胰岛素，按医嘱启动规程备用液，并通知医嘱提供者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Mark the parenteral nutrition as given because it was infusing earlier in the day.","zh":"因为当天早些时候曾在输注，将肠外营养记录为已给。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the scheduled regular insulin and document it as given.","zh":"给予按时常规胰岛素并记录已给药。"},{"id":"D","en":"Give the regular insulin and hold the dextrose backup fluid until 2200.","zh":"给予常规胰岛素，并将葡萄糖备用液延后到 2200。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows parenteral nutrition remains interrupted at 1800 and regular insulin is due at the same time. Under the stated protocol, the nurse should hold the nutritional insulin, start the ordered backup fluid, and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用药记录显示 1800 肠外营养仍中断，同时常规胰岛素到点。根据题干规程，护士应暂缓营养相关胰岛素，启动已开立的备用液，并通知医嘱提供者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When insulin is linked to nutrition, match the insulin due time with the nutrition status before deciding whether to administer it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当胰岛素与营养输注相关时，先把胰岛素到点时间与营养输注状态对应，再决定是否给药。","sourceMetadata":"closed-world unit protocol stated in stem","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1857,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.387","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.387.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.387.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[208,251],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,75],"fullStemEn":"Review the medication administration record. Per facility transition protocol, clarify with the provider before giving a newly scheduled oral anticoagulant if a therapeutic heparin infusion is still running. Which action should the nurse take at 0900?","fullStemZh":"查看用药记录。根据机构转换抗凝治疗规程，如果治疗剂量肝素输注仍在进行，应在给予新安排的口服抗凝药前与医嘱提供者澄清。护士在 0900 应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take at 0900?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在 0900 应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Per facility transition protocol, clarify with the provider before giving a newly scheduled oral anticoagulant if a therapeutic heparin infusion is still running.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据机构转换抗凝治疗规程，如果治疗剂量肝素输注仍在进行，应在给予新安排的口服抗凝药前与医嘱提供者澄清。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Give apixaban at 0900 because it is listed as due.","zh":"因阿哌沙班显示 0900 到点，应立即给药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stop the heparin infusion immediately without contacting the provider.","zh":"不联系医嘱提供者，立即停止肝素输注。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document that the heparin infusion has already been discontinued.","zh":"记录肝素输注已经停止。"},{"id":"B","en":"Clarify the anticoagulant transition before giving apixaban.","zh":"在给予阿哌沙班前澄清抗凝转换方案。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows the therapeutic heparin infusion is still running at 0800, apixaban is due at 0900, and the heparin stop order is not due until 1000. The stated transition protocol requires clarification before giving apixaban.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用药记录显示 0800 治疗剂量肝素仍在输注，0900 阿哌沙班到点，而停止肝素医嘱到 1000 才到点。根据题干转换规程，给阿哌沙班前应先澄清。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For transition-of-therapy items, compare active medication status with the timing of the replacement medication and stop order.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝转换题要比较当前药物状态、替代药物到点时间和停药医嘱时间。","sourceMetadata":"closed-world facility transition protocol stated in stem","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1858,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.388","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.388.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.388.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,54],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes potassium chloride 10 mEq/hr IV. Use the medication label to calculate the infusion pump rate. Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为氯化钾静脉输注 10 mEq/hr。请根据药品标签计算输液泵速率，四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据药品标签计算输液泵速率，四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Use the medication label to calculate the infusion pump rate.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为氯化钾静脉输注 10 mEq/hr。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"mL/hr"},"acceptable":["50","50 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":50,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label shows 20 mEq in 100 mL, which is 0.2 mEq/mL. A prescription for 10 mEq/hr requires 10 divided by 0.2, or 50 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示 100 mL 中含 20 mEq，即 0.2 mEq/mL。医嘱 10 mEq/hr 需要 10 除以 0.2，即 50 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With high-alert electrolyte infusions, calculate the mEq per mL from the bag before setting the pump rate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高警示电解质输注题中，先根据输液袋计算每 mL 含多少 mEq，再设置泵速。","sourceMetadata":"synthetic medication label arithmetic","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1859,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fresh_2026_06_22_vis_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.389","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.389.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.389.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,228],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,73],"fullStemEn":"A client is using a PCA pump after surgery. Use the device screen to calculate the maximum medication dose the client can receive in 1 hour if the client presses the demand button as often as allowed. Round to the nearest tenth.","fullStemZh":"患者术后正在使用 PCA 泵。请根据设备屏幕计算：如果患者按允许的最频繁次数按需给药，1 小时内最多可获得多少药物剂量。四舍五入到最接近的十分位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest tenth.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的十分位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Use the device screen to calculate the maximum medication dose the client can receive in 1 hour if the client presses the demand button as often as allowed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请根据设备屏幕计算：如果患者按允许的最频繁次数按需给药，1 小时内最多可获得多少药物剂量。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mg in 1 hour","zh":"1 小时内 mg"},"acceptable":["1.2","1.2 mg"],"numeric":{"value":1.2,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mg"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The lockout is 10 minutes, so the maximum number of demand doses in 1 hour is 60 divided by 10, or 6. Each demand dose is 0.2 mg, so the maximum dose is 6 times 0.2 mg, or 1.2 mg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"锁定时间为 10 分钟，因此 1 小时内最多按需给药次数为 60 除以 10，即 6 次。每次按需剂量为 0.2 mg，所以最大剂量为 6 乘以 0.2 mg，即 1.2 mg。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For PCA safety calculations, use the lockout interval to find the maximum number of allowed demands before multiplying by the demand dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"PCA 安全计算题中，先用锁定时间算出最多允许按需给药次数，再乘以每次按需剂量。","sourceMetadata":"synthetic PCA pump screen arithmetic","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1860,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.390","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.390.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.390.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[167,268],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,93],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with atrial fibrillation who has taken warfarin for 3 months. The client reports black, tarry stools and new dizziness when standing. Laboratory results show INR 6.2 and hemoglobin decreased from 13.1 g/dL to 10.4 g/dL since last week.","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名因心房颤动服用华法林3个月的患者。患者报告黑色柏油样便，站立时新出现头晕。实验室结果显示 INR 6.2，血红蛋白从上周的 13.1 g/dL 降至 10.4 g/dL。","terminalSentenceEn":"Laboratory results show INR 6.2 and hemoglobin decreased from 13.1 g/dL to 10.4 g/dL since last week.","terminalSentenceZh":"实验室结果显示 INR 6.2，血红蛋白从上周的 13.1 g/dL 降至 10.4 g/dL。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports black, tarry stools and new dizziness when standing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者报告黑色柏油样便，站立时新出现头晕。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Ischemic stroke from inadequate anticoagulation","zh":"抗凝不足导致的缺血性卒中"},{"id":"c3","en":"Chronic iron deficiency anemia without active bleeding","zh":"无活动性出血的慢性缺铁性贫血"},{"id":"c1","en":"Warfarin over-effect with gastrointestinal bleeding","zh":"华法林作用过强并伴胃肠道出血"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Encourage vigorous hallway ambulation","zh":"鼓励在走廊剧烈行走"},{"id":"a2","en":"Notify the provider using the INR, stool finding, dizziness, and hemoglobin change","zh":"用 INR、粪便表现、头晕和血红蛋白变化通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"a3","en":"Administer an additional warfarin dose","zh":"额外给予一剂华法林"},{"id":"a1","en":"Hold the scheduled warfarin dose","zh":"暂停计划给予的华法林剂量"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p2","en":"Blood pressure and heart rate, including orthostatic changes","zh":"血压和心率，包括体位性变化"},{"id":"p4","en":"Daily calf circumference","zh":"每日小腿围"},{"id":"p3","en":"Peak expiratory flow before meals","zh":"餐前呼气峰流速"},{"id":"p1","en":"Stool or emesis for visible or occult blood","zh":"粪便或呕吐物是否有肉眼血或隐血"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The findings indicate warfarin over-anticoagulation with gastrointestinal bleeding. The nurse should hold warfarin and notify the provider, while monitoring bleeding evidence and hemodynamic stability.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这些表现提示华法林抗凝过度并发生胃肠道出血。护士应暂停华法林并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测出血证据和血流动力学稳定性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the anticoagulant result to the symptom pattern. A high INR plus melena and falling hemoglobin points to bleeding, so choose actions that stop further exposure and escalate care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把抗凝结果与症状模式对应起来。INR 升高加上黑便和血红蛋白下降指向出血，因此应选择停止继续暴露并升级处理的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1861,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.391","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.391.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.391.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[194,253],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,79],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with a pulmonary embolism has been receiving an unfractionated heparin infusion for 6 days. The platelet count has decreased from 248 ×10³/µL on admission to 92 ×10³/µL today. The client reports new pain and coolness in the right foot.","fullStemZh":"一名因肺栓塞入院的患者已接受普通肝素静脉输注6天。血小板计数从入院时 248 ×10³/µL 降至今天的 92 ×10³/µL。患者报告右脚新出现疼痛和发凉。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client reports new pain and coolness in the right foot.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者报告右脚新出现疼痛和发凉。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The platelet count has decreased from 248 ×10³/µL on admission to 92 ×10³/µL today.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血小板计数从入院时 248 ×10³/µL 降至今天的 92 ×10³/µL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia with thrombosis risk","zh":"肝素诱导的血小板减少症并有血栓风险"},{"id":"c2","en":"Expected therapeutic anticoagulation from heparin","zh":"肝素达到预期治疗性抗凝"},{"id":"c3","en":"Vitamin K deficiency from poor intake","zh":"摄入不足导致维生素K缺乏"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a1","en":"Stop the heparin infusion per facility protocol","zh":"按机构流程停止肝素输注"},{"id":"a2","en":"Notify the provider of the platelet drop and new right-foot findings","zh":"将血小板下降和右脚新发现通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"a3","en":"Flush the IV line with heparin to maintain patency","zh":"用肝素冲洗静脉管路以保持通畅"},{"id":"a4","en":"Apply a heating pad directly to the cool foot","zh":"将热敷垫直接敷在发凉的足部"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Bowel sounds in all quadrants","zh":"四个象限肠鸣音"},{"id":"p1","en":"Platelet count trend","zh":"血小板计数趋势"},{"id":"p2","en":"Right-foot pulses, capillary refill, color, temperature, and pain","zh":"右足脉搏、毛细血管再充盈、颜色、温度和疼痛"},{"id":"p3","en":"Urine ketones every shift","zh":"每班尿酮"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The platelet drop after several days of heparin with new limb ischemia cues suggests heparin-induced thrombocytopenia with thrombosis risk. The nurse should stop the heparin per protocol and notify the provider while monitoring platelet trend and limb perfusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用肝素数日后血小板下降并出现肢体缺血线索，提示肝素诱导的血小板减少症并有血栓风险。护士应按流程停止肝素并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测血小板趋势和肢体灌注。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not equate a low platelet count during heparin therapy with simple bleeding risk only. A falling platelet count plus new ischemic pain points to a clotting complication that requires stopping heparin exposure and escalation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把肝素治疗期间血小板低只理解为单纯出血风险。血小板下降加上新发缺血性疼痛提示凝血性并发症，需要停止肝素暴露并升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The platelet count has decreased from 248 ×10³/µL on admission to 92 ×10³/µL today.","controlSentenceZh":"血小板计数从入院时 248 ×10³/µL 降至今天的 92 ×10³/µL。"}
{"queueIndex":1862,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.392","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.392.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.392.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,177],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,60],"fullStemEn":"A client who takes clozapine calls the clinic and reports a sore throat, fever, and extreme fatigue. The morning laboratory report shows an absolute neutrophil count of 680/mm3.","fullStemZh":"一名服用氯氮平的患者打电话到门诊，报告咽痛、发热和极度疲乏。当天上午实验室报告显示绝对中性粒细胞计数为 680/mm3。","terminalSentenceEn":"The morning laboratory report shows an absolute neutrophil count of 680/mm3.","terminalSentenceZh":"当天上午实验室报告显示绝对中性粒细胞计数为 680/mm3。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who takes clozapine calls the clinic and reports a sore throat, fever, and extreme fatigue.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名服用氯氮平的患者打电话到门诊，报告咽痛、发热和极度疲乏。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Serotonin syndrome","zh":"5-羟色胺综合征"},{"id":"c3","en":"Tardive dyskinesia","zh":"迟发性运动障碍"},{"id":"c1","en":"Clozapine-associated severe neutropenia","zh":"氯氮平相关严重中性粒细胞减少"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a1","en":"Hold clozapine as prescribed or per protocol","zh":"按医嘱或流程暂停氯氮平"},{"id":"a3","en":"Administer the next clozapine dose before calling","zh":"先给予下一剂氯氮平再联系"},{"id":"a2","en":"Notify the prescriber immediately about fever, sore throat, and ANC","zh":"立即将发热、咽痛和 ANC 通知处方者"},{"id":"a4","en":"Schedule routine follow-up in one month","zh":"安排一个月后的常规随访"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Pupil size every hour","zh":"每小时瞳孔大小"},{"id":"p3","en":"Serum lithium level","zh":"血清锂浓度"},{"id":"p2","en":"Absolute neutrophil count trend","zh":"绝对中性粒细胞计数趋势"},{"id":"p1","en":"Temperature and other infection symptoms","zh":"体温和其他感染症状"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clozapine can cause severe neutropenia, placing the client at high risk for infection. The nurse should hold the medication as prescribed or per protocol and notify the prescriber immediately, while monitoring temperature and neutrophil count.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氯氮平可导致严重中性粒细胞减少，使患者感染风险很高。护士应按医嘱或流程暂停用药并立即通知处方者，同时监测体温和中性粒细胞计数。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With clozapine, infection symptoms are not minor until the neutrophil count is checked. Pair fever and sore throat with a low ANC and choose urgent medication hold and prescriber notification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用氯氮平时，感染症状在确认中性粒细胞计数前不能视为小问题。把发热、咽痛和低 ANC 联系起来，选择紧急暂停用药并通知处方者。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1863,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.393","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.393.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.393.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,60],"fullStemEn":"A client taking lithium for bipolar disorder had vomiting and diarrhea for 2 days. The client now has coarse hand tremors, ataxia, confusion, and a serum lithium level of 2.1 mEq/L.","fullStemZh":"一名因双相障碍服用锂剂的患者呕吐、腹泻2天。现在出现双手粗大震颤、共济失调、意识混乱，血清锂浓度为 2.1 mEq/L。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client now has coarse hand tremors, ataxia, confusion, and a serum lithium level of 2.1 mEq/L.","terminalSentenceZh":"现在出现双手粗大震颤、共济失调、意识混乱，血清锂浓度为 2.1 mEq/L。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client taking lithium for bipolar disorder had vomiting and diarrhea for 2 days.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因双相障碍服用锂剂的患者呕吐、腹泻2天。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c3","en":"Hypoglycemia from missed meals","zh":"漏餐导致的低血糖"},{"id":"c2","en":"Neuroleptic malignant syndrome","zh":"恶性抗精神病药综合征"},{"id":"c1","en":"Lithium toxicity precipitated by fluid loss","zh":"液体丢失诱发的锂中毒"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a1","en":"Hold the scheduled lithium dose","zh":"暂停计划给予的锂剂"},{"id":"a3","en":"Administer the scheduled lithium dose with crackers","zh":"用饼干送服计划剂量的锂剂"},{"id":"a2","en":"Notify the provider of neurologic findings and lithium level","zh":"将神经系统表现和锂浓度通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"a4","en":"Restrict oral fluids unless specifically prescribed","zh":"限制口服液体，除非有明确医嘱"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"Vancomycin peak and trough levels","zh":"万古霉素峰浓度和谷浓度"},{"id":"p1","en":"Level of consciousness, tremor, gait, and seizure activity","zh":"意识水平、震颤、步态和癫痫活动"},{"id":"p2","en":"Intake and output, creatinine, and sodium","zh":"摄入/排出量、肌酐和钠"},{"id":"p4","en":"Visual acuity on the Snellen chart","zh":"Snellen 视力表视力"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Vomiting, diarrhea, neurologic changes, and an elevated serum lithium level indicate lithium toxicity. The nurse should hold lithium and notify the provider, while monitoring neurologic status and renal/fluid indicators.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呕吐、腹泻、神经系统变化和血清锂浓度升高提示锂中毒。护士应暂停锂剂并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测神经状态以及肾功能和液体相关指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For lithium, dehydration can quickly change a stable regimen into toxicity. Neurologic findings plus an elevated level should trigger holding the drug and escalating care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于锂剂，脱水可使原本稳定的用药迅速变成中毒。神经系统表现加上浓度升高，应触发暂停药物并升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1864,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.394","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.394.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.394.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[177,258],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,76],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes received rapid-acting insulin at 0730 but then became nauseated and did not eat breakfast. At 0830 the client is diaphoretic, shaky, and confused. Capillary blood glucose is 48 mg/dL, and the client is awake and able to swallow.","fullStemZh":"一名1型糖尿病患者 0730 接受速效胰岛素后出现恶心，没有吃早餐。0830 患者出汗、发抖、意识混乱。床旁血糖为 48 mg/dL，患者清醒并能吞咽。","terminalSentenceEn":"Capillary blood glucose is 48 mg/dL, and the client is awake and able to swallow.","terminalSentenceZh":"床旁血糖为 48 mg/dL，患者清醒并能吞咽。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0830 the client is diaphoretic, shaky, and confused.","penultimateSentenceZh":"0830 患者出汗、发抖、意识混乱。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Insulin-related hypoglycemia after missed meal","zh":"漏餐后的胰岛素相关低血糖"},{"id":"c2","en":"Diabetic ketoacidosis","zh":"糖尿病酮症酸中毒"},{"id":"c3","en":"Hyperosmolar hyperglycemic state","zh":"高渗高血糖状态"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Leave the client alone to sleep until the next meal","zh":"让患者独自睡到下一餐"},{"id":"a1","en":"Give oral fast-acting carbohydrate per hypoglycemia protocol","zh":"按低血糖流程给予口服快速作用碳水化合物"},{"id":"a3","en":"Administer additional rapid-acting insulin","zh":"追加速效胰岛素"},{"id":"a2","en":"Recheck capillary blood glucose after treatment per protocol","zh":"按流程在处理后复查床旁血糖"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Repeat capillary blood glucose","zh":"复查床旁血糖"},{"id":"p3","en":"Serum ammonia level","zh":"血氨水平"},{"id":"p2","en":"Mental status, diaphoresis, tremor, and ability to swallow","zh":"意识状态、出汗、震颤和吞咽能力"},{"id":"p4","en":"Deep tendon reflex grade","zh":"深腱反射分级"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is developing insulin-related hypoglycemia after receiving rapid-acting insulin without eating. Because the client can swallow, the nurse should give a fast-acting carbohydrate per protocol and recheck glucose soon after treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者在未进食的情况下接受速效胰岛素后发生胰岛素相关低血糖。由于患者能吞咽，护士应按流程给予快速作用碳水化合物，并在处理后尽快复查血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When insulin has been given and food is missed, symptoms such as sweating and shakiness are glucose cues. Check whether the client can safely swallow before choosing oral treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"已经给胰岛素但漏餐时，出汗和发抖是血糖线索。选择口服处理前，要确认患者是否能安全吞咽。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1865,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.395","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.395.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.395.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[206,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,71],"fullStemEn":"A client who has taken prednisone 40 mg daily for several weeks stops it abruptly because the prescription ran out. Two days later the client reports severe weakness, nausea, abdominal pain, and dizziness. Blood pressure is 86/50 mm Hg.","fullStemZh":"一名连续数周每天服用泼尼松 40 mg 的患者因处方用完而突然停药。两天后患者报告严重乏力、恶心、腹痛和头晕。血压为 86/50 mm Hg。","terminalSentenceEn":"Blood pressure is 86/50 mm Hg.","terminalSentenceZh":"血压为 86/50 mm Hg。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two days later the client reports severe weakness, nausea, abdominal pain, and dizziness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"两天后患者报告严重乏力、恶心、腹痛和头晕。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Cushing syndrome from chronic corticosteroid excess","zh":"长期糖皮质激素过量导致库欣综合征"},{"id":"c3","en":"Thyroid storm from excessive levothyroxine","zh":"左甲状腺素过量导致甲状腺危象"},{"id":"c1","en":"Acute adrenal insufficiency from abrupt corticosteroid withdrawal","zh":"突然停用糖皮质激素导致急性肾上腺功能不全"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Administer a diuretic to lower blood pressure","zh":"给予利尿剂以降低血压"},{"id":"a1","en":"Notify the provider of abrupt steroid cessation and hypotension","zh":"将突然停用激素和低血压通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"a2","en":"Prepare to administer prescribed corticosteroid and IV fluids","zh":"准备按医嘱给予糖皮质激素和静脉补液"},{"id":"a3","en":"Teach the client to remain off steroids until the next routine visit","zh":"教导患者在下次常规就诊前继续停用激素"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p2","en":"Blood glucose, sodium, and potassium","zh":"血糖、钠和钾"},{"id":"p1","en":"Blood pressure and heart rate","zh":"血压和心率"},{"id":"p3","en":"Pupillary accommodation","zh":"瞳孔调节"},{"id":"p4","en":"Hearing acuity","zh":"听力敏锐度"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abruptly stopping prolonged systemic corticosteroid therapy can precipitate acute adrenal insufficiency. The nurse should notify the provider and prepare to administer prescribed corticosteroid and fluids, while monitoring blood pressure and glucose/electrolytes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"长期系统性糖皮质激素治疗后突然停药可诱发急性肾上腺功能不全。护士应通知医嘱提供者，并准备按医嘱给予糖皮质激素和补液，同时监测血压以及血糖/电解质。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect prolonged corticosteroid use with the need to taper. Abrupt withdrawal plus hypotension and gastrointestinal symptoms signals adrenal insufficiency rather than routine medication intolerance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把长期使用糖皮质激素与需要逐渐减量联系起来。突然停药加低血压和胃肠症状提示肾上腺功能不全，而不是普通药物不耐受。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Two days later the client reports severe weakness, nausea, abdominal pain, and dizziness.","controlSentenceZh":"两天后患者报告严重乏力、恶心、腹痛和头晕。"}
{"queueIndex":1866,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.396","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.396.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.396.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,247],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,87],"fullStemEn":"A severely malnourished client starts parenteral nutrition after 10 days of minimal intake. Twelve hours later the client becomes weak and short of breath. Laboratory results show phosphorus 1.5 mg/dL, potassium 3.1 mEq/L, and magnesium 1.4 mg/dL.","fullStemZh":"一名严重营养不良的患者在10天几乎没有摄入后开始肠外营养。12小时后患者出现乏力和气短。实验室结果显示磷 1.5 mg/dL、钾 3.1 mEq/L、镁 1.4 mg/dL。","terminalSentenceEn":"Laboratory results show phosphorus 1.5 mg/dL, potassium 3.1 mEq/L, and magnesium 1.4 mg/dL.","terminalSentenceZh":"实验室结果显示磷 1.5 mg/dL、钾 3.1 mEq/L、镁 1.4 mg/dL。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Twelve hours later the client becomes weak and short of breath.","penultimateSentenceZh":"12小时后患者出现乏力和气短。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Refeeding syndrome risk after starting parenteral nutrition","zh":"开始肠外营养后的再喂养综合征风险"},{"id":"c2","en":"Catheter-related bloodstream infection","zh":"导管相关血流感染"},{"id":"c3","en":"Fat overload syndrome from lipid infusion","zh":"脂质输注导致脂肪超载综合征"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Notify the provider of electrolyte changes and symptoms","zh":"将电解质变化和症状通知医嘱提供者"},{"id":"a3","en":"Increase the infusion immediately to the goal rate","zh":"立即将输注提高到目标速率"},{"id":"a4","en":"Add free-water flushes to the central parenteral nutrition line","zh":"向中心静脉肠外营养管路加入游离水冲洗"},{"id":"a1","en":"Slow or hold parenteral nutrition as prescribed or per protocol","zh":"按医嘱或流程减慢或暂停肠外营养"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p2","en":"Respiratory effort, heart rhythm, and vital signs","zh":"呼吸用力、心律和生命体征"},{"id":"p3","en":"Visual fields","zh":"视野"},{"id":"p4","en":"Skin turgor only","zh":"仅皮肤弹性"},{"id":"p1","en":"Phosphorus, potassium, magnesium, and glucose","zh":"磷、钾、镁和血糖"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is developing refeeding syndrome risk after nutrition is restarted. The nurse should slow or hold parenteral nutrition per protocol/prescription and notify the provider, while monitoring electrolytes and cardiopulmonary status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者在重新开始营养支持后出现再喂养综合征风险。护士应按流程或医嘱减慢或暂停肠外营养并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测电解质和心肺状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When feeding is restarted after prolonged poor intake, sudden low phosphorus is a major clue. Choose interventions that pause escalation of calories and trigger prescribed electrolyte correction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"长期摄入不足后重新喂养时，突然低磷是重要线索。选择能够停止继续增加热量并促发医嘱纠正电解质的干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1867,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.397","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.397.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.397.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[209,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,92],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving continuous parenteral nutrition at 75 mL/hr has new polyuria and increased thirst. Capillary blood glucose readings have increased from 142 mg/dL yesterday to 286 mg/dL and 312 mg/dL today. The infusion is running at the prescribed rate.","fullStemZh":"一名持续接受肠外营养 75 mL/hr 的患者新出现多尿和口渴加重。床旁血糖从昨天的 142 mg/dL 升至今天的 286 mg/dL 和 312 mg/dL。输注正按医嘱速率运行。","terminalSentenceEn":"The infusion is running at the prescribed rate.","terminalSentenceZh":"输注正按医嘱速率运行。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Capillary blood glucose readings have increased from 142 mg/dL yesterday to 286 mg/dL and 312 mg/dL today.","penultimateSentenceZh":"床旁血糖从昨天的 142 mg/dL 升至今天的 286 mg/dL 和 312 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Toxicity, adverse effect, or complication the client is developing","zh":"患者正在发生的毒性反应、不良反应或并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Parenteral-nutrition-associated hyperglycemia","zh":"肠外营养相关高血糖"},{"id":"c2","en":"Fluid volume overload from infusion rate","zh":"输注速率导致液体容量过多"},{"id":"c3","en":"Hypoglycemia from interrupted dextrose intake","zh":"葡萄糖摄入中断导致低血糖"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two actions to take","zh":"应采取的两项措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Administer prescribed correction insulin or notify the provider for orders","zh":"给予医嘱纠正胰岛素或通知医嘱提供者开立医嘱"},{"id":"a4","en":"Encourage sugar-sweetened beverages for thirst","zh":"因口渴鼓励饮用含糖饮料"},{"id":"a1","en":"Check capillary glucose on the prescribed schedule","zh":"按医嘱时间表检测床旁血糖"},{"id":"a3","en":"Stop parenteral nutrition abruptly without a protocol or prescription","zh":"未按流程或医嘱突然停止肠外营养"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Capillary blood glucose trend","zh":"床旁血糖趋势"},{"id":"p3","en":"Serum troponin every 6 hours","zh":"每6小时血清肌钙蛋白"},{"id":"p2","en":"Intake and output, thirst, and dehydration signs","zh":"摄入/排出量、口渴和脱水迹象"},{"id":"p4","en":"Bilateral grip strength","zh":"双侧握力"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is developing parenteral-nutrition-associated hyperglycemia. The nurse should check glucose as prescribed and administer prescribed correction insulin or notify the provider, while monitoring glucose trend and fluid status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在发生肠外营养相关高血糖。护士应按医嘱监测血糖，并给予医嘱纠正胰岛素或通知医嘱提供者，同时监测血糖趋势和液体状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Parenteral nutrition contains dextrose, so thirst and polyuria should prompt glucose thinking. Choose prescribed glucose monitoring and insulin/escalation rather than abruptly stopping nutrition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"肠外营养含葡萄糖，因此口渴和多尿应让你想到血糖。选择按医嘱监测血糖和使用胰岛素/升级处理，而不是突然停止营养。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1868,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.398","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.398.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.398.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,60],"fullStemEn":"A client with heart failure has a prescription for carvedilol. Before administering the medication, the nurse notes heart rate 52/min, blood pressure 88/54 mm Hg, dizziness when standing, and new fatigue.","fullStemZh":"一名心力衰竭患者有卡维地洛医嘱。给药前，护士发现心率 52次/分、血压 88/54 mm Hg、站立时头晕和新出现疲乏。","terminalSentenceEn":"Before administering the medication, the nurse notes heart rate 52/min, blood pressure 88/54 mm Hg, dizziness when standing, and new fatigue.","terminalSentenceZh":"给药前，护士发现心率 52次/分、血压 88/54 mm Hg、站立时头晕和新出现疲乏。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with heart failure has a prescription for carvedilol.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名心力衰竭患者有卡维地洛医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{action}} and monitor {{parameter}}.","zh":"护士应{{action}}，并监测{{parameter}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"a3","en":"crush the medication and give it with applesauce","zh":"将药物压碎后与苹果酱同服"},{"id":"a2","en":"give the carvedilol as scheduled","zh":"按计划给予卡维地洛"},{"id":"a1","en":"hold the carvedilol and notify the provider","zh":"暂停卡维地洛并通知医嘱提供者"}],"correct":"a1"},{"id":"parameter","options":[{"id":"p3","en":"pupil reaction and visual acuity","zh":"瞳孔反应和视力"},{"id":"p2","en":"urine ketones and urine color","zh":"尿酮和尿液颜色"},{"id":"p1","en":"heart rate, blood pressure, and dizziness","zh":"心率、血压和头晕"}],"correct":"p1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Carvedilol can worsen bradycardia and hypotension. With low heart rate, low blood pressure, and dizziness, the nurse should hold the dose and notify the provider while monitoring hemodynamic parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"卡维地洛可加重心动过缓和低血压。出现心率低、血压低和头晕时，护士应暂停该剂量并通知医嘱提供者，同时监测血流动力学指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Before giving a cardiovascular medication, make the vital signs the safety checkpoint. Bradycardia plus hypotension points to holding and clarifying rather than routine administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"给心血管药物前，把生命体征作为安全检查点。心动过缓加低血压提示应暂停并澄清，而不是常规给药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1869,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.399","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.399.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.399.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,284],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,82],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes is prescribed metformin. The client is scheduled for a contrast-enhanced CT scan today. The unit protocol states: hold metformin on the day of iodinated contrast administration and restart only when renal function is reassessed and the provider approves.","fullStemZh":"一名2型糖尿病患者有二甲双胍医嘱。患者今天计划进行增强 CT 检查。病区流程规定：使用含碘造影剂当天暂停二甲双胍，只有在重新评估肾功能并经医嘱提供者同意后才可恢复。","terminalSentenceEn":"The unit protocol states: hold metformin on the day of iodinated contrast administration and restart only when renal function is reassessed and the provider approves.","terminalSentenceZh":"病区流程规定：使用含碘造影剂当天暂停二甲双胍，只有在重新评估肾功能并经医嘱提供者同意后才可恢复。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is scheduled for a contrast-enhanced CT scan today.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者今天计划进行增强 CT 检查。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Before transport, the nurse should {{action}} and plan to monitor {{parameter}}.","zh":"转运前，护士应{{action}}，并计划监测{{parameter}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"a1","en":"hold metformin according to the unit protocol","zh":"按病区流程暂停二甲双胍"},{"id":"a3","en":"restart metformin after the scan without further review","zh":"检查后无需进一步评估即恢复二甲双胍"},{"id":"a2","en":"administer metformin immediately before the scan","zh":"检查前立即给予二甲双胍"}],"correct":"a1"},{"id":"parameter","options":[{"id":"p3","en":"platelet count and bleeding time","zh":"血小板计数和出血时间"},{"id":"p2","en":"serum digoxin level and apical pulse","zh":"血清地高辛浓度和心尖脉搏"},{"id":"p1","en":"creatinine/eGFR and blood glucose","zh":"肌酐/eGFR 和血糖"}],"correct":"p1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The local protocol directs the nurse to hold metformin for iodinated contrast exposure and to ensure renal function is reassessed before restart. Creatinine/eGFR and blood glucose are relevant monitoring parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本地流程要求在使用含碘造影剂时暂停二甲双胍，并在重新开始前确保肾功能已复评。肌酐/eGFR 和血糖是相关监测指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem gives a facility protocol, use it as the rule for the item. The safest answer must follow the protocol exactly and monitor the parameters tied to the reason for the hold.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干给出机构流程时，要把它作为本题规则。最安全的答案必须严格遵循流程，并监测与暂停原因相关的指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1870,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.400","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.400.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.400.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,47],"fullStemEn":"A client who takes levothyroxine every morning reports taking the medication with breakfast and an iron supplement. The thyroid-stimulating hormone level remains elevated.","fullStemZh":"一名每天早晨服用左甲状腺素的患者报告自己把药物与早餐和铁剂一起服用。促甲状腺激素水平仍然升高。","terminalSentenceEn":"The thyroid-stimulating hormone level remains elevated.","terminalSentenceZh":"促甲状腺激素水平仍然升高。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who takes levothyroxine every morning reports taking the medication with breakfast and an iron supplement.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名每天早晨服用左甲状腺素的患者报告自己把药物与早餐和铁剂一起服用。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should teach the client to {{teaching}} and monitor {{parameter}}.","zh":"护士应指导患者{{teaching}}，并监测{{parameter}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"teaching","options":[{"id":"t3","en":"skip levothyroxine on any morning breakfast is eaten","zh":"任何吃早餐的早晨都跳过左甲状腺素"},{"id":"t1","en":"take levothyroxine on an empty stomach and separate it from iron","zh":"空腹服用左甲状腺素，并与铁剂分开"},{"id":"t2","en":"take levothyroxine with iron to prevent nausea","zh":"与铁剂同服左甲状腺素以预防恶心"}],"correct":"t1"},{"id":"parameter","options":[{"id":"p2","en":"INR and stool color","zh":"INR 和粪便颜色"},{"id":"p1","en":"TSH trend and hypothyroid symptoms","zh":"TSH 趋势和甲状腺功能减退症状"},{"id":"p3","en":"serum lithium level and tremor","zh":"血清锂浓度和震颤"}],"correct":"p1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Iron and food can reduce levothyroxine absorption. The nurse should teach the client to take levothyroxine on an empty stomach and separate it from iron, while monitoring TSH and hypothyroid symptoms.","rationaleCorrectZh":"铁剂和食物会降低左甲状腺素吸收。护士应指导患者空腹服用左甲状腺素，并与铁剂分开，同时监测 TSH 和甲状腺功能减退症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Persistent abnormal labs can reflect how a medication is taken, not only the dose. Look for interactions in the stem that reduce absorption.","testTakingStrategyZh":"持续异常的实验室结果可能反映服药方式，而不只是剂量问题。寻找题干中会降低吸收的相互作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1871,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_bow_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.401","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.401.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.401.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,60],"fullStemEn":"A client with heart failure takes furosemide daily. The client reports muscle cramps and weakness. The cardiac monitor shows frequent premature ventricular contractions. Laboratory results show potassium 2.9 mEq/L.","fullStemZh":"一名心力衰竭患者每天服用呋塞米。患者报告肌肉痉挛和乏力。心电监护显示频发室性早搏。实验室结果显示钾 2.9 mEq/L。","terminalSentenceEn":"Laboratory results show potassium 2.9 mEq/L.","terminalSentenceZh":"实验室结果显示钾 2.9 mEq/L。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The cardiac monitor shows frequent premature ventricular contractions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"心电监护显示频发室性早搏。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{action}} and monitor {{parameter}}.","zh":"护士应{{action}}，并监测{{parameter}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"a1","en":"notify the provider and prepare prescribed potassium replacement","zh":"通知医嘱提供者，并准备按医嘱补钾"},{"id":"a2","en":"give an extra dose of furosemide","zh":"额外给予一剂呋塞米"},{"id":"a3","en":"teach the client to restrict potassium-rich foods","zh":"指导患者限制富含钾的食物"}],"correct":"a1"},{"id":"parameter","options":[{"id":"p2","en":"absolute neutrophil count and temperature","zh":"绝对中性粒细胞计数和体温"},{"id":"p3","en":"serum phosphate and respiratory effort","zh":"血清磷和呼吸用力"},{"id":"p1","en":"serum potassium and cardiac rhythm","zh":"血清钾和心律"}],"correct":"p1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Furosemide can contribute to hypokalemia, which increases dysrhythmia risk. The nurse should notify the provider and prepare to administer prescribed potassium replacement, while monitoring potassium and cardiac rhythm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呋塞米可导致低钾，增加心律失常风险。护士应通知医嘱提供者，并准备按医嘱给予补钾，同时监测钾水平和心律。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Loop diuretics can waste potassium. When low potassium appears with ventricular ectopy, connect the lab to the rhythm change and choose escalation plus prescribed replacement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"袢利尿剂会导致钾丢失。低钾伴室性异位搏动时，要把实验室结果和心律变化联系起来，选择升级处理并按医嘱补充。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1872,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.402","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.402.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.402.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[465,579],"terminalOffsetsZh":[165,194],"fullStemEn":"A medical-surgical unit policy states: activate the rapid response team for an acute change in condition, including new respiratory distress, SpO2 less than 90% despite oxygen, systolic blood pressure less than 90 mm Hg, or new decreased responsiveness. A client 2 hr after abdominal surgery is restless, difficult to arouse, has SpO2 86% on 4 L/min nasal cannula, RR 8/min, and blood pressure 82/48 mm Hg. The primary provider has not returned a page after 5 min. Complete the bowtie by selecting the situation, two nursing actions, and two parameters to communicate or monitor.","fullStemZh":"某内外科病区政策规定：出现急性病情变化时应启动快速反应小组，包括新发呼吸窘迫、吸氧后 SpO2 仍低于 90%、收缩压低于 90 mm Hg，或新发反应迟钝。某腹部手术后 2 小时的患者烦躁、难以唤醒，鼻导管 4 L/min 吸氧时 SpO2 86%，呼吸 8 次/分，血压 82/48 mm Hg。主管医师 5 分钟后仍未回电。请选择该情况、两项护理措施，以及两项需要沟通或监测的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the situation, two nursing actions, and two parameters to communicate or monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择该情况、两项护理措施，以及两项需要沟通或监测的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The primary provider has not returned a page after 5 min.","penultimateSentenceZh":"主管医师 5 分钟后仍未回电。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Expected postoperative discomfort","zh":"预期的术后不适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Deteriorating client requiring rapid-response activation","zh":"病情恶化且需要启动快速反应的患者"},{"id":"c3","en":"Stable handoff delay","zh":"稳定患者的交班延迟"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two nursing actions","zh":"两项护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Remain with the client and support airway and oxygenation","zh":"留在患者身边并支持气道与氧合"},{"id":"a1","en":"Activate the rapid response team according to policy","zh":"按政策启动快速反应小组"},{"id":"a4","en":"Wait until the provider returns the page","zh":"等待医师回电"},{"id":"a3","en":"Complete routine documentation before calling anyone else","zh":"先完成常规记录再联系他人"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to report or monitor","zh":"两项需报告或监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Respiratory rate and SpO2 response to oxygen","zh":"呼吸频率及吸氧后的 SpO2 反应"},{"id":"p2","en":"Blood pressure trend and level of responsiveness","zh":"血压趋势和反应程度"},{"id":"p3","en":"Percentage of lunch eaten","zh":"午餐进食百分比"},{"id":"p4","en":"Room temperature reading","zh":"病房温度读数"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client meets the stated rapid-response criteria because oxygenation, ventilation, blood pressure, and responsiveness have acutely worsened. The nurse should activate rapid response while continuing immediate supportive nursing care and should report respiratory status and blood pressure trends.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者符合题干中的快速反应启动标准，因为氧合、通气、血压和反应程度均出现急性恶化。护士应启动快速反应，同时继续提供即时支持性护理，并报告呼吸状态和血压趋势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a stem gives facility escalation triggers, match the data to those triggers and do not wait for a delayed call-back when the client is unstable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干给出机构升级触发条件时，应将资料与触发条件对应；患者不稳定时，不应等待迟迟未回的电话。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1873,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.403","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.403.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.403.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[592,612],"terminalOffsetsZh":[158,165],"fullStemEn":"Facility chain-of-command policy states: for an unresolved safety concern that could cause serious harm, the RN notifies the charge nurse and attempts to reach the ordering provider; if the provider does not respond within 10 min or dismisses the concern without assessment, the RN escalates to the nursing supervisor and medical director. A newly admitted client with a documented allergy to iodinated contrast is scheduled for contrast CT in 20 min. The order does not mention premedication or allergy review. The ordering provider says by phone, 'Just send the client,' and ends the call. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"机构指挥链政策规定：对于可能造成严重伤害且未解决的安全问题，注册护士应通知责任护士并尝试联系开单医师；若医师 10 分钟内未回应，或未评估即否定该疑虑，护士应升级至护理主管和医疗主任。某新入院患者记录有碘造影剂过敏史，20 分钟后安排增强 CT。医嘱未提及预处理或过敏复核。开单医师电话中说：“直接送去”，随后挂断。请完成弓形题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The ordering provider says by phone, 'Just send the client,' and ends the call.","penultimateSentenceZh":"开单医师电话中说：“直接送去”，随后挂断。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c5","en":"Routine diagnostic scheduling delay","zh":"常规诊断检查排程延误"},{"id":"c4","en":"Unresolved safety concern requiring chain-of-command escalation","zh":"未解决且需要按指挥链升级的安全问题"},{"id":"c6","en":"Informed-consent teaching need only","zh":"仅为知情同意宣教需要"}],"correct":"c4"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two nursing actions","zh":"两项护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a6","en":"Notify the charge nurse or supervisor per chain-of-command policy","zh":"按指挥链政策通知责任护士或主管"},{"id":"a5","en":"Hold transport until the allergy conflict is addressed","zh":"在过敏冲突处理前暂缓转运"},{"id":"a8","en":"Remove the allergy from the record to avoid delay","zh":"为避免延误而从病历中删除过敏记录"},{"id":"a7","en":"Send the client because the provider gave a verbal instruction","zh":"因医师口头要求而送患者检查"}],"correct":["a5","a6"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two facts to communicate up the chain","zh":"向上级沟通的两项事实"},"tokens":[{"id":"p6","en":"Provider response and time remaining before transport","zh":"医师回应情况及距离转运的剩余时间"},{"id":"p5","en":"Documented iodinated contrast allergy and planned contrast exposure","zh":"已记录碘造影剂过敏史及计划使用造影剂"},{"id":"p7","en":"Client's preferred meal choice","zh":"患者偏好的餐食"},{"id":"p8","en":"Name of the transporter assigned","zh":"被安排转运人员的姓名"}],"correct":["p5","p6"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The situation is an unresolved safety concern requiring chain-of-command escalation. The nurse should hold transport until the conflict is addressed by the appropriate chain and should notify the charge nurse or supervisor while communicating the allergy and order conflict.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该情况属于未解决且可能造成伤害的安全问题，需要按指挥链升级。护士应暂缓转运，直到通过相应指挥链解决冲突，并通知责任护士或主管，同时说明过敏史与医嘱冲突。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For escalation items, protect the client from the immediate hazard while moving up the stated chain rather than carrying out an unsafe plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到升级处理题，应先保护患者免受眼前危险，同时按题干给出的指挥链上报，而不是执行不安全安排。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1874,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.404","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.404.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.404.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[485,505],"terminalOffsetsZh":[148,155],"fullStemEn":"During an external disaster drill, the facility uses START triage. The protocol states: clients who can walk are tagged green; clients who are not breathing after airway repositioning are tagged black; clients with respirations greater than 30/min, absent radial pulse, uncontrolled major bleeding, or inability to follow simple commands are tagged red; other nonwalking clients are tagged yellow. A victim cannot walk, has RR 36/min, a weak radial pulse, and follows simple commands. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"在一次院外灾难演练中，机构使用 START 分诊。协议规定：能行走者标记为绿色；调整气道后仍无呼吸者标记为黑色；呼吸频率大于 30 次/分、桡动脉搏动消失、严重出血未控制，或不能遵从简单指令者标记为红色；其他不能行走者标记为黄色。某伤者不能行走，呼吸 36 次/分，桡动脉搏动弱，能遵从简单指令。请完成弓形题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A victim cannot walk, has RR 36/min, a weak radial pulse, and follows simple commands.","penultimateSentenceZh":"某伤者不能行走，呼吸 36 次/分，桡动脉搏动弱，能遵从简单指令。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Triage situation","zh":"分诊情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c7","en":"Immediate/red START triage priority","zh":"START 分诊红色/立即处理优先级"},{"id":"c8","en":"Delayed/yellow START triage priority","zh":"START 分诊黄色/延迟处理优先级"},{"id":"c9","en":"Minor/green START triage priority","zh":"START 分诊绿色/轻伤优先级"}],"correct":"c7"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two nursing actions","zh":"两项护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a9","en":"Apply a red triage tag","zh":"贴红色分诊标签"},{"id":"a12","en":"Delay tagging until full registration is complete","zh":"等完整登记后再贴标签"},{"id":"a10","en":"Direct the victim to immediate life-saving interventions per protocol","zh":"按协议将伤者送往即时救命干预区域"},{"id":"a11","en":"Send the victim to the walking-wounded area","zh":"将伤者送往可步行轻伤区"}],"correct":["a9","a10"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two START findings to report or reassess","zh":"两项需报告或复评的 START 资料"},"tokens":[{"id":"p12","en":"Complete home medication list","zh":"完整家庭用药清单"},{"id":"p11","en":"Insurance status","zh":"保险状态"},{"id":"p10","en":"Radial pulse quality and ability to follow commands","zh":"桡动脉搏动情况及遵从指令能力"},{"id":"p9","en":"Respiratory rate of 36/min","zh":"呼吸频率 36 次/分"}],"correct":["p9","p10"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The victim meets the stated red/immediate criterion because respiratory rate is greater than 30/min. The nurse should tag the victim red, direct immediate life-saving interventions within protocol, and communicate respiratory rate and perfusion or mental status findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该伤者符合题干中红色/立即处理标准，因为呼吸频率大于 30 次/分。护士应将其标记为红色，按协议安排即时救命干预，并沟通呼吸频率以及灌注或意识状态资料。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In disaster triage, use the protocol in the stem rather than normal one-client prioritization rules.","testTakingStrategyZh":"灾难分诊题应使用题干提供的协议，而不是普通单个患者的优先处理规则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1875,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.405","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.405.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.405.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[427,447],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,107],"fullStemEn":"The emergency department disaster plan states: for suspected chemical exposure, keep potentially contaminated clients outside the clean treatment area, remove contaminated clothing if safe, begin decontamination using the hazardous-materials protocol, and notify the incident command leader. A group arrives after a factory spill. One client has liquid on clothing, eye burning, and coughing, and walks toward the triage desk. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"急诊科灾难预案规定：疑似化学暴露者应留在清洁治疗区外；在安全情况下脱去污染衣物；按危险物质协议开始去污；并通知事件指挥负责人。工厂泄漏后一组人员到达。某患者衣物上有液体，眼部灼痛、咳嗽，并走向分诊台。请完成弓形题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"One client has liquid on clothing, eye burning, and coughing, and walks toward the triage desk.","penultimateSentenceZh":"某患者衣物上有液体，眼部灼痛、咳嗽，并走向分诊台。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c12","en":"Visitor-control issue only","zh":"仅为访客管控问题"},{"id":"c10","en":"Hazardous-materials exposure requiring decontamination before clean-area entry","zh":"危险物质暴露，进入清洁区前需要去污"},{"id":"c11","en":"Routine ambulatory triage presentation","zh":"常规步行分诊就诊"}],"correct":"c10"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two nursing actions","zh":"两项护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a14","en":"Activate the decontamination and incident-command process","zh":"启动去污和事件指挥流程"},{"id":"a16","en":"Offer oral fluids before decontamination","zh":"去污前给予口服液体"},{"id":"a15","en":"Bring the client directly to the triage desk","zh":"将患者直接带到分诊台"},{"id":"a13","en":"Stop the client from entering the clean treatment area","zh":"阻止患者进入清洁治疗区"}],"correct":["a13","a14"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two findings to report or monitor","zh":"两项需报告或监测的资料"},"tokens":[{"id":"p14","en":"Eye burning, cough, and respiratory status","zh":"眼部灼痛、咳嗽和呼吸状态"},{"id":"p13","en":"Visible liquid contamination on clothing","zh":"衣物上可见液体污染"},{"id":"p16","en":"Parking location after arrival","zh":"到达后的停车位置"},{"id":"p15","en":"Employment status at the factory","zh":"在工厂的雇佣状态"}],"correct":["p13","p14"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client represents a hazardous-materials exposure requiring decontamination before entry into the clean area. The nurse should stop the client from entering, activate the decontamination or incident-command process, and report exposure route and symptoms.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者属于危险物质暴露，需要在进入清洁区前去污。护士应阻止其进入清洁区域，启动去污或事件指挥流程，并报告暴露途径和症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For contamination scenarios, protect the care environment before routine registration or room placement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到污染情境，应先保护照护环境，再进行常规登记或安置病房。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1876,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.406","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.406.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.406.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[413,433],"terminalOffsetsZh":[128,135],"fullStemEn":"Facility policy states: if a client arrests and the code status cannot be verified in the health record or with a valid transfer document, staff begin resuscitation while another team member verifies code status. A long-term care resident arrives without paperwork. The family says, 'There is a DNR somewhere,' but the electronic record visible to the ED lists full code. The client becomes pulseless and apneic. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"机构政策规定：若患者心搏骤停且无法在病历或有效转诊文件中核实代码状态，工作人员应开始复苏，同时由另一名团队成员核实代码状态。某长期护理机构居民到达急诊时未携带文件。家属说：“应该有 DNR 文件”，但急诊可见电子病历显示为全力抢救。患者随后无脉搏、无呼吸。请完成弓形题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client becomes pulseless and apneic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者随后无脉搏、无呼吸。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c15","en":"Routine transfer paperwork delay","zh":"常规转诊文件延迟"},{"id":"c13","en":"Code-status conflict with no verified DNR available during arrest","zh":"心搏骤停时无已核实 DNR 的代码状态冲突"},{"id":"c14","en":"Verified DNR order requiring no resuscitation","zh":"已核实且要求不复苏的 DNR 医嘱"}],"correct":"c13"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two nursing actions","zh":"两项护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a18","en":"Have another team member verify code status and transfer documents","zh":"请另一名团队成员核实代码状态和转诊文件"},{"id":"a20","en":"Ask the family to leave before any explanation is given","zh":"未作解释即要求家属离开"},{"id":"a17","en":"Begin resuscitation according to the stated policy","zh":"按题干政策开始复苏"},{"id":"a19","en":"Withhold all resuscitation based only on the family's statement","zh":"仅凭家属陈述停止所有复苏"}],"correct":["a17","a18"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two facts to communicate or verify","zh":"两项需沟通或核实的事实"},"tokens":[{"id":"p18","en":"Pulselessness, apnea, and time resuscitation began","zh":"无脉搏、无呼吸及开始复苏的时间"},{"id":"p19","en":"Preferred room assignment","zh":"偏好的病房安排"},{"id":"p17","en":"Visible full-code status and absence of valid DNR paperwork","zh":"可见全力抢救状态及缺少有效 DNR 文件"},{"id":"p20","en":"Current diet order","zh":"当前饮食医嘱"}],"correct":["p17","p18"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is a code-status/order conflict with unverifiable DNR documentation. Under the stated policy, resuscitation begins while another team member verifies the directive and communicates the discrepancy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是代码状态与医嘱/文件冲突，且 DNR 文件无法核实。根据题干政策，应开始复苏，同时由另一名团队成员核实指示并沟通不一致之处。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When DNR documentation is uncertain during arrest, follow the facility policy in the stem and avoid withholding resuscitation based only on verbal uncertainty.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当心搏骤停时 DNR 文件不明确，应遵循题干中的机构政策，不应仅凭口头不确定信息停止复苏。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1877,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.407","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.407.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.407.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[555,575],"terminalOffsetsZh":[159,166],"fullStemEn":"A competent adult client has a scanned advance directive and current provider order stating 'DNR/DNI; comfort-focused treatment; no intubation.' The client is awake and says, 'I do not want a breathing tube.' The spouse says, 'Do everything, including intubation.' The client's respiratory distress is worsening, but the client can still answer questions. Facility policy states that a competent client's current expressed wishes and valid directive guide care, and disagreements are escalated to the charge nurse, provider, and ethics consult if needed. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名有决策能力的成年患者有已扫描的预立医疗指示及当前医嘱，内容为“DNR/DNI；以舒适为重点；不插管”。患者清醒并说：“我不要呼吸管。”配偶说：“什么都要做，包括插管。”患者呼吸窘迫加重，但仍能回答问题。机构政策规定，有决策能力患者当前表达的意愿和有效指示指导照护；若有分歧，应升级至责任护士、医师，必要时伦理咨询。请完成弓形题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy states that a competent client's current expressed wishes and valid directive guide care, and disagreements are escalated to the charge nurse, provider, and ethics consult if needed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定，有决策能力患者当前表达的意愿和有效指示指导照护；若有分歧，应升级至责任护士、医师，必要时伦理咨询。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c18","en":"Routine family teaching need","zh":"常规家属宣教需要"},{"id":"c16","en":"Family request conflicts with a competent client's valid directive and current wishes","zh":"家属要求与有决策能力患者的有效指示和当前意愿相冲突"},{"id":"c17","en":"Undocumented end-of-life preference","zh":"未记录的临终偏好"}],"correct":"c16"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two nursing actions","zh":"两项护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a22","en":"Notify the provider and charge nurse; request ethics support if conflict persists","zh":"通知医师和责任护士；冲突持续时请求伦理支持"},{"id":"a24","en":"Tell the spouse the request will be ignored and leave the room","zh":"告知配偶其要求会被忽略并离开病房"},{"id":"a21","en":"Advocate for the client's expressed DNR/DNI wishes","zh":"维护患者表达的 DNR/DNI 意愿"},{"id":"a23","en":"Prepare intubation because the spouse requests full treatment","zh":"因配偶要求全力治疗而准备插管"}],"correct":["a21","a22"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to reassess or report","zh":"两项需复评或报告的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p21","en":"Respiratory distress and continued ability to answer questions","zh":"呼吸窘迫程度及是否仍能回答问题"},{"id":"p23","en":"Spouse's insurance information","zh":"配偶的保险信息"},{"id":"p22","en":"Comfort level and response to comfort-focused interventions","zh":"舒适程度及对舒适照护措施的反应"},{"id":"p24","en":"Meal tray delivery time","zh":"餐盘送达时间"}],"correct":["p21","p22"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The situation is a surrogate-family request that conflicts with the competent client's expressed wishes and valid directive. The nurse should advocate for the client's stated preferences, notify the provider and charge nurse, and monitor respiratory distress and comfort while the conflict is addressed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该情况是代理/家属要求与有决策能力患者的表达意愿及有效指示相冲突。护士应维护患者已表达的偏好，通知医师和责任护士，并在处理冲突期间监测呼吸窘迫和舒适程度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a competent client speaks for themselves, the client's current wishes outweigh a conflicting family request, especially when documentation supports the client's choice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有决策能力的患者能够表达意愿时，患者当前意愿优先于相冲突的家属要求，尤其是在文件支持患者选择时。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1878,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.408","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.408.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.408.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[348,383],"terminalOffsetsZh":[99,110],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving a new blood transfusion develops chills, flank pain, and hypotension. Facility policy states: stop the transfusion for suspected transfusion reaction, maintain IV access with normal saline using new tubing, assess the client, notify the provider and blood bank, then document and send required blood/tubing specimens per policy. Place the nursing actions in order.","fullStemZh":"某患者开始输注新的血液制品后出现寒战、腰背痛和低血压。机构政策规定：疑似输血反应时停止输血；使用新输液管以生理盐水维持静脉通路；评估患者；通知医师和血库；随后按政策记录并送检所需血液/输血管路标本。请按顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy states: stop the transfusion for suspected transfusion reaction, maintain IV access with normal saline using new tubing, assess the client, notify the provider and blood bank, then document and send required blood/tubing specimens per policy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：疑似输血反应时停止输血；使用新输液管以生理盐水维持静脉通路；评估患者；通知医师和血库；随后按政策记录并送检所需血液/输血管路标本。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document and send required blood/tubing specimens per policy.","zh":"按政策记录并送检所需血液/输血管路标本。"},{"id":"B","en":"Maintain IV access with normal saline using new tubing.","zh":"使用新输液管以生理盐水维持静脉通路。"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the provider and blood bank.","zh":"通知医师和血库。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the transfusion.","zh":"停止输血。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess vital signs, symptoms, and airway/breathing status.","zh":"评估生命体征、症状以及气道/呼吸状态。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The safest sequence is to stop the possible source of harm, preserve IV access with appropriate fluid and tubing, assess the client, notify the required parties, and then complete documentation and specimen handling according to policy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最安全的顺序是先停止可能造成伤害的来源，用适当液体和新管路维持静脉通路，评估患者，通知相关人员，然后按政策完成记录和标本处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When harm is occurring during an infusion, stop the exposure before reporting and paperwork, while maintaining access for treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"输注过程中发生伤害时，应先停止暴露，同时保留治疗通路，再进行报告和文书处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1879,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.409","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.409.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.409.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[313,340],"terminalOffsetsZh":[99,108],"fullStemEn":"An emergency department receives notice of a bus crash with 30 victims arriving in 10 min. The hospital disaster plan states: activate the incident command system, clear and designate treatment zones, call in disaster staffing, perform rapid triage at arrival, and route victims to treatment zones by triage tag. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"急诊科接到通知：一辆公交车事故中 30 名伤者将在 10 分钟后到达。医院灾难预案规定：启动事件指挥系统；清理并指定治疗区域；召集灾难应急人员；伤者到达时快速分诊；按分诊标签将伤者送至相应治疗区域。请按顺序排列措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The hospital disaster plan states: activate the incident command system, clear and designate treatment zones, call in disaster staffing, perform rapid triage at arrival, and route victims to treatment zones by triage tag.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院灾难预案规定：启动事件指挥系统；清理并指定治疗区域；召集灾难应急人员；伤者到达时快速分诊；按分诊标签将伤者送至相应治疗区域。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Route victims to treatment zones by triage tag.","zh":"按分诊标签将伤者送至治疗区域。"},{"id":"D","en":"Perform rapid triage as victims arrive.","zh":"伤者到达时进行快速分诊。"},{"id":"C","en":"Call in disaster staffing according to the plan.","zh":"按预案召集灾难应急人员。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the incident command system.","zh":"启动事件指挥系统。"},{"id":"B","en":"Clear and designate treatment zones.","zh":"清理并指定治疗区域。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The incident command structure is activated to coordinate the response, then space and staffing are prepared before victims arrive. Rapid triage is performed on arrival, followed by routing to the appropriate treatment areas.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应先启动事件指挥结构以协调应对，然后在伤者到达前准备空间和人员。伤者到达时快速分诊，随后按分诊类别送往相应治疗区域。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In disaster workflows, establish command and capacity before victims arrive, then triage and route rather than using routine rooming processes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"灾难流程中，应在伤者到达前建立指挥和容量准备，随后分诊并分流，而不是使用常规安置流程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1880,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.410","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.410.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.410.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[404,431],"terminalOffsetsZh":[99,108],"fullStemEn":"A client exposed to an unknown powder arrives at the emergency department entrance. The facility hazardous-materials protocol states: prevent entry into the clean area, notify incident command/security, direct the client to the decontamination area, have the client remove contaminated clothing if safe and place it in labeled bags, then begin decontamination before medical screening in the clean area. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名接触未知粉末的患者到达急诊入口。机构危险物质协议规定：阻止其进入清洁区；通知事件指挥/安保；引导患者至去污区；在安全情况下让患者脱去污染衣物并放入标记袋；随后开始去污，再进入清洁区进行医学筛查。请按顺序排列措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility hazardous-materials protocol states: prevent entry into the clean area, notify incident command/security, direct the client to the decontamination area, have the client remove contaminated clothing if safe and place it in labeled bags, then begin decontamination before medical screening in the clean area.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构危险物质协议规定：阻止其进入清洁区；通知事件指挥/安保；引导患者至去污区；在安全情况下让患者脱去污染衣物并放入标记袋；随后开始去污，再进入清洁区进行医学筛查。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Notify incident command/security.","zh":"通知事件指挥/安保。"},{"id":"C","en":"Direct the client to the decontamination area.","zh":"引导患者到去污区。"},{"id":"E","en":"Begin decontamination before clean-area screening.","zh":"在进入清洁区筛查前开始去污。"},{"id":"A","en":"Prevent the client from entering the clean treatment area.","zh":"阻止患者进入清洁治疗区。"},{"id":"D","en":"Have the client remove contaminated clothing if safe and place it in labeled bags.","zh":"在安全情况下让患者脱去污染衣物并放入标记袋。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sequence protects the clean environment and staff, activates command support, moves the client to the correct zone, removes contaminated clothing when safe, and then performs decontamination before clean-area care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该顺序可保护清洁环境和工作人员，启动指挥支持，将患者转至正确区域，在安全时脱去污染衣物，然后在清洁区照护前完成去污。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For hazardous materials, containment and decontamination come before routine medical screening in the clean area.","testTakingStrategyZh":"危险物质情境中，控制污染和去污应先于清洁区内的常规医学筛查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1881,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_esc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.411","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.411.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.411.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[436,463],"terminalOffsetsZh":[119,128],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalized client with decision-making capacity tells the nurse, 'I want to change my code status from full code to DNR.' The current chart still lists full code. Facility policy states: assess immediate safety and capacity cues, notify the provider, ensure the provider discusses and writes the appropriate order if indicated, update the care team after the order is entered, and document the client's statement and notifications. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名住院且有决策能力的患者告诉护士：“我想把代码状态从全力抢救改为 DNR。”当前病历仍显示全力抢救。机构政策规定：评估即时安全和决策能力线索；通知医师；确保医师沟通并在适当时开立相应医嘱；医嘱录入后更新照护团队；记录患者陈述和通知情况。请按顺序排列措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy states: assess immediate safety and capacity cues, notify the provider, ensure the provider discusses and writes the appropriate order if indicated, update the care team after the order is entered, and document the client's statement and notifications.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：评估即时安全和决策能力线索；通知医师；确保医师沟通并在适当时开立相应医嘱；医嘱录入后更新照护团队；记录患者陈述和通知情况。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document the client's statement and notifications.","zh":"记录患者陈述和通知情况。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess immediate safety and decision-making capacity cues.","zh":"评估即时安全和决策能力线索。"},{"id":"D","en":"Update the care team after the new order appears in the chart.","zh":"新医嘱出现在病历后更新照护团队。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider of the client's request.","zh":"将患者请求通知医师。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure the provider discussion occurs and the code-status order is entered if indicated.","zh":"确保医师完成沟通，并在适当时录入代码状态医嘱。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first assesses immediate safety and capacity cues, then notifies the provider so the required discussion and order can occur. Once the order is entered, the team is updated and the nurse documents the statement and notifications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先评估即时安全和决策能力线索，再通知医师，以便进行必要沟通并开立医嘱。医嘱录入后，更新照护团队，并记录患者陈述和通知情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A client's request to change code status requires prompt escalation for provider order entry; the nurse does not independently change the code-status order.","testTakingStrategyZh":"患者要求更改代码状态时，需要及时升级给医师开立医嘱；护士不能自行更改代码状态医嘱。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1882,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.412","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.412.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.412.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[52,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,32],"fullStemEn":"A charge nurse is reviewing disclosure-log entries. Highlight the entry that represents a HIPAA breach.","fullStemZh":"护士长正在审查信息披露记录。请标出表示 HIPAA 违规的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that represents a HIPAA breach.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出表示 HIPAA 违规的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A charge nurse is reviewing disclosure-log entries.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士长正在审查信息披露记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0730 — Client requested that discharge instructions be sent to the secure portal account listed in the chart.","zh":"0730 — 患者要求将出院指导发送到病历中登记的安全门户账户。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"0815 — Nurse verified two client identifiers before discussing the plan of care by phone.","zh":"0815 — 护士在电话中讨论护理计划前核对了患者的两个身份识别信息。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0940 — Nurse told the client’s neighbor in the waiting room that the client is being treated for alcohol withdrawal.","zh":"0940 — 护士在候诊区告诉患者的邻居，该患者正在接受酒精戒断治疗。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"1010 — Case manager released the medication list to the skilled nursing facility named on the transfer form.","zh":"1010 — 个案管理师将用药清单提供给转院表上指定的专业护理机构。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Telling a neighbor protected health information without the client’s permission is an unauthorized disclosure and a HIPAA breach.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未经患者同意向邻居透露受保护的健康信息，属于未经授权披露，是 HIPAA 违规。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate care-related disclosures from casual disclosures. Information shared with unrelated visitors or bystanders is the privacy concern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分与护理相关的信息披露和随意透露。向无关访客或旁观者透露信息才是隐私问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1883,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.413","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.413.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.413.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,38],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is reviewing a handoff note before transfer to a rehabilitation facility. Highlight the line that shows a required handoff element is missing.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查患者转入康复机构前的交班记录。请标出显示缺少必要交班内容的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the line that shows a required handoff element is missing.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出显示缺少必要交班内容的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is reviewing a handoff note before transfer to a rehabilitation facility.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查患者转入康复机构前的交班记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Diagnosis: left hip fracture repair; weight bearing as tolerated with walker.","zh":"诊断：左髋骨折修复术后；可耐受范围内负重，使用助行器。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Medications: acetaminophen scheduled; oxycodone as needed; stool softener prescribed.","zh":"用药：按时使用对乙酰氨基酚；必要时使用羟考酮；已开具软便剂。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Allergies: not included because the receiving nurse can look them up after arrival.","zh":"过敏史：未写入，因为接收护士可在患者到达后再查询。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Follow-up: orthopedic appointment scheduled for 10 days after discharge.","zh":"随访：骨科复诊安排在出院后 10 天。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Equipment: walker sent with client; raised toilet seat to be delivered today.","zh":"设备：助行器随患者转送；加高马桶座今天送达。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Allergies are a core safety element in a transfer handoff. Omitting them creates medication and treatment risk at the receiving facility.","rationaleCorrectZh":"过敏史是转院交班中的核心安全内容。遗漏过敏史会使接收机构在用药和治疗时产生风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For handoff questions, look for missing safety-critical basics: allergies, code status when relevant, current condition, medications, precautions, and pending results.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到交班题，寻找缺失的关键安全基本信息：过敏史、相关时的抢救意愿、当前状况、用药、注意事项和待出结果。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1884,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.414","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.414.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.414.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,48],"fullStemEn":"A client reports that another patient’s family member saw the client’s printed laboratory results at the nurses’ station. Place the nurse’s actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"患者报告说，另一名患者的家属在护士站看到了自己的纸质检验结果。请将护士的处理步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse’s actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的处理步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client reports that another patient’s family member saw the client’s printed laboratory results at the nurses’ station.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者报告说，另一名患者的家属在护士站看到了自己的纸质检验结果。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Document the facts in the facility’s privacy or incident-reporting system.","zh":"在机构的隐私或事件报告系统中记录事实。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask the client what information they believe was seen and who may have seen it.","zh":"询问患者认为哪些信息被看见，以及可能是谁看见了。"},{"id":"A","en":"Move the laboratory results out of public view and secure the document.","zh":"将检验结果移出公众视线，并妥善保管文件。"},{"id":"E","en":"Tell the client the concern will be handled through the facility’s privacy process.","zh":"告知患者该问题会通过机构的隐私处理流程处理。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the charge nurse or privacy officer according to facility policy.","zh":"根据机构政策通知护士长或隐私负责人。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first stops further exposure, then gathers facts, follows the reporting chain, documents objectively, and gives the client a process-based response without speculating.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先阻止信息继续暴露，再收集事实，按报告流程上报，客观记录，并以流程为基础回应患者，避免猜测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In privacy incidents, first contain the breach, then collect facts, report through policy, document objectively, and communicate without blame or speculation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到隐私事件，先控制泄露，再收集事实，按政策上报，客观记录，并避免指责或猜测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1885,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.415","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.415.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.415.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,242],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,70],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews a discharge-instruction sheet for a client who requested a certified medical interpreter and stated, “I do not want my son to interpret my medical instructions.” Highlight the entry that contradicts the client’s stated wishes.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名患者的出院指导单。患者要求使用合格医学口译员，并表示：“我不想让我儿子翻译我的医疗指导。”请标出与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that contradicts the client’s stated wishes.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse reviews a discharge-instruction sheet for a client who requested a certified medical interpreter and stated, “I do not want my son to interpret my medical instructions.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者要求使用合格医学口译员，并表示：“我不想让我儿子翻译我的医疗指导。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Preferred language documented as Mandarin; interpreter need flagged in chart.","zh":"已记录首选语言为普通话；病历中已标记需要口译服务。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Discharge medications reviewed using the client’s adult son as interpreter because he was present.","zh":"因患者成年儿子在场，使用其作为口译员讲解出院用药。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Client demonstrated how to measure the prescribed oral antibiotic dose.","zh":"患者演示了如何量取医嘱口服抗生素剂量。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Follow-up appointment time written in English and Chinese on the instruction sheet.","zh":"随访预约时间已用英文和中文写在指导单上。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client specifically declined having the son interpret medical instructions. Advocacy includes honoring the client’s communication preference and using qualified interpretation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者明确拒绝让儿子翻译医疗指导。维护患者权益包括尊重其沟通意愿，并使用合格口译服务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client states a preference about communication or participation in care, the conflicting documentation is usually the advocacy problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者明确表达沟通或参与护理的偏好时，与该偏好相冲突的记录通常就是维护权益的问题点。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1886,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.416","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.416.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.416.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,53],"fullStemEn":"A nurse disagrees with a colleague about whether a client is ready for discharge teaching after receiving new oxygen equipment. Place the conflict-resolution actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名护士与同事对患者在收到新的氧疗设备后是否已准备好接受出院指导存在分歧。请将冲突处理步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the conflict-resolution actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将冲突处理步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse disagrees with a colleague about whether a client is ready for discharge teaching after receiving new oxygen equipment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名护士与同事对患者在收到新的氧疗设备后是否已准备好接受出院指导存在分歧。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"State the shared goal of a safe discharge and describe the specific concern.","zh":"说明共同目标是安全出院，并描述具体担忧。"},{"id":"C","en":"Listen to the colleague’s assessment and clarify any different information.","zh":"听取同事的评估，并澄清双方掌握的信息差异。"},{"id":"D","en":"Agree on a plan to assess the client’s oxygen-equipment use with teach-back.","zh":"共同制定计划，通过回授法评估患者使用氧疗设备的能力。"},{"id":"F","en":"Document the agreed discharge-readiness plan in the care record.","zh":"在护理记录中记录达成一致的出院准备计划。"},{"id":"E","en":"Escalate to the charge nurse if the disagreement remains unresolved.","zh":"若分歧仍未解决，则上报护士长。"},{"id":"A","en":"Speak with the colleague privately and use a calm, respectful tone.","zh":"私下与同事沟通，并保持冷静、尊重的语气。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Conflict resolution begins privately and respectfully, focuses on the shared goal and objective concern, includes listening, seeks a practical plan, escalates if needed, and documents the resulting plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"冲突处理应先私下尊重沟通，聚焦共同目标和客观担忧，听取对方意见，尝试制定实际计划；若仍未解决再上报，并记录最终计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For workplace conflict, choose the least escalated safe action first, then move up the chain only if direct respectful communication does not resolve the concern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理工作场所冲突时，先选择最低层级且安全的直接沟通；若无法解决，再逐级上报。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1887,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.417","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.417.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.417.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,45],"fullStemEn":"A client is being discharged home with a new wound vacuum and home health visits. Place the discharge-readiness actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者将带新的负压伤口治疗设备出院，并安排家庭护理随访。请将出院准备步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the discharge-readiness actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将出院准备步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is being discharged home with a new wound vacuum and home health visits.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者将带新的负压伤口治疗设备出院，并安排家庭护理随访。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Teach the client when to call for alarms, leaking dressing, fever, or increased drainage.","zh":"指导患者出现报警、敷料漏气、发热或引流增加时何时求助。"},{"id":"E","en":"Send the current wound orders, device settings, drainage description, and contact information to home health.","zh":"将最新伤口医嘱、设备设置、引流情况描述和联系信息发送给家庭护理机构。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use teach-back to confirm the client can explain the plan and emergency contact steps.","zh":"使用回授法确认患者能说明护理计划和紧急联系步骤。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client’s home support, supplies, transportation, and ability to manage the device.","zh":"评估患者的家庭支持、用品、交通以及管理设备的能力。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify prescriptions, equipment delivery, follow-up appointments, and home health referral.","zh":"核对处方、设备送达、随访预约和家庭护理转介。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Discharge planning begins with assessment of barriers and support, then verification of services and supplies, focused teaching, teach-back, and complete handoff to the receiving service.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出院计划应先评估障碍和支持，再核对服务与用品，进行重点宣教，使用回授法确认理解，最后向接收服务方完整交班。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge workflows, think: assess barriers, arrange resources, teach, verify understanding, then hand off to the next care team.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理出院流程题时，可按“评估障碍、安排资源、宣教、确认理解、交班给下一护理团队”的顺序思考。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1888,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.418","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.418.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.418.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[115,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,42],"fullStemEn":"A charge nurse reviews documentation after two staff members disagreed about a delayed discharge teaching session. Highlight the entry that reflects poor conflict-resolution practice.","fullStemZh":"护士长在两名工作人员因出院宣教延迟发生分歧后审查记录。请标出反映冲突处理不当的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that reflects poor conflict-resolution practice.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出反映冲突处理不当的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A charge nurse reviews documentation after two staff members disagreed about a delayed discharge teaching session.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士长在两名工作人员因出院宣教延迟发生分歧后审查记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0900 — Primary nurse asked the colleague to discuss the concern away from the hallway.","zh":"0900 — 责任护士请同事离开走廊，私下讨论该问题。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"0905 — Primary nurse stated, “I am concerned the client cannot safely explain the oxygen setup yet.”","zh":"0905 — 责任护士表示：“我担心患者目前还不能安全说明氧气设备的使用方法。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0910 — Colleague said at the nurses’ station, “You are just trying to make my discharge late again.”","zh":"0910 — 同事在护士站说：“你就是想再次拖延我的出院安排。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"0915 — Both nurses agreed to repeat teach-back before notifying the provider that discharge teaching was complete.","zh":"0915 — 两名护士同意在通知医务人员出院宣教完成前，重新进行回授确认。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Publicly accusing a coworker shifts the focus from client safety to blame and is poor conflict-resolution practice.","rationaleCorrectZh":"公开指责同事会把重点从患者安全转向责备，属于不良冲突处理方式。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Conflict-resolution answers should sound private, respectful, objective, and client-centered. Public blame is unsafe communication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"冲突处理的正确做法通常是私下、尊重、客观并以患者为中心。公开责备属于不安全沟通。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1889,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.419","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.419.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.419.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,44],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews an SBAR handoff before a client transfers to a step-down unit. Highlight the line that identifies a missing handoff element.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查患者转入降阶护理单元前的 SBAR 交班内容。请标出显示缺少交班要素的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the line that identifies a missing handoff element.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出显示缺少交班要素的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse reviews an SBAR handoff before a client transfers to a step-down unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在审查患者转入降阶护理单元前的 SBAR 交班内容。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Situation: client is transferring after treatment for pneumonia and oxygen requirement is improving.","zh":"情况：患者因肺炎治疗后转出，氧气需求正在改善。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Background: history includes COPD and type 2 diabetes.","zh":"背景：既往史包括慢性阻塞性肺疾病和 2 型糖尿病。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Assessment: current oxygen is 2 L/min by nasal cannula; SpO2 94%.","zh":"评估：目前经鼻导管给氧 2 L/分；血氧饱和度 94%。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Recommendation: receiving nurse can check the chart later for the sputum culture that is still pending.","zh":"建议：痰培养结果仍待出，接收护士之后可自行查看病历。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Safety: client ambulates with one-person assist and becomes short of breath with exertion.","zh":"安全：患者需一人协助行走，活动后会气短。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pending results that may change treatment should be actively included in the handoff, not left for the receiving nurse to discover later.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可能影响治疗的待出结果应主动纳入交班，而不是让接收护士之后自行发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In handoff items, look for results, orders, or safety risks that are pushed off to the next nurse instead of being clearly communicated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"交班题中，要寻找那些被推给下一班护士自行查看、而没有明确交代的结果、医嘱或安全风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1890,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.420","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.420.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.420.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[171,235],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,74],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews notes for a client who is alert, oriented, and states, “I want to make my own decision about going to rehab. Please do not let my daughter decide for me.” Highlight the entry that contradicts the client’s stated wishes.","fullStemZh":"护士正在审查一名患者的记录。该患者清醒、定向良好，并表示：“我想自己决定是否去康复机构。请不要让我女儿替我决定。”请标出与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that contradicts the client’s stated wishes.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Please do not let my daughter decide for me.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"请不要让我女儿替我决定。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Client verbalized understanding of home therapy and inpatient rehabilitation options.","zh":"患者表示理解居家治疗和住院康复两种选择。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Daughter asked to speak with case management about available rehabilitation facilities.","zh":"女儿要求与个案管理人员讨论可选择的康复机构。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Case manager documented rehabilitation placement as accepted based only on the daughter’s preference.","zh":"个案管理人员仅根据女儿的偏好记录为已接受康复机构安置。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Nurse offered to review risks and benefits with the client again before a decision is finalized.","zh":"护士提出在最终决定前再次与患者复查风险和益处。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An alert, oriented client’s stated decision-making preference should be honored. Documenting placement based only on the daughter’s preference contradicts the client’s wishes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于清醒且定向良好的患者，应尊重其本人表达的决策意愿。仅根据女儿偏好记录安置决定，违背了患者意愿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem says the client is alert and oriented, prioritize the client’s own informed preferences over family preferences.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干说明患者清醒且定向良好时，应优先尊重患者本人知情后的偏好，而不是家属偏好。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Please do not let my daughter decide for me.”","controlSentenceZh":"请不要让我女儿替我决定。”"}
{"queueIndex":1891,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.421","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.421.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.421.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,30],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is giving a transfer handoff to a receiving unit. Place the handoff actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士正在向接收单元进行转科交班。请将交班步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the handoff actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将交班步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse is giving a transfer handoff to a receiving unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在向接收单元进行转科交班。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document that handoff was completed and include the receiving nurse’s name.","zh":"记录交班已完成，并写明接收护士姓名。"},{"id":"B","en":"Confirm the identity and role of the receiving nurse.","zh":"确认接收护士的身份和职责。"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide the situation, relevant background, current assessment, and recommended follow-up.","zh":"提供当前情况、相关背景、当前评估和建议的后续处理。"},{"id":"D","en":"Pause for questions and clarify any read-back of critical information.","zh":"留出提问时间，并澄清关键资料的复述内容。"},{"id":"A","en":"Review the chart, current assessment, medications, allergies, pending results, and safety risks.","zh":"复查病历、当前评估、用药、过敏史、待出结果和安全风险。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse prepares the essential information first, verifies the correct receiver, gives a structured report, allows questions and read-back, then documents completion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先准备关键信息，再确认正确接收者，进行结构化交班，留出提问和复述澄清时间，最后记录交班完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A safe handoff is prepared, directed to the correct receiver, structured, interactive, and documented afterward.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全交班应先准备，交给正确接收者，结构化表达，允许互动澄清，并在之后记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A nurse is giving a transfer handoff to a receiving unit.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在向接收单元进行转科交班。"}
{"queueIndex":1892,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.422","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.422.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.422.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[41,93],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,30],"fullStemEn":"A nurse manager audits a disclosure log. Highlight the entry that requires privacy follow-up.","fullStemZh":"护士经理正在审核信息披露记录。请标出需要隐私后续处理的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entry that requires privacy follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要隐私后续处理的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse manager audits a disclosure log.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士经理正在审核信息披露记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0800 — Discharge summary faxed to the home health agency listed on the signed release form.","zh":"0800 — 已将出院小结传真给签署授权表上列出的家庭护理机构。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"0830 — Laboratory results discussed with the provider caring for the client.","zh":"0830 — 已与负责该患者的医务人员讨论检验结果。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0915 — Operative report faxed to the number from an old referral form because the current form was unavailable.","zh":"0915 — 因当前表格无法取得，将手术报告传真至旧转诊表上的号码。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"0945 — Medication list sent to the receiving rehabilitation facility through the approved secure transfer system.","zh":"0945 — 通过批准的安全转送系统将用药清单发送给接收康复机构。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Faxing protected information to an unverified old number risks disclosure to the wrong recipient and requires privacy follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"将受保护信息传真到未经核实的旧号码，可能导致信息披露给错误接收者，需要隐私后续处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for whether the recipient and route were verified. Old, informal, or unverified contact information is a privacy red flag.","testTakingStrategyZh":"注意接收者和发送途径是否经过核实。旧的、非正式的或未经核实的联系方式是隐私风险信号。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1893,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_moc_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.423","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.423.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.423.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,63],"fullStemEn":"A client who is alert and oriented wants to be discharged home with services, but the family insists the client must go to a skilled nursing facility. Place the nurse’s advocacy actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名清醒且定向良好的患者希望在安排服务后回家出院，但家属坚持患者必须去专业护理机构。请将护士维护患者权益的步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse’s advocacy actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士维护患者权益的步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client who is alert and oriented wants to be discharged home with services, but the family insists the client must go to a skilled nursing facility.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名清醒且定向良好的患者希望在安排服务后回家出院，但家属坚持患者必须去专业护理机构。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Notify case management or the interdisciplinary team that the client and family disagree about placement.","zh":"通知个案管理或跨专业团队，说明患者与家属对安置去向存在分歧。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess for immediate safety concerns that would make the current discharge plan unsafe.","zh":"评估是否存在会使当前出院计划不安全的紧急安全问题。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the client’s stated preference, teaching provided, safety concerns, and referrals made.","zh":"记录患者表达的偏好、已提供的宣教、安全担忧和已进行的转介。"},{"id":"A","en":"Speak with the client privately to confirm the client’s wishes and understanding of the options.","zh":"私下与患者交谈，确认患者的意愿以及对各项选择的理解。"},{"id":"D","en":"Facilitate a discussion of home services, skilled nursing options, risks, benefits, and follow-up needs.","zh":"协助讨论居家服务、专业护理机构选择、风险、益处和随访需求。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first confirms the competent client’s wishes privately, assesses safety barriers, involves the appropriate team, facilitates informed discussion, and documents objectively.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先私下确认具备能力患者的意愿，再评估安全障碍，通知合适团队，促进知情讨论，并客观记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Advocacy does not mean ignoring safety. Confirm the client’s wishes, assess safety, bring in resources, support informed choice, and document.","testTakingStrategyZh":"维护患者权益并不等于忽视安全。应确认患者意愿、评估安全、引入资源、支持知情选择并记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1894,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.424","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.424.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.424.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[46,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,32],"fullStemEn":"The nurse observes a sterile dressing change. Highlight the documentation line that describes a break in sterile technique.","fullStemZh":"护士观察一次无菌换药操作。请标出记录中描述无菌技术被破坏的一行。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the documentation line that describes a break in sterile technique.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出记录中描述无菌技术被破坏的一行。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes a sterile dressing change.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士观察一次无菌换药操作。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0900 — Nurse performs hand hygiene and places the sterile dressing kit on a dry bedside table.","zh":"0900 — 护士进行手卫生，并将无菌换药包放在干燥的床旁桌上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"0902 — Nurse checks the package integrity and expiration date before opening the kit.","zh":"0902 — 护士在打开换药包前检查包装完整性和有效期。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0904 — Nurse reaches across the open sterile field to adjust the over-bed light.","zh":"0904 — 护士越过已打开的无菌区去调整床上方照明灯。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"0906 — Nurse keeps sterile-gloved hands above waist level while arranging supplies.","zh":"0906 — 护士整理物品时将戴无菌手套的双手保持在腰部以上。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reaching across an open sterile field contaminates the field because the nurse's arm passes over sterile supplies. The procedure should pause and the contaminated field should be replaced.","rationaleCorrectZh":"越过已打开的无菌区会污染无菌区，因为护士的手臂经过无菌物品上方。应暂停操作，并更换被污染的无菌区。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sterile-technique items, look for movement over, below, or outside the sterile field.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到无菌技术题时，重点寻找越过、低于或离开无菌区的动作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1895,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.425","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.425.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.425.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,94],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,26],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse audits a hygiene procedure note. Highlight the line that requires correction.","fullStemZh":"主管护士审核一份卫生操作记录。请标出需要纠正的一行。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the line that requires correction.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要纠正的一行。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse audits a hygiene procedure note.","penultimateSentenceZh":"主管护士审核一份卫生操作记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"1010 — Nurse applies clean gloves before emptying a urinary drainage bag.","zh":"1010 — 护士在倒尿液引流袋前戴清洁手套。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"1012 — Nurse keeps the drainage spout from touching the collection container.","zh":"1012 — 护士避免引流袋出口接触收集容器。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"1014 — Nurse removes gloves, answers the unit phone, then resumes catheter care without hand hygiene.","zh":"1014 — 护士脱下手套后接听护士站电话，随后未进行手卫生就继续导尿管护理。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"1016 — Nurse documents urine amount, color, and odor after completing care.","zh":"1016 — 护士完成护理后记录尿量、颜色和气味。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hand hygiene is required after glove removal and before returning to client care. Gloves do not replace hand hygiene.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脱手套后以及重新进行患者护理前都必须进行手卫生。手套不能代替手卫生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a task is interrupted, reassess whether hand hygiene is needed before care resumes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"操作被中断时，要重新判断继续护理前是否需要手卫生。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1896,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.426","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.426.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.426.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,37],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews a fall-prevention rounding checklist for a client who is dizzy after receiving an antihypertensive medication. Highlight the checklist entry that is unsafe.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名服用降压药后头晕患者的防跌倒巡视清单。请标出不安全的清单记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the checklist entry that is unsafe.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出不安全的清单记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse reviews a fall-prevention rounding checklist for a client who is dizzy after receiving an antihypertensive medication.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名服用降压药后头晕患者的防跌倒巡视清单。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0730 — Call light placed within reach before the nurse leaves the room.","zh":"0730 — 护士离开房间前将呼叫铃放在患者可触及处。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"0730 — Nonskid footwear applied before the client stands.","zh":"0730 — 患者站立前已穿防滑鞋。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0735 — Bed alarm turned off so the client can walk independently to the bathroom.","zh":"0735 — 关闭床旁报警器，以便患者自行走到卫生间。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"0740 — Nurse reminds the client to request help before ambulating.","zh":"0740 — 护士提醒患者下床行走前先请求帮助。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A dizzy client should not ambulate independently. Turning off the bed alarm removes a fall-prevention safeguard and requires correction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"头晕患者不应自行下床行走。关闭床旁报警器会移除防跌倒保护措施，需要纠正。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the safety measure to the current risk cue. Dizziness means independent ambulation is not the safe choice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要把安全措施与当前风险线索相匹配。头晕提示自行行走并不安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1897,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.427","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.427.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.427.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[68,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,33],"fullStemEn":"The nurse completes an equipment check before starting an infusion. Highlight the finding that requires the nurse to remove the device from use.","fullStemZh":"护士在开始输液前完成设备检查。请标出需要护士停止使用该设备的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the finding that requires the nurse to remove the device from use.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要护士停止使用该设备的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse completes an equipment check before starting an infusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在开始输液前完成设备检查。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Pump screen powers on and displays the facility asset number.","zh":"输液泵屏幕能开机并显示机构资产编号。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Battery indicator shows the pump is charging while connected to power.","zh":"电池指示灯显示输液泵接通电源时正在充电。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Power cord insulation is cracked, with inner wiring visible near the plug.","zh":"电源线绝缘层破裂，插头附近可见内部电线。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Alarm test sounds when the tubing door is opened.","zh":"打开管路门时报警测试有声音。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Visible wiring creates an electrical hazard. The nurse should remove the device from service according to facility process and obtain safe equipment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可见内部电线属于电气危险。护士应按机构流程停止使用该设备，并取得安全设备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Any damaged electrical cord, exposed wire, or device defect should trigger removal from use rather than workaround use.","testTakingStrategyZh":"任何电源线损坏、裸露电线或设备缺陷，都应停止使用，而不是勉强继续使用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1898,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.428","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.428.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.428.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,244],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,78],"fullStemEn":"The nurse wore gloves, gown, face shield, and mask for a procedure with expected body fluid splashing. The facility doffing sequence is gloves, gown, hand hygiene, face shield, mask, hand hygiene. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士在一项可能有体液飞溅的操作中穿戴了手套、隔离衣、面屏和口罩。机构规定的脱卸顺序为：手套、隔离衣、手卫生、面屏、口罩、手卫生。请按正确顺序排列护士的操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士的操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility doffing sequence is gloves, gown, hand hygiene, face shield, mask, hand hygiene.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构规定的脱卸顺序为：手套、隔离衣、手卫生、面屏、口罩、手卫生。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Remove gloves using glove-to-glove and skin-to-skin technique.","zh":"用“手套接触手套、皮肤接触皮肤”的方法脱手套。"},{"id":"C","en":"Perform hand hygiene.","zh":"进行手卫生。"},{"id":"D","en":"Remove the face shield by handling the strap.","zh":"抓住固定带取下面屏。"},{"id":"F","en":"Perform hand hygiene again after all PPE is removed.","zh":"所有个人防护用品脱下后再次进行手卫生。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove the gown without touching the outside surface.","zh":"脱下隔离衣，避免接触外表面。"},{"id":"E","en":"Remove the mask by handling the ties or ear loops.","zh":"抓住系带或耳挂取下口罩。"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stem provides the facility sequence. The nurse removes the most contaminated items in the stated order, performs hand hygiene after removing gown and gloves, removes face protection by clean straps or ties, and ends with hand hygiene.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干给出了机构规定的顺序。护士按规定先脱污染较重的物品，脱手套和隔离衣后进行手卫生，通过清洁的固定带或系带取下面部防护用品，最后再次进行手卫生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem provides a local sequence, follow it exactly and use contamination principles to confirm each step.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干提供本机构流程时，要严格按该流程排序，并用污染控制原则核对每一步。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The facility doffing sequence is gloves, gown, hand hygiene, face shield, mask, hand hygiene.","controlSentenceZh":"机构规定的脱卸顺序为：手套、隔离衣、手卫生、面屏、口罩、手卫生。"}
{"queueIndex":1899,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.429","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.429.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.429.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,26],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing a sterile field for a bedside dressing change. Place the actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士准备为床旁换药建立无菌区。请按正确顺序排列操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing a sterile field for a bedside dressing change.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备为床旁换药建立无菌区。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Add sterile supplies by dropping them onto the field from above the field edge.","zh":"从无菌区边缘上方将无菌物品投放到无菌区内。"},{"id":"D","en":"Open the side flaps and then the flap closest to the body without reaching over the field.","zh":"打开两侧包装瓣，再打开靠近身体的一瓣，过程中不要越过无菌区。"},{"id":"B","en":"Perform hand hygiene and clear a clean, dry work surface.","zh":"进行手卫生，并清理出清洁、干燥的操作台面。"},{"id":"A","en":"Open the outer flap of the sterile wrapper away from the body.","zh":"打开无菌包外侧包装，先将远离身体的一瓣向外打开。"},{"id":"C","en":"Check the sterile package for tears, wetness, and expiration date.","zh":"检查无菌包是否破损、潮湿以及是否过期。"}],"correct":["B","C","A","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse prepares a clean dry surface and performs hand hygiene, verifies that the package is safe to use, opens the sterile wrapper without reaching over the field, and then adds sterile supplies without contaminating the field.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先准备清洁干燥的台面并进行手卫生，再确认无菌包可安全使用，随后在不越过无菌区的情况下打开包装，最后以不污染无菌区的方式加入无菌物品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Build the sterile field from clean preparation to package inspection, then opening, then adding supplies.","testTakingStrategyZh":"建立无菌区时，按清洁准备、检查包装、打开包装、加入物品的逻辑进行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1900,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.430","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.430.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.430.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[231,251],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,71],"fullStemEn":"During a sterile central-line dressing change, the nurse opens a sterile kit and dons sterile gloves. While reaching for tape, the nurse's sleeve brushes the sterile drape. The client is afebrile and the insertion site is visible. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"护士为中心静脉导管进行无菌换药时，已打开无菌包并戴上无菌手套。护士伸手取胶布时，袖口擦到无菌洞巾。患者目前无发热，穿刺点可见。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is afebrile and the insertion site is visible.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者目前无发热，穿刺点可见。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Condition or problem to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况或问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c4","en":"Expected sterile-field setup","zh":"预期的无菌区建立过程"},{"id":"c3","en":"Acute bloodstream infection","zh":"急性血流感染"},{"id":"c2","en":"Adhesive allergy","zh":"胶布过敏"},{"id":"c1","en":"Contaminated sterile field","zh":"无菌区被污染"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two immediate nursing actions","zh":"两项立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Cover the contaminated area with clean tape","zh":"用清洁胶布覆盖被污染区域"},{"id":"a3","en":"Wipe the drape with antiseptic and continue","zh":"用消毒剂擦拭洞巾后继续操作"},{"id":"a2","en":"Obtain a new sterile kit and restart using sterile technique","zh":"取得新的无菌包，并按无菌技术重新开始"},{"id":"a5","en":"Delay changing the dressing until the next scheduled shift","zh":"将换药推迟到下一班"},{"id":"a1","en":"Stop the dressing change and discard contaminated sterile supplies","zh":"停止换药并丢弃被污染的无菌物品"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two findings to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的两项发现"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Color of the tape package","zh":"胶布包装的颜色"},{"id":"p3","en":"Client's preferred meal choices","zh":"患者偏好的餐食选择"},{"id":"p2","en":"Temperature or chills after the dressing change","zh":"换药后的体温或寒战"},{"id":"p5","en":"Room television volume","zh":"病房电视音量"},{"id":"p1","en":"Insertion-site redness, drainage, or dressing integrity","zh":"穿刺点发红、渗液或敷料完整性"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A sleeve touching the sterile drape contaminates the sterile field. The nurse should stop, discard contaminated supplies, and restart with a new sterile setup. The nurse monitors the insertion site and systemic cues such as fever or chills.","rationaleCorrectZh":"袖口接触无菌洞巾会污染无菌区。护士应停止操作、丢弃被污染物品，并用新的无菌物品重新建立无菌区。护士还要监测穿刺点以及发热、寒战等全身线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bowtie items, separate the immediate problem from possible later complications. A contaminated field requires immediate replacement before monitoring for infection cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，要区分眼前问题和可能的后续并发症。无菌区污染需要立即更换，然后再监测感染线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1901,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.431","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.431.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.431.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[194,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,61],"fullStemEn":"Before starting an ordered IV infusion, the nurse notices that the infusion pump's power cord is taped near the plug and exposed wire is visible. A charged backup pump is available on the unit. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"在开始医嘱输液前，护士发现输液泵电源线靠近插头处被胶带缠住，并可见裸露电线。科室有一台已充电的备用输液泵。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A charged backup pump is available on the unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室有一台已充电的备用输液泵。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Condition or problem to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况或问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Expected battery maintenance","zh":"预期的电池维护"},{"id":"c3","en":"Medication incompatibility","zh":"药物配伍禁忌"},{"id":"c1","en":"Electrical equipment hazard","zh":"电气设备危险"},{"id":"c4","en":"Client refusal of infusion","zh":"患者拒绝输液"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two immediate nursing actions","zh":"两项立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Use the charged backup pump to start the infusion as prescribed","zh":"使用已充电的备用泵按医嘱开始输液"},{"id":"a5","en":"Cancel the infusion without notifying the prescriber","zh":"不通知开医嘱者而取消输液"},{"id":"a1","en":"Remove the damaged pump from use and label it per facility process","zh":"停止使用损坏的输液泵，并按机构流程贴上标识"},{"id":"a4","en":"Plug the pump in only long enough to start the infusion","zh":"只在开始输液时短时间接通该泵电源"},{"id":"a3","en":"Cover the exposed wire with more tape and proceed","zh":"用更多胶带覆盖裸露电线后继续使用"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p5","en":"Brand name printed on the IV pole","zh":"输液架上印的品牌名称"},{"id":"p1","en":"Infusion rate, start time, and volume infused","zh":"输液速度、开始时间和已输入量"},{"id":"p3","en":"Client's hair color","zh":"患者头发颜色"},{"id":"p2","en":"Device asset number and description of cord damage","zh":"设备资产编号和电源线损坏描述"},{"id":"p4","en":"Television remote location","zh":"电视遥控器位置"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A taped cord with visible wire is an electrical hazard. The nurse removes the pump from use, follows the facility reporting process, and uses safe backup equipment to deliver the prescribed infusion. Infusion details and the device defect should be monitored or reported.","rationaleCorrectZh":"被胶带缠住且可见裸露电线的电源线属于电气危险。护士应停止使用该泵，按机构流程报告，并使用安全的备用设备执行医嘱输液。需要监测或报告输液信息和设备缺陷。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For equipment questions, do not choose a workaround for visible damage. Remove unsafe equipment from use and continue care with safe equipment when available.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到设备题时，不要选择对可见损坏进行临时凑合。应停止使用不安全设备，并在有安全设备时继续护理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1902,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.432","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.432.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.432.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,124],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,35],"fullStemEn":"The nurse audits care provided after a blood glucose check. Highlight the line that describes a standard precautions breach.","fullStemZh":"护士审核一次血糖检测后的护理记录。请标出描述标准预防措施被破坏的一行。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the line that describes a standard precautions breach.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出描述标准预防措施被破坏的一行。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse audits care provided after a blood glucose check.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士审核一次血糖检测后的护理记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0645 — Nurse performs hand hygiene before entering the room.","zh":"0645 — 护士进入病房前进行手卫生。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"0647 — Nurse wears gloves before performing the finger-stick blood glucose check.","zh":"0647 — 护士在进行指尖血糖检测前戴手套。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0649 — Nurse places the used lancet on the bedside table while documenting the result.","zh":"0649 — 护士记录结果时将用过的采血针放在床旁桌上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"0651 — Nurse removes gloves and performs hand hygiene after the procedure.","zh":"0651 — 护士操作后脱手套并进行手卫生。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A used lancet is a contaminated sharp and should be placed directly into an approved sharps container. Placing it on the bedside table creates an exposure risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用过的采血针属于被污染的锐器，应直接放入合规锐器盒。放在床旁桌上会造成暴露风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For blood or body fluid tasks, track where contaminated sharps and supplies go after use.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到血液或体液相关操作时，要关注使用后的污染锐器和物品被放在哪里。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1903,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.433","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.433.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.433.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,38],"fullStemEn":"The nurse observes a sterile urinary catheter insertion setup. Highlight the line that requires the nurse to stop and restart the sterile setup.","fullStemZh":"护士观察一次无菌导尿插管准备过程。请标出需要护士停止并重新建立无菌区的一行。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the line that requires the nurse to stop and restart the sterile setup.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要护士停止并重新建立无菌区的一行。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes a sterile urinary catheter insertion setup.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士观察一次无菌导尿插管准备过程。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"1100 — Nurse opens the sterile catheter kit on a clean, dry bedside table.","zh":"1100 — 护士在清洁干燥的床旁桌上打开无菌导尿包。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"1102 — Nurse keeps the sterile field above waist level.","zh":"1102 — 护士将无菌区保持在腰部以上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"1104 — Sterile forceps slide off the drape and land on the client's blanket.","zh":"1104 — 无菌镊从洞巾上滑落到患者的被子上。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"1106 — Nurse uses sterile gloves to arrange remaining supplies inside the field.","zh":"1106 — 护士戴无菌手套整理无菌区内剩余物品。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A sterile item that contacts the client's blanket is contaminated. The nurse should stop and obtain replacement sterile supplies rather than continue with the contaminated item.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无菌物品接触患者被子后即被污染。护士应停止操作并更换无菌物品，而不是继续使用被污染物品。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Sterile items remain sterile only while they stay within the sterile field and contact only sterile surfaces.","testTakingStrategyZh":"无菌物品只有在留在无菌区内且只接触无菌表面时才保持无菌。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1904,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.434","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.434.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.434.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,50],"fullStemEn":"A nurse finds a client sitting on the floor after attempting to walk to the bathroom. The client is awake and says, \"I slipped.\" Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一名患者尝试走去卫生间后坐在地上。患者清醒，并说：“我滑倒了。”请按正确顺序排列护士的操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士的操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is awake and says, \"I slipped.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者清醒，并说：“我滑倒了。”","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Use safe transfer equipment or additional staff to return the client to bed if assessment allows.","zh":"如评估允许，使用安全转移设备或请额外人员协助患者回床。"},{"id":"B","en":"Call for assistance and stay with the client.","zh":"呼叫协助并留在患者身边。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client for pain, injury, level of consciousness, and vital signs before moving the client.","zh":"移动患者前评估疼痛、受伤情况、意识水平和生命体征。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider and charge nurse according to facility procedure.","zh":"按机构流程通知医师和主管护士。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the event, assessment findings, notifications, and fall-prevention updates.","zh":"记录事件、评估发现、通知对象以及防跌倒措施更新。"}],"correct":["B","A","D","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first stays with the client and gets help, then assesses before moving the client. If it is safe to move the client, the nurse uses safe transfer support, notifies the appropriate team members, and documents the event and updated precautions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先留在患者身边并呼叫协助，然后在移动患者前进行评估。如可安全移动，应使用安全转移支持，随后通知相关人员，并记录事件和更新后的防跌倒措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Post-fall sequences usually start with staying with the client, calling for help, assessing before movement, then notifying and documenting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"跌倒后流程通常先留在患者身边、呼叫协助、移动前评估，然后通知并记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client is awake and says, \"I slipped.\"","controlSentenceZh":"患者清醒，并说：“我滑倒了。”"}
{"queueIndex":1905,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.435","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.435.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.435.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,226],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,54],"fullStemEn":"The nurse finds that a portable suction setup planned for a bedside procedure does not generate suction during the pre-use check. A replacement canister and tubing are available. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士在床旁操作前检查便携式吸引装置，发现无法产生吸引力。现场有备用收集罐和管路。请按正确顺序排列护士的操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按正确顺序排列护士的操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A replacement canister and tubing are available.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现场有备用收集罐和管路。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Check that the suction unit is connected to power or has an adequate battery charge.","zh":"检查吸引装置是否接通电源或电池电量是否充足。"},{"id":"E","en":"Remove equipment from use and report it if suction cannot be restored.","zh":"如果无法恢复吸引功能，停止使用该设备并报告。"},{"id":"D","en":"Confirm that suction is functioning before bringing the setup to the procedure.","zh":"在将设备用于操作前确认吸引功能正常。"},{"id":"C","en":"Replace faulty tubing or canister parts if suction is still not present.","zh":"如果仍无吸引力，更换有问题的管路或收集罐部件。"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify that tubing connections are secure and the canister lid is sealed.","zh":"确认管路连接牢固且收集罐盖密封。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse performs basic pre-use troubleshooting: power source, connections, replacement of available disposable parts, and function confirmation. If suction cannot be restored, the unsafe or nonfunctional equipment is removed from use and reported.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先进行使用前基本排查：电源、连接、更换可用的一次性部件，并确认功能。如果无法恢复吸引，应停止使用该不安全或不能工作的设备并报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For equipment workflows, choose simple checks first, then replacement if available, then remove and report if the device still fails.","testTakingStrategyZh":"设备流程题应先选择简单检查，再在可行时更换部件；若仍故障，则停止使用并报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A replacement canister and tubing are available.","controlSentenceZh":"现场有备用收集罐和管路。"}
{"queueIndex":1906,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.436","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.436.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.436.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,60],"fullStemEn":"During sterile wound irrigation, the nurse dons sterile gloves. While reaching for the irrigation syringe, the nurse's sterile-gloved hand touches the bed rail. The wound is open, and the irrigation has not started. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"护士进行无菌伤口冲洗时已戴无菌手套。伸手取冲洗注射器时，戴无菌手套的手碰到床栏。伤口开放，冲洗尚未开始。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The wound is open, and the irrigation has not started.","penultimateSentenceZh":"伤口开放，冲洗尚未开始。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Condition or problem to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况或问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Contaminated sterile glove","zh":"无菌手套被污染"},{"id":"c3","en":"Allergic reaction to irrigation solution","zh":"对冲洗液过敏反应"},{"id":"c4","en":"Resolved wound contamination risk","zh":"伤口污染风险已解除"},{"id":"c2","en":"Expected wound irrigation step","zh":"预期的伤口冲洗步骤"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two immediate nursing actions","zh":"两项立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a5","en":"Ask the client to hold the irrigation syringe","zh":"请患者拿住冲洗注射器"},{"id":"a3","en":"Rinse the glove with sterile irrigation solution and continue","zh":"用无菌冲洗液冲洗手套后继续操作"},{"id":"a2","en":"Remove the contaminated glove and don a new sterile glove using sterile technique","zh":"脱下被污染的手套，并按无菌技术重新戴无菌手套"},{"id":"a4","en":"Continue because the bed rail is near the sterile field","zh":"继续操作，因为床栏靠近无菌区"},{"id":"a1","en":"Stop before touching the wound or sterile supplies","zh":"在接触伤口或无菌物品前停止操作"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p5","en":"Brand of the bed rail","zh":"床栏品牌"},{"id":"p3","en":"Client's preferred blanket color","zh":"患者偏好的毯子颜色"},{"id":"p4","en":"Number of unused paper towels in the room","zh":"房间内未使用纸巾数量"},{"id":"p1","en":"Wound drainage, odor, redness, or increased pain","zh":"伤口渗液、气味、发红或疼痛加重"},{"id":"p2","en":"Temperature or chills after the dressing procedure","zh":"换药操作后的体温或寒战"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bed rail is not sterile, so the sterile glove is contaminated. The nurse should stop before touching the wound or sterile supplies, replace the contaminated glove using sterile technique, and monitor for local or systemic infection cues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"床栏不是无菌物品，因此无菌手套已被污染。护士应在接触伤口或无菌物品前停止操作，按无菌技术更换被污染手套，并监测局部或全身感染线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When sterile gloves touch anything nonsterile, assume contamination and choose replacement before continuing care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"无菌手套一旦接触非无菌物品，就应视为污染，并在继续护理前更换。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1907,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_sic_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.437","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.437.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.437.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[239,259],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,70],"fullStemEn":"Before transporting a client with intermittent oral secretions, the nurse checks the portable suction unit. The unit powers on, but the pressure gauge stays at zero when the tubing is occluded. A second portable suction unit is available. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"在转运一名偶有口腔分泌物的患者前，护士检查便携式吸引装置。设备能开机，但夹闭管路时压力表仍为零。现场有第二台便携式吸引装置。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A second portable suction unit is available.","penultimateSentenceZh":"现场有第二台便携式吸引装置。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Condition or problem to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况或问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Nonfunctioning suction equipment","zh":"吸引设备不能正常工作"},{"id":"c2","en":"Expected suction readiness","zh":"预期的吸引准备状态"},{"id":"c4","en":"Incorrect diet order","zh":"饮食医嘱错误"},{"id":"c3","en":"Resolved secretion risk","zh":"分泌物风险已解除"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Two immediate nursing actions","zh":"两项立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a3","en":"Proceed with transport because the unit powers on","zh":"因为设备能开机，所以继续转运"},{"id":"a1","en":"Remove the faulty suction unit from use and follow facility reporting process","zh":"停止使用故障吸引装置，并按机构流程报告"},{"id":"a4","en":"Increase the wall oxygen flow to replace suction","zh":"提高墙氧流量来替代吸引"},{"id":"a2","en":"Obtain and test the second suction unit before transport","zh":"取得并测试第二台吸引装置后再转运"},{"id":"a5","en":"Ask the client to avoid coughing during transport","zh":"要求患者转运途中不要咳嗽"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Two parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的两项指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p5","en":"Color of the transport blanket","zh":"转运毯颜色"},{"id":"p1","en":"Suction gauge response and equipment identifier","zh":"吸引压力表反应和设备编号"},{"id":"p3","en":"Client's room wall color","zh":"患者房间墙壁颜色"},{"id":"p2","en":"Client coughing, secretion burden, or ability to clear airway","zh":"患者咳嗽、分泌物量或清理气道能力"},{"id":"p4","en":"Number of staff at the nurses' station","zh":"护士站工作人员人数"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A suction unit that powers on but does not generate pressure is not ready for use. The nurse should remove and report the faulty unit, then test replacement equipment before transport. Equipment function and the client's secretion or airway-clearance status are relevant nursing-monitorable parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"能开机但不能产生负压的吸引装置不能用于护理。护士应停止使用并报告故障设备，然后在转运前测试替代设备。设备功能以及患者分泌物或气道清理情况是护士可监测的相关指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For transport equipment, power alone is not readiness. The device must function for the clinical need before transport starts.","testTakingStrategyZh":"转运设备题中，仅能开机不代表准备就绪。设备必须能满足临床需要，才可开始转运。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1908,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.438","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.438.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.438.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[464,485],"terminalOffsetsZh":[193,198],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is caring for a client 8 hours after an open colectomy. Unit policy states: activate the rapid response team immediately for any 2 of the following: systolic BP less than 90 mm Hg, heart rate greater than 120/min, new confusion, or uncontrolled bleeding. Assessment: BP 82/48 mm Hg, HR 132/min, RR 26/min, SpO2 93% on room air, new confusion, pale skin, and a saturated abdominal dressing. The surgeon is in the operating room and has not returned a page. Complete the diagram.","fullStemZh":"护士正在照护一名开放性结肠切除术后 8 小时的患者。科室政策规定：出现以下任意 2 项时应立即启动快速反应团队：收缩压低于 90 mm Hg、心率大于 120 次/分、新发意识混乱，或出血无法控制。评估：血压 82/48 mm Hg，心率 132 次/分，呼吸 26 次/分，室内空气下 SpO2 93%，新发意识混乱，皮肤苍白，腹部敷料已被血液浸透。外科医生正在手术室，尚未回传呼叫。完成图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The surgeon is in the operating room and has not returned a page.","penultimateSentenceZh":"外科医生正在手术室，尚未回传呼叫。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_routine_call","en":"Stable client needing only a routine surgeon callback","zh":"病情稳定，只需等待外科医生常规回电"},{"id":"c_rrt_postop_bleeding","en":"Rapid response criteria are met for suspected postoperative hemorrhage","zh":"符合快速反应启动标准，疑似术后出血"},{"id":"c_expected_pain","en":"Expected postoperative pain response","zh":"预期的术后疼痛反应"}],"correct":"c_rrt_postop_bleeding"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_abc_bleeding","en":"Stay with the client, keep the client supine, apply oxygen per protocol, and assess the bleeding site","zh":"留在患者身边，使患者保持仰卧，按规程给氧，并评估出血部位"},{"id":"a_walk_bathroom","en":"Assist the client to the bathroom to assess orthostatic tolerance","zh":"协助患者去卫生间以评估体位性耐受"},{"id":"a_activate_rrt","en":"Activate the rapid response team now","zh":"立即启动快速反应团队"},{"id":"a_wait_surgeon","en":"Wait for the surgeon to return the page before escalating","zh":"等待外科医生回传呼叫后再上报"},{"id":"a_give_opioid","en":"Give the PRN opioid first because tachycardia is likely pain-related","zh":"先给予按需阿片类止痛药，因为心动过速很可能与疼痛有关"}],"correct":["a_activate_rrt","a_abc_bleeding"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor/report","zh":"需要监测/报告的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_pain_goal","en":"Whether the postoperative pain goal has been met","zh":"术后疼痛目标是否达成"},{"id":"p_bp_hr_mental","en":"Blood pressure, heart rate, and mental status trend","zh":"血压、心率和意识状态变化趋势"},{"id":"p_dressing_bleeding","en":"Amount and rate of dressing saturation or visible bleeding","zh":"敷料被血液浸透的程度、速度或可见出血量"},{"id":"p_bowel_sounds","en":"Return of bowel sounds","zh":"肠鸣音恢复情况"}],"correct":["p_bp_hr_mental","p_dressing_bleeding"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client meets multiple stated rapid response criteria and has cues of acute postoperative bleeding. The safest management response is immediate team activation while the nurse remains with the client and begins protocol-supported airway/circulation assessment and bleeding assessment. Waiting for a provider callback delays rescue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者符合多个已给出的快速反应标准，并有急性术后出血线索。最安全的管理措施是立即启动团队，同时护士留在患者身边，按规程开始气道/循环评估和出血评估。等待医生回电会延误抢救。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a stem gives an escalation threshold, apply it before choosing routine communication. Rescue first, then notify through the chain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干给出上报阈值时，应先应用该阈值，而不是选择常规沟通。先救援，再按链条通知。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The surgeon is in the operating room and has not returned a page.","controlSentenceZh":"外科医生正在手术室，尚未回传呼叫。"}
{"queueIndex":1909,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.439","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.439.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.439.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[490,511],"terminalOffsetsZh":[165,170],"fullStemEn":"A client with pneumonia has a provider-signed DNR order in the electronic record. The facility policy printed on the order states: DNR limits CPR, defibrillation, and intubation during cardiac or respiratory arrest only; it does not mean comfort-measures-only unless a separate order says so. The client is awake, has a pulse, and says, 'I can't catch my breath.' Current assessment: RR 32/min, SpO2 86% on 2 L/min nasal cannula, BP 148/82 mm Hg. No comfort-measures-only order is present. Complete the diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名肺炎患者在电子病历中有医师签署的 DNR 医嘱。医嘱上印有机构政策：DNR 仅在心跳或呼吸停止时限制 CPR、除颤和插管；除非另有医嘱，否则不等同于仅舒适护理。患者清醒、有脉搏，并说：“我喘不过气。”当前评估：呼吸 32 次/分，鼻导管 2 L/分给氧下 SpO2 86%，血压 148/82 mm Hg。没有仅舒适护理医嘱。完成图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"No comfort-measures-only order is present.","penultimateSentenceZh":"没有仅舒适护理医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_comfort_only","en":"Comfort-measures-only status requiring all oxygen escalation to be withheld","zh":"仅舒适护理状态，必须停止所有升级给氧"},{"id":"c_dnr_nonarrest","en":"Non-arrest respiratory deterioration in a client whose DNR order remains in effect","zh":"DNR 仍有效患者发生非心肺骤停的呼吸恶化"},{"id":"c_cardiac_arrest","en":"Cardiac arrest requiring immediate chest compressions despite DNR","zh":"即使有 DNR 也必须立即胸外按压的心跳骤停"}],"correct":"c_dnr_nonarrest"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_call_family_permission","en":"Call the family for permission before treating the dyspnea","zh":"治疗呼吸困难前先打电话征求家属同意"},{"id":"a_chest_compressions","en":"Begin chest compressions now","zh":"立即开始胸外按压"},{"id":"a_position_o2","en":"Position upright and increase oxygen per facility respiratory-distress protocol","zh":"协助取直立位，并按机构呼吸窘迫规程提高给氧"},{"id":"a_withhold_o2","en":"Keep oxygen at 2 L/min because DNR prohibits escalation","zh":"因 DNR 禁止升级治疗，维持氧流量 2 L/分"},{"id":"a_escalate_rrt_provider","en":"Escalate for urgent evaluation through the rapid response/provider pathway","zh":"通过快速反应/医师通道上报，要求紧急评估"}],"correct":["a_position_o2","a_escalate_rrt_provider"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor/report","zh":"需要监测/报告的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_dnr_scope_wishes","en":"Current DNR scope, absence of comfort-only order, and the client's expressed wishes","zh":"当前 DNR 适用范围、无仅舒适护理医嘱，以及患者表达的意愿"},{"id":"p_daily_weight","en":"Daily weight trend","zh":"每日体重变化趋势"},{"id":"p_spo2_work","en":"SpO2, respiratory rate, and work of breathing after oxygen escalation","zh":"提高给氧后的 SpO2、呼吸频率和呼吸费力程度"},{"id":"p_family_arrival","en":"Family arrival time before any treatment is started","zh":"开始任何治疗前家属到达的时间"}],"correct":["p_spo2_work","p_dnr_scope_wishes"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stem defines DNR as limiting resuscitation during arrest only. This client is awake with a pulse and respiratory distress, so non-arrest treatment and escalation continue while the DNR order is respected. Oxygen response and the documented scope of the directive are the key reportable parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干规定 DNR 只限制心肺骤停时的复苏。该患者清醒且有脉搏，只是出现呼吸窘迫，因此应继续非骤停治疗和上报，同时尊重 DNR 医嘱。给氧后的反应和预立指示的适用范围是关键报告内容。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate code status from current treatment goals. DNR usually answers what not to do during arrest; it does not automatically stop assessment, oxygen, medications, or escalation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要把抢救状态和当前治疗目标分开。DNR 通常说明骤停时不做什么；它不会自动停止评估、给氧、用药或上报。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1910,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.440","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.440.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.440.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[451,472],"terminalOffsetsZh":[158,163],"fullStemEn":"A hospital disaster plan uses adult START triage. The triage card states: clients who can walk are tagged green; if not breathing after one airway repositioning, tag black; if breathing with RR greater than 30/min, tag red; if RR is 30/min or less, assess perfusion and commands. A nurse triages a nonwalking adult after a bus crash. The client is breathing at 34/min, has a palpable radial pulse, and follows the command to squeeze the nurse's hand. Complete the diagram.","fullStemZh":"医院灾难预案采用成人 START 分诊。分诊卡规定：能行走者标记绿色；调整一次气道后仍无呼吸者标记黑色；有呼吸且呼吸频率大于 30 次/分者标记红色；若呼吸频率为 30 次/分或以下，再评估灌注和是否能服从指令。护士在巴士事故后分诊一名不能行走的成人。该患者呼吸 34 次/分，桡动脉脉搏可触及，并能按护士指令握手。完成图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is breathing at 34/min, has a palpable radial pulse, and follows the command to squeeze the nurse's hand.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者呼吸 34 次/分，桡动脉脉搏可触及，并能按护士指令握手。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"START category","zh":"START 分诊类别"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_red_rr","en":"Immediate/red because RR is greater than 30/min","zh":"立即/红色：呼吸频率大于 30 次/分"},{"id":"c_yellow_follows","en":"Delayed/yellow because the client follows commands","zh":"延迟/黄色：患者能服从指令"},{"id":"c_black_nonwalking","en":"Expectant/black because the client cannot walk","zh":"预期/黑色：患者不能行走"},{"id":"c_green_radial","en":"Minor/green because the radial pulse is palpable","zh":"轻伤/绿色：桡动脉脉搏可触及"}],"correct":"c_red_rr"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_report_command","en":"Report the red-tag location and count through the incident command/triage channel","zh":"通过事件指挥/分诊通道报告红色标签患者的位置和数量"},{"id":"a_send_green","en":"Direct the client to the walking-wounded area","zh":"引导患者去可行走轻伤区"},{"id":"a_black_no_care","en":"Tag black and provide no further reassessment","zh":"标记黑色且不再复评"},{"id":"a_tag_red","en":"Apply a red tag and move the client to the immediate treatment area when transport is available","zh":"挂红色标签，并在可转运时送往立即治疗区"},{"id":"a_splint_now","en":"Stop to splint suspected fractures before tagging the next client","zh":"先停下来固定疑似骨折，再分诊下一名患者"}],"correct":["a_tag_red","a_report_command"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor/report","zh":"需要监测/报告的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_resp_airway","en":"Respiratory rate and airway status","zh":"呼吸频率和气道状态"},{"id":"p_insurance","en":"Insurance status and usual primary care provider","zh":"保险状态和常规初级保健医生"},{"id":"p_perfusion_commands","en":"Radial pulse/perfusion and ability to follow commands on reassessment","zh":"复评时桡动脉脉搏/灌注和服从指令能力"},{"id":"p_pain_score","en":"Pain score before any other triage decision","zh":"在任何其他分诊决定前先评估疼痛评分"}],"correct":["p_resp_airway","p_perfusion_commands"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Under the provided START rule, respiratory rate greater than 30/min is sufficient for a red/immediate tag before perfusion or command-following changes the category. The nurse should tag, move/report through the disaster command structure, and continue rapid reassessment of airway, respirations, perfusion, and command-following.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据题干给出的 START 规则，呼吸频率大于 30 次/分已足以标记红色/立即处理，灌注或服从指令不能再把该患者降级。护士应标记、通过灾难指挥结构转运/报告，并快速复评气道、呼吸、灌注和服从指令能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the triage algorithm in the order given. Do not let a later normal finding erase an earlier red criterion.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干给出的分诊算法顺序判断。不要让后面正常的发现抵消前面已满足的红色标准。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1911,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.441","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.441.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.441.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[668,689],"terminalOffsetsZh":[190,195],"fullStemEn":"A client with end-stage heart failure has a valid provider-signed DNR/POLST in the electronic record and a matching wristband. At shift report, the nurse verified that the client lacked decision-making capacity and that no revocation order was entered. The adult daughter is the health care proxy and says, 'I changed my mind. Do everything.' Two minutes later, while the nurse is at the bedside, the client becomes pulseless and apneic. Facility policy states: a verified DNR/POLST remains in effect until the client with capacity revokes it or a provider enters a new order after the surrogate review; during arrest, family request alone does not suspend the order. Complete the diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名终末期心力衰竭患者在电子病历中有有效的医师签署 DNR/POLST，并佩戴相符腕带。交接班时，护士已确认患者无决策能力，且没有撤销医嘱。成年女儿是医疗代理人，她说：“我改主意了，什么都做。”两分钟后，护士在床旁时患者无脉且无呼吸。机构政策规定：已核实的 DNR/POLST 在有能力的患者撤销，或代理人复核后医师开出新医嘱之前持续有效；发生骤停时，家属要求本身不会暂停该医嘱。完成图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy states: a verified DNR/POLST remains in effect until the client with capacity revokes it or a provider enters a new order after the surrogate review; during arrest, family request alone does not suspend the order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：已核实的 DNR/POLST 在有能力的患者撤销，或代理人复核后医师开出新医嘱之前持续有效；发生骤停时，家属要求本身不会暂停该医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Situation to recognize","zh":"需要识别的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_no_code_status","en":"Unknown code status requiring full code until clarified","zh":"抢救状态不明，需先按完整抢救处理"},{"id":"c_valid_dnr_arrest","en":"Cardiopulmonary arrest with a verified DNR/POLST that remains active","zh":"心肺骤停，且已核实的 DNR/POLST 仍然有效"},{"id":"c_revoked_dnr","en":"DNR revoked by a new provider order before arrest","zh":"骤停前已有新医嘱撤销 DNR"}],"correct":"c_valid_dnr_arrest"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_pause_vote","en":"Ask available family members to vote on whether to code the client","zh":"请在场家属投票决定是否进行抢救"},{"id":"a_notify_death_process","en":"Notify the charge nurse/provider and follow the facility DNR death-pronouncement process while supporting the daughter","zh":"通知责任护士/医师，并在支持女儿的同时按机构 DNR 死亡确认流程处理"},{"id":"a_remove_wristband","en":"Remove the DNR wristband until the provider arrives","zh":"在医师到达前取下 DNR 腕带"},{"id":"a_honor_dnr","en":"Do not initiate CPR, defibrillation, or intubation","zh":"不开始 CPR、除颤或插管"},{"id":"a_start_cpr","en":"Start chest compressions because the daughter requests full treatment","zh":"因女儿要求全力治疗而开始胸外按压"}],"correct":["a_honor_dnr","a_notify_death_process"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to assess/document","zh":"需要评估/记录的内容"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_compression_depth","en":"Compression depth and rate during CPR","zh":"CPR 期间胸外按压深度和频率"},{"id":"p_last_meal","en":"Time of the client's last meal","zh":"患者最后进食时间"},{"id":"p_dnr_docs_family","en":"Location/status of the DNR/POLST and the daughter's statement","zh":"DNR/POLST 的位置和状态，以及女儿的陈述"},{"id":"p_absence_vitals","en":"Absence of pulse, respirations, and responsiveness according to facility process","zh":"按机构流程确认无脉搏、无呼吸、无反应"}],"correct":["p_absence_vitals","p_dnr_docs_family"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stem makes the DNR/POLST valid and still active at the moment of arrest. The nurse should not begin resuscitation actions that the order prohibits, but should notify the appropriate team members, follow the facility death-pronouncement/DNR process, support the family, and objectively document the arrest findings and surrogate statement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干说明在骤停发生时 DNR/POLST 有效且仍在执行。护士不应开始该医嘱禁止的复苏措施，但应通知相关人员，按机构死亡确认/DNR 流程处理，支持家属，并客观记录骤停发现和代理人的陈述。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the legal/clinical status given in the stem at the time of arrest. A family objection may require support and later review, but it does not erase a verified active order mid-arrest.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干中骤停发生时的法律/临床状态判断。家属反对需要支持并可事后复核，但不会在骤停过程中抹掉已核实的有效医嘱。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1912,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.442","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.442.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.442.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[612,659],"terminalOffsetsZh":[220,235],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is assigned to primary triage at the scene of a building collapse. The disaster plan requires the nurse to use this START sequence before performing treatment beyond opening an airway once: (1) direct all clients who can walk to a marked green area, (2) for each remaining client, assess breathing and open the airway once if apneic, (3) tag black if still apneic or continue if breathing, (4) tag red if RR is greater than 30/min, (5) if RR is 30/min or less, assess radial pulse/perfusion, (6) if perfusion is adequate, assess ability to follow simple commands and tag red if unable or yellow if able. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"护士被分配到建筑物倒塌现场进行初始分诊。灾难预案要求护士在执行任何治疗（除一次打开气道外）前按以下 START 顺序进行：(1) 指示所有能行走者到标记的绿色区域，(2) 对其余每名患者评估呼吸，如无呼吸则打开气道一次，(3) 若仍无呼吸则标记黑色；若有呼吸则继续，(4) 呼吸频率大于 30 次/分则标记红色，(5) 呼吸频率为 30 次/分或以下则评估桡动脉脉搏/灌注，(6) 若灌注足够，则评估能否服从简单指令，不能则红色，能则黄色。请将护士的行动按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的行动按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The disaster plan requires the nurse to use this START sequence before performing treatment beyond opening an airway once: (1) direct all clients who can walk to a marked green area, (2) for each remaining client, assess breathing and open the airway once if apneic, (3) tag black if still apneic or continue if breathing, (4) tag red if RR is greater than 30/min, (5) if RR is 30/min or less, assess radial pulse/perfusion, (6) if perfusion is adequate, assess ability to follow simple commands and tag red if unable or yellow if able.","penultimateSentenceZh":"灾难预案要求护士在执行任何治疗（除一次打开气道外）前按以下 START 顺序进行：(1) 指示所有能行走者到标记的绿色区域，(2) 对其余每名患者评估呼吸，如无呼吸则打开气道一次，(3) 若仍无呼吸则标记黑色；若有呼吸则继续，(4) 呼吸频率大于 30 次/分则标记红色，(5) 呼吸频率为 30 次/分或以下则评估桡动脉脉搏/灌注，(6) 若灌注足够，则评估能否服从简单指令，不能则红色，能则黄色。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Tag red when the breathing client's RR is greater than 30/min","zh":"有呼吸患者的呼吸频率大于 30 次/分时标记红色"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess radial pulse/perfusion when RR is 30/min or less","zh":"当呼吸频率为 30 次/分或以下时评估桡动脉脉搏/灌注"},{"id":"D","en":"For each remaining nonwalking client, assess breathing and open the airway once if apneic","zh":"对每名剩余不能行走者评估呼吸，如无呼吸则打开气道一次"},{"id":"B","en":"Direct all clients who can walk to the marked green area","zh":"指示所有能行走者到标记的绿色区域"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess command-following for a breathing client with adequate perfusion and assign red or yellow","zh":"对有呼吸且灌注足够的患者评估能否服从指令，并标记红色或黄色"},{"id":"E","en":"Tag black if still apneic after airway repositioning; otherwise continue assessment","zh":"调整气道后仍无呼吸则标记黑色；否则继续评估"}],"correct":["B","D","E","F","C","A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The provided START algorithm first separates walking wounded, then uses breathing/airway, respiratory rate, perfusion, and mental-status commands in that order. Performing splinting, pain care, or later decision points before earlier screens slows primary triage and can misallocate scarce resources.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干给出的 START 算法先分出可行走轻伤者，然后依次使用呼吸/气道、呼吸频率、灌注和精神状态指令。若在早期筛查前先处理固定、疼痛或后续判断，会拖慢初始分诊并可能错误分配稀缺资源。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For ordered-response disaster items, follow the algorithm exactly as written. Avoid inserting treatment tasks into a primary triage sequence unless the stem includes them.","testTakingStrategyZh":"灾难类排序题要严格按题干算法执行。除非题干包含治疗步骤，否则不要把治疗任务插入初始分诊顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The disaster plan requires the nurse to use this START sequence before performing treatment beyond opening an airway once: (1) direct all clients who can walk to a marked green area, (2) for each remaining client, assess breathing and open the airway once if apneic, (3) tag black if still apneic or continue if breathing, (4) tag red if RR is greater than 30/min, (5) if RR is 30/min or less, assess radial pulse/perfusion, (6) if perfusion is adequate, assess ability to follow simple commands and tag red if unable or yellow if able.","controlSentenceZh":"灾难预案要求护士在执行任何治疗（除一次打开气道外）前按以下 START 顺序进行：(1) 指示所有能行走者到标记的绿色区域，(2) 对其余每名患者评估呼吸，如无呼吸则打开气道一次，(3) 若仍无呼吸则标记黑色；若有呼吸则继续，(4) 呼吸频率大于 30 次/分则标记红色，(5) 呼吸频率为 30 次/分或以下则评估桡动脉脉搏/灌注，(6) 若灌注足够，则评估能否服从简单指令，不能则红色，能则黄色。"}
{"queueIndex":1913,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.443","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.443.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.443.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[632,679],"terminalOffsetsZh":[187,202],"fullStemEn":"A stable adult client has a serum potassium of 2.9 mEq/L. The new order reads, 'Potassium chloride 40 mEq IV push now.' Facility policy printed in the medication safety manual states: IV push potassium chloride is never permitted on this unit; the nurse must not administer an order known to violate this policy; clarify with the prescriber; if the prescriber insists, involve the charge nurse and pharmacist, then escalate through the nursing supervisor/medical chain before administration; complete safety-event documentation only after the immediate medication risk is controlled. The prescriber says, 'Just give it as written.' Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名病情稳定的成人患者血清钾为 2.9 mEq/L。新医嘱写着：“氯化钾 40 mEq 立即静脉推注。”药物安全手册中的机构政策规定：本病区绝不允许静脉推注氯化钾；护士不得执行已知违反该政策的医嘱；应与开医嘱者澄清；若开医嘱者坚持，先让责任护士和药师介入，再在给药前通过护理主管/医疗链条上报；只有在眼前用药风险得到控制后，才完成安全事件记录。开医嘱者说：“就按原医嘱给。”请将护士的行动按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的行动按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The prescriber says, 'Just give it as written.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"开医嘱者说：“就按原医嘱给。”","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Complete objective documentation and the safety-event report after the unsafe route has been resolved","zh":"在不安全给药途径已解决后，完成客观记录和安全事件报告"},{"id":"E","en":"Ask the charge nurse and pharmacist to intervene and request a safe replacement order","zh":"请责任护士和药师介入，并要求改为安全替代医嘱"},{"id":"D","en":"Escalate through the nursing supervisor/medical chain because the prescriber continues to insist on the prohibited route","zh":"因开医嘱者继续坚持禁用途径，通过护理主管/医疗链条上报"},{"id":"C","en":"Clarify the order with the prescriber using the potassium value and the unit policy","zh":"结合血钾结果和病区政策，与开医嘱者澄清医嘱"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the unsafe IV-push order and do not prepare or administer the medication by that route","zh":"暂停该不安全的静脉推注医嘱，不按该途径准备或给药"}],"correct":["B","C","E","D","A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first prevents the immediate unsafe administration, then clarifies with the prescriber. Because the prescriber insists on a prohibited route, the nurse uses the stated chain: charge nurse and pharmacist, then supervisor/medical escalation. Safety-event documentation follows once the immediate medication risk is controlled.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先阻止眼前的不安全给药，然后与开医嘱者澄清。由于开医嘱者坚持使用禁用途径，护士按题干链条处理：先找责任护士和药师，再向护理主管/医疗链条上报。安全事件记录应在眼前用药风险得到控制后完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an order is explicitly unsafe by policy, the nurse's first priority is not to carry it out. Then escalate stepwise using the chain given in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干明确说明医嘱违反安全政策时，护士的首要任务是不要执行。随后按题干给出的链条逐级上报。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1914,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc1_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.444","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.444.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.444.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[540,587],"terminalOffsetsZh":[163,178],"fullStemEn":"An alert, oriented client with a current DNR order is scheduled for urgent surgery in 2 hours. The facility perioperative policy states: DNR orders are not automatically suspended for surgery. Before transport, the nurse must verify the active directive with the client, notify the surgeon/anesthesia team that a required reconsideration discussion is needed, confirm that the resulting perioperative code-status plan is documented as an order, communicate the plan in handoff, and ensure the EHR/wristband/documents match the agreed plan. Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名清醒、定向正常且有当前 DNR 医嘱的患者计划 2 小时后接受紧急手术。机构围手术期政策规定：DNR 医嘱不会因手术自动暂停。转运前，护士必须与患者核实有效预立指示，通知外科/麻醉团队需要进行“重新考虑”讨论，确认讨论后的围手术期抢救状态计划已作为医嘱记录，交接时沟通该计划，并确保电子病历、腕带和随行文件与约定计划一致。请将护士的行动按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护士的行动按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Before transport, the nurse must verify the active directive with the client, notify the surgeon/anesthesia team that a required reconsideration discussion is needed, confirm that the resulting perioperative code-status plan is documented as an order, communicate the plan in handoff, and ensure the EHR/wristband/documents match the agreed plan.","penultimateSentenceZh":"转运前，护士必须与患者核实有效预立指示，通知外科/麻醉团队需要进行“重新考虑”讨论，确认讨论后的围手术期抢救状态计划已作为医嘱记录，交接时沟通该计划，并确保电子病历、腕带和随行文件与约定计划一致。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Communicate the perioperative code-status plan and location of documents during the pre-op handoff","zh":"术前交接时沟通围手术期抢救状态计划和文件位置"},{"id":"E","en":"Confirm that the agreed perioperative code-status plan is entered as a provider order/documentation","zh":"确认约定的围手术期抢救状态计划已作为医嘱/记录录入"},{"id":"D","en":"Notify the surgeon and anesthesia team that required reconsideration is needed because DNR is not automatically suspended","zh":"通知外科和麻醉团队：因 DNR 不会自动暂停，需要进行重新考虑讨论"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure the EHR status, wristband, and documents sent with the client match the agreed plan before transport","zh":"转运前确保电子病历状态、腕带和随行文件与约定计划一致"},{"id":"B","en":"Verify the active DNR/directive with the alert client and ask whether the client's wishes remain unchanged","zh":"与清醒患者核实有效 DNR/预立指示，并询问其意愿是否仍未改变"}],"correct":["B","D","E","A","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Because the client is alert and the policy prohibits automatic suspension, the nurse first verifies the client's current wishes. The surgeon/anesthesia team must then complete the required reconsideration discussion. The resulting plan must be documented as an order before handoff, and identifiers/documents must match before transport.","rationaleCorrectZh":"由于患者清醒且政策禁止自动暂停 DNR，护士先核实患者当前意愿。随后外科/麻醉团队必须完成重新考虑讨论。讨论后的计划必须先作为医嘱记录，再进行交接；转运前标识和文件必须一致。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For perioperative DNR questions, reject automatic suspension. Look for verification of the client's wishes, team discussion, documented order, handoff, then matching identifiers.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到围手术期 DNR 题，排除“自动暂停”。寻找顺序：核实患者意愿、团队讨论、记录医嘱、交接、再核对标识一致。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1915,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.445","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.445.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.445.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,342],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,90],"fullStemEn":"Review the incident-report excerpt. Highlight the single entry that documents a confidentiality breach requiring reporting to the privacy officer. Facility policy: voicemail or callback messages may include only the organization name, callback number, and a request to call back unless the recipient's identity and authorization are verified.","fullStemZh":"查看事件报告摘录。标出唯一一条记录了保密违规、需要报告给隐私官的内容。机构政策：除非已核实接收者身份及其授权，否则语音留言或回电信息只能包括机构名称、回电号码以及请对方回电的请求。","terminalSentenceEn":"Facility policy: voicemail or callback messages may include only the organization name, callback number, and a request to call back unless the recipient's identity and authorization are verified.","terminalSentenceZh":"机构政策：除非已核实接收者身份及其授权，否则语音留言或回电信息只能包括机构名称、回电号码以及请对方回电的请求。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the single entry that documents a confidentiality breach requiring reporting to the privacy officer.","penultimateSentenceZh":"标出唯一一条记录了保密违规、需要报告给隐私官的内容。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Incident-report excerpt, day shift:","zh":"事件报告摘录，白班："},{"id":"s2","en":"0735: The client asked that only the spouse receive updates; staff updated the confidential-contact banner.","zh":"0735：患者要求只向配偶提供病情更新；工作人员更新了保密联系人提示栏。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0810: The unit clerk verified two identifiers before faxing wound-care orders to the skilled nursing facility accepting transfer.","zh":"0810：科室文员在将伤口护理医嘱传真给接收转院的专业护理机构前，核对了两个身份标识。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"0945: The nurse left a voicemail on the client's neighbor's phone stating the client's full name, alcohol-withdrawal diagnosis, room number, and expected discharge date.","zh":"0945：护士在患者邻居的电话语音信箱中留下患者全名、酒精戒断诊断、病房号和预计出院日期。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"1015: The charge nurse moved a visitor conversation to a consultation room after the family began asking questions at the nurses' station.","zh":"1015：家属在护士站开始询问问题后，责任护士将访客谈话转到咨询室。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"1130: The case manager sent only the face sheet and medication list requested by the insurer for authorization through the secure portal.","zh":"1130：个案管理师通过安全门户仅发送保险公司为授权所要求的人口学资料首页和用药清单。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"1220: The interpreter documented the session number after assisting with discharge teaching.","zh":"1220：口译员协助出院宣教后记录了本次口译服务编号。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The voicemail disclosed identifiable protected health information to an unverified neighbor and exceeded the facility's callback-message policy. The other entries describe privacy-protective or treatment/payment/operations disclosures using reasonable safeguards.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该语音留言把可识别的受保护健康信息透露给未经核实的邻居，并且超出了机构关于回电留言的政策。其他记录描述的是有隐私保护措施的做法，或为治疗、付款、运营目的并采取合理防护的信息披露。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For confidentiality items, first ask whether the recipient is verified and authorized, then ask whether the information shared is the minimum needed for the stated purpose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做保密题时，先判断接收者是否已核实且获得授权，再判断分享的信息是否限于该目的所需的最低范围。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1916,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.446","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.446.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.446.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,297],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,97],"fullStemEn":"Review the SBAR handoff note. Highlight the single line that makes the handoff incomplete under facility policy. Facility policy: when a client transfers with an active drain, handoff must include drain type/location, last output with time period, and the specific provider-notification threshold.","fullStemZh":"查看 SBAR 交接记录。标出根据机构政策导致交接不完整的唯一一行。机构政策：患者携带仍在使用的引流管转科时，交接必须包括引流管类型/位置、最近一段时间的引流量，以及需要通知医务人员的具体阈值。","terminalSentenceEn":"Facility policy: when a client transfers with an active drain, handoff must include drain type/location, last output with time period, and the specific provider-notification threshold.","terminalSentenceZh":"机构政策：患者携带仍在使用的引流管转科时，交接必须包括引流管类型/位置、最近一段时间的引流量，以及需要通知医务人员的具体阈值。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the single line that makes the handoff incomplete under facility policy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"标出根据机构政策导致交接不完整的唯一一行。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"SBAR handoff note for transfer from PACU to surgical floor:","zh":"麻醉恢复室转外科病房的 SBAR 交接记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"Situation: Client is transferring after laparoscopic cholecystectomy; alert, vital signs stable, pain 3/10.","zh":"现状：患者腹腔镜胆囊切除术后转科；清醒，生命体征稳定，疼痛 3/10。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Background: Jackson-Pratt drain in the right upper quadrant; dressing is dry and intact.","zh":"背景：右上腹有 Jackson-Pratt 引流管；敷料干燥完整。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Assessment: Drain output was 75 mL serosanguineous fluid from 0700 to 1100; bulb remains compressed.","zh":"评估：0700 至 1100 引流量为 75 毫升浆血性液体；负压球仍处于压缩状态。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Recommendation: Continue routine drain care and notify the provider if concerned.","zh":"建议：继续常规引流管护理，如有担心则通知医务人员。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Medication: Last oxycodone 5 mg by mouth was given at 1030; next PRN dose is no earlier than 1430.","zh":"用药：1030 已口服羟考酮 5 毫克；下一次按需给药最早不早于 1430。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Safety: Ambulates with one assist; fall-risk bracelet and non-skid socks are in place.","zh":"安全：需一人协助下床活动；已佩戴跌倒风险腕带并穿防滑袜。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The recommendation line omits the specific provider-notification threshold required by policy. The other lines supply relevant transfer, drain, medication, and safety information.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建议这一行遗漏了政策要求的、需要通知医务人员的具体阈值。其他行提供了转科、引流、用药和安全方面的相关信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a policy lists required handoff elements, compare each line to the policy rather than assuming a vague recommendation is enough.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当政策列出必须交接的要素时，要逐项对照政策，不要认为含糊的建议已经足够。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1917,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.447","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.447.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.447.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[169,240],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,75],"fullStemEn":"The client is alert and states, 'My brother may receive updates and pick me up. Do not tell my employer or my adult daughter that I am here.' Review the disclosure log. Highlight the single entry that contradicts the client's stated wishes.","fullStemZh":"患者清醒并表示：“我的哥哥可以接收病情更新并接我回家。不要告诉我的雇主或成年女儿我在这里。”查看信息披露记录。标出唯一一条与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the single entry that contradicts the client's stated wishes.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出唯一一条与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the disclosure log.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看信息披露记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Disclosure log:","zh":"信息披露记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"0820: Verified the brother's passcode and provided the discharge pickup time and parking instructions.","zh":"0820：核实哥哥的通行码后，提供出院接送时间和停车说明。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"0900: Provided the insurance plan with admission date and diagnosis code through the secure authorization portal.","zh":"0900：通过安全授权门户向保险计划提供入院日期和诊断代码。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"1015: Returned the adult daughter's call and stated, 'Your parent was admitted overnight but is doing well.'","zh":"1015：回拨成年女儿的电话并告知：“你的父/母昨晚住院了，目前情况不错。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"1140: Told the inpatient physical therapist the client's mobility restrictions for today's evaluation.","zh":"1140：告知住院物理治疗师患者今天评估所需的活动限制。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"1245: Declined the employer's request to confirm admission and transferred the caller to medical records for release-of-information instructions.","zh":"1245：拒绝雇主确认住院情况的请求，并将来电者转至病案部门了解信息释放流程。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"1330: Confirmed with the client that the brother remains the only family member approved for updates today.","zh":"1330：向患者确认哥哥仍是今天唯一获准接收更新的家属。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client specifically objected to telling the adult daughter about the admission, so confirming admission and condition to the daughter contradicts the client's stated wishes. The other disclosures either honor the stated contact limits or support care/payment functions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者明确反对将住院情况告知成年女儿，因此向女儿确认入院和病情与患者意愿相矛盾。其他披露要么遵守了患者指定的联系人限制，要么支持护理或付款相关流程。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Relationship alone does not authorize disclosure. Look for the patient's stated permission or objection in the scenario.","testTakingStrategyZh":"亲属关系本身并不等于授权披露。要在题干中寻找患者明确允许或反对的对象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1918,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.448","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.448.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.448.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[200,271],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,77],"fullStemEn":"The client is alert and capable and states, 'I will manage my medications myself. Please do not send instructions to my son; I only want him to drive me home.' Review the discharge-instruction sheet. Highlight the single entry that contradicts the client's stated wishes.","fullStemZh":"患者清醒、有决策能力，并表示：“我会自己管理药物。请不要把说明给我儿子；我只想让他开车接我回家。”查看出院指导单。标出唯一一条与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the single entry that contradicts the client's stated wishes.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出唯一一条与患者明确意愿相矛盾的记录。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the discharge-instruction sheet.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看出院指导单。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Discharge-instruction sheet:","zh":"出院指导单："},{"id":"s2","en":"Review the low-sodium diet and daily weights with the client using teach-back.","zh":"使用复述法与患者复习低钠饮食和每日体重监测。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Give the son a printed medication schedule because he is driving the client home.","zh":"因儿子开车接患者回家，将打印的用药时间表交给儿子。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Arrange heart-failure clinic follow-up for next Tuesday and confirm the client can attend.","zh":"安排下周二心力衰竭门诊随访，并确认患者能够参加。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Provide the pharmacy phone number and refill instructions directly to the client.","zh":"将药房电话号码和续药说明直接提供给患者。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Document the client's preferred pharmacy and transportation plan.","zh":"记录患者首选药房和交通安排。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Ask the client whether any caregiver should be added to teaching before instructions are shared.","zh":"在分享指导内容前，询问患者是否希望加入任何照护者参与宣教。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client declined sharing medication instructions with the son. Driving the client home does not authorize receiving medication details. The other entries provide teaching and planning directly to the client or ask permission before involving a caregiver.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者拒绝与儿子分享用药说明。开车接送患者并不代表有权接收用药细节。其他记录是直接向患者提供宣教和计划，或在让照护者参与前先征得患者同意。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For advocacy questions, protect the capable client's stated preference even when a family member is helpful with logistics.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做患者倡导题时，即使家属在交通等事务上有帮助，也要维护有决策能力患者的明确偏好。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1919,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.449","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.449.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.449.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[275,352],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,98],"fullStemEn":"The client states, 'I read lips and need written instructions or captioned video; I do not understand when people speak with masks on.' Facility policy requires requested communication accommodations to be included in handoff and discharge teaching. Review the handoff note. Highlight the single line that overrides or omits the required accommodation.","fullStemZh":"患者表示：“我靠读唇理解，需要书面说明或带字幕的视频；别人戴口罩说话时我听不懂。”机构政策要求在交接和出院宣教中纳入患者要求的沟通便利措施。查看交接记录。标出唯一一条忽略或否定所需便利措施的内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the single line that overrides or omits the required accommodation.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出唯一一条忽略或否定所需便利措施的内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the handoff note.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看交接记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Handoff note before discharge teaching:","zh":"出院宣教前交接记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"Diagnosis: Left lower-leg cellulitis; IV antibiotics completed, oral antibiotic prescription sent to pharmacy.","zh":"诊断：左小腿蜂窝织炎；静脉抗生素已完成，口服抗生素处方已发送至药房。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Allergies: No known drug allergies documented; verify again before first home dose teaching.","zh":"过敏史：病历记录无已知药物过敏；首次家庭用药宣教前再次核实。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Communication: Client speaks English; captions and written instructions are not needed because the client nodded during teaching.","zh":"沟通：患者会说英语；因患者宣教时点头，所以不需要字幕或书面说明。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Wound care: Marked drainage area on dressing at 1400; recheck before discharge and teach when to call the clinic.","zh":"伤口护理：1400 已标记敷料渗液范围；出院前复查并宣教何时联系门诊。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Safety: Client uses a cane at baseline; ensure cane is within reach before leaving by wheelchair.","zh":"安全：患者平时使用手杖；坐轮椅离开前确保手杖在可及范围内。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Follow-up: Clinic visit scheduled in 48 hours; client has transportation and pharmacy pickup arranged.","zh":"随访：48 小时后门诊复诊；患者已安排交通和取药。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The communication line dismisses the client's stated need for written or captioned teaching. English proficiency does not remove a hearing-related communication accommodation. The other lines are relevant discharge details.","rationaleCorrectZh":"沟通这一行否定了患者明确提出的书面或字幕宣教需求。会说英语并不能取消与听力相关的沟通便利措施。其他行是相关的出院信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not equate nodding or English fluency with comprehension. Key the line that ignores the specific accommodation the client requested.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把点头或会说英语等同于理解。要选择忽略患者具体便利需求的那一行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Review the handoff note.","controlSentenceZh":"查看交接记录。"}
{"queueIndex":1920,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.450","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.450.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.450.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[313,347],"terminalOffsetsZh":[97,112],"fullStemEn":"A Mandarin-speaking client with limited English proficiency is reviewing a surgical consent form. The client's adult child offers to interpret. Facility policy: education for informed consent must be provided through a named language-service role, not through family, unless an emergency exception is documented. The nurse should request a ______.","fullStemZh":"一名以普通话为主要语言且英语能力有限的患者正在查看手术知情同意书。患者的成年子女主动提出帮忙翻译。机构政策：知情同意相关宣教必须由指定的语言服务角色提供，不能由家属翻译，除非已记录紧急例外情况。护士应申请一名 ______。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should request a ______.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应申请一名 ______。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy: education for informed consent must be provided through a named language-service role, not through family, unless an emergency exception is documented.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策：知情同意相关宣教必须由指定的语言服务角色提供，不能由家属翻译，除非已记录紧急例外情况。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"language-service role","zh":"语言服务角色"},"acceptable":["qualified medical interpreter","qualified interpreter","certified medical interpreter","professional medical interpreter","trained medical interpreter","medical interpreter"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The closed-vocabulary role is a qualified medical interpreter. Consent education requires accurate, impartial communication; family members should not replace the interpreter role under the stated policy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"封闭词汇答案是合格医疗口译员。知情同意宣教需要准确、中立的沟通；根据题干政策，家属不能替代口译员角色。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When consent, discharge teaching, or rights information is involved, choose the formal language-service role rather than an available family member.","testTakingStrategyZh":"涉及知情同意、出院宣教或权利告知时，应选择正式语言服务角色，而不是临时可用的家属。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1921,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.451","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.451.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.451.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[270,332],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,89],"fullStemEn":"A client is being discharged with negative-pressure wound therapy. Facility policy: the discharge handoff must name the follow-up destination responsible for the first dressing change within 24 hours. The case manager arranged skilled nursing visits beginning tomorrow. The nurse should list the follow-up destination as the ______.","fullStemZh":"患者将带负压伤口治疗装置出院。机构政策：出院交接必须注明负责 24 小时内首次换药的随访去向。个案管理师已安排从明天开始的专业护理上门服务。护士应将随访去向填写为 ______。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should list the follow-up destination as the ______.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将随访去向填写为 ______。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The case manager arranged skilled nursing visits beginning tomorrow.","penultimateSentenceZh":"个案管理师已安排从明天开始的专业护理上门服务。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"follow-up destination","zh":"随访去向"},"acceptable":["home health agency","home health nursing agency","skilled home health agency","home health nurse","home health nursing","visiting nurse service","visiting nurse agency"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The arranged follow-up destination is the home health agency or home health nursing service. The handoff should identify the service responsible for the first dressing change, not simply state that the client has a device.","rationaleCorrectZh":"已安排的随访去向是居家护理机构或居家护理服务。交接应明确负责首次换药的服务方，而不只是说明患者带有装置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the clues about what was actually arranged. A discharge handoff should identify who owns the first postdischarge task.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据题干中已经安排的服务作答。出院交接应说明出院后第一项护理任务由谁负责。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1922,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_moc2_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.452","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.452.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.452.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[319,367],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,103],"fullStemEn":"A nurse realizes that another client's discharge packet was handed to the wrong client for 3 minutes before it was retrieved unopened. Facility policy: suspected misdirection of protected health information must be secured, the supervisor notified, and the event reported to the role that completes breach-risk review. The nurse should report the event to the ______.","fullStemZh":"护士发现另一名患者的出院资料袋被误交给错误患者，3 分钟后取回且未打开。机构政策：疑似受保护健康信息误交事件必须先确保资料安全、通知主管，并报告给负责违规风险审查的角色。护士应将该事件报告给 ______。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should report the event to the ______.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将该事件报告给 ______。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy: suspected misdirection of protected health information must be secured, the supervisor notified, and the event reported to the role that completes breach-risk review.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策：疑似受保护健康信息误交事件必须先确保资料安全、通知主管，并报告给负责违规风险审查的角色。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"role for breach-risk review","zh":"违规风险审查角色"},"acceptable":["privacy officer","facility privacy officer","HIPAA privacy officer","privacy and compliance officer","compliance and privacy officer","privacy/compliance officer"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The role named by the policy is the privacy officer, who evaluates suspected PHI misdirection for breach risk after the immediate safety steps are taken.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干政策所指角色是隐私官。立即确保资料安全后，隐私官负责评估疑似受保护健康信息误交的违规风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a privacy event has already occurred, separate immediate containment from required reporting. The reporting role is the one assigned breach-risk review in the policy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"隐私事件已经发生时，要区分立即控制风险和规定报告流程。报告对象是政策中负责违规风险审查的角色。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1923,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.453","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.453.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.453.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[372,407],"terminalOffsetsZh":[136,147],"fullStemEn":"At 1800, a client taking warfarin for atrial fibrillation has an INR of 5.6. The target INR is 2.0–3.0. The 1800 warfarin dose has not been given. The unit protocol states: for INR greater than 4.0 without active major bleeding, verify the result, hold the scheduled warfarin dose, assess for bleeding, institute bleeding precautions, and notify the prescriber with SBAR. Place the nursing actions in order.","fullStemZh":"18:00，一名因心房颤动服用华法林的患者 INR 为 5.6。目标 INR 为 2.0–3.0。18:00 的华法林尚未给药。科室流程规定：若 INR 大于 4.0 且无活动性大出血，应先核实结果，暂停本次华法林，评估出血，落实出血预防措施，并用 SBAR 通知开方者。请按顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit protocol states: for INR greater than 4.0 without active major bleeding, verify the result, hold the scheduled warfarin dose, assess for bleeding, institute bleeding precautions, and notify the prescriber with SBAR.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室流程规定：若 INR 大于 4.0 且无活动性大出血，应先核实结果，暂停本次华法林，评估出血，落实出血预防措施，并用 SBAR 通知开方者。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Notify the prescriber using SBAR with the INR, held dose, and assessment findings.","zh":"用 SBAR 向开方者报告 INR、已暂停的剂量和评估结果。"},{"id":"D","en":"Institute bleeding precautions, including fall prevention and avoiding unnecessary venipunctures.","zh":"落实出血预防措施，包括预防跌倒并避免不必要的静脉穿刺。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the scheduled 1800 warfarin dose per protocol.","zh":"按流程暂停 18:00 这次华法林。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess for bleeding, including gums, urine, stool, bruising, and neurologic changes.","zh":"评估是否出血，包括牙龈、尿液、粪便、瘀斑和神经系统变化。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the INR result and compare it with the ordered target range.","zh":"核实 INR 结果，并与医嘱目标范围比较。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The closed protocol creates a unique order: confirm the supratherapeutic INR against the target, prevent additional anticoagulant exposure by holding the due dose, assess whether bleeding is already occurring, reduce injury/bleeding risk, and then report a complete SBAR for additional orders.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干给出的流程使顺序唯一：先确认 INR 高于目标范围，再通过暂停本次剂量避免继续抗凝，随后评估是否已经出血，降低受伤和出血风险，最后用完整 SBAR 报告以便取得后续医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a stem gives a medication protocol, follow that protocol exactly: verify, stop further exposure, assess the client, protect the client, then escalate with complete data.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干给出用药流程时，要按流程排序：核实，停止继续暴露，评估患者，保护患者，再带着完整资料升级报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1924,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.454","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.454.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.454.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[500,535],"terminalOffsetsZh":[164,175],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving an IV unfractionated heparin infusion for a pulmonary embolism has a target aPTT of 60–80 seconds. The current aPTT is 128 seconds, and the infusion is running. The heparin protocol states: for aPTT greater than 100 seconds, stop the infusion immediately, assess for bleeding and hemodynamic instability, notify the prescriber or anticoagulation service, obtain a repeat aPTT in 1 hour, and restart only at the lower protocol rate when the repeat aPTT is within the restart range. Place the nursing actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名因肺栓塞接受静脉普通肝素输注的患者，目标 aPTT 为 60–80 秒。目前 aPTT 为 128 秒，输液正在进行。肝素流程规定：aPTT 大于 100 秒时，立即停止输注，评估出血和血流动力学不稳定，通知开方者或抗凝服务，1 小时后复查 aPTT；只有复查 aPTT 达到可重新开始的范围时，才按较低的流程速率重新开始。请按顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The heparin protocol states: for aPTT greater than 100 seconds, stop the infusion immediately, assess for bleeding and hemodynamic instability, notify the prescriber or anticoagulation service, obtain a repeat aPTT in 1 hour, and restart only at the lower protocol rate when the repeat aPTT is within the restart range.","penultimateSentenceZh":"肝素流程规定：aPTT 大于 100 秒时，立即停止输注，评估出血和血流动力学不稳定，通知开方者或抗凝服务，1 小时后复查 aPTT；只有复查 aPTT 达到可重新开始的范围时，才按较低的流程速率重新开始。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assess vital signs, IV sites, urine, stool, skin, and mental status for bleeding or instability.","zh":"评估生命体征、静脉穿刺处、尿液、粪便、皮肤和意识状态，查找出血或不稳定。"},{"id":"E","en":"Restart heparin at the lower protocol rate only after the repeat aPTT is in the restart range.","zh":"只有复查 aPTT 在可重新开始范围内时，才按较低流程速率重新开始肝素。"},{"id":"D","en":"Obtain the repeat aPTT 1 hour after stopping the infusion.","zh":"停止输注 1 小时后复查 aPTT。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the prescriber or anticoagulation service with the current rate, aPTT, and assessment findings.","zh":"向开方者或抗凝服务报告当前输注速率、aPTT 和评估发现。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the heparin infusion immediately.","zh":"立即停止肝素输注。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The infusion is actively exposing the client to more anticoagulant, so stopping it is first. Assessment determines whether urgent reversal or resuscitation is needed. Notification comes with complete data. The protocol then requires a timed repeat aPTT before any lower-rate restart.","rationaleCorrectZh":"输液正在使患者继续暴露于抗凝药，因此首先停止输注。随后评估是否需要紧急逆转或复苏。带着完整资料通知相关人员。流程接着要求按时复查 aPTT，之后才可按较低速率重新开始。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For an actively infusing high-alert medication, remove the ongoing exposure before collecting follow-up data or restarting therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到正在输注的高警示药物，先移除持续暴露，再收集后续资料或重新开始治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The heparin protocol states: for aPTT greater than 100 seconds, stop the infusion immediately, assess for bleeding and hemodynamic instability, notify the prescriber or anticoagulation service, obtain a repeat aPTT in 1 hour, and restart only at the lower protocol rate when the repeat aPTT is within the restart range.","controlSentenceZh":"肝素流程规定：aPTT 大于 100 秒时，立即停止输注，评估出血和血流动力学不稳定，通知开方者或抗凝服务，1 小时后复查 aPTT；只有复查 aPTT 达到可重新开始的范围时，才按较低的流程速率重新开始。"}
{"queueIndex":1925,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.455","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.455.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.455.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[473,508],"terminalOffsetsZh":[155,166],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer digoxin 0.125 mg PO. The medication safety protocol states: before each dose, measure the apical pulse for 1 full minute and review the current potassium; hold digoxin for apical pulse less than 60/min or potassium less than 3.5 mEq/L; if held, assess for toxicity symptoms and notify the prescriber with the held-dose reason. The client's apical pulse is 56/min, potassium is 3.2 mEq/L, and the client reports nausea and yellow halos. Place the nursing actions in order.","fullStemZh":"护士准备给予地高辛 0.125 mg 口服。用药安全流程规定：每次给药前测量心尖脉 1 整分钟并查看当前血钾；若心尖脉低于 60 次/分或血钾低于 3.5 mEq/L，应暂停地高辛；若暂停给药，需评估中毒症状，并将暂停原因报告开方者。患者心尖脉 56 次/分，血钾 3.2 mEq/L，并诉恶心和看见黄色光圈。请按顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's apical pulse is 56/min, potassium is 3.2 mEq/L, and the client reports nausea and yellow halos.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者心尖脉 56 次/分，血钾 3.2 mEq/L，并诉恶心和看见黄色光圈。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Notify the prescriber with the apical pulse, potassium, symptoms, and held-dose status.","zh":"向开方者报告心尖脉、血钾、症状以及已暂停给药的情况。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess for digoxin-toxicity symptoms such as nausea, visual changes, and worsening bradycardia.","zh":"评估地高辛中毒症状，如恶心、视觉改变和心动过缓加重。"},{"id":"B","en":"Review the current potassium result before giving the dose.","zh":"给药前查看当前血钾结果。"},{"id":"A","en":"Measure the apical pulse for 1 full minute and compare it with the hold parameter.","zh":"测量心尖脉 1 整分钟，并与暂停给药参数比较。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hold the scheduled digoxin dose.","zh":"暂停本次地高辛。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The protocol requires both pre-dose checks before administration. The apical pulse and potassium each meet a hold condition, so the nurse withholds digoxin. Toxicity assessment then supplies clinically important data for the notification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"流程要求给药前完成两项检查。心尖脉和血钾都达到暂停条件，因此护士应暂停地高辛。随后评估中毒症状，为报告提供关键临床资料。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pre-dose safety items, identify the parameters the nurse must check before administration, then apply the stated hold rule before escalating.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到给药前安全题，先找护士给药前必须检查的参数，再按题干给出的暂停规则处理，最后再升级报告。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client's apical pulse is 56/min, potassium is 3.2 mEq/L, and the client reports nausea and yellow halos.","controlSentenceZh":"患者心尖脉 56 次/分，血钾 3.2 mEq/L，并诉恶心和看见黄色光圈。"}
{"queueIndex":1926,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.456","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.456.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.456.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[262,342],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,103],"fullStemEn":"A client with a mechanical mitral valve is receiving enoxaparin while starting warfarin. The bridge protocol states: continue enoxaparin until the laboratory value that measures warfarin effect is within the target range of 2.5–3.5 for two consecutive readings. Before discontinuing enoxaparin, the nurse should verify which laboratory value?","fullStemZh":"一名机械性二尖瓣置换患者在开始华法林治疗的同时接受依诺肝素。桥接流程规定：在反映华法林效果的实验室指标连续两次达到 2.5–3.5 目标范围前，继续使用依诺肝素。停止依诺肝素前，护士应核实哪一项实验室指标？","terminalSentenceEn":"Before discontinuing enoxaparin, the nurse should verify which laboratory value?","terminalSentenceZh":"停止依诺肝素前，护士应核实哪一项实验室指标？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The bridge protocol states: continue enoxaparin until the laboratory value that measures warfarin effect is within the target range of 2.5–3.5 for two consecutive readings.","penultimateSentenceZh":"桥接流程规定：在反映华法林效果的实验室指标连续两次达到 2.5–3.5 目标范围前，继续使用依诺肝素。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Laboratory value","zh":"实验室指标"},"acceptable":["INR","international normalized ratio","International Normalized Ratio","国际标准化比值"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"INR is the laboratory value used to monitor warfarin effect. The protocol gives the target INR range and requires two therapeutic readings before stopping the parenteral bridge.","rationaleCorrectZh":"INR 是用于监测华法林作用的实验室指标。题干流程给出了目标 INR 范围，并要求连续两次达到治疗范围后才停止肠外桥接抗凝。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the anticoagulant to its monitoring test: warfarin links to INR; unfractionated heparin commonly links to aPTT or anti-Xa; enoxaparin usually does not use routine INR monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把抗凝药与监测指标配对：华法林对应 INR；普通肝素常对应 aPTT 或抗 Xa；依诺肝素通常不靠 INR 常规监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The bridge protocol states: continue enoxaparin until the laboratory value that measures warfarin effect is within the target range of 2.5–3.5 for two consecutive readings.","controlSentenceZh":"桥接流程规定：在反映华法林效果的实验室指标连续两次达到 2.5–3.5 目标范围前，继续使用依诺肝素。"}
{"queueIndex":1927,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.457","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.457.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.457.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[315,372],"terminalOffsetsZh":[99,113],"fullStemEn":"A client who received rapid-acting insulin is awake, able to swallow, and has a capillary blood glucose of 54 mg/dL. The unit hypoglycemia protocol states: give 15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate, then recheck capillary blood glucose in the specified time and repeat treatment until the glucose is at least 70 mg/dL. The nurse should recheck the glucose in how many minutes?","fullStemZh":"一名接受速效胰岛素的患者清醒、能吞咽，指尖血糖为 54 mg/dL。科室低血糖流程规定：给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物，然后在规定时间复查指尖血糖，并重复处理直到血糖至少达到 70 mg/dL。护士应在多少分钟后复查血糖？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should recheck the glucose in how many minutes?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应在多少分钟后复查血糖？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit hypoglycemia protocol states: give 15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate, then recheck capillary blood glucose in the specified time and repeat treatment until the glucose is at least 70 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室低血糖流程规定：给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物，然后在规定时间复查指尖血糖，并重复处理直到血糖至少达到 70 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minutes","zh":"分钟"},"acceptable":["15","15 min","15 minutes","15 分钟"],"numeric":{"value":15,"tolerance":0,"unit":"minutes"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For an awake client who can swallow, the protocol uses fast carbohydrate and reassessment in 15 minutes. This checks whether insulin-related hypoglycemia has corrected before repeating treatment or giving a meal/snack.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于清醒且能吞咽的患者，流程是给予快速碳水化合物并在 15 分钟后复查。这样可判断胰岛素相关低血糖是否纠正，再决定是否重复处理或进食。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the protocol's timing cue. For insulin-related hypoglycemia in a conscious client, treat first, then reassess at the stated short interval before moving on.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抓住流程中的时间提示。清醒患者发生胰岛素相关低血糖时，先处理，再在题干规定的短间隔后复查。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1928,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.458","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.458.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.458.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[336,359],"terminalOffsetsZh":[127,133],"fullStemEn":"A client with heart failure has morning medications due: lisinopril 20 mg PO and spironolactone 25 mg PO. The medication protocol states to hold potassium-retaining cardiovascular medications and notify the prescriber for serum potassium 5.5 mEq/L or greater. Morning labs: potassium 5.8 mEq/L, creatinine 1.0 mg/dL, glucose 104 mg/dL. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一名心力衰竭患者早晨需服药：赖诺普利 20 mg 口服、螺内酯 25 mg 口服。用药流程规定：若血清钾 ≥5.5 mEq/L，应暂停保钾相关心血管药物并通知开方者。晨间化验：血钾 5.8 mEq/L，肌酐 1.0 mg/dL，血糖 104 mg/dL。请完成陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Morning labs: potassium 5.8 mEq/L, creatinine 1.0 mg/dL, glucose 104 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"晨间化验：血钾 5.8 mEq/L，肌酐 1.0 mg/dL，血糖 104 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Before administering the morning medications, the nurse should {{action}} because the client is at risk for {{risk}}.","zh":"在给予晨间药物前，护士应 {{action}}，因为患者有发生 {{risk}} 的风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"action_give_as_scheduled","en":"give both medications as scheduled","zh":"按时给予两种药物"},{"id":"action_request_k","en":"request a potassium supplement before giving the medications","zh":"给药前申请补钾"},{"id":"action_hold_glucose_meds","en":"hold only diabetes medications and give the cardiac medications","zh":"只暂停糖尿病药物，并给予心脏药物"},{"id":"action_hold_k_meds","en":"hold the lisinopril and spironolactone and notify the prescriber","zh":"暂停赖诺普利和螺内酯，并通知开方者"}],"correct":"action_hold_k_meds"},{"id":"risk","options":[{"id":"risk_hypoglycemia","en":"hypoglycemia","zh":"低血糖"},{"id":"risk_hypokalemia","en":"hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"},{"id":"risk_hyperkalemia","en":"worsening hyperkalemia","zh":"高钾血症加重"},{"id":"risk_bleeding","en":"anticoagulant bleeding","zh":"抗凝相关出血"}],"correct":"risk_hyperkalemia"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The potassium is 5.8 mEq/L, above the stated 5.5 mEq/L hold-and-notify threshold. Lisinopril and spironolactone can both increase potassium, so giving them would worsen the immediate electrolyte risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钾 5.8 mEq/L，高于题干规定的 5.5 mEq/L 暂停并通知阈值。赖诺普利和螺内酯都可能升高血钾，继续给药会加重当前电解质风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cardiovascular medications, check the parameter the drug can worsen. ACE inhibitors and potassium-sparing diuretics both point to serum potassium.","testTakingStrategyZh":"心血管药物题要检查药物可能恶化的参数。ACE 抑制剂和保钾利尿剂都指向血清钾。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1929,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_pharm_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.459","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.459.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.459.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[412,435],"terminalOffsetsZh":[154,160],"fullStemEn":"A client takes apixaban for atrial fibrillation. The medication safety protocol states: hold the next apixaban dose, assess bleeding, and notify the prescriber for black tarry stool, active bleeding, or a hemoglobin decrease of 2 g/dL or more. Today the client reports black tarry stool. Hemoglobin decreased from 13.1 g/dL yesterday to 10.8 g/dL today. Blood pressure is 102/64 mm Hg and heart rate is 112/min. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一名因心房颤动服用阿哌沙班的患者。用药安全流程规定：若出现黑色柏油样便、活动性出血，或血红蛋白下降 ≥2 g/dL，应暂停下一次阿哌沙班，评估出血，并通知开方者。今天患者报告黑色柏油样便。血红蛋白从昨天 13.1 g/dL 降至今天 10.8 g/dL。血压 102/64 mm Hg，心率 112 次/分。请完成陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Blood pressure is 102/64 mm Hg and heart rate is 112/min.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压 102/64 mm Hg，心率 112 次/分。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{action}} because the findings are most consistent with {{condition}}; the priority laboratory parameter to trend is {{parameter}}.","zh":"护士应 {{action}}，因为这些发现最符合 {{condition}}；优先追踪的实验室指标是 {{parameter}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"action_admin_vitk","en":"administer vitamin K as the direct reversal agent for apixaban","zh":"给予维生素 K 作为阿哌沙班的直接逆转剂"},{"id":"action_hold_apixaban","en":"hold the next apixaban dose, assess bleeding, and notify the prescriber","zh":"暂停下一次阿哌沙班，评估出血，并通知开方者"},{"id":"action_switch_warfarin","en":"start warfarin immediately without contacting the prescriber","zh":"不联系开方者，立即开始华法林"},{"id":"action_give_extra_apixaban","en":"give an extra apixaban dose for stroke prevention","zh":"为预防卒中额外给予一次阿哌沙班"}],"correct":"action_hold_apixaban"},{"id":"condition","options":[{"id":"condition_ischemic_stroke","en":"ischemic stroke from under-anticoagulation","zh":"抗凝不足导致的缺血性卒中"},{"id":"condition_hyperkalemia","en":"medication-related hyperkalemia","zh":"药物相关高钾血症"},{"id":"condition_hit","en":"heparin-induced thrombocytopenia","zh":"肝素诱导性血小板减少症"},{"id":"condition_gi_bleeding","en":"gastrointestinal bleeding while anticoagulated","zh":"抗凝期间胃肠道出血"}],"correct":"condition_gi_bleeding"},{"id":"parameter","options":[{"id":"parameter_aptt","en":"aPTT","zh":"aPTT 活化部分凝血活酶时间"},{"id":"parameter_inr","en":"INR","zh":"INR 国际标准化比值"},{"id":"parameter_hgb_hct","en":"hemoglobin and hematocrit","zh":"血红蛋白和血细胞比容"},{"id":"parameter_potassium","en":"serum potassium","zh":"血清钾"}],"correct":"parameter_hgb_hct"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Black tarry stool plus a hemoglobin drop greater than 2 g/dL meets the stated protocol trigger for suspected bleeding on apixaban. The nurse's immediate actions include holding the next dose, assessing bleeding and stability, notifying the prescriber, and trending hemoglobin/hematocrit rather than INR or aPTT for routine apixaban effect.","rationaleCorrectZh":"黑色柏油样便加上血红蛋白下降超过 2 g/dL，符合题干流程中阿哌沙班用药期间疑似出血的触发条件。护士的立即措施包括暂停下一次给药、评估出血和稳定性、通知开方者，并追踪血红蛋白/血细胞比容，而不是用 INR 或 aPTT 常规监测阿哌沙班效果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With anticoagulants, bleeding cues override routine administration. Match the monitoring parameter to the drug and the complication: suspected blood loss points to hemoglobin and hematocrit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝药题中，出血线索优先于常规给药。将监测指标同时对应药物和并发症：疑似失血应追踪血红蛋白和血细胞比容。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Blood pressure is 102/64 mm Hg and heart rate is 112/min.","controlSentenceZh":"血压 102/64 mm Hg，心率 112 次/分。"}
{"queueIndex":1930,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.460","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.460.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.460.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[269,325],"terminalOffsetsZh":[105,120],"fullStemEn":"A client with end-stage kidney disease is scheduled for tunneled dialysis catheter insertion in 2 hr. Facility policy requires immediate escalation before an invasive procedure for potassium ≥6.0 mEq/L, ionized calcium <0.90 mmol/L, INR ≥1.8, or platelets <50 ×10³/µL. Highlight the result that requires immediate escalation.","fullStemZh":"一名终末期肾病患者将在 2 小时后接受隧道式透析导管置入。院内规定：侵入性操作前若钾 ≥6.0 mEq/L、离子钙 <0.90 mmol/L、INR ≥1.8，或血小板 <50 ×10³/µL，需立即升级处理。请标出需要立即升级处理的结果。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the result that requires immediate escalation.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要立即升级处理的结果。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires immediate escalation before an invasive procedure for potassium ≥6.0 mEq/L, ionized calcium <0.90 mmol/L, INR ≥1.8, or platelets <50 ×10³/µL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"院内规定：侵入性操作前若钾 ≥6.0 mEq/L、离子钙 <0.90 mmol/L、INR ≥1.8，或血小板 <50 ×10³/µL，需立即升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"rrp01_wbc","en":"WBC 7.8 ×10³/µL","zh":"白细胞 7.8 ×10³/µL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp01_hgb","en":"Hemoglobin 10.1 g/dL","zh":"血红蛋白 10.1 g/dL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp01_platelets","en":"Platelets 146 ×10³/µL","zh":"血小板 146 ×10³/µL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp01_k","en":"Potassium 6.2 mEq/L","zh":"钾 6.2 mEq/L","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp01_creatinine","en":"Creatinine 8.4 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐 8.4 mg/dL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp01_inr","en":"INR 1.1","zh":"INR 1.1","selectable":true}],"correct":["rrp01_k"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The potassium is above the stated critical threshold and creates risk for life-threatening dysrhythmias before sedation or line placement. The other values do not meet the facility escalation triggers in the stem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"钾值超过题干给出的危急阈值，操作和镇静前存在致命心律失常风险。其他结果未达到题干中的升级处理触发标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare each value with the protocol thresholds in the stem rather than reacting to every abnormal chronic kidney disease value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先把每个结果与题干中的院内阈值逐一比较，不要因为慢性肾病常见异常值而误选。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires immediate escalation before an invasive procedure for potassium ≥6.0 mEq/L, ionized calcium <0.90 mmol/L, INR ≥1.8, or platelets <50 ×10³/µL.","controlSentenceZh":"院内规定：侵入性操作前若钾 ≥6.0 mEq/L、离子钙 <0.90 mmol/L、INR ≥1.8，或血小板 <50 ×10³/µL，需立即升级处理。"}
{"queueIndex":1931,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.461","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.461.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.461.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[227,286],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,82],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for spinal anesthesia at 0900. The perioperative protocol states: signed consent and site marking must be complete, and prophylactic enoxaparin must be held for at least 12 hr before neuraxial anesthesia. Highlight the checklist entry that is unsafe or incomplete.","fullStemZh":"患者计划 0900 接受脊髓麻醉。围手术期规定：必须完成签署同意书和手术部位标记；预防性依诺肝素在椎管内麻醉前至少停用 12 小时。请标出不安全或未完成的核对项目。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the checklist entry that is unsafe or incomplete.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出不安全或未完成的核对项目。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The perioperative protocol states: signed consent and site marking must be complete, and prophylactic enoxaparin must be held for at least 12 hr before neuraxial anesthesia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"围手术期规定：必须完成签署同意书和手术部位标记；预防性依诺肝素在椎管内麻醉前至少停用 12 小时。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"rrp02_id","en":"Identity verified with name and date of birth.","zh":"已用姓名和出生日期核对身份。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp02_consent","en":"Signed procedure and anesthesia consent are in the chart.","zh":"病历中已有已签署的手术和麻醉同意书。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp02_site","en":"Surgical site marked by the proceduralist.","zh":"手术部位已由操作者标记。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp02_npo","en":"NPO since midnight except sips of water with approved medications.","zh":"午夜后禁食；仅按医嘱用少量水服用允许的药物。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp02_enox","en":"Enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously was administered at 0600.","zh":"0600 已皮下注射依诺肝素 40 mg。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp02_chg","en":"Chlorhexidine bath completed the evening before surgery.","zh":"术前一晚已完成氯己定沐浴。","selectable":true}],"correct":["rrp02_enox"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The enoxaparin dose at 0600 leaves only 3 hr before the planned spinal anesthesia, violating the stated 12-hr hold protocol and increasing spinal/epidural hematoma risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"0600 给依诺肝素距离 0900 脊髓麻醉只有 3 小时，违反题干规定的 12 小时停药要求，并增加脊髓/硬膜外血肿风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pre-op checklist items, match the time-stamped entry to the exact protocol interval.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做术前核对题时，要把带时间的记录与题干给出的具体时间间隔相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1932,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.462","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.462.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.462.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[260,312],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,92],"fullStemEn":"A client returns from a percutaneous liver biopsy. The post-procedure protocol requires immediate reassessment and escalation for systolic blood pressure drop ≥20 mm Hg from baseline, heart rate >110/min, increasing abdominal rigidity, or right shoulder pain. Highlight the complication cue in the progress note.","fullStemZh":"患者经皮肝活检后返回病房。术后规定：若收缩压较基线下降 ≥20 mm Hg、心率 >110 次/分、腹部僵硬加重，或出现右肩痛，需立即重新评估并升级处理。请标出进展记录中的并发症线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the complication cue in the progress note.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出进展记录中的并发症线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The post-procedure protocol requires immediate reassessment and escalation for systolic blood pressure drop ≥20 mm Hg from baseline, heart rate >110/min, increasing abdominal rigidity, or right shoulder pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"术后规定：若收缩压较基线下降 ≥20 mm Hg、心率 >110 次/分、腹部僵硬加重，或出现右肩痛，需立即重新评估并升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"rrp03_dressing","en":"Biopsy dressing dry and intact with a 1-cm shadow of old drainage.","zh":"活检敷料干燥完整，有 1 cm 陈旧渗血痕迹。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp03_position","en":"Client remains on right side as instructed.","zh":"患者按要求保持右侧卧位。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp03_vitals","en":"Reports right shoulder pain 7/10; BP 96/58 from baseline 124/76, HR 118/min.","zh":"主诉右肩痛 7/10；血压从基线 124/76 降至 96/58，心率 118 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp03_puncture","en":"Puncture site has mild localized tenderness.","zh":"穿刺部位有轻度局部压痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp03_urine","en":"Voided 250 mL clear yellow urine.","zh":"排出清亮黄色尿液 250 mL。","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp03_temp","en":"Temperature 98.8 °F (37.1 °C).","zh":"体温 98.8 °F (37.1 °C)。","selectable":true}],"correct":["rrp03_vitals"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Right shoulder pain with hypotension and tachycardia after liver biopsy meets multiple stated triggers and suggests possible intra-abdominal bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝活检后出现右肩痛、低血压和心动过速，符合题干多个触发条件，提示可能有腹腔内出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A clustered change in pain location plus vital signs after a biopsy is stronger than a single expected local finding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"活检后若疼痛部位改变并伴随生命体征变化，比单一局部轻微表现更值得警惕。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1933,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.463","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.463.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.463.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,80],"fullStemEn":"A client is 8 hr post-thyroidectomy. The unit protocol requires immediate escalation for serum calcium ≤7.5 mg/dL, ionized calcium <0.90 mmol/L, or new stridor. Highlight the diagnostic result that requires escalation.","fullStemZh":"患者甲状腺切除术后 8 小时。病区规定：血清钙 ≤7.5 mg/dL、离子钙 <0.90 mmol/L，或新发喉鸣需立即升级处理。请标出需要升级处理的诊断结果。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the diagnostic result that requires escalation.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要升级处理的诊断结果。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit protocol requires immediate escalation for serum calcium ≤7.5 mg/dL, ionized calcium <0.90 mmol/L, or new stridor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区规定：血清钙 ≤7.5 mg/dL、离子钙 <0.90 mmol/L，或新发喉鸣需立即升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"rrp04_wbc","en":"WBC 10.2 ×10³/µL","zh":"白细胞 10.2 ×10³/µL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp04_hgb","en":"Hemoglobin 12.5 g/dL","zh":"血红蛋白 12.5 g/dL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp04_ca","en":"Total serum calcium 7.2 mg/dL","zh":"总血清钙 7.2 mg/dL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp04_mg","en":"Magnesium 1.9 mg/dL","zh":"镁 1.9 mg/dL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp04_phos","en":"Phosphorus 3.6 mg/dL","zh":"磷 3.6 mg/dL","selectable":true},{"id":"rrp04_o2","en":"SpO₂ 97% on room air","zh":"室内空气下 SpO₂ 97%","selectable":true}],"correct":["rrp04_ca"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The serum calcium is below the stated post-thyroidectomy escalation threshold. Hypocalcemia can indicate parathyroid injury or suppression and may progress to tetany or airway compromise.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血清钙低于题干给出的甲状腺术后升级阈值。低钙血症可能提示甲状旁腺损伤或功能受抑，可进展为手足搐搦或气道受威胁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the protocol line to decide which abnormality is time-critical in this specific post-op context.","testTakingStrategyZh":"依据题干中的病区规定，判断在该术后情境中哪项异常具有时间紧迫性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1934,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.464","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.464.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.464.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[237,344],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,124],"fullStemEn":"During a first hemodialysis treatment for severe uremia, the client develops a sudden severe headache, nausea, restlessness, and increasing confusion 90 min after dialysis begins. Blood glucose is 108 mg/dL and the access site is clean. Complete the bowtie by selecting the likely complication, 2 actions, and 2 parameters to monitor or report.","fullStemZh":"一名严重尿毒症患者第一次接受血液透析。透析开始 90 分钟后，患者突然出现剧烈头痛、恶心、烦躁不安，并且意识混乱加重。血糖 108 mg/dL，透析通路部位清洁。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的并发症、2 项处理措施，以及 2 项需要监测或报告的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the likely complication, 2 actions, and 2 parameters to monitor or report.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的并发症、2 项处理措施，以及 2 项需要监测或报告的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Blood glucose is 108 mg/dL and the access site is clean.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血糖 108 mg/dL，透析通路部位清洁。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Likely complication","zh":"最可能的并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp05_c_hemolysis","en":"Dialysis-associated hemolysis","zh":"透析相关溶血"},{"id":"rrp05_c_hypotension","en":"Intradialytic hypotension from excess ultrafiltration","zh":"过度超滤导致的透析中低血压"},{"id":"rrp05_c_dds","en":"Dialysis disequilibrium syndrome","zh":"透析失衡综合征"},{"id":"rrp05_c_access_infection","en":"Dialysis access infection","zh":"透析通路感染"}],"correct":"rrp05_c_dds"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions","zh":"护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp05_a_hypotonic","en":"Administer a rapid hypotonic IV fluid bolus","zh":"快速给予低渗静脉液体冲击"},{"id":"rrp05_a_increase_uf","en":"Increase the ultrafiltration rate to finish fluid removal sooner","zh":"提高超滤率以更快完成脱水"},{"id":"rrp05_a_ambulate","en":"Assist the client to ambulate to reduce restlessness","zh":"协助患者下床走动以减轻烦躁"},{"id":"rrp05_a_slow_stop","en":"Stop or slow dialysis per protocol and call the dialysis nurse/nephrology team","zh":"按流程停止或减慢透析，并通知透析护士/肾脏科团队"},{"id":"rrp05_a_seizure","en":"Institute seizure precautions and maintain airway/oxygen readiness","zh":"实施癫痫发作预防措施，并准备好气道和氧气支持"}],"correct":["rrp05_a_slow_stop","rrp05_a_seizure"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor/report","zh":"需监测/报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp05_p_exit","en":"Exit-site drainage and skin warmth only","zh":"仅监测出口处渗液和皮肤温度"},{"id":"rrp05_p_stool","en":"Stool color and bowel sounds","zh":"粪便颜色和肠鸣音"},{"id":"rrp05_p_weight","en":"Post-dialysis weight at the next routine check","zh":"下次常规检查时的透析后体重"},{"id":"rrp05_p_neuro","en":"Level of consciousness, headache severity, and seizure activity","zh":"意识水平、头痛严重度和癫痫发作情况"},{"id":"rrp05_p_vitals","en":"Blood pressure and heart rate trends during neurologic symptoms","zh":"神经症状期间的血压和心率趋势"}],"correct":["rrp05_p_neuro","rrp05_p_vitals"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New neurologic symptoms early in a first dialysis treatment for severe uremia point to dialysis disequilibrium syndrome. The priority is to reduce/stop the dialysis stressor per protocol, protect the client from seizure or airway injury, and trend neurologic and hemodynamic status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重尿毒症患者首次透析早期出现新的神经系统症状，指向透析失衡综合征。优先措施是按流程降低或停止透析刺激，防止癫痫或气道损伤，并持续观察神经和血流动力学状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bowtie items, let timing and symptom cluster identify the condition, then pick actions that remove the trigger and protect ABC/safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做蝴蝶结题时，先用时间关系和症状组合判断问题，再选择能去除诱因并保护 ABC/安全的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1935,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.465","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.465.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.465.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,349],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,128],"fullStemEn":"During hemodialysis through a tunneled central catheter, the arterial bloodline cap loosens while the clamp is open. The client suddenly coughs, reports chest tightness and dyspnea, SpO₂ falls to 82%, and blood pressure drops to 84/50 mm Hg. Complete the bowtie by selecting the likely complication, 2 actions, and 2 parameters to monitor or report.","fullStemZh":"患者通过隧道式中心静脉导管进行血液透析时，动脉端血路帽松脱且夹闭器处于打开状态。患者突然咳嗽，诉胸闷和呼吸困难，SpO₂ 降至 82%，血压降至 84/50 mm Hg。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的并发症、2 项处理措施，以及 2 项需要监测或报告的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the likely complication, 2 actions, and 2 parameters to monitor or report.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的并发症、2 项处理措施，以及 2 项需要监测或报告的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client suddenly coughs, reports chest tightness and dyspnea, SpO₂ falls to 82%, and blood pressure drops to 84/50 mm Hg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者突然咳嗽，诉胸闷和呼吸困难，SpO₂ 降至 82%，血压降至 84/50 mm Hg。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Likely complication","zh":"最可能的并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp06_c_dialyzer","en":"Dialyzer hypersensitivity reaction","zh":"透析器超敏反应"},{"id":"rrp06_c_infection","en":"Catheter-related bloodstream infection","zh":"导管相关血流感染"},{"id":"rrp06_c_overload","en":"Pulmonary edema from fluid overload","zh":"容量负荷过多导致的肺水肿"},{"id":"rrp06_c_air","en":"Venous air embolism","zh":"静脉空气栓塞"}],"correct":"rrp06_c_air"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions","zh":"护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp06_a_restart","en":"Restart dialysis at a lower blood-flow rate once the cap is tightened","zh":"拧紧血路帽后以较低血流量重新开始透析"},{"id":"rrp06_a_clamp","en":"Clamp the catheter/bloodline immediately and stop dialysis blood flow","zh":"立即夹闭导管/血路并停止透析血流"},{"id":"rrp06_a_flush","en":"Flush the catheter rapidly with normal saline to clear air","zh":"快速用生理盐水冲管以清除空气"},{"id":"rrp06_a_position_o2","en":"Place in left lateral Trendelenburg position, give high-flow oxygen, and activate emergency response","zh":"置左侧卧头低位，给予高流量氧气，并启动急救反应"},{"id":"rrp06_a_upright","en":"Sit the client upright and encourage coughing until symptoms pass","zh":"让患者坐直并鼓励咳嗽，等待症状缓解"}],"correct":["rrp06_a_clamp","rrp06_a_position_o2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor/report","zh":"需监测/报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp06_p_bruit","en":"Arm access bruit and thrill only","zh":"仅评估手臂通路杂音和震颤"},{"id":"rrp06_p_temp","en":"Temperature trend and catheter-exit drainage","zh":"体温趋势和导管出口渗液"},{"id":"rrp06_p_resp","en":"SpO₂, work of breathing, and breath sounds","zh":"SpO₂、呼吸费力程度和呼吸音"},{"id":"rrp06_p_bun","en":"Post-dialysis BUN only","zh":"仅监测透析后 BUN"},{"id":"rrp06_p_cvneuro","en":"Blood pressure, cardiac rhythm, and new neurologic changes","zh":"血压、心律和新发神经系统变化"}],"correct":["rrp06_p_resp","rrp06_p_cvneuro"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An open catheter/bloodline with abrupt respiratory distress, hypoxemia, and hypotension indicates venous air embolism. Priority actions are to stop further air entry, trap air away from pulmonary outflow as much as possible, oxygenate, and activate emergency help.","rationaleCorrectZh":"导管/血路开放后突然出现呼吸困难、低氧和低血压，提示静脉空气栓塞。优先处理是阻止更多空气进入，尽量让空气滞留在较安全位置，给予氧气并启动急救支援。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A sudden mechanical line problem plus abrupt cardiopulmonary collapse should drive immediate line control and ABC response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"机械性管路问题后突然出现心肺崩溃时，应立即控制管路并按 ABC 处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1936,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_22_b_rrp_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.466","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.466.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.466.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[301,408],"terminalOffsetsZh":[88,131],"fullStemEn":"Eight hours after open reduction and internal fixation of a tibial fracture, the client reports deep lower-leg pain 9/10 despite IV opioid analgesia. Pain increases with passive toe extension, the calf feels tense, and the client reports new tingling in the foot. The dorsalis pedis pulse is present. Complete the bowtie by selecting the likely complication, 2 actions, and 2 parameters to monitor or report.","fullStemZh":"胫骨骨折切开复位内固定术后 8 小时，患者诉小腿深部疼痛 9/10，静脉阿片镇痛后仍未缓解。被动伸展脚趾时疼痛加重，小腿触感紧绷，患者报告足部新发麻刺感。足背动脉搏动仍可触及。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的并发症、2 项处理措施，以及 2 项需要监测或报告的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the likely complication, 2 actions, and 2 parameters to monitor or report.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的并发症、2 项处理措施，以及 2 项需要监测或报告的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The dorsalis pedis pulse is present.","penultimateSentenceZh":"足背动脉搏动仍可触及。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Likely complication","zh":"最可能的并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp07_c_cellulitis","en":"Cellulitis at the incision","zh":"切口蜂窝织炎"},{"id":"rrp07_c_expected","en":"Expected postoperative incisional pain","zh":"预期的术后切口疼痛"},{"id":"rrp07_c_dvt","en":"Deep vein thrombosis","zh":"深静脉血栓"},{"id":"rrp07_c_compartment","en":"Acute compartment syndrome","zh":"急性筋膜室综合征"}],"correct":"rrp07_c_compartment"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions","zh":"护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp07_a_ambulate","en":"Encourage ambulation to improve circulation","zh":"鼓励下床走动以改善循环"},{"id":"rrp07_a_loosen","en":"Loosen or remove restrictive external wraps per protocol and keep the limb at heart level","zh":"按流程松开或去除外部限制性包扎，并将患肢保持在心脏水平"},{"id":"rrp07_a_notify","en":"Notify the orthopedic surgeon/rapid response team and prepare for possible fasciotomy","zh":"通知骨科医师/快速反应团队，并准备可能的筋膜切开减压"},{"id":"rrp07_a_reassess_later","en":"Give another analgesic dose and reassess at the end of the shift","zh":"再给一次镇痛药，并在本班结束时复查"},{"id":"rrp07_a_elevate_ice","en":"Elevate the limb above heart level and apply ice packs tightly","zh":"将患肢抬高于心脏水平并紧贴冰袋"}],"correct":["rrp07_a_loosen","rrp07_a_notify"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor/report","zh":"需监测/报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"rrp07_p_drainage","en":"Amount of serous drainage on the dressing only","zh":"仅记录敷料上的浆液性渗液量"},{"id":"rrp07_p_daily_calf","en":"Calf circumference once daily only","zh":"仅每日测量一次小腿围"},{"id":"rrp07_p_neurovascular","en":"Sensation, movement, capillary refill, color, and temperature of the foot","zh":"足部感觉、运动、毛细血管再充盈、颜色和温度"},{"id":"rrp07_p_bowel","en":"Bowel sounds and oral intake","zh":"肠鸣音和经口摄入量"},{"id":"rrp07_p_pain","en":"Pain with passive stretch and response to analgesia","zh":"被动牵拉痛以及对镇痛药的反应"}],"correct":["rrp07_p_pain","rrp07_p_neurovascular"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pain out of proportion, pain with passive stretch, tense compartment, and paresthesia after tibial fracture repair indicate acute compartment syndrome even when a pulse is still present. Remove external constriction when allowed, keep the limb at heart level, escalate immediately, and trend pain and neurovascular status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胫骨骨折修复术后出现与损伤不相称的疼痛、被动牵拉痛、筋膜室紧绷和麻刺感，即使脉搏仍存在，也提示急性筋膜室综合征。应在流程允许时去除外部压迫，将患肢保持心脏水平，立即升级处理，并连续观察疼痛和神经血管状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let the presence of a pulse falsely reassure you; early compartment syndrome is a pain-and-neurovascular trend problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因仍有脉搏而误以为安全；早期筋膜室综合征重点看疼痛和神经血管趋势。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1937,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.467","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.467.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.467.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[592,612],"terminalOffsetsZh":[208,215],"fullStemEn":"A client with severe malnutrition is started on tube feeding at 60 mL/hr. The facility protocol states that new weakness, paresthesias, edema, or tachycardia with a new drop in phosphorus, potassium, or magnesium after calories are restarted should be treated as possible refeeding syndrome: slow or hold calories and replace electrolytes as prescribed. Twelve hours after feeding starts, the client reports leg weakness and tingling. Heart rate is 118/min, respirations are 24/min, phosphorus is 1.1 mg/dL, potassium is 3.0 mEq/L, magnesium is 1.3 mg/dL, and capillary glucose is 148 mg/dL. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名严重营养不良的患者开始经管饲喂，速度为 60 mL/小时。机构流程规定：重新给予热量后，如果出现新的无力、感觉异常、水肿或心动过速，并伴有磷、钾或镁下降，应按疑似再喂养综合征处理：减慢或暂停热量输入，并按医嘱补充电解质。喂养开始 12 小时后，患者诉双腿无力和麻刺感。心率 118 次/分，呼吸 24 次/分，磷 1.1 mg/dL，钾 3.0 mEq/L，镁 1.3 mg/dL，指尖血糖 148 mg/dL。请完成蝴蝶题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Heart rate is 118/min, respirations are 24/min, phosphorus is 1.1 mg/dL, potassium is 3.0 mEq/L, magnesium is 1.3 mg/dL, and capillary glucose is 148 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"心率 118 次/分，呼吸 24 次/分，磷 1.1 mg/dL，钾 3.0 mEq/L，镁 1.3 mg/dL，指尖血糖 148 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc01_cond_refeeding","en":"Refeeding syndrome","zh":"再喂养综合征"},{"id":"bcc01_cond_fluid_overload","en":"Fluid volume overload","zh":"体液容量过多"},{"id":"bcc01_cond_anxiety","en":"Anxiety response to tube feeding","zh":"对管饲的焦虑反应"},{"id":"bcc01_cond_hyperglycemia","en":"Hyperglycemia from nutrition support","zh":"营养支持导致的高血糖"}],"correct":"bcc01_cond_refeeding"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions to take","zh":"应采取的护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc01_act_replace_electrolytes","en":"Administer prescribed phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium replacement","zh":"按医嘱补充磷、钾和镁"},{"id":"bcc01_act_insulin_bolus","en":"Request rapid-acting insulin as the priority intervention","zh":"把申请速效胰岛素作为优先处理"},{"id":"bcc01_act_slow_calories","en":"Slow or hold the feeding per protocol and notify the provider","zh":"按流程减慢或暂停喂养，并通知医务人员"},{"id":"bcc01_act_advance_goal","en":"Advance the tube feeding to the goal rate to improve nutrition","zh":"将管饲加快到目标速度以改善营养"},{"id":"bcc01_act_restrict_fluids","en":"Restrict oral fluids for suspected volume overload","zh":"因疑似容量过多而限制口服液体"}],"correct":["bcc01_act_slow_calories","bcc01_act_replace_electrolytes"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc01_param_neuromuscular","en":"Heart rhythm, respiratory effort, weakness, and paresthesias","zh":"心律、呼吸费力程度、无力和感觉异常"},{"id":"bcc01_param_electrolytes","en":"Serial phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium levels","zh":"连续监测磷、钾、镁水平"},{"id":"bcc01_param_wound","en":"Daily wound drainage color only","zh":"仅每日伤口引流液颜色"},{"id":"bcc01_param_guaiac","en":"Stool guaiac result before each feeding","zh":"每次喂养前的大便隐血结果"}],"correct":["bcc01_param_electrolytes","bcc01_param_neuromuscular"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The electrolyte pattern after calories are restarted, plus neuromuscular symptoms and tachycardia, fits refeeding syndrome. The safest nursing response is to slow or hold calorie delivery according to the stated protocol, notify the provider, replace electrolytes as prescribed, and trend cardiopulmonary and neuromuscular status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重新给予热量后出现低磷、低钾、低镁，并伴神经肌肉症状和心动过速，符合再喂养综合征。最安全的护理处理是按题干流程减慢或暂停热量输入、通知医务人员、按医嘱补充电解质，并连续评估心肺和神经肌肉状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When feeding starts after starvation, connect new weakness or paresthesias with low phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium before focusing on glucose alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"饥饿后重新开始营养时，看到新的无力或感觉异常，要先联想到低磷、低钾、低镁，不要只盯着血糖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1938,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.468","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.468.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.468.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,446],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,158],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews a client receiving continuous enteral feeding and TPN. Select the charted cues that require nursing action under this unit policy: TPN tubing and filter are changed every 24 hours; TPN uses a dedicated central line lumen; the provider is notified for capillary glucose greater than 300 mg/dL; enteral feeding is held and the provider is notified for residual 500 mL or greater or for residual with vomiting or severe distention.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名正在接受连续肠内营养和 TPN 的患者记录。根据本单元流程，选择需要护理处理的记录线索：TPN 管路和过滤器每 24 小时更换一次；TPN 使用专用中心静脉管腔；指尖血糖大于 300 mg/dL 需通知医务人员；胃残余量达到或超过 500 mL，或残余量伴呕吐、严重腹胀时，应暂停肠内营养并通知医务人员。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the charted cues that require nursing action under this unit policy: TPN tubing and filter are changed every 24 hours; TPN uses a dedicated central line lumen; the provider is notified for capillary glucose greater than 300 mg/dL; enteral feeding is held and the provider is notified for residual 500 mL or greater or for residual with vomiting or severe distention.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据本单元流程，选择需要护理处理的记录线索：TPN 管路和过滤器每 24 小时更换一次；TPN 使用专用中心静脉管腔；指尖血糖大于 300 mg/dL 需通知医务人员；胃残余量达到或超过 500 mL，或残余量伴呕吐、严重腹胀时，应暂停肠内营养并通知医务人员。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews a client receiving continuous enteral feeding and TPN.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名正在接受连续肠内营养和 TPN 的患者记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"bcc02_s1","en":"0800 nutrition-safety note:","zh":"0800 营养安全记录："},{"id":"bcc02_s2","en":"TPN is infusing through a right subclavian central venous catheter with a dedicated lumen.","zh":"TPN 正通过右锁骨下中心静脉导管的专用管腔输注。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc02_s3","en":"The TPN bag, tubing, and filter are labeled as hung at 0130 yesterday.","zh":"TPN 袋、管路和过滤器标签显示为昨天 0130 悬挂。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc02_s4","en":"Capillary glucose is 328 mg/dL.","zh":"指尖血糖为 328 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc02_s5","en":"Gastric residual is 120 mL; the client denies nausea and the abdomen is soft.","zh":"胃残余量 120 mL；患者否认恶心，腹部柔软。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc02_s6","en":"The enteral tube is connected to wall suction while the feeding pump continues to run.","zh":"肠内营养管连接墙式负压吸引，同时喂养泵仍在运行。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc02_s7","en":"Head of bed is elevated 35 degrees during the feeding.","zh":"喂养期间床头抬高 35 度。","selectable":true}],"correct":["bcc02_s3","bcc02_s4","bcc02_s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The overdue TPN setup, glucose above the stated notification threshold, and concurrent suction with the feeding pump running all require action. Dedicated central access, a small asymptomatic residual, and head-of-bed elevation are appropriate findings in this stem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"TPN 管路超过更换时限、血糖超过题干规定的通知阈值，以及喂养泵运行时同时连接负压吸引，均需要处理。专用中心静脉通路、少量且无症状的胃残余量、喂养时床头抬高，都是本题中的恰当发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the policy numbers in the stem rather than a memorized residual cutoff, then separate unsafe equipment setup from expected aspiration precautions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干给出的流程数字，而不是死记胃残余量标准；再把不安全设备设置和预防误吸的正确措施区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1939,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.469","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.469.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.469.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[463,483],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,123],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with abdominal pain has increasing cramping, abdominal distention, nausea, and repeated emesis with a fecal odor. The client reports no stool or flatus for 2 days. Bowel sounds are high-pitched and frequent. The unit guideline states that suspected mechanical bowel obstruction is managed by keeping the client NPO, notifying the provider, preparing for prescribed decompression, and avoiding laxatives or enemas until obstruction is ruled out. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名因腹痛入院的患者出现逐渐加重的绞痛、腹胀、恶心，并反复呕吐带粪臭味的内容物。患者诉 2 天无排便、无排气。肠鸣音高调且频繁。单元指南规定：疑似机械性肠梗阻时应禁食、通知医务人员、准备按医嘱减压，并在排除梗阻前避免使用泻药或灌肠。请完成蝴蝶题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit guideline states that suspected mechanical bowel obstruction is managed by keeping the client NPO, notifying the provider, preparing for prescribed decompression, and avoiding laxatives or enemas until obstruction is ruled out.","penultimateSentenceZh":"单元指南规定：疑似机械性肠梗阻时应禁食、通知医务人员、准备按医嘱减压，并在排除梗阻前避免使用泻药或灌肠。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc03_cond_ileus","en":"Paralytic ileus","zh":"麻痹性肠梗阻"},{"id":"bcc03_cond_gastroenteritis","en":"Viral gastroenteritis","zh":"病毒性胃肠炎"},{"id":"bcc03_cond_constipation","en":"Uncomplicated constipation","zh":"单纯便秘"},{"id":"bcc03_cond_obstruction","en":"Mechanical bowel obstruction","zh":"机械性肠梗阻"}],"correct":"bcc03_cond_obstruction"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions to take","zh":"应采取的护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc03_act_enema","en":"Give a cleansing enema before calling the provider","zh":"先给予清洁灌肠再通知医务人员"},{"id":"bcc03_act_high_fiber","en":"Start a high-fiber meal tray","zh":"开始高纤维饮食餐盘"},{"id":"bcc03_act_laxative","en":"Administer a stimulant laxative for constipation","zh":"给予刺激性泻药处理便秘"},{"id":"bcc03_act_npo","en":"Keep the client NPO and notify the provider","zh":"让患者禁食并通知医务人员"},{"id":"bcc03_act_decompression","en":"Prepare for prescribed nasogastric decompression","zh":"准备按医嘱进行鼻胃管减压"}],"correct":["bcc03_act_npo","bcc03_act_decompression"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc03_param_abdomen","en":"Pain pattern, abdominal distention, and bowel sounds","zh":"疼痛模式、腹胀程度和肠鸣音"},{"id":"bcc03_param_emesis","en":"Emesis amount, character, and intake/output balance","zh":"呕吐量、性质以及出入量平衡"},{"id":"bcc03_param_stool_color","en":"Routine stool color after regular meals","zh":"常规进餐后的大便颜色"},{"id":"bcc03_param_sleep","en":"Hours of sleep during the previous night","zh":"前一晚睡眠小时数"}],"correct":["bcc03_param_abdomen","bcc03_param_emesis"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cramping pain, distention, feculent emesis, absent stool and flatus, and high-pitched bowel sounds point to mechanical bowel obstruction. The stated guideline supports NPO status, provider notification, and preparation for decompression while avoiding laxatives, enemas, and high-fiber intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"绞痛、腹胀、粪臭样呕吐、无排便排气以及高调肠鸣音提示机械性肠梗阻。题干指南支持禁食、通知医务人员、准备减压，同时避免泻药、灌肠和高纤维摄入。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Feculent emesis plus no flatus is a red flag for obstruction; avoid constipation treatments that push contents against a blockage.","testTakingStrategyZh":"粪臭样呕吐加无排气是梗阻危险信号；避免使用会把肠内容物推向阻塞处的便秘处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1940,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.470","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.470.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.470.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[45,387],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,112],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews urinary-elimination notes. Select the cues that require intervention under this unit policy: assess for urinary retention if the client voids less than 100 mL with suprapubic discomfort; notify the provider or perform ordered straight catheterization for bladder-scan volume greater than 400 mL; maintain a closed, unobstructed drainage system for indwelling catheters.","fullStemZh":"护士查看排尿相关记录。根据本单元流程，选择需要干预的线索：如果患者排尿少于 100 mL 且有耻骨上不适，应评估尿潴留；膀胱扫描量大于 400 mL 时，通知医务人员或按医嘱行一次性导尿；留置尿管应保持密闭且通畅的引流系统。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the cues that require intervention under this unit policy: assess for urinary retention if the client voids less than 100 mL with suprapubic discomfort; notify the provider or perform ordered straight catheterization for bladder-scan volume greater than 400 mL; maintain a closed, unobstructed drainage system for indwelling catheters.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据本单元流程，选择需要干预的线索：如果患者排尿少于 100 mL 且有耻骨上不适，应评估尿潴留；膀胱扫描量大于 400 mL 时，通知医务人员或按医嘱行一次性导尿；留置尿管应保持密闭且通畅的引流系统。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews urinary-elimination notes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看排尿相关记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"bcc04_s1","en":"Postoperative urinary note:","zh":"术后排尿记录："},{"id":"bcc04_s2","en":"Six hours after epidural removal, the client voided 60 mL and reports lower abdominal pressure.","zh":"硬膜外导管移除 6 小时后，患者排尿 60 mL，并诉下腹部压迫感。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc04_s3","en":"Bladder scan shows 640 mL.","zh":"膀胱扫描显示 640 mL。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc04_s4","en":"The Foley drainage bag is below bladder level and is not touching the floor.","zh":"Foley 引流袋低于膀胱水平，且未接触地面。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc04_s5","en":"Indwelling catheter tubing has a dependent loop filled with urine, and no urine has reached the bag for 3 hours.","zh":"留置尿管管路有一个充满尿液的低垂环，3 小时内无尿液流入引流袋。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc04_s6","en":"Urine in the bag is pale yellow, 45 mL/hr, with no visible blood clots.","zh":"引流袋内尿液淡黄色，45 mL/小时，无可见血块。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc04_s7","en":"The catheter bag was emptied using a clean container without touching the drainage spout.","zh":"使用清洁容器清空引流袋，且未接触引流口。","selectable":true}],"correct":["bcc04_s2","bcc04_s3","bcc04_s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Low-volume voiding with suprapubic pressure, a bladder-scan volume above the stated threshold, and obstructed catheter tubing require intervention. A dependent drainage bag with adequate output and aseptic emptying are appropriate catheter-care findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"少量排尿伴耻骨上压迫感、膀胱扫描量超过题干阈值，以及尿管管路受阻都需要干预。引流袋位置合适、尿量充足以及清空时保持清洁，属于恰当的尿管护理发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pair symptoms with the unit threshold. Catheter tubing problems matter when urine cannot drain by gravity into the bag.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把症状和题干阈值对应起来。尿管问题的关键是尿液是否能靠重力顺畅流入引流袋。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1941,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.471","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.471.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.471.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[507,527],"terminalOffsetsZh":[143,150],"fullStemEn":"A client has been on bedrest for 4 days after a pelvic fracture. The client suddenly reports sharp chest pain with inspiration and shortness of breath. Oxygen saturation is 88% on room air, heart rate is 124/min, and the right calf is warm, tender, and 3 cm larger than the left calf. The unit protocol states that suspected pulmonary embolism requires oxygen, upright positioning as tolerated, rapid provider or rapid-response notification, and no massage or ambulation of the painful leg until evaluated. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名骨盆骨折患者已卧床 4 天。患者突然诉吸气时尖锐胸痛和气短。室内空气下血氧饱和度 88%，心率 124 次/分，右小腿发热、压痛，周径比左侧大 3 cm。单元流程规定：疑似肺栓塞时应给氧、在可耐受范围内取直立位、迅速通知医务人员或启动快速反应，并在评估前不要按摩或让疼痛腿下床活动。请完成蝴蝶题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit protocol states that suspected pulmonary embolism requires oxygen, upright positioning as tolerated, rapid provider or rapid-response notification, and no massage or ambulation of the painful leg until evaluated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"单元流程规定：疑似肺栓塞时应给氧、在可耐受范围内取直立位、迅速通知医务人员或启动快速反应，并在评估前不要按摩或让疼痛腿下床活动。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc05_cond_pneumonia","en":"Hospital-acquired pneumonia","zh":"医院获得性肺炎"},{"id":"bcc05_cond_muscle","en":"Musculoskeletal chest wall pain","zh":"肌肉骨骼性胸壁痛"},{"id":"bcc05_cond_pe","en":"Pulmonary embolism from venous thromboembolism","zh":"静脉血栓栓塞导致的肺栓塞"},{"id":"bcc05_cond_panic","en":"Panic attack related to hospitalization","zh":"住院相关惊恐发作"}],"correct":"bcc05_cond_pe"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions to take","zh":"应采取的护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc05_act_massage","en":"Massage the swollen calf to reduce tenderness","zh":"按摩肿胀小腿以减轻压痛"},{"id":"bcc05_act_ambulate","en":"Ambulate the client to relieve venous stasis","zh":"让患者下床行走以缓解静脉淤滞"},{"id":"bcc05_act_reassure","en":"Use reassurance alone and recheck in 1 hour","zh":"仅给予安慰并 1 小时后复查"},{"id":"bcc05_act_notify","en":"Activate rapid response or notify the provider immediately","zh":"立即启动快速反应或通知医务人员"},{"id":"bcc05_act_oxygen","en":"Apply oxygen and position upright as tolerated","zh":"给氧，并在可耐受范围内取直立位"}],"correct":["bcc05_act_oxygen","bcc05_act_notify"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc05_param_resp","en":"Oxygen saturation, respiratory effort, and chest pain","zh":"血氧饱和度、呼吸费力程度和胸痛"},{"id":"bcc05_param_appetite","en":"Meal intake percentage at the next tray","zh":"下一餐摄入百分比"},{"id":"bcc05_param_bowel","en":"Bowel movement color and consistency","zh":"排便颜色和性状"},{"id":"bcc05_param_leg","en":"Calf size, warmth, tenderness, and neurovascular status","zh":"小腿周径、温度、压痛和神经血管状态"}],"correct":["bcc05_param_resp","bcc05_param_leg"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden pleuritic chest pain, hypoxemia, tachycardia, and unilateral warm calf swelling after immobility are most consistent with pulmonary embolism from venous thromboembolism. Immediate nursing priorities are oxygenation, upright positioning, escalation, and monitoring respiratory and limb findings without massaging or ambulating the affected leg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"长期卧床后突然出现胸膜性胸痛、低氧、心动过速和单侧小腿发热肿胀，最符合静脉血栓栓塞导致的肺栓塞。护理优先事项是改善氧合、直立位、升级求助，并监测呼吸和肢体情况，避免按摩或让患肢活动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Immobility plus unilateral calf changes plus sudden hypoxemia should trigger VTE/PE thinking before anxiety or muscle pain.","testTakingStrategyZh":"卧床不动、单侧小腿改变和突发低氧同时出现时，应先考虑 VTE/PE，而不是焦虑或肌肉痛。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1942,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.472","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.472.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.472.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[99,191],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,53],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews an immobility-risk assessment for a client who has been on bedrest for 72 hours. Select the cues that require follow-up because they may indicate an immobility complication.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名已卧床 72 小时患者的制动风险评估。选择需要跟进的线索，因为这些线索可能提示制动相关并发症。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the cues that require follow-up because they may indicate an immobility complication.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择需要跟进的线索，因为这些线索可能提示制动相关并发症。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews an immobility-risk assessment for a client who has been on bedrest for 72 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名已卧床 72 小时患者的制动风险评估。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"bcc06_s1","en":"Bedrest day 3 assessment:","zh":"卧床第 3 天评估："},{"id":"bcc06_s2","en":"Sacrum has a 3 cm area of nonblanchable redness.","zh":"骶尾部有 3 cm 不褪色红斑。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc06_s3","en":"The client uses the incentive spirometer 10 times each hour while awake.","zh":"患者清醒时每小时使用激励性肺量计 10 次。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc06_s4","en":"Fine crackles are heard at both lung bases, and temperature is 100.6 °F (38.1 °C).","zh":"双肺底可闻细湿啰音，体温 100.6 °F (38.1 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc06_s5","en":"Both heels are floated off the mattress with pillows.","zh":"双足跟用枕头垫起，离开床垫。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc06_s6","en":"Right calf is warm and 2.5 cm larger than the left calf.","zh":"右小腿温热，周径比左侧大 2.5 cm。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc06_s7","en":"Repositioning is documented at least every 2 hours.","zh":"记录显示至少每 2 小时翻身一次。","selectable":true}],"correct":["bcc06_s2","bcc06_s4","bcc06_s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nonblanchable sacral redness suggests pressure injury, crackles with fever may indicate atelectasis or pneumonia, and unilateral warm calf enlargement suggests DVT. Incentive spirometry, heel off-loading, and scheduled repositioning are protective interventions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"骶尾部不褪色红斑提示压力性损伤；湿啰音伴发热可能提示肺不张或肺炎；单侧小腿温热增粗提示 DVT。激励性肺量计、足跟减压和定时翻身是保护性措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For immobility items, sort findings into complications of pressure, lungs, and venous stasis versus interventions that prevent those complications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到制动题，把发现分为压力、肺部、静脉淤滞并发症，以及预防这些并发症的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1943,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.473","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.473.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.473.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,374],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,113],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews a sleep-rest note for a hospitalized adult. Select the findings that require follow-up under this unit policy: hold a bedtime sedative and notify the provider if respiratory rate is below 12/min, the client is difficult to arouse, or an opioid was administered within the previous 2 hours; address sleep-hygiene factors that interfere with nighttime sleep.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名住院成人的睡眠休息记录。根据本单元流程，选择需要跟进的发现：如果呼吸频率低于 12 次/分、患者难以唤醒，或过去 2 小时内已给予阿片类药物，应暂停睡前镇静催眠药并通知医务人员；同时处理影响夜间睡眠的睡眠卫生因素。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the findings that require follow-up under this unit policy: hold a bedtime sedative and notify the provider if respiratory rate is below 12/min, the client is difficult to arouse, or an opioid was administered within the previous 2 hours; address sleep-hygiene factors that interfere with nighttime sleep.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据本单元流程，选择需要跟进的发现：如果呼吸频率低于 12 次/分、患者难以唤醒，或过去 2 小时内已给予阿片类药物，应暂停睡前镇静催眠药并通知医务人员；同时处理影响夜间睡眠的睡眠卫生因素。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews a sleep-rest note for a hospitalized adult.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名住院成人的睡眠休息记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"bcc07_s1","en":"2230 sleep note:","zh":"2230 睡眠记录："},{"id":"bcc07_s2","en":"The client received oxycodone 10 mg at 2130 and requests zolpidem now.","zh":"患者 2130 已服用羟考酮 10 mg，现在要求服用唑吡坦。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc07_s3","en":"Respiratory rate is 10/min, and the client opens eyes only after repeated verbal stimulation.","zh":"呼吸频率 10 次/分，患者需反复言语刺激才睁眼。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc07_s4","en":"The room lights are dimmed and noise is reduced after 2200.","zh":"2200 后病房调暗灯光并减少噪音。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc07_s5","en":"The client reports drinking two large coffees with dinner to stay awake for visitors.","zh":"患者说晚餐时喝了两大杯咖啡，以便等访客时保持清醒。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc07_s6","en":"Call light is within reach and nonskid socks are on before sleep.","zh":"睡前呼叫铃在手边，并穿着防滑袜。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc07_s7","en":"The client plans to walk to the bathroom without assistance after taking a sleep medication.","zh":"患者计划服用睡眠药后无人协助自行走去厕所。","selectable":true}],"correct":["bcc07_s2","bcc07_s3","bcc07_s5","bcc07_s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Recent opioid use, respiratory depression with decreased arousability, evening caffeine, and an unassisted bathroom plan after a sedative all need follow-up. Reduced nighttime stimulation and fall-prevention setup are appropriate sleep-rest supports.","rationaleCorrectZh":"近期使用阿片类药物、呼吸抑制且唤醒困难、晚间摄入咖啡因，以及服用催眠药后打算无人协助去厕所，都需要跟进。夜间减少刺激和做好防跌倒准备是恰当的睡眠休息支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Sleep-rest questions often hide safety cues inside comfort requests; check sedation, opioids, breathing, arousability, and fall risk before giving a sleep medication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"睡眠休息题常把安全线索藏在舒适需求中；给催眠药前先看镇静程度、阿片用药、呼吸、唤醒反应和跌倒风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1944,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.474","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.474.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.474.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[465,485],"terminalOffsetsZh":[147,154],"fullStemEn":"A client reports sleeping 8 hours but waking with morning headaches and feeling sleepy during the day. The partner reports loud snoring and repeated pauses in breathing followed by gasping. Body mass index is 36 kg/m², blood pressure is 154/92 mm Hg, and oxygen saturation drops to 86% during observed sleep. The provider's order set allows the nurse to apply prescribed CPAP at night and avoid sedating sleep medications when obstructive sleep apnea is suspected. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者说自己睡了 8 小时，但早晨醒来头痛，白天嗜睡。伴侣描述患者鼾声很大，反复出现呼吸暂停后又喘气。BMI 为 36 kg/m²，血压 154/92 mm Hg，观察睡眠时血氧饱和度降至 86%。医嘱集允许护士在疑似阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停时夜间使用已开立的 CPAP，并避免使用镇静性睡眠药物。请完成蝴蝶题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider's order set allows the nurse to apply prescribed CPAP at night and avoid sedating sleep medications when obstructive sleep apnea is suspected.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱集允许护士在疑似阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停时夜间使用已开立的 CPAP，并避免使用镇静性睡眠药物。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc08_cond_narcolepsy","en":"Narcolepsy","zh":"发作性睡病"},{"id":"bcc08_cond_osa","en":"Obstructive sleep apnea","zh":"阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停"},{"id":"bcc08_cond_central","en":"Central sleep apnea","zh":"中枢性睡眠呼吸暂停"},{"id":"bcc08_cond_insomnia","en":"Primary insomnia","zh":"原发性失眠"}],"correct":"bcc08_cond_osa"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions to take","zh":"应采取的护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc08_act_cpap","en":"Apply the prescribed CPAP during sleep","zh":"睡眠时使用已开立的 CPAP"},{"id":"bcc08_act_sedative","en":"Administer a sedating sleep medication to deepen sleep","zh":"给予镇静性睡眠药物以加深睡眠"},{"id":"bcc08_act_flat","en":"Keep the client flat to promote airway alignment","zh":"让患者平卧以促进气道对齐"},{"id":"bcc08_act_alcohol","en":"Suggest alcohol near bedtime to reduce awakenings","zh":"建议睡前饮酒以减少觉醒"},{"id":"bcc08_act_position","en":"Elevate the head of bed and encourage side-lying sleep","zh":"抬高床头并鼓励侧卧睡眠"}],"correct":["bcc08_act_cpap","bcc08_act_position"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc08_param_appetite","en":"Preference for bedtime snacks","zh":"睡前点心偏好"},{"id":"bcc08_param_daytime","en":"Morning headache, daytime sleepiness, and CPAP tolerance","zh":"晨起头痛、白天嗜睡和 CPAP 耐受情况"},{"id":"bcc08_param_oxygen","en":"Nocturnal oxygen saturation, snoring, apneic pauses, and gasping","zh":"夜间血氧饱和度、鼾声、呼吸暂停和喘气"},{"id":"bcc08_param_urine","en":"Urine color after breakfast","zh":"早餐后尿液颜色"}],"correct":["bcc08_param_oxygen","bcc08_param_daytime"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Loud snoring, witnessed apneic pauses with gasping, obesity, morning headaches, daytime sleepiness, hypertension, and nocturnal desaturation fit obstructive sleep apnea. CPAP and positioning support airway patency, while sedatives, alcohol, and flat positioning can worsen obstruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"大声打鼾、目击呼吸暂停后喘气、肥胖、晨起头痛、白天嗜睡、高血压和夜间低氧，符合阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停。CPAP 和体位调整有助于保持气道通畅；镇静药、酒精和平卧可能加重阻塞。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Witnessed pauses with gasping and snoring point to obstructive apnea; avoid answers that deepen sedation or relax the airway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"目击呼吸暂停后喘气并伴打鼾，指向阻塞性呼吸暂停；避免选择会加深镇静或放松气道的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1945,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.475","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.475.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.475.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[729,749],"terminalOffsetsZh":[222,229],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving palliative care for metastatic cancer has been taking oral morphine every 4 hours for several days. Pain is 2/10, but the family reports new confusion and seeing insects on the wall. The nurse observes intermittent arm myoclonus, pinpoint pupils, and increased sleepiness. Respiratory rate is 12/min and oxygen saturation is 93% on 2 L/min nasal cannula. The palliative-care protocol states that new hallucinations, myoclonus, or excessive sedation in a client receiving opioids should be reported as possible opioid-induced neurotoxicity or over-sedation; the nurse should hold the next opioid dose pending provider direction if sedation is unsafe, implement safety measures, and continue symptom assessment. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名转移性癌症姑息治疗患者已连续数天每 4 小时口服吗啡。疼痛 2/10，但家属报告患者新出现意识混乱，并说墙上有虫子。护士观察到间歇性上肢肌阵挛、针尖样瞳孔和嗜睡加重。呼吸频率 12 次/分，经鼻导管 2 L/分吸氧时血氧饱和度 93%。姑息治疗流程规定：使用阿片类药物的患者若新出现幻觉、肌阵挛或过度镇静，应按疑似阿片诱导性神经毒性或过度镇静上报；如镇静不安全，护士应在等待医务人员指示期间暂停下一次阿片剂量、采取安全措施，并继续评估症状。请完成蝴蝶题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The palliative-care protocol states that new hallucinations, myoclonus, or excessive sedation in a client receiving opioids should be reported as possible opioid-induced neurotoxicity or over-sedation; the nurse should hold the next opioid dose pending provider direction if sedation is unsafe, implement safety measures, and continue symptom assessment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"姑息治疗流程规定：使用阿片类药物的患者若新出现幻觉、肌阵挛或过度镇静，应按疑似阿片诱导性神经毒性或过度镇静上报；如镇静不安全，护士应在等待医务人员指示期间暂停下一次阿片剂量、采取安全措施，并继续评估症状。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc09_cond_opioid_neurotox","en":"Opioid-induced neurotoxicity or over-sedation","zh":"阿片诱导性神经毒性或过度镇静"},{"id":"bcc09_cond_anxiety","en":"Anxiety related to end-of-life care","zh":"临终照护相关焦虑"},{"id":"bcc09_cond_terminal","en":"Expected terminal disease progression only","zh":"仅为预期的终末期疾病进展"},{"id":"bcc09_cond_uncontrolled_pain","en":"Uncontrolled cancer pain","zh":"癌痛控制不佳"}],"correct":"bcc09_cond_opioid_neurotox"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions to take","zh":"应采取的护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc09_act_safety_assess","en":"Institute safety precautions and perform focused sedation, pain, and respiratory assessment","zh":"采取安全预防措施，并重点评估镇静、疼痛和呼吸"},{"id":"bcc09_act_extra_morphine","en":"Give an extra morphine dose for hallucination-related agitation","zh":"因幻觉相关躁动而额外给予吗啡"},{"id":"bcc09_act_ignore","en":"Document the changes as expected and wait until the next routine round","zh":"将变化记录为预期表现，并等到下一次常规查房"},{"id":"bcc09_act_hold_notify","en":"Hold the next opioid dose if sedation remains unsafe and notify the provider","zh":"若镇静仍不安全，暂停下一次阿片剂量并通知医务人员"},{"id":"bcc09_act_restrain","en":"Apply restraints without additional assessment","zh":"不进一步评估，直接约束患者"}],"correct":["bcc09_act_hold_notify","bcc09_act_safety_assess"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"bcc09_param_weight","en":"Weekly weight trend only","zh":"仅每周体重趋势"},{"id":"bcc09_param_sed_resp","en":"Respiratory rate, oxygen saturation, sedation level, and arousability","zh":"呼吸频率、血氧饱和度、镇静程度和可唤醒程度"},{"id":"bcc09_param_appetite","en":"Food preferences for the next meal","zh":"下一餐食物偏好"},{"id":"bcc09_param_neuro_pain","en":"Hallucinations, myoclonus, confusion, and pain score","zh":"幻觉、肌阵挛、意识混乱和疼痛评分"}],"correct":["bcc09_param_sed_resp","bcc09_param_neuro_pain"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New hallucinations, myoclonus, pinpoint pupils, and increased sleepiness in a client receiving scheduled morphine fit opioid-induced neurotoxicity or over-sedation. Because the pain is controlled, giving more morphine would be unsafe. The nurse should escalate, protect the client from injury, and monitor sedation, respirations, neurologic symptoms, and pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"按时使用吗啡的患者新出现幻觉、肌阵挛、针尖样瞳孔和嗜睡加重，符合阿片诱导性神经毒性或过度镇静。由于疼痛已控制，继续加给吗啡不安全。护士应升级处理、保护患者避免受伤，并监测镇静、呼吸、神经症状和疼痛。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In palliative care, comfort remains the goal, but new opioid toxicity signs still require assessment and dose-safety escalation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"姑息治疗仍以舒适为目标，但新的阿片毒性征象仍需要评估和剂量安全升级处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1946,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bcc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.476","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.476.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.476.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,260],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,74],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews a palliative-care plan for a client with advanced heart failure who has chosen comfort-focused treatment. Select the cues that require follow-up because they show uncontrolled symptoms or a mismatch with the client's documented goals of care.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名晚期心力衰竭患者的姑息照护计划；患者已选择以舒适为重点的治疗。选择需要跟进的线索，因为它们提示症状控制不佳或与患者记录的照护目标不一致。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the cues that require follow-up because they show uncontrolled symptoms or a mismatch with the client's documented goals of care.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择需要跟进的线索，因为它们提示症状控制不佳或与患者记录的照护目标不一致。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews a palliative-care plan for a client with advanced heart failure who has chosen comfort-focused treatment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名晚期心力衰竭患者的姑息照护计划；患者已选择以舒适为重点的治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"bcc10_s1","en":"Palliative-care interdisciplinary note:","zh":"姑息照护多学科记录："},{"id":"bcc10_s2","en":"The signed goals-of-care form states: comfort-focused treatment; do-not-resuscitate; avoid ICU transfer unless needed for comfort.","zh":"已签署的照护目标表写明：以舒适为重点；不实施复苏；除非为了舒适，否则避免转入 ICU。"},{"id":"bcc10_s3","en":"The family requests intubation and ICU transfer if breathing worsens, saying, 'Do everything, even if he said no machines.'","zh":"家属要求若呼吸恶化就插管并转 ICU，并说：“什么都要做，即使他说过不要机器。”","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc10_s4","en":"The client reports dyspnea 8/10 and uses accessory muscles; ordered PRN morphine for dyspnea has not been offered because the nurse is worried about addiction.","zh":"患者诉呼吸困难 8/10，并使用辅助呼吸肌；医嘱中用于呼吸困难的 PRN 吗啡未被提供，因为护士担心成瘾。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc10_s5","en":"Mouth care, sips of water, and ice chips relieve the client's dry mouth.","zh":"口腔护理、少量饮水和冰片缓解了患者口干。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc10_s6","en":"Pain remains 7/10 one hour after the prescribed rescue analgesic, and the client is grimacing.","zh":"按医嘱给予抢救性镇痛药 1 小时后，疼痛仍为 7/10，患者表情痛苦。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc10_s7","en":"The chaplain visit requested by the client is scheduled for this afternoon.","zh":"患者要求的牧灵/灵性关怀探访已安排在今天下午。","selectable":true},{"id":"bcc10_s8","en":"Nausea is 7/10 with two vomiting episodes, and no rescue antiemetic has been requested yet.","zh":"恶心 7/10，并有两次呕吐，目前尚未申请或给予抢救性止吐药。","selectable":true}],"correct":["bcc10_s3","bcc10_s4","bcc10_s6","bcc10_s8"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A family request that conflicts with the documented comfort-focused plan requires clarification and advocacy. Severe dyspnea without appropriate PRN treatment, persistent pain after rescue medication, and uncontrolled nausea/vomiting all require symptom-management follow-up. Mouth care that helps and an arranged chaplain visit support the client's goals.","rationaleCorrectZh":"家属要求与记录中的舒适导向计划冲突，需要澄清并为患者目标发声。严重呼吸困难却未按医嘱给予 PRN 处理、抢救镇痛后疼痛仍明显、恶心呕吐未控制，都需要症状管理跟进。有效的口腔护理和已安排的灵性关怀探访符合患者目标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In palliative-care items, do not equate comfort-focused care with doing nothing; uncontrolled symptoms and goal conflicts are active nursing priorities.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在姑息照护题中，不要把舒适导向理解为“不处理”；症状未控制和目标冲突都是主动护理优先事项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1947,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.477","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.477.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.477.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[270,290],"terminalOffsetsZh":[135,145],"fullStemEn":"A client with a COPD exacerbation becomes increasingly drowsy. The item protocol says pH < 7.30 with a rising PaCO₂ and worsening mental status requires urgent respiratory escalation. ABG: pH 7.28, PaCO₂ 62 mm Hg, HCO₃⁻ 29 mEq/L, PaO₂ 58 mm Hg on 2 L/min nasal cannula. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名 COPD 急性加重患者逐渐嗜睡。本题流程规定：pH < 7.30、PaCO₂ 升高且意识状态变差时，需要紧急呼吸支持升级。动脉血气：pH 7.28，PaCO₂ 62 mm Hg，HCO₃⁻ 29 mEq/L，鼻导管 2 L/min 时 PaO₂ 58 mm Hg。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"ABG: pH 7.28, PaCO₂ 62 mm Hg, HCO₃⁻ 29 mEq/L, PaO₂ 58 mm Hg on 2 L/min nasal cannula.","penultimateSentenceZh":"动脉血气：pH 7.28，PaCO₂ 62 mm Hg，HCO₃⁻ 29 mEq/L，鼻导管 2 L/min 时 PaO₂ 58 mm Hg。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q01_c_met_acidosis_comp","en":"Metabolic acidosis with respiratory compensation","zh":"代谢性酸中毒伴呼吸代偿"},{"id":"q01_c_met_alkalosis","en":"Metabolic alkalosis","zh":"代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"q01_c_resp_acidosis","en":"Acute respiratory acidosis","zh":"急性呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"q01_c_resp_alkalosis","en":"Respiratory alkalosis","zh":"呼吸性碱中毒"}],"correct":"q01_c_resp_acidosis"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q01_a_bicarb","en":"Give sodium bicarbonate for all low pH results","zh":"对所有低 pH 结果给予碳酸氢钠"},{"id":"q01_a_airway_assess","en":"Assess airway, breath sounds, respiratory effort, and level of consciousness","zh":"评估气道、呼吸音、呼吸功和意识水平"},{"id":"q01_a_escalate_vent","en":"Notify the provider/rapid response and prepare noninvasive ventilation per protocol","zh":"通知医务人员/快速反应团队，并按流程准备无创通气"},{"id":"q01_a_sedative","en":"Administer a sedative for anxiety before reassessment","zh":"复查前先给予镇静药缓解焦虑"},{"id":"q01_a_paper_bag","en":"Have the client breathe into a paper bag","zh":"让患者对着纸袋呼吸"}],"correct":["q01_a_airway_assess","q01_a_escalate_vent"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q01_p_pt_inr","en":"PT/INR and platelet count","zh":"PT/INR 和血小板计数"},{"id":"q01_p_lipase","en":"Serum lipase and abdominal pain score","zh":"血清脂肪酶和腹痛评分"},{"id":"q01_p_abg","en":"Repeat ABG trend, especially pH and PaCO₂","zh":"复查动脉血气趋势，尤其是 pH 和 PaCO₂"},{"id":"q01_p_neuro_resp","en":"Level of consciousness, respiratory rate, and work of breathing","zh":"意识水平、呼吸频率和呼吸功"},{"id":"q01_p_urine_ketones","en":"Urine ketones as the main severity marker","zh":"尿酮作为主要严重程度指标"}],"correct":["q01_p_abg","q01_p_neuro_resp"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The ABG shows acidemia with elevated PaCO₂, indicating acute respiratory acidosis in the setting of ventilatory failure. Drowsiness and the stated pH/PaCO₂ rule make airway and ventilation escalation urgent; ABG and neuro-respiratory trends show whether ventilation is improving.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血气显示酸血症并伴 PaCO₂ 升高，符合通气衰竭导致的急性呼吸性酸中毒。嗜睡以及题干给出的 pH/PaCO₂ 规则提示必须紧急处理气道和通气；复查血气和神经呼吸状态可判断通气是否改善。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read pH, then PaCO₂, then HCO₃⁻. A low pH moving in the same direction as high PaCO₂ points to a respiratory cause.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先看 pH，再看 PaCO₂，再看 HCO₃⁻。pH 降低且 PaCO₂ 升高，说明主要问题来自呼吸。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1948,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.478","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.478.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.478.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[367,387],"terminalOffsetsZh":[163,173],"fullStemEn":"A postpartum client with suspected sepsis has bleeding from venipuncture sites and new petechiae. The item rule says the pattern of thrombocytopenia plus prolonged PT/aPTT plus fibrinogen < 100 mg/dL plus markedly elevated D-dimer is treated as DIC until proven otherwise. Labs: platelets 48 ×10³/µL, PT 24 sec, aPTT 62 sec, fibrinogen 72 mg/dL, D-dimer 9,800 ng/mL. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名产后疑似败血症患者静脉穿刺点渗血，并出现新的瘀点。本题规则规定：血小板减少、PT/aPTT 延长、纤维蛋白原 < 100 mg/dL、D-二聚体明显升高的组合，应先按 DIC 处理。实验室：血小板 48 ×10³/µL，PT 24 秒，aPTT 62 秒，纤维蛋白原 72 mg/dL，D-二聚体 9,800 ng/mL。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Labs: platelets 48 ×10³/µL, PT 24 sec, aPTT 62 sec, fibrinogen 72 mg/dL, D-dimer 9,800 ng/mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"实验室：血小板 48 ×10³/µL，PT 24 秒，aPTT 62 秒，纤维蛋白原 72 mg/dL，D-二聚体 9,800 ng/mL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q02_c_hit","en":"Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia","zh":"肝素诱导性血小板减少症"},{"id":"q02_c_vitk","en":"Vitamin K deficiency or warfarin effect","zh":"维生素 K 缺乏或华法林作用"},{"id":"q02_c_dic","en":"Disseminated intravascular coagulation","zh":"弥散性血管内凝血"},{"id":"q02_c_itp","en":"Immune thrombocytopenia","zh":"免疫性血小板减少症"}],"correct":"q02_c_dic"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q02_a_bleed_protocol","en":"Notify the provider and activate the facility bleeding/DIC protocol","zh":"通知医务人员并启动机构出血/DIC 流程"},{"id":"q02_a_heparin_bolus","en":"Administer a heparin bolus for low fibrinogen","zh":"因纤维蛋白原低而给予肝素负荷剂量"},{"id":"q02_a_delay_recheck","en":"Wait for the next routine morning laboratory draw","zh":"等待下一次常规晨间抽血"},{"id":"q02_a_im_injection","en":"Give ordered medications by intramuscular injection","zh":"通过肌内注射给予医嘱药物"},{"id":"q02_a_precautions_prepare","en":"Institute bleeding precautions and prepare ordered blood component support","zh":"实施出血预防措施，并准备医嘱所需血液成分支持"}],"correct":["q02_a_bleed_protocol","q02_a_precautions_prepare"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q02_p_coags","en":"Platelet count, PT/aPTT, fibrinogen, and D-dimer trends","zh":"血小板计数、PT/aPTT、纤维蛋白原和 D-二聚体趋势"},{"id":"q02_p_calcium","en":"Corrected calcium level as the main bleeding marker","zh":"校正钙作为主要出血指标"},{"id":"q02_p_bleeding_sites","en":"New oozing, bruising, hematuria, melena, or neurologic change","zh":"新发渗血、瘀斑、血尿、黑便或神经状态改变"},{"id":"q02_p_troponin","en":"Serial troponin and ST-segment trend","zh":"连续肌钙蛋白和 ST 段趋势"},{"id":"q02_p_peak_flow","en":"Peak expiratory flow after bronchodilator","zh":"支气管扩张剂后的峰流速"}],"correct":["q02_p_coags","q02_p_bleeding_sites"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thrombocytopenia with prolonged PT/aPTT, very low fibrinogen, and markedly elevated D-dimer form the DIC pattern described in the stem. The priority is rapid escalation, bleeding precautions, and preparation for ordered component therapy while trending coagulation and bleeding status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血小板减少合并 PT/aPTT 延长、纤维蛋白原极低、D-二聚体明显升高，符合题干给定的 DIC 模式。重点是快速升级处理、落实出血预防，并准备医嘱血液成分治疗，同时追踪凝血和出血情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate isolated thrombocytopenia from consumption coagulopathy. Low platelets plus prolonged clotting times plus low fibrinogen points to DIC in this stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分孤立性血小板减少和消耗性凝血障碍。血小板低、凝血时间延长、纤维蛋白原低，在本题中指向 DIC。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1949,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.479","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.479.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.479.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[364,384],"terminalOffsetsZh":[113,123],"fullStemEn":"A client is rescued from an enclosed apartment fire. Full-thickness burns are present on the anterior chest and neck. The client has singed nasal hair, soot in the mouth, a hoarse voice, and increasing restlessness. SpO₂ is 94% on room air. The item rule says visible soot plus hoarseness or oral/facial edema is an airway emergency even when SpO₂ is not yet low. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者从封闭公寓火灾中被救出。前胸和颈部有全层烧伤。患者鼻毛烧焦、口腔有烟灰、声音嘶哑并逐渐烦躁。室内空气下 SpO₂ 为 94%。本题规则规定：可见烟灰加声音嘶哑或口腔/面部水肿，即使 SpO₂ 尚未降低，也属于气道急症。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item rule says visible soot plus hoarseness or oral/facial edema is an airway emergency even when SpO₂ is not yet low.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题规则规定：可见烟灰加声音嘶哑或口腔/面部水肿，即使 SpO₂ 尚未降低，也属于气道急症。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q03_c_pain_only","en":"Expected burn pain without airway involvement","zh":"预期烧伤疼痛且无气道受累"},{"id":"q03_c_inhalation","en":"Inhalation injury with impending airway compromise","zh":"吸入性损伤伴即将发生的气道受损"},{"id":"q03_c_carbon_monoxide_only","en":"Carbon monoxide exposure without airway edema risk","zh":"一氧化碳暴露但无气道水肿风险"},{"id":"q03_c_hypovolemic","en":"Early hypovolemic shock from fluid loss","zh":"液体丢失导致的早期低血容量性休克"}],"correct":"q03_c_inhalation"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q03_a_oral_fluids","en":"Encourage oral fluids until transport arrives","zh":"在转运到达前鼓励口服液体"},{"id":"q03_a_supine_flat","en":"Keep the client flat and avoid moving the neck or jaw","zh":"让患者平卧并避免移动颈部或下颌"},{"id":"q03_a_delay_swelling","en":"Reassess in several hours because oxygen saturation is still above 90%","zh":"因氧饱和度仍高于 90%，数小时后再复查"},{"id":"q03_a_airway_team","en":"Call rapid response/anesthesia and prepare for early airway management","zh":"呼叫快速反应团队/麻醉，并准备早期气道处理"},{"id":"q03_a_oxygen","en":"Apply high-flow 100% oxygen by nonrebreather mask per burn protocol","zh":"按烧伤流程使用非再呼吸面罩给予高流量 100% 氧气"}],"correct":["q03_a_oxygen","q03_a_airway_team"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q03_p_bowel","en":"Bowel sounds and last bowel movement","zh":"肠鸣音和最后一次排便"},{"id":"q03_p_creatinine_only","en":"Creatinine as the sole marker of airway risk","zh":"仅用肌酐作为气道风险指标"},{"id":"q03_p_airway_voice","en":"Hoarseness, stridor, facial/oral edema, and work of breathing","zh":"声音嘶哑、喘鸣、面部/口腔水肿和呼吸功"},{"id":"q03_p_cohb_abg","en":"Carboxyhemoglobin, ABG, lactate, and pulse oximetry limitations","zh":"碳氧血红蛋白、动脉血气、乳酸以及脉搏氧饱和度的局限性"},{"id":"q03_p_wound_color","en":"Burn wound color as the main indicator of airway edema","zh":"以烧伤创面颜色作为气道水肿的主要指标"}],"correct":["q03_p_airway_voice","q03_p_cohb_abg"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Enclosed-space fire exposure with soot and hoarseness signals inhalation injury and possible rapid airway edema. High-flow oxygen treats smoke exposure, and early airway-team involvement is needed before swelling makes airway management more difficult.","rationaleCorrectZh":"封闭空间火灾暴露、烟灰和声音嘶哑提示吸入性损伤，气道水肿可能迅速进展。高流量氧可处理烟雾暴露，早期通知气道团队可避免水肿加重后更难处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let a normal-looking SpO₂ override airway cues after smoke exposure. Soot and hoarseness are escalation cues in this stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要让看似正常的 SpO₂ 掩盖烟雾暴露后的气道线索。烟灰和声音嘶哑在本题中就是升级处理信号。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1950,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.480","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.480.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.480.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[509,529],"terminalOffsetsZh":[145,155],"fullStemEn":"A client at 39 weeks is receiving oxytocin. The text-described tracing shows FHR baseline 150/min with moderate variability. With the last six contractions, the fetal heart rate begins to fall after the contraction starts, reaches its lowest point after the contraction peak, and returns to baseline after the contraction ends. Contractions occur every 90 seconds. The item rule says recurrent decelerations with nadir after the contraction peak are late decelerations and require intrauterine resuscitation. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名孕 39 周产妇正在使用催产素。文字描述的胎心监护显示胎心基线 150 次/分，变异性中等。最近 6 次宫缩中，胎心在宫缩开始后下降，在宫缩峰值后达到最低点，并在宫缩结束后才恢复至基线。宫缩每 90 秒一次。本题规则规定：反复出现、最低点在宫缩峰值之后的减速属于晚期减速，需要宫内复苏。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item rule says recurrent decelerations with nadir after the contraction peak are late decelerations and require intrauterine resuscitation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题规则规定：反复出现、最低点在宫缩峰值之后的减速属于晚期减速，需要宫内复苏。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_c_reassuring","en":"Reassuring tracing with no intervention needed","zh":"令人放心的胎心监护，无需干预"},{"id":"q04_c_variable","en":"Umbilical cord compression with variable decelerations","zh":"脐带受压伴变异减速"},{"id":"q04_c_late","en":"Uteroplacental insufficiency with recurrent late decelerations","zh":"子宫胎盘灌注不足伴反复晚期减速"},{"id":"q04_c_early","en":"Fetal head compression with early decelerations","zh":"胎头受压伴早期减速"}],"correct":"q04_c_late"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_a_lateral","en":"Reposition the client to a lateral side-lying position","zh":"将产妇调整为侧卧位"},{"id":"q04_a_ignore_variability","en":"Document only because moderate variability is present","zh":"因存在中等变异，仅记录即可"},{"id":"q04_a_push","en":"Encourage pushing with each contraction","zh":"鼓励每次宫缩时用力屏气"},{"id":"q04_a_amniotomy","en":"Prepare for artificial rupture of membranes to speed labor","zh":"准备人工破膜以加快产程"},{"id":"q04_a_stop_oxy_bolus","en":"Stop oxytocin and increase IV isotonic fluid per unit protocol","zh":"停止催产素，并按科室流程增加等渗静脉液体"}],"correct":["q04_a_lateral","q04_a_stop_oxy_bolus"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_p_apgar","en":"Apgar score before birth","zh":"出生前 Apgar 评分"},{"id":"q04_p_fhr_pattern","en":"Baseline fetal heart rate, variability, and recurrence of late decelerations","zh":"胎心基线、变异性和晚期减速是否反复出现"},{"id":"q04_p_maternal_uterine","en":"Maternal blood pressure, contraction frequency, and uterine resting tone","zh":"产妇血压、宫缩频率和子宫静息张力"},{"id":"q04_p_fundal_height","en":"Fundal height compared with gestational age","zh":"宫高与孕周的比较"},{"id":"q04_p_lochia","en":"Lochia amount and uterine firmness","zh":"恶露量和子宫硬度"}],"correct":["q04_p_fhr_pattern","q04_p_maternal_uterine"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The decelerations start after contractions begin, reach their nadir after the contraction peak, and recover after the contraction ends, matching the stem definition of recurrent late decelerations. Maternal repositioning, stopping oxytocin, and IV fluid support are intrauterine resuscitation actions; FHR and uterine activity show response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胎心减速在宫缩开始后出现、最低点在宫缩峰值之后，并在宫缩结束后恢复，符合题干对反复晚期减速的定义。产妇侧卧、停止催产素和增加静脉液体属于宫内复苏措施；胎心和子宫活动可显示反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For text-only fetal monitoring, key on timing. A deceleration whose lowest point follows the contraction peak is treated as late in this stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"文字版胎心监护要抓时间关系。最低点在宫缩峰值之后的减速，在本题中按晚期减速处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1951,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.481","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.481.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.481.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[383,403],"terminalOffsetsZh":[178,188],"fullStemEn":"A client with pneumonia is febrile and confused. BP is 82/46 mm Hg, MAP 58 mm Hg, HR 128/min, RR 28/min, SpO₂ 92% on 4 L/min, lactate 3.4 mmol/L, urine output 15 mL/hr. Lungs have crackles at the right base; no chest pain is reported. The item sepsis protocol says suspected infection plus MAP < 65 or lactate ≥ 2 requires cultures, antibiotics, fluid resuscitation, and escalation. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名肺炎患者发热并意识混乱。血压 82/46 mm Hg，MAP 58 mm Hg，心率 128 次/分，呼吸 28 次/分，4 L/min 氧气下 SpO₂ 92%，乳酸 3.4 mmol/L，尿量 15 mL/hr。右肺底有湿啰音；无胸痛。本题脓毒症流程规定：疑似感染加 MAP < 65 或乳酸 ≥ 2，需要采集培养、给予抗生素、液体复苏并升级处理。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item sepsis protocol says suspected infection plus MAP < 65 or lactate ≥ 2 requires cultures, antibiotics, fluid resuscitation, and escalation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题脓毒症流程规定：疑似感染加 MAP < 65 或乳酸 ≥ 2，需要采集培养、给予抗生素、液体复苏并升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q05_c_hypovolemic","en":"Hypovolemic shock from isolated fluid loss","zh":"单纯液体丢失导致的低血容量性休克"},{"id":"q05_c_cardiogenic","en":"Cardiogenic shock from pump failure","zh":"泵功能衰竭导致的心源性休克"},{"id":"q05_c_septic","en":"Early septic shock from infection-related vasodilation","zh":"感染相关血管扩张导致的早期脓毒性休克"},{"id":"q05_c_anaphylactic","en":"Anaphylactic shock from allergen exposure","zh":"过敏原暴露导致的过敏性休克"}],"correct":"q05_c_septic"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q05_a_beta_blocker","en":"Administer a beta blocker to lower the heart rate","zh":"给予 β 受体阻滞剂降低心率"},{"id":"q05_a_diuretic","en":"Give a loop diuretic for low urine output before perfusion support","zh":"在灌注支持前因尿量低给予袢利尿剂"},{"id":"q05_a_fluids_rrt","en":"Initiate ordered isotonic fluid bolus and notify rapid response/provider","zh":"开始医嘱等渗液体快速补液，并通知快速反应团队/医务人员"},{"id":"q05_a_cultures_abx","en":"Obtain ordered cultures and administer broad-spectrum antibiotics per sepsis protocol","zh":"按脓毒症流程采集医嘱培养并给予广谱抗生素"},{"id":"q05_a_delay_antibiotics","en":"Delay antibiotics until the fever pattern is observed overnight","zh":"推迟抗生素，观察夜间发热模式"}],"correct":["q05_a_cultures_abx","q05_a_fluids_rrt"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q05_p_daily_weight","en":"Daily weight as the main shock marker","zh":"每日体重作为主要休克指标"},{"id":"q05_p_peak_troponin","en":"Peak troponin as the defining sepsis marker","zh":"以峰值肌钙蛋白作为脓毒症定义指标"},{"id":"q05_p_pain_scale","en":"Incisional pain score as the key perfusion parameter","zh":"切口疼痛评分作为关键灌注参数"},{"id":"q05_p_map_lactate","en":"MAP, lactate trend, and response to fluid resuscitation","zh":"MAP、乳酸趋势以及对补液复苏的反应"},{"id":"q05_p_urine_mental","en":"Urine output, mental status, skin perfusion, and temperature","zh":"尿量、意识状态、皮肤灌注和体温"}],"correct":["q05_p_map_lactate","q05_p_urine_mental"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected infection with hypotension, MAP below the stated threshold, elevated lactate, confusion, and oliguria matches early septic shock in the stem. Cultures and antibiotics address infection, while fluids and escalation address poor perfusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似感染伴低血压、MAP 低于题干阈值、乳酸升高、意识混乱和少尿，符合题干中的早期脓毒性休克。培养和抗生素针对感染，补液和升级处理针对灌注不足。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem gives a protocol trigger, match the data to that trigger before considering less-supported shock types.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干给出流程触发条件时，先把数据与触发条件对应，再考虑支持较少的其他休克类型。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1952,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.482","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.482.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.482.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[388,408],"terminalOffsetsZh":[140,150],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic kidney disease reports weakness and palpitations. Telemetry shows tall peaked T waves and QRS widening. Serum potassium is 6.9 mEq/L, calcium is 9.1 mg/dL, magnesium is 2.0 mg/dL, and sodium is 138 mEq/L. The item protocol says potassium ≥ 6.5 mEq/L with ECG changes is an emergency requiring cardiac monitoring, escalation, and calcium stabilization as prescribed. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性肾病患者诉乏力和心悸。遥测显示高尖 T 波和 QRS 增宽。血钾 6.9 mEq/L，钙 9.1 mg/dL，镁 2.0 mg/dL，钠 138 mEq/L。本题流程规定：血钾 ≥ 6.5 mEq/L 且有心电图改变属于急症，需要心电监护、升级处理，并按医嘱用钙稳定心肌。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item protocol says potassium ≥ 6.5 mEq/L with ECG changes is an emergency requiring cardiac monitoring, escalation, and calcium stabilization as prescribed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题流程规定：血钾 ≥ 6.5 mEq/L 且有心电图改变属于急症，需要心电监护、升级处理，并按医嘱用钙稳定心肌。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q06_c_hypermag","en":"Hypermagnesemia with depressed reflexes","zh":"高镁血症伴反射减弱"},{"id":"q06_c_hyperk","en":"Hyperkalemia with ECG changes","zh":"高钾血症伴心电图改变"},{"id":"q06_c_hypocal","en":"Hypocalcemia with neuromuscular irritability","zh":"低钙血症伴神经肌肉兴奋性增高"},{"id":"q06_c_hyponatremia","en":"Acute hyponatremia with seizure risk","zh":"急性低钠血症伴癫痫风险"}],"correct":"q06_c_hyperk"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q06_a_potassium","en":"Administer potassium chloride replacement","zh":"给予氯化钾补充"},{"id":"q06_a_stop_monitor","en":"Remove telemetry once the client reports feeling better","zh":"患者感觉好转后停止遥测监护"},{"id":"q06_a_kayex_wait","en":"Give a cation-exchange resin and wait to reassess the ECG later","zh":"给予阳离子交换树脂，并等待稍后复查心电图"},{"id":"q06_a_monitor_escalate","en":"Place on continuous cardiac monitoring and notify the provider/rapid response","zh":"置于连续心电监护，并通知医务人员/快速反应团队"},{"id":"q06_a_calcium_protocol","en":"Prepare/administer IV calcium gluconate as prescribed by hyperkalemia protocol","zh":"按高钾流程准备/给予医嘱静脉葡萄糖酸钙"}],"correct":["q06_a_monitor_escalate","q06_a_calcium_protocol"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q06_p_wbc","en":"White blood cell differential trend","zh":"白细胞分类趋势"},{"id":"q06_p_k_ecg","en":"Serum potassium trend and QRS widening/arrhythmias on ECG","zh":"血清钾趋势以及心电图 QRS 增宽/心律失常"},{"id":"q06_p_phosphate","en":"Serum phosphate as the main arrhythmia marker","zh":"血磷作为主要心律失常指标"},{"id":"q06_p_skin_turgor","en":"Skin turgor as the key electrolyte marker","zh":"皮肤弹性作为关键电解质指标"},{"id":"q06_p_glucose","en":"Blood glucose after insulin-dextrose therapy and recurrence of weakness","zh":"胰岛素-葡萄糖治疗后的血糖以及无力是否复发"}],"correct":["q06_p_k_ecg","q06_p_glucose"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium is severely elevated and ECG changes are present, matching the emergency trigger in the stem. Continuous monitoring and urgent escalation are needed, and prescribed IV calcium stabilizes the myocardium while potassium-shifting therapy is arranged.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钾严重升高且出现心电图改变，符合题干的急症触发条件。需要连续监护并紧急升级处理，医嘱静脉钙可在安排降钾治疗时稳定心肌。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pair the electrolyte value with the clinical cue. A high potassium level plus ECG widening is a cardiac emergency.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把电解质数值和临床线索配对。血钾高加心电图增宽就是心脏急症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1953,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.483","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.483.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.483.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[361,381],"terminalOffsetsZh":[157,167],"fullStemEn":"A client with cirrhosis is admitted after black tarry stools. The client is sleepy, disoriented to date, and has asterixis. Labs: ammonia 126 mcg/dL, glucose 96 mg/dL, BUN 28 mg/dL, creatinine 1.1 mg/dL, sodium 136 mEq/L. The item rule says cirrhosis plus confusion and asterixis after GI bleeding indicates hepatic encephalopathy until another cause is shown. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名肝硬化患者因黑色柏油样便入院。患者嗜睡、不能正确说出日期，并有扑翼样震颤。实验室：血氨 126 mcg/dL，血糖 96 mg/dL，BUN 28 mg/dL，肌酐 1.1 mg/dL，钠 136 mEq/L。本题规则规定：肝硬化患者在胃肠道出血后出现意识混乱和扑翼样震颤，应先考虑肝性脑病，除非证实其他原因。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item rule says cirrhosis plus confusion and asterixis after GI bleeding indicates hepatic encephalopathy until another cause is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题规则规定：肝硬化患者在胃肠道出血后出现意识混乱和扑翼样震颤，应先考虑肝性脑病，除非证实其他原因。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_c_hypoglycemia","en":"Hypoglycemia causing acute confusion","zh":"低血糖导致的急性意识混乱"},{"id":"q07_c_uremic","en":"Uremic encephalopathy from renal failure","zh":"肾衰竭导致的尿毒症性脑病"},{"id":"q07_c_hepatic","en":"Hepatic encephalopathy precipitated by gastrointestinal bleeding","zh":"胃肠道出血诱发的肝性脑病"},{"id":"q07_c_stroke","en":"Acute ischemic stroke with focal deficits","zh":"急性缺血性卒中伴局灶神经缺损"}],"correct":"q07_c_hepatic"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_a_safety_aspiration","en":"Institute fall, aspiration, and neurologic safety precautions","zh":"实施跌倒、误吸和神经安全预防措施"},{"id":"q07_a_lactulose","en":"Administer prescribed lactulose and document stool response","zh":"给予医嘱乳果糖并记录排便反应"},{"id":"q07_a_sedative","en":"Administer a sedative to reduce agitation before evaluation","zh":"评估前给予镇静药以减少躁动"},{"id":"q07_a_high_protein","en":"Encourage a very high-protein meal immediately","zh":"立即鼓励进食极高蛋白餐"},{"id":"q07_a_ignore_ammonia","en":"Defer reporting because ammonia is only mildly related to symptoms","zh":"因氨与症状仅轻度相关而暂不报告"}],"correct":["q07_a_safety_aspiration","q07_a_lactulose"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_p_stool_ammonia","en":"Stool frequency/character and ammonia trend as ordered","zh":"按医嘱监测排便次数/性状和血氨趋势"},{"id":"q07_p_mental_asterixis","en":"Orientation, asterixis, agitation, and ability to protect the airway","zh":"定向力、扑翼样震颤、躁动以及保护气道能力"},{"id":"q07_p_pupil_only","en":"Pupil color as the main hepatic marker","zh":"瞳孔颜色作为主要肝性指标"},{"id":"q07_p_peak_flow","en":"Peak expiratory flow every hour","zh":"每小时峰呼气流速"},{"id":"q07_p_tsh","en":"TSH level as the priority mental-status marker","zh":"TSH 作为意识状态的优先指标"}],"correct":["q07_p_mental_asterixis","q07_p_stool_ammonia"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cirrhosis, GI bleeding, confusion, asterixis, and elevated ammonia fit the stem rule for hepatic encephalopathy. Safety precautions reduce injury and aspiration risk; prescribed lactulose therapy is tracked by stool response and mental-status improvement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肝硬化、胃肠道出血、意识混乱、扑翼样震颤和血氨升高，符合题干对肝性脑病的规则。安全预防可降低伤害和误吸风险；医嘱乳果糖的效果通过排便反应和意识改善来追踪。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the predisposing condition. Cirrhosis plus GI bleeding plus asterixis is a hepatic encephalopathy pattern in this item.","testTakingStrategyZh":"利用易感背景。肝硬化加胃肠道出血加扑翼样震颤，在本题中就是肝性脑病模式。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1954,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.484","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.484.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.484.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[474,494],"terminalOffsetsZh":[195,205],"fullStemEn":"A client with known primary adrenal insufficiency has had vomiting for 2 days and missed steroid doses. The client is weak and confused. BP 76/42 mm Hg, HR 118/min, temperature 98.8 °F (37.1 °C). Labs: sodium 123 mEq/L, potassium 6.1 mEq/L, glucose 48 mg/dL, serum ketones negative. The item protocol says known adrenal insufficiency plus hypotension and hypoglycemia after missed steroids is adrenal crisis requiring immediate fluids and prescribed IV steroid replacement. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名已知原发性肾上腺功能不全患者呕吐 2 天，并漏服类固醇。患者虚弱、意识混乱。血压 76/42 mm Hg，心率 118 次/分，体温 98.8 °F (37.1 °C)。实验室：钠 123 mEq/L，钾 6.1 mEq/L，血糖 48 mg/dL，血清酮体阴性。本题流程规定：已知肾上腺功能不全患者漏服类固醇后出现低血压和低血糖，应按肾上腺危象处理，需要立即补液和医嘱静脉类固醇替代。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item protocol says known adrenal insufficiency plus hypotension and hypoglycemia after missed steroids is adrenal crisis requiring immediate fluids and prescribed IV steroid replacement.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题流程规定：已知肾上腺功能不全患者漏服类固醇后出现低血压和低血糖，应按肾上腺危象处理，需要立即补液和医嘱静脉类固醇替代。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q08_c_thyroid_storm","en":"Thyroid storm with hyperthermia and severe tachycardia","zh":"甲状腺危象伴高热和严重心动过速"},{"id":"q08_c_siadh","en":"SIADH with dilutional hyponatremia","zh":"SIADH 伴稀释性低钠血症"},{"id":"q08_c_addisonian","en":"Adrenal crisis with shock and hypoglycemia","zh":"肾上腺危象伴休克和低血糖"},{"id":"q08_c_dka","en":"Diabetic ketoacidosis with osmotic diuresis","zh":"糖尿病酮症酸中毒伴渗透性利尿"}],"correct":"q08_c_addisonian"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q08_a_fluid_restrict","en":"Restrict fluids because sodium is low","zh":"因钠低而限制液体"},{"id":"q08_a_hydrocortisone","en":"Administer prescribed IV hydrocortisone without delaying for routine tests","zh":"给予医嘱静脉氢化可的松，不因常规检查延误"},{"id":"q08_a_fluids","en":"Start ordered rapid isotonic IV fluid resuscitation","zh":"开始医嘱快速等渗静脉液体复苏"},{"id":"q08_a_cooling_blanket","en":"Use cooling blanket as the primary intervention","zh":"以降温毯作为主要干预"},{"id":"q08_a_insulin_drip","en":"Start an insulin infusion for all hyperkalemia","zh":"因所有高钾情况启动胰岛素泵入"}],"correct":["q08_a_fluids","q08_a_hydrocortisone"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q08_p_t3_t4","en":"Free T3/T4 as the immediate resuscitation marker","zh":"游离 T3/T4 作为立即复苏指标"},{"id":"q08_p_na_k","en":"Sodium, potassium, fluid balance, and cardiac rhythm","zh":"钠、钾、液体平衡和心律"},{"id":"q08_p_bp_glucose","en":"Blood pressure/MAP, orthostatic symptoms, and blood glucose","zh":"血压/MAP、体位性症状和血糖"},{"id":"q08_p_sputum","en":"Sputum color and cough frequency","zh":"痰液颜色和咳嗽频率"},{"id":"q08_p_ketone_only","en":"Urine ketones as the defining crisis marker","zh":"尿酮作为危象定义指标"}],"correct":["q08_p_bp_glucose","q08_p_na_k"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Known adrenal insufficiency, missed steroids, vomiting, shock, hyponatremia, hyperkalemia, and hypoglycemia fit the stem's adrenal-crisis rule. Rapid isotonic fluids and prescribed IV hydrocortisone address circulatory collapse and cortisol deficiency.","rationaleCorrectZh":"已知肾上腺功能不全、漏服类固醇、呕吐、休克、低钠、高钾和低血糖，符合题干的肾上腺危象规则。快速等渗补液和医嘱静脉氢化可的松可处理循环衰竭和皮质醇不足。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Tie the crisis to the missing hormone. Missed steroids plus shock, low glucose, low sodium, and high potassium points to adrenal crisis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把危象与缺乏的激素联系起来。漏服类固醇加休克、低血糖、低钠和高钾，指向肾上腺危象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1955,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.485","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.485.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.485.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[418,438],"terminalOffsetsZh":[138,148],"fullStemEn":"A client with diabetes received 12 units of insulin lispro for lunch, but the meal tray was delayed. The client is awake, can swallow, and now reports shakiness. Skin is cool and diaphoretic. Capillary glucose is 42 mg/dL. The item hypoglycemia protocol says a conscious client who can safely swallow and has glucose < 70 mg/dL should receive 15 g rapid-acting carbohydrate, followed by glucose recheck in 15 minutes. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名糖尿病患者午餐前接受赖脯胰岛素 12 单位，但餐盘延迟送达。患者清醒、可吞咽，现在诉发抖。皮肤凉且出汗。指尖血糖 42 mg/dL。本题低血糖流程规定：清醒且可安全吞咽、血糖 < 70 mg/dL 的患者，应给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物，并在 15 分钟后复查血糖。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item hypoglycemia protocol says a conscious client who can safely swallow and has glucose < 70 mg/dL should receive 15 g rapid-acting carbohydrate, followed by glucose recheck in 15 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题低血糖流程规定：清醒且可安全吞咽、血糖 < 70 mg/dL 的患者，应给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物，并在 15 分钟后复查血糖。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q09_c_hypokalemia","en":"Hypokalemia after insulin treatment","zh":"胰岛素治疗后的低钾血症"},{"id":"q09_c_anxiety","en":"Anxiety episode without glucose abnormality","zh":"无血糖异常的焦虑发作"},{"id":"q09_c_hyperglycemia","en":"Uncontrolled hyperglycemia from insufficient insulin","zh":"胰岛素不足导致的未控制高血糖"},{"id":"q09_c_hypoglycemia","en":"Insulin-related hypoglycemia after delayed meal intake","zh":"延迟进餐后的胰岛素相关低血糖"}],"correct":"q09_c_hypoglycemia"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q09_a_carb","en":"Give 15 g of rapid-acting carbohydrate because the client can swallow safely","zh":"因患者可安全吞咽，给予 15 g 快速作用碳水化合物"},{"id":"q09_a_recheck","en":"Recheck capillary glucose in 15 minutes and repeat treatment per protocol if still low","zh":"15 分钟后复查指尖血糖，若仍低则按流程重复处理"},{"id":"q09_a_send_walk","en":"Send the client to walk to the cafeteria for food","zh":"让患者步行去餐厅取食物"},{"id":"q09_a_document_only","en":"Document the result and wait for the next scheduled meal","zh":"记录结果并等待下一餐"},{"id":"q09_a_more_insulin","en":"Administer additional rapid-acting insulin for diaphoresis","zh":"因出汗再给予速效胰岛素"}],"correct":["q09_a_carb","q09_a_recheck"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q09_p_inr","en":"INR trend after carbohydrate intake","zh":"摄入碳水后的 INR 趋势"},{"id":"q09_p_glucose_symptoms","en":"Repeat glucose value and resolution of sweating, tremor, and confusion","zh":"复查血糖值以及出汗、震颤和意识混乱是否缓解"},{"id":"q09_p_pulse_ox","en":"Pulse oximetry as the defining marker of insulin effect","zh":"脉搏氧饱和度作为胰岛素作用的定义指标"},{"id":"q09_p_creatinine_acute","en":"Creatinine alone as the immediate response marker","zh":"仅以肌酐作为立即反应指标"},{"id":"q09_p_meal_med","en":"Meal availability, insulin timing, and recurrent hypoglycemia risk","zh":"餐食是否到位、胰岛素给药时间以及低血糖复发风险"}],"correct":["q09_p_glucose_symptoms","q09_p_meal_med"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rapid-acting insulin was given without timely food, and glucose is below the stem threshold with adrenergic/neuroglycopenic symptoms. The protocol directs 15 g rapid carbohydrate and a timed glucose reassessment; meal timing must be addressed to prevent recurrence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"速效胰岛素已给但食物未及时到位，血糖低于题干阈值，并有肾上腺素样/神经低糖症状。流程要求给予 15 g 快速碳水并定时复查血糖；还需处理餐食时间以防复发。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For insulin safety items, connect medication timing to food timing and the measured glucose value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"胰岛素安全题要把给药时间、进餐时间和实测血糖联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1956,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_bow_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.486","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.486.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.486.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[442,462],"terminalOffsetsZh":[171,181],"fullStemEn":"A client taking apixaban for atrial fibrillation reports black stools and dizziness. BP is 86/50 mm Hg, HR 124/min. Hemoglobin fell from 12.8 g/dL yesterday to 8.9 g/dL today. Platelets are 210 ×10³/µL. No heparin exposure is documented. The item rule says suspected GI bleeding plus hemodynamic instability or hemoglobin drop ≥ 2 g/dL while on an anticoagulant is major bleeding requiring the anticoagulant to be held and urgent escalation. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名因房颤服用阿哌沙班的患者报告黑便和头晕。血压 86/50 mm Hg，心率 124 次/分。血红蛋白从昨天 12.8 g/dL 降至今天 8.9 g/dL。血小板 210 ×10³/µL。未记录肝素暴露。本题规则规定：抗凝期间疑似胃肠道出血，并有血流动力学不稳定或血红蛋白下降 ≥ 2 g/dL，即为重大出血，需要暂停抗凝并紧急升级处理。完成 bowtie。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成 bowtie。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The item rule says suspected GI bleeding plus hemodynamic instability or hemoglobin drop ≥ 2 g/dL while on an anticoagulant is major bleeding requiring the anticoagulant to be held and urgent escalation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题规则规定：抗凝期间疑似胃肠道出血，并有血流动力学不稳定或血红蛋白下降 ≥ 2 g/dL，即为重大出血，需要暂停抗凝并紧急升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q10_c_pe","en":"Pulmonary embolism despite anticoagulant therapy","zh":"抗凝治疗期间发生肺栓塞"},{"id":"q10_c_expected","en":"Expected therapeutic anticoagulant effect without bleeding","zh":"无出血的预期治疗性抗凝作用"},{"id":"q10_c_major_bleed","en":"Major bleeding while taking an anticoagulant","zh":"服用抗凝药期间发生重大出血"},{"id":"q10_c_hit","en":"Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia with thrombosis risk","zh":"肝素诱导性血小板减少症伴血栓风险"}],"correct":"q10_c_major_bleed"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate nursing actions","zh":"立即护理措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q10_a_im_vitamin","en":"Request intramuscular vitamin administration as routine care","zh":"常规请求肌内注射维生素"},{"id":"q10_a_give_dose","en":"Give the next anticoagulant dose to prevent clotting","zh":"给予下一剂抗凝药以预防凝血"},{"id":"q10_a_ambulate","en":"Ambulate the client to reduce venous stasis before assessment","zh":"评估前让患者下床活动以减少静脉淤滞"},{"id":"q10_a_hold_escalate","en":"Hold the next anticoagulant dose and notify the provider/rapid response","zh":"暂停下一剂抗凝药，并通知医务人员/快速反应团队"},{"id":"q10_a_iv_type_screen","en":"Maintain IV access and prepare ordered type-and-screen, blood products, or reversal protocol","zh":"保持静脉通路，并准备医嘱配血、血液制品或逆转流程"}],"correct":["q10_a_hold_escalate","q10_a_iv_type_screen"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor or report","zh":"需要监测或报告的参数"},"tokens":[{"id":"q10_p_platelet_only","en":"Platelet count as the only marker of apixaban effect","zh":"血小板计数作为阿哌沙班作用的唯一指标"},{"id":"q10_p_hemodynamics_hgb","en":"Blood pressure, heart rate, hemoglobin/hematocrit, and symptoms of shock","zh":"血压、心率、血红蛋白/红细胞比容以及休克症状"},{"id":"q10_p_peak_flow","en":"Peak expiratory flow after ambulation","zh":"活动后峰呼气流速"},{"id":"q10_p_temp_only","en":"Temperature as the sole bleeding-severity marker","zh":"体温作为唯一出血严重程度指标"},{"id":"q10_p_bleeding_neuro","en":"Melena, hematemesis, urine/stool blood, neurologic changes, and fall risk","zh":"黑便、呕血、尿/便带血、神经改变和跌倒风险"}],"correct":["q10_p_hemodynamics_hgb","q10_p_bleeding_neuro"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Melena, hypotension, tachycardia, and a hemoglobin drop greater than the stem threshold while taking apixaban match major anticoagulant-associated bleeding. Holding the anticoagulant, urgent escalation, IV access, and preparation for ordered blood or reversal support address the immediate risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"服用阿哌沙班期间出现黑便、低血压、心动过速，并且血红蛋白下降超过题干阈值，符合抗凝相关重大出血。暂停抗凝、紧急升级、保持静脉通路，并准备医嘱血液或逆转支持，可处理当前风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For anticoagulant questions, separate expected anticoagulation from bleeding harm. Hemodynamic instability and hemoglobin drop make the problem unsafe bleeding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抗凝题要区分预期抗凝作用和出血伤害。血流动力学不稳定加血红蛋白下降，说明问题是危险出血。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1957,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.487","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.487.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.487.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"During an oncology clinic visit, highlight the nurse statements that are therapeutic communication responses.","fullStemZh":"在肿瘤门诊访视中，标出属于治疗性沟通的护士回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"During an oncology clinic visit, highlight the nurse statements that are therapeutic communication responses.","terminalSentenceZh":"在肿瘤门诊访视中，标出属于治疗性沟通的护士回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue01_s01","en":"Clinic note: The client says, ‘I cannot stop thinking that the cancer will come back.’","zh":"门诊记录：患者说：“我一直担心癌症会复发。”"},{"id":"cue01_s02","en":"Nurse: ‘It sounds frightening to have that worry keep returning. Tell me what you have been noticing.’","zh":"护士：“这种担心反复出现听起来很可怕。跟我说说你最近注意到了什么。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue01_s03","en":"Nurse: ‘You should try not to think about relapse until the next scan.’","zh":"护士：“在下次检查前，你应该尽量不要去想复发。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue01_s04","en":"Client: ‘My spouse says I am overreacting.’","zh":"患者：“我的配偶说我反应过度。”"},{"id":"cue01_s05","en":"Nurse: ‘What has helped you get through anxious moments in the past?’","zh":"护士：“过去焦虑的时候，哪些方法曾帮助你撑过去？”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue01_s06","en":"Nurse: ‘At least your treatment is finished, so you can move on.’","zh":"护士：“至少你的治疗已经结束了，所以你可以往前看了。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue01_s07","en":"Nurse: ‘Would it help to talk through the follow-up plan and the symptoms that should prompt a call?’","zh":"护士：“我们一起梳理随访计划以及哪些症状需要来电，会不会有帮助？”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue01_s08","en":"Nurse: ‘Lots of survivors feel this way, so it is normal and not worth dwelling on.’","zh":"护士：“很多康复者都会这样，所以这是正常的，不值得多想。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue01_s02","cue01_s05","cue01_s07"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic responses acknowledge emotion, invite exploration, and offer collaborative problem-solving without dismissing the client’s concern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性回应会承认情绪、鼓励进一步表达，并以合作方式解决问题，而不是否定患者的担心。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic communication usually names the feeling, invites the client to say more, or offers collaboration; it does not reassure by shutting the topic down.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性沟通常会说出情绪、邀请患者继续表达，或提供合作；不会用空泛安慰把话题关掉。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1958,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.488","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.488.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.488.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[351,416],"terminalOffsetsZh":[152,167],"fullStemEn":"The facility alcohol-withdrawal protocol says to notify the provider or activate escalation for any seizure, new hallucinations with impaired reality testing, new disorientation, temperature ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C), heart rate >120/min, systolic BP ≥180 mm Hg, diastolic BP ≥110 mm Hg, CIWA-Ar score ≥15, or vomiting that prevents oral medication/fluids. Highlight the assessment findings that meet this escalation rule.","fullStemZh":"机构酒精戒断流程规定：如出现任何癫痫发作、伴现实检验能力受损的新发幻觉、新发定向障碍、体温 ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C)、心率 >120 次/分、收缩压 ≥180 mm Hg、舒张压 ≥110 mm Hg、CIWA-Ar 评分 ≥15，或呕吐导致不能口服药物/补液，应通知医嘱者或启动升级处理。标出符合该升级规则的评估发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the assessment findings that meet this escalation rule.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出符合该升级规则的评估发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility alcohol-withdrawal protocol says to notify the provider or activate escalation for any seizure, new hallucinations with impaired reality testing, new disorientation, temperature ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C), heart rate >120/min, systolic BP ≥180 mm Hg, diastolic BP ≥110 mm Hg, CIWA-Ar score ≥15, or vomiting that prevents oral medication/fluids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构酒精戒断流程规定：如出现任何癫痫发作、伴现实检验能力受损的新发幻觉、新发定向障碍、体温 ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C)、心率 >120 次/分、收缩压 ≥180 mm Hg、舒张压 ≥110 mm Hg、CIWA-Ar 评分 ≥15，或呕吐导致不能口服药物/补液，应通知医嘱者或启动升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue02_s01","en":"Withdrawal flowsheet, 0215:","zh":"戒断观察记录，0215："},{"id":"cue02_s02","en":"CIWA-Ar score increased from 9 to 17 over 2 hours.","zh":"CIWA-Ar 评分 2 小时内从 9 升至 17。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue02_s03","en":"Client reports mild nausea but ate crackers and drank 240 mL water.","zh":"患者诉轻度恶心，但吃了饼干并饮水 240 mL。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue02_s04","en":"Hands tremble when arms are extended.","zh":"双臂伸直时双手震颤。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue02_s05","en":"Client says, ‘Bugs are crawling on the wall,’ and reaches toward an empty wall.","zh":"患者说：“墙上有虫子在爬，”并伸手抓向空墙。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue02_s06","en":"Temperature 100.8 °F (38.2 °C) and heart rate 126/min.","zh":"体温 100.8 °F (38.2 °C)，心率 126 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue02_s07","en":"Client is oriented to name only and cannot state the date or location.","zh":"患者只能说出自己的姓名，不能说出日期或地点。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue02_s08","en":"Client asks whether the next prescribed dose is due soon.","zh":"患者询问下一次医嘱用药是否快到了。","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue02_s02","cue02_s05","cue02_s06","cue02_s07"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The keyed findings meet the escalation criteria stated in the stem: high CIWA-Ar score, hallucination with impaired reality testing, fever/tachycardia above threshold, and disorientation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"被标出的发现符合题干中的升级标准：CIWA-Ar 高分、伴现实检验受损的幻觉、超过阈值的发热和心动过速，以及定向障碍。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the protocol embedded in the stem. Separate ordinary withdrawal symptoms from cues that cross the stated escalation thresholds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干给出的流程判断。把一般戒断症状与达到升级阈值的线索区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1959,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.489","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.489.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.489.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[234,319],"terminalOffsetsZh":[80,100],"fullStemEn":"The unit opioid-safety guideline says to intervene immediately for respiratory rate <10/min, oxygen saturation <92%, new difficult-to-arouse sedation, cyanosis, or withdrawal with repeated vomiting/diarrhea plus orthostatic symptoms. Highlight the findings that need immediate nursing intervention under this guideline.","fullStemZh":"病区阿片类药物安全指南规定：呼吸频率 <10 次/分、血氧饱和度 <92%、新发难以唤醒的镇静、发绀，或戒断伴反复呕吐/腹泻并出现体位性症状时，应立即护理干预。标出符合该指南、需要立即护理干预的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that need immediate nursing intervention under this guideline.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出符合该指南、需要立即护理干预的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit opioid-safety guideline says to intervene immediately for respiratory rate <10/min, oxygen saturation <92%, new difficult-to-arouse sedation, cyanosis, or withdrawal with repeated vomiting/diarrhea plus orthostatic symptoms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"病区阿片类药物安全指南规定：呼吸频率 <10 次/分、血氧饱和度 <92%、新发难以唤醒的镇静、发绀，或戒断伴反复呕吐/腹泻并出现体位性症状时，应立即护理干预。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue03_s01","en":"Substance-use recovery unit note, 0930:","zh":"物质使用康复病区记录，0930："},{"id":"cue03_s02","en":"Client received prescribed methadone 40 mg at 0800.","zh":"患者 0800 服用医嘱美沙酮 40 mg。"},{"id":"cue03_s03","en":"At 0930 the client sleeps through repeated verbal prompts and needs a sternal rub to open eyes.","zh":"0930 患者对反复言语呼唤无反应，需要胸骨摩擦才睁眼。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue03_s04","en":"Respiratory rate is 8/min with shallow breaths.","zh":"呼吸频率 8 次/分，呼吸浅。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue03_s05","en":"Pupils are 2 mm and oxygen saturation is 90% on room air.","zh":"瞳孔 2 mm，室内空气下血氧饱和度 90%。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue03_s06","en":"Client reports yawning, muscle aches, and watery eyes before the morning dose.","zh":"患者晨间用药前诉打哈欠、肌肉酸痛和流泪。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue03_s07","en":"Later, client has four episodes of diarrhea, vomits twice, and becomes dizzy when standing.","zh":"随后患者腹泻 4 次、呕吐 2 次，站立时头晕。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue03_s08","en":"Blood pressure while supine is 124/76 mm Hg.","zh":"仰卧位血压 124/76 mm Hg。","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue03_s03","cue03_s04","cue03_s05","cue03_s07"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The selected findings meet the guideline: difficult-to-arouse sedation, bradypnea, low oxygen saturation, and withdrawal symptoms severe enough to risk volume depletion and falls.","rationaleCorrectZh":"所选发现符合指南：难以唤醒的镇静、呼吸过慢、低氧饱和度，以及严重到可能导致容量不足和跌倒风险的戒断症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For opioid-related items, respiratory status and arousability usually outrank discomfort. Then look for withdrawal severe enough to cause dehydration or injury.","testTakingStrategyZh":"阿片相关题目中，呼吸状态和可唤醒程度通常比不适症状更优先。随后再看戒断是否严重到会导致脱水或伤害。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1960,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.490","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.490.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.490.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,41],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the statements or findings in the behavioral-health intake note that indicate acute suicide risk requiring immediate safety precautions.","fullStemZh":"标出行为健康入院评估记录中提示急性自杀风险、需要立即采取安全预防措施的陈述或发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the statements or findings in the behavioral-health intake note that indicate acute suicide risk requiring immediate safety precautions.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出行为健康入院评估记录中提示急性自杀风险、需要立即采取安全预防措施的陈述或发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue04_s01","en":"Behavioral-health intake, 1840:","zh":"行为健康入院评估，1840："},{"id":"cue04_s02","en":"Client says, ‘I lost my job last month and feel ashamed.’","zh":"患者说：“我上个月丢了工作，觉得很羞耻。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue04_s03","en":"Client says, ‘I decided tonight is the night; I will use the pistol in my closet after my family goes to sleep.’","zh":"患者说：“我决定今晚就是时候了；等家人睡着后，我会用衣柜里的手枪。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue04_s04","en":"Client reports giving a sibling passwords and instructions for the pets.","zh":"患者称已把密码和照顾宠物的说明交给兄弟姐妹。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue04_s05","en":"Client says, ‘I still want my daughter to know I love her.’","zh":"患者说：“我仍然希望女儿知道我爱她。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue04_s06","en":"Client denies current alcohol or drug use.","zh":"患者否认目前使用酒精或毒品。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue04_s07","en":"Client has a history of a medication-overdose attempt 8 months ago.","zh":"患者 8 个月前有药物过量自杀未遂史。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue04_s08","en":"Client says, ‘The voice says I should die before I ruin everyone’s life.’","zh":"患者说：“那个声音说我应该去死，免得毁掉所有人的生活。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue04_s03","cue04_s04","cue04_s07","cue04_s08"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Acute suicide risk is increased by a specific plan, access to lethal means, preparatory behavior, prior attempt, and command hallucination or psychotic content directing self-harm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具体计划、可获得致命手段、事前安排行为、既往自杀未遂，以及命令性幻听或指向自伤的精神病性内容，都会提高急性自杀风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not rely only on mood words. Key immediate risk cues are intent, plan, means, timing, preparation, prior attempt, and command content.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只看情绪用词。立即风险的关键线索包括意图、计划、手段、时间、事前准备、既往未遂和命令性内容。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1961,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.491","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.491.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.491.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,36],"fullStemEn":"During a room-safety walkthrough for a client with postoperative weakness, highlight the environmental hazards that increase injury risk.","fullStemZh":"对一名术后虚弱患者进行房间安全巡视时，标出会增加受伤风险的环境危险因素。","terminalSentenceEn":"During a room-safety walkthrough for a client with postoperative weakness, highlight the environmental hazards that increase injury risk.","terminalSentenceZh":"对一名术后虚弱患者进行房间安全巡视时，标出会增加受伤风险的环境危险因素。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue05_s01","en":"Room-safety note, 0715:","zh":"房间安全记录，0715："},{"id":"cue05_s02","en":"Bed is in the lowest position with wheels locked.","zh":"床已降至最低位，床轮已锁定。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue05_s03","en":"Call light is clipped to the blanket within the client’s reach.","zh":"呼叫铃夹在毯子上，患者伸手可及。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue05_s04","en":"A full urine collection container is on the floor beside the bed.","zh":"装满尿液的收集容器放在床旁地面。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue05_s05","en":"Oxygen tubing crosses the path from bed to bathroom.","zh":"氧气管横跨从床到浴室的通道。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue05_s06","en":"The night-light is on and the bathroom door is open.","zh":"夜灯已打开，浴室门敞开。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue05_s07","en":"Non-skid socks are on the overbed table while the client is barefoot.","zh":"防滑袜放在床旁桌上，患者赤脚。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue05_s08","en":"A walker is folded behind the visitor chair, away from the client’s usual exit side.","zh":"助行器折叠放在访客椅后，远离患者通常下床的一侧。","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue05_s04","cue05_s05","cue05_s07","cue05_s08"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hazards include objects or tubing in the walking path, lack of non-skid footwear when the client may stand, and assistive devices placed out of reach.","rationaleCorrectZh":"危险因素包括行走路径上的物品或管路、患者可能站立时未穿防滑鞋袜，以及助行器放在够不到的位置。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In safety walkthroughs, look for what blocks safe movement: clutter, tubing, footwear, call light access, bed position, lighting, and assistive-device placement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全巡视题要看哪些因素妨碍安全移动：杂物、管路、鞋袜、呼叫铃、床位、照明和辅助器具摆放。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1962,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.492","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.492.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.492.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[100,338],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,89],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the hand-hygiene or personal protective equipment breaches in this charted care sequence. Use standard precautions: perform hand hygiene before and after patient contact, change gloves between dirty and clean tasks, remove gloves before touching clean shared surfaces, and use face/eye protection when splash or spray is likely.","fullStemZh":"标出该护理过程记录中的手卫生或个人防护用品违规。按标准预防原则：接触患者前后执行手卫生，污染任务和清洁任务之间更换手套，接触清洁共用表面前脱去手套，可能喷溅时使用面部/眼部防护。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use standard precautions: perform hand hygiene before and after patient contact, change gloves between dirty and clean tasks, remove gloves before touching clean shared surfaces, and use face/eye protection when splash or spray is likely.","terminalSentenceZh":"按标准预防原则：接触患者前后执行手卫生，污染任务和清洁任务之间更换手套，接触清洁共用表面前脱去手套，可能喷溅时使用面部/眼部防护。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the hand-hygiene or personal protective equipment breaches in this charted care sequence.","penultimateSentenceZh":"标出该护理过程记录中的手卫生或个人防护用品违规。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue06_s01","en":"Charted care sequence, 1010:","zh":"护理过程记录，1010："},{"id":"cue06_s02","en":"Nurse enters the room and adjusts the client’s IV pump without performing hand hygiene.","zh":"护士进入房间后未执行手卫生，直接调整患者静脉泵。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue06_s03","en":"Nurse applies gloves before emptying the urinary drainage bag.","zh":"护士在倒空尿液引流袋前戴上手套。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue06_s04","en":"With the same gloves used on the drainage bag, nurse opens the client’s water pitcher and documents on the workstation keyboard.","zh":"护士用处理引流袋的同一副手套打开患者水壶，并在工作站键盘上记录。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue06_s05","en":"Nurse removes gloves and performs hand hygiene before preparing oral medications.","zh":"护士脱下手套并执行手卫生后准备口服药。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue06_s06","en":"Client begins coughing during tracheostomy suction setup; nurse continues without mask or eye protection.","zh":"患者在气管切开吸痰准备过程中开始咳嗽；护士未戴口罩或护目防护继续操作。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue06_s07","en":"After leaving the room, nurse performs hand hygiene before answering a phone call.","zh":"离开房间后，护士先执行手卫生再接电话。","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue06_s02","cue06_s04","cue06_s06"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The breaches are missing hand hygiene before patient contact, carrying contaminated gloves to clean items and shared surfaces, and omitting face/eye protection when respiratory spray is likely.","rationaleCorrectZh":"违规包括接触患者前未做手卫生、戴着污染手套接触清洁物品和共用表面，以及在可能有呼吸道喷溅时未使用面部/眼部防护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the contamination path. Gloves protect only when they are changed at the right time and removed before clean or shared surfaces.","testTakingStrategyZh":"沿着污染路径判断。手套只有在适时更换、接触清洁或共用表面前脱掉时才真正起保护作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1963,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.493","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.493.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.493.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[291,371],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,119],"fullStemEn":"A postpartum discharge sheet tells the client to call the obstetric provider or seek urgent care for heavy bleeding soaking a pad in an hour, chest pain, trouble breathing, severe headache, vision changes, fever ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C), foul-smelling drainage, or unilateral calf pain/swelling. Highlight the client statements that require follow-up under these instructions.","fullStemZh":"产后出院单告知患者：如出现一小时浸透一片卫生巾的大量出血、胸痛、呼吸困难、严重头痛、视力改变、体温 ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C)、恶臭引流，或单侧小腿疼痛/肿胀，应联系产科医嘱者或紧急就医。标出符合这些说明、需要跟进的患者陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the client statements that require follow-up under these instructions.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出符合这些说明、需要跟进的患者陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A postpartum discharge sheet tells the client to call the obstetric provider or seek urgent care for heavy bleeding soaking a pad in an hour, chest pain, trouble breathing, severe headache, vision changes, fever ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C), foul-smelling drainage, or unilateral calf pain/swelling.","penultimateSentenceZh":"产后出院单告知患者：如出现一小时浸透一片卫生巾的大量出血、胸痛、呼吸困难、严重头痛、视力改变、体温 ≥100.4 °F (38.0 °C)、恶臭引流，或单侧小腿疼痛/肿胀，应联系产科医嘱者或紧急就医。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue07_s01","en":"Postpartum phone call, day 5 after vaginal birth:","zh":"产后电话随访，阴道分娩后第 5 天："},{"id":"cue07_s02","en":"‘I am changing a fully soaked pad about every 45 minutes.’","zh":"“我大约每 45 分钟就要换一片完全浸透的卫生巾。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue07_s03","en":"‘I have mild cramping when I breastfeed.’","zh":"“我哺乳时有轻微腹部绞痛。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue07_s04","en":"‘I have a headache that is severe and my vision has flashing spots.’","zh":"“我头痛很严重，而且眼前有闪光点。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue07_s05","en":"‘My temperature was 100.9 °F (38.3 °C) this morning.’","zh":"“今天早上体温 100.9 °F (38.3 °C)。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue07_s06","en":"‘My lochia is pink-brown and lighter than yesterday.’","zh":"“恶露呈粉棕色，比昨天少。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue07_s07","en":"‘My right calf is swollen and hurts when I walk.’","zh":"“我的右小腿肿了，走路时会痛。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue07_s08","en":"‘My breasts feel full before feeding and softer afterward.’","zh":"“喂奶前乳房胀，喂完后变软。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue07_s02","cue07_s04","cue07_s05","cue07_s07"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The selected statements match the discharge warning signs: heavy bleeding, severe headache with visual symptoms, fever, and unilateral calf pain/swelling.","rationaleCorrectZh":"所选陈述符合出院警示征象：大量出血、伴视力症状的严重头痛、发热，以及单侧小腿疼痛/肿胀。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Postpartum teaching questions often mix normal recovery with warning signs. Match the client’s words to the explicit discharge list in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产后宣教题常把正常恢复和警示征象混在一起。把患者的话与题干给出的出院清单逐项对应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1964,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.494","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.494.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.494.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,47],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing home-safety teaching with the caregiver of an 18-month-old toddler. Highlight the caregiver statements that describe unsafe practices.","fullStemZh":"护士正在与一名 18 个月幼儿的照护者复习居家安全宣教。标出照护者陈述中描述不安全做法的内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the caregiver statements that describe unsafe practices.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出照护者陈述中描述不安全做法的内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing home-safety teaching with the caregiver of an 18-month-old toddler.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在与一名 18 个月幼儿的照护者复习居家安全宣教。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue08_s01","en":"Anticipatory-guidance note:","zh":"预期性指导记录："},{"id":"cue08_s02","en":"‘We keep cleaning pods in a locked cabinet above the washer.’","zh":"“我们把洗衣凝珠放在洗衣机上方上锁的柜子里。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue08_s03","en":"‘The car seat is forward-facing because the toddler’s legs look cramped when rear-facing.’","zh":"“汽车安全座椅面向前方，因为面向后方时孩子的腿看起来很挤。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue08_s04","en":"‘I keep my daily pills in my purse on the sofa so I remember them.’","zh":"“我把每天吃的药放在沙发上的手提包里，这样我会记得吃。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue08_s05","en":"‘We cut grapes lengthwise and stay seated with the child during snacks.’","zh":"“我们把葡萄纵向切开，孩子吃点心时我们坐在旁边看着。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue08_s06","en":"‘The hot-water heater is set to 140 °F (60 °C) because baths cool down quickly.’","zh":"“热水器设在 140 °F (60 °C)，因为洗澡水很快会凉。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue08_s07","en":"‘A five-gallon bucket with mop water sometimes stays in the kitchen until bedtime.’","zh":"“有时装着拖地水的 5 加仑桶会一直放在厨房到睡前。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue08_s08","en":"‘We use safety gates at the stairs and keep windows locked.’","zh":"“我们在楼梯口使用安全门，并锁好窗户。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue08_s03","cue08_s04","cue08_s06","cue08_s07"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Unsafe practices include premature forward-facing car-seat use, accessible medications, scald-risk water temperature, and standing water that creates drowning risk for a toddler.","rationaleCorrectZh":"不安全做法包括过早使用前向汽车座椅、药物可被幼儿拿到、热水温度有烫伤风险，以及放置积水造成幼儿溺水风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For toddler safety, prioritize developmental risks: mobility, curiosity, hand-to-mouth behavior, climbing, choking, burns, poisoning, drowning, and car-seat orientation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"幼儿安全题要优先考虑发育特点带来的风险：会走、好奇、把东西放入口中、攀爬、窒息、烫伤、中毒、溺水和汽车座椅方向。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1965,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.495","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.495.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.495.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,49],"fullStemEn":"A client in the emergency department is pacing, clenching fists, and shouting that staff are ignoring pain. Highlight the nurse responses that are appropriate for verbal de-escalation.","fullStemZh":"急诊科一名患者来回踱步、握紧拳头，并大声喊叫说工作人员无视其疼痛。标出适合语言降级处理的护士回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nurse responses that are appropriate for verbal de-escalation.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出适合语言降级处理的护士回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client in the emergency department is pacing, clenching fists, and shouting that staff are ignoring pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急诊科一名患者来回踱步、握紧拳头，并大声喊叫说工作人员无视其疼痛。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue09_s01","en":"Crisis-intervention note:","zh":"危机干预记录："},{"id":"cue09_s02","en":"Nurse stands near the door, keeps hands visible, and says, ‘I can see you are in pain and angry. I want to understand what you need right now.’","zh":"护士站在靠近门的位置，双手可见，并说：“我看得出你很痛也很生气。我想了解你现在需要什么。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue09_s03","en":"Nurse says, ‘You need to calm down before anyone will help you.’","zh":"护士说：“你得先冷静下来，别人才会帮你。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue09_s04","en":"Nurse says, ‘I will stay a few steps back. Would you rather sit in this chair or walk with me to the quieter room?’","zh":"护士说：“我会保持几步距离。你想坐在这把椅子上，还是和我一起去安静一点的房间？”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue09_s05","en":"Nurse reaches for the client’s shoulder while saying, ‘I know exactly how you feel.’","zh":"护士一边伸手去碰患者肩膀，一边说：“我完全知道你的感受。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue09_s06","en":"Nurse says, ‘I cannot let anyone be hit. I will listen while we both keep our bodies safe.’","zh":"护士说：“我不能让任何人被打。只要我们都保持身体安全，我会听你说。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue09_s07","en":"Nurse says, ‘Security is coming because you are acting out.’","zh":"护士说：“保安要来了，因为你在闹事。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue09_s08","en":"Nurse says, ‘Tell me what happened after you asked for pain medicine.’","zh":"护士说：“你要求止痛药之后发生了什么？跟我说说。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue09_s02","cue09_s04","cue09_s06","cue09_s08"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate de-escalation uses calm validation, safe distance, clear limits without threats, choices, and open-ended assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合适的降级处理包括冷静地承认感受、保持安全距离、非威胁性地设定界限、提供选择，并用开放式问题评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose responses that lower stimulation and preserve dignity: acknowledge, offer choices, set limits calmly, and assess. Avoid threats, labels, arguing, or sudden touch.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能降低刺激并维护尊严的回应：承认感受、提供选择、冷静设限并评估。避免威胁、贴标签、争辩或突然触碰。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1966,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_deepen_2026_06_23_cue_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.496","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.496.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.496.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[361,425],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,116],"fullStemEn":"Hospital policy states: use restraints only after less-restrictive interventions are ineffective or unsafe; obtain a time-limited provider order; tie restraints to the bed frame, not side rails; assess skin, circulation, and need for release at least every 2 hours; and after parenteral sedating medication, monitor respiratory rate and level of consciousness. Highlight the restraint or sedation safety problems in the note.","fullStemZh":"医院政策规定：只有在较少限制措施无效或不安全后才使用约束；需取得有时限的医嘱；约束应系在床架上，不能系在床栏上；至少每 2 小时评估皮肤、循环和是否需要松解；使用肠外镇静药后需监测呼吸频率和意识水平。标出记录中的约束或镇静安全问题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the restraint or sedation safety problems in the note.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出记录中的约束或镇静安全问题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Hospital policy states: use restraints only after less-restrictive interventions are ineffective or unsafe; obtain a time-limited provider order; tie restraints to the bed frame, not side rails; assess skin, circulation, and need for release at least every 2 hours; and after parenteral sedating medication, monitor respiratory rate and level of consciousness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院政策规定：只有在较少限制措施无效或不安全后才使用约束；需取得有时限的医嘱；约束应系在床架上，不能系在床栏上；至少每 2 小时评估皮肤、循环和是否需要松解；使用肠外镇静药后需监测呼吸频率和意识水平。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"cue10_s01","en":"Safety event note, 2310:","zh":"安全事件记录，2310："},{"id":"cue10_s02","en":"Client repeatedly attempts to pull a new central line and climb over the bed rail.","zh":"患者反复试图拔出新置入的中心静脉导管，并试图翻越床栏。"},{"id":"cue10_s03","en":"Nurse documents, ‘No time to try reorientation or a sitter; bilateral wrist restraints applied immediately.’","zh":"护士记录：“没时间尝试再定向或陪护；立即使用双侧腕部约束。”","selectable":true},{"id":"cue10_s04","en":"The restraints are tied to the movable side rails so they can be reached quickly.","zh":"约束带系在可移动床栏上，以便快速够到。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue10_s05","en":"Provider order is entered for restraint use until 0700 with reassessment required per policy.","zh":"医嘱开立约束使用至 0700，并要求按政策重新评估。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue10_s06","en":"Nurse checks fingers for color, warmth, movement, and capillary refill after applying restraints.","zh":"护士在约束后检查手指颜色、温度、活动度和毛细血管再充盈。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue10_s07","en":"Prescribed IM haloperidol is administered; next respiratory-rate and sedation assessment is scheduled for the routine 0400 vital-sign round.","zh":"按医嘱给予肌内注射氟哌啶醇；下一次呼吸频率和镇静评估安排在常规 0400 生命体征巡视。","selectable":true},{"id":"cue10_s08","en":"At 0115, client is sleeping; release, skin, and circulation checks are deferred so the client can rest.","zh":"0115 患者入睡；为让患者休息，暂缓松解、皮肤和循环检查。","selectable":true}],"correct":["cue10_s03","cue10_s04","cue10_s07","cue10_s08"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The selected segments violate the policy stated in the stem: restraints were used without documenting less-restrictive attempts, tied to side rails, sedating medication was followed by delayed respiratory/sedation monitoring, and required restraint checks were deferred.","rationaleCorrectZh":"所选段落违反题干中的政策：未记录较少限制措施尝试即使用约束、约束系在床栏上、镇静药后延迟呼吸/镇静监测，以及推迟必要的约束检查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the policy embedded in the stem. Restraint questions often test least restriction, safe attachment, time-limited orders, reassessment, and respiratory monitoring after sedation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干政策判断。约束题常考较少限制原则、安全固定、有时限医嘱、重新评估，以及镇静后的呼吸监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1967,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.497","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.497.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.497.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[261,302],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,128],"fullStemEn":"A client with a history of asthma is receiving moderate sedation for a closed reduction. The client becomes anxious and says, \"My chest feels tight.\" SpO2 is 93% on 3 L/min by nasal cannula, and breath sounds are diminished bilaterally. The capnogram is shown. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名有 asthma 病史的患者正在接受 moderate sedation 以进行闭合复位。患者变得焦虑并说：“我的胸口很紧。”使用鼻导管 3 L/min 吸氧时 SpO2 为 93%，双侧呼吸音减弱。如下为 capnogram。护士首先应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Document adequate ventilation because capnography is still displaying repeated breaths.","zh":"因为 capnography 仍显示重复呼吸波形，所以记录通气充足。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer naloxone for opioid-induced respiratory depression.","zh":"给予 naloxone 处理 opioid 引起的 respiratory depression。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider to pause the procedure and prepare the prescribed inhaled albuterol.","zh":"通知医护人员暂停操作，并准备医嘱的吸入性 albuterol。"},{"id":"A","en":"Coach the client to slow the breathing pattern and continue the procedure.","zh":"指导患者放慢呼吸，并继续进行操作。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sloped, shark-fin waveform is the load-bearing cue for obstructive/reactive airway physiology. In an asthmatic client with chest tightness and diminished breath sounds, the priority is to pause the stimulus, notify the provider, and prepare bronchodilator therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这个倾斜的 shark-fin waveform 是关键线索，提示 obstructive/reactive airway physiology。对于有 asthma、胸闷和呼吸音减弱的患者，优先措施是暂停刺激性操作、通知医护人员，并准备 bronchodilator 治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not key only on the EtCO2 number. First read the shape: a shark-fin capnogram points to obstruction, then match the action to the asthma context.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只看 EtCO2 数字。先读波形形状：shark-fin capnogram 指向 obstruction，再结合 asthma 情境选择处理措施。","sourceMetadata":"Shikama M et al., Monitoring the Resolution of Acute Exacerbation of Airway Obstruction Using Capnogram Slope Values, Respiratory Care, 2023; describes acute bronchospasm producing a distinct shark-fin capnogram slope.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1968,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.498","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.498.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.498.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[279,301],"terminalOffsetsZh":[146,155],"fullStemEn":"Immediately after endotracheal intubation during a rapid response, bag-valve ventilation through the tube produces no visible chest rise. The nurse hears gurgling over the epigastrium and no bilateral breath sounds. The capnogram is shown. Which actions should the nurse expect? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在 rapid response 中，患者刚完成 endotracheal intubation 后，通过气管管进行 bag-valve ventilation 没有看到胸廓起伏。护士在 epigastrium 听到咕噜声，双侧没有呼吸音。如下为 capnogram。护士应预期采取哪些措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse expect?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预期采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Continue ventilating through the tube because condensation in the tube confirms correct placement.","zh":"继续通过该管通气，因为管内水汽凝结可确认位置正确。"},{"id":"E","en":"Prepare suction and reintubation equipment while oxygenation is restored.","zh":"在恢复氧合的同时，准备 suction 和 reintubation 设备。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assist with tube removal and provide bag-mask ventilation with 100% oxygen.","zh":"协助移除该管，并使用 100% oxygen 进行 bag-mask ventilation。"},{"id":"D","en":"Advance the tube 2 cm and reassess breath sounds.","zh":"将管子再推进 2 cm，并重新评估呼吸音。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop relying on the tube for ventilation and state that tracheal placement is not confirmed.","zh":"停止依赖该管进行通气，并说明 tracheal placement 尚未确认。"}],"correct":["A","B","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A flat waveform immediately after intubation, combined with no chest rise, epigastric gurgling, and absent bilateral breath sounds, supports esophageal rather than tracheal placement. Ventilation should be restored with bag-mask oxygenation while the team prepares to remove and replace the tube.","rationaleCorrectZh":"插管后立即出现 flat waveform，并伴随无胸廓起伏、epigastric gurgling 和双侧无呼吸音，支持 esophageal placement 而不是 tracheal placement。应先用 bag-mask oxygenation 恢复通气，同时准备移除并重新置管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a flat capnogram, ask what the stem adds. Here the immediate post-intubation timing plus epigastric sounds makes esophageal intubation the safest interpretation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"看到 flat capnogram 时，要问题干还给了什么线索。本题中“刚插管后”加上 epigastric sounds，使 esophageal intubation 成为最安全的判断。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association, Part 9: Adult Advanced Life Support: 2025 Guidelines; waveform capnography is highly specific for confirming endotracheal tube position when used with clinical assessment.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1969,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.499","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.499.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.499.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[243,284],"terminalOffsetsZh":[154,166],"fullStemEn":"During CPR for pulseless ventricular tachycardia, compressions are ongoing and an advanced airway is in place. The client has received defibrillation and epinephrine. The next rhythm check is due in 30 seconds. The capnogram changes as shown. Which nursing action is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"患者因 pulseless ventricular tachycardia 正在接受 CPR，胸外按压持续进行，并已放置 advanced airway。患者已接受 defibrillation 和 epinephrine。下一次 rhythm check 还有 30 秒。capnogram 出现如下变化。护士最合适的行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最合适的行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram changes as shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"capnogram 出现如下变化。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Increase ventilation rate to reduce the EtCO2 to less than 20 mmHg.","zh":"提高通气频率，将 EtCO2 降至 20 mmHg 以下。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request sodium bicarbonate because the EtCO2 rise indicates worsening metabolic acidosis.","zh":"要求给予 sodium bicarbonate，因为 EtCO2 上升表示 metabolic acidosis 恶化。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop chest compressions immediately because the capnogram proves return of spontaneous circulation.","zh":"立即停止胸外按压，因为 capnogram 已证明 return of spontaneous circulation。"},{"id":"B","en":"Announce possible ROSC and prepare to assess pulse and blood pressure at the scheduled pause.","zh":"报告可能出现 ROSC，并准备在计划暂停时评估 pulse 和 blood pressure。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An abrupt sustained rise in EtCO2 during CPR is a cue for possible ROSC. It should prompt the team to prepare for pulse and blood pressure assessment at the next appropriate pause, not to stop compressions prematurely.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CPR 过程中 EtCO2 突然持续上升，是可能出现 ROSC 的线索。应提示团队准备在下一次合适暂停时评估 pulse 和 blood pressure，而不是提前停止按压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"During CPR, a sudden EtCO2 jump is a trend cue. Choose the option that anticipates ROSC without causing an unnecessary compression pause.","testTakingStrategyZh":"CPR 中 EtCO2 突然跳升是 trend cue。选择“预期 ROSC 但不造成不必要按压暂停”的选项。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association, Part 9: Adult Advanced Life Support: 2025 Guidelines; end-tidal CO2 trends during CPR are used to monitor physiology and may signal return of spontaneous circulation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1970,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.500","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.500.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.500.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,283],"terminalOffsetsZh":[104,127],"fullStemEn":"In the operating room, a mechanically ventilated client under general anesthesia has a gradually rising EtCO2. Tidal volume and peak airway pressure are unchanged. The capnogram is shown. For each finding or equipment issue, indicate whether it is consistent with the visual pattern.","fullStemZh":"在手术室中，一名接受 general anesthesia 的机械通气患者 EtCO2 逐渐升高。tidal volume 和 peak airway pressure 没有变化。如下为 capnogram。请判断每个发现或设备问题是否与该视觉波形一致。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding or equipment issue, indicate whether it is consistent with the visual pattern.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每个发现或设备问题是否与该视觉波形一致。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Exhausted CO2 absorbent in a circle breathing system","zh":"circle breathing system 中 CO2 absorbent 耗尽"},{"id":"r2","en":"Faulty inspiratory or expiratory unidirectional valve","zh":"inspiratory 或 expiratory unidirectional valve 故障"},{"id":"r3","en":"Acute bronchospasm causing prolonged exhalation","zh":"acute bronchospasm 导致呼气延长"},{"id":"r4","en":"Opioid-induced apnea","zh":"opioid-induced apnea"},{"id":"r5","en":"Excessive minute ventilation causing hypocapnia","zh":"minute ventilation 过高导致 hypocapnia"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not consistent with the visual pattern","zh":"与视觉波形不一致"},{"id":"c1","en":"Consistent with the visual pattern","zh":"与视觉波形一致"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The key visual feature is that the inspiratory baseline does not return to zero, which points to rebreathing in the appropriate anesthesia circuit context. Exhausted absorbent and valve malfunction are consistent causes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键视觉特征是吸气期 baseline 没有回到零，结合 anesthesia circuit 情境，提示 rebreathing。CO2 absorbent 耗尽和 valve 故障都是一致原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For rebreathing, ignore the peak number at first and look at the baseline. If the waveform never returns to zero during inspiration, think circuit or absorber problems.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断 rebreathing 时，先不要只看峰值数字，要看 baseline。如果吸气期波形从不回到零，要想到 circuit 或 absorbent 问题。","sourceMetadata":"Williams EE et al., Capnography waveforms: basic interpretation in neonatal transport, 2024; describes rebreathing as EtCO2 baseline not returning to zero during inspiration.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1971,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.501","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.501.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.501.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[287,309],"terminalOffsetsZh":[112,121],"fullStemEn":"After transfer of an intubated client from the emergency department to the ICU, the nurse connects continuous waveform capnography. SpO2 is 97%, bilateral chest rise is present, and equal breath sounds are heard. The capnogram is shown. Which interpretations or actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名已插管患者从急诊转入 ICU 后，护士连接 continuous waveform capnography。SpO2 为 97%，可见双侧胸廓起伏，听诊双侧呼吸音相等。如下为 capnogram。哪些判断或措施是合适的？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interpretations or actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些判断或措施是合适的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Remove the tube because normal oxygen saturation can temporarily occur with esophageal intubation.","zh":"因为 esophageal intubation 时氧饱和度可能暂时正常，所以移除气管管。"},{"id":"D","en":"Treat bronchospasm with albuterol based on the capnogram morphology.","zh":"根据 capnogram morphology 使用 albuterol 治疗 bronchospasm。"},{"id":"E","en":"Troubleshoot rebreathing because the inspiratory baseline is elevated.","zh":"因为 inspiratory baseline 升高，所以排查 rebreathing。"},{"id":"F","en":"Obtain a chest radiograph when ordered to verify tube depth, while maintaining continuous capnography.","zh":"按医嘱获取 chest radiograph 以确认管深，同时维持 continuous capnography。"},{"id":"A","en":"Document ongoing evidence of ventilation through the artificial airway and continue monitoring.","zh":"记录 artificial airway 通气的持续证据，并继续监测。"},{"id":"B","en":"Recognize this as evidence supporting tracheal placement in the current clinical context.","zh":"将其视为在当前临床情境下支持 tracheal placement 的证据。"}],"correct":["A","B","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The capnogram has a repeated rectangular waveform with EtCO2 in the expected range and a return to baseline. In context, it supports ongoing ventilation through a tracheal tube; chest radiography may verify depth but does not replace continuous capnography.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该 capnogram 为重复的矩形波形，EtCO2 在预期范围内，并回到 baseline。结合情境，它支持 tracheal tube 的持续通气；chest radiograph 可确认管深，但不能替代 continuous capnography。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate tube location from tube depth. A normal repeating capnogram supports ventilation through the airway; a chest x-ray can still be used to check depth.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把管子位置和管子深度分开看。正常重复的 capnogram 支持气道通气；胸片仍可用于检查深度。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association, Part 9: Adult Advanced Life Support: 2025 Guidelines; continuous waveform capnography is used with clinical assessment to confirm and monitor endotracheal tube placement.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1972,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.502","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.502.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.502.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,292],"terminalOffsetsZh":[110,124],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving IV hydromorphone for wound debridement becomes somnolent and stops responding to voice. Respiratory effort is absent, the pulse is 88/min and palpable, and the oxygen tubing remains connected. The capnogram is shown. For each response, indicate whether it is indicated now.","fullStemZh":"一名因 wound debridement 正在接受 IV hydromorphone 的患者变得嗜睡，对声音无反应。患者没有呼吸努力，pulse 为 88/min 且可触及，氧气管路仍连接。如下为 capnogram。请判断每项处理现在是否适用。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each response, indicate whether it is indicated now.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项处理现在是否适用。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Call for help, open the airway, and begin bag-mask ventilation with oxygen.","zh":"呼叫帮助，开放气道，并开始使用氧气进行 bag-mask ventilation。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Prepare naloxone according to protocol or prescription.","zh":"按 protocol 或医嘱准备 naloxone。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Assume esophageal intubation and request immediate tube removal.","zh":"假定 esophageal intubation，并要求立即移除气管管。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Replace the CO2 absorbent in the anesthesia circuit.","zh":"更换 anesthesia circuit 中的 CO2 absorbent。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Continue opioid dosing because the pulse is palpable.","zh":"因为 pulse 可触及，所以继续给予 opioid。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Indicated now","zh":"现在适用"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not indicated now","zh":"现在不适用"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The flat capnogram confirms no exhaled CO2 signal in a client with absent respiratory effort after IV opioid administration. Because the pulse is present, the priority is airway and ventilation support, with naloxone preparation as ordered or per protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"flat capnogram 证实这名 IV opioid 后无呼吸努力的患者没有呼出 CO2 信号。由于 pulse 仍存在，优先是支持 airway 和 ventilation，并按医嘱或 protocol 准备 naloxone。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A flat waveform is not one diagnosis by itself. Use the disambiguators: opioid exposure, no respiratory effort, connected oxygen tubing, and a palpable pulse point to apnea with a perfusing rhythm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"flat waveform 本身不是单一诊断。要用题干限定线索：opioid 暴露、无呼吸努力、氧气管路连接、pulse 可触及，指向有灌注心律下的 apnea。","sourceMetadata":"StatPearls, Capnography and Pulse Oximetry, NCBI Bookshelf, 2023; capnography provides direct monitoring of exhaled carbon dioxide and absent waveform requires clinical correlation with apnea, disconnection, or airway placement context.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1973,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.503","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.503.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.503.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[155,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,77],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is hospitalized with pyelonephritis and is receiving IV fluids and the first dose of antibiotics. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者因 pyelonephritis 住院，正在接受 IV fluids 和第一剂 antibiotics。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪项措施最优先？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施最优先？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider or activate the facility escalation protocol and prepare to support sepsis resuscitation.","zh":"通知 provider 或启动机构 escalation protocol，并准备配合 sepsis resuscitation。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document that the trend is an expected early response after antibiotics are started.","zh":"记录该趋势是开始 antibiotics 后预期的早期反应。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the prescribed acetaminophen and reassess the temperature at the next routine vital-sign check.","zh":"给予医嘱的 acetaminophen，并在下一次常规测量生命体征时重新评估体温。"},{"id":"C","en":"Encourage oral fluids and ambulate the client to improve ventilation.","zh":"鼓励口服液体，并协助患者下床活动以改善通气。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows rising heart rate and respiratory rate with a falling MAP in a client with infection. This pattern suggests worsening sepsis with impaired perfusion and requires urgent escalation rather than routine reassessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示在感染背景下 heart rate 和 respiratory rate 上升，同时 MAP 下降。这提示 sepsis 正在恶化并出现 perfusion 受损，需要紧急升级处理，而不是常规复查。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When infection is in the stem, compare HR, RR, and MAP across time. A falling MAP with rising HR/RR is a perfusion problem, not just a fever problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干有感染时，要跨时间比较 HR、RR 和 MAP。MAP 下降同时 HR/RR 上升，是 perfusion 问题，不只是 fever 问题。","sourceMetadata":"CDC About Sepsis, updated March 23, 2026: sepsis diagnosis uses findings such as fever, increased heart rate, low blood pressure, and trouble breathing; Surviving Sepsis Campaign Guidelines 2021: adult septic shock resuscitation commonly targets MAP 65 mm Hg.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1974,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.504","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.504.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.504.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,223],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,78],"fullStemEn":"Four hours after an open colectomy, an adult client says, 'I feel weak.' The dressing has only a small shadow of drainage. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"成人患者 open colectomy 后 4 小时说：“我觉得很虚弱。”敷料上只有少量渗液阴影。护士查看生命体征趋势。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Give the prescribed opioid and document that pain is the most likely cause of the pulse change.","zh":"给予医嘱 opioid，并记录疼痛最可能导致脉搏变化。"},{"id":"F","en":"Leave the client for the next scheduled assessment because the dressing drainage is minimal.","zh":"因为敷料渗液很少，等到下一次计划评估再处理。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assist the client to a chair and recheck the vital signs after activity.","zh":"协助患者坐到椅子上，活动后再复查生命体征。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the incision, dressing, drain output, and abdomen for bleeding or distention.","zh":"评估 incision、dressing、drain output 和腹部是否有 bleeding 或 distention。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the surgeon or rapid response team and report the serial vital-sign changes.","zh":"通知 surgeon 或 rapid response team，并报告连续生命体征变化。"},{"id":"E","en":"Maintain IV access and anticipate orders for isotonic fluids, blood work, and type and screen.","zh":"维持 IV access，并预期可能需要 isotonic fluids、blood work 和 type and screen 医嘱。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows progressive tachycardia, tachypnea, falling blood pressure, falling MAP, and narrowing pulse pressure after surgery. Small visible drainage does not rule out concealed postoperative hemorrhage, so assessment and urgent escalation are needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示术后 tachycardia、tachypnea 逐渐加重，blood pressure 和 MAP 下降，pulse pressure 变窄。少量可见渗液不能排除 concealed postoperative hemorrhage，因此需要评估并紧急升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not anchor on the dressing alone. After surgery, serial tachycardia plus falling pressure is more important than one small visible drainage finding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只盯着敷料。术后连续 tachycardia 加上压力下降，比单次看到少量渗液更重要。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ PSNet WebM&M, Don't Dismiss the Dangerous: Obstetric Hemorrhage: postoperative tachycardia or hypotension should raise concern for concealed hemorrhage; Merck Manual, Shock: low circulating volume can cause shock with organ hypoperfusion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1975,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.505","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.505.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.505.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,74],"fullStemEn":"An adult client has had vomiting and diarrhea for several hours and has dry mucous membranes. IV fluids have not yet been started. Use the vital signs trend to judge each proposed nursing action.","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者 vomiting 和 diarrhea 已持续数小时，口腔黏膜干燥。尚未开始 IV fluids。请根据生命体征趋势判断每项护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the vital signs trend to judge each proposed nursing action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据生命体征趋势判断每项护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"IV fluids have not yet been started.","penultimateSentenceZh":"尚未开始 IV fluids。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Start or maintain large-bore IV access and prepare isotonic fluid replacement as ordered.","zh":"建立或维持 large-bore IV access，并按医嘱准备 isotonic fluid replacement。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Keep the client in bed with fall precautions while perfusion is reassessed.","zh":"在重新评估 perfusion 时，让患者卧床并采取 fall precautions。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Delay notifying the provider because the systolic pressure was above 100 mm Hg during the first 4 hours.","zh":"因为前 4 小时 systolic pressure 高于 100 mm Hg，延后通知 provider。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Request an antihypertensive because the heart rate is rising.","zh":"因为 heart rate 上升，请求 antihypertensive。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Encourage oral fluids only and wait for the next routine vital-sign interval.","zh":"只鼓励口服液体，并等到下一次常规生命体征测量。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not appropriate","zh":"不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows rising HR and RR with falling SBP/MAP and a narrowing pulse pressure in a dehydrated client. This suggests compensated hypovolemic shock moving toward decompensation, so volume support, safety precautions, and escalation are appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示脱水患者 HR 和 RR 上升，同时 SBP/MAP 下降、pulse pressure 变窄。这提示 compensated hypovolemic shock 正在向 decompensation 发展，因此需要容量支持、安全措施和升级沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for compensation first: HR rises before blood pressure may clearly fall. Narrowing pulse pressure makes the trend more concerning than one blood pressure value alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先看代偿：HR 往往在 blood pressure 明显下降前上升。pulse pressure 变窄让这个趋势比单个血压值更令人担心。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual, Shock: hypovolemia can cause shock and organ hypoperfusion; NCBI Bookshelf StatPearls, Shock: shock reflects circulatory failure leading to tissue hypoxia.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1976,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.506","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.506.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.506.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,111],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with dehydration from gastroenteritis receives an ordered 1-liter 0.9% sodium chloride bolus. The nurse reviews the post-bolus vital signs trend. How should the nurse interpret the response?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者因 gastroenteritis 导致 dehydration，按医嘱接受 1 liter 0.9% sodium chloride bolus。护士查看 bolus 后的生命体征趋势。护士应如何解读该反应？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse interpret the response?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何解读该反应？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the post-bolus vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看 bolus 后的生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The bolus caused fluid overload because the respiratory rate was above 18/min at 15 minutes.","zh":"因为 15 分钟时 respiratory rate 高于 18/min，所以 bolus 导致 fluid overload。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client is deteriorating into shock and needs immediate escalation based on the trend.","zh":"根据趋势，患者正在恶化为 shock，需要立即升级处理。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client is showing improved perfusion after fluid replacement; continue monitoring and reassess urine output.","zh":"患者 fluid replacement 后 perfusion 改善；继续监测并重新评估尿量。"},{"id":"D","en":"The vital signs are unchanged, so repeat the bolus before performing any reassessment.","zh":"生命体征没有变化，所以在任何重新评估前先重复 bolus。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Across the trend, HR and RR decrease while SBP and MAP rise after the isotonic bolus. This supports improved intravascular volume and perfusion, with continued monitoring rather than automatic escalation or repeat bolus.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示 isotonic bolus 后 HR 和 RR 下降，SBP 和 MAP 上升。这支持 intravascular volume 和 perfusion 改善，应继续监测，而不是自动升级或重复 bolus。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For intervention questions, decide whether the trend moves toward or away from normal perfusion. Do not judge the response from the first post-intervention point only.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到 intervention 题，要判断趋势是朝正常 perfusion 方向走，还是远离正常。不要只看干预后的第一个时间点。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual, Shock: hypovolemia impairs perfusion and treatment addresses the underlying volume deficit; NCBI Bookshelf StatPearls, Shock: restoration of circulation is central to reversing tissue hypoxia.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1977,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.507","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.507.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.507.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,277],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,129],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with pneumonia-related sepsis received the ordered initial IV fluid resuscitation. The current urine output is 15 mL/hr. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. For each expected provider order or nursing action, choose whether it is appropriate to anticipate.","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者因 pneumonia-related sepsis 已接受医嘱的初始 IV fluid resuscitation。目前尿量为 15 mL/hr。护士查看生命体征趋势。对于每项可能的 provider order 或护理措施，选择是否适合预期。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each expected provider order or nursing action, choose whether it is appropriate to anticipate.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项可能的 provider order 或护理措施，选择是否适合预期。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Start a vasopressor such as norepinephrine through appropriate access per protocol or order.","zh":"按 protocol 或医嘱通过合适通路开始 vasopressor，例如 norepinephrine。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Continue frequent assessment of mentation, skin perfusion, blood pressure, and urine output.","zh":"继续频繁评估 mentation、skin perfusion、blood pressure 和 urine output。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Hold escalation because the temperature is slightly lower than at baseline.","zh":"因为体温比基线略低，所以暂缓升级处理。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Give a beta-blocker first because the heart rate remains elevated.","zh":"因为 heart rate 仍高，先给予 beta-blocker。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Stop frequent blood pressure monitoring because fluid resuscitation is complete.","zh":"因为 fluid resuscitation 已完成，停止频繁 blood pressure 监测。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not appropriate to anticipate","zh":"不适合预期"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate to anticipate","zh":"适合预期"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Despite initial fluid resuscitation, the trend shows persistent worsening: HR and RR rise while MAP remains below 65 mm Hg and continues to fall, with low urine output. This suggests inadequate perfusion after fluids and the need to anticipate vasopressor support and close monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管已进行初始 fluid resuscitation，趋势仍持续恶化：HR 和 RR 上升，MAP 低于 65 mm Hg 且继续下降，尿量也低。这提示 fluids 后 perfusion 仍不足，需要预期 vasopressor 支持并密切监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In sepsis, a lower fever after treatment can distract you. Prioritize perfusion trends: MAP, urine output, mentation, skin, HR, and RR.","testTakingStrategyZh":"sepsis 题里，治疗后 fever 下降可能是干扰项。优先看 perfusion 趋势：MAP、尿量、意识、皮肤、HR 和 RR。","sourceMetadata":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign Guidelines 2021 (SCCM): for adults with septic shock on vasopressors, recommended initial MAP target is 65 mm Hg; CDC About Sepsis: sepsis findings include increased heart rate, low blood pressure, and trouble breathing.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1978,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t01_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.508","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.508.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.508.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[248,270],"terminalOffsetsZh":[141,149],"fullStemEn":"An older adult from a long-term care facility is admitted with suspected pneumonia. The client is receiving oxygen 2 L/min by nasal cannula while cultures are pending. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名来自 long-term care facility 的 older adult 因 suspected pneumonia 入院。等待 cultures 期间，患者正通过 nasal cannula 接受 oxygen 2 L/min。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Increase oxygen support as allowed by protocol and reassess work of breathing and SpO2.","zh":"按 protocol 允许范围增加 oxygen support，并重新评估 work of breathing 和 SpO2。"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase concern for sepsis progression even though the client is not febrile.","zh":"即使患者没有 fever，也要提高对 sepsis progression 的警觉。"},{"id":"E","en":"Return to routine vital-sign checks because the admission systolic pressure was normal.","zh":"因为入院时 systolic pressure 正常，所以改回常规生命体征监测。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold antibiotics until the temperature rises above 100.4 °F (38.0 °C).","zh":"等体温升到 100.4 °F (38.0 °C) 以上再给予 antibiotics。"},{"id":"F","en":"Ambulate the client before notifying the provider to help mobilize secretions.","zh":"在通知 provider 前先让患者下床活动，以帮助排痰。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider or activate the facility escalation protocol and report the trend.","zh":"通知 provider 或启动机构 escalation protocol，并报告趋势。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows worsening infection-related instability: HR and RR rise, SpO2 falls despite oxygen, temperature falls rather than rises, and MAP drops below 65 mm Hg. Older adults may deteriorate without fever, so escalation and oxygen reassessment are appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示感染相关不稳定在恶化：HR 和 RR 上升，吸氧下 SpO2 下降，体温不是升高而是下降，MAP 低于 65 mm Hg。older adults 可能没有 fever 也会恶化，因此需要升级处理并重新评估氧疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not require fever to recognize sepsis. In an older adult, falling temperature with worsening MAP, RR, HR, and SpO2 can be more dangerous than a high temperature alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别 sepsis 不一定要有 fever。older adult 中，体温下降同时 MAP、RR、HR 和 SpO2 恶化，可能比单纯高热更危险。","sourceMetadata":"CDC About Sepsis, updated March 23, 2026: sepsis diagnosis uses fever, increased heart rate, low blood pressure, and trouble breathing; Surviving Sepsis Campaign Guidelines 2021: adult septic shock resuscitation commonly targets MAP 65 mm Hg.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1979,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.509","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.509.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.509.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[267,312],"terminalOffsetsZh":[132,145],"fullStemEn":"A mechanically ventilated client is turned in bed. Immediately afterward, the ventilator sounds a low-pressure alarm. The endotracheal tube depth marking is unchanged, but chest rise is difficult to see because the client is under the drapes. The capnogram is shown. Which problem should the nurse suspect first?","fullStemZh":"一名使用 mechanical ventilator 的患者在床上翻身后，ventilator 立即出现 low-pressure alarm。endotracheal tube 的深度标记没有变化，但因患者被单遮盖，胸廓起伏不易观察。如下为 capnogram。护士首先应怀疑哪一项问题？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which problem should the nurse suspect first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应怀疑哪一项问题？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Ventilator circuit disconnection","zh":"ventilator circuit 脱开"},{"id":"C","en":"Mainstem bronchus intubation","zh":"mainstem bronchus intubation"},{"id":"D","en":"Anxiety-related hyperventilation","zh":"焦虑相关的 hyperventilation"},{"id":"B","en":"Acute bronchospasm with air trapping","zh":"急性 bronchospasm 合并 air trapping"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A flat capnogram immediately after repositioning plus a low-pressure ventilator alarm and unchanged tube depth most strongly supports a circuit disconnection. The nurse should rapidly inspect and reconnect the breathing circuit while maintaining ventilation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"翻身后立即出现 flat capnogram，加上 ventilator low-pressure alarm 且管子深度未改变，最符合 breathing circuit 脱开。护士应迅速检查并重新连接呼吸回路，同时维持通气。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a flat waveform, do not assume one cause. Pair the visual with the stem: low-pressure alarm after turning points to disconnection, not obstruction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"看到 flat waveform 时不要直接假设单一原因。把波形和题干一起读：翻身后 low-pressure alarm 指向 disconnection，而不是 obstruction。","sourceMetadata":"Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Capnometry and anaesthesia, Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; describes absent expired CO2 with disconnection and other causes of flat capnograms.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1980,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.510","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.510.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.510.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[237,259],"terminalOffsetsZh":[126,134],"fullStemEn":"A client is intubated under general anesthesia using a circle breathing system. SpO2 is 98%, but EtCO2 has been rising over several minutes. The capnogram is shown. Which actions should the perioperative nurse anticipate or assist with? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在 general anesthesia 下已 intubated，并使用 circle breathing system。SpO2 为 98%，但 EtCO2 在数分钟内逐渐升高。如下为 capnogram。围手术期护士应预期或协助哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the perioperative nurse anticipate or assist with?","penultimateSentenceZh":"围手术期护士应预期或协助哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assist with checking the inspiratory and expiratory one-way valves.","zh":"协助检查 inspiratory 和 expiratory one-way valves。"},{"id":"C","en":"Treat the waveform as isolated opioid oversedation.","zh":"将该波形当作单纯 opioid oversedation 处理。"},{"id":"D","en":"Report that the inspiratory baseline is not returning to zero.","zh":"报告 inspiratory baseline 没有回到零点。"},{"id":"A","en":"Prepare to replace or bypass an exhausted CO2 absorber.","zh":"准备更换或绕过耗尽的 CO2 absorber。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document normal ventilation because the SpO2 remains 98%.","zh":"因为 SpO2 仍为 98%，记录 ventilation 正常。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The elevated inspiratory baseline is the load-bearing cue for rebreathing. In a circle anesthesia system, likely causes include exhausted CO2 absorbent or faulty one-way valves, and the nurse should report the baseline abnormality while assisting the anesthesia team.","rationaleCorrectZh":"升高的 inspiratory baseline 是判断 rebreathing 的关键线索。在 circle anesthesia system 中，常见原因包括 CO2 absorbent 耗尽或 one-way valve 故障；护士应报告 baseline 异常，并协助麻醉团队处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In anesthesia circuit questions, look at the baseline. A baseline above zero is about inspired CO2 and rebreathing, not simply oxygenation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到 anesthesia circuit 题时先看 baseline。baseline 高于零代表吸入 CO2 和 rebreathing，不是单纯看氧合。","sourceMetadata":"Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Capnometry and anaesthesia, Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; describes rebreathing as inspired CO2 with a capnogram baseline above zero and links it to absorber or valve problems.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1981,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.511","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.511.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.511.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,258],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,148],"fullStemEn":"A client in cardiac arrest is receiving high-quality CPR with ventilation through an advanced airway. EtCO2 had been 10-12 mmHg for several minutes. The current capnogram is shown. For each team statement, choose whether it is appropriate or not appropriate.","fullStemZh":"一名 cardiac arrest 患者正在接受 high-quality CPR，并通过 advanced airway 通气。EtCO2 已持续数分钟为 10-12 mmHg。如下为当前 capnogram。请判断每个团队说法是 appropriate 还是 not appropriate。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each team statement, choose whether it is appropriate or not appropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每个团队说法是 appropriate 还是 not appropriate。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The current capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为当前 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"\"Announce possible ROSC and prepare to check pulse and rhythm at the next scheduled pause.\"","zh":"“报告可能出现 ROSC，并准备在下一次计划暂停时检查 pulse 和 rhythm。”"},{"id":"r2","en":"\"Stop compressions immediately because the EtCO2 rose abruptly.\"","zh":"“因为 EtCO2 突然升高，立即停止 chest compressions。”"},{"id":"r3","en":"\"Continue compressions until the rhythm/pulse check while the team prepares post-ROSC care.\"","zh":"“在 rhythm/pulse check 前继续 chest compressions，同时团队准备 post-ROSC care。”"},{"id":"r4","en":"\"Ignore the waveform because capnography cannot provide useful information during CPR.\"","zh":"“忽略该波形，因为 CPR 期间 capnography 不能提供有用信息。”"}],"columns":[{"id":"appropriate","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"},{"id":"not_appropriate","en":"Not appropriate","zh":"不适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["not_appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["not_appropriate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An abrupt sustained EtCO2 rise during CPR can indicate return of spontaneous circulation. The team should anticipate ROSC assessment at the next organized pause while maintaining compressions until that check.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CPR 期间 EtCO2 突然且持续升高可提示 return of spontaneous circulation。团队应在下一次有组织暂停时评估 ROSC，但在检查前继续按压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not confuse low EtCO2 during CPR with a flat line. Here the load-bearing feature is the abrupt step up, which changes the team’s next assessment priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把 CPR 期间低 EtCO2 和 flat line 混淆。本题关键是突然阶梯式升高，它改变了团队下一步评估重点。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association Guidelines for CPR and ECC; quantitative waveform capnography during CPR can help assess compression quality and an abrupt sustained EtCO2 rise may indicate ROSC.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1982,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.512","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.512.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.512.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[227,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,124],"fullStemEn":"A client is intubated in the emergency department after a seizure. Breath sounds are equal, and SpO2 is 95% with bag-valve ventilation. The team asks the nurse whether the tube is likely in the trachea. The capnogram is shown. Which response is best?","fullStemZh":"一名患者 seizure 后在急诊被 intubated。双侧呼吸音相等，使用 bag-valve ventilation 时 SpO2 为 95%。团队询问护士 tube 是否可能位于 trachea。如下为 capnogram。哪项回应最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项回应最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"\"Equal breath sounds alone prove placement, so capnography is not needed.\"","zh":"“仅凭双侧呼吸音相等即可证明位置正确，因此不需要 capnography。”"},{"id":"D","en":"\"The EtCO2 is normal, but the waveform shape indicates rebreathing.\"","zh":"“EtCO2 正常，但波形形状提示 rebreathing。”"},{"id":"A","en":"\"The rectangular waveform with repeated exhaled CO2 supports tracheal placement; secure the tube and continue monitoring.\"","zh":"“重复出现呼出 CO2 的矩形波形支持 tracheal placement；固定 tube 并继续监测。”"},{"id":"C","en":"\"The waveform suggests esophageal placement; remove the tube now.\"","zh":"“该波形提示 esophageal placement；现在拔除 tube。”"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A sustained rectangular capnogram with repeated exhaled CO2 is strong evidence of tracheal ventilation in this context. Tube security and continued monitoring are appropriate after confirmation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在此情境下，持续重复的矩形 capnogram 显示呼出 CO2，是 tracheal ventilation 的有力证据。确认后应固定 tube 并继续监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When confirming tube placement, value sustained waveform capnography over breath sounds alone. Read both shape and persistence of exhaled CO2.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确认 tube placement 时，持续 waveform capnography 比单靠 breath sounds 更有价值。要同时看波形形状和呼出 CO2 是否持续存在。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association Guidelines for CPR and ECC and ASA Standards for Basic Anesthetic Monitoring; continuous waveform capnography is used to verify and monitor endotracheal tube position.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1983,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.513","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.513.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.513.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[295,317],"terminalOffsetsZh":[136,144],"fullStemEn":"A client with COPD is in the emergency department for increasing dyspnea. The client is sitting upright, using accessory muscles, and has diffuse expiratory wheezes. SpO2 is 91% on 2 L/min by nasal cannula. The capnogram is shown. Which findings or actions are supported by the stem and visual? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名 COPD 患者因 dyspnea 加重来到急诊。患者端坐、使用 accessory muscles，并有弥漫性 expiratory wheezes。鼻导管 2 L/min 吸氧时 SpO2 为 91%。如下为 capnogram。哪些发现或措施得到题干和图像支持？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings or actions are supported by the stem and visual?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现或措施得到题干和图像支持？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Document that the client is apneic because the baseline returns to zero.","zh":"因为 baseline 回到零点，所以记录患者为 apneic。"},{"id":"B","en":"Prepare prescribed inhaled bronchodilator therapy.","zh":"准备医嘱的 inhaled bronchodilator therapy。"},{"id":"A","en":"The waveform is consistent with obstructive exhalation.","zh":"该波形符合 obstructive exhalation。"},{"id":"E","en":"Hold respiratory treatment because the EtCO2 waveform proves ventilation is adequate.","zh":"因为 EtCO2 waveform 证明通气充足，所以暂停 respiratory treatment。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assume the primary problem is pulmonary embolism because the waveform has a crisp plateau.","zh":"因为波形有清晰 plateau，假设主要问题是 pulmonary embolism。"},{"id":"D","en":"Monitor for worsening obstruction if the shark-fin slope becomes more pronounced.","zh":"如果 shark-fin slope 更明显，应监测 obstruction 是否恶化。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shark-fin morphology, COPD context, wheezing, accessory muscle use, and elevated EtCO2 support obstructive exhalation and bronchodilator preparation. Increasing slope severity would suggest worsening obstruction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"shark-fin morphology 加上 COPD、wheezing、accessory muscle use 和 EtCO2 升高，支持 obstructive exhalation 并应准备 bronchodilator。斜率更明显提示 obstruction 可能恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match waveform shape to physiology before disease labels. Shark-fin means obstruction; the COPD and wheeze details then make bronchodilator therapy relevant.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先把波形形状对应到生理问题，再套疾病标签。shark-fin 意味着 obstruction；COPD 和 wheeze 细节让 bronchodilator therapy 成为相关措施。","sourceMetadata":"Shikama M et al., Monitoring the Resolution of Acute Exacerbation of Airway Obstruction Using Capnogram Slope Values, Respiratory Care, 2023; supports capnogram slope as an airway obstruction marker.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1984,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.514","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.514.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.514.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[282,376],"terminalOffsetsZh":[122,165],"fullStemEn":"An intubated client arrives from interfacility transport. The transport team reports that the tube was secure at departure, but the client became restless during unloading. The nurse notes gurgling over the epigastrium during bagging and minimal chest rise. The capnogram is shown. For each possible interpretation or action, choose whether it is indicated or contraindicated.","fullStemZh":"一名已 intubated 的患者由院际转运到达。转运团队报告出发时 tube 已固定，但卸车时患者变得 restless。护士在 bagging 时听到 epigastrium 有 gurgling，胸廓起伏很小。如下为 capnogram。请判断每项可能解释或措施是 indicated 还是 contraindicated。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each possible interpretation or action, choose whether it is indicated or contraindicated.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项可能解释或措施是 indicated 还是 contraindicated。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Suspect esophageal or displaced tube and call for immediate airway reassessment.","zh":"怀疑 esophageal 或 displaced tube，并呼叫立即重新评估 airway。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Secure the tube in the current position because the client was previously intubated.","zh":"因为患者之前已经 intubated，所以将 tube 固定在当前位置。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Ventilate with bag-mask or other rescue method while the airway is corrected per team protocol.","zh":"在团队按 protocol 纠正 airway 时，使用 bag-mask 或其他 rescue method 进行通气。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Treat the pattern as bronchospasm and delay placement reassessment until after bronchodilator therapy.","zh":"把该波形当作 bronchospasm，等 bronchodilator therapy 后再重新评估位置。"}],"columns":[{"id":"indicated","en":"Indicated","zh":"适用"},{"id":"contraindicated","en":"Contraindicated","zh":"禁忌/不适用"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["indicated"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["contraindicated"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["indicated"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["contraindicated"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A flat capnogram after transport, minimal chest rise, and epigastric gurgling during bagging indicate the airway may not be in the trachea or has become displaced. The priority is immediate airway reassessment and rescue ventilation while the team corrects placement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"转运后 flat capnogram、胸廓起伏很小，以及 bagging 时 epigastric gurgling，提示 airway 可能不在 trachea 或已 displaced。优先是立即重新评估 airway，并在团队纠正位置时提供 rescue ventilation。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Flat waveform questions need context. Epigastric gurgling and poor chest rise make this an airway placement emergency, not a ventilation-pattern nuance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"flat waveform 题必须看上下文。epigastric gurgling 和胸廓起伏差说明这是 airway placement emergency，不是单纯通气波形细节。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association Guidelines for CPR and ECC and Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; waveform capnography verifies tracheal ventilation and absent expired CO2 can indicate esophageal or displaced airway in context.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1985,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.515","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.515.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.515.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[257,304],"terminalOffsetsZh":[150,164],"fullStemEn":"During recovery from procedural sedation, a client who just received an IV antibiotic develops facial flushing, scattered hives, expiratory wheezing, and increasing work of breathing. Oxygen saturation is 91% on supplemental oxygen. The capnogram is shown. Which complication best explains the capnogram?","fullStemZh":"一名患者 procedural sedation 后恢复期间，刚接受 IV antibiotic 后出现面部潮红、散在 hives、呼气性 wheezing 和呼吸做功增加。使用 supplemental oxygen 时 oxygen saturation 为 91%。如下为 capnogram。哪一种并发症最能解释该波形？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which complication best explains the capnogram?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一种并发症最能解释该波形？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Pulmonary embolism with sudden dead-space ventilation","zh":"pulmonary embolism 导致突然 dead-space ventilation 增加"},{"id":"C","en":"Opioid-induced hypoventilation","zh":"opioid-induced hypoventilation"},{"id":"D","en":"Esophageal intubation","zh":"esophageal intubation"},{"id":"A","en":"Bronchospasm from an allergic reaction","zh":"allergic reaction 引起的 bronchospasm"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sloped, shark-fin capnogram indicates obstructive airway physiology. In the setting of hives, wheezing, and recent IV antibiotic exposure, bronchospasm from an allergic reaction is the best explanation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"倾斜的 shark-fin capnogram 提示 obstructive airway physiology。结合 hives、wheezing 和刚使用 IV antibiotic，最符合 allergic reaction 引起的 bronchospasm。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match morphology before numbers: a shark-fin shape means airflow obstruction. Then use the stem to decide the likely cause.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先看 morphology，不要只看数字：shark-fin shape 代表 airflow obstruction。再结合题干判断最可能原因。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Anesthesiologists, Standards for Basic Anesthetic Monitoring; and Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Capnometry and anaesthesia, Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; describe waveform morphology for obstruction, rebreathing, disconnection, and confirmation of ventilation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The capnogram is shown.","controlSentenceZh":"如下为 capnogram。"}
{"queueIndex":1986,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.516","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.516.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.516.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[255,277],"terminalOffsetsZh":[109,117],"fullStemEn":"A client with a new tracheostomy is being repositioned. The client suddenly becomes restless, the tracheostomy ties appear loose, no air movement is felt from the tracheostomy tube, and the capnogram changes as shown. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名新置 tracheostomy 的患者正在翻身。患者突然烦躁，tracheostomy ties 看起来松脱，从 tracheostomy tube 感觉不到气流，capnogram 变化如下。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Assess the tracheostomy tube position and patency","zh":"评估 tracheostomy tube 的位置和通畅性"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide oxygen and ventilation according to facility emergency tracheostomy protocol","zh":"按照机构 emergency tracheostomy protocol 提供氧气和通气"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the capnogram and reassess in 15 minutes","zh":"记录 capnogram，15 分钟后再评估"},{"id":"F","en":"Increase the humidification setting to loosen secretions","zh":"增加 humidification 设置以稀释分泌物"},{"id":"D","en":"Tape the loosened ties tighter without assessing tube position","zh":"不评估 tube position，直接把松脱的 ties 贴紧"},{"id":"A","en":"Call for immediate help while staying with the client","zh":"立即呼叫协助，同时留在患者身边"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A sudden flat capnogram with no air movement from a new tracheostomy suggests loss of effective ventilation, including possible tube displacement. The nurse should call for help, assess the tube, and provide oxygenation and ventilation per emergency protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新置 tracheostomy 患者突然出现 flat capnogram 且从管口感觉不到气流，提示有效通气丧失，包括可能 tube displacement。护士应呼叫协助、评估管子，并按 emergency protocol 提供氧合和通气。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A flat capnogram is a no-ventilation clue. In a new tracheostomy, prioritize airway help, tube assessment, and oxygenation before comfort measures.","testTakingStrategyZh":"flat capnogram 是 no-ventilation 线索。新置 tracheostomy 时，先处理 airway help、tube assessment 和 oxygenation，再考虑舒适措施。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Anesthesiologists, Standards for Basic Anesthetic Monitoring; and Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Capnometry and anaesthesia, Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; describe waveform morphology for obstruction, rebreathing, disconnection, and confirmation of ventilation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1987,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.517","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.517.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.517.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,274],"terminalOffsetsZh":[105,124],"fullStemEn":"During adult CPR, the client is intubated and receiving continuous waveform capnography. Compressions are ongoing with no planned pause for another 45 seconds. The monitor shows the capnogram below. For each team statement, indicate whether it is supported by the capnogram.","fullStemZh":"成人 CPR 过程中，患者已 intubated，并使用 continuous waveform capnography。胸外按压正在进行，距离下一次计划暂停还有 45 秒。监护仪显示如下 capnogram。请判断每个团队陈述是否受到该波形支持。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each team statement, indicate whether it is supported by the capnogram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每个团队陈述是否受到该波形支持。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The monitor shows the capnogram below.","penultimateSentenceZh":"监护仪显示如下 capnogram。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The abrupt sustained rise suggests possible ROSC.","zh":"EtCO2 突然持续升高提示可能 ROSC。"},{"id":"r2","en":"The team should stop compressions immediately for a prolonged pulse check.","zh":"团队应立即长时间停止胸外按压来检查脉搏。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The finding should be communicated so the team is ready to assess pulse and rhythm at the next appropriate pause.","zh":"应报告该发现，使团队准备在下一次合适暂停时评估 pulse 和 rhythm。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The tracing proves the endotracheal tube has moved into the esophagus.","zh":"该波形证明 endotracheal tube 已进入 esophagus。"}],"columns":[{"id":"supported","en":"Supported","zh":"支持"},{"id":"not_supported","en":"Not supported","zh":"不支持"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["not_supported"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["not_supported"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An abrupt sustained EtCO2 rise during CPR is a cue for possible ROSC. It should be communicated and assessed at an appropriate rhythm or pulse check, without causing an unnecessary prolonged interruption in compressions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CPR 期间 EtCO2 突然持续升高是 possible ROSC 的线索。应将该发现告知团队，并在合适的 rhythm 或 pulse check 时评估，不应造成不必要的长时间按压中断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"During CPR, a sudden sustained EtCO2 jump is a ROSC cue, but NCLEX questions still reward minimizing pauses in compressions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"CPR 期间 EtCO2 突然持续跳升是 ROSC 线索，但 NCLEX 仍重视尽量减少胸外按压暂停。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association Guidelines for CPR and Emergency Cardiovascular Care; abrupt sustained rise in quantitative waveform capnography during CPR is associated with return of spontaneous circulation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1988,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.518","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.518.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.518.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[256,316],"terminalOffsetsZh":[161,175],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving monitored anesthesia care with a circle breathing system. The client is sedated but breathing spontaneously. The anesthesia professional asks the nurse to look at the capnogram because the inspired baseline no longer returns to zero. Which equipment problem is most consistent with the tracing?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受 monitored anesthesia care，并使用 circle breathing system。患者已镇静但仍 spontaneous breathing。anesthesia professional 请护士查看 capnogram，因为 inspired baseline 不再回到零点。哪一种设备问题最符合该波形？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which equipment problem is most consistent with the tracing?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一种设备问题最符合该波形？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The anesthesia professional asks the nurse to look at the capnogram because the inspired baseline no longer returns to zero.","penultimateSentenceZh":"anesthesia professional 请护士查看 capnogram，因为 inspired baseline 不再回到零点。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Acute bronchospasm causing expiratory obstruction","zh":"急性 bronchospasm 造成 expiratory obstruction"},{"id":"A","en":"Exhausted CO2 absorbent allowing rebreathing","zh":"CO2 absorbent 耗尽导致 rebreathing"},{"id":"C","en":"Endotracheal tube cuff leak","zh":"endotracheal tube cuff leak"},{"id":"D","en":"Sudden apnea from oversedation","zh":"过度镇静导致 sudden apnea"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A capnogram baseline that does not return to zero during inspiration indicates inspired CO2 and suggests rebreathing. In a circle system, exhausted CO2 absorbent is a classic equipment cause.","rationaleCorrectZh":"capnogram 的 baseline 在吸气期没有回到零，表示吸入了 CO2，提示 rebreathing。在 circle system 中，CO2 absorbent 耗尽是典型设备原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For rebreathing questions, look for the baseline. Failure to return to zero during inspiration is different from shark-fin obstruction or a flat apnea tracing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"rebreathing 题要看 baseline。吸气期不回到零点，与 shark-fin obstruction 或 flat apnea tracing 不同。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Anesthesiologists, Standards for Basic Anesthetic Monitoring; and Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Capnometry and anaesthesia, Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; describe waveform morphology for obstruction, rebreathing, disconnection, and confirmation of ventilation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1989,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.519","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.519.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.519.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[261,358],"terminalOffsetsZh":[158,200],"fullStemEn":"A client received moderate sedation for a closed reduction. The nurse is evaluating ventilation before transferring the client from the procedure room. Oxygen saturation is 98% on 2 L/min nasal cannula, the client responds to voice, and the capnogram is shown. For each finding, decide whether it supports readiness for continued routine recovery monitoring.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因 closed reduction 接受 moderate sedation。护士在患者离开 procedure room 前评估 ventilation。患者使用 nasal cannula 2 L/min 时 oxygen saturation 为 98%，可对声音作出反应，capnogram 如下。请判断每个发现是否支持继续 routine recovery monitoring。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, decide whether it supports readiness for continued routine recovery monitoring.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每个发现是否支持继续 routine recovery monitoring。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Oxygen saturation is 98% on 2 L/min nasal cannula, the client responds to voice, and the capnogram is shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者使用 nasal cannula 2 L/min 时 oxygen saturation 为 98%，可对声音作出反应，capnogram 如下。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Rectangular waveform with return to baseline","zh":"矩形波形且回到 baseline"},{"id":"r2","en":"EtCO2 in the expected adult range","zh":"EtCO2 在成人预期范围内"},{"id":"r3","en":"Oxygen saturation alone confirms adequate ventilation","zh":"只靠 oxygen saturation 就能确认 ventilation 充足"},{"id":"r4","en":"Persistent shark-fin morphology is present","zh":"存在持续 shark-fin morphology"}],"columns":[{"id":"does_not_support","en":"Does not support routine monitoring","zh":"不支持 routine monitoring"},{"id":"supports","en":"Supports routine monitoring","zh":"支持 routine monitoring"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["supports"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["supports"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["does_not_support"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["does_not_support"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The visual shows a normal rectangular waveform that returns to baseline with EtCO2 38 mmHg and respiratory rate 16/min, supporting adequate ventilation in this context. Oxygen saturation alone is not enough because supplemental oxygen can mask hypoventilation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"波形显示 normal rectangular waveform，能回到 baseline，EtCO2 38 mmHg、respiratory rate 16/min，在此情境支持 adequate ventilation。但只看 oxygen saturation 不够，因为 supplemental oxygen 可能掩盖 hypoventilation。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let a normal SpO2 distract you. Capnography answers ventilation; pulse oximetry answers oxygenation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要被正常 SpO2 分散注意力。capnography 评估 ventilation；pulse oximetry 评估 oxygenation。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Anesthesiologists, Standards for Basic Anesthetic Monitoring; ASA monitoring standards include continual evaluation of ventilation and exhaled CO2 during moderate or deep sedation when appropriate.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1990,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"cap_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.520","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.520.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.520.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[260,282],"terminalOffsetsZh":[139,147],"fullStemEn":"A client is intubated after severe status asthmaticus. Breath sounds are present bilaterally but diminished with prolonged expiration, peak airway pressures are rising, and the capnogram is shown. Which interpretations are supported by the stem and capnogram? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名 severe status asthmaticus 患者完成 intubation。双侧可闻及 breath sounds，但声音减弱且呼气延长，peak airway pressures 正在升高，capnogram 如下。哪些判断受到题干和 capnogram 支持？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interpretations are supported by the stem and capnogram?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些判断受到题干和 capnogram 支持？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The pattern is consistent with persistent bronchospasm.","zh":"该 pattern 符合持续 bronchospasm。"},{"id":"A","en":"The capnogram supports severe lower-airway obstruction.","zh":"该 capnogram 支持严重 lower-airway obstruction。"},{"id":"F","en":"A normal rectangular waveform is present, so ventilation is fully corrected.","zh":"目前存在正常矩形波形，因此 ventilation 已完全纠正。"},{"id":"D","en":"The nurse should anticipate therapy to relieve obstruction, such as prescribed bronchodilator treatment.","zh":"护士应预期使用缓解 obstruction 的治疗，例如医嘱 bronchodilator treatment。"},{"id":"E","en":"The bilateral breath sounds and repeated CO2 waves make right mainstem intubation the best explanation.","zh":"双侧 breath sounds 和重复 CO2 波形使 right mainstem intubation 成为最佳解释。"},{"id":"C","en":"The endotracheal tube is most likely in the esophagus.","zh":"endotracheal tube 最可能在 esophagus。"}],"correct":["A","B","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The severe shark-fin waveform, prolonged expiration, bilateral diminished breath sounds, and rising peak pressures support persistent obstructive physiology after intubation. The nurse should anticipate prescribed bronchodilator or obstruction-relieving therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"严重 shark-fin waveform、呼气延长、双侧 breath sounds 减弱和 peak pressures 升高，支持 intubation 后仍有 obstructive physiology。护士应预期使用医嘱 bronchodilator 或其他缓解 obstruction 的治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After intubation, do not automatically blame tube placement. If bilateral breath sounds are present and the waveform is shark-fin, think obstruction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"intubation 后不要自动归咎于 tube placement。若双侧 breath sounds 存在且波形是 shark-fin，要想到 obstruction。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Anesthesiologists, Standards for Basic Anesthetic Monitoring; and Bhavani-Shankar K et al., Capnometry and anaesthesia, Canadian Journal of Anaesthesia, 1992; describe waveform morphology for obstruction, rebreathing, disconnection, and confirmation of ventilation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1991,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.521","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.521.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.521.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,89],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is 3 hours postoperative after an abdominal hysterectomy. The dressing has a small new area of sanguineous drainage. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者 abdominal hysterectomy 术后 3 小时。敷料上出现一小片新的 sanguineous drainage。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪项措施最优先？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施最优先？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Assist the client to sit in a chair to prevent postoperative atelectasis.","zh":"协助患者坐到椅子上，以预防术后 atelectasis。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the prescribed opioid analgesic and reassess the incision after pain improves.","zh":"给予医嘱的 opioid analgesic，并在疼痛改善后重新评估切口。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the surgeon or activate the facility escalation process and prepare for fluid or blood replacement.","zh":"通知 surgeon 或启动机构 escalation process，并准备进行 fluid 或 blood replacement。"},{"id":"A","en":"Reinforce the dressing and recheck the vital signs at the next scheduled interval.","zh":"加固敷料，并在下一次常规时间重新测量生命体征。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows rising heart rate with falling systolic pressure and a narrowing pulse pressure after surgery. Even though the visible drainage is described as small, the serial vital signs suggest evolving postoperative hemorrhage and require urgent escalation and preparation for volume replacement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示术后 heart rate 上升、systolic pressure 下降，并且 pulse pressure 逐渐变窄。虽然可见引流量描述为少量，但连续生命体征提示 postoperative hemorrhage 正在进展，需要紧急升级处理并准备补充容量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let the word small in the dressing description distract you. In a postoperative client, compare the serial HR, SBP, and pulse pressure; a narrowing pulse pressure with tachycardia is a bleeding warning.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要被敷料描述里的“少量”分散注意。术后患者要连续比较 HR、SBP 和 pulse pressure；tachycardia 加 pulse pressure 变窄是出血警讯。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Hypovolemic Shock, updated 2025: severe hemorrhage/hypovolemia can present with tachycardia, systolic hypotension, and narrowed pulse pressure; MSD Manual Professional Shock, 2026: shock manifests as tissue hypoperfusion with tachycardia, hypotension, and oliguria.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1992,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.522","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.522.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.522.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[297,319],"terminalOffsetsZh":[179,187],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with an indwelling urinary catheter has suspected catheter-associated urinary tract infection. Orders are available for blood cultures, serum lactate, broad-spectrum antibiotics, and isotonic IV fluids. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名留置 urinary catheter 的成人患者疑似 catheter-associated urinary tract infection。已有 blood cultures、serum lactate、broad-spectrum antibiotics 和 isotonic IV fluids 的医嘱。护士查看生命体征趋势。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Ambulate the client in the hallway to reduce the risk of atelectasis.","zh":"协助患者在走廊 ambulate，以降低 atelectasis 风险。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the facility sepsis escalation process or notify the provider promptly.","zh":"启动机构 sepsis escalation process，或立即通知 provider。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give acetaminophen and wait 4 hours before reassessing because fever explains the trend.","zh":"给予 acetaminophen 并等待 4 小时后再评估，因为 fever 可以解释这个趋势。"},{"id":"E","en":"Start the ordered isotonic IV fluid bolus and reassess perfusion indicators.","zh":"开始医嘱的 isotonic IV fluid bolus，并重新评估 perfusion 指标。"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold the broad-spectrum antibiotic until the final urine culture report is available.","zh":"等最终 urine culture 报告出来后再给予 broad-spectrum antibiotic。"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain the ordered lactate and blood cultures promptly without delaying antibiotic administration.","zh":"及时取得医嘱的 lactate 和 blood cultures，但不要因此延误 antibiotic administration。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows infection-associated deterioration: HR and RR rise while MAP falls to 64 mm Hg. This pattern requires sepsis escalation, timely cultures and lactate when ordered, prompt antibiotics, and fluid resuscitation rather than delayed reassessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示感染相关恶化：HR 和 RR 上升，同时 MAP 下降到 64 mm Hg。这种模式需要 sepsis 升级处理、按医嘱及时抽取 cultures 和 lactate、迅速给予 antibiotics，并进行 fluid resuscitation，而不是延迟复评。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For suspected infection, look for the cluster, not one number: rising HR, rising RR, fever, and falling MAP together point toward sepsis progression.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到疑似感染，要看“组合”而不是单个数字：HR 上升、RR 上升、fever 和 MAP 下降一起出现，指向 sepsis 进展。","sourceMetadata":"CDC About Sepsis, updated March 23, 2026: sepsis warning findings include fever, fast heart rate, low blood pressure, and difficulty breathing; Surviving Sepsis Campaign adult guidelines: septic shock resuscitation uses MAP around 65 mm Hg and prompt antimicrobials/resuscitation.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1993,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.523","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.523.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.523.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,228],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,103],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with acute pancreatitis and repeated vomiting receives an ordered isotonic IV fluid bolus. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend after the bolus. For each statement, select whether it is supported by the trend.","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者有 acute pancreatitis 和反复 vomiting，按医嘱接受 isotonic IV fluid bolus。护士查看补液后的生命体征趋势。对每个陈述，选择它是否得到趋势支持。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each statement, select whether it is supported by the trend.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每个陈述，选择它是否得到趋势支持。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend after the bolus.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看补液后的生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Perfusion is improving after the fluid bolus.","zh":"fluid bolus 后 perfusion 正在改善。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hypotension is worsening despite the fluid bolus.","zh":"尽管给予 fluid bolus，hypotension 仍在恶化。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Tachycardia is resolving rather than progressing.","zh":"tachycardia 正在缓解，而不是继续进展。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client is stable enough for discharge based on this trend alone.","zh":"仅根据这个趋势，患者已经稳定到可以 discharge。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Respiratory rate is moving toward the expected adult range.","zh":"respiratory rate 正在向成人预期范围靠近。"}],"columns":[{"id":"not_supported","en":"Not supported by trend","zh":"趋势不支持"},{"id":"supported","en":"Supported by trend","zh":"趋势支持"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["not_supported"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["not_supported"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["supported"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After the fluid bolus, MAP rises, SBP rises, HR falls, and RR falls. This supports an improving response to volume replacement, but the trend alone does not justify discharge from care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"fluid bolus 后，MAP 上升、SBP 上升、HR 下降、RR 下降。这支持患者对 volume replacement 反应改善，但仅凭这个趋势不能说明可以出院。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For response-to-intervention items, compare the same variables before and after the intervention. Improvement should show movement in several related values, not just one isolated reading.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到 response-to-intervention 题，要比较 intervention 前后的同一组指标。真正改善通常是多个相关数值一起好转，而不是单一读数。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Hypovolemic Shock, updated 2025: hypovolemia can manifest with tachycardia and hypotension, and management includes restoring circulating volume; MSD Manual Professional Shock, 2026: shock assessment centers on tissue perfusion and hemodynamic response.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1994,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.524","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.524.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.524.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[217,246],"terminalOffsetsZh":[104,112],"fullStemEn":"An adult client developed hives, wheezing, and hypotension shortly after receiving an IV antibiotic. The infusion was stopped, and IM epinephrine and oxygen were administered. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which interpretation is best?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者接受 IV antibiotic 后不久出现 hives、wheezing 和 hypotension。输液已停止，并已给予 IM epinephrine 和 oxygen。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪项解释最恰当？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项解释最恰当？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The client is deteriorating because the heart rate remains above 100 at 15 minutes; prepare atropine.","zh":"患者正在恶化，因为 15 分钟时 heart rate 仍超过 100；准备 atropine。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client is responding to treatment; continue close monitoring and be prepared to repeat epinephrine if airway, breathing, or circulation problems recur.","zh":"患者正在对治疗产生反应；继续密切 monitoring，并准备在 airway、breathing 或 circulation 问题复发时重复给予 epinephrine。"},{"id":"D","en":"The trend most strongly suggests septic shock rather than an allergic reaction.","zh":"这个趋势最强烈提示 septic shock，而不是 allergic reaction。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client is fully stabilized; discontinue pulse oximetry and blood pressure monitoring.","zh":"患者已完全稳定；停止 pulse oximetry 和 blood pressure monitoring。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend after epinephrine shows improving circulation and oxygenation: SBP and MAP rise, SpO2 rises, RR falls, and HR decreases. This supports a positive response, but anaphylaxis still requires close monitoring because symptoms can recur.","rationaleCorrectZh":"epinephrine 后的趋势显示 circulation 和 oxygenation 改善：SBP 和 MAP 上升、SpO2 上升、RR 下降、HR 下降。这支持治疗反应良好，但 anaphylaxis 仍需密切 monitoring，因为症状可能复发。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an intervention has already been given, ask whether several linked values moved in the right direction. In anaphylaxis, improved BP, SpO2, RR, and HR after epinephrine support response, not discharge from monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干已经给出 intervention，要判断多个相关数值是否朝正确方向变化。anaphylaxis 中，epinephrine 后 BP、SpO2、RR 和 HR 改善支持治疗有效，但不等于可以停止 monitoring。","sourceMetadata":"World Allergy Organization Anaphylaxis Guidance 2020 and Resuscitation Council UK Emergency Treatment of Anaphylaxis Guidelines 2021: IM epinephrine is first-line treatment, response is assessed with vital sign monitoring, and repeat IM epinephrine is indicated if airway/breathing/circulation problems persist.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1995,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.525","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.525.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.525.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[214,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[102,110],"fullStemEn":"An adult client admitted with an acute myocardial infarction reports worsening shortness of breath. The nurse notes new crackles at both lung bases and reviews the vital signs trend. Which actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名因 acute myocardial infarction 入院的成人患者报告 shortness of breath 加重。护士听到双肺底新出现 crackles，并查看生命体征趋势。哪些措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Apply or titrate oxygen as prescribed and continue close SpO2 monitoring.","zh":"按医嘱给予或调整 oxygen，并继续密切监测 SpO2。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the provider or rapid response team because the trend suggests worsening shock.","zh":"通知 provider 或 rapid response team，因为趋势提示 shock 正在恶化。"},{"id":"E","en":"Assess perfusion, lung sounds, and urine output while preparing for prescribed cardiac support therapies.","zh":"评估 perfusion、lung sounds 和 urine output，同时准备执行医嘱的 cardiac support therapies。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document that the findings are expected after myocardial infarction and reassess at the next routine vital-sign time.","zh":"记录这些发现是 myocardial infarction 后预期情况，并在下次常规生命体征时间复评。"},{"id":"F","en":"Encourage oral fluids to improve blood pressure because the oxygen level is only mildly low.","zh":"鼓励口服液体以改善血压，因为 oxygen level 只是轻度偏低。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give a rapid 1 L isotonic fluid bolus because all shock states are treated first with large-volume fluids.","zh":"快速给予 1 L isotonic fluid bolus，因为所有 shock 状态都应先大量补液。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In the setting of acute MI with new crackles, the trend of falling MAP/SBP, rising HR/RR, and falling SpO2 suggests cardiogenic shock or acute heart failure deterioration. The nurse should escalate care, support oxygenation, and assess perfusion while preparing for prescribed cardiac therapies.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 acute MI 且出现新 crackles 的背景下，MAP/SBP 下降、HR/RR 上升、SpO2 下降的趋势提示 cardiogenic shock 或 acute heart failure 恶化。护士应升级处理、支持 oxygenation，并评估 perfusion，同时准备执行医嘱的 cardiac therapies。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the stem to classify the shock type. MI plus crackles changes the action: falling BP with falling SpO2 is not an automatic fluid-bolus question.","testTakingStrategyZh":"用题干判断 shock 类型。MI 加 crackles 会改变处理方向：血压下降同时 SpO2 下降，并不自动等于大量补液题。","sourceMetadata":"MSD Manual Professional Shock, updated 2026: shock is tissue hypoperfusion with tachycardia, hypotension, and organ dysfunction; MSD Manual Professional Pulmonary Edema, 2025: cardiogenic pulmonary edema causes severe dyspnea, diaphoresis, wheezing/crackles, and hypoxemia.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1996,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t02_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.526","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.526.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.526.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[199,294],"terminalOffsetsZh":[123,146],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with a gastrointestinal bleed received a rapid response evaluation and is receiving prescribed packed red blood cells and isotonic IV fluids. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. For each nursing interpretation or action, select whether it is appropriate based on the trend.","fullStemZh":"一名 gastrointestinal bleed 成人患者已接受 rapid response evaluation，正在按医嘱输注 packed red blood cells 和 isotonic IV fluids。护士查看生命体征趋势。对每个护理判断或措施，选择它是否基于趋势合适。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nursing interpretation or action, select whether it is appropriate based on the trend.","terminalSentenceZh":"对每个护理判断或措施，选择它是否基于趋势合适。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Interpret the trend as an improving hemodynamic response to replacement therapy.","zh":"将该趋势解释为 replacement therapy 后 hemodynamic response 改善。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Stop the blood transfusion because the trend shows a transfusion reaction.","zh":"停止输血，因为趋势显示 transfusion reaction。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Continue close monitoring and reassess perfusion indicators such as mentation and urine output.","zh":"继续密切 monitoring，并复评 perfusion 指标，例如 mentation 和 urine output。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Prepare for emergency escalation because MAP is progressively falling below 65 mm Hg.","zh":"准备紧急升级处理，因为 MAP 正逐渐降到 65 mm Hg 以下。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Ambulate the client to the bathroom because the trend has completely normalized.","zh":"协助患者走到厕所，因为趋势已经完全 normal。"}],"columns":[{"id":"appropriate","en":"Appropriate based on trend","zh":"基于趋势合适"},{"id":"not_appropriate","en":"Not appropriate based on trend","zh":"基于趋势不合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["not_appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["not_appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["not_appropriate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows improvement after replacement therapy: MAP and SBP rise, HR and RR fall, SpO2 is stable, and temperature does not show a concerning rise. The client still needs close monitoring because hemorrhage can recur and improvement does not mean full normalization.","rationaleCorrectZh":"replacement therapy 后趋势显示改善：MAP 和 SBP 上升，HR 和 RR 下降，SpO2 稳定，体温没有明显上升。患者仍需密切 monitoring，因为 hemorrhage 可能复发，改善并不等于完全 normal。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Improving does not mean normal. In hemorrhage response items, look for MAP rising and HR falling, then choose continued monitoring rather than unsafe activity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"“改善”不等于“正常”。hemorrhage response 题要找 MAP 上升、HR 下降，然后选择继续 monitoring，而不是不安全的活动。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI StatPearls Hypovolemic Shock, updated 2025: hemorrhagic hypovolemia may cause tachycardia, hypotension, and narrowed pulse pressure, and management requires restoring circulating volume; MSD Manual Professional Shock, 2026: hemodynamic improvement should be interpreted with perfusion assessment.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1997,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.527","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.527.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.527.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[165,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,123],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with pneumonia received IV antibiotics and acetaminophen 4 hours ago. The client now says, \"I feel weaker.\" The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. For each finding, select whether it is an escalation cue or insufficient reassurance.","fullStemZh":"一名成人 pneumonia 患者 4 小时前已给予 IV antibiotics 和 acetaminophen。患者现在说：\"我觉得更虚弱。\" 护士查看生命体征趋势。针对每个发现，选择它是 escalation cue，还是不足以让护士放心。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, select whether it is an escalation cue or insufficient reassurance.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每个发现，选择它是 escalation cue，还是不足以让护士放心。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Heart rate and respiratory rate rise across the same time window.","zh":"同一时间段内 heart rate 和 respiratory rate 持续上升。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Temperature moves closer to normal after acetaminophen.","zh":"使用 acetaminophen 后 temperature 接近正常。"},{"id":"r3","en":"MAP falls from the first to the last reading.","zh":"MAP 从第一次读数到最后一次读数下降。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The final MAP is still above 65 mm Hg.","zh":"最后一次 MAP 仍高于 65 mm Hg。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Insufficient reassurance","zh":"不足以让护士放心"},{"id":"c1","en":"Escalation cue","zh":"需要升级处理的线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The fever is lower, but the full trend shows rising HR and RR with a falling MAP and slight oxygenation decline. In a client with pneumonia, this pattern is more concerning for sepsis progression than for recovery from infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"虽然 fever 降低，但完整趋势显示 HR 和 RR 上升、MAP 下降，并且氧合略有下降。对于 pneumonia 患者，这种模式更像 sepsis progression，而不是感染正在好转。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not anchor on the improved temperature. In infection questions, compare the whole trend: HR, RR, MAP, and oxygenation can show deterioration even when fever temporarily improves.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只盯着体温改善。感染题要比较完整趋势：即使 fever 暂时下降，HR、RR、MAP 和氧合也可能显示病情恶化。","sourceMetadata":"CDC About Sepsis, 2026: signs include high heart rate, shortness of breath, confusion, fever or feeling very cold; Surviving Sepsis Campaign 2021/Red Cross sepsis guidance uses MAP around 65 mm Hg as a key septic shock perfusion threshold.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1998,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.528","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.528.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.528.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[203,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[82,90],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is 2 hours after a vaginal birth. The fundus is boggy at the umbilicus, and lochia is described as moderate. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名成人产妇 vaginal birth 后 2 小时。fundus 位于脐部且 boggy，lochia 描述为中等量。护士查看生命体征趋势。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Quantify blood loss and continue frequent fundal and vital-sign assessments.","zh":"量化 blood loss，并继续频繁评估 fundus 和 vital signs。"},{"id":"A","en":"Call for assistance and massage the fundus while reassessing bleeding.","zh":"呼叫协助，并按摩 fundus，同时重新评估出血。"},{"id":"B","en":"Maintain large-bore IV access and prepare prescribed uterotonic medication or fluid replacement.","zh":"维持大口径 IV access，并准备医嘱的 uterotonic medication 或 fluid replacement。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assist the client to shower because the lochia is not described as heavy.","zh":"协助产妇淋浴，因为 lochia 并未描述为大量。"},{"id":"E","en":"Notify the obstetric provider or activate the postpartum hemorrhage escalation process.","zh":"通知 obstetric provider 或启动 postpartum hemorrhage escalation process。"},{"id":"F","en":"Document the trend as expected postpartum physiologic adjustment and recheck in 4 hours.","zh":"将该趋势记录为预期的产后生理调整，并 4 小时后复查。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows rising HR, falling SBP and MAP, and a narrowing pulse pressure in a client with a boggy uterus. Moderate visible lochia can underestimate blood loss. These data support urgent postpartum hemorrhage actions, including fundal massage, escalation, quantitative blood loss assessment, and preparation for uterotonics and volume replacement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示 HR 上升、SBP 和 MAP 下降、pulse pressure 变窄，而且患者 fundus boggy。可见 lochia 为中等量可能低估实际失血。数据支持立即按 postpartum hemorrhage 处理，包括 fundal massage、升级处理、量化失血，并准备 uterotonics 与补容量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Postpartum bleeding can be hidden. When the fundus is boggy, trend HR, BP, MAP, and pulse pressure instead of relying only on the word moderate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产后出血可能被低估。fundus boggy 时，要看 HR、BP、MAP 和 pulse pressure 的趋势，不要只依赖“中等量”这个词。","sourceMetadata":"AAFP Postpartum Hemorrhage: Prevention and Treatment, 2017: tachycardia may be the earliest sign of postpartum hemorrhage and quantitative blood loss plus vital sign tracking are recommended; StatPearls Postpartum Hemorrhage, 2024: uterine massage and uterotonic medications are core treatment for atony-related hemorrhage.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":1999,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.529","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.529.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.529.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[184,239],"terminalOffsetsZh":[98,109],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is admitted with black, tarry stools and dizziness when standing. The client denies chest pain or shortness of breath at rest. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which interpretation is most consistent with the trend?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者因 black, tarry stools 和站立时 dizziness 入院。患者否认静息时 chest pain 或 shortness of breath。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪项解释最符合该趋势？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which interpretation is most consistent with the trend?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项解释最符合该趋势？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Compensated hypovolemic shock is progressing toward decompensation from gastrointestinal blood loss.","zh":"由于 gastrointestinal blood loss，compensated hypovolemic shock 正在向 decompensation 进展。"},{"id":"D","en":"Opioid-induced respiratory depression is the priority interpretation.","zh":"opioid-induced respiratory depression 是优先解释。"},{"id":"B","en":"The trend is most consistent with pain-related anxiety because oxygen saturation remains acceptable.","zh":"该趋势最符合疼痛相关 anxiety，因为 oxygen saturation 仍可接受。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client is improving because the systolic blood pressure stays above 90 mm Hg until the last reading.","zh":"患者正在好转，因为 systolic blood pressure 到最后一次之前都保持在 90 mm Hg 以上。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend requires comparing serial readings: HR rises, SBP and MAP fall, RR rises, and pulse pressure narrows in a client with melena and orthostatic symptoms. This is most consistent with evolving hypovolemia from gastrointestinal bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这题必须比较连续读数：患者有 melena 和站立 dizziness，同时 HR 上升、SBP 和 MAP 下降、RR 上升、pulse pressure 变窄。最符合 gastrointestinal bleeding 导致的 hypovolemia 进展。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Shock can begin before one dramatic low blood pressure reading. Track compensation: rising HR and RR plus narrowing pulse pressure are more important than one acceptable earlier SBP.","testTakingStrategyZh":"shock 可在出现明显低血压前开始。要追踪代偿：HR 和 RR 上升、pulse pressure 变窄，比早期某一次 SBP 还可以更重要。","sourceMetadata":"StatPearls Hypovolemia and Hypovolemic Shock, 2025: hypovolemic shock results from reduced blood volume impairing cardiac output and tissue perfusion; MSD Manual Professional Shock, 2026: shock commonly presents with tachycardia, hypotension, and signs of tissue hypoperfusion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2000,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.530","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.530.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.530.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,70],"fullStemEn":"An adult postoperative client became difficult to arouse after receiving IV morphine. Naloxone was administered at time 0. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which evaluation is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"一名成人术后患者接受 IV morphine 后变得难以唤醒。time 0 时给予 naloxone。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪项评价最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which evaluation is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项评价最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The opioid can be resumed at the same dose now because oxygen saturation has normalized.","zh":"现在可以按原剂量恢复 opioid，因为 oxygen saturation 已恢复正常。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client has failed to respond to naloxone because the heart rate increased slightly.","zh":"患者对 naloxone 无反应，因为 heart rate 略有上升。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client requires immediate chest compressions because respiratory rate was initially 6/min.","zh":"患者需要立即 chest compressions，因为最初 respiratory rate 为 6/min。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client shows improved ventilation and oxygenation, but continued monitoring is needed for recurrent respiratory depression.","zh":"患者 ventilation 和 oxygenation 改善，但仍需继续监测是否出现 recurrent respiratory depression。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After naloxone, RR rises from severely low to an adult range and SpO2 improves from 84% to 96%. The trend supports an effective response, but naloxone can wear off before some opioids, so continued surveillance is necessary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"给予 naloxone 后，RR 从严重偏低升至成人范围，SpO2 从 84% 改善到 96%。趋势支持有效反应，但 naloxone 的作用时间可能短于某些 opioids，因此仍需继续观察。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For response-to-intervention questions, compare before and after the treatment. Improvement does not always mean the risk is gone; think about drug duration and recurrence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"response-to-intervention 题要比较治疗前后。改善不等于风险消失；要想到药物作用时间和复发。","sourceMetadata":"FDA naloxone nasal spray labeling, 2023/2024: monitor the patient and re-administer naloxone if the patient responds and then relapses into respiratory depression; StatPearls Naloxone, 2024: naloxone reverses opioid-induced respiratory depression.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2001,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.531","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.531.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.531.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,275],"terminalOffsetsZh":[112,158],"fullStemEn":"A 47-year-old adult with septic shock from perforated appendicitis received an initial crystalloid bolus. Norepinephrine was started at time 0. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. For each interpretation or action, select whether it is appropriate or unsafe/unsupported.","fullStemZh":"一名 47 岁成人因 perforated appendicitis 发生 septic shock，已接受初始 crystalloid bolus。time 0 时开始 norepinephrine。护士查看生命体征趋势。针对每项解释或措施，选择 appropriate 或 unsafe/unsupported。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each interpretation or action, select whether it is appropriate or unsafe/unsupported.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项解释或措施，选择 appropriate 或 unsafe/unsupported。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Recognize the MAP, HR, and RR trends as an improved hemodynamic response.","zh":"将 MAP、HR 和 RR 趋势识别为 hemodynamic response 改善。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Continue titrating norepinephrine per protocol while monitoring perfusion.","zh":"按 protocol 继续 titrate norepinephrine，并监测 perfusion。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Stop antimicrobial therapy because the blood pressure has improved.","zh":"因为血压改善，停止 antimicrobial therapy。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Assume source control is complete because the temperature decreased slightly.","zh":"因为 temperature 略有下降，就认定 source control 已完成。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Unsafe or unsupported","zh":"不安全或证据不足"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend after norepinephrine shows MAP rising from below 65 to above 65 with HR and RR decreasing, which supports improved hemodynamics. However, vital-sign improvement does not mean infection treatment or source control is complete.","rationaleCorrectZh":"开始 norepinephrine 后，趋势显示 MAP 从低于 65 升至高于 65，HR 和 RR 下降，支持 hemodynamics 改善。但生命体征改善并不代表感染治疗或 source control 已完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate perfusion response from infection control. MAP and HR can improve after a vasopressor while the client still needs antibiotics, source control, and close monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要区分 perfusion response 和 infection control。使用 vasopressor 后 MAP 与 HR 可以改善，但患者仍需要 antibiotics、source control 和密切监测。","sourceMetadata":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign 2021: norepinephrine is recommended as a first-line vasopressor for adults with septic shock and an initial MAP target around 65 mm Hg is used for resuscitation; Red Cross sepsis guidance references persistent MAP less than 65 mm Hg in vasopressor escalation decisions.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the vital signs trend.","controlSentenceZh":"护士查看生命体征趋势。"}
{"queueIndex":2002,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_gpt_2026_07_02_t03_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.532","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.532.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.532.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[241,263],"terminalOffsetsZh":[114,122],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is 3 hours after a transfemoral cardiac catheterization. The groin dressing is dry, but the client reports new lower back and flank pain. The nurse reviews the vital signs trend. Which conclusions or actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者 transfemoral cardiac catheterization 后 3 小时。腹股沟敷料干燥，但患者报告新的 lower back 和 flank pain。护士查看生命体征趋势。哪些判断或措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which conclusions or actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些判断或措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Reassure the client that the dry dressing rules out significant bleeding.","zh":"安慰患者敷料干燥已经排除 significant bleeding。"},{"id":"B","en":"Keep the client on bed rest and promptly notify the provider or rapid response team.","zh":"让患者保持 bed rest，并立即通知 provider 或 rapid response team。"},{"id":"A","en":"Suspect occult internal bleeding such as retroperitoneal hematoma despite the dry dressing.","zh":"即使敷料干燥，也应怀疑 occult internal bleeding，例如 retroperitoneal hematoma。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer only the prescribed analgesic and reassess during routine rounds.","zh":"只给予医嘱 analgesic，并在常规查房时复查。"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare for IV fluid or blood replacement as ordered while continuing neurovascular and site assessment.","zh":"按医嘱准备 IV fluid 或 blood replacement，同时继续 neurovascular 和穿刺部位评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows rising HR and RR with falling SBP, MAP, and narrowing pulse pressure after a femoral-access procedure. New back or flank pain with a dry groin dressing can indicate occult retroperitoneal bleeding, which requires urgent escalation and preparation for volume replacement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示 femoral-access procedure 后 HR 和 RR 上升，SBP、MAP 下降，pulse pressure 变窄。出现新的 back 或 flank pain，即使腹股沟敷料干燥，也可能提示 occult retroperitoneal bleeding，需要紧急升级处理并准备补容量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a procedure site looks clean but the trend shows shock, think about hidden bleeding. New flank or back pain after femoral access is a key disambiguator.","testTakingStrategyZh":"如果操作部位看起来干净，但趋势显示 shock，要想到 hidden bleeding。femoral access 后新的 flank 或 back pain 是关键限制线索。","sourceMetadata":"StatPearls Retroperitoneal Hematoma, 2024/2025: retroperitoneal bleeding can be occult and under-recognized until substantial blood loss; StatPearls Cardiac Catheterization Risks and Complications, 2023: large hematomas after catheterization can cause hemodynamic instability requiring fluids and blood.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2003,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_1344_t1_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.533","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.533.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.533.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[302,323],"terminalOffsetsZh":[112,117],"fullStemEn":"A 22-year-old client with type 1 diabetes arrives with vomiting, abdominal pain, deep rapid respirations, and dry mucous membranes. Laboratory results: glucose 428 mg/dL, pH 7.22, bicarbonate 12 mEq/L, beta-hydroxybutyrate positive, potassium 5.6 mEq/L, sodium 132 mEq/L. The client is alert but weak. Complete the diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名22岁1型糖尿病患者因呕吐、腹痛、深而快的呼吸和黏膜干燥就诊。实验室结果：血糖428 mg/dL，pH 7.22，碳酸氢盐12 mEq/L，β-羟丁酸阳性，血钾5.6 mEq/L，血钠132 mEq/L。患者清醒但虚弱。完成图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is alert but weak.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者清醒但虚弱。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_dka","en":"Diabetic ketoacidosis","zh":"糖尿病酮症酸中毒"},{"id":"c_hhs","en":"Hyperosmolar hyperglycemic state","zh":"高渗高血糖状态"},{"id":"c_resp_alk","en":"Respiratory alkalosis from anxiety","zh":"焦虑导致的呼吸性碱中毒"}],"correct":"c_dka"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_restrict","en":"Restrict oral and IV fluids until glucose normalizes","zh":"在血糖恢复正常前限制口服和静脉液体"},{"id":"a_insulin","en":"Prepare the prescribed regular insulin infusion","zh":"准备医嘱的常规胰岛素输注"},{"id":"a_bicarb","en":"Administer sodium bicarbonate routinely before fluids","zh":"在补液前常规给予碳酸氢钠"},{"id":"a_fluids","en":"Start isotonic IV fluid replacement as prescribed","zh":"按医嘱开始等渗静脉补液"}],"correct":["a_fluids","a_insulin"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_lipase","en":"Serum lipase alone","zh":"仅监测血清脂肪酶"},{"id":"p_peak_flow","en":"Peak expiratory flow","zh":"呼气峰流速"},{"id":"p_k","en":"Serum potassium","zh":"血清钾"},{"id":"p_gap_glucose","en":"Glucose trend and anion gap","zh":"血糖趋势和阴离子间隙"}],"correct":["p_k","p_gap_glucose"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hyperglycemia with metabolic acidosis, low bicarbonate, ketones, dehydration, abdominal pain, and Kussmaul-type respirations supports diabetic ketoacidosis. Initial management includes isotonic fluid replacement and insulin therapy while closely monitoring potassium and closure of the anion gap.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高血糖伴代谢性酸中毒、碳酸氢盐降低、酮体阳性、脱水、腹痛和库斯莫尔样呼吸，支持糖尿病酮症酸中毒。初始处理包括等渗补液和胰岛素治疗，同时密切监测血钾以及阴离子间隙是否闭合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the acid-base pattern to the action: ketones plus low bicarbonate point to DKA, then think fluids, insulin, potassium, and gap closure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将酸碱模式与措施相匹配：酮体阳性加碳酸氢盐降低指向DKA，然后考虑补液、胰岛素、钾和阴离子间隙闭合。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2004,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_1344_t1_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.534","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.534.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.534.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,134],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings in the nurse's note that require prompt follow-up for possible acute kidney injury or electrolyte complication.","fullStemZh":"标出护士记录中需要及时跟进、提示可能急性肾损伤或电解质并发症的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings in the nurse's note that require prompt follow-up for possible acute kidney injury or electrolyte complication.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出护士记录中需要及时跟进、提示可能急性肾损伤或电解质并发症的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"0730 note: Client is 12 hours after a colectomy.","zh":"0730记录：患者结肠切除术后12小时。"},{"id":"s2","en":"Urine output has been 18 mL total over the last 3 hours.","zh":"过去3小时总尿量为18毫升。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Serum creatinine increased from 0.9 to 1.8 mg/dL since admission.","zh":"血清肌酐自入院以来从0.9升至1.8 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Potassium is 5.9 mEq/L.","zh":"血钾为5.9 mEq/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The abdominal dressing has a 2 cm area of dried serosanguineous drainage.","zh":"腹部敷料有2厘米范围的干燥浆血性渗液。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client reports incisional pain of 4 out of 10 after repositioning.","zh":"翻身后患者报告切口疼痛4/10。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Very low urine output, a doubled creatinine, and hyperkalemia are concerning for acute kidney injury with an electrolyte complication. A small area of dried postoperative drainage and moderate incisional pain after repositioning require routine assessment but are not the urgent renal cues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尿量明显减少、肌酐翻倍和高钾血症提示急性肾损伤并伴电解质并发症风险。少量干燥术后渗液和翻身后的中等切口疼痛需要常规评估，但不是紧急肾脏线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In highlight items, separate urgent physiologic trend cues from expected postoperative findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做标记题时，将紧急生理趋势线索与预期术后发现区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2005,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_1344_t1_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.535","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.535.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.535.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[499,548],"terminalOffsetsZh":[143,160],"fullStemEn":"A client in the emergency department said, 'I am going to take all these pills when I leave.' The nurse stayed with the client, called for help, and the pill bottle has been removed from the client's access. The facility protocol says that after immediate safety is secured, the nurse should complete a focused suicide risk assessment, activate suicide safety precautions, notify the provider or crisis team with the assessed risk, give a safety handoff to the observation staff, and then document. Place the next nursing actions in protocol order.","fullStemZh":"急诊科一名患者曾说：“我离开后就把这些药全吃了。”护士已留在患者身边、呼叫协助，并且药瓶已从患者可接触范围内移除。机构流程规定，在即时安全得到保障后，护士应先完成重点自杀风险评估，启动自杀安全预防措施，将评估出的风险通知医护提供者或危机团队，向负责观察的工作人员进行安全交接，然后记录。请按流程顺序排列接下来的护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the next nursing actions in protocol order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按流程顺序排列接下来的护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility protocol says that after immediate safety is secured, the nurse should complete a focused suicide risk assessment, activate suicide safety precautions, notify the provider or crisis team with the assessed risk, give a safety handoff to the observation staff, and then document.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构流程规定，在即时安全得到保障后，护士应先完成重点自杀风险评估，启动自杀安全预防措施，将评估出的风险通知医护提供者或危机团队，向负责观察的工作人员进行安全交接，然后记录。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Document the assessment findings, safety precautions, notifications, handoff, and client response.","zh":"记录评估发现、安全预防措施、通知情况、交接内容和患者反应。"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask directly about current intent, plan details, access to additional means, prior attempts, substance use, and protective supports.","zh":"直接询问目前意图、计划细节、是否还能接触其他手段、既往尝试、物质使用以及保护性支持。"},{"id":"B","en":"Activate suicide safety precautions, including continuous observation and environmental safety measures.","zh":"启动自杀安全预防措施，包括持续观察和环境安全措施。"},{"id":"D","en":"Give a safety handoff to the observation staff, including statements, means removed, and cues that require escalation.","zh":"向负责观察的工作人员进行安全交接，包括患者陈述、已移除的手段以及需要升级处理的线索。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider or crisis evaluation team of the assessed risk and actions already taken.","zh":"将评估出的风险和已采取的措施通知医护提供者或危机评估团队。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stem states that immediate safety has already been secured and gives the facility's next-step protocol. The nurse first completes the focused suicide risk assessment, then activates safety precautions, notifies the provider or crisis team with the assessed risk, gives the safety handoff to observation staff, and documents the assessment and actions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干说明即时安全已经得到保障，并给出了机构后续步骤流程。护士先完成重点自杀风险评估，然后启动安全预防措施，将评估出的风险通知医护提供者或危机团队，向观察工作人员进行安全交接，最后记录评估和措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For ordered-response safety items, identify what has already been done in the stem, then follow the stated protocol before documenting.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做安全类排序题时，先确认题干中哪些措施已经完成，再按给出的流程执行，最后记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2006,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_1344_t1_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.536","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.536.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.536.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[178,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,75],"fullStemEn":"The prescription is heparin 1,200 units/hour IV. The infusion bag contains heparin 25,000 units in 500 mL of D5W. At how many mL/hour should the nurse program the infusion pump? Round to the nearest whole number.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为肝素每小时1,200单位静脉输注。输液袋含肝素25,000单位，溶于500毫升D5W。护士应将输液泵设为每小时多少毫升？四舍五入到最接近的整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At how many mL/hour should the nurse program the infusion pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将输液泵设为每小时多少毫升？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hour","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["24","24 mL/hour","24 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":24,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hour"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The concentration is 25,000 units/500 mL = 50 units/mL. The ordered rate is 1,200 units/hour. 1,200 divided by 50 = 24 mL/hour.","rationaleCorrectZh":"浓度为25,000单位/500毫升 = 50单位/毫升。医嘱速率为每小时1,200单位。1,200除以50 = 每小时24毫升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Find units per mL first, then divide the ordered units per hour by that concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先求每毫升含多少单位，再用每小时医嘱单位数除以该浓度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2007,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_1344_t1_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.537","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.537.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.537.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[172,425],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,138],"fullStemEn":"An adult client weighing 70 kg has partial-thickness and full-thickness burns over 30% total body surface area. The burns occurred at 1400, and the client arrives at 1500. The provider's order says: use the traditional Parkland formula, 4 mL lactated Ringer's x kg body weight x percent TBSA burned; give half of the calculated volume during the first 8 hours from the time of burn injury and the rest over the next 16 hours.","fullStemZh":"一名体重70 kg的成人患者有占体表总面积30%的浅二度及深度烧伤。烧伤发生于1400，患者1500到达。医嘱写明：使用传统Parkland公式，乳酸林格液4 mL x 体重kg x 烧伤TBSA百分比；从烧伤发生时间起前8小时给予计算总量的一半，其余在接下来的16小时给予。","terminalSentenceEn":"The provider's order says: use the traditional Parkland formula, 4 mL lactated Ringer's x kg body weight x percent TBSA burned; give half of the calculated volume during the first 8 hours from the time of burn injury and the rest over the next 16 hours.","terminalSentenceZh":"医嘱写明：使用传统Parkland公式，乳酸林格液4 mL x 体重kg x 烧伤TBSA百分比；从烧伤发生时间起前8小时给予计算总量的一半，其余在接下来的16小时给予。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The burns occurred at 1400, and the client arrives at 1500.","penultimateSentenceZh":"烧伤发生于1400，患者1500到达。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should plan for a total first-24-hour fluid volume of {{1}} and recognize that the first-half timing begins at {{2}}.","zh":"护士应计划首24小时总补液量为 {{1}}，并认识到前一半液体的计时从 {{2}} 开始。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"vol_4200","en":"4,200 mL","zh":"4,200毫升"},{"id":"vol_12600","en":"12,600 mL","zh":"12,600毫升"},{"id":"vol_8400","en":"8,400 mL","zh":"8,400毫升"}],"correct":"vol_8400"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"time_order","en":"the time the IV order is entered","zh":"静脉补液医嘱录入时间"},{"id":"time_arrival","en":"1500, the time of arrival","zh":"1500，即到达时间"},{"id":"time_burn","en":"1400, the time the burns occurred","zh":"1400，即烧伤发生时间"}],"correct":"time_burn"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the stated traditional Parkland formula: 4 mL x 70 kg x 30 = 8,400 mL for the first 24 hours. Half is timed from the burn injury, not arrival, so the first-half window began at 1400.","rationaleCorrectZh":"按题干给出的传统Parkland公式计算：4 mL x 70 kg x 30 = 首24小时8,400毫升。一半液体从烧伤发生时间开始计时，而不是从到达时间开始，因此前一半液体的时间窗从1400开始。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For burn calculations, read the formula and timing rule in the stem before calculating.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做烧伤计算题时，先阅读题干中的公式和计时规则，再进行计算。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2008,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_1344_t1_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.538","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.538.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.538.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[61,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,62],"fullStemEn":"A client is scheduled for electroconvulsive therapy at 0900. For each finding or action, classify whether it is expected preprocedure nursing care or whether it requires holding the procedure and notifying the anesthesia or ECT team before treatment.","fullStemZh":"一名患者计划于0900接受电休克治疗。请将每项发现或措施分类为预期的术前护理，或需要暂停治疗并在治疗前通知麻醉或ECT团队。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding or action, classify whether it is expected preprocedure nursing care or whether it requires holding the procedure and notifying the anesthesia or ECT team before treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每项发现或措施分类为预期的术前护理，或需要暂停治疗并在治疗前通知麻醉或ECT团队。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is scheduled for electroconvulsive therapy at 0900.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者计划于0900接受电休克治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r_npo","en":"Verify that the client has been NPO as required by the facility protocol.","zh":"确认患者已按机构流程禁食禁饮。"},{"id":"r_consent","en":"Confirm that informed consent is present before transport.","zh":"转运前确认已取得知情同意。"},{"id":"r_dentures","en":"Remove dentures and loose removable oral appliances.","zh":"取下假牙和松动的可摘口腔装置。"},{"id":"r_fever","en":"Temperature is 101.5 °F (38.6 °C) with a new productive cough.","zh":"体温101.5 °F (38.6 °C)，并出现新的咳痰。"},{"id":"r_chest_pain","en":"The client reports new crushing chest pain.","zh":"患者报告新发压榨样胸痛。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_expected","en":"Expected preprocedure care","zh":"预期的术前护理"},{"id":"c_hold_notify","en":"Hold and notify team","zh":"暂停并通知团队"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r_npo","columnIds":["c_expected"]},{"rowId":"r_consent","columnIds":["c_expected"]},{"rowId":"r_dentures","columnIds":["c_expected"]},{"rowId":"r_fever","columnIds":["c_hold_notify"]},{"rowId":"r_chest_pain","columnIds":["c_hold_notify"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Routine ECT preparation includes verifying NPO status, consent, and removal of dentures or loose oral appliances. Fever with a new productive cough and new crushing chest pain may affect anesthesia and cardiovascular risk, so the procedure should be held until the team evaluates the client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"常规ECT准备包括确认禁食禁饮状态、知情同意，以及取下假牙或松动口腔装置。发热伴新发咳痰和新发压榨样胸痛可能影响麻醉和心血管风险，因此应暂停治疗，等待团队评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For preprocedure matrix items, separate routine preparation steps from new findings that change anesthesia or cardiovascular risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做术前矩阵题时，将常规准备步骤与会改变麻醉或心血管风险的新发现区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2009,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t1_01_co_exposure_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.539","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.539.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.539.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[262,283],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,85],"fullStemEn":"A school nurse is called to a closed maintenance room where two staff members who were using a gas-powered floor buffer report headache, nausea, and dizziness. One staff member is confused. The pulse oximeter reads 99%. A wall carbon monoxide alarm is sounding. Complete the diagram.","fullStemZh":"学校护士被叫到一间关闭的维修室。两名工作人员刚使用燃气地板打磨机后出现头痛、恶心和头晕，其中一人意识混乱。脉搏血氧仪显示 99%。墙上的一氧化碳报警器正在响。请完成图示。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成图示。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A wall carbon monoxide alarm is sounding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"墙上的一氧化碳报警器正在响。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_panic","en":"Panic attack","zh":"惊恐发作"},{"id":"c_opioid","en":"Opioid toxicity","zh":"阿片类药物中毒"},{"id":"c_co","en":"Carbon monoxide exposure","zh":"一氧化碳暴露"}],"correct":"c_co"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_oxygen","en":"Administer high-flow oxygen by nonrebreather mask per emergency protocol","zh":"按紧急预案使用非再呼吸面罩给予高流量氧气"},{"id":"a_finish_report","en":"Keep the clients in the room until the incident report is completed","zh":"让患者留在房间内直到事件报告完成"},{"id":"a_paper_bag","en":"Coach the clients to breathe into a paper bag","zh":"指导患者对着纸袋呼吸"},{"id":"a_fresh_air","en":"Move the clients to fresh air and activate emergency response","zh":"将患者转移到新鲜空气处并启动紧急应急流程"}],"correct":["a_fresh_air","a_oxygen"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_spo2","en":"Pulse oximeter saturation as the main indicator of oxygenation","zh":"将脉搏血氧饱和度作为氧合的主要指标"},{"id":"p_glucose","en":"Capillary blood glucose every 15 minutes","zh":"每 15 分钟测一次毛细血糖"},{"id":"p_cohb","en":"Carboxyhemoglobin level","zh":"碳氧血红蛋白水平"},{"id":"p_neuro","en":"Level of consciousness and neurologic status","zh":"意识水平和神经系统状态"}],"correct":["p_cohb","p_neuro"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The shared headache, nausea, dizziness, confusion, closed room, gas-powered equipment, and sounding carbon monoxide alarm point to carbon monoxide exposure. The nurse should remove the clients from the exposure, activate emergency response, give high-flow oxygen per protocol, and monitor carboxyhemoglobin and neurologic status. A normal pulse oximeter reading does not rule out this exposure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"两人同时出现头痛、恶心、头晕，一人意识混乱，加上关闭空间、燃气设备和一氧化碳报警器响，最符合一氧化碳暴露。护士应立即脱离暴露环境、启动紧急应急流程、按预案给予高流量氧气，并监测碳氧血红蛋白和神经系统状态。脉搏血氧仪读数正常不能排除此类暴露。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several people become ill in the same enclosed space, prioritize an environmental exposure before assuming a primary psychiatric cause.","testTakingStrategyZh":"多人在同一密闭空间同时不适时，先考虑环境暴露，而不要先假设为单纯心理原因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2010,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t1_02_refusal_communication_or","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.540","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.540.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.540.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[240,284],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,80],"fullStemEn":"An adult client scheduled for a wound dressing change says, “No one listens to me. I do not want anyone touching this dressing.” The dressing is intact with no active bleeding, and the nurse has time to respond before the scheduled change. Put the nursing responses in the best order.","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者原定更换伤口敷料时说：“没有人听我说。我不想让任何人碰这个敷料。”敷料完整、没有活动性出血，护士在预定换药前有时间回应。请按最佳顺序排列护士的回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Put the nursing responses in the best order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最佳顺序排列护士的回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The dressing is intact with no active bleeding, and the nurse has time to respond before the scheduled change.","penultimateSentenceZh":"敷料完整、没有活动性出血，护士在预定换药前有时间回应。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Pause the task and sit at the client’s eye level.","zh":"暂停操作，并坐到与患者视线平齐的位置。"},{"id":"E","en":"Agree on the next step and document the client’s preferences and ongoing refusal if it continues.","zh":"共同确定下一步，并记录患者偏好；若仍拒绝，也记录持续拒绝情况。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask, “Tell me what worries you most about the dressing change.”","zh":"询问：“请告诉我，关于换药您最担心的是什么？”"},{"id":"D","en":"Ask permission to explain the steps and offer choices that preserve wound safety.","zh":"征得同意后解释步骤，并在不影响伤口安全的前提下提供选择。"},{"id":"B","en":"Acknowledge the concern: “It sounds like you felt dismissed.”","zh":"回应患者的担忧：“听起来您觉得自己的感受没有被重视。”"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first stops the task and creates a respectful setting, then validates the emotion, explores the concern with an open-ended question, asks permission to teach and offers safe choices, and finally agrees on and documents the plan. This preserves autonomy without abandoning wound safety.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先暂停操作并建立尊重的交流环境，再确认患者情绪，用开放式问题探索担忧，然后征得同意进行解释并提供安全范围内的选择，最后共同确定并记录计划。这样既尊重自主权，也不放弃伤口安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For communication sequences, move from safety and presence, to validation, to exploration, to education or planning.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到沟通排序题，可按“安全与陪伴 → 确认感受 → 探索原因 → 教育或计划”的顺序思考。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2011,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t1_03_urine_output_fib","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.541","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.541.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.541.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[203,233],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,94],"fullStemEn":"A facility policy flags adult urine output below 0.5 mL/kg/hr for nurse follow-up. A client weighs 76 kg. What is the minimum total urine output, in mL, that would meet this policy over a 4-hour period? Round to the nearest whole mL.","fullStemZh":"某机构规定：成人尿量低于 0.5 mL/kg/hr 需要护士跟进。患者体重 76 kg。按此规定，4 小时内最低总尿量应达到多少 mL 才不需要按低尿量跟进？四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL。","penultimateSentenceEn":"What is the minimum total urine output, in mL, that would meet this policy over a 4-hour period?","penultimateSentenceZh":"按此规定，4 小时内最低总尿量应达到多少 mL 才不需要按低尿量跟进？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"minimum urine output in mL","zh":"最低尿量（mL）"},"acceptable":["152","152 mL"],"numeric":{"value":152,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Use the rule stated in the stem: 0.5 mL × 76 kg × 4 hr = 152 mL. The answer is a total volume for the 4-hour window, not an hourly rate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用题干给出的规则：0.5 mL × 76 kg × 4 hr = 152 mL。答案是 4 小时内的总尿量，不是每小时尿量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Check whether a calculation asks for a rate or a total over time; include the time multiplier only for a total.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算题先判断问的是速率还是一段时间内的总量；若问总量，才要乘以时间。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2012,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t1_04_heparin_rate_highlight","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.542","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.542.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.542.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,60],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the details needed to calculate the initial IV pump rate in mL/hr for this weight-based heparin infusion. Do not highlight details that are used for later monitoring only.","fullStemZh":"请标出计算此按体重给药的 heparin 静脉输注初始输液泵速率（mL/hr）所需的信息。不要标出仅用于后续监测的信息。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not highlight details that are used for later monitoring only.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要标出仅用于后续监测的信息。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the details needed to calculate the initial IV pump rate in mL/hr for this weight-based heparin infusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请标出计算此按体重给药的 heparin 静脉输注初始输液泵速率（mL/hr）所需的信息。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Medication order: heparin infusion 18 units/kg/hr.","zh":"用药医嘱：heparin 输注 18 units/kg/hr。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Client weight: 72 kg.","zh":"患者体重：72 kg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Pharmacy label: heparin 25,000 units in 500 mL D5W.","zh":"药房标签：heparin 25,000 units 溶于 500 mL D5W。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The 0600 aPTT is 51 seconds.","zh":"0600 的 aPTT 为 51 秒。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client has a patent peripheral IV in the left forearm.","zh":"患者左前臂有一条通畅的外周静脉通路。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The current bag was hung 4 hours ago.","zh":"当前输液袋是在 4 小时前挂上的。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pump-rate calculation requires the ordered dose in units/kg/hr, the client’s weight, and the medication concentration from the bag. Monitoring data such as aPTT, IV patency, and bag start time can matter clinically but are not needed to calculate the initial mL/hr rate from this order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算输液泵速率需要医嘱剂量 units/kg/hr、患者体重以及输液袋的药物浓度。aPTT、静脉通路通畅性和挂袋时间在临床上可能重要，但不是根据此医嘱计算初始 mL/hr 速率所必需的信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For dosage highlights, separate calculation inputs from clinical monitoring cues. Highlight only the data needed for the requested math.","testTakingStrategyZh":"剂量计算类 highlight 题要区分“计算输入”和“临床监测线索”；只标出完成题目要求计算所需的数据。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2013,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t1_05_alcohol_withdrawal_dropdown","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.543","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.543.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.543.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[267,499],"terminalOffsetsZh":[103,242],"fullStemEn":"A client was admitted 8 hours after the last alcohol intake. The client reports daily liquor use and a previous withdrawal seizure. Assessment findings include tremors, BP 158/96 mm Hg, HR 112/min, nausea, and the statement, “There are bugs crawling on the blanket.” The facility alcohol-withdrawal protocol states that hallucinations or a history of withdrawal seizures indicates high risk and requires seizure precautions plus the prescribed benzodiazepine protocol before unsupervised ambulation.","fullStemZh":"患者在最后一次饮酒后 8 小时入院。患者报告每日饮用烈酒，且曾有 withdrawal seizure。评估发现震颤、血压 158/96 mm Hg、心率 112/min、恶心，并说：“毯子上有虫子在爬。”机构 alcohol-withdrawal protocol 规定：出现幻觉或有 withdrawal seizure 史属于高风险，需要先实施 seizure precautions，并按医嘱 benzodiazepine protocol 处理，然后再考虑无人陪同下床活动。","terminalSentenceEn":"The facility alcohol-withdrawal protocol states that hallucinations or a history of withdrawal seizures indicates high risk and requires seizure precautions plus the prescribed benzodiazepine protocol before unsupervised ambulation.","terminalSentenceZh":"机构 alcohol-withdrawal protocol 规定：出现幻觉或有 withdrawal seizure 史属于高风险，需要先实施 seizure precautions，并按医嘱 benzodiazepine protocol 处理，然后再考虑无人陪同下床活动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Assessment findings include tremors, BP 158/96 mm Hg, HR 112/min, nausea, and the statement, “There are bugs crawling on the blanket.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"评估发现震颤、血压 158/96 mm Hg、心率 112/min、恶心，并说：“毯子上有虫子在爬。”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is at greatest risk for {{risk}}; the priority action is to {{action}}.","zh":"该患者最主要的风险是 {{risk}}；优先措施是 {{action}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"risk","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"hypoglycemia from missed meals","zh":"漏餐导致低血糖"},{"id":"o2","en":"opioid overdose with respiratory arrest risk","zh":"阿片类药物过量，伴呼吸停止风险"},{"id":"o4","en":"uncomplicated anxiety related to hospitalization","zh":"住院相关的单纯焦虑"},{"id":"o1","en":"severe alcohol withdrawal with seizure or delirium risk","zh":"严重酒精戒断，伴癫痫发作或谵妄风险"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"encourage independent ambulation to reduce agitation","zh":"鼓励患者独自下床活动以减轻烦躁"},{"id":"o4","en":"reorient the client and reassess at the end of the shift","zh":"重新定向患者，并在班末再评估"},{"id":"o1","en":"initiate seizure precautions and administer the prescribed benzodiazepine protocol","zh":"实施癫痫发作预防措施，并按医嘱执行 benzodiazepine protocol"},{"id":"o3","en":"withhold medication until the client has a witnessed seizure","zh":"等患者出现被目击的癫痫发作后再给药"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stem provides the governing protocol: hallucinations and a prior withdrawal seizure history make the client high risk. Tremors, autonomic elevation, nausea, and visual hallucinations support severe alcohol withdrawal. The priority is seizure precautions and the prescribed benzodiazepine protocol before allowing unsupervised ambulation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干给出适用的机构规则：幻觉和既往 withdrawal seizure 史提示高风险。震颤、自主神经兴奋、恶心和视幻觉支持严重酒精戒断。优先措施是在允许无人陪同活动前实施癫痫发作预防措施，并按医嘱执行 benzodiazepine protocol。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a stem states the facility protocol, apply that rule instead of relying on vague memory of withdrawal timelines.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干明确给出机构预案时，应直接套用该规则，而不是凭模糊的戒断时间线记忆作答。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2014,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t1_06_dka_fluid_fib","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.544","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.544.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.544.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,268],"terminalOffsetsZh":[90,103],"fullStemEn":"A facility DKA order set states: “For adults without fluid-volume contraindications, infuse 0.9% sodium chloride at 15 mL/kg during the first hour.” A client with DKA weighs 64 kg and has no contraindication listed. How many mL should be infused during the first hour?","fullStemZh":"某机构 DKA 医嘱集规定：“成人如无液体容量相关禁忌，第一小时输注 0.9% sodium chloride 15 mL/kg。”一名 DKA 患者体重 64 kg，未列出禁忌。第一小时应输注多少 mL？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many mL should be infused during the first hour?","terminalSentenceZh":"第一小时应输注多少 mL？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with DKA weighs 64 kg and has no contraindication listed.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名 DKA 患者体重 64 kg，未列出禁忌。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"first-hour infusion volume in mL","zh":"第一小时输注量（mL）"},"acceptable":["960","960 mL"],"numeric":{"value":960,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Use the order set stated in the stem: 15 mL/kg × 64 kg = 960 mL during the first hour. The item asks for volume, not mL/hr beyond the first-hour order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用题干中的医嘱集：15 mL/kg × 64 kg = 960 mL，表示第一小时输注量。本题问的是输注体积，不是第一小时以外的 mL/hr 速率。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a protocol value is written in the stem, use that exact value and unit; do not substitute another memorized DKA fluid rate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干写明预案数值时，使用该准确数值和单位；不要替换成记忆中的其他 DKA 补液速率。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A client with DKA weighs 64 kg and has no contraindication listed.","controlSentenceZh":"一名 DKA 患者体重 64 kg，未列出禁忌。"}
{"queueIndex":2015,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t2_01_cdiff_spores_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.545","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.545.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.545.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[244,304],"terminalOffsetsZh":[108,124],"fullStemEn":"A client who completed a 10-day course of clindamycin has had 8 watery stools in the past 12 hours with abdominal cramping and a temperature of 100.6 °F (38.1 °C). The client is alert but weak. A stool assay is positive for C. difficile toxin. Complete the bow-tie diagram for the nurse's priority focus.","fullStemZh":"一名患者完成 10 天 clindamycin 疗程后，过去 12 小时有 8 次水样便，伴腹部绞痛，体温 100.6 °F (38.1 °C)。患者清醒但虚弱。粪便检测 C. difficile toxin 阳性。完成图示，确定护士的优先关注点。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram for the nurse's priority focus.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示，确定护士的优先关注点。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A stool assay is positive for C. difficile toxin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"粪便检测 C. difficile toxin 阳性。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_cdiff","en":"C. difficile infection with spore contamination risk","zh":"C. difficile 感染并有芽孢污染风险"},{"id":"c_viral","en":"Uncomplicated viral gastroenteritis","zh":"单纯病毒性胃肠炎"},{"id":"c_uti","en":"Uncomplicated urinary tract infection","zh":"单纯尿路感染"}],"correct":"c_cdiff"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_alcohol_only","en":"Rely on alcohol-based hand sanitizer after all client contact","zh":"所有接触后只依赖含酒精免洗手消毒液"},{"id":"a_airborne","en":"Place the client in airborne isolation with an N95 respirator","zh":"将患者置于空气隔离并使用 N95 呼吸器"},{"id":"a_sporicidal","en":"Clean shared equipment with a facility-approved sporicidal disinfectant","zh":"使用机构批准的杀芽孢消毒剂清洁共用设备"},{"id":"a_contact","en":"Use contact precautions with gown and gloves before room entry","zh":"进房前执行接触隔离，穿隔离衣并戴手套"}],"correct":["a_contact","a_sporicidal"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_hydration","en":"Hydration status and electrolyte imbalance cues","zh":"水合状态和电解质失衡线索"},{"id":"p_stool","en":"Stool frequency and volume","zh":"排便次数和粪便量"},{"id":"p_urineculture","en":"Urine culture colony count","zh":"尿培养菌落计数"},{"id":"p_peakflow","en":"Peak expiratory flow before meals","zh":"餐前峰值呼气流速"}],"correct":["p_stool","p_hydration"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Recent clindamycin use, profuse watery diarrhea, fever, abdominal cramping, and a positive toxin assay point to C. difficile. The nursing priority is preventing spore spread and monitoring for fluid and electrolyte complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"近期使用 clindamycin、大量水样便、发热、腹部绞痛以及 toxin 检测阳性，均支持 C. difficile。护理优先事项是防止芽孢传播，并监测脱水和电解质并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a question names C. difficile toxin, think stoolborne spores: contact precautions, soap-and-water hand hygiene, sporicidal cleaning, and dehydration monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干明确 C. difficile toxin 时，要想到粪便传播的芽孢：接触隔离、肥皂和清水洗手、杀芽孢清洁，以及监测脱水。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2016,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t2_02_imminent_suicide_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.546","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.546.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.546.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[269,329],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,101],"fullStemEn":"A client seen in the outpatient clinic says, \"I cannot keep doing this. Tonight I am going to take the old oxycodone tablets in my backpack with alcohol so I do not wake up.\" The client avoids eye contact and says, \"Do not call anyone. I just needed to tell somebody.\" Complete the bow-tie diagram for the nurse's priority focus.","fullStemZh":"一名门诊患者说：“我真的撑不下去了。今晚我要把背包里的旧 oxycodone 药片和酒一起吃，这样就不会醒来了。”患者回避目光并说：“不要叫任何人。我只是想告诉一个人。”完成图示，确定护士的优先关注点。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram for the nurse's priority focus.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成图示，确定护士的优先关注点。","penultimateSentenceEn":"I just needed to tell somebody.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"我只是想告诉一个人。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely priority problem","zh":"最可能的优先问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_anxiety","en":"Situational anxiety without immediate safety threat","zh":"无立即安全威胁的情境性焦虑"},{"id":"c_imminent","en":"Imminent suicide risk","zh":"迫在眉睫的自杀风险"},{"id":"c_nssi","en":"Nonsuicidal self-injury without current intent","zh":"无当前自杀意图的非自杀性自伤"}],"correct":"c_imminent"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_wait","en":"Schedule a routine counseling visit for next week","zh":"安排下周常规心理咨询"},{"id":"a_contract","en":"Ask the client to sign a no-suicide contract and return home","zh":"要求患者签署不自杀协议后回家"},{"id":"a_remove_means","en":"Activate the suicide safety protocol and remove access to the pills","zh":"启动自杀安全流程并移除患者接触药片的机会"},{"id":"a_stay","en":"Stay with the client and maintain direct observation","zh":"留在患者身边并保持直接观察"}],"correct":["a_stay","a_remove_means"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_intent","en":"Current intent, plan, and ability to maintain safety","zh":"当前意图、计划以及维持安全的能力"},{"id":"p_sleep","en":"Usual bedtime routine before discharge","zh":"出院前的日常睡前习惯"},{"id":"p_means","en":"Access to lethal means","zh":"接触致命手段的可能性"},{"id":"p_appetite","en":"Daily calorie intake as the main safety marker","zh":"将每日热量摄入作为主要安全指标"}],"correct":["p_means","p_intent"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A specific plan, stated timing, lethal means already present, intent to die, and a request for secrecy indicate imminent suicide risk. The nurse must not leave the client alone and must activate emergency safety measures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具体计划、明确时间、已经携带致命手段、表达死亡意图以及要求保密，都提示迫在眉睫的自杀风险。护士不能让患者独处，必须启动紧急安全措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Specific plan plus means plus timing means immediate safety. Do not choose reassurance, contracts, or delayed follow-up as the priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"有具体计划、手段和时间，就是立即安全问题。不要把安慰、不自杀协议或延后随访作为优先答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2017,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t2_03_ect_recovery_dropdown","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.547","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.547.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.547.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[238,266],"terminalOffsetsZh":[104,111],"fullStemEn":"A client returns to the postanesthesia area 15 minutes after electroconvulsive therapy. The client is awake, respirations are 16/min, oxygen saturation is 97%, and the gag reflex is present. The client asks, \"Where am I? What day is it?\" and reports a mild headache.","fullStemZh":"一名患者接受 electroconvulsive therapy 后 15 分钟返回麻醉后恢复区。患者清醒，呼吸 16 次/分，氧饱和度 97%，gag reflex 存在。患者问：“我在哪里？今天星期几？”并诉轻度头痛。","terminalSentenceEn":"and reports a mild headache.","terminalSentenceZh":"并诉轻度头痛。","penultimateSentenceEn":"What day is it?\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"今天星期几？”","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should interpret the confusion as {{finding}} and should first {{action}}.","zh":"护士应将这种意识混乱理解为 {{finding}}，并应首先 {{action}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"finding","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"an expected short-term effect after ECT","zh":"ECT 后预期的短期反应"},{"id":"o2","en":"evidence of acute stroke until proven otherwise","zh":"除非证明不是，否则视为急性中风证据"},{"id":"o3","en":"a sign that the ECT treatment failed","zh":"ECT 治疗失败的表现"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"reorient calmly and continue recovery safety precautions","zh":"平静地重新定向，并继续恢复期安全防护"},{"id":"o3","en":"start oral fluids immediately to relieve the headache","zh":"立即开始口服液体以缓解头痛"},{"id":"o2","en":"leave the client alone to sleep until fully oriented","zh":"让患者独自睡觉直到完全定向"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Brief confusion, disorientation, and mild headache are expected after ECT and anesthesia when airway and vital signs are stable. The nurse should reorient calmly, maintain fall and recovery precautions, and continue monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在气道和生命体征稳定时，ECT 和麻醉后短暂意识混乱、定向障碍和轻度头痛是预期反应。护士应平静重新定向，维持跌倒和恢复期防护，并继续监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After ECT, first separate expected recovery effects from red flags. Stable airway and vital signs make reorientation and safety the best first action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"ECT 后先区分预期恢复反应和危险信号。气道与生命体征稳定时，重新定向和安全防护是最佳第一步。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2018,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t2_04_kcl_duration_fib","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.548","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.548.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.548.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[225,336],"terminalOffsetsZh":[98,132],"fullStemEn":"The provider prescribes potassium chloride 40 mEq IV to replace a low potassium level. The client has a peripheral IV. Facility policy states: potassium chloride through a peripheral IV must not infuse faster than 10 mEq/hr. If the nurse uses the fastest allowed peripheral rate, administer the 40 mEq dose over at least how many hours?","fullStemZh":"医嘱 potassium chloride 40 mEq IV，用于纠正低钾。患者使用外周静脉通路。机构规定：potassium chloride 经外周静脉输注速度不得超过 10 mEq/hr。若护士使用外周静脉允许的最快速度，40 mEq 至少应输注多少小时？","terminalSentenceEn":"If the nurse uses the fastest allowed peripheral rate, administer the 40 mEq dose over at least how many hours?","terminalSentenceZh":"若护士使用外周静脉允许的最快速度，40 mEq 至少应输注多少小时？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy states: potassium chloride through a peripheral IV must not infuse faster than 10 mEq/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构规定：potassium chloride 经外周静脉输注速度不得超过 10 mEq/hr。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"hours","zh":"小时"},"acceptable":["4","4 hr","4 hrs","4 hours","4小时","4 小时"],"numeric":{"value":4,"tolerance":0,"unit":"hours"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the stated policy, divide the total dose by the maximum peripheral rate: 40 mEq ÷ 10 mEq/hr = 4 hours. Faster administration would exceed the safety limit stated in the stem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据题干给出的规定，总剂量除以外周静脉最高速度：40 mEq ÷ 10 mEq/hr = 4 小时。更快输注会超过题干中的安全规则。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For rate-limit items, do not start with the IV bag volume. First use the safety limit: total dose divided by maximum dose per hour.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到限速题，不要先从输液袋容量入手。先用安全限制：总剂量除以每小时最高剂量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2019,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t2_05_palliative_dyspnea_dropdown","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.549","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.549.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.549.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[415,479],"terminalOffsetsZh":[147,176],"fullStemEn":"A client with end-stage lung disease is receiving comfort-focused care. The care plan states: prioritize relief of dyspnea over achieving a target oxygen saturation. A PRN order is available for morphine oral solution 2 mg every 1 hour for dyspnea. The client is sitting upright, anxious, and says, \"I cannot catch my breath.\" Respirations are 28/min and oxygen saturation is 85% on the client's usual oxygen flow. The family asks whether morphine means the nurse is \"giving up.\"","fullStemZh":"一名终末期肺病患者正在接受以舒适为目标的护理。护理计划写明：优先缓解 dyspnea，而不是追求目标氧饱和度。已有 PRN 医嘱：morphine 口服液 2 mg，每 1 小时按需用于 dyspnea。患者端坐、焦虑，并说：“我喘不上气。”呼吸 28 次/分，在平时氧流量下氧饱和度 85%。家属询问使用 morphine 是否表示护士“放弃治疗”。","terminalSentenceEn":"The family asks whether morphine means the nurse is \"giving up.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"家属询问使用 morphine 是否表示护士“放弃治疗”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Respirations are 28/min and oxygen saturation is 85% on the client's usual oxygen flow.","penultimateSentenceZh":"呼吸 28 次/分，在平时氧流量下氧饱和度 85%。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize the priority problem as {{problem}} and should {{action}}.","zh":"护士应将优先问题识别为 {{problem}}，并应 {{action}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"problem","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"distressing dyspnea requiring comfort-focused intervention","zh":"需要舒适护理干预的痛苦性呼吸困难"},{"id":"o2","en":"oxygen saturation below target despite curative escalation","zh":"需以治愈性升级处理的氧饱和度未达标"},{"id":"o3","en":"family misunderstanding that overrides the client's symptoms","zh":"家属误解优先于患者症状"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"administer the prescribed morphine and explain that it is being used to relieve dyspnea","zh":"给予医嘱的 morphine，并解释其用途是缓解呼吸困难"},{"id":"o3","en":"tell the family that morphine is only used when death is expected within minutes","zh":"告诉家属 morphine 只在预计数分钟内死亡时使用"},{"id":"o2","en":"withhold morphine until the oxygen saturation is above 94%","zh":"等氧饱和度升至 94% 以上后再给予 morphine"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The care plan stated in the stem prioritizes dyspnea relief over numeric oxygen targets. Prescribed low-dose morphine can be used for end-of-life dyspnea while the nurse explains the comfort goal and monitors the client's response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干中的护理计划明确优先缓解呼吸困难，而不是追求氧饱和度数字。医嘱的低剂量 morphine 可用于临终期 dyspnea，护士同时解释舒适目标并监测患者反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In palliative questions, read the goals-of-care statement. If comfort is the goal, treat distressing symptoms and teach the family what the medication is for.","testTakingStrategyZh":"姑息护理题要先看照护目标。如果目标是舒适，就处理痛苦症状，并向家属说明药物用途。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Respirations are 28/min and oxygen saturation is 85% on the client's usual oxygen flow.","controlSentenceZh":"呼吸 28 次/分，在平时氧流量下氧饱和度 85%。"}
{"queueIndex":2020,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t2_06_pph_sequence_or","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.550","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.550.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.550.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[336,380],"terminalOffsetsZh":[121,134],"fullStemEn":"A client is 1 hour postpartum after a vaginal birth. The nurse notes a boggy uterus displaced to the right, a saturated perineal pad, and several large clots. Blood pressure is 92/58 mm Hg and pulse is 118/min. The postpartum hemorrhage protocol includes oxytocin infusion and straight catheterization if bladder distention is present. Place the nursing actions in the best order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者阴道分娩后 1 小时。护士发现子宫松软并偏向右侧，会阴垫湿透，有数个大血块。血压 92/58 mm Hg，脉搏 118 次/分。postpartum hemorrhage 流程包括 oxytocin 输注，以及如有膀胱胀满则行直导尿。请按最佳顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the best order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最佳顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The postpartum hemorrhage protocol includes oxytocin infusion and straight catheterization if bladder distention is present.","penultimateSentenceZh":"postpartum hemorrhage 流程包括 oxytocin 输注，以及如有膀胱胀满则行直导尿。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Assess for bladder distention and perform straight catheterization if indicated by the protocol.","zh":"评估膀胱胀满；如流程指示，执行直导尿。"},{"id":"E","en":"Quantify blood loss and continue frequent vital-sign and fundal reassessment.","zh":"量化失血量，并继续频繁复查生命体征和子宫底。"},{"id":"B","en":"Massage the uterine fundus firmly until it becomes firm.","zh":"有力按摩子宫底，直到子宫变硬。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the postpartum hemorrhage protocol and call for additional help.","zh":"启动 postpartum hemorrhage 流程并呼叫额外帮助。"},{"id":"C","en":"Increase or start the oxytocin infusion according to the standing protocol.","zh":"按常规流程增加或开始 oxytocin 输注。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The unstable postpartum client needs immediate escalation and help, then direct treatment of uterine atony with fundal massage and the ordered oxytocin protocol. A right-displaced boggy uterus suggests bladder distention, so bladder management supports uterine contraction. Quantifying blood loss and reassessing continue after immediate hemorrhage-control actions begin.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这名产后不稳定患者需要立即升级处理并呼叫帮助，随后直接处理 uterine atony：按摩子宫底并按医嘱流程使用 oxytocin。子宫松软且偏右提示膀胱胀满，因此处理膀胱有助于子宫收缩。量化失血和复查应在立即止血措施开始后持续进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a postpartum boggy uterus with shock cues, prioritize help and hemorrhage control first; measurement and documentation follow without delaying treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产后子宫松软并有休克线索时，先呼叫帮助并控制出血；测量和记录要做，但不能延误治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2021,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t3_dka_highlight_acid_base_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.551","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.551.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.551.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,43],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that require immediate follow-up because they show worsening perfusion or acid-base compromise in the client with suspected DKA.","fullStemZh":"请标出需要立即跟进的发现，因为这些发现显示疑似 DKA 患者的灌注或酸碱状态正在恶化。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require immediate follow-up because they show worsening perfusion or acid-base compromise in the client with suspected DKA.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要立即跟进的发现，因为这些发现显示疑似 DKA 患者的灌注或酸碱状态正在恶化。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Emergency department note, 0815:","zh":"急诊记录，0815："},{"id":"s2","en":"The client has type 1 diabetes and has had vomiting for 2 days.","zh":"患者有 type 1 diabetes，已呕吐 2 天。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Blood glucose is 482 mg/dL.","zh":"血糖为 482 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Urine ketones are large.","zh":"尿酮体为大量阳性。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Respirations are deep at 32/min with a fruity odor on the breath.","zh":"呼吸深大，32 次/分，呼气有水果味。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Blood pressure is 86/50 mm Hg and heart rate is 132/min.","zh":"血压 86/50 mm Hg，心率 132 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Venous pH is 7.18 and bicarbonate is 10 mEq/L.","zh":"静脉 pH 为 7.18，bicarbonate 为 10 mEq/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"The client is newly difficult to arouse.","zh":"患者新出现不易唤醒。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"The client states, “I missed my insulin yesterday.”","zh":"患者说：“我昨天漏打了 insulin。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["s5","s6","s7","s8"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Deep, rapid respirations with fruity breath suggest compensatory Kussmaul respirations from metabolic acidosis. Hypotension with tachycardia indicates volume depletion and poor perfusion. A pH of 7.18 with bicarbonate 10 mEq/L confirms significant acidosis, and new decreased arousability is a neurologic deterioration that requires urgent follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"深大快速呼吸并伴水果味呼气提示 metabolic acidosis 引起的 Kussmaul respirations。低血压合并心动过速说明容量不足和灌注不良。pH 7.18、bicarbonate 10 mEq/L 证实明显酸中毒；新出现不易唤醒属于神经状态恶化，需要立即跟进。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For highlight items, separate background diagnostic support from unstable assessment cues. Key the findings that change immediate nursing priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 highlight 题时，要把诊断背景线索和不稳定评估线索分开；选择会改变立即护理优先级的发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2022,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t3_clozapine_infection_highlight_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.552","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.552.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.552.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[210,285],"terminalOffsetsZh":[112,128],"fullStemEn":"The medication record shows clozapine 200 mg by mouth at bedtime. The facility protocol states to hold clozapine and notify the prescriber for signs of infection or an absolute neutrophil count below 1,000/uL. Highlight the findings that require follow-up before giving tonight's dose.","fullStemZh":"给药记录显示 clozapine 200 mg 睡前口服。机构 protocol 规定：若出现感染迹象或 absolute neutrophil count 低于 1,000/uL，应暂缓 clozapine 并通知开方者。请标出今晚给药前需要跟进的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require follow-up before giving tonight's dose.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出今晚给药前需要跟进的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility protocol states to hold clozapine and notify the prescriber for signs of infection or an absolute neutrophil count below 1,000/uL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构 protocol 规定：若出现感染迹象或 absolute neutrophil count 低于 1,000/uL，应暂缓 clozapine 并通知开方者。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Evening assessment and laboratory results:","zh":"晚间评估和实验室结果："},{"id":"s2","en":"The client takes clozapine for treatment-resistant schizophrenia.","zh":"患者因 treatment-resistant schizophrenia 服用 clozapine。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Temperature is 101.5 °F (38.6 °C) with chills.","zh":"体温 101.5 °F (38.6 °C)，伴寒战。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client reports a new sore throat and painful mouth ulcers.","zh":"患者报告新出现 sore throat 和疼痛性口腔溃疡。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Absolute neutrophil count is 850/uL.","zh":"absolute neutrophil count 为 850/uL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client reports mild nighttime drooling.","zh":"患者报告夜间轻度流口水。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The last bowel movement was yesterday morning.","zh":"上次排便是昨天早晨。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"The client asks whether the bedtime dose can be taken with water.","zh":"患者询问睡前剂量是否可以用水送服。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clozapine can cause severe neutropenia and serious infection risk. Under the stated protocol, fever with chills, new sore throat or mouth ulcers, and an ANC of 850/uL require holding the dose and notifying the prescriber before administration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"clozapine 可导致 severe neutropenia，并增加严重感染风险。根据题干给出的 protocol，发热伴寒战、新发 sore throat 或口腔溃疡，以及 ANC 850/uL 都要求给药前暂缓剂量并通知开方者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-risk medication questions, match the assessment finding to the safety hold parameter stated in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高风险用药题要把评估发现与题干给出的安全暂缓参数配对。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2023,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t3_post_thyroidectomy_hypocalcemia_highlight_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.553","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.553.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.553.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[63,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,48],"fullStemEn":"A client is 8 hours postoperative after a total thyroidectomy. Highlight the findings that require immediate nursing follow-up.","fullStemZh":"一名患者 total thyroidectomy 术后 8 小时。请标出需要护士立即跟进的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require immediate nursing follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要护士立即跟进的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is 8 hours postoperative after a total thyroidectomy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者 total thyroidectomy 术后 8 小时。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Postoperative assessment:","zh":"术后评估："},{"id":"s2","en":"The dressing has a 2-cm area of dry serosanguineous drainage.","zh":"敷料上有 2 cm 干燥的浆血性渗液。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client reports mild throat soreness when swallowing.","zh":"患者吞咽时报告轻度咽喉疼痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client has new inspiratory stridor.","zh":"患者新出现吸气性 stridor。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client reports tingling around the mouth and fingertips.","zh":"患者报告口周和指尖 tingling。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client's hand spasms when the blood pressure cuff inflates.","zh":"血压袖带充气时患者手部出现痉挛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Serum calcium is 7.1 mg/dL.","zh":"血清 calcium 为 7.1 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"The client is using a call light before getting out of bed.","zh":"患者下床前使用呼叫铃。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s4","s5","s6","s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New stridor after neck surgery is an airway warning sign. Perioral and fingertip tingling, carpal spasm with cuff inflation, and low calcium are consistent with postoperative hypocalcemia from parathyroid disruption and require prompt follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"颈部手术后新出现 stridor 是 airway 危险信号。口周和指尖 tingling、袖带充气诱发手部痉挛以及低 calcium 符合甲状旁腺受影响后的术后 hypocalcemia，需要及时跟进。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After thyroidectomy, prioritize airway cues first, then look for hypocalcemia signs caused by parathyroid disruption.","testTakingStrategyZh":"thyroidectomy 术后先优先处理 airway 线索，再寻找甲状旁腺受影响导致的 hypocalcemia 征象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2024,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t3_insulin_correction_fib_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.554","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.554.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.554.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[264,325],"terminalOffsetsZh":[176,207],"fullStemEn":"A premeal correction-scale order reads: blood glucose 151-200 mg/dL = 2 units insulin lispro; 201-250 = 4 units; 251-300 = 6 units; 301-350 = 8 units; notify the provider if above 350. The client's premeal blood glucose is 312 mg/dL, and the meal tray is present. How many units of insulin lispro should the nurse administer?","fullStemZh":"餐前 correction-scale 医嘱写明：blood glucose 151-200 mg/dL = insulin lispro 2 units；201-250 = 4 units；251-300 = 6 units；301-350 = 8 units；若高于 350 需通知 provider。患者餐前血糖为 312 mg/dL，餐盘已到。护士应给予多少 units 的 insulin lispro？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many units of insulin lispro should the nurse administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应给予多少 units 的 insulin lispro？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's premeal blood glucose is 312 mg/dL, and the meal tray is present.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者餐前血糖为 312 mg/dL，餐盘已到。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"units of insulin lispro","zh":"insulin lispro units"},"acceptable":["8","8 units","8 unit","8 单位"],"numeric":{"value":8,"tolerance":0,"unit":"units"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The blood glucose value of 312 mg/dL falls in the 301-350 mg/dL correction-scale range, so the nurse administers 8 units of insulin lispro according to the order stated in the stem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血糖 312 mg/dL 落在 correction-scale 的 301-350 mg/dL 范围内，因此护士按题干医嘱给予 insulin lispro 8 units。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sliding-scale items, do not interpolate between ranges. Find the row that contains the measured glucose value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 sliding-scale 题时不要在范围之间自行插值；找到包含该血糖值的那一行即可。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2025,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t3_fetal_cloze_late_deceleration_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.555","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.555.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.555.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,308],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,95],"fullStemEn":"During oxytocin augmentation, the fetal heart rate baseline is 140/min with moderate variability. With the last four contractions, the fetal heart rate gradually decreased after each contraction began, reached the lowest point after the contraction peak, and returned to baseline after the contraction ended.","fullStemZh":"在 oxytocin 加强宫缩期间，胎心率基线为 140 次/分，变异性 moderate。最近四次宫缩中，胎心率均在宫缩开始后逐渐下降，在宫缩峰值之后达到最低点，并在宫缩结束后才回到基线。","terminalSentenceEn":"With the last four contractions, the fetal heart rate gradually decreased after each contraction began, reached the lowest point after the contraction peak, and returned to baseline after the contraction ended.","terminalSentenceZh":"最近四次宫缩中，胎心率均在宫缩开始后逐渐下降，在宫缩峰值之后达到最低点，并在宫缩结束后才回到基线。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During oxytocin augmentation, the fetal heart rate baseline is 140/min with moderate variability.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在 oxytocin 加强宫缩期间，胎心率基线为 140 次/分，变异性 moderate。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"This pattern is most consistent with {{pattern}}, so the nurse should first {{action}}.","zh":"这种模式最符合 {{pattern}}，因此护士应首先 {{action}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"pattern","options":[{"id":"variable","en":"variable decelerations from umbilical cord compression","zh":"由脐带受压引起的 variable decelerations"},{"id":"late","en":"late decelerations related to uteroplacental insufficiency","zh":"与 uteroplacental insufficiency 相关的 late decelerations"},{"id":"early","en":"early decelerations from fetal head compression","zh":"由胎头受压引起的 early decelerations"}],"correct":"late"},{"id":"action","options":[{"id":"push","en":"coach the client to begin pushing with each contraction","zh":"指导产妇每次宫缩时开始用力屏气"},{"id":"reposition","en":"reposition the client laterally and assess the response","zh":"协助产妇侧卧并评估反应"},{"id":"increase_oxytocin","en":"increase the oxytocin rate to improve labor progress","zh":"增加 oxytocin 速度以促进产程进展"}],"correct":"reposition"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A gradual deceleration whose nadir occurs after the contraction peak and whose recovery occurs after the contraction ends is a late deceleration pattern. The first nursing action is intrauterine resuscitation such as lateral repositioning and reassessment; increasing oxytocin can worsen uteroplacental stress.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胎心率逐渐下降、最低点出现在宫缩峰值之后，并在宫缩结束后才恢复，符合 late deceleration。护士首先进行宫内复苏措施，如协助侧卧并复评；增加 oxytocin 可能加重子宫胎盘压力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For deceleration questions, match the timing of the nadir to the contraction before choosing the action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做胎心减速题时，先把最低点与宫缩时间关系配对，再选择护理措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2026,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_2026_07_03_2114_t3_hypoglycemia_cloze_rule15_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.556","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.556.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.556.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,68],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes is awake, able to swallow, shaky, and diaphoretic before lunch. Capillary blood glucose is 58 mg/dL. A meal tray will arrive in 25 minutes.","fullStemZh":"一名 type 1 diabetes 患者午餐前清醒、能吞咽，出现发抖和出汗。指尖血糖为 58 mg/dL。餐盘将在 25 分钟后送达。","terminalSentenceEn":"A meal tray will arrive in 25 minutes.","terminalSentenceZh":"餐盘将在 25 分钟后送达。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Capillary blood glucose is 58 mg/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"指尖血糖为 58 mg/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first give {{carbohydrate}} and then {{recheck}}.","zh":"护士应首先给予 {{carbohydrate}}，然后 {{recheck}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"carbohydrate","options":[{"id":"protein","en":"a high-protein snack without carbohydrate","zh":"不含 carbohydrate 的高蛋白点心"},{"id":"wait_meal","en":"no treatment until the meal tray arrives","zh":"等餐盘送达后再处理"},{"id":"fast15","en":"15 g of fast-acting carbohydrate","zh":"15 g 快速起效 carbohydrate"}],"correct":"fast15"},{"id":"recheck","options":[{"id":"hour","en":"recheck the blood glucose in 1 hour","zh":"1 小时后复查血糖"},{"id":"bedtime","en":"wait until the bedtime glucose check","zh":"等到睡前血糖检查"},{"id":"fifteen","en":"recheck the blood glucose in 15 minutes","zh":"15 分钟后复查血糖"}],"correct":"fifteen"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A conscious client who can swallow and has blood glucose below 70 mg/dL should receive fast-acting carbohydrate promptly, then have glucose rechecked in 15 minutes. Waiting for the meal tray delays treatment of symptomatic hypoglycemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"清醒且能吞咽、血糖低于 70 mg/dL 的患者，应立即给予快速起效 carbohydrate，然后 15 分钟后复查血糖。等待餐盘会延误对有症状 hypoglycemia 的处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For hypoglycemia, first decide whether the client can safely swallow. If yes, treat promptly with fast carbohydrate and reassess soon.","testTakingStrategyZh":"hypoglycemia 题先判断患者是否能安全吞咽；若可以，立即用快速 carbohydrate 处理并尽快复评。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2027,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_bt_therapeutic_panic_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.557","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.557.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.557.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[269,297],"terminalOffsetsZh":[78,85],"fullStemEn":"A client with a documented panic disorder suddenly grips the chair, breathes 30 times/min, reports tingling around the mouth, and says, “I am going to die.” A recent medical evaluation ruled out cardiopulmonary causes, and current oxygen saturation is 98% on room air. Complete the bowtie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名已确诊惊恐障碍的患者突然紧抓椅子，呼吸频率为30次/分，诉口周麻刺感，并说：“我要死了。”近期医学评估已排除心肺原因，目前室内空气下血氧饱和度为98%。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A recent medical evaluation ruled out cardiopulmonary causes, and current oxygen saturation is 98% on room air.","penultimateSentenceZh":"近期医学评估已排除心肺原因，目前室内空气下血氧饱和度为98%。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_panic","en":"Panic-level anxiety","zh":"惊恐水平的焦虑"},{"id":"c_delirium","en":"Acute delirium","zh":"急性谵妄"},{"id":"c_gad","en":"Generalized anxiety","zh":"广泛性焦虑"}],"correct":"c_panic"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_leave_alone","en":"Leave the client alone to regain control","zh":"让患者独处以自行恢复控制"},{"id":"a_analyze_trigger","en":"Ask the client to analyze the trigger in detail","zh":"要求患者详细分析诱因"},{"id":"a_stay_brief","en":"Stay with the client and use brief, calm statements","zh":"陪伴患者，并使用简短、平静的语句"},{"id":"a_breathe_quiet","en":"Move to a quiet area and coach slow breathing","zh":"转移到安静区域，并指导缓慢呼吸"}],"correct":["a_stay_brief","a_breathe_quiet"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_sodium","en":"Daily dietary sodium intake","zh":"每日膳食钠摄入量"},{"id":"p_sleep","en":"Usual monthly sleep pattern","zh":"平常每月睡眠模式"},{"id":"p_directions","en":"Ability to follow one-step directions","zh":"执行一步指令的能力"},{"id":"p_resp","en":"Respiratory rate and work of breathing","zh":"呼吸频率和呼吸功"}],"correct":["p_resp","p_directions"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The abrupt intense fear, hyperventilation, paresthesia, and fear of dying after medical causes have been excluded indicate panic-level anxiety. During panic, the nurse stays with the client, reduces stimuli, communicates in short concrete statements, and coaches slower breathing. Respiratory effort and the return of the ability to follow simple directions show whether the episode is resolving.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在排除医学原因后，突发强烈恐惧、过度通气、感觉异常和濒死感提示惊恐水平的焦虑。惊恐发作时，护士应陪伴患者、减少刺激、使用简短具体的语句，并指导减慢呼吸。呼吸状态以及能否重新执行简单指令可反映发作是否缓解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the communication style to the client's anxiety level. At panic level, choose presence, low stimulation, and simple directions rather than insight-oriented discussion.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将沟通方式与患者的焦虑程度相匹配。惊恐水平时应选择陪伴、低刺激和简单指令，而不是进行需要洞察力的讨论。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf, Nursing: Mental Health and Community Concepts, anxiety and therapeutic communication chapters","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2028,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_bt_alcohol_delirium_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.558","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.558.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.558.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[302,330],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,113],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalized client who drank heavily every day had the last alcoholic drink 52 hours ago. The client is disoriented, pulls at the IV tubing, reports seeing insects on the wall, and has coarse tremors, diaphoresis, temperature 100.6 °F (38.1 °C), heart rate 126/min, and blood pressure 172/98 mm Hg. Complete the bowtie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名住院患者过去每天大量饮酒，距最后一次饮酒已52小时。患者定向障碍，拉扯静脉输液管，称墙上有虫子，并出现粗大震颤、出汗、体温100.6 °F (38.1 °C)、心率126次/分及血压172/98 mm Hg。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is disoriented, pulls at the IV tubing, reports seeing insects on the wall, and has coarse tremors, diaphoresis, temperature 100.6 °F (38.1 °C), heart rate 126/min, and blood pressure 172/98 mm Hg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者定向障碍，拉扯静脉输液管，称墙上有虫子，并出现粗大震颤、出汗、体温100.6 °F (38.1 °C)、心率126次/分及血压172/98 mm Hg。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_opioid","en":"Opioid withdrawal","zh":"阿片类药物戒断"},{"id":"c_hallucinosis","en":"Alcohol-induced psychotic disorder with clear orientation","zh":"定向力清楚的酒精诱发精神病性障碍"},{"id":"c_dt","en":"Alcohol withdrawal delirium","zh":"酒精戒断性谵妄"}],"correct":"c_dt"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_restrain","en":"Apply restraints before attempting less restrictive safety measures","zh":"在尝试限制更少的安全措施前先使用约束"},{"id":"a_precautions","en":"Institute seizure and fall precautions in a low-stimulation setting","zh":"在低刺激环境中实施癫痫和跌倒预防措施"},{"id":"a_haloperidol_only","en":"Use haloperidol alone as the primary withdrawal treatment","zh":"仅用氟哌啶醇作为主要戒断治疗"},{"id":"a_benzo","en":"Administer the prescribed benzodiazepine per withdrawal protocol","zh":"按戒断方案给予医嘱的苯二氮䓬类药物"}],"correct":["a_benzo","a_precautions"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_stool","en":"Stool frequency","zh":"排便频率"},{"id":"p_resp_loc","en":"Respiratory status and level of consciousness","zh":"呼吸状态和意识水平"},{"id":"p_lipase","en":"Serum lipase trend","zh":"血清脂肪酶趋势"},{"id":"p_vitals","en":"Heart rate, blood pressure, and temperature","zh":"心率、血压和体温"}],"correct":["p_vitals","p_resp_loc"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Disorientation, visual hallucinations, marked autonomic hyperactivity, fever, and agitation 2 to 4 days after alcohol cessation are consistent with alcohol withdrawal delirium. Benzodiazepines are first-line treatment, while seizure/fall precautions and a low-stimulation environment reduce harm. Frequent monitoring must detect persistent autonomic instability and oversedation or respiratory depression from treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"停酒后2至4天出现定向障碍、视幻觉、明显自主神经亢进、发热和躁动，符合酒精戒断性谵妄。苯二氮䓬类药物是一线治疗，同时实施癫痫和跌倒预防并提供低刺激环境可减少伤害。频繁监测应识别持续的自主神经不稳定，以及治疗导致的过度镇静或呼吸抑制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate hallucinations with intact orientation from hallucinations occurring with delirium and autonomic instability. The latter requires emergency withdrawal management.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分定向力保留时的幻觉与伴谵妄和自主神经不稳定的幻觉；后者需要紧急戒断处理。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Addiction Medicine, The ASAM Clinical Practice Guideline on Alcohol Withdrawal Management, 2020","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2029,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_bt_ect_recovery_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.559","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.559.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.559.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[219,247],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,66],"fullStemEn":"Twenty minutes after electroconvulsive therapy under general anesthesia, a client is awake but drowsy, asks repeatedly where they are, reports a mild headache, moves all extremities equally, and has stable vital signs. Complete the bowtie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在全身麻醉下接受电休克治疗20分钟后已清醒但嗜睡，反复询问自己在哪里，诉轻度头痛，四肢活动对称，生命体征稳定。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Twenty minutes after electroconvulsive therapy under general anesthesia, a client is awake but drowsy, asks repeatedly where they are, reports a mild headache, moves all extremities equally, and has stable vital signs.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在全身麻醉下接受电休克治疗20分钟后已清醒但嗜睡，反复询问自己在哪里，诉轻度头痛，四肢活动对称，生命体征稳定。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_serotonin","en":"Serotonin syndrome","zh":"血清素综合征"},{"id":"c_postictal","en":"Expected transient post-ECT confusion","zh":"ECT后预期的短暂意识混乱"},{"id":"c_stroke","en":"Acute ischemic stroke","zh":"急性缺血性脑卒中"}],"correct":"c_postictal"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_fall","en":"Maintain fall precautions and assist with mobility","zh":"维持跌倒预防并协助活动"},{"id":"a_food_now","en":"Offer food before confirming recovery of protective reflexes","zh":"在确认保护性反射恢复前提供食物"},{"id":"a_reorient","en":"Provide calm, repeated reorientation","zh":"平静并反复地进行定向指导"},{"id":"a_memory_test","en":"Perform repeated detailed memory testing immediately","zh":"立即反复进行详细记忆测试"}],"correct":["a_reorient","a_fall"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_vitals_oxygen","en":"Blood pressure, heart rate, and oxygen saturation","zh":"血压、心率和血氧饱和度"},{"id":"p_orientation","en":"Orientation and neurologic symmetry","zh":"定向力和神经功能对称性"},{"id":"p_bowel","en":"Bowel movement pattern","zh":"排便模式"},{"id":"p_a1c","en":"Hemoglobin A1c","zh":"糖化血红蛋白"}],"correct":["p_orientation","p_vitals_oxygen"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Transient confusion, disorientation, headache, and drowsiness are expected during early ECT recovery when vital signs and neurologic findings are otherwise stable. The nurse reorients the client, prevents falls, and monitors for improving cognition as well as anesthesia- and ECT-related hemodynamic or respiratory complications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当生命体征和神经系统检查其余均稳定时，短暂意识混乱、定向障碍、头痛和嗜睡属于ECT早期恢复期的预期表现。护士应进行定向指导、预防跌倒，并监测认知改善以及麻醉和ECT相关的血流动力学或呼吸并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Expected postprocedure effects are acceptable only when the pattern is transient and the neurologic and cardiopulmonary assessment remains stable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"只有当表现短暂且神经、心肺评估保持稳定时，术后预期反应才可视为正常。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf, StatPearls, Electroconvulsive Therapy, NBK538266","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2030,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_bt_ohss_severe_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.560","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.560.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.560.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[248,276],"terminalOffsetsZh":[80,87],"fullStemEn":"Seven days after an hCG trigger and oocyte retrieval, a client reports rapidly increasing abdominal distention and shortness of breath. Weight increased 2.3 kg (5 lb) in 48 hours, urine output is 20 mL/hr, and oxygen saturation is 91% on room air. Complete the bowtie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在使用hCG触发排卵并取卵7天后，出现腹胀迅速加重和呼吸困难。48小时内体重增加2.3 kg（5磅），尿量20 mL/小时，室内空气下血氧饱和度91%。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Weight increased 2.3 kg (5 lb) in 48 hours, urine output is 20 mL/hr, and oxygen saturation is 91% on room air.","penultimateSentenceZh":"48小时内体重增加2.3 kg（5磅），尿量20 mL/小时，室内空气下血氧饱和度91%。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_torsion","en":"Isolated ovarian torsion","zh":"单纯卵巢扭转"},{"id":"c_ectopic","en":"Ruptured ectopic pregnancy","zh":"异位妊娠破裂"},{"id":"c_ohss","en":"Severe ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome","zh":"重度卵巢过度刺激综合征"}],"correct":"c_ohss"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_iv_eval","en":"Begin prescribed isotonic IV fluid support and urgent specialist evaluation","zh":"开始医嘱的等渗静脉补液并紧急请专科评估"},{"id":"a_diuretic","en":"Give a loop diuretic routinely before assessing intravascular volume","zh":"在评估血管内容量前常规给予袢利尿剂"},{"id":"a_free_water","en":"Encourage unrestricted plain-water intake","zh":"鼓励不受限制地饮用白水"},{"id":"a_oxygen_position","en":"Position in semi-Fowler and administer supplemental oxygen","zh":"取半卧位并给予补充氧气"}],"correct":["a_oxygen_position","a_iv_eval"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_weight_girth","en":"Daily weight and abdominal girth","zh":"每日体重和腹围"},{"id":"p_cycle","en":"Usual menstrual-cycle length","zh":"平常月经周期长度"},{"id":"p_reflexes","en":"Deep tendon reflex grade","zh":"深腱反射等级"},{"id":"p_urine_resp","en":"Urine output and respiratory status","zh":"尿量和呼吸状态"}],"correct":["p_weight_girth","p_urine_resp"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rapid weight gain, ascites-like abdominal distention, dyspnea, hypoxemia, and oliguria after ovarian stimulation indicate severe ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome with third spacing and reduced effective circulating volume. The client needs respiratory support and urgent specialist management with carefully prescribed intravascular volume support. Weight, abdominal girth, urine output, and respiratory status track progression and response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"卵巢刺激后出现体重快速增加、类似腹水的腹胀、呼吸困难、低氧血症和少尿，提示重度卵巢过度刺激综合征，伴第三间隙液体转移和有效循环血容量下降。患者需要呼吸支持及紧急专科处理，并谨慎按医嘱补充血管内容量。体重、腹围、尿量和呼吸状态可追踪病情进展及治疗反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After fertility treatment, connect rapid weight gain plus abdominal enlargement, oliguria, or dyspnea with pathologic capillary leak rather than normal treatment discomfort.","testTakingStrategyZh":"生育治疗后，若体重快速增加并伴腹围增大、少尿或呼吸困难，应联想到病理性毛细血管渗漏，而不是正常治疗不适。","sourceMetadata":"American Society for Reproductive Medicine, Prevention and treatment of moderate and severe ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome: a guideline","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Weight increased 2.3 kg (5 lb) in 48 hours, urine output is 20 mL/hr, and oxygen saturation is 91% on room air.","controlSentenceZh":"48小时内体重增加2.3 kg（5磅），尿量20 mL/小时，室内空气下血氧饱和度91%。"}
{"queueIndex":2031,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_bt_trach_decannulation_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.561","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.561.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.561.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[372,400],"terminalOffsetsZh":[102,109],"fullStemEn":"A spontaneously breathing client has had a tracheostomy for 6 months. During care, the tube is accidentally pulled completely out. The client has noisy ineffective airflow, increasing distress, and oxygen saturation falling from 96% to 86%. The emergency tracheostomy kit is at the bedside, and facility policy authorizes a trained RN to replace a tube in a mature tract. Complete the bowtie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名自主呼吸患者已留置气管切开管6个月。护理过程中导管被意外完全拉出。患者气流嘈杂且无效，呼吸窘迫加重，血氧饱和度从96%降至86%。床旁备有气管切开急救包，机构政策允许受训注册护士在成熟窦道中重新置管。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The emergency tracheostomy kit is at the bedside, and facility policy authorizes a trained RN to replace a tube in a mature tract.","penultimateSentenceZh":"床旁备有气管切开急救包，机构政策允许受训注册护士在成熟窦道中重新置管。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c_mucus","en":"Mucus plug within an intact tracheostomy tube","zh":"完整气管切开管内的黏液栓"},{"id":"c_decannulation","en":"Accidental decannulation with airway compromise","zh":"意外脱管并伴气道受损"},{"id":"c_pneumo","en":"Spontaneous pneumothorax","zh":"自发性气胸"}],"correct":"c_decannulation"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a_replace","en":"Insert the lubricated spare same-size tube with obturator, then remove the obturator immediately","zh":"使用闭孔器插入润滑后的同型号备用管，随后立即取出闭孔器"},{"id":"a_help_oxygen","en":"Call for help and apply oxygen to the face and stoma","zh":"呼叫支援，并向面部和气管造口处供氧"},{"id":"a_force","en":"Force the removed tube through resistance","zh":"遇到阻力仍强行重新插入原导管"},{"id":"a_occlude","en":"Seal the stoma completely with an occlusive dressing","zh":"用密闭敷料完全封闭造口"}],"correct":["a_help_oxygen","a_replace"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p_airflow","en":"Bilateral breath sounds, chest rise, and exhaled airflow","zh":"双侧呼吸音、胸廓起伏和呼出气流"},{"id":"p_spo2","en":"Continuous oxygen saturation","zh":"持续血氧饱和度"},{"id":"p_bowel","en":"Bowel sounds","zh":"肠鸣音"},{"id":"p_glucose","en":"Fasting blood glucose","zh":"空腹血糖"}],"correct":["p_spo2","p_airflow"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The tube is visibly absent and the client is hypoxemic, establishing accidental decannulation with airway compromise. A mature tract permits trained protocol-directed replacement. The nurse calls for help, oxygenates both potential airway routes, inserts the spare tube with the obturator, removes the obturator immediately so airflow can occur, and confirms effective ventilation by oxygen saturation and physical airway findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"导管明显已脱出且患者低氧，说明发生意外脱管并伴气道受损。成熟窦道允许受训护士按方案重新置管。护士应呼叫支援，向两个潜在气道入口供氧，使用闭孔器插入备用导管，随后立即取出闭孔器以恢复气流，并通过血氧饱和度和气道体征确认通气有效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem explicitly states that a mature tracheostomy tract and trained replacement policy are present, prioritize oxygenation, protocol-directed recannulation, and confirmation of ventilation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干明确说明气管切开窦道已成熟且机构允许受训护士重新置管时，应优先氧合、按方案重新置管并确认通气。","sourceMetadata":"National Tracheostomy Safety Project, emergency tracheostomy management algorithms","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2032,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_hl_burn_inhalation_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.562","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.562.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.562.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that indicate a high risk for inhalation injury and impending upper-airway edema.","fullStemZh":"标出提示吸入性损伤及即将发生上气道水肿高风险的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that indicate a high risk for inhalation injury and impending upper-airway edema.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出提示吸入性损伤及即将发生上气道水肿高风险的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Emergency department note:","zh":"急诊科记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The client was rescued from an enclosed apartment fire.","zh":"患者从封闭的公寓火灾现场被救出。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Soot is present around the mouth and inside the nares.","zh":"口周和鼻孔内可见烟灰。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client's voice has become progressively hoarse since arrival.","zh":"自到院后患者声音逐渐嘶哑。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client coughs up dark, carbonaceous sputum.","zh":"患者咳出黑色含炭痰。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"A deep partial-thickness burn is present on the left forearm.","zh":"左前臂有深二度烧伤。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Pain at the forearm is rated 8 out of 10.","zh":"前臂疼痛评分为8/10。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Blood pressure is 142/84 mm Hg.","zh":"血压为142/84 mm Hg。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An enclosed-space fire, soot in the nose or mouth, progressive hoarseness, and carbonaceous sputum are classic inhalation-injury cues. Airway edema can progress rapidly, so these findings require immediate airway evaluation and preparation for early definitive airway management. The extremity burn, pain score, and mildly elevated blood pressure do not specifically indicate inhalation injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"封闭空间火灾、鼻口内烟灰、进行性声音嘶哑和含炭痰是典型吸入性损伤线索。气道水肿可能迅速进展，因此这些发现需要立即评估气道并准备早期建立确切气道。四肢烧伤、疼痛评分和轻度血压升高并不特异提示吸入性损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For burn airway questions, prioritize exposure setting and upper-airway changes over the visible size or pain of an extremity burn.","testTakingStrategyZh":"烧伤气道题应优先关注暴露环境和上气道变化，而不是四肢烧伤的可见面积或疼痛程度。","sourceMetadata":"American Burn Association, Advanced Burn Life Support principles for inhalation injury","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2033,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_hl_ect_preprocedure_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.563","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.563.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.563.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,34],"fullStemEn":"The client is scheduled for electroconvulsive therapy under general anesthesia. Highlight the findings that must be corrected before transport to the procedure area.","fullStemZh":"患者计划在全身麻醉下接受电休克治疗。标出送往治疗区前必须纠正的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that must be corrected before transport to the procedure area.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出送往治疗区前必须纠正的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is scheduled for electroconvulsive therapy under general anesthesia.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者计划在全身麻醉下接受电休克治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Preprocedure checklist:","zh":"术前核对表："},{"id":"s1","en":"The client ate toast and drank coffee 2 hours ago.","zh":"患者2小时前吃了吐司并喝了咖啡。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"A removable partial denture remains in the client's mouth.","zh":"患者口中仍留有可摘局部义齿。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The consent form is unsigned, and the client asks what the treatment will do.","zh":"知情同意书尚未签署，患者询问该治疗会有什么作用。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client voided 20 minutes ago.","zh":"患者20分钟前已排尿。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"A saline lock is patent.","zh":"静脉留置通道通畅。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Blood pressure is 132/78 mm Hg.","zh":"血压为132/78 mm Hg。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ECT uses general anesthesia, so recent solid food creates aspiration risk. Removable dental appliances must be removed to prevent airway obstruction or oral injury. Valid informed consent must be completed before the procedure, and the client's question shows that further explanation by the responsible clinician is needed. Voiding, patent IV access, and a stable blood pressure support readiness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ECT需要全身麻醉，因此近期进食固体食物会增加误吸风险。可摘牙具必须取下，以防气道阻塞或口腔损伤。术前必须完成有效知情同意，患者的提问说明需要由负责的临床人员进一步解释。排尿、静脉通道通畅和血压稳定均支持术前准备充分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat ECT as a brief procedure under anesthesia: verify fasting, remove loose oral appliances, confirm consent, and ensure IV access.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将ECT视为全身麻醉下的短时操作：核实禁食、取下松动口腔器具、确认知情同意并确保静脉通道。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf, StatPearls, Electroconvulsive Therapy; standard anesthesia preprocedure safety","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2034,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_hl_fetal_tachysystole_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.564","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.564.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.564.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,57],"fullStemEn":"A client at 40 weeks is receiving oxytocin. Highlight the fetal-monitoring findings that indicate uterine tachysystole with fetal intolerance and require immediate intrauterine resuscitative actions.","fullStemZh":"一名孕40周的产妇正在接受缩宫素输注。标出提示子宫收缩过频并伴胎儿不耐受、需要立即进行宫内复苏措施的胎儿监护发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the fetal-monitoring findings that indicate uterine tachysystole with fetal intolerance and require immediate intrauterine resuscitative actions.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出提示子宫收缩过频并伴胎儿不耐受、需要立即进行宫内复苏措施的胎儿监护发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client at 40 weeks is receiving oxytocin.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名孕40周的产妇正在接受缩宫素输注。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Ten-minute tracing summary:","zh":"10分钟监护摘要："},{"id":"s1","en":"There are 6 contractions in 10 minutes.","zh":"10分钟内有6次宫缩。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Fetal heart rate baseline is 145/min.","zh":"胎心率基线为145次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Baseline variability is minimal.","zh":"基线变异为最小变异。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Gradual decelerations recur, with each nadir occurring after the peak of the contraction.","zh":"反复出现渐进性减速，每次最低点均在宫缩峰值之后。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Maternal blood pressure is 118/70 mm Hg.","zh":"产妇血压为118/70 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Maternal temperature is 98.2 °F (36.8 °C).","zh":"产妇体温为98.2 °F (36.8 °C)。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"More than 5 contractions in 10 minutes is uterine tachysystole. Minimal variability plus recurrent gradual decelerations whose nadirs occur after contraction peaks identifies fetal intolerance with recurrent late decelerations. With oxytocin infusing, the nurse should stop the oxytocin, reposition the client laterally, increase an isotonic IV infusion as prescribed or per protocol, and escalate if the pattern does not resolve. Routine oxygen is not keyed unless maternal hypoxia is present.","rationaleCorrectZh":"10分钟内超过5次宫缩属于子宫收缩过频。最小变异并伴反复渐进性减速，且最低点位于宫缩峰值之后，提示胎儿不耐受及反复晚期减速。正在输注缩宫素时，护士应停止缩宫素、协助产妇侧卧，并按医嘱或方案增加等渗静脉液体；若图形不缓解则升级处理。除非产妇低氧，否则不将常规吸氧作为关键措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read contraction frequency, variability, and the timing of the deceleration nadir separately, then combine them into one interpretation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分别读取宫缩频率、基线变异以及减速最低点与宫缩的时间关系，再将三者合并判断。","sourceMetadata":"NICHD 2008 fetal heart rate definitions; AWHONN fetal monitoring principles; Project Shrimp NCLEX-Question-Schema fetal_monitoring rules","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2035,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_hl_advocacy_transfusion_refusal_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.565","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.565.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.565.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[172,237],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,64],"fullStemEn":"An alert adult with decision-making capacity refuses a blood transfusion after the risks, benefits, and alternatives are explained. The family insists that blood be given. Highlight the nursing actions that protect the client's autonomy.","fullStemZh":"一名意识清楚且具有决策能力的成年患者在获知输血的风险、获益和替代方案后拒绝输血。家属坚持要求输血。标出保护患者自主权的护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nursing actions that protect the client's autonomy.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出保护患者自主权的护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The family insists that blood be given.","penultimateSentenceZh":"家属坚持要求输血。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Planned nursing actions:","zh":"拟采取的护理措施："},{"id":"s1","en":"Ask the client to explain their understanding of the consequences and available alternatives.","zh":"请患者说明其对后果及可选替代方案的理解。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Document the client's informed refusal and stated preferences in the health record.","zh":"在病历中记录患者的知情拒绝及其表达的意愿。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Communicate the refusal to the care team and ensure the blood product is not administered.","zh":"将拒绝意愿告知医疗团队，并确保不实施输血。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Ask the spouse to sign the transfusion consent instead.","zh":"请配偶代替患者签署输血同意书。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Tell the client that other care may be withheld unless transfusion is accepted.","zh":"告诉患者，若不接受输血，其他治疗也可能被停止。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Delay symptom treatment until the family and client agree.","zh":"在患者与家属达成一致前推迟症状治疗。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A capable adult may refuse recommended treatment. The nurse verifies that the refusal is informed, documents the client's decision, communicates it to the team, and prevents treatment that the client declined. Family members cannot override the decision of a capable client, and coercion or withholding unrelated care violates autonomy and advocacy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具有决策能力的成年人可以拒绝推荐治疗。护士应确认拒绝属于知情决定，记录患者选择，告知医疗团队，并防止实施患者已拒绝的治疗。家属不能推翻有能力患者的决定；强迫或停止无关治疗均违反自主权和患者权益维护原则。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In autonomy conflicts, first identify who currently has decision-making capacity. A capable client's informed choice outranks family preference.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理自主权冲突时，先确定谁目前具备决策能力。具有能力患者的知情选择优先于家属偏好。","sourceMetadata":"American Nurses Association Code of Ethics; informed refusal and patient autonomy principles","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2036,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_fib_reflection_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.566","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Therapeutic Communication","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.566.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.566.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,245],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,80],"fullStemEn":"A client says, “Since the diagnosis, my family looks at me as if I am a different person.” The nurse replies, “You feel that your family now sees you differently.” Enter the one-word therapeutic communication technique demonstrated by the nurse.","fullStemZh":"患者说：“自从确诊以后，家人看我的眼神就像我变成了另一个人。”护士回答：“你觉得家人现在对你的看法不同了。”请输入护士所使用的一个英文单词的治疗性沟通技巧名称。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the one-word therapeutic communication technique demonstrated by the nurse.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入护士所使用的一个英文单词的治疗性沟通技巧名称。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse replies, “You feel that your family now sees you differently.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士回答：“你觉得家人现在对你的看法不同了。”","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Technique","zh":"沟通技巧"},"acceptable":["reflection"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse mirrors the client's expressed perception back to the client without adding advice, interpretation, or a new topic. This technique is reflection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士将患者表达的感受和看法原样反映给患者，没有加入建议、解释或新话题。这种技巧称为reflection（反映）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the nurse returns the client's feeling or idea in nearly the same meaning, identify reflection rather than advice or interpretation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当护士以几乎相同的含义将患者的感受或想法反馈回去时，应识别为reflection，而不是建议或解释。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf, Nursing Fundamentals, therapeutic communication techniques","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2037,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_fib_cows_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.567","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.567.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.567.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,309],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,87],"fullStemEn":"A client who stopped using heroin has resting pulse 104/min, dilated pupils, rhinorrhea, yawning, piloerection, abdominal cramping, and anxiety. The protocol requires the nurse to quantify opioid withdrawal severity before medication dosing. Enter the four-letter abbreviation for the standardized scale used.","fullStemZh":"一名停止使用海洛因的患者出现静息脉搏104次/分、瞳孔扩大、流涕、打哈欠、立毛、腹部痉挛和焦虑。方案要求护士在给药前量化阿片类戒断严重度。请输入所用标准量表的四字母英文缩写。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the four-letter abbreviation for the standardized scale used.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入所用标准量表的四字母英文缩写。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The protocol requires the nurse to quantify opioid withdrawal severity before medication dosing.","penultimateSentenceZh":"方案要求护士在给药前量化阿片类戒断严重度。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Four-letter scale abbreviation","zh":"四字母量表缩写"},"acceptable":["COWS"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"COWS stands for Clinical Opiate Withdrawal Scale. It scores observable and reported opioid-withdrawal findings such as pulse, sweating, restlessness, pupil size, gastrointestinal upset, yawning, rhinorrhea, tremor, anxiety, piloerection, and aches.","rationaleCorrectZh":"COWS代表Clinical Opiate Withdrawal Scale（临床阿片戒断量表）。该量表对脉搏、出汗、坐立不安、瞳孔大小、胃肠道不适、打哈欠、流涕、震颤、焦虑、立毛和疼痛等可观察或患者报告的戒断表现进行评分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link the substance to its dedicated scale: opioid withdrawal uses COWS; do not substitute an alcohol-withdrawal scale.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将物质类型与专用量表对应：阿片类戒断使用COWS，不要用酒精戒断量表代替。","sourceMetadata":"National Institute on Drug Abuse, Clinical Opiate Withdrawal Scale (COWS)","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2038,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_fib_siadh_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.568","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.568.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.568.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[296,343],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,120],"fullStemEn":"Three days after a subarachnoid hemorrhage, a client has serum sodium 122 mEq/L, serum osmolality 260 mOsm/kg, urine osmolality 520 mOsm/kg, urine sodium 58 mEq/L, normal blood pressure, moist mucous membranes, and no edema. Adrenal, thyroid, renal, and glucose abnormalities have been excluded. Enter the acronym for the most likely disorder.","fullStemZh":"蛛网膜下腔出血3天后，一名患者血清钠122 mEq/L、血清渗透压260 mOsm/kg、尿渗透压520 mOsm/kg、尿钠58 mEq/L，血压正常、黏膜湿润且无水肿。已排除肾上腺、甲状腺、肾功能和血糖异常。请输入最可能疾病的英文缩写。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the acronym for the most likely disorder.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入最可能疾病的英文缩写。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Adrenal, thyroid, renal, and glucose abnormalities have been excluded.","penultimateSentenceZh":"已排除肾上腺、甲状腺、肾功能和血糖异常。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Disorder acronym","zh":"疾病缩写"},"acceptable":["SIADH"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"SIADH causes hypotonic hyponatremia with inappropriately concentrated urine and elevated urine sodium in a clinically euvolemic client. A central nervous system injury is a recognized trigger, and the stated exclusions remove major competing causes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"SIADH会导致低渗性低钠血症，同时尿液不适当地浓缩、尿钠升高，而患者临床上处于等容量状态。中枢神经系统损伤是已知诱因，题干已排除主要竞争性原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For hyponatremia, compare serum tonicity, urine concentration, and volume status. Low serum osmolality plus concentrated urine in euvolemia points to SIADH.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析低钠血症时，应比较血清张力、尿液浓度和容量状态。低血清渗透压、尿液浓缩且临床等容量提示SIADH。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf, StatPearls, Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion, NBK507777","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2039,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_fib_suicide_direct_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.569","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.569.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.569.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,85],"fullStemEn":"A client says, “Everyone would be better off without me.” To assess immediate self-harm risk directly, the nurse asks, “Are you thinking about _____?” Enter the exact one-word term that completes the question.","fullStemZh":"一名患者说：“没有我，大家都会过得更好。”为直接评估即时自伤风险，护士问：“Are you thinking about _____?” 请输入完成该问题的准确英文单词。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the exact one-word term that completes the question.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入完成该问题的准确英文单词。","penultimateSentenceEn":"To assess immediate self-harm risk directly, the nurse asks, “Are you thinking about _____?”","penultimateSentenceZh":"为直接评估即时自伤风险，护士问：“Are you thinking about _____?”","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"One-word term","zh":"一个英文单词"},"acceptable":["suicide"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should ask directly and unambiguously about suicide. Asking the question does not introduce the idea; it clarifies risk and supports timely safety assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应直接且明确地询问suicide（自杀）。直接提问不会把这个想法灌输给患者，而是能够澄清风险并及时进行安全评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client makes a possible suicide cue, choose plain direct language rather than reassurance or euphemism.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者出现可能的自杀线索时，应使用明确直接的语言，而不是安慰或委婉表达。","sourceMetadata":"National Institute of Mental Health, Ask Suicide-Screening Questions (ASQ) Toolkit","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"To assess immediate self-harm risk directly, the nurse asks, “Are you thinking about _____?”","controlSentenceZh":"为直接评估即时自伤风险，护士问：“Are you thinking about _____?”"}
{"queueIndex":2040,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_or_hyperkalemia_dialysis_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.570","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.570.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.570.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[212,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,73],"fullStemEn":"A client with end-stage kidney disease missed dialysis and now has potassium 7.1 mEq/L with widened QRS complexes. The client has a functioning dialysis access, and all emergency prescriptions have been entered. Place the nursing actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"一名终末期肾病患者漏做透析，目前血钾7.1 mEq/L并出现QRS波增宽。患者有可用的透析通路，所有急救医嘱均已开具。请将护理措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护理措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has a functioning dialysis access, and all emergency prescriptions have been entered.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者有可用的透析通路，所有急救医嘱均已开具。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place the client on continuous cardiac monitoring.","zh":"为患者进行持续心电监护。"},{"id":"D","en":"Initiate urgent hemodialysis to remove potassium from the body.","zh":"启动紧急血液透析，以从体内清除钾。"},{"id":"E","en":"Recheck serum potassium, blood glucose, and the cardiac rhythm after treatment.","zh":"治疗后复查血钾、血糖和心律。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the prescribed IV regular insulin with dextrose.","zh":"给予医嘱的静脉普通胰岛素和葡萄糖。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer the prescribed IV calcium gluconate.","zh":"给予医嘱的静脉葡萄糖酸钙。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Continuous monitoring is established first because severe hyperkalemia with QRS widening can rapidly cause lethal dysrhythmia. IV calcium then stabilizes the myocardium. Insulin with dextrose temporarily shifts potassium into cells. Urgent hemodialysis definitively removes potassium in this dialysis-dependent client. Potassium, glucose, and rhythm are reassessed for treatment response, rebound hyperkalemia, and hypoglycemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先建立持续心电监护，因为伴QRS增宽的重度高钾血症可迅速导致致命性心律失常。随后静脉钙剂稳定心肌；胰岛素加葡萄糖暂时将钾移入细胞；紧急血液透析在该依赖透析的患者中从体内彻底清除钾。最后复查血钾、血糖和心律，以评估治疗反应、反跳性高钾血症和低血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the sequence monitor → protect the heart → shift potassium → remove potassium → reassess.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用“监护→保护心肌→转移钾→清除钾→复评”的顺序。","sourceMetadata":"UK Kidney Association Clinical Practice Guideline: Treatment of Acute Hyperkalaemia in Adults, 2023","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2041,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_or_dry_chemical_burn_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.571","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Patient & Environment Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.571.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.571.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[258,308],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,81],"fullStemEn":"A client's airway, breathing, and circulation are stable after a dry industrial chemical powder spills over the torso and arms. The product safety sheet confirms that the chemical is not water-reactive and directs water irrigation after dry decontamination. Place the nursing actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"一名患者躯干和双臂被干燥工业化学粉末污染，目前气道、呼吸和循环稳定。产品安全说明书确认该化学品不与水反应，并要求在干式去污后用水冲洗。请将护理措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将护理措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The product safety sheet confirms that the chemical is not water-reactive and directs water irrigation after dry decontamination.","penultimateSentenceZh":"产品安全说明书确认该化学品不与水反应，并要求在干式去污后用水冲洗。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Don appropriate personal protective equipment.","zh":"穿戴适当的个人防护装备。"},{"id":"D","en":"Irrigate the exposed skin with copious tepid water according to the safety sheet.","zh":"按照安全说明书用大量温水冲洗暴露皮肤。"},{"id":"E","en":"Cover the client with a clean dry sheet and prevent hypothermia.","zh":"用清洁干燥床单覆盖患者并预防低体温。"},{"id":"C","en":"Brush all visible dry powder from the skin without rubbing it into tissue.","zh":"将皮肤上所有可见干粉刷除，避免将其揉入组织。"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove contaminated clothing and jewelry while containing the material.","zh":"在控制污染物扩散的同时脱去受污染衣物和首饰。"},{"id":"F","en":"Reassess the skin, pain, temperature, and neurovascular status of the affected extremities.","zh":"重新评估皮肤、疼痛、体温及受累肢体的神经血管状态。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first protects staff from secondary contamination. Contaminated clothing and jewelry are removed and contained, then remaining dry powder is brushed away before water is introduced. Because the safety sheet confirms the substance is not water-reactive, copious tepid irrigation follows. The client is then covered and kept warm, and the nurse reassesses the burn and distal neurovascular status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先防止工作人员受到二次污染。随后脱去并封存受污染衣物和首饰，再在接触水前刷除残留干粉。由于安全说明书确认该物质不与水反应，之后用大量温水冲洗。最后覆盖患者并保暖，重新评估烧伤及远端神经血管状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For dry chemicals, use responder protection → remove the source → brush dry material → irrigate only when water safety is established → warm and reassess.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理干燥化学品时，按“保护救援者→去除污染源→刷除干粉→确认可用水后冲洗→保暖并复评”的顺序。","sourceMetadata":"CDC Chemical Emergencies decontamination guidance; product-specific safety data sheet principles","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2042,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_fmtgap_2026_07_14_or_toddler_choking_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.572","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.572.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.572.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,61],"fullStemEn":"A conscious 2-year-old suddenly cannot speak, cough, or breathe while eating. Another adult is calling emergency services and bringing an AED. Place the rescuer's actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"一名清醒的2岁幼儿进食时突然无法说话、咳嗽或呼吸。另一名成人正在呼叫急救服务并取来AED。请将救援者的操作按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the rescuer's actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将救援者的操作按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Another adult is calling emergency services and bringing an AED.","penultimateSentenceZh":"另一名成人正在呼叫急救服务并取来AED。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"If the child becomes unresponsive, lower the child to a firm surface and begin CPR with chest compressions; look for and remove only a visible object before breaths.","zh":"若幼儿失去反应，将其放到坚硬平面并从胸外按压开始CPR；人工呼吸前仅取出可见异物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Repeat cycles of back blows and abdominal thrusts until the object is expelled or the child becomes unresponsive.","zh":"反复进行背部拍击和腹部冲击，直至异物排出或幼儿失去反应。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give 5 abdominal thrusts.","zh":"给予5次腹部冲击。"},{"id":"A","en":"Give 5 firm back blows between the shoulder blades.","zh":"在两肩胛骨之间给予5次有力背部拍击。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A responsive child older than 1 year with severe airway obstruction receives 5 back blows followed by 5 abdominal thrusts. The rescuer repeats these cycles until the obstruction clears or the child becomes unresponsive. If unresponsive, the rescuer begins CPR with compressions and removes an object only when it is visible; blind finger sweeps are avoided.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于1岁以上、仍有反应但存在严重气道梗阻的儿童，应先进行5次背部拍击，再进行5次腹部冲击。重复这些循环，直至梗阻解除或儿童失去反应。若失去反应，应从胸外按压开始CPR，并且只在看见异物时取出，避免盲目手指清扫。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Age matters: a toddler is older than 1 year, so abdominal thrusts are used after back blows; infants receive chest thrusts instead.","testTakingStrategyZh":"年龄很重要：幼儿大于1岁，因此背部拍击后使用腹部冲击；婴儿则使用胸部冲击。","sourceMetadata":"American Red Cross first aid guidance for choking in a responsive child older than 1 year","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2043,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_bt_client_advocacy_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.573","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.573.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.573.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[351,455],"terminalOffsetsZh":[112,140],"fullStemEn":"A client with sickle cell disease is admitted for a vaso-occlusive crisis. The individualized pain plan calls for prompt analgesia and reassessment, but 45 minutes after reporting pain 9/10, no analgesic has been given. The client is alert, respiratory rate is 18/min, and a clinician says, ‘The client looks too comfortable to be in that much pain.’ Complete the bow-tie to identify the priority issue, two nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名镰状细胞病患者因血管阻塞危象住院。个体化疼痛方案要求及时镇痛并重新评估，但患者报告疼痛 9/10 后已过 45 分钟，仍未获得镇痛药。患者清醒，呼吸频率 18 次/分，一名临床人员说：“患者看起来太舒服，不像有那么痛。”完成蝴蝶结图，确定首要问题、两项护理行动和两项监测指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie to identify the priority issue, two nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图，确定首要问题、两项护理行动和两项监测指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is alert, respiratory rate is 18/min, and a clinician says, ‘The client looks too comfortable to be in that much pain.’","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者清醒，呼吸频率 18 次/分，一名临床人员说：“患者看起来太舒服，不像有那么痛。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority issue","zh":"首要问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Opioid-induced respiratory depression","zh":"阿片类药物所致呼吸抑制"},{"id":"c3","en":"Resolved vaso-occlusive pain","zh":"血管阻塞性疼痛已缓解"},{"id":"c1","en":"Unrelieved acute pain with an advocacy barrier","zh":"急性疼痛未缓解并存在权益维护障碍"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Nursing actions","zh":"护理行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"a3","en":"Wait for tachycardia or hypertension before acting","zh":"等待出现心动过速或高血压后再行动"},{"id":"a1","en":"Reassess pain using the client's self-report and individualized plan","zh":"依据患者自述和个体化方案重新评估疼痛"},{"id":"a4","en":"Label the request as drug-seeking in the handoff","zh":"在交接中把患者描述为“寻求药物”"},{"id":"a2","en":"Escalate through the provider and charge-nurse chain to obtain timely treatment","zh":"通过医护提供者和责任护士汇报链升级处理以获得及时治疗"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"监测指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p2","en":"Respiratory rate and sedation after analgesia","zh":"镇痛后的呼吸频率和镇静程度"},{"id":"p4","en":"INR","zh":"国际标准化比值（INR）"},{"id":"p3","en":"Daily weight","zh":"每日体重"},{"id":"p1","en":"Pain intensity and functional impact","zh":"疼痛强度及对功能的影响"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority issue is unrelieved acute pain complicated by an advocacy barrier: pain is whatever the client reports, and calm appearance does not invalidate the report. The nurse should reassess using the individualized plan and escalate through the clinical chain so prescribed treatment is obtained without further delay. Pain/function and opioid safety findings must then be reassessed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首要问题是急性疼痛未缓解，并存在维护患者权益的障碍：疼痛应以患者自述为准，外表平静不能否定疼痛。护士应依据个体化方案重新评估，并通过临床汇报链升级处理，以便及时获得医嘱治疗。随后必须重新评估疼痛/功能及阿片类药物安全指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the client-reported problem from staff assumptions, then pair advocacy actions with both symptom relief and treatment-safety monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把患者自述的问题与工作人员的主观推断分开，再将维护权益的行动与症状缓解和治疗安全监测配对。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Hematology, 2020 Guidelines for Sickle Cell Disease: Management of Acute and Chronic Pain, Recommendation 1a (rapid assessment and analgesia within 1 hour with reassessment every 30–60 minutes), https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7322963/; The Joint Commission, R3 Report Issue 11, individualized pain assessment, reassessment, and treatment, https://digitalassets.jointcommission.org/api/public/content/565820ca0d27416d957efe6b6e1d4705?v=36bcc020","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2044,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_dc_client_advocacy_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.574","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.574.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.574.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[135,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,57],"fullStemEn":"At a hospital outpatient clinic, a capable adult client says that a nursing student may not observe the client's intimate examination. The licensed clinician can perform the examination without the student.","fullStemZh":"在一家医院门诊，一名有决策能力的成年患者表示，不允许护理学生旁观其私密检查。持证临床人员无需学生在场即可完成检查。","terminalSentenceEn":"The licensed clinician can perform the examination without the student.","terminalSentenceZh":"持证临床人员无需学生在场即可完成检查。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At a hospital outpatient clinic, a capable adult client says that a nursing student may not observe the client's intimate examination.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在一家医院门诊，一名有决策能力的成年患者表示，不允许护理学生旁观其私密检查。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{response}} because the client has a right to {{right}}.","zh":"护士应当{{response}}，因为患者有权享有{{right}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"response","options":[{"id":"r1","en":"honor the request and ask the student to leave","zh":"尊重要求并请学生离开"},{"id":"r2","en":"ask the student to remain but stand farther away","zh":"让学生留下但站得更远"},{"id":"r3","en":"tell the client that observation is required in a teaching hospital","zh":"告知患者教学医院必须允许旁观"}],"correct":"r1"},{"id":"right","options":[{"id":"p3","en":"public access to the clinical encounter","zh":"公众接触临床过程"},{"id":"p1","en":"personal privacy and participation in care","zh":"个人隐私和参与护理"},{"id":"p2","en":"staff convenience during scheduling","zh":"工作人员排班便利"}],"correct":"p1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should honor the request and ask the student to leave. The client retains rights to personal privacy and meaningful participation in care; the teaching mission does not override those rights.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应尊重患者要求并请学生离开。患者仍享有个人隐私和参与护理决策的权利；教学需要不能凌驾于这些权利之上。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a capable client states a preference about who may be present, prioritize privacy and participation unless an immediate safety need requires otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当有决策能力的患者明确表示谁可以在场时，应优先考虑隐私和参与权，除非存在即时安全需要。","sourceMetadata":"42 CFR 482.13(b)(2) and 482.13(c)(1), hospital patient rights to participate in care and personal privacy, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-482/subpart-B/section-482.13","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At a hospital outpatient clinic, a capable adult client says that a nursing student may not observe the client's intimate examination.","controlSentenceZh":"在一家医院门诊，一名有决策能力的成年患者表示，不允许护理学生旁观其私密检查。"}
{"queueIndex":2045,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_bt_confidentiality_hipaa_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.575","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.575.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.575.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[264,285],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,93],"fullStemEn":"A nurse posts in a private social-media group: ‘You would not believe today's 19-year-old trauma case in room 812,’ and includes the admission date and a photo showing the client's distinctive tattoo but not the client's face or name. A coworker reports the post. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名护士在私人社交媒体群组中发帖：“你们绝对想不到今天 812 房那名 19 岁创伤患者的情况”，并附上显示患者独特纹身的照片，但没有显示脸部或姓名。一名同事举报了该帖子。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A coworker reports the post.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名同事举报了该帖子。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely issue","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Properly de-identified educational communication","zh":"已适当去标识化的教学交流"},{"id":"c3","en":"Authorized disclosure for treatment","zh":"为治疗目的获授权的披露"},{"id":"c1","en":"Potential identifiable PHI disclosure requiring privacy and breach assessment","zh":"可能披露可识别 PHI，需要隐私和泄露评估"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Notify the supervisor and privacy officer immediately through the incident process","zh":"立即通过事件流程通知主管和隐私官"},{"id":"a1","en":"Cease further sharing and remove or secure the content as directed by privacy response policy","zh":"停止进一步分享，并按隐私响应政策指示删除或保护相关内容"},{"id":"a3","en":"Rename the private group and leave the post online","zh":"更改私人群组名称并保留帖子"},{"id":"a4","en":"Wait to report unless the client complains","zh":"除非患者投诉，否则等待不报"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Information to monitor or assess","zh":"需监测或评估的信息"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Client platelet count","zh":"患者血小板计数"},{"id":"p2","en":"Mitigation completed and privacy-team breach determination","zh":"已完成的补救及隐私团队的泄露判定"},{"id":"p3","en":"Number of reactions or likes","zh":"互动或点赞数量"},{"id":"p1","en":"Identifiers disclosed, recipients, and potential redisclosure","zh":"披露的识别信息、接收者及可能的再次传播"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The combined details can identify the client even without a name or face, creating a potential impermissible disclosure that requires the organization's privacy and breach-response process. The nurse should stop further disclosure and promptly report the incident; the privacy team must assess identifiers, recipients, mitigation, and breach-notification obligations.","rationaleCorrectZh":"即使没有姓名或脸部，组合信息仍可能识别患者，构成潜在的不当披露，需要启动机构的隐私和泄露响应流程。护士应停止进一步披露并立即报告；隐私团队必须评估识别信息、接收者、补救措施及泄露通知义务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"HIPAA identifiability depends on the whole set of clues, not only whether a name appears.","testTakingStrategyZh":"HIPAA 的可识别性取决于全部线索，而不仅仅是是否出现姓名。","sourceMetadata":"HHS, Guidance Regarding Methods for De-identification of Protected Health Information under 45 CFR 164.514, and 45 CFR 164.400-414 Breach Notification Rule, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/privacy/special-topics/de-identification/index.html ; https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-D","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2046,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_or_confidentiality_hipaa_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.576","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.576.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.576.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[472,499],"terminalOffsetsZh":[136,145],"fullStemEn":"A client submits a written request to amend an inaccurate statement in the electronic health record. Facility policy, consistent with HIPAA, uses this sequence: receive the written request without changing the original entry; route it to Health Information Management (HIM); have the designated reviewer decide and issue the required response; if accepted, append or link the amendment and notify persons the client identifies as having received the disputed information. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者提交书面申请，要求更正电子健康记录中的不准确信息。机构政策与 HIPAA 一致，规定顺序为：接收书面申请且不改动原始记录；转交健康信息管理部门（HIM）；由指定审核人员作出决定并发出规定答复；若接受申请，则追加或链接更正内容，并通知患者指出的曾接收争议信息的人员。请按顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy, consistent with HIPAA, uses this sequence: receive the written request without changing the original entry; route it to Health Information Management (HIM); have the designated reviewer decide and issue the required response; if accepted, append or link the amendment and notify persons the client identifies as having received the disputed information.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策与 HIPAA 一致，规定顺序为：接收书面申请且不改动原始记录；转交健康信息管理部门（HIM）；由指定审核人员作出决定并发出规定答复；若接受申请，则追加或链接更正内容，并通知患者指出的曾接收争议信息的人员。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Receive the written request and preserve the original entry unchanged.","zh":"接收书面申请，并保持原始记录不变。"},{"id":"A","en":"Route the request to HIM for the formal amendment process.","zh":"将申请转交 HIM，进入正式更正流程。"},{"id":"D","en":"Have the designated reviewer decide and issue the required response.","zh":"由指定审核人员作出决定并发出规定答复。"},{"id":"B","en":"If accepted, append or link the amendment and notify the agreed recipients.","zh":"若申请获接受，追加或链接更正内容并通知约定的接收者。"}],"correct":["C","A","D","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The request is first received and the original record preserved, then routed to HIM for the designated review. The reviewer issues the decision and required response. If accepted, the organization appends or links the amendment rather than deleting the original and makes the required notifications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先接收申请并保留原始记录，然后转交 HIM 进行指定审核。审核人员作出决定并发出规定答复。若申请获接受，机构应追加或链接更正内容，而不是删除原始记录，并完成规定通知。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the explicit facility sequence and remember that an amendment supplements the record; it does not erase the original documentation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按照题干给出的机构顺序，并记住更正是补充记录，而不是抹去原始记录。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR 164.526, Amendment of protected health information, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-E/section-164.526","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2047,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_fib_conflict_resolution_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.577","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.577.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.577.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[92,100],"fullStemEn":"The unit uses the TeamSTEPPS DESC script for a difficult conversation: Describe the situation, Express concerns, _____ alternatives, and state Consequences. Enter the missing step.","fullStemZh":"科室使用 TeamSTEPPS 的 DESC 脚本进行困难对话：描述（Describe）情况、表达（Express）担忧、_____ 替代方案，并说明后果（Consequences）。填写缺少的步骤。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the missing step.","terminalSentenceZh":"填写缺少的步骤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit uses the TeamSTEPPS DESC script for a difficult conversation: Describe the situation, Express concerns, _____ alternatives, and state Consequences.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室使用 TeamSTEPPS 的 DESC 脚本进行困难对话：描述（Describe）情况、表达（Express）担忧、_____ 替代方案，并说明后果（Consequences）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Missing DESC step","zh":"缺少的 DESC 步骤"},"acceptable":["Suggest","suggest","Suggest alternatives","suggest alternatives"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"DESC stands for Describe, Express, Suggest, and Consequences. The missing step is Suggest alternatives: state a specific, workable change rather than only describing the problem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DESC 代表 Describe（描述）、Express（表达）、Suggest（建议）和 Consequences（后果）。缺少的步骤是 Suggest alternatives（提出替代方案）：给出具体、可执行的改变，而不只是描述问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For acronym blanks, map each letter to its action and confirm the answer fits grammatically in the sentence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到首字母缩写填空题时，把每个字母对应到行动，并确认答案在句子中语法通顺。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Tool: DESC (Describe, Express, Suggest, Consequences), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/desc.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2048,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_hl_conflict_resolution_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.578","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.578.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.578.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[177,266],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,69],"fullStemEn":"A family member is upset because the unit's quiet-hours policy requires late-night video calls that disturb a roommate to be moved from a semiprivate room to the family lounge. Highlight the nurse's statements that use constructive conflict-resolution communication.","fullStemZh":"一名家属因病区安静时段政策感到不满：如果深夜视频通话打扰室友，通话必须从半私密病房转移到家属休息室。标出护士使用建设性冲突解决沟通的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nurse's statements that use constructive conflict-resolution communication.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出护士使用建设性冲突解决沟通的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A family member is upset because the unit's quiet-hours policy requires late-night video calls that disturb a roommate to be moved from a semiprivate room to the family lounge.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名家属因病区安静时段政策感到不满：如果深夜视频通话打扰室友，通话必须从半私密病房转移到家属休息室。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse says:","zh":"护士说："},{"id":"s2","en":"I can see that staying connected tonight is important to your family.","zh":"我理解今晚保持联系对你们家人很重要。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The roommate is sleeping, and the video call can be heard across the room.","zh":"室友正在睡觉，而且整个房间都能听到视频通话。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The family lounge is open, so we can move there and continue the call.","zh":"家属休息室现在开放，我们可以转移到那里继续通话。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Can we agree to use the lounge for the rest of tonight's call?","zh":"我们能否商定今晚剩余的通话在家属休息室进行？","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"You are being selfish and inconsiderate.","zh":"你们这样做很自私，也不替别人考虑。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"If you make one more sound, I will have security remove you immediately.","zh":"如果你们再发出一点声音，我就立即让保安把你们带走。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Constructive conflict communication acknowledges the person's concern, describes the observable impact without blame, offers a feasible alternative, and seeks agreement. Character attacks and disproportionate threats escalate a nonviolent disagreement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建设性冲突沟通应承认对方的关切，不带指责地描述可观察影响，提出可行替代方案，并寻求一致。人身指责和不相称的威胁会升级原本没有暴力的分歧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose statements that acknowledge, describe facts, offer a workable option, and confirm the next step; reject labels and premature threats.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能够承认关切、描述事实、提出可行选择并确认下一步的陈述；排除贴标签和过早威胁。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Conflict in Teams (including conflict with patients and family caregivers), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/conflict.html; Tool: DESC, objective description, concerns, alternatives, and agreement, https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/desc.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2049,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_bt_discharge_planning_handoff_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.579","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.579.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.579.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[309,330],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,84],"fullStemEn":"A client is ready for discharge after a lymph-node biopsy. The pathology result is still pending. The discharge record lists two specialists, but neither has accepted responsibility for reviewing the result or contacting the client. The client says, ‘I assumed no phone call would mean everything is normal.’ Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在淋巴结活检后准备出院。病理结果仍未出具。出院记录列出两名专科医生，但无人确认负责查看结果或联系患者。患者说：“我以为没人打电话就代表一切正常。”完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client says, ‘I assumed no phone call would mean everything is normal.’","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者说：“我以为没人打电话就代表一切正常。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority transition problem","zh":"首要过渡问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Routine discharge with a complete follow-up plan","zh":"随访计划完整的常规出院"},{"id":"c1","en":"Unsafe discharge transition due to unassigned pending-result follow-up","zh":"待出结果随访无人负责导致不安全出院过渡"},{"id":"c3","en":"Medication-reconciliation discrepancy","zh":"用药核对差异"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions before discharge","zh":"出院前行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"a3","en":"Tell the client that no call means the result is normal","zh":"告诉患者无人来电就代表结果正常"},{"id":"a2","en":"Tell the client and receiving provider what is pending, how results will be communicated, and when follow-up is expected","zh":"告知患者和接收方哪些结果待出、如何通知以及何时预计随访"},{"id":"a1","en":"Identify and document the clinician who accepts responsibility for reviewing and acting on the result","zh":"明确并记录接受审核和处理结果责任的临床人员"},{"id":"a4","en":"Remove the pending test from the discharge summary","zh":"从出院摘要中删除待出检查"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Closed-loop parameters","zh":"闭环指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Final result status and acknowledgment by the responsible clinician","zh":"最终结果状态及负责临床人员的确认"},{"id":"p4","en":"Transportation arrival time","zh":"交通工具到达时间"},{"id":"p2","en":"Completed client contact and documented follow-up action","zh":"已完成的患者联系和记录的随访行动"},{"id":"p3","en":"Daily weight","zh":"每日体重"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is an unsafe transition because ownership of a pending diagnostic result is not assigned and the client has an unsafe 'no news is good news' assumption. Before discharge, the team must identify the responsible clinician, communicate the pending-result plan to the client and receiving provider, and close the loop when the result is reviewed and follow-up occurs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是一次不安全的照护过渡，因为待出诊断结果无人负责，而且患者存在“没有消息就是好消息”的危险假设。出院前，团队必须明确负责的临床人员，向患者和后续医护提供者说明待出结果计划，并在结果被审核和完成随访后闭环。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge safety, look for ownership, communication, and closed-loop confirmation—not merely that a test is listed in the paperwork.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断出院安全时，要寻找责任归属、沟通和闭环确认，而不只是检查项目是否写在文件上。","sourceMetadata":"The Joint Commission, Quick Safety Issue 52, Advancing Safety with Closed-Loop Communication of Test Results, responsibility, escalation, patient engagement, and follow-up, https://www.jointcommission.org/-/media/tjc/newsletters/qs-52-closed-loop-comm-12-3-19-final.pdf; 42 CFR 482.43(c)(5), transfer of necessary medical information at discharge, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-482/subpart-C/section-482.43","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2050,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_fib_discharge_planning_handoff_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.580","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.580.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.580.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[257,369],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,97],"fullStemEn":"Before discharge, the nurse starts a video call with the accepting home-health nurse while the client and daughter are present. The nurse reviews the wound-care plan, the receiving nurse confirms the first visit, and the client corrects the contact number. Enter the name for this transparent transfer of care between two team members in front of the client and family.","fullStemZh":"出院前，护士在患者和女儿在场时，与接收患者的居家护理护士进行视频通话。护士说明伤口护理计划，接收护士确认首次访视时间，患者纠正联系电话。填写这种在患者和家属面前由两名团队成员透明转移照护的名称。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the name for this transparent transfer of care between two team members in front of the client and family.","terminalSentenceZh":"填写这种在患者和家属面前由两名团队成员透明转移照护的名称。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the wound-care plan, the receiving nurse confirms the first visit, and the client corrects the contact number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士说明伤口护理计划，接收护士确认首次访视时间，患者纠正联系电话。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Transfer-of-care method","zh":"照护转移方法"},"acceptable":["warm handoff","warm-handoff","Warm handoff","Warm Handoff","暖式交接"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is a warm handoff. The sending and receiving team members transfer care transparently in front of the client and family, who can hear, clarify, and correct the information.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是暖式交接（warm handoff）。交出方和接收方团队成员在患者及家属面前透明转移照护，使患者和家属能够听取、澄清并纠正信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish a warm handoff from ordinary reporting by looking for both team members and the client or family participating in the transfer.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分暖式交接和普通报告时，要寻找交出方、接收方以及患者或家属共同参与照护转移的线索。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, Warm Handoff: Intervention, definition of a transparent transfer between two healthcare team members in front of the patient and family, https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/reports/engage/interventions/warmhandoff.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2051,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_hl_psychotropic_medications_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.581","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.581.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.581.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[60,157],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,53],"fullStemEn":"A client takes sertraline and began linezolid 24 hours ago. Highlight the findings that support suspected serotonin syndrome and require immediate follow-up.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在服用舍曲林，并于 24 小时前开始使用利奈唑胺。标出支持疑似血清素综合征并需要立即跟进的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that support suspected serotonin syndrome and require immediate follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出支持疑似血清素综合征并需要立即跟进的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client takes sertraline and began linezolid 24 hours ago.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者正在服用舍曲林，并于 24 小时前开始使用利奈唑胺。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Assessment findings:","zh":"评估发现："},{"id":"s2","en":"The client is newly agitated and restless.","zh":"患者新出现躁动和坐立不安。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Temperature is 102.2 °F (39.0 °C) with profuse diaphoresis.","zh":"体温 102.2 °F (39.0 °C)，伴大量出汗。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Deep-tendon reflexes are brisk, with inducible ankle clonus.","zh":"深腱反射活跃，可诱发踝阵挛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client reports mild dry mouth.","zh":"患者报告轻度口干。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Blood pressure is 124/76 mm Hg.","zh":"血压为 124/76 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The client reports no bowel movement for 2 days.","zh":"患者报告 2 天未排便。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Agitation, hyperthermia with diaphoresis, and hyperreflexia with clonus are characteristic serotonin-syndrome findings in a client exposed to serotonergic drugs. Mild dry mouth, isolated constipation, and stable blood pressure do not establish this emergency syndrome.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在接触血清素能药物的患者中，躁动、高热伴出汗、反射亢进伴阵挛是血清素综合征的典型表现。轻度口干、单独便秘和稳定血压不能确立这一急症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Group the findings into mental-status change, autonomic instability, and neuromuscular hyperactivity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把发现分为精神状态改变、自主神经不稳定和神经肌肉过度活动三组。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, ZOLOFT (sertraline) prescribing information, Warnings and Precautions 5.2 Serotonin Syndrome, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=fe9e8b7d-61ea-409d-84aa-3ebd79a046b5; DailyMed, LINEZOLID prescribing information, Warnings and Precautions 5.3, serotonin syndrome with serotonergic agents including SSRIs, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=bc12bd87-5ef0-4ebe-bc00-cbd7896ce08c&type=display","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2052,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_or_psychotropic_medications_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.582","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.582.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.582.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[495,522],"terminalOffsetsZh":[135,144],"fullStemEn":"A client who started lamotrigine 12 days ago develops a widespread blistering rash, oral erosions, and facial edema. Facility policy for a suspected serious medication-related mucocutaneous reaction directs the nurse to: first assess and support immediate airway, breathing, and hemodynamic stability; then withhold the suspected medication; then activate urgent prescriber/rapid-response evaluation; and after stabilization document the reaction and update the allergy/adverse-reaction record. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在开始服用拉莫三嗪 12 天后出现广泛水疱性皮疹、口腔糜烂和面部水肿。机构对疑似严重药物相关皮肤黏膜反应的政策规定：首先评估并支持即时气道、呼吸和血流动力学稳定；随后停用可疑药物；然后启动紧急医护提供者/快速反应评估；患者稳定后记录反应并更新过敏/不良反应记录。请按顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy for a suspected serious medication-related mucocutaneous reaction directs the nurse to: first assess and support immediate airway, breathing, and hemodynamic stability; then withhold the suspected medication; then activate urgent prescriber/rapid-response evaluation; and after stabilization document the reaction and update the allergy/adverse-reaction record.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构对疑似严重药物相关皮肤黏膜反应的政策规定：首先评估并支持即时气道、呼吸和血流动力学稳定；随后停用可疑药物；然后启动紧急医护提供者/快速反应评估；患者稳定后记录反应并更新过敏/不良反应记录。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Withhold lamotrigine and prevent another dose from being administered.","zh":"停用拉莫三嗪并防止再次给药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate urgent prescriber and rapid-response evaluation.","zh":"启动紧急医护提供者和快速反应评估。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess and support airway, breathing, vital signs, and hemodynamic stability.","zh":"评估并支持气道、呼吸、生命体征和血流动力学稳定。"},{"id":"B","en":"After stabilization, document the reaction and update the allergy/adverse-reaction record.","zh":"患者稳定后，记录反应并更新过敏/不良反应记录。"}],"correct":["D","C","A","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The mucosal erosions, blistering rash, and facial edema raise concern for a serious lamotrigine-associated rash. Immediate physiologic stability comes first, followed by withholding lamotrigine, urgent escalation for medical evaluation, and post-stabilization documentation and allergy-record updates.","rationaleCorrectZh":"口腔糜烂、水疱性皮疹和面部水肿提示拉莫三嗪相关严重皮疹。首先确保即时生理稳定，然后停用拉莫三嗪，紧急升级进行医学评估，最后在稳定后完成记录并更新过敏信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the policy's explicit sequence: ABC stability, stop the suspected drug, escalate urgently, then complete durable documentation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按照政策给出的明确顺序：先确保 ABC 稳定，再停用可疑药物，紧急升级处理，最后完成长期记录。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, LAMICTAL (lamotrigine) prescribing information, Boxed Warning and Warnings and Precautions 5.1 Serious Skin Rashes, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=d7e3572d-56fe-4727-2bb4-013ccca22678","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2053,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_hl_parenteral_nutrition_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.583","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.583.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.583.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,40],"fullStemEn":"A client receives parenteral nutrition through a central venous catheter. Highlight the findings that suggest a catheter-related infection and require immediate follow-up.","fullStemZh":"一名患者通过中心静脉导管接受肠外营养。标出提示导管相关感染并需要立即跟进的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that suggest a catheter-related infection and require immediate follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出提示导管相关感染并需要立即跟进的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client receives parenteral nutrition through a central venous catheter.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者通过中心静脉导管接受肠外营养。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Assessment findings:","zh":"评估发现："},{"id":"s2","en":"Temperature is 101.7 °F (38.7 °C), and shaking chills began during the infusion.","zh":"体温 101.7 °F (38.7 °C)，输注期间开始出现寒战。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The insertion site is erythematous and tender with purulent drainage.","zh":"穿刺点发红、压痛并有脓性引流。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Capillary glucose is 146 mg/dL.","zh":"毛细血管血糖为 146 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The transparent dressing is dry, intact, and dated yesterday.","zh":"透明敷料干燥、完整，日期为昨天。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client says, ‘I feel hungry before dinner.’","zh":"患者说：“晚饭前我觉得饿。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fever with shaking chills during an infusion and erythema, tenderness, or purulent drainage at the catheter site are concerning for catheter-related infection. Mild hyperglycemia, hunger, and an intact recently dated dressing do not by themselves indicate a catheter infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"输注期间发热伴寒战，以及导管部位红、痛或脓性引流，提示导管相关感染。轻度高血糖、饥饿感和近期标注日期且完整的敷料本身并不提示导管感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for systemic infection signs plus local catheter-site inflammation or drainage.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找全身感染迹象，以及导管局部炎症或引流。","sourceMetadata":"CDC/HICPAC, Guidelines for the Prevention of Intravascular Catheter-Related Infections, recommendations on catheter-site assessment and suspected infection, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/media/pdfs/Guideline-BSI-H.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2054,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_bt_cardiovascular_endocrine_medications_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.584","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.584.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.584.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[251,272],"terminalOffsetsZh":[93,100],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 2 diabetes takes empagliflozin. After 2 days of poor oral intake, the client has nausea, abdominal pain, deep rapid respirations, glucose 168 mg/dL, positive serum ketones, pH 7.28, bicarbonate 15 mEq/L, and an increased anion gap. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名 2 型糖尿病患者服用恩格列净。进食不良 2 天后，患者出现恶心、腹痛、深快呼吸，血糖 168 mg/dL、血清酮体阳性、pH 7.28、碳酸氢盐 15 mEq/L，阴离子间隙升高。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After 2 days of poor oral intake, the client has nausea, abdominal pain, deep rapid respirations, glucose 168 mg/dL, positive serum ketones, pH 7.28, bicarbonate 15 mEq/L, and an increased anion gap.","penultimateSentenceZh":"进食不良 2 天后，患者出现恶心、腹痛、深快呼吸，血糖 168 mg/dL、血清酮体阳性、pH 7.28、碳酸氢盐 15 mEq/L，阴离子间隙升高。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"c2","en":"Isolated hypoglycemia","zh":"单纯低血糖"},{"id":"c1","en":"SGLT2 inhibitor-associated ketoacidosis with only mild hyperglycemia","zh":"仅轻度高血糖的 SGLT2 抑制剂相关酮症酸中毒"},{"id":"c3","en":"Uncomplicated viral gastroenteritis","zh":"无并发症的病毒性胃肠炎"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Continue empagliflozin until glucose exceeds 250 mg/dL","zh":"继续使用恩格列净，直到血糖超过 250 mg/dL"},{"id":"a1","en":"Withhold empagliflozin and notify the prescriber for urgent ketoacidosis management","zh":"停用恩格列净并通知医护提供者紧急处理酮症酸中毒"},{"id":"a2","en":"Begin prescribed isotonic IV fluids and insulin protocol, adding dextrose as indicated","zh":"开始医嘱等渗静脉补液和胰岛素方案，并按需要加入葡萄糖"},{"id":"a3","en":"Give orange juice as the only treatment","zh":"仅给予橙汁治疗"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"监测指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p2","en":"Serum potassium","zh":"血清钾"},{"id":"p3","en":"INR","zh":"国际标准化比值（INR）"},{"id":"p4","en":"Troponin","zh":"肌钙蛋白"},{"id":"p1","en":"Serum ketones and anion-gap closure","zh":"血清酮体和阴离子间隙闭合"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has SGLT2 inhibitor-associated ketoacidosis despite a glucose below the level commonly expected in classic DKA. Empagliflozin should be withheld and the client needs urgent ketoacidosis treatment with prescribed fluids and insulin. Ketones/anion gap and potassium are essential response and safety parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管血糖低于经典 DKA 常见水平，患者仍符合 SGLT2 抑制剂相关酮症酸中毒。应停用恩格列净，并紧急按医嘱给予补液和胰岛素治疗。酮体/阴离子间隙和血钾是关键疗效与安全指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let a glucose below 250 mg/dL distract from ketones, high-anion-gap acidosis, and SGLT2 inhibitor exposure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因为血糖低于 250 mg/dL 而忽视酮体、高阴离子间隙酸中毒和 SGLT2 抑制剂暴露。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, JARDIANCE (empagliflozin) prescribing information, Warnings and Precautions 5.1 Ketoacidosis, including presentations below 250 mg/dL and treatment with insulin, fluid, and carbohydrate replacement, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=faf3dd6a-9cd0-39c2-0d2e-232cb3f67565; 2024 international consensus report, Hyperglycemic Crises in Adults With Diabetes, fluids, insulin, potassium monitoring, ketones, and resolution criteria, https://diabetesjournals.org/care/article/47/8/1257/156808/Hyperglycemic-Crises-in-Adults-With-Diabetes-A","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2055,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_bt_disaster_emergency_preparedness_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.585","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.585.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.585.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,266],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,73],"fullStemEn":"A hospital loses normal electrical power during a regional heat emergency. The emergency generator serving one inpatient wing repeatedly fails, and several clients there depend on ventilators, oxygen concentrators, and powered infusion devices. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"区域高温紧急事件期间，一家医院失去正常电力。服务于一个住院病区的应急发电机反复故障，该病区多名患者依赖呼吸机、制氧机和电动输液设备。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The emergency generator serving one inpatient wing repeatedly fails, and several clients there depend on ventilators, oxygen concentrators, and powered infusion devices.","penultimateSentenceZh":"服务于一个住院病区的应急发电机反复故障，该病区多名患者依赖呼吸机、制氧机和电动输液设备。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Emergency classification","zh":"紧急事件分类"},"tokens":[{"id":"c3","en":"Airborne infectious-disease outbreak","zh":"空气传播传染病暴发"},{"id":"c2","en":"External mass-casualty surge","zh":"外部大规模伤员激增"},{"id":"c1","en":"Internal utility failure requiring emergency-operations activation","zh":"需要启动应急行动的内部公用设施故障"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"a1","en":"Activate hospital incident command and the emergency operations plan","zh":"启动医院事件指挥系统和应急行动计划"},{"id":"a2","en":"Move critical clients and devices to reliable emergency power or transfer them according to the plan","zh":"按计划将危重患者和设备转移到可靠应急电源区域或转院"},{"id":"a4","en":"Initiate an active-shooter lockdown","zh":"启动主动枪击事件封锁"},{"id":"a3","en":"Begin START triage tagging of current inpatients","zh":"对现有住院患者开始 START 分诊标签"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Resources to monitor","zh":"需监测的资源"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"Wound contamination level","zh":"伤口污染程度"},{"id":"p2","en":"Ventilator, oxygen, and battery runtime for dependent clients","zh":"依赖设备患者的呼吸机、氧气和电池剩余时间"},{"id":"p4","en":"Staff vaccination status","zh":"员工疫苗接种状态"},{"id":"p1","en":"Generator, fuel, and critical-circuit capacity","zh":"发电机、燃料和关键电路能力"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is an internal utility failure that requires activation of the hospital emergency operations plan and incident-command coordination. Clients and critical devices must be moved to reliable emergency power or transferred according to the plan. Teams must continuously track power-system capacity and each client's remaining battery, oxygen, and life-support needs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是一次内部公用设施故障，需要启动医院应急行动计划并由事件指挥系统协调。必须按计划将患者和关键设备转移到可靠的应急电源区域，或转院。团队必须持续追踪供电系统能力，以及每名患者剩余电池、氧气和生命支持需求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the hazard to the emergency plan: a utility failure calls for incident command, continuity of critical services, and resource-duration tracking.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把危险类型与应急计划匹配：公用设施故障需要事件指挥、关键服务连续性和资源持续时间追踪。","sourceMetadata":"ASPR TRACIE, Utility Failures in Health Care Tip Sheet: Electricity, rapid assessment, incident-command triggers, relocation to powered areas, and backup-power capacity planning, https://files.asprtracie.hhs.gov/documents/utility-failures-in-health-care-electricity.pdf; 42 CFR 482.15(a)-(d), hospital emergency preparedness and alternate energy requirements, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-482/subpart-B/section-482.15","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2056,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_hl_ppe_sterile_technique_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.586","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.586.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.586.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,196],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,48],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with fever, cough, conjunctivitis, and a generalized maculopapular rash after a confirmed measles exposure. Highlight the infection-control actions the nurse should implement.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在确认接触麻疹后出现发热、咳嗽、结膜炎和全身斑丘疹并住院。标出护士应实施的感染控制行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the infection-control actions the nurse should implement.","terminalSentenceZh":"标出护士应实施的感染控制行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted with fever, cough, conjunctivitis, and a generalized maculopapular rash after a confirmed measles exposure.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者在确认接触麻疹后出现发热、咳嗽、结膜炎和全身斑丘疹并住院。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Planned actions:","zh":"计划行动："},{"id":"s2","en":"Place the client in an airborne infection isolation room and keep the door closed.","zh":"将患者置于空气感染隔离室并保持房门关闭。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Wear a fit-tested N95 or higher-level respirator before room entry.","zh":"进入病室前佩戴经适合性测试的 N95 或更高级别呼吸器。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Assign immune healthcare personnel and keep susceptible staff out when immune personnel are available.","zh":"安排有免疫力的医护人员；如有免疫人员可用，避免易感员工进入。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Have the client wear a surgical mask during essential transport outside the room.","zh":"患者因必要原因离开病室转运时佩戴外科口罩。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Require a gown and gloves for every room entry regardless of anticipated exposure.","zh":"无论是否预期接触污染物，每次进入都必须穿隔离衣并戴手套。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Allow the nurse to substitute a standard surgical mask for the N95.","zh":"允许护士用普通外科口罩替代 N95。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Suspected measles requires airborne precautions: an airborne infection isolation room with the door closed, a fit-tested N95 or higher-level respirator before entry, preference for immune personnel, and a surgical mask on the client during essential transport. Routine gown and gloves depend on anticipated exposure under Standard Precautions; a surgical mask does not replace the nurse's respirator.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似麻疹需要空气传播预防措施：将患者置于空气感染隔离室并关闭房门，进入前佩戴经过适合性测试的 N95 或更高级别呼吸器，优先安排有免疫力的工作人员，必要转运时让患者佩戴外科口罩。是否常规穿隔离衣和戴手套取决于标准预防下的预期暴露；外科口罩不能替代护士的呼吸器。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For measles, pair airborne engineering control, respirator protection, immune staffing, and source control during transport.","testTakingStrategyZh":"针对麻疹，应同时考虑空气隔离工程控制、呼吸器防护、免疫人员安排和转运时的传染源控制。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Interim Infection Prevention and Control Recommendations for Measles in Healthcare Settings, sections on airborne precautions, AIIR placement, respiratory protection, immune personnel, and transport, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/measles/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2057,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_dc_standard_precautions_hygiene_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.587","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.587.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.587.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[55,173],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,51],"fullStemEn":"The nurse removes bed linen visibly soiled with blood. The facility follows CDC linen-handling principles and has designated leak-resistant laundry bags at the point of use.","fullStemZh":"护士取下肉眼可见血液污染的床单。机构遵循 CDC 的布草处理原则，并在使用地点备有指定的防渗漏洗衣袋。","terminalSentenceEn":"The facility follows CDC linen-handling principles and has designated leak-resistant laundry bags at the point of use.","terminalSentenceZh":"机构遵循 CDC 的布草处理原则，并在使用地点备有指定的防渗漏洗衣袋。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse removes bed linen visibly soiled with blood.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士取下肉眼可见血液污染的床单。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{handle}} and then {{container}}.","zh":"护士应先{{handle}}，然后{{container}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"handle","options":[{"id":"h1","en":"roll or fold the contaminated surface inward without shaking","zh":"将污染面向内卷起或折叠，且不抖动"},{"id":"h2","en":"shake the linen to remove loose debris","zh":"抖动布草以去除松散碎屑"},{"id":"h3","en":"rinse the linen in the client-room sink","zh":"在患者病室水槽中冲洗布草"}],"correct":"h1"},{"id":"container","options":[{"id":"c1","en":"place it directly into the designated leak-resistant bag at the point of use","zh":"在使用地点直接放入指定的防渗漏袋中"},{"id":"c3","en":"sort it on the floor before bagging","zh":"先在地面分类后再装袋"},{"id":"c2","en":"carry it against the uniform to the laundry room","zh":"贴着工作服抱到洗衣房"}],"correct":"c1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Contaminated linen should be handled with minimal agitation: roll or fold the contaminated surface inward without shaking it. Place it directly into the designated leak-resistant container or bag at the point of use so it is not carried against clothing or sorted at the bedside.","rationaleCorrectZh":"污染布草应尽量减少扰动：将污染面向内卷起或折叠，不要抖动。应在使用地点直接放入指定的防渗漏容器或袋中，避免贴身携带或在床旁分类。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For contaminated linen, choose the options that minimize aerosolization and prevent leakage or contact during transport.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理污染布草时，选择能减少污染物散播并防止运输中渗漏或接触的做法。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Guidelines for Environmental Infection Control in Health-Care Facilities, Laundry and Bedding recommendations on minimal agitation and bagging at the point of use, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/environmental-control/laundry-bedding.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2058,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_or_intrapartum_fetal_monitoring_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.588","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.588.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.588.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[566,593],"terminalOffsetsZh":[158,167],"fullStemEn":"A term client undergoing cervical ripening has a dinoprostone vaginal insert in place. Uterine activity is 6 contractions in 10 minutes, averaged over 30 minutes; fetal baseline is 140/min with moderate variability and no decelerations. Facility policy for tachysystole with a removable prostaglandin insert uses this sequence: turn the client laterally and assess the fetal heart rate and uterine activity; remove the insert; increase the isotonic IV fluid per protocol; notify the obstetric provider; if tachysystole persists, administer the prescribed tocolytic. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名足月产妇正在使用地诺前列酮阴道缓释栓进行宫颈成熟。30 分钟平均计算，10 分钟内有 6 次宫缩；胎心基线 140 次/分，变异中等，无减速。机构对可移除前列腺素制剂引起的宫缩过频规定以下顺序：让产妇侧卧并评估胎心和宫缩；取出缓释栓；按方案增加等渗静脉液；通知产科医护提供者；若宫缩过频持续，给予医嘱宫缩抑制剂。请按顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy for tachysystole with a removable prostaglandin insert uses this sequence: turn the client laterally and assess the fetal heart rate and uterine activity; remove the insert; increase the isotonic IV fluid per protocol; notify the obstetric provider; if tachysystole persists, administer the prescribed tocolytic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构对可移除前列腺素制剂引起的宫缩过频规定以下顺序：让产妇侧卧并评估胎心和宫缩；取出缓释栓；按方案增加等渗静脉液；通知产科医护提供者；若宫缩过频持续，给予医嘱宫缩抑制剂。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Remove the dinoprostone vaginal insert.","zh":"取出地诺前列酮阴道缓释栓。"},{"id":"C","en":"Increase the isotonic IV fluid per facility protocol.","zh":"按机构方案增加等渗静脉液。"},{"id":"B","en":"If tachysystole persists, administer the prescribed tocolytic.","zh":"若宫缩过频持续，给予医嘱宫缩抑制剂。"},{"id":"E","en":"Notify the obstetric provider of the tachysystole and response to initial measures.","zh":"将宫缩过频及对初始措施的反应通知产科医护提供者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Turn the client laterally and reassess fetal heart rate and uterine activity.","zh":"让产妇侧卧并重新评估胎心和宫缩活动。"}],"correct":["D","A","C","E","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The tracing has uterine tachysystole even though fetal features are currently reassuring. Follow the stated facility sequence: lateral positioning and reassessment, removal of the dinoprostone insert, IV fluid support, provider notification, and prescribed tocolysis only if excessive uterine activity persists.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管当前胎心表现令人放心，但宫缩活动符合宫缩过频。应按题干给出的机构顺序：侧卧并重新评估，取出地诺前列酮缓释栓，给予静脉液支持，通知医护提供者，仅在宫缩过频持续时按医嘱给予宫缩抑制剂。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The fetal tracing is not the only cue: count contractions, identify a removable uterotonic source, and follow the explicit policy sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要只看胎心图：还要计算宫缩次数，识别可移除的促宫缩药物来源，并按照题干明确顺序处理。","sourceMetadata":"CERVIDIL (dinoprostone vaginal insert) Prescribing Information, Dosage and Administration 2.2 and Warnings and Precautions 5.1 on removal for uterine tachysystole; FDA label, https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2020/020411s032lbl.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2059,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_fib_intrapartum_fetal_monitoring_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.589","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.589.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.589.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,281],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,108],"fullStemEn":"Use this three-tier rule: a sinusoidal fetal heart rate pattern is classified as Category III. A term client's tracing shows a smooth, regular sine-wave-like oscillation of the fetal heart rate at 3 to 5 cycles/min that persists for 20 minutes. Enter the fetal heart rate category.","fullStemZh":"使用以下三级分类规则：正弦波样胎心率图形归类为 Category III（第 III 类）。一名足月产妇的胎心图显示平滑、规则、类似正弦波的振荡，频率为每分钟 3 至 5 个周期，并持续 20 分钟。填写胎心率类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the fetal heart rate category.","terminalSentenceZh":"填写胎心率类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A term client's tracing shows a smooth, regular sine-wave-like oscillation of the fetal heart rate at 3 to 5 cycles/min that persists for 20 minutes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名足月产妇的胎心图显示平滑、规则、类似正弦波的振荡，频率为每分钟 3 至 5 个周期，并持续 20 分钟。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Fetal heart rate category","zh":"胎心率类别"},"acceptable":["Category III","category III","Category 3","category 3","III","3","第III类","第 III 类"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The tracing is Category III because the stated rule classifies a sinusoidal pattern as Category III. The smooth, regular 3-to-5-cycle pattern lasting 20 minutes matches the described sinusoidal morphology.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该胎心图属于 Category III（第 III 类），因为题干规则明确将正弦波样图形归为第 III 类。平滑、规则、每分钟 3 至 5 个周期并持续 20 分钟符合所描述的正弦波样形态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the classification rule given in the stem; do not substitute the categories used for variability alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用题干给出的分类规则；不要用仅针对变异的类别替代整体胎心分类。","sourceMetadata":"Macones GA et al., The 2008 National Institute of Child Health and Human Development Workshop Report on Electronic Fetal Monitoring, Obstetrics & Gynecology 2008;112:661-666, three-tier system and Category III sinusoidal pattern, DOI: 10.1097/AOG.0b013e3181841395","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2060,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance2_2026_07_15_bt_abg_acid_base_interpretation_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.590","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.590.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.590.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[307,328],"terminalOffsetsZh":[128,135],"fullStemEn":"Shortly after extubation in the postanesthesia care unit, a client who received rocuronium is awake and follows commands but cannot sustain a head lift, has a weak cough, and breathes shallowly at 8/min. Quantitative train-of-four ratio is 0.55. ABG results are pH 7.27, PaCO2 58 mm Hg, and HCO3− 26 mEq/L. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名接受过罗库溴铵的患者在麻醉后监护室拔管不久，意识清醒并能遵从指令，但无法持续抬头、咳嗽无力，呼吸浅慢，频率为 8 次/分。定量四联刺激（TOF）比值为 0.55。动脉血气结果：pH 7.27、PaCO2 58 mm Hg、HCO3− 26 mEq/L。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"ABG results are pH 7.27, PaCO2 58 mm Hg, and HCO3− 26 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"动脉血气结果：pH 7.27、PaCO2 58 mm Hg、HCO3− 26 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"c3","en":"Chronic compensated respiratory acidosis","zh":"慢性代偿性呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"c2","en":"Primary metabolic acidosis from hypoperfusion","zh":"低灌注所致原发性代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"c1","en":"Acute respiratory acidosis from residual neuromuscular blockade","zh":"残余神经肌肉阻滞所致急性呼吸性酸中毒"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Give sodium bicarbonate routinely before restoring ventilation","zh":"在恢复通气前常规给予碳酸氢钠"},{"id":"a2","en":"Administer the prescribed neuromuscular-blockade reversal while continuing close respiratory monitoring","zh":"按医嘱给予神经肌肉阻滞拮抗药，同时继续密切监测呼吸"},{"id":"a3","en":"Ambulate the client to clear the remaining anesthetic","zh":"让患者下床活动以清除残余麻醉药"},{"id":"a1","en":"Open the airway, assist ventilation as needed, and summon anesthesia or rapid-response support","zh":"开放气道，按需辅助通气，并呼叫麻醉团队或快速反应支持"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"监测指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Serum amylase","zh":"血清淀粉酶"},{"id":"p3","en":"INR","zh":"国际标准化比值（INR）"},{"id":"p1","en":"Quantitative train-of-four recovery to at least 0.9","zh":"定量 TOF 比值恢复至至少 0.9"},{"id":"p2","en":"Respiratory rate and depth, level of consciousness, and repeat pH and PaCO2","zh":"呼吸频率和深度、意识水平以及复查 pH 和 PaCO2"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The low pH, high PaCO2, and near-normal bicarbonate indicate acute respiratory acidosis. Weakness, shallow ventilation, and a train-of-four ratio of 0.55 after rocuronium support residual neuromuscular blockade as the cause. Airway and ventilatory support take priority while anesthesia is urgently engaged and prescribed reversal is administered. Quantitative recovery and repeat respiratory/ABG findings determine whether the client has recovered safely.","rationaleCorrectZh":"pH 降低、PaCO2 升高且碳酸氢盐接近正常，提示急性呼吸性酸中毒。使用罗库溴铵后出现肌无力、浅慢呼吸且 TOF 比值为 0.55，支持残余神经肌肉阻滞为病因。应优先开放气道并支持通气，同时紧急联系麻醉团队并按医嘱给予拮抗药。定量恢复指标以及复查呼吸和动脉血气结果用于判断患者是否安全恢复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Interpret the ABG first, then use the postoperative weakness and quantitative train-of-four result to identify why ventilation is failing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先解释动脉血气，再利用术后肌无力和定量 TOF 结果判断通气失败的原因。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Anesthesiologists, 2023 Practice Guidelines for Monitoring and Antagonism of Neuromuscular Blockade, quantitative monitoring and train-of-four recovery of at least 0.9, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36520073/; DailyMed, BRIDION (sugammadex) prescribing information, ventilatory support until adequate spontaneous respiration and airway patency are restored, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/getFile.cfm?setid=5171d883-fe8f-482c-97ab-40b00975b64a&type=pdf; Merck Manual Professional, Respiratory Acidosis, acute hypoventilation and ABG pattern, https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/endocrine-and-metabolic-disorders/acid-base-regulation-and-disorders/respiratory-acidosis","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2061,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_bt_discharge_planning_handoff_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.591","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.591.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.591.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[248,277],"terminalOffsetsZh":[87,95],"fullStemEn":"A client with epilepsy is transferring to a skilled nursing facility. The hospital MAR and discharge prescription list levetiracetam 750 mg twice daily, but the transfer medication list says 500 mg twice daily. The time of the last dose is absent. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名癫痫患者将转往专业护理机构。医院 MAR 和出院处方写明左乙拉西坦 750 mg、每日 2 次，但转院用药清单写为 500 mg、每日 2 次；清单还未注明末次给药时间。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The time of the last dose is absent.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院 MAR 和出院处方写明左乙拉西坦 750 mg、每日 2 次，但转院用药清单写为 500 mg、每日 2 次；清单还未注明末次给药时间。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c3","en":"Intentional dose reduction","zh":"有意减量"},{"id":"c1","en":"Incomplete medication handoff","zh":"用药交接不完整"},{"id":"c2","en":"Routine formulary substitution","zh":"常规药品目录替代"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Send the corrected regimen and last-dose time directly to the receiving nurse","zh":"将更正后的方案及末次给药时间直接告知接收护士"},{"id":"a4","en":"Remove levetiracetam from the transfer list until the first follow-up visit","zh":"从转院清单中删除左乙拉西坦，等首次随访再处理"},{"id":"a3","en":"Send both medication lists and let the receiving facility choose","zh":"发送两份清单并让接收机构自行选择"},{"id":"a1","en":"Reconcile the intended dose with the prescriber and pharmacist","zh":"与开方者和药师核对预期剂量"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Evidence that the handoff is resolved","zh":"交接问题已解决的证据"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Dose and timing match across all transfer documents","zh":"所有转院文件中的剂量和时间一致"},{"id":"p3","en":"Receiving room assignment","zh":"接收房间安排"},{"id":"p4","en":"Ambulance arrival time","zh":"救护车到达时间"},{"id":"p2","en":"Receiving nurse confirms the corrected regimen and last dose","zh":"接收护士确认更正后的方案及末次给药"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The record contains a clinically important medication-handoff discrepancy. The nurse should reconcile the dose before transfer and directly communicate the corrected regimen and last-dose time to the receiving nurse. Closure is demonstrated by concordant documents and confirmation from the receiving clinician.","rationaleCorrectZh":"记录中存在具有临床意义的用药交接不一致。护士应在转院前核对剂量，并将更正后的方案和末次给药时间直接告知接收护士。所有文件一致且接收方确认后，才说明交接闭环。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for information that could cause a missed, duplicated, or incorrectly dosed medication after the transition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找可能导致转院后漏药、重复给药或剂量错误的信息。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, Medications at Transitions and Clinical Handoffs (MATCH) Toolkit, comparison of transfer/discharge orders and resolution of dose discrepancies, https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/settings/hospital/match/index.html; TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Tool: Handoff, transfer and confirmation of information, authority, and responsibility, https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/communication/tools/handoff.html; 42 CFR § 482.43(b)(1), transfer or referral of necessary medical information, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-482/subpart-C/section-482.43","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2062,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_hl_client_advocacy_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.592","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.592.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.592.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,211],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,55],"fullStemEn":"A client with severe low vision says the printed preparation instructions cannot be read and asks for an accessible format. Highlight the nurse responses that support effective communication and client advocacy.","fullStemZh":"一名严重低视力患者表示无法阅读纸质准备说明，并要求提供无障碍格式。请标出支持有效沟通和患者权益维护的护士回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nurse responses that support effective communication and client advocacy.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持有效沟通和患者权益维护的护士回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with severe low vision says the printed preparation instructions cannot be read and asks for an accessible format.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名严重低视力患者表示无法阅读纸质准备说明，并要求提供无障碍格式。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse should:","zh":"护士应："},{"id":"s2","en":"ask the client which format works best;","zh":"询问患者哪种格式最合适；","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"arrange audio or large-print instructions;","zh":"安排音频或大字版说明；","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"review the instructions directly with the client and use teach-back;","zh":"直接与患者一起复习说明并使用复述法；","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"tell a family member to read the standard handout at home;","zh":"让家属回家后朗读标准说明单；","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"document “refused teaching” if the client cannot read the handout.","zh":"如果患者无法阅读说明单，就记录“拒绝教育”。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective communication requires consulting the client about the preferred aid, providing an accessible alternative, and confirming understanding with the client. Shifting the duty to family or labeling the client as refusing does not provide equal communication access.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效沟通需要询问患者偏好的辅助方式、提供无障碍替代形式，并直接确认患者理解。把责任转给家属或把无法阅读记录为“拒绝”都不能提供平等的沟通机会。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose actions that give the client direct, equally effective access to the information.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能让患者直接且同等有效地获得信息的措施。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Justice, ADA Requirements: Effective Communication, auxiliary aids and services, https://www.ada.gov/resources/effective-communication/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2063,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_or_client_advocacy_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.593","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.593.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.593.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[474,522],"terminalOffsetsZh":[117,124],"fullStemEn":"A client reports that a staff member mocked the client’s accent. The hospital grievance protocol requires the nurse to complete these steps in this exact order: first ensure immediate safety and privacy; next listen and clarify the client’s concern and requested resolution; then explain the grievance process and offer help contacting the patient representative; next document the client’s words and submit the grievance; finally confirm how and when follow-up will occur. Place the nurse’s actions in the protocol order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者报告某工作人员嘲笑其口音。医院投诉流程要求护士严格按以下顺序处理：首先确保即时安全和隐私；其次倾听并澄清患者的担忧及期望的解决方式；然后解释投诉流程并协助联系患者代表；接着记录患者原话并提交投诉；最后确认后续联系的方式和时间。请按流程排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse’s actions in the protocol order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按流程排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The hospital grievance protocol requires the nurse to complete these steps in this exact order: first ensure immediate safety and privacy; next listen and clarify the client’s concern and requested resolution; then explain the grievance process and offer help contacting the patient representative; next document the client’s words and submit the grievance; finally confirm how and when follow-up will occur.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院投诉流程要求护士严格按以下顺序处理：首先确保即时安全和隐私；其次倾听并澄清患者的担忧及期望的解决方式；然后解释投诉流程并协助联系患者代表；接着记录患者原话并提交投诉；最后确认后续联系的方式和时间。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Confirm who will follow up, the expected time frame, and how the client will be contacted.","zh":"确认由谁跟进、预计时限以及联系患者的方式。"},{"id":"B","en":"Listen privately and clarify the concern and the resolution the client is seeking.","zh":"私下倾听，并澄清患者的担忧及期望的解决方式。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the client’s exact words and submit the grievance through the designated channel.","zh":"记录患者原话，并通过指定渠道提交投诉。"},{"id":"A","en":"Move to a private setting and assess whether the client feels safe from further contact.","zh":"转到私密场所，并评估患者是否担心再次接触该工作人员。"},{"id":"C","en":"Explain the grievance process and offer assistance contacting the patient representative.","zh":"解释投诉流程，并协助联系患者代表。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The stem supplies the facility’s exact grievance sequence. Safety and privacy come first, followed by understanding the client’s concern, explaining access to the grievance process, formally documenting and submitting it, and confirming follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干已提供机构的准确投诉顺序。先确保安全与隐私，再了解患者担忧，说明投诉途径，正式记录并提交，最后确认后续安排。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For an ordered response with a stated policy, map each option to the policy’s sequence words: first, next, then, and finally.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于题干已给出政策顺序的排序题，把每个选项对应到“首先、其次、然后、最后”等顺序词。","sourceMetadata":"42 CFR § 482.13(a)(2), Patient grievance process, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-482/subpart-B/section-482.13","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2064,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_fib_confidentiality_hipaa_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.594","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.594.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.594.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[266,281],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,78],"fullStemEn":"A client submits a written request for an electronic copy of the designated record set. The facility can provide the records without an extension. Under the HIPAA Privacy Rule, the facility must act on the request no later than how many calendar days after receipt? Enter a number.","fullStemZh":"一名患者书面要求取得指定记录集的电子副本。机构无需延期即可提供记录。根据 HIPAA 隐私规则，机构最迟应在收到请求后的多少个日历日内采取行动？请输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter a number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Under the HIPAA Privacy Rule, the facility must act on the request no later than how many calendar days after receipt?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据 HIPAA 隐私规则，机构最迟应在收到请求后的多少个日历日内采取行动？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"calendar days","zh":"日历日"},"acceptable":["30","30 days","30 calendar days"],"numeric":{"value":30,"tolerance":0,"unit":"days"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The HIPAA Privacy Rule requires action on an access request no later than 30 calendar days after receipt when no extension is needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"如果不需要延期，HIPAA 隐私规则要求机构最迟在收到查阅请求后的 30 个日历日内采取行动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish the standard federal response period from any separate facility target that may be shorter.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分联邦规定的标准答复期限与机构可能设定的更短内部目标。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR § 164.524(b)(2)(i), Timely action on access requests, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-E/section-164.524","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2065,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_dc_confidentiality_hipaa_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.595","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.595.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.595.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,179],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,44],"fullStemEn":"A county health department sends a legally authorized request for the laboratory result and demographic fields required to report a confirmed measles case. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"县卫生部门依法要求医院提供上报一例确诊麻疹病例所需的实验室结果和人口学字段。请完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A county health department sends a legally authorized request for the laboratory result and demographic fields required to report a confirmed measles case.","penultimateSentenceZh":"县卫生部门依法要求医院提供上报一例确诊麻疹病例所需的实验室结果和人口学字段。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse may release the requested information {{d1}} and should send {{d2}}.","zh":"护士可以{{d1}}披露所请求的信息，并且应仅发送{{d2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"without a separate client authorization","zh":"无需患者另行授权"},{"id":"o2","en":"only after a new client authorization is signed","zh":"仅在患者新签署授权后"},{"id":"o3","en":"only after a court subpoena is obtained","zh":"仅在取得法院传票后"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the entire inpatient record","zh":"整份住院病历"},{"id":"o3","en":"all records from the previous five years","zh":"过去五年的全部记录"},{"id":"o1","en":"the fields required by the lawful report","zh":"法定报告所需字段"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA permits disclosures without individual authorization when required by law or for authorized public-health activities. The disclosure should be limited to the information the lawful report requires, not the entire chart.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当法律要求或属于获授权的公共卫生活动时，HIPAA 允许在未取得个人授权的情况下披露信息。披露内容应限于法定报告所需信息，而不是整份病历。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify whether HIPAA permits the purpose of the disclosure, then limit the content to what that lawful purpose requires.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断 HIPAA 是否允许该披露目的，再把内容限制在该合法目的所需范围内。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR § 164.512(a)-(b), Uses and disclosures required by law and for public health activities, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-E/section-164.512","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2066,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_bt_conflict_resolution_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.596","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.596.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.596.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[332,361],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,97],"fullStemEn":"At shift change, two nurses with an ongoing personal dispute refuse to give report directly to one another. The outgoing nurse leaves a note with a third coworker, but it omits the current insulin-infusion rate and the time of the last glucose check. The incoming nurse has not acknowledged accepting responsibility for the client. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"交班时，两名长期存在私人矛盾的护士拒绝彼此直接交接。交班护士把一张便条留给第三名同事，但便条未写明当前胰岛素输注速率和末次血糖检查时间。接班护士也尚未确认已接收该患者的照护责任。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The incoming nurse has not acknowledged accepting responsibility for the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"接班护士也尚未确认已接收该患者的照护责任。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely problem","zh":"最可能的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c3","en":"Resolved documentation disagreement","zh":"已解决的记录分歧"},{"id":"c2","en":"Acceptable routine asynchronous handoff","zh":"可接受的常规异步交接"},{"id":"c1","en":"Interpersonal conflict compromising transfer of responsibility","zh":"人际冲突影响照护责任转移"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a1","en":"Have the charge nurse facilitate an immediate direct handoff that includes the missing infusion and glucose information","zh":"由责任护士立即协调直接交接，并补充缺失的输注和血糖信息"},{"id":"a4","en":"Complete both nurses' conduct reports before resuming the handoff","zh":"先完成两名护士的行为报告，再继续交接"},{"id":"a2","en":"Obtain receiver confirmation and address the conduct dispute separately after safe responsibility transfer","zh":"取得接收方确认，并在安全完成责任转移后另行处理行为争议"},{"id":"a3","en":"Ask the third coworker to reconstruct the handoff from the incomplete note","zh":"让第三名同事根据不完整便条重建交接内容"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Outcomes to evaluate","zh":"应评价的结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"A conduct report is filed before transfer","zh":"责任转移前已提交行为报告"},{"id":"p4","en":"Outgoing nurse leaves the unit on schedule","zh":"交班护士按时离开科室"},{"id":"p2","en":"Incoming nurse confirms receipt of information and responsibility","zh":"接班护士确认已接收信息和照护责任"},{"id":"p1","en":"Current insulin-infusion rate and last glucose-check time are verified","zh":"当前胰岛素输注速率和末次血糖检查时间已核实"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The personal dispute has become an interpersonal conflict that is compromising a safety-critical handoff. The charge nurse should first restore a complete, direct transfer of information and responsibility, including confirmation by the receiving nurse. The conduct dispute can then be addressed separately without allowing it to delay or replace the handoff.","rationaleCorrectZh":"私人矛盾已演变为影响安全关键交接的人际冲突。责任护士应先恢复完整、直接的信息与照护责任转移，并由接班护士确认接收。之后可另行处理行为争议，不能让该争议延误或取代交接。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the immediate patient-safety function from the later conduct issue: complete and acknowledge the handoff first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分即时患者安全任务与之后的行为问题：先完成交接并确认接收。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Conflict in Teams (interpersonal conflict and patient-safety effects), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/conflict.html; Tool: Handoff, transfer and confirmation of information, authority, and responsibility, https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/communication/tools/handoff.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2067,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_hl_conflict_resolution_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.597","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.597.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.597.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,252],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,79],"fullStemEn":"After a difficult rapid-response debrief, a coworker tells the nurse, “When you spoke over my assessment twice, the team did not hear the change in breath sounds.” Highlight the nurse’s replies that receive the feedback respectfully and support repair.","fullStemZh":"一次紧张的快速反应事件复盘后，一名同事告诉护士：“你两次打断我的评估，团队因此没有听到呼吸音的变化。”请标出护士既能尊重地接收反馈又有助于修复合作关系的回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nurse’s replies that receive the feedback respectfully and support repair.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出护士既能尊重地接收反馈又有助于修复合作关系的回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After a difficult rapid-response debrief, a coworker tells the nurse, “When you spoke over my assessment twice, the team did not hear the change in breath sounds.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"一次紧张的快速反应事件复盘后，一名同事告诉护士：“你两次打断我的评估，团队因此没有听到呼吸音的变化。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The nurse replies,","zh":"护士回应："},{"id":"s2","en":"“Thank you for telling me; I want to understand what happened.","zh":"“谢谢你告诉我；我想了解当时发生了什么。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"I hear that my interruptions kept your assessment from reaching the team.","zh":"我听到的是，我的打断使你的评估没有传达给团队。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"At the next debrief, I will pause and ask whether you have finished before I respond.”","zh":"下次复盘时，我会先停下来确认你已经说完，再作回应。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"“Everyone interrupts during emergencies, so this is not worth discussing.”","zh":"“紧急情况下大家都会打断别人，所以这不值得讨论。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"“You are too sensitive about how people communicate.”","zh":"“你对别人的沟通方式太敏感了。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Receiving feedback constructively means listening without defensiveness, restating the specific impact to confirm understanding, and committing to a concrete future behavior. Minimization and personal labels block repair.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建设性接收反馈意味着不带防御地倾听，复述具体影响以确认理解，并承诺今后的具体行为。淡化问题和给对方贴标签都会阻碍关系修复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For feedback-repair questions, choose listening, accurate restatement, and a future action; reject minimizing or labeling.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理反馈修复题时，选择倾听、准确复述和今后行动；排除淡化问题或贴标签。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Mutual Support overview, Formative Feedback (timely, respectful, specific, directed toward improvement, and patient focused), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/overview/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2068,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_dc_discharge_planning_handoff_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.598","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.598.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.598.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[208,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,60],"fullStemEn":"A client is transferring to a residential treatment program after receiving a long-acting paliperidone injection. The receiving nurse asks what information is essential to prevent a duplicate or missed dose. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在接受长效帕利哌酮注射后将转入住院式治疗项目。接收护士询问哪些信息对于防止重复或漏打下一剂至关重要。请完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The receiving nurse asks what information is essential to prevent a duplicate or missed dose.","penultimateSentenceZh":"接收护士询问哪些信息对于防止重复或漏打下一剂至关重要。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The handoff should include {{d1}} and {{d2}}.","zh":"交接内容应包括{{d1}}以及{{d2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"the client’s preferred injection site only","zh":"仅患者偏好的注射部位"},{"id":"o2","en":"only the medication class","zh":"仅药物类别"},{"id":"o1","en":"the exact last product, dose, route, and administration date","zh":"准确的末次制剂、剂量、途径及给药日期"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the date of the next routine physical examination","zh":"下次常规体检日期"},{"id":"o3","en":"the pharmacy’s monthly inventory date","zh":"药房每月盘点日期"},{"id":"o1","en":"the date the next injection is due","zh":"下次注射应给药的日期"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The receiving team needs the exact product, dose, route, date of the last administration, and date the next dose is due. These timing details prevent duplicate administration or an unintended gap.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接收团队需要知道准确的制剂、剂量、途径、末次给药日期和下次应给药日期。这些时间信息可防止重复给药或意外中断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For long-acting medications, focus on both sides of continuity: what was already given and when the next dose is due.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于长效药物，要同时关注连续性的两端：已经给过什么，以及下一剂何时到期。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Tool: Handoff, transfer of recent treatment information and the continuing plan, https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/communication/tools/handoff.html; 42 CFR § 482.43(b)(1), transfer or referral of necessary medical information, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-482/subpart-C/section-482.43","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2069,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_bt_dosage_calculations_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.599","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.599.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.599.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[259,286],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,122],"fullStemEn":"An adult has a body surface area (BSA) of 1.72 m². The prescribed doxorubicin dose is 150 mg IV. The protocol-approved dose is 60 to 75 mg/m² per treatment. Calculate the ordered dose in mg/m² by dividing 150 mg by 1.72 m², then complete the bow-tie diagram. Round to the nearest tenth.","fullStemZh":"一名成人的体表面积（BSA）为 1.72 m²。医嘱为多柔比星 150 mg 静脉给药。方案批准剂量为每次 60～75 mg/m²。用 150 mg ÷ 1.72 m² 计算医嘱剂量（mg/m²），四舍五入到小数点后 1 位，然后完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest tenth.","terminalSentenceZh":"用 150 mg ÷ 1.72 m² 计算医嘱剂量（mg/m²），四舍五入到小数点后 1 位，然后完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the ordered dose in mg/m² by dividing 150 mg by 1.72 m², then complete the bow-tie diagram.","penultimateSentenceZh":"方案批准剂量为每次 60～75 mg/m²。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Calculation finding","zh":"计算结果判断"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Ordered dose is above the protocol range (87.2 mg/m²)","zh":"医嘱剂量高于方案范围（87.2 mg/m²）"},{"id":"c3","en":"BSA cannot be determined from the data","zh":"无法根据资料确定 BSA"},{"id":"c2","en":"Ordered dose is within the protocol range","zh":"医嘱剂量在方案范围内"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Round the dose down to 75 mg without a new order","zh":"未经新医嘱直接把剂量改为 75 mg"},{"id":"a2","en":"Independently recalculate and notify the oncology pharmacist or prescriber","zh":"独立复算并通知肿瘤药师或开方者"},{"id":"a1","en":"Withhold the dose pending clarification","zh":"暂缓给药，等待澄清"},{"id":"a3","en":"Administer 150 mg and clarify afterward","zh":"先给予 150 mg，之后再澄清"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Safety parameters to review","zh":"应复核的安全指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Complete blood count","zh":"全血细胞计数"},{"id":"p2","en":"Cardiac function assessment","zh":"心功能评估"},{"id":"p3","en":"Serum amylase","zh":"血清淀粉酶"},{"id":"p4","en":"Visual acuity","zh":"视力"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The calculation is 150 ÷ 1.72 = 87.2 mg/m², which exceeds the stated maximum of 75 mg/m². The nurse should withhold the dose, independently verify the calculation, and clarify the order. CBC and cardiac function are key safety parameters for doxorubicin.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算结果为 150 ÷ 1.72 = 87.2 mg/m²，超过题干规定的最高 75 mg/m²。护士应暂缓给药，独立复核计算并澄清医嘱。CBC 和心功能是多柔比星的重要安全监测指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Perform the BSA division before judging the order; compare the calculated mg/m² directly with both ends of the stated range.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先完成 BSA 除法，再判断医嘱；把计算出的 mg/m² 直接与题干范围上下限比较。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Doxorubicin Hydrochloride for Injection prescribing information, Dosage and Administration 2.1 (single-agent 60–75 mg/m² schedule), Warnings and Precautions 5.1 cardiomyopathy, and 5.4 myelosuppression, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=5f71f79a-4f14-472d-b982-e28c3ce8f972","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2070,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_or_anticoagulant_therapy_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.600","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.600.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.600.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[708,744],"terminalOffsetsZh":[221,228],"fullStemEn":"A client with creatinine clearance 72 mL/min receives enoxaparin 40 mg once daily for prophylaxis and is scheduled for epidural-catheter removal. The hospital protocol, consistent with the drug label, requires this exact sequence: (1) verify the last enoxaparin time and renal function; (2) after at least 12 hours since the last dose, assess for bleeding and new neurologic deficits and notify anesthesia that the removal interval is met; (3) an authorized clinician removes the catheter; (4) begin the scheduled neurologic and insertion-site monitoring; (5) if hemostasis is stable and no neurologic deficit is present, administer the next prescribed enoxaparin dose no earlier than 4 hours after removal. Place the actions in protocol order.","fullStemZh":"一名肌酐清除率 72 mL/min 的患者每日接受依诺肝素 40 mg 预防性用药，现计划拔除硬膜外导管。医院流程与药品说明书一致，并规定严格顺序：（1）核实末次依诺肝素给药时间和肾功能；（2）末次给药至少 12 小时后，评估出血及新发神经功能缺损，并通知麻醉团队已达到拔管时间间隔；（3）由获授权的临床人员拔除导管；（4）开始规定的神经功能和穿刺部位监测；（5）若止血稳定且无神经功能缺损，拔管至少 4 小时后再给予下一剂已开具的依诺肝素。请按流程排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in protocol order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按流程排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The hospital protocol, consistent with the drug label, requires this exact sequence: (1) verify the last enoxaparin time and renal function; (2) after at least 12 hours since the last dose, assess for bleeding and new neurologic deficits and notify anesthesia that the removal interval is met; (3) an authorized clinician removes the catheter; (4) begin the scheduled neurologic and insertion-site monitoring; (5) if hemostasis is stable and no neurologic deficit is present, administer the next prescribed enoxaparin dose no earlier than 4 hours after removal.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院流程与药品说明书一致，并规定严格顺序：（1）核实末次依诺肝素给药时间和肾功能；（2）末次给药至少 12 小时后，评估出血及新发神经功能缺损，并通知麻醉团队已达到拔管时间间隔；（3）由获授权的临床人员拔除导管；（4）开始规定的神经功能和穿刺部位监测；（5）若止血稳定且无神经功能缺损，拔管至少 4 小时后再给予下一剂已开具的依诺肝素。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Begin scheduled neurologic and catheter-site monitoring after removal.","zh":"拔管后开始规定的神经功能和导管部位监测。"},{"id":"B","en":"After at least 12 hours, assess for bleeding and neurologic deficits and notify anesthesia that the interval is met.","zh":"至少 12 小时后，评估出血和神经功能缺损，并通知麻醉团队已达到时间间隔。"},{"id":"C","en":"Have the authorized clinician remove the epidural catheter.","zh":"由获授权的临床人员拔除硬膜外导管。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the time of the last enoxaparin dose and the current renal function.","zh":"核实末次依诺肝素给药时间和当前肾功能。"},{"id":"E","en":"If findings remain stable, administer the next prescribed enoxaparin dose no earlier than 4 hours after removal.","zh":"若评估结果保持稳定，拔管至少 4 小时后再给予下一剂已开具的依诺肝素。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The item tests the exact facility sequence stated in the stem. For the stated prophylactic dose and renal function, the label supports waiting at least 12 hours before catheter removal and considering at least 4 hours before the next dose. These intervals do not eliminate neuraxial-hematoma risk, so neurologic and site monitoring begins immediately after removal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本题考查题干明确给出的机构流程。对于题干所示预防剂量和肾功能，药品说明书支持拔管前至少等待 12 小时，并考虑拔管后至少等待 4 小时再给下一剂。这些时间间隔不能完全消除椎管内血肿风险，因此拔管后应立即开始神经功能和穿刺部位监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor the order to the two time gates: verify before the 12-hour removal gate, then monitor before the 4-hour post-removal dosing gate.","testTakingStrategyZh":"以两个时间节点排序：先在 12 小时拔管节点前完成核实，再于拔管后 4 小时给药节点前完成监测。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Enoxaparin Sodium Injection prescribing information, Boxed Warning and Warnings and Precautions 5.1, neuraxial catheter removal timing, renal-function considerations, post-removal dosing, and neurologic monitoring, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/lookup.cfm?setid=21b095d1-5ade-43e9-9114-30fbfb2331c9","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2071,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_dc_psychotropic_medications_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.601","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.601.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.601.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[33,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,29],"fullStemEn":"A client is starting olanzapine. Complete the monitoring statement using the medication’s prescribing information.","fullStemZh":"一名患者即将开始使用奥氮平。请根据药品说明书完成监测句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the monitoring statement using the medication’s prescribing information.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据药品说明书完成监测句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is starting olanzapine.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者即将开始使用奥氮平。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Before and during therapy, monitor {{d1}} and {{d2}}, and monitor {{d3}} regularly.","zh":"治疗前及治疗期间，应监测{{d1}}和{{d2}}，并规律监测{{d3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"d1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"bleeding time","zh":"出血时间"},{"id":"o2","en":"serum amylase","zh":"血清淀粉酶"},{"id":"o1","en":"fasting blood glucose","zh":"空腹血糖"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"d2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"a fasting lipid profile","zh":"空腹血脂谱"},{"id":"o2","en":"serum copper","zh":"血清铜"},{"id":"o3","en":"arterial blood gases","zh":"动脉血气"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"d3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"body weight","zh":"体重"},{"id":"o2","en":"pupil size","zh":"瞳孔大小"},{"id":"o3","en":"hearing acuity","zh":"听力"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Olanzapine labeling recommends baseline and periodic fasting blood glucose and lipid monitoring, along with regular weight monitoring, because atypical antipsychotics can cause metabolic changes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"奥氮平说明书建议在基线及治疗期间定期监测空腹血糖和血脂，并规律监测体重，因为非典型抗精神病药可能引起代谢变化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For atypical antipsychotics, think metabolic monitoring: glucose, lipids, and weight.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到非典型抗精神病药时，想到代谢监测：血糖、血脂和体重。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Olanzapine tablet prescribing information, Warnings and Precautions 5.5 Metabolic Changes, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=e8626e68-088d-47ff-bf06-489a778815aa","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2072,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_hl_parenteral_nutrition_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.602","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.602.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.602.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[227,282],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,77],"fullStemEn":"An adult receives parenteral nutrition with a lipid injectable emulsion. The facility protocol states: stop the lipid component and notify the prescriber if triglycerides exceed 400 mg/dL or if acute pancreatitis is suspected. Highlight the findings that meet the protocol criteria.","fullStemZh":"一名成人接受含脂肪乳的肠外营养。机构流程规定：若甘油三酯超过 400 mg/dL，或怀疑急性胰腺炎，应停止脂肪成分并通知开方者。请标出符合流程标准的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that meet the protocol criteria.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合流程标准的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility protocol states: stop the lipid component and notify the prescriber if triglycerides exceed 400 mg/dL or if acute pancreatitis is suspected.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构流程规定：若甘油三酯超过 400 mg/dL，或怀疑急性胰腺炎，应停止脂肪成分并通知开方者。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Current findings:","zh":"当前发现："},{"id":"s2","en":"triglycerides 612 mg/dL;","zh":"甘油三酯 612 mg/dL；","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"new severe epigastric pain radiating to the back;","zh":"新发剧烈上腹痛并向背部放射；","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"lipase 620 units/L (reference 13–60 units/L);","zh":"脂肪酶 620 units/L（参考范围 13～60 units/L）；","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"blood glucose 128 mg/dL;","zh":"血糖 128 mg/dL；","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"central-line dressing clean and dry.","zh":"中心静脉导管敷料清洁干燥。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Triglycerides of 612 mg/dL exceed the stated facility threshold. New severe epigastric pain radiating to the back and a markedly elevated lipase support suspected pancreatitis. The other findings do not meet the stated stop criteria.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甘油三酯 612 mg/dL 超过题干给出的机构阈值。新发剧烈上腹痛向背部放射并伴脂肪酶明显升高，支持怀疑胰腺炎。其他发现不符合题干规定的停用标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the exact threshold and syndrome cues stated in the stem; do not select every abnormal-looking detail.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用题干给出的准确阈值和综合征线索，不要把所有看似异常的细节都选上。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, SMOFlipid prescribing information, Warnings and Precautions 5.7 and 5.10, stopping the adult infusion above triglycerides 400 mg/dL and monitoring for consequences including pancreatitis, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=e0e9d917-ff6f-488e-a6a8-0ad59dd17d80; American College of Gastroenterology, 2024 Guideline: Management of Acute Pancreatitis, characteristic pain plus lipase greater than 3 times the upper limit of normal, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13221274/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2073,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_hl_disaster_emergency_preparedness_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.603","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.603.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.603.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[350,407],"terminalOffsetsZh":[97,109],"fullStemEn":"A ransomware incident disables the electronic health record and medication-scanning system. The hospital activates its downtime plan. The plan requires pre-numbered paper records, two patient identifiers, read-back of critical verbal results, contemporaneous paper medication documentation, and reconciliation before data are entered after recovery. Highlight the actions consistent with the activated plan.","fullStemZh":"勒索软件事件导致电子健康记录和用药扫码系统停用。医院启动停机计划。计划要求使用预编号纸质记录、核对两项患者身份、对危急口头结果进行复诵确认、实时记录纸质用药信息，并在系统恢复后录入前先完成核对。请标出符合该计划的措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions consistent with the activated plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合该计划的措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The plan requires pre-numbered paper records, two patient identifiers, read-back of critical verbal results, contemporaneous paper medication documentation, and reconciliation before data are entered after recovery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计划要求使用预编号纸质记录、核对两项患者身份、对危急口头结果进行复诵确认、实时记录纸质用药信息，并在系统恢复后录入前先完成核对。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"During downtime, staff should:","zh":"停机期间，工作人员应："},{"id":"s2","en":"use the unit’s pre-numbered paper records;","zh":"使用科室预编号纸质记录；","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"verify two patient identifiers before medication administration;","zh":"给药前核对两项患者身份；","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"read back critical verbal laboratory results;","zh":"复诵危急口头实验室结果；","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"record each medication on the paper MAR at the time it is given;","zh":"每次给药时立即在纸质 MAR 上记录；","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"reconcile paper records before entering delayed data after recovery;","zh":"系统恢复后补录前先核对纸质记录；","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"send client identifiers and orders through personal text messages;","zh":"通过私人短信发送患者身份信息和医嘱；","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"recreate the medication record from memory at the end of the shift.","zh":"班末凭记忆重建用药记录。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5","s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The safe response follows the downtime plan stated in the case: use controlled paper records, verify identity without barcode scanning, read back critical results, document medications as they are given, and reconcile before retrospective entry. Personal texting and memory-based reconstruction create privacy and medication-safety risks.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全应对必须遵循题干给出的停机计划：使用受控纸质记录，在无法扫码时核对两项身份，复诵危急结果，给药时实时记录，并在事后补录前完成核对。使用私人短信和凭记忆重建记录会造成隐私及用药安全风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use every operational control explicitly named in the activated plan and reject shortcuts that lose traceability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用启动计划中明确列出的每项操作控制，排除会失去可追溯性的捷径。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR § 164.308(a)(7), HIPAA Security Rule contingency plan standard, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-C/section-164.308","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2074,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_bt_ppe_sterile_technique_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.604","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.604.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.604.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,53],"fullStemEn":"A bag of an antineoplastic infusion leaks onto the floor and splashes the nurse’s intact forearm. The facility hazardous-drug spill plan is activated. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一袋抗肿瘤药输液泄漏到地面，并溅到护士完整无破损的前臂皮肤上。机构已启动危险药物泄漏计划。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility hazardous-drug spill plan is activated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构已启动危险药物泄漏计划。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely event","zh":"最可能的事件"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Hazardous antineoplastic-drug spill with occupational exposure","zh":"危险抗肿瘤药泄漏伴职业暴露"},{"id":"c2","en":"Infectious isolation breach","zh":"传染隔离失效"},{"id":"c3","en":"Routine nonhazardous IV-fluid leak","zh":"普通非危险静脉液体泄漏"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Don double chemotherapy gloves, an impermeable gown, eye/face protection, and the plan-specified respirator","zh":"穿戴化疗防护双层手套、不渗透防护衣、眼面防护及流程规定的呼吸防护"},{"id":"a4","en":"Push the liquid into the floor drain with disposable towels","zh":"用一次性毛巾把液体推入地漏"},{"id":"a3","en":"Clean the spill wearing only standard exam gloves","zh":"仅戴普通检查手套清理泄漏"},{"id":"a1","en":"Restrict the area, obtain the hazardous-drug spill kit, and wash the exposed forearm","zh":"限制区域，取得危险药物泄漏包，并清洗暴露前臂"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to evaluate","zh":"应评价的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"Room humidity","zh":"房间湿度"},{"id":"p1","en":"Condition of exposed skin and mucous membranes","zh":"暴露皮肤和黏膜状况"},{"id":"p2","en":"Completion of spill containment and surface decontamination","zh":"泄漏控制和表面去污完成情况"},{"id":"p4","en":"Client meal intake","zh":"患者进食量"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is a hazardous antineoplastic-drug spill with occupational skin exposure. The nurse should restrict the area, use the hazardous-drug spill kit with chemotherapy-rated PPE, and immediately wash exposed skin. Evaluation focuses on successful containment/decontamination and the exposed skin or mucous membranes.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是危险抗肿瘤药泄漏并造成职业性皮肤暴露。护士应限制区域，使用危险药物泄漏包和化疗防护 PPE，并立即清洗暴露皮肤。评价重点是泄漏是否被控制和去污，以及暴露的皮肤或黏膜状况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the hazard first; PPE and cleanup methods must match a hazardous drug, not routine body-fluid precautions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先识别危险类型；PPE 和清理方法必须符合危险药物要求，而不是常规体液防护。","sourceMetadata":"NIOSH, Managing Hazardous Drug Exposures: Information for Healthcare Settings, DHHS Publication 2023-130, spill-cleanup controls and PPE table, https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/docs/2023-130/2023-130.pdf; OSHA, Controlling Occupational Exposure to Hazardous Drugs, immediate soap-and-water cleansing after direct skin contact, https://www.osha.gov/hazardous-drugs/controlling-occex","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2075,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_fib_standard_precautions_hygiene_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.605","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.605.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.605.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[207,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,65],"fullStemEn":"A nurse opens a manufacturer-labeled single-dose vial in a patient-care area and withdraws the prescribed dose. According to CDC safe injection practices, the vial is approved for use for how many patients? Enter a number.","fullStemZh":"护士在患者照护区打开一瓶厂家标注的单剂量药瓶，并抽取医嘱剂量。根据 CDC 安全注射规范，该药瓶获准供多少名患者使用？请输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter a number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"According to CDC safe injection practices, the vial is approved for use for how many patients?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据 CDC 安全注射规范，该药瓶获准供多少名患者使用？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"patient","zh":"名患者"},"acceptable":["1","one"],"numeric":{"value":1,"tolerance":0,"unit":"patient"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A single-dose vial is approved for one patient for one case, procedure, or injection. It must not be retained or shared for another patient.","rationaleCorrectZh":"单剂量药瓶仅批准供 1 名患者的一次病例、操作或注射使用，不得保留或与另一名患者共用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat “single-dose” as a patient-use limit, not a statement that the vial must contain exactly one measured dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把“单剂量”理解为患者使用限制，而不是瓶内必须恰好只有一个计量剂量。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Preventing Unsafe Injection Practices, Key points for single-dose vials, https://www.cdc.gov/injection-safety/hcp/clinical-safety/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2076,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_bt_perioperative_care_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.606","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.606.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.606.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,214],"terminalOffsetsZh":[73,81],"fullStemEn":"In the post-anesthesia care unit, an adult has a core temperature of 95.7 °F (35.4 °C) and is shivering after a 2-hour procedure. The client has 700 mL of IV fluid remaining to infuse. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名成人在接受 2 小时手术后进入麻醉后恢复室，核心体温为 95.7 °F (35.4 °C)，并出现寒战；还有 700 mL 静脉液体需要输注。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has 700 mL of IV fluid remaining to infuse.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名成人在接受 2 小时手术后进入麻醉后恢复室，核心体温为 95.7 °F (35.4 °C)，并出现寒战；还有 700 mL 静脉液体需要输注。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Inadvertent perioperative hypothermia","zh":"意外围手术期低体温"},{"id":"c3","en":"Expected normothermia","zh":"预期正常体温"},{"id":"c2","en":"Malignant hyperthermia","zh":"恶性高热"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Infuse the remaining IV fluid through an approved fluid warmer","zh":"通过获准的液体加温器输注剩余静脉液体"},{"id":"a3","en":"Use only one room-temperature sheet","zh":"仅盖一条室温床单"},{"id":"a4","en":"Apply ice packs rapidly","zh":"快速冰敷"},{"id":"a1","en":"Apply active forced-air warming","zh":"使用强制空气主动保暖"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"Serum uric acid","zh":"血清尿酸"},{"id":"p4","en":"Pupil color","zh":"瞳孔颜色"},{"id":"p1","en":"Serial core temperature and shivering response","zh":"连续核心体温和寒战反应"},{"id":"p2","en":"Skin condition under the warming device","zh":"保暖设备下的皮肤状况"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A core temperature below 96.8 °F (36.0 °C) after surgery is inadvertent perioperative hypothermia. NICE recommends active forced-air warming in recovery and warming IV fluids of 500 mL or more. Core temperature and response to warming, including skin condition, should be monitored.","rationaleCorrectZh":"术后核心体温低于 96.8 °F (36.0 °C) 属于意外围手术期低体温。NICE 建议在恢复室使用强制空气主动保暖，并加温 500 mL 或以上的静脉液体。应监测核心体温、复温反应及皮肤状况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the stated temperature and fluid volume: both cross guideline thresholds that point to active warming.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干中的体温和液体量：两者都跨过了提示主动保暖的指南阈值。","sourceMetadata":"NICE CG65, Hypothermia: prevention and management in adults having surgery, recommendations 1.3.6-1.3.8 and 1.4.1, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg65/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2077,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_hl_procedural_complications_dialysis_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.607","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.607.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.607.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,71],"fullStemEn":"A client is 2 weeks post creation of a left forearm arteriovenous access and reports worsening hand symptoms during hemodialysis. Highlight the findings that support dialysis access–associated distal ischemia and require prompt vascular evaluation.","fullStemZh":"一名患者左前臂建立动静脉通路后 2 周，在血液透析期间出现逐渐加重的手部症状。请标出支持“透析通路相关远端缺血”并需要尽快进行血管评估的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that support dialysis access–associated distal ischemia and require prompt vascular evaluation.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持“透析通路相关远端缺血”并需要尽快进行血管评估的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is 2 weeks post creation of a left forearm arteriovenous access and reports worsening hand symptoms during hemodialysis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者左前臂建立动静脉通路后 2 周，在血液透析期间出现逐渐加重的手部症状。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Assessment findings include:","zh":"评估发现包括："},{"id":"s2","en":"hand pain that becomes severe during dialysis;","zh":"透析期间手痛加重至剧烈；","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"cool, pale fingers on the access side;","zh":"通路侧手指冰凉苍白；","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"capillary refill 5 seconds in those fingers;","zh":"这些手指毛细血管再充盈 5 秒；","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"new fingertip numbness and weaker grip;","zh":"新发指尖麻木和握力减弱；","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"a 2-cm area of fading bruising beside the healing incision;","zh":"愈合切口旁有 2 cm 正在消退的瘀斑；","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"unchanged morning finger stiffness from known osteoarthritis.","zh":"既往骨关节炎所致晨起手指僵硬无变化。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pain that worsens during dialysis, cool pale digits, delayed capillary refill, and sensory or motor change distal to a new access are ischemic findings. Mild bruising near a healing incision and unchanged preexisting arthritis stiffness do not establish distal ischemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"透析时加重的疼痛、手指冰凉苍白、毛细血管再充盈延迟以及新通路远端的感觉或运动改变均提示缺血。愈合切口附近轻度瘀斑和既往关节炎僵硬不支持远端缺血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster distal perfusion findings: pain, pallor/coolness, delayed refill, and new sensory or motor deficit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把远端灌注线索组合起来：疼痛、苍白/冰凉、再充盈延迟，以及新发感觉或运动障碍。","sourceMetadata":"National Kidney Foundation, KDOQI Vascular Access Guideline Implementation Tool, Management of Steal or AV Access-related Hand Ischemia, symptoms, examination findings, severity grading, and early/urgent referral lanes, https://www.kidney.org/sites/default/files/vait-18_management_of_steal_or_av_access-related_hand_ischemia.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2078,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance3_2026_07_16_bt_intrapartum_fetal_monitoring_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.608","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.608.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.608.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,265],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,89],"fullStemEn":"A client at 39 weeks has ruptured membranes for 18 hours, a maternal temperature of 102.4 °F (39.1 °C), uterine tenderness, malodorous amniotic fluid, and a fetal heart rate baseline of 175/min for 12 minutes with moderate variability. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名孕 39 周患者破膜已 18 小时，母体体温 102.4 °F (39.1 °C)，子宫压痛，羊水有异味；胎心基线 175 次/分持续 12 分钟，变异中等。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client at 39 weeks has ruptured membranes for 18 hours, a maternal temperature of 102.4 °F (39.1 °C), uterine tenderness, malodorous amniotic fluid, and a fetal heart rate baseline of 175/min for 12 minutes with moderate variability.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名孕 39 周患者破膜已 18 小时，母体体温 102.4 °F (39.1 °C)，子宫压痛，羊水有异味；胎心基线 175 次/分持续 12 分钟，变异中等。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Suspected intraamniotic infection with fetal tachycardia","zh":"怀疑羊膜腔内感染并伴胎心过速"},{"id":"c3","en":"Placental abruption","zh":"胎盘早剥"},{"id":"c2","en":"Reassuring normal labor pattern","zh":"令人放心的正常产程模式"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Administer prescribed broad-spectrum antibiotics","zh":"给予医嘱的广谱抗生素"},{"id":"a1","en":"Notify the obstetric clinician promptly","zh":"立即通知产科临床人员"},{"id":"a4","en":"Begin amnioinfusion as the infection treatment","zh":"开始羊膜腔灌注作为感染治疗"},{"id":"a3","en":"Prepare for routine discharge home","zh":"准备常规出院回家"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"Maternal visual acuity","zh":"母体视力"},{"id":"p4","en":"Fundal height every 5 minutes","zh":"每 5 分钟测宫底高度"},{"id":"p2","en":"Fetal heart rate baseline","zh":"胎心率基线"},{"id":"p1","en":"Maternal temperature","zh":"母体体温"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Maternal fever of 102.4 °F (39.1 °C) plus uterine tenderness, malodorous fluid, prolonged rupture, and fetal tachycardia strongly support suspected intraamniotic infection. The nurse should notify the obstetric clinician and begin prescribed broad-spectrum antibiotics promptly. Maternal temperature and the fetal heart-rate baseline are key response parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"母体高热 102.4 °F (39.1 °C)，加上子宫压痛、羊水异味、破膜时间延长及胎心过速，强烈支持怀疑羊膜腔内感染。护士应通知产科临床人员，并及时开始医嘱的广谱抗生素。母体体温和胎心基线是关键疗效指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Combine maternal infection cues with the sustained fetal baseline; do not treat moderate variability as proof that the overall situation is benign.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把母体感染线索与持续的胎心基线结合判断；不要把中等变异当成整体情况良性的证据。","sourceMetadata":"American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, Committee Opinion No. 712, Intrapartum Management of Intraamniotic Infection, July 2024 diagnostic update and reaffirmed 2025 recommendations for intrapartum antibiotics, https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/committee-opinion/articles/2017/08/intrapartum-management-of-intraamniotic-infection; Macones GA et al., 2008 NICHD Workshop Report on Electronic Fetal Monitoring, baseline tachycardia nomenclature, DOI: 10.1097/AOG.0b013e3181841395","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2079,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_bt_client_advocacy_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.609","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.609.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.609.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[279,308],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,96],"fullStemEn":"A competent adult scheduled for a nonemergent procedure answers questions only after looking at the partner, who repeatedly says, “Just sign it; we already decided.” When the partner steps out, the client quietly says, “I am not sure I want this, but I do not want an argument.” Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"一名有决策能力的成年人准备接受非急诊操作。回答问题前，患者总是先看伴侣；伴侣反复说：“签字就行，我们已经决定了。”伴侣离开后，患者小声说：“我不确定自己想不想做，但我不想吵架。”完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"When the partner steps out, the client quietly says, “I am not sure I want this, but I do not want an argument.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"伴侣离开后，患者小声说：“我不确定自己想不想做，但我不想吵架。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely concern","zh":"最可能的担忧"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Coercion compromising voluntary decision-making","zh":"胁迫影响自愿决策"},{"id":"c2","en":"Expected preprocedure anxiety","zh":"正常的术前焦虑"},{"id":"c3","en":"Isolated knowledge deficit","zh":"单纯知识缺乏"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a3","en":"Ask the partner to sign the consent","zh":"让伴侣签署同意书"},{"id":"a4","en":"Reassure the client that proceeding will prevent conflict","zh":"安慰患者继续操作可避免冲突"},{"id":"a2","en":"Pause procedure preparation and notify the responsible clinician","zh":"暂停操作准备并通知负责的临床人员"},{"id":"a1","en":"Speak with the client privately","zh":"与患者私下交谈"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to assess","zh":"需要评估的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"Partner's satisfaction with the plan","zh":"伴侣对计划的满意度"},{"id":"p4","en":"Whether routine admission forms are complete","zh":"常规入院表格是否填写完整"},{"id":"p2","en":"Client's teach-back of benefits, risks, and alternatives","zh":"患者复述获益、风险和替代方案的能力"},{"id":"p1","en":"Client's independently stated choice","zh":"患者独立表达的选择"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The cues indicate possible coercion that may compromise a voluntary decision. The nurse should protect private communication, pause progression toward the procedure, and verify that the client's choice and understanding are voluntary before consent is relied upon.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这些线索提示可能存在胁迫，患者的决定未必出于自愿。护士应保护私下沟通，暂停推进操作，并在依赖同意之前确认患者的选择和理解确实是自愿的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a competent client appears pressured, prioritize voluntariness and the client's own voice before procedural efficiency.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当有决策能力的患者似乎受到压力时，应先保障自愿性和患者本人的声音，而不是追求流程效率。","sourceMetadata":"American Nurses Association, 2025 Code of Ethics for Nurses, Provision 3.2 (Advocating for Persons Who Receive Nursing Care), discussion of informed consent free from undue influence, https://codeofethics.ana.org/provision-3-2; American Nurses Association, Provision 1.4 (The Right to Self-Determination), https://codeofethics.ana.org/provision-1-4","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2080,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_sa_client_advocacy_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.610","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.610.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.610.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[235,257],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,74],"fullStemEn":"A client who uses a wheelchair arrives for an outpatient examination. The examination table cannot be lowered, and the client says, “I can transfer with a lift, but not by being carried.” Which nursing actions support client advocacy? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名使用轮椅的患者前来门诊检查。检查床无法降低，患者说：“我可以使用移位吊机转移，但不能被人抱过去。”哪些护理措施体现患者权益倡导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions support client advocacy?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施体现患者权益倡导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Notify the clinic leader that the current room is not accessible","zh":"通知门诊负责人当前房间不具备无障碍条件"},{"id":"E","en":"Have two staff members carry the client onto the table","zh":"让两名工作人员把患者抱到检查床上"},{"id":"D","en":"Provide privacy during equipment-assisted transfer","zh":"在使用设备移位时提供隐私保护"},{"id":"F","en":"Reschedule the client without arranging an accessible alternative","zh":"在未安排无障碍替代方案的情况下改期"},{"id":"B","en":"Obtain a mechanical lift and staff trained to use it","zh":"取得移位吊机并安排受过使用培训的人员"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client to describe the safest usual transfer method","zh":"请患者说明平时最安全的移位方式"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Advocacy includes respecting the client's stated transfer limits, obtaining appropriate equipment and trained help, preserving privacy, and escalating an accessibility barrier rather than improvising an unsafe transfer or delaying care without a plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"权益倡导包括尊重患者说明的移位限制，获得合适设备和受训人员，保护隐私，并上报无障碍障碍；不应临时采用不安全转移，也不应在没有解决方案的情况下推迟护理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select actions that remove the barrier while preserving the client's expressed limits, safety, and dignity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能够消除障碍，同时维护患者所表达的限制、安全和尊严的措施。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Justice, Access to Medical Care for Individuals with Mobility Disabilities, accessible examination equipment, lift transfers, trained assistance, and equal access to care, https://www.ada.gov/resources/medical-care-mobility/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2081,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_mx_client_advocacy_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.611","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.611.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.611.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,47],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalized client is in custody of a correctional officer. The client is alert and has decision-making capacity. Classify each nursing action as supporting or not supporting client advocacy.","fullStemZh":"一名住院患者由惩教人员看守。患者意识清楚并具有决策能力。判断每项护理行为是否支持患者权益倡导。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing action as supporting or not supporting client advocacy.","terminalSentenceZh":"判断每项护理行为是否支持患者权益倡导。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is alert and has decision-making capacity.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者意识清楚并具有决策能力。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Address assessment and consent questions to the client rather than to the officer","zh":"把评估和同意问题直接问患者，而不是问看守人员"},{"id":"r2","en":"Request that the officer stand outside hearing range during sensitive history-taking when safety permits","zh":"在安全允许时，请看守人员在询问敏感病史期间站到听不到的位置"},{"id":"r3","en":"Document the capable client's own treatment preferences in the care plan","zh":"在护理计划中记录有决策能力患者本人的治疗意愿"},{"id":"r4","en":"Give the officer a complete list of the client's unrelated chronic diagnoses","zh":"向看守人员提供患者所有无关慢性病诊断清单"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Supports advocacy","zh":"支持权益倡导"},{"id":"c2","en":"Does not support advocacy","zh":"不支持权益倡导"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Custody does not erase the capable client's autonomy, privacy, or right to clinically appropriate care. The nurse should communicate directly with the client, limit nonclinical observers when feasible, document the client's own treatment preferences, and avoid disclosing unrelated health information.","rationaleCorrectZh":"被羁押并不会取消有决策能力患者的自主权、隐私权或获得适当临床护理的权利。护士应直接与患者沟通，在可行时限制无临床需要的旁观者，记录患者本人的治疗意愿，并避免披露无关健康信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not confuse legal custody with loss of autonomy or confidentiality. Judge each action by whether it protects the client's rights within necessary safety limits.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把法律羁押等同于失去自主权或保密权。应判断每项行为是否在必要安全限制内保护患者权利。","sourceMetadata":"American Nurses Association, 2025 Code of Ethics for Nurses, Provision 1.4 (The Right to Self-Determination), https://codeofethics.ana.org/provision-1-4; Provision 3.1 (Privacy and Confidentiality), https://codeofethics.ana.org/provision-3-1; U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, HIPAA disclosures involving individuals in lawful custody, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/2073/may-covered-entity-collect-use-disclose-criminal-data-under-hipaa.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2082,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_fb_conflict_resolution_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.612","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.612.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.612.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,64],"fullStemEn":"Facility policy states: When a nurse raises the same immediate safety concern twice and the team still does not resolve it, the nurse must activate the formal escalation pathway. The nurse should now use the ________.","fullStemZh":"机构政策规定：当护士针对同一紧急安全问题两次提出异议而团队仍未解决时，护士必须启动正式升级途径。护士现在应使用________。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should now use the ________.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士现在应使用________。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy states: When a nurse raises the same immediate safety concern twice and the team still does not resolve it, the nurse must activate the formal escalation pathway.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：当护士针对同一紧急安全问题两次提出异议而团队仍未解决时，护士必须启动正式升级途径。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Escalation pathway","zh":"升级途径"},"acceptable":["chain of command","the chain of command"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The policy explicitly directs the nurse to use the chain of command after two unresolved safety challenges.","rationaleCorrectZh":"政策明确规定，在两次安全异议仍未解决后，护士应启动指挥链。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a fill-in item with an inline policy, use the exact operational term that matches the stated trigger.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于题干给出机构政策的填空题，应填写与触发条件完全对应的操作术语。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Mutual Support overview (Two-Challenge Rule and chain-of-command escalation), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/overview/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2083,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_bt_conflict_resolution_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.613","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.613.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.613.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[531,560],"terminalOffsetsZh":[162,169],"fullStemEn":"A physical therapist arrives to ambulate a postoperative client. The bedside nurse reports that the client became dizzy and nearly fell when standing 10 minutes earlier. The therapist points to the existing ambulation order and says delaying will impede recovery; the nurse responds, “You never listen to nursing.” Voices rise, the client remains seated, and the plan is unresolved. Facility policy requires a new bedside safety assessment after symptoms during mobility and agreement on readiness criteria before another attempt. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"物理治疗师前来协助一名术后患者下床行走。床旁护士报告，患者在 10 分钟前站立时出现头晕，险些跌倒。治疗师指着现有的行走医嘱说，延迟活动会妨碍康复；护士回应：“你从来不听护理人员的意见。”双方声音越来越大，患者仍坐着，计划尚未解决。机构政策要求患者在活动中出现症状后重新进行床旁安全评估，并在再次尝试前就可活动标准达成一致。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires a new bedside safety assessment after symptoms during mobility and agreement on readiness criteria before another attempt.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策要求患者在活动中出现症状后重新进行床旁安全评估，并在再次尝试前就可活动标准达成一致。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Primary problem","zh":"主要问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Unresolved informational conflict about safe mobilization","zh":"关于安全活动的未解决信息性冲突"},{"id":"c3","en":"Client refusal of postoperative rehabilitation","zh":"患者拒绝术后康复"},{"id":"c2","en":"An interpersonal conflict without a client-safety issue","zh":"不涉及患者安全问题的人际冲突"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Agree who will reassess the client and which findings permit another attempt","zh":"明确由谁重新评估，并商定哪些结果允许再次尝试"},{"id":"a4","en":"File a conduct complaint before resolving the current mobility plan","zh":"在解决当前活动计划前先提出行为投诉"},{"id":"a1","en":"Pause ambulation and hold a brief huddle using the current assessment data","zh":"暂停行走，并利用当前评估数据进行简短团队沟通"},{"id":"a3","en":"Proceed solely because the original ambulation order remains active","zh":"仅因原行走医嘱仍有效就继续活动"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to verify","zh":"需要核实的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Each clinician's preferred usual workflow","zh":"每名临床人员偏好的惯常工作方式"},{"id":"p2","en":"The shared plan and closed-loop confirmation of roles","zh":"共同计划以及对角色的闭环确认"},{"id":"p1","en":"The client's current symptoms and reassessment findings","zh":"患者当前症状和重新评估结果"},{"id":"p3","en":"The original mobility order without the new assessment","zh":"未结合新评估结果的原活动医嘱"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The central problem is unresolved informational conflict about whether current assessment findings support safe mobilization. A brief huddle using the new findings and an agreed reassessment plan address both safety and teamwork. Current symptoms and a shared, closed-loop plan are the key parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"核心问题是：当前评估结果是否支持安全活动这一信息性冲突尚未解决。利用新评估结果进行简短团队沟通，并就重新评估计划达成一致，可同时处理安全与团队协作。当前症状以及经过闭环确认的共同计划是关键指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When voices rise, identify the task-related information that remains unresolved, then choose actions that create a shared, checkable plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当双方声音升高时，先找出尚未解决的任务相关信息，再选择能形成共同且可核实计划的措施。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Conflict in Teams (informational conflict), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/conflict.html; Team Leadership overview (huddles and shared plans), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/team/overview/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2084,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_hl_conflict_resolution_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.614","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.614.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.614.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,44],"fullStemEn":"The charge nurse is facilitating a discussion between two nurses who disagree about shared equipment use. Highlight the statements that demonstrate constructive conflict-resolution communication.","fullStemZh":"责任护士正在协调两名护士关于共用设备使用的分歧。请突出显示体现建设性冲突解决沟通的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the statements that demonstrate constructive conflict-resolution communication.","terminalSentenceZh":"请突出显示体现建设性冲突解决沟通的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The charge nurse is facilitating a discussion between two nurses who disagree about shared equipment use.","penultimateSentenceZh":"责任护士正在协调两名护士关于共用设备使用的分歧。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Charge nurse:","zh":"责任护士："},{"id":"s2","en":"“The infusion pump was unavailable for 20 minutes, which delayed the scheduled medication.”","zh":"“输注泵有 20 分钟无法使用，导致计划用药延迟。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"“Can you describe what was happening on your side?”","zh":"“你能说明一下当时你那边的情况吗？”","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"“Let us use the equipment board and confirm the handoff time together.”","zh":"“我们使用设备登记板，并一起确认交接时间。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"“You always take equipment without thinking about anyone else.”","zh":"“你总是不顾别人就把设备拿走。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"“I will correct you in front of the team so this stops.”","zh":"“我要当着团队的面纠正你，这样你才会停止。”","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Constructive conflict communication states the concern objectively, invites the other person's perspective, and proposes a shared next step. Blame, absolutes, and public humiliation intensify conflict.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建设性冲突沟通应客观说明担忧，邀请对方表达观点，并提出共同的下一步。指责、绝对化用语和公开羞辱会加剧冲突。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for objective observations, curiosity, and a jointly testable next step—not blame or absolute language.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找客观观察、了解对方的态度和可共同执行的下一步，而不是指责或绝对化语言。","sourceMetadata":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, TeamSTEPPS 3.0, Tool: DESC (describe objectively, express concerns, suggest alternatives, seek agreement), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/desc.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2085,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_bt_confidentiality_hipaa_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.615","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.615.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.615.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[399,428],"terminalOffsetsZh":[107,114],"fullStemEn":"During bedside shift report in a semiprivate room, the nurse discusses a client's new cancer diagnosis and genetic test results in a normal speaking voice. The roommate's visitors are seated a few feet away and can hear the report. The curtain is closed, but no effort is made to limit what is said or who can hear it. Facility policy requires suspected privacy incidents to be reported for review. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"在半私密病房进行床旁交班时，护士以正常音量讨论一名患者的新发癌症诊断和基因检测结果。室友的访客坐在几英尺外，能够听到交班内容。虽然拉上了帘子，但没有采取措施限制谈话内容或听众。机构政策要求报告疑似隐私事件以供审查。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires suspected privacy incidents to be reported for review.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策要求报告疑似隐私事件以供审查。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely privacy issue","zh":"最可能的隐私问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Avoidable disclosure without reasonable safeguards","zh":"未采取合理保护措施造成的可避免披露"},{"id":"c3","en":"Unavoidable incidental disclosure despite safeguards","zh":"采取保护措施后仍不可避免的附带披露"},{"id":"c2","en":"Permitted disclosure because a curtain was closed","zh":"因已拉帘而允许的披露"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a3","en":"Ask the visitors to promise not to repeat what they heard","zh":"要求访客承诺不传播所听到的内容"},{"id":"a1","en":"Stop or move the sensitive report to a private setting","zh":"停止敏感交班或移至私密环境"},{"id":"a4","en":"Document the report as routine and take no further action","zh":"把交班记录为常规事项，不再采取其他措施"},{"id":"a2","en":"Follow the facility privacy-incident reporting process","zh":"按照机构隐私事件流程报告"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Information to determine","zh":"需要确认的信息"},"tokens":[{"id":"p1","en":"Which protected details were audible","zh":"哪些受保护信息可被听到"},{"id":"p3","en":"Whether the report followed the unit's usual bedside-handoff workflow","zh":"交班是否遵循病区惯常的床旁交班流程"},{"id":"p2","en":"Who was within hearing range","zh":"谁在可听范围内"},{"id":"p4","en":"Whether the visitors say they were paying attention","zh":"访客是否声称自己当时在留意交班内容"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is an avoidable disclosure because reasonable safeguards were not used despite nearby unauthorized listeners. The nurse should stop or relocate the sensitive discussion and report the event according to privacy policy. The key follow-up is what information was audible and who could hear it.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这是可避免的信息披露，因为在附近有未授权听众时没有采取合理保护措施。护士应停止敏感讨论或移至私密地点，并按隐私政策报告事件。关键后续是确认哪些信息可被听到以及谁听到了。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For incidental-disclosure questions, ask whether reasonable safeguards were used and whether the disclosure was avoidable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于附带披露问题，应判断是否使用了合理保护措施，以及披露是否可以避免。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, HIPAA Privacy Rule guidance, Incidental Uses and Disclosures (reasonable safeguards and avoidable disclosures), https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/privacy/guidance/incidental-uses-and-disclosures/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2086,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_or_confidentiality_hipaa_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.616","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.616.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.616.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[343,370],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,98],"fullStemEn":"A nurse discovers that a hospital-issued smartphone containing a locally stored client assignment list is missing. Facility policy requires the following sequence: first prevent further access if possible; next notify the privacy/security contact; then preserve the facts needed for investigation; finally complete the formal incident report. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"护士发现一部医院配发的智能手机丢失，手机本地存有患者分配清单。机构政策要求以下顺序：首先尽可能阻止继续访问；其次通知隐私/信息安全联系人；然后保留调查所需事实；最后完成正式事件报告。请按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires the following sequence: first prevent further access if possible; next notify the privacy/security contact; then preserve the facts needed for investigation; finally complete the formal incident report.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策要求以下顺序：首先尽可能阻止继续访问；其次通知隐私/信息安全联系人；然后保留调查所需事实；最后完成正式事件报告。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Notify the designated privacy or information-security contact","zh":"通知指定的隐私或信息安全联系人"},{"id":"A","en":"Complete the formal privacy incident report","zh":"完成正式隐私事件报告"},{"id":"B","en":"Use the device-management system to lock or wipe the phone","zh":"使用设备管理系统锁定或清除手机"},{"id":"D","en":"Record the last known location, time discovered, and data believed to be on the phone","zh":"记录最后已知位置、发现时间以及据信存储在手机上的数据"}],"correct":["B","C","D","A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The policy stated in the stem establishes this sequence: remotely lock or wipe the device, notify privacy/security, document factual loss details without altering evidence, and then complete the formal incident report.","rationaleCorrectZh":"题干中的机构政策明确了以下顺序：远程锁定或清除设备，通知隐私/信息安全部门，记录丢失事实且不篡改证据，最后完成正式事件报告。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the stem provides an explicit organizational sequence, order the options by those stated verbs rather than by a generic memory aid.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题干给出明确机构顺序时，应按题干中的动作排序，而不是依赖笼统记忆口诀。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Health Sector Cybersecurity Coordination Center, HPH Mobile Device Security Checklist (remote wiping and immediate reporting of lost or stolen devices), https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/hph-mobile-device-security-checklist-tlpclear.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2087,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_fb_confidentiality_hipaa_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.617","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.617.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.617.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,257],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,70],"fullStemEn":"A quality-improvement analyst asks a nurse for the entire medical record when only medication-administration times are needed for the approved review. Under the HIPAA Privacy Rule, the nurse should disclose only the ________ information needed for the task.","fullStemZh":"质量改进分析员向护士索取整份病历，但经批准的审查只需要用药时间。根据 HIPAA 隐私规则，护士应仅披露完成任务所需的________信息。","terminalSentenceEn":"Under the HIPAA Privacy Rule, the nurse should disclose only the ________ information needed for the task.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据 HIPAA 隐私规则，护士应仅披露完成任务所需的________信息。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A quality-improvement analyst asks a nurse for the entire medical record when only medication-administration times are needed for the approved review.","penultimateSentenceZh":"质量改进分析员向护士索取整份病历，但经批准的审查只需要用药时间。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"HIPAA standard","zh":"HIPAA 标准"},"acceptable":["minimum necessary","the minimum necessary"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The HIPAA principle is the minimum necessary standard: use or disclose only the information reasonably needed for the purpose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA 的原则是“最低必要”标准：仅使用或披露为实现目的而合理需要的信息。","testTakingStrategyEn":"HIPAA questions often test the exact phrase “minimum necessary” when the request is broader than the stated purpose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当信息请求范围大于所述目的时，HIPAA 题目常考准确术语“最低必要”。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, HIPAA Privacy Rule: Minimum Necessary Requirement, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/privacy/guidance/minimum-necessary-requirement/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2088,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_fb_ppe_sterile_technique_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.618","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.618.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.618.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[106,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,64],"fullStemEn":"A nurse dons a fit-tested disposable N95 respirator before entering an airborne-infection isolation room. OSHA requires the nurse to perform a ________ each time the respirator is put on.","fullStemZh":"护士在进入空气传播隔离病房前戴上已完成适合性测试的一次性 N95 呼吸器。OSHA 要求每次戴上呼吸器时都进行________。","terminalSentenceEn":"OSHA requires the nurse to perform a ________ each time the respirator is put on.","terminalSentenceZh":"OSHA 要求每次戴上呼吸器时都进行________。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse dons a fit-tested disposable N95 respirator before entering an airborne-infection isolation room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在进入空气传播隔离病房前戴上已完成适合性测试的一次性 N95 呼吸器。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Required check","zh":"必需检查"},"acceptable":["user seal check","seal check","a user seal check"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A user seal check is performed each time a tight-fitting respirator is donned; it is distinct from periodic fit testing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每次戴上密合式呼吸器时都要进行使用者密合性检查；这与定期适合性测试不同。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish the recurring action from the periodic program requirement: seal check every donning, fit test on the required schedule.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分每次操作和定期项目要求：每次佩戴做密合性检查，按规定周期做适合性测试。","sourceMetadata":"OSHA, Respiratory Protection Standard, 29 CFR 1910.134, user seal checks, https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.134","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2089,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_dc_ppe_sterile_technique_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.619","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.619.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.619.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,170],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,55],"fullStemEn":"A nurse will irrigate a deep wound. Facility policy classifies the procedure as likely to produce splashes of blood or body fluid but not aerosols. Complete the PPE plan.","fullStemZh":"护士将冲洗一个深部伤口。机构政策将该操作归类为可能产生血液或体液飞溅，但不会产生气溶胶。完成个人防护装备计划。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the PPE plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成个人防护装备计划。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy classifies the procedure as likely to produce splashes of blood or body fluid but not aerosols.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策将该操作归类为可能产生血液或体液飞溅，但不会产生气溶胶。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should wear {{1}} and protect the face with {{2}}.","zh":"护士应穿戴{{1}}，并使用{{2}}保护面部。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"sterile gloves only","zh":"仅无菌手套"},{"id":"o3","en":"shoe covers only","zh":"仅鞋套"},{"id":"o1","en":"gloves and a fluid-resistant gown","zh":"手套和防液体渗透隔离衣"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"no additional PPE","zh":"无需其他 PPE"},{"id":"o1","en":"a surgical mask and eye protection","zh":"外科口罩和护目装备"},{"id":"o2","en":"an N95 respirator without eye protection","zh":"N95 呼吸器但不戴护目装备"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For anticipated splash exposure without an aerosol hazard, the nurse uses gloves and a fluid-resistant gown plus protection for the mouth, nose, and eyes. An N95 is not required by the stated hazard classification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于预期有飞溅但无气溶胶危险的操作，护士应使用手套、防液体渗透隔离衣，并保护口、鼻和眼睛。根据题干的危险分类，不需要 N95。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match PPE to the exposure named in the stem: splash protection is different from respiratory aerosol protection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据题干中的暴露类型匹配 PPE：防飞溅与防气溶胶呼吸保护不同。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Core Infection Prevention and Control Practices for Safe Healthcare Delivery in All Settings, Standard Precautions, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/core-practices/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2090,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_sa_ppe_sterile_technique_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.620","itemType":"select_all","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.620.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.620.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[187,209],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,57],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to perform open tracheal suctioning. Facility policy requires sterile technique and anticipates possible respiratory-secretion splash. Which actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士准备进行开放式气管吸痰。机构政策要求采用无菌技术，并预计可能有呼吸道分泌物飞溅。哪些措施适当？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些措施适当？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Reuse the catheter for the next pass after it rests on the bed","zh":"导管放在床上后继续用于下一次吸引"},{"id":"C","en":"Use sterile gloves to handle the suction catheter","zh":"使用无菌手套操作吸痰导管"},{"id":"B","en":"Wear a mask, eye protection, and a gown for splash protection","zh":"佩戴口罩、护目装备和隔离衣以防飞溅"},{"id":"F","en":"Use clean gloves to reposition the sterile catheter tip","zh":"用清洁手套重新调整无菌导管尖端"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene before preparing the equipment","zh":"准备设备前进行手卫生"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the catheter from touching nonsterile surfaces before insertion","zh":"插入前避免导管接触非无菌表面"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Open suctioning under the stated policy requires hand hygiene, appropriate face and clothing splash protection, sterile gloves for the catheter, and maintenance of catheter sterility. Reusing a contaminated catheter or touching it with nonsterile gloves breaks technique.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据题干政策，开放式吸痰需要手卫生、适当的面部和衣物防飞溅保护、使用无菌手套操作导管，并保持导管无菌。重复使用受污染导管或用非无菌手套触碰导管都会破坏无菌技术。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Combine the two cues: sterile device handling plus splash protection. Choose actions that satisfy both.","testTakingStrategyZh":"结合两个线索：无菌器械操作和防飞溅保护。选择同时满足两者的措施。","sourceMetadata":"American Association for Respiratory Care, AARC Clinical Practice Guidelines: Artificial Airway Suctioning (2022), sterile technique for open suctioning, https://www.aarc.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/cpg-artificial-airway-suctioning.pdf; CDC, Core Infection Prevention and Control Practices, PPE selected for anticipated exposure, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/core-practices/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2091,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_bt_standard_precautions_hygiene_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.621","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.621.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.621.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[233,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,59],"fullStemEn":"During medication preparation, a nurse observes a colleague use the same syringe to enter a multidose vial after the syringe was used to inject a client. The colleague then places the vial back in the shared medication refrigerator. Complete the bow-tie diagram.","fullStemZh":"在配药过程中，护士看到同事用刚给患者注射过的同一支注射器再次穿刺多剂量药瓶，然后把药瓶放回共用药品冰箱。完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie diagram.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The colleague then places the vial back in the shared medication refrigerator.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在配药过程中，护士看到同事用刚给患者注射过的同一支注射器再次穿刺多剂量药瓶，然后把药瓶放回共用药品冰箱。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely safety problem","zh":"最可能的安全问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Possible contamination of a shared multidose vial","zh":"共用多剂量药瓶可能被污染"},{"id":"c3","en":"Loss of medication potency from refrigeration","zh":"冷藏导致药效丧失"},{"id":"c2","en":"Routine medication-waste discrepancy","zh":"常规药品浪费记录不符"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Report the event to infection prevention and the appropriate leader","zh":"向感染预防部门和相应负责人报告事件"},{"id":"a1","en":"Remove and quarantine the vial from further use","zh":"停止使用并隔离该药瓶"},{"id":"a3","en":"Replace the needle and continue using the same syringe","zh":"更换针头后继续使用同一支注射器"},{"id":"a4","en":"Return the vial to circulation if the solution looks clear","zh":"如果药液看起来清澈就继续使用"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Information to determine","zh":"需要确认的信息"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"Whether the vial remains within its labeled expiration date","zh":"药瓶是否仍在标示有效期内"},{"id":"p1","en":"Which clients received doses from the vial after the unsafe entry","zh":"不安全穿刺后哪些患者使用过该药瓶"},{"id":"p3","en":"Whether the vial contains a preservative","zh":"药瓶是否含防腐剂"},{"id":"p2","en":"Exposure-evaluation and follow-up recommendations","zh":"暴露评估和随访建议"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reentering a multidose vial with a used syringe can contaminate the vial and expose multiple clients. The nurse should remove the vial from use and report the unsafe injection event so exposed clients can be identified and evaluated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用已用过的注射器再次穿刺多剂量药瓶可能污染药瓶并使多名患者暴露。护士应停止使用并隔离该药瓶，同时报告不安全注射事件，以便识别和评估可能暴露的患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a used syringe reenters shared medication, think beyond one client: stop the source and trace potential exposures.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当已使用的注射器再次进入共用药品时，要考虑不止一名患者：停止污染源并追踪潜在暴露。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Preventing Unsafe Injection Practices, https://www.cdc.gov/injection-safety/hcp/clinical-safety/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2092,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_mx_standard_precautions_hygiene_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.622","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.622.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.622.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[132,217],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,51],"fullStemEn":"A clinic applies respiratory hygiene and cough etiquette to every person with signs of respiratory infection at the point of entry. Classify each action as part of this standard-precautions approach or not part of it.","fullStemZh":"某门诊在入口处对所有有呼吸道感染迹象的人实施呼吸卫生和咳嗽礼仪。判断每项措施是否属于这种标准预防措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each action as part of this standard-precautions approach or not part of it.","terminalSentenceZh":"判断每项措施是否属于这种标准预防措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A clinic applies respiratory hygiene and cough etiquette to every person with signs of respiratory infection at the point of entry.","penultimateSentenceZh":"某门诊在入口处对所有有呼吸道感染迹象的人实施呼吸卫生和咳嗽礼仪。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Ask about cough and respiratory symptoms during arrival screening","zh":"到达筛查时询问咳嗽和呼吸道症状"},{"id":"r2","en":"Offer a mask to a coughing person who can tolerate it","zh":"向能够耐受的咳嗽者提供口罩"},{"id":"r3","en":"Provide tissues and hand-hygiene supplies near the entrance","zh":"在入口附近提供纸巾和手卫生用品"},{"id":"r4","en":"Seat symptomatic persons apart from others when space permits","zh":"空间允许时让有症状者与他人分开就座"},{"id":"r5","en":"Delay urgent assessment until the cough has stopped","zh":"等咳嗽停止后再进行紧急评估"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Part of respiratory hygiene","zh":"属于呼吸卫生"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not part of respiratory hygiene","zh":"不属于呼吸卫生"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Respiratory hygiene includes early identification, source-control masking when tolerated, tissues and hand hygiene, and spatial separation when feasible. Automatically delaying urgent assessment because a person is coughing is not an infection-control measure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呼吸卫生包括尽早识别、在可耐受时佩戴口罩进行源头控制、提供纸巾和手卫生，以及在可行时保持空间距离。仅因咳嗽就自动延迟紧急评估并不是感染控制措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Standard precautions are applied by anticipated exposure and symptoms, not by confirmed diagnosis. Choose source-control and hygiene actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"标准预防依据预期暴露和症状实施，而不是等确诊后才实施。选择源头控制和卫生措施。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Core Infection Prevention and Control Practices for Safe Healthcare Delivery in All Settings, Standard Precautions, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/core-practices/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2093,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_hl_standard_precautions_hygiene_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.623","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.623.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.623.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,31],"fullStemEn":"Review the medication-preparation and administration note. Highlight the actions that break standard precautions or safe medication practice.","fullStemZh":"查看配药与给药记录。突出显示违反标准预防或安全用药操作的行为。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions that break standard precautions or safe medication practice.","terminalSentenceZh":"突出显示违反标准预防或安全用药操作的行为。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the medication-preparation and administration note.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看配药与给药记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Medication-preparation note:","zh":"配药记录："},{"id":"s2","en":"The nurse prepares the medication in the designated clean area.","zh":"护士在指定的清洁区域配药。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"While wearing gloves, the nurse answers a personal phone and then resumes preparation with the same gloves.","zh":"护士戴着手套接听私人电话，然后继续用同一副手套配药。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The nurse disinfects the vial stopper and allows it to dry.","zh":"护士消毒药瓶塞并等待其干燥。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"After giving the injection, the nurse recaps the used needle with two hands before walking to the sharps container.","zh":"给药后，护士在走向锐器盒前用双手回套已使用的针头。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The nurse stores prepared syringes on the counter directly beside the sink.","zh":"护士把已准备好的注射器放在紧邻水槽的台面上。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3","s5","s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Preparing medication in a clean area and disinfecting a vial stopper are appropriate. Handling a phone with gloved hands and returning to preparation, recapping a used needle with two hands, and storing medication beside a sink create contamination or sharps risks.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在清洁区域配药并消毒药瓶塞是适当做法。戴手套操作手机后继续配药、用双手回套已使用针头，以及在水槽旁存放药物都会造成污染或锐器风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate clean preparation steps from actions that introduce contact contamination, splash contamination, or sharps exposure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分清洁配药步骤与引入接触污染、飞溅污染或锐器暴露的行为。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Preventing Unsafe Injection Practices, https://www.cdc.gov/injection-safety/hcp/clinical-safety/index.html; Occupational Safety and Health Administration, Bloodborne Pathogens Standard, 29 CFR 1910.1030(d)(2)(vii), prohibition on contaminated-needle recapping except narrow exceptions and prohibition on two-handed recapping, https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.1030","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2094,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_hl_disaster_emergency_preparedness_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.624","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.624.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.624.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[270,323],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,84],"fullStemEn":"A fire alarm sounds on a hospital unit. Facility fire policy states: clients in immediate danger are moved first; smoke-compartment doors are closed; evacuation proceeds horizontally beyond the nearest smoke barrier before any vertical movement; elevators are not used. Highlight the cues that require immediate correction.","fullStemZh":"医院病区响起火警。机构消防政策规定：先转移处于直接危险中的患者；关闭防烟分区门；先水平疏散至最近防烟屏障之外，再考虑垂直转移；不得使用电梯。突出显示需要立即纠正的情况。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the cues that require immediate correction.","terminalSentenceZh":"突出显示需要立即纠正的情况。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility fire policy states: clients in immediate danger are moved first; smoke-compartment doors are closed; evacuation proceeds horizontally beyond the nearest smoke barrier before any vertical movement; elevators are not used.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构消防政策规定：先转移处于直接危险中的患者；关闭防烟分区门；先水平疏散至最近防烟屏障之外，再考虑垂直转移；不得使用电梯。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Unit status:","zh":"病区情况："},{"id":"s2","en":"A mechanically ventilated client in the room nearest the smoke is left in place while ambulatory clients are moved first.","zh":"离烟雾最近房间的一名机械通气患者被留在原处，而能行走的患者先被转移。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"A staff member closes the smoke-compartment doors.","zh":"一名工作人员关闭防烟分区门。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Another staff member verifies that the smoke-compartment door closes after the evacuation group passes.","zh":"另一名工作人员在疏散小组通过后确认防烟分区门关闭。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"A team plans to use the service elevator for bedbound clients.","zh":"一个小组计划使用货运电梯转移卧床患者。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"An ambulatory client is directed beyond the nearest smoke barrier on the same floor.","zh":"一名能行走的患者被引导到同一楼层最近防烟屏障之外。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Staff begin carrying clients down the stairs before relocating them past the smoke barrier.","zh":"工作人员在把患者转移到防烟屏障之外前就开始沿楼梯向下搬运。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s5","s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The ventilated client nearest the smoke is in immediate danger and must not be left behind. Using an elevator violates policy, and beginning vertical evacuation before horizontal relocation reverses the stated sequence. Closing the smoke-compartment door after passage and moving an ambulatory client beyond the smoke barrier are appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"离烟雾最近的机械通气患者处于直接危险中，不能被留在原处。使用电梯违反政策，在完成水平疏散前开始垂直疏散颠倒了题干顺序。人员通过后确认防烟分区门关闭，以及将能行走的患者转移到防烟屏障之外，均为适当做法。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor to the inline policy: immediate danger first, contain smoke, horizontal before vertical, no elevators.","testTakingStrategyZh":"紧扣题干政策：直接危险优先、控制烟雾、先水平后垂直、禁用电梯。","sourceMetadata":"ASPR TRACIE, St. Louis Hospital Evacuation and Transportation Plan, definitions and use of immediate-danger, horizontal, vertical, and smoke-compartment evacuation, https://files.asprtracie.hhs.gov/documents/st-louis-hospital-evacuation-and-transportation-plan-508.pdf; exact sequence and elevator restriction are supplied by the facility policy in the item","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2095,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_fb_disaster_emergency_preparedness_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.625","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.625.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.625.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,71],"fullStemEn":"Floodwater has entered the hospital's ground floor and is rising. The emergency plan directs staff to move clients and essential services from lower floors to predetermined safe floors within the same building. This movement is called ________ evacuation.","fullStemZh":"洪水已进入医院一楼并持续上涨。应急计划要求工作人员把患者和关键服务从较低楼层转移到同一建筑内预定的安全楼层。这种转移称为________疏散。","terminalSentenceEn":"This movement is called ________ evacuation.","terminalSentenceZh":"这种转移称为________疏散。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The emergency plan directs staff to move clients and essential services from lower floors to predetermined safe floors within the same building.","penultimateSentenceZh":"应急计划要求工作人员把患者和关键服务从较低楼层转移到同一建筑内预定的安全楼层。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Type of evacuation","zh":"疏散类型"},"acceptable":["vertical","vertical evacuation"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Moving occupants between floors within the same building is vertical evacuation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在同一建筑内楼层之间转移人员称为垂直疏散。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Horizontal means same floor; vertical means another floor. Use the direction of movement described in the plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"水平表示同一楼层，垂直表示不同楼层。根据计划描述的移动方向作答。","sourceMetadata":"ASPR TRACIE, St. Louis Hospital Evacuation and Transportation Plan, vertical evacuation defined as movement to a different floor within the facility, https://files.asprtracie.hhs.gov/documents/st-louis-hospital-evacuation-and-transportation-plan-508.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2096,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_mocsic_2026_07_15_dc_disaster_emergency_preparedness_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.626","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.626.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.626.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[293,315],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,86],"fullStemEn":"During an active-shooter event, the hospital's emergency plan directs staff in unaffected locked units to secure in place, silence devices, stay away from doors and windows, and wait for an authenticated all-clear. After the all-clear, clinical teams begin triage in the designated safe area. Complete the response.","fullStemZh":"医院发生活跃枪手事件时，应急计划要求未受影响且已上锁的病区就地防护、将设备静音、远离门窗，并等待经验证的解除警报。解除警报后，临床团队在指定安全区域开始分诊。完成应对措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the response.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成应对措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After the all-clear, clinical teams begin triage in the designated safe area.","penultimateSentenceZh":"解除警报后，临床团队在指定安全区域开始分诊。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Before the authenticated all-clear, the nurse should {{1}}. After the all-clear, the nurse should {{2}}.","zh":"在收到经验证的解除警报前，护士应{{1}}。解除警报后，护士应{{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"enter the corridor to look for casualties","zh":"进入走廊寻找伤员"},{"id":"o1","en":"remain secured and avoid opening the door for an unverified voice","zh":"保持锁闭，不因未经核实的声音而开门"},{"id":"o3","en":"announce the unit location over a personal phone","zh":"用私人手机公布病区位置"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"begin triage in the designated safe area","zh":"在指定安全区域开始分诊"},{"id":"o3","en":"resume routine unit operations without reporting to the designated safe area","zh":"不前往指定安全区域报到，直接恢复病区常规运行"},{"id":"o2","en":"continue lockdown indefinitely without checking instructions","zh":"无限期继续封锁且不查看指示"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Before an authenticated all-clear, the unit follows secure-in-place actions and does not open the door for an unverified voice. After the all-clear, staff transition to clinical triage in the designated safe area; resuming routine operations would skip the plan's post-event response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在收到经验证的解除警报前，病区应执行就地防护措施，不因未经核实的声音而开门。解除警报后，工作人员转入指定安全区域开展临床分诊；直接恢复常规运行会跳过计划规定的事件后应对。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the security phase from the clinical-response phase: secure first, triage after the verified all-clear.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分安全阶段和临床应对阶段：先就地防护，经验证解除警报后再分诊。","sourceMetadata":"Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency, Hospitals and Healthcare Facilities Security Action Guide, lockdown, safe-location, patient-security, and device-silencing guidance, https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/publications/19_0515_cisa_action-guide-hospitals-and-healthcare.pdf; the authenticated all-clear and post-event sequence are supplied by the facility plan in the item","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2097,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_client_advocacy_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.627","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.627.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.627.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,264],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,84],"fullStemEn":"A capable adult enrolled in a clinical study says before the next study-only intervention, “I want to leave the study.” Staff imply that withdrawing could affect ordinary clinical care. Highlight the nursing statements and actions that honor the client's decision.","fullStemZh":"一名具有决策能力、参加临床研究的成年患者在下一项仅用于研究的干预前说：“我想退出这项研究。”工作人员暗示退出可能会影响常规临床护理。请标出尊重患者决定的护理表述和行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the nursing statements and actions that honor the client's decision.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出尊重患者决定的护理表述和行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Staff imply that withdrawing could affect ordinary clinical care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"工作人员暗示退出可能会影响常规临床护理。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q01_s1","en":"The nurse states that participation is voluntary and that withdrawing will not reduce ordinary clinical care.","zh":"护士说明参加研究是自愿的，退出研究不会减少常规临床护理。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s2","en":"The nurse asks the client to complete the next study-only intervention before withdrawal can take effect.","zh":"护士要求患者先完成下一项仅用于研究的干预，退出才会生效。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s3","en":"The nurse stops further research-only interactions and interventions now.","zh":"护士立即停止后续仅用于研究的接触和干预。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s4","en":"The nurse promptly notifies the research team of the client's withdrawal.","zh":"护士立即通知研究团队患者已决定退出。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s5","en":"The nurse follows the study process for documenting the withdrawal while continuing clinically indicated care.","zh":"护士按研究流程记录退出决定，同时继续提供临床上需要的护理。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s6","en":"The nurse warns that the clinical team may reconsider routine treatment if the client leaves the study.","zh":"护士警告患者，如果退出研究，临床团队可能会重新考虑常规治疗。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s7","en":"The nurse continues study follow-up calls until the sponsor approves the withdrawal.","zh":"护士继续进行研究随访电话，直到研究申办方批准退出。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s8","en":"The nurse separates the research decision from the client's ongoing therapeutic relationship with the care team.","zh":"护士将退出研究的决定与患者和医疗团队之间持续的治疗关系区分开来。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q01_s1","q01_s3","q01_s4","q01_s5","q01_s8"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A capable participant may withdraw without penalty or loss of benefits. Once the client withdraws, research-only interactions and interventions stop, the research team is notified, and ordinary clinical care continues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具有决策能力的研究参与者可以退出，不应受到惩罚或失去应有利益。患者退出后，应停止仅用于研究的接触和干预，通知研究团队，并继续常规临床护理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate research participation from treatment. Select actions that stop research-only activity without threatening ordinary care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把研究参与与治疗分开考虑。选择能够停止仅用于研究的活动、同时不威胁常规护理的行动。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR § 46.116(b)(8), voluntary participation and the right to discontinue without penalty or loss of benefits, https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2025-title45-vol1/pdf/CFR-2025-title45-vol1-sec46-116.pdf; HHS Office for Human Research Protections (OHRP), Withdrawal of Subjects from Research Guidance, Guidance A—discontinuing research interactions, interventions, and collection of additional identifiable private information, https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/regulations-and-policy/guidance/guidance-on-withdrawal-of-subject/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2098,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_mx_client_advocacy_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.628","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.628.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.628.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[421,559],"terminalOffsetsZh":[150,190],"fullStemEn":"A stable medical-surgical inpatient uses a trained service dog that alerts to impending seizures. Classify each proposed staff action. Under the ADA, when the dog's task is not obvious, staff may ask only whether the dog is required because of a disability and what work or task it has been trained to perform. Staff may not demand certification or a task demonstration. The handler is responsible for the animal's care. Exclusion is permitted only for a specific allowed reason, such as a dog being out of control and the handler not taking effective action.","fullStemZh":"一名病情稳定的内外科住院患者使用一只经过训练、可预警即将发生癫痫发作的服务犬。请对每项拟议的工作人员行动进行分类。根据 ADA，当服务犬的任务并不明显时，工作人员只能询问该犬是否因残障而需要，以及它受过训练可执行什么工作或任务。工作人员不得要求出示认证或让犬现场演示任务。服务犬的照护由其引导者负责。只有在特定允许理由下，例如服务犬失控且引导者未采取有效纠正措施时，才可将其排除。","terminalSentenceEn":"Exclusion is permitted only for a specific allowed reason, such as a dog being out of control and the handler not taking effective action.","terminalSentenceZh":"只有在特定允许理由下，例如服务犬失控且引导者未采取有效纠正措施时，才可将其排除。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The handler is responsible for the animal's care.","penultimateSentenceZh":"服务犬的照护由其引导者负责。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q02_r1","en":"Allow the service dog to remain with the client in ordinary patient areas.","zh":"允许服务犬在普通患者区域陪伴患者。"},{"id":"q02_r2","en":"If the task is not obvious, ask the two permitted questions described in the stem.","zh":"如果服务犬的任务并不明显，询问题干中说明的两个允许问题。"},{"id":"q02_r3","en":"Require an official service-animal certificate before the dog may stay.","zh":"要求先出示官方服务动物认证，服务犬才可以留下。"},{"id":"q02_r4","en":"Ask the client to have the dog demonstrate its seizure-alert task.","zh":"要求患者让服务犬现场演示癫痫预警任务。"},{"id":"q02_r5","en":"Let the client arrange feeding, toileting, and other routine care for the dog.","zh":"由患者安排服务犬的喂食、排泄和其他日常照护。"},{"id":"q02_r6","en":"If the dog becomes uncontrolled and the handler does not correct it, remove the dog while continuing to offer the client care without the animal present.","zh":"如果服务犬失控且引导者没有纠正，可将犬带离，同时在服务犬不在场的情况下继续为患者提供护理。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q02_c1","en":"Supports client advocacy","zh":"支持患者权益维护"},{"id":"q02_c2","en":"Does not support client advocacy","zh":"不支持患者权益维护"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q02_r1","columnIds":["q02_c1"]},{"rowId":"q02_r2","columnIds":["q02_c1"]},{"rowId":"q02_r3","columnIds":["q02_c2"]},{"rowId":"q02_r4","columnIds":["q02_c2"]},{"rowId":"q02_r5","columnIds":["q02_c1"]},{"rowId":"q02_r6","columnIds":["q02_c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Advocacy means facilitating the trained service dog's access, limiting inquiries to the two ADA-permitted questions when needed, avoiding documentation or demonstration demands, respecting the handler's responsibility for animal care, and using exclusion only for a permitted, individualized reason.","rationaleCorrectZh":"维护患者权益包括允许经过训练的服务犬进入、必要时只询问 ADA 允许的两个问题、不要求证明或演示、尊重引导者负责动物照护，并且只在有允许的个别化理由时排除服务犬。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish access rules from convenience preferences. Certification and demonstrations are not prerequisites, but a specific uncorrected control problem can justify removal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分法律上的进入规则与工作人员的便利偏好。认证和任务演示不是前提，但具体且未被纠正的失控问题可构成排除理由。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Justice, Frequently Asked Questions about Service Animals and the ADA, Q7, Q9, Q14-Q15, Q17, Q25, and Q28, https://www.ada.gov/resources/service-animals-faqs/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2099,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_conflict_resolution_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.629","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.629.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.629.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[273,380],"terminalOffsetsZh":[78,101],"fullStemEn":"During qualified-interpreter-assisted teaching, the nurse and interpreter begin correcting one another in front of the client, and teaching stalls. Facility workflow requires one speaker at a time, short segments, complete interpretation, and direct address to the client. Highlight the responses that resolve the professional disagreement while protecting the teaching encounter.","fullStemZh":"在合格口译员协助的健康教育过程中，护士和口译员开始在患者面前互相纠正，教学因此停滞。机构流程要求一次只由一人说话、使用简短语段、完整口译，并直接对患者说话。请标出既能解决专业分歧又能保护教学过程的回应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the responses that resolve the professional disagreement while protecting the teaching encounter.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出既能解决专业分歧又能保护教学过程的回应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility workflow requires one speaker at a time, short segments, complete interpretation, and direct address to the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构流程要求一次只由一人说话、使用简短语段、完整口译，并直接对患者说话。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q03_s1","en":"Pause the teaching interaction.","zh":"暂停教学互动。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s2","en":"Continue debating the disputed wording so the client can decide who is correct.","zh":"继续在患者面前争论有分歧的措辞，让患者决定谁是正确的。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s3","en":"Move the professional disagreement away from the client.","zh":"把专业分歧移到患者听不到的地方讨论。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s4","en":"State the shared goal: accurate, understandable teaching for the client.","zh":"说明共同目标：为患者提供准确、易理解的教学。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s5","en":"Invite the interpreter to explain the concern and listen to that perspective.","zh":"邀请口译员说明其担忧，并倾听其观点。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s6","en":"Agree to resume using one speaker, short segments, complete interpretation, and direct address to the client.","zh":"同意恢复教学时遵循一次一人说话、短语段、完整口译和直接对患者说话的流程。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s7","en":"Return together and restart the teaching with the nurse speaking directly to the client.","zh":"双方一起返回，并由护士直接对患者说话，重新开始教学。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_s8","en":"Ask the interpreter to summarize only the main points so the session finishes faster.","zh":"要求口译员只概括要点，以便更快结束教学。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q03_s1","q03_s3","q03_s4","q03_s5","q03_s6","q03_s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The team should pause, move the disagreement away from the client, identify the shared goal, hear the interpreter's concern, agree to the stated workflow, and then return jointly. Continuing the argument or using incomplete interpretation undermines communication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"团队应暂停教学，把分歧移到患者听不到的地方，明确共同目标，倾听口译员的担忧，就既定流程达成一致，然后共同返回。继续争论或使用不完整口译都会破坏沟通。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose actions that de-escalate the conflict privately and restore the exact workflow stated in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能够私下缓和冲突并恢复题干所述确切流程的行动。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ TeamSTEPPS 3.0 Two-Day Training Content, Team Leadership module, Facilitating Conflict Resolution and Teamwork (Slide 34), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/team/teach/two-day.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2100,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_bt_conflict_resolution_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.630","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.630.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.630.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[202,302],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,81],"fullStemEn":"Two potassium specimens have hemolyzed. Nursing and laboratory staff blame one another at the bedside while the repeat result needed for a treatment decision is delayed. The client is currently stable. Complete the bow-tie to identify the problem, the two best actions, and the two measures of closure.","fullStemZh":"两份血钾标本均发生溶血。护理人员和检验人员在床旁互相指责，而治疗决策所需的复查结果被延误。患者目前病情稳定。请完成蝴蝶结图，确定问题、两项最佳行动和两项闭环指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie to identify the problem, the two best actions, and the two measures of closure.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图，确定问题、两项最佳行动和两项闭环指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is currently stable.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者目前病情稳定。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Primary problem","zh":"主要问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_c3","en":"Client refusal of repeat specimen collection","zh":"患者拒绝再次采集标本"},{"id":"q04_c1","en":"Unresolved interdepartmental conflict delaying necessary clinical data","zh":"未解决的跨部门冲突正在延误必要的临床数据"},{"id":"q04_c2","en":"Confirmed acute hyperkalemia requiring immediate treatment","zh":"已确诊的急性高钾血症，需要立即治疗"}],"correct":"q04_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_a4","en":"Have both departments collect separate specimens to determine which team is at fault","zh":"让两个部门分别采集标本，以确定哪一方有责任"},{"id":"q04_a1","en":"Hold a brief nursing-laboratory huddle away from the bedside and name the shared goal","zh":"离开床旁进行简短的护理—检验科协调会，并明确共同目标"},{"id":"q04_a3","en":"Wait for both department managers to investigate before recollecting the specimen","zh":"等待两个部门的管理者完成调查后再重新采集标本"},{"id":"q04_a2","en":"Agree on an objective collection, labeling, and transport plan with named roles and a time target","zh":"就客观的采集、标识和运送方案达成一致，并明确责任人和时间目标"}],"correct":["q04_a1","q04_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Measures of closure","zh":"闭环指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_p1","en":"Repeat potassium result is posted and communicated to the treatment team","zh":"复查血钾结果已发布并传达给治疗团队"},{"id":"q04_p2","en":"The agreed nursing-laboratory communication loop is completed with a named receiver","zh":"约定的护理—检验科沟通闭环已完成，并有明确的接收者"},{"id":"q04_p4","en":"The number of complaint emails sent about the incident","zh":"围绕该事件发送的投诉邮件数量"},{"id":"q04_p3","en":"One department accepts responsibility for both hemolyzed specimens","zh":"其中一个部门承担两份溶血标本的责任"}],"correct":["q04_p1","q04_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate management issue is unresolved interdepartmental conflict delaying a needed repeat result. A brief huddle and an objective shared plan restore coordinated work. Closure requires both the clinical result and completion of the agreed communication loop.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前的管理问题是未解决的跨部门冲突延误了所需的复查结果。简短协调会和客观的共同方案可恢复协作。闭环既需要得到临床结果，也需要完成约定的沟通流程。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Because the client is stable, prioritize rapid team alignment and objective workflow repair rather than treating an unverified potassium value or assigning blame.","testTakingStrategyZh":"由于患者病情稳定，应优先快速协调团队并客观修复流程，而不是治疗未经证实的血钾异常或追究责任。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ TeamSTEPPS 3.0 Two-Day Training Content, Team Leadership module, Monitoring and Modifying the Plan—Huddle (Slide 31) and Facilitating Conflict Resolution and Teamwork (Slide 34), https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/team/teach/two-day.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2101,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_dc_confidentiality_hipaa_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.631","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.631.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.631.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,56],"fullStemEn":"An alert client was informed about the hospital directory and explicitly opted out. A caller asks whether the client is admitted and requests the room number.","fullStemZh":"一名神志清醒的患者已被告知医院名录的相关规定，并明确选择不加入名录。一名来电者询问该患者是否住院，并索要房间号。","terminalSentenceEn":"A caller asks whether the client is admitted and requests the room number.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名来电者询问该患者是否住院，并索要房间号。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An alert client was informed about the hospital directory and explicitly opted out.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名神志清醒的患者已被告知医院名录的相关规定，并明确选择不加入名录。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Staff should {{q05_d1}} and should {{q05_d2}}.","zh":"工作人员应当{{q05_d1}}，并且应当{{q05_d2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q05_d1","options":[{"id":"q05_d1_o2","en":"confirm admission but withhold the room number","zh":"确认患者已住院，但不提供房间号"},{"id":"q05_d1_o1","en":"not confirm the client's presence or location","zh":"不确认患者是否在院或其所在位置"},{"id":"q05_d1_o3","en":"provide the room number after asking the caller's relationship","zh":"询问来电者与患者的关系后提供房间号"}],"correct":"q05_d1_o1"},{"id":"q05_d2","options":[{"id":"q05_d2_o2","en":"use the usual directory response because the caller knows the client's name","zh":"因为来电者知道患者姓名，所以按通常名录流程回答"},{"id":"q05_d2_o1","en":"follow the client's directory restriction","zh":"遵守患者的名录限制"},{"id":"q05_d2_o3","en":"transfer the caller to the nursing unit for confirmation","zh":"把来电转接到护理单元进行确认"}],"correct":"q05_d2_o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A client who opts out of the facility directory has restricted disclosure of directory information. Staff must not confirm that the client is present or disclose the room location and must follow the documented restriction.","rationaleCorrectZh":"选择退出医院名录的患者已限制名录信息披露。工作人员不得确认患者是否在院，也不得透露房间位置，并必须遵守已记录的限制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The decisive cue is the explicit directory opt-out. Do not use the default directory response after the client has restricted it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"决定性线索是患者明确退出医院名录。患者已作出限制后，不能再使用默认名录答复。","sourceMetadata":"HHS Office for Civil Rights, HIPAA FAQ 483, facility directory opt-out under 45 CFR 164.510(a), https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/483/does-hipaa-permit-hospitals-to-inform-visitors-about-a-patients-location/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2102,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_confidentiality_hipaa_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.632","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.632.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.632.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[202,279],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,73],"fullStemEn":"A nursing-station whiteboard is directly visible from a public elevator lobby. Facility policy permits only client initials and operational bed status on a whiteboard that is shielded from public view. Highlight the entries and placement facts that violate the stated safeguards.","fullStemZh":"护理站白板可从公共电梯大厅直接看到。机构政策只允许在不被公众看到的白板上记录患者姓名首字母和床位运行状态。请标出违反上述保护措施的内容和放置事实。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entries and placement facts that violate the stated safeguards.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出违反上述保护措施的内容和放置事实。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy permits only client initials and operational bed status on a whiteboard that is shielded from public view.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策只允许在不被公众看到的白板上记录患者姓名首字母和床位运行状态。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q06_s1","en":"The whiteboard faces the public elevator lobby and can be read from there.","zh":"白板朝向公共电梯大厅，从那里可以读到内容。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s2","en":"It lists each client's full name.","zh":"白板列出每位患者的完整姓名。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s3","en":"It lists room numbers next to the names.","zh":"白板在姓名旁列出房间号。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s4","en":"It lists specific diagnoses such as “pancreatic cancer” and “HIV infection.”","zh":"白板列出“胰腺癌”和“HIV 感染”等具体诊断。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s5","en":"A shielded staff-only board uses client initials.","zh":"一块仅供工作人员查看、已遮挡公众视线的白板使用患者姓名首字母。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s6","en":"The shielded staff-only board shows operational status such as “bed ready.”","zh":"仅供工作人员查看、已遮挡的白板显示“床位已准备”等运行状态。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q06_s1","q06_s2","q06_s3","q06_s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA does not make every nursing-station whiteboard inherently prohibited, but reasonable safeguards are required. Under the stated facility policy, public visibility and the use of full names, room numbers, and diagnoses violate the allowed, shielded initials-and-bed-status format.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA 并非一概禁止护理站白板，但必须采取合理保护措施。根据题干中的机构政策，公众可见，以及使用完整姓名、房间号和具体诊断，都违反了仅允许在遮挡白板上使用姓名首字母和床位状态的规定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the facility's stated safeguard rather than assuming all whiteboards are forbidden. Compare each fact with both the allowed content and the required placement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干给出的机构保护措施，不要假设所有白板都被禁止。逐项比较允许的内容和要求的放置位置。","sourceMetadata":"HHS Office for Civil Rights, HIPAA FAQ 200, reasonable safeguards for nursing-station whiteboards and public visibility, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/200/what-safeguards-are-needed-to-continue-practices/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2103,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_bt_discharge_handoff_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.633","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.633.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.633.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[353,374],"terminalOffsetsZh":[104,112],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving maintenance hemodialysis is relocating and is due for the next treatment within 48 hours. A possible receiving center has been named, but acceptance and chair time are unconfirmed. The dialysis prescription, last treatment record, vascular-access information, recent laboratory results, and medication list have not been transmitted. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名接受维持性血液透析的患者即将搬迁，并需在 48 小时内接受下一次治疗。虽然已提出一个可能接收的透析中心，但尚未确认接收资格和透析时段。透析处方、上次治疗记录、血管通路信息、近期检验结果和用药清单均未传送。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The dialysis prescription, last treatment record, vascular-access information, recent laboratory results, and medication list have not been transmitted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"透析处方、上次治疗记录、血管通路信息、近期检验结果和用药清单均未传送。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Transition problem","zh":"转衔问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_c1","en":"Unsafe dialysis transition with no confirmed receiving appointment or clinical handoff","zh":"透析转衔不安全：未确认接收预约，也未完成临床交接"},{"id":"q07_c2","en":"Routine relocation with a fully established dialysis schedule","zh":"常规搬迁，透析安排已完全落实"},{"id":"q07_c3","en":"Client refusal of the next dialysis treatment","zh":"患者拒绝下一次透析治疗"}],"correct":"q07_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_a3","en":"Discharge the client with the center's phone number and ask the client to secure a chair after moving","zh":"让患者带着透析中心电话号码出院，并要求其搬家后自行安排透析时段"},{"id":"q07_a4","en":"Transmit only the medication list because the receiving center can reconstruct the dialysis prescription later","zh":"只发送用药清单，因为接收中心之后可以重新制定透析处方"},{"id":"q07_a1","en":"Contact the receiving center and confirm acceptance with a specific treatment date and chair time","zh":"联系接收中心，确认其接收患者，并确定具体治疗日期和透析时段"},{"id":"q07_a2","en":"Send the dialysis prescription, last treatment record, access information, recent laboratory results, and medication list to the responsible receiving team","zh":"向接收团队发送透析处方、上次治疗记录、通路信息、近期检验结果和用药清单"}],"correct":["q07_a1","q07_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Evidence of transition closure","zh":"转衔闭环证据"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_p4","en":"The client has purchased a home scale","zh":"患者已购买家用体重秤"},{"id":"q07_p2","en":"The receiving team confirms receipt of the clinical handoff and readiness to provide the next treatment","zh":"接收团队确认已收到临床交接资料，并已准备好提供下一次治疗"},{"id":"q07_p3","en":"The client has a general transportation brochure","zh":"患者拿到一份一般交通信息手册"},{"id":"q07_p1","en":"Receiving-center acceptance, date, and chair time are documented and understood by the client","zh":"接收中心的接收确认、日期和透析时段已记录，患者也已理解"}],"correct":["q07_p1","q07_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has an unsafe transition because the next dialysis treatment and the clinical handoff are not secured. The nurse coordinates confirmed acceptance and chair time and transmits the information needed for safe follow-up. Closure requires documented appointment details and confirmation that the receiving team has the handoff and can provide treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者的转衔不安全，因为下一次透析治疗和临床交接尚未落实。护士应协调确认接收和透析时段，并传送安全后续治疗所需的信息。闭环需要记录预约细节，并确认接收团队已收到交接资料且能够提供治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a time-sensitive transition, look for confirmed acceptance, a specific appointment, transmission of essential records, and receipt confirmation—not merely a referral name.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于时间敏感的转衔，应寻找已确认的接收、具体预约、必要资料传送和接收确认，而不仅是一个转诊机构名称。","sourceMetadata":"42 CFR § 494.170(d), transfer of requested dialysis medical-record information to the receiving facility, https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-G/part-494/subpart-E/section-494.170; National Kidney Foundation, Traveling While on Dialysis—arranging destination appointments and transmitting treatment dates, prescription, recent treatment records, access information, laboratory results, and medication information, https://www.kidney.org/news-stories/traveling-while-dialysis-start-here","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2104,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_discharge_handoff_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.634","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.634.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.634.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[200,245],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,59],"fullStemEn":"A school-age child with epilepsy is returning to school after receiving a new rescue-medication prescription. Highlight the discharge-planning gaps that must be addressed before the return to school. Do not apply state-specific delegation rules.","fullStemZh":"一名患有癫痫的学龄儿童在获得新的急救药物处方后准备返校。请标出返校前必须解决的出院计划缺口。不要套用特定州的授权规则。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not apply state-specific delegation rules.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要套用特定州的授权规则。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the discharge-planning gaps that must be addressed before the return to school.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请标出返校前必须解决的出院计划缺口。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q08_s1","en":"No individualized seizure action plan with the required authorization has been sent to the school.","zh":"尚未向学校发送附有所需授权的个体化癫痫发作行动计划。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s2","en":"Rescue-medication instructions and an available supply have not been coordinated with the school nurse.","zh":"尚未与校护士协调急救药物说明和可用药物供应。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s3","en":"There is no confirmation that responsible school staff know the child's response plan.","zh":"尚未确认负责的学校工作人员了解该儿童的应对计划。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s4","en":"The family has an updated list of the child's routine medications.","zh":"家属持有该儿童最新的常规用药清单。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s5","en":"A neurology follow-up visit is scheduled.","zh":"已安排神经科复诊。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s6","en":"The child wears a medical-identification bracelet.","zh":"该儿童佩戴医疗识别手环。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q08_s1","q08_s2","q08_s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe school return requires an individualized seizure action plan, coordinated rescue-medication instructions and supply, and confirmation that responsible staff understand the response plan. The other findings are useful supports but do not close these school-specific handoff gaps.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全返校需要个体化癫痫发作行动计划、已协调的急救药物说明和供应，以及确认负责的工作人员理解应对计划。其他发现可能有帮助，但不能弥补这些学校特定的交接缺口。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on whether the school can carry out the child's individualized emergency response on day one: plan, medication, and trained or informed responsible staff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注学校在返校第一天能否执行该儿童的个体化紧急应对：行动计划、药物以及已接受培训或已知情的负责人员。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Guidance for Schools—Epilepsy, Seizure Action Plans and staff training/rescue-medicine guidance, https://www.cdc.gov/epilepsy/php/guidance-for-schools/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2105,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_dc_psychotropic_medications_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.635","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.635.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.635.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,100],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,42],"fullStemEn":"A client with a documented prior diagnosis of bulimia nervosa receives a new order for bupropion XL.","fullStemZh":"一名病历中记录有既往神经性贪食症诊断的患者收到新的 bupropion XL 医嘱。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client with a documented prior diagnosis of bulimia nervosa receives a new order for bupropion XL.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名病历中记录有既往神经性贪食症诊断的患者收到新的 bupropion XL 医嘱。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should {{q09_d1}} because a current or prior diagnosis of bulimia nervosa is {{q09_d2}} associated with increased seizure risk.","zh":"护士应当{{q09_d1}}，因为当前或既往神经性贪食症诊断是与癫痫发作风险增加相关的{{q09_d2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q09_d1","options":[{"id":"q09_d1_o2","en":"administer the dose with food","zh":"随餐给予该剂量"},{"id":"q09_d1_o1","en":"withhold the dose and clarify the order","zh":"暂不给药并澄清医嘱"},{"id":"q09_d1_o3","en":"administer one-half of the ordered XL tablet","zh":"给予医嘱 XL 片剂的一半"}],"correct":"q09_d1_o1"},{"id":"q09_d2","options":[{"id":"q09_d2_o1","en":"a labeled contraindication","zh":"药品说明书列明的禁忌证"},{"id":"q09_d2_o3","en":"an indication for dose escalation","zh":"增加剂量的适应证"},{"id":"q09_d2_o2","en":"a minor administration precaution","zh":"轻微的给药注意事项"}],"correct":"q09_d2_o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bupropion XL is contraindicated in clients with a current or prior diagnosis of bulimia nervosa because a higher incidence of seizures has been observed. The nurse should withhold the new dose and clarify the order rather than modifying or administering it.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Bupropion XL 禁用于当前或既往诊断为神经性贪食症的患者，因为此类患者使用该药时观察到更高的癫痫发作发生率。护士应暂不给予新医嘱剂量并澄清医嘱，而不是自行修改或给药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat “current or prior” as load-bearing wording. A resolved eating-disorder history still meets the labeled contraindication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把“当前或既往”视为关键措辞。即使进食障碍已缓解，既往诊断仍符合说明书禁忌证。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Bupropion Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets (XL) prescribing information, Contraindications (4) and Warnings and Precautions—Seizure Risk (5.3), https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/getFile.cfm?setid=080853c0-fcab-4645-9ddc-4946e895ac5f&type=pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2106,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_psychotropic_medications_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.636","itemType":"highlight","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.636.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.636.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,182],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,71],"fullStemEn":"A client taking divalproex for bipolar disorder reports several new findings. Highlight the labeled symptom cues that require prompt evaluation for valproate-associated pancreatitis.","fullStemZh":"一名因双相情感障碍服用 divalproex 的患者报告了几项新情况。请标出需要及时评估 valproate 相关胰腺炎的药品说明书症状线索。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the labeled symptom cues that require prompt evaluation for valproate-associated pancreatitis.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要及时评估 valproate 相关胰腺炎的药品说明书症状线索。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client taking divalproex for bipolar disorder reports several new findings.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名因双相情感障碍服用 divalproex 的患者报告了几项新情况。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q10_s1","en":"Persistent severe pain in the upper abdomen","zh":"持续性严重上腹部疼痛","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s2","en":"New nausea with repeated vomiting","zh":"新出现的恶心并反复呕吐","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s3","en":"New loss of appetite","zh":"新出现的食欲减退","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s4","en":"A mild hand tremor that has been unchanged for 6 months","zh":"持续 6 个月且没有变化的轻度手震颤","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s5","en":"Blood pressure 124/76 mm Hg","zh":"血压 124/76 mm Hg","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s6","en":"Oral temperature 98.6 °F (37.0 °C)","zh":"口温 98.6 °F (37.0 °C)","selectable":true}],"correct":["q10_s1","q10_s2","q10_s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The divalproex label identifies abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and anorexia as possible pancreatitis symptoms requiring prompt medical evaluation. The stable tremor and normal vital signs are not the labeled symptom cluster in this item.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Divalproex 药品说明书指出，腹痛、恶心、呕吐和食欲减退可能是胰腺炎症状，需要及时医学评估。本题中的稳定震颤和正常生命体征不属于该说明书症状组合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for the new symptom cluster named in the drug warning rather than requiring a diagnostic enzyme result or selecting unrelated stable findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找药品警示中列出的新症状组合，不要等待诊断性酶结果，也不要选择无关的稳定发现。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Divalproex Sodium Extended-Release Tablets prescribing information, Warnings and Precautions 5.5 Pancreatitis, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=b367d81d-4eca-4e28-b490-34be4c003561","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2107,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_mx_parenteral_nutrition_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.637","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.637.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.637.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[202,365],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,107],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is verifying a prescribed bag of Nutrilipid 20% before administration with parenteral nutrition. The facility requires any order-label mismatch to be held and clarified before administration. Classify each finding as acceptable to continue verification or as requiring the product to be held and not administered; physically defective product is replaced.","fullStemZh":"护士正在核对一袋医嘱的 Nutrilipid 20%，准备与肠外营养一起给药。机构规定，任何医嘱与标签不一致都必须先暂缓并澄清后才能给药。请把每项发现分类为可继续核对，或必须暂缓且不得给药；有物理缺陷的产品应更换。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each finding as acceptable to continue verification or as requiring the product to be held and not administered; physically defective product is replaced.","terminalSentenceZh":"请把每项发现分类为可继续核对，或必须暂缓且不得给药；有物理缺陷的产品应更换。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility requires any order-label mismatch to be held and clarified before administration.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构规定，任何医嘱与标签不一致都必须先暂缓并澄清后才能给药。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q11_r1","en":"The emulsion is homogeneous, white, and milky; the container and seals are intact.","zh":"乳剂均匀、白色、呈乳状；容器和封口完整。"},{"id":"q11_r2","en":"A clear oily layer and white layer are separating.","zh":"可见透明油层与白色乳剂层分离。"},{"id":"q11_r3","en":"Visible particles are suspended in the bag.","zh":"袋内可见悬浮颗粒。"},{"id":"q11_r4","en":"The emulsion has developed gray-brown discoloration.","zh":"乳剂出现灰褐色变色。"},{"id":"q11_r5","en":"The primary bag is leaking near a damaged seal.","zh":"主袋在破损封口附近漏液。"},{"id":"q11_r6","en":"The pharmacy label matches the client, Nutrilipid 20% order, route, and administration time.","zh":"药房标签与患者、Nutrilipid 20% 医嘱、给药途径和给药时间均一致。"},{"id":"q11_r7","en":"The pharmacy label lists a different client than the prescription.","zh":"药房标签所列患者与处方中的患者不一致。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q11_c1","en":"Acceptable to continue verification","zh":"可继续核对"},{"id":"q11_c2","en":"Hold; do not administer","zh":"暂缓；不得给药"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q11_r1","columnIds":["q11_c1"]},{"rowId":"q11_r2","columnIds":["q11_c2"]},{"rowId":"q11_r3","columnIds":["q11_c2"]},{"rowId":"q11_r4","columnIds":["q11_c2"]},{"rowId":"q11_r5","columnIds":["q11_c2"]},{"rowId":"q11_r6","columnIds":["q11_c1"]},{"rowId":"q11_r7","columnIds":["q11_c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nutrilipid 20% should appear as a homogeneous white, milky emulsion in an intact container. Separation, particles, discoloration, or container damage require the product to be discarded or replaced. A label mismatch requires holding and clarification under the stated facility rule.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Nutrilipid 20% 应为均匀、白色、乳状的乳剂，且容器完整。分层、颗粒、变色或容器损坏都需要弃用或更换产品。根据题干所述机构规则，标签不一致必须暂缓并澄清。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected emulsion appearance from defect cues, then apply the stem's explicit hold-and-clarify rule to label mismatches.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分乳剂的预期外观与缺陷线索，然后把题干明确的暂缓并澄清规则用于标签不一致。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Nutrilipid 20% prescribing information, Dosage and Administration 2.2, Preparation Instructions—Steps 1 and 3 (container integrity, homogeneous white/milky appearance, separation, particles, discoloration), https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=193290b1-a0a1-4054-a22a-de5c9e7a8b73","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The facility requires any order-label mismatch to be held and clarified before administration.","controlSentenceZh":"机构规定，任何医嘱与标签不一致都必须先暂缓并澄清后才能给药。"}
{"queueIndex":2108,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_bt_cardiovascular_endocrine_medications_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.638","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.638.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.638.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[210,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,97],"fullStemEn":"Sacubitril/valsartan is due now for a client with heart failure. The medication record shows the last lisinopril dose was given 12 hours ago. The client has no current angioedema and is hemodynamically stable. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名心力衰竭患者现在应使用 sacubitril/valsartan。用药记录显示最后一次 lisinopril 给药是在 12 小时前。患者目前没有血管性水肿，血流动力学稳定。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has no current angioedema and is hemodynamically stable.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者目前没有血管性水肿，血流动力学稳定。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Medication-safety problem","zh":"用药安全问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q12_c1","en":"Unsafe ACE-inhibitor-to-ARNI transition before the required washout is complete","zh":"ACE 抑制剂转换为 ARNI 的过程不安全：规定的洗脱期尚未完成"},{"id":"q12_c3","en":"An isolated ACE-inhibitor cough requiring immediate ARNI administration","zh":"单纯 ACE 抑制剂咳嗽，需要立即给予 ARNI"},{"id":"q12_c2","en":"Expected ARNI initiation after a complete ACE-inhibitor washout","zh":"ACE 抑制剂洗脱期完成后按预期开始 ARNI"}],"correct":"q12_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q12_a4","en":"Administer the full dose now and monitor only for cough","zh":"现在给予全剂量，并只监测咳嗽"},{"id":"q12_a2","en":"Establish at least a 36-hour interval from the last lisinopril dose to the first sacubitril/valsartan dose","zh":"确保从最后一次 lisinopril 到第一次 sacubitril/valsartan 至少间隔 36 小时"},{"id":"q12_a3","en":"Give one-half of the sacubitril/valsartan dose now to shorten the washout","zh":"现在给予一半 sacubitril/valsartan 剂量，以缩短洗脱期"},{"id":"q12_a1","en":"Hold the sacubitril/valsartan dose and clarify the transition order","zh":"暂缓 sacubitril/valsartan，并澄清转换医嘱"}],"correct":["q12_a1","q12_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor after safe initiation","zh":"安全开始用药后应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q12_p4","en":"Serum lipase after every dose","zh":"每次给药后检测血清脂肪酶"},{"id":"q12_p3","en":"Severity of a dry cough as the only safety endpoint","zh":"仅把干咳严重程度作为安全终点"},{"id":"q12_p1","en":"Facial, lip, tongue, or airway swelling consistent with angioedema","zh":"符合血管性水肿的面部、嘴唇、舌头或气道肿胀"},{"id":"q12_p2","en":"Blood pressure and clinical tolerance, including dizziness or symptomatic hypotension","zh":"血压和临床耐受性，包括头晕或症状性低血压"}],"correct":["q12_p1","q12_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sacubitril/valsartan must not be administered within 36 hours of an ACE inhibitor. At 12 hours, the nurse holds and clarifies the dose and ensures the full washout. After safe initiation, angioedema and blood-pressure tolerance are key monitoring concerns.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Sacubitril/valsartan 不得在使用 ACE 抑制剂后的 36 小时内给药。仅间隔 12 小时时，护士应暂缓并澄清医嘱，确保完成整个洗脱期。安全开始用药后，应重点监测血管性水肿和血压耐受性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Calculate elapsed time before interpreting symptoms. The 12-hour interval directly conflicts with the labeled 36-hour washout.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先计算已过去的时间，再考虑症状。12 小时间隔与说明书规定的 36 小时洗脱期直接冲突。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, ENTRESTO (sacubitril/valsartan) prescribing information, Dosage and Administration 2.1, Contraindications 4, Warnings and Precautions 5.2 Angioedema and 5.3 Hypotension, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=14bfc60a-9ddf-cac7-e063-6294a90a597b","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2109,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_disaster_emergency_preparedness_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.639","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.639.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.639.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[333,381],"terminalOffsetsZh":[95,107],"fullStemEn":"After a mass-casualty incident, several unidentified clients arrive while families and media crowd the entrance. The activated hospital plan requires temporary unique identifiers, a continuously updated patient-tracking list, a designated family-reunification channel, and media release only through the public-information function. Highlight the actions consistent with this plan.","fullStemZh":"大规模伤亡事件后，多名身份不明的患者到达医院，家属和媒体挤在入口处。已启动的医院计划要求使用临时唯一标识、持续更新患者追踪清单、设立指定的家属团聚渠道，并且只能通过公共信息职能发布媒体信息。请标出符合该计划的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions consistent with this plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合该计划的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The activated hospital plan requires temporary unique identifiers, a continuously updated patient-tracking list, a designated family-reunification channel, and media release only through the public-information function.","penultimateSentenceZh":"已启动的医院计划要求使用临时唯一标识、持续更新患者追踪清单、设立指定的家属团聚渠道，并且只能通过公共信息职能发布媒体信息。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q13_s1","en":"Assign each unidentified client a separate temporary unique identifier.","zh":"为每名身份不明的患者分别分配一个临时唯一标识。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s2","en":"Maintain one continuously updated patient-tracking list as clients move through the hospital.","zh":"患者在院内转移时，持续更新同一份患者追踪清单。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s3","en":"Route family inquiries to the designated reunification channel.","zh":"将家属查询引导至指定的团聚渠道。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s4","en":"Refer media requests to the hospital's public-information function.","zh":"把媒体请求转交医院的公共信息职能处理。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s5","en":"Use the same “Unknown Client” identifier for all unidentified arrivals until names are learned.","zh":"在查明姓名前，对所有身份不明的到院者使用同一个“未知患者”标识。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s6","en":"Post unidentified-client photographs on the hospital's public social-media account to speed identification.","zh":"在医院公开社交媒体账号上发布身份不明患者的照片，以加快身份确认。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s7","en":"Let bedside staff give reporters unverified casualty details to reduce crowding.","zh":"让床旁工作人员向记者提供未经核实的伤亡信息，以减少拥挤。","selectable":true},{"id":"q13_s8","en":"Allow families to search treatment areas independently rather than using the reunification channel.","zh":"允许家属自行进入治疗区域寻找患者，而不是使用团聚渠道。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q13_s1","q13_s2","q13_s3","q13_s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The activated plan creates controlled identity, tracking, family, and media pathways. Unique temporary identifiers and a current tracking list reduce misidentification; family inquiries and public information are routed through their designated functions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"已启动的计划建立了受控的身份、追踪、家属和媒体信息通道。临时唯一标识和最新追踪清单可减少身份错误；家属查询和公共信息分别通过指定职能处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the activated plan as the governing protocol. Select only actions that preserve unique identity and route information through the named tracking, family, and media functions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把已启动的计划视为应遵循的规程。只选择能够保持唯一身份，并通过指定追踪、家属和媒体职能传递信息的行动。","sourceMetadata":"ASPR TRACIE, Hospital Mass Casualty Incident Response Plan Considerations, Sections 4 Registration and Documentation, 9 Family Support, and 10 Information Management, https://files.asprtracie.hhs.gov/documents/aspr-tracie-mci-response-plan-considerations.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The activated hospital plan requires temporary unique identifiers, a continuously updated patient-tracking list, a designated family-reunification channel, and media release only through the public-information function.","controlSentenceZh":"已启动的医院计划要求使用临时唯一标识、持续更新患者追踪清单、设立指定的家属团聚渠道，并且只能通过公共信息职能发布媒体信息。"}
{"queueIndex":2110,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_bt_standard_precautions_hygiene_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.640","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.640.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.640.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[251,272],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,75],"fullStemEn":"A professional-use blood glucose meter was shared across four clients without cleaning and disinfection between uses. The facility's exposure-response process requires infection-prevention notification and tracing of every potentially exposed client. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一台专业用途血糖仪在四名患者之间共用，但每次使用后均未清洁和消毒。机构的暴露应对流程要求通知感染预防部门，并追踪每一名可能暴露的患者。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility's exposure-response process requires infection-prevention notification and tracing of every potentially exposed client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构的暴露应对流程要求通知感染预防部门，并追踪每一名可能暴露的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Safety problem","zh":"安全问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q14_c3","en":"A medication-dosing error affecting only the fourth client","zh":"只影响第四名患者的用药剂量错误"},{"id":"q14_c1","en":"Potential bloodborne cross-transmission and client exposure from an improperly shared meter","zh":"血糖仪共用不当导致潜在血源性交叉传播和患者暴露"},{"id":"q14_c2","en":"Expected use of a professional meter with no exposure concern","zh":"专业血糖仪的正常使用，不存在暴露问题"}],"correct":"q14_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q14_a3","en":"Wipe the meter once and return it immediately to routine shared use","zh":"把血糖仪擦拭一次后立即恢复常规共用"},{"id":"q14_a2","en":"Notify infection prevention and initiate the facility's trace of all four potentially exposed clients","zh":"通知感染预防部门，并按机构流程追踪全部四名可能暴露的患者"},{"id":"q14_a4","en":"Begin empiric post-exposure drug prophylaxis for all four clients before risk evaluation","zh":"在风险评估前立即给全部四名患者开始经验性暴露后药物预防"},{"id":"q14_a1","en":"Stop use and secure the meter so it cannot be used again pending evaluation","zh":"停止使用并封存血糖仪，在评估完成前防止再次使用"}],"correct":["q14_a1","q14_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Measures of response completion","zh":"应对完成指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q14_p1","en":"Exposure evaluation and follow-up are completed and documented for every traced client","zh":"每名被追踪患者的暴露评估和后续处理均已完成并记录"},{"id":"q14_p4","en":"The staff member who used the meter most often is identified","zh":"已找出使用该血糖仪次数最多的工作人员"},{"id":"q14_p3","en":"All four clients have glucose values within the reference range","zh":"四名患者的血糖值都在参考范围内"},{"id":"q14_p2","en":"Corrective action and audit confirm a meter workflow that prevents reuse without cleaning and disinfection","zh":"纠正措施和审核确认新流程可防止血糖仪未经清洁消毒就再次使用"}],"correct":["q14_p1","q14_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A shared professional meter must be cleaned and disinfected after every use. Failure across four clients creates a potential bloodborne exposure event. The device is stopped and secured, infection prevention initiates tracing, and closure requires both exposed-client evaluation and verified correction of the workflow.","rationaleCorrectZh":"共用的专业血糖仪必须在每次使用后清洁和消毒。连续在四名患者之间未消毒使用，构成潜在血源性暴露事件。应停止并封存设备，由感染预防部门启动追踪；闭环需要完成暴露患者评估，并确认工作流程已纠正。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat the device as a possible blood-contaminated source. The correct response contains both immediate containment and a system-level exposed-client trace.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把该设备视为可能被血液污染的来源。正确应对必须同时包括立即控制设备和系统层面的暴露患者追踪。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Considerations for Blood Glucose Monitoring and Insulin Administration, Blood Glucose Meters section—shared meters must be cleaned and disinfected after every use, https://www.cdc.gov/injection-safety/hcp/infection-control/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2111,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_mx_standard_precautions_hygiene_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.641","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.641.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.641.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[244,265],"terminalOffsetsZh":[76,87],"fullStemEn":"A blood-containing specimen tube breaks on the floor. The cleanup plan requires suitable PPE, mechanical collection of glass, sharps disposal, cleaning before disinfection, use of the disinfectant for its stated contact time, and hand hygiene. Classify each action.","fullStemZh":"一支含血液的标本管在地面破裂。清理计划要求使用合适的 PPE、用机械方法收集玻璃、放入锐器容器、先清洁后消毒、按消毒剂规定的接触时间使用，并进行手卫生。请对每项行动进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项行动进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The cleanup plan requires suitable PPE, mechanical collection of glass, sharps disposal, cleaning before disinfection, use of the disinfectant for its stated contact time, and hand hygiene.","penultimateSentenceZh":"清理计划要求使用合适的 PPE、用机械方法收集玻璃、放入锐器容器、先清洁后消毒、按消毒剂规定的接触时间使用，并进行手卫生。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q15_r1","en":"Put on suitable gloves and any additional PPE needed for splash risk.","zh":"戴上合适的手套，并根据飞溅风险使用其他所需 PPE。"},{"id":"q15_r2","en":"Pick up the glass fragments with bare hands to clear the walkway quickly.","zh":"为了快速清理通道，徒手捡起玻璃碎片。"},{"id":"q15_r3","en":"Use forceps, tongs, or a brush and dustpan to collect the contaminated glass.","zh":"使用镊子、夹钳或刷子和簸箕收集受污染玻璃。"},{"id":"q15_r4","en":"Place the contaminated glass fragments in an appropriate sharps container.","zh":"将受污染的玻璃碎片放入合适的锐器容器。"},{"id":"q15_r5","en":"Remove visible soil, then apply the approved disinfectant and keep the surface wet for the product's stated contact time.","zh":"先去除可见污物，再使用批准的消毒剂，并让表面在产品规定的接触时间内保持湿润。"},{"id":"q15_r6","en":"Perform hand hygiene after removing PPE.","zh":"脱去 PPE 后进行手卫生。"},{"id":"q15_r7","en":"Compress a waste bag by hand to make room for more contaminated material.","zh":"用手压实废物袋，以便装入更多受污染物品。"},{"id":"q15_r8","en":"Use a vacuum cleaner to collect the contaminated glass fragments.","zh":"使用吸尘器收集受污染的玻璃碎片。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q15_c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"},{"id":"q15_c2","en":"Unsafe","zh":"不安全"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q15_r1","columnIds":["q15_c1"]},{"rowId":"q15_r2","columnIds":["q15_c2"]},{"rowId":"q15_r3","columnIds":["q15_c1"]},{"rowId":"q15_r4","columnIds":["q15_c1"]},{"rowId":"q15_r5","columnIds":["q15_c1"]},{"rowId":"q15_r6","columnIds":["q15_c1"]},{"rowId":"q15_r7","columnIds":["q15_c2"]},{"rowId":"q15_r8","columnIds":["q15_c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Blood-contaminated broken glass is handled with PPE and mechanical tools, never bare hands or a vacuum. Fragments go into a sharps container. The surface is cleaned and then disinfected for the labeled contact time, followed by hand hygiene. Waste bags are not compressed by hand because concealed sharps can cause injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"含血液的破碎玻璃应使用 PPE 和机械工具处理，不能徒手或使用吸尘器。碎片应放入锐器容器。地面先清洁，再按标签规定接触时间消毒，最后进行手卫生。不能用手压实废物袋，因为隐藏锐器可能造成损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For contaminated glass, choose methods that keep hands away from sharps and preserve the clean-then-disinfect sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理受污染玻璃时，选择让双手远离锐器的方法，并保持先清洁后消毒的顺序。","sourceMetadata":"OSHA, Enforcement Procedures for the Occupational Exposure to Bloodborne Pathogens, CPL 2-2.44D, contaminated broken glass—mechanical handling, sharps-container disposal, and no vacuum, https://www.osha.gov/enforcement/directives/cpl-2-244d; CDC, Core Infection Prevention and Control Practices, Environmental Cleaning and Disinfection—follow manufacturer instructions including contact time, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/core-practices/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The cleanup plan requires suitable PPE, mechanical collection of glass, sharps disposal, cleaning before disinfection, use of the disinfectant for its stated contact time, and hand hygiene.","controlSentenceZh":"清理计划要求使用合适的 PPE、用机械方法收集玻璃、放入锐器容器、先清洁后消毒、按消毒剂规定的接触时间使用，并进行手卫生。"}
{"queueIndex":2112,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_dc_abg_acid_base_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.642","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.642.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.642.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,231],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,164],"fullStemEn":"A client with a high-output ileostomy has pH 7.29, PaCO2 29 mm Hg, HCO3 14 mEq/L, sodium 138 mEq/L, and chloride 112 mEq/L. Use: anion gap = Na − (Cl + HCO3); normal anion gap = 8–12 mEq/L; expected PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg.","fullStemZh":"一名高输出回肠造口患者的结果为：pH 7.29、PaCO2 29 mm Hg、HCO3 14 mEq/L、钠 138 mEq/L、氯 112 mEq/L。使用以下公式：阴离子间隙 = Na −（Cl + HCO3）；正常阴离子间隙 = 8–12 mEq/L；预期 PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use: anion gap = Na − (Cl + HCO3); normal anion gap = 8–12 mEq/L; expected PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg.","terminalSentenceZh":"使用以下公式：阴离子间隙 = Na −（Cl + HCO3）；正常阴离子间隙 = 8–12 mEq/L；预期 PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a high-output ileostomy has pH 7.29, PaCO2 29 mm Hg, HCO3 14 mEq/L, sodium 138 mEq/L, and chloride 112 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名高输出回肠造口患者的结果为：pH 7.29、PaCO2 29 mm Hg、HCO3 14 mEq/L、钠 138 mEq/L、氯 112 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"These results show {{q16_d1}} caused by {{q16_d2}}, with {{q16_d3}}.","zh":"这些结果显示{{q16_d1}}，由{{q16_d2}}引起，并伴有{{q16_d3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q16_d1","options":[{"id":"q16_d1_o2","en":"high-anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"q16_d1_o1","en":"normal-anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"正常阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"q16_d1_o3","en":"primary respiratory alkalosis","zh":"原发性呼吸性碱中毒"}],"correct":"q16_d1_o1"},{"id":"q16_d2","options":[{"id":"q16_d2_o1","en":"intestinal bicarbonate loss from the ileostomy","zh":"回肠造口导致的肠道碳酸氢盐丢失"},{"id":"q16_d2_o2","en":"lactic acid accumulation from shock","zh":"休克导致的乳酸堆积"},{"id":"q16_d2_o3","en":"carbon dioxide retention from hypoventilation","zh":"低通气导致的二氧化碳潴留"}],"correct":"q16_d2_o1"},{"id":"q16_d3","options":[{"id":"q16_d3_o1","en":"appropriate respiratory compensation","zh":"适当的呼吸性代偿"},{"id":"q16_d3_o3","en":"a superimposed respiratory alkalosis","zh":"合并呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"q16_d3_o2","en":"a superimposed respiratory acidosis","zh":"合并呼吸性酸中毒"}],"correct":"q16_d3_o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pH is acidemic and HCO3 is low, so the primary process is metabolic acidosis. The anion gap is 138 − (112 + 14) = 12 mEq/L, which is normal. A high-output ileostomy causes gastrointestinal bicarbonate loss. Expected PaCO2 is 1.5(14) + 8 = 29 ± 2 mm Hg; the measured 29 mm Hg shows appropriate respiratory compensation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"pH 表示酸血症，HCO3 降低，因此原发过程是代谢性酸中毒。阴离子间隙为 138 −（112 + 14）= 12 mEq/L，属于正常范围。高输出回肠造口可导致胃肠道碳酸氢盐丢失。预期 PaCO2 为 1.5(14) + 8 = 29 ± 2 mm Hg；实测 29 mm Hg，说明呼吸性代偿适当。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Work in three steps: identify the primary disorder, calculate the anion gap, then compare measured PaCO2 with the stated compensation range.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分三步完成：先确定原发紊乱，再计算阴离子间隙，最后把实测 PaCO2 与题干给出的代偿范围比较。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual Professional Edition, Metabolic Acidosis, Causes of Metabolic Acidosis table (normal-gap gastrointestinal bicarbonate loss including ileostomy) and Diagnosis of Metabolic Acidosis (anion-gap evaluation and Winter's formula), https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/nephrology/acid-base-regulation-and-disorders/metabolic-acidosis","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2113,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_bt_perioperative_care_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.643","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.643.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.643.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,263],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,73],"fullStemEn":"Immediately before electrosurgery above the xiphoid, alcohol-based skin preparation remains visibly wet and pooled beneath the client. Open supplemental oxygen is flowing under the drapes. The electrosurgical unit has not yet been activated. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"在剑突以上部位进行电外科操作前，含酒精皮肤消毒液仍明显潮湿，并积聚在患者身下。开放式补充氧气正在手术巾下流动。电外科设备尚未启动。请完成蝴蝶结图。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结图。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The electrosurgical unit has not yet been activated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"电外科设备尚未启动。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate hazard","zh":"即时危险"},"tokens":[{"id":"q17_c3","en":"Primary risk of postoperative wound infection only","zh":"唯一主要风险是术后伤口感染"},{"id":"q17_c1","en":"Imminent surgical-fire risk from fuel, oxidizer, and an ignition source","zh":"燃料、氧化剂和点火源共同造成的迫近手术火灾风险"},{"id":"q17_c2","en":"Routine readiness for electrosurgery with no fire-triangle concern","zh":"电外科常规准备就绪，不存在火三角问题"}],"correct":"q17_c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take before proceeding","zh":"继续操作前应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q17_a1","en":"Stop the ignition step and do not activate electrosurgery","zh":"停止点火步骤，不得启动电外科设备"},{"id":"q17_a4","en":"Activate electrosurgery at a lower power while the open oxygen continues","zh":"在开放氧气继续流动时，以较低功率启动电外科设备"},{"id":"q17_a3","en":"Cover the wet preparation with additional drapes and proceed","zh":"用更多手术巾覆盖潮湿消毒液后继续操作"},{"id":"q17_a2","en":"Remove pooled solution and wet materials, wait for complete drying, and coordinate the open-oxygen and ignition plan with anesthesia and the surgical team","zh":"清除积聚消毒液和潮湿材料，等待完全干燥，并与麻醉和手术团队协调开放氧气与点火计划"}],"correct":["q17_a1","q17_a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Safety conditions to verify","zh":"应核实的安全条件"},"tokens":[{"id":"q17_p2","en":"The open-oxygen arrangement under the drapes has been reassessed and coordinated before ignition","zh":"点火前已重新评估并协调手术巾下的开放氧气安排"},{"id":"q17_p4","en":"The number of electrosurgical instruments on the tray","zh":"器械台上的电外科器械数量"},{"id":"q17_p1","en":"Prep is completely dry with no pooled solution or wet materials","zh":"消毒液已完全干燥，无积聚液体或潮湿材料"},{"id":"q17_p3","en":"The client's postoperative pain score","zh":"患者的术后疼痛评分"}],"correct":["q17_p1","q17_p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Wet pooled alcohol is fuel, open oxygen is an oxidizer, and electrosurgery is an ignition source. Because ignition has not occurred, the team should stop, remove pooled solution and wet materials, wait for complete drying, and coordinate oxygen use before activation. Verification focuses on removal of fuel and control of the oxidizer-ignition arrangement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"潮湿并积聚的酒精是燃料，开放氧气是氧化剂，电外科设备是点火源。由于尚未点火，团队应停止操作，清除积聚液体和潮湿材料，等待完全干燥，并在启动设备前协调氧气使用。核实重点是消除燃料并控制氧化剂—点火源组合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the fire triangle in the present moment. Because ignition has not started, select actions that remove fuel, withhold ignition, and coordinate the oxidizer.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别当前存在的火三角。因为尚未点火，应选择清除燃料、停止点火并协调氧化剂的行动。","sourceMetadata":"FDA, NDA 208288 Other Review—alcohol-based preoperative skin preparation labeling review, directions and flammability warnings to remove pooled solution/wet materials and wait until completely dry before draping or using cautery/laser, https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2018/208288Orig1s000OtherR.pdf; FDA, Practical Advice for Preventing Surgical Fires, pp. 27–28—coordinate oxygen delivery, eliminate pooled alcohol preparation, allow drying, and communicate before activating an electrosurgical ignition source, https://www.fda.gov/files/drugs/published/Slides-from-Webinar--Practical-Advice-for-Preventing-Surgical-Fires--Safety-Strategies-from-the-Front-Lines-%28PDF%29.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2114,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance5_2026_07_16_hl_intrapartum_fetal_monitoring_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.644","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.644.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.644.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,69],"fullStemEn":"During second-stage labor, the external monitor displays a “fetal” rate of 92/min. Highlight the cues and actions that support suspected maternal-heart-rate artifact and verification of signal identity before diagnosing fetal bradycardia.","fullStemZh":"在第二产程中，外部监护仪显示“胎心率”为 92 次/分。请标出支持怀疑母体心率伪差的线索，以及在诊断胎儿心动过缓前用于核实信号身份的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the cues and actions that support suspected maternal-heart-rate artifact and verification of signal identity before diagnosing fetal bradycardia.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持怀疑母体心率伪差的线索，以及在诊断胎儿心动过缓前用于核实信号身份的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During second-stage labor, the external monitor displays a “fetal” rate of 92/min.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第二产程中，外部监护仪显示“胎心率”为 92 次/分。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q18_s1","en":"The external “fetal” rate is 92/min.","zh":"外部监护仪显示的“胎心率”为 92 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s2","en":"The maternal pulse measured at the same time is 92/min.","zh":"同时测得的母体脉搏也是 92 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s3","en":"The displayed rate repeatedly rises and falls in exact coincidence with the maternal pulse.","zh":"显示的心率反复与母体脉搏完全同步升降。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s4","en":"Compare the maternal pulse and displayed fetal rate simultaneously.","zh":"同时比较母体脉搏和显示的胎心率。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s5","en":"Reposition and check the external transducer.","zh":"重新放置并检查外部传感器。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s6","en":"Confirm the fetal rate with an independent appropriate method while continuing maternal-rate comparison.","zh":"在继续比较母体心率的同时，使用另一种适当的独立方法确认胎心率。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s7","en":"Document fetal bradycardia as confirmed before checking which signal is being recorded.","zh":"在核实记录的是哪一种信号之前，就记录已确认胎儿心动过缓。","selectable":true},{"id":"q18_s8","en":"Prepare for emergency operative birth based only on the unverified 92/min signal.","zh":"仅根据未经核实的 92 次/分信号准备紧急手术分娩。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q18_s1","q18_s2","q18_s3","q18_s4","q18_s5","q18_s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In second-stage labor, maternal heart rate is more easily mistaken for fetal heart rate. A displayed rate that equals and repeatedly tracks the maternal pulse raises concern for maternal artifact. The nurse compares both rates simultaneously, checks transducer placement, and confirms the fetal rate by an independent appropriate method before labeling fetal bradycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在第二产程中，母体心率更容易被误认为胎心率。显示心率与母体脉搏相同并反复同步变化，应怀疑母体心率伪差。护士应同时比较两种心率、检查传感器位置，并在诊断胎儿心动过缓前用另一种适当的独立方法确认胎心率。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When fetal and maternal rates match, verify whose heart rate is being recorded before interpreting the fetal category or escalating delivery.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当胎心率与母体心率相同时，应先确认记录的是谁的心率，再解释胎儿监护类别或升级分娩处理。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, Fetal monitoring in labour, Recommendations 1.4.5–1.4.9 and 1.4.34–1.4.36—differentiate maternal and fetal heartbeats, use an appropriate confirmation method, improve transducer signal quality, and apply heightened vigilance in second-stage labor, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2115,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_dc_client_advocacy_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.645","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.645.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.645.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,243],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,79],"fullStemEn":"A capable inpatient tells the nurse, “My close friend is the person I want to visit and support me.” Staff plan to exclude the friend solely because the friend is not legally related to the client. No safety restriction is currently in effect.","fullStemZh":"一名具有决定能力的住院患者告诉护士：“我希望我的亲密朋友来探视并支持我。”工作人员仅因该朋友与患者没有法律亲属关系而计划拒绝其探视。目前没有实施任何安全限制。","terminalSentenceEn":"No safety restriction is currently in effect.","terminalSentenceZh":"目前没有实施任何安全限制。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Staff plan to exclude the friend solely because the friend is not legally related to the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"工作人员仅因该朋友与患者没有法律亲属关系而计划拒绝其探视。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The hospital should {{q01_designation}} unless {{q01_restriction}}.","zh":"医院应当{{q01_designation}}，除非{{q01_restriction}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q01_designation","options":[{"id":"q01_designation_honor","en":"honor the client’s designation of the friend as a visitor","zh":"尊重患者指定该朋友为探视者的决定"},{"id":"q01_designation_kin","en":"require the visitor to prove a legal family relationship","zh":"要求探视者证明其与患者存在法律亲属关系"},{"id":"q01_designation_family","en":"allow the client’s relatives to choose all permitted visitors","zh":"由患者亲属决定所有获准探视者"}],"correct":"q01_designation_honor"},{"id":"q01_restriction","options":[{"id":"q01_restriction_poa","en":"the friend does not hold healthcare power of attorney","zh":"该朋友没有医疗授权委托书"},{"id":"q01_restriction_staff","en":"a staff member is uncomfortable with nonrelative visitors","zh":"工作人员对非亲属探视者感到不自在"},{"id":"q01_restriction_equal","en":"a clinically necessary or otherwise reasonable restriction applies consistently and is explained","zh":"存在临床必要或其他合理限制，且该限制被一致执行并得到说明"}],"correct":"q01_restriction_equal"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A capable client may designate a friend as a visitor. The hospital may apply clinically necessary or otherwise reasonable visitation limits, but it may not exclude the friend merely because the friend is not legally related to the client. Any applicable restriction should be consistently implemented and explained.","rationaleCorrectZh":"具有决定能力的患者可以指定朋友为探视者。医院可以实施临床必要或其他合理的探视限制，但不能仅因该朋友不是法律亲属而拒绝探视。任何适用限制都应一致执行并予以说明。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the client’s right to designate a visitor from the hospital’s ability to impose a genuine, consistently applied safety restriction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将患者指定探视者的权利与医院实施真实且一致执行的安全限制区分开来。","sourceMetadata":"CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix A, 42 CFR 482.13(h), Tags A-0215–A-0217, including patient-designated visitors, clinically necessary or reasonable restrictions, nondiscrimination, and equal visitation privileges: https://www.cms.gov/Regulations-and-Guidance/Guidance/Transmittals/downloads/R75SOMA.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2116,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_mx_client_advocacy_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.646","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.646.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.646.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,246],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,65],"fullStemEn":"A client with dysarthria is alert and has decision-making capacity. The client uses a speech-generating device and communicates slowly. For each proposed staff behavior, indicate whether it supports the client’s communication rights and autonomy.","fullStemZh":"一名构音障碍患者意识清醒并具有决定能力。患者使用语音生成设备，沟通速度较慢。请判断每项工作人员行为是否支持患者的沟通权利和自主性。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each proposed staff behavior, indicate whether it supports the client’s communication rights and autonomy.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项工作人员行为是否支持患者的沟通权利和自主性。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client uses a speech-generating device and communicates slowly.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者使用语音生成设备，沟通速度较慢。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q02_row_method","en":"Ask the client which communication method works best.","zh":"询问患者哪种沟通方式最有效。"},{"id":"q02_row_device","en":"Provide the speech-generating device and allow the client to use it.","zh":"提供语音生成设备并允许患者使用。"},{"id":"q02_row_time","en":"Allow enough time for the client to complete each response.","zh":"给予患者足够时间完成每次回答。"},{"id":"q02_row_direct","en":"Address questions directly to the client.","zh":"直接向患者提问。"},{"id":"q02_row_verify","en":"Respectfully ask the client to repeat or clarify an unclear word.","zh":"对不清楚的词语，礼貌地请患者重复或澄清。"},{"id":"q02_row_finish","en":"Finish the client’s sentences to keep the interview moving.","zh":"为了加快访谈进度，替患者说完句子。"},{"id":"q02_row_companion","en":"Direct all questions to the companion because communication is faster.","zh":"因为沟通更快，把所有问题都问陪同者。"},{"id":"q02_row_capacity","en":"Treat impaired speech as evidence that the client cannot make decisions.","zh":"把言语受损视为患者不能作出决定的证据。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q02_col_supports","en":"Supports advocacy","zh":"支持权益维护"},{"id":"q02_col_not","en":"Does not support advocacy","zh":"不支持权益维护"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q02_row_method","columnIds":["q02_col_supports"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_device","columnIds":["q02_col_supports"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_time","columnIds":["q02_col_supports"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_direct","columnIds":["q02_col_supports"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_verify","columnIds":["q02_col_supports"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_finish","columnIds":["q02_col_not"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_companion","columnIds":["q02_col_not"]},{"rowId":"q02_row_capacity","columnIds":["q02_col_not"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective communication preserves the client’s own voice: use the client’s preferred method, provide the auxiliary aid, allow time, address the client directly, and clarify respectfully. Dysarthria does not establish impaired cognition or decision-making capacity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效沟通应保留患者本人的声音：采用患者偏好的方式、提供辅助设备、给予时间、直接与患者交流，并以尊重的方式澄清。构音障碍并不等于认知或决定能力受损。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not confuse the speed or clarity of speech with the client’s capacity; choose actions that let the client communicate personally.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把言语速度或清晰度与患者能力混为一谈；选择让患者本人能够表达的措施。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. Department of Justice, ADA Requirements: Effective Communication, sections on auxiliary aids for speech disabilities, considering the person’s normal method of communication, allowing more time, and respectfully clarifying unclear speech: https://www.ada.gov/resources/effective-communication/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2117,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_hl_conflict_resolution_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.647","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.647.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.647.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,52],"fullStemEn":"A medication near miss caused no client harm. The facilitator begins a brief team debrief. Highlight the facilitator statements or actions that support an effective, blame-free review.","fullStemZh":"一次用药险情没有造成患者伤害。主持人开始进行简短团队复盘。请标出支持有效、无责备复盘的主持人陈述或行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the facilitator statements or actions that support an effective, blame-free review.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持有效、无责备复盘的主持人陈述或行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facilitator begins a brief team debrief.","penultimateSentenceZh":"主持人开始进行简短团队复盘。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q03_intro","en":"The facilitator says: ","zh":"主持人说："},{"id":"q03_goal","en":"“Our goal is to understand how the medication nearly reached the wrong client and improve the process.”","zh":"“我们的目标是了解药物为何险些给错患者，并改进流程。”","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_facts","en":"“Let’s reconstruct the confirmed sequence from order entry through bedside scanning.”","zh":"“让我们根据已确认的信息，重建从录入医嘱到床旁扫码的过程。”","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_roles","en":"“I want each role to describe what was observed at its step.”","zh":"“我希望每个岗位都说明自己在该环节观察到的情况。”","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_worked","en":"“Which safeguards worked, and what should change before the next medication pass?”","zh":"“哪些防护措施发挥了作用？下次给药前应改变什么？”","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_blame","en":"“The evening nurse is careless, so we already know the cause.”","zh":"“晚班护士粗心，所以我们已经知道原因了。”","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_speculate","en":"“I heard the pharmacist was distracted, although no one has verified that.”","zh":"“我听说药师当时分心了，虽然还没有人核实。”","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_follow","en":"The facilitator assigns the medication-safety lead to test the revised scan alert by Friday and report the result to the team.","zh":"主持人指定用药安全负责人在周五前测试修改后的扫码警报，并向团队报告结果。","selectable":true},{"id":"q03_punish","en":"The facilitator recommends a written warning before reviewing the workflow.","zh":"主持人在审查工作流程前就建议给予书面处分。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q03_goal","q03_facts","q03_roles","q03_worked","q03_follow"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An effective debrief reviews the specific goal and verified facts, invites observations from all involved roles, identifies what worked and what should change, avoids individual blame, and ends with a concrete improvement assignment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效复盘会审查具体目标和已核实事实，邀请所有相关岗位提供观察，识别有效做法和需要改变之处，避免个人责备，并以明确的改进任务结束。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose debrief behaviors that move from objective facts to shared learning and a specific follow-up, not blame or rumor.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择从客观事实走向共同学习和明确后续行动的复盘行为，而不是责备或传闻。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ TeamSTEPPS, Reviewing the Team’s Performance: Debrief, including accurate recounting, what worked and did not work, performance improvement, avoiding individual blame, and assigning goals for improvement: https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/team/tools/debrief.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2118,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_bt_conflict_resolution_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.648","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.648.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.648.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[277,297],"terminalOffsetsZh":[74,81],"fullStemEn":"Day and night shifts repeatedly accuse each other of failing to restock a time-critical airway cart. No client is currently deteriorating. An objective audit shows that responsibility changes at 1900, but the handoff checklist names no owner and includes no verification step. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"日班和夜班反复互相指责未补充需要及时备齐的气道车。目前没有患者病情恶化。客观审计显示，责任在1900交接，但交接清单没有指定负责人，也没有核实步骤。完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An objective audit shows that responsibility changes at 1900, but the handoff checklist names no owner and includes no verification step.","penultimateSentenceZh":"客观审计显示，责任在1900交接，但交接清单没有指定负责人，也没有核实步骤。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Problem sustaining the conflict","zh":"维持冲突的问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_c_role","en":"Role and process ambiguity at shift handoff","zh":"交班时的角色与流程不明确"},{"id":"q04_c_supply","en":"A confirmed hospital-wide supply shortage","zh":"已证实的全院物资短缺"},{"id":"q04_c_skill","en":"A knowledge deficit about airway equipment","zh":"对气道设备的知识不足"},{"id":"q04_c_emergency","en":"An active airway emergency","zh":"正在发生的气道急症"}],"correct":"q04_c_role"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_a_email","en":"Send separate warning emails to each shift","zh":"分别向每个班次发送警告邮件"},{"id":"q04_a_huddle","en":"Hold a joint day-night huddle using the audit facts","zh":"根据审计事实召开日夜班联合短会"},{"id":"q04_a_process","en":"Revise the handoff to name an owner and require closed-loop verification","zh":"修改交接流程，指定负责人并要求闭环核实"},{"id":"q04_a_punish","en":"Discipline the most recent nurse who signed the checklist","zh":"处分最近在清单上签字的护士"},{"id":"q04_a_ignore","en":"Wait for another omission before changing the process","zh":"等再次发生遗漏后再改变流程"}],"correct":["q04_a_huddle","q04_a_process"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Outcomes to monitor","zh":"应监测的结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"q04_p_check","en":"Completion of the new owner-and-verification handoff check","zh":"新的负责人及核实交接检查完成率"},{"id":"q04_p_overtime","en":"Total unit overtime unrelated to restocking","zh":"与补货无关的科室总加班时间"},{"id":"q04_p_omit","en":"Recurrence of airway-cart stock omissions","zh":"气道车物资遗漏是否再次发生"},{"id":"q04_p_complaints","en":"Number of informal complaints about the other shift","zh":"对另一班次的非正式抱怨次数"},{"id":"q04_p_speed","en":"How quickly the huddle ends","zh":"短会结束得多快"}],"correct":["q04_p_check","q04_p_omit"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The audit identifies a recurring ownership and verification gap, not an individual character flaw. A joint huddle creates a shared plan; naming the owner and requiring closed-loop verification makes the handoff accountable. Monitor whether the new check occurs and whether omissions recur.","rationaleCorrectZh":"审计发现的是反复出现的责任归属和核实缺口，而不是个人品格问题。联合短会可形成共同计划；指定负责人并要求闭环核实，可使交接具有明确责任。应监测新检查是否完成以及遗漏是否再次发生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When repeated conflict maps to an unclear workflow, select a shared process correction and measure both compliance and recurrence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当反复冲突对应不明确的工作流程时，应选择共同流程纠正措施，并同时监测执行情况和再次发生率。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ TeamSTEPPS, Huddle tool (adjusting and communicating the plan) and Closed-Loop Communication tool (message, receiver confirmation, sender verification): https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/team/tools/huddle.html ; https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/communication/tools/loop.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"An objective audit shows that responsibility changes at 1900, but the handoff checklist names no owner and includes no verification step.","controlSentenceZh":"客观审计显示，责任在1900交接，但交接清单没有指定负责人，也没有核实步骤。"}
{"queueIndex":2119,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_dc_confidentiality_hipaa_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.649","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.649.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.649.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,48],"fullStemEn":"A client experiencing intimate-partner stalking asks the clinic to send appointment reminders only to a new email address and not to the home telephone or mailing address.","fullStemZh":"一名遭受亲密伴侣跟踪的患者要求诊所只把预约提醒发送到新的电子邮箱，不要发送到家庭电话或邮寄地址。","terminalSentenceEn":"A client experiencing intimate-partner stalking asks the clinic to send appointment reminders only to a new email address and not to the home telephone or mailing address.","terminalSentenceZh":"一名遭受亲密伴侣跟踪的患者要求诊所只把预约提醒发送到新的电子邮箱，不要发送到家庭电话或邮寄地址。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"This is a request for {{q05_request}}; the nurse should {{q05_action}}.","zh":"这是关于{{q05_request}}的请求；护士应当{{q05_action}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q05_request","options":[{"id":"q05_request_amend","en":"amendment of a disputed diagnosis","zh":"修改有争议的诊断"},{"id":"q05_request_conf","en":"confidential communications by an alternative means or location","zh":"通过替代方式或地点进行保密通信"},{"id":"q05_request_access","en":"immediate access to the complete medical record","zh":"立即访问完整医疗记录"}],"correct":"q05_request_conf"},{"id":"q05_action","options":[{"id":"q05_action_continue","en":"continue all existing reminder channels until the client obtains a court order","zh":"在患者取得法院命令前继续使用所有现有提醒渠道"},{"id":"q05_action_route","en":"route and document the request through the covered entity’s confidential-communications process and stop using the unsafe channels as directed","zh":"按照受监管实体的保密通信流程转交并记录该请求，并按要求停止使用不安全渠道"},{"id":"q05_action_explain","en":"require the client to prove the stalking before changing contact methods","zh":"要求患者证明遭跟踪后才改变联系方式"}],"correct":"q05_action_route"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA permits an individual to request communications by an alternative means or at an alternative location. The clinic should use its established process to record and implement the reasonable request rather than continue channels the client has identified as unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA允许个人请求通过替代方式或替代地点进行通信。诊所应使用既定流程记录并实施合理请求，而不是继续使用患者已指出不安全的渠道。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify whether the client wants the record changed, disclosed, or communicated through a safer channel; this scenario is about the channel.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断患者是要修改记录、限制披露，还是改用更安全的通信渠道；本题考查的是通信渠道。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR 164.522(b), Confidential communications requirements, including requests for communications by alternative means or at alternative locations and covered-entity processes: https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-E/section-164.522","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2120,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_hl_confidentiality_hipaa_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.650","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.650.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.650.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,244],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,73],"fullStemEn":"A client asks the covered laboratory provider to restrict disclosure of one laboratory service to the client’s health plan. Highlight the facts and actions that support a mandatory restriction under the HIPAA paid-in-full health-plan provision.","fullStemZh":"一名患者要求受HIPAA约束的检验服务提供者限制向其健康计划披露某项检验服务。请标出支持HIPAA“已全额自费支付”健康计划强制限制的事实和行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the facts and actions that support a mandatory restriction under the HIPAA paid-in-full health-plan provision.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持HIPAA“已全额自费支付”健康计划强制限制的事实和行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client asks the covered laboratory provider to restrict disclosure of one laboratory service to the client’s health plan.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者要求受HIPAA约束的检验服务提供者限制向其健康计划披露某项检验服务。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q06_context","en":"Before any claim is submitted, ","zh":"在提交任何理赔申请之前，"},{"id":"q06_paid","en":"the client pays the specific laboratory service in full out of pocket.","zh":"患者已自费全额支付该项具体检验服务。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_payment","en":"The planned disclosure to the health plan would be for payment or healthcare operations.","zh":"计划向健康计划披露信息的目的为支付或医疗运营。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_treatment","en":"The client also demands that the result be hidden from another clinician who needs it for treatment.","zh":"患者还要求向因治疗需要该结果的另一名临床医生隐瞒信息。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_record","en":"The privacy officer records and routes the restriction for the specific paid service.","zh":"隐私负责人记录并转交针对该项已付费服务的限制。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_nobill","en":"Billing staff are instructed not to submit that service to the health plan.","zh":"通知计费人员不要把该项服务提交给健康计划。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_unpaid","en":"A separate unpaid service from the same visit remains on the account.","zh":"同次就诊的另一项未付款服务仍在账户中。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_late","en":"The client first makes the request after the plan has already paid the claim.","zh":"患者在健康计划已经支付理赔后才首次提出请求。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q06_paid","q06_payment","q06_record","q06_nobill"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The mandatory restriction applies to disclosure to a health plan for payment or healthcare operations when the protected information concerns a specific service paid in full out of pocket. The provider must capture the restriction and avoid billing the plan for that service. It does not create a duty to conceal information needed for another provider’s treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当受保护信息涉及患者已自费全额支付的具体服务，且拟向健康计划披露的目的为支付或医疗运营时，强制限制适用。提供者必须记录该限制，并避免向健康计划计费。该规定并不要求向因治疗需要信息的其他提供者隐瞒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for all three linked elements: a specific service, full out-of-pocket payment, and disclosure to a health plan for payment or operations.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找三个相互关联的条件：具体服务、全额自费支付，以及为支付或运营目的向健康计划披露。","sourceMetadata":"45 CFR 164.522(a)(1)(vi) and 164.522(a)(3), mandatory restriction on disclosure to a health plan for payment or healthcare operations when the item or service is paid in full out of pocket, plus documentation requirements: https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/subtitle-A/subchapter-C/part-164/subpart-E/section-164.522","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2121,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_bt_discharge_planning_handoff_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.651","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.651.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.651.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[374,394],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,113],"fullStemEn":"A client will leave today on outpatient parenteral antimicrobial therapy (OPAT). Infusion supplies will arrive before the first home dose. The prescribed plan is a complete blood count and metabolic panel every Monday and Thursday, but no recipient is named for the results. No clinician or team has accepted responsibility for the OPAT course, and follow-up is not booked. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者今天将带院外静脉抗菌治疗（OPAT）出院。输注用品将在首次居家用药前送达。医嘱监测计划为每周一和周四进行全血细胞计数和代谢检查，但没有指定结果接收者。没有临床医生或团队接受OPAT疗程责任，随访也未预约。完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"No clinician or team has accepted responsibility for the OPAT course, and follow-up is not booked.","penultimateSentenceZh":"没有临床医生或团队接受OPAT疗程责任，随访也未预约。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Transition problem","zh":"过渡问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_c_adherence","en":"Intentional refusal of all treatment","zh":"故意拒绝所有治疗"},{"id":"q07_c_supply","en":"Delayed infusion-supply delivery","zh":"输注用品延迟送达"},{"id":"q07_c_unowned","en":"Unsafe, unowned OPAT transition","zh":"不安全且无人负责的OPAT过渡"},{"id":"q07_c_allergy","en":"Confirmed immediate antimicrobial allergy","zh":"已确认的即刻抗菌药过敏"}],"correct":"q07_c_unowned"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions before discharge","zh":"出院前行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_a_owner","en":"Confirm the OPAT or infectious-diseases clinician/team that accepts responsibility for the course","zh":"确认接受疗程责任的OPAT或感染病临床医生/团队"},{"id":"q07_a_frequency","en":"Replace the prescribed schedule with daily laboratory testing","zh":"把医嘱计划改成每日化验"},{"id":"q07_a_client","en":"Make the client solely responsible for finding a clinician after discharge","zh":"让患者独自负责出院后寻找临床医生"},{"id":"q07_a_wait","en":"Wait for an abnormal result before assigning responsibility","zh":"等出现异常结果后再指定责任人"},{"id":"q07_a_transmit","en":"Transmit the antimicrobial regimen and the prescribed Monday/Thursday monitoring plan to that responsible clinician/team","zh":"把抗菌方案和每周一/周四监测计划传递给该负责临床医生/团队"},{"id":"q07_a_supplies","en":"Discharge because supply delivery alone makes the transition complete","zh":"仅因用品已安排送达就出院"}],"correct":["q07_a_owner","q07_a_transmit"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Outcomes to monitor","zh":"应监测的结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"q07_p_follow","en":"Attendance at follow-up and documented clinical assessment of the OPAT course","zh":"按时随访并记录对OPAT疗程的临床评估"},{"id":"q07_p_labs","en":"Receipt and documented review of the scheduled laboratory results","zh":"按计划化验结果的接收和有记录的审阅"},{"id":"q07_p_boxes","en":"Number of supply boxes delivered","zh":"送达的用品箱数量"},{"id":"q07_p_calls","en":"Number of calls the client makes to locate a clinician","zh":"患者为寻找临床医生拨打电话的次数"},{"id":"q07_p_daily","en":"Completion of unprescribed daily laboratory tests","zh":"完成未开具的每日化验"}],"correct":["q07_p_labs","q07_p_follow"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Supply delivery does not make OPAT safe when clinical ownership, result routing, and follow-up are absent. Before discharge, a responsible OPAT/ID clinician or team must accept oversight and receive the regimen and prescribed monitoring plan. The transition is evaluated by confirming that scheduled results are received and reviewed and that clinical follow-up occurs.","rationaleCorrectZh":"仅有用品送达并不能在缺少临床责任、结果转交和随访时保证OPAT安全。出院前，必须由负责的OPAT/感染病临床医生或团队接受监督责任，并接收抗菌方案和医嘱监测计划。应通过确认计划结果被接收和审阅，以及临床随访确实发生来评价过渡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a complex therapy transition, distinguish delivery logistics from clinical ownership, result routing, and follow-up accountability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于复杂治疗过渡，要区分用品物流与临床责任、结果转交和随访问责。","sourceMetadata":"IDSA, Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Outpatient Parenteral Antimicrobial Therapy, Recommendations 14 and 16 and discussion of responsible oversight and availability of laboratory results to the responsible team: https://www.idsociety.org/practice-guideline/outpatient-parenteral-antimicrobial-therapy/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2122,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_hl_discharge_planning_handoff_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.652","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.652.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.652.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,283],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,74],"fullStemEn":"An adult with uncomplicated mild traumatic brain injury has completed an emergency evaluation that supports discharge. The draft discharge record contains only: “Use acetaminophen as directed and rest tonight.” Highlight the additional elements that should be added before discharge.","fullStemZh":"一名无并发症的轻度创伤性脑损伤成人已完成急诊评估，评估支持出院。出院记录草稿仅写有：“按说明使用对乙酰氨基酚，今晚休息。”请标出出院前应补充的内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the additional elements that should be added before discharge.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出出院前应补充的内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The draft discharge record contains only: “Use acetaminophen as directed and rest tonight.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"出院记录草稿仅写有：“按说明使用对乙酰氨基酚，今晚休息。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q08_s_danger","en":"Provide verbal and written instructions about delayed danger signs and when to seek emergency care.","zh":"口头并书面说明延迟出现的危险征象以及何时寻求急救。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s_friend","en":"With the client’s agreement, tell a chosen family member or friend what symptoms to watch for.","zh":"经患者同意，告知其选择的家人或朋友需要观察哪些症状。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s_follow","en":"Arrange or specify follow-up with the regular clinician within a few days.","zh":"安排或明确在数日内与常规临床医生随访。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s_activity","en":"Give individualized written guidance for return to work, driving, and other activities.","zh":"提供关于恢复工作、驾驶和其他活动的个体化书面指导。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s_ct","en":"Schedule routine repeat head CT tomorrow despite the discharge-supporting evaluation.","zh":"尽管评估支持出院，仍常规安排明日重复头部CT。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s_admit","en":"Require overnight hospital admission solely because mild TBI was diagnosed.","zh":"仅因诊断为轻度脑损伤而要求住院过夜。","selectable":true},{"id":"q08_s_generic","en":"Tell the client to resume all activities whenever the client feels ready, without written limits.","zh":"只告诉患者感觉可以时恢复所有活动，不提供书面限制。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q08_s_danger","q08_s_friend","q08_s_follow","q08_s_activity"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe mild-TBI discharge includes verbal and written danger-sign education, involvement of a chosen support person, follow-up within the stated timeframe, and individualized written return-to-activity guidance. Routine repeat imaging or admission is not required when the completed evaluation supports discharge.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全的轻度脑损伤出院包括口头和书面危险征象教育、让患者选择的支持者了解观察要点、在规定时间内随访，以及个体化书面活动恢复指导。当完成的评估支持出院时，不需要常规重复影像或住院。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Because the stem closes the imaging and admission decision, focus on the missing discharge communication and follow-up elements.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干已经说明影像和住院决策，因此应聚焦缺失的出院沟通和随访要素。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Mild Traumatic Brain Injury and Concussion: Information for Adults—Discharge Instructions, danger signs, family/friend observation, follow-up, and written return-to-activity guidance: https://www.cdc.gov/traumatic-brain-injury/media/pdfs/TBI_Patient_Instructions-a.pdf ; CDC Checklist to Assess for and Manage Adult mTBI, discharge education, follow-up within a few days, and no routine repeat imaging/admission when criteria support discharge: https://www.cdc.gov/traumaticbraininjury/pdf/checklist_adult_mTBI-508.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2123,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_mx_discharge_planning_handoff_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.653","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.653.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.653.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[125,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,71],"fullStemEn":"A client will begin home enteral feeding with a pump. Classify each transition element as ready for discharge or unresolved. This item tests transition readiness, not bedside tube-placement verification.","fullStemZh":"一名患者将开始使用泵进行居家肠内营养。请将每项过渡要素分类为“已准备好出院”或“尚未解决”。本题考查过渡准备情况，不考查床旁导管位置核实技术。","terminalSentenceEn":"This item tests transition readiness, not bedside tube-placement verification.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题考查过渡准备情况，不考查床旁导管位置核实技术。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Classify each transition element as ready for discharge or unresolved.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请将每项过渡要素分类为“已准备好出院”或“尚未解决”。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q09_r_plan","en":"The individualized feeding regimen, goals, and monitoring plan are documented.","zh":"已记录个体化喂养方案、目标和监测计划。"},{"id":"q09_r_demo","en":"The client and caregiver correctly return-demonstrate pump setup and troubleshooting.","zh":"患者和照护者正确回示泵的设置和故障处理。"},{"id":"q09_r_contacts","en":"Routine and emergency contact numbers are available, including after-hours help.","zh":"已提供常规和紧急联系电话，包括非工作时间帮助。"},{"id":"q09_r_delivery","en":"Delivery of formula, pump, tubing, and required ancillaries is confirmed.","zh":"已确认配方、泵、管路和所需辅材送达。"},{"id":"q09_r_support","en":"Community nutrition and home-care support are coordinated.","zh":"已协调社区营养和居家护理支持。"},{"id":"q09_r_video","en":"The caregiver received only a video link; competence was not assessed.","zh":"照护者只收到一个视频链接，未评估其能力。"},{"id":"q09_r_order","en":"Equipment was ordered, but no delivery confirmation is available.","zh":"设备已经订购，但没有送达确认。"},{"id":"q09_r_after","en":"The record lists no after-hours contact for pump or feeding problems.","zh":"记录中没有泵或喂养问题的非工作时间联系方式。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q09_c_ready","en":"Ready","zh":"已准备好"},{"id":"q09_c_unresolved","en":"Unresolved","zh":"尚未解决"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q09_r_plan","columnIds":["q09_c_ready"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_demo","columnIds":["q09_c_ready"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_contacts","columnIds":["q09_c_ready"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_delivery","columnIds":["q09_c_ready"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_support","columnIds":["q09_c_ready"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_video","columnIds":["q09_c_unresolved"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_order","columnIds":["q09_c_unresolved"]},{"rowId":"q09_r_after","columnIds":["q09_c_unresolved"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Home enteral feeding is transition-ready when an individualized regimen and monitoring plan, demonstrated competence, routine and emergency contacts, confirmed supplies, and coordinated multidisciplinary support are in place. Information without competence assessment, an unconfirmed order, or missing after-hours help remains unresolved.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当个体化方案和监测计划、经回示确认的能力、常规和紧急联系方式、已确认的用品，以及协调好的多学科支持均到位时，居家肠内营养才算过渡准备完成。只有信息而未评估能力、仅下单未确认送达，或缺少非工作时间帮助，都仍未解决。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For home-technology discharge, look for a complete chain: plan, demonstrated skill, contacts, confirmed equipment, and ongoing support.","testTakingStrategyZh":"居家技术出院要寻找完整链条：计划、经证明的技能、联系方式、已确认设备和持续支持。","sourceMetadata":"NICE CG32, Nutrition support for adults, Recommendations 1.9.2–1.9.4 on coordinated multidisciplinary home-enteral support, individualized care and monitoring plans, training, routine/emergency contacts, and delivery of equipment, ancillaries, and feed: https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/CG32/chapter/recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":true,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2124,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_bt_caregiver_role_strain_family_coping_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.654","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.654.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.654.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[235,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[74,81],"fullStemEn":"A spouse is listed as the sole helper for a newly dependent stroke client. During discharge planning, the spouse says, “The therapist needed two people for the transfer. I cannot do that alone, and I am afraid I will drop my partner.” Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"一名配偶被列为新近依赖他人照护的脑卒中患者的唯一帮助者。在出院计划中，配偶说：“治疗师转移患者时需要两个人。我一个人做不到，也担心会把伴侣摔下来。”完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"I cannot do that alone, and I am afraid I will drop my partner.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"我一个人做不到，也担心会把伴侣摔下来。”","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Planning problem","zh":"计划问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q10_c_conflict","en":"The spouse is intentionally delaying discharge","zh":"配偶故意拖延出院"},{"id":"q10_c_knowledge","en":"The client has no rehabilitation needs","zh":"患者没有康复需求"},{"id":"q10_c_capacity","en":"The discharge plan exceeds the willing caregiver’s physical capacity","zh":"出院计划超出愿意照护者的身体能力"},{"id":"q10_c_refusal","en":"The caregiver is refusing all participation","zh":"照护者拒绝所有参与"}],"correct":"q10_c_capacity"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q10_a_insist","en":"Tell the spouse that family members are expected to manage after discharge","zh":"告诉配偶家属理应在出院后自行处理"},{"id":"q10_a_practice","en":"Require repeated solo practice until the spouse agrees","zh":"要求配偶反复单人练习直到同意"},{"id":"q10_a_revise","en":"Revise equipment, personnel, and home-support arrangements to match the assessed need","zh":"根据评估需求修改设备、人员和居家支持安排"},{"id":"q10_a_label","en":"Document the spouse as nonadherent","zh":"把配偶记录为不依从"},{"id":"q10_a_reassess","en":"Ask therapy to reassess the transfer method and required level of assistance","zh":"请治疗团队重新评估转移方式和所需协助程度"}],"correct":["q10_a_reassess","q10_a_revise"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Outcomes to monitor","zh":"应监测的结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"q10_p_discharge","en":"Discharge occurs on the original date regardless of support","zh":"无论支持是否到位都按原日期出院"},{"id":"q10_p_signature","en":"The spouse signs a general caregiver form","zh":"配偶签署一般照护者表格"},{"id":"q10_p_schedule","en":"The actual home-support schedule and responsible helpers are confirmed","zh":"确认实际居家支持时间表和负责帮助者"},{"id":"q10_p_demo","en":"A safe transfer plan is demonstrated using the actual recommended assistance and equipment","zh":"使用实际推荐的协助和设备演示安全转移计划"},{"id":"q10_p_confidence","en":"The spouse says, “I will try harder.”","zh":"配偶说：“我会更努力。”"}],"correct":["q10_p_demo","q10_p_schedule"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The spouse is willing but cannot safely provide the two-person transfer alone. The team should reassess the transfer and revise equipment, staffing, or home support. Readiness requires a demonstrated safe method and confirmation that the needed helpers will actually be present.","rationaleCorrectZh":"配偶愿意照护，但无法独自安全完成需要两人的转移。团队应重新评估转移，并修改设备、人员或居家支持安排。只有安全方法得到演示且所需帮助者确实能够到场，才算准备完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat a caregiver’s stated physical limit as discharge data. Match the plan to demonstrated capacity rather than labeling the caregiver unwilling.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把照护者陈述的身体限制视为出院数据。应让计划匹配经证明的能力，而不是把照护者标记为不愿意。","sourceMetadata":"CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix PP, §483.21(c)(1)(iv) and F660/F661 discharge-planning guidance requiring consideration of caregiver/support-person availability, capacity, and capability: https://www.cms.gov/Regulations-and-Guidance/Guidance/Manuals/downloads/som107ap_pp_guidelines_ltcf.pdf ; AHRQ IDEAL Discharge Planning, include and listen to patients/families and assess understanding with teach-back: https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/patients-families/engagingfamilies/strategy4/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2125,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_hl_caregiver_role_strain_family_coping_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.655","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.655.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.655.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,72],"fullStemEn":"The discharge record states that an adult son is “available daily.” The client will need help every morning. The son tells the nurse, “I live two hours away and can come only on weekends.” Highlight the cues and actions that require correction of the plan.","fullStemZh":"出院记录写着成年儿子“每天都能到场”。患者每天早晨都需要帮助。儿子告诉护士：“我住在两小时车程外，只能周末来。”请标出需要纠正计划的线索和行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the cues and actions that require correction of the plan.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要纠正计划的线索和行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The son tells the nurse, “I live two hours away and can come only on weekends.”","penultimateSentenceZh":"儿子告诉护士：“我住在两小时车程外，只能周末来。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q11_s_verify","en":"Verify the son’s actual availability directly with both the son and the client.","zh":"直接与儿子和患者核实儿子的实际可用时间。","selectable":true},{"id":"q11_s_document","en":"Document that the son is available only on weekends and lives two hours away.","zh":"记录儿子只能周末到场且住在两小时车程外。","selectable":true},{"id":"q11_s_gap","en":"Identify that weekday morning assistance remains uncovered.","zh":"识别工作日早晨的协助仍无人承担。","selectable":true},{"id":"q11_s_alternative","en":"Arrange or refer for an alternative weekday support plan before relying on the son.","zh":"在依赖儿子之前，安排或转介工作日的替代支持计划。","selectable":true},{"id":"q11_s_assume","en":"Keep “available daily” because the son is listed as next of kin.","zh":"因为儿子被列为近亲，所以保留“每天都能到场”的记录。","selectable":true},{"id":"q11_s_weekend","en":"Count weekend visits as coverage for the client’s weekday morning need.","zh":"把周末探访算作对工作日早晨需求的覆盖。","selectable":true},{"id":"q11_s_discharge","en":"Proceed without changing the plan because the son did not refuse all help.","zh":"因为儿子没有拒绝所有帮助，所以不修改计划直接出院。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q11_s_verify","q11_s_document","q11_s_gap","q11_s_alternative"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The documented plan conflicts with the caregiver’s actual schedule. The nurse should verify availability, document the real schedule, identify the uncovered weekday need, and establish an alternative support plan before discharge.","rationaleCorrectZh":"记录中的计划与照护者实际时间表冲突。护士应核实可用时间、记录真实安排、识别无人覆盖的工作日需求，并在出院前建立替代支持计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare the timing of the client’s need with the timing of the caregiver’s verified availability; a mismatch is an unresolved discharge gap.","testTakingStrategyZh":"比较患者需求发生的时间与经核实的照护者可用时间；不匹配就是未解决的出院缺口。","sourceMetadata":"CMS State Operations Manual, Appendix PP, §483.21(c)(1)(iv) and F660/F661 guidance on caregiver availability, capacity, and capability and unsafe discharge when support is absent: https://www.cms.gov/Regulations-and-Guidance/Guidance/Manuals/downloads/som107ap_pp_guidelines_ltcf.pdf ; AHRQ IDEAL Discharge Planning, including patient/family partnership and listening to preferences, observations, and concerns: https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/patients-families/engagingfamilies/strategy4/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2126,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_dc_abg_acid_base_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.656","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.656.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.656.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,386],"terminalOffsetsZh":[97,180],"fullStemEn":"A client has prolonged nasogastric suction. Results are pH 7.51, PaCO2 48 mm Hg, HCO3 37 mEq/L, and chloride 88 mEq/L. The client has no chronic lung disease. For this item, use 40 mm Hg as the reference PaCO2. For metabolic alkalosis, expected PaCO2 rises about 0.6–0.75 mm Hg for each 1 mEq/L rise in HCO3 above 24 mEq/L and generally does not exceed 55 mm Hg from compensation alone.","fullStemZh":"一名患者长期接受鼻胃管吸引。检查结果：pH 7.51、PaCO2 48 mm Hg、HCO3 37 mEq/L、氯 88 mEq/L。患者无慢性肺病。本题以40 mm Hg作为PaCO2参考值。代谢性碱中毒时，HCO3每高于24 mEq/L 1 mEq/L，预计PaCO2约升高0.6–0.75 mm Hg；仅由代偿引起的PaCO2通常不超过55 mm Hg。","terminalSentenceEn":"For metabolic alkalosis, expected PaCO2 rises about 0.6–0.75 mm Hg for each 1 mEq/L rise in HCO3 above 24 mEq/L and generally does not exceed 55 mm Hg from compensation alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"代谢性碱中毒时，HCO3每高于24 mEq/L 1 mEq/L，预计PaCO2约升高0.6–0.75 mm Hg；仅由代偿引起的PaCO2通常不超过55 mm Hg。","penultimateSentenceEn":"For this item, use 40 mm Hg as the reference PaCO2.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题以40 mm Hg作为PaCO2参考值。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The findings indicate {{q12_disorder}} with {{q12_compensation}}.","zh":"这些结果提示{{q12_disorder}}，并伴有{{q12_compensation}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q12_disorder","options":[{"id":"q12_disorder_resp","en":"primary respiratory acidosis from chronic lung disease","zh":"慢性肺病导致的原发性呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"q12_disorder_gap","en":"high-anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"q12_disorder_cl","en":"chloride-responsive metabolic alkalosis from gastric acid and chloride loss","zh":"因胃酸和氯丢失导致的氯反应性代谢性碱中毒"}],"correct":"q12_disorder_cl"},{"id":"q12_compensation","options":[{"id":"q12_comp_appropriate","en":"appropriate respiratory compensation","zh":"适当的呼吸性代偿"},{"id":"q12_comp_none","en":"no respiratory compensation","zh":"无呼吸性代偿"},{"id":"q12_comp_acidosis","en":"a superimposed primary respiratory acidosis","zh":"叠加的原发性呼吸性酸中毒"}],"correct":"q12_comp_appropriate"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Alkalemia with elevated HCO3 identifies metabolic alkalosis. Prolonged gastric suction removes hydrogen and chloride, producing a chloride-responsive pattern. HCO3 is 13 mEq/L above 24, so expected PaCO2 is approximately 40 + (13 × 0.6–0.75), or about 48–50 mm Hg. The measured PaCO2 of 48 mm Hg is appropriate compensation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"碱血症伴HCO3升高提示代谢性碱中毒。长期胃内容物吸引会丢失氢离子和氯，形成氯反应性模式。HCO3比24高13 mEq/L，因此预计PaCO2约为40 +（13 × 0.6–0.75），即约48–50 mm Hg。实测PaCO2为48 mm Hg，符合适当代偿。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the primary disorder first, then calculate the expected compensation using the formula supplied in the stem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先确定原发障碍，再使用题干提供的公式计算预计代偿。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual Professional, Metabolic Alkalosis, causes including nasogastric suction and chloride-responsive alkalosis: https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/nephrology/acid-base-regulation-and-disorders/metabolic-alkalosis ; Merck Manual table, Primary Changes and Compensations in Simple Acid-Base Disorders, expected PaCO2 rise of 0.6–0.75 mm Hg per 1 mEq/L HCO3 increase and usual maximum 55 mm Hg: https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/multimedia/table/primary-changes-and-compensations-in-simple-acid-base-disorders","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2127,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_bt_perioperative_care_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.657","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.657.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.657.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[398,418],"terminalOffsetsZh":[101,108],"fullStemEn":"Minutes after a peripheral nerve block, a client reports metallic taste and tinnitus, becomes agitated, has a seizure, and then develops hypotension with a wide-complex dysrhythmia. The facility LAST protocol directs staff to stop local-anesthetic administration, activate the LAST rescue pathway, support the airway, treat the seizure, and administer 20% lipid emulsion according to the protocol. Complete the bowtie.","fullStemZh":"周围神经阻滞后数分钟，患者报告金属味和耳鸣，随后躁动、癫痫发作，并出现低血压和宽QRS心律失常。机构的LAST流程要求停止局麻药给药、启动LAST救援流程、支持气道、处理癫痫，并按流程给予20%脂肪乳。完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility LAST protocol directs staff to stop local-anesthetic administration, activate the LAST rescue pathway, support the airway, treat the seizure, and administer 20% lipid emulsion according to the protocol.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构的LAST流程要求停止局麻药给药、启动LAST救援流程、支持气道、处理癫痫，并按流程给予20%脂肪乳。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Likely complication","zh":"最可能的并发症"},"tokens":[{"id":"q13_c_mh","en":"Malignant hyperthermia","zh":"恶性高热"},{"id":"q13_c_block","en":"Expected peripheral nerve-block effect","zh":"周围神经阻滞的预期作用"},{"id":"q13_c_last","en":"Local anesthetic systemic toxicity (LAST)","zh":"局部麻醉药全身毒性（LAST）"},{"id":"q13_c_anaph","en":"Isolated anaphylaxis","zh":"单纯过敏性休克"}],"correct":"q13_c_last"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q13_a_walk","en":"Ambulate the client to improve circulation","zh":"让患者下床活动以改善循环"},{"id":"q13_a_stop","en":"Stop local-anesthetic administration and activate the LAST rescue pathway","zh":"停止局麻药给药并启动LAST救援流程"},{"id":"q13_a_support","en":"Provide airway/seizure support and begin 20% lipid emulsion per the supplied protocol","zh":"提供气道和癫痫支持，并按既定流程开始20%脂肪乳"},{"id":"q13_a_repeat","en":"Administer another dose of local anesthetic to complete the block","zh":"再给予一剂局麻药以完成阻滞"},{"id":"q13_a_acls","en":"Use routine standard-ACLS medication doses without modification","zh":"不作调整地使用常规标准ACLS药物剂量"},{"id":"q13_a_observe","en":"Observe for 30 minutes before calling for help","zh":"观察30分钟后再呼救"}],"correct":["q13_a_stop","q13_a_support"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Outcomes to monitor","zh":"应监测的结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"q13_p_cv","en":"Cardiac rhythm and hemodynamic stability","zh":"心律和血流动力学稳定性"},{"id":"q13_p_taste","en":"Whether the client still notices the lipid emulsion taste","zh":"患者是否仍能尝到脂肪乳味道"},{"id":"q13_p_numb","en":"Persistence of numbness in the blocked limb","zh":"阻滞肢体麻木是否持续"},{"id":"q13_p_neuro","en":"Neurologic recovery without recurrent seizure or agitation","zh":"神经功能恢复且癫痫或躁动不再复发"},{"id":"q13_p_site","en":"Size of the needle puncture mark","zh":"针刺痕迹大小"}],"correct":["q13_p_cv","q13_p_neuro"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The rapid sequence of metallic taste, tinnitus, CNS excitation/seizure, hypotension, and wide-complex dysrhythmia after local anesthetic exposure is classic for LAST. Treatment differs from routine ACLS and includes immediate cessation, specialized rescue activation, airway and seizure management, and early 20% lipid emulsion. Monitor cardiovascular stability and neurologic recovery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"局麻药暴露后迅速出现金属味、耳鸣、中枢神经兴奋/癫痫、低血压和宽QRS心律失常，是LAST的典型表现。其复苏不同于常规ACLS，包括立即停药、启动专门救援、气道和癫痫处理以及尽早给予20%脂肪乳。应监测心血管稳定和神经功能恢复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Link the timing after local-anesthetic exposure with the paired neurologic and cardiovascular manifestations, then choose the specialized LAST pathway rather than routine ACLS.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把局麻药暴露后的时间与神经及心血管表现联系起来，然后选择专门LAST流程而不是常规ACLS。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Regional Anesthesia and Pain Medicine (ASRA), Checklist for Treatment of Local Anesthetic Systemic Toxicity (LAST), including calling for help, airway/seizure support, early 20% lipid emulsion, modified resuscitation, and post-stability observation: https://asra.com/docs/default-source/guidelines-articles/local-anesthetic-systemic-toxicity-rgb.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2128,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_or_procedural_complications_dialysis_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.658","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.658.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.658.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[453,480],"terminalOffsetsZh":[129,138],"fullStemEn":"A peritoneal-dialysis client reports new cloudy effluent and abdominal pain but is hemodynamically stable. The unit pathway requires this sequence: notify the PD clinician; obtain effluent for cell count with differential, Gram stain, and culture before the first antibiotic dose when doing so will not cause a dangerous delay; begin the prescribed empiric therapy promptly; then reassess symptoms, effluent clarity, and results for regimen adjustment. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名腹膜透析患者出现新的混浊透出液和腹痛，但血流动力学稳定。科室流程规定顺序为：通知腹透临床医生；在不会造成危险延误时，于首次抗生素给药前采集透出液进行细胞计数及分类、革兰染色和培养；立即开始医嘱经验性治疗；随后重新评估症状、透出液清晰度和结果，以调整方案。请按顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit pathway requires this sequence: notify the PD clinician; obtain effluent for cell count with differential, Gram stain, and culture before the first antibiotic dose when doing so will not cause a dangerous delay; begin the prescribed empiric therapy promptly; then reassess symptoms, effluent clarity, and results for regimen adjustment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室流程规定顺序为：通知腹透临床医生；在不会造成危险延误时，于首次抗生素给药前采集透出液进行细胞计数及分类、革兰染色和培养；立即开始医嘱经验性治疗；随后重新评估症状、透出液清晰度和结果，以调整方案。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q14_step_treat","en":"Begin the prescribed empiric therapy promptly after specimens are obtained.","zh":"采集标本后立即开始医嘱经验性治疗。"},{"id":"q14_step_notify","en":"Notify the PD clinician of suspected peritonitis.","zh":"通知腹透临床医生疑似腹膜炎。"},{"id":"q14_step_specimen","en":"Obtain PD effluent for cell count with differential, Gram stain, and culture before the first antibiotic dose, because this can be done without dangerous delay.","zh":"在不会造成危险延误的情况下，于首次抗生素给药前采集腹透液进行细胞计数及分类、革兰染色和培养。"},{"id":"q14_step_reassess","en":"Reassess symptoms and effluent clarity and review results for adjustment of the regimen.","zh":"重新评估症状和透出液清晰度，并审阅结果以调整方案。"}],"correct":["q14_step_notify","q14_step_specimen","q14_step_treat","q14_step_reassess"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cloudy effluent with abdominal pain requires prompt evaluation for PD peritonitis. Under the pathway stated in the stem for a stable client, notify the PD clinician, collect the specified effluent studies before the first antibiotic dose without dangerous delay, start prescribed empiric therapy promptly, and then reassess clinical response and results to refine treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"混浊透出液伴腹痛需要迅速评估腹透相关腹膜炎。针对病情稳定的患者，按照题干给出的流程，应先通知腹透临床医生，在不造成危险延误的情况下于首次抗生素前采集指定透出液检查，然后立即开始医嘱经验性治疗，最后根据临床反应和结果调整治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the dependency stated in the stem: activate the PD pathway, preserve diagnostic yield, avoid treatment delay, then evaluate response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干明确的依赖关系：启动腹透流程、保留诊断价值、避免治疗延误，然后评价反应。","sourceMetadata":"International Society for Peritoneal Dialysis (ISPD), Peritonitis guideline recommendations: 2022 update, diagnostic recommendations for PD effluent cell count/differential, Gram stain, and culture and recommendation to start empiric antibiotics as soon as possible after appropriate microbiologic specimens are obtained: https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/08968608221080586","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2129,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_hl_intrapartum_fetal_monitoring_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.659","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.659.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.659.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[278,326],"terminalOffsetsZh":[80,92],"fullStemEn":"During labor, a previously normal fetal heart tracing develops a single prolonged deceleration/acute bradycardia that has lasted 3 minutes. Oxytocin is infusing. The unit pathway follows NICE guidance for acute bradycardia or a prolonged deceleration lasting 3 minutes or more. Highlight the actions supported by this pathway.","fullStemZh":"分娩过程中，原本正常的胎心监护出现一次持续3分钟的延长减速/急性心动过缓。正在输注催产素。科室流程遵循NICE关于持续3分钟或以上急性心动过缓或延长减速的指导。请标出该流程支持的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions supported by this pathway.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出该流程支持的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The unit pathway follows NICE guidance for acute bradycardia or a prolonged deceleration lasting 3 minutes or more.","penultimateSentenceZh":"科室流程遵循NICE关于持续3分钟或以上急性心动过缓或延长减速的指导。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q15_s_help","en":"Call for urgent obstetric review and assistance.","zh":"呼叫紧急产科评估和协助。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_event","en":"Rapidly assess for an acute event such as cord prolapse or placental abruption.","zh":"迅速评估脐带脱垂或胎盘早剥等急性事件。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_stop","en":"Stop the oxytocin infusion.","zh":"停止催产素输注。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_position","en":"Reposition the laboring client and correct reversible maternal causes, including hypotension when present.","zh":"为产妇改变体位，并纠正可逆的母体原因，包括存在时的低血压。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_prepare","en":"Prepare for urgent birth if the abnormality persists while the rapid evaluation and corrective measures proceed.","zh":"在快速评估和纠正措施进行期间，如异常持续，应准备紧急分娩。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_wait","en":"Wait for the next routine 15-minute reassessment before notifying anyone.","zh":"等到下一次常规15分钟复评后再通知任何人。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_auto","en":"Proceed immediately to operative birth without first performing the rapid assessment or corrective measures.","zh":"不先进行快速评估或纠正措施，立即实施手术分娩。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s_increase","en":"Increase oxytocin to shorten labor.","zh":"增加催产素以缩短产程。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q15_s_help","q15_s_event","q15_s_stop","q15_s_position","q15_s_prepare"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At 3 minutes, acute bradycardia or a prolonged deceleration requires urgent obstetric review, assessment for an acute cause, conservative measures such as stopping oxytocin and repositioning/correcting maternal hypotension, and preparation for urgent birth if the abnormality persists. The pathway does not support routine waiting or automatic operative delivery before rapid assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性心动过缓或延长减速达到3分钟时，需要紧急产科评估、寻找急性原因，并采取停止催产素、改变体位及纠正母体低血压等保守措施；如异常持续，应准备紧急分娩。流程不支持常规等待，也不支持在快速评估前自动实施手术分娩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"At the 3-minute threshold, choose simultaneous escalation, cause assessment, reversible-cause correction, and preparation—not passive waiting or an unassessed automatic procedure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"达到3分钟阈值时，应同时升级处理、评估原因、纠正可逆因素并准备分娩，而不是被动等待或未经评估就自动操作。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, Fetal monitoring in labour, Recommendations 1.5.9–1.5.11 on acute bradycardia or a single prolonged deceleration lasting 3 minutes or more, urgent obstetric review, assessment for acute events, conservative measures including stopping oxytocin and repositioning/correcting hypotension, preparation for urgent birth, and expedited birth if persistence continues: https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2130,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_hl_disaster_emergency_preparedness_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.660","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.660.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.660.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,271],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,74],"fullStemEn":"A hospital is under a municipal boil-water advisory and has activated its emergency water plan. Highlight the actions consistent with the plan. Apply restrictions according to the intended use and patient risk; do not assume every possible use of tap water is prohibited.","fullStemZh":"医院所在市政区域发布了煮沸用水警示，医院已启动紧急供水计划。请标出符合计划的行动。应根据用水目的和患者风险实施限制，不要假设所有自来水用途都被禁止。","terminalSentenceEn":"Apply restrictions according to the intended use and patient risk; do not assume every possible use of tap water is prohibited.","terminalSentenceZh":"应根据用水目的和患者风险实施限制，不要假设所有自来水用途都被禁止。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions consistent with the plan.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请标出符合计划的行动。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q16_s_drink","en":"Stop using tap water and ordinary ice for drinking; provide bottled or appropriately disinfected water.","zh":"停止使用自来水和普通冰块饮用，提供瓶装水或经过适当消毒的水。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_wound","en":"Use water that meets the emergency plan’s safe-water requirements for wound care.","zh":"伤口护理使用符合紧急计划安全水要求的水。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_equipment","en":"Use safe water for equipment and procedures identified in the emergency water plan.","zh":"对紧急供水计划指定的设备和操作使用安全水。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_notify","en":"Notify patients, visitors, and affected departments about the advisory and approved water sources.","zh":"通知患者、访客和受影响部门有关警示及获准使用的水源。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_sterile","en":"Suspend sterile processing if the required water quality cannot be supplied.","zh":"如果无法提供所需水质，应暂停无菌处理。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_ice","en":"Continue serving ice made from the building’s untreated water system.","zh":"继续供应由建筑内未经处理的供水系统制成的冰。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_all","en":"Announce that tap water is forbidden for every use, regardless of the task or patient population.","zh":"宣布无论用途或患者群体如何，所有自来水用途一律禁止。","selectable":true},{"id":"q16_s_rinse","en":"Use untreated tap water to rinse an open surgical wound.","zh":"使用未经处理的自来水冲洗开放性手术伤口。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q16_s_drink","q16_s_wound","q16_s_equipment","q16_s_notify","q16_s_sterile"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"During a boil-water advisory, drinking water and ordinary ice must be replaced with bottled or appropriately disinfected water. Wound care and specified equipment require safe water. Affected users must be notified, and sterile processing must stop if required water quality cannot be maintained. Restrictions remain use- and risk-specific rather than an unsupported claim that every tap-water use is prohibited.","rationaleCorrectZh":"煮沸用水警示期间，饮用水和普通冰块必须改用瓶装水或经过适当消毒的水。伤口护理和指定设备需要安全用水。必须通知受影响人员；若不能维持所需水质，应停止无菌处理。限制应根据用途和风险制定，而不是无依据地声称所有自来水用途都被禁止。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the water source to the clinical use: drinking, wounds, equipment, and sterile processing have specific safety requirements.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把水源与临床用途匹配：饮用、伤口、设备和无菌处理各有具体安全要求。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Guidance for Healthcare Water System Repair and Recovery Following a Boil Water Alert or Disruption of Water Supply, sections on drinking water and ice, wound care, equipment, communication, and sterile processing: https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/reopen-health-facilities/water-system-repair.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2131,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_or_ppe_sterile_technique_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.661","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.661.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.661.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[507,532],"terminalOffsetsZh":[144,151],"fullStemEn":"A nurse with facial hair crossing the sealing surface is assigned to enter an airborne-infection room. The tight-fitting respirator cannot achieve an acceptable seal. The facility respiratory-protection pathway states: do not enter with the failed tight-fitting respirator; notify the respiratory-protection lead; obtain an approved alternative such as a loose-fitting powered air-purifying respirator (PAPR) and complete required inspection and training; then enter using the correctly assembled ensemble. Place the steps in order.","fullStemZh":"一名护士的面部毛发穿过密合面，需要进入空气传播感染病房。紧密贴合式呼吸器无法达到可接受密封。机构呼吸防护流程规定：不要佩戴密封失败的紧密贴合式呼吸器进入；通知呼吸防护负责人；获得获准替代设备（如宽松型动力送风过滤式呼吸器PAPR）并完成所需检查和培训；然后使用正确组装的整套防护装备进入。请按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility respiratory-protection pathway states: do not enter with the failed tight-fitting respirator; notify the respiratory-protection lead; obtain an approved alternative such as a loose-fitting powered air-purifying respirator (PAPR) and complete required inspection and training; then enter using the correctly assembled ensemble.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构呼吸防护流程规定：不要佩戴密封失败的紧密贴合式呼吸器进入；通知呼吸防护负责人；获得获准替代设备（如宽松型动力送风过滤式呼吸器PAPR）并完成所需检查和培训；然后使用正确组装的整套防护装备进入。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q17_step_notify","en":"Notify the facility respiratory-protection lead.","zh":"通知机构呼吸防护负责人。"},{"id":"q17_step_alt","en":"Obtain the approved alternative respirator and complete required inspection and training.","zh":"获得获准替代呼吸器并完成所需检查和培训。"},{"id":"q17_step_enter","en":"Enter the room only after correctly donning and using the approved ensemble.","zh":"仅在正确穿戴并使用获准整套装备后进入病房。"},{"id":"q17_step_stop","en":"Do not enter the room using the tight-fitting respirator that failed to seal.","zh":"不要佩戴密封失败的紧密贴合式呼吸器进入病房。"}],"correct":["q17_step_stop","q17_step_notify","q17_step_alt","q17_step_enter"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Facial hair that crosses a tight-fitting respirator’s sealing surface prevents compliant use. The nurse should not enter with the failed respirator, should activate the facility respiratory-protection process, obtain and prepare an approved alternative such as a loose-fitting PAPR, and enter only after correct use of the complete ensemble. Shaving is not the only possible accommodation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"穿过紧密贴合式呼吸器密合面的面部毛发会使其不符合使用要求。护士不得佩戴密封失败的呼吸器进入，应启动机构呼吸防护流程，获得并准备获准替代设备（如宽松型PAPR），并仅在正确使用整套装备后进入。剃须不是唯一可能的安排。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The safety dependency is simple: prevent exposure first, activate the program, prepare a valid alternative, then enter.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全依赖关系很清楚：先防止暴露，再启动项目、准备有效替代设备，最后进入。","sourceMetadata":"OSHA, Facial Hair Under Seal of Tight-fitting Respirator, interpretation prohibiting facial hair between the sealing surface and face: https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/standardinterpretations/2012-09-14 ; OSHA 29 CFR 1910.134(c)(1), (d)(1), (g)(1)(i)(A), and (k), including the written respiratory-protection program, selection of an appropriate respirator, prohibition on tight-fitting use when facial hair crosses the seal, loose-fitting PAPR classifications, inspection, and training: https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.134","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The facility respiratory-protection pathway states: do not enter with the failed tight-fitting respirator; notify the respiratory-protection lead; obtain an approved alternative such as a loose-fitting powered air-purifying respirator (PAPR) and complete required inspection and training; then enter using the correctly assembled ensemble.","controlSentenceZh":"机构呼吸防护流程规定：不要佩戴密封失败的紧密贴合式呼吸器进入；通知呼吸防护负责人；获得获准替代设备（如宽松型动力送风过滤式呼吸器PAPR）并完成所需检查和培训；然后使用正确组装的整套防护装备进入。"}
{"queueIndex":2132,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6a_2026_07_16_mx_ppe_sterile_technique_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.662","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"PPE & Sterile Technique","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.662.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.662.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[213,333],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,96],"fullStemEn":"Before a sterile procedure, classify each wrapped-set finding under event-related sterility. An apparently old but intact package remains subject to facility dating policy; age alone does not prove contamination. An external chemical indicator shows that a package was exposed to a process, but it does not by itself prove sterility.","fullStemZh":"无菌操作前，请根据事件相关无菌原则对每项包装器械发现进行分类。看起来较旧但完整的包装仍受机构日期政策约束；仅凭存放时间不能证明污染。外部化学指示剂只能显示包装经历了处理过程，本身不能证明无菌。","terminalSentenceEn":"An external chemical indicator shows that a package was exposed to a process, but it does not by itself prove sterility.","terminalSentenceZh":"外部化学指示剂只能显示包装经历了处理过程，本身不能证明无菌。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An apparently old but intact package remains subject to facility dating policy; age alone does not prove contamination.","penultimateSentenceZh":"看起来较旧但完整的包装仍受机构日期政策约束；仅凭存放时间不能证明污染。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q18_r_intact","en":"The package is dry and intact, the seal is intact, and the indicator result is acceptable under facility policy.","zh":"包装干燥完整、密封完好，且指示剂结果符合机构政策。"},{"id":"q18_r_wet","en":"The package is wet.","zh":"包装潮湿。"},{"id":"q18_r_torn","en":"The wrap is torn or punctured.","zh":"包装材料撕裂或穿孔。"},{"id":"q18_r_seal","en":"The seal is broken.","zh":"密封破损。"},{"id":"q18_r_container","en":"The rigid sterilization container is visibly damaged.","zh":"硬质灭菌容器有可见损坏。"},{"id":"q18_r_old","en":"The package appears old but is dry, intact, sealed, and still acceptable under the facility’s dating policy.","zh":"包装看起来较旧，但干燥、完整、密封良好，且仍符合机构日期政策。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q18_c_not","en":"Not usable","zh":"不可使用"},{"id":"q18_c_usable","en":"Usable","zh":"可使用"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q18_r_intact","columnIds":["q18_c_usable"]},{"rowId":"q18_r_wet","columnIds":["q18_c_not"]},{"rowId":"q18_r_torn","columnIds":["q18_c_not"]},{"rowId":"q18_r_seal","columnIds":["q18_c_not"]},{"rowId":"q18_r_container","columnIds":["q18_c_not"]},{"rowId":"q18_r_old","columnIds":["q18_c_usable"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Event-related sterility depends on package integrity and exposure to compromising events. A dry, intact, sealed package that meets facility policy may be used even if it appears old. Wetness, tears, punctures, a broken seal, or container damage compromise the package. An external indicator alone does not establish sterility.","rationaleCorrectZh":"事件相关无菌性取决于包装完整性以及是否发生破坏性事件。干燥、完整、密封良好并符合机构政策的包装即使看起来较旧也可使用。潮湿、撕裂、穿孔、密封破损或容器损坏都会破坏包装。仅有外部指示剂不能证明无菌。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Judge the sterile barrier, not appearance alone: wet, open, torn, punctured, or damaged means not usable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断无菌屏障，而不是只看外观：潮湿、开启、撕裂、穿孔或损坏均不可使用。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Sterilizing Practices, event-related shelf life, package integrity, wet/torn/punctured packages, broken seals, and the limitation of external chemical indicators: https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/disinfection-sterilization/sterilizing-practices.html ; CDC Guideline for Disinfection and Sterilization in Healthcare Facilities, packaging and event-related sterility: https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/154498/cdc_154498_DS1.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2133,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_hl_client_advocacy_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.663","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.663.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.663.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[233,305],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,89],"fullStemEn":"During an adult sexual-assault medical forensic examination, the client previously agreed to medical care and selected evidence-collection procedures. The client now says, ‘Stop—I do not want the genital examination or photographs.’ Highlight the trauma-informed actions the nurse or examiner should take.","fullStemZh":"在成人性侵害医学法医检查过程中，患者先前同意接受医疗护理和部分证据采集程序。患者现在说：“停下——我不想做生殖器检查，也不想拍照。”请标出护士或检查人员应采取的创伤知情照护行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the trauma-informed actions the nurse or examiner should take.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出护士或检查人员应采取的创伤知情照护行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client now says, ‘Stop—I do not want the genital examination or photographs.’","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者现在说：“停下——我不想做生殖器检查，也不想拍照。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q01_s01","en":"Stop the genital examination and photography immediately.","zh":"立即停止生殖器检查和拍照。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s02","en":"Ask which parts of the examination and medical care the client still wants to receive.","zh":"询问患者目前仍希望接受哪些检查和医疗护理。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s03","en":"Explain available options and possible evidence consequences neutrally, without pressuring the client to continue.","zh":"以中立方式说明可选方案以及可能对证据采集造成的影响，不施压要求患者继续。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s04","en":"Document the procedures currently accepted and the procedures declined or stopped.","zh":"记录患者目前同意的程序，以及拒绝或要求停止的程序。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s05","en":"Continue the medical care the client wants, including indicated STI care, whether or not the client completes evidence collection or reports to law enforcement.","zh":"继续提供患者希望接受的医疗护理，包括有指征的性传播感染（STI）护理，不以完成证据采集或向执法部门报案为条件。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s06","en":"Tell the client that photographs are required once the evidence-collection process has begun.","zh":"告诉患者，一旦开始证据采集，拍照就是必须完成的。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s07","en":"Delay STI treatment until the client decides whether to make a police report.","zh":"在患者决定是否报警之前，暂缓性传播感染治疗。","selectable":true},{"id":"q01_s08","en":"Ask the support person to authorize the declined portions so the examination can be completed.","zh":"请陪同支持者代为授权患者已拒绝的部分，以便完成检查。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q01_s01","q01_s02","q01_s03","q01_s04","q01_s05"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Consent for a sexual-assault medical forensic examination is ongoing and procedure-specific. The examiner stops any declined portion, confirms the client's present choices, explains options without coercion, documents the scope of consent, and continues desired medical care independently of evidence collection or law-enforcement reporting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"性侵害医学法医检查的同意是持续性的，并且针对具体程序。检查人员应停止患者拒绝的部分，确认患者当前选择，在不施压的情况下说明方案，记录同意范围，并且不把证据采集或报警作为继续普通医疗护理的条件。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a capable client changes consent during an examination, prioritize stopping the declined portion and preserving voluntary, procedure-specific choice.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当有决策能力的患者在检查中改变同意时，应优先停止其拒绝的部分，并维护自愿、针对具体程序的选择。","sourceMetadata":"U.S. DOJ Office on Violence Against Women, National Protocol for Sexual Assault Medical Forensic Examinations—Adults/Adolescents, informed-consent and scope-of-examination sections, https://www.justice.gov/ovw/media/1367191/dl","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2134,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_hl_client_advocacy_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.664","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Client Advocacy","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.664.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.664.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[242,306],"terminalOffsetsZh":[76,117],"fullStemEn":"An alert adult with an intellectual disability is comparing two treatment options. No guardian or contrary legal order applies. The client asks a chosen supporter to help understand the options but says, ‘I want to make the decision myself.’ Highlight the actions consistent with supported decision-making.","fullStemZh":"一位清醒的智力障碍成年患者正在比较两种治疗方案。目前没有监护人，也没有相反的法律命令。患者希望由自己选择的支持者帮助理解方案，但说：“我想自己作决定。”请标出符合支持性决策（supported decision-making）的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions consistent with supported decision-making.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合支持性决策（supported decision-making）的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client asks a chosen supporter to help understand the options but says, ‘I want to make the decision myself.’","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者希望由自己选择的支持者帮助理解方案，但说：“我想自己作决定。”","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q02_s01","en":"Ask the client what kind of help is wanted from the supporter.","zh":"询问患者希望支持者提供哪种帮助。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s02","en":"Present the treatment information in an accessible format and check the client's understanding.","zh":"以患者容易理解的形式提供治疗信息，并确认患者的理解。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s03","en":"Allow the chosen supporter to assist with understanding or communication as the client requests.","zh":"按照患者的要求，允许其选择的支持者协助理解或沟通。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s04","en":"Direct the consent discussion and decision questions to the client.","zh":"将同意讨论和决策问题直接面向患者。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s05","en":"Document the decision made by the client and the support used.","zh":"记录患者本人作出的决定以及使用的支持方式。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s06","en":"Ask the supporter to choose the treatment because the client has an intellectual-disability diagnosis.","zh":"因为患者有智力障碍诊断，要求支持者替患者选择治疗。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s07","en":"Have the supporter sign the consent form instead of the client.","zh":"让支持者代替患者签署同意书。","selectable":true},{"id":"q02_s08","en":"Exclude the supporter even though the client requested assistance.","zh":"即使患者要求获得帮助，也排除支持者参与。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q02_s01","q02_s02","q02_s03","q02_s04","q02_s05"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Supported decision-making helps a person understand, communicate, and weigh choices while the person retains decision authority. The diagnosis alone does not transfer authority to the supporter or establish incapacity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"支持性决策帮助个人理解、沟通和权衡选择，但决策权仍由本人保留。仅凭智力障碍诊断，不能把权力转移给支持者，也不能据此认定患者无决策能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate assistance from authority: support can improve understanding, but the capable client still makes the decision.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分“协助”和“权力”：支持可以帮助理解，但有决策能力的患者仍由本人作决定。","sourceMetadata":"HHS Administration for Community Living, Supported Decision-Making Program, definition, chosen supporters, and retained decision authority, https://acl.gov/programs/consumer-control/supported-decision-making-program","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2135,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_mx_conflict_resolution_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.665","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.665.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.665.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,179],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,58],"fullStemEn":"A nursing unit is redesigning its staff schedule. For each team statement, classify the conflict behavior as constructive and task-focused or destructive and relationship-focused.","fullStemZh":"一个护理单元正在重新设计人员排班。请将每条团队陈述分类为“建设性、聚焦任务的冲突”或“破坏性、聚焦人际关系的冲突”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each team statement, classify the conflict behavior as constructive and task-focused or destructive and relationship-focused.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每条团队陈述分类为“建设性、聚焦任务的冲突”或“破坏性、聚焦人际关系的冲突”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nursing unit is redesigning its staff schedule.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一个护理单元正在重新设计人员排班。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q03_r01","en":"‘Last quarter, 18% of evening shifts needed last-minute coverage. Can we compare how each proposal addresses that gap?’","zh":"“上季度有18%的晚班需要临时补人。我们能否比较每个方案如何解决这个缺口？”"},{"id":"q03_r02","en":"‘Our shared goal is reliable coverage with a fair weekend rotation.’","zh":"“我们的共同目标是在公平轮转周末班的同时确保可靠覆盖。”"},{"id":"q03_r03","en":"‘What concern do you have about rotating every third weekend?’","zh":"“你对每三个周末轮一次班有什么顾虑？”"},{"id":"q03_r04","en":"‘Let us pilot the two schedules for four weeks and compare uncovered shifts and overtime.’","zh":"“我们可以分别试行这两种排班四周，再比较缺班和加班情况。”"},{"id":"q03_r05","en":"‘You oppose this only because you hate change.’","zh":"“你反对这个方案只是因为你讨厌改变。”"},{"id":"q03_r06","en":"‘Anyone competent could see that your schedule is a bad idea.’","zh":"“任何有能力的人都能看出你的排班方案很糟糕。”"},{"id":"q03_r07","en":"‘I already asked the night staff to vote against Jordan's proposal.’","zh":"“我已经让夜班员工一起投票反对Jordan的方案。”"},{"id":"q03_r08","en":"‘I will not discuss data presented by someone who never works hard.’","zh":"“我不会讨论一个从不努力工作的人提供的数据。”"}],"columns":[{"id":"q03_c01","en":"Constructive, task-focused conflict","zh":"建设性、聚焦任务的冲突"},{"id":"q03_c02","en":"Destructive, relationship-focused conflict","zh":"破坏性、聚焦人际关系的冲突"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q03_r01","columnIds":["q03_c01"]},{"rowId":"q03_r02","columnIds":["q03_c01"]},{"rowId":"q03_r03","columnIds":["q03_c01"]},{"rowId":"q03_r04","columnIds":["q03_c01"]},{"rowId":"q03_r05","columnIds":["q03_c02"]},{"rowId":"q03_r06","columnIds":["q03_c02"]},{"rowId":"q03_r07","columnIds":["q03_c02"]},{"rowId":"q03_r08","columnIds":["q03_c02"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Constructive task conflict uses observable information, shared goals, curiosity, and testable solutions. Destructive relationship conflict attacks motives or competence, organizes opposition against a person, or refuses evidence-based discussion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"建设性的任务冲突使用可观察的信息、共同目标、好奇提问和可检验的解决方案。破坏性的人际关系冲突会攻击动机或能力、拉拢他人反对某个人，或拒绝基于证据的讨论。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for language about data, goals, questions, and experiments versus language that attacks the person or motive.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找关于数据、目标、提问和试验的语言，并与攻击个人或动机的语言区分开。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ TeamSTEPPS, Managing Conflict tool, task-focused conflict and constructive conflict-management behaviors, https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/mutual/tools/conflict.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2136,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_or_conflict_resolution_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.666","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Conflict Resolution","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.666.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.666.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[409,449],"terminalOffsetsZh":[126,133],"fullStemEn":"A secure text thread between two disciplines has become sarcastic and ambiguous. No urgent client danger is present. The facility repair sequence is: pause the escalating asynchronous exchange; move to a brief synchronous huddle; each person states the concern and relevant facts while the other confirms understanding; agree on one plan, owner, and deadline; then send a concise closed-loop written summary. Place the actions in the required order.","fullStemZh":"两个专业团队之间的安全短信对话已经变得讽刺且含糊。目前没有紧急患者危险。机构规定的修复顺序是：暂停不断升级的异步交流；转为简短的同步碰头会；双方分别陈述问题和相关事实，同时由对方确认理解；共同确定一个计划、负责人和截止时间；最后发送简明的闭环书面总结。请按要求排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in the required order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按要求排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility repair sequence is: pause the escalating asynchronous exchange; move to a brief synchronous huddle; each person states the concern and relevant facts while the other confirms understanding; agree on one plan, owner, and deadline; then send a concise closed-loop written summary.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构规定的修复顺序是：暂停不断升级的异步交流；转为简短的同步碰头会；双方分别陈述问题和相关事实，同时由对方确认理解；共同确定一个计划、负责人和截止时间；最后发送简明的闭环书面总结。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q04_o03","en":"Each person states the concern and relevant facts; the other person confirms what was understood.","zh":"双方分别陈述问题和相关事实；另一方确认自己所理解的内容。"},{"id":"q04_o05","en":"Send a concise written summary that closes the loop.","zh":"发送简明的书面总结，完成闭环沟通。"},{"id":"q04_o02","en":"Move the discussion to a brief synchronous huddle.","zh":"将讨论转为简短的同步碰头会。"},{"id":"q04_o04","en":"Agree on one plan, the responsible owner, and a deadline.","zh":"共同确定一个计划、负责人和截止时间。"},{"id":"q04_o01","en":"Pause the escalating secure-text exchange.","zh":"暂停不断升级的安全短信交流。"}],"correct":["q04_o01","q04_o02","q04_o03","q04_o04","q04_o05"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sequence first stops the communication channel that is escalating conflict, then uses a synchronous huddle to clarify facts and confirm understanding. The team next assigns a specific plan, owner, and deadline, and only then sends the written closed-loop summary.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该顺序首先停止正在加剧冲突的沟通渠道，然后通过同步碰头会澄清事实并确认理解。接着团队确定具体计划、负责人和截止时间，最后才发送书面闭环总结。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a communication-repair sequence, stop escalation first, establish mutual understanding next, decide responsibility, and document last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于沟通修复顺序，应先停止升级，再建立共同理解，然后确定责任，最后记录。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ TeamSTEPPS, Huddle tool and Check-Back/Closed-Loop Communication tool, https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/team/tools/huddle.html; https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/communication/tools/loop.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2137,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_dc_confidentiality_hipaa_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.667","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.667.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.667.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,68],"fullStemEn":"A consulting psychiatrist requests separately maintained psychotherapy session notes from another clinician. No listed HIPAA exception for use or disclosure of psychotherapy notes applies. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一位会诊精神科医生向另一位临床人员索取单独保存的心理治疗会谈笔记。目前不适用HIPAA列出的任何心理治疗笔记使用或披露例外。请完成陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"No listed HIPAA exception for use or disclosure of psychotherapy notes applies.","penultimateSentenceZh":"目前不适用HIPAA列出的任何心理治疗笔记使用或披露例外。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Disclosure of these separately maintained notes generally requires the client's {{q05_d01}}; the fact that the requesting psychiatrist will use them for {{q05_d02}} does not by itself remove that requirement.","zh":"披露这些单独保存的笔记通常需要患者的{{q05_d01}}；请求方精神科医生将其用于{{q05_d02}}这一事实本身并不能取消该要求。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q05_d01","options":[{"id":"q05_d01_o03","en":"no authorization because both people are clinicians","zh":"无需授权，因为双方都是临床人员"},{"id":"q05_d01_o02","en":"verbal permission documented by the requester","zh":"由请求方记录的口头许可"},{"id":"q05_d01_o01","en":"valid written authorization","zh":"有效的书面授权"}],"correct":"q05_d01_o01"},{"id":"q05_d02","options":[{"id":"q05_d02_o01","en":"treatment","zh":"治疗"},{"id":"q05_d02_o03","en":"facility directory management","zh":"机构名录管理"},{"id":"q05_d02_o02","en":"appointment scheduling","zh":"预约安排"}],"correct":"q05_d02_o01"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Psychotherapy notes that are maintained separately from the medical record receive special HIPAA protection. With no applicable exception, disclosure requires the client's valid written authorization even when another provider requests the notes for treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与普通病历分开保存的心理治疗笔记受到HIPAA的特殊保护。在没有适用例外时，即使另一位医护人员为治疗目的请求这些笔记，也需要患者有效的书面授权。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify whether the request concerns ordinary mental-health information or separately maintained psychotherapy notes; the latter have a stricter authorization rule.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断请求的是普通精神健康信息，还是单独保存的心理治疗笔记；后者适用更严格的授权规则。","sourceMetadata":"HHS Office for Civil Rights, FAQ 558, disclosure of psychotherapy notes through an HIO and the treatment-purpose authorization rule, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/558/does-hipaa-permit-a-covered-entity-to-disclose-psychotherapy-notes-to-an-hio/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"No listed HIPAA exception for use or disclosure of psychotherapy notes applies.","controlSentenceZh":"目前不适用HIPAA列出的任何心理治疗笔记使用或披露例外。"}
{"queueIndex":2138,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_hl_confidentiality_hipaa_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.668","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.668.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.668.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,46],"fullStemEn":"A clinic is reviewing its waiting-room sign-in and name-calling process. Highlight the entries and safeguards consistent with HIPAA's incidental-disclosure rule.","fullStemZh":"一家门诊正在审查候诊室签到和叫名流程。请标出符合HIPAA附带披露规则的签到内容和保护措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the entries and safeguards consistent with HIPAA's incidental-disclosure rule.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合HIPAA附带披露规则的签到内容和保护措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A clinic is reviewing its waiting-room sign-in and name-calling process.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一家门诊正在审查候诊室签到和叫名流程。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q06_s01","en":"The sign-in sheet requests only the client's name and arrival time.","zh":"签到表只要求填写患者姓名和到达时间。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s02","en":"The sheet omits the diagnosis and detailed reason for the visit.","zh":"签到表不填写诊断和详细就诊原因。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s03","en":"The clipboard is positioned and handled to limit casual viewing of earlier entries.","zh":"合理放置和管理签到夹，减少他人随意看到先前条目的机会。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s04","en":"Staff call the client's name without announcing clinical details.","zh":"工作人员叫患者姓名，但不宣布临床细节。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s05","en":"The sheet asks each client to write the suspected diagnosis beside the name.","zh":"签到表要求每位患者在姓名旁写下疑似诊断。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s06","en":"The completed sheet remains fully visible on the counter throughout the day.","zh":"已填写的签到表整天完全暴露在柜台上。","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s07","en":"Staff announce, ‘Ms. Chen, the diabetes educator is ready for you.’","zh":"工作人员宣布：“陈女士，糖尿病教育员可以接待您了。”","selectable":true},{"id":"q06_s08","en":"The clinic bans all sign-in sheets and all use of client names in the waiting room.","zh":"门诊禁止所有签到表，并禁止在候诊室使用患者姓名。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q06_s01","q06_s02","q06_s03","q06_s04"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA permits sign-in sheets and calling a client's name when only limited information is used and reasonable safeguards reduce unnecessary disclosure. Diagnosis and detailed visit information should not be exposed in the waiting room.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA允许使用签到表和叫患者姓名，前提是只使用有限信息，并采取合理保护措施减少不必要的披露。诊断和详细就诊信息不应在候诊室暴露。","testTakingStrategyEn":"HIPAA questions often turn on limiting information and using reasonable safeguards, not banning ordinary workflow altogether.","testTakingStrategyZh":"HIPAA题目常考“限制信息并采取合理保护措施”，而不是完全禁止日常工作流程。","sourceMetadata":"HHS Office for Civil Rights, FAQ 199, sign-in sheets and calling client names using limited information and reasonable safeguards, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/199/may-health-care-providers-use-sign-in-sheets/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2139,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_dc_confidentiality_hipaa_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.669","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Confidentiality & HIPAA","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.669.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.669.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,239],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,65],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalist asks whether the hospital may send relevant ordinary medical-record information to the specialist who will treat the same client. The request does not involve separately maintained psychotherapy notes. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一位住院医生询问，医院是否可以把相关的普通病历信息发送给将治疗同一患者的专科医生。该请求不涉及单独保存的心理治疗笔记。请完成陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The request does not involve separately maintained psychotherapy notes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该请求不涉及单独保存的心理治疗笔记。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"HIPAA {{q07_d01}} this provider-to-provider disclosure without the client's authorization, and the minimum-necessary requirement {{q07_d02}} to disclosures or requests between providers for treatment.","zh":"HIPAA{{q07_d01}}在没有患者授权的情况下进行这种医护提供者之间的披露；对于医护提供者之间为治疗目的进行的披露或请求，最低必要原则{{q07_d02}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q07_d01","options":[{"id":"q07_d01_o03","en":"permits only after a separate written authorization","zh":"仅在取得单独书面授权后允许"},{"id":"q07_d01_o02","en":"prohibits","zh":"禁止"},{"id":"q07_d01_o01","en":"permits","zh":"允许"}],"correct":"q07_d01_o01"},{"id":"q07_d02","options":[{"id":"q07_d02_o03","en":"applies only because the specialist is outside the hospital","zh":"仅因为专科医生不在本院而适用"},{"id":"q07_d02_o02","en":"requires limiting every disclosure to one page","zh":"要求每次披露限制为一页"},{"id":"q07_d02_o01","en":"does not apply","zh":"不适用"}],"correct":"q07_d02_o01"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"HIPAA allows covered providers to disclose relevant protected health information to another provider for treatment without the client's authorization. The minimum-necessary standard does not apply to disclosures or requests between providers for treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"HIPAA允许受监管的医护提供者在没有患者授权的情况下，为治疗目的向另一位医护提供者披露相关受保护健康信息。最低必要原则不适用于医护提供者之间为治疗目的进行的披露或请求。","testTakingStrategyEn":"First identify the purpose and record type: ordinary information for treatment follows a different rule from separately maintained psychotherapy notes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断用途和记录类型：为治疗目的共享普通信息，与单独保存的心理治疗笔记适用不同规则。","sourceMetadata":"HHS Office for Civil Rights, Treatment, Payment, and Health Care Operations Disclosures FAQs and FAQ 208 on provider-to-provider treatment disclosures and the minimum-necessary exception, https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/treatment-payment-and-health-care-operations-disclosures/index.html; https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/208/wont-minium-necessary-restriction-impede-delivery/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2140,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_bt_discharge_handoff_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.670","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.670.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.670.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[409,430],"terminalOffsetsZh":[115,123],"fullStemEn":"A ventilator-dependent child with a new tracheostomy is scheduled for a first discharge home tomorrow. One parent has completed routine tracheostomy care, but neither caregiver has successfully managed a simulated obstruction or accidental decannulation. Delivery of backup tracheostomy and ventilation equipment is unconfirmed, and no awake, attentive, trained caregiver is available for overnight coverage. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名依赖呼吸机、刚建立气管切开通道的儿童计划明天首次出院回家。一位家长已完成常规气管切开护理培训，但两位照护者都没有成功处理过模拟的气道阻塞或意外脱管。备用气管切开和通气设备的送达尚未确认，夜间也没有清醒、专注且受过培训的照护者。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Delivery of backup tracheostomy and ventilation equipment is unconfirmed, and no awake, attentive, trained caregiver is available for overnight coverage.","penultimateSentenceZh":"备用气管切开和通气设备的送达尚未确认，夜间也没有清醒、专注且受过培训的照护者。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely transition problem","zh":"最可能的转衔问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q08_c01","en":"Unsafe tracheostomy-home transition","zh":"不安全的气管切开居家转衔"},{"id":"q08_c03","en":"Ventilator-setting intolerance requiring a new prescription","zh":"无法耐受呼吸机设置，需要新的处方"},{"id":"q08_c02","en":"Routine discharge readiness with expected caregiver anxiety","zh":"已具备常规出院条件，仅有预期的照护者焦虑"}],"correct":"q08_c01"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q08_a02","en":"Confirm required backup equipment is delivered and functional and arrange awake, trained caregiver coverage for all required periods","zh":"确认所需备用设备已送达且功能正常，并为所有需要时段安排清醒且受过培训的照护者"},{"id":"q08_a01","en":"Delay and revise discharge until intended caregivers successfully demonstrate obstruction and decannulation emergency management","zh":"延迟并修订出院计划，直到预定照护者成功演示阻塞和脱管紧急处理"},{"id":"q08_a04","en":"Rely on emergency medical services as the primary response to obstruction or decannulation","zh":"把急救医疗服务作为发生阻塞或脱管时的主要应对方式"},{"id":"q08_a03","en":"Proceed because successful routine tracheostomy care proves emergency readiness","zh":"继续出院，因为能完成常规气管切开护理就证明已具备紧急处理能力"},{"id":"q08_a05","en":"Send the child home while equipment delivery and nighttime coverage remain pending","zh":"在设备送达和夜间照护仍未落实时让儿童回家"}],"correct":["q08_a01","q08_a02"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Readiness outcomes to verify","zh":"需要核实的准备结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"q08_p03","en":"A state-specific guarantee of a fixed number of home-nursing hours","zh":"由州政策保证固定数量的居家护理小时"},{"id":"q08_p01","en":"Successful caregiver simulation of obstruction and accidental decannulation management","zh":"照护者成功完成阻塞和意外脱管处理模拟"},{"id":"q08_p04","en":"The exact ventilator settings chosen by the learner","zh":"由答题者选择的具体呼吸机设置"},{"id":"q08_p05","en":"A lower caregiver-anxiety score without another skills demonstration","zh":"照护者焦虑评分下降，但未再次演示技能"},{"id":"q08_p02","en":"Verified backup-equipment function and awake trained-caregiver coverage","zh":"已核实备用设备功能及清醒、受训照护者覆盖"}],"correct":["q08_p01","q08_p02"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The home transition is unsafe because emergency tracheostomy competence, backup equipment, and continuously available awake trained caregiving are not established. Discharge should be delayed or revised until emergency skills and the required home support system are verified.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该居家转衔不安全，因为尚未确认气管切开紧急处理能力、备用设备以及持续可用的清醒受训照护者。应延迟或修订出院计划，直到紧急技能和所需居家支持系统得到核实。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For technology-dependent pediatric discharge, distinguish routine-task teaching from demonstrated emergency competence and verified around-the-clock support.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于依赖医疗技术的儿童出院，应区分常规任务培训与经演示验证的紧急能力及全天候支持。","sourceMetadata":"American Thoracic Society, Care of Infants and Children with Tracheostomies, Recommendation 2, Table 2, emergency training competencies, and awake-attentive-trained-caregiver recommendation, https://academic.oup.com/ajrccm/article/211/11/2001/8444168","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2141,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_bt_discharge_handoff_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.671","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.671.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.671.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[390,411],"terminalOffsetsZh":[113,121],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalized client receives maintenance methadone for opioid use disorder and will leave Friday evening. The listed opioid treatment program (OTP) has not accepted the handoff, the weekend dosing plan is unknown, and the client's last verified hospital dose and administration time have not been transmitted. The client has consented to the facility's direct OTP communication workflow. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一位因阿片类药物使用障碍而接受美沙酮维持治疗的住院患者将在周五晚上出院。列出的阿片类药物治疗项目（OTP）尚未接受交接，周末给药计划未知，患者在医院最后一次经核实的剂量和给药时间尚未传送。患者已同意机构与OTP直接沟通的流程。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has consented to the facility's direct OTP communication workflow.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者已同意机构与OTP直接沟通的流程。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely continuity problem","zh":"最可能的连续性问题"},"tokens":[{"id":"q09_c03","en":"Confirmed duplicate outpatient methadone dosing","zh":"已确认门诊美沙酮重复给药"},{"id":"q09_c01","en":"Threatened interruption in medication for opioid use disorder continuity","zh":"阿片类药物使用障碍药物治疗连续性受到威胁"},{"id":"q09_c02","en":"Expected completion of methadone therapy at hospital discharge","zh":"美沙酮治疗将在出院时按预期结束"}],"correct":"q09_c01"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take before discharge","zh":"出院前应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q09_a04","en":"Choose a universal restart dose for the OTP to use if the client misses a day","zh":"为OTP选择一个通用的漏服后重新开始剂量"},{"id":"q09_a05","en":"Discharge the client with instructions to visit an emergency department if withdrawal begins","zh":"让患者出院，并告知若出现戒断再去急诊科"},{"id":"q09_a02","en":"Transmit the verified methadone regimen and the exact last hospital dose and administration time through the approved workflow","zh":"通过获批流程传送经核实的美沙酮方案以及医院最后一次给药的准确剂量和时间"},{"id":"q09_a03","en":"Have the hospital independently prescribe an outpatient weekend methadone supply","zh":"由医院独立开具周末门诊美沙酮供应处方"},{"id":"q09_a01","en":"Obtain direct OTP acceptance and confirm the Friday-evening or weekend dosing plan","zh":"取得OTP直接接受交接的确认，并确认周五晚间或周末给药计划"}],"correct":["q09_a01","q09_a02"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Continuity outcomes to verify","zh":"需要核实的连续性结果"},"tokens":[{"id":"q09_p04","en":"A lower pain score after the last hospital dose","zh":"医院最后一次给药后疼痛评分下降"},{"id":"q09_p01","en":"Confirmed date, time, and location of the next OTP dosing encounter","zh":"已确认下一次OTP给药的日期、时间和地点"},{"id":"q09_p03","en":"A negative urine drug screen before discharge","zh":"出院前尿液药物筛查阴性"},{"id":"q09_p05","en":"Use of the same restart dose for every client after any missed dose","zh":"所有患者漏服后都使用同一个重新开始剂量"},{"id":"q09_p02","en":"No unintended gap between the last hospital dose and the next verified dose","zh":"医院最后一次给药与下一次核实给药之间没有非预期中断"}],"correct":["q09_p01","q09_p02"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The incomplete OTP handoff threatens an unintended interruption in medication for opioid use disorder. Direct acceptance, a confirmed dosing plan, and transmission of the verified regimen and last-dose information are needed before discharge; continuity is verified by the next dosing encounter and absence of a medication gap.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未完成的OTP交接会造成阿片类药物使用障碍药物治疗的非预期中断。出院前需要取得直接接受、确认给药计划，并传送经核实的方案和最后一次给药信息；通过下一次给药安排以及没有用药空档来核实连续性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For discharge medications that depend on a specialized receiving program, verify acceptance, exact last-dose communication, and the next actual encounter—not merely a referral name.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于依赖专门接收项目的出院用药，应核实接受交接、准确传送最后一次给药信息以及下一次实际就诊，而不仅是列出转诊机构名称。","sourceMetadata":"SAMHSA, Advisory: Expanding Access to Methadone Treatment in Hospital Settings, hospital-to-OTP continuity and discharge coordination, https://library.samhsa.gov/product/advisory-expanding-access-methadone-treatment-hospital-settings/pep25-02-007; SAMHSA, Federal Guidelines for Opioid Treatment Programs, medication-continuity discussion pp. 30–31, https://library.samhsa.gov/sites/default/files/federal-guidelines-opioid-treatment-pep24-02-011.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2142,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_hl_caregiver_role_strain_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.672","itemType":"highlight","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.672.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.672.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[200,289],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,89],"fullStemEn":"A capable client wants both adult daughters involved after discharge. Each daughter believes the other is responsible for the evening medication setup and meal check, and repeated gaps have occurred. Highlight the actions that resolve caregiver-role ambiguity and create reliable coverage.","fullStemZh":"一位有决策能力的患者希望两位成年女儿都参与出院后的照护。每位女儿都认为另一位负责晚间摆药和查看进餐情况，因此已经多次出现照护空档。请标出能够解决照护角色不清并建立可靠覆盖的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions that resolve caregiver-role ambiguity and create reliable coverage.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出能够解决照护角色不清并建立可靠覆盖的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Each daughter believes the other is responsible for the evening medication setup and meal check, and repeated gaps have occurred.","penultimateSentenceZh":"每位女儿都认为另一位负责晚间摆药和查看进餐情况，因此已经多次出现照护空档。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q10_s01","en":"Confirm the client's permission, goals, and preferences for involving both daughters.","zh":"确认患者允许两位女儿参与，并了解患者的目标和偏好。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s02","en":"Meet with the client and both daughters together to review the recurring gaps.","zh":"与患者和两位女儿共同会面，回顾反复出现的照护空档。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s03","en":"Assign an accepted primary owner and backup person for each evening task.","zh":"为每项晚间任务指定各方接受的主要负责人和备用人员。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s04","en":"Create one shared schedule or log that requires closed-loop confirmation when a task is completed or handed off.","zh":"建立一个共享日程或记录表，任务完成或交接时必须进行闭环确认。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s05","en":"Verify that each daughter understands and can perform the role she accepts.","zh":"核实每位女儿理解并能够完成自己接受的角色。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s06","en":"Tell the daughters that the recent gaps occurred because neither one cares enough.","zh":"告诉两位女儿，最近的空档是因为她们都不够关心。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s07","en":"Accept the statement, ‘We will both help whenever possible,’ as sufficient coverage.","zh":"把“我们有空都会帮忙”视为足够的照护覆盖。","selectable":true},{"id":"q10_s08","en":"Require the client to choose one daughter and exclude the other from planning.","zh":"要求患者只选择一位女儿，并将另一位排除在计划之外。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q10_s01","q10_s02","q10_s03","q10_s04","q10_s05"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reliable shared caregiving requires the capable client's permission and preferences, explicit assignment of each task and backup, one shared closed-loop system, and verification that each person understands and can perform the accepted role. Vague promises and blame do not create coverage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可靠的共同照护需要尊重有决策能力患者的许可和偏好，明确每项任务及备用人员，使用统一的闭环系统，并核实每个人理解且能够履行所接受的角色。模糊承诺和责备都不能建立可靠覆盖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When shared caregiving fails, choose actions that replace assumptions with named ownership, backup coverage, and confirmation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当共同照护出现失败时，应选择用明确负责人、备用覆盖和确认机制取代相互假设的行动。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ IDEAL Discharge Planning, patient and family as full partners and attention to goals, preferences, observations, and concerns, https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/patients-families/engagingfamilies/strategy4/index.html; AHRQ Re-Engineered Discharge Toolkit, Tool 3, identifying actual caregivers who share responsibilities and confirming understanding, https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/settings/hospital/red/toolkit/redtool3.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2143,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_mx_caregiver_role_strain_11","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.673","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Caregiver Role Strain & Family Coping","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.673.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.673.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[145,230],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,66],"fullStemEn":"Before home discharge with a feeding pump, the caregiver says they are afraid and demonstrates several incorrect setup and alarm-response steps. Classify each team response according to whether it supports safe caregiver capacity.","fullStemZh":"在使用营养泵出院回家之前，照护者表示害怕，并在设备设置和报警处理演示中出现多处错误。请判断每项团队回应是否有助于建立安全的照护能力。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each team response according to whether it supports safe caregiver capacity.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断每项团队回应是否有助于建立安全的照护能力。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Before home discharge with a feeding pump, the caregiver says they are afraid and demonstrates several incorrect setup and alarm-response steps.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在使用营养泵出院回家之前，照护者表示害怕，并在设备设置和报警处理演示中出现多处错误。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q11_r01","en":"Listen to the caregiver's concerns and ask which steps feel most difficult.","zh":"倾听照护者的担忧，并询问哪些步骤最困难。"},{"id":"q11_r02","en":"Demonstrate the setup, then require the caregiver to perform teach-back using the actual pump.","zh":"演示设置过程，然后要求照护者使用实际营养泵进行回示。"},{"id":"q11_r03","en":"Retrain the incorrect alarm-response steps and repeat the skills demonstration.","zh":"重新训练错误的报警处理步骤，并重复技能演示。"},{"id":"q11_r04","en":"Simplify and adapt written or visual instructions to the caregiver's needs.","zh":"根据照护者需要简化和调整书面或图示说明。"},{"id":"q11_r05","en":"Reassess competence and revise the discharge plan if safe performance is not achieved.","zh":"重新评估能力；如果未达到安全操作要求，则修订出院计划。"},{"id":"q11_r06","en":"Say, ‘You should know this by now,’ to motivate better performance.","zh":"说“你现在早该会了”，以激励其表现得更好。"},{"id":"q11_r07","en":"Document the caregiver as ‘noncompliant’ without another assessment or training attempt.","zh":"在不再次评估或培训的情况下，把照护者记录为“不依从”。"},{"id":"q11_r08","en":"Give only the manufacturer's brochure and cancel the hands-on demonstration.","zh":"只提供厂家手册，并取消动手演示。"},{"id":"q11_r09","en":"Proceed with discharge because the supply company can answer questions later.","zh":"继续出院，因为供应公司以后可以回答问题。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q11_c01","en":"Supports safe caregiver capacity","zh":"有助于建立安全照护能力"},{"id":"q11_c02","en":"Does not support safe caregiver capacity","zh":"无助于建立安全照护能力"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q11_r01","columnIds":["q11_c01"]},{"rowId":"q11_r02","columnIds":["q11_c01"]},{"rowId":"q11_r03","columnIds":["q11_c01"]},{"rowId":"q11_r04","columnIds":["q11_c01"]},{"rowId":"q11_r05","columnIds":["q11_c01"]},{"rowId":"q11_r06","columnIds":["q11_c02"]},{"rowId":"q11_r07","columnIds":["q11_c02"]},{"rowId":"q11_r08","columnIds":["q11_c02"]},{"rowId":"q11_r09","columnIds":["q11_c02"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe home use requires listening, tailored education, demonstration and teach-back, retraining, and reassessment of actual performance. If competence is not achieved, the plan must change. Shame, labels, passive brochures, or deferred vendor support do not verify safe capacity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全居家使用需要倾听、个体化教育、演示与回示、重新训练以及对实际操作的再评估。如果未达到能力要求，必须改变计划。羞辱、贴标签、只发手册或把问题推迟给供应商，都不能核实安全能力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For home-device teaching, choose responses that measure actual performance and change the plan when competence is not demonstrated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于居家设备教学，应选择能够测量实际操作表现，并在能力未被证明时改变计划的回应。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ Re-Engineered Discharge Toolkit, Tool 3a, demonstration/teach-back and creating an alternative plan when understanding is not achieved, https://www.ahrq.gov/patient-safety/settings/hospital/red/toolkit/redtool3a.html; NICE Quality Standard QS24, Quality statement 4, self-management competency for artificial nutrition support, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/qs24/chapter/quality-statement-4-self-management-of-artificial-nutrition-support","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2144,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_dc_abg_acid_base_12","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.674","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.674.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.674.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[366,394],"terminalOffsetsZh":[241,247],"fullStemEn":"A client with diabetic ketoacidosis and repeated vomiting has: pH 7.31, PaCO2 27 mm Hg, HCO3 13 mEq/L, Na 140 mEq/L, and Cl 96 mEq/L. Use only these supplied rules: AG = Na − (Cl + HCO3); normal AG = 12 mEq/L. Delta AG = measured AG − 12. Corrected HCO3 = measured HCO3 + delta AG; supplied normal HCO3 range = 22–26 mEq/L. Expected PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg. Complete the interpretation.","fullStemZh":"一位糖尿病酮症酸中毒并反复呕吐的患者检查结果为：pH 7.31、PaCO2 27 mm Hg、HCO3 13 mEq/L、Na 140 mEq/L、Cl 96 mEq/L。仅使用以下给定规则：AG = Na −（Cl + HCO3）；正常AG = 12 mEq/L。Delta AG = 实测AG − 12。校正HCO3 = 实测HCO3 + delta AG；给定的正常HCO3范围 = 22–26 mEq/L。预期PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg。请完成判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the interpretation.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Expected PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"预期PaCO2 = 1.5(HCO3) + 8 ± 2 mm Hg。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The primary disorder is {{q12_d01}}. The measured PaCO2 represents {{q12_d02}}. The corrected HCO3 demonstrates {{q12_d03}}.","zh":"主要紊乱是{{q12_d01}}。实测PaCO2表示{{q12_d02}}。校正HCO3提示{{q12_d03}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"q12_d01","options":[{"id":"q12_d01_o02","en":"normal-anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"正常阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"q12_d01_o01","en":"high-anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"q12_d01_o03","en":"primary respiratory alkalosis","zh":"原发性呼吸性碱中毒"}],"correct":"q12_d01_o01"},{"id":"q12_d02","options":[{"id":"q12_d02_o02","en":"a concurrent respiratory acidosis","zh":"并存呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"q12_d02_o03","en":"a concurrent respiratory alkalosis","zh":"并存呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"q12_d02_o01","en":"appropriate respiratory compensation","zh":"适当的呼吸性代偿"}],"correct":"q12_d02_o01"},{"id":"q12_d03","options":[{"id":"q12_d03_o01","en":"a concurrent metabolic alkalosis","zh":"并存代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"q12_d03_o03","en":"a concurrent normal-anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"并存正常阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"},{"id":"q12_d03_o02","en":"no additional metabolic disorder","zh":"没有其他代谢性紊乱"}],"correct":"q12_d03_o01"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"AG = 140 − (96 + 13) = 31 mEq/L, confirming high-anion-gap metabolic acidosis. Expected PaCO2 is 1.5(13) + 8 ± 2 = 25.5–29.5 mm Hg; the measured 27 mm Hg is appropriate compensation. Delta AG is 31 − 12 = 19, so corrected HCO3 is 13 + 19 = 32 mEq/L, above the supplied 22–26 range and consistent with concurrent metabolic alkalosis from vomiting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"AG = 140 −（96 + 13）= 31 mEq/L，证实高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒。预期PaCO2为1.5（13）+ 8 ± 2，即25.5–29.5 mm Hg；实测27 mm Hg属于适当代偿。Delta AG = 31 − 12 = 19，因此校正HCO3 = 13 + 19 = 32 mEq/L，高于给定的22–26范围，符合反复呕吐导致的并存代谢性碱中毒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use all three calculations: anion gap identifies the primary metabolic process, expected PaCO2 tests compensation, and corrected HCO3 detects a second metabolic disorder.","testTakingStrategyZh":"同时使用三项计算：阴离子间隙判断主要代谢过程，预期PaCO2检验代偿，校正HCO3发现第二种代谢紊乱。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual Professional Edition, Metabolic Acidosis, anion gap, delta gap/corrected bicarbonate, and expected PaCO2 (Winter's formula) discussion, https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/nephrology/acid-base-regulation-and-disorders/metabolic-acidosis","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2145,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_or_perioperative_care_13","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.675","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.675.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.675.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[509,536],"terminalOffsetsZh":[144,151],"fullStemEn":"Before wound closure, the final count is short one radiopaque sponge, and an immediate recount does not resolve the discrepancy. The facility sequence is: announce the discrepancy and stop closure; recount and search the field, wound, room, linen, and waste; notify the surgeon that the discrepancy remains unresolved and complete a methodical wound examination; obtain intraoperative imaging if still unresolved; document the discrepancy and confirmed resolution before the client leaves the operating room. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"在关闭切口前，最终清点少了一块带显影标记的手术海绵，立即复点仍未解决差异。机构规定顺序为：宣布清点差异并停止关闭切口；重新清点并搜索术野、伤口、房间、布类和废弃物；通知外科医生差异仍未解决并进行系统性伤口检查；如果仍未解决则进行术中影像检查；在患者离开手术室前记录差异及已确认的解决结果。请按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility sequence is: announce the discrepancy and stop closure; recount and search the field, wound, room, linen, and waste; notify the surgeon that the discrepancy remains unresolved and complete a methodical wound examination; obtain intraoperative imaging if still unresolved; document the discrepancy and confirmed resolution before the client leaves the operating room.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构规定顺序为：宣布清点差异并停止关闭切口；重新清点并搜索术野、伤口、房间、布类和废弃物；通知外科医生差异仍未解决并进行系统性伤口检查；如果仍未解决则进行术中影像检查；在患者离开手术室前记录差异及已确认的解决结果。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"q13_o02","en":"Recount and search the surgical field, wound, room, linen, and waste.","zh":"重新清点并搜索术野、伤口、房间、布类和废弃物。"},{"id":"q13_o03","en":"Notify the surgeon that the discrepancy remains unresolved and complete a methodical wound examination.","zh":"通知外科医生差异仍未解决，并进行系统性伤口检查。"},{"id":"q13_o04","en":"Obtain intraoperative imaging if the sponge remains unaccounted for.","zh":"如果海绵仍未找到，则进行术中影像检查。"},{"id":"q13_o01","en":"Announce the count discrepancy and stop wound closure.","zh":"宣布清点差异并停止关闭切口。"},{"id":"q13_o05","en":"Document the discrepancy and the confirmed resolution before the client leaves the operating room.","zh":"在患者离开手术室前，记录清点差异和已确认的解决结果。"}],"correct":["q13_o01","q13_o02","q13_o03","q13_o04","q13_o05"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An unresolved incorrect count triggers an immediate surgical stop. The team then performs a structured recount and search, followed by a methodical wound examination. If the item is still missing, intraoperative imaging is obtained. The client does not leave the operating room until the discrepancy and verified resolution are documented.","rationaleCorrectZh":"清点错误未解决时，应立即执行手术停止。随后团队进行结构化复点和搜索，再进行系统性伤口检查。如果物品仍然缺失，则进行术中影像检查。在差异和核实后的解决结果被记录之前，患者不能离开手术室。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For an incorrect surgical count, preserve the search opportunity first, escalate from recount to examination to imaging, and document only after resolution is verified.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于手术清点错误，应先保留搜索机会，再从复点升级到伤口检查和影像检查，并在核实解决后记录。","sourceMetadata":"AHRQ PSNet, Reducing Preventable Patient Harm Due to Retained Surgical Items: The RSI Bundle, surgical STOP, methodical search and wound examination, and imaging before leaving the operating room for unresolved incorrect counts, https://psnet.ahrq.gov/innovation/reducing-preventable-patient-harm-due-retained-surgical-items-rsi-bundle","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2146,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_bt_procedural_complications_dialysis_14","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.676","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.676.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.676.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[496,517],"terminalOffsetsZh":[134,142],"fullStemEn":"During a home peritoneal-dialysis exchange, the transfer set disconnects proximal to an open clamp and the open system is exposed. The client reconnects it and calls immediately; there is no abdominal pain and the effluent is currently clear. The PD program defines this event as wet contamination and directs the client to stop further use and close the system, contact the PD team for transfer-set management and prescribed prophylaxis, and complete the program's symptom and follow-up checks. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"在居家腹膜透析换液过程中，转接管在开放夹的近端脱开，开放系统暴露。患者重新连接后立即来电；目前没有腹痛，流出液清澈。腹膜透析项目将此事件定义为湿性污染，并指示患者停止继续使用并关闭系统，联系腹膜透析团队处理转接管和实施规定的预防措施，同时完成项目规定的症状监测和随访。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The PD program defines this event as wet contamination and directs the client to stop further use and close the system, contact the PD team for transfer-set management and prescribed prophylaxis, and complete the program's symptom and follow-up checks.","penultimateSentenceZh":"腹膜透析项目将此事件定义为湿性污染，并指示患者停止继续使用并关闭系统，联系腹膜透析团队处理转接管和实施规定的预防措施，同时完成项目规定的症状监测和随访。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely complication risk","zh":"最可能的并发症风险"},"tokens":[{"id":"q14_c02","en":"Dry contamination with no connection to the open fluid pathway","zh":"未接触开放液路的干性污染"},{"id":"q14_c01","en":"Wet peritoneal-dialysis system contamination with peritonitis risk","zh":"腹膜透析系统湿性污染并有腹膜炎风险"},{"id":"q14_c03","en":"Dialysis disequilibrium syndrome","zh":"透析失衡综合征"}],"correct":"q14_c01"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take now","zh":"现在应采取的行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q14_a04","en":"Flush several bags through the system before notifying the PD team","zh":"在通知腹膜透析团队前，先用数袋透析液冲洗系统"},{"id":"q14_a03","en":"Continue exchanges because the effluent is clear and the client has no symptoms","zh":"因为流出液清澈且患者无症状，继续换液"},{"id":"q14_a02","en":"Contact the PD team immediately for transfer-set management and the program's prescribed prophylaxis pathway","zh":"立即联系腹膜透析团队，处理转接管并执行项目规定的预防流程"},{"id":"q14_a05","en":"Select an antibiotic, dose, and duration without using the program pathway","zh":"不按照项目流程，自行选择抗生素、剂量和疗程"},{"id":"q14_a01","en":"Close or clamp the system and stop further exchanges through the exposed connection","zh":"关闭或夹闭系统，并停止通过暴露连接继续换液"}],"correct":["q14_a01","q14_a02"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Follow-up findings or completion to monitor","zh":"需要监测的随访发现或完成情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q14_p01","en":"Cloudy effluent or new abdominal pain","zh":"流出液浑浊或新出现腹痛"},{"id":"q14_p03","en":"A single normal blood pressure reading","zh":"单次正常血压读数"},{"id":"q14_p02","en":"Completion of the PD program's transfer-set, prophylaxis, and follow-up plan","zh":"完成腹膜透析项目规定的转接管处理、预防措施和随访计划"},{"id":"q14_p04","en":"Return of appetite before the next exchange","zh":"下次换液前食欲恢复"},{"id":"q14_p05","en":"A fixed antibiotic duration chosen by the learner","zh":"由答题者选择的固定抗生素疗程"}],"correct":["q14_p01","q14_p02"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Exposure of an open PD fluid pathway proximal to an open clamp is wet contamination and carries peritonitis risk even before symptoms develop. The client should stop use, secure the system, and follow the PD team's transfer-set and prophylaxis pathway. Monitoring focuses on early peritonitis symptoms and completion of the program-directed follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"开放夹近端的腹膜透析开放液路发生暴露属于湿性污染，即使尚未出现症状，也有腹膜炎风险。患者应停止使用并保护系统，按照腹膜透析团队的转接管处理和预防流程执行。监测重点是早期腹膜炎症状以及是否完成项目规定的随访。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In a contamination item, use the stated open-versus-closed pathway definition, act before symptoms appear, and avoid inventing an antimicrobial regimen.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在污染题中，应使用题干给出的开放/关闭液路定义，在症状出现前采取行动，并避免臆造抗菌药方案。","sourceMetadata":"International Society for Peritoneal Dialysis, Peritonitis guideline recommendations: 2022 update, dry-versus-wet contamination and prophylaxis discussion, https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/08968608221080586","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2147,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_hl_intrapartum_fetal_monitoring_15","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.677","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.677.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.677.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,210],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,46],"fullStemEn":"Thick meconium is newly noted during labor. The fetal heart tracing is currently normal, and maternal observations are stable. Highlight the actions consistent with the supplied guideline for meconium in labor.","fullStemZh":"产程中刚发现浓稠胎粪。当前胎心监护正常，产妇观察结果稳定。请标出符合所给产程胎粪指南的行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the actions consistent with the supplied guideline for meconium in labor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合所给产程胎粪指南的行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The fetal heart tracing is currently normal, and maternal observations are stable.","penultimateSentenceZh":"当前胎心监护正常，产妇观察结果稳定。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q15_s01","en":"Characterize and document the meconium finding.","zh":"描述并记录胎粪情况。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s02","en":"Complete a full maternal and fetal risk assessment.","zh":"完成全面的产妇和胎儿风险评估。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s03","en":"Explain that meconium can increase risk and discuss continuous cardiotocography (CTG) monitoring.","zh":"说明胎粪可能增加风险，并讨论连续胎心宫缩监护（CTG）。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s04","en":"Support the woman's informed choice after the monitoring options are discussed.","zh":"在讨论监护选项后，支持产妇作出知情选择。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s05","en":"Continue reassessing maternal observations, the fetal tracing, and other risk factors.","zh":"继续重新评估产妇观察结果、胎心监护以及其他风险因素。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s06","en":"Declare an automatic emergency cesarean birth solely because thick meconium is present.","zh":"仅因出现浓稠胎粪就宣布必须紧急剖宫产。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s07","en":"Continue the prior monitoring plan without discussing the new meconium finding or CTG option.","zh":"不讨论新出现的胎粪或连续CTG选项，直接维持原监护计划。","selectable":true},{"id":"q15_s08","en":"Ignore any later fetal-tracing change because the tracing is normal now.","zh":"因为当前胎心监护正常，所以忽略以后出现的任何监护变化。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q15_s01","q15_s02","q15_s03","q15_s04","q15_s05"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New meconium should be characterized and incorporated into a full maternal-fetal risk assessment. The woman should receive an explanation of the increased risk and a discussion of continuous CTG, retain informed choice, and continue to be reassessed. Meconium alone does not mandate emergency cesarean birth.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新出现的胎粪应被描述，并纳入全面的母胎风险评估。应向产妇说明风险增加并讨论连续CTG，同时保留其知情选择，并持续重新评估。仅有胎粪并不自动要求紧急剖宫产。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A new intrapartum risk factor usually calls for assessment, explanation, shared monitoring decisions, and reassessment—not an automatic operative response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产程中新出现的风险因素通常需要评估、解释、共同决定监护方式和重新评估，而不是自动采取手术处理。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, Fetal monitoring in labour, recommendations 1.3.10–1.3.12 on meconium, risk assessment, discussion of continuous CTG, informed choice, and reassessment, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2148,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_bt_disaster_emergency_preparedness_16","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.678","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Disaster & Emergency Preparedness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.678.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.678.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[194,271],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,79],"fullStemEn":"The hospital oxygen-pipeline pressure falls abruptly while several clients depend on high-flow or ventilator oxygen. The facility oxygen utility-failure plan and incident command are activated. Complete the bow-tie without changing any client's prescribed oxygen setting.","fullStemZh":"医院氧气管道压力突然下降，而多名患者依赖高流量氧疗或呼吸机供氧。机构已启动氧气公用系统故障计划和事件指挥系统。请完成蝴蝶结题，不要改变任何患者的处方氧疗设置。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie without changing any client's prescribed oxygen setting.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题，不要改变任何患者的处方氧疗设置。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility oxygen utility-failure plan and incident command are activated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构已启动氧气公用系统故障计划和事件指挥系统。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely emergency","zh":"最可能的紧急事件"},"tokens":[{"id":"q16_c02","en":"Isolated pulse-oximeter equipment failure","zh":"单一脉搏血氧仪设备故障"},{"id":"q16_c01","en":"Oxygen utility failure threatening oxygen-dependent clients","zh":"威胁依赖氧气患者的氧气公用系统故障"},{"id":"q16_c03","en":"Routine reduction in hospital oxygen demand","zh":"医院氧气需求常规下降"}],"correct":"q16_c01"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先行动"},"tokens":[{"id":"q16_a02","en":"Use incident command to coordinate facilities and vendor response and implement the plan's oxygen-conservation priorities","zh":"通过事件指挥协调设施和供应商响应，并执行计划中的氧气节约优先级"},{"id":"q16_a01","en":"Switch affected clients to verified backup or portable oxygen sources while preserving prescribed support","zh":"在保持处方支持的同时，将受影响患者切换到经核实的备用或便携式氧源"},{"id":"q16_a04","en":"Wait for pipeline pressure to recover before moving clients to backup sources","zh":"等待管道压力恢复后再把患者转到备用氧源"},{"id":"q16_a05","en":"Evacuate the entire hospital before checking available backup capacity","zh":"在检查备用容量前先疏散整个医院"},{"id":"q16_a03","en":"Independently lower every client's oxygen prescription to conserve cylinders","zh":"为节约氧气瓶，自行降低所有患者的氧疗处方"}],"correct":["q16_a01","q16_a02"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Response parameters to monitor","zh":"需要监测的响应指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q16_p02","en":"Cylinder inventory and current burn rate","zh":"氧气瓶库存和当前消耗速率"},{"id":"q16_p03","en":"Cafeteria meal production","zh":"食堂餐食生产情况"},{"id":"q16_p04","en":"The number of routine outpatient appointments","zh":"常规门诊预约数量"},{"id":"q16_p01","en":"Client oxygenation and function of each backup oxygen source","zh":"患者氧合情况以及每个备用氧源的功能"},{"id":"q16_p05","en":"A new oxygen prescription selected by the learner","zh":"由答题者选择的新氧疗处方"}],"correct":["q16_p01","q16_p02"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abrupt pipeline pressure loss is an oxygen utility failure that immediately threatens clients dependent on high-flow or ventilator oxygen. The response is to maintain prescribed support using verified backup sources and coordinate repair, supply, and conservation through incident command. Monitoring must track both clinical oxygenation and the remaining backup supply's function and burn rate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"管道压力突然下降属于氧气公用系统故障，会立即威胁依赖高流量氧疗或呼吸机氧气的患者。应使用经核实的备用氧源维持处方支持，并通过事件指挥协调维修、供应和节约措施。监测必须同时关注患者氧合、备用氧源功能以及剩余供应的消耗速率。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In a utility failure, protect dependent clients with verified backup capacity, use incident command for system coordination, and track supply depletion as well as clinical status.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在公用系统故障中，应使用经核实的备用容量保护依赖患者，通过事件指挥协调系统响应，并同时追踪供应消耗和临床状态。","sourceMetadata":"ASPR TRACIE, Utility Failures in Health Care Tip Sheet: Oxygen, pressure loss, backup supply, conservation, partner coordination, inventory, and burn-rate monitoring, https://files.asprtracie.hhs.gov/documents/utility-failure-tip-sheet-oxygen.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2149,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_hl_standard_precautions_hygiene_17","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.679","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.679.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.679.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[288,374],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,112],"fullStemEn":"A nurse wearing artificial fingernail extensions is assigned direct care in the ICU. The facility policy states that artificial extensions are not worn for direct contact with high-risk ICU or operating-room patients and that natural nail tips are kept no longer than 1/4 inch (0.64 cm). Highlight the finding and corrective actions supported by the policy and CDC guidance.","fullStemZh":"一名戴有人工指甲延长物的护士被安排在ICU直接照护患者。机构政策规定：与高风险ICU或手术室患者直接接触时不得佩戴人工指甲延长物，自然指甲尖端不得超过1/4英寸（0.64厘米）。请标出符合该政策和CDC指南的发现及纠正行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the finding and corrective actions supported by the policy and CDC guidance.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出符合该政策和CDC指南的发现及纠正行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The facility policy states that artificial extensions are not worn for direct contact with high-risk ICU or operating-room patients and that natural nail tips are kept no longer than 1/4 inch (0.64 cm).","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：与高风险ICU或手术室患者直接接触时不得佩戴人工指甲延长物，自然指甲尖端不得超过1/4英寸（0.64厘米）。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q17_s01","en":"Artificial fingernail extensions are present during an assignment involving direct contact with high-risk ICU patients.","zh":"在直接接触高风险ICU患者的工作安排中，护士佩戴了人工指甲延长物。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s02","en":"Remove the artificial extensions before providing this direct care or arrange a compliant assignment until they are removed.","zh":"在提供此类直接护理前去除人工指甲延长物，或在去除前安排符合政策的工作。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s03","en":"Follow the facility hand-hygiene and nail policy.","zh":"遵守机构的手卫生和指甲政策。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s04","en":"Maintain natural nail tips at or below the stated 1/4-inch limit.","zh":"自然指甲尖端保持在规定的1/4英寸以内。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s05","en":"Perform hand hygiene at the indicated moments before and after patient contact.","zh":"在患者接触前后等规定时机执行手卫生。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s06","en":"Keep the extensions because wearing gloves replaces the need to follow the nail rule.","zh":"保留人工延长指甲，因为戴手套可以代替遵守指甲规定。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s07","en":"Scrub the artificial extensions for extra time and continue the ICU assignment.","zh":"延长刷洗人工指甲的时间，然后继续ICU工作。","selectable":true},{"id":"q17_s08","en":"State that all intact nail polish is universally prohibited in every clinical setting.","zh":"宣称所有完整无损的指甲油在任何临床环境中都一律禁止。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q17_s01","q17_s02","q17_s03","q17_s04","q17_s05"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Artificial fingernail extensions are not appropriate for direct contact with high-risk ICU or operating-room patients. The nurse should comply with the facility nail policy, keep natural nails within the stated length, and perform indicated hand hygiene. Gloves or longer scrubbing do not replace the restriction, and the cited rule does not establish a universal ban on intact nail polish.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与高风险ICU或手术室患者直接接触时，不应佩戴人工指甲延长物。护士应遵守机构指甲政策，把自然指甲保持在规定长度内，并在规定时机执行手卫生。手套或延长刷洗时间不能替代该限制；所引用规则也没有规定完整无损的指甲油在所有环境中一律禁止。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the exact population and rule in the stem: high-risk direct care triggers the artificial-extension restriction, while unrelated universal claims are distractors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干中的具体人群和规则：高风险直接护理触发人工指甲限制，与此无关的一概而论是干扰项。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Clinical Safety: Hand Hygiene for Healthcare Workers, fingernail safety section on artificial extensions for high-risk patients, https://www.cdc.gov/clean-hands/hcp/clinical-safety/index.html; CDC, Guideline for Hand Hygiene in Health-Care Settings, Recommendations 6.A–6.B on artificial fingernails and natural nail tips less than 1/4 inch, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/media/pdfs/Guideline-Hand-Hygiene-P.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The facility policy states that artificial extensions are not worn for direct contact with high-risk ICU or operating-room patients and that natural nail tips are kept no longer than 1/4 inch (0.64 cm).","controlSentenceZh":"机构政策规定：与高风险ICU或手术室患者直接接触时不得佩戴人工指甲延长物，自然指甲尖端不得超过1/4英寸（0.64厘米）。"}
{"queueIndex":2150,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_balance6b_2026_07_16_mx_standard_precautions_hygiene_18","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.680","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.680.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.680.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,282],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,85],"fullStemEn":"For each reusable ultrasound-probe use, select the minimum required reprocessing level after use. Follow the probe manufacturer's instructions. Cleaning occurs before disinfection or sterilization. A probe cover reduces contamination but does not replace contact-based reprocessing.","fullStemZh":"对于每种可重复使用的超声探头用途，请选择使用后的最低再处理级别。遵循探头制造商说明。清洁应在消毒或灭菌之前进行。探头保护套可减少污染，但不能替代根据接触类型要求的再处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"A probe cover reduces contamination but does not replace contact-based reprocessing.","terminalSentenceZh":"探头保护套可减少污染，但不能替代根据接触类型要求的再处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Cleaning occurs before disinfection or sterilization.","penultimateSentenceZh":"清洁应在消毒或灭菌之前进行。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"q18_r01","en":"The probe contacted only intact skin.","zh":"探头只接触完整皮肤。"},{"id":"q18_r02","en":"The probe contacted a mucous membrane during a transvaginal examination.","zh":"探头在经阴道检查中接触黏膜。"},{"id":"q18_r03","en":"The probe contacted nonintact skin.","zh":"探头接触非完整皮肤。"},{"id":"q18_r04","en":"The probe entered sterile tissue during an invasive procedure.","zh":"探头在侵入性操作中进入无菌组织。"},{"id":"q18_r05","en":"An intact single-use cover was used while the probe contacted a mucous membrane.","zh":"探头接触黏膜时使用了完整的一次性保护套。"}],"columns":[{"id":"q18_c02","en":"Cleaning plus at least high-level disinfection","zh":"清洁加至少高水平消毒"},{"id":"q18_c01","en":"Cleaning plus low-level disinfection","zh":"清洁加低水平消毒"},{"id":"q18_c03","en":"Sterilization","zh":"灭菌"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"q18_r01","columnIds":["q18_c01"]},{"rowId":"q18_r02","columnIds":["q18_c02"]},{"rowId":"q18_r03","columnIds":["q18_c02"]},{"rowId":"q18_r04","columnIds":["q18_c03"]},{"rowId":"q18_r05","columnIds":["q18_c02"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reusable probes are classified by the tissue contacted. Intact-skin contact requires cleaning and low-level disinfection. Mucous-membrane or nonintact-skin contact requires cleaning and at least high-level disinfection. Entry into sterile tissue requires sterilization. A cover does not lower the required level.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可重复使用探头应根据接触组织分类。接触完整皮肤需要清洁和低水平消毒；接触黏膜或非完整皮肤需要清洁和至少高水平消毒；进入无菌组织需要灭菌。保护套不会降低所需再处理级别。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the reprocessing level to the highest-risk tissue contacted, and do not let a probe cover downgrade the classification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据接触的最高风险组织匹配再处理级别，不要因使用探头保护套而降低分类。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Recommendations for Disinfection and Sterilization in Healthcare Facilities, Recommendations 3.a–3.c and 10.b–10.d on critical, semicritical, and noncritical devices and ultrasound-probe reprocessing, https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/disinfection-sterilization/summary-recommendations.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2151,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7a_corrected_sodium","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.681","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.681.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.681.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[296,318],"terminalOffsetsZh":[127,133],"fullStemEn":"An adult with severe hyperglycemia has a measured serum sodium of 128 mEq/L and a serum glucose of 600 mg/dL. For this item, use the following equation:\n\nCorrected sodium (mEq/L) = measured sodium + 1.6 × [(glucose − 100) ÷ 100]\n\nCalculate the corrected sodium. Round to the nearest whole mEq/L. Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"一名严重高血糖的成人，实测血清钠为 128 mEq/L，血糖为 600 mg/dL。本题使用以下公式：\n\n校正血清钠（mEq/L）= 实测血清钠 + 1.6 ×［（血糖 − 100）÷ 100］\n\n计算校正后的血清钠。四舍五入到最接近的整数 mEq/L。只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Corrected sodium","zh":"校正血清钠"},"acceptable":["136"],"numeric":{"value":136,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mEq/L"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The glucose is 500 mg/dL above 100 mg/dL, which is five 100-mg/dL increments. The correction is 1.6 × 5 = 8 mEq/L. Therefore, 128 + 8 = 136 mEq/L.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血糖比 100 mg/dL 高 500 mg/dL，即 5 个 100 mg/dL 的增量。校正值为 1.6 × 5 = 8 mEq/L。因此，128 + 8 = 136 mEq/L。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use only the equation supplied in the stem. Count the number of 100-mg/dL glucose increments before adding the sodium correction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"只使用题干给出的公式。先计算血糖超过 100 mg/dL 后有几个 100 mg/dL 的增量，再加上钠校正值。","sourceMetadata":"Endotext, Hyperglycemic Crises, updated January 31, 2026, Fluid Replacement section (1.6 mmol/L sodium change per 100 mg/dL glucose change), https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK620700/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2152,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7a_effective_osmolality","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.682","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.682.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.682.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[317,339],"terminalOffsetsZh":[139,145],"fullStemEn":"An adult has a measured serum sodium of 152 mEq/L and a serum glucose of 720 mg/dL. For this item, calculate effective serum osmolality using conventional units:\n\nEffective serum osmolality (mOsm/kg) = 2 × sodium (mEq/L) + glucose (mg/dL) ÷ 18\n\nDo not include blood urea nitrogen. Round to the nearest whole mOsm/kg. Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"一名成人的实测血清钠为 152 mEq/L，血糖为 720 mg/dL。本题按传统单位使用以下公式计算有效血清渗透压：\n\n有效血清渗透压（mOsm/kg）= 2 × 血清钠（mEq/L）+ 血糖（mg/dL）÷ 18\n\n不要计入血尿素氮。四舍五入到最接近的整数 mOsm/kg。只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mOsm/kg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mOsm/kg。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Effective serum osmolality","zh":"有效血清渗透压"},"acceptable":["344"],"numeric":{"value":344,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mOsm/kg"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Twice the sodium is 304. Glucose divided by 18 is 40. Effective serum osmolality is 304 + 40 = 344 mOsm/kg. Blood urea nitrogen is excluded because this item asks for effective, not total, osmolality.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血清钠的 2 倍为 304；血糖除以 18 为 40。有效血清渗透压为 304 + 40 = 344 mOsm/kg。本题计算的是有效渗透压而不是总渗透压，因此不计入血尿素氮。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish effective osmolality from total osmolality. Follow the supplied equation exactly and exclude urea.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分有效渗透压与总渗透压。严格按题干公式计算，并排除尿素。","sourceMetadata":"Endotext, Hyperglycemic Crises, HHS diagnostic criteria, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK620700/; ADA Standards of Care in Diabetes—2026, Section 16, Table 16.1 (effective osmolality formula), https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12690180/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2153,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7a_curb65_score","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.683","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.683.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.683.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[479,501],"terminalOffsetsZh":[212,218],"fullStemEn":"An adult with community-acquired pneumonia has the following findings:\n\n• New disorientation to place\n• Serum urea: 8.2 mmol/L\n• Respiratory rate: 28/min\n• Blood pressure: 92/58 mm Hg\n• Age: 72 years\n\nUse CURB65, assigning 1 point for each of the following: new confusion; serum urea above 7 mmol/L; respiratory rate 30/min or greater; diastolic blood pressure 60 mm Hg or less or systolic blood pressure below 90 mm Hg; age 65 years or older.\n\nCalculate the total CURB65 score. Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"一名患有社区获得性肺炎的成人有以下表现：\n\n• 新出现地点定向障碍\n• 血清尿素：8.2 mmol/L\n• 呼吸频率：28 次/分\n• 血压：92/58 mm Hg\n• 年龄：72 岁\n\n使用 CURB65，每满足以下一项计 1 分：新出现意识混乱；血清尿素高于 7 mmol/L；呼吸频率至少 30 次/分；舒张压不高于 60 mm Hg 或收缩压低于 90 mm Hg；年龄至少 65 岁。\n\n计算 CURB65 总分。只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the total CURB65 score.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算 CURB65 总分。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"CURB65 total score","zh":"CURB65 总分"},"acceptable":["4"],"numeric":{"value":4,"tolerance":0,"unit":"points"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client scores for confusion, serum urea above 7 mmol/L, diastolic pressure of 58 mm Hg, and age 72. The respiratory rate is below 30/min, and the systolic pressure is not below 90 mm Hg. Total: 4 points. CURB65 supports assessment but does not replace clinical judgment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者在意识混乱、血清尿素高于 7 mmol/L、舒张压 58 mm Hg 和年龄 72 岁四项各得 1 分。呼吸频率低于 30 次/分，收缩压也不低于 90 mm Hg。总分为 4 分。CURB65 可辅助评估，但不能替代临床判断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Score each criterion independently. For the blood-pressure criterion, either qualifying systolic or qualifying diastolic pressure earns one point, not two.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逐项独立评分。血压项目中，收缩压或舒张压任一达到标准只计 1 分，不是 2 分。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG250, Pneumonia: diagnosis and management, recommendations 1.2.7–1.2.9 and Box 2 CURB65 score, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng250/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2154,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7a_renal_sofa_component","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.684","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.684.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.684.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[539,561],"terminalOffsetsZh":[243,249],"fullStemEn":"An adult with suspected sepsis has a serum creatinine of 3.8 mg/dL and urine output of 620 mL during the previous 24 hours.\n\nUse this renal SOFA component excerpt:\n• Score 0: creatinine below 1.2 mg/dL\n• Score 1: creatinine 1.2–1.9 mg/dL\n• Score 2: creatinine 2.0–3.4 mg/dL\n• Score 3: creatinine 3.5–4.9 mg/dL OR urine output below 500 mL/day\n• Score 4: creatinine above 5.0 mg/dL OR urine output below 200 mL/day\n\nWhen creatinine and urine output indicate different scores, use the higher score. Calculate the renal SOFA component score. Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"一名疑似脓毒症的成人，血清肌酐为 3.8 mg/dL，过去 24 小时尿量为 620 mL。\n\n使用以下肾脏 SOFA 分项评分表：\n• 0 分：肌酐低于 1.2 mg/dL\n• 1 分：肌酐 1.2–1.9 mg/dL\n• 2 分：肌酐 2.0–3.4 mg/dL\n• 3 分：肌酐 3.5–4.9 mg/dL，或每日尿量低于 500 mL\n• 4 分：肌酐高于 5.0 mg/dL，或每日尿量低于 200 mL\n\n当肌酐与尿量对应不同分数时，取较高分。计算肾脏 SOFA 分项得分。只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the renal SOFA component score.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算肾脏 SOFA 分项得分。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Renal SOFA component score","zh":"肾脏 SOFA 分项得分"},"acceptable":["3"],"numeric":{"value":3,"tolerance":0,"unit":"points"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A creatinine of 3.8 mg/dL meets the score-3 range. Urine output of 620 mL/day does not meet the score-3 or score-4 urine-output thresholds. The higher applicable score is therefore 3.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肌酐 3.8 mg/dL 属于 3 分范围。每日尿量 620 mL 未达到 3 分或 4 分的尿量阈值。因此，适用的较高分为 3 分。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the supplied component table rather than recalling SOFA. Evaluate both creatinine and urine output, then choose the higher applicable score.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干提供的分项评分表，不要依赖记忆。分别判断肌酐和尿量，再取适用的较高分。","sourceMetadata":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign: International Guidelines for Management of Sepsis and Septic Shock 2026, screening/diagnosis statements, https://www.sccm.org/survivingsepsiscampaign/guidelines-and-resources/surviving-sepsis-campaign-adult-guidelines; Singer et al., Sepsis-3, Table 1 Sequential Organ Failure Assessment Score, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4968574/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2155,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7a_prbc_basic_rate","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.685","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.685.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.685.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,68],"fullStemEn":"A prescription directs the nurse to transfuse 300 mL of packed red blood cells over 3 hours. Calculate the pump rate in mL/hr. Round to the nearest whole mL/hr. Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"医嘱要求护士在 3 小时内输注 300 mL 浓缩红细胞。计算输液泵速度（mL/hr）。四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Pump rate","zh":"输液泵速度"},"acceptable":["100"],"numeric":{"value":100,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rate equals volume divided by time: 300 mL ÷ 3 hr = 100 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"速度等于容量除以时间：300 mL ÷ 3 小时 = 100 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a one-step rate problem, divide the prescribed blood-product volume by the prescribed administration time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于一步式速度计算，用医嘱规定的血液制品容量除以规定的输注时间。","sourceMetadata":"AABB, Circular of Information for the Use of Human Blood and Blood Components, June 2024, Notice to All Users and Red Blood Cell Components; administration duration is the explicit prescription supplied in the stem, https://www.aabb.org/news-resources/resources/circular-of-information","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","controlSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。"}
{"queueIndex":2156,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7a_prbc_revised_rate","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.686","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.686.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.686.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[333,355],"terminalOffsetsZh":[137,143],"fullStemEn":"A unit of packed red blood cells has a labeled volume of 320 mL. The transfusion began at 1400. At 1510, the pump shows that 80 mL has infused. The prescription and facility policy for this client require this unit to be completed by 1700.\n\nCalculate the revised pump rate needed from 1510 to 1700. Round to the nearest whole mL/hr. Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"一袋浓缩红细胞的标签容量为 320 mL。输注于 14:00 开始。15:10 时，输液泵显示已输注 80 mL。该患者的医嘱和机构政策要求这袋血必须在 17:00 前输完。\n\n计算从 15:10 到 17:00 所需的调整后输液泵速度。四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数 mL/hr。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Revised pump rate","zh":"调整后输液泵速度"},"acceptable":["131"],"numeric":{"value":131,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The remaining volume is 320 − 80 = 240 mL. From 1510 to 1700 is 1 hour 50 minutes, or 110 minutes = 1.833 hours. The required rate is 240 ÷ 1.833 = 130.9 mL/hr, which rounds to 131 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"剩余容量为 320 − 80 = 240 mL。15:10 到 17:00 为 1 小时 50 分钟，即 110 分钟 = 1.833 小时。所需速度为 240 ÷ 1.833 = 130.9 mL/hr，四舍五入为 131 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"First calculate the remaining volume. Then convert the remaining clock time to hours before dividing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先计算剩余容量，再把剩余时间换算为小时后相除。","sourceMetadata":"AABB, Circular of Information for the Use of Human Blood and Blood Components, June 2024, Notice to All Users and Red Blood Cell Components; the 1700 completion deadline is the explicit prescription/facility policy supplied in the stem, https://www.aabb.org/news-resources/resources/circular-of-information","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2157,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7b_inpatient_alcohol_withdrawal_pathway","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.687","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.687.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.687.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[262,304],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,82],"fullStemEn":"A hospitalized adult reports abruptly stopping heavy daily alcohol use yesterday. The client is tremulous and anxious but has no seizure, hallucinations, or delirium. The hospital pathway directs the nurse to complete the following actions in operational order. Place all actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"一名住院成人表示，昨天突然停止了长期大量饮酒。患者有手抖和焦虑，但目前没有癫痫发作、幻觉或谵妄。医院流程要求护士按操作顺序完成以下措施。请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place all actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The hospital pathway directs the nurse to complete the following actions in operational order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院流程要求护士按操作顺序完成以下措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"focused_assessment","en":"Perform a focused assessment of last alcohol use, prior complicated withdrawal, current findings, concurrent illness, and withdrawal severity using the facility’s validated tools.","zh":"使用机构认可的工具，针对末次饮酒时间、既往复杂性戒断、当前表现、合并疾病及戒断严重程度进行重点评估。"},{"id":"notify_start_protocol","en":"Report the assessment findings to the prescribing clinician and initiate the prescribed alcohol-withdrawal protocol.","zh":"向开立医嘱的临床人员报告评估结果，并启动已开立的酒精戒断流程。"},{"id":"reassess_escalate","en":"Repeat the validated withdrawal assessment at the specified interval and escalate the level of care if symptoms or vital signs worsen.","zh":"按规定时间再次使用有效戒断量表评估；若症状或生命体征恶化，则升级照护级别。"},{"id":"monitor_support","en":"Begin the pathway’s prescribed supportive monitoring and safety measures, including serial vital signs, hydration status, orientation, and fall/seizure precautions.","zh":"开始执行流程规定的支持性监测和安全措施，包括连续生命体征、液体状态、定向力以及跌倒/癫痫防护。"}],"correct":["focused_assessment","notify_start_protocol","monitor_support","reassess_escalate"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pathway begins with a focused withdrawal severity and complication-risk assessment. The nurse then communicates the findings and initiates the prescribed protocol, provides the ordered supportive monitoring and safety measures, and finally reassesses response and escalates care if findings worsen.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该流程先进行针对性的戒断严重程度和并发症风险评估；随后报告评估结果并启动已开立的戒断流程；接着实施医嘱规定的支持性监测和安全措施；最后根据反应重新评估，若病情恶化则升级照护。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the pathway stated in the stem: assess first, activate the prescribed plan, implement monitoring/support, then evaluate the response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按照题干给出的流程：先评估，再启动已开立的方案，然后实施监测和支持，最后评价反应。","sourceMetadata":"ASAM Clinical Practice Guideline on Alcohol Withdrawal Management (2020), Recommendations II.1–II.13, V.1–V.5, and VII.12–VII.15, https://www.asam.org/quality-care/clinical-guidelines/alcohol-withdrawal-management-guideline","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2158,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7b_ambulatory_withdrawal_transfer","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.688","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.688.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.688.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[501,540],"terminalOffsetsZh":[144,158],"fullStemEn":"An adult is receiving ambulatory alcohol-withdrawal management with daily check-ins. The written pathway requires transfer to a higher level of care for persistent vomiting, new confusion or hallucinations, seizure, worsening medical illness, oversedation, return to alcohol use, or syncope/unstable vital signs. At today’s visit, the client is newly confused, has persistent vomiting, and has a blood pressure of 84/50 mm Hg.\n\nThe clinic transfer protocol directs the following operational sequence. Place all actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名成人正在接受门诊酒精戒断管理，并每日复诊。书面流程规定，若出现持续呕吐、新发意识混乱或幻觉、癫痫、合并疾病恶化、过度镇静、再次饮酒，或晕厥/生命体征不稳定，应转至更高级别照护。今天复诊时，患者新出现意识混乱、持续呕吐，血压为 84/50 mm Hg。\n\n门诊转运流程规定以下操作顺序。请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place all actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The clinic transfer protocol directs the following operational sequence.","penultimateSentenceZh":"门诊转运流程规定以下操作顺序。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"support_during_transfer","en":"Maintain direct observation and provide airway, positioning, fall-protection, and other supportive stabilization measures while emergency transport is arranged and underway.","zh":"在安排及进行紧急转运期间持续直接观察，并给予气道、体位、跌倒防护及其他支持性稳定措施。"},{"id":"structured_handoff","en":"Give the receiving team a structured handoff of the alcohol-use and withdrawal history, serial findings, medications and times already given, and the client’s response.","zh":"向接收团队结构化交接饮酒及戒断史、连续评估结果、已给予药物及时间，以及患者反应。"},{"id":"repeat_assessment","en":"Immediately repeat the focused withdrawal assessment and vital signs to confirm the criteria and identify threats requiring stabilization during transfer.","zh":"立即重复重点戒断评估和生命体征，确认转诊标准，并识别转运期间需要稳定处理的威胁。"},{"id":"urgent_transfer","en":"Activate emergency transfer to the designated higher level of care and notify the receiving service that the pathway’s transfer criteria have been met.","zh":"启动紧急转运至指定的更高级别照护，并通知接收机构患者已达到流程规定的转诊标准。"}],"correct":["repeat_assessment","urgent_transfer","support_during_transfer","structured_handoff"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first repeats a focused assessment to verify the transfer criteria and immediate risks. Because explicit criteria are met, urgent transfer is activated. The client then receives continuous observation and supportive stabilization while transport occurs, followed by a structured handoff of withdrawal history, serial findings, and treatments already given.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先进行重点复评，以确认转诊标准和当前风险。由于患者已达到明确的转诊标准，应立即启动紧急转运。在等待及转运过程中持续观察并给予支持性稳定措施，最后向接收团队完整交接戒断史、连续评估结果以及已给予的治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not continue an unsafe ambulatory plan. Once the supplied transfer criteria are confirmed, move from reassessment to urgent transfer, support during transfer, and handoff.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要继续不安全的门诊方案。确认题干给出的转诊标准后，依次进行复评、紧急转运、转运期间支持和交接。","sourceMetadata":"ASAM Clinical Practice Guideline on Alcohol Withdrawal Management (2020), Recommendations IV.2, IV.5, IV.6, and IV.11 (ambulatory reassessment, transfer indications, supportive care, agreement to transfer), https://www.asam.org/quality-care/clinical-guidelines/alcohol-withdrawal-management-guideline","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The clinic transfer protocol directs the following operational sequence.","controlSentenceZh":"门诊转运流程规定以下操作顺序。"}
{"queueIndex":2159,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7b_circumferential_burn_perfusion","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.689","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.689.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.689.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[302,344],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,99],"fullStemEn":"An adult with a circumferential full-thickness forearm burn develops increasing pain, delayed capillary refill, cool fingers, diminished sensation, and a weaker Doppler signal than one hour ago. The burn service pathway directs the bedside team to complete the following actions in operational order.\n\nPlace all actions in the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"一名成人前臂有环周全层烧伤，现出现疼痛加重、毛细血管再充盈延迟、手指发凉、感觉减退，并且多普勒信号较 1 小时前减弱。烧伤团队流程要求床旁人员按操作顺序完成以下措施。\n\n请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place all actions in the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The burn service pathway directs the bedside team to complete the following actions in operational order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"烧伤团队流程要求床旁人员按操作顺序完成以下措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"prepare_intervention","en":"Prepare the client, monitoring, analgesia supplies, and equipment to assist with the prescribed escharotomy or other burn-team intervention.","zh":"准备患者、监测、镇痛用品和器械，以协助执行已开立的焦痂切开术或其他烧伤团队干预。"},{"id":"immediate_reassessment","en":"Immediately repeat a bilateral focused neurovascular assessment with Doppler, remove external constriction, and position the limb as the burn-service pathway directs without delaying escalation.","zh":"立即进行双侧重点神经血管复评并使用多普勒，移除外部压迫物，并按烧伤团队流程调整肢体位置，同时不得延误升级处理。"},{"id":"notify_burn_team","en":"Urgently notify the burn surgeon or burn team and report the change from the previous neurovascular assessment.","zh":"紧急通知烧伤外科医生或烧伤团队，并报告与前次神经血管评估相比的变化。"},{"id":"post_reassessment","en":"After the intervention, repeat and document Doppler signals, capillary refill, color, temperature, sensation, movement, and pain using the same comparison points.","zh":"干预后用相同的比较点再次评估并记录多普勒信号、毛细血管再充盈、颜色、温度、感觉、活动和疼痛。"}],"correct":["immediate_reassessment","notify_burn_team","prepare_intervention","post_reassessment"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Worsening distal perfusion requires immediate focused neurovascular reassessment and removal of external contributors while positioning the limb as directed. The nurse then urgently notifies the burn team, prepares for the prescribed decompressive intervention, and repeats the same perfusion assessment after the intervention to evaluate response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"远端灌注恶化时，应立即进行重点神经血管复评，排除外部压迫因素，并按流程调整肢体位置。随后紧急通知烧伤团队，准备执行已开立的减压干预，并在干预后用同样指标再次评估灌注，以判断疗效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the trend: worsening neurovascular findings require reassessment, urgent specialty escalation, preparation for the ordered intervention, then outcome reassessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据趋势判断：神经血管表现恶化时，先复评，再紧急升级至专科，准备执行医嘱干预，最后重新评价结局。","sourceMetadata":"American Burn Association, Orgill and Piccolo, Escharotomy and Decompressive Therapies in Burns, Journal of Burn Care & Research 2009;30(5):759–768, doi:10.1097/BCR.0b013e3181b47cd3, https://academic.oup.com/jbcr/article/30/5/759/4598380; ISBI Practice Guidelines for Burn Care, section 6 Escharotomy and fasciotomy, doi:10.1016/j.burns.2016.05.013","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2160,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7b_pn_administration_safety","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.690","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.690.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.690.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[241,302],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,93],"fullStemEn":"A hospital’s parenteral nutrition (PN) administration checklist specifies that this adult’s total nutrient admixture must run through a dedicated central-lumen line, a new administration set with a 1.2-micron filter, and an electronic pump. Place all checklist actions in the correct operational order.","fullStemZh":"医院的肠外营养（PN）给药核对表规定：该成人的全营养混合液必须经专用中心静脉腔路，使用带 1.2 微米过滤器的新输液管路，并通过电子输液泵输注。请将核对表中的所有措施按正确操作顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place all checklist actions in the correct operational order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将核对表中的所有措施按正确操作顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A hospital’s parenteral nutrition (PN) administration checklist specifies that this adult’s total nutrient admixture must run through a dedicated central-lumen line, a new administration set with a 1.2-micron filter, and an electronic pump.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医院的肠外营养（PN）给药核对表规定：该成人的全营养混合液必须经专用中心静脉腔路，使用带 1.2 微米过滤器的新输液管路，并通过电子输液泵输注。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"initiate","en":"Connect to the dedicated lumen and initiate PN on the electronic pump at the rate and schedule in the current order.","zh":"连接专用腔路，并按当前医嘱规定的速度和时间通过电子输液泵开始 PN 输注。"},{"id":"setup","en":"Using aseptic technique, attach the new administration set and the specified 1.2-micron filter, prime the tubing, and load it into the electronic pump.","zh":"采用无菌技术连接新输液管路和规定的 1.2 微米过滤器，预充管路并装入电子输液泵。"},{"id":"monitor","en":"Monitor blood glucose, ordered laboratory values, fluid balance, clinical tolerance, and the catheter site according to the PN monitoring protocol.","zh":"根据 PN 监测流程，监测血糖、医嘱化验、液体平衡、临床耐受性和导管部位。"},{"id":"verify_order_label","en":"Verify the current PN order, client identifiers, formula, route, total volume, rate, start time, and beyond-use information against the pharmacy label.","zh":"将当前 PN 医嘱与药房标签核对，包括患者身份、配方、途径、总容量、速度、开始时间和使用期限。"},{"id":"inspect","en":"Inspect the bag for integrity, abnormal separation or precipitate, and expiration; then verify that the designated central lumen is patent and reserved for PN.","zh":"检查输液袋完整性、异常分层或沉淀及有效期；随后确认指定中心静脉腔路通畅且专用于 PN。"}],"correct":["verify_order_label","inspect","setup","initiate","monitor"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe PN administration begins by verifying the current order against the product label. The nurse then inspects the bag and dedicated access, assembles the explicitly specified tubing, filter, and pump, initiates the infusion at the prescribed rate, and monitors the supplied metabolic, fluid, and access parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全输注 PN 首先要把当前医嘱与产品标签核对一致；然后检查输液袋和专用静脉通路；按题干明确规定安装管路、过滤器和输液泵；按医嘱速度开始输注；最后监测代谢、液体和静脉通路相关指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The safe sequence moves from order verification to product/access inspection, equipment setup, initiation, and monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全顺序是：核对医嘱、检查产品和通路、设置设备、开始输注、持续监测。","sourceMetadata":"ASPEN Parenteral Nutrition Care Pathway, Step 8 Administer PN Safely and Appropriately and Step 9 Monitor and Reevaluate Patient, https://nutritioncare.org/clinical-resources/enteral-nutrition/aspen-parenteral-nutrition-care-pathway/; ASPEN, Update on the Use of Filters for Parenteral Nutrition and PN Administration Checklist, https://nutritioncare.org/clinical-resources/parenteral-nutrition/pn-preparation-administration/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"A hospital’s parenteral nutrition (PN) administration checklist specifies that this adult’s total nutrient admixture must run through a dedicated central-lumen line, a new administration set with a 1.2-micron filter, and an electronic pump.","controlSentenceZh":"医院的肠外营养（PN）给药核对表规定：该成人的全营养混合液必须经专用中心静脉腔路，使用带 1.2 微米过滤器的新输液管路，并通过电子输液泵输注。"}
{"queueIndex":2161,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7b_home_pn_transition","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.691","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.691.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.691.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[180,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,66],"fullStemEn":"An adult will be discharged on home parenteral nutrition (PN). The health system’s PN transition pathway requires the following steps to be completed in sequence before discharge. Place all actions in the correct order.","fullStemZh":"一名成人即将出院并在家中继续肠外营养（PN）。医疗系统的 PN 转衔流程要求在出院前按顺序完成以下步骤。请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place all actions in the correct order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将所有措施按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The health system’s PN transition pathway requires the following steps to be completed in sequence before discharge.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医疗系统的 PN 转衔流程要求在出院前按顺序完成以下步骤。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"identify_team","en":"Identify and document the outpatient PN prescriber or nutrition-support team and the home-infusion provider responsible after discharge.","zh":"明确并记录出院后负责的门诊 PN 开立者或营养支持团队，以及家庭输液服务机构。"},{"id":"verify_competence","en":"Confirm delivery of PN, pump, filters, dressings, and other supplies; have the client or caregiver demonstrate pump setup and access care; and provide routine and emergency contact numbers.","zh":"确认 PN、输液泵、过滤器、敷料及其他用品已送达；让患者或照护者回示输液泵设置和导管护理；提供日常及紧急联系电话。"},{"id":"reconcile_transmit","en":"Reconcile the final PN prescription and transmit the current order, formula, infusion schedule, laboratory tests, frequency, and monitoring parameters to the responsible outpatient team and home-infusion provider.","zh":"核对最终 PN 处方，并向负责的门诊团队和家庭输液机构传送当前医嘱、配方、输注时间表、化验项目、频率和监测参数。"},{"id":"confirm_followup","en":"Confirm the first follow-up appointment and document exactly who will review each laboratory result, contact the client, and authorize any PN-order change.","zh":"确认首次随访，并明确记录由谁查看每项化验结果、联系患者以及批准任何 PN 医嘱变更。"}],"correct":["identify_team","reconcile_transmit","verify_competence","confirm_followup"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The transition starts by naming the clinician/team responsible for PN after discharge. The finalized PN order and laboratory monitoring plan are then reconciled and transmitted. Next, the team verifies supplies, access-care and pump competence, and emergency contacts. Finally, follow-up and ownership of laboratory results and order changes are confirmed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"转衔首先要明确出院后负责 PN 的临床人员或团队；随后核对并传送最终 PN 医嘱和实验室监测计划；接着确认用品、导管护理与输液泵操作能力以及紧急联系人；最后确认随访安排及由谁负责查看化验结果和修改医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Safe transition requires clear ownership before information is transmitted, competence is verified, and follow-up responsibility is closed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"安全转衔应先明确责任归属，再传送信息、验证能力，最后闭环确认随访责任。","sourceMetadata":"ASPEN Parenteral Nutrition Care Pathway, Step 10 Initiate Discharge Planning for Transition of Care, https://nutritioncare.org/clinical-resources/enteral-nutrition/aspen-parenteral-nutrition-care-pathway/; ASPEN Safe Care Transitions for Patients Receiving Parenteral Nutrition, 2022, https://nutritioncare.org/clinical-resources/parenteral-nutrition/pn-safety/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2162,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7c_exercise_hypoglycemia_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.692","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.692.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.692.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[504,620],"terminalOffsetsZh":[171,207],"fullStemEn":"A client with type 1 diabetes began a new 45-minute cycling routine after work. On three cycling days, the client developed sweating, tremor, and difficulty concentrating during the ride or within one hour afterward; continuous glucose monitor readings were 58–64 mg/dL. On noncycling days, fasting and premeal glucose readings remain 95–140 mg/dL. The client has no fever, vomiting, ketones, or recent illness and has continued the preexisting meal and insulin plan without an exercise-day adjustment.\n\nComplete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, the 2 priority actions, and the 2 parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名 1 型糖尿病患者开始在下班后进行新的 45 分钟骑车锻炼。在 3 个骑车日中，患者在骑行中或结束后 1 小时内出现出汗、手抖和注意力难以集中，连续血糖监测值为 58–64 mg/dL。非骑车日的空腹及餐前血糖仍为 95–140 mg/dL。患者无发热、呕吐、酮体或近期疾病，并且一直沿用原有饮食和胰岛素方案，没有针对锻炼日进行调整。\n\n完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、2 项优先措施和 2 项需要监测的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, the 2 priority actions, and the 2 parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、2 项优先措施和 2 项需要监测的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has no fever, vomiting, ketones, or recent illness and has continued the preexisting meal and insulin plan without an exercise-day adjustment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者无发热、呕吐、酮体或近期疾病，并且一直沿用原有饮食和胰岛素方案，没有针对锻炼日进行调整。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"cond_intercurrent_illness","en":"Intercurrent illness causing unstable glucose","zh":"合并急性疾病导致血糖不稳定"},{"id":"cond_inadequate_insulin","en":"Persistent hyperglycemia from insufficient insulin","zh":"胰岛素不足导致的持续高血糖"},{"id":"cond_exercise_hypo","en":"Activity-associated hypoglycemia from a plan not aligned with the new exercise routine","zh":"因现有方案未与新锻炼习惯协调而发生的运动相关低血糖"}],"correct":"cond_exercise_hypo"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions — select 2","zh":"优先措施——选择 2 项"},"tokens":[{"id":"act_raise_insulin","en":"Increase the pre-exercise insulin dose independently.","zh":"自行增加锻炼前胰岛素剂量。"},{"id":"act_team_plan","en":"Contact the diabetes prescriber or DSMES team to create an individualized exercise-day carbohydrate and medication plan before the next ride.","zh":"在下次骑车前联系糖尿病开立者或 DSMES 团队，共同制定个体化锻炼日碳水化合物和用药方案。"},{"id":"act_hypo_safety","en":"Carry rapid-acting carbohydrate and immediately follow the existing hypoglycemia treatment plan when symptoms or a low reading occurs.","zh":"随身携带速效碳水化合物，并在出现症状或低血糖读数时立即执行已有低血糖处理方案。"},{"id":"act_stop_activity","en":"Stop all physical activity permanently.","zh":"永久停止所有身体活动。"}],"correct":["act_team_plan","act_hypo_safety"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor — select 2","zh":"需要监测的指标——选择 2 项"},"tokens":[{"id":"param_recurrence","en":"Timing and recurrence of hypoglycemia symptoms or readings below the client’s action threshold","zh":"低血糖症状或低于个人行动阈值读数的发生时间及是否复发"},{"id":"param_glucose_pattern","en":"Glucose immediately before, during, and for several hours after cycling","zh":"骑车前、骑车中以及结束后数小时的血糖"},{"id":"param_daily_ketones","en":"Daily urine ketones despite normal glucose and no illness","zh":"在血糖正常且无疾病时每日检测尿酮体"},{"id":"param_resting_bp","en":"Resting blood pressure on nonexercise mornings","zh":"非锻炼日早晨的静息血压"}],"correct":["param_glucose_pattern","param_recurrence"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The repeated low-glucose episodes occur specifically during or shortly after the new exercise routine, while nonexercise readings remain in the stated range and illness cues are absent. This supports activity-associated hypoglycemia caused by a self-management plan that has not yet been aligned with the new routine. Priority actions are to involve the diabetes prescriber/DSMES team in an individualized exercise-day plan and to use the existing hypoglycemia safety plan with rapid carbohydrate readily available. Glucose around exercise and recurrence/timing of symptoms show whether the revised plan works.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低血糖反复发生在新锻炼过程中或结束后不久，而非锻炼日血糖仍处于题干范围，并且没有疾病线索，因此最符合“自我管理方案尚未与新锻炼习惯协调”所导致的运动相关低血糖。优先措施是请糖尿病开立者/DSMES 团队共同制定个体化锻炼日方案，并执行已有低血糖安全方案、随身携带速效碳水化合物。监测锻炼前后血糖以及症状/低血糖是否再次出现，可判断调整后的方案是否有效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Resolve the condition by matching timing and glucose pattern. Choose actions that use the existing hypoglycemia plan for immediate safety and involve the diabetes team in planning for future exercise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据症状发生时间和血糖模式判断状况。选择能立即执行现有低血糖安全方案，并由糖尿病团队共同制定后续锻炼计划的措施。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, About Diabetes Self-Management Education and Support, 7 self-care behaviors and personalized planning, https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/education-support-programs/index.html; ADA Standards of Care in Diabetes—2026, Section 5 Physical Activity and Exercise, https://diabetesjournals.org/care/article/49/Supplement_1/S89/163932/5-Facilitating-Positive-Health-Behaviors-and-Well; Section 6 Recommendations 6.10 and 6.14–6.15, recurrent hypoglycemia review, glucose treatment, and CGM, https://diabetesjournals.org/care/article/49/Supplement_1/S132/163927/6-Glycemic-Goals-Hypoglycemia-and-Hyperglycemic; Section 7 Recommendation 7.11, glucose monitoring before, during, and after exercise, https://diabetesjournals.org/care/article/49/Supplement_1/S150/163922/7-Diabetes-Technology-Standards-of-Care-in","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2163,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7c_heart_failure_action_plan_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.693","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.693.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.693.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[726,842],"terminalOffsetsZh":[218,254],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic heart failure uses an individualized home action plan. The plan defines the yellow zone as a morning weight gain of at least 2 lb in 24 hours together with new swelling or increased exertional dyspnea. Yellow-zone instructions are to call the heart-failure team the same day, follow the agreed sodium/fluid limits, and take the already prescribed one-time extra diuretic dose only after the team confirms it.\n\nFor the past 3 weeks, the client’s morning weight has varied by less than 1 lb. Today the weight is 3 lb above yesterday’s value. The client has new bilateral ankle edema and becomes short of breath walking from the bedroom to the kitchen. There is no chest pain, syncope, or dyspnea at rest.\n\nComplete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, the 2 priority actions, and the 2 parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性心力衰竭患者使用个体化家庭行动计划。计划规定：若晨起体重在 24 小时内增加至少 2 磅，并伴有新出现的水肿或活动后呼吸困难加重，则属于黄色区域。黄色区域指示为：当天联系心衰团队，遵守已经商定的钠和液体限制，并且只有在团队确认后才服用医嘱中预先规定的一次额外利尿剂。\n\n过去 3 周，患者晨起体重波动均小于 1 磅。今天体重比昨天增加 3 磅，出现新的双侧踝部水肿，并且从卧室走到厨房就会气短。无胸痛、晕厥或静息时呼吸困难。\n\n完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、2 项优先措施和 2 项需要监测的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, the 2 priority actions, and the 2 parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、2 项优先措施和 2 项需要监测的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"There is no chest pain, syncope, or dyspnea at rest.","penultimateSentenceZh":"无胸痛、晕厥或静息时呼吸困难。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的状况"},"tokens":[{"id":"cond_normal_variation","en":"Stable day-to-day weight fluctuation","zh":"稳定的日常体重波动"},{"id":"cond_fluid_retention","en":"Worsening fluid retention crossing the client’s yellow-zone threshold","zh":"液体潴留恶化并超过患者的黄色区域阈值"},{"id":"cond_deconditioning","en":"Isolated physical deconditioning without congestion","zh":"无充血的单纯体能下降"}],"correct":"cond_fluid_retention"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions — select 2","zh":"优先措施——选择 2 项"},"tokens":[{"id":"act_wait_week","en":"Wait one week to see whether the weight returns to baseline.","zh":"等待一周，观察体重是否自行恢复到基线。"},{"id":"act_double_diuretic","en":"Double all diuretic doses immediately without contacting the team.","zh":"不联系团队，立即把所有利尿剂剂量加倍。"},{"id":"act_follow_plan","en":"After the heart-failure team confirms the yellow-zone instruction, take the already prescribed one-time extra diuretic dose.","zh":"心衰团队确认黄色区域指示后，服用医嘱中已预先规定的一次额外利尿剂。"},{"id":"act_call_hf","en":"Call the heart-failure team today and report the weight change, edema, and exertional dyspnea.","zh":"今天联系心衰团队，报告体重变化、水肿和活动后呼吸困难。"}],"correct":["act_call_hf","act_follow_plan"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor — select 2","zh":"需要监测的指标——选择 2 项"},"tokens":[{"id":"param_bowel","en":"Daily bowel-movement frequency","zh":"每日排便次数"},{"id":"param_weight","en":"Morning weight on the same scale after urination","zh":"排尿后使用同一台体重秤测得的晨起体重"},{"id":"param_congestion","en":"Dyspnea, ankle edema, and urine response after the plan is implemented","zh":"执行计划后的呼吸困难、踝部水肿和尿量反应"},{"id":"param_a1c","en":"Hemoglobin A1c","zh":"糖化血红蛋白"}],"correct":["param_weight","param_congestion"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has crossed the supplied yellow-zone threshold and has corroborating edema and worsening exertional dyspnea, making worsening fluid retention more likely than ordinary day-to-day weight fluctuation. The priority is to contact the heart-failure team and, after confirmation, take the already prescribed one-time extra diuretic dose while continuing the agreed sodium/fluid limits. Morning weight and congestion symptoms/diuretic response are the most direct outcome measures.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者已超过题干规定的黄色区域阈值，并同时出现水肿和活动后呼吸困难加重，因此比普通日常体重波动更符合液体潴留恶化。优先措施是联系心衰团队，并在团队确认后服用医嘱中已预先规定的一次额外利尿剂，同时继续遵守已商定的钠和液体限制。晨起体重以及充血症状和利尿反应，是最直接的结局指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the client-specific threshold in the stem, not a universal cutoff. Choose only actions already authorized by that plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干中的患者个体化阈值，不要套用通用界值。只选择该行动计划中已经授权的措施。","sourceMetadata":"American Heart Association, Physical Changes to Report for Heart Failure and Managing Heart Failure Symptoms, reviewed June 2025 (daily weight, rapid weight gain, swelling, dyspnea, contact the care team), https://www.heart.org/en/health-topics/heart-failure/living-with-heart-failure-and-managing-advanced-hf/physical-changes-to-report-for-heart-failure; the exact 2-lb threshold and conditional medication instruction are individualized plan data supplied in the stem","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2164,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7c_actionable_diabetes_plan_highlight","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.694","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.694.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.694.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[42,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,34],"fullStemEn":"Review the diabetes self-management note. Highlight the elements that make the plan actionable and individualized.","fullStemZh":"阅读糖尿病自我管理记录。突出显示使该计划具有可执行性和个体化的内容。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the elements that make the plan actionable and individualized.","terminalSentenceZh":"突出显示使该计划具有可执行性和个体化的内容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the diabetes self-management note.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阅读糖尿病自我管理记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h15_goal","en":"The client chose a goal to walk for 20 minutes after dinner on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday.","zh":"患者选择的目标是每周一、周三和周五晚餐后步行 20 分钟。","selectable":true},{"id":"h15_generic_effort","en":"The nurse wrote, “Try harder to control your diabetes.”","zh":"护士写道：“要更努力地控制糖尿病。”","selectable":true},{"id":"h15_monitor","en":"The client will record glucose before and after each planned walk and note any symptoms.","zh":"患者将在每次计划步行前后记录血糖，并注明任何症状。","selectable":true},{"id":"h15_vague_check","en":"The client should check glucose whenever it is convenient.","zh":"患者应在方便时检查血糖。","selectable":true},{"id":"h15_problem","en":"If glucose is below the client’s written exercise threshold, the client will follow the existing low-glucose action plan and postpone the walk until the plan’s recheck criterion is met.","zh":"如果血糖低于个人书面锻炼阈值，患者将执行已有低血糖行动计划，并推迟步行，直到达到计划规定的复测标准。","selectable":true},{"id":"h15_restrict","en":"The client was told to avoid all carbohydrates.","zh":"患者被告知要避免所有碳水化合物。","selectable":true},{"id":"h15_support","en":"A DSMES referral was placed, and the client and nurse scheduled a two-week review of the glucose and activity log.","zh":"已转介至 DSMES，患者和护士安排在两周后复查血糖与活动记录。","selectable":true}],"correct":["h15_goal","h15_monitor","h15_problem","h15_support"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An actionable individualized plan uses a specific shared goal, defines what and when to monitor, gives a concrete problem-solving response, and connects the client with ongoing education/support and a review date. Generic exhortations, overly restrictive advice, and vague monitoring are not actionable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"可执行的个体化计划应包括具体的共同目标、明确监测内容和时间、具体的问题解决措施，以及持续教育/支持和复评日期。泛泛要求、过度限制性建议和模糊监测都不具备可执行性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select statements that specify who will do what, when, how response will be checked, and where support will come from.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能够说明“由谁、做什么、何时做、如何检查效果、从哪里获得支持”的陈述。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Living with Diabetes, Healthy habits and Resources and support, updated January 1, 2026, https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/living-with/index.html; CDC, About DSMES, 7 self-care behaviors, https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/education-support-programs/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2165,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7c_life_change_plan_revision_highlight","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.695","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.695.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.695.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[45,179],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,49],"fullStemEn":"Review the chronic-condition follow-up note. Highlight the cues and actions that support reassessment, shared goal revision, teach-back, and connection to self-management support.","fullStemZh":"阅读慢性病随访记录。突出显示支持重新评估、共同修改目标、回授确认以及连接自我管理支持的线索和措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the cues and actions that support reassessment, shared goal revision, teach-back, and connection to self-management support.","terminalSentenceZh":"突出显示支持重新评估、共同修改目标、回授确认以及连接自我管理支持的线索和措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the chronic-condition follow-up note.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阅读慢性病随访记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h16_shift","en":"The client started a permanent night shift three weeks ago and can no longer attend the morning exercise group.","zh":"患者在 3 周前开始长期夜班，无法再参加早晨锻炼小组。","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_missed","en":"The client reports missing planned meals because the old meal schedule conflicts with overnight work breaks.","zh":"患者表示，旧的进餐时间与夜班休息时间冲突，因此经常漏掉计划中的餐次。","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_blame","en":"The nurse said, “You need to be more disciplined.”","zh":"护士说：“你需要更自律。”","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_shared","en":"The nurse asked which changes felt realistic, and the client chose a revised first goal of packing a balanced meal for three night shifts each week.","zh":"护士询问哪些改变对患者来说可行，患者选择的首个修改目标是每周为 3 个夜班准备一份均衡餐。","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_old_handout","en":"The nurse reprinted the unchanged morning schedule and instructed the client to follow it exactly.","zh":"护士重新打印未修改的早晨时间表，并要求患者完全照做。","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_teachback","en":"The client explained in their own words when the packed meal would be eaten and how progress would be recorded.","zh":"患者用自己的话说明将在何时吃准备好的餐食，以及如何记录进展。","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_support","en":"The nurse connected the client with an evening virtual self-management program and confirmed the referral contact information.","zh":"护士将患者连接到晚间线上自我管理项目，并确认了转介联系信息。","selectable":true},{"id":"h16_label","en":"The note labels the client “noncompliant” without documenting barriers.","zh":"记录在未说明障碍的情况下给患者贴上“不依从”标签。","selectable":true}],"correct":["h16_shift","h16_missed","h16_shared","h16_teachback","h16_support"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A major work-schedule change and missed meals show that the old plan is no longer feasible. The nurse should reassess barriers, revise goals with the client, use teach-back, and connect the client to accessible support. Repeating the old plan, blaming the client, or labeling the client noncompliant does not support effective self-management.","rationaleCorrectZh":"工作时间发生重大变化并出现漏餐，说明旧计划已不可行。护士应重新评估障碍、与患者共同修改目标、使用回授法，并把患者连接到可获得的支持。重复旧计划、责备患者或给患者贴“不依从”标签，都不能促进有效自我管理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select both the life-change cues and the collaborative actions that make the revised plan usable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"同时选择提示生活变化的线索，以及使修改后计划可实施的协作措施。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, About Diabetes Self-Management Education and Support, four key times including life changes that make management harder, https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/education-support-programs/index.html; CDC, Living with Diabetes, Healthy habits and Resources and support, updated January 1, 2026, https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/living-with/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2166,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7c_sepsis_triage_cues_highlight","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.696","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.696.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.696.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,181],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,57],"fullStemEn":"An adult arrives at triage. Highlight only the cues that, in combination, require immediate sepsis evaluation and escalation. Do not use any single screening score as the diagnosis.","fullStemZh":"一名成人到达分诊区。仅突出显示那些组合起来需要立即进行脓毒症评估并升级处理的线索。不要把任何单一筛查评分当作诊断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not use any single screening score as the diagnosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要把任何单一筛查评分当作诊断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight only the cues that, in combination, require immediate sepsis evaluation and escalation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"仅突出显示那些组合起来需要立即进行脓毒症评估并升级处理的线索。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h17_infection","en":"Temperature is 101.7 °F (38.7 °C), and the client reports dysuria and urinary frequency for two days.","zh":"体温为 101.7 °F (38.7 °C)，患者诉排尿疼痛和尿频已 2 天。","selectable":true},{"id":"h17_confusion","en":"The family reports new confusion beginning this morning.","zh":"家属报告患者从今天早晨开始新出现意识混乱。","selectable":true},{"id":"h17_hypotension","en":"Blood pressure is 84/50 mm Hg, with a calculated mean arterial pressure of 61 mm Hg.","zh":"血压为 84/50 mm Hg，计算平均动脉压为 61 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"h17_perfusion","en":"Capillary refill is 4 seconds, and the knees are newly mottled.","zh":"毛细血管再充盈为 4 秒，膝部新出现皮肤花斑。","selectable":true},{"id":"h17_lactate","en":"Serum lactate is 3.6 mmol/L.","zh":"血清乳酸为 3.6 mmol/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"h17_knee","en":"The client has unchanged chronic knee pain rated 3/10.","zh":"患者有长期膝痛，仍为 3/10，与平时相同。","selectable":true},{"id":"h17_glucose","en":"Glucose is 142 mg/dL after the client drank juice.","zh":"患者喝果汁后血糖为 142 mg/dL。","selectable":true}],"correct":["h17_infection","h17_confusion","h17_hypotension","h17_perfusion","h17_lactate"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fever with urinary symptoms provides a plausible infection source. New confusion, hypotension, prolonged capillary refill with mottling, and elevated lactate are evolving organ-dysfunction or hypoperfusion cues requiring immediate sepsis evaluation and escalation. Stable chronic knee pain and a mildly elevated glucose after juice do not contribute to the acute sepsis pattern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"发热伴尿路症状提示可能的感染来源。新发意识混乱、低血压、毛细血管再充盈延长伴皮肤花斑，以及乳酸升高，均属于正在发展的器官功能障碍或低灌注线索，需要立即进行脓毒症评估并升级处理。稳定的慢性膝痛和喝果汁后轻度血糖升高与本次急性脓毒症模式无关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for a plausible infection plus acute organ dysfunction or hypoperfusion. Exclude unrelated chronic or benign findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找“可能感染”加上“急性器官功能障碍或低灌注”的组合，排除无关的慢性或良性表现。","sourceMetadata":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign: International Guidelines for Management of Sepsis and Septic Shock 2026, screening and biomarkers statements, blood lactate recommendation, and medical-emergency/resuscitation good-practice statement, https://sccm.org/clinical-resources/guidelines/guidelines/surviving-sepsis-campaign-international-guidelines-for-management-of-sepsis-and-septic-shock-2026","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2167,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format7c_sepsis_reassessment_highlight","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.697","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.697.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.697.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,171],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,50],"fullStemEn":"Two hours after sepsis treatment began, the nurse reviews the serial reassessment note. Highlight the findings that require continued escalation or treatment reassessment.","fullStemZh":"脓毒症治疗开始 2 小时后，护士查看连续复评记录。突出显示需要继续升级处理或重新评估治疗方案的表现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require continued escalation or treatment reassessment.","terminalSentenceZh":"突出显示需要继续升级处理或重新评估治疗方案的表现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two hours after sepsis treatment began, the nurse reviews the serial reassessment note.","penultimateSentenceZh":"脓毒症治疗开始 2 小时后，护士查看连续复评记录。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h18_temp","en":"Temperature decreased from 102.4 °F (39.1 °C) to 100.8 °F (38.2 °C).","zh":"体温从 102.4 °F (39.1 °C) 降至 100.8 °F (38.2 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_hr","en":"Heart rate decreased from 122/min to 106/min.","zh":"心率从 122 次/分降至 106 次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_map","en":"Mean arterial pressure remains 58 mm Hg after the initial resuscitation steps.","zh":"完成初始复苏措施后，平均动脉压仍为 58 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_lactate","en":"Lactate increased from 4.6 mmol/L to 5.2 mmol/L.","zh":"乳酸从 4.6 mmol/L 升至 5.2 mmol/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_urine","en":"Urine output totals 15 mL during the past 2 hours.","zh":"过去 2 小时尿量总计 15 mL。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_mental","en":"The client is now difficult to arouse and is more confused than at treatment initiation.","zh":"患者现在难以唤醒，且比治疗开始时更加意识混乱。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_spo2","en":"Oxygen saturation remains 96% on the unchanged nasal-cannula setting.","zh":"在鼻导管设置未变的情况下，血氧饱和度仍为 96%。","selectable":true},{"id":"h18_back","en":"Chronic low-back pain remains unchanged at 2/10.","zh":"慢性下背痛仍为 2/10，与平时相同。","selectable":true}],"correct":["h18_map","h18_lactate","h18_urine","h18_mental"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Persistent hypotension, rising lactate, severe oliguria, and worsening confusion show ongoing hypoperfusion or organ dysfunction and require continued escalation and treatment reassessment. A falling temperature and heart rate are favorable trends but do not cancel the persistent danger cues. Stable oxygen saturation and unchanged chronic pain are not reasons for escalation in this context.","rationaleCorrectZh":"持续低血压、乳酸上升、严重少尿和意识混乱恶化提示低灌注或器官功能障碍仍在继续，需要持续升级处理并重新评估治疗。体温和心率下降属于改善趋势，但不能抵消仍存在的危险线索。稳定的血氧饱和度和未变化的慢性疼痛在本情境下不是升级处理的原因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate improving trends from persistent or worsening perfusion and organ-function findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分改善趋势与持续或恶化的灌注及器官功能表现。","sourceMetadata":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign: International Guidelines for Management of Sepsis and Septic Shock 2026, fluid-resuscitation reassessment remarks, serial lactate recommendation, capillary-refill adjunct recommendation, and initial MAP target recommendation, https://sccm.org/clinical-resources/guidelines/guidelines/surviving-sepsis-campaign-international-guidelines-for-management-of-sepsis-and-septic-shock-2026","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2168,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10a_dialysis_disequilibrium_initial_hd","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.698","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.698.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.698.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[337,519],"terminalOffsetsZh":[123,174],"fullStemEn":"A client with a pre-dialysis BUN of 198 mg/dL is 90 minutes into the first hemodialysis treatment. A mild headache progresses to restlessness, confusion, vomiting, and a generalized seizure. Blood pressure remains 148/86 mm Hg, point-of-care glucose is 108 mg/dL, and no unilateral weakness, facial droop, or unequal pupils are present. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions under the dialysis emergency pathway, and two parameters that best track deterioration or response.","fullStemZh":"一名透析前血尿素氮为 198 mg/dL 的患者正在接受首次血液透析，已进行 90 分钟。轻度头痛逐渐发展为烦躁、意识混乱、呕吐和全身性抽搐。血压仍为 148/86 mm Hg，床旁血糖为 108 mg/dL，未见单侧无力、面瘫或双侧瞳孔不等大。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、透析急症路径下的两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪恶化或治疗反应的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions under the dialysis emergency pathway, and two parameters that best track deterioration or response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、透析急症路径下的两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪恶化或治疗反应的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Blood pressure remains 148/86 mm Hg, point-of-care glucose is 108 mg/dL, and no unilateral weakness, facial droop, or unequal pupils are present.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压仍为 148/86 mm Hg，床旁血糖为 108 mg/dL，未见单侧无力、面瘫或双侧瞳孔不等大。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1c3","en":"Hypoglycemia","zh":"低血糖"},{"id":"q1c1","en":"Dialysis disequilibrium syndrome","zh":"透析失衡综合征"},{"id":"q1c2","en":"Intradialytic hypotension","zh":"透析中低血压"},{"id":"q1c4","en":"Acute focal ischemic stroke","zh":"急性局灶性缺血性卒中"}],"correct":"q1c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1a1","en":"Stop hemodialysis immediately and keep the client in the monitored treatment area","zh":"立即停止血液透析，并将患者留在监护治疗区域"},{"id":"q1a4","en":"Give oral carbohydrate and reassess in 30 minutes","zh":"给予口服碳水化合物，30 分钟后复评"},{"id":"q1a2","en":"Activate the emergency response; support airway and oxygenation and urgently evaluate other causes under the pathway","zh":"启动急救反应；支持气道和氧合，并按路径紧急评估其他原因"},{"id":"q1a3","en":"Continue dialysis at the same blood-flow rate until the prescribed time is complete","zh":"按相同血流速度继续透析直至完成规定时间"}],"correct":["q1a1","q1a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1p4","en":"Single-pool Kt/V at the end of the month","zh":"月底单室 Kt/V"},{"id":"q1p1","en":"Serial level of consciousness, pupils, and seizure activity","zh":"连续意识水平、瞳孔及抽搐活动"},{"id":"q1p3","en":"Estimated dry weight at the next monthly review","zh":"下次月度复评时的估计干体重"},{"id":"q1p2","en":"Respiratory rate/SpO₂ and serial blood pressure","zh":"呼吸频率/SpO₂ 及连续血压"}],"correct":["q1p1","q1p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The timing during an initial dialysis treatment and the rapidly progressive, nonfocal neurologic syndrome support dialysis disequilibrium syndrome (DDS), not routine fatigue. Stable blood pressure argues against intradialytic hypotension, normal glucose argues against hypoglycemia, and the absence of a focal deficit makes an acute focal stroke less likely, although other causes still require urgent exclusion. Severe or worsening DDS symptoms require stopping dialysis, supporting airway and oxygenation, activating urgent evaluation, and monitoring neurologic and cardiorespiratory status.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首次透析过程中出现快速进展的非局灶性神经系统综合征，支持透析失衡综合征（DDS），而不是普通疲劳。血压稳定不支持透析中低血压，血糖正常不支持低血糖，缺乏局灶性神经功能缺损使急性局灶性卒中较不可能，但仍需紧急排除其他原因。严重或加重的 DDS 症状要求停止透析、支持气道和氧合、启动紧急评估，并监测神经及心肺状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use timing plus the whole neurologic pattern. A headache alone is nonspecific; progression during the first dialysis to confusion, vomiting, and seizure is the discriminating cluster.","testTakingStrategyZh":"结合发生时间和完整神经系统模式判断。单独头痛缺乏特异性；首次透析过程中进展为意识混乱、呕吐和抽搐，才是关键区分线索。","sourceMetadata":"Mistry K. Dialysis disequilibrium syndrome prevention and management. International Journal of Nephrology and Renovascular Disease. 2019;12:69-77, sections 'Clinical manifestations,' 'Diagnosis,' and 'Treatment' (symptoms during or shortly after dialysis, greatest risk with first treatment; exclusion of hypoglycemia and cerebrovascular events; reduce or stop dialysis for worsening symptoms and provide supportive care), https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6503314/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2169,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10a_life_threatening_asthma_reduced_air_entry","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.699","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.699.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.699.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[532,706],"terminalOffsetsZh":[149,197],"fullStemEn":"A client with asthma is being treated under the emergency department severe-exacerbation pathway. Despite repeated reliever therapy, the client can speak only one or two words, uses accessory muscles, is becoming drowsy, and has SpO₂ 88% while receiving oxygen. The wheeze is now quieter, but bilateral air entry is markedly reduced and peak expiratory flow is 24% of personal best. Breath sounds are reduced equally, and there is no sudden pleuritic chest pain, unilateral leg swelling, or abrupt unilateral loss of breath sounds. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions under the activated pathway, and two parameters that best track ventilation or oxygenation.","fullStemZh":"一名哮喘患者正在急诊科重度急性加重路径下接受治疗。尽管已重复给予缓解治疗，患者只能说一两个词，使用辅助呼吸肌，逐渐嗜睡，吸氧时 SpO₂ 为 88%。喘鸣声反而变轻，但双侧空气进入明显减少，呼气峰流量仅为个人最佳值的 24%。双侧呼吸音同样减弱，无突发胸膜性胸痛、单侧下肢肿胀或单侧呼吸音突然消失。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、已启动路径下的两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪通气或氧合的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions under the activated pathway, and two parameters that best track ventilation or oxygenation.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、已启动路径下的两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪通气或氧合的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Breath sounds are reduced equally, and there is no sudden pleuritic chest pain, unilateral leg swelling, or abrupt unilateral loss of breath sounds.","penultimateSentenceZh":"双侧呼吸音同样减弱，无突发胸膜性胸痛、单侧下肢肿胀或单侧呼吸音突然消失。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2c2","en":"Panic attack with hyperventilation","zh":"惊恐发作伴过度通气"},{"id":"q2c1","en":"Life-threatening asthma exacerbation with impending respiratory failure","zh":"危及生命的哮喘急性加重并有呼吸衰竭前兆"},{"id":"q2c3","en":"Acute pulmonary embolism","zh":"急性肺栓塞"},{"id":"q2c5","en":"Improving bronchospasm","zh":"支气管痉挛正在改善"},{"id":"q2c4","en":"Focal mucus plugging","zh":"局灶性黏液栓塞"}],"correct":"q2c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2a3","en":"Pause treatment and observe because the wheeze is quieter","zh":"因喘鸣变轻而暂停治疗并观察"},{"id":"q2a2","en":"Activate senior/critical-care support and prepare assisted ventilation while treatment continues","zh":"在继续治疗的同时启动高级/重症支持并准备辅助通气"},{"id":"q2a1","en":"Continue controlled oxygen and repeated inhaled rapid bronchodilator therapy under the severe-exacerbation orders","zh":"按重度急性加重医嘱继续控制性氧疗和重复吸入快速支气管扩张治疗"},{"id":"q2a4","en":"Administer a sedative for presumed panic before reassessing breathing","zh":"按疑似惊恐先给予镇静药，再复评呼吸"}],"correct":["q2a1","q2a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2p1","en":"Serial SpO₂ and arterial blood-gas ventilation values","zh":"连续 SpO₂ 及动脉血气通气指标"},{"id":"q2p2","en":"Level of consciousness, respiratory effort, and bilateral air entry","zh":"意识水平、呼吸努力及双侧空气进入"},{"id":"q2p3","en":"Outpatient allergy-panel results","zh":"门诊过敏原检测结果"},{"id":"q2p4","en":"Sputum color alone","zh":"仅痰液颜色"}],"correct":["q2p1","q2p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A quieter wheeze with markedly reduced bilateral air entry is not improvement when work of breathing, oxygenation, peak flow, and alertness are worsening. This cluster supports a life-threatening asthma exacerbation with impending respiratory failure. Immediate management continues oxygen and rapid bronchodilator-based therapy under the severe-exacerbation orders while senior/critical-care help is activated and ventilatory support is prepared. Serial oxygenation, ventilation, mental status, and respiratory effort determine response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当呼吸功、氧合、峰流量和清醒程度都在恶化时，喘鸣变轻而双侧空气进入明显减少并不代表改善。该线索组合支持危及生命的哮喘急性加重并有呼吸衰竭前兆。立即处理包括按重度急性加重医嘱继续氧疗和快速支气管扩张治疗，同时启动高级/重症团队并准备通气支持。连续氧合、通气、意识状态和呼吸努力可判断治疗反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not grade asthma by loudness of wheeze alone. Falling air movement plus exhaustion, hypoxemia, and altered alertness is a danger pattern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要仅按喘鸣声大小判断哮喘严重度。空气流动减少并伴疲惫、低氧血症和清醒程度改变，是危险模式。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, section 'Management of asthma exacerbations in acute care facilities' and severity assessment/initial treatment boxes (drowsiness, hypoxemia, reduced air movement or quiet chest as life-threatening features; oxygen, repeated inhaled bronchodilator treatment, systemic corticosteroid treatment, frequent reassessment, and escalation for ventilatory support), https://ginasthma.org/2026-gina-strategy-report/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2170,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10a_postpartum_preeclampsia_severe_features","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.700","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.700.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.700.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[381,573],"terminalOffsetsZh":[157,211],"fullStemEn":"Five days after an uncomplicated vaginal birth with epidural anesthesia, a client reports a new severe headache that is not positional and is not relieved by acetaminophen, flashing spots, and shortness of breath when lying flat. Blood pressures are 168/112 and 166/110 mm Hg 15 minutes apart. Bibasilar crackles are present, SpO₂ is 91% on room air, and platelets are 88 ×10³/µL. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions under the maternal severe-hypertension pathway, and two parameters that best track deterioration or response.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在无并发症阴道分娩并接受硬膜外麻醉后第 5 天，出现新的严重头痛；头痛与体位无关，服用对乙酰氨基酚后不缓解，并伴闪光样视物和仰卧时呼吸困难。两次血压分别为 168/112 和 166/110 mm Hg，间隔 15 分钟。双肺底可闻及湿啰音，室内空气 SpO₂ 为 91%，血小板为 88 ×10³/µL。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、母体重度高血压路径下的两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪恶化或治疗反应的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions under the maternal severe-hypertension pathway, and two parameters that best track deterioration or response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、母体重度高血压路径下的两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪恶化或治疗反应的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Bibasilar crackles are present, SpO₂ is 91% on room air, and platelets are 88 ×10³/µL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"双肺底可闻及湿啰音，室内空气 SpO₂ 为 91%，血小板为 88 ×10³/µL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4c3","en":"Post-dural-puncture headache","zh":"硬膜穿刺后头痛"},{"id":"q4c2","en":"Migraine","zh":"偏头痛"},{"id":"q4c1","en":"Postpartum preeclampsia with severe features","zh":"伴重度特征的产后子痫前期"},{"id":"q4c5","en":"Uncomplicated postpartum discomfort","zh":"无并发症的产后不适"},{"id":"q4c4","en":"Isolated anxiety or panic","zh":"单纯焦虑或惊恐"}],"correct":"q4c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4a4","en":"Discharge with instructions to recheck blood pressure next week","zh":"出院并嘱下周复查血压"},{"id":"q4a3","en":"Treat as a routine epidural headache and schedule an outpatient anesthesia call","zh":"按普通硬膜外麻醉后头痛处理，并安排门诊麻醉科电话随访"},{"id":"q4a2","en":"Initiate seizure precautions and administer prescribed magnesium sulfate under the pathway","zh":"实施防惊厥措施，并按路径给予医嘱硫酸镁"},{"id":"q4a1","en":"Activate the maternal severe-hypertension response and give the prescribed rapid-acting antihypertensive per protocol","zh":"启动母体重度高血压反应，并按方案给予医嘱的快速降压药"}],"correct":["q4a1","q4a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4p3","en":"Lochia color alone","zh":"仅恶露颜色"},{"id":"q4p1","en":"Serial blood pressure and neurologic status","zh":"连续血压和神经状态"},{"id":"q4p4","en":"Newborn bilirubin level","zh":"新生儿胆红素水平"},{"id":"q4p2","en":"Respiratory rate/SpO₂ and lung findings","zh":"呼吸频率/SpO₂ 及肺部发现"}],"correct":["q4p1","q4p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New persistent severe-range hypertension with a nonpositional refractory headache, visual symptoms, pulmonary edema cues, and thrombocytopenia five days after birth supports postpartum preeclampsia with severe features. The complete cluster is not explained by migraine, anxiety, routine postpartum discomfort, or a typical post-dural-puncture headache. The severe-hypertension response must be activated, prescribed rapid antihypertensive treatment given promptly, seizure prophylaxis initiated as ordered, and maternal neurologic, respiratory, and blood-pressure response closely monitored.","rationaleCorrectZh":"产后第 5 天出现新的持续重度范围高血压，并伴非体位性难治性头痛、视觉症状、肺水肿线索和血小板减少，支持伴重度特征的产后子痫前期。偏头痛、焦虑、普通产后不适或典型硬膜穿刺后头痛均不能解释完整线索组合。必须启动重度高血压反应路径，及时给予医嘱的快速降压治疗，按医嘱开始防惊厥治疗，并密切监测母体神经、呼吸和血压反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Postpartum timing does not make preeclampsia impossible. Severe blood pressure plus end-organ cues outweigh the history of an epidural.","testTakingStrategyZh":"产后发生并不能排除子痫前期。重度血压加终末器官线索的重要性高于硬膜外麻醉史。","sourceMetadata":"Alliance for Innovation on Maternal Health (AIM), Severe Hypertension in Pregnancy Patient Safety Bundle, 2022 revision, 'Recognition and Prevention' and 'Response' elements (pregnant and postpartum patients, standardized escalation and timely treatment of persistent severe hypertension), https://saferbirth.org/psbs/severe-hypertension-in-pregnancy/; American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, 'Preeclampsia and High Blood Pressure During Pregnancy,' severe-features section (severe-range blood pressure, refractory headache/visual change, thrombocytopenia, liver/kidney dysfunction, pulmonary edema), https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/preeclampsia-and-high-blood-pressure-during-pregnancy","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2171,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10a_measles_triage_airborne_pathway","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.701","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.701.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.701.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,299],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,76],"fullStemEn":"The clinic uses the CDC measles infection-control pathway. Highlight only the facts in the triage and exposure note that require immediate patient masking and separation, airborne-infection isolation placement, infection-prevention notification, and public-health coordination for suspected measles.","fullStemZh":"诊所采用 CDC 麻疹感染控制路径。请只标出分诊及暴露记录中要求立即为患者戴口罩并隔离、安排空气传播感染隔离、通知感染预防部门及协调公共卫生部门的事实。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the facts in the triage and exposure note that require immediate patient masking and separation, airborne-infection isolation placement, infection-prevention notification, and public-health coordination for suspected measles.","terminalSentenceZh":"请只标出分诊及暴露记录中要求立即为患者戴口罩并隔离、安排空气传播感染隔离、通知感染预防部门及协调公共卫生部门的事实。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The clinic uses the CDC measles infection-control pathway.","penultimateSentenceZh":"诊所采用 CDC 麻疹感染控制路径。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Triage and exposure note:","zh":"分诊及暴露记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The client returned 8 days ago from a community with active measles transmission and spent an evening in the same room as a laboratory-confirmed measles case.","zh":"患者 8 天前从有麻疹活跃传播的社区返回，并曾与实验室确诊麻疹病例在同一房间共处一晚。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Today the client has fever 102.6 °F (39.2 °C), cough, coryza, and conjunctivitis followed by a generalized maculopapular rash.","zh":"今天患者体温 102.6 °F (39.2 °C)，伴咳嗽、鼻卡他和结膜炎，随后出现全身斑丘疹。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Before the rash was recognized, the client sat unmasked in the common waiting area for 20 minutes.","zh":"在识别皮疹前，患者未戴口罩在公共候诊区停留了 20 分钟。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client cannot locate written documentation of two MMR vaccine doses.","zh":"患者无法找到两剂 MMR 疫苗的书面记录。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The rash is mildly itchy.","zh":"皮疹有轻度瘙痒。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"A sibling has chronic eczema.","zh":"患者的一名兄弟姐妹患有慢性湿疹。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Recent close exposure in an area with active transmission plus a compatible febrile prodrome followed by a generalized rash creates a suspected-measles pathway; the client's unmasked time in a common waiting area also requires immediate infection-prevention exposure assessment and public-health coordination. Unknown vaccination documentation is important for susceptibility assessment but does not replace immediate isolation. Mild pruritus and a sibling's eczema are nondiscriminating.","rationaleCorrectZh":"近期在有活跃传播地区与确诊病例近距离接触，加上相符的发热前驱症状后出现全身皮疹，触发疑似麻疹路径；患者未戴口罩停留在公共候诊区，也要求感染预防部门立即评估暴露并协调公共卫生。疫苗接种记录不明对易感性评估有意义，但不能代替立即隔离。轻度瘙痒和兄弟姐妹的湿疹缺乏区分价值。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the exposure-plus-syndrome cluster and the operational exposure fact. Do not select vaccination uncertainty as though it determines whether isolation begins.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择“暴露加相符综合征”的组合以及实际候诊区暴露事实。不要把疫苗记录不确定误当成是否开始隔离的决定因素。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Interim Infection Prevention and Control Recommendations for Measles in Healthcare Settings, sections 2 'Minimize Potential Measles Exposures,' 3 'Adherence to Standard and Airborne Precautions,' and 7 'Manage Measles Exposure' (facemask and separation at entry, immediate AIIR placement, airborne precautions, infection-control and public-health notification), https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/measles/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2172,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10a_alcohol_withdrawal_escalation_findings","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.702","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Substance Use & Withdrawal","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.702.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.702.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,70],"fullStemEn":"An ambulatory withdrawal-management program follows ASAM Recommendation IV.5. Highlight only the longitudinal findings that require immediate transfer to a more intensive level of care for complicated withdrawal, oversedation, or medical instability.","fullStemZh":"某门诊戒断管理项目遵循 ASAM 建议 IV.5。请只标出纵向记录中因复杂性戒断、过度镇静或医学不稳定而需要立即转至更高强度照护层级的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the longitudinal findings that require immediate transfer to a more intensive level of care for complicated withdrawal, oversedation, or medical instability.","terminalSentenceZh":"请只标出纵向记录中因复杂性戒断、过度镇静或医学不稳定而需要立即转至更高强度照护层级的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An ambulatory withdrawal-management program follows ASAM Recommendation IV.5.","penultimateSentenceZh":"某门诊戒断管理项目遵循 ASAM 建议 IV.5。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Longitudinal ambulatory record:","zh":"门诊纵向记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"At 0800 the client has mild hand tremor, anxiety, and insomnia but is fully oriented and drinks oral fluids without vomiting.","zh":"0800，患者有轻度手部震颤、焦虑和失眠，但定向力完整，能口服液体且无呕吐。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"At 1130 the client begins seeing insects on the wall and cannot state the location or date.","zh":"1130，患者开始看到墙上有昆虫，并无法说出所在地点或日期。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"At 1210 the client has a generalized tonic-clonic seizure.","zh":"1210，患者发生全身强直-阵挛性抽搐。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"At 1330 repeated vomiting is followed by syncope; blood pressure is 86/50 mm Hg on recheck.","zh":"1330，反复呕吐后发生晕厥；复测血压为 86/50 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"After a prescribed sedating medication, the client is difficult to arouse, has slow shallow respirations, and cannot walk without marked ataxia.","zh":"按医嘱给予镇静性药物后，患者难以唤醒，呼吸缓慢浅表，且因明显共济失调无法行走。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The pulse briefly rises to 102/min during anxiety and returns to 88/min after rest and oral fluids.","zh":"焦虑时脉搏短暂升至 102 次/分，休息和口服液体后回到 88 次/分。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mild tremor, anxiety, insomnia, and transient tachycardia can occur in uncomplicated withdrawal when the client remains oriented and can take fluids. New hallucinations with confusion, a seizure, persistent vomiting with syncope and unstable vital signs, and oversedation with respiratory depression or ataxia require immediate transfer/escalation under ASAM Recommendation IV.5.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当患者保持定向力并能摄入液体时，轻度震颤、焦虑、失眠和短暂心动过速可见于无并发症戒断。新出现幻觉并伴意识混乱、抽搐、持续呕吐伴晕厥和生命体征不稳定，以及伴呼吸抑制或共济失调的过度镇静，均按 ASAM 建议 IV.5 需要立即转诊/升级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected mild symptoms from complications. A single tremor is not the same as seizure, delirium, unstable vital signs, or medication-related respiratory depression.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分预期轻症表现与并发症。单一震颤不同于抽搐、谵妄、生命体征不稳定或药物相关呼吸抑制。","sourceMetadata":"American Society of Addiction Medicine, The ASAM Clinical Practice Guideline on Alcohol Withdrawal Management, 2020, Recommendation IV.5 and accompanying discussion, pp. 34-35 (transfer indications: persistent vomiting, marked agitation, hallucinations, confusion, seizure, worsening medical or psychiatric condition, oversedation, syncope, unstable vital signs; oversedation signs include respiratory depression, ataxia, and confusion), https://downloads.asam.org/sitefinity-production-blobs/docs/default-source/quality-science/the_asam_clinical_practice_guideline_on_alcohol-1.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2173,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10b_hemodialysis_access_prompt_followup","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.703","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.703.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.703.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,56],"fullStemEn":"A nurse assesses an established arteriovenous fistula before and during hemodialysis. Highlight the findings that require prompt follow-up for possible access stenosis or dysfunction.","fullStemZh":"护士在血液透析前及透析过程中评估一处已建立的动静脉瘘。请标出需要及时随访以评估通路可能存在狭窄或功能障碍的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require prompt follow-up for possible access stenosis or dysfunction.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要及时随访以评估通路可能存在狭窄或功能障碍的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A nurse assesses an established arteriovenous fistula before and during hemodialysis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在血液透析前及透析过程中评估一处已建立的动静脉瘘。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Access assessment findings:","zh":"血管通路评估发现："},{"id":"s1","en":"The fistula previously had a continuous thrill and low-pitched bruit. Today the thrill is weak and discontinuous, with a high-pitched systolic bruit over the venous segment.","zh":"该瘘管以往可触及持续震颤，并可闻及低调血管杂音。今日震颤微弱且间断，静脉段可闻及高调收缩期杂音。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"During dialysis, the prescribed target blood-flow rate cannot be achieved.","zh":"透析过程中无法达到医嘱的目标血流速率。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Cannulation has become newly difficult after previously uncomplicated sessions.","zh":"以往透析穿刺顺利，但近期新出现穿刺困难。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Bleeding from the needle sites continues longer than usual after each of the last three sessions.","zh":"最近连续三次透析后，针眼出血持续时间均较患者平时更长。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The access-side hand remains warm with brisk capillary refill.","zh":"通路侧手部仍温暖，毛细血管再充盈迅速。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"A small bruise from the prior cannulation is unchanged in size and fading, without warmth, drainage, or pain.","zh":"上次穿刺形成的小瘀斑大小未增加且正在变淡，无温热、引流或疼痛。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Changes from the client's usual access examination—especially a weak or discontinuous thrill and a high-pitched systolic bruit—can indicate stenosis. Inability to achieve the prescribed target blood flow, new cannulation difficulty, and bleeding that lasts longer than usual after three consecutive sessions are dialysis indicators of possible access dysfunction. These findings require follow-up and evaluation after other causes are considered. A warm, well-perfused hand and a small resolving bruise without inflammation or pain are reassuring findings in this scenario.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与患者平时通路检查相比，新出现的微弱或间断震颤及高调收缩期杂音可能提示狭窄。无法达到医嘱目标血流量、新出现的穿刺困难，以及连续三次透析后针眼出血时间均较平时延长，都是通路可能功能障碍的透析指标。在考虑并排除其他原因后，这些发现需要随访评估。本情境中，手部温暖且灌注良好，以及无炎症或疼痛、正在消退的小瘀斑，属于较安心的发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare today's access examination and dialysis performance with the client's usual baseline. New changes and repeated performance problems are more concerning than a stable, resolving cannulation bruise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将今日的通路检查及透析表现与患者平时的基线比较。新出现的变化和反复发生的透析问题，比稳定且正在消退的穿刺瘀斑更值得关注。","sourceMetadata":"National Kidney Foundation, KDOQI 2019 Vascular Access Guideline implementation tool, 'Detection and Management of Clinically Significant AV Access Lesion (Stenosis/Thrombosis),' pp. 2-3, https://www.kidney.org/sites/default/files/vait-15_detection_management_clinically_significant_av_access_lesion-stenosis_thrombosis.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2174,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10b_spinal_infection_compression_red_flags","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.704","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.704.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.704.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[34,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,45],"fullStemEn":"A client presents with back pain. Highlight the findings that require urgent follow-up for possible spinal infection with epidural extension or neural compression.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因背痛就诊。请标出提示可能存在脊柱感染伴硬膜外扩展或神经压迫、需要紧急随访的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require urgent follow-up for possible spinal infection with epidural extension or neural compression.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出提示可能存在脊柱感染伴硬膜外扩展或神经压迫、需要紧急随访的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client presents with back pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者因背痛就诊。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Emergency-department note:","zh":"急诊记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The pain began after lifting a box, worsens with flexion, and improves substantially with rest.","zh":"疼痛在搬箱子后开始，屈曲时加重，休息后明显改善。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The client completed treatment for Staphylococcus aureus bacteremia 2 weeks ago and now has a temperature of 101.3 °F (38.5 °C).","zh":"患者 2 周前刚完成金黄色葡萄球菌菌血症治疗，目前体温 101.3 °F (38.5 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"There is severe focal thoracic pain with exquisite percussion tenderness and worsening pain at night.","zh":"胸椎局部剧痛，叩击时明显压痛，且夜间疼痛加重。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Over 6 hours, bilateral leg strength decreases from 5/5 to 3/5 and a new sensory level appears.","zh":"6 小时内双下肢肌力由 5/5 降至 3/5，并出现新的感觉平面。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client develops new urinary retention and numbness over the perineum and inner thighs.","zh":"患者新出现尿潴留，以及会阴和大腿内侧麻木。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"A stable unilateral shooting pain is reproduced by straight-leg raise; strength and bladder function were normal at that assessment.","zh":"直腿抬高可诱发稳定的单侧放射痛；当时肌力和膀胱功能正常。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The white blood cell count is within the reference interval.","zh":"白细胞计数在参考区间内。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Recent Staphylococcus aureus bacteremia with fever, severe focal percussion pain, progressive bilateral neurologic deficits, and new urinary retention with saddle sensory loss are red flags for spinal infection and possible epidural or neural compression. The absence of the complete classic triad does not exclude spinal epidural infection or compression. IDSA recommends MRI for suspected vertebral infection and a motor/sensory examination that includes bowel and bladder function. Mechanical lifting pain or a stable unilateral radicular pattern without systemic or progressive neurologic cues is less urgent; a normal WBC count does not rule out infection but is not itself an escalation cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"近期金黄色葡萄球菌菌血症伴发热、严重局灶性叩击痛、进行性双侧神经功能缺损，以及新发尿潴留伴鞍区感觉减退，都是脊柱感染及可能硬膜外或神经压迫的危险信号。“经典三联征”不完整并不能排除脊髓硬膜外感染或压迫。IDSA 建议疑似椎体感染时进行 MRI，并完成包括肠膀胱功能在内的运动/感觉检查。搬重物后机械性疼痛，或无全身及进行性神经线索的稳定单侧根性疼痛，紧急性较低；正常白细胞不能排除感染，但本身不是升级线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for infection risk plus focal pain or progressive neurologic/sphincter change. Do not wait for fever, pain, and paralysis to all be present.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找感染风险加局灶疼痛，或进行性神经/括约肌变化。不要等待发热、疼痛和瘫痪全部出现。","sourceMetadata":"Infectious Diseases Society of America, 2015 Clinical Practice Guidelines for Native Vertebral Osteomyelitis in Adults, Recommendations 1-8 and diagnostic evidence summary (new/worsening back pain with fever or bloodstream infection; motor/sensory examination including urinary and intestinal function; spine MRI), https://www.idsociety.org/practice-guideline/vertebral-osteomyelitis/; American College of Radiology, Appropriateness Criteria 'Suspected Spine Infection,' Variant 1 (MRI usually appropriate with new/worsening pain and infection risk factors), https://acsearch.acr.org/docs/3148734/Narrative/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2175,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10b_corrected_count_increment","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.705","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.705.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.705.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[445,514],"terminalOffsetsZh":[192,211],"fullStemEn":"A client receives 4.0 × 10¹¹ platelets. The platelet count is 8 ×10³/µL immediately before transfusion and 32 ×10³/µL 30 minutes after transfusion. Body surface area is 1.8 m². Use the AABB convention: CCI = [(posttransfusion platelet count − pretransfusion platelet count) per µL × BSA in m²] ÷ platelets transfused in units of 10¹¹. Calculate the CCI and round to the nearest whole number. Enter the number only or the number followed by CCI. Do not diagnose platelet refractoriness from this single calculation.","fullStemZh":"一名患者接受 4.0 × 10¹¹ 个血小板。输注前即刻血小板计数为 8 ×10³/µL，输注后 30 分钟为 32 ×10³/µL。体表面积为 1.8 m²。使用 AABB 约定：CCI =［（输注后血小板计数 − 输注前血小板计数，单位 /µL）× 体表面积 m²］÷ 以 10¹¹ 为单位的输注血小板数。计算 CCI，并四舍五入至最接近的整数。只输入数字或“数字 + CCI”。不要根据这一次计算诊断血小板输注无效。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not diagnose platelet refractoriness from this single calculation.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要根据这一次计算诊断血小板输注无效。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Enter the number only or the number followed by CCI.","penultimateSentenceZh":"只输入数字或“数字 + CCI”。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"corrected count increment (CCI)","zh":"校正计数增量（CCI）"},"acceptable":["10800","10,800","10800 CCI","10,800 CCI"],"numeric":{"value":10800,"tolerance":0,"unit":"CCI"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Platelet increment = 32,000 − 8,000 = 24,000/µL. CCI = (24,000 × 1.8) ÷ 4.0 = 43,200 ÷ 4.0 = 10,800. The 30-minute value falls within the AABB 10- to 60-minute posttransfusion timing used for this calculation. A single CCI is arithmetic evidence only and does not by itself establish refractoriness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血小板增量 = 32,000 − 8,000 = 24,000/µL。CCI =（24,000 × 1.8）÷ 4.0 = 43,200 ÷ 4.0 = 10,800。30 分钟结果位于 AABB 用于该计算的输注后 10–60 分钟时间窗内。单次 CCI 只是算术结果，本身不能确定输注无效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the denominator exactly as stated: the transfused dose is already expressed in units of 10¹¹, so divide by 4.0, not by 4.0 × 10¹¹.","testTakingStrategyZh":"严格按题干处理分母：输注剂量已用 10¹¹ 为单位表示，因此除以 4.0，而不是除以 4.0 × 10¹¹。","sourceMetadata":"AABB, Circular of Information for the Use of Human Blood and Blood Components, June 2024, Platelet transfusion response/Corrected Count Increment equation and 10-60 minute posttransfusion timing, p. 30, https://www.aabb.org/docs/default-source/default-document-library/resources/circular-of-information-watermark.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2176,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10b_free_water_deficit","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.706","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.706.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.706.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[328,461],"terminalOffsetsZh":[134,171],"fullStemEn":"A client with hypernatremia has a supplied total body water (TBW) estimate of 36 L. The measured serum sodium is 158 mEq/L, and the clinician's target sodium for this calculation is 140 mEq/L. Use: free-water deficit = TBW × (measured sodium ÷ target sodium − 1). Calculate the deficit in liters and round to the nearest tenth. This item asks only for the mathematical deficit; do not choose a fluid, infusion rate, correction speed, or volume-status diagnosis.","fullStemZh":"一名高钠血症患者的总身体水量（TBW）估计值已给定为 36 L。实测血清钠为 158 mEq/L，本次计算的目标钠由临床人员设为 140 mEq/L。使用公式：自由水缺失量 = TBW ×（实测钠 ÷ 目标钠 − 1）。计算缺失量，单位为升，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。本题只要求数学上的缺失量；不要选择液体、输注速度、纠正速度或容量状态诊断。","terminalSentenceEn":"This item asks only for the mathematical deficit; do not choose a fluid, infusion rate, correction speed, or volume-status diagnosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题只要求数学上的缺失量；不要选择液体、输注速度、纠正速度或容量状态诊断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the deficit in liters and round to the nearest tenth.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算缺失量，单位为升，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"free-water deficit (L)","zh":"自由水缺失量（L）"},"acceptable":["4.6","4.6 L","4.6 liters"],"numeric":{"value":4.6,"tolerance":0,"unit":"L"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Free-water deficit = 36 × (158 ÷ 140 − 1) = 36 × 0.12857 = 4.6286 L, which rounds to 4.6 L. The formula estimates a water deficit; clinical fluid choice and correction planning require separate assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"自由水缺失量 = 36 ×（158 ÷ 140 − 1）= 36 × 0.12857 = 4.6286 L，四舍五入为 4.6 L。该公式估算水缺失量；临床液体选择和纠正方案需要另行评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Complete the parenthesis first, then multiply by the supplied TBW. Keep liters as the final unit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先完成括号内运算，再乘以给定 TBW。最终单位保留为升。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual Professional Edition, Hypernatremia, water-deficit equation (TBW × [(plasma sodium/140) − 1]), https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/endocrine-and-metabolic-disorders/electrolyte-disorders/hypernatremia","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":true,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2177,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10b_average_sodium_correction_rate","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.707","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.707.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.707.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[257,504],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,200],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic hyponatremia and malnutrition has a serum sodium of 112 mEq/L at 0800 and 118 mEq/L at 2000. Calculate the average correction rate using: (later sodium − earlier sodium) ÷ elapsed hours. Report mEq/L/hr and round to the nearest tenth. The hospital pathway cites the Society for Endocrinology cumulative ceiling of no more than 10 mmol/L in the first 24 hours and 8 mmol/L in each 24 hours thereafter; the team may set a more conservative individualized target for high-risk clients.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性低钠血症并营养不良的患者，0800 血清钠为 112 mEq/L，2000 为 118 mEq/L。使用公式：（较晚血钠 − 较早血钠）÷ 经过小时数，计算平均纠正速度。以 mEq/L/hr 报告，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。医院路径引用内分泌学会的累计上限：首个 24 小时不超过 10 mmol/L，此后每个 24 小时不超过 8 mmol/L；对高风险患者，团队可设定更保守的个体化目标。","terminalSentenceEn":"The hospital pathway cites the Society for Endocrinology cumulative ceiling of no more than 10 mmol/L in the first 24 hours and 8 mmol/L in each 24 hours thereafter; the team may set a more conservative individualized target for high-risk clients.","terminalSentenceZh":"医院路径引用内分泌学会的累计上限：首个 24 小时不超过 10 mmol/L，此后每个 24 小时不超过 8 mmol/L；对高风险患者，团队可设定更保守的个体化目标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Report mEq/L/hr and round to the nearest tenth.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以 mEq/L/hr 报告，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"average sodium correction rate (mEq/L/hr)","zh":"平均血钠纠正速度（mEq/L/hr）"},"acceptable":["0.5","0.5 mEq/L/hr","0.5 mmol/L/hr"],"numeric":{"value":0.5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mEq/L/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sodium increased by 6 mEq/L over 12 hours. Average rate = 6 ÷ 12 = 0.5 mEq/L/hr. The cumulative rise so far is 6 mEq/L, below the stated first-24-hour ceiling, but the average hourly rate is not a universal prescription and continued frequent monitoring is required, especially in a high-risk client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钠在 12 小时内上升 6 mEq/L。平均速度 = 6 ÷ 12 = 0.5 mEq/L/hr。到目前为止累计上升 6 mEq/L，低于题干所述首个 24 小时上限，但该平均小时速度不是普遍处方，尤其对高风险患者仍需持续频繁监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the exact elapsed interval: 0800 to 2000 is 12 hours. Compare the cumulative change with the stated pathway only after calculating.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用准确经过时间：0800 到 2000 为 12 小时。先完成计算，再将累计变化与题干路径比较。","sourceMetadata":"Society for Endocrinology, Emergency management of severe symptomatic hyponatraemia in adult patients, Endocrine Connections 2022, treatment limits section (limit sodium increase to 10 mmol/L in first 24 hours and 8 mmol/L during each 24 hours thereafter), https://www.endocrinology.org/media/3436/emergency-management-of-severe-symptomatic-hyponatraemia-in-adult-patients.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2178,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10b_rapid_shallow_breathing_index","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.708","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.708.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.708.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[265,395],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,144],"fullStemEn":"During a spontaneous breathing assessment, the respiratory rate is 24 breaths/min and tidal volume is 300 mL. Use RSBI = respiratory frequency ÷ tidal volume in liters. Convert tidal volume to liters, calculate breaths/min/L, and round to the nearest whole number. This item asks only for documentation of the index; RSBI alone is not required to determine spontaneous-breathing-trial readiness.","fullStemZh":"在一次自主呼吸评估中，呼吸频率为 24 次/分，潮气量为 300 mL。使用公式：RSBI = 呼吸频率 ÷ 以升为单位的潮气量。先把潮气量换算为升，再计算 breaths/min/L，并四舍五入至最接近的整数。本题只要求记录该指数；RSBI 单独并不是判断自主呼吸试验准备度的必需条件。","terminalSentenceEn":"This item asks only for documentation of the index; RSBI alone is not required to determine spontaneous-breathing-trial readiness.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题只要求记录该指数；RSBI 单独并不是判断自主呼吸试验准备度的必需条件。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Convert tidal volume to liters, calculate breaths/min/L, and round to the nearest whole number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"先把潮气量换算为升，再计算 breaths/min/L，并四舍五入至最接近的整数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"RSBI (breaths/min/L)","zh":"RSBI（breaths/min/L）"},"acceptable":["80","80 breaths/min/L","80 breaths/minute/liter"],"numeric":{"value":80,"tolerance":0,"unit":"breaths/min/L"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"300 mL = 0.300 L. RSBI = 24 ÷ 0.300 = 80 breaths/min/L. The AARC guideline describes RSBI as frequency divided by tidal volume in liters and recommends that it not be required as the sole determinant of readiness for a spontaneous breathing trial.","rationaleCorrectZh":"300 mL = 0.300 L。RSBI = 24 ÷ 0.300 = 80 breaths/min/L。AARC 指南将 RSBI 定义为呼吸频率除以升为单位的潮气量，并建议不应要求把它作为判断自主呼吸试验准备度的唯一依据。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert milliliters to liters before dividing; otherwise the answer will be off by a factor of 1,000.","testTakingStrategyZh":"除法前先把毫升换算为升，否则答案会相差 1,000 倍。","sourceMetadata":"American Association for Respiratory Care, Clinical Practice Guideline: Spontaneous Breathing Trials for Liberation From Adult Mechanical Ventilation, 2024, RSBI definition and Recommendation 1 (RSBI not needed to determine readiness for an SBT), https://www.aarc.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/cpg-sbt-2024.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":true,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2179,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10c_pediatric_rabies_pep_sequence","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.709","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.709.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.709.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[390,490],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,145],"fullStemEn":"A healthy, immunocompetent 4-year-old who has never received rabies vaccine is bitten on the forearm by a raccoon that cannot be captured for testing. Saliva entered the puncture wounds. The local health department determines that rabies post-exposure prophylaxis (PEP) is indicated. Place the supplied milestones in order, beginning at the scene and continuing through the vaccine series. Keep human rabies immune globulin (HRIG) and the day-0 vaccine together as one same-visit milestone.","fullStemZh":"一名健康、免疫功能正常且从未接种狂犬病疫苗的 4 岁儿童，前臂被一只无法捕获检测的浣熊咬伤，唾液进入穿刺伤口。当地卫生部门判定需要狂犬病暴露后预防（PEP）。请从现场开始，按顺序排列所给里程碑，直到完成疫苗系列。将人狂犬病免疫球蛋白（HRIG）和第 0 天疫苗保留为同一次就诊的一个里程碑。","terminalSentenceEn":"Keep human rabies immune globulin (HRIG) and the day-0 vaccine together as one same-visit milestone.","terminalSentenceZh":"将人狂犬病免疫球蛋白（HRIG）和第 0 天疫苗保留为同一次就诊的一个里程碑。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Place the supplied milestones in order, beginning at the scene and continuing through the vaccine series.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请从现场开始，按顺序排列所给里程碑，直到完成疫苗系列。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Obtain urgent medical and public-health exposure assessment; confirm the animal, exposure route, prior vaccination, and immune status.","zh":"紧急进行医学及公共卫生暴露评估；确认动物、暴露途径、既往接种及免疫状态。"},{"id":"D","en":"Complete the remaining rabies vaccine doses on days 3, 7, and 14.","zh":"在第 3、7 和 14 天完成其余狂犬病疫苗剂次。"},{"id":"A","en":"Immediately wash and irrigate all bite wounds thoroughly with soap and water.","zh":"立即用肥皂和水彻底清洗并冲洗所有咬伤。"},{"id":"C","en":"At the day-0 visit, give HRIG infiltrated into and around the wound when feasible and give the first rabies vaccine at a separate site.","zh":"第 0 天就诊时，尽可能将 HRIG 浸润注射于伤口内及周围，并在不同部位给予首剂狂犬病疫苗。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Immediate wound washing and irrigation is the first action. The exposure then requires urgent medical and public-health risk assessment; in this case, that assessment has already determined that PEP is indicated. For an immunocompetent child who has never been vaccinated, the day-0 visit bundles HRIG infiltrated into and around the wound when feasible with the first vaccine dose at a separate anatomic site. Remaining vaccine doses are scheduled for days 3, 7, and 14.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先立即清洗和冲洗伤口。随后需要紧急医学及公共卫生风险评估；在本例中，评估已判定需要 PEP。对免疫功能正常且从未接种过狂犬病疫苗的儿童，第 0 天就诊应把尽可能浸润于伤口内及周围的 HRIG，与在不同解剖部位给予的首剂疫苗作为同一次就诊的组合里程碑。其余疫苗安排在第 3、7 和 14 天。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the timeline anchors: immediate local care, same-day assessment, bundled day-0 biologics, then future vaccine dates.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用时间锚点：立即局部处理、当天评估、第 0 天生物制品组合，再到未来疫苗日期。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Rabies Post-exposure Prophylaxis Guidance, sections 'PEP for individuals without previous rabies vaccination' and 'Wound care' (immediate wound cleansing; HRIG plus vaccine on day 0; vaccine days 3, 7, and 14 for immunocompetent persons), https://www.cdc.gov/rabies/hcp/clinical-care/post-exposure-prophylaxis.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2180,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10c_occupational_sharps_hiv_pep_sequence","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.710","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Standard Precautions & Hygiene","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.710.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.710.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[264,325],"terminalOffsetsZh":[75,94],"fullStemEn":"A nurse sustains a deep puncture from a hollow-bore needle just used in a client's vein. The source client's HIV status is unknown, and the nurse is not taking PrEP. During urgent occupational-health evaluation, the clinician determines that HIV PEP is indicated. Place the exposed nurse's postexposure-care actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名护士被刚用于患者静脉的空心针深度刺伤。来源患者的 HIV 状态未知，护士未使用 PrEP。在紧急职业健康评估中，临床人员判定需要 HIV PEP。请按顺序排列暴露护士的暴露后照护措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the exposed nurse's postexposure-care actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列暴露护士的暴露后照护措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During urgent occupational-health evaluation, the clinician determines that HIV PEP is indicated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在紧急职业健康评估中，临床人员判定需要 HIV PEP。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Return within 72 hours for reassessment of PEP tolerability, adherence, counseling needs, and any source result; stop PEP and HIV follow-up if the source is confirmed HIV negative.","zh":"72 小时内复诊，评估 PEP 耐受性、依从性、咨询需求及来源结果；若来源确认 HIV 阴性，停止 PEP 和 HIV 随访。"},{"id":"E","en":"Complete follow-up testing under the occupational pathway, including final HIV Ag/Ab plus NAT at 12 weeks; add 4- to 6-week testing if the guideline's stated conditions apply.","zh":"按职业健康路径完成随访检测，包括第 12 周最终 HIV 抗原/抗体加 NAT；若符合指南所述条件，则增加第 4–6 周检测。"},{"id":"A","en":"Immediately wash the puncture site with soap and water.","zh":"立即用肥皂和水清洗刺伤部位。"},{"id":"C","en":"During the initial evaluation, obtain the exposed worker's baseline tests and start the recommended PEP regimen as soon as possible.","zh":"在初始评估期间采集暴露工作人员的基线检测，并尽快开始推荐的 PEP 方案。"},{"id":"B","en":"Report the exposure immediately and begin occupational-health evaluation.","zh":"立即报告暴露并开始职业健康评估。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First wash the puncture with soap and water. Report the exposure immediately and enter occupational-health evaluation. During the initial evaluation, obtain the exposed worker's baseline tests and start indicated PEP as soon as possible. Source-patient testing proceeds concurrently and must not delay PEP; PEP and HIV follow-up can stop if the source is confirmed HIV negative. Re-evaluate within 72 hours for tolerability, adherence, counseling, and new source information. Complete the scheduled exposed-worker testing, including final Ag/Ab plus NAT at 12 weeks; interim 4- to 6-week testing is added when the 2025 guideline's conditions apply.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先用肥皂和水清洗刺伤。立即报告暴露并进入职业健康评估。在初始评估期间采集暴露工作人员的基线检测，并尽快开始已指征的 PEP。来源患者检测应同步进行，不得延迟 PEP；若来源确认 HIV 阴性，可停止 PEP 和后续 HIV 检测。72 小时内复评耐受性、依从性、咨询需求及新的来源信息。完成计划的暴露工作人员检测，包括第 12 周最终抗原/抗体加 NAT；若符合 2025 指南条件，则增加第 4–6 周中期检测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Order the exposed nurse's care by time horizon: immediate first aid, reporting and evaluation, urgent baseline testing plus PEP initiation, 72-hour reassessment, then scheduled follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按时间阶段排列暴露护士的照护：立即急救、报告和评估、紧急基线检测并开始 PEP、72 小时复评，最后是计划随访。","sourceMetadata":"CDC/NIOSH, Bloodborne Infectious Disease Risk Factors, 'Treatment' section (wash needlestick or sharp punctures with soap and water; report and seek immediate medical care), https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/healthcare/risk-factors/bloodborne-infectious-diseases.html; 2025 U.S. Public Health Service Guidelines for Management of Occupational Exposures to HIV, Recommendations 1-9 and 'Laboratory testing of exposed HCP' (report promptly; initiate PEP as soon as possible up to 72 hours; do not delay for source status; re-evaluate within 72 hours; final Ag/Ab plus NAT at week 12), https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/183609/cdc_183609_DS1.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"During urgent occupational-health evaluation, the clinician determines that HIV PEP is indicated.","controlSentenceZh":"在紧急职业健康评估中，临床人员判定需要 HIV PEP。"}
{"queueIndex":2181,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10c_parenteral_nutrition_discontinuation_plan","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.711","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.711.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.711.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[426,504],"terminalOffsetsZh":[148,172],"fullStemEn":"A client's reliable oral and enteral intake has met the nutrition-support team's individualized non-PN target for 24 hours. The team documents the following parenteral-nutrition discontinuation plan: first verify and document target attainment; adjust the scheduled insulin used specifically for continuous PN; reduce PN to 50% at 1800 for 1 hour; stop PN at 1900; check capillary glucose at 1930. Place the actions in order. The stated times belong to this prescription and are not a universal PN taper.","fullStemZh":"一名患者可靠的口服及肠内摄入已连续 24 小时达到营养支持团队设定的个体化非 PN 目标。团队记录以下肠外营养停用方案：先核实并记录目标已达到；调整专门用于持续 PN 的计划胰岛素；1800 将 PN 降至 50% 持续 1 小时；1900 停止 PN；1930 检查床旁血糖。请按顺序排列措施。题干时间属于本次处方，并非普遍 PN 减量方案。","terminalSentenceEn":"The stated times belong to this prescription and are not a universal PN taper.","terminalSentenceZh":"题干时间属于本次处方，并非普遍 PN 减量方案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"At 1930, check capillary glucose and respond according to the prescribed glucose protocol.","zh":"1930，检查床旁血糖，并按医嘱血糖方案处理。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify and document that reliable oral and enteral intake has met the individualized non-PN target for 24 hours.","zh":"核实并记录可靠的口服及肠内摄入已连续 24 小时达到个体化非 PN 目标。"},{"id":"C","en":"At 1800, reduce the PN infusion to 50% of the current rate for 1 hour.","zh":"1800，将 PN 输注速度降至当前速度的 50%，持续 1 小时。"},{"id":"D","en":"At 1900, stop the PN infusion.","zh":"1900，停止 PN 输注。"},{"id":"B","en":"Before the taper begins, implement the prescribed adjustment to insulin that was scheduled specifically to cover continuous PN.","zh":"在减量开始前，执行针对专门覆盖持续 PN 的计划胰岛素调整医嘱。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adequate reliable non-PN intake is verified before discontinuation. Insulin that was paired with continuous PN must be coordinated before the dextrose delivery falls. The prescribed taper then occurs from 1800 to 1900, followed by stopping PN and checking glucose 30 minutes later. ASPEN teaching supports considering weaning when roughly half of needs are met outside PN, tapering over 1 to 2 hours when appropriate, reducing insulin, and checking glucose 30 to 60 minutes after discontinuation; the exact schedule here is the local order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"停用前先核实可靠的非 PN 摄入已足够。与持续 PN 配套的胰岛素必须在葡萄糖输送下降前协调调整。随后按处方从 1800 到 1900 减量，再停止 PN，并在 30 分钟后检查血糖。ASPEN 教学支持在约一半营养需要由 PN 外途径满足时考虑减量，在适当情况下用 1–2 小时逐步减量、减少胰岛素，并在停用后 30–60 分钟检查血糖；本题具体时间由本地医嘱决定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the supplied clock times after the prerequisites: nutrition adequacy, insulin coordination, taper, stop, post-stop glucose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在先决条件后遵循题干时间：营养充足、协调胰岛素、减量、停止、停用后血糖。","sourceMetadata":"American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN), Back to Basics: Parenteral Nutrition 101, 2025, slide 'How to Safely Wean PN' (consider weaning when approximately 50% of needs are met outside PN; taper over 1-2 hours; reduce insulin if discontinuing PN; check blood sugar 30 minutes to 1 hour after stopping), https://nutritioncare.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Back-to-Basics_Parenteral-Nutrition-101_Glanz.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2182,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10c_ect_continuation_maintenance_plan","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.712","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.712.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.712.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[352,402],"terminalOffsetsZh":[107,118],"fullStemEn":"A client with major depressive disorder reaches remission after an effective acute index ECT course. The team proposes weekly and then biweekly ECT during the first 6 months after remission, with frequency adjusted during periodic symptom and cognitive reviews. If treatment remains necessary after 6 months, sessions may be spaced every 4 to 8 weeks. The client currently has decision-making capacity.","fullStemZh":"一名重度抑郁障碍患者在有效的急性指数 ECT 疗程后达到缓解。团队建议在缓解后的前 6 个月先每周、后每两周进行 ECT，并在定期症状和认知复评中调整频率。如果 6 个月后仍需治疗，疗程可间隔为每 4–8 周一次。患者目前具有决策能力。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client currently has decision-making capacity.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者目前具有决策能力。","penultimateSentenceEn":"If treatment remains necessary after 6 months, sessions may be spaced every 4 to 8 weeks.","penultimateSentenceZh":"如果 6 个月后仍需治疗，疗程可间隔为每 4–8 周一次。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The weekly-to-biweekly phase during the first 6 months is {{1}}. Periodic symptom and cognitive review is used to {{2}}. Consent and capacity should be revisited {{3}}.","zh":"缓解后前 6 个月每周至每两周的阶段属于{{1}}。定期症状和认知复评用于{{2}}。同意和能力应在{{3}}重新审视。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"maintenance ECT after 6 months","zh":"6 个月后的维持期 ECT"},{"id":"o1","en":"continuation ECT","zh":"延续期 ECT"},{"id":"o2","en":"the acute index course","zh":"急性指数疗程"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"measure seizure duration only and keep the schedule fixed","zh":"只测量抽搐持续时间并保持固定日程"},{"id":"o3","en":"replace the need for direct clinical assessment","zh":"取代直接临床评估的需要"},{"id":"o1","en":"balance relapse prevention with adverse effects and dynamically adjust treatment frequency","zh":"平衡复发预防与不良反应，并动态调整治疗频率"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"only after a serious adverse event has already occurred","zh":"仅在严重不良事件已经发生后"},{"id":"o1","en":"before starting continuation or maintenance ECT and again whenever decision-making capacity changes or is regained","zh":"开始延续或维持 ECT 前，以及决策能力改变或恢复时"},{"id":"o2","en":"only once before the original index course, regardless of later changes","zh":"只在原始指数疗程前一次，无论后续如何变化"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ECT used during the first 6 months of remission to consolidate response and prevent relapse is continuation ECT; treatment after 6 months for prophylaxis is maintenance ECT. Periodic clinical and cognitive review is used to balance benefit and adverse effects and dynamically tailor frequency rather than follow a fixed course. Consent must be obtained again before continuation/maintenance ECT because the purpose, frequency, and endpoint have changed, and capacity/consent must be revisited when capacity changes or is regained.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在缓解后的前 6 个月用于巩固疗效和预防复发的 ECT 属于延续期 ECT；6 个月后用于预防的治疗属于维持期 ECT。定期临床和认知复评用于平衡获益与不良反应，并动态调整频率，而不是遵循固定疗程。由于治疗目的、频率和终点已改变，在开始延续/维持 ECT 前必须重新取得同意；当能力改变或恢复时，也必须重新评估能力和同意。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor each blank to a different fact: time phase, purpose of monitoring, and renewed consent/capacity process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"每个空对应不同事实：时间阶段、监测目的以及重新同意/能力流程。","sourceMetadata":"Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Use of Electroconvulsive Therapy, Indian Journal of Psychiatry 2023, sections 'Informed consent,' 'Monitoring of clinical improvement,' 'Monitoring of cognitive adverse effects,' and 'Continuation and maintenance ECT' (continuation through 6 months; maintenance after 6 months; dynamically tailored frequency based on periodic review; renewed consent before C/M ECT and when capacity is regained), https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10096214/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"If treatment remains necessary after 6 months, sessions may be spaced every 4 to 8 weeks.","controlSentenceZh":"如果 6 个月后仍需治疗，疗程可间隔为每 4–8 周一次。"}
{"queueIndex":2183,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10c_dmpa_late_repeat_injection","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.713","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.713.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.713.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[289,333],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,96],"fullStemEn":"A client returns 16 weeks and 3 days after the last DMPA injection. The routine interval is 13 weeks, and the U.S. grace period extends through 15 weeks. The client reports no sexual intercourse since the last injection, and the clinician is reasonably certain the client is not pregnant. The client wants the repeat injection today.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在上次 DMPA 注射后 16 周 3 天返回。常规间隔为 13 周，美国宽限期延长至 15 周。患者报告自上次注射后没有发生性交，临床人员可合理确定患者未妊娠。患者希望今天重复注射。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client wants the repeat injection today.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者希望今天重复注射。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports no sexual intercourse since the last injection, and the clinician is reasonably certain the client is not pregnant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者报告自上次注射后没有发生性交，临床人员可合理确定患者未妊娠。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"At 16 weeks and 3 days, the client is {{1}}. The clinician should {{2}}. Emergency contraception is {{3}}.","zh":"在 16 周 3 天时，患者属于{{1}}。临床人员应{{2}}。紧急避孕{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"within the 15-week grace period","zh":"仍在 15 周宽限期内"},{"id":"o2","en":"within the routine 13-week interval","zh":"仍在常规 13 周间隔内"},{"id":"o1","en":"beyond the 15-week grace period","zh":"已超过 15 周宽限期"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"withhold DMPA until the next menstrual period even though pregnancy is reasonably excluded","zh":"即使可合理排除妊娠，也要停用 DMPA 直到下次月经"},{"id":"o2","en":"give the injection today with no backup protection because any delay under 17 weeks is automatically protected","zh":"今天注射且无需备用保护，因为任何少于 17 周的迟延都自动受保护"},{"id":"o1","en":"give the repeat injection today because pregnancy can be reasonably excluded, then advise abstinence or barrier protection for 7 days","zh":"因可合理排除妊娠而今天重复注射，并建议随后 7 天禁欲或使用屏障避孕"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"automatically required for every injection given after 15 weeks","zh":"每次超过 15 周注射时都自动需要"},{"id":"o1","en":"not indicated because the client reports no intercourse since the last injection","zh":"不需要，因为患者报告上次注射后没有性交"},{"id":"o3","en":"required specifically as ulipristal acetate regardless of sexual history","zh":"无论性交史如何，都必须使用醋酸乌利司他"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At more than 15 weeks, the client is beyond the two-week grace period. Because the clinician is reasonably certain the client is not pregnant, the repeat DMPA injection may be given today, followed by abstinence or barrier protection for 7 days. Emergency contraception is considered only when appropriate after recent unprotected intercourse; in this scenario there has been no intercourse, so it is not indicated. UPA is specifically excluded from the CDC late-injection emergency-contraception consideration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"超过 15 周时，患者已超出两周宽限期。由于临床人员可合理确定患者未妊娠，可在今天给予重复 DMPA 注射，并在随后 7 天禁欲或使用屏障避孕。紧急避孕只在近期无保护性交后适当时考虑；本题没有发生性交，因此不需要。CDC 对迟延注射的紧急避孕考虑中明确排除 UPA。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Calculate weeks first, then apply the exact CDC branch. Do not add emergency contraception when the scenario contains no intercourse.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先计算周数，再应用准确 CDC 分支。情境中没有性交时，不要额外加入紧急避孕。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024, section 'Timing of Repeat Injections' for DMPA (repeat every 13 weeks; up to 15 weeks without additional protection; if more than 15 weeks, inject when reasonably certain not pregnant, use abstinence/barrier protection for 7 days, and consider emergency contraception except UPA if appropriate), https://www.cdc.gov/contraception/hcp/usspr/injectables.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2184,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format10c_latent_vs_active_tuberculosis","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.714","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.714.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.714.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[248,301],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,86],"fullStemEn":"A client has a positive interferon-gamma release assay (IGRA) after workplace screening. The client has no cough, fever, night sweats, weight loss, or fatigue. Chest radiograph is normal, and the medical evaluation finds no evidence of TB disease. If obtained, sputum smears and cultures are negative.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在工作场所筛查后干扰素-γ 释放试验（IGRA）阳性。患者无咳嗽、发热、盗汗、体重下降或疲劳。胸片正常，医学评估未发现结核病证据。如采集痰标本，涂片和培养均为阴性。","terminalSentenceEn":"If obtained, sputum smears and cultures are negative.","terminalSentenceZh":"如采集痰标本，涂片和培养均为阴性。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Chest radiograph is normal, and the medical evaluation finds no evidence of TB disease.","penultimateSentenceZh":"胸片正常，医学评估未发现结核病证据。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The findings are most consistent with {{1}}. The infection-control implication is {{2}}. The positive IGRA means {{3}}.","zh":"这些发现最符合{{1}}。感染控制含义是{{2}}。IGRA 阳性表示{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"latent TB infection","zh":"潜伏性结核感染"},{"id":"o2","en":"active pulmonary TB disease","zh":"活动性肺结核病"},{"id":"o3","en":"no TB infection of any kind","zh":"完全没有结核感染"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"no airborne isolation is needed because latent infection is not contagious","zh":"不需要空气隔离，因为潜伏感染不具传染性"},{"id":"o3","en":"household contacts must be isolated because latent TB spreads through shared air","zh":"家庭接触者必须隔离，因为潜伏结核可经共同空气传播"},{"id":"o2","en":"immediate airborne isolation is required solely because the IGRA is positive","zh":"仅因 IGRA 阳性就必须立即空气隔离"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"TB infection is present, but the test alone does not distinguish latent infection from active disease","zh":"存在结核感染，但该试验单独不能区分潜伏感染与活动性疾病"},{"id":"o2","en":"active contagious pulmonary disease is proven","zh":"已证实活动性传染性肺部疾病"},{"id":"o3","en":"the client is immune to future TB disease and needs no evaluation","zh":"患者对未来结核病已有免疫，无需评估"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A positive IGRA with no symptoms, normal chest imaging, and no microbiologic or clinical evidence of disease supports latent TB infection, not active pulmonary TB. People with latent TB infection cannot spread TB bacteria and do not require respiratory isolation. A positive IGRA indicates TB infection; it cannot by itself distinguish latent infection from active disease, so medical evaluation and chest imaging are needed to exclude disease.","rationaleCorrectZh":"IGRA 阳性而无症状、胸部影像正常，且无微生物或临床疾病证据，支持潜伏性结核感染，而不是活动性肺结核。潜伏性结核感染者不能传播结核菌，不需要呼吸隔离。IGRA 阳性表示结核感染；单独结果不能区分潜伏感染和活动性疾病，因此需要医学评估和胸部影像排除疾病。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate infection from disease. The screening test shows immune sensitization to TB; symptoms, imaging, and microbiology determine whether active disease is present.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分感染与疾病。筛查试验显示对结核菌的免疫致敏；症状、影像和微生物结果决定是否存在活动性疾病。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, Clinical Overview of Latent Tuberculosis Infection and Clinical Overview of Tuberculosis, sections comparing latent TB infection with TB disease (positive test indicates infection; normal chest radiograph and negative sputum with no symptoms support latent infection; latent TB is not contagious and does not require respiratory isolation; further evaluation is needed to exclude disease), https://www.cdc.gov/tb/hcp/clinical-overview/latent-tuberculosis-infection.html; https://www.cdc.gov/tb/hcp/clinical-overview/index.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2185,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8a_haloperidol_qtcf","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.715","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Psychotropic Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.715.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.715.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[270,375],"terminalOffsetsZh":[133,160],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving haloperidol has an ECG with a measured QT interval of 360 ms and an RR interval of 0.729 second. Use the FDA E14 Fridericia correction: QTcF = QT ÷ RR^(1/3), with RR expressed in seconds. Calculate the QTcF and round to the nearest whole millisecond. This item asks only for the corrected interval; do not make a medication decision from this number alone.","fullStemZh":"一名使用氟哌啶醇的患者，其心电图测得 QT 间期为 360 ms，RR 间期为 0.729 秒。请使用 FDA E14 的 Fridericia 校正公式：QTcF = QT ÷ RR^(1/3)，其中 RR 以秒表示。计算 QTcF，并四舍五入至最接近的整数毫秒。本题只要求计算校正后间期；不能仅凭该数值决定是否用药。","terminalSentenceEn":"This item asks only for the corrected interval; do not make a medication decision from this number alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题只要求计算校正后间期；不能仅凭该数值决定是否用药。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the QTcF and round to the nearest whole millisecond.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算 QTcF，并四舍五入至最接近的整数毫秒。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"QTcF (ms)","zh":"QTcF（ms）"},"acceptable":["400","400 ms","400 milliseconds"],"numeric":{"value":400,"tolerance":0,"unit":"ms"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The cube root of 0.729 is 0.9. Therefore, QTcF = 360 ÷ 0.9 = 400 ms. FDA E14 identifies Fridericia correction as QTc = QT/RR^0.33. Haloperidol labeling warns about QTc prolongation and supports ECG and electrolyte monitoring when clinically indicated, but this calculation alone does not determine treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"0.729 的立方根为 0.9。因此，QTcF = 360 ÷ 0.9 = 400 ms。FDA E14 将 Fridericia 校正定义为 QTc = QT/RR^0.33。氟哌啶醇说明书警示 QTc 延长风险，并支持在临床需要时监测心电图和电解质，但单次计算结果不能独立决定治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Keep QT in milliseconds and RR in seconds as specified. Evaluate the cube root of RR before dividing QT.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干要求保留 QT 的毫秒单位和 RR 的秒单位。先求 RR 的立方根，再用 QT 相除。","sourceMetadata":"FDA, E14 Clinical Evaluation of QT/QTc Interval Prolongation and Proarrhythmic Potential for Non-Antiarrhythmic Drugs, section III.A.1 Population-Derived Correction Formulae (Fridericia QTc = QT/RR^0.33), https://www.fda.gov/media/71372/download; DailyMed, Haloperidol Decanoate Injection prescribing information, revised 1/2026, sections 5.2 and 7.1 (QTc risk and ECG/electrolyte monitoring), https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=8ffac6fb-1702-40d6-b085-152d24673cbd","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":true,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2186,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8a_dka_glucose_decline_rate","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.716","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.716.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.716.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[227,272],"terminalOffsetsZh":[89,110],"fullStemEn":"An adult being treated for diabetic ketoacidosis has a blood glucose of 438 mg/dL at 0900 and 318 mg/dL at 1100. Calculate the average glucose decline using: average decline = (earlier glucose − later glucose) ÷ elapsed hours. Enter the rate as a whole number in mg/dL/hr.","fullStemZh":"一名接受糖尿病酮症酸中毒治疗的成人，0900 血糖为 438 mg/dL，1100 血糖为 318 mg/dL。请使用：平均下降速度 =（较早血糖 − 较晚血糖）÷ 经过小时数。以整数填写结果，单位为 mg/dL/hr。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the rate as a whole number in mg/dL/hr.","terminalSentenceZh":"以整数填写结果，单位为 mg/dL/hr。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the average glucose decline using: average decline = (earlier glucose − later glucose) ÷ elapsed hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请使用：平均下降速度 =（较早血糖 − 较晚血糖）÷ 经过小时数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mg/dL/hr","zh":"mg/dL/hr"},"acceptable":["60","60 mg/dL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":60,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mg/dL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The glucose decreased by 120 mg/dL over 2 hours: (438 − 318) ÷ 2 = 60 mg/dL/hr. The 2024 consensus report notes that initial therapy commonly lowers glucose by about 50–70 mg/dL per hour. This calculation evaluates the glucose trajectory; it does not by itself establish DKA resolution.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血糖在 2 小时内下降 120 mg/dL：（438 − 318）÷2 = 60 mg/dL/hr。2024 年共识报告指出，初始治疗时血糖通常每小时下降约 50–70 mg/dL。该计算用于评估血糖变化速度，但单凭此结果不能判断 DKA 已缓解。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Find the absolute decrease first, then divide by the two-hour interval. Do not divide by clock times.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先计算血糖下降的绝对值，再除以 2 小时。不要直接用钟点数字相除。","sourceMetadata":"ADA/EASD/JBDS/AACE/DTS, Hyperglycemic Crises in Adults With Diabetes: A Consensus Report, Diabetes Care 2024;47:1257-1275, Treatment of DKA—fluid therapy and monitoring, https://diabetesjournals.org/care/article/47/8/1257/156808/Hyperglycemic-Crises-in-Adults-With-Diabetes-A","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2187,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8a_car_t_ice_score","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.717","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.717.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.717.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[676,710],"terminalOffsetsZh":[246,259],"fullStemEn":"A nurse performs the adult 10-point Immune Effector Cell-Associated Encephalopathy (ICE) assessment after CAR-T therapy. Use this complete scoring excerpt: orientation to year, month, city, and hospital = 1 point each (4 total); name three objects = 1 point each (3 total); follow one simple command = 1 point; write one standard sentence = 1 point; count backward from 100 by tens = 1 point. Responses: the client states the correct year, an incorrect month, the correct city, and the correct hospital; correctly names a cup and a key but calls a pen a pencil; closes the eyes when asked; writes \"I feel tired today\"; and counts 100, 90, 80, 70. What is the total ICE score? Enter a whole number from 0 to 10.","fullStemZh":"CAR-T 治疗后，护士进行成人 10 分制免疫效应细胞相关脑病（ICE）评估。请使用完整评分摘录：年份、月份、城市和医院各答对得 1 分（共 4 分）；说出 3 件物品名称，每件 1 分（共 3 分）；执行一项简单指令得 1 分；写出一个完整标准句子得 1 分；从 100 开始每次减 10 倒数得 1 分。患者表现：年份正确、月份错误、城市正确、医院正确；能正确说出杯子和钥匙，但把钢笔说成铅笔；按要求闭眼；写出“我今天觉得很累”；并能倒数 100、90、80、70。ICE 总分是多少？请填写 0–10 的整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter a whole number from 0 to 10.","terminalSentenceZh":"请填写 0–10 的整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"What is the total ICE score?","penultimateSentenceZh":"ICE 总分是多少？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"ICE score (0–10)","zh":"ICE 评分（0–10）"},"acceptable":["8","8/10"],"numeric":{"value":8,"tolerance":0,"unit":"points"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Orientation earns 3 points, object naming earns 2, following the command earns 1, writing the sentence earns 1, and counting backward earns 1. Total: 3 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 8. The ICE score is one component of ICANS assessment; the score alone does not establish an ICANS grade.","rationaleCorrectZh":"定向力得 3 分，物品命名得 2 分，执行指令得 1 分，写句子得 1 分，倒数得 1 分。总分：3 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 8。ICE 评分只是 ICANS 评估的一部分，不能仅凭该分数确定 ICANS 分级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Score each domain separately, then add the five domain subtotals. Do not infer a toxicity grade that the question did not ask for.","testTakingStrategyZh":"逐项评分后再相加五个领域的小计。题目只问 ICE 总分，不要额外推断毒性分级。","sourceMetadata":"ASTCT consensus grading for immune effector cell-associated neurotoxicity syndrome, adult ICE assessment table (10-point tool), https://www.astctjournal.org/article/S1083-8791%25252818%25252931691-4/fulltext; ASCO CAR-T adverse-event guideline, neurologic toxicity section, https://ascopubs.org/doi/10.1200/JCO.21.01992","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2188,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8a_ect_seizure_duration","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.718","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.718.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.718.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[155,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,58],"fullStemEn":"During electroconvulsive therapy, the seizure begins at 09:14:22 and ends at 09:15:05. How many seconds should the nurse document as the seizure duration? Enter a whole number.","fullStemZh":"电休克治疗过程中，发作于 09:14:22 开始，于 09:15:05 结束。护士应记录发作持续多少秒？请填写整数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter a whole number.","terminalSentenceZh":"请填写整数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many seconds should the nurse document as the seizure duration?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应记录发作持续多少秒？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"seconds","zh":"秒"},"acceptable":["43","43 seconds","43 sec"],"numeric":{"value":43,"tolerance":0,"unit":"seconds"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"From 09:14:22 to 09:15:00 is 38 seconds, and 5 more seconds gives 43 seconds. ECT guidance emphasizes seizure quality and the overall clinical response rather than treating one fixed duration as proof of adequacy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"从 09:14:22 到 09:15:00 为 38 秒，再加 5 秒，共 43 秒。ECT 指南强调发作质量和总体临床反应，而不是把某个固定持续时间当作疗效充分的证明。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the interval crosses a minute, count to the next full minute first, then add the remaining seconds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"跨分钟计算时，先算到下一个整分钟，再加剩余秒数。","sourceMetadata":"Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Use of Electroconvulsive Therapy, Indian Journal of Psychiatry 2023, seizure monitoring section, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10096214/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2189,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8a_sleep_efficiency_week","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.719","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.719.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.719.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[268,303],"terminalOffsetsZh":[151,166],"fullStemEn":"A seven-night sleep diary records total sleep time (TST) and time in bed (TIB), in hours: Night 1: 6.0/7.5; Night 2: 5.5/7.0; Night 3: 6.5/8.0; Night 4: 6.0/7.5; Night 5: 7.0/8.0; Night 6: 5.0/7.0; Night 7: 6.0/7.0. Use sleep efficiency = total TST ÷ total TIB × 100. Round to the nearest whole percent.","fullStemZh":"七晚睡眠日记记录了总睡眠时间（TST）和卧床时间（TIB），单位为小时：第1晚 6.0/7.5；第2晚 5.5/7.0；第3晚 6.5/8.0；第4晚 6.0/7.5；第5晚 7.0/8.0；第6晚 5.0/7.0；第7晚 6.0/7.0。请使用：睡眠效率 = 总 TST ÷ 总 TIB × 100。四舍五入到最接近的整数百分比。","terminalSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest whole percent.","terminalSentenceZh":"四舍五入到最接近的整数百分比。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Use sleep efficiency = total TST ÷ total TIB × 100.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请使用：睡眠效率 = 总 TST ÷ 总 TIB × 100。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"sleep efficiency (%)","zh":"睡眠效率（%）"},"acceptable":["81","81%"],"numeric":{"value":81,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The seven-night totals are 42 hours of sleep and 52 hours in bed. 42 ÷ 52 × 100 = 80.77%, which rounds to 81%. A sleep-efficiency value is one diary measure and does not by itself diagnose insomnia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"七晚合计睡眠 42 小时，卧床 52 小时。42 ÷ 52 × 100 = 80.77%，四舍五入为 81%。睡眠效率只是睡眠日记的一项指标，不能单独用于诊断失眠。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Add all seven TST values and all seven TIB values before applying the formula; do not average the nightly percentages.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先分别相加七晚的 TST 和 TIB，再代入公式；不要先计算每晚百分比再取平均。","sourceMetadata":"American Academy of Sleep Medicine, sleep-efficiency definition (total sleep time divided by time in bed), https://aasm.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/PharmacologicTreatmentofInsomnia.pdf; VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Chronic Insomnia Disorder and Obstructive Sleep Apnea, 2025, https://www.healthquality.va.gov/guidelines/CD/insomnia/index.asp","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2190,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8a_pf_ratio","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.720","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.720.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.720.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,116],"fullStemEn":"An adult receiving supplemental oxygen has a PaO₂ of 72 mm Hg while the FiO₂ is 0.40. Use P/F ratio = PaO₂ ÷ FiO₂. Calculate the P/F ratio and enter a whole number in mm Hg. This question asks only for the ratio; a ratio alone does not diagnose ARDS.","fullStemZh":"一名接受补充氧疗的成人，PaO₂ 为 72 mm Hg，FiO₂ 为 0.40。请使用：P/F 比值 = PaO₂ ÷ FiO₂。计算 P/F 比值并以整数填写，单位为 mm Hg。本题只要求计算比值；单凭该比值不能诊断 ARDS。","terminalSentenceEn":"This question asks only for the ratio; a ratio alone does not diagnose ARDS.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题只要求计算比值；单凭该比值不能诊断 ARDS。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the P/F ratio and enter a whole number in mm Hg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算 P/F 比值并以整数填写，单位为 mm Hg。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"P/F ratio (mm Hg)","zh":"P/F 比值（mm Hg）"},"acceptable":["180","180 mm Hg","180 mmHg"],"numeric":{"value":180,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mm Hg"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"72 ÷ 0.40 = 180 mm Hg. The global ARDS definition uses oxygenation criteria together with timing, imaging, the origin of pulmonary edema, and the required oxygen-delivery/PEEP conditions; the P/F ratio is not a stand-alone diagnosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"72 ÷ 0.40 = 180 mm Hg。全球 ARDS 定义会把氧合指标与发病时间、影像学、肺水肿原因以及规定的氧疗或 PEEP 条件结合判断；P/F 比值不能单独作为诊断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use FiO₂ as a decimal fraction. Divide by 0.40, not by 40.","testTakingStrategyZh":"FiO₂ 应使用小数形式。应除以 0.40，而不是 40。","sourceMetadata":"Matthay et al., A New Global Definition of Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome, oxygenation table and definition conditions, Am J Respir Crit Care Med. 2024;209:37-47, https://doi.org/10.1164/rccm.202303-0558WS","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":true,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2191,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8b_ulipristal_followup_timeline","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.721","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.721.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.721.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,66],"fullStemEn":"A client took ulipristal acetate emergency contraception today and plans to resume a combined oral contraceptive. The pregnancy test today is negative. Place the supplied CDC follow-up actions in chronological order.","fullStemZh":"一名患者今天服用了醋酸乌利司他紧急避孕药，并计划恢复复方口服避孕药。今天的妊娠试验为阴性。请按时间顺序排列 CDC 建议的后续措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the supplied CDC follow-up actions in chronological order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按时间顺序排列 CDC 建议的后续措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The pregnancy test today is negative.","penultimateSentenceZh":"今天的妊娠试验为阴性。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"During days 0–5 after ulipristal, do not restart the hormonal method; use abstinence or condoms.","zh":"服用乌利司他后的第 0–5 天，不恢复激素避孕；禁欲或使用安全套。"},{"id":"B","en":"On day 6, start or resume the chosen hormonal method.","zh":"第 6 天开始或恢复所选激素避孕法。"},{"id":"C","en":"For 7 days after restarting the pill—or until the next menses, whichever comes first—continue abstinence or condoms.","zh":"恢复口服避孕药后的 7 天内，或直到下次月经来潮（以较早者为准），继续禁欲或使用安全套。"},{"id":"D","en":"At 3 weeks after ulipristal, perform a pregnancy test if no withdrawal bleed has occurred.","zh":"服用乌利司他 3 周后，如未出现撤退性出血，进行妊娠试验。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After ulipristal acetate, wait at least 5 days before starting or resuming a hormonal method. Use abstinence or a barrier method during that waiting period and for 7 days after the hormonal method is started or resumed. If no withdrawal bleed occurs within 3 weeks, perform a pregnancy test.","rationaleCorrectZh":"服用醋酸乌利司他后，至少等待 5 天再开始或恢复激素避孕法。等待期间以及开始或恢复激素避孕法后的 7 天内，应禁欲或使用屏障避孕。如果 3 周内没有撤退性出血，应进行妊娠试验。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor the sequence to the ulipristal dose: five-day delay first, hormonal-method restart second, seven days of backup next, and conditional testing at three weeks last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"以服用乌利司他的当天为起点：先等待 5 天，再恢复激素避孕，随后继续 7 天备用避孕，最后在 3 周时按条件验孕。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024, Use of Regular Contraception After ECPs—Ulipristal Acetate, https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/73/rr/rr7303a1.htm","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2192,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8b_doxorubicin_extravasation","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.722","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.722.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.722.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[295,317],"terminalOffsetsZh":[101,108],"fullStemEn":"During a peripheral doxorubicin infusion, the client reports burning and swelling at the IV site. The facility follows eviQ's SLAP pathway and its doxorubicin plan: after assessment, apply a cold compress for 15–20 minutes and initiate the ordered DMSO 99% protocol. Place the actions in order. Do not flush the line.","fullStemZh":"外周静脉输注多柔比星时，患者诉静脉部位灼痛并出现肿胀。机构采用 eviQ 的 SLAP 流程及多柔比星处理方案：完成评估后，冷敷 15–20 分钟，并开始医嘱中的 99% DMSO 方案。请按顺序排列。不要冲洗管路。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not flush the line.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要冲洗管路。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Assess the site, outline the affected area, and photograph it for the medical record.","zh":"评估部位，标记受累区域，并拍照存入医疗记录。"},{"id":"C","en":"Using a syringe, aspirate residual drug from the device without flushing.","zh":"用注射器经通路抽吸残留药物，不要冲洗。"},{"id":"B","en":"Leave the peripheral vascular access device in place.","zh":"将外周血管通路保留在原位。"},{"id":"E","en":"Initiate the doxorubicin-specific cold-compress and ordered DMSO 99% plan.","zh":"开始多柔比星特异性的冷敷及医嘱中的 99% DMSO 方案。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the doxorubicin infusion immediately and send for help.","zh":"立即停止多柔比星输注并呼叫协助。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The eviQ primary sequence is STOP, LEAVE, ASPIRATE, PLAN. After aspiration, assess, outline, and photograph the area, then initiate the named doxorubicin-specific cold-compress and DMSO plan. Removing or flushing the device before aspiration can spread or lose access to residual vesicant.","rationaleCorrectZh":"eviQ 的首要顺序为 STOP（停止）、LEAVE（保留）、ASPIRATE（抽吸）、PLAN（计划）。抽吸后评估、标记并拍照，再执行题干所指定的多柔比星冷敷与 DMSO 方案。在抽吸前拔除或冲洗通路可能使残留发疱剂扩散，或失去抽吸通道。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the SLAP acronym as the backbone. Assessment and agent-specific treatment occur after residual drug has been aspirated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"以 SLAP 首字母顺序为主线。先抽吸残留药物，再进行评估和药物特异性处理。","sourceMetadata":"eviQ ID 157 v.6, Extravasation management, Primary actions: SLAP and secondary actions, https://www.eviq.org.au/clinical-resources/extravasation/157-extravasation-management; eviQ ID 1002 v.6, Quicklink summary table—Doxorubicin: cold compress and DMSO 99% solution, https://www.eviq.org.au/clinical-resources/extravasation/1002-quicklink-summary-table-treatments-for-extr","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2193,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8b_palliative_breathlessness_plan","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.723","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.723.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.723.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[375,402],"terminalOffsetsZh":[108,115],"fullStemEn":"A comfort-focused client develops distressing breathlessness. The individualized plan directs the nurse to assess for a reversible contributor, use immediate comfort measures, administer the already-prescribed PRN medicine if distress continues, reassess 20 minutes later, and call the palliative-care clinician if distress persists. The client is not known to be hypoxemic. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名以舒适照护为目标的患者出现明显呼吸困难。个体化方案要求护士先评估可逆因素，立即采取舒适措施，如不适持续则给予已有医嘱的 PRN 药物，20 分钟后复评；若仍明显不适则联系姑息治疗临床人员。患者目前无已知低氧血症。请按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is not known to be hypoxemic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者目前无已知低氧血症。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Perform a focused assessment for a reversible contributor to the breathlessness.","zh":"针对可能可逆的呼吸困难因素进行重点评估。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the prescribed PRN medicine because distress remains after the comfort measures.","zh":"舒适措施后呼吸困难仍持续，给予已有医嘱的 PRN 药物。"},{"id":"E","en":"Notify the palliative-care clinician because significant distress persists after reassessment.","zh":"复评后明显不适仍持续，联系姑息治疗临床人员。"},{"id":"B","en":"Sit the client upright, provide calm reassurance, and use cool moving air from a fan.","zh":"协助患者坐起，给予平静安慰，并用风扇提供凉爽流动空气。"},{"id":"D","en":"Reassess breathlessness and adverse effects 20 minutes after the PRN medicine.","zh":"PRN 药物后 20 分钟复评呼吸困难及不良反应。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The plan stated in the stem proceeds from focused assessment to immediate nonpharmacologic comfort, then the prescribed PRN medicine, timed reassessment, and escalation if distress persists. Routine oxygen is not inserted when symptomatic hypoxemia has not been established.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该个体化方案依次为：针对性评估、立即非药物舒适措施、给予已有医嘱的 PRN 药物、按时复评，以及在不适持续时升级处理。题干未证实症状性低氧血症，因此不应自行加入常规氧疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the sequence explicitly supplied by the individualized plan rather than adding a generic intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按照题干给出的个体化方案顺序作答，不要自行加入通用措施。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG31, Care of dying adults in the last days of life, recommendations 1.5.15-1.5.17 (breathlessness), https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client is not known to be hypoxemic.","controlSentenceZh":"患者目前无已知低氧血症。"}
{"queueIndex":2194,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8b_toddler_unknown_ingestion","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.724","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.724.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.724.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[159,258],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,76],"fullStemEn":"A conscious, breathing toddler may have swallowed an unknown household product. The child is currently awake, has no seizure, and has no breathing difficulty. Place the Poison Control actions described in the scenario in the order the nurse should take them.","fullStemZh":"一名意识清醒、呼吸正常的幼儿可能吞下了不明家用产品。孩子目前清醒，无抽搐，也无呼吸困难。请按顺序排列题干限定的 Poison Control 处理流程。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the Poison Control actions described in the scenario in the order the nurse should take them.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列题干限定的 Poison Control 处理流程。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The child is currently awake, has no seizure, and has no breathing difficulty.","penultimateSentenceZh":"孩子目前清醒，无抽搐，也无呼吸困难。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Carry out the product-specific instructions provided by Poison Control or webPOISONCONTROL.","zh":"执行 Poison Control 或 webPOISONCONTROL 提供的产品特异性指示。"},{"id":"C","en":"Contact Poison Control or webPOISONCONTROL with the product container and exposure details ready.","zh":"准备好产品容器和暴露信息，联系 Poison Control 或 webPOISONCONTROL。"},{"id":"B","en":"Rapidly assess for collapse, seizure, trouble breathing, or inability to awaken; call 911 if any is present.","zh":"快速评估是否倒地、抽搐、呼吸困难或无法唤醒；如有任何一项，拨打 911。"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove the product and prevent any further access.","zh":"移走该产品，防止继续接触。"},{"id":"E","en":"Continue monitoring and escalate if directed or if new red-flag symptoms develop.","zh":"继续观察，并在接到指示或出现新的危险症状时升级处理。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First stop further access, then rapidly screen for emergency red flags. Because none are present, contact Poison Control or webPOISONCONTROL with the container and exposure details. Follow the product-specific instructions and continue monitoring or escalation exactly as directed. Do not induce vomiting or give a universal dilution.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先阻止继续接触，然后快速筛查紧急危险信号。由于目前无危险信号，应携带容器及暴露信息联系 Poison Control 或 webPOISONCONTROL。随后按产品特异性指示处理，并依照指示继续观察或升级。不要催吐，也不要自行给予通用稀释液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the emergency screen from Poison Control consultation: 911 red flags would change the branch, but this stem states they are absent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把紧急筛查与 Poison Control 咨询分开。若出现 911 危险信号，流程会改变；本题已明确这些信号不存在。","sourceMetadata":"Poison Control, First aid: Act fast!, swallowed-poison pathway and 911 criteria, https://www.poison.org/first-aid-for-poisonings","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2195,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8b_abg_specimen_workflow","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.725","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.725.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.725.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[321,366],"terminalOffsetsZh":[78,90],"fullStemEn":"A nurse who is trained, credentialed, and acting within facility scope will obtain a radial arterial blood gas specimen. A second trained staff member is available to maintain puncture-site pressure while the collector handles the specimen. Facility policy requires immediate delivery to the laboratory after collection. Place the bounded specimen workflow in order.","fullStemZh":"一名已受训、具备资质且在机构执业范围内的护士将采集桡动脉血气标本。另一名已受训工作人员可在采集者处理标本时持续压迫穿刺点。机构政策要求采集后立即送达实验室。请按顺序排列该限定流程。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the bounded specimen workflow in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列该限定流程。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires immediate delivery to the laboratory after collection.","penultimateSentenceZh":"机构政策要求采集后立即送达实验室。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Label the specimen at the bedside with the required identifiers and collection time.","zh":"在床旁用规定身份信息和采集时间标记标本。"},{"id":"C","en":"Withdraw the needle and have the second trained staff member immediately apply firm pressure to the puncture site.","zh":"拔针后，由另一名已受训工作人员立即牢固压迫穿刺点。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify the client and order, explain the procedure, perform hand hygiene, and prepare the selected radial site using aseptic technique.","zh":"核对患者和医嘱，解释操作，手卫生，并以无菌技术准备所选桡动脉部位。"},{"id":"B","en":"Collect the arterial specimen into the prepared heparinized blood-gas syringe.","zh":"用准备好的肝素化血气注射器采集动脉标本。"},{"id":"F","en":"Send the specimen to the laboratory immediately according to policy.","zh":"按机构政策立即将标本送往实验室。"},{"id":"D","en":"While the second trained staff member maintains firm pressure, expel visible air bubbles, cap the syringe securely, and gently mix the specimen.","zh":"由另一名已受训工作人员持续牢固压迫时，排出可见气泡，牢固封帽，并轻柔混匀标本。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The serial workflow is identity and site preparation, arterial collection, firm pressure, removal of air and secure capping/mixing, bedside labeling, then immediate transport. This item does not treat an Allen test as a universal permission rule.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该顺序为：核对身份并准备部位、采集动脉血、牢固压迫、排出空气并封帽混匀、床旁标记、立即送检。本题不把 Allen 试验作为普遍适用的许可规则。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track what must happen before the specimen leaves the bedside: collect safely, control bleeding, protect specimen integrity, label, then transport.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按标本离开床旁前的必要步骤排序：安全采集、控制出血、保护标本完整性、标记、送检。","sourceMetadata":"World Health Organization, WHO Guidelines on Drawing Blood, chapter 5.2 Arterial blood sampling, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK138661/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Facility policy requires immediate delivery to the laboratory after collection.","controlSentenceZh":"机构政策要求采集后立即送达实验室。"}
{"queueIndex":2196,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8b_cbti_stimulus_control","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.726","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.726.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.726.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[285,312],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,92],"fullStemEn":"A client following a prescribed CBT-I stimulus-control plan has been awake in bed long enough to feel frustrated. The plan says to leave the bed when unable to sleep, use a quiet low-stimulation activity, return only when sleepy, repeat as needed, and keep the same morning wake time. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名遵循处方 CBT-I 刺激控制方案的患者在床上清醒已久，并开始感到烦躁。方案规定：无法入睡时离床，进行安静低刺激活动，仅在困倦时回床，必要时重复，并保持固定晨起时间。请按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The plan says to leave the bed when unable to sleep, use a quiet low-stimulation activity, return only when sleepy, repeat as needed, and keep the same morning wake time.","penultimateSentenceZh":"方案规定：无法入睡时离床，进行安静低刺激活动，仅在困倦时回床，必要时重复，并保持固定晨起时间。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use a quiet, low-stimulation activity outside the bed.","zh":"在床外进行安静、低刺激的活动。"},{"id":"C","en":"Return to bed only after sleepiness develops.","zh":"仅在出现困倦后回床。"},{"id":"E","en":"Get up at the prescribed fixed wake time in the morning.","zh":"早晨按规定的固定时间起床。"},{"id":"D","en":"If wakefulness and frustration return, repeat the leave-activity-return cycle.","zh":"如果再次清醒并烦躁，重复离床—活动—回床的循环。"},{"id":"A","en":"Leave the bed and move to the planned quiet location.","zh":"离开床，前往预定的安静地点。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stimulus control breaks the association between bed and prolonged wakefulness: leave bed, use a quiet low-stimulation activity, return only when sleepy, repeat the cycle if wakefulness recurs, and rise at the fixed wake time.","rationaleCorrectZh":"刺激控制旨在打破床与长时间清醒之间的联系：离床，进行安静低刺激活动，仅在困倦时回床；若再次清醒则重复，并按固定时间起床。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The supplied plan gives a repeating nighttime cycle plus one fixed morning endpoint. Put the fixed wake time last.","testTakingStrategyZh":"题干方案包含可重复的夜间循环和一个固定的早晨终点。固定起床时间应排在最后。","sourceMetadata":"VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder and Obstructive Sleep Apnea, 2025, CBT-I stimulus-control component, https://www.healthquality.va.gov/HEALTHQUALITY/guidelines/CD/insomnia/I-OSA-CPG_2025-Guideline_final_20250915.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The plan says to leave the bed when unable to sleep, use a quiet low-stimulation activity, return only when sleepy, repeat as needed, and keep the same morning wake time.","controlSentenceZh":"方案规定：无法入睡时离床，进行安静低刺激活动，仅在困倦时回床，必要时重复，并保持固定晨起时间。"}
{"queueIndex":2197,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8c_salicylate_mixed_disorder","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.727","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.727.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.727.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[251,424],"terminalOffsetsZh":[124,171],"fullStemEn":"A client with a reported aspirin exposure has tinnitus, vomiting, rapid deep respirations, increasing confusion, new bibasilar crackles, and SpO₂ 89% on room air. Results: pH 7.40, PaCO₂ 20 mm Hg, HCO₃⁻ 12 mEq/L, sodium 138 mEq/L, chloride 102 mEq/L. Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely acid-base condition, two immediate pathway-authorized actions, and two parameters that best track response or deterioration.","fullStemZh":"一名有阿司匹林暴露史的患者出现耳鸣、呕吐、深快呼吸、意识逐渐混乱、新出现双肺底湿啰音，室内空气 SpO₂ 为 89%。检查：pH 7.40，PaCO₂ 20 mm Hg，HCO₃⁻ 12 mEq/L，钠 138 mEq/L，氯 102 mEq/L。完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的酸碱紊乱、两项立即执行的路径措施，以及两项最能追踪反应或恶化的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely acid-base condition, two immediate pathway-authorized actions, and two parameters that best track response or deterioration.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的酸碱紊乱、两项立即执行的路径措施，以及两项最能追踪反应或恶化的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Results: pH 7.40, PaCO₂ 20 mm Hg, HCO₃⁻ 12 mEq/L, sodium 138 mEq/L, chloride 102 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"检查：pH 7.40，PaCO₂ 20 mm Hg，HCO₃⁻ 12 mEq/L，钠 138 mEq/L，氯 102 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"c3","en":"Simple anion-gap metabolic acidosis with appropriate respiratory compensation","zh":"单纯高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒伴适当呼吸代偿"},{"id":"c2","en":"Simple respiratory alkalosis with appropriate renal compensation","zh":"单纯呼吸性碱中毒伴适当肾脏代偿"},{"id":"c1","en":"Salicylate toxicity with mixed respiratory alkalosis and anion-gap metabolic acidosis","zh":"水杨酸盐中毒并存呼吸性碱中毒和高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a2","en":"Urgently notify toxicology and nephrology and prepare for hemodialysis","zh":"紧急联系中毒学与肾脏科并准备血液透析"},{"id":"a1","en":"Begin the prescribed IV sodium bicarbonate alkalinization pathway","zh":"开始医嘱中的静脉碳酸氢钠碱化流程"},{"id":"a3","en":"Delay treatment until a single serum salicylate concentration returns","zh":"等待单次血清水杨酸浓度结果后再治疗"},{"id":"a4","en":"Intubate solely to normalize the rapid respiratory rate","zh":"仅为纠正呼吸过快而进行气管插管"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p3","en":"One normal serum glucose value only","zh":"仅一次正常血糖值"},{"id":"p4","en":"Daily hemoglobin A1c","zh":"每日糖化血红蛋白"},{"id":"p1","en":"Serial blood pH, bicarbonate, and serum potassium","zh":"连续血液 pH、碳酸氢盐和血清钾"},{"id":"p2","en":"Serial salicylate concentration interpreted with neurologic and respiratory status","zh":"连续水杨酸浓度，并结合神经和呼吸状态解读"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The near-normal pH masks two primary processes: low PaCO₂ reflects respiratory alkalosis, while low bicarbonate and an anion gap of 24 reflect anion-gap metabolic acidosis. With altered mental status and pulmonary findings, begin prescribed IV sodium bicarbonate alkalinization while urgently activating toxicology/nephrology and dialysis preparation. Track acid-base/electrolyte status and serial salicylate concentrations together with neurologic and respiratory status; a single level cannot dismiss severity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"接近正常的 pH 掩盖了两个原发过程：低 PaCO₂ 表示呼吸性碱中毒，低 HCO₃⁻ 且阴离子间隙为 24 表示高阴离子间隙代谢性酸中毒。患者已有意识改变和肺部表现，应开始医嘱中的静脉碳酸氢钠碱化，同时紧急启动中毒学、肾脏科及透析准备。需联合追踪酸碱/电解质、连续水杨酸浓度以及神经和呼吸状态；单次药物浓度不能排除严重中毒。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A normal-looking pH can result from opposing disorders. Interpret PaCO₂ and bicarbonate separately, then use the clinical deterioration cues to choose actions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"看似正常的 pH 可能由方向相反的两种紊乱互相抵消。应分别解读 PaCO₂ 和 HCO₃⁻，再根据临床恶化线索选择措施。","sourceMetadata":"American College of Medical Toxicology, Management Priorities in Salicylate Toxicity, acid-base status, alkalinization, serial concentration, and hemodialysis passages, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4371029/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2198,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8c_ici_hypophysitis_adrenal_risk","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.728","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.728.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.728.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[344,455],"terminalOffsetsZh":[143,173],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving nivolumab and ipilimumab reports new severe fatigue, headache, nausea, and dizziness. The client is afebrile; blood pressure is 82/48 mm Hg, sodium 126 mEq/L, glucose 58 mg/dL, 0800 cortisol 1.8 µg/dL, ACTH low, free T4 low, and TSH is not elevated. Blood cultures were obtained and the immune-toxicity pathway is activated. Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions, and two response parameters.","fullStemZh":"一名接受纳武利尤单抗和伊匹木单抗治疗的患者新出现严重乏力、头痛、恶心和头晕。患者无发热；血压 82/48 mm Hg，钠 126 mEq/L，血糖 58 mg/dL，0800 皮质醇 1.8 µg/dL，ACTH 低，游离 T4 低，TSH 未升高。已采集血培养并启动免疫毒性处理路径。完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的病情、两项立即措施和两项反应指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions, and two response parameters.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的病情、两项立即措施和两项反应指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Blood cultures were obtained and the immune-toxicity pathway is activated.","penultimateSentenceZh":"已采集血培养并启动免疫毒性处理路径。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"c1","en":"Immune checkpoint inhibitor–associated hypophysitis with secondary adrenal insufficiency","zh":"免疫检查点抑制剂相关垂体炎并继发性肾上腺功能不全"},{"id":"c4","en":"Septic shock as the only explanation","zh":"仅由脓毒性休克解释"},{"id":"c3","en":"Uncomplicated cancer-related fatigue","zh":"单纯癌症相关疲劳"},{"id":"c2","en":"Primary hypothyroidism alone","zh":"单纯原发性甲状腺功能减退"}],"correct":"c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"a4","en":"Attribute the findings to expected fatigue and continue treatment without urgent evaluation","zh":"把这些表现视为预期疲劳，不作紧急评估并继续治疗"},{"id":"a3","en":"Start thyroid replacement before giving any glucocorticoid","zh":"在给予任何糖皮质激素前先开始甲状腺激素替代"},{"id":"a1","en":"Administer the prescribed stress-dose IV glucocorticoid now","zh":"立即给予医嘱中的应激剂量静脉糖皮质激素"},{"id":"a2","en":"Begin prescribed isotonic IV fluid and hemodynamic support","zh":"开始医嘱中的等渗静脉补液和血流动力学支持"}],"correct":["a1","a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"p4","en":"TSH alone","zh":"仅监测 TSH"},{"id":"p2","en":"Serum sodium and bedside glucose","zh":"血清钠和床旁血糖"},{"id":"p3","en":"Tumor-marker concentration","zh":"肿瘤标志物浓度"},{"id":"p1","en":"Blood pressure and mean arterial pressure","zh":"血压和平均动脉压"}],"correct":["p1","p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The combination of checkpoint-inhibitor exposure, headache, low cortisol with low ACTH, central thyroid-pattern results, hyponatremia, hypoglycemia, and hypotension supports hypophysitis with secondary adrenal insufficiency. Give the prescribed stress-dose glucocorticoid before any thyroid replacement and support circulation with isotonic IV fluid. Track hemodynamics and sodium/glucose. Starting thyroid hormone before cortisol coverage can precipitate adrenal crisis when multiple pituitary deficits coexist.","rationaleCorrectZh":"免疫检查点抑制剂暴露、头痛、低皮质醇合并低 ACTH、中枢性甲状腺功能模式、低钠、低血糖和低血压，共同支持垂体炎并继发性肾上腺功能不全。应先给予医嘱中的应激剂量糖皮质激素，再考虑甲状腺激素，并用等渗静脉液体支持循环。监测血流动力学及钠/血糖。多种垂体激素缺乏并存时，若在皮质醇覆盖前先补充甲状腺激素，可能诱发肾上腺危象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Low ACTH plus low cortisol points to secondary, not primary, adrenal failure. When cortisol and thyroid deficits coexist, protect cortisol first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"低 ACTH 合并低皮质醇提示继发性而非原发性肾上腺功能不全。皮质醇与甲状腺激素缺乏并存时，应先保障皮质醇。","sourceMetadata":"ASCO, Management of Immune-Related Adverse Events in Patients Treated With Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy: Guideline Update, endocrine toxicities table—hypophysitis and adrenal insufficiency, https://ascopubs.org/doi/10.1200/JCO.21.01440","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2199,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8c_ect_recovery_escalation","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.729","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.729.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.729.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[298,345],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,110],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews a post-ECT recovery note. Highlight only the findings that require immediate clinical escalation beyond routine supportive recovery care. Recovery guidance calls for monitoring the airway, oxygen saturation, vital signs, level of consciousness, orientation, and tardive seizures. Do not select every transient post-ECT symptom.","fullStemZh":"护士查看一份 ECT 治疗后恢复记录。请只标出需要立即升级临床处理、而不能仅按常规支持性恢复护理处理的发现。恢复期指南要求监测气道、氧饱和度、生命体征、意识水平、定向力和迟发性发作。不要选择每一种短暂的 ECT 后症状。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not select every transient post-ECT symptom.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要选择每一种短暂的 ECT 后症状。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Recovery guidance calls for monitoring the airway, oxygen saturation, vital signs, level of consciousness, orientation, and tardive seizures.","penultimateSentenceZh":"恢复期指南要求监测气道、氧饱和度、生命体征、意识水平、定向力和迟发性发作。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Post-ECT recovery note:","zh":"ECT 后恢复记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The client reports a headache rated 3/10.","zh":"患者诉头痛 3/10。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The client is drowsy but opens the eyes to name and follows a simple command.","zh":"患者嗜睡，但呼名可睁眼并能执行简单指令。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"After the client had regained consciousness, generalized tonic-clonic activity recurs.","zh":"患者恢复意识后，再次出现全身强直-阵挛性活动。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Breathing becomes shallow with repeated apnea; SpO₂ remains 88% despite airway repositioning and supplemental oxygen.","zh":"呼吸变浅并反复呼吸暂停；重新摆位气道并给予补充氧后，SpO₂ 仍为 88%。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The client briefly gives the wrong date but identifies self and location.","zh":"患者短暂说错日期，但能确认自己身份和所在地点。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"New left facial droop and left-arm weakness are present compared with the preprocedure examination.","zh":"与治疗前检查相比，新出现左侧面瘫和左上肢无力。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Blood pressure is 148/86 mm Hg and is trending downward toward the preprocedure value.","zh":"血压为 148/86 mm Hg，正向治疗前数值回落。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s3","s4","s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A recurrent generalized seizure after consciousness returned is a tardive seizure; repeated apnea with persistent hypoxemia despite airway and oxygen measures is respiratory compromise; and new facial droop with unilateral arm weakness is a focal neurologic emergency. Each needs immediate escalation. Mild headache, transient drowsiness while arousable and following commands, brief date disorientation, and a mildly elevated blood pressure trending down can receive routine monitoring and supportive care in this note.","rationaleCorrectZh":"意识恢复后再次出现全身性发作属于迟发性发作；采取气道与给氧措施后仍反复呼吸暂停并持续低氧属于呼吸功能受损；新出现面瘫合并单侧上肢无力属于局灶性神经急症。这些情况均需立即升级处理。轻度头痛、可唤醒且能执行指令的短暂嗜睡、短暂日期定向错误，以及正在下降的轻度血压升高，在本记录中可继续常规监测和支持性护理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate common transient recovery effects from threats to airway or breathing, a seizure after recovery began, and a new focal neurologic deficit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将常见短暂恢复期反应与气道或呼吸威胁、恢复开始后再次发作，以及新出现的局灶性神经功能缺损区分开。","sourceMetadata":"Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Use of Electroconvulsive Therapy, Indian Journal of Psychiatry 2023, recovery monitoring and postictal adverse-event sections, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10096214/; Queensland Health, The Administration of Electroconvulsive Therapy Guideline, sections 16.1-16.3 (airway, oxygen saturation, consciousness/orientation, tardive-seizure monitoring, and supportive care for self-limited headache/drowsiness), https://www.health.qld.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0028/444763/guideline-administration-electroconvulsive-therapy.pdf; American Stroke Association, Stroke Symptoms and Warning Signs (face drooping and arm weakness), https://www.stroke.org/en/about-stroke/stroke-symptoms","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2200,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8c_fertility_preservation_cues","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.730","itemType":"highlight","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.730.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.730.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[105,278],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,79],"fullStemEn":"A client with a new cancer diagnosis is scheduled to begin a potentially gonadotoxic regimen in 10 days. Highlight only the documented cues and actions that support timely fertility-risk counseling, elicitation of reproductive goals, and referral before treatment when feasible.","fullStemZh":"一名新诊断癌症的患者计划在 10 天后开始可能具有性腺毒性的治疗。请只标出支持及时进行生育风险咨询、了解患者生殖目标，并在可行时于治疗前转诊的记录线索和措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the documented cues and actions that support timely fertility-risk counseling, elicitation of reproductive goals, and referral before treatment when feasible.","terminalSentenceZh":"请只标出支持及时进行生育风险咨询、了解患者生殖目标，并在可行时于治疗前转诊的记录线索和措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with a new cancer diagnosis is scheduled to begin a potentially gonadotoxic regimen in 10 days.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名新诊断癌症的患者计划在 10 天后开始可能具有性腺毒性的治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Oncology consultation note:","zh":"肿瘤科会诊记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The clinician explains that the planned regimen may impair future fertility.","zh":"临床人员说明计划治疗可能损害未来生育力。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The client is 38 years old.","zh":"患者 38 岁。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client says, “I am unsure whether I will want genetically related children later, and I want to understand my options.”","zh":"患者说：“我不确定以后是否想要有遗传关系的孩子，但我想了解有哪些选择。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client is not currently married.","zh":"患者目前未婚。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"With the client's agreement, an urgent reproductive-endocrinology referral is placed before the first treatment.","zh":"经患者同意，在首次治疗前安排加急生殖内分泌转诊。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client has no previous children.","zh":"患者以前没有孩子。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The client's partner did not attend today's visit.","zh":"患者的伴侣今天未参加就诊。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s3","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The record should document treatment-related fertility-risk counseling, the client's own reproductive goals or uncertainty, and timely referral before treatment when feasible. Age, relationship status, parity, gender identity, and whether a partner attended do not determine whether counseling should be offered.","rationaleCorrectZh":"记录应包括治疗相关生育风险咨询、患者本人的生殖目标或不确定性，以及在可行时于治疗前及时转诊。年龄、伴侣关系、既往生育次数、性别认同或伴侣是否到场，都不应决定是否提供咨询。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select statements about counseling, the client's expressed goals, and pre-treatment referral—not demographic assumptions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择与咨询、患者表达的目标及治疗前转诊有关的内容，不要选择人口学假设。","sourceMetadata":"ASCO Guideline Update: Fertility Preservation in People With Cancer, 2025, recommendations for risk counseling, reproductive-goal assessment, and referral before treatment, https://ascopubs.org/doi/10.1200/JCO-24-02782","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2201,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8c_dka_resolution_transition","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.731","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.731.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.731.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[434,535],"terminalOffsetsZh":[168,191],"fullStemEn":"Use the following treatment criteria to determine whether DKA has resolved and whether transition is safe: DKA is resolved when plasma ketone is below 0.6 mmol/L and venous pH is at least 7.3 or bicarbonate is at least 18 mmol/L; glucose should ideally be below 200 mg/dL. For safe transition, basal subcutaneous insulin must be given with 1–2 hours of overlap before stopping IV insulin. Do not use urine ketones or anion gap alone. Highlight only the note findings that satisfy the resolution criteria and safe-transition conditions.","fullStemZh":"采用以下治疗标准判断 DKA 是否缓解以及能否安全过渡：当血浆酮体低于 0.6 mmol/L，且静脉 pH 至少 7.3 或碳酸氢盐至少 18 mmol/L 时，DKA 可视为缓解；血糖理想情况下低于 200 mg/dL。安全过渡时，应先给予基础皮下胰岛素，并与静脉胰岛素重叠 1–2 小时后再停静脉胰岛素。不要仅依据尿酮或阴离子间隙。请只标出满足缓解标准和安全过渡条件的记录发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the note findings that satisfy the resolution criteria and safe-transition conditions.","terminalSentenceZh":"请只标出满足缓解标准和安全过渡条件的记录发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Do not use urine ketones or anion gap alone.","penultimateSentenceZh":"不要仅依据尿酮或阴离子间隙。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Serial treatment note:","zh":"连续治疗记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"Blood glucose fell from 420 mg/dL to 248 mg/dL during the first 3 hours.","zh":"前 3 小时血糖从 420 mg/dL 降至 248 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Current plasma beta-hydroxybutyrate is 0.4 mmol/L.","zh":"当前血浆 β-羟丁酸为 0.4 mmol/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Current venous pH is 7.32 and bicarbonate is 19 mmol/L.","zh":"当前静脉 pH 为 7.32，碳酸氢盐为 19 mmol/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Current blood glucose is 184 mg/dL.","zh":"当前血糖为 184 mg/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The anion gap is now 11 mEq/L.","zh":"当前阴离子间隙为 11 mEq/L。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Urine ketones remain 1+.","zh":"尿酮仍为 1+。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Basal subcutaneous insulin was given at 1400; IV insulin is scheduled to stop at 1600.","zh":"1400 已给予基础皮下胰岛素；计划 1600 停止静脉胰岛素。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The current plasma ketone, venous pH/bicarbonate, and glucose meet the supplied resolution criteria. Basal insulin was administered with a planned two-hour overlap, supporting safe transition. Earlier glucose improvement, a closed anion gap, or persistent urine ketones are not independently keyed resolution evidence.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当前血浆酮体、静脉 pH/碳酸氢盐及血糖满足题干缓解标准。基础胰岛素已给予，并计划与静脉胰岛素重叠 2 小时，支持安全过渡。较早的血糖改善、阴离子间隙关闭或尿酮仍阳性，都不能单独作为本题缓解证据。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply only the criteria printed in the stem. Select the current ketone/acidosis data and the explicit insulin-overlap plan.","testTakingStrategyZh":"只使用题干所列标准。选择当前酮体/酸中毒数据及明确的胰岛素重叠计划。","sourceMetadata":"ADA/EASD/JBDS/AACE/DTS, Hyperglycemic Crises in Adults With Diabetes: A Consensus Report, Criteria for resolution of DKA and transition to subcutaneous insulin, https://diabetesjournals.org/care/article/47/8/1257/156808/Hyperglycemic-Crises-in-Adults-With-Diabetes-A","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2202,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format8c_ici_colitis_escalation","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.732","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.732.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.732.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[400,492],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,142],"fullStemEn":"An oncology nurse reviews a telephone follow-up note for a client receiving an immune checkpoint inhibitor. The oncology service recommends further evaluation for at least 4 stools per day above baseline, blood or mucus in the stool, abdominal pain, fever, signs of dehydration, or peritoneal irritation. One isolated loose stool without other gastrointestinal symptoms does not meet these criteria. Highlight the findings that require further evaluation for possible immune-mediated colitis.","fullStemZh":"肿瘤科护士正在查看一名接受免疫检查点抑制剂治疗患者的电话随访记录。肿瘤科建议对以下情况进一步评估：每日排便次数较基线增加至少 4 次、便中带血或黏液、腹痛、发热、脱水征象或腹膜刺激征。仅有一次稀便且无其他胃肠道症状，不符合这些标准。请标出需要进一步评估是否存在免疫介导性结肠炎的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that require further evaluation for possible immune-mediated colitis.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要进一步评估是否存在免疫介导性结肠炎的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"One isolated loose stool without other gastrointestinal symptoms does not meet these criteria.","penultimateSentenceZh":"仅有一次稀便且无其他胃肠道症状，不符合这些标准。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Telephone follow-up note: The client's usual baseline is one formed stool daily.","zh":"电话随访记录：患者平时的基线为每日 1 次成形便。"},{"id":"s1","en":"Yesterday the client had one loose stool and no other gastrointestinal symptoms.","zh":"昨天患者有 1 次稀便，无其他胃肠道症状。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Today the client has had six watery stools total, which is five stools above baseline.","zh":"今天患者共排出 6 次水样便，较基线增加 5 次。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client reports visible blood and mucus in the last two stools.","zh":"患者报告最近两次大便可见血液和黏液。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client reports new lower-abdominal cramping pain.","zh":"患者新出现下腹部绞痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Temperature is 100.9 °F (38.3 °C).","zh":"体温为 100.9 °F (38.3 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client feels dizzy on standing and has a dry mouth.","zh":"患者站立时头晕，并有口干。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Mild fatigue is unchanged from the previous visit.","zh":"轻度乏力与上次就诊相比无变化。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"The abdomen is soft without guarding or rebound tenderness.","zh":"腹部柔软，无肌紧张或反跳痛。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3","s4","s5","s6"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Six watery stools today—five above the usual baseline of one formed stool daily—along with blood and mucus, abdominal cramping, fever, and orthostatic dehydration cues meet the stated criteria for further evaluation. One isolated loose stool, unchanged fatigue, and a soft abdomen without guarding do not. Infectious causes must also be evaluated before immune-mediated colitis is confirmed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者今天共排出 6 次水样便，较平时每日 1 次成形便的基线增加 5 次；同时有便中血和黏液、腹部绞痛、发热及体位性脱水线索，符合题干所述进一步评估标准。单次孤立稀便、未改变的疲劳，以及腹软无肌紧张均不符合。确诊免疫介导性结肠炎前，还必须评估感染性病因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the exact thresholds and symptoms in the stem. Do not select mild nonspecific findings merely because the client receives immunotherapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"严格使用题干阈值和症状。不要仅因患者接受免疫治疗，就选择轻微非特异性表现。","sourceMetadata":"ASCO, Management of Immune-Related Adverse Events in Patients Treated With Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy: Guideline Update, gastrointestinal toxicities table—diarrhea/colitis evaluation and escalation, https://ascopubs.org/doi/10.1200/JCO.21.01440","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2203,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9a_transfusion_bacterial_contamination","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.733","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.733.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.733.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[377,522],"terminalOffsetsZh":[139,182],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving an apheresis platelet transfusion. Twenty-five minutes after the transfusion begins, the temperature rises from 98.2 °F (36.8 °C) to 102.4 °F (39.1 °C), with severe rigors, nausea, heart rate 128/min, and blood pressure 78/42 mm Hg. The platelet bag looks unusually cloudy. The client has no urticaria, wheezing, back pain, flank pain, or hemoglobinuria. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions, and two parameters that best track deterioration or response.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在输注单采血小板。输注开始 25 分钟后，体温由 98.2 °F (36.8 °C)升至 102.4 °F (39.1 °C)，并出现剧烈寒战、恶心、心率 128 次/分、血压 78/42 mm Hg。血小板袋外观异常浑浊。患者无荨麻疹、喘鸣、背痛、腰痛或血红蛋白尿。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪恶化或治疗反应的指标。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two immediate actions, and two parameters that best track deterioration or response.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的情况、两项立即措施，以及两项最能追踪恶化或治疗反应的指标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has no urticaria, wheezing, back pain, flank pain, or hemoglobinuria.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者无荨麻疹、喘鸣、背痛、腰痛或血红蛋白尿。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1c3","en":"Acute hemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"急性溶血性输血反应"},{"id":"q1c2","en":"Febrile nonhemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"非溶血性发热性输血反应"},{"id":"q1c1","en":"Bacterial contamination with a septic transfusion reaction","zh":"细菌污染所致脓毒性输血反应"},{"id":"q1c4","en":"Allergic transfusion reaction","zh":"过敏性输血反应"}],"correct":"q1c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1a2","en":"Notify the transfusion service; preserve the bag and tubing for testing and obtain prompt patient cultures per protocol","zh":"通知输血服务部门；保留血袋和管路用于检测，并按流程及时采集患者培养标本"},{"id":"q1a1","en":"Stop the platelet transfusion immediately","zh":"立即停止血小板输注"},{"id":"q1a3","en":"Give an antipyretic and restart the same unit when the fever decreases","zh":"给予退热药，待体温下降后重新输注同一单位"},{"id":"q1a4","en":"Discard the platelet bag and administration set in biohazard waste","zh":"将血小板袋和输血管路丢入生物危害废物"}],"correct":["q1a1","q1a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1p1","en":"Serial blood pressure/MAP and heart rate","zh":"连续血压/平均动脉压和心率"},{"id":"q1p3","en":"Direct antiglobulin test and bilirubin only","zh":"仅直接抗人球蛋白试验和胆红素"},{"id":"q1p4","en":"Appearance of the peripheral IV site only","zh":"仅外周静脉穿刺点外观"},{"id":"q1p2","en":"Urine output and mental status","zh":"尿量和意识状态"}],"correct":["q1p1","q1p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The abrupt high fever rise, severe rigors, hypotension, and abnormal platelet-component appearance during transfusion are most concerning for bacterial contamination with a septic transfusion reaction. The transfusion must be stopped immediately. The transfusion service must be notified, and the implicated component and administration set must be preserved for Gram stain/culture while prompt patient blood cultures are obtained under the reaction protocol. Serial hemodynamics and perfusion findings track deterioration and response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"输注过程中突发明显升温、剧烈寒战、低血压及血小板成分外观异常，最应警惕细菌污染所致的脓毒性输血反应。必须立即停止输注，并通知输血服务部门；保留涉事血液成分和输血管路用于革兰染色/培养，同时按输血反应流程及时采集患者血培养。连续血流动力学及灌注指标可追踪病情恶化和治疗反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize the complete cue cluster. High fever plus rigors, hypotension, and an abnormal platelet bag should move bacterial contamination ahead of more benign fever reactions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据完整线索组合判断。明显发热、寒战、低血压和血小板袋外观异常，应使细菌污染优先于较轻的发热反应。","sourceMetadata":"AABB, Circular of Information for the Use of Human Blood and Blood Components, June 2024, Adverse Reactions—Bacterial Sepsis passage (immediate discontinuation; patient blood cultures; Gram stain/culture of container and administration set; report to transfusion service), pp. 10–11, https://www.aabb.org/docs/default-source/default-document-library/resources/circular-of-information-watermark.pdf; CDC NHSN Hemovigilance Module Surveillance Protocol, January 2026, Transfusion-Transmitted Infection case definition and investigation section, https://www.cdc.gov/nhsn/pdfs/biovigilance/bv-hv-protocol-current.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2204,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9a_iad_differential","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.734","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.734.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.734.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[368,389],"terminalOffsetsZh":[96,104],"fullStemEn":"An older adult with frequent urinary and liquid-stool incontinence has burning pain and diffuse, irregular, superficial erythema with small denuded areas across both buttocks, the perineum, and upper inner thighs. The skin changes follow the areas exposed to moisture. The sacral bony prominence is intact, and there is no focal crater, eschar, or deep discoloration. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名老年患者频繁尿失禁并有稀便失禁，双侧臀部、会阴和大腿上内侧出现灼痛、弥漫且边界不规则的浅表红斑，并有少量表皮剥脱。皮肤改变分布在受潮区域。骶骨隆突处皮肤完整，无局灶性凹陷、焦痂或深部变色。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The sacral bony prominence is intact, and there is no focal crater, eschar, or deep discoloration.","penultimateSentenceZh":"骶骨隆突处皮肤完整，无局灶性凹陷、焦痂或深部变色。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2c3","en":"Deep tissue pressure injury","zh":"深部组织压力性损伤"},{"id":"q2c2","en":"Stage 2 sacral pressure injury","zh":"骶部 2 期压力性损伤"},{"id":"q2c1","en":"Incontinence-associated dermatitis","zh":"失禁相关性皮炎"},{"id":"q2c4","en":"Cellulitis","zh":"蜂窝织炎"}],"correct":"q2c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Actions to take","zh":"应采取的措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2a2","en":"Apply a moisture barrier and implement an individualized continence plan","zh":"使用防潮屏障并实施个体化失禁管理方案"},{"id":"q2a4","en":"Cover the entire area with a strongly adhesive occlusive dressing","zh":"用强黏性封闭敷料覆盖整个区域"},{"id":"q2a3","en":"Massage the reddened skin firmly to increase circulation","zh":"用力按摩红斑皮肤以促进循环"},{"id":"q2a1","en":"Gently cleanse after each episode and pat the skin dry","zh":"每次失禁后温和清洁并轻拍干燥"}],"correct":["q2a1","q2a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2p3","en":"A pressure-injury stage number assigned to the dermatitis","zh":"为皮炎指定的压力性损伤分期数字"},{"id":"q2p2","en":"Burning/pain and frequency of moisture exposure","zh":"灼痛/疼痛及受潮频率"},{"id":"q2p1","en":"Extent of erythema and superficial denudement","zh":"红斑和浅表剥脱的范围"},{"id":"q2p4","en":"Serum albumin as the only outcome measure","zh":"仅以血清白蛋白作为结局指标"}],"correct":["q2p1","q2p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The broad, irregular, superficial inflammation over moisture-exposed areas, with an intact sacral prominence, supports incontinence-associated dermatitis rather than a pressure injury. Gently cleanse after episodes, pat dry, and use a moisture-barrier plus an incontinence-management plan. Track the extent/severity of superficial injury and the client's symptoms and moisture exposure; do not assign a pressure-injury stage to IAD.","rationaleCorrectZh":"受潮区域出现广泛、边界不规则的浅表炎症，且骶骨隆突处完整，支持失禁相关性皮炎而不是压力性损伤。每次失禁后应温和清洁、轻拍干燥，并使用皮肤屏障和失禁管理方案。追踪浅表损伤的范围/严重程度以及患者症状和受潮频率；不要将 IAD 按压力性损伤分期。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distribution is the discriminator: moisture-associated damage is broad and irregular, whereas pressure injury is usually localized to pressure and shear sites.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分布是关键鉴别点：潮湿相关损伤通常广泛且边界不规则，而压力性损伤通常局限于受压和剪切部位。","sourceMetadata":"WOCN Society, Best Practice for Clinicians: Incontinence-Associated Dermatitis resources, assessment and prevention/management modules, https://bwap.wocn.org/; Australian Aged Care Quality and Safety Commission, Clinical alert: Incontinence-associated dermatitis and pressure injury, differential features and management sections, https://www.agedcarequality.gov.au/news-publications/clinical-alerts-and-advice/incontinence-associated-dermatitis-and-pressure-injury","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2205,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9a_suspected_uterine_rupture","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.735","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.735.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.735.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[407,428],"terminalOffsetsZh":[134,142],"fullStemEn":"A laboring client at 39 weeks is attempting vaginal birth after one prior low-transverse cesarean birth. Oxytocin is infusing. The client suddenly reports constant tearing abdominal pain between contractions. The presenting part moves from +1 to −2 station, fetal heart rate falls to 70/min for 4 minutes, and maternal heart rate rises to 132/min with blood pressure 84/48 mm Hg. Vaginal bleeding is scant. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名孕 39 周产妇在一次既往低位横切口剖宫产后尝试阴道分娩，正在输注缩宫素。患者突然报告宫缩间歇仍持续的撕裂样腹痛，先露部由 +1 站退至 −2 站，胎心率降至 70 次/分并持续 4 分钟，产妇心率升至 132 次/分、血压 84/48 mm Hg。阴道出血很少。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Vaginal bleeding is scant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阴道出血很少。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3c4","en":"Ordinary active-labor pain","zh":"正常活跃期产痛"},{"id":"q3c1","en":"Suspected uterine rupture","zh":"疑似子宫破裂"},{"id":"q3c2","en":"Placental abruption","zh":"胎盘早剥"},{"id":"q3c3","en":"Uterine tachysystole without rupture","zh":"无破裂的宫缩过频"}],"correct":"q3c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3a1","en":"Stop the oxytocin infusion","zh":"停止缩宫素输注"},{"id":"q3a4","en":"Increase oxytocin to restore contraction strength","zh":"增加缩宫素以恢复宫缩强度"},{"id":"q3a3","en":"Observe the tracing for 30 more minutes before notifying the obstetric team","zh":"继续观察胎心图 30 分钟后再通知产科团队"},{"id":"q3a2","en":"Activate urgent obstetric response, begin maternal stabilization, and prepare for category 1 birth","zh":"启动紧急产科响应、开始母体复苏并准备 1 类紧急分娩"}],"correct":["q3a1","q3a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3p1","en":"Continuous fetal heart rate response","zh":"连续胎心率反应"},{"id":"q3p4","en":"Contraction frequency alone","zh":"仅宫缩频率"},{"id":"q3p2","en":"Maternal blood pressure, heart rate, consciousness, and urine output","zh":"母体血压、心率、意识和尿量"},{"id":"q3p3","en":"Cervical dilation alone","zh":"仅宫颈扩张度"}],"correct":["q3p1","q3p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The prior uterine scar plus sudden persistent pain, loss of fetal station, prolonged fetal bradycardia, and maternal shock supports suspected uterine rupture. Stop oxytocin, summon urgent obstetric help, begin maternal stabilization, and prepare for category 1 birth without waiting for a fixed observation interval. Continuous fetal response and maternal hemodynamic/perfusion findings are the most important monitoring parameters.","rationaleCorrectZh":"既往子宫瘢痕，加上突发持续疼痛、胎先露回退、胎儿持续心动过缓和母体休克，支持疑似子宫破裂。应停止缩宫素，紧急呼叫产科团队，开始母体复苏，并准备 1 类紧急分娩，不应等待固定观察时限。胎心反应及母体血流动力学/灌注指标是最重要的监测参数。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not diagnose from one tracing feature. Combine the tracing with the prior scar, persistent pain, loss of station, and maternal instability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要依据单一胎心图特征诊断。应结合既往瘢痕、持续疼痛、先露回退和母体不稳定综合判断。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, Fetal monitoring in labour, recommendations 1.5.7–1.5.9 (pathological CTG, acute bradycardia/prolonged deceleration, exclude uterine rupture and prepare urgent birth), https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/NG229/chapter/recommendations; NICE NG192, Caesarean birth, recommendation 1.4.2 (suspected uterine rupture as category 1), https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/NG192/chapter/recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2206,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9a_esophageal_button_battery","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.736","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.736.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.736.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[436,488],"terminalOffsetsZh":[126,141],"fullStemEn":"A 2-year-old child was witnessed swallowing a new 20-mm lithium coin-cell battery 40 minutes ago. The child is alert, handles secretions, and can swallow without coughing or choking. The child has no known honey allergy, has eaten nothing since the event, and honey is immediately available. Anteroposterior and lateral radiographs show the battery lodged in the upper esophagus. Breathing is currently unlabored. Complete the bow-tie. Honey must not delay emergency transport or removal.","fullStemZh":"一名 2 岁儿童 40 分钟前被目击吞下一枚新的 20 mm 锂纽扣电池。儿童清醒，能处理口腔分泌物，并可吞咽且不咳嗽或呛咳。儿童无已知蜂蜜过敏，事件后未进食，现场可立即取得蜂蜜。正位和侧位 X 线显示电池卡在上段食管，目前呼吸不费力。请完成蝴蝶结题。蜂蜜绝不能延误急诊转运或取出。","terminalSentenceEn":"Honey must not delay emergency transport or removal.","terminalSentenceZh":"蜂蜜绝不能延误急诊转运或取出。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4c1","en":"Esophageal button-battery impaction","zh":"食管纽扣电池嵌顿"},{"id":"q4c4","en":"Food bolus impaction","zh":"食团嵌塞"},{"id":"q4c2","en":"Button battery already beyond the esophagus","zh":"纽扣电池已通过食管"},{"id":"q4c3","en":"Nonbattery coin ingestion","zh":"普通硬币吞入"}],"correct":"q4c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4a1","en":"Give 10 mL honey every 10 minutes, up to 6 doses, while emergency care proceeds without delay","zh":"在不延误急救的前提下，每 10 分钟给予 10 mL 蜂蜜，最多 6 次"},{"id":"q4a3","en":"Wait at home for the battery to pass spontaneously","zh":"在家等待电池自行排出"},{"id":"q4a4","en":"Induce vomiting to retrieve the battery","zh":"催吐以取出电池"},{"id":"q4a2","en":"Arrange immediate emergency removal of the esophageal battery","zh":"立即安排紧急取出食管内电池"}],"correct":["q4a1","q4a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"High-risk parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的高风险指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4p2","en":"Hematemesis/melena and hemodynamic status","zh":"呕血/黑便及血流动力学状态"},{"id":"q4p1","en":"Voice, stridor, work of breathing, and oxygenation","zh":"声音、喘鸣、呼吸功和氧合"},{"id":"q4p3","en":"Time until the battery appears in stool","zh":"电池出现在粪便中的时间"},{"id":"q4p4","en":"Routine serum lithium level","zh":"常规血锂水平"}],"correct":["q4p1","q4p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Imaging confirms an esophageal button battery, which requires immediate removal because severe tissue injury can develop rapidly. This child meets every Poison Center honey criterion: at least 12 months old, likely lithium coin cell, ingestion within 12 hours, able to swallow, and honey immediately available. Give 10 mL every 10 minutes for up to 6 doses while emergency removal is arranged, without delaying transport or the procedure. Monitor airway changes and sentinel bleeding/hemodynamic deterioration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"影像已证实食管纽扣电池，需要立即取出，因为严重组织损伤可迅速发生。该儿童满足中毒控制中心所有蜂蜜条件：年龄至少 12 个月、可能为锂纽扣电池、吞入不足 12 小时、能够吞咽且蜂蜜可立即获得。在安排紧急取出期间可每 10 分钟给予 10 mL 蜂蜜，最多 6 次，但不得延误转运或手术。应监测气道变化及前哨性出血/血流动力学恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Location drives urgency. Once the battery is in the esophagus, immediate removal is the core action; honey is only a time-limited bridge when every eligibility criterion is explicit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"位置决定紧急程度。一旦电池位于食管，立即取出是核心措施；只有在全部条件明确满足时，蜂蜜才可作为限时过渡措施。","sourceMetadata":"National Capital Poison Center, Button Battery Ingestion Triage and Treatment Guideline, honey eligibility and dosing, imaging, esophageal-removal, and red-flag passages, https://www.poison.org/battery/guideline","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2207,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9a_pretransfusion_discrepancies","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.737","itemType":"highlight","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.737.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.737.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse and a second qualified staff member perform the final bedside check before spiking a red-blood-cell unit. Highlight only the discrepancies that require the nurse to stop before starting the transfusion.","fullStemZh":"护士与另一名具备资质的工作人员在刺入红细胞血袋前进行最终床旁核对。仅标出必须在开始输血前停止处理的差错。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the discrepancies that require the nurse to stop before starting the transfusion.","terminalSentenceZh":"仅标出必须在开始输血前停止处理的差错。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse and a second qualified staff member perform the final bedside check before spiking a red-blood-cell unit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士与另一名具备资质的工作人员在刺入红细胞血袋前进行最终床旁核对。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q5s1","en":"Final bedside check:","zh":"最终床旁核对："},{"id":"q5s2","en":"The wristband reads Elena Ruiz, MRN 552741; the compatibility tag reads Elena Ruiz, MRN 552714.","zh":"腕带显示 Elena Ruiz，病历号 552741；相容性标签显示 Elena Ruiz，病历号 552714。","selectable":true},{"id":"q5s3","en":"The bag unit number is W1234 26 008191, while the compatibility tag lists W1234 26 008119.","zh":"血袋单位编号为 W1234 26 008191，而相容性标签列为 W1234 26 008119。","selectable":true},{"id":"q5s4","en":"The order specifies irradiated, leukoreduced RBCs; the component label states leukoreduced RBCs but has no irradiated designation.","zh":"医嘱要求辐照、去白细胞红细胞；成分标签注明去白细胞红细胞，但没有辐照标识。","selectable":true},{"id":"q5s5","en":"The current time is 1412; the component expiration is 1400 today.","zh":"当前时间为 1412；该血液成分今天 1400 过期。","selectable":true},{"id":"q5s6","en":"The client's confirmed type is O positive, and the RBC unit is O positive.","zh":"患者已确认血型为 O 阳性，红细胞单位也是 O 阳性。","selectable":true},{"id":"q5s7","en":"The bag is intact, with no leaks, clots, discoloration, or abnormal cloudiness.","zh":"血袋完整，无渗漏、凝块、变色或异常浑浊。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q5s2","q5s3","q5s4","q5s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Transfusion must not begin when the recipient identifiers do not match, the unit number differs between the compatibility tag and bag, a required component modification is absent, or the unit is expired. Matching ABO/Rh information and an intact, normal-appearing bag are acceptable findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当患者身份标识不一致、相容性标签与血袋单位编号不一致、缺少医嘱要求的血液成分处理，或血液成分已过期时，不得开始输血。ABO/Rh 信息相符且血袋完整、外观正常属于可接受发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat the bedside check as a hard stop: any unresolved identity, unit, order, expiration, or integrity discrepancy prevents starting the component.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把床旁核对视为硬性停止点：任何未解决的身份、单位、医嘱、有效期或完整性差错都禁止开始输注。","sourceMetadata":"AABB, Circular of Information for the Use of Human Blood and Blood Components, June 2024, General Information Before Transfusion and Identification/inspection/expiration passages, pp. 7–8, https://www.aabb.org/docs/default-source/default-document-library/resources/circular-of-information-watermark.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2208,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9a_npwt_escalation","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.738","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.738.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.738.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[307,378],"terminalOffsetsZh":[114,131],"fullStemEn":"A client is using a 3M/Solventum V.A.C. Therapy device after abdominal wound debridement. The care plan follows the current V.A.C. safety instructions: frank bright-red blood in the tubing/canister, systemic or advancing infection, and therapy interruption longer than 2 hours require immediate escalation. Highlight only the follow-up findings that meet those escalation rules.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在腹部伤口清创后使用 3M/Solventum V.A.C. Therapy 装置。护理计划遵循当前 V.A.C. 安全说明：管路/储液罐内出现鲜红色血液、全身性或进展性感染，以及治疗中断超过 2 小时均需立即升级处理。仅标出符合这些升级规则的随访发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the follow-up findings that meet those escalation rules.","terminalSentenceZh":"仅标出符合这些升级规则的随访发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The care plan follows the current V.A.C. safety instructions: frank bright-red blood in the tubing/canister, systemic or advancing infection, and therapy interruption longer than 2 hours require immediate escalation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"安全说明：管路/储液罐内出现鲜红色血液、全身性或进展性感染，以及治疗中断超过 2 小时均需立即升级处理。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"q6s1","en":"Follow-up note:","zh":"随访记录："},{"id":"q6s2","en":"The nurse sees new frank bright-red blood moving through the tubing toward the canister.","zh":"护士看到新的鲜红色血液沿管路流向储液罐。","selectable":true},{"id":"q6s3","en":"The client now has fever, rigors, and erythema spreading beyond yesterday's marked border.","zh":"患者现出现发热、寒战，且红斑已扩展至昨日标记边界之外。","selectable":true},{"id":"q6s4","en":"The device history shows therapy was off for 2 hours 20 minutes while the client was away from the unit.","zh":"装置记录显示患者离开病区期间治疗中断了 2 小时 20 分钟。","selectable":true},{"id":"q6s5","en":"A small, unchanged amount of dark serosanguineous drainage remains in the canister.","zh":"储液罐内仍有少量且无变化的暗色浆血性引流。","selectable":true},{"id":"q6s6","en":"A low-pressure alarm cleared immediately after the nurse straightened a visibly kinked tube.","zh":"护士拉直明显扭结的管路后，低压报警立即解除。","selectable":true},{"id":"q6s7","en":"The visible wound bed has healthy granulation tissue and the periwound skin is intact.","zh":"可见伤口床有健康肉芽组织，伤口周围皮肤完整。","selectable":true}],"correct":["q6s2","q6s3","q6s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Frank bright-red blood in the tubing, new systemic/advancing infection findings, and a therapy interruption beyond 2 hours meet the stated V.A.C. escalation rules. A small stable amount of serosanguineous drainage, an alarm that resolves after correcting a kink, and intact granulating tissue are not independently escalation findings under the rule stated in the stem.","rationaleCorrectZh":"管路内出现鲜红色血液、新发全身性/进展性感染表现，以及治疗中断超过 2 小时，均符合题干所述 V.A.C. 升级规则。少量稳定的浆血性引流、纠正管路扭结后解除的报警，以及完整的肉芽组织，在本题限定规则下并非单独升级指征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the manufacturer-specific rule named in the stem. Do not generalize alarm behavior or pressure settings from one NPWT system to every device.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干指定的制造商规则。不要把某一种 NPWT 系统的报警行为或压力设置泛化到所有装置。","sourceMetadata":"FDA, Negative Pressure Wound Therapy (NPWT) safety and labeling material, bleeding and infection precautions, https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/guidance-documents-medical-devices-and-radiation-emitting-products/non-powered-suction-apparatus-device-intended-negative-pressure-wound-therapy-npwt-class-ii-special; Solventum, V.A.C. Therapy Clinical Guidelines, bleeding warning and therapy-off-more-than-two-hours instructions, https://assets.solventum.com/is/content/mmmspinco/VAC-Therapy-Clinical-Guidelinespdf; Solventum, V.A.C. Therapy for Patients, https://www.solventum.com/en-us/home/medical/advanced-wound-care/negative-pressure-wound-therapy/vac-therapy/vac-for-patients/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2209,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9b_hydration_trial_review","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.739","itemType":"highlight","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.739.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.739.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,241],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,88],"fullStemEn":"The individualized plan for a client in the last days of life specifies a 24-hour clinically assisted hydration trial, reviewed at least every 12 hours. Highlight only the findings that support reducing or stopping the trial under NICE NG31.","fullStemZh":"一名处于生命最后阶段的患者正在接受个体化的 24 小时临床辅助补液试验，照护方案规定至少每 12 小时复评一次。请只标出依据 NICE NG31 支持减少或停止补液试验的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings that support reducing or stopping the trial under NICE NG31.","terminalSentenceZh":"请只标出依据 NICE NG31 支持减少或停止补液试验的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The individualized plan for a client in the last days of life specifies a 24-hour clinically assisted hydration trial, reviewed at least every 12 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名处于生命最后阶段的患者正在接受个体化的 24 小时临床辅助补液试验，照护方案规定至少每 12 小时复评一次。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"1200 hydration-trial review:","zh":"1200 补液试验复评："},{"id":"s1","en":"The client reports that thirst has improved from 8/10 to 2/10.","zh":"患者报告口渴从 8/10 改善至 2/10。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"New bilateral basal crackles and dependent ankle edema are present, and oxygen flow has increased from 2 to 4 L/min to maintain the prior saturation.","zh":"新出现双侧肺底湿啰音和依赖性踝部水肿；为维持原有血氧饱和度，氧流量已从 2 L/min 增至 4 L/min。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client says clearly, “Please stop the drip; I do not want it continued.”","zh":"患者明确说：“请停掉点滴，我不想继续。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client is more alert and participates briefly in conversation with family.","zh":"患者清醒程度提高，并能短暂参与与家人的交谈。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"A family member says, “Fluids always prolong life, so the infusion must continue.”","zh":"一名家属说：“补液一定能延长生命，所以必须继续输液。”","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Urine output remains similar to the previous 12-hour period.","zh":"尿量与前一个 12 小时阶段相近。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client's new crackles, dependent edema, and increased oxygen requirement suggest harm from fluid overload, while the client's clear request to stop means the trial should not continue against the client's wishes. Improvement in thirst and alertness are possible benefits that support continued review rather than reduction or cessation. NICE advises continuing hydration when there is evidence of benefit and reducing or stopping it when there is evidence of harm, such as fluid overload, or when the person no longer wants it.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者新出现湿啰音、依赖性水肿及氧需求增加，提示补液可能造成液体过多的伤害；患者明确要求停止，也意味着不能违背其意愿继续试验。口渴和清醒程度改善属于可能获益，应支持继续复评，而不是减少或停止。NICE 建议有获益证据时继续补液；出现液体过多等伤害证据，或患者不再愿意接受时，应减少或停止。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the direction in the stem: select evidence of harm or withdrawal of consent, not every finding related to hydration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干方向作答：选择伤害证据或患者撤回意愿，不要选择所有与补液有关的发现。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG31, Care of dying adults in the last days of life, recommendations 1.4.8-1.4.9 (therapeutic trial of clinically assisted hydration; monitor at least every 12 hours; continue if benefit; reduce or stop if harm such as fluid overload or if the person no longer wants it), https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2210,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9b_ect_cognitive_change_review","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.740","itemType":"highlight","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.740.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.740.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[194,263],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,81],"fullStemEn":"The ECT team reviews cognitive monitoring across a treatment course. Highlight only the findings that require clinical review or reassessment of the treatment plan under the 2023 ECT guideline. Do not select expected brief postictal confusion that fully resolves.","fullStemZh":"ECT 团队查看整个疗程中的认知监测记录。请只标出依据 2023 年 ECT 指南需要临床评估或重新审视治疗方案的发现。不要选择完全消退的预期短暂发作后意识混乱。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not select expected brief postictal confusion that fully resolves.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要选择完全消退的预期短暂发作后意识混乱。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings that require clinical review or reassessment of the treatment plan under the 2023 ECT guideline.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请只标出依据 2023 年 ECT 指南需要临床评估或重新审视治疗方案的发现。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Longitudinal ECT record:","zh":"ECT 纵向记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The same cognitive screening tool declined from 28/30 at baseline to 21/30 on two consecutive weekly assessments, with new delayed-recall errors.","zh":"同一认知筛查工具从基线 28/30 降至连续两次每周评估的 21/30，并新出现延迟回忆错误。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"For 15 minutes after today's treatment, the client gave the wrong date; orientation was fully restored before leaving recovery.","zh":"今天治疗后 15 分钟内患者说错日期；离开恢复区前定向力已完全恢复。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The client reports new gaps in memory for recent family events and says the problem is distressing and interfering with work tasks.","zh":"患者报告对近期家庭事件出现新的记忆空白，并表示该问题令其痛苦且影响工作任务。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Family reports repetitive questioning and episodes of disorientation that continue between treatment sessions.","zh":"家属报告患者在两次治疗之间仍持续重复提问，并出现定向障碍。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The depression rating has improved and the client is again eating regular meals.","zh":"抑郁评分改善，患者已恢复规律进餐。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Mild insomnia documented before ECT is unchanged.","zh":"ECT 前已记录的轻度失眠没有变化。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A sustained objective decline from baseline, persistent intersession disorientation reported by family, and new distressing autobiographical memory loss affecting daily function require review of stimulus parameters, treatment frequency, and the risk-benefit plan. Brief postictal date disorientation that resolves during routine recovery is expected and does not by itself require treatment-plan reassessment. Improvement in depression and unchanged baseline insomnia are not cognitive deterioration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与基线相比持续的客观认知下降、家属报告的疗程间持续定向障碍，以及新出现且影响日常功能、令患者痛苦的自传性记忆缺失，都需要重新评估刺激参数、治疗频率及风险获益方案。常规恢复期内完全消退的短暂日期定向错误属于预期表现，本身不要求重新制定治疗计划。抑郁症状改善和基线失眠未改变均不是认知恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare each finding with baseline and recovery timing. Persistent subjective or objective change matters more than a brief expected postictal effect.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将每项发现与基线及恢复时间进行比较。持续的主观或客观变化，比短暂的预期发作后反应更重要。","sourceMetadata":"Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Use of Electroconvulsive Therapy, Indian Journal of Psychiatry 2023, sections 'Monitoring of clinical improvement' and 'Monitoring of cognitive adverse effects' (baseline and serial objective assessment; subjective memory reports; modify treatment when cognitive adverse effects are significant), https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10096214/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2211,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9b_wound_depth_change","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.741","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.741.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.741.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[335,424],"terminalOffsetsZh":[118,145],"fullStemEn":"At two wound-clinic visits, the nurse measures the same wound after cleansing, with the client in the same position and using the same method. The deepest point measured 2.6 cm at baseline and 1.8 cm today. Calculate the absolute decrease in wound depth in centimeters using baseline depth − current depth. Round to the nearest tenth. This single dimension does not by itself establish healing, stage, or tissue composition.","fullStemZh":"在两次伤口门诊复诊时，护士均在清洁伤口后、患者体位相同且测量方法相同的条件下测量同一伤口。基线时最深处为 2.6 cm，今天为 1.8 cm。使用“基线深度 − 当前深度”计算伤口深度的绝对减少值，单位为厘米，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。单一维度本身不能确定伤口已经愈合、伤口分期或组织构成。","terminalSentenceEn":"This single dimension does not by itself establish healing, stage, or tissue composition.","terminalSentenceZh":"单一维度本身不能确定伤口已经愈合、伤口分期或组织构成。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Round to the nearest tenth.","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用“基线深度 − 当前深度”计算伤口深度的绝对减少值，单位为厘米，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"absolute decrease in wound depth (cm)","zh":"伤口深度绝对减少值（cm）"},"acceptable":["0.8","0.8 cm"],"numeric":{"value":0.8,"tolerance":0,"unit":"cm"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Absolute depth decrease = 2.6 cm − 1.8 cm = 0.8 cm. Serial wound dimensions should be obtained with a consistent technique; the depth is measured at the deepest point. A smaller depth is one trend datum and must be interpreted with the rest of the wound assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"深度绝对减少值 = 2.6 cm − 1.8 cm = 0.8 cm。连续伤口尺寸应采用一致方法测量；深度取伤口最深处。深度变小只是一项趋势数据，必须结合其余伤口评估结果解释。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For an absolute decrease, subtract the newer measurement from the baseline and keep the requested unit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算绝对减少值时，用基线测量值减去较新的测量值，并保留题目要求的单位。","sourceMetadata":"Open RN, Nursing Skills, Chapter 20 Wound Care, wound-assessment section (measure the deepest point to the wound surface and document in centimeters), https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK593201/; Federal Bureau of Prisons, Prevention and Management of Acute and Chronic Wounds, wound-assessment table (serial length, width, and deepest-point depth in centimeters), https://www.bop.gov/resources/pdfs/wounds.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2212,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9b_montevideo_units","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.742","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.742.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.742.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[356,427],"terminalOffsetsZh":[141,161],"fullStemEn":"An intrauterine pressure catheter records four contractions during a 10-minute window. Resting tone is 15 mm Hg; peak pressures are 55, 70, 60, and 65 mm Hg. Calculate Montevideo units (MVU) using: for each contraction, subtract the resting tone from the peak pressure, then add all pressure rises during the 10-minute window. Enter a whole number in MVU. Do not diagnose labor arrest or change oxytocin from this number alone.","fullStemZh":"宫内压力导管在 10 分钟内记录到 4 次宫缩。静息张力为 15 mm Hg；峰值压力分别为 55、70、60 和 65 mm Hg。使用以下规则计算 Montevideo 单位（MVU）：每次宫缩用峰值压力减去静息张力，再把 10 分钟内所有压力升高值相加。以整数 MVU 填写。不能仅凭该数值诊断产程停滞或调整缩宫素。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not diagnose labor arrest or change oxytocin from this number alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"不能仅凭该数值诊断产程停滞或调整缩宫素。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Enter a whole number in MVU.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以整数 MVU 填写。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"uterine activity (MVU)","zh":"子宫活动（MVU）"},"acceptable":["190","190 MVU"],"numeric":{"value":190,"tolerance":0,"unit":"MVU"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pressure rises are 40, 55, 45, and 50 mm Hg. Their sum is 190 MVU. MVU quantify uterine activity over 10 minutes; clinical decisions require the full labor context.","rationaleCorrectZh":"各次压力升高值为 40、55、45 和 50 mm Hg，总和为 190 MVU。MVU 用于量化 10 分钟内的子宫活动；临床决策还需结合完整产程背景。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Subtract the same resting tone from every peak before adding; do not add the raw peak pressures.","testTakingStrategyZh":"每个峰值都要减去同一静息张力后再相加；不要直接相加原始峰值。","sourceMetadata":"ACOG Clinical Practice Guideline No. 8, First and Second Stage Labor Management, January 2024, active-phase arrest discussion using an intrauterine pressure catheter and 200 Montevideo units as one contextual adequacy benchmark; NICE NG229, Fetal monitoring in labour, recommendations on uterine-contraction assessment, https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/clinical-practice-guideline/articles/2024/01/first-and-second-stage-labor-management; https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/NG229/chapter/recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2213,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9b_pn_glucose_infusion_rate","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.743","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.743.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.743.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[220,282],"terminalOffsetsZh":[111,145],"fullStemEn":"A parenteral nutrition bag provides 275 g of dextrose over 16 hours to a client whose dosing weight is 68 kg. Use glucose infusion rate (GIR) = dextrose grams × 1000 mg/g ÷ (infusion hours × 60 min/hour × weight in kg). Calculate the GIR in mg/kg/min and round to the nearest tenth.","fullStemZh":"一袋肠外营养在 16 小时内向一名给药体重为 68 kg 的患者提供 275 g 葡萄糖。使用：葡萄糖输注速率（GIR）= 葡萄糖克数 × 1000 mg/g ÷（输注小时数 × 60 min/hour × 体重 kg）。计算 GIR，单位为 mg/kg/min，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the GIR in mg/kg/min and round to the nearest tenth.","terminalSentenceZh":"计算 GIR，单位为 mg/kg/min，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Use glucose infusion rate (GIR) = dextrose grams × 1000 mg/g ÷ (infusion hours × 60 min/hour × weight in kg).","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用：葡萄糖输注速率（GIR）= 葡萄糖克数 × 1000 mg/g ÷（输注小时数 × 60 min/hour × 体重 kg）。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"GIR (mg/kg/min)","zh":"GIR（mg/kg/min）"},"acceptable":["4.2","4.2 mg/kg/min"],"numeric":{"value":4.2,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mg/kg/min"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"GIR = 275,000 mg ÷ (16 × 60 × 68) = 275,000 ÷ 65,280 = 4.212... mg/kg/min, which rounds to 4.2 mg/kg/min. This result is the delivery rate only; it is not an insulin dose or a stand-alone prescription decision.","rationaleCorrectZh":"GIR = 275,000 mg ÷（16 × 60 × 68）= 275,000 ÷ 65,280 = 4.212... mg/kg/min，四舍五入为 4.2 mg/kg/min。该结果只表示葡萄糖输注速率，不是胰岛素剂量，也不能单独决定处方。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert grams to milligrams, convert the infusion duration to minutes, then divide by weight and round once at the end.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先把克换算为毫克，再把输注时间换算为分钟，然后除以体重，并在最后一次性四舍五入。","sourceMetadata":"ASPEN, Back to Basics: Parenteral Nutrition 101, carbohydrate section and glucose infusion rate equation (GIR = dextrose g × 1000 ÷ minutes ÷ kg), https://nutritioncare.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Back-to-Basics_Parenteral-Nutrition-101_Glanz.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2214,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9b_ect_consent_capacity","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.744","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT)","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.744.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.744.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[176,286],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,89],"fullStemEn":"Which documented actions satisfy informed-consent, decision-making-capacity, surrogate, and shared-decision requirements before or during an ECT course? Select all that apply. Apply the governing law and facility process for any surrogate decision; emergency rules vary by jurisdiction.","fullStemZh":"在 ECT 疗程开始前或进行期间，哪些记录措施符合知情同意、决策能力、代理人及共同决策要求？选择所有适用项。任何代理决策均应遵循适用法律和机构流程；紧急情况规则因司法管辖区而异。","terminalSentenceEn":"Apply the governing law and facility process for any surrogate decision; emergency rules vary by jurisdiction.","terminalSentenceZh":"任何代理决策均应遵循适用法律和机构流程；紧急情况规则因司法管辖区而异。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","penultimateSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"The admission consent is treated as blanket authorization for the entire ECT course without further discussion or review.","zh":"把住院同意书视为整个 ECT 疗程的笼统授权，不再讨论或复核。"},{"id":"D","en":"The clinician tells the client that refusal will result in withdrawal of all psychiatric care until the consent form is signed.","zh":"临床人员告诉患者，若拒绝签字，将停止所有精神科照护。"},{"id":"A","en":"Before the first treatment, the clinician discusses the indication, expected benefits, material risks including cognitive effects, alternatives, and the right to refuse or withdraw; the client asks questions and voluntarily agrees.","zh":"首次治疗前，临床人员说明适应证、预期获益、包括认知影响在内的重要风险、替代方案及拒绝或撤回的权利；患者提问后自愿同意。"},{"id":"C","en":"If the client lacks capacity, the team documents the assessment, follows the applicable legally authorized surrogate process, continues to involve the client, and returns consent authority to the client if capacity is regained.","zh":"若患者缺乏能力，团队记录评估，遵循适用的法律授权代理流程，继续让患者参与，并在能力恢复时把同意权交还患者。"},{"id":"F","en":"Because the client occasionally forgets appointments, the team records that the client automatically lacks capacity for ECT.","zh":"因为患者偶尔忘记预约，团队就记录其自动缺乏 ECT 决策能力。"},{"id":"B","en":"The team assesses the client's ability to understand, appreciate, reason about, and communicate this specific ECT decision instead of inferring incapacity from the diagnosis.","zh":"团队评估患者对本次 ECT 决定的理解、权衡、推理及表达选择能力，而不是根据诊断推定无能力。"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Valid ECT consent is individualized, voluntary, and revisited across the course. The team should explain the indication, expected benefits, material risks including cognitive effects, alternatives, and the right to refuse or withdraw; assess decision-specific capacity rather than infer incapacity from diagnosis or ordinary forgetfulness; and, when capacity is absent, use the legally authorized surrogate pathway while continuing to involve the client and returning consent authority to the client if capacity returns. Coercion, blanket admission consent, and automatic incapacity assumptions are invalid.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的 ECT 同意应个体化、自愿，并在整个疗程中持续复核。团队应说明适应证、预期获益、包括认知影响在内的重要风险、替代方案以及拒绝或撤回的权利；应评估与该决定相关的能力，而不能仅凭诊断或普通健忘推定无能力；当患者缺乏能力时，应依法律使用授权代理路径，同时继续让患者参与，并在能力恢复时把同意权交还患者。胁迫、笼统住院同意及自动推定无能力均无效。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose actions that protect voluntariness and assess the specific decision. Reject shortcuts that replace individualized consent with pressure, paperwork, or assumptions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择保护自愿性并评估具体决定的措施。排除用压力、笼统文件或假设取代个体化同意的做法。","sourceMetadata":"Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Use of Electroconvulsive Therapy, Indian Journal of Psychiatry 2023, sections 'Informed consent' and 'Consent in special situations' (information, voluntariness, ongoing consent, surrogate pathway, continued patient participation, and renewed direct consent when capacity returns), https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10096214/; American Academy of Family Physicians, Evaluating Medical Decision-Making Capacity in Practice (understanding, appreciation, reasoning, and communication; decision-specific assessment), https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2018/0701/p40.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2215,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9c_missed_combined_pills","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.745","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Reproductive & Endocrine Health","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.745.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.745.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,365],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,115],"fullStemEn":"At 0900, a client reports missing 2 consecutive active combined oral contraceptive pills in the first week of the pack. The usual pill time is 2100, and unprotected intercourse occurred 3 days ago. Ulipristal acetate is not being used. Place the supplied CDC actions in the time-anchored order the client should carry them out starting now and over the next 7 days.","fullStemZh":"0900，一名患者报告在复方口服避孕药周期的第 1 周连续漏服了 2 片含激素药片。平时服药时间为 2100，3 天前曾有无保护性交。本题不使用醋酸乌利司他。请按患者从现在开始及随后 7 天应执行的时间顺序排列所给 CDC 措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the supplied CDC actions in the time-anchored order the client should carry them out starting now and over the next 7 days.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按患者从现在开始及随后 7 天应执行的时间顺序排列所给 CDC 措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Ulipristal acetate is not being used.","penultimateSentenceZh":"本题不使用醋酸乌利司他。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"At the usual 2100 pill time, take the next scheduled active pill and then continue the pack daily.","zh":"到平时 2100 的服药时间，服用下一片计划含激素药片，之后每天继续本周期。"},{"id":"C","en":"For any intercourse from now until 7 consecutive hormonal pills have been taken, use condoms or abstain.","zh":"从现在起直到连续服用含激素药片 7 天，发生任何性交时均应使用安全套或禁欲。"},{"id":"D","en":"Today without delay, address emergency contraception and consider an appropriate method other than ulipristal acetate.","zh":"今天尽快处理紧急避孕，并考虑醋酸乌利司他以外的适当方法。"},{"id":"A","en":"At 0900, take the most recent missed active pill and discard the earlier missed active pill.","zh":"0900，服用最近漏服的一片含激素药片，并丢弃更早漏服的一片。"}],"correct":["A","D","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At 0900, take the most recent missed hormonal pill and discard the earlier missed pill. Because the missed pills occurred in week 1 and unprotected intercourse occurred within the previous 5 days, address emergency contraception other than ulipristal acetate today without delay rather than postponing it behind the seven-day backup interval. At the usual 2100 time, take the next scheduled pill and continue the pack. Use condoms or abstain until hormonal pills have been taken for 7 consecutive days.","rationaleCorrectZh":"0900，应服用最近漏服的一片含激素药片，并丢弃更早漏服的一片。由于漏服发生在第 1 周，且过去 5 天内有无保护性交，应在今天尽快处理醋酸乌利司他以外的紧急避孕，而不能推迟到 7 天备用避孕期之后。到平时 2100 的服药时间，应服用下一片计划药片并继续本周期。应使用安全套或禁欲，直到连续服用含激素药片 7 天。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the stated clock times and do not defer a time-sensitive emergency-contraception decision until after the seven-day backup period.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干给出的具体时间点，不要把有时间窗的紧急避孕决定推迟到 7 天备用避孕期之后。","sourceMetadata":"CDC, U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024, Figure 1 and section 'Recommended actions after late or missed combined oral contraceptives' (two or more consecutive hormonal pills missed; week 1 emergency-contraception consideration), https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/73/rr/rr7303a1.htm; https://www.cdc.gov/contraception/hcp/usspr/combined-hormonal-contraceptives.html","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2216,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9c_istap_skin_tear_pathway","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.746","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.746.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.746.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,81],"fullStemEn":"An older adult has a new skin tear with a viable skin flap. The facility follows the 2025 ISTAP pathway. Bleeding is controlled before cleansing, and the selected dressing is atraumatic and low adhesive. Place the necessary serial actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名老年患者出现新的皮肤撕裂伤，皮瓣仍有活性。机构采用 2025 年 ISTAP 路径。清洗前先控制出血，并使用无创、低黏性的敷料。请将必要的连续步骤按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the necessary serial actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将必要的连续步骤按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Bleeding is controlled before cleansing, and the selected dressing is atraumatic and low adhesive.","penultimateSentenceZh":"清洗前先控制出血，并使用无创、低黏性的敷料。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"At the planned review, reassess flap viability, wound-edge approximation, infection signs, and dressing performance.","zh":"在计划复评时，重新评估皮瓣活性、伤口边缘贴合、感染迹象及敷料表现。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the skin tear and control active bleeding with gentle pressure.","zh":"评估皮肤撕裂伤，并用轻柔加压控制活动性出血。"},{"id":"C","en":"If the flap remains viable, gently realign it over the wound bed without stretching or tension.","zh":"若皮瓣仍有活性，轻柔地将其复位覆盖伤床，避免拉伸或张力。"},{"id":"B","en":"Gently cleanse or irrigate the wound, pat the surrounding skin dry, and assess the flap.","zh":"轻柔清洗或冲洗伤口，拍干周围皮肤，并评估皮瓣。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply the selected atraumatic low-adhesive dressing and mark the dressing with an arrow showing the direction for removal.","zh":"使用选定的无创低黏性敷料，并在敷料上标记箭头指示移除方向。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The ISTAP pathway begins with assessment and bleeding control, followed by gentle cleansing or irrigation and flap assessment. A viable flap is gently realigned without tension. An atraumatic low-adhesive dressing is then applied and marked to show the direction of removal, followed by planned reassessment for flap viability, closure, infection, and dressing performance. Adhesive closure that can cause further trauma is avoided.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ISTAP 路径从评估和控制出血开始，随后轻柔清洗或冲洗并评估皮瓣。对有活性的皮瓣，应无张力地轻柔复位。然后使用无创低黏性敷料，并标记移除方向；之后按计划复评皮瓣活性、闭合、感染及敷料表现。应避免可能造成进一步损伤的黏性闭合材料。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Protect the flap by following the wound pathway: control bleeding, clean, realign, cover atraumatically, then reassess.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按伤口路径保护皮瓣：控制出血、清洗、复位、无创覆盖，再复评。","sourceMetadata":"International Skin Tear Advisory Panel (ISTAP), Best practice recommendations for the prevention and management of skin tears in aged skin, 2025, assessment and treatment pathway: assess/control bleeding; cleanse/irrigate; reapproximate viable flap; apply atraumatic low-adhesive dressing and mark removal direction; monitor and reassess, https://woundsinternational.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ISTAP25_CD_Skin-tears_WINT_web.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2217,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9c_enteral_tube_occlusion","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.747","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.747.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.747.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[223,337],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,93],"fullStemEn":"A client's gastrostomy feeding tube will not flush. Stop the feeding and medication administration. Tube placement has been verified according to facility policy. Place the supplied ASPEN-based declogging actions in order. Any enzyme preparation or mechanical declogging device must be authorized by the prescriber and facility protocol.","fullStemZh":"一名患者的胃造口喂养管无法冲洗。停止喂养和经管给药。已依机构政策确认导管位置。请按顺序排列所给的、基于 ASPEN 的疏通措施。任何酶制剂或机械疏通装置均须经处方人员授权并符合机构流程。","terminalSentenceEn":"Any enzyme preparation or mechanical declogging device must be authorized by the prescriber and facility protocol.","terminalSentenceZh":"任何酶制剂或机械疏通装置均须经处方人员授权并符合机构流程。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Place the supplied ASPEN-based declogging actions in order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列所给的、基于 ASPEN 的疏通措施。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Inspect the full external tubing and connectors; release any closed clamp and straighten any kink.","zh":"检查全部外部管路和连接处；打开关闭的夹子并拉直任何扭结。"},{"id":"C","en":"If water fails, use the institution-approved pancreatic-enzyme preparation, enzymatic kit, or mechanical declogging device as authorized.","zh":"若水冲洗无效，按授权使用机构认可的胰酶制剂、酶疏通套件或机械疏通装置。"},{"id":"B","en":"Using a large enteral syringe, instill warm water with gentle back-and-forth pressure and allow it time to penetrate the clog.","zh":"使用大容量肠内注射器，以轻柔来回压力注入温水，并留出时间让水渗入堵塞物。"},{"id":"D","en":"If patency is still not restored, stop repeated attempts and notify the prescriber or nutrition-support team for tube evaluation or replacement.","zh":"若仍未恢复通畅，停止反复尝试，并通知处方人员或营养支持团队评估或更换导管。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First rule out an external clamp, kink, or connector obstruction. Water is the first-line declogging fluid; use a large enteral syringe with gentle back-and-forth pressure and allow time for the water to penetrate the clog. If water fails, an institution-approved pancreatic-enzyme solution, enzymatic kit, or mechanical device is second line when authorized. If patency still cannot be restored, stop repeated attempts and arrange expert evaluation or tube replacement. Acidic beverages can worsen formula-protein precipitation, and excessive force or sharp objects can damage the tube.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先排除外部夹闭、扭结或连接处阻塞。水是首选疏通液；应使用大容量肠内注射器轻柔地来回加压，并留出时间让水渗入堵塞物。若水无效，在获得授权时可使用机构认可的胰酶溶液、酶疏通套件或机械装置作为二线措施。若仍不能恢复通畅，应停止反复尝试，并安排专科评估或更换导管。酸性饮料可能加重配方蛋白沉淀，过度用力或尖锐物也可能损坏导管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the least forceful reversible step first: external mechanics, water, authorized second-line declogging, then expert evaluation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先采用力量最小且可逆的步骤：检查外部机械问题、用水冲洗、使用经授权的二线疏通措施，最后安排专科评估。","sourceMetadata":"ASPEN Safe Practices for Enteral Nutrition Therapy, Section 7, EAD patency and tube-occlusion recommendations (external obstruction check; water first line; authorized pancreatic-enzyme solution, enzymatic kit, or mechanical device second line; avoid acidic beverages and excessive pressure), https://aspenjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1177/0148607116673053","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2218,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9c_delayed_hemolytic_reaction","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.748","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transfusion & Blood Products","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.748.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.748.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,357],"terminalOffsetsZh":[87,121],"fullStemEn":"Eight days after an RBC transfusion, a client has hemoglobin decreased from 9.8 to 7.5 g/dL, lower hematocrit, rising indirect bilirubin and LDH, a newly positive direct antiglobulin test (DAT), and a newly identified RBC alloantibody. During and immediately after transfusion there was no high fever, severe rigors, hypotension, dyspnea, or hemoglobinuria.","fullStemZh":"输注红细胞 8 天后，患者血红蛋白从 9.8 降至 7.5 g/dL，红细胞压积下降，间接胆红素和 LDH 升高，直接抗人球蛋白试验（DAT）新转阳，并新检出红细胞同种抗体。输血期间及输血后不久无高热、剧烈寒战、低血压、呼吸困难或血红蛋白尿。","terminalSentenceEn":"During and immediately after transfusion there was no high fever, severe rigors, hypotension, dyspnea, or hemoglobinuria.","terminalSentenceZh":"输血期间及输血后不久无高热、剧烈寒战、低血压、呼吸困难或血红蛋白尿。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Eight days after an RBC transfusion, a client has hemoglobin decreased from 9.8 to 7.5 g/dL, lower hematocrit, rising indirect bilirubin and LDH, a newly positive direct antiglobulin test (DAT), and a newly identified RBC alloantibody.","penultimateSentenceZh":"输注红细胞 8 天后，患者血红蛋白从 9.8 降至 7.5 g/dL，红细胞压积下降，间接胆红素和 LDH 升高，直接抗人球蛋白试验（DAT）新转阳，并新检出红细胞同种抗体。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The overall pattern is most consistent with {{1}}. The new DAT and alloantibody with biochemical hemolysis indicate {{2}}. The absence of hemoglobinuria is {{3}}.","zh":"整体模式最符合{{1}}。新出现 DAT 阳性和同种抗体并伴生化溶血，提示{{2}}。无血红蛋白尿{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"bacterial contamination of the component","zh":"血液成分细菌污染"},{"id":"o2","en":"a febrile nonhemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"非溶血性发热性输血反应"},{"id":"o1","en":"a delayed hemolytic transfusion reaction","zh":"迟发性溶血性输血反应"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"delayed immune destruction of transfused RBCs","zh":"输注红细胞的迟发免疫性破坏"},{"id":"o3","en":"nonimmune dilution of the blood count","zh":"血细胞计数的非免疫性稀释"},{"id":"o2","en":"isolated circulatory fluid overload","zh":"单纯循环液体过多"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"sufficient to exclude a delayed hemolytic reaction","zh":"足以排除迟发性溶血反应"},{"id":"o1","en":"compatible with the diagnosis because hemoglobinemia and hemoglobinuria are uncommon in delayed reactions","zh":"仍与诊断相容，因为迟发反应中血红蛋白血症和血红蛋白尿并不常见"},{"id":"o3","en":"proof that the client instead has TACO","zh":"证明患者实际发生了 TACO"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The 2- to 14-day timing, falling hemoglobin/hematocrit, biochemical hemolysis, positive DAT, and newly detectable alloantibody fit a delayed hemolytic transfusion reaction caused by an anamnestic immune response against transfused RBCs. The absence of hemoglobinuria does not exclude the diagnosis because hemoglobinemia and hemoglobinuria are uncommon in delayed reactions. The lack of acute fever, rigors, hypotension, and respiratory cues makes febrile reaction, bacterial contamination, TACO, and TRALI less consistent.","rationaleCorrectZh":"发生于输血后 2–14 天、血红蛋白/红细胞压积下降、生化溶血、DAT 阳性及新检出同种抗体，符合因回忆性免疫反应破坏输注红细胞所致的迟发性溶血性输血反应。无血红蛋白尿并不能排除，因为迟发反应中血红蛋白血症和血红蛋白尿并不常见。缺少急性高热、寒战、低血压和呼吸线索，使发热性反应、细菌污染、TACO 和 TRALI 更不符合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use timing and the immune laboratory pattern together. Do not let the absence of an uncommon delayed-reaction feature erase the stronger evidence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把发生时间与免疫实验室模式结合判断。不要因缺少迟发反应中不常见的表现，而忽略更强的证据。","sourceMetadata":"AABB, Circular of Information for the Use of Human Blood and Blood Components, June 2024, section 'Delayed Hemolytic Transfusion Reactions' (usually 2-14 days; anamnestic antibody response; positive DAT, decreased hemoglobin/hematocrit, increased bilirubin and LDH; hemoglobinemia/hemoglobinuria uncommon), https://www.aabb.org/docs/default-source/default-document-library/resources/circular-of-information-watermark.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2219,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9c_pn_peripheral_central_access","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.749","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.749.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.749.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[443,560],"terminalOffsetsZh":[145,186],"fullStemEn":"The nutrition-support service uses the following criteria for peripheral and central parenteral nutrition: peripheral PN may be used for a short anticipated duration when the final osmolarity is no more than 900 mOsm/L and the peripheral site can be closely monitored; more hyperosmolar PN requires central venous administration. A 7-day PN order has a final osmolarity of 820 mOsm/L and is prescribed through a healthy forearm peripheral IV. Apply only the criteria stated here; this item does not present 900 mOsm/L as a universal limit outside this context.","fullStemZh":"营养支持团队采用以下外周和中心静脉肠外营养标准：当预计疗程较短、最终渗透浓度不超过 900 mOsm/L，且可密切监测外周静脉部位时，可采用外周肠外营养；渗透浓度更高的 PN 需要中心静脉给药。一份预计 7 天的 PN 医嘱最终渗透浓度为 820 mOsm/L，拟经健康的前臂外周静脉输注。仅应用此处给出的标准；本题不把 900 mOsm/L 描述为所有情境下的通用上限。","terminalSentenceEn":"Apply only the criteria stated here; this item does not present 900 mOsm/L as a universal limit outside this context.","terminalSentenceZh":"仅应用此处给出的标准；本题不把 900 mOsm/L 描述为所有情境下的通用上限。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A 7-day PN order has a final osmolarity of 820 mOsm/L and is prescribed through a healthy forearm peripheral IV.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一份预计 7 天的 PN 医嘱最终渗透浓度为 820 mOsm/L，拟经健康的前臂外周静脉输注。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Under the criteria stated in the stem, this order fits {{1}}, and the priority access-related implication is {{2}}. If the same order is reformulated to 1150 mOsm/L, it should instead use {{3}}.","zh":"根据题干所述标准，该医嘱符合{{1}}，与通路相关的重点是{{2}}。若同一医嘱改配为 1150 mOsm/L，则应改用{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"peripheral parenteral nutrition","zh":"外周肠外营养"},{"id":"o2","en":"central parenteral nutrition as the only acceptable route","zh":"必须使用中心静脉肠外营养"},{"id":"o3","en":"enteral tube feeding","zh":"肠内管饲"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"omitting site checks because the osmolarity is below the supplied limit","zh":"因渗透浓度低于题干上限而不检查输注部位"},{"id":"o3","en":"monitoring glucose only, without assessing the vascular site","zh":"只监测血糖，不评估血管通路部位"},{"id":"o1","en":"frequent assessment of the peripheral site for phlebitis, infiltration, pain, erythema, and patency","zh":"频繁评估外周部位的静脉炎、渗漏、疼痛、红斑及通畅性"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the same forearm peripheral IV without changing the access plan","zh":"不改变通路方案，继续使用同一前臂外周静脉"},{"id":"o1","en":"central venous access with the catheter tip in the central circulation","zh":"导管尖端位于中心循环的中心静脉通路"},{"id":"o3","en":"a feeding tube because the solution is hyperosmolar","zh":"因溶液高渗而改用喂养管"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Under the ASPEN-based criteria stated in the stem, the short duration and 820 mOsm/L formulation fit peripheral PN. The key nursing implication is frequent assessment of the peripheral site for phlebitis, infiltration, pain, erythema, or loss of patency. If the formulation is changed to 1150 mOsm/L, the same criteria support central venous access with the catheter tip in the central circulation rather than continuing through the peripheral IV.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据题干所述的 ASPEN 标准，短期疗程及 820 mOsm/L 配方符合外周 PN。关键护理监测是频繁评估外周部位是否出现静脉炎、渗漏、疼痛、红斑或通畅性丧失。若配方改为 1150 mOsm/L，同一标准支持使用导管尖端位于中心循环的中心静脉通路，而不是继续通过该外周静脉。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the exact route-selection criteria stated in the stem: match osmolarity and anticipated duration to access, then choose monitoring that addresses that access.","testTakingStrategyZh":"严格应用题干给出的通路选择标准：根据渗透浓度和预计疗程匹配通路，再选择针对该通路的监测。","sourceMetadata":"ASPEN, Back to Basics: Parenteral Nutrition 101, vascular access and osmolarity section (peripheral PN for short-term use and final osmolarity ≤900 mOsm/L; central access for more hyperosmolar PN; monitor peripheral access complications), https://nutritioncare.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Back-to-Basics_Parenteral-Nutrition-101_Glanz.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2220,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format9c_noisy_respiratory_secretions","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.750","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.750.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.750.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,70],"fullStemEn":"A client in the last days of life is unresponsive and appears relaxed. A rattling sound is heard in the upper airway. Respirations are unlabored, there is no grimacing or accessory-muscle use, and the lungs have no new crackles or signs of pulmonary edema.","fullStemZh":"一名处于生命最后阶段的患者无反应，但看起来放松。上气道可听到咕噜样声音。呼吸不费力，无皱眉或辅助呼吸肌使用，肺部无新出现湿啰音或肺水肿迹象。","terminalSentenceEn":"Respirations are unlabored, there is no grimacing or accessory-muscle use, and the lungs have no new crackles or signs of pulmonary edema.","terminalSentenceZh":"呼吸不费力，无皱眉或辅助呼吸肌使用，肺部无新出现湿啰音或肺水肿迹象。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A rattling sound is heard in the upper airway.","penultimateSentenceZh":"上气道可听到咕噜样声音。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The finding is most consistent with {{1}}. The nurse should explain to the family that {{2}}. The initial management approach is {{3}}.","zh":"该发现最符合{{1}}。护士应向家属解释{{2}}。初始处理方法是{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"distressing dyspnea","zh":"明显呼吸困难"},{"id":"o3","en":"pulmonary edema","zh":"肺水肿"},{"id":"o1","en":"pooled upper-airway secretions","zh":"上气道分泌物积聚"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the sound proves that the client is choking","zh":"这种声音证明患者正在窒息"},{"id":"o3","en":"the sound guarantees that the client is in pain","zh":"这种声音说明患者一定疼痛"},{"id":"o1","en":"the sound can be distressing to hear but is unlikely to cause discomfort to the dying person","zh":"这种声音可能让听者难受，但不太可能使临终患者感到不适"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"automatically give medication solely to eliminate the sound","zh":"仅为消除声音而自动给予药物"},{"id":"o2","en":"perform routine deep suctioning as the universal first action","zh":"把常规深部吸引作为普遍首选措施"},{"id":"o1","en":"assess possible causes and impact, reposition when appropriate, and provide mouth care","zh":"评估可能原因和影响，适当改变体位并进行口腔护理"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pattern is most consistent with pooled respiratory secretions, not dyspnea or pulmonary edema. NICE advises explaining that the sound can be distressing for family to hear but is unlikely to cause discomfort to the dying person. Initial management includes assessing possible causes and impact, repositioning when appropriate, and mouth care. Medication is considered when secretions are causing distress, and routine deep suction is not a universal first action.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该模式最符合呼吸道分泌物积聚，而不是呼吸困难或肺水肿。NICE 建议向家属解释：这种声音可能让家属难受，但不太可能使临终患者感到不适。初始处理包括评估可能原因和影响、适当改变体位及口腔护理。只有分泌物造成不适时才考虑药物；常规深部吸引不是普遍首选措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the sound from distress. The absence of breathing effort or pulmonary findings directs the answer toward secretion care and family explanation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把声音与不适区分开。无呼吸费力或肺部异常，支持选择分泌物照护及家属解释。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG31, Care of dying adults in the last days of life, recommendations 1.5.29-1.5.34 (assess causes and impact of noisy respiratory secretions; reassure that noise is unlikely to cause discomfort; use nonpharmacological measures; consider medicine if secretions are causing distress; monitor and change or stop treatment), https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng31/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2221,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11a_necrotizing_soft_tissue_infection","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.751","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.751.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.751.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[713,789],"terminalOffsetsZh":[216,238],"fullStemEn":"A client was admitted 6 hours ago for presumed cellulitis of the right thigh and has received the first prescribed antimicrobial dose. The client now reports rapidly worsening deep pain that extends well beyond the visible erythema. Temperature is 102.9 °F (39.4 °C), heart rate 132/min, blood pressure 86/48 mm Hg, and the client is newly confused. The erythema has spread 7 cm beyond the marked border; the skin is tense with dusky patches and hemorrhagic bullae. The thigh remains compressible, distal pulses are present, and there is no recent immobilization. The emergency plan authorizes immediate surgical evaluation, broad empiric IV antimicrobial therapy, and sepsis resuscitation. Complete the bow-tie. Imaging must not delay operative evaluation when clinical suspicion is high.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因疑似右大腿蜂窝织炎于 6 小时前入院，并已接受首剂医嘱抗菌药。患者现报告深部疼痛迅速加重，疼痛范围明显超过可见红斑。体温 102.9 °F (39.4 °C)，心率 132 次/分，血压 86/48 mm Hg，并新出现意识混乱。红斑已越过标记边界 7 cm；皮肤紧张，出现暗紫色斑片和出血性大疱。大腿仍可压缩，远端脉搏存在，且近期无制动史。急诊方案已授权立即外科评估、广谱经验性静脉抗菌治疗及脓毒症复苏。请完成蝴蝶结题。临床高度怀疑时，不得因影像检查延误手术评估。","terminalSentenceEn":"Imaging must not delay operative evaluation when clinical suspicion is high.","terminalSentenceZh":"临床高度怀疑时，不得因影像检查延误手术评估。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1c2","en":"Uncomplicated cellulitis","zh":"单纯蜂窝织炎"},{"id":"q1c3","en":"Deep-vein thrombosis","zh":"深静脉血栓形成"},{"id":"q1c4","en":"Acute compartment syndrome","zh":"急性骨筋膜室综合征"},{"id":"q1c1","en":"Necrotizing soft-tissue infection","zh":"坏死性软组织感染"}],"correct":"q1c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1a4","en":"Massage the thigh to improve circulation","zh":"按摩大腿以改善循环"},{"id":"q1a2","en":"Begin the authorized broad empiric IV antimicrobial and sepsis-resuscitation pathway now","zh":"立即启动已授权的广谱经验性静脉抗菌治疗和脓毒症复苏路径"},{"id":"q1a1","en":"Obtain immediate surgical consultation and prepare for urgent exploration and debridement","zh":"立即外科会诊，并准备紧急探查和清创"},{"id":"q1a3","en":"Continue routine cellulitis care and reassess tomorrow","zh":"继续常规蜂窝织炎护理，明日再复评"}],"correct":["q1a1","q1a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q1p1","en":"Serial hemodynamics, mental status, urine output, and lactate","zh":"连续血流动力学、意识、尿量和乳酸"},{"id":"q1p2","en":"Spread and depth of erythema, bullae, discoloration, and tissue injury","zh":"红斑、大疱、变色及组织损伤的扩展和深度"},{"id":"q1p4","en":"Pain score at a routine outpatient visit","zh":"常规门诊随访时的疼痛评分"},{"id":"q1p3","en":"One distal-pulse check only","zh":"仅一次远端脉搏检查"}],"correct":["q1p1","q1p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rapid progression despite initial therapy, pain extending beyond visible findings, systemic toxicity, hypotension, confusion, dusky skin, and hemorrhagic bullae strongly support necrotizing soft-tissue infection. The priority is immediate surgical consultation with operative exploration and debridement as indicated, together with the already authorized broad empiric IV antimicrobial and sepsis-resuscitation pathway. Serial hemodynamics and perfusion, plus the spread and depth of local tissue findings, track deterioration or response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在初始治疗后仍迅速进展、疼痛超出可见病变范围、全身中毒、低血压、意识混乱、皮肤暗紫及出血性大疱，强烈支持坏死性软组织感染。优先措施是立即外科会诊，并按需要进行手术探查和清创，同时执行已授权的广谱经验性静脉抗菌治疗及脓毒症复苏路径。连续血流动力学和灌注指标，以及局部组织病变的扩展和深度，可追踪恶化或反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize tempo and toxicity. Rapid spread plus pain beyond the visible lesion and shock should override the initial benign label of cellulitis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先看进展速度和全身中毒。迅速扩展、疼痛超出可见病变并伴休克，应推翻最初较轻的蜂窝织炎判断。","sourceMetadata":"IDSA, 2014 Skin and Soft Tissue Infection Guideline, section “Evaluation and Treatment of Necrotizing Fasciitis,” recommendations 1–3 and listed suggestive features: https://www.idsociety.org/practice-guideline/skin-and-soft-tissue-infections/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2222,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11a_acute_primary_angle_closure","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.752","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.752.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.752.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[467,488],"terminalOffsetsZh":[125,133],"fullStemEn":"A client develops abrupt severe right-eye pain, blurred vision with colored halos, frontal headache, nausea, and vomiting. The right cornea is hazy, the pupil is fixed in a mid-dilated position, and the anterior chamber appears shallow. Visual acuity is markedly reduced and intraocular pressure is 54 mm Hg in the right eye and 16 mm Hg in the left. The emergency ophthalmology plan authorizes immediate pressure-lowering treatment and urgent definitive evaluation. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者突然出现右眼剧痛、视物模糊伴彩色光晕、额部头痛、恶心和呕吐。右侧角膜混浊，瞳孔固定于中度散大位，前房看起来较浅。右眼视力明显下降，眼压为 54 mm Hg；左眼眼压为 16 mm Hg。眼科急诊方案已授权立即降低眼压治疗并进行紧急确定性评估。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The emergency ophthalmology plan authorizes immediate pressure-lowering treatment and urgent definitive evaluation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"眼科急诊方案已授权立即降低眼压治疗并进行紧急确定性评估。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2c4","en":"Migraine with visual aura","zh":"伴视觉先兆的偏头痛"},{"id":"q2c1","en":"Acute primary angle closure","zh":"急性原发性闭角"},{"id":"q2c3","en":"Anterior uveitis","zh":"前葡萄膜炎"},{"id":"q2c2","en":"Primary open-angle glaucoma","zh":"原发性开角型青光眼"}],"correct":"q2c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2a2","en":"Activate urgent ophthalmology care and prepare for definitive laser iridotomy as directed","zh":"启动紧急眼科处理，并按指示准备确定性激光虹膜切开术"},{"id":"q2a4","en":"Patch the painful eye and allow the client to sleep","zh":"遮盖疼痛眼并让患者休息"},{"id":"q2a3","en":"Arrange routine ophthalmology follow-up in several weeks","zh":"安排数周后的常规眼科随访"},{"id":"q2a1","en":"Administer the already prescribed emergency intraocular-pressure-lowering regimen","zh":"执行已医嘱的急诊降眼压方案"}],"correct":["q2a1","q2a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q2p2","en":"Visual acuity, pupil and corneal findings, pain, nausea, and vital signs","zh":"视力、瞳孔和角膜所见、疼痛、恶心及生命体征"},{"id":"q2p4","en":"Eyeglass prescription strength","zh":"眼镜处方度数"},{"id":"q2p3","en":"Annual peripheral-field test only","zh":"仅年度周边视野检查"},{"id":"q2p1","en":"Serial intraocular pressure","zh":"连续眼压"}],"correct":["q2p1","q2p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The abrupt painful monocular syndrome with halos, nausea, a hazy cornea, fixed mid-dilated pupil, shallow chamber, and markedly elevated pressure is acute primary angle closure. The nurse should activate urgent ophthalmology care, administer the already prescribed emergency pressure-lowering regimen, and prepare for definitive laser iridotomy when directed. Serial intraocular pressure and visual/ocular findings track response, while vital signs and nausea or vomiting track systemic status and treatment tolerance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"突发单眼剧痛、彩色光晕、恶心、角膜混浊、固定中度散大瞳孔、前房浅及眼压显著升高，符合急性原发性闭角。护士应启动紧急眼科处理，执行已医嘱的急诊降眼压方案，并按指示准备确定性激光虹膜切开术。连续眼压及视力/眼部所见可追踪反应；生命体征和恶心呕吐可反映全身状态及治疗耐受。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the symptom tempo to the examination. Sudden pain plus a fixed mid-dilated pupil, hazy cornea, shallow chamber, and very high pressure is not chronic open-angle disease.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将症状进展速度与检查所见结合。突发疼痛加固定中度散大瞳孔、角膜混浊、前房浅和极高眼压，不是慢性开角型疾病。","sourceMetadata":"Royal College of Ophthalmologists, The Management of Angle-Closure Glaucoma (2022), acute angle-closure presentation, immediate management, referral, and monitoring sections: https://www.rcophth.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/The-Management-of-Angle-Closure-Glaucoma-Clinical-Guidelines.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2223,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11a_postpartum_endometritis","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.753","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.753.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.753.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[559,580],"terminalOffsetsZh":[158,166],"fullStemEn":"On postpartum day 2 after an unplanned cesarean birth following prolonged rupture of membranes, a client has temperature 102.2 °F (39.0 °C), heart rate 122/min, lower-abdominal pain, marked uterine fundal tenderness, and malodorous purulent lochia. The breasts are soft without focal erythema, urination causes no dysuria, and the abdominal incision is dry without drainage or spreading erythema. The maternal-infection plan authorizes ordered cultures when indicated without delaying prescribed broad-spectrum IV antimicrobial therapy and sepsis assessment. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在胎膜长时间破裂后接受非计划剖宫产，产后第 2 天出现体温 102.2 °F (39.0 °C)、心率 122 次/分、下腹痛、明显子宫底压痛及恶臭脓性恶露。双乳柔软，无局灶红斑；排尿无尿痛；腹部切口干燥，无引流或扩展性红斑。产妇感染方案已授权按指征采集培养，且不得延误已医嘱的广谱静脉抗菌治疗和脓毒症评估。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The maternal-infection plan authorizes ordered cultures when indicated without delaying prescribed broad-spectrum IV antimicrobial therapy and sepsis assessment.","penultimateSentenceZh":"产妇感染方案已授权按指征采集培养，且不得延误已医嘱的广谱静脉抗菌治疗和脓毒症评估。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3c2","en":"Lactational mastitis","zh":"哺乳期乳腺炎"},{"id":"q3c4","en":"Cesarean-incision infection","zh":"剖宫产切口感染"},{"id":"q3c3","en":"Urinary tract infection","zh":"尿路感染"},{"id":"q3c5","en":"Septic pelvic thrombophlebitis","zh":"脓毒性盆腔血栓性静脉炎"},{"id":"q3c1","en":"Postpartum endometritis","zh":"产后子宫内膜炎"}],"correct":"q3c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3a4","en":"Massage the tender uterine fundus repeatedly","zh":"反复按摩有压痛的子宫底"},{"id":"q3a3","en":"Discharge the client with routine postpartum follow-up","zh":"让患者出院并常规产后随访"},{"id":"q3a1","en":"Begin the prescribed broad-spectrum IV antimicrobial and sepsis-support pathway","zh":"启动已医嘱的广谱静脉抗菌治疗和脓毒症支持路径"},{"id":"q3a2","en":"Obtain ordered cultures and perform focused source assessment without delaying therapy","zh":"在不延误治疗的情况下采集医嘱培养并进行重点感染源评估"}],"correct":["q3a1","q3a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q3p4","en":"Incision length only","zh":"仅切口长度"},{"id":"q3p3","en":"Newborn weight","zh":"新生儿体重"},{"id":"q3p2","en":"Hemodynamics, mental status, urine output, and organ-function trends","zh":"血流动力学、意识、尿量和器官功能趋势"},{"id":"q3p1","en":"Temperature trend, uterine tenderness, abdominal pain, and lochia","zh":"体温趋势、子宫压痛、腹痛和恶露"}],"correct":["q3p1","q3p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The postpartum timing, uterine fundal tenderness, lower-abdominal pain, and malodorous purulent lochia localize the likely source to postpartum endometritis. The absence of breast, urinary, and incision findings makes common competing sources less likely. Begin the authorized broad-spectrum IV antimicrobial and sepsis-support pathway, obtain ordered specimens without delaying therapy, and reassess if fever does not improve. Temperature, uterine tenderness, lochia, hemodynamics, perfusion, and organ function track response or deterioration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"产后时间、子宫底压痛、下腹痛及恶臭脓性恶露，将最可能感染源定位为产后子宫内膜炎。缺少乳房、泌尿及切口所见，使常见竞争来源较不可能。应启动已授权的广谱静脉抗菌治疗和脓毒症支持路径，在不延误治疗的情况下采集医嘱标本，并在发热未改善时重新评估。体温、子宫压痛、恶露、血流动力学、灌注和器官功能可追踪反应或恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Localize postpartum fever. Uterine tenderness plus foul or purulent lochia points to the uterus, while breast, urinary, and wound findings would point elsewhere.","testTakingStrategyZh":"定位产后发热来源。子宫压痛加恶臭或脓性恶露指向子宫；乳房、泌尿或伤口所见则会指向其他来源。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual Professional, Postpartum Endometritis, “Symptoms and Signs” and “Diagnosis” passages covering timing, uterine localization, competing postpartum fever sources, and persistent-fever reassessment: https://www.merckmanuals.com/en-ca/professional/gynecology-and-obstetrics/postpartum-care-and-associated-disorders/postpartum-endometritis; plus WHO, Recommendations on maternal health (2nd ed., 2025), Table 65, postpartum-endometritis treatment recommendation and resolution findings: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK615643/table/part2.tab65/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2224,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11a_acute_mesenteric_ischemia","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.754","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.754.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.754.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[605,669],"terminalOffsetsZh":[180,199],"fullStemEn":"A 76-year-old client with atrial fibrillation who stopped anticoagulation 1 week ago develops abrupt severe periumbilical pain. The client is restless and rates the pain 10/10, but the abdomen is initially soft with only mild diffuse tenderness. Heart rate is 118/min and blood pressure is 94/58 mm Hg. Lactate is 1.8 mmol/L. There is no vomiting with distention, no profuse diarrhea, and no right-upper-quadrant localization. The emergency plan authorizes immediate CT angiography, surgical/vascular consultation, resuscitation, and the source-control or revascularization pathway. Complete the bow-tie. Do not wait for peritonitis or a high lactate before escalating.","fullStemZh":"一名 76 岁房颤患者 1 周前停用抗凝药，现突然出现严重脐周疼痛。患者烦躁，疼痛评分 10/10，但初始腹部柔软，仅有轻度弥漫压痛。心率 118 次/分，血压 94/58 mm Hg，乳酸 1.8 mmol/L。无伴腹胀的呕吐、无大量腹泻，也无右上腹定位。急诊方案已授权立即 CT 血管造影、外科/血管会诊、复苏以及感染源控制或血运重建路径。请完成蝴蝶结题。不得等待腹膜炎或乳酸升高后再升级处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not wait for peritonitis or a high lactate before escalating.","terminalSentenceZh":"不得等待腹膜炎或乳酸升高后再升级处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4c3","en":"Mechanical bowel obstruction","zh":"机械性肠梗阻"},{"id":"q4c4","en":"Acute gastroenteritis","zh":"急性胃肠炎"},{"id":"q4c2","en":"Acute pancreatitis","zh":"急性胰腺炎"},{"id":"q4c1","en":"Acute mesenteric ischemia","zh":"急性肠系膜缺血"},{"id":"q4c5","en":"Uncomplicated biliary disease","zh":"单纯胆道疾病"}],"correct":"q4c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4a1","en":"Obtain urgent CT angiography without waiting for peritonitis or a high lactate","zh":"立即进行 CT 血管造影，不等待腹膜炎或高乳酸"},{"id":"q4a4","en":"Give a meal and reassess after digestion","zh":"给予进食并在消化后复评"},{"id":"q4a3","en":"Observe until tomorrow because the lactate is normal","zh":"因乳酸正常而观察至明日"},{"id":"q4a2","en":"Activate surgical/vascular consultation and the authorized resuscitation and revascularization/source-control pathway","zh":"启动外科/血管会诊及已授权的复苏和血运重建/感染源控制路径"}],"correct":["q4a1","q4a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q4p4","en":"Daily body weight only","zh":"仅每日体重"},{"id":"q4p2","en":"Serial pain and abdominal examination for evolving peritoneal findings","zh":"连续疼痛及腹部检查以发现进展性腹膜体征"},{"id":"q4p3","en":"The initial lactate value only","zh":"仅初始乳酸值"},{"id":"q4p1","en":"Hemodynamics, urine output, acid-base status, and lactate trend","zh":"血流动力学、尿量、酸碱状态和乳酸趋势"}],"correct":["q4p1","q4p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abrupt severe pain out of proportion to the early abdominal examination in a client with an embolic risk is highly concerning for acute mesenteric ischemia. A normal early lactate does not exclude it. Immediate CT angiography and urgent surgical/vascular involvement are required while resuscitation and the authorized revascularization or source-control pathway proceed. Hemodynamics, perfusion and lactate trends, and serial abdominal findings track deterioration or response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有栓塞风险的患者出现突发剧烈疼痛，且疼痛与早期腹部检查不相称，高度提示急性肠系膜缺血。早期乳酸正常不能排除。应立即进行 CT 血管造影并紧急外科/血管团队参与，同时执行复苏及已授权的血运重建或感染源控制路径。血流动力学、灌注和乳酸趋势以及连续腹部所见可追踪恶化或反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not wait for late findings. In a vascular-risk client, severe abrupt pain with a relatively benign early abdomen is the warning pattern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要等待晚期表现。有血管风险的患者出现突发剧痛而早期腹部体征相对轻，是警示模式。","sourceMetadata":"World Society of Emergency Surgery, Acute mesenteric ischemia: updated guidelines (2022), clinical presentation/laboratory limitations, CTA without delay, resuscitation, antibiotics, and revascularization/source-control recommendations: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9580452/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2225,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11a_immune_ttp","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.755","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.755.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.755.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[613,634],"terminalOffsetsZh":[213,221],"fullStemEn":"A client has new confusion and petechiae. Platelet count is 16 ×10³/µL, hemoglobin 7.9 g/dL, reticulocyte count is elevated, LDH and indirect bilirubin are elevated, haptoglobin is undetectable, and the smear shows numerous schistocytes. PT and aPTT are normal. Creatinine is 1.4 mg/dL. The client has had no heparin exposure and no diarrheal prodrome. The laboratory can obtain an ADAMTS13 sample immediately before any plasma-containing treatment without delaying therapy. The emergency hematology plan authorizes urgent therapeutic plasma exchange and corticosteroid treatment for high-probability immune TTP. Complete the bow-tie.","fullStemZh":"一名患者新出现意识混乱和瘀点。血小板计数 16 ×10³/µL，血红蛋白 7.9 g/dL，网织红细胞升高，LDH 和间接胆红素升高，结合珠蛋白测不到，外周血涂片可见大量裂红细胞。PT 和 aPTT 正常，肌酐 1.4 mg/dL。患者无肝素暴露，也无腹泻前驱症状。实验室可在任何含血浆治疗前立即采集 ADAMTS13 标本，且不会延误治疗。急诊血液科方案已授权对高概率免疫性 TTP 紧急进行治疗性血浆置换和糖皮质激素治疗。请完成蝴蝶结题。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The emergency hematology plan authorizes urgent therapeutic plasma exchange and corticosteroid treatment for high-probability immune TTP.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急诊血液科方案已授权对高概率免疫性 TTP 紧急进行治疗性血浆置换和糖皮质激素治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的情况"},"tokens":[{"id":"q5c5","en":"Typical hemolytic uremic syndrome","zh":"典型溶血尿毒综合征"},{"id":"q5c1","en":"Immune thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura","zh":"免疫性血栓性血小板减少性紫癜"},{"id":"q5c3","en":"Disseminated intravascular coagulation","zh":"弥散性血管内凝血"},{"id":"q5c4","en":"Immune thrombocytopenia","zh":"免疫性血小板减少症"},{"id":"q5c2","en":"Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia","zh":"肝素诱导的血小板减少症"}],"correct":"q5c1"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Immediate actions","zh":"立即措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"q5a1","en":"Obtain the ADAMTS13 sample now before TPE or any plasma-containing blood product","zh":"立即在 TPE 或任何含血浆血液制品前采集 ADAMTS13 标本"},{"id":"q5a4","en":"Treat with routine platelet transfusion alone","zh":"仅常规输注血小板治疗"},{"id":"q5a2","en":"Begin the authorized urgent TPE and corticosteroid pathway now without waiting for the result","zh":"不等待结果，立即启动已授权的紧急 TPE 和糖皮质激素路径"},{"id":"q5a3","en":"Wait until all five historical pentad findings are present","zh":"等待传统五联征全部出现"}],"correct":["q5a1","q5a2"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"q5p3","en":"Prothrombin time alone","zh":"仅凝血酶原时间"},{"id":"q5p4","en":"Remote heparin-exposure history","zh":"远期肝素暴露史"},{"id":"q5p1","en":"Platelet count and hemolysis markers including LDH, bilirubin, and smear trend","zh":"血小板计数及 LDH、胆红素和血涂片趋势等溶血指标"},{"id":"q5p2","en":"Neurologic, renal, cardiac, and hemodynamic status","zh":"神经、肾脏、心脏和血流动力学状态"}],"correct":["q5p1","q5p2"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe thrombocytopenia plus microangiopathic hemolytic anemia, schistocytes, normal coagulation tests, and neurologic change strongly support immune TTP. The historical pentad is not required. Obtain the ADAMTS13 sample immediately before plasma-containing treatment because it is feasible without delay, then begin the authorized urgent TPE/corticosteroid pathway without waiting for the result. Platelet and hemolysis trends, together with neurologic, renal, and perfusion status, track response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重度血小板减少、微血管病性溶血性贫血、裂红细胞、凝血试验正常及神经系统改变，强烈支持免疫性 TTP。无需具备传统五联征。由于可在不延误治疗的情况下完成，应在含血浆治疗前立即采集 ADAMTS13 标本，然后不等待结果，立即启动已授权的紧急 TPE/糖皮质激素路径。血小板和溶血趋势，以及神经、肾脏和灌注状态可追踪反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize MAHA plus thrombocytopenia. Normal coagulation tests and no heparin exposure move the answer away from DIC and HIT; do not wait for the pentad.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别微血管病性溶血加血小板减少。凝血试验正常且无肝素暴露，使答案远离 DIC 和 HIT；不要等待五联征。","sourceMetadata":"ISTH, Guidelines for the diagnosis of TTP (2020), Recommendation 1 steps 1–4: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8146131/; and Guidelines for treatment of TTP, first acute iTTP recommendation: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8091490/. The 2025 focused update reports no change to the acquired-iTTP recommendations: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40533296/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2226,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11a_acute_aortic_syndrome_cues","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.756","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.756.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.756.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[350,396],"terminalOffsetsZh":[94,107],"fullStemEn":"A client presents with chest and back pain. The emergency department uses the ACC/AHA acute-aortic-syndrome high-risk history and examination features to determine whether urgent aortic imaging and specialist evaluation are required. Highlight only the findings in the note that raise concern for acute aortic syndrome or branch-vessel malperfusion. Do not select ordinary hypertension by itself.","fullStemZh":"一名患者因胸背痛就诊。急诊科使用 ACC/AHA 急性主动脉综合征高风险病史和体格检查特征，判断是否需要紧急主动脉影像及专科评估。仅标出记录中提示急性主动脉综合征或分支血管灌注不良的发现。不要仅因普通高血压而选择。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not select ordinary hypertension by itself.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要仅因普通高血压而选择。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings in the note that raise concern for acute aortic syndrome or branch-vessel malperfusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"仅标出记录中提示急性主动脉综合征或分支血管灌注不良的发现。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Emergency note:","zh":"急诊记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"The pain began abruptly while the client was sitting and was maximal at onset, extending from the anterior chest into the interscapular back.","zh":"患者坐位时疼痛突然发生，起始即最剧烈，并从前胸延伸至肩胛间背部。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The right radial pulse is newly weaker than the left; systolic pressure is 178 mm Hg in the left arm and 142 mm Hg in the right arm.","zh":"右侧桡动脉脉搏新出现比左侧弱；左上肢收缩压 178 mm Hg，右上肢 142 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"During the pain episode, the client develops new left-arm weakness and expressive aphasia.","zh":"疼痛发作期间，患者新出现左上肢无力和表达性失语。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"A new early diastolic murmur is heard along the left sternal border, and blood pressure falls to 82/46 mm Hg.","zh":"左胸骨缘可听到新发早期舒张期杂音，血压降至 82/46 mm Hg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"The history lists hypertension treated for 12 years, with no recent change in the regimen.","zh":"病史记录高血压已治疗 12 年，近期方案无变化。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"A small area of left costochondral tenderness reproduces a minor portion of the discomfort.","zh":"左侧肋软骨有一小处压痛，可重现部分轻微不适。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"The client appears mildly anxious while awaiting testing.","zh":"患者等待检查时看起来轻度焦虑。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abrupt maximal-at-onset chest-to-back pain, a new pulse and systolic-pressure differential, a focal neurologic deficit, and a new diastolic murmur with hypotension are ACC/AHA high-risk features for acute aortic syndrome or malperfusion. Chronic hypertension is a risk factor but is not the discriminating examination cluster requested. Reproducible chest-wall tenderness and mild anxiety are nonspecific near-misses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"突发且起始即最剧烈的胸痛向背部放射、新出现脉搏及收缩压差异、局灶神经功能缺损，以及新发舒张期杂音伴低血压，均为 ACC/AHA 所列急性主动脉综合征或灌注不良高风险特征。慢性高血压是风险因素，但不是本题要求的鉴别性检查组合。可重复胸壁压痛和轻度焦虑是非特异性近似项。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the high-risk cluster, not every cardiovascular risk factor. Onset pattern, pulse or pressure asymmetry, malperfusion, and a new aortic-regurgitation finding carry the signal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择高风险线索组合，而不是所有心血管风险因素。起病模式、脉搏或血压不对称、灌注不良及新发主动脉返流所见才是关键信号。","sourceMetadata":"2022 ACC/AHA Guideline for the Diagnosis and Management of Aortic Disease, acute-aortic-syndrome presentation/high-risk examination features and diagnostic-evaluation sections: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9860464/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2227,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11b_rutherford_iib_limb_threat","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.757","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.757.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.757.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,274],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,84],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic peripheral artery disease develops sudden worsening left-leg symptoms. Highlight only the findings that establish an immediately threatened limb classified as Rutherford IIb. Use the supplied vascular assessment; do not infer the class from pain alone.","fullStemZh":"一名患有慢性外周动脉疾病的患者突然出现左腿症状加重。仅标出可确定为 Rutherford IIb 级立即受威胁肢体的发现。使用题干提供的血管评估；不要仅凭疼痛推断分级。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the supplied vascular assessment; do not infer the class from pain alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"使用题干提供的血管评估；不要仅凭疼痛推断分级。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings that establish an immediately threatened limb classified as Rutherford IIb.","penultimateSentenceZh":"仅标出可确定为 Rutherford IIb 级立即受威胁肢体的发现。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Left-leg vascular assessment:","zh":"左腿血管评估："},{"id":"s1","en":"Pinprick and light-touch sensation are newly absent across the forefoot and extend to the midfoot, not just the toes.","zh":"针刺和轻触觉在前足新出现缺失，并延伸至中足，而不只限于足趾。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"The client can move the ankle and toes but has new mild-to-moderate weakness against resistance.","zh":"患者仍能活动踝部和足趾，但对抗阻力时新出现轻至中度无力。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"No arterial Doppler signal is audible at the dorsalis pedis or posterior tibial artery.","zh":"足背动脉和胫后动脉均听不到动脉多普勒信号。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"A venous Doppler signal remains audible at the ankle.","zh":"踝部静脉多普勒信号仍可听到。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"For 2 years, walking three blocks has caused calf aching that resolves with rest.","zh":"过去 2 年，步行三个街区会引起小腿酸痛，休息后缓解。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The lower leg has longstanding shiny skin with sparse hair.","zh":"小腿长期皮肤光亮、毛发稀少。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"A weak left pedal pulse was documented at the last clinic visit 4 months ago.","zh":"4 个月前门诊已记录左足动脉搏动减弱。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Rutherford IIb is defined by sensory loss extending beyond the toes, a mild-to-moderate motor deficit, an inaudible arterial Doppler signal, and a still-audible venous Doppler signal. Chronic claudication, shiny hairless skin, and a longstanding weak pedal pulse describe baseline PAD but do not establish the acute IIb category.","rationaleCorrectZh":"Rutherford IIb 的特征是感觉缺失超过足趾范围、轻至中度运动缺损、动脉多普勒信号听不到，而静脉多普勒信号仍可听到。慢性间歇性跛行、皮肤光亮少毛及长期足背动脉搏动减弱描述基线 PAD，但不能确定急性 IIb 分级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the complete viability pattern: sensory, motor, arterial Doppler, and venous Doppler. Chronic PAD findings are background, not the acute class.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用完整肢体存活模式：感觉、运动、动脉多普勒和静脉多普勒。慢性 PAD 所见只是背景，不是急性分级。","sourceMetadata":"ESVS, 2020 Clinical Practice Guidelines on Acute Limb Ischaemia, clinical presentation and Rutherford limb-viability classification: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31899099/ and open guideline PDF https://solaci.org/_files/2020-02-06-10-1016-j-ejvs-2019-09-006.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2228,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11b_retinal_detachment_emergency_cues","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.758","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.758.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.758.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[205,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,83],"fullStemEn":"An adult calls an eye clinic about new visual symptoms. Highlight only the findings that require urgent retinal evaluation for possible retinal tear or detachment under the National Eye Institute pathway. Stable longstanding findings are included as near-misses.","fullStemZh":"一名成人致电眼科门诊咨询新出现的视觉症状。仅标出依据美国国家眼科研究所路径需要紧急视网膜评估、可能提示视网膜裂孔或脱离的发现。记录中包含稳定的长期表现作为近似干扰项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stable longstanding findings are included as near-misses.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录中包含稳定的长期表现作为近似干扰项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings that require urgent retinal evaluation for possible retinal tear or detachment under the National Eye Institute pathway.","penultimateSentenceZh":"仅标出依据美国国家眼科研究所路径需要紧急视网膜评估、可能提示视网膜裂孔或脱离的发现。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Telephone note:","zh":"电话记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"Bright flashes began suddenly in the left peripheral vision this morning.","zh":"今天早晨左侧周边视野突然出现明亮闪光。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Within an hour, the client noticed a shower of many new dark floaters.","zh":"一小时内，患者注意到大量新发暗色飞蚊，像阵雨一样。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"A gray curtain now seems to move inward from the temporal side.","zh":"现在感觉灰色帘幕从颞侧向中央移动。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"The client cannot see objects in part of the outer visual field.","zh":"患者看不到外侧视野一部分的物体。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"These new symptoms started the day after a ball struck the eye.","zh":"这些新症状在眼睛被球击中后的第二天开始。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Two small floaters have been unchanged for 5 years.","zh":"两个小飞蚊已 5 年无变化。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Nighttime glare has gradually increased over 10 months.","zh":"夜间眩光在 10 个月内逐渐加重。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sudden flashes, a rapid increase in floaters, a curtain or shadow, and new peripheral field loss are classic retinal-detachment warning symptoms. A new cluster after blunt trauma also requires urgent assessment. Stable unchanged floaters and gradual cataract-like glare are not the acute posterior-retinal pattern.","rationaleCorrectZh":"突然闪光、飞蚊迅速增多、帘幕或阴影感，以及新出现周边视野缺损，是典型视网膜脱离警示症状。钝性外伤后出现的新症状组合也需要紧急评估。长期稳定不变的飞蚊和逐渐出现的白内障样眩光不属于急性后段视网膜模式。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for sudden posterior-visual change: flashes, many new floaters, a curtain or shadow, and field loss. Chronic stable symptoms do not belong in the urgent set.","testTakingStrategyZh":"寻找突发后段视觉变化：闪光、大量新飞蚊、帘幕或阴影及视野缺损。慢性稳定症状不属于紧急集合。","sourceMetadata":"National Eye Institute, Retinal Detachment, “Symptoms” and immediate-care passages: https://www.nei.nih.gov/eye-health-information/eye-conditions-and-diseases/retinal-detachment","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings that require urgent retinal evaluation for possible retinal tear or detachment under the National Eye Institute pathway.","controlSentenceZh":"仅标出依据美国国家眼科研究所路径需要紧急视网膜评估、可能提示视网膜裂孔或脱离的发现。"}
{"queueIndex":2229,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11b_giant_cell_arteritis_cues","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.759","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.759.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.759.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,298],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,80],"fullStemEn":"An older adult reports a new headache and visual symptoms. Highlight only the findings that require urgent same-day escalation for suspected giant cell arteritis with cranial ischemia under the named guideline. Do not diagnose from an inflammatory marker alone or wait for biopsy before escalation.","fullStemZh":"一名老年患者报告新发头痛和视觉症状。仅标出依据指定指南需要因疑似伴颅脑缺血的巨细胞动脉炎而当日紧急升级处理的发现。不要仅凭炎症指标诊断，也不要等待活检后才升级。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not diagnose from an inflammatory marker alone or wait for biopsy before escalation.","terminalSentenceZh":"不要仅凭炎症指标诊断，也不要等待活检后才升级。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Highlight only the findings that require urgent same-day escalation for suspected giant cell arteritis with cranial ischemia under the named guideline.","penultimateSentenceZh":"仅标出依据指定指南需要因疑似伴颅脑缺血的巨细胞动脉炎而当日紧急升级处理的发现。","responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s0","en":"Same-day clinic note:","zh":"当日门诊记录："},{"id":"s1","en":"A new focal left-temporal headache began 4 days ago.","zh":"4 天前开始新发局灶性左颞部头痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Brushing the hair causes marked tenderness over the left scalp and temporal artery.","zh":"梳头时左侧头皮和颞动脉区域明显压痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Chewing meat causes new jaw pain and fatigue that resolves when chewing stops.","zh":"咀嚼肉类时新出现下颌疼痛和疲劳，停止咀嚼后缓解。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Yesterday the left eye became dark for 3 minutes and then recovered.","zh":"昨天左眼视野变黑约 3 分钟后恢复。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"ESR and CRP are elevated and the platelet count is 520 ×10³/µL.","zh":"ESR 和 CRP 升高，血小板计数 520 ×10³/µL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The client has had the same visual-aura migraine pattern since age 30, with no change in frequency or features.","zh":"患者自 30 岁起一直有相同的视觉先兆偏头痛模式，频率和特征均无变化。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Mild nasal congestion began after seasonal pollen exposure.","zh":"季节性花粉暴露后出现轻度鼻塞。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A new localized temporal headache, scalp tenderness, jaw claudication, and transient monocular visual loss are high-risk cranial-ischemia features of giant cell arteritis. Elevated inflammatory markers and thrombocytosis strengthen the compatible context but are not diagnostic alone. A longstanding unchanged migraine pattern and mild isolated sinus congestion are near-misses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新发局限性颞部头痛、头皮压痛、咀嚼性下颌跛行及短暂单眼视力丧失，是巨细胞动脉炎颅脑缺血的高风险特征。炎症指标升高和血小板增多可加强相符背景，但不能单独诊断。长期不变的偏头痛模式和轻度孤立鼻窦充血是近似干扰项。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the ischemic symptom cluster, then use laboratory inflammation as support. Do not let an ESR value replace the history and examination.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先选择缺血症状组合，再用炎症实验室结果支持。不要让 ESR 数值取代病史和体格检查。","sourceMetadata":"ACR/Vasculitis Foundation, 2021 Guideline for Management of Giant Cell Arteritis, cranial-ischemia/visual-manifestation definitions and treatment recommendations: https://www.vasculitisfoundation.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/2021-ACR-VF-Guideline-for-Management-of-Giant-Cell-Arteritis-and-Takayasu-Artheritis.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2230,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11b_cockcroft_gault_crcl","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.760","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.760.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.760.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[447,530],"terminalOffsetsZh":[179,213],"fullStemEn":"A 68-year-old female client has a stable serum creatinine of 1.1 mg/dL. The supplied dosing weight for this calculation is 62 kg; use this weight without making another body-size judgment. Use the Cockcroft–Gault equation: creatinine clearance = [(140 − age) × weight in kg] ÷ (72 × serum creatinine in mg/dL), then multiply by the female coefficient 0.85. Calculate estimated creatinine clearance in mL/min and round to the nearest whole number. This is not indexed eGFR and does not by itself select or adjust a medication dose.","fullStemZh":"一名 68 岁女性患者血清肌酐稳定为 1.1 mg/dL。本题提供的计算用体重为 62 kg；直接使用该体重，不需要另行判断体型。使用 Cockcroft–Gault 公式：肌酐清除率 = [（140 − 年龄）× 体重 kg] ÷（72 × 血清肌酐 mg/dL），女性再乘系数 0.85。计算估算肌酐清除率，单位 mL/min，并四舍五入至最接近的整数。该结果不是按体表面积校正的 eGFR，也不能单独决定或调整药物剂量。","terminalSentenceEn":"This is not indexed eGFR and does not by itself select or adjust a medication dose.","terminalSentenceZh":"该结果不是按体表面积校正的 eGFR，也不能单独决定或调整药物剂量。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate estimated creatinine clearance in mL/min and round to the nearest whole number.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算估算肌酐清除率，单位 mL/min，并四舍五入至最接近的整数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"estimated creatinine clearance (mL/min)","zh":"估算肌酐清除率（mL/min）"},"acceptable":["48","48 mL/min","48 mL/minute"],"numeric":{"value":48,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL/min"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CrCl = [(140−68)×62] ÷ (72×1.1) × 0.85 = 4464 ÷ 79.2 × 0.85 = 47.91 mL/min, which rounds to 48 mL/min. The calculation uses the supplied dosing weight and the female coefficient exactly as stated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CrCl = [（140−68）×62] ÷（72×1.1）×0.85 = 4464 ÷ 79.2 ×0.85 = 47.91 mL/min，四舍五入为 48 mL/min。计算严格使用题干提供的给药体重和女性系数。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the equation in order and apply the sex coefficient after the main quotient. Round only once at the end.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按公式顺序计算，在主商值后再乘性别系数。仅在最后一次四舍五入。","sourceMetadata":"National Kidney Foundation, Cockcroft-Gault Equation for Estimating Creatinine Clearance, equation and medication-dosing context: https://www.kidney.org/professionals/kdoqi/cockcroft-gault-equation-estimating-creatinine-clearance","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2231,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11b_pediatric_oxygenation_index","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.761","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.761.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.761.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[251,368],"terminalOffsetsZh":[121,155],"fullStemEn":"An invasively ventilated child has a mean airway pressure of 18 cm H2O, FiO2 of 0.60, and arterial PaO2 of 72 mm Hg. Use oxygenation index: OI = mean airway pressure × FiO2 × 100 ÷ PaO2. Calculate the oxygenation index and round to the nearest tenth. This item tests arithmetic only; do not diagnose pediatric ARDS or change ventilator settings from this number alone.","fullStemZh":"一名接受有创机械通气的儿童平均气道压为 18 cm H2O，FiO2 为 0.60，动脉 PaO2 为 72 mm Hg。使用氧合指数公式：OI = 平均气道压 × FiO2 × 100 ÷ PaO2。计算氧合指数，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。本题仅测试计算；不能仅凭该数值诊断儿童 ARDS 或调整呼吸机设置。","terminalSentenceEn":"This item tests arithmetic only; do not diagnose pediatric ARDS or change ventilator settings from this number alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题仅测试计算；不能仅凭该数值诊断儿童 ARDS 或调整呼吸机设置。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the oxygenation index and round to the nearest tenth.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算氧合指数，并四舍五入到小数点后一位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"oxygenation index","zh":"氧合指数"},"acceptable":["15","15.0","OI 15","OI 15.0"],"numeric":{"value":15,"tolerance":0,"unit":"OI"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"OI = 18 × 0.60 × 100 ÷ 72 = 1080 ÷ 72 = 15.0. The supplied FiO2 is already a decimal, so it is not converted to 60 before the equation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"OI = 18 × 0.60 × 100 ÷ 72 = 1080 ÷ 72 = 15.0。题干中的 FiO2 已是小数，因此代入公式前不能再转换为 60。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use FiO2 as the supplied decimal. The formula already contains ×100, so do not convert 0.60 into 60 first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按题干给出的小数使用 FiO2。公式已包含 ×100，因此不要先把 0.60 转为 60。","sourceMetadata":"PALICC-2, Executive Summary of the Second International Guidelines for PARDS, definition table and oxygenation-index equation: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9848214/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":true,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2232,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11b_ankle_brachial_index","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.762","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.762.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.762.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[397,478],"terminalOffsetsZh":[138,159],"fullStemEn":"For the right leg, brachial systolic pressures are 132 mm Hg on the left and 128 mm Hg on the right. Right dorsalis-pedis pressure is 116 mm Hg and right posterior-tibial pressure is 124 mm Hg. Use the AHA convention: ABI for the leg = the higher ankle pressure for that leg ÷ the higher brachial pressure from either arm. Calculate the right ankle–brachial index and round to two decimal places. Do not diagnose vascular disease or prescribe compression from this number alone.","fullStemZh":"右腿检查中，左臂收缩压 132 mm Hg，右臂收缩压 128 mm Hg。右侧足背动脉压 116 mm Hg，右侧胫后动脉压 124 mm Hg。使用 AHA 约定：该腿 ABI = 该腿较高的踝部压力 ÷ 两侧上臂中较高的压力。计算右侧踝肱指数，并四舍五入到小数点后两位。不能仅凭该数值诊断血管疾病或决定加压治疗。","terminalSentenceEn":"Do not diagnose vascular disease or prescribe compression from this number alone.","terminalSentenceZh":"不能仅凭该数值诊断血管疾病或决定加压治疗。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the right ankle–brachial index and round to two decimal places.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算右侧踝肱指数，并四舍五入到小数点后两位。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"right ankle–brachial index","zh":"右侧踝肱指数"},"acceptable":["0.94","ABI 0.94"],"numeric":{"value":0.94,"tolerance":0,"unit":"ABI"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Use the higher right ankle pressure, 124 mm Hg, and the higher brachial pressure, 132 mm Hg. ABI = 124 ÷ 132 = 0.93939..., which rounds to 0.94.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用右踝较高压力 124 mm Hg，以及较高上臂压力 132 mm Hg。ABI = 124 ÷ 132 = 0.93939...，四舍五入为 0.94。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the higher value within each required pair before dividing. Do not average either the ankle or brachial pressures.","testTakingStrategyZh":"相除前先在每一对所需压力中选择较高值。不要对踝压或肱压取平均。","sourceMetadata":"AHA scientific statement, Measurement and Interpretation of the Ankle-Brachial Index, standardized higher-ankle/higher-brachial calculation convention: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23159553/; open summary of the exact calculation: https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2013/1215/p866.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Calculate the right ankle–brachial index and round to two decimal places.","controlSentenceZh":"计算右侧踝肱指数，并四舍五入到小数点后两位。"}
{"queueIndex":2233,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11c_avulsed_permanent_tooth_first_aid","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.763","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Toddler Safety","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.763.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.763.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[433,470],"terminalOffsetsZh":[106,118],"fullStemEn":"A 10-year-old child falls and completely avulses an upper permanent incisor. The child is conscious, cooperative, and has no facial injury or aspiration risk that would make immediate replantation unsafe. The tooth is intact and only lightly contaminated. In this closed branch, prompt replantation is appropriate and will be performed; storage is used only when replantation cannot be done. A primary tooth must never be replanted. Place the first-aid actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名 10 岁儿童跌倒后，上颌一颗恒切牙完全脱位。儿童清醒、配合，无使立即再植不安全的面部损伤或误吸风险。牙齿完整，仅轻度污染。在本题限定分支中，适合并将实施及时再植；只有无法再植时才使用保存液。乳牙绝不能再植。请将急救措施按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the first-aid actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将急救措施按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A primary tooth must never be replanted.","penultimateSentenceZh":"乳牙绝不能再植。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Confirm that the avulsed tooth is a permanent tooth rather than a primary tooth.","zh":"确认脱落的是恒牙而不是乳牙。"},{"id":"B","en":"Pick up the tooth by the crown only and avoid touching the root.","zh":"只握住牙冠拿起牙齿，避免触碰牙根。"},{"id":"D","en":"Reinsert the tooth promptly into the socket in the correct orientation without forcing it.","zh":"按正确方向迅速将牙齿放回牙槽，不要强行推入。"},{"id":"E","en":"Have the child bite gently on clean gauze to hold the replanted tooth in place.","zh":"让儿童轻咬干净纱布，以固定已再植的牙齿。"},{"id":"F","en":"Obtain immediate dental care for definitive stabilization and follow-up.","zh":"立即就诊牙科，进行确定性固定和随访。"},{"id":"C","en":"If the tooth is contaminated, rinse it briefly and gently without scrubbing, scraping, or drying the root.","zh":"若牙齿受污染，短暂轻柔冲洗，不要刷洗、刮擦或弄干牙根。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First confirm that the tooth is permanent. Pick it up only by the crown, not the root. If contaminated, rinse it briefly and gently without scrubbing or drying the root. Because this branch explicitly permits replantation, replace the tooth promptly in the correct orientation, have the child bite gently on gauze to stabilize it, and obtain immediate dental care. When replantation is not possible, the alternative branch is prompt placement in an approved storage medium while seeking dental care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先确认脱落的是恒牙。只能握住牙冠，不能触碰牙根。如有污染，应短暂轻柔冲洗，不要刷洗或弄干牙根。由于本题分支明确允许再植，应按正确方向迅速将牙齿放回牙槽，让儿童轻咬纱布固定，并立即就诊牙科。若无法再植，则应改走备用分支：迅速放入认可的保存液并寻求牙科处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the tissue-protection sequence: identify the tooth, protect the root, clean gently, replant in the eligible branch, stabilize, and obtain immediate dental care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遵循组织保护顺序：确认牙齿、保护牙根、轻柔清洗、在符合条件的分支中再植、固定并立即就诊牙科。","sourceMetadata":"IADT 2020, Guidelines for the Management of Traumatic Dental Injuries: Avulsion of Permanent Teeth, first-aid/replantation/storage pathway: https://www.aapd.org/media/policies_guidelines/e_avulsion.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2234,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11c_clean_catch_midstream_urine","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.764","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.764.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.764.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[248,288],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,74],"fullStemEn":"The nurse teaches an adult to collect a clean-catch midstream urine specimen using the facility's supplied sex-specific cleansing kit. The labeled specimen must be delivered to the laboratory promptly under the stated facility timing instructions. Place the six supplied actions in order.","fullStemZh":"护士指导一名成人使用机构提供的性别特异性清洁用品采集清洁中段尿标本。已标记的标本必须按机构规定的时间要求迅速送至实验室。请将所给六项操作按顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the six supplied actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将所给六项操作按顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The labeled specimen must be delivered to the laboratory promptly under the stated facility timing instructions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"已标记的标本必须按机构规定的时间要求迅速送至实验室。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Move the container into the established urine stream and collect the midstream specimen without touching the inside of the container or lid.","zh":"将容器移入已建立的尿流中采集中段尿，不触碰容器或盖子内部。"},{"id":"E","en":"Remove the container from the stream and finish voiding into the toilet.","zh":"将容器移出尿流，并在马桶中排完尿液。"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform hand hygiene and prepare the labeled specimen container and cleansing supplies.","zh":"进行手卫生，并准备已标记的标本容器和清洁用品。"},{"id":"C","en":"Begin voiding into the toilet.","zh":"开始向马桶排尿。"},{"id":"F","en":"Cap the container securely, complete the labeling, and route it according to the facility's stated timing instructions.","zh":"牢固盖紧容器、完成标签，并按机构规定的时间要求送检。"},{"id":"B","en":"Cleanse using the supplied sex-specific procedure without touching the container interior.","zh":"按提供的性别特异性程序清洁，不触碰容器内部。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Prepare first with hand hygiene and the labeled container. Cleanse using the supplied procedure without contaminating the container. Begin urinating into the toilet, move the container into the stream to collect the midstream specimen, then finish voiding into the toilet. Finally cap the container securely, complete labeling, and route it promptly according to the facility timing instructions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先洗手并准备已标记的容器。按提供的程序清洁，避免污染容器。先向马桶开始排尿，再把容器移入尿流中采集中段尿，然后在马桶中排完。最后牢固盖紧容器、完成标签，并按机构时间要求迅速送检。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the meaning of midstream: prepare and clean, start in the toilet, collect from the established stream, finish in the toilet, then secure and route the specimen.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据“中段尿”的含义排序：准备和清洁，先排入马桶，从已建立的尿流采集，再排完，最后封好并送检。","sourceMetadata":"MedlinePlus, Clean catch urine sample, adult preparation and midstream-collection procedure: https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/007487.htm","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2235,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11c_home_peak_flow_technique","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.765","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.765.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.765.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[153,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,71],"fullStemEn":"A client is measuring peak expiratory flow at home while standing upright, as specified in the personal action plan. Place the technique steps in order. The task is to obtain the best of three attempts; do not choose a treatment zone or medication.","fullStemZh":"一名患者按照个人行动计划要求，以直立站姿在家测量呼气峰流量。请将操作步骤按顺序排列。本题目标是取得三次尝试中的最高值；不要选择治疗分区或药物。","terminalSentenceEn":"The task is to obtain the best of three attempts; do not choose a treatment zone or medication.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题目标是取得三次尝试中的最高值；不要选择治疗分区或药物。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Place the technique steps in order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"请将操作步骤按顺序排列。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Record the highest of the three readings in the personal action plan rather than calculating an average.","zh":"在个人行动计划中记录三次读数的最高值，而不是计算平均值。"},{"id":"A","en":"Inspect the meter and reset the marker to the bottom of the scale.","zh":"检查峰流量计，并将指示器重置到刻度底端。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stand upright in the position specified by the action plan.","zh":"按行动计划规定保持直立站姿。"},{"id":"E","en":"Read and record the value, reset the marker, and repeat the maneuver until three attempts are completed.","zh":"读取并记录数值，重置指示器，并重复操作直至完成三次尝试。"},{"id":"C","en":"Take the deepest breath possible before placing the mouthpiece.","zh":"在含住咬嘴前尽可能深吸气。"},{"id":"D","en":"Seal the lips tightly around the mouthpiece and blow once as hard and fast as possible.","zh":"嘴唇紧闭含住咬嘴，一次尽可能用力、快速吹气。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Inspect the meter and reset the marker to the bottom of the scale. Stand upright, then inhale fully. Seal the lips around the mouthpiece and blow once as hard and fast as possible. Read and record the value, reset the marker, and repeat until three attempts are completed. Record the highest value, not the average, in the action plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"先检查峰流量计并将指示器重置到刻度底端。直立站好，然后充分吸气。嘴唇紧闭含住咬嘴，一次尽可能用力、快速吹气。读取并记录数值，重置指示器，重复直至完成三次。把最高值而不是平均值记录在行动计划中。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Think of one complete maneuver, then repeat it. The final documentation rule is best of three, not average of three.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先完成一次完整操作，再重复。最终记录规则是三次取最高值，而不是三次平均。","sourceMetadata":"American Lung Association, Measuring Your Peak Flow Rate, Steps 1–8 and three-attempt/highest-reading instruction: https://www.lung.org/lung-health-diseases/lung-disease-lookup/asthma/treatment/devices/peak-flow","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2236,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11c_adrenal_laboratory_localization","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.766","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.766.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.766.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[367,525],"terminalOffsetsZh":[147,204],"fullStemEn":"Interpret three separately labeled, stable endocrine records. Each dropdown refers only to its own client. Record A: Client A has paired 0800 cortisol 2.0 µg/dL and ACTH 186 pg/mL, obtained before treatment. Record B: Client B has potassium 5.8 mEq/L, elevated plasma renin activity, and aldosterone 2 ng/dL; do not use this record to localize adrenal insufficiency. Record C: Client C used prednisone daily for 8 months and stopped abruptly 1 week ago; morning cortisol and ACTH are both low, with no pituitary mass history.","fullStemZh":"解释三份分别标记、情况稳定的内分泌记录。每个下拉框只对应自己的患者。记录 A：患者 A 在治疗前同时测得 0800 皮质醇 2.0 µg/dL、ACTH 186 pg/mL。记录 B：患者 B 血钾 5.8 mEq/L、血浆肾素活性升高、醛固酮 2 ng/dL；不要用该记录定位肾上腺功能不全。记录 C：患者 C 连续 8 个月每天使用泼尼松，1 周前突然停药；晨间皮质醇和 ACTH 均低，无垂体肿块病史。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record C: Client C used prednisone daily for 8 months and stopped abruptly 1 week ago; morning cortisol and ACTH are both low, with no pituitary mass history.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录 C：患者 C 连续 8 个月每天使用泼尼松，1 周前突然停药；晨间皮质醇和 ACTH 均低，无垂体肿块病史。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Record B: Client B has potassium 5.8 mEq/L, elevated plasma renin activity, and aldosterone 2 ng/dL; do not use this record to localize adrenal insufficiency.","penultimateSentenceZh":"记录 B：患者 B 血钾 5.8 mEq/L、血浆肾素活性升高、醛固酮 2 ng/dL；不要用该记录定位肾上腺功能不全。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Record A localizes to {{1}}. In Record B, the aldosterone response is {{2}} for the supplied potassium and renin context. Record C is most consistent with {{3}}.","zh":"记录 A 定位为{{1}}。在记录 B 中，针对题干所给血钾和肾素背景，醛固酮反应为{{2}}。记录 C 最符合{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"central adrenal insufficiency","zh":"中枢性肾上腺功能不全"},{"id":"o1","en":"primary adrenal insufficiency","zh":"原发性肾上腺功能不全"},{"id":"o3","en":"normal hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal localization","zh":"下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺定位正常"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"appropriately preserved","zh":"适当保留"},{"id":"o1","en":"inappropriately low","zh":"不适当偏低"},{"id":"o3","en":"uninterpretable because ACTH was not supplied","zh":"因未提供 ACTH 而无法解释"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"autoimmune adrenal disease","zh":"自身免疫性肾上腺疾病"},{"id":"o3","en":"pituitary disease","zh":"垂体疾病"},{"id":"o1","en":"chronic exogenous-glucocorticoid suppression","zh":"长期外源性糖皮质激素抑制"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Record A shows low cortisol with markedly elevated ACTH, localizing the defect to primary adrenal insufficiency rather than central suppression. In Record B, hyperkalemia and high renin should stimulate aldosterone, so a low aldosterone value is inappropriately low for the physiologic context. Record C most strongly fits chronic exogenous-glucocorticoid suppression of the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, not autoimmune adrenal destruction or a pituitary lesion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"记录 A 显示皮质醇低而 ACTH 显著升高，定位为原发性肾上腺功能不全，而不是中枢性抑制。记录 B 中，高钾和高肾素应刺激醛固酮，因此低醛固酮对于该生理背景属于不适当偏低。记录 C 最符合长期外源性糖皮质激素对下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴的抑制，而不是自身免疫性肾上腺破坏或垂体病变。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Keep the records separate. ACTH localizes the cortisol defect in A, renin and potassium establish aldosterone appropriateness in B, and medication history identifies etiology in C.","testTakingStrategyZh":"保持三份记录彼此独立。A 用 ACTH 定位皮质醇缺陷，B 用肾素和血钾判断醛固酮是否适当，C 用用药史确定病因。","sourceMetadata":"Endotext, Diagnosis and Management of Adrenal Insufficiency, primary-versus-central AI ACTH/mineralocorticoid distinctions and diagnostic tables: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK279122/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2237,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11c_microcytic_anemia_localization","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.767","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.767.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.767.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[279,422],"terminalOffsetsZh":[162,201],"fullStemEn":"Interpret three bounded laboratory records. Record A: hemoglobin 9.4 g/dL, MCV 70 fL, ferritin 7 ng/mL, TIBC 472 µg/dL, transferrin saturation 5%, and CRP normal. Record B: hemoglobin 11.2 g/dL, MCV 65 fL, RBC count 6.1 million/mm³, ferritin 92 ng/mL, CRP normal, and HbA2 5.3%. Record C asks for the next diagnostic step to confirm the pattern in Record B; do not treat the screening pattern as a final genetic diagnosis.","fullStemZh":"解释三项限定实验室记录。记录 A：血红蛋白 9.4 g/dL，MCV 70 fL，铁蛋白 7 ng/mL，TIBC 472 µg/dL，转铁蛋白饱和度 5%，CRP 正常。记录 B：血红蛋白 11.2 g/dL，MCV 65 fL，红细胞计数 610 万/mm³，铁蛋白 92 ng/mL，CRP 正常，HbA2 5.3%。记录 C 要求为记录 B 选择下一步确认路径；不要把筛查模式当作最终遗传诊断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record C asks for the next diagnostic step to confirm the pattern in Record B; do not treat the screening pattern as a final genetic diagnosis.","terminalSentenceZh":"记录 C 要求为记录 B 选择下一步确认路径；不要把筛查模式当作最终遗传诊断。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Record B: hemoglobin 11.2 g/dL, MCV 65 fL, RBC count 6.1 million/mm³, ferritin 92 ng/mL, CRP normal, and HbA2 5.3%.","penultimateSentenceZh":"记录 B：血红蛋白 11.2 g/dL，MCV 65 fL，红细胞计数 610 万/mm³，铁蛋白 92 ng/mL，CRP 正常，HbA2 5.3%。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Record A is most consistent with {{1}}. Record B supports a screening pattern of {{2}}. When definitive confirmation of Record B is required, the next diagnostic step is {{3}}.","zh":"记录 A 最符合{{1}}。记录 B 支持{{2}}的筛查模式。记录 B 需要确定性确认时，下一路径是{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"anemia of chronic inflammation","zh":"慢性炎症性贫血"},{"id":"o3","en":"thalassemia trait","zh":"地中海贫血携带状态"},{"id":"o1","en":"iron-deficiency anemia","zh":"缺铁性贫血"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"beta-thalassemia trait","zh":"β 地中海贫血携带状态"},{"id":"o2","en":"iron-deficiency anemia","zh":"缺铁性贫血"},{"id":"o3","en":"anemia of chronic inflammation","zh":"慢性炎症性贫血"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"empiric iron replacement without further evaluation","zh":"不再评估，直接经验性补铁"},{"id":"o1","en":"confirmatory hemoglobinopathy evaluation with molecular testing and genetic counseling as appropriate","zh":"按需要进行确认性血红蛋白病评估、分子检测和遗传咨询"},{"id":"o3","en":"no further testing because the screening pattern is already a final genetic diagnosis","zh":"无需进一步检测，因为筛查模式已是最终遗传诊断"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Record A has depleted iron stores, high binding capacity, and very low transferrin saturation without an inflammatory confounder, supporting iron-deficiency anemia. Record B has marked microcytosis with a relatively high RBC count, preserved ferritin, and elevated HbA2, supporting a beta-thalassemia-trait screening pattern rather than iron deficiency or anemia of chronic inflammation. When definitive confirmation is needed, the next step is a hemoglobinopathy evaluation with confirmatory molecular testing and genetic counseling as appropriate, not empiric iron or a final genetic label from the screen alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"记录 A 显示铁储备耗竭、结合能力升高及转铁蛋白饱和度极低，且无炎症干扰，支持缺铁性贫血。记录 B 显示明显小细胞性改变、红细胞计数相对较高、铁蛋白保留及 HbA2 升高，支持 β 地中海贫血携带者筛查模式，而不是缺铁或慢性炎症性贫血。需要确定性确认时，下一路径是血红蛋白病评估，并按需要进行确认性分子检测和遗传咨询，而不是经验性补铁或仅凭筛查直接作最终遗传诊断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate iron-store interpretation from hemoglobinopathy pattern recognition. Ferritin must be read with inflammation, while RBC count and HbA2 point toward hemoglobinopathy evaluation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把铁储备解释与血红蛋白病模式识别分开。铁蛋白必须结合炎症判断，而红细胞计数和 HbA2 指向另一条路径。","sourceMetadata":"ARUP Consult, Iron Deficiency Anemia, “Ferritin/Iron and Iron Binding Capacity” and HbA2/RBC-count differential sections, plus the linked IDA-versus-ACD algorithm: https://arupconsult.com/content/iron-deficiency-anemia","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2238,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_format11c_water_deprivation_desmopressin_interpretation","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.768","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.768.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.768.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[592,664],"terminalOffsetsZh":[216,232],"fullStemEn":"In a monitored endocrine unit, a stable client with hypotonic polyuria undergoes a supervised water-deprivation test with protocol stop criteria and serial laboratory monitoring. Baseline serum sodium is 143 mEq/L, plasma osmolality is 292 mOsm/kg, and urine osmolality is 82 mOsm/kg. During deprivation, urine osmolality remains 86–94 mOsm/kg without meaningful concentration; serum sodium rises to 147 mEq/L and plasma osmolality to 304 mOsm/kg, and the test is stopped at the protocol weight-loss limit. After supervised desmopressin administration, urine osmolality rises to 612 mOsm/kg. Partial and indeterminate response patterns are excluded from this item.","fullStemZh":"在内分泌监护病区，一名情况稳定、存在低渗性多尿的患者接受有停止标准和连续实验室监测的监督性禁水试验。基线血钠 143 mEq/L，血浆渗透压 292 mOsm/kg，尿渗透压 82 mOsm/kg。禁水期间尿渗透压保持在 86–94 mOsm/kg，无有意义浓缩；血钠升至 147 mEq/L、血浆渗透压升至 304 mOsm/kg，并在达到方案体重下降上限时停止试验。监督下给予去氨加压素后，尿渗透压升至 612 mOsm/kg。本题排除部分性和不确定反应模式。","terminalSentenceEn":"Partial and indeterminate response patterns are excluded from this item.","terminalSentenceZh":"本题排除部分性和不确定反应模式。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After supervised desmopressin administration, urine osmolality rises to 612 mOsm/kg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"监督下给予去氨加压素后，尿渗透压升至 612 mOsm/kg。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"During water deprivation, the urine shows {{1}}. The desmopressin response is most consistent with {{2}}. The corresponding serum-sodium safety concern is {{3}}.","zh":"禁水期间，尿液表现为{{1}}。去氨加压素反应最符合{{2}}。相应的血钠安全担忧是{{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"an absent concentration response","zh":"浓缩反应缺失"},{"id":"o2","en":"a preserved concentration response","zh":"浓缩反应保留"},{"id":"o3","en":"an indeterminate partial response","zh":"不确定的部分反应"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"complete central diabetes insipidus","zh":"完全性中枢性尿崩症"},{"id":"o2","en":"complete nephrogenic diabetes insipidus","zh":"完全性肾性尿崩症"},{"id":"o3","en":"primary polydipsia","zh":"原发性多饮"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"no sodium risk because urine output is hypotonic","zh":"因尿液低渗而无血钠风险"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypernatremia with worsening hyperosmolality","zh":"高钠血症并伴高渗状态加重"},{"id":"o2","en":"dilutional hyponatremia","zh":"稀释性低钠血症"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The urine fails to concentrate during water deprivation despite rising plasma tonicity, showing an absent concentration response rather than the preserved response expected in primary polydipsia. The large rise from less than 100 to 612 mOsm/kg after desmopressin is a complete central diabetes-insipidus pattern, indicating renal responsiveness to administered vasopressin analog. Because free-water loss is present and serum sodium is already high-normal to elevated, hypernatremia and worsening hyperosmolality are the corresponding safety concerns.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管血浆张力升高，禁水期间尿液仍不能浓缩，说明浓缩反应缺失，而不是原发性多饮中预期的保留反应。去氨加压素后尿渗透压从低于 100 大幅升至 612 mOsm/kg，属于完全性中枢性尿崩症模式，说明肾脏可对外源性加压素类似物作出反应。由于存在自由水丢失，且血钠已在高正常至升高范围，相应安全担忧是高钠血症及高渗状态加重。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Interpret the test in two stages: first ask whether deprivation concentrates urine, then ask whether desmopressin restores concentration. Match the sodium concern to free-water loss.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分两阶段解释：先判断禁水能否使尿液浓缩，再判断去氨加压素能否恢复浓缩。根据自由水丢失匹配血钠风险。","sourceMetadata":"Endotext, Diagnostic Tests for Diabetes Insipidus, water-deprivation and desmopressin-response interpretation, complete central versus nephrogenic DI passages: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK537591/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2239,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_case","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.769","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.769.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.769.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,72],"fullStemEn":"Serial Fetal Assessment During Labor Induction A term client receiving oxytocin induction is monitored with continuous CTG. Use the staged maternal, labor, uterine, and fetal data to judge changes over time.","fullStemZh":"引产期间的连续胎儿评估 一名足月产妇正在接受缩宫素引产并持续进行胎心宫缩监护。请利用分阶段呈现的产妇、产程、宫缩和胎儿资料判断随时间发生的变化。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the staged maternal, labor, uterine, and fetal data to judge changes over time.","terminalSentenceZh":"请利用分阶段呈现的产妇、产程、宫缩和胎儿资料判断随时间发生的变化。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Serial Fetal Assessment During Labor Induction A term client receiving oxytocin induction is monitored with continuous CTG.","penultimateSentenceZh":"引产期间的连续胎儿评估 一名足月产妇正在接受缩宫素引产并持续进行胎心宫缩监护。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Interpret each fetal heart rate finding within the maternal condition, labor progress, uterine activity, prior hourly comparison, and response to intervention. A single CTG label is not a substitute for the whole clinical picture.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应结合产妇状况、产程进展、宫缩活动、上一小时的比较以及干预后的反应来解释每项胎心发现。单一的胎心监护分类不能替代对整体临床情况的判断。","testTakingStrategyEn":"At each stage, first identify what is new, then compare it with the exact prior time point and decide whether the evidence supports observation, review, or escalation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在每个阶段，先找出新出现的信息，再与明确的上一时间点进行比较，判断证据支持继续观察、复核还是升级处理。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, Fetal monitoring in labour, recommendations 1.2.1–1.2.3, 1.3.5–1.3.8, 1.4.1–1.4.33, 1.5.2–1.5.6, 1.5.12, and 1.6.1–1.6.2, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2240,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_part_1_baseline","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,85],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Based on the 09:00 assessment, how should the nurse categorize the current CTG trace?","fullStemZh":"根据09:00的评估，护士应如何对当前胎心宫缩监护图形进行分类？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the 09:00 assessment, how should the nurse categorize the current CTG trace?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据09:00的评估，护士应如何对当前胎心宫缩监护图形进行分类？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"c","en":"Suspicious, because accelerations are present","zh":"可疑，因为可见胎心加速"},{"id":"d","en":"Pathological, because the cervix is only 4 cm dilated","zh":"病理性，因为宫颈仅扩张4 cm"},{"id":"a","en":"Normal, because contractions, baseline rate, variability, and decelerations are all in the white range","zh":"正常，因为宫缩、胎心率基线、变异及减速这4项特征均属于白色范围"},{"id":"b","en":"Suspicious, because the client is receiving oxytocin","zh":"可疑，因为产妇正在接受缩宫素输注"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At 09:00, contractions are fewer than 5 in 10 minutes, the stable baseline is 135/min, variability is 10 beats/min, and there are no decelerations. All four CTG features are white, so the trace is normal. Oxytocin is an intrapartum risk factor that supports continued CTG, but it does not itself make the trace suspicious.","rationaleCorrectZh":"09:00时，每10分钟宫缩少于5次，胎心率基线稳定在135次/分，变异幅度10次/分，且无减速。4项胎心监护特征均为白色，因此图形属于正常。缩宫素是支持持续监护的产时危险因素，但其本身不会使图形被归为可疑。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate CTG feature categorization from the reasons a client needs continuous monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将胎心监护特征分类与需要持续监护的原因区分开来。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, recommendations 1.3.8, 1.4.12, 1.4.15, 1.4.18, 1.4.24, 1.4.30–1.4.32, and 1.5.4, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2241,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_part_2_escalation_cues","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"highlight","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,161],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,44],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings from the 10:00 review that contribute to current concern and should be included when requesting urgent senior-midwife or obstetric review.","fullStemZh":"请标出10:00复核中构成当前担忧、并应在请求高级助产士或产科医生紧急复核时报告的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings from the 10:00 review that contribute to current concern and should be included when requesting urgent senior-midwife or obstetric review.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出10:00复核中构成当前担忧、并应在请求高级助产士或产科医生紧急复核时报告的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"The fetal baseline is 155/min, 20 beats/min higher than the documented baseline exactly 1 hour earlier.","zh":"胎心率基线为155次/分，比整整1小时前记录的基线上升20次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Thick meconium is present in the amniotic fluid.","zh":"羊水中可见浓稠胎粪。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"The oxytocin infusion remains in use.","zh":"缩宫素仍在输注。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Maternal pulse is 88/min.","zh":"产妇脉搏为88次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Contractions occur 4 times in 10 minutes with normal resting tone.","zh":"每10分钟宫缩4次，宫缩间歇期张力正常。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"The cervix has changed from 4 cm to 5 cm dilation.","zh":"宫颈扩张由4 cm进展至5 cm。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The 20-beat/min rise from the documented review exactly 1 hour earlier is an amber baseline feature, making the CTG suspicious when the other features remain white. Thick meconium is an additional intrapartum risk factor, so urgent senior-midwife or obstetric review is required. Ongoing oxytocin use is also an intrapartum risk factor that belongs in the whole-picture review. The stable maternal pulse, four contractions in 10 minutes with normal resting tone, and cervical progress do not independently add concern here.","rationaleCorrectZh":"与整整1小时前记录的复核相比，胎心率基线上升20次/分，属于琥珀色基线特征；当其余特征仍为白色时，整体图形归为可疑。浓稠胎粪是额外的产时危险因素，因此需要高级助产士或产科医生紧急复核。持续使用缩宫素也是应纳入整体评估的产时危险因素。产妇脉搏稳定、每10分钟宫缩4次且间歇期张力正常，以及宫颈进展，在此并不会单独增加担忧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a value remains within an absolute range, check whether the guideline also defines a concerning change from the exact prior review.","testTakingStrategyZh":"即使某数值仍在绝对范围内，也要检查指南是否将其相对于明确上一复核时间点的变化定义为异常。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, recommendations 1.3.5–1.3.8, 1.4.1, 1.4.10, 1.4.15, 1.4.31–1.4.33, and 1.5.6, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2242,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_part_3_stimulation_purpose","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Which statement best explains why finger-performed fetal scalp stimulation is appropriate to consider at 10:08?","fullStemZh":"以下哪项最能解释为什么在10:08可以考虑进行指法胎儿头皮刺激？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement best explains why finger-performed fetal scalp stimulation is appropriate to consider at 10:08?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项最能解释为什么在10:08可以考虑进行指法胎儿头皮刺激？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"c","en":"The maneuver can replace the urgent senior-midwife or obstetric review","zh":"该操作可以替代高级助产士或产科医生的紧急复核"},{"id":"a","en":"The CTG is suspicious and intrapartum risk factors for fetal compromise are present after the required bedside review","zh":"完成所需床旁复核后，胎心监护图形可疑且存在胎儿受损的产时危险因素"},{"id":"b","en":"The CTG is normal, so stimulation is routinely required before continuing labor","zh":"胎心监护图形正常，因此在继续产程前常规需要进行刺激"},{"id":"d","en":"The maneuver will remove thick meconium from the amniotic fluid","zh":"该操作能够清除羊水中的浓稠胎粪"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"NICE recommends considering digital fetal scalp stimulation when the CTG is suspicious and antenatal or intrapartum risk factors for fetal compromise are present. The required senior-midwife or obstetric review has already occurred before the maneuver. Fetal scalp stimulation is not routine for a normal trace, does not replace review, and does not treat meconium.","rationaleCorrectZh":"NICE建议在胎心监护图形可疑且存在胎儿受损的产前或产时危险因素时，考虑指法胎儿头皮刺激。进行该操作前，所需的高级助产士或产科医生复核已经完成。胎儿头皮刺激并非正常图形下的常规操作，不能替代复核，也不能治疗胎粪。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match a bedside maneuver to the exact guideline-defined clinical context, including any review that must occur first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将床旁操作与指南明确规定的临床情境相匹配，并确认必须先完成的复核。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, recommendations 1.5.6 and 1.6.1–1.6.2, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2243,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_part_4_immediate_response","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,71],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,14],"fullStemEn":"Complete the interpretation of the immediate fetal heart rate response.","fullStemZh":"完成对胎心率即刻反应的解释。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the interpretation of the immediate fetal heart rate response.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成对胎心率即刻反应的解释。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The response is {{dd1}}; the team should {{dd2}} before making a final disposition.","zh":"该反应属于{{dd1}}；在作出最终处置决定前，团队应{{dd2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"dd1","options":[{"id":"c","en":"evidence that the tracing is maternal pulse artifact","zh":"图形为产妇脉搏伪差的证据"},{"id":"b","en":"definitive proof of fetal acidemia","zh":"胎儿酸血症的确证"},{"id":"a","en":"reassuring evidence that current fetal compromise is less likely","zh":"提示当前胎儿受损可能性较低的令人放心证据"}],"correct":"a"},{"id":"dd2","options":[{"id":"a","en":"continue CTG and assess whether the improvement is sustained","zh":"继续胎心宫缩监护并评估改善是否持续"},{"id":"c","en":"proceed to expedited birth without reassessment","zh":"不再评估，直接准备加快分娩"},{"id":"b","en":"stop CTG immediately because the test is complete","zh":"因检查已完成而立即停止胎心监护"}],"correct":"a"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The fetal heart rate rises by 20 beats/min for 20 seconds, meeting the definition of an acceleration. An acceleration after fetal scalp stimulation is reassuring, but it is not definitive proof that all risk has resolved. Continued CTG is needed to determine whether improvement is sustained within the whole clinical picture.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胎心率上升20次/分并持续20秒，符合胎心加速的定义。胎儿头皮刺激后出现加速是令人放心的表现，但不能确证所有风险均已解除。仍需持续进行胎心宫缩监护，以结合整体临床情况判断改善是否持续。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Treat a reassuring response as evidence that modifies probability, not as proof that ends surveillance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把令人放心的反应视为改变风险可能性的证据，而不是可以终止监护的确证。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, recommendations 1.4.30 and 1.6.1, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2244,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_c_part_5_closing_plan","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Intrapartum Fetal Monitoring","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.769.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,97],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,32],"fullStemEn":"Which actions should be included in the plan after the 10:30 reassessment? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"10:30再评估后，护理计划中应包括哪些措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should be included in the plan after the 10:30 reassessment?","penultimateSentenceZh":"10:30再评估后，护理计划中应包括哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"b","en":"Repeat and document a full maternal-fetal risk assessment at least hourly","zh":"至少每小时重复并记录一次完整的母胎风险评估"},{"id":"e","en":"Administer maternal oxygen by face mask despite an oxygen saturation of 99% on room air","zh":"尽管室内空气下血氧饱和度为99%，仍给予产妇面罩吸氧"},{"id":"c","en":"Arrange an in-person fresh-eyes review by another clinician before the next hourly assessment","zh":"在下一次每小时评估前安排另一名临床人员进行床旁“新视角”复核"},{"id":"a","en":"Continue continuous CTG and monitor the maternal-fetal clinical picture","zh":"继续持续胎心宫缩监护并监测母胎整体临床情况"},{"id":"f","en":"Prepare immediate expedited birth solely because meconium remains present despite sustained CTG improvement","zh":"仅因胎粪仍然存在，即使胎心监护持续改善也立即准备加快分娩"},{"id":"d","en":"Discontinue CTG because the senior-midwife and obstetric review at 10:08 already assessed the fetal status","zh":"因10:08已由高级助产士和产科医生完成评估而停止胎心监护"}],"correct":["a","b","c"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The acceleration after stimulation is followed by sustained improvement, so continued CTG and monitoring of the clinical picture are appropriate. Meconium remains an intrapartum risk factor, and the client is still in labor; full risk assessment must continue at least hourly, with a fresh-eyes review before the next assessment. The record does not support stopping CTG, routine oxygen in a nonhypoxic client, or immediate expedited birth solely for persistent meconium after sustained improvement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"刺激后出现胎心加速，随后监护显示持续改善，因此应继续胎心宫缩监护并观察整体临床情况。胎粪仍是产时危险因素，且产妇仍处于产程中；必须至少每小时继续进行完整风险评估，并在下一次评估前由另一名临床人员进行“新视角”复核。本病历不支持停止胎心监护、不支持在产妇无低氧时常规吸氧，也不支持仅因胎粪持续存在而在监护已持续改善时立即加快分娩。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose a closing plan that matches the strongest defensible conclusion: improvement supports surveillance, while persistent risk factors prevent premature de-escalation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择与证据所能支持的最强结论相符的后续计划：改善支持继续监护，而持续存在的危险因素不允许过早降级。","sourceMetadata":"NICE NG229, recommendations 1.3.5–1.3.8, 1.5.2–1.5.6, 1.5.12, and 1.6.1, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng229/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2245,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_case","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.770","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.770.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.770.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,33],"fullStemEn":"Acute asthma in the emergency department An adult with asthma undergoes repeated assessment and treatment during an acute exacerbation.","fullStemZh":"急诊科急性哮喘 一名成人哮喘患者在急性加重期间接受连续评估和治疗。","terminalSentenceEn":"Acute asthma in the emergency department An adult with asthma undergoes repeated assessment and treatment during an acute exacerbation.","terminalSentenceZh":"急诊科急性哮喘 一名成人哮喘患者在急性加重期间接受连续评估和治疗。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires the learner to connect objective airflow limitation, serial arterial blood gases, bedside fatigue, treatment safety, and reassessment context without treating any single number as the whole clinical picture.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求学习者综合客观气流受限、连续动脉血气、床旁疲劳表现、治疗安全性和复评背景，而不能把任何单一数值当作完整临床结论。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track what changed, whether support conditions stayed comparable, and whether the client is still able to sustain ventilation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"追踪发生了什么变化、支持条件是否具有可比性，以及患者是否仍能维持通气。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, Chapter 9 acute-care exacerbation assessment, treatment, arterial blood gases, adjunctive therapies, and reassessment, pp. 170 and 185–189, https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2246,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_part_1_abg_indication","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"Which baseline finding independently matches GINA's stated reason to consider arterial blood gas measurement during an asthma exacerbation?","fullStemZh":"哪项基线发现本身符合GINA所述在哮喘急性加重期间考虑进行动脉血气测量的理由？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which baseline finding independently matches GINA's stated reason to consider arterial blood gas measurement during an asthma exacerbation?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项基线发现本身符合GINA所述在哮喘急性加重期间考虑进行动脉血气测量的理由？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Diffuse expiratory wheezes are audible while bilateral air entry remains present.","zh":"双肺可闻及弥漫性呼气性哮鸣音，但双侧仍有空气进入。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client has a known diagnosis of asthma.","zh":"患者已知患有哮喘。"},{"id":"B","en":"Respiratory rate is 30/min.","zh":"呼吸频率为30次/分。"},{"id":"A","en":"Peak expiratory flow is 44% predicted.","zh":"呼气峰流量为预计值的44%。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"GINA states that ABG measurement should be considered when PEF or FEV₁ is below 50% predicted, when the client does not respond to initial treatment, or when the client is deteriorating. The documented PEF of 44% predicted meets the explicit lung-function criterion. Tachypnea, wheeze, and an asthma history require clinical assessment but are not the stated ABG criterion by themselves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"GINA指出，当PEF或FEV₁低于预计值的50%、患者对初始治疗无反应，或病情正在恶化时，应考虑动脉血气测量。记录的PEF为预计值的44%，符合明确的肺功能标准。呼吸急促、哮鸣音和哮喘病史都需要临床评估，但单独并不是该动脉血气标准。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a question cites a published criterion, match the exact denominator and comparison operator: below 50% predicted, not personal best.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当题目引用公开标准时，应精确匹配分母和比较符号：低于预计值的50%，而不是个人最佳值。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, p. 185, arterial blood gas measurement criteria (PEF or FEV1 <50% predicted, nonresponse, or deterioration), https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2247,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_part_2_initial_abg","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,39],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,13],"fullStemEn":"Interpret the 09:25 arterial blood gas.","fullStemZh":"解释09:25的动脉血气。","terminalSentenceEn":"Interpret the 09:25 arterial blood gas.","terminalSentenceZh":"解释09:25的动脉血气。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The primary acid-base disturbance is {{dd1}}.","zh":"主要酸碱紊乱为{{dd1}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"dd1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"acute respiratory acidosis","zh":"急性呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"o4","en":"metabolic alkalosis","zh":"代谢性碱中毒"},{"id":"o1","en":"acute respiratory alkalosis","zh":"急性呼吸性碱中毒"},{"id":"o3","en":"metabolic acidosis","zh":"代谢性酸中毒"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pH is alkalemic at 7.50 and PaCO₂ is low at 28 mm Hg, identifying a primary acute respiratory alkalosis. The low PaCO₂ is consistent with the hyperventilation commonly seen earlier in an asthma exacerbation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"pH 7.50提示碱血症，PaCO₂ 28 mm Hg偏低，表明主要为急性呼吸性碱中毒。低PaCO₂与哮喘急性加重早期常见的过度通气一致。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Start with pH, then identify whether PaCO₂ or bicarbonate moves in the direction that explains the pH.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断pH，再确定PaCO₂或碳酸氢根中哪一项的变化方向能够解释pH。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, p. 185, PaCO2 is often below normal during an asthma exacerbation, https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2248,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_part_3_ventilation_shift","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,78],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"Which physiologic interpretation best explains the change from 09:25 to 09:45?","fullStemZh":"哪项生理学解释最能说明09:25至09:45之间的变化？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which physiologic interpretation best explains the change from 09:25 to 09:45?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项生理学解释最能说明09:25至09:45之间的变化？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The rise in PaCO₂ from 28 to 47 mm Hg, together with shallower breathing, shorter speech, drowsiness, falling PEF, and worsening hypoxemia, indicates loss of effective ventilation from fatigue and respiratory failure.","zh":"PaCO₂从28升至47 mm Hg，并伴呼吸变浅、说话更短、嗜睡、PEF下降和低氧恶化，提示因疲劳而失去有效通气并出现呼吸衰竭。"},{"id":"A","en":"The PaCO₂ moving into the normal range shows that bronchospasm is resolving, despite increasing drowsiness.","zh":"尽管嗜睡加重，PaCO₂回到正常范围说明支气管痉挛正在缓解。"},{"id":"D","en":"The PaO₂ decrease is best explained by excessive oxygen administration because oxygen support was unchanged.","zh":"由于氧支持未改变，PaO₂下降最可能由给氧过多引起。"},{"id":"C","en":"The falling pH with a nearly unchanged bicarbonate level proves a primary metabolic acidosis caused by corticosteroid therapy.","zh":"pH下降且碳酸氢根几乎不变，证明糖皮质激素治疗导致原发性代谢性酸中毒。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In acute asthma, PaCO₂ is often low while the client can sustain hyperventilation. The rise from 28 to 47 mm Hg under unchanged support, together with acidemia, PaO₂ 58 mm Hg, fatigue, somnolence, shallower breathing, worsening speech, and falling PEF, shows loss of effective alveolar ventilation. The serial pattern—not the PaCO₂ endpoint alone—supports respiratory failure and the need for urgent airway intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在急性哮喘中，当患者仍能维持过度通气时，PaCO₂常偏低。在支持条件未变时，PaCO₂从28升至47 mm Hg，并伴酸血症、PaO₂ 58 mm Hg、疲劳、嗜睡、呼吸变浅、说话能力恶化和PEF下降，说明有效肺泡通气正在丧失。支持呼吸衰竭和紧急气道干预需要的是连续变化模式，而不是单独的PaCO₂终点。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not call a number reassuring because it enters the reference range. Interpret the trajectory together with work of breathing, speech, alertness, and PEF.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因为某个数值进入参考范围就认为它令人放心。应把趋势与呼吸功、说话能力、清醒程度和PEF结合解释。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, p. 185, fatigue/somnolence with increasing PaCO2 and respiratory-failure criteria; p. 189, deterioration despite intensive treatment prompts ICU re-evaluation, https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2249,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_part_4_order_safety","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,26],"fullStemEn":"Which proposed medication orders should the nurse clarify before implementation? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士在执行前应澄清哪些拟议用药医嘱？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which proposed medication orders should the nurse clarify before implementation?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在执行前应澄清哪些拟议用药医嘱？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer the prescribed systemic corticosteroid.","zh":"给予医嘱开具的全身性糖皮质激素。"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer a sedative for distress while the client remains non-intubated.","zh":"在患者仍未插管时，为缓解不适给予镇静药。"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer prescribed intravenous magnesium for the severe exacerbation with inadequate initial response and persistent hypoxemia.","zh":"针对初始治疗反应不足且持续低氧的重度急性加重，按医嘱给予静脉硫酸镁。"},{"id":"D","en":"Start an intravenous aminophylline infusion as an add-on bronchodilator.","zh":"开始静脉氨茶碱输注，作为附加支气管扩张治疗。"},{"id":"A","en":"Continue prescribed repeated inhaled short-acting bronchodilator plus ipratropium.","zh":"继续按医嘱重复吸入短效支气管扩张剂联合异丙托溴铵。"},{"id":"F","en":"Start a routine antibiotic solely for the asthma exacerbation despite no evidence of lung infection.","zh":"尽管无肺部感染证据，仅因哮喘急性加重而常规开始抗生素治疗。"}],"correct":["D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"GINA advises against intravenous aminophylline/theophylline because of poor efficacy and safety, states that sedatives must be avoided because of respiratory depression and preventable deaths, and does not support routine antibiotics without strong evidence of lung infection. Repeated inhaled SABA plus ipratropium and systemic corticosteroids are components of severe-exacerbation treatment. Intravenous magnesium may be considered after inadequate initial response with persistent hypoxemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"GINA因氨茶碱/茶碱疗效差且安全性不佳而不建议静脉使用；由于镇静药可抑制呼吸并与可避免的死亡相关，明确要求避免使用；在没有强烈肺部感染证据时，也不支持常规使用抗生素。重复吸入SABA联合异丙托溴铵和全身性糖皮质激素属于重度急性加重治疗组成部分。初始治疗反应不足并持续低氧时，可考虑静脉硫酸镁。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate supported adjuncts used for a defined severe-response problem from drugs that are routinely unsupported or can suppress ventilation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分针对明确重症反应问题使用的有依据辅助治疗，与常规无依据或可能抑制通气的药物。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, pp. 185 and 188–189, concurrent acute-care therapy, intravenous magnesium criteria, nonroutine antibiotics, aminophylline/theophylline not recommended, and sedatives must be avoided, https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2250,"bankPath":"banks/gpt-canonical.json","bankSha256":"61664a6bef854ec8d7a3a0113779a4773135724aabfdec65b970b7ac6464c5d2","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_case","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_casepilot_2026_07_19_d_part_5_support_limited_reassessment","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"ABG & Acid-Base Interpretation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.770.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,167],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,55],"fullStemEn":"At 10:15, which serial comparisons can support a treatment-response conclusion without overstating what the changed support conditions prove? Classify each comparison.","fullStemZh":"在10:15，哪些连续比较可用于支持治疗反应结论，而不会夸大支持条件变化所能证明的内容？请对每项比较进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each comparison.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项比较进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 10:15, which serial comparisons can support a treatment-response conclusion without overstating what the changed support conditions prove?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在10:15，哪些连续比较可用于支持治疗反应结论，而不会夸大支持条件变化所能证明的内容？","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"PaCO₂ and pH from 09:45 and 10:15, interpreted together with alertness, speech, and respiratory depth; no positive-pressure ventilation was used at either time.","zh":"将09:45与10:15的PaCO₂和pH结合清醒程度、说话能力及呼吸深度解释；两个时间点均未使用正压通气。"},{"id":"r2","en":"PEF from 09:45 and 10:15, measured as percent predicted with the same meter and technique, together with bilateral air entry.","zh":"将09:45与10:15的PEF（均以预计值百分比表示，并使用同一仪器和同样方法测量）结合双侧空气进入进行比较。"},{"id":"r3","en":"PaO₂ and SpO₂ from 09:45 and 10:15, when oxygen delivery was increased before the later measurements.","zh":"比较09:45与10:15的PaO₂和SpO₂，但在后一次测量前已提高给氧支持。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Can support a response conclusion","zh":"可支持治疗反应结论"},{"id":"c2","en":"Cannot by itself support a response conclusion","zh":"单独不能支持治疗反应结论"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The PaCO₂/pH trend can be interpreted with the improved bedside findings because no positive-pressure ventilation changed the ventilation comparison. The PEF trend is also comparable because the predicted denominator, meter, and technique were unchanged. The higher PaO₂ and SpO₂ cannot by themselves establish improved underlying oxygen transfer because oxygen delivery was increased before the final measurements.","rationaleCorrectZh":"由于没有正压通气改变通气比较，PaCO₂/pH趋势可结合改善的床旁表现进行解释。PEF趋势也具有可比性，因为预计值分母、仪器和测量方法均未改变。较高的PaO₂和SpO₂本身不能证明基础氧转移改善，因为最终测量前已提高给氧支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A better oxygenation number under more oxygen is not a clean before-and-after comparison. Use unchanged-support measures and bedside findings for stronger causal conclusions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在增加给氧后获得更好的氧合数值，并不是干净的前后比较。应使用支持条件未变的指标和床旁表现来得出更可靠的因果结论。","sourceMetadata":"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA), Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2026, pp. 185 and 189, controlled oxygen context, frequent reassessment, lung-function measurement, and deterioration/response review, https://ginasthma.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GINA-2026-Strategy-Report-WMS.pdf; Respiratory Therapy Zone, ABG Oxygenation Interpretation: PaO2, SaO2, and Hypoxemia (corrected hypoxemia under supplemental oxygen does not represent true normalization of gas exchange), https://www.respiratorytherapyzone.com/abg-oxygenation-interpretation/","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2251,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_sepsis_pneumonia_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,54],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: suspected sepsis with pneumonia A 68-kg older adult arrives from home with fever, cough, worsening confusion, and signs of poor perfusion.","fullStemZh":"展开式病例：疑似肺炎相关脓毒症 一名体重68千克的老年患者因发热、咳嗽、意识混乱加重及低灌注表现从家中来诊。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: suspected sepsis with pneumonia A 68-kg older adult arrives from home with fever, cough, worsening confusion, and signs of poor perfusion.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开式病例：疑似肺炎相关脓毒症 一名体重68千克的老年患者因发热、咳嗽、意识混乱加重及低灌注表现从家中来诊。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires recognizing sepsis with hypoperfusion, initiating time-sensitive infection treatment, calculating the initial crystalloid bolus, and evaluating response without continuing fluids blindly.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求识别伴低灌注的脓毒症，启动有时效性的感染治疗，计算初始晶体液复苏量，并在评估反应后避免盲目继续补液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding sepsis cases, separate infection cues from perfusion cues, then prioritize time-sensitive actions that restore perfusion and start antimicrobials.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到展开式脓毒症病例时，先区分感染线索和灌注线索，再优先执行能恢复灌注并启动抗菌治疗的限时措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2252,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_sepsis_pneumonia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"sepsis_pneumonia_cues_matrix","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,79],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"For each assessment finding, select the interpretation that best fits the case.","fullStemZh":"针对每项评估发现，选择最符合本病例的解释。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, select the interpretation that best fits the case.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项评估发现，选择最符合本病例的解释。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Right lower-lobe infiltrate with productive cough","zh":"右下肺叶浸润影并伴咳脓痰"},{"id":"r2","en":"Lactate 4.6 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸4.6 mmol/L"},{"id":"r3","en":"Cool mottled skin and capillary refill 5 seconds","zh":"皮肤发凉、花斑样改变，毛细血管再充盈5秒"},{"id":"r4","en":"Home use of metformin","zh":"居家使用二甲双胍"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Background finding","zh":"背景资料"},{"id":"c1","en":"Infection cue","zh":"感染线索"},{"id":"c2","en":"Hypoperfusion cue","zh":"低灌注线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The infiltrate and productive cough point to a likely pulmonary infection source. Elevated lactate, mottling, and delayed capillary refill point to impaired tissue perfusion. Metformin is relevant history but is not the primary sepsis cue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"浸润影和咳脓痰提示可能的肺部感染来源。乳酸升高、花斑样皮肤和毛细血管再充盈延迟提示组织灌注受损。二甲双胍是相关病史，但不是本病例的主要脓毒症线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In cue-recognition items, label each detail by what it proves: source of infection, perfusion status, or background risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做识别线索题时，按每个细节能证明什么来分类：感染来源、灌注状态或背景风险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2253,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_sepsis_pneumonia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"sepsis_pneumonia_actions_order","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Place the nursing actions in the order that best supports initial sepsis management.","fullStemZh":"将护理措施按最有利于初始脓毒症处理的顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the order that best supports initial sepsis management.","terminalSentenceZh":"将护理措施按最有利于初始脓毒症处理的顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Obtain ordered blood cultures and repeat lactate without delaying treatment.","zh":"按医嘱采集血培养并复查乳酸，同时不延误治疗。"},{"id":"E","en":"Reassess perfusion and prepare vasopressor support if MAP remains low after fluids.","zh":"重新评估灌注；若补液后平均动脉压仍低，准备血管加压药支持。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the prescribed initial crystalloid bolus.","zh":"给予医嘱的初始晶体液快速补液。"},{"id":"A","en":"Activate the sepsis response and notify the provider of hypotension and elevated lactate.","zh":"启动脓毒症反应，并通知医护团队患者低血压和乳酸升高。"},{"id":"C","en":"Start prescribed broad-spectrum antibiotics.","zh":"开始执行医嘱给予广谱抗生素。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should escalate recognition first, collect cultures and lactate promptly, start antibiotics, administer the initial crystalloid bolus, then reassess perfusion and support blood pressure if shock persists.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应先升级识别病情，及时采集培养和复查乳酸，随后开始抗生素，给予初始晶体液复苏，最后重新评估灌注；若休克持续，则支持血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several actions are urgent, choose the sequence that recognizes shock, obtains time-sensitive data, starts definitive treatment, and then evaluates response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个措施都很紧急时，选择能先识别休克、取得时效性资料、开始关键治疗并随后评估反应的顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2254,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_sepsis_pneumonia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"sepsis_pneumonia_fluid_calc","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"IV Fluid Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[154,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[46,52],"fullStemEn":"The client weighs 68 kg. The prescription is lactated Ringer's 30 mL/kg IV for initial resuscitation. How many mL should the nurse prepare to administer? Enter the number only.","fullStemZh":"患者体重68千克。医嘱为乳酸林格液30 mL/kg静脉用于初始复苏。护士应准备给予多少毫升？只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the number only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse prepare to administer?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应准备给予多少毫升？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Initial crystalloid bolus","zh":"初始晶体液快速补液量"},"acceptable":["2040","2040 mL"],"numeric":{"value":2040,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Multiply 68 kg by 30 mL/kg: 68 x 30 = 2,040 mL. This is the prescribed initial bolus amount, followed by reassessment rather than automatic continued fluids.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用68 kg乘以30 mL/kg：68 x 30 = 2,040 mL。这是医嘱的初始快速补液量，之后应重新评估，而不是自动继续补液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For weight-based fluids, cancel kg and carry the mL unit through the calculation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"进行按体重计算的补液量时，约去kg单位，并在计算中保留mL单位。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2255,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_sepsis_pneumonia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"sepsis_pneumonia_outcomes_cloze","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,67],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"Use the 1000 update to evaluate the client's response to treatment.","fullStemZh":"根据10:00更新评估患者对治疗的反应。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the 1000 update to evaluate the client's response to treatment.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据10:00更新评估患者对治疗的反应。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The finding that best supports improving perfusion is {{1}}. The finding that still requires close follow-up is {{2}}.","zh":"最能支持灌注改善的发现是 {{1}}。仍需密切随访的发现是 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"blood cultures are pending","zh":"血培养结果待回报"},{"id":"o1","en":"lactate decreased from 4.6 to 3.1 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸从4.6降至3.1 mmol/L"},{"id":"o3","en":"the client takes lisinopril at home","zh":"患者居家服用赖诺普利"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"MAP 69 mm Hg on norepinephrine","zh":"使用去甲肾上腺素时平均动脉压69 mm Hg"},{"id":"o1","en":"urine output of 20 mL in the past hour","zh":"过去1小时尿量20 mL"},{"id":"o3","en":"heart rate decreased to 104/min","zh":"心率降至104次/分"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A falling lactate supports improving tissue perfusion. Urine output of only 20 mL in an hour remains concerning and requires ongoing perfusion and renal assessment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乳酸下降支持组织灌注改善。1小时尿量仅20 mL仍令人担忧，需要继续评估灌注和肾功能。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In outcome questions, choose trends that show organ perfusion improving, then look for any organ system that is still underperforming.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做结果评估题时，先选择显示器官灌注改善的趋势，再寻找仍表现不佳的器官系统。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2256,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_preeclampsia_magnesium_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,47],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: preeclampsia with severe features A 35-week pregnant client presents with severe hypertension, neurologic symptoms, and abnormal laboratory values.","fullStemZh":"展开式病例：伴重度特征的子痫前期 一名妊娠35周孕妇出现重度高血压、神经系统症状和实验室异常。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: preeclampsia with severe features A 35-week pregnant client presents with severe hypertension, neurologic symptoms, and abnormal laboratory values.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开式病例：伴重度特征的子痫前期 一名妊娠35周孕妇出现重度高血压、神经系统症状和实验室异常。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires recognizing severe features of preeclampsia, stabilizing the client with seizure precautions and magnesium sulfate, and then responding quickly to magnesium toxicity cues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求识别子痫前期重度特征，采取防惊厥措施并使用硫酸镁稳定病情，随后迅速处理硫酸镁中毒线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In obstetric emergencies, identify the maternal threat first. Stabilize the client before focusing on delivery timing or fetal follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到产科急症时，先识别母体威胁。先稳定孕产妇，再考虑分娩时机或胎儿后续处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2257,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_preeclampsia_magnesium_01","embeddedQuestionId":"preeclampsia_severe_features_sata","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[58,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[17,26],"fullStemEn":"Which findings support preeclampsia with severe features? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些发现支持伴重度特征的子痫前期？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings support preeclampsia with severe features?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现支持伴重度特征的子痫前期？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Blood pressure 166/112 mm Hg","zh":"血压166/112 mm Hg"},{"id":"B","en":"Severe headache unrelieved by acetaminophen","zh":"严重头痛，对乙酰氨基酚后不缓解"},{"id":"D","en":"Right upper-quadrant pain with elevated AST and ALT","zh":"右上腹痛并伴AST和ALT升高"},{"id":"F","en":"Urine protein 2+","zh":"尿蛋白2+"},{"id":"C","en":"Platelet count 92 ×10³/µL","zh":"血小板92 ×10³/µL"},{"id":"E","en":"Fetal heart rate baseline 140/min with moderate variability","zh":"胎心基线140次/分且变异度中等"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Severe-range blood pressure, persistent neurologic symptoms, thrombocytopenia, and liver involvement with right upper-quadrant pain are severe features. Proteinuria supports preeclampsia but is not itself a severe feature, and the fetal tracing described is reassuring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"重度范围血压、持续神经系统症状、血小板减少，以及伴右上腹痛的肝脏受累均为重度特征。尿蛋白支持子痫前期，但本身不是重度特征；所描述的胎心监护较为 reassuring。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not confuse diagnostic criteria for preeclampsia with severe features. Severe features are the danger signs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把子痫前期的诊断标准与重度特征混淆。重度特征才是危险信号。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2258,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_preeclampsia_magnesium_01","embeddedQuestionId":"preeclampsia_initial_priority_mc","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing action is the priority after reviewing the admission data?","fullStemZh":"查看入院资料后，哪项护理措施最优先？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which nursing action is the priority after reviewing the admission data?","terminalSentenceZh":"查看入院资料后，哪项护理措施最优先？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Place the client on seizure precautions and prepare to administer magnesium sulfate as prescribed.","zh":"为患者实施防惊厥措施，并准备按医嘱给予硫酸镁。"},{"id":"A","en":"Reassure the client that delivery can wait until 40 weeks if the fetal tracing is reassuring.","zh":"告知患者若胎心监护正常，分娩可等到40周。"},{"id":"C","en":"Encourage oral fluids to improve urine output.","zh":"鼓励口服液体以改善尿量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Delay medication until the 24-hour urine protein collection is complete.","zh":"等待24小时尿蛋白收集完成后再给药。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has preeclampsia with severe features and is at risk for eclampsia. Seizure precautions and magnesium sulfate are priority stabilization measures, while severe hypertension is treated per protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者存在伴重度特征的子痫前期，有发生子痫的风险。防惊厥措施和硫酸镁是优先稳定措施，同时按方案处理重度高血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When maternal and fetal issues appear together, stabilize the maternal emergency first because fetal well-being depends on maternal stability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当母体和胎儿问题同时出现时，先稳定母体急症，因为胎儿状况依赖母体稳定。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2259,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_preeclampsia_magnesium_01","embeddedQuestionId":"preeclampsia_mag_toxicity_matrix","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"For each finding after magnesium sulfate is started, select the correct interpretation.","fullStemZh":"硫酸镁开始后，针对每项发现选择正确解释。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding after magnesium sulfate is started, select the correct interpretation.","terminalSentenceZh":"硫酸镁开始后，针对每项发现选择正确解释。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Respiratory rate 10/min","zh":"呼吸10次/分"},{"id":"r2","en":"Absent patellar reflexes","zh":"髌腱反射消失"},{"id":"r3","en":"Urine output 20 mL in the past hour","zh":"过去1小时尿量20 mL"},{"id":"r4","en":"Blood pressure decreased to 148/94 mm Hg","zh":"血压降至148/94 mm Hg"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected/therapeutic response","zh":"预期/治疗反应"},{"id":"c2","en":"Magnesium toxicity concern","zh":"硫酸镁中毒疑虑"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Respiratory depression, absent reflexes, and low urine output are toxicity cues because magnesium is renally cleared and can depress neuromuscular and respiratory function. Improved blood pressure after labetalol is an expected therapeutic response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呼吸抑制、反射消失和尿量减少都是中毒线索，因为镁经肾脏清除，并可抑制神经肌肉和呼吸功能。拉贝洛尔后血压改善属于预期治疗反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For magnesium questions, scan first for respiration, reflexes, and urine output.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做硫酸镁相关题时，先查看呼吸、反射和尿量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2260,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_preeclampsia_magnesium_01","embeddedQuestionId":"preeclampsia_mag_toxicity_order","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[47,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[10,23],"fullStemEn":"The nurse suspects magnesium sulfate toxicity. Place the actions in priority order.","fullStemZh":"护士怀疑硫酸镁中毒。请按优先顺序排列护理措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in priority order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按优先顺序排列护理措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse suspects magnesium sulfate toxicity.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士怀疑硫酸镁中毒。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Continue seizure precautions and frequent maternal-fetal monitoring.","zh":"继续防惊厥措施并密切监测母体和胎儿状况。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare to administer calcium gluconate as prescribed or per protocol.","zh":"准备按医嘱或方案给予葡萄糖酸钙。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider and rapid response team per facility policy.","zh":"按机构流程通知医护人员和快速反应团队。"},{"id":"A","en":"Stop the magnesium sulfate infusion.","zh":"停止硫酸镁输注。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess airway and breathing, apply oxygen, and stay with the client.","zh":"评估气道和呼吸，给予氧气，并留在患者身边。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stopping the magnesium source comes first, followed by airway and breathing support. The nurse escalates immediately, prepares the antidote calcium gluconate, and continues seizure and maternal-fetal monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先停止镁来源，其次支持气道和呼吸。护士应立即升级处理，准备解毒药葡萄糖酸钙，并继续防惊厥及母胎监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For suspected medication toxicity, stop the drug first, support ABCs, then escalate and prepare the antidote.","testTakingStrategyZh":"怀疑药物中毒时，先停药，支持ABC，再升级处理并准备解毒药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2261,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_copd_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,63],"fullStemEn":"COPD Exacerbation A 68-year-old male with a history of COPD (GOLD Stage III) presents to the emergency department with increased dyspnea and productive cough.","fullStemZh":"慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）急性加重 一名68岁男性，有COPD病史（GOLD III级），因呼吸困难加重和咳痰就诊于急诊科。","terminalSentenceEn":"COPD Exacerbation A 68-year-old male with a history of COPD (GOLD Stage III) presents to the emergency department with increased dyspnea and productive cough.","terminalSentenceZh":"慢性阻塞性肺疾病（COPD）急性加重 一名68岁男性，有COPD病史（GOLD III级），因呼吸困难加重和咳痰就诊于急诊科。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Management of COPD exacerbation focuses on improving oxygenation while avoiding oxygen toxicity, reducing airway inflammation, and treating underlying infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"COPD急性加重的管理重点是在避免氧中毒的同时改善氧合、减轻气道炎症并治疗潜在感染。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Monitor respiratory status and ABGs closely; maintain SpO2 within the targeted range for COPD.","testTakingStrategyZh":"密切监测呼吸状态和动脉血气；将血氧饱和度维持在COPD目标范围内。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2262,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_copd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_copd_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,88],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,23],"fullStemEn":"Which assessment findings require immediate nursing intervention? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些评估结果需要立即进行护理干预？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which assessment findings require immediate nursing intervention?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些评估结果需要立即进行护理干预？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use of accessory muscles for breathing","zh":"使用辅助呼吸肌呼吸"},{"id":"E","en":"History of hypertension","zh":"高血压病史"},{"id":"F","en":"Respiratory rate of 28/min","zh":"呼吸频率为 28次/分"},{"id":"C","en":"Productive cough with yellow-green sputum","zh":"咳嗽有痰，痰液呈黄绿色"},{"id":"D","en":"PaCO2 of 58 mmHg","zh":"PaCO2 为 58 mmHg"},{"id":"A","en":"SpO2 of 86% on room air","zh":"室内空气下血氧饱和度为 86%"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is in acute respiratory distress and respiratory acidosis. Low SpO2, accessory muscle use, elevated PaCO2, and tachypnea are critical findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者处于急性呼吸窘迫和呼吸性酸中毒状态。低血氧饱和度、使用辅助肌、PaCO2升高和呼吸过快是关键表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on airway, breathing, and circulation (ABCs). Findings indicating acute respiratory failure require immediate action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注气道、呼吸和循环（ABC）。提示急性呼吸衰竭的结果需要立即行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2263,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_copd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_copd_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,40],"fullStemEn":"For each ABG parameter, indicate whether the finding is consistent with respiratory acidosis, respiratory alkalosis, or metabolic compensation.","fullStemZh":"针对每个动脉血气参数，指出该结果是与呼吸性酸中毒、呼吸性碱中毒还是代谢补偿一致。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each ABG parameter, indicate whether the finding is consistent with respiratory acidosis, respiratory alkalosis, or metabolic compensation.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每个动脉血气参数，指出该结果是与呼吸性酸中毒、呼吸性碱中毒还是代谢补偿一致。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"pH 7.31","zh":"pH 7.31"},{"id":"r2","en":"PaCO2 58 mmHg","zh":"PaCO2 58 mmHg"},{"id":"r3","en":"HCO3 28 mEq/L","zh":"HCO3 28 mEq/L"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Respiratory Acidosis","zh":"呼吸性酸中毒"},{"id":"c2","en":"Metabolic Compensation","zh":"代谢补偿"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Low pH and high PaCO2 define respiratory acidosis. The elevated HCO3 indicates the kidneys are attempting to compensate (metabolic compensation).","rationaleCorrectZh":"低pH和高PaCO2定义了呼吸性酸中毒。HCO3升高表明肾脏正在尝试补偿（代谢补偿）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember: ROME (Respiratory Opposite, Metabolic Equal). Low pH + high CO2 = Respiratory Acidosis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住：ROME（呼吸相反，代谢相等）。低pH + 高CO2 = 呼吸性酸中毒。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2264,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_copd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_copd_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,69],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,15],"fullStemEn":"Complete the following sentence based on the client's current status.","fullStemZh":"根据患者当前状态完成以下句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the following sentence based on the client's current status.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据患者当前状态完成以下句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is at greatest risk for {{1}} due to {{2}}.","zh":"由于 {{2}}，该患者面临最大的 {{1}} 风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"respiratory failure","zh":"呼吸衰竭"},{"id":"o2","en":"septic shock","zh":"败血症休克"},{"id":"o3","en":"myocardial infarction","zh":"心肌梗死"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"systemic vasodilation","zh":"全身血管舒张"},{"id":"o3","en":"coronary artery occlusion","zh":"冠状动脉闭塞"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypoventilation and air trapping","zh":"肺泡通气不足和空气滞留"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"COPD exacerbations lead to hypoventilation, air trapping, and ventilation-perfusion mismatch, increasing the risk for acute respiratory failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"COPD急性加重导致通气不足、空气滞留和通气-血流灌注失调，增加了急性呼吸衰竭的风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the primary pathophysiological process of the primary diagnosis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别主要诊断的首要病理生理过程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2265,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_copd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_copd_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[31,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[8,24],"fullStemEn":"The nurse receives new orders. Rank the following actions in the order they should be performed.","fullStemZh":"护士接到新医嘱。请按执行顺序对以下操作进行排序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Rank the following actions in the order they should be performed.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按执行顺序对以下操作进行排序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse receives new orders.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士接到新医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer IV methylprednisolone","zh":"静脉注射甲泼尼龙"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer oxygen via nasal cannula to maintain SpO2 88-92%","zh":"通过鼻导管给氧，维持血氧饱和度在 88-92%"},{"id":"E","en":"Initiate IV antibiotics","zh":"开始静脉注射抗生素"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer nebulized albuterol and ipratropium","zh":"给予沙丁胺醇和异丙托溴铵雾化吸入"},{"id":"C","en":"Collect sputum for culture and sensitivity","zh":"采集痰标本进行培养和药敏试验"}],"correct":["A","B","D","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Oxygenation is the highest priority. Bronchodilators (albuterol/ipratropium) and steroids reduce airway obstruction. Sputum must be collected before the first dose of antibiotics.","rationaleCorrectZh":"氧合是最高优先级。支气管扩张剂（沙丁胺醇/异丙托溴铵）和类固醇可减轻气道阻塞。痰标本必须在首次使用抗生素前采集。","testTakingStrategyEn":"ABC priority followed by 'Culture before Antibiotic' rule.","testTakingStrategyZh":"ABC优先级，随后遵循“先培养后抗生素”原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2266,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_copd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_copd_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Which finding 2 hours after initiating treatment indicates the client's condition is improving?","fullStemZh":"开始治疗2小时后，哪项结果表明患者病情正在好转？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding 2 hours after initiating treatment indicates the client's condition is improving?","terminalSentenceZh":"开始治疗2小时后，哪项结果表明患者病情正在好转？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Breath sounds are absent in the bases","zh":"肺底呼吸音消失"},{"id":"A","en":"HR increased to 125 bpm","zh":"心率增至 125 次/分"},{"id":"B","en":"PaCO2 decreased to 48 mmHg","zh":"PaCO2 降至 48 mmHg"},{"id":"D","en":"SpO2 is 98% on 4L/min oxygen","zh":"4L/分氧气下血氧饱和度为 98%"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A decrease in PaCO2 indicates improved alveolar ventilation. In a COPD exacerbation with hypercapnia, an SpO2 of 98% on 4 L/min is above the usual controlled-oxygen target and may worsen CO2 retention. Absent breath sounds and increased HR indicate worsening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"PaCO2 下降说明肺泡通气改善。对于伴有高碳酸血症的 COPD 急性加重，4 L/分吸氧下 SpO2 达 98% 高于通常的控制给氧目标，可能加重 CO2 潴留。肺底呼吸音消失和心率升高提示病情恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate based on clinical goals for the specific disease process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据特定疾病过程的临床目标进行评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2267,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,142],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,44],"fullStemEn":"Chronic Kidney Disease & Hemodialysis A 54-year-old female with End-Stage Renal Disease (ESRD) arrives for her scheduled hemodialysis session.","fullStemZh":"慢性肾脏病与血液透析 一名54岁女性患有终末期肾病（ESRD），前来参加预定的血液透析。","terminalSentenceEn":"Chronic Kidney Disease & Hemodialysis A 54-year-old female with End-Stage Renal Disease (ESRD) arrives for her scheduled hemodialysis session.","terminalSentenceZh":"慢性肾脏病与血液透析 一名54岁女性患有终末期肾病（ESRD），前来参加预定的血液透析。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ESRD management requires balancing fluid and electrolytes through dialysis while managing chronic anemia and bone mineral disorders.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ESRD管理需要通过透析平衡液体和电解质，同时管理慢性贫血和骨矿物质代谢紊乱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on priority labs (Potassium) and fluid status (Weight) for renal cases.","testTakingStrategyZh":"针对肾脏病例，重点关注优先化验项目（钾）和液体状态（体重）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2268,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"For each lab finding, click to specify if the value is a priority to address before, during, or after dialysis.","fullStemZh":"针对每项化验结果，点击指出该数值是在透析前、透析中还是透析后需要优先处理的。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each lab finding, click to specify if the value is a priority to address before, during, or after dialysis.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项化验结果，点击指出该数值是在透析前、透析中还是透析后需要优先处理的。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Potassium 6.2 mEq/L","zh":"钾 6.2 mEq/L"},{"id":"r2","en":"Hemoglobin 9.1 g/dL","zh":"血红蛋白 9.1 g/dL"},{"id":"r3","en":"Creatinine 7.4 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐 7.4 mg/dL"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Priority: Before/During Dialysis","zh":"优先处理：透析前/透析中"},{"id":"c2","en":"Non-Urgent / Routine","zh":"非紧急/常规"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium 6.2 mEq/L is the urgent before/during-dialysis priority because hyperkalemia can cause fatal dysrhythmias. Hemoglobin 9.1 g/dL and creatinine 7.4 mg/dL are expected chronic ESRD findings that require routine longitudinal management, not the immediate priority.","rationaleCorrectZh":"钾 6.2 mEq/L 是透析前/透析中的紧急优先事项，因为高钾血症可导致致命性心律失常。血红蛋白 9.1 g/dL 和肌酐 7.4 mg/dL 属于 ESRD 常见的慢性异常，需要常规长期管理，而不是当前最紧急的处理重点。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Hyperkalemia is life-threatening and always a priority in renal failure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高钾血症危及生命，在肾衰竭中始终是优先事项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2269,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,76],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"Select the correct manifestations for the identified electrolyte imbalances.","fullStemZh":"为识别出的电解质紊乱选择正确的临床表现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the correct manifestations for the identified electrolyte imbalances.","terminalSentenceZh":"为识别出的电解质紊乱选择正确的临床表现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client's elevated potassium increases the risk for {{1}}, while the low calcium may manifest as {{2}}.","zh":"患者钾升高增加了 {{1}} 的风险，而钙降低可能表现为 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"ST segment depression","zh":"ST段压低"},{"id":"o2","en":"prominent U waves","zh":"明显的U波"},{"id":"o1","en":"tall peaked T waves","zh":"高尖T波"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"constipation","zh":"便秘"},{"id":"o2","en":"decreased deep tendon reflexes","zh":"深反射减弱"},{"id":"o1","en":"positive Trousseau's sign","zh":"Trousseau征阳性"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hyperkalemia causes peaked T waves. Hypocalcemia causes increased neuromuscular excitability (Trousseau's sign).","rationaleCorrectZh":"高钾血症导致T波高尖。低钙血症导致神经肌肉兴奋性增高（Trousseau征）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate electrolytes with specific ECG and neuromuscular findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将电解质与特定的心电图和神经肌肉发现联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2270,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[82,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,28],"fullStemEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include in the teaching plan for this client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士在为该患者制定教学计划时应包含哪些说明？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include in the teaching plan for this client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在为该患者制定教学计划时应包含哪些说明？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Avoid blood pressure readings on the left arm.","zh":"避免在左臂测量血压。"},{"id":"D","en":"Increase intake of dark green leafy vegetables.","zh":"增加深绿色叶菜的摄入。"},{"id":"B","en":"Check for a thrill and bruit daily.","zh":"每天检查震颤和杂音。"},{"id":"C","en":"Sleep with the left arm in a dependent position.","zh":"睡觉时让左臂处于下垂位置。"},{"id":"A","en":"Avoid carrying a heavy bag with the left arm.","zh":"避免用左臂提重物。"},{"id":"E","en":"Take phosphate binders with every meal.","zh":"每餐随餐服用磷酸盐结合剂。"}],"correct":["A","B","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"AV fistula care includes avoiding pressure (heavy bags, BP cuffs) and monitoring patency (thrill/bruit). Phosphate binders must be taken with meals to be effective. High-potassium foods (leafy greens) should be limited.","rationaleCorrectZh":"AVF护理包括避免受压（重物、血压计袖带）和监测通畅性（震颤/杂音）。磷结合剂必须随餐服用才有效。应限制高钾食物（绿叶蔬菜）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on protecting the access site and managing diet/medications for ESRD.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点是保护通路部位并管理ESRD的饮食/药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2271,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[83,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,43],"fullStemEn":"One hour into dialysis, the client reports dizziness and nausea. BP is 88/52 mmHg. What is the priority nursing action?","fullStemZh":"透析一小时后，患者主诉头晕和恶心。血压为 88/52 mmHg。首选的护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the priority nursing action?","terminalSentenceZh":"首选的护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"BP is 88/52 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压为 88/52 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Check the AV fistula for a bruit.","zh":"检查 AVF 的血管杂音。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stop the dialysis immediately and return blood.","zh":"立即停止透析并回血。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer an IV bolus of 500 mL normal saline.","zh":"静脉滴注 500 mL 生理盐水。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client in a supine position with legs elevated and slow the ultrafiltration rate.","zh":"将患者置于仰卧位且抬高双腿，并减慢超滤速度。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypotension is a common complication. Initial actions include positioning to increase venous return and adjusting the dialysis machine settings. Fluid boluses (usually smaller, 100-200mL) are used if positioning isn't enough.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低血压是常见并发症。最初的操作包括调整体位以增加回心血量以及调整透析机设置。如果调整体位不够，则使用补液（通常较小，100-200mL）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the least invasive intervention that addresses the immediate physiological need.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能够满足紧迫生理需求的最少侵入性干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"BP is 88/52 mmHg.","controlSentenceZh":"血压为 88/52 mmHg。"}
{"queueIndex":2272,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_ckd_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,64],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,15],"fullStemEn":"Which post-dialysis finding indicates the session was effective?","fullStemZh":"透析后的哪项结果表明透析有效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which post-dialysis finding indicates the session was effective?","terminalSentenceZh":"透析后的哪项结果表明透析有效？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Weight of 69.2 kg","zh":"体重 69.2 kg"},{"id":"B","en":"BUN of 60 mg/dL","zh":"BUN 60 mg/dL"},{"id":"D","en":"Potassium of 5.2 mEq/L","zh":"钾 5.2 mEq/L"},{"id":"C","en":"BP of 158/90 mmHg","zh":"血压 158/90 mmHg"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Reaching the 'dry weight' (the target weight after fluid removal) is the most reliable indicator of effective ultrafiltration. A potassium of 5.2 and BUN of 60 are still elevated, though improved.","rationaleCorrectZh":"达到“干重”（脱水后的目标体重）是超滤有效的最可靠指标。钾 5.2 和 BUN 60 虽然有所改善，但仍然偏高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Weight change is the best measure of fluid balance in renal patients.","testTakingStrategyZh":"体重变化是衡量肾病患者液体平衡的最佳指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2273,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_asthma_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Pediatric & Adolescent Health","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,31],"fullStemEn":"Pediatric Asthma Management An 8-year-old child with moderate persistent asthma is seen in the outpatient clinic for a follow-up visit.","fullStemZh":"儿童哮喘管理 一名患有中度持续性哮喘的8岁儿童在门诊进行随访。","terminalSentenceEn":"Pediatric Asthma Management An 8-year-old child with moderate persistent asthma is seen in the outpatient clinic for a follow-up visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"儿童哮喘管理 一名患有中度持续性哮喘的8岁儿童在门诊进行随访。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective asthma management in children involves environmental control, correct medication technique, and regular assessment using objective measures like peak flow.","rationaleCorrectZh":"儿童哮喘的有效管理包括环境控制、正确的用药技术以及使用峰流速等客观指标进行的定期评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the difference between preventative and emergency medications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别预防性药物和急救药物之间的区别。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2274,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_asthma_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_asthma_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.4.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,86],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"The child's current peak flow reading falls into which zone of the Asthma Action Plan?","fullStemZh":"该儿童当前的峰流速读数属于哮喘行动计划的哪个区域？","terminalSentenceEn":"The child's current peak flow reading falls into which zone of the Asthma Action Plan?","terminalSentenceZh":"该儿童当前的峰流速读数属于哮喘行动计划的哪个区域？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Emergency Zone","zh":"紧急区域"},{"id":"C","en":"Green Zone","zh":"绿色区域"},{"id":"D","en":"Red Zone","zh":"红色区域"},{"id":"B","en":"Yellow Zone","zh":"黄色区域"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"220/300 = 73%. The Yellow Zone is 50-80% of personal best. This indicates caution is needed as the asthma is not well controlled.","rationaleCorrectZh":"220/300 = 73%。黄色区域是个人最佳值的 50-80%。这表明哮喘未得到良好控制，需要引起注意。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Calculate the percentage of the personal best to determine the zone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"计算个人最佳值的百分比以确定区域。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2275,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_asthma_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_asthma_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.4.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,31],"fullStemEn":"The nurse assesses the home environment. Which findings are potential asthma triggers? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士评估了家庭环境。哪些发现是潜在的哮喘触发因素？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings are potential asthma triggers?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现是潜在的哮喘触发因素？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"A pet cat that sleeps in the child's bed","zh":"一只睡在孩子床上的宠物猫"},{"id":"E","en":"Stuffed animals stored on the child's bed","zh":"孩子床上放着毛绒玩具"},{"id":"F","en":"Parents smoke outside on the balcony","zh":"父母在阳台外吸烟"},{"id":"A","en":"Wall-to-wall carpeting in the bedroom","zh":"卧室铺满地毯"},{"id":"D","en":"Use of unscented cleaning products","zh":"使用无香型清洁用品"},{"id":"B","en":"A HEPA filter in the living room","zh":"客厅装有 HEPA 过滤器"}],"correct":["A","C","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Carpeting, pet dander, and dust mites (stuffed animals) are common allergens. Second-hand smoke (even from outside) can cling to clothes and trigger attacks.","rationaleCorrectZh":"地毯、宠物皮屑和尘螨（毛绒玩具）是常见的过敏原。二手烟（即使是在室外）也会附着在衣服上并诱发哮喘发作。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify items that harbor dust, dander, or irritants.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别含有灰尘、皮屑或刺激物的物品。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which findings are potential asthma triggers?","controlSentenceZh":"哪些发现是潜在的哮喘触发因素？（"}
