）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember NMS is characterized by 'Fever and Rigidity'.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住 NMS 的特征是“发热和僵硬”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2285,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_hip_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,128],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,35],"fullStemEn":"Post-op Total Hip Arthroplasty A 72-year-old female is 4 hours post-op from a right total hip arthroplasty (posterior approach).","fullStemZh":"全髋关节置换术后 一名72岁女性全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）术后4小时。","terminalSentenceEn":"Post-op Total Hip Arthroplasty A 72-year-old female is 4 hours post-op from a right total hip arthroplasty (posterior approach).","terminalSentenceZh":"全髋关节置换术后 一名72岁女性全髋关节置换术（后侧入路）术后4小时。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Post-op care for hip arthroplasty focuses on preventing dislocation through proper positioning and reducing complications like DVT.","rationaleCorrectZh":"髋关节置换术后的护理重点是通过正确的体位预防脱位并减少 DVT 等并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Always avoid internal rotation and hip flexion >90 degrees post-THA.","testTakingStrategyZh":"THA 术后始终避免内旋和髋部屈曲大于 90 度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2286,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_hip_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_hip_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,25],"fullStemEn":"Which findings would indicate a possible dislocation of the surgical hip? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些发现表明手术侧髋关节可能发生脱位？（多项选择）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多项选择）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings would indicate a possible dislocation of the surgical hip?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现表明手术侧髋关节可能发生脱位？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Shortening of the right leg","zh":"右腿缩短"},{"id":"E","en":"Inability to move the right toes","zh":"右脚趾无法活动"},{"id":"C","en":"Internal rotation of the right leg","zh":"右腿内旋"},{"id":"A","en":"Sudden onset of severe pain","zh":"突然发作的剧烈疼痛"},{"id":"D","en":"External rotation of the right leg","zh":"右腿外旋"},{"id":"F","en":"Numbness in the right foot","zh":"右足麻木"}],"correct":["A","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Signs of prosthetic hip dislocation include sudden severe pain, limb shortening, and internal rotation (for posterior approach). Numbness/inability to move toes indicates nerve damage, not necessarily dislocation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"人工髋关节脱位的迹象包括突然剧烈疼痛、肢体缩短和内旋（后侧入路）。麻木/脚趾无法活动提示神经损伤，不一定是脱位。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the physical appearance and pain character of the limb.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注肢体的外观和疼痛特征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2287,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_hip_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_hip_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,83],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Indicate whether each activity is 'Permitted' or 'Contraindicated' for this client.","fullStemZh":"指出以下每项活动对该患者是“允许”还是“禁忌”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Indicate whether each activity is 'Permitted' or 'Contraindicated' for this client.","terminalSentenceZh":"指出以下每项活动对该患者是“允许”还是“禁忌”。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Sitting on a low sofa","zh":"坐在低矮的沙发上"},{"id":"r2","en":"Crossing legs at the ankles","zh":"在踝部交叉双腿"},{"id":"r3","en":"Using an elevated toilet seat","zh":"使用加高的马桶座圈"},{"id":"r4","en":"Bending over to tie shoelaces","zh":"弯腰系鞋带"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Permitted","zh":"允许"},{"id":"c2","en":"Contraindicated","zh":"禁忌"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hip precautions (posterior approach) include: no hip flexion >90 degrees (low sofas/bending), no adduction (crossing legs), and no internal rotation. Elevated seats help maintain flexion <90 degrees.","rationaleCorrectZh":"髋关节预防措施（后侧入路）包括：髋部屈曲不得超过90度（低沙发/弯腰）、不得内收（交叉双腿）以及不得内旋。加高座圈有助于维持屈曲小于90度。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the '90-degree' rule and 'no crossing' rule for hip replacement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住髋关节置换术的“90度”原则和“禁止交叉”原则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2288,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_hip_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_hip_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Palliative & Supportive Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"What is the most effective nursing action to prevent deep vein thrombosis (DVT) in this client?","fullStemZh":"预防该患者发生深静脉血栓（DVT）最有效的护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most effective nursing action to prevent deep vein thrombosis (DVT) in this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"预防该患者发生深静脉血栓（DVT）最有效的护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place a pillow under the knees.","zh":"在膝盖下放一个枕头。"},{"id":"C","en":"Restrict fluid intake to prevent edema.","zh":"限制液体摄入以预防水肿。"},{"id":"D","en":"Massage the calves twice daily.","zh":"每天按摩两次小腿。"},{"id":"B","en":"Encourage early ambulation and ankle pumps.","zh":"鼓励尽早下床活动和进行踝泵运动。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Mobility and active muscle contraction (ankle pumps) promote venous return and are the most effective non-pharmacological methods to prevent DVT. Pillows under knees can cause stasis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"活动和主动肌肉收缩（踝泵）可促进静脉回流，是预防 DVT 最有效的非药物方法。膝下放枕头可能导致血液淤滞。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose mobility-focused interventions for circulatory prevention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"为循环系统预防选择以活动为中心的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2289,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_hip_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_hip_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Mobility & Immobility","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"The nurse prepares discharge teaching for the client's home environment.","fullStemZh":"护士为患者的家庭环境准备出院指导。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse prepares discharge teaching for the client's home environment.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士为患者的家庭环境准备出院指导。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"To maintain safety at home, the client should {{1}} and {{2}}.","zh":"为了维持居家安全，患者应该 {{1}} 并且 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"remove all area rugs","zh":"移除所有小地毯"},{"id":"o3","en":"keep the house dim to rest eyes","zh":"保持室内光线昏暗以休息眼睛"},{"id":"o2","en":"wax the floors to reduce friction","zh":"给地板打蜡以减少摩擦"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"store frequently used items on the floor","zh":"将常用物品放在地板上"},{"id":"o3","en":"use a standard height toilet","zh":"使用标准高度的马桶"},{"id":"o1","en":"install grab bars in the shower","zh":"在淋浴间安装抓杆"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Fall prevention is critical. Removing rugs and installing grab bars are key safety modifications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防跌倒至关重要。移除地毯和安装抓杆是关键的安全改装。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify fall hazards in the home.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别家中的跌倒隐患。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2290,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_hip_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_hip_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[128,177],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,79],"fullStemEn":"The client is prescribed Enoxaparin 30 mg SC every 12 hours for DVT prophylaxis. The pharmacy supplies Enoxaparin 40 mg/0.4 mL. How many mL should the nurse administer per dose?","fullStemZh":"患者被处方依诺肝素 30 mg 皮下注射，每 12 小时一次，用于 DVT 预防。药房提供的依诺肝素规格为 40 mg/0.4 mL。护士每剂应注射多少毫升？","terminalSentenceEn":"How many mL should the nurse administer per dose?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士每剂应注射多少毫升？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The pharmacy supplies Enoxaparin 40 mg/0.4 mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"药房提供的依诺肝素规格为 40 mg/0.4 mL。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["0.3"],"numeric":{"value":0.3,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Calculation: (Desired/Have) * Volume = (30 mg / 40 mg) * 0.4 mL = 0.75 * 0.4 = 0.3 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"计算：(所需/现有) * 体积 = (30 mg / 40 mg) * 0.4 mL = 0.75 * 0.4 = 0.3 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the formula: Desired / Have * Quantity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用公式：所需 / 现有 * 数量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2291,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_dka_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,48],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding Case: Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) An 18-year-old female with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus is admitted with nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.","fullStemZh":"展开式案例：糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 一名18岁患有1型糖尿病的女性因恶心、呕吐和腹痛入院。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding Case: Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) An 18-year-old female with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus is admitted with nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.","terminalSentenceZh":"展开式案例：糖尿病酮症酸中毒 (DKA) 一名18岁患有1型糖尿病的女性因恶心、呕吐和腹痛入院。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"DKA management focuses on aggressive fluid resuscitation, careful insulin titration, and close electrolyte monitoring, especially potassium.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DKA 管理的重点是积极的液体复苏、仔细的胰岛素滴定以及密切的电解质（尤其是钾）监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the priority of electrolyte stability over rapid glucose lowering.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到电解质稳定性优于快速降低血糖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2292,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_dka_01","embeddedQuestionId":"case_dka_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,93],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"For each clinical finding, indicate if it is consistent with DKA or an alternative condition.","fullStemZh":"对于每个临床表现，指示其是否与 DKA 或其他状况一致。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, indicate if it is consistent with DKA or an alternative condition.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每个临床表现，指示其是否与 DKA 或其他状况一致。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Kussmaul respirations","zh":"库斯莫尔呼吸"},{"id":"r2","en":"Fruity breath odor","zh":"烂苹果味呼吸"},{"id":"r3","en":"High urine specific gravity","zh":"尿比重升高"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"DKA","zh":"DKA"},{"id":"c2","en":"Alternative Condition","zh":"其他状况"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Kussmaul respirations and fruity breath are classic compensatory mechanisms for metabolic acidosis in DKA. High urine specific gravity occurs due to osmotic diuresis and dehydration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"库斯莫尔呼吸和烂苹果味呼吸是 DKA 代谢性酸中毒的经典代偿机制。由于渗透性利尿 and 脱水，会出现尿比重升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify cues that specifically relate to acid-base and fluid-electrolyte imbalances in DKA.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别与 DKA 中的酸碱和水、电解质失衡特别相关的线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2293,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_dka_01","embeddedQuestionId":"case_dka_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,75],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"The nurse considers the priority intervention based on current lab results.","fullStemZh":"护士根据当前的实验室结果考虑优先干预措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse considers the priority intervention based on current lab results.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士根据当前的实验室结果考虑优先干预措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should first initiate {{1}} before starting {{2}}.","zh":"护士应在开始 {{2}} 之前，首先启动 {{1}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Intravenous insulin infusion","zh":"静脉胰岛素输注"},{"id":"o1","en":"Potassium supplementation","zh":"补钾"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"Normal saline bolus","zh":"生理盐水快速补液"},{"id":"o1","en":"Insulin therapy","zh":"胰岛素治疗"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"With a potassium level of 3.4 mEq/L, supplementation must be initiated before insulin therapy to prevent life-threatening hypokalemia as insulin shifts potassium into cells.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在血钾水平为 3.4 mEq/L 时，必须在胰岛素治疗前开始补钾，因为胰岛素会将钾转移到细胞内，从而防止致命的低钾血症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize safety: check potassium levels before giving insulin in DKA.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先考虑安全：在 DKA 中给予胰岛素前检查血钾水平。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2294,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"case_dka_01","embeddedQuestionId":"case_dka_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[40,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[7,23],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the physician orders. Which fluid is most appropriate for initial resuscitation in this client?","fullStemZh":"护士审查医嘱。哪种液体最适合该患者的初始复苏？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which fluid is most appropriate for initial resuscitation in this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种液体最适合该患者的初始复苏？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the physician orders.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士审查医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"3% Sodium Chloride","zh":"3% 氯化钠"},{"id":"D","en":"0.45% Sodium Chloride","zh":"0.45% 氯化钠"},{"id":"B","en":"Dextrose 5% in Water","zh":"5% 葡萄糖注射液"},{"id":"C","en":"0.9% Sodium Chloride","zh":"0.9% 氯化钠"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Initial DKA resuscitation uses an isotonic crystalloid to restore intravascular volume. Among these options, 0.9% sodium chloride is the appropriate initial fluid; hypotonic, dextrose-containing, and hypertonic saline solutions are not initial resuscitation fluids.","rationaleCorrectZh":"DKA 初始复苏应使用等渗晶体液以恢复血管内容量。在这些选项中，0.9% 氯化钠是合适的初始液体；低渗液、含糖液和高渗盐水都不是初始复苏液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on isotonic solutions for initial shock/dehydration management.","testTakingStrategyZh":"重点关注用于初始休克/脱水管理的等渗溶液。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the physician orders.","controlSentenceZh":"护士审查医嘱。"}
