{"queueIndex":2369,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ngn_010_ad","embeddedQuestionId":"q10_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,61],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"Why is the heart rate 50 bpm despite the high blood pressure?","fullStemZh":"为什么尽管血压很高，心率却是 50 bpm？","terminalSentenceEn":"Why is the heart rate 50 bpm despite the high blood pressure?","terminalSentenceZh":"为什么尽管血压很高，心率却是 50 bpm？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The client is in cardiogenic shock","zh":"患者处于心源性休克"},{"id":"C","en":"Damage to the SA node","zh":"窦房结受损"},{"id":"B","en":"Parasympathetic compensation above the level of injury","zh":"损伤水平以上的副交感神经代偿"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The brain attempts to lower BP by sending parasympathetic signals via the vagus nerve, causing bradycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"大脑试图通过迷走神经发送副交感信号来降低血压，导致心动过缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze cues carefully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细分析线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2370,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ngn_010_ad","embeddedQuestionId":"q10_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[59,81],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,19],"fullStemEn":"Which actions should the nurse take to identify the cause? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应采取哪些行动来确定原因？（多选）","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"多选）","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take to identify the cause?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些行动来确定原因？（","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Palpate the bladder for distension","zh":"触诊膀胱是否扩张"},{"id":"A","en":"Check the urinary catheter for kinks","zh":"检查导尿管是否扭结"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess skin for pressure sores or tight clothing","zh":"评估皮肤是否有压疮或衣服过紧"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess for fecal impaction per protocol after bladder causes are addressed","zh":"处理膀胱相关原因后按规程评估粪便嵌塞"},{"id":"K","en":"Lay the client flat to rest","zh":"让患者平卧休息"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After sitting the client upright, systematically evaluate common triggers: urinary obstruction or bladder distension, bowel impaction using protocol, and skin or clothing irritation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"让患者坐起后，应系统评估常见诱因：尿路阻塞或膀胱扩张、按规程评估粪便嵌塞，以及皮肤或衣物刺激。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze cues carefully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细分析线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2371,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_ngn_010_ad","embeddedQuestionId":"q10_5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.27.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,48],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,13],"fullStemEn":"Which finding indicates the crisis is resolving?","fullStemZh":"哪项发现表明危机正在解除？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which finding indicates the crisis is resolving?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项发现表明危机正在解除？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Headache intensifies","zh":"头痛加剧"},{"id":"B","en":"Sweating increases below the level of injury","zh":"损伤水平以下的出汗增加"},{"id":"A","en":"Blood pressure returns to baseline","zh":"血压恢复到基础值"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Return of BP to baseline and resolution of symptoms indicate successful management.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血压恢复至基础水平且症状消失表明管理成功。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze cues carefully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细分析线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2372,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.28","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.28.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,60],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: chest tube to water-seal drainage A 58-year-old client is admitted with a spontaneous left pneumothorax and a chest tube is placed and connected to a closed water-seal drainage system with suction.","fullStemZh":"情境演变案例：胸腔引流管接水封引流 一名58岁患者因自发性左侧气胸入院，置入胸腔引流管并连接闭式水封引流系统及负压吸引。","terminalSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: chest tube to water-seal drainage A 58-year-old client is admitted with a spontaneous left pneumothorax and a chest tube is placed and connected to a closed water-seal drainage system with suction.","terminalSentenceZh":"情境演变案例：胸腔引流管接水封引流 一名58岁患者因自发性左侧气胸入院，置入胸腔引流管并连接闭式水封引流系统及负压吸引。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe chest tube management hinges on distinguishing normal drainage-system mechanics (tidaling, intermittent water-seal bubbling, suction-chamber bubbling) from danger signs (continuous water-seal bubbling = air leak; large bright-red output = hemorrhage), and on responding correctly to emergencies: re-establish a water seal in sterile water if the tube disconnects, apply a three-sided occlusive dressing if it pulls out, and avoid prolonged clamping that risks tension pneumothorax.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全管理胸腔引流管的关键在于:区分正常的引流系统机制(潮汐样波动、水封腔间歇冒泡、吸引腔冒泡)与危险征象(水封腔持续冒泡=漏气;大量鲜红色引流=出血);并正确处理紧急情况:引流管脱开时将末端浸入无菌水重建水封,引流管脱出时使用三面固定的密闭敷料,避免长时间夹闭以防张力性气胸。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor on three rules: continuous water-seal bubbling = leak; disconnection = water seal in sterile water; tube out = occlusive dressing taped on three sides.","testTakingStrategyZh":"牢记三条规则:水封腔持续冒泡=漏气;管路脱开=末端浸入无菌水建立水封;引流管脱出=三面固定密闭敷料覆盖。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2373,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"For each chest-drainage finding, indicate whether it is expected for this client or requires immediate follow-up.","fullStemZh":"对于每项胸腔引流相关发现,判断其对此患者是否为预期表现,还是需要立即跟进处理。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each chest-drainage finding, indicate whether it is expected for this client or requires immediate follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项胸腔引流相关发现,判断其对此患者是否为预期表现,还是需要立即跟进处理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Tidaling (water level rises/falls with respiration) in the water-seal chamber","zh":"水封腔出现潮汐样波动(水位随呼吸上下波动)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Gentle continuous bubbling in the suction-control chamber","zh":"负压控制腔轻柔持续冒泡"},{"id":"r3","en":"Intermittent bubbling in the water-seal chamber","zh":"水封腔间歇性冒泡"},{"id":"r4","en":"200 mL of bright red drainage in 1 hour","zh":"1小时内引流出200 mL鲜红色液体"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires immediate follow-up","zh":"需立即跟进"},{"id":"c1","en":"Expected","zh":"预期"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Tidaling reflects pressure changes and can indicate a patent tube. Gentle continuous bubbling in the suction-control chamber is expected with wet suction. Intermittent bubbling in the water-seal chamber can be expected early with a pneumothorax as trapped pleural air evacuates. Bright red drainage of 200 mL/hr is excessive and signals possible hemorrhage requiring immediate provider notification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"潮汐样波动反映胸腔压力变化,可提示引流管通畅。湿式负压吸引时,负压控制腔轻柔持续冒泡属预期。气胸早期胸腔内积气排出时,水封腔间歇性冒泡可为预期表现。每小时200 mL鲜红色引流量过多,提示可能出血,需立即通知医生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate drainage-system mechanics that can be expected in a pneumothorax from red-flag findings. Sudden, large, bright-red output is the outlier.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将气胸中可能预期出现的引流系统机制与危险信号区分开。突发、大量、鲜红色的引流才是异常项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2374,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[111,155],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,36],"fullStemEn":"Two hours later the nurse notes new continuous bubbling in the water-seal chamber that was not present before. What does this finding most likely indicate?","fullStemZh":"两小时后,护士发现水封腔出现此前没有的持续性冒泡。该发现最可能提示什么?","terminalSentenceEn":"What does this finding most likely indicate?","terminalSentenceZh":"该发现最可能提示什么?","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two hours later the nurse notes new continuous bubbling in the water-seal chamber that was not present before.","penultimateSentenceZh":"两小时后,护士发现水封腔出现此前没有的持续性冒泡。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The suction pressure is set too low","zh":"吸引压力设置过低"},{"id":"A","en":"An air leak in the system or at the insertion site","zh":"系统或置管处存在漏气"},{"id":"B","en":"Re-expansion of the lung is complete","zh":"肺已完全复张"},{"id":"D","en":"The tube is kinked or obstructed","zh":"引流管打折或阻塞"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"New or continuous bubbling in the water-seal chamber indicates air is entering the closed system — an air leak, either within the system (loose connection) or at the insertion site. The nurse should assess connections and the dressing and locate the leak.","rationaleCorrectZh":"水封腔出现新发或持续性冒泡提示有空气进入闭式系统,即存在漏气,可能在系统内(接头松动)或置管处。护士应检查各接头和敷料,定位漏气点。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the rule: continuous water-seal bubbling = air leak. Intermittent = normal pneumothorax evacuation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住口诀:水封腔持续冒泡=漏气;间歇冒泡=气胸正常排气。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2375,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,51],"fullStemEn":"At 1330 the chest tube has disconnected from the drainage tubing and the client is short of breath with an SpO2 of 89%. What is the nurse's immediate priority action?","fullStemZh":"在1330,胸腔引流管已与引流管路脱开,患者呼吸困难,SpO2为89%。护士首要的即刻处理措施是什么?","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's immediate priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首要的即刻处理措施是什么?","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1330 the chest tube has disconnected from the drainage tubing and the client is short of breath with an SpO2 of 89%.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在1330,胸腔引流管已与引流管路脱开,患者呼吸困难,SpO2为89%。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Clamp the chest tube near the insertion site with a padded clamp","zh":"用带衬垫的钳子在置管处附近夹闭胸腔引流管"},{"id":"D","en":"Submerge the end of the chest tube in a bottle of sterile water to re-establish a water seal","zh":"将胸腔引流管末端浸入一瓶无菌水中,重新建立水封"},{"id":"C","en":"Lay the client flat and call the rapid response team","zh":"让患者平卧并呼叫快速反应小组"},{"id":"B","en":"Reconnect the tubing after wiping both ends with an alcohol swab","zh":"用酒精棉片擦拭两端后重新连接管路"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"If a chest tube disconnects from the drainage system, the priority is to re-establish a water seal by submerging the open end in sterile water (about 2 cm). This lets pleural air escape while preventing atmospheric air from being drawn back into the pleural space, which would worsen the pneumothorax.","rationaleCorrectZh":"若胸腔引流管与引流系统脱开,首要措施是将开口端浸入无菌水中(约2 cm)以重新建立水封。这样既能让胸腔内空气排出,又能防止大气空气被吸回胸膜腔而加重气胸。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Disconnection from the system → water seal in sterile water. Tube pulled out of the chest → occlusive dressing taped on three sides. Never clamp for long.","testTakingStrategyZh":"与系统脱开→将末端浸入无菌水建立水封;引流管从胸壁脱出→用三面固定的密闭敷料覆盖。切勿长时间夹闭。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2376,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_chest_tube_rrp_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[49,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,37],"fullStemEn":"The seal is restored and the system reconnected. Which later finding best indicates that the client's pneumothorax is resolving as expected?","fullStemZh":"水封已恢复,系统重新连接。以下哪项后续发现最能提示患者的气胸正按预期消退?","terminalSentenceEn":"Which later finding best indicates that the client's pneumothorax is resolving as expected?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项后续发现最能提示患者的气胸正按预期消退?","penultimateSentenceEn":"The seal is restored and the system reconnected.","penultimateSentenceZh":"水封已恢复,系统重新连接。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Continuous bubbling returns in the water-seal chamber","zh":"水封腔再次出现持续冒泡"},{"id":"B","en":"Subcutaneous crepitus develops around the insertion site","zh":"置管处周围出现皮下捻发感"},{"id":"A","en":"Tidaling stops and water-seal bubbling ceases, with improved breath sounds and a re-expanded lung on x-ray","zh":"潮汐样波动停止、水封腔不再冒泡,呼吸音改善,X线示肺复张"},{"id":"C","en":"The collection chamber fills rapidly with bright red fluid","zh":"收集腔迅速被鲜红色液体充满"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"As a pneumothorax resolves, the pleural air is fully evacuated: bubbling stops, tidaling ceases (lung is re-expanded against the chest wall), breath sounds improve, and the chest x-ray confirms re-expansion. These together indicate the expected outcome.","rationaleCorrectZh":"气胸消退时,胸腔内积气被完全排出:冒泡停止,潮汐样波动消失(肺已复张贴向胸壁),呼吸音改善,胸部X线证实肺复张。这些综合表现提示达到预期结局。","testTakingStrategyEn":"\"Resolved\" answers show normal findings trending toward baseline; distractors reintroduce a complication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"表示\"已消退\"的答案体现各项指标趋向正常基线;干扰项则重新引入并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The seal is restored and the system reconnected.","controlSentenceZh":"水封已恢复,系统重新连接。"}
{"queueIndex":2377,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.29","itemType":"case_study","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.29.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[169,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,65],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: immobile older adult with skin breakdown An 82-year-old client with advanced dementia is bedbound, incontinent, and has lost weight over the past month. The nurse completes a head-to-toe skin assessment.","fullStemZh":"情境演变案例:活动受限老年患者出现皮肤破损 一名82岁晚期痴呆患者长期卧床、大小便失禁,近一个月体重下降。护士完成了全身皮肤评估。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse completes a head-to-toe skin assessment.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士完成了全身皮肤评估。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: immobile older adult with skin breakdown An 82-year-old client with advanced dementia is bedbound, incontinent, and has lost weight over the past month.","penultimateSentenceZh":"情境演变案例:活动受限老年患者出现皮肤破损 一名82岁晚期痴呆患者长期卧床、大小便失禁,近一个月体重下降。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Correct pressure injury care requires accurate staging by tissue depth (Stage 1 intact red, Stage 2 shallow dermis, Stage 3 fat visible, Stage 4 deeper structures, unstageable when obscured by slough/eschar), aggressive prevention (turning, heel floating, pressure-redistribution surfaces, moisture control, no massage of bony prominences), and anabolic nutritional support (protein, vitamin C, zinc, calories, supplements) to promote healing in a high-risk, malnourished, immobile client.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的压力性损伤护理需要:按组织深度准确分期(1期皮肤完整发红,2期浅表真皮,3期可见脂肪,4期更深结构,被腐肉/焦痂遮盖则无法分期);积极预防(翻身、足跟悬空、压力再分布支撑垫、控制潮湿、避免按摩骨突);以及合成代谢性营养支持(蛋白质、维C、锌、热量、补充剂),以促进这位高危、营养不良、活动受限患者的伤口愈合。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stage strictly by what you can see; prevent by relieving pressure and moisture; heal by building nutrition. Reject options that add trauma or restrict substrates.","testTakingStrategyZh":"严格按可见组织分期;通过解除压力与潮湿来预防;通过补充营养来促进愈合。排除增加创伤或限制营养物质的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2378,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,61],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Match each skin finding to its correct pressure injury stage.","fullStemZh":"将每项皮肤发现与其正确的压力性损伤分期相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each skin finding to its correct pressure injury stage.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每项皮肤发现与其正确的压力性损伤分期相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Sacrum: full-thickness loss, subcutaneous fat visible, slough present, no bone/tendon/muscle exposed","zh":"骶尾部:全层缺损,可见皮下脂肪,有腐肉,无骨/肌腱/肌肉外露"},{"id":"r2","en":"Right heel: intact skin with non-blanchable redness","zh":"右足跟:皮肤完整,压之不褪色的发红"},{"id":"r3","en":"Left lateral malleolus: partial-thickness loss, shallow pink moist wound bed, no slough","zh":"左外踝:部分皮肤缺损,创面浅、粉红、湿润,无腐肉"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Stage 2","zh":"2期"},{"id":"c3","en":"Stage 3","zh":"3期"},{"id":"c1","en":"Stage 1","zh":"1期"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stage 3 involves full-thickness skin loss with visible subcutaneous fat and possible slough, but no exposed bone, tendon, or muscle (the sacrum). Stage 1 is intact skin with non-blanchable erythema (the heel). Stage 2 is partial-thickness loss with a shallow pink/red moist wound bed and no slough (the malleolus).","rationaleCorrectZh":"3期为全层皮肤缺损,可见皮下脂肪并可能有腐肉,但无骨、肌腱或肌肉外露(骶尾部)。1期为皮肤完整、压之不褪色的红斑(足跟)。2期为部分皮肤缺损,创面浅、呈粉红/红色、湿润且无腐肉(外踝)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Stage by depth: intact + red = 1; open shallow dermis = 2; fat visible = 3; bone/tendon/muscle = 4; obscured by slough/eschar = unstageable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按深度分期:皮肤完整+发红=1期;真皮浅层开放=2期;可见脂肪=3期;骨/肌腱/肌肉外露=4期;被腐肉/焦痂覆盖无法判定=无法分期。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2379,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[101,123],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,36],"fullStemEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the plan of care to prevent further pressure injury? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应在护理计划中纳入哪些措施以预防进一步的压力性损伤?选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse include in the plan of care to prevent further pressure injury?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在护理计划中纳入哪些措施以预防进一步的压力性损伤?","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Float the heels off the bed using a pillow under the calves","zh":"用枕头垫于小腿下使足跟悬空"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the head of the bed elevated above 45 degrees at all times","zh":"始终将床头抬高至45度以上"},{"id":"C","en":"Vigorously massage the reddened heel to improve circulation","zh":"用力按摩发红的足跟以促进血液循环"},{"id":"E","en":"Use a pressure-redistribution support surface","zh":"使用减压/压力再分布支撑垫"},{"id":"F","en":"Keep skin clean and dry and manage incontinence promptly","zh":"保持皮肤清洁干燥,及时处理失禁"},{"id":"A","en":"Reposition the client at least every 2 hours","zh":"至少每2小时为患者翻身一次"}],"correct":["A","B","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Repositioning at least every 2 hours, floating the heels, using a pressure-redistribution surface, and keeping skin clean and dry while managing moisture all reduce sustained pressure and moisture-associated damage. Massaging reddened bony prominences is contraindicated, and keeping the head of bed high increases shear over the sacrum.","rationaleCorrectZh":"至少每2小时翻身、使足跟悬空、使用压力再分布支撑垫,以及保持皮肤清洁干燥并控制潮湿,都能减少持续受压和潮湿相关损伤。按摩发红的骨突处属禁忌,而长时间过高抬高床头会增加骶尾部的剪切力。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Pressure-injury prevention = relieve pressure, reduce shear/moisture. Reject any option that adds friction, shear, or trauma (massage, high HOB).","testTakingStrategyZh":"预防压力性损伤=解除压力、减少剪切与潮湿。凡是增加摩擦、剪切或创伤的选项(按摩、床头过高)均应排除。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2380,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Sleep & Rest","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[123,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,48],"fullStemEn":"Given the client's albumin of 2.8 g/dL, poor intake, and weight loss, which nutrition measures best support wound healing? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"鉴于患者白蛋白2.8 g/dL、进食差及体重下降,哪些营养措施最有利于伤口愈合?选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Given the client's albumin of 2.8 g/dL, poor intake, and weight loss, which nutrition measures best support wound healing?","penultimateSentenceZh":"鉴于患者白蛋白2.8 g/dL、进食差及体重下降,哪些营养措施最有利于伤口愈合?","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Ensure adequate vitamin C and zinc","zh":"确保充足的维生素C和锌"},{"id":"C","en":"Provide adequate calories and hydration","zh":"提供充足的热量和水分"},{"id":"A","en":"Increase dietary protein intake","zh":"增加膳食蛋白质摄入"},{"id":"E","en":"Offer oral nutritional supplements between meals","zh":"在两餐之间提供口服营养补充剂"},{"id":"D","en":"Restrict all dietary fat and protein to reduce metabolic demand","zh":"限制所有膳食脂肪和蛋白质以降低代谢需求"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Wound healing requires increased protein for tissue synthesis, vitamin C and zinc as cofactors for collagen formation and immune function, adequate calories and fluids, and oral supplements to bridge poor intake. Restricting protein and fat would deprive the client of substrates essential for healing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"伤口愈合需要增加蛋白质以合成组织,需要维生素C和锌作为胶原形成与免疫功能的辅因子,需要充足的热量和水分,并通过口服补充剂弥补摄入不足。限制蛋白质和脂肪会剥夺患者愈合所必需的物质基础。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Healing is anabolic: think \"build\" (protein, vitamin C, zinc, calories), not \"restrict.\"","testTakingStrategyZh":"愈合是合成代谢过程:思路应是\"补充建造\"(蛋白质、维C、锌、热量),而非\"限制\"。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2381,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_pressure_injury_bcc_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[142,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,45],"fullStemEn":"Two days later the right heel that was previously intact now has thick black eschar covering the wound bed so the depth cannot be visualized. How should the nurse document this injury?","fullStemZh":"两天后,原本完整的右足跟现被一层厚的黑色焦痂覆盖,无法看清创面深度。护士应如何记录该损伤?","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse document this injury?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何记录该损伤?","penultimateSentenceEn":"Two days later the right heel that was previously intact now has thick black eschar covering the wound bed so the depth cannot be visualized.","penultimateSentenceZh":"两天后,原本完整的右足跟现被一层厚的黑色焦痂覆盖,无法看清创面深度。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Stage 2 pressure injury","zh":"2期压力性损伤"},{"id":"D","en":"Unstageable pressure injury","zh":"无法分期的压力性损伤"},{"id":"B","en":"Deep tissue pressure injury","zh":"深部组织压力性损伤"},{"id":"C","en":"Stage 4 pressure injury","zh":"4期压力性损伤"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When the wound bed is obscured by slough or eschar so that the true depth (and therefore the stage) cannot be determined, the injury is classified as unstageable until enough nonviable tissue is removed to visualize the base.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当创面被腐肉或焦痂覆盖,无法判断真实深度(因而无法确定分期)时,该损伤应归为无法分期,直至清除足够的失活组织能够看清创面基底为止。","testTakingStrategyEn":"If you cannot see the base, you cannot stage it = unstageable. Don't guess a number through eschar.","testTakingStrategyZh":"看不到创面基底就无法分期=无法分期。切勿透过焦痂猜测期别数字。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Two days later the right heel that was previously intact now has thick black eschar covering the wound bed so the depth cannot be visualized.","controlSentenceZh":"两天后,原本完整的右足跟现被一层厚的黑色焦痂覆盖,无法看清创面深度。"}
{"queueIndex":2382,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.30","itemType":"case_study","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.30.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,70],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: hospital-acquired C. difficile infection A 70-year-old client who finished a course of broad-spectrum antibiotics now has frequent watery, foul-smelling diarrhea. A stool test is positive for C. difficile toxin.","fullStemZh":"情境演变案例:医院获得性艰难梭菌感染 一名70岁患者刚完成一个疗程的广谱抗生素治疗,现出现频繁的水样、恶臭腹泻。粪便检测艰难梭菌毒素呈阳性。","terminalSentenceEn":"A stool test is positive for C. difficile toxin.","terminalSentenceZh":"粪便检测艰难梭菌毒素呈阳性。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: hospital-acquired C. difficile infection A 70-year-old client who finished a course of broad-spectrum antibiotics now has frequent watery, foul-smelling diarrhea.","penultimateSentenceZh":"情境演变案例:医院获得性艰难梭菌感染 一名70岁患者刚完成一个疗程的广谱抗生素治疗,现出现频繁的水样、恶臭腹泻。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. difficile is a spore-forming, fecal-orally transmitted organism that demands contact precautions, soap-and-water hand hygiene (alcohol does not kill spores), dedicated equipment, and chlorine-based (sporicidal) surface disinfection. PPE is donned before entry and doffed dirtiest-first (gloves, eye protection, gown) with hand hygiene as the final step, all to prevent transmission to other clients.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艰难梭菌是一种形成孢子、经粪-口途径传播的病原体,需要采取接触隔离、用肥皂流动水洗手(酒精不能杀灭孢子)、使用专用器械,以及使用含氯(杀孢子)消毒剂清洁表面。进入前穿戴PPE,脱卸时遵循最脏先脱原则(手套、护目镜、隔离衣),最后完成手卫生,以防止传播给其他患者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Two C. difficile flags override defaults: soap-and-water (not alcohol) and bleach (not quat) surfaces. Otherwise apply standard contact-precaution and PPE-doffing rules.","testTakingStrategyZh":"两个艰难梭菌要点优先于常规做法:用肥皂流动水(而非酒精)、用含氯漂白剂(而非季铵盐)消毒表面。其余遵循标准的接触隔离和PPE脱卸规则。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: hospital-acquired C. difficile infection A 70-year-old client who finished a course of broad-spectrum antibiotics now has frequent watery, foul-smelling diarrhea.","controlSentenceZh":"情境演变案例:医院获得性艰难梭菌感染 一名70岁患者刚完成一个疗程的广谱抗生素治疗,现出现频繁的水样、恶臭腹泻。"}
{"queueIndex":2383,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Which type of transmission-based precautions should the nurse initiate for this client?","fullStemZh":"护士应为该患者启动哪种基于传播途径的隔离措施?","terminalSentenceEn":"Which type of transmission-based precautions should the nurse initiate for this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应为该患者启动哪种基于传播途径的隔离措施?","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Droplet precautions","zh":"飞沫隔离"},{"id":"D","en":"Protective (reverse) isolation","zh":"保护性(反向)隔离"},{"id":"C","en":"Contact precautions","zh":"接触隔离"},{"id":"B","en":"Airborne precautions","zh":"空气隔离"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"C. difficile is transmitted by the fecal-oral route through contact with contaminated hands, surfaces, and equipment, so contact precautions (gown and gloves, private room when possible) are indicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"艰难梭菌通过粪-口途径,经接触被污染的手、表面和器械传播,因此应采用接触隔离(穿隔离衣、戴手套,尽量安排单人间)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the route to the precaution: enteric/fecal-oral and skin/wound = contact; cough/large droplet = droplet; tiny airborne nuclei = airborne.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将传播途径与隔离类型对应:肠道/粪-口及皮肤/伤口=接触;咳嗽/大飞沫=飞沫;微小空气飞沫核=空气。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2384,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"After providing care for this client, how should the nurse perform hand hygiene?","fullStemZh":"为该患者提供护理后,护士应如何进行手卫生?","terminalSentenceEn":"After providing care for this client, how should the nurse perform hand hygiene?","terminalSentenceZh":"为该患者提供护理后,护士应如何进行手卫生?","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Use an alcohol-based hand rub only","zh":"仅使用含酒精的快速手消毒剂"},{"id":"A","en":"Rinse hands with water alone","zh":"仅用清水冲洗双手"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply alcohol-based hand rub, then don clean gloves","zh":"先使用含酒精手消毒剂,再戴干净手套"},{"id":"B","en":"Wash hands with soap and water","zh":"用肥皂和流动水洗手"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For C. difficile teaching and testing, soap-and-water hand hygiene is preferred after care because spores are not reliably inactivated by alcohol-based hand rubs and mechanical washing helps remove them. Correct glove and gown use remains essential to reduce hand contamination.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在艰难梭菌相关护理教学和考试中,护理后首选肥皂和流动水进行手卫生,因为酒精类免洗手消毒剂不能可靠灭活芽孢,机械性洗手有助于去除芽孢。正确使用手套和隔离衣仍是减少手部污染的关键。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Spore-formers (C. difficile, anthrax, norovirus is non-spore but also alcohol-resistant) = soap and water. Alcohol is not sporicidal.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于形成孢子的病原体(如艰难梭菌)=肥皂加流动水。酒精不能杀灭孢子。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2385,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"matrix","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[52,115],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,30],"fullStemEn":"The nurse observes a student caring for the client. Indicate whether each action is correct or requires correction.","fullStemZh":"护士观察一名学生护理该患者。指出每项操作是正确还是需要纠正。","terminalSentenceEn":"Indicate whether each action is correct or requires correction.","terminalSentenceZh":"指出每项操作是正确还是需要纠正。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes a student caring for the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士观察一名学生护理该患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Dons a gown and gloves before entering the room","zh":"进入病房前穿隔离衣并戴手套"},{"id":"r2","en":"Uses dedicated (single-client) equipment such as a stethoscope and BP cuff","zh":"使用专用(单一患者)器械,如听诊器和血压计袖带"},{"id":"r3","en":"Cleans the room surfaces with a quaternary-ammonium wipe only","zh":"仅用季铵盐类湿巾清洁病房表面"},{"id":"r4","en":"Removes gloves and gown and performs hand hygiene before leaving the room","zh":"离开病房前脱去手套和隔离衣并进行手卫生"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires correction","zh":"需纠正"},{"id":"c1","en":"Correct","zh":"正确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Donning gown and gloves before entry, using dedicated equipment, and removing PPE with hand hygiene before leaving are all correct contact-precaution practices. Routine quaternary-ammonium cleaners are not sporicidal; surfaces must be disinfected with a sporicidal agent such as a chlorine-based (bleach) product.","rationaleCorrectZh":"进入前穿隔离衣戴手套、使用专用器械,以及离开前脱去个人防护用品并进行手卫生,均为正确的接触隔离做法。常规季铵盐类清洁剂不能杀灭孢子;表面必须使用含氯(漂白剂)等杀孢子消毒剂处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For C. difficile, two details flip many answers: soap-and-water hand hygiene and bleach (chlorine) for surfaces. Standard alcohol/quat products are not enough.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于艰难梭菌,两个细节常决定答案对错:用肥皂流动水洗手、用含氯(漂白剂)消毒表面。常规酒精/季铵盐产品不够。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2386,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_cdiff_sic_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Safety and Infection Prevention and Control","topic":"Transmission-Based Precautions","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"Place the steps for removing personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order before leaving the client-care area.","fullStemZh":"将离开患者护理区域前脱去个人防护用品(PPE)的步骤按正确顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the steps for removing personal protective equipment (PPE) in the correct order before leaving the client-care area.","terminalSentenceZh":"将离开患者护理区域前脱去个人防护用品(PPE)的步骤按正确顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Perform hand hygiene with soap and water after removing PPE","zh":"脱去PPE后用肥皂和流动水进行手卫生"},{"id":"A","en":"Remove gloves","zh":"脱手套"},{"id":"B","en":"Remove gown","zh":"脱隔离衣"},{"id":"D","en":"Remove eye protection / goggles","zh":"摘下护目镜/防护眼罩"}],"correct":["A","D","B","C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A safe PPE-removal sequence removes the most contaminated items first: gloves, then eye protection by the clean strap or earpieces, then gown, followed by hand hygiene. For C. difficile teaching, final hand hygiene is performed with soap and water because spores are not reliably removed or inactivated by alcohol rub alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全脱卸PPE的顺序是先脱污染最重的物品:手套,然后通过清洁的带子或镜腿摘下护目镜/眼罩,再脱隔离衣,最后进行手卫生。对于艰难梭菌护理教学,最后的手卫生使用肥皂和流动水,因为单独使用酒精擦手不能可靠去除或灭活芽孢。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For PPE doffing, think contaminated to clean, then hand hygiene. In C. difficile items, choose soap and water when handwashing is tested.","testTakingStrategyZh":"脱卸PPE时按“由污染到清洁”思路,最后进行手卫生。艰难梭菌题目考到洗手时,选择肥皂和流动水。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2387,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.31","itemType":"case_study","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.31.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,232],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,70],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: adult wellness and prevention visit A 66-year-old client with well-controlled type 2 diabetes presents to a primary care clinic for a routine wellness visit. The nurse reviews preventive care and immunization status.","fullStemZh":"情境演变案例:成人健康与预防保健就诊 一名66岁、2型糖尿病控制良好的患者到初级保健诊所进行常规健康体检。护士审查其预防保健和免疫接种情况。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews preventive care and immunization status.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士审查其预防保健和免疫接种情况。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: adult wellness and prevention visit A 66-year-old client with well-controlled type 2 diabetes presents to a primary care clinic for a routine wellness visit.","penultimateSentenceZh":"情境演变案例:成人健康与预防保健就诊 一名66岁、2型糖尿病控制良好的患者到初级保健诊所进行常规健康体检。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Health promotion for an older adult integrates age- and interval-based immunization (annual influenza, pneumococcal at 65, recombinant zoster at 50, Td/Tdap every 10 years), evidence-based screening (colorectal cancer from 45 to 75 regardless of how well the client feels), and recognition that live vaccines are contraindicated in pregnancy and immunosuppression. Glycemic control further reduces this diabetic client's long-term risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"针对老年人的健康促进需综合考虑:基于年龄和间隔的免疫接种(流感每年、肺炎球菌65岁、重组带状疱疹50岁、Td/Tdap每10年);循证筛查(结直肠癌45至75岁,无论自觉是否健康);以及认识到活疫苗在妊娠和免疫抑制者中禁用。控制血糖可进一步降低这位糖尿病患者的长期风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Tie prevention to triggers: vaccines to age/interval, screening to age window, and contraindications to host status (pregnancy/immunosuppression = no live vaccines).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将预防与触发点对应:疫苗对应年龄/间隔,筛查对应年龄窗口,禁忌对应宿主状态(妊娠/免疫抑制=不接种活疫苗)。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2388,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,45],"fullStemEn":"For each immunization, indicate whether it is currently recommended (indicated now) for this 66-year-old client or not indicated at this visit.","fullStemZh":"对于每种疫苗,指出对这位66岁患者目前是否推荐接种(当前有指征),还是本次就诊不需要接种。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each immunization, indicate whether it is currently recommended (indicated now) for this 66-year-old client or not indicated at this visit.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每种疫苗,指出对这位66岁患者目前是否推荐接种(当前有指征),还是本次就诊不需要接种。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Seasonal influenza vaccine","zh":"季节性流感疫苗"},{"id":"r2","en":"Pneumococcal vaccine","zh":"肺炎球菌疫苗"},{"id":"r3","en":"Recombinant zoster (shingles) vaccine","zh":"重组带状疱疹疫苗"},{"id":"r4","en":"Td/Tdap booster","zh":"Td/Tdap加强针"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Indicated now","zh":"当前有指征"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not indicated at this visit","zh":"本次无需接种"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"All four are indicated. Influenza vaccine is recommended annually for nearly all adults and he has not had it this season. Pneumococcal vaccination is recommended for adults age 50 years or older who have not received a pneumococcal conjugate vaccine or whose history is unknown. Recombinant zoster vaccine is recommended for adults 50 and older. A tetanus-containing booster is due because his last dose was 12 years ago (routine interval is every 10 years).","rationaleCorrectZh":"四项均有指征。流感疫苗几乎所有成年人每年都应接种,而他本季尚未接种。对于年满50岁且未接种过肺炎球菌结合疫苗或接种史不明的成年人,建议接种肺炎球菌疫苗。重组带状疱疹疫苗建议50岁及以上成年人接种。含破伤风成分的加强针也已到期,因为上次接种距今12年(常规间隔为每10年一次)。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Anchor adult vaccines to age/interval triggers: flu annually, pneumococcal at 50 (CDC 2024 update), zoster at 50, Td/Tdap every 10 years.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把成人疫苗与年龄/间隔触发点对应记忆:流感每年、肺炎球菌50岁(CDC 2024 更新)、带状疱疹50岁、Td/Tdap每10年。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2389,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,36],"fullStemEn":"The client has never been screened for colorectal cancer and has average risk. Which screening should the nurse expect to be recommended?","fullStemZh":"该患者从未进行过结直肠癌筛查,且为平均风险人群。护士应预期推荐何种筛查?","terminalSentenceEn":"Which screening should the nurse expect to be recommended?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期推荐何种筛查?","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client has never been screened for colorectal cancer and has average risk.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者从未进行过结直肠癌筛查,且为平均风险人群。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Abdominal ultrasound","zh":"腹部超声检查"},{"id":"B","en":"No colorectal screening is needed until age 75 regardless of prior screening","zh":"无论既往是否筛查,75岁前都无需结直肠筛查"},{"id":"C","en":"Colonoscopy (or another approved colorectal screening test)","zh":"结肠镜检查(或其他获批的结直肠筛查方法)"},{"id":"A","en":"Serum carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) as a screening test","zh":"以血清癌胚抗原(CEA)作为筛查方法"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Average-risk adults should be screened for colorectal cancer beginning at age 45 and continuing through 75; an unscreened 66-year-old is overdue. Colonoscopy is a recommended option (stool-based tests are alternatives). Ultrasound and CEA are not colorectal cancer screening tests.","rationaleCorrectZh":"平均风险成人应从45岁开始进行结直肠癌筛查,并持续至75岁;一位66岁、从未筛查者已严重滞后。结肠镜是推荐方案之一(粪便检测为替代方案)。腹部超声和CEA均非结直肠癌筛查手段。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Know the average-risk colorectal window: start at 45, continue to 75. Tumor markers and ultrasound are not screening tools.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住平均风险结直肠筛查窗口:45岁开始、持续至75岁。肿瘤标志物和超声不是筛查工具。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2390,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[196,222],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,59],"fullStemEn":"While at the clinic, the client mentions his adult daughter is pregnant and was just diagnosed with leukemia and is receiving chemotherapy. He asks which vaccine she should NOT receive right now. Which response is correct?","fullStemZh":"就诊时,患者提到他成年的女儿正在怀孕,且刚被诊断为白血病、正在接受化疗。他询问女儿目前不应接种哪种疫苗。哪项回答正确?","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response is correct?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项回答正确?","penultimateSentenceEn":"He asks which vaccine she should NOT receive right now.","penultimateSentenceZh":"他询问女儿目前不应接种哪种疫苗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Live attenuated vaccines (such as MMR or varicella) should be avoided","zh":"应避免接种减毒活疫苗(如麻腮风疫苗或水痘疫苗)"},{"id":"A","en":"The inactivated influenza vaccine should be avoided","zh":"应避免接种灭活流感疫苗"},{"id":"D","en":"The tetanus (Tdap) vaccine should be avoided","zh":"应避免接种破伤风(Tdap)疫苗"},{"id":"C","en":"All vaccines are safe and none should be avoided","zh":"所有疫苗都安全,不需要避免任何疫苗"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Live attenuated vaccines (e.g., MMR, varicella, live nasal influenza) are contraindicated in pregnancy and in significantly immunocompromised clients such as those receiving chemotherapy, because the weakened organism can cause disease. Inactivated vaccines like the injectable influenza and Tdap are not only safe but recommended in pregnancy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"减毒活疫苗(如麻腮风疫苗、水痘疫苗、鼻喷活流感疫苗)在妊娠期及如接受化疗等明显免疫低下患者中属禁忌,因为减毒的病原体可能致病。而灭活疫苗如注射型流感疫苗和Tdap不仅安全,且在妊娠期推荐接种。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Red flag pairs: pregnancy and immunosuppression both contraindicate LIVE vaccines. Inactivated vaccines stay safe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"危险信号组合:妊娠和免疫抑制都禁忌\"活\"疫苗。灭活疫苗仍然安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2391,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_adult_immunization_hpm_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Adult Health & Wellness","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,117],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,33],"fullStemEn":"Which statements by the client indicate correct understanding of his preventive care teaching? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"患者的哪些陈述表明他正确理解了预防保健的健康教育?选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements by the client indicate correct understanding of his preventive care teaching?","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的哪些陈述表明他正确理解了预防保健的健康教育?","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"\"Keeping my blood sugar controlled lowers my risk of complications.\"","zh":"\"控制好血糖能降低我并发症的风险。\""},{"id":"C","en":"\"Since I feel healthy, I can skip the colorectal cancer screening.\"","zh":"\"既然我感觉健康,就可以不做结直肠癌筛查。\""},{"id":"A","en":"\"I should get a flu shot every year.\"","zh":"\"我每年都应该打流感疫苗。\""},{"id":"E","en":"\"The shingles vaccine can help prevent a painful rash and nerve pain.\"","zh":"\"带状疱疹疫苗有助于预防疼痛性皮疹和神经痛。\""},{"id":"B","en":"\"Because my last tetanus shot was over 10 years ago, I'm due for a booster.\"","zh":"\"因为我上次破伤风疫苗已超过10年,我该打加强针了。\""}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Annual influenza vaccination, a tetanus booster every 10 years, glycemic control to reduce diabetic complications, and zoster vaccination to prevent shingles and postherpetic neuralgia all reflect correct understanding. Believing that feeling well removes the need for colorectal screening is a misconception, since colorectal cancer is often asymptomatic early.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每年接种流感疫苗、每10年一次破伤风加强针、控制血糖以减少糖尿病并发症,以及接种带状疱疹疫苗以预防带状疱疹和疱疹后神经痛,均体现正确理解。认为\"感觉健康就无需结直肠筛查\"是错误观念,因为结直肠癌早期常无症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"On \"correct understanding\" items, the wrong choice is usually the one that uses \"feeling fine\" to skip evidence-based screening.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在\"正确理解\"类题目中,错误选项通常是以\"感觉良好\"为由跳过循证筛查的那一项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2392,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.32","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.32.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[227,279],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,75],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: suspected intimate partner violence in the emergency department A 29-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with a wrist injury. Her partner stays at the bedside and answers most questions for her. The nurse notes several findings that raise concern.","fullStemZh":"情境演变案例:急诊科疑似亲密伴侣暴力 一名29岁女性因手腕受伤到急诊科就诊。她的伴侣一直守在床边,并代她回答大部分问题。护士注意到若干引起担忧的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse notes several findings that raise concern.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士注意到若干引起担忧的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her partner stays at the bedside and answers most questions for her.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她的伴侣一直守在床边,并代她回答大部分问题。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Responding to suspected intimate partner violence requires recognizing cues (inconsistent injury history, delayed care, repeated injuries, controlling partner), screening the client privately and alone, then prioritizing safety through a collaborative safety plan and resources while honoring the client's autonomy. Communication must be nonjudgmental and validating, and documentation must be accurate and objective.","rationaleCorrectZh":"应对疑似亲密伴侣暴力需要:识别线索(受伤经过不符、延迟就医、反复受伤、控制型伴侣);在私密、单独的环境中筛查患者;随后在尊重患者自主权的前提下,通过共同制定安全计划和提供资源来优先保障安全。沟通必须不带评判、给予肯定,记录必须准确、客观。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Across IPV items: interview alone, never confront the abuser, support (don't command) autonomy, stay nonjudgmental, and document objectively.","testTakingStrategyZh":"贯穿亲密伴侣暴力题目的原则:单独询问、绝不质问施暴者、支持(而非命令)患者自主、保持不评判、客观记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2393,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[100,122],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,33],"fullStemEn":"Which findings should the nurse recognize as cues that raise concern for intimate partner violence? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应将哪些发现识别为提示亲密伴侣暴力的可疑线索?选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings should the nurse recognize as cues that raise concern for intimate partner violence?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应将哪些发现识别为提示亲密伴侣暴力的可疑线索?","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"The client requesting a written list of her discharge medications","zh":"患者要求一份书面的出院用药清单"},{"id":"A","en":"Injuries in various stages of healing","zh":"处于不同愈合阶段的损伤"},{"id":"D","en":"A partner who answers for the client and is reluctant to leave","zh":"伴侣代患者回答且不愿离开"},{"id":"C","en":"An explanation of injury that is inconsistent with the findings","zh":"受伤解释与体征不相符"},{"id":"B","en":"A delay of two days before seeking care","zh":"受伤后延迟两天才就医"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Injuries at different healing stages, delayed care, an injury story that does not match the physical findings, and a controlling partner who answers for the client and will not leave are all classic red flags for intimate partner violence. Asking for a medication list is normal, appropriate engagement in care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"处于不同愈合阶段的损伤、延迟就医、受伤经过与体征不符,以及一个代答且不愿离开的控制型伴侣,都是亲密伴侣暴力的典型危险信号。索要用药清单则是正常、恰当地参与自身护理的表现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"IPV cues cluster around inconsistency, delay, repeated injury, and a controlling companion. A normal care request is the outlier.","testTakingStrategyZh":"亲密伴侣暴力的线索集中在:经过不符、就医延迟、反复受伤和有控制欲的陪同者。正常的护理请求是例外项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2394,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"What is the most appropriate nursing action to screen the client for intimate partner violence?","fullStemZh":"为筛查患者是否遭受亲密伴侣暴力,最恰当的护理措施是什么?","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most appropriate nursing action to screen the client for intimate partner violence?","terminalSentenceZh":"为筛查患者是否遭受亲密伴侣暴力,最恰当的护理措施是什么?","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Avoid raising the topic unless the client brings it up first","zh":"除非患者主动提起,否则避免谈及该话题"},{"id":"B","en":"Find a private moment to interview the client alone, away from the partner","zh":"找一个私密时机,在伴侣不在场时单独询问患者"},{"id":"A","en":"Ask the client about abuse directly in front of the partner","zh":"当着伴侣的面直接询问患者是否遭受虐待"},{"id":"D","en":"Confront the partner about the suspicious injuries","zh":"就可疑损伤当面质问伴侣"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Screening for IPV must occur privately, with the client alone, so she can answer honestly without fear of the partner. The nurse can use a routine reason (such as a test or specimen) to ask the partner to step out. Asking in front of the partner endangers the client, confronting the partner can escalate violence, and waiting silently misses the chance to offer help.","rationaleCorrectZh":"亲密伴侣暴力的筛查必须在私密环境下、患者单独在场时进行,使其能在不惧怕伴侣的情况下如实回答。护士可借常规理由(如做检查或留取标本)请伴侣暂时离开。当着伴侣的面询问会危及患者,质问伴侣可能激化暴力,而沉默等待则会错失提供帮助的机会。","testTakingStrategyEn":"The first rule of IPV screening: get the client alone. Never screen or confront in front of the suspected abuser.","testTakingStrategyZh":"亲密伴侣暴力筛查的第一原则:让患者单独在场。绝不在疑似施暴者面前进行筛查或质问。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2395,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,44],"fullStemEn":"Once alone, the client tearfully discloses that her partner hit her but says, 'I'm not ready to leave him.' What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"在单独相处后,患者含泪坦言伴侣打了她,但说\"我还没准备好离开他\"。护士的首要措施是什么?","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要措施是什么?","penultimateSentenceEn":"Once alone, the client tearfully discloses that her partner hit her but says, 'I'm not ready to leave him.'","penultimateSentenceZh":"在单独相处后,患者含泪坦言伴侣打了她,但说\"我还没准备好离开他\"。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Insist that she leave the partner immediately before discharge","zh":"坚持要求她在出院前立即离开伴侣"},{"id":"C","en":"Tell her she must press charges against her partner today","zh":"告诉她今天必须对伴侣提起诉讼"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess her immediate safety and help develop a safety plan, including resources she can use","zh":"评估她当前的安全状况,并协助制定安全计划,包括可使用的求助资源"},{"id":"B","en":"Reassure her that the situation will likely improve on its own","zh":"安慰她说情况很可能会自行好转"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse respects the client's autonomy while prioritizing safety: assess immediate danger and collaboratively develop a safety plan and provide resources (hotline, shelter, escape plan). Pressuring her to leave or press charges removes her control, can escalate danger, and may drive her away from help. Falsely reassuring her is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应在尊重患者自主权的同时优先保障安全:评估当前危险程度,与其共同制定安全计划并提供资源(求助热线、庇护所、撤离计划)。强迫她离开或起诉会剥夺其控制权、可能加重危险,并可能使她拒绝接受帮助。虚假地安慰她则不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Support autonomy + safety. The right answer assesses danger and plans for safety; wrong answers command, judge, or falsely reassure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"兼顾自主与安全。正确答案评估危险并制定安全计划;错误答案则是命令、评判或虚假安慰。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2396,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01","embeddedQuestionId":"claude_cs_jun06_ipv_screening_psi_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,43],"fullStemEn":"For each nurse statement or action, indicate whether it is therapeutic/appropriate or non-therapeutic/inappropriate when supporting this client.","fullStemZh":"对于护士的每项陈述或行为,指出在支持该患者时是治疗性/恰当的,还是非治疗性/不恰当的。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each nurse statement or action, indicate whether it is therapeutic/appropriate or non-therapeutic/inappropriate when supporting this client.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于护士的每项陈述或行为,指出在支持该患者时是治疗性/恰当的,还是非治疗性/不恰当的。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"\"This is not your fault, and you did not deserve to be hurt.\"","zh":"\"这不是你的错,你不该受到伤害。\""},{"id":"r2","en":"\"I'm concerned for your safety. Here is a hotline number you can keep.\"","zh":"\"我很担心你的安全。这是一个你可以保留的求助热线号码。\""},{"id":"r3","en":"\"Why do you stay with someone who hurts you?\"","zh":"\"你为什么还和一个伤害你的人待在一起?\""},{"id":"r4","en":"Document the client's own words and objective findings accurately in the record","zh":"在病历中准确记录患者的原话和客观体征"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Non-therapeutic / inappropriate","zh":"非治疗性/不恰当"},{"id":"c1","en":"Therapeutic / appropriate","zh":"治疗性/恰当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Affirming that the abuse is not the client's fault, expressing concern while providing resources, and accurately documenting the client's own words and objective findings are all therapeutic and support safety. Asking 'why do you stay' is judgmental, implies blame, and is non-therapeutic.","rationaleCorrectZh":"明确告知患者虐待不是她的错、在表达关心的同时提供资源,以及准确记录患者原话和客观体征,都是治疗性的并有助于保障安全。质问\"你为什么还留下来\"带有评判、暗示责备,属非治疗性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Therapeutic = nonjudgmental, validating, resource-offering. 'Why' questions that imply blame are almost always non-therapeutic.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗性=不评判、给予肯定、提供资源。带有责备意味的\"为什么\"提问几乎总是非治疗性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2397,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_main","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.33","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.33.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[241,362],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,105],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: Suspected Thyroid Storm A 34-year-old female client is brought to the emergency department by her spouse. The spouse reports the client has been increasingly restless, confused, and sweating profusely over the last 12 hours. The client has a history of Graves' disease but stopped taking methimazole three weeks ago due to gastrointestinal upset.","fullStemZh":"进展性案例：疑似甲状腺危象 一名34岁女性患者由配偶陪同来到急诊室。配偶诉患者在过去12小时内越来越烦躁、意识模糊并大量出汗。患者有毒性弥漫性甲状腺肿（Graves病）病史，但因胃肠道不适于三周前停用甲巯咪唑。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client has a history of Graves' disease but stopped taking methimazole three weeks ago due to gastrointestinal upset.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者有毒性弥漫性甲状腺肿（Graves病）病史，但因胃肠道不适于三周前停用甲巯咪唑。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The spouse reports the client has been increasingly restless, confused, and sweating profusely over the last 12 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"配偶诉患者在过去12小时内越来越烦躁、意识模糊并大量出汗。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thyroid storm requires immediate recognition and sequential intervention. Care begins with airway and cardiovascular stabilization (propranolol) to manage the deadly sympathetic surge. This is strictly followed by halting new thyroid hormone synthesis (PTU) before blocking its release (Lugol's iodine). Concurrently, nursing care focuses on aggressively lowering hyperpyrexia with safe methods (acetaminophen, cooling blankets, avoiding aspirin) and minimizing sensory stimulation. Finally, outcomes must be evaluated by monitoring both the resolution of symptoms (vital sign stability) and vigilance for severe pharmacological side effects, such as PTU-induced agranulocytosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺危象需要立即识别并进行序贯干预。护理从气道和心血管稳定（普萘洛尔）开始，以控制致命的交感神经激增。这必须严格遵循先停止新甲状腺激素合成（PTU），然后再阻断其释放（Lugol液）的顺序。同时，护理工作侧重于使用安全方法（对乙酰氨基酚、冰毯、避免使用阿司匹林）积极降低高热，并将感觉刺激降至最低。最后，必须通过监测症状的缓解情况（生命体征稳定）和警惕严重的药理学副作用（如PTU引起的粒细胞缺乏症）来评估治疗结果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Unfolding cases require tracking clinical trends. Notice the timeline of medication administration and match nursing interventions to the physiological priorities at each stage (cardiac control -> source control -> complication prevention).","testTakingStrategyZh":"进展性案例需要跟踪临床趋势。注意给药的时间线，并将护理干预措施与每个阶段的生理优先事项（心脏控制 -> 根源控制 -> 并发症预防）相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The spouse reports the client has been increasingly restless, confused, and sweating profusely over the last 12 hours.","controlSentenceZh":"配偶诉患者在过去12小时内越来越烦躁、意识模糊并大量出汗。"}
{"queueIndex":2398,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_main","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,229],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,69],"fullStemEn":"The nurse analyzes the client's initial 0800 triage presentation. For each finding, indicate if the cue is expected in uncomplicated hyperthyroidism, or if it specifically indicates a transition to life-threatening thyroid storm.","fullStemZh":"护士分析患者0800最初的分诊表现。针对每一项体征，指出该线索是单纯性甲状腺功能亢进的预期表现，还是明确提示已转变为危及生命的甲状腺危象。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, indicate if the cue is expected in uncomplicated hyperthyroidism, or if it specifically indicates a transition to life-threatening thyroid storm.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每一项体征，指出该线索是单纯性甲状腺功能亢进的预期表现，还是明确提示已转变为危及生命的甲状腺危象。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse analyzes the client's initial 0800 triage presentation.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士分析患者0800最初的分诊表现。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Temperature of 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)","zh":"体温 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Diffuse anterior neck enlargement","zh":"颈前弥漫性肿大"},{"id":"r3","en":"Severe agitation and confusion","zh":"极度烦躁与意识模糊"},{"id":"r4","en":"Heart rate of 152 bpm","zh":"心率 152 次/分"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Expected in Uncomplicated Hyperthyroidism","zh":"单纯性甲亢预期表现"},{"id":"c2","en":"Indicates Thyroid Storm","zh":"提示甲状腺危象"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Thyroid storm is an extreme, life-threatening exacerbation of hyperthyroidism. While hyperthyroidism causes heat intolerance, extreme hyperpyrexia (e.g., 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)) is a hallmark of thyroid storm. Mild anxiety is common in hyperthyroidism, but severe agitation, delirium, and confusion indicate CNS dysfunction specific to thyroid storm. Resting tachycardia (90-110 bpm) is expected in hyperthyroidism, but extreme tachycardia (>130 bpm) or arrhythmias like atrial fibrillation signify thyroid storm. A goiter is an anatomical feature of Graves' disease and hyperthyroidism, not a specific acute marker of a storm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺危象是甲状腺功能亢进的一种极端、危及生命的恶化形式。虽然甲亢会导致怕热，但极端高热（如 104.2 °F (40.1 °C)）是甲状腺危象的标志。轻度焦虑在甲亢中很常见，但极度烦躁、谵妄和意识模糊表明中枢神经系统功能障碍，这是甲状腺危象的特有表现。静息心动过速（90-110 次/分）是甲亢的预期表现，但极度心动过速（>130 次/分）或心律失常（如心房颤动）则标志着甲状腺危象。甲状腺肿是Graves病和甲亢的解剖学特征，并非危象的特异性急性标志。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Distinguish between chronic physiological adaptations to high thyroid levels and the acute, decompensated signs of metabolic crisis. High fever, CNS changes, and extreme tachycardia are the triad of thyroid storm.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分对高甲状腺素水平的慢性生理适应与代谢危机的急性失代偿体征。高热、中枢神经系统改变和极度心动过速是甲状腺危象的三联征。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2399,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_main","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,193],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,50],"fullStemEn":"Based on the 0830 orders, the nurse prepares to administer the prescribed medications. Drag and drop the medications into the correct order of administration to safely manage the thyroid storm.","fullStemZh":"根据0830的医嘱，护士准备给予处方药物。请拖拽药物并按正确的给药顺序排列，以安全地处理甲状腺危象。","terminalSentenceEn":"Drag and drop the medications into the correct order of administration to safely manage the thyroid storm.","terminalSentenceZh":"请拖拽药物并按正确的给药顺序排列，以安全地处理甲状腺危象。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Based on the 0830 orders, the nurse prepares to administer the prescribed medications.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据0830的医嘱，护士准备给予处方药物。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"opt_bb","en":"Administer IV propranolol","zh":"静脉注射普萘洛尔"},{"id":"opt_steroid","en":"Administer IV hydrocortisone","zh":"静脉注射氢化可的松"},{"id":"opt_iodine","en":"Administer Lugol's iodine solution","zh":"给予复方碘溶液 (Lugol液)"},{"id":"opt_ptu","en":"Administer propylthiouracil (PTU)","zh":"给予丙硫氧嘧啶 (PTU)"}],"correct":["opt_bb","opt_ptu","opt_iodine","opt_steroid"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pharmacological sequence in thyroid storm is critical to prevent exacerbating the condition. First, a beta-blocker (propranolol) is administered immediately to block peripheral sympathetic effects, lowering the dangerously high heart rate and preventing cardiovascular collapse. Second, an antithyroid medication like PTU is given to block the synthesis of new thyroid hormones. Third, an iodine solution (Lugol's) is given to block the release of pre-formed thyroid hormones. Crucially, iodine must be delayed for 1-2 hours AFTER PTU; if given first, iodine will act as substrate and fuel massive new thyroid hormone synthesis. Fourth, corticosteroids (hydrocortisone) are administered to treat relative adrenal insufficiency caused by hypermetabolism and to block the peripheral conversion of T4 to active T3.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺危象的药理学用药顺序对于防止病情恶化至关重要。第一，必须立即给予β受体阻滞剂（普萘洛尔）以阻断外周交感神经效应，降低危险的高心率并预防心血管崩溃。第二，给予抗甲状腺药物如PTU以阻断新甲状腺激素的合成。第三，给予碘溶液（Lugol液）以阻断已生成的甲状腺激素的释放。关键在于，碘剂必须在PTU给药后1-2小时延迟使用；如果先给碘，碘将作为底物加速大量新甲状腺激素的合成。第四，给予皮质类固醇（氢化可的松）以治疗由高代谢引起的相对肾上腺功能不全，并阻断外周T4向活性T3的转化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the sequence: Block the effects (Beta blocker) -> Block synthesis (PTU) -> Block release (Iodine) -> Block peripheral conversion (Steroids). Never give iodine before PTU.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住用药顺序：阻断效应（β受体阻滞剂）-> 阻断合成（PTU）-> 阻断释放（碘剂）-> 阻断外周转化（类固醇）。绝对不要在PTU之前给碘。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2400,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_main","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,52],"fullStemEn":"To manage the client's hypermetabolic state and maintain safety between 0800 and 1200, which nursing interventions are indicated? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"为了在0800至1200之间控制患者的高代谢状态并维持安全，需要采取哪些护理干预措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"To manage the client's hypermetabolic state and maintain safety between 0800 and 1200, which nursing interventions are indicated?","penultimateSentenceZh":"为了在0800至1200之间控制患者的高代谢状态并维持安全，需要采取哪些护理干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"opt_aspirin","en":"Administer prescribed aspirin for antipyretic relief.","zh":"遵医嘱给予阿司匹林以退热。"},{"id":"opt_cooling","en":"Apply a cooling blanket and ice packs to axillae and groin.","zh":"使用冰毯并将冰袋置于腋下和腹股沟。"},{"id":"opt_environment","en":"Maintain a cool, dark, and quiet room environment.","zh":"维持凉爽、昏暗且安静的病房环境。"},{"id":"opt_acetaminophen","en":"Administer prescribed acetaminophen for hyperthermia.","zh":"遵医嘱给予对乙酰氨基酚以治疗高热。"},{"id":"opt_fluids","en":"Restrict intravenous fluids to prevent pulmonary edema.","zh":"限制静脉输液以防止肺水肿。"},{"id":"opt_seizure","en":"Initiate seizure precautions.","zh":"启动癫痫预防措施。"}],"correct":["opt_acetaminophen","opt_cooling","opt_environment","opt_seizure"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Nursing care for thyroid storm focuses on reducing hyperthermia, preventing injury from extreme agitation, and providing supportive care. Acetaminophen and physical cooling (cooling blankets, ice packs) are used aggressively to lower core temperature. A cool, dark, quiet environment minimizes sympathetic nervous system stimulation, reducing agitation and cardiac demand. Seizure precautions are necessary because severe hyperpyrexia and CNS hyper-excitability place the client at high risk for seizures. Aspirin is contraindicated because salicylates displace thyroid hormone from binding proteins, increasing free active thyroid hormone levels and worsening the storm. Fluid restriction is incorrect; these clients have profound insensible fluid losses from diaphoresis and hyperventilation and require aggressive IV fluid replacement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺危象的护理重点是降低高热、防止因极度烦躁引起的损伤并提供支持性护理。对乙酰氨基酚和物理降温（冰毯、冰袋）被积极用于降低核心体温。凉爽、昏暗、安静的环境可最大限度地减少交感神经系统刺激，从而减轻烦躁和心脏负荷。由于严重高热和中枢神经系统过度兴奋使患者处于癫痫发作的高危状态，因此必须采取癫痫预防措施。阿司匹林是禁忌的，因为水杨酸盐会将甲状腺激素从结合蛋白上置换下来，增加游离活性甲状腺激素水平并加重危象。限制输液是错误的；这些患者因大量出汗和过度通气会产生严重的不显性失水，需要积极的静脉补液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When selecting medications for symptoms, always consider drug-disease interactions. Remember that aspirin is unsafe in thyroid storm. Treat the hypermetabolism with a calm environment and physical cooling.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在为症状选择药物时，请始终考虑药物与疾病的相互作用。记住阿司匹林在甲状腺危象中是不安全的。通过安静的环境和物理降温来应对高代谢。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2401,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_main","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_thyroid_storm_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[113,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,60],"fullStemEn":"The nurse evaluates the 1200 laboratory results to monitor for severe adverse effects of propylthiouracil (PTU). Which laboratory finding requires immediate notification to the healthcare provider?","fullStemZh":"护士评估1200的实验室结果，以监测丙硫氧嘧啶 (PTU) 的严重不良反应。哪一项实验室发现需要立即通知医疗服务提供者？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory finding requires immediate notification to the healthcare provider?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪一项实验室发现需要立即通知医疗服务提供者？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates the 1200 laboratory results to monitor for severe adverse effects of propylthiouracil (PTU).","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士评估1200的实验室结果，以监测丙硫氧嘧啶 (PTU) 的严重不良反应。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_bun","en":"Blood urea nitrogen (BUN) of 18 mg/dL (6.4 mmol/L)","zh":"血尿素氮 (BUN) 18 mg/dL (6.4 mmol/L)"},{"id":"opt_k","en":"Serum potassium of 3.8 mEq/L (3.8 mmol/L)","zh":"血清钾 3.8 mEq/L (3.8 mmol/L)"},{"id":"opt_wbc","en":"White blood cell count of 2.8 ×10³/µL","zh":"白细胞计数 2.8 ×10³/µL"},{"id":"opt_t4","en":"Free T4 of 4.2 ng/dL","zh":"游离T4 4.2 ng/dL"}],"correct":["opt_wbc"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A severe and potentially fatal adverse effect of propylthiouracil (PTU) and methimazole is agranulocytosis (a profound drop in white blood cells, specifically neutrophils). A total WBC count of 2.8 ×10³/µL is abnormally low (leukopenia) and places the client at extreme risk for life-threatening sepsis, warranting immediate provider notification to stop the drug and implement reverse isolation. The potassium and BUN levels are within normal limits. The Free T4 remains elevated (normal 0.8-2.8 ng/dL); while abnormal, this is an expected finding at this stage, as it takes time for circulating hormone levels to fall even after synthesis and release are blocked.","rationaleCorrectZh":"丙硫氧嘧啶 (PTU) 和甲巯咪唑的一种严重且具有潜在致命性的不良反应是粒细胞缺乏症（白细胞特别是中性粒细胞大幅下降）。2.8 ×10³/µL 的白细胞总数异常偏低（白细胞减少症），使患者面临危及生命的败血症的极高风险，需要立即通知医生停药并实施保护性隔离。钾和BUN水平在正常范围内。游离T4仍然升高（正常值0.8-2.8 ng/dL）；虽然异常，但在这一阶段是预期的发现，因为即使合成和释放被阻断，循环中激素水平下降也需要时间。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When evaluating drug toxicity, look for the known severe complications. For antithyroid medications (PTU, methimazole), always monitor for signs of agranulocytosis (low WBC, fever, sore throat) and hepatotoxicity.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在评估药物毒性时，请寻找已知的严重并发症。对于抗甲状腺药物（PTU、甲巯咪唑），必须始终监测粒细胞缺乏症（白细胞低、发烧、喉咙痛）和肝毒性的迹象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2402,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.34","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.34.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[369,480],"terminalOffsetsZh":[103,134],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding Case: Acute Respiratory Distress A 74-year-old male with a history of chronic heart failure (ejection fraction 30%), hypertension, and atrial fibrillation presents to the emergency department with severe shortness of breath that started two hours ago. He states, \"I feel like I'm drowning.\" He reports having to sleep in his recliner for the past two nights. His wife notes that he has not been taking his furosemide for the past three days because he \"felt dehydrated.\"","fullStemZh":"展开案例：急性呼吸窘迫 一名74岁男性，有慢性心力衰竭（射血分数为30%）、高血压和心房颤动病史，因两小时前开始的严重呼吸短促来到急诊科。他说：“我感觉自己像在溺水。”他报告说过去两晚都不得不在躺椅上睡觉。他的妻子指出，过去三天他没有服用呋塞米，因为他“感觉脱水了”。","terminalSentenceEn":"His wife notes that he has not been taking his furosemide for the past three days because he \"felt dehydrated.\"","terminalSentenceZh":"他的妻子指出，过去三天他没有服用呋塞米，因为他“感觉脱水了”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"He reports having to sleep in his recliner for the past two nights.","penultimateSentenceZh":"他报告说过去两晚都不得不在躺椅上睡觉。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case study focuses on the assessment and immediate management of acute decompensated heart failure presenting as pulmonary edema. It requires the nurse to recognize critical cues, prioritize life-saving interventions based on pathophysiology, formulate a correct clinical hypothesis, and evaluate the direct effect of pharmacological therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例研究侧重于评估和即时管理表现为肺水肿的急性失代偿性心力衰竭。它要求护士识别关键线索，根据病理生理学优先安排救生干预措施，形成正确的临床假设，并评估药物治疗的直接效果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For high-acuity respiratory cases, always follow the sequence of assess, intervene, and evaluate. Prioritize interventions that provide the most immediate benefit to oxygenation and hemodynamics. When evaluating medication effects, link the assessment finding directly to the drug's mechanism of action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于高危呼吸系统病例，始终遵循评估、干预和评价的顺序。优先考虑对氧合和血流动力学提供最直接益处的干预措施。在评估药物效果时，将评估发现与药物的作用机制直接联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2403,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,40],"fullStemEn":"Which findings from the initial assessment are most indicative of acute decompensated heart failure with pulmonary edema? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"初步评估中的哪些发现最能表明患有急性失代偿性心力衰竭伴肺水肿？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings from the initial assessment are most indicative of acute decompensated heart failure with pulmonary edema?","penultimateSentenceZh":"初步评估中的哪些发现最能表明患有急性失代偿性心力衰竭伴肺水肿？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Tripod positioning","zh":"三脚架体位"},{"id":"A","en":"SpO2 of 85% on room air","zh":"室内空气下血氧饱和度为85%"},{"id":"E","en":"S3 gallop","zh":"S3奔马律"},{"id":"B","en":"Bilateral crackles","zh":"双侧湿啰音"},{"id":"C","en":"Blood pressure of 188/102 mmHg","zh":"血压188/102 mmHg"},{"id":"D","en":"History of atrial fibrillation","zh":"心房颤动病史"}],"correct":["A","B","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The classic signs of acute pulmonary edema, a life-threatening manifestation of ADHF, include severe dyspnea (leading to tripod positioning), hypoxemia (low SpO2), and diffuse crackles on auscultation due to fluid in the alveoli. An S3 gallop is a hallmark sign of fluid volume overload and failing left ventricular function. While hypertension is a common precipitating factor and atrial fibrillation is a common comorbidity, they are not as specific to the acute fluid shift into the lungs as the other findings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性肺水肿是ADHF危及生命的表现，其典型体征包括严重呼吸困难（导致三脚架体位）、低氧血症（低SpO2）以及因肺泡积液而在听诊时闻及的弥漫性湿啰音。 S3奔马律是液体容量超负荷和左心室功能衰竭的标志性体征。虽然高血压是常见的诱发因素，心房颤动是常见的合并症，但它们不像其他发现那样对肺部急性液体转移具有特异性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the most specific signs of the condition named in the question (pulmonary edema). Ask, 'Which of these findings directly points to fluid in the lungs or the heart's inability to handle volume?' A history item or a potential cause is less specific than a direct physical assessment finding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注问题中提到的病症（肺水肿）的最具体体征。问问自己，“这些发现中，哪一个直接指向肺部积液或心脏无法处理容量？”病史项目或潜在原因不如直接的体格检查发现具体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2404,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[66,141],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,36],"fullStemEn":"The nurse needs to take immediate action to stabilize the client. Place the following nursing interventions in the correct order of priority.","fullStemZh":"护士需要立即采取行动稳定客户。请将以下护理干预措施按正确的优先顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the following nursing interventions in the correct order of priority.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将以下护理干预措施按正确的优先顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse needs to take immediate action to stabilize the client.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士需要立即采取行动稳定客户。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Place the client in a high-Fowler's position.","zh":"将客户置于高福勒卧位。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen via a non-rebreather mask.","zh":"通过非再呼吸面罩给予补充氧气。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer intravenous furosemide.","zh":"静脉注射呋塞米。"},{"id":"D","en":"Establish intravenous access.","zh":"建立静脉通路。"}],"correct":["B","C","D","A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate priorities are to improve oxygenation and reduce the work of breathing. Placing the client upright (high-Fowler's) immediately reduces venous return to the heart and allows for better lung expansion. Applying oxygen addresses the severe hypoxemia. Establishing IV access is necessary before administering IV medications. Finally, administering a potent loop diuretic like furosemide is critical to remove excess fluid, but this requires IV access and follows the immediate stabilization of breathing.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当务之急是改善氧合和减少呼吸功。将客户置于直立位（高福勒卧位）可立即减少回心血量，并有助于更好的肺扩张。 给予氧气可解决严重的低氧血症。 在给予静脉药物之前，必须建立静脉通路。最后，给予像呋塞米这样的强效袢利尿剂对于清除多余液体至关重要，但这需要静脉通路，并且是在呼吸初步稳定之后进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In acute respiratory distress, always prioritize the least invasive and fastest-acting interventions first. Positioning and oxygen are immediate. Then, prepare for medications (IV access) before administering them. Think 'Airway, Breathing, Circulation' but apply it practically: improve breathing with position/O2, then address circulation with meds.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在急性呼吸窘迫中，始终优先考虑侵入性最小、起效最快的干预措施。体位和氧气是立即可行的。然后，在给药前准备好药物（静脉通路）。思考“气道、呼吸、循环”，但要实际应用：通过体位/氧气改善呼吸，然后用药物处理循环问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2405,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[48,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,30],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is formulating a clinical hypothesis. Complete the following sentence by choosing from the dropdown options.","fullStemZh":"护士正在形成一个临床假设。请从下拉选项中选择，完成以下句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the following sentence by choosing from the dropdown options.","terminalSentenceZh":"请从下拉选项中选择，完成以下句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is formulating a clinical hypothesis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在形成一个临床假设。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is most likely experiencing {{1}} as a result of {{2}}.","zh":"该客户最有可能正在经历 {{1}}，这是由于 {{2}} 的结果。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"a pulmonary embolism","zh":"肺栓塞"},{"id":"o1","en":"cardiogenic pulmonary edema","zh":"心源性肺水肿"},{"id":"o2","en":"an acute asthma exacerbation","zh":"急性哮喘发作"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"an allergic reaction","zh":"过敏反应"},{"id":"o1","en":"medication non-adherence","zh":"药物不依从性"},{"id":"o2","en":"a primary respiratory infection","zh":"原发性呼吸道感染"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client's history of severe heart failure, combined with classic signs of fluid overload (S3, edema, crackles, orthopnea) and the reported non-adherence with his diuretic medication, strongly supports the diagnosis of cardiogenic pulmonary edema. The lack of fever or productive cough makes infection less likely, and the bilateral nature of the findings is not typical for a pulmonary embolism.","rationaleCorrectZh":"客户的严重心力衰竭病史，结合液体超负荷的典型体征（S3、水肿、湿啰音、端坐呼吸）以及报告的利尿剂药物不依从性，有力地支持了心源性肺水肿的诊断。没有发烧或咳痰使得感染的可能性较小，而发现的双侧性特征对于肺栓塞来说并不典型。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For cloze items, evaluate each dropdown independently first, then read the completed sentence to ensure it makes clinical sense. Use the case data to support your choices. The client's history (CHF) and the precipitating event (stopped furosemide) are the key clues here.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于完形填空题，首先独立评估每个下拉选项，然后阅读完整的句子以确保其在临床上合理。使用案例数据来支持您的选择。客户的病史（CHF）和诱发事件（停用呋塞米）是这里的关键线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2406,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_adhf_pulm_edema_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,154],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"After administering 80 mg of intravenous furosemide, which assessment finding would be the most reliable indicator that the medication has been effective?","fullStemZh":"在静脉注射80毫克呋塞米后，哪项评估发现是表明药物有效的最可靠指标？","terminalSentenceEn":"After administering 80 mg of intravenous furosemide, which assessment finding would be the most reliable indicator that the medication has been effective?","terminalSentenceZh":"在静脉注射80毫克呋塞米后，哪项评估发现是表明药物有效的最可靠指标？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"The client's heart rate decreases to 110 beats/minute.","zh":"客户的心率降至110次/分钟。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client has a urine output of 400 mL in the first hour.","zh":"客户在第一个小时内的尿量为400毫升。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client's blood pressure decreases to 150/88 mmHg.","zh":"客户的血压降至150/88 mmHg。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client reports a decrease in anxiety.","zh":"客户报告焦虑减轻。"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Furosemide is a loop diuretic that works by inhibiting water reabsorption in the nephron, leading to significant diuresis. The primary therapeutic effect in pulmonary edema is the rapid removal of excess fluid from the body. Therefore, a brisk and significant increase in urine output is the most direct and reliable indicator of the drug's effectiveness. While other parameters may improve as a consequence of diuresis, they are secondary effects.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呋塞米是一种袢利尿剂，通过抑制肾单位对水的重吸收而起作用，导致显著的利尿。在肺水肿中，其主要治疗效果是快速清除体内多余的液体。因此，尿量迅速而显著的增加是药物有效性的最直接、最可靠的指标。虽然其他参数可能因利尿而改善，但它们是次要效应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When evaluating the effectiveness of a medication, focus on its primary mechanism of action. What is the drug supposed to do? For a diuretic, the answer is 'produce urine.' Look for the option that directly measures this primary effect.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在评估药物的有效性时，请关注其主要作用机制。这种药应该做什么？对于利尿剂，答案是“产生尿液”。寻找直接衡量这种主要效果的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2407,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.35","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.35.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[232,331],"terminalOffsetsZh":[63,91],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding Case: Sudden Cardiac Arrest A 62-year-old female client is brought to the emergency department by emergency medical services after experiencing sudden, crushing substernal chest pain that radiates to her left jaw and arm. She is visibly diaphoretic, clutching her chest, and reports severe nausea and shortness of breath.","fullStemZh":"展开案例：突发心脏骤停 一名62岁女性客户在经历突然的、压榨性的胸骨后疼痛（放射至左下颌和手臂）后，由紧急医疗服务送至急诊科。她明显大汗淋漓，紧捂胸口，并报告有严重的恶心和呼吸短促。","terminalSentenceEn":"She is visibly diaphoretic, clutching her chest, and reports severe nausea and shortness of breath.","terminalSentenceZh":"她明显大汗淋漓，紧捂胸口，并报告有严重的恶心和呼吸短促。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding Case: Sudden Cardiac Arrest A 62-year-old female client is brought to the emergency department by emergency medical services after experiencing sudden, crushing substernal chest pain that radiates to her left jaw and arm.","penultimateSentenceZh":"展开案例：突发心脏骤停 一名62岁女性客户在经历突然的、压榨性的胸骨后疼痛（放射至左下颌和手臂）后，由紧急医疗服务送至急诊科。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This unfolding case study tests the nurse's ability to recognize the classic presentation of an acute myocardial infarction, anticipate its most lethal complication (ventricular fibrillation), and execute the strict, time-sensitive ACLS algorithms for defibrillation and pharmacological resuscitation while accurately evaluating the physiological markers of success.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这个展开式案例研究测试了护士识别急性心肌梗死典型表现的能力，预期其最致命并发症（心室颤动）的能力，以及执行严格的、对时间敏感的 ACLS 除颤和药物复苏算法的能力，同时准确评估成功的生理标志物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In cardiac arrest scenarios, prioritize actions that directly restore perfusion. For V-Fib, electricity (defibrillation) is the cure, and CPR buys time. Medications are secondary. Always look for objective signs of perfusion (like PETCO2 or a palpable pulse) to confirm ROSC, not just a rhythm on the screen.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在心脏骤停场景中，优先考虑直接恢复灌注的操作。对于室颤，电击（除颤）是治愈方法，而 CPR 争取时间。药物是次要的。始终寻找灌注的客观体征（如 PETCO2 或可触及的脉搏）来确认 ROSC，而不仅仅是屏幕上的节律。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2408,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[183,205],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,47],"fullStemEn":"Based on the initial triage assessment, which of the following clinical findings strongly suggest an acute myocardial infarction accompanied by sympathetic nervous system activation? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"根据初步分诊评估，以下哪些临床发现强烈提示急性心肌梗死伴有交感神经系统激活？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Based on the initial triage assessment, which of the following clinical findings strongly suggest an acute myocardial infarction accompanied by sympathetic nervous system activation?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据初步分诊评估，以下哪些临床发现强烈提示急性心肌梗死伴有交感神经系统激活？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"A resting heart rate of 110 beats/minute.","zh":"静息心率为 110 次/分钟。"},{"id":"C","en":"ST-segment elevation in leads V1 through V4.","zh":"导联 V1 至 V4 的 ST 段抬高。"},{"id":"B","en":"Visible, profuse diaphoresis.","zh":"可见的、大量的大汗淋漓。"},{"id":"E","en":"An oxygen saturation of 92% on room air.","zh":"室内空气下血氧饱和度为 92%。"},{"id":"A","en":"Crushing substernal chest pain radiating to the jaw.","zh":"压榨性胸骨后疼痛放射至下颌。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Crushing chest pain radiating to the jaw is the classic ischemic symptom of a myocardial infarction. ST-segment elevation in V1-V4 provides definitive electrocardiographic evidence of an acute anterior wall STEMI. Diaphoresis and tachycardia (HR 110) are direct results of the body's massive sympathetic nervous system (fight-or-flight) response to severe pain and decreased cardiac output. While the SpO2 of 92% is slightly low and warrants oxygen therapy, it is a secondary finding of mild hypoxia, not a direct indicator of sympathetic activation or the infarction itself.","rationaleCorrectZh":"放射至下颌的压榨性胸痛是心肌梗死的典型缺血症状。V1-V4 的 ST 段抬高提供了急性前壁 STEMI 的确切心电图证据。大汗淋漓和心动过速（心率 110）是身体对剧烈疼痛和心输出量减少产生的大量交感神经系统（战斗或逃跑）反应的直接结果。虽然 92% 的 SpO2 略低且需要氧疗，但它是轻度缺氧的次要发现，而不是交感神经激活或梗死本身的直接指标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Break the question into two parts: signs of an MI AND signs of sympathetic activation. Chest pain and ST elevation confirm the MI. Sweating and a fast heart rate confirm the sympathetic 'fight-or-flight' adrenaline surge that accompanies the severe stress of a heart attack.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将问题分为两部分：心肌梗死的体征和交感神经激活的体征。胸痛和 ST 段抬高证实了心肌梗死。出汗和心率加快证实了伴随心脏病发作严重压力的交感神经“战斗或逃跑”肾上腺素激增。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2409,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,41],"fullStemEn":"The client suddenly becomes unresponsive with a chaotic rhythm on the monitor. Arrange the following emergency nursing actions in the most appropriate sequential order.","fullStemZh":"客户突然变得无意识，监护仪上显示混乱的节律。请按最合适的顺序排列以下紧急护理操作。","terminalSentenceEn":"Arrange the following emergency nursing actions in the most appropriate sequential order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按最合适的顺序排列以下紧急护理操作。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client suddenly becomes unresponsive with a chaotic rhythm on the monitor.","penultimateSentenceZh":"客户突然变得无意识，监护仪上显示混乱的节律。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Prepare to administer intravenous epinephrine 1 mg.","zh":"准备静脉注射 1 mg 肾上腺素。"},{"id":"A","en":"Call for the resuscitation team and a defibrillator.","zh":"呼叫复苏团队并要求提供除颤器。"},{"id":"C","en":"Deliver an unsynchronized electrical shock (defibrillation).","zh":"进行非同步电击（除颤）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Initiate high-quality cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) starting with chest compressions.","zh":"开始高质量的心肺复苏 (CPR)，从胸外按压开始。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to Basic Life Support (BLS) and Advanced Cardiovascular Life Support (ACLS) guidelines, the first action upon discovering an unresponsive pulseless client is to call for help and a defibrillator. Immediately after calling for help, the nurse must start high-quality CPR (chest compressions) to maintain minimal perfusion to the brain and heart. As soon as the defibrillator arrives and ventricular fibrillation is confirmed, an unsynchronized shock must be delivered, as early defibrillation is the only definitive treatment for V-Fib. Following the shock, CPR is immediately resumed, and pharmacological interventions like epinephrine are prepared and administered.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据基础生命支持 (BLS) 和高级心血管生命支持 (ACLS) 指南，发现无意识且无脉搏的客户时，第一步操作是呼救并要求提供除颤器。呼救后，护士必须立即开始高质量的 CPR（胸外按压），以维持大脑和心脏的最低灌注。一旦除颤器到达并确认是心室颤动，必须立即进行非同步电击，因为早期除颤是治疗室颤的唯一确切方法。电击后，立即恢复 CPR，并准备和施用肾上腺素等药物干预措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Follow the strict AHA BLS/ACLS algorithm for a witnessed cardiac arrest: 1. Recognize/Call for help. 2. Start CPR. 3. Defibrillate (for VF/pVT). 4. Medications (Epinephrine/Amiodarone). Never delay CPR or defibrillation to draw up medications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遵循美国心脏协会 (AHA) BLS/ACLS 针对目击心脏骤停的严格算法：1. 识别/呼救。2. 开始 CPR。3. 除颤（针对室颤/无脉性室速）。4. 药物治疗（肾上腺素/胺碘酮）。切勿为了抽取药物而延迟 CPR 或除颤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2410,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[118,186],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,42],"fullStemEn":"The resuscitation team is utilizing multiple pharmacological agents during the cardiac arrest and peri-arrest period. Match each medication to its primary pharmacological classification.","fullStemZh":"复苏团队在心脏骤停及围骤停期使用了多种药物。请将每种药物与其主要的药理学分类相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each medication to its primary pharmacological classification.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每种药物与其主要的药理学分类相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The resuscitation team is utilizing multiple pharmacological agents during the cardiac arrest and peri-arrest period.","penultimateSentenceZh":"复苏团队在心脏骤停及围骤停期使用了多种药物。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Amiodarone","zh":"胺碘酮"},{"id":"r2","en":"Epinephrine","zh":"肾上腺素"},{"id":"r3","en":"Aspirin","zh":"阿司匹林"},{"id":"r4","en":"Nitroglycerin","zh":"硝酸甘油"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Vasodilator","zh":"血管扩张剂"},{"id":"c4","en":"Antiarrhythmic","zh":"抗心律失常药"},{"id":"c1","en":"Antiplatelet Agent","zh":"抗血小板药"},{"id":"c3","en":"Vasopressor","zh":"血管加压药"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c4"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Amiodarone is a class III antiarrhythmic used in ACLS to treat refractory ventricular fibrillation and ventricular tachycardia. Epinephrine is a potent vasopressor (alpha- and beta-agonist) given during cardiac arrest to increase aortic diastolic pressure and coronary perfusion. Aspirin is an antiplatelet agent given early in acute coronary syndrome to prevent further clot aggregation in the coronary arteries. Nitroglycerin is a vasodilator used to reduce preload and myocardial oxygen demand, relieving ischemic chest pain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胺碘酮是 ACLS 中用于治疗难治性心室颤动和室性心动过速的 III 类抗心律失常药。肾上腺素是一种强效血管加压药（α 和 β 激动剂），在心脏骤停期间给药以增加主动脉舒张压和冠状动脉灌注。阿司匹林是一种抗血小板药，在急性冠脉综合征早期给药，以防止冠状动脉内血栓进一步聚集。硝酸甘油是一种血管扩张剂，用于降低前负荷和心肌耗氧量，缓解缺血性胸痛。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Group cardiac medications by their primary mechanism. Epinephrine squeezes vessels (pressor). Nitro opens vessels (dilator). Aspirin makes blood slippery (antiplatelet). Amiodarone fixes the electrical rhythm (antiarrhythmic).","testTakingStrategyZh":"按主要机制对心脏药物进行分组。肾上腺素挤压血管（加压药）。硝酸甘油打开血管（扩张剂）。阿司匹林使血液变滑（抗血小板药）。胺碘酮修复电节律（抗心律失常药）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2411,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_stemi_vfib_04_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,54],"fullStemEn":"During the resuscitation effort, the nurse continuously monitors the client's physiological responses. Which specific clinical finding provides the most definitive evidence of the return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC)?","fullStemZh":"在复苏过程中，护士持续监测客户的生理反应。哪项具体的临床发现提供了恢复自主循环 (ROSC) 的最确凿证据？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which specific clinical finding provides the most definitive evidence of the return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC)?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项具体的临床发现提供了恢复自主循环 (ROSC) 的最确凿证据？","penultimateSentenceEn":"During the resuscitation effort, the nurse continuously monitors the client's physiological responses.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在复苏过程中，护士持续监测客户的生理反应。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The appearance of an organized sinus rhythm on the cardiac monitor without a palpable pulse.","zh":"心电监护仪上出现有组织的窦性心律，但无触及脉搏。"},{"id":"C","en":"Bilateral pupillary dilation and unresponsiveness to light.","zh":"双侧瞳孔散大且对光无反应。"},{"id":"D","en":"The presence of occasional, irregular gasping respirations (agonal breathing).","zh":"出现偶尔的、不规则的喘息样呼吸（濒死呼吸）。"},{"id":"A","en":"An abrupt and sustained increase in PETCO2 (end-tidal carbon dioxide) to 40 mmHg.","zh":"PETCO2（呼气末二氧化碳）突然且持续地增加至 40 mmHg。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"An abrupt and sustained increase in end-tidal carbon dioxide (PETCO2), typically to a normal value of 35-40 mmHg, is the earliest and most reliable non-invasive indicator of Return of Spontaneous Circulation (ROSC). During cardiac arrest, PETCO2 is low because blood is not circulating to the lungs to release CO2. When the heart restarts and cardiac output is restored, accumulated CO2 is suddenly washed out of the tissues and delivered to the lungs, causing a sharp spike on the capnography monitor. This often occurs even before a pulse can be reliably palpated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"呼气末二氧化碳 (PETCO2) 突然且持续地增加（通常达到 35-40 mmHg 的正常值）是恢复自主循环 (ROSC) 最早、最可靠的无创指标。在心脏骤停期间，PETCO2 很低，因为血液没有循环到肺部释放 CO2。当心脏重新启动并恢复心输出量时，积聚的 CO2 突然从组织中被冲刷出来并输送到肺部，导致二氧化碳波形图监护仪上出现急剧的峰值。这通常甚至在能够可靠地触及脉搏之前发生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that the monitor lies, but perfusion does not. An ECG rhythm does not guarantee a pulse (PEA). However, a sudden jump in exhaled CO2 (PETCO2) proves that blood is actively moving from the tissues to the lungs, which only happens if the heart is pumping.","testTakingStrategyZh":"请记住，监护仪会说谎，但灌注不会。心电图节律不能保证有脉搏 (PEA)。然而，呼出 CO2 (PETCO2) 的突然跳跃证明血液正在积极地从组织流向肺部，这只有在心脏泵血时才会发生。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2412,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.36","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.36.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[307,416],"terminalOffsetsZh":[85,104],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding Case: Deterioration in an Older Adult An 82-year-old female with a history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and recurrent urinary tract infections (UTIs) is brought to the emergency department by her daughter, who reports the client has been increasingly confused and lethargic over the past 24 hours. The daughter also notes the client has had a decreased urine output and has not been eating or drinking well.","fullStemZh":"展开案例：一名老年成年人的病情恶化 一名82岁女性，有2型糖尿病和复发性尿路感染（UTI）病史，由其女儿送至急诊科。女儿报告说，在过去24小时内，该客户越来越困惑和嗜睡。女儿还注意到客户的尿量减少，饮食不佳。","terminalSentenceEn":"The daughter also notes the client has had a decreased urine output and has not been eating or drinking well.","terminalSentenceZh":"女儿还注意到客户的尿量减少，饮食不佳。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding Case: Deterioration in an Older Adult An 82-year-old female with a history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and recurrent urinary tract infections (UTIs) is brought to the emergency department by her daughter, who reports the client has been increasingly confused and lethargic over the past 24 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"女儿报告说，在过去24小时内，该客户越来越困惑和嗜睡。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case illustrates the rapid identification and management of septic shock, emphasizing the progression from recognizing SIRS and organ dysfunction to implementing time-sensitive, prioritized interventions according to evidence-based guidelines, and finally, evaluating the response to complex pharmacotherapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例展示了脓毒性休克的快速识别和管理，强调了从识别SIRS和器官功能障碍，到根据循证指南实施有时间敏感性的、优先的干预措施，最后评估对复杂药物治疗反应的整个过程。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding case studies, track the client's data over time. Notice how the initial assessment findings (cues) lead to a hypothesis (sepsis), which is then confirmed by labs and worsening vitals (analysis), prompting a specific sequence of actions (intervention) whose effectiveness is then measured by specific endpoints (evaluation).","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式案例研究中，要随时间追踪客户的数据。注意最初的评估发现（线索）如何导出一个假设（脓毒症），然后通过实验室检查和恶化的生命体征（分析）得到证实，从而促使采取一系列特定的行动（干预），其有效性再通过特定的终点（评估）来衡量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Unfolding Case: Deterioration in an Older Adult An 82-year-old female with a history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and recurrent urinary tract infections (UTIs) is brought to the emergency department by her daughter, who reports the client has been increasingly confused and lethargic over the past 24 hours.","controlSentenceZh":"女儿报告说，在过去24小时内，该客户越来越困惑和嗜睡。"}
{"queueIndex":2413,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01_part_1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,81],"fullStemEn":"Based on the initial triage assessment at 1400, for each finding, click to specify if it is consistent with classic SIRS criteria (a foundational infection-response framework still tested on the NCLEX-RN), organ dysfunction, or neither.","fullStemZh":"根据1400时的初步分诊评估，对于每项发现，请点击指明其是否符合经典SIRS标准（一个在NCLEX-RN中仍会考核的基础性感染反应框架）、器官功能障碍或两者皆非。","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the initial triage assessment at 1400, for each finding, click to specify if it is consistent with classic SIRS criteria (a foundational infection-response framework still tested on the NCLEX-RN), organ dysfunction, or neither.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据1400时的初步分诊评估，对于每项发现，请点击指明其是否符合经典SIRS标准（一个在NCLEX-RN中仍会考核的基础性感染反应框架）、器官功能障碍或两者皆非。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Temperature 102.0 °F (38.9 °C)","zh":"体温 102.0 °F (38.9 °C)"},{"id":"r2","en":"Heart Rate 118 beats/minute","zh":"心率 118次/分钟"},{"id":"r3","en":"Blood Pressure 94/52 mmHg","zh":"血压 94/52 mmHg"},{"id":"r4","en":"Altered mental status","zh":"精神状态改变"},{"id":"r5","en":"History of type 2 diabetes","zh":"2型糖尿病史"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Consistent with Organ Dysfunction","zh":"符合器官功能障碍"},{"id":"c1","en":"Consistent with Classic SIRS Criteria","zh":"符合经典SIRS标准"},{"id":"c3","en":"Neither","zh":"两者皆非"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client's fever, tachycardia, and tachypnea meet the criteria for SIRS. Hypotension and altered mental status are critical indicators of sepsis-induced organ dysfunction, signifying progression towards septic shock. The history of diabetes is a risk factor for infection but is not a direct finding of the current inflammatory response or organ failure. Note: The Sepsis-3 consensus (2016) defines sepsis by organ dysfunction rather than requiring SIRS criteria, using SOFA/qSOFA scoring. SIRS remains foundational for NCLEX-RN education and continues to appear in entry-level nursing curricula.","rationaleCorrectZh":"客户的发烧、心动过速和呼吸急促符合SIRS的标准。低血压和精神状态改变是脓毒症引起的器官功能障碍的关键指标，标志着病情正向脓毒性休克发展。糖尿病史是感染的风险因素，但不是当前炎症反应或器官衰竭的直接发现。注意：Sepsis-3共识（2016年）以器官功能障碍（SOFA/qSOFA评分）而非SIRS标准定义脓毒症。SIRS仍是NCLEX-RN护理教育的基础内容，在初级护理课程中继续出现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the definition of SIRS (systemic inflammation) and severe sepsis (inflammation plus organ dysfunction). SIRS criteria are specific vital sign and lab value thresholds. Organ dysfunction involves signs of failure in specific body systems (e.g., brain, kidneys, cardiovascular).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分SIRS（全身性炎症）和严重脓毒症（炎症加器官功能障碍）的定义。SIRS标准是特定的生命体征和实验室数值阈值。器官功能障碍涉及特定身体系统（如大脑、肾脏、心血管）衰竭的迹象。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2414,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01_part_2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[116,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,41],"fullStemEn":"The provider has confirmed septic shock. The nurse should anticipate performing which actions in order of priority? Drag and drop the options into the correct sequence.","fullStemZh":"医生已确认脓毒性休克。护士应按优先顺序预期执行哪些操作？将选项拖放到正确的顺序中。","terminalSentenceEn":"Drag and drop the options into the correct sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"将选项拖放到正确的顺序中。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse should anticipate performing which actions in order of priority?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按优先顺序预期执行哪些操作？","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer broad-spectrum antibiotics intravenously.","zh":"静脉注射广谱抗生素。"},{"id":"C","en":"Initiate a rapid intravenous fluid bolus of 30 mL/kg.","zh":"开始快速静脉输注30 mL/kg的液体。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare to administer a vasopressor infusion (e.g., norepinephrine).","zh":"准备给予血管加压药输注（如去甲肾上腺素）。"},{"id":"B","en":"Obtain blood and urine cultures.","zh":"获取血培养和尿培养。"}],"correct":["C","B","A","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The highest priority in septic shock is to restore tissue perfusion and intravascular volume, which is achieved by aggressive fluid resuscitation. Cultures must be obtained before starting antibiotics to identify the pathogen, but this should not delay treatment. Antibiotics should be administered within the first hour. Vasopressors are used after initial fluid resuscitation if hypotension persists, to maintain a target MAP of ≥ 65 mmHg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脓毒性休克的最高优先级是恢复组织灌注和血管内容量，这通过积极的液体复苏来实现。 必须在开始使用抗生素之前获取培养物以鉴定病原体，但这不应延迟治疗。抗生素应在第一个小时内给予。 如果低血压在初步液体复苏后持续存在，则使用血管加压药以维持≥ 65 mmHg的目标平均动脉压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For prioritization questions in shock states, follow the general principle of Circulation, Airway, Breathing, but apply it to the pathophysiology. In distributive shock like sepsis, restoring circulation (volume) is the most immediate life-saving action. Then, address the cause (infection) and use medications for refractory issues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于休克状态下的优先排序问题，请遵循循环、气道、呼吸的一般原则，但要将其应用于病理生理学。在像脓毒症这样的分布性休克中，恢复循环（容量）是最直接的救生措施。然后，处理病因（感染）并使用药物治疗难治性问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2415,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01_part_3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[180,202],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,57],"fullStemEn":"After two hours of aggressive fluid resuscitation and initiation of antibiotics and a norepinephrine infusion, which of the following findings would indicate clinical improvement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"经过两小时的积极液体复苏、开始使用抗生素和去甲肾上腺素输注后，以下哪些发现表明临床状况有所改善？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"After two hours of aggressive fluid resuscitation and initiation of antibiotics and a norepinephrine infusion, which of the following findings would indicate clinical improvement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"经过两小时的积极液体复苏、开始使用抗生素和去甲肾上腺素输注后，以下哪些发现表明临床状况有所改善？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Lactate level has decreased to 2.0 mmol/L.","zh":"乳酸水平已降至2.0 mmol/L。"},{"id":"E","en":"Skin is cool and clammy.","zh":"皮肤湿冷。"},{"id":"B","en":"Urine output is 40 mL/hour.","zh":"尿量为40 mL/小时。"},{"id":"F","en":"Serum creatinine remains 1.8 mg/dL.","zh":"血清肌酐仍为1.8 mg/dL。"},{"id":"A","en":"Mean arterial pressure (MAP) is 70 mmHg.","zh":"平均动脉压（MAP）为70 mmHg。"},{"id":"C","en":"Client is now oriented to person and place.","zh":"客户现在对人和地点有定向力。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Positive outcomes in septic shock management are indicated by improved organ perfusion. This is evidenced by a MAP ≥ 65 mmHg, adequate urine output (≥ 0.5 mL/kg/hr or >30 mL/hr), improved mental status, and clearance of lactate. Cool, clammy skin suggests worsening shock (compensatory vasoconstriction). A stable but still elevated creatinine does not yet show improvement in renal function.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脓毒性休克管理的积极结果表现为器官灌注的改善。这可以通过MAP ≥ 65 mmHg、足够的尿量（≥ 0.5 mL/kg/hr 或 >30 mL/hr）、改善的精神状态和乳酸清除来证明。湿冷的皮肤表明休克恶化（代偿性血管收缩）。稳定但仍升高的肌酐尚未显示肾功能改善。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For 'evaluate outcomes' questions, think about the goals of the interventions. The goal of sepsis treatment is to restore perfusion. Ask yourself, 'Which of these findings shows that blood is getting to the organs (brain, kidneys, skin) and that cells are getting enough oxygen (lactate)?'","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于“评估结果”类问题，请考虑干预措施的目标。脓毒症治疗的目标是恢复灌注。问问自己，“这些发现中，哪一个表明血液正在到达器官（大脑、肾脏、皮肤），并且细胞获得了足够的氧气（乳酸）？”","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2416,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01","embeddedQuestionId":"cs_sepsis_shock_01_part_4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[141,221],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,85],"fullStemEn":"The client's MAP remains 60 mmHg despite receiving norepinephrine at 10 mcg/min. The provider orders the addition of a vasopressin infusion. What is the primary rationale for adding vasopressin in this clinical situation?","fullStemZh":"尽管接受了10 mcg/min的去甲肾上腺素，客户的平均动脉压（MAP）仍为60 mmHg。医生下令加用血管加压素输注。在这种临床情况下，加用血管加压素的主要理由是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the primary rationale for adding vasopressin in this clinical situation?","terminalSentenceZh":"在这种临床情况下，加用血管加压素的主要理由是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider orders the addition of a vasopressin infusion.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医生下令加用血管加压素输注。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"To replace the body's depleted endogenous stores in a shock state.","zh":"补充休克状态下身体耗尽的内源性储备。"},{"id":"B","en":"To allow for a lower dose of norepinephrine, reducing the risk of peripheral ischemia.","zh":"允许使用较低剂量的去甲肾上腺素，从而降低外周缺血的风险。"},{"id":"C","en":"To directly stimulate beta-1 receptors and increase the heart rate.","zh":"直接刺激β-1受体，增加心率。"},{"id":"A","en":"To provide a potent inotropic effect and increase cardiac contractility.","zh":"提供强效的正性肌力作用，增加心肌收缩力。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In septic shock, there is profound vasodilation. Vasopressin is a non-catecholamine vasopressor that acts on V1 receptors, causing vasoconstriction through a different mechanism than norepinephrine (an alpha-agonist). Adding vasopressin can have a synergistic effect, raising blood pressure and allowing the dose of norepinephrine to be reduced. High doses of norepinephrine are associated with significant adverse effects, including severe peripheral vasoconstriction, tachyarrhythmias, and myocardial ischemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在脓毒性休克中，存在严重的血管舒张。血管加压素是一种非儿茶酚胺类血管加压药，作用于V1受体，通过与去甲肾上腺素（一种α-激动剂）不同的机制引起血管收缩。加用血管加压素可以产生协同效应，升高血压，并允许减少去甲肾上腺素的剂量。高剂量的去甲肾上腺素与显著的不良反应相关，包括严重的外周血管收缩、快速性心律失常和心肌缺血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When multiple vasopressors are used, consider their different mechanisms of action. Norepinephrine is a primary alpha-agonist. Adding another agent like vasopressin suggests a need for a different pathway to achieve vasoconstriction, often to reduce the side effects of the primary agent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当使用多种血管加压药时，请考虑它们不同的作用机制。去甲肾上腺素是主要的α-激动剂。添加像血管加压素这样的另一种药物，表明需要通过不同的途径来实现血管收缩，通常是为了减少主要药物的副作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2417,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.37","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.37.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1898,2017],"terminalOffsetsZh":[576,608],"fullStemEn":"Spinal cord compression from metastatic cancer A 61-year-old woman with a three-year history of stage IV non-small cell lung cancer with known osseous metastases to the thoracic spine (T6, T8) and ribs is admitted to the oncology unit from the emergency department. She was diagnosed with bone metastases eight months ago and has been receiving palliative radiation and systemic therapy. She has a history of well-controlled hypertension managed with amlodipine 5 mg daily and a 30-pack-year smoking history. Home medications include dexamethasone 4 mg PO daily (recently tapered from a higher dose after her last radiation cycle), oxycodone 10 mg PO every 6 hours as needed for back pain, ondansetron 4 mg PO every 8 hours as needed, enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneous daily for VTE prophylaxis, and a bisphosphonate infusion monthly. She presents because her back pain has changed in character and intensity over the past 48 hours, and she is having new difficulty walking. Current admission orders include IV normal saline at 75 mL/hr, continuation of home medications, neurological checks every 4 hours, fall precautions, and a stat MRI of the entire spine with and without contrast.\n\nThe patient reports that her usual mid-thoracic back pain, which she describes as a dull ache rated 4 out of 10 and typically relieved by oxycodone, has escalated over the past two days to a sharp, band-like pain across her mid-back radiating around both flanks, now rated 8 out of 10 and no longer relieved by her usual oxycodone dose. She states that this morning she noticed her legs felt \"heavy and clumsy\" when she tried to walk to the bathroom, and she stumbled twice. She denies any recent falls or trauma. She appears anxious and is lying very still in bed, reluctant to move because movement worsens the pain. She says she has not had a bowel movement in three days but attributes this to her opioid use. She notes that when she urinated this morning, the stream seemed weak and she felt she did not fully empty her bladder.","fullStemZh":"转移性癌症引起的脊髓压迫 一名61岁女性，有3年IV期非小细胞肺癌病史，已知有胸椎（T6、T8）和肋骨骨转移，从急诊科收治入肿瘤科病房。她在8个月前被诊断出骨转移，并一直接受姑息性放疗和全身治疗。她有高血压病史，控制良好，每天口服氨氯地平5 mg，并有30包·年的吸烟史。家庭用药包括每天口服地塞米松4 mg（最近一次放疗周期后从较高剂量逐渐减量）、必要时每6小时口服羟考酮10 mg缓解背痛、必要时每8小时口服昂丹司琼4 mg、每天皮下注射依诺肝素40 mg预防静脉血栓栓塞，以及每月输注一次双膦酸盐。她因过去48小时内背痛的性质和强度发生变化，并新出现行走困难而就诊。目前的入院医嘱包括静脉滴注生理盐水75 mL/hr、继续使用家庭药物、每4小时进行一次神经系统检查、采取防跌倒措施，以及立即进行全脊柱平扫及增强MRI检查。\n\n患者报告，她通常的胸椎中段背痛（她描述为钝痛，评分为4/10，通常可通过羟考酮缓解）在过去两天里加剧为横跨背部中段并放射至双侧侧腹的锐利带状疼痛，目前评分为8/10，且不再能通过通常剂量的羟考酮缓解。她表示今天早上试图走到卫生间时，觉得双腿“沉重且笨拙”，并绊倒了两次。她否认近期有任何跌倒或外伤史。她显得焦虑，非常安静地躺在床上，不愿移动，因为移动会加重疼痛。她说自己已经三天没有排便，但她将此归因于使用了阿片类药物。她注意到今天早上排尿时，尿流似乎很细，并且感觉膀胱没有完全排空。","terminalSentenceEn":"She notes that when she urinated this morning, the stream seemed weak and she felt she did not fully empty her bladder.","terminalSentenceZh":"她注意到今天早上排尿时，尿流似乎很细，并且感觉膀胱没有完全排空。","penultimateSentenceEn":"She says she has not had a bowel movement in three days but attributes this to her opioid use.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她说自己已经三天没有排便，但她将此归因于使用了阿片类药物。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case study focuses on the recognition and nursing management of malignant spinal cord compression (MSCC) in an oncology patient. Prompt identification and emergent pharmacological and surgical interventions are critical to preventing permanent neurological loss.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例分析侧重于肿瘤患者恶性脊髓压迫（MSCC）的识别和护理管理。及时识别并进行紧急药物和手术干预对于预防永久性神经功能丧失至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read the entire case sequentially. Note the trajectory of neurological findings, as decisions depend on recognizing the pattern of decline or improvement over time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按顺序阅读整个病例。注意神经系统发现的变化轨迹，因为决策取决于识别随时间推移的病情恶化或改善模式。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2418,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[51,239],"terminalOffsetsZh":[12,66],"fullStemEn":"Review the patient's baseline assessment findings. The nurse should recognize that the combination of escalating mid-back pain, new bilateral leg weakness, and sensory/bladder changes is most highly suggestive of which oncologic emergency?","fullStemZh":"查阅患者的基线评估结果。护士应认识到，背部中段疼痛加剧、新发双侧下肢无力以及感觉/膀胱改变的综合表现，最强烈提示以下哪种肿瘤科急症？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should recognize that the combination of escalating mid-back pain, new bilateral leg weakness, and sensory/bladder changes is most highly suggestive of which oncologic emergency?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应认识到，背部中段疼痛加剧、新发双侧下肢无力以及感觉/膀胱改变的综合表现，最强烈提示以下哪种肿瘤科急症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the patient's baseline assessment findings.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查阅患者的基线评估结果。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_c","en":"Opioid-induced neurotoxicity","zh":"阿片类药物引起的神经毒性"},{"id":"opt_a","en":"Malignant spinal cord compression","zh":"恶性脊髓压迫"},{"id":"opt_d","en":"Paraneoplastic cerebellar degeneration","zh":"副肿瘤性小脑变性"},{"id":"opt_b","en":"Hypercalcemia of malignancy","zh":"恶性高钙血症"}],"correct":["opt_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The combination of escalating back pain at the level of known metastases, new motor weakness with upper motor neuron signs (hyperreflexia, positive Babinski), a definable sensory level, and autonomic (bladder) dysfunction is the classic presentation of malignant spinal cord compression. This is an oncologic emergency requiring urgent intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"已知转移病灶水平的背痛加剧、伴有上运动神经元体征（反射亢进、巴宾斯基征阳性）的新发运动无力、明确的感觉平面以及自主神经（膀胱）功能障碍的综合表现，是恶性脊髓压迫的典型表现。这是一种需要紧急干预的肿瘤科急症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that a distinct sensory level (e.g., T8) combined with motor weakness and bowel/bladder changes strongly points to a spinal cord lesion rather than a systemic or metabolic issue.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要认识到，明显的感觉平面（例如T8）结合运动无力和排便/排尿改变，强烈提示脊髓病变，而不是全身性或代谢性问题。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2419,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[49,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[14,27],"fullStemEn":"Review the patient's Clinical Course at Stage 1. Which action is the nurse's immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"查阅患者在阶段1的临床病程。哪项操作是护士的当务之急？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the nurse's immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项操作是护士的当务之急？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the patient's Clinical Course at Stage 1.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查阅患者在阶段1的临床病程。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_d","en":"Provide emotional support and reassurance regarding the risk of paralysis","zh":"就瘫痪的风险提供情感支持和安抚"},{"id":"opt_a","en":"Administer the IV dexamethasone bolus as prescribed","zh":"按医嘱给予静脉地塞米松推注"},{"id":"opt_b","en":"Perform a complete head-to-toe nursing assessment","zh":"进行全面的从头到脚护理评估"},{"id":"opt_c","en":"Prepare the patient for the insertion of an indwelling urinary catheter","zh":"准备为患者插入留置导尿管"}],"correct":["opt_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Administering the urgent MSCC dexamethasone dose is the highest-priority pharmacological intervention for malignant spinal cord compression and should not be delayed. It reduces vasogenic edema surrounding the compressed cord, which can halt or slow neurological deterioration while awaiting definitive treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"给予紧急MSCC地塞米松剂量是恶性脊髓压迫的最高优先级药理干预措施，不应延误。它能减少受压脊髓周围的血管源性水肿，从而在等待确定性治疗时阻止或减缓神经功能恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When key assessment data already identify an emergency and a time-sensitive medication is prescribed, do not delay treatment for a routine full assessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当关键评估资料已经提示急症，且已开具具有时间敏感性的药物医嘱时，不要为了常规全面评估而延误治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2420,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[96,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,54],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the patient's bladder scan shows 420 mL of urine and she has new perineal numbness. The nurse should recognize that these findings indicate which of the following?","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，患者的膀胱扫描显示有420 mL尿液，且新出现了会阴部麻木。护士应认识到这些发现提示以下哪种情况？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should recognize that these findings indicate which of the following?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应认识到这些发现提示以下哪种情况？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the patient's bladder scan shows 420 mL of urine and she has new perineal numbness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段1，患者的膀胱扫描显示有420 mL尿液，且新出现了会阴部麻木。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_a","en":"A localized urinary tract infection secondary to impaired mobility","zh":"继发于活动能力受损的局部尿路感染"},{"id":"opt_b","en":"An expected adverse effect of her recent oxycodone administration","zh":"她近期服用羟考酮的预期不良反应"},{"id":"opt_d","en":"Dehydration requiring an increase in her IV fluid rate","zh":"脱水，需要增加其静脉输液速度"},{"id":"opt_c","en":"Interruption of descending autonomic pathways indicating progressive spinal cord compression","zh":"下行自主神经通路中断，提示进行性脊髓压迫"}],"correct":["opt_c"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Urinary retention in the context of thoracic spinal cord compression reflects the interruption of descending autonomic pathways. It is an ominous neurological finding when accompanied by worsening lower-extremity weakness, a rising sensory level, and new perineal sensory change.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在胸髓压迫的情况下，尿潴留反映了下行自主神经通路的中断。当伴有下肢无力加重、感觉平面上升和新发的会阴感觉改变时，这是一个不祥的神经系统发现。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a symptom (retention) occurs alongside localizing neurologic signs (sensory level, perineal numbness), trace the symptom to the central neurologic lesion rather than a side effect.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当症状（尿潴留）与定位性神经体征（感觉平面、会阴麻木）同时出现时，应将症状追溯至中枢神经系统病变，而非副作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2421,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[196,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,62],"fullStemEn":"Review the Clinical Course at Stage 2. The neurosurgeon recommends emergent surgical decompression. Which of the following actions should the nurse take to safely prepare the patient for surgery? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"查阅阶段2的临床病程。神经外科医生建议进行紧急手术减压。护士应采取以下哪些措施来安全地为患者做好手术准备？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following actions should the nurse take to safely prepare the patient for surgery?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取以下哪些措施来安全地为患者做好手术准备？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"opt_f","en":"Explain the surgical risks and prognostic outcome of the laminectomy to the family.","zh":"向家属解释椎板切除术的手术风险和预后结果。"},{"id":"opt_a","en":"Verify that the surgeon has discussed the procedure and obtained informed consent.","zh":"核实外科医生已讨论了手术程序并获得了知情同意。"},{"id":"opt_d","en":"Ensure current laboratories, a type and screen, and imaging are available.","zh":"确保有最新的实验室检查、血型和抗体筛查以及影像学资料。"},{"id":"opt_b","en":"Hold the scheduled enoxaparin dose and communicate this to the surgical team.","zh":"暂停预定的依诺肝素剂量，并将此情况传达给手术团队。"},{"id":"opt_e","en":"Continue serial neurological assessments to document the trajectory of decline.","zh":"继续进行连续的神经系统评估，以记录病情下降的轨迹。"},{"id":"opt_c","en":"Administer a stat dose of regular insulin to correct the steroid-induced hyperglycemia to a target of 100 mg/dL.","zh":"给予立即剂量的常规胰岛素，以将类固醇诱导的高血糖纠正至目标值100 mg/dL。"}],"correct":["opt_a","opt_b","opt_d","opt_e"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Preparing a patient for emergent spinal decompression requires verifying informed consent, ensuring safety (holding anticoagulation), preparing necessary preoperative data (labs, imaging, type and screen), and continuing to monitor the rapid neurological decline. Holding the enoxaparin is critical to prevent epidural hematoma. The nurse's role in consent is to verify it was obtained by the provider, not to explain surgical risks or prognosticate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"为患者进行紧急脊髓减压术做准备需要核实知情同意、确保安全（暂停抗凝治疗）、准备必要的术前数据（实验室检查、影像学、血型和抗体筛查），并继续监测迅速下降的神经功能。暂停依诺肝素对于预防硬膜外血肿至关重要。护士在知情同意中的作用是核实医生已获得同意，而不是解释手术风险或预测预后。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between nursing responsibilities (verifying consent, holding contraindicated medications, monitoring) and provider responsibilities (obtaining informed consent, prognosticating).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分护理职责（核实知情同意、停用有禁忌的药物、监测）和医生职责（获取知情同意、预测预后）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2422,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,42],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the patient's daughter asks the nurse, \"Will surgery make my mother walk again?\" Which is the most appropriate response by the nurse?","fullStemZh":"在阶段2，患者的女儿问护士：“手术能让我母亲再次走路吗？”护士最恰当的回答是哪一项？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which is the most appropriate response by the nurse?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最恰当的回答是哪一项？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the patient's daughter asks the nurse, \"Will surgery make my mother walk again?\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段2，患者的女儿问护士：“手术能让我母亲再次走路吗？”","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_a","en":"\"I understand how frightening this is. The goal of surgery is to take pressure off the spinal cord and prevent further neurologic loss. Some patients regain function, and the fact that your mother still has some leg movement is encouraging, but the neurosurgeon is the best person to discuss expected recovery.\"","zh":"“我理解这有多令人害怕。手术的目的是减轻对脊髓的压迫，防止神经功能进一步丧失。有些患者会恢复功能，你母亲的腿还有一些活动能力这是令人鼓舞的，但神经外科医生是讨论预期恢复情况的最佳人选。”"},{"id":"opt_c","en":"\"The damage from the tumor is usually permanent. Surgery is just a palliative measure to reduce pain, so she will likely need a wheelchair.\"","zh":"“肿瘤造成的损伤通常是永久性的。手术只是一种减轻疼痛的姑息性措施，所以她很可能需要轮椅。”"},{"id":"opt_b","en":"\"Don't worry, the neurosurgeon is highly skilled. The surgery will fix the compression and she will be able to walk again after rehabilitation.\"","zh":"“别担心，神经外科医生医术高超。手术将解决压迫问题，她在康复后将能再次行走。”"},{"id":"opt_d","en":"\"I am not allowed to discuss her prognosis with you. You must wait until the surgeon comes out of the operating room.\"","zh":"“我不能和你讨论她的预后。你必须等到外科医生从手术室出来。”"}],"correct":["opt_a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This response balances honesty, empathy, and safe nursing boundaries. It correctly identifies the primary goal of surgery (preventing further loss), provides grounded hope based on clinical data (remaining motor function is a good prognostic sign), and appropriately refers definitive prognostication to the surgeon.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这个回答平衡了诚实、同理心和安全的护理界限。它正确地指出了手术的主要目标（防止进一步的丧失），基于临床数据提供了有根据的希望（保留的运动功能是良好的预后标志），并适当地将明确的预后预测交给外科医生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Avoid responses that offer false reassurance or definitive prognostic guarantees, but also avoid shutting down communication. Choose responses that state factual goals and refer to the provider for specifics.","testTakingStrategyZh":"避免提供虚假安慰或明确预后保证的回答，但也要避免终止沟通。选择陈述事实目标并将具体细节转交给医生的回答。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2423,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_scc_case_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,254],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,73],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3 (postoperative day 1), the nurse evaluates the patient's neurological response to surgery. For each assessment finding, specify whether it indicates an improvement from the preoperative baseline or indicates persistent spinal cord dysfunction.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3（术后第1天），护士评估患者对手术的神经系统反应。针对以下每项评估发现，请指明它是表明较术前基线有所改善，还是表明存在持续的脊髓功能障碍。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, specify whether it indicates an improvement from the preoperative baseline or indicates persistent spinal cord dysfunction.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对以下每项评估发现，请指明它是表明较术前基线有所改善，还是表明存在持续的脊髓功能障碍。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3 (postoperative day 1), the nurse evaluates the patient's neurological response to surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3（术后第1天），护士评估患者对手术的神经系统反应。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"row_1","en":"Bilateral lower extremity motor strength is 3 out of 5","zh":"双侧下肢肌力为3/5级"},{"id":"row_2","en":"Babinski sign remains positive bilaterally","zh":"双侧巴宾斯基征仍为阳性"},{"id":"row_3","en":"Sensory level is at T8–T9","zh":"感觉平面在T8–T9"},{"id":"row_4","en":"Absence of perineal sensation","zh":"会阴感觉缺失"}],"columns":[{"id":"opt_per","en":"Persistent Dysfunction","zh":"持续的功能障碍"},{"id":"opt_imp","en":"Improvement from Stage 2 Preoperative Status","zh":"较阶段2术前状态改善"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"row_1","columnIds":["opt_imp"]},{"rowId":"row_2","columnIds":["opt_per"]},{"rowId":"row_3","columnIds":["opt_imp"]},{"rowId":"row_4","columnIds":["opt_per"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Evaluation requires serial comparison. Preoperatively, motor strength had dropped to 2/5; 3/5 is an improvement. The sensory level had risen to T6; dropping back to T8–T9 is an improvement. However, positive Babinski signs reflect persistent upper motor neuron damage, and absent perineal sensation reflects persistent autonomic/sacral dysfunction, which typically recovers last.","rationaleCorrectZh":"评估需要进行连续比较。术前，肌力已降至2/5级；3/5级是一种改善。感觉平面曾上升至T6；回落至T8–T9是一种改善。然而，巴宾斯基征阳性反映了持续的上运动神经元损伤，而会阴感觉缺失反映了持续的自主神经/骶神经功能障碍，这通常是最后恢复的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Compare the current assessment data directly against the data from the worst point in the clinical course (Stage 2) to determine if a finding represents an improvement or persistent pathology.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将当前的评估数据与临床病程中最差的时间点（阶段2）的数据直接进行比较，以确定某项发现代表的是改善还是持续的病理状态。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2424,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.38","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.38.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,151],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,56],"fullStemEn":"Cytokine release syndrome following CAR-T cell infusion A patient develops fever, hypotension, hypoxia, and neurocognitive changes after CAR-T therapy.","fullStemZh":"CAR-T 细胞输注后的细胞因子释放综合征 一名患者在 CAR-T 治疗后出现发热、低血压、缺氧和神经认知变化。","terminalSentenceEn":"Cytokine release syndrome following CAR-T cell infusion A patient develops fever, hypotension, hypoxia, and neurocognitive changes after CAR-T therapy.","terminalSentenceZh":"CAR-T 细胞输注后的细胞因子释放综合征 一名患者在 CAR-T 治疗后出现发热、低血压、缺氧和神经认知变化。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This unfolding case requires recognizing CRS, treating neutropenic fever risk concurrently, distinguishing probable ICANS, prioritizing oxygenation and perfusion, and evaluating response after tocilizumab and corticosteroids.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本展开式病例要求识别 CRS，同时处理中性粒细胞减少性发热风险，区分疑似 ICANS，优先处理氧合和灌注，并评估使用托珠单抗和皮质类固醇后的反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Trend the case across stages instead of anchoring on a single abnormal value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按阶段观察病例趋势，不要只锚定某一个异常数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2425,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[192,241],"terminalOffsetsZh":[73,87],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the clinical cues from Stage 1. For each cue, indicate whether it supports early Cytokine Release Syndrome (CRS), neutropenic fever/sepsis risk, or is a nonspecific finding. Each row may have more than one correct category.","fullStemZh":"护士复查阶段 1 的临床线索。对于每一个线索，指出它是支持早期细胞因子释放综合征 (CRS)、中性粒细胞减少性发热/败血症风险，还是非特异性发现。每一行可以有多个正确的类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"Each row may have more than one correct category.","terminalSentenceZh":"每一行可以有多个正确的类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":"For each cue, indicate whether it supports early Cytokine Release Syndrome (CRS), neutropenic fever/sepsis risk, or is a nonspecific finding.","penultimateSentenceZh":"对于每一个线索，指出它是支持早期细胞因子释放综合征 (CRS)、中性粒细胞减少性发热/败血症风险，还是非特异性发现。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Fever, rigors, and myalgias","zh":"发热、寒战和肌肉酸痛"},{"id":"r2","en":"Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) 0.1 × 10³/µL","zh":"绝对中性粒细胞计数 (ANC) 0.1 × 10³/µL"},{"id":"r3","en":"CRP 86 mg/L and ferritin 1,450 ng/mL","zh":"CRP 86 mg/L 且铁蛋白 1,450 ng/mL"},{"id":"r4","en":"Mild fatigue reported at 1600","zh":"1600 报告有轻度疲劳"}],"columns":[{"id":"col1","en":"Supports early Cytokine Release Syndrome (CRS)","zh":"支持早期细胞因子释放综合征 (CRS)"},{"id":"col2","en":"Supports neutropenic fever/sepsis risk","zh":"支持中性粒细胞减少性发热/败血症风险"},{"id":"col3","en":"Nonspecific or expected finding","zh":"非特异性或预期的发现"}],"selectionMode":"multiple_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["col1","col2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["col2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["col1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["col3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Recognizing the clinical signs of both CRS and neutropenic fever is critical in the post-CAR-T setting. Fever, rigors, and myalgias are hallmark initial signs of CRS but are also classic symptoms of sepsis in a neutropenic patient. An ANC of 0.1 × 10³/µL places the patient at profound risk for neutropenic fever and sepsis, requiring immediate intervention. The elevation of CRP and ferritin strongly supports the onset of CRS. Mild fatigue is a nonspecific finding often expected following lymphodepleting chemotherapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 CAR-T 治疗后的环境中，识别 CRS 和中性粒细胞减少性发热的临床症状至关重要。发热、寒战和肌肉酸痛是 CRS 标志性的初始体征，但也是中性粒细胞减少患者败血症的典型症状。0.1 × 10³/µL 的 ANC 使患者面临极高的中性粒细胞减少性发热和败血症风险，需要立即干预。CRP 和铁蛋白的升高强烈支持 CRS 的发作。轻度疲劳是一种非特异性发现，通常在淋巴细胞清除化疗后是可以预料的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate each cue independently against both CRS and neutropenic fever pathophysiology. Avoid assuming symptoms can only belong to one category.","testTakingStrategyZh":"针对 CRS 和中性粒细胞减少性发热的病理生理学独立评估每个线索。避免假设症状只能属于一个类别。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2426,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,35],"fullStemEn":"Based on the Stage 1 findings, which of the following actions should the nurse anticipate or implement? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"基于阶段 1 的发现，护士应预期或执行以下哪些行动？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Based on the Stage 1 findings, which of the following actions should the nurse anticipate or implement?","penultimateSentenceZh":"基于阶段 1 的发现，护士应预期或执行以下哪些行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"o7","en":"Assume the fever is solely expected CRS and defer infection workup.","zh":"假设发热仅仅是预期的 CRS 并推迟感染检查。"},{"id":"o3","en":"Anticipate initiating empiric broad-spectrum antibiotics per neutropenic fever protocol.","zh":"预期按中性粒细胞减少性发热方案开始使用经验性广谱抗生素。"},{"id":"o1","en":"Notify the provider and activate the institutional CRS pathway.","zh":"通知医疗服务提供者并启动机构的 CRS 临床路径。"},{"id":"o4","en":"Administer acetaminophen as ordered for symptom management.","zh":"按医嘱给予对乙酰氨基酚以控制症状。"},{"id":"o2","en":"Obtain blood cultures per protocol, including central-line lumens.","zh":"按方案抽取血培养，包括中心静脉导管腔。"},{"id":"o5","en":"Increase the frequency of vital signs monitoring and continue ICE scoring.","zh":"增加生命体征监测的频率并继续 ICE 评分。"}],"correct":["o1","o2","o3","o4","o5"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In a profoundly neutropenic patient post-CAR-T infusion, a new fever must be treated concurrently as potential Cytokine Release Syndrome (CRS) and a neutropenic fever/sepsis medical emergency. The nurse should notify the provider to activate the CRS pathway, obtain blood cultures per protocol, anticipate initiating broad-spectrum antibiotics, administer acetaminophen for symptom management, and increase the frequency of monitoring and ICE scoring. Waiting for culture results before giving antibiotics or assuming the fever is only CRS can cause fatal delays in treating sepsis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在 CAR-T 输注后严重中性粒细胞减少的患者中，出现新发热必须同时作为潜在的细胞因子释放综合征 (CRS) 和中性粒细胞减少性发热/败血症医疗急症来处理。护士应通知医疗服务提供者启动 CRS 临床路径，按方案抽取血培养，预期开始使用广谱抗生素，给予对乙酰氨基酚以控制症状，并增加监测和 ICE 评分的频率。在给予抗生素前等待培养结果，或仅仅假设发热是 CRS，可能会导致延误治疗败血症的致命后果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify all interventions that promote safety in both the CRS pathway and the neutropenic fever pathway. Avoid actions that delay immediate lifesaving treatments.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别所有能促进 CRS 路径和中性粒细胞减少性发热路径安全的干预措施。避免采取延误立即挽救生命治疗的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2427,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[198,236],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,66],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the patient is experiencing hypoxia, hypotension, and a declining ICE score. The provider has written several new orders. In what order should the nurse implement the following actions? Drag and drop to arrange the sequence.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2，患者出现缺氧、低血压和 ICE 评分下降。医疗服务提供者下达了几项新医嘱。护士应按什么顺序执行以下行动？拖放以排列顺序。","terminalSentenceEn":"Drag and drop to arrange the sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"拖放以排列顺序。","penultimateSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse implement the following actions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行以下行动？","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"s4","en":"Administer dexamethasone IV as ordered for concurrent probable ICANS.","zh":"按并发疑似 ICANS 医嘱静脉给予地塞米松。"},{"id":"s2","en":"Begin the ordered normal saline IV fluid bolus.","zh":"开始静脉推注医嘱的 0.9% 氯化钠注射液。"},{"id":"s5","en":"Prepare for possible ICU transfer while continuing frequent monitoring.","zh":"在继续频繁监测的同时，为可能转入 ICU 做好准备。"},{"id":"s1","en":"Apply low-flow oxygen via nasal cannula and raise the head of the bed.","zh":"通过鼻导管给予低流量吸氧并抬高床头。"},{"id":"s3","en":"Administer tocilizumab IV as ordered for CRS Grade 2.","zh":"按 CRS 2 级医嘱静脉给予托珠单抗。"}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Using the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) framework, the nurse must first stabilize oxygenation by applying low-flow oxygen and raising the head of the bed. Second, initiate the IV fluid bolus to address hypotension and support perfusion. Once basic physiological stability is addressed, pharmacological interventions follow: administer tocilizumab (the definitive treatment for CRS) and then dexamethasone (for concurrent ICANS). Finally, prepare for potential ICU transfer while continuing frequent monitoring. Transfer preparation and team communication may occur in parallel, but they must not delay life-saving oxygen, fluids, or ordered medications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"使用 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）框架，护士必须首先通过给予低流量吸氧和抬高床头来稳定氧合。其次，开始静脉推注补液以解决低血压并支持灌注。一旦基本的生理稳定性得到解决，接下来是药物干预：给予托珠单抗（CRS 的决定性治疗），然后给予地塞米松（用于并发的 ICANS）。最后，在继续频繁监测的同时为可能转入 ICU 做好准备。转运准备和团队沟通可以并行进行，但绝不能延误挽救生命的吸氧、补液或医嘱药物治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) priority framework to physiological instability before moving to pharmacological treatments and logistical tasks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在进行药物治疗和后勤任务之前，将 ABC（气道、呼吸、循环）优先框架应用于生理不稳定状态。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2428,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,175],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,48],"fullStemEn":"Review the clinical findings from Stage 2. For each finding, select the corresponding complication(s) it primarily indicates. Each row may have more than one correct category.","fullStemZh":"复查阶段 2 的临床发现。对于每个发现，选择它主要表明的相应并发症。每一行可以有多个正确的类别。","terminalSentenceEn":"Each row may have more than one correct category.","terminalSentenceZh":"每一行可以有多个正确的类别。","penultimateSentenceEn":"For each finding, select the corresponding complication(s) it primarily indicates.","penultimateSentenceZh":"对于每个发现，选择它主要表明的相应并发症。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Hypotension (BP 88/52) and low-flow oxygen need","zh":"低血压（血压 88/52）和需要低流量吸氧"},{"id":"r2","en":"ICE score 6/10, disorientation, and attention difficulty","zh":"ICE 评分 6/10、定向障碍和注意力困难"},{"id":"r3","en":"Creatinine rising from 1.0 to 1.6 mg/dL with oliguria","zh":"肌酐从 1.0 升至 1.6 mg/dL 伴少尿"},{"id":"r4","en":"Falling fibrinogen with rising D-dimer","zh":"纤维蛋白原下降伴 D-二聚体升高"},{"id":"r5","en":"Persistent fever to 103.6 °F (39.8 °C) and rigors","zh":"持续发热至 103.6 °F (39.8 °C) 和寒战"}],"columns":[{"id":"col1","en":"Indicates CRS progression or severity","zh":"表明 CRS 进展或严重程度"},{"id":"col2","en":"Indicates Immune Effector Cell-Associated Neurotoxicity Syndrome (ICANS)","zh":"表明免疫效应细胞相关神经毒性综合征 (ICANS)"},{"id":"col3","en":"Indicates early end-organ or coagulation dysfunction","zh":"表明早期终末器官或凝血功能障碍"}],"selectionMode":"multiple_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["col1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["col2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["col1","col3"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["col1","col3"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["col1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"CRS severity grading is primarily driven by fever, hypotension, and hypoxia. Therefore, hypotension requiring fluids and hypoxia requiring low-flow oxygen, along with persistent fever, indicate CRS severity. ICANS is distinct and indicated by neurological changes such as a dropping ICE score, disorientation, and attention difficulty. Rising creatinine with oliguria and falling fibrinogen with rising D-dimer suggest early end-organ and coagulation dysfunction, which are consequences of severe systemic CRS inflammation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"CRS 严重程度分级主要取决于发热、低血压和缺氧。因此，需要补液的低血压和需要低流量吸氧的缺氧，连同持续发热，表明了 CRS 的严重程度。ICANS 是独立的，表现为神经系统变化，如 ICE 评分下降、定向障碍和注意力集中困难。肌酐升高伴少尿，以及纤维蛋白原下降伴 D-二聚体升高，提示早期终末器官和凝血功能障碍，这些是严重的全身性 CRS 炎症的后果。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate fever, hypotension, and hypoxia with CRS grading. Associate cognitive and ICE score changes with ICANS. Recognize that severe CRS drives end-organ failure (like renal or coagulopathy).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将发热、低血压和缺氧与 CRS 分级联系起来。将认知和 ICE 评分变化与 ICANS 联系起来。认识到严重的 CRS 会导致终末器官衰竭（如肾脏或凝血功能病变）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2429,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_car_t_crs_2026_06_11_case_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse evaluates the patient's response 12 hours after tocilizumab and dexamethasone administration. Complete the sentences by choosing from the dropdown lists.","fullStemZh":"护士评估患者在给予托珠单抗和地塞米松后 12 小时的反应。从下拉列表中进行选择以完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the sentences by choosing from the dropdown lists.","terminalSentenceZh":"从下拉列表中进行选择以完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates the patient's response 12 hours after tocilizumab and dexamethasone administration.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士评估患者在给予托珠单抗和地塞米松后 12 小时的反应。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The patient's clinical improvement is supported by {{1}} and {{2}}. However, the nurse recognizes that the decline in CRP {{3}}, and therefore {{4}}.","zh":"患者的临床改善得到 {{1}} 和 {{2}} 的支持。然而，护士认识到 CRP 的下降 {{3}}，因此 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"an increased need for oxygen support","zh":"需要增加氧气支持"},{"id":"o1","en":"a resolving fever and improved blood pressure without vasopressors","zh":"发热消退且不使用血管加压药的情况下血压改善"},{"id":"o3","en":"a sustained ICE score of 6/10","zh":"ICE 评分维持在 6/10"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"increasing creatinine levels","zh":"肌酐水平升高"},{"id":"o2","en":"improving urine output and an ICE score of 9/10","zh":"尿量改善且 ICE 评分为 9/10"},{"id":"o3","en":"a rising CRP level","zh":"CRP 水平不断上升"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"confirms complete resolution of the inflammatory process","zh":"证实炎症过程已完全消退"},{"id":"o3","en":"indicates that neurotoxicity is fully reversed","zh":"表明神经毒性已完全逆转"},{"id":"o2","en":"is an unreliable marker alone because tocilizumab suppresses CRP production","zh":"单独作为一个不可靠的标志物，因为托珠单抗抑制 CRP 的产生"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"monitoring can be safely reduced to baseline frequency","zh":"监测可以安全地减少到基线频率"},{"id":"o2","en":"the patient can be immediately discharged","zh":"患者可以立即出院"},{"id":"o3","en":"frequent monitoring must continue because CRS or ICANS can recur","zh":"必须继续频繁监测，因为 CRS 或 ICANS 可能复发"}],"correct":"o3"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Clinical improvement after tocilizumab and dexamethasone must be evaluated using multiple parameters. A resolving fever, improved blood pressure without vasopressors, improved urine output, and an ICE score of 9/10 indicate genuine recovery from CRS and ICANS. However, the nurse must recognize that tocilizumab suppresses CRP production by blocking the IL-6 pathway, making a declining CRP an unreliable marker alone. Frequent monitoring must continue because CRS or ICANS can recur or fluctuate after initial improvement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"必须使用多个参数来评估使用托珠单抗和地塞米松后的临床改善情况。发热消退、不使用血管加压药的情况下血压改善、尿量改善以及 ICE 评分达到 9/10，表明 CRS 和 ICANS 的真正恢复。然而，护士必须认识到，托珠单抗通过阻断 IL-6 途径抑制 CRP 的产生，这使得下降的 CRP 单独作为一个不可靠的标志物。必须继续频繁监测，因为 CRS 或 ICANS 在初步改善后仍可能复发或波动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate clinical outcomes using physiological data (vital signs, urine output, neurological status). Remember the specific pharmacological mechanism of tocilizumab on CRP, which makes it an unreliable standalone marker of improvement.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用生理数据（生命体征、尿量、神经系统状态）评估临床结果。记住托珠单抗对 CRP 的特定药理机制，这使得它作为独立的改善标志物不可靠。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates the patient's response 12 hours after tocilizumab and dexamethasone administration.","controlSentenceZh":"护士评估患者在给予托珠单抗和地塞米松后 12 小时的反应。"}
{"queueIndex":2430,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.39","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.39.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1500,1588],"terminalOffsetsZh":[464,486],"fullStemEn":"Immune checkpoint inhibitor–induced myocarditis with concurrent hepatotoxicity A 61-year-old woman with metastatic melanoma is admitted to the oncology unit for her third cycle of combination immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) therapy with nivolumab (anti–PD-1) plus ipilimumab (anti–CTLA-4). Her cancer was diagnosed eight months ago after excision of a Clark level V lesion on the left scapula; subsequent imaging revealed hepatic and pulmonary metastases. She has a history of well-controlled hypertension managed with amlodipine 5 mg daily and no prior cardiac disease. Echocardiogram before starting immunotherapy three months ago showed a left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) of 62% with no wall-motion abnormalities. Her first two cycles were notable only for grade 1 fatigue and a mild maculopapular rash on the trunk that resolved with topical corticosteroids. Current orders include nivolumab 3 mg/kg IV and ipilimumab 1 mg/kg IV to infuse today, ondansetron 4 mg IV PRN nausea, continuous telemetry during infusion, and baseline labs drawn this morning before treatment.\n\nThe patient arrives to the infusion area reporting that over the past four days she has noticed increasing fatigue beyond her usual level, a vague sense of chest heaviness that is worse when she climbs the stairs to her bedroom, and mild nausea with poor appetite. She attributes these symptoms to \"the chemo catching up with me.\" She denies frank chest pain, syncope, orthopnea, lower-extremity edema, or fever. She appears mildly fatigued but is conversational, ambulatory, and in no acute distress.","fullStemZh":"免疫检查点抑制剂诱发的心肌炎并发肝毒性 一名61岁的转移性黑色素瘤女性患者被收治入肿瘤科，准备接受第三个周期的纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）联合伊匹木单抗（抗CTLA-4）免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）联合治疗。8个月前，她在切除左肩胛骨Clark V级病变后确诊癌症；随后的影像学检查显示有肝脏和肺部转移。患者既往有高血压史，每日服用氨氯地平5 mg控制良好，无既往心脏病史。3个月前开始免疫治疗前的超声心动图显示，左心室射血分数（LVEF）为62%，无室壁运动异常。前两个周期仅出现1级疲劳和躯干轻度斑丘疹，局部使用皮质类固醇后消退。目前的医嘱包括今天静脉输注纳武利尤单抗3 mg/kg和伊匹木单抗1 mg/kg，昂丹司琼4 mg静脉推注用于必要时止吐，输液期间持续心电监护，并在治疗前于今晨抽取基线实验室检查血样。\n\n患者到达输液区，自述在过去4天里感到疲劳感比平时加重，有一种模糊的胸部沉重感，在爬楼梯回卧室时加重，并伴有轻度恶心和食欲不振。她将这些症状归因于“化疗的反应”。她否认有明显的胸痛、晕厥、端坐呼吸、下肢水肿或发热。她显得有些疲劳，但能交谈和走动，无急性病容。","terminalSentenceEn":"She appears mildly fatigued but is conversational, ambulatory, and in no acute distress.","terminalSentenceZh":"她显得有些疲劳，但能交谈和走动，无急性病容。","penultimateSentenceEn":"She denies frank chest pain, syncope, orthopnea, lower-extremity edema, or fever.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她否认有明显的胸痛、晕厥、端坐呼吸、下肢水肿或发热。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case highlights the clinical presentation, diagnosis, and management of immune checkpoint inhibitor–induced myocarditis. The key takeaways are recognizing the combination of elevated troponin, conduction abnormalities, and declining ventricular function as a hallmark of this potentially fatal complication; withholding the offending agent immediately; prioritizing high-dose corticosteroid administration as the definitive treatment; and anticipating multi-organ involvement such as concurrent hepatotoxicity.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例重点介绍了免疫检查点抑制剂诱发的心肌炎的临床表现、诊断和处理。关键要点包括：认识到肌钙蛋白升高、传导异常和心室功能下降是这种潜在致命并发症的标志性表现；立即停用致病药物；优先给予大剂量皮质类固醇作为决定性治疗；以及预期可能出现并发的肝毒性等多器官受累。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When analyzing a multi-part case study on a severe adverse drug reaction, systematically assess how the clinical cues confirm the diagnosis, prioritize actions that remove the offending agent and provide definitive treatment, and plan for monitoring related complications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在分析关于严重不良药物反应的多部分病例分析时，应系统地评估临床线索如何确诊，优先采取停用致病药物并提供决定性治疗的操作，并制定监测相关并发症的计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2431,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,213],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,56],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer the scheduled immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy before Stage 1 begins. Based on the initial assessment and baseline laboratory data, which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备在第1阶段开始前给予计划的免疫检查点抑制剂治疗。根据初步评估和基线实验室数据，护士首先应采取哪项操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the initial assessment and baseline laboratory data, which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据初步评估和基线实验室数据，护士首先应采取哪项操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer the scheduled immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy before Stage 1 begins.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正准备在第1阶段开始前给予计划的免疫检查点抑制剂治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_antiemetic","en":"Administer the PRN ondansetron for the patient's nausea before starting the infusion.","zh":"在开始输液前，给予必要时的昂丹司琼以缓解患者的恶心。"},{"id":"opt_hold","en":"Hold the infusion and immediately notify the oncologist of the laboratory results and patient symptoms.","zh":"暂停输液，并立即将实验室结果和患者症状通知肿瘤科医生。"},{"id":"opt_proceed","en":"Proceed with the infusion and monitor the patient's vital signs every 15 minutes.","zh":"继续输液，并每15分钟监测一次患者的生命体征。"},{"id":"opt_rounds","en":"Hold the infusion and plan to communicate the findings to the oncologist during routine rounds.","zh":"暂停输液，并计划在常规查房期间将发现通知肿瘤科医生。"}],"correct":["opt_hold"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should hold the infusion and immediately notify the oncologist of the elevated troponin I (0.18 ng/mL), elevated BNP, transaminase elevations, new exertional chest symptoms, and resting tachycardia. Immune checkpoint inhibitors can cause fulminant myocarditis, which carries a mortality rate of up to 25–50% when diagnosed late. An elevated troponin in a patient on combination ICI therapy with new cardiac symptoms is a red-flag cue that must be reported before administering another dose of the causative agent, because additional dosing could accelerate the immune-mediated injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应暂停输液并立即将肌钙蛋白I升高（0.18 ng/mL）、BNP升高、转氨酶升高、新发劳力性胸部症状及静息心动过速通知肿瘤科医生。免疫检查点抑制剂可引起暴发性心肌炎，若延迟诊断，其死亡率可高达25-50%。对于接受ICI联合治疗并出现新发心脏症状的患者，肌钙蛋白升高是一个危险信号，必须在给予下一剂致病药物前报告，因为追加给药可能会加速免疫介导的损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a patient receiving high-risk systemic therapy presents with new systemic/cardiac symptoms and abnormal cardiac biomarkers, always prioritize withholding the offending agent and urgent notification over routine interventions or continued administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当接受高危全身治疗的患者出现新的全身/心脏症状和异常的心脏生物标志物时，应始终将暂停致病药物和紧急通知放在常规干预或继续给药之前。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2432,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[45,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,33],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the Stage 1 clinical data. The constellation of findings is most consistent with which clinical hypothesis?","fullStemZh":"护士查阅了第1阶段的临床数据。这一系列表现最符合以下哪种临床假设？","terminalSentenceEn":"The constellation of findings is most consistent with which clinical hypothesis?","terminalSentenceZh":"这一系列表现最符合以下哪种临床假设？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the Stage 1 clinical data.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查阅了第1阶段的临床数据。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_mets","en":"Metastatic disease progression into the cardiopulmonary system.","zh":"向心肺系统转移的转移性疾病进展。"},{"id":"opt_ici_myocarditis","en":"Immune checkpoint inhibitor–induced myocarditis with concurrent immune-mediated hepatitis.","zh":"免疫检查点抑制剂诱发的心肌炎并发免疫介导性肝炎。"},{"id":"opt_viral","en":"Viral myocarditis presenting as an isolated infectious process.","zh":"表现为孤立性感染过程的病毒性心肌炎。"},{"id":"opt_acs","en":"Acute coronary syndrome resulting from atherosclerotic plaque rupture.","zh":"动脉粥样硬化斑块破裂导致的急性冠状动脉综合征。"}],"correct":["opt_ici_myocarditis"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The combination of diffuse (not territory-specific) ST-segment changes, a new conduction abnormality (prolonging PR interval), troponin elevation, BNP elevation, and concurrent hepatic transaminase elevation in a patient actively receiving combination anti–PD-1/anti–CTLA-4 therapy is the hallmark presentation of ICI myocarditis with multi-organ immune-related adverse events. The concurrent hepatotoxicity suggests a systemic immune-mediated process rather than a single-organ etiology.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于正在接受抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4联合治疗的患者，弥漫性（非特定区域）ST段改变、新发传导异常（PR间期延长）、肌钙蛋白升高、BNP升高以及并发肝转氨酶升高，是ICI心肌炎伴多器官免疫相关不良事件的标志性表现。并发的肝毒性提示这是一种系统性的免疫介导过程，而非单器官病因。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When multiple organs (heart, liver) show simultaneous acute dysfunction in a patient on immune checkpoint inhibitors, recognize the pattern of multi-organ immune-related adverse events (irAEs) rather than independent primary diseases.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当接受免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者表现出多个器官（心脏、肝脏）同时急性功能障碍时，应识别出多器官免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的模式，而不是独立的巧合疾病。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2433,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,187],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,54],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the patient is hemodynamically deteriorating. The nurse receives several urgent orders. In what order should the nurse perform the following actions? All options must be used.","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，患者血流动力学出现恶化。护士收到几项紧急医嘱。护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？所有选项都必须使用。","terminalSentenceEn":"All options must be used.","terminalSentenceZh":"所有选项都必须使用。","penultimateSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse perform the following actions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序执行以下操作？","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"ord_telemetry","en":"Ensure continuous telemetry and reliable IV access.","zh":"确保持续心电监护和可靠的静脉通路。"},{"id":"ord_steroids","en":"Administer the high-dose intravenous methylprednisolone.","zh":"静脉注射高剂量甲泼尼龙。"},{"id":"ord_oxygen","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen to maintain SpO₂ ≥ 94%.","zh":"提供补充氧气以维持SpO₂ ≥ 94%。"},{"id":"ord_transfer","en":"Prepare the patient for transfer to a higher-acuity monitored cardiac unit.","zh":"准备将患者转入更高重症级别的带监护心血管病房。"}],"correct":["ord_oxygen","ord_telemetry","ord_steroids","ord_transfer"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After oxygen is applied, the nurse rapidly verifies continuous telemetry and patent IV access so high-dose IV methylprednisolone can be administered without delay. These steps should occur immediately and should not postpone the first steroid dose. Transfer is important but follows oxygenation, monitoring/access verification, and initiation of time-critical immunosuppression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在给予氧气后，护士迅速核实持续心电监护和畅通的静脉通路，以便能够毫不延误地静脉注射大剂量甲泼尼龙。这些步骤应立即进行，不应推迟第一剂类固醇的给药。转科固然重要，但应在氧合、监护/通路核实以及启动争分夺秒的免疫抑制治疗之后进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use ABCs (Airway, Breathing, Circulation) to prioritize oxygenation first. Then, perform actions that allow the administration of the definitive life-saving medication (steroids) before focusing on logistical tasks like transfer.","testTakingStrategyZh":"利用ABCs（气道、呼吸、循环）原则，首先优先考虑氧合。然后执行允许给予决定性救命药物（类固醇）的操作，最后再关注转移等后勤任务。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2434,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[181,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,47],"fullStemEn":"The nurse prepares a comprehensive monitoring plan for the patient following the administration of corticosteroids. Which of the following nursing interventions should be included? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士在给予皮质类固醇后为患者制定全面的监护计划。以下哪些护理干预应包括在内？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing interventions should be included?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些护理干预应包括在内？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"opt_biomarkers","en":"Serial troponin and liver-enzyme monitoring every 6 to 12 hours.","zh":"每6至12小时连续监测肌钙蛋白和肝酶。"},{"id":"opt_glucose","en":"Blood glucose monitoring every 4 to 6 hours.","zh":"每4至6小时监测一次血糖。"},{"id":"opt_discontinue_tele","en":"Discontinuation of cardiac monitoring once the patient's PR interval normalizes.","zh":"一旦患者的PR间期恢复正常，即停止心电监护。"},{"id":"opt_myositis","en":"Assessment for overlapping myositis or myasthenia-like symptoms.","zh":"评估是否重叠出现肌炎或重症肌无力样症状。"},{"id":"opt_arrhythmias","en":"Continuous telemetry with alarms set for arrhythmias and conduction changes.","zh":"持续心电监护，并设置心律失常和传导改变警报。"}],"correct":["opt_arrhythmias","opt_biomarkers","opt_glucose","opt_myositis"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should generate a solution set that includes continuous telemetry with alarms set for arrhythmias and conduction changes (especially worsening AV block, which can progress to complete heart block), serial troponin levels to track trajectory, serial liver-enzyme monitoring, and blood glucose monitoring anticipating steroid-induced hyperglycemia. The nurse should also assess for signs of other immune-related adverse events, because ICI myocarditis can overlap with neuromuscular immune toxicity. Discontinuing cardiac monitoring is unsafe because ICI myocarditis can deteriorate rapidly to complete heart block or fatal arrhythmia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应制定一套方案，包括：设置心律失常和传导改变警报的持续心电监护（尤其是可能进展为完全性心脏传导阻滞的房室传导阻滞恶化）；连续监测肌钙蛋白水平以追踪轨迹；连续监测肝酶；以及预期类固醇可能引起高血糖而进行的血糖监测。护士还应评估其他免疫相关不良事件的体征，因为ICI心肌炎可与神经肌肉免疫毒性重叠。停止心电监护是不安全的，因为ICI心肌炎可能迅速恶化为完全性心脏传导阻滞或致命的心律失常。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select interventions that monitor the target condition (heart, liver), anticipate complications of the treatment (hyperglycemia from steroids), and screen for known related toxicities (neuromuscular).","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能监测目标疾病（心脏、肝脏）、预期治疗并发症（类固醇引起的高血糖）以及筛查已知相关毒性（神经肌肉）的干预措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2435,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,168],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,50],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the oncologist writes an order to permanently discontinue all ICI therapy. What is the most appropriate action by the nurse regarding this medication order?","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，肿瘤科医生开具了永久停用所有ICI治疗的医嘱。关于这项药物医嘱，护士最合适的操作是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most appropriate action by the nurse regarding this medication order?","terminalSentenceZh":"关于这项药物医嘱，护士最合适的操作是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the oncologist writes an order to permanently discontinue all ICI therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第2阶段，肿瘤科医生开具了永久停用所有ICI治疗的医嘱。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_temporary","en":"Document the ICI discontinuation as a temporary hold and inform the patient that therapy will resume after cardiac recovery.","zh":"将ICI停药记录为临时暂停，并告知患者在心脏康复后将恢复治疗。"},{"id":"opt_verify","en":"Verify the ICI is held/discontinued in the MAR per the provider order, ensure the adverse drug reaction is documented, and educate the patient about the permanent discontinuation.","zh":"根据医生医嘱在MAR中确认ICI已暂停/停药，确保不良药物反应得到记录，并就永久停药对患者进行健康教育。"},{"id":"opt_delete","en":"Independently delete the ICI order from the patient's active medication list to prevent inadvertent administration by another nurse.","zh":"独立从患者的有效药物清单中删除ICI医嘱，以防止另一名护士意外给药。"},{"id":"opt_transition","en":"Request an order to transition the patient from combination therapy to single-agent immunotherapy.","zh":"请求医嘱将患者从联合治疗过渡到单药免疫治疗。"}],"correct":["opt_verify"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should verify the ICI is held/discontinued in the MAR per the provider order; document the medication as not given with the clinical reason; notify pharmacy/oncology if the order remains active; ensure the adverse drug reaction is documented per facility policy; and educate the patient that the immunotherapy was stopped because of a serious heart-and-liver immune reaction. Permanent discontinuation is the standard of care for grade 3–4 ICI myocarditis, given the high fatality risk with re-exposure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应根据医生医嘱在MAR中确认ICI已暂停/停药；记录该药物未给药及临床原因；如果医嘱仍然有效，通知药房/肿瘤科；确保按照机构政策记录不良药物反应；并教育患者，由于严重的心肝免疫反应，免疫治疗已停止。鉴于再次暴露有很高的致死风险，永久停药是3-4级ICI心肌炎的标准治疗方案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Select the option that reflects safe nursing scope (verifying orders and documenting) and aligns with the severity of a life-threatening adverse drug reaction (permanent discontinuation and patient education).","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择反映安全护理范围（核实医嘱和记录）并与危及生命的不良药物反应的严重程度（永久停药和患者教育）相一致的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2436,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_icit_case_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,247],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,74],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse evaluates the patient's clinical and laboratory data following 18 to 24 hours of corticosteroid therapy. For each finding, indicate whether it represents a positive response to treatment or a treatment-related adverse effect.","fullStemZh":"在第3阶段，护士在皮质类固醇治疗18至24小时后评估患者的临床和实验室数据。对于每项表现，请指出它是代表对治疗的积极反应，还是与治疗相关的不良反应。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, indicate whether it represents a positive response to treatment or a treatment-related adverse effect.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项表现，请指出它是代表对治疗的积极反应，还是与治疗相关的不良反应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse evaluates the patient's clinical and laboratory data following 18 to 24 hours of corticosteroid therapy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第3阶段，护士在皮质类固醇治疗18至24小时后评估患者的临床和实验室数据。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"columns":[{"id":"col_adverse","en":"Treatment-Related Adverse Effect","zh":"与治疗相关的不良反应"},{"id":"col_positive","en":"Positive Response to Treatment","zh":"对治疗的积极反应"}],"rows":[{"id":"row_trop","en":"Decline in troponin I from 1.42 to 0.64 ng/mL","zh":"肌钙蛋白I从1.42下降至0.64 ng/mL"},{"id":"row_pvc","en":"Resolution of frequent premature ventricular contractions (PVCs)","zh":"频发室性早搏（PVCs）消失"},{"id":"row_glucose","en":"Blood glucose level of 218 mg/dL","zh":"血糖水平218 mg/dL"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"row_trop","columnIds":["col_positive"]},{"rowId":"row_pvc","columnIds":["col_positive"]},{"rowId":"row_glucose","columnIds":["col_adverse"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The decline in troponin I and the resolution of PVCs confirm a positive response to the immunosuppressive therapy, demonstrating that the immune-mediated injury is being suppressed. The blood glucose of 218 mg/dL is a predictable adverse effect of the high-dose methylprednisolone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"肌钙蛋白I的下降和室性早搏的消失证实了对免疫抑制治疗的积极反应，表明免疫介导的损伤正在被抑制。血糖218 mg/dL是高剂量甲泼尼龙可预见的不良反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between signs that the underlying disease process is improving (cardiac markers and rhythms) and new abnormal findings caused by the treatment itself (hyperglycemia from steroids).","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分潜在疾病过程正在改善的体征（心脏标志物和心律）与治疗本身引起的新异常发现（类固醇导致的高血糖）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2437,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.40","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Oncology & Immunotherapy Complications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.40.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1917,1971],"terminalOffsetsZh":[669,681],"fullStemEn":"Severe chemotherapy-induced mucositis with total parenteral nutrition dependence and central line complications A 58-year-old woman with acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is on day 12 of induction chemotherapy (cytarabine and daunorubicin, \"7+3\" regimen) on an inpatient oncology unit. She has a triple-lumen peripherally inserted central catheter (PICC) in her right basilic vein placed on admission. Her medical history includes well-controlled type 2 diabetes (metformin, held during admission; sliding-scale insulin in use), mild chronic kidney disease (baseline creatinine 1.3 mg/dL), and a 30-pack-year smoking history. She is profoundly neutropenic (absolute neutrophil count less than 100/µL) and has been on neutropenic precautions. Five days ago she developed progressive oral and esophageal pain, was unable to swallow liquids, and was started on total parenteral nutrition (TPN) via her PICC line at 85 mL/hr, a dedicated lumen. Current orders include TPN with standard amino acids, dextrose, lipids, electrolytes, and multivitamins; morphine patient-controlled analgesia (PCA) for mucositis pain; fluconazole 400 mg IV daily for antifungal prophylaxis; cefepime 2 g IV every 8 hours for febrile neutropenia coverage; ice chips for comfort as tolerated; chlorhexidine-free sodium bicarbonate mouth rinses every 4 hours; strict intake and output; daily weights; and capillary blood glucose monitoring every 6 hours with sliding-scale insulin coverage.\n\nAt the start of the night shift the nurse receives handoff that the patient has been increasingly miserable over the past 24 hours. She is rating her mouth and throat pain 9 out of 10 despite PCA use, is refusing all oral care attempts, drooling into a basin, and has not voided in the past 5 hours. The day nurse reports the TPN bag was changed 2 hours ago and that the patient \"spiked a temp\" at the end of day shift but the provider was not yet notified. The patient appears flushed and is curled on her side.","fullStemZh":"严重的化疗诱发黏膜炎合并全胃肠外营养依赖及中心静脉导管并发症 一名58岁急性髓系白血病（AML）女性患者，在肿瘤内科住院部接受诱导化疗（阿糖胞苷和柔红霉素，“7+3”方案）第12天。入院时在其右侧贵要静脉留置了三腔经外周静脉穿刺中心静脉导管（PICC）。既往病史包括控制良好的2型糖尿病（二甲双胍，入院期间停用；使用滑动标尺法胰岛素）、轻度慢性肾脏病（基线肌酐 1.3 mg/dL），以及30包年的吸烟史。患者处于重度中性粒细胞减少状态（绝对中性粒细胞计数低于100/µL），并已采取中性粒细胞减少保护性隔离措施。5天前她出现进行性口腔和食管疼痛，无法吞咽液体，开始通过PICC导管专用腔以 85 mL/hr 的速度输注全胃肠外营养（TPN）。目前的医嘱包括：含有标准氨基酸、葡萄糖、脂肪乳、电解质和多种维生素的TPN；用于缓解黏膜炎疼痛的吗啡患者自控镇痛（PCA）；氟康唑 400 mg 静脉注射 每日一次，预防真菌感染；头孢吡肟 2 g 静脉注射 每8小时一次，覆盖中性粒细胞减少伴发热；根据耐受情况提供碎冰块以缓解不适；每4小时使用不含氯己定的碳酸氢钠漱口水漱口；严格记录出入量；每日称重；以及每6小时监测一次末梢血糖，并根据滑动标尺法给予胰岛素。\n\n夜班开始时，护士接班得知患者在过去24小时内越来越痛苦。尽管使用了PCA，她对口腔和咽喉疼痛的评分仍为9分（满分10分），拒绝所有口腔护理尝试，口水流入口杯中，并且在过去5小时内没有排尿。白班护士报告说，TPN输液袋在2小时前已更换，患者在白班结束时“体温飙升”，但尚未通知医生。患者面色潮红，蜷缩侧卧。","terminalSentenceEn":"The patient appears flushed and is curled on her side.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者面色潮红，蜷缩侧卧。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The day nurse reports the TPN bag was changed 2 hours ago and that the patient \"spiked a temp\" at the end of day shift but the provider was not yet notified.","penultimateSentenceZh":"白班护士报告说，TPN输液袋在2小时前已更换，患者在白班结束时“体温飙升”，但尚未通知医生。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case highlights the critical importance of recognizing sepsis in a profoundly neutropenic patient with mucositis, the dangers of abruptly altering continuous TPN, and the safe coordination of alternative access and source control during a catheter-related bloodstream infection.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例强调了在重度中性粒细胞减少伴黏膜炎患者中识别脓毒症的极端重要性、突然改变持续TPN的危险性，以及在导管相关血流感染期间安全协调替代通路和控制感染源的原则。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When approaching unfolding cases, match nursing interventions to the patient's changing hemodynamic status and physical limitations (e.g., severe thrombocytopenia, inability to swallow). Never delay critical systemic treatments for localized interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在处理不断发展的案例时，护理干预必须与患者不断变化的血流动力学状态和生理限制（如重度血小板减少、无法吞咽）相匹配。切勿因局部干预而延误关键的全身性治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2438,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[109,261],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,70],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, after the fluid bolus and electrolyte replacements, the patient's condition continues to worsen. Based on the new clinical findings, what is the most likely emerging complication, and which cue is the highest priority to communicate to the provider?","fullStemZh":"在第1阶段，给予液体推注和电解质补充后，患者病情继续恶化。基于新的临床表现，最可能出现的新发并发症是什么？沟通时优先级最高的临床线索是哪个？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the new clinical findings, what is the most likely emerging complication, and which cue is the highest priority to communicate to the provider?","terminalSentenceZh":"沟通时优先级最高的临床线索是哪个？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, after the fluid bolus and electrolyte replacements, the patient's condition continues to worsen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"基于新的临床表现，最可能出现的新发并发症是什么？","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_C","en":"Localized PICC insertion site infection; new erythema extending 2 cm without purulent drainage.","zh":"局部PICC穿刺部位感染；新发延伸 2 cm 的红斑，无脓性引流物。"},{"id":"opt_B","en":"Hypovolemic shock resulting from severe mucositis-associated dehydration; oliguria of 30 mL over 2 hours.","zh":"重度黏膜炎脱水导致的低血容量性休克；2小时内尿量仅为 30 mL。"},{"id":"opt_A","en":"Sepsis likely originating from a catheter-related bloodstream infection; worsening hypotension despite the fluid bolus.","zh":"可能源自导管相关血流感染的脓毒症；尽管推注液体血压仍持续恶化。"},{"id":"opt_D","en":"Medication-induced anaphylaxis; the onset of shivering with rigors after antibiotic and electrolyte administration.","zh":"药物引起的过敏反应；在给予抗生素和电解质后出现寒战。"}],"correct":["opt_A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should recognize that the constellation of findings—fever in a neutropenic patient, hemodynamic instability unresponsive to fluids, rising lactate, and new PICC insertion site erythema—is most consistent with sepsis, likely from a catheter-related bloodstream infection (CRBSI). The single most critical cue to emphasize is the persistent hemodynamic deterioration despite the fluid bolus, as it signals progression toward septic shock.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应意识到，这一系列临床表现（中性粒细胞减少患者发热、对液体复苏无反应的血流动力学不稳定、乳酸升高以及新发PICC穿刺部位红斑）最符合脓毒症，很可能源于导管相关血流感染（CRBSI）。最需强调的关键线索是尽管推注了液体但血流动力学仍持续恶化，因为这预示着正向脓毒性休克进展。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize systemic, life-threatening hypotheses (sepsis) over localized (site infection) or less acutely critical (dehydration) explanations when signs of shock (hypotension unresponsive to fluids, rising lactate) are present.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当出现休克体征（对补液无反应的低血压、乳酸升高）时，应优先考虑全身性、危及生命的假设（脓毒症），而不是局部的（部位感染）或急性危险较低的（脱水）解释。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2439,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Parenteral Nutrition","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,82],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the patient's blood glucose is 324 mg/dL and rising despite sliding-scale insulin coverage, and the TPN infusion continues at 85 mL/hr. What is the most appropriate nursing action?","fullStemZh":"在第1阶段，尽管使用了滑动标尺法胰岛素，患者的血糖仍升至 324 mg/dL 且呈上升趋势，同时TPN继续以 85 mL/hr 的速度输注。最适当的护理措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the most appropriate nursing action?","terminalSentenceZh":"最适当的护理措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the patient's blood glucose is 324 mg/dL and rising despite sliding-scale insulin coverage, and the TPN infusion continues at 85 mL/hr.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第1阶段，尽管使用了滑动标尺法胰岛素，患者的血糖仍升至 324 mg/dL 且呈上升趋势，同时TPN继续以 85 mL/hr 的速度输注。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_D","en":"Pause the TPN for one hour, administer the sliding-scale insulin, and restart the TPN once the blood glucose drops below 200 mg/dL.","zh":"暂停TPN 1小时，给予滑动标尺法胰岛素，并在血糖降至 200 mg/dL 以下后重新开始TPN输注。"},{"id":"opt_B","en":"Independently stop the TPN infusion immediately to prevent severe hyperglycemia from the continuous dextrose load.","zh":"为防止持续输入葡萄糖负荷导致严重高血糖，立即自行停止TPN输注。"},{"id":"opt_A","en":"Notify the provider of the worsening trend and anticipate an order for a continuous insulin infusion and a possible reduction in the TPN rate.","zh":"向医生报告恶化的血糖趋势，预期医生会开具持续胰岛素静脉泵入医嘱，并可能降低TPN输注速率。"},{"id":"opt_C","en":"Continue monitoring the blood glucose every 6 hours and administer the sliding-scale insulin as ordered.","zh":"继续每6小时监测一次血糖，并遵医嘱给予滑动标尺法胰岛素。"}],"correct":["opt_A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should notify the provider that the TPN dextrose load is exceeding the patient's insulin capacity, exacerbated by sepsis-related insulin resistance. The correct approach is rate reduction plus an insulin drip, which requires provider orders. The nurse must not independently stop or adjust the TPN rate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应通知医生，TPN的葡萄糖负荷超过了患者的胰岛素调节能力，且脓毒症相关的胰岛素抵抗加剧了这一情况。正确的做法是降低输注速率并使用胰岛素泵，这需要医生的医嘱。护士绝对不能自行停止或调整TPN速率。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a prescribed continuous therapy (like TPN) causes adverse effects, do not independently stop or adjust it without an order. Notify the provider, follow institutional protocol, monitor closely, and prepare to adjust concurrent medications (like insulin) or administer prescribed fluids.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当处方的持续治疗（如TPN）引起不良反应时，不要在无医嘱的情况下自行停止或调整。应通知医生，遵循机构方案，密切监测，并准备调整同期药物（如胰岛素）或遵医嘱给予输液。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2440,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[407,450],"terminalOffsetsZh":[117,130],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the nurse receives the preliminary blood culture report indicating the PICC-drawn culture flagged positive before the peripheral culture. This is highly concerning for a catheter-related bloodstream infection, though not definitive until paired cultures grow the same organism with >2-hour differential time to positivity. In what order should the nurse coordinate the subsequent interventions? (Drag the steps into the correct sequence.)","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，护士收到初步血培养报告，提示PICC抽取的培养早于外周培养报阳。这种情况高度怀疑为导管相关血流感染（CRBSI），但在成对培养物生长出相同病原体且报阳时间差大于2小时之前，尚不能确诊。护士应按什么顺序协调后续的干预措施？（拖动步骤以排出正确的顺序）","terminalSentenceEn":"(Drag the steps into the correct sequence.)","terminalSentenceZh":"拖动步骤以排出正确的顺序）","penultimateSentenceEn":"In what order should the nurse coordinate the subsequent interventions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应按什么顺序协调后续的干预措施？（","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"opt_B","en":"Verify that empiric antibiotic coverage (vancomycin) is actively infusing.","zh":"确认经验性抗生素（万古霉素）正在积极输注。"},{"id":"opt_A","en":"Communicate the early flagging of the PICC culture to the provider.","zh":"向医生报告PICC培养提早报阳的情况。"},{"id":"opt_D","en":"Remove the infected PICC line under provider orders.","zh":"在医生医嘱下拔除受感染的PICC导管。"},{"id":"opt_C","en":"Coordinate with the provider for an alternative central access and glycemic management plan.","zh":"与医生协调替代中心静脉通路及血糖管理方案。"}],"correct":["opt_A","opt_B","opt_C","opt_D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The correct sequence ensures safe escalation and source control without compromising essential therapies. First, communicate the differential time to positivity (early flagging of the PICC culture), which strongly suggests CRBSI. Second, ensure that systemic treatment (empiric antibiotics) is actively treating the bacteremia. Third, coordinate alternative central access and a glucose plan, because removing the patient's only central line will abruptly stop the TPN, risking hypoglycemia. Finally, once the replacement plan is secure, remove the infected PICC line.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正确的顺序确保了安全的病情升级报告和感染源控制，同时不会危及基础治疗。首先，报告培养报阳的时间差（PICC培养早报阳），这强烈提示CRBSI。其次，确保全身性治疗（经验性抗生素）正在积极对抗菌血症。第三，协调替代的中心静脉通路和血糖方案，因为拔除患者唯一的中心静脉导管将突然中止TPN，带来低血糖风险。最后，一旦确立了替代方案，再拔除受感染的PICC导管。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the nursing process and safety principles: Assess/notify (communicate lab result), intervene medically for the acute threat (verify antibiotics), plan for safety consequences (alternative access for TPN), and then perform the invasive procedure (remove line).","testTakingStrategyZh":"运用护理程序和安全原则：评估/报告（沟通化验结果），针对急性威胁进行医疗干预（确认抗生素），制定防范安全后果的计划（准备TPN的替代通路），然后再执行侵入性操作（拔管）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2441,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[174,216],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,66],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the patient has not performed mouth rinses in over 6 hours due to severe pain from confluent mucositis with bleeding, and she refuses further oral care attempts. What is the priority nursing intervention?","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，由于融合性黏膜炎伴出血引起的剧烈疼痛，患者已超过6小时未进行漱口，并拒绝进一步的口腔护理尝试。首要的护理干预措施是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the priority nursing intervention?","terminalSentenceZh":"首要的护理干预措施是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the patient has not performed mouth rinses in over 6 hours due to severe pain from confluent mucositis with bleeding, and she refuses further oral care attempts.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第2阶段，由于融合性黏膜炎伴出血引起的剧烈疼痛，患者已超过6小时未进行漱口，并拒绝进一步的口腔护理尝试。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_B","en":"Use a standard soft-bristle toothbrush to thoroughly clean the oral cavity, as skipping oral care increases the risk of secondary infection.","zh":"使用标准软毛牙刷彻底清洁口腔，因为跳过口腔护理会增加继发感染的风险。"},{"id":"opt_A","en":"Coordinate analgesia (PCA bolus or topical analgesic) 15 to 20 minutes before assisting the patient with atraumatic sodium bicarbonate rinses.","zh":"在协助患者使用无创性碳酸氢钠漱口前15至20分钟，先协调使用镇痛药（PCA单次推注或局部镇痛药）。"},{"id":"opt_D","en":"Forcefully swab the oral cavity with a lemon-glycerin swab to ensure mucosal integrity is maintained despite the patient's refusal.","zh":"不顾患者拒绝，强行使用柠檬甘油棉签擦拭口腔，以确保维持黏膜完整性。"},{"id":"opt_C","en":"Defer all oral care until the patient's pain is completely resolved to avoid causing mucosal trauma against her will.","zh":"推迟所有口腔护理，直到患者疼痛完全缓解，以避免违背其意愿造成黏膜损伤。"}],"correct":["opt_A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Oral care is a critical intervention to reduce secondary infection risk, but it must be facilitated through adequate pain management, not forced. The nurse should coordinate analgesia before care and use atraumatic technique (gentle rinses or ultra-soft/sponge swabs) given the severe thrombocytopenia and bleeding risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"口腔护理是降低继发感染风险的关键干预措施，但必须通过充分的疼痛管理来促成，而不能强迫进行。考虑到严重的血小板减少症和出血风险，护士应在护理前协调镇痛，并使用无创性技术（轻柔漱口或超软/海绵棉签）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In pain management scenarios involving essential care, choose the option that proactively addresses the pain (analgesia beforehand) to allow the necessary intervention to proceed safely.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在涉及必要护理的疼痛管理情境中，选择能主动处理疼痛（事先镇痛）以使必要干预能安全进行的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2442,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,114],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse evaluates the patient's clinical response to the interventions. For each clinical finding, indicate whether it demonstrates \"Clinical Improvement\" or requires \"Ongoing Monitoring/Intervention\".","fullStemZh":"在第3阶段，护士评估患者对干预措施的临床反应。对于每一项临床表现，请指出其表明“临床改善（Clinical Improvement）”还是需要“持续监测/干预（Ongoing Monitoring/Intervention）”。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each clinical finding, indicate whether it demonstrates \"Clinical Improvement\" or requires \"Ongoing Monitoring/Intervention\".","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每一项临床表现，请指出其表明“临床改善（Clinical Improvement）”还是需要“持续监测/干预（Ongoing Monitoring/Intervention）”。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the nurse evaluates the patient's clinical response to the interventions.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第3阶段，护士评估患者对干预措施的临床反应。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"row_A","en":"Lactate decreasing from 3.6 to 1.9 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸从 3.6 mmol/L 降至 1.9 mmol/L"},{"id":"row_B","en":"Blood glucose stabilizing at 180–200 mg/dL on the insulin drip","zh":"在胰岛素滴注下血糖稳定在 180–200 mg/dL"},{"id":"row_C","en":"Triglycerides 280 mg/dL","zh":"甘油三酯 280 mg/dL"},{"id":"row_D","en":"Creatinine plateaued at 1.7 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐停滞在 1.7 mg/dL"},{"id":"row_E","en":"Temperature trending down from 102.9 °F (39.4 °C) to 100.6 °F (38.1 °C)","zh":"体温从 102.9 °F (39.4 °C) 呈下降趋势降至 100.6 °F (38.1 °C)"}],"columns":[{"id":"col_2","en":"Ongoing Monitoring/Intervention","zh":"持续监测/干预"},{"id":"col_1","en":"Clinical Improvement","zh":"临床改善"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"row_A","columnIds":["col_1"]},{"rowId":"row_B","columnIds":["col_1"]},{"rowId":"row_C","columnIds":["col_2"]},{"rowId":"row_D","columnIds":["col_2"]},{"rowId":"row_E","columnIds":["col_1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A decreasing lactate, stabilizing blood glucose, and downtrending temperature all indicate a positive response to sepsis treatment and glycemic management. However, elevated triglycerides related to TPN and a persistently abnormal creatinine require ongoing monitoring and potential future intervention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"乳酸下降、血糖稳定和体温呈下降趋势均表明对脓毒症治疗和血糖管理有积极反应。然而，与TPN相关的甘油三酯升高和持续异常的肌酐需要持续监测及未来潜在的干预。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate trends, not just absolute values. Returning toward baseline (fever, lactate, glucose) is an improvement; values that remain abnormally elevated (triglycerides, creatinine) demand continued vigilance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要评估趋势，而不仅仅是绝对数值。向基线恢复（发热、乳酸、血糖）属于改善；仍处于异常升高的指标（甘油三酯、肌酐）则要求持续警惕。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2443,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_tpn_case_mucositis_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[196,273],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,73],"fullStemEn":"Across the case, the nurse must evaluate the appropriateness of the nutritional delivery method. At Stage 3, the patient can tolerate gentle mouth rinses with coaching but cannot swallow liquids. Is it appropriate to discontinue the TPN and transition to enteral nutrition?","fullStemZh":"在整个病程中，护士必须评估营养支持方式的适当性。在第3阶段，患者在指导下能耐受温和的漱口，但无法吞咽液体。此时停用TPN并过渡到肠内营养是否合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Is it appropriate to discontinue the TPN and transition to enteral nutrition?","terminalSentenceZh":"此时停用TPN并过渡到肠内营养是否合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the patient can tolerate gentle mouth rinses with coaching but cannot swallow liquids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第3阶段，患者在指导下能耐受温和的漱口，但无法吞咽液体。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"opt_C","en":"No, because a newly placed PICC line must be used for TPN for at least 72 hours to ensure catheter patency before any enteral trials can begin.","zh":"不合适，因为新放置的PICC导管必须至少用于TPN输注72小时以确保导管通畅，之后才能开始肠内营养试验。"},{"id":"opt_A","en":"No, because the patient has grade IV mucositis with severe systemic inflammation, and tolerating mouth rinses is not equivalent to tolerating nutritional intake.","zh":"不合适，因为患者患有IV级黏膜炎伴重度全身炎症，能耐受漱口不等于能耐受营养摄入。"},{"id":"opt_B","en":"Yes, because the patient's ability to tolerate sodium bicarbonate rinses indicates sufficient mucosal recovery to safely swallow clear liquids.","zh":"合适，因为患者能耐受碳酸氢钠漱口表明黏膜已充分恢复，可以安全吞咽清流质。"},{"id":"opt_D","en":"Yes, because prolonged TPN dependence significantly increases the risk of another central line infection, making enteral nutrition the safer immediate option.","zh":"合适，因为长期依赖TPN会显著增加再次发生中心静脉导管感染的风险，使肠内营养成为当前更安全的直接选择。"}],"correct":["opt_A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"TPN must be continued. Transitioning to enteral nutrition requires evidence that the mucosa can tolerate intake without aspiration or severe pain. Tolerating small volumes of rinses that are spit out is not equivalent to swallowing nutritional volumes through an ulcerated esophagus.","rationaleCorrectZh":"必须继续TPN。向肠内营养过渡需要有证据表明黏膜能耐受摄入，且不会发生误吸或剧痛。能耐受小剂量的漱口水并吐出，并不等同于能通过有溃疡的食管吞咽营养液量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the intervention to the patient's actual capability. The patient cannot swallow liquids; therefore, oral or enteral feeding requiring swallowing cannot be instituted regardless of the risk profile of parenteral feeding.","testTakingStrategyZh":"干预措施必须与患者的实际能力相匹配。患者无法吞咽液体；因此，无论胃肠外营养的风险状况如何，都无法实施需要吞咽的经口或肠内喂养。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the patient can tolerate gentle mouth rinses with coaching but cannot swallow liquids.","controlSentenceZh":"在第3阶段，患者在指导下能耐受温和的漱口，但无法吞咽液体。"}
{"queueIndex":2444,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.41","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.41.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[1627,1906],"terminalOffsetsZh":[457,568],"fullStemEn":"Status epilepticus refractory to first-line benzodiazepine therapy A 27-year-old woman with a three-year history of generalized tonic-clonic epilepsy, managed with levetiracetam 1,000 mg PO twice daily, is brought to the emergency department by paramedics. She lives alone and was found seizing by a coworker who went to check on her after she failed to appear at work. The coworker reports the patient mentioned feeling \"off\" the previous evening. Paramedics document that generalized tonic-clonic seizure activity was observed on their arrival and that four minutes of continuous convulsive activity had already elapsed per the coworker's estimate. The patient's medication bottles were found at home; the levetiracetam bottle appeared mostly full despite a fill date three weeks ago, raising concern for medication nonadherence. She has no other significant medical history and no known allergies. A peripheral IV (20-gauge, right antecubital) was established in the field and lorazepam 4 mg IV was administered seven minutes into the seizure, followed by a second lorazepam 4 mg IV dose at twelve minutes due to ongoing seizure. She is now arriving at the ED, approximately fifteen minutes into continuous seizure activity.\n\nOn ED arrival the patient is on a stretcher in active generalized tonic-clonic seizure. She is unresponsive, with rhythmic bilateral upper- and lower-extremity tonic-clonic movements, jaw clenching, copious oral secretions, and urinary incontinence. There is no purposeful movement and no response to verbal stimuli. The seizure has not stopped despite two adequate doses of prehospital lorazepam. By definition — continuous convulsive seizure activity lasting longer than five minutes — this meets criteria for status epilepticus, and because the initial benzodiazepines have failed, it is now classified as established status epilepticus requiring urgent second-line therapy.","fullStemZh":"对一线苯二氮䓬类治疗无效的癫痫持续状态 一名27岁女性，有3年全身强直-阵挛性癫痫病史，长期口服左乙拉西坦1000 mg 每日两次，由急救人员送至急诊科。她独居，同事发现她未上班前去探望时发现她正在抽搐。同事反映患者前一天晚上曾提到感觉“不舒服”。急救人员记录他们到达时观察到全身强直-阵挛性癫痫发作，且据同事估计持续抽搐已达4分钟。患者的药瓶在家中被找到；尽管3周前刚开药，但左乙拉西坦药瓶看起来几乎是满的，提示可能存在用药依从性差。患者无其他重要病史及已知过敏史。现场在右侧肘前窝建立了20号外周静脉通路，并在癫痫发作7分钟时静脉注射了4 mg劳拉西泮，由于癫痫持续，在发作12分钟时又给予了第二剂4 mg劳拉西泮。她现在到达急诊科，持续癫痫发作约15分钟。\n\n到达急诊科时，患者躺在平车上，处于活动性全身强直-阵挛性癫痫发作状态。患者无反应，双侧上下肢有节律地强直-阵挛性运动，牙关紧闭，口腔分泌物大量，大/小便失禁。无有目的的运动，对言语刺激无反应。尽管院前给予了两剂充足剂量的劳拉西泮，癫痫发作仍未停止。根据定义——持续惊厥性癫痫发作超过5分钟——这符合癫痫持续状态的标准，并且由于初始苯二氮䓬类药物失败，现在被归类为已确立的癫痫持续状态（established status epilepticus），需要紧急进行二线治疗。","terminalSentenceEn":"By definition — continuous convulsive seizure activity lasting longer than five minutes — this meets criteria for status epilepticus, and because the initial benzodiazepines have failed, it is now classified as established status epilepticus requiring urgent second-line therapy.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据定义——持续惊厥性癫痫发作超过5分钟——这符合癫痫持续状态的标准，并且由于初始苯二氮䓬类药物失败，现在被归类为已确立的癫痫持续状态（established status epilepticus），需要紧急进行二线治疗。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The seizure has not stopped despite two adequate doses of prehospital lorazepam.","penultimateSentenceZh":"尽管院前给予了两剂充足剂量的劳拉西泮，癫痫发作仍未停止。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes the prompt recognition and escalation of care in status epilepticus. First-line failure dictates immediate administration of a second-line antiepileptic like fosphenytoin while monitoring cardiovascular status. As the patient progresses to refractory status epilepticus, respiratory decline necessitates prioritizing definitive airway protection (intubation) before initiating continuous midazolam infusions. Continuous EEG is paramount for confirming the cessation of electrographic seizures (targeting burst-suppression), even after motor movements stop. Finally, identifying and treating secondary complications, such as rhabdomyolysis with aggressive fluid hydration, is crucial for preventing acute kidney injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该病例强调了在癫痫持续状态中及时识别和升级治疗的重要性。一线治疗失败要求立即使用诸如磷苯妥英等二线抗癫痫药物，同时监测心血管状态。当患者进展为难治性癫痫持续状态时，呼吸衰退要求在开始持续输注咪达唑仑之前，优先进行确定性的气道保护（气管插管）。即使在运动性动作停止之后，连续脑电图对于确认脑电癫痫发作的停止（目标为爆发抑制）也是至关重要的。最后，识别并治疗继发性并发症，如通过积极的补液治疗横纹肌溶解，对于预防急性肾损伤至关重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Approach status epilepticus systematically: ensure ABCs (airway priority if impending failure), adhere strictly to medication guidelines (recognizing failure of prior doses), rely on objective data (EEG) over physical observation alone, and proactively manage predictable complications like rhabdomyolysis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"系统性地处理癫痫持续状态：确保气道、呼吸和循环（ABCs，如果即将发生衰竭则气道优先），严格遵守用药指南（识别先前剂量的失败），依赖客观数据（脑电图）而不仅仅是身体观察，并主动处理可预测的并发症，如横纹肌溶解。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2445,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[46,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,42],"fullStemEn":"The nurse receives the patient on ED arrival. Which of the following is the most appropriate interpretation of the patient's current status based on the prehospital report?","fullStemZh":"护士在患者到达急诊科时接收患者。根据院前报告，以下哪项是对患者当前状态最恰当的解读？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following is the most appropriate interpretation of the patient's current status based on the prehospital report?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据院前报告，以下哪项是对患者当前状态最恰当的解读？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse receives the patient on ED arrival.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在患者到达急诊科时接收患者。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The patient requires a third dose of intravenous lorazepam in the ED before progressing to second-line agents.","zh":"患者在急诊科需要注射第三剂静脉劳拉西泮，然后再进展到使用二线药物。"},{"id":"A","en":"The patient is experiencing an expected postictal phase after prehospital treatment.","zh":"患者在接受院前治疗后正经历预期的发作后状态。"},{"id":"D","en":"The patient's continuous seizure activity is likely due to prehospital medication administration errors.","zh":"患者持续的癫痫发作活动很可能是由于院前给药错误导致的。"},{"id":"B","en":"The patient is in established status epilepticus because two adequate doses of first-line therapy have failed.","zh":"患者处于已确立的癫痫持续状态，因为两剂充足剂量的一线治疗已经失败。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Status epilepticus is defined as continuous seizure activity lasting more than five minutes or two or more seizures without return to baseline consciousness. Once adequate benzodiazepine doses have failed, the Neurocritical Care Society and AES guidelines direct immediate administration of a second-line agent. Delay increases morbidity, mortality, and the likelihood of pharmacoresistance. Recognizing the failure of first-line therapy is the critical nursing cue that drives the urgency of escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"癫痫持续状态定义为持续惊厥发作超过 5 分钟或两次及以上发作之间未恢复基线意识。一旦足量的苯二氮䓬类药物失败，神经重症监护学会和 AES 指南指导立即给予二线药物。延迟会增加发病率、死亡率和产生耐药性的可能性。认识到一线治疗失败是推动紧急升级的至关重要的护理线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate the clinical criteria for status epilepticus and recognize when escalation of care is indicated based on the failure of initial interventions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估癫痫持续状态的临床标准，并根据初始干预措施的失败认识到何时有必要进行治疗升级。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2446,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[52,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,56],"fullStemEn":"Review the baseline assessment and laboratory data. For each finding, determine if it indicates a primary cause of the status epilepticus or a secondary consequence of the prolonged seizure.","fullStemZh":"回顾基线评估和实验室数据。对于以下各项发现，请确定它是指示癫痫持续状态的主要原因，还是长时间癫痫发作的继发后果。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, determine if it indicates a primary cause of the status epilepticus or a secondary consequence of the prolonged seizure.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于以下各项发现，请确定它是指示癫痫持续状态的主要原因，还是长时间癫痫发作的继发后果。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the baseline assessment and laboratory data.","penultimateSentenceZh":"回顾基线评估和实验室数据。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Subtherapeutic levetiracetam level","zh":"亚治疗水平的左乙拉西坦"},{"id":"r2","en":"Lactate 6.8 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸 6.8 mmol/L"},{"id":"r3","en":"Bicarbonate 16 mEq/L","zh":"碳酸氢盐 16 mEq/L"},{"id":"r4","en":"Mildly elevated CK (480 U/L)","zh":"CK 轻度升高 (480 U/L)"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Secondary Consequence","zh":"继发后果"},{"id":"c1","en":"Likely Precipitating Factor / Major Contributor","zh":"可能的诱发因素 / 主要促成因素"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Medication nonadherence is a common major contributor to status epilepticus in patients with known epilepsy, and the subtherapeutic levetiracetam level strongly supports this. Identifying this helps the team target therapy while continuing evaluation for other precipitants after stabilization. Lactate elevation and metabolic acidosis (low bicarbonate) are expected consequences of sustained seizure-related muscle activity and do not independently require sodium bicarbonate infusion — they resolve when seizures stop. Early CK elevation is a secondary consequence that flags the need for aggressive IV hydration to prevent myoglobin-induced acute kidney injury.","rationaleCorrectZh":"用药依从性差是已知癫痫患者发生癫痫持续状态的常见主要促成因素，亚治疗水平的左乙拉西坦强烈支持这一点。识别出这一点有助于医疗团队进行靶向治疗，同时在患者稳定后继续评估其他诱因。乳酸升高和代谢性酸中毒（低碳酸氢盐）是持续性癫痫相关肌肉活动带来的预期后果，不需要独立地输注碳酸氢钠——当癫痫发作停止时它们就会消退。早期的 CK 升高是一种继发性后果，提示需要进行积极的静脉补液，以防止肌红蛋白诱发的急性肾损伤。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between the underlying triggers of a condition and the physiological derangements resulting from the condition itself.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分疾病的潜在诱因与由该疾病本身造成的生理机能紊乱。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Review the baseline assessment and laboratory data.","controlSentenceZh":"回顾基线评估和实验室数据。"}
{"queueIndex":2447,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[179,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,60],"fullStemEn":"Review the Clinical Course for Stage 1. The nurse is administering the prescribed fosphenytoin IV. Which of the following are priority nursing interventions during this infusion? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"查看阶段 1 的临床病程。护士正在执行医嘱静脉输注磷苯妥英。在输注期间，以下哪些是优先的护理干预措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which of the following are priority nursing interventions during this infusion?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在输注期间，以下哪些是优先的护理干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Administer the infusion as an IV push over 1-2 minutes.","zh":"在 1-2 分钟内静脉推注该药液。"},{"id":"B","en":"Monitor blood pressure every 5 minutes.","zh":"每 5 分钟监测一次血压。"},{"id":"C","en":"Observe for cessation of seizure activity.","zh":"观察癫痫发作活动是否停止。"},{"id":"A","en":"Maintain continuous cardiac monitoring.","zh":"保持连续心电监护。"},{"id":"E","en":"Ensure the infusion rate does not exceed 150 mg PE/min.","zh":"确保输注速度不超过 150 mg PE/min。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse must monitor for cardiac arrhythmias (continuous telemetry), hypotension (blood pressure every 5 minutes during infusion), and observe for seizure cessation as the therapeutic endpoint. Fosphenytoin can cause QT prolongation, bradycardia, and hypotension through its effect on cardiac sodium channels, particularly at rapid infusion rates. Cardiovascular collapse is a known fatal complication of too-rapid administration. The infusion rate must not exceed 150 mg PE/min.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士必须监测心律失常（连续心电监护）、低血压（输注期间每 5 分钟测一次血压），并观察癫痫发作是否停止作为治疗终点。磷苯妥英通过对心脏钠通道的作用，可能导致 QT 间期延长、心动过缓和低血压，特别是在快速输注时。心血管虚脱是已知的一种因给药过快导致的致命并发症。输注速度不得超过 150 mg PE/min。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify safety parameters for high-alert antiepileptic medications, specifically cardiovascular monitoring requirements and maximum infusion rates.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别高危抗癫痫药物的安全参数，特别是心血管监测要求和最大输注速度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2448,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,274],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,97],"fullStemEn":"Review the Clinical Course for Stage 2. The nurse observes that motor seizure activity persists, SpO₂ is 91%, end-tidal CO₂ is 58 mmHg, and the patient has copious secretions with increasing cyanosis. Which of the following problems should the nurse prioritize at this time?","fullStemZh":"查看阶段 2 的临床病程。护士观察到运动性癫痫发作活动仍在持续，SpO₂ 为 91%，呼气末 CO₂ 为 58 mmHg，并且患者有大量分泌物伴有逐渐加重的发绀。此时护士应优先解决以下哪个问题？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following problems should the nurse prioritize at this time?","terminalSentenceZh":"此时护士应优先解决以下哪个问题？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes that motor seizure activity persists, SpO₂ is 91%, end-tidal CO₂ is 58 mmHg, and the patient has copious secretions with increasing cyanosis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士观察到运动性癫痫发作活动仍在持续，SpO₂ 为 91%，呼气末 CO₂ 为 58 mmHg，并且患者有大量分泌物伴有逐渐加重的发绀。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Refractory seizure activity requiring additional antiepileptics","zh":"难治性癫痫发作活动，需要额外的抗癫痫药物"},{"id":"B","en":"Developing rhabdomyolysis","zh":"发展中的横纹肌溶解"},{"id":"C","en":"Compromised airway and impending respiratory failure","zh":"气道受损和即将发生的呼吸衰竭"},{"id":"A","en":"Worsening metabolic acidosis","zh":"恶化的代谢性酸中毒"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Even though terminating the seizure is the ultimate goal, the patient cannot survive the seizure if she cannot oxygenate and ventilate. The falling SpO₂, rising CO₂, and copious secretions signal impending respiratory failure. Applying the ABCs framework, airway protection through intubation takes precedence. Furthermore, the continuous infusion agents used for refractory status epilepticus (midazolam, propofol) cause respiratory depression and require a secured airway before they can be safely administered. Therefore, intubation both protects the patient's breathing and enables definitive seizure treatment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管终止癫痫发作是最终目标，但如果患者不能进行氧合和通气，她将无法在癫痫发作中存活下来。SpO₂ 下降、CO₂ 升高以及大量分泌物标志着呼吸衰竭即将来临。应用 ABCs 框架，通过气管插管保护气道具有优先权。此外，用于难治性癫痫持续状态的持续输注药物（咪达唑仑、丙泊酚）会导致呼吸抑制，并且需要确保气道安全才能安全给药。因此，气管插管既保护了患者的呼吸，也使决定性的抗癫痫治疗成为可能。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the Airway, Breathing, Circulation (ABC) prioritization framework. When a patient has an acute airway issue, it takes precedence over secondary complications or definitive treatments that require a secure airway.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用气道、呼吸、循环（ABC）优先级框架。当患者出现急性气道问题时，它优先于继发性并发症或需要确保气道安全才能进行的决定性治疗。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2449,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[40,131],"terminalOffsetsZh":[13,47],"fullStemEn":"Review the Clinical Course for Stage 3. Visible motor seizure activity has ceased 10 minutes after starting the midazolam infusion.","fullStemZh":"查看阶段 3 的临床病程。在开始咪达唑仑输注 10 分钟后，可见的运动性癫痫发作活动已经停止。","terminalSentenceEn":"Visible motor seizure activity has ceased 10 minutes after starting the midazolam infusion.","terminalSentenceZh":"在开始咪达唑仑输注 10 分钟后，可见的运动性癫痫发作活动已经停止。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Review the Clinical Course for Stage 3.","penultimateSentenceZh":"查看阶段 3 的临床病程。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should interpret that the seizure {{1}} because {{2}}.","zh":"护士应该理解，该癫痫发作 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"will resume within 5 minutes","zh":"将在 5 分钟内恢复"},{"id":"o1","en":"has been fully terminated","zh":"已被完全终止"},{"id":"o2","en":"may be continuing electrographically","zh":"可能仍在脑电水平上继续"}],"correct":"o2"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"cessation of visible motor activity does not equal seizure termination","zh":"可见运动活动的停止并不等于癫痫发作终止"},{"id":"o2","en":"the midazolam dose is too low to produce any effect","zh":"咪达唑仑剂量太低以至于无法产生任何效果"},{"id":"o3","en":"the patient is paralyzed from the succinylcholine alone","zh":"患者仅仅因为琥珀胆碱而处于瘫痪状态"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In status epilepticus, especially after prolonged seizure activity and the administration of neuromuscular blocking agents during RSI (succinylcholine), motor manifestations may cease while cortical seizure activity continues — this is called nonconvulsive status epilepticus. Ongoing electrographic seizure activity causes continued neuronal injury. Continuous EEG is the gold standard for confirming seizure termination. In this case, the ordered therapeutic target for the continuous midazolam infusion is burst-suppression on EEG.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在癫痫持续状态中，特别是在长时间的癫痫发作活动以及在 RSI 期间给予神经肌肉阻滞剂（琥珀胆碱）之后，运动表现可能会停止，而皮层癫痫发作活动仍在继续——这被称为非惊厥性癫痫持续状态。持续的脑电癫痫发作活动会导致持续的神经元损伤。连续脑电图是确认癫痫发作终止的黄金标准。在这个病例中，持续输注咪达唑仑的医嘱治疗目标是达到脑电图上的爆发抑制。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember that neuromuscular blockade and prolonged exhaustion can mask the outward physical signs of a seizure. Cortical electrical activity must be evaluated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住，神经肌肉阻滞和长时间的衰竭可能会掩盖癫痫发作的外部身体体征。必须对皮层电活动进行评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2450,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus_case_se_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[148,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[50,64],"fullStemEn":"Review the Clinical Course for Stage 3. The patient's urine output over the first ICU hour is 120 mL, and the urine myoglobin is markedly positive. Which of the following nursing actions is most appropriate?","fullStemZh":"查看阶段 3 的临床病程。患者在 ICU 第一个小时的尿量为 120 mL，且尿肌红蛋白呈显著阳性。以下哪项护理干预措施最合适？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which of the following nursing actions is most appropriate?","terminalSentenceZh":"以下哪项护理干预措施最合适？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The patient's urine output over the first ICU hour is 120 mL, and the urine myoglobin is markedly positive.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者在 ICU 第一个小时的尿量为 120 mL，且尿肌红蛋白呈显著阳性。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Decrease the IV fluid rate to 50 mL/hr to prevent fluid volume overload during mechanical ventilation.","zh":"将静脉输液速度降低至 50 mL/hr，以防止机械通气期间的容量超负荷。"},{"id":"B","en":"Titrate IV isotonic fluids up toward 300 mL/hr as ordered to manage rhabdomyolysis.","zh":"按医嘱将静脉等渗液体滴定至接近 300 mL/hr，以处理横纹肌溶解。"},{"id":"D","en":"Remove the indwelling urinary catheter to reduce the risk of catheter-associated infection.","zh":"拔除留置导尿管以降低导管相关感染的风险。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer an IV fluid bolus of dextrose 5% in water to correct metabolic acidosis.","zh":"静脉推注 5% 葡萄糖水溶液以纠正代谢性酸中毒。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sustained tonic-clonic muscle activity causes massive skeletal muscle breakdown, releasing myoglobin into the bloodstream. Myoglobin is freely filtered by the glomerulus and precipitates in renal tubules, causing acute kidney injury. The combination of rising CK, dark urine, and positive urine myoglobin confirms rhabdomyolysis. Early aggressive crystalloid hydration (e.g., isotonic fluids titrated to maintain high urine output per protocol, often 1-3 mL/kg/hr or up to 300 mL/hr) is the cornerstone of prevention of renal failure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"持续的强直-阵挛肌肉活动会导致骨骼肌大量分解，将肌红蛋白释放到血流中。肌红蛋白可自由滤过肾小球并沉淀在肾小管中，引起急性肾损伤。CK 的上升、深色尿液和尿肌红蛋白阳性证实了横纹肌溶解的存在。早期积极的晶体液补液（例如，根据方案将等渗液体滴定以维持高尿量，通常为 1-3 mL/kg/hr 或高达 300 mL/hr）是预防肾衰竭的基石。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the classic triad of rhabdomyolysis (elevated CK, dark urine, positive myoglobin) and associate it with the immediate need for aggressive IV fluid resuscitation to protect the kidneys.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别横纹肌溶解的典型三联征（CK升高、深色尿液、肌红蛋白阳性），并将其与为了保护肾脏而立即需要积极的静脉补液复苏联系起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2451,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.42","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.42.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[218,399],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,99],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: discharge medication reconciliation after total knee arthroplasty A 71-year-old client with atrial fibrillation and chronic kidney disease is preparing for discharge after left total knee arthroplasty. The nurse compares the admission home medication list, inpatient MAR, and discharge prescription list and identifies possible medication discrepancies before prescriptions are sent.","fullStemZh":"展开案例：全膝关节置换术后出院用药核对 一名71岁患者有心房颤动和慢性肾病，左全膝关节置换术后准备出院。护士在处方发送前，将入院家庭用药清单、住院给药记录和出院处方清单进行比较，发现可能的用药差异。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse compares the admission home medication list, inpatient MAR, and discharge prescription list and identifies possible medication discrepancies before prescriptions are sent.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士在处方发送前，将入院家庭用药清单、住院给药记录和出院处方清单进行比较，发现可能的用药差异。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: discharge medication reconciliation after total knee arthroplasty A 71-year-old client with atrial fibrillation and chronic kidney disease is preparing for discharge after left total knee arthroplasty.","penultimateSentenceZh":"展开案例：全膝关节置换术后出院用药核对 一名71岁患者有心房颤动和慢性肾病，左全膝关节置换术后准备出院。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes that discharge medication reconciliation is an active safety process, not a paperwork step. The nurse detects two discrepancies before prescriptions are transmitted: a duplicate anticoagulant entry and an unsupported metformin dose increase. Because anticoagulants are high-risk medications and the client has reduced kidney function, the nurse prevents the list from reaching the pharmacy, clarifies the orders with the prescriber, brings in the pharmacist for formal reconciliation, verifies the final corrected list, teaches the client and caregiver using the verified plan, and documents the full closed-loop intervention. Perioperative bridging plans are individualized; the safe nursing judgment is to verify this client's final discharge plan before the family follows it.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例强调，出院用药核对是主动的安全流程，而不是单纯文书步骤。护士在处方发送前发现两个差异：抗凝药重复条目，以及缺乏依据的二甲双胍剂量增加。由于抗凝药属于高风险用药，且患者肾功能下降，护士阻止清单进入药房流程，与开方者澄清医嘱，邀请药师进行正式用药核对，核实最终更正清单，使用已核实方案对患者和照护者宣教，并记录完整闭环干预。围手术期桥接抗凝方案需要个体化处理；安全的护理判断是先核实该患者最终出院方案，再让家属按方案执行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding medication-reconciliation cases, follow the chain: recognize discrepancies, prioritize the highest-harm medication risk, clarify through the correct discipline, verify the final list, teach from the verified list, and document the loop.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在展开式用药核对案例中，按以下链条思考：识别差异，优先处理潜在伤害最大的用药风险，通过正确专业人员澄清，核实最终清单，基于已核实清单宣教，并记录闭环。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2452,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"For each finding in Stage 1, classify whether it requires clarification before discharge prescriptions are transmitted.","fullStemZh":"针对阶段1中的每项发现，判断在出院处方发送前是否需要澄清。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding in Stage 1, classify whether it requires clarification before discharge prescriptions are transmitted.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对阶段1中的每项发现，判断在出院处方发送前是否需要澄清。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Discharge list includes warfarin 5 mg daily and enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously daily for 14 days.","zh":"出院清单同时列有华法林5 mg每日一次和依诺肝素40 mg皮下注射每日一次，共14天。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Discharge list changes metformin to 1000 mg twice daily, while the verified home list and MAR show 500 mg twice daily.","zh":"出院清单将二甲双胍改为1000 mg每日两次，而已核实的家庭用药清单和给药记录均为500 mg每日两次。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Hemoglobin is 10.8 g/dL and stable compared with postoperative day 1.","zh":"血红蛋白10.8 g/dL，与术后第1天相比稳定。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Left knee incision is clean, dry, and intact with mild surrounding ecchymosis.","zh":"左膝切口清洁、干燥、完整，周围轻度瘀斑。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Lisinopril and amlodipine doses match the verified home medication list.","zh":"赖诺普利和氨氯地平剂量与已核实的家庭用药清单一致。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Does not require medication-order clarification","zh":"不需要进行用药医嘱澄清"},{"id":"c1","en":"Clarify before discharge","zh":"出院前需澄清"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The simultaneous warfarin/enoxaparin discharge entries and unexplained metformin dose increase are medication-reconciliation discrepancies that must be clarified before prescriptions are transmitted. The stable hemoglobin, expected incision findings, and unchanged antihypertensive doses do not by themselves indicate a discharge medication-order discrepancy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"华法林与依诺肝素同时出现在出院清单上，以及二甲双胍剂量无依据增加，都是在处方发送前必须澄清的用药核对差异。血红蛋白稳定、切口表现符合预期、降压药剂量未改变，本身并不提示出院用药医嘱差异。","testTakingStrategyEn":"During medication reconciliation, compare lists for additions, omissions, dose changes, duplications, and route/frequency changes; then prioritize high-alert medications.","testTakingStrategyZh":"进行用药核对时，比较清单中的新增、遗漏、剂量改变、重复用药以及给药途径/频次改变；随后优先处理高警示药物。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2453,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,85],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Which action should the nurse take first after identifying the Stage 1 discrepancies?","fullStemZh":"发现阶段1中的差异后，护士应首先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first after identifying the Stage 1 discrepancies?","terminalSentenceZh":"发现阶段1中的差异后，护士应首先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Delete enoxaparin from the list because the nurse recognizes it as a duplicate anticoagulant.","zh":"护士发现依诺肝素是重复抗凝药，因此自行从清单中删除。"},{"id":"D","en":"Proceed with teaching because the client has no current signs of bleeding.","zh":"由于患者目前没有出血征象，因此继续进行出院宣教。"},{"id":"A","en":"Transmit the prescriptions so the pharmacy can begin filling them, then call about the metformin dose.","zh":"先发送处方让药房开始配药，然后再致电询问二甲双胍剂量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the discharge prescription transmission and clarify the duplicate anticoagulant and metformin dose with the prescriber.","zh":"暂缓发送出院处方，并与开方者澄清抗凝药重复和二甲双胍剂量问题。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should stop the prescriptions from reaching the outpatient pharmacy until the prescriber clarifies both discrepancies. Duplicate anticoagulant therapy is the more urgent safety concern, but the unverified metformin dose change also requires resolution. The nurse should not independently alter a prescribed discharge medication list.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应在开方者澄清两个差异前，阻止处方发送至门诊药房。重复抗凝治疗是更紧急的安全问题，但未经核实的二甲双胍剂量改变也必须解决。护士不能自行更改已开具的出院用药清单。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For transition-of-care questions, ask what action prevents the error from reaching the client while staying within nursing scope.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到交接/出院过渡问题时，思考哪项措施既能阻止错误到达患者，又符合护士职责范围。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2454,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[163,185],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,55],"fullStemEn":"The resident is unsure whether the metformin dose change was intentional and says the enoxaparin was not meant to continue. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"住院医师不确定二甲双胍剂量改变是否有意为之，并表示依诺肝素并非打算继续使用。哪些护理行动合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理行动合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Recheck the final discharge list against the verified home list, MAR, and pharmacist documentation before teaching.","zh":"宣教前将最终出院清单与已核实家庭用药清单、给药记录和药师记录再次核对。"},{"id":"A","en":"Request that discharge prescriptions remain on hold until corrected orders are entered.","zh":"要求在录入更正医嘱前继续暂缓出院处方。"},{"id":"D","en":"Remove enoxaparin from the discharge list after the resident verbally agrees it should come off.","zh":"住院医师口头同意删除后，护士自行将依诺肝素从出院清单中移除。"},{"id":"C","en":"Consult the clinical pharmacist to verify the medication history and outpatient dispensing record.","zh":"咨询临床药师，核实用药史和门诊配药记录。"},{"id":"F","en":"Tell the daughter that both anticoagulants should be continued until the INR is therapeutic unless bleeding occurs.","zh":"告诉女儿，在INR达到治疗范围前应继续两种抗凝药，除非发生出血。"},{"id":"B","en":"Ask the prescriber to enter any needed medication changes rather than changing the discharge list independently.","zh":"要求开方者录入所需用药更改，而不是护士自行修改出院清单。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Appropriate actions include keeping prescriptions on hold, obtaining corrected provider orders, involving the pharmacist for formal reconciliation, and closing the loop by rechecking the final list. The nurse should not independently remove medications or give family teaching that contradicts the verified discharge plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"合适的行动包括继续暂缓处方、取得更正后的医嘱、请药师进行正式用药核对，并通过再次核对最终清单完成闭环。护士不应自行删除药物，也不应给予与已核实出院方案相矛盾的家属宣教。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a prescriber is uncertain, use escalation and verification resources; do not solve order conflicts by acting outside nursing authority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当开方者不确定时，应使用上报和核实资源；不要通过超出护士权限的行为解决医嘱冲突。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2455,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,37],"fullStemEn":"After the pharmacist verifies the errors and the resident enters corrected discharge orders, place the nursing actions in the best sequence.","fullStemZh":"药师核实错误且住院医师录入更正后的出院医嘱后，请将护理行动按最佳顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"After the pharmacist verifies the errors and the resident enters corrected discharge orders, place the nursing actions in the best sequence.","terminalSentenceZh":"药师核实错误且住院医师录入更正后的出院医嘱后，请将护理行动按最佳顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Use teach-back to verify warfarin precautions, metformin dose, and follow-up appointments.","zh":"使用回授法核实华法林注意事项、二甲双胍剂量和复诊安排。"},{"id":"A","en":"Compare the corrected discharge prescriptions with the verified home list and pharmacist reconciliation documentation.","zh":"将更正后的出院处方与已核实家庭用药清单和药师用药核对记录进行比较。"},{"id":"B","en":"Confirm that enoxaparin is removed, metformin is 500 mg twice daily, and INR follow-up instructions are present.","zh":"确认依诺肝素已删除、二甲双胍为500 mg每日两次，并有INR复查说明。"},{"id":"C","en":"Review the corrected medication list, purposes, doses, timing, and safety precautions with the client and daughter.","zh":"与患者和女儿复习更正后的用药清单、用途、剂量、时间和安全注意事项。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document the discrepancies found, communications, corrected orders, teaching, and teach-back response.","zh":"记录发现的差异、沟通内容、更正医嘱、宣教以及回授反应。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first verifies that the corrected list actually matches the pharmacist-supported reconciliation, then confirms the specific high-risk corrections and INR follow-up. Teaching comes after the list is verified; teach-back evaluates understanding; documentation records the full safety intervention and education.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先确认更正后的清单确实与药师支持的用药核对结果一致，然后确认具体的高风险更正和INR随访。只有在清单核实后才进行宣教；回授法用于评估理解；文件记录完整的安全干预和宣教过程。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For ordered-response discharge items, sequence from verification, to teaching, to evaluation of understanding, to documentation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出院相关排序题通常按“核实—宣教—评估理解—记录”的顺序思考。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2456,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[28,39],"fullStemEn":"During Stage 3 teaching, the daughter asks why the client is not continuing the abdominal injections at home. Complete the nurse's teaching statement.","fullStemZh":"在阶段3宣教中，女儿询问为什么患者回家后不继续腹部注射。请完成护士的宣教语句。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nurse's teaching statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护士的宣教语句。","penultimateSentenceEn":"During Stage 3 teaching, the daughter asks why the client is not continuing the abdominal injections at home.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段3宣教中，女儿询问为什么患者回家后不继续腹部注射。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Enoxaparin was used in the hospital as {{1}} while warfarin was being restarted. At home, the client should {{2}} and seek urgent help for {{3}}.","zh":"住院期间，依诺肝素在华法林重新开始期间作为 {{1}} 使用。回家后，患者应 {{2}}，并在出现 {{3}} 时立即求助。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"temporary anticoagulant bridging ordered during the inpatient stay","zh":"住院期间医嘱使用的临时桥接抗凝"},{"id":"o3","en":"a medication for incision pain","zh":"用于切口疼痛的药物"},{"id":"o2","en":"a permanent replacement for warfarin","zh":"华法林的永久替代药"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"continue any injections used in the hospital until all syringes are gone","zh":"继续使用住院时用过的所有注射药，直到针剂用完"},{"id":"o3","en":"stop warfarin until the orthopedic follow-up visit","zh":"暂停华法林直到骨科复诊"},{"id":"o1","en":"follow the corrected discharge list and not add injections unless specifically prescribed and verified","zh":"遵循更正后的出院清单，除非有明确且已核实的医嘱，否则不要自行加用注射药物"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"increased appetite after returning home","zh":"回家后食欲增加"},{"id":"o2","en":"mild expected knee soreness after therapy","zh":"治疗后轻度、符合预期的膝部酸痛"},{"id":"o1","en":"blood in urine or stool, prolonged bleeding, severe headache, dizziness, or unusual bruising","zh":"尿中或大便带血、出血不止、严重头痛、头晕或异常瘀斑"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Bridging decisions are individualized and should be taught from the verified discharge orders. In this case, enoxaparin was removed after prescriber-pharmacist clarification, so the family should follow the corrected list and recognize bleeding warning signs while warfarin is continued with INR follow-up.","rationaleCorrectZh":"桥接抗凝决策需要个体化处理，宣教应依据已核实的出院医嘱。本案例中，经开方者和药师澄清后已删除依诺肝素，因此家属应遵循更正后的清单，并在继续华法林和复查INR期间识别出血警示征象。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use patient teaching to close safety gaps: explain the reason for the change, give concrete warning signs, and verify follow-up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"利用患者宣教弥合安全缺口：解释变更原因，给出具体警示征象，并确认随访。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2457,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus1_case_discharge_med_rec_anticoag_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,101],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,26],"fullStemEn":"Which documentation best reflects the nurse's role in this discharge medication-reconciliation event?","fullStemZh":"哪项记录最能体现护士在此次出院用药核对事件中的作用？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which documentation best reflects the nurse's role in this discharge medication-reconciliation event?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项记录最能体现护士在此次出院用药核对事件中的作用？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Client discharged after routine medication teaching. Daughter present.","zh":"患者完成常规用药宣教后出院。女儿在场。"},{"id":"C","en":"Enoxaparin removed from discharge list because it duplicated warfarin; metformin dose corrected by nurse after discussion.","zh":"因依诺肝素与华法林重复，护士已将其从出院清单中删除；讨论后护士更正二甲双胍剂量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Medication discrepancy found, but corrected orders are visible in the electronic health record; no additional documentation needed.","zh":"发现用药差异，但更正医嘱已显示在电子健康记录中；无需额外记录。"},{"id":"B","en":"Resident and pharmacist notified of duplicate anticoagulant and unverified metformin dose; prescriptions held pending clarification; corrected orders verified; warfarin, metformin, bleeding precautions, INR follow-up, and teach-back documented.","zh":"已通知住院医师和药师存在抗凝药重复及二甲双胍剂量未核实；处方在澄清期间暂缓；已核实更正医嘱；已记录华法林、二甲双胍、出血预防、INR随访及回授情况。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Documentation should record the specific discrepancies, escalation to prescriber and pharmacist, the hold on prescriptions, the corrected orders, teaching content, follow-up, and teach-back response. This supports continuity of care and creates an audit trail without claiming the nurse independently changed prescriptions.","rationaleCorrectZh":"记录应包括具体差异、向开方者和药师上报、暂缓处方、更正医嘱、宣教内容、随访安排和回授反应。这有助于照护连续性并形成审计轨迹，同时不声称护士独立更改了处方。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Good documentation is specific, objective, chronological, and clear about who performed each action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"良好的记录应具体、客观、按时间顺序，并清楚说明每项行动由谁执行。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2458,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.43","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.43.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[182,361],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,113],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: postoperative opioid-induced respiratory depression A postoperative client with obstructive sleep apnea becomes difficult to arouse after repeated IV morphine doses. The nurse must recognize opioid-related respiratory compromise, intervene at the bedside, escalate appropriately, anticipate titrated naloxone, and monitor for recurrent sedation.","fullStemZh":"进展性案例：术后阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制 一名有阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停病史的术后患者在多次接受静脉吗啡后变得难以唤醒。护士需要识别阿片类药物相关的呼吸受损，立即采取床旁干预，适当升级处理，预期按规程小剂量滴定纳洛酮，并监测再次镇静。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must recognize opioid-related respiratory compromise, intervene at the bedside, escalate appropriately, anticipate titrated naloxone, and monitor for recurrent sedation.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士需要识别阿片类药物相关的呼吸受损，立即采取床旁干预，适当升级处理，预期按规程小剂量滴定纳洛酮，并监测再次镇静。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: postoperative opioid-induced respiratory depression A postoperative client with obstructive sleep apnea becomes difficult to arouse after repeated IV morphine doses.","penultimateSentenceZh":"进展性案例：术后阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制 一名有阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停病史的术后患者在多次接受静脉吗啡后变得难以唤醒。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on recognizing and managing postoperative opioid-induced respiratory depression in a high-risk client. The key clinical judgment is to connect the timing after repeated IV morphine doses with new somnolence, shallow bradypnea, oxygen desaturation, and miosis, while noting that the dry dressing and stable drain output make bleeding less likely as the primary cause. Nursing priorities progress from stopping further opioid exposure and supporting airway/breathing, to escalating when stimulation and oxygen are insufficient, to anticipating protocol- or order-based titrated IV naloxone. After initial reversal, the client still requires close monitoring because opioid effects can recur as naloxone wanes, and the pain plan should be revised using safer multimodal strategies and OSA precautions such as CPAP during sleep when stable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例重点是识别并处理高风险患者术后阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制。关键临床判断是将多次静脉吗啡给药后的时间关系，与新发嗜睡、浅慢呼吸、血氧下降和瞳孔缩小联系起来，同时注意敷料干燥和引流量稳定，使出血作为主要原因的可能性较低。护理优先事项从停止进一步阿片暴露、支持气道和呼吸，发展到当刺激和给氧不足时升级处理，并预期按规程或医嘱小剂量滴定静脉纳洛酮。初步逆转后，患者仍需密切监测，因为纳洛酮作用减弱后阿片效应可能复发；镇痛方案应采用更安全的多模式策略，并在患者稳定后落实OSA相关措施，如睡眠时使用CPAP。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding cases, track how the same problem evolves over time. A client who improves after naloxone is not automatically safe; compare drug durations, reassess trends, and prevent recurrence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在进展性案例中，要追踪同一问题如何随时间变化。纳洛酮后改善并不代表患者自动安全；要比较药物作用持续时间、重新评估趋势并预防复发。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2459,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,60],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,20],"fullStemEn":"At 0830, how should the nurse interpret each assessment cue?","fullStemZh":"0830时，护士应如何解读每项评估线索？","terminalSentenceEn":"At 0830, how should the nurse interpret each assessment cue?","terminalSentenceZh":"0830时，护士应如何解读每项评估线索？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"POSS score 3; opens eyes only briefly with loud voice and firm tactile stimulation","zh":"POSS 3分；仅在大声呼唤和较强触觉刺激后短暂睁眼"},{"id":"r2","en":"RR 8/min and shallow with SpO2 89% on room air","zh":"呼吸8次/分且浅，室内空气SpO2 89%"},{"id":"r3","en":"Pupils 2 mm bilaterally, constricted but reactive","zh":"双侧瞳孔2 mm，缩小但对光反应存在"},{"id":"r4","en":"Abdominal dressing dry and Jackson-Pratt output not appreciably increased","zh":"腹部敷料干燥，Jackson-Pratt引流量无明显增加"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Would more strongly support bleeding or hypovolemia","zh":"更支持出血或低血容量"},{"id":"c3","en":"Decreases concern for bleeding as the primary cause","zh":"降低出血作为主要原因的可能性"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports opioid-induced respiratory depression","zh":"支持阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most concerning pattern is new oversedation with hypoventilation, oxygen desaturation, and miosis within the expected post-IV morphine effect window. The dry dressing and unchanged drain output make active surgical bleeding less likely as the primary explanation, although perfusion and urine output still require monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最令人担忧的模式是在静脉吗啡作用时间窗内出现新的过度镇静、通气不足、血氧下降和瞳孔缩小。敷料干燥且引流量无明显变化，使活动性手术出血作为主要解释的可能性降低，但灌注和尿量仍需监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster cues instead of chasing one abnormal value. Sedation plus slow respirations plus miosis after an opioid is more specific than a mild blood pressure drop alone.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把线索组合起来判断，不要只追一个异常数值。使用阿片类药物后出现镇静、呼吸减慢和瞳孔缩小，比单独轻度血压下降更具特异性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2460,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[98,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,35],"fullStemEn":"At 0830, which immediate nursing actions are appropriate while the nurse remains with the client? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"0830时，护士留在患者身边时应立即采取哪些护理措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0830, which immediate nursing actions are appropriate while the nurse remains with the client?","penultimateSentenceZh":"0830时，护士留在患者身边时应立即采取哪些护理措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Use loud verbal and tactile stimulation to encourage breathing and assess arousability.","zh":"使用大声语言和触觉刺激以促进呼吸并评估可唤醒程度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold any further opioid dose and reassess sedation and respiratory status before additional analgesia is given.","zh":"暂停任何进一步阿片类药物给药，并在给予额外镇痛前重新评估镇静和呼吸状态。"},{"id":"F","en":"Administer another IV morphine dose if the client wakes and reports severe pain.","zh":"如果患者醒来并报告剧烈疼痛，则再给予一次静脉吗啡。"},{"id":"D","en":"Apply supplemental oxygen and continue close respiratory monitoring.","zh":"给予补充氧气并继续密切监测呼吸。"},{"id":"C","en":"Reposition the client to support the airway, such as elevating the head of bed as tolerated.","zh":"调整患者体位以支持气道，例如在可耐受情况下抬高床头。"},{"id":"E","en":"Document that the client is sleeping and return in 30 minutes to allow rest.","zh":"记录患者正在睡眠，30分钟后再回来以便其休息。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has opioid oversedation with hypoventilation. Immediate nursing actions focus on preventing additional opioid exposure, stimulating respirations, supporting airway positioning, providing oxygen, and reassessing continuously while escalating if the response is inadequate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者出现阿片类药物过度镇静并伴通气不足。立即护理措施应集中于避免继续暴露于阿片类药物、刺激呼吸、通过体位支持气道、给氧，并在反应不足时持续评估和升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an opioid-treated client has decreased arousal and slow respirations, first stop adding to the cause and support airway and breathing.","testTakingStrategyZh":"接受阿片治疗的患者出现清醒度下降和呼吸减慢时，先停止增加诱因，并支持气道和呼吸。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2461,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[170,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,72],"fullStemEn":"At 0838, the client remains minimally responsive with RR 7/min, snoring respirations, apneic pauses, and SpO2 91% despite stimulation, repositioning, and 2 L/min oxygen. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"0838时，尽管已进行刺激、调整体位并给予2 L/分氧气，患者仍反应极少，呼吸7次/分，有鼾样呼吸、呼吸暂停，SpO2 91%。优先行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"优先行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0838, the client remains minimally responsive with RR 7/min, snoring respirations, apneic pauses, and SpO2 91% despite stimulation, repositioning, and 2 L/min oxygen.","penultimateSentenceZh":"0838时，尽管已进行刺激、调整体位并给予2 L/分氧气，患者仍反应极少，呼吸7次/分，有鼾样呼吸、呼吸暂停，SpO2 91%。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Activate or confirm rapid response activation, notify the provider, support ventilation, and prepare naloxone for administration per protocol or order.","zh":"启动或确认快速反应团队已启动，通知医务人员，支持通气，并准备按规程或医嘱给予纳洛酮。"},{"id":"A","en":"Continue stimulation and increase oxygen flow; reassess in 15 minutes because SpO2 improved from 89% to 91%.","zh":"继续刺激并增加氧流量；因SpO2从89%升至91%，15分钟后再评估。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer the next PRN morphine dose early because uncontrolled postoperative pain may be causing shallow breathing.","zh":"提前给予下一次按需吗啡，因为未控制的术后疼痛可能导致浅呼吸。"},{"id":"C","en":"Apply the home CPAP machine and delay further escalation unless the oxygen saturation falls below 88%.","zh":"使用家用CPAP机器，除非血氧低于88%，否则暂缓进一步升级处理。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Persistent hypoventilation, apneic pauses, and inability to follow breathing commands after initial measures indicate that conservative bedside measures are not enough. The nurse should bring emergency support to the bedside, notify the prescriber, continue airway and ventilation support, and prepare naloxone according to facility protocol or order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在初始措施后仍持续通气不足、出现呼吸暂停且不能按指令呼吸，说明保守床旁措施不足。护士应将紧急支援带到床旁，通知开具医嘱者，继续支持气道和通气，并按机构规程或医嘱准备纳洛酮。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let a slightly better oxygen saturation distract from ventilation failure. Slow respirations and apnea after opioids are escalation cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要被血氧略有改善分散注意力。阿片类药物后出现呼吸减慢和呼吸暂停，是需要升级处理的线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2462,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Complete the statement about naloxone use for this postoperative client.","fullStemZh":"完成关于该术后患者使用纳洛酮的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement about naloxone use for this postoperative client.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成关于该术后患者使用纳洛酮的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"For this postoperative client with suspected opioid-induced respiratory depression, the nurse should anticipate naloxone by the {{1}} route in {{2}} doses, titrated to improve {{3}} while limiting abrupt loss of analgesia when possible.","zh":"对于这名疑似阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制的术后患者，护士应预期通过 {{1}} 途径给予纳洛酮，采用 {{2}} 剂量滴定，以改善 {{3}}，同时在可能时限制镇痛作用突然丧失。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"oral","zh":"口服"},{"id":"o3","en":"topical","zh":"外用"},{"id":"o1","en":"IV","zh":"静脉"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"one full vial as a rapid bolus","zh":"一整瓶快速推注"},{"id":"o1","en":"small, repeated","zh":"小剂量、可重复"},{"id":"o3","en":"scheduled oral maintenance","zh":"定时口服维持"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"ventilation and arousability","zh":"通气和可唤醒程度"},{"id":"o2","en":"bowel sounds and oral intake","zh":"肠鸣音和经口摄入"},{"id":"o3","en":"drain color and wound approximation","zh":"引流液颜色和切口对合"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"IV naloxone has rapid onset and can be titrated in small repeated doses in a postoperative client when the goal is to restore adequate ventilation and arousability without causing unnecessary abrupt loss of analgesia. The exact dose and dilution should follow the facility protocol or prescriber order; the case uses 0.04 mg IV increments as an example of titration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"静脉纳洛酮起效快，在术后患者中可采用小剂量重复滴定，目标是恢复足够通气和可唤醒程度，同时尽量避免不必要的镇痛突然丧失。具体剂量和稀释方式应遵循机构规程或医嘱；本案例使用0.04 mg静脉递增作为滴定示例。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For reversal agents, match the dose strategy to the clinical goal. In a postoperative client, reverse dangerous respiratory depression without assuming that all analgesia must be eliminated at once.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用逆转药时，要让给药策略匹配临床目标。术后患者需要逆转危险的呼吸抑制，而不是假设必须一次性消除所有镇痛作用。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2463,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[123,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,61],"fullStemEn":"At 0855, the client is awake enough to follow commands after two small IV naloxone doses but reports incisional pain 7/10. What is the nurse's priority concern for the next period of care?","fullStemZh":"0855时，患者在两次小剂量静脉纳洛酮后已能清醒到听从指令，但报告切口疼痛7/10。护士接下来护理阶段的优先关注点是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority concern for the next period of care?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士接下来护理阶段的优先关注点是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0855, the client is awake enough to follow commands after two small IV naloxone doses but reports incisional pain 7/10.","penultimateSentenceZh":"0855时，患者在两次小剂量静脉纳洛酮后已能清醒到听从指令，但报告切口疼痛7/10。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Severe postoperative hemorrhage because the hemoglobin is lower than the preoperative value.","zh":"因血红蛋白低于术前值，发生严重术后出血。"},{"id":"D","en":"Loss of anticoagulation because sequential compression devices have been in place.","zh":"因已使用序贯加压装置，出现抗凝不足。"},{"id":"A","en":"Recurrent sedation and respiratory depression as naloxone effect decreases before the opioid effect has fully resolved.","zh":"纳洛酮作用减弱而阿片类药物效应尚未完全消退时，可能再次出现镇静和呼吸抑制。"},{"id":"B","en":"Immediate bowel obstruction because absent bowel sounds were present at handoff.","zh":"因交接班时肠鸣音消失，立即发生肠梗阻。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After naloxone response, the client can become sedated again if the antagonist effect wanes while the previously administered opioid remains active. The nurse should maintain continuous respiratory and sedation monitoring, keep escalation resources available, hold further opioids until the prescriber revises the plan, and use ordered non-opioid or nonpharmacologic pain measures as appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"纳洛酮起效后，如果拮抗剂作用减弱而此前给予的阿片类药物仍在发挥作用，患者可能再次镇静。护士应持续监测呼吸和镇静程度，保持升级处理资源可用，在开嘱者调整方案前暂停进一步阿片类药物，并按医嘱或适当使用非阿片或非药物止痛措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After an antidote works, ask whether the original drug can outlast the antidote. If yes, monitor for recurrence rather than assuming the crisis is over.","testTakingStrategyZh":"解毒或拮抗药起效后，要问原药效应是否可能持续超过拮抗药。如果是，就要监测复发，而不是假设危机已经结束。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2464,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus2_case_postop_opioid_respiratory_depression_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,49],"fullStemEn":"Which findings or handoff points should the nurse communicate to help reduce recurrence of opioid-induced respiratory depression? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士应在交接或沟通中说明哪些发现或要点，以帮助减少阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制再次发生？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings or handoff points should the nurse communicate to help reduce recurrence of opioid-induced respiratory depression?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在交接或沟通中说明哪些发现或要点，以帮助减少阿片类药物相关呼吸抑制再次发生？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hydrochlorothiazide and pantoprazole are the most likely direct causes of the sedation episode.","zh":"氢氯噻嗪和泮托拉唑最可能是此次镇静事件的直接原因。"},{"id":"B","en":"BMI 38, which increases risk for airway obstruction and opioid-related respiratory compromise.","zh":"BMI 38，会增加气道阻塞和阿片类药物相关呼吸受损风险。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client has obstructive sleep apnea and his CPAP had not been used while he was sleeping or sedated postoperatively.","zh":"患者有阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停，术后睡眠或镇静时未使用CPAP。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client received three IV morphine doses within the same morning-to-shift interval, including the 0745 dose before deterioration.","zh":"患者在同一夜间至早班时段内接受了三次静脉吗啡，包括恶化前0745的给药。"},{"id":"F","en":"The surgical team should reassess the analgesic plan, consider multimodal non-opioid strategies when appropriate, and continue close sedation and respiratory monitoring.","zh":"外科团队应重新评估镇痛方案，在适当时考虑多模式非阿片策略，并继续密切监测镇静和呼吸。"},{"id":"E","en":"Because the client still reports pain, restarting a smaller morphine dose is the safest immediate plan.","zh":"因为患者仍报告疼痛，立即重新开始较小剂量吗啡是最安全计划。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The recurrence-prevention handoff should identify patient-specific and treatment-related risk factors: obstructive sleep apnea without CPAP during sleep/sedation, obesity, and repeated IV morphine exposure. It should also prompt a revised analgesic and monitoring plan rather than simply restarting opioids after naloxone response.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预防复发的交接应明确患者特异性和治疗相关风险因素：阻塞性睡眠呼吸暂停且睡眠/镇静时未用CPAP、肥胖，以及反复静脉吗啡暴露。同时应推动修订镇痛和监测方案，而不是在纳洛酮起效后简单恢复阿片类药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For adverse drug events, identify both modifiable factors and fixed risk factors. Prevention usually requires communication and a revised plan, not only treatment of the acute episode.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于药物不良事件，要同时识别可改变因素和固定风险因素。预防通常需要沟通并修订计划，而不仅是处理急性发作。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2465,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.44","itemType":"case_study","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.44.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,293],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,90],"fullStemEn":"IV Potassium Replacement With NG Suction Losses A postoperative client with high nasogastric output develops severe hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, and ECG changes. The nurse must recognize the urgent electrolyte risk while also preventing harm from an unsafe peripheral potassium chloride order.","fullStemZh":"胃管负压吸引导致丢失后的静脉补钾安全 一名术后患者因胃管引流量大出现严重低钾血症、低镁血症和心电图改变。护士既要识别紧急电解质风险，也要防止执行不安全的外周静脉氯化钾医嘱造成伤害。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must recognize the urgent electrolyte risk while also preventing harm from an unsafe peripheral potassium chloride order.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士既要识别紧急电解质风险，也要防止执行不安全的外周静脉氯化钾医嘱造成伤害。","penultimateSentenceEn":"IV Potassium Replacement With NG Suction Losses A postoperative client with high nasogastric output develops severe hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, and ECG changes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"胃管负压吸引导致丢失后的静脉补钾安全 一名术后患者因胃管引流量大出现严重低钾血症、低镁血症和心电图改变。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case emphasizes two linked nursing judgments: severe hypokalemia with ECG changes requires prompt, monitored replacement, but IV potassium remains a high-alert medication that must be administered only through a safe, clarified order. The nurse should not give potassium chloride by IV push or administer the original peripheral order unchanged. Safe care includes holding the unsafe order, assessing the client and IV site, clarifying the route/rate/concentration with the provider and pharmacist, using pharmacy-prepared diluted infusions and an infusion pump, maintaining telemetry, correcting magnesium, monitoring renal function and repeat electrolytes, and stopping the infusion if peripheral IV-site complications occur.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例强调两个相互关联的护理判断：严重低钾伴心电图改变需要及时、受监测的补充；但静脉氯化钾属于高警示药物，只能在安全且已澄清的医嘱下给药。护士不应静脉推注氯化钾，也不应原样执行不安全的外周静脉医嘱。安全护理包括暂停不安全医嘱，评估患者和静脉部位，与开立医嘱者和药师澄清途径、速度和浓度，使用药房配制的稀释输液和输液泵，维持心电监护，纠正低镁，监测肾功能和复查电解质，并在外周静脉部位出现并发症时停止输注。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not choose an unsafe medication-administration step simply because the client needs the medication urgently; stabilize, verify, clarify, and then administer the corrected order with monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因为患者急需某药就选择不安全的给药步骤；应先稳定和监测，核对并澄清医嘱，然后在监测下执行修正后的医嘱。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2466,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,113],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"For each finding in Stage 1, indicate whether it is expected in the situation or requires follow-up by the nurse.","fullStemZh":"根据阶段1资料，判断每项发现是该情况中的预期表现，还是需要护士跟进。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding in Stage 1, indicate whether it is expected in the situation or requires follow-up by the nurse.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据阶段1资料，判断每项发现是该情况中的预期表现，还是需要护士跟进。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Potassium 2.8 mEq/L","zh":"钾2.8 mEq/L"},{"id":"r2","en":"Magnesium 1.4 mg/dL","zh":"镁1.4 mg/dL"},{"id":"r3","en":"NG output 1,150 mL over 12 hours","zh":"12小时鼻胃管引流量1150毫升"},{"id":"r4","en":"Creatinine 1.1 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐1.1 mg/dL"},{"id":"r5","en":"Flattened T waves, U waves, and occasional PVCs","zh":"T波低平、U波和偶发室性早搏"}],"columns":[{"id":"expected","en":"Expected/no immediate follow-up","zh":"预期/无需立即跟进"},{"id":"follow_up","en":"Requires follow-up","zh":"需要跟进"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["follow_up"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["follow_up"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["follow_up"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["expected"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["follow_up"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority cues are severe hypokalemia, coexisting hypomagnesemia, high NG losses, and ECG changes/PVCs. The creatinine is not elevated in this exhibit, so it does not independently require urgent follow-up, although renal status must still be monitored during potassium therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先线索是严重低钾血症、合并低镁血症、鼻胃管丢失量大，以及心电图改变/室性早搏。该展项中肌酐未升高，因此本身不需要紧急跟进，但补钾过程中仍必须监测肾功能状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When electrolyte values and rhythm cues appear together, connect the lab abnormality to the immediate safety threat rather than treating the number in isolation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当电解质数值和心律线索同时出现时，要把实验室异常与眼前安全威胁联系起来，而不是孤立看数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2467,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,76],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,21],"fullStemEn":"After reviewing the Stage 1 order, which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"查看阶段1医嘱后，护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"After reviewing the Stage 1 order, which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"查看阶段1医嘱后，护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Hold the potassium infusion and clarify the concentration, route, and rate with the provider and pharmacist before administration.","zh":"暂停氯化钾输注，并在给药前与开立医嘱者和药师澄清浓度、途径和速度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Stop telemetry until after potassium replacement is complete to reduce alarm fatigue.","zh":"为减少报警疲劳，在补钾完成前暂停心电监护。"},{"id":"C","en":"Draw potassium chloride into a syringe and administer it slowly through the peripheral IV.","zh":"将氯化钾抽入注射器，经外周静脉缓慢推注。"},{"id":"A","en":"Start the potassium infusion as ordered because the potassium is critically low.","zh":"因钾值危急，按原医嘱立即开始氯化钾输注。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The original order would deliver 40 mEq over 2 hours through a peripheral IV. Even though the client needs urgent replacement, the nurse should not administer an unsafe or nonstandard potassium order unchanged. The priority is to hold the infusion, maintain monitoring, and clarify or revise the order before administration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"原医嘱会经外周静脉在2小时内输注40 mEq。即使患者需要紧急补钾，护士也不应原样执行不安全或非标准的氯化钾医嘱。优先行动是暂停输注、维持监测，并在给药前澄清或修改医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For medication-safety questions, an abnormal lab may explain why treatment is needed, but the nurse still must question an unsafe route, rate, dose, or concentration before giving the drug.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到用药安全题时，异常实验室值说明需要治疗，但护士仍必须在给药前质疑不安全的途径、速度、剂量或浓度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2468,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[108,137],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,45],"fullStemEn":"The original order was potassium chloride 40 mEq IV over 2 hours. How many mEq/hr would this order deliver? Enter the numeric value only.","fullStemZh":"原医嘱为氯化钾40 mEq静脉输注2小时。该医嘱的输注速度为多少mEq/小时？只输入数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the numeric value only.","terminalSentenceZh":"只输入数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many mEq/hr would this order deliver?","penultimateSentenceZh":"该医嘱的输注速度为多少mEq/小时？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mEq/hr","zh":"mEq/小时"},"acceptable":["20","20 mEq/hr","20 mEq/hour"],"numeric":{"value":20,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mEq/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Divide the total dose by the infusion time: 40 mEq ÷ 2 hr = 20 mEq/hr. Calculating the dose rate helps the nurse recognize why the original peripheral order needs clarification before administration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总剂量除以输注时间：40 mEq ÷ 2小时 = 20 mEq/小时。计算剂量速度有助于护士识别为什么原外周静脉医嘱在给药前需要澄清。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Convert every IV electrolyte order into dose per hour before deciding whether the rate is safe for the ordered route and monitoring level.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断静脉电解质医嘱是否安全前，先把医嘱换算成每小时剂量，再结合给药途径和监测等级判断。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2469,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,129],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the safest order after discovering the original peripheral potassium order has not yet been started.","fullStemZh":"发现原外周静脉补钾医嘱尚未开始后，请将护士行动按最安全顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in the safest order after discovering the original peripheral potassium order has not yet been started.","terminalSentenceZh":"发现原外周静脉补钾医嘱尚未开始后，请将护士行动按最安全顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Obtain the revised pharmacy-prepared potassium order and complete the required independent double-check.","zh":"取得药房配制的修改后补钾医嘱，并完成要求的独立双人核对。"},{"id":"E","en":"Start the revised infusion using an infusion pump and monitor telemetry, the IV site, and repeat laboratory results.","zh":"使用输液泵开始修改后的输注，并监测心电、静脉部位和复查实验室结果。"},{"id":"B","en":"Assess the client, verify telemetry is active, review renal function, and assess the peripheral IV site.","zh":"评估患者，确认心电监护开启，查看肾功能，并评估外周静脉部位。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider and pharmacist that the route/rate/concentration require clarification or revision before administration.","zh":"通知开立医嘱者和药师：给药前需要澄清或修改途径、速度和浓度。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold the original potassium infusion and do not administer it as written.","zh":"暂停原氯化钾输注，不按原医嘱执行。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The first safety step is to prevent administration of the unsafe original order. The nurse then gathers relevant assessment data, escalates the concern for clarification or revision, verifies the corrected pharmacy-prepared product with an independent double-check, and only then administers the revised infusion with ongoing monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第一安全步骤是防止执行不安全的原医嘱。随后护士收集相关评估资料，升级沟通以澄清或修改医嘱，核对修正后的药房配制药液并进行独立双人核对，之后才在持续监测下输注修正后的药液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In ordered-response medication questions, do not let an urgent abnormal lab push an unsafe administration step ahead of clarification and verification.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在用药排序题中，不要因为实验室值紧急就把不安全给药步骤排在澄清和核对之前。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2470,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[97,119],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,31],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate when administering the revised potassium replacement plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"执行修改后的补钾方案时，哪些护理行动是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate when administering the revised potassium replacement plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"执行修改后的补钾方案时，哪些护理行动是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Use an infusion pump for each potassium infusion.","zh":"每袋氯化钾输注均使用输液泵。"},{"id":"F","en":"Review repeat potassium, magnesium, and renal function results as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱查看复查的钾、镁和肾功能结果。"},{"id":"C","en":"Assess the peripheral IV site for pain, redness, swelling, or leaking during therapy.","zh":"治疗期间评估外周静脉部位是否有疼痛、发红、肿胀或渗漏。"},{"id":"B","en":"Continue telemetry while replacement is in progress.","zh":"补充过程中继续心电监护。"},{"id":"E","en":"Verify the dose, dilution, route, rate, and client before each bag.","zh":"每袋输注前核对剂量、稀释液、途径、速度和患者身份。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer one bag by IV push if the telemetry strip shows more PVCs.","zh":"如果心电监护显示室性早搏增多，可将其中一袋静脉推注。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Safe potassium administration includes pump-controlled infusion, telemetry when severe hypokalemia or ECG changes are present, frequent IV-site assessment, verification of dose/dilution/route/rate/client, and follow-up laboratory monitoring. IV push potassium is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全补钾包括使用输液泵控制速度、在严重低钾或有心电图改变时进行心电监护、频繁评估静脉部位、核对剂量/稀释液/途径/速度/患者，以及复查实验室结果。氯化钾静脉推注不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For select-all medication items, choose actions that reduce harm before, during, and after administration: verify, control the rate, monitor the patient, and reassess response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在多选用药题中，选择能在给药前、给药中和给药后减少伤害的措施：核对、控制速度、监测患者并复评疗效。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2471,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus3_iv_potassium_safety_case_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,56],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"During Stage 3, which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"在阶段3中，护士下一步应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"During Stage 3, which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段3中，护士下一步应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Stop the potassium infusion, assess the IV site, maintain IV access with a new site as needed, and notify the provider/pharmacist.","zh":"停止氯化钾输注，评估静脉部位，必要时建立新的静脉通路，并通知开立医嘱者/药师。"},{"id":"B","en":"Increase the potassium rate because the potassium is still below the usual reference range.","zh":"因血钾仍低于通常参考范围，提高氯化钾输注速度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Clamp the NG tube for 8 hours so electrolyte levels rise faster.","zh":"夹闭鼻胃管8小时，使电解质水平更快上升。"},{"id":"C","en":"Tell the client burning is expected and continue the infusion until the bag is empty.","zh":"告知患者灼痛属预期反应，继续输注直至该袋输完。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Burning and redness at a peripheral potassium infusion site suggest irritation, phlebitis, infiltration, or early extravasation. The nurse should stop the infusion and assess the site rather than continue or speed the infusion. Ongoing electrolyte replacement can continue only through a safe, verified route.","rationaleCorrectZh":"外周静脉补钾部位出现灼痛和发红，提示刺激、静脉炎、浸润或早期外渗。护士应停止输注并评估部位，而不是继续或加快输注。只有在安全且核实的通路下，才能继续电解质补充。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a treatment is helping but creates a new safety cue, evaluate the new cue before continuing the intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当治疗有效但出现新的安全线索时，应先评估新的线索，再决定是否继续干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2472,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.45","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.45.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[211,411],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,117],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: SBAR escalation for postoperative deterioration after open cholecystectomy A 72-year-old client is postoperative day 1 after open cholecystectomy for acute cholecystitis with gangrenous changes. The nurse must determine whether subtle changes represent expected recovery or evolving hemorrhagic shock, communicate the trend clearly, and escalate when the initial provider response is inadequate.","fullStemZh":"展开案例：开腹胆囊切除术后病情恶化的 SBAR 升级沟通 一名 72 岁患者因急性胆囊炎伴坏疽性改变接受开腹胆囊切除术后第 1 天。护士需要判断细微变化是预期恢复还是逐渐发展的出血性休克，清楚沟通趋势，并在初始医嘱回应不足时及时升级。","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse must determine whether subtle changes represent expected recovery or evolving hemorrhagic shock, communicate the trend clearly, and escalate when the initial provider response is inadequate.","terminalSentenceZh":"护士需要判断细微变化是预期恢复还是逐渐发展的出血性休克，清楚沟通趋势，并在初始医嘱回应不足时及时升级。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: SBAR escalation for postoperative deterioration after open cholecystectomy A 72-year-old client is postoperative day 1 after open cholecystectomy for acute cholecystitis with gangrenous changes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"展开案例：开腹胆囊切除术后病情恶化的 SBAR 升级沟通 一名 72 岁患者因急性胆囊炎伴坏疽性改变接受开腹胆囊切除术后第 1 天。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires the nurse to synthesize multiple subtle but converging cues rather than normalizing each cue in isolation. The worsening tachycardia, falling blood pressure, declining oxygen saturation, new confusion, oliguria, expanding dressing stain, increasingly sanguineous drain output, rising lactate, and falling hemoglobin form a coherent picture of postoperative hemorrhage with evolving shock. The nurse appropriately uses SBAR to present the trajectory, requests timely bedside assessment, and invokes the chain of command when the first provider response does not match the client’s deterioration. Subsequent evaluation shows persistent hypoperfusion despite initial fluid, supporting urgent blood availability and operative source control. Safe nursing care includes monitoring, maintaining IV access, escalating promptly, avoiding delay for routine charting or tasks, verifying that the appropriate consent process is handled by the surgical team or per policy, and giving a complete SBAR handoff to the OR team.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例要求护士综合多个细微但方向一致的线索，而不是把每个异常单独解释为术后常见现象。心率逐渐增快、血压下降、血氧饱和度下降、新发意识混乱、少尿、敷料渗染扩大、引流液越来越血性、乳酸升高和血红蛋白下降，共同构成术后出血并逐渐进展为休克的图像。护士应使用 SBAR 呈现病情轨迹，请求及时床旁评估；当初始医嘱回应与患者恶化程度不匹配时，应按指挥链升级。后续评估显示初始补液后仍存在低灌注，因此需要确保血制品可用并进行手术控制出血源。安全护理包括持续监测、维持静脉通路、及时升级、避免因常规记录或任务延误处理、核实外科团队或政策规定的同意流程已启动，并向手术室团队进行完整的 SBAR 交接。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding cases, compare each new finding with the client’s baseline and look for several systems changing in the same direction. A provider’s reassurance does not override objective deterioration; choose the action that protects the client and escalates the concern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做展开案例时，要把每个新发现与患者基线比较，并寻找多个系统是否朝同一方向变化。医务人员的安慰性回应不能取代客观恶化证据；应选择保护患者并升级关注的行动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2473,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,51],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: For each finding, classify whether it is a cue supporting escalation for clinical deterioration or a finding that can be managed/monitored when not accompanied by other concerning changes.","fullStemZh":"阶段 1：请判断每项发现是支持因临床恶化而升级处理的线索，还是在没有其他危险变化时可处理/监测的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: For each finding, classify whether it is a cue supporting escalation for clinical deterioration or a finding that can be managed/monitored when not accompanied by other concerning changes.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 1：请判断每项发现是支持因临床恶化而升级处理的线索，还是在没有其他危险变化时可处理/监测的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Heart rate increases from 82 to 102 while blood pressure falls from 134/78 to 112/68","zh":"心率从 82 增至 102，同时血压从 134/78 降至 112/68"},{"id":"r2","en":"New intermittent confusion in a client who was oriented and conversational at 0700","zh":"0700 时定向力正常且能交谈的患者出现新的间歇性意识混乱"},{"id":"r3","en":"Jackson-Pratt output becomes increasingly sanguineous and the dressing stain expands","zh":"Jackson-Pratt 引流越来越血性，敷料渗染扩大"},{"id":"r4","en":"Urine output declines to 20 mL in the 1000–1100 hour","zh":"1000–1100 这一小时尿量降至 20 mL"},{"id":"r5","en":"Hypoactive bowel sounds on postoperative day 1 after open abdominal surgery","zh":"开腹手术后第 1 天肠鸣音减弱"},{"id":"r6","en":"Incisional pain rated 5/10 during the first ambulation attempt","zh":"首次尝试下床活动时切口痛评分 5/10"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Supports escalation for deterioration","zh":"支持因恶化而升级处理"},{"id":"c2","en":"Manage/monitor if isolated","zh":"若单独出现可处理/监测"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The priority cues are not isolated postoperative discomforts; they show worsening perfusion and possible bleeding. Tachycardia with falling blood pressure, acute mental-status change, increasing sanguineous drainage with expanding staining, and declining urine output require prompt escalation. Hypoactive bowel sounds and moderate incisional pain can occur after open abdominal surgery and should be managed and monitored, but they do not by themselves explain the broader deterioration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"优先线索不是孤立的术后不适，而是显示灌注恶化和可能出血。心率增快伴血压下降、急性意识改变、血性引流增加且敷料渗染扩大、尿量下降，都需要迅速升级处理。开腹手术后肠鸣音减弱和中等切口痛可以出现，应处理并监测，但单独并不能解释整体恶化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Trend beats snapshot. Mark findings as concerning when they show acute change from baseline or end-organ hypoperfusion, especially when several cues move together.","testTakingStrategyZh":"趋势比单次数据更重要。若发现相对基线急性改变或终末器官低灌注，尤其多个线索同时变化，应判为危险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2474,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Which hypothesis best explains the overall pattern of findings at 1100?","fullStemZh":"阶段 1：哪一项假设最能解释 1100 时的整体发现模式？","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Which hypothesis best explains the overall pattern of findings at 1100?","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 1：哪一项假设最能解释 1100 时的整体发现模式？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Opioid-related sedation as the primary cause of the client’s change","zh":"阿片类药物相关镇静是患者变化的主要原因"},{"id":"A","en":"Expected inflammatory response after open abdominal surgery","zh":"开腹手术后的预期炎症反应"},{"id":"C","en":"Postoperative hemorrhage with evolving hypovolemic shock","zh":"术后出血并逐渐进展为低血容量性休克"},{"id":"D","en":"Pulmonary embolism as the most likely immediate explanation","zh":"肺栓塞是最可能的即时解释"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The cluster of falling blood pressure, rising heart rate, declining urine output, new confusion, expanding dressing staining, and increasing sanguineous drain output is most consistent with postoperative bleeding and evolving hypovolemic shock. A low-grade fever and leukocytosis may coexist after surgery or with infection risk, but they do not explain the hemorrhagic drainage and hemoperfusion pattern. Opioids can contribute to sedation, but they should not be accepted as the primary explanation when perfusion indicators are worsening.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血压下降、心率升高、尿量减少、新发意识混乱、敷料渗染扩大以及血性引流增加这一组表现，最符合术后出血并逐渐进展为低血容量性休克。低热和白细胞升高可在术后或感染风险中同时存在，但不能解释血性引流和低灌注模式。阿片类药物可导致镇静，但当灌注指标恶化时，不应把它作为主要解释。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Choose the hypothesis that explains the most dangerous findings with the fewest assumptions. Do not let a plausible benign explanation override direct bleeding and perfusion cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"选择能用最少假设解释最多危险发现的假设。不要让看似合理的良性解释掩盖直接出血和灌注线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2475,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[117,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,48],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Which information should the nurse include in an SBAR call to communicate urgency to the surgical resident? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：护士在使用 SBAR 致电外科住院医师时，应包括哪些信息以传达紧急性？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: Which information should the nurse include in an SBAR call to communicate urgency to the surgical resident?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段 2：护士在使用 SBAR 致电外科住院医师时，应包括哪些信息以传达紧急性？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Assessment: present the trend in vital signs from 0700 to 1100 rather than only the most recent values","zh":"评估：呈现 0700 到 1100 的生命体征趋势，而不只是最新数值"},{"id":"E","en":"Recommendation: request bedside assessment now and discuss stat labs, imaging, IV access, or other orders appropriate to the provider’s scope","zh":"建议：请求立即床旁评估，并讨论急查实验室、影像、静脉通路或其他属于医嘱范围的处理"},{"id":"B","en":"Background: emphasize that mild confusion and low-grade fever can be common after surgery","zh":"背景：强调术后轻度意识混乱和低热可能常见"},{"id":"D","en":"Assessment: report the mental-status change, falling urine output, increasing sanguineous drain output, and expanding dressing stain","zh":"评估：报告意识状态改变、尿量下降、血性引流增加和敷料渗染扩大"},{"id":"A","en":"Situation: state that the postoperative client is actively deteriorating and that bleeding is a concern","zh":"情况：说明术后患者正在恶化，并担心出血"},{"id":"F","en":"Recommendation: ask for acetaminophen only and wait for afternoon rounds if the resident is busy","zh":"建议：只请求对乙酰氨基酚；如果住院医师忙，就等下午查房"}],"correct":["A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Effective SBAR communicates the nurse’s concern, relevant background, objective assessment trends, and a specific request for timely provider action. In this case the urgent message is not merely fever or confusion; it is a trajectory of possible bleeding and hypoperfusion. The nurse should request immediate bedside assessment and discuss provider-scope diagnostics or interventions, while avoiding language that minimizes the concern or delays evaluation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"有效的 SBAR 应传达护士的担忧、相关背景、客观评估趋势以及明确的及时处理请求。本例紧急信息不只是发热或意识混乱，而是可能出血和低灌注的病情轨迹。护士应请求立即床旁评估，并讨论属于医嘱范围的诊断或处理，同时避免使用淡化风险或延误评估的措辞。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For SBAR questions, select content that states the concern, gives relevant context, presents objective trends, and asks for a clear next step.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到 SBAR 题时，选择能说明担忧、提供相关背景、呈现客观趋势并提出明确下一步的内容。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2476,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[237,273],"terminalOffsetsZh":[84,95],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The resident dismisses the nurse’s concern and does not come to assess the client. At 1200, the client is more confused, hypotensive, tachycardic, nearly anuric, and has a lactate of 3.8 mmol/L with hemoglobin down to 9.1 g/dL. What is the nurse’s priority action?","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：住院医师未重视护士的担忧，也未到床旁评估。1200 时患者意识更混乱、低血压、心动过速、几乎无尿，乳酸 3.8 mmol/L，血红蛋白降至 9.1 g/dL。护士的优先行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse’s priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的优先行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 1200, the client is more confused, hypotensive, tachycardic, nearly anuric, and has a lactate of 3.8 mmol/L with hemoglobin down to 9.1 g/dL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"1200 时患者意识更混乱、低血压、心动过速、几乎无尿，乳酸 3.8 mmol/L，血红蛋白降至 9.1 g/dL。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Invoke the chain of command per policy, involving the charge nurse and contacting the attending surgeon while continuing close monitoring","zh":"按政策启动指挥链，联系责任护士/护士长并联系主治外科医师，同时继续严密监测"},{"id":"C","en":"Document the resident’s response fully before making any further calls","zh":"先完整记录住院医师的回应，再进行任何进一步电话联系"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold all opioid medication and reassess in 1 hour to see whether the confusion improves","zh":"暂停所有阿片类药物，1 小时后复评意识是否改善"},{"id":"B","en":"Wait for afternoon rounds because the resident has already been notified","zh":"等待下午查房，因为住院医师已经被通知"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client has objective signs of evolving shock: worsening vital signs, altered mental status, near-anuria, elevated lactate, falling hemoglobin, and ongoing sanguineous drainage. When the initial provider response is inadequate for the clinical situation, the nurse should follow the facility chain of command without delay while continuing safety monitoring and documenting the sequence. Documentation is required, but it should not precede urgent escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者有逐渐进展为休克的客观证据：生命体征恶化、意识状态改变、接近无尿、乳酸升高、血红蛋白下降以及持续血性引流。当初始医嘱回应与临床情况严重程度不匹配时，护士应立即按机构指挥链升级，同时继续安全监测并记录过程。记录是必要的，但不应排在紧急升级之前。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client is objectively deteriorating and the first response is inadequate, choose escalation through policy rather than waiting, repeating the same ineffective call, or charting first.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者客观恶化且首次回应不足时，应选择按政策升级，而不是等待、重复同样无效的电话或先记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2477,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Discharge Planning & Handoff","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[54,75],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,27],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: Place the nurse’s priority actions in order. Use each option once.","fullStemZh":"阶段 2：请按优先顺序排列护士行动。每个选项使用一次。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use each option once.","terminalSentenceZh":"每个选项使用一次。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: Place the nurse’s priority actions in order.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段 2：请按优先顺序排列护士行动。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Document objective findings, communication times, provider responses, and escalation after urgent safety actions are underway","zh":"在紧急安全行动已启动后，记录客观发现、沟通时间、医务人员回应和升级过程"},{"id":"B","en":"Invoke the chain of command and request immediate attending-level evaluation because the client is worsening","zh":"因患者正在恶化，启动指挥链并请求主治层级立即评估"},{"id":"C","en":"Obtain or delegate ordered/protocol labs and prepare for anticipated interventions without delaying the escalation call","zh":"在不延误升级电话的前提下，采集或委托采集医嘱/预案所需实验室检查，并为预期干预做准备"},{"id":"A","en":"Keep the client safe in bed, repeat focused ABC/perfusion assessment, start close monitoring, and confirm a patent IV line","zh":"确保患者安全卧床，重复重点 ABC/灌注评估，开始严密监测，并确认静脉通路通畅"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first protects the client and reassesses immediate stability while ensuring monitoring and IV access. Next, escalation is required because definitive evaluation and treatment are provider-level and the resident response was inadequate. Labs and preparation for likely interventions are important and may be delegated, but they should not delay escalation. Thorough documentation follows or occurs concurrently once urgent actions are underway.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先保护患者并重新评估即时稳定性，同时确保监测和静脉通路。随后必须升级，因为明确评估和治疗属于医嘱层级，且住院医师回应不足。实验室检查和为可能干预做准备很重要，可适当委托，但不应延误升级。完整记录应在紧急行动启动后进行或同步进行。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In ordered-response deterioration items, separate life-preserving actions from administrative tasks. Stabilize/monitor and escalate before documentation or routine care.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做病情恶化的排序题时，要区分保命行动和行政性任务。先稳定/监测和升级，再记录或进行常规护理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2478,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus4_case_postop_sbar_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,125],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,44],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: For each nursing action or interpretation before OR transfer, select whether it is appropriate or unsafe/incomplete.","fullStemZh":"阶段 3：对于转入手术室前的每项护理行动或判断，请选择它是适当的，还是不安全/不完整的。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 3: For each nursing action or interpretation before OR transfer, select whether it is appropriate or unsafe/incomplete.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段 3：对于转入手术室前的每项护理行动或判断，请选择它是适当的，还是不安全/不完整的。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Reassess vital signs, urine output, and mental status after the 500 mL fluid bolus","zh":"500 mL 补液后复评生命体征、尿量和意识状态"},{"id":"r2","en":"Interpret HR 116, BP 98/58, urine output 5 mL/hr, and worsening responsiveness as lack of stabilization","zh":"将 HR 116、BP 98/58、尿量 5 mL/hr 和反应性变差判断为尚未稳定"},{"id":"r3","en":"Verify that the surgeon has initiated the consent, surrogate, or emergency-consent process per policy","zh":"核实外科医师已按政策启动知情同意、代理人同意或紧急同意流程"},{"id":"r4","en":"Provide the OR nurse only the current vital signs and CT result because the prior trend is already documented","zh":"只向手术室护士交接当前生命体征和 CT 结果，因为之前趋势已记录在病历中"},{"id":"r5","en":"Delay transport until the confused client can personally sign the surgical consent","zh":"延迟转运，直到意识混乱的患者能亲自签署手术同意书"},{"id":"r6","en":"Communicate blood availability, IV access, allergies if known, last vital signs, interventions performed, and the full deterioration timeline","zh":"交接血制品可用情况、静脉通路、已知过敏史、最后一次生命体征、已执行干预以及完整恶化时间线"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Unsafe or incomplete","zh":"不安全或不完整"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse evaluates whether initial resuscitation is effective by reassessing perfusion indicators. Persistent tachycardia, hypotension, oliguria, and worsening mental status show that the client has not stabilized with crystalloid alone and needs definitive source control and blood availability. The nurse should verify that the responsible provider has addressed the appropriate consent pathway per policy, not attempt to obtain consent from a confused client or delay emergency transport for personal signature. A safe OR handoff includes the full deterioration timeline and interventions, not just the latest snapshot.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士通过复评灌注指标来判断初始复苏是否有效。持续心动过速、低血压、少尿和意识恶化说明患者仅靠晶体液尚未稳定，需要明确控制出血源并确保血制品可用。护士应核实负责医师已按政策处理合适的同意路径，而不是试图让意识混乱的患者签署同意书或因个人签名延误紧急转运。安全的手术室交接应包括完整恶化时间线和已执行干预，而不只是最新数据。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by asking whether perfusion improved after the intervention. For handoff, choose the option that transfers the trajectory, not only the latest values.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估结果时要问：干预后灌注是否改善？交接时应选择能传递病情轨迹的选项，而不只是最新数值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2479,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.46","itemType":"case_study","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.46.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[216,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,76],"fullStemEn":"Unfolding case: informed consent before elective cholecystectomy A Spanish-speaking client with limited English has signed an elective surgical consent, but tells the nurse she did not understand the surgical risks. Her adult daughter offers to interpret.","fullStemZh":"展开案例：择期胆囊切除术前的知情同意 一名以西班牙语为主要语言、英语有限的患者已签署择期手术同意书，但告诉护士她并不理解手术风险。成年女儿提出代为翻译。","terminalSentenceEn":"Her adult daughter offers to interpret.","terminalSentenceZh":"成年女儿提出代为翻译。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Unfolding case: informed consent before elective cholecystectomy A Spanish-speaking client with limited English has signed an elective surgical consent, but tells the nurse she did not understand the surgical risks.","penultimateSentenceZh":"展开案例：择期胆囊切除术前的知情同意 一名以西班牙语为主要语言、英语有限的患者已签署择期手术同意书，但告诉护士她并不理解手术风险。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case centers on the difference between a signed form and valid informed consent. The nurse recognizes that the client's lack of understanding of material surgical risks invalidates the current process, pauses transport, obtains a qualified medical interpreter instead of relying on family interpretation, requires the provider to repeat the risk-benefit-alternative discussion, supports the anxious client during the delay, and documents the new consent process accurately once understanding and voluntariness are demonstrated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例的核心是区分“已签名表格”和“有效知情同意”。护士识别到患者不理解主要手术风险，说明当前同意过程无效；暂停转运；取得合格医学口译员而不是依赖家属翻译；要求医生重新说明风险、益处和替代方案；在等待期间支持焦虑患者；并在患者表现出理解和自愿性后，准确记录新的同意过程。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For consent cases, prioritize autonomy and role clarity: provider explains the procedure, the qualified interpreter enables accurate language access, and the nurse advocates, pauses unsafe workflow, witnesses appropriately, and documents truthfully.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理知情同意案例时，优先考虑患者自主权和职责清晰：医生解释操作，合格口译员确保准确语言沟通，护士负责倡导、暂停不安全流程、适当见证并真实记录。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2480,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,67],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,22],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, how should the nurse interpret the signed consent form?","fullStemZh":"在阶段1，护士应如何理解这份已签名的同意书？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, how should the nurse interpret the signed consent form?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段1，护士应如何理解这份已签名的同意书？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"The consent is not valid for proceeding because the client states she did not understand the risks and felt pressure to sign.","zh":"不能据此推进手术，因为患者表示自己不理解风险，并感到被催促签字。"},{"id":"D","en":"The consent can be accepted if the nurse documents that the client speaks some English.","zh":"只要护士记录患者会说一些英语，就可以接受该同意。"},{"id":"C","en":"The consent is valid if the daughter confirms that the client knows the gallbladder will be removed.","zh":"只要女儿确认患者知道要切除胆囊，同意就有效。"},{"id":"A","en":"The consent is valid because the form is signed and the client appears calm.","zh":"同意有效，因为表格已签名且患者看起来平静。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A signature is evidence of a consent process, not proof that informed consent is valid. The client's statement that she did not understand the risks and signed because the physician seemed to want her to is a direct cue that comprehension and voluntariness are not established. The nurse should not treat this form as sufficient for transport to the operating room.","rationaleCorrectZh":"签名只是同意过程的证据，并不能证明知情同意有效。患者表示不理解风险，并且因为医生似乎希望她签而签字，这是理解和自愿性尚未成立的直接线索。护士不应把这份表格视为足以送往手术室的依据。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In consent questions, separate the physical signature from the informed-consent process. A patient statement showing confusion, pressure, or lack of understanding is the priority cue.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到知情同意题时，要把“签名”与“知情同意过程”区分开。患者表达困惑、受压力或不理解，是优先线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2481,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[16,25],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate at Stage 1? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段1中，哪些护理措施是适当的？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate at Stage 1?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段1中，哪些护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Ask the daughter to interpret the risks because the client trusts her and the daughter is pre-med.","zh":"请女儿翻译风险，因为患者信任她且女儿是医学预科。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the surgical resident that the client did not understand the risk explanation and needs the provider to repeat the consent discussion through an interpreter.","zh":"通知外科住院医患者不理解风险说明，需要医生通过口译员重新进行同意讨论。"},{"id":"E","en":"Independently explain the surgical risks, benefits, and alternatives and obtain a new signature.","zh":"护士自行解释手术风险、益处和替代方案，并取得新的签名。"},{"id":"F","en":"Allow the daughter to remain for emotional support if the client wants, while using the qualified interpreter for clinical interpretation.","zh":"若患者愿意，可让女儿留下提供情感支持，同时由合格口译员进行临床口译。"},{"id":"B","en":"Arrange a qualified medical interpreter for the consent discussion.","zh":"为同意讨论安排合格医学口译员。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold transport to the operating room until valid informed consent is established.","zh":"在有效知情同意成立之前，暂停送往手术室。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should pause the process, obtain a qualified interpreter, and notify the provider that the consent discussion must be repeated because the client has not demonstrated understanding. The daughter may remain as support if the client wants, but she should not serve as the interpreter for this surgical consent discussion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应暂停流程，取得合格口译员，并通知医生必须重新进行同意讨论，因为患者尚未表现出理解。若患者愿意，女儿可作为支持者留在床旁，但不应担任此次手术同意讨论的口译员。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For language-access questions, do not equate bilingual family support with qualified medical interpretation. Also ask who is responsible for the consent explanation: provider explains; nurse advocates and witnesses.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到语言服务题时，不要把双语家属支持等同于合格医学口译。同时要判断谁负责同意说明：医生解释；护士倡导并见证。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2482,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Place the nursing actions in the best order after the Stage 1 consent concern is identified.","fullStemZh":"在阶段1发现同意过程疑虑后，将护理措施按最佳顺序排列。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the best order after the Stage 1 consent concern is identified.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段1发现同意过程疑虑后，将护理措施按最佳顺序排列。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Arrange a qualified medical interpreter rather than using the daughter for the consent discussion.","zh":"安排合格医学口译员，而不是让女儿担任同意讨论的口译员。"},{"id":"D","en":"Use the interpreter to explain the reason for the delay, reassure the client that the goal is understanding, and assess for questions or ambivalence.","zh":"通过口译员解释延迟原因，安抚患者说明目标是确保理解，并评估是否有问题或犹豫。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the surgical resident that the consent discussion must be repeated through the interpreter.","zh":"通知外科住院医必须通过口译员重新进行同意讨论。"},{"id":"A","en":"Hold transport to the operating room because the signed form is not sufficient after the client's statement.","zh":"暂停送往手术室，因为在患者作出该陈述后，已签名表格不足以作为依据。"},{"id":"E","en":"Witness the new consent only after the provider re-explains the procedure and the client verbalizes understanding and voluntary agreement.","zh":"只有在医生重新解释且患者表述理解并自愿同意后，才见证新的同意书。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first prevents an unsafe/legal process error by holding transport, then obtains qualified language access, communicates the barrier to the provider, supports the client during the delay, and witnesses a new consent only after the provider repeats the consent discussion and the client demonstrates understanding and voluntary agreement.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士首先通过暂停转运来防止不安全和法律流程错误，然后取得合格语言服务，向医生沟通障碍，在等待期间支持患者，最后只有在医生重新进行同意讨论且患者表现出理解和自愿同意后，才见证新的同意书。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In ordered-response items, remove the immediate unsafe step first, then secure required resources, notify the responsible provider, support the patient, and document only after the process is valid.","testTakingStrategyZh":"排序题中，先排除眼前不安全流程，再取得必要资源，通知负责医生，支持患者，最后在流程有效后再记录/见证。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2483,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,121],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,41],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the resident says, \"She already signed — we're going to lose our OR time.\" What is the nurse's best response?","fullStemZh":"阶段2中，住院医说：\"她已经签了——我们会错过手术室时间。\" 护士最佳回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's best response?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, the resident says, \"She already signed — we're going to lose our OR time.\"","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段2中，住院医说：\"她已经签了——我们会错过手术室时间。\"","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Give an anxiolytic medication so the client's blood pressure returns to baseline before transport.","zh":"给予抗焦虑药，使患者血压恢复基线后再转运。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ask the daughter to quickly explain the risks so the OR schedule is not disrupted.","zh":"请女儿快速解释风险，以免影响手术室安排。"},{"id":"A","en":"Send the client to the operating room and document that the resident accepted responsibility for consent.","zh":"将患者送往手术室，并记录住院医愿意对同意负责。"},{"id":"B","en":"State that the procedure cannot proceed on the current consent, request provider re-explanation through the interpreter, and involve the charge nurse or chain of command if pressure continues.","zh":"说明不能依据当前同意推进手术，要求医生通过口译员重新解释；若压力持续，则请责任护士或按层级上报。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse has an independent advocacy obligation not to facilitate a procedure when the patient has indicated lack of understanding. Scheduling pressure does not override informed-consent requirements. The correct action is to maintain the hold, request provider re-explanation through the qualified interpreter, and use the charge nurse or chain of command if needed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当患者已表示不理解时，护士有独立的倡导义务，不能促成该操作。排班压力不能凌驾于知情同意要求之上。正确做法是继续暂停流程，要求医生通过合格口译员重新解释，必要时请责任护士或按层级上报。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a provider's request conflicts with patient autonomy or legal safety, choose the option that clearly states the concern, maintains the safety hold, and escalates through the chain of command.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当医生要求与患者自主权或法律安全要求冲突时，选择能清楚说明问题、保持安全暂停并按层级上报的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2484,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus5_case_consent_interpreter_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[157,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,47],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the provider has repeated the consent discussion through the certified VRI interpreter, and the client states she understands and wants surgery. Complete the documentation statement.","fullStemZh":"阶段3中，医生已通过认证VRI口译员重新进行同意讨论，患者表示理解并希望手术。请完成记录陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the documentation statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成记录陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the provider has repeated the consent discussion through the certified VRI interpreter, and the client states she understands and wants surgery.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段3中，医生已通过认证VRI口译员重新进行同意讨论，患者表示理解并希望手术。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse may witness the new consent because {{1}}. Documentation should include {{2}}.","zh":"护士可以见证新的同意书，因为 {{1}}。记录应包括 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"the daughter confirmed that the client trusts her","zh":"女儿确认患者信任她"},{"id":"o2","en":"the original signed form was already in the chart","zh":"原先已签名表格已经在病历中"},{"id":"o1","en":"the client verbalized understanding and voluntary agreement after the provider's interpreted explanation","zh":"患者在医生通过口译解释后表述理解并自愿同意"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"that the nurse personally explained all surgical risks and alternatives","zh":"记录护士亲自解释了所有手术风险和替代方案"},{"id":"o2","en":"only the time the operating room was delayed and the resident's objection","zh":"仅记录手术室延误时间和住院医的异议"},{"id":"o1","en":"the qualified interpreter's name or identification number, the VRI mode, and that the prior form was superseded according to facility policy","zh":"合格口译员姓名或识别号码、VRI方式，以及按机构政策注明先前表格已被取代"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After the provider repeats the consent discussion through a qualified interpreter and the client verbalizes understanding and voluntary agreement, the nurse may witness the new consent. Documentation should identify the interpreter and mode used and accurately show that the earlier defective consent was superseded or handled according to facility policy, without backdating or implying that the nurse provided the surgical consent explanation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在医生通过合格口译员重新进行同意讨论，且患者表述理解并自愿同意后，护士可以见证新的同意书。记录应说明口译员身份和使用方式，并准确反映先前有缺陷的同意书已被取代或按机构政策处理，不应倒签日期，也不应暗示由护士完成手术同意说明。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For documentation questions, choose the record that accurately reflects what occurred and who performed each role. Avoid backdating, blame-focused notes, or statements that imply the nurse obtained provider-level consent.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到记录题时，选择能准确反映发生经过以及各自职责的记录。避免倒签、以指责为中心的记录，或暗示护士完成了医生层级同意说明的说法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2485,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.47","itemType":"case_study","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.47.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[405,504],"terminalOffsetsZh":[116,143],"fullStemEn":"Acute inpatient suicide risk during treatment for a diabetic foot infection A 58-year-old man is admitted to a medical-surgical unit for IV antibiotics and surgical consultation for a non-healing diabetic foot ulcer with cellulitis. He has major depressive disorder, stopped sertraline 8 months ago, lives alone, lost his wife 14 months ago, and has a remote prior suicide attempt by medication overdose. Admission PHQ-2 score was positive, but no full suicide risk assessment was completed at that time.","fullStemZh":"糖尿病足感染住院治疗期间发现急性自杀风险 一名58岁男性因伴蜂窝织炎的糖尿病足溃疡不愈合，被收入内外科病区接受静脉抗生素和外科会诊。他有重性抑郁障碍病史，8个月前自行停用舍曲林，独居，妻子14个月前去世，并有远期服药过量自杀未遂史。入院PHQ-2筛查阳性，但当时未完成完整自杀风险评估。","terminalSentenceEn":"Admission PHQ-2 score was positive, but no full suicide risk assessment was completed at that time.","terminalSentenceZh":"入院PHQ-2筛查阳性，但当时未完成完整自杀风险评估。","penultimateSentenceEn":"He has major depressive disorder, stopped sertraline 8 months ago, lives alone, lost his wife 14 months ago, and has a remote prior suicide attempt by medication overdose.","penultimateSentenceZh":"他有重性抑郁障碍病史，8个月前自行停用舍曲林，独居，妻子14个月前去世，并有远期服药过量自杀未遂史。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This unfolding case requires the nurse to recognize converging suicide-risk cues, ask directly about suicidal thoughts, maintain continuous safety observation after disclosure, reduce environmental hazards without interrupting necessary medical care, use nonpunitive de-escalation, obtain consent before involving family when the client has capacity, and continue reassessment because calmer behavior does not equal resolution of acute suicide risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本案例要求护士识别多项汇聚的自杀风险线索，直接询问自杀想法，在患者披露后保持连续安全观察，在不中断必要医疗护理的前提下降低环境危险，用非惩罚性的方式降级处理激动，在患者有决策能力时取得同意后再联系家属，并持续重新评估，因为情绪较平静并不等于急性自杀风险已经解除。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For acute suicide risk, safety and continuous observation come before routine tasks. Do not let a calmer moment override documented high-risk findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到急性自杀风险时，安全和连续观察优先于常规任务。不要因为患者暂时平静就忽视已记录的高风险结果。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2486,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"select_all","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[87,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,32],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: Which findings require the nurse to perform a direct suicide risk assessment? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"阶段1：哪些发现要求护士进行直接的自杀风险评估？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 1: Which findings require the nurse to perform a direct suicide risk assessment?","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段1：哪些发现要求护士进行直接的自杀风险评估？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Death of his wife 14 months ago and current social isolation","zh":"妻子14个月前去世且目前社会孤立"},{"id":"E","en":"Poor sleep, tearfulness overnight, and refusal to eat breakfast","zh":"夜间睡眠差、流泪且拒绝吃早餐"},{"id":"C","en":"Remote history of a suicide attempt requiring ICU admission","zh":"远期有需要ICU治疗的自杀未遂史"},{"id":"B","en":"Statement, 'What's the point,' with flat affect and poor eye contact","zh":"说“有什么意义”，伴情感平淡和眼神接触差"},{"id":"A","en":"Positive PHQ-2 on admission without follow-up assessment","zh":"入院PHQ-2阳性但未进一步评估"},{"id":"F","en":"Clean, dry, intact left foot dressing","zh":"左足敷料清洁、干燥、完整"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The positive PHQ-2, hopeless statement, depressive affect, prior attempt, bereavement, isolation, poor sleep, tearfulness, and poor intake are converging suicide-risk cues. The wound dressing status is important medical information but does not itself indicate suicide risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"PHQ-2阳性、绝望性表达、抑郁表现、既往自杀未遂、丧偶、孤立、睡眠差、流泪和进食差共同提示自杀风险。伤口敷料情况是重要的医疗信息，但本身并不提示自杀风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster cues. One depressive sign may be nonspecific; multiple converging historical and behavioral cues require direct assessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将线索组合判断。单一抑郁表现可能不特异；多项病史和行为线索汇聚时，需要直接评估。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2487,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,48],"fullStemEn":"Stage 1: After the client discloses active suicidal thoughts, an identified method at home, intent, and a prior attempt, which action is the nurse's priority?","fullStemZh":"阶段1：患者披露主动自杀想法、家中有明确方法、有意图且有既往自杀未遂史后，护士的优先行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 1: After the client discloses active suicidal thoughts, an identified method at home, intent, and a prior attempt, which action is the nurse's priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段1：患者披露主动自杀想法、家中有明确方法、有意图且有既往自杀未遂史后，护士的优先行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Remain with the client or ensure continuous qualified observation while activating immediate help and notifying the charge nurse and provider.","zh":"留在患者身边，或确保由合格人员连续观察，同时立即寻求协助并通知责任护士/护士长和医师。"},{"id":"C","en":"Leave the room to find the charge nurse because the client denies having means in the hospital.","zh":"因患者否认院内有自伤工具，离开病房去找护士长。"},{"id":"B","en":"Finish administering the scheduled morning medications before calling the provider.","zh":"先完成晨间常规给药，再联系医师。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tell the client that these thoughts are common after a loss and reassess at the end of the shift.","zh":"告诉患者丧亲后这些想法很常见，并在班末重新评估。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"High acute suicide risk requires immediate safety action. The nurse should not create an unobserved interval; the nurse should stay with the client or ensure another qualified staff member does so while summoning help and notifying the provider for ordered suicide precautions and psychiatric evaluation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性自杀高风险需要立即采取安全措施。护士不能让患者处于无人观察的间隙；应留在患者身边，或确保另一名合格人员持续观察，同时呼叫协助并通知医师，以开立自杀预防措施和精神科评估。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a client discloses active suicidal intent, choose the answer that keeps the client continuously observed while help is activated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当患者披露主动自杀意图时，选择能在启动协助的同时保持患者连续被观察的答案。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2488,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,91],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: For each item or environmental feature, select the most appropriate safety action.","fullStemZh":"阶段2：针对每个物品或环境特征，选择最合适的安全措施。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 2: For each item or environmental feature, select the most appropriate safety action.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段2：针对每个物品或环境特征，选择最合适的安全措施。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Leather belt in personal belongings","zh":"个人物品中的皮带"},{"id":"r2","en":"Phone charger cord","zh":"手机充电线"},{"id":"r3","en":"Razor in toiletry bag","zh":"洗漱包中的剃刀"},{"id":"r4","en":"Bathroom door can lock from inside","zh":"浴室门可从内部上锁"},{"id":"r5","en":"IV tubing and pulse oximetry cable needed for care","zh":"护理所需的静脉输液管和脉搏血氧导线"},{"id":"r6","en":"IV pole and overbed table needed for treatment and meals","zh":"治疗和进餐所需的输液架与床旁餐桌"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Assess and leave in place with continuous monitoring","zh":"评估后在连续观察下保留"},{"id":"c2","en":"Modify or secure per suicide-precautions protocol","zh":"按自杀预防方案进行改造或固定"},{"id":"c4","en":"No safety action is needed","zh":"无需安全处理"},{"id":"c1","en":"Remove and secure away from the client","zh":"移除并妥善锁放，避免患者接触"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A safety sweep removes sharps and flexible items that can be used for self-harm, modifies unavoidable environmental risks, and preserves medically necessary equipment when it can be made safer and the client is continuously observed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"安全清查应移除可用于自伤的锐器和柔性物品，改造不可避免的环境风险，并在可降低风险且患者持续被观察时保留必要医疗设备。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not choose an all-or-nothing sweep. Remove clear hazards, modify necessary equipment, and keep needed items only after risk assessment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要选择“一律清空”或“一律保留”。明确危险物品要移除，必要设备要改造，所需物品须经风险评估后才保留。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2489,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,42],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2: The client becomes agitated during the room sweep, pulls at his IV, and moves toward the door. Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"阶段2：房间安全清查期间患者变得激动，拉扯静脉针并朝门口走去。护士的最佳回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的最佳回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Stage 2: The client becomes agitated during the room sweep, pulls at his IV, and moves toward the door.","penultimateSentenceZh":"阶段2：房间安全清查期间患者变得激动，拉扯静脉针并朝门口走去。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Stand directly in the doorway and tell him he cannot leave because he caused this by talking about suicide.","zh":"直接站在门口并告诉他，因为他说了自杀想法，所以不能离开。"},{"id":"C","en":"Threaten restraints unless he sits down immediately.","zh":"威胁说如果他不立刻坐下就使用约束。"},{"id":"A","en":"Use a calm tone, acknowledge that the precautions feel intrusive, explain they are to keep him safe while support is arranged, keep observation in place, and notify the team per policy if he attempts to leave.","zh":"用平静语气承认这些措施让他感到被侵犯，说明目的是在安排支持期间保护他的安全，保持观察；若他试图离开，按政策通知团队。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tell the sitter to step out so the client feels less watched.","zh":"让陪护离开，好让患者感觉不那么被监视。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Therapeutic de-escalation validates the client's distress, preserves rapport, explains the safety purpose of precautions, and maintains observation. Coercive threats, blame, or removing observation increase risk and may escalate agitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗性降级沟通应确认患者痛苦，维护信任，解释预防措施的安全目的，并保持观察。威胁、责备或取消观察会增加风险并可能加重激动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For agitation, choose the least restrictive response that maintains safety, validates feelings, and avoids threats.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到激动时，选择限制性最低、能维持安全、认可感受并避免威胁的回应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2490,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Legal & Ethical Principles","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,71],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,18],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: Complete the statement about contacting the client's daughter.","fullStemZh":"阶段3：完成关于联系患者女儿的陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 3: Complete the statement about contacting the client's daughter.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段3：完成关于联系患者女儿的陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Because the client is alert, oriented, and now willing to involve his daughter, the nurse should first {{1}}. The nurse should then {{2}}.","zh":"由于患者清醒、定向力正常，并且现在愿意让女儿参与，护士应首先 {{1}}。然后护士应 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"obtain and document the client's consent and clarify what information may be shared","zh":"取得并记录患者同意，同时明确可以分享哪些信息"},{"id":"o2","en":"call the daughter immediately because she is listed as the emergency contact","zh":"因女儿列为紧急联系人而立即给她打电话"},{"id":"o3","en":"tell the social worker to disclose the full psychiatric assessment","zh":"让社工披露完整精神科评估"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"ask the daughter to remove pills from the home without telling the client what was shared","zh":"在不告知患者分享内容的情况下，请女儿移除家中药物"},{"id":"o2","en":"refuse all contact because psychiatric information can never be shared with family","zh":"拒绝所有联系，因为精神健康信息绝不能与家属分享"},{"id":"o1","en":"facilitate a call with the client present or help him call her, sharing only authorized information","zh":"在患者在场时协助通话，或帮助患者自己打电话，只分享其授权的信息"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"When a client has capacity and is willing to involve family, the consent pathway protects privacy and supports therapeutic trust. The nurse should clarify what may be shared, document consent, and coordinate with social work so the daughter can support means restriction only within the information the client authorizes, unless the team documents an imminent-danger exception.","rationaleCorrectZh":"当患者有决策能力且愿意让家属参与时，取得同意的路径既保护隐私，也维护治疗性信任。护士应明确可分享内容、记录同意，并与社工协调，使女儿在患者授权的信息范围内支持限制自伤手段；除非团队记录存在紧迫危险例外。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Emergency contact status is not the same as unlimited permission to disclose. When the client has capacity, look for consent and limited disclosure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"紧急联系人身份不等于可无限披露信息。患者有决策能力时，应选择取得同意和有限披露。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2491,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01","embeddedQuestionId":"opus12_case_inpatient_suicide_risk_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Psychosocial Integrity","topic":"Suicide & Crisis Intervention","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,109],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,32],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3: Classify each finding as a stabilizing/protective finding or an ongoing concern requiring follow-up.","fullStemZh":"阶段3：将每项发现归类为稳定/保护性发现，或需要跟进的持续担忧。","terminalSentenceEn":"Stage 3: Classify each finding as a stabilizing/protective finding or an ongoing concern requiring follow-up.","terminalSentenceZh":"阶段3：将每项发现归类为稳定/保护性发现，或需要跟进的持续担忧。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The client apologizes, is cooperative, eats half of lunch, and asks for his daughter to be called.","zh":"患者道歉、配合、午餐吃了一半，并要求联系女儿。"},{"id":"r2","en":"The sitter reports no further agitation or attempts to leave while 1:1 observation is in place.","zh":"在1:1观察期间，陪护报告未再出现激动或试图离开。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The stockpiled pills at home have not yet been removed.","zh":"家中囤积的药物尚未被移除。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Vascular surgery evaluation is pending before any amputation decision.","zh":"在作出任何截肢决定前，血管外科评估仍待完成。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Psychiatry recommends daily reassessment and continuation of 1:1 observation.","zh":"精神科建议每日重新评估并继续1:1观察。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Pharmacy-managed vancomycin exposure assessment and renal monitoring remain pending per facility protocol.","zh":"按机构方案，药学管理的万古霉素暴露评估和肾功能监测仍待完成。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Ongoing concern requiring follow-up","zh":"需要跟进的持续担忧"},{"id":"c1","en":"Stabilizing/protective finding","zh":"稳定/保护性发现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Engagement, cooperation, nutrition intake, and no further agitation while observed are reassuring but do not resolve the crisis. Ongoing concerns include access to lethal means at home, a pending amputation-related stressor, the psychiatric recommendation to continue high-risk monitoring, and unresolved medical treatment monitoring that could affect the hospitalization and stress burden.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者愿意互动、配合、进食并在观察下未再激动是令人放心的迹象，但不能说明危机已解除。持续担忧包括家中仍可接触致命手段、截肢相关压力事件待定、精神科建议继续高风险观察，以及可能影响住院过程和压力负担的医疗治疗监测尚未完成。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not equate calm behavior with resolved suicide risk. Separate protective signs from unresolved risks and pending stressors.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把平静表现等同于自杀风险解除。要区分保护性迹象、未解决风险和待定压力源。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2492,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.48","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.48.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[212,440],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,128],"fullStemEn":"Major thermal burn with inhalation injury requiring fluid resuscitation and airway management A 35-year-old man weighing approximately 80 kg is rescued from a smoke-filled bedroom after a residential house fire. The burn injury occurred at 0600, and he arrives in the emergency department at 0640 with facial burns, hoarseness, throat tightness, carbonaceous sputum, hypotension, tachycardia, and extensive anterior partial-thickness burns.","fullStemZh":"重度热烧伤合并吸入性损伤，需要液体复苏和气道管理 一名约80 kg的35岁男性在住宅火灾后从充满烟雾的卧室中被救出。烧伤发生于0600，患者于0640到达急诊，表现为面部烧伤、声音嘶哑、咽喉紧缩感、咳出炭黑色痰、低血压、心动过速，以及广泛前侧部分皮层烧伤。","terminalSentenceEn":"The burn injury occurred at 0600, and he arrives in the emergency department at 0640 with facial burns, hoarseness, throat tightness, carbonaceous sputum, hypotension, tachycardia, and extensive anterior partial-thickness burns.","terminalSentenceZh":"烧伤发生于0600，患者于0640到达急诊，表现为面部烧伤、声音嘶哑、咽喉紧缩感、咳出炭黑色痰、低血压、心动过速，以及广泛前侧部分皮层烧伤。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Major thermal burn with inhalation injury requiring fluid resuscitation and airway management A 35-year-old man weighing approximately 80 kg is rescued from a smoke-filled bedroom after a residential house fire.","penultimateSentenceZh":"重度热烧伤合并吸入性损伤，需要液体复苏和气道管理 一名约80 kg的35岁男性在住宅火灾后从充满烟雾的卧室中被救出。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires recognizing a high-risk burn patient with inhalation injury, calculating burn size accurately, applying the ordered Parkland estimate from the time of burn, titrating fluid to urine output, and later recognizing over-resuscitation. Early airway protection is prioritized because progressive hoarseness, stridor, drooling, carbonaceous sputum, and facial/oropharyngeal edema can progress to complete obstruction before oxygen saturation falls. The burn size is 31.5% TBSA because only anterior surfaces of the head/face, trunk, and arms are burned. Fluid therapy begins from the burn time and is adjusted to a urine output target of 40 to 80 mL/hr. Later excessive urine output with crackles, rising airway pressures, increased abdominal girth, edema of unburned hands, and hemodilution indicates fluid creep rather than successful resuscitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求识别吸入性损伤高危烧伤患者，准确计算烧伤面积，按烧伤发生时间应用医嘱中的Parkland估算，依据尿量滴定液体，并在后期识别过度复苏。声音嘶哑加重、喘鸣、流涎、炭黑色痰以及面部/口咽水肿可在氧饱和度下降前进展为完全气道阻塞，因此需优先保护气道。烧伤面积为31.5% TBSA，因为仅头面部前侧、前躯干和双臂前侧烧伤。液体治疗从烧伤时间开始计算，并按40至80 mL/hr尿量目标调整。后期尿量过高，同时出现湿啰音、气道峰压升高、腹围增加、未烧伤双手水肿和血液稀释，提示液体蠕变/过度复苏，而不是复苏单纯成功。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For burn case studies, separate the first threats in time: airway obstruction can kill before fluid calculations matter, then use TBSA and urine output to guide resuscitation, and finally reassess for complications of both under- and over-resuscitation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理烧伤案例时，要按时间顺序区分威胁：气道阻塞可能在液体计算发挥作用前致命；随后用TBSA和尿量指导复苏；最后同时评估复苏不足和过度复苏的并发症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2493,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[79,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,47],"fullStemEn":"Using the Rule of Nines, calculate the percent total body surface area burned. Include only the entire face/anterior scalp, entire anterior trunk, and both anterior arms from shoulders to wrists.","fullStemZh":"使用九分法计算烧伤总体表面积百分比。仅包括整个面部/前头皮、整个前躯干，以及双侧肩至腕的前臂。","terminalSentenceEn":"Include only the entire face/anterior scalp, entire anterior trunk, and both anterior arms from shoulders to wrists.","terminalSentenceZh":"仅包括整个面部/前头皮、整个前躯干，以及双侧肩至腕的前臂。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the Rule of Nines, calculate the percent total body surface area burned.","penultimateSentenceZh":"使用九分法计算烧伤总体表面积百分比。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"% TBSA","zh":"% TBSA"},"acceptable":["31.5","31.5%","31.5 %"],"numeric":{"value":31.5,"tolerance":0,"unit":"%"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The burned areas are the anterior head/face 4.5%, anterior trunk 18%, right anterior arm 4.5%, and left anterior arm 4.5%, for a total of 31.5% TBSA. The posterior trunk, posterior arms, legs, and perineum are unburned and do not contribute to the calculation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"烧伤部位为前头/面部4.5%、前躯干18%、右臂前侧4.5%、左臂前侧4.5%，合计31.5% TBSA。后躯干、双臂后侧、双腿和会阴未烧伤，不计入计算。","testTakingStrategyEn":"On burn-size questions, first decide anterior versus posterior involvement before adding the Rule-of-Nines percentages.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到烧伤面积题，先判断受累的是前侧还是后侧，再加总九分法百分比。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2494,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,160],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,42],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that support impending upper-airway obstruction requiring emergent intubation rather than continued observation on a non-rebreather mask.","fullStemZh":"请标出支持即将发生上气道阻塞、需要紧急气管插管而不是继续使用非再呼吸面罩观察的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that support impending upper-airway obstruction requiring emergent intubation rather than continued observation on a non-rebreather mask.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持即将发生上气道阻塞、需要紧急气管插管而不是继续使用非再呼吸面罩观察的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h1","selectable":true,"en":"Found in a smoke-filled bedroom.","zh":"在充满烟雾的卧室中被发现。"},{"id":"h2","selectable":true,"en":"Awake but anxious.","zh":"清醒但焦虑。"},{"id":"h3","selectable":true,"en":"Hoarse, raspy voice that worsens over 30 minutes.","zh":"嘶哑粗哑的声音在30分钟内加重。"},{"id":"h4","selectable":true,"en":"Reports throat tightness and difficulty swallowing.","zh":"诉咽喉紧缩和吞咽困难。"},{"id":"h5","selectable":true,"en":"Carbonaceous sputum when coughing.","zh":"咳嗽时有炭黑色痰。"},{"id":"h6","selectable":true,"en":"Posterior pharynx has soot deposits with erythema and edema.","zh":"后咽部有烟灰沉积，并伴发红和水肿。"},{"id":"h7","selectable":true,"en":"Progressive facial and lip edema.","zh":"面部和口唇水肿进行性加重。"},{"id":"h8","selectable":true,"en":"Inspiratory stridor audible without a stethoscope.","zh":"不用听诊器即可听到吸气性喘鸣。"},{"id":"h9","selectable":true,"en":"SpO2 94% on a non-rebreather mask.","zh":"非再呼吸面罩下SpO2为94%。"},{"id":"h10","selectable":true,"en":"Blood pressure 88/58 mmHg and heart rate 130/min.","zh":"血压88/58 mmHg，心率130次/分。"}],"correct":["h1","h3","h4","h5","h6","h7","h8"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Enclosed-space smoke exposure plus worsening hoarseness, throat tightness/dysphagia, carbonaceous sputum, pharyngeal soot/edema, progressive facial/lip edema, and audible stridor indicate inhalation injury with impending upper-airway obstruction. SpO2 can remain deceptively acceptable, especially with carbon monoxide exposure and supplemental oxygen, while edema progresses.","rationaleCorrectZh":"密闭空间烟雾暴露，加上声音嘶哑加重、咽喉紧缩/吞咽困难、炭黑色痰、咽部烟灰和水肿、面部/口唇水肿进行性加重以及可闻及喘鸣，提示吸入性损伤导致即将发生上气道阻塞。即使存在一氧化碳暴露并给予氧气，SpO2仍可能看似尚可，而气道水肿继续进展。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not let an acceptable SpO2 distract you from airway anatomy. Hoarseness, stridor, drooling, and progressive facial/oropharyngeal edema in a burn patient are airway cues.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要因为SpO2尚可而忽视气道解剖问题。烧伤患者出现声音嘶哑、喘鸣、流涎和面部/口咽水肿进展，都是气道线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2495,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[231,346],"terminalOffsetsZh":[91,129],"fullStemEn":"The provider orders lactated Ringer's using the commonly taught Parkland estimate: 4 mL x kg x %TBSA, with half in the first 8 hours from the burn time of 0600. The patient weighs 80 kg, has 31.5% TBSA burned, and arrives at 0640. Calculate the total 24-hour volume and the initial calculated rate from 0640 to 1400 before urine-output titration.","fullStemZh":"医嘱按常用Parkland估算给予乳酸林格液：4 mL x kg x %TBSA，并从0600烧伤时间起前8小时输注一半。患者体重80 kg，烧伤31.5% TBSA，0640到达。请计算24小时总量，以及在根据尿量滴定前从0640至1400的初始计算速度。","terminalSentenceEn":"Calculate the total 24-hour volume and the initial calculated rate from 0640 to 1400 before urine-output titration.","terminalSentenceZh":"请计算24小时总量，以及在根据尿量滴定前从0640至1400的初始计算速度。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The patient weighs 80 kg, has 31.5% TBSA burned, and arrives at 0640.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者体重80 kg，烧伤31.5% TBSA，0640到达。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Total 24-hour volume in mL","zh":"24小时总量，mL"},"acceptable":["10080","10,080","10080 mL","10,080 mL"],"numeric":{"value":10080,"tolerance":0,"unit":"mL"}},{"prompt":{"en":"Initial calculated rate in mL/hr","zh":"初始计算速度，mL/hr"},"acceptable":["687","687 mL/hr","688","690"],"numeric":{"value":687,"tolerance":3,"unit":"mL/hr"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Total volume is 4 mL x 80 kg x 31.5 = 10,080 mL. Half is 5,040 mL due by 1400, which is 8 hours after the 0600 burn. Because the patient arrives 40 minutes after the burn, the remaining first-half window is 7 hours 20 minutes, or 7.33 hours. 5,040 mL divided by 7.33 hours is approximately 687 mL/hr, then the rate is titrated to urine output.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总量为4 mL x 80 kg x 31.5 = 10,080 mL。前一半为5,040 mL，应在烧伤后8小时的1400前完成。患者在烧伤后40分钟到达，前半程剩余时间为7小时20分钟，即7.33小时。5,040 mL除以7.33小时约为687 mL/hr，随后根据尿量滴定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For burn-fluid calculations, underline the burn time. The first-half clock starts at injury time, so late arrival means the remaining rate is higher than the simple 8-hour average.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做烧伤补液计算时，先划出烧伤时间。前一半液体的计时从受伤时间开始，因此延迟到院时，剩余时间内的速度会高于简单8小时平均速度。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2496,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[164,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[59,69],"fullStemEn":"At 1000, the urine output has improved from 25 mL/hr to 35 mL/hr, but the ordered target is 40 to 80 mL/hr. The urine has lightened from dark amber to dark yellow. Which action should the nurse take?","fullStemZh":"1000时尿量从25 mL/hr改善到35 mL/hr，但医嘱目标为40至80 mL/hr。尿液从深琥珀色变为深黄色。护士应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The urine has lightened from dark amber to dark yellow.","penultimateSentenceZh":"尿液从深琥珀色变为深黄色。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Increase the lactated Ringer's infusion rate per the titration protocol and reassess hourly.","zh":"按滴定方案增加乳酸林格液输注速度，并每小时重新评估。"},{"id":"B","en":"Maintain the current rate because the urine color is improving.","zh":"因尿液颜色正在改善，维持当前速度。"},{"id":"C","en":"Decrease the infusion rate to prevent fluid overload because the blood pressure is improving.","zh":"因血压正在改善，为预防液体过负荷而降低输注速度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Stop titrating fluids and request a genitourinary workup for dark urine.","zh":"停止滴定液体，并因尿色深而要求泌尿系统检查。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Urine output remains below the minimum target of 40 mL/hr, so the infusion should be increased per protocol and reassessed hourly. The urine color trend is reassuring but does not replace the urine-output target.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尿量仍低于40 mL/hr的最低目标，因此应按方案增加输液速度并每小时重新评估。尿色改善是令人放心的趋势，但不能替代尿量目标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Trend matters, but target range matters more. A value moving in the right direction is still abnormal if it has not reached the ordered endpoint.","testTakingStrategyZh":"趋势重要，但目标范围更重要。数值即使朝正确方向变化，只要尚未达到医嘱终点，仍然异常。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2497,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[274,296],"terminalOffsetsZh":[83,91],"fullStemEn":"At 1800 to 2000, urine output is 110 to 120 mL/hr, new bilateral basilar crackles are present, peak airway pressures are rising, abdominal girth has increased, and the previously unburned hands are tense with delayed capillary refill. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"1800至2000期间，尿量为110至120 mL/hr，出现新的双侧肺底湿啰音，气道峰压升高，腹围增加，原本未烧伤的双手紧绷且毛细血管再充盈延迟。哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Perform serial hand perfusion assessments including pulses, capillary refill, sensation, and swelling.","zh":"连续评估双手灌注，包括脉搏、毛细血管再充盈、感觉和肿胀。"},{"id":"C","en":"Initiate or continue serial bladder pressure monitoring.","zh":"开始或继续连续监测膀胱压。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the burn team about crackles, rising airway pressures, increasing abdominal girth, and extremity edema.","zh":"将湿啰音、气道峰压升高、腹围增加和肢体水肿通知烧伤团队。"},{"id":"E","en":"Maintain or increase the infusion because the Parkland estimate covers 24 hours.","zh":"因为Parkland估算覆盖24小时，所以维持或增加输液。"},{"id":"F","en":"Treat the crackles by increasing ventilator support without changing the fluid rate.","zh":"在不改变输液速度的情况下，通过增加呼吸机支持来处理湿啰音。"},{"id":"A","en":"Reduce the lactated Ringer's infusion rate according to the titration order.","zh":"根据滴定医嘱降低乳酸林格液输注速度。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The findings indicate fluid creep: urine output is above target and there are signs of pulmonary edema, increased intra-abdominal pressure risk, and extremity edema compromising perfusion. Appropriate nursing actions are to reduce the infusion per protocol, notify the burn team, monitor bladder pressure, and perform serial extremity perfusion assessments.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这些发现提示液体蠕变/过度复苏：尿量高于目标，并出现肺水肿、腹内压升高风险和影响灌注的肢体水肿。合适的护理措施包括按方案降低输液速度、通知烧伤团队、监测膀胱压，并连续评估肢体灌注。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a treatment endpoint overshoots, reassess the treatment itself. High urine output plus new edema and crackles means the fluid rate may now be harmful.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当治疗终点超过目标时，要重新评估治疗本身。尿量过高并伴新发水肿和湿啰音，说明当前补液速度可能已经有害。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2498,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_major_burn_inhalation_fluid_creep_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.49","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Burn Management","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.49.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.49.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[607,719],"terminalOffsetsZh":[184,217],"fullStemEn":"At 1800, 12 hours after a major thermal burn, an intubated 80-kg client with 31.5% TBSA burns has achieved improved blood pressure and heart rate after lactated Ringer's resuscitation. Urine output is now 120 mL/hr for two consecutive hours, above the ordered target of 40 to 80 mL/hr. New bilateral basilar crackles are present, peak airway pressures are rising, abdominal girth is increasing, the hematocrit has fallen from 52% to 38%, and previously unburned hands are tense and edematous. The burn team notes that delivered volume has exceeded the time-phased expected Parkland trajectory by about 20%. Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"1800时，即重度热烧伤后12小时，一名80 kg、31.5% TBSA烧伤且已插管的患者在乳酸林格液复苏后血压和心率改善。尿量已连续两小时为120 mL/hr，高于医嘱40至80 mL/hr的目标。出现新的双侧肺底湿啰音，气道峰压升高，腹围增加，血细胞比容从52%降至38%，原本未烧伤的双手紧绷水肿。烧伤团队指出，已输注量比Parkland分时预期轨迹约高20%。请完成弓形题：选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bowtie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题：选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The burn team notes that delivered volume has exceeded the time-phased expected Parkland trajectory by about 20%.","penultimateSentenceZh":"烧伤团队指出，已输注量比Parkland分时预期轨迹约高20%。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_fluid_creep","en":"Fluid creep from over-resuscitation","zh":"过度复苏导致的液体蠕变"},{"id":"bt_cond_worsening_inhalation","en":"Worsening inhalation injury as the primary problem","zh":"吸入性损伤恶化是主要问题"},{"id":"bt_cond_early_sepsis","en":"Early burn wound sepsis","zh":"早期烧伤创面败血症"}],"correct":"bt_cond_fluid_creep"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_act_increase_vent_only","en":"Increase ventilator support without changing the fluid rate","zh":"不改变输液速度，仅增加呼吸机支持"},{"id":"bt_act_keep_increasing_fluids","en":"Maintain or increase the infusion because resuscitation continues for 24 hours","zh":"因复苏需持续24小时而维持或增加输液"},{"id":"bt_act_reduce_lr","en":"Reduce the lactated Ringer's infusion rate","zh":"降低乳酸林格液输注速度"},{"id":"bt_act_notify_monitor_complications","en":"Notify the burn team and begin serial bladder-pressure and extremity-perfusion monitoring","zh":"通知烧伤团队，并开始连续监测膀胱压和肢体灌注"}],"correct":["bt_act_reduce_lr","bt_act_notify_monitor_complications"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_param_potassium","en":"Serum potassium","zh":"血清钾"},{"id":"bt_param_hourly_uop","en":"Hourly urine output","zh":"每小时尿量"},{"id":"bt_param_cohb","en":"Carboxyhemoglobin level","zh":"一氧化碳血红蛋白水平"},{"id":"bt_param_bladder_pressure","en":"Bladder pressure","zh":"膀胱压"}],"correct":["bt_param_hourly_uop","bt_param_bladder_pressure"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The pattern is fluid creep: urine output is above target and the client has signs of pulmonary edema, rising airway pressures, increasing abdominal girth, extremity edema, and hemodilution after receiving more than the time-phased expected fluid trajectory. The priority is to reduce the infusion rate, notify the burn team, and monitor urine output and bladder pressure so renal perfusion is preserved while over-resuscitation complications are tracked.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这一模式为液体蠕变：尿量高于目标，且在输液量超过分时预期轨迹后出现肺水肿表现、气道压力升高、腹围增加、肢体水肿和血液稀释。优先事项是降低输液速度、通知烧伤团队，并监测尿量和膀胱压，以在保持肾灌注的同时追踪过度复苏并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bowtie items, match the middle condition to the whole pattern, not a single cue. Then choose actions and monitoring parameters that directly reverse or track that condition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，要把中间的情况与整个模式匹配，而不是只看单一线索。随后选择能直接纠正或追踪该情况的措施和监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2499,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.50","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.50.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[306,453],"terminalOffsetsZh":[84,119],"fullStemEn":"Acute gallstone pancreatitis with hypocalcemia and hemoconcentration A 45-year-old woman with known cholelithiasis presents with sudden severe epigastric pain radiating to the back after a large fatty meal, repeated vomiting, scleral icterus, hemoconcentration, hypocalcemia, and markedly elevated lipase. She later develops SIRS with ultrasound-confirmed common bile duct obstruction, undergoes ERCP with stone extraction, and then clinically improves.","fullStemZh":"急性胆石性胰腺炎伴低钙血症和血液浓缩 一名 45 岁女性既往有胆结石，高脂大餐后突发严重上腹痛并放射至背部，反复呕吐，出现巩膜黄染、血液浓缩、低钙血症和脂肪酶显著升高。随后出现 SIRS，超声证实胆总管梗阻，行 ERCP 取石后临床好转。","terminalSentenceEn":"She later develops SIRS with ultrasound-confirmed common bile duct obstruction, undergoes ERCP with stone extraction, and then clinically improves.","terminalSentenceZh":"随后出现 SIRS，超声证实胆总管梗阻，行 ERCP 取石后临床好转。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Acute gallstone pancreatitis with hypocalcemia and hemoconcentration A 45-year-old woman with known cholelithiasis presents with sudden severe epigastric pain radiating to the back after a large fatty meal, repeated vomiting, scleral icterus, hemoconcentration, hypocalcemia, and markedly elevated lipase.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急性胆石性胰腺炎伴低钙血症和血液浓缩 一名 45 岁女性既往有胆结石，高脂大餐后突发严重上腹痛并放射至背部，反复呕吐，出现巩膜黄染、血液浓缩、低钙血症和脂肪酶显著升高。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case requires recognizing biliary pancreatitis at admission, distinguishing etiology cues from severity markers, treating symptomatic true hypocalcemia, identifying Stage 2 deterioration as evolving cholangitis from an impacted CBD stone, and supporting source control with urgent ERCP while maintaining perfusion, oxygenation, analgesia, and glucose management. Improvement after ERCP is evaluated by trends in pain, vital signs, oxygenation, urine output, WBC, bilirubin, lactate, calcium, and oral intake tolerance rather than lipase normalization alone.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例要求在入院时识别胆源性胰腺炎，区分病因线索和严重程度指标，处理有症状的真正低钙血症，识别第 2 阶段病情恶化是 CBD 结石嵌顿导致的进展性胆管炎，并在维持灌注、氧合、镇痛和血糖管理的同时协助紧急 ERCP 进行源控制。ERCP 后是否好转应根据疼痛、生命体征、氧合、尿量、WBC、胆红素、乳酸、钙和进食耐受性等趋势判断，而不是单靠脂肪酶正常化。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding GI emergencies, first identify the cause, then track severity and complications by timeline. Source control matters when obstruction plus infection is present.","testTakingStrategyZh":"展开式胃肠急症题中，先识别病因，再按时间线追踪严重程度和并发症。存在梗阻加感染时，源控制是关键。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2500,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,94],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"Using the admission data only, classify each finding by what it most directly tells the nurse.","fullStemZh":"仅根据入院资料，将每项发现按其最直接提示的信息进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the admission data only, classify each finding by what it most directly tells the nurse.","terminalSentenceZh":"仅根据入院资料，将每项发现按其最直接提示的信息进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r_known_gallstones","en":"Known history of gallstones with pain after a fatty meal","zh":"既往胆结石史，且高脂餐后出现疼痛"},{"id":"r_biliary_labs","en":"ALT 280 U/L, AST 210 U/L, direct bilirubin 2.4 mg/dL, alkaline phosphatase 310 U/L, and mild scleral icterus","zh":"ALT 280 U/L、AST 210 U/L、直接胆红素 2.4 mg/dL、碱性磷酸酶 310 U/L，并有轻度巩膜黄染"},{"id":"r_lipase","en":"Lipase 1,840 U/L","zh":"脂肪酶 1,840 U/L"},{"id":"r_hct","en":"Hematocrit 48% with tacky mucous membranes and concentrated urine","zh":"血细胞比容 48%，伴黏膜发黏和尿液浓缩"},{"id":"r_calcium","en":"Total calcium 7.6 mg/dL and ionized calcium 3.6 mg/dL","zh":"总钙 7.6 mg/dL，离子钙 3.6 mg/dL"},{"id":"r_wbc_glucose","en":"WBC 14.5 ×10³/µL and glucose 180 mg/dL","zh":"WBC 14.5 ×10³/µL，血糖 180 mg/dL"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_biliary","en":"Supports biliary etiology","zh":"支持胆源性病因"},{"id":"c_confirms_ap","en":"Confirms acute pancreatitis","zh":"确认急性胰腺炎"},{"id":"c_volume","en":"Volume depletion marker","zh":"容量不足指标"},{"id":"c_severity","en":"Severity or prognostic marker","zh":"严重程度或预后指标"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r_known_gallstones","columnIds":["c_biliary"]},{"rowId":"r_biliary_labs","columnIds":["c_biliary"]},{"rowId":"r_lipase","columnIds":["c_confirms_ap"]},{"rowId":"r_hct","columnIds":["c_volume"]},{"rowId":"r_calcium","columnIds":["c_severity"]},{"rowId":"r_wbc_glucose","columnIds":["c_severity"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The gallstone history, post-fatty-meal onset, cholestatic/direct bilirubin pattern, ALT-predominant transaminase elevation, and scleral icterus point to a biliary cause. Lipase greater than three times the upper limit confirms acute pancreatitis but does not identify the cause. Hemoconcentration and concentrated urine reflect intravascular depletion from third spacing. Hypocalcemia, leukocytosis, and hyperglycemia are severity markers rather than etiologic clues.","rationaleCorrectZh":"胆结石史、高脂餐后发作、胆汁淤积/直接胆红素升高模式、以 ALT 为主的转氨酶升高以及巩膜黄染提示胆源性病因。脂肪酶超过正常上限 3 倍可确认急性胰腺炎，但不能说明病因。血液浓缩和尿液浓缩反映第三间隙液体丢失导致的血容量不足。低钙血症、白细胞增多和高血糖是严重程度指标，而不是病因线索。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate cause-finding cues from severity cues. A lab can be abnormal and important without explaining the etiology.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把寻找病因的线索与判断严重程度的线索分开。化验异常可以很重要，但不一定解释病因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2501,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,66],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Complete the interpretation of the patient's Stage 1 hypocalcemia.","fullStemZh":"完成对患者第 1 阶段低钙血症的判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the interpretation of the patient's Stage 1 hypocalcemia.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成对患者第 1 阶段低钙血症的判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The patient's true hypocalcemia is most directly caused by {{1}}. The finding that confirms this is not just low-albumin pseudohypocalcemia is {{2}}. The positive Chvostek sign, positive Trousseau sign, and perioral tingling indicate {{3}}.","zh":"患者真正低钙血症最直接由 {{1}} 引起。确认这并非仅由低白蛋白造成的假性低钙血症的依据是 {{2}}。Chvostek 征阳性、Trousseau 征阳性和口周麻木提示 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o_saponification","en":"fat saponification with calcium sequestration","zh":"脂肪皂化导致钙被结合/隔离"},{"id":"o_diet","en":"acute dietary calcium deficiency","zh":"急性膳食钙摄入不足"},{"id":"o_renal","en":"renal calcium wasting from diuretic therapy","zh":"利尿剂治疗导致肾性钙丢失"}],"correct":"o_saponification"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o_ionized","en":"ionized calcium 3.6 mg/dL","zh":"离子钙 3.6 mg/dL"},{"id":"o_magnesium","en":"magnesium 1.7 mg/dL","zh":"镁 1.7 mg/dL"},{"id":"o_albumin","en":"albumin 3.2 g/dL","zh":"白蛋白 3.2 g/dL"}],"correct":"o_ionized"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o_symptomatic","en":"symptomatic neuromuscular irritability requiring provider notification and IV calcium as ordered","zh":"有症状的神经肌肉兴奋性增高，需要通知医嘱者并按医嘱给予 IV 钙剂"},{"id":"o_observe","en":"an expected benign finding that only requires routine morning labs","zh":"预期的良性发现，只需常规晨间复查化验"},{"id":"o_hyperventilation","en":"isolated anxiety-related hyperventilation without electrolyte significance","zh":"单纯焦虑相关过度通气，与电解质无关"}],"correct":"o_symptomatic"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In acute pancreatitis, released lipase digests peripancreatic fat. Free fatty acids bind ionized calcium and form insoluble calcium soaps, lowering physiologically active calcium. The low ionized calcium confirms true hypocalcemia despite low albumin. Provoked facial twitching, carpopedal spasm, and perioral tingling are symptomatic neuromuscular irritability and justify prompt notification and IV calcium replacement as ordered.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性胰腺炎时，释放的脂肪酶消化胰周脂肪，游离脂肪酸与离子钙结合形成不溶性钙皂，降低具有生理活性的钙。离子钙降低说明是真正低钙血症，而不仅是低白蛋白造成的总钙偏低。诱发面部抽动、手足搐搦和口周麻木属于有症状的神经肌肉兴奋性增高，应及时通知并按医嘱给予 IV 钙剂。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For calcium questions, look for ionized calcium and symptoms; these outweigh a reassuring explanation based only on albumin.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到钙相关题，要看离子钙和症状；这些比单纯用白蛋白解释更有决定性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2502,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,73],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"At hour 18, which complication best explains the patient's deterioration?","fullStemZh":"在第 18 小时，哪种并发症最能解释患者病情恶化？","terminalSentenceEn":"At hour 18, which complication best explains the patient's deterioration?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第 18 小时，哪种并发症最能解释患者病情恶化？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Evolving cholangitis from persistent common bile duct obstruction","zh":"持续性胆总管梗阻导致的进展性胆管炎"},{"id":"D","en":"Aspiration pneumonia as the primary source","zh":"吸入性肺炎作为主要感染源"},{"id":"C","en":"Urinary-source sepsis","zh":"泌尿系统来源败血症"},{"id":"B","en":"Infected pancreatic necrosis","zh":"感染性胰腺坏死"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The new fever, SIRS pattern, jaundice, and ultrasound-confirmed dilated common bile duct with an impacted distal stone point to evolving cholangitis superimposed on gallstone pancreatitis. The management implication is urgent biliary decompression with ERCP plus antimicrobial therapy as ordered.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新发发热、SIRS 表现、黄疸，以及超声确认胆总管扩张并远端结石嵌顿，指向胆石性胰腺炎合并进展性胆管炎。处理重点是按医嘱给予抗菌治疗，并紧急行 ERCP 解除胆道梗阻。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the complication to the timeline and source cue. Early fever plus obstructed bile duct points to cholangitis more than pancreatic necrosis.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将并发症与时间线和感染来源线索对应。早期发热加胆管梗阻更支持胆管炎，而不是胰腺坏死。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2503,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[50,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,23],"fullStemEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate at Stage 2? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate at Stage 2?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Confirm blood cultures are obtained and anticipate empiric IV antibiotics as ordered for suspected cholangitis.","zh":"确认已采集血培养，并预期按医嘱为疑似胆管炎给予经验性 IV 抗生素。"},{"id":"C","en":"Facilitate urgent ERCP consultation and preparation for biliary decompression.","zh":"协助紧急 ERCP 会诊和准备，以进行胆道减压。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the provider about declining urine output and rising lactate; reassess volume status and anticipate a fluid bolus or rate adjustment.","zh":"将尿量下降和乳酸升高通知医嘱者；重新评估容量状态，并预期可能需要补液 bolus 或调整输液速度。"},{"id":"D","en":"Titrate supplemental oxygen and monitor for worsening respiratory status related to the pleural effusion.","zh":"调节氧疗并监测胸腔积液相关呼吸状态恶化。"},{"id":"F","en":"Start oral clear liquids now because she has not vomited for eight hours.","zh":"因为 8 小时未呕吐，现在开始口服清流质。"},{"id":"E","en":"Continue ordered IV opioid analgesia and manage hyperglycemia per the insulin sliding scale.","zh":"继续按医嘱给予 IV 阿片类镇痛，并按胰岛素滑动剂量处理高血糖。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient has suspected cholangitis with an obstructing CBD stone plus signs of hypoperfusion, respiratory compromise, persistent pain, and hyperglycemia. Appropriate nursing actions include escalation and reassessment for additional goal-directed fluids, cultures and antibiotics as ordered, ERCP preparation, oxygen/respiratory monitoring, effective analgesia, and insulin per order. Feeding is not appropriate right now because she declines and feels too nauseated during active deterioration. Immediate CT for necrosis would distract from the time-sensitive biliary source control, and the falling hematocrit alone does not override declining urine output and rising lactate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者存在胆总管梗阻结石并疑似胆管炎，同时有低灌注、呼吸受累、持续疼痛和高血糖。合适的护理措施包括升级报告并重新评估是否需要目标导向补液、按医嘱采血培养和使用抗生素、准备 ERCP、氧疗和呼吸监测、有效镇痛以及按医嘱使用胰岛素。她在病情恶化时仍恶心并拒绝进食，因此此刻不宜进食。立即为坏死做 CT 会分散对胆道源控制的时效性处理；血细胞比容下降本身不能抵消尿量下降和乳酸升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For multi-select deterioration items, select all actions that address current threats and source control; do not select an action just because it may become appropriate later.","testTakingStrategyZh":"多选题遇到病情恶化时，选择能处理当前威胁和源控制的措施；不要因为某措施以后可能合适就现在选择。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate at Stage 2?","controlSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段哪些护理措施合适？"}
{"queueIndex":2504,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[48,84],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,32],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, the patient asks to eat after ERCP. Which response by the nurse is best?","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段 ERCP 后患者询问能否进食。护士最佳回应是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which response by the nurse is best?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最佳回应是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, the patient asks to eat after ERCP.","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 3 阶段 ERCP 后患者询问能否进食。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Keep the patient NPO until lipase returns to the normal range.","zh":"让患者继续禁食，直到脂肪酶恢复正常。"},{"id":"A","en":"Offer the ordered low-fat solid food as tolerated because pain is improving, bowel sounds have returned, vomiting has stopped, and she is hungry.","zh":"按医嘱提供可耐受的低脂固体食物，因为疼痛改善、肠鸣音恢复、呕吐停止且患者感到饥饿。"},{"id":"D","en":"Require a clear-liquid to full-liquid to soft-diet progression before any low-fat solid food.","zh":"必须先从清流质、全流质、软食逐步过渡，才能给低脂固体食物。"},{"id":"C","en":"Allow only ice chips for 24 more hours because any oral intake can trigger recurrent pancreatitis.","zh":"再 24 小时只允许含冰片，因为任何口服摄入都会诱发胰腺炎复发。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Readiness for oral intake in improving acute pancreatitis is based on clinical tolerance, not lipase normalization. This patient has decreasing pain, returned bowel sounds, no vomiting with liquids, hunger, and an order for low-fat solid food as tolerated. Lipase may remain elevated after clinical improvement. A mandatory liquid-to-solid progression is not required if low-fat solids are tolerated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性胰腺炎好转时是否可进食，取决于临床耐受性，而不是脂肪酶是否正常。该患者疼痛减轻、肠鸣音恢复、清流质后无呕吐、感到饥饿，并有按耐受进低脂固体食物的医嘱。临床改善后脂肪酶仍可升高。若能耐受低脂固体食物，不需要强制按流质到固体的阶梯过渡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a lab is still abnormal but the patient is clinically improving, ask whether the lab is a treatment target or just a trailing marker.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当化验仍异常但患者临床好转时，要判断该化验是治疗目标，还是滞后的指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2505,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,29],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each trend or finding based on how it should guide the nurse's evaluation.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段，根据每项趋势或发现对护理评估的意义进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each trend or finding based on how it should guide the nurse's evaluation.","terminalSentenceZh":"第 3 阶段，根据每项趋势或发现对护理评估的意义进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r_pain_vitals","en":"Pain 8/10 to 4/10, HR 118 to 92, BP 108/62 to 124/76, temperature 101.1 °F (38.4 °C) to 99.7 °F (37.6 °C)","zh":"疼痛 8/10 降至 4/10，HR 118 降至 92，BP 108/62 升至 124/76，体温 101.1 °F (38.4 °C) 降至 99.7 °F (37.6 °C)"},{"id":"r_oxygen","en":"SpO2 94% on 2 L nasal cannula to 96% on room air","zh":"SpO2 从鼻导管 2 L 下 94% 改善为空气中 96%"},{"id":"r_urine","en":"Urine output improves to 50 mL/hr","zh":"尿量改善至 50 mL/hr"},{"id":"r_labs","en":"WBC, bilirubin, calcium, and lactate improve after ERCP","zh":"ERCP 后 WBC、胆红素、钙和乳酸改善"},{"id":"r_lipase_high","en":"Lipase remains elevated at 980 U/L but is trending down","zh":"脂肪酶仍为 980 U/L，但呈下降趋势"},{"id":"r_worse_fever","en":"Recurrent fever or worsening oxygenation after initial improvement","zh":"初步改善后再次发热或氧合恶化"},{"id":"r_oral_failure","en":"Unable to tolerate oral nutrition after 72 hours","zh":"72 小时后仍不能耐受口服营养"}],"columns":[{"id":"c_improving","en":"Supports improvement","zh":"支持病情改善"},{"id":"c_escalate","en":"Escalation/CT trigger if persistent or worsening","zh":"若持续或恶化需升级/考虑 CT"},{"id":"c_not_target","en":"Not a management target by itself","zh":"本身不是管理目标"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r_pain_vitals","columnIds":["c_improving"]},{"rowId":"r_oxygen","columnIds":["c_improving"]},{"rowId":"r_urine","columnIds":["c_improving"]},{"rowId":"r_labs","columnIds":["c_improving"]},{"rowId":"r_lipase_high","columnIds":["c_not_target"]},{"rowId":"r_worse_fever","columnIds":["c_escalate"]},{"rowId":"r_oral_failure","columnIds":["c_escalate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient is improving because pain, hemodynamics, oxygenation, urine output, bilirubin, WBC, calcium, and lactate are all moving in the right direction after ERCP. Lipase can remain elevated and should not be used alone to decide feeding or recovery. Recurrent fever, worsening oxygenation, organ dysfunction, persistent pain, or inability to tolerate nutrition after 72 hours would require escalation and possible contrast-enhanced CT at an appropriate time to evaluate complications such as necrosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ERCP 后疼痛、血流动力学、氧合、尿量、胆红素、WBC、钙和乳酸均向好转方向变化，说明患者正在改善。脂肪酶可持续升高，不能单独用于决定进食或恢复情况。再次发热、氧合恶化、器官功能障碍、疼痛持续或 72 小时后仍不能耐受营养，均需升级处理，并在合适时机考虑增强 CT 评估坏死等并发症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes with trends across systems, not one enzyme. Ask whether the patient is perfusing, oxygenating, clearing obstruction, and tolerating nutrition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估结果要看多个系统的趋势，而不是一个酶值。要问患者是否灌注改善、氧合改善、梗阻解除、能否耐受营养。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2506,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gallstone_pancreatitis_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.51","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.51.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.51.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[362,456],"terminalOffsetsZh":[174,201],"fullStemEn":"At hour 18, a 45-year-old woman admitted with acute gallstone pancreatitis has T 38.4 C, HR 118, BP 108/62, RR 26, SpO2 94% on 2 L nasal cannula, urine output 30 mL/hr, lactate 2.6 mmol/L, WBC 19.2 ×10³/µL, bilirubin 3.2 mg/dL from admission, and worsening abdominal distention and pain. Ultrasound shows an 11-mm common bile duct with a shadowing distal stone. Select the most likely condition, the two priority actions, and the two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"第 18 小时，一名因急性胆石性胰腺炎入院的 45 岁女性出现 T 38.4 C、HR 118、BP 108/62、RR 26、鼻导管 2 L 下 SpO2 94%、尿量 30 mL/hr、乳酸 2.6 mmol/L、WBC 19.2 ×10³/µL、入院胆红素 3.2 mg/dL，并且腹胀和疼痛加重。超声显示胆总管 11 mm，远端有声影结石。请选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the most likely condition, the two priority actions, and the two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Ultrasound shows an 11-mm common bile duct with a shadowing distal stone.","penultimateSentenceZh":"超声显示胆总管 11 mm，远端有声影结石。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_aspiration","en":"Sepsis from aspiration pneumonia as the primary source","zh":"吸入性肺炎作为主要来源导致的败血症"},{"id":"bt_cond_necrosis","en":"Infected pancreatic necrosis","zh":"感染性胰腺坏死"},{"id":"bt_cond_cholangitis","en":"Acute gallstone pancreatitis complicated by evolving cholangitis from persistent CBD obstruction","zh":"急性胆石性胰腺炎合并持续 CBD 梗阻导致的进展性胆管炎"}],"correct":"bt_cond_cholangitis"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_act_ct_now","en":"Request immediate contrast-enhanced CT for pancreatic necrosis before ERCP","zh":"在 ERCP 前立即要求增强 CT 评估胰腺坏死"},{"id":"bt_act_ercp","en":"Facilitate urgent ERCP consultation and preparation for biliary decompression","zh":"协助紧急 ERCP 会诊和准备，以进行胆道减压"},{"id":"bt_act_cultures_abx","en":"Notify the provider of deterioration, ensure blood cultures are obtained, and anticipate empiric IV antibiotics as ordered","zh":"通知医嘱者病情恶化，确认采集血培养，并预期按医嘱给予经验性 IV 抗生素"},{"id":"bt_act_keep_fluids","en":"Maintain the current fluid rate without reassessment despite urine output 30 mL/hr and lactate 2.6 mmol/L","zh":"尽管尿量 30 mL/hr、乳酸 2.6 mmol/L，仍不重新评估而维持当前补液速度"}],"correct":["bt_act_cultures_abx","bt_act_ercp"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_param_temp_wbc","en":"Temperature and WBC trend after antibiotics and ERCP","zh":"抗生素和 ERCP 后的体温与 WBC 趋势"},{"id":"bt_param_amylase","en":"Serial amylase level to guide immediate biliary decompression decisions","zh":"用连续淀粉酶指导即时胆道减压决策"},{"id":"bt_param_urine","en":"Urine output trend","zh":"尿量趋势"},{"id":"bt_param_lipase","en":"Serial lipase level as the main marker of cholangitis response","zh":"将连续脂肪酶作为胆管炎反应的主要指标"}],"correct":["bt_param_urine","bt_param_temp_wbc"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The unifying problem is gallstone pancreatitis complicated by evolving cholangitis: the patient has fever, SIRS, jaundice/obstructive biliary labs, and an ultrasound-confirmed obstructing distal CBD stone. Priority nursing actions support source control and sepsis management: notify/escalate, ensure cultures and antibiotics as ordered, and facilitate urgent ERCP. Urine output tracks perfusion during resuscitation, and temperature/WBC trends after antibiotics and ERCP help evaluate response to biliary decompression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"统一问题是胆石性胰腺炎合并进展性胆管炎：患者有发热、SIRS、黄疸/胆道梗阻化验模式，以及超声确认远端 CBD 梗阻结石。优先护理措施是支持源控制和败血症处理：通知/升级、确保按医嘱采培养和用抗生素，并协助紧急 ERCP。尿量反映复苏期间灌注情况，抗生素和 ERCP 后的体温/WBC 趋势可评估胆道减压反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bowtie items, choose the condition that explains all zones, then select actions that treat the cause and parameters that show response.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bowtie 题时，先选能解释所有区域的情况，再选处理病因的措施和能显示反应的监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2507,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.52","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.52.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[370,570],"terminalOffsetsZh":[98,155],"fullStemEn":"Guillain-Barre syndrome with progressive respiratory compromise after Campylobacter enteritis A 32-year-old previously healthy man presents with five days of progressive ascending paresthesias, neuropathic leg pain, wide-based gait, bilateral foot drop, and absent lower-extremity deep tendon reflexes after a Campylobacter jejuni diarrheal illness three weeks earlier. Initial oxygenation is normal, but the care team obtains baseline and serial bedside FVC and MIP measurements because Guillain-Barre syndrome can progress rapidly to neuromuscular respiratory failure.","fullStemZh":"弯曲杆菌肠炎后发生进行性呼吸受累的格林-巴利综合征 一名既往健康的32岁男性在3周前发生空肠弯曲杆菌性腹泻后，出现5天进行性上行性感觉异常、神经性腿痛、宽基底步态、双侧足下垂以及下肢深腱反射消失。初始氧合正常，但医疗团队安排基线和连续床旁FVC与MIP测量，因为格林-巴利综合征可迅速进展为神经肌肉性呼吸衰竭。","terminalSentenceEn":"Initial oxygenation is normal, but the care team obtains baseline and serial bedside FVC and MIP measurements because Guillain-Barre syndrome can progress rapidly to neuromuscular respiratory failure.","terminalSentenceZh":"初始氧合正常，但医疗团队安排基线和连续床旁FVC与MIP测量，因为格林-巴利综合征可迅速进展为神经肌肉性呼吸衰竭。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Guillain-Barre syndrome with progressive respiratory compromise after Campylobacter enteritis A 32-year-old previously healthy man presents with five days of progressive ascending paresthesias, neuropathic leg pain, wide-based gait, bilateral foot drop, and absent lower-extremity deep tendon reflexes after a Campylobacter jejuni diarrheal illness three weeks earlier.","penultimateSentenceZh":"弯曲杆菌肠炎后发生进行性呼吸受累的格林-巴利综合征 一名既往健康的32岁男性在3周前发生空肠弯曲杆菌性腹泻后，出现5天进行性上行性感觉异常、神经性腿痛、宽基底步态、双侧足下垂以及下肢深腱反射消失。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows the clinical judgment arc of GBS after Campylobacter infection: recognizing ascending symmetric weakness with areflexia; interpreting albuminocytologic dissociation and demyelinating NCS as supportive diagnostic data; prioritizing GBS over cord compression, transverse myelitis, and myasthenia gravis; using serial FVC and MIP rather than SpO2 alone to detect neuromuscular respiratory decline; preparing for intubation once the case thresholds and airway-protection findings are met; and evaluating plateau-phase recovery while continuing complication prevention and psychosocial support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例体现了空肠弯曲杆菌感染后GBS的临床判断过程：识别对称性上行无力伴反射消失；将蛋白细胞分离和脱髓鞘性神经传导检查解释为支持性诊断资料；在脊髓压迫、横贯性脊髓炎和重症肌无力之间优先考虑GBS；使用连续FVC和MIP而不是仅凭SpO2发现神经肌肉性呼吸下降；当病例阈值和气道保护受损表现达到时准备插管；并在平台期评估恢复，同时继续预防并发症和提供心理社会支持。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Track what changed over time. In GBS, the dangerous change is not oxygenation first; it is loss of respiratory muscle strength, cough, bulbar protection, and autonomic stability.","testTakingStrategyZh":"追踪随时间变化的内容。在GBS中，危险变化首先不是氧合，而是呼吸肌力、咳嗽、延髓/吞咽保护和自主神经稳定性的丧失。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2508,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,46],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that should make the nurse urgently communicate concern for Guillain-Barre syndrome rather than treating the client as stable because he is still ambulatory.","fullStemZh":"请标出哪些发现应使护士紧急沟通对格林-巴利综合征的担忧，而不是因为患者仍能行走就认为其稳定。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that should make the nurse urgently communicate concern for Guillain-Barre syndrome rather than treating the client as stable because he is still ambulatory.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出哪些发现应使护士紧急沟通对格林-巴利综合征的担忧，而不是因为患者仍能行走就认为其稳定。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"h1","en":"Three weeks ago, stool culture grew Campylobacter jejuni after bloody diarrhea with fever.","zh":"3周前血性腹泻伴发热后，粪便培养检出空肠弯曲杆菌。","selectable":true},{"id":"h2","en":"He reports five days of tingling and burning pain that began in both feet and ascended to the mid-thighs.","zh":"他诉5天前双足开始刺痛和烧灼痛，并上行至大腿中部。","selectable":true},{"id":"h3","en":"He had difficulty climbing stairs and now must grip the handrail to climb one flight.","zh":"他爬楼困难，现在爬一层楼必须抓扶手。","selectable":true},{"id":"h4","en":"SpO2 is 98% on room air.","zh":"室内空气SpO2为98%。","selectable":true},{"id":"h5","en":"Upper extremity strength is 5/5 at presentation.","zh":"初诊时上肢肌力为5/5。","selectable":true},{"id":"h6","en":"Lower extremity strength is reduced with bilateral ankle dorsiflexion 3/5 and great toe extension 3/5.","zh":"下肢肌力下降，双侧踝背屈3/5、拇趾伸展3/5。","selectable":true},{"id":"h7","en":"Achilles and patellar reflexes are absent bilaterally.","zh":"双侧跟腱反射和髌腱反射消失。","selectable":true},{"id":"h8","en":"There is no sensory level on the trunk and rectal tone is normal.","zh":"躯干无感觉平面，直肠张力正常。","selectable":true},{"id":"h9","en":"The gait is wide-based with bilateral foot drop.","zh":"步态宽基底并伴双侧足下垂。","selectable":true},{"id":"h10","en":"CBC, electrolytes, CK, ESR, and CRP are unremarkable.","zh":"CBC、电解质、CK、ESR和CRP无明显异常。","selectable":true}],"correct":["h1","h2","h3","h6","h7","h8","h9"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The urgent pattern is a recent Campylobacter infection followed by rapidly progressive, symmetric, ascending sensory symptoms and weakness with areflexia and foot drop. The absence of a sensory level and preserved rectal tone make a spinal cord syndrome less likely, supporting urgent neurologic evaluation for GBS with respiratory monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"紧急模式是近期空肠弯曲杆菌感染后出现快速进展、对称、上行性感觉症状和无力，并伴反射消失和足下垂。无感觉平面且直肠张力保留，使脊髓综合征可能性较低，支持紧急神经科评估GBS并进行呼吸监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In acute weakness questions, first decide whether the pattern is upper motor neuron, lower motor neuron, neuromuscular junction, or muscle. Ascending symmetric weakness with areflexia after infection points to peripheral nerve disease and requires respiratory planning even before oxygen saturation falls.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到急性无力题，先判断模式属于上运动神经元、下运动神经元、神经肌肉接头还是肌肉疾病。感染后对称性上行无力伴反射消失指向周围神经病变，即使氧饱和度尚未下降也需要考虑呼吸计划。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2509,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"For each finding, choose the interpretation that best guides the nurse's understanding of the diagnosis and ongoing monitoring.","fullStemZh":"针对每项发现，选择最能指导护士理解诊断和后续监测的解释。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each finding, choose the interpretation that best guides the nurse's understanding of the diagnosis and ongoing monitoring.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对每项发现，选择最能指导护士理解诊断和后续监测的解释。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"CSF protein 98 mg/dL with CSF WBC 3 cells/uL","zh":"CSF蛋白98 mg/dL，CSF白细胞3个/uL"},{"id":"r2","en":"Nerve conduction studies show slowed conduction, conduction block, and prolonged F-wave latencies","zh":"神经传导检查显示传导减慢、传导阻滞和F波潜伏期延长"},{"id":"r3","en":"Serial bedside FVC and MIP measurements","zh":"连续床旁FVC和MIP测量"},{"id":"r4","en":"SpO2 remains 98% on room air at presentation","zh":"初诊时室内空气SpO2仍为98%"},{"id":"r5","en":"Baseline FVC 42 mL/kg and MIP -62 cmH2O","zh":"基线FVC 42 mL/kg，MIP -62 cmH2O"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Primary respiratory trend to monitor","zh":"主要呼吸趋势监测指标"},{"id":"c4","en":"Indicates bacterial meningitis","zh":"提示细菌性脑膜炎"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports GBS/AIDP diagnosis","zh":"支持GBS/AIDP诊断"},{"id":"c3","en":"Potentially misleading if used alone","zh":"若单独使用可能误导"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Albuminocytologic dissociation and demyelinating nerve conduction findings support GBS/AIDP. FVC and MIP directly track respiratory muscle capacity and must be followed serially. A normal SpO2 can be misleading because oxygenation may remain normal until ventilatory failure is advanced.","rationaleCorrectZh":"蛋白细胞分离和脱髓鞘性神经传导结果支持GBS/AIDP。FVC和MIP直接反映呼吸肌能力，必须连续追踪。正常SpO2可能误导，因为氧合可在通气衰竭已很严重时才下降。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the lungs are healthy but muscles are weak, do not anchor on oxygen saturation. Choose measures that test mechanics: vital capacity, inspiratory force, cough strength, and bulbar protection.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当肺本身健康但肌肉无力时，不要锚定氧饱和度。应选择能测试机械功能的指标：肺活量、吸气力、咳嗽能力和延髓/吞咽保护功能。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2510,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[129,184],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,50],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is comparing the most likely diagnosis with acute spinal cord compression, transverse myelitis, and myasthenia gravis. Which diagnosis best matches the full clinical picture?","fullStemZh":"护士正在将最可能的诊断与急性脊髓压迫、横贯性脊髓炎和重症肌无力进行比较。哪项诊断最符合完整临床表现？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which diagnosis best matches the full clinical picture?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项诊断最符合完整临床表现？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is comparing the most likely diagnosis with acute spinal cord compression, transverse myelitis, and myasthenia gravis.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在将最可能的诊断与急性脊髓压迫、横贯性脊髓炎和重症肌无力进行比较。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Myasthenia gravis crisis","zh":"重症肌无力危象"},{"id":"C","en":"Transverse myelitis","zh":"横贯性脊髓炎"},{"id":"B","en":"Acute spinal cord compression","zh":"急性脊髓压迫"},{"id":"A","en":"Guillain-Barre syndrome, acute inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy variant","zh":"格林-巴利综合征，急性炎性脱髓鞘性多发神经病变型"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"GBS/AIDP best explains postinfectious onset, symmetric ascending weakness, areflexia, albuminocytologic dissociation, demyelinating nerve conduction findings, and lack of cord signs. The other diagnoses have key expected findings that are absent or contradicted by the case.","rationaleCorrectZh":"GBS/AIDP最能解释感染后发病、对称性上行无力、反射消失、蛋白细胞分离、脱髓鞘性神经传导结果以及缺乏脊髓体征。其他诊断预期会出现的关键发现，在本病例中缺失或被事实反驳。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not diagnose acute weakness by the word 'ascending' alone. Match the reflexes, imaging, sensory level, bowel/bladder pattern, and weakness type to the disease process.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要仅凭“上行”一词诊断急性无力。要把反射、影像、感觉平面、大小便模式和无力类型与疾病过程相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2511,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[239,261],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,80],"fullStemEn":"The provider has diagnosed GBS and ordered IVIG, serial FVC/MIP, and ICU notification if respiratory parameters decline. Which statements show correct nursing understanding of the treatment plan and provider-stated respiratory thresholds? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"医生已诊断GBS，并医嘱IVIG、连续FVC/MIP监测，以及若呼吸参数下降则通知ICU。哪些说法体现护士正确理解治疗计划和医嘱规定的呼吸阈值？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements show correct nursing understanding of the treatment plan and provider-stated respiratory thresholds?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些说法体现护士正确理解治疗计划和医嘱规定的呼吸阈值？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Per the case parameters, FVC less than 20 mL/kg or MIP weaker than -30 cmH2O should trigger preparation for intubation/escalation.","zh":"根据本病例参数，FVC低于20 mL/kg或MIP弱于-30 cmH2O时，应准备插管/升级处理。"},{"id":"F","en":"If a corticosteroid order appears for GBS treatment alone, the nurse should clarify it before administration.","zh":"如果出现仅用于治疗GBS的糖皮质激素医嘱，护士应在给药前澄清。"},{"id":"C","en":"A falling FVC and a MIP that becomes less negative indicate weakening respiratory muscles.","zh":"FVC下降且MIP变得不那么负，提示呼吸肌变弱。"},{"id":"A","en":"IVIG and plasma exchange are disease-modifying therapies used for GBS; IVIG should be started as ordered.","zh":"IVIG和血浆置换是GBS的疾病修饰治疗；应按医嘱开始IVIG。"},{"id":"E","en":"Normal SpO2 means the client is not at risk for respiratory failure during the next several hours.","zh":"SpO2正常表示患者在未来数小时内没有呼吸衰竭风险。"},{"id":"B","en":"High-dose corticosteroids are expected first-line therapy because GBS is immune-mediated.","zh":"由于GBS是免疫介导性疾病，预计一线治疗应为大剂量糖皮质激素。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The ordered IVIG is appropriate disease-modifying therapy. Respiratory decisions in this case are driven by serial FVC and MIP: falling FVC and less negative MIP mean worsening muscle strength. The case-stated escalation thresholds are FVC less than 20 mL/kg or MIP weaker than -30 cmH2O. Corticosteroids are not recommended for GBS treatment and should be clarified if ordered for that purpose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"医嘱IVIG是合适的疾病修饰治疗。本病例的呼吸决策由连续FVC和MIP驱动：FVC下降且MIP不那么负表示肌力恶化。病例规定的升级阈值为FVC低于20 mL/kg或MIP弱于-30 cmH2O。糖皮质激素不推荐用于GBS治疗，若为此目的开立应澄清。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a case gives explicit provider thresholds, use those thresholds. Then check whether the action is nursing implementation, monitoring, or clarification of an unsafe order.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当病例给出明确医嘱阈值时，应使用这些阈值。再判断行动属于护理执行、监测，还是澄清不安全医嘱。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2512,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[229,251],"terminalOffsetsZh":[98,106],"fullStemEn":"At hour 20, the client has FVC 19 mL/kg, MIP -26 cmH2O, ineffective cough, diaphoresis, labored RR 28, SpO2 93% on 2 L nasal cannula, autonomic instability, and unilateral absent gag reflex. Which nursing actions are priorities? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第20小时，患者FVC 19 mL/kg、MIP -26 cmH2O、咳嗽无效、出汗、RR 28且费力、2 L鼻导管下SpO2 93%、自主神经不稳定，并有单侧咽反射消失。哪些护理行动是优先事项？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are priorities?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些护理行动是优先事项？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Maintain continuous cardiac telemetry and anticipate treatment of labile blood pressure with short-acting titrated agents as ordered.","zh":"维持连续心电监护，并预期按医嘱使用短效可滴定药物处理血压波动。"},{"id":"A","en":"Prepare for and assist with emergent endotracheal intubation.","zh":"准备并协助紧急气管插管。"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure suction, oxygen delivery equipment, IV access, rapid sequence medication readiness as directed, and continuous monitoring are in place.","zh":"确保吸引、供氧设备、静脉通路、按医嘱准备快速序贯插管用药，以及连续监测到位。"},{"id":"D","en":"Continue the IVIG infusion on schedule through the airway transition unless a separate infusion reaction or safety issue occurs.","zh":"除非发生单独的输注反应或安全问题，应在气道处理过程中按计划继续IVIG输注。"},{"id":"E","en":"Wait for SpO2 to fall below 90% before escalating airway management.","zh":"等待SpO2降至90%以下后再升级气道管理。"},{"id":"B","en":"Initiate BiPAP as the preferred substitute for intubation because he is still awake.","zh":"因为患者仍清醒，优先使用BiPAP替代插管。"}],"correct":["A","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Both provider-stated respiratory thresholds have been crossed, and the clinical signs confirm impending ventilatory failure with poor airway protection. The nurse should prepare for intubation, support safe airway management, continue disease-modifying IVIG, and maintain telemetry because dysautonomia can cause dangerous BP and rhythm swings.","rationaleCorrectZh":"两个医嘱规定的呼吸阈值均已越过，临床表现证实即将发生通气衰竭并伴气道保护差。护士应准备插管，支持安全气道管理，继续疾病修饰性IVIG，并维持心电监护，因为自主神经功能障碍可导致危险的血压和心律波动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When objective thresholds and clinical signs both point to airway failure, act on the airway. Do not use a still-awake client or a not-yet-critical SpO2 as reassurance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当客观阈值和临床表现都指向气道/通气失败时，应处理气道。不要因为患者仍清醒或SpO2尚未极低就感到放心。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2513,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,56],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Complete the nurse's evaluation of the day-5 ICU status.","fullStemZh":"完成护士对ICU第5天状态的评估。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nurse's evaluation of the day-5 ICU status.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护士对ICU第5天状态的评估。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client's day-5 findings are most consistent with {{1}}. Extubation is {{2}} because {{3}}. The narrowing heart-rate and blood-pressure swings suggest {{4}}, and nursing care should continue to include {{5}}.","zh":"患者第5天的表现最符合 {{1}}。因为 {{3}}，所以 {{2}}。心率和血压波动范围缩小提示 {{4}}，护理仍应包括 {{5}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"resolution of GBS and readiness for discharge","zh":"GBS已缓解并准备出院"},{"id":"o1","en":"the expected plateau phase after progression","zh":"进展期后的预期平台期"},{"id":"o2","en":"clear failure of IVIG requiring automatic repeat dosing","zh":"IVIG明确失败，需要自动重复给药"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"unrelated to respiratory muscle measurements","zh":"与呼吸肌测量无关"},{"id":"o1","en":"not yet indicated","zh":"尚不适合"},{"id":"o2","en":"safe now because SpO2 is adequate","zh":"因SpO2足够而现在安全"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"the bowel sounds have returned","zh":"肠鸣音已经恢复"},{"id":"o1","en":"FVC 13 mL/kg and MIP -22 cmH2O remain below the case's safe extubation trajectory","zh":"FVC 13 mL/kg且MIP -22 cmH2O仍低于本病例安全拔管所需趋势"},{"id":"o2","en":"the CSF protein is still elevated","zh":"CSF蛋白仍然升高"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"new bacterial meningitis","zh":"新发细菌性脑膜炎"},{"id":"o2","en":"worsening spinal cord compression","zh":"脊髓压迫加重"},{"id":"o1","en":"improving autonomic stability","zh":"自主神经稳定性改善"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"5","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"stopping rehabilitation until the client can move independently","zh":"在患者能自主活动前停止康复"},{"id":"o1","en":"DVT prevention, passive range of motion, pain control, communication support, and psychosocial care","zh":"DVT预防、被动关节活动、疼痛控制、沟通支持和心理社会护理"},{"id":"o3","en":"repeating lumbar puncture daily to follow CSF protein","zh":"每日重复腰穿以追踪CSF蛋白"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The day-5 findings fit the plateau phase: weakness has stopped worsening and autonomic and bowel findings are improving, but respiratory mechanics remain too weak for extubation. Slow recovery is expected, and nursing care must continue prevention of complications, rehabilitation support, pain management, communication support, and attention to fear and helplessness.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第5天表现符合平台期：无力不再恶化，自主神经和肠道表现改善，但呼吸力学仍太弱，不适合拔管。GBS恢复通常缓慢，护理必须继续预防并发症、支持康复、管理疼痛、提供沟通支持，并关注恐惧和无助感。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For evaluate-outcomes items, compare the trend across systems. Improvement in one domain does not equal readiness for discharge or extubation if the priority domain remains unsafe.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做评估结果题时，要跨系统比较趋势。某一方面改善并不等于可出院或拔管；若优先领域仍不安全，就不能升级为“恢复”。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2514,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_gbs_respiratory_compromise_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.53","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.53.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.53.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[343,456],"terminalOffsetsZh":[120,153],"fullStemEn":"A 32-year-old client with confirmed Guillain-Barre syndrome after recent Campylobacter enteritis has progressive quadriparesis, labile blood pressure, tachycardia, ineffective cough, unilateral absent gag reflex, FVC 1.6 L (19 mL/kg), and MIP -26 cmH2O. He speaks only a few words at a time and is diaphoretic while receiving IVIG in the ICU. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名32岁患者近期空肠弯曲杆菌肠炎后确诊格林-巴利综合征，出现进行性四肢轻瘫、血压波动、心动过速、咳嗽无效、单侧咽反射消失、FVC 1.6 L（19 mL/kg）和MIP -26 cmH2O。他在ICU接受IVIG时一次只能说几个词并出汗。请完成弓形题，选择最可能的状况、两个优先行动和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题，选择最可能的状况、两个优先行动和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"He speaks only a few words at a time and is diaphoretic while receiving IVIG in the ICU.","penultimateSentenceZh":"他在ICU接受IVIG时一次只能说几个词并出汗。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_gbs_resp_failure","en":"GBS/AIDP with impending respiratory failure","zh":"GBS/AIDP伴即将发生的呼吸衰竭"},{"id":"cond_transverse_myelitis","en":"Acute transverse myelitis","zh":"急性横贯性脊髓炎"},{"id":"cond_myasthenic_crisis","en":"Myasthenia gravis crisis","zh":"重症肌无力危象"}],"correct":"cond_gbs_resp_failure"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_give_steroids","en":"Administer high-dose IV corticosteroids to halt GBS progression","zh":"给予大剂量IV糖皮质激素以阻止GBS进展"},{"id":"act_prepare_intubation","en":"Prepare for and assist with emergent endotracheal intubation","zh":"准备并协助紧急气管插管"},{"id":"act_start_bipap","en":"Start BiPAP instead of intubation","zh":"使用BiPAP替代插管"},{"id":"act_continue_ivig","en":"Continue IVIG on schedule through airway stabilization","zh":"在气道稳定过程中按计划继续IVIG"}],"correct":["act_prepare_intubation","act_continue_ivig"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_repeat_csf","en":"Repeat CSF protein level to guide acute airway decisions","zh":"重复CSF蛋白水平以指导急性气道决策"},{"id":"param_fvc_mip","en":"Serial FVC and MIP trends","zh":"连续FVC和MIP趋势"},{"id":"param_hr_bp","en":"Heart-rate and blood-pressure variability","zh":"心率和血压变异范围"},{"id":"param_spo2_alone","en":"SpO2 alone as the primary respiratory marker","zh":"仅以SpO2作为主要呼吸指标"}],"correct":["param_fvc_mip","param_hr_bp"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The bow-tie center is GBS/AIDP with impending respiratory failure. The priority actions are airway stabilization by endotracheal intubation and uninterrupted disease-modifying IVIG. Ongoing monitoring should focus on respiratory mechanics and autonomic stability, not SpO2 alone or repeat CSF protein.","rationaleCorrectZh":"弓形题中心是GBS/AIDP伴即将发生的呼吸衰竭。优先行动是通过气管插管稳定气道，并不中断疾病修饰性IVIG。持续监测应聚焦呼吸力学和自主神经稳定性，而不是单独看SpO2或重复CSF蛋白。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-ties, identify the central threat first. Then pick actions that immediately reduce that threat and monitoring that tracks whether the threat is improving or worsening.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，先确定中心威胁。再选择能立即降低该威胁的行动，以及能追踪威胁改善或恶化的监测指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2515,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.54","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.54.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[345,531],"terminalOffsetsZh":[92,152],"fullStemEn":"Acute pulmonary embolism with right ventricular strain after total knee arthroplasty A 68-year-old man is on postoperative day 2 after an elective right total knee arthroplasty. He has obesity, a history of smoking, recent immobility, refusal of sequential compression devices overnight, and a missed morning ambulation attempt because of pain. He suddenly develops pleuritic chest pain, severe dyspnea, hypoxemia, tachycardia, diaphoresis, borderline hypotension, jugular venous distension, and a warm, swollen, tender right calf.","fullStemZh":"全膝关节置换术后急性肺栓塞伴右心室负荷增加 一名68岁男性在择期右全膝关节置换术后第2天。患者有肥胖、既往吸烟史，近期活动减少，夜间拒绝使用间歇性充气压力装置，早晨因疼痛未能下床活动。随后突然出现吸气时胸痛、严重呼吸困难、低氧血症、心动过速、出汗、血压较基线偏低、颈静脉怒张，以及右小腿发热、肿胀和压痛。","terminalSentenceEn":"He suddenly develops pleuritic chest pain, severe dyspnea, hypoxemia, tachycardia, diaphoresis, borderline hypotension, jugular venous distension, and a warm, swollen, tender right calf.","terminalSentenceZh":"随后突然出现吸气时胸痛、严重呼吸困难、低氧血症、心动过速、出汗、血压较基线偏低、颈静脉怒张，以及右小腿发热、肿胀和压痛。","penultimateSentenceEn":"He has obesity, a history of smoking, recent immobility, refusal of sequential compression devices overnight, and a missed morning ambulation attempt because of pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者有肥胖、既往吸烟史，近期活动减少，夜间拒绝使用间歇性充气压力装置，早晨因疼痛未能下床活动。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows the clinical judgment arc for a postoperative pulmonary embolism. The initial cues are the abrupt pleuritic chest pain, dyspnea, hypoxemia, tachycardia, diaphoresis, blood pressure below baseline, JVD, and unilateral calf warmth, swelling, and tenderness after recent orthopedic surgery and reduced mobility. Diagnostic data then confirm a saddle PE with RV strain: elevated troponin and BNP, respiratory alkalosis with persistent hypoxemia, S1Q3T3 and right precordial T-wave inversions, and CT evidence of RV dilation and septal bowing. Because the client remains without sustained SBP below 90 mmHg, the PE is intermediate-risk/submassive rather than massive/high-risk. Priority nursing care is to support oxygenation, avoid positions that could worsen RV overload, administer the ordered UFH bolus and infusion, monitor for bleeding after therapeutic anticoagulation, and reassess for deterioration requiring escalation. The later data show improvement because heart rate, blood pressure, oxygenation, urine output, lactate, and symptoms are trending favorably despite a small expected troponin rise.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例体现术后肺栓塞的临床判断过程。最初的关键线索是突然出现的吸气性胸痛、呼吸困难、低氧血症、心动过速、出汗、血压低于基线、颈静脉怒张，以及近期骨科手术和活动减少后出现的单侧小腿发热、肿胀和压痛。随后诊断资料证实骑跨型肺栓塞伴右心负荷增加：肌钙蛋白和BNP升高、呼吸性碱中毒伴持续低氧血症、S1Q3T3及右胸前导联T波倒置，以及CT显示右心室扩大和室间隔移位。由于没有持续性收缩压低于90 mmHg，该PE属于中危/次大面积，而不是大面积/高危。护理重点是支持氧合，避免可能加重右心室容量负荷的体位，按医嘱给予UFH推注和泵入，治疗性抗凝后监测出血，并持续评估是否恶化需要升级治疗。后续资料显示总体改善，因为心率、血压、氧合、尿量、乳酸和症状均向好转趋势发展，尽管肌钙蛋白小幅升高。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In postoperative chest pain and dyspnea questions, do not anchor on anxiety or atelectasis when the client has sudden pleuritic pain, hypoxemia, tachycardia, unilateral calf findings, and signs of right-sided strain. Use the hemodynamic status to separate intermediate-risk PE from massive/high-risk PE.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到术后胸痛和呼吸困难题时，如果同时有突然吸气性胸痛、低氧、心动过速、单侧小腿异常和右心负荷增加表现，不要锚定为焦虑或肺不张。用血流动力学状态区分中危PE和大面积/高危PE。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2516,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,120],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that are most concerning for acute pulmonary embolism with possible right ventricular compromise.","fullStemZh":"请标出最提示急性肺栓塞并可能伴右心室受累的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that are most concerning for acute pulmonary embolism with possible right ventricular compromise.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出最提示急性肺栓塞并可能伴右心室受累的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Postoperative day 2 after right total knee arthroplasty.","zh":"右全膝关节置换术后第2天。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Refused SCDs overnight and declined morning ambulation because of knee pain.","zh":"夜间拒绝SCD，早晨因膝痛拒绝下床活动。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Sudden onset of dyspnea and pleuritic right-sided chest pain.","zh":"突然出现呼吸困难和右侧吸气性胸痛。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Temperature 99 °F (37.2 °C).","zh":"体温99 °F (37.2 °C)。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Heart rate 122/min.","zh":"心率122次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Blood pressure 100/70 mmHg, below preoperative baseline 138/82 mmHg.","zh":"血压100/70 mmHg，低于术前基线138/82 mmHg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"SpO2 87% on room air.","zh":"室内空气下SpO2 87%。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Lung sounds clear bilaterally.","zh":"双肺呼吸音清。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Visible jugular venous distension at 45 degrees.","zh":"45度可见颈静脉怒张。","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"Surgical dressing clean, dry, and intact.","zh":"手术敷料清洁、干燥、完整。","selectable":true},{"id":"s11","en":"Right calf warm, erythematous, edematous, and tender with a 5-cm larger circumference than the left.","zh":"右小腿发热、发红、肿胀和压痛，周径比左侧大5 cm。","selectable":true},{"id":"s12","en":"Client is pale, diaphoretic, anxious, and speaking in short phrases.","zh":"患者面色苍白、出汗、焦虑，只能说短句。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s5","s6","s7","s9","s11","s12"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The key cue cluster is sudden pleuritic chest pain, severe dyspnea and hypoxemia, tachycardia, diaphoresis and pallor, blood pressure below baseline, JVD, and unilateral calf findings in a postoperative client with immobility and refusal of SCDs. These findings collectively point to acute PE with DVT source and possible RV strain.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键线索组合是术后患者有活动减少和拒绝SCD，同时突然出现吸气性胸痛、严重呼吸困难和低氧、心动过速、出汗和苍白、血压低于基线、颈静脉怒张以及单侧小腿异常。这些发现共同指向急性PE，可能来源于DVT，并可能已有右心负荷增加。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster cues rather than evaluating them one at a time. A postoperative client with sudden pleuritic dyspnea plus unilateral calf findings is a PE emergency until proven otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要把线索组合起来判断，而不是逐条孤立分析。术后患者突然出现吸气性胸痛/呼吸困难并伴单侧小腿异常，应先按PE急症处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2517,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,104],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"Classify how each finding contributes to the nurse's interpretation of the confirmed pulmonary embolism.","fullStemZh":"请分类每项发现如何帮助护士解释已确认的肺栓塞。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify how each finding contributes to the nurse's interpretation of the confirmed pulmonary embolism.","terminalSentenceZh":"请分类每项发现如何帮助护士解释已确认的肺栓塞。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Troponin I 0.38 ng/mL and BNP 620 pg/mL","zh":"肌钙蛋白I 0.38 ng/mL和BNP 620 pg/mL"},{"id":"r2","en":"CT-PA shows RV/LV ratio 1.4 with septal bowing","zh":"CT肺动脉造影显示RV/LV比值1.4并有室间隔移位"},{"id":"r3","en":"ECG shows S1Q3T3 and T-wave inversions in V1-V3","zh":"心电图显示S1Q3T3和V1-V3导联T波倒置"},{"id":"r4","en":"ABG shows pH 7.47, PaCO2 28, PaO2 68 on non-rebreather","zh":"非再呼吸面罩下ABG显示pH 7.47、PaCO2 28、PaO2 68"},{"id":"r5","en":"D-dimer >5,000 ng/mL FEU in a postoperative client","zh":"术后患者D-二聚体 >5,000 ng/mL FEU"},{"id":"r6","en":"Systolic blood pressure remains above 90 mmHg","zh":"收缩压仍维持在90 mmHg以上"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Distinguishes from massive/high-risk PE","zh":"用于区别大面积/高危PE"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports RV strain/intermediate-risk PE","zh":"支持右心负荷增加/中危PE"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not a severity discriminator here","zh":"此处不能区分严重程度"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The positive cardiac biomarkers, CT evidence of RV dilation and septal bowing, ECG signs of right heart strain, and hypoxemia/respiratory alkalosis support intermediate-risk PE with RV compromise. The D-dimer is elevated but expected after surgery and does not classify severity. The SBP remaining above 90 mmHg prevents classification as massive/high-risk PE at this moment.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心肌标志物阳性、CT显示右心室扩大和室间隔移位、心电图提示右心负荷增加，以及低氧/呼吸性碱中毒，均支持中危PE伴右心受累。D-二聚体升高但术后常见，不能用于区分严重程度。收缩压仍高于90 mmHg，因此此时不能归类为大面积/高危PE。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate diagnostic confirmation from severity classification. In PE, RV dysfunction and positive biomarkers without sustained hypotension point to intermediate-risk/submassive PE.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要区分“诊断确认”和“严重程度分级”。PE中，若有右心功能受累和心肌标志物阳性，但没有持续低血压，应考虑中危/次大面积PE。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2518,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"After reviewing the ECG, chest x-ray, CT-PA, and clinical findings, which condition should the nurse prioritize as the primary problem?","fullStemZh":"护士查看心电图、胸片、CT肺动脉造影和临床发现后，应优先判断哪一项是主要问题？","terminalSentenceEn":"After reviewing the ECG, chest x-ray, CT-PA, and clinical findings, which condition should the nurse prioritize as the primary problem?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士查看心电图、胸片、CT肺动脉造影和临床发现后，应优先判断哪一项是主要问题？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"ST-elevation myocardial infarction requiring immediate coronary catheterization","zh":"ST段抬高型心肌梗死，需要立即冠脉导管介入"},{"id":"C","en":"Aortic dissection requiring impulse control and surgical evaluation","zh":"主动脉夹层，需要控制心率/血压并外科评估"},{"id":"A","en":"Pulmonary embolism with right ventricular strain","zh":"肺栓塞伴右心室负荷增加"},{"id":"D","en":"Postoperative atelectasis requiring incentive spirometry and reassurance","zh":"术后肺不张，需要诱导肺量计和安慰"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The unilateral calf findings, recent orthopedic surgery with reduced prophylaxis adherence, sudden pleuritic dyspnea, hypoxemia, CT-confirmed saddle embolus, elevated RV strain biomarkers, and right-heart-strain ECG findings make pulmonary embolism with RV strain the primary condition.","rationaleCorrectZh":"单侧小腿异常、近期骨科手术且预防依从性不足、突然吸气性胸痛和呼吸困难、低氧、CT证实骑跨型栓塞、右心负荷标志物升高以及心电图右心受累表现，使肺栓塞伴右心室负荷增加成为主要问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When chest pain has multiple dangerous differentials, use the diagnostic test that directly identifies the life threat. CT-PA showing a saddle embolus outranks nonspecific troponin elevation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"胸痛有多个危险鉴别诊断时，要用能直接确认威胁生命问题的检查来判断。CT肺动脉造影显示骑跨型栓塞，比非特异性肌钙蛋白升高更有决定性。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2519,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[81,103],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,30],"fullStemEn":"Which statements best explain the appropriateness of the current treatment plan? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"以下哪些陈述最能解释当前治疗计划的适当性？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements best explain the appropriateness of the current treatment plan?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些陈述最能解释当前治疗计划的适当性？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Recent major orthopedic surgery increases the bleeding risk of systemic thrombolysis while the client remains hemodynamically stable.","zh":"近期大型骨科手术会增加全身溶栓出血风险，而患者目前血流动力学仍稳定。"},{"id":"B","en":"Protamine sulfate can reverse UFH more completely than it reverses LMWH.","zh":"鱼精蛋白对UFH的逆转作用比对LMWH更完全。"},{"id":"C","en":"Systemic thrombolysis is indicated now because a saddle embolus is large, even without sustained hypotension.","zh":"即使没有持续低血压，因骑跨型栓塞体积大，现在也应给予全身溶栓。"},{"id":"F","en":"Therapeutic anticoagulation should be withheld until the chest pain completely resolves.","zh":"应等胸痛完全缓解后再开始治疗性抗凝。"},{"id":"A","en":"UFH can be titrated quickly and has a short half-life, which is helpful if bleeding or urgent intervention occurs.","zh":"UFH可快速调整剂量且半衰期短，若发生出血或需要紧急介入会更有利。"},{"id":"E","en":"If sustained hypotension or obstructive shock develops, escalation to catheter-directed therapy or surgical embolectomy may be considered.","zh":"如果出现持续低血压或梗阻性休克，可考虑升级为导管定向治疗或外科取栓。"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"UFH is a reasonable facility-protocol choice in this high bleeding-risk postoperative context because it can be titrated, stopped quickly, and reversed. Systemic thrombolysis is not the current priority because the client is intermediate-risk/submassive rather than massive/high-risk and is only 2 days from major orthopedic surgery. If he develops sustained hypotension or obstructive shock, escalation to advanced reperfusion options may be considered.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在这种术后出血风险较高的情境中，按机构方案选择UFH是合理的，因为它可调整、可较快停止且可逆转。当前不优先全身溶栓，因为患者属于中危/次大面积PE而非大面积/高危PE，并且距大型骨科手术仅2天。如果出现持续低血压或梗阻性休克，可考虑升级至高级再灌注治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For medication choices, look for the clinical context that modifies the usual rule. Recent surgery shifts the focus to reversibility, titration, and bleeding surveillance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"药物选择题要找出会改变常规选择的临床情境。近期手术会使重点转向可逆转性、剂量可调性和出血监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2520,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[89,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[27,36],"fullStemEn":"The UFH bolus and infusion have been ordered. Which nursing actions are appropriate now? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"已医嘱给予UFH推注和持续泵入。此时哪些护理措施合适？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate now?","penultimateSentenceZh":"此时哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Maintain continuous cardiac monitoring and prepare for ICU transfer.","zh":"持续心电监护并准备转入ICU。"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the ordered UFH bolus and begin the infusion without delaying for ICU transfer.","zh":"给予医嘱的UFH推注并开始泵入，不因等待ICU转运而延误。"},{"id":"E","en":"Place the client supine or in Trendelenburg to increase venous return and improve blood pressure.","zh":"将患者置于平卧位或Trendelenburg位，以增加静脉回流并改善血压。"},{"id":"B","en":"Maintain the non-rebreather mask at 15 L/min with continuous SpO2 monitoring.","zh":"维持15 L/min非再呼吸面罩并持续监测SpO2。"},{"id":"C","en":"Keep the head of the bed elevated in high Fowler's or a semi-recumbent position.","zh":"保持高Fowler位或半卧位。"},{"id":"D","en":"Assess and document the surgical site for new bleeding or expanding hematoma after anticoagulation begins.","zh":"开始抗凝后评估并记录手术部位是否有新出血或扩大血肿。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse should start ordered therapeutic anticoagulation promptly, continue high-flow oxygen with SpO2 monitoring, keep the client upright or semi-recumbent to support ventilation and avoid worsening RV overload, monitor continuously, prepare for ICU transfer, and assess for postoperative bleeding after anticoagulation begins. These interventions are concurrent; ICU transfer preparation should not delay anticoagulation or oxygen support.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士应及时开始医嘱的治疗性抗凝，继续高流量给氧并监测SpO2，保持坐起或半卧位以支持通气并避免加重右心负荷，持续监护，准备转入ICU，并在开始抗凝后评估术后出血。这些措施可并行进行；准备转运ICU不应延误抗凝或给氧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several urgent actions are safe and concurrent, select all actions that address immediate threats: oxygenation, clot propagation, hemodynamic monitoring, and bleeding surveillance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个紧急措施可以安全并行时，选择能处理立即威胁的措施：氧合、血栓扩展、血流动力学监测和出血观察。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2521,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,72],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,16],"fullStemEn":"Complete the nurse's interpretation of the client's response to therapy.","fullStemZh":"请完成护士对患者治疗反应的判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nurse's interpretation of the client's response to therapy.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成护士对患者治疗反应的判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"At 1330, the client's overall trajectory is {{1}} because {{2}}. The slight troponin increase from 0.38 to 0.42 ng/mL should be interpreted as {{3}}, so the nurse should {{4}}.","zh":"13:30时，患者总体趋势为 {{1}}，因为 {{2}}。肌钙蛋白从0.38小幅升至0.42 ng/mL应理解为 {{3}}，因此护士应 {{4}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"ready for discharge teaching","zh":"已准备进行出院宣教"},{"id":"o2","en":"rapidly deteriorating","zh":"正在快速恶化"},{"id":"o1","en":"improving","zh":"正在改善"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"heart rate, blood pressure, oxygenation, urine output, lactate, and pain are trending in the right direction","zh":"心率、血压、氧合、尿量、乳酸和疼痛均向好转方向变化"},{"id":"o2","en":"D-dimer is elevated and confirms that anticoagulation has dissolved the clot","zh":"D-二聚体升高，证实抗凝已溶解血栓"},{"id":"o3","en":"the client no longer requires a non-rebreather mask","zh":"患者已不再需要非再呼吸面罩"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"an expected biomarker trend that does not outweigh the improving clinical status","zh":"预期的标志物变化，不能压过整体临床好转趋势"},{"id":"o2","en":"proof that systemic thrombolysis is now required","zh":"证明现在必须进行全身溶栓"},{"id":"o3","en":"evidence that the primary problem is STEMI instead of PE","zh":"提示主要问题是STEMI而不是PE"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"continue the current plan and monitor for hypotension, worsening hypoxemia, decreased level of consciousness, low urine output, and bleeding","zh":"继续当前计划，并监测低血压、低氧加重、意识水平下降、尿量减少和出血"},{"id":"o2","en":"request immediate systemic thrombolysis based only on the troponin trend","zh":"仅根据肌钙蛋白趋势要求立即全身溶栓"},{"id":"o3","en":"stop the UFH infusion because the chest pain has improved","zh":"因胸痛改善而停止UFH泵入"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The overall trajectory is improving: heart rate is lower, blood pressure is higher, SpO2 and respiratory rate are improved, pain has decreased, urine output has recovered, and lactate has fallen. A small troponin rise can occur after the initial RV strain and does not by itself indicate deterioration when bedside perfusion and oxygenation data are improving. The client still requires ICU monitoring and therapeutic anticoagulation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"总体趋势是改善：心率下降、血压上升、SpO2和呼吸频率改善、疼痛减轻、尿量恢复、乳酸下降。右心室最初受压后肌钙蛋白可能小幅继续升高；如果床旁灌注和氧合资料正在改善，单独的肌钙蛋白变化并不代表恶化。患者仍需ICU监测和治疗性抗凝。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by trend clusters, not by one isolated abnormal value. In acute PE, bedside perfusion and oxygenation trends carry more immediate weight than a small early biomarker rise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估疗效要看一组趋势，而不是单个异常值。急性PE中，床旁灌注和氧合趋势比早期单个标志物小幅升高更有即时意义。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2522,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_pe_2026_06_16_case_pulmonary_embolism_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.55","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.55.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.55.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[490,603],"terminalOffsetsZh":[172,205],"fullStemEn":"A 68-year-old man on postoperative day 2 after total knee arthroplasty has sudden pleuritic chest pain, severe dyspnea, tachycardia, hypoxemia, JVD, and a swollen tender right calf. CT-PA shows a saddle pulmonary embolus with RV/LV ratio 1.4 and septal bowing. Troponin and BNP are elevated. His systolic BP has remained above 90 mmHg after initiation of a facility UFH protocol, and over 4 hours his HR, BP, SpO2, urine output, lactate, and pain improve, although troponin rises slightly. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名68岁男性在全膝关节置换术后第2天突然出现吸气性胸痛、严重呼吸困难、心动过速、低氧、颈静脉怒张，以及右小腿肿胀压痛。CT肺动脉造影显示骑跨型肺栓塞，RV/LV比值1.4并有室间隔移位。肌钙蛋白和BNP升高。按本机构UFH方案开始治疗后，收缩压一直高于90 mmHg；4小时内HR、BP、SpO2、尿量、乳酸和疼痛均改善，但肌钙蛋白小幅升高。请完成弓形题：选择最可能的病情、两项优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成弓形题：选择最可能的病情、两项优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"His systolic BP has remained above 90 mmHg after initiation of a facility UFH protocol, and over 4 hours his HR, BP, SpO2, urine output, lactate, and pain improve, although troponin rises slightly.","penultimateSentenceZh":"按本机构UFH方案开始治疗后，收缩压一直高于90 mmHg；4小时内HR、BP、SpO2、尿量、乳酸和疼痛均改善，但肌钙蛋白小幅升高。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"condition_tension_pneumothorax","en":"Tension pneumothorax","zh":"张力性气胸"},{"id":"condition_intermediate_risk_pe","en":"Intermediate-risk/submassive pulmonary embolism","zh":"中危/次大面积肺栓塞"},{"id":"condition_stemi","en":"ST-elevation myocardial infarction","zh":"ST段抬高型心肌梗死"}],"correct":"condition_intermediate_risk_pe"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"action_icu_monitoring","en":"Maintain ICU hemodynamic monitoring with a clear escalation plan","zh":"维持ICU血流动力学监测，并明确升级处理计划"},{"id":"action_trendelenburg","en":"Place the client supine or in Trendelenburg to raise blood pressure","zh":"将患者置于平卧位或Trendelenburg位以升高血压"},{"id":"action_request_thrombolysis","en":"Request systemic thrombolysis because troponin rose slightly","zh":"因肌钙蛋白小幅升高而要求全身溶栓"},{"id":"action_continue_ufh","en":"Continue the UFH infusion and monitor aPTT per protocol","zh":"继续UFH泵入，并按方案监测aPTT"}],"correct":["action_continue_ufh","action_icu_monitoring"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"parameter_temperature","en":"Temperature 99 °F (37.2 °C)","zh":"体温99 °F (37.2 °C)"},{"id":"parameter_d_dimer","en":"Serial D-dimer level","zh":"连续D-二聚体水平"},{"id":"parameter_spo2_rr","en":"SpO2 and respiratory rate trend","zh":"SpO2和呼吸频率趋势"},{"id":"parameter_hr_bp","en":"Heart rate and blood pressure trend","zh":"心率和血压趋势"}],"correct":["parameter_hr_bp","parameter_spo2_rr"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The most likely condition is intermediate-risk/submassive PE because the client has CT-confirmed saddle PE, RV dilation, septal bowing, elevated troponin and BNP, and ECG/clinical signs of RV strain while maintaining SBP above 90 mmHg. Priority actions are to continue therapeutic UFH and provide ICU-level monitoring with escalation if sustained hypotension or shock occurs. The best monitoring parameters are HR/BP and SpO2/RR because they reflect real-time hemodynamics and oxygenation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能的病情是中危/次大面积PE，因为患者CT确认骑跨型PE，有右心室扩大、室间隔移位、肌钙蛋白和BNP升高，以及心电图/临床右心负荷增加表现，但收缩压维持在90 mmHg以上。优先措施是继续治疗性UFH，并进行ICU级监测；若出现持续低血压或休克则升级。最佳监测参数是HR/BP和SpO2/RR，因为它们反映实时血流动力学和氧合状态。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, first lock the condition using the decisive diagnostic and hemodynamic data, then choose actions and parameters that directly match the immediate threats.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做弓形题时，先用决定性诊断和血流动力学资料锁定病情，再选择直接对应立即威胁的措施和监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2523,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.56","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.56.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,344],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,98],"fullStemEn":"Acute variceal hemorrhage in decompensated alcohol-related cirrhosis A 55-year-old man with alcohol-related cirrhosis, portal hypertension, known esophageal varices, ascites, and intermittent hepatic encephalopathy presents with large-volume bright red hematemesis, hypotension, tachycardia, and evidence of impaired hepatic synthetic function.","fullStemZh":"失代偿性酒精相关肝硬化中的急性静脉曲张出血 一名55岁男性，有酒精相关肝硬化、门静脉高压、已知食管静脉曲张、腹水和间歇性肝性脑病。现因大量鲜红色呕血、低血压、心动过速以及肝脏合成功能受损表现来诊。","terminalSentenceEn":"Acute variceal hemorrhage in decompensated alcohol-related cirrhosis A 55-year-old man with alcohol-related cirrhosis, portal hypertension, known esophageal varices, ascites, and intermittent hepatic encephalopathy presents with large-volume bright red hematemesis, hypotension, tachycardia, and evidence of impaired hepatic synthetic function.","terminalSentenceZh":"现因大量鲜红色呕血、低血压、心动过速以及肝脏合成功能受损表现来诊。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":"失代偿性酒精相关肝硬化中的急性静脉曲张出血 一名55岁男性，有酒精相关肝硬化、门静脉高压、已知食管静脉曲张、腹水和间歇性肝性脑病。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case moves from recognition of presumed variceal hemorrhage, through shock-pattern analysis and variceal-specific stabilization, to post-banding surveillance and recognition of downstream complications. The correct judgment arc is to treat massive hematemesis in a cirrhotic patient with portal hypertension as variceal bleeding; support perfusion without over-transfusing; continue vasoactive therapy and antibiotic prophylaxis; prepare for definitive endoscopic banding; then monitor for rebleeding, hepatic encephalopathy, SBP, and renal deterioration. By Stage 3, stable hemoglobin and normalized lactate argue against recurrent hemorrhagic shock, while confusion with asterixis, ammonia 124 µmol/L, ascitic PMN 484 cells/µL, rising creatinine, and oliguria identify hepatic encephalopathy, SBP, and possible hepatorenal physiology as the new priorities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例的临床判断路径从识别疑似静脉曲张出血开始，经过休克模式分析和静脉曲张出血的特异性稳定措施，再进入套扎后监测和下游并发症识别。正确思路是：肝硬化合并门静脉高压患者出现大量呕血时，先按静脉曲张出血处理；支持灌注但避免过度输血；继续血管活性药物和预防性抗生素；准备内镜套扎这一关键止血措施；随后监测再出血、肝性脑病、SBP和肾功能恶化。到第3阶段，血红蛋白稳定和乳酸恢复不支持复发性失血性休克；而意识混乱伴扑翼样震颤、氨124 µmol/L、腹水PMN 484 cells/µL、肌酐升高和少尿，则提示肝性脑病、SBP以及可能的肝肾综合征相关生理成为新优先事项。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding cases, do not anchor on the first emergency after it has improved. Re-rank priorities whenever new trend data appear.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做展开式病例时，不要在初始急症改善后仍锚定在最初问题上。每当出现新的趋势资料，都要重新排序优先事项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2524,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,114],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that support the pattern of acute variceal hemorrhage in a decompensated cirrhotic patient.","fullStemZh":"请标出支持失代偿性肝硬化患者发生急性静脉曲张出血这一临床模式的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that support the pattern of acute variceal hemorrhage in a decompensated cirrhotic patient.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出支持失代偿性肝硬化患者发生急性静脉曲张出血这一临床模式的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Large-volume bright red hematemesis about 45 minutes before arrival.","zh":"到院前约45分钟出现大量鲜红色呕血。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Second smaller episode of hematemesis occurred during transport.","zh":"来院途中再次出现少量呕血。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"HR 118 beats/min.","zh":"心率118次/分。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"BP 88/54 mmHg.","zh":"血压88/54 mmHg。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Pale, diaphoretic appearance with capillary refill of 3 seconds.","zh":"面色苍白、出汗，毛细血管再充盈时间3秒。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"SpO2 96% on 2 L nasal cannula.","zh":"鼻导管2 L/min吸氧下SpO2为96%。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Clear breath sounds bilaterally.","zh":"双肺呼吸音清晰。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"Moderate-to-large ascites with fluid wave and shifting dullness.","zh":"中到大量腹水，有液波震颤和移动性浊音。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Caput medusae on the anterior abdominal wall.","zh":"腹前壁可见海蛇头样静脉曲张。","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"Spider angiomata on the upper chest.","zh":"上胸部可见蜘蛛痣。","selectable":true},{"id":"s11","en":"Scleral icterus.","zh":"巩膜黄染。","selectable":true},{"id":"s12","en":"No asterixis and coherent speech.","zh":"无扑翼样震颤，讲话连贯。","selectable":true},{"id":"s13","en":"INR 1.9.","zh":"INR 1.9。","selectable":true},{"id":"s14","en":"Platelets 72 ×10³/µL.","zh":"血小板72 ×10³/µL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s15","en":"Albumin 2.4 g/dL.","zh":"白蛋白2.4 g/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s16","en":"Glucose 102 mg/dL.","zh":"血糖102 mg/dL。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5","s8","s9","s10","s11","s13","s14","s15"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The emergency pattern is massive hematemesis with shock physiology, plus clear evidence of portal hypertension and impaired hepatic synthetic function. Normal oxygenation, clear lungs, normal glucose, and absence of asterixis are useful baselines but do not explain the acute hemorrhage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本题的紧急模式是大量呕血伴休克生理表现，同时存在门静脉高压和肝脏合成功能受损的证据。氧合尚可、双肺清晰、血糖正常以及暂时无扑翼样震颤有助于建立基线，但不能解释当前急性出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster cues instead of reacting to one lab. In cirrhosis, hematemesis plus portal-hypertension stigmata and poor hemostatic reserve points to variceal hemorrhage.","testTakingStrategyZh":"要把线索组合起来看，不要只盯着单个化验值。肝硬化患者出现呕血，再加门静脉高压体征和止血储备差，应优先想到静脉曲张出血。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2525,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,65],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,19],"fullStemEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement about the Stage 1 trend.","fullStemZh":"请补全关于第1阶段病情趋势的临床判断。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical judgment statement about the Stage 1 trend.","terminalSentenceZh":"请补全关于第1阶段病情趋势的临床判断。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The Stage 1 findings indicate {{1}} because the patient has {{2}} and {{3}} despite initial crystalloid resuscitation.","zh":"第1阶段的发现提示 {{1}}，因为患者在初步晶体液复苏后仍有 {{2}} 和 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"expected anxiety after seeing blood","zh":"看到出血后的预期焦虑反应"},{"id":"o1","en":"ongoing hemorrhagic shock with inadequate tissue perfusion","zh":"持续性失血性休克并组织灌注不足"},{"id":"o3","en":"stable recovery after the fluid bolus","zh":"补液后已稳定恢复"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"a lactate rise from 3.4 to 4.1 mmol/L","zh":"乳酸从3.4升至4.1 mmol/L"},{"id":"o2","en":"a normal glucose of 102 mg/dL","zh":"血糖102 mg/dL正常"},{"id":"o3","en":"clear bilateral breath sounds","zh":"双肺呼吸音清晰"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"only 25 mL urine output in the first hour","zh":"第1小时尿量仅25 mL"},{"id":"o3","en":"hemoglobin now above the target range","zh":"血红蛋白已高于目标范围"},{"id":"o2","en":"oxygen saturation of 97% on nasal cannula","zh":"鼻导管吸氧下SpO2为97%"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The marginal BP response, persistent tachycardia, repeat hematemesis, rising lactate, and oliguria show that perfusion remains inadequate. A hemoglobin of 7.2 g/dL in this context supports single-unit PRBC transfusion to the stated restrictive target, not liberal transfusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血压仅轻微改善、心动过速持续、再次呕血、乳酸升高以及少尿，说明灌注仍不足。在这种情况下血红蛋白7.2 g/dL支持按限制性目标输注1单位红细胞，而不是宽松输血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For shock questions, trend perfusion markers together: mental status, urine output, lactate, HR/BP response, and ongoing losses.","testTakingStrategyZh":"休克题要把灌注指标放在一起看：意识状态、尿量、乳酸、心率/血压反应以及是否仍在丢失血容量。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2526,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,127],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,34],"fullStemEn":"Which bleeding source should guide the nurse's priority hypothesis and anticipated plan of care before endoscopic confirmation?","fullStemZh":"在内镜确认前，护士应以哪一种出血来源作为优先假设并据此预期护理计划？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which bleeding source should guide the nurse's priority hypothesis and anticipated plan of care before endoscopic confirmation?","terminalSentenceZh":"在内镜确认前，护士应以哪一种出血来源作为优先假设并据此预期护理计划？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Mallory-Weiss tear from forceful retching","zh":"剧烈干呕导致的贲门黏膜撕裂"},{"id":"D","en":"Lower gastrointestinal bleeding from hemorrhoids","zh":"痔疮导致的下消化道出血"},{"id":"A","en":"Esophageal variceal hemorrhage related to portal hypertension","zh":"门静脉高压相关的食管静脉曲张出血"},{"id":"B","en":"Peptic ulcer bleeding from NSAID use","zh":"NSAID使用导致的消化性溃疡出血"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Known cirrhosis, portal hypertension, documented esophageal varices, large-volume hematemesis, ascites, caput medusae, and coagulopathy all point to variceal hemorrhage. The nurse should anticipate variceal-specific therapy while endoscopy is being arranged.","rationaleCorrectZh":"已知肝硬化、门静脉高压、既往食管静脉曲张、大量呕血、腹水、海蛇头样静脉曲张和凝血异常共同指向静脉曲张出血。安排内镜的同时，护士应预期静脉曲张出血的特异性治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the history that changes management. Prior varices plus cirrhosis turns hematemesis into a presumed variceal bleed until proven otherwise.","testTakingStrategyZh":"抓住会改变处理方向的病史。既往静脉曲张加肝硬化，使呕血在证实前应按疑似静脉曲张出血处理。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2527,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Respiratory & Infectious Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,165],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,51],"fullStemEn":"The provider orders 1 unit PRBC with a target hemoglobin of 7-8 g/dL. Which concurrent interventions should the nurse implement or anticipate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"医嘱输注1单位浓缩红细胞，目标血红蛋白7-8 g/dL。护士应执行或预期哪些同步干预？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which concurrent interventions should the nurse implement or anticipate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应执行或预期哪些同步干预？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Maintain NPO status and prepare for emergent EGD with band ligation.","zh":"维持禁食，准备急诊胃镜及套扎止血。"},{"id":"E","en":"Transfuse additional PRBCs until hemoglobin reaches 10 g/dL.","zh":"继续输注红细胞直到血红蛋白达到10 g/dL。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer ceftriaxone prophylaxis as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱给予头孢曲松预防性抗感染。"},{"id":"D","en":"Position with head of bed elevated and maintain airway readiness.","zh":"抬高床头并保持气道准备。"},{"id":"F","en":"Give fresh frozen plasma solely to normalize the INR before endoscopy.","zh":"仅为在内镜前纠正INR而输注新鲜冰冻血浆。"},{"id":"A","en":"Continue the octreotide infusion as ordered.","zh":"按医嘱继续奥曲肽静脉泵入。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Octreotide, ceftriaxone, endoscopy readiness, NPO status, and airway protection are concurrent priorities in suspected variceal hemorrhage. The case protocol sets a restrictive PRBC target; routine liberal transfusion or large-volume plasma just to normalize cirrhosis-related INR can worsen volume/portal-pressure problems and delay definitive hemostasis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"疑似静脉曲张出血时，奥曲肽、头孢曲松、内镜准备、禁食和气道保护是同步优先事项。本病例方案设定限制性红细胞输血目标；常规宽松输血或仅为纠正肝硬化相关INR而大量输注血浆，可能加重容量/门静脉压力问题并延误最终止血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When several actions are ordered for an unstable bleed, separate concurrent stabilizing actions from harmful attempts to normalize every lab value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不稳定出血题中有多项医嘱时，要区分同步稳定病情的措施和“纠正每个异常化验值”的有害做法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2528,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"For each immediate post-banding nursing action or interpretation, indicate whether it is appropriate now.","fullStemZh":"对于内镜套扎后的每项护理行动或判断，请判断当前是否适当。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each immediate post-banding nursing action or interpretation, indicate whether it is appropriate now.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于内镜套扎后的每项护理行动或判断，请判断当前是否适当。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Continue the octreotide infusion per protocol.","zh":"按方案继续奥曲肽泵入。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Monitor for true rebleeding: new hematemesis, hemodynamic decline, or falling serial hemoglobin.","zh":"监测真正再出血迹象：再次呕血、血流动力学恶化或连续血红蛋白下降。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Treat the small amount of melena alone as proof of active rebleeding.","zh":"仅凭少量黑便就认定为活动性再出血。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Stop ceftriaxone because endoscopic hemostasis was achieved.","zh":"因内镜止血成功而停止头孢曲松。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Monitor mental status, ammonia trend, urine output, and creatinine.","zh":"监测意识状态、氨水平趋势、尿量和肌酐。"},{"id":"r6","en":"Transfuse more PRBCs now because hemoglobin is 7.8 g/dL.","zh":"因血红蛋白7.8 g/dL立即继续输注红细胞。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not appropriate now","zh":"当前不适当"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate now","zh":"当前适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After banding, the hemorrhage markers are improving, but early rebleeding, infection, hepatic encephalopathy, and renal injury remain major risks. Melena alone can reflect digested earlier blood when hemoglobin and hemodynamics are stable.","rationaleCorrectZh":"套扎后出血指标改善，但早期再出血、感染、肝性脑病和肾损伤仍是主要风险。在血红蛋白和血流动力学稳定时，单独黑便可来自先前出血的消化血液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After an intervention, evaluate trajectory: what improved, what remains risky, and what finding is expected from earlier events.","testTakingStrategyZh":"干预后要评估趋势：哪些改善了、哪些仍有风险、哪些发现可由先前事件解释。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2529,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[84,106],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,31],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, which conclusions or nursing actions are supported by the current data? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段，根据当前资料支持哪些结论或护理行动？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, which conclusions or nursing actions are supported by the current data?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第3阶段，根据当前资料支持哪些结论或护理行动？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider that ascitic PMN count meets the SBP diagnostic threshold and anticipate antibiotic reassessment.","zh":"通知医护团队腹水PMN计数达到SBP诊断阈值，并预期重新评估抗生素方案。"},{"id":"A","en":"Recognize hepatic encephalopathy and administer lactulose/rifaximin as ordered.","zh":"识别肝性脑病，并按医嘱给予乳果糖/利福昔明。"},{"id":"D","en":"Continue serial neurological assessments, including orientation, level of consciousness, and asterixis.","zh":"继续连续神经系统评估，包括定向力、意识水平和扑翼样震颤。"},{"id":"E","en":"Attribute the confusion to residual procedural sedation and defer lactulose until the next routine assessment.","zh":"将意识混乱归因于操作后残余镇静，推迟乳果糖至下一次常规评估。"},{"id":"C","en":"Closely monitor urine output and creatinine because SBP with AKI raises concern for hepatorenal syndrome.","zh":"密切监测尿量和肌酐，因为SBP合并AKI提示肝肾综合征风险。"},{"id":"F","en":"Give additional PRBCs to raise hemoglobin above 8 g/dL because the patient looks worse.","zh":"因患者看起来更差而追加输注红细胞，使血红蛋白超过8 g/dL。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The hemorrhage appears controlled, but the patient has new hepatic encephalopathy, SBP by ascitic PMN count, and worsening renal function. The nursing priority shifts to treating encephalopathy, communicating SBP results, and tracking neurologic and renal trajectories.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出血似乎已控制，但患者出现新的肝性脑病、腹水PMN计数符合SBP，以及肾功能恶化。护理重点转向治疗脑病、报告SBP结果，并追踪神经和肾功能趋势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a patient worsens after the initial emergency is controlled, ask whether the new data show a complication rather than failure of the first treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"初始急症控制后患者恶化时，要判断新资料是否提示并发症，而不是简单认为第一次治疗失败。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2530,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_variceal_hemorrhage_cirrhosis_2026_06_16_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.57","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.57.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.57.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[452,573],"terminalOffsetsZh":[155,192],"fullStemEn":"A 55-year-old man with decompensated cirrhosis was admitted for acute esophageal variceal hemorrhage. Endoscopic band ligation achieved hemostasis, and his hemoglobin is stable at 7.6 g/dL with no further hematemesis. Twelve to 24 hours later, he is confused and somnolent, has asterixis, ammonia has risen to 124 µmol/L, creatinine has risen to 1.8 mg/dL with urine output 15 mL/hr, and diagnostic paracentesis shows ascitic neutrophils 484 cells/µL. Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名55岁失代偿性肝硬化患者因急性食管静脉曲张出血入院。内镜套扎已成功止血，血红蛋白稳定在7.6 g/dL且无再次呕血。12至24小时后，他出现意识混乱和嗜睡，有扑翼样震颤，氨升至124 µmol/L，肌酐升至1.8 mg/dL且尿量15 mL/hr，诊断性腹腔穿刺显示腹水中性粒细胞484 cells/µL。请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、两个优先护理行动以及两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the bow-tie by selecting the most likely condition, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成蝴蝶结题：选择最可能的状况、两个优先护理行动以及两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Twelve to 24 hours later, he is confused and somnolent, has asterixis, ammonia has risen to 124 µmol/L, creatinine has risen to 1.8 mg/dL with urine output 15 mL/hr, and diagnostic paracentesis shows ascitic neutrophils 484 cells/µL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"12至24小时后，他出现意识混乱和嗜睡，有扑翼样震颤，氨升至124 µmol/L，肌酐升至1.8 mg/dL且尿量15 mL/hr，诊断性腹腔穿刺显示腹水中性粒细胞484 cells/µL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_hypovolemia","en":"Recurrent hypovolemic shock with cerebral hypoperfusion","zh":"复发性低血容量性休克伴脑灌注不足"},{"id":"cond_he","en":"Hepatic encephalopathy precipitated by GI blood load, SBP, and AKI","zh":"由消化道血液负荷、SBP和AKI诱发的肝性脑病"},{"id":"cond_sedation","en":"Residual procedural sedation after endoscopy","zh":"内镜后残余镇静作用"}],"correct":"cond_he"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_transfuse_above8","en":"Transfuse additional PRBCs to raise hemoglobin above 8 g/dL because mental status worsened.","zh":"因意识状态恶化而追加红细胞，使血红蛋白超过8 g/dL。"},{"id":"act_lactulose_rifaximin","en":"Administer lactulose as ordered and rifaximin every 12 hours.","zh":"按医嘱给予乳果糖，并每12小时给予利福昔明。"},{"id":"act_notify_sbp","en":"Notify the provider of SBP-confirming paracentesis results and anticipate albumin/antibiotic reassessment.","zh":"将腹水结果符合SBP及时通知医护团队，并预期评估白蛋白和抗生素方案。"},{"id":"act_defer_sedation","en":"Document likely residual sedation and defer encephalopathy treatment until the next routine assessment.","zh":"记录为可能残余镇静，并推迟肝性脑病治疗至下一次常规评估。"}],"correct":["act_lactulose_rifaximin","act_notify_sbp"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_renal","en":"Urine output and serum creatinine trend","zh":"尿量和血清肌酐趋势"},{"id":"param_neuro","en":"Serial neurological assessments: level of consciousness, orientation, asterixis, ability to follow commands","zh":"连续神经系统评估：意识水平、定向力、扑翼样震颤、执行指令能力"},{"id":"param_alcohol","en":"Blood alcohol level","zh":"血液酒精浓度"},{"id":"param_lactate","en":"Lactate level as the primary marker of the current problem","zh":"将乳酸作为当前问题的主要监测指标"}],"correct":["param_neuro","param_renal"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The best synthesis is hepatic encephalopathy with SBP and renal deterioration as major precipitants and complications. The hemorrhage markers are stable, while the neurological decline, asterixis, hyperammonemia, ascitic neutrophil count above the case threshold, rising creatinine, and oliguria point to encephalopathy, infection, and hepatorenal-risk physiology.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最佳综合判断是肝性脑病，同时SBP和肾功能恶化是重要诱因和并发问题。出血指标稳定，而神经状态下降、扑翼样震颤、高氨血症、腹水中性粒细胞超过本病例阈值、肌酐上升和少尿共同指向脑病、感染和肝肾综合征风险相关生理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In a bow-tie, the correct middle condition must explain the cues and make the actions and monitoring parameters make sense together.","testTakingStrategyZh":"蝴蝶结题中，正确的中间状况必须能解释线索，并让行动和监测指标在逻辑上连成一体。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2531,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.58","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.58.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[290,412],"terminalOffsetsZh":[97,136],"fullStemEn":"Postpartum hemorrhage from uterine atony in a grand multiparous client with pregnancy-induced hypertension A 32-year-old G5P5 client is one hour postpartum after a vaginal birth of a 4.2 kg infant. She has pregnancy-induced hypertension treated with labetalol and mild intermittent asthma. She develops heavy bleeding, a boggy displaced fundus, tachycardia, and hypotension relative to her hypertensive baseline.","fullStemZh":"妊娠期高血压经产妇因子宫收缩乏力发生的产后出血 一名 32 岁 G5P5 产妇在阴道分娩 4.2 kg 新生儿后 1 小时处于产后恢复期。她有妊娠期高血压，使用拉贝洛尔治疗，并有轻度间歇性哮喘。她出现大量出血、子宫底偏移且松软、心动过速，以及相对高血压基线明显下降的血压。","terminalSentenceEn":"She develops heavy bleeding, a boggy displaced fundus, tachycardia, and hypotension relative to her hypertensive baseline.","terminalSentenceZh":"她出现大量出血、子宫底偏移且松软、心动过速，以及相对高血压基线明显下降的血压。","penultimateSentenceEn":"She has pregnancy-induced hypertension treated with labetalol and mild intermittent asthma.","penultimateSentenceZh":"她有妊娠期高血压，使用拉贝洛尔治疗，并有轻度间歇性哮喘。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows recognition, treatment, and evaluation of early postpartum hemorrhage from uterine atony. The decisive cues are heavy bleeding, QBL above the vaginal-birth PPH threshold, a boggy displaced uterus that will not maintain tone, tachycardia, hypotension relative to a hypertensive baseline, poor perfusion, and bladder distention. The intact laceration repair and later exploration narrow the source away from trauma or retained tissue. Priority care is concurrent: maintain uterine compression/massage, administer a safe uterotonic, restore volume through large-bore IV access, prepare blood, and give ordered TXA within the unit protocol. Misoprostol is the safe second-line uterotonic because methylergonovine is contraindicated by pregnancy-induced hypertension and carboprost is unsafe with asthma. Improvement is shown by a firm uterus, decreased lochia, plateaued QBL, clearer mentation, and rising BP; continued concern is shown by anemia, downward fibrinogen trend, oliguria, and persistent tachycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例呈现早期子宫收缩乏力性产后出血的识别、处理和评价。决定性线索包括大量出血、定量失血超过阴道分娩产后出血阈值、子宫底偏移且松软并不能维持张力、心动过速、相对妊娠期高血压基线明显下降的血压、灌注不良以及膀胱充盈。会阴修补处完整以及后续探查结果，使出血来源不支持创伤或胎盘残留。优先护理是并行进行的：维持子宫压迫/按摩，给予安全宫缩药，通过大口径 IV 恢复容量，准备血制品，并按病区方案给予已医嘱的氨甲环酸。米索前列醇是安全的二线宫缩药，因为妊娠期高血压禁用甲基麦角新碱，哮喘病史使卡前列素不安全。改善表现为子宫坚硬、恶露减少、定量失血停止上升、意识转清、血压回升；仍需关注的表现包括贫血、纤维蛋白原下降趋势、少尿和持续心动过速。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For postpartum hemorrhage, use the four-T framework but let uterine tone lead the first hypothesis. A boggy uterus means tone/atony until proven otherwise; management must control the source and restore perfusion at the same time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理产后出血题可使用“四个 T”框架，但第一假设要由子宫张力决定。子宫松软时优先考虑张力问题/子宫收缩乏力；处理必须同时控制出血来源并恢复灌注。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2532,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,112],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,30],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the assessment findings that require immediate follow-up for postpartum hemorrhage from uterine atony.","fullStemZh":"请标出需要立即针对子宫收缩乏力性产后出血进行处理的评估发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the assessment findings that require immediate follow-up for postpartum hemorrhage from uterine atony.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出需要立即针对子宫收缩乏力性产后出血进行处理的评估发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"seg_temp","selectable":true,"en":"Temperature 98.2 °F (36.8 °C).","zh":"体温 98.2 °F (36.8 °C)。"},{"id":"seg_hr","selectable":true,"en":"Heart rate 118 beats/min.","zh":"心率 118 次/分。"},{"id":"seg_bp","selectable":true,"en":"Blood pressure 90/62 mmHg, down from her hypertensive admission baseline of 148/94 mmHg.","zh":"血压 90/62 mmHg，低于入院时 148/94 mmHg 的妊娠期高血压基线。"},{"id":"seg_spo2","selectable":true,"en":"SpO2 97% on room air.","zh":"室内空气下 SpO2 97%。"},{"id":"seg_fundus","selectable":true,"en":"The uterus is two fingerbreadths above the umbilicus, deviated to the right, and boggy.","zh":"子宫底位于脐上两横指，向右偏移，触之松软。"},{"id":"seg_relax","selectable":true,"en":"It does not stay firm after gentle massage.","zh":"轻柔按摩后子宫不能持续变硬。"},{"id":"seg_lochia","selectable":true,"en":"Lochia is heavy with a steady dark-red flow and several small clots.","zh":"恶露量多，持续暗红色流出，并有数个小血块。"},{"id":"seg_repair","selectable":true,"en":"The repaired second-degree perineal laceration has no active bleeding and no visible hematoma.","zh":"已缝合的二度会阴裂伤无活动性出血，也未见血肿。"},{"id":"seg_bladder","selectable":true,"en":"The bladder is palpable above the symphysis pubis.","zh":"耻骨联合上方可触及膀胱。"},{"id":"seg_skin","selectable":true,"en":"Skin is cool and clammy with capillary refill of 3 seconds.","zh":"皮肤湿冷，毛细血管再充盈时间为 3 秒。"},{"id":"seg_ebl","selectable":true,"en":"Estimated blood loss is 600 mL and visibly increasing.","zh":"估计失血量为 600 mL，且肉眼可见仍在增加。"},{"id":"seg_resp","selectable":true,"en":"She denies chest pain or shortness of breath.","zh":"她否认胸痛或气短。"}],"correct":["seg_hr","seg_bp","seg_fundus","seg_relax","seg_lochia","seg_bladder","seg_skin","seg_ebl"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The key cues are a boggy displaced uterus that cannot maintain tone, heavy lochia with clots, blood loss already at 600 mL and increasing, tachycardia, hypotension relative to a hypertensive baseline, poor peripheral perfusion, and a palpable bladder that can worsen uterine displacement. Normal temperature and oxygen saturation do not define the problem, and the intact perineal repair helps narrow the source away from a laceration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"关键线索包括子宫底偏移且松软、不能维持张力，恶露量多伴血块，失血量已达 600 mL 且仍在增加，心动过速，相对于妊娠期高血压基线明显下降的血压，外周灌注差，以及可触及的膀胱充盈（可加重子宫偏移）。体温和血氧正常不能说明当前问题；会阴修补处完整有助于把出血来源从裂伤转向子宫。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In early postpartum bleeding, first connect uterine tone, lochia, blood-loss amount, and perfusion signs. Compare vital signs with the client's baseline, not just the normal range.","testTakingStrategyZh":"早期产后出血题先把子宫张力、恶露、失血量和灌注表现联系起来；生命体征要和该患者的基线比较，而不只看正常范围。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2533,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,79],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"Complete the clinical reasoning statement using the available Stage 1 findings.","fullStemZh":"根据第 1 阶段可获得的资料，完成临床推理陈述。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the clinical reasoning statement using the available Stage 1 findings.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据第 1 阶段可获得的资料，完成临床推理陈述。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The most likely cause of the hemorrhage is {{dd_condition}} because {{dd_best_evidence}}. Uterine inversion is unlikely because {{dd_inversion_ruleout}}.","zh":"最可能的出血原因是 {{dd_condition}}，因为 {{dd_best_evidence}}。子宫内翻的可能性较低，因为 {{dd_inversion_ruleout}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"dd_condition","options":[{"id":"dd_condition_inversion","en":"uterine inversion","zh":"子宫内翻"},{"id":"dd_condition_retained","en":"retained placental tissue","zh":"胎盘组织残留"},{"id":"dd_condition_atony","en":"uterine atony","zh":"子宫收缩乏力"},{"id":"dd_condition_laceration","en":"cervical or vaginal laceration","zh":"宫颈或阴道裂伤"}],"correct":"dd_condition_atony"},{"id":"dd_best_evidence","options":[{"id":"dd_evidence_boggy","en":"the boggy fundus briefly firms with massage but immediately relaxes","zh":"子宫底松软，按摩后短暂变硬但很快又松弛"},{"id":"dd_evidence_type","en":"the client is O-positive with a negative antibody screen","zh":"患者 O 型 Rh 阳性且抗体筛查阴性"},{"id":"dd_evidence_protein","en":"the urinalysis shows 1+ protein","zh":"尿检显示蛋白 1+"},{"id":"dd_evidence_repair","en":"the repaired second-degree laceration is intact","zh":"二度裂伤修补处完整"}],"correct":"dd_evidence_boggy"},{"id":"dd_inversion_ruleout","options":[{"id":"dd_ruleout_clots","en":"several small clots are present","zh":"可见数个小血块"},{"id":"dd_ruleout_fundus","en":"the fundus is palpable above the umbilicus","zh":"子宫底可在脐上触及"},{"id":"dd_ruleout_macrosomia","en":"the infant weighed 4.2 kg","zh":"新生儿体重 4.2 kg"},{"id":"dd_ruleout_oxytocin","en":"oxytocin was used during labor","zh":"产程中使用过催产素"}],"correct":"dd_ruleout_fundus"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A boggy uterus that will not maintain tone after massage identifies uterine atony as the primary mechanism. The intact laceration repair argues against a traumatic lower-tract source. Retained tissue is possible early in a PPH workup, but the placenta was inspected as complete and the defining cue is uterine relaxation. Inversion is unlikely because the fundus remains palpable in the abdomen.","rationaleCorrectZh":"按摩后不能维持张力的松软子宫指向子宫收缩乏力。会阴裂伤修补处完整，不支持下生殖道创伤性出血。胎盘残留在产后出血评估中可以考虑，但胎盘已检查完整，且决定性线索是子宫松弛。子宫底仍可在腹部触及，因此子宫内翻可能性低。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For PPH differentials, ask whether the uterus is firm or boggy. Boggy points to tone; firm with bleeding points more toward trauma or tissue.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分产后出血原因时先问子宫是坚硬还是松软。松软指向“张力”问题；子宫坚硬但仍出血则更偏向创伤或组织残留。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2534,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[41,118],"terminalOffsetsZh":[11,28],"fullStemEn":"The provider orders a second uterotonic. Which medication should the nurse administer from the available unit options?","fullStemZh":"医嘱追加第二种宫缩药。护士应从病区可用药物中给予哪一种？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse administer from the available unit options?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应从病区可用药物中给予哪一种？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider orders a second uterotonic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱追加第二种宫缩药。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"med_carboprost","en":"Administer carboprost tromethamine 250 mcg IM.","zh":"给予卡前列素氨丁三醇 250 mcg IM。"},{"id":"med_methergine","en":"Administer methylergonovine 0.2 mg IM.","zh":"给予甲基麦角新碱 0.2 mg IM。"},{"id":"med_misoprostol","en":"Administer misoprostol 800 mcg rectally.","zh":"给予米索前列醇 800 mcg 经直肠给药。"},{"id":"med_wait","en":"Hold all additional uterotonics until the repeat CBC and coagulation panel result.","zh":"在复查 CBC 和凝血功能结果出来前暂停所有追加宫缩药。"}],"correct":["med_misoprostol"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Misoprostol is the safe second-line uterotonic in this client because methylergonovine is contraindicated by pregnancy-induced hypertension and carboprost is unsafe with asthma. Current hemorrhagic hypotension does not remove the methylergonovine contraindication.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本例中米索前列醇是安全的二线宫缩药，因为妊娠期高血压禁用甲基麦角新碱，哮喘病史使卡前列素不安全。当前因失血导致的低血压并不能解除甲基麦角新碱的禁忌。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When medication choices all treat the same problem, screen each option for patient-specific contraindications before choosing the strongest drug.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当多个药物都能治疗同一问题时，先根据患者个体禁忌证筛选，而不是直接选择作用最强的药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2535,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[73,95],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,28],"fullStemEn":"Which actions should occur now as part of the coordinated team response? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"此时哪些措施应作为团队协作反应立即进行？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should occur now as part of the coordinated team response?","penultimateSentenceZh":"此时哪些措施应作为团队协作反应立即进行？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"act_crossmatch","en":"Have another team member send the type and crossmatch specimen immediately.","zh":"由另一名团队成员立即送检配血标本。"},{"id":"act_massage","en":"Maintain continuous external fundal massage or assist with bimanual compression.","zh":"持续进行外部子宫底按摩，或协助双手压迫子宫。"},{"id":"act_stop_massage","en":"Stop fundal massage so the primary nurse can draw the laboratory specimens first.","zh":"停止子宫底按摩，让责任护士先抽取化验标本。"},{"id":"act_txa","en":"Start tranexamic acid 1 g IV over 10 minutes per the PPH protocol after uterotonic administration is underway.","zh":"宫缩药给药开始后，按产后出血方案给予氨甲环酸 1 g IV，10 分钟输注。"},{"id":"act_fluids","en":"Continue rapid warmed IV fluid resuscitation through large-bore access.","zh":"通过大口径静脉通路继续快速输入温热 IV 液体复苏。"},{"id":"act_uterotonic","en":"Administer the selected second uterotonic without delay.","zh":"立即给予已选择的第二种宫缩药。"}],"correct":["act_massage","act_uterotonic","act_fluids","act_txa","act_crossmatch"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This is not a rigid ordered sequence. The team must maintain source control with massage/compression and a safe uterotonic while restoring circulating volume, starting ordered TXA within the protocol window, and preparing blood products through another team member. Lab and blood-bank tasks should not interrupt uterine compression.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这不是严格的单线顺序题。团队必须同时通过按摩/压迫和安全宫缩药控制出血来源，恢复循环容量，在方案时间窗内启动已医嘱的氨甲环酸，并由其他团队成员准备血制品。化验和血库任务不能中断子宫压迫。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a hemorrhage item lists many tasks, separate source control and resuscitation from tasks that can be assigned to helpers. Do not convert concurrent priorities into a fake sequence.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出血题列出多项任务时，先区分“止血源控制和复苏”与可交给他人完成的任务；不要把并行优先事项误当成严格顺序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2536,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,38],"fullStemEn":"Classify each Stage 3 finding as evidence of early stabilization or as a finding that still requires close monitoring/continued concern.","fullStemZh":"请将第 3 阶段每项发现分类为“早期稳定证据”或“仍需严密监测/持续关注”。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each Stage 3 finding as evidence of early stabilization or as a finding that still requires close monitoring/continued concern.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将第 3 阶段每项发现分类为“早期稳定证据”或“仍需严密监测/持续关注”。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"columns":[{"id":"improving","en":"Evidence of early stabilization","zh":"早期稳定证据"},{"id":"concern","en":"Requires continued concern/monitoring","zh":"仍需持续关注/监测"}],"rows":[{"id":"row_firm_uterus","en":"Uterus is firm and contracted at the umbilicus.","zh":"子宫坚硬收缩，位于脐水平。"},{"id":"row_moderate_lochia","en":"Lochia has decreased to moderate dark-red flow without clots.","zh":"恶露减少为中等量暗红色且无血块。"},{"id":"row_qbl_plateau","en":"Quantitative blood loss has plateaued at 1,450 mL with no new accumulation for 15 minutes.","zh":"定量失血停留在 1,450 mL，15 分钟内无新增积血。"},{"id":"row_mentation","en":"Client is alert, oriented, and no longer confused.","zh":"患者清醒、定向力正常，不再意识混乱。"},{"id":"row_bp","en":"Blood pressure has improved from 80/52 to 94/60 mmHg.","zh":"血压从 80/52 mmHg 改善至 94/60 mmHg。"},{"id":"row_hgb","en":"Hemoglobin is 7.4 g/dL after crystalloid resuscitation and transfusion has begun.","zh":"晶体液复苏后血红蛋白为 7.4 g/dL，输血已开始。"},{"id":"row_fibrinogen","en":"Fibrinogen has trended down from 410 to 280 to 240 mg/dL.","zh":"纤维蛋白原从 410 降至 280 再降至 240 mg/dL。"},{"id":"row_uop","en":"Foley output is 25 mL/hr of concentrated amber urine.","zh":"Foley 尿量为 25 mL/hr，呈浓缩琥珀色。"},{"id":"row_hr","en":"Heart rate is improved but remains 112 beats/min.","zh":"心率较前改善但仍为 112 次/分。"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"row_firm_uterus","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"row_moderate_lochia","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"row_qbl_plateau","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"row_mentation","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"row_bp","columnIds":["improving"]},{"rowId":"row_hgb","columnIds":["concern"]},{"rowId":"row_fibrinogen","columnIds":["concern"]},{"rowId":"row_uop","columnIds":["concern"]},{"rowId":"row_hr","columnIds":["concern"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case is improving because uterine tone is restored, lochia is reduced, QBL has plateaued, mentation is clear, and BP is trending up. She is not fully stable: hemoglobin remains severely low, fibrinogen is falling, urine output is below 30 mL/hr, and tachycardia persists, so transfusion and close monitoring must continue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本例出现改善，因为子宫张力恢复、恶露减少、定量失血停止上升、意识转清、血压回升。但患者尚未完全稳定：血红蛋白仍很低，纤维蛋白原继续下降，尿量低于 30 mL/hr，心动过速持续，因此必须继续输血和严密监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In evaluation items, separate source control from systemic recovery. A firm uterus tells you bleeding is controlled; urine output, HR, hemoglobin, and fibrinogen tell you whether shock and coagulopathy are resolving.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价类题目要把“出血来源控制”与“全身恢复”分开看。子宫坚硬说明出血受控；尿量、心率、血红蛋白和纤维蛋白原反映休克和凝血状态是否恢复。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2537,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.58.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,144],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,33],"fullStemEn":"Which findings would signal the need to anticipate escalation to intrauterine balloon tamponade or surgical intervention? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"哪些发现提示需要预期升级至宫腔球囊填塞或手术干预？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings would signal the need to anticipate escalation to intrauterine balloon tamponade or surgical intervention?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些发现提示需要预期升级至宫腔球囊填塞或手术干预？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"esc_qbl_rising","en":"Quantitative blood loss resumes climbing despite uterotonics and compression.","zh":"尽管已使用宫缩药和压迫，定量失血仍继续上升。"},{"id":"esc_uop_only","en":"Urine output remains 25 mL/hr but bleeding remains controlled.","zh":"尿量仍为 25 mL/hr，但出血保持受控。"},{"id":"esc_boggy_again","en":"The uterus becomes boggy again with renewed heavy lochia.","zh":"子宫再次变松软，并重新出现大量恶露。"},{"id":"esc_fibrinogen_low","en":"Fibrinogen falls below 200 mg/dL with ongoing bleeding risk.","zh":"纤维蛋白原降至 200 mg/dL 以下，并存在持续出血风险。"},{"id":"esc_hgb_only","en":"Hemoglobin is 7.4 g/dL while the uterus is firm and QBL is plateaued.","zh":"子宫坚硬且定量失血停止上升时，血红蛋白为 7.4 g/dL。"},{"id":"esc_hr_improved","en":"Heart rate improves from 132 to 112 beats/min.","zh":"心率从 132 次/分改善至 112 次/分。"}],"correct":["esc_boggy_again","esc_qbl_rising","esc_fibrinogen_low"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Escalation is driven by loss of source control or evolving coagulopathy: recurrent bogginess with heavy bleeding, QBL that rises despite uterotonics and compression, or fibrinogen falling below the critical threshold. Low hemoglobin, oliguria, or persistent tachycardia require treatment and monitoring, but when bleeding is controlled they do not by themselves mandate surgical escalation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"升级处理主要由出血来源失控或凝血障碍进展驱动：子宫再次松软并大量出血、在宫缩药和压迫后定量失血仍上升，或纤维蛋白原低于临界值。低血红蛋白、少尿或持续心动过速需要治疗和监测；但在出血受控时，它们本身不必然要求手术升级。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not treat every abnormal lab or vital sign as a surgical trigger. Escalation follows uncontrolled bleeding, recurrent atony, or coagulopathy crossing a critical threshold.","testTakingStrategyZh":"不要把每个异常化验或生命体征都当作手术触发点。升级处理通常取决于出血失控、子宫收缩乏力复发，或凝血指标跨过关键阈值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2538,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_pph_2026_06_16_case_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.59","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Maternal-Newborn Care & Teaching","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.59.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.59.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[542,628],"terminalOffsetsZh":[186,213],"fullStemEn":"A 32-year-old G5P5 client is 90 minutes postpartum after vaginal birth of a 4.2 kg infant. She has pregnancy-induced hypertension treated with labetalol and mild intermittent asthma. She has persistent heavy bleeding despite oxytocin and fundal massage. QBL is 1,200 mL, HR 132, BP 80/52, and she is confused and pale. The uterus is intermittently boggy and relaxes within seconds after massage. Bedside exploration shows no retained placental fragments and no cervical or vaginal lacerations beyond the repaired second-degree perineal tear. Select the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"一名 32 岁 G5P5 产妇阴道分娩 4.2 kg 新生儿后 90 分钟。她有妊娠期高血压，使用拉贝洛尔治疗，并有轻度间歇性哮喘。尽管已使用催产素和子宫底按摩，她仍持续大量出血。定量失血 1,200 mL，HR 132，BP 80/52，患者意识混乱、面色苍白。子宫间歇性松软，按摩后数秒内又松弛。床旁探查未见胎盘碎片残留，也无宫颈或阴道裂伤，只有已修补的二度会阴裂伤。请选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的情况、两个优先措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Bedside exploration shows no retained placental fragments and no cervical or vaginal lacerations beyond the repaired second-degree perineal tear.","penultimateSentenceZh":"床旁探查未见胎盘碎片残留，也无宫颈或阴道裂伤，只有已修补的二度会阴裂伤。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_cond_coagulopathy","en":"Primary obstetric coagulopathy","zh":"原发性产科凝血障碍"},{"id":"bt_cond_atony","en":"Postpartum hemorrhage due to uterine atony","zh":"子宫收缩乏力导致的产后出血"},{"id":"bt_cond_laceration","en":"Cervical or vaginal laceration","zh":"宫颈或阴道裂伤"}],"correct":"bt_cond_atony"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_act_methergine","en":"Administer methylergonovine 0.2 mg IM","zh":"给予甲基麦角新碱 0.2 mg IM"},{"id":"bt_act_compression","en":"Maintain continuous uterine massage/compression","zh":"持续进行子宫按摩/压迫"},{"id":"bt_act_stop_massage","en":"Stop fundal massage to draw labs and document","zh":"停止子宫底按摩以抽血并记录"},{"id":"bt_act_misoprostol","en":"Administer misoprostol 800 mcg rectally","zh":"给予米索前列醇 800 mcg 经直肠给药"}],"correct":["bt_act_compression","bt_act_misoprostol"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"bt_par_qbl","en":"Quantitative blood loss trend","zh":"定量失血趋势"},{"id":"bt_par_apgar","en":"Neonatal Apgar scores","zh":"新生儿 Apgar 评分"},{"id":"bt_par_tone","en":"Uterine tone and fundal firmness","zh":"子宫张力和子宫底坚硬度"},{"id":"bt_par_creatinine","en":"Serum creatinine as the immediate trajectory marker","zh":"将血清肌酐作为即时病情趋势指标"}],"correct":["bt_par_tone","bt_par_qbl"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Persistent bleeding with a boggy uterus that will not sustain tone after massage identifies uterine atony. Exploration has ruled out retained fragments and unrepaired lacerations, and the coagulation profile has not made coagulopathy the primary driver. Priority actions are continuous uterine compression and a safe uterotonic; misoprostol avoids the client's hypertension and asthma contraindications. The most immediate response parameters are uterine tone and measured blood-loss trend.","rationaleCorrectZh":"持续出血并伴有按摩后不能维持张力的松软子宫，指向子宫收缩乏力。探查已排除胎盘碎片残留和未修补裂伤，凝血资料也不支持凝血障碍为主要驱动因素。优先措施是持续子宫压迫和安全宫缩药；米索前列醇可避开该患者高血压和哮喘相关禁忌。最直接的反应监测参数是子宫张力和定量失血趋势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bowtie items, lock the condition to the most decisive cue first. Here the decisive cue is uterine tone; then choose actions and monitoring that directly control and track that condition.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bowtie 题时，先用最决定性的线索锁定病情。本题决定性线索是子宫张力；随后选择能直接控制并追踪该病情的措施和监测项目。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2539,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.60","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.60.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[320,527],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,141],"fullStemEn":"Celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis presenting as chronic malabsorption A 28-year-old woman is evaluated for six months of steatorrhea, bloating, weight loss, fatigue, aphthous ulcers, microcytic anemia, low calcium, low albumin, and an intensely pruritic papulovesicular rash on the extensor elbows and knees. The unfolding course confirms celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis, identifies hidden gluten exposure, and evaluates response to strict gluten-free diet, supplementation, and dapsone symptom control.","fullStemZh":"以慢性吸收不良表现的乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎 一名28岁女性因6个月脂肪泻、腹胀、体重下降、疲乏、阿弗他溃疡、小细胞性贫血、低钙、低白蛋白，以及肘膝伸侧剧痒丘疹水疱样皮疹就诊。病例展开后确认乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎，识别隐匿麸质暴露，并评估严格无麸质饮食、营养补充和氨苯砜对症控制后的反应。","terminalSentenceEn":"The unfolding course confirms celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis, identifies hidden gluten exposure, and evaluates response to strict gluten-free diet, supplementation, and dapsone symptom control.","terminalSentenceZh":"病例展开后确认乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎，识别隐匿麸质暴露，并评估严格无麸质饮食、营养补充和氨苯砜对症控制后的反应。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis presenting as chronic malabsorption A 28-year-old woman is evaluated for six months of steatorrhea, bloating, weight loss, fatigue, aphthous ulcers, microcytic anemia, low calcium, low albumin, and an intensely pruritic papulovesicular rash on the extensor elbows and knees.","penultimateSentenceZh":"以慢性吸收不良表现的乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎 一名28岁女性因6个月脂肪泻、腹胀、体重下降、疲乏、阿弗他溃疡、小细胞性贫血、低钙、低白蛋白，以及肘膝伸侧剧痒丘疹水疱样皮疹就诊。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows the clinical judgment arc for celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis: recognize the malabsorption-DH cue cluster, confirm celiac disease with interpretable tTG-IgA and duodenal histology, distinguish it from IBD/IBS/contact dermatitis, correct hidden gluten exposures and deficiencies, teach dapsone safety as symptom control rather than definitive treatment, and evaluate improvement through symptoms, nutritional labs, and falling serology while addressing bone-health risk.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例呈现乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎的临床判断路径：识别吸收不良-疱疹样皮炎线索群；用可解释的tTG-IgA和十二指肠组织学确认乳糜泻；与IBD、IBS、接触性皮炎鉴别；纠正隐匿麸质暴露和营养缺乏；教育氨苯砜是对症控制而非根本治疗，并强调安全监测；最后通过症状、营养实验室指标和下降的血清学评估改善，同时处理骨健康风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For unfolding chronic-disease cases, keep the timeline straight: diagnosis, adherence barriers, medication safety, and outcome evaluation each become answerable at different stages.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做展开式慢性病病例时，要理清时间线：诊断、依从性障碍、用药安全和疗效评价分别在不同阶段才可回答。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2540,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"highlight","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,99],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Highlight the findings that form the celiac malabsorption and dermatitis herpetiformis cue cluster.","fullStemZh":"请标出构成乳糜泻吸收不良和疱疹样皮炎线索群的发现。","terminalSentenceEn":"Highlight the findings that form the celiac malabsorption and dermatitis herpetiformis cue cluster.","terminalSentenceZh":"请标出构成乳糜泻吸收不良和疱疹样皮炎线索群的发现。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"highlight","highlight":{"segments":[{"id":"s1","en":"Six months of foul-smelling, pale, bulky stools that are difficult to flush.","zh":"6个月来反复出现恶臭、灰白、量多且难以冲走的大便。","selectable":true},{"id":"s2","en":"Unintentional 10-lb weight loss despite unchanged appetite.","zh":"食欲未变但非故意体重下降10磅。","selectable":true},{"id":"s3","en":"Abdominal bloating and cramping are worse after meals.","zh":"餐后腹胀和腹部绞痛加重。","selectable":true},{"id":"s4","en":"Two small aphthous ulcers are present on the buccal mucosa.","zh":"颊黏膜可见两个小的阿弗他溃疡。","selectable":true},{"id":"s5","en":"Hemoglobin is 10.4 g/dL with MCV 74 fL, pale conjunctivae, and koilonychia.","zh":"血红蛋白10.4 g/dL，MCV 74 fL，并有结膜苍白和匙状甲。","selectable":true},{"id":"s6","en":"Calcium is 7.6 mg/dL and albumin is 3.3 g/dL.","zh":"钙7.6 mg/dL，白蛋白3.3 g/dL。","selectable":true},{"id":"s7","en":"Clusters of intensely pruritic papulovesicular lesions are symmetric on the extensor elbows and knees.","zh":"双侧肘部和膝部伸侧对称分布成簇、剧痒的丘疹水疱样皮损。","selectable":true},{"id":"s8","en":"ESR and CRP are within normal limits.","zh":"ESR和CRP在正常范围内。","selectable":true},{"id":"s9","en":"Stool occult blood is negative.","zh":"粪便隐血阴性。","selectable":true},{"id":"s10","en":"No fever, bloody stool, recent travel, or joint swelling is reported.","zh":"未报告发热、血便、近期旅行或关节肿胀。","selectable":true}],"correct":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5","s6","s7"]}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Steatorrhea, weight loss, postprandial bloating, aphthous ulcers, iron-deficiency-pattern anemia, hypocalcemia/hypoalbuminemia, and a symmetric pruritic papulovesicular extensor-surface rash cluster around proximal small-bowel malabsorption with dermatitis herpetiformis. Normal inflammatory markers and negative occult blood help move inflammatory bowel disease or hemorrhagic causes lower on the differential.","rationaleCorrectZh":"脂肪泻、体重下降、餐后腹胀、阿弗他溃疡、缺铁模式贫血、低钙/低白蛋白，以及伸侧对称分布的剧痒丘疹水疱样皮疹，共同指向近端小肠吸收不良合并疱疹样皮炎。炎症指标正常、隐血阴性，有助于降低炎症性肠病或出血性病因的可能性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster objective findings by body system and pathophysiology. A skin finding can be the decisive cue when it has a disease-specific pattern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"按系统和病理生理把客观发现归类。皮肤表现若具有疾病特异性分布，可能成为关键线索。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2541,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,87],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"For each Stage 1 result, select the interpretation that best fits the clinical picture.","fullStemZh":"针对第1阶段的每项结果，选择最符合临床图像的解释。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each Stage 1 result, select the interpretation that best fits the clinical picture.","terminalSentenceZh":"针对第1阶段的每项结果，选择最符合临床图像的解释。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"tTG-IgA 128 U/mL with total IgA 245 mg/dL","zh":"tTG-IgA 128 U/mL，且总IgA 245 mg/dL"},{"id":"r2","en":"Duodenal biopsy: villous atrophy, crypt hyperplasia, increased intraepithelial lymphocytes","zh":"十二指肠活检：绒毛萎缩、隐窝增生、上皮内淋巴细胞增多"},{"id":"r3","en":"Iron 28 µg/dL, ferritin 8 ng/mL, MCV 74 fL","zh":"铁28 µg/dL、铁蛋白8 ng/mL、MCV 74 fL"},{"id":"r4","en":"Vitamin D 14 ng/mL, low calcium, PTH 78 pg/mL","zh":"维生素D 14 ng/mL、低钙、PTH 78 pg/mL"},{"id":"r5","en":"Vitamin B12 280 pg/mL","zh":"维生素B12 280 pg/mL"},{"id":"r6","en":"Normal ESR/CRP and negative stool occult blood","zh":"ESR/CRP正常且粪便隐血阴性"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Confirms or supports celiac disease","zh":"确认或支持乳糜泻"},{"id":"c2","en":"Shows malabsorption-related deficiency","zh":"显示吸收不良相关缺乏"},{"id":"c3","en":"Expected/sparing pattern or counter-cue","zh":"预期/相对保留模式或反向线索"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Stage 1 confirms celiac disease by pairing markedly positive tTG-IgA with normal total IgA and characteristic duodenal histology. The iron/folate/vitamin D/calcium pattern reflects proximal small-bowel malabsorption. B12 is normal in this case and is not the main proximal-malabsorption signal, while normal ESR/CRP and negative occult blood are counter-cues against active IBD or bleeding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第1阶段通过显著升高的tTG-IgA、正常总IgA和典型十二指肠组织学结果确认乳糜泻。铁/叶酸/维生素D/钙的异常反映近端小肠吸收不良。本病例B12正常，并非主要的近端吸收不良信号；ESR/CRP正常和隐血阴性则是反向线索，不支持活动性炎症性肠病或出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Before interpreting a celiac serology result, check whether total IgA makes the IgA-based test valid. Then map deficiencies to where nutrients are absorbed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"解读乳糜泻血清学前，先确认总IgA是否让IgA类检测有效；再把营养缺乏与吸收部位对应起来。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2542,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,75],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,24],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which diagnosis best explains the complete pattern of findings?","fullStemZh":"在第1阶段，哪项诊断最能解释所有发现的整体模式？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which diagnosis best explains the complete pattern of findings?","terminalSentenceZh":"在第1阶段，哪项诊断最能解释所有发现的整体模式？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Crohn disease with extraintestinal skin manifestations","zh":"克罗恩病伴肠外皮肤表现"},{"id":"C","en":"Irritable bowel syndrome with eczema","zh":"肠易激综合征伴湿疹"},{"id":"D","en":"Contact dermatitis with unrelated dietary intolerance","zh":"接触性皮炎伴无关的饮食不耐受"},{"id":"A","en":"Celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis","zh":"乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The markedly elevated tTG-IgA with normal total IgA, Marsh 3a duodenal biopsy, steatorrhea, proximal malabsorption deficiencies, and classic extensor papulovesicular rash point to celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis. Perilesional skin biopsy is used to confirm the skin manifestation; the duodenal biopsy confirms intestinal celiac disease.","rationaleCorrectZh":"显著升高的tTG-IgA且总IgA正常、Marsh 3a十二指肠活检、脂肪泻、近端吸收不良缺乏和典型伸侧丘疹水疱样皮疹，共同指向乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎。皮损周围皮肤活检用于确认皮肤表现；十二指肠活检确认肠道乳糜泻。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize the diagnosis that explains the most objective data with the fewest unrelated assumptions.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先选择能用最少无关假设解释最多客观数据的诊断。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2543,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[74,96],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,26],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which nursing actions should be included in the plan of care? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在第2阶段，护理计划应包括哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which nursing actions should be included in the plan of care?","penultimateSentenceZh":"在第2阶段，护理计划应包括哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Advise stopping dapsone now because the gluten-free diet should immediately clear the rash.","zh":"建议立即停用氨苯砜，因为无麸质饮食应立刻清除皮疹。"},{"id":"A","en":"Teach the patient that soy sauce containing wheat and standard communion wafers are ongoing gluten exposures.","zh":"教育患者含小麦的酱油和普通圣餐饼仍属于持续麸质暴露。"},{"id":"E","en":"Review cross-contamination prevention and ask the pharmacist to verify medications and supplements for gluten-containing inactive ingredients.","zh":"复习防止交叉污染的方法，并请药师核查药物和补充剂是否含有麸质相关辅料。"},{"id":"C","en":"Reinforce folate supplementation because the folate level is low and red blood cell production must recover.","zh":"强化叶酸补充，因为叶酸水平低且红细胞生成需要恢复。"},{"id":"B","en":"Explain that dapsone can relieve dermatitis herpetiformis symptoms but does not treat intestinal villous injury.","zh":"说明氨苯砜可缓解疱疹样皮炎症状，但不能治疗肠道绒毛损伤。"},{"id":"D","en":"Tell the patient that partial GI improvement means small weekly gluten exposures are acceptable.","zh":"告诉患者胃肠症状部分改善说明每周少量麸质暴露可以接受。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The incomplete response is explained by ongoing hidden gluten exposure and incomplete supplement adherence. The nurse should target the identified gluten sources, reinforce strict lifelong avoidance and cross-contamination prevention, explain dapsone's symptomatic role, and support correction of documented deficiencies.","rationaleCorrectZh":"反应不完全可由隐匿麸质暴露和补充剂依从性不足解释。护士应针对已发现的麸质来源进行教育，强化终身严格避免和防止交叉污染，说明氨苯砜的对症作用，并支持纠正文档记录的营养缺乏。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a chronic disease is improving only partially, look first for adherence barriers and hidden exposures before assuming treatment failure.","testTakingStrategyZh":"慢性病仅部分改善时，先寻找依从性障碍和隐匿暴露，再考虑治疗失败。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2544,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,82],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Classify each teaching statement as appropriate or inappropriate for this patient.","fullStemZh":"判断每项教育内容对该患者是否适当。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each teaching statement as appropriate or inappropriate for this patient.","terminalSentenceZh":"判断每项教育内容对该患者是否适当。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Use only oats labeled gluten-free; introduce them cautiously once the diet is stable.","zh":"只使用标明无麸质的燕麦；饮食稳定后谨慎引入。"},{"id":"r2","en":"All oats must be permanently avoided by every person with celiac disease.","zh":"所有乳糜泻患者都必须永久避免所有燕麦。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The rash may take much longer than GI symptoms to resolve, so dapsone may be used while the diet takes effect.","zh":"皮疹缓解可能比胃肠症状慢得多，因此在饮食起效期间可使用氨苯砜。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Because stools are improving, folate is no longer necessary.","zh":"因为大便在改善，所以不再需要叶酸。"},{"id":"r5","en":"Report cyanosis, shortness of breath, jaundice, fever, sore throat, severe fatigue, or widespread rash while taking dapsone.","zh":"服用氨苯砜期间，如出现发绀、气短、黄疸、发热、咽痛、严重疲乏或广泛皮疹，应报告。"},{"id":"r6","en":"The nurse should stress scheduled blood monitoring early in dapsone therapy.","zh":"护士应强调氨苯砜治疗早期按计划进行血液监测。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate teaching","zh":"不适当教育"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate teaching","zh":"适当教育"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Teaching should be practical and individualized: certified gluten-free oats may be acceptable for many patients, dermatitis herpetiformis often lags behind GI improvement, documented folate deficiency still requires treatment, and dapsone requires toxicity teaching plus monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"教育应实际且个体化：认证无麸质燕麦对许多患者可能可接受；疱疹样皮炎常滞后于胃肠症状改善；已记录的叶酸缺乏仍需治疗；氨苯砜需要毒性症状教育和监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For teaching items, avoid absolute words when the real teaching is conditional, practical, and safety-focused.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做健康教育题时，若真实教育是有条件、实际且以安全为核心，就要避免绝对化说法。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2545,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.60.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,58],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,17],"fullStemEn":"Complete the evaluation of the patient's Stage 3 response.","fullStemZh":"完成对患者第3阶段治疗反应的评价。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the evaluation of the patient's Stage 3 response.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成对患者第3阶段治疗反应的评价。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The patient's overall trajectory indicates {{1}} because symptoms and nutritional markers have improved. The tTG-IgA trend should be interpreted as {{2}}. The DEXA scan is ordered because prior vitamin D deficiency, hypocalcemia, and secondary hyperparathyroidism created risk for {{3}}.","zh":"患者的总体趋势提示 {{1}}，因为症状和营养指标均已改善。tTG-IgA趋势应解释为 {{2}}。安排DEXA检查是因为既往维生素D缺乏、低钙和继发性甲状旁腺功能亢进增加了 {{3}} 的风险。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"new inflammatory bowel disease","zh":"新的炎症性肠病"},{"id":"o2","en":"treatment failure requiring immediate repeat biopsy","zh":"治疗失败，需要立即重复活检"},{"id":"o1","en":"successful response to the gluten-free diet","zh":"对无麸质饮食反应成功"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"proof that she continues to ingest gluten intentionally","zh":"证明她仍在故意摄入麸质"},{"id":"o3","en":"a result that should be ignored once symptoms improve","zh":"症状改善后可忽略的结果"},{"id":"o1","en":"an expected decline that still needs continued follow-up toward normalization","zh":"符合预期的下降，但仍需继续随访至趋于正常"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"reduced bone mineral density","zh":"骨密度降低"},{"id":"o2","en":"terminal ileal B12 malabsorption","zh":"末端回肠B12吸收不良"},{"id":"o3","en":"acute gastrointestinal bleeding","zh":"急性胃肠道出血"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At four months, formed stools, resolved bloating, weight gain, cleared rash, improved energy, normalized hemoglobin/MCV, improved ferritin, folate, vitamin D, calcium, PTH, albumin, and a falling tTG-IgA together indicate response. A tTG-IgA that is still above reference but much lower should prompt continued monitoring and adherence review, not automatic treatment-failure labeling. DEXA addresses bone risk from the earlier calcium/vitamin D/PTH abnormalities.","rationaleCorrectZh":"4个月时，大便成形、腹胀消失、体重增加、皮疹清除、精力改善、血红蛋白/MCV正常化，以及铁蛋白、叶酸、维生素D、钙、PTH、白蛋白改善，并且tTG-IgA下降，共同提示治疗有效。tTG-IgA仍高于参考范围但明显下降，应继续监测并评估依从性，而不是自动判定治疗失败。DEXA用于评估早期钙/维生素D/PTH异常带来的骨风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Evaluate outcomes by integrating symptoms, objective labs, and expected timelines. Do not overreact to one abnormal value when the whole trend is improving.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评价疗效时要整合症状、客观实验室指标和预期时间线。整体趋势改善时，不要因单个异常值过度反应。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2546,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_r1_regen_case_celiac_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.61","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.61.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.61.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[438,532],"terminalOffsetsZh":[146,175],"fullStemEn":"Stage 3 summary: A 28-year-old woman with prior steatorrhea, weight loss, iron/folate/vitamin D/calcium deficiencies, positive tTG-IgA with normal total IgA, Marsh 3a duodenal biopsy, and skin biopsy-confirmed dermatitis herpetiformis has completed three months of strict gluten-free diet after eliminating hidden gluten. Her GI symptoms and rash have resolved, nutritional labs have improved, and tTG-IgA has fallen from 128 to 38 U/mL. Select the most likely condition, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"第3阶段摘要：一名28岁女性曾有脂肪泻、体重下降、铁/叶酸/维生素D/钙缺乏，tTG-IgA阳性且总IgA正常，十二指肠活检Marsh 3a，皮肤活检确认疱疹样皮炎。消除隐匿麸质后，她已严格无麸质饮食3个月。胃肠症状和皮疹已缓解，营养实验室指标改善，tTG-IgA从128降至38 U/mL。请选择最可能的疾病、两项优先护理措施和两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the most likely condition, two priority nursing actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的疾病、两项优先护理措施和两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Her GI symptoms and rash have resolved, nutritional labs have improved, and tTG-IgA has fallen from 128 to 38 U/mL.","penultimateSentenceZh":"胃肠症状和皮疹已缓解，营养实验室指标改善，tTG-IgA从128降至38 U/mL。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_celiac_dh","en":"Celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis","zh":"乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎"},{"id":"cond_crohn","en":"Crohn disease","zh":"克罗恩病"},{"id":"cond_ibs","en":"Irritable bowel syndrome","zh":"肠易激综合征"}],"correct":"cond_celiac_dh"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_gfd","en":"Reinforce strict lifelong gluten-free adherence, including hidden sources and cross-contamination prevention","zh":"强化终身严格无麸质依从性，包括隐匿来源和防止交叉污染"},{"id":"act_dexa","en":"Coordinate the DEXA scan and explain the bone-health rationale","zh":"协调DEXA检查并解释骨健康原因"},{"id":"act_biopsy_now","en":"Label the falling but elevated tTG-IgA as treatment failure and recommend immediate repeat duodenal biopsy","zh":"将下降但仍升高的tTG-IgA判定为治疗失败，并建议立即重复十二指肠活检"},{"id":"act_stop_supp","en":"Stop nutritional supplements because the latest values improved into or near the reference range","zh":"因最新指标已改善至正常或接近正常而停止营养补充剂"}],"correct":["act_gfd","act_dexa"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_esr_crp","en":"ESR and CRP","zh":"ESR和CRP"},{"id":"param_b12","en":"Vitamin B12 level","zh":"维生素B12水平"},{"id":"param_hgb_ferritin","en":"Hemoglobin and ferritin","zh":"血红蛋白和铁蛋白"},{"id":"param_ttg","en":"Serial tTG-IgA levels","zh":"连续tTG-IgA水平"}],"correct":["param_ttg","param_hgb_ferritin"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is celiac disease with dermatitis herpetiformis because the serology is interpretable and markedly positive, the duodenal biopsy shows characteristic celiac histology, the skin biopsy confirms DH, and the patient improves after strict gluten avoidance. Priority nursing actions are long-term diet adherence support and DEXA coordination because gluten avoidance is definitive therapy and prior calcium/vitamin D/PTH abnormalities create bone-health risk. Monitoring tTG-IgA plus hemoglobin/ferritin tracks serologic response and recovery of iron-deficiency anemia/iron stores.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能疾病是乳糜泻合并疱疹样皮炎，因为血清学可解释且显著阳性，十二指肠活检显示乳糜泻特征性组织学，皮肤活检确认疱疹样皮炎，并且严格避免麸质后患者改善。优先护理措施是支持长期饮食依从性和协调DEXA，因为避免麸质是根本治疗，且既往钙/维生素D/PTH异常造成骨健康风险。监测tTG-IgA以及血红蛋白/铁蛋白可追踪血清学反应和缺铁性贫血/铁储备恢复。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In a bowtie item, link the center diagnosis to the strongest objective cues, then choose actions and monitoring parameters that directly manage the remaining risks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做bowtie题时，将中心诊断与最强客观线索相连，再选择直接处理剩余风险的措施和监测参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2547,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.62","itemType":"case_study","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.62.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,356],"terminalOffsetsZh":[78,119],"fullStemEn":"Acute ischemic stroke with tPA eligibility evaluation in a patient on warfarin A 68-year-old man with atrial fibrillation on warfarin presents 45 minutes after last known well with sudden aphasia, right-sided weakness, and left gaze preference. The case follows alteplase eligibility screening, thrombectomy preparation, and post-reperfusion deterioration.","fullStemZh":"服用华法林患者的急性缺血性卒中与 tPA 适用性评估 一名 68 岁男性有房颤并长期服用华法林，最后正常后 45 分钟出现突发失语、右侧无力和向左凝视偏斜。本病例追踪 alteplase 适用性筛查、血栓取出术准备，以及再灌注后病情恶化。","terminalSentenceEn":"The case follows alteplase eligibility screening, thrombectomy preparation, and post-reperfusion deterioration.","terminalSentenceZh":"本病例追踪 alteplase 适用性筛查、血栓取出术准备，以及再灌注后病情恶化。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Acute ischemic stroke with tPA eligibility evaluation in a patient on warfarin A 68-year-old man with atrial fibrillation on warfarin presents 45 minutes after last known well with sudden aphasia, right-sided weakness, and left gaze preference.","penultimateSentenceZh":"服用华法林患者的急性缺血性卒中与 tPA 适用性评估 一名 68 岁男性有房颤并长期服用华法林，最后正常后 45 分钟出现突发失语、右侧无力和向左凝视偏斜。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The clinical arc is acute left MCA ischemic stroke in a client with atrial fibrillation and warfarin exposure. The initial nurse priorities are to recognize cortical stroke cues, use the current stat INR rather than a historical clinic INR when applying the facility alteplase protocol, and support rapid pivot to CTA and thrombectomy evaluation when IV alteplase is excluded. Before thrombectomy, nursing care focuses on ordered titratable BP control, NPO status, IV access, cardiac monitoring, documentation, and proxy consent. After successful reperfusion, sudden decline from an improving neurologic baseline with new ipsilateral pupil dilation is treated as intracranial hemorrhage until proven otherwise; the priority response is immediate team notification, emergent CT, airway readiness, BP control per order, and serial neurologic assessment. Once hemorrhage is confirmed, the nurse evaluates stabilization primarily through GCS/pupils/motor response and systolic BP response while supporting ordered reversal and neurosurgical management.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例主线是房颤且使用 warfarin 的患者发生急性左侧 MCA 缺血性卒中。初始护理重点是识别皮质性卒中线索，按机构 alteplase 流程使用当前急查 INR 而不是既往门诊 INR，并在 IV alteplase 不符合条件时迅速转向 CTA 和机械取栓评估。取栓前护理聚焦于按医嘱可滴定控压、维持 NPO、确保静脉通路、心电监护、完成记录和代理同意。成功再灌注后，患者从改善中的神经基线突然恶化并出现同侧瞳孔扩大，应按颅内出血处理直到排除；优先反应是立即通知团队、急诊 CT、准备气道处理、按医嘱控压，以及连续神经评估。确认出血后，护士主要通过 GCS、瞳孔、运动反应和收缩压反应来评估是否稳定，同时配合医嘱逆转抗凝和神经外科处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding stroke cases, separate time-sensitive eligibility data from background history, then compare each new neurologic finding with the most recent baseline.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做逐步展开的卒中题时，先把有时间敏感性的适用性资料与背景病史分开，再把每一个新的神经发现与最近的基线进行比较。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2548,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,140],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,47],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, classify each assessment finding as consistent with the suspected left MCA stroke syndrome or normal/unrelated to that syndrome.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 1，将每项评估发现分类为符合疑似左侧 MCA 卒中综合征，或属于正常/与该综合征无关。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, classify each assessment finding as consistent with the suspected left MCA stroke syndrome or normal/unrelated to that syndrome.","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 1，将每项评估发现分类为符合疑似左侧 MCA 卒中综合征，或属于正常/与该综合征无关。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Right arm and right leg weakness, with the arm more affected","zh":"右臂和右腿无力，且右臂受累更重"},{"id":"r2","en":"Expressive aphasia with impaired repetition","zh":"表达性失语并伴复述受损"},{"id":"r3","en":"Right lower facial droop","zh":"右下脸下垂"},{"id":"r4","en":"Forced leftward gaze preference","zh":"强迫性向左凝视偏斜"},{"id":"r5","en":"Cardiac rhythm pattern on the baseline telemetry strip","zh":"基线遥测心律条上显示的心律模式"},{"id":"r6","en":"Full strength in the left arm and left leg","zh":"左臂和左腿肌力正常"},{"id":"r7","en":"Equal, reactive 3-mm pupils on arrival","zh":"到达时双侧 3 mm 瞳孔等大且对光反应存在"},{"id":"r8","en":"Clear lung sounds and normal troponin","zh":"肺音清且肌钙蛋白正常"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Normal or unrelated to this stroke syndrome","zh":"正常或与该卒中综合征无关"},{"id":"c1","en":"Consistent with left MCA stroke/cardioembolic mechanism","zh":"符合左侧 MCA 卒中/心源性栓塞机制"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r7","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r8","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Right hemiplegia, expressive aphasia, right lower facial droop, and left gaze preference localize to a dominant left MCA cortical stroke. Atrial fibrillation and sudden onset support a cardioembolic mechanism. Intact left-sided strength, initially equal reactive pupils, clear lungs, and a normal troponin do not explain the focal left MCA syndrome.","rationaleCorrectZh":"右侧偏瘫、表达性失语、右下脸下垂和向左凝视偏斜定位于优势半球左侧 MCA 皮质性卒中。房颤和突发起病支持心源性栓塞机制。左侧肌力完整、初始瞳孔等大且有反应、肺音清和肌钙蛋白正常，不能解释这个局灶性左侧 MCA 综合征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Localize neurologic findings first. Cortical signs such as aphasia and gaze preference help distinguish a large-territory stroke from unrelated normal assessment data.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先定位神经系统发现。失语和凝视偏斜等皮质体征有助于把大血管供血区卒中与无关的正常评估资料区分开。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2549,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[127,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,84],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, the CT shows no hemorrhage, last known well was about 75 minutes ago, BP is 186/102 mmHg, and the stat INR is 1.8. Use the institution's alteplase protocol stated in the chart.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 1，CT 未见出血，最后正常约 75 分钟前，BP 为 186/102 mmHg，急查 INR 为 1.8。请使用病历中说明的本机构 alteplase 流程。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the institution's alteplase protocol stated in the chart.","terminalSentenceZh":"请使用病历中说明的本机构 alteplase 流程。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, the CT shows no hemorrhage, last known well was about 75 minutes ago, BP is 186/102 mmHg, and the stat INR is 1.8.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在阶段 1，CT 未见出血，最后正常约 75 分钟前，BP 为 186/102 mmHg，急查 INR 为 1.8。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The nurse should recognize that IV alteplase is {{1}} because the decisive contraindication is {{2}}. The nurse should promptly {{3}}.","zh":"护士应识别 IV alteplase {{1}}，因为决定性禁忌因素是 {{2}}。护士应立即 {{3}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"contraindicated at this time","zh":"此时禁用"},{"id":"o3","en":"delayed until the clinic INR from five days ago is repeated","zh":"需等待重复 5 天前门诊 INR 后再决定"},{"id":"o2","en":"indicated because the CT is negative","zh":"因 CT 阴性而适用"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"the blood pressure is above 180 systolic","zh":"收缩压高于 180"},{"id":"o1","en":"the current INR of 1.8 exceeds the institutional threshold","zh":"当前 INR 1.8 超过本机构阈值"},{"id":"o3","en":"the client took warfarin this morning regardless of the INR","zh":"无论 INR 如何，患者今晨服用了 warfarin"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"communicate the stat INR and support the pivot to CTA/thrombectomy evaluation","zh":"报告急查 INR，并协助转向 CTA/取栓评估"},{"id":"o3","en":"give aspirin immediately for secondary prevention","zh":"立即给予 aspirin 进行二级预防"},{"id":"o2","en":"prepare alteplase while waiting for the historical clinic INR","zh":"一边等待既往门诊 INR，一边准备 alteplase"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The case states the governing institutional protocol: IV alteplase is contraindicated when the INR exceeds 1.7 at intended administration. This client's current stat INR is 1.8, so the nurse should communicate that finding and support rapid CTA and thrombectomy evaluation rather than focusing on the clinic INR from five days ago or assuming a negative CT alone makes alteplase appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例明确给出本机构流程：计划给药时 INR 超过 1.7 时禁用 IV alteplase。该患者当前急查 INR 为 1.8，因此护士应报告该结果并协助快速进行 CTA 和取栓评估，而不是依赖 5 天前的门诊 INR，或认为 CT 阴性本身就足以使用 alteplase。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For thrombolysis questions, use the current point-of-care data at the time of the decision. A historical lab value may explain risk but does not replace the stat eligibility lab.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做溶栓适用性题时，要使用决策当时的当前资料。既往化验可解释风险，但不能替代急查适用性化验。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2550,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,105],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,28],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which hypothesis best explains the client's presentation and guides the next diagnostic step?","fullStemZh":"在阶段 1，哪一项假设最能解释患者表现并指导下一步诊断？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which hypothesis best explains the client's presentation and guides the next diagnostic step?","terminalSentenceZh":"在阶段 1，哪一项假设最能解释患者表现并指导下一步诊断？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Primary hypertensive encephalopathy; delay vascular imaging until BP is normal","zh":"原发性高血压脑病；等血压正常后再做血管成像"},{"id":"D","en":"Hemorrhagic stroke; prepare anticoagulation reversal before further imaging","zh":"出血性卒中；进一步成像前先准备抗凝逆转"},{"id":"A","en":"Acute ischemic stroke from a likely cardioembolic left MCA occlusion; proceed with CTA for thrombectomy evaluation","zh":"疑似心源性栓塞导致左侧 MCA 闭塞的急性缺血性卒中；进行 CTA 以评估取栓"},{"id":"C","en":"Lacunar stroke from chronic hypertension; no large-vessel imaging is needed","zh":"慢性高血压导致腔隙性卒中；不需要大血管成像"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sudden onset, atrial fibrillation, aphasia, gaze preference, and dense right-sided deficits fit a large-vessel left MCA ischemic stroke, most likely cardioembolic. The initial CT excludes hemorrhage, and alteplase is excluded by the institutional INR criterion, so CTA for large-vessel occlusion and thrombectomy evaluation is the priority.","rationaleCorrectZh":"突发起病、房颤、失语、凝视偏斜和严重右侧缺损符合大血管左侧 MCA 缺血性卒中，最可能为心源性栓塞。初始 CT 排除出血，而 alteplase 因本机构 INR 标准不符合，因此优先进行 CTA 评估大血管闭塞和取栓可能性。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cortical signs plus sudden onset in atrial fibrillation should make you think cardioembolic large-vessel occlusion, not just hypertension or a small-vessel stroke.","testTakingStrategyZh":"房颤患者突发皮质体征时，应想到心源性栓塞性大血管闭塞，而不只是高血压或小血管卒中。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2551,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,183],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,59],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, the client is a thrombectomy candidate with BP 186/102 mmHg. Which nursing actions are appropriate before transfer to the neurointerventional suite? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 2，患者符合取栓条件，BP 为 186/102 mmHg。转入神经介入室前，哪些护理措施合适？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate before transfer to the neurointerventional suite?","penultimateSentenceZh":"转入神经介入室前，哪些护理措施合适？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Maintain strict NPO status until a trained dysphagia screen is completed","zh":"在受训人员完成吞咽筛查前保持严格 NPO"},{"id":"A","en":"Start the prescribed IV nicardipine infusion and titrate per protocol toward the pre-thrombectomy BP threshold","zh":"开始医嘱的 IV nicardipine 输注，并按流程滴定至取栓前血压阈值"},{"id":"F","en":"Request IV nitroprusside as the preferred first-line agent for rapid BP reduction","zh":"要求使用 IV nitroprusside 作为快速降压的一线首选药"},{"id":"C","en":"Ensure two patent IV lines and continuous cardiac monitoring","zh":"确保两条通畅静脉通路并持续心电监护"},{"id":"D","en":"Verify that proxy consent has been obtained because the client cannot provide informed consent due to aphasia","zh":"确认已由代理人同意，因为患者因失语无法提供知情同意"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer oral antihypertensive medication with sips of water to lower the BP gradually","zh":"用少量水给予口服降压药，以逐渐降低血压"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For a thrombectomy candidate, the nurse supports ordered titratable BP control, maintains NPO status because dysphagia risk has not been cleared, ensures IV access and monitoring, and confirms proxy consent when the neurologic deficit prevents informed consent. Oral intake before swallowing screening is unsafe. Nitroprusside is generally avoided as an initial first-line stroke BP agent because it can raise intracranial pressure and cause abrupt hypotension; the case order is nicardipine.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对取栓候选者，护士应配合医嘱进行可滴定控压，因吞咽风险尚未排除而维持 NPO，确保静脉通路和监护，并在神经缺损妨碍知情同意时确认代理人同意。吞咽筛查前经口摄入不安全。Nitroprusside 通常不作为卒中初始一线降压药，因为可能升高颅内压并造成血压骤降；本病例医嘱为 nicardipine。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When actions are concurrent before a procedure, avoid forcing a sequence. Select the actions that reduce immediate risk without delaying definitive reperfusion.","testTakingStrategyZh":"术前多项措施可同时进行时，不要强行排序。选择能降低立即风险且不延误再灌注治疗的措施。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2552,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[212,234],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,78],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, 45 minutes after neuro-ICU arrival, the client becomes drowsy, stops following commands, has no verbal output, and develops a new sluggish left pupil. Which actions should the nurse take immediately? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 3，到达神经 ICU 后 45 分钟，患者变得嗜睡、不再遵循指令、无语言输出，并出现新的左瞳孔对光反应迟钝。护士应立即采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take immediately?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应立即采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Perform and document a rapid focused neurologic assessment compared with the post-procedure baseline","zh":"进行并记录快速重点神经评估，并与术后基线比较"},{"id":"F","en":"Let the client rest until the next scheduled neurologic check because fatigue is expected after the procedure","zh":"让患者休息到下一次计划神经检查，因为术后疲劳是预期表现"},{"id":"E","en":"Continue close BP monitoring while emergency treatment is initiated","zh":"启动急救处理的同时继续密切监测 BP"},{"id":"B","en":"Prepare for emergent non-contrast CT head","zh":"准备急诊头颅非增强 CT"},{"id":"C","en":"Maintain airway patency and prepare for possible intubation","zh":"维持气道通畅，并准备可能的插管"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the neurointerventionalist and neurology team stat","zh":"立即通知神经介入医师和神经科团队"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Abrupt decline from an improving post-thrombectomy baseline, especially with new pupil asymmetry, is a neurologic emergency consistent with intracranial hemorrhage or mass effect until proven otherwise. The nurse should notify the team stat, prepare for emergent CT, protect the airway, rapidly document the neurologic change from baseline, and continue BP monitoring. Waiting for the next scheduled check or focusing on a clean groin site would delay care.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者在取栓后已改善的基线上突然恶化，尤其出现新的瞳孔不对称，应视为神经急症，按颅内出血或占位效应处理直到排除。护士应立即通知团队，准备急诊 CT，保护气道，快速记录与基线相比的神经变化，并继续监测 BP。等待下一次计划检查或把重点放在清洁无血肿的腹股沟穿刺部位会延误处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After reperfusion, compare every change to the most recent neurologic baseline. New decreased consciousness or pupil asymmetry is a red flag, not routine recovery.","testTakingStrategyZh":"再灌注后，要把每个变化与最近的神经基线比较。新的意识下降或瞳孔不对称是危险信号，不是常规恢复过程。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take immediately?","controlSentenceZh":"护士应立即采取哪些措施？"}
{"queueIndex":2553,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.62.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[285,307],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,94],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 4, the CT confirms intracerebral hemorrhage with midline shift. The client is intubated, reversal is ordered, and nicardipine is being titrated to the provider's stat BP target. Which parameters are the priority bedside indicators of stabilization or continued deterioration? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"在阶段 4，CT 确认脑实质内出血并有中线移位。患者已插管，已医嘱逆转抗凝，nicardipine 正在滴定至医师紧急血压目标。哪些参数是床旁判断稳定或继续恶化的优先指标？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which parameters are the priority bedside indicators of stabilization or continued deterioration?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些参数是床旁判断稳定或继续恶化的优先指标？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Systolic BP trend and response to the nicardipine infusion","zh":"收缩压趋势及对 nicardipine 输注的反应"},{"id":"E","en":"Appearance of the right groin dressing as the main marker of intracranial hemorrhage stability","zh":"以右腹股沟敷料外观作为颅内出血稳定性的主要指标"},{"id":"D","en":"Serial troponin levels because the initial rhythm was atrial fibrillation","zh":"因初始心律为房颤而连续监测肌钙蛋白"},{"id":"C","en":"NIHSS score as the primary tool while the client is intubated and nonverbal","zh":"患者已插管且不能说话时，以 NIHSS 作为主要工具"},{"id":"A","en":"Serial neurologic examination: GCS, pupil size/reactivity, and motor response","zh":"连续神经检查：GCS、瞳孔大小/反应和运动反应"}],"correct":["A","B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In acute intracerebral hemorrhage with mass effect, the most actionable bedside indicators are serial neurologic status and BP response. Worsening GCS, fixed or enlarging pupil, or worsening motor response suggests expanding hematoma or rising ICP. Uncontrolled systolic BP can drive hematoma expansion, so response to the nicardipine target must be tracked. NIHSS is less useful in an intubated nonverbal client; troponin and the clean groin site do not evaluate the intracranial hemorrhage.","rationaleCorrectZh":"急性脑实质内出血伴占位效应时，最有行动价值的床旁指标是连续神经状态和血压反应。GCS 恶化、瞳孔固定或扩大、运动反应恶化提示血肿扩大或 ICP 升高。收缩压控制不佳会推动血肿扩大，因此必须追踪对 nicardipine 目标的反应。NIHSS 对已插管、不能说话的患者用处较小；肌钙蛋白和清洁的腹股沟穿刺部位不能评估颅内出血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For evaluation questions, choose parameters that change management in real time. In ICH, bedside neuro trends and BP control are more actionable than unrelated labs or earlier stroke scales.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做评估结果题时，选择能实时改变处理的参数。ICH 中，床旁神经趋势和血压控制比无关化验或较早阶段使用的卒中量表更有行动价值。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2554,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_stroke_2026_06_16_case_acute_ischemic_stroke_warfarin_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.63","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Procedural Complications & Dialysis","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.63.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.63.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[322,459],"terminalOffsetsZh":[110,158],"fullStemEn":"Complete the bow-tie for this Stage 4 situation: after successful left MCA thrombectomy, the client initially improved, then became somnolent with loss of verbal output and a new sluggish left pupil. Emergent CT shows a 3 cm left frontoparietal intraparenchymal hemorrhage with edema and 4 mm left-to-right midline shift. The client is intubated, warfarin reversal has been ordered, and nicardipine is being titrated to the provider's stat systolic BP target.","fullStemZh":"完成此阶段 4 情境的 bow-tie：左侧 MCA 取栓成功后，患者最初改善，随后出现嗜睡、无语言输出，并出现新的左瞳孔对光反应迟钝。急诊 CT 显示左额顶叶脑实质内出血 3 cm，伴水肿和 4 mm 左向右中线移位。患者已插管，已医嘱逆转 warfarin，nicardipine 正在滴定至医师紧急收缩压目标。","terminalSentenceEn":"The client is intubated, warfarin reversal has been ordered, and nicardipine is being titrated to the provider's stat systolic BP target.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者已插管，已医嘱逆转 warfarin，nicardipine 正在滴定至医师紧急收缩压目标。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Emergent CT shows a 3 cm left frontoparietal intraparenchymal hemorrhage with edema and 4 mm left-to-right midline shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急诊 CT 显示左额顶叶脑实质内出血 3 cm，伴水肿和 4 mm 左向右中线移位。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"prompt":{"en":"Most likely condition","zh":"最可能的病情"},"tokens":[{"id":"cond_mca_reocclusion","en":"Re-occlusion of the left MCA after thrombectomy","zh":"取栓后左侧 MCA 再闭塞"},{"id":"cond_post_reperfusion_ich","en":"Post-reperfusion symptomatic intracerebral hemorrhage","zh":"再灌注后有症状性脑实质内出血"},{"id":"cond_sedation_effect","en":"Post-procedural sedation or medication effect","zh":"术后镇静或药物作用"}],"correct":"cond_post_reperfusion_ich"},"actions":{"prompt":{"en":"Priority actions","zh":"优先措施"},"tokens":[{"id":"act_serial_neuro_q15","en":"Maintain serial neurologic assessments every 15 minutes, tracking GCS, pupils, and motor response","zh":"每 15 分钟持续神经评估，追踪 GCS、瞳孔和运动反应"},{"id":"act_titrate_nicardipine","en":"Titrate nicardipine per order to maintain the prescribed systolic BP target","zh":"按医嘱滴定 nicardipine，以维持规定的收缩压目标"},{"id":"act_hourly_neuro","en":"Reduce neurologic checks to hourly because the client is intubated","zh":"因患者已插管，将神经检查减少为每小时一次"},{"id":"act_admin_antiplatelet","en":"Administer aspirin or clopidogrel now for ischemic stroke secondary prevention","zh":"现在给予 aspirin 或 clopidogrel 进行缺血性卒中二级预防"}],"correct":["act_serial_neuro_q15","act_titrate_nicardipine"]},"parameters":{"prompt":{"en":"Parameters to monitor","zh":"应监测的指标"},"tokens":[{"id":"param_sbp_trend","en":"Systolic BP trend on the nicardipine infusion","zh":"nicardipine 输注期间的收缩压趋势"},{"id":"param_neuro_exam","en":"Neurologic examination: GCS, pupil size/reactivity, and motor response","zh":"神经检查：GCS、瞳孔大小/反应和运动反应"},{"id":"param_nihss","en":"NIHSS score as the main measure during intubated ICH management","zh":"插管后 ICH 处理中以 NIHSS 作为主要衡量指标"},{"id":"param_troponin","en":"Serial troponin level","zh":"连续肌钙蛋白水平"}],"correct":["param_neuro_exam","param_sbp_trend"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The best synthesis is post-reperfusion symptomatic intracerebral hemorrhage because the client had initial improvement after successful thrombectomy, then abruptly developed decreased consciousness, loss of speech, and ipsilateral pupil dilation, and CT confirms hemorrhage with midline shift. The nurse's priority actions are frequent neurologic assessment and prescribed BP control because worsening examination or uncontrolled systolic BP can signal or worsen hematoma expansion. The priority parameters mirror those actions: GCS/pupils/motor response and systolic BP trend.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最佳综合判断是再灌注后有症状性脑实质内出血，因为患者成功取栓后最初改善，随后突然出现意识下降、语言丧失和同侧瞳孔扩大，且 CT 确认出血并有中线移位。护士优先措施是频繁神经评估和按医嘱控压，因为神经检查恶化或收缩压控制不佳可能提示或加重血肿扩大。优先监测参数与这些措施对应：GCS/瞳孔/运动反应，以及收缩压趋势。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bow-tie items, first name the condition that explains all cues, then choose nursing actions and monitoring parameters that directly reduce or detect the highest-risk complication.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bow-tie 题时，先确定能解释所有线索的病情，再选择能直接降低或发现最高风险并发症的护理措施和监测指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2555,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_CASE_CONTAINER","questionPath":"questions.64","itemType":"case_study","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.64.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[369,448],"terminalOffsetsZh":[120,142],"fullStemEn":"Prerenal acute kidney injury with hyperkalemia in acute-on-chronic kidney disease A 65-year-old man with stage 3a CKD, type 2 diabetes treated with metformin, hypertension treated with lisinopril, and intermittent ibuprofen use is transferred from a skilled nursing facility after 72 hours of profuse vomiting and watery diarrhea during a confirmed norovirus outbreak. He has minimal oral intake, increasing confusion, and near-absent urine output.","fullStemZh":"慢性肾病基础上发生肾前性急性肾损伤并高钾血症 65 岁男性，既往 3a 期慢性肾病、2 型糖尿病（服用二甲双胍）、高血压（服用赖诺普利），并间断使用布洛芬。在熟练护理机构确认诺如病毒暴发期间，他出现 72 小时大量呕吐和水样腹泻后转入急诊。患者口服摄入极少，意识混乱加重，并几乎无尿。","terminalSentenceEn":"He has minimal oral intake, increasing confusion, and near-absent urine output.","terminalSentenceZh":"患者口服摄入极少，意识混乱加重，并几乎无尿。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Prerenal acute kidney injury with hyperkalemia in acute-on-chronic kidney disease A 65-year-old man with stage 3a CKD, type 2 diabetes treated with metformin, hypertension treated with lisinopril, and intermittent ibuprofen use is transferred from a skilled nursing facility after 72 hours of profuse vomiting and watery diarrhea during a confirmed norovirus outbreak.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在熟练护理机构确认诺如病毒暴发期间，他出现 72 小时大量呕吐和水样腹泻后转入急诊。","responseContext":{},"rationaleCorrectEn":"This case follows severe GI fluid loss causing prerenal AKI on baseline CKD, complicated by dangerous hyperkalemia. The admission pattern is volume depletion with preserved tubular sodium conservation: hypotension, tachycardia, dry mucous membranes, poor turgor, flat neck veins, concentrated urine, urine sodium 8 mEq/L, and FENa 0.4%. Hyperkalemia becomes the immediate threat as ECG changes progress from peaked T waves to PR prolongation and QRS widening. Safe care requires holding renally risky medications, clarifying omitted NSAID orders, stabilizing the myocardium with calcium before potassium-shifting therapy, questioning unsafe oral SPS administration in a vomiting client, monitoring glucose after insulin, and evaluating response by ECG normalization, potassium trend, urine output, creatinine trend, hemodynamics, and mental status. Improvement is real but not final because potassium can rebound and creatinine remains far above baseline.","rationaleCorrectZh":"本病例显示严重胃肠道液体丢失导致慢性肾病基础上的肾前性 AKI，并并发危险性高钾血症。入院模式为容量不足且肾小管仍能保钠：低血压、心动过速、黏膜干燥、皮肤弹性差、颈静脉扁平、尿液浓缩、尿钠 8 mEq/L、FENa 0.4%。随着 ECG 从高尖 T 波进展为 PR 延长和 QRS 增宽，高钾成为最立即威胁。安全护理包括暂停肾脏高风险用药、澄清遗漏的 NSAID 医嘱、先用钙剂稳定心肌再进行转钾治疗、对呕吐患者口服 SPS 的不安全医嘱提出疑问、胰岛素后监测血糖，并通过 ECG 正常化、血钾趋势、尿量、肌酐趋势、血流动力学和意识状态评估反应。改善是真实的，但尚未完全解除风险，因为血钾可能反弹且肌酐仍远高于基线。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In unfolding renal cases, keep two tracks active: diagnose the renal pattern from urine/perfusion cues, and separately prioritize complications that can kill first, especially ECG-changing hyperkalemia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理展开式肾脏病例时，要同时保持两条思路：根据尿液/灌注线索判断肾损伤模式；另行优先处理最先致命的并发症，尤其是出现 ECG 改变的高钾血症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2556,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_q1","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.0","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,89],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,27],"fullStemEn":"For each admission finding, classify the most clinically relevant meaning in this client.","fullStemZh":"请将每项入院评估结果归类为对该患者最有临床意义的含义。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each admission finding, classify the most clinically relevant meaning in this client.","terminalSentenceZh":"请将每项入院评估结果归类为对该患者最有临床意义的含义。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Urine specific gravity 1.032","zh":"尿比重 1.032"},{"id":"r2","en":"Urine sodium 8 mEq/L","zh":"尿钠 8 mEq/L"},{"id":"r3","en":"FENa 0.4%","zh":"钠排泄分数 FENa 0.4%"},{"id":"r4","en":"Creatinine 4.2 mg/dL, baseline 1.4 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐 4.2 mg/dL，基线 1.4 mg/dL"},{"id":"r5","en":"BP 88/54 with HR 112","zh":"BP 88/54，HR 112"},{"id":"r6","en":"Dry mucous membranes, poor skin turgor, flat neck veins","zh":"黏膜干燥、皮肤弹性差、颈静脉扁平"},{"id":"r7","en":"Potassium 6.1 mEq/L with peaked T waves","zh":"钾 6.1 mEq/L，并有高尖 T 波"},{"id":"r8","en":"Clear lung sounds with no crackles","zh":"双肺清，无湿啰音"},{"id":"r9","en":"Bladder scan 40 mL","zh":"膀胱扫描 40 mL"},{"id":"r10","en":"BUN-to-creatinine ratio 16.2:1","zh":"BUN/肌酐比值 16.2:1"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Indicates dangerous hyperkalemia","zh":"提示危险性高钾血症"},{"id":"c4","en":"Not the strongest prerenal cue here","zh":"不是本病例最强的肾前性线索"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supports prerenal AKI from volume depletion","zh":"支持容量不足导致的肾前性 AKI"},{"id":"c3","en":"Rules out or argues against another cause","zh":"排除或不支持其他病因"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r7","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r8","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r9","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r10","columnIds":["c4"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The strongest prerenal pattern is the cluster of severe volume depletion plus kidneys that are still conserving sodium and water: concentrated urine, urine sodium 8 mEq/L, FENa 0.4%, acute creatinine rise, hypotension, tachycardia, dry mucous membranes, poor turgor, flat neck veins, and cool extremities. Potassium 6.1 mEq/L with peaked T waves is a separate immediate danger: hyperkalemia with myocardial irritability. Clear lungs support the absence of fluid overload, and a 40 mL bladder scan argues against urinary retention. The BUN-to-creatinine ratio is elevated but not the strongest cue in this scaffold, so the nurse should not over-weight it over the urine sodium, FENa, concentrated urine, and clinical dehydration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最强的肾前性模式是：严重容量不足，同时肾脏仍在保钠保水，包括尿液浓缩、尿钠 8 mEq/L、FENa 0.4%、肌酐急升、低血压、心动过速、黏膜干燥、皮肤弹性差、颈静脉扁平以及肢端偏凉。钾 6.1 mEq/L 合并高尖 T 波则是另一个立即危险：高钾血症导致心肌电活动不稳定。双肺清支持没有液体过负荷，膀胱扫描 40 mL 不支持尿潴留。BUN/肌酐比值虽升高，但在此病例中不是最强线索，护士不应把它看得比尿钠、FENa、尿液浓缩和临床脱水表现更重要。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Cluster cues before naming the problem: volume-loss history plus concentrated, low-sodium urine points to prerenal AKI, while ECG changes with high potassium create the immediate danger.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先把线索组合起来再判断问题：容量丢失病史加上尿液浓缩、尿钠低，指向肾前性 AKI；高钾合并 ECG 改变则构成立即危险。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2557,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_q2","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[70,92],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,32],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 1, which medication-related nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 1 阶段，哪些与用药相关的护理措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 1, which medication-related nursing actions are appropriate?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 1 阶段，哪些与用药相关的护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Continue holding lisinopril during this hypovolemic AKI episode.","zh":"在本次低容量性 AKI 期间继续暂停赖诺普利。"},{"id":"E","en":"Teach the patient and family not to use over-the-counter NSAIDs during recovery unless the provider approves.","zh":"教育患者和家属：恢复期间除非医嘱允许，不要自行使用非处方 NSAID。"},{"id":"B","en":"Monitor the lactate and acidosis while recognizing hypoperfusion can also contribute.","zh":"监测乳酸和酸中毒，同时认识到低灌注也可能造成这些异常。"},{"id":"A","en":"Continue holding metformin while renal function is acutely impaired.","zh":"在肾功能急性受损期间继续暂停二甲双胍。"},{"id":"F","en":"Give metformin because the admission glucose is 188 mg/dL.","zh":"因入院血糖 188 mg/dL，应给予二甲双胍。"},{"id":"D","en":"Clarify that ibuprofen is explicitly held and documented as contraindicated during the AKI episode.","zh":"与医嘱方确认布洛芬在本次 AKI 期间明确暂停，并记录为禁用。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Metformin, lisinopril, and ibuprofen all matter in this AKI episode. Metformin should be held because reduced renal clearance can increase accumulation and lactic acidosis risk; the elevated lactate needs monitoring, though hypoperfusion is also a plausible contributor. Lisinopril should be held because ACE inhibition can reduce the efferent arteriolar tone that helps preserve glomerular filtration pressure during hypovolemia. Ibuprofen should be explicitly held and documented because NSAIDs can impair prostaglandin-mediated afferent arteriolar dilation and may be inadvertently restarted if not addressed. Teaching should include avoiding OTC NSAIDs during recovery unless approved.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在本次 AKI 中，二甲双胍、赖诺普利和布洛芬都很重要。二甲双胍应暂停，因为肾清除下降可增加药物蓄积和乳酸性酸中毒风险；乳酸升高需要监测，但低灌注本身也可能造成乳酸升高。赖诺普利应暂停，因为 ACE 抑制会降低出球小动脉张力，而这种张力在低容量时有助于维持肾小球滤过压力。布洛芬应明确暂停并记录，因为 NSAID 可影响前列腺素介导的入球小动脉扩张；若不处理，可能被误重新使用。宣教应包括恢复期除非医嘱允许，不自行使用 OTC NSAID。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When AKI is present, screen every home and OTC medication for renal clearance or renal perfusion effects; do not stop at the drugs already addressed in the orders.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出现 AKI 时，要逐一筛查所有居家药和 OTC 药是否影响肾清除或肾灌注；不要只看医嘱已经提到的药。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2558,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_q3","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,68],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,23],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which problem is the nurse's highest immediate priority?","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段，护士最优先立即处理的问题是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which problem is the nurse's highest immediate priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段，护士最优先立即处理的问题是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Creatinine rising from 4.2 to 4.5 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐从 4.2 升至 4.5 mg/dL"},{"id":"D","en":"Nausea that makes oral medications difficult to retain","zh":"恶心导致口服药难以保留"},{"id":"B","en":"Oliguria with urine output 0.14 mL/kg/hr","zh":"少尿，尿量 0.14 mL/kg/hr"},{"id":"A","en":"Worsening hyperkalemia with PR prolongation and QRS widening","zh":"高钾血症恶化，伴 PR 延长和 QRS 增宽"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The potassium has risen to 6.4 mEq/L and the ECG has progressed from peaked T waves to PR prolongation and QRS widening. That pattern signals advancing hyperkalemia-related conduction toxicity and can deteriorate to a lethal rhythm. Oliguria and rising creatinine are serious, but they do not create the same minute-to-minute cardiac arrest risk. The nurse should prepare for emergent membrane stabilization with calcium gluconate while the renal problem continues to be managed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"钾升至 6.4 mEq/L，ECG 从高尖 T 波进展为 PR 延长和 QRS 增宽。这表示高钾相关传导毒性正在进展，可能恶化为致命心律。少尿和肌酐升高也严重，但不像这种 ECG 改变一样具有分钟级心脏骤停风险。护士应准备立即使用葡萄糖酸钙稳定心肌膜，同时继续处理肾脏问题。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In prioritization questions, an electrolyte abnormality with ECG conduction changes usually outranks slower organ-function trends because it can cause sudden death.","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先级题中，电解质异常若已出现 ECG 传导改变，通常优先于较慢的器官功能趋势，因为它可导致猝死。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2559,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_q4","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.3","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,80],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,25],"fullStemEn":"Complete the nurse's clinical reasoning about the Stage 2 hyperkalemia protocol.","fullStemZh":"完成护士对第 2 阶段高钾血症处理方案的临床推理。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the nurse's clinical reasoning about the Stage 2 hyperkalemia protocol.","terminalSentenceZh":"完成护士对第 2 阶段高钾血症处理方案的临床推理。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"Because the client has hyperkalemia with ECG conduction changes, the nurse should give {{1}} first. The next rapid potassium-shifting treatment is {{2}}. The oral sodium polystyrene sulfonate order should be {{3}} because {{4}}. After insulin is administered, the nurse should {{5}}.","zh":"由于该患者高钾血症并出现 ECG 传导改变，护士应首先给予 {{1}}。接下来快速转移钾入细胞的治疗是 {{2}}。口服聚苯乙烯磺酸钠医嘱应 {{3}}，因为 {{4}}。给予胰岛素后，护士应 {{5}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"oral sodium polystyrene sulfonate","zh":"口服聚苯乙烯磺酸钠"},{"id":"o1","en":"calcium gluconate at the ordered/protocol rate","zh":"按医嘱/方案速度给予葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"o2","en":"regular insulin before any calcium","zh":"先给予普通胰岛素，不先给钙剂"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"continuing lisinopril to improve renal perfusion","zh":"继续赖诺普利以改善肾灌注"},{"id":"o3","en":"waiting for creatinine to improve before treating potassium","zh":"等待肌酐改善后再处理血钾"},{"id":"o1","en":"regular insulin with dextrose per protocol","zh":"按方案给予普通胰岛素合并葡萄糖"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"3","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"given immediately despite vomiting","zh":"即使呕吐也立即给予"},{"id":"o3","en":"used as the only urgent intervention","zh":"作为唯一紧急干预"},{"id":"o1","en":"questioned and clarified","zh":"提出疑问并澄清"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"4","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"binders stabilize the myocardium faster than calcium","zh":"钾结合剂比钙剂更快稳定心肌"},{"id":"o1","en":"the client is actively nauseated and vomiting, making oral administration unsafe and unlikely to be retained","zh":"患者正在恶心呕吐，口服不安全且很可能无法保留"},{"id":"o2","en":"the potassium is already normal","zh":"血钾已经正常"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"5","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"restart metformin to prevent hypoglycemia","zh":"重新使用二甲双胍以预防低血糖"},{"id":"o1","en":"recheck blood glucose at protocol intervals and keep dextrose available","zh":"按方案时间复查血糖，并备好葡萄糖"},{"id":"o2","en":"stop ECG monitoring once the insulin is given","zh":"给予胰岛素后停止 ECG 监测"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"With hyperkalemia and ECG conduction changes, calcium gluconate is first because it stabilizes the cardiac membrane quickly but does not lower serum potassium. Insulin with dextrose follows to shift potassium intracellularly. Sodium bicarbonate may also be used because it is ordered in this acidotic client, but oral SPS should be questioned because active nausea and vomiting make oral administration unsafe and unreliable. Insulin can cause delayed hypoglycemia even when dextrose is given, so glucose monitoring must continue after administration.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高钾血症合并 ECG 传导改变时，葡萄糖酸钙应首先使用，因为它能迅速稳定心肌膜，但不会降低血清钾。随后按方案给予胰岛素合并葡萄糖，使钾转入细胞。由于该患者有酸中毒，医嘱中的碳酸氢钠也可使用；但口服 SPS 应提出疑问，因为患者正在恶心呕吐，口服既不安全也不可靠。即使给予了葡萄糖，胰岛素仍可导致延迟性低血糖，因此用药后必须继续监测血糖。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate hyperkalemia care into three jobs: stabilize the membrane first, shift potassium next, and remove potassium when safe and feasible.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把高钾处理分成三件事：先稳定心肌膜，再把钾转入细胞，最后在安全可行时排钾。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2560,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_q5","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.4","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[88,110],"terminalOffsetsZh":[23,31],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 2, which nursing actions should be included in the immediate bedside response? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段，哪些护理措施应纳入床旁立即处置？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At Stage 2, which nursing actions should be included in the immediate bedside response?","penultimateSentenceZh":"第 2 阶段，哪些护理措施应纳入床旁立即处置？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Use fall/safety precautions because the client is lethargic and confused.","zh":"因患者嗜睡、意识混乱，采取跌倒/安全预防措施。"},{"id":"C","en":"Have regular insulin, dextrose, and a glucometer ready at the bedside.","zh":"在床旁备好普通胰岛素、葡萄糖和血糖仪。"},{"id":"D","en":"Set reminders for post-insulin blood glucose checks according to protocol.","zh":"按方案设置胰岛素后复查血糖提醒。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the peripheral IV for patency and infiltration before and during calcium gluconate administration.","zh":"给予葡萄糖酸钙前及过程中评估外周 IV 是否通畅及有无渗漏。"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer calcium gluconate at the ordered/protocol rate while observing continuous ECG monitoring.","zh":"按医嘱/方案速度给予葡萄糖酸钙，并观察连续 ECG 监测。"},{"id":"E","en":"Continue strict intake and output with hourly urine measurements from the Foley catheter.","zh":"继续严格出入量记录，并通过 Foley 导尿管每小时测量尿量。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D","E","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The immediate response is coordinated rather than purely linear. The nurse gives calcium gluconate at the ordered/protocol rate through a patent IV while monitoring ECG response and the IV site, prepares insulin/dextrose and glucose monitoring, continues hourly urine output measurement, and protects the confused client from injury. Rapid uncontrolled calcium administration is unsafe, and oral SPS should not be given unchanged to a client who is actively nauseated and vomiting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"立即处置是协同进行的，而不是完全线性步骤。护士应通过通畅 IV 按医嘱/方案速度给予葡萄糖酸钙，同时监测 ECG 反应和 IV 部位；准备胰岛素/葡萄糖和血糖监测；继续每小时记录尿量；并保护意识混乱患者避免受伤。失控地快速给予钙剂不安全；对正在恶心呕吐的患者，不应照原样给予口服 SPS。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For emergency medication questions, look for the nursing safeguards attached to the drug: route/site assessment, monitoring, predictable adverse effects, and patient safety.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到紧急用药题，要找与药物相关的护理安全措施：给药途径/部位评估、监测、可预见不良反应以及患者安全。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2561,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01","embeddedQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_q6","recordKind":"EMBEDDED_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.5","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.64.caseStudy.questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[0,111],"terminalOffsetsZh":[0,39],"fullStemEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding as evidence of improvement, a reason for continued close monitoring, or both.","fullStemZh":"第 3 阶段，请判断每项结果是改善证据、需要继续严密监测的原因，还是两者兼有。","terminalSentenceEn":"At Stage 3, classify each finding as evidence of improvement, a reason for continued close monitoring, or both.","terminalSentenceZh":"第 3 阶段，请判断每项结果是改善证据、需要继续严密监测的原因，还是两者兼有。","penultimateSentenceEn":null,"penultimateSentenceZh":null,"responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Potassium decreased from 6.4 to 5.4 and then 4.9 mEq/L","zh":"血钾从 6.4 降至 5.4，随后 4.9 mEq/L"},{"id":"r2","en":"PR interval normalized to 0.18 seconds and QRS narrowed to 0.10 seconds","zh":"PR 间期恢复至 0.18 秒，QRS 缩窄至 0.10 秒"},{"id":"r3","en":"Urine output improved to 48 mL/hr, about 0.59 mL/kg/hr","zh":"尿量改善至 48 mL/hr，约 0.59 mL/kg/hr"},{"id":"r4","en":"Creatinine decreased to 3.8 mg/dL but baseline is 1.4 mg/dL","zh":"肌酐降至 3.8 mg/dL，但基线为 1.4 mg/dL"},{"id":"r5","en":"Blood pressure improved to 112/70 and heart rate to 84","zh":"血压改善至 112/70，心率 84"},{"id":"r6","en":"Mental status improved to alert and oriented x3","zh":"意识状态改善为清醒且定向力完整"},{"id":"r7","en":"Potassium may rebound as insulin shifting effect wears off","zh":"胰岛素转钾作用减弱后，血钾可能反弹"},{"id":"r8","en":"Vomiting or diarrhea could recur","zh":"呕吐或腹泻可能复发"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires continued close monitoring","zh":"需要继续严密监测"},{"id":"c1","en":"Evidence of improvement","zh":"改善证据"}],"selectionMode":"multiple_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1","c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1","c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1","c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1","c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r6","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r7","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r8","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The patient is improving because potassium, ECG conduction, urine output, creatinine, hemodynamics, lactate, and mental status are moving in the right direction. The nurse must still monitor closely because potassium can rebound after insulin shifts wear off, the creatinine remains far above baseline, urine output must stay above the perfusion target, and recurrent GI losses could restart the prerenal cycle. Outcome evaluation depends on trajectory and durability, not one isolated better number.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者正在改善，因为血钾、ECG 传导、尿量、肌酐、血流动力学、乳酸和意识状态均朝正确方向变化。但护士仍必须严密监测，因为胰岛素转钾作用减弱后血钾可能反弹，肌酐仍远高于基线，尿量必须持续达到灌注目标，且胃肠道丢失复发可能重新启动肾前性循环。结局评估看趋势和持续性，而不是单个暂时改善的数值。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For outcome evaluation, compare trends against baseline and ask whether the improvement is sustained or only temporary.","testTakingStrategyZh":"评估结局时，要把趋势与基线比较，并判断改善是持续的还是暂时的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2562,"bankPath":"banks/hard-cases-canonical.json","bankSha256":"438c176897a41d3b7f212435e5945bd524c3f0ba5a62931eb5e85843c93d8730","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_case_aki_2026_06_16_case_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia_01_bowtie","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.65","itemType":"bowtie","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.65.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.65.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[503,589],"terminalOffsetsZh":[211,239],"fullStemEn":"Stage 2 synthesis: A 65-year-old man with baseline stage 3a CKD has had 72 hours of vomiting and profuse watery diarrhea during a norovirus outbreak. After 1,500 mL IV fluid, urine output remains about 0.14 mL/kg/hr. Creatinine has risen from a baseline of 1.4 to 4.5 mg/dL. Admission urine was concentrated with urine sodium 8 mEq/L and FENa 0.4%, and bladder scan was 40 mL. Potassium is now 6.4 mEq/L with persistent peaked T waves, PR prolongation to 0.24 seconds, and QRS widening to 0.12 seconds. Select the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","fullStemZh":"第 2 阶段综合判断：65 岁男性，基线为 3a 期 CKD，在诺如病毒暴发期间出现 72 小时呕吐和大量水样腹泻。接受 1,500 mL IV 液体后，尿量仍约 0.14 mL/kg/hr。肌酐从基线 1.4 升至 4.5 mg/dL。入院尿液浓缩，尿钠 8 mEq/L，FENa 0.4%，膀胱扫描 40 mL。当前血钾 6.4 mEq/L，仍有高尖 T 波，PR 延长至 0.24 秒，QRS 增宽至 0.12 秒。请选择最可能的病情、两个优先措施以及两个需要监测的参数。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select the most likely condition, two priority actions, and two parameters to monitor.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择最可能的病情、两个优先措施以及两个需要监测的参数。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Potassium is now 6.4 mEq/L with persistent peaked T waves, PR prolongation to 0.24 seconds, and QRS widening to 0.12 seconds.","penultimateSentenceZh":"当前血钾 6.4 mEq/L，仍有高尖 T 波，PR 延长至 0.24 秒，QRS 增宽至 0.12 秒。","responseContext":{"type":"bowtie","bowtie":{"condition":{"tokens":[{"id":"cond_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia","en":"Prerenal acute kidney injury with life-threatening hyperkalemia","zh":"肾前性急性肾损伤并危及生命的高钾血症"},{"id":"cond_postrenal","en":"Obstructive post-renal acute kidney injury","zh":"梗阻性肾后性急性肾损伤"},{"id":"cond_atn","en":"Acute tubular necrosis","zh":"急性肾小管坏死"}],"correct":"cond_prerenal_aki_hyperkalemia"},"actions":{"tokens":[{"id":"act_insulin_before_calcium","en":"Give insulin and dextrose before calcium gluconate","zh":"先给予胰岛素和葡萄糖，再给予葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"act_oral_sps_vomiting","en":"Administer oral sodium polystyrene sulfonate despite active vomiting","zh":"即使正在呕吐，也给予口服聚苯乙烯磺酸钠"},{"id":"act_insulin_dextrose","en":"Administer regular insulin 10 units IV with 25 g dextrose per protocol","zh":"按方案给予普通胰岛素 10 units IV 合并葡萄糖 25 g"},{"id":"act_calcium_gluconate","en":"Administer calcium gluconate 1 g IV at the ordered/protocol rate","zh":"按医嘱/方案速度给予葡萄糖酸钙 1 g IV"}],"correct":["act_calcium_gluconate","act_insulin_dextrose"]},"parameters":{"tokens":[{"id":"param_hourly_urine_output","en":"Hourly urine output","zh":"每小时尿量"},{"id":"param_hemoglobin_trend","en":"Hemoglobin trend","zh":"血红蛋白趋势"},{"id":"param_ecg_morphology","en":"ECG morphology: PR interval, QRS duration, and T-wave changes","zh":"ECG 形态：PR 间期、QRS 时限和 T 波变化"},{"id":"param_urine_specific_gravity","en":"Urine specific gravity trend after IV fluids","zh":"IV 补液后的尿比重趋势"}],"correct":["param_ecg_morphology","param_hourly_urine_output"]}}},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The condition is prerenal AKI with immediately life-threatening hyperkalemia. The 72-hour GI fluid losses, hypotension/dehydration picture, concentrated urine, urine sodium 8 mEq/L, FENa 0.4%, low bladder volume, and acute creatinine rise support prerenal AKI rather than ATN or obstruction. The ECG progression with potassium 6.4 mEq/L makes calcium gluconate the first priority to stabilize the myocardium, followed promptly by insulin with dextrose to shift potassium intracellularly. ECG morphology and hourly urine output are the two most useful monitoring parameters for immediate cardiac toxicity and renal perfusion recovery.","rationaleCorrectZh":"最可能病情是肾前性 AKI 并立即危及生命的高钾血症。72 小时胃肠道液体丢失、低血压/脱水表现、尿液浓缩、尿钠 8 mEq/L、FENa 0.4%、膀胱容量低以及肌酐急升，支持肾前性 AKI，而不是 ATN 或梗阻。钾 6.4 mEq/L 合并 ECG 进展，使葡萄糖酸钙成为首先要做的措施，用于稳定心肌；随后立即给予胰岛素合并葡萄糖，使钾转入细胞。ECG 形态和每小时尿量分别是监测立即心脏毒性和肾灌注恢复最有用的两个参数。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In bow-tie items, pick the condition that explains the whole cluster, then choose actions that address the threat that can kill first and monitoring that proves the threat is resolving.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做 bow-tie 题时，先选能解释整个线索群的病情，再选处理最先致命威胁的措施，以及能证明威胁正在缓解的监测指标。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2563,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_fib_hf_net_balance_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,205],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,58],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews the 8-hour intake and output record below for a client with heart failure. Calculate the client's net fluid balance for the shift. Record the answer in milliliters (mL), including the sign.","fullStemZh":"护士查看下面一名心力衰竭患者8小时的出入量记录。计算该患者本班次的净体液平衡。以毫升（mL）记录答案，并注明正负号。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record the answer in milliliters (mL), including the sign.","terminalSentenceZh":"以毫升（mL）记录答案，并注明正负号。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Calculate the client's net fluid balance for the shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"计算该患者本班次的净体液平衡。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Net fluid balance","zh":"净体液平衡"},"acceptable":["+580","+580 mL","580","580 mL"],"numeric":{"value":580,"unit":"mL","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 360 + 240 + 500 + 100 = 1,200 mL. Output totals 560 + 60 = 620 mL. Net balance = 1,200 − 620 = +580 mL. A positive balance in heart failure requires continued assessment for fluid overload.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为360 + 240 + 500 + 100 = 1,200 mL。出量合计为560 + 60 = 620 mL。净平衡 = 1,200 − 620 = +580 mL。心力衰竭患者出现正平衡时，需要继续评估液体超负荷。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Add the intake column, add the output column, then subtract output from intake. Keep the sign of the result.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先将入量列相加，再将出量列相加，然后用入量减去出量。保留结果的正负号。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf Nursing Fundamentals: Fluids and Electrolytes; StatPearls Heart Failure and cardiogenic pulmonary edema monitoring","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2564,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_mc_pulmonary_edema_diuresis_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[151,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,58],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with cardiogenic pulmonary edema received an IV loop diuretic at 0800. The nurse reviews the intake and output record below at 1200. Which conclusion is best supported by the record?","fullStemZh":"一名因心源性肺水肿入院的患者在0800接受了静脉袢利尿剂。护士在1200查看下面的出入量记录。该记录最支持哪项结论？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which conclusion is best supported by the record?","terminalSentenceZh":"该记录最支持哪项结论？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the intake and output record below at 1200.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在1200查看下面的出入量记录。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The client is responding to diuresis; continue respiratory, electrolyte, and renal monitoring.","zh":"患者对利尿治疗有反应；继续监测呼吸状况、电解质和肾功能。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client has inadequate urine output and should receive an additional IV fluid bolus.","zh":"患者尿量不足，应再给予一次静脉补液。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client has a positive fluid balance and is at increased risk for worsening pulmonary edema.","zh":"患者呈正液体平衡，肺水肿恶化风险增加。"},{"id":"D","en":"The record cannot be interpreted until the provider prescribes a daily weight.","zh":"在医生开具每日体重医嘱前，无法解释该记录。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 180 mL and output totals 1,710 mL, giving a net balance of −1,530 mL. After a loop diuretic for pulmonary edema, a large negative balance indicates diuresis, but the nurse must continue monitoring respiratory status, electrolytes, and renal function.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为180 mL，出量合计为1,710 mL，净平衡为−1,530 mL。肺水肿患者使用袢利尿剂后出现明显负平衡，说明正在利尿；但护士仍需继续监测呼吸状况、电解质和肾功能。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After diuretic therapy, decide whether output exceeds intake, then connect that trend to both improvement and monitoring risks.","testTakingStrategyZh":"利尿治疗后，先判断出量是否超过入量，再把这个趋势与疗效和监测风险联系起来。","sourceMetadata":"StatPearls Cardiogenic Pulmonary Edema: diuresis monitoring with strict intake/output, electrolytes, and renal function","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2565,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_sata_gastroenteritis_deficit_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,47],"fullStemEn":"An older adult with gastroenteritis has the intake and output record shown below. Which assessment findings would be consistent with the fluid balance shown? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患胃肠炎的老年患者有如下出入量记录。哪些评估发现与图中所示的体液平衡一致？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which assessment findings would be consistent with the fluid balance shown?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些评估发现与图中所示的体液平衡一致？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Orthostatic dizziness","zh":"体位性头晕"},{"id":"F","en":"Decreased urine output","zh":"尿量减少"},{"id":"C","en":"Bounding peripheral pulses","zh":"外周脉搏洪大"},{"id":"D","en":"Concentrated urine","zh":"尿液浓缩"},{"id":"E","en":"New crackles at the lung bases","zh":"肺底新出现湿啰音"},{"id":"A","en":"Dry mucous membranes","zh":"黏膜干燥"}],"correct":["A","B","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 120 mL and output totals 1,270 mL, giving a net balance of −1,150 mL. This fluid deficit is consistent with dehydration cues such as dry mucous membranes, orthostatic symptoms, concentrated urine, and decreased urine output.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为120 mL，出量合计为1,270 mL，净平衡为−1,150 mL。此体液不足与脱水线索一致，如黏膜干燥、体位性症状、尿液浓缩和尿量减少。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For select-all fluid items, first decide whether the balance is positive or negative, then choose findings from the same direction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做体液相关的多选题时，先判断平衡是正还是负，再选择同一方向的体征。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual dehydration symptoms; NCBI Bookshelf Nursing Fundamentals urine output and dehydration cues","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2566,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_matrix_prerenal_aki_recheck_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[207,268],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,75],"fullStemEn":"A client with suspected prerenal acute kidney injury is reassessed after a provider-prescribed fluid challenge. The provider's reassessment goal is at least 240 mL of urine output during this 6-hour period. Using the record shown, classify each nursing interpretation.","fullStemZh":"一名疑似肾前性急性肾损伤患者在医嘱补液试验后接受复评。医生设定的复评目标是在这6小时内尿量至少达到240 mL。根据所示记录，对每项护理解释进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the record shown, classify each nursing interpretation.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据所示记录，对每项护理解释进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The provider's reassessment goal is at least 240 mL of urine output during this 6-hour period.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医生设定的复评目标是在这6小时内尿量至少达到240 mL。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Notify the provider that the urine output goal was not met.","zh":"通知医生尿量目标未达到。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Recognize that intake exceeded output during the reassessment period.","zh":"识别出复评期间入量超过出量。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Increase oral fluids because the client has a negative balance.","zh":"因患者为负平衡而增加口服液体。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Continue to monitor lung sounds while additional fluids are considered.","zh":"在考虑追加液体时继续监测肺音。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate interpretation","zh":"不适当解释"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate interpretation","zh":"适当解释"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 1,120 mL and output totals 210 mL, giving a net balance of +910 mL. The urine output did not meet the stated 240 mL goal, so provider notification is appropriate. Because intake exceeds output, the nurse should monitor for fluid overload while the response to fluids is evaluated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为1,120 mL，出量合计为210 mL，净平衡为+910 mL。尿量未达到题干中规定的240 mL目标，因此应通知医生。由于入量超过出量，在评估补液反应时，护士应监测液体超负荷。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the thresholds stated in the stem, then compare them with the visual. Do not assume the goal was met just because fluids were given.","testTakingStrategyZh":"使用题干给出的阈值，再与视觉资料比较。不要因为已经补液就假设目标已达到。","sourceMetadata":"StatPearls Acute Kidney Injury: urine output and renal-function monitoring during fluid challenge; NCBI Bookshelf Nursing Fundamentals","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2567,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_mc_postop_retention_priority_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Elimination & Comfort","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[186,227],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,52],"fullStemEn":"A client is 8 hours postoperative after the indwelling urinary catheter was removed. The client reports lower abdominal discomfort. The nurse reviews the intake and output record below. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名术后8小时的患者已拔除留置导尿管，主诉下腹部不适。护士查看下面的出入量记录。护士应首先采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应首先采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the intake and output record below.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看下面的出入量记录。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Restrict all oral fluids for the rest of the shift.","zh":"本班次剩余时间内限制所有口服液体。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document that urine output is adequate for the shift.","zh":"记录本班次尿量充足。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess for bladder distention and perform a bladder scan per protocol.","zh":"评估膀胱膨胀，并按流程进行膀胱扫描。"},{"id":"B","en":"Encourage the client to drink another liter of water immediately.","zh":"鼓励患者立即再喝1升水。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 1,500 mL and output totals 140 mL, giving a net balance of +1,360 mL. Very low urine output after catheter removal with lower abdominal discomfort suggests possible urinary retention. The nurse should assess the bladder and use a bladder scan according to protocol before giving more fluid or simply documenting the finding.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为1,500 mL，出量合计为140 mL，净平衡为+1,360 mL。拔除导尿管后尿量很少并伴下腹部不适，提示可能尿潴留。护士应先评估膀胱，并按流程进行膀胱扫描，而不是继续大量补水或仅记录。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When urine output is low after catheter removal, compare it with intake and symptoms; retention is an assessment problem before it is a fluid-intake problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"拔除导尿管后尿量低时，要结合入量和症状判断；尿潴留首先是评估问题，而不是单纯喝水问题。","sourceMetadata":"StatPearls Postoperative Urinary Retention: voiding after Foley removal and bladder-scan evaluation; NCBI Bookshelf Nursing Fundamentals","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2568,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_fib_postop_output_total_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[180,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,56],"fullStemEn":"A nurse is preparing to hand off care for a postoperative client with multiple drains. Using the intake and output record below, calculate the client's total output for the shift. Record the answer in milliliters (mL).","fullStemZh":"护士准备交接一名术后带有多个引流管的患者。根据下面的出入量记录，计算该患者本班次总出量。以毫升（mL）记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record the answer in milliliters (mL).","terminalSentenceZh":"以毫升（mL）记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the intake and output record below, calculate the client's total output for the shift.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据下面的出入量记录，计算该患者本班次总出量。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"Total output","zh":"总出量"},"acceptable":["620","620 mL"],"numeric":{"value":620,"unit":"mL","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Output totals 350 mL urine + 180 mL chest tube drainage + 90 mL Jackson-Pratt drainage = 620 mL. Intake is not needed because the question asks only for total output.","rationaleCorrectZh":"出量合计为尿液350 mL + 胸腔引流180 mL + JP引流90 mL = 620 mL。本题只问总出量，因此不需要计算入量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read the question carefully: if it asks for output only, do not subtract intake.","testTakingStrategyZh":"仔细读题：如果只问出量，就不要减去入量。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf Nursing Fundamentals: intake/output measurement and urine/drainage monitoring","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2569,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_sata_ckd_fluid_overload_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[150,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,42],"fullStemEn":"A client with chronic kidney disease has the intake and output record shown below. Which nursing actions are appropriate before the end of the shift? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名慢性肾病患者有如下出入量记录。本班次结束前哪些护理措施是适当的？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which nursing actions are appropriate before the end of the shift?","penultimateSentenceZh":"本班次结束前哪些护理措施是适当的？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Review scheduled fluid sources before hanging additional IV fluid.","zh":"在悬挂额外静脉液体前复核计划中的液体来源。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess lung sounds and oxygen saturation.","zh":"评估肺音和血氧饱和度。"},{"id":"C","en":"Report the positive balance with low urine output according to unit policy.","zh":"按科室流程报告正平衡伴尿量低。"},{"id":"B","en":"Compare the current weight with the previous daily weight.","zh":"将当前体重与前一日每日体重比较。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage rapid oral fluid intake to improve kidney perfusion.","zh":"鼓励快速大量口服液体以改善肾灌注。"},{"id":"F","en":"Assume the record is expected and take no further action.","zh":"认为该记录属预期情况，不采取进一步措施。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 880 mL and output totals 250 mL, giving a net balance of +630 mL. In chronic kidney disease, a positive balance with low urine output warrants assessment for fluid overload, comparison with daily weight, reporting per policy, and review of additional fluid sources.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为880 mL，出量合计为250 mL，净平衡为+630 mL。慢性肾病患者出现正平衡且尿量低时，应评估液体超负荷、比较每日体重、按流程报告，并在继续给予液体前复核其他液体来源。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In kidney disease, low output plus positive balance points toward overload risk; choose assessment and communication, not automatic fluid loading.","testTakingStrategyZh":"肾病中，低出量加正平衡提示超负荷风险；选择评估和沟通，而不是自动补液。","sourceMetadata":"NCBI Bookshelf Normal and Abnormal Urine Output; Nursing Fundamentals fluid balance monitoring","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2570,"bankPath":"banks/io-canonical.json","bankSha256":"2ce6488e65049ba00cd9dccf889a042e0a624f224387382d564d282e147b2645","topLevelQuestionId":"io_matrix_bowel_prep_deficit_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"matrix","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,45],"fullStemEn":"A client is completing bowel preparation for a colonoscopy. The nurse reviews the intake and output record below. Classify each nursing action.","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在为结肠镜检查进行肠道准备。护士查看下面的出入量记录。请对每项护理措施进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项护理措施进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the intake and output record below.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看下面的出入量记录。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Assess orthostatic vital signs and mucous membranes.","zh":"评估体位性生命体征和黏膜情况。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Encourage allowed clear liquids if not contraindicated.","zh":"如无禁忌，鼓励允许范围内的清流质。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Ignore the balance because stool output is expected during bowel preparation.","zh":"因肠道准备时排便增多属预期情况，所以忽略液体平衡。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Notify the provider of dizziness, hypotension, or inability to maintain intake.","zh":"如出现头晕、低血压或无法维持入量，应通知医生。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate action","zh":"适当措施"},{"id":"c2","en":"Inappropriate action","zh":"不适当措施"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake totals 1,290 mL and output totals 2,500 mL, giving a net balance of −1,210 mL. Stool output is expected with bowel preparation, but the net deficit still requires assessment for dehydration, encouragement of permitted clear liquids if safe, and provider notification for concerning symptoms or inability to maintain intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"入量合计为1,290 mL，出量合计为2,500 mL，净平衡为−1,210 mL。肠道准备时排便增多是预期情况，但净负平衡仍需要评估脱水、在安全情况下鼓励允许的清流质，并在出现相关症状或无法维持入量时通知医生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate expected output from safe response: even expected losses can become clinically important when intake does not keep up.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把“预期出量”与“安全应对”分开：即使是预期的丢失，当入量跟不上时也可能有临床意义。","sourceMetadata":"Merck Manual dehydration symptoms; Nursing Fundamentals intake/output and dehydration assessment","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2571,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_mc_potassium_furosemide_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[45,55],"fullStemEn":"A client with heart failure is scheduled to receive furosemide 40 mg IV now. The nurse reviews the trend shown in the visual before administering the medication. Which action should the nurse take?","fullStemZh":"一名心力衰竭患者现在准备接受呋塞米 40 mg 静脉给药。护士在给药前查看图中实验室趋势。护士应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the trend shown in the visual before administering the medication.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在给药前查看图中实验室趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the furosemide as scheduled and recheck potassium tomorrow.","zh":"按计划给予呋塞米，并明天复查血钾。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give the dose with a full glass of orange juice.","zh":"给药时让患者喝一大杯橙汁。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the dose temporarily and notify the provider of the potassium trend.","zh":"暂缓该剂量，并将血钾趋势通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request a sodium-restricted diet order before giving the medication.","zh":"给药前请求开立限钠饮食医嘱。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Potassium has fallen from low-normal to clearly low. A loop diuretic can further lower potassium, so the nurse should pause administration and notify the provider for replacement or revised orders.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钾已从低正常值下降到明显偏低。袢利尿剂可进一步降低血钾，因此护士应暂缓给药并通知医嘱开立者，以便补钾或调整医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Before giving a medication that changes an electrolyte, compare the current value with the direction of the trend.","testTakingStrategyZh":"给予会影响电解质的药物前，要同时看当前数值和变化方向。","sourceMetadata":"Adult laboratory reference ranges and loop diuretic safety monitoring; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2572,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_mc_sodium_decline_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[120,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,41],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with pneumonia becomes increasingly confused. The nurse reviews the serum sodium trend in the visual. Which provider prescription should the nurse question?","fullStemZh":"一名因肺炎入院的患者意识越来越混乱。护士查看图中的血钠趋势。护士应质疑哪一项医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which provider prescription should the nurse question?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应质疑哪一项医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the serum sodium trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的血钠趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Notify the provider of the change in mental status.","zh":"将意识状态改变通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"B","en":"Start 0.45% sodium chloride at 125 mL/hr.","zh":"以 125 mL/小时开始输注 0.45% 氯化钠。"},{"id":"C","en":"Recheck the serum sodium level in 2 hours.","zh":"2 小时后复查血钠。"},{"id":"A","en":"Place the client on seizure precautions.","zh":"为患者实施癫痫发作防护措施。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sodium is falling rapidly and the client has neurologic changes. Hypotonic IV fluid can worsen hyponatremia, so the nurse should question that prescription.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钠快速下降，且患者出现神经系统改变。低渗静脉液可能加重低钠血症，因此护士应质疑该医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a neurologic symptom appears with a sodium trend, avoid interventions that dilute sodium further.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当神经系统症状伴随血钠趋势变化时，应避免会进一步稀释血钠的干预。","sourceMetadata":"Adult laboratory reference ranges and hyponatremia safety principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2573,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_mc_creatinine_gentamicin_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[159,191],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,58],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving gentamicin for a complicated urinary tract infection has the next dose due now. The nurse reviews the renal laboratory trend in the visual. What is the nurse's best action?","fullStemZh":"一名因复杂性尿路感染正在使用庆大霉素的患者，现在应给予下一剂。护士查看图中的肾功能实验室趋势。护士最应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's best action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士最应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the renal laboratory trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的肾功能实验室趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the gentamicin because the infection is complicated.","zh":"因感染复杂，按时给予庆大霉素。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the dose and notify the provider of the worsening renal trend.","zh":"暂缓给药，并将肾功能恶化趋势通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request a stool culture before administering the medication.","zh":"给药前请求进行粪便培养。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give the dose and encourage the client to drink cranberry juice.","zh":"给予该剂量，并鼓励患者喝蔓越莓汁。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Gentamicin is nephrotoxic and requires renal monitoring. The visual shows a clear rise in creatinine and BUN, so the nurse should hold the dose until the provider evaluates the regimen.","rationaleCorrectZh":"庆大霉素具有肾毒性，需要监测肾功能。图中显示肌酐和尿素氮明显上升，因此护士应暂缓给药，等待医嘱开立者评估用药方案。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For nephrotoxic drugs, a worsening creatinine trend usually matters more than the scheduled administration time.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于有肾毒性的药物，肌酐恶化趋势通常比按时给药更重要。","sourceMetadata":"Adult renal laboratory ranges and aminoglycoside safety monitoring; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the renal laboratory trend in the visual.","controlSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的肾功能实验室趋势。"}
{"queueIndex":2574,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_matrix_sepsis_lactate_wbc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[72,143],"terminalOffsetsZh":[21,42],"fullStemEn":"A client with sepsis received IV fluids and broad-spectrum antibiotics. Use the laboratory trend in the visual to classify each interpretation.","fullStemZh":"一名脓毒症患者已接受静脉补液和广谱抗生素。根据图中的实验室趋势，对每项解读进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the laboratory trend in the visual to classify each interpretation.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据图中的实验室趋势，对每项解读进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with sepsis received IV fluids and broad-spectrum antibiotics.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名脓毒症患者已接受静脉补液和广谱抗生素。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The lactate pattern supports improving tissue perfusion.","zh":"乳酸变化支持组织灌注正在改善。"},{"id":"r2","en":"The WBC pattern supports movement toward the reference range.","zh":"白细胞变化支持正在向参考范围靠近。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The combined trend shows worsening sepsis that requires immediate escalation based on labs alone.","zh":"仅根据实验室趋势，综合变化显示脓毒症恶化，需要立即升级处理。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Ongoing monitoring is still needed because improvement is judged over time.","zh":"仍需持续监测，因为改善需要结合时间趋势判断。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Supported by the trend","zh":"趋势支持"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not supported by the trend","zh":"趋势不支持"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Both lactate and WBC are moving downward after treatment, which supports improvement while still requiring reassessment and monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"治疗后乳酸和白细胞均下降，支持病情改善，但仍需继续复评和监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For sepsis, falling lactate over time is a stronger outcome cue than one isolated lactate value.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在脓毒症中，乳酸随时间下降比单个乳酸值更能提示治疗反应。","sourceMetadata":"Adult laboratory ranges and sepsis response monitoring principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2575,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_matrix_inr_platelets_warfarin_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[80,172],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,52],"fullStemEn":"A client with deep vein thrombosis is taking warfarin. The evening dose is due. Use the lab trend in the visual to determine whether each nursing action is appropriate now.","fullStemZh":"一名深静脉血栓患者正在服用华法林，晚间剂量即将给药。根据图中的实验室趋势，判断每项护理行动此刻是否合适。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the lab trend in the visual to determine whether each nursing action is appropriate now.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据图中的实验室趋势，判断每项护理行动此刻是否合适。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The evening dose is due.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名深静脉血栓患者正在服用华法林，晚间剂量即将给药。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Give the scheduled warfarin dose now.","zh":"现在给予计划中的华法林剂量。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Assess gums, urine, stool, and skin for bleeding.","zh":"评估牙龈、尿液、粪便和皮肤是否有出血。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Administer an IM ketorolac injection for pain.","zh":"肌内注射酮咯酸止痛。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Notify the provider of the supratherapeutic INR trend before giving warfarin.","zh":"在给予华法林前，将 INR 超治疗范围的上升趋势通知医嘱开立者。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate now","zh":"此刻合适"},{"id":"c2","en":"Not appropriate now","zh":"此刻不合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The INR trend is rising above the usual therapeutic range, increasing bleeding risk. The nurse should assess for bleeding and notify the provider before administering more warfarin; IM NSAID injection is unsafe.","rationaleCorrectZh":"INR 趋势升至通常治疗范围以上，出血风险增加。护士应评估出血并在继续给予华法林前通知医嘱开立者；肌内注射 NSAID 不安全。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For anticoagulants, connect the lab trend to bleeding risk before deciding whether to give the next dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理抗凝药时，先把实验室趋势与出血风险联系起来，再决定是否给下一剂。","sourceMetadata":"Adult INR/platelet ranges and warfarin monitoring principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2576,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_or_hyperkalemia_progression_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[184,248],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,67],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute kidney injury has a potassium chloride-containing IV fluid infusing. The nurse reviews the potassium trend in the visual and notes new peaked T waves on telemetry. Place the nursing actions in the order they should be performed.","fullStemZh":"一名急性肾损伤患者正在输注含氯化钾的静脉液。护士查看图中的血钾趋势，并在心电监护上发现新的高尖 T 波。请按应执行的顺序排列护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in the order they should be performed.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按应执行的顺序排列护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the potassium trend in the visual and notes new peaked T waves on telemetry.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的血钾趋势，并在心电监护上发现新的高尖 T 波。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Place the client on continuous cardiac monitoring and assess rhythm.","zh":"为患者连接连续心电监护并评估心律。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider or rapid response team of worsening hyperkalemia with ECG changes.","zh":"将伴心电图改变的高钾血症恶化情况通知医嘱开立者或快速反应团队。"},{"id":"B","en":"Stop the potassium-containing IV fluid.","zh":"停止含钾静脉液。"},{"id":"E","en":"Prepare to administer prescribed insulin with dextrose to shift potassium intracellularly.","zh":"准备按医嘱给予胰岛素加葡萄糖，使钾转移入细胞内。"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepare to administer prescribed IV calcium gluconate.","zh":"准备按医嘱给予静脉葡萄糖酸钙。"}],"correct":["B","A","C","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The harmful potassium source should be stopped first. Continuous monitoring follows because ECG changes are present. The provider or emergency team must be notified, and prescribed calcium protects the myocardium before therapies that shift potassium into cells.","rationaleCorrectZh":"首先应停止正在输入的含钾来源。因已出现心电图改变，应立即持续监测。随后通知医嘱开立者或急救团队；按医嘱先用钙剂保护心肌，再使用促使钾进入细胞内的治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a trend shows a dangerous exposure is continuing, stop the source first, then monitor, notify, and implement ordered rescue therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当趋势显示危险因素仍在持续输入时，先停止来源，再监测、通知并执行医嘱抢救治疗。","sourceMetadata":"Adult potassium ranges and hyperkalemia emergency nursing priorities; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2577,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_or_aki_fluid_response_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[220,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,78],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with dehydration and prerenal acute kidney injury has been receiving isotonic IV fluids. The current assessment shows clear lung sounds and urine output 45 mL/hr. Use the renal lab trend in the visual. Place the nurse's actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名因脱水和肾前性急性肾损伤入院的患者一直在接受等渗静脉补液。目前评估显示肺音清晰，尿量 45 mL/小时。根据图中的肾功能实验室趋势，按顺序排列护士行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nurse's actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据图中的肾功能实验室趋势，按顺序排列护士行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Use the renal lab trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"目前评估显示肺音清晰，尿量 45 mL/小时。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Interpret and document that renal perfusion is improving.","zh":"解读并记录肾脏灌注正在改善。"},{"id":"D","en":"Update the provider and ask whether the plan should transition toward oral hydration or maintenance fluids.","zh":"向医嘱开立者汇报，并询问计划是否应转向口服补液或维持液。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess for fluid overload and confirm current urine output.","zh":"评估是否有液体过负荷，并确认当前尿量。"},{"id":"C","en":"Continue the prescribed fluid therapy while monitoring intake and output.","zh":"继续按医嘱补液，同时监测出入量。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The nurse first reassesses safety and urine output, then interprets the improving BUN/creatinine trend, continues ordered therapy with monitoring, and collaborates about the next plan.","rationaleCorrectZh":"护士先复评安全状况和尿量，再解读 BUN/肌酐改善趋势，随后在监测下继续执行医嘱，并与医嘱开立者协作调整下一步计划。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Use the nursing process: assess first, interpret the trend, continue safe ordered care, then communicate next-step recommendations.","testTakingStrategyZh":"运用护理程序：先评估，再解读趋势，继续安全执行医嘱，最后沟通下一步建议。","sourceMetadata":"Adult renal laboratory ranges and prerenal AKI fluid-response monitoring; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Use the renal lab trend in the visual.","controlSentenceZh":"目前评估显示肺音清晰，尿量 45 mL/小时。"}
{"queueIndex":2578,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_cloze_magnesium_decline_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"prioritize_hypotheses","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[67,130],"terminalOffsetsZh":[15,29],"fullStemEn":"A client with prolonged diarrhea reports tremors and palpitations. Complete the statement using the magnesium trend in the visual.","fullStemZh":"一名长期腹泻患者诉震颤和心悸。请根据图中的镁趋势完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement using the magnesium trend in the visual.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据图中的镁趋势完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with prolonged diarrhea reports tremors and palpitations.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名长期腹泻患者诉震颤和心悸。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The client is at greatest risk for {{1}}; the nurse should anticipate {{2}}.","zh":"该患者最主要的风险是 {{1}}；护士应预期 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"bleeding related to thrombocytopenia","zh":"与血小板减少相关的出血"},{"id":"o1","en":"dysrhythmias related to worsening hypomagnesemia","zh":"与低镁血症恶化相关的心律失常"},{"id":"o2","en":"fluid overload related to hypermagnesemia","zh":"与高镁血症相关的液体过负荷"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"administration of vitamin K","zh":"给予维生素 K"},{"id":"o2","en":"restriction of all oral and IV fluids","zh":"限制所有口服和静脉液体"},{"id":"o1","en":"prescribed magnesium replacement and cardiac monitoring","zh":"按医嘱补镁并进行心电监测"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The magnesium is trending downward to a low level. Hypomagnesemia can contribute to tremors, neuromuscular irritability, and dysrhythmias, so replacement and monitoring are expected.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血镁持续下降至偏低水平。低镁血症可导致震颤、神经肌肉兴奋性增加和心律失常，因此应预期补镁和监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match the symptom cluster to the direction of the electrolyte trend, then choose the intervention that corrects the deficit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将症状群与电解质趋势方向对应，再选择纠正缺乏的干预。","sourceMetadata":"Adult magnesium reference range and hypomagnesemia safety monitoring; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2579,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_cloze_calcium_thyroidectomy_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.8","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.8.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.8.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,152],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,43],"fullStemEn":"A client 18 hours after thyroidectomy reports tingling around the mouth and muscle cramps. Complete the statement using the calcium trend in the visual.","fullStemZh":"一名甲状腺切除术后 18 小时的患者诉口周麻木和肌肉痉挛。请根据图中的钙趋势完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement using the calcium trend in the visual.","terminalSentenceZh":"请根据图中的钙趋势完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client 18 hours after thyroidectomy reports tingling around the mouth and muscle cramps.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名甲状腺切除术后 18 小时的患者诉口周麻木和肌肉痉挛。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The trend is most consistent with {{1}}, so the priority assessment is {{2}}.","zh":"该趋势最符合 {{1}}，因此优先评估 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o2","en":"hypercalcemia from dehydration","zh":"脱水导致的高钙血症"},{"id":"o3","en":"normal postoperative variation without risk","zh":"无风险的术后正常波动"},{"id":"o1","en":"hypocalcemia from possible parathyroid injury","zh":"可能因甲状旁腺受损导致的低钙血症"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"airway patency and signs of laryngospasm","zh":"气道通畅情况和喉痉挛迹象"},{"id":"o2","en":"capillary refill in the operative-side hand","zh":"手术侧手部毛细血管再充盈"},{"id":"o3","en":"bowel sounds before oral calcium intake","zh":"口服钙前的肠鸣音"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"After thyroidectomy, falling calcium with tingling and cramps suggests hypocalcemia, which can progress to tetany and laryngospasm. Airway assessment is the priority.","rationaleCorrectZh":"甲状腺切除术后，血钙下降并伴口周麻木和痉挛，提示低钙血症，可能进展为手足搐搦和喉痉挛。优先评估气道。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After thyroid surgery, connect tingling or cramps with falling calcium and then prioritize airway risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"甲状腺术后出现麻木或痉挛时，要联想到血钙下降，并优先考虑气道风险。","sourceMetadata":"Adult calcium reference range and post-thyroidectomy hypocalcemia monitoring; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2580,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_fib_hemoglobin_drop_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.9","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.9.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.9.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,73],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative client has increasing dizziness when standing. Use the CBC trend in the visual. How many g/dL did the hemoglobin decrease from 0 hr to 12 hr? Enter the numeric value to one decimal place.","fullStemZh":"一名术后患者站立时头晕加重。请根据图中的全血细胞计数趋势回答：从 0 小时到 12 小时，血红蛋白下降了多少 g/dL？请输入保留一位小数的数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the numeric value to one decimal place.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入保留一位小数的数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"How many g/dL did the hemoglobin decrease from 0 hr to 12 hr?","penultimateSentenceZh":"请根据图中的全血细胞计数趋势回答：从 0 小时到 12 小时，血红蛋白下降了多少 g/dL？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"g/dL decrease","zh":"g/dL 下降值"},"acceptable":["2.4","2.4 g/dL"],"numeric":{"value":2.4,"tolerance":0.05,"unit":"g/dL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The hemoglobin at 0 hr is 11.8 g/dL and at 12 hr is 9.4 g/dL. The decrease is 11.8 - 9.4 = 2.4 g/dL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"0 小时时血红蛋白为 11.8 g/dL，12 小时时为 9.4 g/dL。下降值为 11.8 - 9.4 = 2.4 g/dL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For trend calculations, identify the requested analyte first, then subtract the later value from the earlier value when asked for a decrease.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做趋势计算时，先确认题目要求的分析物；若问下降值，用较早数值减去较晚数值。","sourceMetadata":"Adult hemoglobin/hematocrit reference ranges and postoperative bleeding surveillance; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"How many g/dL did the hemoglobin decrease from 0 hr to 12 hr?","controlSentenceZh":"请根据图中的全血细胞计数趋势回答：从 0 小时到 12 小时，血红蛋白下降了多少 g/dL？"}
{"queueIndex":2581,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_mc_platelets_heparin_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.10","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.10.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.10.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[155,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,53],"fullStemEn":"A client has been receiving unfractionated heparin for a pulmonary embolism. The next dose is due now. The nurse reviews the platelet trend in the visual. What action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名肺栓塞患者一直在接受普通肝素治疗，现在应给予下一剂。护士查看图中的血小板趋势。护士首先应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"What action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the platelet trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的血小板趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Administer the dose because the client has a pulmonary embolism.","zh":"因患者有肺栓塞，按时给予该剂量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold the heparin and notify the provider of the platelet trend.","zh":"暂缓肝素，并将血小板趋势通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give the heparin and apply prolonged pressure to injection sites.","zh":"给予肝素，并在注射部位延长按压时间。"},{"id":"D","en":"Request a dietary consult for foods high in vitamin K.","zh":"请求营养会诊，指导富含维生素 K 的食物。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The platelet count has dropped substantially during heparin therapy, which raises concern for heparin-induced thrombocytopenia. The nurse should hold further heparin and notify the provider.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在肝素治疗期间，血小板明显下降，提示可能发生肝素诱导性血小板减少。护士应暂缓继续给予肝素并通知医嘱开立者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a high-alert medication is due, compare the current lab with its trend before focusing only on the diagnosis being treated.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高警示药物给药前，要比较当前实验室值和趋势，不要只关注正在治疗的诊断。","sourceMetadata":"Adult platelet reference ranges and heparin-induced thrombocytopenia safety monitoring; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the platelet trend in the visual.","controlSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的血小板趋势。"}
{"queueIndex":2582,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_mc_ptt_heparin_infusion_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.11","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.11.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.11.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[126,180],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,40],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving a continuous IV unfractionated heparin infusion. The nurse reviews the coagulation trend in the visual. Which provider prescription should the nurse question?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在持续静脉输注普通肝素。护士查看图中的凝血趋势。护士应质疑哪一项医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which provider prescription should the nurse question?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应质疑哪一项医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the coagulation trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的凝血趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Increase the heparin infusion rate by 200 units/hr.","zh":"将肝素输注速度增加 200 单位/小时。"},{"id":"D","en":"Keep the client on bleeding precautions.","zh":"继续为患者实施出血预防措施。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the client for bleeding from gums, urine, stool, and IV sites.","zh":"评估患者牙龈、尿液、粪便和静脉穿刺处是否出血。"},{"id":"C","en":"Recheck the aPTT as prescribed after a rate change or hold.","zh":"在调整或暂停输注后按医嘱复查 aPTT。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The aPTT is rising and is already markedly elevated. Increasing the heparin infusion would increase bleeding risk and should be questioned.","rationaleCorrectZh":"aPTT 正在上升且已明显升高。增加肝素输注速度会增加出血风险，应予以质疑。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For titratable anticoagulants, the direction of the coagulation trend tells you whether increasing or decreasing the dose makes sense.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于可调整剂量的抗凝药，凝血指标的趋势方向能帮助判断应增加还是减少剂量。","sourceMetadata":"Adult coagulation monitoring and IV unfractionated heparin safety principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2583,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_mc_lactate_worsening_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.12","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.12.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.12.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,169],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,48],"fullStemEn":"A client with suspected sepsis received IV fluids and the first dose of antibiotics 6 hours ago. The nurse reviews the trend in the visual. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一名疑似脓毒症患者 6 小时前已接受静脉补液和第一剂抗生素。护士查看图中的趋势。哪项行动最优先？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项行动最优先？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider or rapid response team of worsening markers despite treatment.","zh":"将治疗后指标仍恶化的情况通知医嘱开立者或快速反应团队。"},{"id":"C","en":"Delay reassessment until the next scheduled morning laboratory draw.","zh":"等到下次计划的早晨抽血再复评。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage oral fluids and continue routine vital signs every 8 hours.","zh":"鼓励口服液体，并继续每 8 小时常规测量生命体征。"},{"id":"A","en":"Document expected improvement after antibiotics.","zh":"记录抗生素后出现预期改善。"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Lactate and WBC are rising despite initial treatment, suggesting worsening sepsis or inadequate tissue perfusion. Escalation is the priority.","rationaleCorrectZh":"尽管已开始治疗，乳酸和白细胞仍上升，提示脓毒症恶化或组织灌注不足。优先行动是升级处理。","testTakingStrategyEn":"After treatment begins, worsening trends are outcome cues that require escalation, not reassurance.","testTakingStrategyZh":"治疗开始后，恶化趋势是需要升级处理的结果线索，而不是令人放心的表现。","sourceMetadata":"Adult sepsis response monitoring and lactate interpretation principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2584,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_matrix_dka_potassium_glucose_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.13","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA)","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.13.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.13.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[86,150],"terminalOffsetsZh":[29,50],"fullStemEn":"A client with diabetic ketoacidosis has been receiving IV regular insulin and fluids. Use the lab trend in the visual to classify each interpretation.","fullStemZh":"一名糖尿病酮症酸中毒患者正在接受静脉普通胰岛素和补液治疗。根据图中的实验室趋势，对每项解读进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Use the lab trend in the visual to classify each interpretation.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据图中的实验室趋势，对每项解读进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client with diabetic ketoacidosis has been receiving IV regular insulin and fluids.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名糖尿病酮症酸中毒患者正在接受静脉普通胰岛素和补液治疗。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The glucose trend suggests the insulin is lowering serum glucose.","zh":"血糖趋势提示胰岛素正在降低血糖。"},{"id":"r2","en":"The potassium trend requires prompt follow-up before continuing insulin unchanged.","zh":"血钾趋势需要立即跟进，不能不加改变地继续胰岛素。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The falling potassium is expected and can be ignored because glucose is improving.","zh":"血钾下降是预期现象，因为血糖改善，所以可以忽略。"},{"id":"r4","en":"The client may need potassium replacement according to provider orders and ongoing monitoring.","zh":"患者可能需要按医嘱补钾并持续监测。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not supported by the trend","zh":"趋势不支持"},{"id":"c1","en":"Supported by the trend","zh":"趋势支持"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Glucose is improving, but potassium is falling to a low level during insulin therapy. This requires prompt potassium-focused follow-up rather than simply continuing therapy unchanged.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血糖在改善，但胰岛素治疗期间血钾降至偏低水平。这需要立即针对血钾进行跟进，而不是简单地不变继续治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In DKA, improving glucose does not mean the client is safe; always check potassium movement during insulin therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"在 DKA 中，血糖改善不代表患者已经安全；胰岛素治疗期间必须查看血钾变化。","sourceMetadata":"Adult DKA monitoring and potassium safety principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2585,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_matrix_neutropenia_wbc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.14","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"generate_solutions","stemPathEn":"questions.14.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.14.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[107,136],"terminalOffsetsZh":[31,44],"fullStemEn":"A client taking an immunosuppressant reports a sore throat. The nurse reviews the WBC trend in the visual. Classify each nursing action.","fullStemZh":"一名正在服用免疫抑制剂的患者诉咽痛。护士查看图中的白细胞趋势。请对每项护理行动进行分类。","terminalSentenceEn":"Classify each nursing action.","terminalSentenceZh":"请对每项护理行动进行分类。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the WBC trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的白细胞趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Place the client in a private room if available and reinforce hand hygiene.","zh":"如有条件将患者安排在单人间，并加强手卫生。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Notify the provider of sore throat with a falling WBC trend.","zh":"将咽痛伴白细胞下降趋势通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Encourage fresh flowers and raw fruits from visitors to improve intake.","zh":"鼓励访客带鲜花和生水果，以改善摄入。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Monitor temperature and assess for subtle infection signs.","zh":"监测体温并评估隐匿感染迹象。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Not appropriate now","zh":"此刻不合适"},{"id":"c1","en":"Appropriate now","zh":"此刻合适"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The WBC trend is falling to a low level while the client reports possible infection symptoms. Protective infection-prevention actions, monitoring, and provider notification are appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"白细胞趋势下降至低值，同时患者报告可能的感染症状。保护性感染预防措施、监测和通知医嘱开立者均合适。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When immune labs trend downward, choose actions that reduce organism exposure and detect infection early.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当免疫相关指标下降时，选择减少病原体暴露并早期发现感染的措施。","sourceMetadata":"Adult WBC reference ranges and neutropenia infection-prevention principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the WBC trend in the visual.","controlSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的白细胞趋势。"}
{"queueIndex":2586,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_or_gi_bleed_hgb_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.15","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.15.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.15.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[131,166],"terminalOffsetsZh":[37,48],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted for a gastrointestinal bleed becomes lightheaded when sitting up. The nurse reviews the CBC trend in the visual. Place the nursing actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名因胃肠道出血入院的患者坐起时感到头晕。护士查看图中的全血细胞计数趋势。请按顺序排列护理行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the nursing actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列护理行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the CBC trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的全血细胞计数趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Prepare to obtain type and screen or type and crossmatch as prescribed.","zh":"准备按医嘱采集血型筛查或交叉配血标本。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess airway, breathing, circulation, vital signs, and level of consciousness.","zh":"评估气道、呼吸、循环、生命体征和意识水平。"},{"id":"B","en":"Notify the provider of symptomatic decline with falling hemoglobin and hematocrit.","zh":"将有症状恶化并伴血红蛋白和血细胞比容下降的情况通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"D","en":"Maintain IV access and prepare for prescribed fluid or blood product administration.","zh":"维持静脉通路，并准备按医嘱给予液体或血制品。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assessment comes first because the client is symptomatic. The nurse then escalates the falling CBC trend, obtains ordered blood bank testing, and maintains access for ordered resuscitation or transfusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者已有症状，首先应评估。随后护士应报告 CBC 下降趋势，按医嘱进行血库相关检测，并维持静脉通路以便按医嘱复苏或输血。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For bleeding trends, assess stability first, then escalate and prepare for ordered replacement therapy.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到出血趋势时，先评估稳定性，再升级报告并准备按医嘱补充治疗。","sourceMetadata":"Adult CBC interpretation and GI bleeding nursing priorities; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2587,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_or_hypercalcemia_progression_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.16","itemType":"ordered_response","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.16.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.16.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[173,200],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,61],"fullStemEn":"An older adult taking calcium carbonate and vitamin D supplements reports constipation, thirst, and increasing confusion. The nurse reviews the calcium trend in the visual. Place the actions in order.","fullStemZh":"一名正在服用碳酸钙和维生素 D 补充剂的老年患者报告便秘、口渴和意识越来越混乱。护士查看图中的血钙趋势。请按顺序排列行动。","terminalSentenceEn":"Place the actions in order.","terminalSentenceZh":"请按顺序排列行动。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the calcium trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的血钙趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"ordered_response","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Prepare to administer prescribed isotonic IV fluids if not contraindicated.","zh":"若无禁忌，准备按医嘱给予等渗静脉液体。"},{"id":"C","en":"Notify the provider of symptomatic worsening hypercalcemia.","zh":"将有症状且恶化的高钙血症通知医嘱开立者。"},{"id":"B","en":"Hold calcium and vitamin D supplements pending provider direction.","zh":"在医嘱开立者进一步指示前暂缓钙剂和维生素 D 补充剂。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess neurologic status, cardiac rhythm, hydration status, and fall risk.","zh":"评估神经状态、心律、水合状态和跌倒风险。"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Assessment comes first because the client is symptomatic. The nurse should stop ongoing calcium exposure pending direction, notify the provider, and prepare for ordered therapy such as isotonic fluids if appropriate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者已有症状，首先应评估。护士应在进一步指示前停止持续钙摄入，通知医嘱开立者，并准备按医嘱实施治疗，例如在合适时给予等渗液。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a lab trend worsens because of a possible intake source, assess first, stop the source if safe to hold, notify, then prepare ordered treatment.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当实验室趋势可能因摄入来源而恶化时，先评估；若可安全暂缓则停止来源；再通知并准备医嘱治疗。","sourceMetadata":"Adult calcium reference range and hypercalcemia nursing priorities; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2588,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_cloze_sodium_overcorrection_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.17","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"evaluate_outcomes","stemPathEn":"questions.17.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.17.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[136,159],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,44],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with severe hyponatremia is receiving prescribed hypertonic saline. The nurse reviews the sodium trend in the visual. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一名因严重低钠血症入院的患者正在按医嘱接受高渗盐水。护士查看图中的血钠趋势。请完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the sodium trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的血钠趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The trend suggests {{1}}, so the nurse should {{2}}.","zh":"该趋势提示 {{1}}，因此护士应 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o1","en":"possible overly rapid sodium correction","zh":"可能存在血钠纠正过快"},{"id":"o3","en":"worsening dilutional hyponatremia","zh":"稀释性低钠血症恶化"},{"id":"o2","en":"expected slow correction without concern","zh":"无须担心的预期缓慢纠正"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"stop all neurologic checks because the final sodium is near normal","zh":"因最终血钠接近正常，停止所有神经系统检查"},{"id":"o2","en":"increase the hypertonic saline rate to normalize sodium faster","zh":"增加高渗盐水速度，使血钠更快正常化"},{"id":"o1","en":"notify the provider and anticipate reassessment of the infusion plan","zh":"通知医嘱开立者，并预期重新评估输注方案"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The sodium rises from 118 to 134 mEq/L over 12 hours, a large rapid increase. The nurse should notify the provider because overly rapid correction can cause neurologic harm.","rationaleCorrectZh":"血钠在 12 小时内从 118 升至 134 mEq/L，升幅大且快速。护士应通知医嘱开立者，因为纠正过快可能造成神经系统损害。","testTakingStrategyEn":"With sodium correction, do not judge safety only by whether the final value looks normal; evaluate how fast it changed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"判断血钠纠正是否安全时，不要只看最终值是否接近正常，还要看变化速度。","sourceMetadata":"Adult hyponatremia correction safety principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2589,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_cloze_inr_amiodarone_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.18","itemType":"dropdown_cloze","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.18.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.18.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[103,126],"terminalOffsetsZh":[40,46],"fullStemEn":"A client taking warfarin started amiodarone 1 week ago. The nurse reviews the INR trend in the visual. Complete the statement.","fullStemZh":"一名正在服用华法林的患者 1 周前开始使用胺碘酮。护士查看图中的 INR 趋势。请完成句子。","terminalSentenceEn":"Complete the statement.","terminalSentenceZh":"请完成句子。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the INR trend in the visual.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看图中的 INR 趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"dropdown_cloze","clozeStem":{"en":"The trend indicates increased risk for {{1}}; the nurse should prioritize {{2}}.","zh":"该趋势提示 {{1}} 风险增加；护士应优先 {{2}}。"},"dropdowns":[{"id":"1","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"hypoglycemia from insulin excess","zh":"胰岛素过量导致的低血糖"},{"id":"o2","en":"thrombosis from subtherapeutic anticoagulation","zh":"抗凝不足导致的血栓形成"},{"id":"o1","en":"bleeding from excessive anticoagulation","zh":"抗凝过强导致的出血"}],"correct":"o1"},{"id":"2","options":[{"id":"o3","en":"administering the next warfarin dose early","zh":"提前给予下一剂华法林"},{"id":"o2","en":"teaching the client to increase leafy green vegetables immediately","zh":"指导患者立即大量增加绿叶蔬菜"},{"id":"o1","en":"assessing for bleeding and notifying the provider before the next warfarin dose","zh":"评估出血，并在下一剂华法林前通知医嘱开立者"}],"correct":"o1"}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The INR is rising after a new medication was added and is now supratherapeutic. The nurse should assess for bleeding and notify the provider before giving more warfarin.","rationaleCorrectZh":"加用新药后 INR 持续上升，目前已超治疗范围。护士应评估出血，并在继续给予华法林前通知医嘱开立者。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When a new medication is added to warfarin, trend the INR and connect a rising value to bleeding risk.","testTakingStrategyZh":"华法林治疗中加用新药时，要追踪 INR 趋势，并将上升值与出血风险联系起来。","sourceMetadata":"Warfarin monitoring and medication interaction safety principles; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"normalizedTerminalEqualsClozeStem":false,"normalizedTerminalContainedInClozeStem":false,"clozeStemContainedInStem":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2590,"bankPath":"banks/lab-canonical.json","bankSha256":"1038cb68f6b91f6a2c981562d97ad9e16179db9b1332c75725fd538595c44b05","topLevelQuestionId":"gpt_u3_labtrend_2026_06_09_b_fib_creatinine_increase_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.19","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.19.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.19.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[175,220],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,77],"fullStemEn":"A client receiving IV contrast yesterday has decreasing urine output. Use the renal lab trend in the visual. By how many mg/dL did the creatinine increase from 0 hr to 24 hr? Enter the numeric value to one decimal place.","fullStemZh":"一名昨天接受静脉造影剂的患者尿量减少。请根据图中的肾功能实验室趋势回答：从 0 小时到 24 小时，肌酐升高了多少 mg/dL？请输入保留一位小数的数字。","terminalSentenceEn":"Enter the numeric value to one decimal place.","terminalSentenceZh":"请输入保留一位小数的数字。","penultimateSentenceEn":"By how many mg/dL did the creatinine increase from 0 hr to 24 hr?","penultimateSentenceZh":"请根据图中的肾功能实验室趋势回答：从 0 小时到 24 小时，肌酐升高了多少 mg/dL？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mg/dL increase","zh":"mg/dL 升高值"},"acceptable":["0.9","0.9 mg/dL"],"numeric":{"value":0.9,"tolerance":0.05,"unit":"mg/dL"}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The creatinine is 0.8 mg/dL at 0 hr and 1.7 mg/dL at 24 hr. The increase is 1.7 - 0.8 = 0.9 mg/dL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"0 小时肌酐为 0.8 mg/dL，24 小时为 1.7 mg/dL。升高值为 1.7 - 0.8 = 0.9 mg/dL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For lab-change questions, identify the requested analyte first, then subtract the starting value from the ending value when asked for an increase.","testTakingStrategyZh":"做实验室变化题时，先确认题目要求的指标；若问升高值，用结束值减去起始值。","sourceMetadata":"Adult renal laboratory ranges and AKI surveillance after contrast exposure; review before promotion.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2591,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_av_nodal_blockers_1600_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,218],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,66],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews the medication administration record before the 1600 medication pass for an adult client on telemetry. The client's heart rate is 58/min and blood pressure is 108/62 mm Hg. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"护士在1600给药前查看一名成人遥测监护患者的药物给药记录。患者心率为58次/分，血压为108/62 mm Hg。哪项措施是首要的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施是首要的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's heart rate is 58/min and blood pressure is 108/62 mm Hg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者心率为58次/分，血压为108/62 mm Hg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer both 1600 medications because they were tolerated earlier in the day.","zh":"因当天早些时候患者耐受良好，所以给予两种1600药物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Give the calcium channel blocker first and reassess the beta-blocker in 30 minutes.","zh":"先给予钙通道阻滞剂，30分钟后再评估β受体阻滞剂。"},{"id":"C","en":"Hold all antihypertensive medications for the rest of the shift.","zh":"本班次剩余时间停用所有降压药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess the apical pulse and blood pressure against the prescribed hold parameters before giving the due cardiac medications.","zh":"在给予到时的心脏药物前，根据医嘱停药参数评估心尖脉和血压。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows metoprolol and diltiazem are both due at 1600. Both can slow AV-node conduction and lower heart rate and blood pressure. With a heart rate of 58/min, the nurse should assess against hold parameters and clarify if needed before administering the concurrent rate-lowering medications.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示美托洛尔和地尔硫卓均在1600到时。两者都可减慢房室结传导并降低心率和血压。心率58次/分时，护士应根据停药参数评估，必要时澄清医嘱，再给予这两种同时到时的降心率药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When two medications that slow the heart are due together, pause and assess the client's current heart rate and blood pressure before giving either one.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当两种减慢心率的药物同时到时时，先暂停并评估患者当前心率和血压，再决定是否给药。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed diltiazem labeling; MedlinePlus metoprolol drug information","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2592,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_lispro_meal_delayed_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[206,228],"terminalOffsetsZh":[65,73],"fullStemEn":"At 0730, a client with type 1 diabetes is alert and reports that the breakfast tray has not arrived. The capillary glucose is 92 mg/dL. The nurse reviews the MAR shown. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"0730，一名1型糖尿病患者清醒，并表示早餐餐盘尚未送达。毛细血管血糖为92 mg/dL。护士查看所示MAR。护士应采取哪些措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse take?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应采取哪些措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Ensure the breakfast tray or carbohydrate source is present before administering the rapid-acting dose.","zh":"在给予速效剂量前，确保早餐餐盘或碳水化合物来源已在场。"},{"id":"A","en":"Delay the rapid-acting insulin until the meal is available or clarify the order according to facility protocol.","zh":"在餐食可用前暂缓速效胰岛素，或按机构流程澄清医嘱。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give the insulin lispro now because it is marked due at 0730.","zh":"因为赖脯胰岛素标记为0730到时，所以现在立即给药。"},{"id":"F","en":"Hold all insulin doses for the rest of the day because the glucose is below 100 mg/dL.","zh":"因血糖低于100 mg/dL，所以当天剩余时间停用所有胰岛素。"},{"id":"C","en":"Continue to monitor the client's glucose if the meal remains delayed.","zh":"如果餐食继续延迟，继续监测患者血糖。"},{"id":"D","en":"Substitute the previous evening's insulin glargine for the due breakfast insulin.","zh":"用前一晚的甘精胰岛素替代到时的早餐胰岛素。"}],"correct":["A","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows insulin lispro, a rapid-acting insulin, due with breakfast. Because the meal is not available and the glucose is 92 mg/dL, the nurse should avoid giving the rapid-acting dose before food is available, continue monitoring, and follow protocol or clarify the order.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示赖脯胰岛素（速效胰岛素）随早餐到时。由于餐食尚不可用且血糖为92 mg/dL，护士应避免在食物可用前给予速效剂量，继续监测，并按流程处理或澄清医嘱。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Match insulin onset to food availability. Rapid-acting insulin without a meal is a hypoglycemia setup.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将胰岛素起效时间与食物可用性相匹配。无餐食时给予速效胰岛素容易导致低血糖。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed insulin lispro labeling; ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2593,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_enoxaparin_prior_held_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[133,174],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,46],"fullStemEn":"A client is receiving medication therapy for a pulmonary embolism. Before the 1800 medication pass, the nurse reviews the MAR shown. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在接受肺栓塞药物治疗。护士在1800给药前查看所示MAR。护士首先应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Before the 1800 medication pass, the nurse reviews the MAR shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在1800给药前查看所示MAR。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Replace the held enoxaparin with the scheduled oral stool softener.","zh":"用计划中的口服软便剂替代被暂缓的依诺肝素。"},{"id":"A","en":"Verify why the earlier anticoagulant dose was held and review the most recent safety parameters before giving the 1800 dose.","zh":"在给予1800剂量前，核实早前抗凝剂量被暂缓的原因，并查看最新安全参数。"},{"id":"C","en":"Document the held dose as a medication error and skip the 1800 dose.","zh":"将暂缓剂量记录为给药错误，并跳过1800剂量。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give the 1800 dose immediately because pulmonary embolism always requires uninterrupted anticoagulation.","zh":"立即给予1800剂量，因为肺栓塞总是需要不间断抗凝。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows the 0600 enoxaparin dose was held and the next dose is due at 1800. Because enoxaparin is a high-alert anticoagulant, the nurse should determine why the previous dose was held and review current safety data or parameters before administering another dose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示0600依诺肝素剂量被暂缓，下一剂1800到时。由于依诺肝素是高警讯抗凝药，护士应先确定前一剂暂缓原因，并查看当前安全数据或参数，再给予下一剂。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A held dose of a high-alert medication is a cue to investigate before the next scheduled administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"高警讯药物有暂缓记录时，应在下一次计划给药前先查明原因。","sourceMetadata":"ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings; anticoagulant administration standards","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2594,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_acetaminophen_duplicate_products_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[112,135],"terminalOffsetsZh":[32,40],"fullStemEn":"A postoperative adult reports incisional pain before the 1400 medication pass. The nurse reviews the MAR shown. Which action is safest?","fullStemZh":"一名术后成人患者在1400给药前诉切口疼痛。护士查看所示MAR。哪项措施最安全？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is safest?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施最安全？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the MAR shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看所示MAR。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hold all pain medication until the next shift.","zh":"停用所有止痛药直到下一班次。"},{"id":"B","en":"Give the scheduled acetaminophen and the PRN combination analgesic together because they have different names.","zh":"因两种药名不同，同时给予计划对乙酰氨基酚和PRN复方止痛药。"},{"id":"A","en":"Check the total acetaminophen received from all products before giving another acetaminophen-containing medication.","zh":"在给予另一种含对乙酰氨基酚药物前，核对患者从所有药品中已接受的对乙酰氨基酚总量。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer only the PRN combination analgesic and ignore the scheduled medication record.","zh":"只给予PRN复方止痛药，不理会计划用药记录。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows scheduled acetaminophen and a PRN hydrocodone-acetaminophen product. The nurse must recognize duplicate acetaminophen exposure and check the total from all acetaminophen-containing products before administering more.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示计划对乙酰氨基酚和PRN氢可酮-对乙酰氨基酚复方药。护士必须识别重复的对乙酰氨基酚暴露，并在继续给药前核对所有含对乙酰氨基酚药品的总量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For pain medications, scan for combination products. The same ingredient can appear under more than one medication name.","testTakingStrategyZh":"处理止痛药时，要查找复方制剂。同一成分可能出现在多个药名下。","sourceMetadata":"FDA acetaminophen safety communication; DailyMed acetaminophen labeling","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2595,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_opioid_benzodiazepine_due_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,52],"fullStemEn":"Before the 2200 medication pass, an adult client is difficult to keep awake and has a respiratory rate of 10/min. The nurse reviews the MAR shown. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"在2200给药前，一名成人患者难以保持清醒，呼吸频率为10次/分。护士查看所示MAR。哪项措施是首要的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施是首要的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the MAR shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看所示MAR。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer the 2200 medications because the client is sleeping and comfortable.","zh":"因患者正在睡眠且舒适，给予2200药物。"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the respiratory rate as expected after pain medication and continue routine care.","zh":"将呼吸频率记录为止痛药后的预期表现，并继续常规护理。"},{"id":"C","en":"Give the benzodiazepine first because anxiety can cause slow respirations.","zh":"先给予苯二氮䓬类药物，因为焦虑会导致呼吸变慢。"},{"id":"A","en":"Withhold the sedating due medications, assess sedation and respiratory status, and notify the provider according to protocol.","zh":"暂缓到时的镇静性药物，评估镇静程度和呼吸状态，并按流程通知医生。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows an opioid and a benzodiazepine due at 2200, with an opioid already given at 1800. The client's sedation and respiratory rate of 10/min indicate risk for respiratory depression. The nurse should withhold sedating doses, reassess, and notify the provider according to protocol.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示阿片类药物和苯二氮䓬类药物均在2200到时，且1800已给予过阿片类药物。患者嗜睡且呼吸频率10次/分，提示呼吸抑制风险。护士应暂缓镇静性剂量，重新评估，并按流程通知医生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Sedation plus a low respiratory rate is an acute safety cue. Do not add more CNS depressants.","testTakingStrategyZh":"镇静加呼吸频率低是急性安全线索。不要再增加中枢抑制药物。","sourceMetadata":"FDA opioid and benzodiazepine boxed-warning communications; ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2596,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_warfarin_antibiotic_bleeding_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,163],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,45],"fullStemEn":"A client taking chronic anticoagulation reports new gum bleeding before the evening medication pass. The nurse reviews the MAR shown. Which action is the priority?","fullStemZh":"一名长期抗凝治疗患者在晚间给药前报告新出现牙龈出血。护士查看所示MAR。哪项措施是首要的？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action is the priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪项措施是首要的？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the MAR shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看所示MAR。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Give the warfarin as scheduled because gum bleeding is expected during antibiotic therapy.","zh":"按计划给予华法林，因为抗生素治疗期间牙龈出血是预期现象。"},{"id":"A","en":"Assess for bleeding, review the most recent INR, and notify the provider before administering the evening anticoagulant.","zh":"在给予晚间抗凝药前，评估出血情况，查看最新INR，并通知医生。"},{"id":"C","en":"Stop the antibiotic independently and give the warfarin.","zh":"自行停用抗生素并给予华法林。"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer vitamin K immediately without contacting the provider.","zh":"不联系医生，立即给予维生素K。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows warfarin due in the same medication period as trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole therapy. New gum bleeding is a bleeding cue. The nurse should assess bleeding, review the INR, and notify the provider before giving the next warfarin dose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示华法林到时，同时患者正在接受复方新诺明治疗。新出现牙龈出血是出血线索。护士应评估出血、查看INR，并在给予下一剂华法林前通知医生。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Bleeding plus warfarin is never a routine pass. Check the INR and escalate before giving the next dose.","testTakingStrategyZh":"出血加华法林绝不是常规给药情境。给予下一剂前应查看INR并升级处理。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed warfarin labeling; warfarin interaction monitoring references","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2597,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_missed_antibiotic_followup_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"matrix","category":"Management of Care","topic":"Prioritization & Delegation","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[104,188],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,53],"fullStemEn":"At 0800, a nurse assumes care of a client being treated for suspected sepsis and reviews the MAR shown. For each possible nursing action, select whether it is appropriate or inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"0800，护士接手一名疑似脓毒症治疗患者的护理，并查看所示MAR。对于每项可能的护理措施，选择其是否适当。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each possible nursing action, select whether it is appropriate or inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项可能的护理措施，选择其是否适当。","penultimateSentenceEn":"At 0800, a nurse assumes care of a client being treated for suspected sepsis and reviews the MAR shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"0800，护士接手一名疑似脓毒症治疗患者的护理，并查看所示MAR。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Notify the provider or pharmacist that the 0600 IV antibiotic dose was missed and ask how to adjust the schedule.","zh":"通知医生或药师0600静脉抗生素剂量漏给，并询问如何调整给药时间表。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Give the missed 0600 antibiotic dose and the next scheduled antibiotic dose together.","zh":"将漏给的0600抗生素剂量和下一次计划抗生素剂量一起给予。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Assess the client for clinical deterioration and document the missed dose and follow-up actions.","zh":"评估患者是否有临床恶化，并记录漏给剂量及后续措施。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Ignore the missed dose because another dose is due later in the day.","zh":"忽略漏给剂量，因为当天稍后还有另一剂到时。"}],"columns":[{"id":"inappropriate","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不适当"},{"id":"appropriate","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["inappropriate"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["inappropriate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows the 0600 cefepime dose was missed. The nurse should assess the client, document accurately, and contact the provider or pharmacist for schedule guidance rather than doubling doses or ignoring the omission.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示0600头孢吡肟剂量漏给。护士应评估患者、准确记录，并联系医生或药师获取调整给药时间的指导，而不是加倍给药或忽略漏给。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a missed time-sensitive medication, think: assess, communicate, document, and do not double-dose without an order.","testTakingStrategyZh":"遇到漏给的时间敏感药物时，思路是：评估、沟通、记录；没有医嘱不要加倍给药。","sourceMetadata":"Medication administration standards; sepsis anti-infective timing principles","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2598,"bankPath":"banks/mar-canonical.json","bankSha256":"f12c03a28ff5b52411843f84bc942b4ca5667e989194357ed2d60a394f17641e","topLevelQuestionId":"mar_digoxin_low_pulse_due_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[130,197],"terminalOffsetsZh":[38,53],"fullStemEn":"Before the 0900 medication pass, the nurse obtains an apical pulse of 52/min in an adult client. The nurse reviews the MAR shown. For each action, select whether it is appropriate or inappropriate.","fullStemZh":"0900给药前，护士测得一名成人患者心尖脉为52次/分。护士查看所示MAR。对于每项措施，选择其是否适当。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each action, select whether it is appropriate or inappropriate.","terminalSentenceZh":"对于每项措施，选择其是否适当。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the MAR shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看所示MAR。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Hold the digoxin dose and notify the provider according to the prescribed parameters.","zh":"根据医嘱参数暂缓地高辛剂量并通知医生。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Give digoxin because the medication is marked due on the MAR.","zh":"因为MAR显示地高辛到时，所以给予地高辛。"},{"id":"r3","en":"Assess for dizziness, weakness, nausea, or visual changes before escalating the concern.","zh":"在升级处理前评估是否有头晕、乏力、恶心或视觉改变。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Give an extra dose of furosemide to raise the pulse before giving digoxin.","zh":"在给予地高辛前额外给予一剂呋塞米以提高脉搏。"}],"columns":[{"id":"appropriate","en":"Appropriate","zh":"适当"},{"id":"inappropriate","en":"Inappropriate","zh":"不适当"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["inappropriate"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["appropriate"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["inappropriate"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The MAR shows digoxin is due at 0900. An apical pulse of 52/min is a bradycardia cue. The nurse should hold the dose according to parameters, assess for possible digoxin toxicity or intolerance, and notify the provider rather than administering the dose solely because it is due.","rationaleCorrectZh":"MAR显示地高辛在0900到时。心尖脉52次/分是心动过缓线索。护士应按参数暂缓给药，评估可能的地高辛毒性或不耐受，并通知医生，而不是仅因到时就给药。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For digoxin, a low apical pulse before administration is a stop-and-check cue.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于地高辛，给药前心尖脉偏低是“暂停并核查”的线索。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed digoxin labeling; cardiac medication administration standards","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2599,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_heparin_infusion_rate_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[144,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[43,61],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders a heparin infusion at 1200 units/hour. Using the medication label shown, what rate should the nurse set on the infusion pump? Record your answer in milliliters per hour (mL/hr).","fullStemZh":"医嘱开具肝素输注速率为1200单位/小时。根据所示药物标签，护士应将输液泵设置为多少？以毫升/小时（mL/hr）记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record your answer in milliliters per hour (mL/hr).","terminalSentenceZh":"以毫升/小时（mL/hr）记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, what rate should the nurse set on the infusion pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，护士应将输液泵设置为多少？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["12","12 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":12,"unit":"mL/hr","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label contains 25,000 units in 250 mL, so the concentration is 25,000 ÷ 250 = 100 units/mL. To deliver 1200 units/hour, divide 1200 by 100: 12 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示250 mL中含25,000单位，因此浓度为25,000 ÷ 250 = 100单位/mL。要输注1200单位/小时，用1200除以100，得到12 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Reduce the label to units per mL first, then divide the ordered hourly units by that concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先把标签换算成每mL多少单位，再用医嘱每小时单位数除以该浓度。","sourceMetadata":"ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings; DailyMed heparin sodium injection labeling","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2600,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_morphine_iv_volume_002","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[78,158],"terminalOffsetsZh":[26,45],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders morphine sulfate 4 mg IV now for severe postoperative pain. Using the medication label shown, how many milliliters should the nurse prepare?","fullStemZh":"医嘱为术后重度疼痛患者立即静脉给予硫酸吗啡4 mg。根据所示药物标签，护士应准备多少毫升？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, how many milliliters should the nurse prepare?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，护士应准备多少毫升？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider orders morphine sulfate 4 mg IV now for severe postoperative pain.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为术后重度疼痛患者立即静脉给予硫酸吗啡4 mg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"0.4 mL","zh":"0.4 mL"},{"id":"A","en":"0.2 mL","zh":"0.2 mL"},{"id":"D","en":"2 mL","zh":"2 mL"},{"id":"C","en":"1 mL","zh":"1 mL"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label strength is 10 mg per 1 mL, or 10 mg/mL. The ordered dose is 4 mg, so 4 ÷ 10 = 0.4 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签规格为1 mL含10 mg，即10 mg/mL。医嘱剂量为4 mg，因此4 ÷ 10 = 0.4 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For dose-volume questions, use desired dose divided by available concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"剂量-体积题使用“所需剂量 ÷ 可用浓度”。","sourceMetadata":"ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings; DailyMed morphine sulfate injection labeling","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2601,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_potassium_chloride_rate_003","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[152,203],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,62],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders potassium chloride IV at 10 mEq/hour. Using the premixed medication label shown, what rate should the nurse set on the infusion pump? Record your answer in milliliters per hour (mL/hr).","fullStemZh":"医嘱为静脉输注氯化钾10 mEq/小时。根据所示预混药物标签，护士应将输液泵设置为多少？以毫升/小时（mL/hr）记录答案。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record your answer in milliliters per hour (mL/hr).","terminalSentenceZh":"以毫升/小时（mL/hr）记录答案。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the premixed medication label shown, what rate should the nurse set on the infusion pump?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示预混药物标签，护士应将输液泵设置为多少？","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL/hr","zh":"毫升/小时"},"acceptable":["50","50 mL/hr"],"numeric":{"value":50,"unit":"mL/hr","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The premix contains 20 mEq in 100 mL, so the concentration is 20 ÷ 100 = 0.2 mEq/mL. To infuse 10 mEq/hour: 10 ÷ 0.2 = 50 mL/hr.","rationaleCorrectZh":"预混液100 mL中含20 mEq，因此浓度为20 ÷ 100 = 0.2 mEq/mL。要输注10 mEq/小时：10 ÷ 0.2 = 50 mL/hr。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Keep mEq as the dose unit. Do not convert units; convert only the label amount into mEq per mL.","testTakingStrategyZh":"保持mEq为剂量单位，不做跨单位换算；只把标签换算成每mL含多少mEq。","sourceMetadata":"ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings; DailyMed potassium chloride injection labeling","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2602,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_enoxaparin_volume_004","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[62,145],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,41],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously once daily. Using the medication label shown, how many milliliters should the nurse administer?","fullStemZh":"医嘱为依诺肝素40 mg皮下注射，每日一次。根据所示药物标签，护士应给药多少毫升？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, how many milliliters should the nurse administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，护士应给药多少毫升？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider orders enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously once daily.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为依诺肝素40 mg皮下注射，每日一次。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"0.4 mL","zh":"0.4 mL"},{"id":"A","en":"0.2 mL","zh":"0.2 mL"},{"id":"C","en":"1 mL","zh":"1 mL"},{"id":"D","en":"4 mL","zh":"4 mL"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label concentration is 100 mg/mL. The ordered dose is 40 mg, so 40 ÷ 100 = 0.4 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签浓度为100 mg/mL。医嘱剂量为40 mg，因此40 ÷ 100 = 0.4 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the label is a simple mg/mL concentration, divide the ordered mg by mg per mL.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当标签为简单的mg/mL浓度时，用医嘱mg数除以每mL的mg数。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed Lovenox/enoxaparin sodium injection labeling; ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2603,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_digoxin_tablets_005","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,52],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders digoxin 250 mcg PO once daily. The nurse confirms the apical pulse is within the prescribed parameters. Using the medication label shown, how many tablets should the nurse administer?","fullStemZh":"医嘱为地高辛250 mcg口服，每日一次。护士确认心尖脉搏符合医嘱参数。根据所示药物标签，护士应给几片？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, how many tablets should the nurse administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，护士应给几片？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse confirms the apical pulse is within the prescribed parameters.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士确认心尖脉搏符合医嘱参数。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"tablets","zh":"片"},"acceptable":["2","2 tablets"],"numeric":{"value":2,"unit":"tablets","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Each tablet contains 125 mcg. The ordered dose is 250 mcg. 250 ÷ 125 = 2 tablets.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每片含125 mcg。医嘱剂量为250 mcg。250 ÷ 125 = 2片。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Do not convert units when the order and label already match. Divide mcg ordered by mcg per tablet.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当医嘱和标签单位已经一致时，不要换算单位。用医嘱mcg数除以每片mcg数。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed digoxin tablet labeling; medication administration safety standards","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2604,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_cephalexin_capsules_006","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[44,124],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,36],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders cephalexin 500 mg PO now. Using the medication label shown, how many capsules should the nurse administer?","fullStemZh":"医嘱为立即口服头孢氨苄500 mg。根据所示药物标签，护士应给几粒胶囊？","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, how many capsules should the nurse administer?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，护士应给几粒胶囊？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider orders cephalexin 500 mg PO now.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为立即口服头孢氨苄500 mg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"4 capsules","zh":"4粒胶囊"},{"id":"A","en":"1 capsule","zh":"1粒胶囊"},{"id":"B","en":"2 capsules","zh":"2粒胶囊"},{"id":"C","en":"3 capsules","zh":"3粒胶囊"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label shows 250 mg per capsule. The ordered dose is 500 mg. 500 ÷ 250 = 2 capsules.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示每粒胶囊250 mg。医嘱剂量为500 mg。500 ÷ 250 = 2粒胶囊。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For tablets or capsules, divide the ordered dose by the dose in one unit.","testTakingStrategyZh":"片剂或胶囊题，用医嘱剂量除以每一单位药物的剂量。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed cephalexin capsule labeling; medication administration calculation standards","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2605,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_furosemide_matrix_007","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"matrix","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[43,139],"terminalOffsetsZh":[18,44],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders furosemide 40 mg IV now. Using the medication label shown, classify each calculation statement as accurate or inaccurate.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为立即静脉给予呋塞米40 mg。根据所示药物标签，判断每项计算陈述是准确还是不准确。","terminalSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, classify each calculation statement as accurate or inaccurate.","terminalSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，判断每项计算陈述是准确还是不准确。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A provider orders furosemide 40 mg IV now.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱为立即静脉给予呋塞米40 mg。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"The concentration is 10 mg/mL.","zh":"浓度为10 mg/mL。"},{"id":"r2","en":"The nurse should prepare 2 mL.","zh":"护士应准备2 mL。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The nurse should prepare 4 mL.","zh":"护士应准备4 mL。"},{"id":"r4","en":"One 2-mL vial contains the full ordered dose.","zh":"一支2 mL小瓶含有完整医嘱剂量。"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"Accurate","zh":"准确"},{"id":"c2","en":"Inaccurate","zh":"不准确"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label shows 20 mg in 2 mL, which equals 10 mg/mL. A 40 mg dose requires 40 ÷ 10 = 4 mL. One 2-mL vial contains 20 mg, not the full 40 mg dose.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示2 mL中含20 mg，即10 mg/mL。40 mg剂量需要40 ÷ 10 = 4 mL。一支2 mL小瓶含20 mg，不是完整的40 mg剂量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"In matrix calculations, verify the concentration first, then test each statement against that concentration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"矩阵计算题先确认浓度，再用该浓度逐项核对陈述。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed furosemide injection labeling; medication administration calculation standards","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2606,"bankPath":"banks/medlabel-canonical.json","bankSha256":"cc3bd0053516fc7ea4b23e814e46f186e6d2dbf40888fa713a862c07ea2b3993","topLevelQuestionId":"medlbl_regular_insulin_volume_008","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"fill_in_blank","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,55],"fullStemEn":"A provider orders regular insulin 12 units subcutaneously before breakfast. Using the medication label shown, calculate the equivalent volume. Record your answer in milliliters (mL) to the nearest hundredth.","fullStemZh":"医嘱为早餐前皮下注射常规胰岛素12单位。根据所示药物标签，计算等效体积。以毫升（mL）记录答案，保留到百分位。","terminalSentenceEn":"Record your answer in milliliters (mL) to the nearest hundredth.","terminalSentenceZh":"以毫升（mL）记录答案，保留到百分位。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Using the medication label shown, calculate the equivalent volume.","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据所示药物标签，计算等效体积。","responseContext":{"type":"fill_in_blank","blanks":[{"prompt":{"en":"mL","zh":"毫升"},"acceptable":["0.12","0.12 mL"],"numeric":{"value":0.12,"unit":"mL","tolerance":0}}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The label contains 1000 units in 10 mL, or 100 units/mL. The ordered dose is 12 units, so 12 ÷ 100 = 0.12 mL.","rationaleCorrectZh":"标签显示10 mL中含1000单位，即100单位/mL。医嘱剂量为12单位，因此12 ÷ 100 = 0.12 mL。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For U-100 insulin, confirm the label concentration and keep the answer in mL only when the question explicitly asks for mL.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于U-100胰岛素，先确认标签浓度；只有题目明确要求mL时才以mL作答。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed Humulin R/regular insulin U-100 labeling; ISMP High-Alert Medications in Acute Care Settings","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2607,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"rhy_sinus_brady_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[238,275],"terminalOffsetsZh":[73,84],"fullStemEn":"A nurse reviews the cardiac monitor for a client on a medical unit. The strip shows a regular rhythm with an upright P wave before every QRS complex, a constant PR interval of 0.16 s, a narrow QRS, and a ventricular rate of about 44/min. Which rhythm does the nurse document?","fullStemZh":"护士查看内科病房一名患者的心电监护。心律条显示节律规则，每个QRS波群前均有直立P波，PR间期恒定为0.16秒，QRS波群窄，心室率约44次/分。护士应记录为何种心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which rhythm does the nurse document?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录为何种心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The strip shows a regular rhythm with an upright P wave before every QRS complex, a constant PR interval of 0.16 s, a narrow QRS, and a ventricular rate of about 44/min.","penultimateSentenceZh":"心律条显示节律规则，每个QRS波群前均有直立P波，PR间期恒定为0.16秒，QRS波群窄，心室率约44次/分。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"First-degree atrioventricular block","zh":"一度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"D","en":"Normal sinus rhythm","zh":"正常窦性心律"},{"id":"A","en":"Sinus bradycardia","zh":"窦性心动过缓"},{"id":"B","en":"Junctional escape rhythm","zh":"交界性逸搏心律"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sinus bradycardia is a sinus rhythm with all the normal features of sinus origin - an upright P wave before every QRS, 1:1 conduction, a normal constant PR interval (0.12-0.20 s), and a narrow QRS - but at a rate under 60/min. A rate of about 44/min with otherwise normal sinus morphology meets that definition.","rationaleCorrectZh":"窦性心动过缓是一种窦性心律，具备窦性起源的所有正常特征——每个QRS前有直立P波、1:1传导、PR间期正常且恒定（0.12-0.20秒）、QRS波群窄——但心率低于60次/分。心率约44次/分而其余形态正常的窦性心律即符合此定义。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Read the strip systematically: rate, rhythm regularity, P-wave presence/shape, PR interval, QRS width. The only abnormal feature here is rate, so the answer is the rhythm that differs from normal sinus only by being slow.","testTakingStrategyZh":"系统判读心律条：心率、节律是否规则、P波是否存在及形态、PR间期、QRS宽度。此处唯一异常的是心率，因此答案是仅以心率偏慢区别于正常窦性的那种心律。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2608,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"rhy_vtach_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"take_action","stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[249,271],"terminalOffsetsZh":[83,92],"fullStemEn":"A monitored client suddenly becomes unresponsive. The nurse confirms apnea and no palpable carotid pulse while the monitor displays the rhythm shown (wide-complex, regular, rate about 168/min). Which actions are appropriate immediate interventions? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名心电监护中的患者突然无反应。护士确认其呼吸停止、颈动脉搏动不可触及，同时监护仪显示如图所示的心律（宽QRS、规则、心率约168次/分）。哪些是恰当的即时干预措施？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions are appropriate immediate interventions?","penultimateSentenceZh":"哪些是恰当的即时干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Open the airway and provide ventilations with high-flow oxygen","zh":"开放气道并以高流量氧气给予通气"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer epinephrine 1 mg IV/IO and repeat every 3-5 minutes","zh":"静脉/骨内注射肾上腺素1毫克，每3-5分钟重复一次"},{"id":"E","en":"Administer adenosine 6 mg rapid IV push","zh":"快速静脉推注腺苷6毫克"},{"id":"A","en":"Begin high-quality chest compressions immediately","zh":"立即开始高质量胸外按压"},{"id":"D","en":"Perform synchronized cardioversion at 100 J","zh":"以100焦耳进行同步电复律"},{"id":"B","en":"Deliver an unsynchronized shock (defibrillation) as soon as the defibrillator is ready","zh":"在除颤仪准备就绪后立即给予非同步电击（除颤）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A wide-complex regular tachycardia in a pulseless, apneic client is pulseless ventricular tachycardia - a shockable cardiac arrest rhythm. ACLS care is immediate high-quality CPR, early defibrillation (an unsynchronized shock), epinephrine 1 mg every 3-5 minutes, and airway management with oxygenation/ventilation. Synchronized cardioversion and adenosine are treatments for selected pulse-present tachycardias, not for cardiac arrest.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无脉、无呼吸患者出现宽QRS规则性心动过速即为无脉性室性心动过速——一种可电击的心脏骤停心律。ACLS处理为立即高质量心肺复苏、尽早除颤（非同步电击）、每3-5分钟给予肾上腺素1毫克，以及气道管理与给氧通气。同步电复律和腺苷用于部分有脉搏的心动过速，而不是用于心脏骤停。","testTakingStrategyEn":"First decide pulse vs no pulse. 'Pulseless' moves you out of the stable/unstable-tachycardia algorithms (cardioversion, adenosine) and into cardiac-arrest care: CPR, defibrillation for shockable rhythms, epinephrine, and oxygenation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先判断有无脉搏。‘无脉’意味着脱离稳定/不稳定心动过速流程（电复律、腺苷），进入心脏骤停处理：心肺复苏、对可电击心律除颤、肾上腺素及给氧。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2609,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"rhy_afib_001","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"matrix","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":"analyze_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,287],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,88],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with the rhythm shown (no organized P waves, an irregularly irregular ventricular response at about 134/min, narrow QRS). For each assessment finding, indicate whether it is an anticipated finding for this rhythm or one that requires immediate provider notification.","fullStemZh":"一名患者入院时呈现如图所示的心律（无规整P波、心室反应绝对不规则、心率约134次/分、QRS窄）。请针对每一项评估结果，判断它属于该心律的预期表现，还是需要立即通知医生的表现。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each assessment finding, indicate whether it is an anticipated finding for this rhythm or one that requires immediate provider notification.","terminalSentenceZh":"请针对每一项评估结果，判断它属于该心律的预期表现，还是需要立即通知医生的表现。","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted with the rhythm shown (no organized P waves, an irregularly irregular ventricular response at about 134/min, narrow QRS).","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患者入院时呈现如图所示的心律（无规整P波、心室反应绝对不规则、心率约134次/分、QRS窄）。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Irregularly irregular radial pulse","zh":"桡动脉搏动绝对不规则"},{"id":"r2","en":"New facial droop with right-arm weakness and slurred speech","zh":"新发面部下垂伴右上肢无力及言语含糊"},{"id":"r3","en":"Apical-radial pulse deficit of 12 beats/min","zh":"心尖-桡动脉脉搏短绌12次/分"},{"id":"r4","en":"Blood pressure 84/52 mm Hg with lightheadedness and diaphoresis","zh":"血压84/52毫米汞柱，伴头晕和出汗"},{"id":"r5","en":"Client reports a sensation of fluttering palpitations","zh":"患者诉有心悸扑动感"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Requires immediate provider notification","zh":"需立即通知医生"},{"id":"c1","en":"Anticipated finding","zh":"预期表现"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r5","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Atrial fibrillation produces a chaotic atrial baseline with no organized P waves and an irregularly irregular ventricular response, so an irregularly irregular pulse, a pulse deficit (not every ventricular contraction perfuses to the radial artery), and palpitations are all anticipated. Findings that signal a complication demand urgent notification: focal neurologic deficits suggest an embolic stroke (a fibrillating atrium can throw a clot), and hypotension with lightheadedness and diaphoresis indicates hemodynamic instability from the rapid ventricular rate.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心房颤动产生杂乱的心房基线、无规整P波、心室反应绝对不规则，因此脉搏绝对不规则、脉搏短绌（并非每次心室收缩都能灌注到桡动脉）和心悸都属于预期表现。提示并发症的表现需要紧急通知：局灶性神经功能缺损提示栓塞性卒中（颤动的心房可形成血栓脱落），而低血压伴头晕、出汗提示快速心室率导致的血流动力学不稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the defining features of the rhythm itself (irregular pulse, pulse deficit, palpitations) from signs of its complications (stroke, hemodynamic instability). Expected rhythm features are documented; complication signs get the provider called.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把心律本身的特征（脉搏不规则、脉搏短绌、心悸）与其并发症的体征（卒中、血流动力学不稳定）区分开来。心律的预期特征只需记录，而并发症体征则需通知医生。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2610,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[93,208],"terminalOffsetsZh":[25,55],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the cardiac monitor of a client and notes the following rhythm strip. Which characteristic should the nurse identify as a requirement for classifying this rhythm as normal sinus rhythm?","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看患者的心电监护，并注意到以下心律条图。护士应将下列哪项特征识别为将该心律分类为窦性心律的必要条件？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which characteristic should the nurse identify as a requirement for classifying this rhythm as normal sinus rhythm?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应将下列哪项特征识别为将该心律分类为窦性心律的必要条件？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the cardiac monitor of a client and notes the following rhythm strip.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在查看患者的心电监护，并注意到以下心律条图。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"A QRS duration greater than 0.12 seconds","zh":"QRS波群时限大于0.12秒"},{"id":"D","en":"A heart rate between 50 and 90 beats per minute","zh":"心率在每分钟50至90次之间"},{"id":"A","en":"A PR interval between 0.12 and 0.20 seconds","zh":"PR间期在0.12至0.20秒之间"},{"id":"C","en":"An upright P wave following each QRS complex","zh":"每个QRS波群后都有一个直立的P波"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A normal sinus rhythm requires a PR interval of 0.12 to 0.20 seconds, representing the time it takes for the impulse to travel from the SA node through the AV node. The heart rate must be 60 to 100 bpm, QRS duration should be narrow (0.04 to 0.12 seconds), and each QRS complex must be preceded by (not followed by) a P wave.","rationaleCorrectZh":"正常的窦性心律要求PR间期在0.12至0.20秒之间，这代表冲动从窦房结传导通过房室结所需的时间。心率必须在60至100次/分之间，QRS时限应较窄（0.04至0.12秒），且每个QRS波群前（而不是后）必须有一个直立的P波。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the textbook criteria for normal sinus rhythm. Compare each option directly with normal ECG parameters (Rate: 60-100, PR: 0.12-0.20, QRS: <0.12). Eliminate options that misstate physiological values or sequences.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆教科书上关于窦性心律的标准。将每个选项直接与正常心电图参数（心率：60-100次/分，PR：0.12-0.20秒，QRS：<0.12秒）进行比较。排除错误表述生理数值或顺序的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse is reviewing the cardiac monitor of a client and notes the following rhythm strip.","controlSentenceZh":"护士正在查看患者的心电监护，并注意到以下心律条图。"}
{"queueIndex":2611,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,286],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,90],"fullStemEn":"A 22-year-old marathon runner is admitted for minor orthopedic surgery. The nurse notes the client's cardiac monitor shows the following rhythm. The client is resting comfortably, awake, alert, and oriented with a blood pressure of 118/72 mmHg. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名22岁的马拉松运动员因轻微骨科手术入院。护士注意到患者的心电监护显示以下心律。患者正舒适地休息，清醒，警觉，定向力完整，血压为118/72 mmHg。护士首先应该采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应该采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is resting comfortably, awake, alert, and oriented with a blood pressure of 118/72 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者正舒适地休息，清醒，警觉，定向力完整，血压为118/72 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Request an emergent 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG)","zh":"申请紧急12导联心电图（ECG）"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer atropine 1 mg intravenously","zh":"静脉注射阿托品 1 mg"},{"id":"D","en":"Document the finding and continue to monitor","zh":"记录该发现并继续监测"},{"id":"A","en":"Prepare the client for transcutaneous pacing","zh":"为患者准备经皮起搏"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sinus bradycardia is common and considered a normal physiological finding in well-conditioned athletes due to increased vagal tone. Since the client is completely asymptomatic and hemodynamically stable (normal blood pressure, awake, alert), no intervention is indicated. The nurse should document the finding and continue monitoring.","rationaleCorrectZh":"由于迷走神经张力增加，窦性心动过缓在身体状况良好的运动员中很常见，被认为是正常的生理表现。由于患者完全没有症状且血流动力学稳定（血压正常，清醒，警觉），因此无需进行干预。护士应记录此发现并继续监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the client's presentation: 'resting comfortably, awake, alert... blood pressure of 118/72'. This indicates hemodynamic stability. In NCLEX questions, stable, asymptomatic physiological variations in specific populations (like athletes) require monitoring and documentation, not intervention.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注患者的表现：“舒适地休息，清醒，警觉……血压为118/72”。这表明血流动力学稳定。在NCLEX考试中，特定人群（如运动员）中稳定的、无症状的生理变化只需要监测和记录，不需要干预。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2612,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_sata_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[310,332],"terminalOffsetsZh":[86,94],"fullStemEn":"The nurse in the telemetry unit responds to a monitor alarm indicating bradycardia. The client's ECG strip displays sinus bradycardia at 42 beats per minute. Which assessment findings would indicate to the nurse that the client is experiencing hemodynamic compromise and requires active clinical intervention? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"遥测病房的护士对心动过缓的监护仪报警做出响应。患者的ECG显示窦性心动过缓，心率为每分钟42次。下列哪些评估发现会向护士提示患者正在发生血流动力学受损并需要积极的临床干预？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which assessment findings would indicate to the nurse that the client is experiencing hemodynamic compromise and requires active clinical intervention?","penultimateSentenceZh":"下列哪些评估发现会向护士提示患者正在发生血流动力学受损并需要积极的临床干预？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Acute chest pain or discomfort","zh":"急性胸痛或不适"},{"id":"D","en":"Warm, dry skin with capillary refill of 2 seconds","zh":"皮肤温暖干燥，毛细血管充盈时间为2秒"},{"id":"A","en":"Blood pressure of 82/46 mmHg","zh":"血压为 82/46 mmHg"},{"id":"B","en":"Dizziness and lightheadedness upon sitting up","zh":"坐起时感到头晕和目眩"},{"id":"C","en":"Frequent premature ventricular contractions (PVCs) on the monitor","zh":"监护仪上出现频繁的室性期前收缩（PVC）"},{"id":"F","en":"Increased urine output of 60 mL/hour","zh":"尿量增加至每小时 60 mL"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hemodynamic compromise in bradycardia is marked by poor perfusion to vital organs. Signs include hypotension (BP < 90/60 mmHg), central nervous system signs (dizziness, syncope, confusion), cardiac perfusion issues (chest pain), and ventricular irritability (frequent PVCs) due to myocardial hypoxia. Dry, warm skin and normal urine output indicate preserved perfusion.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心动过缓导致的血流动力学受损以重要器官灌注不良为特征。体征包括低血压（血压 < 90/60 mmHg）、中枢神经系统症状（头晕、晕厥、神志不清）、心脏灌注不足（胸痛）以及由于心肌缺氧引起的心室易激惹（频繁的室性期前收缩/PVC）。皮肤温暖干燥和尿量正常表明灌注尚好。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze each option to see if it represents a sign of organ hypoperfusion (brain, heart, kidneys, skin) or cardiac instability. Select symptoms associated with 'compromise' (low BP, ischemia, hypoperfusion, irritability) and eliminate positive/normal findings.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析每个选项，看它是否代表器官（脑、心、肾、皮肤）灌注不足或心脏不稳定的征象。选择与“受损”相关的症状（低血压、缺血、灌注不足、易激惹），排除好的/正常的发现。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2613,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[217,331],"terminalOffsetsZh":[58,89],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing symptomatic sinus bradycardia with a heart rate of 38 beats per minute, reports feeling faint, and has a blood pressure of 80/42 mmHg. The nurse prepares to administer atropine intravenously. Which dose should the nurse administer first, in accordance with current emergency cardiovascular care guidelines?","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生有症状的窦性心动过缓，心率为每分钟38次，主诉头晕且血压为80/42 mmHg。护士准备静脉注射阿托品。根据最新的紧急心血管护理指南，护士首先应注射哪种剂量的阿托品？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which dose should the nurse administer first, in accordance with current emergency cardiovascular care guidelines?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据最新的紧急心血管护理指南，护士首先应注射哪种剂量的阿托品？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse prepares to administer atropine intravenously.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士准备静脉注射阿托品。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Atropine 1 mg IV push","zh":"阿托品 1 mg 静脉注射"},{"id":"A","en":"Atropine 3 mg IV push","zh":"阿托品 3 mg 静脉注射"},{"id":"B","en":"Atropine 0.5 mg IV push","zh":"阿托品 0.5 mg 静脉注射"},{"id":"C","en":"Atropine 0.1 mg IV push","zh":"阿托品 0.1 mg 静脉注射"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Current AHA guidelines recommend Atropine 1 mg intravenously as the first-line medication for symptomatic bradycardia. It can be repeated every 3 to 5 minutes, up to a maximum total dose of 3 mg. (Note: The first-line dose was increased from 0.5 mg to 1 mg in the 2020 AHA guidelines). Doses less than 0.5 mg to 1 mg can cause a paradoxical slowing of the heart rate due to central vagal stimulation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"目前的AHA指南推荐静脉注射阿托品 1 mg 作为有症状心动过缓的首选药物。可每3至5分钟重复一次，最大总剂量为3 mg。（注：2020年AHA指南中首剂剂量从0.5 mg增加到了1 mg）。小于0.5 mg至1 mg的剂量可能会因为中枢迷走神经刺激而导致心率出现矛盾性减慢。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that this question tests updated clinical guidelines (ACLS). Recall that the current recommended dose of atropine for bradycardia is 1 mg IV push. Eliminate historical (0.5 mg) or extreme (3 mg, 0.1 mg) values.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别出此题测试的是最新的临床指南（ACLS）。回忆当前针对心动过缓推荐的阿托品剂量是1 mg静脉注射。排除历史数值（0.5 mg）或极端数值（3 mg，0.1 mg）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2614,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[382,490],"terminalOffsetsZh":[100,127],"fullStemEn":"A client with a history of heart failure is admitted to the telemetry unit. The cardiac monitor shows the following rhythm. Upon review of the client's medication list, the nurse notes the client accidentally took several extra doses of their prescribed metoprolol succinate 100 mg daily. The client's blood pressure is 92/54 mmHg, and the client reports feeling slightly fatigued. Which drug does the nurse anticipate the provider to order if the condition deteriorates and atropine fails?","fullStemZh":"一名有心力衰竭病史的患者收治到遥测病房。心电监护仪显示以下心律。在查看患者的药物清单时，护士注意到患者不慎多服了几次每天开具的100 mg美托洛尔缓释片。患者血压为92/54 mmHg，主诉轻度疲劳。如果病情恶化且阿托品无效，护士预期医生会开具哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which drug does the nurse anticipate the provider to order if the condition deteriorates and atropine fails?","terminalSentenceZh":"如果病情恶化且阿托品无效，护士预期医生会开具哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's blood pressure is 92/54 mmHg, and the client reports feeling slightly fatigued.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者血压为92/54 mmHg，主诉轻度疲劳。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Glucagon intravenously","zh":"静脉注射胰高血糖素"},{"id":"C","en":"Naloxone intravenously","zh":"静脉注射纳洛酮"},{"id":"B","en":"Calcium gluconate intravenously","zh":"静脉注射葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"A","en":"Digoxin immune Fab intravenously","zh":"静脉注射地高辛免疫Fab"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Metoprolol is a beta-blocker, and metoprolol toxicity/overdose presents as severe bradycardia and hypotension. When atropine is ineffective, glucagon is the specific antidote of choice for beta-blocker overdose. Glucagon bypasses the blocked beta-adrenergic receptors and stimulates adenyl cyclase directly, increasing cyclic AMP and producing positive inotropic and chronotropic effects.","rationaleCorrectZh":"美托洛尔是一种β受体阻滞剂，美托洛尔中毒/过量表现为严重的心动过缓和低血压。当阿托品无效时，胰高血糖素是β受体阻滞剂过量的首选特异性解毒剂。胰高血糖素绕过被阻断的β肾上腺素能受体，直接刺激腺苷酸环化酶，从而增加环磷酸腺苷（cAMP），产生正性肌力和正性频率作用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the drug class from the stem: metoprolol is a beta-blocker. Associate beta-blocker toxicity/overdose with its specific antidote, glucagon. Memorize the clinical antidote pairings for high-alert drugs.","testTakingStrategyZh":"从题干中识别药物类别：美托洛尔是一种β受体阻滞剂。将β受体阻滞剂中毒/过量与其特异性解毒剂——胰高血糖素联系起来。记忆高危药物的临床解毒剂配对。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2615,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.8","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.8.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.8.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[134,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[42,72],"fullStemEn":"A client's monitor alarm sounds, and the nurse observes the following rhythm strip showing sinus tachycardia at 120 beats per minute. Which underlying condition should the nurse investigate first as a common physiological cause of sinus tachycardia?","fullStemZh":"患者的监护仪警报响起，护士观察到以下心律条图显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟120次。护士首先应调查哪种基础疾病，作为窦性心动过速的常见生理原因？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which underlying condition should the nurse investigate first as a common physiological cause of sinus tachycardia?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应调查哪种基础疾病，作为窦性心动过速的常见生理原因？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client's monitor alarm sounds, and the nurse observes the following rhythm strip showing sinus tachycardia at 120 beats per minute.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的监护仪警报响起，护士观察到以下心律条图显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟120次。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hypothyroidism","zh":"甲状腺功能减退症"},{"id":"D","en":"Dehydration or fever","zh":"脱水或发热"},{"id":"B","en":"Hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"},{"id":"C","en":"Vagal nerve stimulation","zh":"迷走神经刺激"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Sinus tachycardia is a physiological response to a demand for increased cardiac output or oxygenation. Common causes include fever, dehydration, pain, anxiety, anemia, hypoxia, and exercise. Addressing the underlying cause is the primary therapeutic goal.","rationaleCorrectZh":"窦性心动过速是心脏对心输出量或氧合需求增加的生理反应。常见原因包括发热、脱水、疼痛、焦虑、贫血、缺氧和运动。针对病因进行治疗是首要的治疗目标。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate between mechanisms that speed up the heart versus slow it down. Hypothyroidism and vagal stimulation slow the rate. Between dehydration/fever and hypokalemia, choose the option containing the most common, physiological triggers requiring nursing volume replacement or antipyretic administration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"区分使心率加快和减慢的机制。甲状腺功能减退和迷走神经刺激会减慢心率。在脱水/发热与低钾血症之间，选择包含最常见、需要护士补充容量或使用退热药的生理性诱因的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2616,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_sata_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.9","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.9.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.9.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[233,255],"terminalOffsetsZh":[64,72],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing sustained sinus tachycardia at a rate of 140 beats per minute. Which findings, if noted by the nurse during assessment, would indicate that the tachycardia is compromising cardiac output and organ perfusion? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生持续的窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟140次。护士在评估中若发现以下哪些情况，将表明心动过速正在损害心输出量和器官灌注？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which findings, if noted by the nurse during assessment, would indicate that the tachycardia is compromising cardiac output and organ perfusion?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在评估中若发现以下哪些情况，将表明心动过速正在损害心输出量和器官灌注？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Systolic blood pressure of 88 mmHg","zh":"收缩压为 88 mmHg"},{"id":"D","en":"New-onset confusion or restlessness","zh":"新发意识模糊或烦躁"},{"id":"C","en":"Warm, flushed skin with strong radial pulses","zh":"皮肤温暖潮红且桡动脉搏动有力"},{"id":"E","en":"Client reports sharp substernal chest pressure","zh":"患者主诉尖锐的胸骨后胸部压迫感"},{"id":"A","en":"Shortness of breath and crackles in lung bases","zh":"呼吸急促且肺底有湿啰音"},{"id":"F","en":"Urine output of 45 mL/hour over the last 4 hours","zh":"过去4小时内尿量为每小时 45 mL"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"At high heart rates (sustained sinus tachycardia > 140 bpm), diastolic filling time is significantly reduced, which decreases stroke volume and cardiac output. Signs of compromise include pulmonary congestion (shortness of breath, crackles), hypotension (SBP < 90 mmHg), cerebral hypoperfusion (confusion, restlessness), and myocardial ischemia (chest pain). Flushed warm skin and normal urine output (>30 mL/hr) do not suggest compromise.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在心率较高（持续窦性心动过速 > 140次/分）时，舒张期充盈时间明显缩短，从而降低搏出量和心输出量。受损体征包括肺淤血（呼吸急促、湿啰音）、低血压（收缩压 < 90 mmHg）、脑灌注不足（意识模糊、烦躁）和心肌缺血（胸痛）。皮肤潮红温暖和尿量正常（>30 mL/小时）不提示受损。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Apply the principles of cardiac output: $CO = HR \times SV$. During tachycardia, diastole decreases, lowering SV and CO. Select assessment findings that represent systemic signs of decreased cardiac output (lungs, brain, blood pressure, heart muscle) and eliminate normal peripheral parameters.","testTakingStrategyZh":"应用心输出量原理：$CO = 心率 \times 搏出量$。在心动过速期间，舒张期缩短，从而降低了搏出量和心输出量。选择代表心输出量减少的全身性评估发现（肺、脑、血压、心肌），排除正常的外周参数。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2617,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.10","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.10.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.10.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[268,320],"terminalOffsetsZh":[75,88],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client who was admitted with severe gastroenteritis, vomiting, and diarrhea. The client's ECG shows the following rhythm at a rate of 125 beats per minute. The client is dizzy and has dry mucous membranes with a blood pressure of 88/50 mmHg. Which prescription should the nurse implement first?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名因严重胃肠炎、呕吐和腹泻入院的患者。患者心电图显示以下心律，心率为每分钟125次。患者感到头晕，黏膜干燥，血压为88/50 mmHg。护士首先应该执行哪项医嘱？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which prescription should the nurse implement first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应该执行哪项医嘱？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is dizzy and has dry mucous membranes with a blood pressure of 88/50 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者感到头晕，黏膜干燥，血压为88/50 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Prepare the client for synchronized cardioversion","zh":"为患者进行同步电复律做准备"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer metoprolol 5 mg intravenously","zh":"静脉注射美托洛尔 5 mg"},{"id":"D","en":"Infuse 0.9% normal saline at 250 mL/hour","zh":"以每小时 250 mL 的速度输注 0.9% 生理盐水"},{"id":"A","en":"Perform carotid sinus massage","zh":"进行颈动脉窦按摩"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is showing signs of hypovolemic shock (dizziness, dry mucous membranes, low blood pressure) secondary to fluid loss from gastroenteritis. The sinus tachycardia is a compensatory physiological response to maintain cardiac output. The correct primary action is volume resuscitation using isotonic IV fluids (0.9% normal saline). Lowering the heart rate pharmacologically with a beta-blocker (metoprolol) would destroy the compensatory mechanism and cause severe hemodynamic collapse.","rationaleCorrectZh":"患者表现出继发于胃肠炎体液丢失的低容量性休克体征（头晕、黏膜干燥、低血压）。窦性心动过速是维持心输出量的代偿性生理反应。正确的首要措施是使用等渗静脉液体（0.9%生理盐水）进行容量复苏。若使用β受体阻滞剂（美托洛尔）进行药物降心率，会破坏这一代偿机制并导致严重的血流动力学崩溃。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze the clinical context: fluid loss (vomiting, diarrhea), hypovolemia signs (dry mucous membranes, BP 88/50), and compensatory sinus tachycardia. In compensatory tachycardia, treat the underlying cause (dehydration → fluids) rather than slowing the heart rate directly.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析临床背景：体液丢失（呕吐、腹泻）、低血容量体征（黏膜干燥、血压88/50）以及代偿性窦性心动过速。在代偿性心动过速中，应治疗根本原因（脱水 → 补液），而不是直接减慢心率。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2618,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_matrix_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.11","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.11.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.11.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[95,194],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,54],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is evaluating ECG parameters for three clients in the cardiac rehabilitation clinic. Match each client's ECG parameter/rhythm characteristic to the correct sinus rhythm classification.","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估心脏康复诊所中三位患者的心电图参数。将每位患者的心电图参数/心律特征与正确的窦性心律分类相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each client's ECG parameter/rhythm characteristic to the correct sinus rhythm classification.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每位患者的心电图参数/心律特征与正确的窦性心律分类相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is evaluating ECG parameters for three clients in the cardiac rehabilitation clinic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在评估心脏康复诊所中三位患者的心电图参数。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"PR interval 0.16 seconds, QRS 0.08 seconds, rate 112 bpm","zh":"PR间期 0.16 秒，QRS 0.08 秒，心率 112 次/分"},{"id":"r2","en":"PR interval 0.15 seconds, QRS 0.08 seconds, rate 75 bpm","zh":"PR间期 0.15 秒，QRS 0.08 秒，心率 75 次/分"},{"id":"r3","en":"PR interval 0.18 seconds, QRS 0.09 seconds, rate 48 bpm","zh":"PR间期 0.18 秒，QRS 0.09 秒，心率 48 次/分"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Normal Sinus Rhythm","zh":"正常窦性心律"},{"id":"c3","en":"Sinus Tachycardia","zh":"窦性心动过速"},{"id":"c1","en":"Sinus Bradycardia","zh":"窦性心动过缓"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c3"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c1"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"All three rhythms demonstrate normal intervals (PR 0.12-0.20s, QRS <0.12s), indicating they originate in the SA node. Row 1 has a rate >100 bpm, indicating Sinus Tachycardia. Row 2 has a rate between 60-100 bpm, representing Normal Sinus Rhythm. Row 3 has a rate <60 bpm, signifying Sinus Bradycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"这三种心律都显示出正常的间期（PR 0.12-0.20秒，QRS <0.12秒），表明它们都起源于窦房结。第1行心率 >100次/分，表示窦性心动过速。第2行心率在60-100次/分之间，代表正常窦性心律。第3行心率 <60次/分，表示窦性心动过缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Inspect the rate parameter in each row description first. Tachycardia is >100 bpm, Normal is 60-100 bpm, and Bradycardia is <60 bpm. Match accordingly.","testTakingStrategyZh":"首先检查每一行描述中的心率参数。心动过速是 >100次/分，正常是60-100次/分，心动过缓是 <60次/分。据此进行匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2619,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b1_mc_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.12","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.12.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.12.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[265,305],"terminalOffsetsZh":[75,89],"fullStemEn":"A client with acute asthma is receiving nebulized albuterol treatments in the emergency department. The client's ECG shows the following rhythm at a rate of 118 beats per minute. The client denies chest pain or shortness of breath other than minor asthma symptoms. Which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"一名患有急性哮喘的患者正在急诊科接受沙丁胺醇雾化吸入治疗。患者的心电图显示以下心律，心率为每分钟118次。患者否认胸痛，除了轻微哮喘症状外无呼吸急促。护士下一步应该采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士下一步应该采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client denies chest pain or shortness of breath other than minor asthma symptoms.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者否认胸痛，除了轻微哮喘症状外无呼吸急促。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Reassure the client that this is an expected medication effect and monitor","zh":"向患者解释这是预期的药物作用并进行监测"},{"id":"D","en":"Hold the next dose of albuterol and notify the healthcare provider immediately","zh":"暂停下一次沙丁胺醇给药并立即通知医生"},{"id":"B","en":"Request an emergent cardiology consultation","zh":"申请紧急心血管科会诊"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare to administer a dose of intravenous beta-blocker","zh":"准备使用一剂静脉β受体阻滞剂"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Albuterol is a short-acting beta-2 adrenergic agonist used as a bronchodilator. Tachycardia and mild tremors are common, expected adrenergic side effects due to spillover stimulation of beta-1 receptors in the heart. Since the client is asymptomatic and hemodynamically stable, the nurse should reassure the client that this is expected, document, and continue to monitor.","rationaleCorrectZh":"沙丁胺醇是一种短效β2肾上腺素能受体激动剂，用作支气管扩张剂。由于刺激心脏β1受体的溢出效应，心动过速和轻微震颤是常见的、预期的肾上腺素能副作用。因为患者没有症状且血流动力学稳定，护士应向患者解释这是预期反应，记录并继续监测。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Connect the medication (albuterol) with its drug class (beta-agonist) and expected side effects (tachycardia, tremor). Understand that expected side effects do not require holding the drug or ordering antidotes unless they cause clinical compromise. Eliminate interventionist options (consults, beta-blockers, holding drug) in favor of monitoring.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将药物（沙丁胺醇）与其类别（β受体激动剂）以及预期副作用（心动过速、震颤）联系起来。理解预期的副作用除非引起临床受损，否则不需要停药或给予解毒剂。排除干预性选项（会诊、β受体阻滞剂、停药），选择监测。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2620,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.13","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.13.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.13.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[156,195],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,61],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing a client's telemetry monitor and notes a rapid, irregular rhythm with no discernible P waves. The baseline appears wavy and chaotic. Which rhythm should the nurse document?","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看患者的遥测监护仪，并注意到一种快速、不规则的心律，没有明显的P波。基线显得波浪起伏且混乱。护士应记录哪种心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which rhythm should the nurse document?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录哪种心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The baseline appears wavy and chaotic.","penultimateSentenceZh":"基线显得波浪起伏且混乱。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Atrial Flutter","zh":"心房扑动"},{"id":"A","en":"Sinus Arrhythmia","zh":"窦性心律不齐"},{"id":"C","en":"Atrial Fibrillation","zh":"心房颤动"},{"id":"B","en":"Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT)","zh":"室上性心动过速"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Atrial fibrillation is characterized by a lack of P waves, a chaotic/wavy baseline (fibrillatory waves), and an 'irregularly irregular' R-R interval. Normal SA node depolarization is replaced by rapid, disorganized electrical impulses from multiple ectopic foci in the atria.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心房颤动的特征是缺乏P波、基线混乱/呈波浪状（颤动波）以及“绝对不规则”的R-R间期。正常的窦房结除极被心房内多个异位起搏点发出的快速、无序的电冲动所取代。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the two main diagnostic features of Atrial Fibrillation: an 'irregularly irregular' rhythm and the absence of clear P waves. Eliminate regular rhythms (Atrial Flutter, SVT) and rhythms that have normal P waves (Sinus Arrhythmia).","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注心房颤动的两个主要诊断特征：“绝对不规则”的心律以及缺乏清晰的P波。排除规则的心律（心房扑动、SVT）和具有正常P波的心律（窦性心律不齐）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2621,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.14","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.14.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.14.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[219,388],"terminalOffsetsZh":[53,96],"fullStemEn":"A client, who has a history of hypertension and diabetes mellitus type 2, is diagnosed with chronic atrial fibrillation. The ECG shows the following rhythm. The client's heart rate is controlled at 85 beats per minute. Which medication should the nurse anticipate the provider prescribing as a priority long-term therapy to reduce the risk of a major systemic complication of this rhythm?","fullStemZh":"一名有高血压和2型糖尿病病史的患者被诊断为慢性心房颤动。心电图显示以下心律。患者的心率控制在每分钟85次。护士预期医生会开具哪种药物作为优先的长期治疗，以降低该心律引起的主要全身性并发症风险？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication should the nurse anticipate the provider prescribing as a priority long-term therapy to reduce the risk of a major systemic complication of this rhythm?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预期医生会开具哪种药物作为优先的长期治疗，以降低该心律引起的主要全身性并发症风险？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's heart rate is controlled at 85 beats per minute.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的心率控制在每分钟85次。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Amiodarone","zh":"胺碘酮"},{"id":"C","en":"Metoprolol","zh":"美托洛尔"},{"id":"B","en":"Apixaban","zh":"阿哌沙班"},{"id":"D","en":"Atropine","zh":"阿托品"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In atrial fibrillation, the lack of coordinated atrial contraction causes blood to pool in the atria, especially in the left atrial appendage, leading to thrombus formation. Embolization of this thrombus can cause an ischemic stroke. Therefore, long-term anticoagulation (e.g., apixaban, warfarin) is a high-priority therapy. Since the heart rate is already well controlled (85 bpm), rate control medications (metoprolol) or rhythm control (amiodarone) are not the primary long-term preventative priority over stroke prevention.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在心房颤动中，心房协调收缩的丧失导致血液在心房内淤滞，尤其是在左心耳处，从而导致血栓形成。该血栓的脱落栓塞可引起缺血性脑卒中。因此，长期的抗凝治疗（如阿哌沙班、华法林）是高优先级的治疗方案。由于心率已得到良好控制（85次/分），控制心率药物（美托洛尔）或心律控制药物（胺碘酮）不是预防脑卒中这一主要长期并发症的首要任务。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the major systemic risk of chronic atrial fibrillation: ischemic stroke due to blood pooling. When the stem states the heart rate is already controlled, focus on preventing thrombus formation. Select the anticoagulant.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识慢性心房颤动的主要全身性风险：血液淤滞引起的缺血性脑卒中。当题干指出心率已得到控制时，应重点防范血栓形成。选择抗凝剂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2622,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.15","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.15.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.15.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[318,360],"terminalOffsetsZh":[92,103],"fullStemEn":"The nurse notes a sudden change on a client's cardiac monitor. The heart rate jumps to 180 beats per minute with narrow QRS complexes, regular rhythm, and P waves that are impossible to identify because they are buried in the T waves. The client reports palpitations but is alert with a blood pressure of 110/70 mmHg. How should the nurse classify this rhythm?","fullStemZh":"护士注意到患者的心电监护发生突然改变。心率跳跃至每分钟180次，伴有窄QRS波群、整齐的心律，并且由于埋在T波中而无法辨认P波。患者主诉心慌，但意识清醒，血压为110/70 mmHg。护士应如何分类此心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse classify this rhythm?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何分类此心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client reports palpitations but is alert with a blood pressure of 110/70 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者主诉心慌，但意识清醒，血压为110/70 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Atrial Fibrillation","zh":"心房颤动"},{"id":"B","en":"Sinus Tachycardia","zh":"窦性心动过速"},{"id":"D","en":"Ventricular Tachycardia","zh":"室性心动过速"},{"id":"C","en":"Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT)","zh":"室上性心动过速"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT) is characterized by a rapid heart rate (typically 150-250 bpm), regular rhythm, and narrow QRS complexes (<0.12 seconds), indicating the pathway originates above the ventricles. P waves are often not visible because they are buried in the preceding T waves due to the rapid rate. Ventricular tachycardia has wide QRS complexes; sinus tachycardia is rarely this fast abruptly and typically has visible P waves.","rationaleCorrectZh":"室上性心动过速（SVT）的特征是心率快速（通常在 150-250 次/分之间）、心律规整以及窄QRS波群（<0.12秒），表明冲动起源在心室以上。由于心率过快，P波通常不可见，因为它们埋在前面的T波中。室性心动过速具有宽QRS波群；窦性心动过速很少突然达到这个速度，且通常有可见的P波。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on two key features in the description: 'narrow QRS complexes' and 'buried P waves'. Narrow QRS complexes eliminate ventricular tachycardia (which is wide). The buried P waves and rapid rate of 180 bpm eliminate sinus tachycardia. Regularity eliminates atrial fibrillation.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注描述中的两个关键特征：“窄QRS波群”和“埋入的P波”。窄QRS波群排除了室性心动过速（宽波群）。埋入的P波和180次/分的高心率排除了窦性心动过速。心律规整排除了心房颤动。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2623,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.16","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.16.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.16.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[188,234],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,72],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) with a heart rate of 195 beats per minute. The client is alert and hemodynamically stable with a blood pressure of 112/74 mmHg. Which action should the nurse implement first?","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生室上性心动过速（SVT），心率为每分钟195次。患者意识清醒，血流动力学稳定，血压为112/74 mmHg。护士首先应执行哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse implement first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应执行哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is alert and hemodynamically stable with a blood pressure of 112/74 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者意识清醒，血流动力学稳定，血压为112/74 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Instruct the client to cough forcefully or bear down","zh":"指示患者用力咳嗽或屏气向下用力"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare the client for emergent synchronized cardioversion","zh":"为患者进行紧急同步电复律做准备"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer adenosine 6 mg rapid IV push","zh":"快速静脉注射腺苷 6 mg"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer metoprolol 5 mg intravenously","zh":"静脉注射美托洛尔 5 mg"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In a hemodynamically stable client experiencing SVT, non-pharmacological vagal maneuvers (such as bearing down like having a bowel movement—Valsalva maneuver, coughing forcefully, or ice water stimulation) are the first-line treatment. These actions stimulate the vagus nerve, which releases acetylcholine to slow conduction through the AV node, potentially terminating the arrhythmia. If stable vagal maneuvers fail, adenosine is administered.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在血流动力学稳定的SVT患者中，非药物性迷走神经反射（如排便样用力——瓦萨瓦动作、用力咳嗽或冰水刺激）是首选治疗方法。这些操作可刺激迷走神经，释放乙酰胆碱以减慢通过房室结的传导，有可能终止心律失常。如果稳定的迷走神经反射失败，则给予腺苷。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Prioritize least invasive to most invasive. Since the client is hemodynamically stable, start with non-pharmacological interventions (vagal maneuvers like coughing/bearing down) before moving to drugs (adenosine, beta-blockers) or electricity (cardioversion).","testTakingStrategyZh":"优先选择侵入性最小的方法。由于患者血流动力学稳定，在转向药物（腺苷、β受体阻滞剂）或电学方法（电复律）之前，先从非药物干预措施（如咳嗽/向下用力的迷走神经动作）开始。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2624,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.17","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.17.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.17.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[189,298],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,76],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing to administer adenosine to a client with supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) whose heart rate is 190 beats per minute. The client's vagal maneuvers were unsuccessful. Which administration technique should the nurse employ to ensure the therapeutic efficacy of this medication?","fullStemZh":"护士正准备为一名室上性心动过速（SVT）患者使用腺苷，该患者心率为每分钟190次。该患者进行的迷走神经动作无效。护士应使用哪种给药技术以确保该药的疗效？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which administration technique should the nurse employ to ensure the therapeutic efficacy of this medication?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应使用哪种给药技术以确保该药的疗效？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's vagal maneuvers were unsuccessful.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该患者进行的迷走神经动作无效。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Administer through a peripheral IV in the hand or foot over 1 minute","zh":"在1分钟内通过手部或足部的外周静脉给药"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer as a rapid intravenous push over 1 to 2 seconds followed immediately by a saline flush","zh":"在1至2秒内快速静脉推注，并立即用生理盐水冲管"},{"id":"C","en":"Dilute the drug in 50 mL of 5% dextrose in water and administer slowly","zh":"将药物稀释在 50 mL 5% 葡萄糖注射液中并缓慢推注"},{"id":"A","en":"Infuse the medication via a microbore tubing pump over 30 minutes","zh":"通过微孔泵在30分钟内输注该药物"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adenosine has an extremely short half-life (less than 10 seconds). Therefore, it must be administered rapidly (over 1-2 seconds) through an intravenous access point closest to the heart (preferably an antecubital IV) using a double-stopcock or parallel port technique, followed immediately by a rapid flush of 20 mL of normal saline. If given slowly or in a distal vein, the drug will be metabolized in the bloodstream before reaching the coronary receptors.","rationaleCorrectZh":"腺苷的半衰期极其短暂（小于10秒）。因此，它必须通过最靠近心脏的静脉通路（首选肘正中静脉）在1-2秒内快速推注，使用双通活栓或平行端口技术，并立即以20 mL生理盐水快速冲管。如果缓慢给药或在远端静脉给药，药物在到达心脏冠状动脉受体前就已经在血流中被代谢了。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the unique pharmacokinetic properties of adenosine: its <10-second half-life. Because of this, the nursing intervention must involve extreme speed: 'rapid' IV push (1-2 seconds) and 'immediate' flush. Eliminate options specifying slow delivery or distal routes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆腺苷独特的药代动力学性质：半衰期小于10秒。正因如此，护士干预必须涉及极快的速度：“快速”静脉推注（1-2秒）和“立即”冲洗。排除指定缓慢给药或远端途径的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2625,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_sata_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.18","itemType":"select_all","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.18.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.18.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[236,258],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,74],"fullStemEn":"A client has just received a rapid IV bolus of adenosine 6 mg for the conversion of supraventricular tachycardia (SVT). Which transient side effects or clinical findings should the nurse anticipate immediately following administration? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者刚刚接受了静脉快速推注 6 mg 腺苷以转复室上性心动过速（SVT）。护士应预期在给药后立即出现哪些短暂的副作用或临床表现？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which transient side effects or clinical findings should the nurse anticipate immediately following administration?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应预期在给药后立即出现哪些短暂的副作用或临床表现？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Shortness of breath or dyspnea","zh":"呼吸急促或呼吸困难"},{"id":"A","en":"A brief period of asystole or cardiac pause on the monitor","zh":"监护仪上出现短暂的心脏停搏或停顿"},{"id":"C","en":"Substernal chest pressure or discomfort","zh":"胸骨后压迫感或不适"},{"id":"D","en":"Generalized seizure activity","zh":"全身性抽搐发作"},{"id":"B","en":"Facial flushing and warmth","zh":"面部潮红和温热感"},{"id":"F","en":"Hypertensive crisis (BP >180/120 mmHg)","zh":"高血压危象（血压 >180/120 mmHg）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Adenosine slows conduction through the AV node, which often causes a brief, transient period of asystole (cardiac pause), which can be alarming but is expected and usually self-limiting. Other common, transient side effects include peripheral vasodilation (facial flushing), bronchospasm (shortness of breath/dyspnea), and chest pressure due to adenosine receptor activation in the heart. Seizures and hypertensive crisis are not side effects of adenosine.","rationaleCorrectZh":"腺苷能够减慢通过房室结的传导，这通常会引起短暂、一过性的心跳停搏（心脏停顿），这可能令人惊慌但属于预期且通常自限的现象。其他常见的、一过性副作用包括外周血管舒张（面部潮红）、支气管痉挛（呼吸急促/呼吸困难）以及由于激活心脏内腺苷受体导致的胸部压迫感。抽搐和高血压危象不是腺苷的副作用。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the classic patient-education points before administering adenosine: 'You will feel a flush, chest pressure, short of breath, and your heart may pause.' Use these common, transient effects to select options A, B, C, and E. Eliminate major dangerous non-side-effects (seizures, severe hypertension).","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆使用腺苷前经典的患者宣教要点：“你会感到发热潮红、胸闷压迫感、呼吸急促，且你的心脏可能会停跳。” 利用这些常见、短暂的效应来选择选项 A、B、C 和 E。排除重大危险的非副作用（抽搐、严重高血压）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2626,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.19","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.19.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.19.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[194,256],"terminalOffsetsZh":[56,73],"fullStemEn":"A client's monitor displays a rapid, regular rhythm with a saw-tooth baseline pattern. The QRS complexes are narrow and occur at a regular interval. The ventricular rate is 75 beats per minute. How should the nurse identify this rhythm on the rhythm strip?","fullStemZh":"患者的监护仪显示出一种快速、整齐的心律，基线呈锯齿状。QRS波群较窄，且以固定的间期出现。心室率为每分钟75次。护士应如何在心律条图上识别该心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse identify this rhythm on the rhythm strip?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何在心律条图上识别该心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The ventricular rate is 75 beats per minute.","penultimateSentenceZh":"心室率为每分钟75次。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Second-Degree Heart Block Mobitz I","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型"},{"id":"B","en":"Atrial Fibrillation","zh":"心房颤动"},{"id":"C","en":"Atrial Flutter with 4:1 conduction","zh":"伴 4:1 传导的心房扑动"},{"id":"D","en":"Ventricular Tachycardia","zh":"室性心动过速"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Atrial flutter is defined by regular, rapid atrial waves presenting as a 'saw-tooth' pattern, termed flutter (F) waves. The atrial rate is typically 250-350 bpm. The AV node acts as a gatekeeper, conducting only a fraction of these impulses (conduction ratio). Here, the atrial rate is 300 bpm and the ventricular rate is 75 bpm, representing a 4:1 conduction ratio (4 atrial waves to 1 QRS complex).","rationaleCorrectZh":"心房扑动的定义为规则、快速的心房波呈“锯齿状”表现，称为扑动（F）波。心房率通常在 250-350 次/分之间。房室结起到门卫的作用，只下传这些冲动中的一部分（传导比例）。这里心房率为 300次/分，心室率为 75次/分，代表了 4:1 的传导比例（4个心房波对应1个QRS波群）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the pathognomonic visual description of 'saw-tooth' pattern which always corresponds to Atrial Flutter. To determine the conduction ratio, divide the atrial rate (300) by the ventricular rate (75), which yields 4, confirming 4:1 conduction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别特征性的“锯齿状”模式视觉描述，它总是对应于心房扑动。要确定传导比例，中心房率（300）除以心室率（75），结果为4，证实是 4:1 传导。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2627,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_mc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.20","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Anticoagulant Therapy","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.20.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.20.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[279,399],"terminalOffsetsZh":[79,105],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the cardiac care unit with new-onset atrial fibrillation. The cardiac monitor shows the following rhythm with a ventricular rate of 145 beats per minute. The client reports mild fatigue but denies chest pain or dyspnea. The blood pressure is 108/68 mmHg. Which medication class should the nurse expect the provider to prescribe first to control the client's ventricular rate?","fullStemZh":"一名新发心房颤动患者收治入心脏重症监护室。心电监护仪显示以下心律，心室率为每分钟145次。患者诉轻度疲劳，但否认胸痛或呼吸困难。血压为108/68 mmHg。护士应预期医生首先开具哪类药物以控制该患者的心室率？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication class should the nurse expect the provider to prescribe first to control the client's ventricular rate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期医生首先开具哪类药物以控制该患者的心室率？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The blood pressure is 108/68 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压为108/68 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Platelet aggregation inhibitors","zh":"血小板聚集抑制剂"},{"id":"C","en":"Intravenous atropine","zh":"静脉注射阿托品"},{"id":"A","en":"Intravenous epinephrine","zh":"静脉注射肾上腺素"},{"id":"B","en":"Beta-blocker or calcium channel blocker","zh":"β受体阻滞剂或钙通道阻滞剂"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In atrial fibrillation with rapid ventricular response (ventricular rate > 100 bpm), the immediate medical goal is rate control to preserve diastolic filling time and cardiac output. First-line agents include calcium channel blockers (e.g., diltiazem) or beta-blockers (e.g., metoprolol, esmolol). Anticoagulation/antiplatelet therapy is crucial long-term, but acute control of a rapid ventricular rate is the immediate priority. Epinephrine and atropine would increase the heart rate and are contraindicated.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在伴有快速心室率的心房颤动（心室率 > 100次/分）中，眼前的治疗目标是控制心率以维持舒张充盈时间和心输出量。首选药物包括钙通道阻滞剂（如地尔硫䓬）或β受体阻滞剂（如美托洛尔、艾司洛尔）。长期抗凝/抗血小板治疗非常关键，但急性控制快速心室率是眼下的首要任务。肾上腺素和阿托品会增加心率，属于禁忌药物。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the patient's condition: AFib with rapid ventricular response (HR 145). Connect the clinical problem (tachycardia due to rapid conduction) to the pharmacological solution: blocking the AV node to slow conduction. Select metoprolol/diltiazem (beta/calcium blockers) which are AV node blocking agents.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定患者状况：伴有快速心室率的房颤（心率145）。将临床问题（传导过快引起的心动过速）与药物治疗方案联系起来：阻断房室结以减慢传导。选择美托洛尔/地尔硫䓬（β/钙通道阻滞剂），这类药物是房室结阻滞剂。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2628,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_sata_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.21","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.21.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.21.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[300,322],"terminalOffsetsZh":[77,85],"fullStemEn":"A client is experiencing new-onset atrial fibrillation. The ECG shows the following rhythm at a ventricular rate of 160 beats per minute. Which clinical manifestations, if observed by the nurse, would indicate the client is hemodynamically unstable and requires immediate synchronized cardioversion? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生新发心房颤动。心电图显示以下心律，心室率为每分钟160次。护士如果观察到以下哪些临床表现，将提示患者血流动力学不稳定，需要立即进行同步电复律？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations, if observed by the nurse, would indicate the client is hemodynamically unstable and requires immediate synchronized cardioversion?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士如果观察到以下哪些临床表现，将提示患者血流动力学不稳定，需要立即进行同步电复律？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"E","en":"Acute pulmonary edema with dyspnea and pink frothy sputum","zh":"急性肺水肿伴呼吸困难和咳粉红色泡沫痰"},{"id":"C","en":"Warm extremities and capillary refill of 1.5 seconds","zh":"四肢温暖且毛细血管充盈时间为1.5秒"},{"id":"B","en":"Chest pain with ECG showing ischemic ST-segment depression","zh":"胸痛伴心电图显示缺血性ST段压低"},{"id":"D","en":"New-onset confusion and lethargy","zh":"新发意识模糊和嗜睡"},{"id":"F","en":"Mild palpitation reports from the client","zh":"患者主诉轻微心慌"},{"id":"A","en":"Systolic blood pressure of 78 mmHg","zh":"收缩压为 78 mmHg"}],"correct":["A","B","D","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"According to ACLS guidelines, unstable tachyarrhythmias (such as rapid AFib at 160 bpm causing systemic hypoperfusion) require immediate synchronized cardioversion. Signs of instability include shock (hypotension, SBP < 90 mmHg), ischemic chest pain, altered mental status (confusion, lethargy), and acute heart failure (pulmonary edema/dyspnea). Mild palpitations and normal extremity perfusion indicate stability, not instability.","rationaleCorrectZh":"根据ACLS指南，不稳定型快速心律失常（例如引起全身灌注不良的160次/分快速房颤）需要立即进行同步电复律。不稳定的体征包括休克（低血压，收缩压 < 90 mmHg）、缺血性胸痛、意识状态改变（意识模糊、嗜睡）以及急性心力衰竭（肺水肿/呼吸困难）。轻微心慌和四肢灌注正常表明状况稳定，而非不稳定。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the ACLS criteria for electrical therapy ('electricity over drugs' for unstable tachycardia). The signs of instability are: hypotension, ischemic chest pain, altered mental status, and heart failure. Select the options that directly match these four criteria.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆ACLS关于电学治疗的标准（对于不稳定型心动过速，“电击优于药物”）。不稳定的指征是：低血压、缺血性胸痛、意识状态改变和心力衰竭。选择与这四个标准直接匹配的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2629,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b2_matrix_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.22","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.22.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.22.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[69,162],"terminalOffsetsZh":[19,45],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is analyzing telemetry strips for three different clients. Match each rhythm's visual characteristics to the correct clinical arrhythmia classification.","fullStemZh":"护士正在分析三位不同患者的心电监护图。将每种心律的视觉特征与正确的临床心律失常分类相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each rhythm's visual characteristics to the correct clinical arrhythmia classification.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种心律的视觉特征与正确的临床心律失常分类相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is analyzing telemetry strips for three different clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在分析三位不同患者的心电监护图。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Chaotic wavy baseline, irregular QRS rhythm, absence of P waves","zh":"混乱波浪状基线，不规则QRS心律，无P波"},{"id":"r2","en":"Regular sawtooth baseline waves (F waves), regular narrow QRS complexes","zh":"规整的锯齿状基线波（F波），规整的窄QRS波群"},{"id":"r3","en":"Rapid, highly regular rate (180 bpm), narrow QRS complexes, P waves buried in T waves","zh":"快速、高度规整的心率（180次/分），窄QRS波群，P波埋在T波中"}],"columns":[{"id":"c3","en":"Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT)","zh":"室上性心动过速"},{"id":"c1","en":"Atrial Fibrillation","zh":"心房颤动"},{"id":"c2","en":"Atrial Flutter","zh":"心房扑动"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Row 1 describes the classic irregular features of atrial fibrillation. Row 2 outlines the sawtooth appearance of atrial flutter. Row 3 details the rapid, regular narrow-complex tachycardia features of SVT.","rationaleCorrectZh":"第1行描述了心房颤动的经典不规则特征。第2行概述了心房扑动的锯齿状表现。第3行详细描述了SVT的快速、整齐的窄波心动过速特征。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Inspect the visual keywords in the rows: 'wavy baseline/irregular' corresponds to AFib; 'sawtooth' corresponds to AFlutter; 'buried P waves/regular' corresponds to SVT. Match accordingly.","testTakingStrategyZh":"检查各行中的视觉关键字：“波状基线/不规则”对应房颤；“锯齿状”对应房扑；“埋入P波/规则”对应SVT。进行相应匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2630,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.23","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.23.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.23.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[213,253],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,69],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is analyzing a client's telemetry strip. The heart rate is 68 beats per minute and regular. Every P wave is followed by a narrow QRS complex. The PR interval is measured at 0.26 seconds and is constant. Which conduction disturbance is present?","fullStemZh":"护士正在分析一名患者的遥测心电图。心率为每分钟68次且规整。每个P波后均有窄QRS波群。测得PR间期为0.26秒且恒定。存在哪种传导障碍？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which conduction disturbance is present?","terminalSentenceZh":"存在哪种传导障碍？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The PR interval is measured at 0.26 seconds and is constant.","penultimateSentenceZh":"测得PR间期为0.26秒且恒定。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Third-Degree (Complete) AV Block","zh":"三度（完全性）房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"D","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz II","zh":"二度AV传导阻滞莫氏II型"},{"id":"A","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz I","zh":"二度AV传导阻滞莫氏I型"},{"id":"B","en":"First-Degree Atrioventricular (AV) Block","zh":"一度房室（AV）传导阻滞"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"First-degree AV block is characterized by a prolonged PR interval (>0.20 seconds) that remains constant from beat to beat, with a 1:1 P-to-QRS ratio (no dropped beats). It represents a delay in conduction through the AV node, but all impulses eventually pass to the ventricles.","rationaleCorrectZh":"一度房室传导阻滞的特征是PR间期延长（>0.20秒）且在每个搏动中保持恒定，伴有 1:1 的P-QRS比例（无QRS波脱落）。这代表冲动通过房室结的传导延迟，但所有冲动最终均能下传到心室。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Observe that the PR interval is prolonged (>0.20s) and 'constant' (not lengthening or varying). Note that there are 'no dropped beats'. These combined characteristics uniquely define a first-degree AV block.","testTakingStrategyZh":"观察到PR间期延长（>0.20秒）且“恒定”（没有延长或变化）。注意“没有脱落搏动”。这些特征的组合唯一地定义了一度房室传导阻滞。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2631,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.24","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.24.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.24.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[397,437],"terminalOffsetsZh":[126,139],"fullStemEn":"A client admitted with coronary artery disease has a cardiac monitor showing the following rhythm. The PR interval is 0.28 seconds. The client is alert, oriented, and denies chest pain or dizziness. The blood pressure is 128/80 mmHg. metoprolol 50 mg PO twice daily is scheduled to be given, and facility protocol requires holding AV nodal blocking agents if the PR interval exceeds 0.24 seconds. Which action should the nurse take next?","fullStemZh":"一名因冠心病入院的患者，心电监护仪显示以下心律。PR间期为0.28秒。患者意识清楚、定向力完整，否认胸痛和头晕。血压为128/80 mmHg。医嘱有美托洛尔 50 mg 口服 每日两次需发放，并且医院方案要求若PR间期超过0.24秒则停用房室结阻滞剂。护士下一步应采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take next?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士下一步应采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The blood pressure is 128/80 mmHg. metoprolol 50 mg PO twice daily is scheduled to be given, and facility protocol requires holding AV nodal blocking agents if the PR interval exceeds 0.24 seconds.","penultimateSentenceZh":"医嘱有美托洛尔 50 mg 口服 每日两次需发放，并且医院方案要求若PR间期超过0.24秒则停用房室结阻滞剂。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Hold the metoprolol and notify the healthcare provider","zh":"暂停使用美托洛尔并通知医生"},{"id":"A","en":"Administer the metoprolol as prescribed and continue to monitor","zh":"按医嘱使用美托洛尔并继续监测"},{"id":"B","en":"Prepare for transcutaneous pacemaker insertion","zh":"准备经皮起搏器植入"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer atropine 1 mg intravenously","zh":"静脉注射阿托品 1 mg"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Beta-blockers (like metoprolol) slow conduction through the AV node and can worsen atrioventricular blocks, potentially progressing a first-degree block to a more severe second- or third-degree heart block. In a client with a documented PR interval prolongation (first-degree AV block), the nurse should hold beta-blockers and notify the provider. Pacing and atropine are not indicated because the client is hemodynamically stable and asymptomatic.","rationaleCorrectZh":"β受体阻滞剂（如美托洛尔）会减慢通过房室结的传导，可能会加重房室传导阻滞，从而可能将一度房室传导阻滞恶化为更严重的二度或三度房室传导阻滞。对于已被证实有PR间期延长（一度房室传导阻滞）的患者，护士应暂停使用β受体阻滞剂并通知医生。阿托品和起搏治疗无指征，因为患者目前血流动力学稳定且没有症状。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify metoprolol as a beta-blocker. Recall that beta-blockers prolong AV conduction. Since the EKG already shows a prolonged PR interval (first-degree AV block), giving the drug is unsafe. Choose the option to hold the drug and notify the provider.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别美托洛尔为β受体阻滞剂。回忆β受体阻滞剂会延长房室传导。由于心电图已显示PR间期延长（一度房室传导阻滞），用药是不安全的。选择停药并通知医生的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2632,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.25","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.25.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.25.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[276,318],"terminalOffsetsZh":[76,87],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is reviewing the telemetry monitor of a client admitted with an acute inferior wall myocardial infarction. The nurse notes a pattern where the PR interval progressively lengthens until a P wave occurs without a subsequent QRS complex, after which the cycle repeats. How should the nurse identify this rhythm?","fullStemZh":"护士正在查看一名因急性下壁心肌梗死入院患者的遥测监护仪。护士注意到一种模式，即PR间期进行性延长，直到出现一个P波后没有紧跟QRS波群，之后该周期重复。护士应如何识别此心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse identify this rhythm?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何识别此心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes a pattern where the PR interval progressively lengthens until a P wave occurs without a subsequent QRS complex, after which the cycle repeats.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到一种模式，即PR间期进行性延长，直到出现一个P波后没有紧跟QRS波群，之后该周期重复。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz II","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏II型"},{"id":"C","en":"First-Degree AV Block","zh":"一度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"D","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz I (Wenckebach)","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型（文氏）"},{"id":"B","en":"Third-Degree (Complete) AV Block","zh":"三度（完全性）房室传导阻滞"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Second-degree AV block Mobitz I (Wenckebach) is defined by progressive prolongation of the PR interval from beat to beat until an electrical impulse is completely blocked at the AV node, resulting in a P wave that is not followed by a QRS complex ('dropped beat'). Following the dropped beat, the PR interval resets to its shortest duration and the cycle repeats.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型（文氏）的定义是PR间期逐搏进行性延长，直到电冲动在房室结处被完全阻断，导致P波后没有紧跟QRS波群（“脱落搏动”）。在脱落搏动后，PR间期重置为其最短时限并重复该周期。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Memorize the classic nursery rhyme for heart blocks: 'Longer, longer, longer, drop! Then you have a Wenckebach.' Match this pattern to Second-Degree Mobitz I.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记忆关于房室传导阻滞的经典口诀：“PR间期越拉越长，直到一个脱落！那就是文氏阻滞（莫氏I型）。” 将此模式与二度莫氏I型相匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2633,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.26","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.26.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.26.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[229,270],"terminalOffsetsZh":[68,80],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is evaluating a client who has transitioned into a second-degree AV block Mobitz I. The heart rate is 52 beats per minute. The client's blood pressure is 114/70 mmHg, extremities are warm, and they are awake and alert. Which action should the nurse prioritize?","fullStemZh":"护士正在评估一名已转变为二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型的患者。心率为每分钟52次。患者血压为114/70 mmHg，四肢温暖，意识清醒且警觉。护士应优先采取哪项行动？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse prioritize?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先采取哪项行动？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's blood pressure is 114/70 mmHg, extremities are warm, and they are awake and alert.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者血压为114/70 mmHg，四肢温暖，意识清醒且警觉。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Apply external pacing pads and initiate pacing at 60 mA","zh":"贴上体外起搏电极板并以 60 mA 开始起搏"},{"id":"D","en":"Obtain consent for emergent cardiac catheterization","zh":"获取紧急心脏导管插入术的知情同意书"},{"id":"A","en":"Document the rhythm, check clinical symptoms, and observe","zh":"记录心律，检查临床症状，并继续观察"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer atropine 1 mg intravenously immediately","zh":"立即静脉注射阿托品 1 mg"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In a client with second-degree AV block Mobitz I (Wenckebach) who is hemodynamically stable (BP 114/70, warm extremities, awake/alert), active interventions such as pacing or atropine are unnecessary and contraindicated. The nurse should document the finding, check for symptoms of hemodynamic compromise, and continue observing the rhythm. Active treatment is reserved for symptomatic bradycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在血流动力学稳定（血压 114/70，四肢温暖，清醒/警觉）的二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型（文氏）患者中，起搏或阿托品等积极干预措施是不必要且不适合的。护士应记录该发现，检查有无血流动力学受损的症状，并继续观察心律。积极治疗仅保留给有症状的心动过缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Determine if the client is stable: BP 114/70, warm extremities, awake, and alert. For stable heart blocks (first-degree and Mobitz I), the standard action is monitoring and documentation rather than immediate invasive therapies. Eliminate options A, B, and D.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定患者是否稳定：血压114/70，四肢温暖，清醒且警觉。对于稳定的房室传导阻滞（一度和莫氏I型），标准措施是监测和记录，而不是立即进行侵入性治疗。排除选项B、C和D。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2634,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.27","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.27.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.27.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[209,238],"terminalOffsetsZh":[48,57],"fullStemEn":"A client's cardiac monitor display is shown below. The nurse notes that the PR intervals of conducted beats are identical and normal, but there are intermittent P waves that fail to conduct to the ventricles. Which rhythm is demonstrated?","fullStemZh":"患者的心电监护仪显示如下。护士注意到下传搏动的PR间期相同且正常，但有间歇性P波未能下传到心室。显示的是哪种心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which rhythm is demonstrated?","terminalSentenceZh":"显示的是哪种心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes that the PR intervals of conducted beats are identical and normal, but there are intermittent P waves that fail to conduct to the ventricles.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到下传搏动的PR间期相同且正常，但有间歇性P波未能下传到心室。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Premature Atrial Contractions (PACs) with block","zh":"房性期前收缩伴阻滞"},{"id":"C","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz II","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏II型"},{"id":"D","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz I","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型"},{"id":"A","en":"Third-Degree AV Block","zh":"三度房室传导阻滞"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Second-degree AV block Mobitz II is characterized by intermittent dropped QRS complexes (non-conducted P waves) where the PR interval of all conducted beats remains constant and identical. Unlike Mobitz I, there is no progressive lengthening of the PR interval. Mobitz II indicates a block below the AV node (usually in the Bundle of His or bundle branches) and has a high risk of progressing to complete heart block.","rationaleCorrectZh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏II型的特征是间歇性脱落QRS波群（非下传P波），其中所有下传搏动的PR间期保持恒定且相同。与莫氏I型不同，其PR间期没有进行性延长。莫氏II型表明阻滞在房室结下方（通常在希氏束或束支），并且有进展为完全性房室传导阻滞的高风险。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Contrast Mobitz I and Mobitz II. Look at the PR interval of the beats before the drop: if they are identical/constant, it is Mobitz II. If they are progressively lengthening, it is Mobitz I. Since the stem states they are 'identical', select Mobitz II.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对比莫氏I型和莫氏II型。看脱落前搏动的PR间期：如果它们相同/恒定，则是莫氏II型。如果它们进行性延长，则是莫氏I型。由于题干指出它们是“相同”的，选择莫氏II型。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2635,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.28","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.28.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.28.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[177,252],"terminalOffsetsZh":[57,79],"fullStemEn":"A client's monitor shows second-degree AV block Mobitz II at a ventricular rate of 45 beats per minute. The client is dizzy and lightheaded with a blood pressure of 86/48 mmHg. Which intervention should the nurse implement first as a clinical priority?","fullStemZh":"患者的监护仪显示二度房室传导阻滞莫氏II型，心室率为每分钟45次。患者感到头晕和目眩，血压为86/48 mmHg。护士首先应执行哪项干预措施作为临床首要任务？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which intervention should the nurse implement first as a clinical priority?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应执行哪项干预措施作为临床首要任务？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client is dizzy and lightheaded with a blood pressure of 86/48 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者感到头晕和目眩，血压为86/48 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Apply transcutaneous pacing pads and prepare to initiate pacing","zh":"贴上经皮起搏电极板并准备开始起搏"},{"id":"B","en":"Instruct the client to perform a Valsalva maneuver","zh":"指导患者进行瓦萨瓦动作"},{"id":"D","en":"Administer atropine 1 mg IV push","zh":"静脉注射阿托品 1 mg"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepare the client for emergent coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG)","zh":"为患者进行紧急冠状动脉旁路移植术（CABG）做准备"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For symptomatic, hemodynamically unstable Mobitz II, transcutaneous pacing (TCP) is the immediate priority. Atropine is generally ineffective for Mobitz II because the conduction block is located below the AV node (in the His-Purkinje system), and increasing SA node rate without improving AV conduction can worsen the block or cause hemodynamic collapse. Pacing pads must be placed immediately.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于有症状、血流动力学不稳定的莫氏II型，经皮起搏（TCP）是当务之急。阿托品对莫氏II型通常无效，因为传导阻滞定位在房室结下方（希氏-浦肯野系统内），直接增加窦房结率而不改善房室传导可能会加重阻滞或导致血流动力学崩溃。必须立即贴上起搏电极板。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Differentiate the response to bradycardia based on the block location. For AV node blocks (sinus bradycardia, Mobitz I), atropine is drug of choice. For sub-AV node blocks (Mobitz II, complete block), atropine is ineffective, and electrical pacing (transcutaneous pacing) is the immediate priority.","testTakingStrategyZh":"根据阻滞部位区分对心动过缓的反应。对于房室结内阻滞（窦缓、莫氏I型），阿托品是首选药物。对于房室结下方阻滞（莫氏II型、完全性阻滞），阿托品无效，电起搏（经皮起搏）是当务之急。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2636,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.29","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.29.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.29.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[276,318],"terminalOffsetsZh":[75,86],"fullStemEn":"A client's monitor demonstrates a ventricular rate of 35 beats per minute with wide QRS complexes, and a regular atrial rate of 80 beats per minute. P waves and QRS complexes occur regularly but have no temporal relationship to each other, resulting in variable PR intervals. How should the nurse classify this rhythm?","fullStemZh":"患者的监护仪显示心室率为每分钟35次伴宽QRS波群，且规整的心房率为每分钟80次。P波和QRS波群整齐出现，但彼此之间没有时间关系，导致PR间期多变。护士应如何分类此心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"How should the nurse classify this rhythm?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应如何分类此心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"P waves and QRS complexes occur regularly but have no temporal relationship to each other, resulting in variable PR intervals.","penultimateSentenceZh":"P波和QRS波群整齐出现，但彼此之间没有时间关系，导致PR间期多变。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"First-Degree AV Block","zh":"一度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"A","en":"Third-Degree (Complete) AV Block","zh":"三度（完全性）房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"B","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz II","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏II型"},{"id":"D","en":"Ventricular Fibrillation","zh":"心室颤动"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Third-degree atrioventricular (complete) AV block represents complete electrical dissociation between the atria and ventricles. The SA node stimulates the atria regularly (producing P waves), while an independent ectopic pacemaker below the block stimulates the ventricles (producing QRS complexes). There is no relationship between P waves and QRS complexes, resulting in variable PR intervals.","rationaleCorrectZh":"三度房室（完全性）传导阻滞代表心房和心室之间电活动的完全分离。窦房结规律地刺激心房（产生P波），而阻滞部位下方的独立异位起搏点独立刺激心室（产生QRS波群）。P波与QRS波群之间没有因果关系，导致PR间期多变。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the key phrase 'no temporal relationship to each other' (or 'AV dissociation'). Complete dissociation of atria and ventricles always indicates a Third-Degree (Complete) AV Block. Select Option D.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别关键短语“彼此之间没有时间关系”（或“房室分离”）。心房和心室的完全分离总是提示三度（完全性）房室传导阻滞。选择选项B。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2637,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_sata_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.30","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.30.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.30.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[227,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[67,75],"fullStemEn":"A client is diagnosed with a third-degree (complete) AV block. The ECG shows a ventricular rate of 30 beats per minute. Which clinical manifestations should the nurse monitor for as indicators of severe hemodynamic compromise? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者被诊断为三度（完全性）房室传导阻滞。心电图显示心室率为每分钟30次。护士应监测以下哪些临床表现，作为严重血流动力学受损的指标？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which clinical manifestations should the nurse monitor for as indicators of severe hemodynamic compromise?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应监测以下哪些临床表现，作为严重血流动力学受损的指标？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Flushed, dry, and warm skin","zh":"皮肤潮红、干燥且温暖"},{"id":"C","en":"Substernal chest pain","zh":"胸骨后胸痛"},{"id":"A","en":"Syncope or loss of consciousness","zh":"晕厥或意识丧失"},{"id":"B","en":"Blood pressure of 72/40 mmHg","zh":"血压为 72/40 mmHg"},{"id":"E","en":"Acute mental status changes (e.g., confusion)","zh":"急性精神状态改变（如意识模糊）"},{"id":"F","en":"Urine output of 50 mL/hour","zh":"尿量为每小时 50 mL"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In complete heart block, the ventricular rate is extremely slow (often 20-40 bpm), which dramatically reduces cardiac output. Severe hypoperfusion manifests as syncope (Stokes-Adams attacks), profound hypotension (BP 72/40), ischemic chest pain due to coronary artery hypoperfusion, and confusion/lethargy due to cerebral hypoxia. Warm flushed skin and normal urine output do not indicate compromise.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在完全性心脏传导阻滞中，心室率极其缓慢（通常为 20-40 次/分），这会急剧减少心输出量。严重的灌注不足表现为晕厥（阿-斯综合征）、严重的低血压（血压 72/40）、由于冠状动脉灌注不足引起的缺血性胸痛，以及由于脑缺氧引起的意识模糊/嗜睡。温暖潮红的皮肤和正常的尿量不提示灌注受损。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the signs of unstable bradycardia. Select symptoms representing severe systemic tissue hypoxia and hypoperfusion (brain: syncope/confusion; heart: chest pain; blood pressure: hypotension). Eliminate stable peripheral findings (warm skin, adequate urine output).","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆不稳定型心动过缓的征象。选择代表严重全身组织缺氧和灌注不足的症状（大脑：晕厥/意识模糊；心脏：胸痛；血压：低血压）。排除稳定的外周发现（温热的皮肤、充足的尿量）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2638,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_mc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.31","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.31.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.31.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[119,215],"terminalOffsetsZh":[34,59],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the telemetry unit with a third-degree AV block and a ventricular rate of 32 beats per minute. Which definitive treatment should the nurse anticipate the provider prescribing for this client?","fullStemZh":"一名患有三度房室传导阻滞且心室率为每分钟32次的患者收治入遥测病房。护士应预期医生会为该患者开具哪种确定性的治疗方案？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which definitive treatment should the nurse anticipate the provider prescribing for this client?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期医生会为该患者开具哪种确定性的治疗方案？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client is admitted to the telemetry unit with a third-degree AV block and a ventricular rate of 32 beats per minute.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名患有三度房室传导阻滞且心室率为每分钟32次的患者收治入遥测病房。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Permanent pacemaker insertion","zh":"永久性起搏器植入"},{"id":"A","en":"Long-term oral atropine therapy","zh":"长期口服阿托品治疗"},{"id":"D","en":"Daily intravenous boluses of calcium gluconate","zh":"每日静脉推注葡萄糖酸钙"},{"id":"B","en":"Coronary angioplasty with stent placement","zh":"伴支架置入的冠状动脉血管成形术"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The definitive, long-term treatment for third-degree (complete) AV block is the insertion of a permanent pacemaker. Pacemakers provide regular electrical impulses directly to the myocardium to ensure a safe, sustained ventricular rate and maintain cardiac output. Atropine is generally ineffective for long-term therapy and incomplete for complete blocks. Angioplasty is not a direct treatment for conduction tissue block unless active ischemia is present. Calcium gluconate is not used for heart block.","rationaleCorrectZh":"三度（完全性）房室传导阻滞的确定性、长期治疗方案是植入永久性起搏器。起搏器直接向心肌提供规律的电冲动，以确保安全、持续的心室率并维持心输出量。阿托品通常不适用于长期治疗，且对完全性阻滞效果有限。血管成形术不是传导系统阻滞的直接治疗方法，除非存在急性缺血。葡萄糖酸钙不用于心脏传导阻滞。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the word 'definitive' in the stem. While temporary pacing is an emergency bridge, a permanent pacemaker is the only definitive long-term solution to ensure electrical conduction in complete heart block. Eliminate drugs and surgical procedures that do not directly address conduction.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注题干中的“确定性”一词。虽然临时起搏是紧急过渡，但永久性起搏器是确保完全性传导阻滞中电传导的唯一确定性长期解决方案。排除不直接解决传导问题的药物和手术程序。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2639,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b3_matrix_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.32","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.32.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.32.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[75,164],"terminalOffsetsZh":[20,46],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is analyzing heart block parameters for three different clients. Match each rhythm's conduction characteristics to the correct heart block classification.","fullStemZh":"护士正在分析三位不同患者的传导阻滞参数。将每种心律的传导特征与正确的心脏传导阻滞分类相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each rhythm's conduction characteristics to the correct heart block classification.","terminalSentenceZh":"将每种心律的传导特征与正确的心脏传导阻滞分类相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is analyzing heart block parameters for three different clients.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士正在分析三位不同患者的传导阻滞参数。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"PR interval >0.20 seconds and constant, all P waves conducted to ventricles (1:1 ratio)","zh":"PR间期 >0.20 秒且恒定，所有P波下传至心室（1:1 比例）"},{"id":"r2","en":"PR interval progressively lengthens until a QRS complex is dropped, then resets","zh":"PR间期进行性延长，直到一个QRS波群脱落，然后重置"},{"id":"r3","en":"PR intervals of conducted beats are constant, but there are sudden dropped QRS complexes","zh":"下传搏动的PR间期恒定，但有突然脱落的QRS波群"}],"columns":[{"id":"c1","en":"First-Degree AV Block","zh":"一度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"c3","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz II","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏II型"},{"id":"c2","en":"Second-Degree AV Block Mobitz I","zh":"二度房室传导阻滞莫氏I型"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c3"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Row 1 outlines the features of first-degree block (prolonged, constant, 1:1 conduction). Row 2 details Mobitz I (progressive lengthening and dropped beat). Row 3 explains Mobitz II (constant PR with sudden dropped beats).","rationaleCorrectZh":"第1行概述了一度房室阻滞的特征（延长、恒定、1:1传导）。第2行详细描述了莫氏I型（进行性延长和脱落搏动）。第3行解释了莫氏II型（PR恒定伴突然脱落搏动）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze the PR interval behavior in each statement: constant and no drop is First-degree; progressively lengthening is Mobitz I; constant but with drops is Mobitz II. Match accordingly.","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析每个陈述中PR间期的表现：恒定且无脱落是一度；进行性延长是莫氏I型；恒定但有脱落是莫氏II型。据此进行匹配。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2640,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.33","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.33.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.33.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[264,311],"terminalOffsetsZh":[82,94],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is observing a client's electrocardiogram (ECG) monitor and notes a normal sinus rhythm interrupted by a single, early, wide, and bizarrely shaped QRS complex (>0.12 seconds) without a preceding P wave. This is followed by a complete compensatory pause. Which rhythm feature should the nurse document?","fullStemZh":"护士正在观察患者的心电图（ECG）监护仪，发现正常的窦性心律中插入了一个提早出现的、宽大且畸形的QRS波群（>0.12秒），之前没有P波。随后是一个完全性代偿间歇。护士应记录哪种心律特征？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which rhythm feature should the nurse document?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录哪种心律特征？","penultimateSentenceEn":"This is followed by a complete compensatory pause.","penultimateSentenceZh":"随后是一个完全性代偿间歇。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Atrial Flutter","zh":"心房扑动"},{"id":"C","en":"First-Degree AV Block","zh":"一度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"B","en":"Premature Ventricular Contraction (PVC)","zh":"室性期前收缩（室早）"},{"id":"A","en":"Premature Atrial Contraction (PAC)","zh":"房性期前收缩（房早）"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A Premature Ventricular Contraction (PVC) is a single ectopic impulse originating in the ventricles, characterized by an early, wide (>0.12 seconds), and distorted/bizarre QRS complex. The T wave of the PVC is usually in the opposite direction of the QRS complex, and a fully compensatory pause typically follows.","rationaleCorrectZh":"室性期前收缩（室早/PVC）是起源于心室的单个异位冲动，其特征是提早出现、宽大（>0.12秒）且畸形/扭曲的QRS波群。室早的T波方向通常与QRS波群主波方向相反，且随后通常是一个完全代偿性间歇。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Focus on the descriptors of the ectopic complex: 'wide and bizarrely shaped' and 'QRS > 0.12 seconds' without a P wave. Wide and bizarre complexes always indicate a ventricular origin, making Premature Ventricular Contraction (PVC) the correct answer. PACs have narrow QRS complexes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"关注异位波群的描述字眼：“宽大且畸形”和“QRS > 0.12秒”且无P波。宽大畸形的波群总是提示室性起源，这使得室性期前收缩（室早/PVC）成为正确答案。房早具有窄QRS波群。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2641,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.34","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Laboratory & Diagnostic Tests","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.34.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.34.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[110,250],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,72],"fullStemEn":"A client's monitor demonstrates frequent premature ventricular contractions (PVCs) at a rate of 6 per minute. Which laboratory value should the nurse review as a clinical priority to identify a common reversible metabolic trigger for this arrhythmia?","fullStemZh":"患者的监护仪显示频繁的室性期前收缩（室早/PVC），频率为每分钟6次。护士应优先查看哪项实验室检查值，以识别引起此心律失常的常见可逆性代谢诱因？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which laboratory value should the nurse review as a clinical priority to identify a common reversible metabolic trigger for this arrhythmia?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应优先查看哪项实验室检查值，以识别引起此心律失常的常见可逆性代谢诱因？","penultimateSentenceEn":"A client's monitor demonstrates frequent premature ventricular contractions (PVCs) at a rate of 6 per minute.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的监护仪显示频繁的室性期前收缩（室早/PVC），频率为每分钟6次。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Serum creatinine level","zh":"血清肌酐水平"},{"id":"C","en":"Hemoglobin level","zh":"血红蛋白水平"},{"id":"D","en":"Serum potassium level","zh":"血清钾水平"},{"id":"A","en":"Serum sodium level","zh":"血清钠水平"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypokalemia (low potassium) and hypomagnesemia (low magnesium) are common metabolic causes of ventricular irritability and ectopy, presenting as frequent PVCs, which can progress to ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. Checking the serum potassium level is a priority nursing action when frequent PVCs are observed.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低钾血症（低钾）和低镁血症（低镁）是导致心室易激惹和异位搏动的常见代谢性原因，表现为频繁的室早（PVC），并可能进展为室性心动过速或室颤。当观察到频繁的室早时，查看血清钾水平是首要的护理措施。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall which electrolytes are critical for myocardial electrical stability. Potassium and magnesium are the primary regulators of cardiac conduction and ventricular irritability. Select potassium as it is the most direct cause of PVCs listed.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆哪些电解质对心肌电生理稳定性至关重要。钾和镁是心脏传导和心室易激惹的主要调节者。选择钾，因为它是所列选项中室早最直接的原因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2642,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.35","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.35.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.35.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[245,269],"terminalOffsetsZh":[72,79],"fullStemEn":"The telemetry nurse notes the sudden onset of the following cardiac rhythm on a client's monitor. The rhythm is highly regular at 160 beats per minute, the QRS complexes are wide and uniform (0.16 seconds), and there are no discernible P waves. Which rhythm is present?","fullStemZh":"遥测护士注意到患者监护仪上突然出现以下心律。该心律高度规整，心率为每分钟160次，QRS波群宽大且形态一致（0.16秒），并且没有可辨认的P波。存在哪种心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which rhythm is present?","terminalSentenceZh":"存在哪种心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The rhythm is highly regular at 160 beats per minute, the QRS complexes are wide and uniform (0.16 seconds), and there are no discernible P waves.","penultimateSentenceZh":"该心律高度规整，心率为每分钟160次，QRS波群宽大且形态一致（0.16秒），并且没有可辨认的P波。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Monomorphic Ventricular Tachycardia","zh":"单形性室性心动过速"},{"id":"C","en":"Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT)","zh":"室上性心动过速"},{"id":"D","en":"Atrial Fibrillation with bundle branch block","zh":"伴有束支传导阻滞的心房颤动"},{"id":"A","en":"Ventricular Fibrillation (VFib)","zh":"心室颤动"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Monomorphic Ventricular Tachycardia is characterized by a rapid ventricular rate (typically 100-250 bpm), highly regular rhythm, wide QRS complexes (>0.12 seconds) that have a uniform shape/appearance, and absence of P waves due to AV dissociation. This indicates a single ectopic focus in the ventricles pacing the heart rapidly.","rationaleCorrectZh":"单形性室性心动过速的特征是心室率快（通常为 100-250 次/分）、心律高度规整、QRS波群宽大（>0.12秒）且形态/外观一致，以及由于房室分离导致P波消失。这表明心室中的单个异位起搏点在快速起搏心脏。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look at the rate and QRS width. A rate of 160 bpm is a tachycardia. A QRS width of 0.16 seconds is wide (>0.12 seconds), indicating a ventricular origin. The regular, uniform shapes of the complexes indicate monomorphic Ventricular Tachycardia. SVT has narrow complexes, and VFib is chaotic.","testTakingStrategyZh":"看心率和QRS波宽度。心率 160次/分是心动过速。QRS波时限 0.16秒是宽波群（>0.12秒），提示心室起源。波群规则、一致的形状提示单形性室性心动过速。SVT有窄波群，而室颤是混乱的。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2643,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.36","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.36.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.36.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[204,272],"terminalOffsetsZh":[54,73],"fullStemEn":"The nurse enters a client's room and finds the client unresponsive. The cardiac monitor displays ventricular tachycardia at a rate of 170 beats per minute. The nurse is unable to palpate a carotid pulse. After calling for help, which action should the nurse perform first?","fullStemZh":"护士进入患者房间，发现患者无反应。心脏监护仪显示室性心动过速，心率为每分钟170次。护士无法触及颈动脉搏动。在呼叫求助后，护士首先应执行哪项操作？","terminalSentenceEn":"After calling for help, which action should the nurse perform first?","terminalSentenceZh":"在呼叫求助后，护士首先应执行哪项操作？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse is unable to palpate a carotid pulse.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士无法触及颈动脉搏动。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Perform synchronized cardioversion at 100 Joules","zh":"以 100 焦耳进行同步电复律"},{"id":"B","en":"Administer amiodarone 150 mg intravenously over 10 minutes","zh":"10分钟内静脉输注胺碘酮 150 mg"},{"id":"D","en":"Perform bag-valve-mask ventilation with 100% oxygen","zh":"使用 100% 氧气进行简易呼吸器面罩通气"},{"id":"C","en":"Deliver an unsynchronized defibrillation shock","zh":"进行非同步电除颤"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Pulseless ventricular tachycardia is a cardiac arrest rhythm and is treated identically to ventricular fibrillation. The immediate, high-priority intervention is early defibrillation (unsynchronized high-energy shock) to depolarize the myocardium and allow the SA node to resume pacing. Synchronized cardioversion is contraindicated because there is no pulse and the machine cannot sync to a reliable R wave. Amiodarone and ventilation are secondary to defibrillation and CPR.","rationaleCorrectZh":"无脉性室性心动过速是一种心脏骤停心律，其治疗方法与心室颤动完全相同。首要、高优先级的干预措施是早期除颤（非同步高能电击），以使心肌除极并允许窦房结恢复起搏。同步电复律是禁忌的，因为没有脉搏且机器无法同步到可靠的R波。胺碘酮和通气对于除颤和CPR来说是次要的。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize that 'unresponsive' and 'unable to palpate a carotid pulse' means cardiac arrest. The rhythm is VTach, which makes it pulseless VTach (a shockable rhythm). The priority treatment for shockable cardiac arrest (VFib/pulseless VT) is immediate unsynchronized shock (defibrillation). Eliminate drugs and synchronized options.","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识到“无反应”和“无法触及颈动脉搏动”意味着心脏骤停。该心律是室房速，这使其成为无脉性室房速（一种可除颤的心律）。对于可除颤的心脏骤停（室颤/无脉性室速），首要治疗是立即非同步电击（除颤）。排除药物和同步的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2644,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.37","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.37.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.37.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[196,267],"terminalOffsetsZh":[62,78],"fullStemEn":"A client is in monomorphic ventricular tachycardia at a rate of 150 beats per minute. The client is awake, talking, alert, and reports minor chest palpitations. The blood pressure is 115/72 mmHg. Which medication does the nurse expect the provider to prescribe first?","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生单形性室性心动过速，心率为每分钟150次。患者清醒、能够说话、警觉，主诉轻微心慌。血压为115/72 mmHg。护士预期医生首先会开具哪种药物？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which medication does the nurse expect the provider to prescribe first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士预期医生首先会开具哪种药物？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The blood pressure is 115/72 mmHg.","penultimateSentenceZh":"血压为115/72 mmHg。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Amiodarone 300 mg rapid IV push","zh":"静脉快速注射胺碘酮 300 mg"},{"id":"B","en":"Adenosine 6 mg rapid IV push","zh":"静脉快速推注腺苷 6 mg"},{"id":"A","en":"Amiodarone 150 mg intravenously infused over 10 minutes","zh":"静脉输注胺碘酮 150 mg，10分钟输完"},{"id":"D","en":"Atropine 1 mg IV push","zh":"静脉推注阿托品 1 mg"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"For a hemodynamically stable client with a pulse experiencing ventricular tachycardia, pharmacological rhythm control is indicated. Amiodarone is a first-line class III antiarrhythmic. The dose for a stable patient with a pulse is 150 mg infused over 10 minutes. The 300 mg rapid bolus is reserved for cardiac arrest (VFib/pulseless VT). Atropine is for bradycardia. Adenosine is for SVT.","rationaleCorrectZh":"对于有脉搏且血流动力学稳定的室性心动过速患者，有药物转复心律的指征。胺碘酮是首选的III类抗心律失常药。对于有脉搏的稳定患者，剂量为150 mg，在10分钟内输注完毕。300 mg快速推注仅保留用于心脏骤停（室颤/无脉性室速）。阿托品用于心动过缓。腺苷用于SVT。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze the client stability: hemodynamically stable (BP 115/72, awake, talking). This is VTach *with a pulse*. Therefore, choose the stable dosing option for Amiodarone (150 mg over 10 minutes) rather than the cardiac arrest cardiac bolus dose (300 mg).","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析患者稳定性：血流动力学稳定（血压115/72，清醒，能说话）。这是*有脉搏*的室速。因此，选择胺碘酮的稳定给药方案（150 mg输注10分钟以上），而非心脏骤停时的推注剂量（300 mg）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2645,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.38","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.38.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.38.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[234,258],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,67],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is looking at the telemetry monitor of a client on the unit and observes the cardiac rhythm shown below. There are no recognizable P waves, QRS complexes, or T waves; the baseline is completely chaotic, irregular, and wavy. Which rhythm is present?","fullStemZh":"护士正在看病房患者的遥测监护仪，观察到如下心脏心律。没有可辨认的P波、QRS波群或T波；基线完全混乱、不规则且呈波浪状。存在哪种心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which rhythm is present?","terminalSentenceZh":"存在哪种心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"There are no recognizable P waves, QRS complexes, or T waves; the baseline is completely chaotic, irregular, and wavy.","penultimateSentenceZh":"没有可辨认的P波、QRS波群或T波；基线完全混乱、不规则且呈波浪状。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Atrial Fibrillation (AFib)","zh":"心房颤动（房颤）"},{"id":"C","en":"Ventricular Fibrillation (VFib)","zh":"心室颤动（室颤）"},{"id":"D","en":"Torsades de Pointes","zh":"尖端扭转型室速"},{"id":"B","en":"Asystole","zh":"心室停搏（平线）"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ventricular fibrillation (VFib) is a lethal cardiac arrest rhythm characterized by completely disorganized, chaotic electrical activity in the ventricles. There are no identifiable P waves, QRS complexes, or T waves on the ECG. The heart muscle simply quivers, producing no mechanical contraction or cardiac output.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心室颤动（室颤/VFib）是一种致命的心脏骤停心律，其特征是心室内电活动完全无序、混乱。心电图上没有可辨认的P波、QRS波群或T波。心肌仅颤动，不产生机械收缩或心输出量。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recognize the visual definition of Ventricular Fibrillation: 'completely chaotic, irregular, and wavy baseline' with 'no recognizable complexes'. VFib has no output and is a medical emergency. Contrast this with AFib (which has narrow QRS complexes) and Asystole (flatline).","testTakingStrategyZh":"认识心室颤动的视觉定义：“完全混乱、不规则且呈波浪状的基线”伴“无任何可辨认的波群”。室颤无心输出量，属于医疗紧急情况。将其与房颤（具有窄QRS波群）和心室停搏（平线）进行对比。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":true,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2646,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_sata_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.39","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.39.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.39.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[171,193],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,49],"fullStemEn":"A client on the telemetry unit goes into ventricular fibrillation. The client is unresponsive, and no pulse is felt. Which actions should the nurse implement immediately? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"遥测病房的一名患者进入心室颤动。患者无反应，且未触及脉搏。护士应立即执行哪些操作？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which actions should the nurse implement immediately?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应立即执行哪些操作？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Activate the emergency response system","zh":"启动紧急医疗响应系统"},{"id":"D","en":"Perform synchronized cardioversion at 50 Joules","zh":"以 50 焦耳进行同步电复律"},{"id":"B","en":"Begin high-quality cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR), starting with chest compressions","zh":"开始高质量心肺复苏（CPR），从胸外按压开始"},{"id":"F","en":"Administer metoprolol 5 mg IV push immediately","zh":"立即静脉推注美托洛尔 5 mg"},{"id":"E","en":"Prepare to administer epinephrine 1 mg intravenously after the first or second shock","zh":"准备在第一或第二次除颤电击后静脉注射肾上腺素 1 mg"},{"id":"C","en":"Deliver an unsynchronized shock (defibrillation) as soon as the defibrillator is ready","zh":"除颤仪准备就绪后立即进行非同步电击（除颤）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Ventricular fibrillation (VFib) is a lethal cardiac arrest rhythm that requires immediate activation of code blue, beginning CPR (compressions first), and prompt defibrillation (unsynchronized shock). Epinephrine 1 mg IV push is administered every 3-5 minutes during ACLS, starting after the second shock. Synchronized cardioversion is contraindicated for VFib. Metoprolol is a beta-blocker and is not used in cardiac arrest rescue.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心室颤动（室颤）是一种致命的心脏骤停心律，需要立即启动紧急呼叫、开始CPR（首先进行按压）并迅速进行除颤（非同步电击）。在ACLS期间，每3-5分钟静脉推注一次肾上腺素 1 mg，在第二次除颤电击后开始给药。同步电复律在室颤中是禁忌的。美托洛尔是一种β受体阻滞剂，不用于心脏骤停的抢救。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the patient state: Cardiac arrest (VFib, unresponsive, pulseless). The primary therapies are CPR, early defibrillation (unsynchronized), and epinephrine. Eliminate options that indicate synchronized shock (option D) or inappropriate medications (option F).","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定患者状态：心脏骤停（室颤、无反应、无脉搏）。首要治疗是CPR、早期除颤（非同步）和肾上腺素。排除表示同步电击（选项D）或不合适药物（选项F）的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2647,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_mc_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.40","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.40.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.40.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[215,262],"terminalOffsetsZh":[60,72],"fullStemEn":"A client is in cardiac arrest. The nurse looks at the monitor and observes a flatline displaying no electrical complexes. The nurse verifies the leads are attached and checks the patient's pulse and responsiveness. Which cardiac rhythm should the nurse document?","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生心脏骤停。护士看监护仪，发现一条显示没有任何电波群的直线。护士核实了导联是否连接，并检查了患者的脉搏和反应。护士应记录哪种心脏心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which cardiac rhythm should the nurse document?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应记录哪种心脏心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse verifies the leads are attached and checks the patient's pulse and responsiveness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士核实了导联是否连接，并检查了患者的脉搏和反应。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Pulseless Electrical Activity (PEA)","zh":"无脉性电活动"},{"id":"B","en":"Third-Degree AV Block","zh":"三度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"C","en":"Ventricular Fibrillation (VFib)","zh":"心室颤动（室颤）"},{"id":"A","en":"Asystole","zh":"心室停搏（平线）"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Asystole is the complete absence of electrical and mechanical cardiac activity, represented on the ECG monitor as a flatline (or nearly flatline). Before declaring asystole, the nurse must confirm the patient is unresponsive, has no pulse, and that the monitor leads are properly attached (not disconnected).","rationaleCorrectZh":"心室停搏（平线）是指心脏完全没有电活动和机械活动，在ECG监护仪上表现为一条直线（或几近直线）。在宣布心室停搏前，护士必须确认患者无反应、无脉搏，且监护仪导联正确连接（没有脱落）。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the cardiac term for 'flatline' which is Asystole. Differentiate this from PEA, which features an organized rhythm on the monitor but no mechanical pulse. Confirm that asystole has zero electrical complexes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别代表“平线”的心脏术语，即心室停搏。将其与PEA区分开来，后者在监护仪上表现为有组织的心律，但没有机械脉搏。确认心室停搏具有零电生理波群。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2648,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_sata_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.41","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.41.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.41.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[124,146],"terminalOffsetsZh":[35,43],"fullStemEn":"A client is in cardiac arrest, and the monitor displays asystole. Which interventions should the nurse perform immediately? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者发生心脏骤停，监护仪显示心室停搏。护士应立即执行哪些干预措施？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which interventions should the nurse perform immediately?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应立即执行哪些干预措施？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Deliver an unsynchronized shock (defibrillation) immediately","zh":"立即进行非同步电击（除颤）"},{"id":"E","en":"Prepare the client for synchronized cardioversion at 100 Joules","zh":"准备为患者进行 100 焦耳的同步电复律"},{"id":"B","en":"Perform high-quality continuous chest compressions","zh":"进行高质量持续胸外按压"},{"id":"D","en":"Search for and treat reversible causes of cardiac arrest (H's and T's)","zh":"寻找并治疗心脏骤停的可逆原因（5H和5T）"},{"id":"F","en":"Confirm the rhythm in a second lead","zh":"在第二导联中确认心律"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer epinephrine 1 mg intravenously as soon as access is established","zh":"建立通路后立即静脉注射肾上腺素 1 mg"}],"correct":["B","C","D","F"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Asystole is a non-shockable rhythm. Therefore, defibrillation (shocking) and synchronized cardioversion are contraindicated and ineffective because there is no electrical activity to reset. Immediate actions include high-quality CPR (chest compressions), intravenous epinephrine 1 mg, search for reversible causes (such as hypoxia, hypovolemia, acidosis, hypo/hyperkalemia, hypothermia—the H's and T's), and confirming the rhythm in a second lead to ensure it is not fine VFib or a loose monitor lead.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心室停搏属于不可除颤的心律。因此，除颤（电击）和同步电复律是禁忌且无效的，因为没有电活动可供重置。立即执行的措施包括高质量CPR（胸外按压）、静脉注射肾上腺素 1 mg、寻找可逆病因（如缺氧、低容量、酸中毒、低/高钾血症、低体温——5H和5T）以及在第二导联中确认心律以确保其不是细颤或导联脱落。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember which arrest rhythms are shockable versus non-shockable. Shockable: VFib and pulseless VTach. Non-shockable: Asystole and PEA. Eliminate all electrical shock therapies (defibrillation, cardioversion) for asystole. Select CPR, drug administration (epinephrine), checking a second lead, and looking for reversible causes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住哪些骤停心律是可除颤的，哪些是不可除颤的。可除颤：室颤和无脉室速。不可除颤：心室停搏和PEA。排除心室停搏的所有电击治疗（除颤、电复律）。选择CPR、药物给药（肾上腺素）、检查第二导联并寻找可逆病因。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2649,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b4_matrix_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.42","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.42.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.42.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[85,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[22,59],"fullStemEn":"The emergency department nurse is preparing to treat four clients in cardiac arrest. Match each rhythm presentation on the monitor/assessment to the correct initial ACLS electrical management status.","fullStemZh":"急诊科护士正准备抢救四名发生心脏骤停的患者。将监护仪/评估中的每种心律表现与正确的初始 ACLS 电学管理状态相匹配。","terminalSentenceEn":"Match each rhythm presentation on the monitor/assessment to the correct initial ACLS electrical management status.","terminalSentenceZh":"将监护仪/评估中的每种心律表现与正确的初始 ACLS 电学管理状态相匹配。","penultimateSentenceEn":"The emergency department nurse is preparing to treat four clients in cardiac arrest.","penultimateSentenceZh":"急诊科护士正准备抢救四名发生心脏骤停的患者。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Ventricular Fibrillation (VFib), unresponsive, pulseless","zh":"心室颤动（室颤），无反应，无脉搏"},{"id":"r2","en":"Ventricular Tachycardia (VTach), unresponsive, pulseless","zh":"室性心动过速（室速），无反应，无脉搏"},{"id":"r3","en":"Asystole (flatline on monitor), unresponsive, pulseless","zh":"心室停搏（监护仪平线），无反应，无脉搏"},{"id":"r4","en":"Normal sinus rhythm on monitor, unresponsive, pulseless (PEA)","zh":"监护仪上为正常窦性心律，无反应，无脉搏（无脉电活动）"}],"columns":[{"id":"c2","en":"Non-shockable rhythm (Requires immediate CPR and epinephrine, no shock)","zh":"不可除颤心律（需要立即CPR和肾上腺素，不可电击）"},{"id":"c1","en":"Shockable rhythm (Requires immediate unsynchronized defibrillation)","zh":"可除颤心律（需要立即非同步电除颤）"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["c1"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["c2"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["c2"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"In cardiac arrest, VFib (Row 1) and pulseless VTach (Row 2) are shockable rhythms requiring immediate unsynchronized defibrillation to reset electrical activity. Asystole (Row 3) and Pulseless Electrical Activity (Row 4, PEA) are non-shockable rhythms where electrical shocks are ineffective and contraindicated; they are treated with high-quality CPR and IV epinephrine.","rationaleCorrectZh":"在心脏骤停中，室颤（第1行）和无脉性室速（第2行）是可除颤的心律，需要立即进行非同步除颤以重置电活动。心室停搏（第3行）和无脉电活动（第4行/PEA）是不可除颤的心律，电击在这些心律中无效且属于禁忌；它们使用高质量CPR和静脉注射肾上腺素进行治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the division of ACLS arrest algorithms. Shockable: VFib/pulseless VT. Non-shockable: Asystole/PEA. Classify rows 1 and 2 under shockable, and rows 3 and 4 under non-shockable.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆ACLS骤停流程的分支。可除颤：室颤/无脉室速。不可除颤：心室停搏/PEA。将第1行和第2行分类为可除颤，将第3行和第4行分类为不可除颤。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2650,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_mc_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.43","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.43.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.43.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[147,225],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,70],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is caring for a client with stage 4 chronic kidney disease. The client's laboratory results reveal a serum potassium level of 6.3 mEq/L. Which ECG change should the nurse anticipate observing on the cardiac monitor?","fullStemZh":"护士正在护理一名4期慢性肾脏病患者。患者的实验室检查结果显示血清钾水平为 6.3 mEq/L。护士应预期在心电监护仪上观察到哪种ECG改变？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which ECG change should the nurse anticipate observing on the cardiac monitor?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应预期在心电监护仪上观察到哪种ECG改变？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's laboratory results reveal a serum potassium level of 6.3 mEq/L.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的实验室检查结果显示血清钾水平为 6.3 mEq/L。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Tall, peaked T waves","zh":"高尖的T波"},{"id":"A","en":"Prominent U waves","zh":"明显的U波"},{"id":"B","en":"Prolonged QT interval","zh":"QT间期延长"},{"id":"C","en":"ST-segment elevation","zh":"ST段抬高"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hyperkalemia (serum potassium > 5.0 mEq/L) alters the cardiac action potential, causing rapid repolarization of the ventricles. This manifests on the ECG as tall, peaked T waves (usually narrow-based). As potassium levels rise further, PR prolongation, QRS widening, flattening of P waves, and ultimately a sine-wave pattern can occur, leading to cardiac arrest.","rationaleCorrectZh":"高钾血症（血清钾 > 5.0 mEq/L）会改变心肌动作电位，引起心室快速复极。这在心电图上表现为高尖的T波（通常基底较窄）。随着钾水平的进一步升高，可能会出现PR间期延长、QRS波群变宽、P波变平，并最终出现正弦波模式，导致心脏骤停。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate the electrolyte imbalance (hyperkalemia) with its classic cardiac symptom: peaked T waves ('K' for potassium, 'K' for peaked). Memorize the distinction between hypokalemia (U wave) and hyperkalemia (peaked T wave).","testTakingStrategyZh":"将电解质失衡（高钾血症）与其经典心脏症状联系起来：高尖T波（“K”代表钾，高尖的T波）。记忆低钾血症（U波）与高钾血症（高尖T波）之间的区别。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2651,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_mc_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.44","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Dosage Calculations","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.44.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.44.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[217,258],"terminalOffsetsZh":[66,78],"fullStemEn":"A client with atrial fibrillation who takes digoxin daily is admitted with reports of nausea, anorexia, and seeing yellow-green halos around lights. The cardiac monitor shows sinus bradycardia at 48 beats per minute. Which action should the nurse take first?","fullStemZh":"一名每日服用地高辛的心房颤动患者因主诉恶心、食欲减退以及看灯光周围有黄绿色光晕入院。心电监护仪显示窦性心动过缓，心率为每分钟48次。护士首先应采取哪项措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which action should the nurse take first?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士首先应采取哪项措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The cardiac monitor shows sinus bradycardia at 48 beats per minute.","penultimateSentenceZh":"心电监护仪显示窦性心动过缓，心率为每分钟48次。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hold the digoxin dose and notify the healthcare provider","zh":"暂停地高辛给药并通知医生"},{"id":"C","en":"Administer the next scheduled dose of digoxin","zh":"使用下一次按计划服用的地高辛"},{"id":"B","en":"Increase the dietary intake of potassium rich foods","zh":"增加膳食中富含钾的食物摄入量"},{"id":"A","en":"Prepare for immediate cardioversion","zh":"准备立即进行电复律"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The client is exhibiting classic signs of digoxin toxicity (nausea, anorexia, visual disturbances like yellow-green halos, and bradycardia). Digoxin slows conduction through the AV node, causing bradycardia or heart blocks. The nurse's priority action is to withhold the medication (hold digoxin) and notify the healthcare provider to check digoxin and electrolyte levels. Administering more digoxin is contraindicated. Cardioversion is not indicated for stable bradycardia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"该患者表现出地高辛中毒的经典体征（恶心、食欲不振、黄绿色光晕等视觉障碍以及心动过缓）。地高辛会减慢通过房室结的传导，引起心动过缓或房室传导阻滞。护士的首要措施是暂停给药（停用地高辛）并通知医生，以检查地高辛浓度和电解质水平。继续给予地高辛是禁忌的。电复律不适用于稳定的心动过缓。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the symptoms: nausea, anorexia, yellow-green halos, bradycardia. Connect these directly to digoxin toxicity (digoxin has a narrow therapeutic index: 0.5-2.0 ng/mL). The safety-first action for suspected toxicity is to hold the drug and contact the provider. Eliminate therapeutic or active feeding options.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定症状：恶心、食欲减退、黄绿色光晕、心动过缓。将这些直接与地高辛中毒联系起来（地高辛治疗窗窄：0.5-2.0 ng/mL）。怀疑中毒时的安全首选措施是停药并联系医生。排除给药或主动喂食的选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The cardiac monitor shows sinus bradycardia at 48 beats per minute.","controlSentenceZh":"心电监护仪显示窦性心动过缓，心率为每分钟48次。"}
{"queueIndex":2652,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_mc_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.45","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.45.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.45.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[217,315],"terminalOffsetsZh":[70,96],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted following an intentional overdose of amitriptyline, a tricyclic antidepressant (TCA). The client's ECG shows sinus tachycardia at 110 beats per minute and a prolonged QT interval of 0.52 seconds. The nurse should identify that this client is at high risk for developing which lethal arrhythmia?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因蓄意过量服用三环类抗抑郁药（TCA）阿米替林入院。患者的ECG显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟110次，QT间期延长，为0.52秒。护士应识别出该患者发生哪种致命性心律失常的风险极高？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should identify that this client is at high risk for developing which lethal arrhythmia?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应识别出该患者发生哪种致命性心律失常的风险极高？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's ECG shows sinus tachycardia at 110 beats per minute and a prolonged QT interval of 0.52 seconds.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的ECG显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟110次，QT间期延长，为0.52秒。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"First-Degree AV Block","zh":"一度房室传导阻滞"},{"id":"C","en":"Atrial Fibrillation","zh":"心房颤动"},{"id":"A","en":"Asystole","zh":"心室停搏（平线）"},{"id":"B","en":"Torsades de Pointes","zh":"尖端扭转型室速"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"A prolonged QT interval (>0.44 seconds in men, >0.46 seconds in women) represents delayed ventricular repolarization, which predisposes the client to a polymorphic ventricular tachycardia known as Torsades de Pointes. TCAs block cardiac sodium channels and prolong repolarization, increasing the risk of this lethal arrhythmia, which can degenerate into ventricular fibrillation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"QT间期延长（男性 >0.44秒，女性 >0.46秒）代表心室复极延迟，这使患者易发生被称为尖端扭转型室速的多形性室性心动过速。TCA阻断心脏钠通道并延长复极过程，增加了这种致命性心律失常的风险，该心律失常可恶化为心室颤动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall the classic correlation: Prolonged QT interval = risk of Torsades de Pointes. Understand that drugs like TCAs, macrolides, and antipsychotics can prolong the QT interval and require ECG monitoring. Select Torsades de Pointes.","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆经典的关联：QT间期延长 = 发生尖端扭转型室速的风险。理解像TCA、大环内酯类和抗精神病药等药物能延长QT间期，需要心电图监测。选择尖端扭转型室速。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2653,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_sata_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.46","itemType":"select_all","category":"Health Promotion and Maintenance","topic":"Chronic Disease Management & Lifestyle","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.46.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.46.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[185,207],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,55],"fullStemEn":"The nurse is preparing a discharge teaching plan for a client who has just received a permanent cardiac pacemaker. Which instructions should the nurse include in the client's teaching? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"护士正为一名刚刚接受了永久性心脏起搏器植入的患者准备出院宣教计划。护士应在宣教中包含哪些指导？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which instructions should the nurse include in the client's teaching?","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士应在宣教中包含哪些指导？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Carry a pacemaker identification card at all times","zh":"随身携带起搏器识别卡"},{"id":"F","en":"Keep cell phones in a shirt pocket directly over the pacemaker site","zh":"将手机放在直接位于起搏器部位上方的衬衫口袋中"},{"id":"B","en":"Check your radial pulse daily and report rates below the pacemaker set limit","zh":"每日检查桡动脉搏动，并报告低于起搏器设定下限的心率"},{"id":"A","en":"Avoid lifting the arm on the pacemaker side above shoulder height for 4 weeks","zh":"术后4周内避免将起搏器侧的手臂抬高过肩"},{"id":"C","en":"Inform all healthcare providers and dentists that you have a pacemaker","zh":"告知所有医务人员和牙医你装有起搏器"},{"id":"E","en":"It is safe to undergo magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scans without restriction","zh":"无限制地接受磁共振成像（MRI）检查是安全的"}],"correct":["A","B","C","D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Discharge teaching for a new permanent pacemaker includes preventing lead dislodgement (avoid raising the arm above shoulder level for 4 weeks), monitoring cardiac activity (daily pulse checks), safety warnings (carrying the ID card, notifying all clinicians), and avoiding electromagnetic interference. MRI scans are contraindicated unless the device is cleared as MRI-conditional. Cell phones should be kept at least 6 inches away from the generator.","rationaleCorrectZh":"新的永久性起搏器出院宣教包括预防电极导线移位（4周内避免抬高手臂过肩）、监测心脏活动（每日自测脉搏）、安全警示（随身携带识别卡、通知所有临床医生）以及避免电磁干扰。禁止进行MRI扫描，除非该设备已被明确为MRI兼容。手机应与起搏器发生器保持至少6英寸的距离。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Analyze post-op safety rules. raising the arm can pull leads (select A). monitoring is needed (select B). medical warnings are standard (select C, D). MRIs are magnetically dangerous (eliminate E). cell phones interfere (eliminate F).","testTakingStrategyZh":"分析术后安全规则。抬起手臂可能会拉扯导线（选择A）。需要进行监测（选择B）。医疗警示是标准操作（选择C、D）。MRI存在磁性危险（排除E）。手机存在干扰（排除F）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2654,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_mc_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.47","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.47.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.47.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[235,318],"terminalOffsetsZh":[69,92],"fullStemEn":"A client presents to the emergency department reporting substernal chest pressure radiating to the left jaw. The client's ECG shows sinus tachycardia at 105 beats per minute and significant ST-segment elevation in leads V2 through V4. The nurse should recognize these findings are diagnostic for which pathophysiology?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因胸骨后压迫感放射至左下颌就诊于急诊科。患者的ECG显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟105次，且在V2至V4导联有显著的ST段抬高。护士应认识到这些发现可诊断为哪种病理生理改变？","terminalSentenceEn":"The nurse should recognize these findings are diagnostic for which pathophysiology?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应认识到这些发现可诊断为哪种病理生理改变？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's ECG shows sinus tachycardia at 105 beats per minute and significant ST-segment elevation in leads V2 through V4.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的ECG显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟105次，且在V2至V4导联有显著的ST段抬高。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Acute anterior myocardial injury/infarction (STEMI)","zh":"急性前壁心肌损伤/梗死（STEMI）"},{"id":"D","en":"Acute pericarditis","zh":"急性心包炎"},{"id":"B","en":"Digoxin-induced cardiac changes","zh":"地高辛引起的心脏改变"},{"id":"A","en":"Chronic stable angina","zh":"慢性稳定性心绞痛"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"ST-segment elevation indicates acute myocardial injury due to complete occlusion of a coronary artery (STEMI). Leads V2, V3, and V4 view the anterior wall of the left ventricle, which is supplied by the left anterior descending (LAD) coronary artery. This is a medical emergency requiring rapid reperfusion therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"ST段抬高提示由于冠状动脉完全闭塞引起的急性心肌损伤（STEMI）。V2、V3和V4导联面对左心室前壁，该部位由左前降支（LAD）冠状动脉供血。这属于医疗紧急情况，需要迅速进行再灌注治疗。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the key ECG finding: ST-segment elevation (STEMI). Localize it using the leads: V2-V4 view the anterior wall of the heart. Connect STEMI + V2-V4 to acute anterior wall myocardial infarction. Eliminate chronic or diffuse options.","testTakingStrategyZh":"确定关键心电图发现：ST段抬高（STEMI）。使用导联进行定位：V2-V4导联面对心脏前壁。将 STEMI + V2-V4 与急性前壁心肌梗死联系起来。排除慢性或弥漫性选项。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The client's ECG shows sinus tachycardia at 105 beats per minute and significant ST-segment elevation in leads V2 through V4.","controlSentenceZh":"患者的ECG显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟105次，且在V2至V4导联有显著的ST段抬高。"}
{"queueIndex":2655,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_sata_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.48","itemType":"select_all","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Endocrine & Neurological Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.48.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.48.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[280,302],"terminalOffsetsZh":[81,89],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the intensive care unit post-cardiac catheterization. The client's cardiac monitor displays sinus tachycardia at 120 beats per minute with low-voltage QRS complexes. Which assessment findings should alert the nurse to the development of cardiac tamponade? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患者在心脏导管插入术后收治入重症监护室。患者的心电监护仪显示窦性心动过速，心率为每分钟120次，伴低电压QRS波群。以下哪些评估发现应警示护士发生了心包填塞？选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which assessment findings should alert the nurse to the development of cardiac tamponade?","penultimateSentenceZh":"以下哪些评估发现应警示护士发生了心包填塞？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"F","en":"Strong, bounding peripheral pulses","zh":"外周动脉搏动有力且洪大"},{"id":"B","en":"Muffled or distant heart sounds","zh":"心音遥远或低钝"},{"id":"E","en":"Pulsus paradoxus (systolic BP drops >10 mmHg on inspiration)","zh":"奇脉（吸气时收缩压下降 >10 mmHg）"},{"id":"D","en":"Hypertension with a widening pulse pressure","zh":"高血压伴脉压变宽"},{"id":"C","en":"Hypotension with narrowing pulse pressure","zh":"低血压伴脉压变窄"},{"id":"A","en":"Jugular venous distention (JVD)","zh":"颈静脉怒张（JVD）"}],"correct":["A","B","C","E"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Cardiac tamponade is a life-threatening compression of the heart due to fluid accumulation in the pericardial sac. Classic signs comprise Beck's triad: hypotension (due to decreased stroke volume), JVD (due to backed-up venous pressure), and muffled heart sounds (due to fluid insulating the heart). Another key finding is pulsus paradoxus (systolic BP drop of >10 mmHg during inspiration). Bounding pulses and widening pulse pressure are not seen; instead, pulses are weak and pulse pressure narrows.","rationaleCorrectZh":"心包填塞是由于心包腔内液体异常积聚导致心脏受压的危及生命的病症。经典体征包含贝克三联征（Beck's triad）：低血压（心搏量减少所致）、颈静脉怒张（静脉压回流受阻所致）以及心音遥远/低钝（液体阻隔心脏所致）。另一个关键发现是奇脉（吸气时收缩压下降 >10 mmHg）。不会出现洪大搏动和脉压变宽；相反，脉搏微弱且脉压变窄。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Recall Beck's Triad for cardiac tamponade (Muffled heart sounds, JVD, Hypotension). Also, remember that pulsus paradoxus is associated with tamponade. Eliminate Cushing's triad features (hypertension, wide pulse pressure) and signs of high cardiac output (bounding pulses).","testTakingStrategyZh":"回忆心包填塞的贝克三联征（心音遥远、颈静脉怒张、低血压）。此外，记住奇脉与心包填塞相关。排除库欣三联征的特征（高血压、宽脉压）以及高心输出量征象（洪大脉）。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2656,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_b5_mc_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.49","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.49.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.49.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[201,254],"terminalOffsetsZh":[55,68],"fullStemEn":"A client with an eating disorder and persistent purging is admitted to the psychiatric unit. The client's ECG shows sinus rhythm with flattening of the T waves and the appearance of prominent U waves. Which electrolyte imbalance should the nurse suspect?","fullStemZh":"一名患有进食障碍且持续导泻呕吐的患者收治入精神科病房。患者的心电图显示窦性心律，伴有T波平坦和明显的U波出现。护士应怀疑哪种电解质失衡？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which electrolyte imbalance should the nurse suspect?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应怀疑哪种电解质失衡？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's ECG shows sinus rhythm with flattening of the T waves and the appearance of prominent U waves.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的心电图显示窦性心律，伴有T波平坦和明显的U波出现。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Hypocalcemia","zh":"低钙血症"},{"id":"C","en":"Hyperkalemia","zh":"高钾血症"},{"id":"D","en":"Hypokalemia","zh":"低钾血症"},{"id":"B","en":"Hypercalcemia","zh":"高钙血症"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Hypokalemia (serum potassium < 3.5 mEq/L) causes delayed ventricular repolarization, which is manifested on the ECG as flattening or inversion of T waves, ST-segment depression, and the development of prominent U waves. Purging leads to loss of potassium through gastric contents and kidneys, commonly triggering hypokalemia.","rationaleCorrectZh":"低钾血症（血清钾 < 3.5 mEq/L）导致心室复极延迟，这在心电图上表现为T波低平或倒置、ST段压低以及明显的U波出现。导泻呕吐导致通过胃内容物和肾脏流失钾，常用诱发低钾血症。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Associate the purge behavior (loss of potassium) with the clinical laboratory correlation (hypokalemia). Memorize the classic ECG signs of hypokalemia: flat T waves, ST depression, and prominent U waves. Select hypokalemia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"将导泻/呕吐行为（流失钾）与临床实验室指标联系起来（低钾血症）。记忆低钾血症的经典心电图表现：T波低平、ST段压低和明显的U波。选择低钾血症。","sourceMetadata":null,"mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2657,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_pacer_failure_to_capture_2026_07_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.50","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Electrolyte Imbalances","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.50.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.50.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[114,147],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,43],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the telemetry strip from a client with a permanent ventricular pacemaker who reports dizziness. Which pacemaker problem is shown?","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名装有永久性心室起搏器且主诉头晕的患者遥测心律条。图中显示哪一种起搏器问题？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which pacemaker problem is shown?","terminalSentenceZh":"图中显示哪一种起搏器问题？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the telemetry strip from a client with a permanent ventricular pacemaker who reports dizziness.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名装有永久性心室起搏器且主诉头晕的患者遥测心律条。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Failure to sense","zh":"未感知（感知失效）"},{"id":"D","en":"Failure to capture","zh":"未夺获（夺获失效）"},{"id":"A","en":"Oversensing","zh":"感知过度"},{"id":"C","en":"Failure to pace","zh":"未起搏（起搏失效）"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Failure to capture occurs when a pacemaker stimulus is delivered but does not depolarize the myocardium. In the strip, some pacing spikes are not followed by a paced QRS complex, so the device is firing but the ventricle is not consistently responding. This can cause symptomatic bradycardia and may occur with lead displacement, battery/output problems, or metabolic disturbances such as hyperkalemia or acidosis.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未夺获（夺获失效）是指起搏器刺激已经发放，但未能使心肌除极。图中心律条有些起搏尖峰波后没有出现起搏性QRS波群，说明起搏器正在发放脉冲，但心室没有持续响应。这可导致有症状的心动过缓，可能与导线移位、电池或输出问题，或高钾血症、酸中毒等代谢异常有关。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Separate the two pacemaker tasks: pacing means the device fires a spike; capture means the myocardium responds with a QRS. Spikes without QRS complexes point to a capture problem.","testTakingStrategyZh":"把起搏器的两个任务分开：起搏表示设备发放尖峰波；夺获表示心肌以QRS波群作出反应。有尖峰波但无QRS波群，提示夺获问题。","sourceMetadata":"Retires and replaces ekg_b5_mc_04; clinical target preserved from reviewed canonical item with visual cue moved into rhythm_strip.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2658,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_pacer_failure_to_sense_2026_07_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.51","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.51.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.51.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,192],"terminalOffsetsZh":[24,52],"fullStemEn":"The nurse reviews the telemetry strip for a client with a temporary ventricular pacemaker. Which pacemaker malfunction should the nurse identify, and which dangerous rhythm can it precipitate?","fullStemZh":"护士查看一名装有临时心室起搏器患者的遥测心律条。护士应识别出哪种起搏器故障，以及它可能诱发哪种危险心律？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which pacemaker malfunction should the nurse identify, and which dangerous rhythm can it precipitate?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应识别出哪种起搏器故障，以及它可能诱发哪种危险心律？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the telemetry strip for a client with a temporary ventricular pacemaker.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看一名装有临时心室起搏器患者的遥测心律条。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Failure to pace, causing bradycardia and cardiogenic shock","zh":"未起搏（起搏失效），导致心动过缓和心源性休克"},{"id":"A","en":"Failure to sense, causing R-on-T phenomenon and ventricular fibrillation","zh":"未感知（感知失效），导致R-on-T现象和心室颤动"},{"id":"B","en":"Oversensing, causing rapid supraventricular tachycardia","zh":"感知过度，导致快速室上性心动过速"},{"id":"D","en":"Failure to capture, causing severe asystole","zh":"未夺获（夺获失效），导致严重心室停搏"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Failure to sense, or undersensing, occurs when the pacemaker does not recognize the client's intrinsic cardiac activity. The strip shows pacer spikes occurring despite intrinsic complexes, including an inappropriately timed spike during repolarization. A stimulus that falls on the vulnerable T-wave period can produce an R-on-T phenomenon and trigger ventricular tachycardia or ventricular fibrillation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未感知（感知失效，也称感知不足）是指起搏器未识别患者自身的心脏电活动。图中在已有固有波群时仍出现起搏尖峰波，其中包括在复极期不合时宜出现的尖峰波。刺激落在脆弱的T波时期可产生R-on-T现象，并诱发室性心动过速或心室颤动。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look for whether the pacemaker respects intrinsic beats. Spikes that occur during the client's own QRS/T cycle mean the device is not sensing native activity, and a spike on the T wave raises concern for R-on-T deterioration.","testTakingStrategyZh":"观察起搏器是否避开固有心搏。如果尖峰波出现在患者自身QRS/T周期内，说明设备未感知固有活动；尖峰波落在T波上时，应担心R-on-T导致恶化。","sourceMetadata":"Retires and replaces ekg_b5_mc_05; clinical target preserved from reviewed canonical item with visual cue moved into rhythm_strip.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2659,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"ekg_pacer_failure_to_pace_2026_07_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.52","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":"recognize_cues","stemPathEn":"questions.52.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.52.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,176],"terminalOffsetsZh":[41,54],"fullStemEn":"A client with a ventricular pacemaker set to maintain a minimum rate of 60/min reports lightheadedness. The nurse reviews the telemetry strip. Which pacemaker problem is shown?","fullStemZh":"一名装有心室起搏器的患者设定最低频率为60次/分，现主诉头晕。护士查看遥测心律条。图中显示哪一种起搏器问题？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which pacemaker problem is shown?","terminalSentenceZh":"图中显示哪一种起搏器问题？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the telemetry strip.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士查看遥测心律条。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Failure to capture","zh":"未夺获（夺获失效）"},{"id":"C","en":"Failure to pace","zh":"未起搏（起搏失效）"},{"id":"D","en":"Normal ventricular capture","zh":"正常心室夺获"},{"id":"B","en":"Failure to sense","zh":"未感知（感知失效）"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Failure to pace means the pacemaker does not generate a stimulus when pacing is expected, so the ECG shows absent pacing spikes during a pause or a rate below the programmed lower limit. In this strip, the pacer captures when it fires, but there is a prolonged interval without pacing spikes despite the 60/min setting.","rationaleCorrectZh":"未起搏（起搏失效）是指在预期需要起搏时，起搏器没有产生刺激，因此心电图可见长间歇或心率低于设定下限时缺乏起搏尖峰波。图中起搏器发放时能够夺获，但在设定为60次/分的情况下出现长时间没有尖峰波的间歇。","testTakingStrategyEn":"First ask whether a spike appears when one is expected. A long pause without spikes at a rate below the pacemaker limit points to failure to pace; spikes without QRS would be failure to capture.","testTakingStrategyZh":"先判断在预期需要起搏时是否出现尖峰波。心率低于起搏器下限时出现长时间无尖峰波，提示未起搏；若有尖峰波但无QRS，则是夺获失效。","sourceMetadata":"Retires and replaces ekg_b5_matrix_10; narrows the former three-row matching item to the previously unrenderable failure-to-pace cue.","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2660,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"iot_hf_ckd_declining_output","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.53","itemType":"select_all","category":"Basic Care and Comfort","topic":"Nutritional & Fluid Support","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.53.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.53.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[197,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[61,70],"fullStemEn":"An adult client with heart failure and chronic kidney disease is receiving scheduled maintenance IV fluids. Which statements about the client's intake and output trend are supported by the record? Select all that apply.","fullStemZh":"一名患有心力衰竭和慢性肾病的成人患者正在按计划接受维持性静脉输液。根据记录，哪些关于该患者液体摄入与排出趋势的陈述有依据？请选择所有适用项。","terminalSentenceEn":"Select all that apply.","terminalSentenceZh":"请选择所有适用项。","penultimateSentenceEn":"Which statements about the client's intake and output trend are supported by the record?","penultimateSentenceZh":"根据记录，哪些关于该患者液体摄入与排出趋势的陈述有依据？","responseContext":{"type":"select_all","options":[{"id":"d","en":"Intake rises at each successive interval.","zh":"摄入量在每个后续时间段均上升。"},{"id":"a","en":"The intake amount is unchanged across the four intervals.","zh":"四个时间段的摄入量保持不变。"},{"id":"e","en":"Output increases after the 8-hour interval.","zh":"排出量在 8 小时时间段之后增加。"},{"id":"c","en":"The positive interval fluid balance becomes larger over time.","zh":"每个时间段的正液体平衡随时间逐渐扩大。"},{"id":"f","en":"The interval fluid balance changes from positive to negative.","zh":"分段液体平衡由正转为负。"},{"id":"b","en":"Output decreases at each successive interval.","zh":"排出量在每个后续时间段均下降。"}],"correct":["a","b","c"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake is 300 mL in every interval. Output falls from 280 mL to 260 mL, 180 mL, and 80 mL. Because intake remains constant while output falls, the positive interval balance widens from +20 mL to +220 mL. Intake does not rise, output does not recover after 8 hours, and no interval has a negative balance.","rationaleCorrectZh":"每个时间段的摄入量均为 300 mL。排出量依次从 280 mL 降至 260 mL、180 mL 和 80 mL。由于摄入量保持不变而排出量下降，每个时间段的正液体平衡从 +20 mL 扩大至 +220 mL。摄入量并未上升，8 小时后排出量也未恢复，并且没有任何时间段出现负平衡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a select-all trend item, compute the interval net (intake minus output) for each time block before judging any option; do not infer the shape from the stem's diagnosis. Check each candidate statement against the actual per-interval numbers rather than the cumulative total, and reject any statement that only fits the final number, not the interval-by-interval pattern.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于全选式趋势题，应先算出每个时间段的分段净值（摄入量减排出量），再判断各选项，不要仅凭题干中的诊断推测趋势形态。用逐段的实际数值而非累积总量来核对每条陈述，凡是只符合最终总量、而不符合逐段变化规律的陈述均应排除。","sourceMetadata":"NICE CG174, Intravenous fluid therapy in adults in hospital, recommendations 1.1.3–1.2.4, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg174/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2661,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"iot_furosemide_late_partial_reversal","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.54","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.54.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.54.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,69],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is receiving scheduled IV furosemide doses for volume overload management. Which statement about the shape of the client's fluid balance over the period is best supported by the record?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者正在按计划接受静脉注射 furosemide，以管理容量负荷过多。根据记录，哪项陈述最能说明该患者在此期间液体平衡的变化形态？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement about the shape of the client's fluid balance over the period is best supported by the record?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据记录，哪项陈述最能说明该患者在此期间液体平衡的变化形态？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An adult client is receiving scheduled IV furosemide doses for volume overload management.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名成人患者正在按计划接受静脉注射 furosemide，以管理容量负荷过多。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"c","en":"The client maintains a negative interval fluid balance during all four intervals.","zh":"患者在全部四个时间段内均保持负的分段液体平衡。"},{"id":"a","en":"The cumulative fluid deficit deepens through 12 hours, then partially reverses as the final interval becomes positive.","zh":"累积液体负平衡持续加深至 12 小时，随后因最后一个时间段转为正平衡而部分逆转。"},{"id":"b","en":"The cumulative balance begins positive, crosses below zero between 8 and 12 hours, and becomes more negative thereafter.","zh":"累积液体平衡起初为正，在 8 至 12 小时之间降至零以下，之后负平衡进一步加深。"},{"id":"d","en":"The interval fluid balance remains unchanged while the cumulative balance declines steadily.","zh":"各时间段的液体平衡保持不变，而累积液体平衡持续下降。"}],"correct":["a"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The interval balances are −200 mL, −150 mL, −50 mL, and then +100 mL. The cumulative deficit therefore deepens from −200 mL to −400 mL through 12 hours, then partially reverses to −300 mL during the final interval. The final interval is positive, so the client does not maintain a negative interval balance throughout.","rationaleCorrectZh":"各时间段的液体平衡依次为 −200 mL、−150 mL、−50 mL，最后为 +100 mL。因此，累积负平衡从 −200 mL 持续加深至 12 小时时的 −400 mL，随后在最后一个时间段部分逆转至 −300 mL。最后一个时间段为正平衡，所以患者并非全程都保持负的分段液体平衡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an item's final cumulative net cannot by itself distinguish the offered shapes, trace the cumulative balance interval by interval and note where it deepens, levels off, or reverses, rather than anchoring on the ending total or the stem's drug name.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当最终累积净值本身不足以区分各选项所描述的形态时，应逐段追踪累积液体平衡，注意其在何处加深、趋于平稳或发生逆转，而不要只依据最终总量或题干中提到的药物名称做判断。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Furosemide injection prescribing information, Clinical Pharmacology 12.2, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=3747bbcd-783d-4baa-bb5b-b6827bf390e3","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2662,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"iot_fluid_challenge_output_divergence","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.55","itemType":"matrix","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.55.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.55.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,224],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,70],"fullStemEn":"An adult with hypotension and rising creatinine is receiving a fluid challenge per protocol, with urine output reassessed at each interval. For each statement, indicate whether it is supported or not supported by the record.","fullStemZh":"一名伴有低血压和 creatinine 升高的成人正按方案接受液体负荷试验，并在每个时间段重新评估尿量。请判断以下每项陈述是否得到记录支持。","terminalSentenceEn":"For each statement, indicate whether it is supported or not supported by the record.","terminalSentenceZh":"请判断以下每项陈述是否得到记录支持。","penultimateSentenceEn":"An adult with hypotension and rising creatinine is receiving a fluid challenge per protocol, with urine output reassessed at each interval.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名伴有低血压和 creatinine 升高的成人正按方案接受液体负荷试验，并在每个时间段重新评估尿量。","responseContext":{"type":"matrix","matrix":{"rows":[{"id":"r1","en":"Intake increases through 12 hours and then remains unchanged in the final interval.","zh":"摄入量持续增加至 12 小时，随后在最后一个时间段保持不变。"},{"id":"r2","en":"Output decreases at every interval while intake increases or remains at its higher level.","zh":"在摄入量增加或维持于较高水平的同时，排出量在每个时间段均下降。"},{"id":"r3","en":"The positive interval fluid balance widens across the record.","zh":"记录中的正分段液体平衡逐步扩大。"},{"id":"r4","en":"Output rises in parallel with the escalating intake.","zh":"排出量随不断增加的摄入量同步上升。"}],"columns":[{"id":"not_supported","en":"Not supported","zh":"无依据"},{"id":"supported","en":"Supported","zh":"有依据"}],"selectionMode":"single_per_row"},"correct":[{"rowId":"r1","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r2","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r3","columnIds":["supported"]},{"rowId":"r4","columnIds":["not_supported"]}]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"Intake rises from 400 mL to 600 mL and 700 mL, then remains at 700 mL. Output moves in the opposite direction, decreasing from 150 mL to 120 mL. The positive interval balance therefore widens from +250 mL to +580 mL. The record does not show output rising in parallel with intake.","rationaleCorrectZh":"摄入量从 400 mL 增至 600 mL 和 700 mL，随后维持在 700 mL。排出量则向相反方向变化，从 150 mL 降至 120 mL。因此，正分段液体平衡从 +250 mL 扩大至 +580 mL。记录并未显示排出量随摄入量同步上升。","testTakingStrategyEn":"For a matrix item classifying several statements against one dataset, evaluate the intake series and the output series independently across every interval before judging any row; mark a statement supported only when the exact recorded numbers confirm it interval by interval, not merely because the final cumulative number is consistent with it.","testTakingStrategyZh":"对于依据同一组数据判断多条陈述的矩阵题，应分别在每个时间段独立核查摄入量序列与排出量序列，再判断每一行；只有当逐段的确切记录数值证实某条陈述时，才判定其为有依据，而不能仅因最终累积数值与之相符就判定有依据。","sourceMetadata":"NICE CG174, Intravenous fluid therapy in adults in hospital, recommendations 1.1.3–1.2.4, https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg174/chapter/Recommendations","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2663,"bankPath":"banks/visual-canonical.json","bankSha256":"e42e2a3fa6aa349a61279e6988e250e65c2b752a6f36d33806a2671e0af0f9e4","topLevelQuestionId":"iot_furosemide_positive_to_negative_crossover","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.56","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Cardiovascular & Endocrine Medications","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.56.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.56.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[91,201],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,69],"fullStemEn":"An adult client is receiving scheduled IV furosemide doses for volume overload management. Which statement about the shape of the client's fluid balance over the period is best supported by the record?","fullStemZh":"一名成人患者正在按计划接受静脉注射 furosemide，以管理容量负荷过多。根据记录，哪项陈述最能说明该患者在此期间液体平衡的变化形态？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement about the shape of the client's fluid balance over the period is best supported by the record?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据记录，哪项陈述最能说明该患者在此期间液体平衡的变化形态？","penultimateSentenceEn":"An adult client is receiving scheduled IV furosemide doses for volume overload management.","penultimateSentenceZh":"一名成人患者正在按计划接受静脉注射 furosemide，以管理容量负荷过多。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"c","en":"The client maintains a negative interval fluid balance during all four intervals.","zh":"患者在全部四个时间段内均保持负的分段液体平衡。"},{"id":"a","en":"The cumulative fluid deficit deepens through 12 hours, then partially reverses as the final interval becomes positive.","zh":"累积液体负平衡持续加深至 12 小时，随后因最后一个时间段转为正平衡而部分逆转。"},{"id":"b","en":"The cumulative balance begins positive, crosses below zero between 8 and 12 hours, and becomes more negative thereafter.","zh":"累积液体平衡起初为正，在 8 至 12 小时之间降至零以下，之后负平衡进一步加深。"},{"id":"d","en":"The interval fluid balance remains unchanged while the cumulative balance declines steadily.","zh":"各时间段的液体平衡保持不变，而累积液体平衡持续下降。"}],"correct":["b"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The interval balances are +150 mL, +30 mL, −200 mL, and −280 mL. Cumulative balance therefore begins positive, rises to +180 mL at 8 hours, crosses below zero by 12 hours, and becomes more negative to −300 mL at 16 hours. The record does not show an initially deepening deficit followed by a late positive interval.","rationaleCorrectZh":"各时间段的液体平衡依次为 +150 mL、+30 mL、−200 mL 和 −280 mL。因此，累积液体平衡起初为正，在 8 小时时升至 +180 mL，到 12 小时时降至零以下，并在 16 小时时进一步降至 −300 mL。记录并未显示负平衡先持续加深、随后在最后一个时间段转为正平衡。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When an item's final cumulative net cannot by itself distinguish the offered shapes, trace the cumulative balance interval by interval and identify where it crosses from positive to negative, rather than anchoring on the ending total or the stem's drug name.","testTakingStrategyZh":"当最终累积净值本身不足以区分各选项所描述的形态时，应逐段追踪累积液体平衡，找出其由正转负的具体时间段，而不要只依据最终总量或题干中提到的药物名称做判断。","sourceMetadata":"DailyMed, Furosemide injection prescribing information, Clinical Pharmacology 12.2, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=3747bbcd-783d-4baa-bb5b-b6827bf390e3","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"An adult client is receiving scheduled IV furosemide doses for volume overload management.","controlSentenceZh":"一名成人患者正在按计划接受静脉注射 furosemide，以管理容量负荷过多。"}
{"queueIndex":2664,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_01","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.0","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.0.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.0.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[161,249],"terminalOffsetsZh":[44,65],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted following a motor vehicle collision. The nurse monitors the client's vital signs over the first 4 hours, as shown in the trend chart below. Based on these trends, which physiological state is the client most likely experiencing?","fullStemZh":"一名患者在机动车碰撞后入院。护士在最初的4小时内监测患者的生命体征，如下面的趋势图所示。根据这些趋势，患者最可能经历哪种生理状态？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on these trends, which physiological state is the client most likely experiencing?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据这些趋势，患者最可能经历哪种生理状态？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse monitors the client's vital signs over the first 4 hours, as shown in the trend chart below.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在最初的4小时内监测患者的生命体征，如下面的趋势图所示。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Increased intracranial pressure","zh":"颅内压增高"},{"id":"A","en":"Decompensated hypovolemic shock","zh":"失代偿性低血容量休克"},{"id":"D","en":"Neurogenic shock","zh":"神经源性休克"},{"id":"B","en":"Compensated hypovolemic shock","zh":"代偿性低血容量休克"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The vitals trend demonstrates a classic compensated shock pattern: the heart rate (HR) is steadily rising to maintain cardiac output, while the systolic blood pressure (SBP) remains relatively stable but the diastolic blood pressure (DBP) rises due to peripheral vasoconstriction, resulting in a narrowing pulse pressure. The mean arterial pressure (MAP) is still maintained above 65 mmHg.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生命体征趋势展示了经典的代偿性休克模式：心率（HR）稳步上升以维持心输出量，同时收缩压（SBP）保持相对稳定，但由于外周血管收缩导致舒张压（DBP）上升，从而导致脉压变窄。平均动脉压（MAP）仍维持在65 mmHg以上。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Look at the distance between SBP and DBP (pulse pressure). If it is narrowing while the heart rate is rising, think 'early shock' (compensated).","testTakingStrategyZh":"观察SBP和DBP之间的距离（脉压）。如果它正在变窄而心率在上升，请考虑“休克早期”（代偿性）。","sourceMetadata":"ATLS Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"The nurse monitors the client's vital signs over the first 4 hours, as shown in the trend chart below.","controlSentenceZh":"护士在最初的4小时内监测患者的生命体征，如下面的趋势图所示。"}
{"queueIndex":2665,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_02","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.1","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Sepsis & Septic Shock","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.1.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.1.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[122,206],"terminalOffsetsZh":[33,61],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with community-acquired pneumonia. The nurse reviews the client's vital signs over the past 8 hours. Based on the trend chart below, which intervention should the nurse anticipate next?","fullStemZh":"一名患者因社区获得性肺炎入院。护士回顾了患者过去8小时的生命体征。基于下面的趋势图，护士应预料到接下来会采取哪项干预措施？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the trend chart below, which intervention should the nurse anticipate next?","terminalSentenceZh":"基于下面的趋势图，护士应预料到接下来会采取哪项干预措施？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse reviews the client's vital signs over the past 8 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士回顾了患者过去8小时的生命体征。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Applying a warming blanket","zh":"使用加温毯"},{"id":"B","en":"Administering a beta-blocker to control heart rate","zh":"给予β受体阻滞剂以控制心率"},{"id":"A","en":"Administration of an antihypertensive medication","zh":"给予降压药"},{"id":"C","en":"Administration of a rapid IV fluid bolus","zh":"快速静脉推注补液"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The vital signs show a concerning trend consistent with developing sepsis/septic shock: persistent tachycardia, rising temperature, and a newly falling mean arterial pressure (MAP) dropping below the critical perfusion threshold of 65 mmHg. The priority intervention for septic shock is rapid fluid resuscitation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生命体征显示出与败血症/感染性休克发展相一致的令人担忧的趋势：持续心动过速、体温升高，以及新出现的平均动脉压（MAP）下降，跌破65 mmHg的临界灌注阈值。感染性休克的首要干预措施是快速液体复苏。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Identify the MAP dropping below the critical line of 65 mmHg. Hypotension + infection (pneumonia) = sepsis. First step: give fluids.","testTakingStrategyZh":"识别降至65 mmHg临界线以下的MAP。低血压+感染（肺炎）=败血症。第一步：补液。","sourceMetadata":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2666,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_03","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.2","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.2.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.2.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[168,204],"terminalOffsetsZh":[47,58],"fullStemEn":"A client is 6 hours postoperative following an open cholecystectomy. The nurse notes the following vital sign trends. The client's surgical dressing is dry and intact. What is the nurse's priority action?","fullStemZh":"一名患者在开放性胆囊切除术后6小时。护士注意到以下生命体征趋势。患者的手术敷料干燥且完好无损。护士的首要行动是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"What is the nurse's priority action?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士的首要行动是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The client's surgical dressing is dry and intact.","penultimateSentenceZh":"患者的手术敷料干燥且完好无损。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"Administer the PRN dose of intravenous morphine.","zh":"给予按需（PRN）剂量的静脉注射吗啡。"},{"id":"B","en":"Document the findings as normal postoperative changes.","zh":"将这些发现记录为正常的术后变化。"},{"id":"D","en":"Encourage the client to use the incentive spirometer.","zh":"鼓励患者使用诱发性肺量计。"},{"id":"A","en":"Notify the healthcare provider immediately.","zh":"立即通知医疗服务提供者。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The chart shows a classic pattern of internal bleeding/hemorrhage: the heart rate is steadily rising while the blood pressure (SBP and MAP) is progressively falling. Even with a dry dressing, these trends strongly suggest internal postoperative hemorrhage, which is a medical emergency requiring immediate provider notification.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图表显示了内出血/出血的经典模式：心率稳步上升，而血压（SBP和MAP）逐渐下降。即使敷料干燥，这些趋势也强烈提示术后内出血，这是一种需要立即通知医生的医疗紧急情况。","testTakingStrategyEn":"A dry dressing does not mean there is no bleeding; blood could be pooling internally. Rely on the vital signs: rising pulse and falling BP always demand immediate action.","testTakingStrategyZh":"敷料干燥并不意味着没有出血；血液可能在内部积聚。依靠生命体征：脉搏上升和血压下降始终需要立即采取行动。","sourceMetadata":"ATLS Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2667,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_04","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.3","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.3.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.3.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[158,212],"terminalOffsetsZh":[52,67],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with severe dehydration and receives 2 liters of 0.9% normal saline over 4 hours. The nurse evaluates the client's vital signs as shown. Which conclusion is most accurate based on these data?","fullStemZh":"一名严重脱水的患者入院，并在4小时内接受了2升0.9%生理盐水的输注。护士评估了患者的生命体征如图所示。根据这些数据，哪项结论最准确？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which conclusion is most accurate based on these data?","terminalSentenceZh":"根据这些数据，哪项结论最准确？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse evaluates the client's vital signs as shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士评估了患者的生命体征如图所示。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"The fluid resuscitation is effective.","zh":"液体复苏有效。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client requires a vasopressor infusion.","zh":"患者需要输注血管加压药。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client is experiencing an allergic reaction to the fluid.","zh":"患者对液体出现了过敏反应。"},{"id":"C","en":"The client is developing fluid volume overload.","zh":"患者正在发生液体负荷过重。"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The chart shows a positive response to fluid resuscitation. As intravascular volume is restored, the initially elevated heart rate (compensatory tachycardia) steadily decreases back into the normal range, while the initially low mean arterial pressure (MAP) steadily rises into the normal range.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图表显示了对液体复苏的积极反应。随着血管内容量的恢复，最初升高的心率（代偿性心动过速）稳步下降回正常范围，而最初较低的平均动脉压（MAP）稳步上升至正常范围。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Normalizing vitals (HR going down to baseline, BP going up to baseline) means your intervention is working.","testTakingStrategyZh":"生命体征恢复正常（HR降至基线，BP升至基线）意味着你的干预措施正在起效。","sourceMetadata":"Fundamentals of Nursing","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2668,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_05","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.4","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Skin & Wound Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.4.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.4.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[162,230],"terminalOffsetsZh":[49,68],"fullStemEn":"A client is being monitored in the neuro-ICU following a severe traumatic brain injury. The nurse observes the following vital sign trends over the last 2 hours. Based on these findings, what is the nurse's most immediate concern?","fullStemZh":"一名严重创伤性脑损伤后的患者正在神经重症监护室接受监测。护士观察到过去2小时内的以下生命体征趋势。基于这些发现，护士最直接的担忧是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on these findings, what is the nurse's most immediate concern?","terminalSentenceZh":"基于这些发现，护士最直接的担忧是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse observes the following vital sign trends over the last 2 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士观察到过去2小时内的以下生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Brainstem herniation","zh":"脑干疝"},{"id":"B","en":"Systemic inflammatory response syndrome (SIRS)","zh":"全身炎症反应综合征（SIRS）"},{"id":"A","en":"Hypovolemic shock","zh":"低血容量休克"},{"id":"C","en":"Spinal shock","zh":"脊髓休克"}],"correct":["D"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The vital signs show Cushing's triad: a progressively widening pulse pressure (systolic BP is rising significantly while diastolic BP remains stable or drops), combined with a plummeting heart rate (bradycardia) and an erratic or dropping respiratory rate. This indicates a life-threatening increase in intracranial pressure with concern for possible impending brainstem herniation.","rationaleCorrectZh":"生命体征显示了库欣三联征：脉压逐渐增宽（收缩压显著上升，而舒张压保持稳定或下降），伴随心率骤降（心动过缓）以及呼吸频率不稳定或下降。这表明颅内压出现了危及生命的升高，存在可能发生脑干疝的担忧。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Opposite arrows: If the blood pressure is going drastically UP (especially systolic) and the heart rate is going drastically DOWN, think brain problem (Cushing's triad).","testTakingStrategyZh":"相反的箭头：如果血压急剧上升（特别是收缩压），而心率急剧下降，请考虑脑部问题（库欣三联征）。","sourceMetadata":"ATLS Guidelines - Head Trauma","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2669,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_06","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.5","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Renal & Gastrointestinal Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.5.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.5.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[140,199],"terminalOffsetsZh":[39,54],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted with massive gastrointestinal bleeding. After 2 hours of observation, the nurse notes the following vital signs trend. Which statement best describes the client's current status?","fullStemZh":"一名发生大面积消化道出血的患者入院。观察2小时后，护士注意到以下生命体征趋势。哪句话最能描述患者目前的状态？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which statement best describes the client's current status?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪句话最能描述患者目前的状态？","penultimateSentenceEn":"After 2 hours of observation, the nurse notes the following vital signs trend.","penultimateSentenceZh":"观察2小时后，护士注意到以下生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"C","en":"The client's compensatory mechanisms are effectively maintaining perfusion.","zh":"患者的代偿机制正在有效地维持灌注。"},{"id":"A","en":"The client has entered the decompensated phase of shock.","zh":"患者已进入休克的失代偿期。"},{"id":"B","en":"The bleeding has spontaneously resolved.","zh":"出血已自发消退。"},{"id":"D","en":"The client is experiencing a vasovagal response.","zh":"患者正在经历血管迷走神经反应。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The chart shows decompensated shock. While the heart rate remains extremely high, the mean arterial pressure (MAP) and systolic blood pressure (SBP) have precipitously dropped below critical thresholds (MAP < 65). The body's compensatory mechanisms have failed to maintain blood pressure.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图表显示了失代偿性休克。虽然心率仍然极高，但平均动脉压（MAP）和收缩压（SBP）已急剧降至临界阈值以下（MAP < 65）。身体的代偿机制未能维持血压。","testTakingStrategyEn":"When the MAP suddenly plummets below 65 despite a high heart rate, the patient has transitioned from compensated to decompensated shock.","testTakingStrategyZh":"尽管心率很高，但当MAP突然骤降至65以下时，患者已从代偿期转为失代偿期休克。","sourceMetadata":"ATLS Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2670,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_07","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.6","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.6.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.6.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[143,198],"terminalOffsetsZh":[36,49],"fullStemEn":"A client is admitted to the emergency department following a high cervical spine injury. The nurse monitors the client's vital signs as shown. Which condition is most consistent with these findings?","fullStemZh":"一名患有高位颈椎损伤的患者被送入急诊室。护士监测患者的生命体征如图所示。哪种情况与这些发现最一致？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which condition is most consistent with these findings?","terminalSentenceZh":"哪种情况与这些发现最一致？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse monitors the client's vital signs as shown.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士监测患者的生命体征如图所示。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"Hypovolemic shock","zh":"低血容量休克"},{"id":"B","en":"Autonomic dysreflexia","zh":"自主神经反射异常"},{"id":"A","en":"Cardiogenic shock","zh":"心源性休克"},{"id":"C","en":"Neurogenic shock","zh":"神经源性休克"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The chart reveals profound hypotension (low MAP) accompanied by bradycardia (low HR). In the setting of a cervical spine injury, this unique combination—loss of sympathetic tone causing vasodilation (hypotension) and unopposed vagal tone (bradycardia)—is the hallmark of neurogenic shock.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图表显示严重的低血压（低MAP）伴心动过缓（低HR）。在颈椎损伤的情况下，这种独特的组合——交感神经张力丧失导致血管扩张（低血压）和无拮抗的迷走神经张力（心动过缓）——是神经源性休克的标志。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Any type of shock involves low blood pressure. If the heart rate is ALSO low, it is neurogenic shock.","testTakingStrategyZh":"任何类型的休克都涉及低血压。如果心率也很低，那就是神经源性休克。","sourceMetadata":"ATLS Guidelines","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2671,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_08","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.7","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies","topic":"Medication Safety & Admin","difficulty":"easy","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.7.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.7.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[102,190],"terminalOffsetsZh":[30,54],"fullStemEn":"A pediatric client is admitted with a high fever. The nurse administers oral acetaminophen at Hour 0. Based on the vitals trend chart, what is the most appropriate evaluation of the therapy?","fullStemZh":"一名儿科患者因高热入院。护士在第0小时给予口服对乙酰氨基酚。基于生命体征趋势图，对该治疗最合适的评估是什么？","terminalSentenceEn":"Based on the vitals trend chart, what is the most appropriate evaluation of the therapy?","terminalSentenceZh":"基于生命体征趋势图，对该治疗最合适的评估是什么？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse administers oral acetaminophen at Hour 0.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士在第0小时给予口服对乙酰氨基酚。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"D","en":"The client is experiencing a severe adverse drug reaction.","zh":"患者正在经历严重的药物不良反应。"},{"id":"A","en":"The therapy is effective; both temperature and heart rate are normalizing.","zh":"治疗有效；体温和心率都在恢复正常。"},{"id":"C","en":"The therapy is ineffective; an alternative antipyretic is needed immediately.","zh":"治疗无效；需要立即使用其他退热药。"},{"id":"B","en":"The client has developed sepsis.","zh":"患者已发展为败血症。"}],"correct":["A"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The trend shows the client's temperature decreasing toward the normal range following the administration of the antipyretic. Additionally, the heart rate (which was elevated due to the fever) is concurrently decreasing toward normal. This demonstrates a successful response to therapy.","rationaleCorrectZh":"趋势显示在服用退热药后，患者体温向正常范围下降。此外，由于发烧而升高的心率也同时向正常范围下降。这证明了对治疗的成功反应。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Remember the physiological link: fever increases metabolic demand, which increases heart rate. Curing the fever cures the tachycardia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"记住生理联系：发烧增加代谢需求，从而增加心率。治愈发烧即可治愈心动过速。","sourceMetadata":"Fundamentals of Nursing","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2672,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_09","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.8","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Physiological Adaptation","topic":"Cardiovascular Disorders","difficulty":"medium","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.8.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.8.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[175,219],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,64],"fullStemEn":"A client is recovering from an acute myocardial infarction. The nurse notes new crackles in the lung bases and observes the following vital signs trend over the last 3 hours. Which complication should the nurse suspect?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在从急性心肌梗死中恢复。护士注意到双肺底出现新的湿啰音，并观察到过去3小时内的生命体征趋势。护士应怀疑发生哪种并发症？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which complication should the nurse suspect?","terminalSentenceZh":"护士应怀疑发生哪种并发症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"The nurse notes new crackles in the lung bases and observes the following vital signs trend over the last 3 hours.","penultimateSentenceZh":"护士注意到双肺底出现新的湿啰音，并观察到过去3小时内的生命体征趋势。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Cardiogenic shock","zh":"心源性休克"},{"id":"C","en":"Pericardial tamponade","zh":"心包填塞"},{"id":"A","en":"Pulmonary embolism","zh":"肺栓塞"},{"id":"D","en":"Aortic aneurysm rupture","zh":"主动脉瘤破裂"}],"correct":["B"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The chart shows a progressive fall in MAP despite a compensatory increase in heart rate and respiratory rate. Combined with the history of myocardial infarction and the new onset of lung crackles (pulmonary edema due to left-sided heart failure), this points to pump failure, resulting in cardiogenic shock.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图表显示尽管心率和呼吸频率出现代偿性增加，但MAP仍在逐渐下降。结合心肌梗死病史和新出现的肺部湿啰音（左心衰竭导致的肺水肿），这指向泵衰竭，导致心源性休克。","testTakingStrategyEn":"Shock (low BP, high HR) + Crackles (fluid in lungs) = Cardiogenic shock.","testTakingStrategyZh":"休克（低BP，高HR）+ 湿啰音（肺内积液）= 心源性休克。","sourceMetadata":"AHA Advanced Cardiovascular Life Support","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":false,"controlSentenceEn":null,"controlSentenceZh":null}
{"queueIndex":2673,"bankPath":"banks/vitals-canonical.json","bankSha256":"5154e25492bced8e4a49d763f04e25e154389c31e085bf37669651e13d411b9d","topLevelQuestionId":"vit_10","embeddedQuestionId":null,"recordKind":"TOP_LEVEL_SCORED_LEAF","questionPath":"questions.9","itemType":"multiple_choice","category":"Reduction of Risk Potential","topic":"Perioperative Care","difficulty":"hard","ngnSkill":null,"stemPathEn":"questions.9.stem.en","stemPathZh":"questions.9.stem.zh","segmentationMethod":"Intl.Segmenter","segmentationConfidence":"HIGH","terminalOffsetsEn":[166,210],"terminalOffsetsZh":[51,63],"fullStemEn":"A client is undergoing general anesthesia using volatile inhaled anesthetics. Ten minutes into the procedure, the nurse notes the following rapid vital sign changes. Which complication is most likely occurring?","fullStemZh":"一名患者正在使用挥发性吸入麻醉剂进行全身麻醉。在手术开始10分钟后，护士注意到以下快速的生命体征变化。最有可能发生哪种并发症？","terminalSentenceEn":"Which complication is most likely occurring?","terminalSentenceZh":"最有可能发生哪种并发症？","penultimateSentenceEn":"Ten minutes into the procedure, the nurse notes the following rapid vital sign changes.","penultimateSentenceZh":"在手术开始10分钟后，护士注意到以下快速的生命体征变化。","responseContext":{"type":"multiple_choice","options":[{"id":"B","en":"Anaphylactic reaction","zh":"过敏反应"},{"id":"C","en":"Malignant hyperthermia","zh":"恶性高热"},{"id":"A","en":"Hemorrhagic shock","zh":"失血性休克"},{"id":"D","en":"Sepsis","zh":"败血症"}],"correct":["C"]},"rationaleCorrectEn":"The chart shows a dangerously rapid increase in both body temperature and heart rate shortly after the induction of general anesthesia. Combined with the exposure to inhaled anesthetics, this rapid hypermetabolic state is highly indicative of malignant hyperthermia, a rare but life-threatening complication requiring immediate administration of dantrolene.","rationaleCorrectZh":"图表显示在全身麻醉诱导后不久，体温和心率呈危险的快速上升。结合暴露于吸入麻醉剂的情况，这种快速的高代谢状态高度提示恶性高热，这是一种罕见但危及生命的并发症，需要立即给予丹曲林。","testTakingStrategyEn":"General anesthesia + extreme fever/tachycardia = Malignant Hyperthermia.","testTakingStrategyZh":"全身麻醉 + 极度发烧/心动过速 = 恶性高热。","sourceMetadata":"Malignant Hyperthermia Association of the United States","mechanicalSignals":{"rawPlaceholderInStem":false,"terminalContainsRawPlaceholder":false,"terminalBeginsThisItemOrQuestion":false,"terminalMentionsLearnerExpectation":false,"terminalFollowsExplicitResponseDemand":false,"exactEnglishTerminalRepeatedElsewhereInItem":false},"controlSelected":true,"controlSentenceEn":"Ten minutes into the procedure, the nurse notes the following rapid vital sign changes.","controlSentenceZh":"在手术开始10分钟后，护士注意到以下快速的生命体征变化。"}
